window.HYPOTHESES = {"published_at": "2026-09-08T21:46:21.756388+00:00", "experiment": "APOE4 vs APOE3 / mock microglia", "discovery": "RNA and protein", "evaluation_features": 618, "baseline": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.5446567723274521, "direction_accuracy": 0.8268608414239482, "hypothesis_id": "constant_positive_one", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7320097087378641, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.5446567723274521, "direction_accuracy": 0.8268608414239482, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7320097087378641, "n_features": 618}}}, "cohorts": [{"id": "opus-original", "label": "Opus / original", "count": 497, "best": 0.5279950098961133, "mean": 0.27902227349610353}, {"id": "sonnet-original", "label": "Sonnet / original", "count": 10, "best": 0.3101171980232298, "mean": 0.11734671255708165}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2", "label": "Opus / evidence-v2", "count": 109, "best": 0.5045434714896747, "mean": 0.31356984493296947}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3", "label": "Astra / original", "count": 20, "best": 0.31591653415995535, "mean": -0.009822704097367563}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2", "label": "Astra / evidence-v2", "count": 10, "best": 0.38066287850977765, "mean": 0.1418304663250905}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "label": "Sonnet / evidence-v2", "count": 10, "best": 0.424771974705316, "mean": 0.28698202653700305}], "hypotheses": [{"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1) with a strong list-wide positive shift, so only within-list rank enrichment, not absolute direction, is interpreted; the logarithm base and pseudocount are unspecified and effects are treated as ordinal.", "Coordinated transcript increases in a nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC/carrier module reflect increased pathway capacity rather than a normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-quality artifact that preferentially inflates highly expressed housekeeping transcripts.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme abundance and for flux at steps where no protein, metabolite, flux or localization measurement is supplied (all of Steps 1-5).", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and show frequent keratin and actin contamination, so no spot is assigned to a unique protein; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-driven astrocyte lipid or APOE secretion could contribute to the microglial state; cell-type deconvolution and any lipid, oxygen-consumption or tracer measurement are absent from the supplied data.", "SREBF1 target induction is assumed to reflect increased SREBP-1 transcriptional activity rather than only compensatory feedback to sterol depletion."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial pyruvate/anaplerotic entry, TCA-cycle enzymes and mitochondrial carriers that outstrips the global upward shift of this differential-expression list, while glycolytic commitment steps are not co-induced. We propose the rate-limiting node is mitochondrial citrate/malate export (SLC25A1-SLC25A11 exchange), which supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA for an SREBF1-associated lipogenic and sterol-esterification program (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, ACAT2, DHCR24), producing neutral-lipid accumulation. Increased lysosomal hydrolase and V-ATPase mRNA (including TFEB) is interpreted as a downstream CLEAR-type response to lipid load rather than the primary defect, because it is weaker than the mitochondrial signal, internally discordant (CTSS, IDS decreased) and not corroborated at the protein-spot level. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, SLC25A1 knockdown or citrate-carrier inhibition (CTPI-2) should lower neutral-lipid droplet content and de novo 13C-glucose incorporation into C16:0/C18:1 toward APOE3 levels, while leaving ETC subunit transcript elevation largely intact. If LD content and glucose-derived fatty-acid labelling are unchanged by SLC25A1 loss, the proposed citrate-export bottleneck is wrong.", "13C-glucose and 13C-glutamine tracing should show higher M+2 citrate enrichment and a higher glucose-derived fraction of cytosolic fatty acid in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Equal or lower enrichment in APOE4 would weaken Steps 1-4.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption in APOE4 without a matched increase in glycolytic rate. A glycolytic rather than oxidative shift, or no OCR difference, would weaken Step 3.", "Discriminating against the lysosomal-capacity alternative: acute lysosomal inhibition (bafilomycin A1 or a pan-cathepsin inhibitor) should increase lipid droplets in both genotypes but should not abolish the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess, whereas DGAT1 or SCD inhibition should collapse that excess. If the APOE4 excess disappears only with lysosomal manipulation, the primary bottleneck is endolysosomal, not the citrate-export node.", "Bulk cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase enzymatic activity and mature-cathepsin immunoblots should not be uniformly higher in APOE4 despite elevated transcripts, matching the bidirectional cathepsin-containing spots. Uniformly higher hydrolase activity plus intact substrate clearance would argue the CLEAR response is sufficient and would weaken Step 6.", "TFEB nuclear translocation should be a consequence of lipid load: pharmacological blockade of neutral-lipid esterification should reduce TFEB target transcripts in APOE4. Persistent TFEB target induction after lipid-storage blockade would place the lysosomal program upstream and falsify the ordering in Step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher mRNA for mitochondrial substrate entry and anaplerosis (MPC2, GLUD1, GLS, NNT). We infer, but did not measure, increased pyruvate and glutamate-derived carbon entry into the matrix.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): TCA-cycle enzyme transcripts (ACO2, OGDH, DLD, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1) are coordinately elevated well above the list-wide shift, implying increased citrate/malate cycling capacity; enzyme activity and metabolite pools were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux partitioning): electron-transport subunit transcripts (NDUFA5, NDUFS7, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5ME and ~35 further subunits) rise while committed glycolytic steps do not (HK2 and PFKP decreased), consistent with an oxidative rather than glycolytic bias; oxygen consumption was not measured.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck, measured RNA only): the exit of carbon from the matrix as citrate via SLC25A1, balanced by SLC25A11 malate/2-oxoglutarate exchange and SLC25A5 adenine-nucleotide exchange, is the step we propose limits how much of this oxidative carbon is diverted to cytosolic acetyl-CoA; ACSS2 provides a parallel acetate-derived route. Cytosolic acetyl-CoA and citrate pools are unmeasured and must not be treated as observed.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply supports an SREBF1-associated program (SCD, DGAT1, ACAT2, SOAT1, DHCR24, INSIG1, LDLR, MYLIP), which we infer channels fatty acid and sterol into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester; SREBP processing, localization and lipid species were not measured.", "Step 6 (secondary, partly discordant): the resulting neutral-lipid and membrane load engages a CLEAR-type transcriptional response (TFEB up; GAA, CTSB, CTSD, and V-ATPase subunit mRNA up), which we treat as compensatory rather than causal because cathepsin- and V-ATPase-containing protein spots move in both directions and CTSS and IDS mRNA are decreased."], "title": "APOE4 microglia bias carbon into a mitochondrial TCA/citrate-export node that feeds SREBF1-driven neutral-lipid esterification, with lysosomal hydrolase transcription rising only as a secondary response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.302168459557284, "cosine_similarity": 0.5279950098961133, "direction_accuracy": 0.5, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mean_absolute_error": 0.512948220064725, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.302168459557284, "cosine_similarity": 0.5279950098961133, "direction_accuracy": 0.5, "mean_absolute_error": 0.512948220064725, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.883722, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential list (all adj. p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive, median +1.46); program directionality is judged against that skewed background, and genes absent from the file (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE) are unknown, not unchanged. The RNA logarithm base is unspecified, so magnitudes are ordinal.", "Coordinated transcript changes in the SREBP-target and CLEAR-target sets are used as read-outs of upstream sterol sensing and TFEB-type activity; neither SREBP2 cleavage, TFEB nuclear localisation, nor hydrolase activity was measured, so activity and flux remain inferred.", "2D-gel spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (mean 4.8) and are used only for compatibility, never as confirmation of a named protein; the strongly increased series protein_spot:043-047 is equally consistent with ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) or TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32) or PSMD7/ACTB, and this ambiguity is preserved.", "Effects are attributed to the APOE4/APOE3 genotype difference in an isogenic pair at day 30 under mock treatment; astrocyte co-culture, cell-composition drift and any dissociation artefact are assumed not to generate the specific lysosome/sterol coherence.", "The mechanism claims an ongoing routing bias in the measured mock condition; any additional fragility (e.g. under lipid or myelin challenge) is a future-challenge prediction, not something these data establish.", "Descriptive coherence (lysosome 23/25 up, sterol synthesis 11/11 up) is not a formal enrichment result; the genes are not independent and no pathway test corrected for the selection."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by an altered lipid-routing cell state: transcripts for lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:C1QA/B/C), for sterol esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:FABP5, gene:CIDEB) and for endolysosomal biogenesis (gene:TFEB +2.38 with 23/25 represented lysosomal genes up, median +2.02) rise together with a complete SREBP-target biosynthetic set (11/11 up: gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD). Continued sterol-synthesis and uptake signalling in the presence of expanded catabolic and storage machinery is best explained by an ER-accessible (regulatory) cholesterol pool that remains low while lipid is held in lysosomes and cholesteryl-ester/droplet stores, rather than by a simple increase in successful lipid throughput. All quantities cited are measured abundances; routing, flux and pool sizes are inferred and unmeasured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, quantify the ER/PM-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4 or PFO-D4 probe) together with lysosomal unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid mass (LC-MS, BODIPY). The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows lower accessible cholesterol with higher lysosomal and esterified sterol. If APOE4 instead shows equal or higher accessible cholesterol and unchanged cholesteryl esters, the routing mechanism is falsified and the 'successful high-throughput anabolic state' alternative is favoured.", "Prospective: acute relief of the routing block (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or SOAT1 inhibition with avasimibe) should, within hours and without changing genotype, normalise the SREBP-target transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24) and reduce droplet content selectively in APOE4. Persistence of the sterol-synthesis signature after the ER pool is restored would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective: per-lysosome degradative flux (DQ-BSA or BODIPY-LDL/myelin degradation normalised to LAMP1 area) should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite the higher hydrolase transcripts, i.e. capacity does not scale with load. A clearly higher per-lysosome flux in APOE4 would refute the 'expanded but not sufficient' component while leaving the storage phenotype to be explained.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should preferentially reduce hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1A) in APOE4 and further increase droplet/cholesteryl-ester load; if lysosomal transcripts fall but lipid storage does not increase, the lysosomal arm is a bystander of a separate activation program rather than a load-driven response.", "Prospective, protein-level test of the unresolved spots: targeted immunoblot/PRM for CTSD, CTSB, ATP6V1E1, ANXA1 and TALDO1 should show ANXA1 increased and mature-CTSD redistributed rather than uniformly increased; TALDO1 protein increasing while gene:TALDO1 is -2.32 would indicate a post-transcriptional layer this mechanism does not describe."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters extracellular/intracellular lipoprotein handling in these microglia (gene:APOE +1.24 is measured; particle composition and transfer activity are not measured), so internalised lipid is delivered to the endolysosome in a form that is exported to the ER less efficiently than in APOE3.", "Uptake and opsonic-recognition transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/gene:C1QB/gene:C1QC, gene:ABCA7), consistent with an increased lipid load entering that compartment.", "The ER-accessible sterol sensor therefore reports insufficiency: the represented SREBP-target program is uniformly up (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD), while oxysterol/LXR-type outputs are also up (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28) \u2014 a compartment-discordant signature rather than uniform sterol excess or deficit.", "Sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are re-esterified and stored instead of returning to the regulatory pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:FABP5, gene:FABP3, gene:CIDEB, gene:MGLL, with membrane-lipid genes gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2), sustaining the low ER-accessible pool.", "The retained luminal load accompanies a TFEB/CLEAR-type expansion of the endolysosome: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF, hydrolases gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1A/gene:ATP6V1H/gene:ATP6V1E1/gene:ATP6V0D1/gene:ATP6AP1, membrane/trafficking gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R, gene:RAB7A, gene:SNX3, gene:VPS26A, gene:SLC38A7. Protein spots do not show matching hydrolase increases (lysosome-candidate spots median +0.14; protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:069 -1.38 and protein_spot:067 -1.00 contain CTSD/CTSB/HEXB among other candidates; protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93 contain ATP6V1E1), so expanded transcript-level capacity is not confirmed at the protein level.", "The net state is a DAM-like, lipid-storing microglial phenotype (gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:FTH1, gene:IGF1, gene:TIMP2 all up; homeostatic markers only weakly changed, gene:TGFBR1 -2.19, gene:CSF1 -5.91) with modest inflammatory output (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:IL18) and no coherent UPR or interferon program, predicting a lipidomic shift toward cholesteryl esters, neutral-lipid droplets and lysosomal sphingolipid substrates in APOE4."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route sterol into lysosomal and esterified stores, keeping the ER-accessible pool low and locking in a TFEB/SREBP lipid-handling state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.44526086474910465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27286187193398587, "cosine_similarity": 0.5045434714896747, "direction_accuracy": 0.6003236245954693, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5448122977346278, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.44526086474910465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27286187193398587, "cosine_similarity": 0.5045434714896747, "direction_accuracy": 0.6003236245954693, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5448122977346278, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.02124275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median 1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); we therefore judge pathways only by contrasts internal to the dataset (hydrolase set versus lysosomal-membrane set) rather than by absolute direction.", "Transcript abundance of hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and SREBP targets is treated as a proxy for pathway capacity and for upstream regulatory state; enzyme activity, protein amount, lysosomal pH, and SREBP cleavage were not measured.", "The lysosomal-membrane/acidification gene panel used here is representative of export and acidification capacity even though NPC1, MCOLN1, LAMP2, PSAP and GRN are absent from the supplied rows.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features; no spot is assumed to identify a specific protein, and the spot data are used only as non-decisive corroboration.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein cargo, so uptake-driven lysosomal loading is possible under mock conditions.", "APOE4 versus APOE3 cells were compared at equal maturation state, so the coordinated shift is not simply a differentiation-stage difference."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) transcriptionally amplify the luminal acid-hydrolase arm of the lysosome (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD; TFEB up, gene:TFEB) while the lysosomal membrane/acidification and sterol-carrier arm (gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:CLCN7, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3) stays at the dataset-wide background shift. We hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck is export of hydrolysis products (sterol and sphingoid/glycosphingolipid backbones) out of the lysosome to the ER, so the ER regulatory sterol pool remains functionally low; SREBP-driven synthesis and lipoprotein-uptake transcripts therefore remain high (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACSS2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCARB1) despite an already lipid-loaded cell, and the surplus lipid is diverted into esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL). Measured here are RNA and 2-D protein-spot abundances only; lysosomal lipid content, hydrolase activity, sterol flux, and SREBP proteolytic activation are inferred, not observed, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (sterol-sensing bypass): loading APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with LDL or myelin should suppress SREBP2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7) less in APOE4 than in APOE3, whereas 25-hydroxycholesterol - which acts directly at ER INSIG/SCAP and bypasses lysosomal egress - should suppress those targets equally in both genotypes. Equal suppression by LDL loading, or a selective failure of 25-hydroxycholesterol suppression in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism and point instead to an intrinsic ER-sensor or SREBP-cleavage defect.", "Relieving lysosomal sterol egress with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 overexpression) should, within 24-48 h in APOE4 cells, lower filipin-positive lysosomal free cholesterol, reduce BODIPY/cholesteryl-ester droplet content, and reduce SREBP-target transcripts toward APOE3 levels; unchanged SREBP targets after clearance of lysosomal sterol would falsify the proposed coupling between the lysosomal bottleneck and the lipogenic program.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should convert the APOE4 phenotype from cholesteryl-ester droplets to elevated free cholesterol with increased toxicity while leaving lysosomal glycosphingolipid retention and the SREBP signature largely intact; if SOAT1 inhibition also normalises the SREBP signature, the storage step, not egress, is the bottleneck.", "Pulse-chase of fluorescent or isotope-labelled lipoprotein/myelin cargo should show comparable or faster internalisation but delayed appearance of label in ER/plasma-membrane sterol pools in APOE4, with prolonged lysosomal colocalisation; equal egress kinetics would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Because hydrolase transcripts are elevated, direct enzymatic assays should show GBA, HEXA/B and SMPD1 activities in APOE4 that are equal to or higher than APOE3 per cell once corrected for lysosome number; markedly reduced hydrolase activity would instead support a hydrolysis-capacity (rather than egress) bottleneck, and unaltered lysosomal lipid content in APOE4 would falsify the hypothesis outright.", "Lysosomal acidification measurement (LysoSensor ratiometric pH) should show a modestly higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH in APOE4; an identical or lower pH would remove the acidification component of Step 3 without necessarily removing the egress component."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia elevate lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptor transcripts, most strikingly gene:SCARB1 (99th percentile of the selected DE distribution) with gene:CD36 and gene:ABCA7, which we infer increases delivery of cholesteryl-ester- and sphingolipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome; cargo load itself is not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A TFEB-type luminal catabolic program is induced far above the global up-shift - glycosphingolipid/sphingolipid hydrolases gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA plus gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD (median effect 5.63 vs global median 1.46), with gene:TFEB itself elevated. This is read as a compensatory response to substrate accumulation, not as proof of increased degradative flux.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, internally controlled contrast): The lysosomal membrane/acidification and lipid-carrier arm is NOT co-scaled (gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:CLCN7, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3; median 1.18, Mann-Whitney p = 0.0027 versus the hydrolase set), and the ER/lysosome lipid-transfer transcript gene:OSBPL8 is decreased. We infer a stoichiometric mismatch that limits acidification-dependent hydrolysis and, principally, the exit of liberated sterol and lipid from the lysosomal lumen.", "Step 4 (inferred localisation and signalling): Because sterol egress to the ER is limited, the ER-resident SCAP/INSIG sterol sensor experiences a low regulatory sterol pool even in a lipid-loaded cell, so SREBP processing remains permissive. Consistent with sustained SREBP output, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:ACSS2, gene:LDLR and the SREBP feedback target gene:INSIG1 are all elevated. SREBP cleavage itself was not measured.", "Step 5 (inferred flux, measured RNA): Continued synthesis plus continued uptake exceeds the disposal arm - no efflux transcript in this dataset rises above background (gene:APOE is at the 38th percentile; ABCA1/ABCG1/NPC1 were not measured) - so surplus free sterol and fatty acid are re-esterified through gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 and stored, predicting cholesteryl-ester-rich lipid droplets and lysosomal glycosphingolipid retention as the APOE4 lipid phenotype.", "Step 6 (weak corroboration, ambiguous identity): Two-dimensional protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal proteins move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and two down spots list ATP6V1E1 among candidates (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065). This is consistent with hydrolase proteoform redistribution rather than a proportional protein increase, but each spot has several candidate genes and cannot identify a protein."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid egress, not hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: luminal hydrolase induction without matched membrane/export capacity keeps the ER sterol sensor blind and sustains an SREBP lipogenic-storage program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.149706457925636, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2719509957709282, "cosine_similarity": 0.4672480753114615, "direction_accuracy": 0.24757281553398058, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5866343042071198, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.149706457925636, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2719509957709282, "cosine_similarity": 0.4672480753114615, "direction_accuracy": 0.24757281553398058, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5866343042071198, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.74004975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_030", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential list (all |effect|\u003e1, adjusted p\u003c0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base, kept as reported; genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged. Program directions were judged against the list's 77.1% positive background (1705 up / 507 down), not against 50/50, and the binomial values quoted are descriptive because co-regulated genes are not independent.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the corresponding protein and enzymatic capacity; no oxygen consumption, fatty-acid oxidation rate, lysosomal lipolysis, membrane potential, NADPH/GSH pool or ROS level was measured, so throughput, routing and 'matched capacity' are inferences, not observations.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (KRT/ACTB dominated); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. protein_spot:017 (CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5, +0.77) and protein_spot:077 (includes PRDX2, +1.07) are only compatible with higher antioxidant protein; hydrolase-containing spots are mostly up (052, 053, 055, 057, 012) but 058, 067, 069 are down, so lysosomal expansion is not confirmed at protein level. No ETC/TCA candidate is represented except non-significant SOD2/GLUD1 spots (020, 074, 075), so the mitochondrial arm is untested by protein.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript counts from 10X Flex are assumed to reflect relative mitochondrial transcript content; only 6 of 13 MT genes are represented and two move up, so the mitonuclear mismatch is provisional and its protein/assembly consequence is assumed, not observed.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some measured transcripts may not be microglia-autonomous, and the global positive skew could partly reflect composition, RNA-content or maturity differences between the isogenic lines rather than pathway induction.", "Steps 1-5 are asserted for the measured mock condition; step 6 (reserve limitation) is asserted as a prospective, challenge-revealed property and is not claimed to be an ongoing defect at day 30. Causality is proposed, not established: steady-state RNA cannot order the lysosomal and mitochondrial arms."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change rather than an oxidative-stress lesion: transcripts for lipid/debris uptake receptors, a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase module, SREBP-driven sterol and fatty-acid re-synthesis/esterification, and nuclear-encoded TCA-carrier-import-ETC machinery are jointly elevated far above the 77%-positive background of this selected DE list, while committed glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP) fall despite higher glucose transporters. We propose this represents increased catabolic-to-oxidative throughput with matched mitochondria-facing antioxidant capacity (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, FTH1) - an adaptation in the measured condition, not a demonstrated defect. The one internal mismatch, lower mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) against uniformly higher nuclear subunits, predicts a stoichiometric ceiling on assembled complexes that would limit respiratory and antioxidant reserve and become a functional defect only under added lipid, inflammatory or ETC challenge. No flux, activity, localization or causal direction was measured; all statements about oxidation rate, lysosomal lipolysis, ROS and assembly stoichiometry are inferences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia, extracellular-flux analysis should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption with a lower ECAR/OCR ratio, and higher lysosomal-lipolysis-dependent respiration. If basal and ATP-linked OCR are equal or lower in APOE4, the increased-throughput mechanism is weakened and a failed-compensation or purely transcriptional-drift explanation is favoured.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: blocking lysosomal lipid liberation (lysosomal acid lipase inhibition with lalistat, or v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1, at doses matched between genotypes) should selectively collapse the APOE4 excess in oxygen consumption and reduce the APOE4-elevated mitochondrial antioxidant transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4) toward APOE3 levels. If APOE4 excess respiration and antioxidant transcripts persist unchanged, the lysosome-to-mitochondria substrate link (steps 2-3) is falsified and a cell-autonomous mitochondrial-biogenesis mechanism is favoured.", "Prospective reserve test: FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration and spare capacity, normalised to basal, should be lower in APOE4, and a challenge (myelin or oxLDL loading, LPS, or low-dose rotenone/antimycin) should produce disproportionately higher MitoSOX/mito-roGFP oxidation and lipid-droplet accumulation in APOE4 despite its higher baseline antioxidant transcripts. Equal spare capacity and equal challenge-induced mitoROS would refute step 6.", "Prospective stoichiometry test: blue-native PAGE plus quantitative immunoblot should show a lower ratio of assembled complex I/III/IV/V to nuclear-encoded subunit protein in APOE4, with reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein and unchanged or increased mtDNA copy number. Preserved assembled-complex stoichiometry would remove the proposed ceiling while leaving steps 1-5 intact.", "Prospective regulator test: TFEB knockdown or SREBP-pathway inhibition in APOE4 microglia should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase and sterol-synthesis transcripts and, per the mechanism, secondarily lower the nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC transcript elevation. If the mitochondrial transcript elevation is unaffected by TFEB knockdown, the proposed ordering (steps 2 before 3) is wrong even if both programs remain elevated.", "Negative prediction from rejecting the redox focus: unstimulated APOE4 microglia should not show a canonical NRF2 damage signature (NQO1, HMOX1, GCLM, TXNRD1, SLC7A11 protein or transcript induction), nor elevated peroxisome number/catalase-dependent H2O2 clearance beyond what higher mitochondrial content explains. Clear NRF2 target induction with normal respiration in mock would favour a primary oxidative-stress mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred routing): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipoprotein/debris uptake and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:FCGR1A/1B/3A, gene:ITGAX; gene:APOE +1.24; 13/13 represented members positive, Pbg=0.034), which we infer increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): a TFEB-associated lysosomal module is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:AP5M1, and eight ATP6V subunits; 31/34 positive, Pbg=0.031), increasing hydrolytic and acidification capacity and, we infer, the liberation of fatty acids, sphingoid bases and sterol from internalised cargo. gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:M6PR -1.72 are exceptions.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): liberated carbon is routed both to mitochondria and back into lipid. Mitochondrial carriers, TCA enzymes, import/translation factors and nuclear-encoded ETC subunits rise together (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B/G, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:TUFM, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44; 38/38 represented nuclear OXPHOS subunits positive, Pbg=1e-4), while SREBP outputs rise (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:ACAT2, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:ACSS2; 18/18 positive, Pbg=0.009), consistent with re-esterification/membrane synthesis rather than efflux.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred routing): carbon entry is biased away from glycolytic commitment, since committed steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) while transporters rise (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC16A1); the pentose-phosphate arm is not raised (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred sufficiency): the inferred increase in electron flux is met by higher mitochondria-facing antioxidant transcripts (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:FTH1 +2.53, gene:SELENOW), whereas the canonical NRF2 damage battery is absent from the selected list; we therefore read this as matched capacity in the mock condition rather than an ongoing oxidative-stress response.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, prospective consequence): mtDNA-encoded core subunits move opposite to the nuclear set (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +1.95, gene:MT-ND5 +1.93). If this mismatch is reproduced at the protein level, assembled complex I/III/IV/V output per imported nuclear subunit is capped, so APOE4 microglia are predicted to hold less spare respiratory and antioxidant reserve and to fail selectively when lipid, inflammatory or ETC load is added - a challenge-revealed limitation, not an established defect at day 30 mock."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an expanded lipid-uptake -\u003e lysosomal-hydrolysis -\u003e mitochondrial-oxidation pipeline with matched antioxidant capacity and a mitonuclear stoichiometry ceiling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5679485285972751, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1986459483821604, "cosine_similarity": 0.46195480644584463, "direction_accuracy": 0.7475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5247993527508091, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5679485285972751, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1986459483821604, "cosine_similarity": 0.46195480644584463, "direction_accuracy": 0.7475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5247993527508091, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.411076, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_061", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression export, not an unbiased transcriptome; the source table contains a balanced up/down block (n=1014, exactly 50% up, mean -0.01) and an up-only filtered block (n=1198, all log fold changes \u003e= 1.0). All pathway inference used here is anchored in the balanced block so that the apparent 77% global up-shift is treated as a selection artefact, not a biological global shift.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; relative comparisons between genes are assumed valid, absolute fold-change magnitudes are not interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for hydrolase protein and for lysosomal degradative capacity; activity, luminal pH, localisation and flux were not measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous mixtures; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and none is used as positive evidence for a named hydrolase.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; pseudobulk signals are assumed to derive predominantly from microglia and not from astrocyte carry-over, which the supplied data cannot verify.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values are taken at face value and single-cell effect sizes may be inflated.", "Lipid species, lipid droplets, lysosomal cholesterol, TFEB localisation and mTORC1 phosphorylation are unmeasured inferred pools, not observations."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly at the endolysosomal step: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors and for acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and the TFEB/MITF CLEAR regulators are coordinately higher, while hydrolase-delivery and protein-level lysosomal readouts are not coordinately higher. We hypothesise that lysosomal catabolic throughput for internalised lipid cargo, not cargo uptake, is the limiting step in APOE4, so that the CLEAR transcriptional expansion is a compensatory response to a persistent luminal lipid/glycolipid load that is partly diverted into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol storage. Causality is not established by these data; the measured quantities are RNA and protein-spot abundances only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking lipid-cargo uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or myelin/oxLDL withdrawal), should collapse the APOE4-specific elevation of CLEAR transcripts (TFEB, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1A) to APOE3 levels within 48-72 h. If the CLEAR elevation persists unchanged without exogenous lipid cargo, the cargo-driven bottleneck is wrong and a cargo-independent, cell-autonomous TFEB de-repression should be preferred.", "Pulse-chase with BODIPY-cholesteryl ester, DQ-BSA or fluorescent myelin should show slower luminal substrate clearance and higher steady-state lysosomal lipid (filipin, LipidSpot) per lysosomal volume in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. Equal or faster clearance with no substrate accumulation would weaken the mechanism and instead support genuinely increased degradative capacity.", "Direct enzymatic assay of GBA, HEXA/B and acid sphingomyelinase in APOE4 lysosomal fractions should show a smaller fold increase than the corresponding transcripts, with unchanged or increased glucosylceramide and sphingomyelin substrate levels. Proportional increases in both activity and substrate clearance would falsify the incomplete-compensation step.", "TFEB knockdown or MiT/TFE inhibition should increase lysosomal lipid load and reduce viability or phagocytic capacity substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3 (genotype x knockdown interaction). Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the claim that the CLEAR program is compensatory.", "SOAT1 inhibition should raise free (filipin-positive) lysosomal and ER cholesterol and further increase CLEAR transcripts preferentially in APOE4. No genotype difference in this response would weaken the re-esterification overflow step.", "APOE4 cells should show lower baseline mTORC1 output (p-S6K, p-4E-BP1) and more nuclear TFEB than APOE3 under mock conditions. Unchanged mTORC1 signalling and unchanged TFEB localisation would falsify the proposed regulatory step even if the transcript pattern is reproduced.", "The mitochondrial consequence step predicts higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and higher mitochondrial peroxide reporter signal in APOE4; absence of any oxidative difference would not falsify the lysosomal bottleneck but would remove step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipid and lipoprotein internalisation machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLA2G7; all 11 uptake/esterification genes in the balanced discovery block are positive, Mann-Whitney p=0.016). We infer, but did not measure, an increased flux of lipid-rich cargo into endosomes and lysosomes.", "Step 2 (inferred, not measured): Luminal delivery of cholesterol, sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid exceeds hydrolytic and export throughput, so undegraded lipid substrate accumulates in the endolysosomal lumen. No lipid, lysosomal pH, or hydrolase-activity measurement is supplied, so this pool is inferred only.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Persistent lysosomal substrate load is associated with de-repression of the TFEB/MITF CLEAR program (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:RRAGD +1.44) and coordinated induction of acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1F). Within the balanced (up-and-down) discovery block the lysosome set has mean +2.80 versus a block mean of -0.01 (n=20, permutation p=4e-5). mTORC1 inhibition and TFEB nuclear translocation are inferred, not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA and protein spots): The compensation is incomplete at the post-transcriptional level. Mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase sorting and selected hydrolases move the other way (gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:IDS -1.56, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:LAPTM5 -1.28), and protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases are not coordinately increased (mean +0.17 across 26 such spots, versus +0.35 for all spots; protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up but protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down). Spot identity is ambiguous, so this is non-corroboration rather than refutation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred storage pool): Sterol and fatty-acid overflow is buffered by esterification and neutral-lipid synthesis rather than by efflux (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:MGLL, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, with gene:LDLR still +1.50 and no coordinate ABCA1/ABCG1 signal in the data). Cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets are predicted, not observed.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred consequence): Catabolic product flux and oxidative load rise, matched by higher transcripts for mitochondrial substrate entry and oxidation (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH) and for peroxide handling (gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4). These genes lie mostly in the up-filtered part of the source table, so this step is the weakest link in the chain and is stated as a consequence, not as evidence for the bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise lipid-cargo delivery into a rate-limited endolysosome and mount a compensatory TFEB/MITF CLEAR-network transcriptional program with re-esterification overflow"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19863013698630136, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2199423128344853, "cosine_similarity": 0.45994138309474353, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5802038834951456, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19863013698630136, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2199423128344853, "cosine_similarity": 0.45994138309474353, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5802038834951456, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.210698, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_065", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every |effect| exceeds 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); we therefore treat position relative to that global median, not sign, as the evidence, and assume the shift is a shared normalisation/selection artefact rather than a true genome-wide upregulation.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway capacity; ERAD flux, dislocation rate, secretion rate, ER retention and lipid-droplet content were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level effects are treated as weak, non-identifying evidence only.", "The measured population is a 2D microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30, so genotype effects may partly reflect differences in differentiation state or cell composition rather than cell-intrinsic ER handling.", "APOE4 protein is assumed to transit the same ER glyco-QC route as APOE3; no APOE protein, glycoform or secretion measurement is supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcriptional increase in ER N-glycosylation and lectin/re-glucosylation quality-control components together with ATF6-arm markers, while the SEL1L/DERL1 retrotranslocation-disposal arm sits below the dataset-wide upward shift; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is ER-to-cytosol dislocation of glyco-QC-engaged cargo, so retained secretory cargo is instead cleared through an expanded TFEB-associated endolysosomal hydrolase system, and this rerouting, combined with SREBP1-type lipogenic and sphingolipid-enzyme induction, produces the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SEL1L (or SYVN1/HRD1) re-expression in APOE4 microglia should increase proteasome-dependent clearance of ER-retained glycoprotein cargo and lower both TFEB-target hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) and BODIPY/neutral-lipid area toward APOE3 levels; if SEL1L overexpression restores ERAD flux yet leaves lysosomal hydrolase induction and lipid load unchanged, the dislocation-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Cycloheximide-chase with parallel MG132 versus bafilomycin A1: APOE4 cells should clear newly synthesised ER cargo (including APOE) with greater bafilomycin sensitivity and lesser MG132 sensitivity than APOE3; equal or greater proteasome dependence in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Reducing lectin retention cycles (MLEC or UGGT1 knockdown, or kifunensine) should decrease ER-retained cargo and blunt the lysosomal hydrolase and lipogenic transcript differences in APOE4 but not APOE3; no genotype-selective effect would weaken step 1-2.", "Chaperone-supply control: pharmacological ATF6 activation (e.g. AA147) should not normalise the APOE4 lipid phenotype if the bottleneck is downstream disposal; a large rescue by ATF6 activation would instead support a chaperone/folding-capacity deficit and falsify the disposal-limited framing.", "Direct proteostasis readouts should show ER retention without a canonical acute UPR: elevated Endo-H-sensitive APOE and unchanged or minimally changed HSPA5/GRP94 protein and XBP1 splicing in APOE4; a clear XBP1s/HSPA5 protein induction would indicate a classical UPR rather than the proposed disposal-limited state.", "Rescue at the lipid end should not correct the proteostatic step: DGAT1 inhibition should reduce lipid droplets without reversing the SEL1L/EDEM1/DERL1 transcript deficit or the lysosomal hydrolase induction; reversal of those upstream measures would place lipogenesis, not ERAD, upstream."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mechanism_steps": ["Elevated ER entry/glycoprotein folding load (inferred, not directly measured): transcripts for oligosaccharyltransferase and ER lectin/re-glucosylation quality control are among the highest in the differential list (gene:MLEC 100th percentile, gene:DDOST 97th, gene:STT3A, gene:UGGT1), together with ER redox/co-chaperone helpers (gene:DNAJC10, gene:DNAJB11, gene:ERO1A, gene:QSOX1) and the ER-stress-responsive genes gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:MANF, gene:CRELD2, gene:SERP1.", "Primary bottleneck: the dislocation/disposal arm is not scaled to this load. gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1, gene:SEC62 and gene:PDIA3 all fall in the bottom fifth of the effect distribution and below the dataset-wide positive shift, so we infer that retrotranslocation of glyco-QC-engaged cargo to the cytosolic proteasome is rate limiting in APOE4 cells (a flux inference, not a measured degradation rate).", "Consequence in the ER: cargo remains in retention/re-glucosylation cycles rather than being dislocated, with retrograde retrieval machinery transcriptionally elevated (gene:COPA, gene:COPE, gene:COPB1, gene:RAB1B) and no evidence of increased ER chaperone protein: the only spots whose candidate lists include ER chaperones (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005) are non-significant and trend negative, arguing against a classical chaperone-supply deficit.", "Compensatory routing to the endolysosome: the lysosomal biogenesis/hydrolase program is coordinately high (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:LAMP1) with late-endosome/retromer sorting components (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1), which we interpret as increased lysosomal disposal capacity for cargo that cannot exit the ER through ERAD.", "Lipid handling is coupled to this rerouting: lipid-cargo and lipid-synthesis transcripts are elevated (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:INSIG1, gene:SOAT1) alongside sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid enzymes (gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA2, gene:CERS6), so lysosomal delivery of lipidated cargo plus continued de novo lipogenesis is predicted to expand neutral-lipid and glycosphingolipid pools (lipid pools themselves were not measured here).", "Net state: a chronic, ATF6-biased, disposal-limited proteostatic configuration rather than an acute unfolded-protein response, consistent with the absence of the canonical IRE1-XBP1/HSPA5 module from the supplied differential list."], "title": "ERAD dislocation capacity, not chaperone supply, is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: lectin-based ER glycoprotein QC load is shunted to a TFEB-lysosomal route with lipogenic co-induction"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34349961230292064, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2563200094635003, "cosine_similarity": 0.4570032628968891, "direction_accuracy": 0.4320388349514563, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5848576051779936, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34349961230292064, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2563200094635003, "cosine_similarity": 0.4570032628968891, "direction_accuracy": 0.4320388349514563, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5848576051779936, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.50150775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e=1) with an unspecified logarithm base; 77% are positive, so program coherence was judged against that 77% background and only the mitochondrial TCA/ETC set clears a simple sign test. Genes are not independent, and descriptive coherence is not a formal enrichment result.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, GRN, PSAP, P2RY12, ISGs) are unknown, not unchanged; the missing efflux and lysosomal-lipase members are exactly the ones that would best test the routing claim.", "Transcript abundance is not activity, flux, or localization: no lipid, cholesterol-ester, lysosomal pH, hydrolase-activity, oxygen-consumption or phagocytic-flux measurement is supplied. Increased catabolic transcripts are read as increased capacity/state, not as demonstrated increased flux; the SREBP-arm increase is read as a sensing/routing inference, not as measured ER sterol depletion.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (92 spots, 2-6 candidate genes each, frequent keratin/actin contaminants); no spot identifies a single protein. Spots are used only for compatibility, and lysosomal-candidate spots split 12 up / 10 down, so protein-level hydrolase increase is explicitly not claimed.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture; genotype effects on microglia could be partly indirect through astrocytes or through differences in differentiation state/cell composition, which the supplied data cannot separate.", "Effects expected in the supplied mock condition are the transcriptional state itself; reduced clearance reserve is a challenge-revealed property and is not asserted as an ongoing defect here."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by interferon or NF-kB activation but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and receptor-mediated ingestion, for esterification/storage, for lysosomal hydrolysis and v-ATPase acidification, and for mitochondrial TCA/ETC catabolism are jointly higher, while ER-sterol-repressed SREBP-arm transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, ACAT2, INSIG1) are simultaneously higher alongside sterol-loading-associated targets (APOE, MYLIP, ABCA7, PLTP, SREBF1, SCD). We propose that in APOE4 the ingested/stored lipid is routed into endolysosomal and esterified pools that do not replenish the ER regulatory sterol pool, so uptake and de novo synthesis stay de-repressed while degradative and oxidative capacity is expanded; the state is buffered at steady state (only modest chemokine elevation, no ISG signature), i.e. it is a feed-forward high-throughput lipid-processing state with narrowed reserve, not a demonstrated ongoing degradative bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, quantitative lipid imaging/mass spectrometry (filipin, BODIPY, cholesteryl-ester and sphingolipid species) should show higher lysosome-associated and esterified lipid in APOE4 while an ER-sterol/SREBP-2 reporter remains more active in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or lower stored/lysosomal lipid together with a less active SREBP-2 reporter, the compartmental mis-sensing step is falsified.", "Prospective: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (or forced lysosomal sterol mobilization) in APOE4 microglia should lower the SREBP-arm transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS, HMGCS1) and the uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36) toward APOE3 levels without requiring loss of the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program. Persistence of the SREBP arm after ester depletion would weaken the routing mechanism and favour a genotype-intrinsic transcriptional set point.", "Prospective challenge: pulse-chase of labelled myelin, apoptotic-cell or acetylated-LDL substrate should show APOE4 taking up at least as much label and, at steady state, degrading it at a normal or faster initial rate (consistent with expanded capacity) but retaining a larger undegraded/esterified residue and saturating earlier under repeated loading. If APOE4 instead shows a lower initial degradation rate with no ester accumulation, the mechanism should be replaced by a primary lysosomal-degradation bottleneck model.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program and disproportionately increase lipid retention and stress in APOE4 relative to APOE3 (challenge-revealed loss of reserve). If TFEB knockdown affects both genotypes equally, the adaptive-expansion step is weakened.", "Prospective negative control for the assigned focus: JAK inhibition or IFNAR blockade should not normalise the lipid/lysosomal/mitochondrial transcript differences; if it does, an interferon-driven explanation would be favoured over this mechanism.", "Prospective: two-dimensional gel spots containing cathepsin candidates should resolve, by targeted immunoblot/parallel-reaction-monitoring, into increased mature cathepsin B/D forms in APOE4; if total and mature cathepsin protein and activity are decreased despite higher transcripts, the 'expanded degradative capacity' step is contradicted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4-associated lipid transfer/handling routes internalized and endogenously made lipid preferentially into endolysosomal and neutral-ester/droplet pools rather than into the ER-accessible sterol pool (inferred routing; lipid pools were not measured here).", "Endolysosomal lipid load is accompanied by a TFEB/MITF-type transcriptional expansion of the degradative compartment: hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, all 9 represented subunits positive) and lysosomal transport/biogenesis (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:LAMP1 +1.38).", "Catabolic output is coupled to increased mitochondrial oxidative gene expression: all 16 represented TCA/ETC members are positive (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ACO2 +3.54), together with lipolytic/beta-oxidation transcripts (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:CROT +1.03); this sign coherence exceeds the 77% positive background of the selected list (binomial p~0.016 for TCA/ETC).", "Because sterol is retained in lysosomal and esterified pools (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29), ER sterol sensing remains 'unsatisfied' and the SREBP arm plus uptake receptors stay de-repressed (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30) even though sterol-loading-associated targets are also up (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:PLTP +1.06). The simultaneous activity of both arms is the key signature of compartmental mis-sensing rather than of simple net clearance.", "The same state raises receptor-mediated ingestion/complement transcripts (gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:C1QB +1.13, gene:C1QC +1.17, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:FCGR3A +1.42, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:GPR34 +2.95, gene:MFGE8 +1.49, gene:SIRPA +2.26, gene:CD47 +2.24, gene:VSIG4 +1.32), sustaining substrate influx and closing a feed-forward loop of uptake -\u003e storage -\u003e continued de-repression.", "At steady state in mock the loop is buffered: there is no interferon program (only gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:IFNAR1 +1.41, gene:IRF2 -1.17 represented; no ISGs such as MX1/ISG15/STAT1 in the list) and chemokine elevation is modest and no better than list background (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CXCL2 +1.65, gene:CXCL1 +1.59, gene:CXCL3 +1.56, gene:NLRP3 +1.09) with negative regulators/ligands also down (gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05, gene:RELB -1.30, gene:CCL4 -1.46), so the APOE4 difference is a lipid-routing cell state whose limits would be revealed by a lipid or phagocytic challenge, not an ongoing inflammatory activation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-sequestering, high-catabolic state in which endolysosomal/esterified lipid routing keeps the ER sterol sensor de-repressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17906066536203522, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24392831414980712, "cosine_similarity": 0.45625909770395784, "direction_accuracy": 0.2961165048543689, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5794368932038835, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17906066536203522, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24392831414980712, "cosine_similarity": 0.45625909770395784, "direction_accuracy": 0.2961165048543689, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5794368932038835, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.917696, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_036", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a thresholded selected DE list (|reported log FC| \u003e= 1, adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705 positive vs 507 negative). Programs are judged against that 77% positive background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged. The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2.", "Program membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge) and every queried member found in the data is reported, including sign-discordant ones; the sets were not trimmed to make directions agree.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein and none for flux: uptake, esterification, hydrolase activity, respiration and lipid-pool distribution are inferred, not measured here.", "2D-gel spots carry 2-6 candidate identities; no spot is treated as evidence for an individual protein. Spot changes are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Co-elevation of uptake, esterification and sterol-synthesis transcripts is interpreted as unsatisfied ER sterol sensing (altered routing); this assumes normal SREBP feedback wiring in these cells.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript decrease is assumed to reflect genuine biology rather than probe-panel or ambient-RNA artefacts of the 10X Flex assay; this is the weakest assumption in the chain.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to have introduced a genotype-specific ambient-RNA bias that produces the global positive skew."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia in these data is not interferon/inflammatory activation (no canonical ISG appears in the thresholded DE list) but a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, cholesterol esterification and triglyceride synthesis, sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, and nuclear-encoded mitochondrial import/TCA/OXPHOS machinery are jointly higher in APOE4, while glycolytic committed steps (HK2, PFKP) and mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are lower. The simultaneous elevation of uptake, esterification and SREBP-type synthesis genes is the signature of altered lipid routing (sterol diverted to lysosomal/ester pools away from the ER sensing pool) rather than of sterol excess or of a purely compensatory response to failed degradation; the nuclear-versus-mtDNA transcript mismatch predicts a limitation of oxidative reserve that these mock-condition data cannot show as an ongoing bioenergetic defect.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/lipidomics in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show more neutral-lipid droplets and a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio with elevated nuclear SREBP2, while ER-accessible cholesterol is not increased. If APOE4 instead shows equal or lower ester/droplet content with normal SREBP2 processing, step 2 and the routing mechanism fail.", "Prospective perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g., avasimibe) or SCARB1/LDLR knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce the ester/droplet pool and collapse the sterol-synthesis and lysosomal-hydrolase transcript elevation toward APOE3 levels without needing any anti-inflammatory intervention. Persistence of the SREBP-target and hydrolase elevation after blocking esterification or uptake would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective bioenergetics: extracellular-flux assay should show APOE4 basal OCR equal to or higher than APOE3, higher OCR:ECAR ratio, and greater dependence on fatty-acid oxidation (etomoxir sensitivity), but a disproportionately small FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration and reduced spare capacity, together with lower assembled complex IV/V (BN-PAGE/in-gel activity) relative to the increased nuclear subunit transcripts. Normal spare capacity and complex assembly scaling with nuclear transcripts would refute the mitonuclear-mismatch step (step 6) while leaving steps 1-5 intact.", "Prospective discrimination against the interferon/inflammatory alternative: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR blockade under mock should not normalise the lipid, lysosomal or OXPHOS transcript differences, and ISG protein levels (MX1, IFIT1/3, measured by targeted immunoassay rather than ambiguous 2D spots protein_spot:008/protein_spot:021/protein_spot:026) should not differ between genotypes. Detection of a coherent ISG protein elevation, or normalisation of the lipid programme by JAK inhibition, would overturn the rejection of the interferon focus.", "Prospective challenge test of reserve versus ongoing defect: a myelin-debris or apoptotic-cell phagocytic load should be cleared at least as fast initially by APOE4 microglia but with slower late clearance, greater undigested-cargo accumulation and stronger DDIT3/DELE1-associated stress induction than APOE3. Equal or better sustained clearance would show the state is a successful adaptation with no reserve penalty and would weaken step 7."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases microglial capture of lipoprotein/lipid cargo: scavenger and lipoprotein-receptor transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24), which is inferred to raise delivery of lipid to endolysosomes (uptake flux not measured).", "Internalized sterol is preferentially esterified and stored, and fatty acids channelled to glycerolipid synthesis (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:MGLL +4.00), so the ER regulatory sterol pool is not satisfied and the SREBP-type synthesis program stays active despite increased uptake (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59).", "The increased lysosomal substrate load is accompanied by a TFEB-associated expansion of degradative capacity at the transcript level (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51); hydrolase activity and luminal pH were not measured, and gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:IDS -1.56 are exceptions.", "Catabolic products are routed into mitochondria rather than into glycolytic commitment: mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA and beta-oxidation transcripts rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24) while committed glycolytic kinases fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) even though glucose transporters rise (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73).", "Nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and mitochondrial import machinery expands coordinately (53 of 54 queried members positive; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:CYCS +2.58, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56), consistent with increased oxidative throughput capacity in the mock condition.", "mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts do not co-increase (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; only gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), creating a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch that limits how much of the imported nuclear subunit pool can be assembled into complexes; low-grade mitochondrial stress signalling is compatible with this (gene:DELE1 +4.82, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51, gene:ATF6 +4.04).", "Net predicted phenotype under mock: APOE4 microglia sustain or exceed APOE3 oxidative and degradative output while carrying a larger stored-lipid pool, but with reduced assembly headroom, so a bioenergetic or phagocytic-load challenge should expose reduced spare capacity rather than a baseline deficit."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route internalized lipid into lysosomal and esterified pools, keeping sterol-synthesis 'on' and expanding lysosomal + nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery without matched mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2804526824945538, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.33709332605585446, "cosine_similarity": 0.4518126406021211, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5817572815533981, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2804526824945538, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.33709332605585446, "cosine_similarity": 0.4518126406021211, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5817572815533981, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1746395, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_081", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a two-part workbook layout (source rows 2-509 = a sign-balanced two-column table, 50.5% positive; rows \u003e=520 = an up-only list, 100% positive). Directional coherence is judged only against the balanced block; genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and magnitudes reach +/-15 log units, so only sign and rank are used; no fold-change size is interpreted quantitatively.", "Transcript increases are treated as changes in expressed capacity, not as measured enzyme activity, degradative flux, lysosomal pH, lipid-droplet content or localization; every flux, routing and causal statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each and a global upward shift (mean +0.35 log2); they are used only for compatibility and contradiction, never to confirm an individual protein such as cathepsin D or actin.", "Pathway membership was defined a priori from canonical gene lists (unverified background knowledge) and queried against the data; sign counts are descriptive, genes are not independent, and no formal enrichment test was performed.", "The claim concerns the mock condition only: it asserts increased lipid handling with matched, remodeled capacity, not an ongoing degradative failure. Any insufficiency of reserve is a prediction about a future lipid or myelin challenge, not an observation here.", "The co-culture with astrocytes is assumed to be the lipid source and to be equivalent between genotypes; genotype effects on astrocyte lipid supply were not measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state rather than by inflammatory activation: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:MRC1, gene:CD14, gene:FCGR1A, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6) rise together with a broad CLEAR-type endolysosomal program (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:IGF2R, gene:LAMP1), with lipid re-esterification/storage and biosynthesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MGLL) and SREBP-2 sterol-synthesis targets (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1) simultaneously elevated, while committed glycolytic steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3) and mitochondrial TCA/FAO/OXPHOS transcripts are represented only among upregulated genes (gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA). The coherent interpretation is increased lipid load with matched, remodeled processing capacity and diversion of recovered sterol into esters/storage away from the ER-accessible pool, which keeps SREBP target expression high; the measured data support increased throughput and adaptation, not an established degradative bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective challenge test: pulsing day-30 APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with fluorescent myelin debris, oxLDL or DQ-BSA should show APOE4 cells with equal or greater initial internalization and degradation rate per cell, together with greater BODIPY/filipin-positive neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation, and a lower reserve on repeated loading. If APOE4 cells instead show reduced DQ-BSA dequenching and reduced bulk cathepsin/glycosidase activity already under mock conditions, the adaptation reading is wrong and a degradative bottleneck is the better mechanism.", "Prospective SOAT1 (ACAT1/2) inhibition, e.g. avasimibe, in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester storage, restore ER-accessible sterol and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR) toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the elevated SREBP-2 target signature after effective esterification blockade would falsify the sterol-routing step.", "Prospective TFEB/MITF knockdown or TFEB nuclear-translocation blockade in APOE4 microglia should collapse the coordinated hydrolase and v-ATPase increase (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A) and increase undigested lipid load; if the hydrolase program remains elevated, the CLEAR-coordination step is wrong and the hydrolase increase must be driven independently.", "Prospective metabolic test: etomoxir or CPT1 inhibition should reduce oxygen consumption and ATP more in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia, while 2-deoxyglucose should have a smaller relative effect in APOE4; equal sensitivity to both would falsify the proposed glycolysis-to-lipid-oxidation shift.", "Prospective uptake-execution test: live imaging of bead or myelin engulfment should show that increased receptor transcripts translate into equal or higher internalization events per APOE4 cell despite decreased gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9 and gene:MYO1F and increased gene:ARHGDIA; if internalization rate is instead reduced, the receptor increase reflects compensation for failed uptake and step 1 of the mechanism is inverted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters lipid/lipoprotein presentation and handling in the microglia-astrocyte co-culture, and APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid- and opsonin-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:MRC1, gene:CD14, gene:FCGR1A, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6), which we infer (not measured) raises the flux of lipid-rich cargo delivered to endosomes.", "The increased endolysosomal cargo load engages a CLEAR-type transcriptional response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) that raises transcripts for acid hydrolases, sphingolipid/glycosaminoglycan catabolic enzymes and v-ATPase subunits (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:IGF2R, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2), i.e. an expansion of degradative capacity in the measured condition; the CTSD/CTSB/GNS-containing spots protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:006 and protein_spot:063 are all increased, which is compatible with this expansion although each spot also contains actin, keratin, TPM3, YWHAG, CAPZB or CLIC1 candidates and cannot confirm any single protein.", "Lipid liberated in the endolysosome is preferentially routed into esterification and neutral-lipid storage plus membrane-lipid synthesis rather than back to the ER regulatory sterol pool: gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2, gene:MGLL and gene:SREBF1 are increased while the ER sterol-transport transcript gene:OSBPL8 is decreased (-1.90).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is inferred to stay low despite the higher lipid load, SREBP-2 target transcription remains on (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR), so uptake, de novo synthesis and esterification are elevated at the same time - a signature of altered routing rather than of sterol repletion.", "The lipid-loaded state reconfigures central carbon use: committed glycolytic enzyme transcripts fall (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3) while pyruvate/TCA/fatty-acid-oxidation and OXPHOS transcripts appear among the increased genes (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:DLD, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFB5, gene:COX5B, gene:ATP5F1B), consistent with disposal of lipid-derived carbon by mitochondrial oxidation.", "This lipid-processing state coincides with partial loss of the homeostatic/motile microglial program (gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:TGFBR1 -2.19, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:ARHGDIA +10.61) without a coherent inflammatory or interferon program (NF-kB members split, gene:TRAF4 -7.17, gene:CCL4 -1.46, only 1 of 25 queried interferon genes represented), so the APOE4 difference is a metabolic/degradative state shift rather than cytokine-driven activation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lipid-load cell state: expanded receptor-mediated lipid uptake and CLEAR-type endolysosomal capacity with sterol routed to esterification/storage and a glycolysis-to-oxidative shift"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3395857179780674, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28892638620014616, "cosine_similarity": 0.45153205280174546, "direction_accuracy": 0.42718446601941745, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5587540453074433, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3395857179780674, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28892638620014616, "cosine_similarity": 0.45153205280174546, "direction_accuracy": 0.42718446601941745, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5587540453074433, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.527414, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_025", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (mean +1.39, 77.1% positive), so only background-relative enrichment, not raw counts of up-genes, is interpreted; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and magnitudes are therefore treated as ordinal.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to index, but not to prove, protein amount, enzymatic activity, transport flux or subcellular localization; no lipid, sterol, cholesteryl-ester or lipid-droplet species was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; the identity of the changed protein within a spot is unknown. Only one cross-modality concordance is used descriptively (gene:ANXA1 +4.15 with the ANXA1/TALDO1-containing up spots protein_spot:043-046, where gene:TALDO1 is negative, favouring ANXA1 as the changed species).", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, PLIN2, HSPA5, XBP1) are absent from the supplied rows; their absence is assumed to reflect the selection filter rather than measured invariance.", "Cells were microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; the measured population is assumed to be microglial, and mock-condition differences are assumed to be a maintained steady state rather than a transient.", "APOE4 protein being a poorer lipid acceptor/less efficient lipid transporter than APOE3 is unverified background knowledge, used only as motivation, not as evidence."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly in endolysosomal lipid handling rather than in ER protein-folding stress: transcripts for lipid uptake, endolysosomal transport and lysosomal hydrolysis/acidification are coordinately higher, yet the SREBP-2 sterol-synthesis program and esterification/desaturation genes are also uniformly higher, a combination most simply explained if cholesterol delivered to the endolysosome is not returned to the ER SCAP/INSIG regulatory pool and is instead diverted into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol storage; the ER unfolded-protein response is not the differentiating axis. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treat APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with 25-hydroxycholesterol (acts directly on ER INSIG, bypassing lysosomal egress) versus LDL loading (requires endolysosomal cholesterol egress). The mechanism predicts 25-hydroxycholesterol suppresses HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS and ACAT2 to comparable levels in both genotypes, while LDL loading suppresses them substantially less in APOE4 than APOE3. If LDL suppresses these transcripts equally in both genotypes, or if APOE4 also fails to respond to 25-hydroxycholesterol, the lysosome-to-ER egress bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Cholesterol-imaging test: unesterified cholesterol probes should show greater LAMP1-colocalized sterol and reduced ER-accessible/plasma-membrane-accessible sterol in APOE4; 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin should lower LAMP1-colocalized sterol and reduce SREBP-2 target transcripts selectively in APOE4. Finding equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 while sterol-synthesis transcripts remain elevated would falsify Step 3-4.", "Esterification test: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g., avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl-ester droplets and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts preferentially in APOE4 by returning free cholesterol to the ER. If SOAT1 inhibition leaves the APOE4-versus-APOE3 sterol-gene gap unchanged, Step 6 is weakened.", "Focus-rejection test: chemical chaperones (4-phenylbutyrate or TUDCA) and IRE1/PERK inhibition should not normalize the APOE4 sterol/lipogenic transcript signature, and BiP protein plus XBP1 splicing should not be substantially higher in APOE4. Observing clear XBP1s/BiP elevation together with 4-PBA-dependent normalization of the lipid program would favour the rejected ER-proteostasis mechanism over this one.", "Lysosomal-capacity test: despite higher hydrolase transcripts, measured cathepsin B/D and GBA enzymatic activity per cell should be equal or lower in APOE4 (consistent with protein_spot:058/:067/:069). If hydrolase activity is proportionally increased and lysosomal lipid clearance is faster in APOE4, the compensatory interpretation in Step 2 fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38) and for endolysosomal transport/maturation components (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.87, gene:NPC2 +1.17), which we infer, but did not measure, to increase lipid delivery into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A coordinated lysosomal degradative program is transcriptionally higher (gene:TFEB +2.39; hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSD +2.86; acidification gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30; gene:LAMP1 +1.38). We interpret this as a compensatory biogenesis response to poorly cleared luminal lipid, not as demonstrated hydrolytic capacity: cathepsin-candidate protein spots are not concordantly increased (protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38).", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): Transfer of unesterified cholesterol from the limiting endolysosomal membrane to the ER SCAP/INSIG-sensing pool is rate-limiting in APOE4. The direct carriers (NPC1, STARD3, GRAMD1/Aster family) were not measured, so this step is an inference from downstream readouts, not an observation.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing state): Downstream of that bottleneck the ER behaves as sterol-depleted: every measured SREBP-2 axis and post-squalene synthesis transcript is elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87 - itself an SREBP target, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50; 11/11 positive).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred precursor flux): Cytosolic acetyl-CoA/NADPH supply genes for continued lipogenesis are higher (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ME1 +1.36, gene:NNT +2.88), consistent with sustained anabolic capacity.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred localization of lipid): Excess sterol and fatty acid are routed to neutral-lipid storage and desaturation rather than to a regulatory membrane pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67), with higher gene:APOE +1.24; esterification removes free cholesterol from the sensing pool and closes a self-sustaining loop (inferred, no lipid species were measured).", "Step 7 (explicit rejection of the assigned focus): The ER-proteostasis/UPR alternative is not the differentiator. Canonical UPR/chaperone transcripts are not enriched above the strongly positive background of this selected list (set AUC 0.585, permutation p=0.21), ERAD components trend downward (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:PDIA3 -1.26), and the ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are non-significant (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005, protein_spot:016). Isolated increases (gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:MANF +2.95, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51) are treated as counter-evidence to be explained, not as a coherent UPR."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: an ER regulatory pool that stays 'sterol-blind' sustains SREBP-driven synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21037181996086105, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22928279546254485, "cosine_similarity": 0.4503402404732361, "direction_accuracy": 0.34951456310679613, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5663818770226537, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21037181996086105, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22928279546254485, "cosine_similarity": 0.4503402404732361, "direction_accuracy": 0.34951456310679613, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5663818770226537, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.94702525, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are 'reported log fold change' with an unspecified logarithm base; only sign, rank and set-level comparisons within the RNA table are used, and RNA effects are never numerically compared with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive), not an unbiased transcriptome; all pathway claims are therefore made against the empirical background of these 2212 rows by permutation, and absence of a gene means untested, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the size of the corresponding protein pool; enzyme activity, complex assembly, metabolite pools, respiration and lipid content were not measured and are inferred.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels are assumed to be an informative, though unreliable, proxy for mitochondrial-genome expression; probe-based 10X Flex chemistry and ambient-RNA effects may distort MT- gene capture, and 2/6 MT- rows move the other way.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous proteoform-level measurements; no spot is assumed to identify a unique protein.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of transcript signal may be non-microglial or ambient; the comparison is assumed isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 as stated in the metadata.", "No causal claim is made: the data are a single genotype contrast at one timepoint with unreported replicate structure."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded TCA/electron-transport and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (notably MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2). We hypothesise that this mito-nuclear imbalance is the primary bottleneck: it limits assembly of proton-pumping/proton-using core complexes and therefore coupled ATP output per unit of expanded mitochondrial machinery. Because the committed glycolytic entry steps (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PFKFB2 transcripts) are simultaneously reduced despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts, imported hexose is predicted to be shunted into glycogen (GYS1, UGP2, GAA) rather than compensatory glycolytic ATP production, and mitochondrial carbon that cannot be fully oxidised is predicted to leave as citrate (SLC25A1) for esterification (ACSS2, SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1), producing the APOE4 neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet phenotype. All statements about assembly, flux, ATP output and localisation are inferred, not measured; only RNA effects and ambiguous 2D protein spots were supplied, and no causal test is available in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: forcing the mtDNA-encoded side of the imbalance should be genotype-selective. Low-dose oligomycin (complex V) or antimycin A applied to APOE3 microglia should phenocopy APOE4 - reduced ATP-linked OCR, increased glucose-to-glycogen labelling and increased BODIPY/neutral-lipid area - whereas APOE4 cells should be markedly less further affected (occlusion). If APOE3 responds instead by raising ECAR and HK2 without accumulating lipid, and if APOE4 shows the same incremental sensitivity as APOE3, the proposed bottleneck and its link to lipid storage are weakened.", "Seahorse respirometry: APOE4 microglia should show lower oligomycin-sensitive (ATP-linked) OCR and lower spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass (TOM20/mtDNA-normalised), with unchanged or lower basal/compensatory ECAR despite higher 2-NBDG glucose uptake. Proportionally increased coupled respiration in APOE4 would falsify Step 2.", "Assembly and stoichiometry: BN-PAGE/immunoblot should show reduced fully assembled complex V (and complex I/III) with increased free F1 and c-ring subcomplexes in APOE4, and a reduced MT-CO1 or MT-ATP6 protein to ATP5F1B/NDUFB8 ratio, with mtDNA copy number per nuclear genome not increased in proportion to nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Balanced mito-nuclear protein stoichiometry in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "13C tracing: U-13C-glucose should contribute less label to citrate, glutamate and palmitate in APOE4 than APOE3, with more glucose label in glycogen, while U-13C-glutamine label into citrate/aspartate increases. Increased glucose carbon entry into TCA and lipid in APOE4 would falsify Steps 3-5.", "Citrate-export test: inhibiting SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) or knocking down ACLY should selectively reduce the APOE4 excess of neutral-lipid droplets and of SCD/DGAT1-dependent triacylglycerol without normalising the nuclear OXPHOS transcript program. No reduction of the APOE4 lipid excess would falsify Step 5 while leaving Steps 1-3 intact.", "Hexokinase measurement (currently missing): HK1, the dominant microglial hexokinase, is absent from the supplied rows. If HK1 transcript and total hexokinase activity are increased in APOE4, the 'committed glycolytic entry throttled' element of Step 3 fails and glucose partitioning must be re-explained.", "Rescue test: restoring mitochondrial translation capacity or ATP-synthase assembly (for example partial cybrid-style replacement of mtDNA, or expression of an assembly factor that rescues Fo) should raise ATP-linked OCR and reduce lipid droplet area in APOE4 without reversing the nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase; unchanged lipid content after respiration rescue would weaken the causal ordering."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred program): APOE4 microglia show a coherent up-shift of nuclear-encoded oxidative transcripts above the strongly up-shifted background of this selected DE list - 37/37 nuclear OXPHOS subunits up (set mean +2.81 vs global +1.39, permutation p=7e-4), TCA/pyruvate-entry genes 12/12 up (mean +4.50, p=1e-4; MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, DLD, PDP1, ACO2, IDH3B/G, GOT1) and mitochondrial carriers up (SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A1, SLC25A46).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred bottleneck): mtDNA-encoded transcripts move in the opposite direction as a set (mean -0.82, permutation p_low=0.023; MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33). We infer that core catalytic subunits (complex V subunit a, complex III cytochrome b, complex I ND4, complex IV COII) become limiting relative to the expanded nuclear subunit pool, so newly made nuclear subunits (including complex V c-ring/F1 members ATP5MC3, ATP5ME, ATP5F1B and the c-subunit methyltransferase ANTKMT) accumulate as unassembled or poorly coupled modules; assembly state and respiration were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred partitioning): glucose import capacity rises (SLC2A1 +2.37, SLC2A3 +3.73) while the committed hexokinase/phosphofructokinase step falls (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, HK3 -1.12, PFKFB2 -1.10; committed-step set mean -2.24, permutation p_low=0.004), so glycolysis cannot provide compensatory ATP; the glycogen/hexose-storage set is instead strongly up (GYS1 +6.10, UGP2 +1.86, GAA +9.96, GALE; mean +4.84, p_high=0.005), predicting futile glucose-to-glycogen cycling with lysosomal glycogenolysis.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): mitochondrial carbon input shifts to non-glucose substrates - glutamine/glutamate handling (GLS, SLC1A5, GLUD1, GOT1), malate-aspartate shuttle components (MDH1, SLC25A11, SLC25A13) and lipid oxidation entry (CD36, ACOX1, HADHA) - so acetyl-CoA/citrate supply is predicted to exceed the capacity set by Step 2.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred output): excess mitochondrial carbon is predicted to be exported as citrate (SLC25A1 +4.47) and converted to neutral lipid, consistent with the up-shifted lipogenesis/esterification set (ACSS2, SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, FADS1; mean +2.92, permutation p_high=0.030) and with increased lipid/lipoprotein uptake transcripts (SCARB1 +8.22, CD36, LDLR, APOE, NPC2); ACLY, PLIN2/3 and any lipid-droplet measurement are absent from these data.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred stress state): the energetic consequence predicted by Steps 2-3 is echoed by stress/energy-sensing transcripts (PRKAA1 +2.01, HIF1A +1.98, DDIT3 +2.79, ATF6 +4.04) and by mitochondrial redox/chaperone transcripts (PRDX3, GPX4, HSPA9, NNT); these are correlative markers, not evidence of AMPK or HIF protein activity."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometric imbalance caps coupled respiration in APOE4 microglia while glucose is diverted from glycolysis to glycogen and carbon to lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30362983656515957, "cosine_similarity": 0.44999490024970173, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5752491909385113, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30362983656515957, "cosine_similarity": 0.44999490024970173, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5752491909385113, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.746501, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds ~1 and every adjusted p is \u003c0.05), so absence of a gene means 'not selected', not 'unchanged'. Pathway claims are therefore made only as enrichment relative to the list's own strong global upward shift (mean +1.39, 77% positive), never against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein-spot effects (log2) are not placed on a common scale.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-unique proteoform-level measurements, used only for direction-of-discordance arguments.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding lysosomal and lipogenic protein pools; enzyme activity, SREBP proteolytic cleavage, TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal pH, and all lipid pools were not measured in this dataset and are inferred.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, so genotype rather than treatment is assumed to be the source of the difference; astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts could reflect non-cell-autonomous astrocyte-derived lipid supply.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision and the possibility of clone- or batch-level confounding cannot be assessed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated endolysosomal-lipid remodeling program: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, the SREBP sterol-synthesis regulon, and the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase network are jointly elevated well above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list, whereas canonical type I interferon and chemokine modules are not enriched. We propose that the rate-limiting step is egress of lysosome-derived sterol and sphingolipid to the ER, so that the ER sterol sensor mis-reports a deficit and cells simultaneously import more lipid and build more lysosomes - a self-reinforcing loop rather than an inflammatory/interferon state. Causality is not established by these data; the abundance changes are transcript and protein-spot measurements, and all flux, localization and sensing steps are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Acutely relieving lysosomal sterol trapping in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or an equivalent lysosome-to-ER sterol delivery bypass) for 12-24 h should normalize the SREBP regulon (SREBF2, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS, LDLR, SCD, INSIG1) toward APOE3 levels BEFORE and largely independently of any change in the TFEB/CLEAR hydrolase transcripts, and should reduce filipin-positive lysosomal sterol. If SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated after lysosomal sterol egress is bypassed, the proposed sensing bottleneck is wrong.", "ORDERING TEST: Blocking SREBP output directly (fatostatin, or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should collapse the sterol-synthesis transcripts in both genotypes while leaving the APOE4-selective excess of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB, HEXA, ATP6V1A/H) largely intact. If the lysosomal program collapses in lockstep with SREBP inhibition, the lysosomal arm is downstream of SREBP rather than a parallel compensation, and the stated bottleneck must be relocated.", "CAPACITY TEST: Because APOE4 is proposed to already operate at the limit of lysosomal degradative capacity, sub-maximal v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) or GBA/GAA inhibition should produce a significantly larger increase in undigested neutral-lipid and sphingolipid load, and a larger drop in myelin- or apoptotic-cargo clearance rate, in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "TRANSLATIONAL-MISMATCH TEST: Immunoblotting should show that the large APOE4 increases in cathepsin and v-ATPase transcripts are not matched by proportional increases in mature (processed) cathepsin B/D and assembled V1 subunits, i.e. an elevated pro-form to mature-form ratio. Proportional increases in mature enzyme would remove the mechanistic basis for the protein-spot discordance we invoke in Step 6.", "NEGATIVE-CONTROL / FOCUS-REJECTION TEST: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade under mock conditions should NOT normalize the APOE4 lysosomal-lipid transcriptional signature, and unbiased whole-transcriptome profiling of the same samples should confirm that canonical ISGs (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1-3, OAS1, STAT1) are not differentially expressed. If ruxolitinib abolishes the signature, or if unbiased profiling reveals a coherent ISG elevation that this selected list omitted, the interferon-independence of this hypothesis is falsified.", "SPECIFICITY TEST: The genotype effect should scale with lipid load, so exogenous cholesterol/myelin loading should widen the APOE4-APOE3 gap in SREBP-target and CLEAR-target transcripts, whereas lipid-free medium should shrink it. No dependence on lipid load would argue for a lipid-independent transcriptional difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and scavenger receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28) relative to APOE3. We infer, but did not measure, an increased flux of cholesteryl-ester-rich and phospholipid cargo into the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): The rate-limiting step is hydrolysis and subsequent export of lysosomal luminal sterol/sphingolipid to the ER. No lipid pool, NPC1/NPC2 protein, or transport rate was measured here; the bottleneck is inferred from the transcriptional signature in Steps 3-4 and from the fact that only gene:NPC2 (+1.17) among sterol-export machinery is present in the list.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): Restricted sterol delivery to the ER membrane keeps the SCAP/INSIG sterol sensor in the 'low-sterol' configuration, so the SREBP regulon is transcriptionally up despite a genotype expected to be lipid-loaded: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, plus the SREBP feedback target gene:INSIG1 +1.87. Activity of SREBP cleavage was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Sterol that does reach the cytosol is diverted into esterification and oxysterol side-routes rather than feedback shutdown - gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24 - which further limits the free-sterol signal reaching the ER sensor and closes the loop with Step 3.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A compensatory TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis program is engaged - gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03 - with coordinated elevation of luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17), acidification machinery (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70) and delivery/membrane components (gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:LAMP1 +1.38). Nuclear TFEB localization and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 6 (measured protein spots, ambiguous): The transcriptional expansion is not clearly matched at the protein-spot level. Spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins go in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58 up; protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 down) and both spots containing ATP6V1E1 fall (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93). Because each spot has several candidate genes, these are not uniquely identified proteins; we interpret them only as evidence that increased hydrolase mRNA does not translate into a uniform increase in mature lysosomal protein, consistent with an unresolved degradative bottleneck rather than restored capacity.", "Step 7 (negative arm): The same data do not support an interferon/inflammatory driver. Not one of 36 canonical type I interferon effectors (ISG15, MX1/2, OAS1-3, IFIT1-3, IFI6/27/44, IFITM1-3, RSAD2, BST2, USP18, XAF1, STAT1/2, IRF3/7/9, CMPK2, HERC5, DDX58, IFIH1, EIF2AK2, PARP9, DTX3L and others) appears in the 2212-gene DE list, and the chemokine module mean (+0.60) sits below the global mean (+1.39). We therefore treat inflammatory signaling as a downstream/secondary consequence, not the bottleneck."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol/lipid egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: ER sterol under-sensing drives a coupled SREBP-uptake and TFEB-lysosome program, not interferon or NF-kB activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22492858579519526, "cosine_similarity": 0.4492756289770247, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936925566343042, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22492858579519526, "cosine_similarity": 0.4492756289770247, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936925566343042, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.67422825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_035", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (all 2212 rows have adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e1) with an unspecified logarithm base and a 77% upward bias; set-level contrasts are therefore made against this selected list, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; assignment of a spot to a lysosomal hydrolase or v-ATPase subunit is provisional and the spot-level contrast is treated as an aggregate capacity readout, not as identified-protein quantification.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the size of the lysosomal biogenesis program; lysosomal pH, hydrolase maturation state, degradative flux, lipid content and MiT/TFE localisation were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred.", "Positive effects mean higher in APOE4 than APOE3, the comparison is isogenic, and the astrocyte co-culture partner does not contribute a confounding compositional shift to the microglial measurement.", "The strongly negative values of housekeeping-type transcripts (e.g. ACTB) alongside spot-level increases indicate possible normalisation or compositional effects; the mechanism assumes the set-level contrasts survive this, which is untested here.", "A single timepoint (day 30) and unreported replicate number mean steady-state accumulation, not kinetics, is being modelled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) up-regulate a coordinated MiT/TFE-type lysosomal transcript program together with sterol/fatty-acid anabolic transcripts, but the measured lysosomal hydrolase- and v-ATPase-containing protein spots are not correspondingly increased; we hypothesise that per-lysosome degradative capacity, not lipid supply, is the rate-limiting step, so incoming and endogenously made lipid is shunted into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores and undigested lysosomal sphingolipid substrate rather than being cleared. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics on the same APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show higher cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols plus higher lysosomal-hydrolase substrates (sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, GM2/GM3) in APOE4, with an increased esterified:free cholesterol ratio; unchanged or lower cholesteryl esters and unchanged sphingolipid substrates would weaken the mechanism.", "Functional lysosome assays should show that per-lysosome degradative capacity does not scale with transcript induction: DQ-BSA dequenching and Magic-Red cathepsin B/L activity per LAMP1 area, and lumenal acidification (LysoSensor/pHrodo ratio), should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite higher CTSB/CTSD/ATP6V transcripts. Proportionally higher cathepsin activity and normal or lower pH in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck step.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring degradative capacity (TFEB overexpression, acidic-nanoparticle or v-ATPase-supporting re-acidification) should lower both stored cholesteryl esters and undigested sphingolipid substrate in APOE4, whereas SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl esters and droplets while leaving sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide accumulation intact. If SOAT1 or SREBP/SCD inhibition normalises the sphingolipid substrates as well, the bottleneck is anabolic input rather than lysosomal clearance and this hypothesis is rejected.", "Immunoblot of CTSB/CTSD should show a reduced mature:pro form ratio, and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein no higher in APOE4 than APOE3, despite elevated transcripts; a coordinated increase in mature hydrolase protein would weaken the RNA-protein discordance step.", "Because the mechanism places inflammation downstream, blocking NF-kB/NLRP3 signalling should not correct the APOE4 lipid accumulation; if it does, the causal ordering proposed here is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with a coherent lysosome/CLEAR-like transcript program (measured RNA: TFEB, MITF, GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, SMPD1, RAB7A, multiple ATP6V/ATP6AP subunits; set mean ~+3.1 vs list background ~+1.4, Mann-Whitney p=0.0026). MiT/TFE nuclear localisation and transcription-factor activity are inferred, not measured.", "In parallel, lipid-anabolic and lipid-uptake transcripts rise (SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, LDLR, SCARB1, CD36), increasing the inferred flux of sterol and fatty-acyl substrate reaching the endolysosome and cytosolic droplet compartments; no lipid or flux measurement is supplied.", "The proteomic layer does not show the matching increase: protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases or v-ATPase subunits average +0.11 log2 versus +0.44 for all other spots, and several such spots are significantly decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), while total-spot bias is upward. Spot identity is ambiguous, so this is a capacity signal, not a proven per-protein decrease.", "Consequently, acidification-dependent lumenal hydrolysis (cholesteryl-ester, sphingomyelin, glycosphingolipid turnover) is inferred to lag behind substrate delivery, i.e. the bottleneck is catabolic capacity per lysosome rather than lysosome number or transcriptional drive.", "Un-hydrolysed substrate is retained in the endolysosome while cytosolic sterol/acyl-CoA is esterified through SOAT1 and DGAT1/AGPAT2, producing a neutral-lipid-storage phenotype with APOE and NPC2 transcript elevation.", "Persistent undigested lipid sustains the lysosomal transcript program (feed-forward) and an inflammatory tone (CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3, IL18, TREM2 transcripts), which is a downstream consequence in this model rather than the initiating lesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a lysosomal transcript program without matching hydrolase/v-ATPase protein, creating a lysosomal catabolic bottleneck that diverts lipid into esterified and undigested pools"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13209393346379647, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2533314824471912, "cosine_similarity": 0.4481959948839136, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5979546925566344, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13209393346379647, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2533314824471912, "cosine_similarity": 0.4481959948839136, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5979546925566344, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.811157, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_061", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance of receptors, hydrolases and synthesis enzymes is used as a proxy for the corresponding protein amounts and for pathway demand; no protein, enzyme-activity, sterol, lipid-droplet or localization measurement of these pools is present in the supplied data, so influx, hydrolytic flux, lysosome-to-ER egress and ER sterol sensing are inferred, not observed.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source workbook and is preserved as reported; only sign and relative ordering are used, and effect magnitudes are not converted to fold changes.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression table, not an unbiased transcriptome. The table is built from two parallel ranked columns (506 rows carrying one up and one down gene, 1200 further rows that are essentially all up), giving a fixed 1705:507 up:down composition; enrichment was therefore tested against that 77% up baseline rather than treating the apparent global positive shift as biology.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and are not treated as identified proteins; they are used neither as support nor as refutation of any single protein's abundance.", "Key nodes of the proposed mechanism (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, STARD3, CPT1A) are absent from the supplied rows, so the egress and storage steps rest on the surrounding genes rather than on the canonical effectors.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply is assumed to be equal for both genotypes, and no causal test of genotype-to-lipid direction is available in these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes express a coordinated scavenger/efferocytic uptake program (21/21 measured receptor transcripts higher than APOE3, including SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, MRC1, CD163, COLEC12, STAB1, MERTK, TREM2, C1QA/B) together with an expanded lysosomal-biogenesis program (TFEB, v-ATPase subunits, LAMP1, RAB7A, and lipid-directed hydrolases GBA, SMPD1, GAA, HEXA/HEXB, CTSB/CTSD). The primary bottleneck we propose is the throughput of lysosomal processing and lysosome-to-ER egress of the scavenged sterol/lipid load, not the influx step: despite the elevated uptake program, every measured SREBP-pathway transcript (SREBF2, SREBF1 and 9 downstream sterol/fatty-acid synthesis genes) is also elevated, the signature expected if the ER regulatory sterol pool is still sensed as insufficient. We predict that the excess lipid that cannot be returned to the ER or exported is esterified by up-regulated SOAT1 and DGAT1 and stored, producing a higher cytoplasmic neutral-lipid-droplet burden and a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio in APOE4 than in APOE3 microglia. All statements about flux, localization, sensing and causal direction are inferences from transcript abundance; no lipid, sterol, enzyme-activity or localization measurement is present in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe or CI-976) in APOE4 microglia should reduce the APOE4-minus-APOE3 excess in neutral-lipid-droplet area (BODIPY/LipidTOX) by at least half and lower the cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio measured by mass spectrometry, while the free-cholesterol pool rises. If SOAT1 inhibition leaves the droplet excess unchanged, step 4 (esterification-dependent diversion) is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation for the bottleneck: mobilizing lysosomal sterol with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, both reduce droplet burden and repress the sterol-synthesis transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24). If cyclodextrin reduces droplets but leaves the synthesis program elevated, or represses it equally in both genotypes, the proposed lysosome-to-ER egress bottleneck is misplaced and a simple lipid-overload or synthesis-driven model is favoured.", "Influx test: knockdown of SCARB1 (or combined SCARB1/CD36 blockade), or culture in lipoprotein-deficient medium without astrocyte-conditioned lipid, should collapse the APOE4\u003eAPOE3 droplet difference. Persistence of the difference under lipid-free conditions would show the phenotype is uptake-independent and would weaken step 1.", "Sensing test: acute cholesterol loading (LDL or cholesterol/cyclodextrin complexes) should repress SREBP2 target transcripts less in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal repression in both genotypes weakens step 3.", "Direct state check: APOE4 microglia should show higher filipin-positive intralysosomal cholesterol co-localizing with LAMP1 and higher LipidTOX droplet area than APOE3 at day 30 mock, with hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXB) per cell not lower than APOE3. Finding equal or lower droplet burden in APOE4, or lower lysosomal hydrolase protein and activity with no sterol retention, would falsify the mechanism as a whole.", "Alternative-mechanism discriminator: if the lipid difference is abolished by restoring mitochondrial translation or ETC stoichiometry (for example by correcting the mtDNA-encoded versus nuclear-encoded imbalance suggested by gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 being lower while 38/38 nuclear OXPHOS transcripts are higher) without any change in scavenger-receptor or SREBP transcripts, the mitochondrial-imbalance model should replace this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for scavenger, lipoprotein and efferocytic receptors and their ligands (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:PLA2G7); inferred consequence is increased receptor-mediated influx of lipoprotein and membrane/debris lipid into the endolysosome (flux not measured).", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred demand): a TFEB-type lysosomal program is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B and ten v-ATPase subunits including gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), together with lipid-directed hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:NPC2). We read this as compensatory biogenesis driven by increased degradative demand rather than as proof of increased degradative capacity.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): hydrolytic processing and lysosome-to-ER egress of liberated sterol do not keep pace with influx, so the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool stays low. The transcriptional read-out consistent with this is that the sterol-feedback program is not repressed: gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1 and gene:LDLR are all higher in APOE4, as are gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1 and gene:LPCAT1. Simultaneous elevation of uptake and de novo synthesis is the discriminating feature; a cell with intact sterol delivery to the ER should repress this arm under a high lipid load.", "Step 4 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): the resulting excess free sterol and fatty acid are channelled into esterification and storage, indicated by higher gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 and by higher lipid-droplet/lysosome-stress-associated transcripts gene:GPNMB and gene:VAT1.", "Step 5 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred metabolic support): nuclear-encoded oxidative phosphorylation and TCA transcripts are uniformly higher (38/38 measured, e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2) while gene:HK2 is lower, suggesting a shift away from glycolysis toward mitochondrial oxidation; no coherent increase in fatty-acid-oxidation transcripts is present, so we do not invoke increased droplet consumption.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype): the net effect is a foamy, lipid-laden APOE4 microglial state with greater cytoplasmic neutral-lipid-droplet area and a raised cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio relative to isogenic APOE3 at day 30, mock."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-shift scavenger-receptor lipid influx faster than lysosomal sterol egress, diverting cholesterol into SOAT1/DGAT1 neutral-lipid droplets"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1350293542074364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2635650492004676, "cosine_similarity": 0.4476427725535563, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5925275080906149, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1350293542074364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2635650492004676, "cosine_similarity": 0.4476427725535563, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5925275080906149, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1280055, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_046", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive with a median of +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base, so only within-list relative comparisons (set rank versus the same list background) are interpreted, never absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for pathway engagement only; enzyme activity, SREBP or TFEB proteolytic activation and nuclear localisation, lysosomal pH, lipid pools, and any flux are inferred and were not measured.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes; spot-level changes are treated as consistent-or-not with the transcript model, never as identified protein quantities.", "Absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, NPC1, HMGCR and SQLE from the list is treated as missing data (not selected), not as evidence that they are unchanged.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the extreme per-gene effect sizes (up to +15.5) may reflect few replicates, normalisation or composition effects; the argument rests on set-level coherence rather than individual large values.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences could arise from altered microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange or from residual astrocyte signal rather than from microglia-intrinsic APOE4 effects."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant isogenic APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in these iPSC-derived microglia is a coordinated lipid-handling state: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, sterol and fatty-acid synthesis, and neutral-lipid esterification are jointly elevated together with TFEB and a broad lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program, whereas inflammatory and interferon-stimulated transcripts are not elevated above the strong global positive shift of this selected differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is lysosomal hydrolytic and sterol-export capacity for delivered lipid, so that continued influx and unsuppressed de novo synthesis are routed into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol storage and undegraded lysosomal lipid, and that the lysosomal transcriptional program is a compensatory response to that load rather than evidence of increased degradative flux. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pulse-chase loading of APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with fluorescent myelin or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester should show slower clearance and greater residual lysosomal lipid in APOE4 despite its higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears the substrate as fast as or faster than APOE3, the lysosomal-capacity bottleneck is falsified and a purely synthesis-driven storage model is favoured.", "Inhibiting SREBP maturation (fatostatin or an SCAP/S1P inhibitor) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area and cholesteryl-ester content in APOE4 towards APOE3 while leaving the TFEB/CLEAR transcript program only partially corrected; no reduction in APOE4 neutral lipid would weaken step 2.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free sterol and increase, not decrease, lysosomal membrane stress markers; if it lowers total lysosomal lipid load instead, the esterification-routing step is wrong.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should further increase lipid-laden lysosome area and reduce substrate clearance, and TFEB activation should reduce them. If TFEB knockdown leaves the APOE4 lipid load unchanged, the CLEAR program is not compensatory as claimed.", "Rejection test for the assigned inflammatory/interferon focus: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IKK/NF-kB inhibition under mock conditions should not normalise the APOE4 lipid-storage or lysosomal-morphology phenotype, and a qPCR ISG panel (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1) should show no coordinated APOE4 elevation. Coordinated ISG elevation, or normalisation of the lipid phenotype by JAK inhibition, would overturn this hypothesis in favour of an interferon-driven mechanism.", "Cathepsin B/D enzymatic activity per lysosome (activity probe normalised to LAMP1 area) should not rise in proportion to the transcript increases; a proportional activity rise would weaken the bottleneck claim while leaving the lipid-influx steps intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and carriage (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28). Inferred, not measured: a higher rate of lipid delivery into the endolysosomal system; no lipid, flux or localisation measurement is present in this dataset.", "Measured: sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06). Inferred: SREBP-type biosynthetic output is not shut off despite the inferred lipid influx, i.e. sterol-sensing feedback is set at an inappropriately permissive level; SREBP proteolytic activation and sterol pools were not measured.", "Measured: esterification/glycerolipid enzymes are higher (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25) alongside neutral-lipid turnover (gene:MGLL +4.00). Inferred: incoming and newly synthesised sterol and fatty acid are preferentially esterified into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores rather than exported; ABCA1/ABCG1/LIPA/NPC1 transcripts are absent from this selected list and were therefore not assessed.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred): per-organelle lysosomal hydrolytic and sterol-export capacity for the delivered lipid load is limiting, so undegraded lipid accumulates in enlarged, lipid-laden endolysosomes. This is an inference about flux, not an observation; only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "Measured compensatory response: TFEB and a broad CLEAR-type lysosomal program are coordinately raised (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.20, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:NPC2 +1.17); the 27-gene lysosomal set sits at rank z = +2.98 and the 15 hydrolases average +3.67 versus a +1.39 list-wide mean (permutation p = 4e-4). Inferred: lysosomal biogenesis is up-regulated to meet, but does not resolve, the lipid load.", "Measured protein-spot level: spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins change in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 up; protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 down). Inferred: a redistribution among processed cathepsin forms rather than a uniform increase in hydrolase protein, consistent with capacity that does not scale with the transcriptional program; spots are not uniquely identified proteins.", "Measured negative result for the assigned focus: interferon-related (gene:IFI27L2, gene:IFI16, gene:IRF5, gene:IRF8, gene:TMEM173, gene:IFNAR1, gene:IRF2) and inflammatory/NF-kB transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:TLR6, gene:NFKBIZ, gene:MYD88, gene:NLRP3, gene:TNFAIP3, gene:GSDMD, gene:CCL4) sit at the list background (rank z = -0.34 and -0.31). Inferred: an interferon- or NF-kB-driven program is not the primary APOE4 differentiator here; any cytokine transcript elevation is secondary to, or independent of, the lipid state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain lipid influx plus SREBP-type lipogenesis and esterification while lysosomal lipid-clearance capacity remains limiting, driving a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR transcriptional expansion rather than an interferon or inflammatory program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13992172211350293, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23602258674732457, "cosine_similarity": 0.44369838168381237, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5922653721682848, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13992172211350293, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23602258674732457, "cosine_similarity": 0.44369838168381237, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5922653721682848, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.70859675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_013", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) that is 77% positive (1705/507) with median effect +1.46 on an unspecified log base; program coherence is judged against that skewed background, and absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Elevated transcripts are assumed to raise the corresponding protein pools and, in aggregate, endolysosomal degradative capacity; no hydrolase activity, luminal pH, lysosome volume, cholesterol-egress rate, lipid-droplet or cholesteryl-ester pool was measured in this dataset, so capacity, flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "Protein 2D-gel spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each; all candidates are retained and no spot is treated as confirmation of an individual protein. Spots containing lysosomal candidates split 15 positive/9 negative, close to the all-spot ratio (64/24), so the proteomic layer is treated as compatible-but-not-confirmatory.", "APOE4-driven change in lipid cargo routing is the assumed upstream trigger; an equally transcript-compatible trigger (e.g. altered mTORC1/TFEB set-point, or astrocyte-derived lipid supply differing by genotype in this co-culture) cannot be excluded from these data.", "The mock condition is interpreted as a compensated steady state; any degradative shortfall is a predicted challenge-revealed reduction of reserve, not an observed ongoing defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change in lipid cargo handling, not by inflammation: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are coherently and strongly elevated together with the MiT/TFEB module (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:RRAGD), while sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, uptake and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts are uniformly elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD) and the entire represented OXPHOS/mitochondrial-carrier set is elevated (38/38 positive). The most parsimonious reading is expanded degradative capacity matched to increased lipid cargo flux, with sterol re-routed into esterification/storage so the ER sterol sensor is not satisfied; this is an adaptation that is compensated in the measured mock condition and predicts reduced spare capacity under a future lipid challenge, not a demonstrated ongoing lysosomal bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE CHALLENGE: loading isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia with a defined lipid cargo (myelin debris, AcLDL or fluorogenic-substrate-labelled apoptotic cells) should show APOE4 with higher baseline lysosome volume/hydrolase activity (e.g. BODIPY-pepstatin, DQ-BSA, Magic Red) but a smaller incremental rise in degradation rate and faster accumulation of cholesteryl ester/lipid droplets. If APOE4 instead matches or exceeds APOE3 in incremental degradative flux with no differential ester/droplet accumulation, the 'sterol re-routed to storage, reserve consumed' core is weakened.", "PROSPECTIVE: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or restoration of lysosomal sterol export should selectively lower SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24) and CLEAR-network transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. If SREBP targets remain elevated after esterification blockade, step 3-4 (sterol routed away from the ER sensing pool) fails.", "PROSPECTIVE: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown or MiT-family inhibition should collapse the genotype difference in hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C) without abolishing the OXPHOS difference. Persistence of the hydrolase/v-ATPase difference would refute MiT/TFEB coordination as the organising step.", "PROSPECTIVE: direct measurement of lysosomal pH and v-ATPase-dependent acidification. Equal or more acidic lysosomes in APOE4 supports expanded working capacity; if APOE4 lysosomes are significantly less acidic despite elevated v-ATPase transcripts (consistent with the two significantly decreased ATP6V1E1-containing spots protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065), the mechanism must be re-cast as failed compensation with a genuine ongoing acidification defect.", "PROSPECTIVE: inhibiting mitochondrial ATP synthesis (oligomycin) or citrate export (CTPI-2/SLC25A1 block) should preferentially reduce APOE4 degradative throughput and lipogenic transcript output; equal sensitivity in both genotypes would argue the OXPHOS elevation is an independent state feature rather than demand-coupled support."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein alters lipoprotein-mediated lipid handling in microglia so that more sterol/sphingolipid/glycolipid cargo transits and dwells in the endolysosomal system (inferred routing change; cargo load, lipid pools and flux were NOT measured here).", "Elevated luminal cargo engages a MiT/TFEB-type transcriptional response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:RRAGD +1.44, gene:LAMTOR5 +1.69, gene:DEPDC5 +1.34), which raises CLEAR-network transcripts: hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:CTSH +1.54, gene:SGSH +1.32; 13/15 represented hydrolases positive, median +2.86 versus +1.46 for the selected list) and acidification/transport machinery (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.29, gene:ATP6AP2 +1.18, gene:ATP6V0D2 +1.12, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CLN3 +1.17); this is expanded transcriptional capacity, not measured hydrolase activity or measured acidification.", "Sterol liberated by this degradative route is preferentially esterified and stored rather than delivered to the ER sensing pool or exported (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CH25H +1.62; ABCA1/ABCG1/PLIN2/LIPA/NPC1 are absent from the supplied list and therefore unknown, not unchanged).", "Because the ER sterol sensor is not satisfied, the SREBP arm stays on: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34 (14/14 represented members positive), creating a feed-forward loop that returns further lipid to the endolysosomal/storage compartments.", "Running proton pumping, biosynthesis and translation simultaneously raises ATP, acetyl-CoA and reductant demand, matched by coordinated mitochondrial transcript elevation: OXPHOS 38/38 positive (median +2.65; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36) with TCA/carrier genes gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, and NADPH/redox support gene:NNT +2.88, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX2 +4.41.", "Net measured state at mock is therefore a matched, apparently successful adaptation (degradative, biosynthetic and bioenergetic capacity all raised; the cytokine set sits at selected-list background: 9 positive/4 negative, median +1.46, gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09 versus gene:CCL23 -2.51, gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05), so the predicted deficit is a reduced spare capacity that should appear only when extra lipid/particulate cargo is imposed."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a MiT/TFEB-coordinated high-throughput endolysosomal lipid-processing state in which liberated sterol is routed to esterification/storage rather than to the ER sensing pool, keeping SREBP synthesis on and raising mitochondrial ATP/acetyl-CoA demand"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4661872761510911, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.232377854420486, "cosine_similarity": 0.4428786334612609, "direction_accuracy": 0.580906148867314, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5218187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4661872761510911, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.232377854420486, "cosine_similarity": 0.4428786334612609, "direction_accuracy": 0.580906148867314, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5218187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.38247, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_083", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of the 2212 supplied rows are positive with median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base, so only set-level shifts above that background (assessed by Mann-Whitney against all supplied rows) are treated as informative.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the corresponding protein and enzymatic activity; no hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number, cargo flux, TFEB localisation or lipid-pool measurement is supplied, so all activity, flux, localisation and directional statements are inferences.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots containing a lysosomal-hydrolase candidate are not distinguishable from all spots (median +0.48 vs +0.48, Mann-Whitney p=0.63), so the protein layer neither supports nor refutes the mechanism and is excluded from the supporting evidence.", "The measured cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on cargo supply may be partly astrocyte-derived and non-cell-autonomous.", "Replicate number is not supplied and effect magnitudes are extreme (up to +15.5), so per-gene magnitudes are treated as ordinal, not quantitative.", "Only the mock condition and one timepoint (day 30) are available; steady-state differences are assumed rather than a demonstrated time course."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an increased flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system whose terminal acid-hydrolase-dependent catabolism is the rate-limiting step; the cells respond with a selective TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR transcriptional program (luminal glycosidases/sphingolipid hydrolases, hydrolase maturation and targeting machinery, and V-ATPase subunits) while routing liberated lipid back into esterification and de novo lipogenesis, so degradative capacity per unit cargo, not hydrolase gene dosage, remains limiting. Causality is not established by these data; the primary bottleneck (per-lysosome cargo throughput) is inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo-clearance assay: pulse-chase APOE4 and isogenic APOE3 microglia with a defined lipid-rich cargo (fluorescently labelled myelin debris or DiI/BODIPY-cholesterol lipoprotein) and image dequenching per LAMP1-positive compartment. The mechanism predicts equal or faster internalisation but slower per-lysosome cargo clearance and longer residence of undegraded lipid in APOE4 despite equal or higher measured hydrolase content. Equal or faster per-lysosome clearance kinetics in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Enzyme/organelle decoupling test: measure GBA, HEXA/HEXB, CTSB and CTSD activities and lysosomal pH. Prediction: activities equal or higher and pH equal or lower (not less acidic) in APOE4, with clearance still impaired. If activities or acidification are markedly reduced in APOE4, the bottleneck relocates from cargo throughput to hydrolase maturation or acidification and step 3 as written is falsified.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown (or constitutive mTORC1 activation) should selectively collapse the hydrolase and V-ATPase transcript excess in APOE4 and exacerbate lipid accumulation under cargo challenge. Persistence of the hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript excess after TFEB knockdown would falsify the CLEAR attribution in step 3.", "Storage-arm test: DGAT1 or SOAT1 inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid droplet load and, if egress is intact, lower SREBF1/SCD transcripts more in APOE4 than APOE3. Absence of a genotype-selective response would weaken step 5.", "Selectivity test: a protein cargo (DQ-BSA or labelled dead-cell protein) should be degraded relatively worse than a glycosphingolipid cargo in APOE4, matching the CTSS-down / glycosidase-up split. Uniformly impaired or uniformly intact degradation of both cargo classes would falsify step 4.", "Rescue test: raising lysosomal capacity (TFEB overexpression or acid-hydrolase supplementation such as recombinant glucocerebrosidase/sphingomyelinase) should normalise APOE4 cargo clearance without changing uptake-receptor transcripts. Normalised clearance accompanied by loss of the uptake-receptor difference would instead point to an uptake-driven rather than capacity-driven mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo receptors and opsonin machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14). Increased internalisation flux and cargo delivery to endosomes is inferred from these abundances; uptake rate itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred trafficking): transcripts for endosome maturation and cargo delivery are elevated (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:WDR91 +3.50, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:SUMF1 +2.01), consistent with more cargo reaching, and more hydrolase being targeted to, late endosomes/lysosomes; localisation and mannose-6-phosphate flux were not measured (gene:M6PR is decreased, -1.72).", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred transcriptional activity): a CLEAR-like program is engaged - gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:RRAGD +1.44 (itself a TFEB target) - accompanied by coordinate induction of luminal hydrolases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:NPC2 +1.17), V-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.19, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68) and lysosomal membrane/efflux components (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:GPNMB +1.11). TFEB nuclear localisation, hydrolase protein maturation and luminal pH were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, selectivity): the program is substrate-class selective rather than a uniform lysosomal expansion - the glycosidase/sphingolipid-hydrolase arm is shifted above the already positive global background (median +2.09 vs global +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.030) while the dominant microglial endopeptidase and a sulfatase are strongly reduced (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:IDS -1.56). This predicts a lipid/glycoconjugate-biased, protein-degradation-poor lysosome.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): liberated lipid is inferred to be re-esterified and supplemented by de novo synthesis rather than exported, sustaining the load (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LSS +2.27). Sterol efflux transporters ABCA1/ABCG1, LIPA and NPC1 are absent from the supplied rows, so lysosomal lipid egress is unmeasured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): spare capacity is further reduced because an additional autophagic input competes for the same lysosomes while a fusion component is decreased (gene:STX17 -2.06, with gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:ATG9A +1.68), so cargo residence time per lysosome is predicted to lengthen even though hydrolase transcripts are high."], "title": "Lipid-cargo load exceeds endolysosomal degradative throughput in APOE4 microglia, driving a compensatory TFEB/MITF CLEAR program with substrate re-esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25579987760535644, "cosine_similarity": 0.4427122545968558, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5877669902912621, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25579987760535644, "cosine_similarity": 0.4427122545968558, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5877669902912621, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.95004425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 11}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_085", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Reported RNA effects use an unspecified logarithm base and come from a selected differential-expression list with a |effect| \u003e= 1 floor and a strong global positive median (+1.46); all module claims here are made relative to that shifted background, not relative to zero.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance for the acid hydrolase module; no lysosomal enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, cargo-clearance rate or lipid species was measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a specific measurement of a named hydrolase or chaperone.", "Key genes for the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, ABCA1, ABCG1, MCOLN1, PLIN2, SQLE, HMGCR) are absent from the supplied list, so the egress and efflux steps are inferred from the surrounding programme rather than observed.", "Astrocyte co-culture means the lipid cargo supply and any acceptor particles are partly non-cell-autonomous; the RNA comparison is not resolved by that source.", "The global upward RNA shift could be partly technical (normalisation, ambient RNA or depth differences; gene:ACTB is strongly decreased), so absolute effect sizes are treated as unreliable and only relative rank/module coherence is used."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a rate-limiting step at the handoff of internalised lipid from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER-accessible/effluxable sterol pool: uptake-receptor and TFEB/MITF-CLEAR hydrolase transcripts rise coordinately far above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list, yet the ER sterol-responsive SREBP programme and the SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification genes remain induced, a combination expected only if the ER regulatory lipid pool stays 'low' while total lipid load rises. This predicts an accumulation of lysosomal sphingolipid substrates and of cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores rather than increased net lipid catabolism. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased lysosomal hydrolase substrates (glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 gangliosides, sphingomyelin, lactosylceramide) together with increased cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol, while the ER/plasma-membrane accessible free-cholesterol pool (D4H* or filipin-based probe) is not increased. Finding lower substrate levels and higher accessible free cholesterol in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: supplying an extralysosomal sterol shunt or acceptor (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or exogenous ApoE3-containing/apoA-I acceptor particles) should, in APOE4 only, lower SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR) and the TFEB/CLEAR hydrolase transcripts toward APOE3 levels and reduce cholesteryl-ester mass. If SREBP targets stay elevated after sterol is chemically extracted from the lysosome, the 'trapped-sterol keeps the ER sensor low' step is wrong.", "Pulse-chase of a traceable lipid cargo (BODIPY- or 3H-cholesteryl-ester-labelled lipoprotein or myelin debris) should show equal or greater internalisation but slower appearance of label in the ER/esterified and effluxed fractions in APOE4. Equal or faster egress kinetics in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Measured per-enzyme catalytic output should lag abundance: APOE4 lysosomal GBA/HEXA/acid sphingomyelinase activity per unit enzyme protein should be equal to or lower than APOE3 despite higher transcripts. A proportional increase in activity and in cargo clearance would weaken the mechanism.", "SOAT1 inhibition should convert the APOE4 cholesteryl-ester pool to free cholesterol and increase, not normalise, the lysosomal/CLEAR hydrolase programme; normalisation of that programme by SOAT1 inhibition would indicate esterification, not lysosomal egress, is the primary bottleneck.", "The alternative that this is generic ER proteostasis failure predicts coordinate induction of HSPA5, XBP1 splicing, ATF4 and HERPUD1 with ERAD components; the supplied data instead show a decreased ERAD module (SEL1L, EDEM1, DERL1) and non-significant, negative HSP90B1/HSPA5-candidate protein spots (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005). Detecting strong XBP1 splicing and BiP protein induction in APOE4 would favour that alternative over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher measured transcript abundance of scavenger and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA) is inferred, not measured, to raise the flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system of APOE4 microglia.", "Rising luminal cargo is inferred to activate the TFEB/MITF CLEAR programme (measured: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), producing the strongest coherent transcript module in the dataset: acid glycosidases and cathepsins (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1), median effect +5.5 versus a +1.5 list-wide median.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK (inferred, not measured): export of liberated sterol and sphingolipid catabolites from the lysosomal lumen/limiting membrane to the ER-accessible regulatory pool and to ApoE-dependent efflux is rate-limiting, so hydrolase abundance rises without a matching rise in net lipid egress; the transport-side genes measured here are not coordinately elevated (gene:M6PR is decreased, gene:NPC2 and lysosomal membrane genes sit at or below the list-wide median while hydrolases sit far above it).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not replenished, the ER sterol sensor is inferred to remain in its low-cholesterol configuration and the SREBP transcriptional programme stays on despite total lipid loading (measured: gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2).", "Sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are inferred to be re-esterified and stored rather than effluxed (measured: gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 transcripts increased; gene:APOE transcript increased, but APOE4 protein acceptor competence is unverified background knowledge and was not measured here), closing a futile synthesis-storage cycle.", "The predicted steady state is an expanded, substrate-loaded lysosomal compartment plus cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets, i.e. a lipid-laden microglial phenotype consistent with the increased gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3 and gene:CTSK transcripts, with lipid composition rather than lipid clearance as the readout."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid-egress bottleneck sustains a futile SREBP synthesis-and-storage cycle in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25077088822218563, "cosine_similarity": 0.4421272426879941, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6032944983818771, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25077088822218563, "cosine_similarity": 0.4421272426879941, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6032944983818771, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.12851475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 12}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_082", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Measured values are abundances only: RNA rows are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base from a pre-selected differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); no flux, enzyme activity, lipid mass, localization or causal direction was measured, and the causal chain proposed here is inferred, not established.", "The selected-list background (1705 up / 507 down) is the correct comparator: a program being mostly positive is expected, so only magnitude and completeness (e.g. lysosomal median +2.38, TCA median +2.65 by permutation against the list background, p ~ 0.013-0.016 uncorrected across ~13 pre-specified sets) are treated as informative; genes within TFEB/CLEAR and TCA modules are co-regulated and not independent, so this is descriptive coherence, not formal enrichment.", "Absent genes are unknown, not unchanged: HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, MVK/MVD, CYP51A1, MSMO1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2/3, SQSTM1 and MAP1LC3B are not in the supplied rows, so the rate-limiting pre-squalene steps, cholesterol efflux and autophagic-substrate load are unmeasured.", "Protein spots are 2-6-candidate 2D-gel spots with frequent keratin/actin co-assignment; no spot uniquely identifies a protein. Spots containing cathepsins are bidirectional (protein_spot:055 +0.585, protein_spot:057 +0.585 vs protein_spot:058 -0.848, protein_spot:067 -1.0, protein_spot:069 -1.379), so they are used only for compatibility, never as confirmation of any individual protein; no sterol-pathway enzyme appears among spot candidates.", "APOE4 vs APOE3 is isogenic and mock-treated, so differences are baseline state differences; cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript changes may reflect non-cell-autonomous lipid/cholesterol supply rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation.", "Increased hydrolase, TCA and sterol-gene transcripts are read as increased capacity/unrepressed signaling, not as demonstrated activation; decreased transcripts (e.g. gene:CTSS, gene:OSBPL8) are not read as rate-limiting defects."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change, not by a single enzyme defect: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, the CLEAR/lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase network (with TFEB and MITF), and mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/ETC machinery are jointly elevated, together with an SREBP1-dominant esterification/phospholipid arm; sterol-synthesis and LDLR transcripts remain elevated rather than repressed, consistent with internalized sterol being routed to lysosomal and esterified/membrane pools instead of restoring the ER-accessible sterol pool. This describes increased processing capacity and altered routing in the measured mock condition; it does not establish a rate-limiting degradation defect, which would be revealed, if present, only by a lipid or phagocytic challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: pulsing APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with labelled lipoprotein/myelin lipid should show APOE4 with equal or higher lysosomal lipid hydrolysis and higher label incorporation into cholesteryl ester/TAG and into TCA-derived CO2 (increased throughput with storage bias). If APOE4 shows lower hydrolysis flux despite the elevated hydrolase transcripts, the mechanism is wrong in direction and should be replaced by a failed-compensation/lysosomal-block model.", "Prospective routing test: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should lower esterified sterol and restore repression of the sterol-synthesis/uptake transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR) toward APOE3 levels without collapsing the lysosomal hydrolase module. Unchanged sterol-synthesis transcripts after effective esterification blockade would falsify step 5 (routing away from the ER-sensing pool).", "Prospective coordination test: TFEB/MiT-family knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the lysosomal-hydrolase plus v-ATPase transcript module (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C) and blunt the TCA/ETC transcript elevation (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH). If the TCA module is fully TFEB-independent, the single coordinated cell-state claim is weakened and the two programs should be treated as separate APOE4 effects.", "Prospective challenge test (reserve, not ongoing defect): after a lipid or phagocytic load, APOE4 microglia should accumulate undigested lysosomal lipid and free cholesterol earlier than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. Equal or slower accumulation under challenge would show the expanded capacity is a sufficient adaptation and remove the reduced-reserve part of the claim.", "Protein-level compatibility test: total mature cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein per cell should be equal or higher in APOE4 by targeted immunoblot; a reproducible decrease would contradict the capacity-expansion interpretation and favour post-transcriptional loss of lysosomal proteins."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases delivery and internalization of lipid/lipoprotein cargo into microglia: uptake and lipid-receptor transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24), an inferred flux, since only transcript abundance was measured.", "The endolysosomal compartment is transcriptionally expanded in a MiT/TFE-consistent pattern (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) with broad hydrolase and acidification/transport members up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SPNS1 +2.58), raising degradative and solute-export capacity (activity not measured).", "Carbon liberated by catabolism is routed toward mitochondrial oxidation and citrate export: pyruvate/TCA/anaplerotic and ETC transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:CYCS +2.58, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65).", "Cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate-fed lipogenesis and esterification are engaged (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:FABP5 +1.13), routing fatty acids and sterol into esters and membrane phospholipid rather than into the free ER-accessible sterol pool.", "Because sterol is diverted to lysosomal, esterified and membrane pools, ER sterol sensing is not repressed: post-squalene and SREBP-2-type transcripts stay up (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SREBF2 +1.06) along with gene:LDLR +1.50, while feedback/oxysterol-disposal genes are also up (gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49), sustaining continued sterol acquisition alongside storage.", "The net measured state is an expanded, storage-biased lipid-processing microglial phenotype (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:GPNMB +1.11) with reduced expression of some homeostatic/effector genes (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:NAMPT -2.62); whether this expansion is sufficient (adaptation) or leaves reduced reserve is not determined by these measurements."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a MiT/TFE-associated lysosome-mitochondria expansion state that routes internalized lipid into hydrolysis and esterified/membrane pools while the ER-sterol-sensing arm stays unrepressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3499243067606986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23416134579582315, "cosine_similarity": 0.44158110336033024, "direction_accuracy": 0.3932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5580809061488673, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3499243067606986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23416134579582315, "cosine_similarity": 0.44158110336033024, "direction_accuracy": 0.3932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5580809061488673, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.036253, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_080", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong upward shift (1705/2212 positive, median 1.46), so only within-dataset relative position is interpreted; the logarithm base is unspecified, so effect sizes are treated as ordinal, not as fold changes.", "The relative depression of mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflects genuinely lower mitochondrial transcript/protein supply per cell rather than a 10X Flex capture, ambient-RNA or normalisation artefact; mtDNA copy number and mitochondrial translation were not measured.", "Transcript abundance of nuclear ETC/TCA genes is taken as a proxy for provision of those subunits; no protein, assembly, respirometry or metabolite measurement is supplied, so activity, flux, localisation and direction are inferred.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (frequently keratin/actin), so no spot is treated as an identified protein and none is used as primary support.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from a non-microglial compartment; no cell-type deconvolution or replicate count is supplied.", "Background pathway knowledge used to group genes (complex membership, TFEB targets, lipid handling) is unverified here because literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia up-regulate the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial module (ETC subunits, TCA enzymes, carriers, import machinery) and the TFEB-type lysosomal/lipid-handling program, but their mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) are relatively depressed; we hypothesise that mtDNA-encoded subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembling functional complexes I/III/IV/V, so terminal electron disposal caps oxidative catabolism of lysosome-derived lipid, producing an over-reduced quinone/NAD pool, a compensatory thiol-peroxidase response, and diversion of fatty acyl units into desaturation and neutral-lipid storage rather than oxidation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Complexome/BN-PAGE plus quantitative proteomics of APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex III2, IV and V per unit mitochondrial mass together with equal or increased free nuclear-encoded subunit pools, i.e. an mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded subunit ratio below 1 in APOE4. If assembled complex levels and that ratio are equal between genotypes, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: xenotopic expression of Ciona alternative oxidase (AOX, bypasses complexes III/IV) or supply of a membrane-permeable quinone electron acceptor in APOE4 microglia should relieve ubiquinol over-reduction, raise uncoupled oxygen consumption toward APOE3 levels, and reduce neutral-lipid droplet area by at least ~30% while leaving the lysosomal transcript program (GAA, GBA, CTSB, TFEB) largely unchanged. If AOX restores respiration but leaves lipid storage unchanged, the terminal-oxidation-to-lipid link is falsified; if AOX fails to change respiration at all, the mtDNA-limited assembly premise is falsified.", "Increasing mitochondrial genome expression (TFAM or mitochondrial-translation boosting) should raise mtDNA-encoded subunit protein and reduce lipid storage in APOE4; no change in either would weaken the mechanism.", "Directionality test: DGAT1/SOAT1 inhibition should lower droplet content without restoring maximal respiration in APOE4. If blocking esterification also normalises respiration, the causal arrow runs from lipid storage to mitochondria rather than as proposed.", "Rejected-focus control: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0/C22:0 ratio, ACOX1-dependent H2O2 production) should be similar between genotypes despite lower gene:ABCD1. Demonstrating a primary peroxisomal import/oxidation defect with intact respiratory-complex assembly would replace this mechanism.", "Single-cell or bulk measurement should show the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit is not accompanied by a proportional loss of mitochondrial mass markers (TOMM22, citrate synthase); a proportional loss would indicate simple mitochondrial depletion rather than mitonuclear imbalance and would weaken the hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): every nuclear-encoded ETC subunit row in the dataset is higher in APOE4 (38/38 positive, mean effect 2.81 vs dataset mean 1.39, permutation p=0.001), together with TCA/anaplerotic and mitochondrial carrier/import rows (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A11, gene:GOT1, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44). INFERRED: increased transcriptional provision of the nuclear half of the respiratory chain and increased delivery of reducing equivalents to the matrix; mitochondrial mass, protein levels and flux were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits of complex I (gene:MT-ND4), III (gene:MT-CYB), IV (gene:MT-CO2) and V (gene:MT-ATP6) sit in the 4th-18th percentile of an otherwise upward-shifted selected DE set. INFERRED (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK): the mtDNA-encoded subunit pool, and not the nuclear pool, limits assembly of the catalytic cores; complex assembly, mtDNA copy number and mitochondrial translation were not measured.", "INFERRED: the resulting stoichiometric mismatch caps electron transfer at complexes III/IV and proton-motive-force use at complex V, so the ubiquinol/NADH pools become more reduced even though upstream dehydrogenase and beta-oxidation capacity is transcriptionally increased (gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:OGDH). This is an inferred flux/redox-poise statement, not a measured one.", "MEASURED (RNA) as a correlate: thiol/selenium peroxidase and mitochondrial-stress transcripts are elevated (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:SELENOW, gene:DDIT3, gene:HSPA9, gene:FIS1). INFERRED: increased electron leak and peroxide load buffered by an antioxidant/mitochondrial-stress response; ROS, glutathione and enzyme activities were not measured, and this arm is a consequence, not the bottleneck.", "MEASURED (RNA): lipoprotein/lipid uptake, lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB rows are strongly elevated (gene:SCARB1, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB, gene:APOE), i.e. lipid entry into the endolysosomal system is transcriptionally amplified while oxidative disposal is inferred to be capped.", "INFERRED endpoint: fatty acyl units released by lysosomal hydrolysis that cannot be oxidised are routed to desaturation and esterification/storage (gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:MGLL), giving the APOE4-specific neutral-lipid accumulation phenotype. No lipid species, droplet or flux measurement is present in the supplied data."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: mtDNA-encoded ETC core subunits limit terminal electron disposal in APOE4 microglia while nuclear mitochondrial, lysosomal and lipid-uptake programs are amplified"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12720156555772993, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27840599859118903, "cosine_similarity": 0.4397004642149867, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mean_absolute_error": 0.566663430420712, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12720156555772993, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27840599859118903, "cosine_similarity": 0.4397004642149867, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.566663430420712, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6344815, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 13}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Higher transcript abundance for a carrier or enzyme is a usable proxy for higher protein amount and pathway capacity in these cells; no matched targeted proteomics or activity assay is supplied and the protein-spot data are multi-candidate, so this step is assumed, not shown.", "The RNA logarithm base is left as reported and unspecified; only the sign and the relative ranking of effects within the supplied list are used, because 77% of the 2212 selected rows are positive and all rows have |effect| \u003e 1, so the list is a thresholded, selected differential-expression set rather than an unbiased transcriptome.", "Enrichment is assessed against the supplied list itself, so conclusions are about pathways shifted relative to the already up-shifted background; absence of a gene (ACLY, FASN, ACACA, CPT1A, PLIN2, ABCA1, PPARGC1A, TFAM) means it was not supplied, not that it is unchanged.", "Cells were microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; the RNA differences are assumed to arise mainly in microglia, although ambient or contaminating astrocyte signal (e.g. gene:S100B) cannot be excluded, and no replicate counts are supplied.", "Protein spots are assumed to contain, but not to identify, their candidate proteins; they are used only as weak corroboration and never as evidence for a specific protein pool.", "The genotype difference is assumed to be steady-state under mock treatment rather than a transient culture artefact of one differentiation batch."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated increase in transcripts for mitochondrial substrate carriers, TCA enzymes and ETC subunits without matched glycolytic-enzyme induction, together with an SREBF1-associated lipogenic/sterol and esterification program and lipoprotein-uptake receptors. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node distinguishing the genotypes is mitochondrial citrate export to the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool (MPC2/TCA -\u003e SLC25A1 axis), which supplies SREBF1-dependent fatty-acid, sterol and glycerolipid synthesis and drives net neutral-lipid storage; the parallel TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase induction is a downstream response to the increased lipid/membrane substrate load rather than the initiating lesion. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, transport, localisation and causal statements are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown), or of ACLY, in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content (BODIPY 493/503 or LipidTOX per-cell intensity) and SREBF1 target transcripts (SCD, FADS1, HMGCS1) toward APOE3 levels while leaving ETC subunit transcripts and mitochondrial mass largely unchanged; if droplet content and SCD are unchanged after effective target engagement, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Substrate-origin test: 13C6-glucose and 13C5-glutamine tracing should show greater label incorporation into citrate and into palmitate and cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3; equal lipogenic labelling despite the transcript differences would falsify the inferred citrate-to-lipid flux.", "Uptake-versus-synthesis discrimination: culturing in lipoprotein-deficient medium or blocking SR-B1/CD36-mediated uptake should not abolish the APOE4 excess in droplets if de novo synthesis dominates; complete normalisation by lipoprotein removal would move the bottleneck to uptake and weaken step 2-3.", "Bioenergetics: extracellular flux analysis should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption in APOE4 without a proportional increase in extracellular acidification; lower APOE4 oxygen consumption would falsify the inferred increase in mitochondrial oxidative capacity read from gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2 and gene:ATP5ME.", "Ordering of the lysosomal arm: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSD) without normalising APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet content, whereas blocking lipogenesis should lower both; if TFEB knockdown alone normalises droplets, the lysosomal program is upstream and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Independent-cohort replication: in fresh isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia the mitochondrial carrier/TCA/ETC transcript set should again shift upward relative to the whole-transcriptome median while glycolytic transcripts do not; loss of that relative shift in unbiased RNA-seq would indicate the pattern is an artefact of the selected list or normalisation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 shows higher abundance of transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate and dicarboxylate carriers and TCA enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5) and of 39/39 detected ETC/OXPHOS subunit transcripts (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:CYCS), while glycolytic enzyme transcripts are not coordinately raised and two are lower (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP). Inferred: greater mitochondrial oxidative and anaplerotic capacity with carbon entering the TCA cycle rather than being exported as lactate; oxygen consumption and lactate flux were not measured.", "Inferred bottleneck step: increased TCA carbon combined with raised gene:SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) transcript raises citrate export from matrix to cytosol; citrate and acetyl-CoA pools, ACLY protein and carrier activity were not measured, so this transport flux is an inference, and ACLY, ACACA and FASN are absent from the supplied differential-expression list.", "Inferred: the enlarged cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool (also supported by higher gene:ACSS2) sustains an SREBF1-associated lipogenic and sterol program that is coherently elevated at RNA level (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2). SREBP proteolytic activation and nuclear localisation were not measured.", "Measured: esterification and lipid-acquisition transcripts are higher (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7). Inferred: synthesised plus internalised fatty acids and sterols are esterified to triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester and stored, giving higher neutral-lipid droplet content in APOE4; no lipid species, droplet or efflux measurement is present in the discovery data.", "Inferred consequence: increased delivery of internalised lipoprotein and membrane lipid to the endolysosome raises catabolic demand, matching higher transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, sphingolipid catabolism and the v-ATPase (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1) and endosomal maturation and sorting components (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1). Lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and cargo degradation rate were not measured.", "Net inferred state: APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-loading, oxidative-biased state rather than a glycolytic inflammatory state; classical inflammatory transcripts are not coordinately elevated above the strong global upward shift of the selected differential-expression list."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial citrate into SREBF1-driven lipogenesis and neutral-lipid esterification, with lysosomal hydrolase induction as a downstream load response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29555440682346856, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2940756868090274, "cosine_similarity": 0.4395929074103402, "direction_accuracy": 0.35275080906148865, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5772233009708738, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29555440682346856, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2940756868090274, "cosine_similarity": 0.4395929074103402, "direction_accuracy": 0.35275080906148865, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5772233009708738, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90209475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 14}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); enrichment is therefore judged only relative to this shifted background, and absolute direction of the whole list is not interpretable.", "The unspecified RNA logarithm base is preserved; no effect is converted to a fold change.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the capacity of a compartment, not for hydrolase activity, luminal pH, sterol flux, or localisation, none of which are supplied.", "2D-gel protein spots each carry 2-6 candidate genes (median 5; KRT1/KRT10/ACTB appear in 33/30/25 of 92 spots), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and spots are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Key pools of the proposed chain were not measured at all: NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1/ABCG1, free and esterified cholesterol, lipid droplets, lysosomal pH and proteolytic activity; their behaviour is inferred.", "The mitochondrially encoded transcripts fall while nuclear OXPHOS transcripts rise, which is compatible with a compositional/normalisation difference between genotypes; the analysis assumes that such a global scaling does not by itself create the lysosomal set's excess over the global mean.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured transcripts could reflect microglia-astrocyte interaction rather than a microglia-autonomous programme; single-cell 10X Flex assignment purity is not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not at the actin-driven engulfment step but at the post-internalisation step: lipid/lipoprotein cargo delivered to the late endosome-lysosome is cleared and exported more slowly, so cells raise a coordinated lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcriptional programme (with TFEB) while the ER sterol sensor remains un-suppressed and continues to drive SREBP-2/SREBP-1 target expression together with continued scavenger-receptor expression, predicting net intracellular lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage rather than efflux. This is a proposed, not demonstrated, causal chain; only transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: give APOE3 and APOE4 microglia a fluorescent cargo whose uptake and clearance can be separated (e.g. BODIPY-LDL, TopFluor-cholesterol-labelled lipoprotein, or pHrodo-myelin). The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalised signal in APOE4 in a short 15-30 min pulse (actin-dependent engulfment intact), but a significantly greater fraction of the internalised label still in LAMP1-positive compartments after 6-24 h. If APOE4 instead shows a lower initial internalisation rate with normal clearance kinetics, the bottleneck is at uptake/engulfment and this mechanism is wrong.", "Sterol-sensing test: loading cells with the same cargo should suppress SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) in APOE3 but suppress them significantly less in APOE4. Equal suppression in both genotypes would falsify the proposed sensing failure.", "Bypass rescue: hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or restoring lysosomal sterol export/acid lipase activity, should in APOE4 lower the lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and normalise SREBP-2 targets while leaving scavenger-receptor transcripts largely unchanged. If cyclodextrin lowers uptake-receptor transcripts but not SREBP-2 targets, the bottleneck is placed incorrectly.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript excess and worsen, not improve, cargo retention and neutral-lipid storage. If hydrolase transcripts are TFEB-independent here, step 3 is wrong.", "Direct capacity check: v-ATPase-dependent acidification and cathepsin B/D activity per lysosome should be equal or higher in APOE4 despite the transcript increase. A measured decrease in v-ATPase protein or lysosomal acidification would weaken the compensatory-biogenesis reading and favour a primary acidification defect instead; the two ATP6V1E1-containing spots (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) are already lower in APOE4 and constitute existing counter-evidence.", "Actin-independence control: an Arp2/3 inhibitor (CK-666) at a dose that equally reduces early internalisation in both genotypes should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in long-timepoint lysosomal cargo retention. If the genotype difference disappears with Arp2/3 inhibition, a cytoskeletal engulfment mechanism is favoured over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["Cargo entry is not the limiting difference: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7), whereas the actin-nucleation/motor module is not coordinately raised above the strong global RNA up-shift and includes clear decreases (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9); engulfment capacity is therefore inferred, not measured, to be intact or increased.", "Delivered cargo, inferred to include APOE4-containing lipoprotein particles, is a poorer substrate for luminal disassembly and sterol release (background assumption, unverified here), so cargo residence time in the late endosome/lysosome is inferred to increase; no lipid, pH, or hydrolase-activity measurement is supplied.", "The cell responds with an MiT/TFE-type lysosomal biogenesis programme: gene:TFEB is higher and the hydrolase/v-ATPase set is coherently raised above the global shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:IGF2R), with gene:GPNMB as an accompanying lysosomal-stress-associated transcript.", "Late-endosomal maturation/trafficking transcripts move with this programme (gene:RAB7A, gene:NPC2), consistent with expansion of the degradative compartment rather than a block at internalisation.", "Because sterol liberated from cargo is inferred not to reach the ER sterol sensor efficiently, SCAP-SREBP-2 remains active: gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1 and gene:MYLIP are all higher in APOE4, alongside the lipogenic arm gene:SREBF1 and gene:SCD.", "Simultaneous high uptake-receptor expression, high de-novo sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and high esterification capacity (gene:SOAT1) with gene:APOE itself raised predicts futile influx: the flux converges on stored neutral lipid and an enlarged, hydrolase-rich but functionally back-logged lysosome, which is the primary bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited downstream of internalisation: a lysosomal luminal catabolism / sterol-egress bottleneck drives compensatory TFEB-type lysosome biogenesis and unrestrained SREBP-2 sterol synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15166340508806261, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2432459650403402, "cosine_similarity": 0.43831492869652183, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885987055016182, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15166340508806261, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2432459650403402, "cosine_similarity": 0.43831492869652183, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885987055016182, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.863454, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 15}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_106", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) in an unspecified logarithm base; enrichment claims are therefore made only relative to the internal background of this list, not to the transcriptome.", "The six MT- rows are treated as representative of the mtDNA-encoded arm even though probe-based 10X Flex capture of mitochondrial transcripts may be incomplete and two of six (MT-ND4L, MT-ND5) are positive.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to constrain, but not equal, subunit protein supply; holo-complex assembly, respiratory flux, citrate export, acetyl-CoA level, lipid-droplet content, lysosomal proteolytic capacity and any causal direction are inferred and were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are used only as weak, ambiguity-limited concordance for cathepsin-containing spots, and no mitochondrial or lipogenic protein pool was measured.", "Genotype effects are assumed to act cell-intrinsically in microglia, although the samples are microglia-astrocyte co-cultures and shifts in cell proportion or ambient RNA could contribute (e.g. S100B +6.0, PTPRC -1.5).", "The global list is 77% positive with median +1.46, so a uniform normalisation or capture offset may inflate all effects; only sets exceeding this internal background are treated as informative."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coherent up-shift of nuclear-encoded TCA-cycle, mitochondrial-carrier and respiratory-chain subunit transcripts together with a down-shift of mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts. We hypothesise that the limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic subunits, so that holo-complex assembly and oxidative flux cannot follow the increased nuclear program; the resulting matrix carbon surplus is exported as citrate (SLC25A1) toward cytosolic acetyl-CoA and an SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/DHCR24 lipogenic-sterol program, while a DELE1/DDIT3-associated stress response and an expanded lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program handle the accumulating lipid. Interferon/ISG signalling is not the differentiating mechanism in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown or pharmacological inhibition of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2) in APOE4 microglia should lower cytosolic acetyl-CoA-dependent lipogenesis and preferentially reduce neutral-lipid/BODIPY droplet area and SCD/DGAT1 transcript levels relative to identically treated APOE3 microglia, without normalising the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit; if SLC25A1 loss leaves the APOE4 lipid excess unchanged, the citrate-export step is wrong.", "Blue-native PAGE or complex-I/IV in-gel activity plus Seahorse on the same cultures should show that APOE4 has assembled holo-complex content and maximal/spare respiration that are flat or reduced despite higher nuclear subunit transcripts, i.e. an assembly-limited state; if assembled complexes and maximal respiration increase in proportion to the nuclear transcript rise, the bottleneck assignment fails.", "ddPCR/qPCR of mtDNA copy number and of mtDNA-encoded versus nuclear-encoded transcripts should reproduce a lower mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded ratio in APOE4; an equal ratio by an orthogonal, non-probe-based assay would falsify the mitonuclear-imbalance premise and reassign the signal to 10X Flex capture bias.", "Blocking the stress relay (DELE1 or HRI knockdown, or ISRIB) should reduce DDIT3 and partially blunt the lipogenic/lysosomal program while leaving the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit intact, separating the stress-response arm from the metabolic bottleneck; if ISR blockade also restores MT- transcripts, the ordering of steps is wrong.", "Negative control for the assigned focus: no type-I interferon signature should be recoverable in APOE4 versus APOE3 mock cultures (no induction of ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1, OAS1, STAT1/2, RSAD2 by qPCR, and no IFN-beta in medium); a robust ISG induction would show the selected list simply missed an interferon axis and would weaken the claim that the metabolic axis is the differentiating mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_106", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia transcriptionally amplify the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program: 73 nuclear mito-related transcripts (complex I/III/IV/V subunits, TCA enzymes, SLC25 carriers, import and mitoribosome-translation factors) have median effect +2.80 versus +1.46 for all 2212 selected rows, 96% positive (permutation p \u003c 5e-5).", "In the same list the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts run the other way (median -1.56, permutation p ~ 0.015), giving a ~4.4 log-unit median gap between the nuclear and mitochondrial-genome arms; we infer, not measure, that mtDNA-encoded catalytic subunits become the stoichiometric bottleneck for assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V.", "Because each of these complexes requires mtDNA-encoded cores, we infer that assembled holo-complex content and electron flux rise less than the nuclear subunit transcripts, i.e. an inferred activity/abundance dissociation rather than a measured respiration defect.", "Carbon entering the matrix (MPC2, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, GLUD1, IDH3B/G all up) exceeds what constrained oxidation can consume, and the strongly increased citrate/isocitrate carrier SLC25A1 (+4.47) plus ACSS2 (+2.93) provide an inferred cytosolic acetyl-CoA route.", "Cytosolic acetyl-CoA feeds an SREBP-type anabolic program (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.71, DHCR7, DGAT1, LDLR, SOAT1, INSIG1, ABCA7; 17/17 lipid-anabolic transcripts positive), predicted to raise neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content in APOE4 microglia.", "Mitochondrial-stress relay and lipid load engage a compensatory catabolic response: DELE1 (+4.82) with DDIT3 (+2.80), CEBPG, EIF2AK3, and a TFEB-associated lysosomal program (TFEB +2.38; GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V subunits; median +2.38, permutation p = 0.026, 96% up), which we interpret as a demand signal for degrading accumulated lipid rather than as evidence of successful clearance."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance in APOE4 microglia: mtDNA-encoded ETC subunit supply is the bottleneck that reroutes citrate-derived carbon into lipogenesis and lysosomal load"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14677103718199608, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26911409614894233, "cosine_similarity": 0.4382209195890124, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_106", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5648543689320388, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14677103718199608, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26911409614894233, "cosine_similarity": 0.4382209195890124, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5648543689320388, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.760105, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 16}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_063", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression subset with an unspecified logarithm base and a |log fold change| \u003e= 1 selection gap; set-level directionality is therefore judged relative to the background median (+1.46), not against zero.", "Elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and CLEAR transcripts are assumed to indicate an increased lysosomal transcriptional program; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number and cargo content were not measured and are inferred.", "MiT/TFE transcript elevation is assumed to accompany increased nuclear TFEB/TFE3-family activity; nuclear localisation and mTORC1 phosphorylation status were not measured.", "The elevated SREBP-target transcripts are assumed to report an unsatisfied ER sterol sensor rather than a purely biosynthetic demand for new lysosomal/plasma membrane; this is the main alternative and is not resolved by the data.", "2-D protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each; spot-level changes are treated as consistency checks only and are not assigned to a named protein or to a pro- versus mature-enzyme form.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipid cargo comparably to both genotypes; genotype-specific astrocyte lipid secretion is an untested confound.", "The global upward RNA shift (77% of selected rows positive; gene:ACTB and several MT- transcripts strongly negative) may partly reflect compositional/normalisation asymmetry rather than uniform transcriptional induction."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in post-uptake endolysosomal cargo handling: transcripts for uptake receptors are uniformly elevated while the acid-hydrolase/CLEAR module is elevated above the already-upward-shifted background (hydrolase set median +2.17 vs background +1.46, MWU p=0.009; CLEAR set p=0.007) together with all three measured MiT/TFE factors (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF) and the lysosomal-stress marker gene:GPNMB. We hypothesise that this reflects an inferred bottleneck in delivering cargo-derived sterol/lipid out of the endolysosome to the ER, so that the ER sterol sensor is not satisfied and SREBP-driven synthesis, esterification and further uptake continue (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), producing a feed-forward load on an expanded but saturated lysosomal compartment. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Pulse-chase of a dual-labelled lipid cargo (e.g. fluorescent myelin or acetylated LDL carrying a traceable sterol) should show equal or greater early internalisation in APOE4 but slower loss of label from LAMP1+ compartments and slower appearance of cargo-derived sterol in the esterified/ER pool. If APOE4 clears cargo from LAMP1+ compartments and esterifies cargo sterol with the same kinetics as APOE3, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is weakened.", "Relieving lysosomal sterol egress pharmacologically (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS) and CLEAR transcripts (CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1H, GPNMB) in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels without reducing uptake-receptor transcripts (MRC1, CD163, TREM2). Persistence of elevated SREBP-2 and CLEAR transcripts after successful egress rescue would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating test versus an acidification-failure variant: measure lysosomal pH and cathepsin/GBA/HEXA activity per lysosome. The hypothesis predicts APOE4 lysosomal pH is not raised and hydrolase activity rises roughly in proportion to the transcript increase, yet undegraded lipid cargo still accumulates. Finding raised lysosomal pH with reduced hydrolase activity despite elevated transcripts would replace this mechanism with an acidification-capacity bottleneck (a reading also compatible with the reduced ATP6V1E1-containing spots protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065).", "Discriminating test versus cargo-independent transcriptional rewiring: culturing APOE4 and APOE3 microglia without astrocytes and without added lipid cargo, or blocking phagocytic uptake, should collapse most of the CLEAR and SREBP transcript difference. If the CLEAR/MiT-TFE elevation persists undiminished in cargo-free conditions, a cargo-load-driven bottleneck is not the primary explanation.", "Single-lysosome imaging should show more, larger, cargo-filled LAMP1+ structures and more filipin-positive or BODIPY-positive lysosomal lipid in APOE4; an unchanged lysosomal volume fraction and lipid content despite the transcript changes would weaken the claim that the transcriptional program reports a real cargo load."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for phagocytic/scavenger uptake receptors are coordinately higher in APOE4 (gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A); inferred, not measured: cargo internalisation flux into the endolysosomal system is maintained or increased.", "Inferred: cargo (lipid-rich membrane and lipoprotein material) accumulates in late endosomes/lysosomes because degradative and lipid-egress throughput per lysosome does not keep pace; no lysosomal cargo pool, pH, or hydrolase activity was measured here.", "Measured: a compensatory CLEAR-type transcriptional response - acid hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DNASE2), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1), lysosomal membrane/solute carriers (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SPNS1), late-endosome trafficking (gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B, gene:VPS18) and all measured MiT/TFE factors (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC); inferred, not measured: increased nuclear MiT/TFE activity and increased lysosome number/volume.", "Inferred: because cargo sterol is retained in the endolysosomal lumen, the ER-accessible cholesterol pool remains low, so SREBP processing stays permissive - consistent with the measured elevation of gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1 and gene:SCD; SREBP cleavage itself was not measured.", "Measured: sterol/lipid disposal and storage transcripts rise in parallel (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:CH25H); inferred: neutral-lipid esterification and droplet storage increase as an overflow route rather than resolving the lysosomal load.", "Net inferred state: an expanded but functionally saturated endolysosomal compartment with sustained lysosomal-stress markers (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:FTH1) and altered lysosomal-hydrolase protein spot distribution (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067), which the 2-D spot data cannot resolve to a single protein form."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain a MiT/TFE-driven lysosomal expansion because cargo-derived lipid/sterol egress, not uptake, is the throughput bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14774951076320939, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21913341482649698, "cosine_similarity": 0.4380949907922715, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mean_absolute_error": 0.601546925566343, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14774951076320939, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21913341482649698, "cosine_similarity": 0.4380949907922715, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.601546925566343, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60999725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 17}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_125", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every supplied row has |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of a gene means it did not pass that filter or was not tested, not that it is unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are used only ordinally, especially since the most statistically confident rows carry the smallest effects (median |effect| 1.4 in the 200 lowest-FDR rows versus 1.98 in the 1000 highest-FDR rows).", "77.1% of supplied RNA rows are positive (median +1.46), so direction alone is uninformative; a set is only treated as informative if its members are both consistently directional and highly ranked by FDR.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for, but not a measurement of, hydrolase activity, lipid flux, sterol localisation, droplet content or secretion; no lipid, sterol, enzyme-activity, efflux or imaging data are supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (e.g. protein_spot:053 lists TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot direction is not used to confirm any gene.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous; replicate number is not supplied, so no variance-based confidence is claimed.", "Causality is not established by these data; the APOE4-versus-APOE3 contrast is associative even though the comparison is isogenic."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step is hydrolysis and export of internalized lipid (cholesterol and sphingolipids) from the endolysosome. Elevated scavenger/phagocytic receptor transcripts imply increased lipid influx, while a coordinated TFEB/MITF-type hydrolase and v-ATPase transcriptional expansion indicates compensation for lipid that remains sequestered; because sequestered sterol is inferred not to reach the ER-accessible pool, SREBP-target sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and ER esterification transcripts stay high instead of being feedback-suppressed, producing a futile uptake-synthesis-storage cycle. The modest ER-stress transcripts present (ATF6, DDIT3, EIF2AK3, MANF, CRELD2) are treated as a secondary consequence of lipid load, not as evidence of a primary unfolded-protein/ERAD defect, which the data do not support.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: mobilising lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or acute ER-directed sterol delivery such as 25-hydroxycholesterol) should collapse the SREBP-target set (SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS, SCD) and the hydrolase/v-ATPase set toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h without lowering scavenger-receptor transcripts, whereas an ER-proteostasis-directed treatment (TUDCA/4-PBA, or PERK inhibition/ISRIB) should not normalise them. The mechanism is weakened if the ISRIB/TUDCA arm normalises the lysosomal-sterol program while cyclodextrin does not.", "Sterol-localisation test: an ER-accessible-cholesterol probe (ALOD4/D4H) should show equal or lower ER-pool sterol in APOE4 despite higher total/lysosomal sterol (filipin) and higher neutral-lipid droplet content. Finding higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 together with sustained SREBP-target expression falsifies step 4.", "Flux test: pulse-chase of fluorescent or isotope-labelled myelin/oxLDL/apoptotic-cell lipid should show slower cholesterol and sphingolipid clearance and greater lysosomal retention in APOE4, with an exaggerated GPNMB and hydrolase response after loading. Equal clearance kinetics between genotypes falsifies the primary bottleneck.", "Activity-versus-RNA test: measured GBA, HEXB and cathepsin B/D activities should rise less than their transcripts (sub-proportional), consistent with the ambiguous spot data (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 decreased while protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 increased). Proportional, fully compensating increases in activity would argue against a clearance bottleneck.", "Esterification test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should increase free cholesterol and suppress SREBP-target transcripts more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3, and increase APOE-dependent efflux; no genotype-by-drug interaction would weaken step 5.", "Negative prediction for the rejected mechanism: APOE4 cells should not show canonical chaperone-arm UPR induction (HSPA5/BiP, XBP1 splicing, HERPUD1, PDIA4) nor increased ERAD flux; observing strong BiP/XBP1s induction and faster ERAD substrate turnover in APOE4 would support a primary ER-proteostasis mechanism instead of this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_125", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher transcripts for scavenger, lectin and complement-linked uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:CD14, gene:CLEC7A, gene:COLEC12, gene:MS4A6A, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA) are interpreted as increased capacity for lipid/lipoprotein and debris internalisation; the internalisation flux itself is inferred, not measured.", "Internalised cargo is routed to late endosomes/lysosomes (gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2 elevated); hydrolysis and NPC-dependent sterol export from this compartment is proposed as the limiting step in APOE4 because APOE4 is a poorer lipid acceptor (background knowledge, unverified here; no lipid or efflux measurement is supplied).", "Cells compensate transcriptionally through a TFEB/MITF-type program: gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GAA, gene:NPC2, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1 are all increased at RNA level; hydrolase protein amount and catalytic activity remain unmeasured and are not claimed.", "Because sterol is inferred to stay in lysosomes and in ester/droplet pools rather than the ER-accessible pool, ER sterol sensing is not satisfied: SREBP-pathway and distal sterol-synthesis transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD) instead of being suppressed by the lipid surplus.", "Surplus lipid is buffered by ER-based esterification and glycerolipid/phospholipid synthesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:CHPT1, gene:CERS6) together with lipid-transport/handling genes (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:FABP5, gene:PLA2G7, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:TSPO), yielding an inferred lipid-laden, GPNMB-high state (gene:GPNMB).", "Chronic membrane-lipid load in the ER is proposed to trigger a limited, bilayer-stress-type response (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:MANF, gene:CRELD2, gene:NUPR1) without a chaperone-arm signature, while ERAD transcripts are lower (gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1), so proteostasis failure is placed downstream of, not upstream of, the lipid bottleneck."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck, not primary ER proteostasis failure, defines the APOE4 microglial state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2455968688845401, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15826152744775152, "cosine_similarity": 0.4376754502146846, "direction_accuracy": 0.40614886731391586, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_125", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5817508090614887, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2455968688845401, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15826152744775152, "cosine_similarity": 0.4376754502146846, "direction_accuracy": 0.40614886731391586, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5817508090614887, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.63753725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 18}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_036", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, NPC1, MCOLN1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, PLIN2) means unreported, not unchanged. All comparisons are therefore made against the supplied background, whose logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "The strong global upward shift of the supplied rows (77% positive, median +1.46 in reported log units) is treated as a technical/selection baseline, so pathway claims rest on enrichment relative to that background rather than on the sign of individual genes.", "Protein spots are mixtures: each carries up to six candidate genes, so cathepsin/HEXB spot changes are treated as ambiguous evidence of a transcript-protein mismatch, not as identified hydrolase measurements.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increase is assumed to indicate an active CLEAR programme; TFEB phosphorylation, nuclear localization and mTORC1 activity were not measured.", "No lipid, cholesterol, sphingolipid, lysosomal pH, or enzyme-activity measurement is present in this dataset; every statement about lipid pools, flux, localization and degradative capacity is inference, not observation.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an astrocyte-derived lipoprotein/lipid supply difference between APOE4 and APOE3 could drive the substrate arm without any microglia-intrinsic defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an increased endolysosomal lipid substrate load (raised lipid-uptake/handling and SREBP-1-type lipogenic transcripts) combined with a limiting lysosomal lipid-catabolic throughput; the coordinate up-regulation of TFEB/MITF and CLEAR-network hydrolase, v-ATPase and LAMP transcripts is best read as a compensatory demand signal rather than as achieved degradative capacity, because 2D-gel spots whose candidate genes include cathepsins and HEXB are not uniformly increased. We propose lysosomal lipid catabolic/egress flux, not interferon or NF-kB inflammatory signalling, as the primary bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: in matched APOE4 and APOE3 microglia, measure per-cell 4-MU enzymatic activity for GBA, HEXA/HEXB and GAA together with the corresponding transcripts. The mechanism predicts that the activity-to-transcript ratio is significantly LOWER in APOE4 while filipin/BODIPY-493 or LipidSpot signal colocalized with LAMP1 is HIGHER in APOE4. If hydrolase activity rises in proportion to the transcript increase AND lysosomal neutral-lipid/free-cholesterol load is equal or lower in APOE4, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "SECOND DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: constitutively active TFEB (TFEB-S211A) or acute mTORC1 inhibition should reduce lysosomal lipid load and normalize the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3 (genotype x treatment interaction). If TFEB activation increases hydrolase transcripts but leaves the APOE4-specific lipid excess unchanged, the compensation-insufficiency step is weakened and a purely upstream lipogenic model is favoured.", "INPUT-ARM TEST: SREBP pathway inhibition (fatostatin) or SCD inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area preferentially in APOE4 WITHOUT normalizing CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts if the lysosomal programme is substrate-driven; if CLEAR transcripts fall in parallel, the two arms are one signal and the model must be simplified.", "SUBSTRATE-CHALLENGE TEST: loading with myelin debris or acetylated LDL should produce greater lysosomal lipid retention and slower clearance kinetics in APOE4 than APOE3 over 24-72 h. Equal clearance kinetics would falsify the throughput bottleneck.", "NEGATIVE / FOCUS-REJECTION PREDICTION: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade should NOT abolish the APOE4-specific lysosomal-lipid phenotype, because interferon-stimulated genes are not enriched above the global background in these data (permutation p ~= 0.43 for a 7-gene ISG/MHC set). If JAK inhibition normalizes the phenotype, an interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "CELL-AUTONOMY TEST: APOE4 microglia monocultured without astrocytes, or cultured in astrocyte-conditioned medium swapped between genotypes, should retain the lysosomal-lipid difference if it is microglia-intrinsic; complete loss of the difference on medium swap would relocate the mechanism to astrocyte lipid supply."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling receptors and carriers (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:C1QA) and for SREBP-1-type de novo lipogenesis and acyl-transfer (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:ACSS2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). INFERRED, not measured: this raises the flux of neutral lipid, sterol ester and membrane lipid delivered to the endolysosome; no lipid pool was measured here.", "STEP 2 (inferred activity/flux): the increased substrate flux raises lysosomal lipid content and lowers the free-sterol signal reaching the ER, an inferred state consistent with the concurrent up-regulation of ER sterol-response transcripts (gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2), which would further increase sterol input in a feed-forward loop.", "STEP 3 (measured abundance): a coherent CLEAR-network transcriptional response is present (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF up, with 22 of 24 mapped lysosomal genes increased: gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1). INFERRED: this reflects TFEB/MITF nuclear translocation downstream of lysosomal stress; neither TFEB localization nor mTORC1 activity was measured.", "STEP 4 (measured abundance, protein): the transcriptional response is not mirrored by a uniform increase in the corresponding protein spots. Spots whose candidate-gene lists include CTSD, CTSB or HEXB are decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) while other cathepsin-containing spots are increased (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055). Because each spot has multiple candidate genes and 2D-gel position also depends on proteolytic maturation and charge, these spots are ambiguous; INFERRED: mature hydrolase protein and specific activity do not scale with transcript.", "STEP 5 (inferred bottleneck): the ratio of lysosomal lipid-catabolic and egress capacity to delivered substrate therefore falls in APOE4, so lipid accumulates in an expanded, transcriptionally activated but functionally under-powered endolysosomal compartment. Loss of two catabolic transcripts within the same compartment (gene:CTSS, gene:IDS strongly decreased) and of fatty-acyl activation (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 decreased) is consistent with a non-uniform, incomplete degradative programme rather than a uniformly enhanced one.", "STEP 6 (downstream, secondary): the resulting lipid-laden lysosomal state is proposed to be permissive for, not caused by, the modest and internally inconsistent inflammatory transcript changes (gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:CXCL8 up but gene:GSDMD, gene:TNFAIP3, gene:CCL4 down); inflammation is placed downstream and is not the bottleneck."], "title": "Substrate-driven lysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a TFEB/MITF CLEAR transcriptional compensation not matched at the hydrolase-protein level"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22371967654986522, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1999773869892802, "cosine_similarity": 0.4369694299650988, "direction_accuracy": 0.3592233009708738, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5866051779935275, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22371967654986522, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1999773869892802, "cosine_similarity": 0.4369694299650988, "direction_accuracy": 0.3592233009708738, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5866051779935275, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8499895, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 19}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_105", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effect column is a log fold change in an unspecified logarithm base; only the sign and the rank/relative magnitude within this column are used, and no absolute fold change is asserted.", "The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so enrichment is judged only against the internal background of these rows (mean +1.39, 77% positive), not against the transcriptome.", "The dataset-wide positive shift (77% of rows up) is at least partly technical (normalization, ambient RNA, cell-composition differences between genotype wells); the mechanism therefore rests on relative enrichment above that shift, not on the raw direction of any single gene.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each, so spot-level effects are treated as constraints on a set of proteins, never as identified proteins; no spot is claimed to measure a specific hydrolase.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a noisy proxy for the size of the corresponding enzyme pool; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, TFEB localization, cargo flux, cholesteryl ester, or lipid-droplet measurement exists in these files.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype effects may be non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein composition), which the supplied data cannot separate.", "Background pathway memberships (CLEAR/TFEB targets, sterol-egress components, APOE4 lipid biology) are unverified prior knowledge, as literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "In mock-treated iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia, the rate-limiting step relative to isogenic APOE3 is lysosomal hydrolysis and onward egress of internalized lipoprotein/membrane lipid, not ER protein folding. Scavenger-uptake transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, ABCA7, ANXA1) and a broad TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR transcript program (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSK, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, DPP7, SLC37A2, LAMP1, RAB7A, ATP6V1H/1A/0C) are coordinately elevated above the dataset-wide upward shift, while the sterol-egress/efflux arm is not correspondingly induced and hydrolase-candidate protein spots are not coordinately increased; the inferred consequence is retained lysosomal lipid that is re-esterified and stored via SOAT1/DGAT1/AGPAT2 with SREBF1/SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl chains. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute lysosomal cholesterol extraction with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 protein supplementation) in APOE4 microglia should, within 24-48 h, reduce filipin/BODIPY-cholesterol lysosomal signal and collapse the CLEAR transcript excess (GAA, GBA, CTSB, HEXA, ATP6V1H, TFEB) toward APOE3 levels while leaving uptake-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2) largely unchanged. If cyclodextrin lowers lysosomal sterol but the CLEAR transcript excess persists unchanged, the proposed sterol-egress bottleneck is not the driver and the mechanism is weakened.", "Functional capacity test: pulse-chase of DQ-BSA and BODIPY-LDL should show slower cargo clearance per lysosomal volume in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase mRNA, i.e. a reduced activity-to-transcript ratio for GBA, HEXA and cathepsin B. Equal or faster clearance and a proportional rise in hydrolase activity in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck step.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should worsen lysosomal lipid load and cargo-clearance kinetics without correcting them; if TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid accumulation, the CLEAR program is causal rather than compensatory and step 3 is wrong.", "Storage-arm test: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl-ester droplets toward free sterol, increase membrane-sterol and cytotoxicity readouts, and leave or increase the CLEAR transcript excess. Normalization of the CLEAR transcript excess by SOAT1 inhibition would place esterification upstream and weaken step 5.", "Uptake test: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36, should proportionally reduce the CLEAR transcript excess and the SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1 arm; an unchanged CLEAR excess under lipid-poor conditions would indicate a cargo-independent, uptake-independent cause.", "Specificity test against the assigned ER focus: APOE4 cells should not show increased XBP1 splicing, ATF4/CHOP protein induction or thapsigargin hypersensitivity relative to APOE3 under mock conditions. Clear constitutive UPR activation in APOE4 would favour an ER-proteostasis mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_105", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:ANXA1 +4.15), which we infer increases delivery of cholesterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system. Cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; inferred activity): the lysosomal hydrolytic/egress capacity per unit delivered lipid is exceeded. Acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are elevated far above the dataset background (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.70, gene:CTSK +7.40, gene:NAGLU +5.94, gene:HEXA +5.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.51, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:SLC37A2 +4.85, gene:ATP6V1H +6.94, gene:ATP6V1A +4.19, gene:ATP6V0C +3.53), but the matching hydrolase-candidate protein spots are not coordinately increased and several are significantly decreased (protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93). Enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and substrate clearance rate were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred transcriptional response): the shortfall engages MiT/TFE-family lysosomal biogenesis. gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) transcripts are elevated together with the CLEAR-type hydrolase/v-ATPase set (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.70, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.89). TFEB nuclear translocation and mTORC1 status were not measured; only transcript abundance is observed.", "Step 4 (inferred localization/flux): sterol and fatty acid released in the lysosome are not efficiently exported. gene:NPC2 rises only +1.17, far below the hydrolase mean, and no efflux/egress gene (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA) appears among the selected differential rows; because the source rows are a filtered DE list, absence is weak evidence, not a measurement of unchanged expression.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid pool): retained sterol/fatty acid is re-esterified and buffered into neutral-lipid stores, supported by gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:AGPAT2 (+6.29), gene:MGLL (+4.00) and a lipogenic desaturation arm gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SCD (+4.17), with oxysterol signalling from gene:CH25H (+1.62). Cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol and lipid-droplet content were not measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (inferred downstream state): the persistently loaded, transcriptionally hyperactivated lysosome coexists with an oxidative-metabolism transcript shift (gene:MDH1 +8.71, gene:OGDH +8.62, gene:MPC2 +8.02, gene:NDUFA5 +7.28) and reduced glycolytic gene:HK2 (-3.67), which we treat as a parallel or consequent state rather than the bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at the lysosomal lipid-catabolism/sterol-egress step, driving a compensatory TFEB/MITF CLEAR transcript program and SOAT1/DGAT1 sterol-ester storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23165953806971015, "cosine_similarity": 0.4366997007531447, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_105", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961035598705502, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23165953806971015, "cosine_similarity": 0.4366997007531447, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961035598705502, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.82534925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 20}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_099", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unstated logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive); only within-dataset relative position, not absolute fold change, is interpreted.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel features with multiple candidate genes; spot effects are treated as ambiguous evidence for a protein class (actin/actin-binding, annexin) and never as identification of a single protein.", "Transcript and spot abundance are assumed to be partial proxies for the size of the corresponding machinery pool; GTPase loading state, F-actin content, cup formation, acidification, uptake flux and lipid pools were not measured in this dataset.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so differences are attributed to genotype and its downstream state rather than to treatment.", "Astrocyte co-culture composition and any cell-composition drift are assumed not to be the sole source of the myeloid actin transcript down-shift.", "Background pharmacology and pathway membership statements are unverified prior knowledge; no literature or database was consulted."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-ordinately down-shift the myeloid actomyosin/Rho-GTPase engulfment module (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, SPN, ARHGAP30, FAM49B all negative against a strongly positive global RNA shift) while ARHGDIA (RhoGDI-1) is among the most increased transcripts, whereas surface uptake receptors and the acidic endolysosomal degradative machinery are increased. We hypothesise that the actin-dependent internalisation/closure step (phagocytic cup and macropinocytic cup), rather than lysosomal hydrolase capacity, is the rate-limiting node in APOE4 microglia, so that lipid entry is biased toward receptor-mediated soluble/lipoprotein uptake with esterification and storage rather than phagolysosomal catabolism of particulate, membrane-rich cargo. All activity, flux, localisation and directional statements are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Uptake assay: with pHrodo-labelled myelin, synaptosomes or 1-3 um beads, APOE4 microglia will internalise fewer particles per cell than APOE3 while 4 C surface binding of the same cargo is equal or higher, and cargo-filled cups will be more frequent per internalised particle by imaging. Equal or higher internalisation with equal binding in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: knockdown of ARHGDIA (or acute Rho/Rac activation) in APOE4 microglia should restore particle internalisation toward APOE3 levels within hours, before and without requiring changes in lysosomal hydrolase or v-ATPase transcripts; restoration of uptake only when hydrolase expression is also changed, or no restoration despite confirmed increased GTP-loaded Rac1/RhoA, would weaken the mechanism.", "Bottleneck localisation: blocking degradation (bafilomycin A1 or leupeptin/pepstatin) should cause a larger accumulation of undigested internalised cargo in APOE3 than in APOE4, because APOE4 flux is proposed to be uptake-limited. Greater accumulation in APOE4 would support a degradation-limited alternative and weaken this hypothesis.", "Lipid readout: APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet excess (BODIPY/LipidTOX) should be present in cargo-free medium and should be reduced by SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition or SCARB1/CD36 blockade, but not by restoring engulfment alone. Droplet excess that appears only after particulate cargo feeding, or that is abolished by ARHGDIA knockdown alone, would weaken the proposed rerouting step.", "Spot-identity test: immunoblot or targeted MS of the ANXA1/TALDO1 spot series (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:047) should show increased ANXA1 (consistent with gene:ANXA1 +4.2) and no increase in TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 is negative). If TALDO1 accounts for those spots, the receptor/annexin arm of the argument loses its cross-modality support.", "Functional cytoskeletal state: APOE4 cells should show reduced phalloidin-positive cortical/cup F-actin and reduced phospho-myosin light chain at contact sites despite equal or higher Arp2/3 subunit protein. Unchanged or increased cup F-actin and pMLC would weaken step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 lowers transcripts of the contractile/monomer-supply arm of the myeloid actin machinery relative to the global upward RNA shift (gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:SPN -7.3, gene:RAC2 -2.0, gene:DOCK8 -2.0, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.2, gene:FAM49B -5.8; 16/36 curated cytoskeletal genes below zero vs 23% genome-wide in these selected rows, binomial P=0.0035), while gene:ARHGDIA (RhoGDI-1, a sequestering inhibitor of Rho/Rac/Cdc42) is the third-highest transcript in the dataset (+10.6).", "Inferred (not measured): a larger RhoGDI-bound cytosolic GTPase pool plus reduced non-muscle myosin II and actin monomer supply lowers the sustained, contractile F-actin work available at nascent phagocytic/macropinocytic cups, even though branched-nucleator transcripts (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5) and actin/capping/severing-containing 2-D spots (protein_spot:036, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:056, protein_spot:063, protein_spot:081, protein_spot:092) are up; a highly capped, short-filament network is inferred to favour ruffling over cup closure.", "Recognition capacity is not the limiting element: uptake and tethering receptor transcripts are at or above the global shift (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:ITGB1 +6.3, gene:ANXA1 +4.2, gene:SIRPA, gene:CD47, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2), and ANXA1-containing spots are the most increased protein spots (protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:043).", "The downstream degradative compartment is expanded rather than deficient: v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSD), late-endosomal/sorting components (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:CHMP4B, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1, gene:PIK3C3) and gene:TFEB are increased, so inferred acidification and hydrolytic capacity exceed the inferred rate of cargo delivery.", "With particulate delivery inferred to be throttled, lipid influx is predicted to proceed through receptor-mediated soluble/lipoprotein routes and be stored: scavenger and lipogenic/esterifying transcripts rise (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE), predicting neutral-lipid droplet accumulation that is independent of phagocytic cargo.", "Elevated TCA/mitochondrial carrier transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A46; set mean +5.4, permutation P\u003c0.001) are read as catabolic capacity aimed at soluble substrates, consistent with an uptake-limited rather than a digestion-limited state."], "title": "An actomyosin-restrained engulfment step, not degradative capacity, limits cargo flux in APOE4 microglia and reroutes lipid handling to receptor-mediated uptake and esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29507617317479834, "cosine_similarity": 0.4359679245780776, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5768802588996764, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29507617317479834, "cosine_similarity": 0.4359679245780776, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5768802588996764, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61517225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 21}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_094", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, assembled from a longer up-column and a shorter down-column), so the 77% positive fraction is a list-construction artifact; directional enrichment is therefore judged only relative to the other genes in the same list, and the logarithm base of the reported effects is unspecified and left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance differences for nuclear-encoded subunits, carriers and enzymes are assumed to translate into proportional protein and transport-capacity differences; no OXPHOS, MPC, SLC25A1 or lipogenic protein was uniquely measured here.", "The lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to indicate a genuine deficit in mtDNA-encoded subunit supply rather than a normalisation/composition effect of single-cell pseudobulk, a difference in mitochondrial mass, or probe-panel/QC filtering.", "Cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation from exported citrate is assumed to occur (ACLY was not in the supplied rows), and increased citrate-carrier transcript is assumed to increase actual citrate efflux.", "The protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30, and astrocyte co-culture contributes equally to both genotypes."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia, the transcriptional program that imports carbon into mitochondria (pyruvate via MPC2/PDH, glutamine-aspartate anaplerosis, malate-aspartate shuttle) is coordinately raised together with every detected nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit, while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are not co-raised (mostly lower). We hypothesise that the resulting sub-stoichiometric supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not substrate supply, is the rate-limiting step for terminal oxidation, so TCA-cycle carbon that cannot be fully oxidised leaves the matrix as citrate through the up-regulated citrate carrier and feeds a SREBP-type sterol/fatty-acid and esterification program, producing the neutral-lipid accumulation phenotype. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; assembly state, respiration, flux and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown) should lower neutral-lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester content substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, and should raise the fraction of glucose/glutamine carbon oxidised to CO2. If APOE4 lipid content is unchanged or falls equally in both genotypes, the citrate-export step of the mechanism is wrong.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20 signal) should show lower ATP-linked and lower FCCP-uncoupled oxygen flux in APOE4 despite the higher nuclear subunit transcripts, and BN-PAGE/immunoblot should show a reduced mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded subunit ratio (e.g. MT-CO1 or MT-ATP6 protein versus ATP5F1B or NDUFB8) with reduced assembled complex I/IV. Equal or higher mass-normalised maximal respiration and an unchanged mitonuclear protein ratio would falsify the assembly-bottleneck claim.", "Stable-isotope tracing with U-13C glucose and 13C5 glutamine should show, in APOE4, unchanged or reduced lactate m+3 labelling (consistent with lower gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP) but increased 13C enrichment of citrate and of the cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol fractions. If the labelled lipid carbon in APOE4 comes predominantly from exogenous fatty-acid uptake with no increase in glucose- or glutamine-derived lipid label, the carbon-routing claim is weakened.", "Blocking mitochondrial pyruvate entry (UK5099) should reduce, not increase, APOE4 lipid droplet accumulation; if lipid accumulation increases upon MPC inhibition, pyruvate-derived citrate is not the main lipid carbon source.", "Artifact control: spike-in-normalised or absolute quantification (qPCR/ddPCR of MT-ATP6, MT-CO2 versus NDUFB8, ATP5F1B, with mtDNA copy number) should reproduce the divergent mitonuclear transcript pattern; if spike-normalised measurement shows no divergence, the pattern was a pseudobulk composition artifact and the hypothesis loses its primary premise.", "Restoring respiratory capacity (e.g. raising mitochondrial complex assembly or providing an alternative electron sink such as NDI1-type bypass) should reduce APOE4-specific droplet accumulation without reducing the nuclear OXPHOS transcript program; unchanged lipid content under restored respiration would weaken the causal chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia raise the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program: all 37 detected structural subunits of complexes I, II, III, IV and V and cytochrome c are higher (e.g. gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:CYCS), along with protein-import and mitochondrial-translation machinery (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:OXA1L, gene:TUFM). Measured: mRNA abundance. Inferred: an increased drive toward mitochondrial biogenesis.", "The mtDNA-encoded core subunits are not co-regulated with this program: gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 and gene:MT-CO2 are lower while only gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 are higher. Inferred (not measured): a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch in which mtDNA-encoded cores limit assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V, making terminal oxidation the pathway bottleneck rather than substrate availability.", "Carbon delivery into the matrix is simultaneously increased: mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating components (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD), glutamine/amino-acid anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:BCAT2), TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G) and the malate-aspartate/oxoglutarate shuttle (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13) are all higher, whereas the committed upper-glycolysis steps gene:HK2, gene:HK3 and gene:PFKP are lower despite higher glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3). Inferred: glucose and glutamine carbon is directed toward the matrix rather than toward glycolytic lactate output.", "With oxidation of NADH and acetyl-CoA constrained by assembly-limited complexes, matrix citrate accumulates and is exported through the up-regulated citrate/isocitrate carrier gene:SLC25A1; an acetate-scavenging route (gene:ACSS2) is also higher. Inferred flux; the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool and ACLY were not measured in this dataset.", "Cytosolic acetyl-CoA supports a lipogenic/sterologenic program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1) that is combined with increased lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR) and esterification/storage capacity (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CIDEB). Inferred: net flux into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets.", "Chronic handling of this lipid load is reflected in a coordinately raised lysosomal/hydrolase program (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) and a stress marker (gene:DDIT3), consistent with, but not proof of, an increased catabolic burden that further favours storage over oxidation."], "title": "Assembly-limited terminal oxidation in APOE4 microglia reroutes mitochondrial carbon from ATP production to citrate export and lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11448140900195694, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28656763416145187, "cosine_similarity": 0.43567669035954504, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5743300970873786, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11448140900195694, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28656763416145187, "cosine_similarity": 0.43567669035954504, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5743300970873786, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97193175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 22}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_034", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not stated in the source; all RNA effects are used as signed, rank-comparable 'reported log fold change' values only, never as literal fold changes.", "The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. LDHA, PDHA1, TFAM, MPC1, all mitoribosome genes) means it failed that filter and must not be read as 'unchanged' or as evidence.", "The dataset-wide upward shift (77.1% of rows positive, median +1.46) is treated as a possible normalisation/compositional offset; pathway claims therefore rest on rank position relative to this background and on the internal nuclear-vs-mtDNA discordance, not on raw sign.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein abundance, and protein abundance a partial proxy for enzyme activity and flux; no metabolite, respirometry, mtDNA copy-number, complex-assembly or localisation measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D-gel features (mean ~4.8 candidate genes per spot); no spot lists an OXPHOS or mtDNA-encoded candidate, so the protein modality neither supports nor refutes the mitochondrial core of this hypothesis and is used only for the glycolytic-enzyme spots, whose identity remains ambiguous.", "Single-cell (10X Flex) quantification of mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed here to reflect biology rather than QC filtering on percent-mitochondrial reads, ambient RNA from the astrocyte co-culture, or probe-panel behaviour; this assumption is untested in the supplied data and is the weakest link in the chain.", "Both genotypes are assumed isogenic and equally represented in cell state, so the signal is assumed not to be driven mainly by a different microglial substate composition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally expand nuclear-encoded mitochondrial carbon-entry, TCA and electron-transport-chain (ETC) subunit programmes while committed upper-glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP) are reduced and mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are not co-upregulated. We hypothesise that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not substrate delivery, is the rate-limiting step for assembled holo-complex III/IV/V capacity, so that pyruvate and glutamine carbon imported into the matrix exceeds terminal oxidative capacity and is preferentially exported as citrate (SLC25A1) toward lipid/sterol esterification, with little glycolytic ATP reserve to buffer the shortfall. Causality is not established; all statements about flux, assembly and localisation are inferred from transcript abundance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) should reduce oxygen consumption and neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, whereas glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) should have a comparatively smaller differential effect. If UK5099 produces equal or smaller differential effects than CB-839, or leaves APOE4 lipid load unchanged, Steps 2 and 5 are wrong.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show reduced assembled complex IV and V (and CIII) holo-complex per unit mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 or citrate-synthase normalised), with an increased free/sub-assembly pool of nuclear-encoded subunits. Normal holo-complex stoichiometry despite higher nuclear subunit protein would falsify the primary bottleneck (Step 4).", "Extracellular-flux assay: APOE4 microglia should show equal or higher basal OCR but disproportionately lower FCCP-stimulated maximal OCR and spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass, together with a blunted oligomycin-induced glycolytic compensation (ECAR reserve) reflecting reduced HK2/PFKP capacity. Higher maximal OCR in APOE4 scaling with the nuclear ETC transcript increase would weaken the mechanism.", "13C tracing: with [U-13C]glucose, APOE4 should show preserved or increased m+2 citrate labelling but a lower ratio of 13CO2 release (or of m+4/m+2 second-turn TCA labelling) to 13C incorporation into fatty acids and sterol esters, relative to APOE3. Equal partitioning of label between CO2 and lipid would falsify Step 5.", "Independent measurement of mtDNA-encoded expression (mtDNA copy number, MT-CO1/MT-ATP6 RT-qPCR and MTCO1 protein, and mitochondrial translation by 35S or puromycin labelling with cytoplasmic translation blocked) should confirm reduced mtDNA-encoded product per nuclear-encoded subunit in APOE4. Equal or higher mtDNA-encoded protein per mitochondrion would falsify Step 4 and, with it, the mitonuclear-imbalance bottleneck.", "Rescue test of direction: increasing mtDNA-encoded core supply (for example TFAM or LRPPRC overexpression, or nicotinamide-riboside-driven biogenesis) should raise assembled CIV/CV and reduce lipid droplet burden in APOE4 without normalising the nuclear-encoded ETC transcript excess. Rescue of lipid burden without any change in assembled complexes would indicate a lipid-handling bottleneck instead of an oxidative one.", "Negative/control prediction: the effect should be substrate-conditional - in galactose medium (which forces oxidative ATP production) APOE4 microglia should show a larger viability/ATP deficit than APOE3, while in high-glucose medium the two should differ little. Equal galactose sensitivity would weaken Steps 1 and 4 jointly."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia reduce transcripts for the committed, ATP-consuming entry steps of glycolysis and the oxidative PPP branch (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:HK3 -1.1, gene:PGD -1.3, gene:TALDO1 -2.3) while hexose transporter transcripts rise (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3); we infer glucose uptake is maintained but glucose-6-phosphate is diverted from committed glycolysis toward glycogen/lysosomal glycan turnover (gene:GYS1 +6.1, gene:UGP2, gene:GAA +10.0), lowering glycolytic ATP and lactate-generating reserve.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Mitochondrial carbon entry is transcriptionally favoured - mitochondrial pyruvate carrier (gene:MPC2 +8.0), PDH-activating phosphatase (gene:PDP1) and the shared E3 subunit (gene:DLD) rise, together with glutamine/glutamate anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC1A5) and matrix exchangers (gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A5). Inferred: more acetyl-CoA and 2-oxoglutarate enter the TCA cycle per cell.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): The TCA cycle and every nuclear-encoded ETC complex are coherently up (gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB, gene:CYCS; 38/38 detected NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH transcripts positive), as are protein import and assembly factors (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:TUFM, gene:COA1, gene:COA8, gene:NDUFAF4). Inferred: an enlarged nuclear-encoded mitochondrial proteome is being built.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred assembly): The mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores do not follow this expansion and are mostly reduced (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.4, gene:MT-CYB -2.3, gene:MT-ND4 -1.8, gene:MT-CO2 -1.3) against a dataset-wide upward RNA shift. Because each of complexes I, III, IV and V requires mtDNA-encoded catalytic subunits, we infer a stoichiometric mismatch in which imported nuclear subunits cannot be assembled into holo-complexes; assembled CIII/CIV/CV capacity, not subunit supply from the nucleus, becomes the flux-limiting step.", "Step 5 (inferred flux/localisation): With terminal oxidation capped, matrix citrate accumulates and is exported via the citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1 +4.5) into a lipogenic/sterol-esterifying programme (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:SCARB1), converting oxidisable carbon into stored neutral lipid and cholesteryl ester rather than CO2 and ATP.", "Step 6 (inferred stress consequence): Unassembled ETC subunits and a reduced ATP margin (no glycolytic reserve from Step 1) produce mild proteostatic/energy-stress signalling (gene:DDIT3, gene:ATF6, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:PRKAA1) and increased lysosomal/degradative load (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A), which we propose is the proximate driver of the APOE4 lipid-laden, low-reserve microglial state."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry limits terminal oxidation in APOE4 microglia: carbon is routed into mitochondria faster than mtDNA-encoded ETC cores can be supplied"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10078277886497064, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3001270339787777, "cosine_similarity": 0.4347957987628146, "direction_accuracy": 0.16828478964401294, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5790841423948221, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10078277886497064, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3001270339787777, "cosine_similarity": 0.4347957987628146, "direction_accuracy": 0.16828478964401294, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5790841423948221, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79419625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 23}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_040", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) and are not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore relative to the internal background of that list, whose median effect is already +1.46.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no fold changes are converted or compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot values.", "Protein spots are two-dimensional gel features with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are read only as evidence about proteoform heterogeneity, not about total protein abundance of a named gene.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate with, but not to demonstrate, enzyme activity, subcellular localization, or metabolic flux; all flux, localization and sensing statements in the mechanism are inferred.", "Key controls of the proposed bottleneck (LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2/PLIN3, GRN, PSAP, MCOLN1, TMEM175) are absent from the supplied list, so the bottleneck is inferred from the surrounding module rather than from a measured transport step.", "No lipid, cholesterol, ROS, lysosomal pH or degradative-flux measurement is supplied in this discovery set; the 'to_lipid' framing of the experiment identifier is not evidence.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes at day 30; astrocyte-derived lipid supply is assumed comparable between genotypes, which was not measured.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the effect magnitudes (some exceeding 8 in unspecified log units, and uncorrelated with adjusted p-value, Spearman -0.03) may be inflated by low replication or by a normalization offset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a bottleneck in lysosomal lipid catabolism and lysosome-to-ER sterol egress, not by an oxidative-stress or peroxisomal defect: the discovery data show a coordinated, above-background induction of the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program together with a uniformly upregulated lipid-uptake, sterol-synthesis and esterification module, a combination expected when internalized lipid is retained in the endolysosome so that the ER sterol sensor continues to read 'low' and newly made sterol/monounsaturated fatty acid is diverted by SOAT1/DGAT1 into stored neutral lipid. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester droplet content, raise the ER-accessible sterol pool, and thereby selectively collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of SREBP targets (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR) while leaving or worsening the lysosomal lipid load; if SREBP targets stay elevated in APOE4 after esterification is blocked, step 4-5 of the chain is wrong.", "Functional flux test: with DQ-BSA and BODIPY-labelled lipoprotein, APOE4 microglia should show more LysoTracker-positive/neutral-lipid-positive volume but lower dequenching per lysosome than APOE3 (reduced degradative flux despite higher hydrolase transcript); equal or higher per-lysosome degradative flux in APOE4 would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts in both genotypes but should increase stored/lysosomal lipid disproportionately in APOE4; if TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid load in APOE4, the CLEAR induction is driving rather than compensating for the phenotype.", "Epistasis/phenocopy test: loading APOE3 microglia with LDL or with a lysosomal lipase/NPC1 inhibitor (e.g. U18666A) should reproduce the APOE4 signature (coordinate CLEAR + SREBP + SOAT1/DGAT1 induction); failure to phenocopy would argue for an APOE4-specific mechanism outside lysosomal lipid handling.", "Redox counter-test (would weaken this hypothesis and revive the assigned focus): if APOE4 microglia show elevated mitochondrial or cytosolic ROS reporters, an activated NRF2 target program (HMOX1, NQO1, GCLM, TXNRD1) and catalase/peroxisomal deficits, while lysosomal neutral lipid and DQ-BSA flux are indistinguishable from APOE3, the lysosomal-bottleneck mechanism should be rejected in favour of an oxidative-stress-primary mechanism.", "Directionality test: acute rescue of lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer (NPC2 supplementation or cyclodextrin) in APOE4 should normalize SREBP-target transcripts within hours without first normalizing hydrolase transcripts; simultaneous or reversed kinetics would weaken the proposed order of steps 2-4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer - but did not measure - increases delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesteryl ester and phospholipid into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; inferred activity): The rate of lysosomal hydrolysis of this lipid cargo and its subsequent egress to the ER is limiting in APOE4. Delivery/fusion and hydrolase-sorting components are discordant with the biogenesis program (gene:STX17 -2.06, gene:M6PR -1.72 versus gene:IGF2R +2.02), and the cathepsin-containing two-dimensional protein spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85), which is consistent with a shift in proteoform/maturation state rather than a uniform increase in mature hydrolase. Hydrolytic flux itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred causal direction): The retained substrate load elicits a compensatory MiT/TFE-driven CLEAR response - lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are induced well above the global shift of this differential-expression list (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:CTSD +2.86; set mean 2.57 versus 1.37 for all other genes).", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing state): Because lipid-derived sterol does not reach the ER pool efficiently, the SREBP program is not switched off despite lipid loading (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06); all 16 members of this uptake/synthesis module are positive, which is unlikely under the 77 percent-up background of this list.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Newly made monounsaturated fatty acid and sterol are channelled to esterification (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72), which we infer diverts lipid into cytoplasmic droplets and further away from oxidation; droplet mass, cholesteryl ester and free cholesterol were not measured here.", "Step 6 (interpretation): The resulting steady state - expanded but flux-limited lysosomes plus esterified lipid storage - is the distinguishing APOE4 feature, while antioxidant/peroxisomal transcripts show no enrichment beyond the global shift and therefore do not support an oxidative-stress-primary explanation."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-catabolism/egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia drives compensatory CLEAR-program induction and SREBP-driven re-esterification into stored lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24035372743049144, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19676478599932778, "cosine_similarity": 0.43475982965745513, "direction_accuracy": 0.38673139158576053, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5820582524271845, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24035372743049144, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19676478599932778, "cosine_similarity": 0.43475982965745513, "direction_accuracy": 0.38673139158576053, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5820582524271845, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.95607825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 24}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_029", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77% positive, median +1.46), so only within-list rank comparisons against the list background are interpreted; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and magnitudes are not converted or treated as linear fold changes.", "Set-level rank enrichment (permutation against the supplied list) reflects coordinated regulation rather than a shared technical bias such as gene length, detection rate or ambient RNA in the 10X Flex pseudobulk comparison.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for lysosomal and biosynthetic enzyme capacity; enzyme activity, TFEB and SREBP nuclear localization, membrane trafficking flux and lipid pools were not measured here and are inferred.", "2D protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-unique; a spot is never claimed to identify a single protein, and the protein layer also shows a global upward shift (70% of spots positive), so spot direction alone is weak evidence.", "NPC1, STARD3, ORP/GRAMD sterol transporters, ABCA1 and lipid species are absent from the supplied data; the egress bottleneck is a proposed, currently untested node inferred from the absence of a coordinate increase in the measured egress-adjacent genes.", "Astrocytes in the co-culture supply APOE-containing lipoproteins; the microglial genotype effect is assumed to act cell-autonomously plus through altered astrocyte-derived particle quality, which this design cannot separate.", "Isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison under mock treatment; causal direction between the lysosomal program, sterol synthesis and lipid load has not been established by these observations."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by an endolysosomal lipid-handling imbalance rather than by altered phagocytic or actin uptake machinery: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, late-endosome maturation factors and glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolism are coordinately elevated above the list-wide shift, yet ER sterol-sensing output (SREBP target transcripts) is simultaneously elevated. We propose that transfer of lipoprotein-derived cholesterol from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER is rate-limiting in APOE4, so cells expand degradative capacity (TFEB/MITF-type program) while the ER continues to report a sterol deficit and drives futile de novo sterol and fatty-acid synthesis. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; lysosomal lipid content, transcription-factor activity and flux are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: Delivering cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool with cholesterol/methyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which bypasses the lysosome) should suppress SREBP target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, SREBF2) in APOE4 microglia down to APOE3 levels, whereas an equivalent sterol dose delivered as LDL/APOE lipoprotein (lysosome-routed) should suppress them substantially less in APOE4 than in APOE3. If both routes suppress SREBP targets equally in APOE4, the lysosome-to-ER egress bottleneck is falsified.", "Filipin or ORP-based sterol imaging should show more free cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions, with a larger LAMP1 volume per cell. Equal lysosomal free-cholesterol density between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Acute NPC1 inhibition (U18666A) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy APOE4 by raising both arms together (CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts and SREBP targets). If NPC1 inhibition raises only the CLEAR arm and lowers SREBP targets, step 4-to-step 5 coupling is wrong.", "TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1A) in APOE4 without normalizing the SREBP target set; if SREBP targets normalize in parallel, the two programs are one TFEB-driven output rather than sequential steps.", "REJECTION TEST FOR THE ASSIGNED FOCUS: Short-pulse internalization of fluorescent beads, myelin or pHrodo-zymosan per cell should not be markedly lower in APOE4 (predicted \u003c25% difference at early timepoints), while degradation of an internalized quenched substrate (DQ-BSA, pHrodo myelin over hours) per unit internalized should be reduced. A clear early internalization deficit with normal lysosomal cholesterol would favour the alternative actin/phagocytic mechanism over this one.", "Lipidomics of sorted APOE4 microglia should show increased cholesteryl ester and glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin species relative to APOE3 under mock treatment; unchanged sterol-ester and sphingolipid pools despite the transcriptional program would weaken the claim of an actual lipid-handling imbalance."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (inferred, not measured): APOE4-associated lipoprotein cargo from the microglia/astrocyte co-culture continues to enter microglia by receptor-mediated endocytosis. Measured receptor transcripts (LDLR, SCARB1, CD36, MERTK, TREM2, C1QA/B/C) are present in the differential list but sit at or below the list-wide positive shift (mean percentile ~0.48), so uptake capacity is inferred to be maintained, not increased; no uptake flux was measured.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA, activity inferred): A coherent CLEAR-type lysosomal program is higher in APOE4 (mean percentile 0.633, permutation p_up=0.0095): TFEB and MITF transcripts, v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V0D1/D2, ATP6V1C1/E1/F) and hydrolases (GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, CTSB, CTSD, GLA, MAN2B1, SGSH). We infer increased lysosomal biogenesis and acidification capacity; TFEB nuclear localization and v-ATPase assembly were not measured.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA, flux inferred): Sphingolipid catabolic transcripts are the most strongly shifted small set (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, GBA2, HEXB, ST3GAL5, SUMF1, CERS6; mean percentile 0.728, p_up=0.0135), together with late-endosome maturation and retrieval components (RAB7A, WDR91, MON1B, PIK3C3, VPS26A, SNX3, IGF2R). We infer elevated luminal sphingolipid turnover that liberates free cholesterol and ceramide inside late endosomes/lysosomes.", "STEP 4 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK; inferred, partly unmeasured): Export of the liberated sterol from the lysosomal lumen to the ER does not scale with steps 2-3. NPC1, STARD3 and ORP/GRAMD sterol-transfer proteins are absent from the supplied differential list (unmeasured); NPC2 is only marginally up (+1.2, below the list median of +1.46) and the hydrolase-sorting receptor M6PR is down (-1.7) while IGF2R is up (+2.0), i.e. no coordinate increase in the egress arm. We therefore predict sterol and ceramide retention in the endolysosomal compartment; no lipid pool was measured in this dataset.", "STEP 5 (measured RNA, activity inferred): The ER sterol sensor consequently reports a cholesterol deficit: SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, SCD and ERLIN1 are elevated above the list-wide shift (mean percentile 0.648, p_up=0.031). We infer SCAP/SREBP processing is increased; cleaved SREBP protein was not measured.", "STEP 6 (predicted consequence): Continued synthesis (SCD, ACAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, SCP2) plus retained lysosomal lipid produces esterified-lipid/droplet accumulation and reduced free degradative reserve per lysosome in APOE4, a degradation/egress-limited state rather than an uptake-limited one. Cytoskeletal and phagocytic machinery show no coordinate increase (actin/Arp2/3/myosin set mean percentile 0.426, p_up=0.90), so the assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal focus is rejected as the primary mechanism."], "title": "Lysosome-to-ER sterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a TFEB-type lysosomal/sphingolipid-catabolic expansion coexists with an activated SREBP sterol-synthesis program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15753424657534246, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19053282083943923, "cosine_similarity": 0.4341019862433467, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6008705501618123, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15753424657534246, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19053282083943923, "cosine_similarity": 0.4341019862433467, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6008705501618123, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61585225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 25}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_021", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; module means are therefore judged against the list background (mean +1.39, 77.1% positive, |effect| \u003e= 1 filter) and not against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative ranking and sign are used.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding enzyme activity and metabolic flux; no protein, activity, metabolite, isotope-tracing or imaging measurement of lipid pools is supplied.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes (keratins and actins dominate the candidate lists) and are treated as ambiguous, weak corroboration only, never as identified proteins.", "Absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, FASN, ACLY, PLIN2, CPT1A, LIPA and PNPLA2 from the list is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change; the efflux arm in particular is largely unmeasured.", "Genotype effects are assumed cell-intrinsic to microglia, although astrocyte co-culture and 10X Flex compositional/ambient-RNA effects could contribute; replicate structure is not supplied, so the direction is treated as associative, not causally established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally configure a lipid-anabolic state: mitochondrial carbon/citrate export and NADPH-supply transcripts, ACSS2, SREBF1/SREBF2 and their sterol and fatty-acid desaturation targets, and lipid-uptake receptors (notably SCARB1) are coordinately higher than in APOE3, while fatty-acid activation/oxidation transcripts are not (ACSL4, ACSL5 lower; oxidation module at background). The primary bottleneck we propose is that oxidative/exportive disposal of acquired and newly synthesized lipid does not scale with the increased input, so flux is inferred to be routed into glycerolipid/sterol-ester assembly and lipid-transfer steps (AGPAT2, SCP2, DGAT1, SOAT1), producing excess neutral-lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester) stores; the coordinately elevated lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB transcripts are interpreted as a coupled downstream response to that lipid load rather than the initiating lesion. Lipid pools, enzyme activities, fluxes and causal direction were not measured here and are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Neutral-lipid phenotype: mock APOE4 microglia should show greater BODIPY/LipidTOX droplet area per cell and higher triacylglycerol plus cholesteryl-ester mass than isogenic APOE3, with a higher monounsaturated:saturated acyl ratio (16:1/16:0, 18:1/18:0) consistent with elevated gene:SCD. Equal or lower TAG+CE and droplet area in APOE4 would falsify the core claim.", "Discriminating perturbation: blocking the anabolic arm (fatostatin or SCAP/SREBF1 knockdown, or combined ACSS2/ACLY inhibition) should remove the majority of the APOE4-minus-APOE3 excess in droplet area and cholesteryl ester while leaving the lysosomal transcript elevation (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB) largely intact; if instead only lysosomal blockade (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/HEXA knockdown) alters the genotype gap and SREBP blockade does not, the primary bottleneck is lysosomal lipid catabolism and this mechanism is wrong.", "Uptake arm: SCARB1 knockdown or culture in lipoprotein-deficient medium should shrink the APOE4-versus-APOE3 cholesteryl-ester gap by a measurable fraction; an unchanged gap would refute the uptake step while leaving the de novo synthesis step open.", "Flux versus abundance: 13C-acetate and U-13C-glucose tracing should show higher labelling of palmitate, oleate and newly synthesized cholesterol in APOE4; equal labelling despite the elevated transcripts would show the transcript-to-flux assumption fails.", "Disposal bottleneck: APOE4 microglia should show equal or lower etomoxir-sensitive fatty-acid oxidation and lower fatty-acid-driven respiration than APOE3; higher fatty-acid oxidation in APOE4 would weaken the proposed disposal bottleneck.", "Specificity of the mitochondrial arm: if nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript elevation reflects genuine biogenesis rather than biosynthetic carbon export, APOE4 should also show increased mitochondrial mass and maximal respiration; increased respiration together with unchanged lipid stores would favour a bioenergetic rather than a lipid-overflow mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate handling and NADPH supply are higher in APOE4 (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACO2, gene:MDH1, gene:NNT, gene:ME1); inferred: greater availability of cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH for lipogenesis (no metabolite or flux measurement supplied).", "Measured: gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1 and gene:SREBF2 and their downstream sterol and desaturation enzymes (gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) are higher in APOE4; inferred: increased SREBP-pathway transcriptional output and de novo fatty-acid/sterol synthesis capacity (SREBP cleavage and enzyme activity not measured).", "Measured: lipid-acquisition receptor transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of this differential-expression list, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2); inferred: increased uptake of astrocyte- and serum-derived lipoprotein lipid in the co-culture.", "Measured: fatty-acid activation/oxidation transcripts are not coordinately raised (gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 decreased; the oxidation/lipolysis module mean is at or below the list background); inferred bottleneck: catabolic disposal capacity fails to match the elevated lipid input.", "Measured: glycerolipid/sterol esterification and intracellular sterol-transfer transcripts are elevated (gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCP2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1); inferred: the excess acyl and sterol carbon is esterified and stored, i.e. increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester content in lipid droplets (droplets and lipid species were not measured).", "Measured: lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and the MiT/TFE factor are elevated (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB), with weak, non-unique protein-spot signals whose candidate lists include cathepsins (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053); inferred: expansion of the lysosomal compartment as a coupled response to the lipid load, downstream of and not upstream of the anabolic overflow.", "Net inferred phenotype: APOE4 microglia carry a larger neutral-lipid and lysosomal lipid burden than isogenic APOE3 microglia at baseline, with the lipogenic/uptake arm as the causal driver to be tested."], "title": "Anabolic lipid overflow: citrate/acetyl-CoA-fed SREBP lipogenesis plus elevated lipid uptake, with unmatched fatty-acid oxidative disposal, drives neutral-lipid storage and a compensatory lysosomal program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1506849315068493, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24627386428346493, "cosine_similarity": 0.43229189108082444, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5735404530744336, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1506849315068493, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24627386428346493, "cosine_similarity": 0.43229189108082444, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5735404530744336, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.14263775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 26}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_056", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression set (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive), not an unbiased transcriptome; module statistics are therefore computed as rank comparisons within this list, and the absence of interferon-stimulated rows may partly reflect selection rather than true absence.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified, so magnitudes are treated as ordinal/relative and only directional coherence is interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for machinery availability; enzymatic activity, complex assembly, mitochondrial membrane potential, respiratory flux, mtDNA copy number, TFEB localisation and lipid pools were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and cannot identify a unique protein; they are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration (e.g. spot 067 down contains CTSB/HEXB, spot 053 up contains CTSD).", "The uniform positive shift of the list could partly reflect normalisation or compositional differences between APOE4 and APOE3 libraries; the mitonuclear inference relies on the discordant direction of mtDNA-encoded rows, which is itself sensitive to mitochondrial-transcript capture in a probe-based 10X Flex assay.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes at a single day-30 mock timepoint, so genotype-driven cell-intrinsic changes cannot be separated from astrocyte-mediated non-cell-autonomous effects, and no replicate count is supplied.", "No causal direction has been established by these data; the ordering of steps is a proposed model."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia mount a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lysosomal degradative machinery and of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery, while mtDNA-encoded respiratory-chain transcripts are not co-elevated; we propose that the resulting mitonuclear subunit imbalance limits assembly of complexes I/III/IV/V, so that lysosome-derived lipid catabolism is not matched by terminal oxidation and carbon is diverted into esterification and de novo lipogenesis. Interferon/inflammatory signalling is not the differentiating mechanism in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating measurement: in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, blue-native PAGE/complexome or paired immunoblot should show an increased ratio of nuclear-encoded to mtDNA-encoded respiratory subunit protein (e.g. NDUFB8 or ATP5F1B relative to MT-CO1/MT-ND1) of at least ~1.3-fold, with assembled complex I and IV holoenzyme levels and maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) oxygen consumption per mitochondrial mass equal to or lower in APOE4 despite the elevated nuclear transcripts. If assembled complexes and maximal respiration instead increase in proportion to the nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase, the assembly-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or POLRMT overexpression, or restoring mtDNA copy number) should selectively in APOE4 increase assembled complex I/IV and maximal respiration, and partially normalise both the nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcript elevation and the lysosomal/lipogenic transcript elevation. If mtDNA transcripts rise but respiration, lipid droplet content and the nuclear compensatory program are unchanged, the mechanism is weakened.", "Substrate-source test: blocking lysosomal acid lipolysis (lalistat/LIPA inhibition) or v-ATPase acidification (bafilomycin A1) should collapse the excess nuclear mitochondrial-catabolic transcript program in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; persistence of that program under lysosomal blockade would indicate a lysosome-independent driver and weaken step 1.", "Interferon-rejection test: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade under mock conditions should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal and OXPHOS transcript differences essentially unchanged. If JAK inhibition normalises these differences, the rejection of the interferon/inflammatory mechanism is wrong.", "Flux prediction: 13C-palmitate or 13C-glucose tracing should show reduced fractional oxidation to CO2/TCA labelling with increased label incorporation into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in APOE4; equal or higher fractional oxidation in APOE4 would falsify step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred cause): APOE4 microglia show a coherent increase in lysosomal hydrolase, sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid catabolic and v-ATPase transcripts together with TFEB transcript (24/25 curated lysosomal rows positive, mean +3.04 reported-log units, Mann-Whitney p=5.3e-3 against all other differential rows), consistent with - but not proof of - an increased lysosomal substrate/lipid load and CLEAR-network engagement; TFEB nuclear localisation and lysosomal lipid content were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): In parallel, every curated nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit row is elevated (37/37 positive, mean +2.81, Mann-Whitney p=1.3e-4; complex I 21/21, complex IV 6/6, complex V 7/7), with TCA-cycle (ACO2, OGDH, MDH1, DLD, SDHB, all positive) and mitochondrial protein-import rows (TOMM22, TIMM8B, HSPA9) also positive - a transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial catabolic capacity that exceeds the strong global positive shift of this selected differential list.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, discordant direction): mtDNA-encoded transcripts are not co-elevated and are mostly reduced (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; 4/6 negative versus 77% positive in the list overall, binomial p=0.028), while mtDNA-expression machinery is barely represented (only TUFM).", "Step 4 (inferred stoichiometry, not measured): Because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded core subunits, we infer that assembled holo-complex formation, not nuclear subunit supply, becomes the rate-limiting step; the predicted state is an elevated nuclear:mtDNA-encoded subunit protein ratio with unassembled subunit turnover and no proportional gain in respiratory flux.", "Step 5 (inferred flux consequence): Lysosomal delivery of lipid catabolites therefore outpaces terminal beta-oxidation and oxidative phosphorylation, and the excess acyl-CoA/sterol pool is re-routed into esterification and lipogenic storage, consistent with the elevated SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), DGAT1 (+1.72), SOAT1 (+1.25), LDLR (+1.50) and INSIG1 (+1.87) rows; lipid droplets, flux and acyl-CoA pools were not measured here.", "Step 6 (negative arm, measured absence): The differentiating signal is not interferon-driven; canonical type I/II interferon-stimulated rows (MX1/2, OAS family, ISG15, IFIT family, IFI6/27/44L, RSAD2, USP18, BST2, STAT1/2, IRF7/9, GBP1/2, CXCL9-11, PSMB8/9, TAP1) are absent from the 2212 differential RNA rows apart from CD74 (+3.84) and TMEM173 (+1.22), and the curated NF-kB target set is indistinguishable from the global background (11 rows, mean +1.45 versus list mean +1.39, z=+0.08), so chemokine rows such as CXCL8 (+3.11) and CXCL16 (+3.66) are better explained by the global shift than by a coherent inflammatory module."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry, not transcript supply, bottlenecks the expanded lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12133072407045009, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26474539191489044, "cosine_similarity": 0.4321249789912478, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5797928802588997, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12133072407045009, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26474539191489044, "cosine_similarity": 0.4321249789912478, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5797928802588997, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.47108725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 27}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_048", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive) in a reported logarithm of unspecified base; program directions were therefore judged against that 77% positive background, and genes not present are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a marker of programme engagement, not of enzyme activity, flux, or subcellular localisation; no lipid, sterol, hydrolase-activity, pH or flux measurement is supplied, so lysosomal retention, cargo residence time and ER sterol pool status are inferred, not observed.", "The 92 protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (median |log2FC| 0.585, 70% positive, 47 flagged significant); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and mixed cathepsin-spot directions are read as proteoform redistribution or as unresolved contradiction.", "Both modalities show a strong positive skew, so a global normalisation or cell-composition shift could inflate positive programme fractions; coherence within programmes is descriptive and genes within a programme are not independent (no formal enrichment test was performed).", "Membership of each programme was fixed a priori from canonical pathway knowledge (labelled unverified background knowledge) and all members were queried; represented members were reported irrespective of sign.", "The assigned sphingolipid focus is retained only as the largest-effect catabolic arm of the broader endolysosomal state; the data cannot show that sphingolipid handling is the causal driver rather than one component of a coordinated cell state.", "Effects attributed to the measured mock condition are steady-state routing differences; any degradative insufficiency would only be revealed by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge and is not claimed here."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzymatic bottleneck but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipid-uptake receptors, MiT/TFE-associated endolysosomal biogenesis (v-ATPase, LAMP1, RAB7A, retromer/ESCRT) and lysosomal sphingolipid catabolism are jointly elevated, together with neutral-lipid esterification and the sterol-synthesis (SREBP) program. The most parsimonious reading is altered routing: internalised membrane/lipoprotein lipid is directed into an enlarged endolysosomal and esterified-storage pool rather than into the ER regulatory sterol pool, so sterol/lipid sensing continues to call for uptake and synthesis, producing a self-reinforcing lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded microglial state. Glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin turnover is the largest-effect catabolic arm of this state, but the data do not identify a sphingolipid-specific driver and do not establish causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia, quantitative lipidomics plus LAMP1 imaging should show higher lysosomal-fraction glucosylceramide/GM3/lactosylceramide and sphingomyelin and higher cholesteryl ester and neutral-lipid droplet content per cell, with increased LAMP1+ volume, despite the elevated hydrolase transcripts. Equal or lower lysosomal sphingolipid/sterol load in APOE4 would weaken the retention/routing step.", "Prospective: enzymatic assays of GBA, HEXA/B and acid sphingomyelinase activity in APOE4 microglia should be equal to or higher than APOE3. If activity is decreased despite the large transcript increases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1), the mechanism should be replaced by a hydrolase-deficiency 'failed compensation' model.", "Prospective: a labelled-lipoprotein or labelled-myelin pulse-chase should show longer label residence in the lysosomal fraction and reduced label appearance in the ER-accessible sterol pool in APOE4, with correspondingly greater SREBP2 cleavage. Identical transfer kinetics and identical SREBP2 processing between genotypes would weaken the routing mechanism.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition or SCARB1/LDLR knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal/stored lipid and normalise SREBP2-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript elevation only partly reduced. If SREBP2 targets remain fully elevated after lipid load is normalised, the feed-forward step is falsified and a genotype-intrinsic MiT/TFE activation independent of lipid sensing is favoured.", "Prospective: acute TFEB or MiT/TFE inhibition (or FLCN/mTORC1 manipulation) should collapse the coordinated v-ATPase-hydrolase-sphingolipid-catabolism block together, whereas selective UGCG or SMPD1 inhibition should move only the sphingolipid arm. If blocking sphingolipid handling alone reproduces the entire lysosomal and SREBP signature, a sphingolipid-specific driver would be favoured over the coordinated-state mechanism proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype sets a microglial transcriptional state with higher lipid- and ligand-uptake receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), which is inferred (not measured) to increase delivery of lipoprotein and membrane-lipid cargo into the endocytic route.", "A coordinated MiT/TFE-type endolysosomal biogenesis program is co-elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92; v-ATPase 16/17 represented members positive, e.g. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51; gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:GNPTG +3.02), enlarging the acidic degradative compartment and lengthening cargo residence in it.", "Within that compartment the highest-magnitude catabolic arm is glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin turnover (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:SGPL1 +1.09; 8/8 represented members positive), while complex-glycosphingolipid synthesis is not coordinately raised (gene:B4GALT5 -1.88 against a 77%-positive list background; gene:ORMDL2 +1.91 consistent with restrained de novo serine-palmitoyltransferase flux) - i.e. membrane sphingolipid is routed toward lysosomal breakdown and ceramide/ceramide-1-phosphate handling (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:GLTP +2.38) rather than toward net complex-GSL accumulation at the plasma membrane.", "Liberated sterol and fatty acid are preferentially esterified and stored rather than returned to the ER regulatory pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:FABP3 +1.35, gene:FABP5 +1.13, gene:ABHD5 +1.04), so the ER sterol sensor is not satisfied despite high influx.", "Consequently the SREBP-driven uptake/synthesis program remains active instead of being suppressed (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LDLR +1.50), closing a feed-forward loop that sustains influx into the expanded lysosomal/storage pool.", "The resulting chronically lipid-handling, lysosome-expanded state is accompanied by modestly raised inflammatory/chemokine and complement tone (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:CD14 +1.41, gene:C1QA +1.25) and by elevated oxidative/TCA transcripts (gene:MDH1 +8.70, gene:OGDH +8.60, gene:MPC2 +8.00, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02), consistent with catabolism of the delivered lipid load; these are downstream correlates, not proof of increased flux.", "Compatibility check at protein level: cathepsin/hydrolase-containing 2D spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.585, protein_spot:055 +0.585, protein_spot:012 +0.678 versus protein_spot:058 -0.848, protein_spot:069 -1.379, protein_spot:067 -1.00), which is compatible with redistribution of hydrolase proteoforms in a remodelled compartment but, because every spot carries 2-6 candidate identities, cannot confirm any individual protein."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a MiT/TFE-associated endolysosomal lipid-routing state in which sphingolipid- and sterol-bearing cargo is retained in an expanded degradative/storage compartment, keeping the SREBP uptake program switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14677103718199608, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2122602018282741, "cosine_similarity": 0.4317721910989778, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6045242718446602, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14677103718199608, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2122602018282741, "cosine_similarity": 0.4317721910989778, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6045242718446602, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.006309, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_053", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00) from a single mock APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, SQSTM1) means not supplied, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect is unspecified; only sign, rank and coherence are used, never absolute fold-change magnitudes.", "The dataset shows a large global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 rows up, median +1.46), so directional coherence of a module is judged against that 0.77 baseline, and part of the shift may be a normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-composition artifact rather than biology.", "Effect size and adjusted p-value are essentially uncorrelated here (Spearman rho = -0.03), so very large effects are treated as low-confidence unless the adjusted p-value is also extreme; the module genes cited above are mostly adj p \u003c 1e-20.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for the size of the corresponding transcriptional program only; enzyme activity, protein maturation, lysosomal pH, compartment volume, cargo flux and lipid pools were not measured.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with multiple candidate genes and frequent keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level direction is used only as weak, ambiguity-flagged corroboration.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype-associated transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous; the comparison is isogenic but the number of biological replicates is not supplied and a single day-30 timepoint is used.", "Causality is not established by these data; every step describing flux, localization or direction is a hypothesis to be tested."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated transcriptional state in which lipid-cargo uptake receptors, a CLEAR-like lysosomal biogenesis/acidification/hydrolase module, and an SREBP-driven sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis plus esterification module are simultaneously elevated. The simultaneous 'more lysosome' and 'ER needs sterol' signature is most parsimoniously explained by a bottleneck in the export of lipid liberated inside the endolysosome to the ER-accessible regulatory pool, rather than by a deficit in acid-hydrolase transcription; the lysosomal program is interpreted as demand-driven compensation. No lipid, cholesterol, pH, enzyme-activity or flux measurement is supplied, so all activity, localization, flux and causal statements are inferences, not observations.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo assay: in a pulse-chase with dual-labelled cargo (BODIPY/filipin-detectable cholesterol-rich myelin or apoptotic cells plus DQ-BSA), APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater DQ-BSA dequenching (bulk proteolysis intact or increased) but significantly prolonged retention of unesterified cholesterol/neutral-lipid signal inside LAMP1-positive compartments relative to isogenic APOE3. If proteolytic dequenching is instead reduced in proportion to the lipid retention, the bottleneck is general lysosomal degradation rather than lipid egress and this mechanism is weakened.", "Rescue of the sensing loop: acute delivery of lysosomal cholesterol to the ER (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/StARD3 overexpression) should, within 24-48 h, lower SREBP-target transcripts (SCD, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR, SREBF2) and lower TFEB-target transcripts (ATP6V0C, GBA, HEXA, CTSD) in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of both modules after successful sterol delivery would falsify the proposed lysosome-to-ER hand-off as the driver.", "Compensation versus driver: TFEB knockdown or MiT-family inhibition should exacerbate, not relieve, lipid retention and chemokine transcript output selectively in APOE4. If TFEB knockdown normalizes lysosomal lipid load, the lysosomal program is a driver rather than compensation and step 2 of the mechanism is wrong.", "Enzyme-activity test of step 5: measured GBA, HEXA/HEXB and cathepsin B/D activities per lysosome (activity-based probes or fluorogenic substrates, normalized to LAMP1 volume) should be at most modestly increased in APOE4 despite the large transcript increases, and pro- versus mature cathepsin D forms should shift on immunoblot. Proportional increases in per-lysosome activity with no proteoform shift would remove the maturation/sorting constraint invoked in step 5.", "Normalization control: reanalysis with spike-in or per-cell total-RNA-anchored normalization, or comparison against size/count-matched pseudobulk, should retain the lysosomal and SREBP modules as elevated relative to the recomputed global median. If both modules collapse to the global background after such normalization, the signature is an artifact of the observed 77% upward shift and the hypothesis is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-cargo uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred compartment state): A CLEAR-like lysosome-biogenesis module is coordinately elevated - transcription factors (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:ATP6V1E1), membrane/transport proteins (gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:CLCN7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:CLN3, gene:NPC2) and glycosidase/sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:GBA2, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:DNASE2). We infer an expanded and at least normally acidified degradative compartment; compartment volume, pH and enzyme activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): Despite this expansion, ER-sterol-sensing output is up, not down (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD). We infer that sterol/lipid liberated in the endolysosome is not reaching the ER-accessible regulatory pool, i.e. the egress/hand-off step is limiting. The lysosomal and ER cholesterol pools themselves were not measured (no NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1 or LIPA row is supplied).", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred storage): Lipid that does reach the ER is preferentially esterified and stored rather than returned to the regulatory pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H), which we infer sustains the apparent sterol deficit and keeps both the SREBP and the TFEB/MITF programs switched on as a self-reinforcing loop.", "Step 5 (measured RNA and protein spots, inferred maturation): Hydrolase transcript elevation need not translate into proportionally more mature luminal enzyme. The two mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcripts move in opposite directions (gene:M6PR down, gene:IGF2R up), one cysteine protease is strongly down (gene:CTSS, also gene:IDS down), and protein spots whose candidate lists contain CTSD/CTSB change in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down). This pattern is compatible with redistribution among cathepsin proteoforms/spots rather than a uniform abundance increase, but the spots are not uniquely identified proteins.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): The predicted net state is lipid-loaded, transcriptionally expanded lysosomes with preserved bulk proteolytic capacity but limited lipid clearance, accompanied by a modest chemokine/complement tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosome-expansion program while the ER sterol sensor reports deficiency: endolysosomal lipid egress, not hydrolase synthesis, is the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12622309197651663, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25998527397550214, "cosine_similarity": 0.43094237501025756, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5877961165048543, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12622309197651663, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25998527397550214, "cosine_similarity": 0.43094237501025756, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5877961165048543, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8312255, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 28}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_028", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every entry has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global up-shift (77% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); all pathway statements are therefore made relative to this list's own background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene means it was not in the list, not that it was unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein-spot effects are not on a common scale and are not compared numerically.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a demand/capacity signal, not as measured enzymatic activity, flux, localization or lumenal pH. No sphingolipid, ceramide, cholesterol or neutral-lipid pool was measured in this dataset; all lipid statements are predictions.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features, not uniquely identified proteins; assignment of the up spots protein_spot:043/044/045 to ANXA1 rather than TALDO1 is an inference supported by the opposite RNA directions of gene:ANXA1 and gene:TALDO1 and could be wrong.", "Key activity-limiting components of the proposed bottleneck (PSAP/saposins, UGCG, ASAH1, GALC, NEU1, ARSA, SPTLC1/2, NPC1, LIPA, MCOLN1, core autophagy genes) are absent from the supplied list, so the bottleneck step is inferred from its flanking enzymes.", "Very large effect magnitudes (e.g. gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:SCARB1, all \u003e5) come with weaker adjusted p-values than many moderate-effect genes and are treated as directionally, not quantitatively, informative; the mechanism is designed to survive using only the moderate high-confidence members (gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GM2A, gene:SCARB2, gene:CTSD).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a cell-extrinsic astrocytic contribution to lipid load cannot be excluded, and no causal direction has been established by these data.", "The comparison is described as isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment; replicate number was not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia deliver more lipoprotein- and membrane-derived sphingolipid cargo to the endolysosome than their lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolysis step can clear. The primary bottleneck is lumenal glycosphingolipid hydrolysis capacity (the GBA/HEXA-HEXB/GLA/SMPD1 step, which depends on unmeasured saposin and activator cofactors, lumenal pH and SCARB2-dependent enzyme delivery), not de novo sphingolipid synthesis. The coordinated rise in hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB/MITF transcripts is interpreted as a compensatory demand signal, and because the export/recycling limb (RAB27A, STX17, STXBP5, M6PR transcripts) is flat or reduced, the predicted consequence is retention of glucosylceramide, lactosylceramide, GM3 and sphingomyelin in an expanded, lipid-laden lysosomal compartment. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundance were measured; no lipid pool, enzyme activity, pH, localization or causal direction was measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a glucosylceramide synthase (UGCG) inhibitor such as Genz-123346/eliglustat for 72 h should lower lysosomal glycosphingolipid load and specifically collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess in CLEAR-network transcripts (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, TFEB targets) and in LAMP1-positive compartment volume, without abolishing the APOE4 uptake-receptor signature. If the CLEAR/hydrolase transcript excess persists unchanged after verified substrate depletion, the substrate-pressure bottleneck is falsified and a load-independent TFEB/MITF-driven lysosome biogenesis program should be preferred.", "Lipidomics prediction: mock APOE4 microglia should show higher per-cell glucosylceramide, lactosylceramide, GM3 and sphingomyelin than APOE3, with the glucosylceramide/lactosylceramide ratio raised in the direction implied by reduced gene:B4GALT5. Equal or lower glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin levels in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Activity-versus-transcript prediction: 4-methylumbelliferyl-glucoside (GBA) and 4MU-GlcNAc (hexosaminidase) activities per mg protein, and acid sphingomyelinase activity, should increase sub-proportionally to their transcript increases in APOE4, and saposin/PSAP protein should not rise in proportion. If enzyme activity rises proportionally to transcript while substrate lipids are unchanged, the capacity-deficit claim fails.", "Specificity prediction versus a generic lysosome-mass explanation: normalising lipid species to LAMP1 protein or to LysoTracker-positive volume should leave glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin species still elevated in APOE4. If every lysosomal lipid and protein scales by the same factor, the sphingolipid-specific framing collapses into non-specific lysosomal expansion.", "Routing prediction: SCARB2/LIMP-2 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should shift lysosomal GBA localization and raise glucosylceramide toward APOE4 levels, and SCARB2 overexpression in APOE4 should partially reduce it. No change in glucosylceramide after SCARB2 manipulation would remove the enzyme-delivery arm of the mechanism.", "Disposal-limb prediction: stimulated lysosomal exocytosis (for example ionomycin-evoked or TFEB-driven surface LAMP1 exposure and extracellular hexosaminidase release) should be lower in APOE4 relative to its enlarged lysosomal compartment. Equal or greater exocytic release per unit lysosomal volume in APOE4 would falsify step 5, leaving the hypothesis dependent on hydrolysis capacity alone."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of sphingolipid-containing cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): Clearance of that cargo requires stepwise lumenal hydrolysis of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids. The activity of this step is set by enzyme delivery (gene:SCARB2 encodes the LIMP-2 receptor that routes GBA to lysosomes), by lipid-presenting activators (GM2A; saposins from PSAP, which is NOT present in these data), and by lumenal acidification. None of these activities, pH values or localizations were measured; only transcripts were.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): A coherent CLEAR-type transcriptional response is present: sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolases and their trafficking/activator components (gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GM2A, gene:SMPD1, gene:SCARB2, gene:GLTP), other lysosomal hydrolases and pumps (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1) and the transcription factors gene:TFEB and gene:MITF. We read this as a response to unmet degradative demand rather than as proof of increased degradative flux.", "Step 4 (asymmetry, measured abundance): The anabolic sphingolipid branch is not co-induced above the strong global up-shift of this selected gene list (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:SGPL1, gene:ORMDL2 sit near the background mean), and the GlcCer-to-LacCer step gene:B4GALT5 is reduced while gene:ST3GAL5 is raised. This argues the sphingolipid signal is turnover/substrate-pressure driven and predicts a shift of the glycosphingolipid profile toward glucosylceramide and GM3 rather than a uniform increase in all species.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred routing): The disposal and retrieval limb is not co-induced: gene:RAB27A, gene:STX17, gene:STXBP5, gene:STXBP2 and gene:M6PR are reduced while gene:VPS26A and gene:SNX3 rise. We infer, without direct measurement, that lysosomal exocytosis, autophagosome-lysosome fusion and hydrolase re-delivery do not scale with the increased hydrolase transcription, so undegraded lipid is retained.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): Lipid spared from hydrolysis is diverted into neutral-lipid esterification and storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1) and the cells adopt a lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded, inflammatory-primed state (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:CLEC7A, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL8, gene:C1QA), with gene:ANXA1 induction corroborated at the protein-spot level (protein_spot:045, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:043)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a substrate-driven lysosomal glycosphingolipid catabolism deficit: CLEAR-network hydrolase transcripts rise as a demand signal while the disposal limb is not co-induced"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12915851272015655, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23152175444263545, "cosine_similarity": 0.43094153371957633, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6062621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12915851272015655, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23152175444263545, "cosine_similarity": 0.43094153371957633, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6062621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.4840505, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 29}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_090", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and every row |effect|\u003e1; absence of a gene (e.g. SOD2, CAT, GSR, G6PD, NFE2L2, PEX genes, most mitoribosome genes) means 'not in the supplied selection', not 'unchanged', so all set statistics are conditioned on selection and were tested against the dataset's own 77%-up, median +1.46 background rather than against zero.", "Directionality is inferred from a within-dataset contrast (nuclear-encoded versus mtDNA-encoded rows) precisely because the global up-shift and the protein-spot up-shift (median +0.485) could partly reflect normalisation, composition or ambient-RNA effects that act on both sets equally.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification by probe-based 10X Flex, and mitochondrial-read fraction generally, is sensitive to probe coverage, ambient RNA and QC filtering; the six MT- rows are treated as a weak but directionally informative measurement.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for subunit protein availability; assembled complex stoichiometry, respiration, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number, ROS and GSH/GSSG or roGFP redox couples were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred quantities only.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (e.g. spot 017: CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5; spot 077: KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB); they are cited only as weakly consistent, non-identifying evidence and no spot is treated as a specific protein measurement.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a non-cell-autonomous astrocytic contribution to the APOE4 microglial state, and cell-state proportion shifts within the microglial population, cannot be excluded.", "Peroxisomal metabolism was considered and rejected as the primary mechanism: no PEX row is present and the assembled peroxisomal set (n=5, median +1.24) is indistinguishable from background (permutation p=0.70)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a coordinated up-shift of nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain and TCA transcripts (38/38 measured NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH rows positive, median +2.64; permutation p=0.001 against the dataset's own 77%-up background) while the measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts move in the opposite direction (4/6 negative, median -1.56). The primary bottleneck we propose is the supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits relative to imported nuclear subunits: complex I/III/IV assembly, not subunit transcription, becomes rate-limiting. The inferred consequences are sub-stoichiometric holo-complex assembly, increased electron leak, and engagement of a matrix thiol-peroxidase/NADPH buffer (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS, NNT transcripts up) plus an OMA1-DELE1-HRI-type integrated stress and TFEB-lysosomal response. Assembly state, respiration, ROS and redox couples were NOT measured here; only RNA and ambiguous protein spots were, so causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Blue-native PAGE with in-gel activity in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show reduced assembled complex I, III2 and IV holo-complex per unit of nuclear-encoded subunit protein (e.g. NDUFA9, UQCRC2, COX4) and accumulation of sub-complexes; equal or higher assembled holo-complex per subunit in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "High-resolution respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOMM20) should show lower coupled/ATP-linked respiration and a higher leak fraction in APOE4 despite the higher nuclear subunit transcripts; unchanged or higher coupling efficiency per mitochondrial mass would falsify Step 4.", "Discriminating perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 (TFAM or POLRMT/mitochondrial-transcription augmentation, or mtDNA-encoded-subunit allotopic/ mitochondrially targeted rescue) should restore the assembled:unassembled complex ratio, lower matrix ROS (MitoSOX or mito-roGFP2-Orp1) and reduce ATF4/DDIT3 reporter output; if boosting mtDNA transcripts corrects none of these while leaving the nuclear program intact, the mitonuclear-imbalance bottleneck is wrong.", "Ordering test: DELE1 or EIF2AK1(HRI) knockout, or ISRIB, should blunt DDIT3/ATF4 induction WITHOUT normalising complex assembly or matrix ROS; if DELE1 loss also normalises assembly and ROS, the relay is upstream and the proposed causal order is falsified.", "Redox-intermediary test: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ, mitoTEMPO or mito-catalase) should reduce the ISR/lysosomal transcript module in APOE4 without correcting the mitonuclear transcript ratio; no reduction of the ISR module would show ROS is not the transmitting signal and would remove the redox arm of the mechanism.", "Quantitative prediction on missing pools: APOE4 microglia should show an elevated nuclear-encoded:mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS protein ratio; if instead mtDNA copy number per cell is reduced proportionally to both transcript classes, or the protein ratio is unchanged, the mechanism reduces to a normalisation artefact.", "Control against the general up-shift: single-molecule FISH or bulk qPCR with spike-in normalisation should confirm that MT-CYB/MT-ATP6 are genuinely lower in APOE4 while NDUFS7/OGDH are higher; concordant movement of both classes after spike-in normalisation would falsify the discordance on which the hypothesis rests."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred program): APOE4 microglia express a coordinated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program - all 38 measured NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH rows and 7/7 measured TCA rows are positive (medians +2.64 and +3.94; permutation p=0.001 and 0.007 versus the dataset background), i.e. a biogenesis-like transcriptional bias rather than a random consequence of the global up-shift.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, opposite direction): the six measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts do not follow this bias (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; Mann-Whitney versus nuclear set p=9e-4), so the two genomes are transcriptionally discordant in the same cells.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck, unmeasured): because complexes I, III and IV require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, the discordance predicts sub-stoichiometric holo-complex assembly with accumulation of unassembled or partially assembled nuclear-encoded modules; assembled-complex abundance is the proposed rate-limiting node, not subunit availability.", "Step 4 (inferred flux/localization): assembly-stalled complex I/III intermediates increase univalent electron leak in the matrix and inner-membrane compartment, lowering ATP yield per unit of expressed subunit; this is a flux/redox claim with no direct measurement in the supplied data.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, consistent with Step 4 but not proof): matrix-facing peroxide-handling and NADPH-supply transcripts are up (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, GPX4 +2.79, GSS +2.11, NNT +2.88, PRDX2 +4.41; CYCS +2.58), consistent with a compensatory buffering demand rather than a general antioxidant program (the wider antioxidant/redox set is not enriched above background, permutation p=0.59).", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): persistent mitochondrial stress engages a relay-plus-degradation response - DELE1 +4.82, DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2AK3 +1.51, with TFEB +2.38 and coordinated lysosomal/v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB +5.52, GBA +6.71, ATP6V1A +4.23; set median +2.17) - which we interpret as downstream of Steps 3-4, not as an independent primary lesion.", "Step 7 (inferred phenotype): the resulting low-efficiency, stress-signalling state co-occurs with a sterol/lipid-handling shift (SCARB1 +8.22, SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, APOE +1.24), which we predict biases APOE4 microglia toward lipid storage and away from ATP-expensive homeostatic functions."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: nuclear-encoded ETC/TCA transcripts rise without matched mtDNA-encoded core subunits, creating an assembly-limited, leak-prone respiratory chain in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11252446183953033, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28765531523473303, "cosine_similarity": 0.43085667984843534, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5765242718446602, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11252446183953033, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28765531523473303, "cosine_similarity": 0.43085667984843534, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5765242718446602, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.65073475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 30}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_015", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Higher transcript abundance for a pathway is a usable proxy for the direction of protein and flux change in that pathway; no enzyme activity, metabolite, sterol pool, lipid droplet or lysosomal pH measurement is supplied, so all flux, localisation and pool statements are inferred.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive), so pathway claims are only meaningful relative to this list's own strong positive shift; I therefore judged every module against the empirical background (median +1.46, 77.1% up) by permutation rather than against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes up to +15.5 are treated as ranks/directions, not as literal fold changes.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a specific protein's abundance.", "The endolysosomal transcript module is interpreted as a compensatory (demand-driven) response rather than as evidence of adequate degradative capacity; the opposite interpretation would invert the bottleneck.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and the astrocyte co-culture contributes comparable lipoprotein supply to both genotypes, so differences are genotype-driven rather than culture-composition driven.", "Compositional/normalisation artefacts (e.g. depth or ambient-RNA differences) do not by themselves generate the module-specific ordering (mitochondrial-carbon \u003e lysosome ~ SREBP \u003e UPR/secretory)."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step is return of internalised lipid from an expanded endolysosomal compartment to the ER regulatory sterol pool; because that return is inferred to be insufficient, sterol-sensing feedback is not satisfied and the SREBP-driven uptake/synthesis program (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36, SREBF1/2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, SCD, FADS1, INSIG1) stays elevated while mitochondrial/citrate-derived carbon supply (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, SLC25A1, ACSS2) and esterification enzymes (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, GPAT4) are also elevated, so newly acquired lipid is repeatedly re-esterified into lysosomal and cytosolic neutral-lipid stores rather than being catabolised. Canonical UPR/ERAD and COPI/COPII secretory programs are not coherently induced and are therefore rejected as the primary bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript and spot measurements are associations under a mock comparison.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute delivery of cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool (cholesterol/methyl-beta-cyclodextrin complex, 1-4 h) should suppress SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS, INSIG1) at least as strongly in APOE4 as in APOE3, and 25-hydroxycholesterol should do the same; if APOE4 cells fail to suppress these targets, the sensor itself, not the lysosome-to-ER sterol return, is broken and this mechanism is wrong.", "Relieving the bottleneck should normalise the program: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or NPC1/lysosomal-egress enhancement should lower SREBF1/2 target transcripts and lower filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol and BODIPY/LipidTOX neutral-lipid area specifically in APOE4; no genotype-selective reduction would weaken the mechanism.", "Blocking esterification with a SOAT1 inhibitor (avasimibe) should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl-ester droplets toward free cholesterol and further raise, not lower, LXR targets (ABCA7, APOE, CH25H) while leaving lysosomal cholesterol elevated; if SOAT1 inhibition instead normalises SREBP targets and lysosomal lipid, the bottleneck lies at esterification rather than at lysosomal egress.", "Direct phenotype test: APOE4 microglia should show a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio and greater LAMP1-colocalised lipid signal than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower neutral lipid and lysosomal lipid in APOE4 would falsify the hypothesis despite the transcript pattern.", "TFEB knockdown should worsen (not relieve) APOE4 lipid accumulation because the CLEAR module is compensatory; if TFEB knockdown reduces lipid load, the lysosomal module is driving rather than compensating and the mechanism is wrong.", "Rejection of the assigned ER-proteostasis focus is itself testable: APOE4 microglia should not show genotype-selective increases in BiP/HSPA5 protein, XBP1 splicing, or ATF6 cleavage, nor increased ER-to-Golgi cargo delay (RUSH assay); a clear XBP1s/BiP induction with slowed secretory transport in APOE4 would favour a UPR/trafficking bottleneck over this lipid-handling one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, unspecified log base). Inferred (not measured): a correspondingly higher flux of extracellular lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Measured: a coherent CLEAR/lysosome transcript module is up (28/28 members detected, 26 up; median +2.10 vs background median +1.46, permutation p=0.030 for fraction-up), including gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD and multiple V-ATPase subunits. Inferred: this is a compensatory biogenesis response to a lipid/substrate load, i.e. hydrolase and acidification capacity is being scaled up because demand exceeds it.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred, not directly measured): sterol/lipid hydrolysis and export from the lysosomal lumen to the ER-accessible regulatory pool is limiting. NPC1 and LIPA are absent from the supplied differential list and only gene:NPC2 (+1.17) is present, so the egress machinery itself was not measured; the bottleneck is inferred from the downstream sensing readout in the next step.", "Measured readout of the inferred low ER regulatory sterol pool: every detected SREBP-pathway transcript is up (13/13, permutation p=0.034 for fraction-up) - gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:LDLR +1.50. Inferred, not measured: unrestrained SCAP/SREBP processing; SREBP cleavage, nuclear SREBP protein and ER cholesterol were not assayed.", "Measured: mitochondrial/anaplerotic carbon-supply transcripts are the most coherently elevated module in the dataset (14/14 up, median +3.35, permutation p=0.002), including gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54 and the citrate exporter gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, with gene:HK2 -3.67. Inferred: cytosolic acetyl-CoA is available (via citrate export and gene:ACSS2) to sustain the sterol/fatty-acid synthesis demanded by step 4 rather than glycolytic lactate output.", "Measured: esterification/storage enzymes are up (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58). Inferred (not measured here): free sterol and fatty acid are buffered as cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol in cytosolic lipid droplets, which keeps them outside the ER regulatory pool and closes a futile uptake-synthesis-storage cycle.", "Net predicted phenotype (not measured in this dataset): higher neutral-lipid droplet and lysosomal lipid burden per APOE4 microglion, with simultaneous engagement of the oxysterol/LXR arm (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:MYLIP +1.28) reflecting sterol excess in a compartment that the SCAP/INSIG sensor does not see."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-hydrolysis/egress bottleneck, not ER unfolded-protein stress, keeps the SREBP lipogenic program switched on and drives neutral-lipid loading in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25367030996098094, "cosine_similarity": 0.4302280961328225, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961650485436893, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25367030996098094, "cosine_similarity": 0.4302280961328225, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961650485436893, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97389825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 31}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_038", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (|reported log fold change| \u003e= 1, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 2212 rows, 77% positive); program directionality was judged against that up-biased background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2, ASAH1, GRN, PSAP, NPC1, LAMP2, MCOLN1, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2 of reported fold change from a 2D-gel workflow.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a read-out of program engagement, not of enzyme activity, flux, localization or lipid pool size; the endolysosomal sterol/glycosphingolipid load that drives step 1 is inferred and was not measured.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (69 of 92 have five), with frequent keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein, and bidirectional cathepsin-containing spots are treated as compatible-with, not proof-of, proteoform redistribution.", "MiT/TFE involvement is inferred from coordinate v-ATPase/hydrolase/LAMP1 transcript elevation together with elevated gene:TFEB; TFEB nuclear localization and mTORC1 status were not measured.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous; the comparison is isogenic APOE4 minus APOE3 under mock, and no causal direction is established by these observational contrasts."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell-state change rather than a single enzymatic defect: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and neutral-lipid storage, for SREBP-dependent sterol synthesis and uptake, and for lysosomal acidification (16/16 represented v-ATPase/TFEB-module genes up) and lumenal hydrolases (including the sphingolipid catabolic set GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1) are jointly elevated above the strongly up-biased selected-list background, together with mitochondrial TCA/ETC genes and reduced HK2/PFKP. We interpret this as an expansion of degradative and lipid-storage capacity driven by an inferred (not measured) endolysosomal sterol/glycosphingolipid load, i.e. successful transcriptional adaptation in the measured condition, with reduced reserve predicted only under challenge because the TGN-to-endosome sorting/fusion arm (M6PR, STX16, GCC1, GCC2, GOLPH3L, STX17, RAB27A down) does not scale with it. De novo sphingolipid synthesis is only weakly represented (CERS4, CERS6, KDSR, ORMDL2, CERK, SGPL1; SPTLC/SGMS/UGCG absent), so sphingolipid biosynthesis is rejected as the primary driver and sphingolipid catabolism is placed downstream of the lysosomal program. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline-capacity test (discriminating adaptation vs ongoing bottleneck): in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, LysoTracker/LAMP1 volume, v-ATPase-dependent acidification and bulk cathepsin B/D, GBA and HEXB enzymatic activity per cell should be equal or higher in APOE4, and DQ-BSA dequenching should not be reduced. If baseline hydrolase activity or DQ-BSA proteolysis is significantly reduced in APOE4 despite the elevated transcripts, the adaptation interpretation is weakened in favour of an ongoing delivery/maturation bottleneck.", "Prospective substrate-removal test (single-driver test): culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium or treating with a SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor or cyclodextrin should attenuate both arms (SREBP targets LDLR/HMGCS1/DHCR24 and TFEB targets ATP6V1H/GBA/HEXA/CTSB) toward APOE3 levels. If the lysosomal/v-ATPase arm remains elevated while only the sterol arm normalizes, the shared lipid-load driver is falsified and two parallel APOE4-intrinsic drivers must be invoked.", "Prospective challenge test (reserve, not baseline): after an acute load of myelin debris, oxLDL or fluorescent LacCer/BODIPY-cholesterol, APOE4 should show slower clearance and greater accumulation of undegraded substrate in LAMP1+ compartments than APOE3, together with increased secretion of pro-forms of cathepsin D/B into the medium (consistent with the reduced M6PR/STX16/GCC1/GOLPH3L sorting arm). Equal clearance kinetics and no pro-cathepsin secretion would weaken the non-scaling-sorting step while leaving steps 1-5 intact.", "Prospective pathway-separation test: SREBP inhibition (fatostatin or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should lower sterol-synthesis transcripts in APOE4 without lowering v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts, whereas TFEB knockdown should lower v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts and reduce lysosomal acidification without normalizing LDLR/HMGCS1. Co-dependence of both arms on either manipulation would falsify the two-branch architecture described in steps 2-4.", "Prospective energetic test: the oxidative shift predicts higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower glycolytic reserve in APOE4; v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin) should reduce the APOE4-APOE3 oxygen-consumption difference disproportionately. If APOE4 shows no oxidative advantage, step 5 is weakened and the mitochondrial transcript signature would instead be read as compositional or stress-related."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters microglial lipid handling so that sterol and glycosphingolipid substrate accumulates in the endolysosomal system (inferred pool, not measured here); the measured correlate is coordinate induction of lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and storage transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:MGLL) and of efferocytic/phagocytic receptors (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:ITGAX, gene:GPR34, gene:MRC1, gene:ANXA1 +4.15).", "Sequestration of sterol away from ER sensing keeps the SREBP arm on: all 11 represented SREBP/sterol genes are up (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:NPC2), sustaining continued sterol synthesis and uptake despite the storage program (esterification via gene:SOAT1).", "The same lumenal load engages a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal biogenesis program: gene:TFEB +2.38 with every represented v-ATPase subunit up (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1/D2, gene:ATP6V1C1/E1/F, gene:ATP6AP1) plus gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, expanding acidification and membrane capacity.", "Lumenal hydrolase transcripts rise as part of the same program, with the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid catabolic module prominent (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:MAN2B1), i.e. sphingolipid turnover is a downstream branch of lysosomal expansion, not an independent biosynthetic switch (de novo genes only gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:ORMDL2, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1, gene:ST3GAL5; gene:B4GALT5 down).", "Acidification and biosynthetic load are supported by an oxidative shift in energy transcripts: mitochondrial TCA/carrier/ETC genes up (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B/G, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:COX5B) while glycolytic entry falls (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite higher transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "The delivery/sorting arm is not coordinately increased: gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:STX16 -4.06, gene:GCC1 -5.01, gene:GCC2 -2.88, gene:GOLPH3L -7.40, gene:STX17 -2.06, gene:RAB27A -2.52 (8 of 16 represented TGN/retrograde genes down vs a 23% down background), while endosomal retromer/retriever/Commander members rise (gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:CCDC22, gene:COMMD4/5/6/8/9/10, gene:IGF2R, gene:GNPTG). Protein spots containing cathepsins run in both directions across distinct spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 containing ATP6V1E1 down), compatible with proteoform/processing redistribution rather than a uniform protein increase; this predicts limited reserve when hydrolase delivery must scale acutely, a defect expected only under a future lipid challenge and not established in mock.", "Net measured state: higher lipid-uptake/storage and higher lysosomal-degradative and oxidative capacity in APOE4, i.e. an adapted lipid-processing microglial state at baseline; the loss of homeostatic gene:CTSS -5.57 with gene:ITGAX, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:CLEC7A up marks this as a distinct activated cell state rather than a graded change."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sit in a lipid-load-adapted endolysosomal state: coordinate MiT/TFE-type lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase induction plus SREBP sterol and neutral-lipid-storage programs, oxidatively fueled, with a non-scaling TGN sorting arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23782446553188347, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27562200836937123, "cosine_similarity": 0.4296490771341177, "direction_accuracy": 0.25728155339805825, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904692556634304, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23782446553188347, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27562200836937123, "cosine_similarity": 0.4296490771341177, "direction_accuracy": 0.25728155339805825, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904692556634304, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1828375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_051", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and preserved as reported; magnitudes up to |15| are treated as ranks/directions only, not as literal fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up); all pathway claims are made relative to this internal background, and the shift itself may be partly technical (composition, normalisation, or one-sided row selection).", "Gene-set membership comes from unverified background knowledge; literature and database retrieval were disabled.", "Protein spots carry 3-5 candidate genes each and are keratin/actin dominated (KRT1 in 33 spots, ACTB in 25); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein.", "Transcript abundance is taken as evidence of transcriptional programme state only; TFEB and SREBP activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase maturation, cholesterol localisation and all lipid pools are inferred or unmeasured.", "Astrocytes in the co-culture may contribute APOE and lipoprotein cues; the measured difference cannot be assigned to microglia-autonomous APOE4 by these data.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision and any batch structure cannot be assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a rate-limiting step in endolysosomal luminal lipid catabolism and delivery of liberated sterol to the ER. Because ER sterol sensing (inferred, not measured) reports a low-sterol state while lipid remains trapped in the endolysosome, the two normally opposed transcriptional modules are elevated together: the CLEAR-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (TFEB, MITF, GAA, GBA, CTSK, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, GM2A, ten V-ATPase subunits) and the SREBP sterol synthesis/uptake program (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, SCARB1, CD36, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24), together with the esterification enzyme SOAT1. We claim this dual induction is a compensatory transcriptional signature of impaired lysosomal lipid flux, not evidence of increased degradative capacity; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: sterol-clamp with 25-hydroxycholesterol or LDL loading of isogenic APOE3 and APOE4 microglia. If the bottleneck is lysosome-to-ER egress, exogenous oxysterol (which reaches the ER independently of the lysosome) should suppress LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24 and INSIG1 similarly in both genotypes, whereas LDL loading (which must transit the lysosome) should suppress them markedly less in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal suppression by LDL in both genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "U18666A or NPC1 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature, raising CLEAR hydrolase/V-ATPase transcripts and SREBP-target transcripts together; failure to reproduce the dual induction would weaken step 2.", "Imaging/lipidomics: APOE4 microglia under mock should show higher filipin-positive lysosomal free cholesterol and higher cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid and hexosylceramide-GM2 content than APOE3. Equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol and cholesteryl ester despite the transcript pattern would falsify the claim.", "Functional flux: DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesterol pulse-chase should show slower substrate clearance and slower lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; if APOE4 flux is equal or faster, the 'compensatory but insufficient' framing fails and the transcript rise should instead be read as increased capacity.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown should collapse the APOE4 hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript elevation and further increase lipid accumulation; if hydrolase transcripts remain elevated after TFEB loss, step 4 is wrong.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should convert stored cholesteryl ester back to free cholesterol and, if the mechanism holds, increase ER-sensed sterol and lower LDLR/HMGCS1 transcripts selectively in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would weaken step 6.", "Protein-level test: quantitative immunoblot of mature CTSD, GBA, LAMP1 and V-ATPase V1A. Proportional protein increases matching the large transcript effects would contradict the incomplete-compensation step inferred from the discordant spot data."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein, expressed by these microglia and their co-cultured astrocytes (gene:APOE RNA higher in APOE4), is hypothesised to change endolysosomal luminal lipoprotein/lipid handling, increasing residence time of cholesterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo. This step is inferred; no lipid, no NPC1/LIPA and no APOE protein measurement is supplied.", "Reduced flux of liberated free cholesterol from the endolysosome to the ER leaves the ER sterol sensor in a functionally low-sterol state (inferred activity, not measured), de-repressing the SREBP module: SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, SCARB1, CD36, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7 and DHCR24 transcripts are all higher in APOE4 (16/16 sterol-set genes positive; binomial p=0.016 against the 77% up background).", "Sustained transcript-level drive of receptor-mediated uptake (LDLR, SCARB1, CD36) and de novo synthesis returns further lipid to the same compartment, so the load on the limiting step increases rather than resolves (predicted flux, not measured).", "Accumulated luminal substrate engages a CLEAR-type stress response: TFEB (+2.38) and MITF (+1.03) transcripts are elevated and downstream acid-hydrolase (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, GM2A +2.01) and V-ATPase transcripts (10/10 subunits positive) rise; 38/41 lysosome/CLEAR genes are positive (binomial p=0.008). TFEB nuclear localisation and V-ATPase-dependent acidification are inferred, not observed.", "Compensation is incomplete at the protein level: 2-D spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00) and RNA and spot effects are uncorrelated (Spearman -0.06, p=0.60), so degradative capacity is not shown to scale with transcript; spot identities are ambiguous.", "Net predicted consequence, not measured here: sterol that does reach the ER is preferentially esterified and stored (SOAT1 +1.25) rather than effluxed, so APOE4 microglia should carry a larger lysosomal free-cholesterol plus cytosolic cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid and glycosphingolipid pool than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions."], "title": "A lysosome-to-ER lipid egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia drives simultaneous CLEAR/hydrolase and SREBP sterol-acquisition transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24010998976545908, "cosine_similarity": 0.4286554202031416, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5934466019417476, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24010998976545908, "cosine_similarity": 0.4286554202031416, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5934466019417476, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.504552, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 32}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_043", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every gene has |effect| \u003e= 1, adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and the logarithm base of the reported effect is not specified; effects are used ordinally/directionally, never as absolute fold changes, and enrichment is tested only against the list's own strongly positive background (mean +1.39, 1705 up vs 507 down).", "The workbook contains two gene columns per row (1706 entries in column 0, mean +1.86; 506 in column 1, mean -0.22) whose provenance is not documented; set-level tests are stratified by column so that direction is not an artefact of column membership.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with a mean of 4.8 candidate genes each and keratin contaminants in 39/92 spots; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level direction is treated as a proteoform-distribution observation, not as a protein's net abundance.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for enzyme content; enzyme activity, luminal pH, lysosome number/volume, cargo flux, lipid content and protein localisation were not measured in this dataset.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous signalling or cell-composition differences rather than a microglia-intrinsic APOE4 effect.", "Central endolysosomal lipid genes are absent from the supplied list (NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1, SQSTM1, ABCA1, PLIN2, most HOPS subunits), so the delivery/egress step is inferred from adjacent genes rather than observed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by running a coordinated CLEAR-type transcriptional expansion of acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits alongside up-shifted lipid-cargo uptake receptors, while the fusion/delivery arm and the lysosomal-hydrolase-containing protein-spot pool do not scale with it; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is post-transcriptional delivery of cargo and of mature hydrolase into the acidified degradative lumen, not hydrolase transcription, so internalised lipid cargo is retained undegraded and the sterol-responsive SREBP program stays induced. Causality is not established by these data; all activity, pH, flux and lipid statements are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo-handling test: in a pulse-chase with a quenched degradation reporter plus a defined lipid cargo (DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester LDL or pHrodo myelin), APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater uptake but a lower per-lysosome degradation rate and accumulation of undegraded cargo when normalised to LAMP1/LysoTracker compartment volume. If APOE4 degrades cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3 per unit lysosome volume, with no undegraded-cargo accumulation, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Transcript-to-activity discordance: direct activity assays for GAA, GBA, HEXA/B and CTSB in APOE4 versus APOE3 should rise far less than their extreme transcript ranks imply (roughly \u003c1.5-fold), and mature-form immunoblots should show redistribution rather than proportional gain. Proportional increases in activity for these enzymes would refute the post-transcriptional-throughput step.", "Bottleneck placement: further activating the transcriptional arm (TFEB overexpression or mTORC1 inhibition) should not normalise APOE4 cargo clearance or lipid load, whereas boosting delivery/fusion (ARL8B/HOPS or STX17-VAMP-dependent fusion restoration) or supplying enzyme directly (recombinant hydrolase, acidifying nanoparticles) should. If TFEB activation alone normalises the APOE4 phenotype, the bottleneck is transcriptional and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Sterol-sensing loop: relieving lysosomal sterol retention (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) should selectively lower SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24 and LDLR transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. No selective reduction would refute the retention-driven SREBP step.", "Discriminating against the mitochondrial alternative: matching ATP supply across genotypes (galactose medium or a non-toxic oligomycin titration to equal ATP/ADP) should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in per-lysosome cargo degradation intact. If that difference disappears once ATP is clamped, the TCA/OXPHOS block is the primary axis and the endolysosomal bottleneck is secondary.", "Single-gene alternative: if restoring CTSS alone (the one strongly decreased hydrolase, 0.7th percentile) normalises APOE4 cargo degradation and lipid load, the broad capacity/throughput framing should be replaced by a single-protease deficit."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mechanism_steps": ["Cargo influx arm: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and phagocytic uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of this differential list, with CD36, MRC1, MERTK, GAS6, FCGR1A, FCGR3A, C1QA/B/C, ABCA7, TREM2, CD33, ITGAX all positive). Measured: transcript abundance. Inferred: increased flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endosomal system.", "Routing arm: late-endosomal maturation and sorting transcripts are up (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B, AP5M1, AP5Z1, AP3D1, EPG5, IGF2R), consistent with cargo being routed toward late endosomes/lysosomes. Measured: transcript abundance only; no localisation or trafficking rate was assayed.", "Compensatory capacity program: MiT/TFE factors (TFEB, TFEC, MITF) and the CLEAR-type target set are induced. 15 of 16 measured acid hydrolases are up (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, DNASE2, MAN2B1, CTSH, GLA, SGSH, ACP5), mean effect +3.48 versus +1.39 background, and all 10 measured ATP6V* subunits are up. We read this as a demand signal, not as demonstrated hydrolytic activity or increased acidification.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK - post-transcriptional luminal throughput: the machinery that must deliver cargo and mature enzyme into that lumen does not follow. Cargo-fusion/tethering transcripts skew negative against the strongly positive background (STX17, VAMP2, STX16, STXBP5, SEC22A, STXBP2), the CD-mannose-6-phosphate receptor M6PR is down, LAPTM5 is down, and CTSS is the single most extreme downward hydrolase (0.7th percentile). At the protein-spot level, spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal proteins are, on average, no higher than other spots (+0.21 vs +0.43 log2), and hydrolase-candidate spots split in both directions (increased 052, 053, 055, 057; decreased 058, 067, 069), with the two decreased ATP6V1E1-candidate spots 064 and 065 opposing the positive ATP6V1E1 transcript. Inferred: mature, correctly delivered hydrolase per unit cargo does not scale with the transcript program.", "Consequence - retained cargo and a sterol-sensing feed-forward loop: undegraded lipid cargo is inferred to persist in APOE4 endolysosomes, so sterol is not returned to the ER sensing pool and the SREBP-driven lipogenic/sterologenic transcripts stay high (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, SREBF2), which would sustain synthesis and uptake and further load the compartment. No lipid species, droplet or free-cholesterol pool was measured here.", "Energetic coupling and competing axis: TCA/OXPHOS transcripts are the single most coherent upward block (13/13 up; MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, GOT1, DLD, SLC25A46, ACO2, ETFA, HADHA, ATP5F1B, NDUFB2, SDHB, UQCRB), which we interpret as ATP supply supporting a sustained v-ATPase and biosynthetic load. This block is at least as strong as the lysosomal block and could instead be a primary, endolysosome-independent metabolic difference."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a compensatory MiT/TFE lysosomal-expansion program whose luminal throughput is limited post-transcriptionally, creating an endolysosomal cargo-processing bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14739873721522725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2427366683848557, "cosine_similarity": 0.42774645316905957, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5898381877022654, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14739873721522725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2427366683848557, "cosine_similarity": 0.42774645316905957, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5898381877022654, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.27457675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 33}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_059", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; all RNA claims are made as ranks/offsets relative to the global median of this differential list (+1.46), never as absolute fold changes, and RNA values are not placed on the same scale as the log2 protein-spot values.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so module enrichment is relative to other selected genes and cannot be read as whole-transcriptome enrichment; the strong global positive shift (77% of rows above zero) is treated as a normalization/selection offset, not as biology.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak consistency checks (e.g. spot 045/044 are consistent with, but do not prove, an ANXA1 increase, which is independently supported by gene:ANXA1 at the 89th percentile while the co-candidate TALDO1 transcript is below median).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to partially track protein amount and pathway capacity; enzyme activity, lipid flux, organelle content and subcellular localization were not measured.", "The postulated bottleneck (lysosomal lipid hydrolysis/egress) is inferred; NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2, PSAP and GRN are not present in the supplied data and are not claimed as observed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so part of the lipid load and of the genotype effect may be non-cell-autonomous; replicate number was not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be judged."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a higher scavenger-mediated lipid influx that outruns endolysosomal lipid clearance/egress; the resulting endolysosomal lipid retention is accompanied by a coordinated TFEB/CLEAR-type lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program, diversion of released acyl chains into glycerolipid/neutral-lipid synthesis (SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1), and a strongly coherent increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS transcripts, predicting a lipid-droplet-loaded, oxidation-dependent APOE4 state. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; the limiting flux step is inferred, not observed, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SCARB1 knockdown or SR-B1 blockade in APOE4 microglia should lower neutral-lipid/droplet content and coordinately damp the lysosomal-hydrolase (GBA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H), lipogenic (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2) and mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS transcript modules toward APOE3 levels; if uptake is reduced yet all three modules and droplet load persist, the influx-driven bottleneck is falsified and a cell-autonomous APOE4 transcriptional program is favoured.", "Lipidomics under mock should show higher cholesteryl ester and MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol (elevated 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 ratios, consistent with SCD) in APOE4; absence of any neutral-lipid increase weakens steps 3-4.", "Because hydrolytic flux, not enzyme transcript level, is claimed to be limiting, GBA and SMPD1 substrates (glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin) should be equal or higher in APOE4 despite higher transcripts; a clear decrease in these substrates would indicate activity scaled with transcript and would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Imaging should show increased filipin-labelled free cholesterol and LipidTox signal overlapping LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4; unchanged lysosomal lipid with droplets only at the ER-cytosol interface would move the bottleneck downstream of the lysosome.", "APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and greater sensitivity to complex-I inhibition (rotenone) than APOE3; equal or lower respiration would show the mitochondrial transcript module is not converted into flux and would weaken step 5 without necessarily falsifying steps 1-4.", "TFEB knockdown should preferentially collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript set in APOE4 and increase lysosomal lipid retention; no genotype-selective effect would weaken step 2.", "Rescue prediction: cyclodextrin-mediated bypass of lysosomal sterol egress should normalize the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 module in APOE4; failure to normalize it would argue the lipogenic module is driven by a sterol-independent route."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express markedly higher SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, 99th percentile of the differential list), with CD36, LDLR, TREM2 and APOE near or below the list median, which we interpret as increased selective lipid/lipoprotein uptake capacity rather than a general phagocytic-receptor program.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): the endolysosomal degradative program is transcriptionally expanded - TFEB plus lipid-directed lysosomal hydrolases (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, GAA), cathepsins (CTSK, CTSB, CTSD), v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) and late-endosome traffic genes (RAB7A, SNX3, DNM2, IGF2R) all rank above the global list median.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck, unmeasured pool): despite this expansion, the rate-limiting step is hydrolysis/egress of lipid out of the endolysosome; the canonical egress machinery (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2, PSAP, GRN) is absent from the supplied differential list, so this step is postulated, and lipid is predicted to be retained in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4.", "Step 4 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): the acyl chains and sterol that do reach the cytosol/ER are re-esterified and stored - a coherent glycerolipid/lipogenic module (SREBF1, AGPAT2, SCD, MBOAT2, LPCAT1, CHPT1, DGAT1; module median 2.58 vs list median 1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.021) predicts MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester droplet formation.", "Step 5 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): fatty acid delivered to mitochondria and the higher catabolic load are matched by the strongest coherent module in the data, nuclear-encoded mitochondrial TCA, carrier and OXPHOS transcripts (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, DLD, ACO2, SLC25A1/5/11, NDUFA5/S7/S8, UQCRC2, ATP5ME; 74 genes, 80% above the list median, p=8.6e-10) together with matrix redox buffering (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4), predicting greater basal oxygen consumption and greater dependence on complex I in APOE4.", "Step 6 (integration): the differentiating APOE4 phenotype under mock is therefore a chronically lipid-loaded, lysosome-plus-mitochondria catabolically primed microglial state, not an activated inflammatory or cytoskeletal/phagocytic-actin state."], "title": "Lysosome-limited handling of internalized lipid drives a storage-plus-oxidation state in mock APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.290588191854669, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31276639547627955, "cosine_similarity": 0.4276384268929457, "direction_accuracy": 0.30906148867313915, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5990776699029127, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.290588191854669, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31276639547627955, "cosine_similarity": 0.4276384268929457, "direction_accuracy": 0.30906148867313915, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5990776699029127, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97089225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 34}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_082", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77.1% of rows are positive with median +1.459 in an unspecified logarithm base, so all directional statements above are percentile ranks within this shifted set, not absolute up/down calls.", "Percentile rank within the supplied rows is an acceptable internal background correction; if the row selection is itself biased toward lysosomal genes, the enrichment (nominal p = 0.035, uncorrected for the ~10 gene sets tested) could be an artefact of selection.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be monotonically related to protein synthesis rate, but not to enzyme activity, lysosomal luminal flux or lipid localisation; activity, flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred throughout and are not measured here.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and ATP6V1E1-containing spots are down (protein_spot:064), so the proteomic layer neither confirms nor uniquely refutes step 2.", "No lipid, sterol, cholesteryl-ester or imaging measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier; lysosomal lipid retention and lipid-droplet storage are predictions, not observations.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcripts may derive from, or be contaminated by, non-microglial RNA, and genotype-associated differences in differentiation state or cell composition could generate the same transcript pattern without any change in lysosomal flux.", "Effect magnitude and adjusted p-value are essentially uncorrelated in these rows (Spearman -0.03), so extreme individual effect sizes (e.g. gene:SCARB1) are treated as directionally informative but quantitatively unreliable.", "Causality is not established by these data; the hypothesis is a mechanistic proposal to be tested by the perturbations below."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a coordinated upward shift of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (strongest for glycosidase/sphingolipid-catabolic genes) together with a markedly elevated lipoprotein-uptake receptor transcript (SCARB1), while sterol-homeostatic transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, INSIG1, LDLR, MYLIP and post-squalene enzymes) sit at background rank with no repression signature. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not hydrolase gene dosage but egress of liberated lipid (sterol and sphingoid species) from the endolysosome to the ER: internalised lipid is retained in a hydrolase-rich lysosomal compartment, the ER-accessible sterol pool is therefore not raised, sterol-feedback repression is not engaged, and overflow lipid is routed to esterification/desaturation (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD). The assigned sterol-synthesis/efflux focus is rejected as a primary driver because that gene set shows no shift relative to the global background of these DE-selected rows.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute bypass of lysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should, within 6-24 h, reduce LAMP1-colocalised unesterified cholesterol and lower SREBP2-arm transcripts (HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS, LDLR) and SCARB1 relative to untreated APOE4, with a smaller change in isogenic APOE3. If lysosomal cholesterol is demonstrably cleared yet these transcripts and cholesteryl-ester content are unchanged, the lysosome-to-ER egress bottleneck is falsified.", "Flux versus abundance: live-cell substrate clearance (BODIPY-lactosylceramide, DQ-BSA, LysoTracker-normalised GBA/HEXA/CTSB activity) should show equal or slower per-lysosome clearance in APOE4 despite higher transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1A). If APOE4 clears substrate faster with no measurable lysosomal lipid or glycosphingolipid accumulation, the bottleneck claim fails and the transcript shift should be reinterpreted as a benign expression difference.", "Input dependence: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade in APOE4 microglia should reduce lysosomal lipid load and blunt the hydrolase transcript signature; no change in either readout would weaken step 1 as the source of substrate.", "Direction of the transcriptional response: TFEB/TFEC knockdown in APOE4 should lower hydrolase transcripts while leaving or worsening lysosomal lipid accumulation, consistent with a compensatory response. If knockdown instead abolishes lipid accumulation, the transcriptional expansion is a driver rather than a compensation and the framing of step 2 is wrong.", "Proteoform test for the ambiguous spot data: targeted immunoblot or MS resolving pro- versus mature cathepsin B/D should explain the discordant spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down). Mature hydrolase protein that is unchanged or reduced in APOE4 despite higher transcripts supports a flux, not dosage, bottleneck; proportional increases in mature enzyme with normal substrate clearance weaken the mechanism.", "Specificity control: the sterol biosynthetic enzymes absent from these rows (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1, CYP51A1) and the efflux genes ABCA1/ABCG1 should be measured directly; a strong coordinated increase of the mevalonate arm with elevated ABCA1 would favour a sterol-synthesis/efflux mechanism over the retention mechanism proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (input, measured RNA / inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors, dominated by SCARB1 (99th percentile of the measured effect distribution, adjusted p 3.4e-117), with APOE, CD36, COLEC12, CD163, MRC1 and TREM2 present near background rank; we infer, but do not measure, increased delivery of lipoprotein-associated lipid into the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): the endolysosomal degradative module is coherently shifted upward relative to the global background of these rows (21 genes, mean percentile rank 63.0 vs 50 expected, permutation p = 0.035), driven by glycosidases and sphingolipid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1 all \u003e=95th percentile), CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, with TFEB and TFEC transcripts also above background; we read this as a CLEAR-type transcriptional response to persistent substrate load, not as proof of higher enzyme activity.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred, not measured): lysosome-to-ER transfer of liberated cholesterol and sphingoid lipid is proposed to be rate-limiting in APOE4. The key nodes of that route (NPC1, LIPA, STARD3, STARD4, ABCA1, ABCG1) are absent from the supplied rows and NPC2 sits below background (35th percentile), so this step is an inference about flux and localisation, not an observed molecular pool.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, negative signature): because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not raised, SREBP2-arm transcripts show no feedback repression: SREBF2 (28th percentile), HMGCS1 (28th), MYLIP (41st), LDLR (51st), INSIG1 (60th), LSS (67th), DHCR7 (73rd), DHCR24 (85th); the sterol set as a whole is indistinguishable from background (10 genes, mean percentile 54.2, p = 0.65). Uptake and synthesis programmes therefore continue rather than being switched off.", "Step 5 (measured RNA / inferred lipid fate): overflow lipid that does reach the cytosolic side is inferred to be esterified and stored rather than exported, consistent with SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD and FADS1 transcripts being present and SCD at the 89th percentile; no lipid, cholesteryl-ester or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so the storage phenotype is predicted, not observed.", "Step 6 (consequence): a chronically substrate-loaded, egress-limited lysosome plus sustained uptake defines the APOE4 microglial state under mock conditions and is accompanied by a downward shift of mitochondrial/OXPHOS-related transcripts (7 genes, mean percentile 26.2, p = 0.028), which we treat as a correlated consequence rather than an established cause."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sit in a hydrolase-expanded but egress-limited endolysosome: lipid substrate is retained in the lysosome instead of being delivered to the ER"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14642026363401395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2014549402315447, "cosine_similarity": 0.42660741461090423, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059967637540453, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14642026363401395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2014549402315447, "cosine_similarity": 0.42660741461090423, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059967637540453, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.77847425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 35}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_064", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are treated as ordered relative changes and are not placed on the same numeric scale as the log2 protein-spot effects.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive median (about +1.46), so only within-list relative comparisons (set median versus global median) are interpreted; no statement is made about absolute transcript numbers per cell.", "The relative deficit of mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflects a real per-cell shortfall of mtDNA-encoded subunit supply rather than a compositional or probe-capture artefact of 10X Flex quantification.", "Transcript abundance of nuclear OXPHOS, TCA and transporter genes is a usable proxy for the direction of protein supply; assembled complex content, enzyme activity, metabolite pools and flux were not measured.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins, so no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme change.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; the measured transcripts are assumed to derive predominantly from microglia, and the APOE4/APOE3 comparison is assumed isogenic as stated in the metadata.", "Day-30 APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed to be at comparable differentiation and proliferative states, so the metabolic contrast is not merely a maturation-stage difference."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, transcripts for mtDNA-encoded core subunits of complexes IV/III/V (gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-ND4) are relatively depleted while nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, TCA-cycle, mitochondrial import/translation and substrate-transporter transcripts are relatively enriched above the strong global positive shift of this selected DE list. We hypothesise that the bottleneck is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for assembly of the respiratory complexes, so that oxidative ATP flux does not scale with the increased nuclear-encoded machinery; because upper glycolysis is not co-upregulated (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2 fall below the global centre despite raised glucose transporters), imported carbon is instead routed through anaplerosis and citrate/malate export (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) into a lipogenic and lysosomal-lipid programme (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA). Only relative RNA abundance and ambiguous protein-spot abundance were measured; assembly, flux, localization and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM or mitochondrial-translation-boosting overexpression, or allotopic/AOX-style bypass of the affected complexes) should restore assembled complex III/IV/V levels by blue-native PAGE, raise ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption, and reduce neutral lipid droplet content, with a significantly larger effect in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3; equal or absent benefit in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show lower ATP-linked and maximal (FCCP) oxygen consumption and reduced spare respiratory capacity in APOE4, with only a blunted oligomycin-induced glycolytic (ECAR) compensation; equal or higher maximal respiration in APOE4, or a robust glycolytic compensation, would weaken it.", "Spike-in-normalised RT-qPCR or single-molecule FISH per cell, plus mtDNA copy number, should confirm a genuine per-cell reduction of MT-CO2/MT-CYB/MT-ATP6 transcripts in APOE4; unchanged per-cell mtDNA-encoded transcript numbers would show the observed decrease is compositional and would falsify the premise of Step 1.", "Stable-isotope tracing should show reduced [U-13C]glucose-derived m+2 citrate and lower fractional pyruvate oxidation in APOE4, with increased [U-13C]glutamine contribution to citrate and to newly synthesised lipid; glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) should preferentially lower ATP, viability and lipid droplet accumulation in APOE4 relative to APOE3. Equal glucose-to-citrate labelling in the two genotypes, or an equal CB-839 effect, would weaken the mechanism.", "Immunoblot/BN-PAGE should show accumulation of unassembled nuclear-encoded subunits with reduced assembled complexes and elevated mitochondrial chaperone/stress proteins (e.g. HSPA9, DDIT3 targets) in APOE4; assembled complexes scaling proportionally with nuclear subunit transcripts would falsify Step 2.", "SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) inhibition or knockdown should reduce APOE4 lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester accumulation without correcting the respiratory deficit; if SLC25A1 blockade instead restores respiration, the proposed direction of carbon rerouting is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, relative abundance): against a global median RNA effect of about +1.46 in this selected DE list, mtDNA-encoded transcripts sit below the centre (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) while nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts sit well above it (median about +2.6; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:COX5B), a mito-nuclear discordance (Mann-Whitney p = 3.7e-4).", "Step 2 (inferred activity/assembly, not measured): the shortfall of mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores relative to imported nuclear subunits makes assembly of complexes III, IV and V, rather than nuclear subunit supply, the rate-limiting step for coupled respiration; increased import/translation transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:TUFM) are read as compensatory supply, not as evidence of higher assembled complex content.", "Step 3 (inferred stress signalling): unassembled subunits and matrix redox load elicit a mitochondrial proteostatic/integrated stress response, consistent with gene:HSPA9, gene:DDIT3, gene:SHMT2 and gene:PRDX3 being raised above the global centre.", "Step 4 (inferred flux compensation): APOE4 cells raise substrate import and anaplerotic/shuttle capacity (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1, gene:SLC25A5) in an attempt to sustain TCA carbon input despite the assembly bottleneck.", "Step 5 (measured counter-direction): upper glycolysis is not co-upregulated (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10 versus global +1.46), so glycolytic ATP cannot be inferred as an effective compensation route even though glucose transporter transcripts rise.", "Step 6 (inferred carbon rerouting): with terminal oxidation limited, mitochondrial carbon is predicted to leave as citrate/malate (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) and feed cytosolic acetyl-CoA and lipogenesis/esterification (gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1), with expanded lysosomal lipid handling (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:SCARB1) rather than being fully oxidised."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch makes mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply the rate-limiting step for oxidative carbon use in APOE4 microglia, diverting glucose/glutamine carbon to citrate export and lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09686888454011741, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2933389574167961, "cosine_similarity": 0.4265896692463565, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mean_absolute_error": 0.580378640776699, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09686888454011741, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2933389574167961, "cosine_similarity": 0.4265896692463565, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "mean_absolute_error": 0.580378640776699, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5203795, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 36}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_124", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so absolute up/down fractions are biased; we therefore rely on rank-based contrasts within the list (nuclear mitochondrial vs the remaining rows, and nuclear vs mtDNA-encoded) rather than on the global positive shift, whose logarithm base is unspecified and is left unconverted.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcripts captured by the 10X Flex probe panel are assumed to be a fair relative readout of mitochondrial transcript abundance; if that panel quantifies MT genes unreliably, Step 2 collapses.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partially predictive of the corresponding protein pool and of complex assembly; no OXPHOS subunit protein, mtDNA copy number, assembled-complex, metabolite, isotope-tracing or respirometry measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (e.g. protein_spot:038 candidates ALDOA/ALDOC/SORD/TKT/ARPC1B; protein_spot:072 candidates PGAM1/CAPG and others), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein or as confirmation of any enzyme.", "The comparison is assumed to reflect microglial cells in the astrocyte co-culture rather than differing cell-type composition, differentiation stage, or proliferative state between APOE4 and APOE3 wells; replicate number is not supplied in the workbook.", "The lipid-storage endpoint is inferred from transcripts only; no lipid, lipid-droplet or cholesteryl-ester measurement is included here."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia mount a coordinated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (OXPHOS subunits, assembly factors, TCA enzymes, inner-membrane carriers, import machinery) while transcripts for mtDNA-encoded core subunits of complexes III, IV and V are relatively reduced. We propose that the availability of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembled respiratory-chain capacity, so the nuclear program cannot be converted into proportional oxidative ATP flux; because the committed glycolytic steps (hexokinase-2, PFKP/PFKFB2) are simultaneously down-regulated despite increased glucose-transporter transcripts, glycolysis cannot compensate, and carbon entering the TCA cycle from glutamine/aspartate is preferentially exported as citrate to acetyl-CoA-consuming lipid esterification and sterol pathways, accompanied by an integrated-stress-response transcriptional signature. All statements about flux, assembly and localization are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (mitochondrial translation/mtDNA supply): boosting mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM or TFB2M overexpression, or allotopic/mitochondrially targeted expression of MT-ATP6 and MT-CO2) should raise fully assembled complex IV and V (BN-PAGE) and maximal FCCP-stimulated oxygen consumption per unit mitochondrial mass toward APOE3 levels WITHOUT normalising the nuclear OXPHOS transcript program. If assembled complexes and respiration are already equal to APOE3 at baseline, or if the rescue changes nothing while nuclear transcripts fall, the bottleneck is misplaced and the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (carbon-source dependency): APOE4 microglia should show a smaller glucose-driven ECAR/lactate increment and greater sensitivity to glutaminase inhibition (CB-839/BPTES: larger fall in ATP and TCA-intermediate pools) than APOE3, while 2-deoxyglucose should hurt APOE4 less. The opposite pattern (greater 2-DG sensitivity, glutaminase resistance in APOE4) would falsify the substrate-switch step.", "Tracer prediction: U-13C-glucose should contribute a lower fraction of citrate m+2 and of newly synthesised palmitate/cholesteryl-ester carbon in APOE4 than APOE3, with a compensating increase from U-13C-glutamine; equal glucose-derived labelling would weaken Steps 4-6.", "Stoichiometry prediction (orthogonal assay): by RT-qPCR or a non-probe-based RNA method plus mtDNA qPCR, the ratio of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2 transcript to nuclear OXPHOS transcript, and probably mtDNA copy number per nucleus, should be lower in APOE4; equal or higher ratios by an orthogonal method would directly falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Ordering prediction: ISRIB or HRI/DELE1 knockdown should blunt the DDIT3/PSPH/SHMT2 signature without restoring assembled complexes or respiration, placing the stress response downstream; if ISRIB restores respiration and complex assembly, the ISR - not mitonuclear mismatch - is the proximal driver.", "Phenotype prediction: hexokinase-2 re-expression alone should not normalise APOE4 oxygen consumption or neutral-lipid content (it should mainly raise lactate); if HK2 re-expression normalises both, the glycolytic step, not the assembly step, is limiting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_124", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coherent up-shift of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts far above the already positive background of this selected DE list - 54/57 nuclear mitochondrial genes positive, mean effect +2.8 vs global mean +1.4, rank-based Mann-Whitney p=1.3e-05 (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2), together with TCA (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD) and import/carrier transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:SLC25A5).", "Step 2 (measured, RNA; the proposed bottleneck): transcripts for mtDNA-encoded core subunits move in the opposite direction (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; percentile ranks 5-19 of the DE list), giving a nuclear-vs-mtDNA discordance (Mann-Whitney p=7.9e-04). We infer, but did not measure, that reduced mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits assembly of complexes III, IV and V.", "Step 3 (inferred activity/flux): assembly-limited complexes cap electron-transport and ATP-synthase flux, so the increased nuclear subunit and TCA transcript pools are not matched by proportional oxidative ATP production; a partly uncoupled/incompletely assembled chain is consistent with the up-regulated matrix chaperone/quality transcripts gene:HSPA9 and mitochondrial translation-elongation transcript gene:TUFM.", "Step 4 (measured, RNA): the glycolytic escape route is restricted at the committed steps - gene:HK2 -3.67 and gene:PFKP -3.08 (bottom 4-6 percentile of the DE list) and gene:PFKFB2 -1.10 - even though glucose-uptake transcripts rise (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73) and downstream glycolytic transcripts are up (gene:GPI, gene:ENO1); oxidative-PPP branch transcripts fall (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1), and gene:GYS1 rises, consistent with inferred diversion of hexose phosphate away from committed glycolysis.", "Step 5 (inferred substrate switch, RNA support): anaplerotic amino-acid entry is up (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2) with citrate and 2-oxoglutarate/malate carriers (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11) and fatty-acid oxidation transcripts (gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA), predicting glutamine/lipid rather than glucose as the dominant TCA carbon source.", "Step 6 (inferred carbon disposal): acetyl-CoA-consuming esterification and sterol programs rise (gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) alongside lysosomal-lipid handling (gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), so carbon that cannot be fully oxidised is predicted to accumulate as neutral-lipid/sterol ester rather than CO2.", "Step 7 (measured stress readout): an integrated-stress-response-like transcriptional signature accompanies the state (gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:PSPH, gene:SHMT2, gene:NUPR1) with gene:PRKAA1 up, consistent with, but not proof of, an energy/mitochondrial stress signal downstream of the bottleneck."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch in APOE4 microglia: an assembly-limited respiratory chain with a closed glycolytic escape route diverts carbon to lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09784735812133072, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2872791386516482, "cosine_similarity": 0.42602367984980627, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_124", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5799190938511327, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09784735812133072, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2872791386516482, "cosine_similarity": 0.42602367984980627, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5799190938511327, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5426835, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 37}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_169", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 up, median +1.46 in an unspecified log base); therefore only the position of a gene set relative to this shifted background, not its direction alone, is treated as evidence.", "Transcript differences for hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and trafficking factors partly translate into protein and organelle-level capacity; measured RNA abundance is not equated with hydrolytic activity, luminal pH, cargo flux or organelle localization.", "TFEB/MITF transcript elevation reflects an active lysosomal-biogenesis program; TFEB activity is set mainly by nuclear translocation, which is not measured here.", "The SREBP target signature reports on the ER-accessible sterol pool; this pool, lysosomal cholesterol and lipid droplets were not measured in this dataset.", "2-D protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each; ACTB, KRT1, KRT10 recur in 25-33 spots), so spot changes are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration that cytoskeletal and lysosomal spot families are perturbed.", "Genotype effects are cell-intrinsic to microglia rather than driven by the astrocyte co-culture partner, which cannot be tested with the supplied data.", "APOE4 lipoprotein particles are less efficiently lipidated and more prone to intracellular retention than APOE3 (unverified background knowledge, not derived from these observations)."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference is best explained by a rate-limiting step downstream of internalization: cargo that is taken up accumulates in the late-endosome/lysosome because per-organelle catabolic and lipid-export capacity is not matched to load. The transcriptional signature is consistent with a compensatory TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-biogenesis program (hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, RAB7A/HOPS/ESCRT/retromer components elevated) running simultaneously with an ER-sterol-deficit program (SREBF1/SREBF2 and downstream sterol/fatty-acid synthesis genes elevated) and with esterification/storage genes (SOAT1, DGAT1) elevated, despite elevated lipid- and debris-uptake receptor transcripts. Simultaneous 'more uptake receptors', 'more lysosomal machinery' and 'more de novo sterol synthesis' is the paradox that identifies the egress/catabolism step, not uptake capacity, as the bottleneck. Increased uptake flux, lysosomal lipid load, hydrolase activity, and organelle localization are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (uptake block vs egress block): treating APOE4 microglia with a dynamin inhibitor or SCARB1/CD36 blockade for 24 h should lower lysosomal neutral-lipid/filipin signal yet leave the SREBP target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, LDLR, SCD, DHCR24) equal or higher, because the ER sterol deficit is caused by failed egress rather than by cargo excess. If uptake blockade instead normalizes SREBP targets down to APOE3 levels, the bottleneck is at uptake and this mechanism is wrong.", "Bypassing the inferred egress step in APOE4 with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 over-expression) should selectively suppress SREBP target transcripts toward APOE3 levels and reduce filipin-positive LAMP1 compartments while leaving uptake-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, MERTK, MRC1) largely unchanged. No fall in SREBP targets despite reduced lysosomal cholesterol would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy test: acute U18666A or NPC1 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the joint APOE4 signature (coordinate rise of hydrolase/v-ATPase/TFEB-target transcripts together with SREBF2 targets). Producing only one of the two arms would weaken the proposed single-bottleneck explanation.", "Flux test separating uptake from degradation: pulse-chase of fluorescent myelin, apoptotic-cell or DQ-BSA cargo should show equal or faster internalization in APOE4 but slower dequenching/clearance per internalized particle. Slower internalization in APOE4 would falsify mechanism step 1; equal clearance per particle would falsify the bottleneck placement.", "Capacity vs activity test: despite elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts, measured lysosomal cathepsin B/D activity and acidification per LAMP1 area in APOE4 should be at most modestly increased and clearly insufficient relative to cargo load; a large, load-matched increase in hydrolytic activity would weaken the compensatory-biogenesis interpretation.", "Cytoskeletal counter-prediction: APOE4 microglia should not show a uniform increase in filamentous-actin phagocytic machinery; F/G-actin ratio and non-muscle myosin IIA protein should be unchanged or reduced consistent with gene:ACTB and gene:MYH9 being lower. A strong coordinate increase in actomyosin protein and phagocytic-cup formation rate would favour a cytoskeletal rather than an endolysosomal-egress mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_169", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipid/debris-recognition receptors and opsonin genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:ITGB5, gene:APOE), which we interpret as increased or at least undiminished capacity for cargo engagement; the internalization step itself is not limiting, since clathrin/dynamin and branched-actin transcripts are also higher (gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:ITSN1, gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5, gene:CFL1, gene:TWF2, gene:SSH1, gene:MYO1E).", "Internalized cargo is routed into a RAB7A-positive maturation pathway whose transcripts are coordinately elevated (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS37B, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:SNX17), so vesicle delivery to the degradative compartment is inferred to be intact or increased.", "Degradative demand exceeds per-organelle capacity, engaging a compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis program: transcripts for the CLEAR-type regulators (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) and for hydrolases, membrane proteins and every measured v-ATPase subunit are raised well above the already up-shifted background (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SMPD1, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D2). Elevated transcript abundance is taken as evidence of a biogenesis response, not as proof of increased hydrolytic flux.", "Despite this uptake- and biogenesis-competent state, the ER sterol sensor behaves as if cholesterol-starved: SREBP genes and their canonical sterol/lipogenic targets are uniformly elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:MYLIP). We infer that lipid derived from internalized cargo is not reaching the ER-accessible sterol pool, i.e. the bottleneck is lysosomal lipid catabolism/export (an inferred flux, with the key exporter NPC1 not measured in this dataset).", "Sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are preferentially esterified and stored rather than used to shut off synthesis or to be effluxed (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ABCA7 elevated), which sustains the apparent ER sterol deficit and closes a futile uptake-synthesis-storage loop.", "The net predicted cell state is a lipid-laden, biogenesis-stressed endolysosomal system with reduced degradative throughput per unit cargo, accompanied by a remodelled rather than uniformly amplified cytoskeleton (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:MYO1F, gene:FAM49B, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8 are lower in APOE4), and by 2-D spot-level changes in cytoskeletal/lysosomal spot families in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:081, protein_spot:036, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:065), consistent with redistribution/modification rather than a simple net increase."], "title": "APOE4 microglia bottleneck at endolysosomal cargo catabolism/sterol egress, not at uptake or actin-driven internalization"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24119539211267052, "cosine_similarity": 0.4259774172699135, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_169", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5922750809061489, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24119539211267052, "cosine_similarity": 0.4259774172699135, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5922750809061489, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71394925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 38}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_055", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a |log fold change| \u003e= 1 selection floor (minimum observed 1.0001) and an unspecified logarithm base; only sign and rank within this list are interpreted, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The strong global upward shift (1705/2212 rows positive, median +1.46) reflects selection and/or normalisation of this pseudobulk comparison, so all set-level claims are made against the internal rank distribution of the supplied rows, not against zero.", "Higher hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript levels are assumed to report demand-driven transcriptional output; they are not assumed to equal hydrolase protein amount, luminal pH, or catabolic rate.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes; spot-level directional discordance is treated as a hypothesis-generating pattern about proteoform distribution, not as identification of CTSB, CTSD, HSPA5 or HSP90B1 abundance.", "No lipid, flux, pH, imaging, autophagy-flux or single-protein immunoblot measurements were supplied; lipid accumulation, esterification flux and fusion competence are inferred, not observed.", "APOE3/APOE4 lines are stated to be isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than clone-specific drift or astrocyte co-culture composition is assumed to drive the differences; replicate numbers were not supplied.", "Background pathway memberships used to group genes are unverified analyst knowledge, not retrieved from any database in this session."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in the endolysosomal-lipid axis, not in ER proteostasis: transcripts for acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB and mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery are coordinately higher (hydrolase set median +3.69, permutation p=0.0003; whole-lysosome set p=0.035), while transcripts for late fusion SNAREs are lower and hydrolase-containing 2D protein spots move in opposite directions. We propose that the rate-limiting step is degradative flux of lipid substrate inside the acidified late endosome/lysosome, that the transcriptional hydrolase/acidification program is a compensatory demand signal rather than evidence of restored catabolic capacity, and that unhydrolysed lipid is shunted into esterification and storage supported by elevated anaplerotic/citrate-export transcripts (TCA set median +4.47, p=0.0001) and lipogenic/sterol transcripts. Causality is not established by these data; RNA and spot abundances are measurements, all fluxes, activities, pH, localisations and lipid pools are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) or a pan-cathepsin/acid-lipase block applied to mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should produce a SMALLER incremental increase in lysosomal undegraded-substrate readouts (DQ-BSA or BODIPY-LacCer/BODIPY-cholesterol retention in LAMP1+ compartments) in APOE4, because APOE4 lysosomes are already near the degradative ceiling; equal or larger incremental responses in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Per-lysosome degradative rate (DQ-BSA dequenching or fluorogenic GBA/HEXA substrate turnover normalised to LAMP1+ volume) should be LOWER in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; if per-lysosome turnover is equal or higher in APOE4, the mechanism fails and the transcript program should instead be read as increased functional capacity.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content preferentially in APOE4 while increasing lysosomal free-sterol and membrane-stress readouts in APOE4 more than APOE3; absence of a genotype-by-drug interaction would weaken step 4.", "Blocking mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1 inhibition or knockdown) or ACSS2 inhibition should normalise the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess in newly synthesised esterified lipid measured by 13C-glucose/13C-acetate tracing; if APOE4 shows no elevated de novo lipogenic flux, step 5 is refuted and the TCA transcript signal must be reinterpreted.", "TFEB knockdown should exaggerate lipid/substrate accumulation and reduce hydrolase transcripts disproportionately in APOE4; if the hydrolase transcript elevation persists unchanged after TFEB knockdown, the compensatory-biogenesis framing in step 1 is wrong.", "Immunoblot of CTSD and CTSB should show an altered pro-form to mature-form ratio (or altered glycoform migration) in APOE4, matching the bidirectional 2D-spot pattern (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069); identical maturation ratios with uniformly higher total hydrolase protein would weaken step 2 and favour a simple capacity increase.", "ER-stress discrimination: BiP/GRP94 protein, XBP1 splicing, phospho-eIF2-alpha and ATF4/CHOP protein should NOT be substantially higher in APOE4 under mock conditions, consistent with the flat ER-stress transcript set (median +1.36, permutation p=0.67) and the non-significant, negative HSPA5/HSP90B1-candidate spots (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005); clear constitutive XBP1 splicing or BiP induction in APOE4 would favour the rejected ER-proteostasis mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lysosomal acid hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1) and for v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1) together with gene:TFEB and gene:LAMP1; we infer, but did not measure, increased TFEB-type transcriptional output driven by unmet luminal degradative demand.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): degradative flux through the acidified late endosome/lysosome is limiting in APOE4 despite the higher hydrolase transcript pool, because delivery/fusion transcripts are discordant (gene:STX17, gene:STX16, gene:VAMP2, gene:M6PR lower; gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R, gene:VPS26A, gene:RAB7A, gene:SNX3 higher) and hydrolase-containing protein spots redistribute in both directions (protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:052 up, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 down) rather than shifting uniformly upward, a pattern compatible with altered proform/mature or glycoform partitioning; spot identities are ambiguous and this step is not directly demonstrated.", "Step 3 (inferred): lipid substrate that is not hydrolysed in the lysosome (free cholesterol, sphingolipid and glycerolipid backbones) accumulates in a compartment that was not measured here; no lipid species were supplied in this dataset.", "Step 4 (measured): the anabolic/esterification arm is transcriptionally elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DHCR24, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36); we infer increased esterification and neutral-lipid storage flux, which was not measured.", "Step 5 (measured): mitochondrial anaplerotic and citrate/acetyl-CoA supply transcripts are the most coherently elevated group (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:MPC2, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:GLUD1, gene:BCAT2) alongside nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFB5), while the few mitochondrially encoded transcripts trend down (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4); we infer that cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply for esterification is sustained, not that respiration is increased.", "Step 6 (measured, subordinate secretory element): the ER N-glycosylation/quality-control and hydrolase-tagging arm is elevated (gene:MLEC, gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:UGGT1, gene:SDF4, gene:GNPTG) whereas canonical ER-stress/ERAD effectors are flat or lower (gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1, gene:PDIA3, gene:SEC62); we therefore assign the ER changes to increased hydrolase biosynthetic/tagging load rather than to an unfolded-protein response."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a lysosomal acid-hydrolase and acidification program with a limiting late-endolysosomal degradative flux, diverting lipid substrate toward mitochondrial-citrate-fed esterification rather than an ER unfolded-protein response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17318982387475537, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18738666772037488, "cosine_similarity": 0.42546141264636755, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027443365695793, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17318982387475537, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18738666772037488, "cosine_similarity": 0.42546141264636755, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027443365695793, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.924373, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 39}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_086", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so set-level statements are interpreted relative to the internal background (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% positive), not as absolute induction; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is left unconverted.", "Higher transcript abundance for lysosomal, V-ATPase and sterol-synthesis genes is assumed to translate into a correspondingly larger/more active compartment and sustained SREBP output; no protein, pH, activity, flux, localisation or lipid measurement in this dataset tests that assumption.", "The global positive shift is assumed to be at least partly technical (compositional/normalisation), supported by strongly negative values for highly expressed transcripts (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35); only within-list relative ordering is used for inference.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-unique multi-gene identifications and are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration, never as identified proteins.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply lipoprotein-borne lipid to microglia in both genotypes so that the genotype contrast reflects microglial handling rather than differential supply.", "The mock, day-30 single timepoint is assumed to represent a steady state rather than a transient."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a bottleneck in hydrolysis and export of internalised lipid/sterol from the endolysosome, not by interferon or NF-kB activation. Transcripts encoding lysosomal acidification, hydrolase and biogenesis machinery, lysosomal-stress markers, and scavenger-uptake receptors are coordinately higher in APOE4, while ER sterol-sensing output (SREBP target and cholesterol-synthesis transcripts) remains high rather than being suppressed, the pattern expected if sterol is retained in a distal compartment and never reaches the ER sensing pool. The apparent expansion of lysosomal machinery is inferred to be a compensatory response to, not a resolution of, this bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute cyclodextrin (HP-beta-CD) treatment, which mobilises sterol out of the lysosomal lumen and bypasses the proposed bottleneck, should in APOE4 but not APOE3 microglia (i) reduce filipin-positive/LAMP1-colocalised sterol and LipidTOX droplet volume and (ii) suppress SREBP target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR, SCD) toward APOE3 levels within 24 h. If SREBP targets remain elevated after luminal sterol is cleared, the sterol-sensing-failure step is wrong.", "Contrasting perturbation that separates a storage bottleneck from an egress bottleneck: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe/CI-976) should lower cholesteryl-ester content in both genotypes but, under this hypothesis, should NOT normalise the APOE4 lysosomal-gene or SREBP-target elevation. If SOAT1 inhibition alone normalises both, the bottleneck is esterification, not lysosomal egress.", "Functional stress test: partial V-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) or TFEB knockdown should disproportionately increase undigested lipid/BODIPY-LDL accumulation and lysosomal galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 relative to APOE3, because the elevated acidification/biogenesis program is proposed to be compensatory. Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the compensation claim.", "Direct state check: APOE4 microglia should show measurably larger LAMP1+ compartment volume, more galectin-3 puncta, and higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio by lipidomics than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal compartment volume and equal lipid content would falsify the core claim even if the transcript differences replicate.", "Negative prediction for the assigned focus: blocking type-I interferon (anti-IFNAR2 or JAK1/2 inhibition) or NF-kB (IKK inhibition) should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal/sterol transcript differences, and no canonical ISG module (MX1, OAS1, IFIT1/3, ISG15, STAT1) should be induced in APOE4. Detection of a coherent ISG induction with genotype-dependent JAK sensitivity would falsify the rejection of the interferon mechanism and this hypothesis's framing.", "Replication requirement: with matched library-size/composition normalisation and true biological replicates, the lysosome/V-ATPase set should retain a positive median shift relative to the measured background. Loss of the shift after correction would indicate the signal is a normalisation artifact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mechanism_steps": ["Elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, with gene:APOE +1.24 itself higher) are inferred to sustain or increase flux of lipid and cholesteryl-ester cargo into the endolysosomal system; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Cargo delivered to the lysosome is inferred to be cleared inefficiently in APOE4, so lipid and free sterol are retained in the lumen and limiting membrane (a retained pool that was NOT measured in this dataset).", "Retention triggers a compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis and acidification program: coordinate higher transcripts for the V-ATPase (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, all 8 measured ATP6V subunits positive), acid hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:MAN2B1), transport/fusion factors (gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2) and the master regulator transcript gene:TFEB. TFEB protein nuclear localisation and actual luminal pH/hydrolase activity are inferred, not measured.", "Persistent membrane stress in this compartment is marked at the transcript level by gene:LGALS3 and gene:GPNMB, both raised in APOE4; galectin-3 recruitment to damaged lysosomes and GPNMB accumulation are inferred activities, not observed localisations.", "Because sterol is inferred to be trapped distal to the ER, the ER sterol sensor reads deficiency and the SREBP program is not switched off: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50 and gene:SCD +4.17 are all positive in APOE4 despite the uptake signature, a futile-synthesis configuration.", "The excess lipid is inferred to be routed into esterified storage and alternative oxysterol disposal rather than efflux: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49 are higher, generating a lipid-laden, GPNMB/LGALS3/CD163/MRC1-high microglial state (gene:CD163, gene:MRC1, gene:TGFBI) instead of an interferon state.", "Consistent with the interferon/inflammation focus being unsupported here, no canonical ISG module is present or elevated above the strong global positive background, and several NF-kB/inflammatory transcripts move down (gene:IRF2 -1.17, gene:RELB -1.30, gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:CTSS -5.57)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at lysosomal lipid clearance: a TFEB/v-ATPase-expanded, damage-marked acidic compartment coexists with an un-suppressed SREBP sterol program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24480089995849266, "cosine_similarity": 0.42520977935297916, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mean_absolute_error": 0.594336569579288, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24480089995849266, "cosine_similarity": 0.42520977935297916, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.594336569579288, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.59164425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 40}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_070", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 on an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77.1% positive); programs were judged against that 77% positive background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is treated as a proxy for expression demand only; no respiration rate, complex assembly, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, ROS level, lipid-droplet or cholesteryl-ester content was measured, so all flux, localisation and capacity statements are inferred.", "Pathway members were fixed a priori from canonical membership (regex families for NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH and SLC25A) and every matched member is reported, including sign-discordant ones; coherence is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test, and genes within a program are not independent.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each; all candidate identities are preserved and no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. The spot set is itself biased upward (38 significant up vs 9 down of 92), so spot direction is used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels in droplet single-cell data are sensitive to ambient RNA and dissociation; the mitonuclear mismatch is therefore a hypothesis requiring protein/assembly confirmation, not an established stoichiometric defect.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes at day 30 under mock treatment; astrocyte-derived lipid supply is part of the condition and is not separately measured.", "Causality is not established by these data; the ordering lipid-state -\u003e mitochondrial expansion is inferred from program coherence and could be reversed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change: sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, lipid uptake and esterification, and lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts are coherently higher (17/17 and 23/25 represented members positive, vs a 77% positive selected-list background), and this is accompanied by the strongest program in the data, a nuclear-encoded mitochondrial expansion program (38/38 detected NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH subunits positive, P~5e-5 vs background; TCA 9/9 positive; carriers SLC25A1/A11/A13/MPC2 positive). Because the six detected mtDNA-encoded subunits are not coordinately increased (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33 vs MT-ND5 +1.93, MT-ND4L +1.95), the elevated nuclear transcripts indicate raised biogenesis demand rather than demonstrated respiratory capacity, and the accompanying antioxidant increases are compartment-restricted (matrix/membrane PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, MGST2, GSS, NNT, UCP2) rather than a peroxisomal or global NRF2 program. The assigned peroxisomal focus is rejected as primary: only 7/41 peroxisomal members are represented, 4 positive (P=0.95 vs background), no PEX or catalase RNA row exists, and OXR1 is strongly negative (-3.63).", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, blue-native PAGE / immunoblot for mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-CO1, MT-CO2, MT-ND1) normalised to mitochondrial mass (TOMM20, mtDNA copy number) will show that assembled complex I/IV and mtDNA-encoded subunit protein do NOT rise in proportion to the nuclear-subunit transcript increase. If assembled complexes, mtDNA-encoded protein and ATP-linked respiration all rise proportionally, the mitonuclear-mismatch element is falsified and the data instead indicate successful increased respiratory throughput.", "Prospective perturbation (discriminating, tests causal ordering): inhibiting cholesterol esterification (SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor) or blocking lipoprotein/scavenger uptake (LDLR/CD36 knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should lower the lysosomal (CTSB/CTSD/ATP6V) and SREBP-target transcripts and shift the nuclear OXPHOS/TCA/carrier program back toward APOE3 levels. If the mitochondrial program is unchanged while lipid genes normalise, lipid routing is not upstream and the mitochondrial program must be treated as primary.", "Prospective, reserve vs ongoing defect: basal OCR in mock APOE4 may equal or exceed APOE3, but FCCP-stimulated maximal and spare respiratory capacity after a lipid or phagocytic load (myelin debris, apoptotic cells) should be lower in APOE4. Equal spare capacity under challenge would weaken the reduced-reserve claim without affecting the measured-state description.", "Prospective, redox compartment test (tests the assigned focus): mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoTEMPO/MitoQ) or PRDX3/PRDX5 knockdown should differentially affect APOE4 (rescue or sensitisation, respectively) more than APOE3, whereas peroxisomal catalase inhibition (3-aminotriazole) or peroxisome proliferation should produce little genotype-selective effect. A strong genotype-selective peroxisomal effect would favour the rejected peroxisomal explanation over the matrix-restricted one.", "Prospective, protein-level test of the lysosomal arm: targeted immunoblot/immunofluorescence for CTSB, CTSD, LAMP1 and GBA (resolving the ambiguous spots protein_spot:052/053/055/057 which increase and protein_spot:058/067/069 which decrease) should show increased mature lysosomal hydrolase protein and expanded LAMP1 area in APOE4. Uniformly unchanged or decreased hydrolase protein would contradict the lysosomal-expansion step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured state): APOE4 microglia show coherently higher transcripts for the full lipid-handling cycle - SREBP factors and sterol/fatty-acid synthesis (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:SCD +4.17), uptake (gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1 +8.2), esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2) and export/carrier (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:PLTP) - together with a lysosomal/TFEB program (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, multiple ATP6V subunits).", "Step 2 (inferred routing, not measured): continued SREBP-target expression despite increased uptake transcripts is most consistent with sterol/lipid being routed into esterified and lysosomal pools rather than restoring the ER regulatory sterol pool, sustaining a self-reinforcing lipid acquisition-and-degradation state; ER free-sterol pool, lipid droplets and SREBP-2 cleavage were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred demand): this state raises demand for mitochondrial carbon exchange and reducing equivalents, matching the observed increase in mitochondrial carriers and shuttle enzymes (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 citrate, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13, gene:MPC2 +8.00, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ME1) and in TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:GLUD1).", "Step 4 (transcriptional response): a nuclear-encoded mitochondrial biogenesis/OXPHOS-subunit program is engaged (all 38 detected subunits positive, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36), together with import/inner-membrane components (gene:TIMM44, gene:CHCHD3, gene:PHB, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77).", "Step 5 (stoichiometry constraint): mtDNA-encoded core subunits do not follow this program (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; only gene:MT-ND5, gene:MT-ND4L positive), so nuclear:mtDNA subunit supply is mismatched and increased nuclear transcripts need not yield proportionally more assembled complexes; assembled-complex amount and respiration are unmeasured. Consistently, no protein spot cleanly reports increased mitochondrial protein (protein_spot:050 MDH1-candidate -0.48 n.s.; protein_spot:059 PHB-candidate +0.38 n.s.; protein_spot:074/075 SOD2-candidate +0.38/-0.14 n.s.).", "Step 6 (redox coupling, compartment-restricted): the redox adjustment accompanying this expansion is matrix/membrane-localised (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:MGST2 +3.32, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:UCP2 +2.38, gene:SLC25A37 +4.48, gene:FTH1 +2.53) and is not a peroxisomal or cytosolic NRF2 program (no PEX/CAT/HMOX1/NQO1/TXNRD1 rows; gene:OXR1 -3.63; gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32 against gene:NNT/gene:ME1 positive).", "Step 7 (predicted consequence): in the unchallenged mock condition oxidative metabolism can be maintained or even elevated, but the mismatched mtDNA subunit supply plus a narrow, matrix-limited antioxidant buffer predicts reduced spare respiratory and redox reserve that would be revealed by a lipid or oxidative challenge; this is a prediction, not an observed ongoing defect."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-storage/lysosomal cell state with an unmatched nuclear mitochondrial expansion program and matrix-restricted redox buffering"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1761252446183953, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2308522452966279, "cosine_similarity": 0.4251944287181639, "direction_accuracy": 0.2928802588996764, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5611941747572815, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1761252446183953, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2308522452966279, "cosine_similarity": 0.4251944287181639, "direction_accuracy": 0.2928802588996764, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5611941747572815, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3662465, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a curated two-column up/down differential list (1705 up, 507 down, all |effect|\u003e=1); the +1.39 mean is a selection artifact, so only within-list relative enrichment is interpreted and the unspecified logarithm base is preserved as reported.", "Transcript differences of hydrolase, v-ATPase and sterol-synthesis genes track corresponding protein and enzymatic activity at day 30; this was not measured here.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes (KRT1 appears in 33 of 92 spots, consistent with keratin contamination), so spot-level changes are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein substrate for the inferred uptake flux; no lipid, sterol, filipin or droplet measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Absence of interferon/NF-kB genes from the list reflects the differential filter and does not prove those pathways are unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional program of increased lipoprotein/lipid uptake and endolysosomal hydrolase-plus-v-ATPase capacity that is not matched by sterol egress from the endolysosome; the inferred consequence is retention of lipid-derived cholesterol in LAMP1/RAB7 compartments, an ER-accessible sterol pool that is sensed as insufficient (sustained SREBP-target transcription), and re-routing of incoming and newly synthesised sterol and fatty acid into SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent cytosolic cholesteryl-ester and triglyceride droplets. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; lipid pools, localisation, flux and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Filipin plus LAMP1 imaging in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show higher unesterified cholesterol inside LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4, with higher BODIPY/neutral-lipid droplet content; if lysosomal free cholesterol is equal or lower in APOE4 while droplets still differ, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong and an ER/synthesis-autonomous mechanism is favoured.", "Relieving lysosomal sterol retention (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 or LAL augmentation) should lower APOE4 SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels and reduce droplet content; persistence of elevated SREBP targets after cholesterol is mobilised would weaken the mechanism.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe) should convert the APOE4 excess from cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol and shrink sterol-ester droplets without normalising the lysosomal transcript program; if total droplet mass is unchanged and is instead DGAT1-dependent triglyceride, the sterol-esterification arm is falsified while the uptake/lysosome arm can stand.", "Discriminating test against the assigned inflammatory/interferon framing: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade in mock APOE4 microglia should leave the lysosomal and sterol transcript differences and the lipid phenotype essentially unchanged; if these normalise, the interferon mechanism outcompetes this one.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should reduce hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts and, if the compartment is the site of retention, increase rather than decrease lysosomal cholesterol while lowering droplet turnover; no change in either lipid readout would argue the lysosomal expansion is a bystander."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: lipid-uptake/scavenger transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:APOE +1.24, reported-log units). Inferred: greater delivery of lipoprotein- and lipid-derived cholesterol to the endolysosome; the delivered lipid pool itself was not measured.", "Measured: an a-priori endolysosomal set (40 genes matched in the list) is shifted up relative to the whole selected list (mean +2.77 vs +1.39, 93% up, Mann-Whitney p=3.6e-4), including gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A and the biogenesis factor gene:TFEB (+2.38). Inferred: expanded acidic degradative compartment (TFEB activity, lysosome number and hydrolytic flux were not measured).", "Bottleneck (inferred): sterol export from that compartment does not scale with input. gene:NPC2 rises only +1.17, the strongest lysosomal-egress components (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) are absent from the supplied differential list, and several significant protein spots whose candidate genes include lysosomal hydrolases or v-ATPase subunits fall (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), so hydrolase/egress capacity is at best unevenly increased.", "Inferred localisation, not measured: cholesterol liberated in the endolysosome is retained there, so the ER-accessible sterol pool is under-filled while total cell cholesterol is not low.", "Measured: SREBP-arm transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SCD +4.17) together with acetyl-CoA supply transcripts (gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:MPC2 +7.98). Inferred: continued de novo sterol and monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis despite adequate cellular sterol.", "Measured: esterification/storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29) while sterol-disposal routes are unmeasured (ABCA1/ABCG1 absent) and gene:MYLIP (+1.28) predicts post-transcriptional LDLR turnover. Inferred: net flux of sterol and fatty acid into cytosolic cholesteryl-ester/triglyceride droplets rather than efflux.", "Predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia accumulate more neutral-lipid droplets and lysosomal free cholesterol than isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock treatment, without a type-I interferon or NF-kB transcriptional signature."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol-egress bottleneck drives cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.281453084631765, "cosine_similarity": 0.42509779042719886, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5785728155339805, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.281453084631765, "cosine_similarity": 0.42509779042719886, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5785728155339805, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7745165, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 41}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Gene set memberships (DAM/phagocytic-lipid, TLR/NF-kB, interferon/ISG) were defined from standard literature annotation before checking direction in this dataset, not selected to force agreement.", "RNA log-fold-change values are treated as relative transcript abundance only; no assumption is made about the logarithm base, and no claim is made about protein abundance, activity, or secretion from RNA changes alone.", "Protein-spot changes are treated as compatible-or-not with the RNA-based program, not as confirmation of any single named protein, because most spots list multiple candidate genes and several candidate genes recur across many unrelated spots.", "The 'mock' condition is assumed to represent an unstimulated/baseline state in which the observed differences reflect a genotype-associated resting transcriptional tone rather than an evoked response to a defined stimulus.", "Absence of a gene from this significant-DE list is treated as 'not detected as significantly different here,' not as evidence of no expression or no biological change (missingness is unknown, not unchanged)."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated increase (measured as RNA abundance) in complement, TREM2/APOE-linked phagocytic-lipid-handling genes, and TLR2/MyD88-coupled cytokine/inflammasome genes relative to APOE3, indicating a shift toward a disease-associated-microglia-like, innate-immune-primed baseline transcriptional state. This program is not accompanied by a type-I interferon-stimulated-gene signature, so classical interferon pathway activation is not supported as the driver. Whether this transcriptional tone reflects increased functional inflammatory output, altered baseline set-point, or a partially compensated state cannot be established from the supplied RNA/protein abundance data alone.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating test: if isogenic APOE3 and APOE4 microglia (same 2D co-culture system) are challenged with a defined TLR2 agonist (e.g., Pam3CSK4) or LPS, and downstream chemokine/cytokine transcripts (CCL2, CXCL8, IL18) and NLRP3-dependent IL-1beta processing are measured, the mechanism predicts APOE4 microglia will show an altered (either exaggerated peak or delayed resolution) response relative to APOE3, reflecting the elevated baseline TLR2/MyD88 transcriptional tone. If challenge responses are quantitatively indistinguishable between genotypes, this would weaken the mechanism by indicating the baseline RNA differences do not translate into a functional signaling difference.", "If targeted knockdown or antagonism of TREM2 in APOE4 microglia normalizes DAM-program transcripts (GPNMB, CLEC7A, FABP5, CTSB, ITGAX) toward APOE3 levels, this would support a TREM2-linked driver; if these transcripts are unchanged after TREM2 perturbation, this would weaken the proposed coupling between TREM2/APOE and the phagocytic-lipid program."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show coordinated higher RNA abundance of TREM2, APOE, ABCA7, complement C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, CD74, and phagocytic-lipid genes GPNMB, CLEC7A, FABP5, ITGAX, LGALS1, LGALS3, CTSD, CTSB relative to APOE3, consistent with a shift toward a DAM-like transcriptional program (measured abundance only; upstream TREM2 ligand engagement and downstream DAP12/TYROBP signaling are not measured).", "In parallel, pattern-recognition/adaptor genes TLR2, MYD88, and TICAM1 are higher along with NF-kB-responsive chemokine/cytokine genes CCL2, CXCL8, IL18 and inflammasome sensor NLRP3, suggesting increased transcriptional capacity for an innate-sensing/cytokine arm alongside the DAM program (pathway coupling is inferred, not measured as protein activity or secreted cytokine).", "Negative-feedback-associated genes are not uniformly reduced: TNFAIP3 and RELB are lower in APOE4 (compatible with reduced restraint), but TRAF3 and NFKBIB are higher (compatible with intact or increased restraint); net effect on NF-kB output cannot be inferred from RNA alone, so a simple single-brake-failure model is not adopted.", "Canonical type-I interferon-stimulated genes (ISG15, MX1, MX2, OAS1-3, OASL, IFIT1-3, IRF7, STAT1, STAT2, IFITM1-3, DDX58, IFIH1, BST2, USP18, HERC5, HERC6, CMPK2, LY6E, etc.) are almost entirely absent from this significant-DE list (34 of 36 queried genes not represented); IFI16 alone (a DNA sensor with inflammasome-adjacent roles) does not establish an ISG/interferon program.", "Protein-spot data give partial, non-confirmatory corroboration: spots whose candidate-gene list includes ANXA1 are majority-positive (6 of 9) and spots including CTSD are mixed (4 up/3 down/1 flat); shared candidate genes across spots prevent attributing any single spot's change to one confirmed protein, so this is treated as compatible, not confirmatory, evidence.", "Net interpretation: the RNA pattern supports a coordinated shift in APOE4 microglial baseline transcriptional state toward heightened complement/phagocytic-lipid and TLR2/MyD88-linked cytokine gene expression, distinct from an interferon-driven program; whether this reflects increased functional signaling flux, a set-point shift without added flux, or an early stage of impaired resolution remains undetermined without protein-activity, secretion, or challenge data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a coordinated DAM-like, TLR2/MyD88-linked inflammatory transcriptional tone without an interferon signature, at baseline"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27531423837843966, "cosine_similarity": 0.424771974705316, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6068025889967638, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27531423837843966, "cosine_similarity": 0.424771974705316, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6068025889967638, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6097547, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_032", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive skew (77% up, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); we assume direction and relative magnitude are interpretable only against that internal background, and we make no claim about genes absent from the list.", "Transcript abundance for sterol-handling enzymes and transporters is assumed to track, imperfectly, protein amount and pathway capacity; no sterol enzyme protein, no sterol mass, no lipidomic and no localization measurement is supplied, so all pool sizes, fluxes and compartment assignments are inferred, not observed.", "Coordinated elevation of SREBP-2-responsive transcripts is assumed to indicate low ER-accessible sterol rather than SREBP-independent transcription (e.g. mTORC1/lipogenic drive), even though gene:SREBF1 and gene:SCD are also elevated and the flux-controlling targets HMGCR and SQLE are not present in the supplied list.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-unique: each carries several candidate genes plus frequent keratin/actin, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific sterol or lysosomal protein.", "The measurements are assumed to derive predominantly from the microglial compartment of a microglia-astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte contribution or ambient RNA could contribute to APOE-related transcripts.", "The APOE4 versus APOE3 contrast is assumed to be the only systematic difference between the compared groups (isogenic background as stated); causality is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in sterol trafficking rather than in sterol supply: transcripts encoding lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors, lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, and ER-resident distal sterol-biosynthetic and SREBP-2-responsive genes are coordinately higher in APOE4, a combination that is expected only if the ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol pool is read as low while lipid is retained in the endolysosome. We propose that egress of endolysosomal sterol to the ER (NPC2- and membrane-contact-site-dependent) is the primary bottleneck, and that the oxysterol-generating and efflux transcripts (CYP27A1, CH25H, ABCA7, APOE, MYLIP) represent a partially engaged bypass rather than restored ER sterol delivery. All statements concern measured RNA abundance; sterol pools, localization, flux and causal direction are inferred and not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute treatment of APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 protein supplementation), which releases sterol from the endolysosome independently of contact-site machinery, should within 6-24 h lower the SREBP-2-responsive transcripts (SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels and reduce lysosomal filipin, while an equimolar inert control does not. If cyclodextrin relieves lysosomal sterol staining but leaves the SREBP-2 transcript elevation intact, the proposed sensing link is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: knockdown of NPC1 or NPC2 in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 pattern (coordinated rise in lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts together with SREBP-2-responsive transcripts and SCARB1); failure to reproduce the joint lysosomal-plus-SREBP-2 signature would argue the APOE4 difference is not an egress defect.", "Direct pool test: quantitative sterol imaging/biochemistry should show, in APOE4 versus APOE3, increased LAMP1-colocalized filipin signal and increased cholesteryl ester fraction, but equal or reduced accessible plasma-membrane cholesterol by a D4H/PFO-derived biosensor. Finding higher accessible plasma-membrane cholesterol in APOE4 would falsify the central 'ER reads low while lipid accumulates' claim.", "Flux test: [13C]-acetate or [2H]-water labelling should show higher de novo cholesterol synthesis rate per cell in APOE4 despite equal or greater total cell cholesterol mass. Equal synthesis flux would show the transcript elevation is not translated into pathway flux and would weaken step 4.", "Uptake test: SCARB1 blockade (BLT-1) or SCARB1 knockdown in APOE4 should reduce lysosomal sterol load and blunt the hydrolase transcript elevation without normalizing it fully; no change in lysosomal sterol would indicate uptake is not the feeding arm.", "Bypass test: inhibition of CYP27A1 should increase, not decrease, lysosomal sterol load in APOE4 and should lower MYLIP and ABCA7 transcripts; if CYP27A1 inhibition instead reduces lysosomal sterol, the oxysterol arm is not acting as a disposal bypass.", "Negative control for global skew: transcript families unrelated to lipid handling that are also globally elevated here (e.g. NDUF-family, EIF-family) should not respond to cyclodextrin or NPC2 manipulation. If they shift in parallel with the sterol genes, the APOE4 signature is a global normalization or composition artefact rather than a sterol-specific mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalization routes (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7), which we infer increases delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosome; cargo flux itself is not measured.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred): transfer of that sterol from the limiting membrane of the late endosome/lysosome to the ER is rate-limiting in APOE4. The only supplied egress-machinery transcripts are modestly changed (gene:NPC2, gene:OSBPL1A, gene:OSBPL3, gene:SACM1L, with gene:OSBPL8 decreased), so the bottleneck is proposed as a functional/lipidation defect at contact sites, not as loss of transporter transcript.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred compartment state): sterol and sphingolipid retention triggers a TFEB-type catabolic expansion, seen as strongly elevated hydrolase and acidification transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2); this increases catabolic capacity but does not by itself move sterol to the ER.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): because the ER-accessible sterol pool stays low, SCAP/INSIG-dependent SREBP-2 output remains on, seen as coordinated elevation of gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2 and gene:LDLR - i.e. the cell continues to signal sterol need while lipid accumulates elsewhere.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred bypass): side-chain and ring hydroxylation transcripts (gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:HSD3B7) and oxysterol/LXR-responsive transcripts (gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP) are also elevated, consistent with oxysterol export being used as an alternative disposal route that signals sufficiency to LXR yet does not replenish the ER pool sensed by SCAP.", "Step 6 (predicted outcome): the combination of sustained uptake plus sustained synthesis plus elevated esterification/storage capacity (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and APOE4-limited acceptor lipidation produces net cholesteryl-ester/lysosomal lipid accumulation and reduced membrane-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 microglia, a state that should be measurable as increased lysosomal filipin/sterol staining with unchanged or reduced plasma-membrane accessible cholesterol."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sequester sterol in an expanded endolysosomal compartment: rate-limiting lysosome-to-ER sterol egress sustains a futile uptake-and-synthesis program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24040981124761857, "cosine_similarity": 0.4238786211595096, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5935566343042071, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24040981124761857, "cosine_similarity": 0.4238786211595096, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5935566343042071, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.608118, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 42}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_134", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strongly positive global shift (median +1.459); only each gene's position relative to that global median, not its absolute magnitude, is interpreted.", "Transcript abundance changes are assumed to translate, at least in rank order, into enzyme/transporter protein abundance; enzyme abundance is further assumed to constrain flux at the committed, non-equilibrium steps (hexokinase, PFK) more than at near-equilibrium steps.", "Key glycolytic genes were not measured in this list (HK1, PKM, GAPDH, PGK1, LDHA/LDHB, PDHA1, PDK1, ACLY, FASN, CS, PC); the model assumes that reduced HK2/HK3/PFKP is not fully compensated by unmeasured HK1/PFKL.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate two-dimensional spots (typically 5 candidate genes); no protein is treated as uniquely identified, and the glycolysis-candidate spots are used only as weak, non-decisive context.", "No metabolite, isotope-tracing, respirometry, lipid-droplet, mtDNA-copy-number or protein-modification (e.g. PDH phosphorylation) measurement is supplied; all flux, localization, and activity statements are inferred, and biological replicate number is not supplied.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and the mock condition is otherwise matched, so genotype rather than line background or astrocyte co-culture composition drives the differences (unverified background knowledge, not testable in these files)."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, the transcript program is consistent with a bottleneck at the committed entry steps of glycolysis (hexokinase and phosphofructokinase isoforms strongly reduced relative to the strongly positive global shift, while glucose-transporter transcripts rise), so that glucose carbon and its oxidative pentose-phosphate branch are under-used while lipoprotein/lipid uptake, lysosomal catabolism, fatty-acid, ketone/acetate and amino-acid oxidation supply the TCA cycle; the resulting mitochondrial carbon is partly exported as citrate and re-esterified, biasing APOE4 microglia toward neutral-lipid accumulation rather than glycolytic-inflammatory metabolism. This is an inferred flux model built from measured RNA abundance and ambiguous protein-spot abundance; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Stable-isotope tracing in mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: with U-13C6 glucose, APOE4 should show lower fractional 13C enrichment of secreted lactate and lower m+2 labeling of citrate/glutamate; with 13C-palmitate, 13C-acetate/beta-hydroxybutyrate or 13C5-glutamine, APOE4 should show higher fractional contribution to TCA intermediates. Equal or higher glucose-derived citrate labeling in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Extracellular flux: APOE4 should show reduced glycolytic capacity/reserve (ECAR after glucose and after oligomycin) with preserved or increased basal oxygen consumption, and greater OCR sensitivity to etomoxir (CPT1) or BPTES (glutaminase) than APOE3. Equal ECAR and equal etomoxir/BPTES sensitivity would falsify the substrate-switch claim.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring committed glycolytic entry in APOE4 (HK2 re-expression, or a PFKFB3/PFK-activating manipulation) should raise lactate output and reduce BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area; conversely, 2-deoxyglucose in APOE3 should phenocopy the APOE4 lipid-storage state. If HK2 restoration normalizes glycolysis but leaves APOE4 lipid load unchanged, the bottleneck is not upstream of lipid storage and the mechanism fails.", "Route-specific test of Step 5: SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) inhibition or DGAT1/SOAT1 inhibition should reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid accumulation without normalizing glucose consumption; if lipid droplets fall only when lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1/CD36) is blocked and citrate export blockade has no effect, the de-novo/citrate arm of the mechanism is wrong while the scavenging arm survives.", "Alternative-mechanism discriminator: measure mtDNA-encoded protein (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6) and respiratory-complex assembly. The competing mitonuclear-imbalance model (nuclear ETC transcripts up while gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 are down) predicts reduced maximal (FCCP) respiration and assembly defects with intact glucose commitment; observing that pattern together with unchanged hexokinase-step flux would replace, not support, the present hypothesis.", "Negative control on inflammation: the reduced glycolytic-entry program should not be explained by a general activation state - APOE4 should not show a coordinated increase in canonical glycolytic-inflammatory markers; observing elevated HK2/PFKP protein with elevated lactate in APOE4 would directly contradict the primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_134", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): the committed glucose-phosphorylating and phosphofructokinase steps are transcriptionally down-weighted in APOE4 (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2 all below the dataset median by 2.6-5.1 log units) even though glucose-uptake capacity transcripts are up (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3); inferred consequence is reduced flux from intracellular glucose into glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-1,6-bisphosphate, not a measured metabolite change.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): with glucose-6-phosphate supply constrained, the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch is also under-supplied (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1 reduced), limiting glucose-derived NADPH and ribose production; NADPH-consuming demand is instead served by transhydrogenase and peroxiredoxin/glutathione-peroxidase transcripts (gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4).", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred substrate switch): carbon demand is met from non-glucose sources - lipoprotein and lipid scavenging (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR), lysosomal hydrolysis of ingested membranes/lipids (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, plus v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A and gene:TFEB), mitochondrial beta-oxidation and electron transfer to the ETC (gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1), ketone/acetate activation (gene:OXCT1, gene:ACSS2), and amino-acid deamination/transamination (gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1, gene:BCAT2, gene:GLS).", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): the mitochondrial oxidative apparatus is transcriptionally expanded (TCA and carriers gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5; nuclear-encoded ETC gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME) and pyruvate dehydrogenase is predicted to be more dephosphorylated/active (gene:PDP1 up), so whatever pyruvate is made is oxidized rather than fermented.", "Step 5 (inferred bottleneck-relief route): mitochondrially generated citrate is predicted to be exported (gene:SLC25A1 up) and, together with acetate-derived acetyl-CoA (gene:ACSS2), fed into sterol/fatty-acid esterification and desaturation (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1), while transcripts for acyl-CoA activation feeding peroxisomal/ER oxidation fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:ABCD1); the net inferred flux is storage of scavenged and de-novo lipid rather than complete oxidation.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype, not measured here): the substrate switch lowers glycolytic reserve and lactate output and raises neutral-lipid (lipid-droplet) content in APOE4 microglia, an inflammatory-metabolism state distinct from the glycolytic commitment seen in acutely activated microglia (gene:CTSS and gene:CCL4 are down while gene:CXCL8 and gene:CCL2 are up, i.e. this is not a generic activation program)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia throttle glucose commitment at the hexokinase/PFK step and run mitochondria on lipid- and amino-acid-derived carbon, exporting citrate to neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08414872798434442, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29992066956051466, "cosine_similarity": 0.4235570256757733, "direction_accuracy": 0.1407766990291262, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_134", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5850776699029125, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08414872798434442, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29992066956051466, "cosine_similarity": 0.4235570256757733, "direction_accuracy": 0.1407766990291262, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5850776699029125, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61159225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 43}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_039", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so all set-level statements are enrichment relative to the other supplied rows (global median reported logFC 1.46, 77% positive), not relative to an unbiased transcriptome; the enrichment is assumed to survive that selection.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and relative magnitudes are used.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the corresponding protein subunit supply; no OXPHOS, TCA, carrier or SREBP protein was measured here.", "The lower mtDNA-encoded transcript signal is assumed to reflect a genuine mitochondrial transcript/copy-number difference rather than probe-capture bias of the 10X Flex assay, ambient-RNA or normalisation artefact.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; none of the 92 spots is used as evidence for a specific mitochondrial, lipogenic or lysosomal protein.", "Cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of the transcript signal may derive from or be shaped by the astrocyte compartment.", "Citrate export, acetyl-CoA levels, respiratory flux, complex assembly state, lipid droplets and sterol pools were not measured and are inferred."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated, direction-uniform increase in transcripts for nuclear-encoded TCA enzymes, mitochondrial substrate carriers and structural OXPHOS subunits (51/51 such measured rows positive, median reported logFC 3.05, permutation p = 5e-5 against the strongly positive global background, median 1.46) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 all negative; MT- set median -1.56, permutation p = 0.014). We hypothesise that the limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores for complexes I, III, IV and V, so that increased nuclear subunit and substrate-carrier expression cannot be converted into proportionally increased respiratory flux; the resulting mismatch is proposed to back up TCA carbon and, via the up-regulated citrate carrier SLC25A1, to feed the up-regulated SREBP/sterol-lipogenic transcript program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, LDLR), biasing APOE4 microglia toward neutral-lipid and sterol accumulation. Only transcript abundances were measured; assembly, flux, localisation, lipid pools and causal direction are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: increasing mtDNA-encoded core supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM over-expression, or mitochondrially targeted/allotopic re-expression of MT-ATP6 and MT-CO2) should raise assembled complex IV and V holoenzyme per unit mitochondrial mass, raise maximal and spare respiratory capacity normalised to citrate-synthase activity or TOMM20, and lower SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) and BODIPY neutral-lipid area toward APOE3 levels. If restored mtDNA-encoded subunit supply normalises respiration but leaves the lipogenic transcripts and lipid droplets unchanged, the proposed causal chain from the respiratory bottleneck to lipid accumulation is wrong.", "Blue-native PAGE / complex-assembly assay: APOE4 mitochondria should show a higher ratio of unassembled nuclear-encoded subassemblies to fully assembled complex I and IV than APOE3, at equal or higher nuclear-encoded subunit protein. Equal assembled-to-free ratios would weaken the mitonuclear-mismatch bottleneck.", "Respirometry: APOE4 microglia should show mtDNA-copy- or citrate-synthase-normalised maximal (FCCP) oxygen consumption equal to or below APOE3 despite elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, with a greater relative deficit for complex-I- and complex-IV-linked than for complex-II-linked respiration. Higher normalised maximal respiration in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "Arm-specific test: pharmacological block of citrate export/utilisation (SLC25A1 inhibition with CTPI-2, or ACLY inhibition) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content and SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4 without correcting the mtDNA-encoded/nuclear transcript ratio; failure to reduce lipid accumulation would exclude the citrate-export arm while leaving the assembly bottleneck itself untested.", "Assay-artefact control: quantify mtDNA copy number (qPCR) and mtDNA-encoded protein (MT-CO1 immunoblot) in the same cultures. If mtDNA copy number and MT-CO1 protein are equal between genotypes, the MT- transcript decrease is a probe/normalisation artefact and the hypothesis is substantially weakened.", "Genotype specificity: the nuclear-up / mtDNA-down transcript pattern and the lipid phenotype should co-segregate with APOE genotype across independent isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia lines; absence of the mtDNA-encoded decrease in a replicate isogenic pair that still shows the lipid phenotype would falsify the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher steady-state transcript levels for nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain structural subunits (all 21 NDUF*, 3 UQCR*, 6 COX*, 7 ATP5*, SDHB rows positive), TCA/redox-shuttle enzymes (ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G, OGDH, DLD, MDH1, GOT1) and mitochondrial substrate carriers (MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A37, SLC25A46).", "Measured, discordant: mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB and MT-ND4 are lower in APOE4, with MT-ATP6 among the most statistically extreme rows in the dataset (adjusted p ~9e-228).", "Inferred bottleneck (not measured): because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, the reduced mtDNA-encoded pool caps holo-complex assembly; nuclear-encoded subunits accumulate as unassembled subcomplexes and respiratory flux per unit mitochondrial mass does not rise in proportion to the transcript increase.", "Inferred (not measured): with substrate import transcripts (MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11) elevated but terminal oxidation assembly-limited, matrix acetyl-CoA/citrate is predicted to rise and to be exported to the cytosol through the citrate carrier encoded by SLC25A1.", "Measured, consistent downstream state: the SREBP-controlled lipogenic and sterol module is coordinately elevated (SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, LDLR, SOAT1; median reported logFC 2.29), as are lipid-handling and lipid-storage-associated genes APOE, ABCA7, SOAT1, DGAT1 and SCARB1.", "Inferred endpoint (not measured): the combination of assembly-limited oxidation, citrate export and an active SREBP program biases APOE4 microglia toward cytosolic lipogenesis, sterol esterification and neutral-lipid droplet accumulation rather than toward complete oxidative disposal of lipid and pyruvate carbon.", "Inferred modifier (not measured): the accompanying uniform up-regulation of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, CTSH, LAMP1, NPC2, GAA; ATP6V0C, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H and 7 further ATP6V rows, all positive) is interpreted as a secondary lipid-clearance/degradative response to the lipid load, not as the initiating lesion."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch: APOE4 microglia over-supply nuclear-encoded TCA/OXPHOS and mitochondrial carrier transcripts while mtDNA-encoded ETC core transcripts fall, creating an assembly-limited respiratory bottleneck that diverts citrate to SREBP-driven lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12035225048923678, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2667902365473274, "cosine_similarity": 0.423532275319728, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5730614886731391, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12035225048923678, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2667902365473274, "cosine_similarity": 0.423532275319728, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5730614886731391, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5505805, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 44}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_162", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all rows have |effect| \u003e= 1.00 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE) is treated as 'no detected genotype difference above threshold', not as an unmeasured or absent gene, and not as proof of no change.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking and set-level comparison, not converted to fold changes.", "77% of the supplied differential rows are positive (mean +1.39, median +1.46), so a positive effect is not by itself evidence of pathway induction; all set-level statements use permutation against the within-list background.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein and transport capacity; no sterol, cholesteryl-ester, oxysterol or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so all lipid pools and all fluxes in this mechanism are inferred.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and cannot be assigned to a single protein; keratins and actin dominate the candidate lists, indicating substantial identification ambiguity and possible contamination.", "The co-culture supplies astrocyte-derived lipoproteins; genotype differences in the astrocyte partner or in microglial purity/composition could contribute to the RNA differences and are not controlled in the supplied data.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', and reported |effect| is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p (Spearman -0.03), so effect sizes may be noisy or on a scale inconsistent with the test statistic."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes transcriptionally up-regulate receptor-mediated lipoprotein and scavenger uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:STAB1) and endolysosomal hydrolase/CLEAR machinery (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:LAMP1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A), while transcripts for the committed mevalonate arm and for lysosome-to-ER/plasma-membrane sterol egress and efflux (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) are not present among the supplied differentially expressed rows. The primary bottleneck we propose is disposal/export capacity of internalized sterol-rich lipid at the endolysosome, not sterol supply: incoming lipid is inferred to be retained and buffered by esterification (gene:SOAT1) and side-chain oxidation (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1), and the resulting lysosomal load is inferred to drive MiT/TFE-dependent lysosomal biogenesis. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: blocking SCARB1-mediated selective lipid uptake (BLT-1 or SCARB1 knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should reduce LysoTracker/LAMP1-positive compartment area and lower the CLEAR transcripts (TFEB, CTSB, GBA, GAA, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels; if the lysosomal expansion phenotype is unchanged after effective SCARB1 loss, the uptake-driven bottleneck is weakened and an intrinsic degradation defect becomes more likely.", "Filipin plus mass-spectrometric lipidomics should show higher LAMP1-colocalized unesterified cholesterol and a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio in APOE4 than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions; equal sterol pools and equal esterification would falsify the retention step.", "APOE4 microglia should efflux less cholesterol to exogenous ApoA-I/HDL acceptors per unit of internalized labelled lipoprotein, despite equal or higher uptake; higher normalised efflux in APOE4 would falsify the export-capacity bottleneck.", "LXR agonism (GW3965) should induce ABCA1/ABCG1 and correct both efflux and the excess lysosomal markers preferentially in APOE4; if efflux is restored but lysosomal expansion persists, the bottleneck relocates downstream to NPC1/LIPA-dependent lysosomal egress rather than plasma-membrane export.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should convert stored ester into free cholesterol and worsen, not relieve, membrane-stress and LGALS3 induction in APOE4 if esterification is a protective buffer; normalisation of the lysosomal program by SOAT1 inhibition would instead indicate that esterification, not export, is the primary defect.", "Statin-mediated blockade of the mevalonate pathway should not equalise APOE4 versus APOE3 lysosomal marker expression, because the proposed load is uptake-derived; if statin treatment abolishes the genotype difference, a synthesis-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "TFEB nuclear translocation (immunofluorescence or CUT&RUN at CLEAR motifs) should be higher in APOE4; equal nuclear TFEB with equal CLEAR-target occupancy would weaken the inferred sensing-to-biogenesis link even if transcripts differ."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_162", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein and scavenger uptake receptors, most extremely gene:SCARB1 (+8.22, adjusted p 3.4e-117), with gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:STAB1 all positive. INFERRED: greater receptor-mediated influx of astrocyte- and serum-derived lipoprotein/sterol cargo into the endolysosomal system (flux not measured).", "INFERRED (capacity mismatch): no rows for ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 or MCOLN1 appear among the supplied differentially expressed genes, so no genotype-driven increase in lysosomal cholesteryl-ester hydrolysis, NPC1-dependent egress, or ABCA1/ABCG1-dependent efflux is detected; the modest rise in gene:APOE (+1.24) and gene:PLTP (+1.06) is inferred to be insufficient for proportional particle-mediated export without increased acceptor lipidation.", "INFERRED (ER sterol handling): sterol that does reach the ER is buffered rather than triggering strong feedback synthesis. Consistent with this, gene:SOAT1 (+1.25, esterification), gene:CH25H (+1.62) and gene:CYP27A1 (+1.49) (oxysterol disposal) are up, gene:INSIG1 (+1.87) and gene:MYLIP (+1.28) are up, whereas the rate-limiting mevalonate/pre-squalene enzymes are absent from the differential list; only post-lanosterol and SREBF1-linked lipogenic genes (gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:DGAT1) move.", "INFERRED (load): net retention of sterol and sphingolipid cargo in late endosomes/lysosomes of APOE4 microglia. This lipid pool is NOT measured in the supplied data and is a prediction, not an observation.", "MEASURED (RNA) + INFERRED (activity): a coordinated MiT/TFE CLEAR-like program is elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:SMPD1, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3). We infer compartment expansion and a nuclear-localization shift of TFEB/MITF (localization not measured); elevated hydrolase transcript abundance is not evidence of increased per-lysosome catabolic flux.", "AMBIGUOUS (protein): cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 and protein_spot:027 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; spot means CTSD +0.06, CTSB -0.23), which we interpret as a proteoform/processing redistribution rather than a uniform increase in mature hydrolase; these spots contain several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified.", "INFERRED (outcome): APOE4 microglia adopt a storage-biased rather than export-biased sterol economy, which would reduce lipidated-APOE particle output to the co-cultured astrocyte compartment and sensitize the cells to further lipid challenge."], "title": "Uptake-egress mismatch: APOE4 microglia raise lipoprotein/scavenger uptake capacity without matching lysosomal sterol egress or export, driving a MiT/TFE lysosomal-expansion state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24337991219910787, "cosine_similarity": 0.42333858727952106, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_162", "mean_absolute_error": 0.594, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24337991219910787, "cosine_similarity": 0.42333858727952106, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "mean_absolute_error": 0.594, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.44802575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 45}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_088", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, SGMS1/2, UGCG, PSAP, ASAH1, GALC and NEU1 is missing data and is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and within-list comparisons are used, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The list is globally shifted upward (median +1.46, 77% positive, every |effect| \u003e 1), so 'up-regulated' alone is uninformative; only relative enrichment and within-module sign coherence are used as evidence, and a compositional/normalisation artefact cannot be excluded.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for enzyme amount; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase maturation state and subcellular localisation were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; the CTSB/CTSD spot pattern is treated as hypothesis-generating only.", "Sphingolipid, ceramide, hexosylceramide, ganglioside and sphingomyelin pools are not present in the supplied data; every statement about them is a prediction.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so an APOE4 effect may be partly non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein composition) rather than microglia-intrinsic.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed and pseudoreplication cannot be excluded.", "Background pathway assignments (CLEAR/TFEB targets, M6P routing, saposin/GM2A cofactor requirement) are unverified background knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-transcribe a lipid-uptake/esterification arm and a MITF/TFE-family lysosomal arm, but the sphingolipid change is turnover- rather than synthesis-driven: the de novo sphingoid-base arm is not co-induced while every measured lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase, cofactor and transporter transcript is raised. We hypothesise that this transcriptional up-regulation is a compensatory response to, not a read-out of, increased catabolic throughput, and that the primary bottleneck is effective luminal hydrolysis of glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin at the late-endosome/lysosome limiting membrane, downstream of transcription (hydrolase maturation/M6P routing and lipid-cofactor presentation), producing a glycosphingolipid-loaded degradative compartment and a routing shift toward neutral-lipid storage. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: in intact APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, per-cell catalytic throughput on a delivered sphingolipid substrate (BODIPY-LacCer or NBD-C6-glucosylceramide pulse-chase, or live-cell 4-MU-beta-glucoside/4-MU-beta-N-acetylglucosaminide) will be equal to or lower than APOE3 despite the large transcript increases, i.e. the activity-to-mRNA ratio for GBA and HEXA will fall at least two-fold in APOE4. If APOE4 instead degrades the pulse proportionally faster, the compensation claim fails and the simple 'increased catabolic flux' alternative is favoured.", "Lipid endpoint: APOE4 microglia will contain more hexosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin per cell than APOE3, with an increased HexCer/Cer ratio, and this will co-localise with LAMP1-positive compartments. No elevation, or a decrease, of these species would weaken the mechanism.", "Synthesis-arm test: stable-isotope labelling (13C/15N-serine or 13C-palmitate) will show unchanged or lower de novo sphingoid-base incorporation per cell in APOE4, and myriocin will not normalise the glycosphingolipid excess. Increased de novo labelling, or myriocin rescue, would falsify Step 3.", "Bottleneck perturbation: augmenting the hydrolytic step (GBA1 over-expression, or a GBA chaperone such as ambroxol/NCGC607) will lower HexCer and GM3 in APOE4 toward APOE3 and will partially reverse the hydrolase/CLEAR transcript module, without changing SREBF1 or SCD. Conversely, acute conduritol-B-epoxide will cause a smaller additional rise in HexCer in APOE4 than in APOE3 because APOE4 is already substrate-limited. If GBA augmentation leaves glycosphingolipids unchanged, the bottleneck lies elsewhere.", "Driver test: TFEB knockdown will coordinately collapse GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD and ATP6V1A transcripts in APOE4 and worsen glycosphingolipid load; if the module remains intact after TFEB loss, Step 2 fails.", "Routing test: immunoblotting for pro- versus mature cathepsin D and GBA, plus conditioned-medium hydrolase assays, will show a higher secreted/intracellular hydrolase ratio and a higher proform/mature ratio in APOE4. Unchanged maturation and secretion would remove the post-transcriptional part of Step 4 and reduce the mechanism to a purely transcriptional description."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake and neutral-lipid esterification (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD; 13/13 positive). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived sphingolipid into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred transcriptional activity): A MITF/TFE-family lysosomal program is engaged (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF) together with 16/16 positive lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic transcripts (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GM2A, gene:SUMF1, gene:GLTP, gene:SPNS1, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SCARB2, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:AGA) and 10/10 positive v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1). TFEB protein, nuclear localisation and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred pathway direction): The de novo sphingoid-base arm is not co-induced. The SPT brake gene:ORMDL2 is up (+1.91) while the ceramide-synthetic transcripts present in the list are only weakly shifted (gene:KDSR +1.27, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:CERS4 +2.52, median at the list background). SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, SGMS1/2, UGCG and CERT1 are absent from this selected DE list, so this step is an inference from missing rather than negative data.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck; partly inferred): Effective hydrolysis per lysosome is set post-transcriptionally, by M6P-dependent hydrolase routing/maturation and by lipid-cofactor presentation at the intralumenal membrane, not by hydrolase mRNA. The routing transcripts are discordant rather than uniformly raised (gene:M6PR -1.72 and gene:AP1M1 -1.03 against gene:IGF2R +2.02 and gene:GNPTG +3.02), and the LIMP-2/GBA delivery receptor is only marginally raised (gene:SCARB2 +1.06). Consistently, 2-D protein spots whose ambiguous candidate lists include CTSB/CTSD move in opposite directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), a pattern compatible with redistribution among protein forms rather than a net increase in mature hydrolase. Spot identity is not unique and no proform/mature assay was supplied.", "Step 5 (predicted, unmeasured lipid state): Substrate influx (Step 1) exceeding effective hydrolysis (Step 4) is predicted to raise luminal hexosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin and to enrich the late-endosomal limiting membrane in ceramide/glycosphingolipid, with a headgroup shift toward GM3 (gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17) rather than extended lacto/neo-series (gene:B4GALT5 -1.88, gene:ST3GAL2 -1.39). No lipid was measured here.", "Step 6 (predicted routing consequence): A glycosphingolipid-rigidified late-endosome membrane is predicted to slow cargo back-fusion, maturation and lysosome exocytosis (gene:RAB27A -2.52) and to bias lipid disposal toward cytoplasmic ester/droplet storage (gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:CIDEB, gene:MGLL up), reinforcing the load that drives Step 2 as a feedback loop rather than a linear cascade."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a MITF/TFE-driven lysosomal glycosphingolipid-catabolic program that lags behind lipid influx, making luminal GlcCer/GM2/sphingomyelin hydrolysis the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22936897684894583, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24794411273675399, "cosine_similarity": 0.42058355756794863, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mean_absolute_error": 0.607284789644013, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22936897684894583, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24794411273675399, "cosine_similarity": 0.42058355756794863, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "mean_absolute_error": 0.607284789644013, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.07980025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 46}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_173", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and all |effect| \u003e= 1 in the unspecified reported logarithm base), so effect sizes are comparable to each other but the 77% upward skew (median +1.46) is a property of the selected list and possibly of normalization, not a demonstrated whole-transcriptome shift; all pathway statements are made relative to this skewed background.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel features with multiple candidate genes; assigning CTSD/CTSB/HEXB/ACP2 to spots 027/052/053/055/057/058/067/069/086/088 is provisional, and ACTB, keratin, ANXA1 and TALDO1 candidates could account for some of these movements.", "Divergent movement of spots sharing the same hydrolase candidate is assumed to reflect redistribution among proteoforms (e.g., pro- versus processed chains, or differential glycosylation) rather than gel artefact; no pro/mature ratio, molecular-weight or pI annotation was supplied.", "Steady-state transcript and spot abundances are assumed to report on capacity, not on flux; degradative flux, luminal pH, hydrolase activity, cargo transit and all lipid pools are unmeasured and are inferred only.", "Astrocyte co-culture contributions and cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells are assumed not to dominate the pseudobulk-like RNA effects.", "The two genotypes are assumed isogenic and matched for differentiation stage at day 30, as stated in the metadata; biological replicate number was not supplied."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 does not fail at transcriptional lysosome biogenesis: TFEB/MITF and a large block of acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are among the most strongly elevated rows relative to the already up-shifted background (hydrolase set n=18, mean effect +3.11 vs background mean +1.39, permutation p=0.0022; 7/18 above the 90th background percentile). The proposed rate-limiting step is instead post-transcriptional: conversion of this transcript program into mature, correctly sorted luminal hydrolase activity, indicated by the fact that 2-D protein spots whose candidate identifications include CTSD/CTSB/HEXB/ACP2 do not move coherently upward (spots 027, 052, 053, 055, 057, 088 up; 058, 067, 069, 086 down) while the sorting receptor transcript M6PR is one of the few strongly reduced endolysosomal rows (-1.72). If degradative flux per unit hydrolase transcript is reduced, internalized lipid cargo is inferred to be catabolised more slowly, keeping ER sterol sensing in a 'sterol-poor' configuration (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS, INSIG1 all elevated) while flux is diverted into esterification and neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SCD, SREBF1; storage set mean +3.32, permutation p=0.023), producing the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pool, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and cargo flux were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, immunoblot the pro- and mature forms of cathepsin D and cathepsin B alongside qPCR of CTSD/CTSB. The mechanism predicts equal or higher transcript with a LOWER mature:pro protein ratio and lower per-cell DQ-BSA dequenching or Magic Red cathepsin B activity in APOE4. If APOE4 shows an equal or higher mature:pro ratio AND equal or higher hydrolytic activity per cell, the proposed maturation/delivery bottleneck is wrong and the hydrolase transcript elevation should instead be read as a successfully executed, sufficient compensation.", "Restoring lumenal acidification independently of the v-ATPase (acidic PLGA nanoparticles) or re-expressing CD-M6PR/M6PR should raise the mature:pro cathepsin ratio and reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet area, without further raising CTSD/CTSB/GAA transcripts. No change in the mature:pro ratio, or a fall in lipid droplets with an unchanged ratio, would weaken the chain and favour a direct esterification-driven mechanism.", "Pulse-chase of fluorescently labelled cargo (oxLDL or myelin debris): APOE4 should show comparable or higher internalization at early time points but significantly delayed intracellular degradation (slower loss of quenched-probe signal) than APOE3. Equal degradation kinetics would falsify Step 4; reduced initial internalization would falsify Step 1.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl-ester droplet content in APOE4 while leaving the mature:pro cathepsin ratio and the elevated SREBF2/LDLR/HMGCS1 transcripts uncorrected. Correction of the cathepsin maturation deficit by SOAT1 inhibition would place the lysosomal step downstream, not upstream, of lipid esterification.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should lower the hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB, HEXA) without proportionally lowering the already limited mature hydrolase pool, and should worsen lipid droplet accumulation. If TFEB knockdown reduces mature hydrolase protein in strict proportion to transcript, the bottleneck is transcriptional and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Targeted mass spectrometry or immunoblot of the excised down-moving spots (058, 067, 069, 086) should confirm cathepsin/hydrolase peptides rather than actin or keratin. Identification of these spots as non-hydrolase proteins would remove the central protein-level evidence for the bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_173", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry elevated transcripts for cargo-uptake and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid/lipoprotein and debris cargo into early and late endosomes.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts; inferred program activity): A lysosome-biogenesis-like transcriptional response is engaged (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) and CLEAR-type targets sit in the extreme upper tail of the selected rows (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA), together with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and late-endosome machinery (gene:RAB7A, gene:AP5M1, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2). This is read as a demand-driven compensatory response, not as an increase in enzyme activity.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured spot abundances, inferred proteoform interpretation): The transcript program is not mirrored by a coherent increase in hydrolase-containing protein spots. Spots whose candidate lists include CTSD/CTSB/HEXB/ACP2 split in both directions (protein_spot:052, :053, :055, :057, :027, :088 increased; protein_spot:058, :067, :069, :086 decreased), and the mannose-6-phosphate sorting receptor transcript is reduced (gene:M6PR -1.72) despite increased tagging and CI-MPR transcripts (gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02). We propose that delivery and proteolytic maturation of pro-hydrolases into the mature luminal pool, not transcript supply, sets the ceiling on hydrolytic capacity. Spot identity is ambiguous and the pro/mature ratio was not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred flux): Reduced mature-hydrolase activity per lysosome lowers catabolism of internalized cholesteryl ester, sphingolipid and membrane cargo, so substrate is retained in the endolysosomal lumen. This luminal lipid pool was not measured in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts; inferred localization/sensing): Because catabolically released sterol does not efficiently reach the ER, sterol sensing remains in a low-sterol configuration and biosynthesis/uptake transcripts stay elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), sustaining Step 1.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts; inferred phenotype): Lipid that escapes or bypasses degradation is routed to esterification and neutral-lipid storage rather than efflux (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67), predicting greater neutral-lipid droplet content in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-scale the endolysosomal hydrolase transcript program but are bottlenecked at hydrolase delivery/maturation, capping degradative flux and diverting cargo lipid into storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1659897352582801, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21066055683014207, "cosine_similarity": 0.42051295568423225, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_173", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5974822006472492, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1659897352582801, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21066055683014207, "cosine_similarity": 0.42051295568423225, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5974822006472492, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.34753875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 47}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_091", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every |effect| exceeds 1 and every adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so pathway enrichment was assessed against the supplied rows themselves, not against an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. LIPA, NPC1, PPARGC1A) means 'not supplied', not 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking and set comparison, never converted to fold changes.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes; any lysosomal interpretation of a spot is provisional and no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein.", "The global positive shift (77% of RNA rows and 70% of protein spots positive) is treated as a possible normalisation/selection artefact; all enrichment statistics were computed by permutation within the supplied effect distribution so that this shift is the null.", "Transcript level is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme abundance; enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, lysosomal lipid content, TFEB localisation and phagocytic flux were not measured in these data.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so per-gene effect sizes cannot be checked for stability and no formal power statement is possible.", "APOE3/APOE4 lines are stated to be isogenic, so differences are attributed to genotype rather than line background; astrocyte co-culture contributions are not separable in these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a lysosome-centred catabolic imbalance: transcripts for sterol/lipid uptake and re-esterification are elevated together with MiT/TFE factors (TFEB, MITF, TFEC) and a broad set of their CLEAR-network targets (acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, LAMP1/SCARB2/CLN3, RRAGD), while the corresponding lysosomal protein spots are not coordinately increased. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is hydrolytic clearance of lipid delivered to the endolysosome, and that the elevated hydrolase transcription is a compensatory (and post-transcriptionally incomplete) response rather than evidence of increased degradative flux. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: blocking lipid input upstream of the lysosome in APOE4 microglia (SOAT1 inhibition with avasimibe, or SCARB1/CD36 knockdown) should reduce the elevated CLEAR transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A) and LAMP1+ lysosomal area toward APOE3 levels, giving a significant genotype x treatment interaction. If CLEAR transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 after lipid input is blocked, the lipid-load-driven bottleneck is wrong and a cell-intrinsic mTORC1/TFEB signalling difference is favoured.", "Functional flux test: despite higher hydrolase transcripts, APOE4 microglia should show equal or slower per-lysosome degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching, BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester or Magic Red cathepsin B turnover normalised to LAMP1 area) and increased LipidSpot/filipin-positive lysosomal lipid. Observing faster normalised degradative flux and no lipid accumulation in APOE4 would falsify the 'bottleneck' claim and reduce the mechanism to a benign transcriptional up-shift.", "Regulator dependence: TFEB knockdown (or combined TFEB/TFE3/MITF loss) should collapse the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation specifically in APOE4 and disproportionately worsen APOE4 lipid accumulation; equal effects in APOE3 and APOE4 would weaken step 3.", "Protein-level resolution: targeted immunoblot of pro- versus mature cathepsin B/D and of ATP6V1A in APOE4 vs APOE3 should show mature-form or specific-activity increases smaller than the transcript increases (translation/processing bottleneck). Proportional increases in mature enzyme and activity would falsify step 5 and argue the lysosomal programme is fully executed.", "Substrate-demand test for step 6: etomoxir or CPT1A inhibition should reduce oxygen-consumption-rate differences between APOE4 and APOE3 and increase APOE4 lysosomal lipid; no genotype-specific effect would indicate the mitochondrial transcript rise is independent of lysosomal lipid handling.", "Uptake prediction: consistent with reduced actin/motor transcripts, APOE4 microglia should show lower initial phagocytic uptake rate (pHrodo synaptosomes or myelin, first 30-60 min) while retaining or exceeding APOE3 lysosomal content at later times; higher initial uptake in APOE4 would weaken step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/sterol uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:ABCA7 +2.14) and for neutral-lipid esterification/desaturation (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17), with the lipogenic regulators gene:SREBF1 +4.67 and gene:SREBF2 +1.06 elevated. Increased delivery of cholesterol/fatty acid to the endolysosome is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Lipid substrate delivered to the endolysosome exceeds the hydrolytic and export capacity of that compartment, producing an accumulating pool of undegraded lipid and lipid-laden lysosomes. No lipid species, lysosomal pH, LIPA or NPC1 measurement is supplied, so this pool is inferred only.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Lysosomal stress de-represses MiT/TFE factors (transcripts up: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.65, gene:MITF +1.03), and their CLEAR targets rise coordinately: acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:CTSH +1.54, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:SGSH +1.32), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70), lysosomal membrane/structure (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:CLN3 +1.17) and the direct TFEB target gene:RRAGD +1.44. TFEB nuclear localisation and mTORC1 status are inferred, not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred trafficking): Late-endosome/lysosome trafficking transcripts rise (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SNX3 +3.90, gene:VPS26A +4.89, gene:AP5M1 +9.78) while actin/motor machinery needed for phagocytic uptake and lysosome motility falls (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B -5.83), and gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:CSF1 -5.91 are strongly reduced; we infer a shift from surface uptake/actin remodelling toward maintenance of an enlarged degradative compartment.", "Step 5 (measured protein spots, inferred bottleneck): The transcriptional compensation is not matched at the protein-spot level. Spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal proteins are not higher than other spots (median +0.36 vs +0.48 log2), and CTSB/CTSD/HEXB/ATP6V1E1-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93). Because spots are multi-candidate and cannot be uniquely assigned, this is treated as failure to confirm a coordinate protein increase, not as proof of reduced enzyme.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred demand): Mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport transcripts are also elevated (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:CYCS +2.58), which we interpret as increased demand for oxidation of lipid-derived substrate and for ATP to sustain lysosomal acidification; no coordinate mitochondrial-biogenesis regulator transcript is present in the supplied rows, so this step is the weakest link and could instead be an independent APOE4 metabolic phenotype."], "title": "APOE4 microglia hit a lysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck that drives a compensatory MiT/TFE (CLEAR) transcriptional programme"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20743639921722112, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1723704354889871, "cosine_similarity": 0.42012461185365146, "direction_accuracy": 0.3446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mean_absolute_error": 0.579663430420712, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20743639921722112, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1723704354889871, "cosine_similarity": 0.42012461185365146, "direction_accuracy": 0.3446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.579663430420712, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88520325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 48}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_014", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. HK1, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, PDHA1, CPT1A, PLIN2, cytosolic ribosomal genes) is assumed to mean it was tested and did not pass threshold, not that it is unmeasured. If those genes were never tested, the inference about which glycolytic step is limiting is weakened.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is not stated and is left unconverted; only ranks, signs and within-dataset percentiles are used, never absolute fold changes.", "The dataset has a strong global positive shift (median +1.46; 77% positive), so a positive sign alone is not evidence; enrichment claims use each gene's percentile within this dataset and Mann-Whitney tests against the remaining rows.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity. No enzyme activity, phosphorylation state (e.g. PDH-E1 phosphorylation), metabolite pool, flux, membrane potential or lipid measurement is present in the supplied data; every activity, flux, localisation and direction statement is inferred.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8) and are not uniquely identified; no spot is treated as a specific enzyme measurement. The up-shifted spot train protein_spot:044/045 and protein_spot:038 are compatible with, but do not demonstrate, changes in TALDO1/ALDOA/TKT, since ANXA1, actins and keratins are equally plausible candidates.", "Astrocyte co-culture means the microglial metabolic state may be partly set by astrocyte-supplied lactate or lipid; the supplied data cannot separate cell-autonomous APOE4 effects from co-culture cross-feeding.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so the reported p-values cannot be re-checked and pseudo-replication cannot be excluded; mtDNA-encoded transcript ratios in 10X Flex data are additionally sensitive to QC filtering."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a coherent re-routing of carbon: transcripts for the committed glucose-phosphorylating/phosphofructokinase step (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and for the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate arm (PGD, TALDO1) are among the most strongly reduced genes in the dataset, while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), PDH activation (PDP1), the TCA cycle (ACO2, IDH3B/IDH3G, OGDH, DLD, SDHB), the malate-aspartate/oxoglutarate and citrate carriers (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A13, SLC25A1, SLC25A5) and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits sit at the top of the distribution. We hypothesise that a low-capacity glycolytic commitment step is the primary bottleneck, so glucose taken up through the induced transporters (SLC2A1, SLC2A3) cannot be committed to glycolysis/PPP at the APOE3 rate; carbon demand is instead met by mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate, glutamine-derived (GLS, GLUD1, SLC1A5, SLC38A2) and fatty-acid-derived (HADHA, ETFA, ACOX1) substrates, and surplus mitochondrial citrate is exported by SLC25A1 into an SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1 lipogenic-esterification arm fed by scavenger uptake (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR), predisposing APOE4 microglia to neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester storage. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, activity, localisation and causal statements are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (MPC block): in mock-treated APOE4 microglia, acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should remove a larger fraction of basal oxygen consumption and should reduce APOE4-specific neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content toward APOE3 levels; if APOE4 OCR is no more UK5099-sensitive than APOE3 and lipid storage is unchanged, the pyruvate-import step of the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (citrate export block): SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or SLC25A1 knockdown should preferentially lower BODIPY/cholesteryl-ester signal in APOE4 microglia while leaving or increasing mitochondrial citrate; no genotype-selective effect on lipid storage would weaken the citrate-to-lipid routing step.", "Isotope tracing: with [U-13C6]glucose, APOE4 microglia should show reduced fractional 13C enrichment in lactate and in citrate m+2 relative to APOE3, whereas with [U-13C5]glutamine they should show equal or greater enrichment in TCA intermediates and in the fatty-acid/sterol pool; equal glucose-derived citrate m+2 enrichment between genotypes would falsify the substrate-switch claim.", "Glycolytic reserve: Seahorse glycolysis stress test should show lower oligomycin-stimulated ECAR (glycolytic reserve) and lower 2-DG-sensitive lactate output in APOE4 with equal or higher basal/maximal OCR; the opposite pattern (higher ECAR, lower OCR in APOE4) would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Rescue: restoring hexokinase capacity (HK2 or HK1 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should raise glycolytic reserve and reduce SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1-dependent lipid esterification without normalising APOE genotype; if lipid accumulation persists unchanged after glycolytic rescue, the bottleneck is elsewhere (e.g. scavenger uptake through SCARB1/CD36 or lysosomal lipid hydrolysis).", "Protein-level test required by the spot ambiguity: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS for HK2, PFKP, MPC2, OGDH, TALDO1 and SLC25A1 should reproduce the transcript directions; if MPC2 and OGDH protein are unchanged or reduced while HK2 protein is unchanged, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails.", "Mito-nuclear variant test: BN-PAGE/complex activity assays should show whether the uniform rise in nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts yields more assembled complex I/III/IV; if assembled complex and maximal respiration are reduced despite the transcript rise (consistent with the reduced MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 rows), the mechanism must be restated as compensatory nuclear induction with a mtDNA-encoded assembly bottleneck rather than genuinely increased oxidative flux."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show strongly reduced transcripts for the committed glycolytic kinases HK2 (-3.67; 3.6th percentile of the measured effect distribution), HK3 (-1.12) and PFKP (-3.08; 5.6th percentile) despite a dataset-wide upward shift (median +1.46, 77% of rows positive). We infer, but did not measure, lower hexokinase/PFK capacity and hence a lower ceiling on glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-1,6-bisphosphate production; PFKM (+2.41), GPI (+2.06) and ENO1 (+2.17) are up, so the inferred restriction is at commitment/isoform composition rather than a uniform loss of glycolytic enzyme mRNA.", "Step 2 (inferred flux consequence): glucose uptake capacity is not the limiting element - SLC2A1 (+2.37) and SLC2A3 (+3.73) are elevated - so restricted commitment is predicted to lower glycolytic and pentose-phosphate throughput per unit of glucose entering the cell; reduced PGD (-1.30) and TALDO1 (-2.32) transcripts are consistent with a smaller PPP/NADPH-regenerating branch, and elevated GYS1 (+6.10) and lysosomal GAA (+9.96) suggest diversion of hexose into glycogen-directed handling.", "Step 3 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred activity): the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier subunit MPC2 (+7.98; 99th percentile) and the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1 (+3.00) are up, together with the E3 subunit DLD (+5.54); we infer increased capacity for pyruvate import and for dephosphorylated (active) PDH, i.e. whatever pyruvate is produced is preferentially oxidised rather than reduced to lactate.", "Step 4 (pathway coherence, measured): TCA-cycle and anaplerotic transcripts are coordinately high relative to background (ACO2 +3.54, IDH3B +2.02, IDH3G +3.94, OGDH +8.56, SDHB +1.65, ME1 +1.36, GLUD1 +3.17, GLS +1.35), as are amino-acid/glutamine transporters (SLC1A5 +1.55, SLC38A2 +4.45) and the redox shuttles MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), SLC25A11 (+4.50) and SLC25A13 (+1.75). 36/36 nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit rows are positive (median +2.64, Mann-Whitney p=1.2e-4 versus all other rows), and the adenine-nucleotide translocase SLC25A5 is +5.56. We infer increased oxidative-machinery expression and increased cytosolic NADH shuttling into mitochondria rather than lactate disposal.", "Step 5 (inferred routing to lipid): the mitochondrial citrate carrier SLC25A1 (+4.47) plus lipogenic/desaturation and esterification transcripts SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), DGAT1 (+1.72), SOAT1 (+1.25) and lipoprotein/scavenger uptake SCARB1 (+8.22), LDLR (+1.50), CD36 (+1.38), with sterol-arm genes DHCR24 (+3.69), DHCR7 (+2.71), LSS (+2.27) and INSIG1 (+1.87), predict export of surplus mitochondrial citrate to cytosolic acetyl-CoA and esterification of fatty acids and sterols into storage lipid.", "Step 6 (inferred sink/phenotype): elevated lysosomal-catabolic transcripts (CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, HEXB +2.17, LAMP1 +1.38, ATP6V1A +4.23, TFEB +2.38, GAA +9.96, NPC2 +1.17) together with the esterification arm are interpreted as an expanded lipid-storage/lysosomal handling compartment. Net prediction: APOE4 microglia carry more neutral lipid and cholesteryl ester at rest, with a small glycolytic reserve, and are hypersensitive to any block on mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate handling.", "Step 7 (constraint on the chain): mtDNA-encoded subunits are mostly reduced (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33, with MT-ND5 +1.93 and MT-ND4L +1.95), so the nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise may reflect a compensatory response to sub-stoichiometric core subunits rather than proportionally higher electron-transport flux; in that variant the carbon still enters mitochondria but is partly spilled to citrate/lipid instead of being fully oxidised."], "title": "Loss of glycolytic commitment forces citrate-exporting mitochondrial carbon routing and lipid esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13460473359672118, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2926070744114014, "cosine_similarity": 0.419963765322164, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5775566343042071, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13460473359672118, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2926070744114014, "cosine_similarity": 0.419963765322164, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5775566343042071, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6813115, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 49}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_114", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1 and 77% are positive, median +1.46); pathway claims are therefore made only relative to that in-list background, and absence of a gene (HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, PDK1-4, PDHA1, CPT1A, G6PD, TFAM, PPARGC1A) is assumed to mean 'not selected', not 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base and scaling of the RNA effect column are unspecified and magnitudes reach 15.5, so only sign, rank and set-level coherence are used; no fold-change magnitude is interpreted quantitatively.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/carrier protein amount and hence capacity; no flux, metabolite, oxygen-consumption, NADPH, membrane-potential or mitochondrial-mass measurement is supplied, so all flux, localization and directionality statements are inferences.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level effects are treated as ambiguous corroboration only.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured, and 10X Flex pseudobulk profiles may include ambient or non-microglial RNA; the genotype comparison is assumed to be isogenic and otherwise matched (biological replicate number not supplied).", "An alternative reading of the same RNA data - compensatory up-regulation of mitochondrial genes in response to impaired oxidative phosphorylation - is assumed to be distinguishable only by the functional predictions below, not by the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial carbon-oxidation machinery (TCA, electron-transport-chain subunits, pyruvate/citrate/oxoglutarate carriers, glutamine catabolism) together with lower transcripts for the committed cytosolic glucose branch (HK2, PFKP) and the pentose-phosphate arm (PGD, TALDO1), despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts. We hypothesise that this configures a state in which reducing equivalents for antioxidant and lipid handling are supplied preferentially by mitochondrial, proton-motive-force-dependent routes (transhydrogenase NNT, malic enzyme ME1) rather than by the oxidative PPP; the rate-limiting step is cytosolic NADPH regeneration through glucose-6-phosphate, making APOE4 microglia disproportionately dependent on intact mitochondrial coupling and on non-glucose substrates (lysosome-derived lipid, glutamine) for oxidative carbon supply. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, localization, activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: oxidative-PPP inhibition (G6PD inhibitor or 6-aminonicotinamide) should reduce the NADPH/NADP+ ratio and increase BODIPY-C11 lipid peroxidation less in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, whereas NNT knockdown or low-dose uncoupling (FCCP/BAM15) should do so more in APOE4 than APOE3. If APOE4 is equally or more sensitive to G6PD inhibition and no more sensitive to NNT loss/uncoupling, the proposed NADPH-sourcing bottleneck is wrong.", "Stable-isotope tracing: [1,2-13C]glucose should give a lower PPP-derived m+1/m+2 lactate ratio in APOE4, while [U-13C]glutamine and 13C-palmitate should give higher TCA-intermediate (citrate, glutamate m+4/m+2) labelling in APOE4. Equal or higher glucose-PPP contribution in APOE4 would weaken the substrate-switch step.", "Respirometry and mass: APOE4 should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a higher oligomycin-insensitive (leak) fraction at comparable citrate-synthase activity or MitoTracker/TMRM-normalised mass, with MPC inhibition (UK5099) plus glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) suppressing APOE4 respiration more than APOE3. If APOE4 oxygen consumption is unchanged or lower despite the higher ETC/TCA transcripts, the 'expanded oxidative capacity' inference fails and only a compensatory-deficit model remains.", "Protein-level confirmation with unambiguous methods (targeted MS or immunoblot) should show higher NDUF/UQCR/ATP5, MPC2, SLC25A1 and NNT protein and lower HK2/PFKP protein in APOE4; unchanged protein for these despite the transcript differences would restrict the mechanism to transcriptional regulation without capacity change.", "Because the supplied TALDO1-containing protein spots (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:045) are increased while gene:TALDO1 RNA is decreased, resolving those spots should assign the increase to a co-migrating candidate (e.g. ANXA1) rather than TALDO1; if TALDO1 protein itself is confirmed to be higher in APOE4, the PPP-limitation step is weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_114", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts (39/39 detected rows positive, mean effect +2.81, permutation p\u003c0.001) and TCA-cycle transcripts (10/10 positive, mean +4.30) are higher in APOE4, as are mitochondrial solute carriers MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11 and SLC25A5. Inferred (not measured): higher mitochondrial oxidative capacity and/or mitochondrial mass per cell.", "Measured: transcripts for the committed glucose-entry isoforms HK2 and PFKP and for PPP enzymes PGD and TALDO1 are lower, while glucose-transporter transcripts SLC2A1 and SLC2A3 are higher. Inferred: glucose is taken up but a smaller fraction of glucose-6-phosphate is committed to the oxidative PPP; net glycolytic flux is not resolved because HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, PKM and LDHA rows are absent from the supplied differential list.", "Measured: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and acidification (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A, TFEB) and lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, APOE) are higher, as are glutamine-handling transcripts (SLC1A5, SLC38A2, GLS, GLUD1). Inferred: increased delivery of lysosome-derived fatty-acid/amino-acid carbon and glutamine anaplerosis to the expanded mitochondrial machinery.", "Bottleneck step (inferred): with the oxidative-PPP branch transcriptionally de-emphasised, cytosolic NADPH regeneration becomes limiting and is partly substituted by mitochondrial sources; consistent with this, NNT (+2.88), ME1 (+1.36) and the NADPH-consuming peroxidase GPX4 (+2.79) transcripts are higher. NNT-derived NADPH depends on the inner-membrane proton-motive force.", "Measured: UCP2 (+2.38) and the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (+4.47) transcripts are higher alongside lipogenic/esterification transcripts SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1. Inferred: part of the oxidised carbon is diverted to cytosolic citrate and neutral-lipid esterification, and increased leak potential would further tax proton-motive-force-dependent NADPH supply.", "Predicted consequence (not measured here): APOE4 microglia sustain baseline redox and lipid handling only while mitochondrial coupling is intact, and are therefore selectively sensitive to uncoupling, NNT loss or MPC/glutaminase blockade, and relatively insensitive to oxidative-PPP inhibition compared with APOE3."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift NADPH and carbon sourcing from the cytosolic glucose-6-phosphate/PPP branch to membrane-potential-dependent mitochondrial oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10176125244618395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27896802931261433, "cosine_similarity": 0.41948941130919803, "direction_accuracy": 0.16990291262135923, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_114", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5796699029126213, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10176125244618395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27896802931261433, "cosine_similarity": 0.41948941130919803, "direction_accuracy": 0.16990291262135923, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5796699029126213, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.45816425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 50}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_086", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect| \u003e 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 up vs 507 down because the source workbook pairs an up column with a shorter down column); program directionality was therefore judged against a ~77% up background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, PLIN2, ASAH1, NPC1, ISG15, MX1, STAT1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA effect unit is a reported log fold change of unspecified base; magnitudes are used only for ranking and relative comparison, never converted to fold changes.", "Program membership was fixed before looking at direction, from canonical pathway rosters written out in full and then intersected with the data; the only post-hoc split is nuclear-encoded versus mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS subunits, which is a structural, not directional, criterion.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding proteins and thereby the capacity (not the flux) of uptake, esterification, lysosomal hydrolysis and mitochondrial transport; no lipid, sterol, respiration or degradation flux was measured in this experiment.", "The 2D-gel protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each; 208 unique candidates over 92 spots); they are used only for compatibility and contradiction, and no spot is treated as identification of a single protein.", "Effects are pseudobulk-style contrasts; simultaneous elevation of nominally opposing modules (SREBP synthesis with gene:CH25H and gene:MYLIP) could in part reflect mixed cell states within the APOE4 culture rather than one cell holding both states.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoproteins; the routing step assumes that this lipid source is available equally to both genotypes.", "The reduced-reserve element of step 5 is a prospective, challenge-revealed prediction; the mock condition data cannot show an ongoing bioenergetic failure."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:NPC2) and for esterification/storage and desaturation (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL) are higher together with a full SREBP synthesis module (12/12 represented members up, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1) and a TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR lysosomal module (27/29 up incl. gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A/H, gene:ATP6V0C). Simultaneous up-regulation of uptake and of sterol-repressible synthesis genes is the discriminating pattern: it is expected if internalised lipid is routed to lysosomal and esterified/storage pools so that the ER sterol-regulatory pool stays low, and is not expected from simple sterol repletion. Cytosolic-acetyl-CoA/NADPH-supplying mitochondrial carrier and TCA transcripts (14/14 up, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1, gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:NNT, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS) accompany this state, while mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS transcripts are the only mitochondrial members that fall (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2) against 23/23 nuclear-encoded subunits up, indicating a nuclear-driven expansion that may not be stoichiometrically matched. A modest chemokine/inflammasome-priming increase (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL1/2/3, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD) is placed downstream of lipid/lysosomal stress; no canonical interferon effector module is represented (only gene:IFNAR1, gene:IRF8, gene:IFI16, gene:TMEM173 up, gene:IRF2 down), so an interferon-driven mechanism is rejected as primary. All statements are transcript/protein-spot abundance; flux, localisation and causality are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should raise ER-accessible/free cholesterol and, if lipid is being diverted from the ER sensor, lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS) and CLEAR transcripts (gene:TFEB targets gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels while cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid staining falls; if SREBP-2 targets stay elevated after esterification is blocked, the routing/sensing step is wrong and a genuine higher sterol demand (successful adaptation) is favoured.", "Prospective: blocking lysosomal cholesterol export with U18666A in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature (co-elevation of uptake, SREBP and CLEAR transcripts); failure to phenocopy weakens the sequestration interpretation.", "Prospective: quantitative imaging/lipidomics at day 30 mock should show more BODIPY/filipin-positive lipid droplets, more cholesteryl ester, and larger LAMP1+ lysosomal area per cell in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or lower neutral-lipid and lysosomal content would falsify the core state change.", "Prospective: despite 23/23 nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts being higher, APOE4 microglia should not show a proportional gain in maximal or spare respiratory capacity (Seahorse FCCP response) and should show lower mtDNA-encoded protein per nuclear-encoded subunit; a matched increase in maximal respiration and in mtDNA-encoded subunit protein would falsify step 5.", "Prospective: because the mechanism places chemokine induction downstream of lipid/lysosomal loading, esterification blockade or lysosomal-lipid clearance should reduce gene:CXCL8 and gene:CCL2 transcripts, whereas blocking type-I interferon signalling (anti-IFNAR1 antibody or a JAK1/TYK2 inhibitor) should leave the lipid, CLEAR and mitochondrial-carrier modules unchanged; a JAK-inhibitor-sensitive collapse of those modules would falsify the rejection of the interferon focus.", "Prospective: lysosomal degradative flux assays (DQ-BSA, myelin or apoptotic-cell cargo clearance) will distinguish failed compensation from successful adaptation; higher hydrolase transcripts with unchanged or lower per-cell cargo clearance supports failed compensation, whereas increased clearance supports increased throughput and would require the claim to be restated as adaptation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:NPC2) than APOE3, indicating increased lipid-acquisition capacity in the mock condition.", "Step 2 (inferred routing): acquired lipid is preferentially routed to lysosomal and neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage compartments rather than to the ER regulatory sterol pool, supported by concurrently raised esterification/storage and desaturation transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL, gene:PLTP) and by the CLEAR module (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R).", "Step 3 (inferred sensing): because ER-accessible sterol remains low, SREBP-driven synthesis stays engaged, giving the otherwise paradoxical co-elevation of uptake and synthesis transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1) and a feed-forward loading of the storage/lysosomal pools.", "Step 4 (inferred demand): sustaining esterification, desaturation and sterol synthesis raises demand for cytosolic acetyl-CoA, oxaloacetate and NADPH, matching the coordinated rise in mitochondrial citrate/malate-aspartate carriers and TCA/anaplerotic transcripts (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:NNT) and the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit rise (gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:COX6B1, gene:CYCS).", "Step 5 (measured discordance, prospective consequence): the mitochondrial expansion is nuclear-genome-biased while mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2; exceptions gene:MT-ND5, gene:MT-ND4L up), predicting that added respiratory-chain capacity is incompletely assembled; this predicts reduced spare respiratory capacity under a future energetic or phagocytic challenge and does not by itself establish an ATP deficit in the mock condition.", "Step 6 (downstream signalling): lysosomal/lipid loading and membrane lipid remodelling raise chemokine and inflammasome-priming transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:CD14, gene:TLR2) as a consequence, not a cause; this branch is weak against the selected-list background (mean effect below list mean) and is accompanied by decreased gene:TNFAIP3, gene:TNIP1, gene:RELB and gene:CSF1, so it is not a canonical NF-kB or interferon activation state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lipid-acquisition and storage state that keeps sterol sensing 'hungry', driving coordinated CLEAR/lysosomal and mitochondrial-anabolic transcription rather than an interferon program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12915851272015655, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2549143032513983, "cosine_similarity": 0.4182366053853886, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5740129449838188, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12915851272015655, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2549143032513983, "cosine_similarity": 0.4182366053853886, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5740129449838188, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.87767, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 11}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_083", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential set (all |log ratio| \u003e= 1.00 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a global upward bias (77.1% positive, mean +1.39); all pathway claims are made relative to that internal background, and the logarithm base is left as reported and not converted.", "Elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and trafficking transcripts indicate an engaged lysosomal biogenesis program, not directly measured enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, compartment volume, or degradative flux; no lysosomal lipid, cholesterol, pH or activity pool was measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin contaminants, so spot-level directions are treated as weak consistency evidence about proteoform redistribution, never as identified single proteins.", "Absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, GRN, PSAP, SQSTM1 and LAMP2 from the list means they were not called differential (or were filtered), not that they are unchanged or unexpressed; the egress arm is therefore 'not co-induced', which is weaker than 'impaired'.", "Astrocyte co-culture, unstated replicate number and possible compositional/normalisation effects could generate part of the global up-shift; the genotype comparison is assumed isogenic and mock-treated as stated.", "Increased cargo load in APOE4 is inferred from receptor transcripts and DAM-like markers; no phagocytic assay is supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal cargo economics: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and late-endosome/lysosome trafficking machinery are coordinately elevated far above the global upward shift of this differential-expression list, together with TFEB/MITF and phagocytic/scavenger receptors and DAM-like markers, whereas the measured hydrolase-containing protein spots are not uniformly increased (some fall) and no sterol-egress component is elevated while sterol re-esterification/storage transcripts (SOAT1, DGAT1) are. We propose that the limiting node is functional degradative and export flux per lysosome for lipid/membrane cargo, not the transcriptional supply of lysosomal genes; the transcriptional expansion is a compensatory CLEAR-type response to retained cargo. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia given an equal, quantified pulse of lipidic cargo (pHrodo/BODIPY-labelled myelin or oxLDL), APOE4 should show longer cargo residence and greater retained undigested lipid per unit LAMP1 compartment volume, i.e. lower normalised degradative flux (DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesterol clearance per LAMP1 volume), despite higher hydrolase mRNA. If APOE4 per-lysosome flux is equal or proportionally higher than APOE3, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Relieving the egress node (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/ABCA1 overexpression) without changing uptake should lower lysosomal cholesterol and reduce the APOE4 excess of hydrolase/v-ATPase/TFEB-target transcripts toward APOE3; if the transcript program stays elevated after cargo lipid is cleared, the compensatory-response step is weakened.", "TFEB knockdown or TFEB nuclear-translocation blockade should abolish the APOE4 excess of hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and further slow cargo clearance; persistence of the transcript excess would falsify step 2.", "SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 sterol from cholesteryl-ester stores to free cholesterol and increase, not decrease, the lysosomal stress/CLEAR transcript signature; a decrease would contradict step 4.", "Quantitative enzymology should show that the APOE4 increase in cathepsin B/D/L and beta-hexosaminidase mRNA is not matched by a proportional increase in mature-enzyme activity per cell, with a relative shift toward pro-forms; strictly proportional activity gains would falsify step 3.", "Control against the alternative global explanation: if a broad, cargo-independent biogenesis shift (nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts are also strongly enriched, p=3e-4) drives the phenotype, then blocking cargo uptake (cytochalasin D or scavenger-receptor blockade) should leave the APOE4 endolysosomal transcript signature intact; the present hypothesis predicts it should be substantially attenuated."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia sit in a higher cargo-uptake state - scavenger/phagocytic and opsonin receptor transcripts are up (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA) alongside DAM-like markers (gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:LGALS3, gene:APOE). Actual uptake rate is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (measured): a coordinated CLEAR-type transcriptional expansion of the endolysosome accompanies this state - gene:TFEB and gene:MITF up, luminal hydrolases up as a set (median log-ratio +2.63 vs +1.46 background; permutation p=7e-4, robust to leave-one-out), all measured v-ATPase subunits up (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D2), and late-endosome/lysosome trafficking and positioning machinery up (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:ARL8B, gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5Z1) with lysosomal solute carriers (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5).", "Step 3 (bottleneck; partly inferred): transcript-level capacity is not converted proportionally into hydrolytic protein and flux. Cathepsin-candidate protein spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and v-ATPase-candidate spots fall (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) despite gene:ATP6V1E1 being up; the mannose-6-phosphate delivery arm is internally discordant (gene:IGF2R and gene:GNPTG up but gene:M6PR down, gene:CTSS strongly down). Spot identities are ambiguous, so this is a consistency argument, not proof of reduced enzyme.", "Step 4 (inferred): with degradation/egress limiting, lipidic cargo is retained in LAMP1/RAB7 compartments (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2 up as expanded-compartment markers). No cholesterol-egress or neutral-lipolysis component appears elevated in this DE list (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA absent, i.e. not called differential), while ER-lysosome sterol-transfer gene:OSBPL8 is down and the storage arm gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 is up - predicting diversion of liberated sterol/fatty acid into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol stores rather than export.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts; inferred bioenergetics): the fraction of lipid that does reach the cytosol supports an elevated oxidative program (nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA transcripts up as a set, permutation p=3e-4; e.g. gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2), consistent with continuous lipid processing demand rather than with a purely inflammatory state.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): sustained retained cargo keeps the CLEAR program, sterol-synthesis transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24) and priming markers engaged, producing the APOE4-specific steady state observed under mock treatment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia over-transcribe a TFEB-type endolysosomal program because per-lysosome catabolic/egress flux for internalised lipid-membrane cargo is the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23687410050470217, "cosine_similarity": 0.4178604806162135, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5953203883495146, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23687410050470217, "cosine_similarity": 0.4178604806162135, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5953203883495146, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.83453325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 51}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_074", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance differences at MPC2, PDP1, SLC25A1 and the OXPHOS/TCA genes are accompanied by proportionate protein and activity changes; no protein or activity measurement of these specific products is supplied (the protein-spot layer contains only ambiguous multi-candidate spots).", "The RNA logarithm base is not stated in the workbook and is preserved as reported; RNA effects (range -7.9 to +15.5) are therefore not on the same scale as the protein-spot log2 values and the two modalities are compared only by direction and rank, never by magnitude.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment claims are made relative to this selected list's own strongly positive background (mean +1.39, 77% positive), which is a conservative but non-standard null.", "The negative mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflect real transcript ratios rather than 10X Flex probe coverage, ambient RNA, or mitochondrial-fraction QC filtering differences between genotypes; this assumption is the weakest link in the chain and Step 4 is the most disposable step.", "Pseudobulk contrasts derive from microglia and not from the co-cultured astrocytes; biological replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so nominal p-values cannot be converted into a confident effect-size estimate.", "No metabolite, isotope-tracing, respirometry, lipid-droplet, membrane-potential or mtDNA copy-number measurement is supplied; every flux, localization and causal-direction statement above is a hypothesis, not an established result.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and are not treated as identified proteins anywhere in this hypothesis."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 not by a generic increase in metabolism but by a selectively coherent transcript program at the mitochondrial carbon-entry node: pyruvate import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation (MPC2, PDP1, DLD), TCA/dehydrogenase and nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain machinery, and the citrate/malate carriers are all raised well above the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list, whereas committed glycolytic enzymes (HK2, PFKP, HK3) are not raised and mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) run against the global up-shift. We hypothesise that this configuration increases pyruvate entry and anaplerotic/citrate turnover faster than terminal, mtDNA-core-dependent oxidation can consume it, so citrate is exported through SLC25A1 to a cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool that feeds the co-elevated SREBP sterol/fatty-acid and neutral-lipid esterification program, with the lysosomal/TREM2-APOE program engaged downstream of the resulting lipid load. All flux, enzyme-activity, localization and directionality statements are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should cut U-13C-glucose carbon entry into citrate (M+2) and into glucose-derived palmitate/cholesterol by a larger fraction than in isogenic APOE3, and should reduce BODIPY/neutral-lipid droplet content toward APOE3 levels without reducing glucose uptake. If APOE4 lipid-droplet content and glucose-to-lipid labelling are unchanged by MPC blockade, the pyruvate-entry bottleneck is wrong.", "U-13C-glucose tracing at steady state should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 in the M+2 citrate fraction and in glucose-derived lipogenic labelling, with equal or lower M+3 lactate fraction. Higher lactate labelling and secreted lactate in APOE4 would falsify Step 2 and Step 3 and support a plain aerobic-glycolysis mechanism instead.", "PDH phosphorylation at Ser293 should be lower in APOE4 than APOE3 (consistent with elevated PDP1); unchanged or higher pSer293 weakens Step 3 even if MPC2 protein is elevated.", "Respirometry should show APOE4 with higher basal and pyruvate/malate-driven oxygen consumption but a maximal (FCCP) respiration and ATP-linked respiration that do not increase in proportion to the nuclear subunit up-shift, i.e. a compressed spare respiratory capacity. If maximal respiration and complex IV/V in-gel activity scale fully with the nuclear transcripts, Step 4 (mtDNA-core limitation) is refuted and the mechanism reduces to a straightforward oxidative-and-lipogenic shift.", "Blocking the export arm - SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or ACLY inhibition - should suppress APOE4 lipid-droplet excess while leaving pyruvate-driven respiration intact or increased; if lipid droplets persist unchanged, the citrate-export route in Step 5 is wrong.", "Quantitative mtDNA copy number and mtDNA-encoded transcript measurement by a non-10X method (ddPCR / bulk RNA-seq without mitochondrial QC filtering) should reproduce the reduced MT-ATP6, MT-CYB and MT-CO2 signal in APOE4; failure to reproduce it would show the mitonuclear imbalance was a single-cell quantification artefact.", "If the mechanism holds, restoring terminal oxidative capacity (e.g. mitochondrially targeted electron carrier / methylene blue or NDI1 expression) should lower citrate export and lipid droplets in APOE4 without changing MPC2 or SREBF1 transcript levels; an unchanged lipid phenotype under restored oxidation would weaken the overflow logic."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show coordinate transcript elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial machinery - TCA/dehydrogenase enzymes (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:DLD, gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1), complex I-V subunits and assembly factors (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:CYCS, gene:COX5B, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:NDUFAF4, gene:COX20), and carriers/import components (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44). This set is enriched above the list-wide positive shift (permutation p\u003c0.001; 36/36 subunit/assembly genes positive), so it is not explained by the global up-shift alone.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, contrasting): committed glycolytic steps are not part of that up-shift - gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP are strongly negative and gene:HK3 negative, while glucose/monocarboxylate transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC16A1) and gene:GPI/gene:ENO1/gene:PFKM are positive. Inferred (not measured): glucose uptake capacity is preserved while cytosolic commitment to lactate output is comparatively reduced.", "Step 3 (inferred activity/flux): elevated gene:MPC2 (largest metabolic-transport effect in the set) and gene:PDP1 (PDH-activating phosphatase) with gene:DLD are inferred to increase mitochondrial pyruvate import and to shift pyruvate dehydrogenase toward its dephosphorylated, active form, raising pyruvate-derived acetyl-CoA entry into the TCA cycle. PDH phosphorylation state, acetyl-CoA and pyruvate pools were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred capacity mismatch): the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores needed to assemble complexes I, III, IV and V run opposite to the global up-shift (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 negative; lower-tail permutation p=0.02; gene:MT-ND5 and gene:MT-ND4L positive, so the set is not uniform). We infer a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch in which coupled, terminal oxidation does not scale with the expanded nuclear-encoded entry and dehydrogenase machinery.", "Step 5 (inferred flux/localization): with carbon entry raised and terminal oxidation capped, citrate accumulates and is inferred to be exported by the elevated citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1, with gene:SLC25A11 supporting malate/oxoglutarate exchange) into a cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool. ACLY, ACACA and FASN were not measured in these data and this cytosolic pool is therefore inferred, not observed.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, downstream): the lipogenic/sterol transcription program is coherently positive (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) together with neutral-lipid esterification (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) and lipoprotein/uptake genes (gene:APOE, gene:SCARB1, gene:NPC2); 16/16 lipid-sterol genes positive (permutation p=0.016 on direction). Inferred: increased triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage in APOE4.", "Step 7 (measured abundance, consequence): a lysosomal/degradative program is co-elevated (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) alongside gene:TREM2, consistent with a cell attempting to clear the inferred stored-lipid load; gene:CTSS is a clear exception."], "title": "APOE4 microglia widen the mitochondrial pyruvate-to-citrate node (MPC2/PDP1/SLC25A1) while glycolytic commitment and mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS cores lag, routing glucose carbon into SREBP-driven lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13264778643429456, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2918497030056701, "cosine_similarity": 0.4177752098237984, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5792233009708737, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13264778643429456, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2918497030056701, "cosine_similarity": 0.4177752098237984, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5792233009708737, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.520266, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 52}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_064", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77.1% positive, median +1.46 on an unspecified log base); program coherence is judged against that biased background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. ACLY, FASN, CPT1A, PDK1, LDHA, PKM, ATF4, PPARGC1A, TFAM, ABCA1, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Canonical pathway memberships were specified from background knowledge (unverified, no literature access) and queried before signs were examined; members were not dropped to make directions agree, and both mixed sets (glycolysis) and discordant sets (mtDNA-encoded) are reported.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme capacity; no flux, enzyme activity, metabolite pool, membrane potential, lipid-droplet content or protein localisation was measured here, and none is reported as observed.", "2-D protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each; 64/92 spots positive overall, median +0.485), so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as identification of an individual protein; all candidate identities are retained.", "Genes within a program are correlated, so the binomial/permutation comparisons quoted are descriptive coherence checks against the selected-list background, not formal pathway-enrichment inference.", "Effects are cross-sectional isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 differences at day 30 under mock treatment in microglia-astrocyte co-culture; any reduced reserve inferred from Step 7 would be a defect revealed only by a future challenge, not an established ongoing deficit in the measured condition.", "Astrocyte co-culture means measured RNA may include non-cell-autonomous influence; genotype effects are not resolved to a purely microglia-intrinsic cause."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (isogenic vs APOE3), the dominant transcriptional difference is a coordinated cell-state change in carbon routing, not a glycolytic shift: committed glucose-entry isoforms are lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) while uptake receptors, lysosomal hydrolase, mitochondrial pyruvate/amino-acid/fatty-acid entry, TCA and nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts are coordinately higher (38/38 nuclear OXPHOS members positive, median +2.64; TCA/pyruvate-entry members 10/10 positive, median +4.74, both far above the 77% positive / +1.46 median background of this selected DE list). Together with citrate/acetyl-CoA export components (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93) and an active SREBP-type lipogenic/sterol module (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69), this predicts that in APOE4 a larger fraction of catabolised lipid- and amino-acid-derived carbon is re-esterified into stored/membrane lipid instead of being fully oxidised. Increased ETC transcript abundance is NOT claimed to be increased respiratory flux: mtDNA-encoded transcripts are discordantly lower (4/6 negative, gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33), so the nuclear increase may be adaptive expansion or compensation for limiting mtDNA-encoded core subunits; the decisive flux is unmeasured. No causality is established by these abundance data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective stable-isotope tracing (U-13C-glucose vs U-13C-glutamine vs 13C-palmitate) in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, a lower glucose-derived fraction of citrate/lactate and a higher glutamine- and fatty-acid-derived fraction of TCA intermediates, plus greater 13C incorporation into cholesterol and fatty acids/cholesteryl esters. If APOE4 instead shows increased glucose-to-lactate flux with unchanged non-glucose contribution, the routing mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating adaptation vs failed compensation: extracellular flux analysis in mock conditions should distinguish successful oxidative expansion (APOE4 basal and maximal OCR and etomoxir/BPTES-sensitive respiration higher than APOE3, spare capacity preserved) from compensation for mtDNA-encoded subunit limitation (APOE4 basal OCR equal or lower and maximal/spare capacity reduced despite 38/38 higher nuclear ETC transcripts). The second result would weaken Steps 4 and 6 while supporting Step 7; assembled complex I/IV holoenzyme quantification (BN-PAGE) plus mtDNA copy number should accompany it.", "Neutral-lipid imaging/lipidomics should show higher lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester content in mock APOE4 microglia; inhibiting the citrate/acetyl-CoA route (SLC25A1 inhibition or ACSS2 knockdown) or SOAT1/DGAT1 should reduce the APOE4-specific excess more than in APOE3. No genotype-selective reduction would weaken Step 5.", "Blocking cargo supply (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lysosomal acid-hydrolase inhibition) should lower the APOE4-specific 13C-lipid-to-sterol/ester labelling and lipid droplet excess; if the APOE4 lipid excess persists unchanged, the lysosome-to-lipogenesis coupling (Steps 1, 2, 5) is wrong and a purely de novo SREBP-driven mechanism is favoured.", "Under an added metabolic challenge (glucose withdrawal or oligomycin), the mechanism predicts APOE4 survives glucose withdrawal at least as well as APOE3 (non-glucose substrate use), whereas the failed-compensation alternative predicts APOE4 is more vulnerable; a clear APOE4 vulnerability to glucose withdrawal would weaken the selected mechanism.", "Targeted proteomics resolving the ambiguous spots should show cathepsin B/D/L and hexosaminidase peptides accounting for the positive lysosomal spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:027); if those spots are instead explained solely by actin/keratin/tropomyosin candidates, the protein-level support for Step 2 is void (RNA-level support would remain)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia express higher lipid/lipoprotein-uptake and phagocytic receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:APOE +1.24), inferred to increase delivery of lipid and lipoprotein cargo to the endolysosome (delivery itself not measured).", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred capacity): A broad lysosomal hydrolase/acidification module is higher (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:TFEB +2.38; 16/18 represented members positive), and lysosome-candidate protein spots are predominantly positive (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.59, protein_spot:027 +0.59, protein_spot:012 +0.68), consistent with expanded lysosomal hydrolytic capacity that liberates fatty acids and sterols intracellularly.", "Step 3 (routing away from glucose commitment): Glucose transporters rise (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37) but the committed hexokinase/phosphofructokinase isoforms fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) with only isoform-switched increases downstream (gene:PFKM +2.41, gene:GPI +2.06, gene:ENO1 +2.17), so a coherent glycolytic-commitment increase is not supported; glucose carbon is not the program that is coordinately amplified.", "Step 4 (mitochondrial substrate entry and TCA): Transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and PDH activation (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54), TCA and redox-shuttle steps (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65), amino-acid anaplerosis (gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS +1.35, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:ABAT +1.54) and lipid catabolism/beta-oxidation support (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:CROT +1.03) are coordinately higher, indicating expanded capacity for oxidising lysosome- and amino-acid-derived carbon.", "Step 5 (carbon export to lipogenesis): Higher gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) and gene:ACSS2 (+2.93) provide routes to cytosolic acetyl-CoA, and the sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification module is uniformly positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06), so a fraction of the mobilised carbon is inferred to be diverted into new fatty acid/sterol and neutral-lipid ester rather than completely oxidised to CO2.", "Step 6 (state-level consequence, partly prospective): The combined uptake + hydrolysis + re-esterification routing predicts higher neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content and larger lipid droplet load in APOE4 microglia under mock conditions, with electron-transport transcript expansion (gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36) accompanying, not necessarily driving, this state.", "Step 7 (explicit uncertainty node): Because mtDNA-encoded ETC transcripts are discordantly lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33 versus gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), nuclear/mtDNA subunit stoichiometry may limit ETC assembly; if so the same routing state would be sustained partly by anabolic disposal of carbon rather than by increased terminal oxidation, and stress-associated transcripts (gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51, gene:SHMT2 +2.22, gene:HSPA9 +2.35, gene:FIS1 +2.31, gene:PRDX3 +3.49) would be the readout of that imbalance."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lysosome-derived and non-glucose carbon into mitochondrial TCA plus citrate/acetyl-CoA export for lipid synthesis and storage, rather than into glycolysis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27556031458848723, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28876096397622847, "cosine_similarity": 0.4175384941178043, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5857702265372169, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27556031458848723, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28876096397622847, "cosine_similarity": 0.4175384941178043, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5857702265372169, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.82308025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 12}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_096", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 positive / 507 negative), so absent genes (e.g., ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, ISG15, MX1, IFIT1) are unknown, not unchanged; all directional comparisons are made against this 77%-positive background, and the logarithm base of 'reported log fold change' is unspecified and preserved as given.", "Transcript abundance is treated as measured; uptake, lysosomal lipid content, ER-accessible sterol, esterification, respiratory and glycolytic flux, TFEB nuclear localization and SREBP proteolytic processing are inferred, not observed.", "Genes were assigned to programs a priori from canonical pathway membership (unverified background knowledge) before directions were inspected; no member was added or dropped to make signs agree, and genes within a program are correlated, so counts are descriptive and not a formal enrichment test.", "2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidate genes over 92 spots, none unique); no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein, and spot-level direction is used only for compatibility/contradiction testing, with processed vs precursor forms and PTM charge trains as an alternative explanation for opposite-direction spots sharing candidates.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcripts (e.g., gene:S100B +6.00, gene:CSF1 -5.91) may reflect non-microglial or cross-talk contributions rather than microglia-intrinsic APOE4 effects.", "Reduced spare respiratory or lysosomal reserve implied by the mitonuclear mismatch is a prospective, challenge-revealed prediction; the mock-condition data do not establish an ongoing bioenergetic defect, and no causal direction has been established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated lipid-handling cell-state change rather than by interferon or NF-kB activation: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification are higher, the lysosomal biogenesis module (TFEB, v-ATPase, hydrolases) is higher, the SREBP sterol-demand program remains coordinately ON despite that uptake, and nuclear-encoded mitochondrial carrier/TCA/ETC transcripts are strongly higher while mtDNA-encoded ETC transcripts are not. We interpret this as altered lipid routing (into lysosomes and cholesteryl/acyl esters, away from the ER-accessible sterol pool) that raises catabolic demand and drives a partly mismatched mitochondrial build-out; interferon signaling is not supported (no canonical ISG is represented in the supplied list) and the NF-kB/chemokine changes are not distinguishable from the list-wide upward bias of this selected result set.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/biochemistry in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show more filipin/LipidTOX-positive lysosomal and neutral-lipid stores and a LOWER ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/D4H probe) than APOE3, with higher nuclear SREBP2 (cleaved) despite higher lipid load. If ER-accessible cholesterol is equal or higher in APOE4 while SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated, the routing/sterol-sensing step (steps 1-3) is wrong.", "Prospective pharmacology: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or lysosomal cholesterol mobilization (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) should normalize SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24) and reduce the TFEB/hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript increase in APOE4 but not APOE3. No genotype-selective normalization would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective flux: Seahorse respirometry should show at most a modest basal OCR difference but a genotype-selective deficit in maximal/spare respiratory capacity and in ATP-linked respiration after a substrate or phagocytic challenge in APOE4, with reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein (MT-CO1) relative to nuclear subunits (NDUFB8, SDHB, UQCRC2, ATP5F1A) by blue-native/western. If APOE4 instead shows proportionally increased maximal respiration and matched complex assembly, the mechanism should be re-labeled successful adaptation/increased throughput and step 5 is falsified.", "Prospective genetic test: TFEB knockdown or Torin-independent TFEB inhibition should blunt the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript increase and, if the mechanism holds, further raise lysosomal lipid accumulation and SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4; if hydrolase induction is TFEB-independent, step 2 is falsified.", "Prospective interferon test (rejecting the assigned focus): APOE4 mock microglia should NOT show elevated ISG15, MX1, IFIT1/3 or phospho-STAT1 relative to APOE3, and blocking IFNAR1 should not change the lysosomal/mitochondrial transcript differences. A robust APOE4 ISG signature or IFNAR-dependent loss of the lipid/lysosome program would falsify the rejection and this mechanism's framing.", "Prospective proteomic disambiguation: targeted MS/immunoblot of the up-shifted spot train (protein_spot:041/043/044/045/046/047) should identify which candidate (e.g., ANXA1 vs TALDO1) is increased; if the increased species is TALDO1, it contradicts gene:TALDO1 (-2.32) and would require an added post-transcriptional step, and if lysosomal hydrolase protein (mature CTSB/CTSD, HEXB) is uniformly LOWER in APOE4 by immunoblot, step 2 is contradicted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases microglial uptake and internal storage routing of lipid/lipoprotein cargo: higher transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein receptors and esterification enzymes (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:APOE +1.24; log fold change, base as reported).", "Increased membrane/lipid cargo raises lysosomal degradative load, accompanied by a coordinated lysosomal biogenesis module: gene:TFEB +2.38 with hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:NAGLU +5.91) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68), 34/37 queried-and-represented members positive.", "Because sterol is retained in lysosomal/esterified pools rather than delivered to the ER sensor, the SREBP program stays ON despite higher uptake: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:CH25H +1.62 (17/17 represented members positive). This is a demand signal, not proof of increased sterol synthetic flux.", "Catabolized lipid- and amino-acid-derived substrate is directed toward mitochondria: mitochondrial carriers and TCA/anaplerotic enzymes are the most strongly shifted represented module (gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:GLS +1.35; 17/17 positive, median +4.5 vs list median +1.46), with beta-oxidation/peroxisomal support (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24) and mixed glycolysis (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:ENO1 +2.17 up but gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08 down).", "The nuclear-encoded ETC build-out is not matched by the mitochondrial genome: all 32 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are positive (e.g., gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36; median +2.59) while mtDNA-encoded transcripts are mostly negative (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95). Assembled-complex stoichiometry and respiratory flux were not measured; this predicts reduced realized gain/spare capacity that would be exposed by a future energetic or phagocytic challenge, not an already-failed respiration in the mock condition.", "The same lipid-laden lysosomal state co-occurs with a lipid-associated/disease-associated microglial surface and iron-handling profile (gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CD74 +3.84, gene:FTH1 +2.53) and with phagocytic/complement receptor transcripts (gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:C1QB +1.13, gene:C1QC +1.17, gene:C5AR1 +1.32, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:MRC1 +1.36; 19/20 positive), consistent with a self-reinforcing uptake-storage loop.", "A modest chemokine output is a secondary, weakly supported consequence of this state (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL1 +1.59, gene:CXCL2 +1.65, gene:CXCL3 +1.56, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NFKBIZ +3.07, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:IL18 +1.46) with brakes lower (gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05, gene:TNIP1 -2.38); as a whole the NF-kB module (16 up / 7 down, median +1.45) is indistinguishable from the selected list's 77% positive, +1.46 median background, and no canonical interferon-stimulated gene is represented at all, so an interferon-driven mechanism is rejected."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lipid/sterol into lysosomal and esterified stores, sustaining a sterol-demand signal and an expanded lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic program with an unmatched mtDNA-encoded arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13894324853228962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21543784520424678, "cosine_similarity": 0.4170293658462423, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5819676375404531, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13894324853228962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21543784520424678, "cosine_similarity": 0.4170293658462423, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5819676375404531, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.68292275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 13}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_044", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript effects are read as directional ranks only: the RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects up to ~15 units are not interpretable as log2 ratios; conclusions rest on coordinated sign and on rank position relative to the list background (median +1.46, 77% positive).", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, so pathway means are only meaningful against the internal background of the same list; absolute enrichment against the genome cannot be assessed.", "Probe-based 10X Flex measurement of the six mtDNA-encoded genes is assumed to reflect their true relative abundance; if the assay under-captures mitochondrial transcripts in a genotype-independent way the comparison holds, but any genotype-linked capture bias would invalidate step 2.", "Nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript increases are assumed to be at least partly translated, so that unassembled subunit pressure is plausible; no OXPHOS protein or assembly measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features and are not treated as identified proteins; none of the 92 spots contains an OXPHOS subunit candidate, so the protein layer neither supports nor refutes the core claim.", "The astrocyte co-culture and the absence of replicate counts mean cell-composition or ambient-RNA differences between genotypes cannot be excluded as contributors to the global positive RNA shift.", "No flux, respirometry, mtDNA copy number, metabolite, glycogen or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied; all flux, localisation and causal statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia express a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes, carriers/import, cristae-shaping genes) while mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts are comparatively reduced; we hypothesise that the resulting shortage of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not a shortage of nuclear subunits, is the rate-limiting step for assembling functional complexes I/III/IV/V, so respiratory flux fails to scale with the expanded nuclear program and glucose-derived carbon is preferentially routed into glycogen synthesis and citrate-export/lipogenic storage rather than into increased glycolytic-plus-oxidative ATP flux. Causality is not established by these association data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20 signal): APOE4 microglia should show lower maximal/uncoupled O2 consumption and lower spare respiratory capacity per unit mass than isogenic APOE3, despite equal or higher nuclear OXPHOS protein. Equal or higher normalised maximal respiration would weaken the mechanism.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome: APOE4 should show reduced assembled complex I, III2, IV and V holoenzyme relative to total nuclear-encoded subunit signal, with accumulation of sub-assemblies. Normal holoenzyme stoichiometry would falsify the assembly-bottleneck step.", "mtDNA copy number per nuclear genome and independent qPCR of MT-CO2/MT-ATP6/MT-CYB should be lower in APOE4; if mtDNA copy number and mt-transcripts are equal between genotypes, step 2 is an assay artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: relieving the mtDNA-encoded supply limit (TFAM or mitochondrial-transcription/translation-capacity boost, or LRPPRC/mitoribosome-supportive rescue) in APOE4 should raise assembled complex IV/V and maximal respiration and reduce glycogen and neutral-lipid storage, WITHOUT normalising the elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Conversely, low-dose doxycycline (mitochondrial translation inhibition) in APOE3 should phenocopy the APOE4 pattern (nuclear OXPHOS transcripts up, glucose carbon shunted to glycogen/lipid). Failure of the APOE3 doxycycline phenocopy, or rescue that works only by lowering nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, would weaken the mechanism.", "U-13C-glucose tracing: APOE4 should show reduced m+2 labelling of TCA intermediates per unit glucose consumed with increased 13C incorporation into glycogen and into fatty acids/DAG-TAG, and increased 13C-citrate export signature; equal glucose oxidation with equal storage labelling would falsify the carbon-rerouting step.", "Substrate-restriction test: switching glucose for galactose (forcing OXPHOS-dependent ATP) should reduce APOE4 ATP and viability more than APOE3; equal tolerance of galactose would argue against an OXPHOS capacity limit.", "Phagocytic challenge (pHrodo bead or myelin uptake) should reveal a larger APOE4 deficit in ATP/uptake than under mock conditions; if APOE4 matches APOE3 under load, the functional-consequence step is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show uniformly higher transcript levels for 37/37 detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (mean effect +2.8 vs +1.39 list background; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME), for TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G) and for mitochondrial carriers/import/cristae genes (gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A46, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:CHCHD3, gene:FIS1). INFERRED: an expanded mitochondrial-biogenesis / compensatory nuclear program; mitochondrial mass, mtDNA copy number and OXPHOS protein levels were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): mtDNA-encoded transcripts run against this trend (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 negative; only gene:MT-ND5 and gene:MT-ND4L positive), giving a nuclear-minus-mitochondrial effect gap of ~3.6 log units (permutation p~1e-4). INFERRED: the pool of core catalytic subunits available for assembly is low relative to the nuclear-encoded accessory subunits.", "INFERRED (bottleneck): stoichiometric mismatch limits maturation of complexes I, III, IV and V, so electron-transport and ATP-synthase capacity per mitochondrion is lower than the nuclear transcript program predicts; unassembled nuclear-encoded subunits add matrix proteostatic load, weakly consistent with elevated stress-response transcripts (gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:EIF2A). Assembly state, respiration and proteostatic load are unmeasured.", "INFERRED (compensation): capacity for delivering cytosolic reducing equivalents and anaplerotic carbon to the matrix is transcriptionally raised (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1) even though matrix NADH reoxidation is assembly-limited; this is inferred capacity, not measured flux.", "MEASURED (RNA): committed glycolytic steps are not coordinately increased (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2, gene:HK3 all negative) while glucose/monocarboxylate transport (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC16A1) and downstream storage routes are increased: glycogen synthesis and lysosomal glycogen turnover (gene:GYS1, gene:UGP2, gene:GAA), citrate export and lipogenesis (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1) and lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR). The oxidative pentose-phosphate arm is not raised (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1 negative). INFERRED: glucose carbon is stored (glycogen, neutral lipid) rather than fully oxidised.", "INFERRED (consequence): APOE4 microglia hold less spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass and depend more on stored carbon, predicting impaired ATP supply when oxidative demand rises (phagocytic or stimulated states) - a state not assayed in these mock-treatment data."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance limits respiratory-chain assembly in APOE4 microglia and reroutes glucose carbon into glycogen and lipid stores"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10273972602739725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27697521293607935, "cosine_similarity": 0.4156901723614165, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mean_absolute_error": 0.58984142394822, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10273972602739725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27697521293607935, "cosine_similarity": 0.4156901723614165, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.58984142394822, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.745627, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 53}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_068", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77% positive, median +1.46) in an unspecified logarithm base; we therefore judge pathway signal only relative to this selected background and preserve the base as reported.", "Genes absent from the list (SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, CERT1, ASAH1, PSAP, NPC1, GALC) are treated as not measured, not as unchanged; de novo sphingolipid synthesis is therefore untested here.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and possibly non-proportional proxy for enzyme protein, and enzyme protein a non-proportional proxy for luminal catalytic activity and flux.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration (e.g. spots containing CTSD/CTSB/HEXB/MAN2B1/CHIT1 candidates change in both directions).", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; we assume the profiled RNA is predominantly microglial, which the supplied metadata does not confirm.", "The global positive RNA shift is assumed to be at least partly a selection/normalisation property rather than a true genome-wide upshift, so all pathway claims are made against that shifted background.", "Correlation between genotype and expression is assumed, not demonstrated, to reflect an APOE4-initiated causal chain; no perturbation was performed in the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background transcriptional induction of lysosomal glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin hydrolases (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1, SUMF1) together with acidification, late-endosomal and lipid-uptake/esterification transcripts. We propose this is a compensatory CLEAR-type response to an increased sphingolipid-containing membrane/lipoprotein cargo load, and that catabolic flux at the luminal glucosylceramide -\u003e ceramide and GM2 -\u003e GM3 steps, not hydrolase transcript abundance, is the primary bottleneck; the resulting substrate retention sustains an enlarged, lipid-loaded late-endosome/lysosome compartment. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; enzyme activity, lipid pools, flux, localization and causal direction are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic reduction of glucosylceramide synthase (UGCG inhibition with eliglustat/miglustat, or UGCG knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should lower LysoTracker/LAMP1-positive compartment volume, reduce GBA/HEXA/SMPD1/TFEB-target transcript induction toward APOE3 levels, and reduce neutral-lipid storage, without lowering SCARB1/CD36 uptake-receptor transcripts. If substrate limitation leaves the hydrolase and lysosomal-expansion signature unchanged, the substrate-load bottleneck is weakened.", "Discriminating alternative arm: supplying enzyme rather than removing substrate (recombinant glucocerebrosidase uptake, GBA overexpression, or SCARB2/LIMP2 co-overexpression) should, if delivery/cofactor capacity is limiting, normalise the phenotype; if enzyme supplementation corrects it while UGCG inhibition does not, the bottleneck is hydrolase delivery, not substrate load, and step 4 as written must be revised.", "Direct lipid test: mass-spectrometry lipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher glucosylceramide/lactosylceramide, GM2 (and/or GM3) and sphingomyelin per cell despite the higher hydrolase transcripts. Equal or lower glycosphingolipid levels in APOE4 would falsify the core claim that turnover flux lags induction.", "Activity-versus-transcript test: in-cell or lysate GBA and beta-hexosaminidase activity assays should show that the fold increase in activity is markedly smaller than the transcript fold change, and that the secreted/cellular activity ratio is higher in APOE4. Activity rising in proportion to transcript, with unchanged secretion ratio, would weaken the decoupling step.", "Cargo-load test: removing the load (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake) should blunt the hydrolase and TFEB-target induction in APOE4. Persistence of the induction under lipid-poor conditions would indicate a cell-autonomous transcriptional difference rather than a compensatory response.", "Specificity control: an unrelated CLEAR-independent module should not show the same above-background elevation; if the hydrolase module's apparent enrichment disappears when compared against size-matched random gene sets from the same differential list (it currently does not; p_up = 1e-4), the signal is a global-shift artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake, sensing and esterification (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:MRC1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD), which we infer increases delivery of sphingolipid-containing membrane and lipoprotein cargo into the endocytic pathway. Cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred compartment state): Cargo converges on an expanded/late-shifted endolysosomal compartment, indicated by gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R, gene:ARL8B, gene:SPNS1 and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP1). Compartment volume, pH and cargo residence time are inferred, not observed.", "Step 3 (inferred trigger): Retained luminal glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin substrate (an unmeasured pool) engages a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR transcriptional response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), which coordinately induces the hydrolase module.", "Step 4 (measured, primary bottleneck): The hydrolase module is induced far above the already positive global shift (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:SUMF1; wider lysosomal set gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD; set mean 4.19 vs 1.39 background, permutation p_up=1e-4). We hypothesise that per-lysosome hydrolytic flux does not scale with these transcripts because the lipid-binding cofactor, carrier and membrane-environment terms are not co-scaled (gene:SCARB2 only +1.06 against gene:GBA +6.71; PSAP, ASAH1, GALC, NPC1 are absent from the supplied differential list and were therefore not measured).", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred routing consequence): Sorting-receptor transcripts move discordantly (gene:M6PR -1.72 while gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:GNPTG +3.02), and retromer/carrier transcripts rise (gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:VAMP3, gene:SCAMP2), consistent with, but not proof of, altered hydrolase delivery/recycling that would further decouple transcript from luminal activity.", "Step 6 (inferred outcome): Incompletely degraded glycosphingolipid is partly re-routed into salvage re-synthesis and storage rather than clearance (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:SGPL1 +1.09, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), producing a self-sustaining lipid-loaded lysosomal state that we propose underlies the APOE4 microglial phenotype under mock conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal glycosphingolipid-hydrolase program that lags a lipid-substrate load, making late-endosomal GlcCer/GM2/sphingomyelin turnover the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14739873721522725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2045206401495526, "cosine_similarity": 0.41413560185209747, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6088058252427184, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14739873721522725, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2045206401495526, "cosine_similarity": 0.41413560185209747, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6088058252427184, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46910625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 54}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_066", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; every claim uses ranks and set-versus-background comparisons inside this one list, never an absolute fold-change interpretation.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1) and not an unbiased transcriptome, so absence of a gene (e.g. most ISGs, HMGCR, NPC1, ABCA1) means 'not in the supplied selected list', not 'unchanged'.", "The whole list is up-shifted (77% positive, median +1.46) and strongly expressed housekeeping transcripts such as ACTB and MT-ATP6 are among the down calls; this pattern is compatible with a normalisation/composition component, so only enrichment relative to this background is treated as signal.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with multiple candidate genes; assigning a spot to a cathepsin/hexosaminidase/v-ATPase is ambiguous, and the spot-level flatness is treated as a weak, non-identifying proxy for hydrolase protein behaviour, not as a measurement of a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for the direction of the biogenesis program only; hydrolase enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, lipid content, and cargo flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcripts may reflect mixed-population or ambient signal; the effect is assumed to be dominated by microglia.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values may be over-optimistic (many are extremely small next to very large fold changes), and set-level statistics are used in preference to single-gene claims."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated increase in scavenger/lipid-uptake and lipogenic-esterification transcripts together with the strongest set-level enrichment in the whole dataset for lysosomal acid hydrolase transcripts (median log FC 2.10 vs global 1.46, Mann-Whitney p = 0.013), while the 2D protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase are the only spot group that fails to follow the global proteome up-shift (median 0.00 vs +0.48 log2, p = 0.085). We hypothesise that increased endolysosomal lipid cargo delivery outstrips luminal hydrolytic capacity, so lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sterol degradation and egress flux is the rate-limiting step of the APOE4 state; the accompanying NF-kB/chemokine transcripts are a secondary, interferon-independent output, since canonical ISGs are essentially absent from the differential list (5/71 ISG members present vs 18/44 hydrolases, Fisher p = 1.9e-5) and GSDMD is strongly down. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (uptake blockade): reducing scavenger-mediated lipid influx in APOE4 microglia (SCARB1 and/or CD36 knockdown or blocking antibody, or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should lower neutral-lipid/LysoTracker load and bring the hydrolase transcript module (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GAA) and CXCL8/CCL2 back toward APOE3 levels within 48-72 h. If the hydrolase transcripts and chemokines stay APOE4-high after uptake blockade, steps 1-3 are wrong and the program is uptake-independent.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (capacity test at the bottleneck): direct enzymatic assays per cell (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, cathepsin B/D activity, lysosomal pH) should show that activity in APOE4 is at most modestly increased and clearly sub-proportional to the transcript increase, and that DQ-BSA / BODIPY-glycosphingolipid clearance rate is slower in APOE4. If APOE4 hydrolase activity and cargo clearance scale with the mRNA increase and lipid load is normal, the proposed bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation 3 (interferon exclusion): blocking type-I interferon signalling (anti-IFNAR1 or a JAK1/2 inhibitor) under mock conditions should leave the lysosomal-hydrolase transcript module, the lipid load, and the chemokine transcripts essentially unchanged in APOE4 cells, and ISG transcripts should be equal between genotypes by targeted qPCR (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1). Detecting a genuine APOE4 ISG signature, or normalisation of the phenotype by IFNAR/JAK blockade, would falsify the interferon-independence of this mechanism and favour an interferon-driven alternative.", "Rescue prediction: increasing luminal degradative capacity specifically (TFEB overexpression combined with, or replaced by, GBA/HEXB overexpression or a chaperone that raises mature hydrolase levels) should reduce lysosomal lipid load and chemokine transcripts in APOE4 without changing the scavenger-receptor transcripts. If raising hydrolase protein and activity fails to reduce lipid load, the bottleneck lies downstream (egress/NPC-type transport or esterification) rather than in hydrolysis.", "Protein-level prediction: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS of mature CTSB, CTSD and HEXB in APOE4 versus APOE3 should show no proportional increase (and possibly a decrease in mature forms with retained pro-forms), consistent with the flat cathepsin-candidate spots. A clear, proportional increase in mature hydrolase protein in APOE4 would weaken step 4 and the whole bottleneck assignment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid scavenging receptors (SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of the differential list, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163, TREM2, ABCA7, PLTP), which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid cargo into the endolysosomal lumen; cargo amount itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the SREBP-axis and esterification transcripts are simultaneously elevated (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LSS, DHCR7, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, DGAT1, SOAT1, LPCAT1), so de novo lipid synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification are inferred not to be shut off by the incoming sterol load, adding to total lipid input rather than compensating for it.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): a compensatory lysosome-biogenesis-type transcript program is induced (TFEB, ATP6V1A, RAB7A, SPNS1, SLC17A5, LAMP1, plus hydrolases CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, SMPD1, GAA, NAGLU, GM2A, MAN2B1, SGSH, DNASE2), with the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid catabolic arm most strongly represented.", "Step 4 (BOTTLENECK; measured protein-spot abundance, inferred capacity): the transcript program is not mirrored in the spot proteome. Spots whose candidate genes include CTSB/CTSD/CTSL/HEXB/ACP2/ATP6V1E1 show a median log2 change of 0.00 and only 47% up, versus median +0.48 and 75% up for all other spots, and several such spots are significantly decreased. Together with the strongly reduced CTSS and IDS transcripts, we infer that mature, correctly delivered luminal hydrolase capacity per unit cargo does not rise in proportion to the mRNA program, making luminal glycosphingolipid/sterol catabolism and downstream cholesterol/sphingoid egress the rate-limiting step.", "Step 5 (inferred, not measured): undegraded glycosphingolipid and sterol cargo therefore accumulates in APOE4 lysosomes, slowing cargo turnover and phagosome/autophagosome resolution. No lipid, lysosomal-pH, or enzyme-activity measurement is supplied, so this pool is inferred and not observed.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, weakest step): the resulting sterile lysosomal lipid stress is proposed to sustain a TLR/NF-kB priming and chemokine output (TLR2, TLR6, CD14, MYD88, TICAM1, NFKBIZ, CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL3, CXCL8, CXCL16, CCL2, NLRP3, PYCARD, IL18) that is explicitly not a type-I interferon program: canonical ISGs are almost absent from the differential list, GSDMD and TNFAIP3 are decreased, and the chemokine set's magnitude does not exceed the global up-shift (set median 1.51 vs global 1.46)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a lipid-uptake-driven lysosomal hydrolase transcript program that is not matched at the protein level, making luminal glycosphingolipid/sterol catabolic capacity the bottleneck (not interferon signalling)"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21923346748883063, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2549114054375293, "cosine_similarity": 0.41301784560799565, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268414239482201, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21923346748883063, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2549114054375293, "cosine_similarity": 0.41301784560799565, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268414239482201, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8861295, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 55}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_052", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so a set is only treated as informative when its mean effect exceeds the strong global positive shift of the selected list (mean +1.39, 77% positive) by permutation; the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript increases for hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits translate into increased lysosomal protein content, and a compensatory (demand-limited) rather than a fully flux-matched interpretation of that induction.", "TFEB transcript elevation reflects increased CLEAR-program output; TFEB protein, phosphorylation and nuclear localisation were not measured.", "Protein spots are ambiguous mixtures of candidate genes; no spot is treated as a unique protein identification and spot evidence is corroborative only.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels are assumed comparably captured by the 10X Flex probe chemistry, which is uncertain; this weakens Step 5 specifically.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoprotein/lipid cargo comparably to both genotypes, so the difference reflects microglial handling rather than differential cargo supply.", "No lipid, flux, pH, respirometry or imaging measurement is supplied; all activity, localisation, flux and causal-direction statements are inferences, and causality is not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background induction of the lysosomal (CLEAR-type) acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program together with mitochondrial pyruvate-import/TCA/Complex-I transcripts, while committed glycolytic steps and mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS subunits are not co-induced. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is lumenal lysosomal degradation of internalised lipid-rich (sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid and lipoprotein) cargo: this step is demand-limited in APOE4, drives compensatory transcriptional expansion of hydrolase and proton-pump capacity, and routes the carbon that is successfully liberated into mitochondrial oxidation, with the residual buffered by SCD/DGAT1-type neutral-lipid esterification. Transcript abundance is measured; hydrolytic flux, lysosomal pH, TFEB localisation, respiratory flux and lipid pools are inferred and not established as causal.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: with a quenched lipid substrate (BODIPY-sphingomyelin or NBD-glucosylceramide) plus DQ-BSA, APOE4 microglia should show greater lysosomal mass/hydrolase content (LAMP1, GBA immunostain) but equal or LOWER degradation rate per unit lysosomal mass, and lipidomics should show accumulated glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin substrate. If APOE4 instead shows higher per-lysosome degradation rate and reduced sphingolipid substrate pools, the demand-limited bottleneck (Step 1) is falsified and the data would instead indicate simple hydrolase over-capacity.", "Phenocopy test: partial inhibition of lysosomal hydrolysis in APOE3 microglia (conduritol-B-epoxide for GBA, or low-dose bafilomycin A1) should reproduce the APOE4 signature, i.e. induce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts together with MPC2/OGDH/NDUF transcripts and neutral-lipid accumulation. Failure of the mitochondrial arm to follow lysosomal inhibition would break the proposed lysosome-to-mitochondria coupling (Steps 3-4).", "Mitochondrial dependence test: APOE4 microglia should show a larger fractional drop in oxygen consumption than APOE3 upon MPC inhibition (UK5099) and upon rotenone, with a smaller compensatory glycolytic reserve. If APOE4 OCR sensitivity is equal or lower and APOE4 is more glycolysis-dependent, Step 4 is weakened.", "Driver test: TFEB nuclear:cytoplasmic ratio (imaging or fractionation) should be higher in APOE4 under mock conditions, and TFEB/TFE3 knockdown should abolish the hydrolase-transcript difference between genotypes. Equal TFEB localisation and TFEB-independent hydrolase induction would falsify Step 2.", "Capacity-ceiling test: BN-PAGE or Complex-I in-gel activity should show that assembled Complex I and Complex V do not increase in proportion to the nuclear-encoded subunit transcripts in APOE4, with unchanged or reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein. Proportional increases in assembled complexes would falsify Step 5 without falsifying Steps 1-4.", "Specificity test (rejects the assigned sterol focus): APOE4 microglia should NOT show increased de-novo sterol synthesis flux (deuterated-water or 13C-acetate labelling into cholesterol) despite SCARB1 elevation. Increased sterol-synthesis flux with coordinated HMGCR/SQLE/FDFT1 induction would favour a sterol-synthesis mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (bottleneck, inferred activity): In APOE4 microglia the hydrolytic capacity of the late endosome/lysosome lumen is insufficient for the delivered lipid-rich cargo, so degradation of sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and ganglioside-type substrates becomes rate-limiting; this activity is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred driver): A CLEAR-type compensatory transcriptional response raises acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, GLA, GAA, GM2A, MAN2B1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, LAMP1, NPC2, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) alongside TFEB transcript; TFEB nuclear localisation and CLEAR-element occupancy are inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred flux): Partial catabolism of the cargo liberates fatty acids, sphingoid bases and amino acids into the cytosol, increasing the demand for a mitochondrial oxidative sink rather than for glycolytic ATP.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Nuclear-encoded mitochondrial pyruvate-import, TCA and Complex-I transcripts increase coordinately (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G, DLD, GOT1, GLUD1, and 19/19 detected NDUF subunits), while the committed glycolytic enzymes HK2 and PFKP fall; we infer a bias of carbon entry toward mitochondrial oxidation in APOE4.", "Step 5 (inferred capacity ceiling): Because mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are not co-induced, the nuclear-encoded expansion is predicted to over-run assembled respiratory-chain capacity, leaving the mitochondrial sink itself only partially able to absorb the liberated carbon.", "Step 6 (inferred lipid outcome): The unoxidised remainder is predicted to be esterified and stored, consistent with elevated SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1 and SOAT1 transcripts, giving APOE4 microglia accumulated undegraded sphingolipid substrate plus increased neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content; no lipid pool was measured here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a demand-limited lysosomal hydrolase program coupled to mitochondrial TCA/Complex-I carbon disposal, not an altered sterol-synthesis program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14481409001956946, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19617959855566, "cosine_similarity": 0.41267244967994615, "direction_accuracy": 0.24110032362459546, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041488673139158, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14481409001956946, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19617959855566, "cosine_similarity": 0.41267244967994615, "direction_accuracy": 0.24110032362459546, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041488673139158, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85630625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 56}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_023", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the supplied file; all RNA statements are used only as direction and within-list rank/magnitude, never as absolute fold changes.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome. Structural inspection shows source rows 2-509 each carry two genes of opposite sign while rows 108-1709 carry a single, almost always positive gene (1705 up vs 507 down, 100% of paired rows sign-discordant). The apparent global positive shift (median +1.46) is therefore treated as a list-construction artifact, and all enrichment tests were run within the up-regulated sub-list. This assumption is central; if the shift is instead a genuine global transcriptional up-shift, the enrichment estimates change.", "Protein spots carry 1-6 candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins. Attribution of protein_spot:052/053/027/058/067/069 to cathepsins and protein_spot:064/065 to a V-ATPase V1 subunit is provisional; many spots are dominated by keratin/actin candidates and no spot-level mass-spectrometric quantification of a named protein is supplied.", "Measured transcript and spot abundance are assumed here to bear on, but not to equal, enzyme activity, luminal pH, subcellular localization, or degradative flux. None of pH, protease activity, cargo clearance, LysoTracker/EM morphology, autophagic flux, or lipid composition was measured.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture; differences in co-culture composition or microglial purity between genotypes could produce apparent cell-intrinsic differences and were not controllable from the supplied data.", "No replicate count is supplied for either modality ('not supplied in workbook'), so effect-size precision cannot be assessed; protein-spot p-values are nominal and the 'reported_significant' flag is inconsistent with p-value in several spots.", "Direction of causality between the lipid-uptake program and the lysosomal program is assumed, not demonstrated; the reverse (a primary lysosomal defect driving compensatory sterol synthesis) is equally consistent with these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by an uncompensated endolysosomal degradative bottleneck: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases and the TFEB/MITF CLEAR module are selectively elevated above the background of co-selected up-regulated genes, while protein spots whose candidate identities include those same hydrolases show no net increase and instead redistribute bidirectionally, and reduced M6PR transcript together with non-uniform V-ATPase subunit transcripts point to the limiting step being delivery/maturation and luminal acidification of hydrolases downstream of transcription. Causality is not established by these data; the transcriptional program is interpreted as a compensatory response to, not the cause of, reduced degradative flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: In APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia, selectively restoring lysosomal acidification/hydrolase delivery - e.g. re-expressing ATP6V1E1 (or applying an acidic-nanoparticle / V-ATPase-assembly-promoting intervention) or re-expressing M6PR - should normalise the mature:pro cathepsin ratio and restore DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester dequenching flux in APOE4, WITHOUT any further increase in GAA/GBA/CTSB/CTSD transcript. In the same experiment, over-expressing the hydrolases themselves (CTSB + CTSD + GAA) should NOT restore cargo clearance. If hydrolase over-expression alone fully restores clearance while acidification/M6PR rescue does not, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is falsified.", "APOE4 microglia should show measurably higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH by ratiometric probe and lower per-lysosome protease activity than APOE3 under mock conditions, despite equal-or-higher hydrolase transcripts. WEAKENING RESULT: indistinguishable lysosomal pH and per-lysosome DQ-BSA rate between genotypes would weaken the acidification arm and would move the bottleneck to a later step (fusion/reformation) or reject the mechanism.", "Immunoblotting APOE4 versus APOE3 lysates for cathepsin D and cathepsin B should show a shifted pro-form:mature-form ratio (relative accumulation of the single-chain/pro species) rather than a uniform increase or decrease in total protein - this is the specific prediction that explains the bidirectional 2D spot redistribution. WEAKENING RESULT: a uniform, proportional increase in total and mature cathepsin protein matching the transcript increase would refute the transcript-protein discordance that this hypothesis is built on.", "Treating APOE3 microglia with a sub-saturating dose of bafilomycin A1 should phenocopy the APOE4 pattern: hydrolase and TFEB transcript induction together with bidirectional cathepsin spot/isoform redistribution and no net hydrolase protein gain. WEAKENING RESULT: if partial V-ATPase inhibition in APOE3 raises hydrolase protein in proportion to transcript, the inferred link between acidification and the observed discordance fails.", "Because the transcriptional program is claimed to be compensatory rather than causal, TFEB knockdown should worsen cargo (lipid/DQ-BSA) accumulation substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3. WEAKENING RESULT: an equal or larger effect of TFEB knockdown in APOE3 would indicate the CLEAR program is not a genotype-specific compensation.", "Limiting the cargo load - blocking SCARB1/CD36-dependent lipoprotein uptake or inhibiting SOAT1 - should reduce the hydrolase/TFEB transcript elevation in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. WEAKENING RESULT: persistence of the full hydrolase transcript signature after cargo-uptake blockade would indicate a cargo-independent, APOE4-intrinsic transcriptional driver and would remove Step 1 from the chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia up-regulate transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid cargo uptake and esterification (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and for lipogenic/sterol control (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD), which we infer increases the lipid-rich cargo load arriving at late endosomes and lysosomes. Cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A CLEAR-like transcriptional response is engaged - gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are up and luminal acid hydrolase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) sit significantly above the background magnitude of other up-regulated genes in this selected list (median 2.86 vs 1.92, Mann-Whitney p=0.019).", "Step 3 (proposed primary bottleneck; measured protein spots + RNA, inferred activity): The transcriptional program is not converted into increased mature hydrolase protein. Spots whose candidate genes include cathepsins/glycosidases move in both directions with no net gain (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; median of hydrolase-candidate spots equals the all-spot median, p=0.76). We infer a limiting step in acid-hydrolase delivery and pro-enzyme maturation rather than in hydrolase synthesis capacity.", "Step 4 (measured RNA + protein spots, inferred cause of the bottleneck): Two candidate limiters of that step are present - reduced mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript (gene:M6PR, 15th percentile of the list) despite intact M6P tagging and CI-MPR transcripts (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R), and non-uniform V-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H and gene:ATP6V1A high; gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D1 near background) with the only two significantly changed spots carrying a V1 subunit candidate both reduced (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065; bottom 5-8% of all spots). We infer, but did not measure, sub-optimal luminal acidification and reduced TGN-to-endosome hydrolase delivery.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred localization/fusion): Terminal degradative steps are further constrained - gene:STX17 (autophagosome-lysosome fusion SNARE) is down and the AP-5 complex transcripts (gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP5S1) are strongly up while their obligate partners gene:SPG11 and gene:SPART are down, an inferred stoichiometric imbalance in the machinery for late-endosomal recycling and lysosome reformation.", "Step 6 (integrated consequence, inferred): Degradative flux per unit of delivered cargo falls in APOE4, undegraded lipid/protein cargo persists in an enlarged late-endosomal compartment, and the sustained TFEB/hydrolase transcriptional drive observed in Step 2 is the compensatory read-out of that persistent, unresolved cargo signal rather than evidence of restored capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a CLEAR-like lysosomal hydrolase transcriptional program that fails to raise hydrolase protein, indicating a post-transcriptional bottleneck in acid-hydrolase delivery/maturation rather than in hydrolase gene expression"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2162539862935701, "cosine_similarity": 0.41242176579192946, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067346278317152, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2162539862935701, "cosine_similarity": 0.41242176579192946, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067346278317152, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.098939, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 57}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_014", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so pathway statements are made relative to the global median log fold change (+1.46, base unspecified) and not as absolute up/down calls; the logarithm base is left as reported.", "Transcript abundance changes of HK2, PFKP, MPC2, SLC25A1 and SREBF1 are assumed to change the corresponding protein and enzymatic/transport capacity in the same direction; no enzyme activity, metabolite, flux or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry 3-5 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous supporting context only (e.g. spot 038 contains ALDOA/ALDOC/TKT, spot 020 contains ENO1/G6PD/GLUD1, spot 053 contains CTSD); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein.", "Signals are assumed to come from the microglial compartment of the microglia-astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived ambient RNA or astrocyte-supplied lactate/lipid could contribute and is not resolvable here.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript ratios from a probe-based 10X Flex assay are assumed to be only weakly informative and are used as secondary, not primary, evidence.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, so genotype is the design variable, but no causal test (rescue, editing back, inhibitor) is present in the data; causality is not established."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a transcriptional configuration in which glucose is still imported but its committed entry into glycolysis and the oxidative pentose phosphate pathway is restricted (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1 all far below the global RNA shift), while glucose-6-phosphate storage (GYS1, GAA), mitochondrial pyruvate import and PDH activation (MPC2, PDP1), TCA/anaplerotic and shuttle enzymes (OGDH, DLD, ACO2, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1, GLUD1, GLS, SLC1A5), and mitochondrial carrier capacity (SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5) are coordinately elevated; we hypothesise that this carbon-partitioning bottleneck at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase forces APOE4 microglia onto amino-acid/pyruvate-fed TCA metabolism whose four-carbon and citrate output is exported to the cytosol and, together with ACSS2-derived acetyl-CoA, feeds an SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24/DGAT1 lipogenic program that produces the APOE4 lipid burden and the accompanying lysosomal-hydrolase expansion. Measured quantities are RNA and protein-spot abundances only; flux, enzyme activity, metabolite pools, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: parallel U-13C6-glucose and U-13C5-glutamine labelling of APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, lower fractional 13C enrichment of lactate and of glucose-derived M+2 citrate and lower glucose-derived labelling of palmitate/cholesterol, with a compensating increase in the glutamine-derived fraction of citrate and of newly synthesised lipid. If glucose-derived carbon contributes equally or more to lipogenic acetyl-CoA in APOE4, the proposed carbon-partitioning bottleneck is wrong.", "Bottleneck-restoration test: expressing HK2 (or hexokinase-bypassing supplementation such as membrane-permeant pyruvate plus glucose-6-phosphate precursors) in APOE4 microglia should raise ECAR/glycolytic capacity and reduce neutral-lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX) content toward APOE3 levels; unchanged lipid content after restored glycolytic flux would weaken the mechanism.", "Export-step test: inhibition of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) or of ACSS2 should reduce lipid-droplet area and SREBP1 target expression (SCD, DHCR24) preferentially in APOE4 relative to APOE3; an equal or larger effect in APOE3 would weaken step 4-5.", "Bioenergetic test: Seahorse profiling should show APOE4 with lower glycolytic capacity after oligomycin and equal or higher basal OCR but reduced spare respiratory capacity, and APOE4 should be more sensitive to substrate withdrawal of glutamine than of glucose; the opposite sensitivity pattern (greater glucose dependence in APOE4) would falsify step 3.", "Redox test: reduced oxidative PPP flux predicts a lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio and lower 13C1- versus 13C6-glucose CO2 release in APOE4, with increased sensitivity to G6PD inhibition (G6PDi-1) or BSO; unchanged NADPH/NADP+ and no differential G6PD-inhibitor sensitivity would weaken the PPP arm (PGD, TALDO1) of the mechanism.", "Specificity control: the TALDO1-containing 2D spots that increase (e.g. spot 045) should, on targeted immunoblot, be explained by a different candidate (ANXA1/ACTB) rather than by TALDO1 protein; if TALDO1 protein is genuinely increased while its transcript is decreased, the PPP-restriction claim must be revised."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show strongly reduced transcripts for the committed glycolytic steps HK2, HK3 and PFKP and for oxidative/non-oxidative pentose phosphate enzymes PGD and TALDO1, all in the bottom ~20% (HK2, PFKP in the bottom 6%) of a data set whose global median log fold change is +1.46; glucose transporter transcripts SLC2A1 and SLC2A3 are instead above the global median.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): if these abundance changes translate into enzyme capacity, glucose uptake is preserved or increased while hexokinase/PFK-1 capacity becomes limiting, so glucose-6-phosphate flux into lower glycolysis and into NADPH-generating PPP is reduced and glucose carbon is preferentially parked in the glycogen cycle (GYS1, UGP2 up; lysosomal GAA up).", "Step 3 (inferred compensation): reduced cytosolic glycolytic ATP/NADPH is compensated by increased mitochondrial carbon uptake and oxidation capacity - MPC2 and PDP1 (PDH-activating phosphatase) up, TCA and shuttle enzymes OGDH, DLD, ACO2, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1 up, and glutamine/glutamate anaplerosis genes GLS, GLUD1, SLC1A5 up - so the TCA cycle is fed increasingly from glutamate/glutamine and scavenged pyruvate rather than from glycolytic pyruvate.", "Step 4 (inferred flux/localisation): elevated inner-membrane carriers SLC25A1 (citrate/malate) and SLC25A11 (2-oxoglutarate/malate) together with cytosolic MDH1 and GOT1 predict increased net export of citrate and malate to the cytosol rather than complete oxidation; nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts are above the global shift (37 NDUF/COX/ATP5/UQCR genes, median +2.65) whereas four of six mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are below it, which would further favour carbon overflow over terminal oxidation.", "Step 5 (inferred flux): cytosolic citrate plus acetate-derived acetyl-CoA (ACSS2 up) supplies an SREBF1-driven lipogenic and sterol program (SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2 up) and esterification/storage (DGAT1 up), consistent with the lipoprotein-uptake receptor SCARB1 being among the highest RNA increases.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): the resulting neutral-lipid and sterol load raises lysosomal degradative demand, matching coordinated induction of CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1A and TFEB, and the combination of low PPP NADPH with high oxidative load is proposed as the state that makes APOE4 microglia lipid-laden and stress-sensitive even without treatment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia block committed glycolytic entry and route carbon through mitochondrial anaplerosis and citrate export into SREBP1-driven lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17080825610161354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25686216158817016, "cosine_similarity": 0.4123490276087331, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5742912621359223, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17080825610161354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25686216158817016, "cosine_similarity": 0.4123490276087331, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5742912621359223, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0265825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 58}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_095", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1, with an empty band between -1 and +1), so all module statements are enrichment relative to the internal background of that list, not whole-transcriptome inference; 77% of rows are positive and the global mean is 1.39, so an unadjusted 'gene is up' claim carries little information.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is not specified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes up to 15.46 are treated as ordinal ranks, not as fold-change estimates on a known scale.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no flux, no lipid species, no protein for most nodes, and no subcellular localization were measured here.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, direction-level corroboration.", "Key nodes of the proposed circuit were not measured at all in the supplied file (ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, FASN, ACACA, HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, ERN1, HERPUD1, SEC23A/SEC31A/SAR1A), so both the efflux bottleneck and the rejection of the UPR rest on the subset that was measured.", "The comparison is a single isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast at day 30 in astrocyte co-culture with an unstated number of biological replicates; genotype-correlated clonal or co-culture effects cannot be excluded, and no causal experiment is present in these data.", "The direction of causality between lipid load and the lysosomal/TFEB program is assumed (load drives the program); the reverse or a shared upstream driver is equally compatible with cross-sectional abundance data."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the differentiating state is an unbalanced lipid-handling economy: transcripts for lipid influx (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, ABCA7, TREM2), for cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply and SREBF1-linked lipogenic/post-squalene sterol enzymes (SLC25A1, ACSS2, ACAT2, SCD, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1), and for esterification into neutral lipid (AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1) are elevated, while the ER-Golgi/exocytic export module is the only coherent module that is relatively suppressed against a strongly positive global background (mean 0.00 vs global 1.39, permutation p=0.008; 46% negative vs 23% globally). The rate-limiting bottleneck we propose is egress of internalized and newly esterified lipid (lipoprotein-particle secretion and vesicular export), whose inferred shortfall forces lipid into esterified stores and drives a compensatory, coordinated lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (25/25 measured members positive, mean 3.31, permutation p=0.0003). The canonical ER unfolded-protein response is explicitly rejected as the driver: the ER-chaperone/ERAD/N-glycosylation module shows no shift relative to the global background (mean 1.49 vs 1.39, permutation p=0.86), with ERAD members SEL1L, EDEM1 and DERL1 negative. All statements about flux, localization, lipid pools and causal direction are inferred, not measured; no lipid, ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA or HMGCR measurement is present in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic blockade of sterol esterification (SOAT1 inhibition, e.g. avasimibe) or of DGAT1 in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid droplet content and, because the sequestered sterol returns to the ER-accessible pool, should suppress the SREBF1-linked transcripts (SCD, ACSS2, LDLR, INSIG1) and the lysosomal/TFEB transcripts more strongly in APOE4 than in APOE3. If SOAT1/DGAT1 blockade lowers stored ester without any genotype-differential effect on the SREBF1 and lysosomal transcript modules, the proposed influx-to-storage-to-TFEB chain is weakened.", "Egress test: supplying an extracellular lipid acceptor (ApoA-I, HDL, or methyl-beta-cyclodextrin) or increasing efflux capacity (LXR agonism) should normalise APOE4 neutral-lipid storage and blunt the lysosomal hydrolase induction toward APOE3 levels. Failure to normalise despite demonstrated efflux would falsify the export/egress bottleneck and favour a purely biosynthetic or catabolic defect.", "Influx test: SCARB1 knockdown or blocking (with CD36 blockade as a co-test) should reduce APOE4 lysosomal hydrolase transcripts and stored lipid toward APOE3. Persistence of the lysosomal program after uptake blockade would show the program is uptake-independent and would weaken step 1.", "UPR-rejection test (the focus we discard): APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should not differ in ER-stress readouts - BiP/HSPA5 protein, XBP1 splicing, phospho-eIF2alpha and ATF4/CHOP protein - and PERK inhibition, ISRIB or IRE1 inhibition should not normalise APOE4 lipid storage. Observing a clear constitutive UPR difference, or rescue of the lipid phenotype by UPR inhibition, would falsify this hypothesis in favour of an ER-proteostasis mechanism.", "Flux test distinguishing storage from degradation: 13C/2H tracing or fluorescent-lipid pulse-chase should show, in APOE4 relative to APOE3, greater incorporation of label into esterified/droplet pools and slower clearance of internalised lipid into the medium, with lysosomal hydrolase activity per cell equal or higher (compensatory) rather than lower. If APOE4 shows reduced lysosomal hydrolase activity despite elevated hydrolase transcripts, the primary bottleneck should be reassigned from egress to lysosomal catabolism.", "Coherence test on the export module: proteomic or imaging assessment should show reduced ApoE-lipoprotein particle secretion per cell in APOE4 and unchanged or reduced Golgi/exocytic machinery, matching the relatively suppressed export transcript module. Equal or increased ApoE particle secretion in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck assignment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry elevated transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake receptors, most strikingly SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, rank 19 of 2212) with CD36, LDLR, ABCA7 and TREM2 also positive; we infer, but do not measure, a higher rate of sterol- and phospholipid-rich cargo internalisation into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): Simultaneously the carbon-supply and lipogenic arm is elevated - SLC25A1 (citrate export), ACSS2, ACAT2, ME1, SREBF1, SCD, and the post-squalene sterol enzymes LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP - so de novo lipid synthesis is inferred to continue rather than be feedback-suppressed while uptake is high; the SREBP target INSIG1 is itself elevated, consistent with an SREBP program that remains ON.", "Step 3 (bottleneck; measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux and localization): The ER-Golgi/SNARE/exocyst export module is relatively suppressed against the up-shifted background (GOLPH3L rank 2211, TRAPPC6B, TRAPPC8, STX16, BET1L, GOSR1, EXOC6, SEC24D, VAMP2 all negative), and APOE transcript rises only modestly (gene:APOE, +1.24, rank 1364 of 2212). We infer that ApoE-lipoprotein-mediated and vesicular lipid egress does not scale with the increased influx and synthesis, making disposal the rate-limiting step.", "Step 4 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred pool): Lipid that cannot leave is inferred to be committed to esterified, storage-competent forms by ER/lipid-droplet acyltransferases whose transcripts are elevated (AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, CERS4); the neutral-lipid pool itself was not measured in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred causal direction): The resulting endolysosomal lipid load is proposed to drive a MiT/TFE-type transcriptional response - TFEB and TFEC are positive and every one of 25 measured lysosomal hydrolase, membrane and v-ATPase genes is positive (GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C), a coherence far above the 77% background up-rate (binomial p = 1.5e-3, permutation p = 3e-4).", "Step 6 (partial compensation; ambiguous protein evidence): Protein-spot data are consistent with only partial hydrolase compensation, since spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins move in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14 and protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38 and protein_spot:067 -1.00); spots are multi-candidate and cannot be assigned to a single protein, so this step is weakly supported and the net degradative capacity is inferred, not established."], "title": "APOE4 microglia divert lipid into esterified storage and a TFEB-type lysosomal program because lipid egress (secretory/export) capacity is not co-induced, not because of an unfolded-protein response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25907395783332715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27252846172322936, "cosine_similarity": 0.41228126048689484, "direction_accuracy": 0.31715210355987056, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875728155339806, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25907395783332715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27252846172322936, "cosine_similarity": 0.41228126048689484, "direction_accuracy": 0.31715210355987056, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875728155339806, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.26628675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 59}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_122", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; protein spots are reported in log2. Effects are therefore compared in rank/direction terms, not as absolute fold changes across modalities.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global upward bias (77.1% positive, median +1.46), so 'up in APOE4' for any single gene is only weakly informative; the hypothesis rests on the joint pattern of several independently high-confidence genes, not on any one direction.", "Genes absent from the file (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, LIPA, PLIN2, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B, NR1H3) are missing, i.e. not selected as differential; they are not measured as unchanged and are not treated as evidence either way.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific sterol enzyme.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/transporter amount; enzyme activity, sterol localization, transport flux and the size of the ER-accessible sterol pool are all inferred and unmeasured here.", "Astrocyte co-culture and medium supply extracellular lipoprotein/cholesterol, so cellular sterol status reflects uptake as well as synthesis; APOE genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "No lipidomic, filipin, cholesteryl-ester or efflux measurement is supplied, so total and compartmental sterol content in this experiment are unknown."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step is delivery of endolysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER regulatory pool: scavenger-uptake and endolysosomal hydrolase/acidification transcripts are coordinately higher while the SREBP-2/SREBP-1 biosynthetic program and the esterification enzymes SOAT1/DGAT1/SCD are simultaneously higher, a combination that is thermodynamically incoherent for a cell with a normally sensed sterol load and is instead predicted if ER-accessible sterol stays low while total cellular sterol is diverted into esterified/lysosomal pools. Causality is not established by these data; the claim is that the APOE4 state is maintained by low ER-accessible sterol, not by low total sterol.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating localization test: in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, an ER/PM-accessible sterol biosensor (e.g. mCherry-D4H) plus filipin should show higher unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1+ compartments and higher cholesteryl-ester/droplet content, but equal or lower ER-accessible sterol. If APOE4 shows equal or higher ER-accessible sterol while SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, LDLR) remain elevated, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and a sterol-independent transcriptional drive should be preferred.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe or Sandoz 58-035) should, in APOE4 specifically, raise ER-accessible sterol, lower cholesteryl ester and droplet load, and reduce SREBF2-target transcripts within 24 h. Failure of ACAT inhibition to lower the SREBP-2 target program in APOE4 weakens the futile-cycle step.", "Mobilizing lysosomal sterol with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or acute delivery of cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool, should suppress the SREBP-2 target program more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3 (larger genotype-by-treatment interaction). Equal suppression in both genotypes weakens the claim that the APOE4 program is driven by a compartment-specific delivery defect.", "The uptake arm should be functionally engaged: APOE4 microglia should internalize more fluorescent LDL/oxLDL or myelin per cell than APOE3, and SCARB1 or CD36 knockdown should reduce lysosomal lipid load and partially normalize SREBP-2 targets. Unchanged or lower uptake in APOE4 would contradict step 1.", "Counter-test on efflux and oxysterol signalling: if ABCA1/ABCG1 transcripts and ApoA1/HDL-acceptor cholesterol efflux are in fact higher in APOE4 (consistent with the elevated gene:CH25H and gene:MYLIP), the 'no compensatory efflux' element of the futile cycle is falsified and the mechanism must be restricted to the lysosome-to-ER delivery step alone.", "Temporal/causal ordering: blocking lipid loading from day 20 (e.g. LXR-independent uptake blockade or lipid-poor medium) should reduce GPNMB/LGALS3/CXCL8 induction in APOE4. If inflammatory transcripts stay elevated while lipid load is normalized, the inferred direction (lipid state upstream of reactive state) is weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_122", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia express higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:SLCO2B1) and for APOE itself (gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), consistent with a lipid-handling microglial state rather than a lipid-starved one.", "Measured: endolysosomal hydrolase, acidification and membrane transcripts are higher (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SMPD1, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB). Inferred, not measured: expanded endolysosomal volume and increased hydrolysis of internalized cholesteryl ester to free sterol inside that compartment.", "Inferred bottleneck: export of that liberated sterol from the limiting membrane of the endolysosome to the ER-accessible regulatory pool is rate-limiting in APOE4; no lipid, sterol-localization or transport-flux measurement is supplied, so this step is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "Measured: the sterol/lipid biosynthetic program that SCAP-INSIG shuts off when ER sterol is high is instead elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1). Inferred: sustained SREBP-2/SREBP-1 processing because ER-accessible sterol remains below the INSIG set point.", "Measured: esterification/storage capacity is higher (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5, gene:FABP3, gene:PPARD). Inferred: sterol that does reach the ER is re-esterified into cholesteryl ester and droplets, which keeps the ER regulatory pool depleted and closes a futile uptake-synthesis-esterification cycle.", "Consequence (inferred): persistent lysosomal and neutral-lipid loading sustains the reactive lipid-associated phenotype accompanying the sterol changes (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:PLA2G7, gene:TGM2, gene:IL18, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3), rather than inflammation being the upstream cause of the sterol program."], "title": "APOE4 microglia bottleneck sterol delivery from an expanded endolysosome to the ER, locking in a SREBP-on, SOAT1-esterifying futile cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2152918805154525, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2425486988103674, "cosine_similarity": 0.412079521573416, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_122", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5648155339805825, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2152918805154525, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2425486988103674, "cosine_similarity": 0.412079521573416, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5648155339805825, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.65422425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 60}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_154", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects use an unspecified logarithm base and are selected differential-expression rows (no observation has |effect| \u003c 1), so they are not an unbiased transcriptome; direction is interpreted relative to the dataset-wide positive shift (median +1.46, 77% of rows positive), not against zero.", "The global positive RNA shift reflects normalisation/composition differences rather than genuine whole-cell transcript amplification; conclusions therefore rest on relative rank within the dataset, not on absolute sign.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, transporter and enzyme capacity; no flux, enzyme activity, phospho-PDH, metabolite, NADPH, mtDNA copy number or assembled-complex measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak concordance/counter-evidence, never as identification of a specific protein pool.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification by probe-based 10X Flex is assumed comparable between genotypes; if MT probe capture or ambient/mitochondrial-content differences drive those six rows, Step 5 fails (background knowledge on Flex chemistry is unverified here).", "Astrocyte co-culture may supply lactate, lipids or glutamine, so measured microglial transcript differences may reflect substrate availability set by the co-culture rather than a cell-autonomous APOE4 program.", "Isogenic labelling is taken at face value; residual clone- or line-specific effects and the absence of stated biological replicate numbers cannot be excluded as an alternative explanation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily at one carbon-routing node: relative to the strong global upward RNA shift in this dataset, transcripts for the committed cytosolic glycolytic kinases (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and for oxidative pentose-phosphate steps (PGD, TALDO1) are lower, while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation (MPC2, PDP1, DLD), TCA enzymes (ACO2, OGDH, IDH3G, IDH3B, MDH1, GOT1), glutamine/amino-acid anaplerosis (GLS, GLUD1, SLC1A5, SLC38A2), citrate export (SLC25A1) and lipogenic effectors (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1) are higher. We hypothesise that APOE4 microglia therefore depend disproportionately on mitochondrial pyruvate/glutamine carbon that is partly diverted as citrate to lipid synthesis rather than fully oxidised, and that this dependence is fragile because mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) fall below the global shift while nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts rise coordinately. Flux, enzyme activity, phospho-PDH status, metabolite pools, mtDNA copy number and assembled-complex levels were not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown will reduce basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption and de novo lipid (neutral lipid droplet) accumulation significantly more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, whereas hexokinase/glycolysis inhibition (2-DG, low dose) will impair APOE3 more than APOE4. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive to MPC inhibition than APOE3, or is the more 2-DG-sensitive genotype, the primary bottleneck is falsified.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing in mock-treated microglia will show higher fractional m+2 citrate/malate labelling and a lower lactate m+3 fraction (lower lactate efflux per glucose consumed) in APOE4; 1,2-13C2-glucose tracing will show a lower oxidative-PPP contribution in APOE4. Equal or higher glycolytic/PPP flux fractions in APOE4 would weaken Steps 1, 2 and 6.", "Blocking citrate export (SLC25A1 inhibitor CTPI-2 or ACLY inhibition) will normalise SCD-dependent lipid-droplet and desaturation-index differences in APOE4 without restoring lactate production; failure to reduce the APOE4 lipid excess would falsify Step 4.", "Mito-nuclear test: APOE4 microglia will show lower mtDNA-encoded transcript and mtDNA copy number per cell and lower assembled complex I/IV/V (BN-PAGE, complex activity) per unit mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOMM20), despite equal or higher nuclear ETC subunit protein. Equal MT transcripts, mtDNA copy number and assembled-complex levels would falsify Step 5 and reduce the mechanism to carbon rerouting alone.", "Substrate-restriction test: in galactose medium (forcing oxidative pyruvate use) APOE4 microglia will show a larger fall in ATP/viability and a larger ISR response than APOE3; in glutamine-free medium APOE4 will lose more spare respiratory capacity. Equivalent genotype responses to both restrictions would weaken Steps 2 and 3.", "Independent quantitative proteomics (not spot-based) will show increased MPC2, ACO2/OGDH/MDH1 and SLC25A1 protein but no proportional increase in mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-CO2, MT-ATP6); if MPC2 and TCA protein are unchanged while transcripts differ, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_154", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): glucose-transporter transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) while the committed, rate-setting glycolytic kinase transcripts are markedly lower against the dataset-wide positive shift (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP). We infer, but did not measure, a reduced cytosolic glycolytic capacity per unit glucose taken up.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred flux): pyruvate handling is routed into the mitochondrion at the MPC-PDH node, with higher gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1 (PDH-activating phosphatase) and gene:DLD (PDH/OGDH E3 subunit). Inferred consequence: a larger fraction of pyruvate is imported and decarboxylated rather than reduced to lactate; PDH phosphorylation state was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): TCA-cycle and anaplerotic transcripts rise together (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:ME1, gene:PCK2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2), consistent with increased carbon load into the cycle from both pyruvate and glutamine/amino acids.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux/localisation): higher gene:SLC25A1 with higher gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR indicates a cytosolic citrate-to-lipid arm; we infer that part of the mitochondrial carbon is exported as citrate for lipogenesis and esterification instead of being fully oxidised, which fits the known APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype (background knowledge, unverified here).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred stoichiometry): nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts are coordinately elevated (36 subunit genes, median +2.64 vs global +1.46; e.g. gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME) together with mitochondrial import/translation transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:HSPA9, gene:TUFM), whereas four of six mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall below the global shift (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2). Inferred: a mito-nuclear subunit imbalance that caps assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V, so the raised nuclear program is compensatory (retrograde) rather than evidence of higher assembled respiratory capacity.", "Step 6 (measured RNA + ambiguous protein, inferred vulnerability): lower gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1 with no significant increase in mitochondrial-candidate protein spots (protein_spot:050, protein_spot:059, protein_spot:074, protein_spot:066) suggests that the reroute is not accompanied by proportionally more mitochondrial protein or more cytosolic NADPH-generating PPP capacity, leaving APOE4 microglia dependent on a mitochondrial carbon route with a limited terminal-oxidation ceiling."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift glucose carbon from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP into MPC2-dependent mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and SLC25A1-citrate export for lipogenesis, with mtDNA-encoded ETC subunits lagging the nuclear ETC program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10665362035225048, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27761723202491845, "cosine_similarity": 0.41150583510213545, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_154", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5820258899676376, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10665362035225048, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27761723202491845, "cosine_similarity": 0.41150583510213545, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5820258899676376, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8044785, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 61}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_025", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 genes have |effect| \u003e 1) from 10X Flex data, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, HSPA5, XBP1, PLIN2, LIPA) means 'not in the supplied list', not 'unchanged'. All enrichment statistics were therefore computed by permutation against the supplied list itself.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified and was preserved; effects are treated as ordered magnitudes, not as fold changes.", "The whole supplied RNA list is shifted positive (77.1% up, mean +1.388). Permutation against this same distribution is assumed to be an adequate control for that shift; if the shift is a normalisation/ambient-RNA artefact that also scales pathway-specifically, the enrichment could be inflated.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; no spot is treated as a specific protein, only as ambiguous, largely non-corroborating evidence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, degradative flux and lipid pools, none of which are measured here.", "gene:TFEB transcript level is used as a proxy for CLEAR-programme output; TFEB is mainly regulated post-translationally, so the inference of pathway activation rests on the coordinate behaviour of its target set rather than on TFEB alone.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be a continuing exogenous source of lipoprotein/lipid cargo; the astrocyte contribution to the measured signal cannot be separated in these data.", "The ER/UPR focus was evaluated and rejected on the data: the 18 measured ER-chaperone/UPR/translocon genes have mean +1.44 versus a +1.388 background (Mann-Whitney p = 0.86), and the ERAD arm is if anything down (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:SEC62 -1.50). ATF6, DDIT3 and MANF are up, so a minor secondary ER component cannot be excluded, but it is not the differentiating mechanism.", "Causality is not established; the direction TFEB-expansion -\u003e compensation (rather than TFEB-expansion -\u003e cause of lipid change) is a hypothesis, and the perturbations below are designed to test that direction."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 primarily at the endolysosomal lipid-degradation step: transcripts for lipid/debris uptake receptors and for essentially the entire CLEAR (TFEB) lysosomal regulon are coordinately elevated, while transcripts for glycerolipid/sterol esterification are also elevated. We propose that internalised lipid cargo delivered to endolysosomes exceeds per-lysosome hydrolytic and egress capacity in APOE4 cells; the CLEAR expansion is a compensatory, incompletely effective response, and the undegraded lipid is diverted into esterified neutral-lipid storage. Degradative flux, lysosomal pH, lipid pools and TFEB nuclear localisation were not measured here, so this is an inferred mechanism and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING (cargo-load dependence): switch both genotypes to lipoprotein-depleted / delipidated medium, or block uptake with combined SCARB1 + CD36 blockade, for 48-72 h and re-measure the CLEAR transcripts (GBA, GAA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, TFEB) by qPCR. If the CLEAR expansion is compensatory and load-driven, the APOE4-minus-APOE3 difference should shrink by at least 50% while genotype is unchanged. If the APOE4 elevation persists (\u003c20% reduction), the bottleneck is not cargo-load-driven and STEP 1-2 are falsified; a cell-autonomous APOE4 -\u003e mTORC1/TFEB mechanism would then be favoured.", "DIRECTIONALITY (compensation vs cause): knock down or knock out TFEB in APOE4 microglia. The mechanism predicts hydrolase transcripts fall AND neutral-lipid/undigested-cargo accumulation gets worse (increased BODIPY-493 area, increased undegraded pHrodo-myelin or DQ-BSA signal). If TFEB loss instead reduces lipid accumulation, the CLEAR programme is a driver rather than a compensation and STEP 3-4 are falsified.", "CAPACITY DEFICIT: measure per-lysosome degradative flux directly (DQ-BSA or BODIPY-sphingomyelin dequenching rate normalised to LAMP1 area) and lysosomal pH (ratiometric LysoSensor/pHluorin). The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows equal or lower normalised degradation rate and equal or higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH despite higher hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts. If APOE4 shows higher normalised degradative flux and a more acidic lumen, STEP 2 and STEP 4 are falsified and the transcript expansion should be read as successful adaptation.", "ESTERIFICATION SHUNT: inhibit DGAT1 (and separately SOAT1) for 24-48 h. The mechanism predicts a genotype-by-drug interaction in which APOE4 cells, deprived of the storage sink, show a larger increase in free ceramide/unesterified cholesterol and in lysosomal-membrane-damage markers (galectin-3 puncta, cathepsin B cytosolic release) than APOE3. Absence of a genotype interaction would falsify STEP 5.", "PROTEIN-LEVEL CHECK: by isoform-resolved western blot, mature (single-chain/heavy-chain) cathepsin B and cathepsin D and LAMP1 should rise in APOE4 far less than the corresponding transcripts, with an increased pro-form to mature-form ratio. If mature hydrolase protein scales proportionally with the transcript increase, STEP 4 (incomplete compensation) is falsified and the model reduces to a simple, effective lysosomal expansion.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL / FOCUS REJECTION: tunicamycin or thapsigargin challenge should induce HSPA5, XBP1 splicing and DDIT3 to a comparable degree in APOE4 and APOE3, and baseline XBP1 splicing and ATF4/CHOP protein should not differ appreciably between genotypes under mock. A clear baseline UPR difference between genotypes would revive the ER-proteostasis alternative and weaken the claim that the endolysosomal step is primary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for scavenger/lipoprotein and apoptotic-debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:STAB1, gene:C1QA). We infer, but did not measure, an increased rate of delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "STEP 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred): luminal hydrolysis and downstream egress of that cargo (sphingolipid, glycosphingolipid and sterol species) becomes rate-limiting relative to the delivered load. This step is a proposed bottleneck; no hydrolytic-flux, lysosomal-pH or lipid measurement is present in the supplied data.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA): the cell responds with a coordinate CLEAR/TFEB-type transcriptional expansion of the lysosome \u2014 gene:TFEB itself plus lipid/glycan hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXB, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2), proteases (gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), and membrane/maturation machinery (gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:PIK3C3, gene:GPNMB, gene:SLC17A5, gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R). TFEB nuclear translocation and mTORC1 status were not measured; TFEB is used only as a transcript-level proxy.", "STEP 4 (inferred insufficiency): the compensation does not restore capacity, because hydrolase maturation/delivery and acidification are not scaled in proportion. Consistent counter-signals in the same dataset are gene:M6PR (-1.72), gene:CTSS (-5.57), gene:IDS (-1.56) and gene:STX17 (-2.06), and protein spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins or a v-ATPase subunit move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down). Spot identities are ambiguous, so this step is the weakest link.", "STEP 5 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred lipid state): lipid that is not catabolised or exported is routed into esterification and neutral-lipid storage, indicated by elevated gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1 and gene:MGLL, together with altered efflux/carrier transcripts gene:ABCA7 and gene:APOE. Triglyceride, cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet abundance were not measured in this dataset.", "STEP 6 (net state): APOE4 microglia therefore sit in a lysosome-expanded, lipid-storing state with reduced degradative reserve per lysosome, rather than in an ER unfolded-protein-response state; the assigned ER/UPR focus was tested and rejected (see assumptions and analysis.md)."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-catabolism bottleneck, not ER proteostatic stress, distinguishes APOE4 microglia: cargo load outruns degradative capacity, driving compensatory TFEB/CLEAR expansion and an esterification shunt"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23488904478824355, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25397724814685924, "cosine_similarity": 0.4105453919654686, "direction_accuracy": 0.2540453074433657, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6181229773462783, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23488904478824355, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25397724814685924, "cosine_similarity": 0.4105453919654686, "direction_accuracy": 0.2540453074433657, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6181229773462783, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.20099125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 62}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_020", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are reported in an unspecified logarithm base and are used only as ranks/relative set contrasts against the list background, not as literal fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.000, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); the positive global mean is treated as a selection/normalisation property, so every pathway claim is made relative to that background rather than against zero.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme and carrier protein amount for the mitochondrial node; no mitochondrial enzyme was unambiguously quantified in the protein data, so this assumption is untested here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level direction is used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Enzyme/carrier capacity is assumed to influence flux; NAD+/NADH ratio, oxygen consumption, lactate output, citrate flux, lipid content and peroxisome number are all unmeasured in the supplied data and are inferred, not observed.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-associated changes in cell composition or ambient RNA could contribute to apparent transcript differences.", "Correlation between the two modalities is essentially absent in the 38 spots with a single DE-list candidate (r = -0.01), so the modalities are treated as independent, partly discordant views."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial pyruvate import, PDH activation, TCA-cycle and malate-aspartate/citrate carrier components (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:NNT) together with nuclear-encoded complex-I subunits, while committed glycolytic steps (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP) are lower; we hypothesise that this makes mitochondrial NADH reoxidation, rather than lactate production, the rate-limiting route for cytosolic NAD+ regeneration in APOE4 cells, lowering glycolytic reserve and biasing carbon toward citrate export and lipid esterification. The peroxisomal and antioxidant/NADPH arms suggested by the assigned focus are not supported and are explicitly rejected. No causal direction is established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or malate-aspartate shuttle inhibition (aminooxyacetate) in isogenic pairs should produce a larger fall in oxygen consumption rate, a smaller compensatory extracellular acidification/lactate increase, and a larger drop in the cytosolic NAD+/NADH ratio (e.g. SoNar/Peredox reporter) in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia; if APOE4 cells compensate at least as well as APOE3 glycolytically, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Uniformly 13C-labelled glucose tracing should show a higher fraction of label in citrate/glutamate and a lower fraction in secreted lactate in APOE4 versus APOE3; higher lactate labelling or unchanged TCA labelling in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Targeted immunoblot or PRM proteomics should show higher MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, GOT1 and SLC25A1 protein in APOE4; unchanged or lower protein for these enzymes (as the ambiguous MDH1-containing protein_spot:050, -0.48, non-significant, already hints) would break the transcript-to-capacity step.", "Growth in galactose instead of glucose (forcing oxidative ATP production) should be better tolerated by APOE4 than APOE3 microglia; equal or worse APOE4 tolerance would weaken the mechanism.", "If the citrate-export limb holds, SLC25A1 or ACLY inhibition should reduce APOE4-specific neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation (BODIPY or lipidomics) without abolishing the APOE4 respiratory phenotype; no change in lipid accumulation would falsify the secondary limb while leaving the primary node intact.", "Rejection test for the assigned focus: if catalase/peroxisome inhibition, PEX5 knockdown, or a redox probe (roGFP2-Orp1, glutathione ratio) reveals a strong APOE4-specific oxidative-stress phenotype with no respiratory or NAD+/NADH difference, the present mechanism should be discarded in favour of a peroxisomal/oxidative-stress mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the whole selected differential-expression list (global mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified-base log units), a mitochondrial carrier/TCA/malate-aspartate set is far above background (n=18, set mean +4.85, permutation p\u003c1e-4), as are nuclear-encoded complex-I subunits (n=21, mean +2.99, p=0.005); this is transcript abundance only.", "Inferred capacity (not measured flux): higher MPC2 and PDP1 transcript levels would raise mitochondrial pyruvate import capacity and the fraction of dephosphorylated, active pyruvate dehydrogenase, moving pyruvate disposal from cytosolic reduction toward matrix oxidation.", "Inferred redox routing: coordinated elevation of the cytosolic and carrier arms of the malate-aspartate shuttle (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A13) plus NNT would make cytosolic NADH reoxidation dependent on shuttle transfer into the matrix and on respiratory chain turnover, instead of on LDH-mediated lactate output (LDHA/LDHB were not in the supplied list, so this arm is unmeasured).", "Measured counterweight: the committed glycolytic steps gene:HK2 (-3.67) and gene:PFKP (-3.08) are lower while glucose-transporter transcripts gene:SLC2A1 and gene:SLC2A3 are higher, so the inferred limiting step in glucose handling sits at hexose phosphorylation/PFK rather than at uptake; APOE4 cells would therefore have little glycolytic headroom to buffer a respiratory block.", "Inferred consequence for carbon fate: elevated gene:SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) alongside the lipogenic/esterification and lipid-uptake transcripts gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36 is compatible with diversion of mitochondrially derived citrate into neutral-lipid synthesis and storage; ACLY was not measured and this lipid arm is not enriched above the list background (permutation p\u003e0.6), so it is offered as a weak, secondary limb.", "Parallel, non-primary: a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program is above background (n=27, mean +3.09, p=0.0007; gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H), which could increase catabolic substrate delivery, but the 2D-gel spots containing cathepsin and v-ATPase candidates are inconsistent in sign (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064 down), so lysosomal hydrolytic capacity is not established.", "Rejected alternative from the assigned focus: peroxisomal genes are indistinguishable from background (gene:SCP2, gene:ACOX1, gene:AMACR, gene:CROT up but gene:ABCD1 down; permutation p=0.91) and the NADPH/antioxidant arm is not coherent (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30; unbiased redox set permutation p=0.84), so peroxisomal beta-oxidation and oxidative-stress defence are not adopted as the bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift cytosolic NAD+ regeneration onto a mitochondrial pyruvate-oxidation/malate-aspartate shuttle node rather than onto peroxisomal or antioxidant defence"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.291504021411193, "cosine_similarity": 0.40986305100052633, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073333333333333, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.291504021411193, "cosine_similarity": 0.40986305100052633, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073333333333333, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71606625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 63}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_045", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are 'reported log fold change' of unspecified logarithm base; all magnitudes are used only on their own reported scale and comparatively (module vs list-wide), never converted to linear fold change.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every adjusted p-value is \u003c0.05), so absence of a gene is uninformative and enrichment can only be assessed relative to the list-wide upward shift (mean +1.39, 77.1% positive), which is what all set statistics here do.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/transporter abundance and hence for oxidative capacity; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, mitochondrial mass, membrane potential and organelle localization were not measured.", "PDP1 up-regulation is assumed to translate into net PDH dephosphorylation/activation, and MPC2 up-regulation into increased functional MPC1/MPC2 heterodimer; MPC1 was not in the supplied list.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 3-6 candidate genes each and no unique protein assignment; spot-level effects are treated as ambiguous and are used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence, never as identified protein abundances.", "The comparison is stated to be isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment; no biological-replicate count is supplied, so the reported p-values may be inflated by pseudoreplication across cells and cannot be used to rank effects (|effect| and -log10 adjusted p are essentially uncorrelated, r = -0.04).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex; residual ambient RNA or differences in microglial maturation-state composition between genotypes could contribute to the shared upward shift and are not excluded.", "No lipidomic, flux, respirometry, imaging or ER-stress-reporter data were supplied; every metabolic-flux and lipid-storage statement is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coherent transcriptional up-shift of the mitochondrial oxidative-catabolism module (mitochondrial pyruvate carrier, PDH activation, TCA-cycle and malate-aspartate shuttle, electron-transport subunits, carriers and import machinery) with concurrent down-shift of proximal glycolytic kinases, accompanied by an expanded endolysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase program and a still-active SREBP-type lipogenic/esterification program. We propose that mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA-cycle carbon oxidation (the MPC2-PDP1-OGDH/MDH1-GOT1 node) is the rate-controlling bottleneck of this APOE4 state, that lysosomal catabolism supplies additional substrate to that sink, and that lipid carbon surplus is diverted into sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification rather than being disposed of; the canonical ER proteostasis/UPR and COPII secretory axes are not coherently engaged and are rejected as the differentiating mechanism. Only steady-state RNA and 2D-gel protein-spot abundances were measured; activity, flux, localization and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in the isogenic pair should produce a significantly larger fractional drop in basal and maximal oxygen consumption rate, and a larger compensatory extracellular-acidification/lactate rise, in APOE4 than in APOE3 (genotype x drug interaction). Absence of a genotype-by-inhibitor interaction, i.e. both genotypes losing the same fraction of respiration, would falsify MPC-gated pyruvate oxidation as the bottleneck.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show higher fractional enrichment of citrate m+2, glutamate m+2 and aspartate m+2 with a lower lactate m+3 fraction in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or reversed enrichment would weaken step 2.", "Independent protein-level assay (immunoblot or targeted MS for NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B, MDH1, citrate-synthase activity, MitoTracker/mtDNA copy number) should show higher mitochondrial content/complex abundance in APOE4. If transcripts are elevated but mitochondrial protein, citrate-synthase activity and mtDNA copy number are unchanged, the RNA module shift is a compositional or normalization artifact and the hypothesis fails.", "Lysosomal arm: v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or pan-cathepsin inhibition should erase more of the APOE4 respiratory advantage than of APOE3 respiration; if the APOE4-APOE3 respiration gap is unchanged, lysosomal substrate supply (step 3) is not feeding the mitochondrial sink and that step must be dropped, even if steps 1-2 survive.", "Lipid arm: APOE4 microglia should contain more BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid droplets and more cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol by lipidomics; SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should selectively reduce APOE4 cholesteryl-ester content and shift free-cholesterol distribution. No genotype difference in neutral-lipid or cholesteryl-ester content would falsify step 4.", "ER/UPR discriminator: APOE4 and APOE3 should not differ under mock treatment in XBP1 splicing, BiP/HSPA5 and GRP94/HSP90B1 protein, phospho-eIF2alpha, or an ATF6-luciferase/ERSE reporter, and both should respond comparably to tunicamycin or thapsigargin. A robust cell-autonomous UPR signature in mock APOE4 (for example constitutive XBP1s and elevated BiP) would overturn the rejection in step 6 and favour an ER-proteostasis mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: within the supplied differential-expression list, nuclear-encoded mitochondrial genes are uniformly higher in APOE4 (43/43 curated members positive; module mean +3.49 vs list-wide mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified-base log units; Mann-Whitney p=3.2e-8 against the rest of the list; label-permutation p\u003c5e-5), spanning TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G), the pyruvate-entry node (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1), carriers (gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:SLC25A1), import/matrix chaperone (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM8B, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9) and ETC/ATP-synthase subunits (gene:UQCRC2, gene:CYCS, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:COX7A2, gene:NDUFB2, gene:SDHB).", "Inferred bottleneck (activity/flux, not measured): increased MPC2 with increased PDP1 (a PDH phosphatase that de-represses pyruvate dehydrogenase) and an up-shifted malate-aspartate shuttle pair (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) makes mitochondrial pyruvate import and NADH oxidation the flux-controlling step in APOE4; the coincident decrease of proximal glycolytic kinases (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3) predicts carbon is routed to mitochondrial oxidation rather than to aerobic glycolysis/lactate.", "Measured: a lysosomal degradative and acidification program is also coordinately higher in APOE4 (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB; 23/24 positive, permutation p=0.001), together with endosome-maturation and cargo-delivery genes (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:DNM2, gene:AP5M1). Inferred: expanded lysosomal hydrolytic capacity delivers amino-acid, sugar and lipid catabolites to the mitochondrial sink defined in step 2 (supported indirectly by gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACSS2).", "Measured: uptake receptors and a sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification program remain elevated in APOE4 despite this catabolic expansion (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7). Inferred: lipid taken up and liberated in lysosomes is not registered as a sufficient sterol/fatty-acid signal at the ER sensing compartment, so synthesis continues and surplus carbon is esterified into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores instead of being fully oxidized.", "Inferred consequence: APOE4 microglia sit at a higher basal oxidative-catabolic set-point with a lipid-storage overflow, which should appear as higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption, greater fractional 13C labelling of TCA intermediates from glucose, and increased neutral-lipid-droplet/cholesteryl-ester content relative to isogenic APOE3, without a cell-autonomous ER stress state.", "Rejection of the ER-proteostasis alternative: the UPR/ERAD/secretory modules are not coherently engaged. Canonical effectors are absent from the selected list (HSPA5, XBP1, ERN1, ATF4, HERPUD1, CALR, CANX, P4HB), the present members are internally contradictory (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3 and gene:MANF up, but gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1 and gene:PDIA3 down; module mean not separable from the list-wide shift), early-secretory genes are flat to down (gene:GOSR1, gene:SEC24D), and the three 2D-gel spots whose candidate list contains the ER chaperone HSP90B1/GRP94 are non-significant and negative on average (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004). We therefore do not adopt the assigned ER/UPR focus."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are set in a mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA-oxidative catabolic state, not an ER unfolded-protein-response state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25207694863936786, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2927829830982553, "cosine_similarity": 0.40963993068891486, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885695792880259, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25207694863936786, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2927829830982553, "cosine_similarity": 0.40963993068891486, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885695792880259, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4743405, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 64}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_056", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2, and every canonical type-I ISG) means unmeasured/unreported here, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only sign and relative rank within this dataset are used, not absolute fold changes. Effect magnitude is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p-value (Spearman rho = -0.03), so very large |effects| are treated as unreliable in magnitude.", "The dataset has a strong global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 RNA rows positive, median +1.46), so every pathway claim is judged against that background by permutation rather than against zero. This shift may itself be technical (selection, normalization or compositional) rather than a true genome-wide induction.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each and frequent keratin/actin co-candidates; no spot uniquely identifies a protein, and spot-level abundance is not evidence for a named gene product.", "Increased hydrolase and V-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to reflect increased lysosomal biogenesis, but enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, proteolytic flux and lipid content were not measured.", "The ER sterol-feedback logic used in STEP 3 (ER-accessible cholesterol represses SREBP-2 targets) is background knowledge, unverified against any supplied measurement.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; differences in culture composition, differentiation efficiency or astrocyte-derived lipoproteins between APOE3 and APOE4 wells could produce the same RNA pattern without any cell-autonomous lysosomal defect. Biological replicate number is not supplied.", "Comparison is APOE4 versus APOE3 at a single timepoint under mock treatment; no time course, no dose, no intervention, so no causal direction can be assigned."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily through a lipid-handling bottleneck at the endolysosome: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake are strongly elevated while the ER-sterol-responsive SREBP target program remains induced rather than repressed, a combination best explained by cholesterol and sphingolipid being retained in a lysosomal/storage pool that the ER sterol sensor does not see; the cell compensates by inducing a coherent TFEB-CLEAR lysosomal-hydrolase program and esterification enzymes, and only secondarily emits a modest NF-kB-type chemokine and inflammasome-priming signature. The assigned interferon/inflammatory focus is rejected as the primary mechanism: no canonical type-I ISG appears among the selected differential RNA rows, STAT5A/STAT5B/STAT6/IRF2 are decreased, and the inflammatory gene set is not enriched above the strong global positive shift of this dataset (permutation p = 0.52), whereas the lysosomal-hydrolase set is (p = 0.0015). Causality is not established; all statements about flux, localization and activity are inferences from RNA and multi-candidate protein spots.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: relieving lysosomal cholesterol egress in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1 over-expression) should, within 24-48 h, repress the SREBP target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR, ACAT2) and reduce the TFEB-CLEAR transcripts (ATP6V subunits, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA/HEXB, GBA, LAMP1) toward APOE3 levels, with little effect in APOE3 cells. If cyclodextrin demonstrably lowers lysosomal unesterified cholesterol yet leaves the SREBP and CLEAR programs elevated in APOE4, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and TFEB/SREBP activation must be driven upstream of lipid retention.", "Direct lipid measurement (filipin, LipidSpot/BODIPY, or LC-MS sterol and hexosylceramide quantification, with LAMP1 co-localization) should show more unesterified cholesterol and more cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid droplets per cell in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Comparable or lower neutral-lipid and lysosomal sterol content in APOE4 would falsify the central inference of STEP 2-3.", "INTERFERON TEST (falsifies the assigned focus if it fails): JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal/lipid transcript difference essentially intact, and IFN-stimulated transcripts (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1) should not differ by genotype at the protein or RNA level. If JAK inhibition collapses the APOE4 lysosomal-lipid signature, or if ISGs are genotype-elevated when measured, this hypothesis should be replaced by an interferon-driven one.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe) should convert the storage pool from esterified to free cholesterol and therefore worsen, not improve, the lysosomal-hydrolase and chemokine transcripts specifically in APOE4. Equal or reduced induction in APOE4 versus APOE3 would argue against esterification acting as an overflow valve downstream of the bottleneck.", "Functional flux assays (DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin B activity, LysoSensor pH) should show that APOE4 lysosomes are more numerous or larger yet have equal or lower per-lysosome degradative flux. If per-cell degradative flux is proportionally increased with the transcript program, the 'insufficient clearance' inference in STEP 4 fails and the phenotype is better described as adaptive lysosomal expansion without a bottleneck.", "ANXA1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should selectively de-repress the chemokine/inflammasome-priming module (CXCL8, CXCL1/2/3, CCL2, IL18) without changing the SREBP or CLEAR transcripts. No change in chemokine output would eliminate the ANXA1 brake in STEP 6 while leaving STEPS 1-4 standing.", "STATISTICAL FALSIFIER: if the lysosomal-hydrolase and lipid gene sets lose enrichment when re-tested against an expression-matched, detection-matched background in the full unbiased transcriptome (i.e. their apparent enrichment is an artefact of the 77% upward selection bias of these rows), the transcriptional support for this mechanism collapses."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher RNA for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors and for APOE itself (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12). INFERRED, not measured: increased delivery of cholesterol and phospholipid cargo into the endolysosomal compartment; no lipid, uptake-assay or localization measurement is supplied.", "STEP 2 (primary bottleneck; inferred): export of unesterified cholesterol and sphingolipid catabolites from the lysosomal lumen to the ER/plasma membrane is rate-limiting relative to this influx. This is an inference, not an observation: NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied selected-DE rows, so their direction is unknown, and only gene:NPC2 is present (modest increase).", "STEP 3 (measured abundance, inferred sensing): despite raised uptake, the ER sterol-sensing output stays ON - gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1 and gene:LDLR are all increased. Under the standard sterol-feedback model (unverified background knowledge) an ER-accessible cholesterol excess should repress these; their persistence is the key discriminating inference that the lipid pool is sequestered rather than bioavailable, and it creates a feed-forward loop back to STEP 1.", "STEP 4 (measured abundance): overflow is routed to esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and a coherent TFEB-CLEAR lysosomal-biogenesis program is induced - gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, with hydrolases gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH. INFERRED: this is compensatory expansion of lysosomal capacity, and degradative flux nevertheless remains insufficient; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and cathepsin maturation were not measured, and gene:CTSS is strongly decreased, so the program is not uniform.", "STEP 5 (measured abundance, inferred licensing): the lipid-laden lysosomal state licenses a limited innate output - chemokines gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, and inflammasome priming gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:IL18, gene:TLR2, gene:CD14, gene:MYD88, gene:TICAM1 - together with disease-associated markers gene:TREM2, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX. INFERRED: this is a downstream consequence of lipid/lysosomal stress, not an interferon-driven program; caspase-1 cleavage, IL-1beta/IL-18 protein and secretion were not measured, and this gene set is NOT enriched above the dataset-wide upward shift.", "STEP 6 (measured abundance, counter-regulation): ANXA1 RNA is strongly increased (gene:ANXA1) and the four largest significant up-shifted protein spots all list ANXA1 among their candidates (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046). INFERRED: an ANXA1-dependent brake restrains the inflammatory arm, keeping the APOE4 phenotype lipid-storage-dominant rather than interferon/cytokine-dominant. The spots are multi-candidate and TALDO1, a co-candidate in three of them, moves the opposite way at RNA level (gene:TALDO1), so the protein identity is unresolved."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal lipid egress, not by interferon signalling: sequestered sterol keeps the SREBP program on and drives a TFEB-CLEAR expansion with only a weak chemokine output"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19431671220092364, "cosine_similarity": 0.409254753340301, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073689320388349, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19431671220092364, "cosine_similarity": 0.409254753340301, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073689320388349, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.70276125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 65}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_100", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1 and every adjusted p is \u003c0.05), so absence of a gene means not selected, not unchanged; all enrichment statements are made within the list against its own strongly up-shifted background (list median +1.46, 77% positive), not against a whole transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effects such as +15.46 are treated as rank/direction information, not as literal fold changes.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence that a named protein changed.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; hydrolytic flux, luminal pH, TFEB/SREBP nuclear localization, lysosomal lipid content and lipid species were not measured in these data.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; some transcript signal could reflect ambient RNA or subtle composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells rather than cell-intrinsic regulation.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be checked for pseudoreplication across cells.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment; no perturbation was applied, so no causal direction is established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by an endolysosomal lipid-handling imbalance: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, acid hydrolases (especially glycosphingolipid- and sphingomyelin-degrading enzymes) and v-ATPase subunits are coordinately higher, whereas transcripts serving post-hydrolytic sterol/lipid export and hydrolase-receptor recycling are not (NPC2 below the list median; M6PR and OSBPL8 lower). We propose the rate-limiting step is export/recycling of hydrolysis products out of the lysosome rather than hydrolysis itself, so lipid is inferred to be retained in the lumen, sustaining a TFEB/MITF-like degradative program and an unsatisfied SREBP-1 lipogenic program in parallel. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are steady-state selected differential abundances, not flux, activity, localization or lipid content.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test of the export bottleneck: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or restoring NPC1/NPC2 or activating ABCA1/ABCG1 with an LXR agonist) should lower lysosomal free-cholesterol/filipin and neutral-lipid staining AND bring the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (e.g. GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H) and the SREBP-1 targets (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels. If lysosomal sterol is normalized but these transcripts remain elevated, the export-limited mechanism is weakened and an APOE4-intrinsic TFEB/MITF drive becomes the better explanation.", "Capacity versus bottleneck: pharmacologic TFEB activation (mTORC1 inhibition or TFEB overexpression) should further raise hydrolase transcripts yet fail to clear lysosomal lipid in APOE4, whereas it should be neutral or mildly clearing in APOE3. Efficient lipid clearance by TFEB activation in APOE4 would falsify the claim that export rather than degradative capacity is rate-limiting.", "Flux prediction: in a pulse-chase with labelled LDL cholesteryl ester or BODIPY-sphingomyelin, APOE4 should show hydrolysis rates equal to or above APOE3 but delayed appearance of label in the ER/plasma-membrane pool (e.g. delayed SOAT1-dependent re-esterification). Equal or faster ER delivery kinetics in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck placement.", "Sensitization prediction: partial inhibition of GBA (conduritol B epoxide) or of acid sphingomyelinase should produce a disproportionately larger increase in lysosomal lipid storage and in CLEAR-gene transcripts in APOE4 than in APOE3, because the system is proposed to be operating near capacity. Equal sensitivity in both genotypes weakens the mechanism.", "Protein-level prediction and current counter-evidence: targeted immunoblot/immunofluorescence should show increased mature cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein and increased LAMP1-positive compartment area in APOE4. The supplied spot data are discordant with this (protein_spot:069 -1.38 and protein_spot:058 -0.85 contain CTSD/CTSB among candidates; protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93 contain ATP6V1E1), so if uniquely identified protein measurements confirm no increase or a decrease in mature hydrolase and v-ATPase protein, step 3 and hence the compensatory-capacity arm of the mechanism is falsified.", "Negative prediction for the assigned focus: if the difference were driven by peroxisomal/oxidative-stress imbalance, an NRF2 activator or peroxisomal beta-oxidation rescue should normalize the APOE4 transcriptional state; we predict it will not, and that catalase/ACOX1/ABCD1-dependent readouts will not differ consistently between genotypes."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer increases delivery of cholesteryl-ester- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosome. Cargo flux and lipid content were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Transcripts of the lysosomal biogenesis transcription factors are higher (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03). We infer increased TFEB/MITF transcriptional output; nuclear localization, phosphorylation state and mTORC1 status were not measured, and no mTORC1/Ragulator transcripts are present in the supplied list.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, statistically above the list background): A coherent acid-hydrolase module is elevated (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:CTSH +1.54, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:SGSH +1.32; set median +2.52 vs list median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.004, median-permutation p=0.033), together with every measured v-ATPase/ion subunit (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.29, gene:ATP6AP2 +1.18, gene:CLCN7 +1.06; 10/10 higher). We infer, but did not measure, greater hydrolytic capacity and lower luminal pH.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck; partly measured, partly missing): The export/recycling arm is not co-induced. gene:NPC2 (+1.17) and gene:SCARB2 (+1.06) sit below the list median, gene:OSBPL8 is -1.90 and gene:M6PR is -1.72 despite gene:IGF2R +2.02 and gene:GNPTG +3.02. NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, STARD3, PSAP and GRN are absent from the supplied selected list and are therefore unmeasured here. We infer that free cholesterol and sphingoid/hexosamine products leave the lumen more slowly than they are generated, making egress the bottleneck.", "Step 5 (inferred signalling consequence): Because the retained pool is inferred not to reach ER sterol sensors, the anabolic program stays on (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06), producing a futile cycle in which newly made and newly taken-up lipid re-enters an already loaded compartment.", "Step 6 (state, not proven cause): The resulting export-limited, lipid-loaded endolysosomal state is proposed to be the basal APOE4/APOE3 difference from which secondary changes follow, including selective chemokine transcripts (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12) and mitochondrial/redox transcripts (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:NNT +2.88), neither of which forms a set enriched above the strongly up-shifted list background."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand endolysosomal hydrolase/acidification capacity while lipid egress lags, creating an export-limited lysosomal lipid-handling state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.46975039692796217, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17673329804126145, "cosine_similarity": 0.40900214388237255, "direction_accuracy": 0.5728155339805825, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mean_absolute_error": 0.553873786407767, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.46975039692796217, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17673329804126145, "cosine_similarity": 0.40900214388237255, "direction_accuracy": 0.5728155339805825, "mean_absolute_error": 0.553873786407767, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03173525, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 66}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_045", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 genes, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program coherence is judged against that 77%-up background, and absent genes (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, GRN, PLIN2, HMGCR) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Program membership was assigned a priori by canonical pathway annotation (name/regex matching of standard CLEAR, SREBP, uptake, esterification, endosomal, OXPHOS and UPR gene families) before directions were inspected; discordant members were retained and reported.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for hydrolase activity, cholesterol egress rate, lipid flux, lipid-droplet content or subcellular localization, none of which were measured here.", "The SREBP-target elevation is interpreted through the standard sterol-feedback rule (ER-accessible sterol suppresses SREBP-2 output); this interpretive rule is unverified background knowledge, and an alternative cause of SREBP-target elevation (e.g. increased lipid demand for membrane expansion) is not excluded.", "2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each and are dominated by keratin/actin contaminants; spot-level changes are treated as compatibility tests only, never as identification of a specific protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein/lipid substrate; the APOE4 vs APOE3 difference is assumed cell-intrinsic to microglia, although the supplied data cannot exclude an astrocyte-mediated indirect effect.", "Any degradative insufficiency is framed as reduced reserve that would be revealed by a future lipid-loading challenge; it is not asserted as an ongoing defect in the measured mock condition."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated day-30 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 not by an unfolded-protein response but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors, MiT/TFE transcription factors and their CLEAR lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase targets, endosomal sorting machinery, and lipid esterification enzymes are higher in APOE4, while SREBP transcription factors and every represented SREBP target are also higher (11/11 up). Because ER-accessible sterol normally suppresses SREBP targets, the simultaneous elevation of uptake and of SREBP output is most consistent with sterol/lipid being routed into lysosomal and esterified/neutral-lipid stores rather than into the ER regulatory pool, with lysosomal catabolic capacity expanded (measured as transcript abundance) but the corresponding flux unmeasured. This is a routing/cell-state claim, not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-routing test: after acute lipoprotein or myelin-lipid loading, APOE3 microglia should suppress SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) and increase ACAT/SOAT-dependent cholesteryl-ester formation from the loaded label, whereas APOE4 microglia should suppress them less and esterify a smaller fraction of exogenous label; equal suppression and equal label esterification in both genotypes would falsify the routing step.", "Prospective bypass test: delivering cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool (cyclodextrin-cholesterol) or adding 25-hydroxycholesterol should suppress SREBP targets equally in both genotypes; if APOE4 still fails to suppress, the defect lies in ER sterol sensing rather than in lysosome-to-ER routing, weakening this mechanism.", "Prospective MiT/TFE dependence test: TFEB/MITF knockdown or MiT/TFE inhibition should collapse the CLEAR hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation and disproportionately increase lysosomal and neutral-lipid accumulation in APOE4; if hydrolase transcripts stay elevated after TFEB/MITF loss, step 2 is wrong.", "Prospective imaging/biochemistry prediction in the unchallenged mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show greater LAMP1-positive compartment volume, more filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol and higher cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol content than isogenic APOE3; equal lysosomal volume and equal neutral-lipid content would substantially weaken the cell-state claim even if transcripts differ.", "Prospective flux discrimination (adaptation vs failed compensation): measuring bulk lysosomal hydrolase activity and degradation of a fluorogenic lipid substrate should show APOE4 activity equal to or above APOE3 at baseline but a smaller further increase after loading; if APOE4 baseline activity is markedly below APOE3, the mechanism should be restated as an ongoing hydrolase bottleneck rather than altered routing with expanded capacity.", "Negative prediction for the rejected focus: ER-stress reporters and UPR outputs (XBP1 splicing, HSPA5/GRP78 protein, ATF4/CHOP protein) should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock treatment; a clear constitutive UPR difference would favour an ER-proteostasis mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling receptors than isogenic APOE3 microglia (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:PLTP +1.06; reported log fold change, base unspecified), which we infer - but did not measure - increases delivery of astrocyte- and medium-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Increased endolysosomal lipid/membrane cargo is accompanied by higher MiT/TFE transcription factor transcripts (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) and by coordinated induction of their CLEAR-network targets: acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:SUMF1 +2.01) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68), i.e. expanded lysosomal biogenesis capacity (28/30 represented members up vs a 77% up selected-list background; exceptions gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:M6PR -1.72).", "Endosome-to-lysosome delivery and retrieval machinery is concurrently elevated (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:VPS18 +1.41, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:SNX15 +3.02, gene:SNX16 +2.86, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:IGF2R +2.02), consistent with an enlarged and actively sorted endolysosomal compartment rather than a stalled early-endosome block.", "Despite this expanded catabolic program, the ER sterol sensor behaves as if under-supplied: SREBP factors and all represented targets are higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SCD +4.17; 11/11 up, none down). We interpret this as continued biosynthetic drive because lysosome-derived sterol does not reach the ER regulatory pool, not as proven increased sterol synthesis flux.", "Lipid is instead directed into esterified/neutral and remodelled membrane lipid pools: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:SCD +4.17, together with sterol-transfer/storage-associated transcripts (gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:TSPO +1.41, gene:OSBPL1A +1.03).", "The same cells raise mitochondrial substrate-import and carrier transcripts that would support acyl-CoA oxidation and cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate export for lipogenesis (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:MPC2 +8.03, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.62, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55), linking the lipid-storage state to a broader anabolic/oxidative-support program.", "Net predicted phenotype in the measured mock condition: APOE4 microglia carry a larger lysosomal/esterified lipid store and a persistently de-repressed sterol program relative to APOE3, i.e. altered lipid routing plus expanded degradative machinery, with degradative sufficiency under a future lipid-loading challenge unresolved by these data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a MiT/TFE-driven endolysosomal lipid-storage state in which lipid is routed to lysosomal and esterified pools instead of resupplying the ER sterol-sensing pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.264944799320607, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2655686945590463, "cosine_similarity": 0.4088815741091462, "direction_accuracy": 0.3284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5818155339805825, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.264944799320607, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2655686945590463, "cosine_similarity": 0.4088815741091462, "direction_accuracy": 0.3284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5818155339805825, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.11337775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 14}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_082", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base; they are used only ordinally and for direction, never converted to a linear fold change.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00, 77% positive, median +1.46), so absence of a gene (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2, TYROBP) is uninformative and cannot be read as unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein amount, and protein amount a partial proxy for enzymatic activity, transport flux and subcellular localisation; none of activity, flux, localisation or lipid mass was measured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D features; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and no protein-level confirmation of the lysosomal or sterol program is claimed.", "The inferred ER-accessible cholesterol pool, lysosomal free-cholesterol pool, cholesteryl-ester mass and lipid-droplet content are unmeasured in the supplied data and are inferences, not observations.", "Module-level coherence is judged against the strongly up-shifted background of this list rather than against zero; enrichment above that background is required before a module is called specific.", "The astrocyte co-culture means genotype-linked transcript differences could partly reflect altered microglia-astrocyte cross-talk or ambient RNA rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 biology; replicate structure was not supplied."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step is delivery of lysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER sterol-sensing pool, not sterol synthesis or sterol sensing per se: APOE4 cells transcriptionally scale up lipoprotein/lipid cargo capture (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, MERTK) and a TFEB-associated degradative-compartment program (v-ATPase subunits, glycosidases, cathepsins, endosomal sorting factors), yet the SREBP-2 target program (SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2) remains elevated rather than repressed, which is the signature expected if catabolised sterol is retained in lysosomal and esterified pools (SOAT1, DGAT1 up) while liberated acyl chains are disposed of oxidatively (nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts up, HK2 and PFKP down). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating localisation test: quantitative imaging of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased unesterified cholesterol inside LAMP1-positive compartments (filipin or a lysosome-targeted sterol probe) and increased cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid mass, while an ER/plasma-membrane accessible-cholesterol probe (e.g. ALOD4/D4H) shows no increase. If APOE4 instead shows a higher ER-accessible sterol pool while SREBP-2 targets stay elevated, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the elevated SREBP-2 transcripts must be explained by sensor-independent transcription.", "Bypass perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol retention with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or sterol delivered directly to the ER pool) should normalise the APOE4 SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR7, DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels and blunt the TFEB-associated hydrolase and v-ATPase program, with little effect in APOE3. Failure of SREBP-2 targets to fall in APOE4 after cyclodextrin would weaken the mechanism.", "Influx perturbation: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade in APOE4 microglia should reduce lipid-cargo uptake and lower the endolysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program and the SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification arm without lowering it in APOE3. If SCARB1 loss leaves the lysosomal program intact, the influx-driven step is falsified even if the retention step survives.", "Specificity control that discriminates from a generic biogenesis explanation: TFEB knockdown should shrink the hydrolase/v-ATPase program but should NOT normalise the SREBP-2 target transcripts if the primary lesion is sterol distribution; if TFEB knockdown fully normalises SREBP-2 targets, the mechanism is better described as TFEB-driven lysosomal biogenesis with secondary sterol effects.", "Direct flux test: pulse-chase of lipoprotein-derived [13C]- or [2H]-cholesterol should show slower appearance of label in the ER/esterified regulatory pool and slower medium efflux in APOE4 than APOE3, with comparable or greater initial uptake. Equal or faster lysosome-to-ER label transfer in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Counter-test of the disposal arm: if the OXPHOS/TCA transcript elevation is a consequence of lysosome-derived fatty-acid load, then blocking lysosomal acid lipase or fatty-acid oxidation should reduce oxygen-consumption differences between genotypes; unchanged genotype difference in respiration under that block would show the metabolic arm is independent of the lysosomal step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance; flux inferred): APOE4 microglia carry markedly higher SCARB1 transcript (effect 8.22, top ~1% of the supplied list) together with CD36, TREM2 and MERTK, which we interpret as increased capacity for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo capture; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured abundance; compartment size inferred): A coordinated degradative-compartment program is higher in APOE4 - TFEB and MITF transcripts, ten v-ATPase subunits (all up), lumenal glycohydrolases (GAA, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, SMPD1) and cathepsins B/D/K, plus LAMP1, SCARB2 and NPC2 - consistent with, but not proof of, an expanded and more acidified/hydrolytic endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 3 (measured abundance; sorting activity inferred): Endosomal sorting and maturation transcripts rise in parallel (RAB7A, PIK3C3, VPS26A, SNX3), indicating remodelling of the sorting machinery that positions cargo for degradation rather than recycling; the dedicated lysosomal sterol-export machinery (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) is absent from this selected differential-expression list, so the export arm is untested and is the inferred bottleneck.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; inferred): Because lysosome-to-ER sterol delivery does not scale with the increased influx and hydrolytic capacity, the ER-accessible cholesterol pool is not raised in APOE4; the SCAP/INSIG sensor therefore continues to permit SREBP-2 output, so SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP and ACAT2 all remain higher in APOE4 instead of being repressed as increased sterol delivery would predict.", "Step 5 (measured abundance; storage flux inferred): Sterol and diacylglycerol esterification transcripts (SOAT1, DGAT1) and MGLL are higher in APOE4, consistent with routing of unesterified sterol and acyl chains into neutral-lipid storage rather than into the regulatory ER pool or export.", "Step 6 (measured abundance; oxidative flux inferred): Acyl chains liberated by lysosomal lipid catabolism are plausibly disposed of oxidatively - nuclear OXPHOS transcripts (38/38 measured up, e.g. NDUFA5) and TCA/pyruvate-import transcripts (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2) are up while glycolytic HK2 and PFKP are down - yielding a lysosome-centred, oxidation-biased lipid-handling state in APOE4."], "title": "Lysosome-retained sterol: APOE4 microglia expand endolysosomal lipid catabolism but fail to raise the ER-accessible sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28240962965698035, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2766211186574447, "cosine_similarity": 0.4086553181614065, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875533980582525, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28240962965698035, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2766211186574447, "cosine_similarity": 0.4086553181614065, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875533980582525, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.41763625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 67}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_017", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (no |effect| below 1 is present and 77% are positive), so all statements are relative to that biased, globally up-shifted background rather than to an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the reported effects is not specified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme and transporter capacity; hydrolase activity, luminal pH, SREBP processing, lipid flux, lipid localization and lipid-droplet content were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a specific protein measurement.", "The absence of NPC1, PSAP, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2 and ASAH1 from the supplied rows is assumed to reflect the selection of the row list rather than proven absence of regulation, so the egress-versus-hydrolase mismatch rests on the measured subset (NPC2, SCARB2, CLN3) only.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype rather than differentiation batch or astrocyte co-culture composition is assumed to be the dominant source of the contrast; biological replicate number is not supplied."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 primarily by an endolysosomal lipid-handling bottleneck: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and for lysosomal acidification and acid hydrolases (including sphingolipid hydrolases) are coordinately elevated well above the strong global positive RNA shift, whereas transcripts for the lysosomal sterol/lipid egress and hand-off module are not, and an SREBP-associated de novo lipogenic and acyl-remodeling program remains high; we propose that lipid delivered to the lysosome is inefficiently exported to the ER regulatory pool, so APOE4 microglia continue to synthesize and esterify lipid while lysosomal sphingolipid substrates accumulate. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: bypass the lysosome. Delivering sterol directly to the ER sensor pool with 25-hydroxycholesterol (or an oxysterol/statin-plus-mevalonate clamp) should suppress SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24 and LDLR to the same low level in APOE4 and APOE3 microglia, whereas supplying the same sterol only as lysosome-routed acetylated LDL should fail to suppress this program in APOE4 while suppressing it in APOE3. If APOE4 cells suppress SREBP targets normally after lysosome-routed lipoprotein loading, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Phenocopy test: acute NPC1 blockade (U18666A) in APOE3 microglia should shift their transcript and lipid profile toward the APOE4 pattern (higher SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1, higher lysosomal hydrolase transcripts, lysosomal cholesterol and sphingolipid accumulation) and should produce a smaller incremental change in APOE4 cells. Equal or larger incremental effects in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Lipidome prediction: quantitative lipidomics on the same cultures should show, in APOE4, increased lysosome-derived sphingolipid substrates (sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, GM-series gangliosides) and increased cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol with a shift toward monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) acyl chains in PC/PE and TAG. A lipidome with unchanged or reduced sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide and unchanged CE/TAG in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Trafficking prediction: pulse-chase with labelled lipoprotein or labelled apoptotic-cell membrane should show prolonged retention of label in LAMP1-positive compartments and delayed appearance in the ER/lipid-droplet pool in APOE4 relative to APOE3. Equal or faster egress kinetics in APOE4 would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Directionality test: TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program in APOE4 without relieving, and probably worsening, lysosomal lipid retention and the SREBP-target elevation, indicating the lysosomal program is compensatory. If TFEB knockdown normalizes SREBF1/SCD and lysosomal lipid load, the lysosomal program is causal upstream rather than compensatory and this mechanism ordering is wrong.", "Counter-evidence already present that must resolve: protein spots containing lysosomal candidate genes average +0.01 log2 versus +0.42 for other spots, and spot 067 (candidates including CTSB and HEXB) and spot 064 (candidates including ATP6V1E1) are decreased. Targeted, unambiguous measurement (immunoblot or activity assay) of CTSB, HEXB, GBA and v-ATPase in APOE4 versus APOE3 should show increased protein and activity; a confirmed decrease would weaken step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Elevated transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein and phagocytic receptors, led by SCARB1 (+8.22, 99th percentile of the measured RNA rows) with smaller increases in CD36, LDLR, MERTK, TREM2 and C1QA/B/C, are interpreted as increased delivery of extracellular and membrane-derived lipid into the APOE4 endolysosomal system. Uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A coherent lysosome-biogenesis-like program is elevated above the already up-shifted background (TFEB +2.38; ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51; CTSK +7.36, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86; NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, HEXB +2.17, GBA +6.71, GBA2 +2.63, SMPD1 +5.63, GLA +1.53; set mean +4.3 versus dataset mean +1.39). This is read as expanded acidification and hydrolase capacity, not as a demonstrated increase in hydrolase activity.", "Step 3 (measured RNA contrast, inferred bottleneck): Genes serving lysosomal lipid egress and hand-off are conspicuously not scaled with the hydrolase program (NPC2 +1.17, 35th percentile; SCARB2 +1.06, 27th percentile; CLN3 +1.17, 35th percentile), and NPC1, PSAP, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured. The proposed primary bottleneck is export of lysosome-derived sterol and fatty acid to the ER/plasma-membrane accessible pool, which is inferred, not observed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred signalling state): Restricted delivery of lysosomal lipid to the ER sensor pool would keep SREBP signalling engaged; consistent with this, SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), DHCR24 (+3.69), ACSS2 (+2.93), DHCR7 (+2.71), LSS (+2.27), INSIG1 (+1.87) and LDLR (+1.50) are all elevated despite the elevated uptake program (set mean +2.62). Simultaneous high uptake and high de novo synthesis is the signature that distinguishes sequestration from lipid sufficiency; SREBP cleavage and nuclear localization were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, predicted lipid output): Newly made monounsaturated acyl chains are predicted to be routed into glycerolipid and neutral-lipid pools through elevated AGPAT2 (+6.29, 97th percentile), MGLL (+4.00), MBOAT2 (+3.26), LPCAT1 (+3.07), CHPT1 (+2.91), GPAT4 (+1.58), DGAT1 (+1.72), SOAT1 (+1.25) and ACAT2 (+2.04). This acyl-remodeling arm is a downstream consequence in this model, not the primary bottleneck: as a gene set it is not significantly shifted above the dataset background.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred support): A strongly coordinated mitochondrial TCA and electron-transport transcript increase (MDH1 +8.72, OGDH +8.56, MPC2 +7.98, DLD +5.54, NDUFA5 +7.34, NDUFS7 +5.68, ATP5ME +5.20; set mean +3.42, permutation p\u003c1e-4) is interpreted as supplying citrate/acetyl-CoA and ATP for the sustained lipogenic and lysosomal programs, and is the main alternative explanation (generalized metabolic activation) that must be excluded."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-egress limitation in APOE4 microglia sustains SREBP-driven lipogenesis and neutral-lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15362035225048923, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1752281565348389, "cosine_similarity": 0.40857297064003717, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.595294498381877, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15362035225048923, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1752281565348389, "cosine_similarity": 0.40857297064003717, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "mean_absolute_error": 0.595294498381877, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.095991, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 68}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_096", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported log fold changes of unspecified base; only their sign and rank relative to the whole supplied list are used, and the strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% of rows up) is treated as a baseline against which percentile position, not raw magnitude, is interpreted.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ISG15, MX1, IL1B) means it was not in the supplied differential list and cannot be scored as unchanged.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each; protein_spot:043/045 (candidates include TALDO1, ANXA1, PSMD7, ACTB) and protein_spot:052 (candidates include CTSL, ACTB, CLIC1) are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration that lysosomal/NADPH-supply proteins may move, not as measurements of a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least in rank order, the corresponding transporter, hydrolase and enzyme activities; no activity, localisation, sterol-pool or flux measurement is supplied.", "No lipid, cholesteryl-ester, filipin, lysosomal-pH or lipid-droplet measurement exists in this dataset, so all storage and egress statements are predictions, not observations.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes at a single day-30 mock timepoint; genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous or maturation-stage differences rather than direct APOE4 action, and replicate structure was not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in lipid handling rather than in inflammatory or interferon signalling: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors (notably SCARB1) and for a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) are among the most strongly APOE4-shifted genes, yet sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR) remain elevated rather than repressed. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is return of lysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER regulatory pool, so ER sterol sensing stays in a 'low-sterol' state, SREBP target transcription is not turned off, and incoming plus newly made lipid is inferred to be retained in lysosomes and esterified neutral-lipid stores. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating bypass test: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or otherwise delivering cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool) should selectively collapse the SREBP target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels and reduce neutral-lipid/filipin staining, while leaving the uptake receptor SCARB1 comparatively unchanged; if SREBP targets remain elevated after the lysosomal cholesterol pool is bypassed, the sterol-return bottleneck step is wrong.", "Upstream test: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade of lipoprotein uptake in APOE4 microglia should lower the TFEB-associated hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD) and reduce lysosomal lipid load; unchanged hydrolase transcripts would falsify the uptake-driven ordering of steps.", "Downstream test: SREBP pathway inhibition (fatostatin or SCAP loss) or SCD inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content in APOE4 without normalising SCARB1 or hydrolase transcripts; if lipid storage is unchanged, the persistent-synthesis step contributes little.", "Negative control that rejects the assigned inflammatory/interferon focus: JAK1/2 inhibition, IFNAR1 blockade or NF-kB inhibition should not normalise the lipid/lysosomal transcript module in APOE4 microglia; if it does, the interferon/inflammation explanation supersedes this mechanism.", "Direct sensor test: a fluorescent ER-accessible-cholesterol reporter (e.g. D4H-type probe) should read lower in APOE4 than APOE3 despite equal or greater total cellular cholesterol; finding equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 while SREBP targets stay elevated would weaken the mechanism.", "Coherence test: single-cell or bulk re-measurement should confirm that canonical interferon-stimulated genes (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1-3, OAS1-3, STAT1) are not differentially expressed between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock; detection of a coherent ISG module would require revising the claim that lipid handling, not interferon signalling, is the dominant axis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia express higher transcript levels of lipoprotein- and lipid-ligand receptors (gene:SCARB1 is the single largest high-confidence increase; gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE also increased), which we infer raises lipoprotein/lipid internalisation flux (flux not measured).", "Internalised lipoprotein cargo is delivered to the endolysosome, where APOE4 cells show a coordinated, top-decile increase in hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts together with the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factor TFEB (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C); we read this as a compensatory expansion of degradative capacity, not as proof of increased hydrolytic activity.", "The step that moves lysosomal free cholesterol to the ER-accessible regulatory pool is proposed to be limiting: cholesterol-egress and lipid-transfer components are not co-induced (gene:NPC2 sits below the median of the APOE4-shifted list, and NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, ASAH1, GRN are absent from the differential list), so the ER sterol sensor is inferred to remain in a low-sterol state.", "Because ER sterol sensing is not satisfied, SREBP-dependent synthesis programmes stay on instead of being repressed by the incoming lipid load (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR all increased); transcription-factor activity is inferred, not measured.", "Newly synthesised and imported lipid is channelled to esterification and storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:CIDEB) with no compensatory induction of the main efflux route (ABCA1 is absent from the differential list; only gene:ABCA7 is increased), predicting net cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid retention in APOE4 microglia; no lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "The resulting state is a lysosomal-lipid-storage phenotype rather than an inflammatory or interferon-activated one: canonical type-I interferon-stimulated genes are entirely absent from the 2212-gene differential list, and NF-kB/inflammasome transcripts sit at the median of the global APOE4 shift with several decreased (gene:TNFAIP3, gene:RELB, gene:CCL4, gene:GSDMD)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise lipoprotein uptake and lysosomal-hydrolase capacity while failing to switch off SREBP-driven lipogenesis, creating a lysosome-to-ER sterol-return bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28953821203406915, "cosine_similarity": 0.4085073949582429, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897831715210355, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28953821203406915, "cosine_similarity": 0.4085073949582429, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897831715210355, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.718594, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 69}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_137", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (a sharp gap between -1 and +1 indicates a |logFC| threshold) with 77% of entries positive; enrichment claims are therefore made relative to this list's own distribution, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and the logarithm base is unspecified and preserved as reported.", "The global positive shift may be partly technical (normalization, ambient RNA, differing capture depth between genotype libraries); the mechanism relies on lysosomal/sphingolipid genes being high RELATIVE to that shift, which is the only inference robust to a uniform offset.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is taken as a usable proxy for the capacity, not the activity, of the encoded step; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number, autophagic flux or lipid species was measured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; spots consistent with lysosomal proteases point in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38), so they are treated as non-confirmatory context only.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply differing between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures).", "Substrate accumulation, ceramide/hexosylceramide levels, free fatty acid flux and neutral-lipid storage are inferred pools; none was measured in this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by an endolysosomal state change: transcripts for the acidified degradative compartment and, selectively, for luminal sphingolipid/glycolipid hydrolases are coordinately elevated above the already up-shifted background of this selected DE list, together with lipid-uptake receptor transcripts. We propose this reflects a compensatory response to a persistently elevated membrane-lipid load reaching lysosomes, in which the bottleneck is not hydrolase gene dosage but the clearance/export of the liberated sphingoid and fatty-acyl products; the surplus is instead routed into SREBF1-associated acyl-chain and glycerolipid re-esterification. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; lysosome number, pH, hydrolase activity, lipid pools and all fluxes are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (genotype x inhibitor interaction): partial pharmacological inhibition of GBA (conduritol-B-epoxide) or acid sphingomyelinase (functional inhibition, e.g. desipramine) at matched sub-maximal doses should cause a significantly LARGER accumulation of glucosylceramide/hexosylceramide and sphingomyelin, and a larger increase in LysoTracker+ compartment area, in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 mock microglia. If the dose-response curves are superimposable across genotypes (no interaction term), the proposed lysosomal sphingolipid bottleneck is wrong even if the transcripts remain elevated.", "Baseline lipidomics prediction: untreated APOE4 microglia should show elevated lysosome-associated sphingolipid substrates and elevated neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content simultaneously with normal or increased hydrolase protein. Finding APOE4 substrates equal to or LOWER than APOE3, i.e. genuinely increased net catabolic flux, would weaken the compensatory-bottleneck framing and favour a simple 'higher degradative throughput' model.", "Flux versus capacity test: pulse-chase of a fluorogenic or isotope-labelled glycosphingolipid should show a longer lysosomal residence half-life in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. Equal or shorter half-life would falsify Step 4.", "Re-esterification arm test: SCD inhibition or DGAT1 inhibition should selectively increase lysosomal membrane permeabilization (galectin-3 puncta) and reduce viability in APOE4 relative to APOE3. Equal sensitivity would indicate that the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 arm is a bystander rather than a load-buffering response.", "Specificity test against the alternative bioenergetic mechanism: if respirometry shows the dominant APOE4 difference is increased maximal respiration and spare capacity with no difference in lysosomal substrate handling, the mitochondrial oxidative transcript program (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:NDUFA5) is the better primary mechanism and this hypothesis should be demoted.", "Robustness test: re-analysis with spike-in or cell-number-anchored normalization should retain lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase genes as high outliers relative to the transcriptome-wide median. If the enrichment disappears once the global offset is removed, the mechanism is an artefact of the selected list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_137", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred flux, from measured RNA): APOE4 microglia deliver more lipid/lipoprotein cargo to the endolysosomal system. Uptake- and lipid-handling receptor transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE). Receptor surface localization and actual uptake rate were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred compartment): The acidified degradative compartment and its trafficking machinery are transcriptionally expanded (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:RAB7A, gene:PIK3C3, gene:EPG5, gene:ARL8B, gene:LAMP1). Lysosome number, volume and luminal pH are not observed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, statistically enriched): Within this compartment the sphingolipid/glycolipid arm is selectively high - gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2 - with lysosomal hydrolases enriched in the top decile of effects (7/20 measured, hypergeometric p=0.0023; sphingolipid subset 4/9, p=0.008) and a median effect (+4.19) far above the list median (+1.46).", "Step 4 (inferred, primary bottleneck): We posit that hydrolase transcript supply is not limiting; the limiting step is downstream disposal/export of the products (ceramide, sphingosine, hexosylceramide-derived and lipoprotein-derived free fatty acid) out of the lysosome. Under this model the hydrolase and v-ATPase induction is a compensatory feedback to substrate that is not cleared, so substrate accumulates despite the expanded program.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred routing): The undisposed acyl load is channelled into re-esterification and acyl-chain remodeling rather than terminal removal - gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:SOAT1 - while two long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases are down (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11) and gene:GPAT3 is down, so this arm is partial and not a coherent lipogenic program on its own.", "Step 6 (inferred state, not a measured phenotype): The net predicted state of mock APOE4 microglia is a chronically lipid-burdened, remodeling-biased endolysosomal set point that coexists with, rather than replaces, a high mitochondrial oxidative transcript program (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:NDUFA5), and that is not a generic activation state because a major microglial protease transcript moves oppositely (gene:CTSS -5.57)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a compensatory TFEB-type expansion of lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid catabolism, with the disposal of hydrolysis products as the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.309603810508437, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18208134916656898, "cosine_similarity": 0.40841020455916427, "direction_accuracy": 0.3883495145631068, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_137", "mean_absolute_error": 0.622673139158576, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.309603810508437, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18208134916656898, "cosine_similarity": 0.40841020455916427, "direction_accuracy": 0.3883495145631068, "mean_absolute_error": 0.622673139158576, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60291625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 70}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_031", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift (about 77 percent of rows positive, median about +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), so only within-list contrasts (significance rank and effect percentile) are treated as informative; the log base is left unspecified throughout.", "Transcript abundance for SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, hydrolases and receptors is assumed to track the corresponding enzyme or receptor activity and flux; no activity, localization or lipid-pool measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used to assert the abundance of a single named protein.", "Efflux (ABCA1/ABCG1), neutral cholesteryl-ester hydrolase (NCEH1), LIPA and NPC1 are absent from the supplied rows; their non-scaling is an assumption, not an observation.", "Effect magnitude and adjusted p-value are essentially uncorrelated in this set (Pearson r about -0.04 between |effect| and -log10 adjusted p), so very large |effect| values are assumed to be unstable estimates from low-expression genes and are down-weighted relative to significance rank.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply and possible non-microglial transcript contamination are assumed to be present but not resolvable here.", "The APOE4 versus APOE3 contrast is assumed isogenic as stated in the metadata, and the observed differences are assumed to be steady-state at day 30 rather than transient."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by an elevated scavenger-receptor/lipid-handling transcriptional program together with elevated esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1) and monounsaturated-fatty-acid supply (SCD, FADS1, SREBF1) transcripts; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is disposal of internalized lipid, with re-esterification into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores acting as the dominant sink, so the ER-regulatory lipid pool stays low, the SREBP-1/uptake program is not switched off, and endolysosomal lipid load rises, driving compensatory TFEB/MITF-associated hydrolase transcription. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed, not demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (for example K-604 or avasimibe, 24-72 h) in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid droplet content, raise the ER-accessible sterol pool, and reduce SREBF1, SCD, FADS1 and the scavenger-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, CD163) toward APOE3 levels. If SOAT1 inhibition reduces esters but leaves SREBF1/SCD and the scavenger program unchanged, the proposed feed-forward bottleneck is weakened.", "Sink-versus-capacity discrimination: increasing degradative capacity alone (TFEB overexpression or recombinant acid lipase supplementation) should not normalise APOE4 neutral-lipid or cholesteryl-ester content while SOAT1/DGAT1 remain active; if boosting lysosomal capacity alone clears the stores, the bottleneck lies in lysosomal hydrolysis rather than in esterification-dominated disposal.", "Flux test: pulse-chase with 13C- or 2H-labelled oleate and fluorescent or labelled LDL/cholesterol, normalised to internalised label, should show a higher fraction of label recovered in cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol pools and a lower fraction released to the medium in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal fractional partitioning would weaken the mechanism.", "Baseline requirement: direct lipidomics or droplet imaging must show elevated cholesteryl ester and/or triacylglycerol per cell in mock-treated APOE4 microglia. Absence of elevated neutral lipid despite the transcript signature would falsify the core claim.", "Supply test: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking CD36/SCARB1-mediated uptake, should reduce droplet accumulation; if droplets and the SOAT1/SCD signature persist unchanged without an extracellular lipid supply, the source of the stored lipid is endogenous synthesis or autophagic membrane turnover rather than scavenger uptake, and step one must be revised.", "Genotype specificity: repeating the isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 edit in an independent donor background should reproduce the coordinated SOAT1, SCD, SREBF1 and scavenger-receptor shift; failure to reproduce it would indicate a donor- or clone-specific effect rather than an APOE4 mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-debris receptors and secreted lipid handlers (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:COLEC12, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLA2G7); inferred (not measured): increased flux of lipoprotein and membrane-debris lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Inferred: delivered lipid raises endolysosomal lipid load; measured correlate is coordinated up-regulation of lysosomal hydrolase and CLEAR-type transcripts (gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ACP5, gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), interpreted as a compensatory response to load rather than as proof of increased degradative flux.", "Measured: esterification and acyl-chain-supply transcripts are up (gene:SOAT1 with among the smallest adjusted p-values in the set, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:SREBF1); inferred: liberated cholesterol and fatty acids are re-esterified into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and stored in cytoplasmic droplets, with SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl chains limiting saturated-fatty-acid lipotoxicity.", "Inferred (bottleneck): because esterification, not catabolic export, is the dominant sink, the ER-accessible sterol/fatty-acid pool stays relatively low, so SREBP-1-linked lipogenic transcripts and scavenger receptors are not feedback-repressed; this closes a feed-forward loop that keeps uptake and storage high.", "Inferred consequence: APOE4 microglia settle into a droplet-laden, lysosome-expanded, scavenging/lipid-associated state (consistent with gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ACP5) whose lipid-processing capacity is committed to storage, reducing the reserve available for stimulus-driven lipid clearance.", "Unmeasured in the supplied rows: ABCA1/ABCG1 efflux, LIPA and NCEH1 hydrolases, NPC1, PLIN2 and any lipid, cholesteryl-ester or droplet measurement; the model assumes efflux/hydrolytic disposal is not scaled up in proportion to uptake and requires direct lipid measurement to test."], "title": "APOE4 microglia divert internalized lipid into SOAT1/DGAT1 esterified stores, creating a feed-forward scavenger-uptake and lysosome-expansion state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10176125244618395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2597041022652445, "cosine_similarity": 0.40837525657522317, "direction_accuracy": 0.16990291262135923, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5908478964401295, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10176125244618395, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2597041022652445, "cosine_similarity": 0.40837525657522317, "direction_accuracy": 0.16990291262135923, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5908478964401295, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.89689975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 71}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong positive median (+1.46); we therefore interpret direction by rank within the list, not by absolute magnitude, and assume the list-wide shift is a selection/normalisation feature rather than a genome-wide induction.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no protein, flux, sterol-pool, localisation or SREBP-processing measurement is supplied for any step.", "Genes absent from the list (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, GRAMD1A/B/C, STARD3, HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, MSMO1) are treated as unmeasured, not unchanged; the egress block and the synthetic-flux increase are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:053, protein_spot:058 both list CTSD) and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a named protein in this mechanism.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular sterol/lipoprotein supply is not cell-autonomous and may itself differ between genotypes.", "Effects are from a single mock-treatment contrast at day 30 with replicate structure not supplied; genotype-associated correlation is assumed, causal direction is not established."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, lipoprotein/sterol delivery to endolysosomes and lysosomal hydrolase capacity are transcriptionally scaled up (SCARB1, TFEB, GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, RAB7A) while the transcripts for the lysosomal sterol-egress and ER-transfer arm are not (NPC2, SCARB2, OSBPL1A near or below the list-wide shift; OSBPL8 strongly down). We hypothesise that the resulting rate-limiting step is cholesterol handoff from the endolysosome to the ER, so the ER-accessible sterol pool (inferred, not measured) stays low, the SREBP/post-squalene sterol module (SREBF1, SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, LDLR, INSIG1, SCD) remains active, and the surplus sterol/fatty acid is diverted into esterification and storage (SOAT1, DGAT1) rather than efficiently exported (APOE, ABCA7, CYP27A1 up only modestly relative to the global shift). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute delivery of sterol directly to the ER-accessible pool, bypassing lysosomal egress (cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin loading, or 25-hydroxycholesterol), should suppress the sterol module (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1) substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, because only APOE4 is proposed to be ER-sterol-deprived. Equal suppression in both genotypes, or failure to suppress in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Imaging/biochemistry: APOE4 microglia should show increased unesterified cholesterol (filipin or D4-domain probe) colocalised with LAMP1+ compartments, together with an equal or reduced ER/plasma-membrane accessible sterol pool (ALOD4-type probe). Finding equal lysosomal sterol, or an elevated accessible pool alongside the active sterol module, would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Egress rescue: relieving lysosomal sterol export (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 or GRAMD1B overexpression) should normalise the APOE4 sterol/lipogenic transcripts and lower SCARB1 and SOAT1 within 24-48 h. Documented clearance of lysosomal cholesterol without transcript normalisation would falsify step 4.", "Upstream-versus-downstream test: SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 inhibition should reduce lysosomal sterol load; if it also abolishes the sterol-synthesis transcript module, delivery rather than egress is limiting and the proposed bottleneck is misplaced.", "Flux test: 13C/D-acetate labelling into sterols should show at most a modest APOE4 increase in de novo synthesis; a large increase in mevalonate-pathway flux with no lysosomal sterol accumulation would favour a primary biosynthetic-drive model over the egress-bottleneck model.", "Coherence test: SREBP-2 cleavage (nuclear N-terminal fragment) should be higher in APOE4 lysates; unchanged SREBP-2 processing despite elevated target transcripts would indicate the transcripts are driven by an SREBP-independent route and weaken step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/sterol-cargo receptors, most strikingly SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22, 99th percentile of the supplied list), with LDLR, CD36, TREM2 and CD163 also present; we infer, but do not observe, increased delivery of cholesteryl-ester-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A TFEB-associated degradative program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:RAB7A), consistent with expanded lysosomal hydrolysis and maturation capacity.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck; partly inferred from missing scaling): The sterol-egress/transfer arm does not scale with steps 1-2. NPC2 (+1.17), SCARB2 (+1.06) and OSBPL1A (+1.03) sit at the 26th-35th percentile of a list whose median effect is +1.46, and the ER-contact-site lipid-transfer transcript OSBPL8 is down (-1.90, 13th percentile). We therefore propose limited non-vesicular cholesterol transfer from the limiting membrane of the endolysosome to the ER. NPC1, LIPA, GRAMD1A/B/C and STARD3 were not measured, so the block itself is inferred, not observed.", "Step 4 (inferred sensing state): Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is the sensed pool, low ER sterol keeps SCAP-SREBP processing permissive; the measured RNA correlate is the sustained sterol/lipogenic module (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD). SREBP proteolytic activation itself was not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are preferentially esterified and stored rather than exported: gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 up, with gene:SCD and gene:MGLL up; the efflux/oxysterol arm (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:CYP27A1, gene:MYLIP) rises only weakly relative to the list-wide up-shift, and ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured.", "Step 6 (systems consequence, inferred): The combination of a futile uptake-plus-synthesis loop and sterol/sphingolipid retention in an expanded lysosomal compartment constitutes chronic lysosomal lipid stress, plausibly contributing to the co-measured inflammatory transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:A2M) without requiring an exogenous stimulus in the mock condition."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: expanded uptake and hydrolytic capacity without matched lysosome-to-ER cholesterol transfer keeps the SREBP sterol program switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2885386399425181, "cosine_similarity": 0.4080884797549887, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5901197411003236, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2885386399425181, "cosine_similarity": 0.4080884797549887, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5901197411003236, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.44432, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 72}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_015", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every adjusted p value is below 0.05) with 77% positive effects; all pathway statements here are enrichment relative to that list background, not relative to an unbiased transcriptome, and the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme capacity; no protein, metabolite, flux, respiration or lipid measurement of these enzymes is supplied, so mitochondrial oxidation, citrate export, acetyl-CoA levels and lipid-droplet content are inferred and unobserved.", "ACLY, FASN, ACACA, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied list; their absence is treated as not measured, not as unchanged, and the acetyl-CoA-to-lipid conversion step is therefore assumed rather than supported.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; no spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme in the mechanism.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-associated transcript differences may be partly non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipid or cholesterol supply differing between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures).", "Isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison under mock treatment at one timepoint; the direction of causality between the metabolic program and the lipid phenotype is assumed, not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent up-shift of TCA-cycle and OXPHOS transcripts together with the mitochondrial citrate carrier SLC25A1 and cytosolic acetyl-CoA/OAA-handling enzymes (ACSS2, MDH1, GOT1, ME1), while glycolytic transcripts are not coordinately raised. We hypothesise that this configuration increases export of mitochondrially derived citrate to the cytosol and that this citrate-derived acetyl-CoA supply is the rate-limiting input to a concurrently up-regulated SREBP/sterol-desaturation and esterification program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, ACAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1), producing genotype-dependent accumulation of neutral lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester) and a compensatory TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program. All transcript changes are measured abundances; every flux, localisation and causal step below is inferred, not observed. The ER-proteostasis/UPR mechanism assigned as focus is rejected because it is not enriched in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown), or of ACLY, should reduce the APOE4-specific excess of neutral lipid (BODIPY/lipid-droplet area, triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the elevated TCA/OXPHOS transcript signature and basal respiration largely intact. If APOE4 lipid excess persists unchanged after SLC25A1/ACLY blockade, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is falsified.", "Source-discrimination: culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium should preserve (or amplify, via SREBP de-repression) the APOE4\u003eAPOE3 neutral-lipid difference if de novo synthesis dominates; if the difference disappears in lipid-free medium, the phenotype is uptake-driven (SCARB1/CD36/LDLR) and Steps 2-4 are demoted.", "Flux test: 13C-U-glucose or 13C-glutamine tracing should show greater label incorporation into palmitate, monounsaturated 16:1/18:1 species and newly synthesised cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3, with a higher cytosolic citrate/acetyl-CoA labelling ratio. Equal or lower lipogenic labelling in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism even if transcripts remain elevated.", "Sink test: SCD inhibition should shift APOE4 lipids toward saturated species and reduce droplet number more in APOE4 than APOE3; no genotype-selective effect would argue that SCD/SREBP transcript elevation is not functionally engaged.", "Hierarchy test: lysosomal hydrolase inhibition (e.g. conduritol-B-epoxide for GBA or bafilomycin) should worsen APOE4 lipid storage without lowering TCA/SREBP transcripts, whereas SLC25A1/ACLY blockade should lower the TFEB-type lysosomal transcript program; the opposite ordering would indicate the lysosomal arm is primary and this hypothesis is misordered.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: APOE4 microglia should not show significant induction of BiP/HSPA5, spliced XBP1, HERPUD1 or ATF4 protein/reporter activity relative to APOE3; a clear UPR induction would support the ER-proteostasis alternative over this metabolic mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show a uniformly positive TCA and respiratory-chain transcript program (9/9 a-priori TCA genes and 37/37 detected NDUF/SDH/UQCR/COX/ATP5 subunits positive; set medians far above the list background), which we interpret as increased mitochondrial oxidative and anaplerotic capacity rather than measured respiration.", "Step 2 (inferred flux, primary bottleneck): increased pyruvate import (MPC2) and citrate formation (ACO2, OGDH, DLD, GLUD1 anaplerosis) combined with strongly increased citrate-carrier transcript SLC25A1 is proposed to raise citrate export from matrix to cytosol; the cytosolic acetyl-CoA generated from this citrate (plus acetate via ACSS2) is the rate-limiting input to lipid synthesis. ACLY itself was not measured, so this step is the weakest link and the explicit test point.", "Step 3 (inferred redox/carbon return): MDH1, GOT1 and ME1 transcript increases are read as an increased cytosolic malate-aspartate/citrate-malate return arm that regenerates oxaloacetate and cytosolic NADPH, allowing sustained rather than transient lipogenic flux; classical oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD, TALDO1) are instead decreased, so NADPH is predicted to come mainly from the malic-enzyme arm.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the acetyl-CoA sink is transcriptionally pre-set - SREBF1 and SREBF2 with post-squalene sterol enzymes (LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, HMGCS1, ACAT2, INSIG1) and the desaturase SCD - so extra cytosolic acetyl-CoA is predicted to be committed to monounsaturated fatty acid and sterol synthesis rather than to oxidation.", "Step 5 (inferred storage): esterification and glycerolipid/phospholipid remodelling transcripts (DGAT1, SOAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, CERS4) plus lipid-uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, ABCA7, TREM2, APOE) are increased, which we infer channels both synthesised and internalised lipid into cytoplasmic lipid droplets and cholesteryl esters instead of into efflux (no ABCA1/ABCG1 measurement is available).", "Step 6 (inferred compensation, not the driver): a TFEB-type lysosomal program (TFEB, GBA, GBA2, SMPD1, HEXA, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, LAMP1, NPC2, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) is coordinately raised, interpreted as a downstream compensatory attempt to catabolise the expanded lipid load; this arm is predicted to be secondary, i.e. blocking Step 2 should reduce it, while blocking lysosomal hydrolysis should not reduce Steps 1-4."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route elevated TCA/OXPHOS carbon through SLC25A1-dependent citrate export into an SREBP-driven esterification program, making cytosolic lipogenic carbon supply the bottleneck for neutral-lipid accumulation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36801683713030314, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3127244341670694, "cosine_similarity": 0.4080604781211393, "direction_accuracy": 0.3365695792880259, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936990291262136, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36801683713030314, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3127244341670694, "cosine_similarity": 0.4080604781211393, "direction_accuracy": 0.3365695792880259, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936990291262136, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8434435, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 73}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_013", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |log FC| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c= 0.05 in an unspecified logarithm base), so absence of a gene means 'not in the selection', not 'unchanged'; set-level statistics are therefore computed against the within-list background (median log FC +1.46, 77% up) rather than against a whole transcriptome.", "The strong global positive shift is treated as a normalisation/composition offset that must be subtracted before any single up-regulated gene is called informative; only relative (background-corrected) set contrasts are used as evidence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for lysosomal protein content; hydrolase activity, lumenal pH, lysosome number/size, cargo half-life, lipid species and APOE protein/lipidation state were NOT measured in these data and are inferred only.", "Protein spots are mixtures with multiple candidate genes (KRT/ACTB-dominated lists indicate handling contamination), so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; they are used only as weak, direction-ambiguous counter-evidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts and any secreted APOE pool may be non-cell-autonomous; the comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at one timepoint (Day 30) under mock treatment with unreported replicate number, so effect sizes (some |log FC| \u003e 8) may be inflated by low-count genes.", "The link from lysosomal lipid retention to the SREBP-target signature assumes ER sterol sensing is intact in both genotypes."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting step is terminal clearance of lipid-rich cargo from the late endosome/lysosome lumen, not cargo uptake and not transcription of degradative machinery: APOE4 cells show a coordinated, background-corrected increase of lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB/MITF transcripts (37/37 lysosome-set genes up, set median log FC 2.02 vs 1.45 dataset background, permutation p=0.05, binomial vs 77% up background p=6.6e-5) together with an all-up sterol-synthesis/SREBP-target and neutral-lipid-esterification signature, a pattern expected if lumenal lipid is retained (ER-accessible sterol sensed as low) while transcriptional lysosomal capacity is being scaled up; we therefore predict a lipidomic phenotype of increased cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol and sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid substrate species in APOE4 microglia, with degradative flux (not enzyme transcript level) as the bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: acute (4-24 h) 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, which removes lumenal sterol without changing hydrolase transcription, should in APOE4 microglia reduce filipin/Bodipy-cholesterol signal in LAMP1+ compartments, lower cholesteryl-ester mass, and normalise SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS) toward APOE3 levels, while leaving the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation largely intact. If cyclodextrin clears lumenal sterol but SREBP targets and cholesteryl esters stay elevated, the egress-bottleneck link in Steps 4-5 is wrong and an ER/plasma-membrane sterol-handling or APOE-lipidation defect is the better explanation.", "FLUX vs CAPACITY: pulse-chase of a degradable lipid/protein cargo (Bodipy-C12 or DQ-BSA plus fluorescent myelin debris) should show LONGER cargo half-life and higher steady-state lumenal cargo in APOE4 despite equal or higher per-cell GBA/beta-hexosaminidase/acid-sphingomyelinase activity. If APOE4 instead clears cargo faster or equally with no lumenal accumulation, the 'capacity does not meet demand' claim fails and the data should be reinterpreted as a matched (non-limiting) expansion of lysosomal capacity.", "COMPENSATION DIRECTION: TFEB knockdown or v-ATPase partial inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin) should WORSEN the APOE4 lipid phenotype (further increase lysosomal cholesterol, CE and glycosphingolipid substrates) relative to APOE3. If TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid droplets and cholesteryl esters, the CLEAR program is a driver rather than a compensatory response and Step 3 must be inverted.", "STORAGE ARM: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should convert the predicted APOE4 cholesteryl-ester excess into free cholesterol with unchanged or increased lysosomal cholesterol staining and no rescue of cargo clearance; a rescue of cargo clearance by SOAT1 inhibition would place the bottleneck in esterification rather than in endolysosomal egress.", "UPTAKE ARM CONTROL: blocking uptake (anti-TREM2/CD36 or cytochalasin-D pretreatment) should blunt the lipid accumulation but should NOT normalise the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation within 24 h if that elevation is a load-driven compensation; simultaneous normalisation of both within hours would argue for a single upstream transcriptional driver rather than a cargo-load feedback loop.", "LIPIDOMIC READOUT: untargeted lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show increased cholesteryl esters, triacylglycerol, sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide and bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate; a lipidome with unchanged or reduced sterol esters and sphingolipids would falsify the predicted downstream consequence of this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia hold higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/debris uptake and opsonic receptors (gene:TREM2, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:SCARB1, gene:MERTK with gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/gene:C1QB/gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A) alongside gene:APOE itself; we infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endocytic/phagocytic route (receptor-set direction is up but its magnitude is not different from the global up-shift, MWU p=0.55).", "STEP 2 (measured abundance; inferred localization/maturation): transcripts for late-endosome maturation, fusion and positioning machinery are higher (gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B, gene:PIK3C3, gene:VPS18), consistent with cargo reaching a late-endosomal/lysosomal compartment rather than stalling at the early endosome; compartment identity itself was not imaged or fractionated here.", "STEP 3 (measured abundance; inferred capacity signal): a CLEAR-like program is coherently elevated - acid hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:AGA, gene:GLA, gene:SUMF1, gene:GM2A), lumenal/membrane lysosomal proteins (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:SLC17A5) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1E1) with gene:TFEB and gene:MITF up. We read this as a demand signal (attempted expansion of lysosomal capacity), not as proof of higher hydrolytic activity, which was not assayed.", "STEP 4 (bottleneck; inferred, partly counter-supported): terminal processing/egress does not scale with the transcriptional program. Enzyme-delivery and fusion components move against the global up-shift (gene:M6PR down, gene:STX17 down, gene:CTSS down, gene:IDS down) and the only protein-level readings that contain lysosomal candidates are split in direction (protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:052 up; protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), so lumenal enzyme load and activity per lysosome may lag transcript induction. Consequence (inferred, unmeasured): lipid cargo is retained in the LE/lysosome lumen and degradative flux per unit cargo falls.", "STEP 5 (measured abundance; inferred sensing): with sterol trapped in the lumenal compartment, the ER-accessible cholesterol pool is sensed as insufficient, so SREBP-target transcripts rise as a block (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2, with lipogenic gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1; 12/12 up, binomial p=0.044) despite the elevated uptake-receptor transcripts of Step 1 - a combination that is hard to explain by cargo excess reaching the ER, but is expected if uptake and egress are uncoupled.", "STEP 6 (measured abundance; inferred flux/lipid outcome): the newly synthesised and salvaged lipid is routed to esterified storage rather than to efflux (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 up; gene:ABCA7 up while ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured), and sphingolipid handling genes shift (gene:ST3GAL5, gene:CERS6, gene:GM2A up) - predicting an APOE4 lipidome enriched in cholesteryl esters, triacylglycerol and lysosomal sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid substrates, with gene:GPNMB up as a lysosomal-stress-associated marker."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by terminal endolysosomal lipid clearance, and the CLEAR-type hydrolase/v-ATPase induction is a compensatory response that shunts lipid into esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13894324853228962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1819056877719021, "cosine_similarity": 0.4077722372702497, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140938511326861, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13894324853228962, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1819056877719021, "cosine_similarity": 0.4077722372702497, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140938511326861, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5200765, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 74}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (all adjusted p\u003c0.05 and all |effect|\u003e=1 in an unspecified logarithm base), not an unbiased transcriptome; all directional claims are therefore made relative to the list's own 77.1% up-fraction, and no absolute pathway-enrichment claim is made.", "The global positive shift (median reported logFC +1.46) is assumed to be partly technical (sparse single-cell/pseudobulk quantification, depth or ambient-RNA differences) rather than a genuine transcriptome-wide increase; the module claim relies on relative excess above this shift, which would fail if the shift is strongly gene-set dependent.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a lower bound on, not a measurement of, hydrolase amount, maturation state, luminal activity, acidification or degradative flux; all activity, flux, localisation and causal statements are inferred.", "Protein spots are 2-D-gel features with about five candidate genes each and are assumed not to identify a unique protein; spot directions are used only as weak, non-identifying evidence for proteoform heterogeneity.", "The co-culture with astrocytes and the absence of replicate/composition information mean genotype effects could partly reflect cell-composition or non-cell-autonomous differences rather than microglia-intrinsic biology.", "Key nodes of the proposed mechanism (lysosomal pH, LAMP1 protein, lipid droplets, ABCA1/ABCG1, NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, SQSTM1/LC3) are absent from the supplied data and are treated as unmeasured, not as observed."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the endolysosomal/v-ATPase/TFEB module together with higher uptake-receptor and sterol-handling transcripts; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not lysosome number or acidification but the conversion of this transcript program into mature luminal hydrolytic throughput per unit of internalised cargo (a hydrolase-delivery/maturation-limited bottleneck marked by the discordant fall in M6PR, IDS and CTSS and by cathepsin- and v-ATPase-candidate protein spots that move in both directions), so that cargo-derived lipid is re-esterified into storage rather than cleared. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed as a testable model.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo pulse-chase: labelling isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 mock microglia with a defined degradable cargo (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-myelin or pHrodo-oxLDL) should show equal or greater internalisation in APOE4 at 30-60 min but a slower degradation rate constant and more retained undegraded cargo in LAMP1+ compartments at 6-24 h. The mechanism is weakened if the per-cell degradation half-time in APOE4 is equal to or shorter than APOE3, or if uptake is lower rather than equal/higher (which would indicate an uptake-limited, not capacity-limited, difference).", "Throughput normalised to compartment mass: activity-based cathepsin probes or fluorogenic substrates normalised to LAMP1 protein should show no increase, or a decrease, in cathepsin activity per unit lysosomal mass in APOE4, with a selectively larger deficit for CTSS-preferring substrates despite increased CTSB/CTSD transcripts. Proportional scaling of per-LAMP1 hydrolase activity with the transcript rise would falsify the bottleneck as stated.", "Acidification control: ratiometric lysosomal pH should be equal or only marginally different between genotypes, consistent with the coherent v-ATPase transcript rise. Markedly less acidic APOE4 lysosomes would relocate the bottleneck to acidification and require revision of Step 4.", "Biogenesis-sufficiency test: further activation of the TFEB axis (Torin1 or TFEB overexpression) should raise lysosomal transcripts in both genotypes but give only partial (\u003c50%) rescue of the APOE4 cargo-clearance deficit; complete normalisation by TFEB activation alone would favour the alternative 'insufficient biogenesis' model over throughput limitation.", "Sorting-arm test: restoring M6PR (or CTSS) expression in APOE4 microglia should increase mature hydrolase content in lysosome-enriched fractions and measurably improve clearance of the pulse-chase cargo; no change in either readout would falsify the hydrolase-delivery component of Step 4 while leaving Steps 1-3 intact.", "Storage arm: SOAT1 inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet burden in APOE4 microglia without normalising the endolysosomal transcript module; if lipid droplets are not elevated in APOE4 in the first place, Step 5 is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): transcripts for lipid/debris uptake and opsonisation receptors are uniformly higher in APOE4 (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, MERTK, TREM2, CLEC7A, ITGAX, C1QA/B/C; 13/13 up, median reported logFC 1.30, binomial p=0.034 against the 77% up-shifted background). We infer, but did not measure, a greater delivery flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localisation): late-endosome maturation and cargo-sorting transcripts are up (RAB7A, MON1B, VPS18, CHMP4B, SNX3, VPS26A, IGF2R, AP5M1), consistent with cargo reaching the late endosome/lysosome; compartment identity and cargo residence time were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): a curated endolysosomal module (hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, LAMP1, SCARB2, TFEB, MITF, RRAGD, PIK3C3) is coherently up (47/50 members up, median reported logFC 2.02; binomial p=1.4e-3 vs the 77% background up-rate; magnitudes above background, Mann-Whitney p=2.6e-3). This is read as a TFEB/MITF-type biogenesis response, i.e. increased compartment mass and acidification machinery at the transcript level only; lysosome number, lysosomal pH and TFEB nuclear localisation were not measured.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; mixed evidence): mature hydrolytic throughput per cargo does not scale with the transcript program. Against the strongly up-shifted background, the hydrolase-sorting receptor M6PR (-1.72), the sulfatase-pathway enzyme IDS (-1.56) and the dominant microglial protease CTSS (-5.57) fall, and 2-D protein spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsin B/D or ATP6V1E1 split in direction (up: spots 052, 053, 055, 027; down: spots 058, 067, 069, 064, 065), which is compatible with redistribution among proteoforms rather than a uniform rise in mature enzyme. Spot identities are ambiguous (about 5 candidate genes per spot), so this step is the weakest link and is stated as inference, not observation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): cargo-derived and de novo lipid is routed to esterification and storage rather than resolution: SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, LDLR, ABCA7, NPC2 and APOE are all up (15/15 lipid-module members up, binomial p=0.020). Lipid-droplet content, free versus esterified cholesterol and the efflux transporters ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred state): persistent undegraded cargo is proposed to sustain a chronically activated, DAM-like microglial state (GPNMB, ITGAX, CLEC7A, CD74, CCL2, A2M up) that feeds back on the biogenesis program in Step 3, producing a stable high-transcript/low-throughput steady state rather than resolution."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand the endolysosomal compartment transcriptionally but are limited in mature hydrolytic throughput per cargo, diverting undegraded lipid cargo into esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20549253299893053, "cosine_similarity": 0.40736222346081935, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6051003236245954, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20549253299893053, "cosine_similarity": 0.40736222346081935, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6051003236245954, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72734, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 75}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_145", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Lower steady-state transcript abundance for the tether/SNARE set translates into proportionally lower protein abundance and lower fusion capacity; no SNARE or tether protein was measured in the supplied data.", "The reported RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base and unspecified scaling (values span -7.9 to +15.5), so only sign and rank, not absolute magnitude, are used.", "The RNA rows are a curated differential-expression export: 506 workbook rows each pair one up gene with one down gene and a further 1200 rows are up-only, so the 77% up fraction is a property of the source table, not evidence of a global transcriptome up-shift; all enrichment inference is therefore direction-based against the 1705:507 within-list background.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (keratin/actin dominated) and cannot identify a unique protein; spots are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal may derive from non-microglial cells or from genotype effects on the astrocyte partner.", "Replicate number is not supplied, and the p-values are taken as reported without access to the underlying model.", "APOE secretion, cargo transit kinetics, lysosomal proteolytic activity, and lipid content are unmeasured; all flux, localisation and directionality statements are inferences."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, the differentially expressed transcript set shows a selective, direction-coherent depletion of Golgi/TGN tethering and SNARE fusion components (GOSR1, BET1L, STX16, VAMP2, SEC22A, STX17, GCC1, GCC2, TRAPPC6B, TRAPPC8, EXOC3, EXOC6; 14/19 of the fusion-tether set in the down direction, Fisher p=3.5e-6) while vesicle coat, cargo-receptor and Rab transcripts are up (COPA, COPE, RAB1B, RAB6A, MCFD2, ERGIC2, TMED1; 13/15 up; fusion-vs-coat contrast p=6e-4). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting lesion in APOE4 is the tether/SNARE-dependent vesicle fusion step downstream of ER exit, not ER chaperone folding capacity: reduced fusion capacity slows delivery of secretory and hydrolase cargo through the Golgi/TGN, is accompanied by ER glycan-quality-control induction (MLEC, UGGT1, DNAJC10, DNAJB11, MANF, ATF6, DDIT3) without a matching classical BiP/GRP94 protein rise, by reduced ERAD retrotranslocation transcripts (SEL1L, DERL1, EDEM1, SEC62), and by a compensatory transcriptional expansion of the acidic degradative compartment (CTSB, CTSD, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H, TFEB) together with sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification programmes (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, SOAT1, DGAT1). Causality is not established by these data; the trafficking bottleneck is an inference from measured transcript abundances.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: a synchronised secretory-cargo release assay (RUSH or cycloheximide chase of endogenous APOE and of a generic ss-reporter) in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show delayed ERGIC-to-Golgi/TGN arrival and a lower secreted:intracellular APOE ratio in APOE4, while ER-exit-site budding and COPII recruitment remain comparable. Equal transit kinetics and equal secretion index would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue: re-expression of STX16 or GOSR1 (or of the missing tether GCC1/GCC2) in APOE4 microglia should partially restore cargo transit and secreted APOE and blunt the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation; no change in transit or secretion after restoring these proteins would falsify the assigned bottleneck.", "Mechanism-discriminating negative: relieving ER folding load should not be sufficient - chemical chaperone (4-PBA/TUDCA) or ISR inhibition (ISRIB) should leave the APOE4 transit delay largely intact even if it lowers DDIT3-arm transcripts. Full normalisation of transit and secretion by ISRIB or a chemical chaperone would show a chaperone/ISR-primary mechanism instead and falsify this hypothesis.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot should show reduced STX16/GS28(GOSR1) protein and unchanged or only modestly changed BiP (HSPA5) and GRP94 (HSP90B1) protein in APOE4, consistent with the non-significant negative HSP90B1/HSPA5-candidate spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004 and protein_spot:005. A clear BiP/GRP94 protein induction with unchanged SNARE protein would weaken the hypothesis.", "Endpoint separation: SOAT1 inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet load in APOE4 microglia without correcting the cargo transit delay, whereas correcting the fusion step should reduce both. If lipid load is unchanged by fusion-machinery rescue, the link from trafficking to the lipid phenotype is falsified even if the trafficking defect is real.", "Specificity control: knockdown of STX16 or GOSR1 in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 endolysosomal transcript expansion and lipid retention; absence of any phenocopy would argue the transcript differences are a consequence rather than a driver."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_145", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show coordinated lower transcript levels for Golgi/TGN tethering factors and SNAREs (gene:GOSR1, gene:BET1L, gene:STX16, gene:VAMP2, gene:SEC22A, gene:STX17, gene:GCC1, gene:GCC2, gene:TRAPPC6B, gene:TRAPPC8, gene:EXOC3, gene:EXOC6) alongside higher coat/cargo-receptor/Rab transcripts (gene:COPA, gene:COPE, gene:RAB1B, gene:RAB6A, gene:MCFD2, gene:ERGIC2).", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux, primary bottleneck): reduced abundance of the tether/SNARE fusion machinery lowers the rate of vesicle docking and fusion at the ERGIC-Golgi and TGN interfaces, so budding and cargo capture remain adequate while membrane-fusion becomes rate-limiting for anterograde secretory flux.", "Step 3 (inferred localisation/consequence in the ER): slowed post-ER consumption of cargo prolongs residence of glycoprotein cargo in the ER/ERGIC, engaging glycan re-glucosylation and chaperone quality control (gene:MLEC, gene:UGGT1, gene:DNAJC10, gene:DNAJB11, gene:MANF, gene:CRELD2, gene:SERP1) and an ATF6/CHOP-associated transcriptional arm (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3) rather than a general chaperone-capacity failure.", "Step 4 (inferred disposal limitation): concurrently lower ERAD retrotranslocation transcripts (gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1, gene:SEC62) predict reduced capacity to clear stalled or terminally misfolded glycoprotein cargo, so backlogged cargo is retained or rerouted rather than degraded at the ER.", "Step 5 (inferred rerouting): cargo and membrane that cannot complete Golgi/TGN transit are diverted toward the endolysosomal route, matching the strong up-direction bias of hydrolase, v-ATPase and CLEAR-network transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB; 29/31 up, p=0.029) and of endosome/retromer transcripts (gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS28).", "Step 6 (inferred lipid endpoint): impaired secretory delivery of APOE-containing lipoprotein cargo despite elevated gene:APOE transcript, combined with induced sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and increased lipid-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36), predicts net intracellular retention of neutral and sterol lipid in APOE4 microglia. No lipid pool was measured in the supplied data; this step is a prediction, not an observation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia have a post-ER tether/SNARE fusion bottleneck that shunts secretory cargo and lipid into an expanded endolysosomal compartment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2878208863550564, "cosine_similarity": 0.40677337668435054, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_145", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5906666666666667, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2878208863550564, "cosine_similarity": 0.40677337668435054, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5906666666666667, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.07287775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 76}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_020", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% positive, mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are therefore relative-to-list-background, not absolute transcriptome enrichment.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein availability; no respiratory-complex assembly, enzyme activity, flux, NAD(H), citrate, acetyl-CoA or lipid measurement is present in the supplied data, so all activity, flux and localization statements are inferred.", "mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to be captured with comparable efficiency in APOE4 and APOE3 by the 10X Flex probe panel; genotype-independent technical capture bias would remove the central discordance.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a definite mitochondrial, lipogenic or antioxidant protein measurement.", "The astrocyte co-culture and the day-30 timepoint are assumed not to be the sole drivers of the microglial mitonuclear pattern; genotype effects are assumed to be cell-intrinsic to the isogenic comparison.", "Causality is not established: the direction from mitonuclear imbalance to lipid storage is a hypothesis consistent with the correlational data only."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia raise the nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, mitochondrial-translation and TCA/carbon-entry transcript program without a matching increase in mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts; the resulting shortfall in mtDNA-encoded core subunits is proposed to be the rate-limiting step for assembling functional complexes I/III/IV/V, so increased pyruvate and anaplerotic carbon entry cannot be matched by terminal oxidation and is instead routed through citrate export and the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification program toward neutral-lipid storage, with glycolytic and antioxidant transcripts rising as secondary compensation. This is a proposed, not established, causal chain.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assay: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, blue-native PAGE/in-gel activity plus immunoblot should show a lower ratio of assembled complex I/IV (and of mtDNA-encoded MT-CO1/MT-ND1 protein) to nuclear-encoded subunit protein (NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) in APOE4. If mtDNA-encoded subunit protein and assembled complex scale proportionally with the elevated nuclear-encoded subunits, the proposed bottleneck is refuted.", "Respirometry: APOE4 should show no increase (or a decrease) in maximal and spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass despite the up-regulated nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, with higher extracellular acidification. Proportionally increased maximal respiration in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism and favour simple mitochondrial biogenesis.", "13C6-glucose (and 13C5-glutamine) tracing: APOE4 should show greater M+2 label incorporation into palmitate, triacylglycerol and cholesteryl esters and a higher citrate/lipid label ratio with unchanged or reduced label release as CO2, relative to APOE3. Equal or lower lipid labelling in APOE4 would falsify the citrate-export-to-lipid route.", "Perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of citrate export (SLC25A1) or of cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation (ACLY) should reduce neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content preferentially in APOE4, without correcting the mitonuclear subunit ratio. No genotype-selective reduction in lipid content would weaken step 5.", "Rescue perturbation: restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit supply or mitochondrial translation capacity (e.g. increasing mtDNA copy number/TFAM, or NAD+ repletion) should raise assembled complex levels and lower citrate export and lipid-droplet load in APOE4 toward APOE3. Persistence of the lipid phenotype after respiratory-complex assembly is normalized would refute the causal ordering.", "Negative prediction for the assigned focus: APOE4 microglia should not show a selective peroxisomal or global oxidative-stress signature (peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux, catalase activity, and protein-carbonyl/4-HNE levels approximately unchanged). A strong, coherent peroxisomal/oxidative-damage phenotype would favour an alternative redox-primary mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia up-regulate the entire detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit/assembly-factor set (40/40 rows positive, e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:COA8) and nuclear-encoded mitochondrial translation/RNA-processing factors (gene:TUFM, gene:GFM2, gene:MTPAP), indicating increased transcriptional demand for respiratory-chain biogenesis (measured abundance only).", "The mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts that are present in the same list are mostly reduced (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2), giving a mitonuclear discordance; we infer, but did not measure, that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits becomes the assembly bottleneck for complexes I, III, IV and V.", "Carbon entry and anaplerosis transcripts rise in parallel (gene:MPC2 pyruvate carrier, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3G, gene:GOT1, gene:MDH1), so pyruvate/glutamate-derived carbon and cytosolic reducing equivalents are inferred to be delivered to a mitochondrion whose terminal electron flux is capped.", "A capped respiratory flux is inferred to raise the mitochondrial NADH/NAD+ ratio and inhibit the NAD+-dependent dehydrogenase steps (IDH3, OGDH) at the activity level despite their higher transcript abundance, causing citrate to accumulate and to be exported through the up-regulated citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1); the citrate, acetyl-CoA and NADH pools themselves were not measured.", "Exported citrate is inferred to feed cytosolic acetyl-CoA (ACLY was not measured in this dataset) into a coordinately induced lipogenic/esterification program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) together with increased lipid uptake and lysosomal lipid hydrolysis capacity (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB), biasing lipid flux toward triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage rather than oxidation.", "Compensatory responses accompany the capped oxidation: a glycolytic/hypoxia-like transcript shift (gene:HIF1A, gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) and modest reductive/peroxide-handling capacity transcripts (gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4; ambiguous catalase-containing protein_spot:017), which we interpret as secondary buffering rather than as the primary lesion."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch in APOE4 microglia diverts TCA carbon to citrate export and lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3066154781203134, "cosine_similarity": 0.4065756857372596, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5926537216828479, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3066154781203134, "cosine_similarity": 0.4065756857372596, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5926537216828479, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84839675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 77}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_034", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for carrier/enzyme abundance and for capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite, flux or complex-assembly measurement is supplied, so every flux and localisation statement is inferred.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong upward baseline (77.1% positive, median +1.46), so set-level conclusions are drawn only from comparison against that internal background, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are treated as ranks/directions, not as literal fold changes.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels from a probe-based 10X Flex assay are assumed to reflect mitochondrial transcript content; if probe coverage or QC filtering distorts them, step 4 loses its main support (only 6 mt genes are present).", "Protein spots have several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid substrate supply and part of the transcriptional state may be non-cell-autonomous.", "Genotype-associated co-expression is assumed to reflect a within-cell metabolic programme; causality has not been established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional program that favours mitochondrial pyruvate entry and first-span TCA turnover while terminal oxidation capacity is stoichiometrically constrained (nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts uniformly raised, mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts shifted down). The primary bottleneck we propose is the citrate/2-oxoglutarate export node (SLC25A1/SLC25A11): carbon entering the cycle is predicted to leave as citrate for cytosolic acetyl-CoA and SREBP-driven sterol/fatty-acid esterification rather than be completely oxidised to CO2, generating the esterified-lipid and lysosomal-storage phenotype. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances are measured; flux, enzyme activity, complex assembly and causal direction are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with uniformly labelled 13C6-glucose, APOE4 microglia should show higher fractional M+2 citrate and higher 13C incorporation into cholesterol and fatty acids than isogenic APOE3, with no increase (or a decrease) in glucose-derived 13CO2 and in M+2 -\u003e M+4 cycling of downstream TCA intermediates. If APOE4 instead shows increased glucose-derived CO2 and unchanged lipid labelling, the bottleneck placement (steps 4-6) is wrong.", "SLC25A1 blockade (CTPI-2 or knockdown) should selectively reduce neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; persistence of APOE4 lipid excess under effective SLC25A1 inhibition weakens the proposed bottleneck.", "Mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) should lower glucose-derived lipid labelling and raise lactate output specifically in APOE4; a glycolysis-driven alternative predicts no reduction in lipid labelling, so this result discriminates between the models.", "Respirometry plus blue-native analysis should show that APOE4 maximal uncoupled oxygen consumption per unit mitochondrial mass is not increased in proportion to the nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise, with reduced assembled complex I/IV relative to nuclear subunit content and reduced mtDNA copy number or mt-encoded protein; if maximal respiration and assembled complexes scale with the nuclear subunit increase, step 4 fails and the mechanism should be revised to an oxidative-capacity gain.", "Overall falsifier: if measured cytosolic acetyl-CoA, citrate and sterol-synthesis flux are unchanged in APOE4 despite the transcript pattern, or if ACLY/ACSS2 inhibition does not attenuate the APOE4 lipid excess, the hypothesis is rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, incoherent glycolysis): APOE4 does not show a coherent glycolytic commitment - HK2 and PFKP transcripts are strongly lower while glucose transporters (SLC2A1, SLC2A3) and mid-pathway ENO1 are higher; we infer that upper-glycolytic capacity is not the driver and that cytosolic pyruvate is not preferentially shunted to lactate.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): higher MPC2, PDP1 and DLD transcripts, together with raised malate-aspartate shuttle components (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11), are inferred to increase pyruvate import and PDH-directed acetyl-CoA formation and to reoxidise cytosolic NADH mitochondrially rather than by lactate dehydrogenase.", "Step 3 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): uniformly higher first-span TCA transcripts (ACO2, IDH3G, OGDH, SDHB) are inferred to raise citrate and 2-oxoglutarate production from the imported carbon.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, inferred): terminal oxidation is proposed to be assembly-limited rather than expression-limited - 38/38 detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts are up (e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5ME) while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are shifted down, so respiratory-chain flux per unit of matrix dehydrogenase capacity is predicted not to rise proportionally; carbon therefore accumulates as citrate.", "Step 5 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): higher SLC25A1 transcript is inferred to increase citrate export; together with ACSS2 this is predicted to raise the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool (this pool is inferred, not measured).", "Step 6 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred phenotype): the SREBP programme (SREBF1, SCD, HMGCS1, DHCR24) plus esterification enzymes (SOAT1, DGAT1) and lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1) are predicted to convert that acetyl-CoA and imported lipid into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol; the parallel rise in TFEB, CTSB and GBA is interpreted as a lysosomal-storage response to this lipid load rather than as its cause."], "title": "Citrate-export bottleneck: APOE4 microglia route glucose carbon through mitochondria into lipogenesis instead of complete oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12188457704094818, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30627808674978824, "cosine_similarity": 0.40649386033550683, "direction_accuracy": 0.15372168284789645, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5916893203883495, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12188457704094818, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30627808674978824, "cosine_similarity": 0.40649386033550683, "direction_accuracy": 0.15372168284789645, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5916893203883495, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.52720475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 78}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_062", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment claims are therefore made against the internal distribution of these rows (mean +1.388, median +1.459, 77.1% positive) and not against a whole-transcriptome background.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes such as +8 to +15 are treated as rank/direction information only, not as literal fold changes.", "Protein spot effects equal log2 of the reported 2D-gel fold change; each spot carries several candidate genes, so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no hydrolase protein pool is claimed as measured.", "RNA (10X Flex, day 30) and the 2D-gel spot data are assumed to interrogate a comparable APOE4-versus-APOE3 state; if they come from different samples or timepoints the RNA/protein discordance used for the bottleneck is uninformative.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal may derive from non-microglial RNA or ambient contamination.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an upper bound on, not a measurement of, enzyme activity, lysosomal acidification, cargo flux, lipid localisation or export."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 elevates transcripts for lipid-cargo receptors (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, MERTK, CLEC7A) and for the TFEB/MITF CLEAR program (v-ATPase subunits, cathepsins, GAA/GBA/HEXA/SMPD1/NAGLU), while the matched 2D-gel protein spots containing lysosomal-hydrolase candidates are not concordantly increased and several are decreased; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is luminal hydrolytic throughput on sphingolipid/glycolipid-rich internalised cargo, so that lysosomal load persists, TFEB/MITF signalling is sustained, and liberated sterol and fatty acid are diverted to esterification/storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, ACAT2, SCD) rather than cleared. The assigned sterol-synthesis/export focus is rejected as primary: the sterol-synthesis set is not enriched above the strong global positive shift (mean 2.05 vs global 1.39, permutation p_up=0.21) and the sterol egress/efflux arm (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN, ASAH1) is absent from the supplied rows, i.e. unmeasured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Capacity test: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, per-lysosome specific activity of acid sphingomyelinase, GBA and beta-hexosaminidase (fluorogenic substrate assay normalised to LAMP1 or lysosome number) will be equal or lower despite the higher transcripts, with increased LysoTracker/LAMP1 area and increased undegraded substrate (BODIPY-sphingomyelin or LacCer, plus filipin sterol) per cell. Proportionally increased activity with no substrate accumulation would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: reducing cargo influx in APOE4 (SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade, or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should lower accumulated lysosomal lipid substrate and bring TFEB/MITF and CLEAR-target transcripts (ATP6V1H, GBA, SMPD1, CTSB) down toward APOE3 values, with little effect in APOE3. If CLEAR transcripts stay elevated in APOE4 after uptake blockade, the load-driven bottleneck is wrong and cell-autonomous TFEB/mTORC1 dysregulation is favoured.", "Bottleneck-placement test: boosting luminal hydrolysis (recombinant acid sphingomyelinase or a GBA chaperone, or restoring acidification with acidic nanoparticles) should reduce lipid accumulation and lower SOAT1/DGAT1-associated neutral-lipid droplet content in APOE4, whereas an egress-directed intervention (cyclodextrin) should not be required. Rescue by cyclodextrin alone with no benefit from hydrolase boosting would relocate the bottleneck from hydrolysis to sterol egress.", "Sterol-focus rejection test: sterol synthesis flux measured directly (13C-acetate or D2O incorporation into sterols) and SREBP-2 target enzymes not in the supplied rows (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1) will not be significantly higher in APOE4, and statin treatment will not normalise the lysosomal or inflammatory phenotype. Strong induction of these enzymes with statin rescue would overturn this hypothesis in favour of a sterol-synthesis/export mechanism.", "Protein-layer confirmation: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS for CTSD, CTSB, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 will show that protein levels rise far less than the corresponding transcripts (or fall), resolving the ambiguous spots. Concordant large protein increases matching the transcript changes would weaken the throughput-ceiling step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein and phagocytic receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22 at the 99.1st percentile of the supplied rows, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CLEC7A, gene:APOE). Inferred (not measured): higher delivery flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Measured: coordinate elevation of gene:TFEB and gene:MITF and of CLEAR-network targets - all ten supplied v-ATPase subunits positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51) and glycosidase/sphingolipidase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU; set mean 3.92 vs global 1.39, permutation p_up=0.002). Inferred: a compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis response to cargo load, not proof of increased degradative flux.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred): luminal hydrolytic throughput per lysosome fails to scale with cargo influx. Counter-scaling evidence at the protein layer: spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase average +0.13 log2 versus +0.44 for other spots, and significant decreases occur in protein_spot:058, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 (candidate lists include CTSD, CTSB, HEXB, ATP6V1E1); spot identities are ambiguous, so this is capacity-limiting evidence, not identification.", "Inferred consequence: undegraded sphingolipid/glycolipid and associated sterol accumulate in the lysosomal lumen. No lipid, filipin, activity or localisation measurement is supplied, and the canonical egress machinery (NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, ASAH1, ABCA1/ABCG1) is not present in the supplied rows; gene:NPC2 (+1.17) and gene:IDS (-1.56) sit at or below the global centre, so the egress/co-factor arm shows no compensatory scaling.", "Measured overflow route: esterification and storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67). Inferred: sterol and fatty acid liberated or trapped in the endolysosome are re-esterified into neutral lipid rather than exported.", "Inferred read-out state: sustained lysosomal load maintains TFEB/MITF drive and an inflammatory/complement transcript tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB), producing the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference under mock treatment. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia hit a lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolism throughput ceiling: cargo uptake and CLEAR-network transcription rise, degradative capacity does not, and lipid is shunted into esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19944326927860076, "cosine_similarity": 0.40602419918556665, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140453074433657, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19944326927860076, "cosine_similarity": 0.40602419918556665, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140453074433657, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.58526225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 79}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_065", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (minimum |effect| = 1.00, 77% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are therefore made only relative to that biased background, and the absolute magnitude of any single gene is treated ordinally.", "Higher transcript abundance for hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and SREBP targets reflects higher biosynthetic demand and, for the SREBP set, ongoing SREBP-2/SREBP-1 processing; neither enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, SREBP cleavage nor sterol flux was measured.", "TFEB and MITF transcript increases are used as a marker of a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal-biogenesis response; MiT/TFE activity is set by nuclear localisation and phosphorylation, which are unmeasured.", "Protein spots are non-uniquely assigned (3-6 candidate genes each, with actin and keratin recurring as likely co-migrating or contaminating species); spot-level changes are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only and never as identified proteins.", "Genes absent from the list (for example NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, HSPA5, XBP1) are assumed to be non-selected rather than proven unchanged; their status is unknown.", "Astrocyte co-culture and multiplexed 10X Flex capture could contribute ambient or cross-cell-type RNA; the isogenic design is assumed to control for genetic background other than APOE.", "No lipid, flux, imaging or replicate-level data are supplied, so all lipid-pool statements are predictions, not observations."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling rather than in ER unfolded-protein signalling: transcripts for lysosomal glyco-/sphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, SGSH, MAN2B1), cathepsins, v-ATPase subunits and the MiT/TFE factors TFEB/MITF are coordinately higher, while SREBP-pathway transcripts for sterol synthesis, lipid uptake and neutral-lipid esterification (SREBF1/2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, LDLR, INSIG1, SCD, ACAT2, ACSS2, SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1) are also uniformly higher. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is egress of lysosome-derived sterol and sphingolipid catabolites to the ER sensing pool, so that catabolic capacity is transcriptionally expanded but flux is limiting, ER sterol sensing continues to read 'low', and carbon is re-routed into esterified neutral lipid. Causality is not established by these data; the abundance changes are measured, the flux, localisation and direction are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely bypass the proposed egress bottleneck by delivering sterol directly to the ER pool (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or exogenous 25-hydroxycholesterol acting on INSIG/SCAP) in APOE4 microglia. The mechanism predicts that this suppresses SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) at least as strongly in APOE4 as in APOE3 and simultaneously lowers lysosomal filipin/LysoTracker signal and the TFEB-linked hydrolase transcripts. If cyclodextrin normalises lysosomal lipid staining but SREBP targets stay elevated in APOE4, the sensing link (Step 4) is wrong; if neither changes, the bottleneck is not lysosomal egress.", "Reverse-direction test: block sterol/fatty-acid synthesis (statin or fatostatin) in APOE4 microglia. The mechanism predicts the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation and lysosomal glycosphingolipid load persist (they are compensatory, downstream of the bottleneck). If statin abolishes the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal difference, then de novo lipogenesis, not lysosomal egress, is primary and this hypothesis is falsified.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts while worsening, not improving, lysosomal lipid accumulation; improvement of lipid load after TFEB knockdown would contradict the compensatory interpretation of Step 3.", "Lipidomics/imaging: APOE4 microglia should show higher glucosylceramide, hexosylceramide and sphingomyelin plus higher cholesteryl ester and neutral-lipid droplet content than isogenic APOE3 under mock. Equal or lower levels of these species would weaken the mechanism substantially.", "Enzyme-activity assays (GBA, HEXA/B, acid sphingomyelinase) and cathepsin maturation blots should show that the transcript increase is not matched by a proportional increase in specific activity or mature enzyme. A proportional increase in activity with no lipid accumulation would falsify the bottleneck.", "Rejection test for the assigned ER-proteostasis focus: if APOE4 microglia show clear XBP1 splicing, HSPA5/GRP78 induction, ATF4/CHOP protein induction and thapsigargin hypersensitivity, then a UPR-centred mechanism should replace this one. The supplied data predict no coherent UPR difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, upstream): APOE4 protein, which is produced by these microglia (gene:APOE higher), binds and delivers lipid less efficiently than APOE3, so lipid entering via receptor- and scavenger-mediated routes (gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7 higher) reaches the endolysosome in a form that is cleared more slowly. This step is not directly measured here.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred flux): Hydrolysis and, critically, export of lysosomal cholesterol and glycosphingolipid catabolites to the ER/plasma-membrane pools becomes rate-limiting in APOE4, so substrate dwell time inside the lysosome increases even though hydrolase transcript levels rise.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A MiT/TFE-type compensatory response is engaged - TFEB and MITF transcripts are higher together with acid hydrolase (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, SGSH, MAN2B1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, CTSH), membrane (LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2) and v-ATPase (ATP6V1A, ATP6V0D1, ATP6V1E1, ATP6AP1) transcripts. Increased transcript abundance is taken as increased biosynthetic demand, not as demonstrated enzymatic activity or acidification.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): Because lysosome-derived sterol does not adequately reach the ER SCAP/INSIG sensor, SREBP processing is not switched off; SREBF1/SREBF2 and their sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis targets (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, SCD, FADS1, ACAT2, ACSS2) plus the SREBP-induced feedback gene INSIG1 and the uptake receptor LDLR remain higher in APOE4. Synthesis flux itself is not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred product): Excess free sterol and fatty acid are buffered by esterification and glycerolipid assembly (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1 higher), which we predict manifests as increased cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol-rich droplets plus retained lysosomal glycosphingolipid. No lipid species were measured in the supplied data.", "Step 6 (consequence, inferred): The combination of expanded endolysosomal compartment traffic (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3 higher) and neutral-lipid storage produces a lipid-laden, partially foamy microglial state that would be expected to blunt further phagocytic lipid handling; this functional consequence is untested here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia carry a lysosomal lipid-egress bottleneck: a MiT/TFE-type hydrolase and v-ATPase program runs in parallel with an unsuppressed SREBP sterol/lipogenic program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25390466344201157, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20138674045516208, "cosine_similarity": 0.40569259622540327, "direction_accuracy": 0.33495145631067963, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6114077669902913, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25390466344201157, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20138674045516208, "cosine_similarity": 0.40569259622540327, "direction_accuracy": 0.33495145631067963, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6114077669902913, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84305225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 80}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_164", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level statements are made only relative to the internal background of this list (median +1.46, 77.1% positive), not to a genome-wide null.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and ranks relative to the list background are interpreted, not absolute fold changes.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein abundance and none of it is a measure of enzyme activity, flux, membrane potential, assembly state or metabolite pool size; no respiration, ATP, mtDNA copy number, or metabolite measurement is supplied.", "The decrease in mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to reflect a real difference in mitochondrial transcript/protein supply rather than a normalisation, ambient-RNA, probe-set or cell-quality artefact of the 10X Flex pseudobulk comparison.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no OXPHOS subunit spot is present, so protein-level support for the bottleneck itself is absent.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to differ systematically between genotypes in a way that alone produces the microglial transcript pattern; genotype-specific astrocyte substrate supply is an untested alternative.", "Causality is assumed only as a hypothesis: APOE4 genotype is the experimental variable, but no intervention in these data establishes that any step causes another."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the primary bottleneck is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core OXPHOS subunits (transcripts for MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are lower in APOE4) relative to a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit program (39/39 detected NDUF/UQCR/COX/ATP5/CYCS/SDHB transcripts higher, median +2.6 versus a +1.46 dataset-wide median). We hypothesise that this imbalance limits assembly of proton-pumping and ATP-synthesising complexes, so that APOE4 microglia sustain or increase mitochondrial carbon uptake (MPC2, PDP1, GLS/GLUD1, malate-aspartate shuttle transcripts) but convert less of that carbon into coupled ATP, instead exporting citrate (SLC25A1) toward lipid esterification (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1) and diverting glucose carbon to serine/one-carbon (PSPH, SHMT1/2) and glycogen (GYS1, UGP2) rather than to a compensatory glycolytic ATP flux, with a DELE1/ISR-type transcriptional response (DELE1, DDIT3, EIF2AK3) and antioxidant transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, NNT, GPX4) as downstream consequences. All statements about assembly, flux, coupling and causal direction are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction: in extracellular-flux assays of mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, the oligomycin-sensitive (ATP-linked) fraction of oxygen consumption will be reduced in APOE4 by a larger margin than basal or FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration, i.e. reduced coupling efficiency, with no compensatory rise in post-oligomycin glycolytic acidification (reduced glycolytic reserve). If APOE4 shows equal or greater ATP-linked respiration and coupling efficiency, or a clear compensatory glycolytic increase, the mechanism is weakened.", "Blue-native PAGE and complex-in-gel activity will show reduced fully assembled complex V (and reduced complex I/III2/IV supercomplex) with a relative excess of free F1 sub-complex in APOE4; metabolic labelling of mitochondrial translation (35S or puromycin/anti-ATP6) will show reduced synthesis of ATP6/COX2/CYB relative to nuclear-encoded ATP5F1B protein. Normal complex V assembly and normal mt-translation rates in APOE4 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Stable-isotope tracing will show, in APOE4, (i) unchanged or increased U-13C-glucose-derived pyruvate entry into TCA intermediates (M+2 citrate) and increased 13C5-glutamine anaplerosis, (ii) increased 13C enrichment of cytosolic citrate-derived products (palmitate, cholesteryl/fatty-acid esters) and of serine/glycine, and (iii) no increase in glucose-to-lactate flux. A Warburg-type pattern (increased lactate labelling, decreased mitochondrial pyruvate entry) would refute step 3-4 and favour a glycolytic-shift mechanism instead.", "Ordering test: ISRIB or HRI/EIF2AK1 knockdown will lower DDIT3, SHMT1/2 and PSPH transcripts in APOE4 without restoring ATP-linked respiration or complex V assembly, whereas increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or mitochondrial-transcription rescue, or allotopic ATP6 expression) will restore coupling and secondarily lower DDIT3. If ISRIB alone restores coupled respiration, the ISR is upstream and the proposed direction is wrong.", "Measurement-artefact control: absolute quantification of MT-ATP6, MT-CO2 and MT-CYB transcripts and of mtDNA copy number per cell (spike-in-normalised RT-qPCR and ddPCR) will confirm a genotype difference in APOE4. If these transcripts and mtDNA copy number are equal between genotypes, the mtDNA-encoded deficit is a normalisation artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "If the bottleneck is real, APOE4 microglia will be selectively vulnerable to oligomycin and to galactose-only medium (forcing oxidative ATP production), showing greater ATP depletion, AMPK activation and reduced phagocytic uptake than APOE3; equal tolerance would weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_164", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred stoichiometry): APOE4 microglia show a coherent increase in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (all 39 detected are positive; complex I set median +2.66, p_MWU=4.5e-4 versus the rest of the list) while the mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are decreased against a strongly upward-shifted background (set median -1.56, p_MWU_less=0.032). We infer, but do not measure, a shortfall of mtDNA-encoded core subunits relative to imported nuclear subunits.", "Step 2 (inferred assembly/activity): The shortfall is proposed to stall late assembly of complexes I, III, IV and especially V (MT-ATP6 shows the largest decrease, -3.35, adjusted p=9.1e-228), leaving nuclear-encoded subunits and sub-complexes in excess and lowering oxygen-coupled, oligomycin-sensitive ATP production per unit substrate oxidised. Assembly state, membrane potential and respiration were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Substrate delivery to mitochondria is not the limiting element: pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating transcripts (MPC2 +7.98, PDP1 +3.00), glutamine anaplerosis (GLS, GLUD1), TCA/shuttle enzymes (OGDH, ACO2, MDH1, GOT1, IDH3B, SDHB) and mitochondrial carriers (SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A1) are all higher in APOE4, consistent with maintained or increased carbon entry into an oxidatively limited matrix.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Carbon is proposed to leave the TCA cycle as citrate (SLC25A1 +4.47) toward desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification (SCD +4.17, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, SCARB1 +8.22), and glucose carbon toward serine/one-carbon (PSPH +3.54, SHMT1 +3.28, SHMT2 +2.22) and glycogen/UDP-glucose (GYS1 +6.10, UGP2 +1.86), rather than into a compensatory glycolytic ATP flux: committed glycolytic and PPP steps are flat or reduced against background (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, PFKFB2 -1.10, PGD -1.30, TALDO1 -2.32; glycolytic set median +0.01 versus background +1.46).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Energetic/proteostatic stress from steps 2-4 is proposed to engage a DELE1-eIF2alpha integrated stress response (DELE1 +4.82, EIF2AK3 +1.51, DDIT3 +2.79, HSPA9 +2.35, PRKAA1 +2.01) and a matrix antioxidant program (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, NNT +2.88, GPX4 +2.79), which reinforces serine/one-carbon transcription and sustains the low-ATP, biosynthesis-biased state.", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): The resulting low coupled-ATP, lipid-esterifying state is predicted to underlie the higher lysosomal/lipid-handling transcript load of APOE4 microglia (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, GAA, TFEB, APOE, TREM2) by limiting ATP-dependent degradative and phagocytic capacity while increasing esterified lipid substrate; this link is speculative and untested here."], "title": "Mito-nuclear OXPHOS stoichiometry imbalance in APOE4 microglia: mtDNA-encoded core subunit deficit caps coupled ATP synthesis and reroutes carbon to citrate export, serine/one-carbon and glycogen synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08904109589041095, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2584713384995119, "cosine_similarity": 0.4054009184910175, "direction_accuracy": 0.14724919093851133, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_164", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5924886731391587, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08904109589041095, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2584713384995119, "cosine_similarity": 0.4054009184910175, "direction_accuracy": 0.14724919093851133, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5924886731391587, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.899197, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 81}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_023", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the internal distribution of that list (mean effect +1.39, 77% positive) and not against a genome-wide background.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks, signs and within-list comparisons are used, never absolute fold-change interpretation.", "Elevated TFEB and MITF transcript abundance is taken as a marker of MiT/TFE pathway engagement, although MiT/TFE control is predominantly post-translational (nuclear translocation), which is not measured here.", "Protein spots are assigned several candidate genes each; spot-level changes are used only as failure-to-corroborate evidence and are never treated as identified cathepsin, hexosaminidase or v-ATPase protein measurements.", "Cargo load, lysosomal pH, organelle number/size, hydrolase enzymatic activity, autophagic flux and lipid content are all unmeasured in the supplied data; every statement about flux, activity, localisation and capacity is inferred.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects measured in the microglial compartment may include non-cell-autonomous contributions.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently checked and pseudoreplication across cells cannot be excluded.", "Background knowledge used to assign genes to endolysosomal, CLEAR, fusion and reformation categories is unverified (literature retrieval was disabled)."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 is associated with a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal degradative module (acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, lysosomal solute carriers, TFEB/MITF) that is not matched by lysosomal-candidate protein-spot abundance, while the transcripts for mannose-6-phosphate-receptor-dependent hydrolase sorting (M6PR), autophagosome-lysosome fusion (STX17) and autophagic lysosome reformation (SPG11) sit low against a strongly up-shifted background. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting bottleneck in APOE4 microglia is terminal cargo delivery to, and fusion with, a competent degradative lysosome - not hydrolase gene transcription - so that the CLEAR-type transcriptional response is a compensatory signature of unmet degradative demand rather than evidence of increased degradative flux. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Cargo pulse-chase: isogenic APOE4 microglia given DQ-BSA, pHrodo-labelled myelin or fluorescently labelled oxidised lipoprotein will internalise cargo at an equal or greater rate than APOE3 but will show a slower per-cell dequenching/degradation rate and greater retention of undegraded cargo in LAMP1-positive compartments at 6-24 h. If APOE4 degrades cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic MiT/TFE activation (Torin1, or TFEB overexpression) will further increase CLEAR transcripts (GAA, HEXA, ATP6V1H) in APOE4 microglia but will NOT normalise the cargo degradation rate, whereas re-expression of STX17 (or forced HOPS/ARL8B-dependent fusion), or lowering cargo load, will. If TFEB activation alone fully restores APOE4 cargo clearance to APOE3 levels, the bottleneck is biosynthetic rather than delivery/fusion and this mechanism is rejected.", "Enzymology versus transcript: measured cathepsin B/D and beta-hexosaminidase specific activity per mg lysate in APOE4 will be at most modestly changed and will not scale with the large transcript increases for GAA, GBA, HEXA and CTSB. If hydrolase specific activity rises in proportion to transcript, the transcript-to-capacity uncoupling claim is weakened.", "Reciprocal knockdown: STX17 or SPG11 knockdown in APOE3 microglia will phenocopy the APOE4 cargo-clearance delay while itself inducing CLEAR transcripts; failure to phenocopy would weaken the assignment of the bottleneck to fusion/reformation.", "Acidification control: ratiometric lysosomal pH measurement will show APOE4 lysosomes are not more alkaline than APOE3 (consistent with elevated v-ATPase transcripts). If APOE4 lysosomes are markedly alkaline and pH rescue alone normalises degradation, an acidification-primary mechanism supersedes this one.", "Specificity control: the mitochondrial oxidative/TCA transcript elevation will not be reversed by relieving the endolysosomal bottleneck if it is an independent module; if blocking cargo delivery in APOE3 reproduces both the CLEAR and the OXPHOS/TCA transcript shifts, the two modules are coupled and the mechanism should be restated with the lysosome upstream."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, not measured here): APOE4 microglia carry a higher steady-state load of internalised lipid/lipoprotein-associated cargo in late endosomes and lysosomes than isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock conditions; no lipid, cargo or organelle measurement is supplied, so this is the untested entry premise.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): a MiT/TFE-type transcriptional program is engaged - TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) - and coordinately raises CLEAR-network transcripts encoding acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1). Transcription factor activity, not just abundance, is inferred.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): lysosomal catabolite-efflux and lumenal transporter transcripts rise in parallel (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC48A1, gene:SLC37A2, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC15A3, gene:SLC66A1), consistent with an attempt to increase throughput of degradation products out of the lumen; efflux flux itself is not measured.", "Step 4 (the proposed bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred capacity): against a background in which 77% of the supplied differential-expression rows are positive, the transcripts for CI-M6PR-dependent hydrolase sorting (gene:M6PR), the autophagosome-lysosome fusion SNARE (gene:STX17), and autophagic lysosome reformation (gene:SPG11) are negative and lie in the bottom ~12-15% of the effect distribution, while the AP-5 complex that acts downstream of SPG11/ZFYVE26 is strongly elevated (gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP5S1). We infer a mismatch in which newly synthesised hydrolases are produced but their receptor-mediated delivery and the fusion/reformation cycle that exposes cargo to them do not scale.", "Step 5 (measured protein spots, non-unique identification): lysosomal-candidate protein spots do not corroborate an increase in degradative protein capacity - spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins or a v-ATPase subunit are inconsistent or decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), unlike the transcript direction. Because each spot has several candidate genes, this is treated as failure to confirm the transcript-level expansion rather than as direct measurement of cathepsin or v-ATPase protein.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): undegraded cargo therefore persists in the late endosome/lysosome compartment of APOE4 microglia despite the enlarged hydrolase transcriptional program, and the coordinately elevated mitochondrial oxidative/TCA transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME) represent either downstream consumption of the catabolites that are still exported or an independent parallel module; the supplied data cannot separate these."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a MiT/TFE-type CLEAR transcriptional expansion while hydrolase delivery and autophagosome/endosome-lysosome fusion remain the limiting step for endolysosomal cargo clearance"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20537174452697105, "cosine_similarity": 0.40502877870450227, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067184466019417, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20537174452697105, "cosine_similarity": 0.40502877870450227, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067184466019417, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73449425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 82}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_061", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list in an unspecified logarithm base with a strong global positive skew (1705/2212 positive, median +1.46); program coherence was judged against that skewed background, and absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, NPC1, PLIN2, LIPA, PSAP, GRN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding uptake receptors, hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits and acyltransferases; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lipid pool or flux measurement is supplied, so uptake rate, degradative flux, sterol routing and localization are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are treated as ambiguous mixtures; all candidate identities are retained and no spot is read as confirmation of an individual protein. Keratins and actins recur as candidates and are treated as likely non-specific.", "SREBP target transcripts remaining elevated is interpreted as the ER-accessible sterol pool not being raised; this interpretation would fail if the SREBP signature instead reflects APOE4 effects on SREBP processing or on cell state independent of sterol sensing.", "The mechanism describes the state present in the supplied mock condition; it does not assert a lysosomal capacity defect. Any shortfall of degradative or storage capacity would be a reserve limitation revealed only by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge, and is not established here.", "Genes within a program are not statistically independent, and descriptive coherence here is not a formal enrichment result; causality has not been established by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (isogenic vs APOE3), the dominant coordinated difference is a lipid-cargo routing state: transcripts for receptor-mediated lipid/lipoprotein/debris internalization (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A/FCGR3A; 14/14 represented members positive) rise together with the largest-magnitude changes in the whole selected list, which fall on lysosomal hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52) plus lysosome-biogenesis/trafficking machinery (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16), while liberated lipid is routed into esterification/neutral-lipid synthesis (gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17) instead of restraining sterol sensing, so the SREBP program remains fully on (12/12 represented members positive: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:MYLIP +1.28). The claim is about coordinated transcriptional routing capacity and its self-reinforcing logic, not about a demonstrated degradative bottleneck: no flux, lipid-pool, pH or activity measurement is supplied, so whether this is successful increased throughput or failing compensation is explicitly undetermined.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show an expanded LAMP1+ compartment together with increased neutral-lipid droplets (BODIPY) and increased esterified/filipin-stainable cholesterol in APOE4. If LAMP1+ compartment volume, droplet content and sterol pools are all indistinguishable between genotypes despite the transcript differences, the routing mechanism is substantially weakened.", "Prospective ACAT/SOAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should redistribute sterol to the ER pool and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS) and lipid-droplet content, with little requirement for change in uptake-receptor transcripts. Persistently elevated SREBP-2 targets after effective ACAT inhibition would falsify the esterification-routing step.", "Prospective flux measurement (DQ-BSA dequenching, live cathepsin B/D activity probes, LysoSensor pH) discriminates the two readings of this state: higher degradative flux with normal acidification in APOE4 supports increased throughput/adaptation, whereas equal or lower flux despite elevated hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts supports a compensatory response to a routing bottleneck. Unchanged hydrolase activity and unchanged compartment size in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism as stated.", "Prospectively limiting substrate entry (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should selectively collapse the APOE4-specific elevation of hydrolase, V-ATPase and TFEB-associated transcripts toward APOE3 levels; if those transcripts remain elevated when cargo influx is blocked, the uptake-driven ordering of the mechanism is wrong and a cargo-independent MiT/TFE or cell-identity driver should be preferred.", "Prospective feeding with myelin or apoptotic-cell cargo should reveal a larger APOE4-versus-APOE3 gap in cargo clearance rate or in droplet accumulation than is seen at baseline; absence of any genotype difference under that challenge would argue the measured transcript differences have no functional consequence for lipid handling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the transcriptional set-point for receptor-mediated internalization of lipoprotein and membrane/debris cargo in microglia (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:ITGB1 all positive), raising the predicted rate of lipid-rich cargo delivery to endolysosomes.", "Delivered cargo is matched by an expanded endolysosomal catabolic and acidification module - hydrolases for glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin, glycogen/glycan and protein cargo (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:MAN2B1) together with V-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, 10/10 represented positive) and MiT/TFE-linked biogenesis and enzyme-delivery machinery (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A).", "Sterol and fatty acid released from this compartment are preferentially re-esterified and stored rather than expanding the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool: acyl-transferase and neutral-lipid/desaturase transcripts increase (gene:ACAT2, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5, gene:FABP3, gene:MGLL) alongside lysosomal sterol handoff components (gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not increased by this routing, SREBP-dependent transcription stays active instead of being switched off by the extra lipid load: every represented SREBP/sterol-synthesis member is positive (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR).", "Continued SREBP output plus elevated uptake-receptor transcripts form a self-reinforcing loop that keeps net lipid entering the esterified/lysosomal pool, which is the state predicted to distinguish APOE4 from APOE3 at day 30 mock; consistent secondary features are the phagocytic/immune-accessory transcripts (gene:CD74 +3.84, gene:CIITA, gene:SIRPA, gene:CD47, gene:C5AR1, gene:CFH) and lipid-laden-microglia markers (gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:APOE, gene:FTH1, gene:CLEC7A, gene:TIMP2, gene:IGF1).", "The proteomic 2-D spot data are compatible but do not confirm any single protein: spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases change in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38), and the strongest increased spot train (protein_spot:043 +1.96, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:047 +0.68) has ANXA1, TALDO1, ACTB and PSMD7 as co-candidates, with ANXA1 the only candidate concordant with RNA (gene:ANXA1 +4.15)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a high-uptake, lysosome-expanded lipid-routing state that diverts sterol into esters and keeps the SREBP synthesis program switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23824386619116272, "cosine_similarity": 0.4049950574953948, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5898478964401295, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23824386619116272, "cosine_similarity": 0.4049950574953948, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5898478964401295, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.958763, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 15}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_084", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all 2212 rows have adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median effect +1.46; 77% positive), so only comparisons made against this internal background - not against zero - are interpreted; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and is left unconverted.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme/carrier protein abundance; no protein, metabolite, flux, membrane-potential, ROS, lipid-droplet, mtDNA-copy-number or respirometry measurement is present in these data, so all activity, flux, assembly and localization statements are inferences.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels are assumed to report mitochondrial genome transcript supply for holocomplex assembly; this assumes the 10X Flex probe panel quantifies mitochondrial transcripts comparably to nuclear ones, which is not verifiable here (unverified background knowledge).", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; spots 038, 072, 039 and 020 are used only as weak, ambiguous protein-level context for glycolytic/pentose enzymes, not as identified proteins.", "The cultures are microglia-astrocyte co-cultures; genotype-associated differences in cell composition or ambient RNA could contribute to the global shift and are not controllable with the supplied data.", "Causality is not established: APOE4 genotype and the metabolic transcript pattern are associated in an isogenic comparison, but no intervention is present in this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally commit carbon away from committed glycolysis/pentose-phosphate steps and toward mitochondrial pyruvate and glutamate oxidation (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, OGDH, MDH1, GOT1, GLUD1, SLC25A11/A1/A5) while simultaneously raising nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunit transcripts; because the mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are not co-elevated and are reduced relative to the measured background, assembly of complexes I/III/IV/V, not substrate supply, becomes the rate-limiting step. The predicted consequence is an assembly-limited, reducing-pressure-prone mitochondrion whose surplus TCA carbon exits as citrate (SLC25A1) into an activated lipogenic/sterol program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DGAT1), accompanied by uncoupling and antioxidant transcript induction (UCP2, NNT, PRDX3, GPX4). All statements about flux, assembly, redox state and lipid pools are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test 1 (bottleneck location): BN-PAGE/in-gel activity plus respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20) in APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show APOE4 with equal or LOWER assembled complex I/III/IV/V and maximal (FCCP) oxygen consumption per mitochondrion despite HIGHER nuclear-encoded subunit protein, i.e. an increased unassembled/free nuclear subunit pool. If APOE4 instead shows assembled complexes and uncoupled respiration rising in proportion to the nuclear subunit increase, the mitonuclear-assembly bottleneck is falsified and the pattern should be reinterpreted as coordinated mitochondrial biogenesis.", "Discriminating test 2 (carbon routing): U-13C-glucose and 13C-glutamine tracing should show APOE4 with higher M+2 citrate enrichment and higher 13C incorporation into palmitate/cholesterol, and a lower fraction of glucose carbon released as lactate, than APOE3. Higher glucose-to-lactate flux in APOE4 would falsify the substrate-reallocation step.", "Discriminating test 3 (targeted perturbation): MPC inhibition (UK5099) or SLC25A1/ACLY inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid accumulation and mitochondrial superoxide (MitoSOX) selectively in APOE4, with little effect in APOE3; equal or larger effects in APOE3 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating test 4 (rescue at the proposed bottleneck): raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression, or restoring mtDNA copy number) should increase assembled complex I/IV and maximal respiration more in APOE4 than APOE3 and lower the lipogenic/UCP2/PRDX3 signature; no genotype-selective rescue would weaken the mechanism.", "Direct measurement check: qPCR/ddPCR of mtDNA copy number and of MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2, MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L should confirm reduced mtDNA-encoded transcript per mtDNA copy in APOE4. Equal mtDNA transcript levels across genotypes by an orthogonal assay would attribute the observed MT- decreases to probe-panel or normalisation artefact and falsify step 3.", "Internal counter-evidence to be resolved: MT-ND5 (+1.93) and MT-ND4L (+1.95) move opposite to MT-ND4/MT-CYB/MT-ATP6/MT-CO2 although they arise from the same heavy-strand polycistron; if orthogonal assays show uniform mtDNA transcript levels, the bottleneck should be relocated to nuclear-subunit import/assembly or rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for mitochondrial carbon entry and matrix oxidation - MPC2 (+7.98), DLD (+5.54), PDP1 (+3.00, the PDH-activating phosphatase; no PDK transcript is present in the supplied rows), OGDH (+8.56), MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), ACO2 (+3.54), IDH3G/IDH3B, plus GLUD1 (+3.17), GLS and SLC1A5 - while committed glycolytic and pentose-phosphate steps are reduced against the same background (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, PFKFB2 -1.10, HK3 -1.12, TALDO1 -2.32, PGD -1.30) despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (SLC2A3 +3.73, SLC2A1 +2.37). Inference: carbon is routed into the matrix rather than to lactate/NADPH-generating branches.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcripts are coherently elevated relative to the differential-expression background (38 NDUF*/COX*/UQCR*/ATP5*/SDHB/CYCS genes, mean background percentile 0.68, permutation p\u003c2e-5), together with import and assembly transcripts (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM8B, COX20, COA8, COA1, NDUFAF4) and adenine-nucleotide/metabolite carriers (SLC25A5 +5.56, SLC25A11 +4.51, SLC25A1 +4.50).", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred assembly): mtDNA-encoded core subunits do not follow - MT-ATP6 -3.35 (padj 9.1e-228), MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33 (mean background percentile 0.28, permutation p=0.032). Because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, we infer that assembled holocomplex number per mitochondrion, not nuclear subunit supply or substrate supply, limits respiratory capacity in APOE4.", "Step 4 (inferred): with matrix dehydrogenase capacity raised but electron-transfer capacity capped, matrix reducing pressure and membrane-potential-linked electron leak rise. Consistent transcript responses are UCP2 (+2.38, padj 2.7e-80), NNT (+2.88), PRDX3 (+3.49), PRDX5 (+1.96), GPX4 (+2.79), TSPO (+1.41), and a mild integrated-stress signature (DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2AK3 +1.51, ATF6 +4.00).", "Step 5 (inferred flux, measured RNA): carbon that cannot be fully oxidised is exported as citrate through SLC25A1 (+4.50) and fed to a raised lipogenic/sterol program (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, INSIG1 +1.87, DGAT1 +1.72, HMGCS1 +1.08), providing a metabolic route to the APOE4 lipid-storage phenotype.", "Step 6 (inferred, secondary): the resulting esterified-lipid and sterol load engages lysosomal/degradative capacity (GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1A +4.23, TFEB +2.38, GAA +9.98, SCARB1 +8.21, ABCA7 +2.14), which we treat as a downstream consequence of the bottleneck rather than its cause."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry bottleneck: APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial carbon import and nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain expression without matched mtDNA-encoded core subunits, diverting TCA carbon to citrate export and lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30596632823566366, "cosine_similarity": 0.40445087827664017, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5941003236245954, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30596632823566366, "cosine_similarity": 0.40445087827664017, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5941003236245954, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.796865, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 83}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_146", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (for example ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, IL1B, STAT1) means not present in this selected list and NOT that it is unchanged.", "The reported RNA log fold changes have an unspecified logarithm base; we use sign, rank and relative magnitude only, never absolute fold change. In this dataset |log fold change| is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p value (Spearman -0.03), so we weight the highly significant, modest-effect genes most.", "The whole selected RNA list is shifted upward (median +1.46, 77 percent positive), so coordinated upregulation of any module is only meaningful relative to that background; we tested modules against a permutation null drawn from the list itself.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used to assert that a named protein changed.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for enzyme activity, degradative flux, subcellular localization or lipid content. No lipid, cholesterol, filipin, droplet or enzyme-activity measurement is present in these files.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid cargo supply is partly non-cell-autonomous and the APOE4 genotype may act in either or both compartments.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so no independent assessment of the reported p values is possible; causal direction is assumed, not demonstrated."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from isogenic APOE3 primarily by a rate limitation in exporting cholesterol and sphingolipid out of the endolysosome after hydrolysis. The discovery data show coordinated transcript elevation of lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors, of essentially the entire lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase module, and of the TFEB/MITF CLEAR regulators, together with SOAT1 and sterol-synthesis/SREBP-target transcripts. We interpret this as a compensatory transcriptional response to a lysosomal lipid load that the cell cannot discharge, with the ER sterol sensor still reading 'low' because the sterol is sequestered. A canonical type I interferon programme is absent from these differential-expression results and the inflammatory changes are confined to sensor/adaptor transcripts without effector cytokine transcripts, so inflammatory or interferon signalling is treated as a downstream, secondary correlate rather than the primary bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Relieving lysosomal cholesterol egress pharmacologically (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or an LXR agonist to raise export capacity) in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal and neutral-lipid content (filipin, LipidSpot, LC-MS cholesteryl esters) toward APOE3 levels AND collapse the CLEAR/hydrolase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, TFEB, GPNMB) within 48-72 h, without requiring any change in TLR2/MYD88/CD14. If lipid load falls but the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation persists unchanged, step 2 is not downstream of the lipid load and the mechanism is weakened.", "SEPARATING HYDROLYSIS FROM EGRESS: Per-cell lysosomal hydrolase activity assays (Magic Red cathepsin B, DQ-BSA dequenching, 4-MU-based GBA/HEXB/GAA activity) should be equal to or higher in APOE4 than APOE3 while unesterified cholesterol accumulates in LAMP1-positive compartments. If hydrolase activity is instead reduced in APOE4 despite elevated transcripts, the bottleneck is hydrolysis rather than egress and step 3 must be replaced.", "STORAGE ARM: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should shift the pool from cholesteryl-ester droplets to unesterified cholesterol without reducing total sterol, and should not normalize the CLEAR transcript programme. If SOAT1 inhibition normalizes total cellular sterol, storage is not merely a terminal sink.", "INFLAMMATION IS SECONDARY: MYD88 or IRAK4 inhibition, or TLR2 blockade, under mock conditions should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal and neutral-lipid difference intact. If blocking MYD88/IRAK4 abolishes the lipid difference, inflammatory signalling is upstream and this hypothesis is wrong.", "INTERFERON REJECTED: Direct assay of a type I interferon module (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1 phosphorylation, secreted IFN-beta) should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference under mock treatment, consistent with zero canonical interferon-stimulated genes appearing in these differential-expression results. Detection of a clear constitutive ISG signature in APOE4 would show that the assigned interferon focus was wrongly rejected.", "GENOTYPE SPECIFICITY: Isogenic conversion of APOE4 back to APOE3, or APOE knockout in the APOE4 line, should reduce lysosomal cholesterol and the CLEAR transcript programme. If APOE knockout in APOE4 does not reduce the lipid load, the effect is not mediated through the APOE protein product.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL FOR THE GLOBAL SHIFT: In a matched unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement, the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module should still sit above the genome-wide APOE4-versus-APOE3 mean. If it does not, the module coherence reported here is an artefact of the selected gene list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_146", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein and lipid uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7) and for the ligand gene:APOE. We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery flux of cholesterol- and phospholipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred activity): The luminal acid-hydrolase module (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:AGA, gene:NPC2, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK) and every measured v-ATPase subunit (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1) are elevated, with the CLEAR regulators gene:TFEB and gene:MITF and the lysosomal-stress marker gene:GPNMB. Transcript abundance is not enzyme activity or degradative flux; we read this as a compensatory biogenesis response, not as proof of faster digestion.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred, not directly measured): The rate-limiting step is post-hydrolytic egress of free cholesterol and sphingolipid from the lysosomal lumen to the ER and plasma membrane, and its APOE-dependent export from the cell. Elevated hydrolase and acidification transcripts alongside a persistent stress marker (gene:GPNMB) and elevated gene:NPC2 and gene:RAB7A are consistent with demand exceeding egress capacity rather than with a hydrolytic-enzyme deficit.", "Step 4 (feed-forward loop, inferred): Sequestration of sterol inside the lysosome keeps ER sterol sensing in the depleted state, sustaining SREBP-2-type output (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1) and therefore continued uptake; gene:MYLIP elevation indicates the counter-regulatory arm is engaged but insufficient.", "Step 5 (lipid disposal into storage, inferred): Free cholesterol that does reach the ER is diverted to cholesteryl esters by elevated gene:SOAT1, while gene:SREBF1 and gene:SCD supply monounsaturated acyl chains and gene:FABP5 is elevated, predicting neutral-lipid droplet accumulation as the terminal sink in APOE4.", "Step 6 (secondary, not the driver): The chronic lipid-laden lysosomal state accompanies sensor-level priming (gene:TLR2, gene:TLR6, gene:TIRAP, gene:MYD88, gene:IRAK4, gene:CD14, gene:CLEC7A, gene:NLRP3) and some chemokine transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2), but no canonical interferon-stimulated genes appear among these differential-expression results, gene:TNFAIP3 is lower and gene:ANXA1 is strongly higher. We place inflammatory tone downstream of, or parallel to, the lipid bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at post-hydrolytic lysosomal lipid egress, not at interferon or NF-kB signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11154598825831702, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22253098206807315, "cosine_similarity": 0.40405947295700223, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_146", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5899805825242719, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11154598825831702, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22253098206807315, "cosine_similarity": 0.40405947295700223, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5899805825242719, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.00606325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 84}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_023", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 positive vs 507 negative), so 'up' is judged against a ~77% positive background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is used only for sign and rank, not fold-size.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for compartment capacity; hydrolase activity, luminal pH, cholesterol egress, autophagic and degradative flux, lipid-droplet content and SREBP-2 proteolytic processing were not measured, so 'ER sterol-poor sensing' is inferred from target-gene direction only.", "2D-gel protein spots are multi-candidate (median 5 candidate genes; KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate as likely co-migrating contaminants), so no spot is treated as identification of one protein; spot changes are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "Members of each program were chosen from standard pathway/complex definitions written before looking at effect signs (full V-ATPase complex, full CLEAR/hydrolase list, full mevalonate-to-cholesterol list, etc.); represented-versus-queried counts are reported so that non-represented members are visible and direction was not used to select membership.", "The comparison is a single genotype contrast at one timepoint with replicate structure not supplied and genes not independent (shared regulons), so binomial sign statistics are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test.", "Effects observed here are those of the mock (unchallenged) condition; any reduced spare capacity or overt cargo backlog is an expectation for a future cargo challenge, not something the supplied data demonstrate."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated cell-state change in which transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors, MiT/TFE-driven lysosomal biogenesis (TFEB, MITF, V-ATPase subunits, acid hydrolases, lysosomal membrane transporters) and endosomal maturation/ESCRT machinery are jointly higher than APOE3, while the SREBP-2 sterol-synthesis module (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, INSIG1) and esterification/lipogenesis genes (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1, SCD) are also higher. We propose that in APOE4 cells sterol arriving in or generated within the endolysosomal compartment is inefficiently handed off to the ER regulatory pool, so the cell simultaneously expands degradative/storage capacity and keeps sterol synthesis and uptake switched on; this routing/sensing mismatch, supported by a fuel shift toward mitochondrial oxidation (OGDH, MDH1, MPC2, ETC subunits up; HK2, PFKP down), is the primary transcriptional difference, and it occurs without an inflammatory or DAM-like identity switch (inflammatory genes sit at the selected-list background; homeostatic identity genes CSF1R, MEF2C, MAFB, IRF8, GPR34 are up, not down). Measured effects are transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances; no flux, activity, localization or causal direction was measured, and the data cannot decide whether the expanded compartment is adequate (adaptation) or already saturated (failed compensation).", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show more unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments and more neutral-lipid droplets than APOE3, while the ER-accessible/regulatory sterol pool (e.g., ALOD4/D4H sensor at the plasma membrane-ER pool, or SREBP-2 cleavage assessed by nuclear-form immunoblot) should be equal or lower in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol and equal or higher ER-accessible sterol while SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) remain elevated, the routing-mismatch mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective rescue of lysosomal sterol egress (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/STARD3-mediated transfer enhancement) in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, ACAT2, DHCR24) and reduce TFEB-target transcripts (ATP6V1H, CTSB, GAA, LAMP1) toward APOE3 levels without changing inflammatory transcripts (CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3). No reduction of SREBP-2 targets after successful egress rescue would falsify step 4.", "Adaptation versus failed compensation (decisive flux test): with a DQ-BSA / BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester / myelin pulse-chase in the unchallenged state, this mechanism predicts APOE4 degradative and esterification throughput per cell to be equal to or higher than APOE3 at baseline, with a smaller fold-increase (reduced headroom) when cargo load is raised. Finding lower baseline degradative flux in APOE4 despite the elevated hydrolase/V-ATPase transcripts would replace this model with an ongoing lysosomal-capacity defect (failed compensation).", "Prospective TFEB (or TFEB+TFE3) knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the CLEAR transcript set (ATP6V1H, CTSB, GAA, LAMP1, SLC17A5) and disproportionately impair APOE4 lipid clearance relative to APOE3; if CLEAR transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 after TFEB loss, step 2's attribution to MiT/TFE control is wrong even if the lysosomal phenotype persists.", "Prospective metabolic test: APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and etomoxir-sensitive oxygen consumption with lower glycolytic (ECAR) reliance than APOE3; equal oxidative rates with higher glycolysis would contradict step 5 without necessarily overturning steps 1-4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (input, inferred routing): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:LDLR +1.50), which we infer increases delivery of lipid/lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (compartment expansion): MiT/TFE transcription factors are up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) together with a broad CLEAR-type output: V-ATPase subunits up in 9/9 represented members (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30), acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81), and lysosomal membrane/transport proteins (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CLN3 +1.17, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SLC38A7 +7.53, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:GPNMB +1.11). This is transcript abundance, i.e., inferred capacity, not measured hydrolase activity or acidification.", "Step 3 (traffic and membrane load): endosome maturation, retromer and ESCRT transcripts rise in parallel (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:MON1B +2.34, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:VPS37B +3.86, gene:VPS28 +2.36, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:AP3D1 +4.42, gene:AP5M1 +9.79), with gene:LGALS3 +2.37, consistent with heavier cargo traffic and increased endolysosomal membrane repair/remodelling demand (localization and damage were not measured).", "Step 4 (the mismatch): despite increased uptake-receptor and hydrolase transcripts, the ER sterol sensor reads as sterol-poor: the SREBP-2 module is uniformly up (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87; 9/9 represented members positive), together with lipogenic/esterification genes (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25). We interpret the coexistence of high uptake and high de novo synthesis as sterol being retained in lysosomal/esterified pools instead of feeding back on SCAP/INSIG in the ER; the ER-accessible sterol pool was not measured.", "Step 5 (metabolic support): the state is accompanied by higher mitochondrial oxidative and TCA transcripts (gene:OGDH +8.62, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +8.00, gene:NDUFA5 +7.31, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65) with lower upper-glycolysis transcripts (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12), which we read as a fuel bias toward oxidation of lipid-derived substrate rather than a glycolytic inflammatory shift.", "Step 6 (state, not activation): the change is not an inflammatory/DAM identity switch: inflammatory genes are split as expected for the selected list (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09 but gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:RELB -1.30, gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05), homeostatic microglial identity genes are up (gene:CSF1R +1.37, gene:MEF2C +1.32, gene:MAFB +1.47, gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:GPR34 +2.95), and the microglial protease gene:CTSS is strongly down (-5.57), so the lysosomal program is not a by-product of classical activation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lipid-ingestion/endolysosomal-expansion state with unrelieved ER sterol-deficit signalling (sterol routing mismatch), not an inflammatory switch"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2687109995199941, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27257299667004, "cosine_similarity": 0.4040471743735509, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5889676375404531, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2687109995199941, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27257299667004, "cosine_similarity": 0.4040471743735509, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5889676375404531, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.191081, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 16}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE and STARD3 is treated as 'no evidence of coordinate induction', NOT as measured non-change or decrease. If those genes were filtered for technical reasons, the core mismatch premise fails.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is kept as reported; RNA effects are therefore not numerically comparable with the log2 protein-spot effects, and magnitude ranks are used only qualitatively.", "Measured transcript abundance is used as a proxy for capacity; hydrolase activity, acidification, transport flux, sterol localisation and esterification rates were all inferred, not measured. No lipid, sterol, filipin, cholesteryl-ester or efflux measurement was supplied.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are not used as support for this mechanism (spot-level effects showed no correlation with the mean RNA effect of their candidate genes, r = -0.05).", "The comparison is bulk-like pseudobulk over an astrocyte co-culture system; genotype-dependent differences in microglial state composition or in astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply could produce the same transcript pattern without any change in per-cell flux.", "The list-wide effect distribution is strongly skewed positive (1705/2212 rows up, mean ~+1.39), so all set-level statements were made relative to that background rather than to zero; replicate structure was not supplied, so effect precision cannot be independently checked."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 cells show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors and of a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program, while neither the rate-limiting de novo sterol-synthesis enzymes nor the sterol egress/efflux machinery appear among the selected differential results. We hypothesise that the resulting mismatch makes post-hydrolytic sterol/lipid egress from the endolysosome (and subsequent efflux) the limiting step, so liberated sterol is retained in the endolysosome and re-routed to ER esterification and storage, sustaining a lipid-laden, ER-sterol-replete, DAM-like microglial state rather than a sterol-starved SREBP2-driven one. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed and testable.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: bypassing the egress step in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or LXR-agonist-driven induction of ABCA1/ABCG1) should lower endolysosomal unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and cholesteryl-ester content and partially normalise the hydrolase/TFEB transcript program toward APOE3 within 24-72 h, whereas simply lowering uptake by SCARB1/CD36 blockade should reduce load without needing export. If cyclodextrin or LXR agonism clears the sterol but leaves the lysosomal program and DAM-like markers unchanged, the proposed causal chain from egress bottleneck to cell state is weakened.", "Direct flux test: APOE4 microglia loaded with fluorescent or isotope-labelled cholesteryl-ester-containing lipoproteins should show equal or greater internalisation and hydrolysis but reduced fractional efflux to ApoA-I/HDL and prolonged lysosomal residence of label relative to APOE3. Equal or greater fractional efflux in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should, under this model, convert stored ester into retained free sterol with little increase in net efflux in APOE4, while producing a proportionally larger efflux increase in APOE3.", "TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase transcript module without normalising sterol retention or the DAM-like markers, since the model places TFEB downstream of load; normalisation of retention after TFEB knockdown alone would indicate the lysosomal program, not egress capacity, is the driver.", "Unbiased whole-transcriptome or proteomic measurement should show HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1 and MSMO1 unchanged or reduced and ABCA1/ABCG1/NPC1 not induced in APOE4; strong coordinate induction of the rate-limiting synthesis enzymes would support a sterol-depletion (SREBP2-driven) alternative and weaken this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for scavenger and lipoprotein receptors (SCARB1 far above the list-wide shift, plus CD36, LDLR, MRC1, TREM2), which we infer - but did not measure - increases receptor-mediated internalisation flux of lipid and lipoprotein cargo.", "A lysosomal biogenesis-type program is coordinately elevated (TFEB, MITF; hydrolases GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD; acidification subunits ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1; LAMP1, NPC2; RAB7A). Mean effect of the lysosomal set is above the already positive list-wide background (permutation p ~0.003; Mann-Whitney p ~0.008), so this is not merely the global upward shift. We infer increased lumenal hydrolysis of internalised lipid/lipoprotein cargo, liberating unesterified sterol and sphingolipid products inside the endolysosome (the sterol pool itself was not measured).", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK: the export arm is not co-scaled. Genes for lysosomal sterol egress and cell-surface efflux (NPC1, STARD3, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) are absent from the supplied selected differential list, whereas the sensing/oxysterol arm is up (INSIG1, SREBF2 modestly, CH25H, CYP27A1, and the LXR-responsive MYLIP and ABCA7). Egress/efflux capacity therefore does not rise in proportion to inferred uptake and hydrolysis flux, making sterol exit from the endolysosomal compartment the rate-limiting step.", "Because rate-limiting synthesis genes (HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1, MVD, FDFT1, MSMO1, CYP51A1) are absent from the list while INSIG1 is up and the curated sterol-synthesis subset shows no enrichment over background (permutation p ~0.26), the ER sterol sensor is inferred to be replete rather than depleted; de novo synthesis is unlikely to be the driver, and the assigned 'sterol synthesis' framing of the focus is rejected in favour of a trafficking/disposal bottleneck.", "Sterol and fatty acid reaching the ER are inferred to be shunted into esterification and neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, SREBF1 up), rather than exported, further reducing the free-sterol pool available for APOE-dependent secretion even though APOE transcript is up.", "Chronic endolysosomal lipid load is proposed to maintain the observed lipid-associated/DAM-like and secretory phenotype (ITGAX, CLEC7A, GPNMB, CD74, CCL2, CXCL8 up) that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 under mock treatment."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol/lipid egress capacity, not sterol synthesis, is the APOE4 bottleneck: uptake and hydrolase expansion outrun the export arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1375401543403611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24255298235090098, "cosine_similarity": 0.4039801596881002, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5978705501618122, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1375401543403611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24255298235090098, "cosine_similarity": 0.4039801596881002, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5978705501618122, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.98591525, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 85}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_069", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression result (1705 positive, 507 negative effects; all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome, so the sign of a gene relative to the list is treated as more reliable than the magnitude, and no whole-transcriptome shift is asserted.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and was left unconverted; effect magnitudes up to ~15 units are treated as ordinal, and the negative source-row block structure (negatives occur only at source_row \u003c= 509) is treated as a possible artefact of two concatenated ranked tables rather than as biological ordering.", "Transcript changes are assumed to partially track the abundance and stoichiometry of the corresponding cortical actin and Rho-regulatory proteins; no protein, phospho, GTP-loading, localization, imaging or flux measurement of these components is supplied, so all activity, force, localization and rate statements are inferred, not observed.", "ACTB's large negative effect may reflect compositional or library-size normalization rather than a real ~5-log drop in beta-actin; the module conclusion is required to hold after ACTB and the other extreme-tail genes are removed.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level evidence is treated as ambiguous corroboration only, and the MYH9-containing spots cited were not reported as significant.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcripts may derive from or be influenced by non-microglial cells; no cell-composition control is supplied.", "No lipid, phagocytosis, motility or metabolic-flux measurement is supplied, so the proposed uptake bottleneck and the esterification bias are predictions, not observations."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 shifts the transcriptional balance of the cortical actin machinery toward inhibition (ARHGDIA strongly up; RAC2, ARHGDIB, DOCK8, PLEK, MYO1F, MYH9, ACTB, VASP, PAK2 in the down-regulated block) while recognition-receptor and lysosomal/endosomal transcripts are in the up-regulated block. We hypothesise that the resulting deficit in membrane-recruited active Rho-family GTPase and non-muscle myosin II activity, rather than a deficit of surface receptors or of degradative enzymes, is the primary bottleneck limiting phagocytic and macropinocytic cargo internalization, producing an uptake-limited but degradation- and esterification-competent endolysosomal state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: siRNA/shRNA knockdown of ARHGDIA (or expression of a fast-cycling Rac1-F28L allele) in APOE4 microglia should raise pHrodo-bead, myelin-debris and synaptosome internalization rate toward APOE3 levels without changing surface TREM2, MERTK or CD36 by flow cytometry. If ARHGDIA knockdown leaves uptake unchanged, or if rescue requires raising surface receptor levels, the mechanism is weakened.", "Binding-versus-internalization split (4 C surface binding then 37 C chase, with trypan-blue or anti-ligand quench): APOE4 should show equal or greater particles bound per cell but a lower internalized fraction than APOE3. If bound particles fall in proportion to internalized particles, the bottleneck is recognition/opsonization, not the cytoskeletal step, and the mechanism is weakened.", "Epistasis: sub-maximal blebbistatin (myosin II) or CK-666 (Arp2/3) applied to APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 uptake deficit and collapse the genotype difference. If APOE4 uptake falls by the same proportional amount as APOE3 under these inhibitors, the actomyosin step is not already limiting in APOE4 and the mechanism is weakened.", "Biochemical test of the inferred activity step: Rac1-GTP/Cdc42-GTP pulldown and membrane-versus-cytosol fractionation should show lower GTP-loaded Rac/Cdc42 and a higher cytosolic RhoGDI1-bound fraction in APOE4. Equal or higher active Rac1/Cdc42 in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism, and FAM49B/CYRIB being down (a Rac1-WAVE inhibitor) makes this the most likely failure mode.", "Degradative capacity should not be limiting: with cargo delivery matched (dose-matched, spinoculated DQ-BSA-coated or fluorophore-quenched beads), APOE4 should show equal or higher per-particle proteolytic and lipolytic dequenching and equal or higher LysoTracker/hydrolase activity. A per-cargo degradation deficit in APOE4 would favour a lysosomal rather than an uptake bottleneck.", "Lipid consequence under cargo-matched delivery: APOE4 microglia given an equal internalized dose of myelin or acetylated-LDL should convert a larger fraction into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol (BODIPY/lipid-droplet area per internalized particle; CE/free-cholesterol ratio), and this bias should be reduced by SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition without correcting the uptake rate. No esterification bias at matched cargo would weaken the sixth mechanism step while leaving the uptake bottleneck testable."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured abundance: APOE4 microglia show one of the largest positive transcript effects in the supplied differential-expression list for the Rho-GDP dissociation inhibitor ARHGDIA, while a coherent myeloid actomyosin/Rho-effector module (RAC2, ARHGDIB, DOCK8, PLEK, MYO1F, MYH9, ACTB, VASP, PAK2, ARHGAP30, FAM49B, SPN) falls in the down-regulated block; 10 of 11 tested module members are negative against a list in which only 23% of rows are negative.", "Inferred activity and localization (not measured here): a higher RhoGDI1-to-Rac/effector ratio is proposed to hold a larger fraction of Rac1/Rac2/Cdc42 in the cytosolic GDI-bound pool, lowering GTP-loaded GTPase at the plasma membrane; together with lower non-muscle myosin IIA (MYH9) this is proposed to reduce branched-actin polymerization and contractile force at nascent phagocytic cups and macropinocytic ruffles.", "Inferred flux: reduced cup extension and closure lowers the number of particles internalized per cell per unit time, i.e. the rate-limiting node is placed at membrane deformation and scission rather than at ligand recognition.", "Counter-node ruled in as non-limiting by the data: recognition-receptor transcripts (TREM2, MERTK, CD36, MRC1, SCARB1, C1QA, FCGR1A, FCGR3A, ITGB1, ITGA6) are almost entirely in the up block (1 of 29 negative versus 6.6 expected), and receptor-proximal SYK is up while the inhibitory phosphatase PTPN6 is down, so receptor supply and proximal signalling are unlikely to be the bottleneck.", "Second counter-node ruled in as non-limiting: TFEB and lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and endosome-maturation transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C, RAB7A, RAB32, SNX3, VPS26A, CHMP4B, AP3D1, DNM2) are up, indicating expanded rather than deficient degradative and sorting capacity downstream of the proposed block.", "Downstream consequence (inferred, weaker evidence): the concurrent rise in mitochondrial citrate/pyruvate carrier and TCA transcripts (SLC25A1, MPC2, MDH1, OGDH) with ACSS2, SREBF1, SCD, SOAT1, DGAT1 and ACAT2, alongside lower committed glycolytic kinases (HK2, PFKP), is proposed to bias whatever lipid cargo does enter toward esterification and storage rather than toward the glycolysis-supported high-throughput uptake state, giving a low-influx, high-esterification endolysosomal phenotype."], "title": "RhoGDI1-biased suppression of the myeloid actomyosin module makes internalization, not receptor supply or lysosomal capacity, the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.287045036545989, "cosine_similarity": 0.4039670444520172, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6075954692556634, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.287045036545989, "cosine_similarity": 0.4039670444520172, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6075954692556634, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.13146775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 86}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_074", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1 in an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77% positive); program directionality is judged against that 77%-positive selected-list background, not 50/50, and binomial p-values quoted in analysis.md are heuristic because genes are not independent.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, PDHA1, CS, MDH2, G6PD, TKT, ACLY, FASN, TFAM, all MRPL/MRPS) are unknown, not unchanged; the mechanism must not be read as claiming they are unaltered.", "Measured quantities are transcript abundance and 2D-gel spot abundance; pyruvate flux, PDH phosphorylation state, respiratory rates, complex assembly, citrate export, NADPH levels, lipid-droplet content and lysosomal pH were not measured and are inferred only.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (log2 of reported fold change) and are used only for compatibility/contradiction; no spot is promoted to identify a single protein. The large up-shifted train protein_spot:043/044/045/046 is jointly consistent with ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) or TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32) and is therefore not evidence of increased transaldolase.", "The measured condition is mock (no exogenous challenge); Step 6 is a prospective capacity statement, not an observed respiratory deficit.", "The decreased mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed biological; in 10X data they can also reflect ambient/QC/normalization differences in mitochondrial read fraction, which would remove the stoichiometry caveat without changing Steps 1-5.", "DE signal is assumed to derive from the microglial population of the microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30, with isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 as the only genotype difference."], "claim": "In isogenic iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs APOE3) shows a coordinated transcriptional re-routing of carbon rather than a glycolytic ramp-up: glucose uptake genes and storage/lysosomal-glycogen genes rise while committed glycolytic and oxidative-PPP steps fall, whereas mitochondrial pyruvate import, PDH-activating, malate-aspartate shuttle, TCA, anaplerotic amino-acid and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts rise together with citrate export (SLC25A1) and PPP-independent NADPH routes (NNT, ME1); this oxidative-anabolic configuration is the metabolic counterpart of the strongly induced sterol/lipid-handling (SREBF1/2, SCD, DHCR24, ACAT2, SOAT1, SCARB1, LDLR) and lysosomal/v-ATPase program. The mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are not co-elevated (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 down), so the nuclear build-out is plausibly stoichiometrically unmatched, which we predict limits spare respiratory capacity under a future challenge rather than proving an ongoing defect in the measured mock condition. Only abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and complex assembly are inferred and unproven, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective stable-isotope tracing in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia: U-13C-glucose should give a higher m+2 citrate/TCA labeling fraction relative to secreted m+3 lactate in APOE4, and U-13C-glutamine should contribute a larger fraction of TCA carbon; if APOE4 instead shows equal or greater lactate labeling/secretion with no increase in glucose- or glutamine-derived TCA labeling, the routing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective Seahorse profiling in the same mock condition: higher basal and ATP-linked OCR (or higher OCR/ECAR ratio) in APOE4; a lower or unchanged basal OCR despite the uniform nuclear TCA/OXPHOS transcript increase would favor the competing 'failed compensation for an mtDNA-expression defect' explanation over increased oxidative use.", "Prospective pharmacologic/genetic test of the hand-off step: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should reduce 13C-glucose incorporation into cholesterol/fatty acids and lower lysosomal acidification (LysoSensor) preferentially in APOE4; equal effects in APOE3 and APOE4, or no reduction in APOE4 sterol labeling, would weaken the causal link between pyruvate import and the sterol-lysosomal program.", "Prospective mitonuclear test (challenge-revealed, Step 6 only): BN-PAGE/complex-activity assays and FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration should show that assembled complex IV/V and spare respiratory capacity do not scale with the nuclear subunit transcript increase in APOE4; if assembled complexes and spare capacity rise proportionally, Step 6 is falsified while Steps 1-5 can still stand.", "Prospective targeted quantitative proteomics (not 2D gels): MPC2, PDP1, OGDH, MDH1 and v-ATPase V1 subunit proteins should be higher in APOE4; absence of any increase in these proteins would weaken the claim that the transcript program is translated into capacity.", "Prospective negative control for the state model: APOE4 should not show an increased oxidative-PPP flux signature (2-13C/1-13C glucose CO2 release, or NADPH/NADP+ ratio driven by G6PD) despite the up-shifted ANXA1/TALDO1-containing spot train; a clear PPP flux increase would contradict the routing model as formulated."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (state): APOE4 microglia adopt a lipid/sterol-handling, lysosome-high state - sterol/lipid anabolism and uptake transcripts up 16/16 represented (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28) and lysosomal genes up 16/17 with all 8 v-ATPase subunits up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:TFEB +2.38); this state raises demand for acetyl-CoA/citrate, NADPH and ATP for acidification.", "Step 2 (routing away from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP): glucose import transcripts rise (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A8 +1.28, gene:SLC2A9 +1.62) while the committed hexokinase/PFK steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) and oxidative/non-oxidative PPP falls (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:NADK -1.14); glycogen synthesis and lysosomal glycogen turnover rise (gene:GYS1 +6.10, gene:UGP2 +1.86, gene:GAA +9.96). Net inference: hexose is not committed to increased glycolytic/PPP throughput.", "Step 3 (pyruvate handed to mitochondria): mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating machinery rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54) and the malate-aspartate shuttle rises (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50), favoring pyruvate oxidation and cytosolic NADH transfer over lactate output (only gene:SLC16A1 +1.12; no LDH gene in the supplied list).", "Step 4 (anaplerotic amino-acid fueling and oxidative expansion): amino-acid catabolism/transport up (gene:GLS +1.35, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:BCAT2 +6.42, gene:BCAT1 +1.32, gene:ABAT +1.54, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45, gene:SHMT2 +2.22) feeding an expanded TCA program (17/17 represented positive: gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:PCK2 +1.21) and a uniformly increased nuclear-encoded OXPHOS program (37/37 positive: gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65) plus carriers/import (gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:SLC25A37 +4.48, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM8B +5.20).", "Step 5 (anabolic and energetic output of the routing): citrate export and PPP-independent NADPH supply rise (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:ME1 +1.36), providing acetyl-CoA/NADPH for the Step-1 sterol/lipid program and ATP for v-ATPase-dependent acidification; the same state accompanies increased phagocytic/complement receptor transcripts (14/14 represented positive: gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:C1QB +1.13, gene:C1QC +1.17, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:FCGR1A +1.59) and phosphagen buffering (gene:GAMT +7.98, gene:GATM +1.20).", "Step 6 (mitonuclear stoichiometry caveat, prospective): mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are not co-elevated (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +1.95, gene:MT-ND5 +1.93), so the nuclear build-out may be unmatched at the level of assembled complexes; we predict this constrains maximal/spare respiration revealed only under a future challenge and does not by itself establish a defect in the measured mock state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route carbon from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP into mitochondrial pyruvate and amino-acid oxidation with citrate export, fueling a sterol-lipid and lysosomal cell state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23912602001255398, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21877878885126797, "cosine_similarity": 0.40328418903905766, "direction_accuracy": 0.33980582524271846, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5678867313915857, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23912602001255398, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21877878885126797, "cosine_similarity": 0.40328418903905766, "direction_accuracy": 0.33980582524271846, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5678867313915857, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.78677975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 17}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_072", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential list (all |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 positive / 507 negative = 77% positive); program coherence is judged against that 77% positive background, and absent genes (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2, LPL, NR1H3) are unmeasured, not unchanged - so cholesterol efflux capacity and several core mevalonate/hydrolysis steps are simply unknown.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are therefore compared only within this dataset, not converted to fold change.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway capacity, not activity: SREBP target elevation is interpreted as ongoing SREBP transcriptional output (an inference), and no sterol pool, esterification rate, lysosomal degradation flux, efflux flux or localisation was measured here.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5, dominated by keratins/actins); all candidate identities are retained and no spot is treated as measurement of a single named protein.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular lipoprotein supply and its APOE isoform differ between arms; the observed uptake/synthesis state may be partly a response to the astrocyte-derived lipoprotein environment rather than a purely cell-autonomous APOE4 effect.", "Effects described here are those expected in the measured mock condition; any inadequacy of the expanded lysosomal/synthetic capacity would only be revealed by a lipid- or phagocytic-load challenge and is not claimed to exist in the measured state."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) show a coordinated cell-state change in which lipid/debris uptake receptors and an MiT/TFE-driven endolysosomal degradative compartment are transcriptionally elevated together with esterification and full de novo sterol-synthesis and LDLR programs; the simultaneous elevation of uptake and of sterol-supply genes (which are normally switched off by sterol repletion) is most consistent with internalised sterol being routed to lysosomal and cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid pools rather than to the ER-accessible pool sensed by SCAP-SREBP, so the cells run a high-turnover uptake-degradation-storage-resynthesis cycle. Whether this represents successful high-throughput adaptation or failing compensation is not resolved by these data, because no sterol pool, efflux or degradation flux was measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-pool test: in APOE4 versus APOE3 mock cultures, esterified cholesterol (and lysosome-associated sterol by filipin/OlyA-type staining) should be higher while ER-accessible free cholesterol (ALOD4/D4H probe or acute SREBP-2 cleavage assay) is equal or lower. If ER-accessible cholesterol is equal or higher in APOE4 while SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1) remain elevated, the routing mechanism is weakened and a sensor-independent transcriptional drive is favoured.", "Prospective SOAT1 (ACAT) inhibition: avasimibe/CI-976 in APOE4 microglia should raise ER-accessible free cholesterol and selectively normalise SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, INSIG1) without requiring reduced uptake-receptor expression. No change in SREBP targets after effective esterification blockade would weaken step 3-4.", "Prospective uptake blockade: reducing cargo delivery (SCARB1 knockdown or blocking anti-CD36, or lipoprotein-depleted astrocyte-conditioned medium) should lower MiT/TFE and v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts while further increasing SREBP targets, because sterol supply becomes demand-limited. If both programs fall together, a shared upstream driver (generic activation or a global upward bias in this selected list) is the better explanation.", "Prospective flux discrimination (adaptation versus failed compensation): pulse-chase of fluorescent/2H-labelled lipoprotein or apoptotic-cell cholesterol should show, in APOE4, equal or faster lysosomal hydrolysis but slower egress to the ER/plasma-membrane pool and greater retention as ester. Equal or faster egress and normal steady-state pool sizes would refute the routing claim and support successful high-throughput adaptation.", "Prospective protein-level test with unambiguous methods: immunoblot/targeted MS of mature CTSB, CTSD, GAA, HEXB and ATP6V1A in the same cells should show net increases consistent with lysosomal expansion; if total mature hydrolase and v-ATPase protein is unchanged or lower (as several down-moving spots such as protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064 permit), the transcriptional lysosome program is not translated into expanded capacity and the mechanism must be restricted to transcriptional state only."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia up-regulate receptors and opsonins for lipoprotein and membrane-debris capture (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A), which is inferred (not measured) to increase delivery of lipid-containing cargo to endosomes.", "Cargo handling capacity is expanded through an MiT/TFE-type lysosomal-biogenesis program (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF, gene:RRAGD) with coordinated v-ATPase subunits (10/10 positive, e.g. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23), hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:NAGLU), lysosomal solute transport (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46) and endosome-to-Golgi/late-endosome trafficking (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1).", "Sterol that exits this compartment is preferentially esterified or stored rather than expanding the ER-accessible free-cholesterol pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:NPC2 +1.17, altered ER-endosome contact-site complement gene:OSBPL1A +1.03 versus gene:OSBPL8 -1.90); the free/esterified partition itself was not measured.", "Because ER-accessible sterol is not increased, SCAP-SREBP output remains high: every represented sterol-synthesis/uptake target is positive (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP; 13/13 positive including the SREBP-1 arm gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2), sustaining synthesis alongside uptake instead of feedback repression.", "A second, compartment-restricted sterol signal coexists: oxysterol-generating and sterol-excess-responsive genes are up (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28), indicating discordant sterol sensing between compartments rather than uniform whole-cell sterol deficiency.", "The resulting high-turnover lipid state is coupled to increased oxidative/anaplerotic and acetyl-CoA-supplying transcripts (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:ACO2, gene:ATP5F1B) with reduced upper-glycolysis transcripts (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08), and to a lipid-handling/reactive microglial surface phenotype (gene:APOE, gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:FTH1, gene:CD74, gene:ANXA1 +4.15).", "At the protein-spot level the expanded-hydrolase prediction is only partially compatible: hydrolase-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:055 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; v-ATPase-candidate protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), which fits redistribution among proenzyme/mature or modified forms as easily as it fits a net increase, and every spot carries \u003e=2 candidate identities."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route acquired lipid into an expanded endolysosomal/esterified sterol pool, leaving the ER sterol sensor in a demand state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24740411702546278, "cosine_similarity": 0.4028177259233677, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5859320388349515, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24740411702546278, "cosine_similarity": 0.4028177259233677, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5859320388349515, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.887722, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 18}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); program directionality is judged against that 77% up-biased background, and absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PLIN2, CPT1A, NR1H2/3, HLA class II transcripts) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative magnitudes are used, and protein spots are on log2 scale, so modalities are not quantitatively equated.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but does not demonstrate, enzyme activity or metabolic flux: SREBP target induction is read as evidence of active processing, and SLC25A1/TCA/OXPHOS transcripts as capacity, not measured citrate export, lipogenic flux or respiration.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidates over 92 spots) and cannot confirm individual proteins; spot-level changes are used only for compatibility/contradiction, and keratins/actins are likely shared or contaminant components.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some lipid supplied to microglia is non-cell-autonomous; the APOE4 effect may be partly mediated by astrocyte-derived lipoprotein composition, which was not measured.", "The condition is mock: no exogenous inflammatory or lipid challenge, so any reserve/capacity deficit (e.g. mito-nuclear mismatch) is prospective, not established in the measured state."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia at day 30, the dominant transcriptional difference is a coordinated lipid-handling cell-state change, not inflammatory or interferon signalling: scavenger/phagocytic uptake and endolysosomal machinery are up together with esterification enzymes, while the full SREBP-1/-2 target set (including LDLR and the post-squalene cholesterol arm) is simultaneously up - a combination expected when acquired lipid is routed into lysosomal and ester/droplet pools so that the ER-sensed regulatory sterol pool stays low. Mitochondrial TCA, citrate/malate carriers and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts rise in parallel, consistent with increased supply of cytosolic acetyl-CoA, NADPH and ATP for this anabolic/storage state rather than with an interferon-driven or classically inflammatory phenotype (only 4 of 2212 selected rows are interferon-associated, all weak; chemokine induction is modest and accompanied by strong induction of IkB-family inhibitors). All statements concern measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, sterol pool location and droplet content are inferred and unmeasured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, discriminating: pharmacologic block of sterol esterification (SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor) or delivery of ER-accessible sterol (e.g. cyclodextrin-cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol) in mock APOE4 microglia should collapse the SREBP target set (SREBF1, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD, HMGCS1) toward APOE3 levels and reduce neutral-lipid droplet area; if SREBP targets and droplets remain APOE4-elevated after ER sterol repletion, the sterol-sensing routing step is wrong.", "PROSPECTIVE: SLC25A1 inhibition or knockdown should reduce 13C-glucose/glutamine incorporation into fatty acids and cholesterol and lower droplet content preferentially in APOE4; unchanged lipogenic labelling would refute the mitochondrial citrate-export supply step while leaving steps 1-3 intact.", "PROSPECTIVE (adaptation vs failed compensation): Seahorse profiling in mock should show APOE4 basal and maximal respiration equal or higher than APOE3 if the nuclear OXPHOS increase is functional adaptation; equal transcripts but lower maximal respiration plus reduced assembled complex I/IV would instead support mito-nuclear assembly limitation and would require replacing step 4's 'supply' interpretation.", "PROSPECTIVE (rejects the assigned focus): JAK1/2 or STAT1 inhibition should not normalize the APOE4-vs-APOE3 transcriptional difference and no baseline ISG signature (MX1, IFIT1-3, OAS, ISG15, HLA class I/II) should be detectable by qPCR; conversely, detection of a coherent baseline ISG module would falsify the claim that interferon signalling is not the driver.", "PROSPECTIVE: targeted immunoblot/immunoprecipitation of the ambiguous up-spots (protein_spot:043-047) must resolve whether ANXA1, TALDO1 or another candidate carries the increase; if TALDO1 protein is increased despite gene:TALDO1 -2.32, the glycolysis/PPP down-shift component (step 4) is weakened without affecting steps 1-3.", "PROSPECTIVE (challenge-revealed): under myelin or apoptotic-neuron loading, APOE4 microglia should show greater droplet accumulation and slower cargo clearance than APOE3 despite higher cathepsin/v-ATPase transcripts; equal or faster clearance would argue for successful adaptation/increased throughput rather than storage-biased routing."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, APOE4 \u003e APOE3): lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and recognition transcripts are higher - SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22), CD36, MERTK, GAS6, MRC1, STAB1, TREM2, APOE, ABCA7 - indicating a cell state configured for increased lipid and debris uptake.", "Step 2 (inferred routing): the expanded endolysosomal compartment (TFEB +2.38; ATP6V1H +6.88 and 8 further v-ATPase subunits; CTSK +7.36, CTSB +5.52, CTSD, CTSH, LAMP1, NPC2; RAB7A, SNX3, VPS26A) plus higher esterification capacity (SOAT1, ACAT2, DGAT1, SCD +4.17, FABP5) sequesters acquired sterol and fatty acid into lysosomal and ester/neutral-lipid pools instead of returning free cholesterol to the ER membrane.", "Step 3 (inferred sensing): with the ER-accessible sterol pool kept low, SREBP-1/-2 processing stays active, producing the observed coherent target program (SREBF1 +4.67, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACSS2, SCD, FADS1) - uptake and de novo synthesis are induced despite ongoing lipid loading, i.e. a feed-forward rather than feedback-limited configuration.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred supply function): mitochondrial anaplerotic/export machinery rises (SLC25A1 citrate carrier +4.47, SLC25A11 +4.50, MDH1 +8.72, ME1, ACO2, OGDH +8.56, IDH3B/G, DLD) together with 38/38 represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (e.g. NDUFA5 +7.34, NDUFS7, UQCRC2, ATP5ME), while upper glycolysis (HK2 -3.67, HK3, PFKP) and PPP transcripts (TALDO1 -2.32, PGD) fall - a pattern fitting citrate/malate-based acetyl-CoA and NADPH provision for lipogenesis/esterification rather than glycolytic-PPP sourcing.", "Step 5 (consequence in the measured condition): the storage-biased state, not cytokine signalling, is the primary APOE4 difference; the modest chemokine/inflammasome-adjacent increases (CXCL8 +3.11, CXCL16 +3.66, CXCL1/2/3, CCL2, IL18, NLRP3 +1.09, CD74, CIITA) occur with concurrent induction of NF-kB inhibitors (NFKBIL1 +4.41, NFKBIB +3.68, NFKBIZ +3.07, NFKBID) and no ISG module, i.e. a restrained, lipid-state-associated low-grade chemokine tone.", "Step 6 (challenge-revealed, not established here): if mtDNA-encoded transcripts are genuinely lower (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4, MT-CO2, against MT-ND4L/MT-ND5 up), the nuclear OXPHOS increase may not translate into extra assembled respiratory capacity, so a defect would appear only under an energetic or phagocytic challenge; in the mock condition the data support altered routing, not a demonstrated bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route lipid into lysosomal/esterified storage, driving a sterol-sensing SREBP program supplied by mitochondrial citrate export, without interferon activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24924500369176975, "cosine_similarity": 0.4027605756292729, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5825145631067962, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24924500369176975, "cosine_similarity": 0.4027605756292729, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5825145631067962, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9748005, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 19}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_181", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; comparisons are made as ranks/residuals within the same unit, not as absolute fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong workbook-position structure (rows \u003c=445: median 0.00, 50% positive; rows \u003e601: median +2.06, 100% positive), so all pathway claims are made relative to that background, never as absolute up-regulation.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel-type features with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot direction is treated as ambiguous between abundance, isoform and processing changes.", "Elevated transcript abundance is assumed to report transcriptional demand, not measured enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lipid flux or subcellular localisation.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein lipid; the microglial transcriptome is assumed not to be materially contaminated by astrocyte RNA in the 10X Flex data.", "Neutral-lipid content, droplet number, hydrolase activity and cholesterol efflux were not measured in the supplied data and are predicted, not observed."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the differentiating state is a lipid-handling imbalance: transcripts for scavenger-receptor lipid influx (SCARB1, top 1% of measured effects) and for a coherent MiT/TFE-type endolysosomal acid-hydrolase / v-ATPase program are jointly elevated, while protein-spot evidence gives no matching net increase in mature hydrolase abundance. We propose that the rate-limiting step is post-uptake lysosomal hydrolysis/export of ingested lipid cargo, and that the excess un-cleared lipid is re-routed through an induced SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification-desaturation module into neutral-lipid storage. Causality is not established by these data; the transcriptional lysosomal expansion is interpreted as a compensatory response to, not proof of, a clearance bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SCARB1 knockdown (or BLT-1 blockade) in APOE4 microglia should lower neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content and droplet number toward APOE3 levels and blunt the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 esterification signature, while SOAT1+DGAT1 inhibition should instead redistribute lipid (fewer esterified droplets, higher free sterol/lysosomal load and greater toxicity) without normalising total ingested lipid. If SCARB1 loss leaves APOE4 lipid load unchanged, the influx-limited arm is wrong.", "Per-cell lysosomal hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, cathepsin B/L) and DQ-BSA or BODIPY-lipid degradation flux in APOE4 should be flat or increased far less than the corresponding transcripts, and lysosomal lipid substrate should accumulate. If APOE4 shows proportionally increased hydrolytic flux with no lipid accumulation, the bottleneck claim fails.", "TFEB activation (constitutively nuclear TFEB or mTORC1 inhibition) should reduce APOE4 lipid droplet burden more than APOE3; no genotype-selective rescue would weaken the compensatory-CLEAR interpretation.", "Immunoblot of individual cathepsins (CTSB, CTSD, CTSL, CTSS) should show pro-form/mature redistribution rather than uniform increases, matching the bidirectional hydrolase-containing spots; uniform large increases in all mature hydrolase proteins would argue against a saturated-capacity state.", "The state should be lipid-handling rather than inflammatory: APOE4 minus APOE3 should show no coordinated interferon-stimulated gene or NF-kB target induction at protein level; a dominant interferon signature would favour an alternative mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_181", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia increase surface scavenger-receptor-mediated uptake of astrocyte- and serum-derived lipoprotein lipid; SCARB1 transcript is the single most extreme lipid-handling change measured (gene:SCARB1, +8.22 in the reported log unit, 99.1st percentile of 2212 selected RNA rows). Uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured.", "Ingested lipid reaches the endolysosome; a coherent MiT/TFE-type CLEAR-like transcriptional program is elevated above the study-wide positive shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:DPP7 plus gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB), consistent with a demand signal from accumulated luminal substrate.", "Luminal catabolic throughput nonetheless remains limiting: protein spots whose candidate lists contain acid hydrolases move in both directions with no net increase (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 containing ATP6V1E1 are down), and the cysteine protease gene:CTSS is the 0.7th-percentile outlier of the whole RNA set. Hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and cargo flux are inferred, not measured.", "Sterol and sphingolipid egress from the limiting membrane is not upregulated in step with influx: gene:NPC2 sits below the study-wide median shift and NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured, so the export arm is unconstrained by these data.", "Lipid that is not degraded or exported is esterified and desaturated in the ER: gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:ACSS2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1 and the sterol carrier gene:SCP2 are elevated, while the de novo cholesterol-synthesis arm (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1) is not elevated above background - a pattern expected when substrate, not sterol scarcity, drives the module.", "The net predicted phenotype is APOE4-selective neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester droplet accumulation with an enlarged but functionally saturated endolysosomal compartment, accompanied by a modest phagocytic/receptor tone (gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:CD36) rather than an interferon or NF-kB inflammatory state."], "title": "SCARB1-driven lipid influx outpaces endolysosomal catabolic throughput in APOE4 microglia, diverting lipid into ER esterification and storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2453014806336078, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2466664727387639, "cosine_similarity": 0.4026937631595923, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_181", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6188446601941748, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2453014806336078, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2466664727387639, "cosine_similarity": 0.4026937631595923, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6188446601941748, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.033674, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 87}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_081", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression selection (all |effect|\u003e1) with a 77.1% up-shift and a median of +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base; all directional claims are made relative to that background, not to zero.", "Absence of a gene from the list (NPC1, ABCA1, LAMP2, MCOLN1, PLIN2, LIPA, GRN, PSAP) means it was not selected as differentially expressed, not that it is unexpressed or unchanged; the export-bottleneck step therefore rests on non-elevation of measured membrane transcripts plus the SREBP-2 paradox, not on a measured NPC1 defect.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal enzymes; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, and lysosomal lipid content were not measured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a specific enzyme measurement.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some lipid cargo and some APOE may be astrocyte-derived; the genotype effect is assumed to act largely cell-autonomously in microglia.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment or line background is assumed to be the dominant driver, though replicate structure was not supplied."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated day-30 iPSC-microglia, the APOE4 transcriptome shows a selective, above-background increase in lysosomal acid-hydrolase transcripts (glycosidases, sphingomyelinase, cathepsins) together with increased lipid/debris uptake receptor transcripts, while transcripts for lysosomal membrane transporters/exporters are only at the global background level. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is export of lipid catabolites (in particular free sterol) across the lysosome-limiting membrane rather than luminal hydrolysis: cargo is delivered and hydrolysed but its products are retained in the lysosome, so ER sterol sensing reports a deficit and drives the uniformly up-shifted SREBP-2 target block (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS, ACAT2, EBP) alongside re-esterification/storage genes (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD). This is a hypothesis about inferred flux and localisation; no lipid, sterol, or lysosomal pool was measured here and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or re-expressing NPC1/NPC2) should relieve lysosomal sterol retention and normalise the SREBP-2 target block (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24) and neutral-lipid content toward APOE3 levels while leaving the hydrolase transcript program largely elevated. If cyclodextrin demonstrably lowers lysosomal free cholesterol yet LDLR/HMGCS1 remain elevated in APOE4, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong and the SREBP-2 signature has another cause.", "Filipin or fluorescent-sterol imaging with LAMP1 co-staining should show a higher fraction of free cholesterol in the LAMP1-positive compartment in APOE4 than APOE3, with increased BODIPY neutral-lipid area. Equal lysosomal sterol fraction between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Blocking cargo delivery (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or withholding myelin/apoptotic-cell substrate) should blunt the hydrolase transcript induction and the SREBP-2 target induction in APOE4; if the hydrolase program is genotype-intrinsic and unchanged by cargo withdrawal, the compensatory-load framing is wrong.", "Direct enzyme assays should show APOE4 GBA, HEXA/HEXB and GAA activity at least matched to their transcript increase. Unchanged or reduced activity would contradict the increased-hydrolytic-capacity step; the supplied 2D spot data already provide no bulk protein support (24 spots containing a lysosomal candidate gene, median +0.58, versus 68 other spots, median +0.43, Mann-Whitney p=0.55), so this is the weakest link.", "SOAT1 inhibition in APOE4 should shift stored cholesteryl ester toward free cholesterol and reduce droplet number without correcting lysosomal sterol retention or the SREBP-2 signature; correction of the lysosomal phenotype by SOAT1 inhibition alone would place the bottleneck downstream in the ER rather than at the lysosomal membrane.", "If APOE4 instead differs primarily through mitochondrial substrate oxidation (TCA/OXPHOS transcripts are also coherently up: 13/13 up, median +3.54), then respirometry should show a genotype difference in maximal respiration that is not corrected by relieving lysosomal sterol; such a result would favour the metabolic alternative over this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (SCARB1 +8.22, ABCA7 +2.14, DGAT1-independent CD36 +1.38, MERTK +1.30, GAS6 +1.33, TREM2 +1.28, APOE +1.24, all in reported log units). Inferred (not measured): increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Measured: a coherent lysosomal acid-hydrolase block is up in APOE4 well beyond the global up-shift of this DE list (16 hydrolase transcripts present, 14 up, median +3.69 vs list median +1.46; permutation p=1.5e-4), including GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GAA, NAGLU, MAN2B1, GLA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, with TFEB transcript +2.38. Inferred: an increased transcriptional set-point for luminal glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and protein catabolism, i.e. a compensatory CLEAR-like response; hydrolase enzymatic activity was not measured.", "Measured: transcripts for lysosome-limiting-membrane proteins and solute exporters that are present in the DE list sit at or below the global background shift (LAMP1 +1.38, SCARB2 +1.06, NPC2 +1.17, CLN3 +1.17, SLC17A5 +2.16, SLC38A7 +7.46; median +1.28, permutation p=0.30), and NPC1, LAMP2, MCOLN1, TMEM175, ABCA1 are absent from the supplied DE rows. Inferred bottleneck: membrane-mediated export of hydrolysis products, especially free cholesterol, does not scale with the increased hydrolytic input, so catabolites are retained in the lysosomal lumen (an unmeasured pool).", "Inferred: retention of sterol in the lysosome lowers sterol delivery to the ER sensing pool, so SCAP/SREBP-2 is de-repressed. Measured consequence: every sterol-synthesis/uptake transcript present in the list is up (SREBF2 +1.06, SREBF1 +4.67, LDLR +1.50, INSIG1 +1.87, HMGCS1 +1.08, LSS +2.27, DHCR7 +2.71, DHCR24 +3.69, ACAT2 +2.04, EBP +1.34; 10/10 up, binomial p=0.07 against the 77% background up-rate). The paradox of simultaneously elevated uptake receptors and elevated de novo synthesis is the discriminating feature of an egress block rather than of genuine sterol shortage.", "Measured: esterification and neutral-lipid handling transcripts are up (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, SCD +4.17, MGLL +4.00) while no efflux transporter transcript (ABCA1, ABCG1) appears in the DE list. Inferred: sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are re-esterified and stored rather than effluxed, converting the futile uptake-plus-synthesis cycle into cytoplasmic neutral-lipid accumulation.", "Inferred net state: APOE4 microglia occupy a substrate-loaded endolysosomal state with high hydrolase transcription, retained luminal lipid catabolites, constitutive SREBP-2 drive and increased neutral-lipid storage; the hydrolase up-regulation is compensatory and does not resolve the load. This predicts lipid-handling and phagocytic-clearance deficits without an interferon or classical inflammatory program (0/28 interferon genes and only 1/26 core autophagy genes appear in the DE list)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate a lysosomal acid-hydrolase program without matched lysosomal export capacity, creating a luminal lipid-catabolite egress bottleneck that drives futile SREBP-2 sterol synthesis and neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2555105339369162, "cosine_similarity": 0.4025953374033772, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5943268608414239, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2555105339369162, "cosine_similarity": 0.4025953374033772, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5943268608414239, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.66916375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 88}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_092", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), so only rank/permutation comparisons against this list's own background are treated as evidence; absolute magnitudes are not interpreted and the RNA log base is left unspecified and not converted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain and delay, the abundance of the corresponding hydrolase, v-ATPase and transporter proteins; no activity, pH, localization or flux measurement is available in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry a mean of ~4.8 candidate genes each and are dominated by ACTB/keratin candidates, so cathepsin-candidate spots are treated as ambiguous corroboration only, never as identified CTSB/CTSD abundance.", "Cholesterol, cholesteryl ester, sphingolipid and any other lipid pool are unmeasured here; all statements about sequestered sterol are inferred, not observed.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, MCOLN1, ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE) are absent from the supplied list, so the egress arm is argued from the non-enrichment of the measured membrane/egress genes rather than from a measured decrease.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes and S100B is among the strongly elevated rows, so some signal may be non-cell-autonomous or ambient RNA from astrocytes; genotype effects are assumed cell-intrinsic for the purpose of the mechanism.", "Correlation only: nothing in these data establishes causal direction between APOE4 genotype, the hydrolase program and any lipid pool."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinate, selective transcriptional expansion of soluble lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits that is NOT matched by lysosomal-membrane carrier/egress or fusion transcripts, while lipoprotein-uptake (SCARB1) and neutral-lipid esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD) transcripts rise; we propose the rate-limiting step is export of catabolites (notably sterol) out of the endolysosome to ER/plasma membrane, so luminal degradation products are sequestered and re-esterified, and the MiT/TFE-type hydrolase program is a sustained compensatory response rather than a demonstrated increase in clearance flux. The pure sterol-synthesis focus is rejected as primary: the cholesterol-biosynthesis gene set is not enriched above this dataset's own strongly upward-shifted background.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely bypassing lysosomal sterol egress with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 re-supply) in APOE4 microglia should lower LAMP1-colocalized unesterified sterol AND, within 24-48 h, selectively reduce the elevated hydrolase transcripts (GBA, GAA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD) toward APOE3 levels without lowering SCARB1; if hydrolase transcripts remain elevated after sterol is cleared from lysosomes, the compensatory-feedback link in Steps 4-6 is weakened.", "Direction test: TFEB/MITF knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript set but should NOT normalize lysosomal lipid accumulation, because the proposed bottleneck is membrane egress; if knockdown abolishes the accumulation, the hydrolase program is causal rather than compensatory and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Kinetic test: after an acute lipoprotein load, APOE4 cells should show equal or faster cargo hydrolysis (dequenching of a self-quenched labelled lipoprotein) but delayed suppression of SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1) and delayed appearance of newly formed cholesteryl ester relative to APOE3; equal suppression kinetics in the two genotypes would weaken the ER-sequestration claim of Step 6.", "Capacity-mismatch test: quantitative imaging/proteomics should show a higher hydrolase-per-LAMP1 (or hydrolase-per-lysosomal-membrane-area) ratio in APOE4 than APOE3; an unchanged ratio with proportional LAMP1/SCARB2/NPC2 protein increase would refute Step 3 and favour a simple proportional lysosome-biogenesis model.", "Stress test: SOAT1 inhibition should be more toxic (more free-sterol crystals, more cell death or IL1B release) in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia; equal tolerance would weaken the esterification-buffering step.", "Specificity test: the cholesterol-biosynthesis enzymes should not behave as a coordinately induced module under sterol depletion in APOE4 relative to APOE3 beyond the shared response; strong APOE4-selective SREBP-2 target induction after statin challenge would favour the rejected sterol-synthesis focus over this trafficking mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Markedly higher SCARB1 transcript, with higher APOE, ABCA7 and TREM2 transcripts, is taken to indicate increased delivery of lipoprotein/lipid cargo into the APOE4 endolysosomal system; cargo influx itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): An MiT/TFE-type program (TFEB, MITF, and the TFEB target RRAGD transcripts elevated) is inferred to drive the coordinate elevation of soluble acid hydrolase transcripts (GBA, GAA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, NAGLU, SGSH, MAN2B1, SMPD1, DNASE2, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) and of every measured v-ATPase subunit, raising luminal hydrolytic and acidification capacity. TFEB nuclear localization and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, contrast): Lysosome-limiting-membrane and egress-associated transcripts (LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2, CLN3) rise only at the background level of this differential-expression list, and the autophagosome-lysosome fusion SNARE STX17 falls, so membrane-dependent export/fusion capacity is inferred not to scale with luminal hydrolase capacity.", "Step 4 (inferred pool, not observed): The resulting capacity mismatch is proposed to leave sterol and sphingolipid catabolites sequestered in late endosomes/lysosomes of APOE4 cells; no lipid or sterol pool was measured in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Elevated SOAT1, DGAT1 and SCD transcripts are interpreted as increased esterification/storage capacity that buffers whatever sterol and fatty acid does reach the ER, converting egressed lipid into cholesteryl ester/triacylglycerol rather than returning it to regulatory pools.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): ER sterol sensing is not repressed - SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, HMGCS1 transcripts are all up but as a set are not enriched relative to background - which is consistent with sterol being sequestered away from the ER sensor rather than the ER being cholesterol-loaded, and with the hydrolase program being sustained in a feed-forward manner by unresolved luminal load."], "title": "Hydrolase-dominant, membrane-lagging endolysosome remodeling creates a lipid/sterol egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08610567514677103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2570325189296979, "cosine_similarity": 0.40255472531994574, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945857605177993, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08610567514677103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2570325189296979, "cosine_similarity": 0.40255472531994574, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945857605177993, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71812775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 89}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_072", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive and the median effect is +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base, so only rank position within the supplied list (not raw sign or magnitude) is treated as evidence of pathway-specific change.", "Absence of a gene from the list (HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, CPT1A, PLIN2) is missing data, not evidence that those transcripts are unchanged.", "Higher hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to reflect at least partly increased mature enzyme and acidification capacity; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, compartment volume and cargo clearance rate were not measured.", "The nuclear-versus-mtDNA transcript divergence is assumed to reflect biology rather than probe-panel or ambient-RNA behaviour of a 10X Flex probe-based assay, which is not verifiable from the supplied data.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as ambiguous, non-confirmatory context.", "The microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an APOE4 astrocyte-derived, non-cell-autonomous input to the microglial state cannot be excluded.", "Background pathway memberships used to group genes are unverified prior knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 mainly by an unresolved endolysosomal cargo load. The rate-limiting step is degradative throughput inside the acidic compartment, not sterol biosynthesis or sterol export. The coordinated rise in acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts is read as a compensatory (TFEB-associated) capacity expansion, and it is accompanied by a transcriptional commitment away from upper glycolysis toward TCA/electron-transport-chain carbon use; because mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts move in the opposite direction to nuclear-encoded subunits, the compensatory oxidative capacity is predicted to be stoichiometrically capped, leaving lysosomal clearance rate-limiting. All lipid, sterol, cargo, ATP and flux pools in this claim are inferred; only RNA and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo-clearance test: given a matched pulse of a quenched degradable cargo (DQ-BSA or fluorogenic myelin/acLDL) and chased for 2-24 h, isogenic APOE4 microglia will retain more undegraded cargo per unit LAMP1-positive compartment than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears the cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3 per unit compartment, the bottleneck step (Steps 1-2, 5) is wrong.", "Discriminating metabolic test: acute oligomycin (mitochondrial ATP block) will impair lysosomal acidification and cargo degradation disproportionately in APOE4, whereas acute 2-deoxyglucose will impair APOE3 disproportionately. Equal genotype sensitivity to both drugs, or the reverse pattern, falsifies Steps 3-4.", "Mitonuclear test: APOE4 microglia will show a higher nuclear-encoded to mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS protein ratio (e.g. NDUFB8/SDHB versus MT-CO1/ATP6 by blot) and lower maximal respiration per unit mitochondrial mass than APOE3. Equal ratios and equal respiratory capacity would remove Step 4.", "Compensation-versus-driver test: TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts in both genotypes and worsen APOE4 cargo retention more than APOE3. If TFEB knockdown instead abolishes the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in cargo retention, the hydrolase program is a driver rather than a compensation and this mechanism is weakened.", "Focus-rejection test: blocking the mevalonate pathway (statin) or activating LXR (GW3965) will not normalise the APOE4 hydrolase/OXPHOS/glycolysis transcript signature, and 13C-acetate labelling will show no APOE4-specific increase in de novo sterol synthesis flux. If statin or LXR agonism does normalise the signature, or if APOE4 shows clearly increased sterol synthesis flux, the rejected sterol focus should replace this mechanism.", "Substrate-specificity test: SCARB1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia will reduce the GPNMB/CTSB/CTSD transcript elevation and the cargo-retention gap; no effect would mean the increased cargo delivery arm of Step 1 is not receptor-driven.", "Protein-level test: mature cathepsin B/D and beta-hexosaminidase activities will be higher in APOE4 lysosomal fractions. Unchanged or lower activities despite higher transcripts would break Step 2 (note that the supplied protein spots are already ambiguous here: spots with CTSD/CTSL candidates move up, protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053, while spots with CTSD/CTSB/HEXB candidates move down, protein_spot:058 and protein_spot:067)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, upstream): APOE4 changes the composition or handling of material delivered to the microglial endolysosome (lipoprotein/lipidic and membrane cargo), increasing the amount of cargo that is not cleared per unit time. No cargo, lipid or sterol pool was measured here; this step is a postulate, supported only indirectly by the scavenger/lipid-handling identity of the most statistically robust transcripts (gene:GPNMB, gene:APOE, gene:CTSH, gene:CD163, gene:MRC1, gene:PLA2G7, gene:CLEC7A, gene:TREM2) and by the strongly increased lipoprotein-receptor transcript gene:SCARB1.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A coherent acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program is higher in APOE4 (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GAA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ACP5, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2) together with gene:TFEB. This set is elevated above the internal rank background of the selected differential-expression list, whereas gene:CTSS moves strongly the other way. We interpret the program as compensatory capacity expansion; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and compartment volume were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Upper glycolysis transcripts are reduced (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3) while TCA and fatty-acid/acyl-CoA oxidation transcripts rise (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:MGLL), consistent with routing of degradation-derived carbon into mitochondrial oxidation rather than glycolysis. Flux was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred assembly constraint): Every detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcript is higher in APOE4 (e.g. gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME) while most detected mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2). We infer a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch that caps assembled complex I/III/IV/V capacity, so the oxidative compensation of Step 3 cannot fully cover the ATP demand of acidification and degradation.", "Step 5 (inferred outcome): Because glycolytic reserve has been transcriptionally withdrawn (Step 3) and oxidative capacity is capped (Step 4), the expanded hydrolase program (Step 2) does not resolve the cargo load; APOE4 microglia persist in a GPNMB-high, cathepsin-high scavenging state with lipid diverted to storage/esterification-associated transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5) rather than to an upregulated efflux program.", "Step 6 (focus test, negative): The assigned sterol-synthesis/sensing/export focus is rejected as the primary bottleneck. Post-squalene and SREBP-axis transcripts that are present (gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF2) rise no more than the overall list background, and no rate-limiting mevalonate enzyme (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, CYP51A1, MVD, IDI1, FDPS) and no ABCA1/ABCG1/NR1H3 transcript appears in the supplied list at all, so neither sterol synthesis nor sterol efflux can be asserted as the differentiating driver."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal degradative throughput, not by sterol synthesis: a compensatory hydrolase/v-ATPase program coupled to a glycolysis-to-mitochondrial-oxidation switch with mitonuclear subunit mismatch"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15459882583170254, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1742239895854101, "cosine_similarity": 0.4020508617162851, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956084142394822, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15459882583170254, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1742239895854101, "cosine_similarity": 0.4020508617162851, "direction_accuracy": 0.255663430420712, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956084142394822, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.981424, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 90}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of 2212 rows are positive (median +1.46), so all pathway statements are made relative to that list background and could still reflect selection bias.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; relative ordering, not absolute fold change, is used.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 1-6 candidate genes each; assignment of any spot to CTSD, CTSB, ATP6V1E1, ANXA1 or another single protein is unverified, and the same protein can occupy several spots as distinct proteoforms.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for the transcriptional demand signal only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, lipid content and organelle localization were not measured in this dataset.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect differing culture composition; biological replicate numbers were not supplied.", "Background pathway membership assignments (lysosomal, endocytic, lipogenic, ESCRT sets) come from unverified background knowledge, not from any supplied annotation file."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells primarily by an endolysosomal throughput bottleneck: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake, endosome-to-lysosome delivery and luminal hydrolases (including a higher TFEB transcript) are coordinately elevated, yet the measured protein-spot pattern for lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase candidate spots shows redistribution rather than a matching net increase, so the inferred rate-limiting step is the mature, correctly compartmentalised hydrolytic capacity per lysosome rather than transcript supply; the resulting inferred persistence of partially digested lipid/membrane cargo is accompanied by elevated transcripts of membrane-damage and ESCRT repair components. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pulse-chase a defined degradable cargo (DQ-BSA plus fluorescently labelled myelin or acetylated/oxidised lipoprotein) in isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia and measure internalised cargo and per-cell dequenching/clearance separately. The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalisation in APOE4 but a slower clearance rate per unit internalised cargo and a longer substrate half-life, with equal or larger LAMP1-positive area. If APOE4 clears cargo at the same or a faster normalised rate, the throughput bottleneck is falsified.", "In-lysate maximal activity of GBA, GAA, HEXA/HEXB and CTSB at optimal pH should be equal to or higher than APOE3, tracking the elevated transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB), while in-cell (organelle-resident) activity assays and the ratio of mature to pro-forms on immunoblot should fail to scale. If both in-lysate and in-cell activity rise in proportion to transcripts, the bottleneck at step 4 is weakened.", "Lysosomal pH measured with ratiometric probes should be equal or higher (less acidic) in APOE4, and APOE4 cells should be more sensitive to sub-maximal v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin dose-response shift). A lower or equal pH with normal bafilomycin sensitivity would specifically weaken the V1-sector sub-step suggested by protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 without necessarily refuting steps 1-3.", "Reducing cargo influx (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-poor medium) should lower LGALS3-positive puncta and partially normalise the hydrolase transcript elevation (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB) in APOE4. If these transcripts and damage markers stay elevated after cargo restriction, a load-independent, genotype-intrinsic transcriptional cause is favoured over the load-versus-capacity loop.", "Supplying processed degradative capacity that bypasses transcription (recombinant hydrolase uptake or acidic-nanoparticle restoration of pH) should shorten cargo clearance half-life and reduce galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 more than in APOE3. Equal or greater benefit in APOE3 would argue the deficit is not APOE4-specific."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 cells carry higher transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake and lipogenic machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:APOE +1.24). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred trafficking): transcripts for endocytic and late-endosomal delivery machinery are elevated (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:AP5Z1 +3.78, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS18 +1.41), consistent with sustained, not reduced, cargo arrival at the lysosome; localization and transport rates were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred regulation): a CLEAR-like hydrolase/acidification transcript program is elevated (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:TFEB +2.38). We interpret this as a compensatory demand signal, not as proof of increased degradative activity.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured abundance, inferred activity): the protein-spot data do not show a matching net increase in lysosomal-candidate spots. Spots whose candidate lists contain CTSD or CTSB change significantly in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00), and both ATP6V1E1-containing spots decrease (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93). We infer that mature/processed hydrolase pools and V1-sector availability, not transcript supply, limit luminal degradation rate; enzyme activity, proteoform identity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred damage): transcripts of lysosomal membrane damage sensing and ESCRT-dependent repair are elevated (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:ANXA1 +4.15, gene:ANXA6 +1.77, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:CHMP6 +1.20), and ANXA1-candidate spots are among the largest protein increases (protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:043 +1.96). We infer intermittent limiting-membrane stress from undigested cargo; membrane permeabilisation itself was not measured.", "Step 6 (inferred feedback): incomplete cargo clearance sustains the TFEB-type transcriptional response and diverts unhydrolysed lipid into storage/re-esterification (gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:MGLL +4.00), producing a self-reinforcing load-versus-capacity imbalance rather than a simple gain or loss of lysosome number."], "title": "Cargo-load-limited lysosomal throughput in APOE4 microglia: hydrolase transcripts scale, mature degradative capacity does not"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2207842558062253, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1442932753086757, "cosine_similarity": 0.40118860375709614, "direction_accuracy": 0.35436893203883496, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897184466019418, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2207842558062253, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1442932753086757, "cosine_similarity": 0.40118860375709614, "direction_accuracy": 0.35436893203883496, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897184466019418, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.711728, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 91}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_031", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1) in an unspecified logarithm base, and 77% of rows are positive; we therefore treat the direction of any single gene as weak evidence and rely on the joint pattern of pathway members plus their adjusted p-values, and we do not convert effects to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes and receptors; no enzymatic activity, uptake flux, esterification rate, or protein localisation was measured.", "Protein spots have 3-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin and actin candidates, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; the split direction of cathepsin-candidate spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) is treated as uninformative about net cathepsin abundance.", "Cholesterol efflux transporters (ABCA1, ABCG1), NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2 and LXR (NR1H3) are absent from the supplied rows; absence is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change, so no claim of efflux failure is made.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype-associated transcript differences may be secondary to altered astrocyte-microglia lipid exchange rather than microglia-autonomous.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at a single timepoint; correlation between genotype and transcript state is observed, causality is not established, and clone/batch effects cannot be excluded from the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcriptional state in which lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors, lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase genes and neutral-lipid esterification genes are all higher than in APOE3, while SREBP-dependent sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis transcripts remain elevated rather than repressed. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is post-lysosomal delivery of internalized sterol to the ER-accessible pool: sterol that arrives via scavenger-mediated uptake is retained in the endolysosome and shunted into SOAT1/DGAT1/AGPAT2-dependent ester storage, so the ER sterol sensor continues to signal deficiency and the cell keeps synthesising lipid while accumulating it. Only RNA and protein-spot abundances were measured; uptake flux, sterol localisation, lipid-droplet content and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content and, because unesterified sterol then reaches the ER, should lower SREBP2-target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1, SCD) toward APOE3 levels, while leaving uptake-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, CD163) largely unchanged. If SOAT1 inhibition lowers droplet content but leaves the sterol-synthesis programme still elevated in APOE4, the proposed bottleneck at ER sterol delivery is wrong.", "Imaging prediction: filipin plus LAMP1 co-staining should show a greater fraction of unesterified sterol in the LAMP1 compartment, and BODIPY/LipidSpot should show more neutral-lipid droplets, in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal sterol and droplet content in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Load-response prediction: after acLDL or myelin-debris loading, APOE3 microglia should repress LDLR, HMGCS1 and DHCR24 more strongly than APOE4 microglia at matched internalised sterol; comparable repression in both genotypes would falsify the 'ER sterol sensing reads low' step.", "Rescue prediction: hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or restoration of lysosomal sterol egress) should normalise the SREBP-target transcripts and reduce droplet load in APOE4 with little effect in APOE3; a genotype-independent effect would argue for a general lipid-overload phenotype rather than an APOE4-specific egress bottleneck.", "Specificity control: TFEB knockdown should reduce lysosomal hydrolase transcripts in both genotypes but should NOT normalise the APOE4 sterol-synthesis/esterification programme. If TFEB knockdown alone abolishes the APOE4-APOE3 difference in SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD and DHCR24, then lysosomal biogenesis, not sterol egress, is the primary driver and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Negative prediction: the mechanism predicts no coordinated APOE4 increase in canonical NF-kB/interferon effector output under mock conditions; a strong mock-state IL1B/TNF/ISG protein signature in APOE4 would indicate an inflammatory rather than a lipid-storage primary mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/debris receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:CD14, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7). We infer, but did not measure, an increased receptor-mediated lipid and lipoprotein uptake flux into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): The degradative compartment programme is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:NPC2), consistent with a TFEB/CLEAR-like expansion of lysosomal biogenesis; lysosomal proteolytic and acidification activity itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): Despite increased uptake and degradative capacity, transfer of liberated sterol from the late endosome/lysosome to the ER-accessible sterol pool is limiting in APOE4. This step is inferred, not measured; NPC1 and other egress components were not present in the supplied rows.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensor state): The SREBP-controlled biosynthetic programme stays elevated rather than being switched off as an ER-sterol-replete cell would do (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1). The simultaneous elevation of uptake receptors and of sterol/FA synthesis genes is the internal contradiction that identifies the egress/ER-delivery step as the bottleneck.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid pool): Acyl-transferases that esterify sterol and diacylglycerol and build droplets are higher (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:CIDEB, gene:SCD), predicting accumulation of cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol in droplets. Neutral lipid, droplet number and sterol localisation were not measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, state-level consequence): The resulting chronically lipid-loaded state is accompanied by a lipid-associated/disease-associated microglial transcript profile (gene:APOE, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS1, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:PLA2G7, gene:FABP5) without a coordinated NF-kB/cytokine feedback increase (gene:CISH, gene:TRAF4 and gene:CTSS are lower in APOE4), i.e. a storage-biased rather than a classically inflammatory divergence."], "title": "APOE4 microglia divert internalized lipid into esterified storage because sterol egress from the endolysosome to the ER is limiting, leaving ER sterol sensing 'low' despite an expanded uptake-degradation apparatus"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25012000147694124, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29605840339930894, "cosine_similarity": 0.4004268561975453, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5931521035598705, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25012000147694124, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29605840339930894, "cosine_similarity": 0.4004268561975453, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5931521035598705, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60181075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 92}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_054", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an apparent |effect| \u003e= 1 filter and a strong global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, mean +1.39); pathway claims are therefore made only where a gene set exceeds this shifted background, and absence of a gene (e.g. HK1, PKM, LDHA, ACLY, FASN, CS, PDHA1) is assumed to mean 'not reported', not 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking and for comparison with the same-column background, never converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite level, flux, ATP, oxygen-consumption or lipid measurement is supplied, so every flux, localisation and directionality statement is an inference.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are assumed NOT to identify a unique protein; no protein spot is used as evidence for any step (see analysis.md for the ALDOA/GAPDH and TALDO1/ANXA1 ambiguities).", "Assumed that HK2/HK3/PFKP transcript loss is not fully compensated by an unmeasured isoform (HK1, PFKL); this is the weakest link and is directly tested by prediction 2.", "10X Flex probe-based counts and per-cell normalisation are assumed not to be the sole cause of the mtDNA-encoded transcript decreases; a compositional artefact remains a live alternative, which is why the mitonuclear step is kept subsidiary.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular substrate availability (lactate, glutamine, lipoproteins) is shaped by a second cell type that was not profiled; genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "Causality is not established by these data; the hypothesis proposes a directed chain that the predictions below are designed to break."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally down-weight the committed glucose-phosphorylation/PFK step while up-weighting glucose and amino-acid import, TCA/anaplerotic enzymes, nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits and mitochondrial carriers; we hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck at glycolytic commitment (rather than at glucose uptake) makes APOE4 microglia rely on glutamine- and lipid-derived carbon for mitochondrial oxidation and shunt a larger fraction of TCA carbon out as citrate into an SREBF1-driven esterification programme, producing a glucose-sparing, lipid-storing state. All flux, localisation and causal steps are inferred; only RNA effects and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Parallel U-13C-glucose and U-13C-glutamine tracing in mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, a lower fractional enrichment of glucose carbon in citrate (m+2) and in secreted lactate (m+3), and a higher fractional enrichment of glutamine carbon in citrate/malate (m+4) and in newly synthesised palmitate/cholesteryl ester. WEAKENING RESULT: equal or higher glucose-to-citrate and glucose-to-lactate labelling in APOE4.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio in APOE4 and, critically, an equal or LOWER maximal glycolytic capacity (post-oligomycin ECAR) despite the higher gene:SLC2A1/gene:SLC2A3 transcripts; APOE4 cells should also be less sensitive than APOE3 to 2-deoxyglucose in ATP-linked and phagocytic assays. WEAKENING RESULT: APOE4 shows greater glycolytic capacity or greater 2-DG sensitivity, which would refute the glucose-commitment bottleneck.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pharmacological or genetic blockade of mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1 inhibition/knockdown, with ACLY inhibition as an orthogonal arm) should collapse the APOE4-specific excess of BODIPY-positive neutral lipid and of SCD-dependent monounsaturated species while leaving OCR largely intact, i.e. an APOE4\u003eAPOE3 genotype-by-drug interaction. WEAKENING RESULT: an equal proportional lipid reduction in both genotypes, or no reduction of the APOE4 lipid excess, would falsify the citrate-export-to-lipid arm.", "Restoring the committed step (HK2 or PFKP re-expression in APOE4 microglia) should partially normalise the glucose-to-lactate flux and reduce the transcript excess of the TCA/OXPHOS module (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:NDUFA5-type subunits). WEAKENING RESULT: unchanged glycolytic flux or unchanged oxidative module after restoration would place the bottleneck elsewhere (e.g. purely mitochondrial or lysosomal).", "Targeted proteomics or immunoblotting of unambiguous single proteins should confirm higher NDUFA/ATP5 and OGDH/MDH1 protein in APOE4, and should test whether mtDNA-encoded MT-CO1/MT-ND1 protein fails to scale with them. WEAKENING RESULT: no protein-level increase in the nuclear oxidative module would indicate the RNA module is not translated and would undercut steps 3-4; proportional scaling of mtDNA-encoded subunits would specifically retire the subsidiary mitonuclear step without affecting the main chain.", "Substrate-restriction test: APOE4 microglia should show a larger drop in viability/ATP than APOE3 upon glutamine withdrawal or GLS inhibition (CB-839) in normal glucose. WEAKENING RESULT: equal or lesser glutamine dependence in APOE4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: glucose/monocarboxylate transporter transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC16A1 +1.12) while every measured transcript for the two committed, ATP-consuming glycolytic kinase steps is lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10). Inferred: hexokinase/PFK-1 capacity, not sugar import, becomes the rate-limiting node for glucose carbon entry into lower glycolysis (the primary bottleneck).", "Inferred consequence: with less glucose-derived pyruvate available, APOE4 cells must draw TCA carbon from non-glucose substrates. Consistent measured transcripts: amino-acid import and glutamine catabolism (gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45, gene:GLS +1.35, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:ABAT +1.54) and lipid uptake/beta-oxidation-associated genes (gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24), plus a coherent lysosomal-catabolic programme (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:LAMP1 +1.38) that could supply fatty acids and sterols.", "Measured: the nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery is coordinately elevated far above the strong global positive RNA shift - TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:PCK2 +1.21), the PDH-activating phosphatase gene:PDP1 +3.00, and 39 nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:NDUFA11 +4.37, gene:NDUFA12 +3.71, gene:CYCS +2.58). Inferred: increased biosynthetic capacity for oxidative phosphorylation and for the malate-aspartate shuttle; increased flux is not measured.", "Measured: inner-membrane solute carriers and mitochondrial protein-handling transcripts rise (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 citrate carrier, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50 2-oxoglutarate carrier, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56 adenine-nucleotide translocase, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:TUFM +6.46, gene:OXA1L +4.90). Inferred: enhanced capacity for mitochondrial citrate export to the cytosol and for exchange of TCA intermediates, i.e. carbon leaves the cycle rather than being fully oxidised to CO2.", "Measured: a lipogenic/esterification and sterol-handling programme is elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28). Inferred: exported citrate is converted to cytosolic acetyl-CoA and directed into monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis and into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester formation rather than into complete oxidation. ACLY, ACACA and FASN were not measured, so this conversion step is unobserved.", "Inferred integrated state: APOE4 microglia are predicted to have a lower glycolytic contribution to ATP and lactate, a higher oxidative and glutamine/lipid-dependent contribution, and a larger neutral-lipid pool at steady state; this should be accompanied by reduced glycolytic reserve when an acute energetic demand (e.g. phagocytic or inflammatory challenge) requires rapid glucose flux.", "Subsidiary, weaker observation kept separate from the main chain: four of six measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) while two are higher (gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), which would predict partial mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance limiting assembly of the newly transcribed nuclear subunits. This is not required by the hypothesis and is treated as an alternative/aggravating factor."], "title": "Glucose-commitment restriction reroutes carbon into anaplerotic mitochondrial oxidation and citrate-derived lipid esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15613115238341393, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2600178419783143, "cosine_similarity": 0.40011455013406444, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5955533980582525, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15613115238341393, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2600178419783143, "cosine_similarity": 0.40011455013406444, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5955533980582525, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7358485, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 93}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_182", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strongly positive global shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median effect +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); all directional claims are therefore made as percentile ranks within this list, not as absolute up/down calls, and absence of a gene means unmeasured rather than unchanged.", "Transcript percentile rank is assumed to track protein and functional capacity for the transporters, hydrolases and enzymes named; none of these proteins, their activities, their subcellular localisation, or any lipid pool was measured in the supplied data.", "Protein-spot observations are excluded as evidence because each spot lists 2-6 candidate genes and cannot identify a protein uniquely; spots containing CTSB/CTSD/CTSL candidates change in both directions (e.g. protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), so they neither support nor refute the RNA-based lysosomal claim.", "The influx/catabolism versus egress/efflux gene sets were assembled after inspecting the data, so the permutation p-value is descriptive of the contrast, not a pre-registered test.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, STARD3, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE) are absent from the supplied list, so the egress/efflux deficit is inferred from the measured subset only.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein/sterol acceptors and donors that were not measured; genotype effects on the astrocyte compartment could contribute to the microglial signature."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the transcriptional arm that acquires and hydrolytically liberates lipoprotein-derived sterol (SCARB1 plus lysosomal hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits) is induced far above the global upward shift of this differential-expression list, whereas the arm that moves sterol out of the endolysosome and out of the cell (NPC2, OSBPL1A, OSBPL8, ABCA7, APOE) sits at or below that background; we hypothesise that this mismatch makes post-lysosomal cholesterol egress/efflux rate-limiting, so free cholesterol is retained in the endolysosome and the fraction reaching the ER is disposed of by SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification into neutral-lipid droplets and by CYP27A1/CH25H side-chain oxidation, with the resulting oxysterol-responsive (LXR-type) program (SREBF1, APOE, ABCA7, MYLIP) induced while the canonical SREBP-2 target set is not. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving the egress step directly with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or recombinant NPC2 delivery) in APOE4 microglia should lower LAMP1-colocalised filipin/free-cholesterol signal, lower cellular cholesteryl-ester mass and lower SCARB1, SOAT1, CYP27A1, CH25H and SREBF1 transcripts toward APOE3 values within 24-48 h. If cyclodextrin normalises the lysosomal sterol pool but leaves this transcriptional signature and the cholesteryl-ester excess unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Free-cholesterol topology: APOE4 microglia should show increased LAMP1-compartment free cholesterol with equal or lower ER-accessible/plasma-membrane-accessible cholesterol (ALOD4 or PFO* probe) than APOE3. Finding elevated ER-accessible cholesterol with no endolysosomal excess would weaken the mechanism.", "Efflux flux: cholesterol efflux from APOE4 microglia to exogenous apoA-I or HDL acceptors should be lower per unit cell cholesterol than from APOE3, and adding lipidated ApoE3 particles or an LXR agonist plus acceptor should reduce the APOE4 cholesteryl-ester excess. Equal or higher efflux in APOE4 would falsify the efflux limb.", "Lipidomic endpoint: APOE4 microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester species and higher 27-hydroxycholesterol/25-hydroxycholesterol relative to total cholesterol than APOE3, with total free cholesterol not lower. Unchanged or reduced cholesteryl ester and oxysterols in APOE4 would weaken the disposal-branch steps.", "Upstream influx test: SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade in APOE4 microglia should reduce endolysosomal free cholesterol and cholesteryl-ester mass without requiring a change in lysosomal hydrolase transcripts; if sterol load is unaffected by blocking SCARB1, the acquisition limb of the model is wrong even if the egress deficit stands.", "Counter-test of the sterol-starvation alternative: sterol depletion should still be able to induce SREBP-2 targets (HMGCS1, LDLR) in APOE4 cells; a constitutively maximal SREBP-2 target program in APOE4 at baseline would favour an ER-sterol-starvation model over this storage/efflux-limited model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_182", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SCARB1 RNA is the 99.1st-percentile change of the supplied RNA list (effect +8.22) and lysosomal luminal hydrolase / V-ATPase transcripts (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, CTSD) occupy the 72nd-99.7th percentiles. Inferred, not measured: increased selective lipoprotein-lipid uptake and increased hydrolytic liberation of free cholesterol and sphingolipid inside the endolysosome.", "Measured: transcripts for the sterol egress and efflux arm are at or below the list background - NPC2 34.7th percentile, OSBPL1A 25.6th, OSBPL8 12.7th (negative effect), ABCA7 65.1st, APOE 38.3rd; median percentile of a 12-gene egress/efflux set is 40.1 versus 79.6 for a 22-gene influx/catabolism set (post hoc permutation p = 3.5e-4). Inferred: egress/efflux capacity does not scale with acquisition and hydrolysis, making it the bottleneck.", "Inferred consequence (not measured here): free cholesterol accumulates in the LAMP1-positive late-endosome/lysosome compartment and its transfer to the ER and plasma membrane is slowed; the sterol pool that does reach the ER is buffered rather than exported.", "Measured: SOAT1 (effect +1.25, adj p 1.8e-125) and DGAT1 (+1.72) RNA are up, as are CYP27A1 (+1.49, adj p 2.3e-82) and CH25H (+1.62). Inferred: increased esterification of free cholesterol into cytosolic cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplets and increased side-chain oxysterol production as an alternative disposal route.", "Measured: an oxysterol/LXR-responsive set is coordinately up (SREBF1 +4.67, 91.8th percentile; MYLIP +1.28; ABCA7 +2.14; APOE +1.24) together with lipogenic targets (SCD +4.17, 89.1st percentile; ACSS2 +2.93; ACAT2 +2.04; FADS1 +1.59), while canonical SREBP-2 targets are unremarkable against background (SREBF2 27.5th, HMGCS1 28.3rd, LDLR 51.1st, INSIG1 60.1st percentile). Inferred: sterol sensing at the ER is not in a starved state; MYLIP/IDOL induction is inferred to further limit LDLR-family-dependent flux.", "Predicted net lipid state (the untested endpoint): APOE4 microglia hold more cholesterol as endolysosomal free cholesterol plus cytosolic cholesteryl ester and oxysterol, and release less cholesterol to extracellular acceptors, than isogenic APOE3 microglia at matched total sterol acquisition."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol egress/efflux capacity, not sterol acquisition or hydrolysis, is the limiting step in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2803332061158776, "cosine_similarity": 0.39957116550638444, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_182", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5910453074433657, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2803332061158776, "cosine_similarity": 0.39957116550638444, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5910453074433657, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.4922435, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 94}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_044", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; directions are compared against that 77%-positive background, and absent genes (e.g. ACLY, CPT1A, G6PD, PC, LDHA, PKM, TFAM, most mitoribosome genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes and carriers; no flux, respiration, membrane potential, metabolite, NADPH, lipid-droplet or mtDNA copy-number measurement is supplied, so all routing, flux and localization statements are inferences.", "Pathway membership was taken from a priori canonical lists written before directions were inspected, and every represented member was reported including sign-discordant ones; genes within a program are co-regulated, so per-program permutation p-values are descriptive, not independent-gene enrichment tests.", "Protein 2D-gel spots each carry 2-6 candidate identities (median 5; 208 candidate genes across 92 spots, no single-identity spot) and are used only for compatibility/contradiction; no spot is treated as evidence about an individual protein.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels from probe-based 10X Flex pseudobulk may be affected by probe design and by library composition/normalization; the mitonuclear mismatch step is therefore the least technically secure step.", "The astrocyte co-culture supplies substrate (lactate, lipoproteins) that is not measured; some of the routing difference could reflect a different extracellular substrate mix reaching APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia.", "Effects expected in the supplied mock condition are the transcriptional state and inferred lipid/oxidative commitment; reduced glycolytic and NADPH reserve is a challenge-revealed property and is not claimed to be an ongoing baseline defect."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated carbon-routing cell state rather than by a simple loss of a single enzyme: transcripts for the committed cytosolic glucose-consuming steps (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and for oxidative/non-oxidative PPP steps (PGD, TALDO1) are lower, while glucose/monocarboxylate transporters, mitochondrial pyruvate and citrate carriers, PDH activation, TCA-cycle enzymes, malate-aspartate shuttle, nuclear-encoded ETC subunits, lipid uptake/lysosomal hydrolase and SREBP lipogenic/esterification transcripts are higher. We infer (not measure) that glucose- and lipid-derived carbon is preferentially directed into mitochondria and then out as citrate/acetyl-CoA into lipid synthesis and storage, while the four mtDNA-encoded core ETC transcripts that are represented are lower, so terminal electron transport capacity probably does not scale with the nuclear program. This predicts a lipid-loaded, oxidation-committed state with reduced glycolytic/NADPH reserve that would become functionally limiting mainly under challenge; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective U-13C-glucose tracing in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show a lower fraction of glucose carbon in secreted lactate and lower PPP-derived labeling (m+1 lactate, labeled ribose-5-phosphate) but equal-or-higher m+2 labeling of citrate/glutamate and of newly made fatty acid/cholesteryl ester. If APOE4 shows unchanged or increased glucose-to-lactate labeling with no increase in glucose carbon reaching citrate or lipid, the routing mechanism is wrong.", "Prospective MPC blockade (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in mock APOE4 microglia should reduce TCA labeling from glucose and reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation more in APOE4 than APOE3, and force a larger compensatory lactate efflux in APOE4. If APOE4 lipid accumulation and TCA labeling are insensitive to MPC inhibition, step 3 fails and the lipid load is uptake-driven rather than pyruvate-derived.", "Prospective respirometry: APOE4 maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) respiration should NOT increase in proportion to the ~3-fold-scale nuclear ETC transcript elevation, and complex IV/complex I-linked capacity per unit mitochondrial mass should be flat or lower, while glycolytic reserve (post-oligomycin ECAR) is lower. If maximal respiration scales with the nuclear transcript increase and glycolytic reserve is intact, the mitonuclear-mismatch step (step 6) is refuted and the state is better described as successful adaptation with increased throughput.", "Prospective challenge test: an oxidative or phagocytic burst (H2O2, myelin/synaptosome load, or LPS-plus-ATP) should produce greater ROS and slower GSH/NADPH recovery in APOE4 than APOE3, and this difference should be attenuated by supplying an NADPH-sparing substrate or by restoring PPP flux; equal ROS handling under challenge would weaken the reduced-reserve claim without affecting steps 1-5.", "Prospective quantitative immunoblot of unambiguous single proteins (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, TALDO1, HK2, MT-CO1) in the same mock comparison: the mechanism predicts higher MPC2/OGDH/MDH1, lower HK2 and TALDO1, and unchanged-or-lower MT-CO1. Concordant transcript-only changes with no protein-level differences would demote the mechanism to a transcriptional state change with no inferred metabolic consequence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred load): APOE4 microglia increase lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lysosomal catabolic transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:TFEB), consistent with a larger internalized lipid/glycogen-derived substrate load; lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 2 (routing at the cytosolic commitment step): transcripts for the inducible hexokinase and phosphofructokinase isoforms are reduced (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) and PPP transcripts are reduced (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32) even though glucose uptake transcripts rise (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC16A1) and mid/lower glycolysis is not uniformly reduced (gene:GPI, gene:ENO1, gene:PFKM up), i.e. a routing change rather than global glycolytic loss; glycogen handling transcripts also rise (gene:GYS1 +6.10, gene:UGP2, gene:GAA).", "Step 3 (carbon entry to mitochondria): mitochondrial pyruvate import and PDH activation transcripts rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54), with anaplerotic/amino-acid and fatty-acid feeds (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1, gene:CROT, gene:SCP2, gene:FABP3, gene:FABP5).", "Step 4 (mitochondrial oxidative program expands coordinately): all 24 represented TCA-cycle, carrier, shuttle and nuclear-encoded ETC members are positive (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB, gene:SLC25A5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:ATP5F1C, gene:UQCRC2, gene:UQCRB, gene:NDUFB8, gene:COX5B, gene:COX6B1, gene:COX7A2, gene:COX8A; median +3.26 vs +1.46 for the whole selected list, permutation p~4e-4).", "Step 5 (carbon exits as lipid): citrate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA/SREBP lipogenic and esterification transcripts rise (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:MGLL), so part of the mitochondrial carbon is inferred to leave the cycle for lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage instead of full oxidation. ACLY was not represented, so this export step is inferred, not measured.", "Step 6 (capacity constraint, inferred): the represented mtDNA-encoded core subunits are mostly lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND5, gene:MT-ND4L positive; group median -1.56, permutation p~0.012, against a 77%-positive background), so assembled ETC stoichiometry probably lags the nuclear program; mitochondrial-stress/ISR-associated transcripts are up (gene:DELE1 +4.82, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:NUPR1, gene:PSPH, gene:SHMT2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4).", "Step 7 (state, not proven defect): the net measured-condition phenotype is an oxidation- and lipid-storage-committed microglial state with reduced glycolytic/PPP reserve; an ATP or NADPH shortfall is expected to be revealed by a phagocytic/inflammatory or oxidative challenge rather than to be demonstrated at baseline."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route carbon from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP into mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and citrate-derived lipid esterification, with mtDNA-encoded ETC subunits not co-upregulated"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2736033674260606, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2577710592766522, "cosine_similarity": 0.3982512476323157, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mean_absolute_error": 0.586747572815534, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2736033674260606, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2577710592766522, "cosine_similarity": 0.3982512476323157, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "mean_absolute_error": 0.586747572815534, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.610315, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 20}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_086", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with an up-regulated block roughly 3.4x larger than the down-regulated block; module tests are therefore made against the within-list up-block background, and absence of a gene from the list is treated as uninformative rather than as no change.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified, so only direction and within-list rank/magnitude ordering are interpreted, never absolute fold changes.", "Direction of transcript change is assumed to translate, at least in sign, into hydrolase protein and activity; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, flux, lipid or metabolite measurement was supplied.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot changes are treated as weak, direction-only corroboration (e.g. ANXA1-containing spots), not as protein-level identification.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some inferred lipid supply and some transcripts may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect residual non-microglial signal.", "Effect magnitude in this list increases with source-row order and decreases with significance, so very large effects in late rows are treated as lower-confidence than large effects in early, highly significant rows."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated up-regulation of the acid-hydrolase/CLEAR lysosomal program together with membrane-damage-repair and mitochondrial oxidative transcripts, while canonical type-I interferon and NF-kB output modules are not enriched. We propose that the rate-limiting step is degradation and export of internalized lipid substrate inside the endolysosome: substrate delivery (scavenger-receptor/APOE-TREM2 route) is inferred to exceed lysosomal catabolic and egress capacity, provoking a TFEB-type compensatory hydrolase program, lysosomal-membrane damage sensing/repair, sustained SREBP-driven uptake and synthesis (a futile loading cycle), and a shift of transcriptional support toward mitochondrial oxidative metabolism. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed, not demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Imaging of mock isogenic pairs should show, per cell, more LAMP1+ compartment volume and more filipin/BODIPY-positive lysosomal lipid in APOE4 than APOE3, together with more galectin-3 (LGALS3) puncta on LAMP1+ membranes. Equal or lower lysosomal lipid and equal or fewer galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Substrate-unloading test: 48 h of 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or blockade of SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake, should move APOE4 hydrolase/CLEAR transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSD, LAMP1, TFEB targets) and SREBP targets toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the full hydrolase program after substrate removal would indicate a load-independent, cell-autonomous transcriptional rewiring and weaken steps 1-4.", "Causal-direction test: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase transcripts in both genotypes but should disproportionately increase lysosomal lipid accumulation and galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 relative to APOE3. If TFEB knockdown produces no genotype-differential worsening, the CLEAR program is not a compensatory response to a genotype-specific load.", "Discriminating test against the inflammatory/interferon alternative: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IKKbeta inhibition in mock culture should NOT abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in hydrolase transcripts or in lysosomal lipid load. If either inhibitor removes that difference, an interferon/NF-kB-driven mechanism is favoured and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Metabolic test of step 5: Seahorse profiling should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a higher OCR/ECAR ratio in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Unchanged or lower respiration would falsify the inferred oxidative flux shift while leaving the lysosomal bottleneck testable by the predictions above.", "Sterol-sensing test of step 4: APOE4 cells should show equal or greater total cellular cholesterol yet equal or greater nuclear (processed) SREBP2 than APOE3, consistent with an ER-sterol-poor regulatory pool. Reduced nuclear SREBP2 in APOE4 despite the elevated synthesis transcripts would falsify the sequestration step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein capture and handling (SCARB1, CD36, ABCA7, APOE, TREM2, SCARB2, NPC2). We infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): Endolysosomal hydrolysis/egress capacity is the limiting step. A CLEAR-type compensatory program is transcriptionally up (TFEB, GAA, GBA, GBA2, CTSK, CTSB, CTSD, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, MAN2B1, SGSH, LAMP1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0D1); this module is the strongest magnitude-enriched module in the up-regulated list. Enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and substrate clearance were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA + ambiguous protein spots, inferred localization): Retained lipid substrate is proposed to stress the lysosomal limiting membrane, engaging damage sensing and repair (LGALS3, CHMP4B, ANXA1, ANXA6 transcripts up; several protein spots whose candidate lists include ANXA1 are among the largest increases). Spot identity is ambiguous and membrane rupture itself was not observed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sterol pool): Because sterol is inferred to be retained in the endolysosome rather than reaching the ER regulatory pool, SREBP-dependent uptake and synthesis genes remain high despite increased uptake (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, EBP, HMGCS1, SCD, ACSS2, SOAT1), creating a self-reinforcing loading cycle. ER cholesterol and SREBP processing were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Sustained catabolic/biosynthetic demand is accompanied by up-regulated TCA-cycle, pyruvate-import and electron-transport transcripts (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, DLD, ACO2, SLC25A1, NDUFA5, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5F1B, SDHB) with lower glycolytic transcripts (HK2, PFKP), predicting an oxidative bias; respiration was not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred consequence): Diversion of capacity toward lysosomal handling coincides with reduced transcripts for phagocytic/motility machinery and the immune protease CTSS (ACTB, MYH9, DOCK8, CTSS down), i.e. a lipid-handling-stressed rather than an interferon- or NF-kB-activated state (no core ISG module present; chemokine/NF-kB genes are up only at the background rate of this up-biased list)."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid-processing bottleneck, not interferon/NF-kB activation, distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 microglia under mock treatment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21067637395847494, "cosine_similarity": 0.39814485281464146, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mean_absolute_error": 0.596789644012945, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21067637395847494, "cosine_similarity": 0.39814485281464146, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.596789644012945, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.969961, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 95}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_093", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up); only signs, ranks and within-list enrichment are used, never absolute fold sizes.", "The CTSS transcript decrease reflects at least a partial decrease in CTSS protein and CTSS-selective endoproteolytic activity; if CTSS protein/activity is unchanged the mechanism fails at its first inferential step.", "The very low CTSS value is biological and not an artefact of normalisation or cell-composition differences, despite other highly expressed transcripts (ACTB -4.98, MT-ATP6 -3.44, MYH9 -6.42) also being strongly negative.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each (e.g. protein_spot:058 lists CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1) and are treated only as ambiguous proteoform-level signals, never as identified cathepsin protein amounts.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for compartment capacity; organelle number, luminal pH, hydrolase activity, cargo flux, lipid content and protein localisation were not measured in this dataset.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes and replicate numbers are not supplied, so some signal may be non-microglial or under-powered; no causal direction is established by these correlative APOE4-vs-APOE3 measurements.", "Background biochemical knowledge used to link CTSS to invariant-chain (CD74) processing and to microglial cargo proteolysis is unverified here, because literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally expand cargo uptake and lysosomal biogenesis/acidification machinery (TFEB/TFEC, 8/8 measured v-ATPase subunits, 14/16 measured acid hydrolases) while selectively collapsing CTSS transcript (-5.57, 17th lowest of 2212 selected rows) together with the CD-M6PR sorting receptor; we hypothesise that the resulting deficit in CTSS-dependent luminal endoproteolysis, not acidification or glycosidase capacity, is the rate-limiting step for degrading internalised protein-lipid cargo, so cargo residence time rises, an invariant-chain/CD74 processing signature and CLEAR-type compensation appear, and freed lipid is re-routed into esterification and lipogenesis (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1, SCD) rather than cleared. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assay: in matched mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, a CTSS-selective fluorogenic activity assay (inhibitor-subtracted) shows \u003e=2-fold lower CTSS activity in APOE4, while total cathepsin B/L activity, beta-hexosaminidase and beta-glucocerebrosidase activity, and v-ATPase-dependent acidification (LysoSensor ratiometric pH, bafilomycin-sensitive) are equal or higher in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows equal/higher CTSS activity, or a uniform decrease of all hydrolase activities plus raised lysosomal pH (general lysosomal failure), this selective-proteolysis mechanism is falsified.", "Cargo-flux prediction: pulse-chase of fluorescent protein-lipid cargo (DQ-BSA, or labelled apoE-lipoprotein/myelin) shows longer degradation half-life in APOE4 with equal or greater internalisation (pHrodo uptake) and equal or greater LAMP1+ area. Equal degradation half-life despite the transcript pattern would weaken the mechanism.", "Substrate-specific readout: the CTSS-dependent invariant-chain p10 fragment accumulates by immunoblot in APOE4 lysates relative to total CD74; absence of p10 accumulation would remove the main substrate-level support for a CTSS bottleneck.", "Phenocopy: selective CTSS inhibition or knockdown in APOE3 microglia reproduces slowed DQ-BSA hydrolysis, p10 accumulation, increased BODIPY-positive neutral lipid and induction of CLEAR-type transcripts (v-ATPase subunits, hydrolases). No change in cargo degradation or neutral lipid after CTSS loss falsifies the bottleneck assignment.", "Rescue and ordering: CTSS re-expression in APOE4 microglia restores cargo degradation rate and lowers neutral-lipid content while leaving the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript increase largely intact. If instead the OXPHOS/TCA program must be manipulated to restore cargo handling, or CTSS rescue changes nothing, the mitochondrial-primary alternative is favoured over this hypothesis.", "Specificity control: acidification rescue alone (e.g. acidic nanoparticles) does not normalise cargo degradation in APOE4, whereas exogenous lysosomal cysteine-protease supplementation does; the opposite result would point to an acidification rather than a proteolysis bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris scavenging receptors are higher in APOE4 (SCARB1 +8.22, ABCA7 +2.14, COLEC12 +1.53, CD36 +1.38, CD163 +1.38, MRC1 +1.36, TREM2 +1.28, APOE +1.24). Inferred (not measured): increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Measured: a coordinate lysosome-biogenesis-like transcript program (TFEB +2.38, TFEC +1.65; ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51 and all 8 measured v-ATPase subunits up; RAB7A +2.65, AP5M1 +9.79, SLC38A7 +7.49, LAMP1 +1.38, LGALS3 +2.37, GPNMB +1.11). Inferred: expansion and maintained/increased acidification of the degradative compartment, i.e. compensatory organelle capacity rather than proven per-organelle degradative flux.", "Measured discordance: within this uniformly up-shifted lysosomal set, CTSS is an extreme negative outlier (-5.57, 0.7th percentile; padj 1.2e-26) while glycosidases and lipid hydrolases rise strongly (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, DPP7 +4.52, CTSD +2.86, HEXB +2.17); the hydrolase-sorting receptor M6PR (-1.72) and IDS (-1.56) also fall while IGF2R rises (+2.02). Inferred: a selective, arm-specific deficit in cysteine-endoprotease capacity and in CD-M6PR-dependent hydrolase delivery, on a background of intact-to-increased acidification and sugar/lipid hydrolysis.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred, not measured): proteolytic cleavage of the protein scaffolds of internalised cargo (apolipoprotein/membrane-protein components, and the MHC-II invariant chain) becomes rate-limiting, lengthening cargo residence time and leaving partially degraded, lipid-rich luminal material. Consistent transcript marker: CD74 +3.84 (86.7th percentile) with only median-level CIITA (+1.50, 50.9th percentile), i.e. the Ii axis rises more than its main transcriptional driver; the p10 Ii fragment itself was not measured.", "Inferred consequence: lipid freed slowly from retained cargo, plus continued uptake, is re-esterified and shunted to storage/lipogenesis instead of efflux (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, LDLR +1.50, NPC2 +1.17); no lipid-droplet or efflux gene (PLIN2, LIPA, ABCA1/ABCG1, NPC1, PSAP, GRN) was measured, so storage is a prediction, not an observation.", "Parallel, non-bottleneck response: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts rise coherently (56-gene mitochondrial set median +2.62, 95% up; OGDH +8.63, MDH1 +8.71, MPC2 +8.02) while mitochondrially encoded transcripts trend down (MT-ATP6 -3.44). We place this downstream/parallel to the endolysosomal load rather than as the differentiating bottleneck, and this ordering is explicitly testable."], "title": "Selective loss of the cysteine endoprotease arm (CTSS) makes luminal proteolysis the bottleneck in an otherwise expanded, TFEB-type endolysosomal compartment in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27355010522956535, "cosine_similarity": 0.39808410015553514, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5903074433656958, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27355010522956535, "cosine_similarity": 0.39808410015553514, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5903074433656958, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6709815, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 96}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_032", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance differences translate at least partly into enzyme/receptor protein and therefore into flux; no sterol flux, cholesteryl-ester mass, filipin-stainable free cholesterol, SREBP-2 cleavage or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so every flux and localization statement is inference.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, NCEH1, HMGCR, SQLE) means it was not in the supplied selection and must not be read as unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are therefore compared only within this dataset, never converted to fold change.", "The strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 RNA rows positive; 85% of the q\u003c1e-20 subset) is treated as a shared baseline, so pathway claims rest on within-dataset relative enrichment and on per-gene significance rank rather than on sign alone.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and no sterol-pathway protein is present among the spots.", "APOE4 protein being a less efficient cholesterol acceptor than APOE3 is unverified background knowledge, not something measured in this dataset.", "Cell-composition differences in the microglia/astrocyte co-culture (e.g. gene:S100B +6.00) and normalization effects (gene:ACTB -4.98; gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35 are among the most significant rows) could inflate the apparent coordinate upregulation and are not controlled here.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed for pseudo-replication across single cells."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by running a net sterol-influx-and-storage program: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1, CD36, SCARB2, LDLR) and for ER esterification and neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, ACAT2, DGAT1, CIDEB) are coordinately higher, together with a lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase module and the APOE/ABCA7/PLTP/CYP27A1/CH25H disposal machinery. We propose that the rate-limiting step is regeneration of efflux-competent free cholesterol from the esterified/lysosomal pool, gated by SOAT1-driven esterification; because free sterol is diverted into esters rather than into the plasma-membrane and ER-accessible pools, the SREBP-2 arm (SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP) is not switched off, and uptake, synthesis and futile disposal signalling persist. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; all fluxes, sterol pools, localization and causal direction are inferred and unproven.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (K-604 or avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should (a) lower the cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio, (b) increase APOE/ABCA7-dependent cholesterol efflux to added acceptors, and (c) shift SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24 and the lysosomal hydrolase transcripts toward APOE3 levels. If SOAT1 inhibition raises free cholesterol but leaves efflux and these transcript programs unchanged, esterification is not the bottleneck and the mechanism is weakened; the bottleneck would instead be acceptor-side (APOE4 lipidation).", "ACCEPTOR TEST: supplying exogenous lipid-poor acceptors (ApoA-I or lipidated APOE3 particles) to APOE4 microglia should partially normalize sterol storage and the SREBP-2/lysosomal transcript programs only if the acceptor arm is limiting; full rescue by acceptor alone, with no additive effect of SOAT1 inhibition, would argue against the esterification bottleneck.", "MASS PREDICTION: quantitative sterol lipidomics should show APOE4 microglia with equal or higher total cholesterol than APOE3 but a higher cholesteryl-ester fraction and higher filipin-positive lysosomal/perinuclear sterol. Finding lower total cholesterol in APOE4 would replace this model with simple sterol deficiency driving SREBP-2.", "UPTAKE TEST: blocking SCARB1 (BLT-1) or CD36 should reduce esterified-sterol accumulation and lipid-droplet number in APOE4 microglia. No change would indicate the stored sterol derives mainly from de novo synthesis, contradicting Step 1.", "SENSING TEST: APOE4 microglia should show more nuclear-form SREBP-2 and higher SCAP-SREBP-2 ER-to-Golgi transit than APOE3 at matched total sterol. Equal SREBP-2 processing would break the inferential link in Step 4 while leaving the storage phenotype intact.", "ARTIFACT CONTROL: with spike-in-normalized or absolute quantification, the sterol-storage module (SOAT1, SCARB1, CD36, APOE, CYP27A1) should remain higher in APOE4 while the global positive shift shrinks. If the module's direction disappears under alternative normalization, the transcriptional evidence for this mechanism is invalidated."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, q=3.4e-117; gene:CD36 +1.38, q=1.8e-102; gene:SCARB2 +1.06, q=1.0e-120; gene:LDLR +1.50) and for gene:APOE itself (+1.24, q=6.9e-223, the most significant row supplied). Inferred, not measured: increased sterol/lipoprotein influx flux into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module is enriched above the already up-shifted background (20 lysosomal genes, mean +3.29 vs background +1.74, permutation p=0.005; gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB). We infer an expanded lysosomal compartment handling an increased internalized-lipid load; lysosomal cholesterol content itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck): elevated gene:SOAT1 (+1.25, q=1.8e-125, top 5% by significance), gene:ACAT2 (+2.04), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72) and gene:CIDEB (+1.06) are inferred to raise ER acyl-CoA:cholesterol acyltransferase flux, esterifying free cholesterol into cytosolic cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet stores. No cholesteryl-ester hydrolase (LIPA, NCEH1) appears among the supplied selected DE rows, so the return arm is not evidenced as co-upregulated. Consequence (inferred): the efflux-competent plasma-membrane free-cholesterol pool and the ER-accessible regulatory pool are depleted relative to total cell sterol.", "Step 4 (inferred sensing consequence): a low ER-accessible sterol pool keeps SCAP-SREBP-2 processing partly active, sustaining the biosynthetic/uptake transcripts gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87), gene:HMGCS1 (+1.08), gene:LSS (+2.27), gene:DHCR7 (+2.71), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69, q=2.4e-78), gene:EBP (+1.34) and gene:MYLIP (+1.28) despite adequate or excess total sterol. SREBP-2 cleavage state was not measured.", "Step 5 (compensatory disposal arm that does not resolve the bottleneck): the oxysterol side-path and acceptor machinery are up (gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, q=2.3e-82; gene:CH25H +1.62; gene:ABCA7 +2.14; gene:PLTP +1.06; gene:APOE +1.24). Assuming APOE4 protein is a poorer lipidation acceptor than APOE3 (unverified background knowledge; APOE protein and particle lipidation were not measured here), transcriptional upregulation of this arm does not translate into proportional net cholesterol export.", "Step 6 (net state): APOE4 microglia sit in a chronic esterified/lysosomal sterol-storage state with simultaneous uptake, synthesis and disposal signalling - a futile cycle - whereas APOE3 microglia resolve the same load through efflux. Reduced gene:OSBPL8 (-1.90) and gene:LBR (-1.69) are consistent with, but do not establish, altered non-vesicular sterol handling at ER contact sites."], "title": "SOAT1-dependent cholesteryl-ester sequestration limits the efflux-competent sterol pool in APOE4 microglia, locking in a futile uptake-storage-resynthesis cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28002679243598816, "cosine_similarity": 0.39790302517725484, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5919967637540453, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28002679243598816, "cosine_similarity": 0.39790302517725484, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5919967637540453, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73146375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 97}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_019", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive) in an unspecified log base; program directionality is therefore judged against that 77%-positive selected background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. RAC1, CDC42, ACTR2/3, ABCA1, PLIN2, LRP1, PICALM) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with unknown lag, the abundance of the corresponding machinery; no flux, enzymatic activity, membrane localization, lysosomal pH, lipid-droplet content or engulfment rate was measured here.", "2D protein spots are multi-candidate: each spot's effect is attributed to an unresolved set of candidate proteins (e.g. protein_spot:043-047 are ANXA1/TALDO1/ACTB/PSMD7-ambiguous), so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction testing, never as confirmation of a named protein.", "Genes within a program are correlated and were chosen from fixed a-priori canonical membership lists before directions were inspected; the reported counts are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test with independence.", "The isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast under mock is assumed to isolate genotype effects; astrocyte co-culture composition and any cell-proportion shift in the 10X Flex data could contribute to apparent bulk-like transcript differences.", "Reduced Rac2/DOCK8/myosin-II transcripts are assumed to lower engulfment/migration reserve; this is a predicted challenge-revealed deficit and is not claimed as an ongoing functional defect in the unchallenged mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by generalized activation but by a coordinated routing/cell-state change: transcripts for lipoprotein-scavenger receptors and the clathrin/dynamin/Arp2/3 endocytic module, for MITF/TFEB CLEAR-type endolysosomal machinery (v-ATPase, hydrolases, retromer/ESCRT), for sterol and fatty-acid synthesis/esterification, and for mitochondrial oxidative catabolism are coherently increased, while the leukocyte-specific Rac2/DOCK8/ARHGDIB/myosin-II actin module and glycolytic/oxidative-PPP entry transcripts are coherently decreased against a strongly up-skewed selected-DE background (1705/2212 positive). We propose that APOE4-associated lipid/lipoprotein cargo is preferentially internalized and routed into an expanded degradative-oxidative compartment with lipid re-esterification, at the expense of the actin machinery that supports motile, large-particle (cup-forming) phagocytosis. Whether this represents increased successful throughput or a lysosomal load that is only transcriptionally compensated is not resolved by abundance data; no causality is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective cargo-discrimination assay: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, uptake of soluble/receptor-mediated cargo (fluorescent AcLDL, oxLDL, dextran) should be equal or higher in APOE4, while engulfment of large particles requiring actin-cup formation (IgG-opsonized 2-6 um beads, synaptosomes, myelin debris) and random/chemotactic migration should be lower. If APOE4 shows reduced uptake of ALL cargo classes, or no deficit in large-particle engulfment, the proposed routing shift is wrong.", "Prospective rescue specificity: restoring the depleted actin module (expression of RAC2 or DOCK8, or a constitutively active Rac allele) should selectively rescue large-particle engulfment and lamellipodial spreading in APOE4 cells WITHOUT normalizing the lysosomal/CLEAR (GAA, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) or OXPHOS transcript signature. If the rescue also normalizes lysosomal/OXPHOS transcripts, the actin change is downstream of the metabolic/lysosomal state rather than a parallel routing arm.", "Prospective flux test distinguishing successful throughput from failed compensation: DQ-BSA/BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester degradation, mature cathepsin activity, and Seahorse OCR (basal and maximal, with lipid substrate) should be equal or increased in APOE4 under mock. Increased hydrolase and OXPHOS transcripts accompanied by REDUCED lysosomal proteolytic flux or reduced OCR would falsify the 'increased/adapted throughput' reading and favor an unresolved lysosomal lipid load with only transcriptional compensation.", "Prospective TFEB dependence: TFEB/MITF knockdown (or mTORC1 activation) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript increase and increase undegraded neutral-lipid/lipoprotein cargo, while leaving the Rac2/DOCK8/MYH9 decrease intact. If TFEB knockdown also restores Rac2-module transcripts, the two arms share an upstream regulator and the mechanism must be reformulated.", "Prospective proteoform test for protein spots: 2D-resolved immunoblot or targeted MS of the CTSD/CTSB and ANXA1/TALDO1 spot regions should show APOE4 shifting cathepsin signal from pro- to mature-form spots (consistent with protein_spot:052/053 up vs protein_spot:058/069 down) and should assign protein_spot:044-046 to ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) rather than TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32). Assignment of those spots to TALDO1, or no cathepsin proteoform redistribution, would remove the protein-level support for the expanded degradative compartment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and opsonin-linked surface uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:C1QA/B/C +1.13..+1.25, gene:FCGRT +4.42, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), predicting increased receptor-mediated internalization capacity rather than increased inflammatory activation (chemokine set is indistinguishable from the up-skewed background).", "Step 2 (routing): the internalization arm that is transcriptionally supported is the clathrin/dynamin/Arp2/3 endocytic module (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:ARPC1B +2.15, gene:ARPC5 +1.94, gene:ARPC4 +1.93, gene:CFL1 +1.80, gene:RHOA +1.61, gene:MYO1E +1.35, gene:IQGAP1 +1.23, 14/14 represented members positive), whereas the leukocyte Rho/Rac motility and cup-contractility module is selectively decreased (gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B/CYRIB -5.83, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:ARHGDIB -1.98, gene:RAC2 -1.97; 7/8 negative vs a 77% positive background). This is a routing change, not a global cytoskeletal loss.", "Step 3 (compartment expansion): increased delivery of lipidic cargo is accompanied by an MITF/TFEB-type endolysosomal biogenesis signature (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) with v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46; 29/31 represented members positive) plus retromer/ESCRT/late-endosome sorting (gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS18 +1.41, gene:AP5M1 +9.78).", "Step 4 (disposal of released lipid): sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification-storage transcripts rise coordinately (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:NPC2 +1.17; 14/14 positive), consistent with re-esterification/retention of liberated lipid rather than efflux.", "Step 5 (catabolic coupling): carbon handling is biased to mitochondrial oxidation (39/39 represented OXPHOS/TCA members positive, median +2.81; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5ME +5.20) while glycolytic entry and the oxidative PPP are decreased against background (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10; 6/11 negative, binomial p=0.023 vs 77% positive).", "Step 6 (state consequence, partly prospective): in the measured mock condition this yields a lipid-handling, degradative-oxidative APOE4 state with intact or increased receptor-mediated endocytic capacity; the decreased Rac2/DOCK8/myosin-II module predicts reduced motile and large-particle engulfment capacity, a deficit expected to become overt mainly under a phagocytic or migratory challenge rather than at baseline."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift cargo routing from Rac2/myosin-II actin-driven engulfment to receptor/clathrin-mediated lipid uptake feeding a TFEB-MITF-expanded, OXPHOS-coupled endolysosomal compartment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09393346379647749, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25164675251994834, "cosine_similarity": 0.39773228326483057, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.587378640776699, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09393346379647749, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25164675251994834, "cosine_similarity": 0.39773228326483057, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.587378640776699, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.89899275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 21}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_034", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are 'reported log fold change' of unspecified logarithm base; only relative comparisons (gene set versus the same-list background) are interpreted, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; the whole list is skewed positive (median 1.46, 77% positive), so every claim above is framed as set-versus-background rank enrichment, not as 'most genes go up'.", "MT- transcript effects reflect genuine mitochondrial transcript abundance differences rather than ambient RNA, probe-panel coverage or mitochondrial-fraction QC filtering in the 10X Flex workflow; only 6 of 13 mtDNA protein-coding genes appear in the list.", "Nuclear OXPHOS transcript increases translate at least partly into protein; no OXPHOS protein was measured here, and 2D protein spots carry 4.8 candidate genes on average and cannot identify a specific protein.", "Measured transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme/carrier availability; enzyme activity, metabolite flux, complex assembly and citrate localisation are inferred and unmeasured.", "Signals are attributed to microglia despite astrocyte co-culture, and no biological replicate count was supplied in the workbook."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coherent transcript-level increase in nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, TCA and mitochondrial-carrier genes that is NOT matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (4 of 6 measured MT- genes decreased against a background in which only 23% of selected genes are negative). We hypothesise that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, rather than the abundance of glycolytic enzymes, is the limiting step for assembled respiratory-chain capacity, and that the compensatory transcriptional program reroutes carbon away from complete glucose oxidation toward glutamate/BCAA anaplerosis and SLC25A1-dependent citrate export into SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1-directed lipid esterification. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, assembly and localisation statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating substrate test: uniformly labelled 13C-glucose versus 13C-glutamine tracing in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, a lower glucose-derived (M+2) fraction of citrate/malate and a higher glutamine/glutamate-derived fraction, together with higher glutamine-derived labelling of fatty acids. If APOE4 shows equal or greater glucose-derived citrate labelling and no anaplerotic shift, steps 4-6 are refuted.", "Assembly/capacity test: BN-PAGE plus quantitative immunoblot should show a reduced mtDNA-encoded core (MT-CO1/MT-ND1/MT-CYB) to nuclear-accessory (NDUFA/NDUFB, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) protein ratio and reduced assembled complex I/IV in APOE4, with lower maximal and spare respiratory capacity in permeabilised pyruvate/malate assays despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Equal or higher assembled complex I and maximal OCR in APOE4 would weaken the primary bottleneck.", "Stress test of the bottleneck: switching glucose for galactose (forcing ATP production through OXPHOS) should cause a larger ATP/viability deficit in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia. Equal tolerance would argue that respiratory capacity is not limiting.", "Efflux test: SLC25A1 knockdown or citrate-carrier inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty-acid content selectively in APOE4, without normalising the nuclear OXPHOS transcript elevation. Unchanged lipid content, or loss of the OXPHOS transcript signature after SLC25A1 knockdown, would falsify step 6 or invert the proposed direction.", "Rescue/attribution test: boosting mitochondrial translation capacity or mtDNA copy number (e.g. TFAM overexpression, or mitochondrially targeted rescue) should raise mtDNA-encoded core subunit protein and normalise both respiration and the compensatory nuclear OXPHOS transcript elevation in APOE4; if the nuclear transcript elevation persists unchanged while respiration is restored, the compensatory interpretation of step 3 fails.", "Negative control prediction: pharmacological hexokinase or PFK inhibition should NOT differentially impair APOE4 versus APOE3 ATP levels, because glycolytic enzyme abundance is not coherently changed (set p=0.69). A selective APOE4 vulnerability to glycolytic inhibition would favour a glycolysis-centred alternative over this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 cells carry a coordinate elevation of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (36/36 measured nuclear OXPHOS genes positive, set median 2.64 vs background median 1.46, Mann-Whitney p=1.2e-4; complex I NDUF subset 21/21 positive) together with TCA-cycle transcripts (8/8 positive, median 3.74, p=4.6e-3) and mitochondrial carrier/import transcripts (SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5, TOMM22, TIMM44).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, primary bottleneck): mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts do not follow the nuclear program (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; only MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 positive; binomial p=0.028 versus the 22.9% background negative rate). We infer, but did not measure, that per-cell mtDNA-encoded core protein becomes limiting for assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V.", "Step 3 (inferred activity/flux): assembly-limited electron transport lowers NADH re-oxidation capacity per TCA turn; the elevated nuclear OXPHOS/TCA/carrier transcripts are read as a compensatory, unsuccessful response rather than as proof of increased respiration. Supporting redox-shuttle and redox-buffer transcripts are raised (MDH1 8.72, GOT1 6.43, NNT 2.88).", "Step 4 (inferred carbon routing): glycolysis is not coordinately induced (glycolytic set median 2.06, Mann-Whitney p=0.69, not different from background; HK2 -3.67 and PFKP -3.08 decreased while SLC2A1, SLC2A3, GPI, ENO1, PFKM increased and PDP1 +3.00), so we infer glucose uptake is maintained for biosynthesis while upper-glycolytic pyruvate supply to the matrix is not the expanded input.", "Step 5 (inferred anaplerosis): amino-acid carbon entry is favoured instead (GLUD1 3.17, GLS 1.35, GOT1 6.43, BCAT1/BCAT2 up to 6.42, ABAT 1.54, SLC38A2 4.45), replenishing TCA intermediates whose oxidation is limited downstream.", "Step 6 (inferred efflux to lipid): raised SLC25A1 (4.47) is predicted to export citrate to the cytosol, where SREBF1 (4.67), SCD (4.17), DGAT1 (1.72), SOAT1 (1.25) and SCARB1 (8.22) direct carbon into fatty-acid desaturation and neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage; lipid pools themselves were not measured in this dataset."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry, not glycolytic induction, is the bottleneck: APOE4 microglia raise nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts fall, forcing amino-acid anaplerosis and citrate export to lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08708414872798434, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2790775746326002, "cosine_similarity": 0.3976782429582259, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5874563106796117, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08708414872798434, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2790775746326002, "cosine_similarity": 0.3976782429582259, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5874563106796117, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.51259125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 98}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_095", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and are therefore not an unbiased transcriptome; the global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46) is treated as a baseline against which modules are compared, not as evidence of global induction.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no fold-change conversion is assumed and effect magnitudes are used only for ranking and module comparison.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with several candidate genes each; spot-level changes are treated as ambiguous evidence about a protein family/processing state, never as unique protein identifications, and the same gene appearing in up and down spots is interpreted only as a possible redistribution among processed/modified forms.", "Transcript-level co-elevation of CLEAR-network members is used as an indicator of TFEB/MITF-associated transcriptional activity; neither TFEB nuclear localisation nor its activity was measured.", "Lysosomal lipid content, lysosomal pH, hydrolase enzymatic activity, lipid-droplet content and secretory flux are unmeasured in the supplied data and are inferred quantities in every step where they appear.", "Biological replicate structure is not supplied, and the microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous or driven by residual astrocyte signal.", "Causal direction (uptake load -\u003e hydrolase program, rather than an independent APOE4 transcriptional effect on both) is hypothesised, not established by these observational contrasts."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling, not in ER unfolded-protein signalling: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors and for a coordinated CLEAR-like set of luminal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and lysosomal transporters are elevated (module median ~2.10 vs a global selected-list median of ~1.46 on the reported log scale, permutation p~0.04, 91% of module members up), while the corresponding hydrolase- and v-ATPase-candidate protein spots are directionally split or decreased. We hypothesise that the bottleneck is conversion of this transcriptional capacity into mature, acid-active hydrolytic flux, so that lipid substrate persists in the endolysosome, ER sterol/lipid sensing continues to signal deficiency (SREBP-target transcripts remain high), and fatty acid is shunted into desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification. Causality is not established by these data; abundance is measured, flux, localisation and activity are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction: in live APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, per-cell lysosomal hydrolase activity (4-MU-glucoside for GBA, 4-MU-GlcNAc for HEXA/HEXB, DQ-BSA for bulk proteolysis) will increase far less than the corresponding transcripts (activity-to-transcript ratio clearly below 1) and will be accompanied by increased LAMP1-compartment filipin/BODIPY-lipid signal. If APOE4 instead shows hydrolase activity rising in proportion to transcript and no lipid accumulation, the capacity-limited bottleneck is wrong and the data are better described as a resolved, adaptive lysosome expansion.", "Restoring lysosomal degradative output in APOE4 (acidifying nanoparticles, GBA chaperone/ambroxol, or TFEB overexpression) should lower LAMP1-compartment lipid and neutral-lipid droplets and bring SREBP-target transcripts (SCD, DHCR24, SREBF1) toward APOE3 levels; if lysosomal lipid clears but SREBP targets stay elevated, step 5 is falsified.", "Bypassing the lysosome to load ER sterol directly (cyclodextrin-cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should suppress SREBP targets equally in both genotypes; a genotype-specific failure to suppress would relocate the defect to ER sterol sensing rather than lysosomal egress.", "Reducing cargo delivery (SCARB1 knockdown, or lipoprotein-free medium) should blunt the APOE4 lysosomal-hydrolase transcript module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H); if the module remains fully elevated, the substrate-driven direction of steps 1-3 is falsified and a direct APOE4 transcriptional effect is favoured.", "Rejection test of the assigned ER focus: XBP1 splicing, BiP/GRP94 protein and ATF4/CHOP reporter activity should not differ appreciably between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock; a clear coordinated UPR induction would support an ER proteostasis mechanism instead of this one.", "Mature-versus-pro cathepsin immunoblotting should show an APOE4 shift in the mature/pro ratio (or in glycoform pattern) rather than a uniform bulk increase; a uniform increase of mature cathepsins with no maturation shift would weaken step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/lipid uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:COLEC12, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE), which we infer increases delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosome; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred, unmeasured pool): The resulting luminal load of glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and sterol-ester substrate rises. No lipid species, lysosomal pH or LAMP1-compartment measurement is supplied, so this pool is inferred, not observed.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): A coherent, TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR-like transcriptional program is engaged - luminal glycosidases and sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GM2A), cathepsins (gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD), acidification subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6AP1), lysosomal transport/adaptor genes (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:IGF2R, gene:GNPTG) and the transcription factors gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF. Transcription-factor activity is inferred from target-transcript coherence, not measured.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck; measured spot abundance, inferred maturation): The transcript expansion is not matched by a uniform increase in mature hydrolase or acidification protein. Cathepsin-candidate spots run in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:052 +2.14 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85), v-ATPase V1-subunit-candidate spots are decreased (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93), and the CD-mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript is down (gene:M6PR -1.72) while gene:IGF2R is up. We infer a limit at hydrolase maturation/targeting or lumen acidification rather than at hydrolase gene expression. Spot identities are ambiguous (multiple candidate genes per spot).", "Step 5 (inferred): Because hydrolytic flux does not scale with substrate, undegraded lipid persists in the endolysosome and sterol/lipid delivered to the ER remains functionally low, so SREBP-driven lipogenic and sterol-pathway transcripts stay elevated instead of being suppressed (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1) - a futile uptake-plus-synthesis configuration.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred consequence): Newly available fatty acid is desaturated and esterified into neutral-lipid stores (gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:MGLL +4.00), while several canonical microglial secretory/effector transcripts are among the most decreased (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:MYH9 -6.36, gene:SPN -7.29), consistent with a storage-biased, less secretory state.", "Step 7 (explicit rejection of the assigned focus): ER proteostasis/UPR is not supported as the primary axis. Among measured UPR genes the module median (+1.73) is indistinguishable from the global selected-list background (+1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.84) and the direction is incoherent (gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:MANF +2.95 up but gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:PDIA3 -1.26 down); ER-chaperone-candidate spots are near zero and not significant (protein_spot:001 -0.48, protein_spot:004 -0.68, protein_spot:005 -0.14, protein_spot:016 +0.14)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a substrate-driven, transcript-level lysosomal hydrolase expansion whose mature-enzyme/acidification output is the limiting step, diverting lipid into storage and sustaining SREBP-target expression"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1901696275264245, "cosine_similarity": 0.39753703329470425, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137216828478965, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1901696275264245, "cosine_similarity": 0.39753703329470425, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137216828478965, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90037425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 99}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_015", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); program direction was judged against that up-biased background, not 50/50, and absent genes (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, GRN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects are preserved on their reported scale; protein spots are log2 fold changes on a different platform, so cross-modality magnitudes are not directly comparable.", "Program members were chosen a priori from canonical pathway membership (background knowledge, unverified; literature retrieval was disabled) before inspecting sign, and all represented members were reported including opposite-direction ones; co-regulated members are not statistically independent, so the direction counts are descriptive.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but does not measure, SREBP proteolytic activation, TFEB nuclear localization, hydrolase activity, sterol pool size or lipid flux; each of these is inferred.", "Every protein spot carries 2-6 candidate identities; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot-level directions are used only for compatibility/contradiction testing.", "The mechanism describes the measured mock condition; any degradative or handling insufficiency would be expected to appear as reduced reserve under a future lipid/phagocytic challenge, which was not tested here.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein lipid, so uptake-driven load is plausible in this system; the deconvolution of microglial versus astrocytic signal in the supplied rows is assumed adequate."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia (isogenic, day 30, co-cultured with astrocytes), the dominant discovery-supported difference is a coordinated lipid-routing/cell-state change rather than a protein-folding unfolded-protein response: transcripts for lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24) and for esterification/storage (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) are higher together with a fully positive SREBP sterol/lipogenic module (13/13 represented members positive, e.g. gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17) and a large-magnitude TFEB/lysosomal module (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51). Co-activation of the sterol-synthesis arm (which is repressed when ER-accessible sterol is replete) with expanded uptake, esterification and lysosomal-hydrolase machinery is most parsimoniously explained by lipid being retained in lysosomal/cholesteryl-ester pools that do not replenish the ER regulatory pool. This is an inference about routing and pool distribution; no sterol pool, flux, hydrolase activity or SREBP cleavage was measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective pool measurement: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/PFO* probe or ER-membrane fractionation) should be lower while filipin-positive lysosomal sterol and LC-MS cholesteryl-ester content are higher. If ER-accessible sterol is equal or higher in APOE4 while gene:SREBF2/gene:HMGCS1/gene:LSS/gene:DHCR7 stay elevated, the routing/mis-sensing step is wrong and the mechanism is substantially weakened.", "Prospective perturbation A: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or lysosomal sterol mobilization (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) and reduce TFEB-target hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB, HEXA, GBA, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels. No coordinated reduction in either module would weaken the self-reinforcing-loop claim.", "Prospective perturbation B (discriminates from the folding-UPR alternative): ATF6 inhibition (Ceapin-A7) or ISR inhibition (ISRIB) should not normalize the lipogenic or lysosomal transcript modules in APOE4. If either drug largely abolishes the SREBP and TFEB signatures, a primary ER protein-folding stress mechanism is favored over lipid routing.", "Prospective flux/challenge test: with 13C-acetate labeling and pulse-chase of fluorescent lipoprotein or myelin debris, APOE4 microglia should show higher de novo sterol synthesis and higher uptake but not higher net sterol release to acceptor medium; under a lipid-loading challenge they should show slower cholesteryl-ester turnover than APOE3. Equal or greater net efflux and equal turnover in APOE4 would support the competing 'increased successful throughput/efflux' explanation instead.", "Prospective protein-level test: 2D-spot ambiguity should be resolved by targeted immunoblot/MS in APOE4 vs APOE3 for GRP94/HSPA5 and for mature versus pro-forms of CTSD/CTSB. The mechanism predicts no net increase in ER chaperones and a shift of cathepsin signal between processed forms rather than a uniform decrease; a clear, uniform reduction of total mature cathepsin protein despite the large transcript increases would indicate a degradative-capacity failure that this mechanism does not currently assert."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype raises microglial lipoprotein/lipid internalization capacity relative to APOE3: gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:TREM2 (+1.28), gene:APOE (+1.24), gene:IGF2R (+2.02) are higher, delivering more lipid substrate into the endolysosomal route (measured as transcript abundance; uptake flux inferred).", "Internalized and newly made sterol is preferentially routed into esterified/stored and lysosome-retained pools rather than to the ER-accessible regulatory pool: gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:FABP3 (+1.35), gene:FABP5 (+1.13) are higher, while lysosomal sterol/sphingolipid handling transcripts rise (gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA +6.71).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not replenished, SCAP-SREBP2/SREBP1 output remains high: every represented member of the sterol/lipogenic module is positive (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93), a direction bias unlikely even against this up-biased selected list (binomial p~0.03 versus the list background of 77% positive; members are co-regulated, so this is descriptive, not a formal enrichment).", "The rising substrate load engages a TFEB-type degradative expansion: gene:TFEB (+2.38) with hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:DNASE2 +2.03), v-ATPase subunits (9/9 represented positive: gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.29, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6AP2 +1.18), and trafficking/late-endosome components (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:ATG9A +1.68, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82).", "Partial offloading is attempted but does not close the loop: oxysterol-generating and LXR-linked transcripts rise (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:OSBPL1A +1.03) while gene:OSBPL8 (-1.90) falls, so continued uptake plus continued synthesis feed the same sequestered compartment - a self-reinforcing routing loop rather than a discrete bottleneck.", "Secondary, weaker consequences at the ER are compatible with lipid-loaded membranes but are not a canonical folding UPR: gene:ATF6 (+4.04), gene:DDIT3 (+2.79), gene:MANF (+2.95), gene:ERO1A (+1.21), gene:EIF2AK3 (+1.51), gene:CRELD2 (+1.01) rise, yet the ERAD/dislocation limb is negative against an up-biased list (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:NGLY1 -2.20, gene:PDIA3 -1.26) and the ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are not increased (protein_spot:001 -0.485 p=0.11; protein_spot:004 -0.678 p=0.14; protein_spot:005 -0.138 p=0.25, candidates include HSP90B1/HSPA5 among other proteins).", "Net predicted cell state: an APOE4 microglial phenotype with enlarged lysosomal/esterified lipid pools, elevated biosynthetic and degradative transcriptional capacity in the unstressed (mock) condition, and reduced spare capacity that would be revealed only by a lipid or phagocytic challenge; the mock data do not establish an ongoing degradative failure."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain a lipid-sequestering cell state: sterol routed to lysosomal and esterified pools keeps SREBP and TFEB programs simultaneously ON"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24033526566480817, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2829816438779266, "cosine_similarity": 0.3974317999265663, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5994045307443366, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24033526566480817, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2829816438779266, "cosine_similarity": 0.3974317999265663, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5994045307443366, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.873236, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 22}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_035", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base; only sign, rank, and relative magnitude within the same column are used, never absolute fold changes.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, and 77% of rows are positive (mean 1.39). All module claims are made relative to this internal background, not against zero.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a readout of transcriptional program state only; hydrolase activity, SREBP-2 cleavage, transporter function, sterol flux, esterification rate, and organelle localisation are inferred and unmeasured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a named protein pool.", "No lipid, sterol, cholesteryl-ester, lipid-droplet, imaging, or flux measurement is supplied; the pools central to this mechanism are inferred, not observed.", "Replicate number is not supplied and effects reach |LFC| \u003e 15, so individual gene magnitudes are treated as unreliable and only coordinated module direction is used.", "Astrocyte co-culture means the lipid environment is non-cell-autonomous; the transcript state may partly reflect astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply rather than a microglia-intrinsic block."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a transcriptionally expanded acidic degradative compartment (TFEB with coordinate hydrolase and v-ATPase subunit transcripts) that is not matched by a comparable increase in the sterol-export machinery of that compartment (NPC2 is the weakest member of the module). We hypothesise, without claiming causality has been established, that the rate-limiting step is transfer of liberated cholesterol from the endolysosomal lumen/limiting membrane into the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool; the resulting ER pool deficit keeps SCAP-SREBP-2 target transcription (SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, EBP, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) and uptake receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36) elevated, while the sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are diverted into esters (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, SREBF1), so whole-cell sterol excess (oxysterol-arm transcripts APOE, ABCA7, MYLIP, PLTP) coexists with a sensing-pool deficit. Nothing in the supplied data measures cholesterol, esters, droplets, flux, or localisation; every lipid pool in this claim is inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING ROUTE TEST: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with sterol by a route that bypasses endolysosomal export (cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or 25-hydroxycholesterol acting directly on INSIG/SCAP) should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS) to the same extent in both genotypes, whereas loading via a route that requires endolysosomal export (LDL, apoptotic cells, myelin) should suppress them significantly less in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal suppression by both routes, or equally impaired suppression by the bypass route, would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "ER-accessible cholesterol measured with a domain-4 perfringolysin sensor or ER-targeted reporter should be lower in APOE4 than APOE3 while filipin or sterol signal in LAMP1-positive compartments is higher. Equal or higher ER-accessible sterol in APOE4 with SREBP-2 targets still elevated would weaken the mechanism and favour a sensing-independent transcriptional difference.", "Relieving the postulated export step (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1 over-expression) in APOE4 should lower SREBF2-target transcripts and lysosomal-module transcripts toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h; no change in SREBP-2 targets after clearing lysosomal sterol would weaken the mechanism.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 should reduce cholesteryl-ester mass and droplet number and, because the ER free-sterol pool is relieved of esterification, should partially suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts. If SOAT1 inhibition removes droplets while SREBP-2 targets stay elevated and free sterol stays lysosomal, the esterification step (step 5) is dispensable and only the transport step survives.", "Quantitative, uniquely identified proteomics or activity assays should show lysosomal hydrolase protein and activity increased in APOE4 in proportion to their transcripts; a flat or reduced hydrolase protein level would show the lysosomal module is transcript-only compensation and would weaken step 2. The supplied gel spots already lean this way (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 are negative and list CTSB/CTSD/HEXB among candidates), so this is a live risk.", "PATHWAY-EXCLUSION TEST: if a UPR/ER-proteostasis mechanism were primary instead, HSPA5, XBP1 splicing, ATF4, DDIT3 protein, HERPUD1 and ER chaperones should be coordinately induced and thapsigargin sensitivity should differ by genotype. Coordinate UPR induction with no genotype difference in lysosomal sterol handling would replace this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 apoE protein (only the APOE transcript is measured, gene:APOE +1.24) is inferred to off-load lipid less efficiently to extracellular acceptors, so ingested and endogenous lipid remains inside the endolysosomal system. This step is entirely inferred, not measured here.", "A TFEB-associated lysosome-biogenesis program is transcriptionally up in APOE4 (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A); the a-priori lysosome gene list is the only module that exceeds the strongly up-shifted background of this selected DE list (mean 2.78 vs 1.39, permutation p = 0.007). Increased hydrolase activity and compartment volume are inferred, not measured.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK (inferred): export of liberated cholesterol from the endolysosome to the ER-accessible pool is not scaled with catabolic capacity. The only measured member of this export step, gene:NPC2 (+1.17), is the smallest change in the lysosomal module (hydrolases +5 to +10), and gene:OSBPL8 is down (-1.90); NPC1 and the GRAMD1/Aster transporters are absent from the supplied rows, so the block is postulated, not observed.", "A sub-set-point ER regulatory sterol pool is inferred to leave SCAP-SREBP-2 processing active, sustaining sterol-synthesis and uptake transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36; 12/13 up, all sterol-biosynthesis members up). Transcript abundance is measured; SREBP-2 cleavage, nuclear localisation, and sterol flux are inferred.", "Sterol and fatty acid arriving at the ER are inferred to be esterified and stored rather than returned to the sensing pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCP2 up), which would remove free cholesterol from the ER sensor and make the cycle self-sustaining.", "Because total cell sterol is inferred to be high while the ER pool is low, oxysterol-responsive transcripts rise in parallel (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:MYLIP, gene:PLTP). Simultaneous activity of the two opposing sensing arms is the signature predicted by mis-compartmentalisation rather than by simple sterol deficiency or simple sterol excess."], "title": "Endolysosome-to-ER cholesterol handoff, not degradative capacity, is the limiting step that locks APOE4 microglia into a sterol-synthesis-plus-storage state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10818594690396188, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2920502187440552, "cosine_similarity": 0.39728640443873703, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mean_absolute_error": 0.591378640776699, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10818594690396188, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2920502187440552, "cosine_similarity": 0.39728640443873703, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.591378640776699, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5112135, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 100}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list is dominated by a positive shift (1705 up vs 507 down, median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base), so only within-list relative ranks were interpreted, never raw direction alone.", "The list-wide positive shift may be partly technical (normalisation, ambient RNA, composition between genotypes); the mechanism relies on set-vs-set contrasts that are invariant to a constant offset.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for capacity of a compartment; enzymatic activity, protein amount, flux, localisation and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "TFEB/MITF transcript elevation is treated as a marker of a lysosomal-biogenesis program, not as evidence of TFEB nuclear translocation, which was not measured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each (ACTB appears in 25 spots, keratins in many), so no spot is treated as identifying a protein; spot data are used only as ambiguous, non-decisive context.", "No lipid, sterol, droplet, phagocytic-uptake or degradation-rate measurement is supplied; all lipid-pool and flux statements are predictions.", "Key egress genes (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, STARD3, PLIN2) are absent from the list, so 'egress not co-upregulated' is an inference about the measured subset, not evidence that egress genes are suppressed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects need not be microglia cell-autonomous.", "Replicate number is not supplied, and no set-level test survives multiple-testing correction across the ~24 sets examined."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 (vs APOE3) shows a coordinated transcript increase in post-uptake endocytic sorting and lysosomal luminal catabolic machinery (with TFEB/MITF also higher), while phagocytic-receptor and actomyosin engulfment transcripts are not elevated above the list-wide shift and several are strongly lower. Because transcripts for sterol/lipid export and efflux out of the endolysosome are only at background level, we hypothesise that lipid egress from the endolysosome to the ER, not particle uptake or degradative capacity, is the primary bottleneck; the ER then behaves as sterol-poor, sustaining an SREBP-type synthesis/uptake and esterification program that we infer (not measure) diverts retained lipid into esters and droplets. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating: treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, which mobilises sterol out of the endolysosome independently of NPC1, should produce a genotype x treatment interaction, normalising APOE4 SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, SCD) and lysosomal filipin/sterol signal toward APOE3. If cyclodextrin leaves the APOE4 SREBP-target elevation unchanged while 25-hydroxycholesterol suppresses it equally in both genotypes, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong and cell-autonomous SREBP hyperactivation is favoured.", "A pulse-chase with fluorescent myelin or apoptotic-cell cargo should show equal or lower initial internalisation rate in APOE4 (consistent with no elevation of phagocytic-receptor and actomyosin transcripts) but prolonged retention of undegraded lipid cargo in LAMP1-positive compartments at chase times. A higher initial uptake rate in APOE4 would weaken mechanism step 2 and shift the bottleneck upstream.", "Per-cell activity assays for GBA, HEXA/HEXB and CTSB in APOE4 should be equal to or higher than APOE3, matching the transcript ranks. Lower hydrolase activity in APOE4 would place the bottleneck in degradation rather than in egress and would falsify the core claim.", "Knockdown of TFEB should lower hydrolase transcripts in both genotypes and worsen APOE4 cargo/lipid retention, consistent with the catabolic up-regulation being compensatory. If TFEB knockdown instead reduces APOE4 lipid retention, the compensatory interpretation is wrong.", "Inhibiting sterol esterification (SOAT1 inhibitor) should increase free sterol and reduce esterified/droplet signal preferentially in APOE4 without correcting cargo retention; if it also corrects cargo retention, storage rather than egress is the limiting node.", "If the dominant genotype difference is instead mitochondrial (the OXPHOS/TCA transcript set ranked highest, e.g. OGDH, MDH1, ACO2), then respirometry should show a large APOE4 OCR difference while cyclodextrin has no effect on the lipid/SREBP readouts; that outcome would favour the alternative mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts of endosome-to-lysosome sorting/delivery machinery (gene:AP5M1, gene:DNM2, gene:VPS26A, gene:AP3D1, gene:SNX3, gene:RAB7A, gene:CLTB) and of lysosomal luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) plus V-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) rank above the list-wide positive shift in APOE4; gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are also higher. Inferred (not measured): higher biosynthetic capacity of the degradative compartment, consistent with a TFEB/MITF-type program.", "Measured: phagocytic-receptor transcripts (gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:CD36, gene:ITGB1, gene:SCARB1) and actin/Rho effector transcripts sit at or below the list-wide shift, with gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8 and gene:ARHGAP30 strongly lower. Inferred: the APOE4 shift is located in the post-internalisation endolysosomal arm rather than in actin-driven engulfment; engulfment rate is inferred, not measured.", "Measured: transcripts for endolysosomal sterol export and efflux (gene:NPC2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:OSBPL1A, gene:OSBPL8, gene:MYLIP) are at or below the list-wide shift, i.e. they are not co-scaled with the catabolic arm (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, STARD3 were not measured). Inferred: export flux out of the endolysosome becomes rate-limiting relative to delivery and hydrolysis.", "Inferred signalling consequence: ER sterol sensing reads as sterol-poor despite catabolic input, indicated by higher SREBP-pathway and target transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1, gene:AGPAT2). Activity of SREBP cleavage is inferred, not measured.", "Inferred routing: sustained synthesis plus esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCP2) diverts retained and newly made lipid into esters and cytoplasmic droplets; no lipid species or droplet measurement is supplied, so this pool is predicted, not observed.", "Inferred net state: a futile cycle in which APOE4 microglia continue to synthesise and internalise lipid while endolysosomal egress lags, progressively loading the degradative compartment and limiting further cargo clearance even though hydrolase transcript levels are high."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-scale endosome-to-lysosome delivery and luminal hydrolase capacity without matching sterol/lipid egress, making lysosome-to-ER lipid export the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2545155176242527, "cosine_similarity": 0.3971115074682345, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5888284789644013, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2545155176242527, "cosine_similarity": 0.3971115074682345, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5888284789644013, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.91928975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 101}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_084", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 in an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77% positive); absent genes (e.g. CPT1A, PDHA1, MPC1, PDK1-4, TFAM, mitoribosomal genes, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA) are unknown, not unchanged, so every program count is a lower bound and program-level directionality is judged against the 77% positive background, not 50/50.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity, not activity or flux: increased gene:MPC2/gene:PDP1/OXPHOS transcripts do not demonstrate higher pyruvate oxidation or respiration, and decreased gene:HK2/gene:PFKP does not demonstrate a rate-limiting glycolytic defect; PDH phosphorylation, oxygen consumption, extracellular acidification and 13C label routing are all unmeasured.", "2-D protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate identities each; median 5) and are used only for compatibility, never as confirmation of a single protein: the strongly increased series protein_spot:043-046 is compatible with ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) or TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32) or other co-migrating candidates, and CTSB/CTSD-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053/055/057 up; protein_spot:058/067/069 down), consistent with proform/mature or PTM redistribution rather than a net change in any one protein.", "TFEB/MiT-family involvement is inferred from transcript levels only; nuclear translocation, mTORC1 status and CLEAR-target occupancy were not measured, so the lysosomal expansion is described as coordinated, not as proven TFEB-driven.", "Cargo delivery, lysosomal degradative flux, lipid-droplet content and intracellular free fatty-acid or glucose pools are inferred, not observed; no lipid or metabolite measurement is supplied in this file.", "Pseudobulk 10X Flex effect sizes here are large and occasionally internally inconsistent (gene:ACTB -4.98; gene:MT-ND4L +1.95 versus gene:MT-ND4 -1.80 although they derive from one bicistronic mitochondrial transcript), so individual gene magnitudes and especially the mtDNA-encoded arm may carry quantification artefact; the mechanism rests on multi-gene direction, not on single magnitudes.", "Astrocyte co-culture means substrate availability (lactate, lipids) is partly non-cell-autonomous, and the genotype effect could be partly indirect; replicate number is not supplied in the workbook."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated cell-state change in carbon routing rather than by a single enzymatic block: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and endolysosomal hydrolysis are broadly increased, together with mitochondrial pyruvate import (gene:MPC2), PDH-activating phosphatase (gene:PDP1), TCA/anaplerotic enzymes and essentially every represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit (38/38 positive), while the high-flux glucose-committing isoforms (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3) and oxidative-PPP/transaldolase transcripts (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) are decreased against a discovery list that is 77% positive overall. We claim increased oxidative and catabolic capacity with re-routed glucose commitment (glycogen/storage and mitochondrial oxidation favoured over glycolytic-PPP flux), plus lipid esterification/storage (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). We do not claim a measured flux, an established bottleneck, or that this state is maladaptive in the mock condition; discordant mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 decreased) raise, but do not establish, the possibility that the expanded machinery is stoichiometrically incomplete and would be exposed only under an energetic challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock-treated APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, extracellular flux analysis should show equal or higher basal oxygen consumption and an equal or lower basal glycolytic rate (ECAR / glucose-derived lactate), with a larger fraction of basal OCR sensitive to acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows lower basal OCR with higher lactate output, the oxidative-routing mechanism is falsified.", "Prospective: 13C tracing should show increased [U-13C]glutamine and lysosome-derived fatty-acid contribution to TCA intermediates (citrate, malate, aspartate) in APOE4, with reduced [1,2-13C]glucose labelling of PPP-derived ribose/sedoheptulose relative to APOE3. Unchanged or increased glucose-to-PPP labelling would weaken step 5.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: blocking lysosomal acidification or lysosomal acid lipase/GAA-dependent cargo breakdown (bafilomycin A1, or LAL inhibition) should selectively collapse the APOE4 oxygen-consumption advantage and lower TCA intermediate labelling from cargo, with a much smaller effect in APOE3. If APOE4 respiration is insensitive to lysosomal inhibition, the lysosome-to-mitochondria substrate link (steps 1-3) is wrong and an autonomous mitochondrial-biogenesis mechanism should be preferred.", "Prospective challenge test of the mitonuclear caveat: BN-PAGE / complex-activity assays plus mtDNA copy number should show nuclear-encoded subunit protein increased with unchanged or reduced assembled complex I/III/IV/V activity per mitochondrion in APOE4, and reduced FCCP-stimulated spare respiratory capacity, while basal ATP-linked respiration is not deficient in mock. Equal assembled-complex activity and normal spare capacity would remove the incomplete-stoichiometry clause without refuting the routing claim; a basal ATP-linked respiration deficit in mock would instead favour a failed-compensation model.", "Prospective: MPC2 or PDP1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and force a compensatory lactate increase and, if the state is adaptive, impair lipid-cargo clearance and reduce lipid-droplet turnover more in APOE4 than APOE3; no genotype-differential effect would indicate that MPC2/PDP1 transcript increases are not functionally engaged.", "Prospective proteomic disambiguation: targeted MS or immunoblot should resolve protein_spot:043-046 as ANXA1 rather than TALDO1; detection of increased TALDO1 protein despite the decreased transcript would contradict the PPP de-emphasis component of step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA/B/C), which we infer raises delivery of lipid and glycoconjugate cargo to the endolysosome (delivery itself not measured).", "The endolysosomal degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H/ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C, with gene:TFEB and gene:MITF transcripts up), inferred to liberate fatty acids, sugars and amino acids intracellularly; TFEB nuclear localization and hydrolytic flux were not measured.", "Carbon entry into mitochondria is favoured at the transcript level: gene:MPC2 (+7.98) for pyruvate import and gene:PDP1 (+3.00, PDH-activating phosphatase) with gene:DLD (+5.54), alongside carriers gene:SLC25A1 (citrate), gene:SLC25A11 (oxoglutarate/malate), gene:SLC25A13 (aspartate-glutamate) and gene:SLC25A5 (ANT2); no PDK transcript is represented, so PDH phosphorylation state remains unknown.", "Anaplerotic and oxidative machinery expands coordinately: gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1 (+6.43), gene:MDH1 (+8.72), gene:OGDH (+8.56), gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB, gene:ME1, beta-oxidation/electron transfer gene:HADHA and gene:ETFA, and 38/38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2), an all-positive block that is unlikely against the 77% positive background.", "In parallel, glucose commitment to high-flux glycolysis and the oxidative PPP is de-emphasized while uptake capacity is retained: gene:HK2 (-3.67), gene:PFKP (-3.08), gene:HK3 (-1.12), gene:PGD (-1.30) and gene:TALDO1 (-2.32) decrease although gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3 and gene:SLC16A1 increase and gene:GYS1 (+6.10)/gene:UGP2 divert hexose toward glycogen; gene:GPI, gene:PFKM and gene:ENO1 remain up, so this is an isoform/branch re-routing rather than a global glycolytic shutdown.", "Lipid carbon that is not oxidized is esterified and stored (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:MGLL, gene:FABP5, gene:PLTP), giving the lipid-laden, DAM-like phenotype also indicated by gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:GPNMB and gene:APOE.", "Because mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts move in the opposite direction (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) while nuclear subunits rise, the expanded holo-complex pool may be stoichiometrically incomplete; we predict this manifests as reduced spare respiratory capacity under a future energetic or phagocytic challenge rather than as a deficit of ATP production in the measured mock state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-fed, mitochondrial-oxidative carbon-routing state with de-emphasized glycolytic/PPP commitment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2628401580327142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2684085312467874, "cosine_similarity": 0.39706925950973415, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5907346278317153, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2628401580327142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2684085312467874, "cosine_similarity": 0.39706925950973415, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5907346278317153, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1757125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 23}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77% positive); program directions are judged against that 77%-positive selected-list background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PICALM, SORL1, HMGCR, TYROBP, MYH10) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source, so effects are used as ordered, same-scale values and are not converted to fold changes; protein spots are on a separate log2 scale.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for machinery capacity, not for flux: no uptake rate, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, ER-accessible sterol, droplet content, respiration or migration measurement is supplied.", "The 2D-gel protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each; every candidate is retained and no spot is treated as evidence for a single named protein. Spot-level agreement is used only for compatibility/contradiction testing.", "The coherent nuclear-OXPHOS-up / mtDNA-down pattern is assumed to be at least partly biological, but it is the pattern most vulnerable to single-cell normalization or cell-composition differences between genotypes, so the mechanism does not depend on it.", "Effects reflect the genotype contrast in the mock (unchallenged) state; any capacity limitation is a predicted challenge-revealed property, not an observed mock defect.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein/debris cargo; the observed receptor and lysosomal program is assumed to act on such cargo, which was not directly measured."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state shift of the lipid-cargo handling axis rather than by a demonstrated degradative bottleneck: transcripts for scavenger/opsonic uptake receptors, branched-actin and clathrin/dynamin/retromer-ESCRT routing, and lysosomal acidification/hydrolase machinery are jointly elevated, while contractile/migratory actin transcripts fall; simultaneously sterol-esterification/neutral-lipid-storage transcripts and the full represented SREBP biosynthetic target set are elevated, a combination expected if internalized sterol is routed toward lysosome and stored ester/droplet pools rather than toward the ER regulatory sterol pool, so biosynthesis and uptake are not feedback-suppressed and lipid load is self-reinforcing. Increased degradative capacity, lipid flux, ER free-sterol levels and droplet content are inferred, not measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia, neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content (BODIPY, LipidTOX, or lipidomic CE species) and filipin-detectable free cholesterol should be higher, and ACAT/SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should lower ester/droplet content AND reduce the SREBP target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, SREBF2) toward APOE3 levels by restoring ER-accessible sterol. If blocking esterification leaves SREBP targets elevated and ER sterol unchanged, the sterol-diversion step is wrong.", "Prospective: cargo-handling flux in the measured (mock) condition should be equal or higher, not lower, in APOE4: pHrodo-myelin/bead uptake per cell, DQ-BSA dequenching, and LysoTracker/lysosomal pH should show intact or increased acidification and degradation. If APOE4 shows lower degradative flux with less acidic lysosomes despite elevated v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts, this coordinated-state model fails and a failed-compensation (degradative bottleneck) model is favored.", "Prospective challenge test: after an acute myelin or apoptotic-cell load, APOE4 should show earlier saturation - greater undigested cargo accumulation and larger droplet expansion than APOE3 - even though mock-state processing was equal or higher. Equal challenge performance would refute the predicted reduced reserve.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should collapse the v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript elevation and disproportionately worsen APOE4 cargo accumulation under challenge; if TFEB knockdown affects APOE4 and APOE3 identically, the lysosomal-expansion arm is not genotype-specific.", "Prospective: Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) should reduce APOE4-specific particle internalization more than APOE3, while APOE4 microglial migration/chemotaxis should be equal or reduced (consistent with lower MYH9/ACTB/RAC2/MYO1F transcripts). Increased APOE4 migration with unchanged uptake would contradict the routing-shift step.", "Prospective: unambiguous targeted proteomics or immunoblot for CTSB, CTSD, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 should show protein increases matching the transcript direction. Confirmed protein decreases (as the decreased hydrolase-candidate spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 and the ATP6V1E1-containing protein_spot:064/protein_spot:065 would allow) would seriously weaken the expanded-capacity claim and support post-transcriptional degradative failure."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcript-level capacity for particle/debris capture: scavenger and opsonic receptor transcripts are up (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:FCGRT +4.42, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD33 +1.78, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:FCGR1B, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:GAS6, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C; 18/19 represented members positive vs 77% positive in this selected list), with gene:CR1 (-2.35) the clear exception. Surface protein levels and actual uptake rate are not measured.", "Internalization/routing machinery is shifted toward branched-actin-dependent endocytosis and endosome maturation and away from contractile/migratory actin: gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:ARPC1B/ARPC4/ARPC5 (+1.9 to +2.2), gene:CFL1 +1.80, gene:CORO1B +2.15, gene:MYO1E +1.35, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:SNX15/16, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS18, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:RAB7A +2.65, versus gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:CORO2A -3.70, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:SYNJ1 -2.43, gene:RAC2 -1.97. Ambiguous 2D-gel spots containing actin/actin-regulator candidates are mostly increased (protein_spot:036 +0.68 [ACTR2, CAPG, ACTB, SERPINB1, KRT1], protein_spot:063 +0.68 [CAP1, GNS, PTGES2, ARPC2, EEF1A2], protein_spot:081 +1.20 and protein_spot:082 +0.68 [KRT10, ARPC5, ACTG2, KRT1, ...], protein_spot:092 +0.77 [PFN1, ...], protein_spot:028/029 +0.85/+0.93 [actin isoforms, VIM, ...]); these spots are multi-candidate and cannot confirm any single protein.", "The endolysosomal degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded rather than reduced: gene:TFEB +2.38 with every represented v-ATPase subunit positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, plus ATP6V1C1/E1/F, ATP6V0D1/D2) and hydrolases up (gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSH, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2); gene:CTSS -5.57 is the main exception. Lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and cargo degradation rate are unmeasured.", "Sterol and lipid liberated from routed cargo are inferred to be channelled into esterification and neutral-lipid storage/turnover instead of the ER-accessible regulatory pool: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:MGLL +4.00, with gene:TSPO +1.41 and gene:PLA2G7 +1.13; no efflux transporter (ABCA1/ABCG1) appears in the supplied selected list, so efflux status is unknown, not unchanged.", "Because ER-accessible free sterol is inferred to stay low, SREBP-dependent biosynthesis remains switched on instead of being suppressed by the lipid load: all 11 represented members are positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06) alongside gene:MYLIP +1.28 and gene:APOE +1.24, closing a self-reinforcing uptake-synthesis-storage loop.", "The energetic and anabolic demand of this state co-occurs with a strongly coherent nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript increase (36/36 represented members positive; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36) while most represented mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) and upper glycolysis transcripts split (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37 up but gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08). This nuclear/mtDNA mismatch predicts reduced reserve when demand rises but does not by itself establish an ongoing respiratory defect in the mock condition.", "Net predicted phenotype in mock: equal-or-higher steady-state cargo uptake and lysosomal processing with greater esterified/stored lipid and a mild secretory-inflammatory tone (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:MYD88 +2.34, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:CD74 +3.84, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:FTH1 +2.53); overt failure of degradation is expected only when an acute cargo challenge exceeds this already-loaded state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a constitutive lipid-cargo uptake-and-routing state in which sterol is diverted to esterification/storage, leaving SREBP-driven biosynthesis de-repressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21574434968797276, "cosine_similarity": 0.3965131680676369, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.586495145631068, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21574434968797276, "cosine_similarity": 0.3965131680676369, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "mean_absolute_error": 0.586495145631068, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.807802, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 24}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_075", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (77% positive, median +1.46); pathway claims are therefore judged against that background, and only the acid-hydrolase module exceeded it (permutation p~0.012).", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway engagement; enzymatic activity, flux, protein levels, subcellular sterol distribution and SREBP processing are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; spots are treated as weak, non-unique corroboration only, never as identified proteins.", "No lipid, lipid-droplet, cholesteryl-ester, lysosomal pH, or hydrolase-activity measurement is supplied, so the terminal lipid-accumulation step is a prediction, not an observation.", "Biological replicate structure is not supplied, and the extreme tail of reported fold changes (up to ~15) suggests residual normalization/selection artefact, so individual gene effects are weighted less than module-level direction.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may reflect non-cell-autonomous signalling or cell-type mixing rather than microglial autonomy.", "APOE genotype is assumed to act here through lipid handling rather than through a primary secretory/folding defect of the APOE protein itself; this is an assumption, not a measurement."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a rate-limiting step in lysosomal catabolism/egress of internalized lipid: uptake-receptor and acid-hydrolase transcripts are coordinately elevated (acid hydrolases are the only module whose median effect exceeds the dataset-wide upward shift, permutation p~0.012), yet SREBP-target transcripts for sterol synthesis, LDLR uptake and esterification remain high, which is the pattern expected if lysosome-derived sterol fails to reach the ER regulatory pool and lipid is instead shunted into esterified storage. ER-proteostasis/UPR activation is present but marginal and internally inconsistent, so it is proposed as a consequence rather than the primary bottleneck; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating sterol-clamp test: acute 25-hydroxycholesterol (which acts directly on ER INSIG/SCAP and bypasses lysosomal egress) should suppress LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR24 and SREBF-target transcripts to a similar degree in APOE4 and APOE3, whereas LDL or myelin loading (which requires lysosomal hydrolysis and egress) should suppress them significantly less in APOE4. If APOE4 also fails to respond to 25-hydroxycholesterol, the delivery-bottleneck model is wrong and the defect lies in the ER sensor itself.", "2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, which bypasses NPC1-dependent lysosomal cholesterol egress, should lower SREBP-target and acid-hydrolase transcripts and reduce neutral-lipid staining selectively in APOE4; no genotype-selective normalization would weaken the mechanism.", "Transcript-versus-flux dissociation: pulse-chase of fluorescent LDL/myelin plus fluorogenic GBA and HEXA substrates should show equal or lower per-cell lipid-degradation rate in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. Demonstrably faster lysosomal lipid clearance in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck step.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should shift APOE4 cells from cholesteryl-ester storage toward free sterol and produce greater suppression of LDLR/DHCR24/INSIG1 than in APOE3; unchanged SREBP-target transcripts would falsify the esterification-sink step.", "TFEB knockdown should reduce acid-hydrolase transcripts and worsen lipid accumulation in APOE4 without lowering SCARB1/LDLR transcripts; if TFEB loss instead reduces uptake-receptor transcripts, step 2 is misordered.", "ER-proteostasis control: chemical chaperone or IRE1/PERK inhibition should not normalize the lipid or hydrolase signature in APOE4. If UPR inhibition does normalize SREBP-target and hydrolase transcripts, the rejected ER-proteostasis mechanism should replace this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and phagocytic uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:FCGR1A). Inferred (not measured): increased delivery flux of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Measured: a coordinated acid-hydrolase transcript program is elevated (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:DPP7) together with TFEB/MITF, M6P-tagging and receptor transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A). Inferred: a TFEB/MITF-associated compensatory expansion of lysosomal catabolic capacity responding to substrate load; hydrolase enzymatic activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Inferred bottleneck: despite this transcriptional compensation, per-cell lysosomal lipid degradation and sterol egress remain rate-limiting, consistent with reduced ER-endosome lipid-transfer and fusion transcripts (gene:OSBPL8 -1.9, gene:STX17 -2.1) and a lysosomal-damage-associated marker (gene:LGALS3 +2.4). Lysosomal membrane integrity, sterol localization and transfer flux are inferred, not observed.", "Consequence for the ER sensor: because sterol does not reach the ER SCAP-INSIG regulatory pool, SREBP output is not switched off; SREBP-target transcripts stay elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:MYLIP, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1). SREBP cleavage, nuclear localization and ER sterol concentration were not measured.", "Feed-forward lipid loading: continued uptake plus continued synthesis exceeds disposal, and excess sterol/fatty acid is inferred to be esterified and stored via elevated esterification transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD) with autocrine APOE available (gene:APOE). Lipid droplets, cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol were not measured in this dataset.", "Secondary ER response: ER stress/UPR transcripts are only partly and inconsistently engaged (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:MANF, gene:EIF2AK3 up but gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1, gene:PDIA3 down), and protein spots containing ER chaperone candidates are not significant (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005, protein_spot:016), so lipid-bilayer/sterol-driven ER signalling is placed downstream of the lysosomal bottleneck rather than upstream of it."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck, not ER protein misfolding, uncouples ER sterol feedback in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21282781508020923, "cosine_similarity": 0.3963681762740832, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5987087378640776, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21282781508020923, "cosine_similarity": 0.3963681762740832, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5987087378640776, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.856818, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 102}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every row exceeds |effect| ~1 and all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, mean 1.39); all enrichment statements are therefore relative to this pre-filtered background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified, so RNA magnitudes are treated as ordinal (ranks/percentiles) and are not converted to fold changes or compared numerically with the log2 protein spot effects.", "Each protein spot carries 4.8 candidate genes on average; assignment of protein_spot:064/065 to V-ATPase V1E1 and of protein_spot:052/053/058/067/069 to cathepsins is provisional, and a spot change may reflect a different co-migrating protein or a proteoform (e.g. pro- versus mature enzyme) shift rather than total pool abundance.", "Transcript changes are assumed to be largely cell-intrinsic to microglia rather than driven by shifted microglial state proportions, astrocyte co-culture contribution, or ambient RNA in the 10X Flex data; replicate numbers were not supplied, so dispersion cannot be checked.", "Lipid pools, lysosomal pH, protease activity, cargo flux, and protein localization were not measured here; all statements about flux, acidification, activity and lipid storage are inferences, not observations.", "Key endolysosomal lipid-handling genes (NPC1, LIPA, GRN, PSAP, MCOLN1, LAMP2, TPP1, CTSA) are absent from the supplied rows, so the specific hydrolytic/egress step that limits throughput is not identified by these data.", "Causal direction between the lipid/uptake program and the lysosomal transcript program is not established; the observational design permits the reverse ordering."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia raise transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits and TFEB together with lipid-uptake/esterification genes, yet the 2D-gel protein spots containing lysosomal hydrolase and V-ATPase candidates show no corresponding increase (V1E1-containing spots decrease and cathepsin-containing spots are split). We hypothesise that the bottleneck is the conversion of this transcriptional lysosome-biogenesis response into functional degradative capacity (mature acid-hydrolase content plus V-ATPase-dependent acidification), so that endolysosomal cargo throughput per unit cargo delivered is lower in APOE4, undegraded lipidic cargo is retained and re-esterified, and the unresolved cargo sustains the TFEB program as a feed-forward, non-resolving compensation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knocking down SCARB1 (or removing lipoprotein cargo from the medium) in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and partially normalise the lysosomal transcript program, whereas TFEB overexpression alone should NOT normalise lipid accumulation because the limit is post-transcriptional. If TFEB overexpression fully rescues lipid accumulation while SCARB1 knockdown does not, the capacity-ceiling bottleneck is wrong and the defect is transcriptional insufficiency instead.", "Per-lysosome functional assay: single-cell imaging of DQ-BSA/BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester dequenching and cathepsin activity probes normalised to LAMP1 volume should show APOE4 with equal or lower degradative activity per unit lysosome volume, together with equal or higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH by ratiometric pH probe, despite higher hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts. Finding that APOE4 lysosomes are proportionally more acidic and more proteolytically active per unit volume, matching the transcript increase, would weaken the mechanism.", "Pulse-chase of fluorescent APOE-lipoprotein or myelin debris: APOE4 should internalise at an equal or greater rate but show delayed luminal degradation and prolonged LAMP1 colocalisation of the undegraded label. Equal degradation half-time between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Protein-level test of the spot inference: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS should show that in APOE4 the mature (processed) cathepsin D/B forms and the V-ATPase V1 subunit protein are not increased in proportion to their transcripts, and that ATP6V1E1 protein is decreased. Detection of proportionally increased mature hydrolase and V1 subunit protein would falsify step 3 and the primary bottleneck.", "Bafilomycin/chloroquine challenge: if capacity is already near ceiling, a sub-maximal V-ATPase inhibition should produce a disproportionately larger increase in undegraded cargo and lipid droplet content in APOE4 than APOE3. An equal or smaller APOE4 response would weaken the mechanism.", "CTSS specificity test: restoring CTSS expression in APOE4 microglia should improve degradation of CTSS-preferred substrates without normalising bulk lipid storage; if CTSS restoration alone fully normalises lipid accumulation, the bottleneck is a single protease deficit rather than a capacity ceiling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry markedly higher transcripts for scavenger-receptor lipid uptake and lipogenic/esterifying enzymes (gene:SCARB1 is in the top 1% of the supplied effect distribution; gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). We infer, but did not measure, a higher rate of lipid/lipoprotein cargo delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A coherent lysosome-biogenesis/CLEAR transcript program is elevated (gene:TFEB; hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD; V-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C; gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A). Its mean effect (2.76 for a 35-gene lysosome set) is well above the mean of all supplied differential rows (1.39; permutation p ~ 0.001), i.e. it is elevated beyond the pre-selected list's global upward shift.", "Step 3 (measured protein spots, inferred capacity): The proteomic layer does not mirror this amplification. Both spots whose candidate list contains the V-ATPase subunit V1E1 decrease (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) while gene:ATP6V1E1 RNA is up; cathepsin/hexosaminidase-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), and spots carrying any lysosomal candidate average +0.18 log2 versus +0.41 for all other spots. We therefore infer that acidification competence and mature hydrolase content do not scale with the transcript response.", "Step 4 (measured RNA): The protease repertoire is reconfigured rather than uniformly expanded - gene:CTSS is one of the most strongly decreased transcripts in the dataset while other cathepsins rise - so specific cargo-processing steps are not covered by the compensatory program.", "Step 5 (inferred): Degradative flux per unit delivered cargo falls; luminal lipid and protein cargo is retained, and sterol/fatty-acid that does escape hydrolysis is diverted to esterified storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), producing the neutral-lipid accumulation phenotype that this dataset does not itself measure.", "Step 6 (inferred, feed-forward): Cargo-loaded lysosomes sustain lysosome-surface signalling and TFEB-dependent transcription (gene:TFEB, gene:RRAGD, gene:LAMTOR5, gene:PIK3C3), keeping the transcript program chronically on without restoring capacity; gene:NPC2, a luminal sterol-transfer transcript, rises only weakly (35th percentile of the supplied effects), consistent with egress not scaling with the rest of the program."], "title": "A lysosomal capacity ceiling: APOE4 microglia amplify the CLEAR transcript program but do not convert it into matched hydrolase/V-ATPase protein output, so endolysosomal cargo processing becomes rate-limiting"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21825499390761732, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25516127179350284, "cosine_similarity": 0.3963280124777951, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6212783171521036, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21825499390761732, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25516127179350284, "cosine_similarity": 0.3963280124777951, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6212783171521036, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.407849, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 103}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of the 2212 rows are positive and all have |effect| \u003e 1, so direction of any single gene is weak evidence and only set-level contrasts against this biased background were used.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effects are not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for the capacity of a machinery, not for its flux or activity; lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity, sterol transport rate, droplet content and efflux were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots (e.g. protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053) contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are treated only as ambiguous, non-identifying corroboration; ACTB and cathepsins appear in many spots in both directions.", "Key carriers of the proposed bottleneck step (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2, STARD3) are absent from the supplied rows; their state is assumed, not observed.", "Astrocyte co-culture and medium supply extracellular lipoprotein substrate equally to both genotypes, so genotype-linked differences are not driven by unequal substrate availability.", "The genome-wide up-shift is assumed not to be purely a normalization/compositional artifact; set-level permutation against the observed background partially controls for it, but it cannot be excluded, and no causal direction is established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, endosome-to-lysosome trafficking and lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase machinery, while the step that returns liberated sterol from the endolysosome to the ER/plasma membrane and exports it (APOE-dependent efflux) remains the flux-limiting bottleneck; the resulting ER sterol under-sensing keeps the SREBP-axis transcriptional program on and routes lipid into SOAT1/DGAT1-mediated esterified storage. The assigned actin/cytoskeletal engulfment mechanism is rejected as primary because that module is the only tested set that fails to share the global up-shift and is internally contradictory.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Sterol localization: filipin plus LAMP1 imaging and lipidomics in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments AND increased cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid droplets in APOE4. If neither lysosomal free cholesterol nor cholesteryl ester is elevated in APOE4, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Discriminating perturbation (uptake vs egress): loading both genotypes with a matched, saturating dose of fluorescent acLDL or myelin, then chasing. The model predicts equal or higher internalization per cell in APOE4 with slower conversion of internalized label to effluxed/exported sterol (reduced apoA-I/HDL-acceptor efflux of labelled cholesterol and slower loss of lysosomal label). If APOE4 instead shows reduced internalization with normal fractional efflux, the mechanism is falsified and the actin/engulfment alternative is supported.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe or CI-976): should reduce neutral-lipid droplets in APOE4 more than in APOE3 and, by raising ER free sterol, should suppress the SREBP-2 targets HMGCS1, LDLR and DHCR24 preferentially in APOE4. Persistence of elevated SREBP-2 targets and unchanged droplet content in APOE4 after SOAT1 inhibition would weaken the mechanism.", "Bypassing the egress step with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or supplying exogenous lipid-free apoA-I as an acceptor, should normalize the APOE4 SREBP-axis and lysosomal/TFEB target transcripts toward APOE3 within 24-48 h without requiring changes in uptake-receptor transcripts. No normalization would weaken the mechanism.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown should collapse the APOE4-specific hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) but should not by itself normalize cholesteryl-ester storage; if TFEB knockdown removes the storage phenotype entirely, the bottleneck lies in lysosomal biogenesis rather than in sterol egress.", "Cytoskeletal counter-test: quantitative bead/zymosan phagocytic index and phalloidin phagocytic-cup counts should not be lower in APOE4 despite gene:ACTB (-4.98) and gene:MYH9 (-6.38); a reproducible reduction in engulfment rate with intact sterol egress would falsify this hypothesis in favour of the rejected cytoskeletal mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipid/particle uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:STAB1, gene:COLEC12). Inferred (not measured): increased receptor-mediated lipoprotein/lipid influx per cell.", "Measured: transcripts for clathrin/dynamin and endosome-maturation and retromer components are higher (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1). Inferred: cargo delivery to late endosomes/lysosomes is maintained or increased, i.e. uptake and delivery are not the bottleneck.", "Measured: a coherent lysosomal-biogenesis-like program is up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF; hydrolases 15/15 up, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD; v-ATPase 9/9 up, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C; gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2). Inferred (not measured): expanded acidified degradative compartment, consistent with a compensatory response to a downstream disposal limit rather than to a hydrolase deficit.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred, not directly measured): transfer of hydrolysis-liberated free cholesterol out of the endolysosomal lumen to the ER/plasma membrane and its subsequent APOE-dependent efflux is rate-limiting in APOE4, because APOE4 is a poorer lipid acceptor; the key carriers of this step (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1) are absent from the supplied rows, so the bottleneck is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "Measured consequence at the ER sensor: the SREBP axis and its sterol-synthesis targets are up rather than suppressed (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD +4.17). Inferred: the ER sterol sensor behaves as if sterol-poor despite high uptake and hydrolase expression, the signature expected when sterol is trapped upstream of the ER.", "Measured: esterification/storage transcripts are up (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL, gene:ABHD5) while measured efflux capacity is only weakly changed (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14; ABCA1 unmeasured). Inferred endpoint (not measured here): net accumulation of cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid droplets and lysosomal lipid, i.e. a futile uptake-synthesis-storage cycle rather than clearance."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand endolysosomal uptake and hydrolase capacity but are limited at post-lysosomal sterol egress/efflux, diverting lipid into SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23833526902974472, "cosine_similarity": 0.39630420053406945, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5822297734627832, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23833526902974472, "cosine_similarity": 0.39630420053406945, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5822297734627832, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79592625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 104}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_042", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all RNA statements are relative comparisons within this dataset and no fold-change is converted to a linear scale.", "The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression result: every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and no row has |effect| \u003c 1. Absence of a gene (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B, PLIN2, LPL, P2RY12) therefore means it did not pass the filter, not that it is unchanged and not that it was unmeasured biologically. Enrichment statements are conditional on this filtered background.", "The global RNA shift is strongly positive (median +1.46, 1705 of 2212 rows up). We assume part of this is a normalization, composition or selection artifact rather than a true whole-transcriptome upshift, so all pathway claims are made as within-dataset percentiles or as Mann-Whitney comparisons against the full 2212-row distribution, never against zero.", "The extreme positive tail (86 rows with |effect| \u003e 6, top gene ITGA6 at +15.5, with essentially zero correlation between |effect| and -log10 adjusted p, r = -0.04) is treated as low-precision. We therefore weight coordinated, highly significant, moderate-effect modules over single extreme values; SCARB1 is retained because it combines a 99th-percentile effect with adjusted p 3.4e-117.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel-style features with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no spot is used as primary evidence.", "No lipid, sterol, cholesteryl-ester, filipin, lysosomal-pH, flux or imaging measurement is supplied. All statements about sterol pools, lysosomal cholesterol, lipid droplets, esterification flux, synthesis flux, localization and lysosome number are inferences, not observations.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so effect precision cannot be judged; the RNA and protein assays may come from different cultures and are not paired.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so a fraction of the RNA and protein signal may be non-cell-autonomous or of astrocytic origin; the deconvolution is not supplied.", "SREBP, TFEB, LXR and TGF-beta pathway activities are inferred from target-gene transcript patterns only; no phosphorylation, nuclear-localization or reporter measurement is supplied.", "Causality is not established. The design is a genotype contrast at a single timepoint under mock treatment, so uptake, lysosomal expansion, esterification and identity loss are correlated features whose ordering is proposed, not demonstrated."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a post-uptake endolysosomal handling bottleneck for sterol-rich cargo. Transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake (SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of this dataset, CD36, MRC1, CD163, COLEC12, TREM2, CD14, C1Q) and a coordinated MiT/TFE-driven CLEAR lysosomal program (TFEB, MITF, and 24 of 26 detected lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts) are elevated, while the genes that would move sterol out of the endolysosome and into membranes are not correspondingly elevated (NPC2 below the global median, M6PR and OSBPL8 down; NPC1, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1 not measured). Sterol that does reach the ER is inferred to be diverted into esterified/neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, ACAT2, DGAT1, SREBF1, SCD up) rather than into new synthesis, since the canonical SREBP2 de novo module is absent or sub-median (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, MVD, FDPS not in the differential list; SREBF2 and HMGCS1 below the global median). The lipid-laden lysosomal state co-occurs with collapse of the TGF-beta-dependent homeostatic microglial program (TGFBR1, CSF1, CTSS all in the bottom decile). Causality is not established by these data; the sterol pools themselves were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION (bottleneck localization by epistasis/occlusion). Treat isogenic APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with the NPC1 sterol-egress blocker U18666A. If the APOE4 bottleneck is already at lysosomal sterol egress, U18666A should shift APOE3 cells substantially toward the APOE4 signature (up SCARB1, SREBF1, SCD, SOAT1, TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A; down CTSS, TGFBR1) while producing a markedly smaller incremental shift in APOE4 cells, i.e. a significant genotype x drug interaction with occlusion in APOE4. If instead APOE4 cells shift by the same or a larger increment than APOE3, the egress step is not the operative bottleneck and the mechanism is falsified.", "Direct pool test. Filipin or cholesterol-oxidase quantification with LAMP1 co-staining should show higher unesterified cholesterol in the LAMP1-positive compartment of APOE4 than APOE3, and lipidomics should show a higher cholesteryl-ester to free-cholesterol ratio, while 13C- or D-acetate labelling should show NO increase in de novo sterol synthesis flux in APOE4. Finding increased acetate-to-cholesterol flux, or no excess LAMP1-associated unesterified cholesterol, would weaken the mechanism and favour a synthesis-driven model.", "Cargo-mobilization rescue. 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (24-48 h, sub-cytotoxic) should mobilize trapped lysosomal sterol and normalize the APOE4-specific transcripts SCARB1, SREBF1, SCD, SOAT1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A and GPNMB toward APOE3 levels, with a significantly larger normalization in APOE4 than in APOE3. Failure of cyclodextrin to reduce this signature in APOE4 would weaken step 3.", "Ordering test that separates storage from the bottleneck. SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown should raise free cholesterol and reduce neutral-lipid droplets in APOE4 WITHOUT reversing the TFEB/CLEAR program, because esterification is placed downstream of the bottleneck. If SOAT1 inhibition instead normalizes TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A and SCARB1, esterification rather than lysosomal egress is primary and step 3 is wrong.", "Identity-versus-lipid test. TGF-beta1 supplementation or TGFBR1 restoration in APOE4 microglia should restore CTSS, TGFBR1 and CSF1 transcripts while leaving lysosomal unesterified cholesterol and the CLEAR transcript program largely elevated. If TGF-beta1 add-back fully normalizes lysosomal cholesterol and the CLEAR program, then loss of homeostatic identity is upstream of the lipid phenotype and the proposed direction in step 5 is falsified.", "Uptake-limb test. SCARB1 knockdown or blocking antibody in APOE4 microglia should reduce lipoprotein-derived sterol delivery, lower LAMP1-associated unesterified cholesterol and partially reverse the CLEAR and SOAT1 transcript program. If SCARB1 loss reduces uptake but leaves lysosomal cholesterol and the CLEAR program unchanged, the uptake limb (step 1) is not a necessary contributor.", "Negative/specificity control. Because ABCA1, ABCG1 and NR1H3 were not measured here, direct measurement of ApoA-I- and ApoE-acceptor-dependent cholesterol efflux is required. The mechanism predicts efflux capacity is at most modestly reduced and is NOT the primary lesion; a large, selective APOE4 efflux defect that is rescued by LXR agonism and that by itself normalizes the CLEAR and SREBF1/SCD program would replace this mechanism with an export-block model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein and scavenger uptake receptors, most strikingly SCARB1 (effect +8.22, 99.1st percentile of all 2212 differential RNA rows, adjusted p 3.4e-117) plus CD36, MRC1, CD163, COLEC12, TREM2, CD14 and C1QA/B/C. We infer, but did not measure, an increased endocytic delivery of sterol- and lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred organelle state): The MiT/TFE lysosomal biogenesis program is engaged: TFEB (+2.39) and MITF (+1.03) are up and 24 of 26 detected CLEAR-network transcripts are up with a median effect of +1.91 versus a global median of +1.46 (one-sided Mann-Whitney p = 0.02), including GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, CTSH, DPP7, MAN2B1, ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1, ATP6V1E1 and LAMP1. We read this as a compensatory expansion response, i.e. an inference that cargo load exceeds per-lysosome degradative capacity, not as a direct measurement of lysosome number or acidity.", "Step 3 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK; partly measured, largely inferred): Sterol egress from the endolysosome is the rate-limiting step and is not scaled with steps 1-2. The egress-associated transcripts that were measured lag the dataset: NPC2 +1.17 (34.7th percentile, below the global median), M6PR -1.72, OSBPL8 -1.90 (12.7th percentile, adjusted p 3.7e-33). NPC1, STARD3, STARD4, GRAMD1A/B, LIPA and OSBP were not measured, so the egress module is only partially observed. The consequence, increased residence time and accumulation of unesterified sterol inside LAMP1-positive compartments, is an unmeasured pool and is asserted as inference only.", "Step 4 (measured RNA; inferred routing): Sterol and fatty-acyl carbon that does reach the ER is routed to esterification and neutral-lipid storage rather than to new sterol synthesis. SOAT1 (+1.25, adjusted p 1.8e-125), ACAT2 (+2.04), DGAT1 (+1.72), SREBF1 (+4.67, 91.8th percentile), SCD (+4.17, adjusted p 1.9e-165) and the post-squalene reductases DHCR24 (+3.69) and DHCR7 (+2.71) are up, whereas the pre-squalene SREBP2 flux module is not: HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, MVD, MVK, PMVK and FDPS are absent from the differential list and SREBF2 (+1.06, 27.5th pct) and HMGCS1 (+1.08, 28.3rd pct) sit below the global median. Cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred causal direction): The same cells lose the TGF-beta-dependent homeostatic microglial program, TGFBR1 -2.19 (10.3rd percentile, adjusted p ~0), CSF1 -5.91 (0.5th percentile) and CTSS -5.57 (0.7th percentile), while GPNMB (adjusted p ~0) and APOE (adjusted p 6.9e-223) mark a phagolysosomal, lipid-handling state. We propose the lysosomal lipid burden of steps 2-4 sustains this identity switch; the reverse direction, identity loss driving the lipid program, is not excluded by these data.", "Step 6 (measured protein spots; deliberately weak): Lysosomal hydrolase transcript induction is not mirrored by a uniform protein increase. Spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins move in both directions: protein_spot:052 (+2.14, candidates include CTSL) and protein_spot:053 (+1.54, candidates include CTSD) are up while protein_spot:058 (-0.85), protein_spot:067 (-1.00, candidates include CTSB and HEXB) and protein_spot:069 (-1.38) are down. Because each spot has several candidate genes and cannot be assigned to one protein, this is only consistent with, and does not demonstrate, a mismatch between transcriptional lysosome biogenesis and delivered hydrolase capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at lysosomal sterol egress, not at de novo sterol synthesis: high-uptake, CLEAR-expanded endolysosomes route sterol into esterified storage while TGF-beta homeostatic identity is lost"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08904109589041095, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25363717489024146, "cosine_similarity": 0.39561631612125236, "direction_accuracy": 0.1488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5888964401294499, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08904109589041095, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25363717489024146, "cosine_similarity": 0.39561631612125236, "direction_accuracy": 0.1488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5888964401294499, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.722552, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 105}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_043", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1 log unit, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive), not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are relative to this already up-shifted background and the logarithm base is unspecified, so magnitudes are treated as ordinal.", "Coordinated transcript increases in hydrolase, v-ATPase and MiT/TFE genes are read as a demand/biogenesis signal; they are not evidence of increased lysosomal enzymatic activity, acidification or degradative flux, none of which were measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are used only as weak, non-attributive evidence of transcript-protein discordance. The protein series is itself globally up-shifted (70% of spots positive, median +0.485 log2), so individual spot signs are weakly informative.", "No lipidomic, imaging, pH, cargo-degradation, respirometry or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied; the lipid endpoint and every flux/localization statement is predicted, not observed.", "The measured population is assumed to be the microglial compartment of a microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30; astrocyte contribution and replicate structure are not stated in the workbook metadata.", "APOE4-specific background biology (poor APOE lipidation, lipid-droplet-laden microglia) is unverified background knowledge, not supported by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in late-endosomal/lysosomal cargo throughput: sustained lipid/lipoprotein cargo influx exceeds terminal luminal degradation and egress capacity, which is associated with a coordinated MiT/TFE-type transcriptional expansion of hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits (a demand signal, not proof of surplus capacity), while the lipid carbon that is released is routed preferentially into mitochondrial oxidative catabolism and into re-esterification/neutral-lipid storage rather than efflux. The transcript program is measured; lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, cargo half-life, lipid pools and all fluxes are inferred and were not measured here, so causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Primary discriminator: in a pulse-chase with defined lipid-rich cargo (fluorescent myelin debris or labelled lipoprotein) delivered at matched load, APOE4 microglia should show longer intracellular cargo half-life and greater accumulation of undegraded cargo in LAMP1-positive compartments than APOE3, despite equal or higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears the same cargo load at an equal or faster rate, the throughput bottleneck is rejected.", "Capacity test: measured per-LAMP1 mature cathepsin B/D (mature/pro ratio by immunoblot) and in-situ cathepsin/GBA/HEXA activity should be unchanged or reduced in APOE4 relative to the size of the transcript increase, and lysosomal pH should be equal or higher (less acidic). If activity and acidification scale proportionally with the transcript increases, step 4 fails and the program should instead be read as increased, not deficient, capacity.", "Bypass test that separates the lysosome from mitochondria: delivering cholesterol/fatty acid directly to the cytosol-ER route (HP-beta-cyclodextrin sterol complex or albumin-bound oleate) in APOE3 should reproduce the storage and oxidative transcript pattern, whereas in APOE4 it should NOT further worsen LAMP1-compartment cargo accumulation. If the OXPHOS/TCA signature in APOE4 is unaffected by relieving lysosomal load, the mitochondrial program is primary rather than downstream and this mechanism is weakened.", "Rescue: raising lysosomal capacity (TFEB overexpression or acidifying nanoparticle treatment) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester content in APOE4 toward APOE3 without normalizing APOE genotype; no reduction in stored lipid would weaken the causal chain from step 2 to step 6.", "Phenocopy: sub-lethal v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or cathepsin inhibition in APOE3 microglia should shift them toward the APOE4 pattern (higher TFEB/hydrolase transcripts, increased LAMP1-compartment lipid, increased droplet content). Failure to phenocopy would argue the APOE4 difference does not act through lysosomal throughput.", "Negative control on the inflammatory alternative: the difference should persist without a coordinated cytokine/NF-kB induction, consistent with the flat inflammatory transcript set here (mean +1.12, p~0.66). A dominant IL1B/TNF-driven signature under mock conditions would favour an inflammatory-activation explanation instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (upstream load, partly inferred): APOE4 microglia maintain or increase the lipid/lipoprotein uptake and opsonic-recognition arm at the transcript level (gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:IGF2R), so cargo delivery into the endolysosomal system is not transcriptionally downregulated.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred): terminal processing and egress of this lipid-rich cargo within the late endosome/lysosome becomes rate-limiting in APOE4; cargo residence time and luminal lipid load rise. This step is an inference about flux, not an observed pool.", "Step 3 (compensatory transcription, measured): a MiT/TFE-type response raises lysosomal biogenesis transcripts - gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) with acid hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1; set mean +2.8 log units, permutation p~0.014 against the dataset background), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1; set mean +2.56, p~0.07), M6P tagging (gene:GNPTG) and structural/limiting-membrane genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:NPC2).", "Step 4 (capacity shortfall, inferred): the transcript expansion is not uniformly mirrored at the protein-spot level; cathepsin- and v-ATPase-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), and selected delivery/hydrolase genes fall (gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:IDS -1.56, gene:CTSS -5.57), so per-lysosome mature hydrolase activity and acidification may lag the transcriptional demand signal.", "Step 5 (downstream carbon routing, measured transcripts / inferred flux): fatty acids and other catabolites that do exit are matched by an oxidative rather than glycolytic transcriptional bias - TCA and mitochondrial carrier genes (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11) and OXPHOS subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5; 38-gene set mean +2.81, p~0.0004) rise while glycolysis does not (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08; 9-gene set mean +0.67, p~0.80).", "Step 6 (predicted lipid endpoint, not measured): the remaining lipid is esterified and stored rather than effluxed (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:MGLL), predicting higher cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplet content and LAMP1-compartment lipid in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions."], "title": "Lysosomal cargo-throughput bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a compensatory MiT/TFE hydrolase-acidification program with lipid diverted to mitochondrial oxidation and neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20636313463283462, "cosine_similarity": 0.3953341072043016, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961423948220065, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20636313463283462, "cosine_similarity": 0.3953341072043016, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961423948220065, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.684675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 106}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_036", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% up, median +1.46) in an unspecified logarithm base; enrichment claims are therefore made only relative to this internal up-shifted background, and absolute magnitudes are treated as ordinal.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with delay, the corresponding enzyme and transporter capacity; no hydrolase activity, flux, membrane potential, lysosomal pH or localization measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a unique protein identification and no spot is used as primary evidence for a pathway.", "Lipid abundance, lipid droplets, ABCA1/ABCG1 efflux, LIPA, PLIN2 and CPT1A/CPT2 were not measured; the lipid endpoint and the carnitine-shuttle step are inferred, not observed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a genotype effect measured in the microglial transcript readout may be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so between-line and batch confounding cannot be excluded and the isogenic labelling is taken at face value."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase and mitochondrial electron-transport transcript expansion combined with an all-up SREBP1/glycerolipid-esterification module and reduced long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts (ACSL4, ACSL5); we propose the rate-limiting step is acyl-CoA-dependent routing of lysosome-derived fatty acid into mitochondrial oxidation, so that hydrolysed lipid is preferentially re-esterified into neutral-lipid stores. A canonical type I interferon program is absent from the measured RNA rows, and the modest NF-kB/chemokine transcript elevation is not enriched above the strongly up-shifted background, so inflammatory or interferon signalling is proposed as a downstream/parallel consequence rather than the primary bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treat mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia in parallel with (a) a DGAT1 inhibitor (or SCD inhibitor) and (b) IFNAR1-blocking antibody or a JAK1/2 inhibitor. The mechanism predicts that (a) reduces APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet area toward APOE3 while leaving lysosomal transcripts (TFEB, CTSB, ATP6V1A) elevated, whereas (b) leaves droplet load essentially unchanged. If IFNAR/JAK blockade normalizes the APOE4 lipid and chemokine phenotype while DGAT1/SCD inhibition does not, the mechanism is wrong and an interferon-driven model should replace it.", "Direct imaging/lipidomics should show higher neutral-lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX) content and higher triacylglycerol plus cholesteryl-ester fraction in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, together with expanded LAMP1-positive area; absence of a droplet or ester difference despite the transcript pattern would weaken the proposed esterification bias.", "Flux test of the proposed bottleneck: 13C- or 3H-palmitate tracing should show reduced fractional fatty-acid oxidation and increased incorporation into triacylglycerol in APOE4 despite higher or equal maximal respiratory capacity by Seahorse; equal or higher fatty-acid oxidation in APOE4 would falsify the acyl-CoA-routing bottleneck.", "Rescue test: re-expression of ACSL4/ACSL5 (or provision of a carnitine-independent medium-chain fatty-acid substrate) in APOE4 microglia should lower droplet load without lowering lysosomal-hydrolase transcripts; no reduction would falsify the specific bottleneck while leaving the broader storage-bias claim intact.", "Interferon-negativity test: qPCR/protein for ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1, OAS1 and phospho-STAT1 should show no APOE4\u003eAPOE3 induction under mock conditions; a clear ISG signature would show the RNA row selection hid an interferon program and would weaken the claim that inflammatory output is secondary.", "Lysosomal-capacity check: if the lysosomal transcript expansion instead reflects a functional hydrolytic defect, DQ-BSA and LysoTracker/pH assays should show reduced degradation capacity and elevated lysosomal pH in APOE4; normal degradation with enlarged compartment supports the compensatory-expansion interpretation used here, while a severe hydrolytic defect would move the bottleneck upstream of esterification."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-cargo receptors and carriers (gene:SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of the supplied rows, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:APOE); increased cargo uptake flux is inferred, not measured.", "A TFEB-type lysosomal program is transcriptionally expanded (gene:TFEB plus 27/28 lysosomal/v-ATPase rows up, set median +2.17 versus a 77%-up, median +1.46 background; sign-test p about 0.006), which we infer raises luminal hydrolase capacity and liberation of free fatty acid, sterol and sphingoid species inside lysosomes; hydrolytic activity, pH and localization were not measured.", "Long-chain acyl-CoA activation transcripts fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 in the bottom ~10% of rows) while carnitine-shuttle genes were not measured, creating the proposed bottleneck: liberated fatty acid is poorly activated for mitochondrial beta-oxidation.", "In parallel the SREBP1/esterification module is uniformly up (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:INSIG1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1; 14/14 a-priori members up, sign-test p about 0.03), which we infer channels fatty acid and sterol into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester rather than oxidation.", "Mitochondrial oxidative transcripts rise coherently (38/38 electron-transport rows up, median +2.65, sign-test p about 5e-5; gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2), consistent with a compensatory oxidative-capacity response that cannot clear lipid if substrate entry is limited; respiration and beta-oxidation flux were not measured.", "The predicted net outcome is genotype-dependent neutral-lipid (droplet) accumulation coexisting with an enlarged lysosomal compartment in APOE4 microglia; this lipid endpoint is not present in the supplied data.", "Low-grade NF-kB/chemokine and inflammasome transcript elevation (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:TLR6, gene:MYD88, gene:NLRP1, gene:PYCARD) is interpreted as a lipid-stress-associated secondary output: as a set it is not enriched over background (29/34 up, median +1.46, permutation p about 0.5), and no ISG15/IFIT/MX/OAS/STAT1 rows are present, arguing against a type I interferon driver."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase and OXPHOS transcript program but keep fatty-acid disposal esterification-biased, not interferon-driven"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1248199977845881, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2988396041590611, "cosine_similarity": 0.3952201257823925, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5935566343042071, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1248199977845881, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2988396041590611, "cosine_similarity": 0.3952201257823925, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5935566343042071, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.851094, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 107}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_161", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; every claim of 'enrichment' is made relative to the other supplied rows, and absence of a gene (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE) means unmeasured here, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and some magnitudes are implausibly large (up to ~15), so gene-set inferences rest on ranks and direction rather than on absolute fold-change values.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for pathway demand/biogenesis, not for enzyme activity, lysosomal acidification, protein localisation or lipid flux; none of these were measured.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each (with frequent keratin/actin co-assignment), so protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are treated as weak, non-identifying support for increased cathepsin-containing spot abundance, not as identified CTSL/CTSD protein.", "The whole differential list is up-shifted (77% positive, mean effect +1.39); the mechanism assumes this shift is a shared technical/compositional baseline against which the lysosomal block is genuinely rank-enriched, rather than the lysosomal block itself being an artefact.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoproteins, so measured microglial uptake-receptor transcripts plausibly correspond to real lipid cargo availability.", "No lipid, flux, replicate-level or single-cell composition data were supplied; the lipid endpoint of the mechanism is a prediction only."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coherent, above-background transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal luminal-hydrolase and v-ATPase program (GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A, with TFEB itself elevated) together with an extreme increase in the lipoprotein/sterol uptake receptor SCARB1, whereas transcripts of the sterol-egress/hydrolase-delivery arm are not co-scaled (NPC2 and SCARB2 sit near the low end of the differential list, M6PR is decreased). We hypothesise that the limiting step is cholesterol/lipid export out of the endolysosome rather than intra-lysosomal hydrolytic capacity: retained lipid keeps the ER-accessible sterol pool functionally low, sustaining an SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 anabolic program, and the surplus lipid is buffered as neutral-lipid esters (SOAT1, DGAT1 elevated). The predicted, currently unmeasured consequence is APOE4-selective accumulation of cholesteryl esters, monounsaturated triacylglycerols and lysosomal substrate lipids (glycosphingolipids, sphingomyelin, BMP-rich membranes). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving endolysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/egress-restoring treatment) should, without changing APOE genotype, lower cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid-droplet content and secondarily repress the SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 transcript signature toward APOE3 levels while leaving the hydrolase transcripts high or reduced only late. If cyclodextrin reduces droplets but the SREBF1/SCD signature is unchanged, the 'ER senses sterol-poor because sterol is trapped' step is wrong; if neither droplets nor signature move, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "SOAT1 inhibition (Sandoz 58-035 or avasimibe) should convert the APOE4 excess from cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol with loss of the droplet difference and increased APOE4-selective sensitivity, without normalising the lysosomal hydrolase transcript block. Unchanged cholesteryl-ester content under SOAT1 inhibition would weaken the esterification-buffering step.", "Functional lysosome assays should show increased lysosomal number/volume (LysoTracker, LAMP1 area) in APOE4 but no proportional increase in substrate clearance (DQ-BSA dequenching, GBA/HEXA activity per lysosome, LDL-derived cholesterol transfer to the ER-accessible pool measured with a D4H-type probe). If APOE4 lysosomes show proportionally increased hydrolytic flux and normal cholesterol transfer to the ER pool, the bottleneck is not egress.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a coordinated increase in cholesteryl esters and in monounsaturated (SCD-product, 16:1/18:1-containing) triacylglycerols together with increased glucosylceramide/hexosylceramide, sphingomyelin and BMP species. Increased free cholesterol with no cholesteryl-ester or glycosphingolipid difference would weaken the mechanism.", "SCD inhibition should reduce the APOE4-selective monounsaturated triacylglycerol/droplet excess and increase saturated-lipid stress markers; if droplet content is unaffected by SCD inhibition, the SREBP-1/desaturation feed-forward arm contributes little.", "Because CSF1, CCL4, RELB and TNFAIP3 transcripts are decreased and the NF-kB set is not rank-enriched, blocking NF-kB or TLR signalling should not abolish the APOE4 lysosomal/lipid difference; if it does, an inflammation-driven alternative explanation is favoured over the lipid-trafficking bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_161", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry a strongly enriched lysosomal catabolic transcript block (GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA2, HEXB, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0D1) that ranks in the top ~5-20% of an already up-shifted differential list (Mann-Whitney vs all other rows p~5e-4), with TFEB transcript also elevated; inferred: an mTORC1/TFEB-associated lysosomal-biogenesis response to a chronic lysosomal cargo load, not necessarily increased per-lysosome hydrolytic flux.", "Measured: SCARB1 is the strongest lipid-related transcript change (99th percentile of the list) with LDLR, CD36, TREM2, ABCA7 and APOE also elevated; inferred: increased delivery of lipoprotein- and lipid-derived cargo into the endolysosomal compartment (uptake flux itself is not measured).", "Measured: transcripts of the egress/delivery arm are not co-scaled with the hydrolases (NPC2 and SCARB2 near the 27-35th percentile of the list, M6PR decreased ~15th percentile); NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 do not appear in the supplied differential rows and are therefore unmeasured here; inferred: hydrolysed sterol and lipid leave the limiting endolysosomal membrane more slowly than it arrives, creating the primary bottleneck.", "Inferred: because sterol is retained in the endolysosome, the ER sterol sensor operates as if sterol-poor, sustaining the SREBP-1/post-squalene program that is measured as elevated SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACSS2, ACAT2, LPCAT1 and INSIG1 transcripts; this is a feed-forward loop that adds endogenously synthesised lipid to the retained pool.", "Measured: SOAT1, DGAT1 and CIDEB transcripts are elevated; inferred: the surplus free cholesterol and fatty acid that does reach the ER is esterified and stored, converting a trafficking defect into a neutral-lipid-droplet phenotype rather than acute sterol toxicity.", "Predicted lipid endpoint (not measured in the supplied data): APOE4 microglia accumulate cholesteryl esters and SCD-product monounsaturated triacylglycerol species plus undegraded lysosomal substrate lipids (glucosylceramide, hexosylceramides, sphingomyelin, BMP), with a reduced ER-accessible free-cholesterol pool relative to total cholesterol."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid egress, not hydrolase supply, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia, forcing sterol re-esterification and a feed-forward SREBP-1/SCD lipogenic program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14579256360078277, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17250004264812863, "cosine_similarity": 0.3951301531333174, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_161", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6071197411003236, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14579256360078277, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17250004264812863, "cosine_similarity": 0.3951301531333174, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6071197411003236, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7492975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 108}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_053", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression selection (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so absence of a gene means 'not in the selected list', not 'unchanged'; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is left as reported.", "The strong global asymmetry of the selected rows (77.1% up, median +1.46) is treated as a baseline, so only the direction-coherence of the endolysosomal set, not its median magnitude, is used as evidence; permutation tests against this background give p_median = 0.11 (hydrolases) and 0.34 (V-ATPase), i.e. the set medians are not distinguishable from background.", "Protein spots are assumed to be 2D-gel features with 3-6 candidate genes each; assignment of a spot's change to a named lysosomal protein is provisional, and the spot data may derive from a different sample or platform than the RNA (single-candidate spot-versus-RNA Pearson r = -0.01, n = 38).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an upper bound on, not a measure of, enzyme activity, acidification, cargo flux or localisation; no lysosomal pH, enzyme activity, lipid, autophagy-flux or cargo-clearance measurement is present in these data.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on the RNA profile could be partly non-cell-autonomous, and any compositional or ambient-RNA difference between genotypes could inflate the global up-shift."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells transcriptionally expand the endolysosomal system (TFEB and a broad hydrolase, V-ATPase, lysosomal-transporter and endosomal-sorting transcript set) while simultaneously raising scavenger/phagocytic receptor transcripts, yet the protein-spot layer shows no matching increase (and a relative decrease) for spots whose candidate identities include cathepsins, HEXB, ACP2 and ATP6V1E1. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 is degradative capacity per unit delivered cargo - the effector acid-hydrolase/acidification protein pool failing to scale with the transcriptional program and with inferred cargo influx - which leaves lipid-rich cargo incompletely hydrolysed in the endolysosomal lumen and keeps ER-sensed sterol subsaturating, sustaining SREBP-axis, esterification/storage and APOE/ABCA7 transcripts in a feed-forward loading loop. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Cargo pulse-chase in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia (pHrodo-myelin, DiI-oxLDL or DQ-BSA): APOE4 should show equal or greater uptake at 1 h but a lower fractional degradation rate at 6-24 h, with retained BODIPY/filipin-positive endolysosomal lipid. Equal or faster degradation with no cargo retention would weaken the mechanism.", "Per-cell activity assays (Magic Red cathepsin B, fluorogenic GBA/HEXA/GAA, LysoSensor pH): the APOE4:APOE3 activity ratio should be far below the corresponding transcript ratio (e.g. under ~1.5-fold activity against \u003e4-fold transcript for gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:GAA) and lysosomal pH should not be lower in APOE4. Activity and acidification scaling proportionally with transcripts would falsify the capacity bottleneck.", "Discriminating perturbation: further driving the transcriptional program (TFEB overexpression or Torin1) should NOT normalise cargo clearance or neutral-lipid load in APOE4, whereas bypassing the enzymatic step (delivery of recombinant hydrolase, or cyclodextrin-mediated sterol egress) should. Full rescue of clearance and of the SREBP-axis transcripts by TFEB alone would falsify the claim that the bottleneck is post-transcriptional capacity.", "Immunoblot of cathepsin D/B pro- versus mature forms: APOE4 should show a lower mature:pro ratio (or unchanged mature protein) despite higher gene:CTSD and gene:CTSB transcripts, matching the spot redistribution seen for protein_spot:053 versus protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:058. Proportionally increased mature hydrolase protein would weaken step 3.", "Ordering test: blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein/debris-free medium) should lower the CLEAR-like transcript set (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1H) in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels if the program is demand-driven; persistence of the full program under cargo restriction would argue for a cell-intrinsic transcriptional difference instead and weaken steps 1-2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for uptake and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:C1QA), which we infer - but did not measure - raises lipoprotein/debris influx into the endosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A coordinate CLEAR-like transcript response is present (gene:TFEB +2.38; all ten detected V-ATPase subunit transcripts up, e.g. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1; hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:DPP7; membrane/transport gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:LAPTM4A, gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5; sorting gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:AP5M1). We read this as a demand or stress signal, not as evidence that degradative flux is increased.", "Step 3 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): The spot layer does not follow the transcripts. Spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases or V1 subunits have median log2FC -0.13 versus +0.48 for all other spots, and 6 of 12 significant such spots are decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:086) versus 3 of 35 elsewhere, while cathepsin-D-containing spots redistribute rather than rise (protein_spot:053 up, protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:058 down). We infer that the mature hydrolase/acidification protein pool, or its processed-form distribution, does not scale with the transcript induction; the spots do not uniquely identify these proteins.", "Step 4 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Consequently the degradative capacity per delivered cargo is the bottleneck, so lipid-rich cargo is incompletely hydrolysed and retained in late endosomes/lysosomes. This luminal lipid pool was not measured in the supplied data.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): Because sterol is retained in the endolysosomal compartment rather than reaching the ER sensor, SREBP-axis transcripts stay high (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) together with esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD).", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred loop): Continued uptake plus lipid-handling and efflux transcripts (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) and a mild inflammatory tilt (gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB, gene:FTH1) sustain the loading loop, giving the APOE4 steady state its distinctive transcript-versus-protein discordance."], "title": "Lysosomal degradative capacity, not lysosomal gene transcription, is the APOE4 bottleneck: a CLEAR-like transcript program uncoupled from hydrolase/V-ATPase protein output under raised cargo uptake"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21179162698496193, "cosine_similarity": 0.39501010063924746, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5992556634304207, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21179162698496193, "cosine_similarity": 0.39501010063924746, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5992556634304207, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7312235, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 109}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_040", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression subset, so all enrichment claims are made against that selected background (median log fold change 1.46, 77 percent positive), not against an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "The relative depletion of mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflects a real per-cell change in mitochondrial transcript pool rather than a compositional consequence of library-size normalisation in the presence of a large global upward nuclear shift, or of probe-based 10X Flex capture differences; this assumption is untested here and is the main threat to the mechanism.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy for protein availability and complex assembly; no OXPHOS protein, assembled-complex, membrane-potential, ATP, NADPH, ROS or mtDNA copy-number measurement is present in this dataset.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate two-dimensional gel features, so protein_spot:077 (candidates including PRDX2 among keratins, RAB1A and ACTB) is treated as ambiguous corroboration only and not as identified PRDX2 protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent differences in cell state, maturation or ambient RNA are assumed not to be the sole driver of the mitonuclear contrast.", "Peroxisomal metabolism is assumed not to be the bottleneck because no PEX gene, CAT, ACAA1 or HSD17B4 row is present in the supplied differential-expression list and the assembled peroxisomal set is not enriched (median 1.13, below background, permutation p about 0.51); absence from a selected list is not evidence of no change."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally amplify the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA program while transcripts for the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (notably MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are relatively depleted; we propose that this mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch, not a peroxisomal defect, is the primary bottleneck, limiting assembly of complexes III/IV/V, increasing electron leak at the matrix face, and forcing a compensatory NADPH/peroxiredoxin-dependent matrix antioxidant load (PRDX3/PRDX5/NNT) that is measured only as RNA abundance here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Blue-native PAGE or complexome profiling of APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex V (with a relative accumulation of free F1 subcomplex) and reduced complex III/IV holoenzyme despite equal or higher nuclear-encoded subunit protein levels; equal assembled-complex levels across genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show lower oligomycin-sensitive (ATP-linked) oxygen consumption and a higher proton-leak fraction in APOE4, with maximal FCCP-stimulated respiration not increased in proportion to the elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcript program; unchanged ATP-linked respiration and leak would weaken it.", "Discriminating test against a normalisation artifact: absolute per-cell quantification (spike-in normalised or single-molecule FISH for MT-ATP6 and MT-CO2, plus qPCR mtDNA:nuclear DNA copy ratio) should show a genuine reduction in mtDNA-encoded transcript or template copies per APOE4 cell; if absolute mtDNA copy number and absolute MT transcript counts are equal between genotypes, the apparent mitonuclear imbalance is compositional and the mechanism fails.", "Rescue prediction: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression, or allotopic nuclear-recoded ATP6 expression) in APOE4 microglia should restore ATP-linked respiration and lower matrix H2O2 reporter oxidation toward APOE3 levels; failure to rescue while nuclear OXPHOS transcripts remain elevated would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Redox prediction: matrix-targeted roGFP2-Orp1 or PRDX3 redox-shift immunoblot should report a more oxidised matrix in APOE4, and NNT knockdown should selectively worsen APOE4 but not APOE3 microglia; an equally oxidised matrix in both genotypes, or equal NNT-knockdown sensitivity, would remove the compensatory-antioxidant step while leaving the assembly step to be tested separately.", "Negative prediction that discriminates against the assigned peroxisomal focus: peroxisome number, catalase activity and C26:0 very-long-chain fatty-acid levels should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock treatment; a clear peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect would favour an alternative mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia raise the nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and TCA transcript program relative to the selected differential-expression background (nuclear OXPHOS median log fold change 2.64 vs a background median of 1.46; TCA set median 3.94), indicating increased demand for, or biogenesis of, matrix oxidative metabolism.", "Transcripts for mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits move in the opposite direction (median -1.56; MT-ATP6 -3.35 with the strongest adjusted p-value in the mitochondrial set), producing a stoichiometric mismatch between imported nuclear subunits and the mtDNA-encoded cores they must nucleate.", "Inferred, not measured: the resulting subunit imbalance limits assembly and turnover of complex V (nuclear F1 subunits ATP5F1B/ATP5ME up while the mtDNA-encoded Fo subunit a transcript is down), complex III (UQCR subunits up, MT-CYB down) and complex IV (COX subunits up, MT-CO2 down), so assembled holoenzyme flux does not scale with the nuclear program.", "Inferred: partially assembled or under-supplied complexes III/IV together with reduced oligomycin-sensitive ATP synthase capacity increase the reduced state of upstream carriers and the probability of superoxide/H2O2 generation at the matrix face, while UCP2 (RNA +2.38) marks a leak-tolerant state rather than an efficient one.", "Inferred compensation: the matrix thiol-peroxidase system is placed under load, consistent with coordinated RNA increases in PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, GSS and the NADPH-regenerating transhydrogenase NNT, plus iron sequestration (FTH1); this is a weakly enriched, post-hoc set and is the least secure step.", "Inferred downstream: a redox- and ATP-constrained state, together with the strong lysosomal/hydrolase and lipid-handling transcript increases (CTSD, SCARB1, APOE), biases APOE4 microglia toward lipid storage and lysosomal processing rather than complete beta-oxidative disposal of internalised lipid."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry failure: mtDNA-encoded core subunit deficit against an amplified nuclear OXPHOS/TCA program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10371819960861056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22546289735018657, "cosine_similarity": 0.3942242889206865, "direction_accuracy": 0.17313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5929611650485437, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10371819960861056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22546289735018657, "cosine_similarity": 0.3942242889206865, "direction_accuracy": 0.17313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5929611650485437, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6953095, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 110}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_025", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong positive skew (2212 rows, 77.1% positive, median +1.46); all pathway statements are therefore relative to this internal background and not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified, so RNA magnitudes are used only for ranking and sign, never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each (frequent keratin/actin contaminants), so no spot is treated as identifying a single protein; spots are used only as weak, ambiguity-flagged corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for pathway capacity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, SREBP proteolytic processing, sterol localisation and lipid flux were not measured and are inferred.", "No lipid, lipidomic, imaging or flux measurement is supplied, so the storage phenotype is a prediction, not an observation.", "The astrocyte co-culture and the pooled 10X Flex design mean some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous or composition-driven; biological replicate number is stated as not supplied.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism describes an inferred, testable direction only."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from isogenic APOE3 cells primarily by a coordinated up-shift of the lysosomal degradative module (hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB) that is not matched by the machinery returning liberated sterol from the endolysosome to the ER; the resulting inferred cholesterol-delivery deficit at the ER keeps an SREBP-type synthesis/uptake/esterification transcript program active, biasing APOE4 microglia toward lipid storage rather than efflux or oxidation. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is rejected because the UPR/ER-chaperone transcripts are indistinguishable from the selected-list background and internally incoherent, and because chaperone-candidate protein spots are non-significant and negative in point estimate.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should lower SREBP-type transcripts (SREBF2, DHCR24, LSS, LDLR, SCD) toward APOE3 levels and reduce neutral-lipid/filipin signal, while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript up-shift largely intact. If SREBP targets and lipid load remain unchanged after successful cholesterol removal, the egress-bottleneck step is falsified.", "Reverse-direction control: SCAP knockdown or fatostatin should lower lipid storage but should NOT normalise the lysosomal module (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, ATP6V1H, TFEB). If it does normalise the lysosomal module, the causal ordering proposed here is wrong.", "Imaging: APOE4 microglia should show more LAMP1-colocalised unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and more BODIPY-positive droplets than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal free cholesterol in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Negative prediction for the rejected ER-stress mechanism: APOE4 cells should not show elevated BiP/GRP94 protein, XBP1 splicing, or ATF4/CHOP reporter activity relative to APOE3 under mock conditions; a clear, reproducible UPR signature (e.g., \u003e1.5-fold XBP1s) would overturn the decision to reject the ER-proteostasis focus in favour of this lysosome-to-ER lipid mechanism.", "Capacity test: acute lipid-cargo challenge (myelin debris or oxLDL) should widen the APOE4-APOE3 gap in droplet accumulation and in SREBP-target transcripts; if APOE4 cells clear the challenge as fast as APOE3 with equal sterol-sensing feedback, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Proteomic expectation: unbiased LC-MS/MS should show lysosomal hydrolases at most modestly changed in APOE4, consistent with the supplied spots (protein_spot:055, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 mixed in sign); a large, uniform increase in lysosomal hydrolase protein would instead favour a simple biogenesis-driven model over an egress bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia maintain or increase uptake-competent surface and opsonin machinery at the transcript level (gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:MRC1), so lipid-rich cargo delivery into the endolysosome is inferred to be at least as high as in APOE3.", "The lysosomal degradative module is transcriptionally elevated above the internal DE-list background (median +2.02 vs +1.46 global; gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:TFEB), indicating increased lysosomal biogenesis/hydrolytic demand at the mRNA level (activity and acidification are inferred, not measured).", "The step that exports liberated unesterified cholesterol from the lysosomal lumen to the ER is not coordinately up-shifted: the one measured component, gene:NPC2 (+1.17), lies below the global median of this DE list, and gene:M6PR (-1.72) and gene:IDS (-1.56) are down while other hydrolase-delivery genes rise (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R); NPC1, GRN, LIPA and ASAH1 were not measured. A functional lysosome-to-ER sterol-egress bottleneck is therefore inferred, not observed.", "Reduced sterol arrival at the ER membrane is inferred to leave SCAP-SREBP de-repressed, matching the uniformly positive SREBP-type transcript set (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD; 10/10 members positive).", "Newly synthesised and imported lipid is inferred to be esterified and stored rather than oxidised or effluxed (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACSL4 direction mixed), while glycolytic/pentose-phosphate transcripts fall relative to background (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD, gene:HK3), consistent with a storage-biased, less glycolytic APOE4 state.", "The loop is self-sustaining: cargo continues to arrive and be hydrolysed, sterol continues to be poorly returned to the ER, and the SREBP-type program is not switched off, so neutral-lipid load in APOE4 cells is predicted to exceed APOE3 without an accompanying canonical UPR (HSPA5/BiP does not appear in the supplied DE rows at all; gene:DDIT3 and gene:ATF6 rise but gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1 and gene:PDIA3 fall; protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 non-significant)."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol-egress bottleneck, not ER unfolded-protein stress, sustains an SREBP-type lipogenic program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2432706864084481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29509831534116554, "cosine_similarity": 0.3940108853881028, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5943948220064725, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2432706864084481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29509831534116554, "cosine_similarity": 0.3940108853881028, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5943948220064725, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.780509, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 111}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Increased transcript abundance for lysosomal hydrolases and TFEB is treated as evidence of a transcriptional program change, not as direct evidence of increased enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH change, or degradative flux, which were not measured.", "Genes are grouped into lipid-uptake, phagocytic/complement, and CLEAR/lysosomal categories based on established gene function annotations (background/unverified knowledge), not on a supplied pathway annotation file; membership was fixed by these functional categories before checking direction, not selected to force agreement.", "The RNA rows are a pre-selected significant differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% of 2212 rows positive), so the elevated positive rate and large effect sizes in the lysosomal/lipid/phagocytic gene sets are interpreted relative to this already up-skewed background, not against a naive 50/50 expectation.", "Protein-spot observations are treated as compatible-or-contradictory tests only, because each spot lists 2-5 candidate genes and cannot be attributed to a single confirmed protein.", "No claim is made that TFEB activation, cargo load, or lysosomal flux differences were directly measured; these are inferred links bridging the observed transcript pattern to a plausible mechanism."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 iPSC-microglia (mock, Day30, co-cultured with astrocytes), the selected differential-expression list shows coordinated increases in transcripts for lipid/cholesterol uptake and esterification (SCARB1, LDLR, ABCA7, SOAT1, DGAT1, CH25H), complement/efferocytic uptake receptors (C1QA, C1QB, C1QC, MERTK, GAS6, FCGR3A, DNM2), and the CLEAR lysosomal biogenesis regulon (TFEB plus CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SGSH, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, LAMP1, NPC2, RAB7A). This pattern is compatible with a model in which APOE4 genotype increases delivery of lipid/receptor cargo into the endolysosomal system and elicits a transcriptional program that expands lysosomal hydrolase and acidification machinery, rather than establishing a rate-limiting lysosomal defect. Whether this transcriptional expansion is sufficient to match increased cargo influx (successful adaptation/increased throughput) or is an incomplete/failing compensation cannot be determined from expression data alone, and two components move in the opposite direction (CTSS, IDS decreased), showing the response is selective, not uniform.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating: If TFEB is knocked down or its nuclear activity is pharmacologically blocked in APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the coordinated increase in CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C, and LAMP1 transcripts should be substantially blunted relative to APOE4 controls; if these hydrolase/ATPase transcripts remain elevated despite TFEB loss, the proposed TFEB-linked driver of this mechanism would be weakened (an alternative TFEB-independent driver would be needed).", "Prospective: Direct measurement of lysosomal proteolytic/lipolytic flux (e.g., DQ-BSA or cathepsin activity assays, or lipid-droplet/cholesterol-ester accumulation) in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under this same mock condition should show flux increased in proportion to the transcript increases if this represents successful compensation; unchanged or reduced flux despite elevated transcripts, or measurable accumulation of undigested lipid/protein cargo, would indicate failed or exhausted compensation rather than increased functional capacity, weakening the 'successful adaptation' interpretation while still being compatible with the transcriptional steps above.", "Prospective, challenge-specific: Only under an added lysosomal/lipid challenge (e.g., myelin debris or cholesterol loading) should reduced reserve become apparent in APOE4 cells (e.g., blunted further TFEB/hydrolase induction or disproportionate cargo accumulation compared with APOE3); observing an equally strong additional induction and equivalent cargo clearance in APOE4 under challenge would argue against a reserve-limited defect and instead favor a fully adaptive, non-limiting compensatory state in the mock condition."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with increased transcript abundance for lipid/cholesterol uptake, transport and esterification machinery (SCARB1, LDLR, ABCA7, SOAT1, DGAT1, CH25H), suggesting increased delivery of lipid-derived cargo into the cell.", "APOE4 microglia also show increased transcripts for phagocytic/efferocytic and complement-opsonization receptors and endocytic machinery (C1QA, C1QB, C1QC, MERTK, GAS6, FCGR3A, DNM2), consistent with increased routing of extracellular material toward endolysosomal compartments.", "Convergent lipid and particulate cargo delivered to endolysosomes is inferred (not measured) to increase substrate/cholesterol load on the lysosomal compartment.", "TFEB transcript itself is increased (gene:TFEB, log2FC 2.38), consistent with, but not proof of, activation of the CLEAR transcriptional program that normally responds to lysosomal/nutrient stress.", "A broad, coordinated set of CLEAR-network lysosomal hydrolase, membrane and acidification transcripts is elevated (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SGSH, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, LAMP1, NPC2, RAB7A), consistent with a transcriptional attempt to expand lysosomal degradative capacity.", "This upregulation is not uniform: CTSS (immune-associated cysteine protease) and IDS (a sulfatase) are decreased, indicating the transcriptional response is selective rather than a blanket increase, and may leave specific substrate classes (e.g., glycosaminoglycan turnover, CTSS-dependent processing) relatively under-serviced.", "Because only mRNA and ambiguous, multi-candidate protein-spot data are available, it is unknown whether increased hydrolase/transporter transcripts translate into increased functional proteolytic/lipolytic flux (successful adaptation) or whether cargo still accumulates faster than it is cleared (failed or exhausted compensation); this decisive activity/flux measurement is missing."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show coordinated transcriptional upregulation of a lipid-uptake-to-lysosome cargo axis, consistent with a compensatory (not yet proven adequate) increase in lysosomal degradative capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2806842730322705, "cosine_similarity": 0.39392764832028626, "direction_accuracy": 0.10679611650485436, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151391585760518, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2806842730322705, "cosine_similarity": 0.39392764832028626, "direction_accuracy": 0.10679611650485436, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151391585760518, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6357676, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_016", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (every row has |effect| \u003e 1) with a global positive shift (77.1% up, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); module coherence is therefore judged by direction uniformity and significance rank, not by absolute counts of up-genes.", "Reduced TGFBR1 transcript is assumed to lower TGFBR1 protein and SMAD2/3 phosphorylation flux; neither protein nor phospho-protein was measured here.", "Scavenger-receptor transcript increases are assumed to raise surface receptor density and lipoprotein uptake flux; no uptake, lipidomic, or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and are used only as weak corroboration; spots 052/053/058/067 list CTSL/CTSD/CTSB/HEXB among several candidates and cannot identify a unique protein.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to differ systematically in contamination between genotypes; S100B (+6.00) is a caveat to this assumption.", "Absence of a gene from the list is assumed to mean it did not pass the selection filter, not that it is unexpressed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a lower TGFBR1 transcript pool than isogenic APOE3 cells; the primary bottleneck is TGF-beta receptor-I-dependent SMAD signalling capacity, and its reduction is proposed to release the TGF-beta-maintained homeostatic microglial program, permitting a coherent, highly significant CD163/MRC1/STAB1/COLEC12/SCARB1/CD36 scavenger-receptor and SOAT1/DGAT1/TFEB-lysosomal storage program that biases the cells toward lipoprotein uptake and neutral-lipid esterification rather than toward interferon or classical NF-kB inflammation. Causality is not established by these data; the ordering is a hypothesis.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological TGFBR1 kinase inhibition (e.g. SB-431542) applied to isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock conditions should phenocopy APOE4 by raising CD163, MRC1, STAB1, SCARB1, CD36 and SOAT1 transcripts and increasing BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area and cholesteryl-ester content, while recombinant TGF-beta1 or TGFBR1 re-expression in APOE4 should lower them. If the APOE4 scavenger/lipid phenotype is unchanged by both directions of TGFBR1 manipulation, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Phospho-SMAD2/3 immunoblot or ELISA at day 30 mock should be lower in APOE4 than APOE3, and nuclear SMAD2/3 localization reduced. Equal phospho-SMAD2/3 and equal nuclear localization between genotypes would falsify the signalling-capacity step even though TGFBR1 mRNA differs.", "Ordering test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 should shift stored cholesteryl ester toward free cholesterol and shrink lipid droplets without normalizing CD163, MRC1 or SCARB1 transcripts. If SOAT1 inhibition also reverses the identity markers, storage is upstream of identity and the step order is wrong.", "Flux test: blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should reduce neutral-lipid accumulation substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal reduction would indicate the difference lies in synthesis/hydrolysis rather than uptake flux.", "Interferon exclusion test: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade under mock conditions should not normalize the APOE4 scavenger/lipid phenotype, and APOE4 cells should show no elevation of ISG15, MX1 or IFIT1 protein. Detection of a robust APOE4 interferon signature that is required for the lipid phenotype would falsify the rejection of the interferon mechanism and this hypothesis's framing.", "Lysosomal-compensation test: if the hydrolase module is compensatory, LAMP1/CTSD protein and cathepsin activity should be higher in APOE4 and further inhibition (e.g. GBA or acid-lipase blockade) should disproportionately increase APOE4 lipid load. Equal cathepsin activity with equal lipid load would weaken step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: TGFBR1 transcript is lower in APOE4 (effect -2.19, adjusted p ~0, 4th most significant of 2212 selected RNA rows), with SMAD2 and SMAD7 transcripts also lower. Inferred (not measured): reduced TGFBR1 protein at the plasma membrane and reduced SMAD2/3 phosphorylation flux; SMAD7 is used here as a transcriptional read-out of pathway output, not as a measured activity.", "Inferred: lower TGF-beta/SMAD flux weakens maintenance of the TGF-beta-dependent homeostatic microglial identity program (unverified background knowledge), lowering the transcriptional constraint on scavenger/perivascular-macrophage-type genes.", "Measured: a directionally uniform scavenger/CD163-type module is higher in APOE4 (MRC1, CD163, F13A1, RNASE1, SLCO2B1, STAB1, COLEC12, CD14, MS4A7, MS4A4A, FOLR2, SELENOP, PLA2G7, SIGLEC1, MERTK; 13/13 tested members up, median significance rank ~42/2212), together with the lipoprotein receptors SCARB1 and CD36 and with APOE itself.", "Inferred (flux, not measured): the elevated receptor transcripts translate into greater surface scavenger-receptor density and higher lipoprotein/lipid uptake flux; no uptake assay, no lipid pool and no protein-level receptor measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Measured: esterification and storage machinery is higher in APOE4 (SOAT1, DGAT1, plus SREBF1, SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD), consistent with routing of incoming sterol/fatty acid into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol rather than efflux (ABCA1 and ABCG1 are not present in the selected list, so efflux cannot be scored).", "Measured: a lysosomal hydrolase / TFEB module is higher (TFEB, CTSD, CTSB, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, ATP6V1A, LAMP1, NPC2, GPNMB), interpreted as a compensatory expansion of degradative capacity under an increased lipid substrate load; CTSS is a clear exception and moves strongly down.", "Predicted state (not measured): APOE4 microglia sit in a lipid-laden, storage-biased scavenger state with normal-to-low interferon output; the interferon effector module (STAT1, STAT2, IRF7, IRF9, ISG15, MX1, OAS1, B2M, HLA-A) is entirely absent from the selected differential list, so an interferon-driven mechanism is rejected for this dataset."], "title": "Reduced TGFBR1-dependent SMAD signalling capacity licenses a scavenger-receptor / lipid-storage macrophage program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21732247408240532, "cosine_similarity": 0.39324654110891544, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5878608414239482, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21732247408240532, "cosine_similarity": 0.39324654110891544, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5878608414239482, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.21284325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 112}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_023", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, not an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1, TMEM175, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B) means untested, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no conversion to log2 is assumed, so magnitudes are compared only within the RNA modality.", "The whole supplied RNA list is up-shifted (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77.1% positive). Set-level claims are therefore made against this internal background, not against zero; a global normalisation or cell-composition offset cannot be excluded.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins: each carries multiple candidate genes, so no spot is treated as evidence for a specific protein's abundance or for a specific proteoform.", "Increased hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to report unmet degradative demand (a compensatory CLEAR response). The competing reading, that capacity is simply higher in APOE4, is not excluded by these data.", "No lysosomal pH, hydrolase enzymatic activity, autophagic or endocytic flux, cargo half-life, cholesterol pool size, lysosome number/size, or subcellular localisation was measured; all such statements are inferences.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so the reported adjusted p values cannot be independently assessed for pseudoreplication across cells versus differentiations.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; genotype effects on the astrocyte partner or on cell-state composition of the microglial pool could contribute to the pseudobulk differences.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: APOE4 genotype is associated with, not shown to cause, the described endolysosomal state."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 state is distinguished by a coherent, direction-consistent elevation of endolysosomal cargo-uptake and acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts together with lysosomal-stress and sterol-handling markers. We hypothesise the primary bottleneck is terminal cargo-clearance throughput per lysosome relative to an increased scavenger-receptor-mediated cargo influx: the transcriptional programme is read as compensation for unmet degradative demand rather than as demonstrated extra capacity, with the consequence that cargo-derived sterol is diverted to SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification and APOE export instead of reaching the ER sterol sensor, leaving the SREBP synthesis programme on. Causality is not established by these data; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and all activity, flux, pH, localisation and cargo-load statements below are inferences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING KINETIC TEST. Pulse-chase isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with an equal, saturating dose of labelled cargo (fluorescent myelin debris or DiI-oxLDL) plus a parallel DQ-BSA probe. Prediction: APOE4 shows a longer cargo half-life and greater residual undegraded label per cell at 6-24 h chase, while per-lysosome bulk proteolytic reporting (DQ-BSA rate normalised to LAMP1+ volume) and LysoSensor-reported pH are equal to or better than APOE3. WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: if APOE4 clears the matched cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3, the 'influx exceeds throughput' bottleneck is refuted, and the transcript programme should be reinterpreted as a genuine capacity increase.", "CARGO-DEPENDENCE TEST. Remove or block the influx limb (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or withholding myelin/apoptotic cargo) for 48-72 h. Prediction: GPNMB, CTSD, CTSB, GAA and TFEB-target transcripts fall substantially toward APOE3 levels in APOE4 cells. WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: if these transcripts stay elevated in cargo-free conditions, the driver is cell-intrinsic TFEB/mTORC1 signalling rather than cargo load, and step 1 is not the entry point.", "ACIDIFICATION ALTERNATIVE. Measure lysosomal pH directly (ratiometric LysoSensor or Oregon-Green dextran). Prediction under this hypothesis: APOE4 pH is not higher than APOE3 (throughput, not acidification, is limiting). WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: a significantly higher APOE4 lysosomal pH with reduced hydrolase activity would relocate the bottleneck to v-ATPase-dependent acidification, an alternative made live by the two decreased spots whose candidate lists include ATP6V1E1 (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065).", "COMPOSITION ALTERNATIVE. Deconvolve the 10X Flex data by microglial substate and compare lysosomal transcripts within matched states. Prediction: the lysosomal/CLEAR elevation persists within state-matched cells. WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: if the entire lysosomal signal is explained by a larger fraction of CD163+/MRC1+/F13A1+ scavenger-like cells in APOE4, with state-matched cells identical, the effect is a composition artefact of pseudobulk and not a per-cell endolysosomal difference.", "CAPACITY-RESCUE TEST. Independently raise degradative capacity (TFEB overexpression or acid-hydrolase supplementation) at constant cargo load. Prediction: residual cargo and GPNMB fall in APOE4 toward APOE3. WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: no improvement despite verified capacity gain would indicate that egress or fusion, not hydrolysis, is limiting; note that gene:STX17 is decreased (-2.06), which already flags autophagosome-lysosome fusion as a competing bottleneck to be excluded.", "PROTEOFORM TEST. Immunoblot mature versus pro-cathepsin D and cathepsin B, and measure activity with cleavable substrates. Prediction: increased mature-form and increased activity in APOE4. WEAKENS THE MECHANISM: unchanged or reduced mature cathepsin protein and activity, despite gene:CTSD (+2.86) and gene:CTSB (+5.52), would show that the transcript programme is not translated into hydrolytic capacity, which the ambiguous, bidirectional cathepsin-candidate spots (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) cannot currently resolve."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux). APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of scavenger/lipoprotein and phagocytic uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:STAB1 +1.13, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:F13A1 +1.11, all at very small adjusted p). We infer, but did not measure, a correspondingly higher rate of lipid/lipoprotein cargo delivery into early and late endosomes.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred unmet demand). An a-priori lysosomal gene set is coherently up in APOE4 (37/40 present members positive; gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DNASE2, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2) alongside gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) and all ten measured v-ATPase subunits (e.g. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51). We interpret this as a TFEB/CLEAR-type biogenesis response to a cargo backlog, not as verified increased hydrolase activity or verified acidification.", "Step 3 (marker inference). Transcriptional compensation is proposed to be insufficient to restore spare clearance capacity per lysosome, so undegraded, lipid-rich cargo persists in a storage-type compartment; gene:GPNMB (adjusted p reported as 0) and gene:FTH1 (+2.53) are read as markers of this stressed, cargo-laden lysosomal state. No storage material, lysosome number, size or pH was measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred routing). Sterol and lipid that do exit or accumulate are inferred to be re-esterified and stored or exported rather than returned to the regulatory ER pool: gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:MGLL (+4.00) and gene:APOE (+1.24) are elevated. Esterification and export fluxes were not measured.", "Step 5 (coherence test / inferred sensing state). Consistent with cargo-derived sterol failing to relieve ER sterol sensing, the SREBP synthesis programme remains elevated (12/12 measured members positive: gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:LDLR, gene:EBP, gene:MYLIP). This is a transcriptional read-out only; ER free-cholesterol content was not measured.", "Step 6 (net state). The predicted net phenotype is a chronically cargo-loaded, TFEB-high APOE4 endolysosomal system with reduced spare clearance capacity: at matched cargo challenge, APOE4 microglia should degrade and dispose of new cargo more slowly than APOE3 despite equal or higher hydrolase transcript levels."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a cargo-loaded endolysosome: scavenger-receptor influx outstrips terminal degradative throughput, forcing a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR biogenesis program and sterol re-esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14187866927592954, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1631640516280322, "cosine_similarity": 0.3928020423890118, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6097249190938512, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14187866927592954, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1631640516280322, "cosine_similarity": 0.3928020423890118, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6097249190938512, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.96237825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 113}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are log fold changes in an unspecified logarithm base; all statements use relative rank within the supplied list rather than an absolute fold-change scale.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene means absent from this selection, not measured-and-unchanged. Pathway claims are therefore made as within-list percentile enrichment against the list's own strongly positive background (median effect +1.46, 77% positive), not as absolute pathway induction.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific gene product.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate at least in rank with the corresponding enzyme protein pool; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number, lipid content, cytokine secretion and TFEB nuclear localisation are inferred or unmeasured, never observed here.", "The measured population is microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences are assumed to arise within the microglial compartment rather than from altered cell-type proportions or astrocyte cross-talk, which the supplied data cannot resolve.", "The isogenic design is assumed to control for background genetic effects, so the contrast is attributed to APOE genotype; no causal test is contained in these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant coherent difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is not an interferon program but a compensatory transcriptional expansion of lysosomal acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and endolysosomal trafficking machinery, accompanied by transcriptional diversion of lipid into neutral-lipid esterification rather than efflux. We propose that lysosomal degradative throughput for glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin cargo, not transcript supply of the enzymes, is the rate-limiting node in APOE4; the resulting persistent endolysosomal lipid cargo sustains a sterile, NF-kB-restricted chemokine/inflammasome-priming state (CXCL8, CXCL1, CXCL2, CCL2, NLRP3, PYCARD, IL18) while type-I interferon signalling remains unengaged and the pyroptotic executioner arm (GSDMD, NEK7) is transcriptionally reduced. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed and testable.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION 1 (bottleneck test): Chaperone or enzyme augmentation of the glycosphingolipid branch in APOE4 microglia (e.g. ambroxol or recombinant glucocerebrosidase for GBA, or acid sphingomyelinase supplementation) should raise measured lysosomal hydrolase activity AND normalise the APOE4 excess of secreted CXCL8 and CCL2 and of BODIPY/filipin-stained lipid load toward APOE3 levels, while leaving APOE transcript unchanged. If activity rises but chemokine secretion and lipid staining are unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the hydrolase up-shift is an epiphenomenon.", "DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION 2 (interferon exclusion): Blocking type-I interferon signalling (anti-IFNAR2 antibody or a JAK1/2 inhibitor) under mock conditions should NOT reduce the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess in CXCL8/CXCL1/CCL2 secretion, and APOE4 cells should show no elevated ISG15/MX1/IFIT1 protein or transcript. Detection of an elevated ISG signature or IFNAR-dependent chemokine excess in APOE4 falsifies STEP 5 and the interferon-independence of this mechanism.", "DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION 3 (priming without execution): On nigericin or ATP challenge, APOE4 microglia should release more IL-18 and IL-1beta per cell than APOE3 but show equal or LESS LDH release and less gasdermin-D N-terminal cleavage product. Equal cytokine release with greater lysis in APOE4 would falsify STEP 6.", "PREDICTION 4 (regulator dependence): TFEB knockdown should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A) with a significantly larger absolute reduction in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal or greater dependence in APOE3 would falsify the compensatory-CLEAR framing in STEP 1.", "PREDICTION 5 (storage diversion): SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplet content in APOE4 while INCREASING, not decreasing, CXCL8/CCL2 secretion and lysosomal membrane permeabilisation markers, because storage is proposed to be a protective sink. A decrease in chemokine output on SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition would falsify STEP 3.", "PREDICTION 6 (load dependence): Loading both genotypes with myelin debris or apoptotic-neuron cargo should widen, not narrow, the APOE4-versus-APOE3 gap in undigested lysosomal lipid and in chemokine output; convergence of the two genotypes under high load would weaken the throughput-limitation claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA abundance; inferred cause): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits far above the already-positive background shift of this selected differential-expression list (GAA, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, SGSH, MAN2B1, DPP7, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1E1, ATP6V0D2, LAMP1), together with the master CLEAR-network regulator transcript TFEB and endolysosomal trafficking transcripts (RAB7A, VPS26A, AP5M1). We interpret this as a compensatory demand signal, not as proof of increased enzyme activity or lysosome number, neither of which was measured.", "STEP 2 (inferred activity/flux; the proposed bottleneck): The enriched enzymes cluster on the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid and glycan-catabolic branch (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, GLA, GAA, SGSH, MAN2B1). We propose that per-lysosome catabolic throughput on this branch fails to keep pace with cargo influx in APOE4, so the transcriptional up-shift is a compensation that does not resolve the load. Lysosomal lipid content, luminal pH and enzyme activity are unmeasured here.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA abundance; inferred flux): Rather than exporting the excess, APOE4 cells transcriptionally favour storage and re-esterification (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, FABP5, SREBF1) alongside continued lipid acquisition (SCARB1 strongly up, LDLR, CD36, NPC2, ABCA7, APOE), which we infer diverts liberated fatty acid and sterol into neutral-lipid pools instead of relieving the lysosomal load. Lipid droplet content and efflux flux are not measured.", "STEP 4 (measured RNA abundance; inferred signalling): Persistent endolysosomal lipid cargo and cathepsin-rich compartments provide a sterile priming stimulus that engages the MYD88/TICAM1/IRAK4-NF-kB arm, seen as elevated NLRP3, PYCARD, IL18, CASP4, TLR2, NFKBIZ and the chemokines CXCL8, CXCL1, CXCL2, CCL2. Inflammasome assembly, caspase activity and cytokine secretion were not measured.", "STEP 5 (measured RNA abundance; discriminating negative): This priming is interferon-independent. Only IFI16 and TMEM173 from a 30-gene canonical type-I interferon panel appear in the differential list, both below the list-wide median effect, and no ISG15/MX/OAS/IFIT/STAT1/STAT2/IRF7/IRF9 transcripts appear, whereas 20 of 20 canonical NF-kB/inflammasome genes queried are present. We therefore reject an interferon-driven or interferon-suppressed mechanism for this contrast.", "STEP 6 (measured RNA abundance; inferred phenotype): The executioner arm is uncoupled from priming, with GSDMD near the bottom of the distribution and NEK7 reduced, predicting that APOE4 microglia accumulate a chronically primed, chemokine-secreting, lipid-laden state rather than proceeding to rapid pyroptotic lysis."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/CLEAR-type lysosomal catabolic expansion whose limiting step is glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin turnover, yielding interferon-independent NF-kB chemokine priming with a blunted pyroptotic executioner arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1932823839001244, "cosine_similarity": 0.39278708061732875, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6174336569579288, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1932823839001244, "cosine_similarity": 0.39278708061732875, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6174336569579288, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.565841, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 114}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_136", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1, ISG15/MX1/STAT1) means not supplied, not measured-and-unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects span -7.9 to +15.5 with a strongly non-zero centre (median +1.46, 77% positive), so all claims use ranks within the supplied list rather than absolute fold changes; the shift may be technical (normalization/selection) rather than a true global upregulation.", "Transcript abundance is treated as a proxy for pathway capacity only; hydrolase activity, TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal pH, lipid pools, respiration and glycolytic rates were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with several candidate genes each; no spot uniquely identifies a protein, and spots containing cathepsins move in both directions (protein_spot:052/053/057 up, protein_spot:058/067 down), so protein data are treated as weakly corroborating at best.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at a single timepoint under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived signals and cell-composition differences could contribute to the microglial signature, and causality by APOE genotype is not established by these data.", "Inflammatory/interferon suppression is claimed only as absence of enrichment in the supplied list, not as demonstrated repression of interferon signalling."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) differ from APOE3 primarily through a lysosomal substrate-handling bottleneck rather than through inflammatory or interferon signalling: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake (SCARB1) and for acid hydrolases that degrade glyco-/sphingolipid and glycogen substrates (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) are coordinately among the highest-ranked changes in the supplied differential list, together with a mitochondrial TCA/ETC and beta-oxidation-support program (OGDH, MDH1, MPC2, ACO2, DLD, NDUFA5, ETFA, HADHA, SCP2) and peroxiredoxin/GPX4 antioxidant transcripts, while committed glycolytic and pentose-phosphate steps (HK2, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD) fall below the list-wide shift; canonical type I interferon effectors are absent from the differential list altogether and NF-kB/inflammasome transcripts sit at the list-wide background, so an interferon- or inflammation-driven mechanism is rejected as unsupported here. We infer, but have not shown, that APOE4 raises lysosomal lipid load so that degradation and post-hydrolytic disposal, not transcript availability, limit flux, forcing carbon into mitochondrial oxidation and leaving little glycolytic reserve for acute inflammatory activation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: loading APOE3 microglia with lysosomal lipid (acid-lipase inhibition with lalistat, or U18666A-mediated block of lysosomal cholesterol egress) should reproduce the APOE4 signature - coordinate rise in GAA/GBA/HEXA/SMPD1/CTSB/CTSD transcripts with increased basal oxygen consumption and reduced HK2/PFKP transcripts and glycolytic reserve - whereas the same treatment in APOE4 cells should add little further change (occlusion). If lipid loading in APOE3 fails to reproduce the hydrolase-up/glycolysis-down pattern, or if it is fully additive in APOE4, the bottleneck assignment is weakened.", "Relieving the bottleneck should reverse the state: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should reduce LAMP1-compartment neutral-lipid/filipin signal and normalize the hydrolase, MPC2/OGDH/MDH1 and HK2/PFKP transcript differences toward APOE3. No reduction of lysosomal lipid, or lipid reduction without transcriptional normalization, would weaken the mechanism.", "Flux prediction: extracellular-flux assay should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and lower glycolytic capacity/reserve in APOE4 than APOE3, with a larger etomoxir- or CPT1-inhibitor-sensitive OCR fraction in APOE4. Equal OCR, or APOE4 being the more glycolytic genotype, falsifies steps 4-5.", "Causal test of step 2: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown or a MiT-family degrader should collapse the APOE4-specific hydrolase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, SLC38A7) and worsen lysosomal lipid accumulation; unchanged hydrolase transcripts after TFEB loss would falsify the MiT/TFEB attribution while leaving the load hypothesis intact.", "Negative interferon prediction: at baseline, APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should not differ in phospho-STAT1, ISG15/MX1/IFIT1 protein or secreted IFN-beta/CXCL10; a genuine baseline interferon signature in APOE4 (or ISG induction that precedes lysosomal lipid accumulation in a time course) would overturn the rejection of the interferon/inflammation mechanism and favour an IFN-driven alternative.", "Functional consequence prediction: on acute LPS or 2-h phagocytic challenge, APOE4 microglia should show a blunted glycolytic burst (extracellular acidification rate) and reduced degradation of pHrodo/DQ-BSA cargo per internalized particle relative to APOE3, despite equal or higher hydrolase transcript levels; equal cargo degradation rates would weaken the claim that throughput, rather than transcript availability, is limiting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_136", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 raises transcript levels of the selective lipoprotein/cholesteryl-ester uptake receptor SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, effect +8.22, list percentile 0.99), which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein-derived lipid to the endolysosome; lipid delivery itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred transcription-factor activity): the resulting substrate load is proposed to raise MiT/TFEB-family transcriptional activity, seen as increased TFEB transcript (gene:TFEB +2.38) and coordinate induction of 11 of 12 measured acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17) plus the lysosomal amino-acid efflux transporter gene:SLC38A7 (+7.46); nuclear TFEB localization and hydrolase enzymatic activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): despite hydrolase induction, post-hydrolytic disposal of sterol/lipid remains limiting, because re-esterification (gene:SOAT1 +1.25) and the cholesterol-transfer protein transcript gene:NPC2 (+1.17) sit at or below the list-wide median shift while uptake and hydrolase transcripts are at the top of the distribution, and the dominant microglial protease transcript gene:CTSS is strongly reduced (-5.57, percentile 0.01), indicating a compositional rather than uniformly expanded degradative apparatus; lipid pools, LIPA and NPC1 were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): fatty acids and amino acids liberated in the lysosome are inferred to be routed to mitochondria, matching elevated pyruvate/TCA/ETC and lipid-transfer transcripts (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:HADHA +2.86) and antioxidant transcripts consistent with increased oxidative load (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79).", "Step 5 (measured RNA): committed glycolytic and pentose-phosphate steps are relatively suppressed against the list-wide upward shift (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, all in the bottom quintile of the list), so we infer reduced glycolytic and NADPH-generating reserve even though glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) are up.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, negative arm): consistent with a metabolically constrained rather than interferon-activated state, no canonical type I interferon effector appears in the supplied differential list, and interferon-adjacent sensor/TF transcripts that are present rank at or below the list-wide shift (gene:IFI16 +1.25 percentile 0.31, gene:TMEM173 +1.22, gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:IRF2 -1.17), while NF-kB/inflammasome transcripts as a set sit at the background rank (permutation p = 0.65); the APOE4 phenotype is therefore attributed to lysosomal-metabolic constraint, not to interferon or NF-kB drive."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are constrained by lysosomal lipid-catabolic throughput, not by interferon/NF-kB activation: a MiT/TFEB hydrolase + mitochondrial-oxidative, glycolysis-poor state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2165700129825281, "cosine_similarity": 0.39229762804516577, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_136", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5992750809061488, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2165700129825281, "cosine_similarity": 0.39229762804516577, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5992750809061488, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.58691725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 115}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_089", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a supplied, pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; module directions were therefore judged against that 77%-positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, most ARP2/3 and clathrin adaptor members) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Program membership was assigned from prior pathway knowledge (unverified, no literature retrieval available) before looking at effect signs, and all represented members were kept including sign exceptions.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for activity or flux: no cholesterol esterification rate, ER-accessible sterol pool, lysosomal pH, protease activity, lipid droplet content or cargo clearance rate was measured in these data.", "Protein rows are 2D-gel-style spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (KRT1/KRT10/ACTB are frequent contaminant-like candidates); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot-level changes are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply extracellular lipoproteins and debris, so uptake-receptor capacity is relevant even under mock treatment; this substrate supply was not measured.", "Coherent direction within a module is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test; module members are co-regulated and non-independent, so binomial comparisons against the list background are indicative only (lysosome 33/36 positive, p~0.045; lipid 28/30, p~0.03; uptake receptors 23/25, p~0.09).", "Effects are group-level between two genotypes and could partly reflect differing proportions of microglial substates rather than a uniform per-cell change; replicate structure was not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a broken engulfment apparatus but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors and for endosome-to-lysosome routing are coherently increased, lipid arriving in the endolysosome is preferentially retained in lysosomal and esterified pools rather than replenishing the ER-accessible sterol pool, and the resulting persistent low-ER-sterol read-out plus lysosomal cargo load keeps SREBP target genes and a TFEB-associated hydrolase/v-ATPase program transcriptionally on. This is an inferred routing/cell-state difference; no lipid flux, ER sterol pool, or degradation rate was measured, so an ongoing degradative failure is not established and may only be revealed by a lipid challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective challenge (discriminating): pulse APOE4 and isogenic APOE3 microglia with a defined lipid load (myelin debris, acetylated LDL, or cholesterol/methyl-beta-cyclodextrin). The mechanism predicts equal or greater initial internalisation in APOE4 but a larger and longer-lasting increase in neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content and a failure to shut off SREBP2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7) within hours. If APOE4 clears the load at least as fast as APOE3 and suppresses SREBP2 targets with the same kinetics, the sequestration mechanism is weakened and the increased-throughput adaptation alternative is favoured.", "Prospective pharmacology: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should shift sterol from esterified to ER-accessible pools and suppress SREBP2 target transcripts and the TFEB-associated hydrolase/v-ATPase program more strongly in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes, or none, would weaken step 3-4.", "Prospective flux measurement in the measured mock condition: DQ-BSA and fluorescent-myelin pulse-chase plus lysosomal pH (LysoSensor) should show APOE4 with normal-or-higher lysosomal mass and acidification but a lower fractional degradation rate of lipid-rich cargo. Higher fractional degradation with normal lipid content in APOE4 would refute the sequestration reading and support successful adaptation.", "Prospective genetic test: TFEB knockdown should preferentially collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program and unmask exaggerated lipid accumulation in APOE4 relative to APOE3; if APOE4 lipid content is unchanged by TFEB knockdown, the biogenesis response is not load-driven as proposed.", "Prospective proteoform test resolving the ambiguous spots: 2D-gel plus targeted immunoblot for CTSD, CTSB and ATP6V1E1 should show an APOE4 shift between pro- and mature-form spots rather than a uniform increase in total protein (spots protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:052 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down). A uniform, proteoform-independent decrease in total mature cathepsin or v-ATPase protein in APOE4 would contradict the biogenesis step and favour a primary lysosomal-capacity defect instead.", "Prospective specificity test: the mechanism does not require an actin/engulfment defect. Bead or synaptosome engulfment assays should show APOE4 uptake per cell that is unchanged or increased despite reduced MYH9/MYO1F/RAC2/DOCK8 transcripts; a clear reduction in engulfment index under mock would favour the phagocytic-machinery alternative over this lipid-routing mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts encoding lipoprotein/debris uptake and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:ITGB1 +6.3, gene:ANXA1 +4.2, gene:SIRPA, gene:CD47, gene:ABCA7, gene:ITGAX, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2; 23 of 25 represented members positive vs a 77% positive selected-list background), which is expected to increase capacity for internalising astrocyte-derived lipoproteins and debris (capacity inferred, uptake flux not measured).", "Transcripts for clathrin/dynamin uptake and endosome-to-late-endosome/lysosome routing are also up (gene:DNM2 +5.8, gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:AP3D1 +4.4, gene:SNX3 +3.9, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:RAB7A +2.7, gene:CLTB +2.1), consistent with cargo being routed to the degradative compartment rather than recycled (routing inferred from transcripts, not imaged).", "Lipid delivered to that compartment is preferentially held in lysosomal and esterified pools instead of returning sterol to the ER regulatory pool: esterification/storage and lysosomal lipid-handling transcripts rise together (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:MGLL +4.0, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SCP2 +6.0, gene:LAMP1 +1.4, gene:SCARB2 +1.1).", "Because the ER-sensed sterol pool is not repleted, the SREBP-driven synthesis-and-uptake program stays on: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87 (10/10 represented members positive), with a parallel fatty-acid/phospholipid arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:FADS1 +1.59). This closes a feed-forward loop with step 1.", "Lysosomal cargo load engages a TFEB-associated biogenesis response: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, all 11 represented v-ATPase/acidification members positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6V0C +3.5, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.3, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.7, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:CLCN7), and 17/19 represented hydrolases positive (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.4, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:HEXB +2.2, gene:MAN2B1 +1.8, gene:SUMF1 +2.0). Whether this expanded machinery restores degradative flux is unknown.", "The state is accompanied by selective, not global, cytoskeletal retuning rather than a uniform engulfment deficit: branched-actin/regulator transcripts rise (gene:ARPC4 +1.9, gene:ARPC5 +1.9, gene:ARPC1B +2.2, gene:CFL1 +1.8, gene:CORO1B +2.2, gene:TWF2 +2.7, gene:RHOA +1.6) while motor/leukocyte-motility transcripts fall (gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:VASP -3.4, gene:RAC2 -2.0, gene:DOCK8 -2.0, gene:ARHGDIB -2.0), and a mild NF-kB/chemokine tone is present (gene:CXCL8 +3.1, gene:NFKBIZ +3.1, gene:CCL2 +2.1, gene:MYD88 +2.3).", "Predicted functional consequence in the measured mock condition: a lipid-laden, degradation-expanded microglial state with reduced reserve for a further lipid/debris load, rather than a demonstrated ongoing clearance failure."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-uptake-to-endolysosomal-storage state in which sterol is sequestered away from the ER sensor, sustaining feed-forward SREBP and TFEB-associated lysosomal-biogenesis transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22650740316803897, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2489856633117523, "cosine_similarity": 0.3915255779930836, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5853786407766991, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22650740316803897, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2489856633117523, "cosine_similarity": 0.3915255779930836, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5853786407766991, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.589121, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 25}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_078", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects (logarithm base not specified in the workbook) rank genes correctly; only relative ranks within the same list, not absolute magnitudes, are used.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, no |effect| \u003c 1) with 77% of rows positive, so all module statements are made against the internal background of this list, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "Increased hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to translate into some increase in lysosomal enzyme protein and acidification capacity; this was not measured and the 2D-gel spots cannot test it because each spot has multiple candidate genes.", "Prosaposin/saposins, ASAH1, UGCG, SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2 and all lipid species are unmeasured; the bottleneck at the hydrolysis step is inferred from the transcript asymmetry plus inferred substrate influx, not observed.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may reflect non-cell-autonomous signalling or residual astrocyte contamination.", "A compensatory (substrate-driven) interpretation is assumed for the coordinated hydrolase induction; the opposite interpretation (successful, fully compensating clearance) is not excluded by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the differentiating state is an expanded late-endosome/lysosome catabolic program aimed at complex sphingolipids (transcripts for GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLA, SMPD1, SCARB2, NPC2, GLTP and v-ATPase subunits are among the most strongly increased, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63 in the reported log units), whereas transcripts of the de novo ceramide-synthesis arm that were measured are not increased above the global shift (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:ORMDL2, gene:SGPL1; catabolic vs synthetic arm one-sided Mann-Whitney p = 0.025). We hypothesise that increased delivery of sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo into the endolysosome (inferred from strongly increased lipid-uptake and storage transcripts gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) exceeds hydrolytic clearance capacity, so that lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolysis is the bottleneck and the hydrolase/acidification transcript increase is a compensatory (CLEAR/TFEB-type) response rather than evidence of resolved flux. The predicted lipid-level consequence is a shift of the APOE4 sphingolipidome toward retained hexosylceramide/lactosylceramide/GM3 and ceramide with a lower sphingomyelin-to-ceramide ratio, generated by salvage/turnover rather than by serine-palmitoyltransferase flux. No causality is established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer prediction: pulse-chase of exogenous labelled complex sphingolipid (e.g. 13C/NBD-sphingomyelin or labelled apoptotic-cell/myelin membranes) will show higher hydrolysis-derived ceramide and sphingosine in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia, while de novo flux from 13C3,15N-serine/palmitate into dihydroceramide will not differ significantly; if instead the APOE4-APOE3 ceramide difference is abolished by myriocin (SPT inhibition) and de novo label flux is higher in APOE4, the turnover-bottleneck mechanism is wrong.", "Steady-state lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia will show increased hexosylceramide, lactosylceramide/GM3 and ceramide with a decreased sphingomyelin/ceramide ratio; if all sphingolipid classes are within ~10% between genotypes while cholesteryl esters or triacylglycerol carry the entire difference, the sphingolipid mechanism is rejected in favour of a neutral-lipid/cholesterol-storage mechanism.", "Perturbation: low-dose GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) or GBA knockdown will produce a larger absolute increase in glucosylceramide, LysoTracker signal and lysosomal lipid-load, and a larger drop in phagocytic substrate clearance, in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3; equal or smaller sensitivity in APOE4 would weaken the claim that GBA-dependent hydrolysis is the limiting node.", "Rescue: increasing hydrolytic capacity (recombinant/overexpressed GBA plus HEXA/HEXB, or an SMPD1-independent chaperone such as ambroxol) will normalise the APOE4 glycosphingolipid excess and lysosomal enlargement without changing APOE expression; failure to normalise despite verified increased enzyme activity would point instead to a cofactor (saposin/BMP) or lipid-presentation defect.", "Specificity control: if a re-analysis with matched normalisation shows the lysosomal/sphingolipid module is no more shifted than unrelated modules (the OXPHOS-annotated genes here have a higher mean effect, +4.81 vs +3.17 for the lysosomal set), and enzyme activity assays show no genotype difference, the pathway-coherence argument collapses into a global-shift artefact.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot or targeted MS of GBA, HEXB and CTSD in sorted microglia will show increased mature enzyme in APOE4; the ambiguous 2D-gel spots (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 increased; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 decreased) contain CTSB/CTSD/HEXB among several candidates and currently give conflicting directions, so a uniformly unchanged or decreased mature hydrolase level would weaken Step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show markedly increased transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and neutral-lipid esterification (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, 99th percentile; gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1). We infer, but did not measure, a higher influx of membrane- and lipoprotein-derived sphingolipid into the endocytic pathway.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization): Endolysosomal maturation and acidification transcripts are coordinately increased (gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1; gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), consistent with an enlarged, more acidic degradative compartment; compartment size, pH and vesicle flux were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred enzymatic activity): The lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase module is disproportionately induced (gene:GBA 98th percentile, gene:HEXA 96th, gene:SMPD1 95th, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, plus the GBA-delivery receptor gene:SCARB2, the sulfatase-activating gene:SUMF1, the lipid-presentation/transfer genes gene:NPC2 and gene:GLTP). Transcript abundance is not activity: saposin/prosaposin (PSAP), ASAH1, GALC and ARSA were not measured, so cofactor-limited hydrolysis remains possible.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, contrast): The measured biosynthetic arm is flat relative to the global up-shift (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1 near the median; gene:B4GALT5 -1.88, 13th percentile), so the sphingolipid signal is asymmetric toward turnover/salvage rather than net new synthesis; SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2 and DEGS1 were not measured.", "Step 5 (inferred bottleneck): Because substrate delivery (Step 1-2) is inferred to rise faster than effective hydrolase activity (Step 3), luminal glycosphingolipid intermediates upstream of GBA and of the HEXA/HEXB-GM2A step (GlcCer, LacCer, GM2/GM3) are predicted to accumulate at steady state, while increased gene:SMPD1 and increased ceramide-reacylation capacity (gene:CERS4 +2.52) shift the pool toward ceramide and away from sphingomyelin.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Reduced gene:RAB27A (-2.52, 8th percentile) together with increased efflux/handling transcripts (gene:SPNS1, gene:SLC17A5, gene:ABCA7, gene:IGF2R with decreased gene:M6PR) is interpreted as biased routing toward intracellular retention and recycling rather than lysosomal exocytic disposal of sphingolipid catabolites; secretion and exocytosis were not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a substrate-driven lysosomal sphingolipid-turnover program: glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolysis, not de novo synthesis, is the rate-limiting node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2153195731639774, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23290661060829557, "cosine_similarity": 0.3908399504678218, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137864077669902, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2153195731639774, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23290661060829557, "cosine_similarity": 0.3908399504678218, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137864077669902, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.55837575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 116}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_069", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level statistics are computed as ranks within this selected background, and absolute log-fold-change magnitudes (logarithm base unspecified, up to 15.5) are treated as ordinal only.", "The strong global upward shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46) is at least partly technical/normalisation-related; only direction relative to that background is interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the capacity of a compartment, not for its flux, pH, localisation or enzymatic activity, none of which were measured here.", "TFEB transcript elevation is assumed to accompany, but does not demonstrate, increased TFEB nuclear activity; an alternative is transcript-level compensation without activation.", "Coordinate SREBP-target elevation is assumed to reflect ER sterol-sensor state; HMGCR, SQLE and most pre-squalene mevalonate genes were not measured, so the sterol-synthesis arm is incompletely sampled.", "NPC1, MCOLN1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2 and LAMP2 are absent from the supplied rows; the proposed egress bottleneck is therefore an inference from the hydrolysis/sensing mismatch, not a measured defect.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; spot-level changes may reflect isoform, fragment or post-translational shifts rather than total protein abundance.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous consequences of APOE4 astrocyte lipid handling.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values (all \u003c0.05, median 2.4e-25) cannot be independently assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally at a degradative/export step of the endolysosome rather than at internalization: lysosomal hydrolase and V-ATPase-subunit transcripts and TFEB are coordinately elevated (rank-permutation p=0.0023 against the study's own selected-gene background), yet ER sterol-responsive and lipogenic transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, SREBF1, SCD, SCP2, SOAT1, DGAT1) are simultaneously elevated. Simultaneous 'more lysosome' and 'ER senses sterol deficit' signatures are most parsimoniously explained by hydrolysed cholesterol failing to reach the ER, i.e. limited lysosome-to-ER sterol egress, which we propose as the primary bottleneck. The assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal focus is not supported: phagocytic-receptor transcripts are indistinguishable from the global upward shift (p=0.35) and actin/motility-contractility transcripts are significantly shifted downward relative to background (p=0.0086). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating rescue: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or restoring NPC1-dependent export, should normalise SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, ACAT2) and blunt the CLEAR/hydrolase and V-ATPase mRNA induction toward APOE3 levels, without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, MERTK, TREM2). If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated after cholesterol is removed from the lysosomal lumen, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Imaging: filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol and LipidSpot-positive neutral lipid should be increased specifically within LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4. If total sterol is unchanged, or excess sterol is found at the plasma membrane/ER with normal lysosomal filipin, the mechanism is weakened.", "Uptake versus degradation split: pHrodo-labelled bead, myelin or apoptotic-cell internalisation rate in APOE4 should be equal to or lower than APOE3, whereas DQ-BSA or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester dequenching (degradation/processing) should be delayed. A clear increase in initial internalisation rate would support a phagocytic-uptake mechanism instead and falsify the 'downstream of internalisation' claim.", "Cytoskeletal test of the rejected focus: APOE4 microglia should show reduced or unchanged Arp2/3-dependent lamellipodial spreading and reduced migration velocity, consistent with lower ACTB/MYH9/RAC2/DOCK8 transcripts. Increased spreading and phagocytic-cup formation would falsify the rejection of the cytoskeletal alternative.", "Acidification/throughput: LysoSensor or lysosomal pH ratiometric measurement plus cathepsin-B/L activity assays should show that lysosomal pH is not lower and hydrolase activity is not proportionally higher in APOE4 despite elevated hydrolase and V-ATPase mRNAs (consistent with protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067). Finding proportionally increased acidification and hydrolase activity would remove the proposed capacity/throughput mismatch.", "Esterification test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol and increase lysosomal stress markers without normalising SREBP-2 target transcripts; normalisation of SREBP-2 targets by SOAT1 inhibition alone would place the bottleneck at ER esterification rather than lysosomal egress.", "Directional control: acute lipid loading of APOE3 microglia (e.g. myelin debris or oxLDL) should reproduce the coupled CLEAR-plus-SREBP signature; if loading APOE3 induces CLEAR genes but suppresses SREBP-2 targets as expected for normal egress, the APOE4-specific uncoupling is supported, and failure to see any uncoupling difference would weaken the hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype (APOE transcript itself modestly higher, gene:APOE) changes the composition/handling of internalised lipoprotein and lipid cargo delivered to the endolysosome; cargo flux is inferred, not measured.", "Endosome-to-lysosome maturation and retrograde/late-endosomal transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:DNM2, gene:IGF2R, gene:AP5M1), consistent with an enlarged or more active degradative compartment; compartment size, position and fusion rate are inferred, not measured.", "A CLEAR-type transcriptional programme is induced: gene:TFEB is elevated together with luminal hydrolase mRNAs (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) and V-ATPase subunit mRNAs (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1). TFEB nuclear localisation and transcription-factor activity are inferred; only transcript abundance is measured.", "Hydrolytic capacity is nonetheless not translated into effective sterol delivery to the ER: the ER sterol sensor behaves as if sterol-deficient, since SREBP-2/post-squalene and lipogenic targets rise (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:INSIG1). This mismatch defines the proposed primary bottleneck: NPC-dependent lysosome-to-ER cholesterol export (NPC1 and MCOLN1 were not measured; gene:NPC2 is only modestly higher).", "Sterol/lipid that does reach the ER is preferentially re-esterified and stored rather than effluxed, favoured by higher gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD and gene:SCP2; ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured, so the efflux arm is unconstrained by these data.", "The resulting feed-forward loop (continued receptor-mediated uptake plus continued synthesis, limited egress) predicts progressive lysosomal/neutral-lipid accumulation, while motility and contractile actin transcripts fall (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:MYO1F, gene:VASP, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:PLEK), predicting slower cargo processing and migration rather than increased engulfment.", "Protein-spot data are only weakly consistent and partly discordant: spots whose candidate lists include V-ATPase V1 and cathepsin subunits are lower in APOE4 (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069), so we predict that acidification/hydrolase protein does not scale with the mRNA induction, further limiting degradative throughput. Spot identities are ambiguous (multi-gene candidate lists) and cannot assign these changes to a named protein."], "title": "A post-uptake endolysosomal cholesterol-egress bottleneck, not increased phagocytic or actin machinery, drives coupled TFEB/CLEAR and SREBP transcriptional induction in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17820255993661227, "cosine_similarity": 0.3903311034640768, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961391585760517, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17820255993661227, "cosine_similarity": 0.3903311034640768, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961391585760517, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.76781075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 117}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_021", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Higher transcript abundance for the carrier/TCA/lysosome modules corresponds to at least proportionally higher enzyme and transporter protein capacity; this is unverified here, because the 92 protein spots contain no mitochondrial candidate genes and RNA vs spot effects are uncorrelated (r=-0.06 over 118 gene-spot pairs).", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is left unspecified; only ranks and relative module shifts are used, and the whole-module comparison is made against the strongly right-shifted background of the selected rows (77% positive, mean 1.39) rather than against zero.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, all |effect|\u003e1), so absent genes (ACLY, FASN, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2) are of unknown status and enrichment statistics are conditional on this selection.", "The measurement is attributed to microglia in a microglia-astrocyte co-culture; a shift in cell-state or cell-type composition between genotypes could produce the same pseudobulk pattern.", "Replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so the reported p-values cannot be checked for pseudoreplication, and the global upward shift is assumed to be at least partly biological rather than entirely a normalisation or depth artifact.", "Metabolite pools (citrate, acetyl-CoA, cholesteryl ester), lipid droplets, respiration and lysosomal pH were not measured; all flux, localisation and directional statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated increase in mitochondrial oxidative/anaplerotic gene expression whose functional core is the pyruvate- and citrate-handling carrier node (MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11 with cytosolic MDH1/GOT1); we hypothesise that this node is rate-controlling for cytosolic acetyl-CoA/NADPH supply, and that its increased capacity, combined with elevated lysosomal hydrolase and lipid-receptor transcripts, drives higher SREBP-target sterol synthesis and SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification, predicting cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol accumulation in APOE4 microglia. Only transcript (and ambiguous protein-spot) abundances were measured; flux, localisation, metabolite pools and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, SLC25A1 knockdown or citrate-carrier inhibition (CTPI-2) should reduce 13C-glucose- or 13C-pyruvate-derived labelling of cholesterol and cholesteryl ester and should close at least half of the APOE4-minus-APOE3 neutral-lipid-droplet gap, while leaving the ETC transcript difference intact. If labelled carbon entry into sterol/CE is equal between genotypes, or if the lipid gap is unchanged by SLC25A1 loss, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Substrate-source discrimination: culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium should preserve most of the APOE4 excess in cholesteryl ester if mitochondrially exported carbon dominates; if the excess disappears without exogenous lipoprotein, the mechanism must be reassigned to SCARB1/CD36/LDLR-mediated uptake rather than to the carrier node.", "Capacity check: Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and maximal OCR and a higher OCR/ECAR ratio in APOE4; equal or lower respiration despite the 38 up ETC transcripts would show the RNA shift is not converted into oxidative capacity and would weaken steps 1-2.", "Protein-level requirement: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS must show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for SLC25A1, MPC2, MDH1 and OGDH protein; unchanged protein for these four would falsify the assumption linking the RNA module to enzymatic capacity, given the near-zero RNA/protein-spot concordance in the supplied data.", "Substrate-supply arm: inhibiting lysosomal acid lipase (lalistat) or v-ATPase (bafilomycin A1) should lower cholesteryl-ester synthesis more in APOE4 than APOE3; an equal or larger effect in APOE3 would weaken step 3 without necessarily falsifying the carrier-node step.", "Specificity: SOAT1 inhibition should convert the APOE4 excess from cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol without abolishing the elevated citrate-derived sterol labelling; loss of the labelling difference under SOAT1 inhibition would indicate the esterification step, not carbon export, is rate-controlling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts of 67 mitochondrion-annotated genes are higher in APOE4 (96% up, mean effect 3.28 vs 1.39 for all 2212 selected RNA rows; permutation p=5e-5), including all 38 detected ETC subunits (gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:SDHB). Inferred, not measured: greater mitochondrial oxidative capacity and/or mitochondrial mass; no respiration, membrane-potential or mtDNA measurement is supplied.", "Measured: the carbon-entry and shuttle module is the most strongly shifted subset - gene:MPC2 (pyruvate carrier), gene:SLC25A1 (citrate/malate carrier), gene:SLC25A11 (2-oxoglutarate/malate), gene:MDH1 and gene:GOT1 (cytosolic malate-aspartate shuttle), gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:GLUD1 (mean effect 5.7). Inferred: increased pyruvate import, NADH shuttling and cataplerotic citrate export to the cytosol; the citrate and acetyl-CoA pools themselves are unmeasured, and ACLY is absent from the supplied rows.", "Measured: lysosomal transcripts are coordinately elevated (23-gene set mean 3.01, permutation p=0.0014): gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB and eight v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C). Together with lipid-uptake receptors gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7 this suggests, but does not demonstrate, greater delivery of exogenous and membrane lipid into an acidified degradative compartment; lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and lipid-droplet content were not measured.", "Inferred coupling step: hydrolysis-derived acetyl units and pyruvate enter the TCA cycle, and the elevated MPC2/SLC25A1 carrier node exports citrate to the cytosol, where gene:ACSS2 (acetate salvage), gene:ACAT2 (acetoacetyl-CoA thiolase) and gene:ME1 (cytosolic NADPH) provide the remaining substrate and reducing equivalents for sterol synthesis. This is the proposed bottleneck: carrier-limited export of mitochondrial carbon, not enzyme abundance in the sterol pathway itself.", "Measured: the sterol/lipogenic transcriptional arm is up in APOE4 - gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SCD - as are the esterifying enzymes gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1. Inferred: higher flux into cholesterol and into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol storage rather than efflux (ABCA1 and ABCG1 are not in the supplied rows, so the efflux arm is untested).", "Predicted phenotype (not measured here): APOE4 microglia hold more neutral lipid in cytoplasmic droplets and more cholesteryl ester per cell than isogenic APOE3, with a larger fraction of sterol carbon derived from mitochondrially exported citrate."], "title": "Mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate export (MPC2-SLC25A1 node) as the rate-controlling step channelling lysosome- and uptake-derived carbon into SREBP-driven sterol synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30360018068523603, "cosine_similarity": 0.39031536703191383, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5895501618122977, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30360018068523603, "cosine_similarity": 0.39031536703191383, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5895501618122977, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.46841075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 118}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_092", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, median +1.46 in the unspecified log base); enrichment is therefore judged by within-list rank percentiles rather than by sign or raw magnitude.", "Rank-percentile permutation enrichment of a curated lysosomal gene set reflects a genuine coordinated program rather than gene-length, detection-rate or ambient-RNA artefacts of the 10X Flex pseudobulk comparison.", "Transcript abundance of hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits is a proxy for compartment biogenesis, not for measured enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, protein abundance or localization, none of which are supplied.", "TFEB and MITF transcript elevation is used as an indicator of program engagement; their activity is set by phosphorylation and nuclear translocation, which are not measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes, so spot-level changes cannot be attributed to any single lysosomal protein; they are used only as ambiguity/counter-evidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture and possible genotype-dependent differences in cell state, cell-cycle or capture efficiency are assumed not to be the sole source of the global shift.", "Key sterol nodes (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, PLIN2) are absent from the supplied list, so the sterol arm is under-measured rather than shown to be unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background elevation of lysosomal hydrolase, V-ATPase and endolysosomal-maturation transcripts together with the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors TFEB and MITF. We propose that the rate-limiting node is luminal catabolic throughput per lysosome relative to internalized substrate flux: transcriptional expansion of the degradative compartment is a compensatory response that is incompletely matched at the protein and hydrolase-delivery level (M6PR and CTSS transcripts fall; lysosomal-candidate protein spots move in both directions), so degradative flux is predicted to lag transcript abundance. Sterol synthesis, sensing and export transcripts are only elevated to the same degree as the strong global upward shift of these selected differential-expression rows and are therefore treated as a secondary, non-enriched arm rather than the primary bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown or pharmacological inhibition of TFEB (with MITF) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript elevation towards APOE3 levels and increase accumulation of undegraded phagocytic cargo; if the hydrolase transcript elevation persists essentially unchanged after TFEB/MITF loss, the proposed transcriptional driver step is wrong.", "Flux-versus-transcript test: DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin-B activity and pHrodo/LysoSensor readouts normalised per LAMP1 area should show APOE4 degradative flux and per-lysosome activity equal to or lower than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; proportional, matched increases in flux would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Sterol-focus discriminator: relieving lysosomal cholesterol egress (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1 overexpression) should not normalise the lysosomal transcript program if the bottleneck is general catabolic throughput; full normalisation of hydrolase/TFEB transcripts by cyclodextrin would support a sterol-egress bottleneck instead and falsify this hypothesis as stated.", "Protein-level test: targeted or label-free MS resolving the ambiguous spots (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:053) should show mature cathepsin B/D and HEXB protein rising far less than their transcripts, and a fall in cation-dependent M6PR; concordant, proportional protein increases would weaken the incomplete-compensation step.", "Substrate challenge: loading with synaptosomes or myelin should produce greater persistence of undegraded material in APOE4 than APOE3 over 24-48 h with a further TFEB-target transcript rise; equal clearance kinetics would weaken the mechanism.", "Independent-cohort replication: in a fresh isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia dataset analysed as an unbiased whole transcriptome, the lysosomal gene set should retain above-background rank enrichment while cholesterol-biosynthesis and sterol-export sets should not; enrichment of the sterol sets with loss of the lysosomal signal would falsify the choice of bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters the composition and handling of endocytosed apoE-lipid and other phagocytic cargo in microglia (inferred; cargo pools, uptake rate and lipid species were not measured here).", "Cargo that is catabolised slowly accumulates in late endosomes/lysosomes, so luminal substrate flux exceeds per-lysosome hydrolytic and acidification capacity (inferred flux, not measured).", "This load engages the MITF/TFEB-family lysosomal-biogenesis program; TFEB and MITF transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, unspecified log base), which we read as increased program output, not as measured nuclear TFEB localization or dephosphorylation.", "Downstream, acid hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts rise coherently above the global shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK; gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1; plus gene:LAMP1, gene:CLN3, gene:SCARB2, gene:SLC38A7), consistent with expansion of the degradative compartment.", "Endolysosomal maturation and hydrolase-sorting transcripts also rise (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP3D1, gene:MON1B, gene:VAC14, gene:IGF2R, gene:GNPTG), while gene:M6PR and gene:CTSS fall, predicting a compositionally skewed rather than uniformly scaled lysosome.", "Because compensation is partial, undegraded lipid is inferred to be re-routed into esterification and storage and to keep an ER sterol/lipogenic arm mildly active (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1); this arm is not enriched above background and is stated as a consequence, not as the driver.", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia carry a larger, transcriptionally hyperactive but flux-limited lysosomal compartment, with degradative capacity per unit LAMP1 no higher than APOE3."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-biogenesis program that indexes a bottleneck in luminal degradative throughput, not in sterol synthesis or export"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1901968924781519, "cosine_similarity": 0.3902549384246639, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6038770226537217, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1901968924781519, "cosine_similarity": 0.3902549384246639, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6038770226537217, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.603559, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 119}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_055", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no supplied value has |effect| \u003c 1 and 77% are positive), so all statements are relative ranks within that list, not unbiased whole-transcriptome changes; the logarithm base is unspecified and left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein amount and for flux; no enzyme activity, lipid, cholesterol, filipin, droplet, SREBP-cleavage or trafficking measurement is supplied, and lysosomal or ER free-cholesterol pools were not observed.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes; spot-level changes are treated as ambiguous evidence of processed-form redistribution, not as identified proteins.", "Effect magnitude and p-value are essentially uncorrelated in the supplied RNA rows (Spearman |effect| vs -log10 p = -0.03), so extreme magnitudes are treated as ranks rather than calibrated fold changes.", "RNA is assumed to come from the microglial compartment despite astrocyte co-culture; NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2, HSPA5 and XBP1 are absent from the supplied list and their status is unknown.", "The APOE4-versus-APOE3 comparison is isogenic and unperturbed (mock), so differences are genotype-associated; no intervention was performed, so causal direction is assumed, not established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 primarily by a transport bottleneck in the endolysosome-to-ER handoff of liberated lipid, not by an unfolded-protein response: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and for a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase/V-ATPase program are among the highest-ranked in the supplied differential list, while the lysosomal lipid-export/sorting module (NPC2, M6PR) sits at the bottom of the same list; the inferred consequence is that the ER regulatory sterol pool stays low, SREBP-target and desaturation/esterification transcripts remain high despite increased uptake, and excess lipid is routed into ester/droplet storage. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol retention in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC2/NPC1 overexpression) should lower SREBP-target transcripts (SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, HMGCS1) and reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content toward APOE3 levels while lysosomal hydrolase transcripts fall only later; if SREBP targets and droplets are unchanged after egress is restored, the ER-sensing bottleneck is wrong.", "Reciprocal test: blocking lysosomal cholesterol egress in APOE3 microglia (U18666A) should phenocopy the APOE4 profile (higher SREBP-target and hydrolase transcripts, more droplets); if APOE3 instead suppresses SREBP targets, the mechanism fails.", "Uptake dependence: culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-deficient medium, or knocking down SCARB1, should collapse most of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid-load and SREBP-target difference; persistence of the difference would favour a cell-autonomous de novo lipogenesis mechanism instead.", "Storage step: SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol and, if the ER sensor is functional, suppress SREBP targets more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3; failure to suppress would place the defect upstream in delivery rather than in esterification.", "Rejection of the ER-proteostasis alternative: if direct assays show elevated XBP1 splicing, BiP/HSPA5 induction, eIF2-alpha phosphorylation or ERAD substrate stabilisation in APOE4 under mock conditions, the proteostasis mechanism should replace this one; conversely, the present model predicts no XBP1 splicing difference and no BiP induction, and it is weakened if lysosomal free cholesterol (filipin) and droplet content are equal between genotypes."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 raises the transcript program for receptor-mediated lipid and lipoprotein internalisation (gene:SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of the supplied list; gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2 positive), which we infer, but did not measure, increases lipid delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): A coordinated lysosomal degradation/acidification program is elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1), accompanied by ER N-glycosylation/glycoprotein-maturation machinery needed to build these glycosylated hydrolases (gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:MLEC, gene:UGGT1); this is read as biosynthetic support for hydrolase production, not as an unfolded-protein response.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured transcripts, inferred transport): The lysosomal lipid-export and hydrolase-sorting module fails to scale with Steps 1-2 - gene:NPC2 lies in the bottom third of the positively shifted list and gene:M6PR is decreased, while gene:APOE and gene:ABCA7 are only modestly changed - so we infer limited transfer of liberated free cholesterol from the lysosomal lumen to the ER and limited efflux.", "Step 4 (inferred activity): Because the ER-membrane regulatory sterol pool is not replenished, SCAP-INSIG-SREBP remains in its low-sterol configuration; consistent with this, sterol/lipogenic transcripts stay high despite high uptake (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LPCAT1). Nuclear SREBP processing itself was not measured.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): Continued synthesis plus continued uptake is disposed of by ER-resident esterification and storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and by increased oxidative/TCA transcript capacity (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2), predicting cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet accumulation as the APOE4 endpoint phenotype (lipids were not measured here).", "Step 6 (protein-level correlate, ambiguous identity): Hydrolase-candidate protein spots redistribute rather than rise uniformly - protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 and protein_spot:057 increase while protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 decrease - consistent with altered processing/compartmental distribution of lysosomal hydrolases; each spot has several candidate genes and none is uniquely identified."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolysis without matching lysosome-to-ER sterol egress, leaving the ER sterol sensor 'blind' and sustaining a futile uptake-plus-lipogenesis loop"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3552966805745301, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.308868181072741, "cosine_similarity": 0.3898584768500778, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6005177993527508, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3552966805745301, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.308868181072741, "cosine_similarity": 0.3898584768500778, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6005177993527508, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.68767875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 120}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so pathway claims are made as relative enrichment against the within-list background (median approx +1.46), not against an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene is uninformative.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein-spot log2 effects are not placed on a common scale.", "The reduced mtDNA-encoded transcript signal reflects a real per-cell reduction in mitochondrial transcript or mtDNA copy number rather than a droplet-QC, ambient-RNA or library-size normalisation artefact.", "Steady-state subunit transcript levels are at least partially predictive of the corresponding protein pools available for assembly; no OXPHOS subunit protein, assembled complex, respiration rate, membrane potential, ROS level, mtDNA copy number, or lipid species was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:077 lists KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB; protein_spot:017 lists CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and are therefore treated as weakly consistent, not as identified PRDX2 or catalase protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may reflect altered microglia-astrocyte cross-talk rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects; genotype is isogenic but replicate structure was not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be judged.", "TFEB, HIF1A and SREBF1 transcript increases are used as markers of programme engagement; their nuclear localisation and transcriptional activity were not measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a discordant respiratory-chain transcript program in which nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA subunits are coordinately elevated while mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are reduced. We hypothesise that mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for holoenzyme assembly, so that oxidative ATP-generating flux capacity is constrained despite an expanded nuclear mitochondrial program; the resulting bioenergetic and redox strain is compensated by HIF1A/SLC2A1 glycolytic bias, a TFEB-associated lysosomal-hydrolase program, and SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1-driven diversion of lipid into storage rather than oxidation. This is a proposed causal chain, not an established one: only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and no assembly, flux, or localisation measurement is available.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show reduced assembled complex V, III and IV holoenzyme relative to APOE3, together with normal or increased free nuclear-encoded subunit pools (an increased unassembled-to-assembled ratio). If assembled holoenzyme levels are equal or higher in APOE4 while free subunit pools are unchanged, the assembly-bottleneck step is falsified.", "Extracellular flux (Seahorse) should show reduced ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption and reduced spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 mock microglia, with increased basal ECAR/OCR ratio. Unchanged or increased maximal OCR would weaken the mechanism at Step 4.", "mtDNA copy number and absolute per-cell mitochondrial transcript counts (spike-in normalised) should be lower in APOE4. If absolute MT transcript per cell is unchanged and the apparent MT decrease is purely a compositional/normalisation consequence of the global positive shift, Step 2 and the whole bottleneck claim collapse.", "Rescue prediction: restoring mtDNA-encoded core supply (TFAM overexpression, or allotopic/nuclear-recoded ATP6 expression, or mtDNA-replication support) should raise assembled complex V, increase ATP-linked OCR, and partially normalise the downstream lipid-storage and lysosomal-hydrolase transcript programme (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, CTSB, GBA, ATP6V1H). Failure to reduce lipid storage despite restored respiration would break Step 6.", "Reciprocal prediction: pharmacological inhibition of ATP synthase (oligomycin) or complex III (antimycin) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 transcript signature (up HIF1A/SLC2A1, up TFEB-lysosomal genes, up SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1). Absence of phenocopy would argue the APOE4 programme is not downstream of an OXPHOS constraint.", "Negative/discriminating control against the interferon alternative: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade should NOT normalise the mitonuclear discordance, the lysosomal programme, or lipid storage in APOE4 microglia. If IFN blockade rescues these phenotypes, an interferon-driven mechanism should be preferred over this one.", "Direct lipid test: APOE4 microglia should show increased neutral-lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester content with reduced 13C-palmitate oxidation to CO2 relative to APOE3 under mock. Equal or higher fatty-acid oxidation flux in APOE4 would weaken Step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia carry an elevated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcript program - 36 nuclear OXPHOS subunit genes sit well above the already-positive background of this selected DE list (median approx +2.6 vs +1.5 background; 78% above the global median), together with TCA-cycle (MDH1, OGDH, DLD, ACO2) and mitochondrial import/chaperone transcripts (TOMM22, TIMM44, HSPA9, PHB, CHCHD3).", "Step 2 (measured, RNA; discordant): mtDNA-encoded core subunits move in the opposite direction (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4 all reduced; MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L increased), a within-sample discordance that is significant against the nuclear set and is not attributable to the global positive shift.", "Step 3 (inferred, not measured): because complexes III, IV and V each require an mtDNA-encoded catalytic core, reduced core-subunit supply limits holoenzyme assembly; imported nuclear-encoded subunits should therefore accumulate as unassembled or partially assembled modules rather than as functional complexes. No assembled-complex, BN-PAGE or subunit-protein pool was measured here.", "Step 4 (inferred activity/flux): constrained assembly lowers coupled respiration and ATP-synthase capacity and increases electron leak. Consistent transcript correlates are an antioxidant/thiol-peroxidase program (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, FTH1, NNT) and mitochondrial proteostatic/ISR markers (DDIT3, EIF2AK3, HSPA9, PHB); these are abundance readouts, not activity or ROS measurements.", "Step 5 (inferred compensation): the energetic shortfall is buffered by a glycolytic shift (HIF1A, SLC2A1, PRKAA1 transcripts elevated) and by a TFEB-associated lysosomal-catabolic program (TFEB, CTSB, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C).", "Step 6 (inferred, links to lipid phenotype): with mitochondrial beta-oxidation/acetyl-CoA disposal capacity constrained and lipogenic/esterification transcripts elevated (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, plus sterol-pathway DHCR24, LSS, ABCA7), lipid carbon is diverted into neutral-lipid and sterol-ester storage and into the lysosomal compartment, producing the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype. No lipid pool was measured in this dataset."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply is the assembly bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, driving a compensatory glycolytic-lysosomal-lipogenic state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08317025440313111, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24536836941916826, "cosine_similarity": 0.3897740616747256, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904077669902913, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08317025440313111, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24536836941916826, "cosine_similarity": 0.3897740616747256, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904077669902913, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6626825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 121}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_174", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are reported log fold changes of unspecified base; the analysis uses only ranks, signs and within-dataset comparisons so that conclusions do not depend on the base.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 0.5, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive, median +1.46), not an unbiased transcriptome; every set-level statement is therefore made against the internal 77.1%-up / +1.46-median background rather than against zero.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance, and enzyme abundance a partial proxy for capacity; no measurement of enzyme activity, metabolite level, isotope flux, membrane potential or ATP was supplied, so all flux, localisation and directionality statements are inferred.", "HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA/LDHB, PDHA1 and CS are absent from the supplied list, so total hexokinase/PFK capacity is unknown; the bottleneck claim assumes that the inducible, myeloid-biased HK2/PFKP pool contributes materially to the microglial glycolytic reserve.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; spots 077, 038 and 072 are cited only as weak, non-identifying consistency checks, not as measurements of PRDX2, ALDOA or PGAM1 protein.", "Only 6 of 13 mtDNA-encoded protein genes appear in the list, and MT-ND4 and MT-ND4L (co-transcribed on one bicistronic RNA) move in opposite directions, so the mitonuclear-mismatch step (Step 5) is assumed to reflect biology rather than 10X Flex probe/mapping behaviour; this is the weakest link in the chain.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular lactate, glutamine and lipid availability are set partly by the astrocyte compartment; genotype-specific substrate exchange was not measured and is assumed not to invert the direction of the inferred microglial fluxes.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so no power or reproducibility assessment was possible.", "Background knowledge used to assign genes to pathways (glycolysis, TCA, OXPHOS complex membership, mtDNA-encoded gene set, SREBP targets) is unverified, since literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 by a transcriptional configuration in which the ATP-consuming committed steps of glycolysis (HK2, PFKP, plus HK3 and PFKFB2) are selectively repressed while glucose transporters, lower-glycolytic enzymes, the full nuclear-encoded OXPHOS set, TCA enzymes and glutamine/anaplerotic import machinery are coordinately elevated. We hypothesise that the primary metabolic bottleneck in APOE4 microglia is glucose commitment at the hexokinase/phosphofructokinase step, not glucose uptake, so that carbon for ATP and for the lipogenic citrate pool is drawn disproportionately from glutamine and other non-glucose substrates; because mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunits do not follow the nuclear OXPHOS expansion, the resulting oxidative dependence has a low ceiling and is accompanied by integrated-stress and antioxidant transcriptional responses. All statements refer to measured transcript/protein-spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer prediction: parallel U-13C6-glucose and U-13C5-glutamine labelling of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under identical mock conditions should show, in APOE4, lower fractional 13C enrichment of lactate and lower glucose-derived m+2 citrate/malate, together with higher glutamine-derived (m+4/m+5) enrichment of TCA intermediates and of exported citrate. If APOE4 shows equal or greater glucose-derived lactate and TCA labelling, or no increase in glutamine-derived TCA labelling, the proposed bottleneck and the substrate switch are falsified.", "Dependency prediction: glutamine withdrawal or glutaminase inhibition (e.g. CB-839) should reduce ATP content and viability disproportionately in APOE4 relative to APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose should be comparatively better tolerated by APOE4. Equal glutamine dependence in the two genotypes, or greater APOE4 sensitivity to 2-deoxyglucose, would weaken the mechanism.", "Reserve prediction: extracellular-flux analysis should show reduced glycolytic reserve in APOE4 (smaller ECAR rise after oligomycin and after an acute inflammatory or ATP-demand challenge) despite unchanged or higher basal glucose uptake, consistent with a commitment-step rather than an uptake limitation. A normal or enhanced APOE4 glycolytic reserve would falsify Step 2.", "Bottleneck-identity prediction: doxycycline-inducible HK2 (or PFKP) re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore glucose-derived lactate labelling and glycolytic reserve and reduce glutaminase-inhibitor sensitivity, without requiring correction of the OXPHOS transcripts. If HK2/PFKP restoration leaves glucose flux unchanged, the assigned primary bottleneck is wrong and an HK1/PFKL-dominated or downstream (PKM/LDH) limitation should be considered instead.", "Mitonuclear-ceiling prediction (tests Step 5 separately): blue-native PAGE and in-gel activity, plus complex IV and complex V specific activities normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or mtDNA copy number), should show that assembled holoenzyme activity in APOE4 does NOT scale with the uniform increase in nuclear subunit transcripts, and that spare respiratory capacity is reduced. If assembled complex IV/V activity and spare respiratory capacity rise in proportion to the nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, Step 5 is falsified while Steps 1-3 could still stand, and the phenotype should be re-interpreted as a genuine, unconstrained oxidative shift.", "Directionality prediction: acute APOE4-to-APOE3 gene correction (or APOE knockdown) in the same isogenic background should move HK2/PFKP transcripts and glucose-derived lactate labelling back toward APOE3 values within the same differentiation window. Failure of the metabolic phenotype to track the corrected allele would indicate that the differences are clone- or differentiation-derived rather than APOE4-driven; the present mock-treatment comparison cannot establish causality."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_174", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show selectively reduced transcript abundance for the committed, ATP-consuming glycolytic steps (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, HK3 -1.12, PFKFB2 -1.10 in the reported log units; HK2 and PFKP sit in the 3.6th and 5.5th percentile of a differential-expression list whose median is +1.46), while glucose-transport and lower-glycolysis transcripts are increased (SLC2A3 +3.73, SLC2A1 +2.37, PFKM +2.41, ENO1 +2.17, GPI +2.06, SLC16A1 +1.12).", "Step 2 (inferred flux): with uptake capacity preserved but glucose-6-phosphate/fructose-1,6-bisphosphate production capacity reduced, net glycolytic flux and the ability to expand lactate output are predicted to be lower in APOE4, i.e. a reduced glycolytic reserve rather than an absolute block.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred compensation): transcripts for glutamine uptake and deamination and for anaplerotic shuttles are coordinately raised (GOT1 +6.43, SLC25A11 +4.50, SLC25A1 +4.47, GLUD1 +3.17, SLC1A5 +1.55, ME1 +1.36, GLS +1.35), together with TCA-cycle and PDH-activating transcripts (MDH1 +8.72, OGDH +8.56, DLD +5.54, IDH3G +3.94, ACO2 +3.54, PDP1 +3.00, IDH3B +2.02, SDHB +1.65); we infer increased reliance on glutamine/glutamate-derived and other non-glucose carbon to fill the TCA cycle and to supply exported citrate.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): every nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript in the dataset is increased (38/38 up, median +2.64 versus the +1.46 list median; complex I 21/21, III 3/3, IV 6/6, V 7/7), as is mitochondrial protein-import machinery (TIMM8B +5.20, TOMM22 +4.63, TIMM44 +2.46, TIMM17B +2.00), consistent with an expanded demand for oxidative ATP generation rather than a glycolytic one.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred ceiling): mtDNA-encoded core subunits do not follow the nuclear expansion (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; only MT-ND4L +1.95 and MT-ND5 +1.93 are up), so the stoichiometry needed to assemble complexes I, III, IV and V is predicted to be mismatched and assembled-holoenzyme capacity to lag behind nuclear subunit supply.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred consequence): stress-response transcripts consistent with mitochondrial-to-nuclear signalling and redox load are elevated (DELE1 +4.82, ATF6 +4.04, DDIT3 +2.79, SHMT2 +2.22, EIF2AK3 +1.51; PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, NNT +2.88, GPX4 +2.79), and one significant protein spot whose candidate list includes PRDX2 is increased (+1.07); we infer a chronically stressed, low-reserve oxidative state rather than a healthy increase in oxidative capacity.", "Step 7 (inferred phenotype): the net predicted state is an APOE4 microglion that cannot mount a glycolytic switch on demand, depends on glutamine/lipid-derived oxidative ATP with limited spare respiratory capacity, and diverts mitochondrial citrate into the elevated lipogenic/sterol program (SREBF1 +4.67, LDLR +1.50, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, HMGCS1 +1.08, SREBF2 +1.06, CD36 +1.38)."], "title": "Committed-step glycolytic restriction (HK2/PFKP) forces APOE4 microglia onto glutamine-fed mitochondrial oxidation whose capacity is capped by a mitonuclear subunit mismatch"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07240704500978473, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2750005793187618, "cosine_similarity": 0.3895847607177257, "direction_accuracy": 0.12135922330097088, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_174", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5918867313915858, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07240704500978473, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2750005793187618, "cosine_similarity": 0.3895847607177257, "direction_accuracy": 0.12135922330097088, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5918867313915858, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.434198, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 122}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_129", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all RNA statements are relative comparisons within this dataset only.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1), not an unbiased transcriptome; module claims are therefore made relative to the pervasive global up-shift (median +1.46) rather than to zero.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein abundance and for contractile/degradative activity; this proxy is unverified here for MYH9, ACTB, MYO1F and the cathepsins.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates, so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "No lipid, cholesterol, phagocytic-flux, motility, lysosomal-pH, enzyme-activity or imaging measurement is present in the supplied data; every such statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an APOE4 effect could be cell-extrinsic (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein composition) rather than microglia-intrinsic; the mechanism does not distinguish these.", "Background pathway assignments (myosin-II in cup closure and phagolysosome resolution; SREBP sterol sensing; LAM/foamy microglial markers) are unverified background knowledge, since literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 cells by a coordinated, direction-discordant loss of the leukocyte actomyosin/motility transcript module (MYH9, ACTB, VASP, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGAP30, PLEK, SPN, FAM49B, CTSS; module median approximately -3.7 in the reported log scale against a +1.46 median for all 2212 selected DE rows) combined with a higher-ranked scavenger-receptor and lysosomal hydrolase/acidification program (SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163, TREM2, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H, TFEB) and a lipid-storage/foamy signature (GPNMB, LGALS3, APOE, ACP5, FABP5, SOAT1, DGAT1). We propose that reduced actomyosin contractile capacity, not reduced degradative enzyme capacity, is the primary bottleneck: it limits actin-dependent uptake of large particulate cargo and limits tubulation/fission-dependent resolution of the phagolysosome, so cargo that still enters through non-contractility-dependent scavenger and lipoprotein routes is retained in an expanded acidic compartment and is diverted into esterified/stored lipid. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, activity, localization and lipid statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo-split assay: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, uptake per cell of actomyosin-dependent particulate cargo (3 um pHrodo beads, pHrodo myelin, synaptosomes) and myosin-II-dependent process motility will be lower in APOE4, while uptake of soluble receptor-mediated cargo (DiI-acLDL, 10 kDa dextran) will be equal or higher, with higher BODIPY neutral-lipid content. If APOE4 shows equal or greater particulate engulfment and unchanged motility, the actomyosin bottleneck is falsified.", "Phenocopy test: acute myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or ROCK inhibition in APOE3 microglia will increase BODIPY/filipin lipid load and prolong pulse-chase retention of labelled myelin without increasing acLDL uptake rate. Failure to phenocopy weakens the causal ordering.", "Arm-dissociation test: SCARB1 and/or CD36 blockade or knockdown in APOE4 microglia will lower neutral-lipid and lysosomal cholesterol load but will not restore particulate engulfment or motility. If receptor blockade restores engulfment/motility, then uptake-receptor overload, not actomyosin loss, is the primary bottleneck.", "Resolution vs capacity test: pulse-chase with DQ-BSA and labelled myelin will show longer cargo residence time and more persistent residual bodies in APOE4 despite equal or higher cathepsin B/D enzymatic activity. If measured cathepsin activity is lower in APOE4, the competing degradative-capacity-deficit model supersedes this one.", "Proxy-validation test: immunoblot/immunofluorescence will show lower MYH9 protein and lower phospho-myosin-light-chain in APOE4 microglia. If MYH9 protein and phospho-MLC are unchanged, the transcript-to-activity assumption fails and the mechanism must be discarded even if the phenotype persists.", "Artifact-control test: re-analysis with an independent normalization (e.g. spike-in or cell-number-anchored counts) and matched sequencing depth will retain the coordinated down-shift of the actomyosin module relative to other high-expression transcripts. If the module down-shift disappears under alternative normalization, the observation is a compositional artifact and the hypothesis is unsupported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_129", "mechanism_steps": ["State (measured, RNA only): APOE4 microglia show coordinated lower transcript abundance for the actomyosin/leukocyte-motility module (gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB, gene:VASP, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:PLEK, gene:SPN, gene:TMSB10, gene:PAK2, gene:HCK, gene:CTSS). These are down against a strongly positive global background (median +1.46 across all selected rows), so they are conservative calls.", "Inferred activity (not measured): lower non-muscle myosin-II/actomyosin contractile capacity and reduced Rac2-DOCK8-dependent protrusive signalling reduce the force-generating steps of phagocytic cup closure for large particulate cargo and reduce myosin/actin-dependent tubulation and fission that resolve mature phagolysosomes.", "State (measured, RNA only): scavenger and lipoprotein-uptake receptors and complement opsonin transcripts are simultaneously higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2, gene:CLEC7A, gene:C1QA, gene:CD14, gene:FCGRT), together with lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase/biogenesis transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB).", "Inferred flux (not measured): cargo entry is therefore biased toward receptor-mediated soluble/lipoprotein routes that do not require myosin-II contractility, while the actomyosin-dependent particulate route and the resolution step downstream of degradation become rate-limiting; net cargo residence time in the endolysosomal compartment increases even though hydrolase transcripts are higher.", "Inferred consequence (not measured): retained lipid cargo is shunted into esterification and storage rather than export, consistent with higher gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ABCA7 and with the lipid-associated/foamy microglial signature (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:APOE, gene:ACP5, gene:FABP5, gene:PLA2G7, gene:NPC2), which is the most significance-enriched module in the dataset (mean p-value percentile rank 0.063, permutation p \u003c 1e-4).", "Inferred feed-forward loop (not measured): because the accumulated lipid is sequestered away from the ER sterol sensor, sterol-synthesis and uptake transcripts are not switched off (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR), sustaining further lipid loading and locking the APOE4 cell into a low-motility, lipid-laden state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose the actomyosin engulfment/resolution module while expanding scavenger-lysosomal lipid handling, making myosin-II-dependent cargo internalization and phagolysosome resolution the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2111563531742563, "cosine_similarity": 0.389535108681808, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_129", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5892944983818771, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2111563531742563, "cosine_similarity": 0.389535108681808, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5892944983818771, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90201925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 123}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_089", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (no supplied row has |effect| \u003c 1) and not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made relative to the other selected rows, not to all genes.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; RNA effect magnitudes are therefore not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot effects, and only directions and within-modality ranks are used.", "2D-gel spots contain several candidate genes; every protein statement is a statement about a mixed spot, not about a uniquely identified protein, and a spot change may reflect a co-migrating protein, a proteoform shift (processing, cleavage, modification) or a mobility change rather than total abundance.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the size of the corresponding machinery; enzyme activity, luminal pH, vesicle flux, protein localisation and cargo residence time were not measured and are inferred.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex; some transcript signal could arise from ambient or non-microglial RNA, and biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect precision cannot be assessed.", "No lipid, lipid-droplet, phagocytosis, degradation-rate or pH measurement is present in the supplied data; the lipid-storage endpoint is a prediction, not an observation.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30, so differences are attributed to genotype-linked steady state rather than to an acute stimulus."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the clathrin/dynamin-endosome-retromer-lysosome axis (CLTB, DNM2, RAB7A, SNX3, VPS26A/VPS35L, ESCRT, TFEB/MITF, V-ATPase subunits, luminal hydrolases) that is not matched at the protein-spot level for mature hydrolase- and V-ATPase-containing spots; we hypothesise that cargo internalisation capacity is increased while terminal degradative throughput per lysosome is limiting, so internalised lipid-rich cargo dwells longer in LAMP1+ compartments and is shunted into esterification/storage (SOAT1, DGAT1) alongside an SREBF1-driven lipogenic program. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance measurements; the mechanism is proposed, not demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake-versus-degradation test: pulse APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with a dual-labelled cargo (pH-insensitive uptake tracer plus DQ-BSA or a quenched cathepsin substrate). The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalised cargo in APOE4 but a lower dequenching rate per unit internalised cargo and longer cargo residence in LAMP1+ compartments. If APOE4 internalises less cargo, or degrades each internalised unit at the same or a faster rate, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Lysosomal capacity test: measure lysosomal pH (ratiometric probe) and mature cathepsin B/D activity per LAMP1 area. The mechanism predicts higher lysosome number/LAMP1 area in APOE4 with equal or lower activity and higher (less acidic) pH per lysosome. If per-lysosome activity and acidification scale with the elevated hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts, the transcript-to-protein bottleneck step is falsified.", "Cytoskeletal arm test: Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) should reduce cargo internalisation more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3 and lower downstream neutral-lipid accumulation, whereas myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) should have a smaller differential effect. Equal CK-666 sensitivity in both genotypes would remove the branched-actin internalisation step.", "Epistasis test: forcing further lysosome biogenesis (TFEB overexpression or mTORC1 inhibition) should not normalise per-cargo degradation if maturation of hydrolases/V-ATPase is limiting, whereas raising terminal capacity (acidifying nanoparticles, recombinant hydrolase supplementation, or cathepsin-activity restoration) should shorten cargo residence and reduce SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent ester accumulation. Full rescue by TFEB alone would favour a biogenesis-deficit model instead.", "Downstream-lipid test: SOAT1 (or DGAT1) inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet load in APOE4 without shortening cargo residence time in LAMP1+ compartments. If SOAT1 inhibition also normalises cargo residence time, esterification is upstream of, rather than downstream of, the proposed bottleneck.", "Modality-resolution test: targeted immunoblot or MS re-identification of the reduced spots (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) should show reduced mature cathepsin B/D or ATP6V1E1 in APOE4. If those spots resolve to unrelated co-migrating proteins, or mature cathepsin protein is increased in APOE4, the central RNA-protein discordance supporting the bottleneck collapses.", "Specificity test: an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement should retain endolysosomal enrichment after correcting for the global positive shift of this selected list. If endolysosomal genes are no more shifted than a size-matched random gene set in unbiased data, the mechanism loses its transcriptional support."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts encoding clathrin-mediated entry and endosome maturation machinery are higher in APOE4 (gene:CLTB, gene:DNM2, gene:RAB7A, gene:RAB32, gene:SNX3, gene:SNX17, gene:PIK3C3). Inferred (not measured): an increased rate of vesicular cargo internalisation and delivery to late endosomes.", "Measured: retromer/SNX-BAR and ESCRT transcripts are among the most elevated rows (gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:VPS37B, gene:VPS28, gene:CHMP4B), and two up-changed spots list retromer candidates (protein_spot:044 candidate VPS26A, protein_spot:076 candidate VPS29). Inferred: enlarged/remodelled sorting endosome capacity; spot identity is ambiguous and retromer localisation was not measured.", "Measured: a lysosome-biogenesis transcriptional signature is elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:LAMP1, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1). Inferred: attempted compensatory expansion of the degradative compartment; TFEB nuclear localisation and lysosome number were not measured.", "Measured (discordance, the proposed bottleneck): spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins or the V-ATPase E1 subunit are reduced or bidirectional rather than uniformly increased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 decreased; protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 increased). Inferred: transcriptional biogenesis is not converted into proportionally increased mature hydrolase and proton-pump protein, limiting acidification-dependent catabolic throughput per lysosome. Enzyme activity, luminal pH and cargo residence time were not measured.", "Measured: actin-nucleation and filament-turnover candidates dominate the increased protein spots (protein_spot:036 ACTR2/CAPG, protein_spot:038 ARPC1B, protein_spot:081 and protein_spot:082 ARPC5, protein_spot:061 and protein_spot:063 ARPC2, protein_spot:055/056/057 CAPZB, protein_spot:092 PFN1, protein_spot:041 TWF2, protein_spot:012 WDR1, protein_spot:017 CORO1C, protein_spot:006/007 GSN), whereas contractile/late-engulfment transcripts are reduced (gene:MYH9, gene:RAC2, gene:MYO1F) and a MYL12B-candidate spot is reduced (protein_spot:079). Inferred: the cytoskeletal shift favours branched-actin-dependent vesicular internalisation over myosin-II-dependent large-particle engulfment; no phagocytosis assay was supplied.", "Measured: ANXA1 is elevated in both modalities (gene:ANXA1; increased ANXA1-candidate spots protein_spot:041, protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:047). Inferred: increased Ca2+/phospholipid-dependent membrane engagement supporting cargo capture and endomembrane repair; ANXA1 localisation and FPR2 signalling were not measured.", "Measured: sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts are elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) together with a low-grade inflammatory set (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:HIF1A). Inferred and explicitly not observed here: accumulation of cholesteryl esters and lipid droplets as the downstream consequence of limited lysosomal catabolism; no lipid species were measured in this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand endocytic delivery and lysosome-biogenesis transcription while terminal hydrolytic/acidification protein capacity fails to scale, making per-cargo lysosomal catabolism the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09295499021526418, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.231432939874018, "cosine_similarity": 0.38902385973526193, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956699029126215, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09295499021526418, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.231432939874018, "cosine_similarity": 0.38902385973526193, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956699029126215, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.658512, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 124}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_016", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77% up, median +1.46); all pathway statements are therefore made relative to that biased background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effects (log2) are not placed on a common scale.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme and receptor protein levels; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, sterol localization and lipid content are inferred, not measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes, so spot-level changes are treated as proteoform-level observations of unidentified proteins, not as quantification of a named protein.", "Signal is assumed to arise from the microglia rather than from co-cultured astrocytes or ambient RNA; no cell-type deconvolution or replicate structure is supplied to test this.", "Genotype is assumed to be the only systematic difference (isogenic pair, mock treatment); causality is not established by these association-level data."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, increased scavenger/lipoprotein-mediated lipid cargo delivery outstrips the capacity of the endolysosome to hydrolyse and export that cargo; the resulting luminal lipid retention drives a TFEB-associated compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis transcriptional program while the ER continues to read a sterol-poor state and keeps SREBP target genes high. Interferon/ISG signaling is not detectably engaged and is rejected as the differentiating mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test of the egress bottleneck: load APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with cholesterol by two routes - LDL (lysosome-routed) versus methyl-beta-cyclodextrin:cholesterol (delivered directly to the plasma membrane/ER). SREBP target transcripts (SCD, DHCR7, LDLR, INSIG1) should be suppressed equally in both genotypes by cyclodextrin:cholesterol, but significantly less in APOE4 than APOE3 after LDL loading. If APOE4 suppresses SREBP targets as efficiently as APOE3 after LDL loading, the lysosomal-egress bottleneck is weakened and an uptake- or biosynthesis-driven model should be preferred.", "Imaging: unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and LysoTracker/LAMP1-positive compartment volume should be higher in mock APOE4 than APOE3 microglia, with filipin signal colocalising with LAMP1. Absence of increased lysosomal cholesterol or of compartment expansion despite the hydrolase transcript elevation would weaken step 2-3.", "Relieving the bottleneck (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or enhancing lysosomal sterol export) should lower SREBP target transcripts and the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the hydrolase program after the lysosomal lipid load is cleared would argue for a TFEB-independent, genotype-intrinsic transcriptional difference instead.", "TFEB knockdown or MiT/TFE-family inhibition should blunt the coordinated hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4; if hydrolase transcripts remain elevated, the TFEB-coordination step (step 3) is wrong even if the bottleneck holds.", "Negative control for the rejected interferon branch: JAK1/2 or IFNAR1 blockade in mock APOE4 microglia should leave the lysosomal and SREBP transcript modules essentially unchanged, and an ISG panel (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1) should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference at baseline. Detection of a coherent baseline ISG elevation, or normalisation of the lysosomal module by JAK inhibition, would revive an interferon-driven mechanism and falsify the rejection.", "Functional flux: a quenched lysosomal substrate assay (DQ-BSA or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester turnover) should show reduced per-lysosome cargo clearance rate in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; equal or faster clearance would falsify the core claim that capacity, not enzyme message, is limiting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors and ligands are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:APOE). Inferred (not measured): greater flux of lipoprotein and membrane-lipid cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Inferred bottleneck: luminal hydrolysis plus sterol/sphingolipid export from the late endosome-lysosome is rate-limiting in APOE4, so lipid substrate is retained in the lysosomal lumen. The lipid pool itself is unmeasured in this dataset.", "Measured compensatory response: a coordinated up-shift of lysosomal-biogenesis transcripts above the already up-shifted background of this filtered list (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH; cathepsins gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51; gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A, gene:CLCN7, gene:CLN3). Inferred: expanded/acidified degradative compartment; enzyme activity and localization are not measured.", "Measured: SREBP-axis transcripts are simultaneously high (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SREBF2). Inferred causal direction: sterol delivered to the lysosome is not reaching the ER sensor, so SREBP cleavage remains permissive despite increased uptake - the signature expected of an egress, not an uptake, defect.", "Inferred downstream disposal: retained neutral lipid is re-esterified and stored rather than exported (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:MGLL +4.00), consistent with a lipid-laden, less homeostatic microglial state (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:LGALS1 +2.75, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:ABCA7 +2.14).", "Protein-spot level (ambiguous identifications): spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins change in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38). Inferred: redistribution among proteoforms/spot positions rather than a uniform increase in cathepsin protein; no single protein is identified by these spots.", "Rejected alternative branch: no coherent interferon program is present. Of 57 queried canonical type-I/II IFN and ISG genes, only gene:IFI16 (+1.25) appears in the 2212-gene list, at the 39th percentile of its effect distribution; chemokine transcripts (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12) sit at the list median and are treated as a secondary or non-specific correlate, not the driver."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-catabolism/egress bottleneck, not interferon signaling, distinguishes APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12818003913894324, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17565281266212485, "cosine_similarity": 0.38844419487911874, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6068996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12818003913894324, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17565281266212485, "cosine_similarity": 0.38844419487911874, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6068996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.50330475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 125}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_091", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance differences approximate differences in the corresponding protein amounts and hence in maximal capacity of uptake, hydrolysis and esterification; enzyme activity, cargo flux and sterol localisation were not measured.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified log base), so only within-list relative enrichment (rank and significance rank) is interpreted, not absolute direction of the whole transcriptome; a normalisation or cell-composition shift could generate part of the global offset.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increases are used as a proxy for CLEAR-network engagement; their activity is regulated post-translationally (mTORC1-dependent phosphorylation and nuclear translocation) and was not measured here.", "The lipid identity of the accumulating cargo is inferred from receptor and enzyme identity; no lipid, sterol or lipid-droplet measurement is present in the discovery data.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified, so no spot is used as evidence for a specific protein; cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions and are treated as uninformative.", "Key egress genes (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, LIPA, CPT1A) and homeostatic markers (P2RY12, TMEM119, CX3CR1) are absent from the supplied rows, so the bottleneck step and the identity loss are only partially covered.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, an external source of lipoproteins; the observed genotype effect may require this extrinsic lipid supply and is not shown to be cell-autonomous. Causality has not been established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, highly significant increase in scavenger/lipoprotein-receptor and lysosomal-hydrolase transcripts together with loss of homeostatic identity transcripts; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in this state is export of hydrolysed lipid (free cholesterol and fatty acid) out of the endolysosome to the ER/plasma membrane, so that internalised lipid is retained and re-esterified into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplets rather than cleared, while ER sterol feedback stays disengaged. All measurements are RNA and non-unique protein-spot abundances; uptake, hydrolytic flux, sterol localisation and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Primary lipid prediction: day-30 mock APOE4 microglia will contain more neutral lipid and, specifically, more cholesteryl ester per cell than isogenic APOE3 (BODIPY/LipidTOX imaging plus LC-MS sterol-ester quantification), together with larger LAMP1-positive lysosomal volume and increased filipin-stainable cholesterol that colocalises with LAMP1. If APOE4 cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content are equal to or lower than APOE3, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation 1 (source of load): culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking uptake with anti-SCARB1/CD36 or a scavenger-receptor inhibitor, should collapse most of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in lipid-droplet content and in lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, GAA). Persistence of the full difference under lipid-poor conditions would refute step 1 and favour a purely cell-intrinsic synthesis or degradation defect.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (bottleneck test): relieving lysosomal sterol retention with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or over-expressing NPC1, should reduce APOE4 cholesteryl ester and lower SREBP2-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1) more in APOE4 than APOE3. No genotype-selective response would refute step 3, the proposed primary bottleneck.", "Discriminating perturbation 3 (routing test): SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol, engage ER sterol feedback and repress LDLR/HMGCS1 selectively in APOE4. If SREBP2 targets remain unrepressed and free cholesterol does not rise, step 4 is wrong.", "Regulatory test: TFEB knockdown should blunt the APOE4 hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation and further increase undigested lipid; unchanged hydrolase transcripts after TFEB loss would refute step 2.", "Mitochondrial arm test (secondary): if the TCA/OXPHOS transcript elevation reflects genuine capacity, APOE4 basal and maximal oxygen consumption should exceed APOE3; unchanged or reduced respiration would restrict step 6 to a compensatory, non-productive response without falsifying steps 1-5.", "Technical control: if per-cell RNA content or spike-in-normalised re-analysis removes the global positive offset and the scavenger/lysosomal modules lose their significance-rank enrichment, the transcriptional basis of the hypothesis is undermined."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/scavenger and opsonin-phagocytic receptors and their ligand APOE (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:CLEC7A, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE); inferred consequence is increased flux of lipoprotein and membrane-debris cargo into the endolysosome (internalisation rate not measured).", "Step 2 (inferred regulatory activation): transcripts of the CLEAR-network transcription factors TFEB and MITF and of their canonical lysosomal targets rise together (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ACP5, gene:NPC2), consistent with a lysosome-biogenesis response to a sustained degradative load; TFEB nuclear localisation and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (proposed primary bottleneck): egress of liberated cholesterol and fatty acid from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER and plasma membrane does not scale with the uptake and hydrolase increase, so sterol accumulates in a compartment that the ER sensor does not read; the key transporters (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1) are absent from the supplied rows, so this step is an inference, supported only indirectly by the failure of SREBP2-target transcripts to be repressed (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1) despite an increased lipid supply, and by elevated oxysterol-generating and LXR-responsive transcripts (gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7, gene:SREBF1).", "Step 4 (metabolic routing): retained sterol and fatty acid are re-esterified and stored rather than exported, consistent with coordinate elevation of esterification and lipogenic transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:ACSS2); the predicted, currently unmeasured pool is an increase in cholesteryl-ester- and triacylglycerol-rich lipid droplets.", "Step 5 (state consolidation): the chronic lipid-handling load coincides with loss of homeostatic microglial transcripts (gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:TGFBR1 decreased) and gain of lipid-associated/phagolysosomal markers (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:FTH1, gene:SLC11A1, gene:PLA2G7), i.e. a stable lipid-associated microglial state rather than a transient response.", "Step 6 (secondary, weaker arm): transcripts for pyruvate import, TCA enzymes and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are strongly elevated (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH) while a mitochondrially encoded transcript is reduced (gene:MT-ATP6); we treat this as a candidate compensatory attempt to oxidise excess lipid carbon, not as established increased respiratory flux."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a scavenger-receptor-fed, TFEB/MITF-expanded lysosomal program whose lipid egress step is limiting, diverting sterol and fatty-acid carbon into esterified neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2059677220982344, "cosine_similarity": 0.38842053429934015, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5868996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2059677220982344, "cosine_similarity": 0.38842053429934015, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5868996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.188368, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 126}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_096", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) and are therefore not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the internal background of this list (mean effect +1.39, 77% positive), not against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes up to +15.5 are treated as ordinal, and effect size is uncorrelated with adjusted p-value in this list (rank correlation about -0.03), so extreme values (e.g. gene:ITGA6, gene:SLC31A2) are not weighted more heavily.", "The global positive shift (z = 25.5 for the up-fraction) may partly reflect composition or normalization differences between genotypes rather than uniform induction; the hypothesis relies only on relative enrichment above that shift.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features, not uniquely identified proteins; a spot is treated as consistent-with, never as evidence-for, a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for demand and biosynthetic capacity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, sterol localization, lipid-droplet content, TFEB nuclear localization and SREBP-2 cleavage were not measured in this dataset and are inferred.", "Cultures are microglia-astrocyte co-cultures under mock treatment with no supplied replicate count, so genotype effects cannot be separated from astrocyte-derived lipoprotein differences or from clone/batch effects.", "Causality is not established: all statements about direction of flux and about inflammation being downstream are hypotheses, not results."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the dominant coherent transcriptional difference is a coordinated expansion of the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program together with lipoprotein-receptor and SREBP-axis sterol/fatty-acid synthesis transcripts. We propose that the rate-limiting step is post-uptake lysosomal hydrolysis and egress of lipoprotein-derived sterol and sphingolipid: cargo enters the endolysosome faster than it can be catabolised and returned to the ER-accessible sterol pool, so sterol sensing stays de-repressed (SREBP targets up) while TFEB-driven CLEAR transcription is chronically raised, and a low-grade NF-kB/chemokine tone follows as a consequence. A canonical type-I interferon program is not detectable in these data and is rejected as the differentiating mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving the lysosomal sterol-egress step in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should, within 24 h, lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS) by most of the APOE4-minus-APOE3 gap while leaving the CLEAR hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A) only partially reduced - i.e. the two modules decouple. If SREBP-2 targets remain fully elevated after egress rescue, Step 4 and the chosen bottleneck are wrong.", "Interferon-rejection test: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade should close less than ~20% of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 gap in the lysosomal hydrolase and SREBP modules. If JAK inhibition normalizes those modules, an interferon-driven mechanism is the better explanation and this hypothesis fails.", "Localization test: filipin or a D4H sterol biosensor should show increased unesterified cholesterol colocalized with LAMP1 and reduced ER/plasma-membrane-accessible sterol in APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3, with increased BODIPY-positive lipid droplets. Equal sterol distribution between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Capacity-versus-transcript test: mature cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase enzymatic activity per microgram lysosomal protein should rise less than the transcript increase, or fall, in APOE4 (predicted activity:transcript ratio lower than APOE3), consistent with the mixed direction of cathepsin-containing 2D spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down). Proportional activity gains would argue the lysosome is not the bottleneck but merely expanded.", "Order-of-events test: pulse-chase of fluorescent AcLDL/myelin lipid should show equal or greater internalization but delayed degradation and delayed appearance of label in the ER/droplet compartment in APOE4. Equal degradation kinetics with equal uptake would falsify Steps 2-3.", "Downstream-inflammation test: NF-kB inhibition (IKK-beta inhibitor) should reduce CXCL8/CCL2 transcripts in APOE4 without correcting the lysosomal hydrolase or SREBP modules; if it also corrects them, inflammation is upstream and Step 6 is inverted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid receptors and apolipoprotein handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:NPC2), which we infer - not measure - increases delivery of astrocyte- and self-derived lipoprotein lipid into the endocytic route.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization): Endosome maturation and retromer/ESCRT transcripts rise (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:PIK3C3), consistent with increased traffic of that cargo to the late endosome/lysosome; organelle position and cargo identity are not measured here.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred capacity deficit): Luminal hydrolysis and acidification become rate-limiting for the delivered lipid load. The cell responds with a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR output: gene:TFEB, gene:MITF plus acid hydrolases gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK and v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP1. Transcript increase is a demand signal; we do not claim measured enzyme activity.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sterol pool): Despite raised uptake transcripts, the ER-accessible sterol pool is inferred to remain low, because SREBP-axis targets stay high (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:MYLIP). Simultaneous high uptake and high de novo synthesis transcripts is the signature of sterol trapped upstream of the ER, not of sterol excess.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Esterification/storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), which we infer diverts newly available sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl-ester/triglyceride storage rather than into the regulatory ER membrane pool, reinforcing the futile synthesis-plus-storage cycle in Step 4.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred causal direction): Chronic lysosomal lipid load provides a permissive, low-amplitude NF-kB/inflammasome-priming tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:CCL2, gene:MYD88, gene:NLRP3, gene:IL18, gene:PYCARD, gene:CD14, gene:TLR2) that we place downstream of, not upstream of, the lysosomal bottleneck; no canonical type-I interferon module is present to support an interferon-driven alternative (gene:IRF8, gene:IFNAR1, gene:IRF5, gene:IFI16 are the only IFN-adjacent rows and are unremarkable against this list's background)."], "title": "A lysosomal lipid-catabolism/egress bottleneck, not interferon signaling, distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1842252712156083, "cosine_similarity": 0.3882678632787811, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163106796116504, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1842252712156083, "cosine_similarity": 0.3882678632787811, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163106796116504, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.67363375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 127}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_066", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Selected RNA rows are a filtered differential list (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705/2212 positive); program directions are judged against that 77%-positive background, and absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, STAT1/2, ISG15, MX1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and preserved as reported; magnitudes are treated as ranks/directions, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Transcript increases are treated as changed abundance only; increased hydrolase, v-ATPase, SREBP-target and OXPHOS transcripts are not evidence of increased enzyme activity, acidification, sterol flux or respiration.", "Lipid droplet content, cholesteryl-ester mass, ER-accessible sterol, lysosomal pH and efflux were not measured in this dataset; storage/routing is inferred, not observed.", "2D-gel protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate identities each; actin/keratin candidates appear in a majority of spots), so no spot is read as confirmation of an individual protein; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured signal may reflect microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange rather than a microglia-autonomous program.", "Deficits that would appear only after a lipid challenge (myelin, oxLDL) are not claimed as ongoing defects in the mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by interferon/inflammatory activation but by a coordinated transcriptional cell-state change that couples increased lipid/debris uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:C1QA +1.25) to an expanded endolysosomal-hydrolytic compartment (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52) and to esterification/membrane-lipid synthesis (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:SCD +4.17), while the sterol-synthesis/SREBP module remains simultaneously elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87). Co-elevation of uptake, storage and de-novo synthesis is the signature of a routing/sensing mismatch (sterol diverted to lysosomal and esterified/droplet pools rather than replenishing the ER-accessible pool) that sustains its own drive, rather than of a single degradative bottleneck or of a shut-down, sterol-satiated adaptation. Lipid content, flux and ER-accessible sterol were not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, an ER-accessible-cholesterol probe (ALOD4/D4H) should show LOWER ER-pool sterol while total sterol, cholesteryl-ester fraction and BODIPY/LipidSpot droplet area are equal or higher. If ER-accessible sterol is equal or higher while SREBP-target transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS) remain elevated, the routing/sensing-mismatch step is wrong and a sterol-independent SREBF1/lipogenic driver is favoured.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl esters, raise ER-accessible sterol, and normalise the sterol-synthesis module toward APOE3; persistence of elevated gene:DHCR24/gene:LSS/gene:LDLR after effective SOAT1 blockade weakens the feed-forward loop.", "SCARB1 and/or CD36 knockdown should reduce droplet accumulation in APOE4 and blunt the esterification module without abolishing the TFEB/v-ATPase/hydrolase module; if the lysosomal module collapses in parallel, lysosomal expansion is driven by uptake rather than being a co-regulated state.", "Functional lysosomal readouts (DQ-BSA dequenching, LysoTracker, BODIPY-cholesterol egress) should be equal or higher in mock APOE4 if this is increased throughput; a measured decrease despite elevated hydrolase transcripts would replace this mechanism with failed compensation at the degradative step.", "Interferon prediction (rejecting the assigned focus): unstimulated APOE4 microglia should show no increase in a canonical ISG panel (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1) or in secreted IFN-beta relative to APOE3; a clear ISG/IFN-beta increase would show the supplied selected list simply omitted the driving program.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not ongoing defect): after myelin or oxLDL loading, APOE4 should clear labelled cholesterol more slowly and accumulate more esters than APOE3; a slower-clearance result under challenge alone would not establish an ongoing mock-condition defect, and equal clearance would argue the mock-state program is adaptive."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype raises transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and opsonic-phagocytic receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:MFGE8, gene:FCGR1A, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C; 20/20 represented receptor members positive), inferred to increase lipid and debris ingestion.", "Ingested cargo is delivered into an expanded, more acidified endolysosomal compartment: a TFEB-consistent module rises (gene:TFEB, 8/8 v-ATPase subunits incl. gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, hydrolases gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) together with late-endosome/retromer/ESCRT transport (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B).", "Lipid liberated in that compartment is preferentially re-esterified and channelled into storage and membrane glycerophospholipid synthesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL) rather than being fully exported or oxidised.", "Because sterol is held in lysosomal/esterified pools, the ER sterol sensor continues to read deficiency, so SREBP-driven synthesis and uptake genes stay on (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR), closing a feed-forward loop with step 1.", "Increased catabolic/anabolic load is accompanied by a nuclear-encoded mitochondrial and TCA/carbon-entry transcript increase (37/37 nuclear OXPHOS members positive, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:HADHA), interpreted as increased oxidative capacity demand; mtDNA-encoded transcripts move oppositely (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35), so actual oxidative flux is unresolved.", "Net predicted state in mock APOE4: greater intracellular neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal load with only modest chemokine change (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, within the list's 77%-positive background; gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05) and no represented interferon-stimulated-gene program, i.e. lipid routing, not interferon signalling, is the primary genotype difference."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a feed-forward lipid-acquisition/lysosome-expansion state that routes sterol into esterified and membrane-lipid stores instead of the ER regulatory pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2828342502676956, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2564543138588859, "cosine_similarity": 0.38823730443427173, "direction_accuracy": 0.3333333333333333, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5916957928802589, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2828342502676956, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2564543138588859, "cosine_similarity": 0.38823730443427173, "direction_accuracy": 0.3333333333333333, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5916957928802589, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.93819725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 26}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_059", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705/2212 positive); program coherence is judged against that 77%-positive background, and unlisted genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, LIPA, PLIN2, TYROBP) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base and scaling are unspecified and the extreme tail (|effect|\u003e8) contains functionally miscellaneous genes, so directional coherence, not magnitude ranking, carries the program signal.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding proteins/enzymes; no enzymatic activity, uptake rate, lysosomal pH, sterol pool or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so 'increased capacity' and 'routing to storage' are inferences.", "SREBP-target transcript induction is assumed to report low ER-accessible sterol rather than a sterol-independent driver (e.g. LXR loss, growth signalling, or differences in astrocyte-supplied lipid in the co-culture).", "2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each and keratins/ACTB dominate; spot direction is used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of a named protein.", "Spot-level and gene-level distributions are both ~73-77% positive, so a global normalization or selection bias may inflate all positive programs; the mechanism relies on relative coherence and on the sign discordance of the glycolysis/PPP and actin-motor sets.", "Genes within a program are co-regulated and not independent, so the quoted binomial/MWU p-values are descriptive, not formal enrichment statistics.", "Any clearance or lipid-handling failure is a predicted reserve deficit under a future lipid/myelin challenge; the mock data cannot establish an ongoing degradative defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single defective gene but by a coordinated cell-state shift: uptake/opsonin-receptor transcripts are uniformly higher (26/26 represented members positive vs a 77% positive selected-list background, sign p~0.002), the TFEB/CLEAR endolysosomal-hydrolase and V-ATPase program is higher and larger in magnitude than background (24/26 positive, median +1.92 vs +1.46, MWU p=0.045), endosome/retromer/ESCRT transcripts are strongly higher (12/13 positive, median +3.54, MWU p=0.002), and yet SREBP-1/-2 target and lipid-esterification/storage transcripts are also uniformly higher (17/17 positive). Because sterol-sensing output (SREBF1/2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, EBP, DHCR7, DHCR24) remains induced at the same time as uptake capacity, we infer that cholesterol acquired through this expanded uptake-degradation route is not restoring the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool but is being re-esterified (SOAT1) and stored with newly made TAG/monounsaturated FA (DGAT1, AGPAT2, ACSS2, SCD, FABP3/FABP5), giving a self-reinforcing lipid-storing state whose predicted endpoint is increased neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester load; ATP demand for this state is met oxidatively (TCA/ETC transcripts up, median +3.78, MWU p=1e-4) rather than glycolytically (HK2, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD, HK3 down). Only transcript and ambiguous 2D-spot abundances were measured; no flux, sterol pool, uptake rate or droplet measurement is supplied, so causality and any degradative insufficiency are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/biochemistry in the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show higher neutral-lipid droplet content (BODIPY 493/503) and higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio, together with increased LysoTracker/LAMP1 compartment volume. If APOE4 droplet load and esterified-cholesterol fraction are equal to or lower than APOE3, the storage-routing core of the mechanism fails.", "Prospective SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should lower droplet/cholesteryl-ester load and, if sterol routing is the driver of Step 2, partially normalize SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, INSIG1) toward APOE3 levels. Persistent SREBP-target induction after esterification blockade, with unchanged free-cholesterol distribution, would falsify the ER-sterol-sensing step and favour a sterol-independent driver.", "Prospective TFEB knockdown/inhibition should reduce the hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript module in APOE4. If lipid-droplet load and SREBP targets are unchanged by that reduction, the lysosomal expansion is a parallel state marker rather than a step in the lipid-routing chain.", "Discriminating throughput test (prospective): pulse-chase of fluorescent/13C-labelled myelin or acetylated-LDL. The 'successful adaptation / increased throughput' alternative predicts APOE4 clears and oxidizes the label faster with no label accumulation; this hypothesis predicts equal or greater initial uptake but greater retention of undegraded/esterified label and slower conversion of label-derived sterol into the ER-accessible pool (assayed as slower SREBP-target repression after loading). Faster complete clearance with prompt SREBP-target repression in APOE4 would falsify the hypothesis.", "Cytoskeletal-defect alternative test (prospective): bead or apoptotic-cell engulfment index and F-actin cup formation should not be markedly reduced in mock APOE4 despite lower MYH9/ACTB/FAM49B/MYO1F/VASP transcripts; a clear reduction in engulfment index with normal lipid-droplet load would favour a cytoskeletal/engulfment-machinery mechanism over the lipid-routing mechanism.", "Because uptake receptors and hydrolase transcripts are up, an acute myelin or apoptotic-neuron challenge should reveal APOE4-specific accumulation of undigested lipid and blunted further induction of the CLEAR module; if APOE4 instead clears the challenge as well as APOE3 and induces CLEAR normally, the predicted reserve deficit is absent."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, unmeasured): APOE4 apolipoprotein handling in the mock microglia-astrocyte co-culture delivers cholesterol/phospholipid to microglia in a form whose sterol is less efficiently returned to the ER-accessible regulatory pool than with APOE3 (APOE transcript itself is only modestly higher, gene:APOE +1.24).", "Step 2 (measured RNA): Sterol sensing therefore stays in the 'low ER sterol' output mode - SREBP factors and their targets are uniformly higher (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:ACSS2), raising both de novo synthesis and lipoprotein-uptake capacity.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): In parallel the surface acquisition program is coherently higher across receptor families (gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:SCARF1, gene:STAB1, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:PROS1, gene:MFGE8, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:ITGB1, gene:ITGB5, gene:ITGA6, gene:ANXA1), increasing the capacity to bind lipid-rich and apoptotic cargo (binding/engulfment rate itself was not measured).", "Step 4 (measured RNA): Cargo routing and degradative compartment capacity expand together - endosome/retromer/ESCRT/late-endosome transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:AP5M1, gene:RAB28) and a TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal module (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP1) are the largest-magnitude coherent programs in the list.", "Step 5 (inferred flux, measured only as RNA): Sterol and fatty acid emerging from this expanded lysosomal route are re-esterified and stored rather than suppressing SREBP - gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD, gene:SCP2, gene:FABP5, gene:FABP3 up, with lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid catabolism (gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH) feeding the same lipid pool; the ER-accessible pool therefore stays low and Steps 2-4 are sustained (a futile storage cycle rather than a corrected deficit).", "Step 6 (measured RNA): The state is energetically oxidative rather than inflammatory-glycolytic (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:UQCRC2, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFB2, gene:COX6B1, gene:ATP5F1B up; gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1 down), consistent with lipid substrate handling and with a DAM-like but non-glycolytic profile (gene:TREM2, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB, gene:FTH1, gene:CD74 up).", "Step 7 (predicted consequence, prospective): The stored/esterified lipid load and the sustained sterol-hungry sensing state reduce the reserve available for a subsequent lipid or myelin challenge; in the supplied mock condition this predicts increased neutral-lipid droplets and lysosomal volume, not necessarily any ongoing clearance failure."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a sterol-unsatisfied scavenger-lysosomal state that routes acquired lipid into esterified/neutral-lipid storage instead of the ER-accessible sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27947420891334046, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2493446391599673, "cosine_similarity": 0.38771206782093204, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897540453074434, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27947420891334046, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2493446391599673, "cosine_similarity": 0.38771206782093204, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5897540453074434, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.72674025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 27}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_179", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77.1% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are made relative to this biased background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and the log base is left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein amount and, less securely, for enzymatic activity, sterol transfer rate, organelle localization and flux; none of these were measured here.", "No lipid, sterol, filipin, lysosomal pH, or degradation-rate measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier mentioning lipid, so the central bottleneck (lysosome-to-ER cholesterol handoff) is inferred from the joint direction of SREBP-2 and CLEAR-type transcripts, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-identified; they neither confirm nor cleanly refute the lysosomal arm (e.g. protein_spot:052 up, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:058 down, all containing cathepsin candidates).", "Key pathway members are absent from the supplied list (NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, HMGCR, SQLE, MCOLN1, PLIN2, LAMP2), so absence of change cannot be asserted; one row has an unresolved symbol (gene:??).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous (APOE from astrocytes); single-cell composition or ambient-RNA differences could contribute to the global positive shift.", "Pathway membership assignments are from unverified background knowledge (no literature or database retrieval was permitted); the isogenic design is taken from the supplied metadata.", "The Agent tool was not available in this session; no independent reviewer was simulated."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step is not lipid capture or hydrolase supply but the egress of endolysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER: transcript data show coordinate up-regulation of lipid-scavenging receptors, of the TFEB/MITF CLEAR-type hydrolase and v-ATPase program, and of SREBP-2 sterol-synthesis targets simultaneously, a combination expected only if ER-accessible cholesterol stays low while lysosomal lipid load rises, with excess carbon diverted to SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification rather than to the ER regulatory pool. Actomyosin internalization effectors are transcriptionally reduced and are proposed as a secondary brake, not the primary lesion; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol sequestration in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or by re-expressing an ER-endosome sterol-transfer route) should, within 24-48 h, lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels AND lower TFEB-target hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB) and lysosomal filipin signal. If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated after lysosomal sterol is demonstrably released, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Ordering test: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program without normalizing SREBP-2 targets. If TFEB knockdown also normalizes SREBP-2 targets to APOE3 levels, the lysosomal program is upstream of the sterol-sensing difference and the mechanism as ordered is weakened.", "Storage-arm test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should increase free cholesterol reaching the ER and suppress SREBP-2 targets in APOE4 more than in APOE3, without increasing hydrolase transcripts. No genotype-selective suppression would weaken Step 4.", "Uptake-versus-egress test: blocking actomyosin-dependent internalization (blebbistatin or MYH9 knockdown) should NOT normalize the lysosomal or SREBP-2 transcript programs if internalization is a secondary brake. If blocking internalization normalizes both programs, the bottleneck is at uptake and this hypothesis is falsified in favour of a phagocytic/cytoskeletal mechanism.", "Direct falsifier: quantitative lipidomics or filipin/ER-accessible-cholesterol biosensor showing equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol and equal ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock conditions would refute the core claim.", "Protein-level check: targeted immunoblot for cathepsin B/D, GBA and ATP6V1A should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 protein. Uniformly unchanged or reduced hydrolase protein despite elevated transcripts would weaken Step 2 and favour a purely transcriptional or translationally uncoupled explanation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_179", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein capture (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7), which we infer increases delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system; no uptake flux or lipid pool was measured.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred transcriptional activity): TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) together with a coherent lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:SLC38A7), consistent with compensatory lysosomal biogenesis rather than with met demand.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): despite increased capture and hydrolase transcripts, cholesterol released in the lysosome is inefficiently transferred to the ER; ER sterol sensing therefore behaves as sterol-poor and sustains SREBP-2 output (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2). Reduced gene:OSBPL8 is consistent with weakened ER-endosome lipid transfer capacity; localization and transfer rate are not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): carbon that does reach the cytosol is routed to storage and de novo lipogenesis rather than to the regulatory ER pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:MGLL, gene:SCP2), which further isolates cholesterol from ER feedback and sustains the loop of Step 3.", "Step 5 (consequence, inferred organelle state): persistent luminal lipid load stresses the lysosomal compartment, indicated by elevated gene:LGALS3 and gene:FTH1; galectin-3 puncta, membrane permeabilization and iron handling were not measured, so this step is inference from abundance only.", "Step 6 (secondary brake, not the bottleneck): actomyosin internalization effectors are transcriptionally reduced against a strongly up-shifted background (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, with gene:ARHGDIA +10.61), which we propose limits further particle internalization downstream of the lipid-handling defect; the broader phagocytic/cytoskeletal gene set is not enriched relative to the list background, so this is offered as a modifier rather than the primary mechanism."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at lysosome-to-ER sterol handoff, driving coupled TFEB/MITF lysosomal expansion and SREBP-2 activation with esterified lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917265766683008, "cosine_similarity": 0.38732649462729735, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_179", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5931456310679613, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917265766683008, "cosine_similarity": 0.38732649462729735, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5931456310679613, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.50292725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 128}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; two side-by-side workbook blocks of 1705 higher-in-APOE4 and 507 lower-in-APOE4 entries). Program sign patterns were therefore compared against a 77.1% positive background, not 50/50. Genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes above about |4| are used only for sign and coherence, not as quantitative fold changes.", "Measured transcript abundance is assumed to track, but does not demonstrate, protein amount, enzymatic activity or metabolic flux. SREBP proteolytic cleavage, TFEB nuclear localization, mTORC1 status, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, cholesterol esterification rate and lipid-droplet content were not measured here.", "The proposed low ER-accessible sterol pool is an inference from coordinated SREBP-target transcript elevation; the pool itself was not measured and no lipid measurements were supplied.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (keratin/actin dominated) and quantized fold changes; no spot is assigned to a single protein. Spots are used only for compatibility testing, never as confirmation of an individual protein.", "Program membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway rosters using unverified background knowledge, fixed before signs were examined; all represented members, including opposite-direction exceptions, are reported. Descriptive coherence across non-independent, co-regulated genes is not a formal enrichment result.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply that itself differs by APOE genotype could contribute to the microglial lipid load; the supplied data cannot separate cell-autonomous from co-culture-driven effects.", "Effects described are those expected in the supplied mock condition. Any reduced handling reserve would only be revealed by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge and is not claimed as an ongoing defect here.", "No causal direction is established: SREBP-module elevation and lysosomal-module elevation are concurrent, and the data cannot determine which is upstream."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 not by a canonical unfolded-protein response but by a coordinated lipid-routing cell state: transcripts for lipid uptake and for ER-membrane esterification/storage enzymes are higher, the full SREBP sterol/fatty-acid synthesis module is uniformly higher (13/13 represented members positive), mitochondrial citrate-export and oxidative transcripts are higher while glycolytic commitment transcripts are lower, and a CLEAR/TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis plus mannose-6-phosphate hydrolase-routing module is higher. We propose that APOE4-dependent routing of sterol into esterified/stored and endolysosomal pools keeps the ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol pool low, so SREBP-target transcription remains constitutively engaged and feeds forward into further lipid storage, with lysosomal biogenesis expanded to handle the increased lipid load. This is a coordinated altered-routing/cell-state change; the supplied RNA and protein-spot data do not measure flux and do not establish that degradative capacity is failing in the mock condition, nor that the pathway is causal.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: direct measurement of the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (e.g. ALOD4/perfringolysin-O domain-4 probe or ER-targeted sterol sensor) in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a LOWER accessible ER pool in APOE4 despite equal or greater total/esterified cellular cholesterol. If APOE4 shows equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol while SREBP targets remain elevated, the routing-and-sensing core of this mechanism is wrong.", "Prospective: ACAT/SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should deplete cholesteryl ester, refill the ER regulatory pool and reduce the sterol-synthesis transcript module (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels. Persistent elevation of those transcripts after confirmed cholesteryl-ester depletion would weaken the feed-forward step.", "Prospective: SREBP-pathway blockade (fatostatin, or SCAP/MBTPS1 knockdown) should reduce the sterol/fatty-acid synthesis transcripts and neutral-lipid storage in APOE4 more than in APOE3, and should partially reduce the lysosomal module if lipid load drives it. If the lysosomal module (TFEB, ATP6V1A, GBA, HEXA, CTSD) is unchanged by SREBP blockade, lysosomal biogenesis is an independent arm rather than a downstream consequence.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and increase stored neutral lipid selectively in APOE4. If the lysosomal transcripts are TFEB-independent in these cells, step 5 is weakened.", "Prospective, distinguishing this mechanism from the ER-stress alternative: ISRIB or a PERK inhibitor, and separately IRE1 RNase inhibition, should NOT normalize the sterol-synthesis or lysosomal transcript modules under mock conditions, and quantitative immunoblot should show no increase in BiP/HSPA5 or GRP94/HSP90B1 protein in APOE4. Detection of increased BiP/GRP94 protein, XBP1 splicing, or normalization of the lipid modules by UPR inhibition would favor an unfolded-protein-response mechanism instead.", "Prospective, future challenge only (reserve, not an ongoing defect): after a myelin-debris, apoptotic-neuron or oxidized-LDL load, APOE4 microglia should show greater neutral-lipid accumulation and slower cargo clearance than APOE3 despite their higher lysosomal transcript module. Equal or faster clearance would indicate successful adaptation with adequate throughput rather than a storage-biased state, and would argue against interpreting the coordinated modules as a lipid-handling liability."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters ApoE-dependent lipid handling in microglia: APOE transcript itself is higher (gene:APOE +1.24, adj p 6.9e-223) together with lipid-uptake and lipoprotein-receptor transcripts (gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:NPC2 +1.17). Inferred, not measured: increased lipid influx/handling load.", "Sterol and fatty acid are routed at the ER membrane into esterified and stored forms rather than into the free ER regulatory pool: gene:SOAT1 +1.25 (cholesteryl-ester synthesis), gene:DGAT1 +1.72 (triacylglycerol synthesis), gene:FABP5 +1.13, gene:CH25H +1.62; a parallel share is routed into the endolysosomal system. Inferred, not measured: the size of the ER-accessible sterol pool and actual lipid-droplet content.", "Because the ER sterol sensor reads a low regulatory pool, SREBP-target transcription stays engaged: every represented member of the sterol/fatty-acid synthesis module is positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93; 13/13 positive versus a 77.1% positive selected-list background, binomial p=0.034). Inferred, not measured: SREBP cleavage and nuclear occupancy.", "Carbon for this synthesis is biased toward mitochondrial citrate export and away from glycolytic commitment: gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54 (12/12 represented members positive, p=0.044), while gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32 are lower despite higher transporters gene:SLC2A1 +2.37 and gene:SLC2A3 +3.73.", "Stored and delivered lipid loads the endolysosomal system, and a coordinated CLEAR/TFEB-type biogenesis program is higher (30/33 represented members positive, p=0.037): gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70; hydrolases gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65. Inferred, not measured: lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity and degradative flux.", "Delivery of that hydrolase cargo requires secretory-route capacity, and the corresponding transcripts are higher: N-glycosylation/oligosaccharyltransferase and glycoprotein quality control (gene:STT3A +3.39, gene:DDOST +6.22, gene:MLEC +10.21, gene:UGGT1 +2.58, gene:RPN1 +1.06, gene:STT3B +1.40), mannose-6-phosphate tagging and receptor (gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02), and anterograde coat components (gene:COPA +4.27, gene:COPB1 +1.04). This is increased biosynthetic routing capacity, not a canonical UPR: classical ER-chaperone output transcripts are absent from the selected list and ERAD components are lower (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:SEC62 -1.50), while ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are not increased (protein_spot:005 -0.14, protein_spot:004 -0.68, protein_spot:001 -0.49; all non-significant).", "The net result is a self-reinforcing lipid-storage microglial state with disease/lipid-associated surface and secreted markers higher (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:TIMP2 +1.65, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:C1QB +1.13, gene:C1QC +1.17, gene:ANXA1 +4.15; 11/11 represented members positive, p=0.057), rather than an acute stress or inflammatory-cytokine response."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a sterol-storage cell state: lipid routed to esterified and endolysosomal pools keeps the ER regulatory sterol pool low, driving feed-forward SREBP lipogenesis and TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.248975208780278, "cosine_similarity": 0.3861467144564434, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5933559870550162, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.248975208780278, "cosine_similarity": 0.3861467144564434, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5933559870550162, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.896144, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 28}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_089", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every adjusted p-value is \u003c0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median about +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); all set-level claims are therefore made as ranks relative to that internal background, not as absolute up/down calls, and the log base is left unconverted.", "Transcript-level differences in the RAC2/DOCK8/MYH9 module are assumed to change the corresponding protein and GTPase activity levels; no Rac-GTP, F-actin, phospho-myosin or protein-level measurement of these specific proteins is present in the data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes and cannot be uniquely assigned; keratin- and ACTB-containing spots are treated as potentially contaminated, and spot-level statements are used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Phagocytic rate, macropinocytosis, cargo flux, lysosomal lipid content, cholesteryl esters and lipid droplets are unmeasured here and are inferred, not observed.", "The APOE4 and APOE3 lines are isogenic as stated in the metadata, and the co-cultured astrocytes contribute equally in both genotypes; replicate number is not supplied, so effect precision cannot be assessed.", "Microglial identity is assumed preserved (CSF1R, SYK, TREM2, C1Q, MPEG1 all at or above background), so the module down-shift is interpreted as an effector-repertoire change rather than loss of myeloid identity."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a selective, coordinated reduction of haematopoietic-restricted actin regulators and motors (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, PLEK, FAM49B/CYRI-B, MYO1F, MYH9, ACTB) while ubiquitously expressed cytoskeletal paralogues (ARHGDIA, ARHGAP1, ARHGAP35, RHOA, MYO1D, ACTN4, ARPC1B/4/5) and endolysosomal hydrolase transcripts are at or above the strong global positive RNA shift. We propose that this repertoire switch, not loss of Arp2/3 subunits or of microglial identity, is the primary bottleneck: it is predicted to lower Rac-GTP-driven branched-actin polymerisation and MYH9 actomyosin contractility at nascent phagocytic/macropinocytic cups, so that bulk actin-dependent internalisation of particulate lipid-rich cargo becomes rate-limiting, and the cell instead sustains its lipid pools through SREBP-driven synthesis (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LSS), receptor/scavenger uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36) and esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1) while an expanded hydrolase transcript programme (TFEB, CTSB, CTSK, HEXA, GBA) is not matched by increased mature cathepsin spot abundance. Causality is not established by these data; all activity, flux, localisation and directionality statements are inferences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring RAC2 (or DOCK8, or expressing a constitutively active/photoactivatable Rac) in APOE4 microglia should raise the phagocytic index for large particulate cargo (beads, myelin, synaptosomes) and pHrodo-labelled cargo toward APOE3 levels, and should lower SREBF1/SCD transcripts, without appreciably changing ARPC1B/ARPC4/ARPC5 levels. If Rac restoration leaves internalisation of large cargo unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Reciprocal phenocopy: partial myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or MYH9 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 internalisation deficit and the shift toward synthesis/esterification transcripts. Failure to phenocopy weakens the contractility arm.", "Route specificity: cargo delivered by an actin-independent soluble route (AcLDL/LDL, liposomes) should load lysosomal lipid similarly in APOE4 and APOE3, whereas particulate myelin loading should be lower in APOE4. Equal deficits for both routes would point to a downstream lysosomal defect instead.", "Capacity mismatch: mature cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase protein levels and lysosomal proteolytic activity (DQ-BSA) should not be increased in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; an increase in measured degradative activity proportional to the transcript rise would weaken step 5.", "Falsifier for the whole mechanism: if live imaging at matched surface-receptor levels shows APOE4 microglia forming cups and internalising particles at rates equal to or greater than APOE3, with unchanged Rac-GTP pulldown and unchanged cup F-actin, the mechanism is refuted regardless of the transcript pattern.", "Specificity control: single-cell or bulk re-measurement should confirm that ubiquitous paralogues (ARHGDIA, ARHGAP1/35, MYO1D) are higher while haematopoietic paralogues (RAC2, ARHGDIB, MYO1F) are lower in the same cells; if instead the whole Rho/actin family moves down together, the repertoire-switch framing is wrong and a general transcriptional or maturation-state explanation is favoured."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 selectively lowers transcripts of the haematopoietic-restricted actin/Rho module (gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:ARHGDIB, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:PLEK, gene:FAM49B, gene:MYO1F, gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB) against a background in which the median selected gene is strongly up, whereas ubiquitous paralogues (gene:ARHGDIA, gene:ARHGAP1, gene:ARHGAP35, gene:RHOA, gene:MYO1D, gene:ACTN4) and Arp2/3 subunits (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5) are at or above that background; this is a repertoire switch, not a global cytoskeletal shutdown.", "Step 2 (inferred activity): reduced RAC2 with reduced DOCK8 (Rac GEF) and reduced FAM49B/CYRI-B and ARHGAP30 (Rac-pathway modulators) is predicted to lower the amount and spatial focusing of Rac-GTP at the plasma membrane; the Arp2/3 complex remains available (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC5; protein_spot:081, protein_spot:082, protein_spot:061, protein_spot:063 not reduced) but is inferred to be under-activated. Rac-GTP and F-actin were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred contractility): reduced MYH9 transcript, weakly echoed by two MYH9/SWAP70-candidate spots that are lower in APOE4 (protein_spot:010, protein_spot:011, both non-significant), is predicted to lower actomyosin tension required for phagocytic cup closure and scission.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, inferred flux): actin- and contractility-dependent internalisation of large particulate, lipid-rich cargo (myelin/debris-like) becomes the rate-limiting step for delivery of exogenous lipid to the endolysosome in APOE4 microglia; internalisation rate and cargo flux were not measured here.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred mismatch): the degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:RAB7A) yet cathepsin-candidate protein spots are not increased and several are decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069), so increased hydrolase message is inferred not to translate into increased degradative capacity per delivered cargo.", "Step 6 (lipid consequence, inferred): with exogenous particulate lipid input constrained, sterol/fatty-acid sensing remains permissive and the cell fills lipid pools through de novo lipogenesis and non-actin-dependent uptake (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36) and stores them as esters (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), producing the APOE4-specific lipid phenotype; the lipid pools themselves were not measured in this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia swap the myeloid-restricted RAC2/DOCK8-MYH9 actin effector repertoire for a ubiquitous one, making actin-dependent internalisation the bottleneck and pushing lipid supply toward synthesis and scavenger uptake"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2586303389657732, "cosine_similarity": 0.38609069591847983, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5848834951456311, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2586303389657732, "cosine_similarity": 0.38609069591847983, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5848834951456311, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.11415975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 129}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_045", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base; all statements are made on the reported scale and are rank-normalised against the list's own strongly positive median (+1.46) rather than treated as absolute fold changes.", "The global positive RNA shift is partly technical (selection, normalisation or composition in 10X Flex data); therefore only sets that are enriched by rank against that background are treated as signal.", "Each 2D protein spot contains several candidate genes and keratin/actin contaminants, so spot changes are treated as ambiguous evidence about spot-form redistribution, never as identified-protein abundance.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a weak proxy for enzyme activity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase localization and lipid content were not measured in this dataset.", "Causality is not established: APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences here are correlative, isogenic-background associations at a single day-30 timepoint with unreported replicate numbers.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts could derive from non-microglial cells if demultiplexing was imperfect."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the differentiating lesion is not ER proteostasis but a post-transcriptional bottleneck in delivering and maturing acid hydrolases at the endolysosome: TFEB-type hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and lipid-uptake/esterification transcripts rise well above the strong global RNA up-shift, while transcripts for M6P-receptor and TGN/endosome SNARE machinery are among the most down-ranked genes and cathepsin-containing 2D protein-spot trains redistribute in opposite directions instead of increasing coherently; we infer (not measure) that hydrolytic capacity per lysosome lags substrate delivery, so sphingolipid and lipoprotein-derived lipid accumulate in the endolysosomal compartment and are shunted into esterified storage.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Enzyme-activity assay: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, mature cathepsin B/D, GBA and HEXA specific activities (per LAMP1 signal) will rise much less than their transcripts (predicted \u003c1.5-fold despite \u003e4-fold transcript differences for gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA). If activities scale roughly with transcript increases, the maturation/delivery bottleneck is falsified.", "Pulse-chase maturation: APOE4 cells will show a higher fraction of pro-cathepsin D secreted into the medium and slower conversion to the mature heavy chain than APOE3; identical maturation kinetics and secretion fractions would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating rescue: supplying mature hydrolase bypassing biosynthetic sorting (uptake of recombinant GBA or cathepsin D, or re-expression of M6PR/STX16) will reduce endolysosomal lipid load (BODIPY-lactosylceramide clearance, filipin, LipidSpot) in APOE4 without first reducing TFEB-target transcripts; no reduction in lipid load under restored hydrolase delivery would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating against the ER/UPR alternative: ISRIB, 4-PBA or ATF6 knockdown will not normalise APOE4 lysosomal lipid accumulation or hydrolase maturation; if these ER-directed manipulations do normalise the phenotype, an ER proteostasis mechanism should replace this one.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown will worsen, not improve, APOE4 lipid accumulation, confirming the transcriptional program is a response rather than the driver; improvement after TFEB knockdown would falsify the compensatory framing.", "Acidification control: lysosomal pH (LysoSensor ratiometric) will be similar or slightly lower in APOE4 despite higher v-ATPase transcripts; a markedly alkalinised APOE4 lysosome would move the bottleneck from hydrolase delivery to acidification and weaken step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated lysosomal/CLEAR-type transcript increase that exceeds the global up-shift of this selected DE list (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSD at rank percentiles 0.69-0.99 versus a median-centred background), together with v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C); we infer, but did not measure, increased lysosomal biogenesis signalling.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): lipid-entry and lipid-esterification transcripts are also high (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1), from which we infer increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosome and increased capacity to esterify sterol/fatty acid into storage lipid.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): transcripts for the trans-Golgi-to-endosome hydrolase sorting and fusion machinery are strongly down-ranked against that same up-shifted background (gene:M6PR 0.15, gene:STX16 0.03, gene:GOSR1 0.05, gene:VAMP2 0.13, gene:STX17 0.12); we infer reduced mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery and reduced autophagosome-lysosome fusion, an activity/localization claim that was not directly measured.", "Step 4 (measured protein spots): cathepsin-containing spot trains do not scale with their transcripts; some spots rise (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057) while others fall significantly (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:068). Because each spot carries several candidate genes, this is read only as redistribution among charge/size forms rather than a coherent increase in mature hydrolase, consistent with a maturation/processing constraint.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): hydrolytic flux per lysosome fails to match substrate influx, so glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and cholesteryl-ester substrates accumulate in the endolysosome and in cytoplasmic droplets; no lipid species were measured in this dataset, so this is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 6 (inferred feedback): the undigested luminal load sustains the lysosomal transcriptional program and the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 esterification program, giving a self-reinforcing storage state; the incoherent ER-stress transcripts (gene:ATF6 and gene:DDIT3 up, but gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:PDIA3, gene:SEC24D down and BiP/GRP94-containing spots unchanged) indicate the load is distal to the ER folding compartment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand the lysosomal transcriptional program but are bottlenecked at TGN-to-endolysosome hydrolase delivery/maturation, limiting lipid catabolic flux"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1268507920097478, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18045044246234132, "cosine_similarity": 0.3856749190467084, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6155339805825243, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1268507920097478, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18045044246234132, "cosine_similarity": 0.3856749190467084, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6155339805825243, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7593795, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 130}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_083", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set comparisons are made against the internal background of this list (median +1.46) rather than a genome-wide null.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; the very large magnitudes (up to +15.5) suggest a low-replicate pseudobulk contrast, so effects are interpreted as ranks rather than calibrated ratios.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with delay, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal proteins; no lysosomal protein, protease activity, pH, cargo-clearance rate, autophagic flux or lipid species was measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; no spot is assumed to identify a unique protein, and spot changes are used only as ambiguous corroboration.", "CTSS is assumed to be a quantitatively dominant contributor to terminal endolysosomal proteolysis in these microglia; the bottleneck claim leans on this single transcript together with STX17 and M6PR.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so cargo supply, lipid transfer and any genotype effect on astrocytes are uncontrolled confounders of the microglial state.", "The global positive shift of the list may partly reflect normalisation or cell-composition differences between genotypes; only relative within-list enrichment is interpreted."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated, above-background increase in transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and MiT/TFE factors (TFEB, MITF), set against a selective collapse of the dominant microglial endolysosomal protease transcript CTSS and of the sorting and fusion factors M6PR and STX17. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is terminal proteolytic clearance of internalised cargo in the late endosome/lysosome, not hydrolase gene supply or acidification: the transcriptional expansion is a demand-driven (compensatory) response to cargo that is delivered and acidified but incompletely degraded, so lipid liberated from retained cargo is re-esterified (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1, SCD transcripts up) instead of cleared. All measurements are steady-state abundances; degradative flux, lysosomal pH, protease activity and lipid pools were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, pulse-chase of protein-containing cargo (DQ-BSA or DQ-ovalbumin dequenching, or labelled apoptotic-cell/myelin debris) normalised per LAMP1-positive lysosomal volume should show a LOWER degradation rate per unit lysosomal volume in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. Equal or faster cargo degradation per lysosomal volume in APOE4 falsifies the proteolysis-bottleneck mechanism.", "Acidification control: ratiometric lysosomal pH (LysoSensor or pHrodo-dextran) should be equal or lower (more acidic) in APOE4, consistent with all v-ATPase rows being positive. Significantly less acidic APOE4 lysosomes would place the bottleneck at acidification and weaken this mechanism.", "Node test: restoring CTSS expression, or supplying an equivalent cysteine-protease activity, in APOE4 microglia should raise cargo proteolysis and lower the elevated hydrolase and MiT/TFE-target transcripts toward APOE3 levels. No change in either readout refutes the CTSS-centred step.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown should reduce hydrolase transcripts and worsen cargo retention and neutral-lipid load more in APOE4 than APOE3. If TFEB knockdown instead relieves cargo retention, the compensatory reading of the CLEAR-like signature is wrong.", "Downstream lipid test: APOE4 microglia should hold more undegraded internalised cargo and more neutral lipid/cholesteryl ester per cell, and SOAT1 inhibition should shift lipid from esters to free sterol without correcting the cargo degradation rate. Absence of lipid accumulation, or correction of degradation rate by SOAT1 inhibition, weakens the flux-mismatch chain.", "Specificity test: mild acute cathepsin inhibition in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 transcript pattern (raised hydrolase and MiT/TFE-target transcripts with retained cargo); failure to reproduce it argues the signature is not downstream of a proteolysis deficit."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: within a selected, globally up-shifted RNA list (2212 rows, median log fold change +1.46, 77 percent positive), luminal acid-hydrolase transcripts are raised disproportionately above that internal background (set median +2.40, Mann-Whitney BH p=0.016), with extreme members GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB and DPP7 plus HEXB, GLA, SGSH, MAN2B1 and DNASE2; TFEB (+2.38) and MITF (+1.03) are up and every detected v-ATPase row (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1E1 and four others) is positive, as are LAMP1, SCARB2, TMEM192, IGF2R, GNPTG and RAB7A.", "Inferred (not measured): these coordinated transcript changes reflect MiT/TFE-associated CLEAR-network activation and an enlarged lysosomal compartment in APOE4; transcript abundance is treated as a demand signal, not as evidence of increased hydrolytic activity, localisation or flux.", "Measured counter-current within the same up-shifted list: CTSS sits at the 0.8th percentile (-5.57) while M6PR (-1.72), STX17 (-2.06) and IDS (-1.56) also fall. Inferred: loss of the principal microglial cysteine protease, together with reduced CD-MPR-dependent hydrolase sorting and reduced autophagosome/amphisome-to-lysosome fusion, prevents the transcriptional expansion from being converted into proportional terminal cargo proteolysis. This mismatch is the proposed primary bottleneck.", "Inferred: protein-containing cargo (lipoprotein particles, membranes and apoptotic-cell debris that microglia ingest continuously, including from co-cultured astrocytes) is retained in acidified late endosomes/lysosomes in a partially degraded state, sustaining the TFEB/hydrolase transcriptional signal as feedback rather than resolving the load. Increased uptake is unlikely to be the driver: uptake and phagocytic receptor transcripts (TREM2, MERTK, MRC1, CD36, SCARB1) are positive but statistically indistinguishable from the global shift (set median +1.38, p=0.83).", "Inferred metabolic consequence, supported only by transcripts: lipid liberated from retained cargo is re-esterified and stored rather than exported, consistent with SOAT1 (+1.25), DGAT1 (+1.72), SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), ABCA7 (+2.14) and APOE (+1.24). No lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Ambiguous protein-level correlate: 2D-gel spots whose candidate lists include CTSD or CTSB change in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) and the two spots listing ATP6V1E1 fall (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93). Inferred: redistribution among processed or charge forms rather than a net abundance change; spots carry several candidate genes each and cannot identify a specific protease, so this is compatible with, but does not demonstrate, altered cathepsin maturation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an expanded but proteolysis-limited endolysosome: CLEAR-like hydrolase/acidification transcription rises while CTSS-dependent terminal cargo proteolysis and STX17-dependent fusion fall"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2487274862614883, "cosine_similarity": 0.3856591481063792, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936181229773463, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2487274862614883, "cosine_similarity": 0.3856591481063792, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936181229773463, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9696715, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 131}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_013", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; all RNA effects are used only as monotonic, same-scale directional quantities, never converted to a linear fold change.", "The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, no values between -1 and +1), so absence of a gene is not evidence of no change, and all enrichment statements are made relative to this already up-shifted background (77.1% of rows positive, median +1.46), not to a whole transcriptome.", "The global positive shift is assumed to be at least partly biological rather than entirely a library-size/ambient-RNA normalisation artefact; if it is purely technical, the apparent nuclear-up / mtDNA-down contrast could instead reflect a shift in mitochondrial read fraction between genotypes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for subunit availability; assembled complex amount, respiratory flux, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass and lipid pools were not measured here and are inferred only.", "The 92 protein spots each carry several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are therefore not used as evidence for any mitochondrial, lysosomal or v-ATPase protein pool, and their fold changes are on a stated log2 scale from a different assay than the RNA.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of the genotype effect may be mediated by astrocyte-derived signals or by ambient/cross-cell contamination rather than being microglia-autonomous.", "Background pathway-membership assignments used to build the gene sets are unverified prior knowledge (no literature or database retrieval was performed)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (39/39 detected OXPHOS structural subunits, TCA/anaplerotic enzymes, SLC25 carriers, TOM/TIM import machinery) while mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits of complexes I, III, IV and V are lower. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, so the amplified nuclear program cannot be converted into proportionally more assembled, coupled respiratory chain; the resulting demand/supply mismatch drives compensatory anaplerotic substrate delivery, matrix redox defence, a stress-response arm and citrate-fuelled lipogenic/sterol gene induction. Lysosomal-capacity failure is explicitly rejected as the primary bottleneck because the measured endolysosomal degradative program is up, not down, and is not separable from the global positive RNA shift.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: In APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia, blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling will show reduced fully assembled complex I, III, IV and V holoenzyme with an increased ratio of free or sub-assembled nuclear-encoded subunits (e.g. NDUFS/NDUFA modules, ATP5F1 F1 head) to holoenzyme, while total nuclear-encoded subunit protein is equal or higher. If assembled holoenzyme levels and the free-subunit ratio are unchanged, the assembly-bottleneck step is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING: Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial content will show reduced maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) oxygen consumption and reduced spare respiratory capacity per unit citrate-synthase activity or per mtDNA copy in APOE4, together with equal or increased citrate synthase activity. Equal or higher OCR/CS ratio in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "RESCUE: Increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or POLRMT/TFB2M overexpression, or allotopic/mitochondrially targeted expression of MT-ATP6 and MT-ND4) should raise assembled complex levels and maximal OCR and should blunt the nuclear OXPHOS transcript overshoot and the PRDX3/DDIT3 stress signature. Failure of such rescue to raise assembled complex or OCR would falsify the causal direction proposed here.", "DIRECTIONALITY: Suppressing the compensatory anaplerotic arm (glutaminase inhibition, or MPC inhibition with UK5099) should reduce the PRDX3/GPX4 and DDIT3 stress-transcript elevation in APOE4 without normalising the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit; if instead MPC or GLS inhibition restores MT-ATP6/MT-CYB levels, the proposed upstream ordering is wrong.", "COUNTER-TEST OF THE REJECTED FOCUS: Functional endolysosomal assays (DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin B activity, LysoTracker intensity, pHrodo bead degradation) should show equal or higher lysosomal degradative activity in APOE4 at day 30 mock. If APOE4 instead shows clearly reduced cathepsin activity, raised lysosomal pH and accumulated undegraded cargo before any respiratory deficit appears, then the endolysosomal-capacity mechanism should replace this hypothesis.", "LIPID BRANCH: Inhibiting citrate export (SLC25A1/CIC inhibition) or ACLY should selectively reduce neutral-lipid droplet content and SREBF1 target expression in APOE4 relative to APOE3. No genotype-selective effect would weaken step 5 while leaving steps 1-4 intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA abundance): APOE4 microglia carry a coordinated upregulation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - every detected OXPHOS structural subunit (e.g. NDUFA5 +7.34, NDUFS7 +5.68, ATP5ME +5.20, UQCRC2 +4.02, COX7A2 +3.39, CYCS +2.57), TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (OGDH +8.56, MDH1 +8.72, MPC2 +7.98, GOT1, DLD, ACO2, GLUD1, GLS), inner-membrane carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5) and protein-import components (TOMM22 +4.63, TIMM44, TIMM8B, OXA1L, TUFM). INFERRED: this represents increased demand for mitochondrial biogenesis, not proven increased respiration.", "MEASURED (RNA abundance): in the same comparison, 4 of 6 detected mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are up), and two mtDNA-maintenance transcripts (MGME1, TOP1MT) are down. Nuclear vs mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS medians differ (+2.64 vs -1.56). INFERRED: mitochondrial gene-expression output does not scale with the nuclear program.", "INFERRED (assembly, not measured): because MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ATP6 are obligate catalytic/core components of complexes I, III, IV and V, their relative shortfall makes holoenzyme assembly the bottleneck; imported nuclear-encoded subunits accumulate as unassembled or sub-complex modules rather than increasing coupled electron transport.", "INFERRED (flux/ROS): with electron transport and ATP-synthase capacity capped but substrate delivery raised (MPC2, SLC25A1/A11, GLS/GLUD1/GOT1), electron pressure and matrix oxidant load rise, consistent with the measured increase in matrix/peroxide-handling transcripts (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5, GPX4) and with the measured stress-arm transcripts (DDIT3 +2.79, ATF6, EIF2AK3).", "INFERRED (metabolic re-routing): acetyl-CoA/citrate that cannot be fully oxidised is exported (SLC25A1 up) and used for lipid and sterol synthesis, consistent with the measured induction of SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LDLR, ACAT2 and INSIG1 - the weakest link in the chain, since this set is not statistically separable from the global RNA shift.", "INFERRED (cell-state consequence): APOE4 microglia therefore occupy a high-biogenesis / low-assembled-capacity state with lipid-biased carbon disposal, rather than a state of failed lysosomal degradation; the coordinated rise in lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB transcripts (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, ATP6V1H +6.88, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, TFEB +2.38, LAMP1) is interpreted as accompanying biogenesis/compensation, not as the primary lesion."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit supply is the bottleneck limiting oxidative capacity in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0958904109589041, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24926692467431819, "cosine_similarity": 0.38563816995043654, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5950097087378641, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0958904109589041, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24926692467431819, "cosine_similarity": 0.38563816995043654, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5950097087378641, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2910195, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 132}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1) with a strong global positive shift (77% positive, median +1.46), so all enrichment statements are made relative to that biased background and not to a whole transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes are therefore not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no protein, metabolite, flux, mitochondrial-mass, mtDNA-copy-number or lipid measurement is supplied, so all activity, localization and directionality statements in the mechanism are inferences.", "The mtDNA-encoded arm rests on only six transcripts, two of which move upward (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L); probe-based 10X Flex capture of mitochondrial transcripts may be incomplete, so the mitonuclear mismatch step is the weakest measured link and is stated as inference.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as ambiguous corroboration, never as evidence for a named protein pool.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts and spots may derive from, or be influenced by, the non-microglial compartment or ambient RNA; genotype effects are assumed to be microglia-intrinsic, which is untested here.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at one timepoint (Day 30); replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size stability cannot be assessed and no causal direction is claimed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a metabolic re-routing rather than by a phagocytic/cytoskeletal program: nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain and TCA transcripts are coordinately higher while the measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower, a stoichiometric mismatch that we infer limits assembled respiratory-complex capacity; with pyruvate entry (MPC2) and TCA transcripts high, we infer that carbon overflows as citrate through SLC25A1 into cytosolic acetyl-CoA and is committed by an SREBF1-associated esterification program (SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1) to triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage, with elevated endolysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts as an accompanying degradative response. Causality is not established by these data; the RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift, and no lipid, flux, or ETC-assembly measurement is supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Respirometry normalized to mitochondrial mass (citrate-synthase activity or MitoTracker-independent mtDNA copy number) should show lower maximal/FCCP-uncoupled oxygen consumption and lower assembled complex I and IV in-gel activity (BN-PAGE) in APOE4 than APOE3 despite the higher nuclear ETC transcripts; if APOE4 shows equal or higher assembled complex activity and maximal respiration per mitochondrial mass, the bottleneck step is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pharmacological or genetic blockade of the citrate-export/pyruvate-entry route (SLC25A1 inhibition or knockdown, or MPC inhibition with UK5099) should reduce BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area and cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol content in APOE4 microglia toward APOE3 levels, with a markedly smaller effect in APOE3; if APOE4 lipid storage is unchanged by SLC25A1/MPC blockade, the proposed supply-side bottleneck is wrong.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show greater M+2/M+4 enrichment of palmitate, cholesterol and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 than APOE3, with proportionally less 13C reaching CO2; equal glucose-derived carbon flow into lipid would weaken the mechanism.", "Model discrimination against a purely transcriptional SREBP-driven model: SREBF1/SCAP knockdown should lower SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 transcripts in both genotypes but should not fully normalize APOE4 lipid droplets, whereas SLC25A1 blockade should; the opposite pattern would favour SREBP drive over the oxidation bottleneck.", "If the endolysosomal arm is a consequence of lipid load, then blocking esterification (DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition) should lower cathepsin/v-ATPase transcript and LysoTracker signal in APOE4; persistence of the endolysosomal elevation after esterification blockade would indicate an independent lysosomal mechanism rather than the proposed downstream response.", "Focus-rejection test: APOE4 microglia should NOT show increased actin-dependent uptake; pHrodo bead/synaptosome phagocytosis per cell should be equal or reduced in APOE4, and phalloidin-measured F-actin cup formation unchanged. A clear increase in actin-driven phagocytic uptake in APOE4 would show the cytoskeletal focus was wrongly rejected and would require revisiting the primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA, unspecified log base): nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation transcripts are coordinately elevated above the strongly positive background of this differential-expression list (37 NDUF/UQCR/COX/ATP5/SDH genes, median +2.64 vs list median +1.46, permutation p=0.003), together with TCA and mitochondrial carrier transcripts (MDH1 +8.7, OGDH +8.6, MPC2 +8.0, GOT1 +6.4, SLC25A1 +4.5, ACO2 +3.5).", "MEASURED (RNA) and INFERRED: the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts present move oppositely (median -1.56; MT-ATP6 -3.4, MT-CYB -2.3, MT-ND4 -1.8, MT-CO2 -1.3; nuclear-ETC vs mtDNA-encoded Mann-Whitney p=0.001). We infer, but do not measure, that this mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch limits assembly of complexes I/III/IV/V, so terminal oxidation rather than substrate entry becomes the flux-limiting step (the primary bottleneck).", "INFERRED FLUX: with pyruvate import (MPC2) and TCA transcripts high but terminal oxidation limited, citrate accumulates and is exported by SLC25A1 to the cytosol, where ACSS2 (+2.9) provides an additional acetyl-CoA route; neither citrate, acetyl-CoA, nor any flux was measured.", "MEASURED (RNA) with INFERRED activity: the esterification/storage arm is transcriptionally raised (AGPAT2 +6.3, SREBF1 +4.7, SCD +4.2, LPCAT1 +3.1, DGAT1 +1.7, SOAT1 +1.3; also DHCR24 +3.7, DHCR7 +2.7, LSS +2.3, ACAT2 +2.0, LDLR +1.5), which we infer commits cytosolic acetyl-CoA/acyl-CoA to triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester rather than to oxidation. Lipid droplets themselves are an unmeasured pool here.", "MEASURED (RNA) with UNRESOLVED DIRECTION: endolysosomal degradative transcripts are high (CTSK +7.4, GBA +6.7, NAGLU +5.9, HEXA +5.7, SMPD1 +5.6, CTSB +5.5, ATP6V1H +6.9, ATP6V1A +4.2, GAA +10.0, TFEB +2.4, RAB7A +2.7, VPS26A +4.9, DNM2 +5.8), consistent with a CLEAR-type response to an increased lipid/substrate load; these data cannot say whether this is a cause or a consequence of the lipid-storage state.", "MEASURED (RNA) counter-direction for the assigned focus: core motility/phagocytic-cup transcripts are among the most reduced (MYH9 -6.4, FAM49B/CYRIB -5.8, ACTB -5.0, ARHGAP30 -5.2, MYO1F -3.7, SPN -7.3, CTSS -5.6), and neither an actin/Arp2/3 set (n=14, median +1.58, p=0.81) nor a phagocytic-receptor set (n=22, median +1.36, p=0.62) is enriched above the list background, so we reject a primary phagocytic/cytoskeletal bottleneck and treat any uptake change as a downstream, untested consequence."], "title": "Mitonuclear ETC mismatch makes terminal oxidation the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, diverting TCA carbon through citrate export into esterified lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19477162795849795, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31710359853175285, "cosine_similarity": 0.38480581636034134, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6043300970873786, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19477162795849795, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31710359853175285, "cosine_similarity": 0.38480581636034134, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6043300970873786, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8352175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 133}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base; only their sign and rank relative to other rows in the same table are used, never an absolute fold change.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene means unmeasured/unreported, not unchanged.", "The apparent global positive shift (1705 up versus 507 down; overall median +1.46) is treated as a source-table layout artifact: 506 source rows each carry exactly one positive and one negative entry (an up-list/down-list column pair) and 1200 rows carry a single, almost always positive entry. All enrichment claims therefore use up-genes-only, source-row-local background comparisons.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme capacity; no protein level, post-translational modification, allosteric state, metabolic flux, or subcellular localization for any of these enzymes was measured.", "Neutral lipid, lipid droplets, citrate, acetyl-CoA, NADPH, ACLY, FASN, PLIN2, LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured in this dataset and are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a specific protein.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture and single-cell 10X Flex data can carry ambient RNA, so some transcript differences may reflect cell-composition or contamination rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation; biological replicate number was not supplied.", "Causality is not established by these correlative genotype-associated abundance differences."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, selectively strong up-regulation of the pyruvate-to-citrate-export axis (MPC2, DLD, ACO2, SLC25A1) coupled to cytosolic oxaloacetate/NADPH recycling (MDH1, GOT1, ME1) and a SREBF1/SCD monounsaturated-fatty-acid and esterification program (AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1) plus scavenger uptake (SCARB1, CD36, APOE). We propose that mitochondrial citrate export into this cytosolic lipogenic sink, not interferon or NF-kB signalling, is the rate-limiting node that biases APOE4 microglial carbon toward esterified neutral lipid; the assigned interferon/inflammatory focus is rejected because canonical ISG effectors are essentially absent from the differential-expression rows and the few interferon-pathway genes present rank at or below the local background of the same table.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) in APOE4 microglia should reduce esterified neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content toward APOE3 levels and reduce U-13C-glucose incorporation into palmitate and oleate, while leaving lysosomal gene expression (TFEB, CTSB, GAA) largely unchanged. If SLC25A1 inhibition leaves droplet content and 13C-glucose-to-fatty-acid labelling unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "U-13C-glucose tracing should show higher fractional labelling of citrate and of de novo palmitate/oleate in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. If labelling is equal or lower in APOE4, the carbon-rerouting step is falsified and an uptake-dominated model should replace it.", "SCD inhibition should lower triacylglycerol and droplet content in APOE4 more than in APOE3, and exogenous oleate should rescue that reduction. Failure of oleate to rescue would falsify the MUFA-limited esterification step.", "Discriminating against the assigned interferon focus: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade should not normalize the APOE4 lipid phenotype, and ISG effector transcripts (ISG15, MX1, OAS1, IFIT1) should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference under mock treatment. Detection of a coherent ISG signature with those effectors up in APOE4 would falsify the rejection of the interferon mechanism and require revising the primary bottleneck.", "Discriminating against a generic mitochondrial-mass explanation: after normalizing to mitochondrial content (mtDNA copy number or citrate synthase activity), the cytosolic/transport components (SLC25A1, MDH1, GOT1) should remain selectively elevated at the protein level relative to ETC subunits. If all mitochondrial proteins scale uniformly with mitochondrial mass, the mechanism reduces to increased mitochondrial biogenesis and the selective-rerouting claim is weakened.", "Blocking storage rather than supply (combined DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition) should redirect the same carbon into free fatty acid and increase lipotoxic stress in APOE4 without lowering total lipid uptake; if total cellular lipid falls instead, the esterification-sink step is misplaced."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Increased transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and citrate-forming steps (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:OGDH +8.56) are interpreted as increased capacity, not measured flux, for delivering glycolytic carbon into the mitochondrial citrate pool in APOE4.", "Elevated gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) is proposed to raise mitochondrial-to-cytosolic citrate export; this export step is the primary bottleneck because the downstream cytosolic acetyl-CoA-generating enzyme (ACLY) was not measured, so acetyl-CoA supply is inferred, not observed.", "Coordinated cytosolic gene:MDH1 (+8.72), gene:GOT1 (+6.43) and gene:ME1 (+1.36) are proposed to regenerate oxaloacetate/pyruvate and cytosolic reducing equivalents, allowing the citrate-malate-pyruvate cycle to run continuously rather than stalling after a single round.", "A lipogenic transcriptional arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.67 with gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93) is proposed to convert the exported carbon into monounsaturated fatty acid; the sterol arm is comparatively unremarkable (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08), so we predict a fatty-acyl rather than sterol-synthetic bias.", "Esterification and uptake genes (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24) are proposed to channel both newly made and imported acyl chains into esterified neutral lipid (triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester), an inferred pool that was not measured here.", "An expanded lysosomal/degradative compartment (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:LAMP1 +1.38) is interpreted as a compensatory response to the increased lipid load rather than its cause, and it is only modestly elevated relative to the local background of the same table.", "Because interferon effector transcripts are absent and the interferon/NF-kB genes present (gene:IFNAR1, gene:IRF8, gene:IFI16, gene:TMEM173, gene:IRF5, gene:IRF2) sit at or below local background, we assign no causal role to type I/II interferon signalling in the APOE4-versus-APOE3 mock difference."], "title": "APOE4 microglia reroute mitochondrial citrate to a cytosolic SREBF1/SCD lipogenic sink rather than mounting an interferon response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15515267880220063, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24789000824965932, "cosine_similarity": 0.384577708827663, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5909611650485437, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15515267880220063, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24789000824965932, "cosine_similarity": 0.384577708827663, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5909611650485437, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.967859, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 134}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_039", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene is not evidence of no change, and the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified, so only signs and relative ranks are used.", "Direction of transcript change is assumed to translate, at least partly, into protein and activity change for RAC2/DOCK8/ARHGDIA; no GTPase protein, GTP-loading, phosphorylation or localisation was measured.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; assignment of increased spots to actin/Arp2/3/capping or to ANXA1 is provisional, and keratin candidates in many spots indicate possible contamination.", "The ~77% upward skew of the DE list implies a global normalisation or compositional shift; down-going genes are therefore treated as the more informative signal, and the apparent decreases in very highly expressed transcripts (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9) could partly be compositional artefacts.", "Cells are assumed to be microglia rather than the co-cultured astrocytes; no per-cell-type deconvolution, replicate count, or cell-composition information was supplied.", "Phagocytic index, endocytic flux, lysosomal degradation rate, cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content were not measured in this dataset; all flux and storage statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show coordinated transcript loss of the haematopoietic Rho-GTPase activation module (RAC2, DOCK8, PLEK, ARHGAP30, MYO1F, ARHGDIB, HCK, PTPRC, SPN) against a strongly upward-shifted differential-expression list, together with one of the largest increases in the RhoGDI-1 transcript ARHGDIA and increases in Rho-GAP transcripts, while engulfment receptors, actin building blocks, endocytic carriers, lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase and sterol-esterification transcripts all rise. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia is the spatially restricted GTP-loading of Rac/Cdc42 needed to build the actin-driven phagocytic cup, so that cargo recognition and downstream degradation/lipid storage capacity outstrip the cell's ability to internalise large particulate cargo. Causality is not established by these data; the GTPase activity state, uptake flux and lipid pools were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, ARHGDIA knockdown (or expression of a RhoGDI-insensitive/constitutively active Rac1) should raise Rac-GTP and restore engulfment of large particulate cargo (pHrodo beads, synaptosomes, myelin) toward APOE3 levels within hours, without increasing surface TREM2/CD36/ITGB1. If Rac-GTP is successfully raised but particulate uptake remains unchanged, or if baseline Rac-GTP (PBD pull-down or PAK-biosensor FRET) is not lower in APOE4, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Dissociation prediction: APOE4 microglia should show reduced particulate/large-cargo uptake per cell but equal or greater uptake of soluble receptor-mediated cargo (AcLDL, transferrin, dextran) and equal or greater lipid/cholesteryl-ester load. Finding both routes equally reduced, or particulate uptake unchanged or increased, would weaken the mechanism.", "Step-placement prediction: measured lysosomal proteolytic capacity per internalised cargo (DQ-BSA, cathepsin B/D activity, v-ATPase-dependent acidification) should be equal or higher in APOE4, placing the defect before lysosomal delivery. Lower degradative capacity per cargo would relocate the bottleneck downstream and falsify the pre-lysosomal placement.", "Specificity prediction: inhibiting the storage arm (SOAT1 inhibition) should reduce cholesteryl-ester load without restoring particulate engulfment; if SOAT1 inhibition rescues engulfment, lipid storage rather than Rac-dependent actin remodelling is the primary constraint.", "Imaging prediction: fixed and live imaging should show fewer and shorter-lived F-actin-positive phagocytic cups per bound particle in APOE4, with unchanged or higher total F-actin and Arp2/3 protein. Equal cup frequency and lifetime with unchanged cup F-actin intensity would weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia down-regulate a haematopoietic-restricted Rho-GTPase activation/adaptor module at the RNA level (gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:PLEK, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:MYO1F, gene:ARHGDIB, gene:HCK, gene:PTPRC, gene:SPN; set mean -2.1 versus a global DE-list mean of +1.39, permutation p\u003c1e-4), while the ubiquitous RhoGDI-1 transcript gene:ARHGDIA is the third-largest positive effect in the dataset and Rho-GAP transcripts gene:ARHGAP1 and gene:ARHGAP35 also rise.", "Inferred activity (not measured): the shifted GDI/GEF/GAP transcript balance lowers the fraction of Rac1/Rac2/Cdc42 that is membrane-delivered and GTP-loaded at sites of cargo contact; total GTPase protein need not fall.", "Measured: actin building blocks and nucleation/severing/capping machinery are not depleted - gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5, gene:CFL1 and gene:ACTG1 transcripts rise, and protein spots whose candidate lists contain actin, Arp2/3 or capping proteins are predominantly increased (protein_spot:028, protein_spot:029, protein_spot:036, protein_spot:081, protein_spot:082, protein_spot:052). Inferred: the constraint is on productive, GTPase-directed assembly rather than on component supply.", "Measured: cargo recognition and tethering components increase (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:ITGB1, gene:ITGA6, gene:C1QA, gene:ANXA1, with ANXA1-containing spots protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046 strongly increased). Inferred: recognition and surface dwell of cargo are maintained or increased while actin-dependent cup closure lags, biasing net flux toward clathrin/receptor-mediated and soluble routes (gene:CLTB, gene:DNM2, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3).", "Measured: degradative and lipid-processing capacity expands (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, plus gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE). Inferred: internalised sterol and lipid are preferentially esterified and stored rather than cleared or effluxed.", "Predicted system-level state (inferred, not observed here): APOE4 microglia become uptake-limited for large particulate cargo per cell yet lipid-loaded and degradation-competent, a dissociation between recognition/degradation capacity and internalisation flux."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are internalization-limited at the Rac/Cdc42-dependent actin step, with receptor recognition and endolysosomal-lipid processing capacity preserved or expanded"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27989171103606714, "cosine_similarity": 0.3845269678531028, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976763754045307, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27989171103606714, "cosine_similarity": 0.3845269678531028, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976763754045307, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79159325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 135}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_025", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression compilation, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list contains an internal block structure (one part ~50% up with mean effect -0.11, another ~95-100% up with mean +2.41), so all pathway claims were re-tested inside the direction-balanced part and only sets that survived there (lysosomal, uptake receptors, ETC) are treated as coherent.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are therefore compared only in rank/relative terms, never converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme and transporter protein abundance; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo residence time, TFEB nuclear localization, respiration and lipid content are inferred and were not measured here.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level changes are treated as ambiguous and never as identification of a specific protein pool.", "Pseudobulk-style genotype contrasts can reflect shifts in cell-state proportions (e.g., a larger DAM-like/lipid-laden subpopulation in APOE4) rather than per-cell flux changes; the mechanism assumes, but does not demonstrate, a per-cell change.", "Astrocyte co-culture and 10x Flex probe-based quantification (which handles mitochondrially encoded transcripts differently from nuclear ones) are assumed not to dominate the genotype contrast.", "No causal claim is made: APOE4 genotype association with these transcript patterns is observational."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent transcriptional expansion of endolysosomal uptake and degradation machinery together with mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport subunit transcripts, while ER folding/ERAD transcripts are flat-to-decreased. We propose that the bottleneck is lysosomal hydrolytic/efflux flux relative to receptor-mediated lipid-cargo influx: the measured CLEAR-like hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript increase is a compensatory response to an unresolved substrate load rather than evidence of successful clearance, and the coordinated nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC transcript increase reflects downstream routing of liberated catabolic substrate. Flux, enzyme activity, cargo retention, TFEB localization and causal direction are inferred, not measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (cargo pulse-chase): with matched cargo dose, APOE4 microglia should retain more undegraded cargo per unit lysosomal volume than APOE3 (slower DQ-BSA dequenching or slower BODIPY-LDL/myelin clearance) despite higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3 per unit lysosomal volume, and lysosomal enzyme activity assays (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXB) scale with the transcript increase with no substrate retention, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (remove the influx): culturing both genotypes 48-72 h in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SR-B1/CD36-mediated uptake, should reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences in hydrolase, v-ATPase and nuclear ETC/TCA transcripts by at least half. If those genotype differences persist essentially unchanged when cargo influx is removed, the influx-driven ordering of steps 1-4 is wrong and a cell-autonomous mitochondrial or chromatin-level difference should be preferred.", "Ordering test: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or CPT1 inhibition should selectively blunt the APOE4 excess in oxygen consumption and in ETC/TCA transcripts and increase neutral-lipid droplet content, without lowering hydrolase or v-ATPase transcripts. If hydrolase transcripts fall in parallel, the mitochondrial arm is upstream of, not downstream of, the lysosomal program.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown should worsen cargo retention and lysosomal-stress markers (GPNMB, DRAM1, LGALS3) selectively in APOE4; equal effects in both genotypes would argue the CLEAR-like induction is not a genotype-specific compensation.", "Mitonuclear test: BN-PAGE or complex-specific assays should show that assembled complex I/IV and maximal respiration in APOE4 rise proportionally less than the nuclear ETC subunit transcripts, with an unchanged or reduced mtDNA-encoded:nuclear subunit protein ratio. Proportional increases in assembled complexes and spare respiratory capacity would refute step 5 while leaving steps 1-4 intact.", "Rejection of the assigned ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 cells should not show a coherent UPR signature (no XBP1 splicing increase, no HSPA5/HSP90B1 protein increase, no thapsigargin-like ATF4/CHOP protein induction) and should not be preferentially rescued by chemical chaperones (4-PBA/TUDCA) relative to lysosome-directed intervention. A clear XBP1-splicing or BiP protein increase in APOE4 would revive the ER-stress explanation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, CD163, STAB1, COLEC12, TREM2, LDLR; 13/13 such genes up in the direction-balanced part of the list, mean +1.85 vs background -0.14, Mann-Whitney p=0.015), which we infer increases receptor-mediated delivery of lipid/lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system. Uptake rate itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (proposed bottleneck; inferred): Cargo delivery exceeds per-lysosome hydrolytic and sterol/lipid-efflux capacity, so undegraded lipid cargo is retained. No lipid, cargo-clearance or enzyme-activity measurement is supplied; the bottleneck is an inference from the co-occurrence of elevated uptake receptors with elevated lysosomal-stress-associated transcripts (GPNMB +1.11 at adjusted p~1e-250 rank, DRAM1 +2.92, LGALS3 +2.37).", "Step 3 (measured RNA; inferred activity): A compensatory lysosome-biogenesis program is engaged: TFEB (+2.38) plus hydrolases and lysosomal membrane/acidification components rise coherently (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, CTSB +5.52, DPP7 +4.52, CTSD +2.86, HEXB +2.17, MAN2B1 +1.81, LAMP1 +1.38, SCARB2 +1.06; ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51). In the direction-balanced block this set gives mean +3.10 vs background -0.17 (p=2e-4). Increased mRNA is not evidence of increased hydrolase activity or acidification.", "Step 4 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Substrate liberated by catabolism is routed to mitochondria, seen as coordinated increases in mitochondrial carriers and oxidative enzymes (MPC2 +7.98, SLC25A1 +4.47, SLC25A11 +4.50, SLC25A5 +5.56; OGDH +8.56, MDH1 +8.72, GOT1 +6.43, DLD +5.54, ACO2 +3.54) and in every detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunit (38/38 up, mean +2.81, permutation p=2e-4; 6/6 up with mean +4.05 in the balanced block, p=6e-4). Respiration was not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred): Compensation is incomplete and oxidatively costly: antioxidant/iron-handling transcripts rise (PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, GPX4 +2.79, PRDX5 +1.96, FTH1 +2.53) while several mitochondrially encoded subunit transcripts fall (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33), a mitonuclear mismatch we infer limits assembly of complexes I/III/IV/V; MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are up, so this step is the weakest link in the chain.", "Step 6 (measured RNA; inferred state): The net inferred state is an expanded but flux-limited degradative compartment in a DAM-like activated microglial state (CLEC7A +1.46, ITGAX +1.69, TREM2 +1.28, CSF1R +1.37, LGALS3 +2.37), with sterol-synthesis transcripts still up (DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, SREBF2 +1.06), consistent with cargo-derived sterol not being sensed as an ER sterol surplus; this sterol set is not statistically distinguished from the list background and is supportive at best."], "title": "Lysosomal clearance capacity, not ER folding, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: scavenger-receptor-driven cargo influx outpaces an expanded hydrolase/v-ATPase program and spills catabolic flux into mitochondria"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17782236310462493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3844445208559706, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6020679611650485, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17782236310462493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3844445208559706, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6020679611650485, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2835325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 136}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_016", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance differences for hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits translate into a corresponding change in lysosomal degradative capacity; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and cholesterol content were not measured.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression export, and the visible structure (one symmetric up/down ranked block plus one essentially all-positive block) is a selection artefact; only the symmetric block is treated as directionally unbiased, and the enrichment claim is tested there.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effect column is treated as constant across rows, so only relative magnitudes and signs are interpreted.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each (e.g. cathepsin-containing spots also list actins, tropomyosin, keratins), so they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration and never as evidence for a specific protein.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some transcripts may derive from non-microglial cells despite single-cell resolution being stated for the method.", "APOE genotype is isogenic and mock-treated, so differences are taken as genotype-associated rather than treatment-associated; causality is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated increase in lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts together with increased lipid-uptake, esterification and de novo sterol-synthesis transcripts. This combination is most parsimoniously explained if sterol that enters the endolysosome is inefficiently delivered to the ER/plasma-membrane accessible pool, so the ER sterol sensor remains de-repressed (SREBP program on) while degradative-compartment machinery is transcriptionally amplified; the rate-limiting step is inferred lysosomal cholesterol/sphingolipid egress, not interferon or NF-kB signalling, for which the data provide no coherent module.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute relief of lysosomal sterol trapping in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1 over-expression) should, within hours and before any change in inflammatory tone, lower SREBP2-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, LDLR) and reduce filipin-stainable cholesterol in LAMP1+ compartments, while leaving APOE4 lipid-uptake receptor transcripts largely unchanged. If SREBP2 targets stay elevated after lysosomal cholesterol is demonstrably cleared, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong.", "Contrasting perturbation that separates supply from egress: statin inhibition of HMGCR should NOT normalize the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4 if the bottleneck is egress; if statin alone collapses the lysosomal program, the mechanism is better described as excess de novo synthesis and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Direct pool measurement: unesterified cholesterol and cholesteryl ester per cell should be equal to or higher in APOE4 than APOE3 despite the active synthesis program, with the excess enriched in the lysosomal fraction. Finding lower total sterol in APOE4 would falsify the 'de-repressed sensor despite adequate sterol' logic.", "Activity versus abundance: cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase enzymatic activity and DQ-BSA degradation rate should be higher or at least unchanged in APOE4; if hydrolase activity is actually lower despite higher transcripts, the model must be replaced by a failed-maturation/impaired-acidification mechanism.", "Interferon control test: APOE4 versus APOE3 mock cultures should show no significant induction of a canonical type-I interferon module (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1/3, OAS1, STAT1) by targeted qPCR or protein assay; detection of a coherent ISG module would support the rejected interferon alternative over this metabolic bottleneck.", "Ordering test: knocking down TFEB in APOE4 microglia should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation without normalizing lysosomal cholesterol load, whereas relieving cholesterol load should reduce both; the reverse ordering would falsify step 3 as compensatory."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance of lipid-uptake and lipid-handling receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP), which we infer increases flux of lipoprotein-associated sterol and lipid cargo into the endolysosomal system; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Inside the endolysosome, egress of unesterified cholesterol and turnover of sphingolipid/glycolipid cargo is inferred to be rate-limiting in APOE4; NPC1 and LIPA transcripts are absent from the supplied selection, so this step is an inference from downstream signatures, not an observation.", "Cells compensate by amplifying degradative capacity: acid-hydrolase transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1), and lysosome-associated genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:RAB7A, gene:GPNMB) are coordinately higher, consistent with (but not proof of) increased MiT/TFE transcriptional activity (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF measured as transcripts only; nuclear localization not measured).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is inferred to remain low, SREBP-dependent transcription is not switched off: sterol-synthesis and uptake transcripts stay elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD). Elevated INSIG1 is read as a SREBP target, not as evidence of active feedback inhibition.", "Sterol and fatty acid that do reach the cytosol are inferred to be diverted into esters and neutral-lipid storage rather than membrane sterol, supported by higher gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1; lipid-droplet and cholesteryl-ester pools were not measured.", "The resulting chronically loaded, hydrolase-rich lysosomal state is proposed to be the proximal APOE4 phenotype and to act upstream of a modest, non-interferon chemokine tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2), rather than being driven by it."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand an acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase lysosomal program while ER sterol sensing stays de-repressed, indicating a lysosome-to-ER cholesterol egress bottleneck rather than an interferon program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18835594427898975, "cosine_similarity": 0.3841248735416049, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11839530332681017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18835594427898975, "cosine_similarity": 0.3841248735416049, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61434025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 137}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_141", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1 and all adjusted p \u003c 0.05); enrichment statements are made relative to this selected background (77.1% of rows up, median +1.46), not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are therefore not directly comparable to the log2 protein-spot values.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a readout of transcriptional program state only; enzyme activity, protein level, subcellular localization, and metabolic flux are inferred and unmeasured.", "SREBP-target, CLEAR/lysosome and OXPHOS gene memberships come from unverified background knowledge (no literature or database access was permitted); set definitions were fixed before testing but are hand-curated and incomplete.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on microglial lipid load may be partly non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply), which this hypothesis does not separate.", "The global upward shift of the selected rows may partly reflect normalization, ambient RNA, or capture differences between genotypes rather than true coordinated induction."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and the MiT/TFE regulator TFEB are coordinately higher than in APOE3, yet SREBP-pathway and sterol-biosynthetic transcripts (SREBF1/2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7/DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, SCD, FADS1, LPCAT1) and the uptake receptor transcripts LDLR/SCARB1/CD36/ABCA7 are also higher. We hypothesise that this normally antagonistic combination arises because delivery of lysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER is rate-limiting in APOE4, so the ER sterol sensor behaves as sterol-poor while endolysosomal lipid load rises; the predicted consequence is a futile uptake/synthesis cycle terminating in SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterified lipid storage. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: acutely bypassing lysosomal cholesterol egress with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or direct ER-targeted sterol delivery) in mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should suppress SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, SREBF2) substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3, and should reduce filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol preferentially in APOE4. If cyclodextrin lowers SREBP targets equally in both genotypes, or fails to lower them in APOE4, the proposed egress bottleneck (STEP 3/4) is weakened.", "FLUX TEST: pulse-chase of fluorescent or isotopically labelled LDL/apoE-lipoprotein cholesterol should show a lower rate of appearance of newly esterified cholesteryl ester per unit internalized cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3, despite equal or higher lysosomal hydrolase specific activity (GBA, HEXA/B, cathepsin B/D activity assays per lysosome). Equal or faster esterification kinetics in APOE4 falsify the bottleneck placement.", "STORAGE TEST: APOE4 microglia should contain more neutral-lipid droplets and a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio than APOE3 under mock conditions; SOAT1 inhibition should convert this into elevated free cholesterol with genotype-selective ER stress or toxicity in APOE4. Absence of any droplet or ester difference would falsify STEP 5.", "CAPACITY TEST: TFEB knockdown should worsen lipid accumulation and lysosomal cholesterol staining disproportionately in APOE4, whereas constitutively active TFEB (or TFEB overexpression) should normalize SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4. If TFEB manipulation changes lipid load equally in both genotypes, the compensation interpretation of STEP 2 is weakened.", "ALTERNATIVE-MECHANISM TEST: if inhibiting mitochondrial pyruvate import (UK5099) or complex I (rotenone, low dose) reproduces the APOE4 lysosomal/SREBP transcript signature in APOE3 cells, the mitochondrial arm (STEP 6) rather than lipid egress is primary and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "REPLICATION/CONFOUND TEST: with an unfiltered transcriptome and per-genotype library-size and ambient-RNA controls, the lysosomal and SREBP sets should remain up relative to a matched-expression background. If the coordinated upshift disappears after such control (as would be expected for a normalization artefact), essentially all steps are weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_141", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for APOE and for lipid/lipoprotein-uptake receptors (SCARB1 +8.22, ABCA7 +2.14, LDLR +1.50, CD36 +1.38, MERTK +1.30, TREM2 +1.28) in the reported log scale; we infer, but did not measure, an increased flux of lipid and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "STEP 2 (inferred load, measured transcriptional response): The resulting luminal lipid load (unmeasured) is proposed to drive a MiT/TFE-associated CLEAR response: TFEB +2.38 and MITF +1.03 RNA, with 28/29 curated lysosomal genes up (GAA +9.96, AP5M1 +9.78, SLC38A7 +7.46, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51, CTSD +2.86, HEXB +2.17, LAMP1 +1.38, NPC2 +1.17, SCARB2 +1.06). This is interpreted as compensation (demand signal), not as demonstrated degradative capacity.", "STEP 3 (proposed bottleneck, inferred): Transfer of unesterified cholesterol from the lysosomal lumen/membrane to the ER is limiting in APOE4. This step is inferred, not observed; the canonical carrier NPC1 and the acid lipase LIPA are absent from the supplied rows, so only the downstream sensor readout is available.", "STEP 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensor state): Because ER sterol remains sub-threshold, the SREBP arm stays active despite lipid loading: SREBF1 +4.67, SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87, HMGCS1 +1.08, LSS +2.27, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, EBP +1.34, ACAT2 +2.04, SCD +4.17, FADS1 +1.59, LPCAT1 +3.07, LDLR +1.50 (16/16 curated SREBP-responsive genes up).", "STEP 5 (measured RNA, inferred storage pool): Continued synthesis plus uptake in the face of limited egress is predicted to be buffered by esterification and neutral-lipid storage, consistent with higher SOAT1 (+1.25) and DGAT1 (+1.72) RNA; cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplet pools were not measured in this dataset and are therefore predicted, not observed.", "STEP 6 (correlated, not required): An accompanying anabolic/ATP demand arm is visible as coordinated upregulation of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA/carrier transcripts (all 39 curated nuclear OXPHOS genes up, e.g. NDUFA5 +7.34, ATP5ME +5.20; MDH1 +8.72, OGDH +8.56, MPC2 +7.98, SLC25A11 +4.50, SLC25A1 +4.47) while mitochondrially encoded transcripts do not follow (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32). We treat this as a correlate of the lipid-handling state and as the leading alternative primary mechanism, not as an established consequence."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain a TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal expansion program while the ER sterol sensor still reads 'low': lysosome-to-ER cholesterol egress is the proposed bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1889007864712181, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3195239376524901, "cosine_similarity": 0.38396263994164964, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_141", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6050194174757282, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1889007864712181, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3195239376524901, "cosine_similarity": 0.38396263994164964, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6050194174757282, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.639747, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 138}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_022", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive and the median effect is +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, so all pathway statements are made relative to that global shift and absolute magnitudes are not interpreted.", "Transcript differences for hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits are treated as capacity signals only; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, proteolytic flux, autophagic flux and TFEB nuclear localization are inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D features; no spot is assumed to report a single named protein, and directional spot differences are used only as a hint of proteoform redistribution.", "Replicate structure is not supplied; single-cell derived adjusted p-values may be inflated by cell-level pseudoreplication, so ranking rather than nominal significance is used.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; RNA is assumed to come from the microglial population and protein spots may include non-microglial material, which is not verifiable from the supplied files.", "Background pathway memberships used to group genes are unverified background knowledge, not derived from the supplied data.", "The assigned sterol focus is set aside as primary: cholesterol biosynthesis, uptake and LXR/efflux gene groups are not shifted beyond the global background (Mann-Whitney p 0.29-0.99), and ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR and SQLE are absent from the supplied rows, so a sterol-export or sterol-synthesis bottleneck cannot be supported or excluded."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an elevated scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake transcriptional state coupled to a coordinated TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR transcript program (luminal hydrolases plus V-ATPase subunits). We propose that this transcript program is a compensatory response to a shortfall in acidification-coupled lysosomal degradative throughput relative to delivered cargo, so that the bottleneck lies at hydrolase maturation/acidification per lysosome rather than at lysosomal gene transcription, at cholesterol biosynthesis, or at sterol export. Causality is not established by these data; the discovery set contains only associations in a selected differential-expression list plus ambiguous protein spots.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Cargo-dependence test (discriminating): culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake, should reduce the APOE4-minus-APOE3 gap in the lysosomal hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript module by at least half within 48 h. If the lysosomal module remains fully elevated in APOE4 with cargo influx blocked, the cargo-driven step of this mechanism is wrong and a cargo-independent MiT/TFE or genotype-intrinsic transcriptional cause is favoured.", "Per-organelle flux test (discriminating): quantitative imaging should show APOE4 microglia with greater LAMP1-positive lysosomal volume but equal or lower DQ-BSA dequenching rate normalized to that volume, and equal or less acidic lysosomal pH by ratiometric probe, despite higher V-ATPase transcripts. If normalized degradative rate and acidification are proportionally higher in APOE4, the proposed throughput bottleneck is rejected and the transcript program should be reinterpreted as genuinely increased capacity.", "Maturation test: immunoblot of cathepsin D and beta-hexosaminidase should show an increased pro-form to mature-form ratio in APOE4 relative to APOE3. If mature forms increase in proportion to transcript levels, the hydrolase-maturation step is weakened even if the flux prediction holds.", "TFEB-dependence test: TFEB knockdown, or constitutive mTORC1 activation, should collapse the APOE4 lysosomal transcript module toward APOE3 levels with a larger effect in APOE4. Persistence of the elevated module after effective TFEB knockdown would falsify the proposed transcriptional driver.", "Sterol-axis control test: direct measurement of free and esterified cholesterol, filipin staining, and expression of the unmeasured sterol genes (HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) is predicted to show no coordinate genotype shift of the sterol synthesis/export axis larger than the global background shift, with any lipid accumulation confined to the LAMP1-positive compartment. Coordinate induction of HMGCR/SQLE with suppressed ABCA1 and non-lysosomal cholesterol accumulation would support the sterol focus instead of this mechanism.", "Rescue test: enhancing lysosomal acidification or hydrolase delivery (for example acidic nanoparticles or TFEB-independent V-ATPase support) should normalize the APOE4 lipid-associated marker transcripts GPNMB, LGALS3 and ITGAX; failure to move these markers while degradation is measurably restored would place them outside this pathway."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/scavenger receptors and lipid-handling genes (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:CD163, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:LDLR). Inferred (not measured): a correspondingly greater rate of endocytic/phagocytic delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosomal lumen; no uptake assay, cargo mass or lipid pool is present in this dataset.", "Inferred: the increased luminal cargo load reduces free lysosomal degradative reserve and relieves mTORC1-dependent inhibition of the MiT/TFE transcription factors; the only measurements consistent with this are transcript increases in gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03). TFEB nuclear localization, phosphorylation and mTORC1 activity are not measured.", "Measured (RNA): a coherent CLEAR-type output, with 24 of 25 detected lysosomal genes higher in APOE4 (median effect 2.30 vs global 1.46): luminal hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, plus V-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1 and membrane/trafficking genes gene:LAMP1, gene:LAPTM4A, gene:CLN3, gene:NPC2, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred, only weakly indexed by data): the mature, correctly processed and acidified hydrolase pool does not scale with these transcripts. Two-dimensional spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal proteins move in opposite directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14 and protein_spot:053 +1.54 up, versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00 and protein_spot:069 -1.38 down; the two spots containing ATP6V1E1 as a candidate, protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93, are down). Spots have several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins, so this pattern is a proteoform-redistribution hint, not evidence of any named protein pool.", "Consequence (inferred): cargo that is delivered faster than it is hydrolysed accumulates in an expanded but per-organelle less efficient lysosomal compartment; the cell shifts toward storage/esterification (gene:SOAT1 up) rather than catabolism, while the secreted protease transcript gene:CTSS is strongly reduced (-5.57), which would further bias degradation toward the intracellular compartment. Cholesteryl-ester, free-cholesterol, lipid-droplet and pH pools were not measured here.", "Readout (measured, RNA): the resulting state resembles a lipid-associated/phagocytic activation phenotype distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:TREM2, gene:CD14, gene:APOE all higher), which we interpret as downstream of the cargo/degradation mismatch rather than as an independent inflammatory program (canonical NF-kB cytokine transcripts are not coordinately raised in this list)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal-biogenesis program whose degradative throughput per unit internalized cargo, not sterol synthesis or export, is the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18984265894537833, "cosine_similarity": 0.38389217643767803, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137152103559871, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18984265894537833, "cosine_similarity": 0.38389217643767803, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137152103559871, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.76214175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 139}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; only sign and rank ordering are used, and no set-level claim depends on the numeric base.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome, so all enrichment statements are made against the supplied rows as background by permutation. Genes absent from the file (for example NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, SQSTM1, ASAH1, HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4) are untested, not unchanged.", "The whole supplied RNA set is shifted upward (mean +1.388; 1705/2212 rows positive; |effect| \u003e= 1.0 for every row), which could reflect a genotype-level normalization, RNA-content or cell-composition difference; the mechanism assumes the CLEAR set exceeds this shift for biological rather than technical reasons.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a marker of transcription-factor activity and of biosynthetic capacity, not as a measure of lysosome number, luminal pH, hydrolase catalytic activity, membrane-contact-site transfer or lipid flux, none of which are measured.", "Protein spots each carry 2-6 candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level effects are treated as weak corroboration only and never as identification of a named protein.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some measured RNA/protein signal may not be microglia-autonomous; replicate number is stated as not supplied in the workbook.", "MiT/TFE transcript elevation is assumed to precede and cause CLEAR target elevation; the cross-sectional data cannot order these events, and no lipid measurement is supplied to close the chain."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coherent, statistically enriched MiT/TFE (TFEB/TFEC/MITF) CLEAR transcriptional program covering lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and endolysosomal trafficking machinery, which we interpret as a compensatory response to a rate-limiting bottleneck in lysosomal lipid catabolism and export rather than as evidence of increased clearance; because sterol-acquisition and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts (SCARB1, LDLR, SREBF1, SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1) are simultaneously elevated rather than suppressed, acquired lipid is predicted to be routed into cytosolic cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores and toward ceramide, giving APOE4 microglia a storage-shifted lipidome. An ER-proteostasis / unfolded-protein-response mechanism is explicitly rejected: the UPR gene set is not enriched above the supplied-row background (mean 0.79 vs global 1.388, permutation p_up = 0.80) and several ER-quality-control transcripts are decreased. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Compensatory-direction test: TFEB knockdown or knockout in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels while increasing, not decreasing, endolysosomal lipid load (filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol, LipidSpot/BODIPY). If TFEB loss instead reduces both the transcripts and the lipid load, the CLEAR program is the driver rather than a compensation and this mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester and droplet content and raise the free-cholesterol fraction while leaving the CLEAR transcript elevation essentially intact. If SOAT1 inhibition also normalizes the lysosomal/v-ATPase transcript program, the bottleneck lies at esterification rather than at the lysosome and step 5 fails.", "Lipidomic prediction: untargeted lipidomics on the same mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol species and a decreased sphingomyelin:ceramide ratio in APOE4. Absence of any cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol elevation and no sphingolipid shift would falsify the storage-diversion arm.", "Acidification dependence: partial v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) should enlarge, not shrink, the APOE4-minus-APOE3 lipid-accumulation difference, because the elevated v-ATPase transcripts are posited to be load-compensating. Equal or reduced genotype difference under bafilomycin weakens step 3.", "Explicit rejection test for the assigned ER/UPR focus: pharmacological UPR modulation (ISRIB, PERK inhibitor GSK2606414, or IRE1 RNase inhibitor) should not normalize the lysosomal transcript program or the APOE4 lipid phenotype, and XBP1 splicing plus HSPA5/HERPUD1 induction should not differ between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock treatment. Detection of genotype-dependent XBP1 splicing or HSPA5 induction, or rescue of the lipid phenotype by UPR blockade, would overturn the rejection of the ER-proteostasis mechanism.", "Cross-modal check: quantitative immunoblot or targeted proteomics for mature cathepsin B/D, LAMP1 and GAA should show increased protein in APOE4, resolving the ambiguity that lysosomal candidate genes currently appear in both increased (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055) and decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) spots. Flat or reduced mature hydrolase protein despite elevated transcripts would restrict the mechanism to a transcriptional response without increased degradative capacity."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, not measured here): the APOE4 protein isoform is a poorer lipid acceptor/efflux partner than APOE3 in microglia, so lipid that enters the endolysosomal system is exported more slowly. Only APOE transcript abundance is measured (gene:APOE, +1.24); no APOE protein, lipoprotein-particle or efflux flux measurement is supplied.", "Step 2 (inferred activity from measured abundance): rising luminal lipid/substrate load in the endolysosome increases MiT/TFE transcription-factor activity. We measure only transcript abundance of the family (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.65, gene:MITF +1.03); nuclear translocation, mTORC1 status and phosphorylation are not measured.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): the CLEAR target program is coordinately elevated - acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1), all ten detected v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2) and membrane/lumen components (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLCN7, gene:RRAGD). Set mean +3.01 versus global +1.388, permutation p_up = 0.0002. Increased lysosome number, acidification and hydrolase activity are inferred, not observed.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): hydrolase-delivery and endolysosomal maturation/recycling machinery is also up (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:VPS18, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS37B), consistent with increased biosynthetic and recycling traffic into and out of the compartment.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred sensing state): despite the expanded degradative program, sterol-acquisition and ER-sterol-handling transcripts are elevated rather than repressed (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:ACAT2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1). We infer that the ER-accessible sterol pool is not being reported as replete while lysosomal load rises, i.e. the limiting step is lysosomal handling/egress, not sterol supply. This inference is weaker than steps 2-4 (permutation p_up = 0.14).", "Step 6 (measured abundance, predicted lipid outcome): esterification and droplet-forming capacity is raised (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:CIDEB, gene:MGLL) and sphingolipid transcripts shift toward ceramide generation (gene:SMPD1, gene:CERS4), so incoming sterol and fatty acid are predicted to be diverted into cytosolic cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol stores and into ceramide, producing the APOE4 lipid phenotype. Lipid species themselves are not measured in the supplied data."], "title": "MiT/TFE-driven CLEAR expansion marks a lysosomal lipid-catabolism bottleneck that diverts sterol and fatty acid into esterified storage pools in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2823357825942473, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2876383608429285, "cosine_similarity": 0.38295085065101836, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6176763754045307, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2823357825942473, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2876383608429285, "cosine_similarity": 0.38295085065101836, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6176763754045307, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.33188975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 140}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_094", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the whole list is shifted positive (mean +1.39 in the unspecified reported log base, 77% up), so only enrichment relative to this list background, not the sign alone, is treated as informative.", "Transcript abundance for MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11 and TCA enzymes is assumed to translate into proportional protein and transport capacity; no protein or activity measurement of these carriers was supplied.", "The reported RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; relative ranking, not absolute fold change, is used.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; they are used only as weak, non-identifying context.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment is assumed to be the main driver; astrocyte co-culture could contribute ambient or cross-species-of-cell RNA that is not resolvable here.", "Key nodes of the proposed chain (ACLY, FASN, ACACA, PDHA1/PDHB, PDK isoforms, MPC1, CS, MDH2, IDH1/IDH2, CPT1A, PLIN2, lactate output, acetyl-CoA and citrate pools, lipid droplets) were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred only.", "Causality is not established by these abundance data; the hypothesis states a testable direction, not a demonstrated one."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional shift that favours mitochondrial pyruvate uptake (MPC2), malate-aspartate/citrate carrier exchange (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A1) and TCA-cycle plus respiratory-chain gene expression, while committed cytosolic glycolytic (HK2, PFKP) and oxidative pentose-phosphate (PGD, TALDO1) genes fall relative to the strongly upward-shifted differential-expression background; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting node is mitochondrial pyruvate import/citrate export, whose increased capacity supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA for an SREBF1-driven lipogenic and sterol program (SCD, DGAT1, DHCR24, LSS) and thereby drives the lipid-handling and lysosomal phenotype (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA, TFEB) of APOE4 microglia. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid content and 13C6-glucose-derived labelling of palmitate/oleate towards APOE3 levels while leaving glucose uptake and extracellular acidification comparatively intact. If APOE4 lipid content and glucose-to-lipid labelling are unchanged (or increase) after MPC blockade, the pyruvate-import bottleneck is falsified.", "13C6-glucose tracing should show higher fractional m+2 labelling of citrate, alpha-ketoglutarate and malate, and higher m+2/m+4 labelling of fatty acids, in APOE4 than APOE3, without a proportional increase in m+3 lactate. Higher lactate labelling with unchanged citrate labelling would weaken the mechanism and favour a glycolytic rather than mitochondrial-routing explanation.", "Seahorse respirometry should show a larger UK5099-sensitive fraction of basal oxygen consumption in APOE4 than APOE3; equal UK5099-sensitive fractions would weaken step 1-2 even if total OCR differs.", "SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or knockdown should reduce SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty-acid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation selectively in APOE4, whereas SCD inhibition should reduce lipid droplets without reducing TCA labelling; if SCD inhibition also collapses TCA labelling, the proposed upstream-to-downstream ordering is wrong.", "Targeted immunoblot or targeted proteomics should confirm higher MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1 and GOT1 protein in APOE4; absence of protein-level differences despite the large transcript differences would substantially weaken the mechanism, since the supplied protein spots do not identify these proteins.", "If the entire signature instead reflects a shifted cell-state or ambient-RNA composition, then single-cell subclustering should place the MPC2/TCA/SREBF1 program in a specific microglial subpopulation whose frequency differs by genotype, and within-subpopulation comparison should abolish the enrichment; that result would falsify a cell-autonomous carbon-routing switch."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier subunit MPC2 (gene:MPC2, +7.98, 99th percentile of the differential list) and for the pyruvate-dehydrogenase E3 subunit and activating phosphatase (gene:DLD, gene:PDP1), while committed glycolytic isoforms fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Step 2 (inferred flux): we infer that a larger fraction of pyruvate is imported and oxidised rather than reduced to lactate or diverted to the oxidative pentose-phosphate branch, consistent with reduced gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1; net glycolytic throughput is inferred to be unchanged-to-lower, not increased.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): TCA and redox-shuttle transcripts are coordinately elevated above the already positive background (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A5), supporting increased capacity for malate-aspartate shuttling of cytosolic NADH and for TCA turning.", "Step 4 (inferred flux/localisation): increased gene:SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) capacity is inferred to raise mitochondrial citrate export to the cytosol; together with gene:ACSS2 this is inferred to enlarge the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool. The acetyl-CoA pool itself and ACLY were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred activity): the lipogenic/sterol transcriptional arm is elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR), with lipid-uptake genes gene:SCARB1 and gene:CD36 also raised; we infer increased synthesis and esterification of monounsaturated fatty acids and sterol esters.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): the resulting neutral-lipid load is inferred to increase demand on the lysosomal/hydrolase system, matching elevated gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A and gene:TFEB, and to be the proximate metabolic difference between APOE4 and APOE3 microglia under mock conditions.", "Step 7 (inferred constraint): nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain transcripts rise (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:COX7A2 and others) while several mtDNA-encoded subunits fall (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4); we infer that increased carbon entry is not matched by proportionally increased mtDNA-encoded core subunits, so ATP-coupled respiration may be inefficient and carbon is preferentially exported as citrate rather than fully oxidised."], "title": "APOE4 microglia reroute glucose carbon through mitochondrial pyruvate import and citrate export into lipogenesis rather than cytosolic glycolysis/pentose-phosphate flux"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21891999938000892, "cosine_similarity": 0.3829382791704923, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5891521035598706, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21891999938000892, "cosine_similarity": 0.3829382791704923, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5891521035598706, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.628047, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 141}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_101", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all pathway claims are made relative to the strong global positive shift of the selected rows (median approximately +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), not relative to zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified; only ranks and relative comparisons within the RNA set are used, and RNA and protein effect magnitudes are never combined arithmetically.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for the transcriptional program, not for enzyme activity, protein amount, subcellular localization or metabolic flux; lysosomal volume, pH, hydrolase activity, cholesterol distribution, SREBP-2 cleavage state and neutral-lipid content were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8), so no spot identifies a unique protein; spots are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration or counter-evidence.", "The APOE4 versus APOE3 comparison is isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype rather than treatment or line background is the contrast; replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be assessed.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies APOE-containing lipoprotein substrate, making receptor-mediated lipid influx a plausible upstream input; the lipoprotein pool itself was not measured.", "Key genes for the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, STARD3) are absent from the supplied rows, so the egress step is inferred from the pattern of the measured genes rather than observed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated increase in lipid/lipoprotein uptake and CLEAR-type lysosomal degradative transcripts that is NOT accompanied by feedback repression of ER sterol-synthesis transcripts. We propose the rate-limiting step is export of internalized, hydrolysed lipid (cholesterol and fatty acids) from the late endosome/lysosome to the ER-accessible regulatory pool: internalized lipid is retained in the endolysosome and re-routed into esterified/stored neutral lipid instead of shutting off synthesis or being fully oxidised, producing higher steady-state neutral-lipid content in APOE4. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are selected differential RNA abundances and ambiguous protein spots, and the transfer step itself was not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely raising lysosome-to-ER cholesterol egress in APOE4 microglia (for example cyclodextrin-mediated removal of lysosomal unesterified cholesterol, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should, without changing uptake-receptor transcripts, both reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content toward APOE3 levels and lower the sterol-synthesis transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24). If lipid stores fall while sterol-synthesis transcripts stay high, or if neither changes, the egress-bottleneck step is falsified even if the uptake and lysosomal transcript differences replicate.", "Blocking the proposed influx arm (SCARB1 knockdown or SR-BI blockade, or lipoprotein-free medium) should reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid excess more than APOE3. If APOE4 lipid excess persists unchanged under lipoprotein-free conditions, the uptake-driven arm is wrong and a cell-autonomous synthesis or oxidation defect should be preferred.", "Direct imaging should show more filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol colocalised with LAMP1-positive compartments and more BODIPY-positive droplets in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal lysosomal cholesterol with equal droplet content would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Because the model asserts a transfer bottleneck and not a hydrolysis failure, lysosomal hydrolase activity per cell (for example GBA, HEXA/B, GAA fluorogenic assays) should be equal or higher in APOE4. Lower hydrolase activity in APOE4 would replace the egress bottleneck with a degradation-capacity bottleneck.", "SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol and reduce droplet number without normalising the lysosomal transcript signature; if SOAT1 inhibition abolishes the genotype difference in total lysosomal cholesterol as well, the storage step is upstream of, not downstream of, the proposed bottleneck.", "Alternative-mechanism discriminator: 13C-palmitate or 13C-glucose tracing should show that APOE4 does not oxidise lipid carbon to CO2 faster than APOE3 despite higher nuclear-encoded TCA transcripts, and mtDNA-encoded transcript or mtDNA copy number per nuclear-encoded subunit should be lower in APOE4. Higher complete oxidation and matched mitonuclear stoichiometry in APOE4 would favour a primary mitochondrial-biogenesis mechanism over this lipid-sequestration mechanism.", "Replication requirement: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome re-analysis with matched library normalisation, the lysosomal/CLEAR gene set should remain enriched above the genome-wide background shift. Loss of enrichment once the global shift is removed would show the signature is a normalisation artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_101", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-binding and phagocytic uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22 with the third-smallest adjusted p in the set, gene:ITGB1, gene:ABCA7, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:RAB7A). Inferred (not measured): increased flux of exogenous lipid/lipoprotein into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Measured: an MITF/TFE-family and CLEAR-type degradative program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF; all eight measured v-ATPase subunits positive; gene:GNPTG and gene:IGF2R for hydrolase targeting; hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1). Inferred: an expanded acidified lysosomal compartment with raised luminal hydrolytic capacity; compartment volume, pH and enzyme activity were not measured.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred, not measured): transfer of the hydrolysis products, in particular unesterified cholesterol, from the lysosomal lumen/limiting membrane to the ER-accessible sterol pool is rate-limiting in APOE4, so the internalized lipid does not reach the SCAP/INSIG sensing pool.", "Consistent with a bottleneck rather than successful delivery: sterol-synthesis and LDLR transcripts are not repressed despite elevated uptake transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1 are all positive and statistically indistinguishable from the global positive shift). Inferred: continued SREBP-2-type drive on top of continued import.", "Measured: esterification and monounsaturated-acyl supply transcripts are elevated (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL, gene:SREBF1). Inferred: liberated sterol and fatty acid are re-esterified into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol-rich stores rather than exported or oxidised.", "Measured: the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative program rises strongly (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B) while the six measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts are mostly negative (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2) and NADPH-generating pentose-phosphate transcripts fall (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1). Inferred: transcriptional demand for oxidative disposal exceeds matched terminal-oxidation and reductive capacity, so oxidative clearance does not offset the storage route.", "Net inferred phenotype: APOE4 microglia hold more lipid as esterified/stored neutral lipid at steady state than APOE3, with the lysosome and lipid droplet acting as the sink."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lipid uptake and lysosomal hydrolase capacity but bottleneck at lysosome-to-ER lipid egress, sequestering sterol/lipid into stored neutral lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22370121478418195, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28786254401433115, "cosine_similarity": 0.3828732261500298, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_101", "mean_absolute_error": 0.596546925566343, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22370121478418195, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28786254401433115, "cosine_similarity": 0.3828732261500298, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "mean_absolute_error": 0.596546925566343, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8651995, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 142}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77.1% of the 2212 rows are positive with median +1.46 in the reported logarithm of unspecified base, so all set-level claims are made relative to this internal background rather than to zero.", "Coordinate transcript elevation of a functionally related module is taken as evidence of transcriptional demand for that module; it is not evidence of enzyme activity, protein amount, correct lysosomal localization, or degradative flux, none of which are measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (208 candidates over 92 spots, dominated by keratins and actins); no spot is treated as a unique protein identification, and the bidirectional cathepsin/v-ATPase spot pattern is used only as non-corroboration, not as proof that hydrolase protein is unchanged or redistributed among proteoforms.", "Lipid species, lysosomal pH, enzyme activity, autophagic flux, lysosome number/size, cargo identity and the APOE lipoprotein pool itself are not supplied; steps invoking them are explicitly inferred.", "The isogenic APOE4-versus-APOE3 mock contrast at day 30 is assumed to reflect a steady-state genotype difference in a microglia-astrocyte co-culture, so astrocyte-derived lipid supply may contribute to the inferred cargo load.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so nominal p-values and adjusted p-values in the file are used only for ranking, not as calibrated error rates."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting step of endolysosomal cargo processing is luminal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolysis rather than cargo delivery: transcripts for the sphingolipid-degrading hydrolases and their activator (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, SMPD1, NAGLU), for v-ATPase subunits, for lysosomal solute exporters and for late-endosome maturation/retrieval factors are coordinately higher in APOE4, together with the lysosomal transcription factors TFEB/MITF, whereas cathepsin- and v-ATPase-containing protein spots show no corresponding net increase; we therefore propose that APOE4 sustains a chronic luminal sphingolipid substrate load whose degradative flux (an inferred, unmeasured quantity) remains limiting, driving a demand-type transcriptional response and diversion of undegraded lipid into esterification/storage. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Baseline lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show elevated GBA/HEXB/SMPD1 substrates - hexosylceramide/glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3-type gangliosides and sphingomyelin - in APOE4, with cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol elevated as a secondary storage consequence. If sphingolipid substrate classes are unchanged and only neutral lipids differ, the sphingolipid-hydrolysis bottleneck is wrong even if a storage phenotype exists.", "Discriminating perturbation: partial pharmacological inhibition of glucocerebrosidase (conduritol-B-epoxide) or HEXB knockdown should sensitize APOE4 disproportionately, producing a larger increase in hexosylceramide, lysosome expansion and TFEB-target transcripts in APOE4 than in APOE3, while glucosylceramide-synthase inhibition (eliglustat/GENZ-123346), which lowers substrate delivery without touching cargo uptake, should specifically normalize the APOE4 hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation and the excess hexosylceramide. Equal responses in APOE3 and APOE4 to CBE, or failure of glucosylceramide-synthase inhibition to reduce the APOE4 lysosomal transcript program, would weaken the mechanism.", "Measured per-cell GBA, HEXA/HEXB and cathepsin B/D enzymatic activities and mature-form protein should rise sub-proportionally to their transcript differences in APOE4 (activity ratio markedly below the transcript ratio). If activities scale proportionally with transcripts while substrates are unchanged, the claim that hydrolysis remains limiting fails.", "Because the v-ATPase transcript rise is proposed to be compensatory rather than sufficient, APOE4 lysosomal pH should be equal to or higher (less acidic) than APOE3, and DQ-BSA or fluorescent-substrate degradation rate per lysosome should be equal or lower in APOE4. Significantly lower APOE4 lysosomal pH together with faster per-lysosome degradation would falsify the bottleneck direction and favour a simple increase in lysosomal capacity.", "The mechanism predicts the transcript module is cargo-load dependent: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking scavenger/lipid uptake, should collapse the APOE4-specific hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB-target transcript excess toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the full transcript excess under lipid-poor conditions would indicate a cargo-independent, cell-autonomous transcriptional difference instead.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/mitochondrial-import transcript module is more strongly enriched here than the lysosomal module, so if inhibiting mitochondrial respiration (or restoring it) abolishes the APOE4 lysosomal transcript signature while sphingolipid substrates remain equal between genotypes, the primary bottleneck should be reassigned to mitochondrial-energetic remodelling rather than to lysosomal sphingolipid catabolism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 changes the composition or residence time of lipid-rich cargo delivered to the microglial endolysosome (inferred; no cargo, flux or lipid measurement is supplied).", "Cargo transit toward the degradative compartment is not the limiting step: transcripts for late-endosome maturation, ESCRT and retrieval components are coordinately higher in APOE4 (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS37B, gene:CHMP4B, gene:SNX3, gene:SNX16, gene:VPS18), as are AP-5 subunits (gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5S1, gene:AP5Z1).", "The limiting step is luminal hydrolysis of sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid cargo; APOE4 cells raise the corresponding transcripts most strongly (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GBA2), together with bulk protease and acidification transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and lysosomal transcription factors (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) - a demand signature, not a measurement of activity.", "Increased transcript supply is accompanied by increased transcripts for luminal catabolite export (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:MFSD10, gene:MFSD11), consistent with an attempt to relieve product inhibition of luminal catabolism (inferred).", "The compensation appears incomplete at the protein layer: spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins or a v-ATPase subunit move in both directions and show no net increase (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), so per-lysosome hydrolytic capacity is inferred to lag the transcript response.", "Persisting undegraded lipid is inferred to be routed to esterification and storage and to keep sterol-responsive transcription active (gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:AGPAT2), predicting a baseline lipid-storage phenotype in APOE4 microglia."], "title": "Luminal sphingolipid catabolism is the endolysosomal bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, met by a compensatory CLEAR-type transcript expansion that is not matched at the protein layer"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11350293542074363, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17896598886060322, "cosine_similarity": 0.38274165297895596, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6141941747572816, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11350293542074363, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17896598886060322, "cosine_similarity": 0.38274165297895596, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6141941747572816, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.919499, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 143}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_092", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1) from 10X Flex data, so absence of a gene (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE) means it was not selected, not that it was measured and unchanged; the export-limitation step rests on this weaker inference.", "The reported RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as given; effects are compared only in rank/direction terms, and the very large |effect| values (up to 15.5) are treated as unreliable in magnitude because effect size and adjusted p-value are uncorrelated in this table (Spearman about -0.03).", "The whole RNA list is shifted upward (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 1705 up vs 507 down), so the sterol module's absolute positive sign is not by itself informative; the argument relies on which sterol/lysosomal genes were selected at all and on their internal coherence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; enzymatic activity, sterol flux, subcellular sterol localisation, cholesteryl-ester mass, lipid-droplet content and efflux rate are all inferred and none are measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots each carry 2-6 candidate genes and cannot identify a specific sterol enzyme; they are not used as evidence for any named protein pool.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some sterol supplied to microglia may be astrocyte-derived; the 10X Flex measurement may include ambient RNA and cell-composition contributions that are not corrected here.", "The APOE3 and APOE4 lines are stated to be isogenic, so the difference is attributed to APOE genotype rather than to background genetics, but differentiation-stage differences at day 30 are not excluded."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 primarily in sterol disposal capacity, not in sterol supply. Transcripts for sterol uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, COLEC12, CD163, MRC1), distal (post-squalene) cholesterol conversion (LSS, EBP, DHCR7, DHCR24), esterification/neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD) and lysosomal hydrolysis (CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GAA, NPC2, GPNMB) are coordinately higher in APOE4, whereas no canonical free-cholesterol efflux transporter transcript (ABCA1, ABCG1) appears among the selected differential rows even though 77 percent of those rows are increased. We hypothesise that the bottleneck is the step at which internalised and newly made sterol is handed to ApoE-containing acceptor particles for export: because that hand-off is limiting in APOE4, surplus sterol is shunted by SOAT1/DGAT1 into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets and retained in late endosomes/lysosomes, which keeps the ER-accessible (SCAP/INSIG-sensed) sterol pool low and sustains the uptake and distal-synthesis transcriptional program as a futile cycle. Causality is not established by these data; this is a proposed, testable mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: Acute pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe or CI-1011) in APOE4 microglia should deplete cholesteryl ester, raise ER-accessible free cholesterol, and therefore SUPPRESS the sterol-sensing readouts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR24, SREBF2 transcripts) toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h. If cholesteryl ester falls but these transcripts stay elevated in APOE4, the proposed ER-pool-under-reading bottleneck is wrong.", "DISCRIMINATING: In a cholesterol-efflux assay with defined acceptors, APOE4 microglia should export a smaller fraction of labelled cellular cholesterol per unit total cell cholesterol than APOE3, and supplying exogenous acceptors (ApoA-I or reconstituted HDL) should reduce APOE4 cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal filipin signal. Equal fractional efflux and no acceptor benefit would weaken the export-limitation step.", "Direct lipid measurement should show higher cholesteryl-ester to free-cholesterol ratio and more filipin-positive LAMP1 compartments in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower CE:FC in APOE4 would falsify the storage-shunt step.", "Stable-isotope (deuterated water or 13C-acetate) tracing should show that APOE4 total de novo sterol synthesis flux is NOT proportionally increased relative to the large distal-enzyme transcript changes, consistent with the absence of HMGCR/SQLE from the differential rows. A large proportional increase in mevalonate-pathway flux would favour a simple SREBP-2 hyperactivation model instead.", "DHCR24 inhibition (raising desmosterol) should, in this model, suppress SREBP-2 targets and induce ABCA1 more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond identically, the DHCR24 component of the mechanism is not genotype-specific.", "GLOBAL FALSIFIER: If a normalisation-corrected, unbiased re-analysis removes the whole-list upward shift and the sterol-handling and lysosomal modules no longer separate from the transcriptome background, the entire mechanism should be abandoned as a scaling artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36). INFERRED: sterol and lipoprotein influx per cell is increased; influx flux itself is not measured here.", "MEASURED (RNA): distal, post-squalene sterol-conversion transcripts are raised (gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ACAT2 +2.04) while proximal rate-limiting mevalonate enzymes (HMGCR, SQLE, FDPS, IDI1, MVD, MVK, CYP51A1, MSMO1) are absent from the selected differential rows. INFERRED: the difference lies in conversion/handling of sterol intermediates rather than in a full de novo mevalonate flux increase; no flux measurement is supplied.", "MEASURED (RNA): esterification and neutral-lipid storage transcripts are raised with very strong statistics (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, adjusted p 1.8e-125; gene:DGAT1 +1.72; gene:SCD +4.17). INFERRED (BOTTLENECK): free cholesterol arriving at the ER is esterified and deposited in lipid droplets, lowering the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool. Cholesteryl-ester mass, droplet number and free-cholesterol distribution are NOT measured in this dataset.", "MEASURED (RNA): a lysosomal-degradative module is coordinately raised (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSH +1.54, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GAA +10.02, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:TFEB +2.38), while gene:OSBPL8 is decreased (-1.90). INFERRED: an expanded late-endosome/lysosome sterol compartment with reduced retrograde endosome-to-ER sterol delivery; organelle sterol localisation is inferred, not observed.", "MEASURED (RNA): export-side transcripts are only partially represented - gene:APOE +1.24 and gene:ABCA7 +2.14 are up, but ABCA1 and ABCG1 do not appear among the selected differential rows. INFERRED: net free-cholesterol export capacity does not scale with the increased inflow and storage, making acceptor loading the limiting step. Absence from a selected list is weak evidence and could reflect selection, not equality.", "INFERRED (integration): with the ER-accessible pool held low by esterification and lysosomal retention, SCAP/INSIG-dependent sterol sensing under-reads the true sterol load, so uptake and distal-synthesis transcripts remain elevated (gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:LDLR +1.50) even as oxysterol-generating enzymes rise (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, and gene:MYLIP +1.28 as an LXR-responsive counter-brake). The predicted steady state is a sterol-overloaded, ester- and lysosome-laden APOE4 microglion that keeps behaving as if sterol-starved."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route sterol into esterified and lysosomal storage instead of ApoE-lipoprotein export, so the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool stays low and the uptake/distal-synthesis program is never switched off"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07436399217221135, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24602851640629209, "cosine_similarity": 0.38235694820004484, "direction_accuracy": 0.12459546925566344, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945695792880259, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07436399217221135, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24602851640629209, "cosine_similarity": 0.38235694820004484, "direction_accuracy": 0.12459546925566344, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945695792880259, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46724675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 144}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_091", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; every pathway statement here is a comparison of a gene set against the same selected background (global mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77.1% of rows positive), not against an unbiased zero baseline.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is not specified in the workbook and was not converted or assumed; only signs, relative ranks and set means on the reported scale are used.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity only. Enzyme activity, lysosomal acidification, protein localization, TFEB nuclear translocation and all metabolic fluxes in the mechanism are inferred, not measured.", "The 92 protein rows are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and none is used as supporting evidence for a specific enzyme.", "No lipid, sterol, lipid-droplet or efflux measurement is present in the supplied data; all lipid-pool statements are predictions.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; the RNA rows are assumed to represent the microglial compartment (10X Flex), and cell-state or cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed not to fully explain the module-level shifts.", "Absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR and SQLE from the rows is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change; the export-arm limitation is therefore an inference from what was measured plus background knowledge (unverified, no literature access)."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, above-background elevation of TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal transcripts (26/27 measured CLEAR genes up, set mean +3.26 vs global +1.39, permutation p=1e-4) together with lipid-uptake (SCARB1) and lipid-esterification/storage transcripts (9/9 up, p=0.033), while the measured lipid-export arm (APOE, ABCA7, PLTP) is only marginally changed and the canonical exporters are not in the supplied rows. We propose that the differentiating bottleneck is inferred flux of hydrolysis-derived lipid out of the endolysosome to the ER regulatory pool and to extracellular acceptors, so that APOE4 microglia route internalized lipid into an expanded acidic compartment and into esterified neutral-lipid stores instead of exporting it, and keep sterol-responsive synthesis/uptake genes de-repressed. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Imaging at day 30 mock: APOE4 microglia will contain more filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol colocalized with LAMP1 and more BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area per cell than isogenic APOE3. Equal or lower lysosomal sterol and neutral lipid in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation (egress vs degradation bottleneck): pulse-chase a traceable lipoprotein or [13C]-cholesteryl-ester load, then measure (a) rate of lysosomal hydrolysis of the label and (b) appearance of label in the ER-esterified fraction and in medium on ApoA-I/HDL acceptors, normalized to internalized label. The mechanism predicts APOE4 hydrolyses label at least as fast as APOE3 but exports a smaller fraction per unit internalized. If instead APOE4 accumulates undegraded substrate (sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide) with normal fractional export, the bottleneck is hydrolytic capacity, not egress, and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation (bypass the proposed bottleneck): 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or an LXR agonist that raises ABCA1/ABCG1-dependent export should reduce stored neutral lipid AND partially normalize the CLEAR/lysosomal and SREBP-target transcript elevation specifically in APOE4, with a smaller effect in APOE3. If stored lipid falls but the CLEAR and SREBP transcript elevations persist unchanged, the proposed feedback loop (steps 4-6) is falsified even if lipid storage differs.", "TFEB dependence: nuclear TFEB (or TFE3) should be higher in APOE4 microglia, and TFEB knockdown should collapse the coordinated hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript difference between genotypes. If nuclear TFEB is unchanged and TFEB knockdown does not shrink the genotype difference, step 1 is wrong and the module is more likely driven by cell-state composition or another factor.", "Specificity control: knocking down SCARB1 (or blocking scavenger-receptor lipid uptake) should reduce the APOE4-specific lysosomal lipid and neutral-lipid excess without abolishing the genotype difference in mitochondrial ETC transcripts. If ETC transcripts track the lipid rescue one-for-one, the OXPHOS program is more likely the primary driver and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Negative/counter-evidence check: the mechanism predicts that lysosomal hydrolase protein and activity assays (unambiguous, e.g. cathepsin B/D activity, GBA and acid sphingomyelinase activity) will be equal or higher in APOE4. A reproducible decrease in mature hydrolase protein or activity - consistent with the down-shifted 2D spots containing CTSD/CTSB/HEXB candidates - would weaken step 3 and point instead to a lysosomal-degradation-failure mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels across the CLEAR/lysosomal module - TFEB (gene:TFEB +2.38) and its target-type genes GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SGSH, MAN2B1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, LAMP1, SCARB2, CLCN7, RRAGD, SLC38A7 and ten v-ATPase subunits (10/10 up). Inference (not measured): increased TFEB-dependent transcription and an expanded, more acidified endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): lipid-uptake receptor transcripts are higher, dominated by gene:SCARB1 (+8.22) with smaller increases in CD36, LDLR, TREM2, MERTK, STAB1, COLEC12 and CD163. Inference: greater delivery of lipoprotein-, membrane- and debris-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): lipid-directed lysosomal hydrolase transcripts are among the largest increases in the module (SMPD1 +5.63, GBA +6.71, GBA2 +2.63, HEXA +5.68, HEXB +2.17, NAGLU +5.91, GAA +9.96). Inference: increased intralysosomal generation of free sterol, ceramide/sphingoid bases and fatty acid from internalized substrate.", "Step 4 (bottleneck; inferred flux, not measured): the export arm is not scaled to steps 2-3. The only measured efflux-associated transcripts (APOE +1.24, ABCA7 +2.14, PLTP +1.06) sit at or just above the selection threshold and are below the global up-shift median (+1.46), and ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1 and LIPA are absent from the supplied rows. We therefore propose that egress of hydrolysis-derived lipid from the lysosome (to ER and to extracellular acceptors) is the rate-limiting step that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3.", "Step 5 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred sink): esterification and neutral-lipid storage transcripts are uniformly up (AGPAT2 +6.29, SCP2 +5.95, MBOAT2 +3.26, LPCAT1 +3.07, MBOAT1 +2.65, DGAT1 +1.72, GPAT4 +1.58, SOAT1 +1.25, CIDEB +1.06). Inference: lipid that does reach the ER is preferentially esterified into cholesteryl ester/triacylglycerol stores rather than exported.", "Step 6 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred feedback): sterol- and lipogenesis-responsive transcripts remain elevated (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, ACAT2 +2.04, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, SREBF2 +1.06, ACSS2 +2.93, CH25H +1.62). Inference: the ER regulatory sterol pool is not replenished in proportion to total cellular lipid load, so synthesis/uptake stays partly de-repressed and reinforces loading. The parallel elevation of TCA/ETC subunit transcripts (37/37 measured NDUF/COX/ATP5/UQCR/SDH genes up, mean +2.81, permutation p=4e-4) is treated as a co-occurring energetic program, not as a causal step."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate a CLEAR/lysosomal-catabolic plus lipid-esterification transcriptional program without a matched lipid-export arm, making lysosomal lipid egress the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5738009083188715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25654345441839904, "cosine_similarity": 0.3822591255067501, "direction_accuracy": 0.5841423948220065, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5917831715210355, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5738009083188715, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25654345441839904, "cosine_similarity": 0.3822591255067501, "direction_accuracy": 0.5841423948220065, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5917831715210355, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.15777875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 145}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_113", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 genes up, median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base); all pathway claims are made relative to that internal background rather than to an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene from the list is not evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for compartment composition; hydrolase activity, luminal pH, lysosomal lipid content, degradative flux, and protein localization were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:053 is cited only as weak, ambiguous corroboration because it could equally reflect KRT1, TPM3, YWHAE or YWHAG.", "TFEB and MITF transcript elevation is assumed to reflect increased CLEAR-network output; TFEB activity is set mainly by dephosphorylation and nuclear translocation, which were not measured.", "The comparison is treated as isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 as stated in the metadata, so clone-, differentiation- and astrocyte-co-culture-derived ambient-RNA effects are assumed not to dominate; replicate numbers were not supplied and could not be checked.", "Sterol-biosynthesis transcript induction is assumed to report a low ER-accessible sterol pool rather than an independent growth or SREBF1-driven lipogenic demand.", "No lipidomic, imaging, or flux measurement is present despite the experiment identifier referring to lipid, so the lipid-retention step is entirely inferred."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly in endolysosomal cargo handling: the rate-limiting step is inferred to be export of sterol and sphingolipid catabolites out of the LAMP1+ lumen, not a shortage of hydrolase or V-ATPase transcript. Consistent with this, the selected differential-expression list shows a coherent, direction-consistent elevation of CLEAR-network transcripts (TFEB gene:TFEB +2.39, MITF gene:MITF +1.03; 49/53 curated lysosomal genes up, permutation p_mean=0.001, p_up=0.004 against the list's own strongly positive background), together with induction of SREBP-2/sterol-biosynthesis and re-esterification transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1), the transcriptional signature expected when the ER-accessible sterol pool is read as low while lipid is retained in an expanded degradative compartment. All statements are about measured RNA abundance in a pre-selected DE list; lysosomal lipid content, pH, hydrolase activity, and degradative flux were not measured here, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating mock APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression), which bypasses luminal sterol egress without altering uptake, should within 24-48 h reduce LAMP1-colocalized filipin/unesterified-cholesterol signal and normalize both SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24) and CLEAR transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, GBA, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels, with cargo internalization rate unchanged. If lysosomal cholesterol falls but SREBP-2 targets and CLEAR transcripts stay elevated, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong.", "Pulse-chase with fluorescently labelled myelin or acetylated LDL: APOE4 should show equal or higher initial internalization but slower decay of LAMP1-colocalized cargo and delayed appearance of cholesteryl ester. If APOE4 shows reduced internalization with normal per-lysosome clearance kinetics, the bottleneck lies at uptake and this mechanism is weakened (the strongly reduced gene:ACTB and gene:MYH9 transcripts make this alternative live).", "TFEB knockdown should selectively lower hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts and worsen lipid/cargo accumulation more in APOE4 than APOE3, identifying the CLEAR elevation as compensation. If TFEB knockdown leaves hydrolase transcripts unchanged, the proposed TFEB/MITF-dependent compensation step fails.", "Abundance-versus-activity test: despite higher V-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts, APOE4 lysosomal pH should be equal to or higher than APOE3 and bulk degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching, cathepsin B/D activity per LAMP1 volume) should not exceed APOE3. If APOE4 lysosomes are significantly more acidic with proportionally higher degradative flux and no cargo retention, the capacity-limitation claim is falsified.", "Specificity control: pharmacological SREBP-2 blockade (statin or fatuostatin) should suppress LDLR/HMGCS1/DHCR7 induction without normalizing CLEAR transcripts or lysosomal cargo retention; if it also normalizes CLEAR transcripts and lysosomal lipid, the causal order proposed here (retention upstream of sterol re-synthesis) is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_113", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4-associated lipoprotein/lipid cargo is delivered into the endolysosomal system at least as efficiently as in APOE3 (scavenging and phagocytic receptor transcripts are higher: gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24; uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured).", "Export of luminal catabolites (unesterified cholesterol, sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid breakdown products) to the ER/plasma membrane becomes the rate-limiting step, so cargo accumulates inside LAMP1+ compartments (inferred; the principal egress components NPC1, LIPA, PSAP and GRN are absent from the supplied list, and only gene:NPC2 +1.17 and gene:GM2A +2.01 are measured).", "Retained luminal load and altered lysosomal nutrient signalling activate the TFEB/MITF CLEAR program, raising transcripts for luminal hydrolases (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:GAA +9.96), V-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30) and membrane/transport components (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:CLCN7 +1.06, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ARL8B +1.12).", "This compensation expands hydrolytic capacity in transcript terms but does not relieve an export bottleneck, and it may be partly ineffective at the protein level: the mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript that routes newly made hydrolases is lower (gene:M6PR -1.72) while gene:IGF2R +2.02 moves oppositely, and spot-level protein measurements containing cathepsin candidates are mixed rather than uniformly up (protein_spot:053 +1.54).", "Because sterol is trapped in the degradative compartment rather than reaching the ER sensor pool, SREBP-2-type target transcripts and the sterol-synthesis arm are induced (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), together with a lipogenic/desaturase arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17).", "Newly available sterol and fatty acid are shunted into esterification/storage rather than efflux (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.72; the efflux transporter ABCA1 is absent from the supplied list), producing a futile uptake-synthesis-storage cycle and a lipid-laden, functionally saturated endolysosomal compartment.", "The net predicted cellular state is an expanded but flux-limited degradative system with reduced spare capacity for new cargo, accompanied by an activation-like microglial transcript profile (gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:FTH1 +2.54)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by post-hydrolytic lipid egress from late endosomes/lysosomes, driving a compensatory TFEB/MITF CLEAR program and sterol-sensing-driven re-synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2092568906783026, "cosine_similarity": 0.3819794528855171, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_113", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027540453074434, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2092568906783026, "cosine_similarity": 0.3819794528855171, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027540453074434, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.93638025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 146}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_031", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (1705 positive, 507 negative entries, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) drawn from two workbook columns; sign coherence of a program is therefore judged against a ~77% positive selected-list background, not 50/50. Genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, ACLY, FASN, PLIN2, ATF4, mitoribosome, TFAM) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook; effects are used only as ranks/directions on their original reported scale and are not converted. Protein spots are on a separate log2 scale.", "Transcript abundance is taken as evidence of capacity/allocation, not of enzymatic activity, metabolite flux, or organelle localization; acetyl-CoA, citrate, cholesterol, cholesteryl-ester and ATP pools were not measured.", "2D-gel spots carry 2-6 candidate identities; every candidate is retained. No spot is treated as confirmation of a named protein, and spot-level up/down changes are read only as compatibility tests.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some transcript differences may reflect microglia-astrocyte interaction or sorting purity rather than microglia-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied; adjusted p-values are taken as reported. Single-cell probe-based (10X Flex) quantification of mtDNA-encoded transcripts and composition-dependent normalization are unreliable, so the mitonuclear discordance in step 7 is weakly supported (6 genes, 2 discordant).", "Reduced oxidative or lysosomal reserve inferred for a future challenge is not asserted as an ongoing functional defect in the mock condition."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture), APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated cell-state change in substrate routing, not by inflammatory activation: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and for an expanded acidified degradative compartment are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, all 10 supplied ATP6V*/ATP6AP* subunits positive incl. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65), mitochondrial substrate-entry and oxidative machinery are coherently higher (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, 10/10 supplied TCA genes positive incl. gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, and 42/42 supplied nuclear-encoded ETC/assembly transcripts positive, median +2.64), upper-glycolytic commitment is selectively lower despite higher glucose transporters (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12 vs gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73), and the sterol/lipogenic program with esterification is uniformly higher (19/19 supplied members positive: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72). We claim increased routing/allocation of lipid- and glutamine-derived carbon through lysosomal catabolism and the TCA cycle toward citrate export and cytosolic sterol/fatty-acid re-synthesis and esterification; we do not claim that oxidative flux, cholesterol flux, degradation rate, or causality have been measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, 13C tracing plus respirometry should show a greater fraction of basal oxygen consumption and of TCA/citrate labelling derived from lysosome-released lipid/amino-acid carbon (13C-palmitate, 13C-glutamine) and a lower fraction of glucose carbon reaching lactate. If basal and maximal OCR, substrate preference and glucose-to-lactate flux are indistinguishable between genotypes, the routing claim is weakened to a capacity-only or transcript-level phenomenon.", "Discriminating perturbation: blocking lysosomal catabolism (bafilomycin A1 or lysosomal acid lipase inhibition) should, in APOE4 more than APOE3 (genotype x drug interaction), collapse the TCA/ETC and sterol-synthesis transcript program (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:NDUFA5, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24) and reduce newly synthesized/esterified sterol. If the APOE4 oxidative and sterol programs persist unchanged under lysosomal blockade, lysosome-to-mitochondria routing is not the driver.", "Citrate-export link: SLC25A1 (or ACLY) inhibition should selectively reduce APOE4-excess de novo sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and SOAT1-dependent cholesteryl-ester accumulation with comparatively little effect on oxygen consumption; no genotype-selective loss of sterol synthesis would falsify step 4.", "Failed-compensation discriminator: quantify mtDNA-encoded proteins (MT-CO1/MT-ATP6), assembled complex I/IV in-gel activity and an ISR readout (ATF4/ATF5/GDF15/MTHFD2). Proportional increases in assembled complexes without ISR induction support increased oxidative capacity/throughput; accumulation of unassembled nuclear subunits with ISR induction would favour the competing mitonuclear-imbalance mechanism over the routing mechanism.", "Storage readout: APOE4 microglia in mock should show more neutral-lipid droplets and cholesteryl ester per cell (LipidTOX/filipin, lipidomics) despite the higher synthesis program; equal or lower stored sterol would contradict the retention/storage step.", "Future-challenge only: after myelin, oxLDL or apoptotic-cell loading, APOE4 should show smaller spare respiratory capacity and slower cargo clearance than APOE3; an equal reserve would remove the challenge-revealed limitation predicted from the mtDNA-encoded transcript pattern without invalidating steps 1-6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (uptake/degradative capacity, measured as transcripts): APOE4 raises scavenger/lipoprotein-receptor and lysosomal transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12) together with a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-biogenesis module (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A, all supplied v-ATPase subunits, hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2), inferring an expanded acidified compartment for lipid/membrane catabolism.", "Step 2 (routing into mitochondria): catabolite carriers and mitochondrial import transcripts rise (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC38A7, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9), with glutamine/glutamate anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1), while upper-glycolytic commitment falls (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2) despite higher transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) - i.e. carbon entry is biased toward mitochondrial oxidation rather than glucose-to-lactate.", "Step 3 (oxidative capacity scaled up): the nuclear-encoded TCA and electron-transport program is raised coherently and with larger effects than the selected up-list background (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:ACO2, gene:PDP1, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS, gene:OXA1L, gene:COX20, gene:NDUFAF4), consistent with increased demand for oxidative processing of lysosome-derived substrate.", "Step 4 (citrate/NADPH export to cytosol): elevated gene:SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) with gene:MDH1, gene:ME1, gene:NNT and gene:SCP2 provides the inferred cytosolic acetyl-CoA and reducing-equivalent supply for lipid synthesis; the acetyl-CoA and citrate pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 5 (re-synthesis and storage instead of efflux): the SREBP-type sterol/fatty-acid program and esterification enzymes are uniformly higher (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) even though uptake transcripts are also higher; we infer that regulatory ER sterol is not repleted because sterol is retained in lysosomal/esterified pools (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:PLA2G7, gene:MGLL), with oxysterol disposal routes engaged (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1) and only a modest gene:APOE increase (+1.24); efflux transporters (ABCA1/ABCG1) were not supplied and remain unknown.", "Step 6 (state outcome, not inflammatory activation): the net APOE4 state is oxidative and lipid-storing; chemokine/innate transcripts are positive but with effects at or below the selected-list background (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL1 +1.59, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:NLRP3 +1.09; gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:CCL23 -2.51; gene:CTSS -5.57), so an inflammatory-glycolytic switch is not the leading explanation.", "Step 7 (limit on realized flux, partly future-challenge): mtDNA-encoded ETC transcripts do not scale with the nuclear program (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), so the raised nuclear transcripts may represent demanded capacity that exceeds assembled-complex output; this predicts reduced oxidative reserve under a future lipid or ETC challenge and does not by itself establish an ongoing defect in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-fed mitochondrial-oxidative state that re-routes internalized lipid carbon into sterol/lipid re-synthesis and storage instead of glycolysis or efflux"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09393346379647749, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2341459751589642, "cosine_similarity": 0.381802562082256, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885728155339806, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09393346379647749, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2341459751589642, "cosine_similarity": 0.381802562082256, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5885728155339806, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.277829, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 29}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_042", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway capacity only; no sterol, cholesteryl-ester, oxysterol, ER-accessible-cholesterol, SREBP2-cleavage, lysosomal-pH or flux measurement is supplied, so every statement about activity, flux, localisation and direction is inferred rather than observed.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a large global positive shift (median reported log fold change about +1.46; 77% of rows positive), so only relative, ordinal comparisons within the list are interpreted; the logarithm base is unspecified and effects are never exponentiated.", "Because of that global shift, 'sterol-synthesis transcripts are elevated' is read conservatively as 'not repressed relative to the rest of the selected list', not as demonstrated SREBP2 activation.", "Canonical rate-limiting SREBP2 targets (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, FDPS, CYP51A1) and the key trafficking/efflux genes (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, STARD3, STARD4, NR1H3) are absent from the supplied rows; their behaviour is assumed, not measured.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin-containing spots are treated only as weak, ambiguous corroboration of altered lysosomal protease content or processing, not as measurements of a named protein.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply cannot be separated from cell-autonomous microglial effects at this single day-30 mock timepoint.", "Very large absolute effects in this list come predominantly from rows with weaker adjusted p-values, so sparse high-magnitude genes are assumed less reliable than low-magnitude, very-low-p genes."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia run a higher-throughput lipid/lipoprotein scavenging-to-endolysosome route (transcripts for SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163, TREM2 and for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are higher than in APOE3), while transcripts for the ER esterification enzyme SOAT1 and for the SREBP2-dependent sterol-synthesis module (LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, EBP, SREBF2) are simultaneously higher rather than repressed. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not sterol acquisition or synthesis but delivery of liberated sterol to the ER-accessible regulatory pool: internalised sterol is inferred to be retained in the endolysosomal compartment and re-esterified by SOAT1 into cholesteryl-ester stores, so the SCAP/INSIG sensor continues to read a sterol-poor ER and keeps the uptake-plus-synthesis program on, generating a futile acquire-esterify-resynthesise cycle. Causality is not established by these data; the sterol pools, esterification flux and SREBP2 processing were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Direct pool test: quantitative lipidomics plus an ER/plasma-membrane accessible-cholesterol probe (ALOD4 or D4H) should show, in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3, a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio and more filipin/LipidSpot-positive LAMP1 compartments but an equal or LOWER accessible ER pool. If APOE4 shows an equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol pool, the central bottleneck claim is falsified.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (K-604 or avasimibe) should produce a genotype-by-drug interaction: a larger fall in cholesteryl esters, a larger rise in ER-accessible cholesterol, and a larger repression of LDLR, INSIG1 and HMGCS1 transcripts plus reduced nuclear SREBP2 in APOE4 than in APOE3. If the two genotypes respond identically, or if SREBP2 targets in APOE4 fail to fall, the esterification-diversion step is wrong.", "Acute sterol loading (LDL or cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin) should repress the SREBP2 module less in APOE4 than in APOE3 (blunted repression of LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1 and of SREBP2 cleavage). Normal, equal repression in APOE4 would falsify the sensing-insufficiency step.", "Occlusion test with the NPC1-pathway inhibitor U18666A: if endolysosomal sterol egress is already limiting in APOE4, U18666A should shift APOE3 toward the APOE4 phenotype while adding little further change in APOE4 (sub-additive interaction). A fully additive effect in APOE4 would argue that egress is not the operative bottleneck and would favour a simple lysosomal-biogenesis or identity-shift explanation.", "SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade should reduce lysosomal neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation and lower GPNMB/LGALS3/ACP5 transcripts more in APOE4 than in APOE3. No genotype difference would weaken the scavenging-influx step.", "Specificity control: forcing sterol out of storage with a liver-X-receptor agonist plus apoA-I acceptors should normalise the APOE4 transcript state; if instead the scavenger/lysosomal program persists unchanged while esters fall, the program is driven by something other than sterol load (for example the reduced gene:TGFBR1 identity axis)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid scavenging receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2) and for the APOE/PLTP lipid-particle machinery (gene:APOE, gene:PLTP). Inferred, not measured: increased flux of lipoprotein-borne cholesteryl ester and membrane lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Measured: higher transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, acidification subunits and CLEAR-network regulators (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:TFEB), together with a lipid-laden macrophage marker set (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ACP5). Inferred: expanded degradative compartment where internalised sterol esters are hydrolysed.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred, not measured): egress of liberated free sterol from the limiting membrane of that compartment to the ER-accessible/regulatory pool is rate-limiting in APOE4; the sterol therefore accumulates in endolysosomal and ester stores rather than reaching the SCAP/INSIG sensor.", "Measured: gene:SOAT1 is one of the most statistically robust increases in the dataset. Inferred: increased ER-localised acyl-CoA:cholesterol acyltransferase activity re-esterifies whatever free sterol does reach the ER, further lowering the regulatory free-sterol pool and consolidating cholesteryl-ester storage.", "Consequence (inferred causal direction): because the ER sensor reads sterol-poor, SREBP2 processing is not switched off, so synthesis and uptake transcripts stay elevated (gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:SREBF2), coexisting with the storage program instead of being reciprocally repressed.", "Parallel oxysterol arm (measured transcripts only): gene:CH25H and gene:CYP27A1 are higher, and the LXR-responsive genes gene:MYLIP and gene:ABCA7 are higher, indicating that some sterol is diverted to oxysterol/efflux-signalling rather than to the ER pool; ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not supplied, so net efflux capacity is untested.", "Net predicted cell state: chronic cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal lipid load with persistent uptake and synthesis drive, accompanied by loss of homeostatic TGF-beta receptor signalling capacity (gene:TGFBR1 is the strongest decrease in the dataset) and a scavenger/lipid-handling identity shift."], "title": "SOAT1-biased esterification and endolysosomal sequestration starve the ER regulatory sterol pool in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12873389210944133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2504924039408132, "cosine_similarity": 0.38159861215212687, "direction_accuracy": 0.1650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5893462783171521, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12873389210944133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2504924039408132, "cosine_similarity": 0.38159861215212687, "direction_accuracy": 0.1650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5893462783171521, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60175875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 147}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_024", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so pathway comparisons are made against the internal background of that list (median +1.46) and not against an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and is left unconverted.", "The strong global positive skew (77% of rows positive) reflects at least partly a normalisation/composition or selection asymmetry; only sets exceeding this internal background (nuclear OXPHOS, shuttles, lipogenesis) are treated as informative.", "Only six mtDNA-encoded rows are present and two are positive; the mitonuclear gap is therefore assumed, not established, and low mtDNA transcript counts may also reflect 10X Flex probe design or ambient-RNA handling rather than true mtDNA expression.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme and carrier protein abundance; assembled complex amount, PDH phosphorylation state, carrier flux, citrate compartmentation and lipid content were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:038 lists ALDOA/ALDOC/SORD/ARPC1B/TKT; protein_spot:072 lists PGAM1 and four others); they are used only as weak, non-identifying consistency checks, never as identified proteins.", "Astrocyte co-culture means substrate supply (lactate, lipids, cholesterol) is non-cell-autonomous, and no medium or flux measurement was supplied.", "APOE4-vs-APOE3 is treated as isogenic per the supplied metadata; replicate number was not supplied, so effect-size precision is unknown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional build-up of nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, pyruvate-import and malate-aspartate-shuttle components without a matching supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits; we hypothesise that this mitonuclear mismatch, not a glycolytic (Warburg-type) switch, is the primary bottleneck, so that carbon entering mitochondria as pyruvate and glutamate is only partially oxidised and is instead exported as citrate (SLC25A1) to feed an SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 lipogenic and sterol-esterifying program, producing the excess neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet load of APOE4 microglia. All statements are correlational; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1: knockdown or pharmacological inhibition of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (or of ACLY downstream) in APOE4 microglia should lower neutral-lipid/droplet content and 13C-glucose- and 13C-glutamine-derived label in palmitate/oleate toward APOE3 levels, without normalising the nuclear OXPHOS transcript excess. If APOE4 lipid excess is unchanged by SLC25A1/ACLY blockade, the citrate-export limb is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation 2: forcing oxidative ATP production by replacing glucose with galactose should preferentially reduce APOE4 ATP, growth or viability relative to APOE3 if terminal oxidation is the bottleneck; equal or better APOE4 performance in galactose would falsify the bottleneck assignment.", "Mitonuclear test: quantitative protein measurement (targeted MS or immunoblot) plus BN-PAGE should show, in APOE4, higher nuclear-encoded subunits (e.g. NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) but equal or lower mtDNA-encoded MT-CO1/MT-ND1 and equal or lower assembled complex I/IV, i.e. an increased nuclear:mtDNA-encoded ratio at protein level. Proportional increases in mtDNA-encoded protein and assembled complexes would weaken the mechanism.", "Flux prediction: Seahorse profiling should show APOE4 maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) respiration and spare respiratory capacity increased less than, or not at all in proportion to, the nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase, with no increase in glycolytic ECAR (consistent with gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP being negative). A clear APOE4 glycolytic (high ECAR, low OCR) phenotype would falsify the substrate-routing claim.", "Unmeasured-modality prediction: lipidomics of the same APOE4 cultures should show increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester with an elevated 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 desaturation index (SCD signature) and altered glucosyl-/sphingomyelin species; absence of neutral-lipid excess or of an SCD desaturation signature would weaken the lipogenic output limb.", "Specificity control: markers of inflammatory activation, interferon signalling and phagocytic receptors are not enriched above the internal background in this dataset; if the APOE4 lipid phenotype is instead abolished by NF-kB or interferon blockade while SLC25A1/SCD blockade has no effect, this metabolic mechanism should be rejected in favour of an inflammatory one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (37/37 detected NDUF*/UQCR*/COX*/ATP5* rows positive, median +2.65 in the reported log unit vs +1.46 for the whole selected DE list) and for mitochondrial protein-import components (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:CHCHD3).", "Step 2 (measured abundance, opposite direction): mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are mostly lower in APOE4 (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 negative; gene:MT-ND4L, gene:MT-ND5 positive), giving a ~4-unit median nuclear-minus-mitochondrial gap.", "Step 3 (inferred activity/flux, not measured): because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded core subunits, the nuclear surplus cannot be converted into proportionally more assembled, electron-transporting holoenzyme; assembled complex number and maximal electron flux, not enzyme mRNA, become the rate-limiting step.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): carbon delivery to mitochondria is nonetheless up-wired - pyruvate carrier gene:MPC2, PDH-activating phosphatase gene:PDP1 and gene:DLD, TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB), glutamine/glutamate route (gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1) and cytosolic malate-aspartate arms (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11) - while upper glycolysis and the oxidative pentose-phosphate arm are not coherently induced (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1 negative despite gene:SLC2A1 and gene:SLC2A3 positive), arguing against a glycolytic switch.", "Step 5 (inferred flux/localisation): with terminal oxidation capped, matrix NADH/acetyl-CoA and citrate accumulate; citrate is exported through the elevated carrier gene:SLC25A1 to the cytosol, supplemented by acetate-derived acetyl-CoA (gene:ACSS2).", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred causal direction): cytosolic acetyl-CoA and an induced SREBP program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1) raise desaturation and esterification capacity (gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) plus sterol synthesis (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS), while lipid uptake/scavenging is high (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2).", "Step 7 (inferred phenotype, unmeasured here): the combination of restricted oxidative disposal, elevated esterification and elevated lysosomal lipid-hydrolase transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB) yields net storage of monounsaturated triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in droplets and altered sphingolipid handling in APOE4 microglia."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch caps terminal oxidation in APOE4 microglia and reroutes pyruvate/glutamine carbon through citrate export into SREBF1-driven lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15557729941291584, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18661612673147293, "cosine_similarity": 0.3814790521705076, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5750582524271846, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15557729941291584, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18661612673147293, "cosine_similarity": 0.3814790521705076, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5750582524271846, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.620064, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 148}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_152", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong positive global shift (77% positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified log base), so only effects compared with that median are treated as informative; the log base is preserved and not converted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme abundance and pathway capacity; no protein, flux, localization or sterol-pool measurement for DHCR24, SREBP-1, SCARB1 or LXR targets is present in these data.", "Desmosterol, cholesterol, cholesteryl ester and lipid-droplet pools are unmeasured here and are inferred, not observed.", "ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3/NR1H2, HMGCR, SQLE and most mevalonate genes are absent from the supplied rows; their absence is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and contain no sterol-pathway candidate, so the protein layer neither supports nor refutes the sterol steps and is not used as identification evidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein lipid, so uptake-dependent steps are assumed to have available substrate.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment is assumed to drive the differences; batch/composition confounding in single-cell differential expression cannot be excluded."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 cells show a coordinated transcriptional shift at the distal (post-lanosterol) sterol-reduction step (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS above the strongly positive global RNA median) together with a high SREBP-1 lipogenic module (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, ACSS2) and a very high lipoprotein/cholesteryl-ester uptake receptor transcript (SCARB1), whereas SREBF2 and the mevalonate module are not elevated. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node is the ER sterol-sensing set point: increased DHCR24-catalysed conversion of desmosterol to cholesterol removes the desmosterol-dependent brake on SREBP-1 processing and on LXR-driven efflux gene expression, so sterol and acetyl-CoA carbon entering the cell are channelled into monounsaturated glycerolipid and cholesteryl-ester storage inside an expanded lysosomal compartment instead of into exported/effluxed lipid. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Sterol GC-MS/lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a lower desmosterol/cholesterol ratio and a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio with enrichment of 18:1-containing esters in APOE4. Equal or higher desmosterol fraction in APOE4 would weaken the central node.", "Pharmacological DHCR24 inhibition (e.g. SH-42 or triparanol) in APOE4 microglia should raise desmosterol, induce LXR targets (ABCA1, ABCG1, APOE), lower SREBF1/SCD transcripts and reduce cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet load toward APOE3 levels. If desmosterol rises but LXR targets, SCD and neutral-lipid load are unchanged, the desmosterol-brake mechanism is falsified.", "Ordering test: SCD inhibition or knockdown in APOE4 should reduce MUFA-rich droplet lipid without restoring desmosterol or LXR target expression, whereas DHCR24 inhibition should move both. If SCD inhibition also restores desmosterol/LXR targets, the proposed hierarchy is wrong.", "SCARB1 blockade or knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce lipoprotein-derived cholesteryl-ester accumulation without changing DHCR24 transcript or desmosterol, separating the influx arm from the sensing arm; no reduction in cholesteryl ester would remove the uptake step from the mechanism.", "Immunoblot/immunofluorescence should show a higher nuclear (cleaved) SREBP-1 fraction in APOE4 than APOE3 despite comparable or lower SREBP-2 processing. Equal nuclear SREBP-1 with equal SREBP-2 would show the SREBF1 transcript change does not reach pathway activity and would weaken the mechanism.", "13C-acetate tracing should show increased label incorporation into monounsaturated fatty acids and cholesteryl esters in APOE4, with de novo cholesterol synthesis flux not proportionally increased (consistent with an unchanged SREBF2/mevalonate arm). Proportionally increased de novo cholesterol synthesis flux would favour a simple SREBP-2 upregulation model instead.", "LXR agonism (GW3965) should normalise cholesteryl-ester and droplet load in APOE4 without altering DHCR24 expression; failure to normalise would indicate the storage phenotype is not efflux-limited."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_152", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for the distal sterol-reduction enzymes DHCR24 (+3.69), DHCR7 (+2.71) and LSS (+2.27) are above the global RNA median (+1.46) for these selected differential-expression rows; SREBF2 (+1.06, 28th percentile) and the pre-squalene mevalonate genes are not elevated or not present.", "Inferred (activity/flux, not measured): higher DHCR24 protein activity increases flux from desmosterol to cholesterol, lowering the steady-state desmosterol pool at the ER.", "Inferred (signalling): loss of desmosterol, an ER sterol that both restrains SCAP/SREBP processing and acts as an endogenous LXR ligand, raises the fraction of SREBP-1 that is processed to its nuclear form and lowers LXR-dependent efflux/apolipoprotein output; measured correlates are high SREBF1 (+4.67, 92nd pct) with only median-level APOE (38th pct), MYLIP (41st pct) and SOAT1 (39th pct).", "Measured downstream of that node: the SREBP-1 lipogenic output transcripts SCD (+4.17, 89th pct), AGPAT2 (+6.29, 97th pct) and ACSS2 (+2.93, 77th pct) are coherently high, predicting (inferred) increased monounsaturated fatty-acid and glycerolipid synthesis; INSIG1 (+1.87) is consistent with an active, feedback-engaged SREBP axis.", "Measured in parallel: SCARB1 (+8.22, 99th percentile, adj p 3.4e-117) implies (inferred) increased selective uptake of lipoprotein cholesteryl ester, providing exogenous sterol load that is not offset by any measured increase in efflux machinery (ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured).", "Measured: a strong lysosomal hydrolase/biogenesis signature (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, TFEB all \u003e69th pct) indicates (inferred) an expanded, lipid-loaded endolysosomal compartment in which delivered lipoprotein lipid is hydrolysed and re-esterified rather than exported.", "Net inferred cellular phenotype: APOE4 microglia sit at a lower desmosterol/cholesterol ratio with a higher cholesteryl-ester and MUFA-rich neutral-lipid burden than APOE3, i.e. a storage-biased rather than efflux-biased sterol economy."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose the distal-sterol (desmosterol) brake on SREBP-1 lipogenesis while retaining high lipoprotein-sterol influx, diverting sterol into esterified storage rather than efflux-competent free cholesterol"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22564295708973817, "cosine_similarity": 0.38123019106631845, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_152", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5846699029126214, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22564295708973817, "cosine_similarity": 0.38123019106631845, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5846699029126214, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5391145, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 149}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_084", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so pathway claims are made only relative to the internal list background (median +1.46, 77% positive in an unspecified logarithm base), not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance for MPC2, PDH-regulatory and ETC genes is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding proteins and their transport/catalytic capacity; no protein or flux measurement of these components is supplied.", "The lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to reflect genuine biology (mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial transcription or transcript stability) rather than an artefact of probe-based 10X Flex capture, ambient-RNA correction or high-mito-fraction cell filtering.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; no spot is assumed to report a specific enzyme's abundance.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies a comparable extracellular substrate environment (glucose, lactate, glutamine, lipid) to both genotypes, so genotype effects are cell-intrinsic rather than driven by differing medium composition.", "Mock-treated day-30 cells are near steady state, so transcript ratios reflect a maintained metabolic configuration rather than a transient response."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 is associated with a coordinate transcript increase in mitochondrial carbon-import and TCA machinery (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, ACO2, OGDH, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A1/A11/A13) and in nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (38/38 measured positive, median +2.64 vs +1.46 list background), while the mtDNA-encoded core subunits MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB and MT-ND4 are lower. We hypothesise that the limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for holo-complex assembly: pyruvate and glutamine carbon delivery to the matrix rises faster than oxidative capacity, so APOE4 microglia run a mitochondrially committed but respiration-capped state in which surplus carbon leaves as citrate for SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1-directed lipid synthesis and esterification, with reduced cytosolic PPP support (TALDO1, PGD lower). All statements refer to measured RNA and protein-spot abundances; flux, activity, localisation and direction of causation are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should reduce basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption and reduce 13C-glucose-derived M+2 citrate and M+2/M+4 lipid labelling substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia; if APOE4 oxygen consumption and glucose-derived citrate labelling are no more MPC-dependent than APOE3, Step 1-2 and the carbon-rerouting claim are weakened.", "Mitonuclear bottleneck test: APOE4 microglia should show lower mtDNA copy number and/or lower mtDNA-encoded protein and lower assembled complex I/III/IV/V by BN-PAGE and lower maximal (FCCP-stimulated) respiration per unit mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 or citrate synthase normalised), despite higher nuclear-encoded subunit transcripts; equal assembled complex levels and equal maximal respiration per mitochondrial mass would refute the chosen bottleneck and favour a simple 'more mitochondria' interpretation.", "Overflow test: [U-13C]glucose and [U-13C]glutamine tracing should show, in APOE4, a higher fraction of TCA intermediates labelled from glutamine, higher labelled citrate exported into fatty acid and cholesteryl-ester pools, and unchanged or lower labelled lactate output per glucose consumed; increased lactate output with unchanged citrate-to-lipid labelling would weaken Steps 3-5.", "PPP vulnerability test: APOE4 microglia should have lower oxidative PPP flux ([1,2-13C]glucose CO2/lactate labelling ratio) and lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio, and should lose viability or accumulate lipid peroxidation faster than APOE3 under G6PD inhibition or glutamine withdrawal; equal PPP flux and equal sensitivity would refute Step 6 without necessarily refuting Steps 1-3.", "Rescue test: restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (for example by increasing mitochondrial transcription/translation capacity or by cybrid-style mtDNA complementation) should raise maximal respiration and lower neutral-lipid accumulation in APOE4 without reversing the nuclear TCA/ETC transcript increase; a rescue that also normalises the nuclear transcript program would indicate that the nuclear increase is a downstream compensation and would require reordering the mechanism.", "Protein-level test: two-dimensional spot ambiguity should be resolved by targeted immunoblot or targeted MS; TALDO1 protein should be lower in APOE4 in line with gene:TALDO1, whereas confirmation that TALDO1 protein is genuinely increased in the spots reported as up (protein_spot:043) would contradict Step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and PDH activation (gene:MPC2 +7.98, padj 2.6e-51; gene:PDP1; gene:DLD) together with higher glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) despite lower gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP, i.e. transporter-level glucose entry is not the constrained node.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): increased MPC2/PDH-activating machinery plus increased amino-acid entry and anaplerosis transcripts (gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1) is predicted to raise carbon delivery into the TCA cycle, matched by coordinate TCA transcript increases (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3G, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) and mitochondrial carriers (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13) that support citrate export and the malate-aspartate shuttle.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, partly inferred): nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts rise coherently (gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B) while mtDNA-encoded core subunits fall (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4); we infer a mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch that caps the number of assembled, functional complexes I, III, IV and V per unit of imported nuclear subunit and per unit of delivered carbon.", "Step 4 (inferred consequence): with matrix NADH input exceeding assembled ETC capacity, redox load is buffered by shuttle and NADPH/antioxidant components whose transcripts are increased (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:ME1, gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3) rather than by proportionately increased oxygen consumption.", "Step 5 (inferred carbon overflow): citrate exported by SLC25A1 supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA that, with the increased lipogenic/esterification program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) and APOE4-associated lipid handling transcripts (gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), is predicted to be stored as neutral lipid instead of fully oxidised.", "Step 6 (inferred vulnerability): reduced non-oxidative/oxidative PPP transcripts (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD) predict lower cytosolic NADPH and ribose regeneration capacity, so APOE4 microglia should depend disproportionately on mitochondrial NADPH sources and be sensitised when ETC or glutamine input is blocked."], "title": "APOE4 microglia commit glucose- and glutamine-derived carbon to mitochondria while mtDNA-encoded ETC core subunits lag, making assembled respiratory-chain capacity the bottleneck and diverting citrate to lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2880409286931597, "cosine_similarity": 0.3811983467845672, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5985145631067961, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2880409286931597, "cosine_similarity": 0.3811983467845672, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5985145631067961, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.44658725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 150}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effects is constant across rows, so only relative ranks within the list are used; every gene is judged against the list median of +1.46 rather than against zero, because 77.1% of the 2212 rows are positive (binomial p ~1e-150) and this global shift may be biological RNA-content difference or a normalisation/composition artefact.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome, so percentile ranks describe position within this biased list and are not enrichment statistics for the genome.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding transport and hydrolase capacity; no sterol pool, transfer flux, esterification rate, localisation or protein level of any sterol gene was measured here.", "Protein spots 052 and 053 have five-gene candidate lists (ACTB, CTSL, TPM3, CLIC1, NT5C1A and TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1); they are treated only as weak, non-identifying support for increased abundance of some cathepsin-containing species, and other spots whose candidate lists include CTSD, CTSB, HEXB or ATP6V1E1 move in the opposite direction.", "The cells are co-cultured with astrocytes and S100B is +6.00 in the RNA list, so some measured RNA may derive from or be contaminated by the astrocyte partner rather than microglia.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, STARD3, GRAMD1/Aster family, HMGCR, SQLE) are absent from the supplied list, so the egress deficit is inferred from the genes that are present."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) show a coordinated transcriptional increase in lipoprotein-sterol uptake (SCARB1) and in lysosomal acidification and luminal hydrolase capacity (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) that is far above the strong global positive shift of this differential-expression list, whereas the transcripts for non-vesicular sterol transfer and acceptor-mediated export (OSBPL8, OSBPL1A, NPC2, APOE, ABCA7, SOAT1, MYLIP) sit at or below that global shift. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 is delivery of endolysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER regulatory pool and to extracellular acceptors, not sterol synthesis; the predicted consequence is retention of sterol in a LAMP1-positive acidic compartment with compensatory SREBP-1-driven fatty-acid/membrane remodelling (SREBF1, SCD, LPCAT1, FADS1) rather than a proportionate SREBP-2 cholesterogenic response (SREBF2, HMGCS1, EBP, LDLR all at or below the list median). Sterol pools, transfer flux, protein levels of these genes and causal direction were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute SCARB1 blockade (BLT-1 or SCARB1 knockdown, 24-48 h, mock conditions) should lower filipin- or D4H-detectable cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments and lower cholesteryl-ester content in APOE4 microglia significantly more than in isogenic APOE3, without requiring any change in the lysosomal hydrolase transcripts. If SCARB1 loss leaves the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal sterol and cholesteryl-ester difference unchanged, the uptake-driven inflow step is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: relieving the egress block with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or by re-expressing an ER-directed sterol transfer protein should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, redistribute sterol out of LAMP1-positive compartments and suppress the residual SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR) while leaving SCARB1 high. Equal suppression in both genotypes, or no redistribution, weakens the bottleneck placement.", "Lipidomic prediction: mock APOE4 microglia should show a higher cholesteryl-ester-to-free-cholesterol ratio and higher lysosome-enriched free cholesterol and sphingomyelin-derived ceramide than APOE3, together with a raised 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 desaturation index consistent with the SREBF1/SCD arm. Finding no sterol or cholesteryl-ester difference while the desaturation index is raised would reduce this to a fatty-acid remodelling mechanism and falsify the sterol framing.", "Sensing prediction: the ER-accessible sterol pool reported by an ALOD4/ANTH-type probe should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite higher total cellular sterol. If the ER-accessible pool is higher in APOE4, the proposed low-ER-sterol explanation for the flat SREBP-2 arm is falsified.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot or targeted proteomics should confirm increased SCARB1, ATP6V1 subunit and mature cathepsin B/D protein in APOE4 with unchanged or reduced OSBPL8 protein. Increased OSBPL8 protein, or unchanged SCARB1 protein despite the large transcript effect, would weaken the mechanism.", "Negative control: bafilomycin-A1 de-acidification should not further increase the APOE4-specific lysosomal sterol excess if retention is caused by an egress bottleneck downstream of liberation; a large further increase would favour an upstream hydrolysis-limited model instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SCARB1 transcript is the 99th-percentile change of the supplied list (+8.22 in the reported log unit, padj 3.4e-117) and LDLR is present (+1.50). Inferred: APOE4 microglia have greater capacity for selective uptake of lipoprotein cholesteryl ester and whole-particle uptake, raising sterol flux into the endolysosomal system (flux not measured).", "Measured: v-ATPase subunit transcripts (ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51) and luminal hydrolase transcripts (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86) are all above the 75th percentile of the list, with TFEB +2.38 and RAB7A +2.65. Inferred: an expanded, more acidic and more hydrolytically loaded late-endosome/lysosome compartment, including higher acid sphingomyelinase and glucocerebrosidase capacity that liberates free cholesterol from sphingolipid-rich luminal membranes (activity and compartment volume not measured).", "Measured: transcripts encoding routes out of that compartment are not scaled with it - OSBPL8 is absolutely decreased (-1.90, 12.7th percentile, padj 3.7e-33), and OSBPL1A (+1.03, 25.6th pct), NPC2 (+1.17, 34.7th pct), APOE (+1.24, 38.3rd pct), SOAT1 (+1.25, 39.4th pct), MYLIP (+1.28, 40.8th pct) and ABCA7 (+2.14, 65th pct) all lie at or below the list median of +1.46. Inferred bottleneck: ER-contact-site sterol transfer and apolipoprotein/transporter-mediated efflux become rate-limiting relative to inflow and luminal liberation.", "Inferred consequence: unesterified cholesterol is retained in the acidic compartment and the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool is not proportionately raised, so the SREBP-2 cholesterogenic arm stays near baseline (SREBF2 +1.06 at the 27.5th pct, HMGCS1 +1.08 at 28.3rd pct, EBP +1.34, LDLR +1.50 at the median) despite the increased inflow. This pool was not measured.", "Measured: the SREBP-1/monounsaturated-lipid arm is instead high (SREBF1 +4.67, 92nd pct; SCD +4.17, 89th pct; LPCAT1 +3.07, 79th pct; FADS1 +1.59; MGLL +4.00; DGAT1 +1.72; DHCR24 +3.69). Inferred: APOE4 microglia compensate by remodelling membrane and neutral-lipid composition toward monounsaturated species and triacylglycerol rather than by exporting sterol.", "Inferred systems-level outcome: a self-reinforcing lipid-storage state in which continued SCARB1-driven inflow plus limited egress produces lysosomal sterol/sphingolipid retention and cytosolic lipid droplets, which is the lipid phenotype expected to differentiate APOE4 from APOE3 at day 30 under mock treatment. Causality has not been established by these data."], "title": "Sterol egress from an expanded acidic hydrolytic compartment is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: uptake and luminal catabolism scale up while ER/acceptor-directed sterol export does not"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.31829007126241554, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25277211257702725, "cosine_similarity": 0.3808278514167938, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6031521035598706, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.31829007126241554, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25277211257702725, "cosine_similarity": 0.3808278514167938, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6031521035598706, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72067375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 151}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All functional annotations and causal links are unverified background knowledge; no literature or databases were consulted. The observations measure RNA expression and protein-spot abundance, not genomic variants. Positive effects mean higher in APOE4; every RNA number retains the unspecified reported logarithm base. The RNA background is a selected list with 77.08% positive rows, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence is unknown and panel coherence is not enrichment.", "The proposed change is greater ongoing basal throughput with adequate acidification in the supplied mock condition, not merely reduced reserve under a future overload. Translation, hydrolase maturation, localization and assembly must support the RNA program. Higher TFEB RNA does not establish TFEB activation or identify it as the unique cause. Comparable viable-cell normalization and separation of microglial effects from co-culture composition/signaling are required.", "Protein evidence is ambiguous and does not establish individual enzyme abundance or activity. All CTSD-candidate spots and their complete candidate sets are: protein_spot:027 +0.585 [ACTG1, ACTA1, CTSD, ST13P4, BCAT1]; protein_spot:053 +1.536 [TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1]; protein_spot:058 -0.848 [CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1]; protein_spot:060 +0.678 [ACTB, CTSD, KRT1, RBPMS2, GSTO1]; protein_spot:066 +0.000 [ACTB, ACTBL2, ARHGDIB, PDPR, CTSD]; protein_spot:069 -1.379 [ACTB, CTSD, GPS2]; protein_spot:070 +0.138 [CTSD, ACTB, CAPG, CLPP, PGLS]; protein_spot:090 -0.263 [COTL1, KRT1, KRT10, KRT9, CTSD]. Their opposite directions could reflect co-migrants or protein forms; no maturation state is assigned.", "The strongest contrary spot evidence is: protein_spot:064 -1.202 [ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1]; protein_spot:065 -0.926 [ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART]; protein_spot:075 -0.138 [SOD2, VPS29, CAP1, RAP1B, ATP6V1H]. All effects here are log2 spot abundance changes. These decreases could indicate compromised acidification, but cannot be assigned to pump subunits. Failed compensation remains plausible until basal pH and flux are measured.", "No cargo accumulation, cholesterol, esterified lipid, ATP, lysosomal pH, organelle mass or respiration was measured. The nuclear/mitochondrial RNA discordance is unexplained, and the metabolic program could precede or independently accompany lysosomal remodeling. Replicates and baseline abundances were not supplied; causality has not been established."], "claim": "Under day-30 mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture, APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia are hypothesized to adopt a cargo-processing state in which increased acquisition and endosomal delivery are matched by expanded functional lysosomal capacity, raising basal substrate recovery and downstream lipid esterification. The ATP cost of processing contributes to the associated mitochondrial transcriptional program. This is a tentative causal model; abundance measurements do not establish successful throughput.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline test: in matched day-30 mock co-cultures, quantify calibrated lysosomal pH, acidified compartment volume, mature hydrolase activity and cargo turnover per viable microglial cell. The mechanism predicts increased functional processing capacity and basal turnover with maintained acidic pH; pH need not be lower than APOE3. Tracer-dose pulse-chases that do not materially increase cargo load should show preserved or faster clearance per unit internalized cargo and greater per-cell cargo-derived sterol exit/esterification. Slower uptake-normalized clearance with retention and impaired acidification would weaken successful adaptation.", "Prospective causal perturbation: inducibly reduce RAB7A-dependent late-endosomal delivery in both genotypes, verify the routing block, control viability and initial cargo entry, and include an RNAi-resistant rescue. The mechanism predicts loss of the APOE4 excess in cargo degradation and cargo-derived lipid esterification; rescue should restore it. Persistence of those differences despite a verified delivery block would weaken the proposed routing-to-recycling link and favor an independent source such as synthesis. A generic reduction in both genotypes alone would not discriminate the mechanism.", "Prospective discrimination from failed compensation: measure basal pH and clearance before attempting a calibrated lysosome-targeted acidification rescue toward the APOE3 pH range, while holding cargo entry constant. The selected mechanism predicts no pre-existing APOE4 acidification deficit whose correction selectively unlocks stalled basal processing. A documented APOE4 pH defect, slow basal degradation and selective flux restoration upon acidification would strongly weaken it. A phenotype seen only after high cargo loading would instead describe reserve and would not establish a defect in mock conditions.", "Prospective downstream test: during a short, verified reduction of cargo delivery that preserves mitochondrial integrity, measure the cargo-dependent component of oxygen consumption/ATP demand alongside processing flux. Loss of the APOE4 processing advantage should reduce its associated energetic demand. Unchanged excess energetic demand despite suppressed processing would weaken the proposed lysosome-to-metabolic-demand connection, without alone disproving increased lysosomal capacity."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Under day-30 mock co-culture, APOE4 is proposed to shift microglia toward greater basal cargo acquisition. Higher receptor-associated RNAs gene:TREM2 (+1.28), gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:SCARB1 (+8.22) and gene:LDLR (+1.50) motivate this inference; receptor activity and uptake were not measured. No unique initiating gene is identified.", "Greater cargo entry is proposed to be matched by delivery to degradative compartments and hydrolase targeting. Supporting RNA increases are gene:RAB7A (+2.65), gene:IGF2R (+2.02), gene:GNPTG (+3.02) and gene:AP5M1 (+9.78). This routing inference is qualified by lower gene:M6PR (\u22121.72) and gene:SPG11 (\u22121.83), which could limit successful delivery.", "Coordinated expression is proposed to expand functional, acidified lysosomal capacity under mock conditions: gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:LAMP1 (+1.38), gene:CLCN7 (+1.06), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.23), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.70) and gene:ATP6V1H (+6.88) accompany gene:CTSD (+2.86), gene:CTSB (+5.52), gene:GBA (+6.71), gene:SMPD1 (+5.63), gene:HEXA (+5.68) and gene:GAA (+9.96). If translated, matured and correctly localized, this machinery could maintain acidic processing while increasing total cargo degradation. TFEB nuclear activity, lysosomal volume and proton pumping are unmeasured; decreased gene:CTSS (\u22125.57) and gene:IDS (\u22121.56) preclude uniform hydrolase activation.", "Successful processing is proposed to increase basal recovery and routing of cargo-derived substrates. Higher gene:NPC2 (+1.17) is compatible with lysosomal sterol transfer, while gene:SOAT1 (+1.25) and gene:DGAT1 (+1.72) suggest downstream esterification capacity. Increased lysosomal exit and cargo-derived esterification are predictions, not observed lipid pools. Higher gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:DHCR7 (+2.71) and gene:DHCR24 (+3.69) show that synthesis could also contribute; lysosomal recovery need not be the sole substrate source.", "ATP consumption by enhanced trafficking and proton pumping is proposed to help couple this cargo-processing state to mitochondrial capacity transcription: gene:MPC2 (+7.98), gene:OGDH (+8.56), gene:NDUFA5 (+7.34), gene:COX5B (+2.33) and gene:ATP5F1B (+2.65). This demand-driven connection predicts an energetic cost of ongoing processing, without establishing respiratory flux. Lower gene:MT-ATP6 (\u22123.35), gene:MT-CO2 (\u22121.33), gene:MT-CYB (\u22122.32) and gene:MT-ND4 (\u22121.80) remain a serious unresolved challenge."], "title": "Coordinated endolysosomal expansion supports basal cargo recycling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06262230919765166, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.265395175500244, "cosine_similarity": 0.38066287850977765, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6155436893203884, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06262230919765166, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.265395175500244, "cosine_similarity": 0.38066287850977765, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6155436893203884, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.4232854999999995, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_153", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; only sign, rank and relative magnitude within the RNA modality are used, and RNA effects are never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B, TFE3, MTOR) means no differential call was supplied, not that the gene is unchanged, so all set statistics are conditional on this selection.", "The list-wide upward bias (1705/2212 rows positive, 77.1%) is treated as the null background rate; enrichment claims are made against that background rather than against zero. This bias may itself reflect normalization, ambient RNA, or cell-composition differences in the astrocyte co-culture rather than a true global increase in transcript abundance.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel-like features with 2-6 candidate genes each and no unique identification; a spot containing CTSD, CTSB or ATP6V1E1 is assumed only to be consistent with, not proof of, a change in that protein. The interpretation that opposite-direction spots for the same candidate reflect proenzyme/mature or assembly-state redistribution is an inference that the data cannot resolve.", "Measured quantities are steady-state RNA and protein-spot abundance only. Lysosomal pH, V1-V0 assembly, cathepsin activity, autophagic and phagocytic flux, cholesterol trafficking, neutral lipid and droplet content, and TFEB localization are all inferred and were not measured in the supplied data.", "Replicate structure, cell numbers and whether RNA and protein were collected from the same cultures are not supplied; the two modalities are assumed to describe the same genotype contrast under mock treatment at day 30.", "The comparison is stated to be isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3, so genotype rather than line background is assumed to be the manipulated variable; no genomic variant data were inspected and none are claimed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal may not be microglial; no purity or cell-type deconvolution measure is supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily at a post-transcriptional endolysosomal step: transcripts for acid hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits and late-endosome/retromer machinery are coordinately higher (median log fold change ~+2.5 for hydrolases versus +1.46 for the rest of the differential list), together with higher TFEB and MITF transcripts, yet the protein spots whose candidate lists contain V-ATPase V1 subunits are significantly lower and cathepsin-containing spots move in opposite directions rather than uniformly up. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting bottleneck is mature, acidification-competent lysosomal degradative capacity per unit of delivered cargo, so lipid-rich endolysosomal cargo is hydrolysed and exported more slowly in APOE4; the resulting failure to deliver cargo-derived sterol to the ER keeps SREBP-target and sterol-esterification transcripts elevated (SREBF1, SCD, LDLR, SCARB1, SOAT1, DGAT1, ACAT2, DHCR24, LSS, INSIG1: 17/17 lipid-handling genes in the list are positive) and drives a compensatory, TFEB-associated biogenesis response. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript program could equally be a response to, rather than a cause of, the proposed bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: low-dose bafilomycin A1 or ATP6V0C/ATP6AP1 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy APOE4 (increased LysoTracker load with reduced DQ-BSA dequenching, increased BODIPY neutral-lipid content, increased SREBF1/SCD/LDLR transcripts), and the same dose applied to APOE4 should produce a markedly smaller incremental effect (occlusion). If APOE4 responds to V-ATPase inhibition with the same or larger increment than APOE3, i.e. no occlusion, the acidification/degradative-capacity bottleneck is weakened.", "Rescue: restoring degradative capacity in APOE4 (constitutively active TFEB, acidic nanoparticle re-acidification, or exogenous mature cathepsin/acid lipase supplementation) should normalize DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester clearance AND lower SREBF1/SCD/SOAT1/DGAT1 transcripts. If lysosomal pH and DQ-BSA proteolysis are normalized but the SREBP-target and esterification transcripts remain elevated, step 5 is falsified and the lipid program must be driven independently of lysosomal cargo processing.", "Direct capacity test at protein level: quantitative immunoblot of APOE4 versus APOE3 should show a higher pro/mature ratio for CTSD (~48 kDa versus 32/14 kDa) and CTSB, and a reduced membrane-associated V1/V0 ratio, despite higher CTSD, CTSB and ATP6V1A/ATP6V1H transcripts. If mature hydrolase forms and V1 membrane association scale proportionally with the transcript increases, the central transcript-protein discordance (step 3) collapses and the hypothesis should be rejected.", "Kinetic cargo test: after a pulse of BODIPY-LDL or fluorescent myelin/apoptotic-cell cargo, APOE4 microglia should show slower luminal dequenching and delayed SREBP2 cleavage/ER sterol arrival, with cargo retained in LAMP1-positive compartments at time points where APOE3 has cleared it. Equal clearance kinetics between genotypes would falsify the bottleneck.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: if lysosomal pH, cathepsin activity and cargo clearance are indistinguishable between genotypes while oxygen consumption rate, ATP and the OXPHOS protein complement differ, then the coherent 37/37 OXPHOS transcript increase, not endolysosomal capacity, is the primary axis and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Specificity control: the sharp decrease in gene:CTSS should be reflected by reduced CTSS-specific proteolytic activity in APOE4; if total endolysosomal protease activity is instead increased in APOE4, the proposed reduction in effective degradative capacity is contradicted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_153", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (cargo load, inferred flux): higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28, scavenger receptors such as MSR1 were not called differential) are interpreted as increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system in APOE4. Only transcript abundance is measured; uptake flux, cargo composition and lipid pools are not measured here.", "Step 2 (compensatory biogenesis transcription, measured as RNA only): a CLEAR-like program is elevated - gene:TFEB +2.38 and gene:MITF +1.03 with coordinate increases in acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17), in all measured V-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.29, gene:ATP6V0D2 +1.12, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6AP2 +1.18), in hydrolase targeting (gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02) and in membrane/lumenal components (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CLN3 +1.17). TFEB transcriptional activity and nuclear localization are inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (the bottleneck, measured as protein spots with ambiguous identity): mature degradative/acidification capacity does not scale with the transcript program. The two spots whose candidate lists include a V-ATPase V1 subunit are both significantly decreased (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93 log2), and cathepsin-containing spots redistribute bidirectionally rather than increasing (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:027 +0.59, protein_spot:055 +0.59, protein_spot:057 +0.59 versus protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:086 -0.93). We infer a shift in the proenzyme/mature and assembly state of hydrolases and of the V1 sector, i.e. lower catalytically competent capacity per lysosome, rather than a change in total protein; spot identity is ambiguous and no protease activity, luminal pH or V1-V0 assembly state was measured.", "Step 4 (traffic without resolution, inferred): late-endosome and retromer/ESCRT transcripts increase (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:SNX17 +1.05) and a VPS26A-containing spot is among the largest increases (protein_spot:044 +2.38), while the CI-M6P receptor transcript falls (gene:M6PR -1.72) and the dominant homeostatic microglial protease transcript falls sharply (gene:CTSS -5.57). We infer increased delivery to, and recycling from, late endosomes feeding an unresolved terminal degradative step, not increased degradation itself.", "Step 5 (downstream sterol consequence, inferred): if cargo lipid is not hydrolysed and exported, cargo-derived cholesterol does not reach the ER sterol sensor, so SREBP-driven and storage transcripts stay high despite high uptake-receptor transcripts (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:MYLIP +1.28; 17/17 positive, binomial p~0.012 against the 77.1% background up-rate of this list). Neutral lipid, cholesteryl ester and droplet content were not measured in these data.", "Step 6 (energetic accompaniment, alternative-explanation checkpoint): all 37 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts are higher (median +2.65, Mann-Whitney p=7e-5 versus the rest of the list; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20), while mitochondrially encoded transcripts trend down (6 MT- genes, median -1.56). Under this hypothesis the OXPHOS shift is a parallel or downstream demand signal for V-ATPase-dependent acidification and lipid handling; it is explicitly acknowledged as the strongest competing primary mechanism."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a CLEAR-type lysosomal transcript program that is not matched at the level of mature acid-hydrolase/V-ATPase protein, creating a terminal endolysosomal cargo-processing bottleneck that keeps ER sterol sensing 'low'"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1278292655909611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1796321050335424, "cosine_similarity": 0.38065841415222124, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_153", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6112427184466019, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1278292655909611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1796321050335424, "cosine_similarity": 0.38065841415222124, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6112427184466019, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.94405275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 152}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_043", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are on an unspecified logarithm base and are used only as directions and relative magnitudes on that common scale; positive means higher in APOE4.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (1705 up-rows and 507 down-rows sharing duplicated source_row indices, all with adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1), not an unbiased transcriptome; the 77%-up composition is therefore treated as a property of the list, and all enrichment statements are conditional on this background. Absence of a gene is not evidence of no change.", "Because the global list is up-shifted, the mechanism relies on an internal contrast (mtDNA-encoded versus nuclear-encoded subunits of the same complexes), which is robust to a uniform additive normalisation shift.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is used as a proxy for subunit supply; mitochondrial translation, mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass, membrane potential, holoenzyme assembly and respiration were not measured and are inferred only.", "Single-cell mtDNA-transcript quantification (10X Flex, probe-based) is assumed to reflect true mitochondrial transcript content rather than probe-panel, ambient-RNA or mito-fraction QC-filtering artefacts; this assumption is unverified and is the main technical risk.", "Protein spots are ambiguous mixtures: protein_spot:074 lists SOD2 among five candidate genes (RAC2, SOD2, KRT10, RHOG, PRDX1) and is cited only as weak, non-identifying corroboration of an oxidative-stress direction, not as measured SOD2 protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture composition, maturation state and cell-cycle differences between the APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed not to be the dominant driver of the mitonuclear contrast; this was not testable with the supplied data.", "Background pathway memberships (which subunits are mtDNA-encoded, ISR target identity) are unverified literature knowledge applied to the supplied gene symbols."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a selective, high-confidence loss of mtDNA-encoded core respiratory-chain transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2) while nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits, assembly factors and mitochondrial protein-import components are coordinately elevated. We hypothesise that the limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for holoenzyme assembly, so that the nuclear-encoded modules cannot be incorporated into complete complexes; the resulting assembly/respiration constraint is inferred to drive the integrated stress response (EIF2AK3, DDIT3 and ATF4-type one-carbon/serine targets) and a compensatory feed-forward increase in nuclear OXPHOS transcription. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: blocking mitochondrial translation in APOE3 microglia (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol, 48-72 h, doses that spare cytosolic translation) should phenocopy the APOE4 signature, i.e. raise nuclear-encoded NDUF/ATP5/COX/UQCR transcripts and DDIT3/PSPH/SHMT2 while lowering MT-ATP6/MT-ND4/MT-CYB, and should minimally further change APOE4 (occlusion). If APOE3 cells treated this way fail to reproduce the nuclear-up/mtDNA-down/ISR pattern, or if the effect is fully additive in APOE4 rather than occluded, the mechanism is weakened.", "BN-PAGE/complexome and Seahorse on isogenic pairs: APOE4 should show reduced fully assembled complex I, III2IV and V holoenzymes with accumulation of nuclear-encoded subassemblies (e.g. F1 without Fo, complex I Q/N-module), and lower ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption, despite equal or higher nuclear-encoded subunit protein. Equal or higher holoenzyme levels and ATP-linked OCR in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "Normalisation control: absolute quantification (spike-in normalised mt-transcript per cell, mtDNA:nuclear DNA qPCR, MitoTracker/TOMM20 mitochondrial mass) should show reduced mt-transcript per mtDNA or reduced mtDNA copy number in APOE4. If mt-transcripts per cell and mtDNA copy number are unchanged and only the relative fraction differs, the observation is a normalisation/compositional artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "Ordering test: PERK inhibition or ISRIB should suppress the DDIT3/PSPH/SHMT2 elevation and blunt the compensatory nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise without restoring MT-ATP6/MT-ND4/MT-CYB levels or holoenzyme assembly. If ISR inhibition normalises the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit, the ISR is upstream and the proposed step order is wrong.", "Rescue test: increasing mitochondrial genome expression in APOE4 (TFAM overexpression, or mitochondria transfer from APOE3 cells) should restore the mtDNA/nuclear transcript ratio, lower ISR markers and improve ATP-linked respiration; failure to improve respiration despite a restored ratio would weaken the causal chain.", "ALTERNATIVE-MECHANISM DISCRIMINATOR (assigned focus): if functional endolysosomal assays (DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin activity, LysoSensor pH, myelin/apoptotic-cell degradation kinetics) show a large APOE4 deficit while BN-PAGE assembly and ATP-linked OCR are unchanged, then an endolysosomal-capacity bottleneck, not mitonuclear imbalance, is primary and this hypothesis should be discarded."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA abundance): mtDNA-encoded transcripts for the catalytic cores of complex V (MT-ATP6), complex I (MT-ND4), complex III (MT-CYB) and complex IV (MT-CO2) are among the most significant down-regulated genes in APOE4 versus APOE3, whereas nuclear-encoded subunits of the same four complexes are coordinately up (median difference ~4 reported log units). INFERRED: the intra-mitochondrial pool of newly made core subunits, which was not measured, is reduced relative to the imported nuclear-encoded subunit pool.", "MEASURED (RNA abundance): mitochondrial import channels/motor components (TOMM22, TIMM8B, TIMM44), inner-membrane organisers (CHCHD1, CHCHD3), the mitochondrial elongation factor TUFM and complex-specific assembly factors (NDUFAF4, COA1, COA8, COX20) are elevated. INFERRED: import flux of nuclear-encoded subunits into mitochondria is maintained or increased, not decreased.", "INFERRED (activity/flux, not measured): the mismatch stalls assembly at the mtDNA-encoded core modules (ND4/ND5 membrane module of complex I, cytochrome b of complex III, COX2 of complex IV, subunit a of Fo), so fully assembled holoenzymes and ATP-linked respiratory flux fall despite higher nuclear subunit transcripts; unassembled or partially assembled nuclear-encoded modules accumulate.", "INFERRED then MEASURED: the resulting proteostatic/energetic stress engages the integrated stress response; consistent with this, EIF2AK3, EIF2A, EIF2S3, DDIT3 and the ATF4-type serine/one-carbon targets PSPH and SHMT2 are elevated, and peroxiredoxin/glutathione-peroxidase transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4) rise as expected for increased electron leak. The ISR is placed downstream of the assembly deficit; the data cannot order these events.", "INFERRED (feed-forward): ISR/retrograde signalling further raises nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, carrier (SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11) and biosynthetic transcription, which cannot correct the deficit because the limiting subunits are mtDNA-encoded; this predicts a persistent transcriptional 'compensation without capacity' state rather than a genuine increase in respiratory capacity.", "INFERRED (downstream phenotype, weakly supported here): constrained terminal oxidation with elevated citrate carrier and lipogenic transcripts (SLC25A1, SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, ACSS2) biases APOE4 microglia toward reductive/lipid-anabolic metabolism; this step is a prediction, not a claim supported by flux data."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: a deficit of mtDNA-encoded core OXPHOS subunit transcripts against an up-regulated nuclear OXPHOS/import program is the primary bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0675146771037182, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25754965367925314, "cosine_similarity": 0.3805629981713313, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6065857605177993, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0675146771037182, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25754965367925314, "cosine_similarity": 0.3805629981713313, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6065857605177993, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.74748825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 153}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; magnitudes (median +1.46, range -7.9 to +15.5) are treated as ranks/directions only, not as interpretable fold changes.", "The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive, so only contrasts relative to that background (or internal contrasts) are treated as informative. The sterol/lipogenic set is 10/10 up and the endolysosomal set 25/26 up, above the 77% background (binomial p=0.074 and p=0.010), and the lysosomal set exceeds the background distribution (Mann-Whitney p=0.016).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track the corresponding protein/enzyme abundance for the cited genes; no protein-level measurement of SREBP cleavage, SOAT1, NPC1 or v-ATPase assembly is supplied.", "SREBP transcriptional activity, ER-accessible sterol level, lysosomal sterol content, esterification flux and lipid-droplet content are all inferred; none is measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots each carry several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified, so no spot is used as primary support; spot-level cathepsin signals are internally contradictory (protein_spot:053 up, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 down).", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein lipid, so the loop is assumed to operate with a continuous extracellular lipid source; a lipid-poor medium could abolish it.", "Key nodes are missing from the supplied rows (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, LIPA, APOC1), so the sterol-synthesis and efflux arms are only partially observed.", "Causality is not established: this is an association between genotype and transcript state in a single mock-treatment contrast with unreported biological replicates."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, the difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is best explained not by inflammatory/interferon activation but by a lipid-trafficking bottleneck: delivery of cholesterol from an expanded endolysosomal compartment to the ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol pool is limiting in APOE4. Because the ER sensor reads sterol as low, SREBP-driven sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and lipoprotein-uptake transcripts stay ON while esterification transcripts rise, predicting a feed-forward accumulation of cholesteryl ester and lipid droplets despite adequate total lipid. All abundances here are transcript (and ambiguous protein-spot) measurements; SREBP cleavage, sterol pool localization and esterification flux are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should both reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content AND, by returning free sterol to the ER, suppress the SREBP target transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1, INSIG1) preferentially in APOE4 relative to APOE3. If SOAT1 inhibition lowers cholesteryl ester but leaves the APOE4 SREBP program elevated, the proposed ER-sensing bottleneck is wrong.", "Sensor-integrity control that distinguishes delivery failure from sensor failure: exogenous 25-hydroxycholesterol or LDL-free sterol loading should suppress SREBP targets equally in APOE4 and APOE3 (the sensor itself is intact). If APOE4 fails to suppress, the bottleneck lies in the SCAP/INSIG sensor rather than in lysosome-to-ER delivery, weakening this mechanism as stated.", "Bypassing the lysosomal step with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin should collapse the APOE4-specific elevation of sterol-synthesis transcripts and reduce filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol; no genotype-selective change would weaken the mechanism.", "Direct imaging/biochemistry: APOE4 microglia should show higher LAMP1-colocalized filipin signal and higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio than isogenic APOE3, with equal or lower ER-accessible sterol measured by an ALOD4/D4H probe. Equal lysosomal sterol and equal cholesteryl-ester fraction would falsify the core claim.", "Negative prediction against the assigned inflammatory/interferon focus: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR blockade under mock conditions should not normalize the APOE4 sterol/lysosomal transcript program, and APOE4 microglia should not show an ISG signature (no MX1/IFIT/OAS/ISG15 induction). Detection of a coherent type-I IFN signature that is upstream of the lipid program would favour the rejected alternative.", "v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) should exacerbate, not relieve, the APOE4 sterol-synthesis transcript program; relief would contradict the direction of Step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated increase in endolysosomal transcripts - luminal hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and the lysosomal-biogenesis factor gene:TFEB - consistent with (but not proof of) an expanded, more acidic degradative compartment receiving lipid cargo.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): Cholesterol liberated in that compartment is inefficiently transferred to the ER-accessible regulatory pool. This is the proposed rate-limiting step; it is not measured here. gene:NPC2 is elevated only modestly relative to the strong hydrolase increase, and the obligate partner NPC1 was not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred activity from measured targets): With ER regulatory sterol low, SREBP-2/SREBP-1 processing stays active. Consistent with this, every measured sterol/lipogenic gene is up - gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1 (itself an SREBP target), gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1 - a state that would be switched OFF if ER sterol were replete.", "Step 4 (measured): Uptake capacity is simultaneously raised (gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), so the cell keeps importing lipoprotein lipid while behaving as though sterol-starved.", "Step 5 (measured, flux inferred): Esterification/storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CIDEB, gene:ABHD5), which would divert incoming free cholesterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol droplets rather than into the ER regulatory pool, closing the feed-forward loop and keeping Step 2 unresolved.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype): The net APOE4 state is a lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded microglial phenotype (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ANXA1 elevated) with increased demand on mitochondrial catabolism, rather than a cytokine- or interferon-driven activation state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sequester sterol in an expanded lysosomal/esterified pool, leaving the ER sterol sensor in a chronic 'low' state that drives feed-forward lipid loading"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10763209393346379, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22924232112605147, "cosine_similarity": 0.38053646093770704, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mean_absolute_error": 0.588284789644013, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10763209393346379, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22924232112605147, "cosine_similarity": 0.38053646093770704, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "mean_absolute_error": 0.588284789644013, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.75357025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 154}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a fold-change on an unspecified logarithm base; magnitudes are used only for ranking and direction and are never converted or compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot values.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the empirical distribution of the supplied list and, where possible, within the source-row block that the gene came from.", "Protein spots are mixtures with several candidate genes each; a spot is treated as weak, non-unique evidence about any one protein, and the lysosomal spot argument rests on the aggregate of many spots rather than on any single assignment.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for the size of the corresponding protein pool, and neither is assumed to report enzymatic activity, luminal pH, organelle number, or flux.", "The mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison is assumed to be isogenic and confounded only by genotype, as stated in the metadata; replicate number is not supplied, so the reported p-values are taken at face value.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to have contaminated the microglial single-cell profiles, and the two source-row blocks are assumed to be two parts of one comparison rather than two different comparisons."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia sit in a scavenger-receptor-high, lipid-associated activation state whose transcriptome shows a large coordinated induction of lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase genes, yet the lysosomal-candidate protein spots show no matching increase (mean +0.11 log2 vs +0.44 for all other spots; the two ATP6V1E1-containing spots and three cathepsin-containing spots decrease significantly). We hypothesise that luminal lysosomal catabolism of internalised lipid cargo, not cargo uptake and not transcriptional supply, is the rate-limiting step, and that the un-catabolised sterol/fatty-acid pool is routed to SOAT1/DGAT1/SCD-dependent esterification and desaturation, predicting neutral-lipid (cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol) accumulation in APOE4 cells. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pool itself was not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, raising lysosomal catabolic capacity (TFEB overexpression, or mTORC1 inhibition) should lower BODIPY/LipidTOX neutral-lipid area and cholesteryl-ester content toward APOE3 levels AND relax the excess CLEAR transcripts, whereas SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition should lower droplet content while leaving the CLEAR transcript excess intact. If TFEB activation leaves lipid content unchanged while SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition clears it, the bottleneck is esterification rather than lysosomal capacity and this mechanism is wrong.", "Capacity assay: per-cell mature cathepsin B/D activity (Magic Red, BODIPY-FL-pepstatin), DQ-BSA proteolysis rate and LysoTracker-normalised acidification in APOE4 should be equal to or lower than APOE3 despite the several-fold higher CTSB/CTSD/GBA/HEXA/ATP6V transcripts. Proportional increases in hydrolase activity and normal or lower lysosomal pH in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck step.", "Cargo challenge: after a pulse of fluorescent oxLDL or myelin, APOE4 cells should show equal or greater uptake at 1 h but significantly more undegraded cargo and more lipid droplets at 6-24 h; bafilomycin A1 or leupeptin should add proportionally less extra lipid accumulation in APOE4 than in APOE3 (occlusion). Equal degradation kinetics, or an equal bafilomycin increment in both genotypes, would weaken the mechanism.", "RNA-protein step: immunoblot of mature (single-chain and heavy-chain) cathepsin D and B and of ATP6V1E1 should show no increase, or a decrease, in APOE4 despite elevated transcripts, with increased pro-cathepsin D in conditioned medium if M6PR-dependent missorting contributes. Proportional increases in mature hydrolase protein would falsify the discordance on which this mechanism rests.", "Specificity control: knocking down SCARB1 or CD36 in APOE4 should reduce lipid cargo influx and lower both droplet content and the CLEAR transcript excess without correcting the hydrolase-protein deficit; if the CLEAR excess persists unchanged after uptake blockade, the demand-signal interpretation of step 3 is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["State: APOE4 microglia express a scavenger/phagocytic, lipid-associated activation program (measured RNA increases in MRC1, CD163, CD14, CLEC7A, GPNMB, C1QA, TREM2, APOE; decreased TGFBR1 as loss of the homeostatic TGF-beta axis). Increased engulfment flux is inferred, not measured.", "Cargo influx: transcripts for lipid- and lipoprotein-binding receptors rise (SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, SLCO2B1, PLA2G7), from which we infer greater delivery of cholesterol- and phospholipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Demand signal: a coordinated CLEAR-type transcriptional response follows (MITF, TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, GBA, GAA, HEXA, NAGLU, SGSH, DNASE2, SCARB2, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1H, ATP6AP1). We read this as a compensatory demand signal for degradative capacity, not as evidence that degradation has increased; nuclear TFEB localisation and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "BOTTLENECK: degradative capacity does not scale with the transcriptional program. Lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase-candidate protein spots are flat to reduced (spots 058, 064, 065, 067, 069 significantly decreased) while a concordant control (ANXA1 RNA up, its spots up, e.g. 044, 045) shows the spot assay can register increases. Reduced M6PR RNA is a candidate contributor via impaired mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery, and reduced CTSS and IDS RNA show the hydrolase induction is not uniform. Lower catabolic flux per unit cargo is inferred, not measured.", "Diversion: the sterol and fatty acid liberated from cargo is preferentially re-esterified and desaturated rather than oxidised (increased SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, SREBF1, MGLL, DHCR24; decreased ACSL5 and ABCD1 as reduced channelling toward beta-oxidation).", "Predicted outcome: net expansion of a cytoplasmic neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester pool and of undegraded lysosomal lipid in APOE4 relative to APOE3. This pool is a prediction of the model; no lipid species were measured in the supplied data."], "title": "Lysosomal degradative capacity is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a scavenger-receptor-high state induces a CLEAR hydrolase transcriptional program that is not matched at the protein level, diverting internalised lipid into esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08023483365949119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2499970456403615, "cosine_similarity": 0.3805056193981346, "direction_accuracy": 0.1343042071197411, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6021067961165049, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08023483365949119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2499970456403615, "cosine_similarity": 0.3805056193981346, "direction_accuracy": 0.1343042071197411, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6021067961165049, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.37471575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 155}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= ~1) with an unspecified logarithm base; effects are used on their reported scale and program patterns are judged against the selected-list background (77.1% positive, median +1.46), not against a 50/50 expectation.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g., HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, P2RY12, CX3CR1, MX1, OAS1, HLA class II, B2M) are unknown, not unchanged; the sterol and interferon calls rest only on represented members.", "Program membership was defined a priori from standard pathway families by symbol pattern before looking at signs; no member was dropped to make directions agree (gene:CTSS, gene:HK2, gene:TALDO1, gene:CCL4 and other discordant members are retained and reported).", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity/state, not as flux: lipid uptake rate, lysosomal hydrolase activity, ER-accessible cholesterol, oxygen consumption and cholesterol efflux are inferred and unmeasured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D features; no spot is assigned to a single protein, and spot directions are used only for compatibility or contradiction.", "Permutation comparisons against the selected list are descriptive: pathway members are co-regulated and not independent, so the quoted p-values are not formal enrichment statistics.", "The mock-condition claim is about an ongoing routing/state difference; any reduced buffering capacity of APOE4 cells would be revealed only by a future lipid or debris challenge and is not asserted as an established defect in the measured condition.", "Gene-level transcript differences could partly reflect cell-composition or technical differences between the APOE4 and APOE3 cultures (very wide effect range, up to +15.5; a spliceosome control set is also 10/10 positive), so the state interpretation is provisional."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state in which transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid internalization, TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase machinery, sterol esterification/storage, and mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS capacity are jointly higher, while the SREBP sterol-synthesis arm remains fully on rather than feedback-suppressed - a pattern indicating that internalized sterol is routed into lysosomal/esterified storage pools instead of satisfying ER sterol sensing. Canonical interferon and NF-kB effector programs are not distinguishable from the selected-list background and are rejected as the differentiating mechanism. This is a measured-abundance, transcript-level state description; lipid flux, hydrolase activity and ER-accessible sterol were not measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, imaging of neutral lipid (LipidTOX/BODIPY) and unesterified cholesterol (filipin) plus an ER-accessible cholesterol probe (ALOD4/D4H) should show increased lysosomal/lipid-droplet sterol and neutral lipid in APOE4 with equal or LOWER ER-accessible cholesterol; if APOE4 shows equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol with no increase in stored lipid, Step 3 and the routing mechanism are weakened.", "Prospective: acute loading with LDL, oxLDL or myelin debris should suppress SREBP-arm transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR7) less efficiently in APOE4 than APOE3; equally efficient suppression in both genotypes would falsify the unrelieved-sterol-demand step.", "Prospective: culturing in lipoprotein-depleted medium or blocking scavenger uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should lower the elevated lysosomal/TFEB-target transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; unchanged lysosomal transcripts after uptake blockade would falsify the proposed causal ordering (uptake -\u003e lysosomal expansion).", "Prospective, throughput versus compensation: extracellular flux and tracer assays should show higher basal and lipid-dependent oxygen consumption in APOE4 with no increase in glycolytic rate, together with slower clearance/efflux of a pulse of labelled cholesterol or myelin lipid; if APOE4 shows equal oxygen consumption AND equal lipid clearance despite the transcript differences, the mechanism is substantially weakened (transcript-only difference without state change).", "Prospective, focus test: baseline (mock) secretome and ISG protein readouts (IFN-beta, CXCL10, MX1, ISG15, IL-6, TNF) should not be materially higher in APOE4; a robust baseline interferon or NF-kB effector signature at protein level would revive the rejected inflammatory explanation and contradict the rejection of that focus.", "Prospective, protein-level resolution: targeted MS or immunoblot of the ambiguous spots should show ANXA1 (not TALDO1) increased in APOE4 and should test lysosomal hydrolase protein (CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, GBA) and v-ATPase subunit levels; a uniform decrease in lysosomal hydrolase protein alongside the elevated transcripts would contradict Step 2 as an expansion and argue instead for a degradative-protein deficit."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (routing input): APOE4 microglia express higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalization and scavenging (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:APOE +1.24), consistent with greater delivery of lipid into the endolysosomal route; uptake rate itself is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (compartment expansion): A lysosomal biogenesis-type program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:IGF2R +2.02), 25/26 members positive versus 77.1% positive in the selected background (permutation p~0.009); gene:CTSS -5.57 is the clear exception.", "Step 3 (sterol routing, not sensing): Sterol/lipid storage and esterification transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:MGLL +4.00) while every represented SREBP-arm member stays positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:NPC2 +1.17; 14/14 positive, p~0.03). Simultaneous uptake plus synthesis induction is the signature expected when internalized sterol is stored or retained in lysosomes rather than reaching the ER-accessible pool that would impose feedback.", "Step 4 (oxidative disposal capacity): Mitochondrial catabolic transcripts rise disproportionately (OXPHOS 40/43 positive, median +2.33, p~0.007: gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36; TCA/pyruvate 7/7 positive, median +5.54, p~0.0001: gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SDHB +1.65) together with fatty-acid oxidation members (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24), whereas upper glycolysis and the oxidative pentose-phosphate arm are mixed to lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, versus gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:ENO1 +2.17). The state is oxidative-catabolic, not the glycolytic commitment typical of inflammatory activation.", "Step 5 (redox accompaniment): Peroxide-handling and iron-storage transcripts accompany the oxidative shift (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:FTH1 +2.53), compatible with higher mitochondrial and lysosomal lipid turnover; oxidant levels themselves were not measured.", "Step 6 (emergent state, immune arm not required): The result is a lipid-laden, DAM-like microglial state (gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:CD33 +1.78, gene:TREM2 +1.28) reached without canonical interferon or NF-kB effector induction: the IFN-like set is background-level (n=7, median +1.25, p~0.73; only gene:IFI27L2 +5.34, gene:IFI16 +1.25, gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:IRF5 +1.22, gene:TMEM173 +1.22, gene:IFNAR1 +1.41, gene:IRF2 -1.17; no MX/OAS/IFIT/HLA/B2M rows supplied) and the NF-kB/cytokine set is indistinguishable from background (n=26, 0.81 positive p~0.43, median +1.62 p~0.33; gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12 offset by gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:CCL23 -2.51, gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05, gene:TRAF4 -7.17).", "Step 7 (protein-spot compatibility only): 2D spots are multi-candidate and give compatibility, not confirmation: the largest increases (protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:043 +1.96) list ANXA1 and TALDO1 among candidates, and gene:ANXA1 +4.15 versus gene:TALDO1 -2.32 makes ANXA1 the RNA-compatible candidate without resolving spot identity; cathepsin- and v-ATPase-candidate spots are bidirectional (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93), so lysosomal protein amount is untested."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-routing cell state: endolysosomal-mitochondrial expansion with unrelieved ER sterol-demand signaling, not interferon/NF-kB activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08708414872798434, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23776996140982395, "cosine_similarity": 0.3804667155296371, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5902297734627832, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08708414872798434, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23776996140982395, "cosine_similarity": 0.3804667155296371, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5902297734627832, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.868686, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 30}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_029", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1 and every adjusted p is below 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% positive, median +1.46), so only enrichment relative to that shifted background is interpreted, not the sign of individual genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are treated as ordinal within this dataset only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for hydrolase protein and activity; no hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, lipid, sterol, or SREBP-processing measurement was supplied, so degradative flux, lysosomal cholesterol content, and TFEB localisation are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin and actin candidates, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; spots are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Genes central to the proposed egress step (NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B) are absent from the supplied list; their absence is treated as unmeasured, not as unchanged.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex, so ambient/cross-cell-type RNA and pseudobulk composition differences could inflate a subset of the extreme effects (172 rows exceed |5|); the mechanism relies on set-level coherence rather than any single extreme gene.", "Background knowledge about APOE4, MiT/TFE-CLEAR regulation, and SREBP sterol sensing is unverified here because literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "At baseline (mock), the dominant reproducible difference between APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is not the engulfment/actin arm but the lumen of the endolysosome: APOE4 cells show a selective, statistically enriched up-shift of acid-hydrolase transcripts (glycosidases, sphingomyelinase, cathepsins B/D/K) with MiT/TFE factors and v-ATPase subunits, while sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and LDLR transcripts remain high. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is post-uptake clearance of lipid-rich cargo out of the endolysosome (egress/handoff to the ER pool), so hydrolase expansion is a compensatory response to unmet luminal demand rather than a sign of increased degradative flux; internalisation capacity and actomyosin engulfment machinery are not the bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Baseline imaging: APOE4 microglia will show more unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and neutral lipid (LipidTOX) inside LAMP1-positive compartments than isogenic APOE3, with equal or larger LAMP1 area. If lysosomal lipid and LAMP1 compartment content are indistinguishable between genotypes, the mechanism is falsified.", "Loading test discriminating egress from uptake: after a pulse of fluorescent acLDL, myelin debris or apoptotic-cell membranes, APOE4 cells will internalise at a rate equal to or greater than APOE3 (no engulfment deficit) but will fail to suppress SREBP targets (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7 transcript/protein) that APOE3 suppresses. Normal SREBP suppression in APOE4 after loading, or a clear reduction in internalisation rate, would weaken the mechanism.", "Primary discriminating perturbation: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or forced NPC1/StARD3-mediated egress) applied to APOE4 microglia should lower LAMP1-compartment cholesterol and normalise SREBP target transcripts toward APOE3 without lowering cargo internalisation rate; whereas simply blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should lower cargo load but leave the elevated SREBP target signature and the hydrolase-transcript signature largely uncorrected. The opposite pattern - uptake blockade normalising SREBP targets while cyclodextrin does not - would falsify the egress-bottleneck assignment and support an uptake-driven mechanism.", "Hydrolase-capacity control: bulk luminal proteolysis and glycosidase reporters (DQ-BSA dequenching, PFB-FDGlu for GAA, fluorogenic HEXA/GBA substrates) will be equal to or higher in APOE4 than APOE3 per lysosome, consistent with compensatory hydrolase expansion. If these activities are lower in APOE4, the bottleneck is hydrolase capacity rather than egress and this hypothesis must be revised.", "Direction-of-causality test on the transcriptional arm: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should worsen, not relieve, lysosomal lipid accumulation, identifying the hydrolase program as compensatory. If TFEB knockdown reduces lysosomal lipid load, the program is a driver rather than a response and the compensatory framing is wrong.", "Cytoskeletal negative control: despite low MYH9 and ACTB transcripts, bead, zymosan and synaptosome engulfment indices in APOE4 will not be reduced by more than a small margin relative to APOE3. A large engulfment deficit would favour an actomyosin-limited mechanism over the endolysosomal one proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinated higher transcript abundance for luminal acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:GLA +1.53) with median far above the already up-shifted background of this selected DE list (set median +5.52 vs list median +1.46; Mann-Whitney p=1.6e-4). Inferred, not measured: increased lysosomal hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity, and increased lysosome number/volume.", "Measured: MiT/TFE transcription factors (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) and v-ATPase/lysosomal membrane transcripts (gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:CLCN7) are all higher. Inferred: MiT/TFE nuclear translocation and CLEAR-network activation downstream of a lysosomal stress/load signal; the acidification and membrane arm is only weakly enriched over background (Mann-Whitney p=0.61), so the response is biased toward luminal catabolic capacity rather than uniform lysosome biogenesis.", "Measured: cargo-delivery receptor and endocytic transcripts are uniformly, but only modestly, higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:COLEC12, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:CD163, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:STAB1, gene:SNX17; 14/14 positive but Mann-Whitney p=0.34 against the up-shifted background). Inferred: uptake capacity is permissive and possibly raised, supplying lipid-rich cargo, but it is not the discriminating bottleneck.", "Measured: SREBP transcription factors and their sterol/lipogenic targets stay high (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06). Inferred causal step: the ER-accessible sterol pool is sensed as low despite continued uptake and hydrolase expansion, which is the signature expected if catabolically released sterol/lipid is retained in the endolysosome instead of reaching the ER. This is an inference about localisation and flux; no lipid, sterol or SREBP-cleavage measurement was supplied.", "Measured: esterification/storage transcripts are also higher (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ABHD5 +1.04). Inferred: lipid that does reach the ER is shunted into esterified stores rather than suppressing synthesis, sustaining a futile import-plus-synthesis cycle.", "Measured: the shift is compositional and selective, not a generic 'more phagocyte' state - gene:CTSS is strongly down (-5.57) while other cathepsins rise, and the actomyosin/engulfment set is not enriched at all (Mann-Whitney p=0.93) with gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:RAC2 -1.97 opposing gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC5, gene:ARPC4, gene:CORO1B, gene:TWF2. Inferred phenotype: enlarged, cargo-laden LAMP1-positive compartments with retained undegraded/unexported lipid at baseline, rather than a faster phagocytic cell."], "title": "APOE4 microglia carry an endolysosomal cargo-clearance bottleneck: a selective MiT/TFE-type acid-hydrolase expansion coexisting with persistent SREBP output, indicating lipid retained in the lysosome rather than delivered to the ER"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3895432559169959, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25611134197895363, "cosine_similarity": 0.37970247139034585, "direction_accuracy": 0.37216828478964403, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5947669902912621, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3895432559169959, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25611134197895363, "cosine_similarity": 0.37970247139034585, "direction_accuracy": 0.37216828478964403, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5947669902912621, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9858885, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 156}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_065", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a large positive global shift (mean +1.39, 1705/2212 up), so all pathway claims are made relative to that biased background using permutation against the supplied list, not against a whole transcriptome. The logarithm base of the reported log fold change is unspecified and was never converted.", "Elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and OXPHOS transcripts are assumed to translate into increased protein and into increased lysosomal and mitochondrial catabolic capacity. Protein, enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, organelle number, cholesterol/sphingolipid pools, oxygen consumption and lipid flux were NOT measured in this dataset.", "TFEB/MITF/TFEC transcript elevation is assumed to reflect increased CLEAR-program transcriptional activity; TFEB nuclear localization and mTORC1 status were not measured (MTOR, RPTOR, FLCN, RRAGA are absent from the list).", "Protein spots are treated as ambiguous multi-candidate features, not identified proteins. Cathepsin-candidate spots are cited only as weak, internally inconsistent corroboration, since spots containing CTSB/CTSD candidates move in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 vs protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:069 -1.38); this could equally reflect redistribution of one protein between pro- and mature spots rather than any net abundance change.", "The cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-associated transcript differences could partly reflect differing ambient/contaminating RNA or altered astrocyte cross-talk rather than a cell-intrinsic microglial program; no purity or ambient-RNA control is supplied.", "The direction of causality between the lysosomal and mitochondrial programs is assumed (lysosome upstream) but is NOT established by these data; the two programs could be parallel outputs of a common upstream regulator."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the acidic-lysosomal degradative compartment - v-ATPase subunits plus sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid and protein hydrolases, with the CLEAR-family factors TFEB/MITF/TFEC elevated - together with a strong, nearly uniform elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS/fatty-acid-oxidation transcripts, while glycolytic and pentose-phosphate transcripts are not elevated relative to the list-wide background. We propose that the rate-limiting step is luminal lysosomal hydrolysis and export of lipid-rich cargo (sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide/GM2-type glycosphingolipids and cholesteryl ester), and that the mitochondrial program is a downstream compensatory sink for fatty acids liberated by that lysosomal catabolism. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux and organelle coupling; only transcript abundances and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION (lysosome-upstream test): Acute pharmacological block of lysosomal lipid hydrolysis in mock-treated APOE4 and APOE3 microglia - v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1 or concanamycin A) or selective glucocerebrosidase/hexosaminidase inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide; PUGNAc) - should reduce basal and maximal oxygen consumption significantly MORE in APOE4 than APOE3 and should cause a disproportionate APOE4-specific accumulation of LAMP1-colocalized neutral lipid and of glucosylceramide/GM2 measured by lipidomics. If OCR falls equally in both genotypes, or if APOE4 OCR is insensitive to lysosomal blockade, the proposed lysosome-to-mitochondria coupling is falsified and the two programs should instead be treated as parallel.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION (fuel test): CPT1 inhibition with etomoxir, or CPT1A/HADHA knockdown, should suppress basal OCR and increase BODIPY/LipidTOX neutral-lipid area more in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal etomoxir sensitivity between genotypes, or an APOE4 OCR that is instead selectively glucose- or glutamine-dependent, would weaken step 4.", "DIRECTIONALITY TEST: TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) and, if lysosomal flux is genuinely upstream, should also blunt the APOE4 elevation of TCA/OXPHOS transcripts (NDUFA5, UQCRC2, MDH1, OGDH). If TFEB knockdown removes the lysosomal signature while leaving the mitochondrial signature intact, the primary-bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "RECIPROCAL TEST: Mitochondrial inhibition (oligomycin or rotenone, sub-lethal) should NOT reduce lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts if the lysosome is upstream; a strong reciprocal suppression would indicate mitochondria-first causality and weaken the mechanism.", "ORGANELLE-STATE PREDICTION: APOE4 microglia should show increased LAMP1+ volume with equal or lower lysosomal pH (LysoSensor/ratiometric) and increased DQ-BSA and lipid-substrate degradation per cell but reduced degradation per unit lysosomal volume (i.e. capacity increased, per-lysosome efficiency not increased). Finding equal LAMP1+ volume, or per-lysosome efficiency already higher in APOE4, would falsify the 'compensating for a limiting step' framing.", "NEGATIVE PREDICTION (rejects the assigned ER/UPR focus): APOE4 microglia should NOT show a coherent unfolded-protein response - HSPA5/BiP protein, XBP1 splicing, eIF2-alpha phosphorylation and ATF4/CHOP protein should be comparable to APOE3, and ISRIB or PERK inhibition should not normalize the lysosomal or mitochondrial transcript signatures. Observing a genuine ATF6/IRE1-driven UPR with elevated BiP protein, or ISRIB-dependent reversal of the lysosomal program, would falsify this hypothesis in favour of an ER-proteostasis mechanism.", "SPECIFICITY PREDICTION: Untargeted lipidomics should show APOE4-selective accumulation of lysosomal sphingolipid species (glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 gangliosides, sphingomyelin, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate) and of cholesteryl esters. If the APOE4 lipid difference is confined to phospholipids or to plasma-membrane sterol with no sphingolipid or cholesteryl-ester change, step 3 is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred cargo load): APOE4 microglia handle a larger or more slowly cleared load of lipid-rich cargo, indicated by elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK) and for the microglial lipid-handling module gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB. Cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcriptional response): A CLEAR-type lysosome-biogenesis program is induced - gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC up, with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1) and lysosomal hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) coordinately elevated. A curated lysosomal acidification+hydrolase set is enriched above the strongly up-shifted background (n=30, mean +2.85 vs background mean +1.39, permutation p=8e-4); the sphingolipid-catabolic subset is enriched at mean +4.06 (p=0.006). Increased transcript does not prove increased hydrolase activity or lysosomal acidification.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck): Luminal hydrolysis and subsequent egress of lipid catabolites from the lysosome is the rate-limiting step. Under this model the hydrolase/v-ATPase induction is a compensatory response to an unmet degradative demand rather than evidence that degradation is already sufficient; sustained induction of the machinery is the expected signature of a step that remains limiting.", "Step 4 (inferred fatty-acid overflow and oxidative sink): Fatty acids and sphingoid bases released by lysosomal lipid hydrolysis are routed to mitochondria. Transcripts for carnitine/citrate carriers and beta-oxidation (gene:SLC25A46, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1) and for the TCA/OXPHOS machinery (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:TOMM22) are elevated; the combined mitochondrial set is the most coherent program in the data (n=48, 47 up, mean +3.21, permutation p\u003c5e-5).", "Step 5 (inferred fuel re-partitioning): Glycolytic and pentose-phosphate transcripts are not elevated above background (glycolysis n=8 mean +0.55; PPP/NRF2 n=4 mean +0.07, including gene:TALDO1 and gene:PGD decreased), consistent with a shift of ATP and reducing-equivalent supply toward mitochondrial oxidation of lysosome-derived lipid rather than toward glucose. Actual fuel usage was not measured.", "Step 6 (inferred lipid disposal branch): Catabolites that are neither exported nor oxidized are predicted to be re-esterified and stored, consistent with elevated gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 and with the lipogenic transcripts gene:SREBF1 and gene:SCD; note that this sterol/lipogenic arm is NOT enriched above the biased background (permutation p=0.16-0.23; HMGCR and SQLE are absent from the supplied list), so it is the weakest link in the chain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are locked in a lysosome-limited lipid catabolic state that is compensated by mitochondrial oxidative expansion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13174465457020046, "cosine_similarity": 0.3794712155747397, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6253106796116505, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15655577299412915, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13174465457020046, "cosine_similarity": 0.3794712155747397, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6253106796116505, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03605925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 157}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_156", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; we therefore rely on within-list relative ranking (nuclear OXPHOS at the 82nd-99th percentile versus mtDNA-encoded rows at the 5th-19th percentile) rather than on absolute direction, and we assume the selection did not systematically deplete interferon genes.", "The reported RNA effects use an unspecified logarithm base; only signs and relative magnitudes are used, never absolute fold changes.", "Steady-state transcript level for mtDNA-encoded subunits is assumed to be at least partly informative about the supply of the corresponding translated subunits; if mitochondrial translation is post-transcriptionally buffered, step 3 fails.", "Assembled complex amount, respiration, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number, metabolite pools, lipid species, lysosomal pH and hydrolase activity were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:065 and protein_spot:064 list ATP6V1E1 among several candidates) and are treated only as weak, non-identifying corroboration, never as identified proteins.", "The microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous astrocytic signalling or ambient RNA rather than APOE4-intrinsic biology.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the very small adjusted p-values may be inflated by treating cells as independent units."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcript program while the mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts that must partner with it (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are relatively reduced. We hypothesise that this mismatch, not a type-I/II interferon or NF-kB program, is the rate-limiting step: it constrains assembly of complete respiratory/ATP-synthase complexes and therefore oxidative flux, so TCA-derived citrate is exported (SLC25A1) and consumed by an activated SREBF1/SREBF2 lipogenic-sterol program (SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, LDLR, SOAT1, DGAT1), whose lipid/sterol load is matched by a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript expansion (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1A/1H/0C). Causality is not established by these data; only steady-state RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacologically block the proposed downstream arm without touching mitochondria (SCD inhibition, ACSS2 inhibition, or SLC25A1/citrate-carrier inhibition) in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia. The mechanism predicts neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and the lysosomal hydrolase program normalise while ATP-linked respiration and the MT-ATP6/MT-CYB transcript deficit remain unchanged. If instead respiration and the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit are corrected by blocking lipogenesis, the causal direction is reversed and this mechanism is wrong.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling should show APOE4 microglia with a lower ratio of fully assembled complex V (and complex I/III/IV) to free nuclear-encoded subunits or sub-assemblies, and Seahorse should show reduced ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption per mitochondrial mass. Equal or higher assembled complex V and equal or higher ATP-linked OCR in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism decisively.", "Quantitative measurement of mtDNA copy number and of mitochondrial translation (35S or OP-Puro labelling in the presence of cytosolic-translation inhibitor) should show reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit synthesis in APOE4; unchanged mitochondrial translation with unchanged mtDNA copy number would falsify step 3 and would instead support the transcript deficit being a probe/ambient-RNA artefact.", "Interferon test (assigned focus, predicted negative): baseline ISG15/MX1/IFIT1/STAT1 protein or transcript should not differ between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock, and JAK1/2 inhibition should leave the lipid and lysosomal phenotypes intact. Detection of a coherent baseline ISG elevation, or normalisation of the lipogenic/lysosomal program by JAK inhibition, would overturn the rejection of the interferon mechanism.", "Rescue test: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (allotopic or mitochondria-targeted expression of ATP6, or mitochondrial transfer/cybrid replacement with APOE3-derived mitochondria) should reduce citrate export, SREBF1/SCD transcript levels and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts in APOE4 cells without altering APOE genotype. No change in the lipogenic program after successful restoration of ATP-synthase assembly would weaken the proposed chain.", "Internal consistency check: the mtDNA deficit should be uniform across the mitochondrial polycistronic transcripts. The supplied data already violate this in part (gene:MT-ND4L +1.95 and gene:MT-ND5 +1.93 rise while gene:MT-ND4, on the same bicistronic ND4L/ND4 message, falls -1.80); if targeted RT-qPCR confirms that mtDNA-encoded transcripts are not coordinately reduced, step 2 is an artefact and the hypothesis should be discarded in favour of a primary lysosomal-lipid mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_156", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): every nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcript in the supplied differential-expression rows is higher in APOE4 (38/38 NDUF/UQCR/COX/ATP5/SDH rows, all effects \u003e= +1.02, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME +5.20), together with TCA transcripts (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54), so the nuclear side of the machine is transcriptionally expanded relative to the selected-gene background (median effect +1.46).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, contrast): the mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts fall in the bottom fifth of the same list (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, 5th percentile, adjusted p 9.1e-228; gene:MT-CYB -2.32; gene:MT-ND4 -1.80; gene:MT-CO2 -1.33), giving a nuclear-versus-mitochondrial contrast that is independent of the overall upward shift of the list (Mann-Whitney p = 9.1e-04).", "Step 3 (inferred, unmeasured): because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded core subunits in fixed stoichiometry, the reduced mtDNA-encoded supply is proposed to cap the number of fully assembled complexes (especially ATP synthase, whose MT-ATP6 transcript shows the largest deficit) despite the surplus of nuclear subunits; assembled-complex amount, membrane potential and respiration were not measured here.", "Step 4 (inferred flux): with oxidative disposal of acetyl-CoA/NADH constrained, TCA intermediates are predicted to be exported rather than fully oxidised, consistent with the strongly elevated citrate carrier transcript gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47), gene:ACSS2 (+2.93) and adenine-nucleotide carrier gene:SLC25A5 (+5.56); no metabolite or isotope-tracing data are supplied.", "Step 5 (measured RNA): a lipogenic/sterol transcriptional program is co-elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87) along with esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) and gene:APOE (+1.24), which we interpret as increased flux into fatty acid, sterol and neutral-lipid synthesis.", "Step 6 (measured RNA): the degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded in parallel (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSK +7.36; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51; hydrolase set enriched versus background, Mann-Whitney p = 3.6e-03), which we read as an adaptive response to an increased lipid/sterol and membrane-turnover load rather than as a primary lesion.", "Step 7 (inferred stress signalling, not interferon): mitochondrial-stress relay transcripts gene:DELE1 (+4.82) and gene:DDIT3 (+2.79) are elevated while the NAD salvage transcript gene:NAMPT is reduced (-2.62), whereas canonical interferon-stimulated genes are absent from the supplied differential rows and NF-kB target transcripts are not enriched above the shifted background (Mann-Whitney p = 0.17); we therefore assign the phenotype to metabolic rather than innate-immune signalling."], "title": "Mito-nuclear OXPHOS stoichiometry mismatch, not interferon/inflammatory signalling, is the primary bottleneck in APOE4 microglia and diverts carbon into SREBP-driven lipogenesis with lysosomal expansion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26381863161392755, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2717187205214222, "cosine_similarity": 0.37905646198628684, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_156", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875954692556634, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26381863161392755, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2717187205214222, "cosine_similarity": 0.37905646198628684, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5875954692556634, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.798775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 158}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_135", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base; only the sign and the relative rank of effects within this list are interpreted, never the absolute fold change, and set-level statements are made against the strongly up-shifted background of this list (median effect +1.46, 77% positive) rather than against zero.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway engagement only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, SREBP-2 cleavage, cholesterol localization, esterification flux and efflux are inferred and were not measured here.", "Protein spots have multi-gene candidate lists (median 5 candidates per spot), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spots are used only as weak corroboration or as an absence of a strong chaperone signal.", "Genotype effects are assumed to be cell-intrinsic to microglia despite astrocyte co-culture; ambient RNA, cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures, and clone-specific effects are not excluded, and biological replicate structure was not supplied.", "Causality is not established by these data: the loop described is a proposed generator of the observed pattern, and directionality must be tested by the perturbations below."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting step is delivery of hydrolysis-derived lipid (cholesterol and sphingolipid backbones) out of the endolysosome to the ER, not luminal hydrolase capacity and not ER protein-folding stress. The discovery data show a coherent, rank-enriched induction of lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB-associated transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB) together with an internally consistent sterol-synthesis and sterol-uptake transcript program (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1), a combination expected when total cellular lipid load is high but the ER-accessible sterol pool that gates SCAP/SREBP-2 remains low. We propose, not demonstrate, that this coexistence reflects lysosomal sequestration of lipid; the sterol program then increases uptake and synthesis, and the surplus is esterified (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD) into stored neutral lipid rather than being returned to the regulatory ER pool, closing a feed-forward loop. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is retained only as an alternative: as a gene set it is not enriched above the strongly up-shifted background and the ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are unchanged (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005).", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely mobilizing lysosomal cholesterol to the ER in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 re-supply) should, within hours and before any change in lysosomal biogenesis transcripts, collapse the sterol-synthesis program (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR transcripts) and reduce nuclear SREBP-2 toward APOE3 levels. If the sterol program remains elevated after lysosomal cholesterol is demonstrably mobilized, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Localization test: filipin or a D4H/GRAM ER-accessible-cholesterol reporter should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 lysosomal free cholesterol with equal or lower ER-accessible cholesterol. Finding a high ER-accessible pool in APOE4 together with elevated SREBP-2 targets would falsify the sensing-based step and favour direct transcriptional rewiring.", "Feed-forward test: blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or LDLR knockdown) should reduce lysosomal lipid load and partially normalize both the lysosomal and the sterol-synthesis transcript modules in APOE4; no reduction in the lysosomal module would weaken the loop claim.", "Storage-arm test: SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester into free sterol, raise ER-accessible cholesterol and lower SREBP-2 targets while increasing free-cholesterol toxicity; unchanged SREBP-2 targets under confirmed esterification blockade would weaken step 5.", "Negative/specificity prediction that would weaken the whole mechanism if it fails in the opposite direction: reducing ER folding stress (PERK inhibition, IRE1 inhibition or TUDCA) should NOT normalize the sterol-synthesis or lysosomal transcript modules. If UPR inhibition alone normalizes them, the assigned ER-proteostasis mechanism should replace this one.", "Functional prediction: APOE4 microglia should show reduced clearance of an exogenous lipid load (fluorescent LDL, myelin or apoptotic-cell cargo) measured as delayed disappearance of label from LAMP1-positive compartments, despite equal or greater hydrolase transcript and activity levels; equal clearance kinetics would falsify the bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_135", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred compartment state): APOE4 microglia carry higher steady-state transcript levels for lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and endolysosomal regulators (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB). We infer an expanded or chronically engaged endolysosomal compartment; compartment volume, acidification and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred flux bottleneck, not measured): lipid cargo delivered per unit time exceeds the capacity of the lysosome-to-ER sterol/sphingoid export step, so free cholesterol and sphingolipid intermediates accumulate in the lysosomal lumen. NPC1 and LIPA transcripts are absent from the supplied differential list and no lipid, filipin or organelle-fractionation measurement is supplied, so this luminal pool is an inference, not an observation. gene:NPC2 and gene:GBA transcript increases are read as compensation, not as evidence of restored egress; the decreased autophagosome-lysosome SNARE transcript gene:STX17 is consistent with, but does not prove, a delivery/fusion constraint.", "Step 3 (inferred regulatory consequence): because the ER/SCAP-accessible sterol pool is not replenished, SREBP-2 processing stays de-repressed despite a high total lipid burden, producing the coherent sterol-synthesis transcript program (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1). gene:INSIG1 induction is itself an SREBP target and indicates pathway activity, not feedback shutdown. Nuclear SREBP-2 protein was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): the same de-repressed state raises lipid- and lipoprotein-uptake transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), so more substrate is routed back into the constrained endolysosome, closing a feed-forward loop that sustains steps 1-3 under mock conditions.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred storage): surplus sterol and fatty acid are channelled into esterification and desaturation (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL), which we infer diverts lipid into cytoplasmic neutral-lipid stores that are metabolically inert with respect to the ER sensor; droplet number, cholesteryl-ester mass and efflux (ABCA1/ABCG1 not in the supplied data) were not measured.", "Step 6 (negative arm, partly measured): ER protein-folding stress is not the primary driver. Individual UPR transcripts rise (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3), but the ER-proteostasis set as a whole sits at the background rank and includes decreases (gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:PDIA3), and the spots whose candidate lists contain the ER chaperones GRP94/BiP show no significant change (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005). We therefore place UPR activity downstream or parallel, secondary to lipid handling."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid egress, not ER folding stress, is the APOE4 bottleneck: trapped lysosomal sterol keeps the ER sterol sensor de-repressed and drives a feed-forward uptake-synthesis-esterification loop"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24096296569803935, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2644971260929213, "cosine_similarity": 0.37880814207089863, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_135", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6024983818770226, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24096296569803935, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2644971260929213, "cosine_similarity": 0.37880814207089863, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6024983818770226, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71361, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 159}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_104", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |log fold change| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with an unspecified logarithm base; we therefore interpret each gene only by its rank relative to the other selected rows, not by absolute magnitude, and treat absent genes (HK1, PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, G6PD, CPT1A, PDK1) as unmeasured rather than unchanged.", "Directional transcript changes in HK2/HK3/PFKP and in MPC2/ACSS2/OXCT1/TCA/ETC genes translate at least partly into corresponding enzyme abundance and pathway flux; no enzyme activity, metabolite, isotope-tracing or respirometry measurement is supplied.", "The strong global upward shift (RNA mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77% of rows positive) reflects selection and possible compositional normalisation, so genes that move downward against this background (the hexokinase/PPP set) carry more directional weight than upward-moving genes.", "The 92 protein spots each carry 5-6 candidate genes and cannot identify a specific protein; they are excluded from the supporting evidence and used only as a limitation.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture; the extracellular lactate, ketone and fatty-acid supply that this mechanism assumes is available was not measured, and part of the genotype effect could be transmitted through astrocytes.", "Cell-intrinsic APOE4 causation is assumed only as a hypothesis; the isogenic design supports genotype association, not an established causal chain."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a transcriptional configuration in which the committed glucose-phosphorylation step of glycolysis and the glucose-6-phosphate-consuming pentose-phosphate arm are selectively down-weighted (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PFKFB2, PGD, TALDO1 all fall below the strongly upward global background), while glucose-transport capacity, mitochondrial pyruvate import, alternative-substrate catabolism (acetate, ketone body, fatty-acid, amino-acid) and TCA/nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts rise coordinately. We hypothesise that the hexokinase step, not glucose supply, is the primary bottleneck, so APOE4 microglia sustain ATP and acetyl-CoA production from non-glucose carbon and are correspondingly less able to mount a rapid hexokinase-dependent glycolytic burst; causality is not established by these correlative RNA and protein-spot measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or combined BPTES/etomoxir should depress oxygen consumption rate and ATP more strongly in APOE4 than in APOE3 microglia, whereas hexokinase inhibition with 2-deoxyglucose should depress ATP, phagocytic capacity and extracellular acidification more strongly in APOE3 than in APOE4. If APOE4 is equally or more sensitive to 2-deoxyglucose, or shows no extra sensitivity to UK5099/BPTES/etomoxir, the proposed bottleneck and substrate switch are both weakened.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show a lower fraction of glucose-derived carbon (m+2 citrate, m+3 lactate) in APOE4, while 13C-glutamine, 13C-palmitate, 13C-acetate or 13C-beta-hydroxybutyrate should contribute a higher fraction to TCA intermediates. Equal or higher glucose-derived labelling in APOE4 falsifies step 2.", "Seahorse profiling should show lower glycolytic capacity/reserve after oligomycin in APOE4 with equal or higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption rate. Reduced oxygen consumption together with reduced glycolysis would instead favour a general mitochondrial-deficiency alternative.", "Hexokinase enzymatic activity and HK2 protein in APOE4 lysates should be lower than APOE3; because HK1 was not measured, equal total hexokinase activity with normal glucose-6-phosphate levels would specifically weaken step 2 while leaving step 4 intact.", "Genetic rescue: HK2 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore glycolytic reserve and 2-deoxyglucose sensitivity toward APOE3 values without requiring change in MPC2 or TCA transcripts; failure to restore glycolytic reserve would show the bottleneck lies elsewhere.", "Blue-native analysis of complex IV/V assembly and mtDNA copy number should not be reduced in APOE4; a clear assembly deficit combined with the observed decrease in mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) would favour the mitonuclear-mismatch alternative in which nuclear ETC/TCA upregulation is compensatory rather than a marker of higher oxidative flux."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_104", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): glucose-transport transcripts increase (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73) together with the monocarboxylate importer gene:SLC16A1 (+1.12), so trans-membrane substrate uptake capacity is not the limiting element.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred enzyme activity/flux): the committed phosphorylation of glucose is down-weighted - gene:HK2 (-3.67, adj p 8e-191), gene:HK3 (-1.12), with gene:PFKP (-3.08) and gene:PFKFB2 (-1.10) down and the PFK-1 brake gene:TIGAR (+1.14) up; all sit in the lowest quintile-to-third of a distribution whose median is +1.46. Inferred, not measured: lower glucose-6-phosphate generation and lower glycolytic flux per unit glucose taken up.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred partitioning): the glucose-6-phosphate-consuming pentose-phosphate arm is also reduced (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32), so the restricted hexose-phosphate pool is not simply rerouted to NADPH/ribose production; NADPH itself is unmeasured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): non-glucose carbon entry routes are up - mitochondrial pyruvate carrier gene:MPC2 (+7.98), acetate activation gene:ACSS2 (+2.93), ketone-body utilisation gene:OXCT1 (+4.72), fatty-acid uptake/handling gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:FABP5 (+1.13), gene:HADHA (+2.86), gene:ETFA (+3.55), gene:ACOX1 (+1.24), gene:CROT (+1.03), and amino-acid catabolism gene:BCAT1 (+1.32), gene:BCAT2 (+6.42), gene:GLUD1 (+3.17), gene:GLS (+1.35), gene:GOT1 (+6.43), gene:ABAT (+1.54), gene:SLC1A5 (+1.55).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred oxidative capacity): TCA-cycle and nuclear-encoded electron-transport transcripts rise coherently above background (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3G, gene:MDH1, gene:SDHB, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1, gene:NDUFB8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS; 26-gene mitochondrial set median +3.04, permutation p_up=0.0006 against the same dataset), with gene:PCK2 (+1.21) indicating cataplerotic remodelling rather than glucose-fed anaplerosis.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred consequence): surplus acetyl-CoA and fatty-acid carbon is directed into esterification and storage rather than glycolytic intermediates (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:APOE +1.24); lipid pools, droplets and localisation were not measured here."], "title": "Hexokinase-step restriction of glucose commitment redirects APOE4 microglial carbon to mitochondrial oxidation of non-glucose substrates"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17956750153142498, "cosine_similarity": 0.3784932004398119, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_104", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5955307443365696, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17956750153142498, "cosine_similarity": 0.3784932004398119, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5955307443365696, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61456075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 160}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_071", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level statistics are therefore judged against the selected list's own strongly positive background (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, 77% up), not against zero.", "The global upward RNA shift is at least partly technical (normalisation, ambient RNA, or per-cell RNA-content differences between genotypes) rather than genuine global transcriptional amplification; if it is entirely biological the lysosomal enrichment shrinks but does not invert.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for lysosomal enzyme and v-ATPase protein amount; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, luminal lipid, cholesterol pools, droplets, TFEB localisation, and any uptake or degradation flux were NOT measured in this dataset and are inferred only.", "Protein spots are ambiguous: each carries multiple candidate genes, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; spot-level direction is used only as weak corroboration.", "Astrocyte co-culture means part of the genotype effect may be non-cell-autonomous (APOE4 astrocyte lipid supply) rather than microglia-intrinsic.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the extremely small adjusted p-values may be inflated by pseudoreplication across cells within few donors/wells."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, above-background induction of CLEAR/lysosomal transcripts (hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, lysosomal membrane proteins) together with lysosomal-stress and lipid-scavenging markers, while sterol-synthesis transcripts are not suppressed. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is lysosomal degradation-and-egress capacity for internalised lipid/lipoprotein cargo: uptake flux exceeds clearance flux, lysosomal cargo accumulates, MiT/TFE signalling compensates transcriptionally, and the ER regulatory sterol pool is never repleted, locking cells into a self-sustaining lipid-laden state. All flux, localisation, and causal statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: In APOE4 microglia, relieving the egress/clearance bottleneck (e.g. 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or an NPC1/NPC2-independent sterol-shuttling manoeuvre) should reduce filipin/BODIPY-positive lysosomal lipid AND simultaneously repress the sterol-synthesis transcripts (LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR24, SREBF2) toward APOE3 levels, while at most modestly reducing uptake-receptor transcripts. If lysosomal lipid falls but SREBP-target transcripts stay elevated, the proposed sensing-uncoupling step is wrong.", "SEPARATING BOTTLENECK FROM UPTAKE: Blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or knockdown, or lipoprotein-free medium) should collapse the CLEAR/hydrolase and LGALS3/GPNMB induction in APOE4 cells to near-APOE3 levels. If the lysosomal transcript program persists at full amplitude with no exogenous lipid load, the driver is a cell-intrinsic MiT/TFE or lysosomal-biogenesis defect rather than cargo overload, weakening this mechanism.", "TESTING THE COMPENSATION CLAIM: Despite higher hydrolase transcripts, measured bulk lysosomal degradative flux per cell (DQ-BSA or LysoSensor-normalised cathepsin activity, and DQ-lipid dequenching) in APOE4 should be equal to or LOWER than APOE3. If APOE4 shows proportionally increased degradative flux matching its transcript increase, the 'capacity is limiting' claim fails.", "TFEB DEPENDENCE: TFEB/TFE3/TFEC knockdown should abolish the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript difference between genotypes and worsen lipid accumulation in APOE4 more than in APOE3. No genotype-selective worsening would weaken step 4.", "SPECIFICITY CONTROL: The genotype difference should be lipid-load dependent - loading APOE3 microglia with myelin debris or acetylated LDL should phenocopy the APOE4 lysosomal transcript signature. Failure to phenocopy would argue for an APOE4-specific mechanism unrelated to cargo load.", "NEGATIVE/WEAKENING RESULT: Because 32/34 lysosomal genes are up against a background that is already 77-89% up, if a properly normalised unbiased transcriptome (e.g. spike-in normalised) removes the global shift and the lysosomal set then shows no enrichment over the residual background, this hypothesis is substantially weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake and opsonin machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22 q=3.4e-117; gene:CD36; gene:COLEC12; gene:STAB1; gene:MRC1; gene:CD163; gene:CLEC7A; gene:TREM2; gene:SLCO2B1; gene:APOE), which we infer raises internalisation flux of lipoproteins and lipid-rich debris into the endolysosome. Internalisation rate itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred, primary bottleneck): Delivered cargo exceeds the hydrolytic and sterol-egress capacity of the lysosome, so undigested lipid/sterol accumulates in the lysosomal lumen and limbs of the pathway downstream of uptake. This is the proposed rate-limiting node; luminal lipid was not measured here.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): Lysosomal stress/expansion markers rise coherently - gene:LGALS3 (+2.37 q=1.0e-113, a lysosomal-membrane-damage sensor), gene:GPNMB (+1.11 q~0), gene:ACP5, gene:SLC11A1, gene:SCARB2 - consistent with, but not proof of, luminal overload and limited membrane integrity.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): MiT/TFE transcription factor transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38; gene:TFEC +1.71 q=5e-141) and 32/34 measured CLEAR/lysosomal genes move up, with a set median of +1.75 versus the global selected-gene median of +1.46 (q-stratum-matched permutation p_up=0.033; q\u003c1e-20 subset p_up=0.012). We infer increased MiT/TFE transcriptional activity as the compensatory response; TFEB nuclear localisation and protein were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): The compensatory hydrolase/v-ATPase induction (gene:CTSB +5.52; gene:CTSD +2.86 q=4.7e-226; gene:CTSH; gene:GBA +6.71; gene:GAA +9.96; gene:HEXA; gene:HEXB; gene:SMPD1; gene:NAGLU; gene:SGSH; gene:ATP6V1A; gene:ATP6V0D1) does not restore clearance, because the limiting step is post-hydrolysis sterol egress rather than hydrolase amount; gene:M6PR (-1.70 q=5e-92) and gene:IDS (-1.62) are down, indicating the induction is incomplete and mannose-6-phosphate-dependent enzyme delivery may be constrained.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred sterol sensing): The ER regulatory sterol pool is inferred to remain unrepleted, since SREBP-pathway and sterol-handling transcripts stay at or above the global background rather than being repressed (gene:SREBF2; gene:SREBF1 +4.67; gene:LDLR; gene:INSIG1; gene:DHCR24; gene:DHCR7; gene:LSS; gene:ACAT2; gene:SCD +4.17) while esterification/storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1; gene:DGAT1), which we interpret as diversion of sterol into cholesteryl-ester/droplet pools instead of the sensing pool. This arm is the weakest evidentially (not enriched above background).", "Step 7 (inferred network state): Continued uptake plus unsatisfied sterol sensing plus limited egress forms a positive-feedback loop that stabilises a lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded APOE4 microglial state rather than a transient stress response."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a MiT/TFE-driven lysosomal hydrolase expansion that fails to clear an increased scavenger-receptor lipid/debris load, leaving lysosomal degradative-and-egress capacity as the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1680801707517089, "cosine_similarity": 0.3783683924436762, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6086990291262135, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1680801707517089, "cosine_similarity": 0.3783683924436762, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6086990291262135, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.936366, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 161}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_085", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 genes, all adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e=1 in an unspecified log base, 77% positive); program coherence is judged against that skewed background, genes within a program are co-regulated and not independent, and absent genes (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, CPT1A, NPC1, MRPL/MRPS) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for measured flux: no respiration, hydrolase activity, sterol-sensor state, lipid pool or trafficking rate was measured in this experiment; increased ETC/lysosomal transcripts do not by themselves establish increased oxidation or degradation, and decreased HK2/PFKP does not by itself establish a glycolytic bottleneck.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (keratin/actin dominated); all candidate identities are retained and no spot is treated as confirming an individual protein. No spot maps to an OXPHOS subunit, so the mitochondrial arm is untested at protein level.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3, day 30, mock, in 2D microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; replicate number is not supplied, so large single-gene effects (e.g. gene:ITGA6 +15.5, gene:ACTB -4.98) may partly reflect normalization, composition or subpopulation shifts rather than per-cell regulation.", "Effects described here are proposed for the measured mock condition; any inference about reduced reserve or failure under lipid/inflammatory challenge is prospective and not established by these data.", "Causality is not established: the ordering uptake -\u003e lysosome -\u003e mitochondria -\u003e SREBP is a hypothesis about routing consistent with the measured directions, not a demonstrated flux chain."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipid uptake receptors and a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program, for mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport and pyruvate/citrate carriers, and for SREBP-controlled sterol and fatty-acid synthesis plus esterification are all higher, while cytosolic glycolytic-entry and pentose-phosphate transcripts are lower. We propose this reflects increased routing of internalized lipid through lysosomal hydrolysis into mitochondrial oxidation with concurrent re-esterification into stored neutral lipid (a higher-throughput lipid-cycling state), rather than a rate-limiting ER unfolded-protein/secretory defect; the ER/secretory set is no more directionally coherent than the selected-list background (25/35 positive vs ~77% positive overall; permutation p_pos=0.84), so the assigned ER-proteostasis focus is rejected as primary. Flux, protein activity and lipid pools were not measured here; the claim is about a transcript-level state and its predicted, testable lipid and respirometry consequences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective respirometry: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, basal and maximal oxygen consumption should be higher with a larger etomoxir-/lalistat-sensitive (lipid-derived) fraction and a lower 2-DG-sensitive glycolytic fraction. Equal or lower APOE4 oxygen consumption, or an unchanged lipid-dependent fraction, would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective lipidomics (discriminates successful adaptation from failed compensation): APOE4 should show increased cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol with SCD-type monounsaturated acyl enrichment, while lysosomal hydrolase substrates (glucosylceramide, GM3, sulfatide, sphingomyelin, free cholesterol in the late endosome) are unchanged or lower despite higher gene:GBA/gene:HEXA/gene:SMPD1/gene:GLA. Concurrent accumulation of those hydrolase substrates would favour the competing interpretation of failed compensation for a lysosomal degradation block and would falsify the increased-throughput version of this mechanism.", "Prospective lysosome-to-mitochondria coupling test: inhibiting lysosomal acid lipase (lalistat) or v-ATPase (bafilomycin, low dose) should abolish most of the APOE4-specific increase in lipid-dependent oxygen consumption and should blunt the sterol-synthesis transcript signature (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR). If APOE4 respiration and sterol-gene induction are insensitive to these inhibitors, the proposed routing step is wrong.", "Prospective ER-stress control: chemical chaperones or UPR inhibition (TUDCA/4-PBA, ATF6 or PERK inhibition, ISRIB) in mock should NOT normalize the mitochondrial, lysosomal or sterol transcript differences. If they do normalize them, the rejected ER-proteostasis alternative should be preferred over this mechanism.", "Prospective sterol-sensor test: loading APOE4 microglia with exogenous free cholesterol (or U18666A-independent delivery of accessible ER cholesterol) should suppress the SREBP target set in APOE4 at least as strongly as in APOE3; a failure to suppress would indicate a sensing/egress defect and would require replacing the resynthesis step with a cholesterol-trapping mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (input, inferred): APOE4 changes lipoprotein/lipid handling so that more lipid cargo is delivered to the endolysosome; supported only indirectly by increased uptake/opsonin-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:APOE) - uptake flux itself is not measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): A CLEAR/TFEB-type lysosomal program is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:DPP7; acidification gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1; 23/25 represented members positive, median +2.30), raising hydrolytic and acidification capacity.", "Step 3 (inferred routing): Hydrolysis products (fatty acids, sphingoid/sterol backbones) are routed to mitochondria; represented beta-oxidation/anaplerotic transcripts are up (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:OXCT1 +4.72, gene:ACOX1, gene:CROT, gene:GLUD1) together with carriers (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56).", "Step 4 (measured transcripts): Mitochondrial oxidative machinery is expanded in a highly coherent way - 47/47 represented canonical ETC/TCA members positive (median +2.80; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS), permutation p_pos=2e-5 against the selected-list background.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts): Cytosolic glucose commitment is reduced despite higher transporters (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30 versus gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1), biasing ATP/redox supply toward the mitochondrial route in step 4.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts, feedback): ER/Golgi sterol-sensing output is high (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:MYLIP) with esterification/acylation genes (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07), i.e. liberated lipid is partly re-synthesised and re-esterified rather than fully consumed.", "Step 7 (downstream state): The combined loop is accompanied by a modest activated/lipid-associated microglial tone (gene:GPNMB, gene:CLEC7A, gene:ITGAX, gene:CD33, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:TREM2, gene:CXCL8, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD), predicting APOE4-specific neutral-lipid (cholesteryl ester/TAG, MUFA-enriched) accumulation with maintained or increased glycosphingolipid turnover."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-to-mitochondria lipid-catabolic state with SREBP-driven lipid resynthesis, not an ER-proteostasis defect"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4946183953033268, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2670936603344557, "cosine_similarity": 0.37835388502966294, "direction_accuracy": 0.4919093851132686, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mean_absolute_error": 0.57584142394822, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4946183953033268, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2670936603344557, "cosine_similarity": 0.37835388502966294, "direction_accuracy": 0.4919093851132686, "mean_absolute_error": 0.57584142394822, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.22431225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 31}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_015", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Elevated transcript abundance for lysosomal and lipogenic genes corresponds to increased protein and enzymatic capacity; this is not verified here, and the 2D-gel layer is neutral-to-contradictory (spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases average +0.13 log2 versus +0.35 for all 92 spots).", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong positive global shift (mean +1.39; 77.1% positive), so set-level enrichment is judged against that internal background rather than against zero; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and effects are left on the reported scale.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin identifications, so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein or as independent confirmation of any gene.", "The bottleneck assignment relies on relative under-induction of NPC2 inside an otherwise strongly induced CLEAR set; NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are not present in the supplied rows, so the egress module is only partially observed.", "Steady-state genotype comparison at one timepoint under mock treatment cannot establish direction of causation between the lysosomal, sterol-synthetic and lipogenic programs; a shared upstream driver (e.g. APOE4 lipoprotein particle properties) could induce all three in parallel.", "Cell-intrinsic interpretation assumes the astrocyte co-culture contributes similarly to APOE4 and APOE3 conditions."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated CLEAR/TFEB transcriptional program (22/22 lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB/MITF rows positive, mean effect +3.39 vs +1.39 list background) in which the sterol-transfer component NPC2 is only marginally induced (+1.17, 35th percentile of the list). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is lysosomal cholesterol/lipid egress rather than lysosomal hydrolysis: sterol delivered by upregulated uptake receptors is hydrolysed but poorly exported to the ER, so the ER regulatory sterol pool is inferred to remain low, SREBP-2 and SREBP-1 target transcripts stay induced (9/9 and 7/7 positive, including HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR, SREBF1, SCD), and the excess flux is predicted to be routed into SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent neutral-lipid stores and into secondary glycosphingolipid accumulation. Causality is not established by these data; all activity, flux, localisation and directionality statements are inferences from steady-state RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute cyclodextrin (HP-beta-CD) treatment or NPC2 overexpression in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal unesterified cholesterol (filipin/lysosome-targeted sterol sensor) AND normalise SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, DHCR7, LDLR) and cholesteryl-ester content toward APOE3 within 24-48 h, without first requiring reduction of hydrolase transcripts. If lysosomal sterol falls but SREBP-2 targets and cholesteryl esters remain APOE4-like, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong.", "Phenocopy: blocking lysosomal sterol egress in APOE3 microglia with U18666A should reproduce the joint signature (CLEAR/hydrolase induction plus persistently induced SREBP-2 targets plus increased cholesteryl esters and hexosylceramide). Failure to reproduce the co-induction pattern weakens the mechanism.", "Flux discrimination: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or SCD inhibition should reduce APOE4 cholesteryl-ester and monounsaturated triacylglycerol species while leaving the CLEAR transcriptional program elevated; if these inhibitors also abolish the lysosomal program, esterification is upstream rather than downstream and the ordering in the mechanism is wrong.", "Direct lipid test: quantitative lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia should show increased total and unesterified cholesterol, increased cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols enriched in 16:1/18:1 chains, and increased hexosylceramide/bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate. Absence of any cholesterol-pool or glycosphingolipid difference, with only phospholipid or ether-lipid changes, would falsify the claim.", "Rejection of the assigned ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 cells should NOT show canonical UPR activation (no BiP/HSPA5 protein induction, no XBP1 splicing, no eIF2-alpha-P/ATF4/CHOP protein rise), and PERK or IRE1 inhibitors should not normalise the lipid phenotype. Strong BiP/XBP1s induction, or rescue of the lipid phenotype by UPR inhibition, would favour an ER-stress mechanism over this one.", "Capacity test: lysosomal enzyme activity assays (GBA, HEXA, acid sphingomyelinase) and LAMP1 immunostaining should show increased lysosomal mass/activity in APOE4; if enzyme activity and lysosomal mass are unchanged despite the transcript differences, the assumed transcript-to-capacity link fails and the mechanism collapses to a transcriptional-only observation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE) and of endolysosomal trafficking components (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:DNM2). Inferred (not measured): increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosome.", "Measured: a coherent CLEAR-type program is elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:LAMP1). Inferred: expanded acidified degradative compartment with increased hydrolase capacity; enzymatic activity, lysosome number and pH were not measured.", "Measured: within this program the cholesterol-transfer protein transcript gene:NPC2 is induced far less (+1.17) than the hydrolases (set mean +3.50 excluding NPC2); NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, ABCA1 and ABCG1 rows are absent from the supplied data. Inferred bottleneck: hydrolytic capacity outruns the capacity to move unesterified sterol out of the lysosomal lumen to the ER/plasma membrane.", "Inferred: restricted lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer keeps the ER regulatory sterol pool low. Measured consequence consistent with this: every detected SREBP-2 target is up (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2), i.e. the cell transcriptionally behaves as sterol-poor despite elevated uptake-receptor transcripts.", "Measured: the lipogenic arm is also up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:FABP5). Inferred: increased monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply and ER esterification capacity divert the mislocalised sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets instead of efflux.", "Inferred lipid-phenotype endpoint: APOE4 microglia accumulate lysosomal unesterified cholesterol plus monounsaturated-chain-enriched cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols, together with secondary glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin-pathway intermediates that the induced gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA and gene:GLA transcripts are a compensatory response to; none of these lipid pools were measured here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a TFEB/MITF-driven lysosomal degradative program without matching lysosomal sterol-egress capacity, sustaining SREBP-driven synthesis and neutral-lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15851272015655576, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1600825226947011, "cosine_similarity": 0.3782735560453389, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6039935275080907, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15851272015655576, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1600825226947011, "cosine_similarity": 0.3782735560453389, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6039935275080907, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.107647, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 162}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_168", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strongly positive median (+1.46); all pathway claims are made relative to that internal background, and effect magnitudes are treated as ordinal, not as absolute fold changes.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; assigning protein_spot:027/053/055/057/058/067/069 to cathepsin D/B/HEXB processing forms is an assumption, not an identification, and the protein set has its own positive shift (median +0.48).", "Transcript changes in this astrocyte co-culture are attributed to the microglial compartment as reported by the 10X Flex comparison; replicate number is not supplied, so no independent variance estimate is possible.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, pH, lysosomal-morphology, autophagic-flux or protein-localization measurement is supplied; substrate accumulation, luminal hydrolytic flux, hydrolase maturation state and TFEB nuclear localization are inferred, not observed.", "Key sphingolipid genes (SPTLC1/2, CERS2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, ASAH1, PSAP, NEU1, GALC) and most autophagy/mTORC1 genes are absent from the supplied rows; absence is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast is assumed free of clone-specific confounders beyond genotype; correlation in this dataset does not establish causal direction."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia by carrying a higher endolysosomal degradative load: transcripts for acid hydrolases that act on sphingolipids and other glycoconjugates (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1, GBA2) and for v-ATPase subunits and TFEB are elevated well above the already positive background of this selected DE list, yet the hydrolase-candidate protein spots do not show a matching uniform increase and instead split in both directions. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is post-transcriptional: the amount/maturation of active luminal hydrolase (and its cofactor-dependent activity on membrane-embedded glycosphingolipid substrates) does not scale with the transcript induction, so effective catabolic flux per transcript is lower in APOE4, undegraded sphingolipid/glycolipid substrate accumulates in late endosomes-lysosomes, and this sustains the compensatory TFEB-type transcript program and a re-esterification/lipogenic transcript bias. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating activity-vs-transcript test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, mature-enzyme activity assays (GBA with LIMP2/saposin-competent lysate, total HEXA/HEXB, acid sphingomyelinase) should rise far less than their transcripts, i.e. an APOE4/APOE3 activity ratio near or below 1 despite large transcript increases, together with elevated LC-MS glucosylceramide, LacCer, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin. If activity scales proportionally with transcripts and these substrates are unchanged or lower in APOE4, the bottleneck claim is falsified and increased (not blocked) turnover becomes the better model.", "Reserve-capacity perturbation: acute partial GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) or ASM inhibition should produce a disproportionately larger increase in LysoTracker/LAMP1 area, glucosylceramide accumulation and lysosomal transcript induction in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal or smaller APOE4 responses would weaken the reduced-reserve-capacity step.", "Flux-restoring rescue: substrate reduction with a UGCG inhibitor (e.g. GENZ-123346/eliglustat) or GBA chaperone (ambroxol), or SCARB2/LIMP2 overexpression to improve GBA delivery, should selectively normalise lysosomal size, substrate lipids and the lysosomal/TFEB transcript module in APOE4 without a comparable effect in APOE3. No genotype-selective normalisation would falsify the sphingolipid-load framing and favour a generic lysosome-biogenesis or cell-state difference.", "Maturation-step test: immunoblot/pulse-chase of cathepsin D, cathepsin B and HEXB should show an APOE4 shift toward pro-forms or altered glycoforms (lower mature/pro ratio) matching the divergent 2D spots. If mature forms are increased in proportion to transcripts with an unchanged pro/mature ratio, mechanism step 4 fails and a purely transcriptional, flux-competent lysosome expansion should be adopted instead.", "Specificity control: if TFEB knockdown abolishes the hydrolase transcript module in APOE4 but leaves substrate lipids and lysosomal morphology unchanged, the transcript module is a bystander readout and the causal placement of the lysosomal lipid bottleneck upstream of the activation transcripts (APOE, TREM2, GPNMB) is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_168", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinate elevation of a lysosome-biogenesis transcript module above the list-wide background (TFEB +2.38; ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51; CTSK +7.36, GAA +9.96, NAGLU +5.91, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86; LAMP1 +1.38, SCARB2 +1.06); permutation mean of the combined lysosomal module is +3.13 vs list mean +1.39 (p=1e-4).", "Measured: within this module the sphingolipid-directed hydrolases are among the largest effects (GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, GBA2 +2.63, HEXB +2.17, GM2A +2.01, GLA +1.53; permutation mean +3.77, p=0.008), while sphingolipid de novo synthesis genes are largely absent from the supplied DE rows and glycosphingolipid-branch genes diverge (ST3GAL5 +2.17, GLTP +2.38 vs B4GALT5 -1.88).", "Inferred (not measured): the transcript induction is a demand signal rather than proof of flux; we posit that glucosylceramide/GM2-GM3/sphingomyelin substrate turnover per cell is limiting in APOE4, which would explain why the catabolic arm, not the synthetic arm, is the coherent transcriptional response.", "Inferred bottleneck: delivery/maturation of active hydrolase into the lumen is limiting. Consistent transcript-level signal is a split M6P-targeting pathway (GNPTG +3.02 and IGF2R +2.02 up but M6PR -1.72 down) and, at protein level, hydrolase-candidate 2D spots that change in opposite directions (protein_spot:027 +0.58, :053 +1.54, :055 +0.58, :057 +0.58 versus :058 -0.85, :067 -1.00, :069 -1.38), a pattern expected from redistribution between processing/PTM forms rather than a uniform rise in mature enzyme. Spot identities are ambiguous (multi-candidate), so this step is the weakest link.", "Inferred consequence: accumulation of partially degraded sphingolipid/membrane lipid in the late endosome-lysosome keeps TFEB-type signalling engaged (feed-forward with step 1) and diverts liberated lipid into storage/esterification and de novo membrane lipid synthesis, consistent with SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25.", "Inferred downstream state: the lipid-laden lysosomal phenotype accompanies only a modest lipid-response/activation transcript shift (APOE +1.24, TREM2 +1.28, GPNMB +1.11), all near the list median (+1.46), so we place the lysosomal lipid bottleneck upstream of, and not explained by, a strong inflammatory activation program."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase transcript program that is not matched by mature hydrolase protein, making luminal sphingolipid/glycolipid catabolism the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12391537126610788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1757865935404277, "cosine_similarity": 0.37826466934945757, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_168", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6206472491909385, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12391537126610788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1757865935404277, "cosine_similarity": 0.37826466934945757, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6206472491909385, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.707406, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 163}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_053", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive offset (median +1.46, 77% positive), so only within-list relative comparisons (set median vs global median, percentile rank) are interpreted; absolute fold-change magnitudes are taken as ordinal, not quantitative.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the size of a transcriptional program, not for enzyme activity, protein amount, acidification, localisation or degradative flux; no pH, lipid, flux or imaging measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots average ~4.8 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are cited only as weak, direction-mixed corroboration and never as identified cathepsin or v-ATPase abundance.", "Key members of the proposed limiting module were not measured in this list (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, GRN, PSAP, MCOLN1, LAMP2, CD63, PLIN2), so the 'membrane/egress lags' claim rests on the measured subset LAMP1/SCARB2/NPC2/CLN3/M6PR.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured; genotype effects on microglia could be partly non-cell-autonomous, and the mock, single-timepoint (day 30) design gives no temporal ordering."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia the luminal degradative program (TFEB/MITF-family targets: acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits) is transcriptionally scaled up well above the global upward shift of this differential-expression list, whereas the limiting endolysosomal membrane/export-receptor module (LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2, CLN3, M6PR) is not; we hypothesise that the resulting mismatch makes egress of digested lipid cargo from the endolysosome, rather than hydrolytic enzyme supply, the rate-limiting step, so that cargo-derived sterol and fatty acid are re-routed into esterification and storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, SREBF1) while ER sterol sensing stays unsatisfied (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, ACAT2, LDLR, INSIG1) and lysosomal-stress markers (LGALS3, GPNMB, FTH1) remain elevated. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, pH, localisation and lipid-pool statements are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving the membrane-side export step (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or re-expression/overexpression of a sterol-export component such as NPC1/NPC2, in APOE4 microglia) should lower stored cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content, reduce gene:SREBF2/gene:HMGCS1/gene:LSS/gene:LDLR transcripts and reduce gene:LGALS3/gene:GPNMB, while leaving the hydrolase transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:GAA) unchanged or lower. If instead overexpressing hydrolases (e.g. CTSB or GBA) normalises lipid storage and stress markers while export relief does not, the bottleneck is hydrolase dosage and this mechanism is wrong.", "Flux test: pulse-chase of a defined lipid-rich cargo (fluorescent myelin, oxLDL or apoptotic-cell membranes) should show slower per-lysosome cargo clearance and greater retention of cargo-derived sterol in LAMP1+ compartments in APOE4 than APOE3, despite equal or greater cathepsin activity per cell (measured by activity probe, not abundance). Equal or faster clearance with equal luminal retention would weaken the mechanism.", "Directional test of the storage arm: SOAT1 inhibition should redistribute cholesterol from cholesteryl esters to free cholesterol and worsen (not improve) LGALS3-positive lysosomal membrane damage in APOE4; if SOAT1 inhibition restores normal lysosomal morphology and lowers LGALS3/GPNMB, the esterification step is compensatory-protective in a different sense and the proposed loop is falsified.", "Specificity test against an acidification-primary alternative: ratiometric lysosomal pH and v-ATPase activity should be similar between APOE4 and APOE3 despite the raised v-ATPase transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C). A measurably higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH in APOE4 would relocate the bottleneck to acidification and weaken the egress-limited model.", "Protein-level test of the mismatch: quantitative immunoblot/targeted MS should show APOE4/APOE3 ratios for mature cathepsins and glycosidases exceeding those for LAMP1, SCARB2 and NPC2. Proportional scaling of membrane proteins with hydrolases would falsify the capacity-mismatch premise, as would demonstration that gene:M6PR loss is fully compensated by gene:IGF2R with unchanged hydrolase mannose-6-phosphate sorting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts of the MiT/TFE lysosomal-biogenesis factors (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC) and of many luminal acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1); the hydrolase set median (+2.86) is above the global list median (+1.46; permutation p ~0.009). Inferred: a lysosome-biogenesis program is engaged, not that hydrolase activity or acidification is higher.", "Measured: the endolysosomal membrane / cargo-export and hydrolase-receptor module does not scale with it (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CLN3 +1.17 all at or below the global median; gene:M6PR -1.72; set median at the 35th percentile, permutation p ~0.79). Inferred: per-lysosome membrane-side export capacity, including sterol handover and receptor recycling, lags behind luminal enzyme dosage.", "Measured: cargo-delivery and lipoprotein/lipid-uptake receptor transcripts are maintained or raised (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC). Inferred: continued or increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into an endolysosomal compartment whose export step is limiting, i.e. inferred cargo backlog rather than measured luminal lipid.", "Inferred flux consequence: sterol and fatty acid released by hydrolysis leave the endolysosome inefficiently and, once released, are captured by esterification/storage enzymes whose transcripts are raised (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:MGLL), biasing lipid disposal towards cytoplasmic cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol stores instead of return to the ER-plasma-membrane pool or efflux (efflux transporters other than gene:ABCA7 were not measured).", "Measured: the ER sterol-responsive program is simultaneously up (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1) despite high uptake-receptor expression. Inferred: ER-accessible sterol remains low because sterol is sequestered in endolysosomes and esterified stores, sustaining uptake and synthesis and feeding the backlog (a feed-forward loop).", "Measured: lysosome-stress/damage-associated transcripts are elevated (gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB, gene:FTH1) alongside the biogenesis program. Inferred: chronic membrane stress from undigested/undelivered lipid cargo keeps MiT/TFE signalling on, so lysosome number/enzyme transcripts rise without a matching rise in per-cargo clearance flux, which was not measured."], "title": "Membrane-limited endolysosomal cargo egress, not hydrolase dosage, is the APOE4 bottleneck in iPSC-microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24344568089103097, "cosine_similarity": 0.3777897223296725, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956796116504854, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24344568089103097, "cosine_similarity": 0.3777897223296725, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956796116504854, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5868745, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 164}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_079", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive and every row has |effect|\u003e1, so pathway direction was judged against that shifted background by permutation, and absence of a gene from the list means unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes (up to 15.5) are treated as rank/direction evidence only, not as fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding transporter, hydrolase and enzyme pools; no activity, flux, sterol pool, lipid droplet, or localisation measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous, corroborating-at-best evidence; no spot is assigned to a single protein.", "The two genotypes are assumed isogenic and matched for microglial differentiation state and for astrocyte content of the co-culture; ambient RNA from co-cultured astrocytes (e.g. gene:S100B) could contribute to some effects.", "TFEB and MITF transcript increases are assumed to indicate an active biogenesis program, although nuclear translocation, the actual regulated step, was not measured."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia the coordinated transcriptional increase in scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake receptors and in TFEB/MITF-type endolysosomal machinery is not matched by a shutdown of sterol-synthesis and uptake feedback; we propose that the rate-limiting step is egress of lysosome-derived sterol to the ER sensing pool, so that internalized lipid is re-esterified and stored (SOAT1, DGAT1) while SREBP targets stay on, producing lipid-loaded endolysosomes, a chemokine-biased state, and a shift of clearance capacity away from actin/Rho-dependent particulate engulfment. Causality is not established by these data; the bottleneck is inferred from measured RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 overexpression) should lower filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol AND suppress SREBP targets (SCD, HMGCS1, LDLR, SREBF1) toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h, without requiring any change in cathepsin/v-ATPase transcripts. If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal cholesterol but leaves the SREBP target elevation intact, the proposed egress/feedback bottleneck is wrong and the SREBP arm is driven cell-autonomously by something upstream of sterol sensing.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should convert stored cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol and, if egress is the bottleneck, should NOT normalise SREBP targets while increasing free-sterol stress markers; normalisation of SREBP targets by SOAT1 inhibition alone would weaken the model.", "Uptake selectivity test: APOE4 microglia should show equal or higher DiI-AcLDL / fluorescent-lipoprotein uptake but equal or lower pHrodo-bead and apoptotic-neuron engulfment index relative to APOE3. If particulate engulfment is increased in proportion to receptor transcripts, mechanism step 5 fails and the cytoskeletal arm should be dropped.", "Capacity test: bafilomycin A1 or cathepsin inhibition should impair lipid clearance similarly in both genotypes (no genotype x drug interaction). A strong genotype-specific sensitivity would indicate that degradative capacity, not egress, is limiting and would weaken the primary bottleneck choice.", "Protein-level check: LAMP1/CTSD immunoblot or LysoTracker area should be higher in APOE4 while NPC1 protein and ER-sterol-dependent SREBP2 cleavage behave as predicted (increased nuclear SREBP2). Failure to see any increase in lysosomal compartment size or in nuclear SREBP2 would contradict steps 2 and 3, which currently rest on RNA plus ambiguous spots protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 and are opposed by protein_spot:067 and gene:CTSS."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and apoptotic-cell uptake receptors are uniformly higher in APOE4 (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, STAB1, MERTK, GAS6, PROS1, MFGE8, TREM2, LDLR, ABCA7, APOE; 18/18 receptor-set genes positive). Inferred, not measured: higher surface receptor density and higher receptor-mediated lipid/lipoprotein internalisation flux.", "Measured: the late-endosome/retromer/ESCRT and lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase modules are coherently higher (RAB7A, VPS26A, VPS35L, SNX3, CHMP4B, VPS28, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GAA, SMPD1, ATP6V1A/1H/0C) together with the biogenesis factors TFEB and MITF. Inferred: expansion and acidification competence of the degradative compartment, i.e. a TFEB/MITF-type response to cargo load, not a defect in hydrolase gene dosage.", "Measured: despite this load, ER sterol-feedback targets remain elevated (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, SCD, LDLR). Inferred: the ER/ACAT-accessible sterol pool is not sensed as replete, which is the proposed primary bottleneck - transfer of lysosome-derived cholesterol out of the limiting membrane to the ER (an NPC1/NPC2- and contact-site-dependent step whose key components NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 were not measured here).", "Measured: esterification and neutral-lipid storage enzymes are higher (SOAT1, DGAT1) with lipid-binding/handling genes FABP3, FABP5, SCD. Inferred: sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are routed to cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplets rather than to efflux or to feedback inhibition, sustaining a futile uptake-plus-synthesis cycle.", "Measured: actin/motor and Rho-GTPase effector transcripts are not co-elevated and several are strongly negative against a positively shifted background (ACTB, MYH9, RAC2, DOCK8, MYO1F, CORO2A down; ARHGDIA, ARHGAP1, ARHGAP35 up). Inferred and weakly supported: actin-dependent phagocytic-cup formation is not scaled up with receptor and lysosome capacity, so the extra capacity favours soluble/lipoprotein cargo over large particulate targets.", "Measured: chemokine/inflammasome-associated transcripts are higher (CXCL8, CXCL16, CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL3, CCL2, NLRP3, PYCARD, IL18, MYD88). Inferred: lipid-laden, sterol-mishandling endolysosomes are a plausible upstream driver of this secretory bias, but the direction of this link is not testable in the supplied data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand receptor-mediated lipid uptake and endolysosomal degradative capacity but stall at post-lysosomal sterol egress, diverting sterol into SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterified storage instead of feedback shutdown"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2423273676218978, "cosine_similarity": 0.37775724497957586, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mean_absolute_error": 0.595611650485437, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2423273676218978, "cosine_similarity": 0.37775724497957586, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.595611650485437, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.26175825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 165}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_068", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program coherence is judged against that 77% positive background, and absent genes (e.g. NPC1, ASAH1, PSAP, UGCG, ABCA1, SGMS1/2, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript increases for hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and SREBP targets are treated as changes in expressed capacity, not as measured enzyme activity, acidification, sterol pools, ceramide/glycosphingolipid levels, droplet content, or flux; every flux and localisation statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "Protein-spot measurements are multi-candidate 2D spots (69 of 92 spots list 5+ candidates; KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate) and are used only for compatibility tests; no spot is read as confirmation of an individual protein.", "The transcriptional differences are read as a stable APOE4 cell state under mock rather than a response to an acute stimulus; no time course is supplied and replicate structure is 'not supplied in workbook'.", "Descriptive coherence and the resampling comparisons used here treat genes as independent; they are not formal enrichment tests, and co-regulated genes inflate apparent coherence.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipid/lipoprotein cargo; the cargo source itself was not measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell-state shift: transcripts for lipid/debris uptake receptors, endolysosomal acid hydrolases (with sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid-degrading enzymes among the largest effects) and the vacuolar ATPase are coherently higher, while esterification/storage and SREBP-driven sterol-synthesis transcripts are also higher. We propose that increased cargo influx is met by increased degradative capacity, but the liberated sterol/lipid is preferentially routed to esterification, droplet storage and lipid re-synthesis rather than to the ER regulatory pool, so ER sterol sensing continues to signal deficit and drives feed-forward LDLR/SREBP output. This is a mis-routed high-throughput state, not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck; all fluxes and pools are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating (routing vs matched throughput): in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, quantitative lipidomics/imaging should show higher cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid droplet content and higher lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin-derived species in APOE4 despite the higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 shows equal or lower stored/esterified lipid with equal lysosomal lipid, the routing-to-storage step (Step 4) fails and the mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective: SOAT1 (or DGAT1) inhibition in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, LSS) toward APOE3 levels by restoring ER-accessible sterol, without abolishing the lysosomal-hydrolase increase. Unchanged SREBP targets after esterification blockade would weaken Steps 4-5.", "Prospective: blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, TREM2 loss, or removal of astrocyte-derived lipid cargo) should attenuate the lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and SREBP transcript differences in APOE4. Persistence of these differences with uptake blocked would show the program is cell-autonomous transcriptional rewiring upstream of cargo, weakening Step 1 as the driver.", "Prospective challenge (distinguishes increased capacity from failed compensation): after a bolus of fluorescent myelin or BODIPY-sphingomyelin, APOE4 should show initial degradation rate greater than or equal to APOE3 (higher capacity) but greater late neutral-lipid retention. Slower initial degradation and substrate accumulation in APOE4 would favour a degradative bottleneck / failed compensation instead of the proposed mis-routed high-throughput state.", "Prospective: acidification and selected hydrolase activity assays (lysoSensor/ratiometric pH, GBA, HEXA/B, acid sphingomyelinase activity) should show APOE4 activity equal to or above APOE3 in the mock condition. Reduced enzyme activity or a less acidic lysosome despite the higher transcripts would contradict Step 2 and reframe the transcript increases as compensation for a defect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 raises expression of scavenger/phagocytic/efferocytic receptors and opsonin machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:ITGB5, gene:C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, gene:ANXA1 +4.15; 20/20 represented members positive vs 77% positive in this selected list), which we infer increases delivery of membrane-lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts; inferred capacity): A coordinated endolysosomal biogenesis program is higher (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC; 24/26 represented acid hydrolases positive, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86; v-ATPase/lysosomal membrane 16/16 positive, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:ARL8B), raising nominal acidification and hydrolytic capacity in parallel with cargo.", "Step 3 (focus arm, supported but not selective): Sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid catabolic transcripts are among the most extreme members of this program (gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:SUMF1 +2.01, gene:SGPL1 +1.09; 10/10 positive), with ceramide-handling/transfer and headgroup genes moderately higher (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERK, gene:GLTP +2.38, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17; exception gene:B4GALT5 -1.88). Their median effect (2.40) is not separable from non-sphingolipid hydrolases (1.92), so sphingolipid turnover is a prominent component of the general lysosomal program, not an identified selective driver.", "Step 4 (routing step; inferred): Sterol and fatty acid released from degraded cargo are channelled to esterification, storage and re-synthesis (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5, gene:FABP5, gene:FABP3) rather than replenishing the ER-accessible sterol pool.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts): Consistent with an ER pool that still reads sterol deficit, the SREBP axis and its targets are uniformly higher (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP +1.28), giving feed-forward influx and de novo synthesis despite the raised uptake.", "Step 6 (downstream state): The combination stabilises a lipid-associated/degradative microglial identity (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:LGALS1, gene:CLEC7A, gene:ITGAX, gene:APOE, gene:IGF1, gene:SLC11A1, gene:ATP6V0D2; 15/15 positive) with remodelled endosomal sorting and fusion machinery (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:VAMP3 +2.99; opposing gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:RAB27A -2.52, gene:STX17 -2.06), i.e. altered routing rather than uniformly increased late-endosomal traffic."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt an uptake-and-storage-biased lipid state: raised endolysosomal catabolic capacity with lipid routed to esterification/storage instead of the ER sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14187866927592954, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13317678591132487, "cosine_similarity": 0.3774343406683766, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140453074433657, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14187866927592954, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13317678591132487, "cosine_similarity": 0.3774343406683766, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6140453074433657, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.28026025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 32}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_056", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |reported log fold change| \u003e= 1.0), so the correct null for any module is the list-wide shift (mean +1.39, 77% positive), not zero; all module claims here are made against that background.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no conversion or absolute fold-change interpretation is made.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein/complex availability only at the level of direction; no lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, autophagic flux, oxygen consumption, ATP level, lipid pool, or protein localization was measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous proteoform-level measurements, never as identified proteins; they are used only as weak or counter-evidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture, differentiation efficiency and cell-composition differences between the APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed not to be the sole driver of the module-level differences; this is untested here because replicate structure and cell-type proportions were not supplied.", "The strong global upward shift could partly reflect normalization, depth or selection asymmetry rather than genuine global upregulation; module-level comparisons are used specifically to be robust to this."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily through a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the TFEB/CLEAR endolysosomal machinery (v-ATPase subunits, cathepsins, luminal glycosidases/sphingolipid hydrolases) together with strong induction of nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcripts, which we interpret as a compensatory response to a rate-limiting step at ATP-dependent endolysosomal acidification and cargo degradation rather than as an achieved increase in degradative flux; the canonical interferon-stimulated and NF-kB inflammatory modules are not elevated above the strong global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list, so an inflammatory/interferon mechanism is rejected for this dataset.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (throughput vs capacity): Load isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a fixed, quantified cargo (DQ-BSA, pHrodo-labelled myelin or synaptosomes) and measure internalized cargo and degradation separately. The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalization in APOE4 but a lower degraded-fraction per internalized particle and equal-or-higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH by ratiometric LysoSensor/pHrodo, despite the higher CLEAR transcript levels. If APOE4 instead degrades cargo faster or equally per particle and has a more acidic lysosomal pH, the bottleneck claim is falsified and the CLEAR induction should be read as increased capacity.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (bioenergetic dependence): Force oxidative ATP production by replacing glucose with galactose. The mechanism predicts a genotype-by-substrate interaction, with APOE4 showing a disproportionate fall in cargo degradation rate and lysosomal acidification and a disproportionate fall in spare respiratory capacity relative to APOE3. Absence of any genotype-by-substrate interaction weakens step 4-6.", "Prediction 3 (TFEB dependence): TFEB knockdown should selectively collapse cargo clearance and v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript levels in APOE4 more than in APOE3, while TFEB or TFEB-S211A overexpression should only partially rescue APOE4 clearance and should not normalize it if ATP supply is co-limiting. A full rescue by TFEB overexpression alone would argue that transcriptional capacity, not throughput, is limiting.", "Prediction 4 (v-ATPase specificity): Sub-saturating bafilomycin A1 or concanamycin A titration should produce a left-shifted dose-response for cargo-degradation failure in APOE4 versus APOE3 (reduced reserve of acidification). Identical dose-response curves would weaken the acidification-throughput bottleneck.", "Prediction 5 (rejection of the interferon/inflammation alternative): Blocking IFNAR1 or inhibiting JAK1/2 (ruxolitinib) under mock conditions should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences in CLEAR and nuclear OXPHOS transcripts and in cargo clearance essentially unchanged, and unbiased whole-transcriptome profiling should not reveal a coherent ISG effector signature (MX1, OAS1/2/3, IFIT1/3, ISG15, STAT1/2). Detection of such a signature, or normalization of the APOE4 phenotype by JAK inhibition, would falsify the negative arm of this hypothesis and support an interferon mechanism instead.", "Prediction 6 (mitonuclear arm, weakest link): Targeted assays (mtDNA copy number, strand-specific quantification of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2/MT-ND4 and of assembled complex I/III/IV/V by BN-PAGE or complex-specific activity) should show reduced assembled holo-complex per unit nuclear-subunit protein in APOE4. Equal holo-complex assembly and equal mtDNA-encoded transcript levels by an orthogonal method would remove step 5, which the discovery data already flag as unreliable because MT-ND4L and MT-ND4 arise from one bicistronic transcript yet move in opposite directions."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): Transcripts for cargo-binding uptake receptors are uniformly higher in APOE4 (SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, STAB1, MFGE8, FCGR1A/FCGR3A, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, MERTK/GAS6; 20/20 positive, module mean +2.19). Increased cargo influx into the endolysosomal system is INFERRED flux, not measured here.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred transcriptional activity): TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated and the CLEAR target set moves coherently above the list-wide background (30 genes, mean +2.58 vs global +1.39, permutation p = 0.011; MWU p = 0.011), including nine v-ATPase subunit genes, CTSB/CTSD/CTSH/CTSK, GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, SMPD1, MAN2B1, LAMP1, IGF2R and GNPTG. We infer this is a demand-driven compensatory program; TFEB nuclear localization and CLEAR occupancy are not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): The rate-limiting node is ATP-dependent lumenal acidification and hydrolytic turnover per unit of internalized cargo. Transcript-level expansion of hydrolases and pumps is proposed to be a response to, not a resolution of, insufficient degradative throughput; no lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity or cargo-clearance rate is measured in these data.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): Nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation subunit transcripts are the single most coherently elevated module (34 genes, all positive, mean +2.85, permutation p = 0.0007), consistent with an increased mitochondrial ATP-supply demand created by sustained v-ATPase and biosynthetic load. Respiration and ATP flux are inferred, not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred assembly constraint): Four mitochondrially encoded catalytic core subunits are reduced (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33) while nuclear subunits rise, suggesting a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch that could cap holo-complex assembly and prevent the transcriptional OXPHOS response from translating into proportional ATP flux. This step is the weakest link because MT-ND4L (+1.95) and MT-ND5 (+1.93) move oppositely despite MT-ND4L/MT-ND4 sharing one bicistronic transcript.", "Step 6 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred compensation): Glucose-import and glycolytic transcripts (SLC2A3 +3.73, SLC2A1 +2.37, PFKM +2.41, ENO1 +2.17, GPI +2.06, SLC16A1 +1.12) and a stress-response signature (ATF6 +4.04, DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2AK3 +1.51) are elevated, which we read as compensation for constrained oxidative ATP supply under lysosomal load; HK2 (-3.67) and PFKP (-3.08) are discordant counter-evidence.", "Step 7 (negative arm, measured): Neither the interferon-associated module (9 genes, mean +0.47, permutation p = 0.30, no canonical ISG effectors such as MX1, OAS, IFIT, ISG15, STAT1/2 present in the 2212-gene list) nor the TLR/NF-kB inflammatory module (23 genes, mean +1.04, permutation p = 0.51, with TNFAIP3 -1.05 and RELB -1.30) exceeds the global upward shift, so the APOE4/APOE3 difference is not explained by interferon or NF-kB activation in these measurements."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/CLEAR endolysosomal-biogenesis program with a bioenergetically constrained degradative throughput bottleneck, not an interferon or NF-kB inflammatory program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1690926890511029, "cosine_similarity": 0.37709521959859077, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6060711974110032, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1690926890511029, "cosine_similarity": 0.37709521959859077, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6060711974110032, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.89345025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 166}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_085", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance for ERAD and retention-cycle components is a usable proxy for the corresponding protein capacity and therefore for pathway flux; no ERAD protein levels, substrate half-lives or ubiquitination states are supplied.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive, median +1.46), so every enrichment statement is relative to that biased background and not to an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, HERPUD1, SYVN1, VCP, NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2) means untested, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and relative magnitudes are used, and the very large values (up to +15.5) are treated as ordinal.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with multiple candidate genes and cannot identify a specific protein; the HSP90B1/HSPA5-containing spots are used only as weak, non-identifying counter-evidence against a large ER chaperone protein surge.", "The partition of ER quality-control genes into 'retention/folding' versus 'disposal' groups was made after inspecting the data, so the associated permutation and binomial p-values are descriptive, not confirmatory.", "Replicate number, and the astrocyte versus microglia contribution to the 10X Flex signal, are not supplied; genotype-driven cell-intrinsic regulation rather than composition or normalisation drift is assumed for the coordinate ERAD-down signature.", "Activity states (SREBP cleavage, TFEB nuclear translocation, IRE1 oligomerisation, PERK phosphorylation) are inferred from target-transcript patterns and were not measured."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting defect is not ER protein entry or folding capacity but the terminal ERAD disposal step: transcripts encoding the SEL1L-retrotranslocation/mannose-trimming/deglycosylation arm (SEL1L, DERL1, EDEM1, NGLY1, PDIA3) are the only coordinately lower ER quality-control transcripts in a globally up-shifted differential-expression list, while N-glycan attachment and glycoprotein retention/re-folding transcripts (MLEC, DDOST, STT3A, UGGT1, DNAJC10, DNAJB11, MANF) are strongly higher. We hypothesise that reduced ERAD disposal capacity prolongs residence of misfolded glycoproteins in the ER lectin cycle, sustains a low-grade ATF6/PERK-arm transcriptional state (ATF6, DDIT3, EIF2AK3 transcripts up) without a classical BiP/GRP94 protein surge, and shifts the burden of clearance and of ER-membrane lipid handling onto SREBP-driven lipogenic/sterol transcription (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, INSIG1, SOAT1) and a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase program (TFEB, GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSK, ATP6V1A), producing the APOE4 lipid-handling phenotype. Causality is not established by these data; the direction is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: re-expressing SEL1L (or its partner HRD1/SYVN1) in APOE4 microglia should shorten the half-life of a glycosylated ERAD reporter substrate (e.g. NHK alpha1-antitrypsin or CD3delta-YFP, cycloheximide chase) toward APOE3 values and should reduce the MLEC/DDOST/UGGT1 retention-cycle transcripts and the neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester load; if SEL1L restoration normalises substrate half-life but leaves retention-cycle transcripts and lipid storage unchanged, the proposed ERAD-to-lipid chain is falsified.", "Baseline flux test: APOE4 microglia should show a measurably longer half-life and greater calnexin/malectin co-immunoprecipitation of an endogenous or reporter ER glycoprotein than isogenic APOE3; equal degradation kinetics and equal lectin-cycle association would remove the primary bottleneck claim.", "Phenocopy test: knockdown of SEL1L or DERL1, or NGLY1 inhibition, in APOE3 microglia should raise MLEC, DDOST and UGGT1 transcripts, raise lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB) and increase neutral-lipid staining; failure to move the lipid readout would show ERAD limitation is not sufficient.", "Direction test against the lysosome-primary alternative: lowering lipid load or lysosomal demand in APOE4 microglia (SOAT1/ACAT inhibition, cholesterol depletion, or reduced lipid/debris feeding) should leave the ERAD-disposal transcript deficit and retention-cycle induction essentially unchanged; if these ER signatures normalise when lipid or lysosomal load is relieved, the causal direction is reversed and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Arm-specificity test: APOE4 microglia should show ATF6 processing and modest eIF2alpha phosphorylation without a large XBP1 splicing or BiP/GRP94 protein increase; a strong XBP1s and BiP protein induction, or unchanged ATF6 processing, would contradict step 4 (the non-significant HSP90B1/HSPA5-candidate spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004 and protein_spot:005 already argue against a large chaperone protein surge).", "Null-result criterion: if proteasome-independent bulk protein synthesis, ER morphology and glycoprotein secretion rates are indistinguishable between genotypes while lysosomal hydrolase activity and lipid droplets still differ, the bottleneck should be relocated from ERAD to the endolysosomal-lipid branch."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show lower transcript abundance for the SEL1L-associated retrotranslocation/trimming/deglycosylation components SEL1L, DERL1, EDEM1 and NGLY1, plus the ER oxidoreductase PDIA3; all five are below zero in a differential-expression list whose median effect is positive (~+1.46 reported log units), and all five carry adjusted p-values below 2e-3.", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux, not measured): the reduced abundance of these components lowers the flux capacity of the terminal ERAD step (substrate extraction to the cytosol and N-glycan removal before proteasomal handoff); ERAD substrate half-life, ubiquitination and retrotranslocation were not measured here.", "Step 3 (inferred residence/localisation): with disposal limited, glycoprotein clients are re-routed through the malectin/UGGT1 re-glucosylation retention cycle, consistent with the very large increases in MLEC (+10.21, top ~0.2% of the list), DDOST (+6.22), STT3A (+3.39), UGGT1 (+2.58), DNAJC10 (+4.73), DNAJB11 (+2.22) and MANF (+2.95); increased transcript abundance is interpreted here as increased retention-cycle capacity/demand, not as a measured retained protein pool.", "Step 4 (inferred signalling): prolonged client residence sustains a chronic, low-amplitude ER stress signal biased to the ATF6 and PERK arms (ATF6 +4.04, EIF2AK3 +1.51, DDIT3 +2.79, ERO1A +1.21, CRELD2 +1.01, SERP1 +2.20 transcripts) rather than an acute IRE1/BiP surge; XBP1, HSPA5, ATF4 and HERPUD1 were not present in the supplied rows, and the protein spots whose candidate lists include HSP90B1/HSPA5 are not significantly changed (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005).", "Step 5 (inferred lipid consequence): chronic ER-membrane load plus ATF6/PERK-arm signalling maintains SREBP-dependent lipogenic and sterol transcription (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, SREBF2 +1.06) and esterification/storage capacity (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1), which would expand the neutral-lipid pool; no lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (inferred compensation): clearance is shifted to the endolysosomal route, matching the coherent lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (TFEB +2.38, GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, CTSK +7.36, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, CTSB +5.52, SMPD1 +5.63, ATP6V1A +4.23, CTSD +2.86; 17 hydrolases, mean +2.73 versus list mean +1.39, permutation p = 0.015), which we interpret as a downstream compensatory branch rather than the primary bottleneck.", "Step 7 (net phenotype): the combination of restricted ER disposal, sustained lipogenic transcription and expanded lysosomal hydrolase capacity yields an APOE4 microglial state that accumulates and stores lipid instead of clearing ER-derived and internalised cargo efficiently."], "title": "An ERAD disposal bottleneck (SEL1L/DERL1/NGLY1) traps glycoproteins in the calnexin-malectin-UGGT1 retention cycle and diverts APOE4 microglia toward lysosomal-lipid compensation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30393604844367317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2669717182408859, "cosine_similarity": 0.3770448468554554, "direction_accuracy": 0.31715210355987056, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5963624595469256, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30393604844367317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2669717182408859, "cosine_similarity": 0.3770448468554554, "direction_accuracy": 0.31715210355987056, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5963624595469256, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.93209275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 167}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_054", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not a whole-transcriptome survey; enrichment is therefore judged as rank position within this selected, strongly right-shifted list (median +1.46 in unspecified reported log units) rather than as absolute fold change, and the unresolved global shift is assumed not to differentially distort the low-tail glycolytic genes.", "Transcript abundance for HK2/PFKP, TCA, carrier and amino-acid catabolic genes is assumed to track the corresponding enzyme/transporter protein and, in the case of the committed glycolytic step, enzymatic capacity; none of these protein or activity levels were measured here (HK1, PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, ACLY, CS, MDH2 and GOT2 rows are absent from the file).", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific enzyme; they are used only as weak, non-confirmatory context.", "Cells are mock-treated isogenic APOE3/APOE4 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-linked differences in culture composition, astrocyte-supplied substrate, or cell-state proportion could generate part of the pseudobulk signal; effect direction is assumed to be APOE4-intrinsic.", "Flux, localisation, redox state and lipid content are inferred, not observed; no metabolite, respirometry or imaging measurement is present in the supplied data, so no causal claim is established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a transcriptional program in which the committed upper-glycolytic step (HK2/PFKP) is selectively depressed against a strongly right-shifted background, while mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA-cycle, nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, malate-aspartate/citrate carrier and amino-acid catabolic transcripts are coordinately elevated. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is glucose-6-phosphate/fructose-1,6-bisphosphate production, so that glucose-derived pyruvate and lactate output fall and mitochondrial carbon is supplied instead by glutamate/aspartate/BCAA anaplerosis, with SLC25A1-mediated citrate export feeding a lipogenic/esterification program; this predicts substrate inflexibility (glutaminolysis dependence, low glycolytic reserve) rather than a global increase in energy production. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: parallel U-13C6-glucose and U-13C5-glutamine labelling of mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, lower fractional m+3 lactate and lower glucose-derived m+2 citrate, with a higher glutamine-derived (m+4 citrate / m+4 malate) contribution to the TCA pool. Equal or greater glucose contribution to lactate and citrate in APOE4 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Pharmacological dependence test: glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) or transaminase inhibition (aminooxyacetate) should reduce basal and maximal oxygen consumption and total ATP production rate more in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose or a galactose substitution should be better tolerated by APOE4. An equal or larger CB-839 effect in APOE3, or greater 2-DG sensitivity in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Bottleneck-restoration test: hexokinase-2 (or PFKP) re-expression in APOE4 microglia should raise lactate secretion and glucose-derived citrate labelling and reduce the CB-839 sensitivity gap, without requiring correction of the TCA/OXPHOS transcript program. No change in glucose-derived labelling after restoration would place the bottleneck elsewhere.", "Capacity test: enzyme assays or immunoblots should show lower hexokinase and PFK activity in APOE4 lysates while OGDH/MDH/glutamate dehydrogenase activities are equal or higher; equal hexokinase/PFK activity between genotypes would falsify the primary bottleneck claim.", "Downstream lipid test: SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) or ACLY inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content preferentially in APOE4 while leaving APOE3 largely unchanged; if APOE4 droplet content is unaffected, the citrate-export arm of the mechanism is wrong even if the glycolytic bottleneck holds.", "Mitonuclear check: BN-PAGE or complex-specific activity should show that the elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcript program is not matched by proportional complex I/III/IV assembly in APOE4 (consistent with the low-tail mtDNA-encoded transcripts); proportional increases in assembled complexes would argue instead for a genuinely expanded, non-limited respiratory chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA): glucose transporter transcripts SLC2A1 and SLC2A3 are elevated (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, 69th/86th percentile of a right-shifted distribution) while the committed-step kinases gene:HK2 (-3.67, 3.6th percentile), gene:PFKP (-3.08, 5.5th percentile) and gene:HK3 (-1.12, 21st percentile) sit in the low tail. Inferred (not measured): glucose import capacity is retained but flux commitment into glycolysis below G6P/F1,6BP is constrained in APOE4.", "Inferred consequence: reduced glucose-derived pyruvate and lactate output and reduced G6P entry into the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch, consistent with the low-tail transcripts gene:TALDO1 (-2.32) and gene:PGD (-1.30). Lactate, G6P and NADPH pools were not measured.", "Measured (RNA): mitochondrial pyruvate handling and TCA transcripts are among the highest in the dataset (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65), and 39 nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts have median +2.64 versus background +1.45 (Mann-Whitney p=5.8e-5). Inferred: increased mitochondrial oxidative and pyruvate-oxidising capacity, i.e. the cell maximises use of whatever pyruvate reaches the matrix; respiration rate itself was not measured.", "Measured (RNA): amino-acid uptake/catabolism transcripts rise (gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:BCAT2 +6.42, gene:BCAT1 +1.32, gene:ABAT +1.54, gene:GLS +1.35, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45; set median +3.17, p=0.012) together with malate-aspartate/organic-acid carriers (gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1; set p=0.0039). Inferred: glutamate/aspartate and branched-chain carbon substitutes for glycolytic pyruvate as anaplerotic TCA input, and cytosolic reducing equivalents are shuttled into mitochondria rather than consumed by lactate dehydrogenase.", "Measured (RNA): the citrate exporter gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) and lipogenic/lipid-handling transcripts gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:CD36 (+1.38) are elevated. Inferred: a fraction of anaplerotic TCA carbon leaves as citrate for cytosolic acetyl-CoA and lipid esterification; no lipid, citrate or acetyl-CoA pool was measured in this dataset.", "Net inferred state: APOE4 microglia are substrate-inflexible - low glycolytic reserve, high reliance on amino-acid oxidation and on an expanded but mtDNA-limited electron transport chain (4 of 6 mtDNA-encoded transcripts are in the low tail, e.g. gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32), which predicts genotype-selective sensitivity to glutaminase/transaminase inhibition and poor compensation when oxidative phosphorylation is blocked."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose glycolytic commitment at the hexokinase/PFK step and become dependent on amino-acid-fuelled TCA carbon, with citrate export toward lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.05283757338551859, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29878594024801225, "cosine_similarity": 0.3769937867088855, "direction_accuracy": 0.0889967637540453, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6039158576051781, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.05283757338551859, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29878594024801225, "cosine_similarity": 0.3769937867088855, "direction_accuracy": 0.0889967637540453, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6039158576051781, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.439805, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 168}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_032", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; only directions and within-modality ranks are used, and genes absent from the list (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track the transcriptional output of the sterol-sensing and lysosomal-biogenesis programs; no enzyme activity, sterol pool size, cholesterol flux, esterification rate, efflux rate or subcellular localization was measured here, so activation and rate limitation are inferred, not observed.", "Program membership was defined from prior curated pathway knowledge (unverified, no literature access) before signs were examined; all represented members are reported, including discordant ones, and members are co-regulated rather than independent, so coherence is descriptive and not a formal enrichment test.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (92 spots, 208 candidate identities, keratin/actin-dominated); spot effects are treated only as compatibility checks and are never taken as measurement of an individual protein.", "Effects are cell-population averages from a mixed microglia-astrocyte co-culture at one timepoint; APOE4-specific differences in the astrocyte compartment could contribute to the microglial readout.", "The mechanism describes the state present in the measured mock condition; any reduced lipid-handling reserve would only be revealed by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge and is not claimed as an ongoing defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 by a coordinated re-routing of sterol/lipid handling rather than by loss of a single enzyme: transcripts for lipoprotein and phagocytic uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA/B/C), for an expanded endolysosomal degradative compartment (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:TFEB), and for sterol/lipid storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) are all elevated, yet the SREBP-target biosynthetic module remains uniformly elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR; 13/13 positive). We propose that in APOE4 cells incoming sterol is preferentially retained in endolysosomal and esterified/stored pools, so the ER-accessible sterol pool that sets SREBP cleavage is not satisfied, while oxysterol/LXR-responsive output (gene:CH25H, gene:MYLIP, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:ABCA7) is simultaneously on. This is a compartmental mis-partitioning (altered routing) of sterol, not a demonstrated block in any single step; measured abundances cannot establish flux or causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-pool test: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under the same mock condition, ER-accessible cholesterol (ALOD4/D4H probe or ER-targeted sensor) should be equal or lower while total cellular cholesterol, cholesteryl ester (SOAT1 product) and filipin-positive LAMP1+ compartments are higher. Finding higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 together with unchanged cholesteryl ester would weaken the mis-partitioning mechanism.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation (mis-sensing versus increased demand): acute LDL or cholesterol-cyclodextrin loading should suppress the SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) less in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes would favor a simple higher-throughput/increased-demand adaptation and weaken this hypothesis.", "Prospective routing perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should raise ER-accessible cholesterol and reduce SREBP-target transcripts preferentially in APOE4, and should shift stored sterol from esters toward free cholesterol; no genotype-selective effect on the SREBP module would weaken step 3-4. Conversely, NPC1 inhibition (U18666A) in APOE3 should reproduce the APOE4 pattern of simultaneous hydrolase and SREBP-target elevation.", "Prospective capacity versus reserve test: under a lipid or myelin/apoptotic-cell load challenge, APOE4 cells should show greater lysosomal cholesterol/lipid accumulation and slower cargo clearance than APOE3 despite the higher hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance kinetics would indicate successful adaptive expansion rather than mis-routing.", "Cross-modality check: quantitative targeted proteomics (not 2D spots) should show increased CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXB and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein in APOE4. Because the supplied cathepsin-containing spots are bidirectional (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055/057 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) and ATP6V1E1-containing spots are negative (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), failure to confirm increased lysosomal hydrolase protein would substantially weaken step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters extracellular lipid/lipoprotein handoff in the astrocyte co-culture; the microglial response includes elevated transcripts for lipoprotein and phagocytic uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC), predicting increased sterol/lipid influx (influx itself not measured).", "Internalized lipid is delivered to a transcriptionally expanded endolysosomal degradative compartment: hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GNPTG), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2), and endosome/lysosome trafficking-biogenesis genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:CHMP4B, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:TFEB); this set is shifted upward even against the strongly positive selected-DE background.", "Sterol egress from that compartment to the ER is not matched to influx and ER free cholesterol is drained into esters/neutral lipid (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72; gene:OSBPL8 -1.90 as the one represented ER-contact sterol-transfer transcript, gene:OSBPL1A +1.03, gene:NPC2 +1.17; NPC1, LIPA, STARD3/4, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not supplied and are unknown).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool stays low, SREBP-driven transcription remains on despite high influx: gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:INSIG1 and gene:LDLR are all positive with no represented member negative.", "In parallel an oxysterol/LXR-responsive arm is transcriptionally active (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:ABCA7 +2.14); induced MYLIP (IDOL) opposes LDLR protein accumulation, so the two arms send conflicting instructions and the ER sterol signal is not resolved in the measured (mock) state.", "Net cell state: a storage/degradation-biased sterol economy with an enlarged lysosomal load, which is compatible with the partially induced stress/chemokine transcripts (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:IL18 +1.46, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:ATF6 +4.04) without requiring frank lysosomal failure at day 30."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lysosome-biased sterol economy: high lipid uptake and endolysosomal degradative expansion coexist with an unresolved ER sterol-deficit signal"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24143776295395428, "cosine_similarity": 0.3763536259573484, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961585760517799, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24143776295395428, "cosine_similarity": 0.3763536259573484, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961585760517799, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.04461775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 33}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_062", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore relative to the supplied list, not to all expressed genes.", "The RNA rows separate into two source-row blocks: 1012 genes on 506 doubly-occupied rows that are sign-balanced (median effect ~0.00, exactly one positive and one negative member per row) and 1200 genes on singly-occupied rows that are 100% positive (median +2.08). We assume the balanced block is the directionally interpretable one and base the primary claim on it; the all-positive block is treated as directionally uninformative (this affects gene:TFEB, gene:SCARB2, gene:CD36, gene:DGAT1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:SCP2, gene:MDH1, gene:NDUFS7, gene:SLC25A46).", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking, not as fold-change estimates. Effect magnitude is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p value in this list (Spearman rho = -0.03), so large magnitudes are not assumed to be the most reliable.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a measurement of a named protein pool.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme protein, but not for enzyme activity, luminal pH, cargo delivery rate, or substrate clearance; none of these were measured.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at one timepoint in a microglia-astrocyte co-culture, so astrocyte-derived lipid supply and any capture of astrocyte transcripts could contribute to the signal.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so the reported p values cannot be independently assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated up-shift in transcripts encoding acid glycosidases/sphingolipid hydrolases, cathepsins and v-ATPase subunits, together with mitochondrial TCA/carrier transcripts. We propose that the rate-limiting step is the effective luminal degradative flux for lipid-rich cargo inside APOE4 lysosomes: the transcriptional expansion is a compensatory response to a chronically unmet substrate load rather than evidence of increased degradative output, and the mitochondrial and lipid-esterification changes are downstream consequences. The assigned sterol-synthesis/trafficking/export focus is rejected as the primary mechanism because its rate-limiting nodes (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, MVD, LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NCEH1) are absent from the supplied rows and the measured sterol-transport set is not distinguishable from background. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (bottleneck test): loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a defined lipid cargo (fluorescent myelin debris or BODIPY-sphingomyelin liposomes) should show APOE4 with equal or higher per-cell mature GBA/HEXA/CTSB protein and Magic-Red cathepsin B signal, yet a LOWER substrate clearance rate constant per unit enzyme and measurable accumulation of glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin and GM2 by lipidomics. If APOE4 cells clear the cargo at the same or a faster per-cell rate with no accumulation of these species, the saturated-hydrolysis bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation (bottleneck versus the rejected sterol-export focus): boosting luminal hydrolysis in APOE4 (GBA1 or SMPD1 overexpression, or a GBA chaperone) should reduce neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet load and blunt both the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation and the TCA/carrier transcript elevation. If instead only LXR agonism acting through ABCA1/ABCG1 export normalises the phenotype while hydrolase boosting has no effect, the bottleneck is sterol export and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Epistasis prediction: partial v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1 or concanamycin A) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 lipid and lysosomal-transcript state and collapse the genotype difference. Persistence or widening of the APOE4-APOE3 difference under complete acidification block would indicate an acidification-independent mechanism and weaken step 2.", "Ordering prediction: acute pharmacological blockade of mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA entry (UK5099 or an OGDH inhibitor) should NOT reverse the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4, whereas relieving lysosomal load should reduce it. Reversal of the lysosomal program by mitochondrial inhibition would invert the proposed causal ordering.", "Measurement-robustness prediction: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome re-analysis with a symmetric background, the lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase sets should still rank above background (one-sided empirical p \u003c 0.05), and cathepsin/hydrolase protein should be resolved by targeted immunoblot rather than gel spots. Loss of the hydrolase enrichment against a symmetric background, or immunoblots showing unchanged mature GBA/HEXA/CTSB protein, would substantially weaken the mechanism.", "Heterogeneity prediction: single-cell scoring of the hydrolase/v-ATPase module should show the APOE4 shift across the bulk of the microglial population rather than only in a small lipid-droplet-high subcluster. Confinement to a rare subcluster would favour a composition-shift explanation over a cell-autonomous bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA, balanced source-row block): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels than APOE3 for lysosomal acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH) and for v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D2), against a within-block background whose median log fold change is ~0. This is transcript abundance only; enzyme activity, maturation and luminal pH are not measured here.", "INFERRED (regulatory state): This CLEAR-like coordinate induction, together with elevated gene:TFEB and gene:SLC38A7, is interpreted as a compensatory transcriptional response to a persistent, unmet luminal degradative demand, i.e. an adaptive rather than a satisfied state. The alternative reading, that APOE4 lysosomes simply degrade more, is not excluded by transcript levels.", "INFERRED (flux and localization): If demand exceeds effective luminal hydrolysis, sphingomyelin-, glucosylceramide- and GM2-type substrates handled by SMPD1/GBA/HEXA are predicted to accumulate in the late-endosomal/lysosomal lumen and limiting membrane, lowering the rate of lipid egress from that compartment. No lipid species, lysosomal pH, or lysosome-localised protein pool is measured in the supplied data.", "MEASURED plus INFERRED (cargo entry and storage arm): Uptake and esterification/storage transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP), while the rate-limiting sterol-synthesis and sterol-export genes are not present in the supplied rows. We therefore infer, but do not observe, a routing of retained lipid toward esterified/neutral-lipid storage rather than efflux.", "MEASURED plus INFERRED (mitochondrial sink): Mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/carrier and respiratory-chain transcripts are among the strongest APOE4-high signals (gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:NDUFS7, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:ATP5ME, gene:TIMM8B, gene:DLD, gene:GOT1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:SCP2). We infer this is a downstream catabolic sink for fatty acids liberated by residual lysosomal hydrolysis, not an independent primary lesion; oxygen consumption and beta-oxidation flux are not measured.", "INFERRED (causal ordering, unproven): We place lysosomal degradative saturation upstream of the storage and mitochondrial shifts. The cross-sectional, single-timepoint design cannot order these events, and a reversed order (primary mitochondrial change driving lysosomal compensation) remains possible."], "title": "Saturated lysosomal hydrolytic clearance of lipid cargo, not de novo sterol synthesis or sterol export, is the primary bottleneck distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14935568437765387, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15783640693669493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3763119476309452, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mean_absolute_error": 0.612032362459547, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14935568437765387, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15783640693669493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3763119476309452, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "mean_absolute_error": 0.612032362459547, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0795745, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 169}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway coherence was therefore judged by rank/percentile against the 2212 supplied effects rather than by direction alone, because 77% of supplied rows are positive (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, which is preserved and never converted).", "Steady-state transcript differences are assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding carrier and enzyme proteins; no protein measurement of MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, PDH or any ETC subunit is supplied, so enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, sub-mitochondrial localisation and flux are inferred, not observed.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit is assumed to reflect real mitochondrial transcript or mtDNA-copy differences rather than a probe-based (10X Flex) detection artefact for mitochondrial genes; only six mtDNA-encoded rows are supplied and two of them (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L) are positive.", "Protein spots are ambiguous: each spot lists several candidate genes, so no spot is treated as evidence for or against a named enzyme; spot effects are on a stated log2 scale while RNA effects are on an unspecified reported log scale, so the two modalities are not quantitatively combined.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular substrate availability (glucose, lactate, glutamine, lipoproteins) is partly non-cell-autonomous and may differ between genotypes for reasons outside the microglia.", "Cell-state composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures (e.g. a more activated/lipid-laden subpopulation) could generate the same pseudobulk pattern without any per-cell rewiring; biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the transcriptional feature that most coherently separates APOE4 from APOE3 is a carbon-routing imbalance rather than a simple glycolytic or oxidative shift: transcripts encoding mitochondrial pyruvate/dicarboxylate/citrate carriers and TCA-input enzymes are among the most APOE4-elevated in the supplied differential list (MPC2, MDH1, OGDH, GOT1, DLD, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5 all at the 91st-99th percentile of the measured effect distribution), while committed upper-glycolytic enzymes (HK2, PFKP, HK3, PFKFB2, 4th-22nd percentile) and most mtDNA-encoded electron-transport core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are among the most decreased. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node (bottleneck) is terminal oxidation capacity set by mtDNA-encoded complex III/IV/V core subunits, so that the extra pyruvate and glutamine/aspartate carbon entering the APOE4 matrix cannot be fully oxidised and is instead exported as citrate/malate to feed cytosolic acetyl-CoA-dependent desaturation and sterol/neutral-lipid esterification (SREBF1, SCD, ACSS2, SOAT1, DGAT1 elevated) with an increased lysosomal lipid-handling load (CTSB, GBA, TFEB elevated). All flux, activity, localisation and directional statements are inferred from steady-state RNA and are not established as causal.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Stable-isotope tracing in mock-treated isogenic microglia: with U-13C6 glucose, APOE4 should show higher fractional M+2 citrate labelling and higher transfer of glucose-derived 13C into cholesterol/cholesteryl ester and 16:1/18:1 fatty acids than APOE3, while secreted M+3 lactate per glucose consumed is equal or lower. Observing higher lactate output with unchanged or lower citrate and lipid labelling in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: the MPC inhibitor UK5099 (or MPC2 knockdown), and separately SLC25A1 inhibition/knockdown, should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and citrate-derived lipogenic labelling significantly more in APOE4 than in APOE3 (a genotype x drug interaction), whereas partial glycolytic inhibition (2-deoxyglucose) or HK2 re-expression should not selectively correct APOE4. Absence of a genotype-selective effect of MPC/SLC25A1 blockade, or correction of the APOE4 lipid phenotype by 2-DG/HK2 restoration instead, would weaken the mechanism.", "Respirometry and complex assays: APOE4 should show lower FCCP-stimulated maximal oxygen consumption and lower complex IV (and complex V) activity normalised to citrate-synthase activity or mitochondrial mass, i.e. reduced spare respiratory capacity despite equal or higher basal oxygen consumption. Equal or higher normalised maximal respiration and complex IV activity in APOE4 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Orthogonal quantification (RT-qPCR/ddPCR of mtDNA copy number and of MT-CO1/MT-CO2/MT-ATP6 transcripts, plus immunoblot of MT-CO2 versus nuclear-encoded ATP5F1B or NDUFB8): APOE4 should show a reduced mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded protein ratio. Equal ratios would indicate the mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit is a detection artefact and would remove the bottleneck step while leaving the carbon-import observations intact.", "Substrate-swap test: replacing glucose with galactose (forcing oxidative ATP production) should impair APOE4 viability/ATP more than APOE3 and should collapse the genotype difference in neutral-lipid content. If APOE4 tolerates galactose as well as APOE3 and retains its lipid excess, a terminal-oxidation bottleneck is not the differentiating step.", "Single-cell re-analysis of the same cultures: the elevated MPC2/SLC25A1/TCA transcripts and the elevated lysosomal/lipogenic transcripts should be co-elevated within the same microglial cells across a broad fraction of the population. Confinement of these programmes to a small, mutually exclusive subpopulation would favour a composition-shift explanation over cell-intrinsic carbon rerouting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: MPC2 (+7.98), SLC25A11 (+4.50), SLC25A1 (+4.47) and SLC25A5 (+2.6 log units above the dataset median, +5.56) transcripts are higher in APOE4. Inferred: greater capacity for pyruvate uptake into the matrix and for malate/citrate/adenine-nucleotide exchange across the inner membrane; carrier protein amount, membrane insertion and directional flux are not measured.", "Measured: committed glycolytic enzymes HK2 (-3.67), PFKP (-3.08), HK3 (-1.12) and PFKFB2 (-1.10) are lower in APOE4 (set median at the ~13th percentile of all measured effects, Mann-Whitney p=0.011 versus the whole list), whereas PDP1 (+3.00) and DLD (+5.54) are elevated. Inferred: less glucose committed to glycolytic overflow/lactate and a larger dephosphorylated (active) pyruvate-dehydrogenase fraction, i.e. glucose-derived carbon is preferentially directed into, not away from, the matrix; PDH phosphorylation state and lactate output are not measured.", "Measured: anaplerotic and shuttle transcripts SLC1A5 (+1.55), GLS (+1.35), GLUD1 (+3.17), GOT1 (+6.43), MDH1 (+8.72), OGDH (+8.56), ACO2 (+3.54), IDH3G (+3.94), ME1 (+1.36), NNT (+2.88) are elevated. Inferred: additional glutamine/aspartate carbon and cytosol-matrix redox shuttling supplement pyruvate entry, raising total carbon input to the TCA cycle.", "BOTTLENECK (mixed measured/inferred): mtDNA-encoded core subunits MT-ATP6 (-3.35), MT-CYB (-2.32), MT-ND4 (-1.80) and MT-CO2 (-1.33) are lower in APOE4 while nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts sit at or above the dataset median (mtDNA-encoded versus nuclear-encoded one-sided Mann-Whitney p=0.004). Inferred: a mito-nuclear stoichiometry imbalance limits assembled complex III/IV/V, so matrix NADH reoxidation and terminal oxidation do not scale with the increased carbon input; assembled complex content, respiration and membrane potential are not measured.", "Inferred consequence: with input exceeding oxidative capacity, matrix citrate and malate accumulate and are exported through the elevated SLC25A1/SLC25A11 carriers, with cytosolic MDH1/GOT1/ME1 completing the citrate-malate-pyruvate and malate-aspartate arms; no metabolite, redox-ratio or flux measurement is supplied for this step.", "Measured: SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), ACSS2 (+2.93), DHCR24 (+3.69), DGAT1 (+1.72), SOAT1 (+1.25) and APOE (+1.24) are elevated; lysosomal CTSB (+5.52), GBA (+6.71), HEXA (+5.68), SMPD1 (+5.63), CTSD (+2.86) and TFEB (+2.38) are elevated (lysosomal set Mann-Whitney p=0.008 versus the whole list). Inferred: cytosolic acetyl-CoA derived from exported citrate is channelled into monounsaturated fatty acid, sterol and neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester synthesis, and the resulting lipid load raises lysosomal hydrolase demand; ACLY, FASN and ACACA were not measured, so the acetyl-CoA-producing step itself is unobserved."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial carbon import above terminal-oxidation capacity, routing citrate to cytosolic lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22467968836539526, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2989693633031949, "cosine_similarity": 0.37597322712289766, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5959288025889967, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22467968836539526, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2989693633031949, "cosine_similarity": 0.37597322712289766, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5959288025889967, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.76564775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 170}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a reported log fold change of unspecified base; all statements use it on its own scale and only as relative ordering, never converted to linear fold change.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% are positive with median +1.46, so only comparisons against this internal background (percentiles, permutation) are treated as informative, and absence of a gene (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, PLIN2, LIPA, MCOLN1) means unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level values are used only as weak, direction-level evidence and as counter-evidence against a large ER-chaperone induction.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate, with unknown gain, with the corresponding enzyme activity and organelle capacity; no enzymatic activity, pH, flux, sterol pool or lipid-droplet measurement is present in these data.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured, so part of the lipid/lipoprotein input is non-cell-autonomous, and pseudobulk 10X Flex measurements may mix microglial subsets and any residual astrocyte signal.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the very large reported log fold changes (up to +15.5) may include low-expression instability; the mechanism relies on module-level coherence rather than single extreme rows.", "Causality is not established by these data; the direction APOE4 genotype -\u003e catabolic/egress imbalance -\u003e lipid storage is an inference from a single mock-treatment cross-sectional contrast."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally scale up an acidified, hydrolase-rich lysosomal compartment (TFEB, v-ATPase subunits, GAA/GBA/HEXA/CTSB/CTSD) while lipid-uptake receptor transcripts remain at or above the global shift and the sterol-egress arm (NPC2, OSBPL8, OSBPL1A) does not scale with it; the primary bottleneck is therefore post-hydrolytic sterol/lipid export from the endolysosome, which is predicted (not measured here) to route liberated cholesterol and fatty acids into ER-based esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1) supported by an active MUFA/glycerolipid supply arm (SCD, AGPAT2, SREBF1), producing a cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet-biased state rather than a canonical ER unfolded-protein-response state.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess of cholesteryl ester and neutral-lipid droplets while shifting sterol into the free/effluxable pool, without normalizing the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module. If cholesteryl-ester excess persists unchanged under SOAT1 inhibition, the esterification-diversion step is wrong.", "Removing exogenous lipid input (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake) should shrink the APOE4-APOE3 neutral-lipid gap by a majority; if the gap is unchanged, de novo lipogenesis (SCD/SREBF1 arm) rather than uptake-plus-lysosomal-catabolism flux is the driver and this mechanism is weakened.", "Restoring egress capacity (LXR agonism or forced NPC1/ABCA1-dependent efflux) should reduce lysosomal free-sterol staining and droplet load in APOE4 more than in APOE3; failure to reduce droplets while efflux is demonstrably increased would falsify the export-bottleneck bottleneck assignment.", "Blunting lysosomal acidification/hydrolysis (low-dose bafilomycin A1 or hydrolase inhibition) should reduce, not increase, the APOE4-specific cholesteryl-ester excess; an increase would indicate that lysosomal catabolism is protective and would refute the proposed direction of flux.", "UPR discriminator: PERK/ISR inhibition (GSK2606414 or ISRIB), IRE1 inhibition, or chemical chaperone (4-PBA/TUDCA) should leave the APOE4-APOE3 lipid-storage difference essentially intact, and BiP/GRP94/PDI protein abundance should remain non-different as suggested by protein_spot:005, protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004 and protein_spot:016; if UPR inhibition normalizes the lipid phenotype, an ER-proteostasis mechanism should replace this one.", "Imaging prediction: in APOE4 microglia, filipin-positive free sterol should be enriched inside LAMP1-positive compartments and adjacent LipidTox-positive droplets should be increased; absence of intra-lysosomal sterol enrichment despite increased hydrolase transcripts would weaken the imbalance claim.", "Dose-ordering prediction: the size of the APOE4-APOE3 droplet difference should track lysosomal load (myelin or oxLDL feeding) monotonically; a flat or inverted response to increasing catabolic load would weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits than APOE3 microglia, well above the pervasive positive shift of this selected DE set (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38; module mean +3.33 vs set-wide mean +1.39, permutation p=1e-4), together with the biogenesis factor gene:TFEB (+2.38).", "Inferred activity (not measured): this transcriptional program corresponds to increased acidified lysosomal volume and higher hydrolytic flux on internalized lipoprotein/membrane cargo; hydrolase protein abundance is not resolvable here because cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00) and are multi-candidate spots.", "Measured: lipid-acquisition transcripts are maintained or elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, 99th percentile of this set; gene:LDLR +1.50; gene:CD36 +1.38; gene:TREM2 +1.28; gene:APOE +1.24), so catabolic input is not transcriptionally throttled.", "Bottleneck (inferred): the sterol-egress/inter-organelle transfer arm does not scale with the catabolic arm - gene:NPC2 (+1.17, 35th percentile) and gene:OSBPL1A (+1.03, 26th) sit below the set median (+1.46) and gene:OSBPL8 is decreased (-1.90, 13th percentile); NPC1, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied rows, so export capacity is inferred from an incomplete panel and is explicitly not an observed molecular pool.", "Inferred flux consequence: sterol and fatty acid liberated in the lysosome exceed export/efflux capacity and are re-esterified at the ER by acyl-transferases whose transcripts are elevated in absolute terms (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) with an elevated precursor-supply arm (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69), yielding cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol stored in cytoplasmic droplets.", "Alternative arm rejected as primary: canonical ER proteostasis stress is not coherently supported - the UPR/ER-chaperone transcript module is not enriched above the global shift (mean +1.08, mean percentile 0.47), ERAD/folding genes are decreased (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:PDIA3 -1.26), ER-exit/Golgi genes are mixed-to-down (gene:SEC24D -1.39, gene:GOSR1 -3.19), and every protein spot containing an ER chaperone candidate is non-significant and near or below zero (protein_spot:005 -0.14, protein_spot:001 -0.48, protein_spot:004 -0.68, protein_spot:016 +0.14). Elevated gene:DDIT3 (+2.79) and gene:ATF6 (+4.04) are therefore interpreted as a lipid-bilayer/metabolic stress readout downstream of the storage state, not as the driving proteostasis defect."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal catabolic capacity faster than sterol egress, diverting lysosome-derived lipid into ER esterification and neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24718458073330132, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2542050672837759, "cosine_similarity": 0.3757207229678948, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5995048543689321, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24718458073330132, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2542050672837759, "cosine_similarity": 0.3757207229678948, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5995048543689321, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88554025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 171}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_048", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; magnitudes are therefore not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot values and set tests were run against the selected-gene background, not a whole transcriptome.", "The strong global upward RNA shift (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46) is treated as a property of the selection/normalisation, so only set-versus-background contrasts and directional discordances are interpreted, not the sign of any single gene alone.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes; a spot change is assumed to be an ambiguous mixture measurement and is used only as an aggregate discordance statistic, never as an identified protein pool.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for the capacity being built, while hydrolase activity, TFEB nuclear localization, cargo flux, compartment pH, and all lipid pools are inferred and unmeasured in this dataset.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some RNA signal may be non-microglial or non-cell-autonomous; biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment, so genotype is assumed to be the only systematic difference, but no causality is established by association alone."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by an amplified transcriptional program for lysosomal acid hydrolases (including the glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin-degrading set GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, SMPD1), v-ATPase subunits, and endosomal sorting/recycling machinery (retromer/Commander/AP-5), together with increased lipid-uptake receptor transcripts; because the 2D protein-spot data show no corresponding coherent increase in hydrolase- or v-ATPase-containing spots, we propose that the bottleneck is post-transcriptional delivery/maturation of degradative capacity into lipid-laden late endosomes/lysosomes, so the transcriptional program is a compensatory response to a persisting lysosomal lipid-clearance shortfall rather than evidence of increased degradative flux. Sphingolipid de novo synthesis is explicitly rejected as the driver. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: supplying degradative capacity directly (recombinant/overexpressed GBA plus acid sphingomyelinase, or acid-lipase supplementation) should reduce lysosomal lipid load and LAMP1/LysoTracker-positive compartment volume in APOE4 more than in APOE3, whereas constitutively active TFEB overexpression - which further raises the same transcripts already elevated - should give little additional benefit in APOE4. If TFEB overexpression rescues APOE4 lipid load as well as or better than direct enzyme supplementation, the post-transcriptional delivery bottleneck is wrong.", "Enzymatic prediction: per-cell activity of GBA, HEXA/HEXB, acid sphingomyelinase, and mature (processed) cathepsin D in APOE4 versus APOE3 should be flat or increased far less than the corresponding transcript changes (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSD), with an increased pro-form to mature-form ratio. Proportional, stoichiometric increases in activity and normal maturation would falsify the bottleneck.", "Substrate-dependence prediction: removing lipoprotein/lipid cargo (delipidated medium, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should substantially blunt the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4 within 24-72 h. Persistence of the full CLEAR-like program under lipid-free conditions would indicate a cargo-independent, cell-autonomous transcriptional difference and weaken Steps 1-3.", "Focus-rejection prediction: inhibiting sphingolipid de novo synthesis (myriocin, serine palmitoyltransferase) or ceramide synthase (fumonisin B1) should not normalise the APOE4 lysosomal phenotype, consistent with the unenriched de novo set (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:ORMDL2, gene:SGPL1, gene:CERK, gene:ST3GAL5). A strong myriocin rescue would show that sphingolipid synthesis, not degradative delivery, is the driver.", "Routing prediction: quantitative imaging should show CI-M6PR/IGF2R-positive carriers retained on RAB7A-positive late endosomes with reduced endosome-to-Golgi return in APOE4, and VPS35/VPS26A knockdown should worsen APOE4 lipid accumulation disproportionately. Equal retrograde recycling kinetics between genotypes, or an equal knockdown effect in both, would weaken Step 4.", "Metabolic prediction: APOE4 microglia should show lower glycolytic rate (ECAR) with preserved or higher oxygen consumption than APOE3 (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP down; gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5 up). An unchanged or higher glycolytic rate in APOE4 would remove Step 5 as a consequence of the same state."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred flux, from measured transcripts): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein cargo receptors and ligand (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer raises the rate of lipid cargo entering the endolysosomal system; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): The luminal degradative capacity delivered to those compartments does not scale with cargo, because hydrolase- and v-ATPase-containing protein spots are not coordinately increased (median log2 change of 25 lysosome-candidate spots +0.58 versus +0.48 for the other 67 spots), with several significantly decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) despite very large transcript increases; spot identities are ambiguous, so this is a discordance signal, not a measured enzyme pool.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): Undegraded lipid substrate load is inferred to activate a TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR-like program: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, and acid hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53. TFEB nuclear localization and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred routing): Endosomal sorting and recycling machinery is transcriptionally reconfigured rather than uniformly raised - retromer/SNX3 and Commander up (gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:COMMD9 +3.06, gene:CCDC22 +2.06), AP-5 late-endosomal pathway up (gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:AP5Z1 +3.78), gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, while gene:M6PR -1.72 and gene:WASHC4 -2.10 fall; we infer altered mannose-6-phosphate-receptor cycling and hydrolase delivery efficiency, consistent with the protein-spot discordance in Step 2.", "Step 5 (inferred metabolic consequence): Lipid that is taken up but incompletely hydrolysed is diverted to esterification/storage and lipogenic remodeling (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), while carbon handling shifts away from glycolysis toward mitochondrial oxidation (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08 versus gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34); no lipid species or flux was measured here.", "Step 6 (net state): APOE4 microglia therefore sit in a transcriptionally compensated but functionally lipid-overloaded endolysosomal state; the glycosphingolipid-catabolic transcripts rise as part of this general lysosomal response and are not statistically separable from other lysosomal hydrolases (set medians 2.17 versus 2.03), whereas sphingolipid de novo synthesis transcripts are indistinguishable from background (median 1.27, permutation p ~0.70)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a CLEAR-like lysosomal-hydrolase and endosomal-recycling transcriptional program that is not matched at the protein-spot level, implicating lysosomal degradative delivery (not sphingolipid de novo synthesis) as the rate-limiting step for internalized lipid clearance"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1698041247102102, "cosine_similarity": 0.3757188858265298, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151974110032362, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1698041247102102, "cosine_similarity": 0.3757188858265298, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151974110032362, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85120325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 172}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); program directions were judged against this up-biased background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects were not rescaled; protein spots are log2 and were used only for compatibility testing.", "Transcript increases in lysosomal, sterol-synthesis and mitochondrial modules are assumed to translate into a proportionate change in the corresponding protein/enzyme pools; no enzyme activity, sterol pool, lipid mass or flux was measured in the supplied data.", "SREBP-target induction is interpreted as reduced ER-accessible sterol; the ER sterol pool, SREBP-2 cleavage and nuclear localisation are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidates over 92 spots); no spot is treated as evidence for an individual protein, and spot-level splits (e.g. CTSD/CTSB candidates up in protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 and down in protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) are treated as ambiguous proteoform-level information.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoproteins, so uptake-driven routing is possible in this condition; the astrocyte contribution to the measured transcriptome is assumed to have been excluded by the single-cell (10X Flex) assignment.", "One RNA row has an uninterpretable identifier (observation_id gene:??) and was excluded from program assignment.", "Causality is not established by these observations; the ordering of steps is a proposed model, and reduced reserve under challenge is a prediction, not a measured defect in the mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) show a coordinated cell-state change in which lipid/sterol taken up through scavenger and lipoprotein receptors is routed into an expanded endolysosomal and esterified-storage compartment instead of the ER-accessible sterol pool; the ER sterol sensor consequently reads deficiency and drives the full SREBP synthesis module while oxysterol/LXR-responsive genes are simultaneously up, and mitochondrial TCA/ETC and phagocytic-receptor transcripts rise to support the increased catabolic-anabolic cycle. The observed pattern is best read as an adaptive high-throughput lipid-processing state, not as a failed ER unfolded-protein or ERAD bottleneck; no flux, sterol-pool or activity measurement in the supplied data establishes causality or a rate limitation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-pool test: in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, ER-accessible cholesterol probes (ALOD4/D4H) should be lower and lysosomal/esterified sterol (filipin plus cholesteryl-ester mass) higher at equal or higher total cholesterol, with more cleaved nuclear SREBP-2. If ER-accessible sterol is equal or higher in APOE4 while SREBP targets remain elevated, the misrouting mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective rescue test: relieving lysosomal sterol sequestration (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 augmentation) should normalise the SREBP module (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24) and reduce CLEAR-network transcripts (CTSB, GBA, ATP6V1A) preferentially in APOE4. Failure of cyclodextrin to lower the SREBP module in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective adaptation-versus-failure test: basal lysosomal proteolytic/lipolytic flux (DQ-BSA, Magic Red, LipidTOX turnover) and basal oxygen consumption should be equal to or higher in APOE4 under mock. If APOE4 shows reduced basal degradative flux and reduced oxygen consumption despite elevated transcripts, the state is a failing compensation rather than the proposed increased-throughput adaptation, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Prospective ER-proteostasis discrimination: pharmacological ER stress readouts (XBP1 splicing, HSPA5/HSP90B1 protein, ATF4/CHOP reporter) should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 in mock, consistent with the near-background UPR sign distribution (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:MANF, gene:EIF2AK3 up but ERAD genes gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1 down and ER-chaperone-candidate spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 not increased). Clear constitutive XBP1 splicing plus increased GRP78/GRP94 protein in APOE4 would favour a primary ER-proteostasis mechanism instead.", "Prospective routing perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should redirect sterol to the ER, lowering SREBP-target transcripts and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts in APOE4 without inducing DDIT3; if SOAT1 inhibition leaves the SREBP module unchanged, the esterification branch of the routing model is falsified.", "Prospective challenge-only prediction: a myelin, apoptotic-cell or oxLDL load should saturate APOE4 microglia at a lower cargo dose (earlier lysosomal pH rise, greater droplet accumulation, larger drop in phagocytic index) than APOE3, revealing reduced reserve that is not claimed to exist as an ongoing defect in the mock condition."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters ApoE-dependent extracellular lipid handling, and receptor-mediated lipid/lipoprotein uptake transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24; effects on the reported log scale, base unspecified).", "Incoming lipid is routed to the endolysosomal system, coinciding with a MiT/TFE-type CLEAR expansion at the transcript level (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:RRAGD +1.44) with 26/28 represented lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and membrane genes increased (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SCARB2 +1.06).", "Sterol is retained in lysosomal and neutral-ester/droplet pools rather than reaching the ER membrane pool, consistent with increased esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:CIDEB +1.06).", "The ER SCAP-INSIG-SREBP sensor therefore signals sterol deficiency: every represented sterol/lipid synthesis gene is up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08), while oxysterol/LXR-responsive genes are also up (gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24) - a sensor discordance expected when sterol is compartmentally misplaced rather than globally scarce.", "Simultaneous degradation and de novo synthesis raise acetyl-CoA, NADPH and ATP demand, matched by an increased mitochondrial oxidative/carbon-shuttle transcript module (gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55) and antioxidant transcripts (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10).", "The resulting state keeps, rather than loses, microglial identity and phagocytic receptor expression (23/24 represented genes up: gene:GPR34 +2.95, gene:CSF1R +1.37, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:SIRPA +2.26, gene:CD47 +2.24, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:C5AR1 +1.32, gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:MEF2C +1.32), with only a modest inflammatory shift (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09) that does not exceed the up-biased background of this selected list.", "Predicted consequence, not observed here: because storage and degradative capacity are already committed at baseline, spare capacity for an added lipid or protein-cargo load is lower in APOE4, which would only be revealed by a future challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia misroute sterol into lysosomal/esterified pools, producing a MiT/TFE-coordinated high-throughput lipid-catabolic state with ER sterol-sensor discordance rather than ER-proteostasis stress"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3399641841745744, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25471340900898615, "cosine_similarity": 0.3739495842125298, "direction_accuracy": 0.3705501618122977, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.591915857605178, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3399641841745744, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25471340900898615, "cosine_similarity": 0.3739495842125298, "direction_accuracy": 0.3705501618122977, "mean_absolute_error": 0.591915857605178, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.11553475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 34}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_033", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00) and are not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore rank-based within this list, not genome-wide.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no RNA effect is converted to a linear fold change.", "The apparent nuclear-vs-mtDNA discordance is a per-cell biological difference rather than an artefact of library-size/compositional normalisation or of probe-based 10X Flex capture of mitochondrial transcripts. This assumption is not testable in the supplied data and is the largest single risk to the mechanism.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy; respiratory-complex assembly state, respiratory flux, membrane potential, mitochondrial mass, lysosomal pH and neutral-lipid content were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot directions are used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence, never as identification of a named protein.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some transcript differences may reflect altered cell-type proportion or ambient RNA rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation; replicate structure was not supplied, so reported adjusted p-values may be anticonservative.", "Background knowledge about APOE4, mitochondrial biology and lipid droplets used in framing is unverified here because literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, TCA, carrier and import transcripts that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts. We hypothesise that the limiting step is assembly of catalytically competent complexes I, III, IV and ATP synthase at the inner membrane (mtDNA-encoded core supply), not the abundance of nuclear subunit mRNA. The resulting shortfall in terminal oxidative flux, occurring alongside increased lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and an active SREBP-type lipogenic and sterol-esterification program, is predicted to divert fatty-acyl and sterol carbon into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol storage rather than into complete oxidation. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript and spot measurements are correlative.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial mitoribosome inhibition of APOE3 microglia (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol, titrated to reduce mtDNA-encoded subunit protein without killing cells) should phenocopy APOE4 by raising nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts and increasing BODIPY/neutral-lipid content; if APOE3 responds with the transcript rise but no lipid accumulation, or if APOE4 is no more sensitive than APOE3 to this inhibition, the proposed bottleneck is weakened.", "Blue-native PAGE/complexome profiling should show, in APOE4 versus APOE3, reduced fully assembled CI, CIII2CIV and CV with accumulation of nuclear-encoded sub-assemblies, while total nuclear subunit protein is equal or higher. Equal assembled-complex levels with equal or higher flux would refute step 3.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20 signal) should show lower maximal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption per unit mitochondrial mass in APOE4 despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Equal or higher normalised respiration would refute the mechanism.", "Normalisation control: mtDNA copy number by ddPCR and mtDNA-encoded transcripts expressed per mtDNA copy should remain lower in APOE4. If per-copy mtDNA transcript levels are equal between genotypes, the observed MT-transcript decrease is a compositional artefact and step 2 fails.", "Lipid outcome: APOE4 microglia should contain more cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol per cell than APOE3 under mock, and combined DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition should reduce droplet mass while further increasing free fatty-acid/lipotoxic stress markers; unchanged neutral lipid between genotypes would remove the phenotypic endpoint of steps 4-5.", "Bottleneck specificity versus the rejected lysosomal alternative: raising lysosomal degradative capacity (TFEB overexpression or acidic-nanoparticle restoration of lysosomal pH) should not normalise respiration per mitochondrial mass in APOE4. If it does normalise respiration and lipid load, the primary bottleneck is endolysosomal rather than mitochondrial and this hypothesis should be replaced."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, nuclear program up): every detected nuclear-encoded structural subunit of complexes I, II, III, IV and V in the supplied differential list is higher in APOE4 (38/38 up; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B), together with TCA/anaplerotic enzymes, mitochondrial solute carriers and an import receptor (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:TOMM22).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, mtDNA-encoded core relatively lower): four of six detected mtDNA-encoded transcripts move in the opposite direction (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 down). We infer, but did not measure, a stoichiometric mismatch between the nuclear-encoded subunit pool and the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores of CI, CIII, CIV and CV.", "Step 3 (inferred assembly/flux bottleneck): if mtDNA-encoded cores are limiting, the enlarged nuclear subunit pool cannot be converted proportionally into holo-complexes; we infer accumulation of nuclear-encoded sub-assemblies and a lower respiratory flux per unit of mitochondrial protein, with a retrograde feed-forward that further raises nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Neither assembly state nor oxygen consumption was measured here.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, substrate supply raised, glycolytic escape not engaged): lipid uptake receptors and lipid-mobilising/beta-oxidation genes are up (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:MGLL) while upper glycolysis is not coordinately induced (gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP are down), so we infer that carbon delivery to mitochondria rises while an alternative ATP route is not transcriptionally reinforced.", "Step 5 (inferred carbon diversion to storage lipid): with terminal oxidation inferred to be assembly-limited, excess acyl-CoA and sterol are predicted to be esterified rather than oxidised, consistent with the concurrent lipogenic/sterol and esterification transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCP2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). Neutral lipid mass itself is not measured in the supplied data.", "Step 6 (parallel, not primary): a lysosomal hydrolase, V-ATPase and TFEB transcript program is also raised (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB), which we treat as a co-occurring catabolic/biogenesis response rather than the primary bottleneck, because it is internally inconsistent (gene:CTSS strongly down, gene:STX17 down, gene:LAMP1 only marginal) and is not corroborated by the protein spots (protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065, whose candidate lists include ATP6V1E1, are lower in APOE4; protein_spot:067, candidate list including HEXB and CTSB, is lower)."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch creates an OXPHOS assembly bottleneck that reroutes ingested lipid into neutral-lipid storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.05185909980430528, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2735307795039003, "cosine_similarity": 0.3738445612653457, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5991715210355987, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.05185909980430528, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2735307795039003, "cosine_similarity": 0.3738445612653457, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5991715210355987, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.67256075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 173}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_053", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Source RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive) from 10X Flex pseudobulk-style testing; the logarithm base is unspecified, so effects are compared on their own reported scale and programs are judged against the 77% positive background, not a 50/50 null. Genes absent from the list (e.g. PSAP, GRN, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, MCOLN1, most homeostatic-microglia markers) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Program membership was fixed a priori from canonical pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge) before checking directions, and negatives were retained; the coherence reported is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test, and the member genes are not statistically independent (shared regulation, shared cells).", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to track, but does not demonstrate, protein amount, hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo degradation flux, lipid pool size or subcellular localization; none of these were measured.", "MiT/TFE transcript increases are assumed to reflect an active CLEAR-type program; nuclear TFEB localization and mTORC1 activity were not measured, and increased TFEB mRNA alone does not establish activation.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (92 spots, 2-6 candidate genes each, 208 unique candidates, keratin/actin contaminants frequent). No spot is treated as identifying a single protein; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply is a plausible but unmeasured cargo source, and any cell-composition or global-normalization shift could inflate the shared upward direction.", "Reserve deficits inferred from reduced glycolytic/PPP transcripts are explicitly predictions about a future challenge, not observed defects in the mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state change rather than a lysosomal bottleneck: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris scavenging receptors rise together with MiT/TFE-family regulators and a broad acid-hydrolase, v-ATPase and lysosomal-transporter program (39/42 represented members positive, vs 77% positive in this selected list), while sterol/acyl esterification and mitochondrial oxidative catabolism transcripts rise and rate-controlling glycolytic and oxidative-PPP transcripts (HK2, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1) fall. We propose that increased receptor-mediated cargo uptake is matched by MiT/TFE-associated expansion of endolysosomal degradative and acidification capacity, with liberated lipid routed to esterified/stored and mitochondrially oxidized pools instead of glycolysis; the resulting state is degradation-competent in the measured mock condition and carries a reduced glycolytic/NADPH reserve that would be exposed only by a future acute challenge. Degradative flux, lysosomal pH, mature hydrolase activity and actual lipid pools were not measured, so causality and the adaptation-versus-failed-compensation distinction are not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating (adaptation vs failed compensation): in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, per-cell cargo degradation flux measured as DQ-BSA or pHrodo-myelin dequenching rate and cleared BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester per unit time should be equal to or greater than APOE3, with equal or lower lysosomal pH (LysoSensor/ratiometric probe) despite larger LAMP1+ volume and higher mature cathepsin B/D activity. If APOE4 instead shows slower degradation, higher lysosomal pH, or accumulated undigested cargo per LAMP1 volume, the mechanism is falsified in favor of a lysosomal-capacity bottleneck with failed compensatory CLEAR induction.", "Prospective: blocking uptake upstream (scavenger-receptor blockade or SCARB1/CD36 knockdown) in APOE4 should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the lysosomal program after uptake blockade would show it is cargo-independent and would weaken steps 2-3.", "Prospective: TFEB/TFEC knockdown in APOE4 should selectively collapse the hydrolase, v-ATPase and lysosomal-transporter transcript increases and cause measurable undigested lipid accumulation; unchanged hydrolase transcripts after knockdown would falsify step 3.", "Prospective (routing arm): SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition should convert the APOE4 esterified/droplet lipid pool into free sterol with increased galectin-3 lysosomal-damage puncta and reduced degradation rate, with a larger effect in APOE4 than APOE3; equal responses in both genotypes would weaken step 4.", "Prospective (reserve, challenge-only claim): an acute challenge that demands glycolysis or NADPH (2-deoxyglucose plus phagocytic myelin load, or an oxidant/respiratory-burst challenge) should impair APOE4 more than APOE3 in phagocytic index and viability, while basal mock ATP levels and basal phagocytosis are equal or higher in APOE4. If APOE4 already shows a basal phagocytic or bioenergetic deficit under mock, the 'adapted, degradation-competent' framing is wrong; if APOE4 matches APOE3 under challenge, the metabolic-routing arm (step 5) is weakened.", "Prospective (protein-level resolution): targeted immunoblot or MS of the ambiguous spots should show increased mature CTSB/CTSD and ANXA1 in APOE4; if instead the decreased spots (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) are resolved as reduced mature cathepsin B/D and reduced HEXB protein while transcripts are elevated, a post-transcriptional maturation failure would be supported and this mechanism would be substantially weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 biases the microglial transcriptional state toward lipoprotein/apoptotic-debris scavenging: scavenger and opsonic receptor transcripts increase coherently (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.44, gene:CD163 +1.40, gene:COLEC12 +1.51, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:CD14, gene:CLEC7A, gene:C1QA, gene:F13A1, gene:APOE +1.24), alongside increased macrophage state regulators (gene:MAFB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF, gene:CSF1R) and decreased gene:CSF1 (-5.91); 30/31 such represented members are positive.", "Inferred, not measured: higher surface scavenger-receptor capacity increases receptor-mediated internalization, raising the flux of lipoprotein/membrane cargo delivered to endosomes and lysosomes.", "MiT/TFE-family transcripts increase (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.65, gene:MITF +1.03) together with a CLEAR-like expansion of degradative capacity: acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:ACP5), all eight represented v-ATPase subunits plus accessory subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP2), lysosomal solute carriers and membrane proteins (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:LAPTM4A, gene:GPNMB), and endosome-to-lysosome trafficking machinery (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS28, gene:CHMP4B, gene:PIK3C3, gene:ARL8B, gene:AP5M1, gene:DNM2). This is capacity expansion matched to load, not evidence of reduced hydrolytic capacity.", "Lipid liberated in the endolysosome is routed toward esterification and storage rather than accumulating as free sterol: gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:ACAT2 (+2.04), gene:SCP2 (+5.90), gene:FABP3, gene:FABP5, gene:MGLL (+4.00), gene:NPC2, gene:PLTP, gene:PLA2G7, with sterol/lipogenic regulators up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7) and gene:OSBPL8 the single represented negative.", "Catabolic carbon is directed to mitochondria rather than glycolysis: mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/beta-oxidation and ETC transcripts rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1D, gene:CHCHD2; 17/18 represented positive), while rate-controlling glycolytic and oxidative-PPP transcripts fall (gene:HK2 -3.67 at adjusted p 8e-191, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32), an exception to the 77% upward bias of this selected list.", "Net effect in the measured mock condition: an adapted, high-throughput lipid-scavenging state with expanded endolysosomal capacity, expanded esterified/stored lipid, and oxidative rather than glycolytic ATP/NADPH supply; the contracted glycolytic/PPP transcript capacity constitutes a reserve deficit predicted to become functionally limiting only under a future acute phagocytic, lipid-loading or oxidant challenge, not an ongoing defect demonstrated here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a scavenger-driven, MiT/TFE-expanded endolysosomal lipid-processing state that routes cargo to esterified storage and mitochondrial oxidation while contracting glycolytic/PPP capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3019791012812465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21775786723668036, "cosine_similarity": 0.37369748474498526, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5840906148867314, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3019791012812465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21775786723668036, "cosine_similarity": 0.37369748474498526, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5840906148867314, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.30506675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 35}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_062", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| \u003e= 1.00, all adjusted p \u003c= 0.048) with a strong global positive shift (77% up, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base). All set-level claims are made relative to that internal background, not to an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene from the list is uninformative about its true change.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is not specified and is preserved as reported; effects are not converted to fold changes and RNA and protein-spot (log2) magnitudes are never compared numerically.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins; each carries several candidate genes, so no spot is treated as a measurement of a named protein.", "Increased hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB transcript abundance is assumed to reflect MiT/TFE-family transcriptional engagement rather than a change in mRNA stability or in cell-cycle/ maturation composition of the 10X Flex libraries.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply is assumed comparable between genotypes, which was not measured.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied in the workbook', so the reported adjusted p-values may reflect cell-level rather than donor/replicate-level variance and are treated as ranking statistics only.", "No lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, TFEB localization, lipid species, uptake rate or flux measurement is present in the supplied data; all activity, flux, localization and directionality statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an increased endolysosomal lipid-cargo load relative to hydrolytic capacity. This is associated with coordinate transcript induction of the MiT/TFE (CLEAR) lysosomal module - TFEB itself, luminal glycosidases, sphingolipid hydrolases and cathepsins, v-ATPase subunits, and late-endosome/lysosome trafficking factors - well above the strong global positive shift of this selected differential-expression list, while protein spots containing cathepsin and v-ATPase candidates are not coordinately increased. We propose that the resulting bottleneck at lysosomal hydrolysis/egress, together with induced mitochondrial citrate-export and acetyl-CoA-generating transcripts and terminal SREBP-target lipogenic enzymes, is what reroutes carbon and remodels sphingolipid and desaturated-lipid pools in APOE4 microglia. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["TFEB dependence (discriminating): knockdown or degradation of TFEB (with TFE3 co-depletion as a control for redundancy) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the coordinate hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript module (GBA, GAA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the mitochondrial acetyl-CoA transcripts (SLC25A1, ACSS2, OGDH) comparatively unaffected. If the hydrolase/v-ATPase module in APOE4 is unchanged after TFEB (and TFE3) loss, Step 3 and the CLEAR framing are wrong.", "Capacity versus transcript (discriminating): APOE4 microglia should show more LAMP1/LysoTracker-positive lysosomal volume than APOE3, but per-cell DQ-BSA dequenching rate and cathepsin B/D activity should increase far less than proportionally to the transcript differences, and clearance of a pulse of fluorescent myelin or ApoE-lipoprotein cargo should be slower or unchanged in APOE4. If APOE4 shows proportionally increased hydrolytic activity and faster cargo clearance, the 'bottleneck with incomplete compensation' claim (Steps 2 and 4) is falsified and the data instead indicate genuinely enhanced degradative flux.", "Load dependence (discriminating): loading APOE3 microglia with myelin debris or ApoE-containing lipoproteins should reproduce the CLEAR module, and blocking uptake in APOE4 (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or dynamin inhibition) should blunt it. Persistence of the full APOE4 CLEAR module with uptake blocked would favour a load-independent, cell-autonomous transcriptional difference instead.", "Lipid readout: inhibiting GBA (conduritol B epoxide) or acid sphingomyelinase should cause a larger accumulation of glucosylceramide and sphingomyelin, respectively, in APOE4 than in APOE3 if basal lysosomal sphingolipid flux is higher. Equal accumulation in both genotypes would show the hydrolase transcript increase does not translate into flux.", "Rejection of the sterol-synthesis focus: statin inhibition of HMGCR should not normalize the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase module or the cargo-clearance difference. If a statin abolishes the lysosomal module and the clearance phenotype, a de-novo sterol-synthesis mechanism (the assigned focus, which the supplied data do not support statistically) should be preferred over this one.", "Protein-level test: targeted immunoblot or PRM for cathepsin B, cathepsin D, GBA, GAA and ATP6V1A should resolve the ambiguous spots. Coordinate increases of all five in APOE4 would weaken Step 4 (and argue for successful compensation); mixed or decreased mature-form levels despite increased transcripts would support it."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (cargo delivery, inferred flux): transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 far above the list-wide median, plus gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7). Measured quantity is mRNA abundance only; uptake rate, receptor surface localization and cargo composition were not measured, so increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo to endosomes is inferred, not observed.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck): the rate of hydrolysis and of egress of lipid cargo from the endolysosomal lumen is proposed to be limiting in APOE4 relative to APOE3. No luminal lipid pool, pH, or hydrolase activity was measured here; the bottleneck is an inference from the transcriptional response in Step 3.", "Step 3 (compensatory CLEAR transcription): MiT/TFE signalling is engaged, with gene:TFEB transcript increased and a coordinate rise in CLEAR-type targets - luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DPP7, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), all measured v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2), mannose-6-phosphate targeting (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R), membrane/trafficking components (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B) and lysosomal solute exporters (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC66A1). TFEB nuclear localization and phosphorylation state were not measured.", "Step 4 (compensation incomplete): the transcriptional expansion is not mirrored by a coordinate increase in the corresponding protein spots. Spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins or a v-ATPase subunit are split in direction (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 decreased; protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:013, protein_spot:012 increased) and as a group are not shifted relative to all other spots. Because each spot carries several candidate genes, this is ambiguous evidence for a post-transcriptional or proteostatic ceiling, not proof of it.", "Step 5 (carbon rerouting): transcripts for mitochondrial/ cytosolic acetyl-CoA and citrate-export machinery are increased (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A11) while several upper-glycolytic and pentose-phosphate transcripts are decreased (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD). Flux was not measured; we infer a bias toward lipid- and TCA-derived acetyl-CoA rather than glycolytic ATP.", "Step 6 (lipid output): terminal SREBP-target lipogenic and post-squalene sterol enzymes are increased (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, gene:SOAT1), predicting a lipidome shift toward monounsaturated species and toward esterified/altered sterol handling downstream of the lysosomal step. Note the flux-controlling proximal enzymes HMGCR and SQLE and the lysosomal lipase LIPA are absent from the supplied rows, so sterol-synthesis flux cannot be claimed.", "Step 7 (phenotype): the combination of a hydrolysis/egress bottleneck and increased sphingolipid-hydrolase transcription predicts an altered sphingolipid balance (sphingomyelin and hexosyl-/gangliosides versus ceramide and sphingosine) in APOE4 microglia, plus reduced clearance of exogenous lipid-rich cargo. No lipid species were measured in this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by endolysosomal degradative capacity, driving a TFEB/CLEAR hydrolase-and-v-ATPase transcriptional expansion that is not matched at the protein-spot level"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27535723516597127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13632385591166105, "cosine_similarity": 0.3732612089093079, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6054660194174757, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27535723516597127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13632385591166105, "cosine_similarity": 0.3732612089093079, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6054660194174757, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.849582, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 174}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_059", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list thresholded at |effect| \u003e= 1 with an unspecified logarithm base; set-level medians are therefore interpreted only relative to the list's own strongly positive global median (+1.46), not as absolute up/down calls.", "Lower transcript levels for RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, MYH9 and MYO1F translate into proportionally lower protein pools; this was not measured, and the discordance of ACTB (RNA -4.98 versus mostly increased ACTB-candidate protein spots) shows the assumption can fail for abundant cytoskeletal genes.", "2D protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots 010 and 011 (MYH9 among candidates, effects -1.00 and -1.26) are directionally consistent but statistically non-significant (p=0.41, 0.32) and cannot establish a MYH9 protein decrease.", "The genotype effect is cell-intrinsic to microglia rather than a shift in microglial substate proportions or ambient RNA from the co-cultured astrocytes; no replicate structure or cell-composition data were supplied to test this.", "Net Rac/Rho activity is assumed to fall despite concurrent loss of negative regulators (ARHGAP30, FAM49B/CYRI-B, ARHGDIB), on the unverified background premise that RAC2 protein stability requires its GDI and that the hematopoietic Rac2 pool is not fully substituted by RAC1.", "No phagocytosis, actin imaging, lysosomal activity or lipid measurements are present in the supplied data; all flux, localisation and causal statements are inferences to be tested."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly at the internalization step of phagocytosis rather than at cargo recognition or cargo degradation: RNA for the leukocyte-restricted Rho-GTPase/actomyosin engulfment module (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, FAM49B/CYRI-B, MYO1F, MYH9, PLEK, SPN) is coordinately lower against a globally up-shifted differential-expression background, whereas recognition receptors are unchanged relative to that background and endolysosomal/hydrolase machinery is coordinately higher. We hypothesise that reduced RAC2/myosin-IIA-dependent cup extension and closure lowers particulate uptake flux per receptor engagement, while an up-regulated endolysosomal and SREBP-lipogenic program leaves the cell over-equipped to degrade and re-esterify the little cargo it internalises. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Live-imaging uptake assay with pHrodo-labelled large particles (myelin debris, synaptosomes or zymosan): APOE4 microglia will show fewer completed internalisation events per cell and slower cup closure than isogenic APOE3, while 4 C surface binding of the same particles is equal or greater. Equal internalisation rates, or binding that falls in proportion to uptake, would weaken the mechanism by relocating the defect to recognition or eliminating it.", "Myosin-II occlusion test: para-nitroblebbistatin (or Rac inhibition with EHT1864) will reduce particle internalisation strongly in APOE3 but produce little additional reduction in APOE4 (sub-additive/occluded interaction). A fully additive inhibition in both genotypes would falsify actomyosin/Rac2 capacity as the APOE4 bottleneck.", "Cargo-size dissociation: clathrin/dynamin-dependent small-cargo endocytosis (fluorescent transferrin, dextran) will be preserved or increased in APOE4 (consistent with higher DNM2, CLTB, SNX3, VPS26A RNA) while large-particle phagocytosis falls. A matched decrease in transferrin uptake would point instead to a general membrane-traffic or energetic defect.", "Uncoupling test: after normalising for the number of internalised particles, per-phagosome acidification and cargo proteolysis (DQ-BSA, pHrodo ratio) will be equal or faster in APOE4. Slower per-phagosome degradation would contradict the claim that the degradative arm is intact and would favour a lysosomal-dysfunction mechanism instead.", "Rescue specificity: re-expression of RAC2 (or a constitutively active Rac allele) in APOE4 microglia will restore internalisation rate without normalising the elevated CTSB/GBA/HEXA/ATP6V1A transcript program. Failure of RAC2 restoration to improve uptake would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Protein-level requirement: targeted immunoblot or PRM mass spectrometry must show reduced RAC2, DOCK8 and MYH9 protein in APOE4 versus APOE3. Unchanged protein for all three, despite the RNA differences, would substantially weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show lower RNA for RAC2, its GEF DOCK8, the GDI ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, FAM49B/CYRI-B, MYO1F, MYH9, PLEK and SPN (11 of 12 module genes below the global median of a list whose median is +1.46; permutation p=0.0003). Inferred: a smaller cellular pool of the leukocyte-specific Rac2/myosin-IIA machinery that drives pseudopod extension and contractile closure of the phagocytic cup. Protein pools and GTPase activity were not measured.", "Measured: RNA for ubiquitous Arp2/3 subunits and actin-turnover factors is at or above background (ARPC1B, ARPC4, ARPC5, CFL1, TWF2, IQGAP1, MYO1E, RHOA) and Arp2/3-containing 2D protein spots are increased, while integrin RNA rises steeply (ITGA6, ITGB1) as the anti-adhesive sialomucin SPN falls. Inferred: actin polymerisation capacity is retained but re-allocated toward integrin-anchored adhesive/spreading structures rather than Rac2/myosin-II-driven cup formation; localization of actin structures was not measured.", "Measured: opsonic and scavenger recognition receptors (TREM2, MERTK, CD36, C1QA, FCGR1A, FCGR3A, MRC1, ITGAX, SIRPA, CD47) sit at the global background median (set permutation p=0.76), with SCARB1 the outlier (+8.2). Inferred: cargo binding capacity is not the limiting element, so the bottleneck lies downstream of ligation at cup closure/scission.", "Inferred bottleneck: fewer completed internalisation events per bound particle in APOE4, i.e. reduced particulate flux into the endocytic pathway, despite normal binding.", "Measured: the endolysosomal/degradative program is coordinately raised (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, DNM2, AP5M1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, GAA, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, IGF2R, TFEB; set p=0.047 above an already positive background). Inferred: per-cargo degradative and acidification capacity is preserved or increased and is therefore uncoupled from the reduced uptake step; hydrolase activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Measured: SREBP-linked lipid synthesis and esterification RNA is uniformly up (SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, LDLR, ACAT2, SOAT1, DGAT1) together with SCARB1. Inferred: with less lipid entering as particulate cargo, lipid supply shifts toward receptor-mediated lipoprotein uptake and de novo synthesis/esterification, biasing APOE4 microglia toward stored neutral lipid; no lipid species were measured here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia downshift the hematopoietic RAC2-DOCK8-myosin-IIA engulfment module while over-building the endolysosomal degradative arm, making phagocytic cup closure the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11192445445482405, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2880330165539133, "cosine_similarity": 0.37233121864130914, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5986375404530745, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11192445445482405, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2880330165539133, "cosine_similarity": 0.37233121864130914, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5986375404530745, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.70114825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 175}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_079", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e1) with an unspecified logarithm base; module-level conclusions are therefore drawn from ranks and from permutation against the observed, strongly up-shifted background (median +1.46, 77% positive), not from absolute fold changes.", "Genes absent from the list are untested, not measured-as-unchanged; several canonical fusion components (e.g. STX7, VAMP7, VAMP8, HOPS subunits) are simply not present and their state is unknown.", "Transcript level is used as a proxy for the availability of the corresponding machinery; fusion rate, acidification, GTPase nucleotide state, protein localisation and lipid content were not measured.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (ACTB and keratins recur in many spots), so no spot is attributed to a single protein; spot-level directionality is treated as weak, ambiguous evidence and multiple spots per candidate may reflect proteoforms rather than total abundance.", "The global positive RNA shift is assumed to be at least partly biological rather than entirely a normalisation or cell-composition artefact of the APOE4 versus APOE3 pseudobulk comparison; if it is purely technical, all module contrasts must be read as relative ranks only.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so no independent assessment of variance is possible."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the internalisation and lysosome-biogenesis arms of the endolysosomal system (uptake/adhesion receptors, dynamin/clathrin, Rab7-retromer-ESCRT sorting, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB-type hydrolases) while the SNARE/tethering fusion module and the actomyosin contractile module are coordinately lower than the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is therefore not receptor-mediated internalisation nor hydrolase gene dosage but SNARE-dependent delivery/fusion of internalised cargo with acidified lysosomes, so that cargo and lipid dwell in pre-degradative late-endosomal/phagosomal compartments while lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, SMPD1) continue to feed the lipid pool. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: pulse-chase of pHrodo-labelled myelin or synaptosomes in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should dissociate the two steps - internalisation per cell at 15-30 min equal to or higher in APOE4, but the fraction of cargo reaching a degradative compartment (DQ-BSA dequenching rate, cargo-LAMP1 colocalisation, Magic Red cathepsin signal per internalised particle) lower in APOE4. If APOE4 shows a proportional or greater increase in degradative flux, the bottleneck is misplaced and the mechanism is weakened.", "Restoring the fusion step in APOE4 (STX17 or a compensating Qa/R-SNARE re-expression, or HOPS/RAB7-effector-promoting manipulation) should reduce accumulation of undegraded cargo and neutral-lipid stores without lowering hydrolase transcripts; conversely STX17/SNARE knockdown in APOE3 should phenocopy the APOE4 cargo- and lipid-retention phenotype. No effect of either manipulation would weaken the mechanism.", "Because terminal degradative flux is predicted to be already limited in APOE4, v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or cathepsin inhibition should produce a smaller incremental increase in undegraded cargo and LC3-II/cargo accumulation in APOE4 than in APOE3 (occlusion). Equal-magnitude responses in both genotypes would argue that acidification-coupled degradation is not the limiting node.", "Untargeted or targeted lipidomics (the unmeasured endpoint here) should show higher cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol and sphingomyelin/ceramide-pathway species in APOE4 mock microglia, with the excess localised to LAMP1-positive/BODIPY-positive compartments; absence of any lipid-storage difference would falsify the downstream limb.", "Cytoskeletal counter-test: if the true bottleneck were actin cup formation rather than fusion, Arp2/3 (CK-666) or myosin II (blebbistatin) inhibition should erase the genotype difference in internalisation; observing that these inhibitors equalise uptake while leaving the degradation deficit intact would support the fusion bottleneck, whereas equalisation of both uptake and degradation would relocate the bottleneck to engulfment.", "Protein-level check: quantitative immunoblotting should show STX17 and MYH9 protein lower in APOE4 while mature cathepsin B/D and ATP6V1E1 are not increased despite higher transcripts; finding STX17 and MYH9 protein unchanged or higher would weaken the proposed chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts of surface uptake and adhesion receptors (gene:ITGA6 +15.5, gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:ITGB1 +6.3, with gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2 above zero), which we infer, but do not measure, increases the capacity for particle and lipoprotein internalisation.", "Transcripts for scission and endosomal sorting rise in parallel (gene:DNM2 +5.8, gene:CLTB +2.1, gene:SNX3 +3.9, gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:RAB7A +2.7), consistent with an expanded early-to-late endosomal itinerary; vesicle flux itself is inferred, not observed.", "A TFEB-type lysosome-biogenesis program is transcriptionally engaged (gene:TFEB +2.4; gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK; gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C all up), predicting more hydrolase and proton-pump synthesis rather than a hydrolase-dosage deficit.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK: the fusion/tethering module runs against this trend (gene:STX17 -2.1, gene:VAMP2 -1.9, gene:STXBP2 -1.2, gene:STX16 -4.1, gene:BET1L -3.8, gene:STXBP5 -5.5; module mean -1.2 vs background +1.39, permutation p=0.0012), and the actomyosin/motor arm needed for phagosome closure and centripetal transport is likewise low (gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:MYO1F -3.7, with gene:ARHGDIA +10.6 predicted to sequester Rho/Rac-GDP). We infer a reduced rate of heterotypic phagosome/autophagosome-to-lysosome fusion; fusion rate, GTPase activity and localisation are not measured here.", "At the protein-spot level the degradative machinery does not track its transcripts: ATP6V1E1-containing spots fall (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93) and cathepsin-containing spot trains split rather than rise uniformly (protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 versus protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.59), which is compatible with unchanged or redistributed mature hydrolase/pump pools; spots contain several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins.", "Consequence: internalised and endogenously synthesised lipid (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:DHCR24 +3.7, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7) is delivered to a compartment with limited terminal fusion, so APOE4 microglia should accumulate undegraded, lipid-laden late-endosomal/phagosomal structures and neutral-lipid/sterol-ester stores; no lipid species were measured in this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia scale uptake and lysosome-biogenesis transcripts but not the fusion/actomyosin execution machinery, creating a terminal cargo-delivery bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1669682088394934, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11362143581698111, "cosine_similarity": 0.3722427027248366, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6374142394822007, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1669682088394934, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11362143581698111, "cosine_similarity": 0.3722427027248366, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6374142394822007, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.739196, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 176}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_115", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive). All enrichment statements therefore use the list itself as background, and no claim is made about genome-wide directional bias.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; relative ordering, not absolute fold change, is used. Very large values (up to +15.5) are assumed to come from low-count genes and are down-weighted in favour of genes with the smallest adjusted p-values.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding enzyme/receptor capacity. Enzyme activity, protein localization, sterol pools, lipid-droplet content, SREBP cleavage, lysosomal pH and all metabolic fluxes were not measured in this dataset and are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-diagnostic corroboration or counter-evidence, never as identification of a specific protein.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some APOE and lipid supply is non-cell-autonomous; the microglial phenotype is assumed to reflect the microglial genotype rather than an astrocyte-driven artefact, which is untested here.", "Biological replicate number was not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values are assumed to reflect cell-level rather than donor-level replication and are treated as ranking statistics only.", "The genotype difference is assumed not to be confounded by differing differentiation maturity between the APOE3 and APOE4 lines."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in lipid handling, not in ER unfolded-protein signalling: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors and for a broad set of lysosomal acid hydrolases are coordinately higher, yet sterol-synthesis and neutral-lipid-esterification transcripts are also higher. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the handoff of lysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool: SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification and lipid-droplet storage divert incoming sterol so that ER sterol sensing continues to read deficiency, sustaining SREBP target expression and creating a futile uptake-hydrolysis-re-esterification cycle. Direction of causation is not established by these data; only steady-state abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. Sandoz 58-035 or avasimibe) in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should raise the ER-accessible sterol pool, reduce SREBP2-target transcripts (DHCR24, LSS, ACAT2, INSIG1, HMGCS1) and reduce neutral-lipid-droplet area, with a significantly larger genotype-by-drug interaction in APOE4 than in APOE3. If SOAT1 inhibition leaves SREBP2 targets elevated in APOE4 (or lowers them equally in both genotypes), the proposed esterification bottleneck is wrong.", "Direct pool measurement: an ER-accessible-cholesterol probe (ALOD4/PFO* domain) plus quantification of nuclear SREBP2 should show lower accessible ER sterol and higher nuclear SREBP2 in APOE4 despite higher total cellular cholesteryl ester by lipidomics. Finding equal or higher accessible ER sterol in APOE4, or no increase in cholesteryl ester, falsifies the core claim.", "Site-of-block discrimination: blocking lysosomal cholesterol egress with U18666A should produce a similar proportional increase in cholesteryl ester and SREBP2 targets in both genotypes if the bottleneck is downstream esterification; if APOE4 cells are already maximally blocked and show little further change, the bottleneck is lysosomal egress (NPC1/NPC2) rather than esterification, weakening this hypothesis.", "Rejection of the ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 microglia should not show elevated BiP/HSPA5 or GRP94/HSP90B1 protein, XBP1 splicing, or ATF4/CHOP protein relative to APOE3, and IRE1 or PERK inhibition or 4-PBA should not normalise the lipid-droplet or SREBP-target phenotype. If UPR markers are elevated at protein level and PERK/IRE1 inhibition normalises the lipid phenotype, an ER-stress-primary mechanism should replace this one.", "Flux prediction: pulse-chase of fluorescent or isotope-labelled acetylated-LDL or myelin debris should show faster uptake and faster lysosomal hydrolysis in APOE4 but a smaller fraction of label reaching the ER free-sterol pool and a larger fraction in cholesteryl-ester droplets. Equal partitioning between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Metabolic corollary: Seahorse profiling should show lower glycolytic rate and higher fatty-acid-dependent oxygen consumption in APOE4, and etomoxir should preferentially impair APOE4 microglia. Equal or higher glycolysis in APOE4 would contradict the fuel-shift step without necessarily falsifying the sterol bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_115", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher expression of lipoprotein and scavenger uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR) is inferred to raise the flux of lipoprotein- and debris-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system. Flux itself was not measured; only transcript abundance was.", "Coordinate elevation of lysosomal acid hydrolase and lysosome-biogenesis transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:ACP5, gene:TFEB) is inferred to expand lysosomal catabolic capacity, generating free cholesterol and sphingolipid catabolites inside the lysosome. Enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and lipid content were not measured.", "The bottleneck: cholesterol released in the lysosome is inferred not to equilibrate with the ER-accessible regulatory pool. Instead, elevated esterification and storage machinery (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5, gene:ABHD5, gene:MGLL) is inferred to channel free sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol in lipid droplets, lowering the ER sterol activity that SCAP/INSIG senses.", "Because the ER sensor reads sterol deficiency, SREBP processing is inferred to remain active, sustaining the elevated sterol-synthesis and lipogenic transcript program observed (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:HMGCS1) together with the SREBP feedback target gene:INSIG1. SREBP2 cleavage and nuclear localization were not measured.", "Newly synthesised plus imported sterol re-enters the same esterification sink, producing a self-sustaining lipid-loading cycle; oxysterol-generating and efflux-adjacent transcripts (gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:ABCA7) rise as a partial, insufficient relief valve.", "The cycle is inferred to be supported by a fuel shift away from glycolysis (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD lower) toward mitochondrial oxidation of the liberated fatty acids (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:CHCHD2, gene:ATP5F1D, gene:ATP5F1B higher), consistent with the hypoxia/lipid-handling regulator gene:EPAS1 being higher. Metabolic flux was not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lipid uptake and lysosomal hydrolase capacity but esterify the liberated sterol, leaving the ER regulatory sterol pool functionally low and the SREBP program locked on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23446442417752833, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28071137284324255, "cosine_similarity": 0.3718109501427034, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_115", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6070355987055016, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23446442417752833, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28071137284324255, "cosine_similarity": 0.3718109501427034, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6070355987055016, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.831738, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 177}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_121", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported on an unspecified logarithm base and are a preselected differential-expression list (no |effect| below 1 is present), so absence of a gene is not evidence of no change and RNA magnitudes are not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot values.", "The selected RNA list is not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level claims were therefore tested against the observed, already positive global distribution (median about +1.46, 1705 up versus 507 down) rather than against zero.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; several candidates (for example ANXA1 in nine spots, ACTB in twenty-five) appear in many spots with opposite signs, so spot-level direction is assigned to a co-migrating feature, not to a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an upper bound on, not a measure of, hydrolase activity; proenzyme maturation, mannose-6-phosphate targeting, luminal pH and saposin availability are unmeasured.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, lysosomal-pH, autophagic-flux or respirometry data were supplied; lipid accumulation and reduced catabolic flux are predictions, not observations.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous, and replicate number and normalisation details were not supplied, leaving a global scaling or ambient-RNA artefact unexcluded.", "Causal direction between lipid load, lysosomal program and mitochondrial/inflammatory transcripts is assumed, not demonstrated."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling: transcripts for lipid-acquisition receptors and lipogenic regulators and, far more strongly, for lipid-directed lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase/CLEAR-network genes are coordinately higher in APOE4, whereas the lysosomal-hydrolase-candidate protein spots show no matching coherent increase. We hypothesise that cargo delivery to the endolysosome exceeds mature luminal hydrolase capacity in APOE4, so that lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic throughput (not transcription of the hydrolases) is the primary bottleneck, driving a feed-forward TFEB-like compensatory transcriptional response and secondary mitochondrial and inflammatory tilts. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Enzyme-capacity test: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, LAMP1/LysoTracker lysosomal volume and neutral-lipid/filipin staining will be higher, but GBA and acid sphingomyelinase specific activity and the mature two-chain CTSD fraction, expressed per unit lysosomal mass, will increase far less than the corresponding transcripts (predicted activity ratio below about 1.3-fold). If APOE4 lysosomes show hydrolase activity rising in proportion to transcripts and no lipid accumulation, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation (capacity versus delivery): selectively raising luminal capacity in APOE4 only - GBA1 overexpression or chaperone/recombinant-enzyme supplementation, or TFEB overexpression - should lower glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin and the accumulated cargo and dampen the CLEAR-network transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1H) without lowering gene:SCARB1 or gene:CD36; blocking delivery instead (SR-B1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-free medium) should also lower cargo but should lower the CLEAR transcripts while leaving hydrolase specific activity unchanged. If neither intervention reduces the accumulated lipid, or if enzyme augmentation raises measured activity yet leaves cargo and the CLEAR program unchanged, the bottleneck lies elsewhere (for example NPC-dependent sterol export or lipid-droplet esterification) and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Secondary-consequence test: restoring lysosomal catabolic throughput in APOE4 should normalise the mitonuclear transcript mismatch (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH up with gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB down) and the reactive tilt (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2). If mitochondrial and inflammatory phenotypes persist unchanged after lysosomal rescue, the mitochondrial arm is a parallel primary defect rather than a downstream consequence.", "Artefact test: re-normalising the same libraries with spike-ins or total-RNA-per-cell scaling and re-running the comparison should preserve the lysosomal-hydrolase set as an outlier relative to the global shift. If the enrichment disappears once the global positive shift is removed, the transcript evidence for this mechanism is an artefact.", "Protein-level test: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS of CTSB, CTSD, GBA and HEXB in the same lysates should show pro-form/mature-form redistribution rather than a uniform increase, matching the divergent cathepsin-candidate spots (protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:067 down). A uniform, large increase of all mature hydrolase forms in APOE4 would weaken the post-transcriptional-bottleneck step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_121", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipid-acquisition and lipid-esterification machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid cargo (lipoprotein/membrane/myelin-like) into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): The cell responds with a CLEAR/TFEB-like lysosomal program - gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2 and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1) are up, and the lipid-directed luminal hydrolases are the single most strongly shifted coherent set (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:DPP7, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:CTSD), median far above the already positive global median of the selected DE list.", "Step 3 (measured protein spots, inferred capacity): Protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases do not show a matching coherent increase - their median equals the median of all spots, and CTSD- and CTSB-candidate spots split into up and down spots (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052, protein_spot:027 up versus protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 down; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:075 carry v-ATPase candidates and are not up). We infer that mature, catalytically competent luminal hydrolase capacity per lysosome does not scale with the transcript increase; spot identity is ambiguous, so this is a capacity inference, not a protein identification.", "Step 4 (inferred, primary bottleneck): Because delivery (Step 1) rises while functional luminal hydrolysis (Step 3) does not rise proportionally, undegraded sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide/ganglioside and sterol-ester cargo is predicted to accumulate in an expanded acidic compartment; the resulting lysosomal stress sustains the TFEB-like program of Step 2 as a feed-forward compensation rather than a resolution.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred consequence): Downstream of a lipid-loaded lysosome, nuclear-encoded oxidative-metabolism transcripts rise (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5) while mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4), a mitonuclear mismatch consistent with, but not proof of, impaired mitochondrial output; in parallel APOE4 shows a mild reactive tilt (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD up) with loss of homeostatic/antigen-processing markers (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.91)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a CLEAR/TFEB-like lysosomal lipid-catabolism transcript program that is not matched at the hydrolase protein level, making luminal glycosphingolipid degradation the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17870989181405308, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1213629661790619, "cosine_similarity": 0.3717936601115042, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_121", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6290582524271844, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17870989181405308, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1213629661790619, "cosine_similarity": 0.3717936601115042, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6290582524271844, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6735595, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 178}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_091", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 positive, median +1.46), so only percentile/rank-based contrasts within the list are interpreted; absolute enrichment against an unbiased transcriptome cannot be assessed from the supplied data.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and magnitudes reach +15.5; effect sizes are used only for ranking, not as literal fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is treated as a proxy for enzyme availability; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cholesterol/lipid localisation, egress flux, esterification flux and beta-oxidation flux are all inferred, not measured here.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration that some lysosomal-hydrolase-containing spots move up.", "No lipid, lipidomic, imaging, flux or metabolite measurement is supplied, so the predicted lipid-droplet/lysosomal-lipid endpoint is unobserved in this dataset.", "Key nodes of the proposed circuit (ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA, ACLY, PLIN2, CPT1A, FASN, ACACA) are absent from the supplied rows, so the pathway is reconstructed from partial coverage.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular lipoprotein/APOE supply is genotype-matched but cell-mixed; some genotype effects may be non-cell-autonomous.", "Association only: no causal direction between APOE genotype, the lysosomal program and the lipogenic program has been established by these observations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD) sit far above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list (mean percentile 0.71, z=+3.05), while transcripts for lysosomal membrane/egress machinery (NPC2, SCARB2, LAMP1, CLN3, M6PR, SLC17A5, RAB7A) sit at background (mean percentile 0.48, z=-0.32; hydrolase\u003eegress Mann-Whitney z=2.30, p=0.021) and the fatty-acid oxidation module is not elevated (mean percentile 0.40, z=-0.86; ACSL4 -2.14, ACSL5 -3.11). We hypothesise that the resulting mismatch between luminal hydrolysis and post-hydrolysis export/oxidation is the primary bottleneck, and that lipid liberated in the lysosome is instead diverted into an active SREBP-type lipogenic/acylation and esterification program (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, ACSS2, DHCR24, DGAT1, SOAT1; module z=+2.46), producing a neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet-loaded, sterol-retaining APOE4 microglial state rather than an inflammatory one (NF-kB/inflammation module z=-0.91).", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving the egress step in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should reduce filipin-positive and LipidTOX-positive signal within LAMP1-positive compartments and, within 24-72 h, normalise the APOE4-high hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, NAGLU, SMPD1) and TFEB toward APOE3 levels. If lysosomal lipid load falls but the hydrolase program stays elevated, the 'egress bottleneck drives compensatory hydrolase induction' step is wrong.", "Opposite-arm control: enhancing hydrolysis alone (TFEB overexpression) should raise hydrolase transcripts and activity but should NOT reduce, and may increase, APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet area; if TFEB overexpression clears the droplets, the bottleneck is degradative capacity rather than egress and this hypothesis is falsified.", "Storage-route test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) plus DGAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 microglia from esterified droplet lipid to free cholesterol/free fatty acid with a genotype-selective rise in ER stress and toxicity; no APOE4-selective effect would weaken the esterification/storage step.", "Flux test: APOE4 microglia should show no increase, or a decrease, in 13C-palmitate-derived CO2/acetyl-CoA oxidation and in cholesterol efflux to lipid-free ApoA-I or HDL relative to APOE3, despite the high TCA transcript module; an APOE4 increase in fatty-acid oxidation flux or in cholesterol efflux would falsify the 'disposal not scaled' step and favour the mitochondrial-oxidation alternative.", "Direct measurement: quantitative lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased cholesteryl esters and/or triacylglycerol and increased glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin-derived species; absence of any neutral-lipid or sphingolipid difference would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Activity check: GBA, beta-hexosaminidase and cathepsin B/D enzymatic activity in APOE4 lysates should be equal or higher than APOE3; clearly lower activity despite higher transcripts would indicate a degradative-failure mechanism instead of the proposed egress bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mechanism_steps": ["Lipoprotein and lipid influx into the endolysosome is at least as high in APOE4 as APOE3: the HDL/lipoprotein selective-uptake receptor transcript SCARB1 is among the most strongly increased rows in the dataset (gene:SCARB1, +8.22, ~top 1% of 2212 selected rows), with CD36 and LDLR also increased (inferred flux, not measured uptake).", "The cell responds with a coordinated expansion of luminal acid-hydrolase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) alongside increased TFEB transcript (gene:TFEB, +2.38); we infer this is a compensatory transcriptional response to a lipid/substrate load rather than a primary driver.", "The export arm is not scaled with hydrolysis: transcripts for lysosomal cholesterol/solute transfer and membrane machinery (gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:LAMP1, gene:CLN3, gene:SLC17A5, gene:RAB7A) and the down-regulated sorting receptor gene:M6PR remain at or below the list-wide median, making post-hydrolysis egress the rate-limiting step (inferred flux/localisation, not measured).", "Catabolic disposal of the liberated fatty acids is likewise not up-scaled: beta-oxidation/activation transcripts are at background or reduced (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:CROT +1.03), so oxidation cannot absorb the released acyl load even though mitochondrial TCA/carrier transcripts are high (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:DLD).", "Carbon is instead routed to lipid assembly and storage: acetyl-CoA supply and lipogenic/acylation transcripts are coherently elevated (gene:ACSS2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1) together with esterification enzymes (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) and a still-active sterol-synthesis arm (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1), which is the transcriptional signature expected when sterol is sequestered away from the ER sensor rather than delivered to it.", "The predicted cellular endpoint is APOE4-selective accumulation of cholesteryl ester/triacylglycerol droplets and of undigested or unexported lipid within LAMP1-positive compartments, with limited efflux capacity (only gene:ABCA7 +2.14 and gene:APOE +1.24 measured; ABCA1 and NPC1 are absent from the supplied rows), and without a dominant inflammatory activation program."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid egress, not degradative capacity, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 iPSC-microglia: a hydrolase-heavy lysosomal program without matched export or oxidation reroutes lipid into esterification and membrane/neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29590518037145075, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25938765161256944, "cosine_similarity": 0.37117057222144045, "direction_accuracy": 0.3656957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mean_absolute_error": 0.612411003236246, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29590518037145075, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25938765161256944, "cosine_similarity": 0.37117057222144045, "direction_accuracy": 0.3656957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.612411003236246, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.87716625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 179}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_080", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1.0, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, n = 2212, 77.1% positive, median +1.46) in an unspecified logarithm base; all directional statements are judged against that 77% positive background, and absent genes (e.g. CAT, SOD1/2, G6PD, ATF4, mitoribosomal genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for activity, flux, assembly or localisation; no respiration, ROS, GSH/NADPH, mtDNA copy number or lysosomal-degradation flux was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots (n = 92, mean 4.8 candidate genes per spot, frequent keratin/actin candidates) are treated as ambiguous multi-identity measurements; they are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of a named protein.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript values from probe-based 10X Flex chemistry, and the strong global positive skew of the selected list, may partly reflect assay/normalisation composition rather than biology; the mito-nuclear contrast (4/6 negative) rests on only six transcripts.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some APOE4-vs-APOE3 differences may be non-cell-autonomous; the isogenic design controls background genotype but not this.", "The predicted reserve deficit (cytosolic NADPH/NAD arm, mito-nuclear stoichiometry) is a challenge-revealed property, explicitly not claimed as an ongoing defect in the measured mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant transcriptional difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) is a coordinated cell-state change, not a peroxisomal or oxidative-damage lesion: APOE4 cells coordinately raise lipoprotein/lipid handling, TFEB-type lysosomal-degradative machinery and nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery (38/38 represented ETC structural subunits up; TCA, carrier and import transcripts up with large effects), while cytosolic NAD/NADPH-regenerating transcripts (NAMPT, NADK, PGD, TALDO1) fall and matrix-directed reducing-equivalent routes rise (MDH1/GOT1 malate-aspartate shuttle, SLC25A11/SLC25A13, mitochondrial NAD carrier SLC25A51, NNT). Increased matrix thiol-peroxidase/thioredoxin transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, TXNDC17, TXNL1, MSRA, SELENOW) are best read as proportionate buffering of a higher oxidative load (successful adaptation / increased catabolic throughput), not as evidence of an ongoing oxidative-stress failure; the narrowed cytosolic NADPH/NAD arm and the non-coordinate mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts constitute a predicted loss of reserve that would be revealed only by a future oxidative or cargo challenge. Causality is not established; these are abundance measurements, and no flux, activity or localisation was measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective extracellular-flux assay of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption and higher maximal respiration, with equal or lower glycolytic ECAR. If APOE4 instead shows equal/lower OCR, low spare respiratory capacity and higher ECAR, the increased-throughput interpretation fails and the failed-compensation alternative (nuclear upregulation compensating an ETC/mtDNA-expression defect) is favoured.", "Prospective substrate-dependence test: acute inhibition of lysosomal acidification/hydrolysis (low-dose bafilomycin A1 or lysosomal acid lipase inhibition) or SCARB1/CD36 knockdown should collapse the APOE4-over-APOE3 OCR difference. Persistence of the OCR difference would refute the lysosome-to-mitochondria substrate-routing step.", "Prospective redox-reserve challenge: with roGFP2-Grx1 (cytosolic and mito-targeted) plus NADPH/NAD(H) biosensors, APOE4 and APOE3 should be indistinguishable in the mock steady state, but APOE4 should oxidise faster and die more after menadione, H2O2 or myelin/oxLDL loading, with rescue by NAD precursor (NR/NMN) or G6PD/PPP support. Baseline cytosolic oxidation already present in mock APOE4, or equal challenge sensitivity, would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective mito-nuclear stoichiometry test: BN-PAGE/complex-activity and mtDNA copy number should show assembled complex I/IV increased roughly in proportion to nuclear subunit protein in APOE4. A selective fall in assembled complex IV or in mtDNA-encoded protein per nuclear subunit would contradict this hypothesis and support a mtDNA-expression bottleneck instead.", "Prospective quantitative proteomics (replacing ambiguous 2D spots): matrix proteins PRDX3, MDH2/MDH1, OGDH, NDUFB8 and lysosomal CTSB/CTSD/HEXB should be increased in APOE4, whereas NAMPT, TALDO1 and PGD should be unchanged or decreased. A decrease in ETC/TCA proteins despite increased transcripts would indicate translational or assembly failure and refute the increased-capacity claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid capture, esterification and sterol/fatty-acid synthesis (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1; 19/19 represented members positive), increasing the lipid cargo entering the endolysosomal system (uptake flux itself not measured).", "A lysosome-biogenesis-type program expands degradative capacity (gene:TFEB, all ten represented V-ATPase subunits including gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A, and hydrolases gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), plus amino-acid/nutrient efflux-import transporters (gene:SLC38A7 +7.5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:SLC1A5, gene:GLS), supplying fatty acids and amino acids as oxidative substrate.", "Nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery is coordinately increased: every represented ETC structural subunit is up (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:SDHB; 38/38, median +2.6), together with TCA/anaplerotic and substrate-entry components (gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA) and import/assembly-supporting transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:TUFM, gene:SLC25A46, gene:PRELID3B), i.e. increased oxidative capacity rather than a compensatory response to an energy crisis.", "Reducing-equivalent and NAD traffic is repartitioned toward the matrix: malate-aspartate shuttle and carrier transcripts rise (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5), the mitochondrial NAD carrier gene:SLC25A51 and gene:NNT rise, while cytosolic NAD salvage/NADPH transcripts fall (gene:NAMPT -2.6, gene:NADK -1.1, gene:PGD -1.3, gene:TALDO1 -2.3), so cytosolic NADPH supply for glutathione/thioredoxin recycling is predicted to be narrower even though matrix NADPH routes are favoured.", "Matrix-facing thiol antioxidant transcripts increase roughly in proportion to the oxidative program (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:MSRA, gene:SELENOW), consistent with buffering of a higher electron flux; there is no coherent integrated-stress or glycolytic-crisis block among represented genes (only gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3 up; gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1 down), arguing for adaptation rather than failed compensation.", "The same state down-weights motility/immune-effector transcripts (gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:SPN -7.3, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.2, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:CTSS -5.6, gene:CSF1 -5.9) while adhesion transcripts rise (gene:ITGA6 +15.5, gene:ITGB1, gene:ARHGDIA), i.e. a less migratory, more degradative/oxidative microglial state.", "Predicted consequence (not observed here): with cytosolic NAD/NADPH regeneration transcripts reduced and mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts not co-upregulated (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.4, gene:MT-CYB -2.3, gene:MT-ND4 -1.8, gene:MT-CO2 -1.3 versus gene:MT-ND5 +1.9, gene:MT-ND4L +2.0), APOE4 microglia should have reduced antioxidant and assembly reserve that is exposed by oxidative or lipid-loading challenge rather than by the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-fuelled mitochondrial oxidative state with reducing-equivalent traffic repartitioned from cytosol to matrix"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3458350256618543, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22294705661225414, "cosine_similarity": 0.3711582065981086, "direction_accuracy": 0.3802588996763754, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5919449838187703, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3458350256618543, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22294705661225414, "cosine_similarity": 0.3711582065981086, "direction_accuracy": 0.3802588996763754, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5919449838187703, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.88471875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 36}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_142", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive skew (77.1% positive, median +1.459 in an unspecified logarithm base); the mechanism assumes the direction, not the magnitude, of the sterol and lysosomal modules survives an unbiased, independently normalised measurement.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for pathway engagement only; SREBP-2 cleavage, HMGCR/SQLE flux (both unmeasured), NPC1-dependent egress, esterification rate, lysosomal pH and cholesterol localisation are all inferred and unmeasured.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as non-corroboration, never as evidence that a named protein changed.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some transcript differences may reflect altered microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange or imperfect cell-type deconvolution rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are stated to be isogenic, so differences are attributed to genotype rather than background; replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently weighted."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia the rate-limiting step distinguishing them from isogenic APOE3 is delivery of endolysosome-derived cholesterol to the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool. Transcript-level data are consistent with an ER sterol pool that the SCAP/INSIG/SREBP-2 sensor reads as low, so APOE4 microglia simultaneously raise post-squalene synthesis, receptor-mediated lipid uptake and sterol-ester/triacylglycerol storage transcripts while expanding a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program - a futile acquire-store-degrade cycle rather than a net cholesterol deficit. Sterol pool sizes, SREBP-2 cleavage, transport flux and causal direction were not measured and are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: load APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with LDL/myelin-derived cholesterol versus 25-hydroxycholesterol. 25-HC acts directly on INSIG/SCAP and bypasses lysosome-to-ER transport, so it should suppress HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR and INSIG1 equally in both genotypes, whereas LDL-derived cholesterol should suppress them significantly less in APOE4. Equal suppression by both sterol sources, or equal failure of both, would refute the transport bottleneck and point instead to a sensor-level or purely transcriptional difference.", "ER-accessible cholesterol measured with a non-lytic ALOD4/D4H probe should be lower in APOE4 while filipin/total and LAMP1-colocalised cholesterol is equal or higher. If ER-accessible cholesterol is equal or higher in APOE4 despite elevated SREBP-2 target transcripts, the mechanism is falsified.", "Nuclear (cleaved) SREBP-2 relative to precursor should be higher in APOE4 by immunoblot; if the precursor/cleaved ratio is unchanged, the transcript module reflects SREBP-2-independent regulation and Step 2 fails.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should raise ER-accessible cholesterol and suppress the SREBP-2 target transcripts more in APOE4 than APOE3; if SOAT1 inhibition leaves the SREBP-2 module unchanged in APOE4, the esterification-diversion arm (Step 3) is wrong.", "The lysosomal module should be reproduced at the protein and activity level in APOE4 (CTSB/GBA/HEXA activity assays, v-ATPase-dependent acidification). The supplied 2D spot data do not support it - spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases average +0.01 log2 and include significant decreases (protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064) - so a failure to detect increased hydrolase activity would demote Step 4 to an mRNA-only change and weaken the compensatory-expansion interpretation.", "Independent normalisation control: qPCR or spike-in-normalised RNA should confirm that HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24 and INSIG1 are elevated in APOE4 relative to housekeeping transcripts. If the sterol module collapses to null once the global positive shift is removed, the whole hypothesis is an artefact of the selected, skewed row set."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_142", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, primary bottleneck): In APOE4 microglia, cholesterol liberated in late endosomes/lysosomes is transferred inefficiently to the ER-accessible pool. Only indirect transcript proxies are measured (gene:NPC2 +1.17 modest; gene:OSBPL8 -1.90, an ER-anchored lipid-transfer ORP, decreased); NPC1, GRAMD1/Aster, STARD3 and VAPA/VAPB transcripts are absent from the supplied rows, so the transfer machinery itself is largely unmeasured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): The SCAP/INSIG-SREBP-2 sensor behaves as if ER sterol is low. Every measured post-squalene and sterol-regulated transcript is increased in APOE4 (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1; 10/10 positive). Increased gene:INSIG1, itself an SREBP-2 target, is used as an inferred read-out of active SREBP-2 processing, not as evidence of restored feedback; SREBP-2 cleavage was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Lipid acquisition and storage arms are co-induced rather than reciprocally regulated - gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), with lipogenic gene:SREBF1 (+4.67) and gene:SCD (+4.17). Inferred consequence: incoming sterol is esterified and diverted to storage/organellar pools instead of equilibrating with the ER sensor, sustaining Step 2.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): A coordinated lysosomal-degradative program is the quantitatively strongest coherent module (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65). Interpreted as a compensatory TFEB-associated expansion of the compartment where lipid is retained; lysosome number, pH, sterol content and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred output): Sterol-disposal transcripts also rise (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:MYLIP +1.28). Because ABCA1, ABCG1 and NPC1 are not in the supplied rows, efflux capacity is unresolved; the co-induction of oxysterol-generating and LXR-target transcripts alongside SREBP-2 targets is treated as internal counter-evidence requiring compartmental separation of sterol pools (ER-accessible pool low, endolysosomal/esterified pool normal or high).", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): The resulting futile cycle - continued synthesis and uptake feeding an expanding, poorly exported lysosomal/ester pool - imposes a chronic biosynthetic and lysosomal load that would degrade APOE4 microglial responses to further lipid challenge. This is an inference, not an observation; no functional, lipidomic or imaging data are supplied."], "title": "An endolysosome-to-ER cholesterol delivery bottleneck keeps the SCAP/SREBP-2 sterol sensor de-repressed in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23319385150199126, "cosine_similarity": 0.3710515046699549, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_142", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936666666666667, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23319385150199126, "cosine_similarity": 0.3710515046699549, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5936666666666667, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.321506, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 180}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_011", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (1705 positive, 507 negative effects), so set-level statements are made relative to that list's own distribution (median effect 1.46) and not to an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment is assessed by rank tests against the other supplied genes.", "The RNA logarithm base is not stated in the workbook and is preserved as reported; no effect size is converted to a linear fold change, and RNA and protein-spot (log2) magnitudes are not compared numerically.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for enzyme activity and metabolic flux; every flux, localisation and activity statement in the mechanism is inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots are assumed to be mixtures: each carries up to six candidate genes (frequently actin and keratin), so no spot is treated as a unique protein identification, and spot-level directions are used only as weak, mixed evidence about hydrolase and v-ATPase protein distribution.", "The 3.4:1 excess of up over down calls is assumed to be at least partly a property of list construction or normalisation rather than a true global transcriptional amplification; the mechanism therefore rests on relative, within-list contrasts (for example lysosomal hydrolases versus the list median, mitochondrially encoded versus nuclear OXPHOS).", "Cells are assumed to be correctly assigned microglia despite astrocyte co-culture; ambient RNA from astrocytes could inflate some shared transcripts.", "Key pools of the proposed pathway were not measured at all (no LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2/PLIN3, ABCA1, ABCG1, FASN, ACACA, CPT1A rows; no lipidomic, imaging or flux data), so lysosomal lipolysis, cholesterol efflux and droplet content are assumptions rather than observations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 primarily in lipid handling flux rather than in lipid-sensing per se: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid acquisition (SCARB1, CD36, APOE, TREM2, ABCA7, PLA2G7, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163) and for a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal hydrolase program (CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, CTSK, GBA, GAA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1) are coordinately higher, while the transcriptional signals that would support oxidative disposal of the liberated fatty acids are not (long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4/ACSL5 lower; mitochondrial-genome-encoded OXPHOS transcripts lower despite higher nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts). We propose that the primary bottleneck is disposal of lysosome-derived fatty acyl and sterol carbon by mitochondrial oxidation, and that APOE4 cells therefore commit that carbon to monounsaturated neutral-lipid esters via an SREBF1/SCD/ACSS2/SLC25A1 lipogenic arm and AGPAT2/GPAT4/LPCAT1/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification enzymes, producing a stored-ester (lipid-droplet) phenotype. The stored-lipid pool itself was not measured here; it is the predicted, currently unobserved endpoint. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of DGAT1 plus SOAT1 in APOE4 microglia should substantially reduce neutral-lipid ester content (BODIPY/LipidTOX droplet area, TG and cholesteryl-ester species by lipidomics) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, TFEB) largely intact and raising free fatty-acid and lyso-phospholipid species. If instead the hydrolase program collapses in parallel, the proposed direction (load first, hydrolase induction second, esterification as the terminal sink) is wrong.", "If the bottleneck is truly post-lysosomal oxidation, APOE4 microglia should show lower etomoxir-sensitive fatty-acid-driven oxygen consumption and lower 13C-palmitate incorporation into TCA intermediates than APOE3, with a higher fraction of 13C-palmitate and 13C-acetate carbon appearing in TG/CE. Equal or higher fatty-acid oxidation flux in APOE4, with no increase in esterification flux, would weaken the mechanism.", "Blocking acquisition (SCARB1 or CD36 knockdown, or removing lipoprotein/apoptotic-cell substrate from the medium) should lower APOE4 ester accumulation and dampen the hydrolase transcript program; if ester accumulation persists unchanged without exogenous lipid, the dominant source is de novo lipogenesis rather than ingested lipid and step 1 must be demoted.", "SCD inhibition should shift APOE4 cells from droplet storage toward saturated-acyl-CoA stress (higher ER-stress and lipotoxicity markers, reduced droplet area); unchanged droplet area under SCD inhibition would argue that the SREBF1/SCD arm is a bystander correlate.", "Because mitochondrially encoded transcripts are lower while nuclear OXPHOS transcripts are higher, APOE4 microglia should show a measurable mismatch (lower mtDNA-encoded protein such as MT-CO1 per unit of nuclear-encoded complex subunit, or lower mtDNA copy number per cell). Finding intact mtDNA-encoded protein and normal maximal respiration would remove the proposed capacity limit and favour a purely biosynthetic (SREBP-driven) explanation.", "Restoring lysosomal function alone (TFEB overexpression or acidification rescue) is predicted to reduce lysosomal substrate markers but not to normalise stored esters unless oxidative disposal is also restored; full normalisation of ester content by TFEB alone would relocate the bottleneck to lysosomal catabolism and falsify the stated primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid acquisition and scavenging receptors and secreted lipid-handling factors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:PLA2G7, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:SLCO2B1). We infer, but did not measure, an increased rate of lipid/lipoprotein delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred activity): A coordinated lysosomal-hydrolase and lysosome-biogenesis transcript program is elevated (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:RRAGD). We read this as a compensatory response to substrate load; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and mature-enzyme levels are inferred, not measured, and the protein-spot data are mixed (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down for cathepsin-containing spots; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 contain a v-ATPase subunit candidate and are down), which is compatible with redistribution/processing changes rather than a uniform increase in mature hydrolase protein.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred capacity; the proposed bottleneck): The oxidative disposal arm is not scaled up with the load. Long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts are lower (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5) and mitochondrial-genome-encoded OXPHOS transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2) even though nuclear-encoded TCA/OXPHOS transcripts are higher (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:MPC2, gene:ATP5F1B). We infer a mismatch between nuclear-driven mitochondrial biogenesis signalling and actual electron-transport capacity, i.e. limited beta-oxidation throughput; no oxygen-consumption or flux measurement is supplied.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Carbon that cannot be oxidised is instead activated and desaturated through a cytosolic lipogenic arm whose transcripts are elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ME1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24), supplying monounsaturated acyl-CoA and sterol intermediates.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Esterification enzymes that terminate this route are elevated (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CERS4), predicting increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester synthesis and their sequestration in cytosolic droplets. This lipid pool is unmeasured in the supplied data.", "Step 6 (state consequence, inferred): Persistent ester storage plus lysosomal substrate load sustains a lipid-associated/disease-associated microglial transcriptional state (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:LGALS1, gene:FTH1, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:CTSD) rather than a homeostatic surveillance state, and this state, not an acute inflammatory program, is what most robustly separates APOE4 from APOE3 under mock treatment (gene:NLRP3 and gene:CCL2 rise no more than the list-wide background, and gene:CCL4 falls)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route ingested lipid into an SREBF1/SCD-supported esterification-and-storage arm because post-lysosomal fatty-acid disposal, not acquisition or hydrolase transcription, is the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11137060148432595, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22718199552843354, "cosine_similarity": 0.37062321186447583, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5968932038834951, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11137060148432595, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22718199552843354, "cosine_similarity": 0.37062321186447583, "direction_accuracy": 0.1796116504854369, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5968932038834951, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.26509875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 181}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_019", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, 77% positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base), so pathway claims are only meaningful relative to this global upward shift; we assume the shift is a shared technical/normalisation or composition offset rather than a true genome-wide induction.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for lysosomal compartment size and hydrolase supply; enzyme maturation, acidification, localisation and catalytic flux were not measured.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel features with 2-6 candidate genes each, so no spot is assumed to identify a unique protein; spot-level statements are treated as ambiguous corroboration only.", "Pseudobulk-like genotype contrasts from 10X Flex data are assumed to reflect per-cell regulation, but could equally reflect a shifted mixture of microglial substates or differing astrocyte co-culture contribution; replicate number is not supplied.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed isogenic and equivalently differentiated at day 30 as stated in the metadata, so genotype rather than differentiation stage drives the contrast.", "Lipid content, lysosomal pH, protease activity and respiration are inferred, not observed; the experiment identifier mentions lipid, but no lipid measurement is present in the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coherent transcriptional expansion of the acidic endolysosomal compartment (TFEB/MITF, v-ATPase subunits, glycosidases and cathepsins, RAB7A, LAMP1, IGF2R) together with elevated scavenger/lipoprotein uptake transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, MERTK, APOE) and sterol esterification/synthesis transcripts (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1/2, DHCR24, LSS, ACAT2), whereas the actin-myosin motility/phagocytic-cup and Rho-GTPase modules are NOT coordinately induced relative to the strong global upward shift in this differential-expression list and contain large decreases (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGAP30). We therefore propose that the primary APOE4-versus-APOE3 bottleneck is degradative throughput per unit internalized cargo downstream of uptake: lysosome number/acidification machinery is scaled up transcriptionally, but mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery (M6PR, AP1M1 decreased) and the dominant microglial cysteine protease CTSS are decreased, so cargo-clearance capacity per lysosome is predicted to fall and sterol is predicted to be routed to esterification/storage rather than cleared. All statements about flux, activity, localization, lipid content and causal direction are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake-versus-degradation test: pulse APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with pHrodo- and DQ-labelled myelin or oxLDL. Prediction: early (15-30 min) internalised amount is equal or lower in APOE4, while the degradation index (DQ dequenching per internalised particle after 2-6 h) is lower in APOE4 despite greater LAMP1/LysoTracker area. If APOE4 instead shows higher cytochalasin-D-sensitive early uptake with proportional degradation, the post-uptake bottleneck is wrong and the actin/phagocytic-cup mechanism should be preferred.", "Hydrolase-supply test: measure mature cathepsin activity (e.g. Z-FR-AMC and cathepsin B/D activity probes) and mature-form immunoblots normalised per LAMP1 area. Prediction: APOE4 shows lower protease activity per unit lysosomal area with unchanged or increased pro-forms, consistent with reduced M6PR/AP1M1-dependent delivery and CTSS loss. Equal or higher activity per lysosome in APOE4 would weaken step 3.", "TFEB-dependence test: TFEB knockdown should reduce v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts and worsen undigested-cargo accumulation preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-differential effect would weaken step 2.", "Lipid-routing test: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl ester and lipid-droplet content and shrink the expanded lysosomal compartment selectively in APOE4; unchanged lipid droplets or lysosomal area would weaken step 4.", "Bioenergetic-coupling test: APOE4 should show higher basal/maximal oxygen consumption, and oligomycin or v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) should collapse lysosomal acidification and cargo degradation more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal respiration and equal bafilomycin sensitivity would weaken step 5 without necessarily refuting steps 1-3.", "Global-shift control: after re-normalising the same contrast against a housekeeping-independent spike-in or after quantile matching, the lysosomal, sterol and OXPHOS modules should remain above the recalculated background while the actin/Rho modules should not. If the lysosomal module loses its excess over background, the entire hypothesis is unsupported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for scavenger and lipoprotein receptors and opsonin/efferocytosis receptors (gene:SCARB1 the most extreme, plus gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:APOE), which we infer raises receptor-mediated internalization capacity for lipid-rich cargo. Uptake rate itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred compartment size): A TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-biogenesis module is up as a block above the global positive shift (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:IGF2R; 27 of 28 members positive, set median ~2.1 vs global median ~1.46, Mann-Whitney p=5e-3). We infer an expanded/late-endosomal-biased acidic compartment, not a higher per-lysosome degradation rate.", "Step 3 (bottleneck; measured RNA plus inference): Despite hydrolase transcript induction, the hydrolase-sorting receptor gene:M6PR and adaptor gene:AP1M1 are decreased and the dominant microglial cysteine protease gene:CTSS is the strongest lysosomal decrease in the dataset, so we predict mature, correctly delivered protease activity per lysosome does not scale with compartment expansion; degradative throughput per unit internalized cargo becomes rate-limiting.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred lipid fate): Sterol/lipid liberated from limited cargo hydrolysis is predicted to be routed into esterification and de novo lipogenesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS) rather than efflux, producing cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet accumulation. No lipid pool was measured in the supplied data and ABCA1 is absent from the list, so this step is unverified.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred bioenergetics): Nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA transcripts form the single most coherent up-shifted module (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME; NDUF set n=21, p=1e-3; TCA set p=1e-3), consistent with increased ATP demand for sustained v-ATPase-dependent acidification and lipid re-esterification. Respiration was not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred phenotype; rejects the assigned cytoskeletal framing): The motility/surveillance program is down-shifted rather than up (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:CSF1, gene:PTPRC), and curated actin/Arp2/3/myosin and Rho-GTPase sets sit at or below the global background (mean rank 0.45 and 0.42, p\u003e0.2), so an actin-driven increase in phagocytic-cup formation is not supported; we predict a less motile, degradation-committed, lipid-loaded state (gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB up)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a TFEB-linked lysosomal compartment while hydrolase delivery and cathepsin repertoire lag, making post-endocytic degradative throughput - not actin-driven uptake - the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1717814572879803, "cosine_similarity": 0.3705615227169413, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6129935275080906, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1717814572879803, "cosine_similarity": 0.3705615227169413, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6129935275080906, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.751085, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 182}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_078", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression export (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive overall; the sub-table occupying source_row 2-509 is only 46% positive), so directional coherence of a program must be judged against a strongly up-biased background, not 50/50; genes absent from the list (e.g. ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1-3, NPC1, PSAP, LIPA, ABCA1, SQSTM1, ACLY) are unknown, not unchanged. The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein/enzyme pool; it is explicitly not assumed to establish hydrolase activity, lipid flux, cargo clearance rate, or compartment localisation.", "Protein measurements are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (frequent keratin/actin co-assignment); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot-level changes are read only as compatibility or contradiction.", "SREBP-target transcript elevation is assumed to report reduced ER-accessible sterol sensing; increased anabolic demand for membrane biogenesis is an alternative reading that this dataset cannot exclude.", "The measurement is a bulk-of-population comparison in microglia-astrocyte co-culture; differences could partly reflect a shifted proportion of lipid-processing microglial states, ambient/astrocyte contamination, or maturation differences rather than a uniform per-cell change; replicate structure was not supplied.", "'Reduced clearance reserve' is prospective: nothing in the mock condition measures cargo clearance, so no ongoing degradative failure is claimed as observed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by loss of lysosomal hydrolase gene expression but by an altered lipid-routing cell state: transcripts for lipid/debris uptake receptors, TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, late-endosomal sorting machinery, and neutral-lipid esterification are coordinately higher, yet the entire SREBP sterol/fatty-acid synthesis module is also higher, which is the signature expected when internalized lipid accumulates in endolysosomal and ester/storage compartments rather than replenishing the ER-accessible sterol pool. Within this expanded compartment the induced hydrolases are skewed toward sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid breakdown and ceramide-generating steps (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA, CERS4/6), while ceramide-consuming steps were not measured, predicting a shifted lysosomal sphingolipid balance and reduced clearance reserve that would be exposed by a lipid challenge. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity, lipid pools and localization were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective pulse-chase lipid challenge (not performed here): loading APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia with fluorescent myelin debris, oxLDL or BODIPY-lipoprotein should show equal or greater initial internalisation in APOE4 but greater persistence of cargo and of filipin-positive/BODIPY-positive material in LAMP1+ compartments during chase. If APOE4 clears cargo at least as fast as APOE3 with no lysosomal lipid retention, the routing-limitation mechanism is weakened and successful adaptation with increased throughput becomes the better explanation.", "Sterol-pool test: acute cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol loading should suppress SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD) in both genotypes; if APOE4 remains refractory, ER sterol delivery is limited. Conversely, if SOAT1 inhibition alone normalises the APOE4 SREBP module, the operative routing step is esterification/storage diversion rather than lysosomal retention - a refinement, not a refutation, of the routing claim.", "Lipidomics prediction: APOE4 microglia in the same mock condition should show higher ceramide and/or hexosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin than APOE3, consistent with elevated gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:CERS4/CERS6. Finding no sphingolipid class difference would remove the sphingolipid arm (Step 5) while leaving Steps 1-3 intact.", "Activity versus transcript test: DQ-BSA proteolysis, cathepsin B/L activity probes, LysoTracker/lysosomal pH and direct GBA/acid-sphingomyelinase activity assays should be equal or higher in APOE4 if hydrolase capacity is genuinely expanded. If instead lysosomal proteolytic and sphingolipid hydrolase activity are lower in APOE4 - as protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 (candidates including CTSD, CTSB, HEXB) and protein_spot:064/protein_spot:065 (candidates including ATP6V1E1) might hint - the mechanism must be replaced by a degradative-capacity-loss model.", "Dependency test: TFEB knockdown should reduce the lysosomal/hydrolase transcript module (ATP6V1H, GAA, CTSB, HEXA, GBA, SMPD1) in APOE4; if the module is TFEB-independent, the proposed TFEB-associated compartment expansion in Step 2 is wrong even if the lipid-routing claim survives."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred routing): APOE4 microglia show coordinate increases in lipoprotein/debris uptake and opsonin-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:STAB1, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6, gene:PROS1, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, gene:FCGR1A/FCGR3A, gene:APOE +1.24; 20/20 represented members positive), which is inferred to increase delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): The degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded rather than deficient - gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1), hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH), and late-endosome/sorting machinery (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:ARL8B, gene:HOOK3 +4.29, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B). Increased hydrolase transcripts do not establish increased hydrolase activity.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts, inferred sterol sensing): Despite increased uptake and hydrolase transcripts, the ER regulatory sterol pool behaves as if depleted - every represented SREBP-module member is up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP, gene:SCD +4.17), together with esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72). This combination favours diversion of lipid into lysosomal and ester pools over efficient return of sterol to the ER; the free/esterified cholesterol split was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, associated metabolic state): The simultaneous catabolic and lipogenic load coincides with an oxidative rather than glycolytic configuration - nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA and carrier transcripts up (44/44 represented positive; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, supplying citrate-derived acetyl-CoA for the Step 3 lipogenic program) while glycolytic entry enzymes fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12). This step is correlative; no flux was measured.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence, partly prospective): Inside the expanded compartment the induced sphingolipid arm is weighted toward sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis and ceramide generation (gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17, gene:GLTP +2.38, gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR, gene:CERK), whereas ceramide-consuming/exporting steps (ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1-3, NPC1, PSAP) are absent from the supplied list and therefore unknown. The predicted result is a ceramide/hexosylceramide-shifted lysosomal lipid pool and reduced spare clearance capacity - an ongoing state difference in mock, but a clearance deficit that is expected to become visible mainly under a lipid/myelin challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-expanded lipid-routing state in which internalized lipid is diverted into lysosomal and ester/storage pools instead of the ER regulatory sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23097515046339032, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19085199369689496, "cosine_similarity": 0.3705415203378033, "direction_accuracy": 0.2459546925566343, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mean_absolute_error": 0.613527508090615, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23097515046339032, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19085199369689496, "cosine_similarity": 0.3705415203378033, "direction_accuracy": 0.2459546925566343, "mean_absolute_error": 0.613527508090615, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.69823675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 37}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 genes, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; only sign and rank of effects are used, and absent genes (e.g. PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, PDHA1, MPC1, PDK1-4, CS, MDH2, GOT2, CPT1A) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript differences are assumed to track enzyme/transporter protein abundance in the same direction; no enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, metabolite level or flux was measured, so PDH activity, MPC flux, lactate efflux and respiration remain inferred.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5) with no uniquely identified spot, so they can only test compatibility; all candidate identities are retained.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification in a probe-based 10X Flex assay is assumed to reflect mitochondrial RNA rather than a probe-panel artifact; a compositional/normalization shift (lower mitochondrial read fraction in APOE4) could inflate all nuclear transcripts and is not excluded by these data.", "Nuclear ETC subunit transcript increase is treated as increased biogenesis/capacity signalling, not as increased assembled respirasome content or ATP output.", "Reduced glycolytic reserve is an expectation for a future stimulus challenge, not an observed deficit in the supplied mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated transcriptional re-routing of carbon: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry, PDH activation, malate-aspartate/organic-acid carriers, TCA enzymes, amino-acid anaplerosis and nuclear-encoded electron-transport subunits are uniformly higher, while the committed high-flux glycolytic isoforms (HK2, PFKP, HK3) and pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD, TALDO1) are lower even though glucose transporters and glycogen-synthesis transcripts are higher. We propose this constitutes an altered-routing cell state that raises inferred mitochondrial oxidative capacity and lowers inferred glycolytic/PPP capacity; increased respiratory flux is NOT demonstrated, because the mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) move in the opposite direction, so assembled-complex stoichiometry may lag the nuclear program. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective extracellular flux (Seahorse) on isogenic mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio; if OCR/ECAR is unchanged or lower in APOE4, the routing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective MPC inhibition (UK5099) or PDH-flux blockade: APOE4 basal OCR and ATP-linked respiration should fall proportionally more than APOE3, revealing greater dependence on mitochondrial pyruvate import; equal sensitivity in the two genotypes would weaken Steps 1-2.", "Prospective 13C6-glucose tracing: APOE4 should show higher m+2 labelling of citrate/glutamate relative to m+3 lactate than APOE3; if lactate labelling fraction is equal or higher and citrate m+2 is not increased, the mechanism is falsified.", "Prospective BN-PAGE/immunoblot of assembled complexes plus MT-CO2 and MT-ATP6 protein: if nuclear-encoded subunit proteins rise without proportional assembled complex I/IV/V, the nuclear program is capacity without matched assembly (Step 5 alternative); if assembled complexes and mtDNA-encoded proteins rise in parallel with the nuclear transcripts, Step 5's stoichiometric-mismatch caveat is rejected while routing survives.", "Prospective LPS or phagocytic challenge: APOE4 should show a blunted rapid ECAR rise (lower glycolytic reserve) relative to APOE3 despite comparable or higher OCR; an equal or larger glycolytic burst in APOE4 would falsify Step 7 and undercut the claim that committed glycolytic capacity is reduced.", "Prospective 2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown: APOE3 microglia should lose ATP/viability faster than APOE4 if APOE4 is less glycolysis-dependent; equal or greater APOE4 vulnerability would contradict the reduced-glycolytic-capacity arm."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured): In APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (mock), transcripts controlling pyruvate entry and cytosolic-NADH transfer into mitochondria are all higher - MPC2 (gene:MPC2, +7.98), PDH phosphatase PDP1 (gene:PDP1, +3.00), the E3 dihydrolipoamide dehydrogenase DLD (gene:DLD, +5.54), and the malate-aspartate/organic-acid carrier module MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), SLC25A11 (+4.50), SLC25A13 (+1.75), SLC25A1 (+4.47) with adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5 (+5.56).", "Step 2 (inferred routing): Higher MPC2 and higher PDP1 (predicted more dephosphorylated, active PDH) plus a fully positive shuttle module are expected to route pyruvate and cytosolic reducing equivalents into the matrix rather than to cytosolic lactate; PDH phosphorylation state, lactate efflux and pyruvate flux were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured, opposing arm): The committed/high-flux glycolytic and pentose-phosphate isoforms are lower against a selected list that is 77% positive - HK2 (-3.67), PFKP (-3.08), HK3 (-1.12), PGD (-1.30), TALDO1 (-2.32) - while glucose uptake (SLC2A1 +2.37, SLC2A3 +3.73), a low-Km hexose step (GPI +2.06), PFKM (+2.41), ENO1 (+2.17), SLC16A1 (+1.12) and glycogen synthesis (GYS1 +6.10, UGP2 +1.86) are higher, i.e. glucose entry is retained but committed glycolytic/PPP capacity and carbon storage are re-partitioned.", "Step 4 (measured, downstream capacity): Oxidative machinery transcripts are coherently higher - TCA/anaplerosis (OGDH +8.56, ACO2 +3.54, IDH3G +3.94, IDH3B +2.02, SDHB +1.65, ME1 +1.36, PCK2 +1.21, GLUD1 +3.17, GLS +1.35, ABAT +1.54) and 37/37 represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (e.g. NDUFA5 +7.34, NDUFS7 +5.68, ATP5ME +5.20, UQCRC2 +4.02, COX7A2 +3.36, ATP5F1B +2.65), with mitochondrial import/translation support (TOMM22 +4.63, TIMM44 +2.46, HSPA9 +2.35, TUFM +6.46, CYCS +2.58).", "Step 5 (measured constraint on the claim): mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are discordant with the nuclear program (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; MT-ND5 +1.93, MT-ND4L +1.95), so the nuclear increase is a capacity/biogenesis signal that may not be matched by assembled complexes I, III, IV and V; assembled-complex amount, mtDNA copy number and respiration are unmeasured.", "Step 6 (state-level consequence, partly prospective): The same cells raise lysosomal/lipid-handling transcripts (ATP6V0C/0D1/0D2/1A/1C1/1E1/1F/1H all positive, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, CTSK +7.36, TFEB +2.38, SCARB1 +8.22, SREBF1 +4.67, ACAT2 +2.04, SOAT1 +1.25, LDLR +1.50, APOE +1.24), a state compatible with lipid/organic-acid substrate supply feeding the oxidative arm; no inflammatory or interferon activation accompanies it (only 1/26 queried IFN genes represented; NFKB/cytokine members 4/7 positive, indistinguishable from list background), so this is a metabolic cell-state difference rather than an inflammation-driven switch.", "Step 7 (revealed only by challenge, not claimed for mock): Because committed glycolytic isoform transcripts are lower, APOE4 microglia are predicted to have reduced glycolytic reserve for a rapid stimulus-driven burst; a functional deficit in the measured mock condition is not asserted."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt an oxidation-biased carbon-routing state: pyruvate/NADH import and TCA-ETC capacity transcripts rise while committed glycolytic and PPP isoform transcripts fall"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2457781942722652, "cosine_similarity": 0.3702896854718721, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961100323624595, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2457781942722652, "cosine_similarity": 0.3702896854718721, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5961100323624595, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97905175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 38}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_029", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, logarithm base unspecified); genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged, so all program statements are conditional on this selected background (77.1% of listed genes positive) and are descriptive coherence, not formal enrichment with independent genes.", "Coordinate transcript increases across OXPHOS, v-ATPase and hydrolase gene families are read as increased biosynthetic capacity for those complexes; respiratory flux, lysosomal pH, protease activity, lipid content and phagocytic rate were not measured and are inferred only.", "The 2D protein spots are ambiguous: every spot carries 2-6 candidate identities (KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate the candidate lists and are contamination-prone), so no spot is treated as confirmation of an individual protein; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "Step 1 (endolysosomal retention of sterol keeping the ER-sensed pool low) is an inference from the direction of SREBP-target transcripts co-occurring with up uptake receptors; no sterol pool, SREBP cleavage or TFEB localisation was measured.", "The reduced leukocyte actomyosin module is a transcript-level reallocation in the measured mock condition; a functional engulfment or migration deficit is a prediction under future challenge and is not established here (reduced reserve under challenge would not by itself prove an ongoing defect in mock).", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent difference in cell composition or library normalisation could contribute to the global 77% positive bias; program calls were therefore made against that within-list background rather than against a 50/50 expectation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, D30) differ from APOE3 by a coordinated cell-state change rather than by a single defective gene: sterol/lipid-responsive (SREBP-target) and TFEB/CLEAR-type endolysosomal genes plus essentially the entire nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA machinery are coherently higher (OXPHOS 39/39 represented genes positive, median +2.65 vs a selected-list background that is only 77% positive; P(pos\u003e=39)=3.9e-5 against that background), while the leukocyte-restricted actomyosin/immune-signalling motility module (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, FAM49B/CYRIB, ARHGAP30, ARHGDIB, PTPRC, SPN, PTPN6, PLEK) is coherently and strongly lower (15/28 negative, median -1.20, P(neg\u003e=15)=4.2e-4), with Rho-inactivating regulators (ARHGDIA +10.6, ARHGAP1 +4.7, ARHGAP35 +4.8) up. Cargo-recognition receptors are modestly up (SCARB1 +8.2, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, MERTK, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, all near the +1.1-1.5 list floor) while microglial identity TFs are preserved or up (SPI1-axis IRF8, MAFB, MEF2C, CSF1R, GPR34), so this is a selective module reallocation, not dedifferentiation. We propose that APOE4-associated retention of lipid/sterol in the endolysosomal compartment (inferred, not measured) keeps the ER-sensed sterol pool low, sustaining SREBP-target and TFEB-type transcription and an oxidative catabolic program, and that this state is accompanied by reduced transcriptional support for Rac/Rho-driven actomyosin work. Direction of causality is not established; increased transcripts are capacity, not measured flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective Seahorse on mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a lower ECAR/OCR ratio, matching the 39/39 OXPHOS and HK2/PFKP-down transcript pattern. Equal or lower OCR in APOE4 would show the OXPHOS transcript increase is not increased oxidative capacity and would weaken Step 4.", "Prospective lipid-load and lysosomal-function assay: mock APOE4 microglia should show greater neutral-lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX) and cholesterol (filipin) content in LAMP1-positive compartments together with equal or faster DQ-BSA dequenching. If APOE4 shows no lipid excess and identical lysosomal load, the driver in Steps 1-3 fails and the state must be explained by an APOE4 effect upstream of lipid handling.", "Prospective SREBP-pathway test: treating APOE4 microglia with an SREBP-processing inhibitor (fatostatin or PF-429242) should normalise the lipogenic/esterification transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, LDLR, DHCR24) without abolishing the OXPHOS block if the two arms are separately driven; if instead adding exogenous cholesterol/cyclodextrin-cholesterol to APOE4 cells collapses both the SREBP-target and the TFEB/v-ATPase-hydrolase induction, Steps 2-3 share the proposed sterol-sensing driver, whereas persistence of both after cholesterol repletion would weaken them.", "Prospective challenge test of the routing claim: on pHrodo-labelled myelin/synaptosome or 3 um bead challenge, APOE4 should internalise fewer large particles per cell at early times (Rac/actomyosin-dependent step) yet degrade internalised cargo at an equal or higher rate, and should show reduced Rac1-GTP and lower F-actin/phalloidin and spreading area. Equal internalisation with equal Rac1-GTP and F-actin would falsify Step 5-6; equal internalisation but reduced degradation would invert the mechanism to a clearance bottleneck.", "Prospective TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should selectively remove the v-ATPase/hydrolase induction (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, GAA, GBA, CTSB, HEXA); persistence of the full lysosomal induction after TFEB knockdown would falsify Step 3 as written.", "Direct protein-level contradiction test: unambiguous quantification (immunoblot or targeted MS) of ACTB, MYH9 and ATP6V1E1. The spot data are discordant with Step 5 for actin (many ACTB-candidate spots up, e.g. protein_spot:043/044/052) and with Step 3 for v-ATPase (ATP6V1E1-candidate protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93). If unambiguous assays show ACTB/MYH9 protein unchanged or higher and ATP6V1E1 protein lower in APOE4, the transcript-based reading of Steps 3 and 5 is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (state input, inferred): APOE4 protein handles lipid/lipoprotein cargo differently from APOE3 in the mock co-culture, so internalised sterol and lipid accumulate in the endolysosomal compartment instead of equilibrating with the ER regulatory sterol pool. Consistent transcript evidence: APOE itself (gene:APOE +1.2), lipid/lipoprotein receptor transcripts up (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:MRC1 +1.4, gene:COLEC12 +1.5, gene:MERTK +1.3, gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:STAB1 +1.1). The lipid pool itself was NOT measured.", "Step 2: A low ER-sensed sterol signal sustains SREBP-target transcription: gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SREBF2 +1.1, gene:INSIG1 +1.9, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:HMGCS1 +1.1, gene:LSS +2.3, gene:DHCR7 +2.7, gene:DHCR24 +3.7, plus esterification/storage genes gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SCD +4.2 (18 of 19 represented lipid genes positive; only gene:ACSL4 -2.1). Co-induction of uptake, synthesis and esterification indicates the cell behaves as if it must keep routing lipid into stored/esterified form.", "Step 3: The same load engages a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR response that expands acidified degradative capacity: gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF +1.0, all represented v-ATPase subunits positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, ATP6V1A +4.2, ATP6V0C +3.5, ATP6AP1 +2.3, ATP6V1E1 +1.7, ATP6V1F +1.7, ATP6V0D1 +1.7, ATP6V1C1 +1.3, ATP6AP2 +1.2, ATP6V0D2 +1.1), hydrolases up (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:NAGLU +5.9, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:HEXB +2.2), plus delivery/maturation genes gene:GNPTG +3.0, gene:IGF2R +2.0, gene:LAMP1 +1.4, gene:SCARB2 +1.1, gene:NPC2 +1.2, gene:RAB7A +2.7. Exceptions: gene:CTSS -5.6, gene:IDS -1.6, gene:M6PR -1.7.", "Step 4: Catabolic output is routed to mitochondria rather than to glycolysis: every represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit is positive (39/39; gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7 +5.7, gene:ATP5ME +5.2, gene:UQCRC2 +4.0, gene:COX7A2 +3.4, gene:SDHB +1.7 ...), as are TCA/substrate-entry genes (gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:GOT1 +6.4, gene:BCAT2 +6.4, gene:DLD +5.5, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5, gene:ACO2 +3.5, gene:HADHA +2.9, gene:GLUD1 +3.2, 14/14 positive), while inducible glycolytic and PPP genes fall (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:HK3 -1.1, gene:TALDO1 -2.3, gene:PGD -1.3; glycolysis/PPP 5 up / 5 down, far below the 77% positive background).", "Step 5: In the same cells, transcriptional investment in Rac/Rho-driven actomyosin work is withdrawn: gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:FAM49B(CYRIB) -5.8, gene:RAC2 -2.0, gene:DOCK8 -2.0, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.2, gene:ARHGDIB -2.0, gene:PLEK -2.5, gene:PTPN6 -3.0, gene:PTPRC -1.5, gene:SPN -7.3, while Rho-inactivating regulators rise (gene:ARHGDIA +10.6, gene:ARHGAP35 +4.8, gene:ARHGAP1 +4.7, gene:ARHGAP21 +1.1, gene:ARHGAP26 +1.4). Generic actin-nucleation genes are not uniformly down (gene:ARPC1B +2.2, gene:ARPC5 +1.9, gene:ARPC4 +1.9, gene:CFL1 +1.8, gene:ACTG1 +1.2), so the change is specific to the leukocyte-restricted motility/immune-synapse subset, not to actin machinery as a whole.", "Step 6 (predicted functional consequence, prospective, not observed here): the APOE4 state should favour receptor-mediated internalisation and endolysosomal/oxidative processing of lipid cargo while lowering the reserve for Rac/actomyosin-dependent large-particle engulfment, spreading and migration. Whether this is successful adaptation (higher clearance throughput) or an ongoing handling failure is NOT determined by these measurements."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-directed endolysosomal-oxidative state that reallocates transcriptional investment away from the leukocyte actomyosin motility/engulfment module"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27162967212080413, "cosine_similarity": 0.36967884007193885, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mean_absolute_error": 0.603789644012945, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27162967212080413, "cosine_similarity": 0.36967884007193885, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.603789644012945, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.71663825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 39}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_042", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, |effect| \u003e= 1, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directionality is judged against that 77.1% positive selected-list background, and absent genes (ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, FASN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript changes are taken as indicators of transcriptional program engagement, not of enzyme activity, sterol flux, sterol localisation, or protein amount; SREBP-2 cleavage, LXR occupancy, hydrolase activity, esterification rate and efflux rate are all unmeasured here.", "The joint elevation of SREBP-2-type and oxysterol/LXR-type targets is interpreted as compartment-specific sterol sensing (ER pool low, oxysterol/whole-cell pool high); an alternative that both signatures arise from a shared upstream activator without any sterol mislocalisation is not excluded by these data.", "2D-gel protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each with heavy keratin/actin contamination; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot changes are used only for compatibility/contradiction testing.", "Effects are cell-population averages from a mixed microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30; genotype-driven differences in cell size, RNA content or composition could inflate the global positive skew.", "Any impairment implied by the mechanism is a reduced reserve that would be revealed by a future lipid challenge; the mock condition alone does not establish an ongoing clearance or efflux defect, and causality is not established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes occupy a high-throughput lipid-handling state in which transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2), sterol esterification and droplet handling (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CIDEB, gene:ABHD5, gene:MGLL) and a broad TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal hydrolase program (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, v-ATPase subunits) are coordinately higher, yet SREBP-2-type biosynthetic transcripts remain up (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2) alongside oxysterol-generating and LXR-target transcripts (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:ABCA7, gene:MYLIP, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). We hypothesise that cholesterol delivered to APOE4 microglia is preferentially routed into lysosomal and cholesteryl-ester/droplet pools rather than into the ER-accessible regulatory pool, so two normally opposed sterol-sensing outputs are simultaneously engaged; this is an adaptive routing/cell-state change in the measured condition, not a demonstrated rate-limiting defect, and its cost is predicted to appear only under a lipid challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipid phenotyping of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 cultures: APOE4 should show higher cholesteryl-ester (and/or lysosomal unesterified sterol by filipin/ALOD4-inaccessible signal) with an ER-accessible cholesterol pool that is not increased, plus increased nuclear SREBP-2. Finding lower esterified sterol, or reduced nuclear SREBP-2, in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should redirect sterol to the ER and suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR) markedly more in APOE4 than APOE3, with comparatively little effect on TFEB targets (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB). If SREBP-2 targets are unchanged by SOAT1 inhibition, or if lysosomal and SREBP-2 targets move together in lockstep, the routing/sensing-mismatch mechanism is weakened in favour of a generic TFEB-driven activation state.", "Prospective challenge test (reserve, not baseline): after myelin, apoptotic-neuron or oxLDL loading, APOE4 should accumulate more droplets/cholesteryl ester and show blunted further induction of the lysosomal program relative to APOE3; equal loading kinetics and equal induction would contradict the predicted reduced reserve.", "Knockdown of SCARB1 or CD36 in APOE4 microglia should reduce ester/droplet accumulation and lower LXR-target transcripts (gene:ABCA7, gene:MYLIP, gene:PLTP) without normalising SREBP-2 targets to APOE3 levels; if uptake knockdown normalises all four arms equally, a simple uptake-driven overload model is preferred over compartmental mislocalisation.", "Direct efflux measurement (ApoA-I/HDL acceptor, ABCA1/ABCG1 protein and cholesterol-efflux rate, none measured here): despite elevated LXR-target transcripts, APOE4 efflux capacity should not exceed APOE3 in proportion; a clearly higher efflux rate in APOE4 would support successful adaptation rather than storage-biased routing."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype increases transcript levels of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, plus gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:PROS1, gene:C1QA/B/C), which we infer increases routing of extracellular lipid and debris into the endolysosomal system (flux not measured).", "Incoming sterol is directed into storage and degradative compartments rather than to the ER: esterification/droplet transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:CIDEB, gene:ABHD5, gene:MGLL) and a broad lysosomal/CLEAR program rises with gene:TFEB +2.38 and gene:MITF +1.03 (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2).", "Sterol that reaches oxysterol-forming enzymes engages the oxysterol/LXR arm: gene:CH25H +1.62 and gene:CYP27A1 +1.49 are up together with canonical LXR-responsive transcripts gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67 and gene:SCD +4.17, indicating the cell reads a whole-cell/oxysterol sterol surplus (receptor activity itself not measured).", "Despite that surplus signal, the ER-accessible sterol pool is inferred to remain low, because SREBP-2-type target transcripts stay elevated (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF2 +1.06); altered inter-organelle sterol transfer transcripts are consistent with re-routing (gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:TSPO +1.41, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:OSBPL3 +1.25, gene:OSBPL1A +1.03, gene:OSBPL8 -1.90).", "The two arms therefore do not cancel: continued uptake plus continued synthesis feeds an expanding esterified/lysosomal sterol pool, while gene:MYLIP induction is predicted to cap LDLR protein and gene:SREBF1/gene:SCD shift membrane lipid toward monounsaturated species, stabilising a high-flux, storage-biased steady state rather than net offload (efflux capacity is unmeasured; ABCA1 and ABCG1 rows are absent).", "Downstream, this state links to the represented phagocytic/complement program (gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:ITGAX, gene:STAB1, gene:SIRPA, gene:CD47, gene:C1QA/B/C) and a modest chemokine output (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CXCL2, gene:IL18, gene:NFKBIZ), i.e. an activated lipid-clearing microglial state; the predicted functional cost is reduced spare capacity for an acute lipid load, not an ongoing clearance failure in mock."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lipid into lysosomal/esterified sterol stores while the ER sterol sensor stays de-repressed, producing a dual SREBP-2 + oxysterol/LXR transcriptional state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2871266107890559, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24128228156466835, "cosine_similarity": 0.36952992780415683, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5938317152103559, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2871266107890559, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24128228156466835, "cosine_similarity": 0.36952992780415683, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5938317152103559, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.033708, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 40}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_061", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome: every row has |effect| \u003e= 1.00 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, so absence of a gene (NPC1, ABCA1, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE) means not present in this list, not measured-and-unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are compared only within this dataset and are not converted to fold changes.", "The list carries a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 rows up, median effect +1.46), so a set is only treated as coherent if it exceeds that shifted background on rank and/or is concentrated in the most statistically confident tier. Some of that shift may be normalisation or composition, not biology.", "Effect magnitude and adjusted p-value are essentially uncorrelated in this list (r = 0.06); very large magnitudes (up to 15.5) are assumed to be unstable estimates from sparsely detected genes, so the argument rests on set-level rank plus significance rank, not on individual extreme values.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin, so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no spot is used as primary evidence for any single gene product.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for protein abundance and a weak proxy for activity, flux and localisation; no lipid, cholesterol, cholesteryl-ester, lysosomal-pH, or degradative-flux measurement is supplied, and none is claimed as observed.", "Biological replicate counts are not supplied in the workbook, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be checked for pseudoreplication across cells.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; ambient RNA or composition differences (e.g. gene:S100B) could contribute to apparent genotype effects.", "This is an isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison under mock treatment at a single timepoint; association between genotype and transcript state is observed, causal direction is assumed, not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coherent, high-confidence increase in transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors together with a TFEB/MITF/TFEC-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program, while SREBP-linked sterol-synthesis transcripts and SOAT1 remain elevated rather than suppressed. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not uptake or hydrolase supply but export of internalised sterol from the late-endosome/lysosome lumen into the ER-accessible regulatory pool; cargo retained upstream of that step drives compensatory lysosome biogenesis, SOAT1-mediated esterification, and a lysosomal-stress-associated chemokine tone. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating sterol-delivery test: load APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with LDL (which requires lysosomal egress to reach the ER sensor) versus 25-hydroxycholesterol or an oxysterol that acts directly on INSIG/SCAP at the ER. The mechanism predicts that 25-hydroxycholesterol suppresses HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR and INSIG1 equally in both genotypes, while LDL suppresses them significantly less in APOE4 than in APOE3. If LDL suppresses these transcripts equally in the two genotypes, the lysosome-to-ER egress bottleneck is refuted and an ER-sensing or pure-demand model should be preferred.", "Localisation test: sterol probes (filipin plus an ER-accessible-cholesterol probe such as ALOD4/D4H) with LAMP1 co-staining should show, in APOE4, a higher LAMP1-colocalised unesterified-cholesterol fraction and a lower ER-accessible fraction at equal or higher total cellular cholesterol. Finding equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Relief-of-bottleneck test: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, which bypasses lysosomal cholesterol export, should in APOE4 lower the TFEB-target lysosomal transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXB, ATP6V0C, LAMP1) and the sterol-synthesis transcripts toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h. No normalisation of either module would weaken the mechanism.", "Upstream-flux test: culturing in lipoprotein-deficient serum, or knocking down SCARB1 and CD36, should reduce the lysosomal and LGALS3/GPNMB modules more in APOE4 than in APOE3. Persistence of the full APOE4 lysosomal signature under lipoprotein-free conditions would indicate a cell-autonomous lysosomal defect rather than an uptake-driven overload and would weaken step 1.", "Esterification test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should lower cholesteryl esters and partially normalise the SREBP-linked transcripts in APOE4; if SOAT1 inhibition lowers cholesteryl esters but leaves the sterol-synthesis module unchanged, the esterification-reinforcement step (step 5) is falsified even if the egress bottleneck survives.", "Protein-level test with resolved identity: targeted immunoblot or MS quantification of CTSB, CTSD and mature-versus-pro forms, plus LAMP1 and GPNMB, should show increased mature hydrolase and LAMP1 protein in APOE4. Because the supplied cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and ATP6V1E1-containing spots are down (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), a clean identity-resolved measurement showing no increase in lysosomal protein would weaken step 3.", "Downstream-consequence test: degradative flux assays (DQ-BSA, dextran chase, LysoTracker/pH ratiometry) should show reduced cargo clearance per unit lysosome in APOE4 despite the higher hydrolase transcript program; equal or faster clearance would contradict the bottleneck framing."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance for lipoprotein and scavenger uptake receptors (SCARB1, SCARB2, CD36, CD163, MRC1, COLEC12, STAB1, LDLR, CLEC7A, MPEG1, CD14, MS4A6A, FOLR2, SLCO2B1, C1QA, C1QC, TREM2) and for APOE itself. Inferred, not measured: a correspondingly higher flux of lipoprotein/lipid cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Inferred: internalised APOE4-containing and scavenged lipid cargo is delivered to late endosomes/lysosomes, where sterol must be released from the lumen and handed to ER-facing membrane contact sites. This luminal-to-ER egress step is proposed as the primary bottleneck. It is an inference: NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2 and MCOLN1 are absent from the supplied differential-expression list, so the egress machinery itself was not measured here.", "Measured: a broad lysosomal-biogenesis transcriptional response is elevated above the already positive global background - the TFEB/MITF/TFEC transcription factors, luminal hydrolases (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, CTSH, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, MAN2B1, DPP7), v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C, ATP6V0D1, ATP6V1E1), LAMP1, RAB7A and NPC2. Inferred: this is compensatory expansion of degradative capacity downstream of retained cargo, not evidence of increased degradative flux, which was not measured.", "Measured: sterol-synthesis and SREBP-associated transcripts are up, not down (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, SCD, LDLR), alongside increased SOAT1 and DGAT1. Inferred: if delivered sterol reached the ER sensor normally, increased uptake should lower this program; its co-elevation is consistent with an ER-accessible sterol pool that is not sensed as replete, i.e. sterol held upstream of, or esterified away from, the ER regulatory pool.", "Inferred: SOAT1-dependent esterification and storage further remove free cholesterol from the ER-accessible pool, forming a reinforcing loop that keeps both the synthetic and the lysosomal programs switched on. The cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet pools were not measured in this dataset and are not claimed as observed.", "Measured: markers associated with lysosomal load and membrane stress (LGALS3, GPNMB, ACP5) and an innate-inflammatory chemokine/inflammasome-adaptor module (MYD88, TLR2, NLRP3, PYCARD, IL18, CXCL8, CXCL1, CXCL2, CCL2) are elevated. Inferred: lysosomal stress arising from retained cargo contributes to this tone; activation state, inflammasome assembly and cytokine secretion were not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia upregulate lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and a TFEB-family lysosomal program while sterol-synthesis genes stay high, indicating a bottleneck at lysosome-to-ER cholesterol egress"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2361234580001311, "cosine_similarity": 0.3694329967187965, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956601941747572, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2361234580001311, "cosine_similarity": 0.3694329967187965, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5956601941747572, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6410325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 183}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_069", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive); programs are therefore judged against a 77% positive background, and genes absent from the file (for example ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, PNPLA2) are unknown, not unchanged, so no claim is made about efflux or lipolytic capacity.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; effects are used only as signed, ordered magnitudes on their reported scale, and the very large values (up to +15.5) are treated as scale-uncertain, with sign coherence weighted more than magnitude.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but not to equal, protein and enzymatic activity; no uptake rate, lysosomal hydrolytic or lipolytic flux, esterification rate, oxygen consumption rate, lipid-droplet mass or cholesterol efflux rate was measured in this experiment.", "Protein measurements are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidates across 92 spots; keratins and ACTB recur as candidates), so spots are used only for compatibility or contradiction; no spot is treated as identification of a single protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be the extracellular source of lipoprotein cargo driving step 1 (background expectation, unverified here; no lipid or lipoprotein species were measured in the supplied data).", "The reduced Rac/actomyosin transcripts are assumed to lower motility and large-particle engulfment reserve only when those functions are challenged; reduced reserve is not claimed as an ongoing functional defect in the measured mock condition.", "Causality is not established by these association data; the mechanism is a directed hypothesis, and mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS transcripts run opposite to the nuclear set (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 all negative), so increased respiratory capacity is assumed only as a partial, testable sink."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the APOE4 genotype shifts cells into a coordinated lipid-handling cell state rather than producing a single enzymatic block: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-cargo uptake receptors, MiT/TFE-associated lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, lipid esterification/remodelling enzymes, and nuclear-encoded TCA/OXPHOS genes are coordinately higher than in APOE3, while glycolytic/pentose-phosphate transcripts are lower. I propose that cargo lipid liberated in an expanded lysosomal compartment is routed into esterified/stored and membrane-remodelling pools (and partly into mitochondrial oxidation) rather than into the ER regulatory sterol pool, so SREBP-target uptake/synthesis transcription remains switched on in parallel with degradation; the predicted lipid consequence is a net expansion of cholesteryl-ester, triacylglycerol and sphingolipid-derived species in APOE4 relative to APOE3 under mock conditions. All measurements are RNA and 2D-gel protein-spot abundances; uptake, lysosomal, esterification and respiratory fluxes were not measured and are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol content and a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio, with increased ceramide/hexosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin (consistent with gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA). If APOE4 instead shows equal or lower esterified lipid with higher free cholesterol, the storage-routing core of the mechanism (steps 3-4) is falsified.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (for example avasimibe) plus DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and, because the ER regulatory sterol pool would be restored, lower SREBP-target transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:SCD, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF1) toward APOE3 levels. If esterification blockade reduces stored lipid but leaves the SREBP-target transcripts elevated, step 4 (sequestration-driven unsatisfied sterol sensing) is wrong and an APOE4-intrinsic transcriptional driver should be preferred.", "Prospective TFEB knockdown or MiT/TFE inhibition in APOE4 microglia should lower hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H) and, per step 2-3, reduce the lipid-ester excess; unchanged ester content after effective TFEB knockdown would weaken the CLEAR-driven step.", "Prospective cargo-withdrawal test: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake, should collapse most of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 ester excess. Persistence of the excess would falsify step 1 and favour de novo lipogenesis as the dominant source.", "Prospective respirometry and mitonuclear test: if the nuclear TCA/OXPHOS transcript increase is functional, APOE4 should show higher basal and fatty-acid-dependent oxygen consumption and higher assembled complex I/IV levels. Unchanged or lower respiration despite the transcript increase, consistent with the opposite-direction mtDNA-encoded transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB), would remove the oxidative sink from step 5 and shift the interpretation toward failed rather than successful adaptation.", "Prospective challenge-only prediction: under a phagocytic or migratory challenge (large-particle or myelin engulfment, chemotactic assay), APOE4 microglia should show reduced actin-intensive engulfment and motility while receptor-mediated lipoprotein/DiI-LDL uptake is preserved or increased. Equal or better large-particle engulfment and motility would falsify step 6 without affecting steps 1-5; reduced receptor-mediated lipid uptake would instead contradict step 1."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (delivery, inferred): APOE4 microglia carry coordinately higher transcripts for lipid- and lipoprotein-cargo receptors and opsonin machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:ANXA1 +4.15, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:C1QA +1.25), 25/26 represented members positive versus a 77% positive selected-list background, predicting greater delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome; receptor transcript abundance does not establish uptake rate.", "Step 2 (expanded degradative capacity): a MiT/TFE-associated CLEAR-like program is elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) together with lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits (gene:GAA +9.99, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GBA +6.72, gene:HEXA +5.72, gene:SMPD1 +5.60, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:ATP6V1H +6.87, gene:ATP6V1A +4.20, gene:ATP6V0C +3.53, gene:LAMP1 +1.38), 28/30 positive, so acid hydrolysis of cargo lipid esters, sphingomyelin and glycolipids is expected to increase, liberating sterol, fatty acyl and sphingoid products inside the endolysosome.", "Step 3 (routing to storage/remodelling): liberated lipid is channelled into re-esterification, neutral-lipid and phospholipid synthesis rather than to the ER regulatory sterol pool (gene:AGPAT2 +6.33, gene:SCP2 +5.94, gene:SCD +4.22, gene:LPCAT1 +3.11, gene:CHPT1 +2.87, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.67, gene:GPAT4 +1.62, gene:SOAT1 +1.34, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 supplying citrate/acetyl-CoA), predicting growth of cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol pools and altered phosphatidylcholine/sphingolipid species.", "Step 4 (unsatisfied sterol sensing sustains the cycle): despite the increased delivery and hydrolysis implied by steps 1-2, SREBP-arm and sterol-pathway transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.70, gene:DHCR24 +3.72, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:INSIG1 +1.90, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SREBF2 +1.09, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CYP27A1 +1.50), which is the signature expected when regulatory ER sterol is sequestered in esters/lysosomes rather than raised; uptake plus synthesis therefore continue alongside degradation and the stored pool expands.", "Step 5 (fuel reallocation): fatty acyl and carbon flux is directed toward mitochondrial oxidation instead of glycolysis/PPP (all 21 represented nuclear TCA/OXPHOS members positive: gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.62, gene:MPC2 +8.00, gene:NDUFA5 +7.30, gene:TUFM +6.53, gene:GOT1 +6.44, gene:BCAT2 +6.39, gene:HADHA +2.89, gene:ACOX1 +1.20; opposed by gene:HK2 -3.66, gene:PFKP -3.10, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:HK3 -1.12), giving a partial catabolic sink that limits, but on this evidence does not prevent, ester accumulation.", "Step 6 (reallocation away from actin-intensive surveillance, weakest step): the Rac/actomyosin myeloid motility module is transcriptionally reduced (gene:SPN -7.30, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B -5.80, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:RAC2 -1.97, with gene:ARHGDIA +10.62), predicting reduced actin-intensive motility and large-particle engulfment reserve in APOE4 while receptor-mediated lipid uptake is preserved; this step is contradicted in part by increased Arp2/3 and actin-regulator transcripts (gene:ARPC1B +2.15, gene:ARPC5 +1.94, gene:CFL1 +1.80, gene:TWF2 +2.74) and by predominantly increased ACTB-candidate protein spots, so it is held as a challenge-revealed prediction, not an established defect in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a storage-routed endolysosomal-oxidative lipid-handling state in which internalized lipid is esterified and sequestered instead of satisfying ER sterol sensing"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4961230292065133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24863449700870416, "cosine_similarity": 0.3694292186322133, "direction_accuracy": 0.511326860841424, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6431359223300971, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4961230292065133, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24863449700870416, "cosine_similarity": 0.3694292186322133, "direction_accuracy": 0.511326860841424, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6431359223300971, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4504745, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 41}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_032", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA effects are 'reported log fold change' of unspecified logarithm base; they are used ordinally (rank/percentile within this table) and their magnitudes are not converted to fold changes.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, MSR1, LPL and PLIN2 from the table is uninformative and cannot be read as 'unchanged'.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein amount and an even weaker proxy for enzymatic activity, transport flux and subcellular localization; no cholesterol, cholesteryl ester, oxysterol, filipin or efflux measurement is supplied, so all sterol pools in this hypothesis are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots have several candidate genes each; protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are treated only as weak, non-identifying support because CTSL/CTSD are among many candidates.", "APOE4 protein being a poorer cholesterol acceptor than APOE3 is unverified background knowledge, not something measured here.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply extracellular lipoproteins; astrocyte-side APOE genotype effects are a confound that these microglia-level measurements cannot separate.", "The comparison is assumed to reflect genotype effects on a comparable microglial population rather than a difference in differentiation efficiency or cell-state composition between lines.", "Correlation only: no causal direction is established by this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) run a coordinated lipoprotein-scavenging and lysosomal-hydrolase transcriptional program (SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163, TREM2, CLEC7A, PLA2G7, GPNMB; GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, ATP6V subunits, TFEB) while the sterol-export arm (APOE-lipoprotein acceptor formation) is functionally rate-limiting, so cholesterol liberated in the endolysosome is inferred to be routed into esterified/lysosomal storage (SOAT1, DGAT1 up) and into oxysterol output (CH25H, CYP27A1 up) rather than out of the cell; because the stored sterol does not replenish the ER-accessible pool, SREBP-2-type targets (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, EBP) remain elevated, sustaining a futile uptake-plus-synthesis cycle and lysosomal expansion. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, localization and activity statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating acceptor test: supplying an extracellular sterol acceptor (lipid-free apoA-I, HDL, or 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) to mock APOE4 microglia should increase [3H]/BODIPY-cholesterol efflux and reduce filipin-positive lysosomal free cholesterol, cholesteryl-ester mass, LAMP1 area and the GPNMB/CTSB/GBA/GAA transcript module toward APOE3 values. If acceptor addition demonstrably raises efflux yet leaves the lysosomal/GPNMB module and stored sterol unchanged, the export-bottleneck claim is weakened.", "Storage-versus-export discrimination: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe/ACAT inhibitor) should convert stored cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol and should not normalize - indeed should aggravate - lysosomal expansion and the GPNMB/hydrolase module, whereas an efflux-directed intervention (LXR agonist or ABCA1 overexpression) should normalize both. If SOAT1 inhibition alone normalizes the lysosomal module, esterification rather than export is the bottleneck and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Sensor-pool test: using ALOD4/D4H sterol biosensors plus nuclear SREBP-2 immunoblot, APOE4 cells should show equal or greater total/lysosomal cholesterol but not-reduced mature nuclear SREBP-2 and no increase in ER-accessible cholesterol relative to APOE3. Observing higher ER-accessible cholesterol together with reduced nuclear SREBP-2 in APOE4 falsifies step 5.", "Phenocopy test: blocking lysosomal sterol egress in APOE3 microglia (U18666A) should reproduce the joint signature of lysosomal-hydrolase/TFEB induction plus un-repressed SREBP-2 targets; failure to reproduce this co-activation would weaken the sequestration step.", "Genotype-direction test: isogenic reversion of APOE4 to APOE3, and APOE knockout in the APOE3 line, should respectively reduce and phenocopy (partially) the scavenger/lysosomal module; if APOE knockout in APOE3 moves the module in the opposite direction to APOE4, the acceptor-function mechanism is weakened.", "Composition control: single-cell deconvolution should show the scavenger/lysosomal module shifting within matched microglial clusters; if it is fully explained by a higher proportion of a macrophage-like (MRC1/CD163/F13A1-high) population in APOE4, the mechanism is confounded by differentiation state rather than sterol handling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance of lipoprotein/lipid-scavenging receptors and lipid-handling surface genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:CLEC7A, gene:CD14, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:PLA2G7); we infer, but did not measure, increased lipoprotein/sterol influx flux.", "Step 2 (inferred flux and localization): Internalized lipoprotein cholesteryl ester is delivered to the endolysosome, where a coordinately elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1) together with gene:TFEB indicates lysosomal biogenesis/expansion; gene:GPNMB is consistent with a lipid-laden phagocyte state. Lysosomal cholesterol itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred activity): The export step - formation of lipidated APOE acceptor particles and transfer of sterol to extracellular acceptors - does not scale with influx. gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7 and gene:PLTP transcripts are higher in APOE4, so the deficit is proposed at the level of APOE4 protein acceptor function and/or unmeasured ABCA1/ABCG1 activity, not transcript amount (unverified background knowledge: APOE4 is a poorer lipid acceptor than APOE3).", "Step 4 (inferred routing): Sterol that cannot be exported is diverted into storage and side-outputs: gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 (esterification/neutral-lipid storage) and gene:CH25H and gene:CYP27A1 (oxysterol production), whose products would sustain an LXR-type transcriptional output consistent with elevated gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7 and gene:PLTP.", "Step 5 (inferred sensing state): Because sterol accumulates in lysosomal and esterified pools rather than the ER-accessible pool, ER SCAP/INSIG-dependent repression is not engaged, so SREBP-2-type targets remain elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:MYLIP, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD); this predicts continued uptake and synthesis on top of an already loaded cell.", "Step 6 (consequence): The resulting expanded, lipid-loaded lysosomal compartment is predicted to have reduced degradative throughput per lysosome, providing a mechanism by which APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 at baseline (mock) without any inflammatory-program enrichment in these data."], "title": "Sterol export is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: scavenger-driven lipoprotein influx and lysosomal hydrolysis outrun APOE4-dependent efflux, forcing esterified/lysosomal storage while the ER sterol sensor stays un-repressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23151014885615978, "cosine_similarity": 0.36936391197785956, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945501618122978, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23151014885615978, "cosine_similarity": 0.36936391197785956, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5945501618122978, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8285305, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 184}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_138", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so absolute enrichment cannot be computed; all pathway statements use within-list percentile ranks, which control for the strong global positive skew (median effect +1.46, 77% positive, unspecified logarithm base preserved and never exponentiated).", "The global positive skew is treated as possibly technical (compositional normalisation, ambient RNA, or asymmetric selection of the reported rows) rather than as evidence of a genome-wide upshift; the mechanism relies only on relative rank within the list.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots containing cathepsin or glycosidase candidates are treated as weak, non-attributable corroboration only, and none is claimed to measure a specific lysosomal protein pool.", "Elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to be a readout of transcriptional programme activity, not of enzyme activity, protein amount, correct lysosomal delivery, luminal pH, or degradative flux - none of which is measured here.", "TFEB and MITF transcript increases are assumed to co-occur with, but not to demonstrate, increased nuclear TFEB/MITF activity; no phosphorylation or localisation data are supplied.", "No lipid, sphingolipid, flux, imaging, pH, replicate-level or unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement is supplied, so cargo load, lysosome number and sphingolipid pools are inferred, never observed.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to be the sole source of the signal; genotype-specific astrocyte contribution or differentiation-efficiency differences between APOE4 and APOE3 lines cannot be excluded from these data alone.", "Background pathway membership used to build gene sets is unverified prior knowledge, not derived from the supplied files.", "No causal claim is made: this is an isogenic association under mock treatment, and causality has not been established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant coherent difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia in these selected differential-expression rows is a TFEB/MITF-associated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal degradative module - luminal acid hydrolases plus V-type ATPase subunits plus late-endosomal maturation and retromer/ESCRT components. Sphingolipid-degrading hydrolases (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1, GBA2, NPC2) rise as part of this generic module and are not enriched beyond non-sphingolipid hydrolases, while de novo sphingolipid synthesis and ceramide-routing genes are absent or unshifted. We therefore reject a sphingolipid-synthesis/vesicular-routing-specific mechanism and propose instead that lysosomal catabolic capacity relative to endocytic/lipid substrate load is the limiting node in APOE4, with the measured transcript elevation interpreted as an inferred compensatory response rather than a demonstrated increase in degradative flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING (sphingolipid-specific versus generic capacity): pharmacological blockade of sphingolipid synthesis or routing in APOE4 microglia - myriocin (SPTLC), Genz-123346/eliglustat (UGCG), or fumonisin B1 (CerS) at non-toxic doses - should NOT collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in the coordinated hydrolase plus v-ATPase transcript module (predicted \u003c25% reduction in the module's mean effect size), whereas the same module should be strongly attenuated by lowering cargo load (blocking phagocytosis/lipoprotein uptake) or by TFEB knockdown. If a sphingolipid-synthesis inhibitor alone normalises the module, this hypothesis is wrong and the sphingolipid-synthesis mechanism is correct.", "TFEB (with MITF) knockdown or degradation in APOE4 microglia should reduce GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GAA, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A and ATP6V1H transcripts toward APOE3 levels coordinately. If individual hydrolase transcripts remain elevated after TFEB/MITF loss, the proposed common transcriptional node is falsified and step 3 must be replaced.", "TFEB overexpression or torin-1-driven TFEB nuclear entry in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy a substantial fraction (predicted \u003e50% by rank correlation) of the APOE4 hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript signature without reproducing APOE4-specific non-lysosomal changes. Failure to phenocopy weakens the mechanism.", "Functional flux test of the capacity-limitation claim: DQ-BSA dequenching and myelin/oxLDL degradation per internalised cargo should be equal to or LOWER in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts, with LysoTracker/LAMP1 volume increased. If APOE4 instead shows proportionally increased degradative flux with no cargo retention, the bottleneck framing collapses and the module should be reinterpreted as a benign biogenesis gain.", "Delivery-mismatch test: immunoblot/activity assays should show that the transcript increase in GBA, HEXA and CTSD is not matched by a proportional increase in mature, lysosome-localised enzyme, with a measurable fraction of pro-enzyme secreted into APOE4 conditioned medium, consistent with the decreased M6PR transcript. Proportional mature-enzyme increase with no secretion excess would weaken step 6 (but not the whole hypothesis).", "GENERAL WEAKENING RESULT: if untargeted lipidomics of the same APOE4 versus APOE3 mock comparison shows a selective, large increase in ceramide/hexosylceramide species with no accumulation of non-sphingolipid lysosomal substrates (undigested protein, cholesteryl ester, glycogen from GAA cargo) and no change in bulk degradative flux, the generic-capacity claim is falsified in favour of the sphingolipid-specific alternative.", "REPLICATION CONTROL: in a second isogenic APOE4/APOE3 pair, the within-list rank enrichment of the lysosomal hydrolase plus v-ATPase module should reproduce (one-sided p \u003c 0.05) while the de novo sphingolipid synthesis module should remain non-enriched. Reproducing the sphingolipid arm alone would overturn the rejection of the assigned focus."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_138", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED: In APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, transcripts encoding luminal lysosomal hydrolases are elevated well above the already positively skewed background of this selected DE list (within-list percentile permutation test: sphingolipid-catabolic hydrolase set n=8, mean percentile 0.72, p=0.013; non-sphingolipid hydrolase set n=10, mean percentile 0.71, p=0.011), together with V-type ATPase subunits (n=7, mean percentile 0.69, p=0.045) and the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors TFEB and MITF.", "MEASURED/NEGATIVE: Genes of de novo sphingolipid synthesis and ceramide export are either absent from the list (SPTLC1, SPTLC2, DEGS1, CERT1, UGCG, SGMS1, ASAH1, ACER3, SPHK1) or not shifted relative to background (synthesis set n=8, mean percentile 0.43, p=0.75), and B4GALT5 is decreased; the sphingolipid module is therefore not distinguishable from the generic hydrolase module.", "INFERRED (transcription-to-protein step, not measured as a lysosomal protein pool): coordinated elevation of the CLEAR-type regulon is most parsimoniously explained by increased TFEB/MITF-dependent transcriptional output; TFEB activity is set post-translationally, and no phosphorylation, nuclear-localization or mTORC1-activity measurement is supplied here (mTORC1/Ragulator regulator set n=8, p=0.40, uninformative).", "INFERRED (causal direction unresolved): the coordinated increase in hydrolase plus proton-pump transcripts is read as a compensatory demand signal produced by a higher per-cell load of endocytosed/phagocytosed membrane and lipid cargo reaching late endosomes in APOE4, consistent with the concomitant elevation of APOE, TREM2, SCARB1, CD36, SOAT1 and DGAT1 transcripts; the alternative direction (a primary lysosome-biogenesis gain that increases cargo handling) is not excluded by these data.", "MEASURED: late-endosome maturation, retromer and ESCRT transcripts move with the same module (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B, VPS53, AP5M1; endosomal set n=6, mean percentile 0.83, p=0.0013), placing the change at the endosome-to-lysosome interface rather than at Golgi sphingolipid synthesis.", "INFERRED (functional consequence, unmeasured): if hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript expansion does not fully match cargo delivery - notably because the cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript M6PR is decreased while IGF2R is increased - net luminal degradative flux per unit cargo can remain unchanged or fall in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase mRNA, producing substrate retention in enlarged late endosomes/lysosomes.", "PREDICTED SYSTEM-LEVEL STATE: APOE4 microglia occupy a high-capacity, load-compensating endolysosomal state in which any sphingolipid change is a downstream cargo consequence, so sphingolipid-pathway manipulation should not normalise the genotype difference."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a coordinated, non-sphingolipid-selective expansion of lysosomal luminal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts, indicating degradative capacity (not sphingolipid synthesis/routing) as the limiting node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2319944002653046, "cosine_similarity": 0.3690355984793245, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_138", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5944757281553399, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2319944002653046, "cosine_similarity": 0.3690355984793245, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5944757281553399, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5675435, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 185}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1) with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong positive global shift (median +1.46; 77% up), so only within-list contrasts, not sign relative to zero, are treated as informative.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway demand and capacity; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, sterol localisation and droplet content were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; divergent CTSD/CTSB/ATP6V1E1-containing spots are treated only as evidence against a uniform coordinate protein increase, not as proteoform assignments.", "Key egress-arm genes (NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, ABCA1, MCOLN1, STARD3, PLIN2) are absent from the supplied list, so 'egress arm not scaled' rests on the four measured members and is provisional.", "Cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes with unreported replicate structure, so some differential signal may reflect composition or ambient RNA rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 effects.", "The APOE4/APOE3 comparison is isogenic and under mock treatment, so genotype is assumed to be the only systematic difference."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors and for luminal lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are induced above the already up-shifted background of this differential-expression list, while the measured lysosomal limiting-membrane and sterol-egress arm (NPC2, SCARB2, LAMP1, CLN3) is not scaled up and lysosome-candidate protein spots are not coordinately increased; we hypothesise that post-hydrolysis sterol export from the endolysosome, rather than cargo internalisation or luminal hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step, so liberated cholesterol is retained in the endolysosomal compartment and re-routed by SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification into cytoplasmic neutral-lipid droplets, giving APOE4 microglia a higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol load than isogenic APOE3 microglia. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2/STARD3 overexpression), which bypasses NPC-dependent lysosomal sterol egress, should lower lysosomal unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of cholesteryl ester and neutral-lipid droplets without changing hydrolase transcript induction; if cyclodextrin leaves the APOE4 cholesteryl-ester excess unchanged, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is weakened.", "Lipidomics should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 in cholesteryl esters (and secondarily triacylglycerol), with the ratio of esterified to free whole-cell cholesterol increased; an APOE4 lipidome dominated instead by accumulation of hydrolase substrates (sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, gangliosides, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate) with no cholesteryl-ester excess would favour a hydrolysis-failure rather than egress-failure bottleneck.", "Functional cargo assays should show intact or increased bulk luminal proteolysis/acidification in APOE4 (DQ-BSA dequenching, LysoSensor ratio comparable to or above APOE3) alongside impaired sterol egress; reduced DQ-BSA dequenching and raised lysosomal pH in APOE4 would refute Step 3 and reassign the bottleneck to hydrolytic capacity.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should convert the APOE4 droplet excess into an increase in free cholesterol with the lysosomal retention phenotype preserved; complete loss of any APOE4-versus-APOE3 sterol difference under SOAT1 inhibition would indicate an esterification-driven rather than egress-limited mechanism.", "TFEB knockdown should worsen, not relieve, the APOE4 lipid-storage phenotype if hydrolase induction is compensatory; a reduction of APOE4 droplet load after TFEB knockdown would contradict the compensatory interpretation in Step 2.", "Immunoblot/immunofluorescence should show that the induced hydrolase transcripts do not yield a proportional increase in mature CTSD/CTSB or in NPC2 protein per lysosome in APOE4; a proportional coordinate increase in all measured lysosomal proteins including NPC2 would weaken the capacity-mismatch claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:APOE, gene:PLA2G7), which we infer -- not measure -- corresponds to increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): Luminal acid hydrolase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) and v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), together with gene:TFEB, are elevated relative to the list background (hydrolase median 2.17 vs background median 1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.013); we interpret this as a demand-driven CLEAR-type transcriptional response, an inference about regulation rather than a measurement of TFEB nuclear localisation or enzyme activity.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, internal contrast): The measured lysosomal limiting-membrane / sterol-egress arm is flat at background (gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:CLN3 +1.17; hydrolase+v-ATPase vs egress-arm medians 2.03 vs 1.17, p=0.043), and lysosome-candidate protein spots are not coordinately raised (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 decreased while protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 increased); we infer a mismatch in which hydrolytic/acidification capacity is scaled but export capacity is not.", "Step 4 (inferred flux/localisation): Cholesterol liberated from ingested lipoprotein and membrane cargo therefore accumulates in the endolysosomal lumen/limiting membrane instead of reaching the ER; this pool is not measured here.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Sterol that does escape, plus lipogenic drive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:INSIG1, gene:CH25H, gene:MYLIP), feeds esterification (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), which we infer converts retained sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol stored in cytoplasmic droplets.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred state): Persistent undigested/undischarged cargo is reflected in stress/storage-associated transcripts (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3) and in a non-uniform hydrolase response (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:IDS -1.56), consistent with a compartment under chronic load rather than a uniformly expanded, fully competent lysosomal system."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol egress capacity, not hydrolase induction, limits endolysosomal lipid cargo clearance in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03913894324853229, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.290972637748156, "cosine_similarity": 0.36893607622731084, "direction_accuracy": 0.06634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6042362459546926, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03913894324853229, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.290972637748156, "cosine_similarity": 0.36893607622731084, "direction_accuracy": 0.06634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6042362459546926, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.49138775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 186}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_058", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are two side-by-side selected differential-expression lists (1705 increased, 507 decreased); absence of a gene means it was not selected, not that it is unchanged.", "The RNA effect column is a reported log fold change of unspecified base and is used here only for within-list ranking, not as an absolute fold change.", "Protein spots are mixtures with 3-6 candidate genes (including keratin/actin contaminants); no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and possibly non-linear proxy for enzyme protein, and enzyme protein a partial proxy for luminal activity and flux.", "No lipid, pH, activity, imaging or flux measurement is supplied; all statements about substrate pools, localization, acidification and flux are predictions, not observations.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-linked differences in cell composition or capture efficiency are assumed not to fully generate the hydrolase signal, which is not verifiable here.", "Background pathway memberships used to group genes are unverified prior knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 by a coordinate transcriptional expansion of luminal lysosomal hydrolases and endolysosomal trafficking machinery together with lipid-uptake/lipogenic transcripts. We propose the rate-limiting step is luminal degradation and clearance of lipid-rich cargo inside the late endosome/lysosome: cargo delivery is inferred to rise faster than degradative throughput, so the hydrolase transcript increase is a compensatory (unmet-demand) response rather than evidence of achieved higher catabolic flux. The assigned sphingolipid-specific framing is rejected as a primary mechanism: sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts rise, but no more than non-sphingolipid lysosomal hydrolases, and de novo sphingolipid synthesis transcripts are not elevated above the list background.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely raising cargo load in mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia (myelin debris, oxLDL or apoptotic-neuron fragments, 4-24 h) should produce a disproportionately larger accumulation of undegraded internalized label and a larger further induction of GAA/CTSB/CTSD/GBA/HEXA transcripts in APOE4; if the two genotypes clear the load with equal kinetics and equal transcriptional response, the cargo-clearance bottleneck is falsified.", "Reducing delivery rather than boosting enzymes should be the effective intervention: blocking scavenger-receptor uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or knockdown) or limiting lipid loading should normalize the hydrolase/TFEB transcript program and LAMP1 compartment size in APOE4; if uptake blockade leaves the hydrolase program unchanged, the compensatory-response step is wrong.", "Per-lysosome degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching, cathepsin-B/L FRET substrates, LysoSensor pH) should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; if flux per lysosome scales up in proportion to the transcripts, the mechanism collapses to a benign capacity increase.", "Sphingolipid-specificity test: glucosylceramide-synthase inhibition (UGCG blockade) should NOT normalize the APOE4 hydrolase/TFEB program or lysosome enlargement if the bottleneck is generic cargo clearance; a full normalization by UGCG inhibition would support the rejected sphingolipid-specific alternative and weaken this hypothesis.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB/MITF knockdown should suppress the hydrolase transcript increase and worsen cargo retention in APOE4 more than in APOE3; unchanged cargo retention after TFEB knockdown would refute the compensatory interpretation.", "Lipidomics prediction (currently unmeasured): APOE4 lysosome-enriched fractions should show increased substrate-to-product ratios across several catabolic classes (e.g., sphingomyelin/ceramide, GlcCer/ceramide, plus non-sphingolipid substrates such as glycogen and free cholesterol); accumulation restricted to sphingolipids only would favour the rejected focus, and no accumulation in any class would falsify the bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and lipid-handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7). INFERRED: increased delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-containing membrane cargo into the endolysosomal lumen (uptake flux and cargo composition were not measured).", "MEASURED (RNA): endosome maturation/retrieval and ESCRT transcripts are elevated (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VAMP3, gene:AP5M1), while the autophagosome-lysosome fusion SNARE gene:STX17 is decreased. INFERRED: cargo reaches late endosomes but the terminal fusion/clearance step is not proportionally supported (fusion events, compartment size and localization were not measured).", "MEASURED (RNA): a broad luminal hydrolase set is strongly up-shifted within the up-regulated list (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:DNASE2), with CLEAR-network regulators also up (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) and v-ATPase subunits up (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1). INFERRED: TFEB/MITF-associated compensatory transcription downstream of persistent undegraded luminal cargo; transcription-factor activity, nuclear localization and enzyme activity were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): sphingolipid catabolic genes (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2, gene:SUMF1) rise no more than non-sphingolipid lysosomal hydrolases, and de novo/anabolic sphingolipid genes sit near the floor of the up list (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:SGPL1, gene:CERK, gene:ST3GAL5) with gene:B4GALT5 decreased. INFERRED: the difference is a general degradative-load phenotype; any sphingolipid intermediate accumulation is a consequence of bulk membrane-cargo backlog, not of a dedicated synthetic or routing lesion.", "MEASURED (RNA): transcript up-regulation is not uniform across lysosomal genes (gene:CTSS strongly decreased, gene:IDS decreased) and protein-spot layers do not confirm a uniform hydrolase protein rise (protein_spot:053 increased, protein_spot:069 decreased, protein_spot:067 decreased; each spot has several candidate genes). INFERRED: transcript-to-active-enzyme conversion is incomplete, so degradative capacity per lysosome may lag the mRNA signal (protein identity, glycosylation, mannose-6-phosphate sorting and pH were not measured).", "INFERRED (causal, unestablished): a feed-forward loop in which undegraded lipid-rich cargo sustains TFEB/MITF-associated hydrolase transcription, enlarges the LAMP1 compartment and supports a low-grade inflammatory tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:TLR2, gene:CD74), making cargo clearance the primary bottleneck of the APOE4 state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at late-endosome/lysosome cargo clearance, not at sphingolipid synthesis: a TFEB-associated hydrolase expansion is compensatory"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24271683343795, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22394145837007054, "cosine_similarity": 0.3689321471987549, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6190453074433657, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24271683343795, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22394145837007054, "cosine_similarity": 0.3689321471987549, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6190453074433657, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72718425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 187}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_088", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a reported log fold change of unspecified base; only sign and rank order are used, and its magnitudes are never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot values.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (1705 up, 507 down of 2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene means it was not in the supplied list, not that it is unchanged.", "The apparent global positive shift (mean +1.39) is treated as a property of list composition, not as evidence for genome-wide transcriptional up-regulation.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes and are treated as non-identified; no spot is asserted to measure a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be only a weak proxy for enzyme activity; lysosomal pH, enzyme activity, enzyme localisation, lipid levels, autophagic flux and lysosome number are unmeasured here.", "Effects are attributed to the microglia in an astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte contribution or differentiation-state drift between APOE3 and APOE4 lines is not excluded.", "Positive effect means higher in APOE4; the comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so no acute stimulus is assumed."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 differs from APOE3 by a directionally uniform induction of transcripts for lysosomal luminal glycosphingolipid hydrolases and their accessory/acidification machinery (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, NAGLU, SMPD1, GAA, MAN2B1, AGA, SUMF1, NPC2, SCARB2, CLN3, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, DPP7, TFEB, ten v-ATPase subunits), while de novo sphingolipid-synthesis transcripts are indistinguishable from the list background. We hypothesise that this signature is a compensatory CLEAR-type response to an increased endolysosomal glycosphingolipid/sterol substrate load, and that the rate-limiting step is the conversion of that transcript program into luminal hydrolytic flux (enzyme routing, delivery and fusion), so that measured transcript abundance overstates the inferred, unmeasured catabolic activity. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: substrate reduction with a glucosylceramide-synthase (UGCG) inhibitor, or GBA/HEXA over-expression, in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal glucosylceramide/GM2 and blunt the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels, with little effect in APOE3. If the CLEAR-type transcript program in APOE4 is unchanged after substrate reduction, the compensatory-response step is falsified.", "Lipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher glucosylceramide, LacCer, GM2/GM3 and/or sphingomyelin per cell despite equal-or-higher GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 transcript levels. If APOE4 shows no glycosphingolipid excess, or shows lower glycosphingolipid, the substrate-load premise fails.", "Enzyme activity assayed per lysosome (4-MU-GlcCer, 4-MU-GlcNAc, sphingomyelinase) together with LysoTracker/pH-ratiometric imaging should show that activity rises much less than the transcript change and/or that luminal pH is not lower in APOE4. If per-lysosome hydrolase activity and acidification scale proportionally with the transcript increases and no substrate accumulates, the flux-bottleneck claim is falsified and the alternative 'successful adaptive lysosomal expansion' explanation is favoured.", "Routing test: blocking hydrolase delivery (GNPTAB knockdown or M6P-receptor blockade) should exaggerate the APOE4 glycosphingolipid phenotype far more than the APOE3 one, whereas boosting delivery (recombinant GBA or STX17/STX16 restoration) should reduce it. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond identically to these routing manipulations, step 4 is unsupported.", "Protein-level test: identification of the CTSB/CTSD/HEXB-candidate spots by mass spectrometry plus immunoblotting should show a shift in the pro-form/mature-form ratio in APOE4 rather than a uniform abundance increase. A uniform proportional increase in mature hydrolase protein matching the transcript changes would weaken the mechanism.", "Negative prediction that must hold: de novo sphingolipid-synthesis flux (stable-isotope serine/palmitate labelling into ceramide) should not be higher in APOE4. Increased de novo synthesis flux would move the primary bottleneck away from catabolism and weaken this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia up-regulate lipoprotein/sterol uptake and handling transcripts (SCARB1 +8.2, ABCA7 +2.1, SOAT1 +1.3, NPC2 +1.2, APOE +1.2, TREM2 +1.3, LGALS3 +2.4), which we infer increases delivery of membrane- and lipoprotein-derived glycosphingolipid and cholesterol cargo to the endolysosome. Cargo delivery itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred, unmeasured pool): The luminal pool of glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2, sphingomyelin and unesterified cholesterol rises, increasing demand for glycosidase and sphingomyelinase activity. No lipid was measured in this dataset; this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts): A TFEB/CLEAR-type transcriptional response raises hydrolase and acidification transcripts (TFEB +2.4; GAA +10.0, CTSK +7.4, GBA +6.7, NAGLU +5.9, HEXA +5.7, SMPD1 +5.6, CTSB +5.5, DPP7 +4.5, CTSD +2.9, GBA2 +2.6, HEXB +2.2, GM2A +2.0, GLA +1.5; ATP6V1H +6.9, ATP6V1A +4.2, ATP6V0C +3.5, ATP6AP1 +2.3, ATP6V1E1 +1.7; SLC38A7 +7.5, CLCN7 +1.1, TMEM192 +2.1). All 19 hydrolase/accessory genes and all 10 v-ATPase subunits present in the list move upward.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts; inferred limitation): Conversion of these transcripts into luminal enzyme activity is constrained at biosynthetic routing and fusion steps, because Golgi/endosome routing and fusion transcripts move oppositely (GOLPH3L -7.4, STXBP5 -5.5, GCC1 -5.0, STX16 -4.1, STX17 -2.1, VAMP2 -1.8, M6PR -1.7) even though partial compensation is present (GNPTG +3.0, IGF2R +2.0, RAB7A +2.7, VPS26A +4.9, SNX3 +3.9, AP5M1 +9.8). Routing rates, enzyme maturation and localisation were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): 2-D spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases change in both directions rather than uniformly upward (up: spot 053 +1.54, 013 +0.77, 012 +0.68, 027/055/057/006 +0.58; down: spot 069 -1.38, 067 -1.00, 058 -0.85, and ATP6V1E1-containing spots 064 -1.20 and 065 -0.93). We interpret this as consistent with redistribution among pro-/mature or modified enzyme forms rather than a proportional protein increase, but the spots are not uniquely identified and cannot assign a gene.", "Step 6 (inferred): Because clearance capacity rises less than substrate load, glycosphingolipid and sterol persist in the lysosome, sustaining the CLEAR program at steady state and biasing APOE4 microglia toward a lipid-laden phenotype (GPNMB +1.1, ITGAX +1.7, LGALS3 +2.4) without a strong cytokine signature in these data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a compensatory lysosomal glycosphingolipid-catabolism program whose bottleneck is per-lysosome hydrolytic flux, not enzyme transcript supply"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15830864355966306, "cosine_similarity": 0.36881347751935456, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6235307443365695, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15830864355966306, "cosine_similarity": 0.36881347751935456, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6235307443365695, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.957431, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 188}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_011", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong positive global shift (mean reported log fold change +1.39, 1705/2212 positive); all pathway claims here are relative to that empirical background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks and relative comparisons are used, not absolute fold changes.", "Transcript differences for MPC2, SLC25A1, ACSS2 and the sterol/esterification genes are assumed to translate into corresponding protein and enzymatic activity changes; no protein-level or activity measurement of these enzymes is available here.", "Citrate, acetyl-CoA, cholesteryl-ester, triacylglycerol and lipid-droplet pools, and all fluxes, localisations and directions of causation, are inferred and were not measured in this dataset.", "ACLY, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, FASN, CPT1A, LIPA and NPC1 are absent from the supplied rows, so the chain from citrate to cytosolic acetyl-CoA, and the efflux/storage arms, are not directly observed.", "Protein spots are ambiguous multi-candidate 2-DE features (e.g. protein_spot:050 lists MDH1 among five candidates including keratins) and are not treated as identified proteins or as evidence for or against specific enzymes.", "Replicate number is not supplied, and the astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may arise from non-cell-autonomous signalling rather than microglial genotype alone."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated transcriptional up-regulation of mitochondrial carbon entry and TCA/anaplerotic machinery together with the citrate carrier SLC25A1 and the acetate-to-acetyl-CoA enzyme ACSS2; we hypothesise that mitochondria-to-cytosol citrate/acetyl-CoA export is the rate-limiting node that converts this elevated oxidative carbon flux into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol synthesis (SREBF1, SCD, ACAT2, DHCR24, DGAT1, SOAT1), and that the coincident TFEB-associated lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase program is a compensatory response to the resulting lipid-ester load rather than its cause. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools, fluxes and enzyme activities are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SLC25A1 inhibition (e.g. CTPI-2) or MPC inhibition (UK5099) applied to mock-treated APOE4 microglia should reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of neutral lipid esters (cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol by lipidomics or BODIPY/filipin imaging) by a substantial fraction and lower SREBF1/SCD transcripts, while leaving the upstream TCA transcript differences (MPC2 excepted, OGDH, MDH1, GOT1) largely intact. If neutral lipid excess is unchanged or increased after citrate-export blockade, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "13C tracing: with U-13C-glucose and, separately, U-13C-glutamine, APOE4 microglia should show higher fractional 13C enrichment in citrate and in newly synthesised palmitate/cholesterol than APOE3, with glutamine contributing more than glucose. Equal or lower lipogenic enrichment in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism and favour a purely catabolic-oxidation interpretation.", "Directionality test of the lysosomal arm: blocking lysosomal acid hydrolysis (e.g. Lys05 or GBA/HEXB knockdown) should increase, not decrease, APOE4 lipid-ester load; if lysosomal inhibition instead reduces the APOE4-APOE3 lipid difference, the lysosomal program is upstream driver rather than compensation and this hypothesis is falsified.", "ACSS2 inhibition should produce a partial (smaller than SLC25A1 inhibition) reduction of the APOE4 lipid-ester excess; equal or greater effect would relocate the bottleneck to acetate-derived acetyl-CoA.", "Protein/activity check: targeted immunoblot or activity assays should show higher SLC25A1, MPC2 and SCD protein or activity in APOE4; failure to detect any protein-level or activity increase for these enzymes would substantially weaken the RNA-only inference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS) and for respiratory-chain subunits (gene:NDUFB2, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:SDHB), while a glycolytic entry enzyme is lower (gene:HK2). Inferred: greater mitochondrial oxidative and anaplerotic capacity, with carbon supplied partly by glutamine/aspartate-malate exchange rather than by increased glycolytic pyruvate.", "Inferred (not measured): the enlarged TCA/anaplerotic pool raises mitochondrial citrate; the measured increase in the citrate carrier transcript (gene:SLC25A1) is proposed to set the rate of citrate export to the cytosol. This export step is the primary bottleneck of the hypothesis; ACLY was not measured in this dataset, and gene:ACSS2 provides a parallel, measured route to cytosolic acetyl-CoA.", "Measured (RNA): lipogenic, sterol-synthetic and esterifying transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). Inferred: cytosolic acetyl-CoA is directed to fatty-acid desaturation, sterol synthesis and ester formation rather than to full oxidation.", "Inferred (not measured): net accumulation of neutral lipid esters (cholesteryl esters, triacylglycerol) in cytoplasmic droplets in APOE4 relative to APOE3; increased delivery of these and of membrane sphingolipids to the endolysosomal system.", "Measured (RNA): a coherent lysosomal program is higher in APOE4 (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A). Inferred: compensatory lysosomal biogenesis and hydrolase capacity that is insufficient to normalise the lipid-ester load, so the APOE4 lipidome remains shifted toward stored esters and sphingolipid catabolites.", "Inferred causal direction (untested): perturbing the citrate-export/acetyl-CoA node should move the APOE4 lipid phenotype toward APOE3 without abolishing the upstream TCA transcript differences."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial carbon to cytosolic acetyl-CoA via a citrate-export bottleneck, driving lipid esterification and a compensatory lysosomal hydrolase program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30425364902632335, "cosine_similarity": 0.3686717197287374, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6198025889967638, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.30425364902632335, "cosine_similarity": 0.3686717197287374, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6198025889967638, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.64959575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 189}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_074", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and 77% are positive, global median +1.46); we assume the selection is not systematically biased for or against glycolytic versus mitochondrial genes, and we therefore judge every gene set against this shifted background rather than against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks, signs and set-level contrasts are interpreted, not absolute fold changes.", "Steady-state transcript abundance of MPC2, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, HK2 and PFKP is assumed to track the corresponding protein and transport/enzyme capacity in the same direction; none of these proteins, their post-translational regulation, or their submitochondrial localisation was measured.", "Absence of LDHA, LDHB, PKM, PDHA1, PDK1-4, MPC1, GAPDH, ALDOA, ACLY, CPT1A and PPARGC1A from the list is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change; the fermentative and fatty-acid-oxidation arms are therefore only partially observed.", "Protein spots are assumed to be ambiguous mixtures: each spot carries 3-6 candidate genes, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific enzyme, and spot effects are used only as weak, non-decisive checks.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to differ between genotypes in a way that itself imposes the substrate environment; genotype-specific astrocyte lactate or lipid supply is an untested alternative driver.", "The comparison is cross-genotype at a single day-30 timepoint with replicate number not supplied, so differences in differentiation state or cell-composition drift between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures could generate the same transcript pattern without any change in flux."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in carbon routing rather than in total metabolic gene output: transcripts for the committed upper-glycolytic kinases HK2 and PFKP are among the most strongly reduced in the dataset, while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), PDH activation (PDP1), the complete cytosolic arm of the malate-aspartate shuttle (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A13), TCA enzymes (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, DLD) and nuclear-encoded ETC subunits are coordinately elevated above an already upward-shifted background. We hypothesise that this configuration makes cytosolic NAD+ regeneration, and therefore glycolytic ATP flux, obligately dependent on mitochondrial electron transport in APOE4 cells, and diverts surplus mitochondrial carbon out as citrate (SLC25A1) into an ACSS2/SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1 lipogenic sink. The measurements are steady-state RNA abundances from a selected differential-expression list plus non-uniquely-identified protein spots; flux, enzyme activity, metabolite pools and organelle localisation were not measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or malate-aspartate shuttle inhibition (aminooxyacetate) in mock-treated isogenic microglia should cause a substantially larger fractional loss of basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption in APOE4 than APOE3, and APOE4 should fail to mount a compensatory extracellular acidification/lactate increase. If APOE4 compensates by lactate production as well as or better than APOE3, or if the two genotypes lose equal OCR, the proposed shuttle/MPC dependence is wrong.", "Uniformly labelled 13C-glucose tracing should show, in APOE4 relative to APOE3, a lower fraction of glucose carbon appearing as secreted lactate and a higher fraction appearing as m+2 citrate/glutamate, with an increased contribution of 13C-glutamine, 13C-leucine or 13C-acetate to TCA intermediates. Equal or higher glucose-to-lactate labelling in APOE4 would falsify Steps 1-3.", "Seahorse glycolytic stress testing should show reduced glycolytic reserve and a higher OCR/ECAR ratio in APOE4; and after LPS or another activating stimulus APOE4 should show a blunted rapid glycolytic burst. A normal or enhanced glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue prediction: restoring upper glycolytic commitment (HK2 re-expression or membrane-permeant fructose-1,6-bisphosphate bypass) should restore glycolytic reserve in APOE4 without requiring correction of TCA/ETC transcripts; conversely, ETC inhibition (rotenone, oligomycin) should reduce APOE4 ATP and viability more than APOE3. Equal sensitivity to rotenone would argue against ETC-coupled glycolysis.", "Sink prediction: inhibition or knockdown of the citrate carrier SLC25A1 or of ACSS2 should reduce neutral-lipid-droplet content (BODIPY) preferentially in APOE4 microglia. Unchanged lipid droplets after SLC25A1 blockade, or no genotype difference in droplet content at baseline, would falsify Step 6.", "Protein-level check: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS should show increased MPC2, MDH1 and GOT1 and decreased HK2 protein in APOE4. If MPC2 and MDH1 protein are unchanged despite the large transcript differences, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails and the mechanism should be discarded.", "Stoichiometry check (Step 7): if the nuclear/mitochondrial ETC transcript mismatch is real, APOE4 should show reduced assembled complex I/complex IV holoenzyme (BN-PAGE) and increased sensitivity to doxycycline-mediated mitochondrial translation inhibition. Normal holoenzyme levels would confine the mechanism to Steps 1-6 without altering its core claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia reduce transcripts for the committed, ATP-consuming entry steps of glycolysis (gene:HK2 at the 3.6th percentile of all effects, gene:PFKP at the 5.5th, gene:PFKFB2 negative) while retaining or increasing glucose-uptake transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) and downstream isomerase/enolase transcripts (gene:GPI, gene:ENO1, gene:PFKM). We infer lowered maximal glucose-to-pyruvate commitment capacity, not lowered glucose uptake.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux routing): pyruvate that is produced is preferentially imported and oxidised rather than fermented, because the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier subunit transcript (gene:MPC2, +7.98, 99th percentile) and the PDH-activating phosphatase transcript (gene:PDP1) are elevated, together with gene:DLD; no lactate dehydrogenase or PDK transcript appears in the supplied differential list, so fermentative capacity is unmeasured rather than shown to be increased.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred bottleneck): cytosolic NAD+ regeneration is shifted onto the malate-aspartate shuttle, whose entire cytosolic and carrier arm is strongly up (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75; set median +5.46 versus global median +1.46). Because shuttle-borne NADH can only be reoxidised through complex I, glycolytic flux in APOE4 becomes coupled to, and rate-limited by, electron transport. This coupling is the primary bottleneck we propose.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): matching oxidative machinery is elevated - TCA transcripts (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB; set median +3.54, Mann-Whitney p=0.0024 against the shifted background) and nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (n=37, median +2.65, p=0.0021), with adenine nucleotide translocase (gene:SLC25A5) and matrix antioxidant transcripts (gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4) also up, consistent with sustained rather than collapsed respiratory demand.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): oxidative capacity is fed by diversified non-glucose carbon - branched-chain (gene:BCAT2 +6.42), glutamate (gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:ABAT), ketone/short-chain (gene:OXCT1 +4.72, gene:ACSS2) and glycogen/lysosomal glucose (gene:GYS1, gene:GAA) transcripts are elevated, so mitochondrial carbon supply is not contingent on the reduced glycolytic entry step.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred sink): surplus mitochondrial carbon is inferred to exit as citrate through the elevated citrate carrier transcript (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47) into a lipogenic/storage sink (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACSS2), alongside elevated lipoprotein-uptake and lysosomal-catabolism transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA), predicting neutral-lipid accumulation as a downstream consequence rather than as an observed pool.", "Step 7 (inferred fragility, partly counter-evidenced): the same cells show reduced mitochondrially encoded ETC transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2; MT median -1.56 versus nuclear ETC +2.65, p=0.001) and reduced oxidative-PPP/NAD-salvage transcripts (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD, gene:NAMPT), so the ETC on which APOE4 glycolysis now depends may itself be stoichiometrically or cofactor-limited, predicting poor tolerance of any respiratory challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia transcriptionally hard-wire pyruvate and cytosolic NADH into mitochondria, replacing fermentative glycolytic flexibility with ETC-coupled, citrate-exporting oxidative metabolism"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10622899974153527, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27804593446765075, "cosine_similarity": 0.36859598529066817, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067346278317152, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10622899974153527, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27804593446765075, "cosine_similarity": 0.36859598529066817, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6067346278317152, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.2178045, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 190}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_095", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the global median effect is about +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, so only within-list relative ordering, not absolute enrichment, is interpretable.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway output; SREBP proteolytic activation, TFEB nuclear translocation, ATF6 cleavage, hydrolase activity and all lipid fluxes are inferred, not measured.", "No sterol, cholesteryl-ester, lipid-droplet, ER-membrane-fraction or organelle-imaging measurement is supplied, so the proposed ER regulatory sterol pool is an unmeasured inferred pool.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes; spots 001/004/005/016 are treated only as 'no evidence for an ER-chaperone (HSPA5/HSP90B1/PDIA3) increase', not as identified chaperone quantification, and spot 002 is not treated as a specific cytosolic HSP90 measurement.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous APOE signalling or ambient RNA rather than microglia-intrinsic biology.", "Effect magnitudes up to about 15 log units indicate noisy or non-standard scaling; rank/direction is assumed more reliable than magnitude.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: all steps are correlational associations in one isogenic mock comparison."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the limiting step differentiating them from isogenic APOE3 is delivery of lipid-derived sterol from the expanded endolysosomal compartment to the ER regulatory sterol pool. Because the ER sensor does not register repletion, SCAP-SREBP-driven synthesis/uptake and esterification transcripts stay high at the same time as TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts, creating a self-reinforcing lipid cycle whose ER readout is a transmembrane/bilayer-stress-type signature (ATF6, EIF2AK3, DDIT3, MANF transcripts up) without the ERAD and ER-chaperone expansion expected from an unfolded-protein load (SEL1L, EDEM1, DERL1, PDIA3 transcripts down; ER chaperone-containing protein spots unchanged). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: delivering cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool in APOE4 microglia (cholesterol-loaded methyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should collapse the SREBP-target transcripts (SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1) and the ATF6/DDIT3 readout toward APOE3 levels while leaving TFEB/hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, GAA, CTSB) still elevated. If SREBP targets fail to normalize, or if the lysosomal program collapses in lockstep with them, the proposed sterol-return bottleneck is weakened.", "Rejection test of the proteostatic UPR alternative: chemical chaperones or UPR-arm inhibitors (4-PBA/TUDCA, GSK2606414, KIRA6) should NOT normalize the lipogenic or lysosomal transcript programs, and BiP/GRP94/PDIA3 protein should show no APOE4-vs-APOE3 difference by immunoblot, consistent with protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 and protein_spot:016. Observing genotype-elevated BiP protein or elevated XBP1 splicing, or normalization of lipid transcripts by 4-PBA, would falsify the bilayer-stress framing and favour a classical unfolded-protein-response mechanism.", "Phenocopy test: blocking lysosomal cholesterol export in APOE3 microglia (U18666A) should reproduce the APOE4 signature of simultaneously elevated SREBP targets and TFEB/hydrolase transcripts; failure to phenocopy would weaken step 2.", "Bilayer-specificity test: SCD inhibition should increase ATF6-reporter and DDIT3 induction preferentially in APOE4, and an ATF6 sensor mutated in its lumenal folding-sensing region should still show a genotype difference; equal tunicamycin responses in both genotypes with no genotype difference in the transmembrane-only sensor would weaken step 5.", "Direct measurement test: ER-enriched membrane lipidomics should show lower free cholesterol and a higher monounsaturated/saturated acyl-chain ratio in APOE4 despite equal or greater total cellular sterol and larger LAMP1+ lipid-laden compartments. No genotype difference in ER-fraction sterol or desaturation index would falsify the central claim.", "Epistasis test: SOAT1 inhibition should lower cholesteryl esters and, if free sterol then reaches the ER, reduce SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4; a further rise in SREBP targets would indicate the block is upstream of esterification and would require revising step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry a coordinate increase in endolysosomal biogenesis and hydrolase transcripts (TFEB, MITF, GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, SMPD1, GM2A, ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1, RAB7A). We infer, but did not measure, larger/more acidic lysosomes carrying a higher lipid catabolic load; lipid content, hydrolase activity and TFEB nuclear localization are unmeasured.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred flux): Export of liberated sterol from the endolysosome to the ER regulatory membrane pool is rate-limiting, so the ER sterol sensor continues to read 'sterol-poor'. This pool and the transfer flux are not measured here; the transcript pattern is the only indirect evidence.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Consequently the SCAP-SREBP output remains high in APOE4 - SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, SCD, DHCR24, LSS, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LDLR, FADS1 - together with uptake and handling genes (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, ABCA7, APOE, CH25H, MYLIP). SREBP cleavage/nuclear forms were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred flux): Continued synthesis and uptake against a blocked ER-return route is disposed of by esterification and storage (SOAT1, DGAT1 transcripts up), and re-enters the lysosome, so the lysosomal and lipogenic arms reinforce each other instead of cancelling; neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester pools are unmeasured.", "Step 5 (inferred membrane composition): Sustained SCD and FADS1 output plus altered sphingolipid transcripts (ST3GAL5, CERS6, SMPD1, GM2A) shift ER bilayer acyl-chain and sphingolipid composition. This activates the membrane-domain-sensing arms of the ER stress response - transcripts ATF6, EIF2AK3, DDIT3, MANF, SERP1, CRELD2, ERO1A up - while the ERAD/glycoprotein-disposal arm is not expanded (SEL1L, EDEM1, DERL1, PDIA3 down) and ER chaperone-containing protein spots show no genotype increase, which is why we assign bilayer stress rather than unfolded-protein load.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred phenotype): This chronic lipid-handling state co-occurs with a DAM/inflammatory transcriptional tone (APOE, TREM2, CXCL8, CCL2, PYCARD, NLRP3), which we propose is downstream of, not upstream of, the sterol-return bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at lysosome-to-ER sterol return, producing a futile lipogenic/lysosomal cycle and lipid-bilayer-type ER stress rather than a protein-folding UPR"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1837037994313776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1825615546051548, "cosine_similarity": 0.3678825595400542, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904433656957929, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1837037994313776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1825615546051548, "cosine_similarity": 0.3678825595400542, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5904433656957929, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.02080175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 191}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_019", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (no |effect| below 1; 77% positive), so direction within a gene set is interpretable but the apparent global increase is a selection artefact and cannot be used as evidence of transcriptome-wide up-regulation.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative ranks are used, not absolute fold changes.", "Transcript differences are assumed to translate at least partly into protein and complex abundance for the actin/motor module; no protein-level measurement of RAC2, DOCK8, WASHC4 or MYH9 is available here.", "2D-gel spots contain several candidate genes each (and frequent keratin contaminants), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration, and spots whose candidate lists overlap change in both directions, consistent with spot redistribution rather than net abundance change.", "Lipid, cholesterol, filipin, lipid-droplet, phagocytic-flux, lysosomal-pH and localisation measurements are absent from this dataset; every statement about sterol pools, ER sterol sensing, flux, tubulation and droplet accumulation is an inference or prediction, not an observation.", "The comparison is stated to be isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture at day 30 with mock treatment; differences in microglial maturation state, purity or co-culture composition between genotypes are assumed not to be the sole driver of the myeloid-module decrease.", "SREBP pathway activity is inferred from the coordinate direction of its component and target transcripts; SREBP proteolytic processing was not measured."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia not by a general cytoskeletal defect but by a selective transcriptional reduction of the haematopoietic-restricted branched-actin/motor module (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, MYO1F, ARHGAP30, WASHC4, MYH9, ACTB) set against uniformly increased uptake-receptor, endosomal-coat, acidification and hydrolase transcripts. We hypothesise that this stoichiometric imbalance makes actin-dependent tubulation/retrieval from maturing phagosomes and late endosomes the rate-limiting step, so internalised lipid cargo is retained in an expanded LAMP1+ acidic compartment, sterol delivery to the ER is limited, and the resulting SREBP-type biosynthetic and esterification programme (SREBF1/2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, SCD, SOAT1, DGAT1) diverts lipid into stored esters, giving the lipid-droplet/LDAM-like state. Causality is not established by these data; all activity, flux, localisation and lipid-pool statements are inferences from transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: re-expressing RAC2 (or restoring WASH-complex function via WASHC4) in APOE4 microglia should reduce LAMP1+ filipin/cholesterol signal and neutral-lipid droplet area and lower SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR) without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, MERTK); if the module is restored to APOE3 levels yet lysosomal lipid retention and SREBP targets are unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Bypass test: acute hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or an equivalent lysosome-to-ER sterol bypass) should normalise SREBP-target transcripts and reduce droplet load in APOE4 within hours while leaving RAC2/DOCK8/WASHC4/MYH9 transcripts unchanged; failure to normalise SREBP targets would falsify the 'sterol trapped upstream of the ER' step.", "Pulse-chase phagocytosis: with pHrodo-myelin or opsonised beads, APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater internalisation at 30-60 min but significantly greater cargo retention and reduced recycling-receptor return to the surface at 6-24 h relative to APOE3; if APOE4 instead shows a reduced initial internalisation rate, the bottleneck lies at cup formation rather than retrieval and this version must be revised.", "Phenocopy: Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) or Rac inhibition in APOE3 microglia should reproduce cargo retention plus SREBP-target induction and droplet accumulation; absence of that phenocopy weakens the mechanism.", "Independent measurement: quantitative protein or activity assay should confirm lower RAC2/WASH-complex and MYH9 protein in APOE4 microglia; equal protein levels despite the transcript differences would remove the mechanistic basis of step 3.", "Specificity: a generalised cytoskeletal collapse is not predicted; Arp2/3 subunit, CFL1 and DNM2 protein levels and clathrin-mediated transferrin uptake should be comparable between genotypes, and a global reduction in all actin machinery would argue for an alternative, non-selective explanation such as a maturation-state difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for scavenger, opsonic and phagocytic uptake receptors and bridging factors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, MERTK, MRC1, FCGR1A/FCGR3A, C1QA/B/C, GAS6, STAB1, ANXA1, CLEC7A, ITGAX); inferred: capacity for lipid/debris internalisation is at least maintained and probably increased.", "Measured: coat/sorting, RAB, ESCRT, v-ATPase, hydrolase and TFEB transcripts are coordinately higher (SNX3, SNX17, VPS26A, VPS35L, VPS28, CHMP4B, RAB7A, ATP6V1H/1A/0C/1E1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, LAMP1, TFEB); inferred: an enlarged, acidified late-endosomal/lysosomal compartment receiving that cargo.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred activity, not measured): the actin nucleation-promoting and motor arm needed to form and sever retrieval tubules from phagosomes and late endosomes is limiting, because the myeloid-restricted module is transcriptionally down (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, MYO1F, ARHGAP30, WASHC4) together with ACTB and MYH9, even though Arp2/3 subunits, CFL1, DNM2 and RHOA are up; coat components therefore outnumber the actin machinery that they require.", "Inferred consequence: membrane and cargo retrieval/egress from the degradative compartment is slowed, prolonging cargo residence and biasing flux toward degradation and storage rather than recycling; this pool of lysosomal lipid was not measured here.", "Inferred sensing step: reduced sterol delivery from the endolysosome to the ER de-represses SREBP-type transcription, consistent with the coordinated rise of SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, EBP, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2 and SCD despite unchanged or increased uptake capacity.", "Measured transcripts plus inferred flux: esterification and storage genes (SOAT1, DGAT1) and a lipid-droplet/LDAM-like identity programme (APOE, LGALS3, GPNMB, FABP5, ITGAX, ABCA7) are up, predicting accumulation of cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid droplets in APOE4 microglia as the downstream phenotype."], "title": "An actin-retrieval bottleneck downstream of uptake: APOE4 microglia up-regulate lipid/debris internalisation and lysosome biogenesis while the myeloid branched-actin/motor module is reduced, trapping sterol in the degradative compartment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23078724532879738, "cosine_similarity": 0.36735494154706516, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5950226537216828, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23078724532879738, "cosine_similarity": 0.36735494154706516, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5950226537216828, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.655987, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 192}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_022", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected DE list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, adj p \u003c 0.05) assembled from two blocks: a balanced 506-up/506-down table and a 1200-gene, 1199-positive up-only list; sign coherence was therefore judged only within the balanced block, and unlisted genes (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, PSAP, GRN, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and was preserved; magnitudes above ~6 may be inflated by sparse single-cell counts, so direction is weighted more than size.", "Transcript direction is assumed to track the direction (not the magnitude) of the corresponding protein and functional capacity; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lipid mass, uptake rate, oxygen-consumption or efflux measurement is supplied.", "Protein 2-D spots carry a median of five candidate identities (39/92 include keratins); cathepsin- and other lysosome-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, :053 up vs :058, :067, :069, :064, :065 down), so they are used only as compatibility/contradiction tests and no individual protein is treated as confirmed.", "Genes within a module are co-regulated and not independent, so the binomial statements are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment result.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript signal may not be microglia-autonomous, and one day-30 timepoint cannot separate a primary APOE4 effect from an established adaptation.", "The mechanism describes the mock (unchallenged) condition; any reduced reserve capacity for a lipid or myelin challenge is a prospective inference, not something the supplied data establish as an ongoing defect."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated day-30 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 shifts cells into a coordinated lipid/debris-handling state rather than causing one isolated enzymatic block: transcripts for scavenger and opsonic uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A) rise together with a TFEB-type endolysosomal module (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, v-ATPase subunits, gene:LAMP1) and with mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/beta-oxidation transcripts (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:MGLL), while glycolytic/oxidative-PPP transcripts are the only coherently reduced module (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD). Sterol released from this cargo is inferred to be routed into esterified/oxysterol pools (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:HSD3B7) rather than to the ER, which is compatible with the persistently elevated SREBP-target transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24) despite increased uptake capacity. All statements about uptake, degradation, oxidation and efflux are inferred flux; only transcript and 2-D spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE cargo-flux test (primary discriminator): pulse-chase of fluorescently labelled myelin debris or acetylated-LDL plus DQ-BSA in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher internalisation and equal-or-higher per-cell degradation rate in APOE4, with a raised cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio. If APOE4 instead shows equal or reduced internalisation, or accumulates undigested cargo with reduced DQ-BSA dequenching, the routing/high-throughput mechanism is weakened and the competing failed-degradation explanation is favoured.", "PROSPECTIVE fuel test: extracellular-flux measurement should show APOE4 with a higher basal oxygen-consumption:extracellular-acidification ratio and greater sensitivity to CPT1/beta-oxidation inhibition, despite unchanged or higher glucose uptake. Unchanged OCR/ECAR ratio would falsify step 4.", "PROSPECTIVE sterol-routing test: SOAT1 inhibition (for example avasimibe) should raise ER-accessible/free cholesterol and lower SREBP-target transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR7) more in APOE4 than APOE3. If SREBP targets remain elevated after esterification block and after cholesterol loading, step 5 is wrong and the sterol module must be reassigned to a genotype-intrinsic transcriptional difference.", "PROSPECTIVE capacity test: TFEB knockdown should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H) and reduce cargo clearance selectively in APOE4; if clearance is unaffected, the lysosomal module is a passenger rather than the load-bearing arm.", "PROSPECTIVE protein-level resolution: targeted immunoblot or MS of the ambiguous spots should show increased mature CTSB/CTSD and v-ATPase subunits in APOE4. Finding that the decreased spots (protein_spot:058, :067, :069, :064, :065) represent reduced mature cathepsin or ATP6V1E1 protein despite elevated transcripts would contradict the increased-capacity reading and support compensatory, unsuccessful induction."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 raises expression of lipoprotein/debris receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK with gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A), which is expected to increase receptor-mediated internalisation of lipid-rich material; internalisation rate itself was not measured.", "STEP 2 (measured transcripts): a TFEB-associated endolysosomal program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB, hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:DNASE2; acidification gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1; gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2), indicating expanded degradative capacity matched to step 1. Capacity is not the same as measured hydrolytic activity.", "STEP 3 (measured transcripts, inferred routing): sorting components are rebalanced toward the late-endosome/lysosome route (gene:IGF2R +2.0 up with gene:M6PR -1.7 down, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1 up), consistent with re-routing of hydrolases and cargo rather than with uniform scaling of one compartment.", "STEP 4 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): catabolic products are directed to mitochondrial oxidation rather than glycolysis: gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACO2, gene:GLUD1, gene:SDHB, gene:CYCS, gene:ATP5F1B and lipolytic/beta-oxidation genes gene:MGLL, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1 are up, whereas gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3, gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1 are down even though glucose transporters gene:SLC2A1 and gene:SLC2A3 are up (uptake preserved, downstream glycolytic/PPP commitment reduced).", "STEP 5 (measured transcripts, inferred compartmental sterol distribution): liberated sterol is channelled into esterified, oxysterol and export-associated pools (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:HSD3B7, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:NPC2, gene:MYLIP) instead of repleting the ER-accessible pool, which is compatible with the simultaneous elevation of SREBP-target transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). ER sterol content was not measured, and HMGCR/SQLE/ABCA1/ABCG1/NPC1/LIPA are absent from the supplied list.", "STEP 6 (measured transcripts): the same state carries a chemokine/activation signature (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:GPNMB, gene:NLRP3, gene:IL18, gene:A2M) expected of lipid-loaded, phagocytically engaged microglia; this is a correlate of the state, not a required step."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a scavenger-uptake / endolysosomal-catabolic state that routes lipid cargo toward mitochondrial oxidation and esterified stores rather than glycolysis, leaving the ER-accessible sterol pool unrepleted"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07436399217221135, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23127025093107387, "cosine_similarity": 0.36719639195756865, "direction_accuracy": 0.12459546925566344, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5954271844660194, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07436399217221135, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23127025093107387, "cosine_similarity": 0.36719639195756865, "direction_accuracy": 0.12459546925566344, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5954271844660194, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.62342075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 42}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are log fold changes in an unspecified logarithm base; only sign and rank are used, and every set-level statement is made relative to the observed global median of +1.46 rather than to zero.", "The supplied 2212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (100% have |effect| \u003e 1), so absence of a gene (e.g. SPTLC1, SGMS1, UGCG, P2RY12, PSAP) is not evidence of no change and was not used as evidence.", "Lowered TGFBR1/SMAD2 transcript abundance corresponds to lowered TGF-beta receptor signalling flux; phospho-SMAD2 was not measured.", "Increased scavenger-receptor transcripts correspond to increased surface receptor density and increased cargo internalisation rate; no uptake, localisation or lipid measurement is present in the data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; spots 027/053/055 are treated as consistent-but-not-identifying support because CTSD/CTSB share each spot with actins, tropomyosin, YWHA proteins and others.", "The APOE4-vs-APOE3 comparison is isogenic and mock-treated as stated, so genotype rather than treatment or line background drives the contrast; biological replicate number was not supplied.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex; we assume the RNA contrast reflects microglial state and not differential astrocyte carry-over or ambient RNA, which is not verifiable here.", "Background pathway memberships (TGF-beta/SMAD, MAFB, CLEAR/TFEB, sphingolipid catabolism, GPNMB as a lysosomal-lipid-stress marker) are unverified prior knowledge; literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 primarily by a reduced TGF-beta type-I receptor signalling module (TGFBR1, SMAD2 and the feedback target SMAD7 are the rare strongly significant down-shifts in a globally up-shifted RNA list). We hypothesise that this lowered TGFBR1-dependent tone is the rate-limiting node that permits a MAFB-associated scavenger/endocytic receptor program (MRC1, CD163, STAB1, COLEC12, SLCO2B1, F13A1, SIGLEC1, MS4A6A/MS4A7, CD36, SCARB1), which raises endolysosomal lipid and lipoprotein cargo delivery and is matched by coordinate expansion of lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, GAA, ACP5, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, TFEB) including a glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic arm (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1) and the lysosomal-lipid-stress marker GPNMB. We explicitly reject sphingolipid synthesis/turnover as the primary bottleneck: the sphingolipid arm is not separable from the general lysosomal expansion in these data (permutation p = 0.15 against the shifted background), de novo synthesis genes are absent from the supplied list, and no lipid species were measured. Causality is not established; the receptor-first ordering is the hypothesis under test, not an observation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Primary discriminating perturbation: pharmacological TGFBR1 kinase inhibition (e.g. SB-431542) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature, raising MAFB, MRC1, CD163, STAB1, COLEC12 and GPNMB and secondarily CTSB/CTSD/GBA/HEXA, while recombinant TGF-beta1 or a constitutively active TGFBR1 in APOE4 microglia should lower them toward APOE3 levels. If SB-431542 reduces phospho-SMAD2 in APOE3 yet leaves the scavenger and lysosomal transcripts unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Ordering test: removing the cargo (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking MRC1/CD163/CD36-mediated uptake) should blunt the lysosomal-hydrolase arm (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, GPNMB) in APOE4 without normalising TGFBR1, SMAD2 or MAFB. If TGFBR1/SMAD2/MAFB also normalise, the receptor-first causal ordering is refuted and a lipid-first model is favoured.", "Protein-level check: APOE4 microglia should show higher LAMP1-positive lysosomal volume per cell and higher DQ-BSA and Bodipy-lipid degradation per cell, with cathepsin B/D protein increased on an unambiguous immunoblot. If lysosomal volume and bulk degradative flux are unchanged or reduced despite the hydrolase transcript rise, Step 5 fails and the transcript rise must be reinterpreted as compensatory rather than capacity-increasing.", "Sphingolipid rejection test: lysosome-normalised lipidomics should show APOE4 glucosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin elevated no more than the general lysosomal expansion (i.e. flat after LAMP1 normalisation). Selective, disproportionate GlcCer/GM2 accumulation with unchanged lysosomal volume would overturn the rejection and reinstate a sphingolipid-turnover bottleneck.", "Metabolic consequence: APOE4 microglia should show lower extracellular acidification rate and lower glycolytic reserve than APOE3 and greater sensitivity to hexokinase or MPC inhibition on Seahorse, with a blunted LPS-induced glycolytic burst. Equal or higher glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would falsify Step 7 without necessarily affecting Steps 1-6.", "Specificity control against a global artefact: qPCR or bulk RNA-seq with spike-in normalisation should reproduce the direction-discordant down-shift of TGFBR1, SMAD2, SMAD7 and HK2 while most transcripts are unchanged. If those four normalise to no change once composition-independent normalisation is applied, the entire signature is a scaling artefact of the supplied differential list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred activity). APOE4 microglia carry lower TGFBR1, SMAD2 and SMAD7 transcript abundance against a strongly positive global RNA background (gene:TGFBR1 -2.19, gene:SMAD2 -1.79, gene:SMAD7 -1.68, global median +1.46). We infer, but did not measure, reduced TGFBR1 protein and reduced phospho-SMAD2 signalling flux; SMAD7 (a direct negative-feedback target) falling with its upstream receptor is the internal consistency check.", "Step 2 (inferred transcriptional de-repression). Lowered TGF-beta receptor tone releases a MAFB-associated mononuclear-phagocyte identity program (gene:MAFB +1.47). MAFB activity itself is not measured; only its transcript.", "Step 3 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred surface receptor density). This program raises transcripts for scavenger, lectin and lipoprotein-handling receptors (gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:COLEC12, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:F13A1, gene:SIGLEC1, gene:MS4A6A, gene:MS4A7, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1). Surface localisation and uptake rate are inferred, not observed.", "Step 4 (inferred flux). Increased receptor-mediated internalisation raises the lipid/lipoprotein cargo flux arriving in late endosomes and lysosomes. No lipid pool, uptake assay or cargo measurement exists in the supplied data.", "Step 5 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred capacity). The cell answers the load with a coordinate CLEAR-type lysosomal build-out: acid hydrolases and acidification machinery rise (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GAA, gene:ACP5, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB, gene:NPC2), and two ambiguous protein spots whose candidate lists contain CTSD/CTSB are increased (protein_spot:027, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055). Enzyme activity and lysosomal pH are inferred, not measured.", "Step 6 (subordinate, not the bottleneck). Within that build-out a glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic arm is among the highest-moving members (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1) alongside gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3 and gene:APOE, consistent with lipid-laden lysosomes; we treat this as a consequence of Steps 3-5 rather than as an autonomous sphingolipid-synthesis defect.", "Step 7 (inferred downstream metabolic consequence). The lipid-scavenging, oxidative-catabolic state is accompanied by suppression of the committed glycolytic entry step (gene:HK2 -3.67, one of only ~18 highly significant down-shifted genes), predicting reduced glycolytic reserve for acute immune activation in APOE4 even though this experiment is mock-treated."], "title": "Attenuated TGFBR1/SMAD2 receptor tone licenses a MAFB-linked scavenger-receptor and lysosomal lipid-catabolic program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14884241930684383, "cosine_similarity": 0.3671518943078054, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6098996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1379647749510763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14884241930684383, "cosine_similarity": 0.3671518943078054, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6098996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.29663675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 193}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77% positive); program coherence was therefore judged against that biased background and by randomization within the list, not against a 50/50 expectation. Genes absent from the list (e.g., NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, CAT, NFE2L2, most PEX genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; effects are used only as signed, ordered magnitudes on their original reported scale, and are not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate with, but not to demonstrate, protein amount, enzymatic activity, subcellular localization or metabolic flux; no sterol, cholesteryl-ester, lipid-droplet, lysosomal-pH or hydrolase-activity measurement was supplied.", "Coordinate elevation of SREBP-pathway transcripts is interpreted as a de-repressed ER sterol-sensing state; this assumes SREBP-2 processing tracks its target transcripts and that no independent transcriptional driver (e.g., a growth/anabolic program) explains the same genes.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate identities each, mean 4.8; keratins/actins dominate the candidate pool), so no spot is treated as confirming an individual protein; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "The proposed accumulation is a state expected in the measured mock condition; any additional impairment of clearance capacity would be revealed only by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge and is not claimed here.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may reflect altered microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake and for TFEB/MITF-family lysosomal biogenesis are strongly higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:TFEB +2.38, all ten represented v-ATPase subunits positive), yet the ER sterol/SREBP program that lipid loading should switch off is also uniformly higher (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1, gene:ACAT2 all positive, 15/15 members positive vs 77% positive in this selected list, randomization p=0.02). We propose that in APOE4 the sterol delivered by uptake is preferentially routed to esterified/lysosome-associated pools (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCP2 +5.95) rather than to the ER-accessible pool, so uptake and de novo synthesis continue simultaneously and the degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded, predicting greater neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester load in APOE4 microglia in the measured mock condition. This is a routing/sensing mismatch, not primarily an oxidative-stress or peroxisomal defect (peroxisomal members are few, modest and mixed: gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:CROT +1.03, gene:AMACR +1.12, gene:ABCD1 -1.64; median below the selected-list background). Causality is not established; only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, quantify esterified vs ER-accessible cholesterol (LC-MS cholesteryl esters plus an ALOD4/D4H accessible-cholesterol probe) with LipidTOX/filipin imaging. The mechanism predicts higher cholesteryl ester and lysosome/droplet-associated sterol in APOE4 with ER-accessible cholesterol not increased. If APOE4 shows equal or lower stored lipid, or clearly higher ER-accessible cholesterol alongside the elevated SREBP transcripts, the routing/mis-sensing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective: acute SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g., avasimibe) should shift APOE4 cholesterol from ester to free/ER-accessible pools and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the elevated SREBP program after esterification blockade would argue for a sensor-level or independent transcriptional driver instead.", "Prospective: sterol loading (LDL or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should suppress LDLR/HMGCS1/DHCR24 in APOE4 to a similar degree as in APOE3 if the sensor itself is intact and only routing differs; failure of APOE4 to suppress would falsify the routing interpretation in favour of a defective ER sterol-sensing step.", "Prospective: direct lysosomal assays (GBA, GAA, CTSB activity; LysoSensor/LysoTracker; DQ-BSA) should show increased or unchanged hydrolase activity and normal acidification in APOE4 despite lipid accumulation. Reduced hydrolase activity or elevated lysosomal pH despite the higher transcripts would replace this mechanism with a failed-compensation, clearance-bottleneck mechanism (a possibility already hinted at by decreased cathepsin/v-ATPase-candidate spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064).", "Prospective negative control for the assigned redox focus: APOE4 microglia in mock should not show a substantially greater cellular ROS, lipid-peroxidation (BODIPY-C11, 4-HNE) or NRF2-target signature than APOE3; a strong ongoing oxidative-stress phenotype with induced NRF2 targets would indicate that redox stress, rather than lipid routing, is the primary differentiating axis.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4 and, if lysosomal expansion is a downstream response to lipid load, should increase stored lipid without lowering SREBP targets; if TFEB knockdown instead abolishes the SREBP-program difference, the causal ordering proposed here is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and phagocytic recognition (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:MERTK, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A), implying increased delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosomal system (delivery flux inferred, not measured).", "Cargo-derived sterol and lipid are preferentially channelled into esterified and lysosome-associated storage pools rather than to the ER-accessible pool, consistent with higher esterification/lipid-transfer transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:MGLL +4.03).", "Because ER-accessible cholesterol is not sensed as replete, the SREBP arm remains de-repressed and continues to drive sterol and fatty-acid synthesis and further LDLR-mediated uptake (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59); uptake and synthesis therefore run together instead of being reciprocally regulated.", "The accumulating lipid load engages a TFEB/MITF-family transcriptional response that expands the degradative compartment: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.70, gene:MITF +1.00, CLEAR-type hydrolases gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.86, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.53, gene:CTSD +2.86, acidification machinery gene:ATP6V1H +6.94, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, and trafficking genes gene:RAB7A +2.72, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:SLC17A5 +2.22.", "Higher catabolic and biosynthetic demand accompanies increased mitochondrial/OXPHOS transcript abundance (gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:NDUFB2 +2.11, gene:SDHB +1.65; 15/15 represented members positive) and modestly higher peroxide-handling transcripts (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:FTH1 +2.53), interpreted as a secondary load response rather than the primary difference.", "Net predicted consequence in the measured mock condition: APOE4 microglia carry a larger stored/esterified lipid pool and an enlarged, transcriptionally amplified lysosomal compartment; whether hydrolytic flux keeps pace is unknown, and ambiguous 2D protein spots are internally inconsistent on this point (protein_spot:052 +2.14 and protein_spot:053 +1.54 up vs protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:064 -1.20 down, each with 3-6 candidate identities)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lipoprotein-derived sterol into lysosomal/ester storage while the ER sterol-sensing arm stays de-repressed, driving a self-sustaining uptake-plus-synthesis lysosomal-expansion state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2300252815124543, "cosine_similarity": 0.3671193104830752, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5953592233009709, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2300252815124543, "cosine_similarity": 0.3671193104830752, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5953592233009709, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84781575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 43}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_166", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved; all RNA inferences use rank/direction and within-dataset comparisons only, never absolute fold-change arithmetic.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression result, not an unbiased transcriptome: every row has |effect| \u003e 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, so the 77% upward fraction and the +1.46 median are treated as a selection/normalization property of the supplied list, not as a demonstrated whole-transcriptome global shift. All pathway tests are made against this same filtered background.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and 'spot up/down' is treated as evidence about a mixture, not about one gene product.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for enzyme protein abundance, and enzyme protein abundance a partial proxy for catalytic activity in the acidic lumen. No enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, autophagic/degradative flux, protein localization, or lipid species was measured in the supplied data.", "The 'demand-driven' direction (substrate load causes the transcriptional program) is assumed, not established; the reverse (a primary transcriptional change causing altered lipid handling) is not excluded by these data.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied'; single-cell-derived p-values may be inflated by pseudo-replication, so p-values are used only for ranking, not as calibrated evidence strength.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes and APOE is expressed by both; the supplied observations are assumed to reflect the microglial compartment, and cross-genotype astrocyte contribution cannot be excluded.", "Key nodes of the proposed chain (NPC1, PSAP, MCOLN1, ABCA1, SQLE, HMGCR, classical ISGs) are absent from the supplied list; their absence is treated as 'not measured', not as 'unchanged'."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant reproducible difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is not interferon or NF-kB activation but a coordinated transcriptional up-regulation of lysosomal acid hydrolases for glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin and glycoconjugate catabolism (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GBA2, GM2A, SMPD1, NAGLU, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) together with TFEB/MITF and every measured v-ATPase subunit. We hypothesise that this is a demand-driven compensation for a bottleneck in luminal lipid hydrolysis/egress that is NOT relieved, because the corresponding 2-D protein spots containing cathepsin, hexosaminidase and v-ATPase candidates are not coordinately increased and several are decreased, and because the CD-MPR hydrolase-sorting receptor transcript (M6PR) is reduced. The unrelieved luminal sequestration is proposed to lower ER-accessible sterol, de-repressing an SREBP-type synthesis/uptake/esterification module (SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, LDLR, SCARB1, SOAT1, DGAT1) that feeds more lipid back to the same bottleneck. Only transcript and spot abundances are measured; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, lipid pools, localization and all causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Substrate reduction by glucosylceramide-synthase (UGCG) inhibition (e.g. eliglustat / Genz-123346) in mock APOE4 microglia should, within 48-72 h, collapse the APOE4-specific excess of the hydrolase/CLEAR transcript module (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GAA, CTSB, TFEB) toward APOE3 levels and reduce LysoTracker-positive and BODIPY/filipin-positive area, without requiring any change in interferon or NF-kB signalling. If UGCG inhibition lowers glycosphingolipid substrate but leaves the hydrolase transcript program elevated, the demand-driven direction in STEP 2-3 is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "SECOND DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or cGAS/STING inhibition should NOT reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in the hydrolase or SREBP transcript modules. If either treatment normalises those modules, the explicit rejection of the interferon/inflammatory focus is falsified and the hypothesis should be replaced.", "ACTIVITY-VERSUS-TRANSCRIPT TEST (core of the bottleneck claim): Measure GBA, total beta-hexosaminidase and cathepsin B specific activity per cell and DQ-BSA proteolytic flux plus ratiometric lysosomal pH in APOE4 versus APOE3. The mechanism predicts transcripts strongly up but specific activity and DQ-BSA flux flat or reduced (activity/transcript ratio significantly lower in APOE4) with equal or higher lysosomal pH and increased LysoTracker volume. If activity and degradative flux rise in proportion to transcript and substrate load is unchanged, STEP 4 fails and the program is a successful, not a failing, compensation.", "PROCESSING TEST: Immunoblot for pro- versus mature cathepsin D/B and pro- versus mature HEXB. The mechanism predicts an increased pro:mature ratio and/or increased secreted pro-enzyme in APOE4 conditioned medium, consistent with a delivery/maturation-limited step and with the divergent directions of the cathepsin-containing spots. Equal pro:mature ratios across genotypes would weaken STEP 4.", "EPISTASIS/ORDER TEST: Acute cholesterol repletion of the ER pool (cholesterol-loaded methyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should abolish the APOE4 excess of SREBF2/LDLR/DHCR24/LSS/ACAT2 transcripts while leaving the hydrolase module elevated, placing SREBP downstream. Conversely, empty methyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which extracts sequestered sterol) should reduce both modules. If the SREBP module remains elevated after full ER sterol repletion, STEP 5-6 is falsified.", "GENOTYPE-SELECTIVE VULNERABILITY: Pharmacological GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) or v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) should produce a significantly larger increase in neutral-lipid/glycosphingolipid accumulation and a larger drop in phagocytic clearance of myelin or apoptotic-neuron cargo in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia. Equal sensitivity across genotypes would argue that lysosomal hydrolytic capacity is not the limiting node.", "SPECIFICITY CONTROL: The APOE4 hydrolase-module elevation should be reproduced by an orthogonal assay (targeted qPCR or a hydrolase-activity panel) in an independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 pair. Failure to reproduce would indicate the signal is an artefact of the thresholded DE list rather than a genotype effect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_166", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (inferred, partly measured): APOE4 alters microglial lipoprotein-lipid handling in the astrocyte co-culture so that endolysosomes receive glycosphingolipid- and sterol-rich cargo whose clearance is slower than in APOE3. Measured as transcript abundance only: APOE (gene:APOE), and elevated uptake/handling transcripts SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1), CD36 (gene:CD36), ABCA7 (gene:ABCA7), TREM2 (gene:TREM2). Cargo flux and lipid pool size are inferred, not measured.", "STEP 2 (measured transcripts; inferred activity): Sustained luminal substrate load raises MiT/TFE-family transcriptional output. TFEB (gene:TFEB, +2.38) and MITF (gene:MITF, +1.03) transcripts are elevated. TFEB nuclear localization and activity were not measured and are inferred.", "STEP 3 (measured transcripts): The downstream CLEAR-type output is dominated by lysosomal acid hydrolases acting on sphingolipids and glycoconjugates: GBA (+6.71), HEXA (+5.68), SMPD1 (+5.63), NAGLU (+5.91), GAA (+9.96), CTSK (+7.36), CTSB (+5.52), plus GBA2, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, CTSD, LAMP1; all eight measured v-ATPase subunit transcripts (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1E1, ATP6V1F, ATP6V0D1, ATP6V1C1, ATP6V0D2) are positive. Seven of eighteen measured lysosomal hydrolase genes fall in the top 6% of effect sizes (hypergeometric p = 5.6e-5).", "STEP 4 (primary bottleneck; measured abundance, inferred flux): The transcriptional program does not translate into a matching increase in mature hydrolase protein or acidification machinery, so hydrolytic capacity per lysosome remains rate-limiting. Protein spots whose candidate lists include CTSB/CTSD/HEXB/ATP6V1E1/ACP2 have a median effect equal to the overall spot median (+0.48) and several are significantly decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) while others increase (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:012, protein_spot:063). The CD-MPR sorting-receptor transcript M6PR is decreased (-1.72) despite increased IGF2R and GNPTG, and the major microglial protease CTSS is strongly decreased (-5.57). Spot identities are ambiguous multi-gene assignments; enzyme activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "STEP 5 (inferred consequence): Persistent luminal sequestration of sterol and sphingolipid lowers the ER-accessible cholesterol pool sensed by SCAP/INSIG. The ER sterol pool was not measured.", "STEP 6 (measured transcripts): Consistent with de-repressed SREBP signalling, the sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, uptake and esterification module is elevated: SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17), DHCR24 (+3.69), DHCR7 (+2.71), LSS (+2.27), ACAT2 (+2.04), INSIG1 (+1.87), LDLR (+1.50), SREBF2 (+1.06), SOAT1 (+1.25), DGAT1 (+1.72). All eleven measured cholesterol-synthesis genes are positive, though the module is not significant against this thresholded background (Mann-Whitney p = 0.22).", "STEP 7 (net inferred state): APOE4 microglia occupy an 'activated-but-inefficient lysosome' state with feed-forward lipid acquisition, rather than an interferon- or NF-kB-driven inflammatory state. The interferon focus is rejected: only four genes of a 30-gene interferon panel appear (CD74, CIITA, IFI16, TMEM173) with no classical ISG (no ISG15/MX1/OAS/IFIT/STAT1/IRF7) and no enrichment (p = 0.81); the NF-kB panel is mixed (CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3 up but TNFAIP3, RELB, CCL4 down; p = 0.50)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic transcriptional program that is not matched at the hydrolase-protein level, leaving luminal lipid clearance as the rate-limiting step and de-repressing SREBP-driven lipid acquisition"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14585383013126318, "cosine_similarity": 0.3669203396116045, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_166", "mean_absolute_error": 0.62326213592233, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1223091976516634, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14585383013126318, "cosine_similarity": 0.3669203396116045, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.62326213592233, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.24656775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 194}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so set-level statements are made only relative to the internal list background (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein-spot magnitudes (log2) are therefore compared by direction and rank, never as a quantitative ratio.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with several candidate genes each; group-level spot statistics are treated as weak, ambiguous evidence about the named proteins and no single spot is claimed to identify one protein.", "gene:TFEB and gene:MITF transcript levels are used only as proxies for MiT/TFE pathway engagement; nuclear localization, phosphorylation and transcription-factor activity were not measured.", "Lysosomal lipid content, cholesteryl esters, enzyme activities, pH and degradative flux were not measured in these data and are inferred, not observed.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype rather than line background is the main difference; replicate structure is 'not supplied in workbook', so effect precision cannot be independently checked."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting step distinguishing them from isogenic APOE3 cells is luminal lysosomal catabolism of endocytosed lipid cargo. Transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:SOAT1, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), endosome-to-lysosome delivery (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B) and a coordinated MiT/TFE-type lysosomal program (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF with 13/14 measured acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits up, median RNA effect +3.7 vs +1.46 list background, permutation p=0.0005) are elevated, yet protein spots whose candidate genes include lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase are, as a group, not elevated relative to other spots (median +0.26 vs +0.48 log2, permutation p=0.035) and several are decreased (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:065). We therefore hypothesise a substrate-driven, transcriptionally compensated but flux-limited lysosome: measured RNA increases reflect demand signalling rather than achieved degradative activity. ER-chaperone/UPR mechanisms are rejected as primary: the UPR RNA set is not enriched above the list background (median +1.74, p=0.31) and the only spots containing ER chaperone candidates (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005) trend downward and are not significant. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: reduce cargo influx in APOE4 microglia (SCARB1 knockdown, or lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SOAT1 inhibition). The mechanism predicts that lysosomal lipid load falls and the CLEAR-like RNA elevation (GBA, HEXA, GAA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) collapses toward APOE3 levels within 48-72 h. If those transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 while lysosomal lipid is normalised, the substrate-driven step is falsified and a cargo-independent, cell-autonomous MiT/TFE activation should be preferred.", "Per-cell enzymatic assays (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GAA, cathepsin B/D activity, normalised to cell number and lysosome volume) should show APOE4:APOE3 activity ratios far smaller than the corresponding transcript ratios, and DQ-BSA or BODIPY-LacCer/filipin clearance should be slower in APOE4. If activities scale proportionally with transcripts and clearance is faster in APOE4, the 'capacity bottleneck' claim is weakened and an enhanced-degradation interpretation would be favoured.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should worsen lipid/substrate accumulation and lower hydrolase transcripts, whereas constitutively nuclear TFEB or enzyme augmentation (recombinant/chaperone-boosted GBA) should improve clearance without lowering gene:SCARB1. If TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid accumulation, the compensatory role assigned to MiT/TFE signalling is wrong.", "Rejection test for the assigned ER focus: if pharmacological UPR inhibition (PERK or IRE1 inhibitor) or ER-chaperone induction normalises the APOE4 phenotype, or if BiP/GRP94 protein and XBP1 splicing are in fact clearly elevated, then the present rejection of an ER-proteostasis bottleneck (based on the non-enriched UPR RNA set and the non-significant, downward protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005) is wrong.", "Immunoblotting for cathepsin B/D pro- versus mature forms should show a shift in APOE4 (relative accumulation of pro/intermediate forms or altered glycoforms) explaining why hydrolase-containing spots move in opposite directions (protein_spot:053 up, protein_spot:069 down). If mature-form levels rise in proportion to transcripts with no proteoform shift, step 5 is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein handling components (gene:SCARB1, gene:SOAT1, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7), which we infer - but did not measure - increases delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesterol/sphingolipid cargo into the endocytic pathway.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred trafficking): elevated late-endosomal/retromer/ESCRT transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:RAB28) are consistent with cargo being routed to and concentrated in lysosomes; localization itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck): luminal hydrolysis of glycosphingolipid and cholesteryl-ester cargo saturates. Sphingolipid-directed hydrolase RNAs are the most strongly raised subgroup (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA; subgroup median +5.6, p=0.0009), the pattern expected when substrate accumulates and signals for more enzyme.", "Step 4 (measured RNA; inferred transcription factor activity): MiT/TFE-type signalling (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF +1.0 as abundance proxies only) drives a coherent CLEAR-like program - hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:DPP7, gene:HEXB), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and gene:LAMP1 - as a compensatory response to the bottleneck, not as its cause.", "Step 5 (measured protein spots): compensation fails to reach the mature enzyme pool. Spots whose candidate lists contain hydrolases/v-ATPase subunits are lower as a group than other spots (p=0.035); protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:090 (CTSD-containing), protein_spot:067 (CTSB/HEXB-containing) and protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 (ATP6V1E1-containing) are decreased, while only protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are increased, indicating redistribution rather than a uniform rise in hydrolase abundance.", "Step 6 (predicted consequence, unmeasured here): degradative flux per lysosome falls below cargo influx, so undigested lipid persists in the endolysosome, sustaining MiT/TFE signalling in a feed-forward loop; the strong loss of gene:CTSS and gene:IDS indicates the shift is a re-specification of hydrolase composition, not a uniform increase in degradative capacity."], "title": "Lysosomal hydrolytic capacity, not ER proteostasis, is the APOE4 bottleneck: MiT/TFE-type transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal lipid-catabolic program is not matched by mature hydrolase protein-spot abundance"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15849420530031497, "cosine_similarity": 0.36600713332947094, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6165436893203884, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15849420530031497, "cosine_similarity": 0.36600713332947094, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6165436893203884, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90963875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 195}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, 77.1% positive; 87% positive among rows with adjusted p \u003c 1e-50) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directionality is judged against this up-biased selected background, and absent genes (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1, FDPS, CYP51A1, MSMO1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged. Effect magnitude and adjusted p are essentially uncorrelated here (r = -0.04), so the very large log-FCs are treated as low-precision and the mechanism rests on the highly significant, moderate-effect rows.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein/pathway capacity; no sterol, cholesteryl-ester, lipid-droplet, oxysterol, efflux or phagocytic-flux measurement is supplied, so routing, ER-pool depletion, SREBP-2 proteolytic activation and LXR ligand occupancy are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (92 spots, 2-6 candidate genes each, no uniquely identified spot, no sterol-pathway candidate on any spot); they are used only for compatibility, never to confirm an individual protein.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 pseudobulk-style DE from a mixed microglia/astrocyte co-culture, so an apparent cell-state shift could partly reflect a change in the proportion of scavenger-like microglial states rather than a change within a single uniform state.", "Descriptive coherence within curated gene sets is not a formal enrichment test; members are correlated and were queried from canonical membership lists defined before directions were inspected."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, D30) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzymatic bottleneck but by an altered routing of lipid/sterol: transcripts for lipoprotein- and debris-scavenging receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:LDLR; 16/16 represented members positive, median log-FC +1.29, median adjusted p ~1e-138) rise together with a coordinated MiT/TFE lysosomal-biogenesis module (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF, 11 v-ATPase subunits, gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2; 17/17 positive) and with sterol/neutral-lipid esterification and storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:ABHD5) plus oxysterol/efflux-associated transcripts (gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:MYLIP). Critically, transcripts whose expression is normally lowered when the ER regulatory sterol pool is replete (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR) are instead elevated (10/10 represented members positive). We claim the most parsimonious interpretation is that internalized and newly made sterol in APOE4 is preferentially routed into endolysosomal and esterified/stored pools and into oxysterol/APOE-dependent export attempts, so the ER regulatory pool does not report repletion and the acquisition program is not switched off, producing a self-sustaining scavenger/lipid-processing cell state rather than a return to homeostatic microglial identity (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS1, gene:LGALS3, gene:ANXA1, gene:CD74, gene:CCL2 up; gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:CCL4 down). Measured quantities are transcript and protein-spot abundances only; routing, flux, sterol pool sizes and causality are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (prospective): loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with fluorescently traceable cholesterol-rich substrate (e.g. labelled myelin or acetylated LDL) and measuring the esterified/free cholesterol ratio, lysosomal (filipin/LipidSpot) sterol and the ER-pool readout (SREBP-2 cleavage plus HMGCR/SQLE/LDLR mRNA) should show, in APOE4, higher esterified and lysosomal sterol with failure to suppress SREBP-2 targets. If APOE4 instead suppresses SREBP-2 targets at least as strongly as APOE3 while esterified sterol is unchanged, the routing mechanism is falsified and a plain increased-throughput adaptation is favoured.", "Prospective: acute SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should shift sterol back to the ER pool and lower gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1 and gene:SREBF2 toward APOE3 levels without lowering TFEB-driven v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts first; if lysosomal-program transcripts fall before the SREBP-axis transcripts, step 3 is mis-ordered.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce gene:ATP6V1A/gene:ATP6V1H/gene:CTSB/gene:GBA transcripts and increase lysosomal lipid retention without restoring homeostatic markers; if hydrolase transcripts are TFEB-independent here, step 2 is wrong.", "Prospective flux test: pulse-chase of internalised labelled cholesterol should show slower appearance of the label in the ER/plasma-membrane accessible pool and in APOE-containing supernatant particles in APOE4; equal or faster appearance would weaken the routing claim.", "Falsifier internal to this dataset's logic: single-cell re-analysis showing that the scavenger/lysosomal signature comes from a shifted proportion of a distinct macrophage-like cluster, with within-cluster APOE4-vs-APOE3 sterol-axis differences absent, would replace this mechanism with a composition/state-abundance explanation.", "Prediction with a stated non-claim: the mock-condition data predict no ongoing inflammatory or interferon activation (consistent with gene:CCL4, gene:TNFAIP3 down and absence of an ISG module); observing constitutive IL1B/TNF/ISG induction in APOE4 mock cultures would indicate a different driver than the proposed lipid-routing state."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipoprotein/debris receptor and opsonin transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE), consistent with an increased capacity for lipoprotein and lipid-debris internalization into the endolysosomal system (uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured).", "Step 2 (inferred signaling): The increased endolysosomal lipid/substrate load is met by a MiT/TFE-family transcriptional response (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF up) that expands lysosomal number/acidification and hydrolase content (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1 and 7 further v-ATPase subunits; gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SMPD1; gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A).", "Step 3 (altered routing, inferred): Sterol liberated in this expanded compartment is preferentially channelled to esterification/neutral-lipid storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:ABHD5) and to oxysterol/export routes (gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:MYLIP) rather than efficiently equilibrating with the ER regulatory sterol pool; gene:NPC2 and gene:OSBPL1A are up while gene:OSBPL8 is down, i.e. the sterol-transfer arm is remodelled, not uniformly increased.", "Step 4 (consequence in the measured condition): Because the ER regulatory pool is not signalling repletion, SREBP-axis and post-squalene sterol-synthesis transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP) alongside gene:LDLR, so acquisition and synthesis drive are maintained simultaneously with storage and export - a feed-forward acquisition-storage loop rather than a closed feedback loop.", "Step 5 (cell-state consequence): The loop locks APOE4 microglia into a scavenger/lipid-processing state with raised catabolic and mitochondrial transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:ACO2) and lipid-associated markers (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS1, gene:LGALS3, gene:ANXA1, gene:CD74, gene:TSPO), with loss of some homeostatic/immunoregulatory transcripts (gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:CCL4, gene:TNFAIP3 down), without a general inflammatory or interferon program.", "Step 6 (prospective only): The re-allocation of capacity to constitutive uptake and storage is predicted to reduce spare handling capacity when an acute lipid load (myelin debris, oxidised LDL, apoptotic cells) is imposed; this is a predicted challenge-revealed limitation and is NOT established by the mock-condition data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an acquisition-and-storage sterol routing state: scavenger uptake plus MiT/TFE lysosomal expansion with esterification and oxysterol export, while ER-sterol-dependent SREBP output stays on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23451032235886676, "cosine_similarity": 0.365960714577083, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5966796116504854, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23451032235886676, "cosine_similarity": 0.365960714577083, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5966796116504854, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.131611, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 44}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_055", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected significant differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705/2212 positive), so program coherence was judged against a 77%-positive background; genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (HSPA5, XBP1, ERN1, ATF4, HERPUD1, ABCA1, LIPA, PLIN2, CPT1A, LDHA, mitoribosomal genes are all unmeasured here).", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and some magnitudes are extreme (up to 15.5), so effects are treated as ranked directional evidence on their original reported scale, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Coordinated transcript increases in lysosomal, TCA and OXPHOS genes are assumed to reflect a coordinated transcriptional state (TFEB/PGC1-type programs); they are abundance measurements and do not establish hydrolase activity, respiration, ATP production or lipid flux, none of which were measured.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (2-92 with 2-6 candidate genes each, dominated by keratin/actin contaminants) and are used only for compatibility, never to confirm an individual protein; the ANXA1/TALDO1 spots (043-047) are compatible with the ANXA1 transcript rise (+4.15) but TALDO1 transcript falls (-2.32), and no OXPHOS, TFEB or v-ATPase-specific unambiguous spot exists.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein cargo, so the lipid-handling arm assumes an extracellular lipid source that was not measured.", "Reduced mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to index mitochondrially encoded subunit supply; 10X Flex probe-based quantification of mitochondrial transcripts may be unreliable, so the stoichiometric-mismatch step is the weakest link and concerns reserve under future challenge, not a demonstrated defect at mock."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture), APOE4 shifts cells into a coordinated cargo-handling state in which lipoprotein/debris uptake and TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcription rise together with mitochondrial substrate-carrier, TCA and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts, while glycolytic commitment transcripts (HK2, PFKP) fall and lipid re-esterification/storage transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1) rise; this is a routing/cell-state change toward lysosomal catabolism feeding mitochondrial oxidation, and the assigned ER/UPR-secretory program is not differentially coherent in these data. Because mitochondrially encoded subunit transcripts are not co-elevated (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 lower), the state is predicted to have reduced oxidative reserve that would be revealed only by a future challenge, not an established defect in the measured mock condition.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, extracellular flux measurement should show basal oxygen consumption equal or modestly higher in APOE4 with a lower spare respiratory capacity after FCCP, and lower extracellular acidification; if APOE4 basal respiration and spare capacity are both unchanged or higher, the routing/limited-reserve mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective: acute inhibition of the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier (UK5099) or of CPT1-independent lysosomal acid lipase-derived fatty-acid oxidation (etomoxir) should reduce ATP-linked respiration more in APOE4 than APOE3; equal sensitivity would argue the oxidative transcripts are not carrying extra substrate flux.", "Prospective: blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or v-ATPase-dependent hydrolysis should collapse the APOE4-specific TCA/OXPHOS transcript elevation and cause neutral-lipid (BODIPY) accumulation preferentially in APOE4; persistence of the OXPHOS transcript elevation would show the mitochondrial arm is not downstream of lysosomal catabolism.", "Prospective: myelin or apoptotic-neuron loading should reveal a larger lipid-droplet burden and a smaller increment in oxygen consumption in APOE4 than APOE3, i.e. a challenge-revealed reserve deficit; equal handling would refute the reserve prediction.", "Prospective (focus test): ER-stress reporters at mock (XBP1 splicing, BiP/HSPA5 protein, ATF4/CHOP protein) should not differ appreciably between APOE4 and APOE3 despite gene:ATF6 +4.04 and gene:DDIT3 +2.79; a clear constitutive UPR at mock would favour an ER-proteostasis mechanism over the one proposed here.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should blunt the APOE4-specific hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation and the downstream TCA/OXPHOS elevation; if hydrolase transcripts fall but mitochondrial transcripts do not, the two arms are parallel APOE4 effects rather than a causal chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters lipoprotein/lipid cargo handling in microglia; uptake and opsonin-receptor transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ANXA1 +4.15), increasing delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal route (uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured).", "Increased endolysosomal cargo load is accompanied by a TFEB/TFEC-associated lysosomal biogenesis program: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.65, all eight measured v-ATPase subunits up (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, others +1.1 to +1.7) and lipid/glycan hydrolases up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17), 27/29 lysosomal members positive versus a 77% positive selected-list background (binomial p=0.024).", "Hydrolytic release of fatty acids, sterols and amino acids from lysosomal cargo is coupled to increased transcription of mitochondrial substrate import and TCA machinery: gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS +1.35 (14/14 positive, effect magnitudes larger than background, Mann-Whitney p=5e-4).", "Downstream, every measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit is higher in APOE4 (38/38 positive, median +2.64; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:SDHB +1.65; binomial p=5e-5), together with mitochondrial import/biogenesis transcripts (gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM8B +5.20, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:HSPA9 +2.35, gene:CYCS +2.60), indicating a transcriptionally expanded oxidative apparatus (respiration rate not measured).", "In parallel the glycolytic commitment steps are lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) while glucose transporters and the pyruvate carrier are higher (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:MPC2 +7.98), consistent with carbon being routed to mitochondrial oxidation rather than glycolytic/lactate output.", "Fatty acid and sterol not oxidised are routed to storage/re-esterification rather than efflux: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:FABP5 +1.13 (ABCA1 not measured; only gene:ABCA7 +2.14 represents efflux-associated transcripts).", "The expanded nuclear oxidative program is not matched by mitochondrially encoded core subunit transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; 4/6 negative, binomial p=0.028 versus background), so assembly stoichiometry may cap usable capacity; this predicts reduced oxidative reserve under a future lipid or phagocytic challenge rather than an ongoing bioenergetic failure in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-to-mitochondria lipid-catabolic cell state, not an ER-proteostasis stress state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24110299569054117, "cosine_similarity": 0.3655347077175024, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6000938511326861, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24110299569054117, "cosine_similarity": 0.3655347077175024, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6000938511326861, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.07564425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 45}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_155", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded, pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong positive global shift (mean +1.39, 77% up in an unspecified logarithm base); all pathway claims are made relative to that shifted background by permutation within the supplied list, and absence of a gene (e.g. HSPA5, NPC1, XBP1) means 'not in the selected list', not 'unchanged'.", "Coordinate transcript elevation of hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and MiT/TFE factors reflects a demand-driven CLEAR-type response; this assumes transcript abundance tracks a regulatory signal, not that degradative flux, lysosomal pH or mature enzyme activity is increased (none were measured).", "Lysosomal lipid substrate accumulation, cholesterol localization, ER sterol pool, TFEB nuclear translocation, mTORC1 status, XBP1 splicing, ATF6 cleavage and eIF2-alpha phosphorylation are inferred, not observed; no lipidomic, imaging or phospho measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features (many contaminated by keratins/actin) and are treated as ambiguous, non-unique identifications used only as weak corroborating or counter-evidence, never as identified protein pools.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and equally differentiated, so the genotype comparison is not dominated by differences in microglial maturation state or astrocyte co-culture composition; cell-composition and maturation covariates were not supplied.", "Causality is not established by these data: all steps are correlational associations organized into a testable chain."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a rate limitation in lysosomal luminal catabolism of lipid cargo (glycosphingolipids, sphingomyelin, and lipoprotein-derived sterol). The measured coordinate elevation of lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and MiT/TFE transcripts is interpreted as a compensatory demand signal rather than as evidence of increased degradative flux; because sterol is retained in the endolysosome and diverted to esterification/storage, the ER SCAP-INSIG sensing pool still reports sterol demand, sustaining SREBP target transcription and lipid uptake in a feed-forward loop. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is rejected: ERAD transcripts are coordinately reduced and ER-chaperone-containing protein spots are unchanged.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (flux vs capacity): in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, Lyso-IP lipidomics plus filipin/BODIPY and LysoTracker imaging should show higher lysosomal cholesterol and glycosphingolipid substrate together with equal-or-lower degradative flux per lysosome (DQ-BSA and fluorescent myelin/apoptotic-cell pulse-chase) despite the higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 lysosomes instead show equal or lower lipid substrate and equal-or-higher flux, the bottleneck claim fails and the transcript rise should be reinterpreted as genuinely increased capacity.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (site of the sterol-sensing defect): mobilizing lysosomal cholesterol with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or bypassing the lysosome with 25-hydroxycholesterol, should suppress SREBP targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, SCD) markedly more in APOE4 than in APOE3, collapsing the genotype difference. If LDL loading alone suppresses these targets equally in both genotypes, the trapped-sterol/ER-sensing step is weakened.", "Prediction 3 (compensation, not cause): acute TFEB/TFE3 knockdown should abolish the APOE4-specific hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript excess and worsen lysosomal lipid accumulation selectively in APOE4; if TFEB loss leaves the hydrolase excess intact, Step 3 is wrong.", "Prediction 4 (bottleneck relief): augmenting the specific luminal enzymes (GBA/HEXA activation or overexpression, or acid-lipase/GBA chaperone treatment) should reduce lysosomal lipid load and lower the CLEAR and SREBP transcript signatures in APOE4 toward APOE3; no reduction would weaken the enzyme-limited formulation and favour an export/trafficking-limited variant (e.g. NPC-type transfer or ABCA1/ABCA7 efflux).", "Prediction 5 (transcript-protein decoupling): mature hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity per lysosome (mature CTSD/CTSB, GBA and HEXA activity assays) should not scale with the large transcript increases; observing proportional increases in mature enzyme activity would argue against a hydrolytic-capacity bottleneck.", "Prediction 6 (rejection test of the ER focus): APOE4 microglia should not show increased BiP/GRP94 protein, XBP1 splicing, ATF6 cleavage or eIF2-alpha phosphorylation under mock conditions, and ISRIB/PERK inhibition should not normalize the lysosomal/lipid transcript signature. Demonstrating a genuine constitutive UPR with UPR-inhibitor-reversible lysosomal changes would refute this hypothesis in favour of the ER-proteostasis alternative."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_155", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; flux inferred): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts of lipid/lipoprotein uptake and lipid-handling receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7), which we infer increases delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosomal lumen; cargo delivery itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck; substrate pool NOT measured): luminal hydrolysis of glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and glycogen/glycoconjugate cargo becomes the rate-limiting step, so undigested lipid substrate accumulates inside lysosomes. No lipidomic or imaging measurement of this pool exists in the supplied data.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts; activity inferred): a MiT/TFE-type CLEAR compensation raises transcripts of the master regulators (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:RRAGD) and of essentially the whole hydrolase and proton-pump machinery (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC38A7). Transcript abundance is measured; nuclear TFEB localization, lysosomal pH and per-lysosome enzyme activity are inferred and unmeasured.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts; localization inferred): sterol that is not exported is esterified and stored (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4) while lysosomal sterol transfer capacity is only modestly changed (gene:NPC2), so the ER-resident SCAP-INSIG sterol-sensing pool remains sub-saturated.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts; pathway activity inferred): consequently the SREBP transcriptional programme stays engaged in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD), which feeds back on Step 1 and further loads the endolysosome \u2014 a feed-forward cycle rather than resolution.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts; flux inferred, alternative explanations acknowledged): mitochondrial oxidative machinery transcripts rise coherently (gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2), which we interpret as increased catabolic/ATP capacity supporting acidification and disposal of liberated fatty acids; this step could equally reflect an independent APOE4 metabolic difference.", "Step 7 (rejection of the assigned focus): the ER arm shows no coherent proteostatic overload \u2014 ERAD/retrotranslocation transcripts fall (gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1, gene:PDIA3), and protein spots whose candidate lists contain the ER chaperones HSP90B1/HSPA5 are not increased (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005), so the difference is placed in the lysosome, with the ER contributing only as the sterol-sensing compartment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal lipid-catabolic clearance, not by ER proteostasis: a CLEAR-type compensatory hydrolase program with persistent ER sterol-demand signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1679466824207067, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11981198653955022, "cosine_similarity": 0.36531678658080335, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_155", "mean_absolute_error": 0.63, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1679466824207067, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11981198653955022, "cosine_similarity": 0.36531678658080335, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "mean_absolute_error": 0.63, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88874025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 196}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_016", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment claims are made against the within-list background (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% positive) using rank-based tests, and the logarithm base of the RNA values is left unspecified and is not assumed to be 2.", "Coordinate transcript elevation of a hydrolase or carrier module is used as a proxy for demand on that module; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, lysosomal pH, membrane localisation and lipid pool sizes were not measured and are inferred only.", "Protein spots are mixtures with multiple candidate genes; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and the cathepsin/hydrolase spot interpretation assumes at least part of the signal in those spots derives from the named lysosomal candidate.", "The shared positive offset in both modalities (RNA median +1.46; protein-spot median +0.485, 70% positive) is assumed to contain a normalisation/composition component, so only relative, within-modality contrasts are interpreted.", "APOE4-associated lipid handling in microglia is background knowledge and is unverified here; no lipid, cholesterol, glycosphingolipid, oxygen-consumption or lysosomal-pH measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from or be influenced by the non-microglial partner; cell-type deconvolution is not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) mount a coordinate transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase module (led by sphingolipid and glycosidase enzymes GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, GAA, GLA and cathepsins B/D/K) together with a much stronger mitochondrial substrate-carrier and TCA/ETC module (MPC2, SLC25A1/5/11/46, MDH1, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, NDUFA5, UQCRC2), while glycolytic transcripts are not coordinately raised. We hypothesise that the primary rate-limiting step is luminal lysosomal degradation of APOE4-associated lipid cargo: the hydrolase transcript surge is a demand-driven compensation that is not matched at the level of mature lysosomal enzyme protein (2D-gel cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions and RNA and spot changes are uncorrelated), so undegraded lipid is instead routed to mitochondrial oxidation. Causality is not established by these data; the direction of the lysosome-to-mitochondrion link is inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of lysosomal glucocerebrosidase/hexosaminidase (e.g. conduritol-B-epoxide or GBA/HEXB knockdown) in isogenic APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature, i.e. raise the mitochondrial carrier/TCA transcript module (MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1, OGDH, ACO2) without a matching rise in HK2/PFKP. If APOE3 hydrolase inhibition raises lysosomal substrate but leaves the mitochondrial module unchanged, the proposed lysosome-to-mitochondrion causal link is wrong.", "Reciprocal rescue: augmenting lysosomal degradative capacity in APOE4 microglia (TFEB overexpression, recombinant/chaperone-boosted GBA, or acid-sphingomyelinase supplementation) should lower lysosomal glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin and normalise the mitochondrial carrier/TCA transcripts toward APOE3 while APOE4 genotype is unchanged. Persistence of the mitochondrial program after successful substrate clearance would weaken the mechanism.", "Flux discrimination: APOE4 microglia should show higher mitochondrial pyruvate-carrier- and citrate-carrier-dependent oxygen consumption (UK5099- and CTPI-sensitive OCR) with no proportional increase in glycolytic ECAR. Equal proportional increases in OCR and ECAR would instead indicate a generic biomass/normalisation shift and would weaken the mechanism.", "Protein-level test of the bottleneck: immunoblot or activity assay should show that mature (processed) cathepsin B/D and GBA activity per cell are NOT increased in proportion to their transcripts in APOE4, with an altered pro-form:mature ratio. If mature enzyme protein and activity scale with the transcript increase, the 'transcription without capacity' bottleneck is refuted and the data would instead support a successfully expanded, non-limiting lysosome.", "Interferon rejection test: unbiased profiling should show no coordinate type-I interferon signature in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia (no elevation of STAT1, ISG15, MX1, IFIT1-3, OAS1, USP18), and IFNAR1 blockade should not normalise the lysosomal or mitochondrial modules. Detection of a coherent ISG module plus IFNAR-dependent rescue would falsify this hypothesis in favour of an interferon-driven mechanism.", "Functional consequence: on an added lipid/phagocytic challenge (myelin debris or apoptotic-neuron feeding), APOE4 microglia should show earlier lysosomal substrate saturation, greater lipid-droplet accumulation and blunted incremental oxygen consumption relative to APOE3. Equal or superior handling of the challenge by APOE4 would weaken the 'narrowed degradative reserve' claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein handling and lipoprotein-associated lipid delivery increase the load of glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and sterol-ester cargo reaching the microglial endolysosome (inferred; the lipid pool itself is not measured here).", "Cargo accumulation raises a lysosomal-stress/TFEB-type transcriptional demand signal, seen as coordinate elevation of acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:GLA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H) and of endolysosomal trafficking transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:CHMP4B, gene:AP5M1).", "This transcriptional demand is not converted into proportional mature luminal hydrolase activity: mannose-6-phosphate targeting transcripts are internally discordant (gene:IGF2R up, gene:M6PR down), and cathepsin-bearing protein spots redistribute rather than uniformly rise (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 down), so degradative flux remains rate-limiting even though enzyme transcripts are high.", "Lipid that escapes lysosomal degradation is re-esterified/stored and partially exported to mitochondria, matched by increased expression of SREBP-linked acyl-chain remodelling and storage transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) and of the sterol/lipoprotein uptake receptor transcript gene:SCARB1.", "To oxidise this diverted carbon, APOE4 microglia upregulate mitochondrial substrate import and TCA/ETC machinery (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:TOMM22, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B) plus anaplerotic amino-acid entry (gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:SLC38A7).", "Because the compensation is oxidative rather than glycolytic, glycolytic transcripts are flat or reduced (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3 down), predicting an APOE4 state with raised mitochondrial substrate oxidation, persistent lysosomal substrate retention, and a narrowed reserve for handling an additional phagocytic lipid challenge."], "title": "Lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic capacity is the APOE4 bottleneck, forcing a compensatory mitochondrial substrate-oxidation program in mock-treated iPSC microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15459882583170254, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12379909252108966, "cosine_similarity": 0.3652332939440728, "direction_accuracy": 0.25728155339805825, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268446601941747, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15459882583170254, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12379909252108966, "cosine_similarity": 0.3652332939440728, "direction_accuracy": 0.25728155339805825, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268446601941747, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.78592175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 197}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_175", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no gene has |effect| \u003c 1 and 77% are positive); we assume that the relative representation of pathway members in this list is informative, and that the strong global positive shift is at least partly technical (normalisation/compositional), so only within-list contrasts are interpreted.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is not specified and is preserved as reported; only sign and rank are used, never fold-change arithmetic.", "2D-gel spots are not uniquely identified proteins; each carries several candidate genes, so spot-level directions constrain but do not prove the behaviour of any named protein, and a protein present in several spots may be redistributing between proteoforms rather than changing in total amount.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a noisy upper bound on the corresponding protein pool; the transcript-versus-spot mismatch is assumed to reflect translation, maturation, sorting or turnover, not purely gel detection limits.", "SREBP, TFEB and cargo-flux activities are inferred from target-gene abundance; no reporter, activity, cholesterol, lipid-droplet or trafficking measurement is supplied.", "Astrocyte co-culture composition and cell-type proportion differences between genotypes are assumed not to be the dominant driver of the RNA contrast; this is untested here."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference is best explained by a degradative bottleneck in the endolysosome rather than by an ER unfolded-protein response: lipid/lipoprotein cargo delivery genes and a MiT/TFEB CLEAR-network transcriptional program (hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits) are coordinately higher in APOE4, yet the 2D-gel spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits are not correspondingly higher (median +0.14 log2 versus +0.48 for other spots, with several significantly lower), so inferred luminal hydrolytic/egress capacity fails to track transcript supply; the resulting inferred shortfall of cholesterol reaching the ER sensing pool keeps SREBP target and uptake transcripts elevated and diverts sterol and fatty acid into esterification/storage enzymes. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should release free cholesterol to the ER sensing pool and lower SREBP-target transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA) largely unchanged. If SREBP targets stay elevated after esterification block, or if the CLEAR program collapses in parallel, Steps 4-6 are wrong.", "Capacity test: pulse-chase of fluorescent lipoprotein/myelin plus mature cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase activity assays should show, in APOE4, higher hydrolase mRNA but equal or lower mature enzymatic activity per cell and slower cargo clearance and slower lysosome-to-ER cholesterol egress. If mature hydrolase activity and clearance kinetics scale up with the mRNA increase and match or exceed APOE3, the central bottleneck claim fails.", "Compensation test: TFEB knockdown should worsen lipid/cholesterol accumulation and cargo-clearance delay disproportionately in APOE4 relative to APOE3; equal effects in both genotypes would argue the CLEAR induction is not compensatory.", "Bypass test: enhancing lysosomal cholesterol egress (cyclodextrin or NPC2 supplementation) should normalise APOE4 SREBP-target transcripts and esterification enzymes without needing to change hydrolase transcription; no normalisation would weaken the egress-limitation step.", "Negative prediction rejecting the ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 microglia should NOT show BiP/GRP94 induction, XBP1 splicing or ATF4/CHOP-driven translational attenuation above APOE3 under mock conditions; observing clear XBP1 splicing plus BiP protein induction in APOE4 would favour a UPR-centred mechanism over this one (currently the HSP90B1/HSPA5-candidate spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004 and protein_spot:005 are flat-to-lower and non-significant).", "Directionality control: if a proteoform-resolved measurement shows that the down-shifted cathepsin-candidate spots (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) reflect pro-to-mature processing shifts with unchanged total hydrolase protein and unchanged activity, the protein-level pillar of the argument is void."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_175", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and phagocytic cargo receptors and for late-endosomal transport machinery (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:TREM2), which we interpret - not observe - as increased delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts; inferred transcription-factor activity): a MiT/TFEB CLEAR-type program is transcriptionally higher (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) together with lysosomal hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSH), acidification machinery (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:CLCN7) and lysosomal membrane/transport genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:SLC38A7).", "Step 3 (measured spot abundance; inferred protein pool): the transcript increase is not mirrored by the corresponding 2D-gel spots. Spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins, HEXB or V-ATPase subunits are flat or significantly lower (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), while hydrolase-free spots are on average higher; hydrolase-maturation/sorting transcripts are internally discordant (gene:GNPTG and gene:IGF2R higher, gene:M6PR and gene:AP1M1 lower). We infer that mature, correctly delivered hydrolase and proton-pump capacity per unit cargo is the rate-limiting step.", "Step 4 (inferred localization of a sterol pool, not measured): because luminal hydrolysis/egress is limiting, less lipoprotein-derived cholesterol reaches the ER/PM sensing pool; the sterol-sensing machinery therefore continues to read a low-cholesterol state.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts; inferred SREBP activity): consistent with sustained SREBP signalling, sterol-synthesis and uptake transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1), which would reinforce Step 1 as a feed-forward loop.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts; predicted lipid phenotype, not measured here): overflow sterol and fatty acid are routed to esterification and neutral-lipid storage rather than efflux (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7), predicting cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet accumulation and sphingolipid substrate build-up in APOE4.", "Step 7 (specificity): the phenotype is metabolic/degradative rather than classical activation - homeostatic microglial identity transcripts persist (gene:CSF1R, gene:IRF8, gene:MAFB, gene:GPR34, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC) and no interferon-stimulated gene reached the supplied differential list."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal lipid-clearance capacity, not by ER unfolded-protein signalling: a TFEB/CLEAR transcriptional compensation that is not matched at the hydrolase protein level sustains sterol uptake, synthesis and esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19911014289406637, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18583387515716776, "cosine_similarity": 0.36492407447779873, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_175", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6313462783171522, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19911014289406637, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18583387515716776, "cosine_similarity": 0.36492407447779873, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6313462783171522, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.87126875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 198}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_075", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so enrichment was judged against the list's own strongly positive background (mean +1.39, 77.1% positive) rather than against an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is treated only ordinally.", "Transcript abundance of transporters, hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding protein amount and compartmental activity; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, sterol pool, lipid-droplet or flux measurement is supplied.", "The list-wide positive shift is assumed to be at least partly biological rather than purely a normalization or ambient-RNA artifact; all pathway claims are therefore stated relative to that background.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-unique: each spot carries several candidate genes, so spot-level changes are used only as weak concordance or counter-evidence, never as identification of a specific protein.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1/ABCG1, PLIN2, STARD3) are absent from the supplied rows and are assumed, not observed, to behave as the model requires.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic and equally differentiated, so transcript differences are not driven by differing microglial maturity or astrocyte co-culture composition.", "Causal direction is assumed, not established: the data are a single steady-state genotype contrast with no perturbation or time course."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the rate-limiting step of lipid handling is proposed to be export of sterol/lipid from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER, not uptake, lumenal hydrolysis, or ER protein folding. The discovery data show coordinated higher transcript levels for lipid/debris uptake receptors (13/13 positive), for TFEB and v-ATPase subunits (10/10 positive), and for lumenal lysosomal hydrolases (mean +3.25 versus a +1.39 list-wide background, permutation p=0.002), while genes for inter-organelle lipid transfer are not elevated (mean +0.62; OSBPL8 -1.90, VPS13B -4.65) and sterol-synthesis/SREBP-2 target transcripts remain uniformly positive (10/10, including LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, ACAT2) together with SREBF1 (+4.67) and SCD (+4.17). We interpret this as a futile cycle in which APOE4 microglia ingest and hydrolyse lipid but deliver too little sterol to the ER sensing pool, so biosynthetic and uptake programs stay on and surplus lipid is esterified (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72) and stored. All statements about flux, lysosomal pH, sterol pools, localization and causal direction are inferred, not measured; the assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is rejected because ERAD and ER-chaperone transcripts are not coherently elevated above the strong list-wide upward shift and ER-chaperone-containing protein spots are not significantly changed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Bypassing lysosomal egress with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or delivering cholesterol directly to the plasma membrane/ER) should lower the APOE4-specific excess of SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS) toward APOE3 levels while clearing unesterified sterol from LAMP1-positive compartments. If lysosomal sterol is demonstrably cleared yet the SREBP-2 target excess persists, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is weakened.", "Direct probing of sterol pools (ALOD4/D4H accessibility for ER/PM sterol, filipin or lysosome-fractionated sterol assay) should show higher unesterified sterol in the APOE4 endolysosomal fraction with equal or lower ER-accessible sterol. Equal or higher ER-accessible sterol in APOE4 despite elevated SREBP-2 targets would falsify the sensing step and point to SREBP-independent transcription.", "Blocking influx (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or withdrawal of myelin/lipoprotein cargo) should reduce the APOE4 elevation of v-ATPase and lumenal hydrolase transcripts but should leave SREBP-2 target transcripts unchanged or higher, because the ER pool becomes even more sterol-poor. If influx blockade lowers both arms in parallel, a simple whole-cell lipid-overload model fits better than a compartmental egress block.", "Lysosomal pH and bulk hydrolase activity (LysoSensor, DQ-BSA, Bodipy-substrate assays) should be similar or modestly improved in APOE4 relative to APOE3. Substantially alkalinized APOE4 lysosomes with reduced hydrolase activity would replace this mechanism with an acidification-failure model in which the v-ATPase and hydrolase transcript increases are failed compensation.", "Because the ER-proteostasis alternative is rejected, chemical UPR blockade (PERK or IRE1 inhibition) should not normalize the APOE4 lipid-gene signature; if PERK/IRE1 inhibition abolishes the SREBP and lysosomal transcript differences, the ER-stress mechanism supersedes this one.", "Immunoblot or targeted proteomics with unambiguous identification should confirm higher GBA/HEXA/CTSB-type hydrolase protein in APOE4; uniformly unchanged or lower hydrolase protein, consistent with the mixed cathepsin-containing spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069), would undercut step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with higher transcript abundance of phagocytic and lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:ITGB1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1); we infer, but did not measure, a correspondingly greater lipid and debris influx into the endolysosomal system.", "Ingested material is routed to an expanded degradative compartment: gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:PIK3C3 and ten v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C and others) are all positive, which we read as a CLEAR-type biogenesis/acidification response; acidification itself and lysosome number were not measured.", "Lumenal catabolic capacity for lipid substrates is transcriptionally amplified well beyond the list-wide background (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), implying that hydrolysis of sphingolipid, glycolipid and lipoprotein cargo is not the limiting step.", "The export arm that moves liberated sterol from the endolysosome limiting membrane to the ER (contact-site and lipid-transfer machinery) is not co-amplified: gene:OSBPL8 and gene:VPS13B are negative and gene:OSBPL1A, gene:VPS13C, gene:SCP2 give a set mean below background; NPC1 and LIPA transcripts are absent from the supplied rows. We designate this transfer step as the primary bottleneck (inferred, not measured).", "Because ER-accessible sterol is inferred to stay low, SREBP-2 and SREBP-1 target transcription remains engaged (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:ACAT2, gene:MYLIP, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1), sustaining de novo sterol and fatty-acid synthesis and further receptor-mediated uptake despite an already high lipid load.", "Surplus lipid that cannot reach regulatory ER pools is esterified and stored (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:MGLL) and accumulates in the endolysosome/lipid-droplet compartment, which we propose maintains the low-grade activation signature seen as gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL8, gene:NLRP3, gene:GPNMB and gene:C1QA/B/C."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain a lysosomal lipid-egress bottleneck: influx and lumenal hydrolysis capacity are transcriptionally amplified while lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer is not, keeping SREBP-driven synthesis switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27734187497692275, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21853006144694279, "cosine_similarity": 0.36490658444198104, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976407766990292, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27734187497692275, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21853006144694279, "cosine_similarity": 0.36490658444198104, "direction_accuracy": 0.2669902912621359, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976407766990292, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.74158875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 199}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_036", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |reported log FC| \u003e= 1.0 and all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 up, mean +1.39); all pathway claims here are made relative to that shifted background by permutation, and absence of a gene from the list means 'not in the selected set', not 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are therefore compared only within the RNA modality and never converted to protein-scale log2 values.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes/transporters; no enzymatic activity, transport flux, organelle pH, protein localization or lipid pool was measured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence that a named protein changed.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so part of the microglial transcriptional difference may be an indirect response to APOE4 astrocytes rather than microglia-autonomous; replicate number was not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values may be inflated by pseudoreplication of cells.", "Direction of causation is assumed for exposition only; these are steady-state associations at one timepoint (day 30) and causality has not been established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 not by an interferon or NF-kB inflammatory program but by a coherent transcriptional state in which lipid/lipoprotein uptake and endolysosomal catabolic machinery are elevated while sterol export from the endolysosome to the ER is rate-limiting; the resulting low ER-sensed sterol keeps the SREBP-target synthesis program on, and the excess sterol and fatty acid are inferred to be routed to SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent neutral-lipid storage, with elevated electron-transport-chain and acetyl-CoA-supply transcripts as a coupled compensatory arm. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, localization, lipid pools and causality are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should relieve the esterification sink, raise ER-accessible free cholesterol, and therefore suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR) and reduce neutral-lipid droplets substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3. If SREBP-2 targets stay elevated in APOE4 after SOAT1 inhibition, the 'ER senses sterol deficiency because egress is blocked' step is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Direct lipid test: APOE4 microglia should show a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio and more filipin-positive endolysosomal cholesterol than APOE3 under mock. Finding equal or lower esterified cholesterol, or free cholesterol accumulating at the plasma membrane/ER rather than in LAMP1+ compartments, would falsify the egress-bottleneck claim.", "Egress rescue: providing an egress bypass (cyclodextrin, or NPC1/ABCA1 overexpression) should normalize the APOE4 SREBP-target and TFEB/v-ATPase transcript elevation; if the lysosomal-biogenesis module remains elevated after cholesterol egress is restored, then lysosomal expansion is an independent APOE4 phenotype rather than a downstream compensation.", "Metabolic test: despite up-regulated ETC transcripts, APOE4 microglia are predicted to show reduced glycolytic rate (extracellular acidification) because of HK2 loss, with equal or increased ATP-linked oxygen consumption and increased dependence on fatty-acid oxidation (etomoxir sensitivity). Observing increased glycolysis or unchanged/decreased respiration would weaken steps 5-6.", "Negative prediction for the assigned focus: blocking type-I interferon (JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade) or NF-kB (IKK inhibition) under mock conditions should not normalize the APOE4 lysosomal, sterol or ETC transcript modules. If JAK or IKK inhibition collapses these modules, an inflammatory/interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "Targeted RNA/protein follow-up: canonical ISGs (ISG15, MX1, OAS1, IFIT1/3, STAT1, B2M, HLA class I) are predicted to be at most weakly changed (well below the +1.39 median shift of this list) in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock; a coherent ISG module at or above the list-wide shift would falsify the 'no interferon signature' component."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), which we infer increases delivery of lipid cargo into the endolysosome; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): A coordinated TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-biogenesis module is elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, 8/8 detected v-ATPase subunits up, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2; module mean +3.05, permutation p=0.002 against the list's own positively shifted background), consistent with an expanded, more acidified degradative compartment responding to lipid load.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck, inferred): Despite this catabolic expansion, movement of liberated free cholesterol out of the endolysosome to the ER membrane pool is limiting in APOE4. Direct egress components (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA) are absent from the supplied selected DE list, so the bottleneck is inferred from its downstream signature, not observed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Because ER-accessible sterol stays low, the SREBP arm is not switched off: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCD +4.17 remain elevated, i.e. a futile synthesis-plus-uptake loop that adds to, rather than relieves, the lipid load.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Carbon for this loop is inferred to come from non-glycolytic acetyl-CoA supply: gene:ACSS2 +2.93 and gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 are up while the first committed glycolytic step is down (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08) even though glucose transporters and gene:HIF1A are up, so glucose-to-lactate flux is predicted to be reduced rather than increased.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): 38/38 detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (NDUF*, UQCR*, COX*, ATP5*, SDHB) are up (mean +2.81, permutation p=0.0003), together with gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B/G, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, indicating increased oxidative and fatty-acid-oxidation capacity that we interpret as a compensatory arm coupled to lipid disposal, not as evidence of increased respiration per se.", "Step 7 (predicted end state, unmeasured): Sterol and fatty acid that can neither be exported nor fully oxidized are esterified (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) and stored, predicting a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio and greater neutral-lipid droplet burden in APOE4. No lipid species was measured in this dataset."], "title": "Endolysosomal cholesterol/lipid egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, forcing esterification-and-storage routing with compensatory lysosomal and oxidative expansion (no interferon signature)"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28419119004541593, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2732628468376222, "cosine_similarity": 0.3648539936067439, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078867313915858, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28419119004541593, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2732628468376222, "cosine_similarity": 0.3648539936067439, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078867313915858, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73101425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 200}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_015", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and 77% are positive), so pathway claims rest on enrichment relative to that biased upward background, not on absolute direction.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative magnitudes and signs are used.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; the downward group shift of hydrolase/v-ATPase-containing spots is treated as weak, non-identifying evidence and could instead reflect co-migrating actin/keratin candidates or redistribution of a protein between spots (e.g. pro- versus mature cathepsin forms).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for demand, not for hydrolytic activity, lysosomal pH, sterol localisation or SREBP cleavage state, none of which were measured.", "Lipid, cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content were not measured in the supplied data; storage phenotypes are predictions, not observations.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript changes may be non-cell-autonomous, and causal direction between APOE4 genotype and the lysosomal/SREBP state is not established by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, transcript-level expansion of the lipid-uptake and lysosomal hydrolase/acidification program is not matched by a corresponding increase in lysosomal hydrolase protein spots, so internalised cholesterol and sphingolipid are inferred to be retained in the endolysosome; the ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol pool therefore stays low, SREBP target transcription (SREBF1/2, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, SCD, AGPAT2) and SOAT1 remain elevated, and lipid is inferred to be routed into esterified/stored pools rather than returned to the ER for feedback. The ER unfolded-protein-response arm is not supported by these data and is explicitly rejected as the primary bottleneck.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: bypassing the lysosomal step with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or acute lysosomal cholesterol mobilisation) in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP target transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS) and SOAT1 toward APOE3 levels within hours while leaving APOE4 genotype unchanged; if SREBP targets stay elevated after lysosomal cholesterol is mobilised, the lysosome-to-ER return step is not the bottleneck and the mechanism is weakened.", "Mature cathepsin B/D and beta-hexosaminidase enzymatic activity, and v-ATPase-dependent lysosomal acidification, should be flat or reduced in APOE4 despite the large transcript increases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A); if activity scales with transcript level, the post-transcriptional bottleneck is falsified.", "SOAT1 inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/droplet storage and increase free-sterol-dependent feedback (lower SREBF2/LDLR/HMGCS1) without normalising the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program; normalisation of the hydrolase program by SOAT1 inhibition would invert the proposed causal order and weaken the mechanism.", "Loading with cholesterol-rich substrate (myelin debris or acetylated LDL) should widen the APOE4-versus-APOE3 gap in retained lysosomal sterol and in SREBP target transcripts; equal handling by both genotypes under load would weaken the mechanism.", "TFEB overexpression alone should not rescue APOE4 lipid storage if the block is post-transcriptional; full rescue by TFEB would favour a purely transcriptional-capacity model instead.", "ER-proteostasis rejection test: APOE4 cells should show no increase in ER chaperone protein or in XBP1 splicing and ATF4/CHOP protein relative to APOE3 under mock conditions; a clear UPR protein signature would revive the rejected ER-stress alternative."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalisation receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), which is inferred to increase lipid flux into the endolysosomal system; the internalised lipid pool itself was not measured.", "A coordinated lysosomal transcriptional program is elevated above the strongly upward global background (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:LAMP1), consistent with a demand signal for degradative capacity.", "Protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are, as a group, shifted downward relative to other spots (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:058), so the transcriptional program is inferred not to translate into proportionally increased mature hydrolase abundance/activity; hydrolase activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "The resulting inferred shortfall in hydrolytic and sterol-export throughput retains cholesterol and sphingolipid within the endolysosome (retention is inferred, not measured; gene:NPC2 and gene:GBA transcripts are up while NPC1, LIPA and ASAH1 are not in the supplied rows).", "Because sterol reaching the ER sensing pool stays low, SREBP-dependent transcription remains active despite lipid loading (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:SCD); activation state of SREBP protein was not measured.", "Elevated esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5) are inferred to divert free sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol pools, so newly made and imported lipid is sequestered rather than feeding back on synthesis.", "The combination sustains a futile cycle: continued uptake and synthesis with limited lysosomal catabolic return, predicted to manifest as increased esterified-lipid storage in APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3, without requiring an ER unfolded-protein response (gene:PDIA3, gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1 are decreased; protein_spot:005, protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:016 show no chaperone increase)."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-clearance throughput, not ER proteostasis, is the APOE4 bottleneck: endolysosomal sterol/sphingolipid retention keeps the ER-accessible sterol pool low and locks SREBP-driven synthesis plus SOAT1 esterification on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21797806742236825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17866855599431766, "cosine_similarity": 0.3646876987687197, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078705501618122, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21797806742236825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17866855599431766, "cosine_similarity": 0.3646876987687197, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6078705501618122, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.793292, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 201}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_021", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 1705 up / 507 down, unspecified logarithm base) drawn from two parallel up/down workbook columns; the correct null for direction is therefore ~77% up, not 50/50, and absent genes (e.g. all cytosolic ribosomal, mitoribosomal, interferon-stimulated and most mitochondrial-biogenesis regulator genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The list-wide up-shift also affects other nuclear housekeeping families (spliceosome 16/16 up, median +2.18; EIF/EEF 10/11 up, median +4.59), so the nuclear OXPHOS increase alone is not treated as a specific finding; the mechanism rests mainly on the discordant direction of mtDNA-encoded transcripts and on programs (lysosome, lipid uptake, glycolytic commitment) whose internal contrasts survive that bias.", "10X Flex probe-based quantification of mtDNA-encoded transcripts and per-cell normalisation are assumed comparable between genotypes; if APOE4 cells differ in total RNA content or mitochondrial probe capture, the discordance could be technical.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (keratins/actins frequent); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot direction changes may reflect isoform/processing redistribution rather than total protein amount.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly predictive of the corresponding protein and pathway capacity; enzyme activities, respiratory flux, lysosomal degradative flux, complex assembly and organelle localisation were not measured and causality is not established.", "Astrocyte co-culture composition is assumed matched between genotypes; a genotype-dependent difference in the astrocyte compartment or in microglial capture could contribute to the apparent programs."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the most interpretable difference is a mitonuclear discordance: every represented nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcript is higher (38/38, median +2.64 on the reported log scale) together with TCA, mitochondrial-carrier and import transcripts, while 4 of the 6 represented mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are lower - a direction that runs against the list-wide 77% up bias. We propose this reflects a relative shortfall of mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores against an amplified nuclear mitochondrial program, and that APOE4 microglia hold ATP/precursor supply by expanding lysosomal-hydrolytic and lipid-uptake routing (TFEB, v-ATPase subunits, GAA, GBA, HEXA/B, SMPD1, CTSB/CTSD, SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, SREBF1/SCD) rather than by committing glucose to glycolysis (HK2, PFKP, HK3 lower). All statements are about measured RNA/protein-spot abundance; respiratory flux, complex assembly and lysosomal degradative flux were not measured and the causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective (decisive for the core step): in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, blue-native PAGE / immunoblot should show a lower ratio of mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-CO1, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) to nuclear subunits (NDUFB8, ATP5F1B, UQCRC2) and no proportional increase in assembled complex I/IV/V despite the elevated nuclear transcripts; if APOE4 shows an equal or higher mtDNA-encoded:nuclear protein ratio and proportionally more assembled complexes, the mitonuclear-discordance step is falsified.", "Prospective (adaptation vs failed compensation): Seahorse in mock conditions should show basal OCR in APOE4 similar to or only modestly above APOE3 but maximal (FCCP-driven) OCR and spare respiratory capacity not increased in proportion to the ~4-6x transcript elevation; if maximal OCR and ATP-linked respiration scale with the transcript increase, the successful-increased-throughput alternative is favoured and this mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective (routing dependence): acute lysosomal blockade (bafilomycin A1) or lysosomal acid lipase inhibition (lalistat-2) should reduce ATP-linked OCR and raise the ADP/ATP ratio more in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas hexokinase/glycolysis blockade (2-deoxyglucose, or glucose withdrawal) should be tolerated similarly or better by APOE4; equal lysosomal dependence in both genotypes, or greater APOE4 sensitivity to 2-DG, would weaken the re-routing claim.", "Prospective (identity disambiguation of the strongest protein change): targeted immunoblot/MS of the +2 to +3 log2 spot train (protein_spot:043-046) should detect increased ANXA1 rather than TALDO1 protein, consistent with gene:ANXA1 +4.2 and gene:TALDO1 -2.3; if TALDO1 protein is the increased species, the assumed transcript-protein coupling underlying the mechanism is undermined for this dataset.", "Prospective (specificity control for the list-wide up-shift): spike-in normalised bulk RNA-seq or single-molecule FISH for MT-ND4/MT-CO2 versus NDUFA5/MPC2 in the same cells should reproduce opposite directions for mtDNA- and nuclear-encoded transcripts; if all measured transcripts shift up together after spike-in normalisation, the discordance is an artefact of relative normalisation and the mechanism fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, APOE4 vs APOE3 mock): a broad nuclear transcriptional up-shift includes a fully concordant mitochondrial oxidative module - all represented NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDHB subunits (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7 +5.7, gene:ATP5ME +5.2, gene:UQCRC2 +4.0, gene:COX7A2 +3.4), TCA/shuttle enzymes (gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:DLD +5.5, gene:ACO2 +3.5), substrate carriers and import components (gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:SLC25A46 +8.8, gene:SLC25A11 +4.5, gene:TOMM22 +4.6, gene:TIMM44 +2.5).", "Step 2 (measured, direction opposite to list background): mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts are mostly lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.4, gene:MT-CYB -2.3, gene:MT-ND4 -1.8, gene:MT-CO2 -1.3; exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +2.0, gene:MT-ND5 +1.9). Inferred, not measured: the nuclear:mtDNA subunit ratio is shifted, so holoenzyme assembly rather than nuclear subunit supply becomes the plausible limiting node for added respiratory capacity.", "Step 3 (measured): a coordinated lysosomal/CLEAR-type program is higher (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.3, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.7, gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:CTSK +7.4), together with lipid/lipoprotein uptake and esterification transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:APOE +1.2, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2). Inferred: increased delivery of lipid-derived substrate to lysosomes and thence to mitochondria.", "Step 4 (measured, contrast within the same up-biased list): committed glycolytic steps are not co-elevated and are partly lower (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:HK3 -1.1) despite higher glucose-transport/HIF transcripts (gene:SLC2A1 +2.4, gene:SLC2A3 +3.7, gene:HIF1A +2.0). Inferred: routing of carbon toward mitochondrial oxidation of lysosome-derived substrate rather than glycolytic commitment.", "Step 5 (protein-level compatibility test, ambiguous identities): no mitochondrial-candidate spot is significantly increased (protein_spot:059 [PHB/ACTB/VIM/KRT10/KRT1] +0.38 ns; protein_spot:074 [RAC2/SOD2/KRT10/RHOG/PRDX1] +0.38 ns; protein_spot:050 [ANXA1/KRT1/KRT10/MDH1/KRT9] -0.48 ns; protein_spot:020 [GLUD1/FSCN1/ENO1/G6PD/EPX] +0.38 ns), and cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58 vs protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38). Inferred: the transcriptional program is not matched by a demonstrable increase in mitochondrial or bulk hydrolase protein, consistent with re-routing/processing changes rather than proven capacity gain.", "Step 6 (state consequence in the measured mock condition): APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-dependent, oxidatively-biased catabolic state with a stress/remodelling signature (protein_spot:043 +1.96, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, all significant; candidates include ANXA1, TALDO1, PSMD7, ACTB, and gene:ANXA1 +4.2 is compatible while gene:TALDO1 -2.3 is not). Prospective only: reduced spare respiratory capacity and reduced glycolytic fallback would be revealed by challenge, not asserted as an ongoing deficit in mock."], "title": "Mitonuclear expression discordance with lysosome-fed catabolic re-routing in mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24033526566480817, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2757065698050843, "cosine_similarity": 0.36450814006085847, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6136699029126214, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24033526566480817, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2757065698050843, "cosine_similarity": 0.36450814006085847, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6136699029126214, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.37840025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 46}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are pre-filtered differential-expression results (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) in a logarithm of unspecified base; all set-level inference is therefore made relative to the dataset's own global median (+1.46) rather than to zero, and absolute fold changes are not interpreted.", "The dataset-wide positive RNA shift (77% of rows up) is treated as a possible normalization, composition or selection artifact, not as evidence of global transcriptional activation.", "Transcript abundance is not equated with protein abundance, enzyme activity, lysosomal acidification, or degradative flux; every flux, localization and causal statement in the mechanism is labelled as inferred.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each, so CTSB/CTSD/HEXB/GNS assignments are ambiguous and are used only to argue that no consistent hydrolase protein increase is demonstrated, never as identified proteins.", "No lipid, lipid-droplet, cholesterol, sphingolipid, LysoTracker, pH or flux measurement is supplied in this workbook; lysosomal substrate accumulation is a prediction of the model, not an observation.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture and biological replicate numbers are not supplied, so genotype-intrinsic microglial attribution and statistical power are both assumed rather than shown.", "Background pathway memberships (CLEAR/MiT-TFE targets, SREBP targets, lysosomal storage enzymes) come from unverified background knowledge, as literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a rate limitation in lysosomal luminal catabolism of lipoprotein-derived and glycosphingolipid cargo: the coordinated elevation of every measured MiT/TFE (CLEAR) transcript, led by acid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) and v-ATPase subunits, is read as a compensatory transcriptional response to unresolved luminal substrate load rather than as evidence of increased degradative flux, and it is accompanied by a de novo lipogenic/sterol-synthetic and lipid-esterification program consistent with cytosolic/ER sterol sensing remaining low while lipid is retained in the endolysosome. The canonical type I interferon module is absent from these data and inflammatory-named genes are, as a group, no higher than the global RNA shift, so an interferon-driven mechanism is not supported.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely lowering lysosomal lipid/glycosphingolipid substrate load in APOE4 microglia without touching genotype (e.g. 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, an ACAT/SOAT1 inhibitor, or lipoprotein-free medium plus SCARB1/LDLR knockdown) should collapse the CLEAR transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, TFEB) toward APOE3 levels and simultaneously normalize the SREBP-axis transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, INSIG1). If the CLEAR and SREBP transcript differences persist unchanged after verified reduction of lysosomal lipid, the bottleneck is not substrate load and this mechanism is weakened.", "Flux test: with a fluorogenic in-cell assay, APOE4 microglia should show lower substrate turnover per unit hydrolase protein (DQ-BSA, fluorogenic GBA/HEXA substrates, Bodipy-cholesteryl-ester clearance) together with higher LysoTracker/filipin/neutral-lipid staining than APOE3. Equal or higher per-cell degradative flux with no lipid or LysoTracker difference would falsify the central 'flux, not transcription' claim and favour a straightforward TFEB-driven biogenesis gain instead.", "Compensation-versus-driver test: TFEB knockdown should reduce hydrolase transcripts and make lysosomal lipid accumulation worse in APOE4 than in APOE3. If TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid accumulation, the CLEAR program is a driver rather than a compensation and step 3 fails.", "Delivery-arm test: restoring mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery or autophagosome-lysosome fusion (M6PR or STX17 re-expression) should raise mature hydrolase protein and clearance in APOE4 with little further change in hydrolase mRNA. No change in clearance would weaken step 4.", "Negative control that separates this model from the assigned focus: JAK1/2 or IFNAR blockade should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal and lipogenic transcript differences essentially intact. Substantial normalization by interferon blockade would support an interferon mechanism and weaken this one.", "Ordering prediction: in a time course from the HPC stage, elevation of SCARB1 and the lipogenic/esterification transcripts should precede or coincide with, and never follow, the CLEAR hydrolase elevation in APOE4. CLEAR elevation appearing first, with lipid uptake genes lagging, would contradict the proposed causal order."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and opsonic recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE); we infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of cholesteryl-ester- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred activity): luminal hydrolysis of that cargo becomes rate-limiting; the limiting quantity is catalytic flux per lysosome (hydrolase protein delivery, saturable acidification, activator/substrate access), not hydrolase mRNA, which is elevated.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): sustained substrate load engages MiT/TFE-family transcription (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) and the CLEAR output; all 35 measured CLEAR-type genes are positive, with acid hydrolases shifted above the dataset-wide RNA up-shift (set median +2.75 vs global +1.46, one-sided permutation p=0.014) and v-ATPase subunits uniformly positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51).", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred causal direction): the compensation is incomplete because the hydrolase delivery/fusion arm does not follow: gene:M6PR is decreased (-1.72) and gene:STX17 is decreased (-2.06) while gene:IGF2R and gene:RAB7A rise, and the 2-D protein spots whose candidate lists include CTSD, CTSB or HEXB change in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 and protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 down), so no net increase in mature hydrolase protein is demonstrated.", "Step 5 (inferred localization and flux): lipid retained in the lysosomal lumen keeps ER/cytosolic sterol sensing in a lipid-poor state, which is consistent with the elevated SREBP-axis transcripts (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) and with re-esterification/storage enzymes (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ABCA7, gene:NPC2, gene:CH25H); this closes a feed-forward loop that returns further neutral lipid to the same compartment.", "Step 6 (secondary, weakly supported): the modest, non-interferon chemokine elevation (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL1) is placed downstream of chronic lysosomal/lipid stress rather than upstream of it, because type I interferon-stimulated genes are essentially unrepresented and immune-named genes as a class sit at or below the global RNA median."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lysosomal lipid/glycosphingolipid clearance bottleneck with compensatory MiT/TFE CLEAR transcription, not an interferon program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12824096627506296, "cosine_similarity": 0.3641811558187406, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6372880258899676, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12824096627506296, "cosine_similarity": 0.3641811558187406, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6372880258899676, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.92322875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 202}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_071", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with an unspecified logarithm base; module enrichment is therefore judged only against the other selected rows, not against an unbiased transcriptome, and effect magnitudes are not compared with the log2 protein values.", "Coordinate transcript increases across a physically defined complex (nuclear OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes, acid hydrolases) reflect a regulated program rather than a gene-length, GC or high-expression normalisation bias of the 10X Flex per-cell scaling.", "The mtDNA-encoded decrease reflects mitochondrial transcript content per cell and is not purely a compositional consequence of normalising against a nuclear program that is itself increased.", "2D-gel spots are mixtures of candidate proteins; direction of a spot is treated as evidence about proteoform distribution only, never as identification of a named protein's total abundance.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme availability; enzymatic activity, mitochondrial membrane potential, lysosomal pH, lipid-droplet content and acyl-chain composition were not measured in this dataset.", "Astrocyte co-culture, day-30 differentiation state and replicate structure (not supplied in the workbook) are comparable between the APOE4 and APOE3 lines, so the difference is genotype-attributable rather than a differentiation-stage difference."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional amplification of lipid uptake and lysosomal acid hydrolysis together with the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery, while the mtDNA-encoded respiratory subunit transcripts and the redox-defence set behave as if terminal electron-transport output is the limiting step; the resulting mismatch between substrate delivery and oxidative disposal is predicted to route lysosome-derived and citrate-derived carbon into SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent monounsaturated neutral-lipid esters and to leave sphingolipid substrates unresolved. Only transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances were measured; every flux, activity and localisation statement here is inferred, and no causal direction has been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (or DGAT1 inhibition) should collapse the excess neutral-lipid ester pool and raise free saturated fatty acid and lipotoxic/ER-stress readouts, while leaving the nuclear OXPHOS and lysosomal hydrolase transcript amplification largely intact; if the APOE4-versus-APOE3 neutral-lipid excess is unchanged by SCD1/DGAT1 inhibition, step 5 and the esterification arm are wrong.", "Respirometry with mitochondrial-mass normalisation: despite markedly higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, APOE4 maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) oxygen consumption and spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass should be equal to or lower than APOE3, and BN-PAGE assembled complex III/IV/V should not scale with subunit transcript increases. A proportional increase in maximal respiration and in assembled complexes would falsify the proposed bottleneck (step 4).", "Lipidomic prediction for the same mock comparison: APOE4 should show a higher triacylglycerol + cholesteryl-ester fraction with elevated desaturation index (16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0) and retained glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin species, with total glycerophospholipid roughly unchanged. A lipidome showing lower neutral lipid or depleted sphingolipid substrates in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Stable-isotope tracing (U-13C palmitate or 13C-glucose): APOE4 should oxidise a smaller fraction of label to CO2 and incorporate a larger fraction into TAG/CE than APOE3; equal oxidised fractions would weaken steps 4-5.", "Demand test: blocking upstream substrate delivery (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/acid-hydrolase inhibition, or SCARB1 blockade) should attenuate the APOE4-specific nuclear OXPHOS and TCA transcript amplification if that amplification is demand-driven; persistence of the full OXPHOS signature under substrate blockade would argue for a lysosome-independent, cell-intrinsic mitochondrial program instead.", "Technical falsifier: if the nuclear OXPHOS/TCA enrichment disappears when tested against an expression- and length-matched background from the full unbiased transcriptome, or if the mitonuclear protein ratio (mtDNA-encoded COX1 versus VDAC or nuclear NDUFB8) is unchanged between genotypes, the central asymmetry of this hypothesis is not real."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lysosomal biogenesis (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:GAA), which we infer increases delivery of lipid substrate into the endolysosome; the lipid pool itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Acid hydrolases acting on sphingolipids and glycolipids are coordinately higher (gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2), consistent with a demand-driven expansion of lysosomal lipid hydrolysis rather than with a completed catabolic step; the 2D-gel cathepsin spot train is split up and down (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), so mature hydrolase protein is not shown to scale with transcript.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): The nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery is amplified as a single coherent block above the strong global positive shift - 37/37 measured nuclear OXPHOS subunits up (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2), 8/8 TCA enzymes up (gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD) and mitochondrial carriers up (gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5) - which we read as a compensatory/anticipatory demand signature, not as demonstrated respiration.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, inferred): Terminal respiratory-chain output does not scale with this nuclear program: mtDNA-encoded subunits of complexes III/IV/V are lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.4, gene:MT-CYB -2.3, gene:MT-CO2 -1.3) and the thiol/peroxide defence set is uniformly raised (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17), as expected when electron flux is delivered to an under-stoichiometric chain.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Carbon that is not terminally oxidised is predicted to leave the matrix as citrate and be re-esterified: the citrate/malate shuttle components (gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1) and the SREBP1-linked desaturation and esterification genes (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) are all higher in APOE4.", "Step 6 (predicted, unmeasured phenotype): The net APOE4 lipid state should therefore be an enlarged neutral-lipid ester pool (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester) with a raised monounsaturated:saturated acyl ratio, accompanied by retained glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin substrates, rather than a global loss of membrane phospholipid."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify a lysosome-to-mitochondria lipid catabolic program whose terminal oxidative step does not scale, diverting acyl carbon into desaturated neutral-lipid esters"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08610567514677103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2220163941405462, "cosine_similarity": 0.36414154702423196, "direction_accuracy": 0.14401294498381878, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5977540453074434, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08610567514677103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2220163941405462, "cosine_similarity": 0.36414154702423196, "direction_accuracy": 0.14401294498381878, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5977540453074434, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86752, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 203}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_056", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, 77% positive, median +1.46) in an unspecified log base; genes absent from the list (including core ISGs, ABCA1/ABCG1, PLIN2, FASN, ASAH1) are unknown, not unchanged, and program calls are made relative to this skewed background, not a 50/50 expectation.", "Program membership was fixed from canonical pathway rosters that include members absent from the list; no member was dropped because its direction disagreed, so exceptions (gene:CTSS, gene:GPAT3, gene:ACSL4/5, gene:TNFAIP3, gene:MT-ND4L/ND5) are retained.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to index, but does not measure, hydrolase activity, respiratory flux, beta-oxidation, lipogenic flux, droplet content or lysosomal pH; no flux, activity, localisation or lipid measurement is supplied here.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (median 5 candidate identities per spot; keratins/ACTB dominate) and are used only for compatibility: e.g. spots whose candidate lists contain CTSD/CTSB/GNS/HEXB/ACP2 change in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.58 up; protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 down). No spot is treated as confirming an individual protein.", "Both modalities show a global upward shift (RNA 77% positive; protein 38 significant up vs 9 down, median +0.48), so direction alone is weak evidence and normalisation/composition artefacts cannot be excluded.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; some signal may derive from non-microglial cells or from genotype effects on the astrocyte partner. mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification on a probe-based 10X Flex assay is treated as low-confidence (unverified background knowledge).", "Storage-biased routing is claimed for the measured mock condition; any reduced oxidative or degradative reserve would only be revealed by a future challenge and is not asserted as an ongoing defect. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and TFEB, for TCA/mitochondrial-carrier and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits, and for SREBP-linked desaturation/esterification enzymes are jointly elevated well beyond the strong upward bias of this selected differential-expression list, while mitochondrially encoded ETC transcripts are not. We propose that APOE4 increases endolysosomal lipid substrate load and hydrolytic release of fatty acids/sterols/sphingoid bases, and that this liberated carbon is preferentially re-esterified into neutral lipid (triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester, monounsaturated species) instead of being fully oxidised, producing a storage-biased lipidome in the unchallenged state; this is a state/routing change, not an established causal bottleneck, and it is not an interferon or classical inflammatory activation state.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics on the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher neutral lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester, increased TG/phospholipid ratio) and MUFA-enriched (16:1, 18:1) glycerolipid species in APOE4, plus shifted hexosylceramide/ceramide intermediates. If TG and CE are unchanged or lower in APOE4 despite the elevated SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 transcripts, the storage-routing claim is weakened.", "Prospective perturbation: DGAT1 inhibition (or SCD inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should reduce droplet TG and divert liberated fatty acid to oxidation, raising basal and fatty-acid-dependent oxygen consumption more in APOE4 than APOE3. If APOE4 cells cannot raise oxygen consumption after DGAT1/SCD inhibition (or show lower basal OCR than APOE3 despite 37/37 positive nuclear OXPHOS transcripts), the mechanism should be replaced by a mitochondrial-capacity/failed-compensation model.", "Prospective perturbation: blocking lysosomal acidification or hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/acid-lipase inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should lower the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 transcript elevation and neutral-lipid accumulation, because the mechanism makes hydrolytic substrate release upstream of esterification. If lipogenic transcripts and droplet content are unaffected by lysosomal blockade, the proposed lysosome-to-esterification causal step fails.", "Prospective specificity test: type-I interferon receptor blockade or JAK inhibition under mock should not abolish the APOE4 lysosomal/mitochondrial/lipogenic transcript differences or the lipid phenotype. Substantial reversal would indicate an interferon-driven state and falsify the rejection of the interferon focus.", "Prospective mito-nuclear test: quantify mtDNA-encoded protein subunits (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6) versus nuclear subunits and mtDNA copy number in APOE4 vs APOE3. Proportionate protein-level increases with intact complex assembly support the increased-capacity reading; a selective mtDNA-encoded subunit or assembly deficit would favour the competing failed-compensation mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters lipoprotein/lipid handling by microglia (APOE itself is modestly higher, gene:APOE +1.24; scavenger/uptake transcripts gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50), increasing lipid substrate delivered to the endolysosomal system (uptake flux itself not measured).", "A coordinated lysosomal/degradative transcript program is elevated far above the selected-list background (25 of 26 represented members positive; gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51), consistent with expanded hydrolytic capacity that liberates free fatty acids, sterols and sphingoid bases; the notable exception is gene:CTSS -5.57.", "Mitochondrial catabolic machinery is up as a block: pyruvate/citrate/malate handling and anaplerosis (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56) and 37/37 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits positive (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02), with import/translation support (gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:TUFM +6.46): oxidative capacity is being built, but flux is not measured.", "Mitochondrial citrate export (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47) plus acetate activation (gene:ACSS2 +2.93) supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA to an SREBP-linked lipogenic/esterification arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), together with droplet turnover (gene:MGLL +4.00).", "Because mitochondrially encoded ETC transcripts are not co-elevated (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +1.95, gene:MT-ND5 +1.93), terminal oxidative disposal is unlikely to scale with hydrolytic release, so the predicted net APOE4 phenotype under mock is storage-biased routing: higher triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester content, MUFA-enriched (16:1/18:1) glycerolipids, and altered glycosphingolipid/ceramide intermediates.", "This state is accompanied by, but not driven by, inflammatory signalling: NF-kB/chemokine members (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CCL2 +2.12) are indistinguishable from the list-wide 77%-positive background and are accompanied by inhibitors (gene:NFKBIL1 +4.41, gene:NFKBIZ +3.07) and by gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05, while core type-I interferon effectors are absent from the selected list and the few represented members are small (gene:IFI16 +1.25, gene:IFNAR1 +1.41, gene:TMEM173 +1.22); the interferon/inflammation focus is therefore rejected as the primary mechanism."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-plus-mitochondrial catabolic state whose liberated lipid carbon is routed into esterification and storage rather than inflammatory/interferon activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19672857512092456, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24953734171690212, "cosine_similarity": 0.3638498031872878, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057734627831716, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19672857512092456, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24953734171690212, "cosine_similarity": 0.3638498031872878, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057734627831716, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.122753, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 47}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list-wide up-shift (2212 rows, 77% positive, median +1.46) is treated as a technical/selection baseline, and only enrichment relative to that baseline is used as evidence.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified; effects are used ordinally and comparatively, never as absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but not to demonstrate, protein amount, enzyme activity, organelle acidification, lipid localization or metabolic flux; every activity, flux and localization statement above is inferred.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not treated as identifications; no spot is used as evidence that a specific protein changed.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences could reflect altered microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange or cell-composition/ambient-RNA effects rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 biology.", "No lipid, sterol, filipin, lysosomal pH or flux measurement is supplied, so the storage and retention pools invoked in steps 3 and 5 are predictions, not observations.", "Replicate number was not supplied, so per-gene p-values cannot be independently weighted; set-level direction consistency is used instead.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment is assumed to be the only systematic difference."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling: transcript modules for lysosome biogenesis/hydrolysis (CLEAR-type) and for SREBP-driven sterol and monounsaturated-fatty-acid synthesis plus esterification are coordinately elevated above the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list, whereas genes for sterol egress from the lysosome are not. The most parsimonious mechanistic reading is that egress/redistribution of lysosome-derived cholesterol and sphingolipid catabolites (an inferred flux, not measured here) limits delivery of sterol to the ER sensing pool; the cell responds by expanding lysosomal catabolic capacity and by de novo sterol/MUFA synthesis, whose products are re-esterified (SOAT1, DGAT1) into a storage pool rather than restoring ER sterol. Causality is not established by these data; interferon or NF-kB signaling is not supported as the differentiating mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute cholesterol-egress bypass with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should, within hours, lower filipin-positive sterol in LAMP1 compartments and specifically collapse the SREBP target module (SREBF2, LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1, SCD) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts comparatively less affected. If egress bypass reduces lysosomal sterol but leaves the SREBP module elevated, the proposed ER-sterol-starvation link (step 4) is falsified.", "Imaging/lipidomic test: APOE4 microglia should show higher lysosome-associated free cholesterol and a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio than APOE3 under mock conditions, despite equal or higher in-vitro cathepsin B/D and beta-glucocerebrosidase activity. Equal lysosomal sterol with equal esterification would weaken the whole mechanism.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl-ester droplets and further de-repress SREBP targets in APOE4 without lowering the CLEAR/lysosomal transcript module; if CLEAR transcripts fall in parallel, the lysosomal arm is downstream of esterification rather than upstream as proposed.", "TFEB knockdown should, if the CLEAR module is compensatory, worsen lysosomal lipid retention and increase filipin signal in APOE4 more than in APOE3; if TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid retention, the lysosomal program is a driver rather than a compensation and step 2 must be reversed.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR2 blockade should not normalise the sterol/lysosomal modules or the lipid phenotype in mock-treated APOE4 microglia; if interferon blockade does normalise them, this hypothesis is wrong and an interferon-driven mechanism should replace it.", "Bulk-independent replication: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome APOE4-vs-APOE3 microglia dataset with proper normalisation, the CLEAR and SREBP modules should remain enriched after the global shift is removed; loss of enrichment would indicate the signal is a selection/normalisation artefact of this row list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and APOE-pathway receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), which we interpret as increased cargo delivery to the endolysosome; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): a coherent CLEAR-type lysosomal module is elevated above the list-wide background (34/35 genes up vs 77% background, binomial p=0.0013; Mann-Whitney vs rest p=2.6e-3), including gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:GAA, gene:SMPD1, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:IGF2R and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C). We treat this as lysosome biogenesis capacity, not as demonstrated hydrolase activity or acidification.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck): the egress arm is not coordinately induced - gene:NPC2 (+1.17) sits at the list background and NPC1, ABCA1, STARD3 and other export components are absent from the supplied rows - so hydrolysed sterol and sphingolipid are predicted to be retained in LAMP1-positive compartments rather than delivered to the ER/plasma-membrane pools. This retention is an inference; no lipid, localization or flux measurement is supplied.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred sensing state): the ER sterol sensor behaves as if sterol-depleted despite high lipid load - gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCD +4.17 (18/18 sterol-lipogenic genes up, binomial p=0.009 against the 77% background). SREBP proteolytic activation was not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): newly synthesised sterol and MUFA are channelled toward esterified storage rather than membrane repletion (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, with gene:SCD supplying oleate), predicting a higher cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplet pool in APOE4; no lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): the resulting chronic catabolic/biosynthetic load, not an inflammatory program, accounts for the accompanying elevation of nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation and peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin transcripts, while interferon- and NF-kB-associated rows (gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:IFI16 +1.25, gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:NLRP3 +1.09) sit at or near the list background and include down rows (gene:CTSS -5.57 in myeloid activation, gene:TRAF4, gene:RELB down), so an interferon/inflammation-driven mechanism is rejected for this comparison."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol/sphingolipid egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, driving a compensatory CLEAR-lysosomal program with ER-sterol-starved SREBP activation and esterification-biased lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20240613842271452, "cosine_similarity": 0.36365386261411, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6050970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08806262230919765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20240613842271452, "cosine_similarity": 0.36365386261411, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6050970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0770585, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 204}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e=1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705/2212 positive = 77.1% positive). All program comparisons were made against this 77.1% background, not a 50/50 expectation. Genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (e.g., NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2, LIPA, CPT1A, G6PD, LAMP2, MCOLN1, GRN, PSAP were not supplied).", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source ('reported log fold change'); effects are used only by sign and rank, never converted to fold changes. Protein spots are log2 of a reported 2D-gel fold change.", "Protein spots are ambiguous: every spot carries 2-6 candidate identities (208 unique candidates over 92 spots), so no spot is treated as evidence for a single named protein. Cathepsin-D-containing spots span -1.38 to +1.54 (protein_spot:069, 058, 090, 066, 070, 027, 060, 053) and CTSB-containing spots span -1.0 to +0.58, so the spot data are compatible with, but do not confirm, increased lysosomal protein content; they equally permit redistribution among pro/mature forms. Four spots flagged reported_significant have p\u003e0.05 (protein_spot:032, 033, 063, 092).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for capacity but not for activity, flux, localization or direction of causality. No lysosomal proteolysis, cholesterol egress, respiration or glycolytic flux was measured in this dataset; the routing step (Step 3) and the ER sterol-sensing state (Step 4) are inferred, not observed.", "The measured population is a microglia/astrocyte co-culture, so some transcript differences may reflect altered microglia-astrocyte cross-talk or cell-composition differences rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 effects.", "The proposed reserve deficit (Step 5) is a challenge-revealed property. Nothing in the mock condition establishes an ongoing degradative or bioenergetic failure; causality has not been established by these observations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, the dominant difference between APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) is a coordinated cell-state change in lipid routing rather than a simple lysosomal block: APOE4 cells show higher transcripts for scavenger/phagocytic cargo receptors, a broad MITF/TFEB-associated lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase program (37/40 represented lysosomal genes positive, p=0.022 against the 77%-positive selected-list background), and a uniformly positive mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS/beta-oxidation program (27/27 represented members positive, p=0.0019) with decreased committed-glycolysis and oxidative-PPP transcripts (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32). Concurrently the SREBP axis and sterol esterification/storage transcripts are up (15/15 positive, p=0.030; gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72), which is the signature expected when internalized sterol is degraded/stored or retained in the endolysosome instead of restoring the ER-sensed sterol pool. We therefore propose increased, re-routed catabolic throughput with an unmet sterol-return step, which predicts a reduced glycolytic/NADPH reserve that would be exposed only by a future challenge, not an established ongoing degradative failure in the measured mock condition. All effects are measured abundances (RNA log fold change of unspecified base; protein spots log2); no flux, activity or localization was measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test (adaptation vs failure): in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under the same mock condition, measure lysosomal proteolytic flux (DQ-BSA dequenching with bafilomycin control), unesterified cholesterol distribution (filipin/ALOD4) and respirometry. The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows equal or higher DQ-BSA flux, higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower ECAR and lower glycolytic reserve, and increased cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content while SREBP2 target transcripts remain elevated. If APOE4 instead shows reduced DQ-BSA flux with accumulation of undigested cargo and enlarged LysoTracker-positive compartments, the re-routing/adaptation mechanism is wrong and a lysosomal-capacity failure with futile TFEB compensation is favored.", "Prospective: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier or CPT1 inhibition (UK5099, etomoxir) should disproportionately impair APOE4 microglia (ATP, phagocytic index, survival) and force a larger compensatory glycolytic swing than in APOE3. Equal tolerance in both genotypes would weaken Step 3.", "Prospective: SREBP pathway inhibition (fatostatin) or statin plus mevalonate control should reduce the APOE4-specific increases in LDLR/SCD/DHCR24 and lipid-droplet load. The mechanism predicts the lysosomal/v-ATPase program remains elevated (parallel arm); if SREBP inhibition also normalizes the lysosomal program, the sterol arm is upstream and Step 2 must be reordered.", "Prospective challenge: myelin-debris or oxLDL loading should saturate APOE4 microglia earlier than APOE3 (slower cargo clearance, greater lipid-droplet accumulation, larger drop in NADPH/GSH consistent with decreased gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1), while the two genotypes are near-equivalent in unchallenged mock. Equal clearance kinetics under load would remove the predicted reserve deficit.", "Prospective protein-level resolution of the ambiguous spots: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS for mature cathepsin B/D, HEXB, GAA and v-ATPase V1 subunits. The mechanism predicts increased mature hydrolase protein and increased V1 subunit protein in APOE4. Finding unchanged or decreased mature hydrolase protein despite the elevated transcripts (consistent with the decreased CTSD/CTSB/ATP6V1E1-containing spots protein_spot:058, 067, 069, 064, 065) would indicate a post-transcriptional limit and favor failed compensation over increased throughput."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (cargo influx, inferred from abundance): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger and phagocytic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:C1QA/gene:C1QB/gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A; 17/18 represented positive), predicting greater delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system. Uptake rate itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (compartment expansion): A MITF/TFEB-family-associated lysosomal program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:CLN3 +1.17, hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:DPP7 +4.52, and 11/11 represented v-ATPase subunits including gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51), together with late-endosome/sorting machinery (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:AP5M1 +9.78), consistent with an enlarged acidified degradative compartment.", "Step 3 (routing of liberated carbon to mitochondria, not to the ER sterol pool): Lipid-catabolic and mitochondrial oxidative transcripts rise coordinately (gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:DLD +5.54, plus 17/17 represented OXPHOS subunits) while committed glycolysis and the oxidative PPP fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32) despite increased glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73). This predicts oxidation of lysosome-derived fatty acids rather than sterol return to ER membranes.", "Step 4 (persistent low-sterol ER signal and storage): Because sterol is not returned to the ER sensor, SREBP transcripts and their synthesis/uptake targets stay up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCD +4.17), while esterification/storage transcripts rise in parallel (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:APOE +1.24), a combination expected to divert newly made and re-taken-up sterol into cholesteryl-ester/triglyceride storage rather than into the regulatory ER pool.", "Step 5 (net state and reserve cost): The result is a higher-throughput, lipid-catabolic, oxidation-biased microglial state in APOE4 that is largely compensated at baseline (mock) but carries a futile synthesis/storage cycle and a lowered glycolytic and NADPH-generating reserve (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1 decreased), a vulnerability that should be revealed only when acute demand (phagocytic burst, immune activation, lipid overload) requires glycolytic or antioxidant surge capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route internalized lipid cargo into an expanded lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic axis while the ER sterol pool stays unreplenished, sustaining SREBP-driven synthesis, storage and loss of glycolytic reserve"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23935679208359487, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.262967199681129, "cosine_similarity": 0.36294103499138, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5939838187702265, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23935679208359487, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.262967199681129, "cosine_similarity": 0.36294103499138, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5939838187702265, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8157785, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 48}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_077", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e= 1) with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, median 1.46), so only module enrichment relative to this internal background is interpreted; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is not converted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway capacity; hydrolase activity, protein abundance, organelle number, lipid pools, localization and flux were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots containing cathepsin/lysosomal candidates are cited only as ambiguous and mixed-direction, not as protein-level confirmation.", "Coordinated transcript elevation of lysosomal biogenesis and hydrolase genes is read as compensation for an unresolved substrate load rather than as increased completed degradative throughput; the opposite reading is possible from these data alone.", "Cells were profiled in microglia-astrocyte co-culture, so a non-cell-autonomous astrocyte-derived lipid supply could contribute to the same transcript pattern.", "Several decisive genes (LIPA, NPC1, ASAH1, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, ABCA1, PLIN2, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B, HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1, FDPS, CYP51A1) are absent from the supplied DE rows, so both the lysosomal-egress and the sterol-synthesis limbs are incompletely observed.", "Curated gene sets were tested by label permutation against the supplied DE background without multiple-testing correction, and the sets overlap."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a rate-limiting step in endolysosomal luminal lipid hydrolysis/egress rather than in lipid uptake or in glycerolipid synthesis per se: lysosomal biogenesis, v-ATPase and sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolase transcripts are coordinately elevated far above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list, while the ER sterol/lipid-sensing arm (SREBF1/SREBF2/INSIG1/LDLR) and a SREBP1-linked MUFA-synthesis and acyl-remodeling module (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2) are secondarily induced, predicting that liberated and newly made acyl chains are routed into neutral-lipid storage and remodeled phospholipids instead of completing degradative turnover. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: after a matched pulse of fluorescently labelled myelin, oxLDL or Bodipy-cholesterol, APOE4 microglia should show slower per-cargo clearance and greater lysosome-localized lipid retention (filipin/Lysotracker/Nile-Red colocalization) than isogenic APOE3 despite equal or higher uptake; if per-cargo degradation rate is equal or faster in APOE4, the bottleneck at step 2 is falsified.", "Epistasis ordering: relieving lysosomal lipid egress (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or GBA/acid-sphingomyelinase augmentation) should lower SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1 and LPCAT1 transcripts and reduce droplet content in APOE4 toward APOE3; if these lipogenic transcripts are unchanged after egress is restored, the proposed lysosome-upstream ordering is weakened.", "Reverse-direction control: SCD or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid storage but should NOT normalize the lysosomal/CLEAR transcript module (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V subunits, GBA, HEXA); if these lysosomal transcripts fall with SCD/DGAT1 inhibition, the bottleneck is downstream of glycerolipid synthesis and this hypothesis is wrong.", "TFEB dependency: TFEB knockdown should selectively and disproportionately impair labelled-lipid clearance and increase lysosomal lipid accumulation in APOE4 relative to APOE3; equal impairment in both genotypes would argue the CLEAR induction is not a genotype-specific compensation.", "Lipidomic test of the focus branch: APOE4 microglia should show increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester and a higher monounsaturated/saturated ratio in phosphatidylcholine species; absence of any acyl-chain compositional shift would falsify step 4 while leaving steps 1-3 testable.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot or targeted proteomics (not ambiguous 2-D spots) should show increased LAMP1, CTSB/CTSD and GBA protein and increased hydrolase activity per cell in APOE4; unchanged or reduced hydrolase protein/activity would weaken the compensatory-biogenesis interpretation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (cargo delivery, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia retain or increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), so endolysosomal lipid cargo delivery is inferred to be at least as high as in APOE3; delivery flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK, inferred): luminal hydrolysis and egress of sphingolipid/sterol cargo is rate-limiting; the cell responds with a coordinated TFEB/CLEAR-type transcriptional expansion of lysosomes (gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and of luminal lipid hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA). Elevated transcript abundance is measured; increased lysosomal lipid load, hydrolase activity and organelle number are inferred.", "Step 3 (sensing, inferred): incomplete egress limits the sterol/lipid pool reaching the ER sensor compartment, and the SREBP arm is transcriptionally engaged (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2). Transcript levels are measured; SREBP cleavage, nuclear localization and ER free-sterol concentration are not.", "Step 4 (downstream lipid branch, partially supported): SREBP1-associated monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis and glycerolipid assembly/acyl remodeling are induced (gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2) together with sterol esterification capacity (gene:SOAT1), predicting a shift of acyl chains toward triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage and toward remodeled (more monounsaturated) phospholipids. Lipid species, droplet content and acyl-chain composition were not measured.", "Step 5 (counter-flow constraint): acyl-CoA activation and one glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase isoform move the other way (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3, gene:PNPLA1), so the branch is an isoform-selective re-routing of glycerolipid flux, not a uniform increase in glycerolipid pathway capacity.", "Step 6 (consequence, associative): sustained endolysosomal and ER load co-occurs with stress and inflammatory transcripts (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:NLRP3), the proposed functional cost of reduced degradative throughput per unit of internalized lipid cargo."], "title": "An endolysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck in APOE4 microglia drives compensatory CLEAR-program induction and SREBP1-linked diversion of acyl chains into storage and phospholipid remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2462799542148211, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19137250929351063, "cosine_similarity": 0.3626668767880303, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6313139158576051, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2462799542148211, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19137250929351063, "cosine_similarity": 0.3626668767880303, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6313139158576051, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.849719, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 205}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_081", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77% up, mean +1.39 in the unspecified reported log base); pathway claims are therefore made only as enrichment relative to this internal background, and absence of a gene (e.g. ACLY, CPT1A, ABCA1, PLIN2, NPC1, LIPA) is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is not specified and is preserved as reported; only signs, relative ranks and set-level contrasts are used, not absolute fold magnitudes.", "Protein spots carry 3-5 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots 027/053/055/057 are cited only as ambiguous, direction-consistent corroboration of cathepsin-containing spots and are not treated as measurements of CTSB or CTSD protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly reflected in enzyme protein and activity; lysosomal acidification, hydrolytic flux, citrate export, acetyl-CoA supply, esterification rate, droplet content and lipid uptake were not measured and are inferred.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein/lipid substrate for the proposed uptake arm; genotype effects are assumed to be cell-intrinsic to microglia rather than secondary to astrocyte differences, which the supplied data cannot resolve.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so significance values are taken at face value and the very large reported effect magnitudes are assumed not to be an artefact of a single-replicate or pseudobulk scaling issue."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcriptional increase in scavenger-receptor-mediated lipid uptake (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR) and in lysosomal hydrolase / v-ATPase / endolysosomal trafficking genes (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A/1H/0C, RAB7A, TFEB), together with the esterification-desaturation machinery (AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, SCD, ACSS2, ACAT2, SREBF1) and mitochondrial pyruvate-citrate genes (MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1, OGDH, DLD, ACO2), whereas fatty-acid oxidation-associated transcripts that were measured are not co-elevated (ACSL4, ACSL5, ABCD1 decreased). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is the disposal of lysosome-derived free fatty acid and sterol: because oxidative/efflux disposal does not scale with the increased uptake and hydrolytic capacity, esterification into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol becomes the dominant sink, predicting a higher steady-state neutral-lipid-droplet load in APOE4 than APOE3. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux; the discovery data measure transcript and protein-spot abundance only and do not establish causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer/blockade test: in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, blocking scavenger-receptor uptake (SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1) should remove most of the APOE4 excess neutral-lipid-droplet (BODIPY/LipidTOX) signal, while U-13C-glucose labelling of triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester should show similar fractional de novo contribution in both genotypes. If instead 13C-glucose-derived label into TAG/CE is markedly higher in APOE4 and SCARB1 blockade leaves the droplet excess intact, the uptake-plus-hydrolysis bottleneck is wrong and a citrate/ACLY-driven de novo lipogenesis mechanism is favoured.", "SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should convert the excess stored lipid into free sterol/fatty acid: droplet number should fall while filipin-detectable unesterified cholesterol, lysosomal membrane permeabilisation and cell death rise more in APOE4 than APOE3. No genotype difference in this switch would weaken step 3-4.", "Lysosomal-arm test: v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or GBA/acid-hydrolase inhibition should blunt the APOE4-specific droplet excess, because the model requires lysosomal hydrolysis to supply the esterified pool; if the APOE4 droplet excess is unchanged or increased in a way indistinguishable from APOE3 after hydrolase blockade, the lysosome-to-droplet routing is falsified.", "Quantitative validation of measured layer: independent qPCR/immunoblot in the same isogenic lines should confirm APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for SCARB1, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, SCD and AGPAT2 protein or mRNA at day 30 mock. Failure to reproduce the direction for the majority of these, especially SCARB1 and the hydrolases, would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Oxidative-arm test (fills a data gap): Seahorse FAO (etomoxir-sensitive OCR) and CPT1A/ACSL1 measurement should show that APOE4 microglia do not increase fatty-acid oxidation capacity in proportion to their uptake/hydrolysis increase. If APOE4 shows a matching or greater etomoxir-sensitive OCR, the proposed disposal bottleneck is wrong even if the uptake and lysosomal modules replicate.", "Negative/specificity prediction: proteostasis, proteasome, actin-cytoskeleton and interferon programmes should not differ coherently between genotypes under mock conditions (they were not enriched here); a strong interferon or proteasome phenotype on independent testing would indicate a different primary axis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia transcribe more lipid-uptake receptor mRNA, dominated by SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1) with smaller increases in CD36, LDLR, TREM2 and APOE itself; we infer, but did not measure, a higher influx of lipoprotein- and astrocyte-derived lipid.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): the lysosomal/autophagic module is coherently up (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) together with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C) and endolysosomal trafficking genes (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:CHMP4B); we infer an expanded, acidified degradative compartment with greater hydrolytic capacity for glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and cholesteryl-ester-containing cargo.", "Step 3 (inferred flux, primary bottleneck): the products of that hydrolysis - free fatty acid, sphingoid bases and unesterified sterol - must leave the lysosome. Among measured genes the catabolic/efflux options are not co-elevated relative to the strongly up-shifted background (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 and gene:ABCD1 are decreased; ACOX1, CROT, HADHA, ETFA are near background), so oxidative/export disposal is proposed to be the limiting arm.", "Step 4 (measured abundance supporting the alternative sink): esterification and desaturation genes are uniformly up (gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:ACAT2, gene:ACSS2), and mitochondrial pyruvate import/TCA/citrate-export genes are the single most coherent up-regulated module (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2), providing inferred cytosolic acetyl-CoA and glycerolipid backbone for re-esterification.", "Step 5 (inferred phenotype): the combination of higher influx plus higher hydrolysis plus a re-esterification-biased sink routes carbon into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol, producing a larger neutral-lipid-droplet pool and a larger acidic compartment in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia at day 30 under mock conditions.", "Step 6 (consequence, inferred): storage rather than oxidation or export leaves APOE4 microglia with reduced spare capacity to handle an additional lipid load, which would be seen as disproportionate droplet growth and lysosomal lipid retention when exogenous lipid is added."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand an uptake-plus-lysosomal-hydrolysis arm whose liberated sterol and fatty acid is routed into esterified neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2696894731012074, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26256632384132494, "cosine_similarity": 0.36262002701542073, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6181585760517799, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2696894731012074, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26256632384132494, "cosine_similarity": 0.36262002701542073, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6181585760517799, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.65847125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 206}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_126", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |log FC| \u003e 1, 77.1% positive, list-wide mean +1.39) in an unspecified logarithm base; enrichment claims are therefore made against that shifted list background, not against an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene means it was not supplied rather than unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme and receptor protein amount; hydrolase activity, receptor surface localization, TFEB nuclear translocation, mTORC1 activity, ApoE lipidation, lysosomal pH and any lipid pool were not measured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (e.g. protein_spot:052 lists ACTB, CTSL, TPM3, CLIC1, NT5C1A); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level changes are assumed to be interpretable only as weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic as stated, so genotype rather than donor background is assumed to drive the contrast; microglia-astrocyte co-culture composition and ambient-RNA differences are assumed not to fully generate the lysosomal/lipid module.", "The very large log fold changes (up to +15.5) are assumed to arise from low-detection genes in single-cell pseudobulk testing, so set-level medians and permutation tests rather than individual extreme values carry the argument."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling rather than in interferon or NF-kB signalling: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, SCARB2, TREM2) and for a coherent CLEAR-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase module (GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A/1H/1E1/0D1, LAMP1) are coordinately higher alongside TFEB and MITF, while the export arm is not correspondingly represented (NPC2 only +1.17, APOE +1.24, MYLIP +1.33, no LXR/ABCA1-ABCG1 rows). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is egress of hydrolase-liberated sterol and fatty acid from the endolysosome to the ER/plasma membrane; the resulting flux is rerouted into cytosolic ester storage (SOAT1, DGAT1) so the ER regulatory sterol pool remains low and the SREBP-1 lipogenic/desaturation program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, INSIG1) stays on, predicting a cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol-loaded, lysosome-expanded APOE4 microglial state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content (BODIPY/CE by lipidomics) and, by restoring free sterol to the ER, lower SREBP-1 target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) while leaving the CLEAR hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA) still elevated relative to APOE3, because the lysosomal load is upstream. If SOAT1 inhibition instead normalises the hydrolase module without changing SREBP-1 targets, the proposed ordering (lysosomal load -\u003e esterification -\u003e sustained SREBP-1) is wrong.", "TFEB knockdown or a TFEB-null APOE4 line should selectively lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts and worsen lysosomal lipid accumulation (increased filipin-positive and LysoTracker-positive area, increased lysosomal sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide) more in APOE4 than APOE3. Failure of TFEB knockdown to reduce GBA/HEXA/CTSB/GAA in APOE4 would falsify the TFEB/MITF-associated step.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols with equal or lower sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide (catabolic capacity up). Accumulation of sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide together with unchanged cholesteryl esters would weaken the mechanism and favour a primary hydrolase-insufficiency model instead.", "Blocking influx (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should reduce both droplet load and the hydrolase module in APOE4 towards APOE3; enhancing export (LXR agonist, ApoE lipidation, or 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin) should reduce droplets and lower SREBP-1 targets without requiring hydrolase induction. If neither influx blockade nor export enhancement changes the APOE4/APOE3 gap, the uptake-versus-egress imbalance framing fails.", "Interferon test (rejects the assigned focus): a targeted ISG panel (ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1, OAS1, STAT1, IRF7, BST2) and phospho-STAT1 staining should show no APOE4/APOE3 difference under mock, and JAK1/2 inhibition should not narrow the lysosomal-lipid transcript gap. A clear APOE4 ISG elevation or a JAK-inhibitor-sensitive lysosomal module would overturn this hypothesis in favour of an interferon-driven mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_126", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 genotype with modestly higher APOE transcript (gene:APOE, +1.24). Inferred, not measured: altered ApoE4 particle lipidation and reduced capacity to accept/export cholesterol and phospholipid from microglia.", "Measured: higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB2, gene:TREM2, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1). Inferred: increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosomal compartment (flux and receptor surface localization not measured).", "Measured: coordinate elevation of a CLEAR-type lysosomal module (22 curated members, mean log FC +3.52 versus the +1.39 list-wide mean, permutation p\u003c1e-4) together with gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03). Inferred: TFEB/MITF transcriptional activation as a compensatory response to lysosomal lipid load; nuclear translocation, mTORC1 status and hydrolase enzymatic activity were not measured.", "Bottleneck (inferred): egress of liberated cholesterol and fatty acid out of the lysosome and onward efflux is not scaled with uptake and hydrolysis. The supplied rows contain only a weak export arm (gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14) plus gene:MYLIP (+1.33), an E3 ligase that lowers LDLR protein; ABCA1/ABCG1/NR1H3 were not measured, so this step is an inference from missing/weak representation, not an observed deficit.", "Measured: higher esterification transcripts gene:SOAT1 (+1.25) and gene:DGAT1 (+1.68). Inferred: rerouting of the lipid that does reach the ER into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol stored in cytosolic droplets rather than being effluxed.", "Measured: SREBP-1/sterol-synthesis arm elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.72, gene:DHCR7 +2.72, gene:LSS +2.30, gene:INSIG1 +1.94, gene:HMGCS1 +1.11, gene:SREBF2 +1.11). Inferred: the ER regulatory sterol pool is not sensed as replete because lipid is sequestered in lysosomes and esters, so lipogenesis and desaturation continue and amplify droplet load.", "Measured: sphingolipid catabolic hydrolases are among the largest increases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.71, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:NAGLU +5.87). Inferred outcome: an APOE4 lipid phenotype dominated by neutral-lipid (CE/TAG) accumulation with relatively increased sphingolipid turnover, accompanied only by a mild, non-interferon chemokine tilt (gene:CXCL8 +3.13, gene:CCL2 +2.11, gene:NLRP3 +1.10, gene:PYCARD +2.36)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-hydrolase program whose bottleneck is post-lysosomal lipid egress, diverting liberated lipid into SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification while ER sterol sensing stays de-repressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2900620315326958, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27907928579703684, "cosine_similarity": 0.36256374188485085, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_126", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976569579288026, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2900620315326958, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27907928579703684, "cosine_similarity": 0.36256374188485085, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5976569579288026, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5845405, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 207}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_039", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directions are judged against that 77% positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Coordinated increases of the represented SREBP-2 target ensemble are taken to indicate ongoing sterol-sensing in acquisition mode; SREBP-2 cleavage, nuclear SREBP, and the ER regulatory sterol pool were not measured and transcript increases alone do not establish protein activity.", "Increased hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are assumed to reflect lysosomal biogenesis capacity, not measured hydrolytic flux or lumenal pH; likewise increased OXPHOS subunit transcripts are assumed to reflect an intended oxidative bias, not measured respiration.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (39/92 contain keratin candidates); no spot is assigned to a single protein, and spot changes are used only for compatibility, not confirmation.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture, so differences in cell-state composition or maturation between lines (10X Flex, replicate number not supplied) could contribute to the globally positive selected list; this is treated as a limitation on causal interpretation.", "Any clearance or capacity deficit is framed as revealed by a future lipid/myelin challenge, not as an established ongoing defect in the mock condition."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture), APOE4 differs from APOE3 by a coordinated cell-state change rather than a single blocked step: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, lysosomal hydrolysis and acidification, and neutral-lipid esterification are jointly increased, yet the full sterol-biosynthetic/SREBP-2 target set is also increased, indicating that sterol liberated from the increased lipid-handling load is routed into esterified/lysosomal storage and does not register at the ER sterol sensor, so acquisition signaling is not switched off; the resulting futile acquisition-storage cycle is accompanied by a uniformly increased nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and mitochondrial-carrier transcript program with relatively decreased glycolytic transcripts, consistent with an oxidative acetyl-CoA/ATP supply bias. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; the sterol pools, esterification flux and respiration flux that would establish this causal chain remain unmeasured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should return the regulatory sterol pool to the ER and lower the sterol-biosynthetic transcript set (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels while raising free/unesterified cholesterol; if these transcripts remain elevated and unesterified sterol does not rise, the sequestration step is falsified.", "Prospective: direct lipid measurement in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 should show increased cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid and lysosome-associated lipid with detectable nuclear SREBP-2; equal esterified lipid with equal SREBP-2 processing would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Prospective: Seahorse profiling should show APOE4 basal and maximal oxygen consumption equal or higher than APOE3 with a lower ECAR/OCR ratio; if respiration is unchanged or lower despite 37/37 nuclear OXPHOS transcripts being increased, the energetic step must be reassigned to unrealized mitonuclear imbalance (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB).", "Prospective challenge: after myelin or oxLDL loading, APOE4 should clear a smaller additional lipid fraction per cell and show earlier lysosomal saturation than APOE3, despite equal or higher uptake receptor expression; equal incremental clearance would show the state is a successful high-throughput adaptation rather than a futile cycle.", "Prospective: TFEB activation or lysosomal acid lipase supplementation should reduce, not increase, sterol-synthesis transcripts in APOE4 if the block is downstream routing; an increase in those transcripts would contradict the proposed ER-sensing step.", "Falsifier for the focus rejection: if unbiased phagocytosis or actin-dynamics assays show a large APOE4 defect in mock uptake, the endocytic/cytoskeletal machinery would need a primary role that this selected-list evidence (actin 30/38 positive, endosomal sorting 30/36 positive, both indistinguishable from the 77% background) does not support."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the expression of lipid- and lipoprotein-uptake and phagocytic recognition machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CSF1R, gene:ITGAX; 22/23 queried receptor members positive but with small effects near the selection threshold), increasing routing of extracellular lipid toward the endolysosome.", "A TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis program is coordinately up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1; 26/28 positive, larger effects than the selected-list background), increasing hydrolytic/acidification capacity for that load; gene:CTSS (-5.57) is the notable exception and marks a shift away from a homeostatic microglial profile.", "Liberated sterol and fatty acid are directed into esterified and membrane-lipid storage rather than back to the ER regulatory pool: gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:MGLL, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:NPC2 are increased (12/13 phospholipid-synthesis members positive, median +2.52).", "Because the regulatory ER sterol pool is not replenished, sterol-sensing stays in acquisition mode: every represented member of the sterol-synthesis/SREBP axis is increased (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR; 13/13 positive), which is the opposite of the sterol-replete repression expected if increased hydrolysis had simply raised free cellular sterol.", "Sustaining simultaneous hydrolysis, acidification and de novo sterol/lipid synthesis raises cytosolic acetyl-CoA and ATP demand; citrate/acetate-to-acetyl-CoA and oxidative machinery transcripts rise (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2, gene:ACAT2; nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and carriers 37/37 positive, median +2.64, e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46), while glycolytic/PPP transcripts are relatively decreased (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD; 5/11 positive, below the 77% background).", "The predicted consequence in the measured mock condition is an expanded esterified/lysosomal lipid pool with unchanged or increased basal handling, not an overt clearance failure; a clearance deficit is expected only when an additional lipid or myelin load is imposed, and the mtDNA-encoded transcripts that fall (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4) suggest the transcriptional OXPHOS gain may not be fully realized as respiratory capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-acquisition/storage state in which sterol regulatory signaling stays in acquisition mode, supported by an oxidative acetyl-CoA/ATP program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42682679171435955, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26250090053078645, "cosine_similarity": 0.3624066921927085, "direction_accuracy": 0.4029126213592233, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137540453074434, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42682679171435955, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26250090053078645, "cosine_similarity": 0.3624066921927085, "direction_accuracy": 0.4029126213592233, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137540453074434, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.112883, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 49}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_123", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) from APOE4-vs-APOE3 microglia, not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level statements are made relative to the global shift of these selected rows (77% positive, median effect 1.46 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base).", "The global positive RNA shift is at least partly a normalisation/compositional artefact (gene:ACTB and mitochondrially encoded transcripts are strongly negative), so only relative enrichment against this background is interpreted.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; a spot containing CTSB/CTSD/HEXB/ACP2 candidates is not evidence for a uniquely identified protein, and opposite-direction spots are treated as ambiguous proteoform/identity information, not as a measured pro- versus mature-hydrolase ratio.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, sterol localisation or TFEB nuclear translocation; none of these were measured here.", "Cells were microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a genotype-dependent difference in the extracellular lipid/lipoprotein supply from astrocytes could contribute to step 1.", "Several key genes for the mechanism (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1) are absent from the supplied rows; their status is unknown, not normal."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a higher lipid/lipoprotein cargo load into the late-endosome/lysosome and mount a compensatory CLEAR-type transcriptional expansion of luminal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and lysosomal solute carriers; because the rate-limiting step is post-hydrolytic egress of sterol-rich cargo from the endolysosome to the ER rather than transcript-level degradative capacity, the ER regulatory sterol pool is sensed as low and SREBP-1/SREBP-2 target genes are co-induced, producing a self-reinforcing lipid-handling burden. Causality is not established by these data; the association is transcript- and spot-level only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Pulse-chase of fluorescent lipid cargo (BODIPY-LDL or labelled myelin debris) plus DQ-BSA in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show comparable or higher internalisation but slower per-cell cargo clearance and higher filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol colocalised with LAMP1. Equal or faster APOE4 clearance with no difference in lysosomal cholesterol would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: acute relief of endolysosomal sterol egress with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 protein supplementation) for 24 h should normalise SREBP-2 target transcripts (DHCR24, DHCR7, HMGCS1, LDLR, INSIG1) in APOE4 toward APOE3 while leaving hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA) largely unchanged in the same window. If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated after cargo sterol is liberated, the bottleneck is not egress and the mechanism is falsified in favour of a cell-autonomous synthesis or sensing defect.", "Cargo-dependence test: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SR-B1/CD36-mediated uptake, should reduce the APOE4-specific elevation of hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts. Persistence of the lysosomal program in the absence of cargo would show the program is cargo-independent and would weaken step 1-2 ordering.", "Capacity-versus-activity test: enzymatic assays for GBA, HEXA and GAA and mature-cathepsin immunoblots should show that the increase in enzyme activity per cell is proportionally smaller than the transcript increase; activity scaling fully with transcript and normal cargo clearance would weaken step 3.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: if Seahorse respirometry and TCA flux tracing reveal a large APOE4 mitochondrial difference (consistent with gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2) while cargo handling, lysosomal cholesterol and SREBP-2 targets are unchanged after cyclodextrin, the mitochondrial-reprogramming explanation should be preferred over this one.", "Negative control prediction: inflammatory activation markers should not be required; blocking NF-kB or TLR signalling should not correct the lipid-handling phenotype, consistent with the immune gene set not being enriched above the global shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_123", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:ITGB5); increased internalisation flux is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): a coordinated CLEAR-like lysosomal-biogenesis program is transcriptionally elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:RRAGD; hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C; carriers gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5), together with late-endosome maturation and sorting genes (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B); TFEB nuclear activity and lysosomal acidification are inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; inferred): despite this transcriptional expansion, hydrolysed sterol/lipid does not efficiently leave the endolysosomal lumen for the ER, so functional degradative-plus-export throughput per unit cargo is lower in APOE4 than in APOE3. Consistent, non-uniform proteoform behaviour is seen in cathepsin-candidate spots that move in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up vs protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), and one major microglial hydrolase transcript is strongly reduced (gene:CTSS), so mature hydrolase protein is not assumed to scale with transcript.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): the ER-accessible sterol pool is read as insufficient, and SREBP-2/SREBP-1 target transcripts rise coherently (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:MYLIP, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2), i.e. de novo sterol/fatty-acid synthesis is engaged even while uptake receptors are elevated.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred storage): lipid reaching the ER is preferentially re-esterified and stored rather than exported (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE), while endosome-ER lipid-transfer machinery is discordant (gene:OSBPL1A up, gene:OSBPL8 down); neutral-lipid and lysosomal cholesterol pools were not measured.", "Step 6 (predicted consequence): steps 1, 4 and 5 keep adding lipid to a compartment whose egress step is limiting, giving a chronic, low-grade lysosomal-load state that constrains further cargo clearance without an overt inflammatory transcriptional response (gene:CD74, gene:C1QA and other immune genes are not enriched above the global shift)."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid-cargo egress, not degradative gene dosage, is the limiting step in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09784735812133072, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20446189417264768, "cosine_similarity": 0.36231039677873506, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_123", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6051909385113269, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09784735812133072, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20446189417264768, "cosine_similarity": 0.36231039677873506, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6051909385113269, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9314905, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 208}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_094", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong upward skew (77% positive, median 1.46), so pathway claims are made relative to this biased background, not to an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved, so RNA magnitudes are not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the availability of the corresponding subunits; assembled complex amounts, protein levels of any OXPHOS subunit, mtDNA copy number, membrane potential, oxygen consumption, metabolite pools and lipid droplet content were not measured in these data and are inferred only.", "MT-transcript quantification by a probe-based single-cell platform (10X Flex) is assumed to reflect genuine genotype differences rather than ambient RNA, probe-set coverage, or dying-cell artefacts; only 6 of 13 mtDNA-encoded genes appear in the supplied rows.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and identify no OXPHOS, TCA or lipogenic protein uniquely; spot 038 (ALDOA/ALDOC/SORD/ARPC1B/TKT) and spot 020 (GLUD1/FSCN1/ENO1/G6PD/EPX) are treated as ambiguous, weak corroboration only.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; no information on cell-type deconvolution, replicate number or cell-cycle/maturation state is supplied, so a cell-state or maturation difference between genotypes cannot be excluded as an upstream cause.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, so the direction of causality between the APOE4 allele, the mitonuclear imbalance and the lipid programme is assumed but not established."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, nuclear-encoded mitochondrial modules (OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes, pyruvate/glutamate/citrate carriers) are transcriptionally raised well above the already upward-skewed background, whereas mtDNA-encoded core subunits of complexes III/IV/V are among the most reduced transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4). We hypothesise that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not substrate delivery or nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembling proton-pumping and ATP-synthesising complexes, so that APOE4 cells increase carbon entry into mitochondria but cannot increase terminal oxidative flux; because glycolytic overflow is also constrained (HK2 and PFKP transcripts down), surplus TCA carbon is exported as citrate (SLC25A1 up) into SREBP-driven fatty-acid desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1 up), producing the lipid-laden APOE4 microglial state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM overexpression, or restoring mtDNA copy number/mt-translation capacity) should increase assembled complex IV/V (BN-PAGE, in-gel activity) and FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration, and should lower SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent neutral-lipid accumulation, while leaving nuclear OXPHOS transcript induction largely unchanged. If assembled complex IV/V and maximal respiration normalise but lipid storage in APOE4 is unchanged, steps 5-6 are wrong.", "Respirometry and stoichiometry: APOE4 should show reduced maximal and spare respiratory capacity and a reduced ratio of assembled complex V (or complex IV activity) to nuclear-encoded subunit protein and to mitochondrial mass, with mtDNA:nDNA ratio equal to or lower than APOE3. If APOE4 shows equal or higher maximal OCR and equal or higher assembled complex V per unit mitochondrial mass, the primary bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Isotope tracing: with U-13C-glucose or U-13C-glutamine, APOE4 should show reduced label flux to CO2/oxidative TCA turnover but increased 13C incorporation into palmitate, oleate and cholesteryl esters relative to APOE3. Equal or lower lipid labelling in APOE4 would weaken the citrate-overflow step.", "Citrate-carrier dependence: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SLC25A1 (or ACLY) should reduce lipid droplet and cholesteryl-ester content selectively in APOE4 and not in APOE3. Absence of a genotype-selective effect would falsify step 5.", "Selectivity of the mtRNA deficit: orthogonal RT-qPCR/RNA-FISH should confirm a subunit-selective reduction of MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 with preserved or increased MT-ND5/MT-ND4L in APOE4. Uniform mtRNA levels across all 13 genes by an orthogonal assay would attribute the signal to probe or ambient-RNA artefact and weaken the whole mechanism.", "Glycolytic non-compensation: extracellular acidification and lactate output per cell should not be higher in APOE4 despite raised SLC2A1/SLC2A3, consistent with reduced HK2/PFKP. A clear glycolytic (Warburg-like) compensation in APOE4 would favour an alternative glycolysis-switch model over this bottleneck model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - all 38 detected nuclear OXPHOS subunits are up (median ~2.6 vs background median ~1.46 for the selected DE rows), together with TCA enzymes (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2), the pyruvate carrier MPC2, PDH-activating PDP1/DLD, glutamine-anaplerosis genes (GLS, GLUD1) and mitochondrial carriers (SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A1).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, opposite direction): mtDNA-encoded core subunits of complexes IV, III, V and I are reduced (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2), placing MT-ATP6 in the lowest ~5% of all supplied effects; MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are exceptions and are up.", "Step 3 (inferred, not measured): the resulting mismatch between nuclear-encoded and mtDNA-encoded subunit supply limits assembly of holo-complexes III, IV and V, so respiratory-chain and ATP-synthase capacity per mitochondrion does not scale with the induced nuclear programme; assembled complex levels, mtDNA copy number and respiration were not measured here.", "Step 4 (inferred flux consequence): with substrate import transcripts up but terminal oxidation capped, electron pressure and matrix redox stress rise, consistent with induction of matrix redox-buffering transcripts (PRDX3, GPX4, NNT); this is an inference about flux and redox state, not an observed metabolite or ROS measurement.", "Step 5 (inferred flux routing): glycolytic overflow is not an available sink because rate-controlling glycolytic transcripts HK2 and PFKP are strongly down despite raised glucose transporters (SLC2A1, SLC2A3), so accumulating TCA intermediates are preferentially exported as citrate via the up-regulated citrate carrier SLC25A1.", "Step 6 (inferred endpoint): cytosolic citrate plus SREBP activation (SREBF1, SCD up) and uptake/esterification machinery (CD36, DGAT1, SOAT1 up) channels carbon into neutral lipid and cholesteryl ester storage, with downstream lysosomal/degradative load (TFEB, CTSB up), i.e. an APOE4-selective lipid-storage phenotype driven by an oxidative bottleneck rather than by increased substrate supply."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance caps terminal oxidation in APOE4 microglia and diverts TCA carbon to citrate-fuelled lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2345242898813184, "cosine_similarity": 0.36221160734332014, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041779935275081, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0684931506849315, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2345242898813184, "cosine_similarity": 0.36221160734332014, "direction_accuracy": 0.11488673139158576, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041779935275081, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.26411325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 209}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_059", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; direction is interpreted only relative to the list-wide positive shift, and absence of a gene (e.g. RAC1, CDC42, ARPC3, LAMP2, GRN, NPC1) is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The reported RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect sizes up to |15| are treated as ranks/directions, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Transcript abundance for MYH9, ACTB, MYO1F, RAC2 and ARHGDIA is assumed to track the corresponding cellular protein pools and the free-versus-GDI-bound GTPase balance closely enough to change contractile output; no protein, phospho-MLC, F-actin or GTPase-loading measurement is available.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each, so protein_spot:010 and protein_spot:011 are treated only as weak, non-significant (p=0.41, p=0.32) directional concordance for a MYH9-containing spot, not as MYH9 quantification.", "The comparison is assumed to reflect a within-cell regulatory difference at Day 30 rather than a difference in microglial purity or subpopulation composition in the astrocyte co-culture; biological replicate number is not supplied.", "Mock condition means no exogenous cargo load, so the inferred internalization deficit is a capacity difference that must be revealed by an added-cargo assay."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, the discriminating step is the cortical actomyosin and myeloid Rho-GTPase-cycling module that drives phagocytic/macropinocytic cup closure and nascent-vesicle scission: transcripts for non-muscle myosin IIA, beta-actin, myeloid myosin-I, RAC2 and its myeloid regulators are among the most reduced measurements while the RhoGDI transcript ARHGDIA is the third most increased, whereas uptake-receptor transcripts move only with the pervasive positive shift and endolysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and lipogenic/esterification transcripts rise well above it. We therefore predict an APOE4 state with high degradative and lipid-esterification capacity but low actomyosin-dependent cargo internalization flux, i.e. capacity uncoupled from delivery; internalization rate, contractile force, GTPase loading and lipid flux were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake assay: pulsed pHrodo-myelin, apoptotic-cell or 1-2 um bead uptake with surface receptor staining should show lower internalized cargo per cell in APOE4 than APOE3 at equal or higher surface TREM2/CD36/MERTK, and para-nitro-blebbistatin or a Rac inhibitor applied to APOE3 should phenocopy APOE4. Equal or higher APOE4 internalization at matched receptor levels would weaken the mechanism.", "Capacity-versus-flux separation: DQ-BSA or BODIPY-myelin degradation per cell should be lower in APOE4 while cathepsin B/GBA/beta-hexosaminidase activity measured in cell lysates or on isolated lysosomes is equal or higher. If lysate hydrolase activity is instead reduced in APOE4, the bottleneck is degradative rather than internalization, and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Rescue direction: ARHGDIA knockdown or MYH9 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should raise cargo internalization and lower neutral-lipid droplet area without needing to change receptor transcripts; no change in internalization after either manipulation would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Imaging prediction: live imaging should show more frequent stalled, unclosed phagocytic cups and lower phospho-myosin-light-chain and cortical F-actin intensity at contact sites in APOE4. Normal cup closure kinetics and normal pMLC would weaken the mechanism.", "Composition control: if flow-sorted, purity-matched APOE4 microglia lose the MYH9/ACTB/MYO1F/SPN/CTSS transcript deficit, the signal reflects cell-state composition rather than the proposed machinery difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the strongly positive global RNA shift of this selected differential-expression list (median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified log base), the myeloid cortical-actomyosin transcripts gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB, gene:MYO1F, gene:FAM49B, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:SPN, gene:PTPN6, gene:RAC2 and gene:DOCK8 are all negative (module median -2.79) while gene:ARHGDIA is +10.61 (rank 3 of 2212).", "Inferred (not measured): a lower cortical actin/myosin-IIA supply together with a higher RhoGDI-to-GTPase transcript ratio reduces Rac/Rho loading at the plasma membrane and the contractile force applied to phagocytic cups and nascent macropinosomes, lowering internalization and scission rate per receptor engagement rather than receptor occupancy.", "Measured: uptake and opsonin-receptor transcripts (gene:TREM2, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:SCARB1) are positive but at or near the background median of this list, so receptor transcript availability is not the differentiating variable; the receptor and cortical-actomyosin modules separate completely in rank.", "Measured: endolysosomal transcripts rise clearly above the global shift (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:TFEB +2.38), consistent with a TFEB-associated expansion of degradative capacity; inferred: this is compensatory and does not by itself increase substrate arrival.", "Measured: lipogenic and esterification transcripts are also elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25); inferred: with internalized cargo flux limited, sterol and fatty-acid carbon is preferentially routed to esterified storage rather than to cargo-driven catabolism.", "Inferred phenotype: APOE4 microglia should show reduced particulate/myelin uptake per cell at normal or increased surface receptor and hydrolase content, with increased neutral-lipid storage; the bottleneck is at internalization, not at hydrolase synthesis."], "title": "Actomyosin/Rho-cycling limitation on cargo internalization, not receptor or hydrolase supply, differentiates APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14421408263486318, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2639033709666118, "cosine_similarity": 0.3620972479065042, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057119741100323, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14421408263486318, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2639033709666118, "cosine_similarity": 0.3620972479065042, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057119741100323, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.203243, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 210}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_170", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a monotone log fold change in an unspecified base, identical in base and direction for all gene rows, so only relative comparisons (set versus background, mt-encoded versus nuclear-encoded) are interpreted, not absolute magnitudes.", "The supplied gene rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so the absence of CAT, SOD2, SOD1, GSR, GCLM, TXN2 and most PEX genes is missing data, not evidence of no change.", "Lower steady-state mtDNA-encoded transcript abundance in APOE4 reflects a genuine reduction in mitochondrially translated core subunit supply rather than probe-panel, 3'-bias, ambient-RNA or QC/normalisation artefacts of the 10X Flex assay.", "Transcript abundance for nuclear mitochondrial genes is at least partly translated and imported, so the nuclear/mtDNA transcript ratio is a usable proxy for subunit supply stoichiometry; assembly state, membrane potential, oxidant concentration and respiratory flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots are mixtures with several candidate genes, so spot-level changes (including the PRDX2- and CAT-containing spots) are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Astrocyte co-culture and cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells are assumed not to be the dominant driver of the pseudobulk mito-nuclear contrast; this was not testable with the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia express a strongly expanded nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (TCA enzymes, complex I/III/IV/V structural subunits, import and assembly factors, carriers) while transcripts for several mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are lower than in APOE3. We hypothesise that the limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for holo-complex assembly (most acutely complex V and complex III/IV), so that nuclear subunits accumulate in unassembled or partially assembled form; the resulting inefficient, leak-prone electron transfer raises matrix oxidant load and lowers ATP-coupled flux, which is met by a compensatory matrix antioxidant/NADPH and uncoupling response (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT, UCP2), an integrated stress response (DDIT3, EIF2AK3, NUPR1, SHMT2), and a lysosomal-lipogenic shift (TFEB, cathepsins, SREBF1, SCD). Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; assembly state, flux, ROS and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assembly test: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex V, III2 and IV holoenzymes with a preserved or increased pool of free nuclear-encoded subunits and subassemblies (increased subassembly-to-holoenzyme ratio). If APOE4 shows equal or greater assembled holo-complex levels and no accumulation of unassembled nuclear subunits, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Flux/coupling test: Seahorse respirometry should show lower ATP-linked oxygen consumption and lower maximal respiration per mitochondrial mass in APOE4, with a higher proton-leak fraction (consistent with higher UCP2) and higher matrix-targeted H2O2 signal (MitoPY1/mito-roGFP2-Orp1) but no proportional rise in cytosolic peroxide reporter. Equal ATP-linked respiration and coupling efficiency, or a cytosol-dominant oxidant signal, would weaken the mechanism.", "Direction-of-causality test by phenocopy: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation in APOE3 microglia (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol, or MT-ATP6/MT-CYB knockdown by mitoTALEN/DdCBE-independent means) should reproduce the APOE4 signature - higher DDIT3/NUPR1/SHMT2, higher PRDX3/PRDX5/UCP2, higher SREBF1/SCD and lysosomal genes - while APOE4 cells should be hypersensitive to the same dose. Failure of APOE3 to move toward the APOE4 profile would argue the mt-subunit deficit is not upstream.", "Rescue test separating oxidant load from assembly: matrix-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ, SkQ1 or mito-catalase expression) should lower DDIT3, NUPR1, PRDX3/PRDX5 and the SREBF1/SCD lipogenic arm in APOE4 without restoring MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2 transcript levels or holo-complex assembly; conversely, allotopic or nuclear-encoded replacement of the missing core subunits should restore both assembly and the stress/lipogenic arms. If mito-antioxidant fully restores assembly and mt-transcripts, the ordering in the mechanism is inverted.", "Specificity test against a mtRNA artefact: an orthogonal, non-10X quantification (spike-in-normalised RT-qPCR or long-read RNA-seq of mt-transcripts, plus mtDNA copy number by qPCR) should confirm a subunit-selective deficit of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2/MT-ND4 with preserved or increased MT-ND5/MT-ND4L and unchanged or modestly reduced mtDNA copy number. A uniform proportional change across all mt-transcripts, or no difference by the orthogonal assay, would identify the signal as a normalisation/ambient artefact and falsify the hypothesis.", "Redox-buffer dependency test: NNT knockdown or GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) should selectively sensitise APOE4 microglia (greater loss of viability, greater lipid peroxidation) relative to APOE3 at matched doses. Equal sensitivity across genotypes would weaken the claim that the antioxidant transcript increase is a compensation for a real oxidant load.", "Peroxisomal alternative (explicitly predicted negative): peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0 / very-long-chain fatty-acid ratios, catalase activity, PMP70 punctae) should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock conditions; a clear peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect would support a competing peroxisomal mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_170", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia show coordinated higher abundance of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - TCA/matrix dehydrogenases (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, DLD, IDH3B), structural subunits of complexes I/II/III/IV/V (e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, UQCRC2, COX6B1, ATP5F1B), carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11) and import/assembly factors (TOMM22, TIMM8B, TIMM44, CHCHD3, COA1, COA8) - exceeding the already upward-shifted background of this selected differential-expression list (permutation p ~ 3e-4 for both the OXPHOS-subunit and TCA sets).", "Step 2 (measured, RNA; opposite direction): transcripts for mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 are lower in APOE4 (4 of 6 mt-transcripts down against a list in which 77% of genes are up; binomial p ~ 0.03), while MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are higher, i.e. the deficit is subunit-selective rather than a uniform loss of mitochondrial RNA.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck, not measured): because complexes III, IV and V each require one or more of these mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, their availability - not the abundant nuclear subunit pool - becomes rate-limiting for holo-complex assembly, leaving nuclear subunits in unassembled subcomplexes and lowering the number of fully coupled respirasomes per unit of expressed machinery.", "Step 4 (inferred activity/flux): partially assembled complex III/IV and a limiting ATP synthase proton-conducting core increase the residence time of reduced quinone/heme carriers and lower ATP-coupled respiration relative to electron input, raising univalent electron leak and matrix H2O2 production per unit of TCA flux.", "Step 5 (measured, RNA; interpreted as compensation): APOE4 cells raise matrix peroxide-handling and NADPH/uncoupling transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT, UCP2, GLUD1) rather than cytosolic pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD and TALDO1 RNA are lower), consistent with an intramitochondrial rather than cytosolic oxidant load.", "Step 6 (measured, RNA; interpreted as downstream stress signalling): the mismatch engages an integrated stress response (EIF2AK3, DDIT3, NUPR1, SHMT2 higher) that, together with a lysosomal-lipogenic shift (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1), diverts carbon into lipid storage and lysosomal turnover instead of oxidative ATP production - the metabolic phenotype that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 at baseline.", "Step 7 (predicted consequence, not measured): the resulting lower ATP-coupled reserve and higher basal oxidant tone lowers the threshold for inflammatory and lipid-laden microglial states (CD74, CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3, GPNMB, ITGAX higher) without a global loss of homeostatic identity (CSF1R, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, MERTK, P2RY12-type genes not reduced)."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch: mtDNA-encoded core subunit deficit against an expanded nuclear OXPHOS/TCA program creates a leak-prone, ISR-activated redox state in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17391815820080228, "cosine_similarity": 0.36148197227423906, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_170", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5892233009708737, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1360078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17391815820080228, "cosine_similarity": 0.36148197227423906, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5892233009708737, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6536065, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 211}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a 77% positive skew (1705/2212); program directions were judged against that skewed background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, CPT1A) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects are kept on the reported scale; protein spots are log2 fold change. RNA and protein were not matched per gene.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for pathway capacity, not for flux, enzyme activity, localization or lipid pool size; no oxygen consumption, lysosomal pH, cholesterol pool, esterification or efflux measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Cathepsin- and v-ATPase-containing spots include both increased (protein_spot:052, 053, 055, 057) and decreased (protein_spot:058, 067, 069, 064, 065) spots, so protein-level support for step 2 is compatible but unresolved.", "The coordinated positive direction of ETC/TCA and lysosomal transcripts is assumed not to be an artifact of pseudobulk normalization or of cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures (10X Flex, astrocyte co-culture); genes are not statistically independent, and the program summaries are descriptive, not formal enrichment tests.", "Effects are attributed to the isogenic APOE4 genotype in the measured mock condition; any reduced reserve under lipid or inflammatory challenge is a prospective expectation, not an observed defect."], "claim": "Under mock treatment at day 30, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 by a coordinated cell-state change in which transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalization and MiT/TFE-type acid-hydrolytic degradation are elevated together with an unusually uniform increase in mitochondrial electron-transport and TCA/carbon-entry transcripts, while committed upper-glycolysis transcripts fall; this pattern is best read as increased catabolic throughput and carbon routing into mitochondria that supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA/NADPH (SLC25A1, ACSS2, ACAT2, NNT, ME1) for a modest SREBP-linked sterol/fatty-acid re-synthesis and esterification/storage branch, not as a sterol shortage or a demonstrated degradative failure. Measured quantities are transcript and protein-spot abundances; flux, sterol pools, lysosomal pH and efflux were not measured, so causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE FLUX TEST: In matched day-30 APOE4 vs APOE3 mock cultures, extracellular flux and 13C tracing should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and greater incorporation of lipoprotein/palmitate-derived 13C into TCA intermediates in APOE4, with equal or lower glycolytic rate. If APOE4 instead shows lower oxygen consumption and higher glycolysis, the routing mechanism (steps 3-4) is falsified even though the ETC transcripts are increased.", "PROSPECTIVE LYSOSOME-MITOCHONDRIA COUPLING TEST: Blocking lysosomal acidification/hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/cathepsin inhibition) should abolish the APOE4-selective excess of lipoprotein-derived carbon entering the TCA cycle and blunt the APOE4-selective increase in SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 transcripts. Persistence of the APOE4 excess under this block would show the lysosomal program is not the substrate source.", "PROSPECTIVE PRECURSOR-SUPPLY TEST: Citrate-carrier (SLC25A1, e.g. CTPI-2) or ACSS2 inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content and SREBP-target transcripts more in APOE4 than APOE3 without lowering lysosomal hydrolase transcripts. No genotype-selective effect would falsify step 4-5 coupling.", "DISCRIMINATION AGAINST THE FAILED-COMPENSATION ALTERNATIVE: Direct sterol imaging/assays (filipin, ER-accessible sterol sensor, free vs esterified cholesterol) should show APOE4 with equal or greater ER-accessible sterol and increased esterified rather than lysosome-trapped free cholesterol. Finding lysosomal free-cholesterol accumulation with reduced ER-accessible sterol and impaired NPC2-dependent egress would favour the competing 'sterol trapped in a failing lysosome drives compensatory SREBP-2 activation' model over this one.", "PROSPECTIVE PROTEIN-LEVEL TEST: Targeted immunoblot/activity assays (not 2-D spots) should show increased mature cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein and increased complex I activity in APOE4. Decreased ATP6V1E1 protein or unchanged complex I activity despite the transcript increases would weaken step 2-3 and favour a transcript-only, non-functional signature.", "CHALLENGE-ONLY PREDICTION (reserve, not an ongoing defect): after a myelin/oxLDL or LPS load, APOE4 should show earlier saturation of lipid clearance and greater CXCL8/IL18 induction than APOE3; absence of any genotype difference under challenge would argue the state is a fully sufficient adaptation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (uptake capacity, measured as RNA): APOE4 raises transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and phagocytic receptors - gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:TREM2 (+1.28), gene:COLEC12 (+1.53), gene:MFGE8 (+1.49), gene:MERTK (+1.30), gene:FCGR1A (+1.59), gene:C1QA/B/C - increasing the potential delivery of extracellular lipid and debris to the endolysosome (inferred routing, not measured uptake).", "STEP 2 (degradative capacity, measured as RNA): a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal program is coordinately elevated - gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:MITF (+1.03), all ten represented v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.94, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.53, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2) and high-magnitude hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.98, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1), plus late-endosomal transport/egress components gene:RAB7A (+2.65) and gene:NPC2 (+1.17). The signature is expanded acid-hydrolytic capacity, i.e. it does not by itself indicate lysosomal failure.", "STEP 3 (substrate routing, measured as RNA): catabolic products are directed to mitochondria: 30 of 31 represented electron-transport transcripts are increased (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.29, gene:NDUFS7 +5.71, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:CYCS +2.58), together with pyruvate/TCA entry and turnover (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:GLUD1 +3.17) and fatty-acid/electron-transfer partners (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24), whereas committed upper glycolysis is reduced (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite higher transporters (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37).", "STEP 4 (cytosolic precursor supply, inferred): increased citrate export and acetyl-CoA/NADPH-generating transcripts (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:ME1 +1.36) with decreased non-oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) would shift cytosolic acetyl-CoA/NADPH sourcing toward mitochondrion-derived carbon.", "STEP 5 (sterol/lipid branch, measured as RNA): this supply sustains a modest but consistently positive lipogenic/sterol arm - gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:HMGCS1 (+1.08), gene:LSS (+2.27), gene:DHCR7 (+2.71), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:EBP (+1.34), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87) - routed toward esterification/storage and oxysterol formation (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:FABP5 +1.13, gene:FABP3 +1.35, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14). Sterol synthesis is a downstream branch of the state, not its strongest or rate-limiting element (canonical gene:HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1, FDFT1, MSMO1, CYP51A1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA rows are absent from the supplied selected list and are therefore unknown, not unchanged).", "STEP 6 (cell-state consequence, partly inferred): the resulting APOE4 state combines high lipid-handling throughput with low-grade innate priming (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:PYCARD +2.43, gene:MYD88 +2.34, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:TLR2 +1.20, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:GPNMB +1.11) and loss of a homeostatic/TGF-beta cue (gene:TGFBR1 -2.19, gene:CSF1 -5.91); reduced spare capacity would be expected to appear only under a future lipid or inflammatory challenge, and is not claimed for the measured mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic routing state that funds a secondary sterol/lipid re-synthesis and esterification branch, rather than a sterol-supply bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24718458073330132, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2975356750893923, "cosine_similarity": 0.3614092168061687, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163009708737864, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24718458073330132, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2975356750893923, "cosine_similarity": 0.3614092168061687, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163009708737864, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.09010225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 50}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_051", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook; effects are used as reported and only compared with each other, never converted to fold changes or compared with the log2 protein scale.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up), so all set-level claims are made against this internal background by permutation, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a read-out of programme induction only; protein abundance, enzyme activity, organelle content, localisation and metabolic flux are inferred and were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each (KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate) and are therefore treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a named protein.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of the RNA signal may be non-cell-autonomous or of mixed cellular origin; biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size reliability cannot be assessed.", "The global up-shift could be partly technical (normalisation, ambient RNA, differences in total mRNA content per cell); set-level enrichment above that shift is assumed to be biological.", "No lipid, sterol, pH, respiration or lysosomal-morphology measurement is supplied; the lipid phenotype is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a lipid-handling imbalance whose bottleneck is lysosomal degradation/egress of internalized lipid cargo: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors (notably SCARB1) are strongly higher, transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits plus TFEB are coordinately higher than the already up-shifted background, sterol-synthesis transcripts are not feedback-repressed, and esterification/neutral-lipid and mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS transcripts are higher while mtDNA-encoded respiratory transcripts are lower. We hypothesise (causality not established) that cargo influx exceeding lysosomal hydrolytic and sterol-egress flux drives compensatory lysosome biogenesis, diversion of lipid into cholesteryl-ester/triglyceride stores, and an oxidative gene program whose realised respiratory capacity is capped by mitonuclear subunit imbalance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown of SCARB1 (or blockade of lipoprotein uptake) in APOE4 microglia should shrink the APOE4-vs-APOE3 gap in lysosomal transcripts (v-ATPase subunits, GBA, HEXA, CTSB/D) and in LysoTracker/filipin-positive lysosomal area, and should reduce cholesteryl-ester content. If lysosomal expansion and the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript excess persist unchanged after uptake blockade, the uptake-driven bottleneck is wrong.", "Lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 cultures should show increased cholesteryl esters and/or triglycerides and increased lysosomal substrates (glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin) in APOE4; if APOE4 instead shows equal or lower cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid content, the esterification/storage arm and the bottleneck are weakened.", "Filipin or LAMP1-colocalised sterol imaging should show more unesterified cholesterol retained in APOE4 lysosomes; a normal lysosomal sterol distribution with unchanged ER sterol sensing would weaken step 2 and step 4.", "SOAT1 inhibition should convert the predicted APOE4 cholesteryl-ester excess into free cholesterol with increased efflux/toxicity rather than reducing total sterol; no baseline cholesteryl-ester excess to redistribute would falsify step 5.", "Low-dose v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin) or hydrolase inhibition should impair lipid clearance and increase lipid-droplet accumulation disproportionately in APOE4 relative to APOE3; equal sensitivity would argue against a lysosomal capacity bottleneck.", "Mitonuclear sub-prediction: assembled complex I/IV levels and basal/maximal oxygen consumption should NOT increase in APOE4 in proportion to the large nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase (mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower); a proportional increase in respiration would falsify the mitonuclear-imbalance step, though not the lysosomal bottleneck.", "Because the mechanism is uptake- and cargo-driven rather than identity-driven, core microglial identity genes should stay near background (observed: CSF1R, P2RY12-class genes near the global shift); a genotype effect dominated instead by an interferon or NF-kB inflammatory programme would favour an alternative mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA only): the lipoprotein/lipid uptake module is higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22 in the reported log unit; gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE all positive). Inferred, not measured: a higher rate of lipoprotein/lipid internalisation into the endolysosomal system; no uptake flux, lipid mass or receptor protein was measured.", "Inferred bottleneck: delivered cholesterol/sphingolipid cargo exceeds the hydrolytic and lysosome-to-ER sterol-egress flux of the APOE4 lysosome, so cargo dwell time in the lysosomal lumen increases. Lysosomal lipid content, pH and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Measured (RNA): a coordinated lysosomal-biogenesis-like signature (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB; set mean +2.79 vs +1.39 global mean, permutation p\u22480.0015). Inferred: MiT/TFE-type compensatory expansion of the degradative compartment; increased hydrolase protein or activity is NOT established (protein spots are multi-candidate and mixed in direction).", "Measured (RNA): sterol-synthesis/SREBP-associated transcripts remain positive rather than repressed (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1) despite the large uptake-receptor increase. Inferred: ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol is not raised in APOE4, consistent with sterol being retained in lysosomal or esterified pools; no sterol pool was measured.", "Measured (RNA): esterification/neutral-lipid and desaturation transcripts are higher (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD). Inferred: lipid that cannot be exported as free sterol is routed into cholesteryl-ester and triglyceride stores, predicting a lipid-droplet-biased lipidome in APOE4.", "Measured (RNA): nuclear-encoded TCA/carrier and OXPHOS transcripts are higher than background (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47; nuclear OXPHOS set mean +2.81, permutation p\u22480.0003, e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2), while mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2; set mean -0.82, one-sided p\u22480.02). Inferred: increased ATP/acetyl-CoA demand for acidification and lipid turnover, with mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance that may cap the actual increase in assembled respiratory complexes; respiration, complex assembly and ATP flux were not measured."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-disposal capacity is the limiting step in APOE4 microglia: receptor-driven lipid uptake outruns hydrolysis/egress, forcing TFEB-type lysosome expansion, neutral-lipid esterification and an oxidative mitochondrial gene program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1413582489201911, "cosine_similarity": 0.36132206472867273, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6171359223300971, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1413582489201911, "cosine_similarity": 0.36132206472867273, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6171359223300971, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8473125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 212}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_080", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive); only within-list relative rank/percentile comparisons are interpreted, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme capacity; NADPH/NADP+ ratio, peroxide levels, PPP flux, respiration, Prx oxidation state and lipid peroxidation were not measured in this dataset and are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes (e.g. CAT in protein_spot:017, PRDX2 in protein_spot:077, TKT in protein_spot:038, G6PD/GSR/PGD in protein_spot:021) and are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only; spot-level RNA-protein correlation across spots with measured candidates is ~0 (r=-0.05).", "The peroxisomal arm of the assigned focus is rejected: no PEX, CAT, HSD17B4, AGPS, GNPAT or FAR RNA rows are present, ABCD1 is down and ACOX1/CROT/SCP2 are unremarkable relative to the global shift, so peroxisomal beta-oxidation is not invoked as the bottleneck.", "Cell-intrinsic interpretation assumes the APOE4/APOE3 difference is not dominated by differing microglia:astrocyte composition or by cell-state/library-size normalisation differences in the co-culture."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a larger oxidant-handling load than APOE3 (higher transcripts for mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport machinery, lysosomal hydrolases and lipid uptake/esterification) and up-regulate the peroxidase side of the thiol-redox system (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GSS, MSRA, NNT), while transcripts for cytosolic NADPH regeneration (TALDO1, PGD, NADK) sit in the low tail of the same differential-expression list; we hypothesise that reductant (NADPH) regeneration, not peroxidase protein abundance, is the rate-limiting step, so peroxiredoxin/glutathione cycles in APOE4 run in a more oxidised steady state and sustain a chronic, sub-lethal oxidative-signalling and lipid-storage phenotype. This is a proposed, not established, causal chain.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Direct metabolite test: in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, the NADPH/NADP+ ratio and oxidative-PPP flux (1,2-13C glucose lactate labelling) should be lower in APOE4 despite equal-or-higher PRDX2/PRDX3/GPX4 protein; equal or higher NADPH/NADP+ and PPP flux in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation (reductant-limited vs scavenger-limited): partial inhibition of NADPH supply (G6PDi-1, or TALDO1/TKT knockdown) at a dose that barely changes APOE3 should disproportionately increase Prx2/Prx3 dimer and hyperoxidised (Prx-SO2/3H) fractions and cytosolic/mitochondrial roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation in APOE4; conversely, over-expressing peroxidase capacity alone (GPX4 or PRDX3) should NOT normalise APOE4 redox poise, whereas expressing an NADPH-independent peroxide sink (mitochondria-targeted catalase) or restoring supply (G6PD over-expression, cytosolic IDH1) should. Equal sensitivity of both genotypes to G6PD inhibition, or full rescue by GPX4/PRDX3 over-expression alone, would falsify the bottleneck placement.", "Mito-nuclear step: immunoblot/absolute proteomics should show a lower mtDNA-encoded (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6, MT-CYB) to nuclear-encoded (NDUFS1, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) subunit ratio and higher mitochondrial H2O2 (MitoPY1/mito-roGFP2-Orp1) in APOE4; an unchanged ratio with unchanged mitochondrial peroxide would remove step 1 while leaving steps 3-4 testable.", "Phenotypic coupling: NADPH-supply restoration or mito-catalase should reduce neutral-lipid (BODIPY) and lysosomal (LysoTracker/CTSB activity) expansion in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; unchanged lipid/lysosome phenotype after full normalisation of redox poise would show the redox node is a bystander.", "Negative control from the same data: because ACSL4 and ALOX15 transcripts are low and GPX4 is high in APOE4, we predict no increased ferroptosis sensitivity (RSL3/erastin EC50 unchanged or shifted to resistance); increased ferroptosis sensitivity in APOE4 would indicate a lipid-peroxidation-driven mechanism rather than the proposed NADPH-limitation mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation and TCA/pyruvate-import transcripts are shifted upward relative to the rest of the selected DE list (nuclear OXPHOS set n=39, mean percentile 0.68, rank-sum z=+4.0; TCA/pyruvate set n=8, mean percentile 0.85, z=+3.5), whereas the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts trend downward (mean percentile 0.28, z=-1.9). Inferred (not measured): a mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch during complex assembly that raises electron leak and matrix H2O2 production per unit respiration.", "Measured: lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts (GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H/1A) and lipid uptake/esterification/desaturation transcripts (SCARB1, SMPD1, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1) are high in APOE4. Inferred: increased flux of lipid substrate into lysosomal catabolism and into NADPH-consuming reductive steps (desaturation, sterol synthesis), adding peroxide and lipid-hydroperoxide load on top of step 1.", "Measured: the peroxidase/thiol-repair arm is coordinately elevated (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GSS, MSRA, SELENOW, MGST2, AKR1A1, NNT; n=12, mean percentile 0.81, z=+3.8). Inferred: a compensatory transcriptional response to an existing oxidant load rather than an increase in achieved antioxidant flux.", "Measured: transcripts for the NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate/NAD-kinase arm are among the down-shifted minority in a list whose global median effect is positive (TALDO1 percentile 0.10, PGD 0.19, NADK 0.21, ME1 0.45; demand-set vs supply-set rank test z=+2.9, p=0.004). Inferred (bottleneck): NADPH regeneration capacity per cell does not scale with the enlarged peroxidase demand.", "Inferred consequence (not measured here): peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin and glutathione couples operate at a lower reduced fraction in APOE4, so peroxide clearance becomes reductant-limited and Prx2/Prx3 spend more time in disulfide/hyperoxidised forms; this is a redox-poise change, not a change in scavenger protein amount.", "Inferred output: persistent low-grade oxidative signalling reinforces lipid esterification/storage and lysosomal expansion instead of efficient lipid oxidation, giving the APOE4-versus-APOE3 steady-state difference observed under mock treatment."], "title": "NADPH-regeneration is the limiting node for an expanded thiol-peroxidase demand in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2442491599896614, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2759064643496031, "cosine_similarity": 0.36067753009745995, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6270388349514563, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2442491599896614, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2759064643496031, "cosine_similarity": 0.36067753009745995, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6270388349514563, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61182025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 213}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_049", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46; 77% positive) and an unspecified logarithm base; all module claims are made as rank/median enrichment relative to that internal background, not as absolute up-regulation.", "Coordinated transcript changes across a pathway are taken as a proxy for changed enzymatic capacity; enzyme protein, activity, localization and metabolic flux were not measured, and transcript-to-flux coupling may fail (especially for SCD, SLC25A1, ACSS2 and the lysosomal hydrolases).", "The mitochondrial module is interpreted as carbon-export capacity rather than respiratory biogenesis because mtDNA-encoded subunits move in the opposite direction; this interpretation would change if mitochondrial mass were shown to be increased.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features and are not treated as uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as identification of a lysosomal, mitochondrial or lipogenic protein.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex pseudobulk-style comparison; ambient RNA from astrocytes, differing capture depth and unreported replicate structure could inflate or distort module-level effects.", "APOE4 acts here through the protein variant rather than through APOE transcript level (APOE effect +1.24, below the global median shift)."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated, direction-consistent transcript program for lysosomal hydrolysis, mitochondrial citrate/anaplerotic carbon handling, and SREBP-1-dependent fatty-acid desaturation plus esterification. We propose the rate-limiting node is cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate supply (mitochondrial citrate export via SLC25A1 plus acetate salvage via ACSS2), which converts lysosome-liberated and mitochondrially processed carbon into de novo monounsaturated fatty acid and sterol synthesis and then into esterified neutral lipid, rather than into terminal oxidation or efflux. Causality is not established by these data; only RNA and ambiguous 2D protein spots were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: inhibiting the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) or ACLY (BMS-303141) in mock APOE4 microglia should reduce 13C-glucose incorporation into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester and collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 neutral-lipid droplet difference, while leaving lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, GBA, ATP6V1A) and TFEB transcript essentially unchanged. If droplet excess and lipid labeling persist unchanged after this block, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Upstream ordering test: v-ATPase or cathepsin inhibition (bafilomycin A1, E64d/pepstatin) should increase undigested substrate in both genotypes but should NOT abolish the APOE4-specific SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1 transcript elevation if the bottleneck is downstream. If v-ATPase inhibition equalizes the lipogenic program between genotypes, the lysosomal arm is upstream-limiting and this hypothesis must be re-ordered.", "Lipidome direction: APOE4 lipids should be enriched in monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester species; SCD inhibition should shift APOE4 toward saturated species and induce integrated-stress markers (e.g., DDIT3) more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3. A lipidome with no genotype difference in MUFA-containing neutral lipids weakens the mechanism.", "Respiration control: Seahorse profiling should NOT show a proportional APOE4 increase in maximal Complex I-linked respiration matching the nuclear NDUF transcript shift; a uniform increase in respiration with no increase in citrate export or lipogenic labeling would favor a simple mitochondrial-biogenesis explanation over this hypothesis.", "Artifact control: after depth-matched pseudobulk resampling and ambient-RNA correction, the lysosomal/CLEAR, mitochondrial-carbon and lipogenic modules should retain their positive rank offset relative to the global shift. If these modules lose enrichment under such controls, the observation base for the hypothesis is technical rather than biological.", "Rejected focus test: phagocytic-receptor and actin-cytoskeletal transcript modules are not enriched over the global shift here, so live-cell phagocytic uptake rate (bead/synaptosome) should differ little between APOE4 and APOE3 at baseline; a large baseline uptake deficit that is unaffected by SLC25A1/ACLY inhibition would point to a cytoskeletal/phagocytic mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show coordinately higher transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and the v-ATPase (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C, LAMP1, NPC2) together with the CLEAR-network transcription factor TFEB. We infer, but did not measure, an expanded acidified lysosomal compartment with increased hydrolytic capacity that liberates free fatty acids and sterols from internalized lipid substrate (uptake receptors SCARB1 and CD36 transcripts are also higher). Lysosomal protein abundance, pH, TFEB nuclear localization and hydrolase activity are NOT measured here.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Mitochondrial carbon-handling transcripts are coordinately higher (MPC2 pyruvate carrier, ACO2, OGDH, MDH1, IDH3B, DLD, and the carriers SLC25A1 citrate and SLC25A11), while mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB) are lower. We therefore infer increased capacity for TCA-cycle carbon handling and citrate export, not a general increase in respiratory-chain flux.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck; largely inferred): Exported citrate plus ACSS2-dependent acetate salvage raises the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool. This node is rate-limiting for the downstream lipogenic program. ACLY, ACACA and FASN transcripts are absent from the supplied differential-expression list, and no metabolite or flux measurement is supplied, so the acetyl-CoA pool itself is unmeasured and must not be treated as observed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA; inferred activity): The SREBP-controlled biosynthetic program is uniformly higher in APOE4 (SREBF1, SCD, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, DHCR7, ACAT2, LDLR, INSIG1; 15/15 lipogenic genes positive). We infer increased de novo synthesis of monounsaturated fatty acids and of post-squalene sterol intermediates; SREBP proteolytic activation and nuclear SREBP protein were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Esterification and storage enzymes are higher (AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1), predicting diversion of the newly made and lysosome-derived lipid into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester rather than membrane turnover or export.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype, not measured): The net APOE4-specific consequence is an enlarged, monounsaturated-enriched neutral-lipid droplet pool with cholesteryl-ester accumulation, which would secondarily blunt sustained phagocytic and inflammatory responses. No lipidomic, droplet-imaging or efflux (ABCA1/ABCG1 unmeasured) data are supplied to test this step."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lysosome-derived and mitochondrial carbon into a cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate-export bottleneck that drives SREBP-1 desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2814311560757671, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23720261722474908, "cosine_similarity": 0.36012883581521504, "direction_accuracy": 0.27993527508090615, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5998608414239482, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2814311560757671, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23720261722474908, "cosine_similarity": 0.36012883581521504, "direction_accuracy": 0.27993527508090615, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5998608414239482, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1055365, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 214}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_035", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook, so only sign, rank and percentile within this list are used; no absolute fold-change is claimed.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a thresholded, pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) with a strong global positive skew (77% up, median +1.46). Enrichment is therefore judged against this list's own background, and absence of a gene (e.g. HSPA5, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2) is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Protein spots carry 2-8 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level effects are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate, at least in rank, with the corresponding protein and enzymatic capacity; enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, membrane integrity, lipid-droplet content and any lipid or sterol pool were not measured in the supplied data.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so p-values may be inflated by a pseudo-replicated single-cell design; extreme effects (|effect| \u003e 6) are treated as unreliable in magnitude and used only qualitatively.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype-associated transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous rather than intrinsic to APOE4 microglia.", "The comparison is a static isogenic contrast under mock treatment; no causal direction between uptake, lysosomal load and storage has been established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by an expanded lipid/lipoprotein scavenging and endolysosomal catabolic transcriptional program (scavenger receptors, MiT/TFE factors TFEB/MITF/TFEC, lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits) that is accompanied by increased neutral-lipid esterification and desaturation machinery (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, SREBF1). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is lysosomal hydrolysis/export of internalised lipid: cargo influx exceeds clearance capacity, the shortfall is sensed as a lysosomal-demand signal that drives compensatory MiT/TFE-dependent lysosome-biogenesis transcription, and unclearable sterol/fatty acid is re-routed to ER-based esterification and droplet-type storage rather than efflux, locking APOE4 microglia into a lipid-laden, GPNMB/APOE-high, glycolysis-lowered state. Only RNA abundance and ambiguous 2-D protein spots were measured; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, lipid flux and lipid-droplet content were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pulse-chase loading of APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with labelled lipoprotein, myelin debris or BODIPY-cholesteryl ester. The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalisation but slower per-cell degradation/clearance of the lipid label in APOE4, with accumulation in LAMP1-positive compartments despite the higher hydrolase transcript program. Equal or faster lipid clearance kinetics in APOE4 would falsify the capacity-limited bottleneck.", "SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester/droplet content and raise free-sterol-dependent readouts while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase/MiT-TFE transcript elevation largely intact, because storage is downstream of the bottleneck. If SOAT1 inhibition abolishes the CTSD/GBA/TFEB transcript elevation, storage is upstream and step 5 is wrong.", "Removing the sterol load (cyclodextrin or an LXR agonist promoting efflux) should normalise the APOE4-specific lysosomal and lipogenic transcript program more than in APOE3. If the lysosomal program is unchanged after cellular sterol is lowered, a lipid-load-driven demand signal is not the driver.", "TFEB knockdown (or MiT/TFE triple knockdown) should preferentially worsen lipid accumulation and cargo clearance in APOE4 relative to APOE3, because the program is compensatory. If TFEB loss has no genotype-selective effect, step 4 is not compensatory.", "Direct activity assays should show that GBA, HEXA and cathepsin B/D specific activity per cell is not increased in proportion to their transcript elevation in APOE4. If activity scales fully with transcript and lipid clearance rate matches APOE3, the compensation is sufficient and the mechanism is weakened.", "ER-stress test of the rejected alternative: APOE4 cells should not show baseline XBP1 splicing, BiP/GRP94 protein induction or eIF2alpha-P elevation over APOE3 under mock conditions, and PERK or IRE1 inhibition should not normalise the lysosomal/lipid transcript program. Observing baseline XBP1 splicing plus rescue by UPR inhibition would overturn this hypothesis in favour of the ER-proteostasis model.", "Golgi-collapse alternative: if the incoherent Golgi/tether signal (gene:GOLPH3L, gene:GCC1, gene:TRAPPC6B down but gene:GOLPH3, gene:TRAPPC3, gene:COG7 up) reflects real biology, APOE4 cells should show measurably delayed anterograde cargo (RUSH assay) and Golgi fragmentation; absence of such a defect supports treating that signal as noise, as assumed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/lipid scavenging receptors and lipid-handling ectoenzymes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:MRC1, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:PLA2G7). We infer, but did not measure, a higher rate of lipid and lipoprotein internalisation.", "Step 2 (inferred trafficking): increased cargo raises traffic through the maturing endosome-lysosome, consistent with elevated endolysosomal maturation and sorting transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:STX12, gene:IGF2R). Localization and cargo delivery were not directly measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): hydrolytic and export capacity of the lysosome for sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo is exceeded. Persistent undegraded cargo, plus a lysosomal membrane-stress marker (gene:LGALS3), constitutes the demand signal; the neutral lipid ester and free-sterol pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): the cell responds with a coordinated MiT/TFE-type lysosome-biogenesis transcriptional program - transcription factors (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC) with hydrolases and acidification machinery (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:ACP5, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1). We read this induction as compensation for unmet demand, not as proof of increased hydrolase activity.", "Step 5 (inferred routing): because clearance is limiting, lipid is diverted to esterified storage rather than disposal - cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol synthases and their monounsaturated fatty-acid supply are up (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:FABP5), with an intact/raised SREBP-type program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24) implying that ER-accessible free sterol is not perceived as high; this creates a feed-forward uptake-storage loop.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, phenotypic output): the resulting state is the lipid-laden, APOE-high scavenging phenotype (gene:APOE, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS1, gene:MPEG1, gene:SLC11A1, gene:CPVL) with reduced glycolytic commitment (gene:HK2 decreased), predicted to lower spare capacity for further phagocytic/lipid cargo.", "Step 7 (explicit rejection of the assigned focus): a canonical ER unfolded-protein-response bottleneck is not supported - the UPR/ERAD gene set is not shifted relative to this list's own strongly positive background (module median +1.98 vs background median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.41), ERAD components move down (gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1, gene:PDIA3), core UPR genes (HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, HERPUD1, CALR, CANX, SEC61 subunits) are absent from the supplied list, and the protein spots whose candidate lists include ER chaperones are non-significant and slightly negative (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal lipid-clearance capacity, not by ER unfolded-protein signalling: scavenger-driven lipid influx forces a MiT/TFE lysosomal program and diversion of sterol into SOAT1/DGAT1 esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1771037181996086, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09031041862621642, "cosine_similarity": 0.3600749105705402, "direction_accuracy": 0.29449838187702265, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6178349514563107, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1771037181996086, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09031041862621642, "cosine_similarity": 0.3600749105705402, "direction_accuracy": 0.29449838187702265, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6178349514563107, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03478, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 215}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a supplied selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base; 77% (1705/2212) of rows are positive, so 'most members up' is judged against that skewed background, not 50/50, and absolute magnitudes are compared by rank within the same list.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, PLIN2, LIPA, FASN, ACLY) are unknown, not unchanged; the sterol-synthesis and efflux modules are therefore only partially observed.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for capacity, not activity: elevated hydrolase/v-ATPase mRNA does not establish increased lysosomal degradation, and elevated SREBP-2 target mRNA is treated as an indirect readout of low ER regulatory sterol, not as a measurement of that pool.", "Pathway members were pre-specified from canonical membership before their signs were inspected; members were not dropped to make directions agree, and genes are not independent (shared transcription factors), so coherence is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate identities; all candidates are preserved and no spot is credited to one protein. Spot 043-046 (+1.96 to +3.05) are compatible with ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) rather than TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32) but do not confirm either.", "The measured system is a microglia-astrocyte co-culture; some transcript differences may reflect altered cell-state proportions or astrocyte contribution rather than cell-autonomous microglial regulation.", "The mechanism asserts an ongoing routing bias in the mock condition; any additional fragility (e.g. to myelin or lipoprotein loading) is a future-challenge prediction, not something demonstrated by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the selected RNA changes describe one coordinated cell state rather than a single failing enzyme: lipid/lipoprotein acquisition (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:C1QA +1.25), an expanded TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-degradative module (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:NPC2 +1.17), mitochondrial acetyl-CoA/citrate supply (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93), esterification/neutral-lipid storage and monounsaturated lipid synthesis (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ABHD5 +1.04, gene:CIDEB +1.06), and an UNREPRESSED SREBP-2/sterol-synthesis program (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08) are all elevated at once, while oxysterol-generating/LXR-arm genes are also elevated (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14). Simultaneous activation of a sterol-deficiency-type program and a sterol-excess-type program is the signature of compartmental mis-routing: sterol and fatty acid are preferentially channelled into esterified storage and the lysosomal compartment instead of the ER-accessible regulatory pool, so uptake and de novo synthesis are not switched off. This is a claim about measured transcript abundance plus inferred routing; no flux, lipid pool, enzyme activity or localization was measured here, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, discriminating: acute SOAT1/ACAT1 inhibition (avasimibe or CI-976) in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should raise the ER-accessible sterol pool and repress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) toward APOE3 levels while lowering cholesteryl ester content. If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated after esterification is blocked, the 'sterol trapped in storage/lysosome' routing step is wrong and a sterol-independent driver (e.g. mTORC1/LXR-driven anabolic state) is favoured.", "PROSPECTIVE lipidomic prediction in the same mock condition: APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for cholesteryl esters and for monounsaturated (16:1/18:1-containing) triacylglycerol, with a reduced free-cholesterol:cholesteryl-ester ratio; the ratio prediction is the strong one. Finding equal or higher free-cholesterol:cholesteryl-ester ratio and no neutral-lipid excess in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition should shift APOE4 neutral lipids toward saturated species and, if storage capacity is the sink, reduce the elevation of the SREBP-2 target program; no change in either would argue that gene:SCD elevation is a passive marker.", "PROSPECTIVE phenocopy test: blocking lysosomal cholesterol export in APOE3 microglia (U18666A) should reproduce the APOE4 signature of simultaneously high SREBP-2 targets and high TFEB/CLEAR transcripts; failure to reproduce it would argue the two programs are independently driven in APOE4.", "PROSPECTIVE activity test of the unmeasured decisive variable: direct measurement of lysosomal hydrolase activity and of nuclear SREBP-2 protein. The mechanism predicts increased or preserved hydrolase activity (not a degradative bottleneck) together with increased nuclear SREBP-2 despite higher total cellular sterol. Reduced hydrolase activity with reduced nuclear SREBP-2 would refute this mechanism and support a simple lysosomal-degradation failure instead.", "PROSPECTIVE challenge-only prediction (explicitly not claimed for the measured condition): loading with myelin debris or acetylated LDL should produce a larger cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet increment in APOE4 than APOE3; equal increments would show the baseline routing bias does not reduce reserve."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and phagocytic-receptor genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6), consistent with greater delivery of exogenous lipid to the endolysosomal system; delivery rate itself is not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred routing): The delivered load enters an expanded, TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal compartment (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H/ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C/ATP6AP1, hydrolases gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA/HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, cholesterol carrier gene:NPC2), i.e. degradative capacity is scaled up rather than transcriptionally lost.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Carbon for lipid anabolism is supplied by an unusually strongly elevated mitochondrial TCA/citrate-export and acetate module (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2), the highest-magnitude coherent module in the data, while glycolysis/oxidative PPP genes are mixed-to-down (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) - an oxidative, biosynthetic rather than glycolytic state.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Acetyl-CoA and fatty acid are directed into esterified storage species: sterol esterification (gene:SOAT1), triacylglycerol/glycerolipid assembly (gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, with gene:GPAT3 -2.23 and gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11 indicating re-routing rather than uniform lipogenic induction) and desaturation to monounsaturates (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59).", "Step 5 (inferred state, the discriminating step): Because sterol is consumed by esterification and retained in lysosomal/storage compartments, the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool stays low, so SREBP-2 target transcription is not switched off despite high uptake (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR all up), while a separate excess-sensing arm is engaged elsewhere (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7). The two arms are contradictory for a single well-mixed sterol pool and are jointly explicable only by compartmentalisation.", "Step 6 (predicted consequence in the measured mock condition): The uptake + synthesis + esterification cycle is self-reinforcing and predicts a neutral-lipid-loaded APOE4 state at baseline - higher cholesteryl ester and monounsaturated (16:1/18:1) triacylglycerol content, a lower free-cholesterol:cholesteryl-ester ratio, and altered sphingolipid handling downstream of the elevated hydrolase/glycosphingolipid module (gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXA/HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27) - rather than a defect revealed only by later challenge.", "Step 7 (protein-level compatibility, not confirmation): 2-D spot data are compatible with, but cannot confirm, this state: spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal proteins are split (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:057 +0.59, protein_spot:063 +0.68 up vs protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 down), so no individual hydrolase or v-ATPase protein increase is established."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route acquired and newly made lipid into esterified/lysosomal storage, leaving the ER regulatory sterol pool low and locking in a dual SREBP-2 + lysosomal-biogenesis state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2626647712587232, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24477133913331553, "cosine_similarity": 0.35993785504302445, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6062621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2626647712587232, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24477133913331553, "cosine_similarity": 0.35993785504302445, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6062621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.69604925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 51}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_083", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a |effect| \u003e= 1 filter and an unspecified logarithm base; relative rank within this list, not absolute fold change, is used as evidence.", "The genotype-wide upward shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46) is partly technical/compositional, so only genes clearly displaced from that shift (e.g. gene:M6PR down, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H far up) are treated as informative.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D features; ATP6V1E1 and cathepsin attributions are provisional and could instead reflect co-migrating ANXA1, ACTB, keratin or other candidates.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an upper bound on, not a measure of, hydrolase activity, luminal delivery, lumenal pH or degradative flux, none of which were measured.", "Cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect altered cell-type proportions or ambient RNA rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcript-level expansion of the lysosomal/CLEAR program (acid hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits, TFEB) that is not matched at the protein-spot level, while the mannose-6-phosphate sorting receptor M6PR is one of the few strongly downregulated transcripts against a genotype-wide upward RNA shift; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is post-transcriptional degradative capacity per endolysosome (receptor-mediated hydrolase delivery plus V1-V0 acidification), so that cargo processing flux lags an increased uptake/lipogenic load rather than being limited by hydrolase transcription. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: re-expressing CD-MPR (M6PR) in APOE4 microglia, or re-acidifying lysosomes with acidic nanoparticles, should raise luminal mature-hydrolase content and DQ-BSA/BODIPY-cargo degradation rate and lower stored neutral lipid, without requiring any further increase in hydrolase transcripts. If DQ-BSA dequenching per lysosome and mature-cathepsin content are already equal to or greater in APOE4 than APOE3 at baseline, the capacity-bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Ratiometric LysoSensor/LysoTracker-independent pH measurement should show a modestly higher (less acidic) lysosomal pH in APOE4; identical lysosomal pH across genotypes would remove step 4.", "Immunoblot should show an increased pro-cathepsin D : mature cathepsin D ratio intracellularly and increased hydrolase activity in conditioned medium in APOE4; a uniform increase in mature cathepsin with no secretion difference would contradict steps 3 and 5.", "TFEB overexpression alone should not normalise cargo degradation or lipid storage in APOE4 (transcription is not the limiting step), whereas combined TFEB induction plus restored acidification/delivery should; correction by TFEB alone would weaken the bottleneck assignment.", "Pulse-chase of fluorescent oxLDL/myelin cargo should show slower cargo clearance in APOE4 with normal or increased internalisation rate; equal clearance kinetics with increased uptake only would favour a pure uptake-driven alternative.", "If instead the primary difference is mitochondrial (the TCA/OXPHOS transcript set is the most extreme set here), then inhibiting oxidative phosphorylation should reproduce the APOE4 lipid phenotype in APOE3 cells while lysosomal re-acidification fails to rescue APOE4; that outcome would displace this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred demand): APOE4 microglia carry a higher lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and lipogenic transcript load (gene:SCARB1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:IGF2R), which we infer increases endolysosomal cargo delivery; cargo flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A CLEAR-type degradative program is transcriptionally elevated above the genotype-wide upward shift (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:DPP7, gene:CTSK, gene:RAB7A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C); we interpret this as a compensatory demand signal, not as proof of increased enzyme activity.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck, measured RNA + inferred trafficking): The M6P delivery arm is discordant - the tagging subunit transcript is up (gene:GNPTG) while the CD-mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript is strongly down (gene:M6PR, 15th percentile of a list whose median effect is +1.46) and the CI-MPR transcript only tracks background (gene:IGF2R). We infer reduced receptor-mediated routing of newly made hydrolases to the lumen, with a shift toward constitutive secretion of immature enzyme.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck, protein spots + RNA, inferred activity): Acidification capacity does not scale with transcript. V-ATPase V1-subunit candidate spots are significantly lower in APOE4 (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065) despite up V-ATPase transcripts, and gene:PSEN1 is down; we infer lower assembled/active V1-V0 per lysosome and a less acidic lumen. Lysosomal pH was not measured and spot identities are ambiguous.", "Step 5 (protein spots, inferred processing): Cathepsin-candidate spots are redistributed rather than uniformly raised (protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:052 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:055 up), consistent with altered pro-enzyme/mature-enzyme processing or charge/mass isoform shift rather than with a net increase in mature hydrolase; assignment to CTSD/CTSB/CTSL/HEXB is not unique.", "Step 6 (inferred outcome): Degradative flux per unit cargo therefore falls below load, undegraded lipid and membrane cargo is inferred to accumulate in late endosomes/lysosomes, and continued SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1 activity diverts sterol and fatty acid into stored neutral lipid; lipid species were not measured here.", "Step 7 (feed-forward): Persistent sub-threshold luminal degradation is inferred to keep the TFEB/CLEAR transcriptional program engaged, producing the observed RNA-up / protein-flat-to-down discordance in the same pathway."], "title": "APOE4 microglia transcriptionally expand the CLEAR/hydrolase program but are bottlenecked at M6PR-dependent hydrolase delivery and V-ATPase acidification capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12035225048923678, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12439292730480778, "cosine_similarity": 0.35944417358172726, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6420906148867314, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12035225048923678, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12439292730480778, "cosine_similarity": 0.35944417358172726, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6420906148867314, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.970091, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 216}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_024", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive); genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged, and all sign patterns are judged against this 77% up background, not 50/50.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and the magnitudes are implausibly large for log2 (range -7.9 to +15.5), so RNA effects are treated as directional/ordinal on their original reported scale, not as quantitative fold changes.", "Co-regulated pathway members are not statistically independent; the descriptive sign coherence reported here (e.g. 33/33 nuclear ETC subunits up) is not a formal enrichment test.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a proxy for direction of program engagement only. PDH activity, ETC complex assembly, citrate export flux, SREBP processing, TFEB nuclear localization, NADPH/ATP levels and lipid-droplet content were not measured; all flux, activity and localization statements are inferred.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels from a probe-based 10X Flex assay are assumed to reflect genotype biology rather than capture/normalization artefact; only 6 mtDNA-encoded rows are supplied, so this arm rests on few observations.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each, keratin/actin-dominated); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot directions are used only for compatibility/contradiction testing.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of the RNA signal could be non-microglial or ambient; genotype-specific astrocyte contribution is unmeasured.", "Causality is not established: the mechanism describes the most parsimonious causal reading of correlated abundance changes in one mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative program (all 33 represented nuclear ETC subunits up, plus import, assembly, chaperone, TCA and malate-aspartate shuttle transcripts) that is discordant with lower steady-state mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 down), while glycolytic-commitment and pentose-phosphate transcripts fall (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1) despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3). We propose this represents demand-driven routing of carbon into mitochondrial oxidation and citrate export (SLC25A1) toward an SREBP-linked sterol/lipid-storage and lysosomal program, in a state that is compensated at rest but has a narrowed cytosolic glycolytic/PPP buffer and an assembled-ETC capacity limited by mtDNA-encoded subunits; increased nuclear transcripts are not evidence of increased assembled complexes or of higher measured flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, mtDNA copy number per nuclear genome and mtDNA-encoded protein (MT-CO1/MT-CO2 immunoblot) normalized to mitochondrial mass (TOMM20/citrate synthase) will be lower, while nuclear-encoded subunits (NDUFB8, ATP5F1B, UQCRC2) are equal or higher, and BN-PAGE will show reduced assembled complex I/IV/V relative to the nuclear subunit pool. If assembled complexes and mtDNA-encoded proteins scale up in proportion with the nuclear transcripts, the mitonuclear-discordance core of the mechanism is falsified and the data are better explained by successful expansion of oxidative capacity.", "Prospective (discriminating, adaptation vs limited reserve): Seahorse profiling in mock will show APOE4 basal OCR equal or modestly higher than APOE3 but reduced FCCP-stimulated spare respiratory capacity and reduced post-oligomycin glycolytic reserve, with no increase in basal ECAR. Higher maximal OCR plus equal or greater glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism and favour increased oxidative throughput without a narrowed buffer.", "Prospective: U-13C-glucose and U-13C-glutamine tracing will show, in APOE4, reduced labelling of oxidative/non-oxidative PPP intermediates (6-phosphogluconate, sedoheptulose-7-phosphate, ribose-5-phosphate) consistent with lower HK2/PFKP/PGD/TALDO1 transcripts, together with equal or increased citrate labelling and increased 13C incorporation into cholesterol, cholesteryl ester and monounsaturated fatty-acid pools. Unchanged 13C flow into sterol/lipid pools would falsify the citrate-export routing step (step 5) while leaving steps 1-4 intact.", "Prospective perturbation: pharmacological block of the citrate carrier (CTPI-2) or ACLY knockdown will reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation and SREBP target transcripts (SCD, HMGCS1, DHCR24) preferentially in APOE4 relative to APOE3, and will not further lower APOE4 basal OCR. An equal-magnitude genotype-independent effect, or a selective OCR collapse in APOE4, would argue the lipid program is not fed by the proposed mitochondrial citrate route.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not ongoing defect): switching glucose for galactose, or adding a low-dose complex I/V inhibitor or a phagocytic lipid load (myelin, apoptotic neurons), will cause a larger fall in ATP/viability and a larger rise in ISR markers in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas mock ATP levels are similar between genotypes. Equal challenge sensitivity would show no reduced reserve and would weaken the mechanism; conversely a large mock ATP deficit would indicate an ongoing defect stronger than proposed.", "Prospective identity test for the ambiguous spots: targeted immunoblot/MS of the strongly increased spot series (protein_spot:043-047) will assign the increase to ANXA1 (RNA gene:ANXA1 +4.15) rather than TALDO1 (RNA gene:TALDO1 -2.32). If TALDO1 protein is confirmed as increased in those spots, the reduced-PPP element of step 3 is contradicted and must be dropped."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry a mitonuclear expression mismatch at rest: the four mtDNA-encoded transcripts MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are lower (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L higher) while every represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcript is higher (e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFB6, UQCRC2, CYCS, COX7A2, ATP5ME, ATP5MC3). This is measured abundance; mtDNA copy number, transcription rate and assembled complex content were not measured.", "Accompanying this mismatch is an inferred retrograde/compensatory nuclear response: transcripts for mitochondrial protein import (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM8B), complex assembly and insertion (OXA1L, COX20, COA1, NDUFAF4), matrix chaperone and peroxide handling (HSPA9, PRDX3, PRDX5), organellar translation factors (TUFM, GFM2) and stress-relay components (DELE1, DDIT3, EIF2AK3) are all increased, indicating signalling for more mitochondrial biogenesis/quality control rather than proof that capacity increased.", "In parallel the cytosolic branch of glucose use is transcriptionally narrowed at committed steps: HK2, HK3 and PFKP are strongly decreased and the pentose-phosphate transcripts PGD and TALDO1 are decreased, even though glucose uptake (SLC2A1, SLC2A3) and lactate/pyruvate export (SLC16A1) transcripts rise; we infer reduced routing of glucose carbon into glycolytic commitment and NADPH-generating PPP, not a proven drop in glycolytic rate.", "Mitochondrial carbon handling is reinforced: PDP1 (PDH phosphatase, inferred to favour PDH dephosphorylation/activation), TCA enzymes (ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G, OGDH, DLD, SDHB), glutamine anaplerosis (SLC1A5, GLS, GLUD1) and the malate-aspartate shuttle/carriers (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5) are all up, consistent with pyruvate and glutamine carbon being directed into the matrix and cytosolic NADH being shuttled inward.", "Matrix citrate is inferred to be exported through the up-regulated citrate carrier SLC25A1 into a cytosolic sterol/lipid-anabolic program (SREBF1, SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, SCD, ACAT2) coupled to lipid uptake and esterified storage (LDLR, CD36, SCARB1, SOAT1, DGAT1, APOE, TREM2), so that mitochondrially processed carbon is partly diverted to lipid rather than complete oxidation to CO2.", "The lipid load is handled by an expanded lysosomal/degradative arm (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GAA, LAMP1, ATP6V1A, NPC2) together with phagocytic receptor transcripts (MERTK, FCGR1A, SYK, RAB7A), closing a lipid-uptake-to-storage loop that keeps the cell viable at rest.", "Net predicted state in the supplied mock condition: apparent steady-state compensation with reduced cytosolic glycolytic/PPP reserve and an ETC whose assembled capacity is capped by mtDNA-encoded subunits; a functional deficit is expected to become measurable only under challenge (ETC inhibition, galactose or glucose limitation, oxidative or phagocytic load), and reduced reserve under challenge would not by itself prove an ongoing defect in mock."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry discordance with carbon routing away from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP into mitochondrial TCA and citrate export in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23135361665989734, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2759443833761798, "cosine_similarity": 0.35927967298376084, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6025631067961166, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23135361665989734, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2759443833761798, "cosine_similarity": 0.35927967298376084, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6025631067961166, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.82068925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 52}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_109", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong positive shift (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); all directional statements are therefore made as ranks within this selected distribution, not as absolute up/down calls against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is not specified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2. RNA and protein effects are not assumed to be on a common scale.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (frequent keratin and ACTB co-assignment) and are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying corroboration only; no protein spot is claimed to measure a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein pool; MYH9, ARHGDIA and cathepsin protein levels, Rho-GTPase GTP loading, F/G-actin ratio, MRTF-A localisation, phagocytic rate, lysosomal pH and lipid content were not measured here.", "The ARHGDIA-to-MRTF/SRF link is background pathway knowledge (unverified within these data) used to connect the measured ARHGDIA high tail to the measured contractile-transcript low tail.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured; some transcript differences may reflect genotype effects on the co-culture or on cell-state composition in the 10X Flex pseudobulk rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation.", "Module-level rank comparisons (e.g. contractile set median -4.33 vs dataset +1.46) were partly defined after inspecting the tails and are exploratory, not pre-registered tests."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells transcriptionally reconfigure the uptake machinery: the Rho-GTPase sequestering factor ARHGDIA is one of the most strongly elevated transcripts (gene:ARHGDIA, rank 3 of 2212) while the contractile actomyosin module is at the extreme low tail (gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB, gene:MYO1F, gene:TAGLN), whereas branched-actin nucleators, clathrin/dynamin components, endosome-sorting factors and lysosomal hydrolases are at or above the dataset-wide positive shift. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is myosin-IIA-dependent contractile closure of the phagocytic cup, not actin nucleation and not lysosomal degradative capacity, so that APOE4 microglia are selectively impaired at internalising large particulate cargo while receptor-mediated/soluble uptake and hydrolase-rich endolysosomes are preserved or expanded. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed and testable.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: ARHGDIA knockdown (or expression of a RhoGDI-insensitive, membrane-targeted Rac1/RhoA) in APOE4 microglia should raise Rho-family GTP loading, restore MYH9 and ACTB transcript/protein toward APOE3 levels, and rescue uptake of large particulate cargo (beads, synaptosomes, myelin, fibrillar Abeta) by a substantially larger fraction than it changes soluble dextran or acLDL uptake. If ARHGDIA knockdown demonstrably increases GTP-loaded Rac1/RhoA yet leaves particulate uptake and MYH9 unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Cargo-class dissociation: in mock conditions APOE4 microglia should show reduced particulate uptake index but equal or greater receptor-mediated lipoprotein/fluid-phase uptake and greater neutral-lipid (BODIPY) and LysoTracker signal than APOE3. Finding equal or higher particulate uptake in APOE4, or a uniform reduction across all cargo classes, weakens the mechanism.", "Phenocopy: myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or MYH9 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 particulate-uptake deficit with relatively spared soluble uptake, and should produce little additional deficit in APOE4 (non-additivity). Full additivity in APOE4 would indicate myosin IIA is not the limiting node.", "Step localisation by imaging: APOE4 cups should initiate (F-actin/ARP2/3-positive cup formation rate normal, consistent with undiminished gene:ARPC1B and gene:CORO1B) but show longer cup lifetimes and lower closure fraction; normal closure kinetics with fewer initiated cups would relocate the bottleneck upstream to receptor engagement and weaken this hypothesis.", "Downstream specificity: because degradative capacity is predicted not to be limiting, cathepsin activity assays should be equal or higher in APOE4 despite lower particulate clearance; if bulk cathepsin/hydrolase activity is instead lower in APOE4, the coherent hydrolase transcript elevation is not translated and the degradation-capacity arm of the model fails.", "Transcriptional link: MRTF-A should be more cytoplasmic in APOE4 and MRTF/SRF inhibition in APOE3 should lower MYH9, ACTB and TAGLN; equal MRTF-A nuclear fraction between genotypes would break the proposed ARHGDIA-to-contractile-transcript step even if the uptake phenotype survives."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_109", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: ARHGDIA RNA is at the top of the selected differential-expression distribution (gene:ARHGDIA, effect +10.61, 99.9th percentile) while ARHGDIB, RAC2 and DOCK8 RNAs are in the lower tail (gene:ARHGDIB, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8). Inferred, not measured: a larger cytosolic RhoGDI-bound pool and less membrane-localised, GTP-loaded Rho-family GTPase at nascent uptake sites; no GTP-loading, F/G-actin ratio or localisation was assayed.", "Inferred: reduced Rho/Rac-driven F-actin polymerisation lowers MRTF-A/SRF-dependent transcription of the contractile-actin regulon, which is consistent with the measured coordinate decrease of gene:MYH9 (-6.38, 0.3rd percentile), gene:ACTB (-4.98), gene:TAGLN (-3.63) and gene:MYO1F (-3.69). MRTF localisation and SRF activity were not measured.", "Measured contrast: branched-actin nucleation and turnover transcripts are not decreased (gene:ARPC1B +2.15, gene:CORO1B +2.15, gene:CFL1 +1.80, gene:CYFIP1 +1.38, gene:MYO1E +1.35), so the deficit is placed at contractile force generation and cup closure rather than at actin nucleation.", "Inferred functional bottleneck: with low non-muscle myosin IIA and MYO1F, phagocytic cups can form but close and internalise large particles inefficiently; measured elevation of the 'don't-eat-me' receptor transcript gene:SIRPA (+2.26) and the low-tail gene:CR1 (-2.35) are consistent with, but do not demonstrate, lowered engulfment set-point.", "Measured: alternative, actomyosin-independent entry and sorting routes are elevated relative to the dataset median (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:AP5M1 +9.78), so soluble/lipoprotein cargo entry and endosome maturation capacity are inferred to be maintained.", "Measured: lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are coherently high (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:TFEB +2.38), and lipogenic transcripts are high (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69). Inferred: degradative capacity is not the limiting step; the combination predicts lipid-laden, hydrolase-rich lysosomes downstream of an uptake step that is biased away from particulate cargo.", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia are selectively engulfment-poor for large particles yet lipid-loading-prone, i.e. a cargo-class dissociation rather than a global endocytic failure."], "title": "RhoGDI-high, myosin-IIA-low state makes actomyosin cup closure the rate-limiting step of APOE4 microglial engulfment, diverting cargo into an expanded endolysosomal-degradative route"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24505224679688364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23801741973262153, "cosine_similarity": 0.358022247656833, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_109", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6109611650485437, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24505224679688364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23801741973262153, "cosine_similarity": 0.358022247656833, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6109611650485437, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79340725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 217}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_171", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; only the rank of a gene set relative to the list's own strongly upward-shifted background (77% of rows positive, median +1.46) is treated as evidence, not the absolute sign.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein and complex abundance; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, NADH/NAD+ ratio, membrane potential, lipid droplet content and lysosomal degradative flux were not measured and are inferred.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels are assumed to be quantified comparably to nuclear transcripts by the 10X Flex probe panel; if mitochondrial probes behave differently, the mito-nuclear discordance in Step 2 could be technical.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified: each carries up to six candidate genes, so protein_spot:077 (PRDX2 among candidates), protein_spot:017 (CAT among candidates) and protein_spot:045 (ANXA1/TALDO1 among candidates) are treated as weak corroboration only.", "506 of 1706 workbook rows carry two gene symbols, so gene-to-effect assignment for ~23% of RNA rows (including several cited genes) could be ambiguous; the conclusion is assumed to rest on set-level coherence rather than any single gene.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some APOE4-vs-APOE3 transcript differences (notably APOE, A2M) may reflect ambient RNA or non-cell-autonomous astrocyte effects rather than microglial autonomy.", "The genotype comparison is assumed isogenic and confounder-free apart from APOE, as stated in the metadata; replicate number was not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated transcriptional build-out of the mitochondrial oxidative/anaplerotic apparatus and of cytosol-mitochondria redox shuttles that is NOT matched by mtDNA-encoded electron-transport-chain subunit transcripts. We hypothesise that assembled ETC capacity, not dehydrogenase supply, is the rate-limiting step, so matrix and cytosolic NADH reoxidation becomes the bottleneck; the excess carbon (citrate/acetyl-CoA) and reducing equivalents are routed into fatty-acid desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification, and the resulting lipid load drives the expanded lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase programme. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux and stoichiometry; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured and no causal direction has been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: expressing a NADH oxidation bypass (mitochondrial LbNOX or yeast NDI1) in APOE4 microglia should lower the NADH/NAD+ ratio and reduce BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area and LAMP1/LysoTracker volume toward APOE3 levels without changing APOE genotype or APOE transcript; if bypass expression normalises redox state but leaves lipid droplet and lysosomal expansion unchanged, the mechanism is falsified.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 or mtDNA copy number) should show that APOE4 maximal FCCP-uncoupled and NADH-linked (complex I) respiration per mitochondrion is equal to or LOWER than APOE3 despite higher nuclear ETC transcripts; a proportional increase in maximal respiration in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling should show that assembled complex I, III2 and IV holoenzyme levels in APOE4 are not increased in proportion to nuclear subunit transcripts, with a relative excess of unassembled nuclear-encoded subunits or subassemblies; proportional holo-complex increase falsifies Step 3.", "APOE4 microglia should be selectively dependent on the proposed lipid sink: SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572) or SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) should reduce neutral-lipid accumulation and disproportionately increase saturated:monounsaturated lipid ratios, ER stress and death in APOE4 relative to APOE3; equal sensitivity of both genotypes would weaken Step 5.", "Lipidomics of the same cultures should show higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol content and a higher monounsaturated:saturated acyl-chain ratio in APOE4; absence of any neutral-lipid or desaturation-index difference would falsify the carbon-overflow arm.", "Lysosomal expansion should be a consequence, not a driver: limiting lipid supply (lipoprotein-depleted medium or SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition) should shrink the APOE4 lysosomal compartment, whereas TFEB knockdown should increase lipid droplet burden without normalising the mitochondrial transcript signature; if TFEB knockdown abolishes the mitochondrial/shuttle signature, the causal ordering proposed here is wrong.", "Quantitative measurement of mtDNA-encoded transcripts and proteins (qPCR plus targeted MS, independent of the Flex probe panel) should confirm that mtDNA-encoded subunits are not co-elevated with nuclear subunits in APOE4; co-elevation would remove the stoichiometric mismatch that the hypothesis depends on."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_171", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show a coherent increase in nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation subunit transcripts (38/38 NDUF/COX/ATP5/UQCR/SDH genes present in the differential list are positive, median ~2.6) together with TCA/pyruvate-entry transcripts (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:SDHB).", "Step 2 (measured abundance, discordance): mtDNA-encoded transcripts do not follow the same direction (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 negative; gene:MT-ND4L, gene:MT-ND5 positive), giving a mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch in the transcript pool.", "Step 3 (inferred stoichiometry/activity): because complexes I, III, IV and V require mtDNA-encoded cores, we infer that holo-complex assembly and therefore maximal NADH-linked respiratory flux per mitochondrion do not scale with the elevated nuclear subunit and dehydrogenase transcripts; matrix NADH reoxidation becomes the limiting step.", "Step 4 (inferred compensatory flux): the cell expands alternative NAD+-regenerating and electron-shuttling routes - cytosolic malate-aspartate arm and carriers (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13), adenine-nucleotide translocase (gene:SLC25A5), malic enzyme (gene:ME1), glutamine anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1) - and increases mitochondrial antioxidant transcripts (gene:PRDX3, gene:NNT, gene:GPX4) consistent with a more reduced, ROS-prone electron chain.", "Step 5 (inferred carbon/electron sink): with oxidation limited, citrate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2) feed a lipogenic/desaturation and esterification programme (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:POR, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DHCR24) alongside altered lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE); desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification act as carbon and reducing-equivalent sinks. Lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, downstream): the predicted lipid/membrane load is accompanied by a strongly upregulated lysosomal-catabolic programme (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1), which we interpret as compartment expansion in response to substrate load rather than as demonstrated increased degradative flux."], "title": "A mitochondrial NADH-reoxidation bottleneck in APOE4 microglia diverts carbon and reducing equivalents into desaturated/esterified lipid and a TFEB-type lysosomal expansion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20613484473655058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20251519750752617, "cosine_similarity": 0.3579244813748969, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_171", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5903398058252427, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20613484473655058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20251519750752617, "cosine_similarity": 0.3579244813748969, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5903398058252427, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.228204, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 218}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks and within-dataset comparisons are used, never absolute fold-change interpretation.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome, so absence of a gene family is weak evidence and set enrichment is judged relative to the +1.46 median of the selected rows rather than to zero.", "The strong global positive shift (77% of rows positive) is treated as a technical/compositional baseline; genes near the median (for example gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:SOAT1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36) are treated as unchanged after centring.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzyme or carrier; no proteomic confirmation of any named enzyme exists because protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified.", "SREBP-1 and TFEB nuclear translocation, citrate export flux, de novo lipogenic flux, neutral-lipid droplet content, lysosomal pH and respiration are all unmeasured inferences, not observations.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some measured transcript differences may arise from altered microglia-astrocyte lipid exchange rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally at a metabolic bottleneck: carbon that would be terminally oxidised is instead exported as citrate (SLC25A1) and supplemented by ACSS2, feeding an SREBF1-associated desaturation/esterification program (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, DGAT1) alongside strongly elevated SCARB1-associated lipid uptake; the resulting lipid load is inferred to raise catabolic demand on the endolysosome, matching a coordinated TFEB-type increase in acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts. No interferon or NF-kB program accompanies this state, so the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference under mock conditions is proposed to be a lipid-handling/organelle-load difference rather than an innate-immune activation difference. Causality is not established by these data; all statements about flux, SREBP or TFEB nuclear activity, droplet content and lysosomal degradation rate are inferences from transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: inhibiting or knocking down the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (for example CTPI-2) or ACSS2 in APOE4 microglia should reduce 13C-glucose- and 13C-acetate-derived label in triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and monounsaturated fatty acid, lower BODIPY neutral-lipid content toward APOE3 levels, and secondarily lower TFEB-target hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB), while leaving nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts largely unchanged. If APOE4 neutral lipid and hydrolase transcripts are unaffected by SLC25A1/ACSS2 blockade but fall when SCARB1-mediated uptake is blocked (BLT-1 or SCARB1 knockdown), the bottleneck is uptake rather than citrate-fed synthesis and the proposed mechanism is wrong.", "Flux test: 13C tracing should show a higher fraction of glucose- or glutamine-derived carbon in lipid and a lower fraction in CO2 in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal de novo lipogenic flux between genotypes despite the transcript differences would weaken the mechanism.", "Ordering test: SCD inhibition should produce greater lipotoxic or ER-stress sensitivity in APOE4 than APOE3, and DGAT1/SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from esterified to free species with amplified stress. No genotype difference in sensitivity would weaken step 3.", "Compensation test: acute TFEB knockdown should not reduce APOE4 lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2) if lysosomal biogenesis is downstream; if TFEB loss abolishes the lipogenic difference, the causal order in steps 3-5 is inverted.", "Bottleneck test: restoring mitochondrial-encoded subunit stoichiometry or raising respiratory capacity should reduce citrate export and lipid label incorporation in APOE4. Unchanged basal and maximal oxygen consumption between APOE4 and APOE3 would weaken step 2 while leaving steps 3-5 intact.", "Rejection test for the assigned focus: APOE4 microglia should show no genotype-driven increase in phospho-STAT1, ISG15/MX1 protein or secreted CXCL10 under mock conditions. Detection of a clear ISG protein signature would revive the interferon alternative and contradict step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for mitochondrial carbon-export and anaplerotic machinery (gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2), all in the top 15% of the selected rows and far above the +1.46 global median. We infer, but did not measure, increased citrate/malate-aspartate shuttling that raises the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool; gene:ACSS2 provides a second, acetate-dependent route to the same pool.", "Step 2 (bottleneck, inferred): Terminal oxidation of that carbon is proposed to be the constrained arm. Nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts are coordinately raised (rank-sum z=+3.95 versus the remaining rows) while the six measured mitochondrially encoded transcripts sit below background (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2), a stoichiometric discordance consistent with compensatory nuclear upregulation against limited assembled complex III/IV/V capacity. Actual respiration was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Acetyl units are instead committed to lipid. gene:SREBF1 and its canonical desaturation/glycerolipid targets gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1 and gene:DGAT1 are elevated; transcript level is taken as a proxy for, not proof of, nuclear SREBP-1 activity.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred transport): Exogenous lipid supply is added through markedly increased gene:SCARB1 (99th percentile) with modest sterol-arm support (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2). Net esterification into droplets or cholesteryl ester is inferred only; no neutral-lipid, LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2, ACLY or FASN measurement exists in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): The combined lipid load is proposed to raise degradative demand, matching a coherent CLEAR-type increase (rank-sum z=+3.04) in gene:TFEB, acid hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C). Increased hydrolase transcripts indicate biogenesis, not proven increased luminal degradation flux.", "Step 6 (negative arm, measured): The state is immunologically quiet. Zero canonical interferon-stimulated genes appear among 2212 differentially expressed rows, and the measurable inflammatory/IRF set is at background (rank-sum z=-0.45 and -0.36), so an interferon or NF-kB driver is rejected as the primary bottleneck for this comparison."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial citrate/acetyl-CoA into an SREBF1-directed lipogenic-esterification program, with lysosomal biogenesis as a downstream compensation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17660525052616033, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25703447008233715, "cosine_similarity": 0.3579021932806692, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6038058252427184, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17660525052616033, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25703447008233715, "cosine_similarity": 0.3579021932806692, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6038058252427184, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.889777, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 219}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_050", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row |effect| \u003e= 1 with adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); absent genes (e.g. SOD1, SOD2, CAT, HMOX1, NQO1, GCLM, NFE2L2, PPARGC1A, TFAM, CPT1A, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged, so program coverage is partial.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA magnitudes are therefore not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot scale, and the very large RNA values may include scaling or single-cell pseudobulk artefacts.", "Increased transcript abundance is taken as increased component abundance only; ETC activity, respiration, ROS production, glutathione/NADPH pools, lipid flux and lysosomal proteolytic flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each, dominated by keratin/actin candidates); no spot is treated as identification of a single protein, and spot-level directions are used only for compatibility, not confirmation.", "Coordinate direction within a manually defined gene family is descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test on independent genes; permutation against the selected list (not 50/50) was used only to gauge whether a program exceeds this up-biased background.", "Microglial attribution is assumed from the 10X Flex single-cell design despite astrocyte co-culture; the protein-spot fraction may contain astrocyte-derived material.", "Reduced reserve is a challenge-revealed property; under the supplied mock condition the mechanism predicts an altered but buffered steady state, not established damage."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state change toward higher lipid acquisition/esterification and lysosomal hydrolysis feeding an expanded nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative apparatus (all five ETC complexes, TCA enzymes, carriers, import), with matched induction of mitochondrial thiol-peroxidase/NADPH-supplying systems, so redox handling scales with the oxidative program rather than reflecting an ongoing oxidative-stress emergency; because mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are not co-elevated, the expansion is stoichiometrically constrained and predicts reduced respiratory reserve that would only be revealed by a future challenge. Causality is not established by these abundance measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, extracellular-flux assay should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption and higher citrate-synthase-normalised complex I/IV activity, but a proportionally smaller FCCP-stimulated spare capacity; if basal respiration and ETC activities are equal or lower in APOE4 despite the transcript increases, the increased-throughput reading is wrong and failed compensation for a respiratory defect becomes the better explanation.", "Prospective: steady-state mitochondrial peroxide and BODIPY-C11 lipid peroxidation should be at most modestly elevated in mock APOE4, yet GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) or thioredoxin-reductase inhibition (auranofin) should cause a genotype-selective, larger increase in oxidation and loss of viability in APOE4 than APOE3; equal sensitivity would weaken the antioxidant-scaling step.", "Prospective: restricting lipid input (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SCARB1/LDLR knockdown, or lysosomal acid-lipase/cathepsin inhibition) should collapse the APOE4-specific induction of TCA and nuclear ETC transcripts toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the OXPHOS induction would refute the substrate-routing step and favour a lipid-independent biogenesis or compensatory-signalling driver.", "Prospective: quantifying mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass (TOM20) and the NDUFB8/MT-CO1 protein ratio should show increased mass with an upward-shifted nuclear:mtDNA-encoded subunit ratio and increased free (unassembled) nuclear subunits by BN-PAGE in APOE4; equal NDUFB8/MT-CO1 ratio and normal complex assembly would refute the stoichiometric-constraint step.", "Prospective: a peroxisomal-beta-oxidation-specific mechanism is not predicted; ACOX1 activity, plasmalogen levels and catalase activity should not differ substantially between genotypes. A large peroxisomal deficit (e.g. ABCD1-dependent VLCFA accumulation) would indicate the wrong compartment was chosen."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the lipid-acquisition/handling transcriptional program (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:APOE +1.24), routing more lipid into esterified stores and membranes (uptake and esterification flux inferred, not measured).", "In parallel the lysosomal/v-ATPase degradative program is up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86; exceptions gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:IDS -1.56), increasing capacity to hydrolyse lipid/membrane cargo into fatty acids, sterols and amino acids.", "These catabolic products are routed to mitochondria: carrier and import transcripts rise (gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:TIMM8B +5.20, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46) together with matrix oxidative enzymes (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:HADHA +2.86).", "Nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunits increase coordinately across all five complexes (38/38 represented members positive, median ~+2.6; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:SDHB +1.65), i.e. expanded respiratory-chain component abundance; enzymatic activity and oxygen flux were not measured.", "Higher oxidative catabolic throughput increases mitochondrial peroxide production, and peroxide-detoxifying/NADPH-supplying transcripts rise in proportion (gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:SELENOW +5.47, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:TXNL1 +4.33, gene:AKR1A1 +4.15, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:MGST2 +3.32, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:MSRA +2.64, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:PRDX5 +1.96), so the steady state in mock is buffered rather than overtly damaged; ambiguous spots protein_spot:077 (candidates KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB; +1.07) and protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5; +0.766) are compatible but cannot confirm individual antioxidant proteins.", "mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts do not follow the nuclear expansion (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +1.95, gene:MT-ND5 +1.93), so nuclear:mtDNA subunit stoichiometry is mismatched and limits how much of the expanded nuclear program can be assembled into functional complexes.", "Net predicted APOE4 state in mock: higher lipid-fuelled oxidative throughput with proportionate antioxidant buffering and only background-magnitude inflammatory change (gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:HIF1A +1.98, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37), with reduced spare respiratory and peroxide-buffering reserve that a future oxidative or phagocytic challenge would expose."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lipid-catabolic, nuclear-driven mitochondrial oxidative state with proportionate thiol-peroxidase scaling, constrained at the mtDNA-encoded core"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.46792268212531846, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27211567558396565, "cosine_similarity": 0.35666497578685447, "direction_accuracy": 0.470873786407767, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6265113268608414, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.46792268212531846, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27211567558396565, "cosine_similarity": 0.35666497578685447, "direction_accuracy": 0.470873786407767, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6265113268608414, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3145115, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 53}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_183", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1 and 77% are positive) and the logarithm base is unspecified; all inference uses relative rank within this list, not absolute fold changes, and the list is not an unbiased transcriptome.", "Higher transcript abundance for a metabolic enzyme or carrier is taken as a proxy for higher protein and pathway capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, flux, or membrane-potential measurement is supplied.", "The mito-nuclear discordance is assumed to reflect genuine mtDNA-encoded transcript differences rather than probe-set behaviour, ambient RNA, or QC filtering in 10X Flex; only six MT- rows are present and two of them are up, so this step is the weakest link.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and are not treated as identified proteins; they are used only as a coarse consistency check, and no mitochondrial or lipogenic protein spot is informative.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may reflect altered microglia-astrocyte cross-talk or cell-state composition rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 metabolism.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the extreme adjusted p-values cannot be interpreted as calibrated evidence of reproducibility across donors."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of anaplerotic (glutamine/malate-aspartate) carbon entry, TCA enzymes and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/import machinery, while mitochondrially encoded core subunits are not co-elevated; we propose that assembled respiratory throughput therefore cannot absorb the increased carbon load, and that mitochondrial citrate export through SLC25A1 becomes the rate-limiting egress step that channels surplus carbon into cytosolic acetyl-CoA and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification. Lysosomal-CLEAR transcripts also rise, but only marginally above the pervasive upward shift of this DE list and without matching protein-spot support, so endolysosomal degradative capacity is treated as a parallel/secondary feature rather than the primary bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or SLC25A1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content (BODIPY, LipidTOX, or lipidomics) substantially more than in isogenic APOE3, while leaving basal oxygen consumption largely intact or increased. If SLC25A1 blockade changes lipid load equally in APOE4 and APOE3, the proposed citrate-export bottleneck is wrong.", "13C5-glutamine tracing should show greater fractional labelling of citrate, and greater transfer of glutamine-derived carbon into palmitate/oleate and cholesteryl esters, in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal labelling would weaken steps 1-2 and 5.", "Glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) should reduce basal and maximal OCR and lipid droplet number preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would falsify the anaplerotic-input claim.", "Because nuclear subunits rise while mtDNA-encoded subunits do not, the ratio of assembled complex I/IV in-gel activity (BN-PAGE) to total nuclear-encoded subunit protein should be lower in APOE4, and maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) OCR should rise less than proportionally to the transcript increase. If APOE4 shows proportionally higher assembled complex activity and maximal respiration, step 4 and the bottleneck placement fail.", "Discriminating against the endolysosomal alternative: blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or knocking down TFEB should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in OXPHOS/anaplerotic transcripts or in glutamine-derived citrate labelling. If TFEB knockdown normalises the mitochondrial program, the lysosomal axis is upstream and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Immunoblot for mature cathepsin B/D/L and ATP6V1E1 should show no APOE4 increase (consistent with the flat/negative cathepsin- and v-ATPase-candidate spots). A clear, reproducible increase in mature cathepsin protein and lysosomal proteolytic rate (DQ-BSA) in APOE4 would revive lysosomal capacity as a competing primary mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_183", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance for glutamine anaplerosis and the malate-aspartate shuttle (GLS, GLUD1, GOT1, MDH1, SLC25A11, SLC25A13). Inferred: increased anaplerotic carbon and reducing-equivalent entry at alpha-ketoglutarate, not directly measured as flux.", "Measured: TCA-cycle enzyme transcripts are coordinately higher (ACO2, OGDH, DLD, IDH3B, SDHB; set median +4.47 versus list background +1.46, one-sided MWU p=5.2e-5). Inferred: raised catalytic capacity of the cycle; enzyme activity and metabolite pools were not measured.", "Measured: all 37 detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits across complexes I, II, III, IV and V are up, together with protein-import and adenine-nucleotide carrier transcripts (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM17B, TIMM8B, SLC25A5). Inferred: increased demand for NADH re-oxidation and an attempt to scale electron-transport capacity.", "Measured: mitochondrially encoded core subunit transcripts are predominantly lower (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 down; MT-ND4L, MT-ND5 up). Inferred (weakly supported, probe-based assay): mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch so assembled holo-complex throughput does not scale with nuclear subunit supply, leaving surplus mitochondrial carbon.", "Primary bottleneck. Measured: the citrate carrier transcript SLC25A1 is up (+4.47) alongside cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation (ACSS2 +2.93). Inferred: carbon that cannot be fully oxidised leaves the matrix as citrate; SLC25A1 capacity sets the rate at which this overflow reaches the cytosol. Flux, direction of transport and localization were not measured.", "Measured: lipogenic/esterification transcripts are up (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, FABP3, FABP5, ABCA7, LDLR, INSIG1), although as a set they are not distinguishable from the list-wide upward shift (p=0.12). Inferred: cytosolic acetyl-CoA is routed to monounsaturated fatty acid synthesis and to triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage, a lipid-laden APOE4 microglial state.", "Measured: lysosomal-CLEAR transcripts rise modestly (TFEB, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, LAMP1), but CTSS falls sharply and cathepsin/v-ATPase-candidate protein spots are not elevated (median +0.14 versus +0.48 for all spots). Inferred: lysosomal biogenesis signalling is engaged as a downstream response to lipid load rather than acting as the upstream limiting step."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand glutamine-fuelled mitochondrial carbon flux, with SLC25A1-dependent citrate egress as the rate-limiting node coupling TCA overflow to lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24234026042325346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3560061716514885, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_183", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6061035598705502, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24234026042325346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3560061716514885, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6061035598705502, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.619171, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 220}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_063", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of effects are positive with median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, so only rank position within this list, not sign or raw magnitude, is treated as informative.", "Increased hydrolase transcript abundance is assumed to translate into increased mature, correctly trafficked luminal hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity; this is not measured here and the ambiguous 2-D protein spots do not confirm it.", "Limiting-membrane and egress capacity per lysosome is assumed to be approximately proportional to transcripts of LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2, CLN3 and SLC17A5; post-transcriptional control could break this proportionality.", "NPC1, LIPA, PLA2G15, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, LAMP2, TMEM175, SQSTM1 and MAP1LC3B are absent from the supplied list; absence is treated as 'not reported', not as 'unchanged'.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-identifying; no spot is used as evidence that a specific named protein changed.", "The two genotypes are isogenic and the RNA differences are not dominated by cell-composition, ambient-RNA or astrocyte-carryover differences in the 10X Flex co-culture; this is not testable from the supplied data.", "No lipid, pH, degradation-flux, morphology or replicate-level data were supplied, so all flux, localisation and causal-direction statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a transcriptional expansion of soluble lysosomal acid hydrolases that is disproportionately large relative to the lysosomal limiting-membrane and lumen-to-ER lipid-egress machinery (LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2, CLN3, SLC17A5, TFEB/MITF), which sit near the background level of this differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 endolysosomal cargo processing is not luminal hydrolysis but export of hydrolysis products (chiefly unesterified sterol and sphingolipid catabolites) across the limiting membrane, so that catabolites accumulate in the lumen and are shunted into esterification/storage and lipogenic programmes while priming an inflammasome/chemokine state. Causality is not established by these data; the abundance changes are measured, all flux, pH, localisation and directional statements are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: load APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a dual-reporter cargo (DQ-BSA plus NBD/BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester or fluorescent myelin). The mechanism predicts that APOE4 shows equal or faster luminal hydrolysis (DQ-BSA dequenching, ester cleavage) but slower appearance of the freed sterol/lipid label in ER and plasma-membrane pools, with prolonged LAMP1-colocalised retention. If APOE4 instead shows slower luminal dequenching, the bottleneck is hydrolysis rather than egress and this mechanism is wrong.", "Egress rescue: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression, should reduce filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol and LAMP1-colocalised lipid in APOE4 microglia and lower NLRP3/CXCL8 output, without reducing acid-hydrolase transcripts. Failure of egress enhancement to reduce lipid load or inflammatory output weakens the mechanism.", "Opposing-direction perturbation: TFEB overexpression, which further raises the hydrolase programme, should NOT normalise APOE4 lipid accumulation and may worsen it. If TFEB overexpression fully rescues the APOE4 phenotype, the bottleneck is lysosomal biogenesis rather than export and the hypothesis is falsified.", "Acidification control: lysosomal pH measured by ratiometric probe should be equal to or lower (more acidic) in APOE4 than APOE3, consistent with the v-ATPase transcripts. A significantly less acidic APOE4 lysosome would relocate the bottleneck to acidification and weaken this mechanism.", "Protein-level test with uniquely identified proteins: targeted MS or immunoblot should show increased mature GAA, GBA, HEXA and CTSB protein and increased corresponding enzyme activity in APOE4 lysosome-enriched fractions, while LAMP1 and NPC2 protein increase proportionally less. If mature hydrolase protein and activity are unchanged or decreased despite the RNA increase, step 2 fails.", "Storage dependence: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should increase free-cholesterol-driven ER stress and cell death more in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia. Equal sensitivity across genotypes weakens the proposed diversion of escaped sterol into esterification."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises endolysosomal lipid/lipoprotein cargo delivery: uptake and opsonic/scavenger receptor transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:C1QA, gene:APOE). Measured = RNA abundance; increased internalisation flux is inferred, not observed.", "A coordinate CLEAR-type output raises luminal acid-hydrolase transcripts to the extreme upper tail of the supplied list (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK at the 95th-99.7th percentile of all 2212 RNA effects), alongside a modest rise of the regulators gene:TFEB and gene:MITF and of v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1A). Inferred: increased delivery of hydrolase protein and preserved or increased acidification.", "In the same list, lysosomal limiting-membrane, ion/metabolite export and luminal sterol-transfer components rise only to about the list median (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:SLC17A5, gene:ATP6AP2). Inferred: the per-lysosome export/limiting-membrane capacity does not scale with the hydrolytic capacity, creating a stoichiometric mismatch.", "Inferred flux consequence: cargo lipid is hydrolysed inside the lumen but the products, in particular unesterified cholesterol and glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolites, leave the lysosome more slowly than they are generated, so the luminal pool expands. No lipid pool was measured in this dataset.", "The cell diverts the sterol/fatty-acid that does escape into re-esterification and storage rather than membrane use, and maintains a lipogenic/sterol-synthetic transcriptional programme (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2), consistent with an ER compartment that senses sterol insufficiency despite a loaded lysosome. Inferred: cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet accumulation.", "Chronic luminal lipid load and limiting-membrane stress prime an inflammasome and chemokine state (gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:IL18, gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:CCL2, gene:LGALS3, gene:FTH1). Inferred: increased inflammasome licensing; no cytokine release or caspase activity was measured."], "title": "Hydrolase-loaded but egress-limited lysosomes: APOE4 microglia scale luminal acid-hydrolase transcripts far above limiting-membrane and lipid-export machinery"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24994461470295018, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23769582136015316, "cosine_similarity": 0.355975715620244, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6025372168284789, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24994461470295018, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23769582136015316, "cosine_similarity": 0.355975715620244, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6025372168284789, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.68648175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 221}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_065", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05) with 77% of rows positive; all pathway claims are therefore made as rank comparisons inside this list, and absence of a gene means not measured/not selected, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only sign and within-list rank are used, never cross-gene magnitude arithmetic.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme activity, glycosylation/maturation state, lysosomal pH and subcellular localisation, none of which are measured here.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some differential RNA may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect ambient/cross-cell contamination in the 10X Flex data.", "Library-composition effects (notably lower mitochondrially encoded transcript fraction in APOE4) could inflate nuclear-gene effects globally; rank-based tests are assumed to partly control for this.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the effective statistical support for individual rows cannot be verified."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 (vs APOE3) shows a coherent transcriptional expansion of lysosomal acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and MiT/TFE factors together with lipid-uptake and lipid-esterification transcripts, while ER chaperone/UPR-output transcripts are absent from the differential list and ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are unchanged. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not ER folding capacity but the conversion of the up-regulated lysosomal transcript program into acidified, catalytically competent degradative capacity matched to an increased lipid-rich cargo load; the unresolved load is re-routed into esterification/storage and sustains a reactive lipid-associated microglial state. Causality is not established by these correlative RNA and protein-spot data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, measure acid-hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXB, cathepsin B/D fluorogenic assays) and lysosomal pH normalised to lysosome volume/LAMP1 content. The mechanism predicts higher hydrolase transcripts and higher lysosome volume in APOE4 but equal or lower activity per unit lysosome and equal or less acidic pH, with increased neutral-lipid/sterol accumulation (BODIPY, filipin). If activity per lysosome scales proportionally with the transcript increase and lipid does not accumulate, the bottleneck step is refuted.", "Cargo-load test: reducing lipid cargo delivery (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or CD36/SCARB1 blockade) for 48-72 h should lower the APOE4 hydrolase/v-ATPase/MiT-TFE transcript elevation toward APOE3 without changing ERAD-L transcripts. Persistence of the full CLEAR elevation under cargo restriction would weaken the compensatory-response interpretation and favour a cargo-independent MiT/TFE-intrinsic mechanism.", "Focus-rejection test: ER-directed intervention (4-PBA/TUDCA chemical chaperones, ISRIB, or PERK inhibition) should not normalise the APOE4 lysosomal transcript signature or the lipid accumulation. If it does, an ER-proteostasis-primary mechanism is supported and this hypothesis is weakened.", "Capacity-versus-enzyme test: restoring acidification/degradative capacity (v-ATPase-supporting acidic nanoparticles, or TFEB-independent enhancement of lysosomal acidification) should reduce APOE4 lipid accumulation more than overexpression of any single hydrolase (e.g. GBA or CTSD) alone. Equal rescue by a single hydrolase would argue for a specific enzyme deficiency rather than a general capacity bottleneck.", "Analytical control: re-normalising the RNA data with mitochondrially encoded transcripts excluded (or with spike-ins) should preserve the rank enrichment of acid hydrolases relative to the list background. Loss of the enrichment would indicate a composition artefact and weaken the entire hypothesis.", "Counter-evidence to be explained: CTSS RNA is strongly decreased while other cathepsins increase; the mechanism predicts CTSS protein/activity behaves differently from CTSB/CTSD in APOE4 (e.g. selective loss), whereas a uniform decrease of all cathepsin activities would favour a general lysosomal-collapse model instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia elevate transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris receptors and their ligand (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), which we infer - not measure - increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A MiT/TFE-associated CLEAR-type program is elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF) together with acid hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1), membrane/traffic components (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:RAB7A, gene:NPC2) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1); hydrolase transcripts rank above the already up-shifted background of this selected list.", "Step 3 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK; inferred activity/localisation): The increased transcript program is hypothesised not to translate proportionally into mature, correctly acidified, catalytically active lysosomal capacity. Consistent with, but not proof of, this step, protein spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins split in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and the two spots whose candidate lists contain the v-ATPase subunit ATP6V1E1 are decreased (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065). Spot identities are ambiguous, so this is a hypothesis about maturation/activity, not a measurement of any specific protein pool.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Lipid that is not catabolised is hypothesised to be re-routed into esterification and neutral-lipid storage rather than hydrolysis and efflux, consistent with elevated gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1 and gene:SCD; lysosomal lipase and sterol-efflux genes (LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2) are absent from the supplied differential list and were therefore not measured here.", "Step 5 (measured RNA): The persisting cargo/lipid load is hypothesised to maintain a reactive lipid-associated microglial state (gene:GPNMB, gene:CLEC7A, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CCL2, gene:CTSK) and to feed back on the MiT/TFE program, making Step 2 a compensatory response rather than a resolved adaptation.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, modifier): ERAD-L and ER export/translocation transcripts are coordinately low against the list background (gene:SEL1L, gene:EDEM1, gene:DERL1, gene:SEC62, gene:SEC24D, gene:PDIA3, gene:NGLY1), which we propose shifts additional disposal burden onto the lysosome rather than constituting a classical unfolded-protein response; no ER chaperone induction is detectable (ER-chaperone-candidate spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 are non-significant and not increased)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a MiT/TFE-linked lysosomal hydrolase and acidification program but are bottlenecked at converting it into active lysosomal lipid-clearance capacity, diverting lipid into esterification/storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12000147694125465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1465799763244898, "cosine_similarity": 0.3557958944899628, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mean_absolute_error": 0.622242718446602, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12000147694125465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1465799763244898, "cosine_similarity": 0.3557958944899628, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.622242718446602, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.67146125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 222}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_099", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no |log FC| below 1 is present) and are not an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified, so effect signs and relative ranks are used, absolute magnitudes are not.", "Row-block structure was detected: source rows \u003c600 contain both directions (50-59% up) whereas rows \u003e=600 are 100% up. The apparent whole-list up-shift is therefore at least partly a workbook-assembly artifact, and pathway direction was judged against the within-list median (+1.46 overall, +1.09 for rows \u003c600) rather than against zero.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and no spot is used as the sole support for any step.", "RNA abundance is assumed to be at least partly reflected in protein abundance, and protein abundance in enzymatic/transport activity; neither link was measured here.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes; some transcripts may derive from non-microglial cells or ambient RNA, and no cell-type deconvolution or replicate structure was supplied.", "Sterol egress transporters (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1), lipid species, lysosomal pH, and any imaging or flux readout are absent from the supplied data; their behaviour is predicted, not observed.", "Causality is not established: this is an isogenic genotype contrast at a single timepoint with no perturbation arm."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcriptional increase in lipid-scavenging surface receptors together with the clathrin/dynamin-to-RAB7 maturation machinery and a TFEB/MITF-associated hydrolase and v-ATPase program, while transcripts for sterol/lipid re-esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1) also rise. We propose that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is not internalization and not lysosomal proteolytic capacity but the egress of internalized sterol/lipid from the expanded late-endosome-lysosome compartment: cargo that enters is retained and shunted into esterified storage. All abundances are RNA or 2D protein-spot measurements; compartment volume, flux, acidification, hydrolase activity, sterol egress and lipid content were not measured and are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION: In a pulse-chase with fluorescent AcLDL or labelled myelin, APOE4 microglia will internalize an equal or greater amount than APOE3 during the pulse (consistent with step 1-2) but will clear significantly less of the internalized label during the chase, while DQ-BSA dequenching (bulk lysosomal proteolysis) is equal to or higher in APOE4. If DQ-BSA dequenching is instead reduced in APOE4, the bottleneck is degradative capacity rather than egress and this mechanism is falsified.", "APOE4 microglia will accumulate more cholesteryl ester and more BODIPY/Nile-Red-positive droplet area per cell at baseline and after AcLDL loading; SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) will reduce esterified sterol in APOE4 toward APOE3 without reducing AcLDL internalization. Unchanged droplet content in APOE4, or a SOAT1 inhibitor that also lowers uptake, weakens step 5.", "Blocking uptake upstream (SCARB1/CD36 antibody or sulfo-N-succinimidyl oleate, or SCARB1 knockdown) will normalize APOE4 lipid retention; if lipid retention persists at APOE3 uptake rates, the mechanism is uptake-independent and is weakened.", "Imaging will show enlarged LAMP1/RAB7 double-positive compartments with filipin-detectable unesterified sterol in APOE4, and U18666A (NPC1 sterol-egress block) applied to APOE3 will phenocopy the APOE4 lipid phenotype while producing little additional effect in APOE4 (occlusion). Additive rather than occlusive behaviour weakens the egress-bottleneck placement.", "Targeted immunoblot will confirm increased CTSD/CTSB and v-ATPase subunit protein and increased mature-to-pro cathepsin ratio in APOE4; a decrease in mature cathepsin protein would contradict step 3 and force a degradation-capacity model instead.", "Because step 6 is treated as permissive, myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) in APOE3 should NOT by itself reproduce the APOE4 lipid-retention phenotype; if it fully reproduces it, the primary bottleneck should be reassigned to actomyosin-dependent phagosome resolution."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred protein/surface density): APOE4 raises transcripts for lipid- and debris-scavenging receptors (SCARB1 +8.22; CD36, MRC1, CD163, COLEC12, STAB1, TREM2, MERTK, ABCA7, CLEC7A, CD14 all ~+1.1 to +1.5 with adjusted p\u003c1e-25). We infer, but did not measure, higher surface receptor density and higher ligand-binding capacity.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Transcripts for the internalization and early-to-late maturation machinery rise well above the within-list median (DNM2 +5.82, CLTB +2.10, SNX3 +3.95, VPS26A +4.86, CHMP4B +3.82, RAB7A +2.65, PIK3C3 +2.92). We infer increased capacity for dynamin/clathrin-dependent internalization and for delivery of cargo to a RAB7-positive late compartment; vesicle number, localization and transport rates were not measured.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA and ambiguous protein spots; inferred activity): A TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal program is coordinately elevated (TFEB +2.38, MITF +1.03, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51, ATP6AP1 +2.30, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, CTSH +1.54, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, HEXB +2.17, GLA +1.53, SMPD1 +5.63, LAMP1 +1.38, GPNMB +1.11). Cathepsin/hexosaminidase-candidate 2D spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:052 +2.14 up; protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85 down), which is compatible with altered proenzyme-to-mature processing rather than a uniform loss; spot identities are ambiguous. We therefore infer that degradative (proteolytic/glycosidic) capacity is maintained or increased, not lost.", "STEP 4 (BOTTLENECK; inferred, not measured): Because uptake capacity (step 1-2) and hydrolase/acidification capacity (step 3) both rise, the rate-limiting step for lipid handling shifts downstream, to the export of liberated sterol and fatty acid out of the RAB7-positive endolysosome. Transporters that would relieve this step (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1) are absent from the supplied differential-expression list, so no increase in egress capacity is documented; NPC2 rises only modestly (+1.17).", "STEP 5 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Retained lipid is predicted to be routed into esterified storage rather than efflux, consistent with elevated SOAT1 (+1.25, adjusted p 1.8e-125), DGAT1 (+1.72), SREBF1 (+4.67), LDLR (+1.50), FABP5 (+1.13), PLTP (+1.06), APOE (+1.24) and PLA2G7 (+1.13). Neutral lipid, cholesteryl ester and lipid-droplet content were not measured in this dataset.", "STEP 6 (secondary, mixed evidence): The actin machinery is remodelled asymmetrically - branched-actin nucleators rise at RNA level (ARPC1B +2.15, ARPC5 +1.94, ARPC4 +1.93) with concordant ARPC5-candidate spot protein_spot:081 (+1.20), while MYH9 (-6.38) and ACTB (-4.98) fall at RNA level. We treat this as a permissive, non-load-bearing accompaniment (branched-actin-dependent small-cargo uptake favoured over contractile large-particle engulfment) because the ACTB/MYH9 RNA magnitudes are implausibly large for such highly expressed genes and are contradicted by ACTB-candidate spots (mean +0.57 across 25 spots) and by MYL12A (+1.93)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia couple scavenger-receptor uptake to an expanded RAB7/v-ATPase endolysosome whose sterol egress, not its hydrolase capacity, is the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23446442417752833, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24185975053424585, "cosine_similarity": 0.3549906698029135, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6033559870550163, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23446442417752833, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24185975053424585, "cosine_similarity": 0.3549906698029135, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6033559870550163, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79741875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 223}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_019", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1.00) with 1705 positive and 507 negative entries; we assume the 0.771 up-fraction is the correct null for directional enrichment and that the remaining transcriptome is not systematically opposite. If the up-shift is a normalization or ambient-RNA artefact of the 10X Flex pseudobulk comparison, all set-level means are inflated.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are treated as ranks and signs, not as fold changes.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-DE features; assigning ANXA1 to spots 43-47 and ATP6V1E1/H to spots 64, 65, 75 is an interpretation, not an identification. Spots 64 and 65 also list ANXA1, so the v-ATPase reading is confounded.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the size of the corresponding protein pool; no hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, membrane localization or lipid measurement is supplied, so all flux, activity and localization statements are inferred.", "The gene sets were assembled by the analyst after seeing the data (post hoc); the reported binomial and permutation p values are descriptive coherence statistics, not multiplicity-corrected discoveries.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and biological replicate counts are not supplied, so genotype effects may partly reflect non-cell-autonomous astrocyte signalling or unreplicated variation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally downstream of engulfment: transcripts for lipid/debris uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, TREM2, MERTK, FCGR1A/3A, C1QA-C, ITGB1) and for the TFEB-type endolysosomal battery (TFEB, ATP6V1H/1A/0C, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, GAA, SMPD1) are coordinately higher, while the actin/contractile engine of the phagocytic cup is not (ACTB, MYH9, RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB lower) and the 2-DE spots whose candidate lists contain CTSB and ATP6V1E1/ATP6V1H are not correspondingly higher. We propose that the rate-limiting step is lysosomal degradative/lipid-egress capacity per lysosome rather than internalization or actin-driven engulfment, and that the elevated endolysosomal transcription is a demand-driven compensation accompanied by rerouting of sterol and fatty acid into esterified neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, ACAT2, DGAT1, SCD, SCP2 up). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Kinetic uptake versus clearance split (primary discriminator): loading APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with fluorescent myelin, acetylated-LDL or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester should give equal or higher initial internalization in APOE4 at 15-30 min but significantly slower loss of the label and greater neutral-lipid-droplet area at 24 h. If APOE4 instead shows reduced initial internalization, the bottleneck is at uptake and this mechanism is wrong.", "Capacity versus transcript discordance: cathepsin B/D specific activity (per lysosome, e.g. Magic Red or DQ-BSA normalized to LAMP1 area) and lysosomal acidification (LysoSensor ratio) should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite the higher CTSB, CTSD and ATP6V transcripts. If cathepsin activity and acidification rise in APOE4 in proportion to the transcript increase, step 3 fails and the mechanism is weakened.", "Actin dependence control: Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) or a myosin-II inhibitor should suppress cargo internalization similarly in both genotypes and should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in retained cargo or droplet load. If CK-666 removes the genotype difference, an actin/phagocytic-cup mechanism dominates and hyp_019 should be rejected.", "Esterification is compensatory, not causal: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester droplets while increasing free-sterol and lysosomal cargo retention in APOE4 without normalizing cathepsin activity. If ACAT inhibition normalizes cargo clearance, the esterification step is upstream rather than a downstream sink and the ordering in the mechanism is wrong.", "Compensation direction: TFEB knockdown should worsen retained cargo and droplet load in APOE4 relative to APOE3, whereas TFEB overexpression or an mTORC1 inhibitor that drives TFEB nuclear entry should partially rescue clearance. If TFEB knockdown reduces the APOE4 lipid phenotype, the TFEB-type program is a driver rather than a compensation and step 5 is falsified.", "Proteoform test for the 2-DE reading: two-dimensional Western or targeted mass spectrometry for cathepsin B/D and ANXA1 should show redistribution between pro- and mature/charge-variant forms in APOE4 with little change in total pool. If total CTSB and CTSD protein simply increase in proportion to their transcripts, the discordance argument built on spots 058, 064, 065, 067, 069 collapses."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry uniformly higher transcript levels for scavenger/opsonic uptake receptors (18/18 members of the tested set positive, mean +2.32 in the unspecified reported-log unit, binomial p=0.0092 against the 0.771 up-fraction of the differential-expression list). We infer, but did not measure, an equal-or-greater receptor-mediated internalization flux for lipoprotein and membrane-debris cargo.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization/flux): Endosomal maturation and sorting transcripts are coordinately raised (DNM2, CLTB, RAB7A, SNX3, SNX12/15/16, VPS26A, VPS35L, CHMP4B; 20/22 positive), so cargo is inferred to reach late endosomes/lysosomes rather than stalling at the plasma membrane.", "Step 3 (measured RNA vs measured protein spots; the bottleneck): Transcription of the acidification and hydrolase battery rises (24/26 positive, mean +2.80, permutation p=0.0021; TFEB itself +2.38), yet the protein spots whose candidate lists include ATP6V1E1/ATP6V1H (spots 64, 65, 75) are all negative and CTSB/CTSD-containing spots average near zero with opposite-signed members. We therefore infer that per-lysosome proteolytic and lipolytic capacity does not scale with the transcriptional demand; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and cargo flux were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred): Cargo lipid that is not hydrolysed or exported accumulates in the endolysosome; free sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are esterified and stored, consistent with coordinated increases in SOAT1, ACAT2, DGAT1, SCD, SCP2, AGPAT4 and the post-squalene sterol enzymes DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, EBP (17/17 positive, binomial p=0.0120). Lipid droplets, cholesteryl ester mass and lysosomal lipid were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; direction of the compensation): The TFEB transcript increase and the whole lysosomal battery are interpreted as a feedback response to unmet degradative demand rather than as the primary lesion; the discovery data cannot distinguish these directions.", "Step 6 (measured RNA and protein; exclusion of the assigned focus): The actin/myosin engine of engulfment is not upregulated (13/18 positive, mean +0.27, far below the list background mean of +1.39, permutation p=0.97; ACTB -4.98, MYH9 -6.38, RAC2 -1.97, DOCK8 -1.99, ARHGDIB -1.98), so we place the constraint after internalization. The strongly increased ANXA1-containing spot train (spots 43-47, up to +3.05 log2, with ANXA1 RNA +4.15 while the co-listed TALDO1 RNA is -2.32) is compatible with, but does not prove, increased Ca2+/phospholipid-binding protein at stressed endolysosomal or plasma membranes."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise uptake-receptor and TFEB-type endolysosomal transcription but not matching hydrolase/v-ATPase proteoforms, placing the bottleneck at post-internalization lysosomal cargo clearance and diverting lipid into esterified storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15877190563645605, "cosine_similarity": 0.3543039217431083, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6149417475728155, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15877190563645605, "cosine_similarity": 0.3543039217431083, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6149417475728155, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97936175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 224}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_079", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 1705/2212 rows are positive and the median is +1.46, so only enrichment RELATIVE to this shifted background (not raw direction) is treated as informative. The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no base conversion is applied and no absolute fold-change magnitude is claimed.", "Increased hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to translate into increased lysosomal degradative and acidification capacity. Enzyme activity, protein level, luminal pH and lysosome number were not measured.", "The lipid-egress bottleneck is inferred from what is ABSENT or unmoved, not from a measured flux: NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, PLIN2 and NPC1-dependent transport were not measured at all. If those unmeasured components are strongly induced in APOE4, the bottleneck is misplaced.", "Cholesterol mass, cholesteryl-ester mass, lipid-droplet number, sphingolipid species and efflux rate were not measured in this dataset; the lipid-storing end state is a prediction, not an observation.", "2D-gel protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous. Spots containing cathepsin candidates move in BOTH directions (protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down), so no protein spot is used as primary evidence for any single gene product.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture and the measurement is described as single-cell 10X Flex, but the supplied rows carry no cell-type deconvolution or replicate count ('not supplied in workbook'), so an altered microglia:astrocyte or microglial-state proportion between genotypes could generate part of the apparent shift.", "Comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at day 30 under mock treatment; the direction convention (positive = higher in APOE4) is taken as given."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent, high-magnitude induction of the TFEB-associated lysosomal degradative and v-ATPase acidification program (22/22 measured members up, mean reported logFC +3.61, permutation p=1.5e-4 against the already up-shifted background) that is NOT matched by the lipid-egress arm of the same compartment (NPC2, SCARB2, CLN3 all sit at the 27th-35th percentile of the observed effect distribution). We hypothesise that this imbalance makes NPC1/NPC2-dependent export of hydrolase-liberated cholesterol and sphingolipid out of the endolysosome the rate-limiting step: luminal lipid accumulates, the ER sterol sensor reads a deficit, and the SREBP program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, INSIG1) plus scavenger-receptor uptake (SCARB1) and acyl-transfer/storage enzymes (AGPAT2, LPCAT1, DGAT1) are engaged, converting the cell to a lipid-storing state. We explicitly reject the assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal framing: the phagocytic-receptor set is indistinguishable from background (n=16, mean +1.11 vs background +1.39, p=0.25) and the actomyosin motility module is significantly BELOW background (n=13, mean -1.05, p=0.0035; ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, PLEK among the most negative rows), so increased phagocytic uptake is not supported. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: bypassing the lysosomal export step with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should, without lowering hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) or TFEB, normalise the SREBP arm (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS) and SCARB1 toward APOE3 levels and reduce neutral-lipid droplet content. If cyclodextrin clears droplets but leaves the SREBP arm and SCARB1 elevated, the proposed ER-sensing link is wrong; if it changes nothing, the export bottleneck is wrong.", "Filipin/cholesterol and BODIPY imaging should show a greater fraction of unesterified cholesterol co-localised with LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4 than APOE3, with lysosomal cholesterol excess preceding droplet excess in a time course. Equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol fraction in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Pulse-chase with LDL-derived [3H]cholesterol should show slower conversion to cholesteryl ester per unit internalised (i.e. slower lysosome-to-ER delivery) in APOE4 despite equal or higher uptake. Equal or faster ER delivery in APOE4 falsifies the bottleneck.", "REJECTION TEST OF THE ASSIGNED FOCUS: APOE4 microglia should NOT show increased Arp2/3-dependent phagocytic-cup formation or increased bead/synaptosome/myelin internalisation RATE relative to APOE3; if anything, actomyosin-dependent motility and spreading should be equal or reduced (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, PLEK all in the bottom 2% of effects). A clear, large increase in phagocytic uptake rate in APOE4 with unchanged lysosomal lipid burden would favour a phagocytic-overload mechanism over this one.", "Blocking esterification (SOAT1 inhibitor plus DGAT1 inhibitor) should be selectively toxic to APOE4 microglia and should raise free-cholesterol and ER-stress markers more in APOE4 than APOE3, because the storage route is the only sink available when egress is limited. Equal tolerance in both genotypes weakens the storage-sink step.", "COMPETING-MODEL TEST: if the primary lesion is mito-nuclear imbalance rather than lysosomal, then restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit expression (e.g. rescuing MT-ATP6/MT-CYB translation) should normalise the lysosomal and lipogenic transcripts. Observing that lysosomal/SREBP transcripts are insensitive to mitochondrial rescue, while cyclodextrin does normalise them, supports this hypothesis over the mitochondrial alternative."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED: APOE4 microglia show coordinated high positive reported logFC for lysosomal acid hydrolases and the v-ATPase, including glycosphingolipid/glycan hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB) and V0/V1 subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), together with the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factor gene:TFEB and the lysosomal amino-acid transporter gene:SLC38A7. This is transcript abundance only; hydrolase activity, protein level and luminal pH were not measured.", "INFERRED (activity/flux): the expanded hydrolase and acidification program increases intra-lysosomal release of unesterified cholesterol, ceramide and sphingoid bases from ingested lipoprotein and membrane substrate, raising the luminal free-lipid load.", "PROPOSED BOTTLENECK (inferred, not measured): the machinery that moves that lipid out of the lysosomal lumen does not scale with it. Among measured members, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2 and gene:CLN3 are only +1.06 to +1.17 (27th-35th percentile of all observed effects, below the +1.46 background median), while the hydrolase arm is +3 to +10. NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured, so the export block is a hypothesis, not an observation. Net predicted flux: cholesterol and sphingolipid are retained in the endolysosome.", "INFERRED (localization/signalling): sequestration of sterol in the endolysosome lowers the ER-accessible cholesterol pool, so SCAP/INSIG de-represses SREBP even though total cellular lipid is not low. Consistent MEASURED transcripts: gene:SREBF1 (+4.67, 92nd pct), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:DHCR7 (+2.71), gene:LSS (+2.27), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87), gene:SREBF2 and gene:HMGCS1 (both ~+1.1, i.e. only at background - a partial, not uniform, sterol-synthesis induction).", "MEASURED plus INFERRED: lipid influx is simultaneously increased rather than throttled - gene:SCARB1 is the second-highest lipid-related row in the dataset (+8.22, 99th pct) - so uptake continues while egress is limited. Two independent 2D-gel spots whose candidate lists contain pentose-phosphate enzymes (protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046 with TALDO1; protein_spot:038 with TKT) are increased, which would be consistent with NADPH supply for SCD-dependent desaturation; spot identity is ambiguous and cannot be assigned to a single protein.", "PREDICTED OUTCOME: newly synthesised and imported acyl chains are routed into glycerolipid acylation and neutral-lipid storage (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.14, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) rather than efflux, yielding the APOE4 lipid-droplet/lipid-laden phenotype. Droplet number, cholesteryl-ester mass and efflux to ApoA-I were not measured here.", "SIDE ARM (alternative or compensatory): all 38 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are up (mean +2.81, p=1e-4) while 4 of 6 mitochondrially encoded subunits are down (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.44, gene:MT-CYB -2.34, gene:MT-ND4 -1.79, gene:MT-CO2 -1.30). This mito-nuclear imbalance could instead be the primary lesion, with lysosomal induction secondary; it is retained as the leading competing explanation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase capacity without matched lysosomal lipid egress, creating a sterol-export bottleneck that drives SREBP-dependent lipogenesis and neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.40254033895801794, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29801014544172855, "cosine_similarity": 0.3543019256387219, "direction_accuracy": 0.36893203883495146, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6435404530744337, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.40254033895801794, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29801014544172855, "cosine_similarity": 0.3543019256387219, "direction_accuracy": 0.36893203883495146, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6435404530744337, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.96669375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 225}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_139", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the median of this same list (+1.46 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base), not against zero.", "The list-wide positive shift (77% of rows positive) is treated as a normalisation/selection offset; only genes and sets displaced beyond this offset are used as evidence.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins. Assignments of spots 064/065/075 to v-ATPase V1 subunits, 058/067/069 to cathepsins/HEXB and 043-046 to ANXA1 are candidate-list inferences; the alternative candidates (e.g. TALDO1 in the ANXA1 spots, whose transcript is -2.3, or ARPC1B/ANXA1 in spots 064/065) are not excluded.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to report transcriptional programme, not enzyme activity; spot abundance is assumed to report a protein form, not localisation, maturation state or catalytic activity.", "Lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, cargo uptake rate, autophagic flux and all lipid species are unmeasured in the supplied data and are inferred or predicted, not observed.", "The RNA (10X Flex single-cell) and 2D protein-spot data are assumed to come from comparable microglial populations in the astrocyte co-culture; replicate number and any astrocyte contribution to the protein spots are not supplied.", "Reported protein significance flags are internally inconsistent with the supplied p-values for 14 of 92 spots, so spot-level significance is treated as approximate."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in the endocytic-to-lysosomal arm rather than in surface phagocytic-receptor or actin-motor programs: transcripts for endosome maturation (RAB7A, PIK3C3, VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B, DNM2, AP5M1), for the lipid-directed acid hydrolases (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, NAGLU) and for v-ATPase subunits are raised well above the strong global positive RNA shift, yet the protein spots whose candidate lists contain v-ATPase V1 subunits and cathepsins/HEXB are at or below the protein-spot median. We hypothesise that degradative throughput per unit of internalised lipid cargo (luminal acid hydrolysis, dependent on acidification and mature hydrolase protein) is the rate-limiting step, so that lipid-rich cargo transits to a compartment it cannot fully clear, and released or unhydrolysed lipid is shunted into re-esterification/storage lipids by the concurrently raised glycerolipid and sterol-ester synthesis transcripts (AGPAT2, LPCAT1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in mock-treated isogenic pairs, directly restoring luminal degradative capacity (recombinant/enhanced GBA or acid sphingomyelinase delivery, or acidifying nanoparticles/cAMP-independent v-ATPase support) should reduce the APOE4-specific accumulation of sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide and cholesteryl ester and shrink lipid droplets, whereas further transcriptional induction alone (TFEB overexpression, which raises hydrolase mRNA) should not normalise the lipids. If TFEB overexpression normalises the lipid difference while direct hydrolase/acidification support does not, the 'transcription-uncoupled protein bottleneck' claim is falsified.", "Per-cell functional assay: APOE4 microglia should show lower or unchanged DQ-BSA dequenching, BODIPY-sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide hydrolysis rate and LysoTracker-normalised acidification per lysosome despite higher CTSB/CTSD/GBA/SMPD1 transcripts, and immunoblot should show mature cathepsin D/B heavy chains and ATP6V1E1 protein that are not increased in proportion to their transcripts. Proportional increases in mature enzyme protein and in hydrolysis rate would weaken the mechanism.", "Cargo-dependence: removing or reducing lipid cargo (serum/lipoprotein-free medium, or blocking internalisation with DNM2 knockdown or dynasore) should collapse most of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid divergence and blunt the hydrolase/TFEB transcript elevation; persistence of the same lipid difference under cargo-free, uptake-blocked conditions would falsify the delivery-load arm.", "Class specificity: the lipid difference should be biased toward substrates of the induced-but-unmatched hydrolases (SM, HexCer, GM2-type glycolipids, plus stored CE/TAG) rather than a uniform increase in all lipid classes; a pure de novo fatty-acid/TAG signature with unchanged sphingolipids would favour a lipogenic rather than a catabolic-bottleneck mechanism.", "Rejected-alternative test (focus check): APOE4 microglia should NOT show a proportional increase in initial phagocytic uptake rate (bead, synaptosome or myelin uptake in the first 30-60 min) or in Rac/Arp2/3-dependent ruffling, because phagocytic-receptor transcripts (TREM2, MERTK, CD36, C1QA-C, FCGR) sit at the list median and actin regulators change in both directions; a large, coherent increase in early uptake rate with unchanged degradation would relocate the bottleneck to the uptake step and weaken this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_139", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for clathrin/dynamin-dependent internalisation and endosome maturation/sorting are raised far above the list-wide RNA shift (gene:AP5M1 +9.8, gene:DNM2 +5.8, gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:SNX3 +4.0, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:PIK3C3 +2.9, gene:RAB7A +2.7; set median 3.95 vs global median 1.46, permutation p\u003c0.001), together with the lipid-cargo receptor transcript gene:SCARB1 (+8.2). Inferred (not measured): a higher rate of lipid-rich membrane/lipoprotein cargo delivery into late endosomes in APOE4.", "Measured: a coherent CLEAR-type transcriptional response - gene:TFEB (+2.4) with gene:GAA (+10.0), gene:GBA (+6.7), gene:NAGLU (+5.9), gene:HEXA (+5.7), gene:SMPD1 (+5.6), gene:CTSB (+5.5), gene:CTSD (+2.9), gene:HEXB (+2.2) and v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H (+6.9), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.2), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.5), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.7). Inferred: this is a demand-driven compensatory programme rather than a spontaneous gain of degradative capacity.", "Measured at the protein-spot level, the compensation is not realised: spots whose candidate lists include v-ATPase V1 subunits are below the spot median (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93, protein_spot:075 -0.14; median -0.93 vs spot median +0.49, permutation p~0.04) and several cathepsin/HEXB-containing spots are among the most decreased (protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85). Inferred: mature hydrolase and proton-pump protein pools, and hence luminal acidification and hydrolytic activity per compartment, do not scale with cargo load. Neither pH, enzyme activity nor spot identity is directly measured.", "Inferred bottleneck: hydrolysis of sphingolipid and phospholipid cargo inside the late endosome/lysosome becomes rate-limiting relative to delivery, so substrates of the induced-but-unmatched enzymes (sphingomyelin for SMPD1, glucosylceramide/HexCer for GBA, GM2-type glycolipids for HEXA/HEXB, phospholipids liberated by cathepsin-dependent lipoprotein proteolysis) persist in the compartment.", "Measured: strong induction of glycerolipid/ester synthesis transcripts (gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SOAT1 +1.3) and of the Ca2+/phospholipid-binding annexin gene:ANXA1 (+4.2), whose candidate spots dominate the up-changed protein spots (protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:043 +1.96; ANXA1-containing spot median +0.68, p~0.03). Inferred: expanded internal PS/phospholipid-rich membrane and a route diverting released fatty acid and sterol into stored neutral lipid.", "Predicted consequence (not measured here): APOE4 microglia carry a larger poorly degraded endolysosomal lipid pool (sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, gangliosides, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate-associated species) plus increased cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol in droplets, without a proportional increase in bulk uptake capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand endolysosomal cargo delivery and CLEAR-type hydrolase transcription without matched acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase protein, creating a luminal lipid-catabolism bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1242220559781769, "cosine_similarity": 0.3542255336438969, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_139", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6429093851132686, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13272163349702765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1242220559781769, "cosine_similarity": 0.3542255336438969, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6429093851132686, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9199255, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 226}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_014", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; only the sign and the rank/relative magnitude against the same-file background are used, and no absolute fold change is claimed.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. HK1, PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, CS, MDH2, PDHA1, ACLY, FASN, TOMM20) means not supplied, not unchanged. All set-level statements are therefore made relative to the median of the supplied rows, not to a whole-transcriptome null.", "The strong global positive shift (median about +1.46, 77% of rows positive) reflects selection and/or normalisation and is treated as a nuisance baseline, so only deviation from that baseline is treated as signal.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels measured by a probe-based single-cell assay are assumed to reflect relative mitochondrial transcript availability; if the probe panel quantifies mitochondrial transcripts unreliably, step 2 fails.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly predictive of the corresponding protein and complex-subunit availability at day 30; no mitochondrial protein was uniquely identified in the proteomic spots.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not treated as identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for any step here.", "The astrocyte co-culture partner is assumed not to be the dominant source of the microglial genotype effect; cell-type deconvolution was not supplied.", "Effect direction is assumed to mean higher in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock treatment, as stated in the file metadata."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia express a coordinately expanded nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (TCA enzymes, mitochondrial carriers, import/translation factors, and nuclear subunits of complexes I/III/IV/V) while the measured mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are relatively lower than the strong global upward shift of this differential-expression set. We hypothesise that supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit or matrix-enzyme supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembling functional complexes III/IV/V, so oxidative-phosphorylation flux fails to scale with the enlarged matrix/carrier capacity; the resulting mismatch, combined with reduced committed glycolytic entry (HK2, PFKP down) despite increased glucose-transporter transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3), shifts APOE4 microglia toward glutamate/aspartate-fed anaplerosis and toward citrate export via SLC25A1 into cytosolic lipogenic/sterol-esterifying pathways rather than terminal oxidation. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, assembly, localisation and causal statements are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (e.g. mitochondrially targeted TFAM/mtDNA-copy-number boost, or allotopic/rescued expression of the limiting core subunit) should selectively increase ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption and lower SLC25A1-dependent citrate export and SREBP target transcripts (SCD, DHCR24, SOAT1) in APOE4 without a comparable effect in APOE3. If APOE4 respiration and lipogenic transcripts are unchanged by restored mtDNA-encoded subunit supply, the primary bottleneck is refuted.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling should show, in APOE4 versus APOE3, a lower ratio of fully assembled complex V, III and IV to nuclear-encoded subunit or matrix-enzyme content, with accumulation of nuclear-subunit subassemblies. Equal or higher assembled-complex stoichiometry in APOE4 would weaken steps 2-3.", "Stable-isotope tracing: U-13C6-glucose should contribute a smaller fraction of citrate m+2 and of palmitate label in APOE4 than APOE3, while U-13C5-glutamine should contribute a larger fraction of citrate and of newly synthesised lipid. If glucose carbon contribution to citrate and lipid is equal or higher in APOE4, step 5 is refuted.", "Pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) should reduce neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation preferentially in APOE4 microglia while leaving oxygen consumption unimproved or slightly improved. If SLC25A1 loss does not reduce APOE4 lipid storage, step 6 is refuted.", "Hexokinase-step rescue: overexpressing HK2 in APOE4 microglia should increase glycolytic rate and extracellular acidification but should not normalise maximal respiration or spare respiratory capacity. Full normalisation of respiration by HK2 alone would indicate a glycolytic rather than a mitonuclear bottleneck and would weaken the hypothesis.", "Global weakening result: if Seahorse shows APOE4 microglia with equal or higher ATP-linked respiration and spare respiratory capacity per unit citrate-synthase activity or TOMM20 protein, the entire proposed oxidative bottleneck fails regardless of the transcript pattern."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Nuclear-encoded mitochondrial capacity is transcriptionally expanded in APOE4 relative to APOE3 and relative to the global upward shift of this DE set: TCA/carrier genes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11) and nuclear OXPHOS subunits (gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:CYCS), together with import and mitochondrial-translation machinery (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:TUFM, gene:DARS2). This is measured abundance of transcripts, not measured enzyme activity or organelle mass.", "In the same cells the mtDNA-encoded core subunits that nucleate complexes V, III, IV and I are not co-scaled and are mostly negative (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2), against a global DE median that is strongly positive. We infer a stoichiometric shortfall of mtDNA-encoded subunits per unit of nuclear-encoded subunit; mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass and assembled-complex levels were not measured.", "Because complexes III, IV and V cannot assemble without their mtDNA-encoded cores, we infer that assembly, not matrix enzyme content, becomes the bottleneck: proton-pumping and ATP-synthase capacity, and therefore ATP-linked respiration and NADH reoxidation, do not increase in proportion to the expanded TCA/carrier program. This is inferred flux, not observed.", "A partial block of NADH reoxidation raises matrix NADH/NAD+, which we infer inhibits NAD+-dependent dehydrogenases and favours retention of TCA intermediates; mitochondrial stress/integrated-stress signalling transcripts are concordantly elevated (gene:DELE1, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3), and antioxidant transcripts are elevated (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX2, gene:GPX4), consistent with, but not proof of, increased electron leak.", "Glucose is not used to compensate at the committed step: glucose-transporter and upper/mid-glycolytic transcripts are higher (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1, gene:PFKM, gene:SLC16A1) while the hexokinase and PFKP steps are lower (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP). We infer that glucose-6-phosphate production, not transport, limits glycolytic pyruvate supply, so carbon entering the TCA cycle is preferentially derived from glutamate/aspartate anaplerosis and shuttle activity (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1, gene:MDH1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13).", "Citrate that is not fully oxidised is inferred to be exported by the elevated citrate/isocitrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1) to the cytosol, where reducing equivalents from gene:ME1 support a lipogenic and sterol program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) and esterification/storage steps (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1). ACLY, ACACA and FASN were not measured, so cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation is inferred, not observed.", "The predicted consequence is a shift of APOE4 microglial carbon use away from complete glucose oxidation toward glutamine/aspartate-fed anaplerosis with citrate-derived neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester synthesis, accompanied by an increased lysosomal lipid-hydrolase demand (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1) as stored lipid is turned over."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance caps oxidative flux in APOE4 microglia and reroutes TCA carbon out as citrate"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1476756637004763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23041375349898724, "cosine_similarity": 0.35416455555090276, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6164822006472491, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1476756637004763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23041375349898724, "cosine_similarity": 0.35416455555090276, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6164822006472491, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71288575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 227}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_075", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified log base); therefore only magnitudes/ranks relative to this background, not direction alone, are treated as informative.", "Transcript abundance of lysosomal hydrolases, sterol-synthesis enzymes and acyltransferases is used as a proxy for pathway activity; enzyme activity, flux, protein level and subcellular localisation were not measured.", "SREBP proteolytic activation and ER-accessible cholesterol are inferred from the target-gene pattern only; no sterol sensor, lipidomic or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied in this dataset.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme's abundance.", "Gene sets were curated by function after inspecting the data, so the enrichment statistics are exploratory and partly post hoc.", "The 2D iPSC microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30 is assumed to have comparable APOE4/APOE3 cell-state composition; ambient RNA or state-composition differences could inflate coordinated module shifts."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a bottleneck in delivering endo-lysosomally derived cholesterol to the ER-accessible sterol pool. The transcriptome shows a simultaneously expanded lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (TFEB-type), elevated lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors, and an un-switched-off SREBP-type sterol-synthesis program together with esterification and glycerolipid enzymes - a combination expected only if the ER sterol sensor reports low cholesterol while sterol is retained in lysosomal and neutral-lipid compartments. We propose this feed-forward loop (low ER-accessible sterol -\u003e more synthesis and uptake -\u003e more SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification and storage) is the mechanism differentiating APOE4 from APOE3, not an unfolded-protein response. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely restoring ER-accessible sterol in APOE4 microglia (e.g. 2-6 h 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin/cholesterol complex, or SOAT1 inhibition with avasimibe to release esterified sterol) should collapse the sterol-synthesis program (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, DHCR7, LDLR) to APOE3 levels within hours while lysosomal hydrolase transcripts stay elevated. If SREBP targets remain high after ER sterol repletion, the 'sterol-poor ER sensor' bottleneck is wrong.", "Direct pool test: filipin/ALOD4-type staining plus neutral-lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX) imaging should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 sterol in LAMP1-positive compartments and more lipid droplets, but equal or LOWER ER-accessible cholesterol. Equal lysosomal sterol with equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 would falsify the mechanism.", "SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol mass in APOE4 more than in APOE3 and shift free sterol toward the ER; no genotype-selective lipid change would weaken the storage-routing step.", "TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts without normalising the sterol-synthesis program, showing lysosomal expansion is compensatory; if TFEB knockdown also normalises SREBP targets, the causal order proposed here is wrong.", "Rejection of the ER-proteostasis alternative: pharmacological ATF6 or PERK inhibition should not normalise the APOE4 lysosomal-lipid transcript module; conversely, if UPR inhibition abolishes the sterol/lysosome differences, the primary bottleneck is ER proteostasis, not lipid egress."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein poorly lipidates and exports cholesterol/phospholipid from microglia (inferred, not measured here); APOE, ABCA7 and TREM2 transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2), consistent with an attempted but insufficient efflux/sensing response.", "Primary bottleneck: sterol and sphingolipid substrate that reaches the endo-lysosome is not efficiently transferred to the ER-accessible pool. Measured correlates are an expanded lysosomal catabolic/acidification transcript program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A) with the lysosomal-biogenesis factor TFEB elevated (gene:TFEB); the transport step itself and lysosomal lipid content are inferred, not observed.", "Because ER-accessible cholesterol is inferred to be low, SREBP-type processing at the ER is not repressed: sterol-synthesis and sterol-sensing transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 (gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:ERLIN1). Activity of SREBP cleavage is inferred from target-transcript pattern, not measured.", "In parallel the cell keeps importing lipid: uptake/scavenger receptor transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:NPC2, gene:OSBPL1A), so total sterol/lipid influx is predicted to exceed egress capacity.", "Excess free sterol and fatty acid are routed to storage rather than membrane use: esterification and glycerolipid/desaturase enzymes are coordinately elevated (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:MBOAT2), predicting increased cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol (lipid-droplet) mass in APOE4. These lipid pools were not measured in the supplied data.", "The stored/lysosomal sterol never relieves the ER sensor, closing a feed-forward loop that stabilises the APOE4 state; secondary ER membrane-lipid stress markers (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3, gene:MANF) rise modestly as a consequence, but classical ER chaperone/ERAD transcripts do not (gene:SEL1L, gene:PDIA3, gene:SEC62 are lower), so this is treated as downstream and non-diagnostic rather than as a canonical unfolded-protein response."], "title": "A lysosomal cholesterol-egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia keeps the ER sterol sensor in a 'sterol-poor' state, driving uptake plus esterification into neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20937488461396447, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2792962178937031, "cosine_similarity": 0.35366659507874737, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6162750809061489, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20937488461396447, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2792962178937031, "cosine_similarity": 0.35366659507874737, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6162750809061489, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86397525, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 228}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_049", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (mean +1.39, 77% of rows positive, unspecified logarithm base preserved); all statements are relative comparisons within this biased background, not whole-transcriptome enrichment.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the abundance of the corresponding hydrolase, transporter and esterification proteins; enzyme activity, lipid flux, and subcellular localization were not measured.", "SREBP-target transcript elevation is interpreted as an inferred readout of ongoing SREBP transcriptional output; SREBP cleavage, nuclear form, and ER sterol content were not measured.", "The relative-magnitude argument (hydrolases up far more than NPC2) is assumed to reflect a real stoichiometric imbalance in the degradative compartment rather than gene-specific dynamic range or selection of DE rows; NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, PLIN2, MCOLN1, GRN and PSAP are not in the supplied data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and keratin-dominated spots are treated as likely contaminants.", "Astrocyte co-culture and unreported replicate structure could contribute genotype-associated composition differences that are not separable in these summary data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a transcript program in which lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase genes are among the most strongly elevated rows (CTSB, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H, CTSD, with TFEB up), while the lysosomal cholesterol-egress carrier NPC2 rises only to the background level; we propose that the rate-limiting step is export of hydrolysis-derived sterol/lipid from the lysosome to the ER, so ER-based feedback is not engaged, an SREBP-type uptake-and-synthesis program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, INSIG1, plus scavenger receptors SCARB1, CD36) stays on, and carbon supplied by citrate/acetate routes (SLC25A1, ACSS2) is esterified by SOAT1/DGAT1 into stored neutral lipid rather than being sensed or disposed of. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating route test: load APOE4 and APOE3 microglia either with lipoprotein/myelin (which must transit the lysosome) or with cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin delivered directly to membranes, then measure SREBP-target transcripts (SCD, LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR24) and SREBP2 nuclear form. The mechanism predicts a genotype-by-route interaction: APOE4 represses these targets poorly after lipoprotein/myelin loading but normally after direct cholesterol delivery. If APOE4 fails to repress after both routes (or represses normally after both), the lysosomal-egress bottleneck is falsified and the defect lies in ER sensing or nowhere.", "SOAT1 inhibition (or DGAT1 inhibition) should reduce cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplet content selectively in APOE4 and increase free sterol, while leaving the SREBP-target transcripts still elevated; if esterification blockade normalises the SREBP-target program, the storage step rather than lysosomal egress is the controlling node.", "TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1H) and worsen, not relieve, APOE4 lipid retention; if TFEB knockdown also abolishes the SREBP/esterification signature, the proposed hierarchy (lysosome upstream, ER program downstream) is wrong.", "Filipin or LipidSpot imaging with lysosomal counterstain should show increased lysosome-localised unesterified sterol in APOE4 alongside increased cytoplasmic droplets; absence of lysosomal sterol accumulation, or reduced (not increased) cathepsin/GBA enzymatic activity despite the transcript increases, would weaken the mechanism.", "Because the assigned cytoskeletal/phagocytic focus is not supported here, the mechanism additionally predicts that bulk particle uptake (bead or pHrodo-zymosan phagocytic index) will differ little between APOE4 and APOE3, while the fraction of internalised lipid converted to cholesteryl ester will differ strongly; a large uptake deficit with normal esterification partition would favour an actin/phagocytosis mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia show strongly increased transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and the v-ATPase (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:MAN2B1) together with gene:TFEB; inferred: an expanded, acidified degradative compartment with increased hydrolytic capacity (activity, not measured here).", "Measured: within that same compartment the sterol-egress carrier gene:NPC2 rises only +1.17, at the background median of these selected rows, while hydrolases rise +2.9 to +6.9; inferred (primary bottleneck): post-hydrolytic transfer of liberated cholesterol/lipid out of the lysosomal lumen toward the ER is rate-limiting relative to hydrolysis, producing luminal retention of lipid (a pool not measured in this dataset).", "Inferred: because regulatory sterol does not reach the ER pool efficiently, SREBP-type processing is not repressed; measured consequence is a uniformly elevated SREBP-target transcript set (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1), 14/14 rows positive despite the cell already being lipid-loaded.", "Measured: uptake receptors gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1 and gene:APOE itself are elevated; inferred: continued lipoprotein/lipid influx into the same blocked endolysosomal route, sustaining substrate delivery.", "Measured: cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH supply routes are elevated (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:ME1, gene:ACO2) alongside broadly increased nuclear-encoded OXPHOS rows; inferred: carbon and reducing equivalents are available for desaturation (gene:SCD) rather than being limiting.", "Measured: the esterification enzymes gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1 are elevated; inferred: the dominant disposal route for the excess free fatty acid and any ER-delivered sterol is esterification into cytoplasmic neutral-lipid droplets, which buffers lipotoxicity but does not restore feedback, giving the APOE4 lipid-accumulating phenotype.", "Measured/ambiguous corroboration: 2D protein spots containing lysosomal and membrane-lipid-binding candidates are increased (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:063) and the three largest spot increases (protein_spot:046, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:043) all contain ANXA1, whose transcript is also strongly up (gene:ANXA1); inferred only as consistency, since each spot has several candidate genes."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at post-hydrolytic lysosomal lipid egress, leaving ER sterol feedback disengaged and shunting lipid into SOAT1/DGAT1 neutral-lipid stores"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23250747701510172, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2664916185549715, "cosine_similarity": 0.35326967259030395, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6295728155339806, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23250747701510172, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2664916185549715, "cosine_similarity": 0.35326967259030395, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6295728155339806, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.23848725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 229}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_014", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all with adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e1), not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway statements are therefore made relative to the dataset-wide median (+1.46) rather than to an absolute zero, and absence of a gene is not evidence of no change.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given; magnitudes are used only for ranking and relative comparison, not as literal fold changes.", "mRNA abundance is treated as a partial proxy for enzyme/subunit availability; enzyme activity, metabolite pools, flux, membrane potential and respiration were not measured in these data and are explicitly inferred.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript capture by the 10X Flex probe chemistry is assumed to be at least internally comparable between the isogenic genotypes; a genotype-independent probe or capture bias against MT transcripts would invalidate the mitonuclear-imbalance step.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are cited only as weak, ambiguous corroboration and never as identified enzyme measurements.", "Astrocyte co-culture means extracellular substrate supply (glucose, lactate, glutamine) is partly non-cell-autonomous, so measured microglial transcripts reflect both intrinsic genotype effects and altered substrate environment.", "Positive effects mean higher in APOE4 than APOE3 at day 30, mock treatment; replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes, carriers/import) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts, while committed glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2) sit below the dataset-wide upward shift despite higher glucose/monocarboxylate transporter transcripts. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for respiratory-chain assembly, so the enlarged nuclear mitochondrial program raises TCA/anaplerotic carbon input capacity without a proportional gain in oxidative ATP flux; the resulting mismatch favours citrate export and lipogenic/sterol and lysosomal programmes rather than complete substrate oxidation. This is an association-based mechanistic proposal; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assembly test: blue-native PAGE/complexome or in-gel activity plus Seahorse on isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show assembled complex I/IV holoenzyme and maximal (FCCP) oxygen consumption that are equal to or lower than APOE3, and a reduced mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded subunit protein ratio, despite the higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. If assembled complexes and maximal respiration rise in proportion to the transcript increase, the assembly bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation A (bottleneck identity): boosting mitochondrial gene expression (TFAM overexpression, or rescue of mtDNA copy number/mt-translation) should increase assembled complex I and maximal respiration substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3. Discriminating perturbation B (substrate input): glutaminase inhibition (CB-839) should lower 13C-glutamine labelling of citrate strongly in APOE4 with only a modest change in maximal respiration. If instead CB-839 collapses APOE4 respiration while TFAM rescue does nothing, the bottleneck is substrate input, not assembly, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Substrate-use test: galactose-for-glucose substitution (forcing OXPHOS-dependent ATP) should reduce ATP/viability more in APOE4 than APOE3, while 2-deoxyglucose should reduce ATP less in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or better APOE4 performance in galactose would weaken the mechanism.", "13C tracing: U-13C-glucose should give a lower fractional contribution to lactate (M+3) and to citrate (M+2) in APOE4, and U-13C-glutamine a higher fractional contribution to citrate/malate, with increased 13C label appearing in fatty acids/sterols consistent with SLC25A1-dependent citrate export. Equal glucose-to-citrate contribution and no shift in glutamine labelling would falsify the substrate-switch step.", "Independent measurement of the mitonuclear ratio by probe-independent RT-qPCR or bulk RNA-seq (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 versus NDUFA5, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) should reproduce the lower mtDNA-encoded:nuclear ratio in APOE4; if the ratio is unchanged with the alternative assay, the central mitonuclear imbalance step is a Flex probe artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "Protein-level check on the glycolytic step: hexokinase-2 and PFKP protein and hexokinase enzymatic activity should be lower in APOE4 lysates while GLUT1 surface glucose uptake is equal or higher; unchanged HK2/PFKP protein and activity with equal glycolytic flux (ECAR, lactate efflux) would remove the glycolytic-repression arm of the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured abundance: transcripts of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial machinery are coordinately higher in APOE4 than APOE3 relative to the dataset-wide shift (49 mapped genes across OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes and SLC25 carriers/TOM-TIM import; set median 2.65 vs global 1.46 in the reported, unspecified-base log units; permutation p=0.0004).", "Measured abundance, opposite direction: the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts present sit below the same background (median -1.56, permutation p=0.03; nuclear OXPHOS vs mtDNA-encoded Mann-Whitney p=7e-4), i.e. a mitonuclear expression imbalance at the RNA level.", "Inferred activity/stoichiometry (not measured here): because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded core subunits, this imbalance predicts assembly-limited holoenzyme formation, so the extra nuclear-subunit transcripts are only partially converted into assembled, flux-competent complexes; no assembled-complex, protein or respiration measurement is available in these data.", "Inferred flux at the glycolytic entry point: committed glycolytic steps are relatively repressed (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2, HK3 all negative) while glucose and monocarboxylate transporter transcripts are positive (SLC2A3, SLC2A1, SLC2A8, SLC16A1) and mitochondrial pyruvate import/PDH-activating transcripts are strongly positive (MPC2, PDP1); we infer lower glycolytic ATP production per unit of imported carbon, with the pyruvate that is formed preferentially routed into mitochondria rather than to lactate.", "Inferred anaplerotic substitution: higher glutamine/glutamate handling and aspartate-malate transcripts (GLS, GLUD1, GOT1, SLC1A5, SLC38A2, SLC25A11, MDH1, OGDH, DLD) indicate increased capacity for non-glucose carbon entry into the TCA cycle, sustaining or increasing TCA intermediate pools even if terminal oxidation is capped.", "Inferred downstream consequence: with terminal oxidation assembly-limited but TCA input capacity raised, citrate export (SLC25A1 transcript up) is predicted to feed the lipogenic/sterol programme (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, HMGCS1, DHCR24) and to co-occur with an expanded lysosomal/degradative programme (CTSB, GBA, HEXA, TFEB), giving a lipid-loaded, energetically constrained APOE4 microglial state under mock conditions."], "title": "Assembly-limited respiratory chain in APOE4 microglia: an up-regulated nuclear mitochondrial program outruns mtDNA-encoded core subunits, shifting carbon from glycolysis to anaplerotic/citrate-export routes"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11699220913488165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22462584527667986, "cosine_similarity": 0.35311124071335465, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5998899676375405, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11699220913488165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22462584527667986, "cosine_similarity": 0.35311124071335465, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5998899676375405, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.874858, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 230}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_028", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected significant-DE list with an unspecified logarithm base and a 77% positive background (1705+/507-); program calls are made relative to that background, and absent genes (SPTLC1/2, ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1, PSAP, GRN, NPC1, ABCA1) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and OXPHOS transcripts translate at least partly into protein and into per-cell enzymatic capacity; none of these activities, nor lysosomal pH, lipid species levels or any flux, were measured here.", "Protein spots are ambiguous 2D-gel features (2-6 candidate genes each, keratin/actin-dominated); spots containing CTSL/CTSD/CTSB/MAN2B1/GNS candidates (protein_spot:052, :053, :012, :006, :007, :063 up; protein_spot:058, :067, :069 down) are used only as a compatibility/contradiction test and are never treated as measurements of a named protein.", "The genotype comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so differences reflect a baseline cell state; any claim of reduced clearance reserve applies to a future challenge, not to the measured condition.", "Co-regulated genes are not independent, so the descriptive coherence reported is not a formal enrichment result, and no single gene is asserted as the causal node."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state shift, not a single enzyme lesion: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein recognition and uptake, for endolysosomal acidification and hydrolysis (with the sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolase arm among the largest effects), and for mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS are jointly elevated, while glycolytic commitment steps fall; this pattern is best read as increased routing of lipid cargo through an expanded acidic degradative compartment toward oxidative disposal and re-esterification, with SREBP-associated sterol-synthesis transcripts remaining high, indicating that the ER regulatory sterol pool is not repleted by this increased traffic. The measurements are abundances; the corresponding hydrolase activities, lysosomal pH, lipid pools and fluxes were not measured, so increased throughput is inferred, not observed, and reduced clearance reserve would only be revealed by a future lipid challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under mock, per-cell activity assays (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, cathepsin B/D), lysosomal pH/LysoTracker and lysosome volume should show higher or equal acid-hydrolase activity and equal-or-lower pH in APOE4, with no accumulation of the corresponding substrates (glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3, sphingomyelin, unesterified cholesterol) by lipidomics/filipin. If instead APOE4 shows substrate accumulation and flat or reduced hydrolase activity despite the elevated transcripts, the increased-throughput mechanism is falsified in favour of failed compensation.", "Prospective: an isotope-traced lipid load (e.g. 13C/D-labelled myelin debris or oxLDL) should be cleared at least as fast in APOE4 as APOE3, with greater label appearance in CO2/TCA intermediates and in cholesteryl/triglyceride esters; slower clearance with equal uptake would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective: blocking cargo delivery (SR-B1/CD36 blockade, or lipid-poor medium) should attenuate the elevated lysosomal, sphingolipid-hydrolase and SREBP-associated transcript sets in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the full lysosomal program under lipid-free conditions would show it is cargo-independent and would weaken step 1-2 of the mechanism.", "Prospective: acute sterol repletion of the ER (LDL loading or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should suppress SREBP-target transcripts equally in both genotypes if sensing and delivery are intact; failure to suppress in APOE4 would support the inferred endolysosomal sterol retention, whereas equal suppression would remove step 5 without affecting steps 1-4.", "Prospective challenge test of reserve: v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin) or GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) plus a lipid load should impair clearance and viability disproportionately in APOE4; equal sensitivity would argue that the expanded lysosomal program confers no altered dependence and would weaken the routing claim.", "Prospective proteomic test: targeted immunoassay or LC-MS/MS resolving the ambiguous spots should show higher mature GBA, HEXA/HEXB and SMPD1 protein in APOE4 with unchanged or lower CTSS; finding lower mature hydrolase protein, matching the down spots protein_spot:058/:067/:069, would contradict the capacity-expansion step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid- and debris-recognition/uptake machinery (gene:SCARB1 8.22, gene:CD36 1.38, gene:LDLR 1.50, gene:MERTK 1.30, gene:GAS6 1.33, gene:MFGE8 1.49, gene:TREM2 1.28, gene:APOE 1.24), which is inferred to increase delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endosomal system (uptake rate not measured).", "In parallel the endolysosomal compartment's degradative machinery is transcriptionally expanded: acidification subunits (gene:ATP6V1H 6.88, gene:ATP6V1A 4.23, gene:ATP6V0C 3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 2.30), membrane/biogenesis components (gene:LAMP1 1.38, gene:SCARB2 1.06, gene:TFEB 2.38, gene:MITF 1.03) and hydrolases (gene:GAA 10.0, gene:CTSK 7.36, gene:NAGLU 5.91, gene:CTSB 5.52, gene:CTSD 2.86, gene:MAN2B1 1.81), consistent with greater degradative capacity rather than loss of it.", "The sphingolipid arm of this program is prominent and uniformly positive (gene:GBA 6.71, gene:HEXA 5.68, gene:SMPD1 5.63, gene:GBA2 2.63, gene:HEXB 2.17, gene:GLTP 2.38, gene:ST3GAL5 2.17, gene:GM2A 2.01, gene:SUMF1 2.01, gene:GLA 1.53, gene:NPC2 1.17), so sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid turnover capacity is predicted to be raised together with lysosomal capacity; the de-novo ceramide arm (gene:CERS4 2.52, gene:KDSR 1.27, gene:CERS6 1.06, gene:ORMDL2 1.91, gene:CERK 1.23, gene:SGPL1 1.09) is not distinguishable from the selected-list background and is not claimed as driver.", "Catabolic products are inferred to be routed to oxidative disposal and storage rather than glycolysis: TCA/OXPHOS transcripts are the strongest program by median (gene:MDH1 8.7, gene:OGDH 8.6, gene:ATP5ME 5.2, gene:SLC25A1 4.5, gene:CYCS 2.58, gene:COX6C 2.17, gene:NDUFB2 2.11, gene:SDHB 1.65) and esterification/storage transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 1.25, gene:DGAT1 1.72, gene:SCD 4.17), while committed glycolytic steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08).", "Despite elevated uptake transcripts, SREBP-associated sterol/lipid-synthesis transcripts remain high (gene:SREBF2 1.06, gene:SREBF1 4.67, gene:INSIG1 1.87, gene:HMGCS1 1.08, gene:LSS 2.27, gene:DHCR7 2.71, gene:DHCR24 3.69, gene:ACAT2 2.04, gene:EBP 1.34, gene:LDLR 1.50), which is interpreted as the ER regulatory sterol pool not being repleted, i.e. sterol retained in the endolysosome or diverted to esters; this is an inference about localization, not a measured pool.", "Net predicted state in the mock condition: a lipid-handling, lysosome-expanded, oxidatively biased APOE4 microglial state with altered protease routing (gene:CTSS -5.57 down and gene:M6PR -1.72 down while gene:IGF2R 2.02 is up), which may nonetheless have reduced spare clearance capacity that only a lipid or myelin-debris challenge would expose."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-expanded lipid-catabolic state that routes ingested lipid, including sphingolipid, to hydrolysis and mitochondrial oxidation while ER sterol sensing stays unsatisfied"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2626647712587232, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2335082448238781, "cosine_similarity": 0.35274904357612824, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5987508090614887, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2626647712587232, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2335082448238781, "cosine_similarity": 0.35274904357612824, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5987508090614887, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.137029, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 54}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_092", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1, 77.1% positive); program coherence is judged against that upward-biased background, and genes absent from the list (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MVD, IDI1, CYP51A1, MSMO1, PLIN2, SQSTM1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes (range -7.94 to +15.46) are not assumed comparable to the protein log2 scale.", "Increased transcripts for enzymes and receptors are treated as capacity indicators only; SREBP2 proteolytic processing, SOAT1 esterification flux, LDLR surface protein (opposed by increased MYLIP/IDOL), lysosomal hydrolase activity, cholesterol mass and its subcellular distribution were not measured here.", "Sign coherence within a co-regulated program (SREBP2 targets, CLEAR targets) is not statistically independent evidence; descriptive binomial checks against the 77.1% background (lysosome 20/21 up, p~0.03; sterol set 13/13 up, p~0.03) are illustrative, not formal enrichment.", "Protein spots are ambiguous: median 5 candidate genes per spot, with KRT1/KRT10/KRT9 (33/30/14 spots) and ACTB (25 spots) recurring; no spot lists any sterol-pathway enzyme, so the sterol arm is untested at the protein level and no spot is read as confirming an individual protein.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture at day 30; astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply is part of the system and is not controlled by these measurements.", "No causal direction is established by these data; the mechanism is a testable interpretation of a steady-state cross-genotype contrast."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia occupy a coordinated lipid-handling cell state in which sterol is routed toward endolysosomal degradation, esterification/neutral-lipid storage and oxysterol conversion rather than to the ER-accessible regulatory pool; the transcriptome therefore shows simultaneous 'sterol-low' SREBP2 output (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, LDLR, INSIG1, SREBF2 all increased) and 'sterol-sufficient' oxysterol/LXR-arm output (CH25H, CYP27A1, APOE, ABCA7, MYLIP increased) together with a TFEB-linked lysosomal expansion program and increased scavenger/phagocytic receptor transcripts. The claim is about routing and sensed compartmental distribution, not about a demonstrated rate-limiting defect: the data cannot distinguish a successfully expanded sterol-processing throughput from a failing one, and cholesterol mass, esterification flux and efflux were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, discriminating: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, orthogonal cholesterol probes should show a compartment discordance - ER/PM-accessible cholesterol (ALOD4 or D4H biosensor) equal or lower in APOE4 while total plus esterified cholesterol (cholesteryl-ester mass spectrometry, filipin/LipidTOX in LAMP1+ compartments) is higher. If APOE4 shows equal-or-higher ER-accessible cholesterol together with the observed elevated SREBP2 targets (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24), the routing mechanism is weakened and a sterol-independent driver of the SREBP program is favored.", "PROSPECTIVE perturbation: blocking the esterification/storage sink (SOAT1 inhibitor, e.g. avasimibe) or restoring lysosome-to-ER sterol delivery should selectively normalize the SREBP2 target set in APOE4 (reduction of gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR toward APOE3) with a smaller effect in APOE3. Equal reduction in both genotypes, or no reduction in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE: TFEB knockdown should lower the CLEAR transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A) in both genotypes; if the expanded lysosomal compartment is the sterol sink, TFEB knockdown should raise ER-accessible cholesterol and lower SREBP2 targets specifically in APOE4. No genotype-specific effect on the sterol arm would argue that the lysosomal and sterol programs are parallel outputs of a shared state rather than causally linked.", "PROSPECTIVE, adaptation vs deficit: LDLR surface protein and DiI-LDL / acetylated-LDL uptake should be measured. If LDLR surface protein is not increased in APOE4 despite increased gene:LDLR (consistent with increased gene:MYLIP), the SREBP2 signature reflects unresolved sensing rather than realized uptake; if instead uptake is increased and cholesteryl-ester storage rises without loss of viability or phagocytic capacity, the state is successful adaptation/increased throughput and the 'unresolved sensing' framing must be revised.", "PROSPECTIVE challenge test (reserve, not ongoing defect): after myelin-debris or apoptotic-cell loading, APOE4 should show greater cholesteryl-ester accumulation and slower cargo clearance than APOE3, and greater sensitivity to statin or SQLE inhibition. Equal handling under challenge would indicate the mock-state differences do not constitute a reduced reserve."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalization receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:STAB1 +1.13, complement opsonin genes C1QA/B/C ~+1.2), which is compatible with greater delivery of lipid-rich cargo to endosomes; the internalization rate itself is unmeasured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA + ambiguous protein): a TFEB/CLEAR-type lysosomal program is co-elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:RAB7A +2.65), enlarging the degradative compartment that receives internalized sterol; cathepsin/glycosidase-containing spots are mostly increased (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58, protein_spot:012 +0.68, protein_spot:006/007 +0.58) but every such spot also lists actin/keratin candidates, so no individual hydrolase is confirmed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred routing): sterol emerging from this compartment is preferentially esterified/stored and side-converted rather than added to the ER regulatory pool - gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:FABP3 +1.35, gene:FABP5 +1.13, plus oxysterol-generating gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49 and gene:HSD3B7 +2.74.", "Step 4 (measured RNA): oxysterol-responsive/LXR-arm transcripts are up (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:MYLIP +1.28), indicating that some sterol-sufficiency signal is being generated, while non-vesicular ER-directed transfer capacity is not uniformly increased (gene:OSBPL8 -1.90 against gene:OSBPL1A +1.03).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): despite that sufficiency signal, the ER sterol sensor output remains in the 'low' configuration - every represented SREBP2/SREBP1 target is increased (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:FADS1 +1.59). Co-occurrence of SREBP2-on and LXR-on outputs is the signature of a compartmentally discordant sterol distribution rather than of a uniformly low or uniformly high cellular sterol level.", "Step 6 (net state, direction unresolved): the result is a self-reinforcing acquisition-plus-storage state - more uptake capacity, more degradative capacity, more esterification/storage capacity - whose steady-state consequence is a shift of sterol into lysosomal and esterified pools. Whether this is adequate adaptation in the mock condition or a reduced reserve that only fails under a lipid/myelin/apoptotic-cell challenge is not determined by these data; efflux capacity (ABCA1, ABCG1) and NPC1/LIPA were not among the supplied rows and are unknown, not unchanged."], "title": "Compartment-discordant sterol routing in APOE4 microglia: expanded endolysosomal/esterified sterol sinks keep the ER-accessible pool low, sustaining SREBP2-driven synthesis and uptake"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22663663552782187, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.244752276624727, "cosine_similarity": 0.35167494161886076, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059644012944984, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22663663552782187, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.244752276624727, "cosine_similarity": 0.35167494161886076, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059644012944984, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.033727, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 55}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_023", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list itself is globally up-shifted (median about +1.46 in the reported, unspecified-base logarithm; 77% positive). All pathway statements are therefore claims about relative rank and directional coherence within this list, and assume the global up-shift is at least partly biological rather than entirely a normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-composition artefact of the pseudobulk 10X Flex co-culture design.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only monotone ordering and sign are used, never absolute fold-change arithmetic.", "Transcript level is used as a proxy for availability of the corresponding protein and enzyme; this is unverified here, since protein spots have multiple candidate genes and spot effects show essentially no correlation with candidate-gene RNA effects (Pearson r about -0.05 across 71 spots).", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin- and hydrolase-containing spots are treated only as ambiguous, mixed-direction evidence, not as measurements of CTSB, CTSD, HEXB or GNS abundance.", "Lysosomal pH, luminal free cholesterol, lipid-droplet content, hydrolase activity, cargo-degradation flux and lipid efflux were not measured; every statement about activity, flux, localization or compartment load is an inference.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, so genotype rather than treatment is assumed to be the source of the difference; astrocyte co-culture and possible microglial state-composition differences are assumed not to generate the coordinated lysosomal/sterol pattern on their own.", "The hypothesis asserts a mechanistic model consistent with the observations; causality has not been established by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 shifts the endolysosomal system toward a cargo-loaded state in which export of hydrolysis products (sterol and sphingolipid-derived lipid) from the lumen to the ER/cytosolic pool is the rate-limiting step. Transcripts encoding uptake receptors, acidification machinery and acid hydrolases are coordinately higher in APOE4, yet the ER sterol-regulated program is simultaneously higher, a combination expected when lysosomal lipid is degraded but not delivered to the ER sensing pool; the TFEB/MITF-CLEAR-like transcript increase is therefore inferred to be a compensatory response to the egress limit rather than evidence of increased clearance flux, and the excess carbon is inferred to be diverted into esterification and neutral-lipid storage. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or another lysosomal sterol-export bypass) for 24-48 h should lower the ER sterol-regulated transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS) and the CLEAR-type transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:GAA) toward APOE3 values, while leaving uptake-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:MRC1) comparatively unchanged. If lysosomal free cholesterol is demonstrably normalized yet these sterol and CLEAR transcripts stay elevated, the egress-bottleneck step is refuted in favour of cell-autonomous SREBP/TFEB dysregulation.", "Imaging: filipin or a lysosome-targeted sterol sensor combined with LAMP1 should show a higher fraction of free cholesterol in the LAMP1-positive compartment in APOE4, with a lower ER/plasma-membrane-accessible sterol pool (e.g. D4H probe). Equal or lower lysosomal sterol in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Causal direction of the compensatory arm: TFEB knockdown or degradation in APOE4 should reduce hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and should leave lysosomal lipid load unchanged or worse, and should not rescue cargo clearance. If TFEB loss instead reduces lysosomal lipid accumulation, the CLEAR response is not compensatory and the proposed direction is wrong.", "Flux discrimination between hydrolysis and egress: pulse-chase of fluorescently or isotopically labelled cholesteryl-ester-LDL or myelin should show in APOE4 equal or greater internalization and equal or greater luminal hydrolysis (cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol) but delayed appearance of label in the ER-esterified pool. If hydrolysis itself is slower, or per-lysosome cathepsin B/D, GBA and HEXA activities are reduced by more than about 40% despite the transcript increases, the bottleneck is hydrolase insufficiency and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Downstream test of the storage arm: SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 should increase free-cholesterol stress markers and further raise CLEAR transcripts without normalizing the ER sterol-regulated program; normalization of the sterol program by esterification blockade would contradict step 5.", "Specificity control: if the same coordinated up-shift of lysosomal, sterol and uptake transcripts is reproduced by a technical up-shift control (e.g. matched sequencing-depth or ambient-RNA-corrected reanalysis showing pathway ranks collapse to the list background), the transcript-based support for this mechanism is void."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/debris uptake and opsonin receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA, gene:FCGR1A, gene:STAB1), from which we infer, but did not measure, an equal or greater rate of lipid-rich cargo delivery into the endosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred trafficking): Machinery for endosome maturation and late-endosome/lysosome identity is higher (gene:RAB7A, gene:MON1B, gene:PIK3C3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:SNX3, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:DNM2), so cargo is inferred to reach the degradative compartment; the autophagosome-fusion arm is not coordinately raised (gene:STX17 decreased), indicating the change is selective rather than a uniform up-shift of all vesicular genes.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; inferred, not measured): Export of hydrolysis products out of the lysosomal lumen to the ER-accessible sterol pool is limiting. The discriminating signature is simultaneity: the ER sterol-regulated program is uniformly higher (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:SCP2, gene:INSIG1, gene:MYLIP; 11/11 positive) even though the degradative program is also higher, i.e. the ER behaves as sterol-deficient while the lysosome is inferred to be lipid-loaded. Only gene:NPC2 (+1.17, one of the smallest effects in this group) reports on luminal sterol handoff; NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, ABCA1 and STARD3 were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred regulation): Luminal load is inferred to activate a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR response: gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are up, all eight measured v-ATPase subunits are up (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V0D2), 18/19 measured acid hydrolases are up (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), and lysosomal membrane/solute-export transcripts are up (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLCN7, gene:SPNS1, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC38A7).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred metabolic routing): Because export is limiting, cytosolic lipid is inferred to be routed into esterification and de novo lipogenesis rather than efflux: gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL, gene:FABP5 are up. Lipid droplets, neutral-lipid mass and efflux were not measured.", "Step 6 (associative only): The loaded-lysosome state co-occurs with a primed reactive transcript profile (gene:CD74, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:PYCARD, gene:IL18, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3); no directional link between the lysosomal state and these transcripts is demonstrated here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by post-hydrolytic lipid egress from the endolysosome, not by hydrolase supply: sterol retention drives a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR expansion and ER sterol-starvation signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26720636561680755, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2097406748173521, "cosine_similarity": 0.3515823520030777, "direction_accuracy": 0.23786407766990292, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_023", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6036925566343042, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26720636561680755, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2097406748173521, "cosine_similarity": 0.3515823520030777, "direction_accuracy": 0.23786407766990292, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6036925566343042, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.311472, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 231}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered significant differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, no |effect| \u003c 0.5) with an unspecified logarithm base and a 77% positive sign bias; program coherence is therefore judged against that biased background, and absent genes (e.g. most ISGs, HMGCR, ABCA1, PLIN2, ACLY) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Elevated transcripts for hydrolases, v-ATPase, sterol enzymes and respiratory subunits are treated as indices of programmatic capacity, not as measured hydrolytic activity, lysosomal pH, cholesterol pools, respiration or lipid flux; none of these fluxes were measured here.", "Every protein observation is a 2-D gel spot with 2-6 candidate identities; spots are used only for compatibility, and no spot is read as evidence for a single named protein.", "The sign discordance between nuclear-encoded and mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to be at least partly biological, but internal inconsistency within co-transcribed mtDNA units (gene:MT-ND4 down while gene:MT-ND4L up) means normalisation/ambient effects in 10X Flex data cannot be excluded.", "APOE genotype is assumed to act cell-autonomously enough in this astrocyte co-culture that the microglial transcript differences are not solely secondary to astrocyte-derived lipoprotein differences.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 lipoproteins are poorer lipid/cholesterol acceptors and that TFEB/SREBP coordinate the observed target sets is unverified here (no literature access) and is used only to motivate, not to support, the mechanism."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by interferon or a dominant inflammatory program but by a coordinated re-routing of lipid handling: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake receptors, for an expanded TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase compartment, for sterol/fatty-acid biosynthesis and re-esterification, and for mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are jointly elevated. The simultaneous elevation of uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR), degradation (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB) and de-novo sterol synthesis (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF2) indicates that sterol reaching the ER regulatory pool is not sufficient to switch the biosynthetic program off, so APOE4 microglia run a continuous, carbon- and ATP-expensive acquire/degrade/re-synthesise/re-esterify cycle whose demand is met by the strongest program in the data (39/39 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts up, TCA and gene:MPC2 up). Modest chemokine output (gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL16) is a downstream accompaniment of this lysosomal-lipid state, not an interferon response. This is a cell-state/routing change with sustained biosynthetic demand; the data do not establish an ongoing rate-limiting defect, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test of the sterol-routing step: in mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, measure ER-accessible free cholesterol (e.g. ALOD4/D4H probe) alongside total and esterified cholesterol. The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows equal or higher total/esterified and lysosomal sterol but equal or lower ER-accessible free cholesterol, with SREBP-2 target transcripts still elevated. If APOE4 shows normal or increased ER-accessible cholesterol while HMGCS1/LSS/DHCR24/LDLR remain elevated, the 'sterol fails to satisfy ER demand' step is wrong and the pattern is better read as generic anabolic growth signalling.", "Prospective flux test of the demand-coupling step: Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption in APOE4 in the mock condition, and acute SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or statin-mediated block of sterol synthesis should lower APOE4 oxygen consumption toward APOE3 without abolishing the lysosomal hydrolase program. Equal or lower basal respiration in APOE4 despite 39/39 elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcripts would refute demand-coupling and favour the competing model in which nuclear OXPHOS transcripts are a compensatory response to a mitochondrial capacity defect (consistent with gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB).", "Prospective test of degradative throughput versus failed compensation: DQ-BSA/dextran degradation and cathepsin-activity assays plus lysosomal pH should be equal or higher in APOE4 under mock conditions, with divergence (slower cargo clearance, alkalinised lysosomes, lipid-droplet accumulation) appearing only after myelin or oxLDL loading. Reduced degradation already in the unchallenged mock state would replace 'costly successful routing' with an ongoing lysosomal bottleneck.", "Prospective test rejecting the interferon interpretation: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should not normalise CXCL1/CXCL2/CXCL3/CXCL8/CCL2, whereas blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or sterol re-esterification should modulate them. Loss of APOE4 chemokine elevation under JAK inhibition, or detection of a coherent ISG signature by targeted qPCR, would reinstate interferon signalling as the differentiating mechanism.", "Prospective genetic test of directionality: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript set and, if the causal order proposed here holds, secondarily reduce the TCA/OXPHOS transcript elevation without restoring SREBP-2 targets to APOE3 levels; if TFEB knockdown normalises SREBP-2 targets but leaves OXPHOS transcripts elevated, the mitochondrial program is upstream or independent and the proposed chain must be reordered."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the fraction of extracellular lipid/lipoprotein and debris cargo directed into the endolysosomal system: uptake and opsonic-receptor transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24; measured abundance only, uptake flux not measured).", "The degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded and acidification machinery is co-induced (gene:TFEB +2.38; gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:NPC2 +1.17; gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51), consistent with increased catabolic capacity rather than a transcriptional shutdown of degradation.", "Despite this catabolic capacity, ER sterol sensing is not satisfied: SREBP pathway and its targets remain elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCD +4.17) together with uptake (gene:LDLR) \u2014 a combination expected when liberated sterol is retained/esterified rather than delivered to the ER regulatory pool (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72), and with sterol-turnover/efflux transcripts also raised (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:ABCA7 +2.14).", "Sustained lipid and sterol biosynthesis plus lysosomal acidification create a persistent demand for acetyl-CoA/citrate, NAD(P)H and ATP, which is met by up-regulation of mitochondrial pyruvate import and the TCA cycle (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94) and by uniformly increased nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunits (39/39 represented, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:CYCS +2.58).", "The lysosomal-lipid state, not interferon signalling, accompanies the modest chemokine/NF-kB output seen (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CXCL1 +1.59); this module is no more one-sided than the 77% up-biased selected background and is buffered by co-induced inhibitors (gene:NFKBIZ +3.07, gene:NFKBIB +3.68) with gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05 and gene:CCL4 -1.46, while the type-I interferon core is essentially unrepresented (only gene:IFI27L2, gene:IFI16, gene:TMEM173, gene:IFNAR1) and interferon-candidate protein spots are small/non-significant (protein_spot:008, protein_spot:021, protein_spot:026).", "Prospectively, the cycle's cost predicts reduced spare capacity: mtDNA-encoded transcripts are discordant with the nuclear program (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80 versus gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), so an assembled-complex or respiratory ceiling may only be revealed by lipid loading or an inflammatory challenge; this is an inference about a future challenge, not an observed defect in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-centred lipid-processing state in which sterol liberated from internalised cargo does not satisfy ER sterol demand, sustaining coupled biosynthetic and TCA/OXPHOS transcriptional programs"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25226648057555195, "cosine_similarity": 0.3506060259742911, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027346278317153, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25226648057555195, "cosine_similarity": 0.3506060259742911, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6027346278317153, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1083405, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 56}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_058", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, two concatenated up/down source tables giving 1705 positive vs 507 negative rows); program directionality was judged against that 77% positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2, DEGS1, ASAH1, NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2, SQSTM1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; effects are used on their reported scale and only compared within that scale.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity/state, not activity: no hydrolase activity, cholesterol esterification rate, ER-accessible sterol pool, lipid-droplet content, uptake rate or lysosomal pH was measured here.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (69/92 have five); no spot is uniquely assigned, so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction and never as confirmation of an individual protein. Spot abundances are globally shifted upward (64/92 positive, median +0.485), so single-spot directions carry little weight.", "Elevated SREBP-target transcripts are interpreted as ER sterol sensing not being satisfied; this inference assumes canonical SCAP/INSIG regulation operates in these cells and would be void if SREBP transcripts here are driven by an unmeasured route (e.g. growth or ER-stress signalling; gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51 are present).", "The mechanism describes the measured mock condition. Any reduced clearance reserve is a challenge-revealed property and is NOT claimed as an ongoing degradative defect under mock.", "The assigned sphingolipid focus is retained only as a component: sphingolipid catabolic genes move with the general lysosomal program (non-sphingolipid hydrolases GAA, NAGLU, CTSK, SGSH, MAN2B1 are equally or more elevated), so the data cannot support a sphingolipid-specific primary mechanism.", "Genes within a program are correlated and were chosen by canonical pathway annotation before looking at direction; the descriptive coherence reported is not a formal, independence-based enrichment test."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) occupy a coordinated lipid-handling cell state in which transcripts for scavenger/opsonic cargo receptors, endolysosomal delivery and luminal hydrolases (including glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin hydrolases), and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification are jointly elevated, while SREBP-pathway and LDLR transcripts remain elevated rather than feedback-suppressed. The most parsimonious reading is altered routing of internalized lipid into esterified and lysosomal storage pools that keeps the ER-regulatory sterol pool low, so uptake and sterol biosynthesis run at the same time in a self-reinforcing storage state. This is an inferred routing bias from transcript abundances; no lipid flux, enzyme activity, or lipid pool was measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, primary discriminator: in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, ER/accessible cholesterol (D4H or ALOD4 probe, or ER-cholesterol reporter) should be equal or LOWER in APOE4 while total sterol, cholesteryl-ester (mass spectrometry) and neutral-lipid droplet content are HIGHER. If APOE4 instead shows higher ER-accessible cholesterol together with the elevated SREBP-target transcripts, the sequestration/routing mechanism is falsified.", "PROSPECTIVE perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe or CI-976) should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, redirect sterol to the ER and suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS) and scavenger-receptor transcripts within 24-48 h. Failure to suppress these transcripts in APOE4, or equal suppression in both genotypes, weakens the mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE, distinguishes increased throughput from failed compensation: enzymatic activity assays (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, cathepsin B/D) and cargo-degradation kinetics (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-LDL or labelled myelin) under mock should be equal to or higher in APOE4, matching the elevated transcripts. If activities or degradation rates are LOWER in APOE4 despite higher transcripts, the mechanism should be replaced by compensatory transcription for a lysosomal degradative defect.", "PROSPECTIVE, challenge-only: after myelin, oxLDL or apoptotic-neuron loading, APOE4 microglia should accumulate more cholesteryl ester and lysosomal glycosphingolipid and clear it more slowly than APOE3 - a reserve deficit revealed only by challenge. Equal loading and clearance kinetics would restrict the mechanism to a benign steady-state routing difference.", "PROSPECTIVE, peripheral branch: APOE4 microglia should show reduced migration/process motility consistent with the down-shifted actin/motility transcripts (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:FAM49B, gene:MYO1F, gene:DOCK8, gene:RAC2). Normal motility would not falsify the lipid-routing core but would sever step 6.", "PROSPECTIVE, identity resolution: targeted immunoblot or MS re-identification of the ambiguous cathepsin/v-ATPase spots (protein_spot:052, 053, 055, 057, 058, 067, 069, 064, 065) should show increased mature cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase V1 subunit protein in APOE4; if these proteins are unchanged or reduced while their transcripts are strongly elevated, the transcript-to-capacity assumption in step 2 fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid-cargo and opsonic uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:STAB1 +1.13, gene:MERTK +1.30 with gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:C1QA/B/C ~+1.1-1.25, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:FCGR3A +1.42; 19/19 represented members positive), which we infer increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "STEP 2 (coordinated cell-state change, not a bottleneck): the degradative compartment program is transcriptionally expanded in parallel - CLEAR-type transcription factors (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.32, gene:ATP6V0D2 +1.12), luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:SGSH +1.32), and endosome-to-lysosome traffic (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:AP5M1 +9.80).", "STEP 3 (membrane-lipid catabolic arm, subsumed not autonomous): sphingolipid and glycosphingolipid catabolic capacity moves with this program (gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:GLTP +2.38), consistent with increased membrane-lipid cargo turnover rather than a sphingolipid-specific block; ceramide-handling transcripts are mixed (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:SGPL1 +1.09, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17 versus gene:B4GALT5 -1.88, gene:ST3GAL2 -1.41), and the de novo synthesis arm was not represented in the supplied list.", "STEP 4 (routing to storage): liberated sterol and fatty acid are inferred to be routed preferentially into esterified/stored pools rather than the ER-regulatory pool, based on gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FABP5 +1.13, gene:FABP3 +1.35, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABCA7 +2.14.", "STEP 5 (unsatisfied ER sterol sensing = the discriminating pattern): despite elevated uptake transcripts, the SREBP-2 axis stays on (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.29, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50; 14/14 represented members positive). Simultaneous uptake and synthesis is what a sequestration/routing bias predicts and is not expected if internalized sterol reached the ER regulatory pool.", "STEP 6 (associated downstream state, weaker causal support): the same state carries a low-grade chemokine tone without interferon activation (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CXCL1 +1.59, gene:CXCL2 +1.65, gene:IL18 +1.46, gene:NLRP3 +1.09, gene:PYCARD +2.43, gene:CD14 +1.41, gene:TLR2 +1.20; only gene:CIITA +1.50 of 27 queried interferon genes) and reduced actin/motility transcripts (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.42, gene:SPN -7.31, gene:FAM49B -5.79, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:DOCK8 -2.02, gene:RAC2 -2.00, gene:PLEK -2.54), consistent with a less motile, lipid-laden microglial state."], "title": "Sequestration-biased lipid routing: APOE4 microglia expand uptake, lysosomal catabolic and esterification programs while keeping ER sterol sensing unsatisfied"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1838330317911605, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2783027747273275, "cosine_similarity": 0.3505389910616255, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6005242718446603, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1838330317911605, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2783027747273275, "cosine_similarity": 0.3505389910616255, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6005242718446603, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.314191, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 57}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_096", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are made against the internal background of this list (median effect +1.46, 77% positive) rather than against all genes.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are therefore not quantitatively comparable to the log2 protein-spot effects.", "Transcript abundance changes are taken as a proxy for protein and enzymatic capacity for SCARB1, SCD, SOAT1/DGAT1 and the lysosomal hydrolases; no protein or activity measurement of these enzymes is supplied.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots containing CTSB/CTSD/HEXB (protein_spot:053, :058, :067) are treated as ambiguous and non-decisive.", "No lipid, lipidomic, filipin/droplet-imaging, flux or localization measurement is supplied, so cholesteryl-ester and droplet accumulation, lysosomal sterol load and ER-accessible sterol are predicted quantities, not observations.", "Egress-arm genes NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied list; their behaviour is unknown and the inferred egress limitation rests on that gap.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect genotype effects transmitted through astrocyte-derived lipoproteins rather than microglia-autonomous regulation.", "Correlation between APOE genotype and these abundances is observational; causality has not been established by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3), the differentiating program is lipid-handling, not interferon/NF-kB signaling: strongly elevated lipoprotein-lipid uptake (SCARB1) together with an expanded lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program (GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, ATP6V1A/1H/0C, with TFEB and MITF up) generates more luminal free cholesterol, sphingoid bases and fatty acids than the cells can export from the endolysosome; the surplus is inferred to be re-esterified through an SREBF1/SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA pool (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, ACAT2 up) and stored as cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplets, while the ER sterol-sensor pool stays functionally unsatisfied (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, INSIG1, LDLR still up). All flux, localization and causal steps are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation A (bypass of the bottleneck): treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or with 25-hydroxycholesterol which reaches the ER sensor without lysosomal egress, should suppress DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, INSIG1 and LDLR and lower lysosomal sterol staining substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes, or no reduction in APOE4 lysosomal sterol, weakens the egress-bottleneck step.", "Discriminating perturbation B (storage arm): pharmacological SCD inhibition, or SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition, should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area and the cholesteryl-ester : free-cholesterol ratio in APOE4 toward APOE3 values without reducing SCARB1, GAA or GBA transcripts. If droplet load and CE ratio are unchanged, the SCD/esterification diversion step is wrong.", "Upstream test: SCARB1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower droplet and lysosomal lipid load and blunt the elevation of the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts; persistence of both after knockdown would indicate an uptake-independent lysosomal program.", "Direct measurement test: quantitative lipidomics or droplet imaging of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher cholesteryl ester and monounsaturated triacylglycerol species and a lower ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/PFO probe) in APOE4. Equal or lower neutral-lipid content in APOE4 falsifies the central claim.", "Specificity test against the rejected inflammatory alternative: JAK inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IKK/NF-kB inhibition should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid-droplet and lysosomal-gene differences essentially intact. Normalisation of the lipid phenotype by these inhibitors would support an inflammatory/interferon-driven mechanism instead and falsify this hypothesis.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot or targeted proteomics should show higher SCARB1, GBA, GAA and SCD protein in APOE4; unchanged protein for these while transcripts remain elevated would break the abundance-to-capacity assumption."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show a large increase in the selective lipoprotein-lipid receptor transcript SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22, top 1% of the supplied list) with smaller increases in CD36, LDLR and APOE itself; we infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesteryl ester and fatty acid to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred capacity): A coordinated CLEAR-type program is elevated above the global up-shift of the list - TFEB and MITF plus hydrolases GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK and v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C, ATP6V0D1 (lysosomal set median 2.38 vs 1.46 background, Mann-Whitney p=0.011). We infer expanded luminal acidification and hydrolysis, i.e. more liberated free cholesterol, ceramide/sphingosine and free fatty acid inside lysosomes.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): Export of the liberated sterol and sphingolipid from the lysosomal lumen to the ER/plasma-membrane pools is the rate-limiting step. Only NPC2 (+1.17, near list median) is measured on this arm; NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured, so the egress deficit is inferred from the mismatch between influx/hydrolase capacity and the modest egress-arm signal, not observed.", "Step 4 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): SREBF1 (+4.67) and SCD (+4.17, padj 1.9e-165) raise the monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply, and DGAT1, SOAT1 and ACAT2 are up, so surplus sterol and fatty acid are inferred to be re-esterified into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and sequestered in cytoplasmic lipid droplets rather than exported.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): Sequestration keeps the ER-accessible sterol pool low, so distal sterol-pathway and SREBP-target transcripts (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, INSIG1, LDLR) remain elevated despite an overall lipid surfeit - a futile uptake-store cycle rather than feedback shutdown.", "Step 6 (qualitative shift, not global loss): Lysosomal composition is remodelled rather than uniformly increased; CTSS is one of the most decreased transcripts in the list (-5.57), predicting altered substrate selectivity of the degradative compartment alongside the expanded bulk hydrolase program.", "Step 7 (explicit rejection of the assigned focus): Canonical interferon signaling is essentially unrepresented (only IRF8 +1.39 and TMEM173 +1.22 of 64 queried ISGs are present in the supplied list) and an NF-kB/inflammatory set is not enriched over the global up-shift (median 1.62 vs 1.46, p=0.98) with several members down (TNFAIP3, RELB, CCL4), so inflammatory or interferon signaling is not proposed as the differentiating mechanism."], "title": "Endolysosomal sterol/sphingolipid egress, not inflammatory signaling, is the APOE4 bottleneck: uptake and CLEAR-type catabolic capacity outrun export and are diverted into SCD-dependent neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23837831850238156, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22143705828318397, "cosine_similarity": 0.3503598046451267, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6154045307443365, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23837831850238156, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22143705828318397, "cosine_similarity": 0.3503598046451267, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6154045307443365, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.750957, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 232}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_024", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are differential-expression results selected by threshold (all 2212 rows have |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, G6PD, CS, PDHA1, CPT1A) means no supplied measurement, not absence of change.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified, so all RNA statements are treated as directions and ranks within this dataset, never as absolute fold-changes.", "The dataset has a strong global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46), so only rank-based comparisons against that background (and genes moving down against it) are treated as informative; the shift itself may be technical (normalisation, ambient RNA, capture efficiency).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding enzyme or carrier; enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, allosteric regulation, metabolite pools and flux were not measured.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified, so no spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; genotype effects could partly reflect shifts in microglial state proportions or astrocyte-derived signals rather than cell-intrinsic rewiring.", "Causal direction from APOE4 genotype to the metabolic transcript state is assumed only as a hypothesis; the data are a cross-genotype association at one timepoint (day 30, mock)."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional state in which the committed upper-glycolytic isoenzymes (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2) and oxidative pentose-phosphate enzymes (TALDO1, PGD) are among the few strongly down-shifted genes against a globally up-shifted background, while glucose transporters, glycogen synthesis, mitochondrial pyruvate import/PDH activation, TCA-cycle and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts are coordinately raised. We hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck is glycolytic flux capacity at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase, so that APOE4 microglia become dependent on mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate and anaplerotic amino-acid carbon and export surplus citrate toward lipogenic storage, leaving little glycolytic reserve. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and localisation are inferred and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Extracellular-flux assay: APOE4 microglia should show lower 2-deoxyglucose-sensitive glycolytic capacity and reserve (ECAR after oligomycin, and after an acute LPS or ATP challenge) with equal or higher basal oxygen-consumption-to-ECAR ratio than isogenic APOE3. If APOE4 shows equal or greater glycolytic reserve, the proposed upper-glycolytic bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating tracer test: with uniformly labelled 13C-glucose, APOE4 cells should show reduced fractional labelling of lactate and of pentose-phosphate-derived ribose-5-phosphate/sedoheptulose-7-phosphate, increased label retention in glycogen, and preserved or increased m+2 labelling of citrate/malate; with 13C-glutamine the APOE4 contribution to TCA intermediates should rise. Reduced glucose labelling of citrate together with unchanged lactate labelling would refute the routing step.", "Substrate-dependence perturbation: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or PDH inactivation should reduce ATP/NAD(P)H and viability, and lower BODIPY-positive lipid-droplet area, more in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose should be better tolerated by APOE4. No genotype difference in UK5099 sensitivity would weaken step 3 and step 5.", "Rescue test: restoring HK2 and PFKP expression (or bypassing the step with a cell-permeable fructose-1,6-bisphosphate donor) in APOE4 microglia should restore the stimulus-induced ECAR burst without abolishing the raised TCA/OXPHOS transcript program; failure to restore the burst would indicate the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g. at unmeasured HK1 or in ETC assembly).", "Capacity-versus-compensation test: blue-native PAGE/complex-activity assays and maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) respiration should be measured. If nuclear OXPHOS transcript elevation is not accompanied by increased assembled complex I/IV and maximal respiration, the mechanism must be reframed as compensatory transcription against an mtDNA-encoded shortfall rather than genuinely increased oxidative capacity.", "Specificity control: the down-shift of HK2/PFKP/PGD/TALDO1 should be reproducible by qPCR/protein immunoblot in independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 lines; if immunoblots show unchanged or increased HK and PFK protein, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 lowers transcripts of the committed, effectively irreversible upper-glycolytic isoenzymes HK2 (-3.67, 4th percentile of all reported effects) and PFKP (-3.08, 6th percentile) and of the allosteric activator-producing PFKFB2 (-1.10), while glucose-transporter transcripts SLC2A1/SLC2A3 and downstream reversible enzymes GPI, PFKM, ENO1 are raised; inferred consequence is that glucose entry is preserved but flux through the committed steps, not uptake, becomes limiting.", "Step 2 (inferred routing): hexose-phosphate carbon that cannot pass the committed step is diverted to glycogen (GYS1 +6.10, 97th percentile; UGP2 +1.86) and away from the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (PGD -1.30, TALDO1 -2.32), predicting reduced glucose-derived NADPH and ribose rather than reduced glucose consumption.", "Step 3 (inferred mitochondrial pyruvate entry): the pyruvate that is produced is preferentially imported and decarboxylated, indicated by MPC2 (+7.98, 99th percentile) and the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1 (+3.00); this is a transcript-level inference about carrier and phosphatase capacity, not a measured PDH phosphorylation state or pyruvate flux.", "Step 4 (measured coherence): a coordinated nuclear-encoded oxidative program is raised well above the global up-shift (40 nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts, median +2.64, all positive, Mann-Whitney p=3.2e-05; TCA/anaplerotic set median +4.74, p=2.0e-04, including OGDH +8.56, MDH1 +8.72, ACO2 +3.54, IDH3G +3.94, GOT1 +6.43, GLUD1 +3.17, SLC25A11 +4.50), consistent with increased capacity for mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate plus glutamate/aspartate-derived carbon.", "Step 5 (inferred carbon overflow): surplus mitochondrial carbon is inferred to exit as citrate through the raised carrier SLC25A1 (+4.47) into a raised lipogenic/lipid-esterification program (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, ACSS2 +2.93, ACAT2 +2.04, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25), providing a metabolic route to the lipid-laden APOE4 microglial phenotype.", "Step 6 (functional consequence): with the committed glycolytic steps capacity-limited and carbon committed to oxidation and storage, APOE4 microglia are predicted to have low glycolytic reserve and to depend on mitochondrial substrate oxidation; because mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts move opposite to the nuclear ones (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; nuclear vs mtDNA contrast p=1.1e-03) this dependency may be served by an incompletely matched electron-transport chain, consistent with the raised stress transcript DDIT3 (+2.79)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are constrained at the committed upper-glycolytic step and route glucose carbon into glycogen and mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation with citrate export to lipid synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07142857142857142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23160150744216318, "cosine_similarity": 0.35029254896661455, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073948220064725, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07142857142857142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23160150744216318, "cosine_similarity": 0.35029254896661455, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6073948220064725, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7332755, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 233}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_046", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); enrichment statements are made relative to this biased within-list background, and absence of a gene means 'no differential evidence', not 'unchanged' or 'decreased'.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is preserved; only signs and rank/relative magnitudes are used, no absolute fold-change is claimed.", "Higher hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript abundance is assumed to translate into a larger acidic degradative compartment; enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux and lipid pools were not measured in this dataset.", "Sterol egress and efflux genes (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1) are assumed not to be induced in APOE4; this rests on their absence from the differential list and must be verified directly.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; spots containing CTSB/CTSD/GNS are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, and their mixed signs are compatible with different processed forms or with a different protein dominating the spot.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture and the RNA comparison is attributed to microglia; any cross-contamination of the pseudobulk signal, and the unreported number of biological replicates, could inflate effect sizes.", "No causal direction is established by these data; TFEB-driven lysosomal induction may equally be a compensatory response to, rather than a cause of, lipid retention."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling, not in interferon signalling: transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD), v-ATPase subunits and TFEB are strongly higher, and lipoprotein/debris receptors are higher, whereas no canonical interferon-stimulated gene appears anywhere in the 2212-row differential list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is the export of hydrolysed lipid (in particular sterol) out of the endolysosome, which is not scaled with the induced uptake and hydrolysis program; the resulting shortfall of ER-accessible cholesterol keeps the SREBP program (SREBF2, SREBF1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, SCD, INSIG1) switched on, and the lipid that does reach the ER is esterified/stored (SOAT1, DGAT1), producing a lipid-laden, lysosome-stressed microglial state with only modest chemokine changes.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with labelled LDL or myelin and then treating with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which bypasses NPC1-dependent lysosomal sterol egress) should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, reduce filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol, reduce neutral-lipid droplets and lower SREBP2 target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1). If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal sterol but leaves SREBP2 targets and droplets unchanged, the egress-bottleneck step is wrong.", "APOE4 microglia should show higher filipin/lysosomal cholesterol and higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio at baseline while an ER-accessible-cholesterol reporter (e.g. GRAM1A/ALOD4-type probe) reads lower than in APOE3; equal lysosomal sterol with equal ER-accessible sterol would falsify steps 3-4.", "SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol and shrink droplets without normalising SREBP2 target transcripts; normalisation of SREBP2 targets by SOAT1 inhibition alone would favour an esterification-driven rather than egress-driven sensing defect.", "TFEB knockdown should worsen, not relieve, lysosomal lipid accumulation and hydrolase-substrate build-up in APOE4 if the hydrolase program is compensatory; if TFEB knockdown reduces lysosomal lipid load, step 2 must be reframed as driver rather than compensation.", "Interferon negative control: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade under mock conditions should leave the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid and lysosomal phenotype essentially unchanged, and an ISG panel (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, STAT1) should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference. Detection of a clear baseline ISG elevation, or normalisation of the lipid phenotype by JAK inhibition, would overturn the rejection of the interferon mechanism.", "Unambiguous protein-level test: immunoblot or targeted MS (not 2D spots) should show increased mature cathepsin B/D, GBA and HEXA protein and increased LAMP1-positive compartment area in APOE4; unchanged hydrolase protein despite the large transcript differences would break the RNA-to-capacity link in step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript abundance of lipoprotein/scavenger and phagocytic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:ABCA7). We infer, but have not measured, an increased flux of lipoprotein and membrane-lipid cargo into the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A coordinate TFEB-type lysosomal program is higher (gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2) together with acidification and maturation genes (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R). This is transcript abundance; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and cargo clearance were not measured.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck, inferred): The sterol-egress/efflux arm is not co-induced - NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN and STARD4 are absent from the differential list, i.e. there is no evidence that egress capacity scales with steps 1-2 (absence in a selected list is not evidence of down-regulation). We propose that transfer of liberated cholesterol and sphingolipid out of the limiting membrane, rather than hydrolysis, is rate-limiting in APOE4, so lipid is retained in the endolysosome.", "Step 4 (inferred sensing, measured RNA output): Retention lowers the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (not measured). The SREBP module therefore stays on despite a high total lipid load: gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SCD and gene:INSIG1 are all higher in APOE4 (12/12 sterol-synthesis genes present in the list are positive), creating a futile uptake-plus-synthesis cycle.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred storage): Lipid that does reach the ER is channelled into esterified storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL, gene:FADS1, gene:ACOX1 higher), predicting cytoplasmic lipid-droplet and cholesteryl-ester accumulation in APOE4; droplets themselves were not measured here.", "Step 6 (interferon arm rejected): No canonical type I/II interferon-stimulated gene (ISG15, IFIT/MX/OAS family, STAT1/2, IRF7/9, B2M, HLA class I, TAP1, PSMB8/9, GBP1/2, CXCL9/10) appears among the 2212 differential rows, so the APOE4 state is not explained by tonic interferon signalling; the modest chemokine changes (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL1/2/3, gene:CXCL16) are interpreted as a downstream consequence of lipid/lysosomal stress rather than an interferon-driven program."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program while sterol-egress and efflux genes are not co-induced, driving lysosomal lipid retention, futile SREBP-driven synthesis and neutral-lipid storage rather than an interferon response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21478020307248166, "cosine_similarity": 0.35019958210200863, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041035598705502, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21478020307248166, "cosine_similarity": 0.35019958210200863, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6041035598705502, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.747625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 234}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 in an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 2212 genes, 77.1% positive). Genes absent from the list (e.g. MPC1, PDHA1, PDHB, LDHA, LDHB, CS, ACLY, CPT1A, G6PD, TKT, PPARGC1A, TFAM) are unknown, not unchanged. Only sign and rank of effects are interpreted; the log base is preserved and not converted.", "Program membership was fixed a priori from canonical pathway lists written before looking at effects; both agreeing and disagreeing members are reported, and each program is compared against the 77.1% positive background of this selected list, not against 50/50.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding carrier/enzyme protein. No pyruvate, acetyl-CoA, NADPH, lactate or ATP pool was measured, and no respiration or isotope flux was measured; all routing, flux, activity and localization statements are inferred.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (82/92 have \u003e= 4 candidate identities, dominated by keratin/actin); no spot uniquely reports an OXPHOS, TCA or MPC protein, so the proteome can neither confirm nor refute the mitochondrial arm. All candidate identities are retained.", "The global positive skew of the list could partly reflect single-cell (10X Flex) library-size/mitochondrial-fraction normalization; the mtDNA-encoded decreases in particular could be compositional rather than biological. Replicate number is not supplied, so effect precision cannot be judged.", "The proposed reduced glycolytic/PPP surge reserve is a property predicted for a future challenge; it is not claimed to be an ongoing functional defect in the measured mock condition.", "Causality is not established: APOE4 genotype is the only manipulation, and the ordering lysosomal/lipid load -\u003e oxidative routing is a hypothesis, not a demonstrated sequence."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzymatic lesion but by a coordinated cell-state change: an expanded lysosomal/scavenging/lipid-handling transcript program is accompanied by uniformly increased transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD), TCA enzymes and mitochondrial carriers, amino-acid anaplerosis, and all 38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits, while the inducible cytosolic glycolytic and pentose-phosphate branch (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NAMPT) contracts. We propose that APOE4 microglia are transcriptionally configured for higher mitochondrial oxidative throughput of pyruvate and amino-acid carbon (an adaptation to degradative/lipid load) at the cost of glycolytic and NADPH surge reserve; the reserve deficit is predicted to appear only under a future acute challenge, and no respiratory or labelling flux was measured here, so throughput and any mito-nuclear assembly mismatch remain inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE flux test: in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, extracellular flux analysis plus U-13C-glucose tracing should show equal-or-higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption, a higher fraction of citrate/glutamate m+2 derived from glucose, and equal-or-lower lactate labelling/ECAR. If APOE4 instead shows lower basal OCR and lower m+2 labelling despite the uniform nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase, the 'increased oxidative routing' mechanism is wrong and the mito-nuclear failed-compensation alternative is favoured.", "PROSPECTIVE dependency test: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or PDH inhibition should reduce OCR and ATP-linked respiration significantly more in APOE4 than APOE3, and force a larger compensatory lactate rise. Equal sensitivity in the two genotypes would show the gene:MPC2/gene:PDP1/gene:DLD increases are not functional and would weaken step 2.", "PROSPECTIVE reserve test (challenge-revealed, not claimed for mock): after an acute oxidative or phagocytic burst (myelin/pHrodo bead load, or menadione), APOE4 microglia should show slower GSH/GSSG recovery and a smaller PPP flux increase (1-13C versus 6-13C glucose) than APOE3, with no difference at baseline. Equal PPP induction and equal redox recovery would falsify the 'reduced NADPH surge reserve' cost in step 5.", "PROSPECTIVE discriminating measurement of the main alternative: quantify mtDNA-encoded proteins (MT-CO1, MT-ND1) and mtDNA copy number relative to nuclear-encoded subunits (NDUFS7, ATP5F1B) with BN-PAGE in-gel complex I/IV activity. Stoichiometric assembly with preserved activity supports the adaptive-routing mechanism; a selective loss of mtDNA-encoded subunits with reduced complex I/IV activity would replace it with mito-nuclear imbalance / failed compensation.", "PROSPECTIVE upstream test: reducing the degradative/lipid load (TREM2 blockade, or removing lipid/apoptotic substrate from the co-culture) should blunt the APOE4-specific increases in gene:MPC2, TCA and nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. If these mitochondrial transcript increases persist unchanged when load is removed, the causal ordering in step 1 is wrong even if the metabolic state description survives."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts, inferred load): APOE4 microglia show a broad increase in lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB-axis transcripts (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:GAA +9.98, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB +2.38) together with scavenging/phagocytic and lipid-handling transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:APOE), consistent with a higher steady-state membrane/lipid substrate processing load. Load itself is inferred, not measured.", "STEP 2 (routing): Transcripts controlling entry of pyruvate carbon into mitochondria rise coherently - gene:MPC2 (+7.98, mitochondrial pyruvate carrier), gene:PDP1 (+3.00, PDH-activating phosphatase), gene:DLD (+5.54, shared E3 of PDH/OGDH) - with no represented PDK. We infer increased capacity for pyruvate import and oxidative decarboxylation rather than cytosolic retention.", "STEP 3 (oxidative core): TCA and carrier transcripts increase uniformly (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB, gene:ME1, gene:PCK2; gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77), and 38/38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are positive (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:CYCS), expanding transcript-level electron-transport and ATP-synthase capacity.", "STEP 4 (anaplerosis): Amino-acid entry into the same cycle is reinforced (gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:BCAT2 +6.42, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS, gene:BCAT1, gene:ABAT, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45, gene:SLC38A7 +7.53), so TCA carbon is supplied from glutamate/BCAA as well as pyruvate; this makes the state robust to glycolytic contraction.", "STEP 5 (cost): Despite higher glucose-uptake transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:PFKM, gene:ENO1, gene:SLC16A1), the inducible/high-flux glycolytic isoforms and the oxidative PPP contract (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10, gene:TIGAR +1.14, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NAMPT -2.62). We infer glucose carbon is routed through glycolysis into mitochondria rather than accumulating in a lactate/PPP-biased inflammatory configuration, with partial NADPH re-sourcing via gene:ME1, gene:NNT (+2.88) and peroxiredoxins (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4).", "STEP 6 (state-level consequence, condition-specific): In the measured mock condition this predicts equal or higher basal oxidative ATP production in APOE4 with greater dependence on MPC/PDH and amino-acid anaplerosis; the predicted deficit is a reduced glycolytic and PPP surge reserve that would only become limiting under a future acute inflammatory, phagocytic or oxidant challenge. Whether the uniform nuclear OXPHOS increase is matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunits is unresolved (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33 versus gene:MT-ND4L +1.95, gene:MT-ND5 +1.93)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-loaded, oxidative-catabolic state that routes carbon into mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA/OXPHOS while contracting the inducible glycolytic-PPP branch"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2372244581471772, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26767624742535534, "cosine_similarity": 0.3488040388276063, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6286310679611651, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2372244581471772, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26767624742535534, "cosine_similarity": 0.3488040388276063, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6286310679611651, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.14194425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 58}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a directional differential-expression statistic in an unspecified logarithm base; because every |effect| is \u003e= 1.00009 (n=2212, minimum 1.00009), a magnitude filter (or a signed fold-change convention) is likely, so only signs and within-block ranks were used and magnitudes were never converted or exponentiated.", "The RNA rows are a curated selection of significant differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; genes absent from the file (e.g. TFAM, POLRMT, PPARGC1A, ATF4, G6PD, most mitoribosome genes) are missing data, not evidence of no change.", "The workbook contains at least three distinct list blocks (source rows 2-509 column 1 and column 2, both signed; source rows 510-1709 column 1, all positive with minimum +1.00); enrichment was judged within block, and positivity inside the all-positive block carries no directional information.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript estimates from probe-based 10X Flex single-cell data reflect genuine mitochondrial transcript abundance rather than compositional normalisation, ambient RNA or probe-coverage artefact; this assumption is unverified and is the main threat to the mitonuclear arm.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot was used as evidence for any mitochondrial protein pool, and no mitochondrial protein abundance is claimed as observed.", "Assembly state, respiratory flux, mitochondrial mass, mtDNA copy number, membrane potential, lysosomal acidification and lipid-droplet content were not measured in this dataset; all statements about them are predictions.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous, and biological replicate number was not supplied, so the reported p-values cannot be independently re-derived."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (OXPHOS structural subunits, TCA enzymes, inner-membrane carriers, import machinery) while the sign-informative mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS transcripts (MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ATP6, MT-ND4) are decreased; we hypothesise that this mismatch, not a deficit of nuclear subunit expression, is the primary bottleneck, so that holo-complex III/IV/V assembly and oxidative flux per unit mitochondrial mass fail to rise in proportion to the transcriptional expansion, and the accompanying TFEB/lysosomal-hydrolase and lipid-handling transcript increases represent a compensatory degradative/retrograde arm rather than an inflammatory activation. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; assembly, flux and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, absolute quantification (RT-qPCR of MT-CO2/MT-CYB/MT-ATP6 normalised to mtDNA copy number with spike-in controls) plus blue-native PAGE will show reduced mtDNA-encoded transcript per mtDNA copy and unchanged-or-reduced assembled complex IV/V holoenzyme together with increased free or sub-assembled nuclear-encoded subunits (e.g. NDUFA9, ATP5F1B) in APOE4; if mtDNA-encoded transcripts per mtDNA copy are unchanged and assembled holo-complexes rise in proportion to the nuclear transcript increase, the mitonuclear-imbalance bottleneck is falsified.", "Seahorse respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 signal or mtDNA copy) will show equal or lower FCCP-stimulated maximal oxygen consumption and reduced spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 despite higher OXPHOS transcripts; a proportional increase in mass-normalised maximal respiration would weaken the mechanism.", "Restoring mtDNA expression (TFAM or POLRMT overexpression, or mitoribosome-supporting intervention) will increase assembled complex IV/V and mass-normalised maximal respiration more in APOE4 than APOE3 and will blunt the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial and TFEB/hydrolase transcript elevation; equal or absent genotype-selective rescue weakens the mechanism.", "Low-dose mitochondrial-translation inhibition (doxycycline or chloramphenicol) will sensitise APOE4 microglia, producing a leftward shift in the dose at which maximal respiration and ATP-linked OCR collapse relative to APOE3; equal or greater resistance in APOE4 would argue against an already assembly-limited chain.", "Causal-direction test between the two arms: blocking lysosomal acidification or lipid uptake (bafilomycin A1, or SCARB1/LDLR knockdown) will not normalise the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcript elevation, whereas the alternative lysosomal-lipid-overload-primary model predicts that it will; normalisation of the mitochondrial arm by lysosomal blockade would favour that alternative over this hypothesis.", "If the mitonuclear signal is a normalisation artefact, then re-analysis with cell-number-matched spike-ins or an orthogonal assay (single-molecule FISH for MT-CO2 per cell) will show unchanged mtDNA-encoded transcript density in APOE4; that result would falsify step 2 and hence the stated bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts are coordinately higher in APOE4 than APOE3 (76 of 80 matched genes positive; median effect +2.76 vs global +1.46; within-workbook-block Mann-Whitney p=0.005/0.030/0.006), including complex I subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7), TCA/shuttle enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2), carriers (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A46, gene:SLC25A11) and import components (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44).", "Measured: in the two workbook blocks that contain both signs, all four mtDNA-encoded transcripts are decreased (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2); the two positive mtDNA entries lie in an all-positive filtered block and are therefore directionally uninformative.", "Inferred (not measured): the ratio of mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits to imported nuclear-encoded subunits falls, so newly imported subunits accumulate as unassembled or partially assembled intermediates and holo-complex III/IV/V assembly becomes the rate-limiting step for electron transport.", "Inferred (not measured): assembly-limited respiration lowers spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass despite elevated biogenesis transcripts, generating retrograde mitochondrial stress signalling (a proteostatic/integrated-stress-type response) that further drives nuclear mitochondrial-biogenesis transcription - a feed-forward loop that explains the magnitude of the nuclear arm.", "Measured, interpreted as the compensatory degradative arm: a coherent lysosomal/CLEAR transcript increase (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A) enriched above block background (p=8.3e-05 and 0.027 in the two sign-informative blocks), consistent with increased autophagic/mitophagic and substrate-processing demand.", "Measured, secondary: lipid and lipoprotein-handling transcripts are also raised (gene:SCARB1, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE), providing oxidisable substrate and cargo that would further load an assembly-limited respiratory chain, while inflammatory/interferon transcripts show no coherent shift (combined p=0.98), arguing against a cytokine-driven state change."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance makes respiratory-chain assembly, not nuclear subunit supply, the limiting step in mock-treated APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14243252224642763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18224636366660582, "cosine_similarity": 0.3486334296405268, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6045404530744336, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14243252224642763, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18224636366660582, "cosine_similarity": 0.3486334296405268, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6045404530744336, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.25351925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 235}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_084", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of ACLY, FASN, ACACA, PDHA1, MPC1, CS, MDH2, GOT2, PKM, GAPDH and LDHA/LDHB means the pathway is reconstructed from a biased subset and gaps are inferred, not observed.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; comparisons are therefore made as within-dataset percentile ranks rather than as absolute fold changes.", "Both modalities carry a strong global positive offset (RNA median +1.46, 77% positive; protein spots median +0.48, 70% positive), so we assume that only the relative position of a gene within the dataset, not the raw sign, is informative about direction.", "We assume steady-state transcript abundance is a partial proxy for enzyme and carrier protein amount, and that protein amount is a partial proxy for capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, isotope flux, membrane potential or subcellular localisation was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a measurement of a named enzyme.", "We assume the APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison is isogenic as stated and that the astrocyte co-culture contributes comparably to both genotypes; cell-composition or maturation differences are not excluded by these data.", "Causality is not established by any observation here; the genotype-to-flux direction is a hypothesis."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in how carbon is routed rather than in how much glucose they burn: transcripts for committed upper-glycolysis steps (HK2, PFKP) are among the most negative in the dataset while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), the TCA segment feeding citrate/2-oxoglutarate (ACO2, IDH3G, OGDH, DLD), the citrate and oxoglutarate-malate carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and the cytosolic shuttle arm (MDH1, GOT1) are among the most positive. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node is mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1) operating in a cytosolic citrate-malate-pyruvate shuttle supported by MDH1/GOT1, which converts oxidatively generated citrate into cytosolic acetyl-CoA and reducing equivalents for SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1-directed lipid esterification, so that TCA cycling in APOE4 serves biosynthesis rather than increased ATP-coupled respiration. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux; none of the fluxes, metabolite pools, or causal directions were measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute inhibition of the citrate carrier (CTPI-2 or SLC25A1 knockdown) in mock APOE4 microglia should lower neutral-lipid droplet content, SCD/DGAT1-dependent triacylglycerol and cytosolic acetyl-CoA-dependent histone acetylation substantially more than in isogenic APOE3, i.e. a genotype x drug interaction. If SLC25A1 inhibition reduces droplets equally in both genotypes, or leaves the APOE4 excess intact, the citrate-export bottleneck is wrong and an uptake/lysosomal-catabolism bottleneck (also supported here by high GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB and SCARB1) is favoured instead.", "Stable-isotope tracing with U-13C6-glucose and U-13C5-glutamine should show, in APOE4 relative to APOE3, a lower fraction of glucose carbon appearing in lactate, unchanged-or-higher M+2 labelling of citrate, and higher 13C incorporation into palmitate/cholesteryl esters, with a larger glutamine contribution to 2-oxoglutarate. Equal or higher lactate labelling in APOE4 would weaken step 1.", "Respirometry should show APOE4 basal oxygen consumption that is disproportionately sensitive to MPC inhibition (UK5099) but no increase, or a decrease, in maximal/ATP-linked respiration and spare capacity relative to APOE3, matching the lower mitochondrially encoded OXPHOS transcripts. A clear increase in APOE4 maximal respiration and spare capacity would falsify the 'biosynthetic not bioenergetic' framing in step 7.", "Targeted protein and activity measurement (immunoblot or targeted MS, not 2-D spots) should confirm higher MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1 and GOT1 protein and higher cytosolic MDH/GOT activity in APOE4, and lower HK2/PFKP protein with equal or lower hexokinase activity. If MPC2, SLC25A1 and MDH1 protein and activity are unchanged despite the transcript differences, the mechanism is weakened to a transcription-only difference with no flux consequence.", "The mechanism predicts rescue directionality: raising cytosolic acetyl-CoA disposal capacity should not rescue, but blocking the sink should. DGAT1 inhibition should trap the rerouted carbon as free fatty acid/acyl-CoA and increase lipotoxic stress markers in APOE4 more than APOE3, whereas MPC or SLC25A1 inhibition should prevent both droplet accumulation and that stress. Absence of any genotype-dependent difference in these interventions would weaken the whole chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia lower the transcripts for the two committed upper-glycolysis isoenzymes normally induced in activated myeloid cells (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, both in the bottom ~5% of this differential-expression list), which we infer caps glucose-6-phosphate/fructose-1,6-bisphosphate generation and therefore limits cytosolic pyruvate-to-lactate overflow.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred transport activity): Transcripts for the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier subunit MPC2 and for the pyruvate/2-oxoacid dehydrogenase E3 component DLD, together with the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1, are strongly higher, which we infer increases the fraction of available pyruvate that is imported and decarboxylated rather than reduced to lactate. MPC1, PDHA1 and LDHA/LDHB were not measured, so the carrier and dehydrogenase complexes themselves are only partially observed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): The citrate-generating and 2-oxoglutarate-generating TCA segment (gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB) plus glutamate entry (gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2) is coordinately higher, consistent with anaplerotic filling of the cycle from glutamine/amino-acid carbon that compensates for the capped glycolytic input.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred transport): Citrate leaves the matrix through the citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1, +4.47) in exchange for malate re-imported by the oxoglutarate-malate carrier (gene:SLC25A11, +4.50); we propose this exchange, not oxidation per se, is the rate-limiting step that determines how much mitochondrial carbon reaches the cytosol in APOE4.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred cytosolic redox cycle): The cytosolic limb of that shuttle - MDH1 (+8.72, ~99th percentile of this list) and GOT1 (+6.43) with ME1 - is expanded, which we infer regenerates cytosolic oxaloacetate/malate and NADPH; combined with ACSS2 this would raise the cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH available for lipid synthesis. ACLY, FASN and ACACA were not measured and are inferred, not observed.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred phenotype): Downstream lipogenic/esterification transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) and the lipoprotein scavenger receptor gene:SCARB1 are higher, providing the sink that we hypothesise converts the exported citrate carbon into stored neutral lipid, giving the APOE4 lipid phenotype without a general increase in respiratory chain output.", "Step 7 (measured RNA, constraint on the model): All four mitochondrially encoded OXPHOS transcripts that decreased (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2) argue against the simpler alternative that APOE4 merely has more respiration; the mechanism therefore predicts biosynthetic, not ATP-maximising, use of the cycle."], "title": "APOE4 microglia rewire carbon at the mitochondrial pyruvate-citrate node: capped upper glycolysis with expanded citrate export and cytosolic MDH1/GOT1 shuttling toward lipogenic acetyl-CoA"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06555772994129158, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25105268291909505, "cosine_similarity": 0.3485573267168335, "direction_accuracy": 0.11003236245954692, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6144983818770227, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06555772994129158, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25105268291909505, "cosine_similarity": 0.3485573267168335, "direction_accuracy": 0.11003236245954692, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6144983818770227, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5955425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 236}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_102", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive skew (77.1% positive, mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base); set-level enrichment was therefore judged only by permutation against this same list, and absence of a gene (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, MVK, IDI1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA) means it was not in the selected list, not that it was measured and unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partially predictive of the corresponding lysosomal enzyme protein level and of compartment capacity; the data contain no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, compartment volume, localisation or lipid measurement.", "Protein spots are treated as ambiguous multi-candidate features, not identified proteins; no spot is used to assert the abundance of a named protein.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype rather than background or treatment is assumed to be the differing variable; biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be assessed.", "The mitochondrial and lysosomal transcript modules are assumed to reflect the same cell population rather than a shift in microglial subtype composition or in the astrocyte co-culture fraction; composition was not measured.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: the direction TFEB/MITF -\u003e hydrolase transcripts, and load -\u003e compensation, is a proposal to be tested, not an established relation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia sit in a chronically substrate-loaded endolysosomal state: transcripts for lipid-directed acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and the TFEB/MITF regulators are coordinately higher than in isogenic APOE3 cells (permutation mean +2.96 log units, p=0.003 against the supplied differential-expression background), together with higher lipoprotein/debris uptake receptor transcripts and a mitochondrial pyruvate-TCA-ETC program, whereas the mevalonate/SREBP-2 sterol-synthesis module is indistinguishable from background (p=0.27). We propose the bottleneck is luminal hydrolytic clearance of internalised lipid cargo, and that the elevated hydrolase transcript abundance is a compensatory response to that bottleneck rather than a readout of increased degradative flux. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; hydrolase activity, cargo flux, lysosomal pH, lipid pools and causal direction are all inferred and unmeasured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pulse-chase APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a quenched degradable lipid cargo (e.g. BODIPY- or DQ-labelled lipoprotein/myelin) and measure dequenching kinetics plus residual intracellular substrate. The mechanism predicts APOE4 cells clear cargo more slowly per unit internalised and accumulate more undegraded substrate despite higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clearance kinetics equal or exceed APOE3 with no substrate accumulation, the bottleneck claim fails and the hydrolase elevation should instead be read as increased successful throughput.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB (and MITF) knockdown or nuclear-translocation blockade in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels and aggravate cargo retention. Persistence of the module after TFEB/MITF loss would falsify mechanism step 3.", "Sterol-focus discriminator: HMGCR inhibition (statin) should NOT preferentially normalise the APOE4 lysosomal signature (no genotype x statin interaction on the hydrolase module), whereas pharmacological inhibition of lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis (e.g. GBA or acid sphingomyelinase inhibition) in APOE3 cells should shift them toward the APOE4 transcript and cargo-retention phenotype. If statin normalises the APOE4 profile and hydrolase inhibition does not reproduce it, sterol synthesis rather than lysosomal clearance is primary and this hypothesis is rejected.", "Metabolic coupling: if the pyruvate-TCA-ETC transcript shift reflects flux, APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a higher OCR/ECAR ratio than APOE3, and blocking mitochondrial pyruvate carrier or glutamate anaplerosis should selectively impair APOE4 cargo clearance. Equal respiration between genotypes would weaken mechanism step 5 without falsifying steps 1-4.", "Enzyme-level check: measured acid hydrolase specific activities (GBA, HEXA/B, GAA, acid sphingomyelinase) and lysosomal pH should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite higher transcripts. Proportionally higher activity with normal pH would argue the transcript rise is productive and would weaken the compensatory interpretation.", "Uptake decoupling: reducing scavenger/lipoprotein uptake in APOE4 (SCARB1 or CD36 loss, or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module toward APOE3 levels. If the module is uptake-independent, the load-driven ordering of steps 1-3 is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_102", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance of endocytic/scavenger uptake receptors SCARB1 (+8.22), ABCA7 (+2.14), LDLR (+1.50), CD36 (+1.38), MRC1 (+1.36), MERTK (+1.30), TREM2 (+1.28) and APOE (+1.24). INFERRED: greater capacity for lipoprotein and membrane-debris internalisation into the endolysosomal system; actual uptake flux and receptor surface localisation were not measured.", "INFERRED BOTTLENECK: luminal hydrolysis of the internalised sphingomyelin-, glycosphingolipid- and sterol-containing cargo does not keep pace with delivery, so undegraded lipid substrate is retained in late endosomes/lysosomes. No lipid pool, substrate level or degradation rate is present in the supplied data; this step is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "MEASURED (RNA): the transcriptional stress response to that load is a coordinate rise in TFEB (+2.38) and MITF (+1.03) with CLEAR-type targets GAA (+9.96), CTSK (+7.36), GBA (+6.71), NAGLU (+5.91), HEXA (+5.68), SMPD1 (+5.63), CTSB (+5.52), CTSD (+2.86), HEXB (+2.17), DNASE2 (+2.03), MAN2B1 (+1.81), GLA (+1.53), LAMP1 (+1.38), SGSH (+1.32), NPC2 (+1.17), CLN3 (+1.17), SCARB2 (+1.06), plus v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A (+4.23), ATP6V1F (+1.70), ATP6V0D1 (+1.68) and the lysosomal transporters SLC38A7 (+7.46) and RAB7A (+2.65). INFERRED: expanded lysosomal biogenesis programme; compartment size, acidification and enzyme activity are not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): sterol handling is skewed toward uptake, esterification and side-chain oxidation (SOAT1 +1.25, CH25H +1.62, CYP27A1 +1.49, MYLIP +1.28) with only weak, non-enriched movement of biosynthetic/sensor genes (HMGCS1 +1.08, SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87, LSS +2.27, DHCR7 +2.71, DHCR24 +3.69). INFERRED: sterol demand is met largely from internalised lipoprotein sterol routed through the lysosome, not from a coordinately induced mevalonate pathway; SREBP-2 cleavage state and free/esterified sterol pools were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): a mitochondrial pyruvate-entry, TCA and anaplerotic programme is elevated (MPC2 +7.98, MDH1 +8.72, OGDH +8.56, GOT1 +6.43, DLD +5.54, ACO2 +3.54, GLUD1 +3.17) with ETC subunits up (ATP5MC3 +4.70, UQCRC2 +4.02) while upper-glycolytic HK2 (-3.67) and PFKP (-3.08) are lower. INFERRED: a shift of ATP and acetyl-CoA supply toward oxidation of lysosome- and lipid-derived catabolites; no flux, oxygen consumption or metabolite measurement supports this directionality here.", "INFERRED CONSEQUENCE: the combination of high uptake capacity, compensatory hydrolase transcription and oxidative catabolic bias defines the APOE4 steady state; if clearance remains limiting, retained lipid cargo and altered lysosomal membrane composition would progressively constrain further phagocytic and degradative turnover. This is the falsifiable endpoint of the mechanism, not an observation."], "title": "Lysosomal catabolic clearance, not SREBP-2 sterol synthesis, is the rate-limiting node distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 iPSC-microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13467858065945426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11790239718487992, "cosine_similarity": 0.34758645569092994, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_102", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6435469255663431, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13467858065945426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11790239718487992, "cosine_similarity": 0.34758645569092994, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6435469255663431, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.797069, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 237}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_047", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA effects are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base; only their sign, rank and relative magnitude are used, and the RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1), not an unbiased transcriptome.", "Because 77.1% of the supplied RNA rows are positive (median +1.46), every pathway statement here is made relative to that in-list background by permutation, not against zero; the global shift itself may be technical (normalization, ambient RNA, cell-size or capture-efficiency differences in the 10X Flex data).", "2D protein spots are mixtures: median 4.8 candidate genes per spot, with KRT1/KRT10/ACTB present in 33/30/25 spots. Assignment of any spot to a specific hydrolase or v-ATPase subunit is an inference, and spot-level up/down splits are interpreted only as 'not a coordinate increase / possible redistribution', never as identified proteoform measurements.", "No lipid, lysosomal pH, hydrolase-activity, mature/pro-enzyme, mitochondrial-mass or flux measurement is supplied; cargo load, degradative flux, sterol bioavailability and localization are all inferred, not observed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and no replicate structure is reported, so genotype-intrinsic versus co-culture-driven and pseudoreplication effects cannot be separated.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are stated to be isogenic, so the contrast is attributed to genotype rather than background."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step relative to APOE3 is delivery of mature, active acid hydrolases to an expanded endolysosomal compartment: uptake-receptor and CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts are coordinately elevated, but the measured hydrolase-containing protein spots are not coordinately increased (several are significantly decreased and redistributed), predicting reduced degradative flux per unit internalized lipid cargo, retention of sterol/sphingolipid cargo in the lysosome, and secondary sterol-synthesis, integrated-stress and mitochondrial-catabolic transcriptional compensation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Cargo pulse-chase (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-LacCer, Cy5-labelled myelin or apoptotic-cell membranes) in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show equal or greater internalization but a lower per-cargo degradation rate constant and larger undegraded residue at 6-24 h. Equal or faster degradation per internalized cargo in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "Form-resolved immunoblot plus activity assay for CTSD, CTSB, GBA and HEXA/B: APOE4 should show an increased pro/intermediate-to-mature ratio and mature-enzyme activity per cell that is flat or reduced despite the strongly elevated transcripts (gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA). If mature-enzyme protein and activity scale proportionally with the transcript increase, the mechanism is falsified and a simple compartment-expansion model is favoured.", "Discriminating perturbation: bypassing maturation by feeding exogenous M6P-tagged recombinant hydrolase (rhCTSD or rhGBA), or bypassing lysosomal sterol export with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, should normalize SREBP-target transcripts (gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCD) and lysosomal neutral-lipid/filipin load in APOE4 toward APOE3 without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36). Failure of both bypasses to reduce the sterol-synthesis signature would weaken the mechanism.", "Transcriptional versus post-transcriptional discrimination: TFEB overexpression (or mTORC1 inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should further raise hydrolase mRNA yet produce sub-proportional gains in mature hydrolase activity and only partial rescue of cargo clearance, whereas full rescue by TFEB alone would relocate the bottleneck to transcription and falsify step 3.", "Lysosomal acidification test: LysoSensor ratiometric pH and v-ATPase-dependent acidification rate should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite elevated ATP6V1A/ATP6V1H transcripts; a measurably more acidic APOE4 lysosome with normal hydrolase maturation would weaken the mechanism.", "Negative prediction against the acyl-remodeling alternative: untargeted lipidomics should show APOE4 accumulation dominated by glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate and cholesteryl-ester species rather than a coordinate PUFA-to-MUFA acyl-chain shift of PC/PE. A dominant PC/PE acyl-chain remodeling signature with normal sphingolipid and sterol-ester handling would support the rejected glycerolipid-remodeling mechanism instead.", "Mitochondrial arm is secondary: acutely restoring degradative flux (bypass above) should reduce the mitochondrial catabolic and integrated-stress transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:DDIT3) in APOE4; if these remain elevated while cargo clearance normalizes, the mitochondrial module is independent and step 6 is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia elevate transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and debris uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, ABCA7, MERTK, TREM2, APOE), which we infer - but do not measure - raises the endolysosomal delivery of cholesteryl-ester-, sphingolipid- and membrane-rich cargo.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): The endolysosomal/CLEAR transcriptional module is coordinately induced (TFEB, acid hydrolases GAA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, GLA, DPP7, MAN2B1; v-ATPase ATP6V1A/ATP6V1H; ESCRT/retromer/late-endosome VPS26A, VPS35L, VPS18, RAB7A; LAMP1), consistent with a compartment-expansion / demand response rather than a transcriptional deficiency.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured protein spots, inferred identity): Despite the transcript increase, protein spots whose candidate lists contain acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are not coordinately up and several are significantly reduced or redistributed between spots (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:086, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down versus protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:013 up). We infer a post-transcriptional bottleneck in hydrolase maturation/M6P-dependent delivery and/or acidification-dependent activation (accompanied by GNPTG and IGF2R transcript increase but M6PR decrease), not an increase in mature hydrolase pool.", "Step 4 (inferred flux and localization): Reduced mature-hydrolase activity per unit cargo lowers lysosomal degradation of glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and cholesteryl-ester cargo and lowers lysosome-to-ER sterol export, so cargo-derived lipid is retained in the endolysosomal lumen and membranes.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): The ER sterol sensor behaves as if sterol-poor despite high uptake - SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, SCD and LDLR transcripts are elevated - which is the expected read-out of sequestered rather than bioavailable cholesterol.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred compensation): Persistent undegraded cargo and catabolic ATP demand accompany integrated-stress/ER-stress transcripts (DDIT3, EIF2AK3, ATF6, NUPR1) and a coordinate rise in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial catabolic transcripts (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, SLC25A1), which we interpret as downstream compensation, not as the initiating lesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at lysosomal hydrolytic throughput, not at lipid-uptake or hydrolase transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1073005401144085, "cosine_similarity": 0.34742704272090996, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6422686084142395, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12524461839530332, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1073005401144085, "cosine_similarity": 0.34742704272090996, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6422686084142395, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.95180275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 238}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All gene effects quoted above are reported RNA log fold changes, with logarithm base unspecified; protein-spot effects are log2 fold changes. Positive means higher in APOE4. RNA rows are selected differential-expression results: 1,705/2,212 (77.08%) are positive. Directional coherence is descriptive, not formal enrichment, and missing members are unknown.", "Biochemical roles and the proposed serial links are unverified background knowledge. RNA changes must translate into appropriately localized functional capacity, and available mock-culture cargo must reach this route. Unrepresented requirements, including NPC1, LIPA and other lipid-processing enzymes, cannot be assumed unchanged or deficient.", "The proposed cell state increases basal cargo-to-product throughput. Failed lysosomal compensation remains a serious alternative because lower CTSS and negative ambiguous hydrolase/acidification spots accompany the positive RNA programs. No ongoing acidification defect, oxidative stress, lipid accumulation or successful redox adaptation is established.", "All candidates for every cited spot are retained in step 3. Spot changes can reflect mixtures or proteoforms and cannot confirm individual proteins. The observation ID index includes the explicitly discussed counter-evidence. Biological replicate counts and cell-state proportions are unavailable; isogenic comparison does not resolve intrinsic versus co-culture-mediated causation.", "The large nuclear respiratory RNA program and opposite directions among represented mitochondrial respiratory transcripts are not explained by this lipid-routing chain. The upstream signal and respiratory flux remain unidentified; antioxidant or peroxisomal defects are not required assumptions.", "This mechanism predicts activity in the actual mock condition. Any free-lipid burden or oxidative sensitivity revealed only after a future inhibitor or cargo overload is a perturbation response, not evidence of an existing basal defect."], "claim": "In day-30 human iPSC-derived 2D microglia co-cultured with astrocytes under mock treatment, APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3 promotes a coordinated lipid-handling state that increases acquisition and lysosomal processing of available lipid cargo and its routing into newly esterified lipids in the ER. Increased cargo-to-product flux is the falsifiable causal proposal; the supplied RNA expression and ambiguous protein-spot abundances do not establish it.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective basal test: in matched day-30 mock co-cultures, use a non-overloading trace-dose lipid-cargo pulse\u2013chase that separates newly re-esterified products from input esters. APOE4 should show greater uptake and faster transfer of internalized cargo into newly synthesized cholesteryl esters/triacylglycerols, with maintained acidic lysosomes. Normalize to cell number and internalized tracer and measure lysosomal label retention. Equal or lower cargo-to-product transfer, especially with prolonged retention and reduced acidification, would weaken the proposed ongoing throughput increase and favor failed compensation.", "Prospective serial-pathway perturbation: after matched tracer uptake, acutely and partially inhibit V-ATPase with verified lysosomal pH target engagement and viability controls. The APOE4 excess in cargo-derived newly esterified products should fall as lysosomal retention rises, while esterification of substrates supplied directly to the ER is relatively preserved. Persistence of the APOE4 excess despite verified blockade of lysosomal cargo processing would weaken the proposed lysosome-to-ER causal link.", "Prospective downstream perturbation: after matched cargo uptake, acutely inhibit DGAT1 and SOAT1 with verified target engagement. APOE4 should lose its excess conversion into the corresponding newly esterified products and show greater transient retention of cargo-derived nonesterified substrates, without an immediate reduction of initial uptake. No APOE4 excess before inhibition, or persistence of that excess after effective inhibition, would weaken the proposed esterification-dependent route. Such inhibitor-induced substrate accumulation would not establish basal lipid accumulation or oxidative damage."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["1. APOE4 biases the co-cultured microglia toward a coupled lysosomal and lipid-synthetic transcriptional state. Measured RNA changes include gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:SREBF1 +4.67 and gene:SREBF2 +1.06, with gene:LSS +2.27 and gene:DHCR24 +3.69. These mark the proposed state; they do not demonstrate TFEB nuclear localization, SREBP cleavage or a unique initiating regulator.", "2. Within this state, greater lipid acquisition supplies the endolysosomal route during the actual mock condition. Higher gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:SCARB1 +8.22 and gene:TREM2 +1.28 support this proposed input arm. Uptake rates and the composition or origin of available cargo were not measured.", "3. Coordinated acidification and hydrolytic capacity processes the additional cargo: gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:CTSB +5.52 and gene:CTSD +2.86 are higher. Increased basal processing is inferred and requires functional acidification/hydrolases. gene:CTSS \u22125.57 shows selective remodeling. protein_spot:053 +1.536 [TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1] is compatible, but protein_spot:064 \u22121.202 [ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1], protein_spot:067 \u22121.000 [PSMA3, ACTG2, CTSB, HEXB, LRIF1] and protein_spot:069 \u22121.379 [ACTB, CTSD, GPS2] challenge this step; none resolves an individual protein.", "4. Processed cargo supplies sterols and fatty-acid substrates to ER esterification, coupling lysosomal turnover to lipid reuse. Higher gene:NPC2 +1.17 is compatible with lysosomal sterol handling; gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58 and gene:SCD +4.17 support esterification and acyl-lipid synthesis capacity. gene:GPAT3 \u22122.23 is an exception. The proposed outcome is faster appearance of cargo-derived label in newly synthesized cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols under mock conditions; neither those pools nor their synthesis rates were measured."], "title": "APOE4 couples lysosomal lipid processing to ER re-esterification under mock conditions"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.036203522504892366, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2631651901672481, "cosine_similarity": 0.3472661325428677, "direction_accuracy": 0.061488673139158574, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6315469255663431, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.036203522504892366, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2631651901672481, "cosine_similarity": 0.3472661325428677, "direction_accuracy": 0.061488673139158574, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6315469255663431, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.7452145000000003, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_049", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive, logarithm base unspecified); effects are treated as ordinal within that list and absent genes are treated as unknown, not unchanged.", "Coordinate transcript increases in receptor, endolysosomal, hydrolase, v-ATPase and mitochondrial machinery are assumed to translate into proportionally increased protein and functional capacity; no uptake, acidification, hydrolase, sterol-pool or respiration flux was measured here.", "The inference that ER-accessible cholesterol is low (driving the SREBP-arm transcripts) is indirect; free versus esterified and lysosomal cholesterol pools were not measured.", "The increased gene:ARHGDIA transcript is assumed to reduce the GTP-loaded fraction of Rho-family GTPases; GTPase loading was not measured, and lower gene:ACTB is not assumed to lower total actin protein because ACTB-containing spots are mostly increased.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidates over 92 spots, KRT1/KRT10 present in 33/30 spots as likely contaminants); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spots are used only for compatibility or contradiction.", "Program membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge) before looking at signs; genes are not independent, so sign counts are descriptive comparisons against the 77% positive list background, not formal enrichment tests.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipid/lipoprotein ligands, so the state is assumed to be substrate-exposed rather than lipid-starved; ligand availability was not measured."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change rather than by a single failed step: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger and phagocytic recognition receptors, clathrin/dynamin and endosome-to-lysosome sorting machinery, TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase machinery, and mitochondrial TCA/ETC/beta-oxidation machinery are coordinately higher, while glycolytic/PPP transcripts are mixed-to-lower; sterol-biosynthetic and SREBP-arm transcripts are simultaneously higher, which we interpret as internalized lipid being routed into lysosomal and esterified stores so that ER sterol sensing remains unsatisfied. In parallel the actin-regulatory arm is retuned (RhoGDI1 transcript strongly higher; hematopoietic Rac/actomyosin effector transcripts strongly lower) while branched-actin subunit transcripts are higher and actin-containing protein spots are not decreased, predicting a routing bias toward receptor/clathrin-mediated uptake with reduced Rac-dependent large-particle engulfment reserve. No uptake, degradative or respiratory flux was measured, so increased capacity and reduced engulfment reserve are inferred, not observed, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, mock condition: per-cell uptake of soluble receptor ligands (DiI-AcLDL, fluorescent dextran) and per-cell lysosomal degradative activity (DQ-BSA dequenching, cathepsin B activity probe) plus basal and maximal oxygen consumption should be equal or higher in APOE4 than isogenic APOE3, with a lower ECAR/OCR ratio. If hydrolase activity or oxygen consumption is instead lower despite the higher gene:CTSB, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:MDH1 and gene:OGDH transcripts, the 'expanded functional capacity' reading fails and failed compensation for a degradative block becomes the better model.", "Prospective challenge, not a claim about the measured condition: on large-particle challenge (pHrodo beads, myelin, synaptosomes) APOE4 should show a lower phagocytic index per cell, fewer/smaller F-actin engulfment cups, and lower Rac1/Rac2-GTP by pulldown with unchanged total Rac. Equal or higher particle uptake with unchanged Rac-GTP would falsify the actin-retuning step while leaving the endolysosomal steps intact.", "Prospective: APOE4 cells should show higher esterified/neutral-lipid and LAMP1-colocalized filipin-positive cholesterol with lower ER-accessible cholesterol; relieving sequestration (SOAT1 inhibition or cyclodextrin) should lower SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, SCD) in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Insensitivity of these targets would falsify the 'unsatisfied ER sterol signal' step.", "Prospective, discriminating: ARHGDIA knockdown (or expression of a fast-cycling Rac allele) in APOE4 microglia should restore large-particle engulfment toward APOE3 levels without changing lysosomal hydrolase transcripts or oxygen consumption; failure to restore engulfment, or loss of the endolysosomal signature after ARHGDIA knockdown, would weaken the proposed separation of an actin-effector arm from the uptake-catabolism arm.", "Prospective specificity control: blocking receptor-mediated lipoprotein uptake (LDLR/SCARB1 knockdown or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should collapse the APOE4-specific lysosomal and mitochondrial oxidative transcript excess; persistence of that excess would indicate an upstream, ligand-independent driver and weaken the routing mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts for lipid/ligand recognition and uptake receptors relative to APOE3 in mock (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:STAB1 +1.13, gene:CD163 +1.38; 25/25 represented members positive versus a 77% positive background in this selected differential-expression list), increasing inferred capacity for ligand binding and receptor-mediated internalization, not a measured uptake rate.", "Internalization and endosome-to-lysosome sorting machinery is coordinately higher (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:VAMP3 +2.99, gene:STX12 +1.00; exception gene:GOLPH3L -7.40), so internalized ligand is inferred to be routed preferentially into the late endosome/lysosome rather than recycled.", "A TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal program is expanded (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46; 28/30 positive), giving higher inferred lysosomal acidification and hydrolytic capacity; gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:IDS -1.56 are the notable exceptions and argue against a uniform lysosomal upshift.", "Catabolic products are inferred to be oxidized rather than fermented: mitochondrial TCA/ETC/beta-oxidation transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65; 19/19 positive) while glycolytic/PPP transcripts are mixed-to-lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30 against gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:ENO1 +2.17).", "Despite this uptake-plus-catabolism expansion, the sterol/lipid biosynthetic arm is also higher (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), which is most simply explained if lipid is sequestered in lysosomal and esterified/neutral-lipid pools so ER-accessible cholesterol remains low; the sterol pools themselves were not measured.", "The same state retunes actin control rather than actin supply: gene:ARHGDIA (RhoGDI1) +10.61 with gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:ARHGDIB -1.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:FAM49B/CYRIB -5.83, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:MYH9 -6.38 and gene:ACTB -4.98, against higher gene:ARPC1B +2.15, gene:ARPC4 +1.93, gene:ARPC5 +1.94, gene:CFL1 +1.80, gene:RHOA +1.61 (16/24 positive, below the 77% list background); actin-containing protein spots are mostly increased (protein_spot:044 +2.379, protein_spot:043 +1.964, protein_spot:052 +2.138, protein_spot:028 +0.848, protein_spot:029 +0.926), so a depleted actin protein pool is not supported and the inferred change is reduced Rac-loaded, actomyosin-dependent engulfment capacity.", "Net predicted phenotype in the measured mock condition: higher receptor/clathrin-mediated uptake and lysosomal-oxidative processing of lipid ligands supplied by the astrocyte co-culture, with a lower reserve for actin-intensive large-particle phagocytosis that would only be revealed by a particle challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a receptor-endolysosome-mitochondria lipid-scavenging state with an unsatisfied ER sterol signal and a retuned actin-effector arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27440645423328286, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24298711640562284, "cosine_similarity": 0.3470913586017517, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6174919093851133, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27440645423328286, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24298711640562284, "cosine_similarity": 0.3470913586017517, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6174919093851133, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.972285, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 59}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| \u003e 1, every adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and 77% of rows are positive, so all pathway claims are made relative to the observed up-shifted background, not against zero; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and only direction and relative rank are used.", "Increased steady-state transcript abundance for lysosomal, esterification and mitochondrial genes is treated as evidence of programme induction, not of protein amount, enzyme activity, organelle number, metabolic flux or subcellular localisation, none of which were measured here.", "TFEB/MITF transcript elevation is assumed to be accompanied by increased nuclear TFEB activity; this was not measured and could instead reflect autoregulatory feedback of a stalled programme.", "Lipid pools themselves (lysosomal cholesterol, sphingolipids, cholesteryl esters, triacylglycerol, lipid droplets) are entirely unmeasured in this dataset; their accumulation is an inference and a prediction, not an observation.", "2D-gel protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are used only as ambiguous, non-decisive evidence.", "Cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes profiled by probe-based 10X Flex, so some rows (e.g. gene:S100B, gene:A2M) may reflect non-microglial or ambient RNA, and mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification in a probe panel is assumed to be less reliable than nuclear transcripts (unverified background knowledge).", "Replicate number is 'not supplied in the workbook', so the extremely small adjusted p-values may be inflated by cell-level rather than donor-level statistics; the comparison is stated to be isogenic, so residual clone/line effects are assumed small but not excluded."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal degradative machinery (v-ATPase subunits plus glycosidase/sphingolipid/protease hydrolases, with TFEB and MITF transcripts elevated) together with lipid-uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36, ABCA7, TREM2, MERTK) and lipid-esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1) transcripts, and a strongly enriched nuclear-encoded TCA/beta-oxidation/OXPHOS gene program whose mtDNA-encoded partner subunits are not concordantly elevated. We propose that the rate-limiting step is luminal lysosomal hydrolysis and onward export of lipoprotein/membrane-derived lipid: transcriptional CLEAR up-regulation is a compensatory response to a lipid load that it does not fully clear, so undegraded lipid is retained in the endolysosome and escaping sterol/fatty acid is diverted into cytoplasmic ester/droplet storage rather than into a proportionally increased respiratory flux. All statements are transcript- and spot-abundance measurements plus explicitly inferred activity/flux; causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pulse-chase isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a traceable lipid cargo (e.g. fluorescent-cholesterol-labelled or BODIPY-labelled myelin/oxLDL) and measure uptake and lysosomal degradation separately. Prediction: APOE4 shows equal or greater internalisation but a lower fractional hydrolysis rate per delivered cargo, with retained filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments and increased cytoplasmic neutral-lipid droplets at 24 h. If APOE4 cells clear the cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3 with no lysosomal or droplet lipid retention, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Blocking the proposed escape valve should be selectively toxic: SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition (avasimibe plus a DGAT1 inhibitor) during lipid loading should raise free-sterol stress markers and reduce viability more in APOE4 than in APOE3, without reducing lysosomal cargo retention. Equal sensitivity in both genotypes, or rescue of lysosomal retention by these inhibitors, would weaken step 5.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown or dominant-negative expression in APOE4 microglia should collapse the v-ATPase and hydrolase transcript block (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) toward APOE3 levels and worsen lipid retention. If those transcripts remain elevated after TFEB loss, step 2/3 is falsified and an alternative driver (e.g. a distinct activation-state shift) is favoured.", "Flux versus transcript test: despite 37/37 nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts being up, Seahorse respirometry should show no proportional increase (and plausibly a decrease) in maximal oxygen consumption and complex IV/V-linked respiration in APOE4, with BN-PAGE showing unchanged or reduced assembled complex I/IV. A clear, proportional increase in respiratory flux in APOE4 would falsify step 7 and shift the mechanism to a genuinely hypermetabolic rather than substrate-retentive state.", "Orthogonal capacity readout: lysosomal proteolytic and glycosidase capacity per cell (DQ-BSA dequenching, live GBA/HEXA activity probes) should be flat or reduced in APOE4 relative to the large transcript increases, and LysoTracker-positive volume should be increased. Concordant proportional increases in measured hydrolase activity would refute the 'transcript up, capacity not matched' core of the hypothesis.", "Lipidomics prediction: APOE4 microglia should show elevated glucosylceramide/GM2-type glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin species plus increased cholesteryl esters relative to APOE3 under mock conditions; absence of any such lipid difference would remove the phenotypic endpoint the mechanism requires."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30) alongside higher gene:APOE, which we infer (not measure) increases delivery of cholesterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred transcription-factor activity): gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) transcripts and the TFEB target gene:RRAGD (+1.44) are elevated, consistent with, but not proof of, increased nuclear CLEAR-network activity; nuclear localisation of TFEB protein was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts): the CLEAR output is up as a coherent block above the already up-shifted background - v-ATPase subunits 10/10 up (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51) and luminal hydrolases 15/17 up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81).", "Step 4 (bottleneck; inferred, partly counter-supported): the expansion is incomplete and non-stoichiometric - the mannose-6-phosphate sorting receptor gene:M6PR (-1.72), gene:IDS (-1.56) and the dominant microglial protease gene:CTSS (-5.57) move the opposite way, and 2D-gel spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins or a v-ATPase subunit move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down). We therefore infer that hydrolytic/export capacity per unit delivered lipid does not scale with the load, leaving undegraded lipid (unmeasured pool) in the lysosome.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred routing): sterol/fatty-acid that reaches the cytosol is routed to storage rather than feedback inhibition - gene:SOAT1 (+1.25) and gene:DGAT1 (+1.72) are up while the SREBP-driven sterol-synthesis arm is not switched off (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50), which is the signature expected when the accumulated sterol is mislocalised to the lysosome and not sensed at the ER.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts, flux NOT measured): a catabolic mitochondrial program is induced downstream - TCA and pyruvate/citrate carriers (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54), beta-oxidation/electron transfer (gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24) and 37/37 detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits up, while glycolytic transcripts are not enriched; we infer substrate-driven induction of lipid oxidation rather than a glycolytic shift.", "Step 7 (measured transcripts, inferred limitation): the mtDNA-encoded core subunits are not concordantly increased (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33 versus gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), so we predict the respiratory-chain response is assembly-limited and the transcriptional program over-predicts any increase in actual oxygen consumption; APOE4 cells should therefore hold lipid in lysosomes and droplets instead of oxidising it away."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-CLEAR expansion that is substrate-limited: lysosomal lipid hydrolysis/export is the bottleneck, forcing sterol/fatty-acid re-esterification and a compensatory mitochondrial catabolic transcriptional program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11360076502345513, "cosine_similarity": 0.3468923451370183, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6371553398058253, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13111545988258316, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11360076502345513, "cosine_similarity": 0.3468923451370183, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6371553398058253, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.77801025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 239}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_045", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base); all pathway claims are therefore made relative to this list's own background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least in rank order, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal and sterol-pathway proteins; no hydrolase activity, sterol flux, membrane-contact-site or localisation measurement is supplied.", "Elevated SREBP target transcripts are assumed to report low ER-accessible sterol rather than SREBP-independent transcriptional drive (e.g. direct APOE4 effects on chromatin or a normalisation artefact).", "Protein spots are mixtures: each spot lists 2-6 candidate genes, so no protein is uniquely identified and no protein-level claim about a specific cathepsin, HSP90B1 or annexin is made.", "The lipid endpoint implied by the experiment identifier (cholesteryl ester, lipid droplets, lysosomal free cholesterol) was not measured in the supplied data and is an inference.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may reflect altered cross-talk or residual non-microglial signal rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 biology.", "Several effects are extreme (21 genes above +8 in the reported log units), which is atypical for log2 fold changes and suggests scaling, pseudobulk or low-expression instability; conclusions are therefore based on set-level rank statistics rather than individual large effects."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the dominant APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference is not an ER unfolded-protein response but a lipid-handling imbalance: transcripts encoding lysosomal acid hydrolases and the TFEB/v-ATPase module are coordinately higher in APOE4 (median effect ~2.9 versus a list-wide background of ~1.4; rank test p=0.006), yet sterol-sensing-dependent transcripts (SREBF1/2, INSIG1, LDLR and the post-squalene enzymes LSS, DHCR24, DHCR7, EBP, ACAT2) are simultaneously higher (10/10 up) together with uptake and esterification genes (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is transfer of lysosome-derived unesterified sterol to the ER sensing pool; because that step is limiting, the ER reports a sterol deficit, SREBP-dependent synthesis and uptake remain on despite an expanded degradative compartment, and the excess sterol/fatty acid is diverted into SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterified storage rather than efflux. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol export in APOE4 microglia (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/STARD3 overexpression) should, within 24 h and without changing TFEB target transcripts, normalise the SREBP2 module (SREBF2, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24) toward APOE3 levels and reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet content. If cyclodextrin lowers droplets but leaves the SREBP2 module elevated, or leaves droplets unchanged, the lysosome-to-ER transfer bottleneck is weakened.", "Filipin/ester assay: APOE4 microglia should show higher unesterified cholesterol within LAMP1-positive compartments and a lower ER-accessible (SCAP-reporter or ALOD4-inaccessible) sterol pool than isogenic APOE3. Equal or higher ER-accessible sterol in APOE4 despite elevated SREBP2 targets would falsify step 3.", "Genotype-by-drug interaction: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should raise free cholesterol and suppress SREBP2 target transcripts more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3, and should convert stored ester into a free-sterol stress phenotype. An equal response in both genotypes argues that esterification is not the compensating sink.", "Statin control: HMG-CoA reductase inhibition should lower SREBP2-target-driven synthesis in both genotypes yet fail to normalise lysosomal free cholesterol or the hydrolase/TFEB module in APOE4. If statin alone fully normalises the APOE4 lysosomal phenotype, the primary lesion is de novo synthesis, not lysosome-to-ER transfer.", "Negative prediction for the ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 cells should not show elevated XBP1 splicing, ATF4/CHOP protein, or thapsigargin hypersensitivity relative to APOE3 under mock conditions. Clear constitutive XBP1s/BiP induction in APOE4 would favour a UPR-primary mechanism over this one.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should reduce hydrolase transcripts but, by itself, should not normalise the SREBP2 module; normalisation of both by TFEB knockdown alone would place TFEB upstream and weaken the proposed bottleneck ordering."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises the measured abundance of TFEB/MITF and of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1), consistent with an enlarged or more biosynthetically loaded endolysosomal compartment; hydrolytic flux itself is inferred, not measured.", "Inferred bottleneck: export of the resulting unesterified sterol (and sphingoid backbone) from the limiting membrane of the late endosome/lysosome to the ER sterol-sensing pool is rate-limiting in APOE4. The transporters/contact-site machinery for this step are largely absent from the supplied differential list (NPC1, STARD3, VAPA/VAPB not present); OSBPL8 is lower (gene:OSBPL8) while OSBPL1A is marginally higher (gene:OSBPL1A), so this step is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "Because the ER sterol pool is sensed as low, SCAP-SREBP processing stays permissive and SREBP target transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24), i.e. de novo synthesis capacity is not switched off despite an expanded catabolic compartment.", "In parallel, lipoprotein/lipid uptake and scavenging transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:PLTP, gene:NPC2), so substrate delivery into the same bottlenecked route continues.", "The resulting cytosolic-facing excess of sterol and fatty acyl species is inferred to be routed to esterification and storage rather than efflux: SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD and TSPO transcripts are higher (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:TSPO), while classical efflux transporters (ABCA1, ABCG1) do not appear in the supplied differential list and the LXR target MYLIP is higher (gene:MYLIP), which would further limit LDLR protein-level uptake.", "Net predicted cellular state (not measured here): APOE4 microglia accumulate lysosomal unesterified sterol/sphingolipid and cytoplasmic cholesteryl-ester and triglyceride droplets, with a chronically 'sterol-hungry' ER transcriptional signature; the 2-D gel spots containing cathepsin candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), so the protein layer neither confirms nor refutes increased hydrolase protein."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolase capacity but are bottlenecked at lysosome-to-ER sterol delivery, driving a futile SREBP-driven synthesis-and-esterification cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20940255948820907, "cosine_similarity": 0.34629140487878896, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6114012944983819, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20940255948820907, "cosine_similarity": 0.34629140487878896, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6114012944983819, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.51782325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 240}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_172", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; every effect has magnitude \u003e1 and 77% are positive (mean +1.39 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base). All pathway claims are therefore stated as enrichment relative to this list's own background, and the global positive shift is treated as a possible normalisation/compositional artefact rather than a real genome-wide induction.", "The reported log fold changes use an unspecified logarithm base and are preserved as given; magnitudes are treated as unreliable rank information because |effect| is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p-value (r = -0.04), so direction and set-level coherence carry the argument, not individual extreme genes.", "Protein spots are mixtures: each carries 2-6 candidate genes (median 5), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level discordance is treated as absence of corroboration, not as evidence of decreased hydrolase protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme amount; enzyme specific activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number, cargo flux, lipid species and cholesterol pools were not measured in this dataset.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply extracellular lipoprotein/lipid cargo, making cargo-handling capacity a physiologically loaded axis at day 30; the isogenic design is assumed to control genetic background so that differences track APOE genotype rather than clone identity, with no replicate count supplied.", "Cell-composition or maturation-state differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells could generate a coordinated lysosomal transcript module without any change in per-cell lysosomal biology; this alternative is not excluded by the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent, above-background induction of the TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal (CLEAR) transcript module - sphingolipid/glycolipid hydrolases, cathepsins and v-ATPase subunits - together with lipid-cargo uptake receptor transcripts and neutral-lipid esterification/storage transcripts, whereas the cholesterol-biosynthetic and LXR/efflux modules are not enriched beyond the global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is the per-lysosome catabolic clearance capacity for internalised lipid cargo: APOE4 raises lysosomal lipid substrate load, the cell responds transcriptionally through a CLEAR-type program, but this compensation is not corroborated at the protein-spot level, so undigested lipid is retained and diverted into esterified/stored neutral lipid rather than being fully catabolised and exported. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript pattern is equally compatible with a compensatory response to, rather than a cause of, lipid retention.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (load-versus-capacity): pulse-chase APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a defined traceable cargo (fluorogenic sphingomyelin or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester lipoprotein, or labelled myelin debris). The mechanism predicts a genotype x time interaction, with slower substrate degradation/clearance and greater residual lysosomal lipid in APOE4 despite its higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears the cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Capacity-per-lysosome test: measure GBA, HEXA/HEXB and cathepsin B/D specific activities and protein normalised to LAMP1-positive compartment volume. The mechanism predicts activity per unit lysosome is unchanged or reduced in APOE4 while transcripts are elevated. Proportional increases in activity per lysosome, together with no accumulation of glucosylceramide, GM2/lactosylceramide, sphingomyelin or unesterified cholesterol, would substantially weaken the mechanism.", "TFEB dependence with genotype interaction: TFEB (with MITF) knockdown, or sustained mTORC1 activation, should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module and should increase lysosomal lipid load and reduce cargo clearance more in APOE4 than in APOE3 (significant genotype x knockdown interaction). Equal effects in both genotypes would indicate the module is a genotype-independent cell-state feature rather than a compensation for an APOE4-specific load.", "Sterol-focus discriminator: statin (HMG-CoA reductase inhibition) or 25-hydroxycholesterol should not normalise the APOE4 lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module, because sterol-biosynthetic and LXR/efflux gene sets show no enrichment above the list background here (permutation p = 0.44 and 0.94). If statin or LXR agonism abolishes the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal module, the sterol-synthesis/efflux axis rather than lysosomal cargo digestion is primary and this hypothesis is rejected.", "Downstream-diversion test: SOAT1 (ACAT) inhibition should convert stored cholesteryl ester into a larger unesterified-cholesterol/lipid-droplet-free pool preferentially in APOE4 and further slow cargo clearance; if SOAT1 inhibition produces identical lipid redistribution in both genotypes, the esterification-diversion step (step 5) is not APOE4-specific.", "Independent-cohort transcript check: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome APOE4-versus-APOE3 microglia measurement with proper normalisation, the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase set should remain elevated relative to a matched-expression background after removal of the global shift. Loss of the enrichment there would indicate the present signal is an artefact of the selected list and of the global +1.39 offset."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_172", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; flux inferred): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipid/lipoprotein-cargo uptake and opsonic-recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB2, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid cargo to the endolysosome in an astrocyte co-culture that supplies lipoproteins.", "Step 2 (inferred, unmeasured pool): The increased cargo raises the luminal load of sphingomyelin, glycosphingolipids, glycoconjugates and lipid-associated protein in lysosomes. No lipid species, cholesterol pool or lysosomal substrate was measured in this dataset.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): A CLEAR-type transcriptional response is engaged - gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are up, together with luminal hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:GM2A, gene:GBA2, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GAA), cathepsins (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) and every measured v-ATPase subunit (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2), plus gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:RAB7A. Hydrolase-set mean effect is roughly 2.5-fold the mean of the surrounding selected list (permutation p\u003c0.001); this is transcript abundance, not enzyme activity, lysosomal pH or degradative flux.", "Step 4 (measured protein spots, discordant): Protein spots whose candidate-gene lists contain lysosomal hydrolases are not coordinately increased (protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 slightly up; protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058 down), unlike the remaining spots. Because each spot carries several candidate genes, this is not proof of unchanged cathepsin protein, but it withholds corroboration for the assumption that the transcript induction is converted into proportionally greater hydrolytic capacity per lysosome.", "Step 5 (inferred): Consequently the per-lysosome digestion and egress of lipid cargo remains rate-limiting. Liberated sterol and fatty acid are predicted to be re-routed into esterified/stored neutral lipid rather than exported: gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1 and gene:MGLL transcripts are up, while cholesterol-synthesis (gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:MYLIP) and LXR/efflux (gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:PLTP) modules sit at, not above, the list background - i.e. de novo sterol synthesis is not the differentiating axis.", "Step 6 (measured RNA; state inferred): The resulting lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded state is accompanied by a modest inflammatory/chemokine tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:IL18) and a discordant loss of gene:CTSS and gene:STX17, consistent with a shifted degradative-compartment composition rather than a uniform lysosome-number increase."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal lipid-cargo digestion, not by sterol synthesis: a TFEB/CLEAR hydrolase-and-v-ATPase transcriptional compensation without matching protein-level capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10934713948888698, "cosine_similarity": 0.34607380628015266, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_172", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6472880258899676, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12426614481409001, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10934713948888698, "cosine_similarity": 0.34607380628015266, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6472880258899676, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.02560675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 241}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, all with adjusted p \u003c 0.05, not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway coherence is therefore evaluated relative to the other selected rows and not against the whole genome.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as given; effect magnitudes (range -7.94 to 15.46) are treated as ranks/directions only and are not interpreted as literal fold changes.", "77.1% of selected RNA rows are positive (median 1.46), so a global upward shift, normalisation or compositional difference may inflate all positive sets; only the relative contrast of a set against this background is used.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme protein, luminal localisation and catalytic activity; no hydrolase activity, lipid species, pH, or flux measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8) and often include actin/keratin, so no spot is treated as a unique protein identification; spots are used only as weak, direction-ambiguous evidence.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect differing maturation state rather than direct APOE4 action.", "Association only: no perturbation within this dataset tests direction of causation between APOE4 genotype, lipid load and the lysosomal program."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by an endolysosomal state in which transcripts for lipid uptake/esterification and for glycosphingolipid- and sphingomyelin-degrading lysosomal hydrolases (GBA, GBA2, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, SUMF1, GLA) plus v-ATPase subunits are coordinately higher, while the complex-glycosphingolipid Golgi step B4GALT5 and several Golgi-exit/sorting transcripts (M6PR, AP1M1, STX16, GOLPH3L) are lower. We propose this transcriptional pattern is a compensatory response to an unmet luminal glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin hydrolysis demand, so that per-lysosome sphingolipid turnover flux - not de novo sphingolipid synthesis - is the primary bottleneck; increased hydrolase mRNA is measured abundance and is not evidence of increased degradative flux, and causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of genotype-matched microglia should show higher glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin (and their lyso-species) in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions despite the higher hydrolase transcripts; unchanged or lower glycosphingolipid levels would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of glucosylceramide synthase (UGCG; e.g. eliglustat/Genz-123346) in APOE4 microglia should lower GlcCer/GM2, shrink the LAMP1+/LysoTracker+ compartment, and move the CLEAR-type transcripts (GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, TFEB targets) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the mitochondrial/TCA transcript signature (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2) essentially unchanged; if UGCG inhibition fails to reduce the lysosomal program, or normalises the mitochondrial signature to the same degree, the sphingolipid-specific bottleneck is rejected in favour of a general metabolic/maturation difference.", "Lyso-IP or per-lysosome assays (PFB-FDGlu for GBA, MUG for HEXA/B, normalised to LAMP1 or lysosome number) should show APOE4 hydrolase activity per lysosome equal to or lower than APOE3 despite higher mRNA; proportionally higher per-lysosome activity together with unchanged substrate would falsify the compensatory-bottleneck claim.", "Substrate selectivity: fluorescent BODIPY-LacCer/GlcCer clearance should be slower in APOE4 while DQ-BSA bulk proteolysis is unchanged or increased; equally impaired bulk proteolysis would indicate a general lysosomal failure rather than the proposed sphingolipid-specific bottleneck.", "Augmenting the bottleneck enzyme (GBA1 overexpression, recombinant enzyme uptake, or ambroxol chaperoning) should reduce GlcCer/GM2 load and normalise LAMP1/v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4 microglia; no change in lysosomal expansion after successful GBA activity increase would weaken step 5.", "If hydrolase sorting is limiting (step 4), blocking mannose-6-phosphate-independent or -dependent delivery should affect APOE3 more than APOE4, and rescuing sorting (M6PR/AP-1 restoration) should raise luminal hydrolase activity in APOE4 without further raising hydrolase mRNA; failure of any sorting manipulation to change luminal activity would remove step 4 while leaving steps 1-3 intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Higher transcripts of lipoprotein/lipid-uptake and lipid-esterification genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1) in APOE4 are proposed to increase delivery of cholesterol- and sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo into the endolysosomal lumen; the cargo flux itself is inferred, not measured here.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): A TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-biogenesis program is transcriptionally higher (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) together with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and lysosomal membrane/transport genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:SPNS1, gene:SLC17A5, gene:TMEM192), consistent with a compensatory expansion signal rather than with resolved demand.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): Within sphingolipid metabolism the induction is asymmetric and catabolic - gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:SUMF1, gene:GLA, gene:GLTP, gene:ST3GAL5 are higher while the complex-GSL synthetic step gene:B4GALT5 is lower; ceramide-synthase/first-committed-step genes that were measured change only modestly (gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:ORMDL2), and SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1, ASAH1, PSAP and GALC are absent from the supplied rows, so a de novo synthesis mechanism is not supported by these data.", "Step 4 (inferred activity/localization): Hydrolase transcript induction is proposed not to translate into a proportional rise in active luminal hydrolase per lysosome, because mannose-6-phosphate/Golgi-exit sorting transcripts are lower (gene:M6PR, gene:AP1M1, gene:STX16, gene:GOLPH3L) and 2D protein spots containing cathepsin candidates move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down); spot identity is ambiguous and enzyme activity was not measured.", "Step 5 (inferred state): Consequently glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 and sphingomyelin turnover remains rate-limiting in APOE4 late endosomes/lysosomes, and undegraded sphingolipid accumulates in limiting and intraluminal membranes; no lipid species was measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred consequence): Sphingolipid-loaded late-endosomal membranes are proposed to slow maturation and cargo recycling, matched by higher late-endosome/retromer-retriever and AP-5 transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5S1, gene:AP5Z1) and by loss of a major microglial degradative protease transcript (gene:CTSS), predicting reduced net clearance capacity despite an expanded lysosomal compartment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB-associated lysosomal glycosphingolipid-catabolism program whose luminal hydrolysis step, not sphingolipid synthesis, is the rate-limiting bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12195842410368127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13922524090763877, "cosine_similarity": 0.3456151467852172, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.623621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12195842410368127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13922524090763877, "cosine_similarity": 0.3456151467852172, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.623621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.66067875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 242}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_131", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a proposed ordering of an observed association between APOE4 genotype and a filtered differential-expression pattern.", "Transcript changes are assumed to translate into proportional changes in enzyme/carrier protein amount and hence maximal capacity; no protein measurement of MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1, GOT1, ACLY, SCD or DGAT1 is available in the supplied protein-spot data (the only MDH1-containing spot, protein_spot:050, is -0.48 and not reported significant).", "The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook, so effect sizes are treated as ordinal/relative, not as literal fold changes; the very large values (up to 15.5) suggest an unconventional or noisy scaling.", "The supplied RNA rows are a filtered, selected DE table (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00 and all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705 positive versus 507 negative entries in two side-by-side workbook blocks), so the apparent global up-shift may be a reporting/truncation asymmetry rather than a true transcriptome-wide shift; enrichment was therefore assessed only relative to other genes inside this table.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level changes are treated as ambiguous and are not used as primary support.", "Metabolite pools (citrate, acetyl-CoA, NAD+/NADH), lipid species, lipid droplets, oxygen consumption and mitochondrial mass were not measured in this dataset and are inferred quantities only.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the precision of both modalities is unknown; astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from a mixed or imperfectly deconvolved population."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia coordinately elevate transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA/anaplerotic enzymes, the malate-aspartate shuttle and the citrate carrier SLC25A1, while glycolytic/pentose-phosphate transcripts are not co-elevated; we propose that the resulting SLC25A1/MPC2-dependent supply of cytosolic acetyl-CoA is the rate-limiting node that drives an SREBF1-associated esterification program (SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, ACAT2/SOAT1) and thereby the APOE4 neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet phenotype, with lysosomal hydrolase induction acting as a downstream compensatory response rather than the primary driver.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the citrate carrier (SLC25A1, e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown) or of the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier (UK5099) should collapse the APOE4-minus-APOE3 difference in neutral-lipid staining (BODIPY/LipidTOX) and in SCD/DGAT1 expression, without equally reducing the APOE3 baseline; if APOE4 lipid excess persists undiminished after effective SLC25A1/MPC blockade, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "13C6-glucose or 13C-pyruvate tracing should show greater M+2 enrichment of citrate and of de-novo palmitate/cholesteryl-ester in APOE4 than APOE3, with no increase (or a decrease) in lactate labelling; equal acetyl-CoA-derived lipid labelling with unchanged lactate would weaken the mechanism.", "Discrimination against a generic mitochondrial-biogenesis explanation: mitochondrial mass markers and maximal respiration should be similar between genotypes, because ETC subunit transcripts are only weakly shifted (mean within-up percentile 0.58, permutation p = 0.16) whereas TCA/carrier/shuttle transcripts are strongly shifted (0.86, p = 1e-4); a uniform APOE4 increase in mtDNA copy number, TOMM20 protein and maximal OCR would favour mitochondrial mass over selective carbon routing.", "Discrimination against a lysosome-primary explanation: acute lysosomal inhibition (bafilomycin A1 or GBA/LIPA inhibition) should increase lipid storage in both genotypes but should not abolish the genotype gap; conversely, if TFEB overexpression fully normalises APOE4 lipid content while citrate export is unchanged, a lysosomal-catabolism bottleneck is the better model.", "Protein-level test: MPC2, SLC25A1, MDH1/GOT1 and SCD protein should be measurably higher in APOE4 microglia by targeted immunoblot; unchanged protein for these carriers despite the large transcript differences would break the link between the measured RNA and the inferred flux."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_131", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 cells show higher transcript levels for mitochondrial pyruvate entry and oxidative decarboxylation machinery (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.50, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB, gene:GLUD1), which we infer, but did not measure, increases pyruvate/glutamate-supported TCA flux.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): The full cytosol-mitochondria redox shuttle set is elevated (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56), which we infer raises malate-aspartate shuttle capacity so cytosolic NAD+ can be regenerated without lactate overflow.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred pool): Elevated gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) together with Step 1/2 is proposed to increase mitochondrial citrate export, making the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool - which was NOT measured here - the rate-limiting node; gene:ACSS2 (+2.93) provides a parallel acetate-derived route. ACLY does not appear in the supplied differential list, so its status is unknown.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred direction of carbon): Glycolytic and oxidative-PPP transcripts are not part of the up-shift (gene:HK2 -3.72, gene:PFKP -3.10, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30), consistent with glucose carbon being routed toward mitochondrial oxidation and citrate export rather than glycolytic/PPP overflow.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred synthetic flux): Downstream of the acetyl-CoA node, an esterification/lipogenic program is elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SOAT1 +1.25) alongside lipid-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50) and post-squalene sterol enzymes (gene:DHCR24 +3.67), which we infer increases triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester synthesis and lipid-droplet load; droplets themselves were not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred compensation): Lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts rise moderately (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.61, gene:TFEB +2.38), interpreted as a secondary catabolic/TFEB-associated response to increased lipid and membrane load rather than the initiating lesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route pyruvate-derived carbon through a citrate-export/malate-aspartate shuttle node into cytosolic acetyl-CoA for lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23935679208359487, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24114417754588424, "cosine_similarity": 0.34555750942778407, "direction_accuracy": 0.21035598705501618, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_131", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6084498381877023, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23935679208359487, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24114417754588424, "cosine_similarity": 0.34555750942778407, "direction_accuracy": 0.21035598705501618, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6084498381877023, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.19082225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 243}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_061", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so all set-level statements are made relative to the internal background of that list (median effect +1.46, 77% positive), not to an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified, so only ranks/directions are interpreted, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "Gene-set memberships used to define the glycolysis-entry, PPP, mitochondrial, lysosomal and sterol modules come from unverified background knowledge (no database retrieval was permitted) and are incomplete for every module.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least in rank order, the corresponding enzyme protein abundance for HK2/PFKP and the mitochondrial module; no protein spot uniquely identifies any of these enzymes, so this link is untested here.", "Enzyme abundance is assumed to constrain pathway flux; no metabolite, respirometry, NADPH, membrane-potential, lipid-droplet or isotope-tracing measurement is present in the supplied data, so all flux, activity, localisation and directional statements are inferences.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; spots are used only as weak, non-unique corroboration of increased lysosomal hydrolase-like and glycolytic/PPP-adjacent spot intensity, never as identified proteins.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic and comparably differentiated, and the astrocyte co-culture composition is assumed similar; replicate numbers were not supplied, so uncertainty in each effect is unknown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally at one metabolic control point: transcripts for the committed cytosolic glucose-entry enzymes (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate arm (PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NAMPT) are selectively below the background of this differential-expression set, while a highly coherent nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative-catabolism module (ETC complexes I-V subunits, TCA enzymes, the pyruvate carrier MPC2, the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1, fatty-acid and amino-acid oxidation entry genes) and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts are selectively above it. We hypothesise that this transcript configuration reflects, and predicts, a shift of carbon flux away from glycolysis/PPP toward lysosome- and lipid-fed mitochondrial oxidation, with citrate export (SLC25A1) feeding cytosolic acetyl-CoA into sterol/neutral-lipid esterification, leaving APOE4 microglia with low glycolytic reserve and low NADPH-regenerating capacity. Causality is not established by these data; the flux, activity and localisation statements are inferences from measured abundances only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in matched isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia, acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or etomoxir plus rotenone should reduce ATP/viability substantially more in APOE4, while 2-deoxyglucose should reduce ATP more in APOE3; if APOE4 is equally or less sensitive to MPC/ETC inhibition and more sensitive to 2-DG, the mechanism is falsified.", "Extracellular flux: APOE4 should show a lower basal and lower maximal (post-oligomycin) ECAR and glycolytic reserve, with a higher OCR/ECAR ratio and higher spare respiratory capacity, than APOE3; equal or higher glycolytic reserve in APOE4 weakens the mechanism.", "Isotope tracing: with U-13C6-glucose, APOE4 should show lower fractional m+2 citrate labelling and lower glucose-derived lactate; with U-13C-palmitate or U-13C-glutamine, higher fractional TCA labelling. Equal glucose-derived citrate labelling across genotypes would weaken step 1 and step 4.", "Rescue specificity: restoring the bottleneck (HK2 overexpression, or membrane-permeant methyl-pyruvate bypass) should normalise the stimulus-induced glycolytic burst and effector output of APOE4 microglia; failure of HK2 restoration to change ECAR or downstream phenotype while OXPHOS inhibitors still act would relocate the bottleneck and weaken the hypothesis.", "Protein-level validation with unambiguous assays (immunoblot or targeted MS, not 2D spots): HK2, PFKP and TALDO1 lower and MPC2, NDUFB8/OXPHOS-cocktail subunits, CTSB/CTSD higher in APOE4; if HK2 and PFKP protein are unchanged or higher despite lower transcripts, the abundance-to-activity assumption fails.", "Downstream lipid readout: APOE4 microglia should contain more neutral lipid/cholesteryl ester (BODIPY, LC-MS) than APOE3, and this excess should be reduced by SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe); no genotype difference in neutral lipid, or no reduction by these inhibitors, would falsify step 5.", "Specificity control: the mitochondrial module elevation should be reproducible in an independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia pair and should not be explained by a global increase in mitochondrial mass alone; if citrate-synthase activity or mtDNA copy number scales with all mitochondrial transcripts and the glycolysis-entry genes are unchanged on re-measurement, the mechanism reduces to non-specific mitochondrial biogenesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (bottleneck, inferred activity from measured RNA): reduced transcript levels of the committed glucose-entry enzymes hexokinase (gene:HK2, gene:HK3) and phosphofructokinase-platelet (gene:PFKP) restrict commitment of glucose to glycolysis in APOE4 microglia, despite unchanged-to-higher transporter and lower-glycolysis transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1), so the constriction is at the ATP-consuming priming steps rather than at glucose uptake.", "Step 2 (inferred): the same node starves the pentose-phosphate arm (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) and NAD(P) supply (gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT), lowering cytosolic NADPH-regenerating capacity; a partly compensatory redox transcript program is co-elevated (gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4, gene:FTH1, gene:UCP2).", "Step 3 (measured abundance): a coordinated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative module is higher in APOE4 across complexes I-V (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFB8, gene:SDHB, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:CYCS, gene:ATP5F1B), the TCA cycle (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD) and mitochondrial carriers (gene:SLC25A46, gene:PRELID3B), which we interpret as increased mitochondrial oxidative capacity, not as measured respiration.", "Step 4 (inferred routing): with glycolytic pyruvate limited, mitochondrial carbon is supplied by (a) the pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating machinery that remain elevated (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD), (b) fatty-acid oxidation entry (gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1) fed by lipid uptake and hydrolysis transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MGLL) and by an elevated lysosomal hydrolase/CLEAR-like program (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A), and (c) glutamate/amino-acid anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1, gene:ABAT).", "Step 5 (inferred disposal of excess acetyl units): elevated citrate export (gene:SLC25A1) with cytosolic acetyl-CoA and sterol/ester machinery (gene:ACSS2, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) directs oxidative overflow into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol synthesis rather than into cytosolic ATP production, predicting neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet accumulation in APOE4.", "Step 6 (functional consequence, untested here): because rapid microglial effector responses require a glycolytic burst, the constricted HK/PFK node predicts blunted stimulus-induced glycolysis and increased dependence on mitochondrial substrate oxidation for ATP in APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are transcriptionally locked into mitochondrial oxidative catabolism with a constricted hexokinase/PFK glucose-entry node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2636432448399365, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2701415336584417, "cosine_similarity": 0.34546944941809193, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_061", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163074433656958, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2636432448399365, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2701415336584417, "cosine_similarity": 0.34546944941809193, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6163074433656958, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1666965, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 244}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_046", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a large global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up) in an unspecified logarithm base; we therefore treat only set-level deviation from that background as evidence, not the raw sign of individual genes.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzymatic capacity; no flux, metabolite, lipid, oxygen-consumption or NADPH measurement is present in these data, so all statements about oxidation, glycolytic flux, lipid droplets, cholesteryl esters and lysosomal load are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Absence of a gene from the list (e.g. ISG15, MX1, STAT1, G6PD, CPT1A, PLIN2, HMGCR) is uninformative about its true change, because the list is selected, not whole-transcriptome.", "The microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes and the transcript pool is assigned to microglia; genotype effects transmitted through astrocytes are not separable here.", "Causal direction is assumed, not established: the data are a single cross-genotype static contrast with no perturbation and no reported replicate structure."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the transcriptional difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is not an interferon-stimulated or NF-kB effector program; instead APOE4 cells show coordinated up-regulation of lipoprotein/sterol uptake, esterification and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts together with the strongest above-background enrichment in TCA-cycle, anaplerotic and electron-transport-chain transcripts, while transcripts for the committed, inducible glycolytic and oxidative-pentose-phosphate steps (HK2, PFKP, HK3, PGD, TALDO1) are among the down-regulated minority. We propose that glucose commitment at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase is the rate-limiting node in APOE4 microglia, so that these cells run on lipid- and amino-acid-derived mitochondrial oxidation and, as an inferred consequence, cannot execute the glycolysis-dependent inflammatory burst even though their pattern-recognition transcripts (TLR2, CD14, MYD88, IRAK4, TICAM1) are elevated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia challenged with LPS or poly(I:C), APOE4 will show a smaller inducible increase in extracellular acidification rate and lactate output and correspondingly lower IL1B/CXCL8/CCL4 and ISG induction, while basal oxygen consumption and the OCR:ECAR ratio are higher in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows an equal or larger glycolytic burst and equal or higher cytokine/ISG induction, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Restoring the bottleneck node should rescue: HK2 (or PFKP) re-expression, or bypassing the block with methyl-pyruvate-independent glycolytic rescue, in APOE4 microglia will restore the LPS-induced glycolytic burst and cytokine output toward APOE3 levels; conversely 2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown in APOE3 will phenocopy the APOE4 low-output state. Failure of HK2/PFKP manipulation to move inflammatory output in either genotype weakens the mechanism.", "Fuel-dependence test: CPT1 inhibition (etomoxir), SCARB1 blockade or lysosomal acid lipase/GBA inhibition will suppress basal oxygen consumption significantly more in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal sensitivity would argue the oxidative program is not lipid-fuelled and would weaken step 2-3.", "Direct lipid measurement (BODIPY/filipin imaging or LC-MS of neutral lipid and cholesteryl esters, none of which is present in these data) will show higher stored neutral lipid and cholesteryl ester per cell in APOE4; no difference would falsify the storage arm.", "Interferon-rejection test: unstimulated APOE4 microglia will not show elevated phospho-STAT1, ISG15/MX1 protein or secreted IFN-beta relative to APOE3. Detection of a clear basal type-I interferon signature would overturn the rejection of the interferon focus and favour an alternative interferon-driven mechanism.", "Normalization control: re-analysis with spike-in or cell-number-anchored normalization will preserve the above-background enrichment of TCA/anaplerotic transcripts (currently Mann-Whitney p = 2.7e-3 vs all listed genes) and the down-regulation of HK2/PFKP. If the enrichment disappears once the global +1.46 shift is corrected, the entire mechanism should be treated as a normalization artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts for lipoprotein and lipid uptake and for sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and esterification (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE); we infer, but did not measure, an increased neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal lipid load.", "A lysosomal-hydrolase and TFEB-associated program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2), which we infer expands lysosomal lipid catabolic capacity and the flux of liberated fatty acids and sphingolipid intermediates to mitochondria; catabolic flux itself was not measured.", "Mitochondrial catabolic capacity transcripts rise coherently and above the list-wide background shift: TCA/anaplerotic (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1, gene:IDH3B, gene:ME1, gene:GLS, gene:ABAT), PDH de-repression (gene:PDP1), citrate/acyl handling (gene:SLC25A1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACSS2, gene:ACOX1, gene:CROT) and ETC/ATP-synthase subunits (gene:NDUFA2, gene:NDUFB2, gene:NDUFB5, gene:SDHB, gene:UQCRB, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX5B, gene:COX6B1, gene:COX6C, gene:COX7A2, gene:COX8A, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:ATP5F1C).", "Concurrently the committed glycolytic and oxidative-PPP steps are down-regulated (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) despite up-regulated glucose transporters and lower glycolytic enzymes (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1, gene:PFKM); we propose hexokinase/PFKP capacity, not glucose supply, as the primary bottleneck, so glucose-6-phosphate commitment and cytosolic NADPH regeneration are inferred to be constrained.", "The inferred consequence is a low-glycolytic, oxidative, lipid-storing steady state. Because the inducible inflammatory burst of myeloid cells requires rapid HK2/PFKB-dependent glycolytic and PPP flux (unverified background knowledge), APOE4 microglia are predicted to convert pattern-recognition input into weaker cytokine and interferon output than APOE3.", "Consistent with this, the mock-state data contain no coherent interferon-stimulated or NF-kB effector signature: only 6 of 38 queried interferon genes appear and all sit at or below the list median (gene:IFI16, gene:TMEM173, gene:IRF8, gene:MNDA, gene:IFNAR1, gene:SIGLEC1), inflammatory effectors are indistinguishable from background, and several execution genes fall (gene:GSDMD, gene:CCL4, gene:RELB, gene:TNFAIP3). We therefore reject interferon or NF-kB activation as the differentiating mechanism and interpret the elevated sensing transcripts (gene:TLR2, gene:CD14, gene:MYD88, gene:IRAK4, gene:TICAM1, gene:PYCARD) as primed sensing with restricted execution."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are locked in a lipid-fuelled oxidative state with a hexokinase/PFKP glycolytic-commitment bottleneck, not in an interferon or NF-kB-driven inflammatory state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2665786655835764, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264688308983687, "cosine_similarity": 0.34511440600878324, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151941747572816, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2665786655835764, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264688308983687, "cosine_similarity": 0.34511440600878324, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6151941747572816, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.62582175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 245}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The unspecified logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is consistent across all rows, so rank/median comparisons between gene sets and the global background are valid even though absolute fold changes cannot be interpreted.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore made relative to the internal background of the 2212 selected genes (median +1.46, 77.1% up), not to an unbiased transcriptome. Genes absent from the list are assumed non-selected, not assumed unchanged.", "The genome-wide positive shift is assumed to be a shared scaling/composition offset that affects nuclear transcripts approximately uniformly in log space, so that the excess of the nuclear-OXPHOS set above that offset reflects a real relative change.", "MT- transcript levels are assumed to be measurable by the 10X Flex probe panel and to be affected by the same per-cell normalisation as nuclear transcripts; if APOE3 and APOE4 differ in mitochondrial read fraction, the MT-down arm could be a normalisation artefact.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the availability of the corresponding subunit for assembly; no OXPHOS protein, mtDNA copy number, complex assembly, respiration, ROS or metabolite measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying evidence only; no protein spot is assigned to an OXPHOS subunit.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect altered astrocyte cross-talk rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "No causal direction is established by these data; the mechanism is a hypothesis about direction, not a demonstrated one."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated up-shift of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (36/36 measured nuclear OXPHOS subunits up; TCA, mitochondrial import and translation genes up above the already-positive background) that is NOT accompanied by the mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits (4/6 MT- transcripts down, including MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4). We hypothesise that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit supply and not glycolytic capacity, is the rate-limiting bottleneck for assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V in APOE4 microglia; because glycolytic genes are not coordinately induced (only 6/9 up, below the 77% genome-wide up-fraction, with mutually contradictory glycolytic protein spots), the cells cannot offset the capped respiratory flux and instead divert TCA-derived carbon (citrate/malate carriers SLC25A1, SLC25A11 up) into an SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1 lipogenic program. All statements about assembly, flux, respiration and causality are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING - complex-resolved assembly: in BN-PAGE/complexome profiling of isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under mock conditions, the ratio of free/sub-assembled nuclear subunits to fully assembled holoenzyme should be higher in APOE4 for complexes I, III, IV and V, while assembled complex II (fully nuclear-encoded) is unchanged or higher. If all five complexes, including complex II, scale up proportionally with the nuclear transcript increase, the mitonuclear-imbalance bottleneck is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING - substrate-resolved respiration: in permeabilised APOE4 microglia, complex I-linked (pyruvate+malate) and complex IV-linked (TMPD/ascorbate) respiration normalised to citrate synthase activity should be reduced relative to APOE3, whereas complex II-linked respiration (succinate + rotenone) should be preserved. Equal reduction of complex II-linked respiration would point to a generic mitochondrial mass/membrane defect and weaken this mechanism.", "Intact-cell bioenergetics: APOE4 microglia should show reduced FCCP-stimulated maximal and spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass with no compensating increase in basal or maximal ECAR / lactate export. Increased glycolytic flux or lactate secretion in APOE4 would falsify step 5 and support a glycolytic-shift alternative instead.", "Rescue: restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression, or nicotinamide-riboside/mitochondrial-translation-supporting intervention that raises MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2 transcript and protein levels) should normalise assembled complex I/IV/V levels and maximal respiration in APOE4 without further changing nuclear subunit transcripts. Failure to restore respiration despite restored MT subunit protein would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Sensitising perturbation: low-dose inhibition of mitochondrial translation (doxycycline or chloramphenicol, mitoribosome-selective doses) should reduce maximal respiration and ATP-linked OCR disproportionately more in APOE4 than APOE3, because APOE4 is predicted to already sit closer to the mtDNA-supply limit. Equal or smaller sensitivity in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Carbon routing: U-13C-glucose and U-13C-glutamine tracing should show, in APOE4, increased 13C enrichment in cytosolic citrate-derived lipid (palmitate, TAG) and unchanged or reduced fractional oxidation to CO2, without increased 13C lactate; ACLY or SLC25A1 inhibition should reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid droplet content toward APOE3. Increased 13C lactate with unchanged lipid labelling would falsify step 6.", "Technical control: recomputing the differential expression after excluding MT- reads and after matching mitochondrial read fraction between genotypes should preserve the nuclear-OXPHOS enrichment above the nuclear background. Loss of that enrichment would indicate a normalisation artefact and falsify the transcript basis of step 1."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred program): APOE4 microglia express an anterograde mitochondrial-biogenesis transcript program - every measured nuclear-encoded subunit of complexes I, III, IV and V is higher in APOE4 (36/36 up, binomial p~8.6e-5 against the 77.1% genome-wide up-fraction; set median +2.64 vs global +1.46, permutation p=0.001), together with TCA enzymes (median +3.74, permutation p=0.002) and mitochondrial import/translation transcripts (TOMM22, TIMM44, TUFM, OXA1L, DARS2).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred imbalance): the mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits are not co-regulated - MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are lower in APOE4 while only MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 are higher (2/6 up, binomial p=0.028), i.e. the two genomes move in opposite directions relative to the global shift. mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial transcription rate and MT protein levels were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck - PRIMARY): because MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 are obligatory catalytic cores of complexes V, III, IV and I, their relative shortfall makes mtDNA-encoded subunit supply the assembly bottleneck; nuclear subunits and assembly factors (NDUFAF4, COA1, COX20, OXA1L all up) accumulate as sub-assemblies rather than holoenzymes. Complex II, which is entirely nuclear-encoded, should escape the bottleneck (SDHB is up, +1.65).", "Step 4 (inferred consequence): incompletely assembled, electron-leaky respiratory chain raises matrix oxidative and proteostatic load; consistent transcript correlates are PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4 and DDIT3 up, and mitochondrial chaperone HSPA9 up. Redox state, ROS and stress-protein levels were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, negative): the cells do not mount a compensating glycolytic program - HK2, HK3, PFKP and PFKFB2 are down while only GPI, PFKM, ENO1, SLC2A1, SLC2A3 and SLC16A1 are up, giving a set median (+2.06) and up-fraction (6/9) at or below the global background, so glycolysis shows no enrichment (permutation p=0.19). Protein spots containing glycolytic candidates are contradictory (protein_spot:038 up, protein_spot:039 down) and are not uniquely identified.", "Step 6 (inferred flux rerouting): with terminal oxidation capped and glycolysis not up-regulated, TCA-cycle carbon is predicted to be exported rather than fully oxidised - citrate and 2-oxoglutarate/malate carriers SLC25A1 and SLC25A11 and the adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5 are up, feeding an active lipogenic and lipid-handling program (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, LDLR, ABCA7, APOE up), which would manifest as neutral-lipid accumulation rather than increased lactate output. No metabolite, lipid or flux measurement is supplied."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: APOE4 microglia raise nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts without matching mtDNA-encoded core subunits, capping oxidative capacity and shunting carbon to lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24707825287229795, "cosine_similarity": 0.3449382649449491, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6139741100323625, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24707825287229795, "cosine_similarity": 0.3449382649449491, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6139741100323625, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.64896375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 246}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_068", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect sizes are reported in an unspecified logarithm base and are preserved as given; conclusions use only relative ordering and comparison to the internal background of the same list.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list is strongly shifted positive (median +1.46, 77% positive, all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so pathway claims are made only relative to that internal background and absence of a gene is treated as uninformative.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly predictive of hydrolase protein synthesis; enzyme activity, lysosomal localisation, luminal pH and lipid flux were not measured and are inferred.", "TFEB/MITF activity is inferred from target-transcript abundance; no nuclear-translocation or mTORC1 measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry a mean of 4.8 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no protein spot alone supports the claim.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex without supplied replicate numbers; ambient RNA and cell-type admixture (for example gene:S100B +6.00) could inflate some effects.", "No lipid, lipidomic or enzyme-activity measurement is present in the supplied data despite the experiment identifier; every sphingolipid pool statement is a prediction, not an observation.", "Causality is not established; the APOE4 versus APOE3 contrast is associative even though the lines are isogenic."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an endolysosomal sphingolipid-turnover state: transcripts for acid sphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1, GBA2, SUMF1) and for lysosome-biogenesis/acidification machinery are coordinately elevated far above the already-positive background of this selected DE list, while the de novo sphingolipid-synthesis arm is not co-induced and the cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript falls. We hypothesise that the flux-limiting step is luminal catabolism of glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin delivered as membrane and lipoprotein cargo, and that hydrolase delivery via M6P-dependent routing does not scale with the transcriptional response, so measured transcript induction is a compensatory readout of unmet degradative demand rather than of achieved degradative flux. All lipid pools, enzyme activities, localisations and directions of causation here are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (cargo versus synthesis): in APOE4 microglia, inhibiting de novo sphingolipid synthesis (myriocin against serine palmitoyltransferase, or eliglustat/PPMP against UGCG) will fail to normalise lysosomal glucosylceramide/GM2 load or the GBA/HEXA/CTSB/TFEB-target transcript elevation (\u003c25% reduction), whereas restricting extracellular lipid cargo (lipoprotein-depleted medium, astrocyte-conditioned-medium withdrawal, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade) will reduce both by \u003e=50%. The reverse outcome - normalisation by UGCG or SPT inhibition and no effect of cargo restriction - would falsify the cargo-load premise of steps 1, 3 and 4.", "Flux versus transcript scaling: mature GBA and HEXA/HEXB activity per LAMP1-positive lysosome in APOE4 will rise sub-proportionally to their transcript fold changes (activity ratio well below the transcript ratio) and acid-hydrolase activity in conditioned medium will be higher in APOE4 than APOE3. If lysosomal enzyme activity scales proportionally with transcript and no extracellular hydrolase increase is seen, the routing bottleneck in step 5 is weakened.", "Rescue by bypassing routing: uptake of M6P-tagged recombinant glucocerebrosidase (imiglucerase/velaglucerase), or M6PR re-expression, will lower lysosomal glucosylceramide/GM2 and blunt CLEAR-target transcripts in APOE4 without changing APOE genotype; no reduction in lipid load or CLEAR transcripts would weaken steps 5 and 6.", "Transcription-factor dependence: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia will abolish the coordinated hydrolase induction (GBA, HEXA, CTSB) and further increase lysosomal sphingolipid retention; persistence of the hydrolase induction after TFEB loss would falsify step 2.", "Specificity control: the same hydrolase and routing signature should be reproducible as protein-level and activity-level differences in an independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia pair under mock treatment; failure to reproduce, or an equally strong signature in matched non-lysosomal gene sets after correcting for the global positive shift, would indicate the pattern is an artefact of the selected, upward-shifted DE list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and sterol handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1). We infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of sphingolipid-rich membrane and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system of astrocyte-co-cultured microglia.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred transcription-factor activity): A lysosome-biogenesis (CLEAR-type) program is transcriptionally elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DPP7). TFEB/MITF nuclear localisation and activity are inferred from target-gene abundance only.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): Within that program the sphingolipid-directed acid hydrolases are the most strongly elevated arm (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:SUMF1 +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53), consistent with increased demand for glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin degradation.", "Step 4 (measured absence, inferred): The de novo synthesis arm is not co-induced - SPTLC1, SPTLC2, SPTSSA, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1, SGMS2 do not appear in this selected DE list, and only gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:ST3GAL5 change modestly. We therefore attribute the sphingolipid pressure to catabolic/cargo load rather than to increased synthesis; because the list is a selected DE result, absence is weak evidence.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Hydrolase-delivery machinery is remodelled discordantly - gene:GNPTG +3.02 (M6P tagging) and gene:IGF2R +2.02 rise while gene:M6PR -1.72 falls, with endosome-to-Golgi retrieval components up (gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:RAB7A +2.65). We infer that a fraction of newly made hydrolase is mis-routed or secreted, so mature lysosomal enzyme does not increase in proportion to transcript.", "Step 6 (inferred state): The predicted net state is chronic retention of glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin in late endosomes/lysosomes of APOE4 microglia with persistent CLEAR-gene induction. Cross-modality protein-spot data are ambiguous and directionally split (protein_spot:027 +0.58, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38), which is compatible with, but does not demonstrate, a redistribution rather than a uniform increase of cathepsin/hexosaminidase-family protein forms."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB-type lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolism program without matched de novo synthesis or mannose-6-phosphate routing capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12933259078906975, "cosine_similarity": 0.3447331143745903, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6162168284789644, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1095890410958904, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12933259078906975, "cosine_similarity": 0.3447331143745903, "direction_accuracy": 0.18284789644012944, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6162168284789644, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.53918975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 247}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_006", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every supplied RNA effect has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base); all module claims are therefore made relative to that internal background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene from the file means 'not in the supplied selection', not 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effect sizes (protein in log2) are not placed on a common scale.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used to assert the abundance of a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a readout of transcriptional output only; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, luminal localisation, TFEB nuclear translocation and degradative flux are inferred and unmeasured.", "No lipid, lipidomic, imaging, flux or activity measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier referring to lipid; all lipid-pool statements are predictions.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so a cell-autonomous APOE4 effect in microglia is assumed but not demonstrated by these data; astrocyte-derived lipoprotein differences are an untested alternative source of the cargo term.", "Causality is not established by this observational isogenic comparison; direction of the proposed chain is hypothesis, not result."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally through an endolysosomal degradative bottleneck: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases that clear sphingolipid, glycoconjugate and glycogen/lipoprotein-derived cargo (GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, MAN2B1) rise coordinately together with TFEB and MITF, which we interpret as a compensatory CLEAR-network response to undegraded luminal substrate rather than as evidence of restored degradative flux; the accompanying rise in sterol/neutral-lipid esterification and SREBP-pathway transcripts (SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS) is predicted to divert the excess lipid into stored cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol pools. A type I interferon or canonical inflammatory-priming mechanism is explicitly rejected as the primary driver because interferon-associated transcripts are not enriched above the strongly up-shifted background of this pre-filtered differential-expression list.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: culture APOE4 and APOE3 microglia in lipoprotein-depleted medium (or block SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake). If the bottleneck is hydrolytic capacity, APOE4 lysosomes should retain excess sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid and cholesteryl ester relative to APOE3 even at matched reduced influx, while the acid-hydrolase and TFEB transcript excess only partially normalises. If instead lipid load and the whole hydrolase/TFEB signature collapse to APOE3 levels under lipoprotein depletion, the bottleneck is cargo influx and this mechanism is wrong.", "Enzyme-activity versus transcript test: measured GBA, HEXA/B, SMPD1 and cathepsin activities per lysosome in APOE4 should increase sub-proportionally to their transcript increases. Activity gains matching or exceeding transcript gains, with normal DQ-BSA and BODIPY-LDL degradation kinetics, would weaken the capacity-limitation step.", "TFEB-dependence test: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower the hydrolase transcripts and further increase LysoTracker/Filipin/BODIPY lysosomal lipid load; conversely, TFEB overexpression or an hydrolase-augmenting intervention should reduce stored lipid. No change in lipid load in either direction would weaken steps 3-4.", "Storage-routing test: SOAT1 (ACAT1) inhibition in APOE4 should shift cholesterol from cholesteryl-ester droplets to free sterol and further raise the hydrolase/TFEB transcript signature; if cholesteryl-ester content and the transcript signature are both unaffected, step 6 fails.", "Interferon rejection test: IFNAR1 blockade or JAK1/2 inhibition should leave the APOE4 hydrolase/TFEB transcript excess and the predicted lipid load essentially unchanged. If JAK inhibition normalises the lysosomal-lipid program, an interferon-driven mechanism would supersede this hypothesis.", "Protein-level test: two-dimensional or targeted immunoblot separation of cathepsin B/D pro- and mature forms should show a redistribution (shifted pro:mature ratio) in APOE4 rather than a uniform abundance rise; a uniform proportional rise in mature hydrolase protein with unchanged processing would weaken step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 changes the lipoprotein/lipid cargo delivered to the microglial endolysosome (inferred, not measured here); transcripts of lipid- and debris-uptake receptors are modestly higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), but this set is not enriched relative to the global up-shift, so cargo influx is a weak, non-established input rather than an observation.", "Luminal hydrolysis of sphingolipid, glycosphingolipid and glycoconjugate cargo becomes rate-limiting relative to that load. This is the proposed primary bottleneck; it is an inferred flux limitation, not a measured pool.", "Sensing of undegraded luminal cargo is proposed to relieve mTORC1-dependent restraint of MiT/TFE factors, consistent with the measured increase in gene:TFEB and gene:MITF transcripts (transcript abundance measured; nuclear localisation and transcription-factor activity are inferred, not observed).", "A CLEAR-type transcriptional output raises acid-hydrolase and lysosome-membrane transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:RAB7A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and endosomal sorting components (gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L). Measured: transcripts. Inferred: enzyme activity per lysosome.", "Compensation is proposed to be incomplete because hydrolase delivery and maturation are not uniformly increased (gene:M6PR is decreased and gene:CTSS and gene:IDS are decreased despite the overall induction), so measured transcript gain is predicted to translate sub-proportionally into luminal enzymatic activity.", "Persisting undegraded sterol and lipid is routed to esterified storage rather than efflux, consistent with higher gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS and gene:ABCA7 transcripts; the resulting lipid-droplet load is a predicted, unmeasured pool.", "The end state is a lipid-laden, storage-biased microglial phenotype (gene:ITGAX, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:FTH1 transcripts higher in APOE4) whose degradative reserve is consumed at baseline, without a coordinated interferon program."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal luminal hydrolytic capacity, not by interferon signalling: a TFEB/CLEAR-associated acid-hydrolase compensation with sterol re-esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11823211772223244, "cosine_similarity": 0.34434613038306944, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6409546925566343, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11823211772223244, "cosine_similarity": 0.34434613038306944, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6409546925566343, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.3377155, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 248}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_013", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source; all statements use the reported values as-is and only rank/direction comparisons within the supplied set, never a converted fold change.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; source_row ordering shows two blocks (rows 2-601 roughly balanced 54% up, rows 602-1709 exclusively up), so all enrichment statistics quoted here are rank-based permutations computed inside the balanced block against the supplied genes as background.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features; a spot is treated as evidence about a mixture, never as a uniquely identified cathepsin, HEXB, ACP2 or ATP6V1E1 protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme protein; the whole hypothesis rests on the assumption that mRNA rise without matched mature-enzyme rise is real and not a spot-resolution artifact.", "TFEB/MITF transcriptional activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolytic flux, lysosomal cholesterol and lipid-droplet content, autophagic flux and cargo load are all unmeasured in this dataset and are inferred quantities.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous consequences of APOE4 astrocyte lipid handling; the comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so no ligand-driven activation is assumed.", "GRN, PSAP, NPC1, LAMP2, CD63, MCOLN1, LIPA, ASAH1, CTSL, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B, PLIN2, ABCA1, HMGCR and SQLE are absent from the supplied rows, so key parts of the pathway are untested rather than unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated increase in transcripts for endolysosomal cargo uptake, acidification and acid-hydrolase machinery (TFEB, MITF, v-ATPase subunits, GAA/GBA/HEXA/HEXB/SMPD1/NAGLU/CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, SLC38A7, SLC17A5, RAB7A, AP5M1/AP5Z1) that is NOT matched at the level of mature hydrolase protein spots and that is accompanied by reduced mannose-6-phosphate sorting-receptor (M6PR) and CTSS transcripts; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is delivery/maturation of functional hydrolase into acidified lysosomes relative to cargo influx, so that transcriptional lysosome biogenesis is compensatory rather than corrective and downstream sterol sensing (SREBP-target transcripts) reports lipid that is retained in the endolysosomal system rather than metabolically accessible. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript and spot measurements are correlative.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring hydrolase delivery without touching biogenesis - CD-MPR/M6PR re-expression, or feeding cells M6P-tagged recombinant hydrolase (e.g. GBA or cathepsin D) - should increase measured degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching rate, Magic Red cathepsin B) and clearance of a defined cargo (fluorescent myelin, oxLDL, BODIPY-LDL) in APOE4 back toward APOE3, and should lower SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1), while TFEB overexpression alone should NOT correct clearance. If TFEB overexpression corrects clearance and M6PR restoration does not, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Per-cell DQ-BSA/Magic-Red degradation rate in APOE4 should be equal to or lower than APOE3 despite the large positive CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA and GAA transcript differences; if degradation rate rises roughly in proportion to those transcripts, the capacity-mismatch claim is falsified.", "Immunoblot of mature versus pro-forms: APOE4 should show unchanged or reduced mature cathepsin D/B heavy chain with an increased pro-form:mature ratio and increased pro-hydrolase secreted into conditioned medium, plus reduced M6PR protein. Proportional increases in mature enzyme would weaken the mechanism.", "Lysosomal pH (ratiometric probe) in APOE4 should be equal to or higher (less acidic) than APOE3 despite higher v-ATPase subunit transcripts; measurably more acidic APOE4 lysosomes with higher flux would falsify the acidification-capacity part of step 2/3.", "Sterol-sensing test: cyclodextrin or an NPC-bypass treatment should normalise SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, ACAT2, HMGCS1) in APOE4 within 24 h if those transcripts report endolysosomally trapped cholesterol; no response would mean step 5 is driven by something else (e.g. an APOE4 lipoprotein secretion defect) and that step should be discarded.", "Specificity control against the alternative mitochondrial explanation: if inhibiting cargo uptake (blocking SCARB1/CD36 or phagocytosis) normalises the lysosomal and SREBP transcript modules but leaves the OXPHOS/TCA transcript module elevated, the endolysosomal bottleneck is upstream; if instead the OXPHOS module normalises first and the lysosomal module does not, the primary bottleneck should be reassigned to mitochondrial substrate handling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/particle uptake and opsonin receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:C1QA/B/C; balanced-block rank-enrichment p=0.035), which we infer - but do not measure - increases the rate of cargo delivery into early and late endosomes.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): a lysosome-biogenesis-type transcript program is coordinately higher in APOE4 - gene:TFEB and gene:MITF, all measured v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C; p=0.007), acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK; p=0.0004) and luminal transporters (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5). Nuclear TFEB/MITF activity is inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (measured, discordant): the hydrolase-delivery arm moves the other way - gene:M6PR (CD-MPR) and gene:IDS are decreased and gene:CTSS is strongly decreased - and the 2-D protein spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins, HEXB, ACP2 or ATP6V1E1 show no coherent increase (significant decreases at protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:086 against increases at protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057). We infer that the pool of correctly sorted, proteolytically matured luminal hydrolase does not scale with the mRNA increase; spot identity is ambiguous, so this is an inference, not an identified-protein measurement.", "Step 4 (inferred activity/flux, not measured): the mismatch between step 1 (influx) and step 3 (mature luminal hydrolytic capacity per compartment) makes intraluminal cargo processing the bottleneck; undegraded lipid/glycoconjugate cargo is predicted to accumulate in an expanded but under-equipped endolysosomal compartment. No lipid, pH, LysoTracker or degradation-flux measurement is present in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred cause): sterol/lipogenic transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1; balanced-block p=0.0018), the pattern expected if ER sterol sensors report low accessible cholesterol while cholesterol is retained upstream in the endolysosome; re-esterification/storage enzymes (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) divert this lipid to stored esters instead of clearance.", "Step 6 (systems consequence): continued receptor-mediated influx plus compensatory biogenesis without matched luminal capacity produces a self-sustaining cargo backlog; the coordinate rise in mitochondrial/TCA-OXPHOS transcripts is interpreted here as a parallel or downstream catabolic adjustment, not as the primary bottleneck."], "title": "In APOE4 microglia a TFEB/MITF-type lysosome-biogenesis transcript program outruns delivery of mature luminal hydrolases, making per-lysosome cargo processing the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1226853033073835, "cosine_similarity": 0.34357945055977257, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6379773462783171, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1226853033073835, "cosine_similarity": 0.34357945055977257, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6379773462783171, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.929737, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 249}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_069", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no |effect| below 1; 77% positive; median +1.46), so all enrichment statements are relative to that biased list background and not to an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified and magnitudes are used only as ranks/directions.", "Transcript abundance of endolysosomal genes is taken as a proxy for compartment expansion; hydrolase activity, luminal pH, compartment volume, cargo flux and localization are inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features (ACTB appears in 25 of 92 spots), so no spot is treated as a unique protein readout; spot changes may reflect proteoform/pI shifts rather than total abundance.", "The measured population is a genotype comparison in astrocyte co-culture; differences in cell composition, capture efficiency or library normalisation between APOE4 and APOE3 samples could generate part of the global positive shift and are not excluded by these data.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, ABCA1, lysosomal cholesterol, lipid droplets, phagocytic rate) were not measured here; they are predictions, not observations.", "Correlation between the RNA module shift and any lipid phenotype is assumed, not demonstrated; no causal direction is established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinate transcriptional expansion of the endocytic/lysosomal degradative module (v-ATPase subunits, luminal hydrolases, RAB7A, retromer/retriever, ESCRT, sorting nexins, TFEB) that is NOT accompanied by a proportional increase in the cortical actomyosin internalization arm or in transcripts for lysosomal sterol egress; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is resolution/egress of lipidic cargo from the late endosome-lysosome, which keeps ER sterol sensing in a 'deprived' state and sustains SREBP-directed lipid synthesis and uptake transcripts, producing a futile influx-versus-clearance cycle and lipid storage. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should selectively lower filipin-positive lysosomal unesterified cholesterol in APOE4 and normalise SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, DHCR24, HMGCS1, LDLR, SCARB1) toward APOE3, while leaving most hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, GAA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) still elevated. If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal sterol but SREBP targets remain APOE4-high, the egress-bottleneck ordering is wrong and a primary lipogenic (ER-first) drive is favoured.", "Pulse-chase of a fluorogenic/lipidic cargo (DQ-BSA, TopFluor-cholesterol myelin or oxLDL): APOE4 should show equal or LOWER initial internalisation rate per cell (consistent with an un-upregulated actomyosin arm) but LONGER cargo residence and higher steady-state LysoTracker/lysosome volume. Observation of faster internalisation together with normal cargo residence in APOE4 would weaken steps 2-3.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module without correcting lipid accumulation if egress is limiting; correction of lipid load by TFEB knockdown alone would weaken the bottleneck assignment.", "Bafilomycin A1 or a cathepsin-B/D inhibitor should NOT further increase APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid storage proportionally if hydrolysis is already in excess of egress; a strongly super-additive lipid increase would indicate hydrolysis, not egress, was near-limiting.", "Restoring the uptake arm (constitutively active RAC1 or forced ARPC/actin expression) should increase internalisation in APOE4 but should NOT normalise lysosomal lipid load; normalisation of lipid load by this manipulation alone would falsify the egress bottleneck and support a cytoskeletal primary defect.", "GENERAL WEAKENING RESULT: if the endolysosomal module shift disappears when tested against a full unbiased transcriptome background with matched expression-level and detection controls, or if unbiased quantitative proteomics shows no increase in LAMP1/v-ATPase/cathepsin protein in APOE4, the mechanism's foundation is removed."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred compartment state): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels across an endolysosomal machinery module (regex-defined set of 73 genes, median reported logFC +2.21 vs +1.46 for the whole selected list, Mann-Whitney p = 4.0e-5), including acidification (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:DPP7), maturation/sorting (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS37B, gene:SNX3, gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:PIK3C3) and the lysosomal-biogenesis factor gene:TFEB. We infer an enlarged or transcriptionally stressed late-endosome/lysosome compartment; compartment volume, pH, hydrolase activity and flux were not measured.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): The cortical actomyosin/Rho arm that builds phagocytic cups and macropinosomes is not coordinately raised (regex-defined 40-gene cytoskeletal set, median +1.37, Mann-Whitney p = 0.29 vs the same background), with several core components among the most negative rows in an otherwise 77%-positive list (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:CORO2A) against only modest Arp2/3 increases (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC5). We therefore reject the variant of this focus in which APOE4 microglia simply up-tune phagocytic/actin uptake machinery.", "STEP 3 (inferred bottleneck): Within the up-shifted lysosomal module, the components required to move hydrolysed lipid out of the lumen and to resolve endosomal tubules are the laggards: gene:NPC2 (+1.17, 35th percentile of the list, lowest of the lysosomal set), gene:WASHC4 (-2.10, WASH-complex-dependent retromer tubule scission) and gene:VPS13B (-4.65, bulk lipid transfer). We hypothesise that sterol/sphingolipid egress from the LE/Lys lumen, not hydrolysis or acidification, is the limiting step. NPC1, ABCA1 and lysosomal lipid content are not present in these data and are not claimed as observed.", "STEP 4 (inferred signalling consequence): Restricted egress keeps ER/ Golgi sterol sensors in a low-sterol state, so SREBP-directed transcripts stay high despite lipid load: gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, plus lipid-uptake and neutral-lipid genes gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2. Sterol-sensor occupancy and SREBP cleavage are inferred, not measured.", "STEP 5 (predicted phenotype): Continued influx/synthesis (STEP 4) into a compartment that cannot export (STEP 3) with no compensatory increase in uptake machinery (STEP 2) yields a net APOE4 state of lysosomal lipid storage plus cytoplasmic neutral-lipid accumulation and reduced surveillance/uptake dynamics, rather than a genuinely higher clearance flux. No lipid species were measured in the supplied data.", "STEP 6 (protein-level caveat as part of the model): Spot-level 2-D data do not corroborate a proportional rise in mature hydrolase or v-ATPase protein (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 contain CTSB/CTSD and are down; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 contain ATP6V1E1 and are down), which the model accommodates as post-transcriptional or proteoform-level limitation of the same egress-limited compartment; these spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand endolysosomal degradative machinery without matching cargo-egress or uptake capacity, making late-endosome/lysosome lipid resolution the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1350293542074364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11893955334552365, "cosine_similarity": 0.34301045114403234, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6178608414239483, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1350293542074364, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11893955334552365, "cosine_similarity": 0.34301045114403234, "direction_accuracy": 0.22330097087378642, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6178608414239483, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3919275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 250}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_046", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive); absent genes (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, NPC1, all classical ISGs) are unknown, not unchanged, and program calls rest on represented members only.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects are used only as signed, ranked magnitudes on their original reported scale; the strongly positive list-wide sign bias is used as the comparison background instead of an assumed 50/50 split.", "Coordinate transcript elevation of CLEAR and SREBP target sets is taken as evidence of upstream TFEB/MITF and SREBP pathway engagement; neither transcription-factor activity, nuclear localization, nor proteolytic processing was measured.", "Lysosomal, droplet and ER sterol pools, cholesteryl-ester content, lipid-droplet number, degradative flux and fatty-acid oxidation rate were not measured in this dataset; their states are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (ACTB in 25 spots, keratins frequent), so no spot is attributed to a single protein; spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Transcript-level differences are assumed to reflect the co-cultured microglial population rather than differing cell-composition or normalization between APOE4 and APOE3 samples; extreme effects (|effect| \u003e 5, n = 172) tend to have weaker adjusted p-values and may reflect sparsely detected genes.", "Genes within a program are not statistically independent, so the descriptive coherence reported here is not a formal enrichment result."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by inflammatory or interferon activation but by an altered lipid-routing state: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase and the TFEB-MITF CLEAR program, for SREBP-dependent sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and lipoprotein uptake/esterification, and for TCA/OXPHOS carbon disposal are coordinately elevated, indicating that acquired lipid is routed into lysosomal and esterified storage pools while the ER regulatory sterol pool is sensed as insufficient, so acquisition programs stay on and the lysosomal compartment expands. Interferon and inflammatory programs are not represented in the selected differential list, so the assigned inflammatory/interferon focus is rejected as the primary mechanism. This is an inferred routing/set-point change; no lipid, flux, localization or transcription-factor activity was measured here, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating perturbation: in mock-treated APOE4 microglia, blocking cholesterol esterification (SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor, e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 should raise the ER-accessible sterol pool and, within 24-48 h, reduce SREBP2/SREBF1 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, SCD, LSS) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the CLEAR hydrolase set (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA, ATP6V1A) elevated or increased. If SREBP targets stay high (or fall equally in APOE3), the 'sensing-low because sterol is routed to storage' step is wrong.", "Prospective: filipin/cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid imaging in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 should show higher esterified/lysosomal sterol with an unchanged or lower ER-accessible pool (e.g. by a sterol biosensor or SREBP2 cleavage assay). Finding equal total and ER-accessible sterol with equal SREBP2 cleavage would falsify the mechanism and favour simple increased throughput.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation and, if the routing model holds, further increase esterified lipid and SREBP targets; if hydrolase transcripts are TFEB-independent, step 2 is misattributed.", "Prospective challenge test (reserve versus ongoing defect): after a myelin-debris or oxLDL load, APOE4 microglia should show slower cargo degradation (DQ-BSA / myelin clearance) and greater droplet accumulation than APOE3 despite their higher baseline hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance kinetics would show the baseline state is successful adaptation, not reduced reserve.", "Prospective negative control for the assigned focus: neither genotype should show induction of ISG transcripts (ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1, OAS1, STAT1) or IFN-beta secretion under mock; detection of a robust APOE4 ISG signature, or loss of the lipid phenotype after JAK or STING inhibition, would show that interferon signalling, not lipid routing, is primary.", "Prospective: fatty-acid oxidation and TCA flux (13C tracing, oxygen-consumption rate) should be higher in APOE4; if oxidation is instead lower despite elevated OGDH/MDH1/MPC2 transcripts, the disposal step must be replaced by a mitochondrial bottleneck model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred from measured transcripts): APOE4 changes the handling of ApoE-associated lipid in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and esterification transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:NPC2 +1.17), consistent with cargo being directed toward endolysosomal and esterified/droplet pools rather than to the ER regulatory sterol pool.", "Step 2 (measured, transcript level): the endolysosomal-degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded - the CLEAR regulators gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) and a broad hydrolase/v-ATPase/transport set rise (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:LAMP1 +1.38), i.e. increased demand signalling on the lysosome, not a transcriptional loss of hydrolase capacity.", "Step 3 (inferred activity, not measured): because sterol is held in lysosomal/esterified pools, ER sterol sensing under-reports and the SREBP branch remains active, sustaining synthesis and uptake (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06) - a combination not expected of a cell that simply senses itself lipid-replete.", "Step 4 (measured, transcript level): carbon liberated by lipolysis/hydrolysis is directed to mitochondrial oxidation and citrate export that can feed lipogenesis (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:CYCS +2.58, gene:COX6C +2.17, gene:NDUFB2 +2.11, gene:SDHB +1.65), so the state is high-throughput lipid cycling rather than a simple catabolic block.", "Step 5 (state-level consequence): the cell settles into a lipid-storage-biased, mildly activated microglial identity (gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CLEC7A +1.46, gene:FTH1 +2.53, gene:CD74 +3.84) with loss of selected effector/trophic transcripts (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:RELB -1.30, gene:TNFAIP3 -1.05), while type-I/II interferon effectors are absent from the differential list and cytokine transcripts are mixed - the change is metabolic routing, not immune activation.", "Step 6 (prospective, not established here): the futile acquisition-plus-storage loop consumes lysosomal and mitochondrial reserve, so a defect in clearance capacity should appear only when the cells are given an additional lipid or phagocytic load; the mock condition shows the altered set point, not a demonstrated ongoing clearance failure."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a sterol-'sensing-low' lipid-storage state: lysosomal/CLEAR expansion plus sustained SREBP-driven acquisition and mitochondrial disposal of lipid, without interferon or NF-kB induction"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2382029317283905, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24506907843320008, "cosine_similarity": 0.34296461251632365, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6110064724919093, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2382029317283905, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24506907843320008, "cosine_similarity": 0.34296461251632365, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6110064724919093, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0848325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 60}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression selection (no effects between -1 and +1; 77% positive; median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base), so only ranks relative to that shifted background, not absolute magnitudes or the fact of being 'up', are treated as evidence.", "Transcript ranks for hydrolases, SCARB1 and SREBP-2 targets are assumed to track protein and activity for those gene products; no hydrolase activity, SREBP-2 cleavage, or transport assay was supplied.", "The SREBP-2-type signature is assumed to report ER-accessible sterol rather than a generic growth or maturation program; SREBF1 and SCD up mean a lipogenic/SREBP-1 component cannot be excluded.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin and actin; no spot is treated as identifying a specific lysosomal or sterol protein.", "Cells were pseudobulk-profiled from microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so ambient or contaminating astrocyte RNA (relevant to SCARB1, APOE, A2M, S100B, all up) is assumed not to dominate the signal - an assumption the data cannot test.", "Genotype is assumed to act cell-autonomously in microglia; astrocyte-mediated indirect effects of APOE4 are not excluded.", "No causal direction is established: the ordering of uptake, lysosomal expansion and sterol sensing is a proposal, not an observation."], "claim": "In mock-treated iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia, transcripts encoding lysosomal luminal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits and the sterol-uptake receptor SCARB1 are among the most strongly elevated in the supplied differential-expression set (median rank ~92nd-99th percentile of a background that is itself globally shifted upward), whereas the transcripts for the direct lysosomal cholesterol-export/handoff machinery that is present in the data (NPC2, OSBPL1A) sit at or below the background median and OSBPL8 is one of the few downregulated genes. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is the transfer of lysosome-derived cholesterol into the ER-accessible pool: sterol acquisition and lysosomal catabolic capacity are increased without a matched increase in egress capacity, so the ER sterol sensor reads 'sterol-poor' and sustains SREBP-2-type target expression (LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, all up) while incoming sterol and fatty acid are shunted into esters and droplets (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD up). This is a hypothesis about lipid distribution and flux; only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and no cholesterol pool, transport rate, or causal direction has been demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (route-of-delivery test): loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with cholesterol by a lysosome-independent route (methyl-beta-cyclodextrin:cholesterol, or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1, DHCR24) to the same degree in both genotypes, whereas loading via LDL/acetyl-LDL, which requires lysosomal egress, should suppress them substantially less in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal suppression by both routes, or greater LDL-driven suppression in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Pool-distribution test: quantitative imaging or probe-based assays (filipin plus an ALOD4/D4H accessible-cholesterol probe, with lysosome co-label) should show, in APOE4, higher lysosome-associated cholesterol and a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio with an unchanged or lower ER/PM-accessible pool, despite equal or higher total cholesterol. Finding a lower total and lower lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4 would instead favour a synthesis or uptake deficit and falsify the egress-bottleneck claim.", "Bottleneck-relief test: increasing egress capacity (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC2/ORP1L/StARD3 re-expression) should normalise the SREBP-2 target signature and lower lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4 without reducing hydrolase transcripts; if the SREBP-2 signature persists after cholesterol is released from lysosomes, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Sink test: SOAT1 inhibition should raise free cholesterol and further suppress SREBP-2 targets in APOE3 but produce a blunted response in APOE4 if egress, not esterification, is limiting; a fully equal response in both genotypes would argue the difference lies in the esterification sink rather than in lysosomal egress.", "Corroboration test for step 2: immunoblot and enzymatic assays (GAA, GBA, HEXA/B, CTSB, CTSD) should show increased lysosomal hydrolase protein and activity in APOE4; the supplied 2D-gel spots that list cathepsins or v-ATPase subunits among their candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:064 down), so unchanged hydrolase protein and activity on clean assays would weaken step 2 and with it the whole chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (acquisition capacity, measured as RNA): APOE4 microglia raise sterol-acquisition transcripts, most strikingly SCARB1 (99.1st percentile of the supplied effects) with LDLR and APOE also up; we infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesteryl ester to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (degradative compartment expansion, measured as RNA; activity inferred): a coherent block of luminal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts is elevated far above the global shift (GAA, CTSK, ATP6V1H, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, CTSD, HEXB, GLA, MAN2B1, SUMF1; set median 92nd percentile, Mann-Whitney p=7e-6 versus all supplied RNA rows) together with TFEB and RAB7A, consistent with an enlarged, catabolically loaded late-endosome/lysosome; hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck, inferred): the machinery that hands cholesterol from the lysosomal lumen/limiting membrane to ER contact sites does not scale with steps 1-2. NPC2 (34.7th percentile) and OSBPL1A (25.6th) are below the background median and OSBPL8 is negative (12.7th percentile), while NPC1, STARD3, GRAMD1/Aster and ABCA1/ABCG1 rows are absent from the supplied set. Concurrent up-regulation of the soluble sterol carrier SCP2 (96.3rd percentile) is read as demand for non-vesicular sterol movement rather than as evidence that egress succeeds.", "Step 4 (sensing consequence, inferred activity from measured RNA): a persistently low ER-accessible sterol pool keeps SCAP-SREBP-2 processing active, giving the observed uniformly positive SREBP-2-type target set (10/10 up: HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, SREBF2, plus SREBF1), i.e. the cell keeps signalling 'make and import more' although total cellular sterol need not be low.", "Step 5 (storage sink, measured as RNA): sterol and fatty acid that do reach the cytosolic compartment are esterified and stored rather than made available to membranes, consistent with SOAT1, DGAT1 and SCD up; this closes a futile acquire-esterify-store loop that cannot relieve the ER sensor.", "Step 6 (downstream state, inferred): the resulting lipid-laden, oxysterol-generating state (CH25H, CYP27A1 up) coexists with a mildly raised inflammatory tone (CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3, TLR2 up) and is proposed to be the cell-autonomous difference between APOE4 and APOE3 microglia under mock treatment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand the lysosomal hydrolase compartment but do not scale lysosome-to-ER sterol egress, leaving the ER-accessible cholesterol pool low and a futile acquire-and-store sterol program on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2391814053096038, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26293804853325536, "cosine_similarity": 0.3426065707471735, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6301067961165049, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2391814053096038, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26293804853325536, "cosine_similarity": 0.3426065707471735, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6301067961165049, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7269935, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 251}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_043", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adj-p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive) on an unspecified log base; program directions are interpreted against that 77%-up background, and genes absent from the list are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Coordinated transcript increase of CLEAR-type targets together with gene:TFEB and gene:MITF is taken as evidence of transcription-factor pathway engagement; TFEB nuclear localization, mTORC1 status and promoter occupancy were not measured.", "Every protein spot retains all listed candidate identities; no spot is treated as measuring a single protein, and directional disagreement between spots sharing a candidate (e.g. CTSD in protein_spot:053 up and protein_spot:069 down) is interpreted only as proteoform ambiguity.", "Higher endolysosomal cargo load, lysosomal sterol sequestration, lipid-droplet content, lysosomal pH, hydrolase maturation state and degradative flux are inferred, not observed; measured values are RNA abundance and 2-D spot abundance only.", "The mock condition is assumed unstressed; any reduced degradative reserve would be revealed only by a future cargo challenge and is not claimed as an ongoing defect here.", "APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic as stated, so line-of-origin and maturation-stage differences are assumed not to be the sole driver of the coordinated program; this is not verifiable from the supplied data.", "No causal direction is established; the uptake-receptor step rests on sign consistency (19/19) whose amplitude does not exceed the selected-list background."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, high-amplitude transcriptional expansion of the endolysosomal degradative apparatus (TFEB/MITF, acid hydrolases, M6P tagging, every represented v-ATPase subunit, lysosomal membrane transporters, RAB7A/retromer/ESCRT sorting) occurring together with induction of sterol synthesis and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification rather than efflux; the pattern is best read as a demand-driven expansion response to lipid-rich endolysosomal cargo, in which increased transcript supply is not matched by a coherent increase in mature hydrolase or v-ATPase V1 proteoforms in the 2-D spot layer. Increased degradative flux, lysosomal acidity and cargo clearance were not measured, so neither increased capacity nor an ongoing degradation defect is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: pulse-chase APOE4 and APOE3 microglia (mock) with DQ-BSA and with pHrodo/BODIPY-labelled lipoprotein or myelin, normalizing degradation signal to internalized cargo and to LAMP1+/LysoTracker lysosomal volume per cell. The mechanism predicts expanded lysosomal volume and hydrolase transcript levels in APOE4 with degradation rate per unit lysosomal volume no higher than APOE3, plus accumulation of undigested neutral lipid/cholesteryl ester. If APOE4 shows proportionally increased per-lysosome degradative flux and no substrate accumulation, the 'demand-driven, unmatched capacity' claim is wrong and successful adaptation is favored.", "Prospective dependency test: knockdown/degron of TFEB (and TFE3/MITF) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C) toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the elevation after TFEB/MITF loss would falsify mechanism step 2.", "Prospective proteoform test: activity-based probes and immunoblots for pro- versus mature cathepsin B/D/L and for v-ATPase V1 subunits should show that the large transcript increases yield at most a modest, non-proportional increase in mature active enzyme, with a shifted pro/mature ratio matching the divergent spots (protein_spot:053 up vs protein_spot:069 down; protein_spot:064/protein_spot:065 down). A proportional increase in mature active hydrolase and V1 protein would weaken step 6 and support increased capacity.", "Prospective routing test: SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia should reduce cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet accumulation and, if storage-biased routing is what sustains the response, partially normalize the CLEAR transcript elevation; unchanged CLEAR transcripts despite loss of esterification would show the lipid-routing branch is dissociable from the lysosomal program.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not current defect): after a myelin or oxidized-lipoprotein load, APOE4 should show slower clearance and greater lysosomal-pH or cathepsin-activity shortfall than APOE3 despite equal or higher baseline hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance under challenge would argue the expansion is fully compensatory.", "Specificity control: the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS elevation with reduced mtDNA-encoded transcripts (gene:NDUFA5 up, gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35) is predicted to be downstream/parallel; if blocking lysosomal cargo delivery normalizes the mitonuclear pattern, the lysosomal axis is upstream, whereas an unchanged mitonuclear pattern indicates a separate primary axis this hypothesis does not explain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry a higher endolysosomal load of lipid-rich cargo, accompanied by uniformly increased transcripts for lipoprotein/phagocytic uptake and opsonin receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:FCGR1A, gene:C1QA; 19/19 represented members positive, though their amplitude is at the selected-list background).", "Cargo/sterol retention in the endolysosome engages a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR transcriptional response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), which coordinately raises acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DPP7), hydrolase M6P targeting (gene:GNPTG +3.02), all represented v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D2; 10/10 up) and lysosomal membrane/solute machinery (gene:LAMP1, gene:TMEM192, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC48A1).", "The same response upregulates the endosome-to-lysosome routing machinery that delivers and recycles this cargo (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ARL8B, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, all 8 represented SNX genes positive, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS37B, gene:VPS18), consistent with expanded, not blocked, trafficking capacity at the transcript level.", "Liberated sterol/lipid is routed toward re-esterification and de novo synthesis instead of efflux: gene:SOAT1 +1.25 and gene:DGAT1 +1.72 rise while the sterol-synthesis and uptake arm remains induced (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:SCD, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:APOE +1.24) \u2014 a pattern expected when sterol is sequestered in the endolysosomal compartment rather than sensed at the ER (inferred localization, not measured; no efflux transporter transcript is represented).", "This high-turnover, storage-biased state is supported by a catabolic/oxidative bias in the transcript layer: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA/beta-oxidation transcripts are uniformly up (gene:NDUFA5 +7.30 and 21/21 NDUF genes, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:UQCRC2, gene:OGDH +8.63, gene:MPC2, gene:HADHA) while committed glycolytic and PPP steps fall below background (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30).", "Protein-spot data do not corroborate a matching increase in mature degradative protein: significant down spots carry acid-hydrolase candidates (protein_spot:058 -0.85 with CTSD/CTSB; protein_spot:067 -1.00 with CTSB/HEXB; protein_spot:069 -1.38 with CTSD) and both ATP6V1E1-containing spots fall (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93), whereas other hydrolase-containing spots rise (protein_spot:052 +2.14 with CTSL, protein_spot:053 +1.54 with CTSD, protein_spot:055/protein_spot:057 +0.59 with CTSB, protein_spot:012 +0.68 with MAN2B1, protein_spot:013 +0.77 with DPP7). All these spots are multi-candidate, so this indicates redistribution among proteoforms with no net confirmed gain \u2014 the transcriptional expansion is therefore consistent with attempted, not demonstrated, capacity increase."], "title": "Cargo-lipid-loaded APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/MITF-type endolysosomal expansion program with storage-biased lipid routing, without demonstrated gain in degradative capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19857824802575347, "cosine_similarity": 0.34248914393904556, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059449838187702, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19857824802575347, "cosine_similarity": 0.34248914393904556, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6059449838187702, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.96945675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 61}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_119", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, 1705/2212 positive), so every enrichment statement is a relative shift within that biased list, not an unbiased whole-transcriptome result; the logarithm base of the reported effects is unspecified and magnitudes are used ordinally only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme and complex capacity closely enough to bias flux; no oxygen consumption, ATP, lysosomal pH, lipid, or metabolite measurement is supplied, so mitochondrial and lysosomal flux, TFEB nuclear localization, and lipid pool size are inferred and unmeasured.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each (39/92 contain a keratin, 64/92 contain an actin/cytoskeletal candidate); no spot uniquely identifies a protein, and multiple spots sharing a candidate can be distinct proteoforms, so spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in microglia-astrocyte co-culture; with no astrocyte-only or monoculture arm supplied, cell-intrinsic APOE4 effects cannot be separated from astrocyte-derived lipoprotein effects, and replicate structure is stated as not supplied.", "The global positive shift (mean +1.39, median +1.46) is assumed to be at least partly a selection/normalization property of the supplied list rather than a true genome-wide upshift; module tests were therefore rank-based against the supplied list itself.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: the ordering of steps is a proposed, testable chain, not an established one."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcriptional shift toward lipoprotein/lipid uptake plus lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase capacity, with mitochondrial carbon entry and oxidative phosphorylation transcripts uniformly raised while glycolytic commitment steps (HK2, PFKP) are lowered. We hypothesise that mitochondrial pyruvate/acetyl-CoA entry and Complex I-linked TCA oxidation (MPC2-OGDH-MDH1-NDUF axis) becomes the primary, poorly substitutable disposal route for lysosome-derived carbon in APOE4, and that the concurrent, coordinated reduction of the myeloid Rac/WAVE-myosin actin module (SPN, MYH9, FAM49B/CYRIB, ARHGAP30, ACTB, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8) leaves APOE4 microglia in a lipid-catabolic, oxidation-dependent, low-motility state despite unreduced phagocytic receptor transcripts. All flux, localization and causal statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: titrate a Complex I inhibitor (piericidin A or rotenone) and the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibitor UK5099 in parallel with 2-deoxyglucose. The mechanism predicts APOE4 microglia lose ATP, LysoTracker/pHrodo lysosomal acidification signal, and myelin/oxLDL clearance at inhibitor doses that APOE3 tolerates, while APOE3 is the more 2-DG-sensitive genotype. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive to Complex I/MPC inhibition than APOE3, or is the more 2-DG-sensitive genotype, the bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Extracellular flux (Seahorse) should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a higher OCR/ECAR ratio with lower glycolytic reserve in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Equal or lower OCR in APOE4 would show the uniform 36/36 OXPHOS and 11/11 TCA transcript increases do not translate into capacity and would substantially weaken steps 3-4.", "Separating the metabolic and cytoskeletal arms: APOE4 microglia should show reduced lamellipodial area, reduced random/directed migration and slower bead or synaptosome internalization despite unchanged or higher surface TREM2/MERTK/FcgammaR binding. Re-expressing CYRIB/FAM49B or expressing constitutively active Rac1 should restore motility and internalization without normalizing OCR; conversely, methyl-pyruvate or nicotinamide riboside should restore ATP without restoring motility. If ATP repletion alone fully restores APOE4 motility, step 5 is demoted to a downstream energetic consequence; if Rac1 rescue fails, step 5 is wrong.", "The MiT/CLEAR inference requires that APOE4 microglia show increased nuclear TFEB and increased LAMP1-positive compartment volume by imaging. If TFEB nuclear fraction and lysosome volume are unchanged despite the raised gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1H and hydrolase transcripts, step 2 collapses to transcript-only and the model must be restricted to the mitochondrial arm.", "Lipid outcome: neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester content should be higher in APOE4 at baseline and should increase further, disproportionately versus APOE3, after 24 h of Complex I inhibition or MPC inhibition. No genotype-by-inhibitor interaction on lipid load would falsify the proposed lysosome-to-mitochondria carbon coupling.", "Protein-level test replacing the ambiguous 2D-gel spots: targeted immunoblot or MS of NDUFB8, SDHB, UQCRC2, MT-CO1, ATP5F1A, CTSD, CTSB and ATP6V1A. The mechanism predicts higher OXPHOS subunit protein in APOE4; the supplied spots protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 (v-ATPase candidates) and protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 (cathepsin candidates) are significantly decreased, so if unambiguous immunoblot confirms lower v-ATPase and cathepsin protein in APOE4, the lysosomal-capacity arm (step 2) is falsified even though its transcripts rise."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_119", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/sterol uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1) and for sterol/lipid synthesis regulators (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2), which we infer increases delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosome. Lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): Lysosomal hydrolase and acidification transcripts rise coherently (gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1) alongside gene:TFEB and gene:TFEC, consistent with an MiT/CLEAR-type biogenesis program. TFEB nuclear localization and lysosomal pH were not measured, so the program is inferred, not observed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Carbon exit routes from the lysosome toward mitochondria are transcriptionally reinforced (gene:SCP2, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:SLC25A1, gene:MPC2, gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1), so we infer increased mitochondrial carbon entry rather than storage-only handling.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred flux): Complex I-linked TCA oxidation is the proposed rate-limiting sink. Every detected TCA/carrier transcript (11/11) and every detected OXPHOS subunit transcript (36/36) is higher in APOE4, led by gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, while glycolytic commitment steps gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP are lower. We infer that APOE4 ATP supply becomes OXPHOS-dependent with reduced glycolytic reserve.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred phenotype): The myeloid Rac/WAVE-myosin actin and motility module is coordinately reduced (gene:SPN, gene:MYH9, gene:FAM49B, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:ACTB, gene:CORO2A, gene:MYO1F, gene:PLEK, gene:DOCK8, gene:ARHGDIB, gene:RAC2, gene:CSF1, gene:CTSS), which we infer lowers lamellipodial/process actin turnover and cell-autonomous motility.", "Step 6 (inferred integration): Because phagocytic receptor transcripts are not reduced (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:FCGR3A, gene:ITGB1, gene:MRC1), we predict the APOE4 defect is not in cargo recognition but in the actin-dependent internalization/migration arm and in the ATP-dependent maintenance of an expanded acidified lysosomal compartment, producing lipid retention whenever oxidative capacity is constrained."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift catabolic load onto a Complex I-linked TCA bottleneck and downshift the Rac/WAVE-myosin actin motility program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28908355795148244, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23534190923386084, "cosine_similarity": 0.3421536759388395, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_119", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6120485436893204, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28908355795148244, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23534190923386084, "cosine_similarity": 0.3421536759388395, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6120485436893204, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.07940725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 252}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_033", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all statements use within-list percentiles and relative comparisons rather than absolute fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list has a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive), so only relative (within-list) enrichment is interpreted, and the global shift is assumed to be at least partly technical (normalisation, RNA content, ambient signal) rather than a true genome-wide increase.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are treated as ambiguous corroboration only, never as measurement of a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a weak proxy for enzyme protein and no proxy at all for activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux or compartment localisation - none of which were measured here.", "No lipid, autophagic-flux, pH, cell-composition or replicate-level data are supplied; equal microglial purity and comparable astrocyte co-culture composition between APOE4 and APOE3 wells are assumed.", "Mock condition means no exogenous cargo challenge, so the inferred cargo load is endogenous (myelin-free) debris, apoptotic material and astrocyte-derived lipoprotein."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal cargo processing: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases that degrade lipid, glycan and glycogen cargo (GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, MAN2B1, SGSH, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK) are among the most strongly elevated in the supplied differential list, whereas lysosomal membrane/structural and acidification-machinery genes (LAMP1, SCARB2, NPC2, CLN3, ATP6V0D2) sit at or below the list median and no coordinate increase is seen in protein spots whose candidate lists contain hydrolase or V-ATPase subunits. We hypothesise that this pattern reflects a compensatory, substrate-driven induction of catabolic enzymes on top of a per-lysosome degradative capacity that does not scale, so undegraded lipid cargo persists in the limiting compartment; sequestration of sterol away from the ER sensor is proposed to explain the concurrent elevation of SREBP-pathway transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, INSIG1). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show selective accumulation of the substrates of the induced hydrolases - hexosylceramide/glucosylceramide (GBA), sphingomyelin (SMPD1), GM2/higher gangliosides and other glycosphingolipids (HEXA/HEXB), plus cholesteryl esters and bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate - with a larger relative increase in these species than in bulk phosphatidylcholine. If APOE4 shows no increase (or a decrease) in hexosylceramide, sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid species, and differs only in triacylglycerol, the throughput-bottleneck claim is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: give APOE4 and APOE3 microglia a pulse of a defined degradable cargo (BODIPY-LacCer or NBD-sphingomyelin plus DQ-BSA) and chase. The mechanism predicts equal or greater internalisation but a slower per-cargo degradation rate in APOE4, and hydrolase activity measured per LAMP1 (acid SMase, GBA, beta-hexosaminidase) that is NOT increased in proportion to the large transcript differences. If per-lysosome activity scales with the transcript increase and cargo clearance rates are equal, the mechanism is falsified.", "Second discriminating perturbation: increasing capacity rather than enzyme message - TFEB overexpression, or restoring acidification with acidic nanoparticles - should reduce substrate-lipid accumulation in APOE4 and secondarily normalise the SREBP transcript program; whereas blocking de novo synthesis (statin or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should lower SREBP targets WITHOUT correcting glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin accumulation. If statin/25-HC fully corrects the substrate lipids, the primary bottleneck is lipogenesis, not luminal catabolism, and this hypothesis fails.", "Substrate-driven versus genotype-autonomous test: loading APOE3 microglia with an equivalent lipid cargo (apoptotic cells or cholesterol-loaded lipoprotein) should phenocopy the hydrolase transcript induction (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1) seen in APOE4. If loaded APOE3 cells fail to induce these transcripts, induction is genotype-intrinsic and the demand-driven step (step 3) is wrong.", "Technical falsifier: re-normalising the RNA data with spike-ins or depth-matched pseudobulk should leave the acid-hydrolase set above the recentred list median. If, after recentring, the hydrolase set is indistinguishable from the background and only the OXPHOS/TCA set survives, the endolysosomal mechanism should be abandoned in favour of a mitochondrial one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show high transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 top ~1% of the list, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), which we infer - but did not measure - increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization): late-endosomal maturation and fusion transcripts are modestly up (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS26A), consistent with cargo reaching the degradative compartment rather than being retained in early endosomes; compartment localization itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): the luminal, cargo-degrading enzymes are the most extreme members of the endolysosomal program (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB all \u003e=94th percentile of the 2212-row list), a substrate-matched pattern (glycogen, glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin, heparan-sulfate, protein cargo) that we interpret as demand-driven induction downstream of accumulated substrate.", "Step 4 (measured RNA and protein spots, inferred capacity): the components that set capacity per lysosome are not co-scaled - gene:LAMP1 (46th pct), gene:SCARB2 (27th), gene:NPC2 (35th), gene:CLN3 (35th), gene:ATP6V0D2 (31st) - and protein spots whose candidate gene lists include cathepsins, HEXB or V-ATPase V1E1 are flat-to-down (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065). Enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and lysosome number were not measured; capacity is inferred, not observed.", "Step 5 (inferred): because throughput is limited by acidification/membrane capacity and product export rather than by enzyme message, per-cargo degradation rate stays low and hydrolase substrates (sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide/gangliosides, unesterified cholesterol, glycogen) persist in the limiting compartment.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred causal direction): sterol sequestered in that compartment is not sensed by the ER, so SREBP target transcripts rise (gene:SREBF1 92nd pct, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1), adding newly synthesised and esterified lipid to a compartment that is already the bottleneck - a feed-forward loop rather than a satisfied demand."], "title": "Substrate-matched acid-hydrolase induction without proportional lysosomal membrane/acidification capacity: a luminal catabolic throughput bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10361583729851506, "cosine_similarity": 0.3420783504159296, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6430129449838188, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10361583729851506, "cosine_similarity": 0.3420783504159296, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6430129449838188, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.75116475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 253}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_185", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all rows pass adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1, with no |effect| \u003c 1 present), so absence of a gene means untested or below threshold, not unchanged; pathway statements are restricted to measured members.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and within-dataset comparisons are used, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The dataset shows a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 transcripts up, median +1.46), which may include normalisation or compositional bias; all enrichment claims are made relative to this internal background rather than versus zero.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no protein, lipid, sterol-pool, flux, localisation or SREBP-cleavage measurement is supplied, so activity, direction and causality are inferred, not established.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are dominated by keratin/actin contaminants; they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence, never as identified proteins.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context metadata, and astrocyte co-culture contributions cannot be separated in these bulk-style measurements."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by a canonical unfolded-protein response but by a lipid-handling state in which cholesterol/fatty acid is retained in endolysosomal and neutral-lipid (ester/droplet) compartments instead of reaching the ER regulatory sterol pool; the resulting persistent SREBP-type output (LDLR, SCARB1, INSIG1, SREBF1/2, DHCR7/DHCR24/LSS, ACSS2, SCD) together with esterification enzymes (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1) and a TFEB-associated hydrolase/V-ATPase program creates a self-sustaining futile lipid-storage cycle. The proposed rate-limiting step is transfer of lysosome- and membrane-derived cholesterol to the ER sensing pool, not synthesis capacity, chaperone capacity, or ER protein folding.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: blocking SCAP-SREBP activation (25-hydroxycholesterol or the site-1-protease inhibitor PF-429242) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of LDLR, SCARB1, INSIG1, DHCR24, SCD and ACSS2 transcripts and abolish the predicted genotype difference in neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content, while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase/TFEB transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) still elevated. If SREBP blockade normalises the sterol-gene set but the lipid-storage difference persists, the SREBP arm is not the driver and the mechanism is weakened.", "Pool-localisation test: delivering cholesterol directly to the ER-accessible pool (cyclodextrin-cholesterol, or SOAT1 inhibition with avasimibe to convert esters back to free cholesterol) should suppress SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4 at least as strongly as in APOE3 if the defect is upstream supply; failure of APOE4 cells to suppress after direct loading would instead localise the defect to the sensor itself and would falsify the transfer-bottleneck version of the claim.", "Direct-state test: immunoblot of cleaved nuclear SREBP-2 and filipin/neutral-lipid imaging should show higher nuclear SREBP-2 and higher lysosomal plus esterified cholesterol in APOE4; finding unchanged or reduced nuclear SREBP-2, or lower neutral-lipid content in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Specificity/rejection test for the assigned focus: pharmacological UPR readouts (XBP1 splicing, HSPA5/DDIT3 protein, eIF2-alpha phosphorylation) and IRE1/PERK inhibition should show no genotype difference and no rescue of the lipid phenotype; any finding that IRE1 or PERK inhibition normalises the sterol-gene set would overturn the rejection of the ER-proteostasis mechanism.", "Lysosomal-arm test: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase/V-ATPase transcripts without correcting the SREBP-target excess, and should worsen rather than relieve neutral-lipid accumulation; a full normalisation of the sterol arm by TFEB knockdown would indicate the lysosomal program is causal upstream and would falsify the proposed ordering."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_185", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, every sterol/lipid-handling transcript present in the differential-expression list is increased (24/24 up), spanning uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36), post-squalene sterol synthesis (LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, HMGCS1, ACAT2), acetyl-CoA supply (ACSS2), desaturation/glycerolipid assembly (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1) and esterification (SOAT1, DGAT1), alongside INSIG1 and SREBF1/SREBF2.", "Inferred (not measured): this transcript pattern reflects elevated nuclear SREBP transcriptional activity, i.e. the ER sterol sensor behaves as if the ER regulatory cholesterol pool is subnormal; SCAP/SREBP cleavage, nuclear SREBP protein and sterol pool sizes were not assayed.", "Inferred bottleneck: cholesterol is not globally scarce but mis-partitioned. Oxysterol-generating and LXR-responsive transcripts are simultaneously raised (CYP27A1, CH25H, MYLIP, ABCA7, APOE), which is incompatible with simple whole-cell sterol depletion and instead points to a spatial dissociation between a sterol-loaded endolysosome/plasma-membrane compartment and a sterol-poor ER sensing pool.", "Inferred flux: SREBP output that raises uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36) is routed into esters and droplets by SOAT1/DGAT1/AGPAT2/GPAT4 rather than into the ER regulatory pool, so the sensing deficit is never corrected and the cycle persists; esterified lipid and droplet content were not measured here.", "Measured, compensatory: a lysosomal degradative program is co-elevated (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, NPC2, LAMP1, SCARB2, RAB7A, ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C/ATP6AP1) with the transcription factor TFEB, consistent with increased lysosomal catabolic capacity that still fails to relieve the ER-directed transfer step.", "Measured, permissive: a TCA/citrate-export and reductant-supply program is raised (SLC25A1, ACO2, OGDH, MDH1, DLD, NNT, ME1), which would supply cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH for the lipogenic arm; this is transcript-level only and no metabolic flux was measured.", "Consequence: the APOE4 genotype difference is predicted to manifest as increased neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage with sustained sterol-demand signalling, rather than as ER protein-folding stress; canonical UPR/ERAD transcripts are not coherently induced and several ERAD components are decreased."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mis-partition sterol away from the ER regulatory pool, locking in an SREBP-driven uptake-and-esterification cycle despite an expanded lysosomal catabolic program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14644795628253887, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22475234114650164, "cosine_similarity": 0.34184783398735774, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_185", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6098187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14644795628253887, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22475234114650164, "cosine_similarity": 0.34184783398735774, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6098187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.007023, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 254}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_051", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level statements are therefore made relative to the list's own upward background (median +1.46, 77% positive), not to zero.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given; only relative ranking and sign are interpreted, not absolute fold magnitude.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for the size of the corresponding nuclear-encoded subunit pool; assembly state, enzyme activity, flux, redox ratio, protein localization and lipid pools were not measured and are inferred.", "The mtDNA-encoded arm rests on 6 MT- rows measured with a probe-based 10X Flex assay; it is assumed that MT- probe capture is comparable between the two isogenic lines and that these rows report the mitochondrial transcript pool rather than an assay artefact.", "Protein spots each carry several candidate genes (median 5, dominated by keratin/actin contaminants) and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific mitochondrial or lipogenic protein.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so pseudobulk signal is assumed to be predominantly microglial; a shift in cell-state or cell-type composition rather than a within-cell rewiring is not excluded.", "ACLY, ACSS2, CPT1A, mtDNA copy number, assembly factors and lipid species were not measured; steps invoking them are hypothesis, not observation.", "Causality is not established: the correlation between the APOE4 genotype and these transcript differences is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, the proposed chain."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells primarily by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative program (all 37 detected NDUF/UQCR/COX/ATP5 rows raised, median +2.65 versus list median +1.46; TCA, pyruvate-import and protein-import rows raised) that is NOT accompanied by a matching rise in mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 sit in the bottom 4-18% of the list). We hypothesise that supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembled electron-transport capacity in APOE4 cells; the resulting mismatch between dehydrogenase/anaplerotic input and NADH re-oxidation is proposed to back up the TCA cycle, promote citrate export (SLC25A1 +4.47) and SREBP-directed lipogenic/sterologenic gene expression (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, ACAT2 +2.04, DHCR24 +3.69, DGAT1 +1.72), with little glycolytic buffer because the committed glycolytic steps HK2 (-3.67) and PFKP (-3.08) are among the most negative rows in the dataset. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; assembly, flux, redox state and lipid pools are inferred, and no causal direction has been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol, titrated to leave APOE3 near-unaffected) should reduce ATP:ADP, maximal OCR and viability substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, because APOE4 cells are proposed to already run at the mtDNA-encoded core-subunit limit with no glycolytic buffer. If APOE4 cells are equally or less sensitive than APOE3, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "DISCRIMINATING RESCUE: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or mitochondrial-transcription/translation support, or increasing mtDNA copy number) should normalise assembled complex I/IV levels and spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 cells AND lower the SREBP-target lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) and neutral-lipid content. If respiration is restored but lipogenic transcripts and lipid droplets are unchanged, Steps 4-5 (citrate-export coupling) are falsified even if Step 3 survives.", "ASSEMBLY VERSUS ABUNDANCE: on BN-PAGE / complexome or complex activity assays, APOE4 microglia should show assembled complex I, III, IV and V holo-enzyme (and MT-CO1/MT-ATP6 protein) that is unchanged or reduced relative to APOE3 while nuclear-encoded subunit protein (e.g. NDUFA5/NDUFB8/ATP5F1B class) is raised, i.e. a reduced assembled-complex-per-subunit ratio with detectable sub-assemblies. If assembled complexes and maximal respiration rise in proportion to the nuclear subunit transcripts, the mechanism is falsified.", "BIOENERGETIC PHENOTYPE: in Seahorse assays APOE4 cells should show unchanged or reduced maximal/spare respiratory capacity and reduced glycolytic reserve (consistent with HK2/PFKP), and should lose viability faster than APOE3 when glucose is replaced by galactose. Increased spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "LIPID OUTPUT: APOE4 cells should accumulate more neutral lipid/cholesteryl ester (BODIPY, LipidTOX or lipidomics) with a higher SCD desaturation index (C16:1/C16:0, C18:1/C18:0) than APOE3, and pharmacological block of citrate export or cytosolic acetyl-CoA production (SLC25A1 inhibitor CTPI-2, or ACLY inhibition) should reduce this excess preferentially in APOE4. Equal lipid-droplet content between genotypes, or an equal effect of ACLY/SLC25A1 inhibition in both genotypes, would falsify the citrate-export arm.", "SPECIFICITY CONTROL: the mitonuclear discordance should be reproducible in an unbiased whole-transcriptome or nuclear-run-on measurement of the same lines, with MT- transcripts below and nuclear OXPHOS transcripts above the genome-wide centre. If, in an unbiased assay, nuclear OXPHOS genes are no more elevated than the transcriptome-wide shift, or MT- transcripts are equally elevated, the signature is a selection/normalisation artefact and the hypothesis fails at Step 1-2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia carry a coherent, sign-consistent elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - every detected complex I/III/IV/V subunit row is positive (37/37; permutation p ~ 0.002 against the list's own upward background), together with TCA and pyruvate-entry rows (MPC2 +7.98, OGDH +8.56, MDH1 +8.72, GOT1 +6.43, DLD +5.54, ACO2 +3.54, IDH3G +3.94, PDP1 +3.00) and mitochondrial import/dynamics rows (TOMM22 +4.63, TIMM44 +2.46, SLC25A46 +8.77).", "STEP 2 (measured RNA, discordance): the mtDNA-encoded core subunits are not co-regulated with this program - MT-ATP6 (-3.35), MT-CYB (-2.32), MT-ND4 (-1.80) and MT-CO2 (-1.33) fall in the lowest 4-18 percentiles of the same list (median of MT- rows below the list median, permutation p ~ 0.014), while only MT-ND5/MT-ND4L are modestly positive.", "STEP 3 (inferred assembly, PRIMARY BOTTLENECK): because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits, we infer that assembled holo-complex number per cell in APOE4 cells is set by mtDNA-encoded subunit supply and therefore does not scale with the raised nuclear subunit and import transcripts; excess nuclear subunits are predicted to remain as unassembled or sub-assembly pools rather than as added respiratory capacity.", "STEP 4 (inferred flux/redox): with dehydrogenase and anaplerotic input transcripts raised (GLUD1 +3.17, GLS +1.35, HADHA +2.86, ETFA +3.55, plus the cytosolic malate-aspartate shuttle arms MDH1 and GOT1) but NADH re-oxidation capped at Step 3, matrix NADH/NAD+ is predicted to rise and TCA turnover to become back-pressured rather than accelerated, despite the transcriptional appearance of increased oxidative capacity.", "STEP 5 (inferred partitioning, measured RNA support): back-pressured citrate is predicted to be exported through the citrate carrier (SLC25A1 +4.47) into cytosolic acetyl-CoA, consistent with the coordinated raising of SREBP-target lipogenic and sterologenic rows (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, ACAT2 +2.04, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50) and of neutral-lipid esterification rows (DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25), predicting increased neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage and a higher SCD desaturation index in APOE4 cells.", "STEP 6 (inferred consequence, measured RNA support): the cells have little glycolytic escape route - the committed steps HK2 (-3.67), PFKP (-3.08) and HK3 (-1.12) are strongly negative against a list whose median is +1.46 - so the state is predicted to run with low spare respiratory capacity, chronic integrated-stress signalling (DDIT3 +2.79) and heavy reliance on lysosomal catabolic substrate supply (GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1A +4.23, CTSD +2.86, TFEB +2.38)."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch: APOE4 microglia expand a nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA program that mtDNA-encoded core subunits do not match, capping respiratory flux and diverting citrate to SREBP-driven lipid synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3360502898497212, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23206282352506397, "cosine_similarity": 0.340976738304879, "direction_accuracy": 0.3640776699029126, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5969223300970874, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3360502898497212, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23206282352506397, "cosine_similarity": 0.340976738304879, "direction_accuracy": 0.3640776699029126, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5969223300970874, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2518285, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 255}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["TFEB/MITF and downstream hydrolase transcript increases are interpreted as evidence of increased transcriptional program activity, not as direct proof of increased lysosomal enzymatic activity, acidification, or lipid clearance flux, which are not measured here.", "The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all supplied adjusted p-values \u003c= 0.048, background sign split ~77% positive/23% negative in this list), so within-program positive skew is compared against this selected-list background rather than an assumed 50/50 split; genes absent from the list are unknown, not necessarily unchanged.", "The reported RNA log fold-change base is unspecified in the source; magnitudes are compared only in relative/ranked terms, not converted across bases.", "Protein-spot candidate gene lists are ambiguous (2-6 candidates per spot, dominated recurrently by high-abundance genes like ACTB and keratins); any single spot's fold-change is not attributed to one candidate protein.", "Isogenic co-culture with astrocytes means microglial transcript changes could partly reflect altered paracrine lipid/cytokine signaling from astrocytes, which is not separately measured.", "No biological replicate count is supplied, so the precision of individual gene effect sizes cannot be independently verified from this file."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-microglia display a broad, internally coherent increase in transcripts for cholesterol uptake/efflux/esterification (LDLR, SCARB1, SCARB2, ABCA7, SOAT1, SREBF1, SREBF2, CH25H, HMGCS1, INSIG1), the master lysosomal-biogenesis regulators TFEB and MITF, downstream lysosomal hydrolases and acidification machinery (GBA, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, HEXB, NPC2, SGSH, LAMP1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C), and disease-associated-microglia (DAM)/complement markers (TREM2, CD33, AIF1, ITGAX, CLEC7A, C1QA/B/C, CFH, C2). This pattern is most consistent with a coordinated transcriptional response to a lipid/cholesterol-handling burden that engages a CLEAR-like (TFEB/MITF) lysosomal expansion program together with a DAM-like state shift. Whether this response represents successful adaptive expansion of degradative capacity or an insufficient/failed compensation cannot be determined from transcript and protein-spot data alone, because directly relevant functional readouts (lysosomal proteolytic/lipolytic flux, cholesterol pool size, phagocytic capacity) are not measured here, and paired protein-spot evidence for cathepsins is itself discordant.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of TFEB/MITF activity in APOE4 microglia (not yet tested here) should blunt induction of the co-regulated hydrolase/V-ATPase panel (e.g., reduced CTSB, CTSD, GBA, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C transcripts) if TFEB/MITF are actually driving this program; if inhibition fails to reduce these transcripts, the proposed TFEB/MITF-driven mechanism would be weakened.", "Prospective: direct functional assays in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under the same mock condition (lysosomal proteolytic flux by DQ-BSA or similar, free/esterified cholesterol quantification, and a phagocytosis assay) should show increased degradative flux and altered cholesterol handling if this transcriptional program reflects successful adaptive expansion; unchanged or reduced flux/phagocytosis despite the transcript induction would instead support a failed-compensation interpretation and weaken the 'successful adaptation' framing without weakening the existence of the transcriptional program itself."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show broad transcriptional induction of cholesterol/lipid-handling genes spanning uptake, efflux, esterification and biosynthetic-feedback nodes (gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:SCARB2, gene:ABCA7, gene:SOAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:CH25H, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:APOE), consistent with altered intracellular cholesterol/lipid handling.", "In parallel, the master lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors TFEB and MITF are increased (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), consistent with activation of a CLEAR-like lysosomal gene network rather than an isolated single-gene change.", "Downstream, transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and acidification machinery are broadly elevated (gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NPC2, gene:SGSH, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), consistent with an attempt to expand lysosomal degradative capacity.", "Microglia simultaneously shift toward a DAM/lipid-associated and complement-competent transcriptional state (gene:TREM2, gene:CD33, gene:AIF1, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:GPNMB, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:CFH, gene:C2), a state pattern often linked to lipid/cholesterol stress in microglia.", "This transcriptional induction does not establish increased functional flux: cathepsin-associated protein spots are discordant, with some spots trending up (protein_spot:027, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057) and others trending down (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069) despite consistently positive RNA for CTSB/CTSD/HEXB, and each spot carries multiple unresolved candidate identities.", "Cytoskeletal/phagocytic-machinery transcripts move in the opposite direction (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9 both strongly decreased), while many ACTB-candidate protein spots trend positive but are ambiguous (multiple co-migrating candidates per spot), so actual phagocytic/motility capacity in this state is not established by these data.", "Net effect: the data support a coordinated transcriptional lysosomal-biogenesis/cholesterol-handling and DAM-state program in APOE4 microglia under mock conditions, but whether this constitutes adequate compensation, excess/maladaptive activation, or an early failing response to a lipid-handling burden remains undetermined without direct flux, lipid-content, or phagocytosis measurements."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a coordinated TFEB/MITF-linked lysosomal-biogenesis and cholesterol-handling transcriptional program accompanying a DAM-like activation shift"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.04892367906066536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25379371413510293, "cosine_similarity": 0.3402880837273193, "direction_accuracy": 0.0825242718446602, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6087216828478964, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.04892367906066536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25379371413510293, "cosine_similarity": 0.3402880837273193, "direction_accuracy": 0.0825242718446602, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6087216828478964, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.7701051, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_051", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive, median +1.46, logarithm base unspecified); program directions are judged against that skewed background and absent genes (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, PSAP, GRN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Elevated transcripts for hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits, ETC subunits and receptors indicate expressed capacity only; lysosomal acidification, hydrolytic flux, receptor-mediated uptake rate, respiration and sterol transfer to the ER were not measured here.", "Sustained SREBP-target expression is taken as a readout of a non-repleted ER-accessible sterol pool; this inference assumes the canonical SCAP/INSIG sensing relation holds in these cells and that SREBF1/SCD elevation is not driven solely by an independent lipogenic input.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate (92 spots, 2-6 candidates each, 208 unique candidates); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot directions are used only for compatibility or contradiction.", "The coherent directional patterns are descriptive, computed over non-independent genes with no formal enrichment test and no supplied replicate structure; APOE-genotype background knowledge invoked in interpretation is unverified (literature retrieval disabled).", "Effects described are those of the measured mock condition; any reduced reserve is a prospective inference that would require a challenge to test."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by immune activation but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake, endosome-to-lysosome trafficking, lysosomal acidification and hydrolysis, and mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport machinery are coherently elevated, while SREBP-target sterol-synthesis and LDLR transcripts remain elevated rather than suppressed. The most parsimonious reading is that in APOE4 lipid/sterol cargo is preferentially routed into an expanded acidified endolysosomal compartment and its catabolic sinks instead of restoring the ER-accessible sterol pool, producing a self-reinforcing uptake+synthesis+degradation state. This is a measured-abundance (transcript capacity) pattern; the corresponding fluxes (uptake rate, lysosomal hydrolysis, respiration, sterol transfer to ER) were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging in mock-treated isogenic lines: APOE4 microglia should show larger acidic/LAMP1+ compartment volume and greater lysosomal free/esterified cholesterol and neutral lipid than APOE3, while the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/D4H-type probe) is equal or lower. If APOE4 shows equal lysosomal lipid and an equal-or-higher ER-accessible sterol pool while SREBP targets remain elevated, the routing/non-repletion step is wrong.", "Prospective sterol-loading challenge (acLDL, myelin debris or 25-hydroxycholesterol): APOE3 should suppress LDLR/HMGCS1/DHCR24 transcripts more completely than APOE4, and APOE4 should retain more label in the lysosomal fraction. Equal suppression kinetics in both genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective flux test: if the mitochondrial transcript increase reflects substrate-driven demand, blocking lysosomal degradation (bafilomycin A1 or combined cathepsin inhibition, short-term) should selectively collapse the APOE4-specific elevation of TCA/ETC transcripts; no change would show the mitochondrial program is coordinated independently (e.g. by MiT/TFE biogenesis) and would remove step 4 from the causal chain.", "Prospective respirometry and complex-assembly assay: despite 38/38 nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts being higher, APOE4 basal and maximal OCR and assembled complex IV/V levels may be unchanged or reduced, consistent with the negative mitochondrially encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4). A proportional increase in respiration and assembled complexes would favour successful adaptation/increased throughput over the mis-routing reading and would require the claim to be rewritten.", "Prospective TFEB loss-of-function: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should reduce the hydrolase and V-ATPase transcript elevation and increase lysosomal lipid retention without normalising SREBP-target expression; if SREBP targets normalise, the lysosome-centric step, not ER sensing, is the dominant driver.", "Prospective targeted proteomics (unambiguous, single-protein assays for CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, GAA, ATP6V1E1, NDUFA5): the transcript increases should be accompanied by increased mature hydrolase protein. Given that the supplied ambiguous spots go in both directions (protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:052 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), a clear failure of hydrolase and V-ATPase protein to rise would falsify the 'expanded degradative capacity' step and favour a purely transcriptional stress response."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the expressed capacity for lipoprotein/debris capture: scavenger and phagocytic receptor transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, one of the 20 largest effects in the list; gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:FCGR1A; 12/12 represented members positive, but with near-background magnitudes).", "Cargo is directed along the degradative route rather than recycled: endosome-to-lysosome and sorting transcripts are up with large effects (gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.93, gene:RAB7A +2.68, gene:PIK3C3 +2.90, gene:VPS18 +1.40).", "A MiT/TFE-type lysosomal biogenesis program expands acidification and hydrolytic capacity: gene:TFEB +2.38 with every represented V-ATPase subunit positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.90, gene:ATP6V1A +4.24, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70) and glycosidase/protease/lipid-hydrolase transcripts strongly up (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.72, gene:NAGLU +5.90, gene:HEXA +5.74, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:LAMP1 +1.42); gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:IDS -1.62 are exceptions.", "Carbon liberated by, or accompanying, this catabolic state is matched by increased mitochondrial oxidative/anaplerotic transcript capacity: all 38 represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunits are positive (gene:NDUFA5 +7.27, gene:NDUFS7 +5.69, gene:UQCRC2 +4.01, gene:COX7A2 +3.39, gene:ATP5F1B +2.63), with TCA and carrier transcripts (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.46, gene:ACO2 +3.53, gene:IDH3G +3.93, gene:SDHB +1.72, gene:SLC25A1 +4.51, gene:SLC25A5 +5.57, gene:SLC25A11 +4.47) and import/chaperone transcripts (gene:TUFM +6.51, gene:HSPA9 +2.44, gene:TIMM44 +2.52); mitochondrially encoded subunits are the exception (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.40, gene:MT-CYB -2.30, gene:MT-ND4 -1.79, gene:MT-CO2 -1.32), so higher assembled OXPHOS capacity is not demonstrated.", "The ER sterol sensor does not read repletion: SREBP-axis and sterol-synthesis transcripts stay up alongside uptake (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.70, gene:INSIG1 +1.86, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.09, gene:DHCR24 +3.71, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.30, gene:EBP +1.29, gene:ACAT2 +1.99, gene:SCD +4.24), together with esterification/handling transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:NPC2 +1.22, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.09, gene:PLTP +1.05, gene:MYLIP +1.29). Continued synthesis plus continued uptake sustains delivery into the same endolysosomal compartment, closing a self-reinforcing loop.", "The resulting APOE4 state is metabolic/organellar rather than inflammatory in the mock condition: the interferon program is essentially unrepresented (only gene:TMEM173 +1.20 of 34 queried), NF-kB/cytokine members are mixed with strong negatives (gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:TRAF4 -7.17, gene:CCL4 -1.50) despite gene:CXCL8 +3.10 and gene:CCL2 +2.14, and homeostatic identity transcripts are not lost (gene:GPR34 +2.97, gene:CSF1R +1.36, gene:MEF2C +1.30, gene:IRF8 +1.38); efferocytosis/lipid-handling markers rise modestly (gene:ANXA1 +4.15, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:GPNMB +1.11)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-centric catabolic organelle state in which lipid cargo is routed to degradative/storage compartments without repleting the ER-regulatory sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18560546119049054, "cosine_similarity": 0.33829063310692253, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6021715210355987, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18560546119049054, "cosine_similarity": 0.33829063310692253, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6021715210355987, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.43273, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 62}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims therefore rest on rank-based comparison against that biased background, not on an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript differences are assumed to translate into proportional enzyme activity and metabolic flux; no proteomic, activity, isotope-tracing or lipidomic measurement of SCD, SREBP processing, AGPAT2, DGAT1 or SOAT1 is supplied.", "Protein-spot observations are 2D-gel spots with several candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; none is treated as a uniquely identified lipid-pathway protein, so the hypothesis is supported by RNA only.", "Key nodes of the proposed circuit were not measured (ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, FASN, ACACA, NPC1, PLIN2/PLIN3, LIPA, NCEH1); the efflux and droplet-coat arms are inferred by absence, not observed.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed isogenic, equally differentiated and equally represented in the 10X Flex dataset, so that composition or ambient-RNA differences (which could also produce a coordinated small-gene up-shift, e.g. the 38/38 positive OXPHOS subunit rows) are not the sole driver of the lipid signal.", "The reported logarithm base is preserved as given; magnitudes up to |15| are treated as ordinal, not as literal fold changes."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia express a coordinated lipid-anabolic transcriptional program (SREBF1/SREBF2 and their sterol-synthesis, lipoprotein-uptake and acyl-transfer targets) in which the SCD-generated monounsaturated fatty-acyl pool is the rate-limiting node; we propose this converts increased sterol and fatty-acid acquisition into stored triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in lipid droplets, with a secondary TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase response, rather than into membrane or export-directed lipid. All lipid pools, enzyme activities and fluxes are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) or SCD knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area (BODIPY 493/503 or LipidTOX) toward APOE3 levels and lower the 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 desaturation indices within the triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester fractions; if droplet burden and the APOE4-APOE3 difference persist unchanged under SCD inhibition, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher total triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester with a raised MUFA:SFA ratio and increased 18:1-containing phosphatidylcholine; equal neutral-lipid mass, or an APOE4 excess carried by polyunsaturated rather than monounsaturated species, would weaken the mechanism.", "DGAT1 inhibition should not normalise the genotype difference but instead redistribute lipid from droplets into free fatty acid, diacylglycerol and ceramide with increased ER-stress markers in APOE4; a clean rescue with no redistribution would argue for an upstream acquisition block rather than a storage-routing mechanism.", "Isotope tracing (U-13C-acetate or 13C-oleate) should show greater label incorporation into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 than APOE3 with no proportional increase in fatty-acid oxidation; equal esterification flux despite the transcript differences would show the RNA program is not translated into flux.", "If the lysosomal hydrolase arm is causal upstream rather than secondary, blocking lysosomal acid lipase or GBA should change droplet content more than SCD inhibition does; observing that outcome would displace the SCD/MUFA bottleneck in favour of a lysosomal-catabolism-limited mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for the SREBP module and its sterol-arm targets (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP) together with the lipoprotein-lipid receptor transcript gene:SCARB1, which we infer raises sterol acquisition and de novo sterol synthesis flux; no sterol pool was measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): The same program raises acetyl-CoA/acyl-supply and desaturation transcripts (gene:ACSS2, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1), which we infer increases the monounsaturated fatty-acyl (MUFA) pool available for esterification.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck): Because efficient esterification of both fatty acid into triacylglycerol and sterol into cholesteryl ester depends on monounsaturated acyl donors, SCD-derived MUFA availability is proposed as the rate-limiting step that determines how much of the acquired lipid is stored rather than oxidised or exported.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred localization): Elevated glycerolipid and phospholipid acyltransferase transcripts (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1) with modestly elevated gene:SOAT1 are inferred to channel these acyl chains into droplet-destined neutral lipid and into remodelled phosphatidylcholine at the ER, a localization that is inferred and not imaged here.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred load): Increased droplet and membrane-lipid turnover is proposed to engage a lysosomal catabolic program (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1), consistent with higher lysosomal substrate load in APOE4; lysosomal lipid content was not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred phenotype): The resulting lipid-laden state is reflected in higher lipid-handling and lipid-droplet-associated microglial marker transcripts (gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3), predicting a net APOE4-over-APOE3 excess of MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester."], "title": "SREBP1-linked, SCD-dependent monounsaturated acyl supply routes excess acquired sterol and fatty acid into neutral-lipid droplet storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09295499021526418, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18754491207244975, "cosine_similarity": 0.33826783078865524, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5980000000000001, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09295499021526418, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18754491207244975, "cosine_similarity": 0.33826783078865524, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5980000000000001, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6979395, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 256}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_049", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |reported log fold change| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46), so only within-list rank enrichment, not raw direction, is treated as evidence; the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance and, less securely, for pathway flux; no protein, metabolite, isotope-tracing or lipid measurement of this axis is supplied.", "Key nodes of the proposed chain (ACLY, FASN, ACACA, PLIN2, ATGL/PNPLA2, LIPA, ABCA1) are absent from the supplied list; absence is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for or against the lipid axis.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so part of the lipid substrate could be exogenous and astrocyte-derived; the model assumes intracellular routing differs by genotype regardless of substrate origin.", "Genotype-associated correlation is assumed, not demonstrated, to be causal; single-cell composition or state-frequency differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures could generate the same pseudo-bulk pattern."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional configuration for carbon entry into mitochondria (MPC2, TCA enzymes, nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits) together with citrate/acetate-to-lipid routing (SLC25A1, ACSS2) and an SREBF1-driven desaturation/esterification program (SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1) plus high lipoprotein-lipid uptake capacity (SCARB1, LDLR); we hypothesise that SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA is the rate-limiting node that converts this excess carbon and taken-up sterol into stored neutral lipid, so that APOE4 microglia adopt a store-and-degrade (droplet + lysosomal hydrolase) rather than an efflux/oxidise configuration. Only transcript and 2-D protein-spot abundances were measured; desaturation flux, acetyl-CoA pools, droplet content and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. CAY10566/A939572) in mock-treated isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should abolish the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess in neutral-lipid droplet content (BODIPY/LipidTOX) and lower the lipidomic 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 desaturation indices more in APOE4, while raising saturated-species ER-stress markers preferentially in APOE4; if the droplet difference between genotypes is unchanged by SCD inhibition, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Source test: 13C6-glucose tracing should show greater label enrichment in APOE4 triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester and MUFA species, and SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or ACLY knockdown should reduce glucose-derived lipid label selectively in APOE4; if APOE4 lipid label comes almost entirely from exogenous 13C-oleate/palmitate with equal glucose-derived label in both genotypes, the mitochondrial-carbon-routing arm (steps 1-2) is falsified.", "Node test: DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from esterified droplet pools to free fatty acid and free cholesterol with greater cytotoxicity/lysosomal stress in APOE4 than APOE3; equal responses in both genotypes would weaken step 4.", "Protein-level test: SREBP-1 nuclear (cleaved) fraction and SCD protein should be higher in APOE4 microglia; if SCD protein and desaturation index are equal between genotypes despite the RNA difference, the mechanism is weakened to a transcript-only observation.", "Rejected-alternative test: if instead phagocytic/cytoskeletal capacity is primary, APOE4 microglia should show a uniform genotype difference in bead/synaptosome uptake that is unaffected by SCD or DGAT1/SOAT1 inhibition; such a result would displace this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): higher transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2, TCA enzymes (MDH1, OGDH, ACO2) and nuclear-encoded complex I/OXPHOS subunits (e.g. NDUFA5) indicate an expanded capacity for pyruvate oxidation and citrate production in APOE4; actual flux and mitochondrial mass were not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred): elevated SLC25A1 transcript is proposed to increase citrate export to the cytosol, and elevated ACSS2 to add an acetate-salvage route, together raising the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool available for lipogenesis; ACLY and FASN were not measured, so this acetyl-CoA pool is unobserved.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): increased SREBF1 with concordant targets (SCD, ACSS2, INSIG1, LDLR) indicates raised SREBP-1 transcriptional output; SREBP-1 cleavage/nuclear localisation was not measured.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, inferred): SCD-catalysed desaturation of saturated acyl-CoA to 16:1/18:1 is the rate-limiting supply step for esterification; the MUFA produced is consumed by AGPAT2 and DGAT1 for triacylglycerol synthesis and, with sterol taken up via SCARB1/LDLR and late sterol enzymes (DHCR24), by SOAT1 for cholesteryl-ester synthesis, so droplet loading tracks SCD output.", "Step 5 (inferred phenotype): the esterified lipid is stored rather than exported, since APOE transcript is only modestly raised (rank below the list median) and no efflux measurement exists; the parallel TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (CTSB, GBA, SMPD1) provides the degradative arm of the same store-and-degrade state.", "Step 6 (prediction-generating consequence): because esterification depends on SCD-derived MUFA, blocking SCD should convert the APOE4 lipid-storage excess into saturated-lipid/ER stress rather than simply lowering total lipid."], "title": "SCD-dependent monounsaturated-lipid esterification is the bottleneck routing mitochondrial-derived carbon into neutral-lipid storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.281255769301776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2259871027753647, "cosine_similarity": 0.33808377449021926, "direction_accuracy": 0.27346278317152106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5995631067961166, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.281255769301776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2259871027753647, "cosine_similarity": 0.33808377449021926, "direction_accuracy": 0.27346278317152106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5995631067961166, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.588185, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 257}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_144", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive), so the list is not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level claims are made rank-wise against this list background, not against all genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and effects range to |8-15|; only sign and rank are interpreted, never fold magnitudes.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; activity, post-translational control (e.g. PDH phosphorylation, allosteric F2,6BP control) and localization were not measured.", "Flux, oxygen consumption, extracellular acidification, lactate, citrate, acetyl-CoA and lipid pools were not measured in this dataset; all flux and carbon-routing statements are inferences.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified, so no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific metabolic enzyme.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes; ambient/cross-cell RNA and differing cell-state proportions could contribute to the apparent coordinated mitochondrial signal.", "Direction of causality (APOE4 -\u003e metabolic state vs. metabolic state -\u003e APOE4-associated phenotype) is not established by an association measured at a single timepoint."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a transcriptional configuration in which the committed, flux-controlling glycolytic steps (hexokinase and phosphofructokinase/PFKFB isoforms expressed in these cells) are selectively lowered while glucose transporters, mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA enzymes, the entire nuclear-encoded electron transport chain and the citrate exporter/lipogenic module are raised. We hypothesise that the flux bottleneck in APOE4 sits at glucose phosphorylation/PFK commitment rather than at mitochondrial capacity, so that glucose carbon that does enter glycolysis is preferentially oxidised in mitochondria and exported as citrate for sterol/fatty-acid esterification, leaving APOE4 microglia with little spare glycolytic reserve for demand-driven activation. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and metabolite pools were not measured and the causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or ETC inhibition (oligomycin/rotenone) should cause a larger fall in ATP and a smaller compensatory ECAR rise in APOE4, whereas 2-deoxyglucose should reduce ATP less in APOE4 than in APOE3. If APOE4 instead shows equal or greater 2-DG sensitivity and unimpaired compensatory glycolysis, the proposed hexokinase/PFK bottleneck is wrong.", "[U-13C6]glucose tracing should give APOE4 microglia a lower m+3 lactate fraction and a higher m+2 citrate/glutamate fraction than APOE3, with increased 13C from glucose appearing in palmitate/oleate and cholesteryl-ester pools (SLC25A1/ACSS2 route). Unchanged or increased lactate labelling with unchanged citrate labelling would weaken the mechanism.", "Seahorse profiling should show higher basal and maximal OCR and a lower glycolytic reserve (ECAR after oligomycin minus basal ECAR) in APOE4; equal glycolytic reserve would weaken the low-reserve claim.", "Immunoblot/targeted proteomics (not spot gels) should confirm decreased HK2 and PFKP protein and increased MPC2 and complex-I subunit protein in APOE4; if HK2/PFKP protein is unchanged while transcripts fall, the bottleneck step is not implemented at the protein level and the mechanism weakens.", "Functional consequence: on acute stimulation (LPS or ATP/P2X7), APOE4 microglia should show a blunted early ECAR/lactate burst and blunted glycolysis-dependent responses relative to APOE3, and re-expression of HK2 (or growth in galactose to force oxidation, which should equalise the genotypes) should shift the difference; no genotype difference in stimulated ECAR would weaken the hypothesis.", "Technical control: re-analysis with spike-in or housekeeping-anchored normalisation must retain the ETC-subunit up-shift relative to matched non-mitochondrial genes; if the ETC coherence disappears after renormalisation, the mitochondrial arm of the mechanism is an artifact of the global positive shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_144", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype (cell-intrinsic, isogenic background) shifts the microglial transcriptional program while cells are unstimulated (mock).", "Transcripts for the committed glycolytic control points expressed in these microglia are lower in APOE4 (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2), whereas glucose uptake capacity transcripts are higher (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3); we infer, but did not measure, that maximal glycolytic flux capacity (glucose-\u003elactate) is reduced relative to glucose entry, making hexokinase/PFK the rate-limiting node.", "In parallel, transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD) and for TCA enzymes (gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) are higher in APOE4; the inferred consequence is that the pyruvate that is produced is preferentially imported and oxidised rather than reduced to lactate.", "A coherent, near-uniform increase of nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunit transcripts (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME) together with mitochondrial import/carrier transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11) indicates increased build-up of oxidative machinery; respiration rate itself is inferred, not observed.", "Increased citrate carrier and cytosolic acetyl-CoA/lipogenic transcripts (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DHCR24) predict that a share of mitochondrially generated citrate is exported and used for fatty-acid desaturation and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification rather than for full oxidation, providing a carbon sink that keeps the TCA cycle turning.", "Anaplerotic and uncoupling transcripts (gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:SLC1A5, gene:UCP2) suggest partial substitution of glutamine-derived carbon and reduced coupling efficiency, so the increased oxidative machinery need not translate into proportionally increased ATP output.", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia are oxidation-dependent with low glycolytic reserve, and should fail to mount a rapid glycolytic burst when acutely challenged, while accumulating esterified lipid."], "title": "APOE4 microglia constrain the glycolytic commitment step and reroute glucose carbon into mitochondrial oxidation and citrate-derived lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.050880626223091974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24097294422261795, "cosine_similarity": 0.3380089124783608, "direction_accuracy": 0.08576051779935275, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_144", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6131035598705502, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.050880626223091974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24097294422261795, "cosine_similarity": 0.3380089124783608, "direction_accuracy": 0.08576051779935275, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6131035598705502, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.615606, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 258}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_027", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so all enrichment statements are relative ranks within this list (global median log fold change +1.46, 1705/2212 positive), not genome-wide enrichment; the logarithm base is unspecified and is left uninterpreted.", "Rank-based comparisons are assumed robust to the unexplained global positive shift, which may be a normalisation or composition artefact of the pseudobulked 10X Flex data.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme capacity for HK/PFK and for mitochondrial oxidation at least ordinally; no enzyme activity, metabolite, flux or lipidomic measurement was supplied.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous corroboration only; no protein in this dataset is uniquely identified, and no glycolytic entry enzyme is unambiguously measured at the protein level.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values may be inflated by pseudoreplication across cells; effect ranks are used in preference to p-values.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to have generated a genotype-specific substrate environment that alone accounts for the microglial transcript pattern.", "The assigned focus on acyl-chain remodelling and glycerolipid synthesis was tested and rejected as the primary mechanism (see analysis.md); lipid catabolism is retained only as the inferred substrate feeding Step 4."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a restriction at the committed glucose-entry step of glycolysis (HK2/PFKP transcripts are among the most depleted in the dataset) while transcripts for lysosomal acidification/hydrolysis, lipid-substrate uptake and mitochondrial pyruvate/fatty-acid oxidation are coordinately among the most elevated. We hypothesise that this configuration makes APOE4 microglia dependent on lysosome-derived lipid and mitochondrial oxidation for ATP and limits the rapid glycolytic commitment normally used to power actin-based motility and phagocytic effector functions, which is reflected transcriptionally by a coordinately reduced leukocyte cytoskeletal/effector module (SPN, MYH9, ACTB, FAM49B/CYRIB, ARHGAP30, CSF1, CTSS). Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: extracellular flux analysis with sequential glucose and oligomycin plus 2-deoxyglucose should show APOE4 microglia with a lower glycolytic reserve and a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio than isogenic APOE3; forced expression of HK2 (or bypassing the entry step with exogenous fructose-1,6-bisphosphate or a membrane-permeant glucose-6-phosphate precursor) should selectively raise APOE4 ECAR and restore the depleted motility/effector transcripts (SPN, MYH9, FAM49B, CTSS) and measured migration/phagocytic uptake toward APOE3 levels. If HK2 restoration raises ECAR but leaves the effector module and phagocytic index unchanged, the causal link in Steps 5-6 is falsified.", "Etomoxir or CPT1/beta-oxidation blockade, or v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1, should cause a larger fall in basal OCR and a larger AMP-activated stress response in APOE4 than APOE3, and APOE4 should fail to compensate by raising ECAR; equal glycolytic compensation in both genotypes would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Stable-isotope tracing should show a lower fraction of U-13C-glucose carbon in lactate and citrate and a higher fraction of 13C-palmitate or 13C-lysosomally derived lipid carbon in citrate in APOE4 than APOE3; comparable glucose-derived citrate labelling in the two genotypes would falsify Steps 2 and 4.", "Targeted immunoblot or activity assay should show reduced hexokinase and PFK protein/activity in APOE4 while downstream enzymes such as aldolase and transaldolase (candidates in protein_spot:038) are unchanged or increased; unchanged or increased hexokinase activity in APOE4 would falsify Step 1-2 and favour a transcript-only artefact.", "If the mechanism is a metabolic bottleneck rather than a fixed transcriptional identity, an acute LPS or fibrillar-amyloid challenge should elicit a blunted glycolytic burst in APOE4 despite comparable or greater CXCL8/CCL2 induction; an intact glycolytic burst with normal migration under challenge would weaken the whole hypothesis.", "Because no lipidomic data were supplied, a direct test is required: APOE4 microglia should accumulate lysosome-associated neutral lipid and show higher lysosomal lipid hydrolysis rate; absence of any measurable lipid-substrate excess or lysosomal expansion in APOE4 would remove the inferred substrate supply in Step 3-4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show markedly reduced transcripts for the committed, effectively irreversible glycolytic entry enzymes hexokinase and phosphofructokinase (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) against a dataset whose median log fold change is +1.46, i.e. these sit in the bottom 4-21th percentile of the selected list, while downstream glycolytic transcripts (gene:GPI, gene:ENO1) and glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) are only at or near the list background.", "Step 2 (inferred flux, primary bottleneck): we infer that lowered hexokinase/PFK capacity, not glucose import or downstream glycolytic enzyme content, is the rate-limiting step for glucose-derived carbon and for any rapid, inducible glycolytic burst in APOE4 microglia.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, compensating supply): transcripts for lysosomal acidification and lipid-directed hydrolysis (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB), for scavenger/lipid uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:ABCA7, gene:MGLL) and for mitochondrial substrate import and oxidation (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B) are coordinately high.", "Step 4 (inferred flux and localisation): we infer that APOE4 microglia meet ATP and acetyl-CoA demand by routing internalised and lysosomally hydrolysed lipid, plus residual pyruvate, into the mitochondrial matrix for beta-oxidation and TCA/oxidative phosphorylation, i.e. a shifted oxidative-to-glycolytic flux ratio rather than a globally raised total ATP flux.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): because actin-driven motility, membrane ruffling and phagocytic engulfment in myeloid cells are supported by locally generated, hexokinase-dependent glycolytic ATP, the entry-step restriction limits the biosynthetic and cytoskeletal effector programme rather than cytokine transcription per se.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, read-out): consistent with Step 5, a leukocyte cytoskeletal/effector transcript module is coordinately depleted (gene:SPN, gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB, gene:FAM49B, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:SEMA4A, gene:CSF1, gene:CTSS), whereas chemokine/antigen-handling transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:CD74, gene:LYZ) remain high, so the predicted phenotype is reduced motile-phagocytic capacity with preserved or increased secretory output, not global immune silencing.", "Step 7 (inferred causal direction, unproven): we propose APOE4 acts upstream through altered lipid delivery and lysosomal load; the alternative direction, in which an oxidative/lysosomal transcriptional programme is primary and the glycolytic entry genes fall secondarily, is not excluded by these data."], "title": "Glucose-commitment bottleneck at hexokinase/PFK forces APOE4 microglia onto lysosome-fed mitochondrial oxidation and suppresses the motile-phagocytic effector module"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24914152789572794, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25872010445493965, "cosine_similarity": 0.33774458153905784, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6156957928802589, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24914152789572794, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25872010445493965, "cosine_similarity": 0.33774458153905784, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6156957928802589, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.155255, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 259}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected significant differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LIPA, CTSA, LGMN, ATG/LC3 genes and most LXR targets have no supplied row).", "Program membership was fixed a priori from canonical annotation (unverified background knowledge) before signs were inspected; all represented members, including discordant ones, are reported. Coherence is descriptive; genes are not independent and no formal enrichment test is claimed.", "Transcript increases in hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and receptors are assumed to translate into some increase in lysosome number/hydrolase content; hydrolase activity, acidification, cargo flux and cholesterol egress rate were not measured.", "SREBP-target transcript induction is assumed to report a low ER-accessible sterol pool; this pool was not measured, and the co-occurring APOE/ABCA7/MYLIP increases indicate the sensing picture is mixed rather than a uniform sterol deficit.", "2D-gel spots contain 2-6 candidate identities each and are dominated by keratin/actin contaminants; no spot is treated as identification of an individual protein, and spot-level directions are used only for compatibility testing.", "Effects predicted here apply to the measured mock condition; any additional degradative shortfall would be a reserve limitation revealed only by a future cargo challenge, not an established ongoing defect.", "Astrocyte co-culture provides lipid/lipoprotein cargo; the microglial genotype effect is assumed to be cell-autonomous in direction, which was not tested."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (isogenic vs APOE3, co-cultured with astrocytes), the dominant coherent transcriptional change is a coordinated increase in the uptake-to-lysosome axis (scavenger/opsonic receptors, endosome maturation, v-ATPase and luminal hydrolases, TFEB/MITF) that occurs together with, rather than instead of, induction of SREBP-type sterol-synthesis genes; we propose that APOE4 shifts lipid cargo into a larger, transcriptionally reinforced endolysosomal compartment from which sterol return to the ER-accessible pool is proportionally insufficient, so cells simultaneously build degradative capacity, re-synthesise and re-esterify sterol, and maintain a low-grade chemokine output. Measured values are transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances; expansion, egress rate and hydrolase activity are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/biochemistry in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show greater LAMP1+ compartment volume, higher filipin-stainable unesterified cholesterol within LAMP1+ organelles and more neutral-lipid droplets than isogenic APOE3, while the ER-accessible sterol pool (ALOD4/D4H probe) is equal or lower. If the ER-accessible pool is higher in APOE4 while SREBF2 targets remain up, or if lysosomal cholesterol is not increased, the sequestration step is weakened.", "Prospective flux test: pulse-chase of BODIPY- or [3H]-cholesteryl-ester-labelled lipoprotein/apoptotic-cell cargo should show comparable or faster internalisation but slower conversion of lysosomal free cholesterol into ER-esterified cholesterol in APOE4. Equal egress kinetics with higher hydrolase activity would favour successful adaptation/higher throughput and falsify the proposed routing limitation.", "Prospective rescue: bypassing lysosomal sterol export with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should normalise the SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) and reduce droplet load in APOE4 with little effect in APOE3; failure to normalise these transcripts would weaken the mechanism and favour a primary transcriptional lipogenic drive.", "Prospective discrimination against 'general activation': acute TFEB inhibition or v-ATPase inhibition should exaggerate the APOE4-specific sterol-synthesis and chemokine signature more than in APOE3, whereas if APOE4 simply runs a globally higher biosynthetic state, these perturbations should affect both genotypes proportionally.", "Prospective proteomic follow-up: targeted immunoblot/activity assay (Magic Red for CTSB, DQ-BSA, CTSS activity) should show increased CTSB/CTSD mature forms but decreased CTSS activity in APOE4; uniformly increased activity of all cathepsins including CTSS would contradict the altered-processing-composition step, and uniformly decreased activity would contradict the capacity-expansion step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4-associated lipoprotein/lipid ligand handling increases engagement of uptake and opsonic receptors: transcripts for SCARB1 (+8.22), CD36, MRC1, MERTK/GAS6, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, FCGR1A/FCGR3A, ITGB5, ANXA1 (+4.15) are higher (16/17 represented members positive), consistent with (but not proof of) increased routing of lipid-rich cargo into endosomes.", "Cargo delivery is matched by a transcriptional endolysosomal expansion program: TFEB (+2.38) and MITF (+1.03) with endosome-maturation and fusion machinery (RAB7A, MON1B, VPS18, PIK3C3, VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B, AP3D1, DNM2) and lysosomal structure/acidification genes (LAMP1, SCARB2, CLN3, NPC2, SLC17A5, nine v-ATPase subunits all positive).", "Luminal hydrolase transcripts rise broadly (GAA +9.96, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, MAN2B1, GLA, AGA, DNASE2; 34/37 members of the combined degradative set positive, permutation p_pos~0.02 against this 77%-positive selected list), indicating higher capacity for glycosphingolipid/glycogen/protein cargo processing at the transcript level.", "Despite increased uptake and hydrolase transcripts, the sterol-sensing output behaves as if ER-accessible cholesterol is low: SREBF1/SREBF2 and downstream HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, plus LDLR and INSIG1 are all positive (11/11 represented). We infer that sterol egress from the endolysosome to the ER lags cargo influx, i.e. sterol is compartmentally mis-distributed rather than globally depleted.", "The diverted lipid is directed to esterification/storage and APOE/ABCA7-dependent redistribution (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, APOE +1.24, ABCA7 +2.14), predicting neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation in APOE4 microglia in the measured mock condition.", "The same loaded, expanded compartment supports a low-grade secretory/inflammatory tone (CXCL8, CCL2, CXCL1/2/3, IL18, NLRP3, MYD88 positive) while proteolytic composition is qualitatively altered rather than uniformly increased (CTSS -5.57, IDS -1.56, LAPTM5 -1.28; cathepsin- and ATP6V1E1-containing 2D spots move in both directions)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route more lipid-rich cargo into an expanded endolysosomal compartment while ER-accessible sterol remains low, driving a sequestration-plus-resynthesis state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264589176633865, "cosine_similarity": 0.3376278365162171, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6228640776699029, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264589176633865, "cosine_similarity": 0.3376278365162171, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6228640776699029, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1230135, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 63}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46). All enrichment statements are made relative to that list's own background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and could be distorted by normalisation or compositional effects.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effects are therefore not assumed to be on the same scale (protein spots are log2).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for lysosomal protein content; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, organelle volume, mTORC1 activity and TFEB nuclear localisation were not measured and are inferred only.", "Protein spots have 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; a single spot may contain several proteoforms, so directional agreement with a named transcript is weak evidence.", "Lysosomal lipid content, cholesteryl esters, sphingolipids and lipid droplets were not measured in this dataset; the lipid-load bottleneck is an inference, not an observation.", "Key egress and efflux genes (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, TFE3) are absent from the supplied list; absence is uninformative because the list is selected.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; the astrocyte genotype and the lipoprotein composition of the medium are not stated, so part of the lipid delivery term may be extrinsic to the microglial genotype.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, and some reported effects are very large (up to 15.5), so individual gene effect sizes are treated as unreliable; the argument rests on set-level coherence.", "Single genotype pair, single timepoint (day 30) and mock treatment only: no time course to distinguish a cause from a chronic adapted state."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 primarily by a coherent, coordinated upregulation of the TFEB/MITF (CLEAR) lysosomal-biogenesis program together with lipoprotein-uptake and lipid-esterification transcripts. We propose that the rate-limiting step is disposal (hydrolysis plus export) of lipoprotein-derived cholesterol and sphingolipid delivered to the endolysosome: delivery exceeds clearance capacity, luminal lipid accumulates, TFEB/MITF are activated, and the resulting hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript increase is a compensatory response that does not normalise lipid flux, leaving APOE4 microglia in a lysosome-expanded, ester-storing state. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript and spot measurements are abundances, and all flux, localisation and activity statements are inferences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: culturing APOE4 and APOE3 microglia for 48-72 h in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or with SR-B1/CD36 blockade (e.g. BLT-1 plus anti-CD36), should collapse the genotype difference in CLEAR transcripts (GBA, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, ATP6V1H) by more than half and reduce TFEB nuclear fraction in APOE4 toward APOE3. If CLEAR transcripts and TFEB nuclear localisation stay elevated in APOE4 after lipid delivery is normalised, the load-driven-compensation mechanism is wrong and a cell-intrinsic, uptake-independent TFEB activation should be preferred.", "Imaging: filipin plus LAMP1 co-staining should show higher lysosome-localised unesterified cholesterol and greater LAMP1-positive volume per cell in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal lysosomal cholesterol and equal lysosomal volume would weaken the mechanism at Steps 2-4.", "Capacity test (flux, not abundance): per-lysosome degradation rate of BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester-loaded or DQ-BSA-loaded lipoprotein should be equal to or lower in APOE4 despite the higher hydrolase transcripts, i.e. the activity-to-transcript ratio should fall. Finding a higher per-lysosome degradation flux in APOE4 would refute the 'bottleneck' framing and favour a simple higher-throughput lysosome.", "Genetic test of compensation: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should lower CLEAR transcripts and hydrolase activity and increase lysosomal lipid accumulation and cell stress, while TFEB overexpression in APOE3 should reproduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase signature without reproducing the SCARB1/CD36/SOAT1 uptake-storage signature. If TFEB knockdown reduces lipid accumulation instead of increasing it, the compensatory direction is inverted and the hypothesis fails.", "Esterification test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) in APOE4 should convert cholesteryl esters to free cholesterol, further raise CLEAR transcripts and increase toxicity relative to APOE3. No change in CLEAR transcripts would weaken Step 5.", "Lipidomic prediction for the planned lipid readout: APOE4 microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester and glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin species than APOE3 under mock treatment. Equal or lower neutral-lipid and sphingolipid levels in APOE4 would weaken the whole hypothesis.", "Specificity control: the competing mitochondrial-oxidative interpretation predicts increased oxygen consumption rate in APOE4; if APOE4 shows higher maximal respiration but no difference in lysosomal volume, lysosomal cholesterol or TFEB localisation, the mitochondrial program, not the lysosomal one, is the primary axis and hyp_041 should be discarded."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid receptors and the ligand itself (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:APOE +1.24). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery flux of astrocyte- and self-derived lipoprotein lipid into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Luminal hydrolysis and export of that lipid (unesterified cholesterol, sphingomyelin, glycosphingolipid) is the proposed bottleneck. The relevant egress/efflux components NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied differential-expression list, so lysosomal lipid content and export capacity are inferred, not observed.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred signalling): Lipid-loaded, capacity-limited lysosomes are proposed to lower mTORC1 output on the lysosomal surface and activate the MiT/TFE transcription factors; consistent with this, gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) are elevated while gene:CALM2 (-1.00) and gene:DEPDC5 (+1.34) indicate rewired lysosomal nutrient-sensing components. TFEB nuclear localisation and mTORC1 activity were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): The CLEAR output module is coherently induced above the already positively shifted background of this selected gene list: 42 CLEAR genes, 95% up, median log fold change +2.01 versus list background +1.46 (Mann-Whitney p = 2.6e-3). It includes all ten measured v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30), acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:DNASE2 +2.03, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81), membrane/trafficking components (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SCARB2 +1.06) and the sphingolipid hydrolase set specifically (12 genes, median +2.40, p = 6.0e-3). We interpret this as an inferred expansion and acidification of the lysosomal compartment; organelle volume, pH and enzyme activity were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred sterol sensing): Despite elevated uptake transcripts, the ER sterol-sensing arm behaves as if sterol were low, consistent with cholesterol being sequestered in lysosomes and esterified rather than reaching the ER sensor: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, together with esterification/storage enzymes gene:SOAT1 and gene:DGAT1. Sterol location and cholesteryl-ester content were not measured.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype, partly counter-supported): The net inferred state is a lipid-laden, lysosome-expanded microglial phenotype with a shifted, not uniformly increased, protease repertoire: gene:CTSS is strongly decreased (-5.57) and gene:IDS (-1.56), gene:M6PR (-1.72) and gene:LAPTM5 (-1.28) fall, so the program is selective rather than a blanket lysosomal induction. Protein spots containing lysosomal hydrolase candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027 up; protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064 down), which we treat as ambiguous, possibly proteoform-level, evidence rather than confirmation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB/MITF-driven CLEAR lysosome expansion that compensates for a lipid-disposal bottleneck in the endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08352635179757917, "cosine_similarity": 0.3369164033727036, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mean_absolute_error": 0.647957928802589, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13307240704500978, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08352635179757917, "cosine_similarity": 0.3369164033727036, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.647957928802589, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9165565, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 260}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_064", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression selection with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are therefore made on within-list rank/percentile deviations, not on raw sign.", "Transcript abundance is a usable but imperfect proxy for enzyme and transporter capacity; no flux, metabolite, oxygen-consumption, extracellular-acidification or lipid measurement is supplied in these files.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as non-identifying; no protein is asserted to be measured.", "Key nodes of the proposed route (ACLY, ACACA, FASN, CS, MDH2, GOT2, G6PD, PLIN2, LDHA, PKM) are absent from the supplied list and are inferred, not observed.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so the contrast reflects genotype rather than treatment.", "Unverified background knowledge (no literature access in this session) is used only for pathway membership assignments, not as evidence."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the primary metabolic bottleneck is the committing step of upper glycolysis (hexokinase/phosphofructokinase, transcripts gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3 among the most negative in a globally upward-shifted differential list), not glucose uptake (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3 higher). We hypothesise that this restriction, together with a lowered oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1), shifts APOE4 microglia onto mitochondrial oxidation of non-glycolytic substrates (gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:GLS, gene:BCAT2) whose carbon is exported as citrate (gene:SLC25A1) and consumed by an SREBP-driven esterification programme (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1), producing APOE4-biased neutral-lipid/sterol-ester storage with an NADPH supply displaced off the pentose-phosphate pathway (gene:NNT, gene:ME1). All statements about flux, localisation and direction are inferred from transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with U-13C-glucose, APOE4 microglia should show a LOWER fractional 13C enrichment in triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester acyl chains and in M+2 citrate than APOE3, while U-13C-glutamine should give HIGHER enrichment of APOE4 lipid carbon. If APOE4 droplet lipid is instead predominantly glucose-derived, or glucose and glutamine contributions are equal between genotypes, the bottleneck placement at HK2/PFKP with glutamine-fed citrate export is wrong.", "SLC25A1 inhibition or knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid/sterol-ester droplet content toward APOE3 levels without lowering glucose uptake or SLC2A1/SLC2A3 transcripts. Unchanged droplet content after effective SLC25A1 loss would weaken the citrate-export step.", "Extracellular-flux profiling should show APOE4 with reduced glycolytic reserve (small ECAR rise after oligomycin) and preserved or higher basal oxygen consumption; MPC inhibition (UK-5099) should lower APOE4 oxygen consumption at least as much as APOE3. A Warburg-like APOE4 pattern (higher ECAR, larger glycolytic reserve, lower OCR) would falsify the mechanism.", "Ordering test: SCD or SREBP inhibition should reduce APOE4 droplet lipid while leaving gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1 and gene:HK2 differences intact; conversely, forced HK2 re-expression should raise glycolytic reserve and lactate output. If HK2 restoration also abolishes the citrate/lipogenic transcript differences, the upper-glycolysis step is upstream in a way this linear scheme does not capture.", "NADPH-margin test: because the PPP branch is predicted to be low, APOE4 microglia should be more sensitive than APOE3 to G6PD inhibition or to GPX4 inhibition/lipid-peroxidation challenge, and NNT loss should exaggerate this. Equal or lower APOE4 sensitivity would weaken step 2.", "Negative control: glucose-uptake assays (2-NBDG or 3H-2-deoxyglucose initial rate) should not be lower in APOE4; a clear reduction in uptake would relocate the bottleneck to transport and falsify the stated commitment-step claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for the glucose-committing enzymes are strongly below the global shift of this DE list (gene:HK2 -3.67, 4th percentile; gene:PFKP -3.08, 6th; gene:HK3 -1.12, 21st; list median +1.46), while glucose-transporter transcripts are above it (gene:SLC2A3 86th, gene:SLC2A1 69th). Inferred: glucose entry capacity is not limiting, but phosphorylation/commitment of glucose-6-phosphate flux is reduced in APOE4.", "Measured: pentose-phosphate transcripts are low (gene:PGD 19th, gene:TALDO1 9th percentile). Inferred: less glucose carbon is diverted to ribose-5-phosphate and to PPP-derived cytosolic NADPH, so NADPH for reductive lipid synthesis must come from transhydrogenase/malic-enzyme routes (gene:NNT 76th, gene:ME1 45th).", "Measured: the mitochondrial pyruvate-import, PDH-activating, TCA and malate-aspartate-shuttle module is coherently high relative to the same list (gene:MPC2 99th, gene:DLD 95th, gene:PDP1 78th, gene:OGDH 99th, gene:MDH1 99th, gene:GOT1 97th, gene:ACO2 84th, gene:IDH3G 88th, gene:SLC25A11 91st, gene:SLC25A5 95th), alongside anaplerotic amino-acid catabolism (gene:BCAT2 97th, gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS). Inferred: mitochondrial carbon oxidation in APOE4 is supported preferentially by glutamine/BCAA and shuttled reducing equivalents rather than by high glycolytic pyruvate output.", "Measured: the mitochondrial citrate carrier and the acetate-to-acetyl-CoA enzyme are high (gene:SLC25A1 91st, gene:ACSS2 77th). Inferred: a larger fraction of TCA-cycle citrate is exported to the cytosol as lipogenic carbon instead of being fully oxidised; this export node, not ATP demand, sets the fate of oxidised carbon.", "Measured: an SREBP/lipid-esterification and lipoprotein-uptake programme is elevated (gene:SREBF1 92nd, gene:SCD 89th, gene:DHCR24 85th, gene:DHCR7, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1 99th, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:CD36), with a lysosomal/lipid-handling shift (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:MGLL, gene:LPCAT1, gene:APOE). Inferred: cytosolic acetyl-CoA plus imported lipid is desaturated and esterified into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester rather than oxidised.", "Inferred net state: APOE4 microglia operate with low spare glycolytic capacity, mitochondrial oxidation of non-glucose substrates, a citrate-export carbon leak into storage lipid, and a narrow non-PPP NADPH margin - a configuration that predicts droplet accumulation and lipid-peroxidation sensitivity without requiring any change in glucose uptake.", "Ambiguous protein-level support only: protein_spot:038 (candidates ALDOA/ALDOC/SORD/ARPC1B/TKT, +1.07) and protein_spot:072 (candidates include PGAM1, +0.585) are higher in APOE4, and protein_spot:001 (candidates include HK3) is not significantly changed; these spots cannot identify a single protein and are used only as weak, non-decisive evidence."], "title": "APOE4 microglia commit less glucose at the HK2/PFKP step and route mitochondrial citrate carbon into stored neutral lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3323671675959089, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.33149441405169067, "cosine_similarity": 0.3357424035544707, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6273462783171521, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3323671675959089, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.33149441405169067, "cosine_similarity": 0.3357424035544707, "direction_accuracy": 0.22815533980582525, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6273462783171521, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7585645, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 261}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_033", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, 77.1% positive, all adjusted p\u003c0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; program sign patterns were judged against that 77.1% up background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, ABCA1/ABCG1, most core autophagy genes: only 2/26 represented) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a marker of program engagement, not of enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, degradative flux, sterol transport rate or SREBP proteolytic processing; every flux/localization statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "2-D protein spots are multi-candidate (2-6 candidate genes each, 92 spots, 208 candidate identities); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Spots are used only for compatibility: spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases split in direction (13 up / 5 down of 20; e.g. protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 up vs protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38), which is compatible with isoform/processing redistribution but confirms no individual protein.", "Members of each program were chosen from a fixed a priori pathway vocabulary written before looking at directions; all represented members are reported including sign-discordant ones (CTSS, IDS, M6PR, VPS13B, OSBPL8, ACSL4, RAB27A).", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment; effects attributed here to lipid routing could partly reflect the astrocyte co-culture lipoprotein supply or genotype-dependent differences in microglial maturation state rather than a cell-autonomous endolysosomal difference.", "The proposed cycle is claimed as an ongoing state in the measured mock condition; any additional degradative shortfall (e.g. on myelin, apoptotic-cell or amyloid challenge) is a predicted reduced reserve that these data do not demonstrate."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes (day 30), APOE4 cells differ from APOE3 not by a generic loss of lysosomal capacity but by an altered lipid-routing state: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, MiT/TFE-associated lysosomal biogenesis (TFEB, MITF), v-ATPase subunits, luminal hydrolases and endosomal sorting machinery are coordinately higher, yet the ER sterol-sensing arm reads sterol-poor (SREBF1/SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, EBP, SCD all higher) with esterification/storage genes (SOAT1, DGAT1) also higher. The most parsimonious explanation is that cholesterol derived from internalized cargo is sequestered in the endolysosomal/esterified compartment rather than delivered to the ER regulatory pool, producing a self-reinforcing cycle of continued uptake, lysosomal expansion and futile de novo sterol synthesis, with a shift of metabolic transcripts from glycolytic/oxidative-PPP commitment steps toward OXPHOS subunits. Causality is not established; only abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective imaging/biochemistry in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia will show greater lysosomal/esterified cholesterol (filipin or BODIPY-cholesterol colocalized with LAMP1; cholesteryl-ester mass) together with a LOWER ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4 or GRAM1b sensor) than APOE3. If ER-accessible cholesterol is equal or higher in APOE4 while SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated, the routing/sequestration mechanism is weakened and a sterol-independent driver of the SREBP program is favoured.", "Prospective perturbation: relieving lysosomal sterol sequestration with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or SOAT1/ACAT inhibition to unmask free sterol) will normalize the APOE4-vs-APOE3 elevation of LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24 and SREBF2 by at least half, and reduce the TFEB/v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript elevation, without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts to below APOE3 levels. Failure of cyclodextrin to lower the SREBP-target elevation would seriously weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective flux discrimination between failed compensation and increased throughput: in a pulse-chase with fluorescent lipoprotein or myelin plus DQ-BSA, bulk proteolytic processing rate in mock APOE4 will be equal to or GREATER than APOE3 (no global hydrolytic block), while cargo-derived sterol reaching the ER, measured as post-load suppression of SREBP-target transcripts, will be delayed or blunted. Markedly slower bulk degradation with no ER-delivery-specific delay would favour a general lysosomal-capacity deficit instead.", "Prospective genetic test of hierarchy: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia will reduce v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts and increase lysosomal lipid accumulation, but will NOT normalize the SREBP-target elevation; if TFEB knockdown abolishes the SREBP-target difference, lysosomal biogenesis is the driver rather than a response, contradicting the proposed ordering.", "Prospective challenge-only prediction (reduced reserve, not an ongoing defect): after an acute lipid or myelin load, APOE4 microglia will accumulate more undegraded cargo per cell than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; equal accumulation would indicate the expanded machinery is fully compensatory."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors (18/18 represented members positive vs a 77% positive background in this selected list: SCARB1 +8.2, SIRPA +2.3, CD47 +2.2, ABCA7 +2.1, FCGR1A, COLEC12, CLEC7A, CD14, CD36, MRC1, ITGB5, GAS6, MERTK, TREM2, STAB1, FCGR3A), which is inferred (not measured) to route more lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system in the astrocyte co-culture.", "Cargo load is matched by transcriptional expansion of degradative capacity: MiT/TFE factors (TFEB +2.4, MITF +1.0), all represented v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H +6.9, ATP6V1A +4.2, ATP6V0C +3.5, and 5 more), most hydrolases (GBA +6.7, NAGLU +5.9, HEXA +5.7, SMPD1 +5.6, CTSB +5.5, CTSD +2.9), and endosomal sorting/retromer/ESCRT genes (VPS26A +4.9, SNX3 +3.9, VPS37B +3.9, VPS35L +3.5, RAB7A +2.7); this argues against a global collapse of lysosomal machinery expression in the measured condition.", "Despite high uptake plus expanded lysosomal machinery, the ER sterol-sensing output behaves as if cholesterol-deficient: 11/11 represented SREBP-pathway members are positive (SREBF1 +4.7, SCD +4.2, DHCR24 +3.7, DHCR7 +2.7, LSS +2.3, ACAT2 +2.0, INSIG1 +1.9, LDLR +1.5, EBP +1.3, SREBF2 +1.1, HMGCS1 +1.1). This inferred mismatch between cargo influx and ER sterol repletion is the central proposed defect: sterol handoff/egress, not bulk hydrolysis.", "Cargo-derived and newly synthesized sterol/fatty acid is directed to esterification and storage rather than to regulatory pools (SOAT1 +1.3, DGAT1 +1.7, FABP5 +1.1, FABP3 +1.4, APOE +1.2, NPC2 +1.2), while transcripts for an ER-endosome lipid-transfer protein and a long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase are lower (OSBPL8 -1.9, ACSL4 -2.1), consistent with altered routing between compartments rather than with sterol scarcity of the whole cell.", "The routing state is accompanied by a metabolic re-balance: all 9 represented OXPHOS subunits are positive (UQCRC2 +4.0, COX7A2 +3.4, ATP5F1B +2.7, median +2.2), whereas glycolytic commitment and oxidative-PPP transcripts fall against the up-skewed background (HK2 -3.7, PFKP -3.1, TALDO1 -2.3, PGD -1.3, HK3 -1.1; 5/9 negative, one-sided p~0.034), even though glucose transporters rise (SLC2A3 +3.7, SLC2A1 +2.4).", "Net predicted cell state in mock: sustained lysosomal-lipid retention with continued sterol synthesis and esterification, i.e. an ongoing routing abnormality with expanded but non-satiating degradative machinery, plus a partially non-uniform hydrolase program (CTSS -5.6, IDS -1.6, M6PR -1.7) that could locally limit specific substrate classes and hydrolase delivery."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an uptake-expanded endolysosomal state in which cargo-derived sterol is retained/re-esterified instead of reaching the ER sensing pool, so lysosomal biogenesis and SREBP sterol synthesis are co-activated"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1918461264610248, "cosine_similarity": 0.3356658272814896, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6022362459546926, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1918461264610248, "cosine_similarity": 0.3356658272814896, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6022362459546926, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.946968, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 64}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome sample; the background sign ratio in this list is ~77% positive (1705/2212), so a mostly-positive redox/lipid program is compared against that skewed background, not a 50/50 null.", "The RNA log-fold-change base is not specified and is not assumed to be log2; protein-spot values are explicitly log2. Effects across the two modalities are not placed on a common numeric scale.", "Absence of canonical redox genes not in this DE list (e.g., CAT, SOD1/2, NQO1, HMOX1, KEAP1, NFE2L2, most PEX genes) is treated as unknown/unmeasured-in-this-list, not as evidence of no change.", "Protein spots 017 and 077 each list multiple candidate genes (CAT with CORO1C, ENTPD5; PRDX2 with several keratins/actin/RAB1A); the spot-level fold-change cannot be attributed to a single candidate protein.", "Transcript and protein-spot abundance changes are treated as indirect evidence for pathway engagement, not as direct measures of enzymatic activity, ROS levels, GSH/GSSG ratio, or peroxisomal oxidation flux, none of which are supplied.", "This is a mock-treatment (baseline) comparison; the hypothesis describes a baseline transcriptional/proteomic state difference, not a demonstrated functional deficit that would only appear under an oxidative or metabolic challenge."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, elevated cholesterol/lipid-handling transcripts (SREBF1, LDLR, CD36, SOAT1, ABCA7, APOE) co-occur with a coordinated rise in peroxisomal beta-oxidation and thiol/peroxide-detoxifying transcripts and protein spots (ACOX1, SCP2, PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, GSS, TXNL1, TXNDC17, TXNL4A, NNT, FTH1, protein_spot:017 candidate CAT, protein_spot:077 candidate PRDX2), while the peroxisomal VLCFA-CoA importer ABCD1 is reduced. This pattern is more consistent with an actively engaged antioxidant/peroxisomal-remodeling response to increased lipid oxidative burden than with an unopposed or failing redox defense, but whether the response is sufficient to normalize net oxidative damage is not established by abundance data alone.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: measuring steady-state H2O2/ROS levels and the GSH:GSSG ratio in mock-treated APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should discriminate compensation states: if APOE4 net ROS/oxidized-glutathione is not elevated despite higher PRDX/GPX4/GSS/TXN transcripts, this supports engaged, adequate compensation; if net ROS/oxidized glutathione is elevated despite these increases, this indicates insufficient compensation. A finding of no genotype difference in ROS, GSH:GSSG, or peroxisomal beta-oxidation (ACOX1 activity/VLCFA oxidation rate) despite the transcript/protein differences would weaken the claim that this signature reflects a functionally engaged redox/peroxisomal mechanism.", "Prospective, discriminating perturbation: CRISPRi/siRNA knockdown of ABCD1 in APOE3 microglia is predicted to raise very-long-chain fatty acid levels and induce a subset of the antioxidant program (e.g., PRDX2, GPX4) toward APOE4-like levels if reduced ABCD1 is a proximal driver of the peroxisomal/redox signature; failure of ABCD1 knockdown to induce this program would weaken the proposed link between altered peroxisomal fatty-acid import and the antioxidant transcriptional response, favoring an alternative driver such as generalized lipid burden or inflammatory/ER-stress signaling."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with markedly increased transcripts for cholesterol/lipid uptake and synthesis (SREBF1, LDLR, CD36, SOAT1, ABCA7, APOE), interpreted as increased lipid-handling burden in microglia (abundance evidence only; flux not measured).", "Increased lipid burden is expected to raise substrate delivery to fatty-acid oxidation pathways; consistent with this, the peroxisomal beta-oxidation enzyme ACOX1 and the lipid-transfer protein SCP2 transcripts are strongly elevated.", "In contrast, ABCD1, which imports very-long-chain fatty acyl-CoA into peroxisomes for oxidation, is reduced, marking a discordant node: peroxisomal fatty-acid handling capacity may be altered/rerouted rather than uniformly increased.", "Concurrently, a broad set of thiol/peroxide-detoxifying and NADPH-supplying transcripts and protein spots are elevated (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS, TXNL1, TXNDC17, TXNL4A, NNT, FTH1; protein_spot:017 CAT-candidate; protein_spot:077 PRDX2-candidate), consistent with a transcriptional/proteomic response to increased peroxide or electrophile burden from altered oxidative lipid metabolism.", "Because these antioxidant effectors are elevated rather than depleted, the observed pattern favors an engaged compensatory redox-buffering response over a collapsed antioxidant system; abundance alone cannot show whether net ROS or oxidative damage is actually normalized.", "This redox/peroxisomal signature occurs alongside, but is not shown to be causally upstream or downstream of, elevated lysosomal (CTSB, CTSD, GBA) and complement (C1QA, C1QB, C1QC, CFH) transcripts, indicating APOE4 microglia occupy a broader activated, lipid-stressed transcriptional state of which redox rebalancing is one measured component."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a lipid-burden-linked peroxisomal/antioxidant transcriptional shift consistent with engaged, not failed, redox compensation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1526370642574573, "cosine_similarity": 0.3345628770681661, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6281618122977346, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1526370642574573, "cosine_similarity": 0.3345628770681661, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6281618122977346, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.099142, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are pre-selected differential-expression results thresholded at |log fold change| \u003e= 1 in an unspecified logarithm base; 77% of rows are positive, so pathway claims are only made relative to that shifted background (permutation tests against the same 2212 rows).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, lysosomal enzyme protein and degradative activity; no enzyme activity, acidification, flux or localisation was measured.", "No lipid measurement is supplied: cholesterol, cholesteryl ester, oxysterol, lipid-droplet and ER-accessible sterol pools are inferred, never observed.", "SREBP-2 activation is inferred from target-gene direction only; SCAP, MBTPS1/2, HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1 and FDFT1 are absent from the supplied rows and SREBP cleavage was not measured.", "The proposed bottleneck rests partly on unmeasured genes (NPC1, LIPA, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B/C, ABCA1, ABCG1); NPC2 is used as a proxy for the export module, which may be wrong if the module is post-transcriptionally regulated.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions, so the 2D-gel data are treated as non-discriminating rather than confirmatory.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are isogenic and the astrocyte co-culture, differentiation state and cell-composition are assumed comparable; a differentiation/composition difference could generate the same transcript pattern.", "Direction of causality (sterol congestion -\u003e DAM-like state vs DAM-like state -\u003e lysosomal expansion) is not established by these data."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the endolysosomal system is transcriptionally expanded (MiT/TFEB-type hydrolase and v-ATPase program) and sterol delivery is increased (SCARB1, CD36, phagocytic receptors), but the lysosome-to-ER cholesterol export module is not scaled in proportion (NPC2 sits at the bottom of the lysosomal module; NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 and GRAM-domain transporters are unmeasured). We hypothesise that this mismatch creates a kinetic bottleneck at lysosomal cholesterol egress, so the ER-accessible sterol pool is functionally low despite total sterol load; the ER SCAP/INSIG sensor therefore keeps SREBP-2 target genes (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, SREBF2) and uptake receptors induced, producing a futile uptake/synthesis cycle whose overflow is routed into esterification (SOAT1) and oxysterol formation (CH25H, CYP27A1) rather than efficient APOE-mediated efflux. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute relief of lysosomal sterol with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should raise the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/D4H probe) and, within 12-24 h, lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, LDLR, HMGCS1) and SCARB1 toward APOE3 levels, with a markedly smaller effect in APOE3. If ER-accessible cholesterol does not rise, or SREBP-2 targets stay elevated after the lysosomal pool is emptied, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Imaging/biochemistry: APOE4 microglia should show more unesterified cholesterol inside LAMP1+ compartments (filipin or D4H colocalisation) with an equal or lower ER-accessible/plasma-membrane accessible pool than APOE3. Finding equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol, or a higher ER-accessible pool, in APOE4 weakens the mechanism.", "Sink-versus-block discrimination: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should increase free lysosomal/cellular cholesterol in APOE4 but only weakly suppress SREBP-2 targets if egress, not esterification, is limiting; a strong normalisation of SREBP-2 targets by SOAT1 inhibition alone would relocate the bottleneck to esterification.", "Delivery-versus-egress discrimination: SCARB1 knockdown should reduce lysosomal sterol load and lipid droplets in APOE4; if the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program and SREBP-2 targets persist unchanged after SCARB1 knockdown, uptake is not the driver and the model must be restricted to the egress step.", "Normalisation control for the global positive shift: spike-in-normalised qPCR or bulk RNA-seq should keep GAA, GBA, CTSB, SMPD1 and ATP6V1H elevated in APOE4 relative to expression-matched non-lysosomal genes; loss of this relative enrichment would show the module is a compositional/normalisation artifact.", "Functional prediction: APOE4 microglia should degrade a fluorescent cholesteryl-ester-containing lipoprotein or myelin load with normal or increased hydrolysis but delayed appearance of the sterol in the ER-accessible pool (delayed SREBP-2 shut-off after loading); equal ER delivery kinetics in APOE3 and APOE4 would weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: an internally coherent endolysosomal transcript program is higher in APOE4 (lysosomal hydrolases GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, MAN2B1; all ten detected v-ATPase subunits, e.g. ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C; MiT-family TFEB, TFEC, MITF). Inferred (not measured): increased lysosome number, acidification and degradative flux.", "Measured: sterol/lipid delivery receptors are higher in APOE4 (SCARB1 in the top 1% of all rows, CD36, MRC1, MERTK, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, LGALS3). Inferred: greater flux of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived cholesterol into the endolysosomal lumen.", "Measured mismatch: within this expanded lysosomal module the only detected sterol-export component, NPC2, is near the bottom (effect +1.17, 35th percentile of all rows) while hydrolase median is +2.75; NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 and GRAMD1A/B/C are absent from the supplied rows. Inferred bottleneck: lysosomal cholesterol egress and hand-off to the ER does not keep pace with delivery and hydrolysis.", "Inferred consequence: the ER-accessible (SCAP/INSIG-sensed) cholesterol pool is functionally low even if total cellular sterol is normal or high; this pool was not measured.", "Measured read-out consistent with step 4: every detected sterol-synthesis/sensing row is positive (DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, ACAT2 +2.04, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, EBP +1.34, MYLIP +1.28, HMGCS1 +1.08, SREBF2 +1.06, SREBF1 +4.67), i.e. an SREBP-type transcriptional output that would sustain further uptake and synthesis (a futile cycle). Inferred: SREBP-2 proteolytic activation; SREBP processing and protein were not measured.", "Measured: overflow-handling genes are elevated (SOAT1 esterification, CH25H and CYP27A1 oxysterol formation, APOE, ABCA7, PLTP), while ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured. Inferred: sterol is buffered as cholesteryl ester and side-chain oxysterols rather than cleared by efficient APOE-lipoprotein efflux.", "Inferred net state: sterol-congested, hydrolase-rich lysosomes accompanying a DAM-like transcriptional shift (ITGAX, CLEC7A, GPNMB, CTSB, CTSD, TREM2, APOE) with loss of CTSS; this is a proposed consequence, not a demonstrated cause, of the egress bottleneck."], "title": "Lysosomal cholesterol egress is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: catabolic/uptake capacity scales up while the sterol-export module does not, leaving the ER sterol sensor reading 'low'"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2168518997156888, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2481849205655083, "cosine_similarity": 0.3339292602816414, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6060420711974109, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2168518997156888, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2481849205655083, "cosine_similarity": 0.3339292602816414, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6060420711974109, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8206575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 262}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_022", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77 percent of the 2212 genes are positive (median +1.46). We therefore rely on set-level comparison against this shifted internal background rather than on raw fold-change sign, and the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme protein abundance; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, membrane potential, submitochondrial and lysosomal localization, and causal direction were not measured and are inferred.", "No lipidomic, metabolomic, flux-tracing, respirometry or imaging data were supplied. Acetyl-CoA, citrate, free cholesterol, cholesteryl ester and lipid-droplet pools are inferred quantities, not observations.", "Protein spots each map to several candidate genes and are dominated by keratin and actin candidates, so no spot is treated as a unique protein identification and none is used as primary evidence for this mechanism.", "Key rate-limiting sterol genes (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1), ACLY, FASN, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied rows, so the sterol synthesis and efflux arms are only partially observable.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex at a single timepoint with unreported replicate numbers; some genotype-associated signal may reflect altered astrocyte cross-talk, differentiation-state drift, ambient RNA, or normalization/compositional effects rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 biology.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment, so the mechanism is proposed as a baseline state difference, not a stimulus response."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coherent transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial carriers, TCA enzymes and every measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit while the committed glycolytic steps HK2 and PFKP are lower. We propose that the rate-limiting node distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is carrier-gated entry and exit of TCA carbon (mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2 and citrate carrier SLC25A1): increased carrier capacity routes pyruvate and lysosomally liberated lipid substrate into oxidation and exports citrate for cytosolic acetyl-CoA, which supports a secondary sterol/MUFA-synthesis and esterification arm (ACAT2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, SCD, SOAT1, DGAT1) that stores rather than exports lipid. The assigned sterol focus is retained only as this downstream arm, because the mevalonate/SREBP-2 gene set is directionally coherent but not enriched above the strong global upward baseline of this selected differential-expression list. All statements about flux, activity, localization, acetyl-CoA, cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet pools are inferred; only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in extracellular-flux assays, mock APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a lower ECAR/OCR ratio than isogenic APOE3, and acute MPC inhibition with UK-5099 (or MPC1/MPC2 knockdown) should abolish the genotype difference in OCR, lowering APOE4 respiration toward APOE3 with a much smaller effect in APOE3. If APOE4 OCR is not higher at baseline, or if UK-5099 lowers OCR proportionally in both genotypes, the carrier-gated bottleneck is falsified.", "SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or SLC25A1 knockdown should reduce neutral-lipid-droplet content and lower ACAT2, HMGCS1, DHCR24 and SCD transcripts preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would falsify Steps 4-5 while leaving Steps 1-3 intact.", "Stable-isotope tracing with U-13C glucose should give greater M+2 enrichment of citrate and greater 13C incorporation into newly synthesized sterol intermediates and 16:1/18:1 species in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or lower label flow into sterol in APOE4 would refute the sterol-synthesis arm and force the mechanism to be re-stated as oxidation-only.", "Blocking lysosomal acid hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/acid-lipase inhibition) should shrink the APOE4 respiration advantage if lysosomal catabolism supplies the oxidized substrate; if the APOE4 OCR advantage is unchanged, Step 3 is falsified and substrate supply must come from another source.", "Direct lipid measurement should show a higher cholesteryl-ester-to-free-cholesterol ratio and larger LipidTOX-positive droplet area in APOE4, with SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) reversing the difference. Equal ester ratios, or higher free rather than esterified sterol, would falsify Step 6.", "Global falsifier: if APOE4 microglia are instead more glycolytic (higher lactate output and ECAR with unchanged or lower OCR, consistent with the observed higher HIF1A, SLC2A1 and SLC2A3 transcripts), the entire proposed direction of carbon routing is wrong.", "Artifact control: if re-normalizing the same libraries (for example by spike-in or median-of-ratios on the full transcriptome) removes the OXPHOS/TCA set enrichment relative to background, the observation is a compositional artifact and the hypothesis loses its primary support."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for mitochondrial substrate carriers (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5) while the committed glycolytic kinases gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP are lower; this is the proposed bottleneck node. Inferred, not measured: pyruvate import flux and citrate export flux are increased and carbon is routed away from lactate.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB) and all 38 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B) are higher. Inferred: expanded respiratory-chain and TCA capacity, i.e. higher oxygen consumption per cell; respiration itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): A lysosomal hydrolase / v-ATPase / TFEB-associated program is higher (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C), together with beta-oxidation and lipid-uptake transcripts (gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR). Inferred: lysosomal catabolism liberates fatty acids and sterol that supply the mitochondrial pool created in Step 1-2; substrate flow and lysosomal localization were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred activity from measured abundance): Citrate exported through SLC25A1, plus acetate-derived acetyl-CoA (gene:ACSS2 higher), raises cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability. ACLY, ACACA and FASN were not measured, so this cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool is inferred and must not be read as observed.", "Step 5 (measured abundance): A sterol and monounsaturated-lipid synthesis arm is uniformly higher but of modest magnitude (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:SCD), consistent with, but not proof of, acetyl-CoA-supported sterol synthesis downstream of Step 4.", "Step 6 (inferred fate): Esterification transcripts (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) and oxysterol-generating transcripts (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1) are higher while the classical efflux transporters ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured (only gene:ABCA7 and gene:APOE are available). We infer that newly made and internalized lipid is preferentially esterified and stored rather than effluxed, keeping ER-accessible free sterol low and sustaining SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR) despite adequate total sterol. Cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet pools were not measured."], "title": "Carrier-gated mitochondrial carbon routing (MPC2/SLC25A1) in APOE4 microglia diverts lysosome-derived substrate into oxidation and esterified lipid storage rather than glycolysis or sterol export"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28321271646420265, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24637081497216157, "cosine_similarity": 0.3339180453787999, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6100032362459548, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28321271646420265, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24637081497216157, "cosine_similarity": 0.3339180453787999, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6100032362459548, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5036455, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 263}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_085", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive, all |effect| \u003e 1) in an unspecified logarithm base; all claims are therefore made on within-list rank rather than on absolute fold change, and the shift may partly reflect normalisation or composition rather than biology.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme and carrier capacity; enzymatic activity, metabolite pools (citrate, acetyl-CoA), transport flux and organelle localisation were not measured.", "ATP-citrate lyase, ACACA, FASN, PLIN2, NPC1 and most ER chaperones are absent from the supplied list, so the acetyl-CoA-to-malonyl-CoA step and the lipid-droplet coat are assumed, not observed.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and show their own positive shift (median +0.48, 64/92 up); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and none is used as primary support.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a cell-autonomous microglial origin of the signature is assumed but not demonstrated; replicate numbers were not supplied.", "Background pharmacology and gene-set membership used to interpret the genes is unverified literature knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the differential transcriptome is dominated by a coherent elevation of mitochondrial pyruvate/2-oxoglutarate handling and citrate/malate export machinery (MPC2, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5, GLUD1) together with the cytosolic malate-aspartate/citrate-cycle arm (MDH1, GOT1), which exceeds the concurrent rise in oxidative-phosphorylation subunit transcripts. We hypothesise that this configuration raises cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADH/NADPH-linked reducing equivalents, and that acetyl-CoA export capacity - not electron-transport capacity, not ER unfolded-protein handling - is the rate-limiting step that channels carbon into SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty acid, glycerolipid (AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, DGAT1) and sterol (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2) synthesis, yielding an APOE4 microglial state enriched in monounsaturated neutral lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester) with a parallel TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase program. Causality is not established by these data; only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with U-13C-glucose and, separately, U-13C-glutamine, APOE4 microglia should show higher fractional 13C enrichment in fatty-acyl chains and in newly synthesised sterol than isogenic APOE3, with a larger APOE4/APOE3 difference in the lipid acetyl units than in the citrate/2-oxoglutarate pools themselves; equal lipid labelling despite the transcript differences would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: inhibiting the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2) or ATP-citrate lyase (e.g. BMS-303141) should abolish the APOE4-minus-APOE3 excess in neutral lipid (BODIPY 493/503 area, triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester by lipidomics) while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcript difference (GBA, HEXA, CTSB) largely intact; persistence of the lipid excess under either inhibitor, or loss of the lysosomal difference in parallel, would weaken the proposed ordering.", "Species-level prediction: the APOE4 lipid excess should be concentrated in 16:1- and 18:1-containing triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester species and should be reversed by SCD inhibition; an excess dominated by polyunsaturated or by phospholipid/sphingolipid species, or one insensitive to SCD inhibition, would weaken the mechanism.", "Metabolite prediction: APOE4 microglia should show higher cytosolic citrate and acetyl-CoA (or higher acetyl-CoA-dependent histone acetylation) than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower cytosolic citrate would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Alternative-mechanism discriminator: markers of ER unfolded-protein signalling (HSPA5 protein, XBP1 splicing, ATF4/CHOP reporter, phospho-eIF2alpha) should differ little between genotypes, and ISRIB or 4-phenylbutyrate should not normalise the lipid difference; a strong constitutive UPR that, when blocked, removes the lipid difference would displace this mechanism in favour of an ER-proteostasis mechanism.", "Ordering test: acute SLC25A1 inhibition should reduce neutral lipid before lysosomal hydrolase transcripts change, whereas TFEB knockdown should not reduce (and may increase) the APOE4 neutral-lipid excess; a TFEB knockdown that removes the lipid excess would invert the proposed causal order."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and 2-oxoglutarate/citrate metabolism (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54) and for glutamine-derived anaplerosis (gene:GLUD1 +3.17) are elevated in APOE4 at the 90th-99th percentile of this selected differential-expression list, well above its global positive median (+1.46, unspecified log base).", "Measured: the mitochondrial carrier and cytosolic shuttle arm that exports four- and six-carbon units is coordinately elevated (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 citrate carrier, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50 oxoglutarate/malate carrier, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56 adenine-nucleotide carrier, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43); inferred, not measured: increased mitochondria-to-cytosol citrate and malate flux and a larger cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool (ATP-citrate lyase transcript was not in the supplied list).", "Inferred bottleneck: cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply, rather than respiratory chain capacity, limits lipid synthesis, because the export/anaplerosis transcripts sit far above the electron-transport subunit transcripts in the same dataset (median +5.55 vs +2.25; permutation p = 0.003).", "Measured: downstream desaturation and esterification transcripts are elevated (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) alongside post-squalene sterol synthesis (gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:INSIG1 +1.87); inferred: ER-localised SREBP processing and acyl-transfer activity, i.e. flux into monounsaturated glycerolipid and cholesteryl ester, is increased.", "Measured: scavenger and lipoprotein-uptake transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50); inferred: exogenous lipid uptake adds to the synthesised pool, so the two inputs converge on cytosolic esterification rather than on export.", "Measured: a lysosomal hydrolase/CLEAR-like program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88; set median +2.40, rank percentile 0.66, permutation p = 0.036); inferred: this is a downstream/compensatory response to increased lipid load rather than the initiating lesion, since it does not by itself specify the observed carbon-export signature.", "Predicted phenotype: net storage of monounsaturated triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 microglia; lipid content, droplet number, localisation and flux were not measured here and are inferred."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate mitochondrial citrate/malate export and anaplerosis, making cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply the bottleneck for MUFA-rich neutral-lipid accumulation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27440645423328286, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22142742422932388, "cosine_similarity": 0.33207795097349635, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057605177993528, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27440645423328286, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22142742422932388, "cosine_similarity": 0.33207795097349635, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6057605177993528, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.5840005, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 264}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_066", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (no |effect| below ~1) with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, median +1.46), so module-level claims were tested against the empirical distribution of this list, not against an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, HMGCR, ABCA1, STAT1) means unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effects are treated as ranks/relative magnitudes, not as fold changes on a known scale.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein/enzyme availability; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, flux, or lipid pool was measured in this dataset.", "SREBP target transcript abundance is used as an indirect readout of ER-accessible cholesterol; alternative regulators (mTORC1, PI3K, hypoxia) could also drive these transcripts.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level changes are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, and keratin/actin-dominated spots are treated as likely contaminant-driven.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect sizes cannot be checked for replicate-level stability; astrocyte co-culture means non-microglial RNA may contribute."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, lipid (sterol/sphingolipid) that enters or is generated in the endolysosome is inefficiently exported to the ER sterol-sensing pool. Because the ER continues to read 'low sterol', the SREBP-driven synthesis and uptake program stays on while a TFEB-type lysosomal-biogenesis program is co-induced as compensation, and elevated mitochondrial citrate export plus ACSS2 supply cytosolic acetyl-CoA for SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification; the predicted end state is neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester storage rather than restored free-sterol homeostasis. Cholesterol pools, lysosomal pH, and enzyme activities were not measured here; the transcript and protein-spot data are correlative and do not establish causality or direction.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute treatment of APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression), which mobilizes lysosomal cholesterol to the ER without changing synthesis enzymes, should lower ER-sensor-dependent SREBP targets (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24) and lower lysosomal cholesterol (filipin/ALOD4-negative lysosomes) toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h; if lysosomal cholesterol falls but the SREBP target module stays elevated, the egress bottleneck is falsified and a synthesis-drive or direct APOE4-SREBP mechanism is favoured.", "SOAT1 (ACAT1/2) inhibition in APOE4 should reduce cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid droplet content while leaving lysosomal free-cholesterol accumulation and the elevated hydrolase/TFEB transcripts unchanged or increased; if SOAT1 inhibition instead normalizes lysosomal cholesterol and the lysosomal transcript module, the primary bottleneck is esterification, not egress.", "Direct measurement prediction: APOE4 microglia will show a higher lysosome-to-ER cholesterol ratio (filipin or BODIPY-cholesterol colocalized with LAMP1 versus ALOD4/D4H ER-accessible probe) than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol with equal ER-accessible cholesterol would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Flux prediction: LC-MS or radiolabel tracing should show increased 13C-acetate/glucose incorporation into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol in APOE4, and SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) or ACSS2 inhibition should blunt this incorporation without normalizing lysosomal cholesterol; unchanged label incorporation despite elevated SLC25A1/ACSS2 transcripts would show the mitochondrial-carbon arm is not active.", "Phenocopy prediction: partial inhibition of lysosomal sterol egress in APOE3 microglia (U18666A) should reproduce the joint signature of elevated hydrolase/TFEB transcripts plus elevated SREBP targets; failure to reproduce this joint signature would argue the APOE4 pattern arises from a different upstream cause.", "Interferon counter-prediction: type-I interferon effector transcripts and phospho-STAT1 should NOT be elevated in APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment; a clear ISG/pSTAT1 elevation would support the rejected interferon mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinated higher transcript abundance across the lysosomal/CLEAR module (TFEB, GNPTG, IGF2R, acid hydrolases GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SGSH, GLA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK and v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C); we infer, but did not measure, increased lysosomal biogenesis and hydrolytic capacity.", "Measured: the sterol-synthesis and lipoprotein/sterol-uptake program is simultaneously higher (SREBF1, SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, SCARB1, APOE); because SREBP output is normally switched off by ER-accessible cholesterol, we infer that the ER sterol sensor is not receiving the sterol that the cell is taking up and degrading.", "Inferred bottleneck: transfer of hydrolysis-derived free cholesterol (and sphingolipid backbones) out of the endolysosome to the ER is rate-limiting in APOE4; the only egress-machinery transcript in the supplied list, NPC2, is only marginally above the selection floor (+1.17) while the hydrolase module is far higher, so degradative supply outruns export capacity. NPC1, PSAP and GRN were not measured.", "Measured: mitochondrial/cytosolic carbon-export transcripts are the single most elevated coherent module (SLC25A1 citrate carrier, SLC25A11, MDH1, GOT1, MPC2, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, ACSS2); we infer increased cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability, not measured flux.", "Measured: esterification and neutral-lipid enzymes are elevated (SOAT1, DGAT1, SCD, FABP5, FABP3, MGLL); with acetyl-CoA supply and continued SREBP drive, we infer that sterol and fatty acid reaching the ER/droplet compartment is preferentially esterified and stored rather than returned to a regulatory free-sterol pool.", "Inferred feed-forward loop: sequestration in lysosomes plus esterification into droplets keeps ER-accessible cholesterol low, which sustains SREBP target transcription and further uptake (LDLR, SCARB1) and further substrate delivery to an already saturated lysosome, producing progressive lipid storage in APOE4 relative to APOE3 under mock conditions.", "Inferred consequence for microglial state: a chronic storage/compensation state (TREM2, ITGAX, GPNMB, CLEC7A, CD36, MERTK modestly up; CTSS and CSF1 strongly down) rather than an interferon-driven activation state; type-I interferon effectors are absent from the differential list."], "title": "Endolysosomal cholesterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, driving a futile SREBP-plus-lysosome expansion cycle with acetyl-CoA-fed esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24603072037809695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2572420290455866, "cosine_similarity": 0.33154444186979376, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6253818770226537, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24603072037809695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2572420290455866, "cosine_similarity": 0.33154444186979376, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6253818770226537, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.672949, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 265}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_100", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an absolute effect threshold and a strong positive skew (median about +1.46 in unspecified log units, 77% positive); we therefore treat direction only relative to the internal distribution of this list, and assume that ranking within the list is not systematically distorted by the selection or by the unknown normalisation.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is not converted; only relative magnitude and sign are used.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features. We assume no spot uniquely identifies a protein; spots are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration and never as evidence that a named protein changed.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the maximum capacity of the corresponding enzymatic step; no flux, redox-couple ratio, localization or post-translational state was measured in this dataset.", "The mitonuclear step assumes that lower mtDNA-encoded transcript levels reflect reduced mitochondrial transcript supply rather than only mitochondrial-content or ambient-RNA differences in the 10X Flex data.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to differ systematically between genotype arms in a way that alone generates the microglial redox and lipid signatures.", "Causality is not established: all steps are hypothesised directional relations derived from a single mock-condition genotype contrast."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia express a coordinately higher lipid-uptake/anabolic and mitochondrial oxidative transcriptional program while transcripts for cytosolic NADP(H) supply (PGD, TALDO1, NADK) are among the few strongly reduced genes in a globally up-shifted differential-expression list. We hypothesise that this mismatch makes cytosolic NADPH regeneration, not oxidant production per se, the rate-limiting node: APOE4 microglia maintain redox homeostasis at baseline only by shifting reductant supply to mitochondrial/one-carbon routes (NNT, ME1, GLUD1, SHMT1/2) and by up-regulating thiol-peroxidase, glutathione-synthetic and iron-sequestering transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, GSS, TXNL1, TXNDC17, MGST2, FTH1) while down-regulating ferroptosis executors (ACSL4, ALOX15), producing a compensated state with low spare reductive capacity that should fail selectively when NADPH demand is raised. The peroxisomal arm of the assigned focus is rejected as unsupported by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological block of the oxidative PPP (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide) or NNT knockdown in the isogenic pair should lower NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG and increase peroxide- or myelin-load-induced lipid peroxidation (BODIPY-C11) and death substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive than APOE3 to these blocks, the NADPH-bottleneck claim is falsified.", "13C6-glucose tracing should show lower oxidative-PPP flux (reduced label entry into the non-oxidative branch / lower 1-13C-derived CO2 relative to 6-13C) in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or higher PPP flux in APOE4 would weaken step 3 even if the transcript differences replicate.", "Baseline metabolite measurement should show only small genotype differences in GSH/GSSG and NADPH/NADP+ (compensated state) with a markedly larger APOE4 collapse after tert-butyl hydroperoxide challenge. A large baseline deficit with no challenge amplification would favour uncompensated chronic oxidative stress instead of this reserve-depletion model.", "Immunoblot of mtDNA-encoded (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6) versus nuclear-encoded (NDUFB8, UQCRC2) subunits should show a reduced mtDNA/nuclear protein ratio and higher MitoSOX/mito-roGFP oxidation in APOE4. An unchanged ratio and unchanged matrix oxidation would remove the proposed oxidant source in step 2 without necessarily refuting step 3.", "PRDX3 or GPX4 knockdown should selectively kill or lipid-peroxidise APOE4 microglia at doses tolerated by APOE3; equal sensitivity would weaken the claim that the antioxidant transcript increase is load-bearing compensation rather than an incidental difference.", "Peroxisomal counter-prediction: if catalase activity, plasmalogen levels and very-long-chain fatty-acid ratios (C26:0/C22:0) differ strongly between genotypes, the rejected peroxisomal mechanism would be reinstated over this one; the present data predict little or no peroxisomal difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry higher steady-state transcript levels for lipid uptake, storage, desaturation and sterol reduction (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7) together with lysosomal hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB). Inferred, not measured: increased flux through a lysosome-to-lipid-droplet cycle whose desaturation and sterol-reduction steps are NADPH-consuming.", "Transcripts for mitochondrial substrate import, TCA turnover and nuclear-encoded electron-transport subunits are coordinately higher (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME), whereas several mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2). Inferred, not measured: a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch during complex assembly that raises the probability of electron leak and matrix superoxide/peroxide generation.", "Cytosolic NADP(H) provisioning transcripts move against the global upward shift of this list (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK are in the lowest ~10-21% of all measured effects). Inferred, not measured: reduced pentose-phosphate-pathway flux and a smaller cytosolic NADPH regeneration reserve; the cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ pool itself was not measured, and G6PD RNA is absent from the supplied rows.", "Reductant supply is inferred to be re-routed to compartments that bypass the cytosolic PPP: nicotinamide nucleotide transhydrogenase, malic enzyme, glutamate dehydrogenase and serine/one-carbon enzymes are up (gene:NNT, gene:ME1, gene:GLUD1, gene:SHMT1, gene:SHMT2). This is an abundance-level inference about capacity, not a measured flux.", "Peroxide-disposal and iron-handling capacity is raised, dominated by thiol-based, largely mitochondrial systems rather than a canonical NRF2 module (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:GSS, gene:TXNL1, gene:TXNDC17, gene:MGST2, gene:FTH1; ambiguous supporting spots protein_spot:077, protein_spot:017), while lipid-peroxidation executors are suppressed (gene:ACSL4, gene:ALOX15). Inferred: an actively buffered state in which oxidative damage is limited at baseline.", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia are redox-compensated but reserve-depleted. Genotype differences in glutathione and NADPH redox couples, lipid peroxidation and viability should therefore be small under mock conditions and large when NADPH demand is increased (oxidant challenge, lipid/myelin load) or when the compensating routes (PPP, NNT, PRDX3) are blocked."], "title": "Cytosolic NADPH-regeneration capacity is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a lipid-anabolic, mitochondrially oxidative state compensated by matrix thiol-peroxidase and non-PPP reductant routes"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2761880146217184, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2643237088402944, "cosine_similarity": 0.33132473713769756, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mean_absolute_error": 0.623799352750809, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2761880146217184, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2643237088402944, "cosine_similarity": 0.33132473713769756, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.623799352750809, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0645205, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 266}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_065", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e=1 on an unspecified log base, adjusted p\u003c=0.048) with a 77% positive background; program coherence is judged against that background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, PLIN2, LIPA, HSPA5, XBP1, HMGCR) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for machinery capacity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, sterol transport, esterification flux and respiration were not measured, so all flux, localization and causal statements are inferred.", "SREBP-type target transcripts are assumed to report the ER-accessible sterol sensing state; this is background knowledge (unverified here) and is contradicted in part by gene:MYLIP (+1.28), an LXR-type sterol-replete signal, so compartmentalised sensing is assumed.", "2-D protein spots each carry \u003e=3 candidate identities with heavy keratin/actin contamination; they are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never to confirm an individual protein.", "Genes within a program are not statistically independent (shared regulons), so the binomial values are descriptive, not formal enrichment tests.", "The astrocyte co-culture and any ambient-RNA/global-scaling effects of the 10X Flex pseudobulk comparison are assumed not to be the sole source of the uniform positive shift in mitochondrial and lysosomal transcripts."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (vs isogenic APOE3), the dominant transcriptional difference is a coordinated cell-state change, not an unfolded-protein response: a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (31 members represented, 29 up, e.g. gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:TFEB +2.38) rises together with nuclear-encoded OXPHOS (34/34 up) and TCA/anaplerotic transcripts while glycolytic control points fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08). Simultaneously, lipid-acquisition (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38), SREBP-type sterol-synthesis (gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF2) and esterification/storage transcripts (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) are all elevated. Because SREBP-type targets are not repressed despite expanded lysosomal machinery, we propose that in APOE4 the lipid delivered to and liberated in endolysosomes is preferentially routed into cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid stores rather than into the ER-accessible sterol pool, producing an esterification-biased lipidome with expanded oxidative capacity. This is a routing/state hypothesis: no flux, activity, localization or causal direction was measured, and no ongoing degradative bottleneck is claimed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, direct lipidomics/imaging should show a higher esterified-to-free cholesterol ratio and higher neutral-lipid (cholesteryl-ester/TAG) content per cell, while the ER-accessible/free sterol pool (filipin-accessible or PFO/D4H-accessible) is not higher; finding equal or lower total cholesteryl ester with an increased ER-accessible sterol pool would weaken the routing mechanism.", "Prospective: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (or DGAT1 inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should shift sterol from ester stores toward the ER-accessible pool and suppress the SREBP-type transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS) more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3; if SREBP-type transcripts stay elevated after esterification blockade, the proposed esterification sink is not what sustains them.", "Prospective: bulk-lipid challenge (myelin debris or oxLDL loading) should reveal a larger increase in lipid-droplet area and a smaller increase in free/effluxed cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3, consistent with a routing bias that is not necessarily a defect in the unchallenged mock state; equal handling under challenge would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective: extracellular flux measurement should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower glycolytic rate in APOE4 microglia, matching the OXPHOS/TCA-up and HK2/PFKP-down transcript pattern; an unchanged or lower OCR/ECAR ratio would falsify the oxidative-shift step.", "Prospective: lysosomal function assays (DQ-BSA/cathepsin activity, LysoSensor pH) should show equal or higher, not reduced, degradative capacity in mock APOE4; a clear ongoing hydrolytic deficit in mock conditions would move the explanation from altered routing toward failed lysosomal catabolism.", "Prospective: ER-stress readouts (XBP1 splicing, ATF4/CHOP protein, BiP induction, thapsigargin sensitivity) should not differ appreciably between mock APOE4 and APOE3; a robust constitutive UPR in APOE4 would support the rejected ER-proteostasis alternative over this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype shifts microglia into a lysosome-biogenesis-like transcriptional state: gene:TFEB (+2.38) with coordinated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:LAMP1 +1.38); 29/31 represented members positive versus a 77% positive selected-list background (binomial p=0.016). Measured as transcript abundance; hydrolase activity and acidification are inferred, not observed.", "In parallel, lipid-acquisition transcripts rise (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), increasing the predicted delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosomal system.", "Despite this expanded degradative and uptake machinery, sterol-synthesis transcripts that are normally repressed when the ER sterol pool is replete remain elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SREBF1 +4.67), which we interpret as the ER-accessible sterol pool not being repleted in proportion to lipid load (inferred sensing state; sterol pools were not measured).", "Co-induced esterification and neutral-lipid storage enzymes (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MGLL +4.00) provide a sink that routes newly acquired and newly synthesized sterol/fatty acid into cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol rather than into free-sterol membrane repletion or export.", "The ATP and reducing-equivalent demand of this expanded lysosomal-lipid processing state is met by an oxidative rather than glycolytic shift: nuclear-encoded complex I/IV/ATP-synthase transcripts are uniformly increased (gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5ME +5.20; 34/34 positive, p=1.4e-4) together with TCA and anaplerotic transcripts (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:GLUD1 +3.17), while glycolytic and pentose-phosphate control points fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) despite higher glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37).", "Net predicted phenotype in the measured mock condition: an esterification-biased, lysosome- and mitochondria-loaded lipid state with preserved (not failing) proteostasis, consistent with 2-D spot data in which cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.59 vs protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) while ER-chaperone-candidate spots are non-significant (protein_spot:001 -0.49, protein_spot:004 -0.68, protein_spot:005 -0.14, protein_spot:016 +0.14). Any degradative insufficiency is expected to be revealed only by a future lipid challenge, not asserted for the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome- and mitochondria-expanded lipid-handling state that routes sterol into esterified storage instead of repleting the ER-accessible sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29836982609016727, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2911681075556858, "cosine_similarity": 0.33125743010753206, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_065", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6224822006472492, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29836982609016727, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2911681075556858, "cosine_similarity": 0.33125743010753206, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6224822006472492, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3966765, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 65}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_099", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c= 0.048) with a 77.1% up background; program directionality is judged against that background, absent genes (e.g. P2RY12, CX3CR1, TYROBP, VPS35, ABCA1) are unknown rather than unchanged, and the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and preserved.", "Coordinated transcript changes across independently defined families (v-ATPase, hydrolases, sorting, OXPHOS) approximate changes in the abundance of the corresponding machinery; they do not measure lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity, uptake rate, respiration or motility, all of which are inferred.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (2-6 candidate identities, keratin-rich); they are used only for compatibility, never as identification of a single protein. Actin/Arp2/3/capping-candidate spots skewing positive and MYH9-candidate protein_spot:010 / protein_spot:011 being negative are compatible with, not proof of, the proposed actin re-allocation.", "The hematopoietic amoeboid-motility set was curated by annotation category but only after large negative effects were noticed there; objective family prefixes (MYO*, ARHGAP*/DOCK*/RHO*/RAC*) are not globally negative, so this arm is the most selection-sensitive part of the mechanism.", "Genes are not independent (shared regulators, shared cells, unknown replicate number), so the reported binomial comparisons are descriptive, not formal enrichment statistics; a compositional or sequencing-depth artefact in the selected list could inflate any 'up' program.", "Reduced motility/engulfment capacity is proposed as a state property of the mock condition, but a defect in large-particle clearance would mainly be revealed by a future phagocytic or chemotactic challenge; reduced reserve under challenge would not by itself prove an ongoing defect at baseline."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia occupy a different steady cell state rather than a single broken step: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, endosome-to-lysosome sorting, v-ATPase and lysosomal hydrolases, lipid esterification and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA components are coordinately higher than the strongly up-biased selected-list background, while the hematopoietic amoeboid-motility module (non-muscle myosin II, RAC2-DOCK8, MYO1F, VASP, CYRIB/FAM49B) is coordinately lower and beta1-integrin adhesion transcripts are higher. We propose that APOE4 shifts cytoskeletal and metabolic investment from myosin-II-dependent motile surveillance/large-particle engulfment toward adherent, branched-actin-based lipid internalization feeding an enlarged degradative compartment; only abundances were measured, so uptake rate, degradative flux and motility are inferred, not observed, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under identical mock culture, live imaging plus flow cytometry should show (a) higher internalization of fluorescent lipoprotein/lipid cargo (DiI-AcLDL, BODIPY-labelled myelin lipid) and higher LysoTracker/LAMP1 lysosomal content in APOE4, together with (b) lower mean process/soma displacement velocity and lower uptake of large myosin-II-dependent particles (2-3 um beads, zymosan, synaptosomes). Observing equal-or-greater large-particle engulfment and unchanged lipid uptake in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective: pharmacological myosin-II or ROCK inhibition of APOE3 microglia should shift them toward the APOE4 phenotype (reduced motility and large-particle uptake with preserved or increased lipoprotein uptake); if APOE4 cells instead respond to these inhibitors identically to APOE3 across both readouts, the proposed actomyosin re-allocation arm is not carrying the phenotype.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown/inhibition should selectively collapse the endolysosomal-hydrolase arm (LAMP1, cathepsin activity by Magic Red, v-ATPase-dependent acidification) and increase neutral-lipid droplet accumulation in APOE4 more than APOE3, without restoring motility; if TFEB loss also restores motility, the two arms are not separable and the routing model must be replaced by a single upstream regulator model.", "Prospective flux test distinguishing adaptation from failed compensation: pulse-chase of a quenched lipid or protein cargo (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-cholesteryl ester) should show equal or faster per-lysosome degradation in APOE4 if the state is adaptive throughput; slower degradation with accumulating undigested cargo despite higher hydrolase transcripts would refute the adaptive reading and support failed lysosomal compensation.", "Prospective mitochondrial test: APOE4 cells should show higher maximal and basal oxygen consumption or higher respiratory-complex protein per cell, consistent with the 38/38 nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase; unchanged or reduced respiration with unchanged complex protein would show that these transcript increases are not functionally realized and would weaken the metabolic support step.", "Prospective specificity control: exogenous lipid-poor vs lipid-loaded ApoE3 particles added to APOE4 cells should partially normalize the lipid-uptake/esterification transcripts (SCARB1, SOAT1, DGAT1, SREBF1) if secreted ApoE4 lipoprotein drives the state; no change would indicate an intracellular, particle-independent mechanism and require narrowing the claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype raises transcripts for surface lipid/lipoprotein and opsonin-type uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:COLEC12, gene:MERTK, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A), which we infer increases routing of extracellular lipid and lipoprotein cargo into the endocytic pathway (uptake rate not measured).", "Internalized cargo is handled by an expanded sorting-and-degradation route: endosomal sorting/retromer-Commander transcripts rise (gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:COMMD9; 25/27 positive), together with gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1 and a TFEB-axis signature (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:RRAGD, gene:MITF, gene:LAMTOR5).", "Degradative machinery transcripts follow the same direction: v-ATPase subunits are 10/10 positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1) and hydrolases rise strongly (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD), predicting more lysosomal volume/content per cell.", "Lipid liberated in this compartment is inferred to be re-esterified and stored rather than exported, since esterification/synthesis transcripts rise coordinately (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:LPCAT1, gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:MGLL) alongside a sterol arm (gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1) and gene:ABCA7.", "Supporting this catabolic-anabolic load, nuclear-encoded respiratory chain and TCA transcripts increase uniformly (38/38 positive; gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2) while 4/6 mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4), indicating nucleus-driven mitochondrial remodeling with a mito-nuclear mismatch of unmeasured functional consequence.", "The same state redistributes actin usage: hematopoietic amoeboid-motility transcripts fall sharply against a 77%-up background (gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:VASP, gene:FAM49B, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:SPN, gene:PTPRC, gene:CTSS; 16/17 negative), whereas branched-actin/capping components rise (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5, gene:CFL1, gene:TWF2, gene:CORO1B; actin/Arp2/3/capping-candidate spots protein_spot:036, protein_spot:038, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:052 positive) and beta1-integrin adhesion transcripts rise (gene:ITGA6 +15.5, gene:ITGB1 +6.3, gene:ITGB1BP1, gene:ITGB5).", "Net predicted phenotype in the measured mock condition: maintained or increased lipid/small-cargo internalization and lysosomal content with lipid storage and higher oxidative gene dosage, but reduced myosin-II-dependent motility and reduced large-particle engulfment reserve; whether degradative output keeps pace (successful adaptation) or lags (failed compensation) is not resolved by abundance data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route toward scavenger-receptor lipid internalization and an expanded endolysosomal-oxidative state at the expense of the amoeboid actomyosin motility module"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22482738249086143, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23541856930394375, "cosine_similarity": 0.3307649886610218, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6285857605177994, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22482738249086143, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23541856930394375, "cosine_similarity": 0.3307649886610218, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6285857605177994, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3848605, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 66}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_089", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% are positive with median +1.46 and all |effect|\u003e1, so only within-list relative enrichment (hydrolase/v-ATPase set above the list background, p=0.002-0.006) is treated as informative, and no absolute direction claim is made for individual genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking, not as fold-changes.", "Elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are assumed to translate into increased hydrolase protein and acidification capacity; this was not measured (protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel spots and cannot identify CTSD, CTSB or ATP6V1E1 uniquely).", "MiT/TFE (TFEB/MITF) is assumed to be the proximal driver of the coherent CLEAR-target elevation; transcription-factor localisation and activity were not measured.", "Lipid, cholesteryl-ester and sphingolipid pools, lysosomal pH, lysosome number/size and all uptake and degradation fluxes are unmeasured in the supplied data; they are inferred, not observed.", "Microglial identity, maturation state and astrocyte co-culture composition are assumed comparable between APOE4 and APOE3 lines; no replicate count was supplied, so effect precision cannot be assessed.", "Protein spots and RNA come from the same nominal comparison but need not come from matched samples or timepoints."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a selectively coherent transcriptional expansion of lysosomal acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits (median effect ~+2.2, hydrolases ~+4.5, versus a +1.46 median across all selected differential rows; Mann-Whitney p=0.002-0.003), together with elevated lipoprotein/scavenger-receptor and sterol-esterification transcripts, while actin/phagocytic-cup and cargo-egress transcripts are not co-elevated (RAC2, DOCK8, MYO1F, ACTB, CTSS, RAB27A are among the most decreased rows). We hypothesise that this pattern is a compensatory response to a persistent endolysosomal lipid/substrate load, and that the bottleneck in APOE4 is disposal of internalised lipid cargo downstream of hydrolysis (egress/exocytosis and re-export), not hydrolase transcript availability or receptor-mediated uptake. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pool itself, protein-level hydrolase content, lysosomal pH, localisation and all fluxes were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: TFEB (plus MITF) knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (GBA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels while making the inferred lipid/substrate accumulation worse (increased BODIPY-LDL or filipin signal). If those transcripts stay elevated after TFEB/MITF loss, or if lipid accumulation is unchanged, STEP 3 is wrong and a TFEB-independent driver (inflammatory or global transcriptional up-shift) must be invoked.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Removing the cargo (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should normalise the APOE4 CLEAR-gene elevation within 24-72 h. Persistence of the hydrolase/v-ATPase program under cargo withdrawal would refute the 'compensation for a cargo load' causal direction in STEPS 1-3 and favour a cell-intrinsic, load-independent APOE4 transcriptional state.", "FUNCTIONAL TEST OF THE BOTTLENECK: In pulse-chase (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-LDL, or NBD-sphingomyelin), APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater initial internalisation and equal or lower lysosomal pH, but a slower fractional clearance/egress rate per lysosome than APOE3. If APOE4 clearance rate is equal to or faster than APOE3 despite the hydrolase program, the proposed downstream-disposal bottleneck (STEP 4) fails.", "EGRESS-SPECIFIC TEST: Restoring lysosomal exocytosis/egress (RAB27A re-expression, or TRPML1/MCOLN1 agonist-driven exocytosis) should reduce accumulated lipid in APOE4 without further raising hydrolase transcripts. No reduction in accumulation would weaken the egress interpretation of STEP 4 and point instead to a hydrolysis-composition defect (e.g., loss of CTSS).", "REJECTION TEST FOR THE ENGULFMENT ALTERNATIVE: Live phagocytosis assays (pHrodo synaptosomes or myelin) should show that APOE4 uptake rate is not increased relative to APOE3, and that actin/Arp2/3 or Rac inhibition changes uptake equally in both genotypes. If APOE4 instead shows a large genotype-specific engulfment defect that is rescued by Rac/Arp2/3 pathway restoration, the primary bottleneck is cytoskeletal engulfment, not endolysosomal disposal, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "STORAGE-ARM TEST: SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from cholesteryl ester to free sterol and increase efflux/toxicity readouts without normalising the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program; normalisation of that program by SOAT1 inhibition alone would place the bottleneck upstream, at esterification rather than at disposal."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo receptors and for APOE itself (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery rate of lipid-rich cargo into the endosomal system.", "STEP 2 (measured transcripts; inferred localisation): Machinery for internalisation, late-endosome conversion and endosomal sorting is transcriptionally elevated (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS18 +1.41, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95), consistent with cargo transiting to a degradative compartment; compartment identity and transit rate are inferred, not observed.", "STEP 3 (measured transcripts; inferred regulator activity): A MiT/TFE-type CLEAR program is engaged: gene:TFEB +2.38 and gene:MITF +1.03 accompany coordinated elevation of acid hydrolases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:LAMP1 +1.38). TFEB nuclear localisation and transcription-factor activity are inferred from target coherence, not measured.", "STEP 4 (bottleneck; measured transcripts, inferred capacity): The compensatory arm is unmatched by cargo-disposal routes. Lysosome-related exocytosis and one dominant microglial protease are among the strongly decreased rows (gene:RAB27A -2.52, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:IDS -1.56), while sterol/neutral-lipid re-esterification transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:NPC2 +1.17). We propose the rate-limiting node is conversion of hydrolysed lipid into exported or stored-but-mobilisable pools, so material dwell time in the endolysosome increases.", "STEP 5 (measured transcripts; rejects the engulfment arm of the assigned focus): Phagocytic-cup/actin machinery is NOT selectively up-scaled relative to the strong global up-shift of these selected rows (actin/motor set median +1.61, p=0.64; phagocytic-receptor set median +1.35, p=0.82; both indistinguishable from the +1.46 background), and several core components are strongly decreased (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:DOCK8 -1.99). Engulfment capacity therefore does not scale with degradative-enzyme transcription, biasing the system toward storage rather than clearance.", "STEP 6 (predicted phenotype, unmeasured here): The net inferred state is an enlarged, enzyme-rich but functionally back-pressured endolysosomal compartment in APOE4 microglia, in which per-lysosome substrate clearance rate is lower than the hydrolase transcript elevation would predict."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-scale a MiT/TFE-linked acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase program without matching engulfment or cargo-egress machinery, making endolysosomal lipid disposal the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20987844538706682, "cosine_similarity": 0.3305245209463353, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137605177993527, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20987844538706682, "cosine_similarity": 0.3305245209463353, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6137605177993527, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85457225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 267}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_063", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) from a selected gene set, not an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is not stated and is preserved as reported, so effect magnitudes are treated as ordinal within this list.", "A global upward bias exists in the supplied list (77% of 2212 rows positive, mean +1.39), so only pathway signals exceeding this background (permutation against all supplied RNA rows) are treated as informative.", "2D protein spots are assigned 4-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8) and 39/92 spots include keratins; spot-level directions are treated as proteoform-resolved abundance signals of ambiguous identity, never as unique protein quantification.", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to be a proxy for synthesis demand, not for enzyme activity, lumenal pH, localization, or degradative flux, none of which were measured.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture; genotype effects attributed to microglia are assumed, not demonstrated, to be microglia-intrinsic.", "Key controls of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, LIPA, GRN, PSAP, MCOLN1, LAMP2, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B) are absent from the supplied rows, so the bottleneck is inferred from the measured hydrolase/V-ATPase axis only.", "No causal claim is made: all observations are steady-state genotype associations under mock treatment at day 30."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 cells transcriptionally up-regulate cargo-uptake receptors together with a TFEB/MITF-associated endolysosomal degradation program (luminal hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits, late-endosomal transport), yet the matched 2D protein-spot data show no net increase in lysosomal-hydrolase-containing spots and consistently decreased V1-ATPase-containing spots; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is post-transcriptional generation of acidified, hydrolytically mature lysosomes, so that degradative throughput per unit internalised cargo is reduced and the transcriptional expansion is a compensatory feedback response rather than an increase in realised degradative flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pulse-chase of a quenched degradable cargo (DQ-BSA or DQ-myelin) plus ratiometric lysosomal pH in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show equal or higher initial internalisation in APOE4 but a lower dequenching rate normalised per LAMP1-positive compartment area and a higher (less acidic) mean lumenal pH; if APOE4 shows equal per-compartment dequenching rate and equal pH while simply having more lysosomes, the bottleneck claim is refuted and the data instead indicate proportional compartment expansion.", "Immunoblot of CTSD and CTSB should show an increased pro-form to mature-form ratio and no proportional increase in mature heavy chain in APOE4 despite higher gene:CTSD and gene:CTSB transcripts; proportional scaling of mature enzyme with mRNA would weaken step 3.", "Low-dose bafilomycin A1 or ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C knockdown in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 transcriptional signature (induction of gene:TFEB targets such as gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:LAMP1 plus retained cargo), whereas restoring acidification in APOE4 (acidic nanoparticles or V-ATPase assembly enhancement) should normalise cargo clearance without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts; failure of either arm weakens the mechanism.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should abolish the hydrolase/transporter transcript excess while leaving the OXPHOS/TCA transcript excess (for example gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5) intact; if TFEB knockdown removes both, the lysosomal signature is not a separable module and a shared upstream driver (for example mitochondrial-metabolic or compositional) is the better explanation.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show that the large transcript increases for gene:GAA, gene:GBA and gene:HEXA do not translate into proportionally higher cell-normalised activity in APOE4; matched proportional activity increases would refute the post-transcriptional bottleneck and favour a genuine capacity gain.", "If the bottleneck is real, APOE4 lysosomes should accumulate undegraded lipidic cargo (filipin-positive or BODIPY-positive LAMP1 compartments) after a myelin or acetylated-lipoprotein challenge; absence of any cargo retention difference despite the transcriptional differences would refute step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of phagocytic/lipoprotein-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA, gene:STAB1, gene:ITGA6, gene:APOE), which we infer - but did not measure - increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization): Transcripts for late-endosome-to-lysosome delivery and positioning are coordinately higher (gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B, gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP5S1, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:CHMP4B), consistent with, but not proof of, increased cargo trafficking toward the degradative compartment.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA vs measured protein spots): Although hydrolase and proton-pump transcripts are strongly elevated (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1), protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases show no net increase and bidirectional, spot-specific changes (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and every spot whose candidate list contains a V1-ATPase subunit is negative (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:075); we infer that mature, correctly targeted pump and hydrolase pools, and hence lumenal acidification and proteolytic/glycosidic throughput per lysosome, do not scale with the mRNA increase.", "Step 4 (inferred activity/feedback): Reduced per-lysosome processing of delivered cargo sustains a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR feedback signal, observed here only as elevated transcripts of the transcription factors and their targets (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:LAMP1, gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SPNS1, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3, gene:SCARB2), i.e. compartment expansion rather than demonstrated flux.", "Step 5 (inferred lipid consequence; not measured): Incompletely catabolised lipidic cargo is retained in the endolysosomal lumen, so ER sterol sensing remains unsatisfied and the sterol-synthesis/esterification/storage program stays active (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1); no lipid species, lysosomal pH, or cargo-degradation rate was measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (secondary consequence, inferred): The same load state accompanies a shifted innate-immune tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL16, gene:NLRP3, gene:NLRP1 up; gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:CR1 down), which we treat as correlated output, not as a required step."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand the CLEAR/lysosomal transcriptional program while mature acidification-hydrolase capacity fails to scale, making per-lysosome cargo processing the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10701423311567056, "cosine_similarity": 0.3298087300755016, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6237928802588997, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11643835616438356, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10701423311567056, "cosine_similarity": 0.3298087300755016, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6237928802588997, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.92241925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 268}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_052", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not a whole-transcriptome measurement, so absence of a gene (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1) means unmeasured, not unchanged; all pathway statements are conditional on the measured subset.", "The dataset-wide positive shift (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% of rows positive) is treated as a baseline offset, so only median-centred changes are interpreted as gene-specific; if that shift is real biology rather than normalisation/compositional offset, NPC2 is genuinely increased and the relative-deficit argument weakens.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are therefore used only for ranking, especially because |effect| is uncorrelated with adjusted p-value in this table (Spearman rho = -0.03, p = 0.21).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme and transporter capacity; SREBP cleavage, NPC1/NPC2 protein, lysosomal pH, cholesterol pools, esterification flux and efflux were not measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin-containing spots are cited only as compartment-consistent, not as cathepsin quantification.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect altered astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply rather than a microglia-intrinsic defect.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 at one timepoint under mock treatment, with biological replicate number not supplied, so clone- and batch-level confounding cannot be excluded."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the transcript program for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lysosomal acid-hydrolase capacity is raised far above the dataset-wide upward shift (SCARB1, GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSK, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, TFEB), whereas the transcript for the lysosomal sterol-transfer step NPC2 is not (its change sits below the global median). We hypothesise that the resulting mismatch makes NPC2/NPC1-dependent egress of unesterified cholesterol out of the endolysosome the rate-limiting step, so sterol accumulates in the endolysosomal compartment while the ER sterol sensor pool stays low, which keeps an SREBP-target module (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, SCD) and sterol-carrier/esterification genes (SCP2, SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2) engaged and drives a feed-forward lipid-loading loop. Causality is not established by these data; the lysosomal and ER sterol pools themselves were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: supplying the missing egress step (recombinant NPC2 or NPC2/NPC1 overexpression, or 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin to bypass NPC2) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the SREBP-target transcript module (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD) toward APOE3 levels while leaving the hydrolase module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) and SCARB1 largely intact within 24-48 h. If the SREBP module falls only when the hydrolase module falls in parallel, or does not fall at all, the specific egress bottleneck is falsified in favour of generic lysosomal stress or an APOE4 effect upstream of uptake.", "Compartment measurement: filipin or cholesterol-oxidase imaging with LAMP1 co-localisation, or lysosome immunoprecipitation followed by sterol LC-MS, should show a higher unesterified-cholesterol content per lysosome and a higher lysosome:ER free-cholesterol ratio in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or lower lysosomal free cholesterol in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism, since step 4 is entirely inferred.", "Sensing test: acute LDL or cholesterol-cyclodextrin loading should suppress SREBP-target transcripts less in APOE4 than APOE3 (blunted ER sterol sensing). Equivalent suppression in both genotypes would falsify the claim that the ER sterol pool is selectively low in APOE4.", "Flux test: 13C-acetate or D2O labelling should show higher de novo sterol and fatty-acid synthesis flux and higher cholesteryl-ester mass in APOE4; if labelling flux and cholesteryl-ester mass are unchanged, the transcript module is not converted into flux and the feed-forward loop in step 6 fails.", "Uptake test: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade in APOE4 microglia should reduce lysosomal cholesterol load and lower the hydrolase/TFEB module; no change in lysosomal sterol after SCARB1 loss would falsify step 1 as the main delivery route.", "Protein-level check: immunoblot or targeted MS in the same cultures should show increased mature GBA, GAA, HEXA and cathepsin B/D protein in APOE4 with unchanged or reduced NPC2 protein. Increased NPC2 protein in proportion to the hydrolases would falsify the proposed bottleneck even if the transcript ratio holds."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipoprotein/lipid-uptake receptors, most strikingly SCARB1, alongside CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163 and APOE itself, which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein-associated cholesterol, cholesteryl ester and sphingolipid into the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A coherent acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, SMPD1, NAGLU, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1) plus TFEB is elevated well above the dataset-wide shift, consistent with expanded luminal catabolic capacity that liberates free cholesterol and sphingoid bases inside the lumen.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck): The measured transcript for the luminal cholesterol-shuttle NPC2 is not scaled with that module (+1.17 versus a global median of +1.46 and hydrolase values of +4 to +10), so we propose that NPC2/NPC1-mediated transfer of unesterified cholesterol to the limiting membrane becomes the rate-limiting step of the pathway; the exporters NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1 and LIPA were not measured here.", "Step 4 (inferred localization): Cholesterol therefore accumulates as a late-endosomal/lysosomal pool rather than reaching the ER sterol-sensing pool at the SCAP-INSIG site.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A low ER sterol signal keeps SREBP processing permissive, which we infer from the elevated SREBP-target/ processing module (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, SCD) despite an apparently lipid-replete cell.", "Step 6 (inferred flux, feed-forward): Continued LDLR/SCARB1-driven uptake plus sterol esterification and glyceride synthesis (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SCP2) route the trapped sterol into esterified/droplet storage instead of efflux, closing a feed-forward loop that sustains the lysosomal-lipid microglial state (GPNMB, CTSD, TREM2, APOE) seen in APOE4."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol-egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: hydrolase/uptake capacity scales up while NPC2-dependent export does not, leaving the ER sterol-poor and SREBP targets induced"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2295720562714618, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29026761113058236, "cosine_similarity": 0.32886255048312, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6218964401294498, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2295720562714618, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.29026761113058236, "cosine_similarity": 0.32886255048312, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6218964401294498, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.99053975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 269}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The uniform positive offset of the supplied RNA table (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% of 2212 rows positive, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0) is at least partly a selection/normalisation/composition artefact; the mechanism relies on the relative ordering of modules within this table, not on the absolute sign of any single gene.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so absence of a gene (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, MSR1, P2RY12, CX3CR1 are all absent) means not reported, not unchanged; the bottleneck step (NPC1/NPC2-dependent egress) is therefore only partially represented (gene:NPC2).", "Transcript abundance changes are assumed to translate at least monotonically into protein and enzymatic capacity for SOAT1, SCD, LDLR and the lysosomal hydrolases; no sterol-pathway protein was resolvable in the protein-spot data, so this is untested here.", "Protein spots each carry 2-6 candidate genes (median 5) and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for any specific enzyme in this mechanism.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effects is preserved; module comparisons use ranks and signs within the same table so they do not depend on the base.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an APOE4-dependent change in astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply could drive the same microglial transcriptional state; astrocyte lipoprotein composition was not measured.", "Sterol pool size, cholesteryl-ester content, lipid-droplet number, subcellular cholesterol localization, SREBP-2 cleavage and all fluxes are inferred; none were measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily at the step where internalized lipoprotein/membrane-derived cholesterol is returned from the late-endosome/lysosome to the ER regulatory pool. Transcript data show a coordinated rise in scavenger-uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, COLEC12, MRC1, CD163, STAB1), in esterification/storage capacity (SOAT1 with its oleate supplier SCD, plus DGAT1), and in lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts, while every measured SREBP-pathway transcript (SREBF2, SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, ACAT2, ACSS2, MYLIP) is simultaneously higher rather than feedback-suppressed. We propose that the combination of esterification-driven diversion and endolysosomal retention keeps the ER-accessible sterol pool functionally low despite increased total sterol influx, producing a self-sustaining import/synthesis cycle. Sterol pool sizes, esterification flux, localization and causal direction are inferred, not measured; only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were supplied and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (avasimibe or CI-976) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the cholesteryl-ester sink, raise ER-accessible sterol, and therefore reduce the SREBP-2 target set (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, LSS) toward APOE3 levels and reduce nuclear/cleaved SREBP-2 by immunoblot, while leaving scavenger-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, CD163) largely unchanged. If SOAT1 inhibition lowers cholesteryl esters (confirmed by lipidomics or Nile-red/filipin ratio) but leaves the SREBP-2 target elevation and cleaved SREBP-2 unchanged, the esterification-sink step is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Filipin plus LAMP1 imaging should show a higher fraction of unesterified cholesterol in the LAMP1-positive compartment in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions, with a correspondingly lower ER/plasma-membrane accessible pool measured by a genetically encoded sterol sensor (e.g. D4H-mCherry). Equal LAMP1-compartment filipin signal and equal D4H recruitment between genotypes would falsify the localization claim.", "Occlusion test: acute NPC1 blockade with U18666A should produce a smaller incremental increase in lysosomal free cholesterol and a smaller incremental induction of SREBP-2 targets in APOE4 than in APOE3, because the egress step is already partially limiting in APOE4. An equal or larger incremental response in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck assignment.", "Rescue test: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or an LXR agonist that restores acceptor-directed efflux should normalise the APOE4 SREBP-2 target elevation and reduce GPNMB/LGALS3/CCL2 transcripts within 24-48 h. Persistence of the SREBP-2 elevation after sterol extraction would indicate a sterol-independent transcriptional driver.", "Normalisation control: the SREBP-2 module elevation must survive spike-in or housekeeping-anchored quantification (qPCR or nascent-transcription assay on HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, INSIG1) against a background of unchanged non-sterol genes. If the module elevation disappears once the global +1.46 median offset is removed by an independent normalisation, the sterol arm of this hypothesis is not supported and the lysosomal-hydrolase module (the only module significantly above the global shift, permutation p \u003c 0.001 on the mean) becomes the preferred primary lesion.", "Flux test: [3H]- or [13C]-acetate incorporation into sterols and [3H]oleate incorporation into cholesteryl esters should both be higher in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia under mock conditions, while cholesterol efflux to apoA-I/HDL acceptors should not be proportionally higher. Higher efflux that matches the increased influx would falsify the accumulation claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-binding scavenger and endocytic receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2), which we infer raises the flux of exogenous sterol-bearing cargo into the endolysosomal system; receptor surface density and uptake rate were not measured.", "Increased cargo load is accompanied by a coordinated rise in lysosomal acid-hydrolase and acidification transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:NPC2, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB), consistent with an expanded degradative compartment; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and compartment volume are inferred, not observed.", "Sterol that reaches the cytosolic face is diverted into storage rather than to the ER sensor: SOAT1 transcript rises together with SCD, which supplies the oleoyl-CoA that SOAT1 prefers, and with DGAT1; we infer an increased cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid sink. No cholesteryl-ester, free-cholesterol or lipid-droplet measurement was supplied.", "Because esterification and endolysosomal retention lower the ER-accessible (regulatory) sterol pool, SCAP/INSIG-dependent sensing reads 'sterol-poor' and SREBP-2 processing is inferred to remain active, sustaining the uniformly elevated SREBP module (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:ACSS2) and the lipogenic arm (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). SREBP-2 cleavage and nuclear occupancy were not measured.", "Sustained LDLR-driven import plus continued endogenous synthesis feed back into step 1, so uptake and storage rise together instead of being counter-regulated; partial counter-regulation is visible (gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:PLTP) but is inferred to be insufficient because it acts on import and on the extracellular acceptor step rather than on the endolysosomal egress bottleneck.", "The resulting lipid-laden state is inferred to shift microglial identity toward a scavenger/lipid-handling macrophage-like program (gene:GPNMB, gene:F13A1, gene:FOLR2, gene:SELENOP, gene:RNASE1, gene:MAFB, gene:SLCO2B1, gene:A2M, gene:LGALS1, gene:LGALS3, gene:PLA2G7) with a modest inflammatory component (gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL8, gene:TLR2, gene:NLRP3, gene:MYD88, gene:CD14), rather than to a clean homeostatic microglial state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sequester internalized sterol in an expanded endolysosomal/esterified pool, so the ER regulatory cholesterol pool under-reads and uptake-plus-synthesis programs stay switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22017309889943967, "cosine_similarity": 0.32841899704109434, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6135954692556634, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22017309889943967, "cosine_similarity": 0.32841899704109434, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6135954692556634, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.213476, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 270}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_069", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so relative rank within the list, not absolute enrichment against a whole transcriptome, is the interpretable quantity.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effects is preserved; only the sign and the relative ordering of RNA effects are used, never an absolute fold-change value.", "Changes in ARHGDIA/ARHGAP transcript abundance translate into an increased GDI/GAP-mediated restraint on Rho-family nucleotide cycling; Rac-GTP itself was not measured, and RAC1 and CDC42 transcripts are absent from the supplied list.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; a spot is treated only as evidence that the actin/cytoskeletal and lysosomal protein classes are present and not globally depleted, never as identification of a specific protein.", "The strong global upward shift of the RNA list (about 77% of rows positive) is treated as a possible normalisation, ambient-RNA or cell-composition effect of the astrocyte co-culture, so directionally down-shifted coherent modules are weighted more heavily than up-shifted ones.", "Microglial identity, engulfment rate, lysosomal flux, lipid content and cell-surface receptor protein levels were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred, not observed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by loss of uptake receptors or of degradative capacity, but by a coordinated transcriptional shift in the Rho-GTPase regulator layer - large increase in the Rac/Cdc42 sequestering factor ARHGDIA plus increases in RhoGAPs, together with loss of the haematopoietic Rac-activation and actomyosin module (RAC2, DOCK8, PLEK, FAM49B, MYO1F, ACTB, MYH9). We propose this lowers the pool of GTP-loaded Rac available at nascent phagocytic cups, so that particulate-cargo internalisation becomes the rate-limiting step, while ligand binding, receptor abundance and downstream TFEB-linked lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase capacity are unchanged or elevated. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript changes are measured, the GTPase activity and flux steps are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, a PAK-PBD pull-down or Rac-FRET assay should show reduced active Rac-GTP as a fraction of total Rac at the cell cortex, with total Rac protein and Arp2/3 (ARPC2/ACTR2) protein unchanged or higher. Equal or higher Rac-GTP fraction in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Expressing constitutively active Rac1 (or knocking down ARHGDIA) in APOE4 microglia should restore per-cell uptake of particulate cargo (beads, synaptosomes, myelin) toward APOE3 levels without normalising the lysosomal transcript programme (TFEB, CTSB, GBA, ATP6V1H). If ARHGDIA knockdown normalises lysosomal genes but not uptake, the bottleneck is downstream, not at Rac.", "Pulse-chase separation of steps: APOE4 cells should show near-normal surface binding of opsonised or TREM2/MERTK-ligand cargo at 4 degrees C but reduced internalised fraction at 37 degrees C, and near-normal or faster degradation of cargo that is delivered by an actin-independent route (soluble DQ-BSA, LDL). Reduced degradation of already-internalised cargo would instead support a lysosomal-flux bottleneck and weaken this hypothesis.", "Rho-side test: ROCK or myosin-II inhibition (Y-27632, blebbistatin) should not rescue, and should preferentially impair, APOE4 uptake if the defect is Rac-limited rather than caused by excess RhoA-driven contractility; a clear rescue by ROCK inhibition would favour a contractility-based alternative.", "Specificity test: if the down-shift of RAC2, DOCK8, PLEK, MYO1F, ACTB and MYH9 disappears after correcting for astrocyte-derived ambient RNA or for myeloid-fraction differences between the APOE4 and APOE3 samples, the transcriptional basis of the hypothesis is an artefact and the mechanism should be rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with a transcriptional state in which the Rho-family regulator balance is shifted toward inhibition: ARHGDIA (RhoGDI1) is among the most strongly increased transcripts and the RhoGAPs ARHGAP1 and ARHGAP35 are also increased, whereas the myeloid Rac activation/effector module (RAC2, DOCK8, PLEK, VAV-associated signalling) is decreased (measured RNA; the GDP/GTP loading state itself is not measured).", "Inferred step: a larger GDI-bound, GDP-loaded Rho-family reserve and increased GAP-mediated hydrolysis reduce the local, membrane-associated Rac-GTP that is required to nucleate branched actin at a forming phagocytic cup, even though Arp2/3 subunit transcripts (ARPC1B, ARPC4, ARPC5), CFL1 and actin-related protein spots are not depleted.", "Inferred step: loss of the actomyosin components that close and constrict the cup (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F strongly decreased at RNA level; FAM49B/CYRIB decreased) further limits cup extension and scission, so the block is at internalisation of large particulate cargo rather than at ligand recognition.", "Receptor-level engagement is preserved or increased (TREM2, MERTK, CD36, MRC1, SCARB1, FCGR1A, C1QA, ITGB1/ITGA6 all increased), so surface-bound and actin-independent, fluid-phase/lipoprotein routes continue to deliver soluble lipid cargo while particulate uptake lags.", "Downstream of the block, a TFEB-associated endolysosomal programme is coordinately increased (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, LAMP1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, RAB7A, VPS26A, CHMP4B), i.e. degradative capacity is expanded and is therefore unlikely to be the limiting node; the increase in SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24/LDLR indicates a parallel lipogenic/sterol programme rather than a hydrolase deficit.", "Net inferred phenotype: APOE4 microglia bind but under-internalise particulate cargo per cell, accumulate an expanded but comparatively under-loaded degradative compartment, and drift away from a motile, immune-effector myeloid programme (SPN, CTSS, CSF1, PTPRC-associated genes decreased)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift the Rho-family regulator balance toward Rac sequestration, making Rac-dependent actin remodelling at the engulfment step the bottleneck while receptor and endolysosomal capacity are increased"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14438946940885425, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1802576276390098, "cosine_similarity": 0.32827784294303747, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_069", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6081747572815533, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14438946940885425, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1802576276390098, "cosine_similarity": 0.32827784294303747, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6081747572815533, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.661736, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 271}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_012", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every |effect| is \u003e= 1.000, 77% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); we assume the direction of each reported effect is reliable but treat magnitudes and absences (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, GRAMD1 family were not supplied) as uninformative.", "We assume transcript differences translate at least partly into protein and enzymatic capacity; the supplied 2-D protein spots contain 3-5 candidate genes each, do not include any sterol enzyme, and show no correlation with candidate-gene RNA (Spearman rho = -0.06, n = 71 spots), so proteome data neither confirm nor refute steps 1-6.", "Cholesterol pool sizes (ER-accessible, lysosomal, plasma-membrane), cholesteryl-ester mass, oxysterol levels, transport flux and efflux to acceptors were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred quantities in this hypothesis.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so exogenous astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply may differ between genotypes; we assume the intracellular routing difference, not a difference in extracellular sterol supply alone, dominates.", "Biological replicate structure is 'not supplied in workbook' and the data are 10X Flex single-cell derived, so extremely small adjusted p-values may reflect cell-level pseudoreplication rather than independent replicates; no causal direction is claimed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coherent transcriptional state in which endolysosomal hydrolase/acidification machinery and sterol-esterification/storage genes are raised together with lipoprotein-uptake and cholesterol-biosynthesis genes. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the return of internalised cholesterol from the late-endosome/lysosome to the ER-accessible regulatory pool: sterol that is taken up (SCARB1/CD36/LDLR-associated routes) is retained in acidic and esterified compartments (SOAT1, DGAT1, CIDEB, expanded hydrolase system), so ER sterol sensing continues to read 'low' and keeps SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, LSS, EBP, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2) elevated, producing a futile uptake-and-storage cycle rather than efflux. Transcript abundance is measured; sterol pool sizes, transport flux, esterification flux, efflux and enzyme activities are inferred, not observed, and no causal direction is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (sterol-loading challenge): acute loading with LDL or cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR24) in APOE3 microglia; APOE4 should show markedly blunted suppression (at least 2-fold smaller log-suppression) together with a smaller rise in an ER-accessible cholesterol probe (ALOD4/GRAM-domain biosensor). If APOE4 suppresses these transcripts as efficiently as APOE3 and its ER-accessible cholesterol probe signal rises equally, the proposed ER-delivery bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (esterification block): SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, shift cholesteryl ester to free cholesterol, raise the ER-accessible pool and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts; no change in the SREBP-2 signature after effective esterification blockade would weaken step 4-5.", "Discriminating perturbation 3 (occlusion test): pharmacological block of endolysosomal sterol export (U18666A) in APOE3 should phenocopy the APOE4 pattern (raised SREBP-2 targets plus raised hydrolase transcripts), whereas the same treatment should produce a substantially smaller incremental change in APOE4 because the step is already limiting; equal-magnitude responses in both genotypes argue against a pre-existing transport bottleneck.", "Separating lysosome biogenesis from sterol sensing: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) but, if the bottleneck is transport rather than lysosome number, should not normalise the SREBP-2 target signature; normalisation of SREBP-2 targets by TFEB knockdown would favour the alternative that lysosomal expansion is the primary driver and the sterol genes are passengers.", "Lipid-level prediction: APOE4 microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio, more filipin/cholesterol signal within LAMP1-positive compartments, lower desmosterol:cholesterol (consistent with raised DHCR24) and no increase in ApoA-I- or HDL-acceptor cholesterol efflux; finding equal or higher efflux and an unchanged CE:FC ratio in APOE4 would weaken the whole storage-sink mechanism.", "Counter-evidence-driven falsifier: raised gene:SMPD1 and gene:GBA predict more sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide hydrolysis, which should liberate plasma-membrane accessible cholesterol and oppose ER sterol depletion. If APOE4 cells show an increased, not decreased, ER-accessible cholesterol pool alongside the elevated SREBP-2 transcripts, the sensing-mismatch model must be replaced (for example by SREBP-independent transcriptional drift)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/lipid-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 the 99th-percentile effect of the supplied list, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR) and of the microglial lipoprotein/phospholipid-handling set (gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2), which we interpret as increased capacity for lipid internalisation, not as measured uptake flux.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred organelle state): the endolysosomal system is transcriptionally expanded (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:SCARB2, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A); this set is the only panel enriched in effect magnitude above the already up-shifted background, and we infer enlarged/acidified degradative compartments where internalised sterol accumulates.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): delivery of that endolysosomal cholesterol to the ER-accessible (sensor-facing) pool is limiting. Transcripts for the non-vesicular ER-directed sterol-transfer step are either reduced (gene:OSBPL8) or absent from this selected list (NPC1, GRAMD1/Aster, STARD3 were not measured), so the bottleneck is a hypothesis about transport flux, not an observation.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): sterol that does reach the ER is preferentially esterified/stored rather than expanding the free ER pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:CIDEB, with gene:SREBF1 and gene:SCD supporting a lipogenic/storage-permissive state), further limiting the regulatory free-sterol pool.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred signalling): because ER-accessible sterol stays low, SCAP/INSIG-dependent SREBP-2 output remains active: gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24 and gene:LDLR are all higher in APOE4, closing a futile loop of continued synthesis plus uptake into the same storage sink.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts, inferred lipid consequence): raised gene:DHCR24 (and gene:DHCR7) would consume desmosterol/7-dehydrocholesterol, and raised gene:CH25H and gene:CYP27A1 indicate oxysterol-generating capacity; we predict a lipidomic signature of higher cholesteryl ester relative to free cholesterol, lower desmosterol:cholesterol, and higher 27-hydroxycholesterol in APOE4, with no measured increase in ABCA1/ABCG1-dependent export (those genes were not measured here)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route cholesterol into an expanded endolysosomal/esterified store, leaving the ER-accessible sterol pool low and the SREBP-2 uptake program persistently on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22565816194660857, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2615958038744888, "cosine_similarity": 0.32782196296789723, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6219288025889967, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22565816194660857, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2615958038744888, "cosine_similarity": 0.32782196296789723, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6219288025889967, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.75255925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 272}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Gene-symbol-to-function assignments (e.g., LPCAT1 = lysophosphatidylcholine re-acylation, AGPAT2/GPAT4 = glycerol-3-phosphate/lysophosphatidic-acid acyltransferases, DGAT1/ABHD5 = triacylglycerol synthesis/lipid-droplet regulation, ACSL4/ACSL5 = long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases) reflect unverified background biochemical knowledge, not a measurement in this dataset.", "The unspecified RNA log fold-change base is treated consistently as reported; no attempt was made to convert or assume log2 vs natural log across genes.", "Reported log fold changes are treated as steady-state transcript abundance differences at Day 30 mock condition; they are not assumed to equal protein abundance, enzyme activity, or metabolic flux.", "Absence of a given lipid-family gene from the discovery list (e.g., LPCAT2-4, MBOAT7, DGAT2, LPIN1-3, PLA2G4A) is treated as unknown/not-selected, not as evidence that gene is unchanged.", "Protein-spot candidate-gene lists are treated as ambiguous identities; no single candidate gene within a multi-gene spot is treated as confirmed to be the changed protein.", "The 3:1 positive:negative skew of the overall selected RNA list is treated as the relevant background for judging whether any pathway subset is unusually one-directional, rather than assuming a 50/50 null."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-microglia display a broad, positively-skewed lipid-gene transcriptional program in which phospholipid re-acylation and triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet synthesis genes are elevated together with sterol-biosynthesis/sensing and glycosphingolipid-catabolism genes, while a subset of acyl-CoA-activating and alternative-lipase genes are reduced. This pattern is consistent with an altered routing of glycerolipid metabolism toward membrane phospholipid remodeling and lipid storage rather than toward long-chain acyl-CoA-dependent oxidative or lysophospholipid-clearing pathways, but whether this reflects increased flux, successful adaptation, or a transcriptional attempt without functional follow-through is not established by these RNA/protein-spot data alone.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating prediction: In matched APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-microglia under the same mock condition, a pulse-chase acyl-chain incorporation assay (e.g., 13C- or BODIPY-labeled fatty acid pulse followed by LC-MS/imaging) should show increased incorporation into phosphatidylcholine/triacylglycerol pools and increased lipid-droplet number/size in APOE4 relative to APOE3 if the proposed re-acylation/storage routing shift is functionally real. If labeled fatty-acid incorporation into phospholipids/TAG and lipid-droplet content are not increased (or are decreased) in APOE4 despite the transcript pattern, this would weaken the mechanism and favor a transcriptional-only or failed-compensation interpretation rather than increased routing/throughput.", "A second, weaker-condition test: pharmacologic SREBP inhibition (e.g., fatostatin) or exogenous cholesterol/LDL loading in APOE4 microglia should reduce LPCAT1/AGPAT2/DGAT1 transcript elevation if these are downstream of a shared sterol-sensing trigger; failure of SREBP inhibition or cholesterol loading to change these transcripts would argue the glycerolipid remodeling program is driven independently of the sterol-sensing arm, undermining the proposed coordinated single-trigger mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated (in this dataset) with a genome-wide-selected list of differentially expressed transcripts that is already ~77% positive (gene:?? plus 1704 others), so any pathway-level positivity must be interpreted against this skewed background rather than a 50/50 null.", "Within this background, glycerophospholipid re-acylation (Lands-cycle) transcripts LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, AGPAT2, AGPAT4, GPAT4 and the neutral-lipid synthesis/lipid-droplet regulators DGAT1 and ABHD5 are elevated (observed RNA log fold changes, e.g. gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ABHD5 +1.04), consistent with increased transcriptional capacity for phospholipid remodeling and triglyceride/lipid-droplet formation.", "In the same list, the alternative acyltransferase isoform GPAT3 (-2.23), the lysophospholipase/lipid-droplet-associated patatin-domain enzyme PNPLA1 (-1.55), and the long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4 (-2.14) and ACSL5 (-3.12) are reduced, indicating that not all glycerolipid-handling enzymes move in the same direction; specifically the isoforms that feed long-chain acyl-CoA into oxidation or into rapid lysophospholipid turnover are down while re-acylation/storage enzymes are up.", "This selective pattern co-occurs with a fully one-directional elevation of the SREBP-associated sterol program (SREBF1 +4.67, SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87, HMGCS1 +1.08, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, SOAT1 +1.25, LDLR +1.50, NPC2 +1.17; 11/11 positive) and glycosphingolipid/sphingolipid catabolic genes (GBA +6.71, GBA2 +2.63, SMPD1 +5.63, CERS4 +2.52, CERS6 +1.06; 5/5 positive), suggesting a coordinated, multi-arm lipid-handling transcriptional state rather than an isolated single-gene change.", "Protein-spot data cannot confirm any single glycerolipid enzyme (no acyl-transferase or lipase candidate genes appear among the 208 candidate identities across 92 ambiguous multi-gene spots), but a partially overlapping set of lysosomal hydrolase/vacuolar-ATPase/retromer candidate spots (e.g., protein_spot:052 CTSL-containing +2.14, protein_spot:053 CTSD-containing +1.54, protein_spot:067 CTSB/HEXB-containing -1.00, protein_spot:064/065 ATP6V1E1-containing -1.20/-0.93) shows a mixed but net-positive-leaning pattern (17 positive vs 9 negative of 29 spots touching lysosomal/degradative candidates), which is compatible with, but does not confirm, altered lysosomal/membrane lipid turnover accompanying the transcriptional shift.", "Because RNA abundance does not establish enzymatic activity, flux, or subcellular routing, and no lipidomic, lipid-droplet imaging, or direct enzymatic-activity measurement is supplied, the coordinated transcript pattern is best interpreted as evidence for altered transcriptional routing/capacity for glycerolipid handling in APOE4 microglia at baseline, not as proof of increased phospholipid re-acylation flux, increased triglyceride storage, or a functional membrane-turnover defect.", "The decisive unmeasured link is whether this transcript-level shift translates into measurable changes in lipid-droplet content, membrane phospholipid acyl-chain composition, or acyl-CoA flux; without that measurement the mechanism remains a plausible, testable routing hypothesis rather than an established causal chain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a coordinated transcriptional shift toward glycerophospholipid re-acylation and neutral-lipid storage, diverting acyl-CoA away from long-chain-CoA-dependent routes"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5426651404940368, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24099193800725507, "cosine_similarity": 0.32776074201539457, "direction_accuracy": 0.5388349514563107, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5977378640776699, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.5426651404940368, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24099193800725507, "cosine_similarity": 0.32776074201539457, "direction_accuracy": 0.5388349514563107, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5977378640776699, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.766293, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_049", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are on an unspecified logarithm base; only signs and within-dataset rank comparisons are used, and no absolute fold change is asserted.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a |log fold change| \u003e= 1.000 floor and a strong global positive shift (1705/2212 up, median +1.46), so every set-level claim is made relative to that shifted background by permutation, not against zero.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme capacity, not for measured activity, flux, localization or protein amount; PDH phosphorylation, respiration, lysosomal pH and lipid species were not measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and heavy keratin contamination, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; they are used only as non-confirmatory or counter-evidence.", "The APOE4 and APOE3 lines are isogenic and the pseudobulk contrast reflects genotype rather than differences in microglial maturation state or astrocyte ambient-RNA contamination; biological replicate number was not supplied and this assumption is untested here.", "Genes absent from the list (ACLY, HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, PLIN2, PDK1, CPT1A, LDHA, P2RY12) are unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Background pathway memberships used to group genes are unverified prior knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 principally at one rate-controlling node: mitochondrial pyruvate import and oxidative decarboxylation (MPC2-PDH-TCA). Transcript abundances for this node and for the downstream electron-transport chain, malate-aspartate shuttle and citrate carrier are coordinately higher in APOE4 while upper-glycolytic transcripts (HK2, PFKP) are lower, whereas the assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal/endocytic machinery shows no enrichment beyond the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list. We propose that APOE4 shifts catabolic mode toward mitochondrial oxidation, that an elevated lysosomal hydrolase/lipid-receptor program supplies additional lipid-derived substrate, and that SLC25A1-mediated citrate export feeds cytosolic acetyl-CoA into the sterol arm and into SOAT1/DGAT1 esterification, producing an APOE4-selective increase in cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol. All statements about flux, enzyme activity, localization and direction are inferred; only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: MPC blockade (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should collapse the genotype difference - reducing pyruvate-driven oxygen consumption, 13C-glucose M+2 labelling of citrate/glutamate, and cholesteryl-ester plus triacylglycerol content toward APOE3 levels - while leaving phagocytic uptake of beads or myelin largely unchanged. If MPC inhibition leaves APOE4 neutral lipid and respiration unchanged, or if it changes APOE3 equally, the primary bottleneck is wrong.", "U-13C-glucose tracing should show higher fractional labelling of TCA intermediates and of newly synthesised cholesterol/cholesteryl ester in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or lower labelling in APOE4 falsifies Steps 2-5.", "Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and maximal OCR and a lower ECAR/OCR ratio in APOE4; a more glycolytic APOE4 phenotype would falsify Step 1 and Step 3.", "SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should lower cholesteryl ester and raise free cholesterol selectively in APOE4; absence of a genotype-selective effect weakens the esterification-sink step without necessarily falsifying the mitochondrial node.", "Lysosomal acidification blockade (bafilomycin A1) or combined CTSB/CTSD inhibition should reduce the APOE4-specific excess of TCA-intermediate labelling from 13C-lipid substrate; if lysosomal blockade does not attenuate the APOE4 oxidative excess, Step 4 is wrong and the mitochondrial shift is lysosome-independent.", "Immunoblot for phospho-PDHA1(Ser293) should show a lower phospho/total ratio in APOE4 (consistent with PDP1 +3.00); an unchanged or higher ratio would weaken Step 2, which is the step with the largest inference gap.", "Negative control for the assigned focus: phagocytic index, F-actin/phalloidin cup formation and transferrin or dextran endocytosis rate should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock; a large phagocytic or actin-dependent deficit would indicate the rejected focus mechanism is primary instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia lower upper-glycolytic capacity - HK2 -3.67 and PFKP -3.08 - despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (SLC2A1 +2.37, SLC2A3 +3.73), which we infer reduces glycolytic lactate output rather than glucose uptake. Neither flux nor lactate was measured.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): the mitochondrial pyruvate gateway is transcriptionally up-scaled - MPC2 +7.98, PDP1 +3.00 (PDH-activating phosphatase), DLD +5.54 - which we infer raises PDH activity and acetyl-CoA entry. PDH phosphorylation state and PDK transcripts were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): TCA and respiratory capacity rise coordinately - ACO2 +3.54, OGDH +8.56, IDH3G +3.94, IDH3B +2.02, SDHB +1.65, plus 38 nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits with median +2.64 versus a global DE median of +1.46 (permutation p = 0.0013) - together with the malate-aspartate shuttle (MDH1 +8.72, GOT1 +6.43, SLC25A11 +4.50) and adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5 +5.56. We infer increased oxidative flux and cytosolic-NADH transfer; no respirometry, ATP or membrane-potential measurement exists here.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred substrate delivery): a TFEB-associated degradative program (TFEB +2.38, TFEC +1.65, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, NAGLU +5.91, GM2A +2.01; hydrolase set median +2.40, permutation p = 0.047) and elevated lipid-uptake receptors (SCARB1 +8.22, LDLR +1.50, CD36 +1.38, ABCA7 +2.14, APOE +1.24) are inferred to increase delivery of lipid- and lipoprotein-derived substrate into the endolysosomal-mitochondrial catabolic system. Lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and lipid uptake rate were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1 +4.47) is inferred to supply cytosolic acetyl-CoA to ACAT2 +2.04 and to a mildly activated sterol arm (SREBF1 +4.67, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, HMGCS1 +1.08, SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87). ACLY, HMGCR and SQLE are absent from this filtered list and must not be treated as measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, predicted lipid phenotype): the esterification sink is up-scaled (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, FABP5 +1.13), which we predict converts sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol, giving APOE4-selective neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet accumulation. No lipid species and no droplet imaging are present in the supplied data."], "title": "APOE4 iPSC-microglia commit carbon to mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and citrate export, converting lysosome-derived and imported lipid into esterified neutral lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24700919395931026, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2690034986522419, "cosine_similarity": 0.3277132009518954, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_049", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6278381877022654, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24700919395931026, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2690034986522419, "cosine_similarity": 0.3277132009518954, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6278381877022654, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90385325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 273}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_149", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Effects are reported as log fold change of APOE4 relative to APOE3 under mock treatment; the RNA logarithm base is unspecified, so only sign, rank and relative magnitude are used, never absolute fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05); genes absent from the file (e.g. RAC1, ACTR2/3, WASF2, LIPA, NPC1, GRN) are unmeasured here and must not be read as unchanged.", "77% of supplied RNA rows are positive, so an increase is weak evidence on its own; the mechanism therefore rests mainly on the coordinate decreases, which run against the global shift. This assumes the global up-shift is a normalisation/selection property and does not systematically drive abundant transcripts such as ACTB, MYH9 and TMSB10 negative.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding protein pools; no actin, myosin, GTPase-GTP loading, phagosome or lipid pool was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots each carry ~5 candidate genes and were therefore not used as identity-level support; no protein observation is cited as evidence for a named protein.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype differences may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect altered microglial-astrocyte composition rather than an intrinsic microglial program.", "Association only: nothing in this dataset establishes that the ARHGDIA/actomyosin changes cause any uptake phenotype."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a coordinate transcriptional decrease in core actomyosin/Rac engulfment machinery (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, FAM49B, ARHGDIB, TMSB10) together with a large increase in the Rho-GTPase sequestering factor ARHGDIA, while cargo-recognition receptors and endolysosomal/hydrolase transcripts are increased. We propose that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is actin/non-muscle-myosin-II-driven phagocytic cup extension and closure: APOE4 microglia bind and signal on cargo and retain (even elevate) downstream degradative capacity, but internalize large particulate cargo less efficiently, biasing uptake toward small-scale clathrin/dynamin- and scavenger-receptor-mediated endocytosis of soluble and lipoprotein cargo. All statements about GTPase activity, actin dynamics, uptake flux and causal direction are inferences from RNA abundance, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake assay: with dual-labelled large cargo (pHrodo plus non-quenched surface label; myelin, synaptosomes or 3-6 um beads), APOE4 microglia should show equal or higher surface-bound cargo but a lower internalized:bound ratio and a longer time-to-closure by live imaging than isogenic APOE3. If the internalized:bound ratio is equal or higher in APOE4, the engulfment-step bottleneck is falsified.", "Cargo-size dissociation: soluble/small-cargo uptake (transferrin, 10 kDa dextran, DiI-AcLDL) should be preserved or increased in APOE4 while large-particle uptake is reduced. If both are reduced to a similar degree, a general endocytic or energetic defect, not an actin-cup defect, is the better explanation.", "Phenocopy and occlusion: blebbistatin (NMII inhibition) or MYH9/ACTB knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 uptake profile, and the same treatments should produce a smaller additional decrement in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal fractional sensitivity in both genotypes weakens the mechanism.", "GTPase-sequestration test: ARHGDIA knockdown in APOE4 microglia should increase GTP-loaded Rac1/Cdc42 in pulldown assays and partially restore large-particle engulfment without increasing receptor transcripts (MERTK, TREM2, CD36). If active Rac1/Cdc42 rises but engulfment does not improve, the ARHGDIA step is wrong even if the actomyosin bottleneck survives.", "Protein-level check: immunoblot or targeted MS should show lower MYH9 and lower total beta-actin in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia. Unchanged or higher MYH9/beta-actin protein would show the transcript decreases are not propagated and would substantially weaken the mechanism.", "Degradation is not limiting: once cargo is delivered intracellularly (e.g. by centrifugation-forced or receptor-independent loading), DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester dequenching rates in APOE4 should be equal to or faster than APOE3. Slower intracellular degradation would move the bottleneck downstream to the lysosome and falsify the stated primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_149", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts encoding the structural core of the engulfment cytoskeleton are lower in APOE4 (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:TMSB10 -1.30) as is the haematopoietic Rac module (gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:DOCK8 -1.99) and the WAVE-regulatory component gene:FAM49B (-5.83); this 11-gene core module averages -1.49 against a strongly positive background (permutation p=5e-4), i.e. it moves against the global up-shift.", "Measured: gene:ARHGDIA (RhoGDI-1) is among the largest increases in the dataset (+10.61) while gene:ARHGDIB (RhoGDI-2, the myeloid paralogue) falls (-1.98). Inferred (not measured): a higher RhoGDI-1:Rac/Cdc42 stoichiometry sequesters prenylated Rho-family GTPases in the cytosol and lowers the pool of membrane-bound GTP-Rac1/Cdc42 available at nascent phagocytic cups.", "Inferred: reduced actin/NMII building blocks plus reduced membrane-delivered active Rac lower the force and F-actin turnover needed for pseudopod extension and cup closure, making internalization of large particulate cargo (apoptotic material, myelin, synaptosomes, beads) the rate-limiting step, while receptor engagement is unaffected.", "Measured, upstream of the bottleneck: recognition/opsonic receptor transcripts are up (gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:C1QA +1.25). Inferred: cargo binding and receptor-proximal signalling are preserved or increased, so bound-but-not-internalized cargo accumulates.", "Measured, downstream of the bottleneck: small-vesicle endocytic and endolysosomal transcripts are up (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.10, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:CHMP4B +3.82) as are hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits and gene:TFEB (+2.38; gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51). Inferred: degradative and clathrin/dynamin-dependent uptake capacity is not the limiting element; uptake is biased toward soluble/lipoprotein cargo (gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCARB1 +8.22).", "Inferred consequence: a recognition-high / engulfment-low / degradation-high configuration produces slow clearance of particulate cargo with continued lipid and lipoprotein internalization, which is a plausible route to the lipid-loaded, clearance-poor APOE4 microglial state (background knowledge, unverified here)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at the actomyosin-dependent engulfment step, not at recognition or degradation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12188457704094818, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21100254835710605, "cosine_similarity": 0.32731831556823426, "direction_accuracy": 0.15372168284789645, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_149", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6063818770226538, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12188457704094818, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21100254835710605, "cosine_similarity": 0.32731831556823426, "direction_accuracy": 0.15372168284789645, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6063818770226538, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.34770725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 274}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_044", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported on an unspecified logarithm base and are treated only as signed, monotone effect sizes; all comparisons are made against the +1.46 median of this selected DE list rather than against zero, because the supplied rows are pre-selected differential-expression results and not an unbiased whole transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme capacity; no enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, allosteric regulation (e.g. F2,6BP, mitochondrial HK1 binding), localisation, metabolite level or flux was measured in the supplied data.", "The unmeasured dominant isoenzymes (HK1, PFKL, PKM, LDHA, G6PD, ACLY, PDHA1, MPC1, CPT1A are absent from the supplied rows) do not fully compensate for the reduced HK2/HK3/PFKP transcripts; if they do, the proposed bottleneck fails.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with several candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying corroboration only; no spot is claimed to be a specific protein.", "The mtDNA-versus-nuclear contrast is assumed not to be purely a library-size/compositional normalisation artefact of the 10X Flex quantification; this cannot be tested with the supplied data.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply extracellular substrate (e.g. lactate, glutamine, lipoprotein lipid) that both genotypes access equally, so genotype differences reflect microglial intrinsic wiring.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so no independent assessment of the reported p-values is possible."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia, the transcriptional program is reorganised so that the committed glucose-phosphorylation/priming step (HK2, HK3, PFKP) is selectively reduced against a strongly upward-shifted differential-expression background, while glucose transporters, mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA/malate-aspartate machinery and the SREBF1/SCD lipogenic-desaturation arm are increased; we hypothesise that this makes glucose-6-phosphate supply, rather than glucose uptake or mitochondrial enzyme abundance, the rate-limiting node, forcing APOE4 microglia onto glutamate/malate-fed mitochondrial carbon that is exported as citrate into lipid rather than fully oxidised, with mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts falling relative to the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program. Causality is not established by these data; the flux, activity and metabolite claims are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or glutaminase/GLUD inhibition should reduce ATP level, basal oxygen consumption and neutral-lipid/desaturation index disproportionately in APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose or a low-glucose challenge should impair APOE3 more than APOE4. If both genotypes respond equally to UK5099/glutamine withdrawal, or if APOE4 is the more 2-DG-sensitive line, the proposed carbon-routing bottleneck is weakened.", "Stable-isotope tracing: U-13C glucose should give lower fractional labelling of lactate and lower oxidative-PPP labelling (m+0/m+1 ribose-5-phosphate pattern) in APOE4, while U-13C or U-15N glutamine should give higher labelling of citrate, aspartate and of newly synthesised fatty acid in APOE4. Equal or higher glucose-to-lactate labelling in APOE4 would falsify Step 1-2.", "Rescue: doxycycline-inducible HK2 (or PFKP) expression in APOE4 microglia should restore glycolytic rate (ECAR), restore oxidative-PPP flux and lower SCD-dependent monounsaturated-lipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation without needing to change APOE itself. Failure of HK2/PFKP restoration to move lipid content would weaken the causal chain even if flux is restored.", "Mitonuclear test: BN-PAGE or complex-specific activity assays normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOMM20) should show reduced assembled complex I/III/IV/V and reduced FCCP-stimulated spare respiratory capacity in APOE4, together with reduced mtDNA-encoded protein per nuclear-encoded subunit. Equal or higher assembled complex content and equal maximal respiration per mitochondrial mass would falsify Step 5.", "Targeted protein confirmation: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS should show lower HK2 and PFKP protein and higher MPC2, SLC25A1 and SCD protein in APOE4. If HK2/PFKP protein is unchanged while transcripts are reduced, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails and the hypothesis should be discarded in favour of a post-transcriptional model.", "Negative-control prediction: fatty-acid oxidation should not differ substantially between genotypes (the supplied FAO transcript module sits at the list median, with ACSL4 and ACSL5 low), so etomoxir should have comparable effects on both genotypes. A strong APOE4-selective etomoxir sensitivity would indicate a different substrate mechanism than the one proposed."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): transcripts for the committed glucose-priming enzymes are low relative to the +1.46 median of this selected DE list - HK2 (effect -3.67, 3.6th percentile), PFKP (-3.08, 5.5th), HK3 (-1.12, 21st) - whereas glucose transporters SLC2A3 (+3.73) and SLC2A1 (+2.37) and HIF1A (+1.98) are above median. Inference (not measured): hexokinase/PFK1 capacity, not glucose entry, limits glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-1,6-bisphosphate production in APOE4.", "Step 2 (inferred consequence): restricted glucose-6-phosphate supply lowers flux into the oxidative pentose phosphate branch; consistent transcript evidence is PGD (-1.30) and TALDO1 (-2.32) with NADK (-1.14) and NAMPT (-2.62) also low (module centered median -2.76). Inferred, not measured: reduced cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity per unit glucose. No metabolite or NADPH/NADP+ measurement is supplied.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): the mitochondrial pyruvate-oxidation and anaplerotic modules are coordinately high - MPC2 (+7.98, 99th percentile), OGDH (+8.56), MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), DLD (+5.54), SLC25A5 (+5.56), SLC25A11 (+4.50), SLC25A1 (+4.47), IDH3G (+3.94), ACO2 (+3.54), GLUD1 (+3.17), PDP1 (+3.00). Inference: cytosolic reducing equivalents and carbon are shunted into mitochondria via the malate-aspartate shuttle and MPC rather than to lactate, and glutamate/aspartate anaplerosis substitutes for the throttled glycolytic carbon.", "Step 4 (inferred routing): elevated SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) together with ACSS2 (+2.93), SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17) and ACAT2 (+2.04) indicates that mitochondrially generated citrate/acetyl units are preferentially committed to fatty-acid desaturation and sterol-ester synthesis instead of complete oxidation. Cytosolic acetyl-CoA, citrate and lipid pools were not measured here.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, stoichiometric mismatch): four of six mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS transcripts are below the list median - MT-ATP6 (-3.35), MT-CYB (-2.32), MT-ND4 (-1.80), MT-CO2 (-1.33) - while 64 nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts are shifted up (centered median +1.18, permutation p = 2e-4). Inference: assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V is capped by the mtDNA-encoded core, so the enlarged nuclear mitochondrial program yields biosynthetic (citrate/aspartate-exporting) rather than proportionally increased ATP-generating capacity.", "Step 6 (net predicted state): APOE4 microglia occupy a low-glycolytic, low-PPP, anaplerosis-dependent, lipogenically biased metabolic state with limited spare respiratory capacity and limited NADPH headroom, which is the proposed metabolic difference from APOE3 under mock conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia throttle glucose commitment at the hexokinase/PFK entry step and route carbon through mitochondrial anaplerosis and citrate export to lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19622704553099546, "cosine_similarity": 0.32719502493881225, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mean_absolute_error": 0.611621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19622704553099546, "cosine_similarity": 0.32719502493881225, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.611621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0440495, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 275}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_052", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (1706 positive-column entries vs 506 negative-column entries; 77.1% of rows positive, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05); program directionality was judged against this 77.1% positive background, and absent genes (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; effects are used only as signed, ranked magnitudes on their original reported scale, never converted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the capacity of the corresponding step; no enzymatic activity, sterol pool size, esterification flux, acidification, degradative flux, respiration, or SREBP/LXR/TFEB nuclear localisation was measured here.", "Membership of each program was fixed a priori from canonical pathway rosters (all members queried, positives and negatives reported), not chosen to make directions agree.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with a mean of 4.8 candidate identities each and frequent keratin/actin contaminants; they are used only for compatibility, and every candidate identity is retained (e.g. cathepsin-containing spots protein_spot:053/055/057 up but protein_spot:058/067/069 down).", "Descriptive coherence within a program is not a formal enrichment result; genes within these programs are co-regulated and not independent, so the quoted binomial-style comparisons are heuristics only.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein/lipid; the routing interpretation assumes cargo is available in the measured condition.", "Causality is not established; the mechanism is a hypothesis consistent with steady-state genotype-difference measurements."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional state in which lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, MiT/TFE-associated lysosomal biogenesis and hydrolases, sterol esterification/transfer, oxysterol-generating and LXR-type lipidation genes, AND SREBP-arm cholesterol/fatty-acid synthesis genes are all elevated together. Simultaneous engagement of normally opposing arms is best explained by altered routing (compartmental sequestration) of cholesterol into endolysosomal and esterified/oxidised pools so that the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool is not raised, rather than by a simple global sterol deficit or by a purely successful increase in lipid-handling throughput. The accompanying rise in nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation, mitochondrial carrier and TCA transcripts, without matched mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts, indicates the energetic support of this state and a possible assembly ceiling that would be revealed only by a future challenge. Causality is not established by these measurements; only steady-state RNA and ambiguous 2D protein spots were supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, discriminating: acute cholesterol/LDL or ac-LDL loading of the same isogenic microglia should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, INSIG1, LDLR) less in APOE4 than APOE3, and an ER-accessible-cholesterol probe (ALOD4/anthrolysin-O domain 4) should show a lower ER/PM-accessible sterol signal in APOE4 despite equal or greater total cell cholesterol. If APOE4 cells instead show equal or greater ER-accessible sterol and normal suppression on loading, the routing/sequestration mechanism is falsified and the 'increased successful throughput' alternative is favoured.", "PROSPECTIVE: blocking esterification (SOAT1/ACAT inhibitor, e.g. avasimibe) or promoting lysosomal sterol egress should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, lower SREBP-2 target transcripts and reduce filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol; no genotype difference in these responses would weaken the mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE: acidification/hydrolase capacity should be higher, not lower, in APOE4 at baseline (LysoSensor ratio, DQ-BSA and Bodipy-cholesteryl-ester degradation, cathepsin B/D activity). Finding reduced baseline lysosomal acidification/hydrolase activity would contradict the expansion step and favour a lysosomal failure model instead.", "PROSPECTIVE, challenge-revealed: Seahorse profiling should show similar or higher basal respiration in APOE4 at mock but a smaller FCCP-stimulated spare respiratory capacity and a blunted response to myelin/apoptotic-cell or LPS challenge, with unchanged or reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein relative to nuclear-encoded subunits (BN-PAGE / complex IV:complex II ratio). Equal spare capacity and matched subunit stoichiometry would remove the mitonuclear component without removing steps 1-4.", "PROSPECTIVE: knockdown of TFEB (and MITF/TFEC) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript elevation; if SREBP-2 target transcripts then rise further (more sequestration relieved less) or stay elevated while lysosomal genes fall, step 2 is downstream/parallel as claimed, whereas loss of the sterol-synthesis signature together with the lysosomal signature would indicate a single upstream driver rather than the proposed routing relationship."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and recognition - SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22), LDLR (gene:LDLR, +1.50), CD36 (gene:CD36, +1.38), TREM2 (gene:TREM2, +1.28), MRC1 (gene:MRC1, +1.36) - consistent with increased, not decreased, capacity to internalise lipid cargo. Uptake flux itself was not measured.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA): The endolysosomal compartment is transcriptionally expanded - MiT/TFE factors TFEB (+2.38), TFEC (+1.65), MITF (+1.03); 14/14 represented v-ATPase subunits positive (ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51, ATP6AP1 +2.30, ATP6V1E1/1F/0D1 ~+1.7, ATP6V1C1 +1.29, ATP6AP2 +1.18, ATP6V0D2 +1.12); LAMP1 +1.38, SCARB2 +1.06, CLN3 +1.17, RAB7A +2.65; hydrolases GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, DPP7 +4.52, CTSD +2.86, HEXB +2.17 (exceptions CTSS -5.57, IDS -1.56). Degradative flux and acidification were not measured.", "STEP 3 (inferred routing): Sterol reaching this compartment is preferentially routed to storage, non-ER transfer and oxidation rather than to the ER sensor - SOAT1 (+1.25), DGAT1 (+1.72), SCP2 (+5.95), OSBPL3 (+1.25), OSBPL1A (+1.03), NPC2 (+1.17), with oxysterol-generating CH25H (+1.62), CYP27A1 (+1.49), HSD3B7 (+2.74) and an LXR-type lipidation/efflux arm ABCA7 (+2.14), APOE (+1.24), PLTP (+1.06), MYLIP (+1.28), SREBF1 (+4.67), SCD (+4.17). OSBPL8 (-1.90) is a contrary member of the transfer set.", "STEP 4 (key logical step): Because sterol is not delivered to / retained in the ER-accessible pool, SREBP-2 output remains engaged in the same cells: SREBF2 (+1.06), INSIG1 (+1.87), HMGCS1 (+1.08), ACAT2 (+2.04), LSS (+2.27), DHCR7 (+2.71), DHCR24 (+3.69), EBP (+1.34), LDLR (+1.50) - 9/9 represented members positive. Co-elevation of synthesis with esterification and oxysterol enzymes is the pattern expected from compartment-separated sterol, not from a sterol-replete ER.", "STEP 5 (downstream energetics, measured RNA): The acidification, hydrolase and lipogenic load co-occurs with an increase in oxidative machinery transcripts - 38/38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits positive (median +2.65; NDUFA5 +7.34, ATP5ME +5.20, UQCRC2 +4.02, COX7A2 +3.36, SDHB +1.65), mitochondrial import TOMM22 (+4.63), TIMM44 (+2.46), and TCA/carrier genes MDH1 (+8.72), OGDH (+8.56), MPC2 (+7.98), SLC25A1 (+4.47), SLC25A11 (+4.50), plus HADHA (+2.86), ACOX1 (+1.24). Respiration was not measured.", "STEP 6 (challenge-revealed, not an ongoing defect): mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are not coordinately raised (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; only MT-ND5 +1.93, MT-ND4L +1.95), so complex stoichiometry may cap the achievable increase. This predicts reduced spare respiratory and lipid-buffering reserve under a future lipid or immune challenge; it does not by itself establish a respiratory defect in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route sterol into an expanded endolysosomal/esterified pool, leaving the ER sterol sensor unsatisfied so uptake, de novo synthesis and oxysterol/lipidation arms run simultaneously"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2452057387143811, "cosine_similarity": 0.32601925094465517, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6306440129449838, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2452057387143811, "cosine_similarity": 0.32601925094465517, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6306440129449838, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.250639, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 67}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_044", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1 and every adjusted p-value is \u003c0.05) from one APOE4-vs-APOE3 mock comparison; absence of a gene (e.g. PKM, GAPDH, LDHA, ALDOA, PDHA1, CPT1A, CS, PPARGC1A, TFAM) means it was not in the supplied list, not that it is unchanged. Pathway claims are therefore made against the internal background of this list, not a whole transcriptome.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect sizes reach implausible magnitudes (up to +15.5), so only the sign and the rank/percentile of each effect are treated as interpretable; absolute fold changes are not.", "The whole RNA list is up-shifted (1705/2212 positive, median +1.46). Every enrichment statement here is made relative to that internal background, and the shift itself may reflect normalisation, composition or depth differences rather than global transcriptional activation.", "Nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly proportional to protein and complex content; no OXPHOS, TCA or hexokinase protein was measured in the 92 2D-gel spots, so this link is unverified here.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific metabolic enzyme in this hypothesis.", "Mitochondrially encoded transcript levels in droplet single-cell data are strongly influenced by ambient RNA, dissociation stress and normalisation; the mito-nuclear imbalance in Step 5 is treated as a hypothesis-generating observation only (n=6 MT genes).", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so the microglial transcript profile may reflect a non-cell-autonomous metabolic division of labour (astrocyte-derived lactate/lipid) rather than a cell-intrinsic APOE4 defect. Genotype-to-metabolism causality is not established by these data.", "Unverified background knowledge (not from the supplied files) used for interpretation: HK2/PFKP catalyse committed glycolytic steps; MPC2 imports pyruvate; MDH1/GOT1/SLC25A11 form the malate-aspartate shuttle; SLC16A1 imports lactate; DDIT3/EIF2AK3 mark the integrated stress response."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture) show a coherent transcriptional reconfiguration of carbon entry: the committed glucose-phosphorylating step is selectively down-regulated (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3, gene:PFKFB2 in the lowest ~10% of an otherwise strongly up-shifted DE list) while glucose/monocarboxylate transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC16A1), mitochondrial pyruvate import (gene:MPC2), PDH-activating and TCA machinery (gene:PDP1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1), the malate-aspartate/citrate carriers (gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A1) and every measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit (39/39 up) are raised, together with a lysosomal/lipid catabolic and lipogenic program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). We hypothesise that the hexokinase/PFK-P commitment step, not transporter capacity and not mitochondrial demand, is the primary bottleneck on glucose-derived carbon in APOE4, making the cells disproportionately dependent on imported monocarboxylate and lysosome/lipid-derived carbon to supply the TCA cycle. All statements are about measured transcript (and 2D-gel spot) abundance; flux, enzyme activity, respiration and substrate origin are inferred, not measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING TRACER TEST: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, uniformly 13C-labelled glucose should give a lower fractional enrichment of intracellular/secreted lactate and a lower m+2 fraction of citrate, glutamate and malate in APOE4, while total TCA-intermediate pool sizes are maintained or increased; in parallel 13C-lactate, 13C-palmitate or 13C-labelled myelin/lipid substrate should contribute a larger fraction of TCA carbon in APOE4. If glucose-derived m+2 labelling of citrate and glucose-derived lactate output are equal to or greater in APOE4, the hexokinase-commitment bottleneck is falsified.", "PHARMACOLOGICAL DEPENDENCY TEST: APOE4 ATP production and extracellular acidification should be less sensitive to 2-deoxyglucose than APOE3 (smaller fractional drop), but more sensitive to MCT1 blockade (AR-C155858), lysosomal acid lipase inhibition (lalistat) or CPT1 inhibition (etomoxir at fatty-acid-selective dose). Equal or greater 2-DG sensitivity in APOE4, or no differential sensitivity to MCT1/lysosomal lipolysis blockade, weakens the mechanism.", "RESCUE TEST: restoring hexokinase-2 (doxycycline-inducible HK2, or HK2-fusion targeted to the outer mitochondrial membrane) in APOE4 microglia should raise glucose-derived lactate output and partially normalise the lysosomal/lipid-catabolic and nuclear-OXPHOS transcript module toward APOE3; unchanged glucose flux or unchanged module after HK2 restoration would indicate HK2 is a marker rather than the bottleneck.", "CAPACITY-VS-SIGNAL TEST (separates measured transcripts from inferred activity): if the nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise reflects real capacity, BN-PAGE/immunoassay should show higher assembled complex I and IV and higher FCCP-uncoupled maximal respiration in APOE4; if instead it is compensatory mito-nuclear imbalance, assembled complexes and maximal respiration will be unchanged or lower despite the transcript rise, and ISR reporters (ATF4/CHOP) and GDF15 secretion will be elevated. Elevated transcripts together with elevated assembled complexes AND unchanged ISR markers would falsify Step 5.", "SPECIFICITY TEST: the effect should track APOE genotype dose and be reversible - APOE4-to-APOE3 gene correction (or APOE knockout in both backgrounds) should abolish the HK2/PFKP down-shift; persistence of low HK2/PFKP after correction would indicate a clone- or culture-specific artefact rather than an APOE4-driven mechanism.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL FOR THE GLOBAL SHIFT: because 77% of supplied RNA rows are positive, the OXPHOS/TCA module must remain enriched after quantile- or spike-in-based renormalisation and against a size-matched random gene background; loss of enrichment after renormalisation would attribute the oxidative signature to a technical global shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 cells lower transcripts for the committed, high-Km/inducible glucose-phosphorylating and phosphofructokinase steps (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) while raising hexose and monocarboxylate transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC16A1). Inferred: glucose uptake capacity is preserved or increased but its phosphorylation/commitment to glycolysis is restricted, so glucose-6-phosphate and glycolytic pyruvate production per cell fall.", "Step 2 (inferred flux consequence): with glucose commitment restricted, cytosolic pyruvate is increasingly supplied by imported lactate/pyruvate (gene:SLC16A1 up; astrocytes are present in the co-culture) and by carbon released from lysosomal and lipid catabolism (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36 all up; gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1A up).", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred transport): raised mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating transcripts (gene:MPC2 +7.98, top 1%; gene:PDP1; gene:DLD) plus malate-aspartate shuttle and citrate-carrier transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A1) are consistent with, but do not demonstrate, increased routing of pyruvate and cytosolic reducing equivalents into the matrix rather than to lactate.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): the TCA cycle and the nuclear-encoded electron transport chain are transcriptionally amplified as a set (gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB, gene:MDH1; 39/39 measured NDUF/COX/ATP5/UQCR/SDH/ETF genes positive, mean +2.83 vs +1.39 background, Mann-Whitney p=5.9e-5). Inferred: increased oxidative demand/capacity signalling, not necessarily increased respiration.", "Step 5 (counter-balancing, inferred limitation): the mitochondrially encoded subunits measured are mostly negative (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; only gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 positive) and integrated-stress/mitochondrial-chaperone transcripts are up (gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:HSPA9, gene:SHMT2, gene:FIS1). Inferred: the nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise may be a compensatory mito-nuclear imbalance response, so assembled complex content and maximal respiration need not scale with the transcript increase.", "Step 6 (phenotypic consequence, inferred): the combination of a restricted glycolytic commitment step and an oxidative program that is potentially assembly-limited predicts reduced metabolic flexibility in APOE4 microglia - i.e. impaired ability to mount a fast glycolytic burst and greater dependence on extracellular monocarboxylate and lysosome/lipid-derived carbon for ATP, alongside the lipogenic/lipid-storage shift (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift carbon entry away from hexokinase-committed glycolysis toward imported/lysosome-derived substrates feeding an up-regulated mitochondrial oxidative program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1451925562160765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1908465480120015, "cosine_similarity": 0.32571334222643783, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6095307443365696, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1451925562160765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1908465480120015, "cosine_similarity": 0.32571334222643783, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6095307443365696, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6753465, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 276}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_021", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level statistics are conditional on this selection and cannot be read as genome-wide enrichment.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified, so only sign and relative rank are interpreted, never fold-change magnitude.", "A strong global positive shift is present (77% of rows positive, mean +1.39), plausibly technical/compositional; inference therefore rests on within-list relative ranks, not absolute direction of any single gene.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme/transporter abundance and, only as an explicit inference, pathway flux; no enzyme activity, metabolite, lipid, flux or localisation measurement is supplied.", "TFEB transcript elevation is not evidence of TFEB nuclear localisation or activity.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are not used as evidence for any specific enzyme.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects could partly reflect altered astrocyte-microglia cross-talk rather than microglia-autonomous wiring.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia by a coordinated transcriptional program that raises endolysosomal acidification/hydrolase capacity and mitochondrial anaplerotic TCA entry while simultaneously raising the cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate-to-lipid esterification module; we hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is at carbon disposal (citrate export via SLC25A1 plus ACSS2/ACAT2-derived acetyl-CoA feeding SREBF1-driven SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification), so degraded lipid cargo is re-esterified into neutral-lipid stores instead of being cleared, rather than a defect in degradation capacity itself. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with U-13C6-glucose and U-13C5-glutamine in mock conditions, APOE4 microglia should show both higher 13C enrichment in citrate/malate and disproportionately higher 13C incorporation into cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol pools than APOE3. Equal or lower 13C incorporation into neutral lipid in APOE4, despite the higher lipogenic transcripts, would weaken the mechanism.", "Node perturbation: inhibiting citrate export/consumption (SLC25A1 inhibitor CTPI-2 or SLC25A1 knockdown) or SOAT1 (avasimibe) should reduce LipidTOX/cholesteryl-ester content preferentially in APOE4 and shrink the APOE4-APOE3 gap, whereas inhibiting mitochondrial pyruvate entry (UK5099) should mainly lower TCA labelling with a smaller lipid effect. If SLC25A1 or SOAT1 blockade leaves the genotype difference in neutral lipid intact, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Capacity-versus-bottleneck test: measured lysosomal hydrolytic flux (DQ-BSA, BODIPY-LacCer, Magic Red cathepsin B) and oxygen consumption should be equal or higher in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows reduced hydrolytic flux and reduced OCR, the bottleneck lies in degradation, not disposal, and this hypothesis fails.", "Regulator test: SREBF1/SREBP1 processing and nuclear SREBP1 should be higher in APOE4; SREBF1 knockdown should normalise SCD, AGPAT2 and DGAT1 transcripts and neutral-lipid content in APOE4 without restoring the down-ranked actin/motility genes. Unchanged nuclear SREBP1, or loss of the lipid phenotype only when actin genes are also restored, would favour an alternative uptake-limited mechanism.", "Specificity control: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript arm; if it also abolishes the genotype difference in neutral lipid, the lysosomal arm, not the esterification node, is primary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA only): APOE4 cells show higher transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, ABCA7, TREM2, APOE) and for v-ATPase subunits and acid hydrolases (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSK, CTSD) together with TFEB; inferred (not measured): increased endolysosomal delivery, acidification and hydrolysis of lipid/glycolipid/glycogen cargo.", "Inferred flux step: catabolites leave the lysosome and enter mitochondria via elevated carrier and anaplerotic transcripts (SLC38A7, MPC2, SLC25A11, SLC25A13, GLS, GLUD1), supporting increased TCA turnover (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G, MDH1, GOT1, DLD) rather than glycolytic commitment, which is relatively lower (HK2, PFKP down despite SLC2A1/SLC2A3 up).", "Primary bottleneck (inferred): disposal of this carbon is anabolic, not catabolic. Elevated SLC25A1 (citrate export) and ACSS2/ACAT2 (cytosolic acetyl-CoA) transcripts, with SREBF1 and its lipogenic targets SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1, DHCR24, would channel acetyl-CoA/citrate into fatty-acyl, glycerolipid and sterol-ester synthesis.", "Predicted consequence (unmeasured pool): net accumulation of cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol in lipid droplets in APOE4 microglia, i.e. a degrade-then-re-store cycle with low net efflux; no lipid, flux, or localisation measurement is supplied here.", "Parallel, relatively suppressed arm: actin/Rho-effector and myeloid motility transcripts are far below the list-wide centre (ACTB, MYH9, FAM49B, RAC2, MYO1F, ARHGAP30, DOCK8, SPN, CSF1 down) while the Rho-GTPase sequestering factor ARHGDIA is among the highest; inferred reduced actin-dependent internalisation and migration would keep stored lipid from being turned over or handed off.", "Net inferred state: APOE4 microglia sit in a lipid-loading, oxidatively fuelled, storage-biased configuration; the discriminating node is the citrate/acetyl-CoA-to-ester step, not hydrolase abundance."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lysosome- and TCA-derived carbon into SLC25A1/ACSS2-fed SREBF1 esterification, making anabolic lipid re-storage, not degradation, the rate-limiting disposal step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.35381973931986854, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3284361451810559, "cosine_similarity": 0.32423092355908817, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6280906148867315, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.35381973931986854, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.3284361451810559, "cosine_similarity": 0.32423092355908817, "direction_accuracy": 0.22653721682847897, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6280906148867315, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88790025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 277}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_055", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so enrichment was judged only against that list as background; the nuclear-mitochondrial set is assumed not to be preferentially retained by the selection filter.", "The reported RNA effect units are a log fold change of unspecified base; only sign, rank and relative magnitude are used, never an absolute fold change.", "The six MT- rows are assumed to be representative of mtDNA-encoded transcript behaviour, although mtDNA-encoded genes absent from the list may be unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a lower bound proxy for the corresponding protein pool; no mitochondrial protein, assembly, membrane-potential, respiration, mtDNA copy-number or lipid measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are keratin/actin dominated, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein; the mitochondrial-candidate spots are used only as absence of confirmation.", "The APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated, so genotype rather than clone-specific background or differing cell-state composition drives the contrast.", "Activity, flux, localization and causal direction throughout are inferred; the data are a single-timepoint association at day 30."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia run a strongly upregulated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (OXPHOS structural subunits, TCA enzymes, carriers, import and mitochondrial translation factors) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts, which are mostly lower; the resulting shortage of mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores is proposed as the rate-limiting step for assembly of respiratory complexes, so the nuclear program cannot be converted into proportional oxidative flux and instead coincides with integrated-stress-response and lysosomal/sterol-handling transcripts. Causality is not established by these data; the ER unfolded-protein/secretory arm assigned as focus is not supported and is rejected.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partially blocking mitochondrial translation in APOE3 microglia (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol, or IMT1 inhibition of POLRMT) should phenocopy APOE4 - raising nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts, DDIT3/CEBPG and the TFEB-lysosomal and SREBP-sterol programs while lowering MT- transcripts. If APOE3 acquires the mtDNA-transcript deficit but none of the nuclear OXPHOS, ISR, lysosomal or sterol arms, the proposed chain is wrong.", "Direct test of the bottleneck: BN-PAGE/complexome or complex I and IV in-gel activity plus Seahorse should show APOE4 with equal or lower assembled complex I/IV holoenzyme and lower maximal and spare respiratory capacity despite higher NDUF/ATP5/UQCR transcripts, and a lower mtDNA:nuclear DNA ratio or lower MT-transcript-to-nuclear-OXPHOS-transcript ratio. Finding APOE4 with proportionally higher assembled complexes and higher spare respiratory capacity falsifies the bottleneck.", "Directionality test: ISRIB or HRI/GCN2 inhibition should suppress DDIT3, CEBPG, PSPH and SHMT2 in APOE4 without restoring the mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded transcript ratio or assembled complex levels. If ISRIB also normalises the nuclear OXPHOS overshoot and the mito-nuclear ratio, the ISR is upstream and the mechanism is weakened.", "Rescue test: restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression, nucleoside/NAD+ precursor supplementation, or mitochondrially targeted allotopic ATP6/ND4 expression) should normalise ISR transcripts and reduce the sterol and lysosomal programs in APOE4 with no change in APOE genotype. Persistence of the sterol/lysosomal program after full respiratory rescue would show those arms are parallel APOE4 effects rather than downstream consequences.", "Rejection test for the assigned focus: thapsigargin or tunicamycin dose-response should reveal no lower ER-stress threshold in APOE4, and XBP1 splicing, ATF6 cleavage and BiP protein should be indistinguishable between genotypes under mock. Detection of constitutive XBP1 splicing or ATF6 processing in mock APOE4 would reinstate the ER-proteostasis mechanism and weaken this one.", "Bias control: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome re-analysis without the differential-expression filter and with size-factor normalisation, the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial set should remain elevated relative to all expressed genes. If the enrichment disappears once the global upward shift is normalised, the mechanism is an artefact of list selection."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinate elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - complex I/III/IV/V structural subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3), TCA/shuttle enzymes (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:GOT1), metabolite carriers (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5), import components (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44) and the mitochondrial translation elongation factor gene:TUFM. Inferred, not measured: a transcriptionally driven attempt at increased mitochondrial biogenesis.", "Measured: mtDNA-encoded transcripts in the same list are predominantly lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2; only gene:MT-ND5 and gene:MT-ND4L higher). Inferred: the supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits does not scale with the nuclear program (mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial translation rate and subunit protein pools were not measured).", "Inferred bottleneck: assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V is limited by mtDNA-encoded cores, so imported nuclear-encoded subunits accumulate as unassembled intermediates and respiratory chain holoenzyme formation, not transcript supply, sets oxidative flux.", "Inferred consequence: orphan-subunit load and matrix proteostatic strain engage an eIF2alpha/ATF4-type integrated stress response; consistent measured transcripts are gene:DDIT3, gene:CEBPG, gene:NUPR1, gene:EIF2AK3 and the serine/one-carbon genes gene:PSPH and gene:SHMT2 (kinase activity, eIF2alpha phosphorylation and ATF4 protein were not measured).", "Inferred metabolic rerouting: with oxidative ATP/NAD+ regeneration capacity constrained, cytosolic redox shuttling and anabolic lipid handling are favoured; measured correlates are a uniformly raised sterol/lipogenic program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:SCD, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1) together with gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7 and gene:SCARB1.", "Inferred compensation: gene:TFEB with lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1) indicates increased lysosomal biogenesis to catabolise the added lipid/organelle load; lysosomal proteolytic and lipolytic flux were not measured.", "Rejected alternative within the same data: the ER unfolded-protein/secretory arm is incoherent - inducers and effectors move in opposite directions (gene:ATF6, gene:MANF, gene:DNAJB11, gene:UBE2J1 up but gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1, gene:PDIA3 down) and neither the UPR nor the COPI/COPII/ER-translocon set is enriched above the differential-expression background."], "title": "Mito-nuclear subunit imbalance, not ER unfolded-protein stress, is the bottleneck distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13558320717793448, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1592427460301187, "cosine_similarity": 0.32375211382040975, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6084724919093851, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13558320717793448, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1592427460301187, "cosine_similarity": 0.32375211382040975, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6084724919093851, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.664962, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 278}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_075", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of HSPA5, HSP90B1, XBP1, ERN1, ATF4, HERPUD1 and SYVN1 from the list is treated as 'not reported as differential', not as 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given; directions and relative ranks, not absolute magnitudes, carry the argument.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the capacity of a machinery step; enzymatic activity, retrotranslocation flux, client folding state, ER residence time, XBP1 splicing, eIF2alpha phosphorylation and ATF6 proteolytic cleavage were not measured.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with several candidate genes each; no spot uniquely identifies BiP, GRP94 or PDIA3, and spot-train shifts can reflect post-translational modification or processing rather than total abundance, so the unchanged chaperone-candidate spots are suggestive counter-evidence, not proof that BiP/GRP94 protein is constant.", "The dataset shows a strong global upward RNA shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46), so all pathway statements are made relative to that background rather than to zero; a normalisation or composition artefact affecting the shift cannot be excluded.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes and biological replicate number is not supplied; some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous or batch/replicate effects rather than the APOE4 allele.", "APOE4 protein misfolding propensity and the pro-degradative roles of SEL1L/DERL1/EDEM1/NGLY1 are background knowledge and are unverified here (literature retrieval was disabled)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an imbalance inside the ER glycoprotein folding cycle: transcripts encoding the entry/retention arm (OST subunits, malectin, UGGT1 re-glucosylation) are coordinately high while transcripts encoding the terminal disposal arm (EDEM1 mannose trimming, SEL1L/DERL1 retrotranslocation, NGLY1 cytosolic deglycosylation) are low, and no expansion of the classical BiP/GRP94 chaperone pool is detectable at the protein level. We propose that the rate-limiting bottleneck is SEL1L-DERL1-dependent dislocation of terminally misfolded glycoproteins, so clients (plausibly including APOE4 itself) are held in futile calnexin/malectin re-glucosylation cycles; the cell compensates through ATF6/PERK-arm transcriptional output and through lysosomal/reticulophagic routing rather than through increased chaperone capacity, and anterograde secretory throughput is biased downward. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring the bottleneck step by overexpressing SEL1L (or SEL1L plus SYVN1/HRD1) in APOE4 microglia should shorten the ER residence of misfolded glycoprotein clients, increase the endoglycosidase-H-resistant and secreted fraction of APOE in pulse-chase, and lower ATF6 and DDIT3 transcripts toward APOE3 levels, without requiring any change in APOE transcription. If SEL1L/HRD1 restoration leaves APOE secretion kinetics and ATF6/DDIT3 unchanged, the proposed dislocation bottleneck is wrong.", "Metabolic pulse-chase of APOE in isogenic pairs should show slower ER exit and a larger EndoH-sensitive intracellular pool in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions; comparable secretion kinetics and glycan maturation between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Because entry is already saturated and disposal already limited, kifunensine (ER mannosidase/EDEM inhibition) should produce a smaller incremental increase in intracellular misfolded-client accumulation in APOE4 than in APOE3, whereas UGGT1 knockdown should preferentially relieve client retention and reduce ATF6/DDIT3 in APOE4; equal kifunensine sensitivity in both genotypes, or no UGGT1-knockdown genotype interaction, would weaken the retention-cycle claim.", "The response should remain chaperone-sparing: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS should show no significant APOE4-versus-APOE3 increase in BiP/HSPA5 and GRP94/HSP90B1 protein and little XBP1 splicing, while ATF6 cleavage and CHOP/DDIT3 protein rise. Detection of a coordinated BiP/GRP94/PDI protein increase with strong XBP1 splicing would falsify the specific 'entry-disposal imbalance without chaperone expansion' formulation and favour a generic proteotoxic-load UPR instead.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: pharmacological SREBP blockade (for example fatostatin) or cholesterol depletion should normalise the lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) but should not normalise the entry-versus-disposal transcript imbalance or ATF6/DDIT3 if the ERAD bottleneck is primary; if lipid-pathway blockade abolishes the ER signature, a lipid-bilayer-stress mechanism is the better explanation.", "Proteasome-versus-lysosome partitioning: in APOE4 microglia, bafilomycin A1 or cathepsin inhibition should cause a larger accumulation of undegraded ER-derived glycoprotein clients than epoxomicin does, reversing the ratio seen in APOE3; if proteasome inhibition dominates equally in both genotypes, the proposed shift of disposal to the lysosome is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for N-glycosylation and glycoprotein-retention machinery are coordinately elevated in APOE4 (MLEC +10.21, DDOST +6.22, STT3A +3.39, UGGT1 +2.58, STT3B +1.40, RPN1 +1.06; set median +2.99 vs dataset median +1.46, permutation p=0.055). Inferred, not measured: higher flux of nascent glycoproteins into, and prolonged residence within, the calnexin/malectin re-glucosylation cycle.", "Measured: transcripts for the terminal ERAD arm are among the minority of down-shifted genes (SEL1L -2.09, NGLY1 -2.20, EDEM1 -1.37, DERL1 -1.19; 4 of 7 present ERAD-list genes negative where 23% of all rows are negative, binomial p=0.053). Inferred: reduced capacity for mannose-trimming commitment and for SEL1L-DERL1 retrotranslocation, i.e. a disposal step that cannot keep pace with entry. This step is the proposed primary bottleneck.", "Inferred consequence (not directly measured): misfolded glycoprotein clients accumulate in the ER lumen in retention cycles rather than being dislocated to the cytosol; APOE itself is transcriptionally higher in APOE4 (APOE +1.24), so the secreted APOE4 glycoprotein is a candidate jamming client, but its ER residence time and folding state were not measured here.", "Measured: UPR sensor and effector transcripts are up (ATF6 +4.04, DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2AK3 +1.51) together with selected lumenal folding/redox factors (DNAJC10 +4.73, MANF +2.95, DNAJB11 +2.22, CRELD2 +1.01, SERP1 +2.20), while HSPA5, HSP90B1, PDIA4/6, P4HB, HERPUD1 and XBP1 are absent from the differential list and the protein spots whose candidate lists contain HSPA5, HSP90B1 or PDIA3 are unchanged and non-significant (protein_spot:005 -0.138; protein_spot:001 -0.485; protein_spot:004 -0.678; protein_spot:016 +0.138). Inferred: a signalling-level, ATF6/PERK-biased response without a proportional expansion of the bulk ER chaperone pool, which distinguishes a retention/disposal imbalance from a classical proteotoxic-load UPR.", "Measured: anterograde export components are down (GOSR1 -3.19, SEC62 -1.50, SEC24D -1.39) while retrograde/Golgi components are up (COPA +4.27, GOLPH3 +3.68, RAB1B +1.67, COPB1 +1.04). Inferred: a retention-biased ER-to-Golgi balance and reduced secretory throughput per unit cargo; no secretion rate was measured.", "Measured: an alternative degradative route is transcriptionally raised (TFEB +2.38, RAB7A +2.65, ARL6IP1 +3.16, GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, CTSK +7.36, HEXA +5.68, CTSB +5.52, LAMP1 +1.38). Inferred: ER-phagy/lysosomal disposal partially substitutes for the limited SEL1L-DERL1 route, shifting the degradative load from proteasome-coupled ERAD to lysosomal hydrolysis and predisposing APOE4 microglia to lysosomal cargo accumulation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand ER glycoprotein quality-control entry while the SEL1L-DERL1 dislocation step lags, creating an ERAD disposal bottleneck resolved by lysosomal rather than chaperone-based compensation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11681682236089058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21479985000511972, "cosine_similarity": 0.32217384561577816, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6124045307443365, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11681682236089058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21479985000511972, "cosine_similarity": 0.32217384561577816, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6124045307443365, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72550975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 279}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_086", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 entries have |effect| \u003e 1); absence of a gene such as ABCA1, ABCG1 or MX1 means it did not pass selection, not that it was measured and unchanged. The efflux and interferon arguments therefore rest on absence of evidence within a biased list.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only sign, rank and within-list comparisons are used, and no fold-change magnitude is converted.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity, not for flux: uptake flux, esterification rate, lysosomal degradative flux, TFEB nuclear localization and NF-kB activity are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (keratins and actins dominate the candidate lists), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spots are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration of cathepsin/cytoskeletal remodeling.", "The list-wide upward skew (77.1% of entries positive, median +1.46) is assumed to reflect a real asymmetry plus possible normalization or ambient-RNA/composition effects in the 10X Flex microglia-astrocyte co-culture; set-level statements are made relative to this +1.39 list background rather than to zero.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed and the two modalities are assumed to come from comparable APOE4 versus APOE3 isogenic mock samples.", "No lipid, lipidomic, flow-cytometry or imaging measurement is supplied; the central lipid-accumulation pool is an unmeasured inference."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally expand lipoprotein/lipid uptake and sterol-esterification capacity without a matched induction of cholesterol-efflux machinery; the rate-limiting step is disposal of internalized sterol and sphingolipid from the endolysosome, and the resulting inferred substrate load is mirrored by a coordinated TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal-hydrolase program and by NF-kB/inflammasome priming transcripts, while canonical type-I interferon-stimulated genes are absent from the differential list, arguing against interferon signaling as the differentiating mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, blocking sterol esterification with an ACAT/SOAT1 inhibitor (e.g. avasimibe) or restoring efflux with an LXR agonist plus ApoA-I acceptor should lower cholesteryl-ester and neutral-lipid content and reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of the CLEAR hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, GAA) and of CXCL8, CCL2 and NLRP3, without changing type-I ISG levels. If lipid stores fall but the hydrolase and chemokine differences persist, the proposed bottleneck ordering is wrong.", "Removing the lipid supply (lipoprotein-depleted medium) or blocking uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or SCARB1 knockdown) should collapse most of the APOE4-APOE3 difference in the lysosomal and chemokine modules; persistence of the difference under lipid-free conditions would indicate a cell-intrinsic transcriptional difference upstream of lipid handling and would weaken the mechanism.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should abolish the hydrolase/v-ATPase induction and, because that program is proposed to be compensatory, should worsen lipid accumulation and further increase CXCL8/IL18 transcripts; if TFEB knockdown instead eliminates the chemokine difference, the CLEAR program is upstream rather than compensatory and this hypothesis is falsified.", "Interferon-arm control: IFNAR1 blockade or JAK1/2 inhibition should not reduce the APOE4-APOE3 differences in lysosomal or chemokine transcripts, and a directly measured ISG panel (MX1, ISG15, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1) should show no APOE4 elevation. Detection of a coherent ISG elevation, or loss of the phenotype under IFNAR blockade, would overturn the IFN-independent claim.", "Direct test of the unmeasured pool: filipin/BODIPY and LysoTracker imaging plus lipidomics should show higher cholesteryl-ester, sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide and lysosomal volume in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Equal or lower lipid load in APOE4, despite the transcript pattern, would falsify the bottleneck.", "Functional prediction with a built-in counter-test: pulse-chase of fluorescent LDL or myelin debris should show equal or faster internalization but slower cargo clearance (delayed degradation) in APOE4; equal clearance kinetics would mean disposal is not rate-limiting and would weaken step 3. Independently, CTSS is strongly reduced (-5.57) while CTSB and CTSD are increased, so cathepsin-S-dependent proteolysis should be selectively impaired even though bulk hydrolase transcripts rise."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein and lipid uptake receptors (SCARB1 +8.22, LDLR +1.50, CD36 +1.38, TREM2 +1.28, APOE +1.24) in the reported log scale; we infer, but did not measure, increased flux of lipid cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred partitioning): sterol-esterification, neutral-lipid storage and sterol/fatty-acid synthesis transcripts are coordinately higher (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, SCD +4.17, SREBF1 +4.67, SREBF2 +1.06, DHCR24 +3.69, DHCR7 +2.71, LSS +2.27, ACAT2 +2.04, INSIG1 +1.87), which we interpret as a shift of internalized sterol toward esterified/stored pools rather than export. No cholesterol-efflux transporter (ABCA1, ABCG1) or LXR (NR1H3) transcript appears in the supplied differential list, so an efflux arm matched to uptake is not evidenced.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): hydrolysis and egress of internalized cholesteryl ester and sphingolipid from the late endosome/lysosome becomes rate-limiting relative to uptake, so lipid substrate accumulates intracellularly. This pool is inferred; no lipid, lipid-droplet or lysosomal-content measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, compensatory response): a CLEAR-type lysosomal program is elevated (GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, GAA +9.97, GLA +1.53, SGSH +1.32, NPC2 +1.17, SCARB2 +1.06, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86) together with v-ATPase and trafficking/biogenesis transcripts (ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6AP1 +2.30, ATP6V0D2 +1.12, LAMP1 +1.38, RAB7A +2.65, TFEB +2.38, MITF +1.03); mean effect of the hydrolase set is +3.97 versus a +1.39 list background (empirical p = 0.0007). We read this as substrate-driven compensation, not as demonstrated increased lysosomal degradative flux.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, downstream priming): lipid-laden endolysosomes license NF-kB-dependent priming rather than interferon signaling: pattern-recognition and adaptor transcripts (TLR2 +1.20, TLR6 +3.75, CD14 +1.41, MYD88 +2.34, TICAM1 +2.09), chemokines (CXCL8 +3.11, CXCL16 +3.66, CCL2 +2.12, CXCL1 +1.59, CXCL2 +1.65, CXCL3 +1.56) and inflammasome components (NLRP3 +1.09, NLRP1 +3.55, PYCARD +2.43, CASP4 +1.24, IL18 +1.46) are higher, while the NF-kB brake TNFAIP3 is lower (-1.05). Cytokine secretion, caspase-1 activity and NF-kB nuclear localization were not measured.", "Step 6 (mechanism boundary): the interferon arm is not engaged. 17 of 21 canonical type-I ISGs queried (ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1/2, OAS1-3, RSAD2, STAT1/2, IRF7, IRF9, BST2, XAF1, USP18) are absent from the differential list, so the APOE4 state is proposed to be a lipid-storage/lysosomal-load state with IFN-independent inflammatory priming."], "title": "Endolysosomal lipid-disposal bottleneck, not interferon signaling, drives an IFN-independent primed state in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09037526931411795, "cosine_similarity": 0.32197708873488673, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6421488673139158, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11545988258317025, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09037526931411795, "cosine_similarity": 0.32197708873488673, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6421488673139158, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.334469, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 280}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_186", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 reported log units); we therefore interpret only within-list relative rank, and assume that this shift is a shared normalisation/selection property rather than a pathway-specific signal. If the shift is a technical artefact, all absolute directions become unreliable.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and preserved as reported; no fold-change conversion is assumed. Some magnitudes (up to +15.5) are implausibly large for base-2 biology, so ranks are treated as more reliable than magnitudes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme protein abundance and, more weakly, for hydrolytic activity per lysosome; activity, lysosomal pH and localisation were not measured.", "TFEB/MITF transcript elevation is assumed to accompany, but does not demonstrate, increased nuclear TFEB activity; the CLEAR-like coherence of downstream targets is the main indirect support.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:067 down) are treated as ambiguous and non-decisive.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may originate from altered microglia-astrocyte cross-talk rather than microglia-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "Absence of a gene from the supplied rows (e.g., NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, most canonical interferon-stimulated genes) is uninformative about that gene's true behaviour because the list is preselected.", "No causal direction is established by these data; the mechanism is a hypothesis about direction of flux, not a demonstrated cause."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in endolysosomal lipid handling: transcripts for luminal acid hydrolases that degrade sphingolipid, glycolipid, glycogen and protein cargo (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSK, CTSD) and for v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6AP1) are coordinately elevated above the strong global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list, together with TFEB and MITF, while a sterol/fatty-acid biosynthetic program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, ACSS2, INSIG1, LDLR) remains simultaneously high. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is degradation and onward export of lipid cargo from the APOE4 endolysosome: cargo lipid is retained in the acidic compartment, ER sterol/fatty-acid sensing is therefore not satisfied, and the cell holds both a compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis program and a lipogenic program on at the same time, a combination that is normally mutually exclusive in lipid-replete cells. Interferon and NF-kB programs are not the differentiator in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving lysosomal lipid load in APOE4 microglia (e.g. 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or substrate-reduction with a UGCG inhibitor) should selectively collapse the lipogenic arm toward APOE3 levels (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, SCARB1 transcripts, and nuclear SREBP-1/2 by immunoblot) while also reducing the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript excess (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1A). If lipid mobilisation leaves SREBF1/SCD unchanged, the 'unsatisfied ER sterol sensing' step is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "TFEB knockdown or dominant-negative TFEB in APOE4 microglia should abolish the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript excess and worsen, not improve, lysosomal neutral-lipid and cholesterol accumulation (LipidSpot/filipin, LysoTracker). If TFEB loss reduces lipid accumulation, the lysosomal program is a driver rather than a compensation and this mechanism is falsified.", "Direct measurement should show, in APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock conditions, higher lysosomal cholesterol and glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin content and larger LAMP1-positive compartment volume per cell, with hydrolase activity per unit lysosomal volume equal to or lower than APOE3 despite higher transcript levels. Equal or lower lysosomal lipid content in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Interferon test (rejects the assigned focus): JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade under mock conditions should not normalise the APOE4 hydrolase/lipogenic signature, and canonical ISG protein readouts (MX1, ISG15, STAT1 phosphorylation) should not differ between genotypes. Detectable APOE4-specific ISG induction that is abolished by JAK inhibition, together with loss of the lysosomal signature, would falsify this hypothesis in favour of an interferon mechanism.", "Rescue specificity: acute lipid loading of APOE3 microglia (myelin debris or oxLDL) should phenocopy the APOE4 hydrolase+SREBP-1 co-elevation; if APOE3 responds by suppressing SREBF1/SCD while inducing hydrolases, the simultaneous co-elevation is APOE4-specific as claimed, whereas identical co-elevation in both genotypes would show the signature is a generic loading response and not the APOE4 differentiator.", "Flux prediction: pulse-chase of fluorescent BODIPY-cholesterol or NBD-sphingomyelin delivered on APOE particles should show slower lysosome-to-ER transfer (delayed ACAT-dependent esterification) in APOE4; equal transfer kinetics would weaken the proposed rate-limiting step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_186", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred protein/particle behaviour): APOE transcript is modestly higher in APOE4 (gene:APOE, +1.24 reported log units, 38th percentile of this list); we assume, unverified here, that APOE4 protein forms poorly lipidated, aggregation-prone lipoprotein particles whose lipid cargo is harder to release after endocytosis. Particle composition and lipid content were not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): Cargo lipid reaching the late endosome/lysosome (gene:RAB7A elevated, +2.65) requires luminal hydrolysis and export to the ER. We posit that this luminal degradation/egress step, not uptake, is rate-limiting in APOE4. Lysosomal lipid content, hydrolase enzymatic activity and lysosomal pH were not measured in this dataset.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, compensatory response): A coherent CLEAR-network-like transcriptional response is elevated well above the list-wide background: acid hydrolases gene:GAA (+9.96, 99.7th pct), gene:CTSK (+7.36), gene:GBA (+6.71), gene:NAGLU (+5.91), gene:HEXA (+5.68), gene:SMPD1 (+5.63), gene:CTSB (+5.52), gene:CTSD (+2.86); v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H (+6.88), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.23), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.51), gene:ATP6AP1 (+2.30); and the transcription factors gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03). The combined hydrolase + v-ATPase set has median +1.81 versus background median +1.45 (Mann-Whitney one-sided p = 0.005; 8/31 members in the top decile, hypergeometric p = 0.009). TFEB nuclear localisation and activity were not measured; only transcript abundance was.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing state): Despite this degradative expansion, the ER sterol/lipogenic arm reads as unsatisfied: gene:SREBF1 (+4.67, 92nd pct), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:ACSS2 (+2.93), gene:DHCR7 (+2.71), gene:LSS (+2.27), gene:ACAT2 (+2.04), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87), gene:LDLR (+1.50), plus the selective lipid-uptake receptor gene:SCARB1 (+8.22, 99th pct). SREBP cleavage, nuclear SREBP protein and ER free-cholesterol were not measured; the inference of unsatisfied sterol sensing rests on transcript output only.", "Step 5 (inferred futile cycle): Continued synthesis and receptor-mediated uptake feed further lipid into a compartment whose clearance is limiting, with esterification/storage routes available (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) and efflux only partially represented (gene:ABCA7 +2.14; ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied rows). The predicted consequence is expanded, lipid-laden acidic compartments and neutral-lipid stores in APOE4, none of which were measured here.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, functional consequence): The homeostatic/trophic microglial axis is depressed in the same cells (gene:CSF1 -5.91, 0.5th pct; gene:CTSS -5.57, 0.7th pct; gene:TGFBR1 -2.19, 10th pct), consistent with a lipid-handling-stressed state rather than an interferon- or NF-kB-driven activation state (gene:IFNAR1 +1.41, gene:IRF8 +1.39, gene:TMEM173 +1.22 all at list background; gene:GSDMD -3.18)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase expansion alongside an unsatisfied SREBP-1 lipogenic program, indicating a lysosomal lipid-clearance bottleneck rather than interferon or NF-kB activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1405494221467341, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09097187321823592, "cosine_similarity": 0.32162443661499757, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_186", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6276278317152104, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1405494221467341, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09097187321823592, "cosine_similarity": 0.32162443661499757, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6276278317152104, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9566325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 281}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_022", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook; all RNA effects are used only in their reported units and compared with the global median (+1.459) of the same rows, never converted to a fold change.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome (no ribosomal-protein or other housekeeping families are present), so enrichment statistics are conditional on that selection and are computed against the supplied rows as background.", "The strong global positive RNA shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.459) is at least partly technical/compositional; only effects clearly above or below that median are treated as pathway signal.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are treated as ambiguous evidence about specific gene products and 2D spots may separate proteoforms of the same protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for degradative capacity; no lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, lipid, sterol, oxygen-consumption or flux measurement is supplied, so all flux, localization and capacity statements are inferences.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultures, so some genotype-associated RNA differences could reflect altered astrocyte-derived cargo or signalling rather than a microglia-intrinsic programme.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied and several effect magnitudes are implausibly large for an isogenic comparison (e.g. gene:CSF1 at -5.91), so individual gene effects are treated as unreliable and only multi-gene coherence is used.", "Causality is not established by this cross-sectional genotype comparison; direction of the proposed chain is hypothesis, not observation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal degradative machinery (acid hydrolases plus v-ATPase subunits, with TFEB RNA elevated) together with elevated endolysosomal trafficking and mitochondrial TCA/anaplerotic/ETC transcripts, consistent with a state in which lysosomal hydrolytic throughput on internalized lipid-rich cargo is the limiting step and is compensated transcriptionally, while homeostatic microglial transcripts (CSF1, CTSS, TGFBR1) fall. Mevalonate-pathway and sterol-export programmes show no coherent enrichment above the strong global positive shift and are therefore not proposed as the bottleneck. All statements about degradative flux, lysosomal pH, lipid load, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: loading APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with a defined quenched/fluorogenic lipid-rich cargo (e.g. DQ-BSA-labelled myelin debris or labelled lipoprotein) should show slower per-lysosome substrate degradation and greater accumulation of undigested cargo in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 degrades cargo at the same or faster per-lysosome rate with matched lysosomal volume, the hydrolytic-throughput bottleneck is refuted and the signature would instead reflect a primary transcriptional (TFEB-activation) or lysosome-biogenesis difference with no capacity limit.", "TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown or inhibition should selectively collapse the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript excess in APOE4 (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H) and worsen cargo accumulation. If those transcripts remain elevated after TFEB loss, Step 3 as written is wrong.", "Upstream cargo dependence: blocking lipid-cargo uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or culture without lipoprotein/debris cargo) should shrink the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in both the lysosomal and the mitochondrial TCA/ETC transcript sets. Persistence of both signatures in cargo-free conditions would show the programme is cargo-independent and would weaken Steps 1-2 and 5.", "Lysosome-to-mitochondria coupling: acute inhibition of lysosomal acidification or of lysosomal lipase/hydrolase activity should abolish the genotype difference in mitochondrial oxygen consumption and in TCA-gene expression. If mitochondrial respiration in APOE4 stays elevated when lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked, the proposed catabolite-supply link in Step 5 fails and an independent mitochondrial mechanism should be preferred.", "Protein-level test of the transcript-protein mismatch: targeted immunoblot or activity assay of mature CTSB/CTSD, GBA, HEXA/B and v-ATPase V1 subunits should show that mature-enzyme protein and activity rise less than the corresponding transcripts in APOE4. Proportional increases in mature enzyme and activity would remove the compensation-failure element of Step 4.", "Sterol-focus negative control: sterol depletion/repletion should not produce a genotype-specific mevalonate-pathway transcriptional divergence, and ABCA1/ABCG1-dependent cholesterol efflux (not measured here) should not differ between genotypes in proportion to the lysosomal signature. A strong genotype-specific SREBP-2/efflux difference would support the rejected sterol mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE), which we infer, but did not measure, increases the rate of endocytic delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred localization): transcripts for late-endosome maturation and cargo delivery are coordinately raised (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:RAB28), consistent with more cargo reaching the lysosomal lumen rather than being recycled.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred capacity): luminal hydrolysis of this cargo exceeds baseline degradative capacity, and the cell responds with a CLEAR-type transcriptional programme: acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D1) rise well above the global RNA shift, with gene:TFEB itself elevated. Acidification and enzyme activity were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA + ambiguous protein spots): the transcriptional compensation is not matched by uniform protein-level increase; 2D spots containing cathepsin and v-ATPase candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:013, protein_spot:012, protein_spot:047 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), which we interpret as an inferred mismatch between transcriptional demand and delivered/mature hydrolase protein, i.e. the throughput limitation persists.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): catabolites released by lysosomal hydrolysis are inferred to feed mitochondria, whose transporter, anaplerotic and oxidative transcripts are the most strongly enriched set (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A46, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5MC3), a state we infer to be oxidative-catabolic rather than glycolytic.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred cell state): the resource commitment to degradation/oxidation accompanies loss of homeostatic microglial transcripts (gene:CSF1, gene:CTSS, gene:TGFBR1), giving a degradative, less homeostatic APOE4 microglial state under mock conditions."], "title": "Lysosomal hydrolytic throughput, not sterol synthesis or export, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: a CLEAR-type degradative expansion coupled to mitochondrial catabolic oxidation and loss of homeostatic identity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08537062474951713, "cosine_similarity": 0.3215888164324094, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6193624595469256, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08537062474951713, "cosine_similarity": 0.3215888164324094, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6193624595469256, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.838734, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 282}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so set-level enrichment was judged against the supplied list background, not against an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene means not supplied, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified and is left unconverted; only relative rankings and directions are used.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein abundance, and enzyme abundance to constrain (not equal) metabolic flux; no flux, metabolite, acetyl-CoA, citrate, NADPH, ROS or lipid pool was measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a specific lipogenic or TCA enzyme.", "The strong global positive skew of the supplied RNA list (about 77 percent up) is assumed not to be a pure normalization or composition artifact; if it is, apparent up-regulation of abundant metabolic genes would be inflated.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-driven astrocyte lipid supply could contribute to the same downstream lipid phenotype.", "Day-30 mock condition is assumed to reflect a steady state rather than a transient differentiation-stage difference between lines."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a transcriptional shift that favours mitochondrial pyruvate entry and TCA/malate-aspartate shuttle capacity while lowering committed glycolytic steps, together with elevated citrate-carrier and SREBP1 lipogenic/esterification transcripts. The proposed rate-limiting node (bottleneck) is mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1-dependent) supplying cytosolic acetyl-CoA for de novo monounsaturated fatty-acid, glycerolipid and neutral-lipid synthesis; the coordinated rise in mitochondrial thiol-peroxidase transcripts is interpreted as a compensatory response to greater matrix oxidative flux, not as evidence of a peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect or a canonical NRF2 antioxidant response. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, inhibiting mitochondrial pyruvate carrier (UK5099) or the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (CTPI-2) should reduce neutral-lipid/droplet content and U-13C6-glucose incorporation into palmitate and oleate toward APOE3 levels, whereas blocking lysosomal acid lipolysis or scavenger-receptor uptake should not abolish the APOE4 excess. If the reverse holds (uptake/lysosomal block removes the difference and MPC/SLC25A1 block does not), the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show higher m+2 citrate enrichment and higher glucose-derived labelling of de novo fatty acids in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower labelling in APOE4 would weaken Steps 1-4.", "Lipidomics should show APOE4-biased increases in MUFA-containing triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester and a lower saturated:monounsaturated ratio in phosphatidylcholine; SCD inhibition should shift this ratio more in APOE4 than APOE3. An APOE4 lipid excess dominated by sphingolipid or unmodified exogenous species instead would favour the lysosomal alternative.", "Oxygen-consumption measurement should show higher basal and maximal mitochondrial respiration and a lower extracellular-acidification:oxygen-consumption ratio in APOE4; unchanged respiration with preserved lipid phenotype would falsify the flux premise while leaving the lipogenic module intact.", "The redox change should be secondary: mitochondria-targeted roGFP/peroxide reporters should show higher matrix oxidation in APOE4 that is normalized by MPC or SLC25A1 inhibition, and NRF2 knockdown should not remove the PRDX3/GPX4 transcript difference. If canonical NRF2 targets (NQO1, HMOX1, GCLM, TXNRD1) are induced at protein level and NRF2 knockdown abolishes the difference, Step 6 is wrong and a primary oxidative-stress mechanism should be preferred.", "If peroxisomal beta-oxidation were the driver, ABCD3/ACOX1 protein and C26:0 very-long-chain fatty acid or plasmalogen levels would differ strongly between genotypes; finding such a difference without any TCA/citrate-export flux difference would replace this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA abundance): transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA/malate-aspartate shuttle enzymes are coordinately higher in APOE4 (MPC2, MDH1, GOT1, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G, SDHB, SLC25A11); inferred (not measured) consequence is increased capacity for pyruvate oxidation and cytosolic-to-mitochondrial reducing-equivalent transfer.", "Step 2 (measured RNA abundance, mixed): committed glycolytic steps HK2 and PFKP are lower while glucose transporters and downstream glycolytic transcripts are higher; inferred consequence is reduced glycolytic commitment of imported glucose carbon and preferential routing of pyruvate to mitochondria. Glycolytic flux itself is not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck, inferred flux): higher SLC25A1 (citrate carrier) and ACSS2 transcripts are proposed to raise citrate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply. The acetyl-CoA and citrate pools are unmeasured; ACLY was not present in the supplied data and is not claimed as observed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA abundance): the SREBP1-type lipogenic and esterification module is elevated (SREBF1, SCD, FADS1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, CHPT1, DGAT1, SOAT1, ACAT2), with NADPH-supply transcripts shifted from the oxidative pentose-phosphate route (PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NAMPT lower) toward mitochondrial/malic routes (NNT, ME1 higher); inferred consequence is increased de novo synthesis of monounsaturated fatty acids, phosphatidylcholine-type glycerophospholipids and neutral esters.", "Step 5 (inferred lipid phenotype, unmeasured here): the combined routing predicts accumulation of MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester in lipid droplets and altered membrane phospholipid saturation in APOE4 microglia; no lipid species were measured in the supplied data.", "Step 6 (secondary redox consequence): increased mitochondrial oxidative flux is proposed to raise matrix peroxide load, matching higher mitochondrial/thiol peroxidase transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, TXNDC17, GSS); this is offered as a consequence of Step 1, not as an independent peroxisomal or NRF2-driven stress program.", "Step 7 (parallel, not the bottleneck): a lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program is also elevated (TFEB, CTSB, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) alongside scavenger-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36); this provides an alternative lipid source that the discriminating predictions below are designed to separate from the de novo route."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route pyruvate through the TCA cycle and export citrate to feed an SREBP1 lipogenic program, with thiol-peroxidase induction as a downstream consequence rather than a peroxisomal/NRF2 stress program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.281255769301776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22645949563849996, "cosine_similarity": 0.32141169346046555, "direction_accuracy": 0.2750809061488673, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5926116504854368, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.281255769301776, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22645949563849996, "cosine_similarity": 0.32141169346046555, "direction_accuracy": 0.2750809061488673, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5926116504854368, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0238265, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 283}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_039", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong positive offset (median +1.46, 77% positive); all claims are therefore stated as rank/relative comparisons within this list, which are invariant to a uniform additive shift, and no absolute fold change is asserted.", "Transcript differences for RAC2, DOCK8, MYH9, MYO1F and ACTB are assumed to translate into lower protein and lower Rac-GTP/myosin-II activity at nascent phagocytic cups; neither protein levels of these specific gene products, GTP loading, F-actin content, nor cup morphology were measured here.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (median 5) and 39/92 spots list keratins, so no spot is treated as a unique protein identification; spot values are used only as ambiguous, non-decisive context.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. RAC1, CORO1A, WASF2, PLIN2, P2RY12) are unmeasured or unselected, not unchanged; the lipid, myelin, apoptotic-cell and bead-uptake pools themselves were never measured.", "Astrocyte co-culture and possible cell-composition or normalisation differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells could contribute to the global positive shift; the analysis assumes such effects are approximately uniform across genes.", "APOE4 versus APOE3 is assumed to be the only systematic genetic difference (stated isogenic comparison), and mock treatment is assumed to represent an unstimulated steady state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by loss of phagocytic receptor transcripts (which are relatively higher) nor by loss of degradative capacity transcripts (lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and TFEB are among the most strongly higher transcripts), but by a coordinated relative reduction of the small-GTPase/actomyosin executor module (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, MYH9, MYO1F, HCK, PIK3CB, TMSB10, ACTB) that drives F-actin-dependent phagocytic cup extension and closure; we hypothesise that this makes actin-dependent particle internalisation, rather than particle binding or lysosomal degradation, the primary bottleneck in APOE4 microglial cargo clearance, with the expanded endolysosomal/lipid-esterification program acting as a parallel or compensatory arm. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake-versus-degradation assay: in a pulse of pH-independent fluorescent, opsonised beads or labelled myelin with external-quench (trypan blue) separation of bound from internalised particles at 5, 15 and 30 min, APOE4 microglia should show a lower internalised:bound ratio than APOE3 with equal or higher total binding. If binding and the internalised:bound ratio are indistinguishable and only downstream cargo degradation (DQ-BSA or BODIPY-myelin decay per internalised particle) is slower, the internalisation bottleneck is wrong and a degradation/lysosomal-flux bottleneck is favoured instead.", "Executor rescue: acute expression of constitutively active Rac1/Rac2 (or DOCK8 restoration) in APOE4 microglia should raise the internalised:bound ratio and F-actin cup intensity toward APOE3 without normalising the TFEB/cathepsin transcript program. If Rac reactivation normalises the lysosomal transcript program instead of internalisation, the proposed ordering of steps is wrong.", "Phenocopy: myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) in APOE3 microglia should reduce the internalised:bound ratio to APOE4 levels; failure to phenocopy would weaken step 3.", "Protein-level check: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS in the same cultures should show lower RAC2, DOCK8 and MYH9 protein in APOE4 while total actin and cathepsin B/D protein need not fall; if RAC2, DOCK8 and MYH9 proteins are unchanged or higher, the mechanism is substantially weakened, since it rests on transcript-to-activity inference.", "Capacity test: increasing cargo load (excess opsonised substrate) should not close the APOE4-APOE3 clearance gap under this hypothesis, whereas lowering the actomyosin demand of uptake (small soluble cargo taken up by fluid-phase/clathrin routes, e.g. dextran or transferrin) should show little or no APOE4 deficit; a proportional APOE4 deficit in fluid-phase uptake as well would point to a general endocytic or membrane-lipid defect rather than the actomyosin cup module."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): Relative to APOE3, APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for opsonic/scavenger/adhesion receptors (SCARB1, ITGB1, ITGAX, CD36, MERTK, TREM2, C1QA) and for the microglial identity receptor CSF1R, so surface recognition capacity is unlikely to be transcriptionally limiting.", "Step 2 (measured, RNA; inferred activity): Within the same selected DE list, a pre-specified leukocyte actomyosin engulfment module is shifted downward relative to the list-wide distribution (module mean +0.21 vs list mean +1.39, permutation p=0.021), driven by RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, MYH9, MYO1F, HCK, PIK3CB, TMSB10 and ACTB. We infer, but did not measure, lower Rac-GTP loading, lower branched-actin/myosin-II tension and reduced F-actin at nascent cups.", "Step 3 (inferred flux/localisation): Reduced DOCK8-Rac2 GEF output and reduced non-muscle myosin IIA contractility limit pseudopod extension around bound particles and the final scission/closure step, so bound cargo is internalised more slowly per bound particle; receptor-cargo complexes are predicted to dwell longer at the plasma membrane.", "Step 4 (measured, RNA; inferred compensation): A TFEB-associated endolysosomal program is the most strongly enriched coherent set in the data relative to the shifted background (mean +3.06, permutation p=0.0012: TFEB, GAA, GBA, CTSK, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A, LAMP1, plus RAB7A and retromer/ESCRT genes VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B). We interpret this as an expanded or stressed degradative compartment operating downstream of a constrained delivery step, not as evidence that flux through that compartment is increased.", "Step 5 (measured, RNA; inferred metabolic consequence): Higher SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1 and SOAT1 transcripts indicate a shift toward fatty-acid desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification, which we propose converts slowly cleared lipid cargo into stored esters rather than efflux, reinforcing the lysosome-loaded, uptake-limited state (this lipid set is not enriched above the list background, so it is the weakest link in the chain).", "Step 6 (system-level prediction): The net APOE4 phenotype is receptor-rich and lysosome-rich but internalisation-poor; measured cargo clearance should saturate at low internalisation rate even when opsonised cargo and degradative capacity are in excess."], "title": "APOE4 microglia down-tune the Rac2/DOCK8-actomyosin internalisation module while expanding a TFEB-associated endolysosomal compartment, making phagocytic cup closure the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17410890271873522, "cosine_similarity": 0.3207750272960568, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6071909385113269, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17410890271873522, "cosine_similarity": 0.3207750272960568, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6071909385113269, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71782225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 284}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_042", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strongly positive global shift (median +1.46, 77% positive, all |effect|\u003e1); we therefore treat only within-distribution rank/percentile contrasts as informative and assume the selection did not systematically enrich one direction for glycolytic versus mitochondrial genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "Transcript abundance of MPC2, PDP1, TCA and complex I genes is assumed to track enzyme/carrier capacity; measured abundance is not measured activity, flux, or localisation, and no metabolite, oxygen-consumption or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme in this mechanism.", "Cell-intrinsic interpretation assumes the APOE4-versus-APOE3 RNA difference is not dominated by a change in microglial subpopulation proportions or by the co-cultured astrocytes, which cannot be checked from the supplied summary rows (no replicate or cell-composition data).", "Causality is not established by these data; the isogenic comparison supports association of genotype with the expression pattern only."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional repositioning of the carbon-flux bottleneck: upper-glycolytic entry capacity (HK2, PFKP, and the oxidative pentose-phosphate branch) is selectively reduced against a globally positive differential-expression background, while mitochondrial pyruvate import, PDH-activating, TCA-cycle, malate-aspartate shuttle, complex I and ATP-synthase transcripts are among the most strongly elevated. We hypothesise that this makes mitochondrial pyruvate/NADH oxidation, rather than sterol handling, the rate-setting node of APOE4 microglial metabolism, with citrate-export capacity (SLC25A1) and an SREBF1-high desaturation/esterification programme diverting surplus mitochondrial carbon into stored lipid rather than into cholesterol synthesis or efflux. All statements about flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred from measured RNA abundance, not measured directly.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in the isogenic pair should reduce basal and maximal oxygen consumption and impair viability/phagocytic capacity significantly more in APOE4 than in APOE3 microglia, and should force a larger compensatory lactate/ECAR rise in APOE3. If the two genotypes are equally sensitive, or APOE4 is less sensitive, the proposed mitochondrial-pyruvate bottleneck is weakened.", "Baseline flux test: extracellular-flux assay should show higher basal and maximal OCR and a lower glycolytic reserve (ECAR after oligomycin minus basal) in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or lower OCR in APOE4 despite the elevated TCA/complex I transcripts would falsify the flux inference drawn from Step 3-4.", "Tracing test: U-13C-glucose labelling should give a higher M+2 fractional enrichment of citrate, glutamate and aspartate and a lower lactate M+3 fraction in APOE4; unchanged labelling would show the transcript pattern does not translate into flux.", "Directionality test: inhibiting the downstream lipid arm (SCD or DGAT inhibition) should not normalise APOE4 OCR or glycolytic reserve if the mitochondrial node is upstream; if SCD inhibition restores the APOE3-like respiratory phenotype, the ordering of Steps 4 and 6 is wrong.", "Sterol-focus counter-test: pharmacological cholesterol loading or LXR agonism should not reproduce the APOE4 glycolytic-entry repression (HK2/PFKP) in APOE3 cells; if it does, a sterol-sensing mechanism upstream of the metabolic shift should replace this hypothesis.", "Protein-level test: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS should show increased MPC2, OGDH and complex I subunit protein in APOE4; absence of any protein-level increase would restrict the claim to transcript abundance and weaken the capacity inference, since the supplied 2D spots (e.g. protein_spot:038, protein_spot:044) are multi-candidate and cannot test this."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, selected DE list): APOE4 microglia show reduced transcripts for the committed glycolytic entry steps (gene:HK2 at the 3.6th percentile, gene:PFKP 5.5th, gene:HK3 21st of the DE distribution whose median is positive), and reduced oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1). Inference: lowered capacity for glucose-6-phosphate generation and its diversion to NADPH/ribose.", "Step 2 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and PDH-activating phosphatase transcripts are strongly increased (gene:MPC2 99th percentile, gene:PDP1), which we infer increases the fraction of available pyruvate entering the matrix and being decarboxylated rather than reduced to lactate; the pyruvate dehydrogenase subunits themselves are not in the supplied list, so this is an inference about capacity, not a measured PDH activity.", "Step 3 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): TCA and NADH-handling transcripts occupy the extreme upper tail (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G; carriers gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13-class, gene:SLC25A5), consistent with an expanded malate-aspartate shuttle and increased matrix NADH turnover; permutation test versus the whole DE distribution gives p\u003c0.001 for the TCA set (mean +4.96, median +4.74 vs global median +1.46).", "Step 4 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred capacity): respiratory-chain transcripts, particularly complex I (21 NDUF genes, mean +2.99, p=0.003) and ATP synthase subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME), are coordinately elevated, so we infer higher oxidative ATP-producing capacity and a correspondingly greater dependence on complex I for NAD+ regeneration.", "Step 5 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred fuel breadth): alternative anaplerotic/acetyl-CoA routes are up (gene:OXCT1 ketone-body activation, gene:GLUD1 glutamate deamination, gene:ACSS2 acetate activation), which we infer compensates for the reduced glycolytic supply of pyruvate.", "Step 6 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred lipid disposal): the citrate/isocitrate carrier transcript (gene:SLC25A1) and an SREBF1-high desaturation/esterification programme (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD) are elevated, whereas sterol-synthesis/sensing transcripts are not distinguished from background (gene:SREBF2 at the 27th percentile). We infer that surplus mitochondrial carbon leaving as citrate is routed to monounsaturated fatty-acid and neutral-lipid formation rather than to a sterol programme. ACLY, FASN, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1 and LIPA are absent from the supplied rows, so the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool and any sterol efflux step are unmeasured and are stated only as inference.", "Step 7 (system-level consequence): because glycolytic entry capacity is the reduced element, APOE4 microglia are predicted to have little glycolytic reserve, so any demand that normally requires rapid aerobic glycolysis (immune activation, phagocytic bursts) or any block of mitochondrial pyruvate entry/complex I should impair APOE4 cells disproportionately relative to isogenic APOE3."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift the glucose-carbon bottleneck from glycolytic entry to mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation (MPC2/PDP1-TCA-complex I), leaving a low glycolytic reserve"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12133072407045009, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1423133306164342, "cosine_similarity": 0.3207022080559941, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5918058252427184, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12133072407045009, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1423133306164342, "cosine_similarity": 0.3207022080559941, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5918058252427184, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.51097575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 285}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_079", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected, thresholded differential-expression results (no |effect| below 1) with 77% of rows positive; we therefore treat mere up-direction as weakly informative and rely on effect magnitude relative to the list-wide distribution and on within-pathway discordance.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no fold-change conversion is assumed.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for machinery availability only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo localization, uptake flux and sterol pools are inferred and were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous corroboration only, never as identified proteins; the ANXA1-candidate and CTSD/CTSB-candidate spots could equally reflect TALDO1, ACTB, TPM3, CAPZB or keratin contaminants.", "The list-wide positive shift could be technical (normalization, ambient RNA, differing capture depth between genotypes); the S100B row suggests possible astrocyte-derived signal in a co-culture, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "Extreme single-gene values (for example ACTB, ARHGDIA, GAA) are treated as unreliable individually and are used only as part of set-level patterns.", "No lipidomic, imaging, flux or replicate-level data were supplied, so the lipid-retention state central to the claim is a prediction rather than an observation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a post-internalization bottleneck: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors and for a TFEB/MITF-type hydrolase-plus-v-ATPase lysosomal program are coordinately higher, yet ER sterol-sensing (SREBP-2 target) and esterification/storage transcripts are also higher rather than suppressed. We hypothesise that internalised lipid is retained in an expanded, hydrolase-rich late-endosome/lysosome compartment and is delivered inefficiently to the ER-accessible sterol pool, so the lysosomal-biogenesis and sterol-synthesis programmes are compensatory responses to that retention. Because the actin engulfment-execution transcripts are not coordinately raised (several are strongly lower), the limiting step is placed downstream of particle internalization rather than at the phagocytic cup. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating sterol-loading test: after acute loading with fluorescent/oxidised LDL or myelin debris, APOE3 microglia should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR24) while APOE4 microglia should suppress them substantially less, with a higher fraction of unesterified cholesterol (filipin) inside LAMP1-positive compartments. Equal SREBP-2 suppression and equal lysosomal cholesterol in the two genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Egress rescue: bypassing lysosomal sterol export (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or forced lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer) should normalise SREBP-2 target and TFEB-target transcripts and reduce LGALS3 puncta in APOE4 without lowering uptake-receptor transcripts. Failure to normalise the sterol-synthesis signature would weaken the mechanism.", "Ordering test: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should worsen lysosomal lipid retention and leave the SREBP-2 signature elevated or higher. If TFEB knockdown abolishes the APOE4 lipid-retention phenotype, the lysosomal programme is causal rather than compensatory and this mechanism is wrong.", "Cytoskeletal negative control (rejects the assigned focus if it fails): blocking actin-dependent internalization (cytochalasin D or ARP2/3 inhibition) or restoring myosin-IIA/Rac function should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in lysosomal hydrolase and SREBP-2 target expression under mock conditions. If actin blockade equalises the genotypes, the bottleneck is at engulfment, not at egress.", "Uptake-rate test: live-cell uptake kinetics of a soluble lipoprotein tracer should be equal or faster in APOE4, while the tracer's degradation/clearance half-life inside the cell should be longer. Slower initial uptake in APOE4 would contradict step 1 and weaken the mechanism.", "Protein-level check: immunoblot for cathepsin B/D, GBA and v-ATPase subunits with unambiguous antibodies should confirm higher mature protein in APOE4; unchanged protein despite the large transcript effects would indicate the RNA shift is technical and weaken the whole chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for scavenger/lipoprotein and efferocytic receptors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, ABCA7, MERTK with its bridging ligands GAS6, MFGE8, ANXA1). We infer, but did not measure, an increased receptor-mediated lipid/lipoprotein uptake flux.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred localization): Late-endosomal/lysosomal delivery components are higher (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, DNM2, CLTB, PIK3C3) while retrieval/recycling and mannose-6-phosphate sorting components are lower (WASHC4, M6PR, SYNJ1). We infer a routing bias towards terminal late endosome/lysosome over recycling; no cargo tracing was measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA; inferred activity): A CLEAR-type lysosomal programme is transcriptionally expanded well beyond the list-wide shift (TFEB, MITF up; hydrolases GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD; v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1, ATP6V0D1). Hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and lysosome number were not measured.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; inferred): Delivery of lysosome-derived sterol/lipid to the ER-accessible pool is rate-limiting, so the sterol sensor continues to signal deficiency despite raised uptake. The signature of this is that SREBP-2 pathway transcripts are up, not down (SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24), alongside SREBF1 and SCD.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred storage flux): Retained lipid is diverted into esterified/stored pools and provokes lysosomal stress markers (SOAT1, DGAT1, LGALS3, GPNMB, NPC2 up). No lipid, cholesteryl-ester or droplet measurement is present in these data, so the lipid pool itself is inferred, not observed.", "Step 6 (localizing the bottleneck): The actin engulfment-execution arm is discordant rather than coordinately raised (MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, ACTB lower; ARPC1B, ARPC4, ARPC5, CFL1, ACTG1 higher), which argues against a simple gain of phagocytic-cup capacity and places the limiting step after internalization."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at endolysosomal lipid egress, not at engulfment: receptor-driven lipid intake plus TFEB-type lysosomal expansion with a persistent ER sterol-deficit signal"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1736675368329616, "cosine_similarity": 0.319382984629249, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6086537216828479, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07534246575342465, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1736675368329616, "cosine_similarity": 0.319382984629249, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6086537216828479, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.69792575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 286}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_075", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); program coherence was judged against that 77%-positive, median +1.46 background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, P2RY12, most COPII/ERAD members) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and preserved as reported; effect magnitudes up to 15 are treated as ordinal, and part of the global positive skew may be technical (probe-based 10X Flex pseudobulk, depth/composition), so sign coherence, not magnitude, carries most of the weight.", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to track catabolic and oxidative capacity; respiration rate, lysosomal proteolytic/lipolytic flux, neutral-lipid and cholesteryl-ester content, and TFEB nuclear localisation were not measured and are inferred only.", "2D protein spots are multi-candidate; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Cathepsin-containing spots go in both directions (protein_spot:052/053 up, protein_spot:058/067/069 down) and are used only for compatibility testing.", "Genes within a program are not independent (shared regulons, co-detection), so the reported counts are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins; the lipid-acquisition step assumes an extracellular lipid source present in the mock condition.", "Effects attributed to the measured mock condition are capacity/state differences; any claim of degradative failure would require a challenge (lipid or myelin load) and is not asserted for the measured state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of a lipid-handling axis: higher lipoprotein/lipid acquisition and lysosomal acid-hydrolase plus v-ATPase machinery feeding an unusually strongly up-regulated nuclear-encoded TCA/oxidative-phosphorylation program, with part of the released sterol and fatty-acid load routed into esterification/desaturation and storage. The pattern is best read as an increased-capacity, homeostatic-identity-preserving catabolic state (adaptation/throughput), not as an unfolded-protein-response or ER-secretory bottleneck; because only steady-state RNA and ambiguous 2D protein spots were measured, oxidative and lysosomal flux remain inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, live-cell respirometry should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a larger etomoxir/CPT1-sensitive fraction in APOE4. If APOE4 OCR is equal to or lower than APOE3 despite the 39/39 up ETC transcript set (gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME), the increased-throughput reading is falsified and the failed-compensation alternative is favoured.", "Prospective lysosomal-flux test: DQ-BSA and BODIPY-C12/myelin-degradation assays should show faster cargo hydrolysis and equal-or-lower undegraded substrate in APOE4. Accumulation of undegraded lipid with high hydrolase transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB) would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective upstream-dependency test: culturing in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SR-BI/CD36 uptake, should collapse the APOE4-specific lysosomal and OXPHOS transcript signature (gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:MDH1, gene:NDUFA5) toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the OXPHOS program after lipid removal would show lipid acquisition is not upstream.", "Prospective routing test: SOAT1 inhibition should, under this mechanism, shift cholesteryl ester to free sterol with increased oxidation/efflux and without induction of a coherent UPR. If SOAT1 inhibition instead triggers ER-stress markers and toxicity selectively in APOE4, storage was masking an ongoing overload and the adaptive reading is weakened.", "Prospective ER-proteostasis test (rejection of the assigned focus): APOE4 cells should show no greater XBP1 splicing, ATF6 cleavage, eIF2alpha phosphorylation or secretory-cargo retention than APOE3 in mock, despite gene:ATF6 and gene:DDIT3 being elevated. Detection of constitutive UPR activation or slowed VSVG/cargo transit in APOE4 would falsify the rejection and re-open an ER-secretory mechanism.", "Prospective mitonuclear test: given gene:MT-CO2 and gene:MT-ATP6 decreased while all nuclear ETC subunits increased, assembled complex IV/V (BN-PAGE) should still be equal or higher in APOE4. A selective deficit in assembled complex IV/V would indicate an assembly bottleneck rather than expanded oxidative capacity."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and sensing machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1), predicting greater delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesterol and fatty acids into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2: A TFEB-associated lysosomal program is co-elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD; acidification subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C and all eight represented ATP6V genes), expanding the capacity to hydrolyse ingested lipid, sphingolipid and glycolipid cargo.", "Step 3: Catabolic products are routed to mitochondria: TCA and beta-oxidation transcripts (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA), pyruvate/adenine-nucleotide carriers (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A5) and 39/39 represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:CYCS) are increased, with the largest effects in the whole selected list.", "Step 4: Load exceeding immediate oxidation is buffered by esterification/desaturation and storage (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACAT2, gene:FABP5), and by mitochondrial antioxidant capacity (gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4), keeping free sterol and unsaturated free fatty acid away from the ER.", "Step 5: Consistent with buffering rather than proteotoxic failure, the ER-stress/ERAD set is not coherently induced (gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51, gene:MANF up, but gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:PDIA3 -1.26; sign split indistinguishable from the 77%-positive list background), and ER-chaperone-candidate protein spots are non-significant and slightly negative (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 containing HSP90B1/HSPA5).", "Step 6: Homeostatic microglial identity genes are retained/elevated (gene:CSF1R, gene:MERTK, gene:GPR34, gene:IRF8, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:AIF1; 10/10 positive) with only mild activation markers (gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:GPNMB) and gene:CCL4 decreased, so the state is a metabolic re-specification rather than an inflammatory or degenerative collapse."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-acquisition/lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic cell state with sterol/fatty-acid overflow into esterification, not an ER-proteostasis defect"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26838246555146084, "cosine_similarity": 0.3192496850491705, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_075", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6167216828478964, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26838246555146084, "cosine_similarity": 0.3192496850491705, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6167216828478964, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72998925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 68}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Causality is not established by these data; the hypothesis proposes a direction that must be tested by perturbation.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows \u003e 0, median +1.46); enrichment is judged only against that internal background, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes/transporters; no enzyme activity, sterol flux, lipid mass, or subcellular localisation was measured in the supplied files.", "SOAT1/DGAT1 and SREBP pathway activities are inferred from transcript levels, not from cleaved SREBP-2, esterification rate, or ER-accessible cholesterol measurements.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a specific lipid enzyme.", "Key pathway members are absent from the supplied rows (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, CYP51A1, FDFT1, mevalonate-kinase enzymes, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, TFE3), so the pathway reconstruction is partial and the efflux arm is entirely unmeasured.", "The astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoproteins; genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous and the RNA readout may mix microglial and co-culture-driven states."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional state in which lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase genes, lipoprotein- and sterol-uptake genes, distal sterol-synthesis genes, and neutral-lipid esterification genes are all higher than in APOE3. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is not lipid ingestion or lysosomal hydrolysis capacity but the onward transfer of lysosomally liberated cholesterol to the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool; because that pool stays functionally low, SREBP-dependent uptake and distal synthesis genes remain de-repressed while SOAT1/DGAT1-dependent esterification diverts sterol and fatty acid into stored esters, closing a feed-forward loop that expands the lysosomal/lipid-droplet lipid burden. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR/secretory focus is rejected: UPR and secretory-trafficking transcripts are not enriched above the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list, and the protein spots whose candidate lists contain the ER chaperones HSPA5/HSP90B1 are non-significant and negative.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester mass, raise the ER-accessible/free cholesterol pool, and consequently REDUCE SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, SCARB1) toward APOE3 levels. If cholesteryl ester falls but SREBP-2 targets stay elevated or increase, the proposed sequestration-to-de-repression link is wrong and a primary ER sterol-delivery or sensing defect should be favoured instead.", "Bypass test: delivering cholesterol directly to membranes/ER with methyl-beta-cyclodextrin-cholesterol should suppress SREBP-2 targets equally in APOE4 and APOE3, whereas cholesterol supplied only as lipoprotein (requiring lysosomal egress) should suppress them less in APOE4. Equal suppression by both routes would falsify the lysosome-to-ER bottleneck step.", "Localisation test: ER-accessible cholesterol biosensor (D4H*) plus filipin/LipidSpot imaging should show, in APOE4, increased sterol and neutral lipid in LAMP1-positive compartments and droplets but equal or reduced ER/plasma-membrane accessible cholesterol. Higher ER-accessible cholesterol in APOE4 would falsify the core claim.", "Ordering test: TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A) without correcting, and probably worsening, cholesteryl-ester and droplet accumulation, supporting the lysosomal program as compensatory rather than causal. If TFEB knockdown normalises lipid storage, the compensatory ordering is wrong.", "Uptake-arm test: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade should reduce lipid loading and SREBP-target expression more in APOE4 than APOE3. Genotype-independent effects would weaken the feed-forward uptake step.", "Negative prediction (rejects the assigned focus): APOE4 microglia should NOT show a canonical UPR signature under mock conditions - no genotype increase in XBP1 splicing, BiP/GRP94 protein, ATF4/CHOP protein, or secretory cargo delay. Clear XBP1 splicing or BiP induction in APOE4 would support an ER-proteostasis mechanism over this lipid-handling one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts encoding lipoprotein/sterol uptake and lysosomal lipid handling are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, reported log units). Inferred (not measured): increased flux of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived cholesteryl ester and phospholipid into the endolysosome.", "Measured: a coherent TFEB-type lysosomal module is up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SUMF1; 15/15 up, permutation p_mean=0.006). Inferred: expanded lysosomal hydrolytic capacity as a compensatory response, i.e. hydrolysis is not the limiting step.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred, not measured): export of liberated cholesterol from the lysosomal lumen/limiting membrane to the ER-accessible regulatory pool is rate-limiting in APOE4, so the sterol sensed at the ER remains functionally low despite a high total cellular lipid load.", "Measured consequence: SREBP-pathway transcripts and distal sterol-synthesis enzymes are uniformly higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1; 11/11 up). Inferred: sustained SREBP-2/SREBP-1 transcriptional output that further raises uptake (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR) and distal synthesis.", "Measured: esterification and neutral-lipid/glycerolipid assembly transcripts are up as a block (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:SCD, gene:ABHD5, gene:MGLL; 10/10 up, permutation p_mean=0.032), with reductant/acetyl-CoA supply genes gene:ACSS2, gene:NNT, gene:ME1 also up. Inferred: sterol and fatty acid entering the ER are re-esterified into cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and stored rather than returned to the regulatory pool or exported.", "Inferred feed-forward closure: storage keeps the ER-accessible pool low, so steps 4 and 5 persist; oxysterol/LXR-type markers (gene:CH25H, gene:MYLIP, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) rise in parallel, consistent with a spatially split sterol state in which total sterol is high while the ER-sensed pool is not.", "Predicted cellular phenotype (not measured here): larger cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet stores and lipid-laden lysosomes in APOE4 microglia, with reduced availability of free cholesterol for membrane/efflux functions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at delivery of lysosomal cholesterol to the ER-accessible pool, driving a TFEB-hydrolase plus SREBP-uptake/esterification feed-forward storage loop"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.431368386072444, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264568738204832, "cosine_similarity": 0.31889876250235555, "direction_accuracy": 0.39805825242718446, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6478220064724919, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.431368386072444, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.264568738204832, "cosine_similarity": 0.31889876250235555, "direction_accuracy": 0.39805825242718446, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6478220064724919, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.909511, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 287}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_011", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong positive offset (median about +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base), so only effects ranked well above that background are treated as informative; the logarithm base is preserved as reported and not converted.", "Transcript abundance of carriers and enzymes is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding transport and enzymatic capacity; no flux, metabolite, NADPH or acetyl-CoA pool was measured.", "ACLY, FASN, ACACA, CPT1A and all lipid species are absent from the supplied data; the acetyl-CoA-to-fatty-acid conversion step is inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots 043-046 contain TALDO1 among four to five candidate genes each; they are used only as weak, non-identifying support for altered NADPH-linked pentose-phosphate protein abundance, not as a measurement of TALDO1.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein substrate, so uptake and de-novo routes coexist; the hypothesis concerns the relative bias, not exclusivity.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be re-checked and clonal or batch effects of the isogenic lines cannot be excluded."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated transcriptional up-shift of the inner-mitochondrial-membrane carriers and cytosolic shuttle enzymes that move pyruvate-derived carbon and reducing equivalents into the cytosol (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) together with the SREBF1-driven desaturation/acylation arm (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:ACSS2). We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is cytosolic acetyl-CoA (and associated NADPH) supply set by citrate/malate export, and that raising this supply biases APOE4 microglia toward de-novo synthesis of monounsaturated fatty acids and their incorporation into neutral and membrane glycerolipids, with the lysosomal hydrolase program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB) rising as a downstream response to the increased lipid load rather than as the initiating lesion. Causality is not established by these data; only steady-state abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the mitochondrial citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in newly synthesised monounsaturated glycerolipid (13C6-glucose or D2O tracing into 16:1 and 18:1 acyl chains and into triacylglycerol) by more than half, while leaving lipoprotein-derived (exogenous, labelled-LDL) lipid uptake largely unchanged. If SLC25A1 inhibition leaves the APOE4 excess of labelled MUFA glycerolipid intact, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "SCD inhibition should normalise the APOE4 desaturation index (16:1/16:0, 18:1/18:0) and reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid-droplet area toward APOE3 levels; if the APOE4 droplet excess is fully MUFA-independent (unchanged after SCD inhibition), step 4 fails.", "Untargeted lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show the APOE4 excess concentrated in unsaturated triacylglycerol and MUFA-containing phospholipid species rather than in saturated species or in free cholesterol; a purely free-cholesterol or purely sphingolipid-dominated difference would weaken the mechanism and favour the lysosomal-catabolism-primary alternative.", "Seahorse/isotope measurement should show higher pyruvate-dependent oxygen consumption and higher fractional citrate export in APOE4 microglia; equal or lower pyruvate oxidation despite the transcript up-shift would break step 1 and imply the RNA changes are not translated into flux.", "If the lysosomal program is the primary lesion instead, blocking lysosomal acid hydrolysis (e.g. bafilomycin or LIPA inhibition) in APOE3 cells should reproduce the APOE4 carrier/shuttle transcript signature; observing that would demote step 6 from consequence to cause and falsify the ordering claimed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for mitochondrial pyruvate and citrate/malate carriers (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13) and for TCA/oxidative enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB, gene:GLUD1). We infer, but did not measure, increased pyruvate entry and citrate production.", "Step 2 (inferred transport/localisation): Increased SLC25A1-mediated citrate efflux, coupled to the cytosolic malate-aspartate arm (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13), is proposed to raise cytosolic acetyl-CoA and cytosolic NADPH availability. ACLY, FASN and ACACA were not measured in this dataset, so this step is an assumption; gene:ACSS2 provides a measured parallel acetyl-CoA-generating route.", "Step 3 (bottleneck): Cytosolic acetyl-CoA/NADPH supply, not the terminal esterifying enzymes, is the rate-setting node: transcripts for the esterification enzymes are close to the background of this differential-expression set (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:GPAT4), whereas the carrier/shuttle module sits at the top of the distribution.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred activity): The SREBF1 arm is elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24), predicting increased stearoyl-CoA desaturase activity and a higher 16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 ratio in newly made acyl chains; gene:AGPAT2 provides the acylation capacity to route these acyl-CoAs into phosphatidic-acid-derived glycerolipids.", "Step 5 (predicted lipid phenotype, not measured here): The net output is an APOE4-biased pool of monounsaturated-acyl-chain glycerolipids (unsaturated triacylglycerol and MUFA-containing phospholipid), with neutral lipid stored in droplets even without induction of DGAT1/SOAT1 transcripts.", "Step 6 (downstream response): The elevated lipid/lipoprotein load reaching the endolysosomal system (gene:SCARB1, gene:RAB7A, gene:AP5M1, gene:IGF2R) is proposed to drive the coordinated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A) as a compensatory catabolic response."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate mitochondrial citrate/malate export machinery, making cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply the rate-setting node for SREBF1-SCD monounsaturated lipogenesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13992172211350293, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09460897802464946, "cosine_similarity": 0.3187752514404438, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5813203883495146, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13992172211350293, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09460897802464946, "cosine_similarity": 0.3187752514404438, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5813203883495146, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7402065, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 288}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_056", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so all set-level statements are relative to the shifted internal background (global median approx +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base) and not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance of hydrolases is treated as a readout of transcriptional demand only; enzyme protein amount, maturation and catalytic activity, lysosomal pH, and lipid flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each (mean approx 4.8), so no spot is assumed to identify a single protein; spot-level directions are used only as weak, non-identifying concordance/discordance checks.", "TFEB/MITF transcript elevation is assumed to reflect, at least partly, an increase in the lysosomal biogenesis program; nuclear translocation and mTORC1 status were not measured.", "The APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the metadata, so genotype rather than treatment or background explains the contrast; replicate number was not supplied, so effect-size precision is unknown.", "No lipid, lipidomic or lysosomal-morphology measurement is present in these files; the lipid-storage endpoint is a prediction, not an observation.", "Causality is not established by these data; direction of the proposed cascade is a model to be tested."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a substrate-driven, TFEB-associated induction of acid hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSK) together with raised endolysosomal acidification/transport transcripts, which we interpret as compensation for a rate-limiting step in lysosomal luminal glycosphingolipid/glycoconjugate clearance and downstream lipid egress; the un-cleared lipid is predicted to be routed into desaturated neutral-lipid stores (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, MGLL transcripts elevated) rather than being disposed of, while a canonical type-I/II interferon transcriptional program is absent from these data and is therefore rejected as the differentiating mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: inhibiting glucosylceramide synthase (UGCG) to lower lysosomal glycosphingolipid input should, in APOE4 but not APOE3, normalise the elevated hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, GAA, CTSB) and reduce neutral-lipid-droplet area toward APOE3 levels, whereas simply raising enzyme dose (recombinant/overexpressed GCase or hexosaminidase) should not normalise droplet load; if enzyme supplementation alone corrects the phenotype and substrate reduction does not, the bottleneck is enzyme amount rather than luminal clearance/egress flux and this mechanism is weakened.", "Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin species and higher desaturated (MUFA-rich) triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester; unchanged or lower glycosphingolipid and neutral lipid despite the hydrolase transcript elevation would falsify the substrate-load premise.", "Enzyme-activity assays (4-MU-GlcCer, 4-MU-GlcNAc, cathepsin B) and GCase/HEXB immunoblots should show APOE4 activity flat or sub-proportional relative to its transcript increase; a proportional or greater increase in activity would remove the transcription/flux discordance the mechanism requires.", "Mild V-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) or NPC1 inhibition (U18666A) should produce a disproportionately larger increase in LysoTracker/filipin/droplet signal in APOE4 than APOE3; equal sensitivity would argue the APOE4 lysosome is not already operating near capacity.", "Interferon test: APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia should show no significant elevation of a canonical ISG panel (ISG15, IFIT1, MX1, OAS1, STAT1) by qPCR and no elevated phospho-STAT1; detection of a coherent ISG induction would support an interferon-driven alternative and weaken the claim that the difference is a lysosomal-lipid bottleneck.", "Rescuing lysosomal lipid egress (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or NPC2 supplementation) should reduce APOE4 droplet load and lower hydrolase transcripts without abolishing the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript elevation; if the OXPHOS/mtDNA transcript mismatch resolves first and precedes lysosomal normalisation in a time course, a mitochondria-primary alternative should replace this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases delivery and/or retention of lipid- and glycoconjugate-rich cargo in the microglial endolysosome (inferred flux; the only measured proxies are elevated uptake/receptor transcripts gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7 and lysosomal-trafficking transcripts gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A).", "Accumulating luminal substrate activates a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis response, seen as coordinated elevation of acid hydrolase transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD) and of gene:TFEB and gene:MITF; this is measured RNA abundance, not enzyme activity.", "The bottleneck lies downstream of transcription: per-lysosome hydrolytic and egress capacity (enzyme maturation, saposin/activator supply, acidification, sterol/sphingoid export) does not scale with the induced transcripts, so luminal glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and glycogen-derived substrate persists (inferred; the ambiguous cathepsin/hexosaminidase-containing spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 are lower in APOE4 and are at least not concordant with a proportional protein increase).", "Compensatory acidification/solute-transport machinery is engaged (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:SLC38A7, gene:CLCN7) yet the sterol-sensing arm is not activated above the dataset background (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR near the global median), arguing that the ER free-cholesterol pool is not starved and that lipid is retained or stored rather than mobilised.", "Fatty acids and sterols released or diverted from this compartment are channelled into desaturation and esterification (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:MGLL), predicting expansion of desaturated triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester droplets in APOE4 - a lipid pool that was not measured here.", "Mitochondria are transcriptionally re-tuned in parallel: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA transcripts rise (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2) while mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4), a mitonuclear mismatch consistent with, but not proof of, increased lipid-derived oxidative demand at the mito-lysosome interface.", "The genotype difference is therefore metabolic rather than immune-activational: chemokine changes are modest and mixed (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2 up; gene:CCL4, gene:TNFAIP3, gene:RELB down) and no interferon-stimulated gene module is present, so interferon signalling is not invoked as the driver."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited by lysosomal glycolipid catabolic flux, not by interferon signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1268507920097478, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0941994400057054, "cosine_similarity": 0.31785677787716216, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_056", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6271650485436894, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1268507920097478, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0941994400057054, "cosine_similarity": 0.31785677787716216, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6271650485436894, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86176025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 289}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_112", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression set (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77% positive, gene:ACTB at -4.98); we therefore interpret within-list percentiles and set-versus-background permutation tests, assuming this shift is a shared normalisation/composition offset rather than a genuine transcriptome-wide doubling.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and effects up to +15.5 are implausible as log2 fold changes, so only rank and sign are treated as informative.", "Absence of a gene from the list (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, STARD3, HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, NR1H3) means it was not among the selected DE rows; it is not evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal, transfer and esterification proteins; no sterol, oxysterol, cholesteryl-ester or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, and none is claimed as observed.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as ambiguous, non-confirmatory context.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so extrinsic lipoprotein supply may differ between genotypes and is assumed constant in the reasoning above."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in where sterol sits rather than in how much they synthesise it: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid internalisation (SCARB1, CD36, SLCO2B1) and for a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program are raised far above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list, whereas transcripts for sterol egress and export (NPC2, OSBPL8, APOE, PLTP, MYLIP, SOAT1) are at or below the list median. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is non-vesicular transfer of lysosome-derived free sterol to the ER/plasma membrane, so that sterol is retained in an endolysosomal and cholesteryl-ester pool, the ER sterol-sensing pool stays relatively unsatisfied (SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR and post-squalene enzymes remain induced), and desmosterol consumption by elevated DHCR24 further lowers endogenous LXR tone for export. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, localisation and activity statements are inferred from RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating occlusion test: blocking NPC1-dependent lysosomal sterol egress with U18666A should produce a markedly smaller incremental increase in lysosomal filipin-positive free cholesterol and a smaller further induction of SREBP-2 targets (LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR24) in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, because the egress step is already limiting in APOE4. If APOE4 responds equally or more strongly than APOE3, the egress-bottleneck step is weakened.", "Direct pool test: quantitative lipidomics/imaging should show, in mock APOE4 versus APOE3, higher lysosome-localised free cholesterol and a higher cholesteryl-ester-to-free-cholesterol ratio with no increase, or a decrease, in ER-accessible cholesterol. Equal lysosomal sterol, or a higher ER-accessible pool in APOE4, falsifies the central claim.", "Ligand/export test: DHCR24 inhibition or desmosterol supplementation, and separately an LXR agonist (GW3965), should restore apoA-I/HDL-acceptor cholesterol efflux in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels with induction of ABCA1/ABCG1. Absence of a genotype-selective rescue weakens Step 6.", "Rerouting test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should reduce cholesteryl-ester and lipid-droplet content and increase efflux preferentially in APOE4; if APOE4 instead accumulates free sterol without gaining efflux, the storage-versus-export partitioning in Step 5 is wrong.", "Program-specificity test: TFEB knockdown should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase induction (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A) in APOE4; if hydrolase transcripts are TFEB-independent here, Step 2 must be reassigned to another driver.", "Protein-level test: if NPC2 and NPC1 protein, and the measured lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer rate (ER sterol biosensor), are equal to or higher in APOE4 than APOE3 despite the transcript pattern, the mechanism as a whole is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_112", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise scavenger/lipid-uptake transcripts far above the global shift of this list (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, 99.1st percentile of all 2212 RNA rows whose median is +1.46; gene:CD36, gene:SLCO2B1), which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein-derived sterol and lipid into the endolysosomal system. Lipid uptake itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A coordinated TFEB/MITF-associated degradative program is induced (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF; hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A). The 14-gene hydrolase set averages +3.52 versus a global mean of +1.39 (permutation p=0.002), so hydrolytic capacity, and therefore luminal liberation of free sterol from esters and of sphingolipid intermediates, is inferred to expand.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; partly inferred from non-scaling and from missing genes): Egress machinery does not scale with influx. gene:NPC2 (+1.17) sits at the 34.7th percentile and gene:OSBPL8 (-1.90) at the 12.7th percentile, i.e. below the list median, so ER-endolysosome contact-site and carrier-mediated sterol transfer is predicted to be limiting. NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 and ABCA1/ABCG1 were not measured, so this step is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 4 (inferred sensing state): Because lysosome-derived sterol is inferred not to reach the ER sensing pool efficiently, the SREBP-2 module stays on rather than being repressed: gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2 are all positive. As a set these are not enriched above the global shift (permutation p=0.52), so the claim is persistence of an active biosynthetic/uptake program under lipid load, not hyper-induction of synthesis.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred partitioning): Sterol that reaches the ER is predicted to be esterified and stored rather than exported (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72 up in absolute terms), while the sterol-carrier gene:SCP2 (+5.95, 96th percentile) rises, consistent with rerouting toward storage and peroxisomal/cytosolic carriers rather than plasma-membrane export.", "Step 6 (inferred ligand and export tone): Elevated gene:DHCR24 (+3.69, 85th percentile) is predicted to lower the desmosterol pool, an endogenous LXR agonist, and the LXR-responsive export transcripts measured here (gene:APOE 38th, gene:PLTP 27th, gene:MYLIP 41st, gene:ABCA7 65th percentile) are at or below the list median, so net efflux capacity per unit internalised sterol is inferred to fall. ABCA1 and ABCG1 transcripts and all sterol pools were not measured."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: TFEB-associated hydrolase/uptake expansion outpaces NPC2/ORP-dependent transfer to the ER, sustaining SREBP-2 output and an esterified, export-poor sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2328509725829212, "cosine_similarity": 0.31784735589354224, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_112", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6279773462783171, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2328509725829212, "cosine_similarity": 0.31784735589354224, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6279773462783171, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72283325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 290}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_098", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1 on an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); program directions were judged against that 77% positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. SPTLC1/2, UGCG, ASAH1, PSAP, NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, MCOLN1) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, autophagic/degradative flux, cholesterol and sphingolipid pools, ER-accessible sterol, lipid-droplet content and oxygen consumption were not measured, so all routing and flux statements are inferences.", "Elevated SREBP-target transcripts are assumed to reflect low ER-accessible sterol rather than sterol-independent SREBF1 induction; this is untested here (HMGCR and SQLE have no supplied rows).", "Protein-spot rows are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (mean 4.8) and heavy keratin/actin contamination; no spot identifies a single protein, so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of individual proteins.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increases are assumed to accompany, not prove, increased TFEB nuclear activity; mTORC1 activity and TFEB localisation were not measured.", "Astrocyte co-culture and the day-30 timepoint are assumed not to confound genotype assignment of these transcripts (no cell-type deconvolution data were supplied)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) show a coordinated cell-state change rather than a single enzymatic bottleneck: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28), for a broad CLEAR-type endolysosomal module (43/45 queried members represented, 40 up; gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88), and for mitochondrial TCA/beta-oxidation/ETC capacity (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47) are jointly elevated, while SREBP-target sterol/lipogenic transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:SCD +4.17) and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72). We interpret this as increased lipid handling capacity with sterol routed into lysosomal hydrolysis, esterification/storage and oxidation instead of replenishing the ER-accessible sterol pool, keeping the SREBP arm de-repressed. Sphingolipid hydrolase induction (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:GM2A +2.01) is best explained as part of this general lysosomal expansion, not as a sphingolipid-selective program, because sphingolipid biosynthetic transcripts are indistinguishable from the selected-list background (7/21 represented, median +1.27 vs +1.46 list-wide; gene:B4GALT5 -1.88). Directions and magnitudes are transcript abundance on the reported (unspecified-base) log scale; flux, enzyme activity and lipid pools were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with exogenous cholesterol (LDL or 25-hydroxycholesterol) should suppress SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR) at least as strongly in APOE4 as in APOE3 while leaving the lysosomal/CLEAR module elevated; if APOE4 SREBP targets are already sterol-insensitive or if the CLEAR module collapses in parallel, the 'sterol routed away from the ER pool' step is wrong.", "Prospective flux test of adaptation vs failed compensation: pulse-chase of fluorescent/labelled lipoprotein, myelin or BODIPY-LacCer should show equal or higher per-cell lysosomal hydrolysis rate and equal or higher etomoxir-sensitive oxygen consumption in APOE4 under mock conditions; measurably slower degradation or lower fatty-acid-driven respiration despite the elevated hydrolase and mitochondrial transcripts would falsify the 'expanded capacity with altered routing' mechanism in favour of a degradative bottleneck.", "Prospective specificity test: TFEB/MITF knockdown should coordinately reduce GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, CTSB, GAA and v-ATPase transcripts in APOE4; persistence of the sphingolipid hydrolases after TFEB/MITF loss would show a sphingolipid-selective regulator and falsify step 3.", "Prospective challenge test: the mechanism predicts APOE4 cells are not defective at baseline but have reduced reserve; a myelin or oxLDL overload challenge should produce greater ceramide/glycosphingolipid and cholesteryl-ester accumulation and more enlarged LAMP1 compartments in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas equal handling under overload would weaken the claim that the state is load-driven.", "Prospective protein-level test: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS (not 2D spots) should show increased GBA, HEXA/B, CTSB and ATP6V1A protein in APOE4; the current gel data are equivocal, since significant spots containing CTSD/CTSB/HEXB/ATP6V1E1 candidates move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:055 +0.59 up versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:064 -1.20), and a confirmed decrease in hydrolase protein would contradict the capacity-expansion step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters microglial lipoprotein/lipid handling in the mock state, accompanied by higher transcript levels for scavenger and lipoprotein receptors and lipid carriers (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24), inferred to increase delivery of lipid cargo to the endolysosomal system.", "A CLEAR-type transcriptional program is engaged (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), raising transcripts for acidification (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30), hydrolase delivery (gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02), membrane proteins (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06) and lysosomal solute export (gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46), i.e. expanded degradative capacity (capacity inferred, flux not measured).", "Sphingolipid and glycoconjugate hydrolases rise as members of this same module rather than as a selective sphingolipid response (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:SUMF1 +2.01, gene:NPC2 +1.17), predicting increased ceramide/glycosphingolipid turnover capacity proportional to overall lysosomal expansion.", "Lipid liberated in this compartment is inferred to be routed to esterified storage and to mitochondrial oxidation rather than to the ER regulatory sterol pool: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:MGLL +4.00 alongside a fully positive nuclear-encoded mitochondrial module (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:COX5B +2.33, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, carriers gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56).", "Because ER-accessible sterol is not restored, SREBP-driven transcripts stay up in the unstressed state (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SCD +4.17), sustaining synthesis and uptake and feeding the loop back to step 1.", "This state is accompanied by lower transcripts for homeostatic/motile microglial functions (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:FAM49B -5.83, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:SPN -7.26, gene:CSF1 -5.91) and by mixed glycolytic transcripts (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73 but gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08), consistent with reallocation toward lipid catabolism/oxidation rather than with generic activation.", "Predicted consequence in the measured condition: normal-to-increased basal degradative and oxidative throughput with an enlarged lysosomal/esterified-lipid compartment; a degradative deficit would be revealed only under a future lipid or myelin challenge that exceeds this expanded capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-and-mitochondria-expanded lipid-processing state in which sterol is routed to hydrolysis, esterification and oxidation rather than to the ER regulatory pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2391814053096038, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22290946911416515, "cosine_similarity": 0.31670759437932916, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6023721682847897, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2391814053096038, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22290946911416515, "cosine_similarity": 0.31670759437932916, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6023721682847897, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.279665, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 69}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the reported log fold changes are kept in their unspecified logarithm base and only relative ordering within this list is used.", "Transcript abundance for hydrolases and routing factors is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding protein amount and enzymatic or fusion activity; this is not shown here and the protein-spot data do not confirm it.", "Protein spots have 3-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8) and are treated as ambiguous; no spot is used as identification of a specific protein.", "The endolysosomal compartment expansion, hydrolytic flux, ceramide accumulation, lipid localisation and causal direction are inferred, not measured; no lipid, enzyme-activity, flux or imaging measurement is present in this dataset.", "Genotype effects are assumed to be cell-intrinsic to microglia rather than caused by APOE4-dependent differences in the co-cultured astrocytes, differentiation state or cell-composition of the day-30 cultures.", "The down-regulated routing set was selected post hoc from the negative tail; it is used descriptively and no enrichment claim is made for it.", "The built-in Agent tool was not available in this session, so all analysis was performed by this single session with local Python; no external literature, database or independent reviewer was consulted, and any pathway membership statements come from unverified background knowledge."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, a TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR transcriptional program preferentially raises transcripts for luminal hydrolases that convert sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids into ceramide (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLA, GBA2) and for acidification machinery, while transcripts of the vesicular routing and egress arm (STX17, M6PR, AP1M1, STX16, RAB27A, VAMP2) are decreased and the ceramide re-glycosylation/sphingoid-exit steps are not co-induced (B4GALT5 down, SGPL1 and CERK only marginally up). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 cells is therefore disposal of lysosome-generated ceramide/sphingoid species and export of degraded lipid cargo, not hydrolase transcription, so sphingolipid intermediates are predicted to accumulate in an expanded endolysosomal compartment and to sustain lipogenic (SREBF1/SCD) and innate-immune (CXCL8, CCL2, NLRP3) tone. Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (flux versus capacity): pulse-chase of a traceable sphingolipid substrate (for example NBD/BODIPY-sphingomyelin or -glucosylceramide) in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show slower in-cell clearance and greater retention of label in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4, even though GBA, acid sphingomyelinase and beta-hexosaminidase Vmax measured in cell lysates at acidic pH are equal or higher in APOE4. If in-cell clearance is faster in APOE4 in proportion to the higher lysate enzyme activity, the bottleneck is not post-hydrolytic disposal and the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (substrate reduction test of the sphingolipid focus): partial UGCG inhibition (for example Genz-123346 or eliglustat) or ASAH1 over-expression should lower hexosylceramide/GM2 and ceramide, shrink the LAMP1/LysoTracker-positive compartment, and blunt the APOE4-specific induction of GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB and CXCL8 toward APOE3 levels. If the CLEAR/hydrolase transcript induction and lysosomal expansion persist unchanged under substrate reduction, sphingolipid load is not the driver and this mechanism should be rejected in favour of a sterol-load or general catabolic/OXPHOS explanation.", "Discriminating perturbation 3 (routing arm): restoring egress - re-expression of STX17, or stimulating Ca2+-dependent lysosomal exocytosis with an MCOLN1 agonist (ML-SA1) - should reduce lysosomal ceramide/hexosylceramide and lower CXCL8 and CCL2 in APOE4 without further raising hydrolase transcripts. No change in lipid retention after these manipulations would weaken step 4.", "Direct lipid prediction: quantitative lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia (and of LAMP1-immunoisolated fractions) should show higher ceramide (C16:0 and C24:1) and higher hexosylceramide and GM2 with a lower sphingomyelin-to-ceramide ratio in APOE4. Equal or lower ceramide and hexosylceramide in APOE4 would falsify the central claim.", "Protein-level prediction: immunoblot or targeted proteomics with unambiguous antibodies should show mature GBA, acid sphingomyelinase and HEXB protein increased in APOE4 lysosomal fractions in the same direction as their transcripts. Persistent absence of protein increase - as suggested by the decreased ambiguous spots protein_spot:067 (HEXB among candidates) and protein_spot:064/protein_spot:065 (ATP6V1E1 among candidates) - would instead support a translational or delivery block upstream of step 2 and would require the mechanism to be reformulated.", "Specificity prediction: the same manipulations should not equalise the OXPHOS/mitochondrial transcript module between genotypes; if UGCG inhibition normalises the mitochondrial module as strongly as the lysosomal one, the sphingolipid framing is not the primary axis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia show coordinated up-regulation of a CLEAR-type endolysosomal program - TFEB (+2.38) and MITF (+1.03) transcripts, v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51), LAMP1 (+1.38), RAB7A (+2.65) and cathepsins B/D/K - which we interpret as increased endolysosomal biogenesis and acidification capacity, an inference not directly measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): within this program the ceramide-generating luminal hydrolases are among the most extreme induced rows in the supplied differential-expression list - GBA (+6.71, 98th percentile of the RNA effects), SMPD1 (+5.63), HEXA (+5.68), HEXB (+2.17), GM2A (+2.01), GLA (+1.53), GBA2 (+2.63), with the ceramide/glycolipid transfer protein GLTP (+2.38); we infer, but did not measure, increased capacity for sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and GM2 hydrolysis to ceramide.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts, inferred flux imbalance): the routes that consume ceramide or export sphingoid products are not scaled to that input - B4GALT5 (LacCer synthase) is decreased (-1.88), SGPL1 (+1.09) and CERK (+1.23) are only marginally raised, and the de-novo/ceramidase arm (SPTLC1/2, CERS1/2, DEGS1, SGMS1/2, UGCG, ASAH1, PSAP) is absent from the supplied rows, so the ceramide node is inferred to be the least-buffered step.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, inferred localisation/routing): transcripts for lysosome-directed fusion, sorting and exocytosis are decreased - STX17 (-2.06, autophagosome-lysosome fusion), M6PR (-1.72) and AP1M1 (-1.03) and STX16 (-4.06) (mannose-6-phosphate receptor sorting and endosome-to-TGN retrieval), RAB27A (-2.52) and VAMP2 (-1.85) (Ca2+-dependent lysosomal exocytosis) - predicting that both hydrolase delivery cycling and lipid-laden cargo clearance out of the compartment are limited even while hydrolase transcripts rise.", "Step 5 (predicted, unmeasured pool): the combination of high hydrolytic input and low egress is predicted to raise steady-state ceramide and hexosylceramide/GM2 inside LAMP1-positive membranes of APOE4 microglia; no lipid species was measured in this dataset, so this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts, inferred consequence): the predicted lysosomal lipid load is proposed to drive the accompanying compensatory lipogenic/esterification program (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, ABCA7 +2.14, APOE +1.24) and to keep an activated microglial tone (CXCL8 +3.11, CCL2 +2.12, NLRP3 +1.09, TREM2 +1.28, ITGAX +1.69, GPNMB +1.11); the direction of this link is assumed, not demonstrated."], "title": "APOE4 microglia induce a ceramide-generating lysosomal hydrolase module without matching sphingolipid egress, making post-hydrolytic lysosomal sphingolipid disposal the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20455636377063102, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1628897268447105, "cosine_similarity": 0.316048825443682, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6208090614886732, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20455636377063102, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1628897268447105, "cosine_similarity": 0.316048825443682, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6208090614886732, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60693425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 291}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Unverified background knowledge: SEL1L participates in HRD1-associated ERAD, DERL1 and EDEM1 support aspects of ER quality control, MLEC and UGGT1 participate in glycoprotein surveillance, and ER stress can influence lysosomal transcription. These functional assignments were not verified by literature or database retrieval.", "The SEL1L transcript decrease reduces functional SEL1L protein enough to limit substrate clearance; the other machinery remains sufficient for SEL1L restoration to be informative. Increased EDEM2 and UBE2J1 RNA (gene:EDEM2, gene:UBE2J1) may compensate and could invalidate this assumption.", "ERAD substrate supply persists, making reduced clearance consequential. Accumulated misfolded cargo, ER overload, altered secretion, molecular lipid pools and lipid flux are predictions or unknowns, not supplied observations.", "The selected RNA rows do not represent an unbiased transcriptome: their broadly positive direction cannot establish a global increase in cellular RNA. The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is not assumed to be base 2. Absence from these selected rows does not imply unchanged or absent expression.", "Every protein spot has multiple candidate genes, so no spot establishes SEL1L, chaperone or lysosomal protein abundance. Protein significance flags and nominal p-value thresholds also disagree for some supplied spots.", "ER stress precedes at least part of the lysosomal transcriptional response rather than simply following a primary lysosomal or secretory-trafficking change. Cell-state composition, astrocyte-derived signals and technical differences do not fully explain the pattern; biological replicate information is unavailable."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced functional SEL1L-dependent ER-associated degradation (ERAD) is hypothesized to be the primary bottleneck: delayed disposal of ER quality-control substrates prolongs glycoprotein retention, impairs maturation of susceptible secretory cargo, and elicits compensatory stress and lysosomal transcription. The supplied abundance measurements motivate this mechanism but do not establish its causal direction.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In independent, matched mock co-cultures, APOE4 microglia should have lower specifically measured SEL1L protein and slower pulse-chase turnover of a validated luminal SEL1L-dependent ERAD reporter, after matching reporter synthesis, cell state and viability. An ERAD-independent degradation control should be relatively spared. Normal SEL1L abundance together with normal ERAD-reporter turnover would directly weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Microglia-restricted restoration of SEL1L to the APOE3 protein level in APOE4 should accelerate ERAD-reporter clearance and subsequently improve Endo H-resistant maturation and extracellular recovery of an independently validated N-glycosylated secretory reporter, normalized to synthesis and viability. Reciprocal partial SEL1L depletion in APOE3 should reproduce these defects. Failure of SEL1L restoration despite confirmed protein restoration and HRD1 association would weaken SEL1L as the primary limiting component; clearance rescue without cargo-maturation rescue would weaken the proposed secretion consequence.", "Compare SEL1L restoration with SEC24D restoration, motivated by lower SEC24D RNA (gene:SEC24D). A primary SEL1L-dependent clearance defect predicts that SEL1L restoration corrects ERAD-reporter turnover before improving stress and cargo-transit readouts; SEC24D restoration may improve export without correcting that turnover. Rescue of the full phenotype by SEC24D alone, with no effective SEL1L rescue, would favor a primary export defect and weaken this mechanism.", "If clearance failure drives the stress and lysosomal program, restoration of reporter turnover should precede reduced biochemical ER-stress readouts, such as cleaved ATF6 or phosphorylated PERK, and later attenuation of DDIT3, TFEB, GAA and CTSB transcription. No biochemical stress increase at baseline, or persistence of the lysosomal program across an adequate time course after clearance and stress normalize, would weaken the claimed downstream connection and favor an independent cell-state or lysosomal response."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Lower SEL1L RNA, accompanied by lower DERL1 and EDEM1 RNA (gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1), is hypothesized to reduce functional SEL1L-dependent ERAD capacity. These observations measure transcripts, not component protein abundance or degradation activity.", "If ERAD clearance is limiting, quality-control substrates should persist longer in the ER. Higher MLEC and UGGT1 RNA (gene:MLEC, gene:UGGT1) is compatible with increased glycoprotein surveillance, but neither an accumulated substrate pool nor prolonged ER residence was measured.", "Persistent ER quality-control burden is predicted to delay productive maturation and secretion of susceptible glycoprotein cargo. This is a downstream consequence of the proposed clearance bottleneck; cargo localization, glycan maturation and secretion were not measured.", "The retained-substrate burden is proposed to engage ER stress signaling. Higher EIF2AK3, ATF6 and DDIT3 RNA (gene:EIF2AK3, gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3) is compatible with this response but does not demonstrate PERK activation, ATF6 cleavage or any specific active unfolded-protein-response branch.", "The resulting stress is proposed to promote a compensatory lysosomal transcriptional program, consistent with higher TFEB, GAA and CTSB RNA (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB). TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal enzyme activity and degradative flux remain unmeasured."], "title": "SEL1L-limited ER quality-control clearance in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0663558307966642, "cosine_similarity": 0.31591653415995535, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6022135922330097, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13013698630136986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0663558307966642, "cosine_similarity": 0.31591653415995535, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6022135922330097, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.9209985, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_025", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705/2212 = 77% positive), so program coherence is judged against that 77% positive background, not 50/50; absent genes (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, ATF4, ERN1, NPC1, ABCA1, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative magnitudes are used. Protein spots are log2.", "Elevated transcripts for hydrolases, v-ATPase and SREBP targets indicate transcriptional program state, not measured enzymatic activity, protein amount, lysosomal pH or sterol flux; SREBP cleavage and the ER-accessible cholesterol pool were not measured and are inferred.", "Co-induction of SREBP-target and oxysterol/LXR-target transcripts is interpreted as compartmentalised sterol (endolysosome-rich, ER-poor); this interpretation is background knowledge (unverified here) and is not proven by the supplied data.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate identities each; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Lysosomal-hydrolase-candidate spots go both up (protein_spot:052, :053, :055) and down (protein_spot:058, :067, :069), so spot data are compatibility evidence only.", "Genes within a program are correlated and were chosen from standard pathway membership before looking at their signs; the counts are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test with independence.", "The described state is the ongoing mock (unchallenged) condition; any inadequacy of lysosomal capacity relative to load is a prediction about future lipid challenge, not an observed defect here."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3), the dominant difference is not a canonical unfolded-protein response but a coordinated re-routing of lipid handling: transcripts for the TFEB/MITF-driven endolysosomal degradative compartment and for lipid uptake are coherently higher (gene:TFEB 2.38, gene:MITF 1.03, gene:GBA 6.71, gene:HEXA 5.68, gene:SMPD1 5.63, gene:CTSB 5.52, gene:GAA 9.96, gene:ATP6V1A 4.23, gene:SCARB1 8.22, gene:CD36 1.38, reported log FC, base unspecified), yet SREBP-target sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and LDLR-axis transcripts are simultaneously higher (gene:SREBF2 1.06, gene:INSIG1 1.87, gene:HMGCS1 1.08, gene:LSS 2.27, gene:DHCR24 3.69, gene:LDLR 1.50) together with oxysterol/LXR-output genes (gene:CH25H 1.62, gene:CYP27A1 1.49, gene:ABCA7 2.14, gene:APOE 1.24, gene:MYLIP 1.28). Co-elevation of an ER-sterol-deficit program with an oxysterol/efflux program is the signature expected when sterol is compartmentalised away from the ER-accessible pool rather than when cells simply have more cholesterol available; the state is accompanied by lower glycolytic/PPP transcripts (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) and uniformly higher TCA/oxidative transcripts (gene:MPC2 7.98, gene:OGDH 8.56, gene:MDH1 8.72, gene:ACO2 3.54, gene:HADHA 2.86). We propose that mislocalised, endolysosome-retained sterol/sphingolipid is the causal node linking these programs. This is a transcript- and spot-level inference; no flux, sterol pool, enzymatic activity or localisation was measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, imaging of free cholesterol (filipin) plus an ER-accessible-sterol probe (ALOD4/D4H) should show increased sterol in LAMP1+ compartments with an equal or reduced ER-accessible pool. If the ER-accessible pool is equal or higher in APOE4 while SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated, the sterol-mislocalisation node is weakened and a sensing-independent activation program is favoured.", "Prospective: nuclear/cleaved SREBP-2 should be increased in APOE4; if nuclear SREBP-2 is unchanged despite elevated gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, then the transcript rise is not driven by ER sterol sensing and mechanism step 3 fails.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: mobilising sequestered sterol with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or acute statin-independent sterol loading of the ER) should selectively normalise the SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR) in APOE4 toward APOE3 without abolishing the CLEAR/hydrolase elevation; if cyclodextrin leaves SREBP targets elevated, or collapses both programs equally, the proposed feed-forward loop is wrong.", "Prospective: TFEB knockdown should lower hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts in both genotypes and, if the loop is real, should increase neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would argue the lysosomal arm is incidental.", "Prospective metabolic test: extracellular flux measurement should show lower glycolytic rate and lower PPP flux ([1,2-13C]glucose) with higher fatty-acid-dependent oxygen consumption in mock APOE4; unchanged or higher glycolysis would weaken step 5 while leaving the lipid-routing core intact.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not current defect): after myelin or oxLDL loading, APOE4 should clear cholesteryl ester more slowly and accumulate more droplets than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance would indicate successful adaptation/increased throughput rather than a compensating but insufficient program.", "Prospective negative control for the rejected focus: ER stress reporters (XBP1 splicing, HSPA5 protein, ATF4/CHOP protein) should not differ substantially between mock APOE4 and APOE3; a clear constitutive UPR difference would favour the assigned ER-proteostasis explanation over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein (transcript gene:APOE 1.24 higher) alters lipoprotein/lipid particle handling by microglia; together with higher scavenger/uptake receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 8.22, gene:CD36 1.38, other phagocytic/scavenger receptor transcripts gene:MRC1 1.36, gene:STAB1 1.13, gene:TREM2 1.28) this increases delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endocytic route (inferred routing, not measured uptake).", "Cargo is retained in the late-endosome/lysosome, and a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR program is engaged: higher transcripts for acid hydrolases (gene:GBA 6.71, gene:HEXA 5.68, gene:HEXB 2.17, gene:SMPD1 5.63, gene:NAGLU 5.91, gene:GAA 9.96, gene:CTSB 5.52, gene:CTSD 2.86, gene:CTSK 7.36, gene:MAN2B1 1.81, gene:DPP7 4.52), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A 4.23, gene:ATP6V1E1 1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 1.68, gene:ATP6AP1 2.30) and compartment machinery (gene:LAMP1 1.38, gene:RAB7A 2.65, gene:SCARB2 1.06, gene:NPC2 1.17, gene:VPS26A 4.86, gene:PIK3C3 2.92), i.e. expanded degradative capacity (capacity inferred; hydrolase activity and lysosomal pH not measured).", "Because sterol is held in this compartment, export to the ER-accessible pool is limited, so the ER sterol sensor continues to signal deficiency: SREBP-2/SREBP-1 target transcripts stay elevated (gene:SREBF1 4.67, gene:SREBF2 1.06, gene:INSIG1 1.87 as a direct-target readout, gene:HMGCS1 1.08, gene:LSS 2.27, gene:DHCR7 2.71, gene:DHCR24 3.69, gene:EBP 1.34, gene:ACAT2 2.04, gene:SCD 4.17, gene:FADS1 1.59, gene:LDLR 1.50). SREBP proteolytic activation and nuclear SREBP-2 were not measured; ER-to-Golgi machinery is represented (gene:COPA 4.27, gene:COPE 4.33, gene:COPB1 1.04, gene:RAB1B 1.67) but gene:SEC24D is -1.39.", "Simultaneously the sequestered/oxidised sterol pool drives oxysterol-generating and LXR-output transcripts (gene:CH25H 1.62, gene:CYP27A1 1.49, gene:ABCA7 2.14, gene:APOE 1.24, gene:MYLIP 1.28) and esterification/storage genes (gene:SOAT1 1.25, gene:DGAT1 1.72), so synthesis, uptake and storage run together instead of being switched off - a feed-forward loop that keeps lipid entering the same compartment.", "The resulting lipid-loaded, phagocytic-activated cell state shows lower glycolytic/PPP transcripts (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:NAMPT -2.62, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) and uniformly higher TCA/beta-oxidation transcripts (gene:MPC2 7.98, gene:OGDH 8.56, gene:MDH1 8.72, gene:DLD 5.54, gene:SLC25A1 4.47, gene:ACO2 3.54, gene:HADHA 2.86, gene:ETFA 3.55, gene:ACOX1 1.24), consistent with carbon being routed to mitochondrial oxidation rather than to glucose-derived biosynthesis (flux not measured).", "Membrane/phospholipid-binding and cortical-actin machinery is co-remodelled with this state: gene:ANXA1 4.15 with a train of strongly increased protein spots whose candidate lists include ANXA1 (protein_spot:043 1.96, protein_spot:044 2.38, protein_spot:045 3.05, protein_spot:046 2.81, log2), and multiple increased actin/ARP2/3/tropomyosin-candidate spots (protein_spot:028, protein_spot:029, protein_spot:036, protein_spot:052), compatible with an engulfment/membrane-trafficking-biased phenotype. Spot identities are ambiguous (each spot lists 2-6 candidates) and are used only as compatibility evidence."], "title": "APOE4 routes lipid into an expanded endolysosomal compartment while ER sterol sensing still reports deficit, sustaining a feed-forward sterol synthesis/uptake state with oxidative-metabolic reprogramming"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14481409001956946, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09827816337077785, "cosine_similarity": 0.31559790115905345, "direction_accuracy": 0.23948220064724918, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_025", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5990711974110032, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14481409001956946, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09827816337077785, "cosine_similarity": 0.31559790115905345, "direction_accuracy": 0.23948220064724918, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5990711974110032, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.50746375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 70}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_038", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are pre-selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of UGCG, ASAH1, PSAP, SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, GALC, NEU1, NPC1, LIPA and GRN rows is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "The reported RNA log fold changes use an unspecified logarithm base and are not rescaled here; because 77% of rows are positive (median +1.46), only percentile rank within the supplied distribution is treated as informative, and |effect| is essentially uncorrelated with adjusted p (r = -0.04), so magnitudes are treated as noisy.", "2D protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are used only as absence-of-corroboration, never as evidence that a named hydrolase protein changed.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, pH, or imaging measurement is supplied; all statements about sphingolipid pools, hydrolytic flux, membrane localisation and storage are inferences.", "Transcript increases in a catabolic arm are assumed to indicate a compensatory response to substrate load rather than a primary increase in clearance capacity; the opposite direction is a live alternative.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 but in astrocyte co-culture with unstated replicate number, so genotype-driven differences in microglial state or cell-composition sampling (10X Flex) could contribute."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a selective, top-of-distribution increase in transcripts for the three lysosomal enzymes that clear the major sphingolipid classes (GBA for glucosylceramide, HEXA/HEXB with GM2A for GM2/GA2, SMPD1 for sphingomyelin), together with increased scavenger-receptor and endosome-maturation/retromer transcripts, while transcripts for de novo ceramide synthesis sit at the global background, lactosylceramide synthase B4GALT5 and the CD-MPR sorting receptor M6PR are among the few down rows, and the ambiguous 2D protein spots containing cathepsin and v-ATPase candidates split in both directions. We hypothesise that this signature reflects a compensatory (substrate-driven) CLEAR-type response to an increased sphingolipid load reaching the late endosome/lysosome, and that the rate-limiting step is luminal sphingolipid hydrolysis capacity per delivered substrate rather than hydrolase transcription; the unhydrolysed glycosphingolipid load is proposed to slow endolysosomal cargo turnover and to bias APOE4 microglia toward re-esterified neutral-lipid storage (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SCD, SREBF1 transcripts up). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological substrate reduction with a glucosylceramide-synthase (UGCG) inhibitor (e.g. eliglustat/GENZ-123346) applied to APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should lower GlcCer/LacCer/GM2 by lipidomics and, if the transcript program is substrate-driven, should selectively collapse the APOE4-over-APOE3 excess of GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD and ATP6V1H transcripts and of LAMP1-positive lysosomal area, while leaving the sterol/lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, SOAT1, DGAT1) comparatively unchanged. If UGCG inhibition depletes glycosphingolipid but the APOE4 hydrolase/CLEAR transcript excess and lysosomal expansion persist, the substrate-driven compensatory step is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Activity-versus-transcript test: enzymatic assays (4-MU-glucoside for GBA, 4-MU-GlcNAc for HEXA/B, fluorogenic SMPD1) normalised to LAMP1 or to total lysosome number should show APOE4 activity equal to or below APOE3 despite the higher transcripts, with mass-spectrometry lipidomics showing elevated GlcCer, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin in APOE4. Proportionally increased activity together with reduced or unchanged GlcCer/GM2 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Sensitisation test: partial GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) or HEXA/B knockdown should produce a larger increase in GlcCer/GM2, in lysosomal volume and in neutral-lipid droplet area in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 cells; equal sensitivity across genotypes would argue the sphingolipid step is not closer to saturation in APOE4.", "Delivery/maturation test: pulse-chase of newly synthesised GBA and HEXA (and CI-/CD-MPR-dependent sorting) should show a longer transit to the LAMP1 compartment or increased secretion of immature enzyme into the medium in APOE4, consistent with the down M6PR row; equal maturation kinetics and equal secreted-hydrolase fraction would weaken step 3 and shift the mechanism toward simple lysosome biogenesis.", "Causal-direction test: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase transcript excess and, if the response is genuinely compensatory, aggravate glycosphingolipid and neutral-lipid accumulation preferentially in APOE4; if TFEB knockdown reduces lipid accumulation instead, the compensatory interpretation is inverted.", "Specificity test: targeted immunoblot of GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSD and ATP6V1E1 (replacing the ambiguous 2D spots) should show hydrolase protein increases that are smaller than the transcript differences; protein increases matching or exceeding the transcript differences would remove the transcript-protein mismatch that this hypothesis rests on."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry elevated lipid-uptake/scavenger transcripts (gene:SCARB1, 99th percentile of the supplied distribution; gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2), which we infer - not measure - increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived sphingolipid to the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): Transcripts encoding the three principal lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase activities are each in the top 5% of the supplied differential-expression distribution (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1), with the cofactor/partner subunits also above the global median (gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2, gene:GLTP), while de novo ceramide-synthesis transcripts sit at or below the global median (gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:ORMDL2). We read this as a catabolic-arm-selective transcriptional response, not activated biosynthesis.", "Step 3 (measured RNA + measured spots, inferred protein activity): The transcriptional response is not corroborated at the protein level. No supplied protein spot uniquely identifies a sphingolipid hydrolase; spots whose candidate lists contain hydrolase or v-ATPase subunits change in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), and the cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript is one of the few down rows (gene:M6PR, 15th percentile) despite gene:GNPTG and gene:IGF2R being up. We therefore infer that mature, correctly delivered hydrolase activity does not scale with transcript.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, inferred): Luminal hydrolysis of glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin per unit delivered substrate becomes the limiting step. Glycosphingolipid is retained in late-endosomal/lysosomal limiting membranes; this is a flux/localisation claim and no lipid species was measured in the supplied data.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred compensation): Retained cargo drives a coherent endosome-maturation and recycling response (gene:RAB7A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB up; retromer/Commander set gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:VPS35L, gene:CCDC22 with median rank in the 79th percentile), together with a shifted glycosphingolipid-headgroup routing signature (gene:ST3GAL5 up, gene:B4GALT5 down).", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred lipid outcome): Lipid that is not cleared through the sphingolipid catabolic route is inferred to be re-esterified and stored, consistent with increased gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:SCD and gene:SREBF1 transcripts, producing the APOE4-specific lipid-accumulation phenotype in the absence of any treatment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a transcript-level lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic response (GBA/HEXA-HEXB-GM2A/SMPD1) that is not matched at the hydrolase-delivery and protein level, making luminal glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin hydrolysis the limiting step and diverting lipid into neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27307720710408745, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18141743047575926, "cosine_similarity": 0.31425753321045075, "direction_accuracy": 0.24757281553398058, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6428964401294498, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27307720710408745, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18141743047575926, "cosine_similarity": 0.31425753321045075, "direction_accuracy": 0.24757281553398058, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6428964401294498, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8108415, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 292}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect values are reported log fold changes of unspecified logarithm base; only ranks and within-list relative positions, not absolute fold changes, are used.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive), so the apparent global up-shift is at least partly a selection artefact; enrichment claims are made relative to this list's own median/mean, not to a whole transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for hydrolase protein and catalytic capacity; no enzyme activity, protein-level hydrolase quantity, pH, or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel-type features with multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot changes are treated as ambiguous isoform/charge-state redistribution, not as protein abundance of a named gene.", "Ceramide, glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin, sphingosine and S1P pools are inferred, never observed; the bottleneck step relies on genes (ASAH1, ACER3, SGMS1/2, CERT1, SPHK1/2, PSAP, UGCG, SPTLC1/2) that are absent from the supplied rows, so absence of amplification there is unverified for those genes.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; the supplied contrast cannot separate cell-autonomous APOE4 effects from astrocyte-derived lipid supply, and no replicate count or dispersion is supplied.", "The comparison is a single timepoint (day 30) under mock treatment, so steady-state imbalance rather than a kinetic response is assumed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally amplify the lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic input arm (GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA, SMPD1) far above the pervasive upward shift of this differential-expression list, while the terminal ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal and re-routing arm (SGPL1, CERS6, KDSR, CERK; ASAH1, ACER3, SGMS1/2, CERT1, SPHK1/2 not measured) is not co-amplified. We hypothesise that the resulting imbalance, not hydrolase supply, is the rate-limiting step: ceramide/sphingoid intermediates are predicted to accumulate in late endosomes/lysosomes and bias membrane traffic away from tubular recycling and secretory egress (RAB27A, STX12, CTSS lower) toward degradative retention (RAB7A, VPS18, CHMP4B, VPS26A, SNX3 higher), with lipogenic/esterification transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1) acting as an overflow route. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (bottleneck test): in APOE4 microglia, raising terminal ceramide/sphingoid disposal capacity - acid ceramidase (ASAH1) overexpression, SGPL1 overexpression, or CerS blockade with fumonisin B1 to prevent salvage re-acylation - should lower endolysosomal ceramide/HexCer (lipidomics or BODIPY-ceramide), restore lysosomal tubulation and recycling/exocytic egress (Rab27a/Rab11 cargo release, dextran or LysoTracker efflux), and normalise degradative throughput, WITHOUT reducing GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 transcript or activity levels. If disposal capacity is raised, ceramide falls, and egress/recycling remains APOE4-like, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Substrate-demand test: reducing glycosphingolipid substrate load with a UGCG inhibitor (eliglustat/PPMP) should blunt the APOE4-specific excess of GBA/HEXA/HEXB/GM2A transcripts toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the full hydrolase excess after substrate depletion would weaken step 3 (compensatory-demand induction) and favour a substrate-independent TFEB-driven program.", "Co-occurrence test: direct assay should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for lysosomal GBA/HEXA/ASM enzymatic activity per cell AND simultaneously higher ceramide/HexCer and higher ceramide:sphingosine-1-phosphate ratio. If activity is higher while ceramide and HexCer are unchanged or lower in APOE4, the imbalance claim is falsified even though the transcript observations stand.", "Directionality test: acute inhibition of GBA (conduritol-B-epoxide) or SMPD1 (amitriptyline) in APOE4 microglia should shift the lipid profile from ceramide toward its glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin precursors and partially relieve, not worsen, the egress/recycling defect. Worsening of egress under these inhibitors would support a substrate-storage (Gaucher/NPC-like) bottleneck upstream of ceramide instead.", "Protein-level prediction: the bidirectional cathepsin-candidate spots (protein_spot:027, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down) should resolve, by targeted immunoblot, into a redistribution between pro- and mature CTSB/CTSD/HEXB forms with little change in total protein. A uniform decrease in total cathepsin and HEXB protein in APOE4 would instead indicate reduced hydrolase delivery and would contradict step 2/3.", "Negative/scope prediction: de novo sphingolipid synthesis flux (stable-isotope serine/palmitate labelling into dihydroceramide) should NOT be substantially higher in APOE4, consistent with the non-enriched synthesis arm here (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:ORMDL2; SPTLC1/2 unmeasured). A large de novo flux increase would move the mechanism from catabolic imbalance to synthesis-driven ceramide gain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, 99th percentile of this list; gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), which we infer increases delivery of sphingolipid-containing membrane and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system. Lipid influx itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred program activity): A TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis signature is elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:IGF2R), which we infer increases hydrolase delivery and lumenal acidification capacity; neither v-ATPase activity nor pH was measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred enzymatic capacity): Within this catabolic program, sphingolipid-specific hydrolase transcripts are selectively extreme (gene:GBA +6.71, 98th pct; gene:HEXA +5.68, 96th pct; gene:SMPD1 +5.63, 95th pct; gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA; set mean +4.37 vs list mean +1.39, permutation p=1e-4), inferring increased lumenal conversion of glucosyl-/ganglio-series glycosphingolipids and sphingomyelin to ceramide.", "Step 4 (bottleneck; inferred pool, not observed): The disposal/exit arm is not co-amplified - gene:SGPL1 (+1.09, 29th pct), gene:CERS6 (26th pct), gene:KDSR (41st pct), gene:CERK (38th pct) sit below the median of this up-shifted list, and ASAH1, ACER3, SGMS1/2, CERT1, SPHK1/2 are absent from the supplied rows. We therefore predict a stoichiometric mismatch in which ceramide and free sphingoid bases accumulate in late endosome/lysosome membranes. No lipid species was measured; this pool is inferred, not observed.", "Step 5 (inferred membrane behaviour and localization): Ceramide-enriched, rigidified endolysosomal membranes are predicted to impair tubulation, budding and fusion-competent egress. The transcriptome is consistent with such a routing bias: fusion/maturation and retromer/ESCRT components rise (gene:RAB7A, gene:RAB7B, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B) while recycling/secretory-arm transcripts fall or lag (gene:RAB27A -2.52, 8th pct; gene:STX12 23rd pct; gene:CTSS -5.57, 1st pct; gene:B4GALT5 -1.88; gene:IDS -1.56). Localization and vesicle flux were not measured.", "Step 6 (compensation): Overflow of undegraded/undelivered lipid is predicted to be buffered by esterification and de novo lipogenesis transcripts (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1), giving a lipid-laden, degradation-competent but egress-limited APOE4 microglial endolysosome rather than a globally hypofunctional lysosome."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matching ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal, creating a ceramide-limited endolysosomal egress bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21185799209836428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15219674100184546, "cosine_similarity": 0.3130187692086715, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.630252427184466, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21185799209836428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15219674100184546, "cosine_similarity": 0.3130187692086715, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.630252427184466, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.97781775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 293}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_035", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 positive; 87% positive among the best-powered rows). Program directions are judged against that ~77-87% positive background, not against 50/50. Genes absent from the list (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, CALR, CANX, NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified ('reported log fold change'); all RNA effects are kept on that scale and are not converted. Protein spots are log2. The two scales are not compared numerically.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for pathway capacity, not for activity or flux. SREBP proteolytic processing, LXR ligand occupancy, TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity, cholesterol pool sizes and cargo degradation rates were not measured in this dataset.", "Program membership was assigned from canonical pathway knowledge (unverified background) before inspecting member directions; members were not dropped to make signs agree, and the discordant members (CTSS, IDS, CR1, mitochondrially encoded OXPHOS subunits) are retained and reported.", "Descriptive coherence within these modules is not a formal enrichment test; genes within a module are co-regulated and therefore not independent, so binomial-style counts overstate significance.", "Each 2D-gel spot carries 2-6 candidate identities (median 5). No spot is treated as confirmation of a named protein; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction.", "APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences here are measured under mock treatment only. Any degradative or buffering deficit that would appear only under a lipid or phagocytic challenge is a future-challenge prediction, not an observed defect in this condition.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins and debris; the inferred cargo routing assumes such substrate is present, which was not measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 not by an unfolded-protein/ER-chaperone response but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for scavenger/phagocytic receptors, for a near-uniform CLEAR-type lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module, and for neutral-lipid esterification are all elevated, while ER-sterol-sensor-dependent (SREBP-target) cholesterol-synthesis and LDLR transcripts are simultaneously elevated rather than suppressed. We propose that internalized and endogenous sterol is preferentially routed into an expanded endolysosomal/cholesteryl-ester storage compartment so that the ER-accessible sterol pool is not repleted; the persistent uptake-plus-synthesis-plus-esterification program is therefore self-reinforcing and is accompanied by reduced expression of the leukocyte surface-receptor and actomyosin-motility module. Sterol pool sizes, SREBP proteolytic activation, LXR occupancy and lysosomal degradative flux were NOT measured here; only transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances were.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, discriminating: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, filipin/ER-sterol-reporter imaging plus lipidomics should show increased cholesteryl ester and neutral lipid in LAMP1-positive and droplet compartments with NO increase (or a decrease) in the ER-accessible free-sterol pool. If APOE4 cells instead show an equal or larger ER-accessible sterol pool, STEP 4 fails and the mechanism is wrong.", "PROSPECTIVE: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester mass AND normalize the SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS) toward APOE3 levels, because blocking esterification returns sterol to the ER sensor. If cholesteryl ester falls but SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated, the proposed routing step is not what sustains the synthesis program.", "PROSPECTIVE: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce CLEAR transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A/H). If lipid load then FALLS, lysosomal expansion was part of the storage state (supports this mechanism); if lipid load RISES, the expansion was compensatory to a degradative deficit and the 'routing/storage state' framing should be replaced by failed compensation.", "PROSPECTIVE, distinguishing adaptation from defect: pulse-chase of fluorescent oxLDL or myelin in mock culture should show APOE4 cells internalizing MORE cargo but hydrolysing a similar or greater absolute amount per cell (successful high-throughput handling with retained ester product). If APOE4 cells show slower per-cell hydrolysis with unchanged uptake, the mechanism should be revised from 'routing to storage' to 'lysosomal catabolic bottleneck'.", "PROSPECTIVE, rejects the ER-proteostasis alternative: BiP/GRP94/PDI protein levels, XBP1 splicing and ATF4/CHOP reporter output should NOT be substantially elevated in mock APOE4 versus APOE3. Detection of frank UPR activation (spliced XBP1, elevated BiP protein, translational attenuation) would support an ER-proteostasis mechanism over this one.", "PROSPECTIVE, cell-state prediction: APOE4 microglia should show reduced process motility/chemotactic migration and reduced surface CD45/CD43 protein under mock conditions, matching STEP 6. Equal migration and equal surface CD45 would show the transcript downshift is not translated into a state change and would weaken STEP 6 without necessarily affecting STEPS 1-4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred routing): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipoprotein/debris scavenging and opsonic receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:FCGR1A, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:GPNMB), which we infer increases delivery of lipid-bearing cargo to the endolysosomal system. Cargo flux itself was not measured.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA): A CLEAR/TFEB-type lysosomal module is coherently up (26 of 28 represented members positive: gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, and v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V0D2), indicating transcriptional expansion of acidic degradative compartment capacity. Exceptions gene:CTSS (-5.6) and gene:IDS (-1.6).", "STEP 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Esterification/storage enzymes are co-induced (gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1), so sterol and fatty acid reaching the ER/droplet interface are inferred to be converted to cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol and retained rather than kept as ER-accessible free sterol.", "STEP 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensor state): Despite the scavenging program, every represented SREBP-target/sterol-synthesis gene is positive (13/13: gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:ACSS2, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD, gene:MYLIP), the pattern expected when the ER SCAP/INSIG sensor reads a sterol-poor ER membrane. Concurrent elevation of late-endosome/oxysterol-linked LXR targets (gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP) indicates the two sterol-sensing compartments are reading different pools. SREBP cleavage and LXR activity were not measured.", "STEP 5 (predicted lipid consequence): Sustained uptake plus sustained synthesis plus esterification creates a feed-forward loop whose expected output in the same mock condition is increased neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content in LAMP1-positive and droplet compartments, i.e. a foam-cell-like lipid-laden APOE4 microglia. No lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "STEP 6 (measured RNA, cell-state cost): The same cells coordinately reduce a leukocyte surface-receptor/ITAM-ITIM signaling and actomyosin motility module (16 of 19 and 11 of 20 represented members negative against a 77%-positive list background: gene:PTPRC, gene:SPN -7.3, gene:SELL, gene:CD52, gene:CD69, gene:PTPN6, gene:CSK, gene:HCK, gene:SASH3, gene:RASAL3, gene:LAPTM5, gene:LST1, gene:CD300LF, gene:SIGLEC5, gene:RGS1, gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:ACTB -5.0, gene:MYO1F, gene:VASP, gene:RAC2, gene:ARHGDIB, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:TMSB10), consistent with a trade of motile immune-effector identity for a storage/degradative state rather than with generalized activation.", "STEP 7 (compatibility, protein spots, identities unresolved): 2D-gel spots do not show uniform proportional increases of lysosomal hydrolase protein; spots whose candidate lists contain CTSD or CTSB change in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.58, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:067 -1.00), which is compatible with redistribution among proteoforms (pro- versus mature, glycoforms) inside an expanded compartment, but each spot has 2-6 candidate identities and none of these proteins is individually confirmed."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-and-storage-biased scavenger state in which sterol is routed away from the ER sensing pool, so uptake and sterol-synthesis programs stay on while leukocyte surface-signaling/motility identity is downshifted"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38450319388546317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27745955693762364, "cosine_similarity": 0.311846539683058, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6423689320388349, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38450319388546317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.27745955693762364, "cosine_similarity": 0.311846539683058, "direction_accuracy": 0.2896440129449838, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6423689320388349, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.64299375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 71}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA log-fold-change direction (APOE4 vs APOE3) approximates the direction of the corresponding protein's synthesis rate; this is not verified by matched protein data for most genes.", "The discovery gene list is a pre-filtered significant/large-effect differential expression list (all |logFC|\u003e~1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05), so apparent pathway coherence must be judged against a background that is already ~77% positive-signed, not a neutral 50/50 expectation.", "Increased ATF6/EIF2AK3/DDIT3 transcripts are treated as evidence of UPR transcriptional signaling, not as direct evidence of ATF6 cleavage, PERK kinase activity, or eIF2\u03b1 phosphorylation, none of which are measured here.", "Decreased SEL1L/DERL1/EDEM1 transcripts are treated as reduced ERAD-pathway transcriptional capacity, not as a directly measured reduction in ERAD substrate degradation flux.", "Protein-spot candidate-gene lists are treated as ambiguous; no single protein identity is confirmed from a multi-candidate spot.", "Missing genes (e.g., HSPA5, XBP1, CANX, CALR, HERPUD1) are treated as unmeasured/unknown in this selected list, not as unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional pattern in which unfolded-protein-response (UPR) sensors/effectors and general ER oxidative-folding/N-glycosylation machinery are increased while a subset of ERAD substrate-recognition/retrotranslocation genes are decreased; combined with an altered COPI/COPII trafficking gene balance, this pattern is more consistent with an unresolved, partially compensated proteostasis state than with a fully successful adaptive or purely inflammatory transcriptional program, and may contribute to reduced secretory/proteostatic reserve in APOE4 microglia at baseline.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating test: in isogenic APOE3/APOE4 microglia at this same baseline (mock) condition, measuring ERAD flux directly (e.g., cycloheximide-chase degradation kinetics of a model ERAD substrate, or ubiquitinated/glycosylated protein accumulation by pulse-chase) should show slower degradation and/or greater accumulation of misfolded glycoprotein species in APOE4 than APOE3. If ERAD flux is equal or faster in APOE4, this would weaken the proposed disposal-limited mechanism and favor a bystander or purely adaptive-upregulation interpretation instead.", "A second discriminating prediction: acute pharmacological ERAD inhibition (e.g., Eeyarestatin I or kifunensine) or an added proteotoxic challenge (tunicamycin/thapsigargin) should produce a disproportionately larger CHOP/BAX transcript increase and reduced viability in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, reflecting reduced proteostatic reserve; a similar-magnitude response in both genotypes would argue against a genotype-specific ERAD-capacity deficit and instead support a generalized transcriptional difference unrelated to secretory reserve."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with increased transcript levels of UPR sensor/effector genes ATF6, EIF2AK3 (PERK), and downstream effector DDIT3 (CHOP), indicating heightened UPR transcriptional output relative to APOE3 (gene:ATF6, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3).", "In parallel, transcripts for ERAD-specific substrate recognition and retrotranslocation components SEL1L, DERL1, and EDEM1 are reduced, while general ER oxidative-folding and N-glycosylation/glycoprotein-quality-control transcripts (STT3A, STT3B, RPN1, UGGT1, ERO1A, MLEC) are increased, with the ERAD paralog EDEM2 as a notable exception that is increased (gene:SEL1L, gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1, gene:EDEM2, gene:STT3A, gene:STT3B, gene:RPN1, gene:UGGT1, gene:ERO1A, gene:MLEC).", "This asymmetry (more folding/glycosylation-sensor capacity, less dedicated disposal capacity) is inferred, not directly measured, to slow clearance of terminally misfolded glycoproteins, allowing a larger client burden to persist in the ER lumen despite ongoing UPR signaling; no misfolded-protein load or ERAD flux assay is present in this dataset.", "Persistently elevated CHOP (DDIT3) transcript, together with increased BAX transcript, indicates a shift toward the pro-apoptotic arm of UPR output rather than a return to a resolved, low-stress transcriptional state (gene:DDIT3, gene:BAX); this reflects transcript-level priming, not measured caspase activity or cell death.", "A coordinated shift in vesicular trafficking transcripts -- increased COPI coat subunits (COPA, COPB1, COPE) and the Golgi ARF-GEF ARFGEF1, alongside decreased SEC24D (a COPII cargo-selective isoform) and decreased GOLPH3L -- suggests altered routing with relatively favored retrograde Golgi-to-ER retrieval versus a specific anterograde export component (gene:COPA, gene:COPB1, gene:COPE, gene:ARFGEF1, gene:SEC24D, gene:GOLPH3L); the identity and direction of the affected cargo class are not established by these data.", "Protein-spot data for candidate ER chaperones (HSP90B1, HSPA5, PDIA3) are ambiguous (multi-gene spots) and, where interpretable, are flat to negative rather than clearly increased (protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005, protein_spot:016), which does not confirm increased chaperone protein abundance and tempers a simple 'successful compensatory upregulation' reading.", "Net inference: the transcript-level pattern is more consistent with a partially compensated, disposal-limited proteostasis state in APOE4 microglia at baseline (mock) than with either full adaptive resolution of ER stress or a purely secondary bystander effect of generalized transcriptional upregulation; whether this constitutes an ongoing functional defect versus a latent vulnerability revealed only under additional proteotoxic challenge is not resolved by this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a maladaptive UPR configuration: coordinated increase of ER folding/glycosylation and stress-sensor transcripts alongside reduced ERAD disposal transcripts, favoring proteostatic imbalance over resolved adaptation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20058708414872797, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.023236728902550685, "cosine_similarity": 0.31084173284484506, "direction_accuracy": 0.3333333333333333, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5763106796116505, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20058708414872797, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.023236728902550685, "cosine_similarity": 0.31084173284484506, "direction_accuracy": 0.3333333333333333, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5763106796116505, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6670746, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_040", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1, logarithm base unspecified, 77.1% positive); absent genes (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, ACLY, HMGCR, SQLE, NFE2L2 targets) are unknown, not unchanged, and program coherence is judged against the 77.1% up background, not 50/50, and without a formal enrichment test or independence assumption.", "Transcript increases in hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits and biosynthetic enzymes are assumed to raise the corresponding protein and compartment capacity; no enzymatic activity, lipid pool size, localization or flux was measured here.", "SREBP target transcripts are assumed to read out ER-accessible sterol availability; the alternative that they are driven by a genotype-linked transcriptional or growth-state difference independent of sterol sensing cannot be excluded from these data.", "2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (frequent keratin/actin contaminants); all candidate identities are preserved and no spot is treated as confirmation of one protein. The mixed-sign cathepsin- and ANXA1/TALDO1-containing spot trains are treated as compatible-but-ambiguous, possibly charge/processing variants.", "Effects are cross-genotype differences in the mock condition; they describe the steady state actually measured and do not by themselves establish reduced reserve or a defect that would appear only under a future lipid or inflammatory challenge.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipid; the routing step assumes lipid entry is not limiting in either genotype."], "claim": "Under mock conditions at day 30, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzymatic bottleneck but by a coordinated cell-state change in which increased lipid/lipoprotein uptake capacity is coupled to an expanded MiT/TFE-driven endolysosomal compartment and to persistently de-repressed SREBP sterol/fatty-acid biosynthetic transcripts; because internalized lipid is retained in lysosomal membranes and esterified into neutral-lipid stores, the ER-accessible sterol pool is not reported as replete, so uptake, synthesis and esterification remain simultaneously elevated and net neutral lipid (cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol) and lysosomal sphingolipid substrate should accumulate in APOE4. Redox transcripts are shifted upward only as a downstream lipid-peroxide/thiol buffering tone; peroxisomal beta-oxidation and NRF2 core targets are not coordinately represented, so an oxidative-stress or peroxisomal-defect mechanism is rejected as primary. Causality is not established by these abundance measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of the same day-30 mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol/neutral lipid-droplet content and increased lysosome-resident sphingolipid substrates (sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide) in APOE4; equal or lower APOE4 cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol with unchanged sphingolipid substrates would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective test of the routing step: enhancing lysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 (cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) should repress SREBP target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, SCD) and lower cholesteryl esters more in APOE4 than APOE3; if APOE4 SREBP targets stay de-repressed after egress rescue, the lysosomal-retention step is wrong and a sterol-sensing-independent driver is favoured.", "Prospective discrimination of storage versus throughput: SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition should convert the APOE4 excess into free cholesterol and free fatty acid with induction of stress/toxicity markers rather than normalizing total lipid; if total lipid normalizes without redistribution, the adaptation (increased successful catabolic throughput) alternative is favoured.", "Prospective test of the MiT/TFE step: TFEB knockdown should reduce hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts and shrink the lysosomal compartment in APOE4; if the cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol difference versus APOE3 persists unchanged, lysosomal expansion is a parallel marker rather than a required step.", "Prospective redox test (focus rejection): APOE4 should not show a coordinated peroxisomal beta-oxidation or NRF2 core induction at protein/activity level in mock; measurable increases in catalase, plasmalogen synthesis and very-long-chain fatty-acid oxidation activity accompanied by high protein carbonyl/GSSG in mock would favour an oxidative/peroxisomal primary mechanism instead of this lipid-routing mechanism.", "Prospective challenge distinction: exogenous myelin or oxLDL loading should widen the APOE4-APOE3 cholesteryl-ester and lysosomal substrate gap and reveal slower clearance kinetics in APOE4; comparable clearance kinetics under load would show the mock-state differences are a benign set-point shift rather than a routing constraint."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lipid-handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14), consistent with increased, not decreased, lipid entry capacity (uptake flux itself unmeasured).", "Step 2 (inferred routing): Internalized lipid is delivered into an expanded MiT/TFE-programmed endolysosomal compartment (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03; all eight represented V-ATPase subunits up, e.g. gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51; hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86), while sterol/sphingolipid egress components are barely represented (gene:NPC2 +1.17; NPC1 not supplied), so a larger fraction of lipid resides in lysosomal membranes rather than reaching the ER sensing pool.", "Step 3 (inferred sensing consequence): Because ER-accessible cholesterol is not repleted, SREBP-dependent biosynthetic transcripts stay de-repressed despite high uptake (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:MYLIP +1.28); 14/14 represented members are positive versus a 77.1% up background in this selected list.", "Step 4 (supporting supply): Carbon and reducing-equivalent supply favouring cytosolic lipogenesis is transcriptionally reinforced (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ME1 +1.36, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54) while glycolytic committed steps are mixed (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37); ACLY and total flux were not measured.", "Step 5 (storage output): Excess sterol and fatty acid are esterified and stored, and membrane glycerophospholipid remodelling is increased (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.28, gene:LPCAT1 +3.12, gene:MBOAT2 +3.30, gene:CHPT1 +2.90, gene:MGLL +4.00), predicting higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet pools in APOE4 under mock.", "Step 6 (downstream buffering, not primary cause): The lipid-loaded state engages peroxide/thiol buffering (gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:FTH1 +2.53; ambiguous protein_spot:077 +1.07 and protein_spot:017 +0.77) without a coordinated peroxisomal beta-oxidation or NRF2 core response (peroxisome biogenesis 0/16 represented; gene:ACOX1 only +1.24; gene:ABCD1 -1.64; gene:TALDO1 -2.32; gene:PGD -1.30), so lipid disposal by oxidation is not scaled with lipid entry."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a MiT/TFE-lysosomal plus SREBP-anabolic state that routes lipid into lysosomal and neutral-ester storage instead of the ER-regulatory sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2504707750249234, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23824005396196493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3105529304974868, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6570970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2504707750249234, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23824005396196493, "cosine_similarity": 0.3105529304974868, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6570970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.23364075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 72}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows, though a curated/selected differential-expression subset rather than a whole-transcriptome measurement, are assumed to represent real relative transcript abundance differences for the genes listed (log base unspecified, treated only as monotonic fold-change).", "Transcript-level increases in TFEB and CLEAR-network genes are treated only as evidence of increased transcriptional output, not as direct evidence of increased TFEB protein activity, nuclear localization, or actual lysosomal enzymatic flux, all of which are unmeasured/inferred.", "Protein-spot fold-changes are treated as ambiguous readouts because each spot lists multiple candidate genes; attribution of a spot's change to any single named lysosomal candidate gene is an assumption, not a confirmed identification.", "RNA and protein-spot measurements are assumed to derive from comparable APOE4-vs-APOE3 mock-treatment sample sets even though biological replicate numbers are not supplied, so magnitude comparisons across modalities are approximate.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 impairs cellular cholesterol efflux/lysosomal cholesterol clearance is used only as motivating (unverified) context and is not itself established by this dataset."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, the transcriptome shows a large, coordinated, unidirectional increase in TFEB and its canonical CLEAR-network targets (vacuolar-ATPase subunits, cathepsins B/D, GBA, LAMP1, RAB7A) together with cholesterol/lipoprotein-handling transcripts (APOE, LDLR, SCARB1, CD36, SOAT1, SREBF1/2, CH25H), consistent with an inferred compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis transcriptional program; however, protein-spot measurements covering candidate lysosomal proteins (a V-ATPase subunit and several cathepsin-containing spots) show small, mixed, and in some cases opposite-direction changes relative to the RNA signal, suggesting a bottleneck between transcript induction and accumulation of stable lysosomal protein machinery that may limit the cell's capacity to expand functional lysosomal/cholesterol-handling capacity.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction: if lysosomal V-ATPase subunit protein (e.g., ATP6V1E1/ATP6V1H) is quantified by an orthogonal, gene-specific method (targeted mass spectrometry or immunoblot) in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, its fold-change should be much smaller than, or opposite in direction to, the several-fold RNA increase observed here (consistent with protein_spot:064/065 showing decreases despite RNA increases). A result in which V-ATPase protein rises proportionally with the multi-fold RNA increase would weaken or refute the proposed post-transcriptional bottleneck.", "Perturbation prediction: pharmacological activation of TFEB nuclear translocation (e.g., mTORC1 inhibition) in APOE4 microglia is predicted to further increase CLEAR-target transcripts without producing a matched further increase in lysosomal protein abundance or lysosomal number/function; if TFEB activation instead produces a proportional increase in lysosomal protein and measurable lysosomal capacity, this would weaken the mechanism and instead implicate insufficient transcriptional drive (rather than a downstream bottleneck) as limiting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show markedly elevated TFEB transcript (gene:TFEB, log-fold-change +2.38) together with coordinated upregulation of essentially all detected CLEAR-network lysosomal genes: vacuolar-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70), hydrolases (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71), and trafficking/membrane genes (gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65) -- an inferred increase in TFEB-driven transcriptional output, not a measured increase in TFEB protein activity or nuclear localization.", "In parallel, cholesterol/lipoprotein-handling transcripts rise in the same direction (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:CH25H +1.62), consistent with an inferred compensatory attempt to increase cholesterol capture, esterification, and lysosomal delivery; the driver of this coordinated induction (e.g., accumulated intracellular cholesterol/lipid) is not measured in this dataset.", "Protein-spot data that include a V-ATPase subunit candidate (ATP6V1E1; protein_spot:064 effect -1.20, protein_spot:065 effect -0.93) show decreased abundance despite the corresponding transcript increasing, a direct RNA-protein discordance for this candidate gene.", "Cathepsin-containing protein spots are heterogeneous: some spots increase (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:027 +0.59) while others decrease (protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38); across all 24 protein spots whose candidate-gene list intersects the lysosomal gene set, the mean log2 fold-change is only about +0.14, far smaller and less consistent than the RNA mean of about +2.9 for the same gene set, indicating the transcriptional signal is not cleanly propagated to measured protein abundance.", "Because each 2D-gel protein spot lists multiple candidate genes, no single spot can be attributed with certainty to one lysosomal protein; this ambiguity means the RNA-protein discordance is suggestive, not proof, of a block acting on the lysosomal proteins specifically rather than on a co-migrating candidate.", "Within the RNA data itself the lysosomal program is not uniform: CTSS (a lysosomal/immune cysteine protease) is strongly decreased (gene:CTSS -5.57) while CTSB/CTSD are strongly increased, and LRP10 (an APOE-interacting trafficking receptor) is decreased (gene:LRP10 -3.87) while LDLR/SCARB1/CD36 rise -- arguing against a simple, uniform 'more lysosomes' expansion and instead pointing to a selective, potentially imbalanced remodeling of the lysosomal/lipid-receptor repertoire.", "The combined pattern -- strong, broad transcriptional induction of the CLEAR/lysosomal-cholesterol program with weak, inconsistent, or discordant protein-level readout for the same gene set -- supports a primary bottleneck located at or after translation/protein assembly (e.g., limited translation efficiency, complex assembly, or accelerated turnover of newly synthesized lysosomal membrane/hydrolase proteins), constraining the cell's realized lysosomal capacity despite an active compensatory transcriptional response."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a coordinated TFEB/CLEAR transcriptional lysosomal-biogenesis response that is not matched by protein-level lysosomal machinery, indicating a post-transcriptional bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.637210355987055, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "mean_absolute_error": 0.637210355987055, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5658901, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 1}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_012", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All pathway assignments and biochemical relationships are unverified background knowledge; literature and database retrieval were not used. SOAT1 is the proposed cholesterol-esterifying enzyme; a gene named ACAT2 must not be substituted for SOAT2.", "SOAT1 protein activity and esterification flux increase sufficiently to limit ER regulatory cholesterol, with adequate fatty-acyl substrates and sterol supply. The modest SOAT1 RNA increase alone cannot establish this key assumption.", "SCAP\u2013INSIG sterol sensing remains responsive to restored ER cholesterol. SREBF2 RNA abundance is not assumed to measure mature nuclear SREBP2.", "The selected differential-expression list is not an unbiased transcriptome: its broad upward skew limits pathway specificity, and missing genes do not imply unchanged or absent expression. RNA logarithm base is unspecified and no RNA fold ratios are inferred.", "Genotype-associated RNA differences reflect a microglial response under comparable culture conditions rather than differing maturation, normalization or astrocyte contributions. Biological replicate counts and enough design details to establish this are not supplied.", "Protein spots each contain multiple candidate genes and supply no specific validation of the proposed sterol mechanism. Cholesterol pools, esterification, synthesis, localization and export were not measured; no export defect or total-cholesterol increase is required by this hypothesis."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, increased SOAT1-dependent cholesterol esterification may limit free cholesterol available to the ER SCAP\u2013INSIG sensor, sustaining SREBP2 processing and the sterol-acquisition/synthesis transcriptional response. The primary bottleneck is sensor-accessible ER free-cholesterol availability; this causal mechanism is proposed, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In future matched APOE4/APOE3 cultures with controlled sterol supply, measure sensor-accessible ER cholesterol, mature nuclear SREBP2 and tracer-normalized cholesterol esterification. APOE4 should show lower ER regulatory cholesterol, higher mature nuclear SREBP2 and a greater fraction of newly entering cholesterol converted to cholesteryl esters. Equal or higher ER regulatory cholesterol together with no excess SREBP2 processing, or no increase in esterification flux, would weaken the mechanism. None of these outcomes is present in the supplied data.", "Acute selective SOAT1 inhibition, corroborated by an independent inducible genetic reduction with verified target engagement, should reduce esterification, raise sensor-accessible ER free cholesterol and then decrease nuclear SREBP2 before lowering sterol-synthesis transcripts. The APOE4/APOE3 gap in ER cholesterol and SREBP2 processing should narrow under matched conditions. A fall in esterification without restoration of ER cholesterol or suppression of SREBP2 would weaken the proposed bottleneck; equivalent generic responses that leave the genotype gap intact would not explain the APOE4 difference. Maintain matched viability and extracellular sterol supply.", "After a calibrated cholesterol-loading pulse that demonstrably raises ER regulatory cholesterol, both genotypes should suppress SREBP2 processing. Following washout, APOE4 should lose this suppression sooner as esterification removes regulatory cholesterol, and SOAT1 inhibition should diminish that faster rebound. Persistent APOE4 SREBP2 processing despite matched elevated ER cholesterol would favor an intrinsic sensing defect over the proposed esterification sink; persistently low ER cholesterol despite blocked esterification would instead favor deficient delivery."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher SREBF1, SCD and SOAT1 RNA (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:SOAT1) motivates the proposed initiating change: increased fatty-acyl substrate provision and SOAT1-mediated cholesterol esterification. Neither enzyme activity nor fatty-acyl substrate abundance was measured.", "Proposed primary bottleneck: SOAT1-mediated conversion of ER free cholesterol to cholesteryl esters outpaces replenishment of the sensor-accessible ER cholesterol pool. Reduced availability at this compartment is inferred; neither ER free cholesterol nor cholesteryl esters were measured.", "Insufficient sterol feedback is proposed to permit continued SCAP-dependent SREBP2 processing and nuclear entry despite increased INSIG1 RNA. Higher SREBF2 and INSIG1 RNA (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1) is compatible with this response but does not establish processing, localization or sensor failure.", "Continued nuclear SREBP2 is proposed to sustain the observed higher sterol-synthesis and acquisition transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR). These are measured RNA changes; increased cholesterol synthesis and receptor-mediated uptake remain predictions.", "Higher SCARB1 RNA (gene:SCARB1) suggests additional capacity for sterol exchange under suitable extracellular lipoprotein conditions, without establishing net influx. If incoming or newly synthesized cholesterol is preferentially esterified, it can sustain ester storage without fully restoring ER feedback, maintaining the transcriptional response. No storage, influx or export flux was measured."], "title": "SOAT1-dependent esterification limits ER sterol feedback in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_012", "mean_absolute_error": 0.637210355987055, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "mean_absolute_error": 0.637210355987055, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.5387135, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The unspecified RNA log-fold-change base is consistent across all gene_expression rows, so relative ranking and uniform positive sign across the sterol regulon are meaningful even though absolute magnitude comparisons across genes are not.", "This RNA panel is a pre-selected differential-expression list (background ~77% positive among 2211 rows), not a whole transcriptome; absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, CYP46A1, HMGCR, SCAP, and other pathway members means their status is unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript-level increases in synthesis, uptake, and esterification genes are treated as evidence of altered SREBP2 transcriptional activity, not as direct evidence of increased enzymatic flux, protein abundance, or net cellular cholesterol content.", "The claimed link from APOE4 protein lipidation/trafficking properties to ER regulatory-pool sterol sensing is background knowledge and is not directly measured in this dataset.", "Protein-spot data (all spots ambiguous, 3-5 candidate genes each) contain no sterol-pathway enzymes and therefore can only be used to check general compatibility (e.g., lysosomal/proteolytic protein spots trending positive), not to confirm or refute the RNA-level sterol program."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, the near-uniform up-regulation of SREBP2-regulon transcripts spanning sensing (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1), synthesis (HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24, LSS), uptake (LDLR, SCARB1), intracellular trafficking (NPC2), esterification (SOAT1, ACAT2), and one efflux transporter (ABCA7), together with elevated APOE and TSPO transcripts, indicates that APOE4 microglia chronically interpret their ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool as insufficient and sustain SREBP2 transcriptional output, without measured evidence here of whether this transcriptional response is matched by, exceeds, or fails to be matched by actual efflux/catabolic flux (ABCA1, ABCG1, CYP46A1 status unknown, not in the significant list) or by protein-level pathway activity (no sterol-pathway enzymes are represented among the ambiguous protein spots). This program co-occurs with, but is not shown to be caused by, a partial microglial activation signature (TREM2, AIF1, CCL2, C1QA/B/C, TLR2, IRF8 up; CSF1 down), so the sterol program may be a component of a broader APOE4-associated cell-state shift rather than an isolated biosynthetic lesion.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: if APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia are assayed for free (unesterified) cholesterol pool size, lipid droplet number/area, and ApoA-I- or HDL-mediated cholesterol efflux capacity under the same mock condition, the failed-compensation version of this mechanism predicts increased lipid droplets/esterified cholesterol with efflux capacity not increased proportionally to biosynthetic/uptake gene induction. Finding efflux capacity increased in proportion to (or exceeding) the biosynthetic induction, or no change in lipid droplet/esterified cholesterol content, would weaken the mechanism and instead support a successful, load-matched adaptive response.", "If pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SREBP2 processing (e.g., SCAP/SREBP cleavage blockade) in APOE4 microglia fails to reduce the coordinated synthesis/uptake transcript signature or fails to normalize any observed lipid accumulation phenotype, this would weaken the proposed SREBP2-centered causal chain in favor of an SREBP2-independent driver (e.g., generalized transcriptional activation tied to the broader immune/DAM-like state)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype alters the lipid-carrier properties or trafficking efficiency of the APOE protein produced by microglia (background knowledge, not directly measured here).", "This is proposed to reduce delivery or perceived availability of cholesterol to the ER regulatory pool sensed by the SCAP-SREBP-INSIG system, even if total cellular sterol is not reduced.", "Perceived regulatory-pool insufficiency keeps SREBP2 transcriptionally active, producing coordinated up-regulation of its own regulon: SREBF1/SREBF2/INSIG1 (sensing/feedback), HMGCS1/DHCR7/DHCR24/LSS (synthesis), and LDLR/SCARB1 (uptake) (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1).", "Concurrent up-regulation of NPC2 (intracellular sterol trafficking), SOAT1/ACAT2 (esterification/storage), APOE, and ABCA7 (efflux transporter) transcripts indicates the cell is simultaneously mobilizing handling/export machinery for the additional sterol influx (gene:NPC2, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7).", "Because canonical bulk efflux (ABCA1, ABCG1) and catabolic (CYP46A1) transcripts are absent from this significant/selected list, whether export keeps pace with synthesis and uptake cannot be determined from this data; net cholesterol accumulation versus successful clearance is not established.", "TSPO up-regulation (gene:TSPO), together with a partial activation signature (gene:TREM2, gene:AIF1, gene:CCL2, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:TLR2, gene:IRF8) and reduced CSF1 (gene:CSF1), suggests the sterol program is embedded in a broader coordinated microglial cell-state change rather than acting in isolation.", "The net functional consequence for membrane cholesterol content, lipid droplet formation, or cholesterol efflux capacity is not measured and remains the decisive unknown distinguishing failed compensation from successful adaptation."], "title": "APOE4 drives coordinated SREBP2-regulon activation reflecting a cholesterol-sensing/trafficking imbalance rather than confirmed net accumulation or depletion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6295242718446602, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022504892367906065, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24917074805828346, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101171980232298, "direction_accuracy": 0.038834951456310676, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6295242718446602, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5644945, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_071", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705 up / 507 down in two row-numbered blocks) in an unspecified logarithm base; absent genes (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, GRN, PSAP) are unknown, not unchanged, and program membership was pre-specified from canonical background knowledge (unverified) with all represented members reported including discordant ones.", "Because 77% of RNA rows and 64/92 spots are positive, agreement in direction alone is weak evidence; we rely on effect magnitude relative to that skewed background and on the few strong opposite-direction members (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:CTSS).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but does not demonstrate, enzyme activity or flux: increased hydrolase and TCA transcripts are read as capacity, not as measured lysosomal degradation rate or oxidative flux; decreased gene:HK2/gene:PFKP is read as reduced capacity, not as a demonstrated glycolytic block in mock.", "2D-gel spots are multi-candidate; spots are used only for compatibility. Lysosomal-hydrolase-containing spots are split (protein_spot:052, :053, :055, :057, :013, :012, :063, :088 up; :058, :067, :069, :064, :065 down), so no individual protein is treated as confirmed, and the strongly up ANXA1/TALDO1 spot train (protein_spot:043-:047) is only compatible with gene:ANXA1 (+4.2) since gene:TALDO1 is -2.3.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein/lipid; APOE4-dependent differences in that supply, rather than a cell-intrinsic microglial change, could initiate the same state, and the data cannot separate these.", "Cell composition and cell-size/normalisation differences between genotypes are assumed not to generate the specific pattern (lysosomal + anaplerotic up, HK2/PFKP down), an assumption the supplied data cannot test."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state rather than by an inflammatory or a single rate-limiting defect: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors, for a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal hydrolase-acidification-targeting program, and for desaturation/esterification/phospholipid-remodelling enzymes are jointly higher, while committed glycolytic steps fall and mitochondrial anaplerotic/oxidative transcripts rise sharply. We interpret this as altered routing of lipid carbon (uptake -\u003e lysosomal hydrolysis -\u003e re-esterification/membrane remodelling and mitochondrial oxidation) that is largely compensated in the measured mock condition, with reduced glycolytic reserve as a liability that would only be revealed by challenge. Measured abundances are transcript and 2D-gel spot levels; degradation flux, lipid pool sizes, localisation and causal direction were not measured and are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, neutral-lipid stores (LipidTOX, cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol by lipidomics) will be higher per cell while bulk lysosomal degradation rate (DQ-BSA dequenching, LysoTracker-normalised acid hydrolase activity) is equal or higher; if APOE4 instead shows a lower degradation rate with accumulated undigested substrate, the 'routing/compensated capacity' mechanism is weakened in favour of a lysosomal degradation bottleneck.", "Prospective: acute SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in APOE4 microglia will reduce ester stores and lower gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:APOE and gene:ABCA7 transcripts toward APOE3 levels; if these transcripts are unchanged after esterification blockade, step 3 (sterol-replete signalling driven by stored/hydrolysed lipid) is falsified.", "Prospective: Seahorse profiling will show APOE4 basal OCR equal or higher than APOE3 with a lower glycolytic reserve after oligomycin, and greater proportional OCR loss on MPC inhibition (UK5099); higher glycolytic reserve in APOE4, or no differential UK5099 sensitivity, would weaken steps 4-5.", "Prospective: 13C-oleate and 13C-glucose tracing will show a greater fraction of fatty-acid carbon entering cholesteryl-ester/TAG and TCA intermediates in APOE4, with a smaller glucose contribution to lactate; equal tracer partitioning would falsify the routing claim.", "Prospective: challenge with myelin debris or oxLDL will reveal the reserve deficit - APOE4 microglia will clear a smaller fraction of an added lipid load per cell and fail to raise glycolysis, despite their higher basal hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance and equal glycolytic induction would show the state is fully adaptive and would remove the challenge-revealed component of the hypothesis.", "Prospective: isogenic correction of APOE4 to APOE3 (or APOE knockout in both backgrounds) will collapse the joint lysosomal + lipogenic/esterification + anaplerotic signature together; dissociation of these modules after correction would indicate they are independent genotype effects rather than one coordinated state."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases delivery of lipid/lipoprotein cargo to the endolysosome (inferred, not measured): scavenger/lipoprotein and phagocytic-receptor transcripts are higher - gene:SCARB1 (+8.2), gene:CD36 (+1.4), gene:LDLR (+1.5), gene:TREM2 (+1.3), gene:MERTK (+1.3), gene:GAS6 (+1.3), gene:C1QA/B/C (+1.1..+1.2), gene:MRC1 (+1.4) - against a selected-list background that is 77% up (1705/2212).", "A MiT/TFE-type lysosomal program expands catabolic capacity: gene:TFEB (+2.4), gene:MITF (+1.0) with acid hydrolases gene:GAA (+10.0), gene:CTSK (+7.4), gene:GBA (+6.7), gene:NAGLU (+5.9), gene:HEXA (+5.7), gene:SMPD1 (+5.6), gene:CTSB (+5.5), gene:DPP7 (+4.5), gene:CTSD (+2.9), gene:HEXB (+2.2), hydrolase targeting/maturation gene:GNPTG (+3.0), gene:SUMF1 (+2.0), gene:IGF2R (+2.0), and V-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H (+6.9), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.2), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.7); 7/29 represented members exceed +5 versus 6.2% of all rows. Exceptions that limit the claim: gene:CTSS (-5.6), gene:M6PR (-1.7), gene:IDS (-1.6).", "Lipid liberated in that compartment is sensed as replete rather than scarce, so the cell runs a lipogenic/desaturating/esterifying and lipid-export-signalling arm instead of the rate-limiting mevalonate arm: gene:SREBF1 (+4.7), gene:SCD (+4.2), gene:AGPAT2 (+6.3), gene:LPCAT1 (+3.1), gene:CHPT1 (+2.9), gene:ACSS2 (+2.9), gene:DGAT1 (+1.7), gene:SOAT1 (+1.3), gene:FADS1 (+1.6), gene:MGLL (+4.0), gene:APOE (+1.2), gene:ABCA7 (+2.1), gene:PLTP (+1.1), gene:MYLIP (+1.3), gene:CH25H (+1.6); only post-squalene sterol genes are represented (gene:DHCR24 +3.7, gene:DHCR7 +2.7, gene:LSS +2.3, gene:EBP +1.3, gene:HMGCS1 +1.1, gene:SREBF2 +1.1) while HMGCR/SQLE/IDI1/FDFT1 are absent from the supplied list and therefore unknown.", "Lipid-derived and amino-acid-derived carbon is routed to mitochondria: gene:MPC2 (+8.0), gene:MDH1 (+8.7), gene:OGDH (+8.6), gene:GOT1 (+6.4), gene:DLD (+5.5), gene:ACO2 (+3.5), gene:GLUD1 (+3.2), gene:GLS (+1.4) - 9/9 represented members positive with median +5.5, the largest coordinated magnitude shift in the data - with nuclear-encoded respiratory transcripts up (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.7, gene:ATP5F1B +2.6, gene:CYCS +2.6).", "Committed glycolysis is simultaneously reduced (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:HK3 -1.1) despite higher gene:SLC2A1 (+2.4) and gene:ENO1 (+2.2), and mtDNA-encoded transcripts fall (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.4, gene:MT-CYB -2.3, gene:MT-ND4 -1.8), so the switch is a re-routing of substrate use with a narrowed glycolytic and mtDNA-encoded reserve rather than a global energy failure.", "The resulting state is a lipid-storing, lysosome-rich microglial phenotype that is compensated under mock - there is no canonical interferon signature (0/24 queried interferon genes represented) and NF-kB members are mixed (gene:CXCL8 +3.1, gene:MYD88 +2.3, gene:CCL2 +2.1 versus gene:TRAF4 -7.2, gene:RELB -1.3, gene:CCL4 -1.5, gene:TNFAIP3 -1.0) - so the predicted APOE4 deficit is loss of surge capacity (glycolytic/lysosomal) that appears only under a future lipid or immune challenge, not an ongoing failure in the measured condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-routing cell state: expanded lysosomal (MiT/TFE-type) catabolic machinery plus sterol-replete lipogenic/esterification signalling that channels lipid carbon into storage and mitochondrial anaplerosis rather than glycolysis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43234685965365727, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2905666919735507, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101107925987953, "direction_accuracy": 0.39967637540453077, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mean_absolute_error": 0.632504854368932, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43234685965365727, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2905666919735507, "cosine_similarity": 0.3101107925987953, "direction_accuracy": 0.39967637540453077, "mean_absolute_error": 0.632504854368932, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.597527, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 73}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_054", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); absent genes (e.g. LDHA, PKM, GAPDH, HK1, PFKL, CS, MDH2, CPT1A, PPARGC1A, TFAM) are unknown, not unchanged, so no claim is made about whole-pathway coverage.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source ('reported log fold change'); effects are used only as signed, ranked magnitudes on their original scale and are not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate, in direction only, with the abundance of the corresponding transport/enzyme protein; enzyme activity (e.g. PDH phosphorylation state set by PDP1/PDK balance, MPC transport rate), metabolite levels, respiration and lactate flux were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features (2-6 candidate genes each); they are used only for compatibility/contradiction and never as identification of a single protein. Spot pairs with shared candidates change in opposite directions (protein_spot:038 +1.07 vs protein_spot:039 -0.766 sharing ALDOA/ALDOC; protein_spot:052 +2.138 / protein_spot:053 +1.536 vs protein_spot:058 -0.848 / protein_spot:067 -1.0 / protein_spot:069 -1.379 sharing cathepsins and actins), consistent with isoform/processing redistribution rather than a single-direction change.", "Members of each program were chosen a priori from canonical pathway membership (glycolysis, TCA/carriers, ETC subunit families matched by NDUF|COX|ATP5|UQCR|SDH prefixes, malate-aspartate shuttle, lysosome/v-ATPase, lipid, microglial activation) and every represented member was scored regardless of sign; membership was not curated to make directions agree.", "Coordinated positive direction alone is weak evidence given the 77% positive background of this selected list; the argument rests on effect magnitude (ETC subunits median +2.64, TCA/entry module median +4.20 vs background median +1.46) and on the sign exceptions (HK2/HK3/PFKP/PFKFB2 and mtDNA-encoded transcripts) that run against that background.", "Cells were profiled as microglia co-cultured with astrocytes (10X Flex, day 30, mock); genotype-associated differences in cell state or composition within the microglial population could contribute to apparent pathway-level shifts, and mtDNA transcript capture by probe-based Flex chemistry may be unreliable.", "The mtDNA/nuclear stoichiometry step describes a predicted capacity limit revealed under challenge; the supplied mock data do not establish any ongoing respiratory defect."], "claim": "In mock-treated iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (vs isogenic APOE3), the dominant coherent signal in the supplied selected differential-expression list is a coordinated cell-state shift in carbon routing: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54), the malate-aspartate shuttle (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75), TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:ME1 +1.36) and 38/38 represented nuclear-encoded ETC/ATP-synthase subunits are increased, while the myeloid inducible glycolytic committed-step isoforms are decreased (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) despite increased glucose-uptake and HIF1A transcripts (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:HIF1A +1.98). This oxidative, lysosome-fed routing state is proposed to be an adaptive/throughput shift in the measured mock condition, not an established ongoing energetic bottleneck; the only capacity-limiting signal is that mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts do not track the nuclear increase (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33, with gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), predicting reduced reserve that would be revealed only by a future challenge. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity and localization were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective 13C6-glucose tracing in mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show higher fractional M+2 labelling of citrate/malate/glutamate and a lower lactate-to-glucose-consumption ratio in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or lower glucose-derived TCA labelling with equal or higher lactate output, the carbon re-routing mechanism is wrong.", "Prospective acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or PDH re-inhibition (DCA-reversible PDK manipulation) should reduce basal oxygen consumption and ATP-linked respiration substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal sensitivity in both genotypes would weaken the claim that pyruvate import/PDH activation carries the extra oxidative routing (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1).", "Prospective glycolytic-challenge test (LPS or oligomycin-stimulated ECAR, and 2-DG sensitivity) should reveal a smaller inducible glycolytic increment in APOE4 despite equal or greater glucose uptake, matching reduced gene:HK2/gene:HK3/gene:PFKP with increased gene:SLC2A1/gene:SLC2A3. An equal or larger glycolytic burst in APOE4 would falsify the reduced-committed-step-reserve component.", "Prospective immunoblot/BN-PAGE of the ratio of mtDNA-encoded (MT-CO1, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) to nuclear-encoded (NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) subunits, plus FCCP-uncoupled maximal respiration, should show a lower mtDNA/nuclear subunit ratio and a spare respiratory capacity that does not scale with the nuclear transcript increase in APOE4. If maximal respiration and assembled complex levels rise proportionally with the nuclear subunit transcripts, the stoichiometric-cap step is falsified while the routing steps could still stand.", "Prospective lysosomal-hydrolysis blockade (bafilomycin A1 or LIPA/GAA inhibition) should lower TCA-intermediate pools and basal respiration more in APOE4 than APOE3, linking gene:GAA/gene:GBA/gene:CTSB/gene:ATP6V1H-associated catabolism to the oxidative state; no genotype difference in this dependence would remove the lysosome-to-mitochondria substrate-supply step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with an expanded lysosomal/lipid-handling transcriptional state (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92), which is inferred (not measured) to liberate lipid- and glycogen-derived catabolic substrates inside the cell.", "In the same cells, transcripts for mitochondrial carbon entry increase: mitochondrial pyruvate carrier (gene:MPC2 +7.98), the PDH-activating phosphatase (gene:PDP1 +3.00) and the shared E3 subunit (gene:DLD +5.54), together with anion carriers (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50) and import machinery (gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46); this is proposed to bias pyruvate and acetyl-unit routing into the matrix rather than to lactate.", "Cytosolic reducing equivalents are re-routed toward mitochondria through the malate-aspartate shuttle (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75), reducing dependence on LDH-mediated NAD+ regeneration (LDHA/LDHB rows were not supplied, so cytosolic NAD+ handling is inferred, not observed).", "Downstream, the TCA cycle and anaplerotic amino-acid input transcripts rise (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS +1.35, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45), and every represented nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit is increased (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:NDUFS8 +4.93, gene:NDUFB6 +4.58, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56), defining an oxidative-biased cell state.", "Concurrently the committed, inducible glycolytic steps used by myeloid cells for a glycolytic burst are transcriptionally reduced (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10) even though glucose-transporter and HIF1A transcripts are increased (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:HIF1A) and other glycolytic transcripts are up (gene:PFKM +2.41, gene:GPI +2.06, gene:ENO1 +2.17); the proposed consequence in the mock condition is preserved glucose uptake with carbon committed to oxidation instead of lactate export (gene:SLC16A1 +1.12 only modestly changed).", "Because mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts do not follow the nuclear increase (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33), holoenzyme assembly stoichiometry is predicted to cap how much of the increased nuclear capacity becomes realized respiratory capacity; this predicts a reduced spare/maximal reserve that is revealed by a future metabolic or inflammatory challenge rather than an ongoing deficit at rest.", "The oxidative, lysosome-fed state is proposed to co-occur with a shift away from the motile/homeostatic surveillance program (gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:CSF1 -5.90) and toward a lipid-loaded reactive phenotype (gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:CD33 +1.78, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route carbon into mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation while down-regulating committed glycolytic isoforms, with mtDNA-encoded subunits failing to track the nuclear OXPHOS increase"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21484197827775042, "cosine_similarity": 0.3088362724640255, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6180550161812298, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21484197827775042, "cosine_similarity": 0.3088362724640255, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6180550161812298, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.093949, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 74}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_082", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and carry a large positive global shift (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base, 77% of rows positive); all module claims are therefore made relative to this list-wide median, not to zero, and the logarithm base is left unspecified.", "Absence of a gene from the list (HMGCR, SQLE, IDI1, ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, NPC1, LIPA, SCAP) is treated as 'not called differential', which is weak evidence of no change rather than a measurement of no change.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the corresponding lysosomal, lipogenic and esterification protein activities; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, localisation or lipid pool was measured in these data.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as ambiguous, non-decisive corroboration.", "Very large |effect| values (up to 15.5) are assumed to be dominated by low-expression/high-variance rows, so module conclusions are based on medians and rank statistics rather than the extreme tails.", "The astrocyte co-culture composition is assumed comparable between APOE4 and APOE3 wells; a genotype-dependent difference in microglial purity or activation state could produce the same list-wide shift."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background elevation of lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (with TFEB/MITF) together with an SREBP1-type lipogenic module (SREBF1, SCD, ACSS2, AGPAT2, DGAT1), while the SREBP2 sterol-synthesis/uptake/efflux arm stays at the list-wide background and the ER sterol-repletion markers INSIG1 and MYLIP are up. We propose the rate-limiting step is not sterol synthesis but disposal of lysosome-derived lipid: cholesterol and fatty acid released by expanded lysosomal catabolism are inferred to be channelled into SOAT1-dependent cholesteryl ester and SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1-dependent glycerolipid storage rather than into efflux, giving APOE4 microglia a larger esterified neutral-lipid pool. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should convert cholesteryl ester into free cholesterol and de-repress the SREBP2 output (HMGCR, LDLR, HMGCS1 transcripts and LDL uptake) significantly more in APOE4 than APOE3, because APOE4 is predicted to carry the larger esterification flux. If APOE4 shows an equal or smaller de-repression than APOE3, or no measurable cholesteryl-ester pool difference, the esterification-bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Source test: blocking lysosomal acidification/hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or combined GBA/acid-lipase inhibition) for 24-48 h should shrink the APOE4-specific neutral-lipid droplet excess. If droplets are unchanged or increase while lipogenic transcripts stay high, the lipid is coming from de novo SREBP1 lipogenesis rather than from lysosomal catabolism, weakening steps 2 and 5.", "SCD inhibition should reduce droplet number/size and cholesteryl-ester content disproportionately in APOE4; equal effects in both genotypes would weaken the SREBP1 arm.", "LXR agonism or ABCA1 over-expression should normalise the APOE4 excess esterified sterol; failure to do so despite confirmed ABCA1 induction would argue the block is upstream of efflux (e.g. lysosomal sterol egress via NPC1/NPC2) rather than at export.", "Direct state test: lysosomal pH and DQ-BSA/hydrolase activity should be normal or increased in APOE4. If APOE4 lysosomes are instead less acidic and hydrolytically impaired, the transcript expansion is compensatory to a degradation failure and the proposed 'expanded catabolic input' direction is wrong.", "Filipin/free-cholesterol imaging should show APOE4 sterol enriched in droplet-adjacent/ER compartments rather than trapped in LAMP1+ lysosomes; predominant LAMP1+ free-cholesterol trapping with unchanged ester content would favour a lysosomal egress block instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSD, gene:NAGLU) and for v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1) are higher in APOE4 than APOE3 and sit above the list-wide median shift, alongside the CLEAR-network regulators gene:TFEB and gene:MITF. Inferred (not measured): greater lysosomal biogenesis and degradative/acidification capacity.", "Inferred flux: increased hydrolysis of membrane and lipoprotein cargo in the endolysosome liberates free cholesterol, sphingolipid-derived species and fatty acids. No lipid pool, lysosomal pH, or hydrolase activity was measured here.", "Measured: the ER sterol-sensing/SREBP2 arm is not mobilised above background \u2014 gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:HMGCS1 (+1.08) and gene:LDLR (+1.50) lie at or below the list median (+1.46), the mevalonate/squalene enzymes (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, MVD) are absent from the differential list, whereas gene:INSIG1 and gene:MYLIP are up. Inferred: ER-accessible sterol is sensed as replete, so no compensatory synthesis/uptake program is engaged.", "Measured: an SREBP1-type lipogenic module is elevated well above background (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1). Inferred: increased supply of monounsaturated fatty acid and diacylglycerol for esterification.", "Measured: gene:SOAT1 is up with very strong statistical support, gene:SCARB1 and gene:CD36 (uptake) are up, gene:OSBPL8 (an ER\u2013organelle lipid-transfer protein) is down, and no LXR/efflux program appears in the differential list (ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3 not called differential; gene:APOE and gene:ABCA7 rise only near the global shift). Inferred: esterification/storage outcompetes efflux as the exit route for liberated sterol.", "Predicted state (not measured here): APOE4 microglia accumulate a larger cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplet pool per cell, with sterol retained in the lysosome\u2013droplet compartment rather than exported, which would rationalise the ambiguous, bidirectional cathepsin-containing protein spots (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) as altered processing/partitioning rather than uniform hydrolase loss."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase program coupled to SREBP1 lipogenesis, routing liberated lipid into esterified storage instead of sterol-synthesis or efflux responses"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23320752066203165, "cosine_similarity": 0.30824479586498854, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6296278317152104, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24131373924602148, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23320752066203165, "cosine_similarity": 0.30824479586498854, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6296278317152104, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6820305, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 294}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_048", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Reported RNA effects are differential expression in the stated direction (positive = higher in APOE4) on an unspecified logarithm base; only the sign and rank ordering, not the absolute base, are used.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive), so all enrichment statements are made against the internal distribution of this list, not against an unbiased transcriptome; genes absent from the list (e.g. ACLY, FASN, SPTLC1/2, UGCG, ASAH1, PSAP) may be unchanged or simply filtered, and their pools are treated as unmeasured.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme capacity; enzyme activity, post-translational regulation, substrate flux, organelle localisation and metabolite pools (citrate, acetyl-CoA, acyl-CoA, TAG, cholesteryl ester, ceramide) were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:077 and protein_spot:038 are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, and the spot data cannot confirm which candidate changed.", "Replicate number, dispersion and batch structure are not supplied ('biological_replicates: not supplied in workbook'), and very large reported effects (up to 15.5) suggest unstable per-gene estimates, so set-level rather than single-gene inference is used.", "The astrocyte co-culture contributes to the microglial lipid environment, but no astrocyte-specific measurement is supplied; genotype effects are attributed to microglia only by assumption."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated transcriptional shift away from glycolytic/oxidative-PPP commitment and toward mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA and electron-transport-chain capacity, coupled to mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1), acetate/acetyl-CoA salvage (ACSS2) and an SREBF1/SCD-driven desaturation-esterification arm. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting (bottleneck) node in APOE4 cells is SCD-dependent conversion of mitochondria-derived and imported saturated acyl-CoA into monounsaturated acyl-CoA for AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification, so that APOE4 microglia dispose of oxidative carbon as MUFA-enriched neutral lipid (TAG/cholesteryl ester, lipid droplets) rather than as ATP-yielding complete oxidation; sphingolipid catabolism changes are a parallel, non-enriched feature rather than the driver. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) or SCD knockdown in mock-treated APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should abolish most of the APOE4-minus-APOE3 difference in lipid-droplet content and in MUFA-containing TAG/CE species (genotype x drug interaction, larger absolute effect in APOE4). If SCD inhibition reduces droplets equally in both genotypes, or leaves the APOE4/APOE3 difference intact, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Lipidomic discrimination against the sphingolipid alternative: untargeted lipidomics of the same mock cultures should show APOE4 elevated in the neutral-lipid desaturation index (18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0 in TAG and CE) rather than a selective, class-wide rise in hexosylceramide, GM2/GM3 gangliosides or sphingomyelin. Predominant sphingolipid-class changes with an unchanged desaturation index would falsify this mechanism and support the sphingolipid-turnover alternative.", "Flux test: U-13C-glucose and U-13C-glutamine tracing should show greater 13C enrichment in citrate and in cytosolic palmitate/oleate in APOE4 than APOE3, and blocking citrate export (SLC25A1 inhibition, CTPI-2) or MPC (UK5099) should reduce APOE4 lipogenic labelling and droplet content more than APOE3. Equal labelling of citrate and oleate between genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Respiratory test: Seahorse profiling should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower or unchanged extracellular acidification in APOE4 versus APOE3; if APOE4 instead shows lower OCR and higher ECAR, the inferred oxidative-capacity step is contradicted.", "Negative/specificity control: inhibiting lysosomal glucosylceramidase (conduritol-B-epoxide) or acid sphingomyelinase should not normalise the APOE4 neutral-lipid desaturation phenotype; if it does, the sphingolipid-turnover mechanism, not the SCD node, is primary.", "Protein-level check with unambiguous identification: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS should show higher SCD1 and SLC25A1 protein in APOE4; absence of any protein-level increase in these two nodes despite the transcript differences would substantially weaken the hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:GOT1) and for ETC/ATP-synthase subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5MC3; 32/32 ETC-set genes positive, set median 2.62 versus list median 1.46, permutation p=0.003) are higher in APOE4, while committed glycolytic kinases (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP) and oxidative-PPP transcripts (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) are lower. Inferred, not measured: higher mitochondrial oxidative capacity and reduced glycolytic/PPP commitment; no flux, respiration or metabolite pool was measured here.", "Inferred: increased TCA turnover plus amino-acid anaplerosis (gene:GOT1, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:BCAT2, gene:ABAT all higher) raises the mitochondrial citrate pool beyond ATP demand in resting (mock) microglia.", "Measured: higher gene:SLC25A1 (citrate/malate carrier) and gene:ACSS2 with higher gene:SREBF1 and gene:INSIG1. Inferred: increased citrate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability, with SREBP1-programme engagement; ACLY and FASN transcripts are absent from the supplied list, so the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool itself is unmeasured.", "Measured: higher gene:SCD together with gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1 and lipid-uptake transcripts gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:APOE. Inferred bottleneck: stearoyl-CoA desaturase activity sets the rate at which newly made and imported saturated acyl-CoA is converted to 16:1/18:1 species that AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 can esterify; ER localisation of this step and the acyl-CoA pools are inferred, not observed.", "Inferred consequence: carbon that enters mitochondria is partly re-routed into MUFA-rich triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester stored in lipid droplets, giving APOE4 microglia a higher neutral-lipid desaturation index and lower net oxidative ATP yield per carbon than APOE3, without requiring any change in sphingolipid synthesis.", "Measured: mitochondrial/thiol antioxidant transcripts are higher (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:CCS, gene:NNT, gene:ME1) and a peroxiredoxin-candidate spot is increased (protein_spot:077). Inferred: elevated ETC flux and desaturase-linked peroxide production impose a redox/NADPH load that, with reduced oxidative-PPP transcripts (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1), further constrains the SCD node and can spill over into saturated-lipid stress if SCD capacity is exceeded.", "Measured but not enriched: several lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts are high (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A). Interpretation: these are consistent with increased substrate handling downstream of the lipid-storage phenotype, but they do not exceed the strongly up-shifted background of this selected DE list and are therefore assigned a secondary, non-bottleneck role."], "title": "Citrate-export-fed SCD1 desaturation/esterification is the carbon-disposal bottleneck that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 microglia at rest"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14145404866521433, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1751802692896406, "cosine_similarity": 0.30810462449030385, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5973689320388349, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14145404866521433, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1751802692896406, "cosine_similarity": 0.30810462449030385, "direction_accuracy": 0.18608414239482202, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5973689320388349, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.06382575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 295}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directions are therefore judged against that 77% up-biased background, and absent genes (HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, MSMO1, IDI1, FDPS, CYP51A1, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, ACLY, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Transcript increases in synthesis, uptake and hydrolase genes are treated as capacity/pathway-output readouts, not as measured cholesterol mass, esterification rate, efflux flux, SREBP-2 cleavage or lysosomal hydrolase activity; the routing step and the ER-pool state are inferred, not observed.", "Elevated gene:LDLR need not raise LDLR protein because gene:MYLIP (IDOL) is also elevated; uptake capacity is assumed but unmeasured.", "apoE4 particle behaviour (poorer lipidation/exchange) is background knowledge (unverified here); only gene:APOE abundance was measured.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate identities each with frequent keratin/actin contaminants, so no spot is treated as confirming an individual protein; spot direction is used only for compatibility testing.", "Members of each program were chosen a priori from canonical pathway membership (or, for the respiratory chain, by the symbol-prefix rule NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH applied to the supplied list) before looking at effect signs; genes were not dropped for disagreeing in direction.", "The mock condition captures a steady state; reduced reserve under a lipid challenge is a prediction, not an observation, and no causal direction between the sterol, lysosomal and mitochondrial programs is established."], "claim": "In mock-treated iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (vs isogenic APOE3), the transcriptional state is best explained by altered sterol routing rather than by a single enzymatic block: sterol acquisition (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, ranked 19th of 2212 rows for SCARB1) and post-squalene sterol synthesis (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, with gene:SREBF2 +1.06 and gene:INSIG1 +1.87) are elevated at the same time as the whole-cell sterol-excess/oxysterol-LXR arm (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17) and the esterification/storage and lysosomal-hydrolase arms (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88). Co-activation of two normally reciprocal sterol-sensing outputs, together with a coordinately raised mitochondrial oxidative/carbon-export program (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:NNT +2.88, all 38 represented NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH rows positive), indicates an adapted high-throughput sterol acquisition-storage cycle in which the ER-accessible sterol pool is under-filled, not an ongoing catabolic bottleneck. Directions are transcript/spot abundances; no sterol mass, flux, efflux or SREBP-2 cleavage was measured, so causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective feedback test: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with 25-hydroxycholesterol, LDL or myelin debris should suppress SREBP-2 targets (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) less in APOE4, with a lower ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4/PFO* biosensor accessibility) and a higher cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet fraction despite equal or greater total sterol; equal suppression and an equal or higher ER-accessible pool in APOE4 would weaken the mis-routing mechanism.", "Prospective routing test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or SCARB1 knockdown should reduce cholesteryl-ester accumulation and lower SREBP-2 target transcripts preferentially in APOE4; if these transcripts fall equally in both genotypes, or SCARB1 knockdown does not change APOE4 ester content, the acquisition-storage cycle is not the driver.", "Prospective test against the competing 'generic oxidative/anabolic scale-up' explanation: partial respiratory-chain or SLC25A1/ACSS2 inhibition should reduce sterol-synthesis transcripts similarly in both genotypes and should not normalise the APOE4-specific co-activation of SREBP-2 and oxysterol/LXR outputs; if it does abolish the genotype difference, the mitochondrial program, not sterol routing, is primary.", "Prospective challenge/reserve test: APOE4 microglia should show reduced efflux of acquired sterol to apoE/HDL acceptors and impaired clearance of a debris bolus even though the mock-state lysosomal and oxidative transcript programs are elevated; equal efflux and equal clearance kinetics would show the elevated programs are simple increased throughput without a routing defect.", "Prospective identity test for the protein layer: targeted immunoblot/MS should show increased ANXA1 (concordant with gene:ANXA1 +4.15) and unchanged or decreased TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32) in the protein_spot:043-protein_spot:046 series series; a TALDO1 increase with no ANXA1 change would break the transcript-protein link used for compatibility and require an independent pentose-phosphate branch not otherwise supported by RNA (gene:PGD -1.30)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia express more sterol-acquisition machinery than APOE3 (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36) alongside higher gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7 and gene:MYLIP; inferred, not measured: apoE4-containing particles exchange/export sterol less efficiently, so acquired sterol is retained intracellularly.", "Step 2 (inferred routing): retained sterol and membrane lipid are routed to the endolysosome and to cytosolic ester/neutral-lipid stores rather than to the ER regulatory pool, consistent with elevated gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:NPC2 and gene:TSPO, and with a TFEB-type lysosomal expansion (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:MAN2B1, gene:LAMP1).", "Step 3 (sensing consequence): with sterol sequestered away from ER sensors, SCAP/SREBP-2 output stays on (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2, gene:LDLR) while whole-cell excess is reported through oxysterol/LXR-type outputs (gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1, gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD); these two outputs are normally reciprocal, and their simultaneous elevation is the discriminating pattern.", "Step 4 (support of the cycle): sustained synthesis requires cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH, matched by increased mitochondrial oxidative and carbon-export transcripts (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:NNT, gene:ME1) and by uniformly positive respiratory-chain rows (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2).", "Step 5 (net state in the supplied mock condition): the genotype difference is an adapted, higher-throughput lipid-handling state (expanded uptake, storage, hydrolase and oxidative capacity) with only modest inflammatory tone (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:C1QA +1.19, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:LGALS3 +2.37) and no interferon signature; a lipid-handling defect is predicted to become rate-limiting only under a future sterol/debris challenge, and is not claimed as an ongoing failure here.", "Step 6 (protein-level compatibility, not confirmation): the strongest protein-spot increases are ambiguous charge-train-like spots whose shared candidates are ANXA1/TALDO1 (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046); gene:ANXA1 is +4.15 while gene:TALDO1 is -2.32, so the spots are compatible with an increased membrane-binding/phagocytic ANXA1 pool but cannot be assigned to one protein; cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and therefore neither confirm nor refute the transcript-level lysosomal expansion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mis-route acquired sterol into lysosomal/ester storage, leaving the ER regulatory sterol pool unsatisfied and driving a mitochondria-fuelled acquisition-plus-synthesis cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23428903740353726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2503902909087609, "cosine_similarity": 0.30792078538883755, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6275469255663431, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23428903740353726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2503902909087609, "cosine_similarity": 0.30792078538883755, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6275469255663431, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1944495, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 75}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA transcript abundance changes for this gene set are assumed to reflect corresponding changes in encoded protein activity and pathway flux; no protein-spot observation in this dataset maps to a sterol-pathway candidate gene, so this assumption is unverified by the protein modality here.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 impairs cholesterol trafficking/efflux is treated as unverified prior context used only for interpretive framing, not as evidence from the supplied data.", "The unspecified logarithm base for reported RNA fold changes is assumed to be applied consistently across all cited genes, so relative magnitude comparisons within this RNA panel are assumed valid even though the base itself is not confirmed.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (not an unbiased transcriptome survey); the sterol-gene module's directional coherence is interpreted against this dataset's own global positive-effect background rate rather than against an assumed neutral 50/50 baseline."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, RNA abundance for the SREBP2-responsive cholesterol synthesis/uptake module (SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, LDLR) plus lysosomal/storage and oxysterol-handling genes (NPC2, SOAT1, CYP27A1, MYLIP, ABCA7) is coordinately elevated, consistent with an inferred, unresolved deficit in accessible-sterol sensing that drives a compensatory synthesis-and-uptake transcriptional program rather than an efflux-dominant response; this imbalance is proposed as one contributor to, not the sole cause of, the broader APOE4 microglial activation state.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["If accessible ER sterol sensing is the limiting bottleneck, then experimentally restoring the ER-accessible cholesterol pool in APOE4 microglia (e.g., delivering a soluble cholesterol-cyclodextrin complex) should reduce SREBF2, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24 and LDLR transcript levels toward APOE3-like values; if these specific transcripts fail to decrease while unrelated activation markers (e.g., CD36, GPNMB, ITGAX) also remain unchanged, this would favor a nonspecific global-activation explanation over the proposed sterol-sensing bottleneck, weakening this mechanism.", "If an LXR agonist (engaging the pathway partly indicated by MYLIP and CYP27A1 induction) fails to lower LDLR/SREBP2-target transcript levels specifically in APOE4 relative to APOE3 microglia, this would argue against a sterol-sensing/efflux-linked bottleneck and instead support a genotype-independent generalized transcriptional activation state, weakening this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA log-fold-change values show SREBF2 and its direct target INSIG1, together with cholesterol biosynthetic enzymes HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7 and DHCR24, and the uptake receptor LDLR, are all significantly higher in APOE4 than APOE3 (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR) -- an RNA abundance pattern, not a direct measurement of SREBP2 proteolytic activation or pathway flux.", "SREBP2 target genes are canonically repressed when ER/plasma-membrane-accessible ('regulatory') sterol is sufficient; sustained co-induction of this whole module is therefore consistent with (inferred, unmeasured) inadequate accessible-sterol sensing at the ER in APOE4 microglia, despite APOE4 being associated in prior unverified literature with impaired cholesterol trafficking/efflux.", "Concurrent RNA increases in NPC2 (lysosomal cholesterol egress) and SOAT1 (ER cholesterol esterification for neutral-lipid storage) (gene:NPC2, gene:SOAT1) suggest an inferred shift of cellular sterol handling toward lysosomal processing and storage rather than toward confirmed membrane availability.", "RNA increases in CYP27A1 (generates the oxysterol 27-hydroxycholesterol, an alternative sterol-elimination/LXR-ligand route) and MYLIP/IDOL (an LXR target that promotes LDLR protein degradation) plus ABCA7 (a non-LXR-restricted lipid/cholesterol transporter) (gene:CYP27A1, gene:MYLIP, gene:ABCA7) indicate partial engagement of compensatory export-adjacent pathways, while canonical LXR-driven efflux transporters ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from this measured gene set and cannot be evaluated (missing data).", "Because measured uptake/synthesis induction (LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24) is not matched by any measured canonical efflux transporter induction, the inferred net effect is a synthesis/uptake-biased sterol economy that could favor intracellular cholesterol and cholesteryl-ester accumulation over time; this flux conclusion is inferred, not observed.", "This sterol-handling imbalance is proposed as a plausible contributor to the broader disease-associated-microglia-like transcriptional shift also present in this dataset (e.g., gene:CD36, gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:FABP5, gene:APOE all elevated), representing a candidate convergence point rather than an established upstream cause of that state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show uncoupled SREBP2-driven sterol synthesis/uptake induction without matching measured efflux transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.023483365949119372, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2413858696707616, "cosine_similarity": 0.30580389089966165, "direction_accuracy": 0.040453074433656956, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6294563106796117, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.023483365949119372, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2413858696707616, "cosine_similarity": 0.30580389089966165, "direction_accuracy": 0.040453074433656956, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6294563106796117, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.4696864, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 2}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_024", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are on an unspecified logarithm base; only the sign and the rank of each gene within the supplied distribution are used, never an absolute fold-change magnitude.", "The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1), so absence of a gene such as HK1, PKM, LDHA or GAPDH means it did not pass that filter, not that it is unchanged or unmeasured; no unmeasured metabolite, ATP, NADPH, lactate or flux pool is claimed as observed.", "Because 77% of the supplied rows are positive (median +1.46), directionality is judged relative to the distribution median rather than to zero; this assumes the global up-shift is a normalisation/selection offset shared by all genes rather than a true uniform transcriptional amplification.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme protein and, in turn, for capacity; the hypothesis assumes rate control resides at HK/PFK rather than at a downstream step, which is not measured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; protein_spot:038 (ALDOA/ALDOC/SORD/ARPC1B/TKT), protein_spot:020 (GLUD1/FSCN1/ENO1/G6PD/EPX) and protein_spot:001 (HSP90B1/ACTN1/KRT1/HK3/KRT9) are treated as weak, non-assigning support only.", "Genotype comparison is isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the metadata, but biological replicate number is not supplied, and co-culture with astrocytes means some measured RNA may not be microglia-intrinsic.", "Causality is not established: APOE4 could act upstream of this metabolic program, or the program could reflect a different steady-state cell composition or maturation stage."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 lowers transcripts for the committed, ATP-consuming steps of upper glycolysis (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and for the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (PGD, TALDO1) while raising glucose-transporter, TCA-cycle, anaplerotic and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts; we hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck at glucose-6-phosphate formation and its phosphofructokinase step shifts carbon commitment from glycolysis/PPP to a mitochondrial, glutamine/glutamate-supported TCA program whose citrate is exported through SLC25A1 into an SREBF1-associated lipogenic route, making APOE4 microglia disproportionately dependent on glutamine anaplerosis rather than on glucose. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, activity, localisation and causal claims are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating substrate-tracing prediction: in the same isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, [U-13C6]glucose labelling should show lower fractional enrichment of lactate and of m+2 citrate/malate in APOE4, while [U-13C5]glutamine labelling should show higher m+4 succinate/malate and higher m+5/m+4 citrate enrichment in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or greater glucose-derived m+2 TCA labelling, or no gain in glutamine-derived labelling, the proposed carbon-commitment switch is falsified.", "Perturbation prediction (dependency flip): glutamine withdrawal or GLS inhibition (e.g. CB-839) should reduce basal and maximal oxygen consumption, ATP-linked respiration and phagocytic capacity more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose or a GLUT inhibitor should impair APOE3 more than APOE4. Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes to both drugs would weaken the mechanism.", "Bottleneck-identity prediction: total hexokinase and PFK Vmax in lysates, and HK2/PFKP protein by immunoblot, should be lower in APOE4; because HK1 did not pass the differential-expression filter, an unchanged total hexokinase activity would falsify HK-level control and force relocation of the bottleneck to PFK or to a downstream step.", "Rescue prediction: restoring flux past the block (HK2 or PFKP re-expression, or supplying membrane-permeant methyl-pyruvate) should normalise the APOE4 glutamine dependence and lower SREBF1/SCD-associated neutral-lipid droplet content; if lipid droplets are unchanged after rescue, the citrate-export-to-lipogenesis link (step 6) is falsified while the upstream block could still hold.", "Mito-nuclear prediction (weak step 7): quantitative mtDNA-encoded transcript and ATP6/CYB protein measurement with an assay independent of the probe-based single-cell platform should confirm reduced mtDNA-encoded subunits and reduced complex V/complex III assembly relative to nuclear subunits in APOE4. Concordant mtDNA-encoded transcripts, or normal supercomplex assembly, would remove step 7 without disproving steps 1-6.", "Negative-control prediction: the shift should be metabolic rather than a global amplification artefact - a spike-in-normalised or total-RNA-normalised assay should still show HK2, PFKP, PGD and TALDO1 below, and OGDH, MDH1, SLC25A1 above, the genotype-matched mean. If all genes move up together after such normalisation, the entire directional interpretation collapses."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show reduced transcripts for the committed upper-glycolytic kinases HK2, HK3 and PFKP (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP), each in the lowest quartile of the whole selected differential-expression distribution, despite increased glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux): if hexokinase and phosphofructokinase-P protein levels track these transcripts, imported glucose is poorly committed to glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-1,6-bisphosphate, so glycolytic flux, not glucose uptake capacity, becomes the bottleneck; downstream enzymes that are not rate-setting (gene:GPI, gene:ENO1) can still rise without relieving it.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred flux): the glucose-6-phosphate-consuming pentose-phosphate branch is also transcriptionally reduced (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1), consistent with less glucose carbon entering NADPH/ribose production, with gene:NNT and gene:PRDX3 up as an inferred mitochondrial NADPH/peroxide-handling compensation.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): a coherent mitochondrial oxidative program is coordinately higher in APOE4 - TCA and pyruvate-dehydrogenase-activating enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:SDHB, gene:PDP1), glutamine/glutamate and aspartate-malate anaplerosis (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC38A2, gene:SLC25A11) and 37 of 37 detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS8, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B), together with the adenine-nucleotide carrier gene:SLC25A5.", "Step 5 (inferred flux/localisation): with glucose-derived pyruvate limited, mitochondrial carbon is inferred to be supplied preferentially by glutamine/glutamate through GLS-GLUD1-GOT1 into 2-oxoglutarate, generating a glutamine-dependent oxidative ATP and citrate supply.", "Step 6 (inferred flux, links to lipid phenotype): increased gene:SLC25A1 is inferred to export TCA citrate to the cytosol where gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD and gene:DGAT1 transcripts define a lipogenic/desaturation-esterification route, coupling the carbon switch to neutral-lipid accumulation, while gene:SCARB1 marks an additional inferred lipid-uptake input.", "Step 7 (constraint on the compensation, lower confidence): several mtDNA-encoded ETC subunit transcripts are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2) while nuclear subunits rise, so the inferred oxidative compensation may be stoichiometrically incomplete; this step is flagged as weak because two mtDNA transcripts from the same heavy-strand unit move the other way (gene:MT-ND4L, gene:MT-ND5)."], "title": "Hexokinase/PFK-level restriction of glucose commitment forces APOE4 microglia onto a glutamine- and citrate-fed mitochondrial carbon program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0547945205479452, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2066078795423855, "cosine_similarity": 0.3056393306195543, "direction_accuracy": 0.09223300970873786, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6185566343042072, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0547945205479452, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2066078795423855, "cosine_similarity": 0.3056393306195543, "direction_accuracy": 0.09223300970873786, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6185566343042072, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.611887, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 296}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_005", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 1705 of 2212 rows are positive with median +1.46 in unspecified log units, so all pathway claims are made relative to this inflated internal background rather than to an absolute zero.", "Transcript abundance differences translate at least partially into enzyme abundance and pathway flux; no enzyme activity, metabolite, isotope-labelling or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are treated only as weakly consistent with increased cathepsin-family abundance and could be driven by other candidates in their lists (ACTB, TPM3, CLIC1, YWHAG/E, keratins).", "The 2D iPSC microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30 is at steady state under mock treatment, so differences reflect a chronic genotype-driven set point rather than an acute transient.", "The unmeasured steps of the proposed route (ACLY, FASN, ABCA1/ABCG1, LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2, CPT1A, neutral-lipid pools) behave as assumed rather than opposing the flux direction.", "No causal direction has been established by these data; APOE4 could act upstream of the esterification node or the transcriptional pattern could be a homeostatic response to an already-altered lipid state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional shift that moves carbon away from upper glycolysis/pentose-phosphate branches into mitochondrial TCA entry and citrate export, and couples this to an SREBF1-associated esterification module (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, SOAT1) together with raised lipid-import transcripts (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR). We hypothesise that the SCD-dependent monounsaturated-fatty-acid/esterification step is the rate-controlling bottleneck that converts this carbon and lipid supply into stored neutral lipid, and that the concurrent TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase induction is a downstream compensatory catabolic response rather than the initiating lesion. Flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not measured; the lipid pool itself is not measured in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566, 48-72 h, mock conditions) applied to isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should reduce the APOE4-minus-APOE3 difference in BODIPY/LipidTOX neutral-lipid signal by at least half, with a larger absolute effect in APOE4 than APOE3, while leaving the TCA and lysosomal hydrolase transcript elevations largely intact. If the genotype difference in neutral lipid is unchanged by SCD inhibition, or if SCD inhibition normalises the TCA/lysosomal transcript signature before affecting lipid, the proposed esterification bottleneck is wrong.", "Second discriminating test: 13C6-glucose and 13C2-acetate tracing should show greater label incorporation into APOE4 triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester, and SLC25A1 blockade (CTPI-2) or ACSS2 inhibition should preferentially suppress that labelled fraction in APOE4. If the APOE4 lipid excess is entirely derived from exogenous labelled fatty acid or lipoprotein and is insensitive to SLC25A1/ACSS2 blockade, the mitochondrial citrate-export step should be dropped in favour of a pure uptake/efflux-imbalance model.", "Flux direction test: Seahorse and 13C-TCA labelling should show equal or higher basal oxygen consumption and citrate/glutamate labelling in APOE4. Observing lower mitochondrial flux in APOE4 despite the elevated TCA transcripts would falsify the inference that these transcript changes report increased TCA carbon throughput.", "Ordering test: DGAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 lipid from droplet triacylglycerol toward free fatty acid and increase lipotoxicity/ER-stress markers, whereas SCD inhibition should lower total neutral lipid without that free-fatty-acid rise. A failure to separate these two outcomes would argue that the esterification module is not the controlling node.", "Sufficiency/necessity test: SCARB1 or CD36 knockdown should only partially reduce the APOE4 lipid excess, whereas TFEB overexpression (raising lysosomal hydrolase capacity) should not normalise it. If TFEB overexpression alone abolishes the genotype difference, the lysosomal step is primary and this hypothesis is demoted.", "Negative control from the assigned focus: canonical UPR readouts (HSPA5/BiP and PDIA3 protein, XBP1 splicing, ATF4/CHOP protein) should not be substantially higher in mock APOE4 than APOE3. Clear constitutive UPR activation would favour an ER-proteostasis mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry, TCA enzymes and mitochondrial carriers are coordinately higher in APOE4 (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, OGDH, ACO2, IDH3B, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A46; set median +4.5 reported log units vs +1.46 list-wide, Mann-Whitney p~1e-6), while upper-glycolysis and pentose-phosphate transcripts are lower (HK2, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD; set median -1.2). Inferred, not measured: a greater share of carbon is committed to mitochondrial TCA turnover rather than glycolytic/PPP side branches.", "Measured: the mitochondrial citrate/malate carrier SLC25A1 and the acetate-activating enzyme ACSS2 are elevated. Inferred: increased cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply. This step is weakly constrained because ACLY, ACACA and FASN are absent from the supplied differential-expression rows and no acetyl-CoA pool was measured.", "Measured: an SREBF1-associated esterification module is elevated (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, SOAT1, LPCAT1, FADS1; set median +3.0, p~0.01, above the size-matched permutation null upper bound of +2.9). Proposed bottleneck: SCD-generated monounsaturated acyl chains are the rate-controlling substrate for triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester synthesis, so esterification capacity, not lipid supply, sets the APOE4 lipid phenotype.", "Measured: lipid-import and lipoprotein-handling transcripts are higher (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, APOE, TREM2, ABCA7), although this set is not distinguishable from the inflated list background (p~0.7). Inferred: additional exogenous lipid entering the same esterification node; efflux transporters ABCA1 and ABCG1 were not measured, so the balance of efflux cannot be assessed.", "Measured: TFEB and a broad lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript set are elevated (GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, MAN2B1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H; median +2.4, p~0.02), and several protein spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins are increased. Inferred: a compensatory catabolic/lysosomal response to the esterified lipid load, not the primary driver.", "Predicted consequence (not observed here): APOE4 microglia accumulate more neutral lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester) in droplets and lysosomes under mock conditions, and this accumulation should be more sensitive to SCD or DGAT1 blockade than to changes in lipid uptake or lysosomal hydrolase capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial citrate/acetyl-CoA into an SREBF1-SCD esterification node, making neutral-lipid esterification the rate-controlling step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3118192223904294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31889297630168045, "cosine_similarity": 0.3038396532493289, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6288349514563107, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3118192223904294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.31889297630168045, "cosine_similarity": 0.3038396532493289, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6288349514563107, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.82909, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 297}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_044", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA log fold changes (base not specified in the workbook) are directionally comparable across genes, and pathway claims are made only relative to the global median (+1.46) of this selected, non-whole-transcriptome list.", "Transcript abundance is a partial proxy for enzyme/carrier protein amount; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, flux, respiration rate or lipid measurement is present in these data.", "The six mtDNA-encoded transcripts in the list are representative of mitochondrial gene expression and their reduction is biological rather than an ambient-RNA, QC-filtering or normalisation artefact of 10X Flex pseudobulk.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous, weakly corroborating evidence only; no spot is assumed to identify a unique protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture and iPSC-microglia differentiation state are matched between APOE3 and APOE4 arms, so genotype rather than cell-composition drift drives the difference.", "Causal direction (APOE4 -\u003e mitonuclear mismatch -\u003e citrate overflow -\u003e esterification) is hypothesised; the data are a single cross-sectional isogenic contrast and cannot establish it."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, transcripts for nuclear-encoded TCA, pyruvate/metabolite-carrier and respiratory-chain subunits are selectively elevated above the strongly positive global background while the six measured mtDNA-encoded respiratory transcripts are not (4/6 reduced). We propose that this mitonuclear subunit mismatch is the primary bottleneck: carbon entry into mitochondria is increased but terminal oxidation capacity (complexes III/IV/V, which need mtDNA-encoded cores) is not, so citrate/acetyl-unit carbon is exported through SLC25A1 and consumed by a SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 esterification program rather than being fully oxidised. Glycolysis is not coherently upregulated (rate-limiting HK2 and PFKP transcripts are among the most reduced), so the genotype difference is a routing difference in carbon fate, not a simple Warburg-like glycolytic switch. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity, localisation and direction of causation are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with U-13C-glucose and, separately, U-13C-glutamine, APOE4 microglia should show a higher fraction of label reaching cytosolic lipid pools (M+2 series in palmitate/oleate, cholesteryl esters, TAG) and a lower ratio of 13CO2 release to citrate labelling than isogenic APOE3. If APOE4 shows equal or lower lipid labelling from both tracers while CO2 release is unchanged or higher, the citrate-overflow mechanism is refuted.", "Assembly test: BN-PAGE or complexome profiling should show reduced assembled complex IV and complex V (and lower assembled-complex-per-nuclear-subunit ratio) in APOE4 despite the elevated nuclear-subunit transcripts, and Seahorse should show ATP-linked and maximal OCR that are not increased in proportion to those transcripts. If assembled complexes and ATP-linked/maximal OCR are increased in APOE4 in proportion to nuclear subunit transcripts, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Node-specific perturbation: inhibiting the citrate carrier (CTPI-2 / SLC25A1 knockdown) or SCD/DGAT1 should reduce APOE4-selective neutral-lipid droplet content without normalising the nuclear-versus-mtDNA transcript mismatch; failure to lower droplet content, or loss of the mismatch after these treatments, weakens the ordering of steps 3-5.", "Upstream rescue: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit availability (TFAM overexpression, or mitochondrial-biogenesis/NAD+ precursor treatment) should increase ATP-linked respiration and decrease lipid esterification markers in APOE4 more than in APOE3; equal or no response in APOE4 weakens the mitonuclear-mismatch claim.", "Glycolysis control test: 2-deoxyglucose or GLUT1 inhibition should not preferentially collapse APOE4 versus APOE3 ATP levels, because glycolytic transcripts are not coherently up (HK2 and PFKP reduced); a strong APOE4-selective glycolysis dependence would favour a glycolytic-shift alternative instead.", "Technical control: quantitative RT-PCR of MT-ATP6/MT-CO2/MT-CYB normalised to mtDNA copy number and to nuclear housekeeping RNA should confirm the reduction in APOE4; if the reduction disappears under this control, the mitonuclear evidence collapses and only the TCA/carrier elevation and lipid program survive."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured): Relative to the global positive shift of this selected differential-expression list (median +1.46 in the reported log unit), transcripts for mitochondrial carbon import and TCA enzymes are selectively high (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A5, gene:ACO2; set median +4.47, Mann-Whitney p=1.8e-5), together with glutamine-derived anaplerosis inputs (gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC1A5, gene:GLS).", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux): Increased carrier and dehydrogenase transcript abundance is assumed to raise pyruvate, malate-aspartate-shuttle and glutamate flux into the TCA cycle; the flux itself is not measured here.", "Step 3 (measured, primary bottleneck): Nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcripts are elevated (37 genes, median +2.64, p=1.6e-4; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2) whereas the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are not (median -1.56; gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 reduced; nuclear-vs-mtDNA contrast p=5.3e-4), predicting sub-stoichiometric assembly and a ceiling on complex III/IV/V-dependent terminal oxidation and ATP synthesis.", "Step 4 (inferred): With matrix carbon supply exceeding terminal oxidation capacity, citrate accumulates and is exported by the citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1, 91st percentile) and converted to cytosolic acetyl units, with gene:ACSS2 providing an additional acetate-derived route.", "Step 5 (measured downstream): A lipid-esterification program is coordinately high (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2; set median +2.04, p=0.03), predicting channelling of the exported carbon into monounsaturated fatty acids, glycerolipids and cholesteryl esters rather than CO2.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): Constrained ATP-linked respiration plus neutral-lipid accumulation produces the APOE4-specific state; a mitochondrial-stress/integrated-stress arm (gene:DELE1, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3) and a raised lysosomal-catabolic tone (gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1) are read as accompanying responses to lipid load, not as the initiating lesion."], "title": "Mitonuclear mismatch in APOE4 microglia caps terminal oxidation and diverts TCA carbon to citrate export and lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29382823173208283, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24295465348663894, "cosine_similarity": 0.3036381235627233, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_044", "mean_absolute_error": 0.63742071197411, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29382823173208283, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24295465348663894, "cosine_similarity": 0.3036381235627233, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.63742071197411, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6888195, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 298}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_035", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all effect magnitudes are compared on that unspecified scale and are not converted to fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1.0), so all enrichment statements are relative to that selected background (mean +1.39, 77% positive), not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The 10X Flex probe-based assay is assumed to quantify mtDNA-encoded transcripts in a way that is comparable between genotypes; if probe coverage, polyadenylation-dependent capture or an ambient/QC mitochondrial-fraction difference drives the MT- signal, step 2 collapses. This is the single most fragile assumption.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track subunit synthesis rate; no mitochondrial protein, complex-assembly, membrane-potential, mtDNA copy-number or respiration measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-confirmatory evidence about direction.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes; genotype-linked transcripts could partly reflect microglia-astrocyte cross-talk or ambient RNA rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be judged and the very large reported log values (up to 15.5) are treated as unreliable in magnitude but informative in direction."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-ordinately raise the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (every measured nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcript, plus TCA, carrier, import, mitochondrial-translation and complex-assembly transcripts) while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are relatively lower than the same cells' global RNA shift. We hypothesise that the availability of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of respiratory complexes I, III, IV and V; the resulting orphan nuclear-encoded subunit load is proposed to engage a mitochondrion-to-cytosol integrated stress response (DELE1 transcript strongly elevated, DDIT3/EIF2A/NUPR1/MANF elevated) in the absence of a canonical ER unfolded-protein response, and to be accompanied by citrate/acetyl-CoA-fuelled lipogenesis and a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal expansion. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION (mito-ISR vs ER-UPR): treating APOE4 microglia with ISRIB or with HRI/EIF2AK1 knockdown should normalise DDIT3, NUPR1 and MANF transcripts and blunt the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal program, while the nuclear-versus-mtDNA OXPHOS transcript imbalance persists; by contrast the IRE1 inhibitor 4u8C and the ATF6 inhibitor Ceapin-A7 should leave DDIT3 unchanged. If 4u8C or Ceapin-A7 suppresses DDIT3 as effectively as ISRIB, an ER-UPR origin is favoured and this mechanism is weakened.", "DELE1 knockout in APOE4 microglia should abolish DDIT3 induction without correcting the nuclear/mtDNA transcript ratio. Persistent DDIT3 induction in DELE1-null APOE4 cells would falsify the proposed relay step.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling should show, in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3, reduced assembled complex I, III, IV and V holoenzyme relative to total imported nuclear-encoded subunit protein, i.e. accumulation of sub-complexes and free nuclear-encoded subunits. Equal holo-complex levels and equal free-subunit pools would falsify the bottleneck.", "Raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or POLRMT overexpression, or mitochondrially targeted rescue of ND4/CYB/CO2/ATP6) should increase assembled complexes, lower DELE1 and DDIT3, and reduce lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts in APOE4 cells. No change in DELE1/DDIT3 after successful rescue of mtDNA-encoded transcripts would weaken the mechanism.", "Conversely, partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation (doxycycline or chloramphenicol) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature: coordinate nuclear OXPHOS subunit up-regulation, DELE1/DDIT3 induction, and CLEAR expansion, without induction of HSPA5, XBP1s, HERPUD1 or DNAJB9. Induction of the ER-UPR module in that phenocopy, or failure to reproduce the nuclear OXPHOS rise, would weaken the mechanism.", "Seahorse respirometry should show reduced maximal and spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrion (normalised to citrate-synthase activity or TOMM20) in APOE4 despite the elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcript program; equal or higher normalised maximal OCR would directly contradict the claimed assembly bottleneck.", "Orthogonal quantification (ddPCR for mtDNA copy number and mtDNA-encoded transcripts, plus RNA-FISH) should confirm lower MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2/MT-ND4 per cell in APOE4. Equal levels by these platform-independent assays would indicate the MT- signal is a 10X Flex capture artefact and would falsify step 2 and therefore the whole hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coherent increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - all 38 measured NDUF/COX/ATP5/UQCR/SDH subunit rows are positive (mean +2.81 in the reported log unit vs +1.39 for all 2212 selected DE rows; permutation p_up = 0.0003; 38/38 positive vs 77% background, binomial p ~ 6e-5), together with TCA/carrier genes (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, DLD, MPC2, SLC25A46), the import motor (TIMM44), mitochondrial translation factors (TUFM, GFM2, MTPAP) and assembly factors (NDUFAF4, COX20). INFERRED: increased synthesis of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits and increased demand for matrix import and assembly.", "MEASURED (RNA): in the same comparison the six mtDNA-encoded rows behave oppositely to the global upward shift (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; MT-ND4L +1.95, MT-ND5 +1.93; set mean -0.82, permutation p_down = 0.019). Nuclear vs mtDNA-encoded contrast: Mann-Whitney p = 4.6e-4, difference of means 3.63. INFERRED: the mtDNA-encoded transcript pool does not scale with the nuclear program.", "PROPOSED BOTTLENECK (inferred, not measured): assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V stalls at incorporation of their mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores (ND4/ND4L, CYB, CO2, ATP6), so imported nuclear-encoded subunits accumulate as unassembled 'orphan' species in the matrix and inner membrane and holo-complex flux fails to rise in proportion to subunit transcription. No complexome, in-gel activity, respirometry or mitochondrial protein measurement is supplied, so this step is a prediction, not an observation.", "INFERRED SIGNALLING: orphan-subunit proteotoxic load and inner-membrane stress engage the OMA1-DELE1-HRI relay to the eIF2-alpha arm of the integrated stress response. Consistent RNA evidence: DELE1 +4.82, DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2A +9.25, EIF2AK3 +1.51, NUPR1 +1.24, MANF +2.95. The activated protein states (cleaved DELE1, phospho-eIF2-alpha, ATF4 protein) are NOT measured here.", "COUNTER-DIRECTIONAL to an ER origin: the ER-restricted UPR module is not co-induced. ERAD and ER-lumen genes that pass the same DE threshold are negative (SEL1L -2.09, EDEM1 -1.37, DERL1 -1.19, PDIA3 -1.26, SEC24D -1.39, GOSR1 -3.19), the ERAD set trends below background (permutation p_down = 0.084), and the three 2-D spots whose candidate lists contain the ER chaperones HSP90B1/HSPA5 are non-significant and negative (spots 001, 004, 005). The ER-proteostasis focus is therefore rejected as the primary bottleneck; DDIT3 is read as an ISR, not an ER-UPR, marker.", "DOWNSTREAM CONSEQUENCE (inferred): with terminal oxidation constrained, mitochondrial carbon is rerouted to lipogenesis rather than glycolysis - citrate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA genes rise (SLC25A1 +4.47, ACSS2 +2.93, ME1 +1.36) and sterol/fatty-acid genes rise (SREBF1 +4.68, SCD +4.16), whereas the glycolytic set is not raised (mean -0.13, median -1.12, below the +1.39 background).", "COMPENSATORY ORGANELLE RESPONSE (inferred): damaged-mitochondria and lipid-ester cargo drive a TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal expansion - TFEB +2.38, MITF +1.03, lysosomal hydrolases (GAA +10.0, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.68, HEXA +5.72, SMPD1 +5.60, CTSB +5.53; set mean +3.29, permutation p_up = 0.002) and v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H +6.90, ATP6V1A +4.24; set mean +2.55, p_up = 0.076)."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance, not ER unfolded-protein stress, distinguishes APOE4 microglia: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply is the OXPHOS assembly bottleneck that relays an OMA1-DELE1-type integrated stress response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2734279806520695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19756859824391002, "cosine_similarity": 0.30315116863238867, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_035", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6266375404530744, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2734279806520695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19756859824391002, "cosine_similarity": 0.30315116863238867, "direction_accuracy": 0.2605177993527508, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6266375404530744, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.64785275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 299}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_020", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e=1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a strong global upward bias (77.1% up, median +1.46); all set-level claims are made relative to that internal background, and the log base is left as reported.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for subunit supply; enzyme activity, assembly state, respiratory flux, membrane potential, oxidant concentrations and mtDNA copy number were not measured in these data.", "The lower MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-ND4/MT-CO2 values reflect a genuine genotype difference in mtDNA-encoded transcript abundance rather than a 10X Flex probe-set, ambient-RNA or cell-QC artefact; the discordant MT-ND5/MT-ND4L increases are treated as noise or transcript-specific processing differences.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features, not uniquely identified proteins; no spot contains an OXPHOS subunit candidate, so the protein layer is treated as neutral for the core claim (e.g. the largest spots 043-046 are consistent with ANXA1, whose transcript is +4.15, as much as with TALDO1, whose transcript is -2.32).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on microglial transcripts may be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "The observed differences are associations with APOE4 genotype in an isogenic comparison; no perturbation establishing causality is present in the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, TCA and mitochondrial-import transcripts that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 lower in APOE4). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is assembly of complete, mtDNA-subunit-containing respiratory complexes (notably CIV/CV): the nuclear pool is expanded while the matrix-encoded core is relatively scarce, so respiratory chain assembly and coupled electron flux - not mitochondrial mass - become limiting. The inferred consequences are increased electron leak and matrix oxidant load (matching selective upregulation of matrix/membrane antioxidant transcripts PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT rather than a cytosolic NRF2 or peroxisomal catalase program), an integrated stress response (DDIT3, EIF2AK3), AMPK-alpha1 and TFEB induction, and compensatory glucose-transporter/glycolytic-entry transcription. Causality is not established by these data; the discovery layer measures transcript and spot abundance only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, the ratio of mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded subunit protein (MT-CO1/COX4I1, MT-ATP6/ATP5F1A by immunoblot) will be reduced, and blue-native PAGE will show relatively increased CIV/CV subassemblies with preserved or increased nuclear-subunit input; unchanged ratios and normal assembly profiles would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20 signal) will show lower ATP-linked and maximal oxygen consumption per unit mass in APOE4, with mass equal or higher; equal or higher mass-normalised respiration would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy test: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation in APOE3 microglia (doxycycline or chloramphenicol, titrated to preserve viability) should reproduce the APOE4 pattern - nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts up, DDIT3 and PRKAA1 up, PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4 up, SLC2A1/SLC2A3 up; absence of this pattern would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue test: increasing mtDNA-encoded output or bypassing the deficit (mitochondrially targeted rescue of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB, or expression of yeast NDI1/AOX to relieve chain congestion) should lower DDIT3 and PRDX3/GPX4 transcripts and restore mass-normalised respiration in APOE4; persistence of the stress signature after functional rescue would falsify step 4-5.", "Compartment test for the assigned redox focus: matrix-targeted roGFP2-Orp1/mito-SOX signal should be more oxidised in APOE4 while peroxisome-targeted HyPer and catalase activity are unchanged; a peroxisome-dominant oxidation shift, or induction of CAT/PEX transcripts on deeper sequencing, would support the peroxisomal alternative I reject here.", "Normalisation control: after re-quantification with spike-in or median-of-ratios normalisation on the full transcriptome, nuclear OXPHOS transcripts should remain enriched relative to the genome-wide background while MT-encoded transcripts remain relatively depleted; loss of this relative contrast would indicate the pattern is a global normalisation artefact and would falsify the hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with induction of a nuclear-encoded mitochondrial biogenesis-like transcriptional program: 38/38 measured nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts are higher in APOE4 (median +2.64 vs +1.46 background; permutation p~0.001), together with TCA/pyruvate-entry transcripts (OGDH, MDH1, MPC2, DLD, ACO2, IDH3B/G, SDHB; 8/8 up) and outer/inner-membrane import and chaperone transcripts (TOMM22, TIMM8B, TIMM44, HSPA9, PHB).", "The mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are not co-induced and are mostly lower in APOE4 (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 down; 4/6 measured MT genes down against a 77% up-shifted background, binomial p~0.03). Inferred, not measured: the ratio of mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded subunit protein available for assembly falls.", "Because CIV and CV cores and the CIII cytochrome b subunit are mtDNA-encoded, we infer that holo-complex assembly, not subunit supply from the nucleus, becomes the flux-limiting step; imported nuclear subunits accumulate in subassemblies or are degraded, so respiration per unit mitochondrial mass falls even though mitochondrial content markers rise.", "Inferred consequence: partially assembled/poorly coupled chains increase electron leak and matrix oxidant load. This is consistent with the selective transcript increase of matrix and membrane antioxidant/NADPH systems (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT, GSS, MGST2, PRDX2) in the absence of a canonical cytosolic NRF2 program (HMOX1, NQO1, GCLC/GCLM, TXNRD1, SOD1/2, CAT are not in the differential list) and in the absence of a peroxisomal response (no PEX genes; ABCD1 down); oxidant levels themselves were not measured here.", "Energetic and proteostatic stress signalling is engaged: PRKAA1 (AMPK-alpha1), DDIT3 (CHOP) and EIF2AK3 (PERK) transcripts are up, consistent with an ATF4/CHOP-type integrated stress response to mito-nuclear imbalance; direction of causality between this response and the OXPHOS transcript increase is not resolved by these data.", "Compensation and downstream burden: glucose-transport/glycolytic-entry transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3, GPI, ENO1, HIF1A) and a TFEB-associated lysosomal/lipid-handling program (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V subunits, SCARB1, LDLR, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, APOE) are up, which we interpret as an ATP- and NAD+-sparing shift plus increased lysosomal/lipid-droplet routing of substrate that cannot be fully oxidised."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch: an upregulated nuclear OXPHOS/TCA program outruns mtDNA-encoded core subunits in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14474024295683638, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2044295986235092, "cosine_similarity": 0.302968957390228, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6250970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14474024295683638, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2044295986235092, "cosine_similarity": 0.302968957390228, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6250970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8062915, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 300}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set statistics are enrichment relative to this already-biased background (77% of rows positive, median +1.46), not relative to all genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect sizes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes up to +15.5 are treated as ordinal, not as fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein supply; no lysosomal protein, enzyme-activity, pH, cargo-flux, autophagic-flux or lipid measurement is supplied, so all flux, localisation and capacity statements are inferred.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "The isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast under mock treatment is assumed free of clone-specific and batch artefacts; replicate structure is stated as not supplied in the workbook.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous (e.g. via astrocyte-derived lipoproteins) rather than intrinsic to microglia.", "Gene-set membership was assigned from unverified background knowledge of lysosomal biology (no literature or database retrieval was performed); set boundaries are therefore approximate."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 selectively raises transcripts encoding luminal lysosomal glycosidases and sphingolipid hydrolases above the strong global up-shift of this selected differential-expression set, while transcripts for cargo delivery, autophagosome-lysosome fusion, mannose-6-phosphate-receptor sorting and endosomal recycling are not coordinately raised and several are reduced. We hypothesise that the resulting stoichiometric mismatch makes substrate delivery to, and product egress from, the late endosome-lysosome the rate-limiting step, so that increased hydrolase gene supply does not translate into proportional clearance of internalised glycoconjugate and lipid cargo; the hydrolase program is therefore read as a compensatory, load-driven response rather than as evidence of increased degradative flux. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: in APOE4 microglia, restoring the delivery/fusion arm (STX17 re-expression, or HOPS/ARL8B- or TRPML1-agonist-driven fusion) should reduce accumulated LacCer/BODIPY- or filipin-positive endolysosomal cargo and lower the hydrolase transcript excess, whereas over-expressing a single luminal hydrolase (GBA or HEXB) or constitutively active TFEB should NOT normalise cargo. If hydrolase or TFEB over-expression alone normalises cargo clearance, the delivery-limited bottleneck is wrong and enzyme supply was limiting.", "FLUX TEST: pulse-chase of a defined cargo (DQ-BSA, fluorescent myelin or acLDL) should show APOE4 with equal or greater cargo internalisation and equal or greater lysosomal hydrolase protein, but a lower degradation rate per unit internalised cargo. If normalised degradation rate is equal to or higher than APOE3, the mechanism is weakened.", "LOAD-DEPENDENCE TEST: culturing APOE4 microglia in lipoprotein-poor medium or blocking scavenger-mediated uptake should collapse the glycosidase/sphingolipid-hydrolase transcript excess toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the hydrolase excess under cargo-free conditions would refute the load-driven feed-forward step and favour a constitutive transcriptional difference.", "CARGO SELECTIVITY TEST: APOE4 should show a glycosphingolipid/glycoconjugate-biased accumulation with relatively preserved bulk proteolysis (consistent with the divergent cathepsin pattern including gene:CTSS). A uniform deficit across protein, glycolipid and nucleic-acid cargo would argue for a generic lysosomal failure rather than the proposed selective mismatch.", "SPECIFICITY VS BIOENERGETIC ALTERNATIVE: ratiometric lysosomal pH and V-ATPase-dependent acidification should be at most mildly different between genotypes, and the hydrolase enrichment should survive expression-matched background correction. If lysosomal pH is markedly raised and the hydrolase enrichment disappears once genes are matched to expression-level-matched controls, the signal is better explained by the global up-shift and by the stronger nuclear-OXPHOS transcript shift than by a lysosome-specific mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (transcript abundance only): the luminal glycosidase/sphingolipid-hydrolase group (GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SGSH, MAN2B1, GLA, SMPD1, AGA) is shifted upward relative to the rest of the supplied differential-expression rows (group median +2.40 vs global median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified-base log units; Mann-Whitney p=0.011), i.e. it exceeds the pervasive 77%-up background of this row set.", "INFERRED (activity/regulation, not measured): this pattern reflects a MiT/TFE-type compensatory transcriptional response to an increased undegraded cargo load; TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) but TFEB phosphorylation, nuclear localisation and lysosomal mTORC1 signalling were not measured.", "MEASURED (transcript abundance only): the machinery that delivers cargo and hydrolases to lysosomes and recycles membrane is not coordinately elevated (delivery/fusion/recycling group median +1.41, indistinguishable from background, Mann-Whitney p=0.82), and several members are decreased (gene:STX17 -2.06, gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:WASHC4 -2.10, gene:STAM2 -1.67) while others are only at background (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:ARL8B +1.05, gene:EPG5 +2.96).", "INFERRED BOTTLENECK (flux, not measured): because hydrolase supply rises but delivery, fusion and receptor-mediated hydrolase sorting/recycling do not, degradative flux per unit internalised cargo becomes limited by substrate-hydrolase encounter and by product egress rather than by enzyme availability; no pH, DQ-BSA, LysoTracker, autophagic-flux or lipid measurement is present in these data to test this directly.", "INFERRED CONSEQUENCE (composition/localisation, not measured): partially degraded glycosphingolipid and other glycoconjugate cargo accumulates in APOE4 late endosomes/lysosomes, sustaining the hydrolase program as a feed-forward loop; lipogenic and sterol transcripts that would accompany diversion of lipid to storage are elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25) but are NOT enriched above the global up-shift (p=0.22), so this step is the weakest link in the chain.", "MEASURED DIVERGENCE: the proteolytic arm is not co-regulated with the glycosidase arm (cathepsins as a group are not enriched, p=0.26; gene:CTSS -5.57 opposes gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36), predicting a cargo-selective rather than a global degradative deficit in APOE4."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate the luminal glycosidase/sphingolipid-hydrolase arm without matched cargo-delivery and recycling machinery, leaving endolysosomal degradative flux delivery-limited"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10435151994877942, "cosine_similarity": 0.30247149635473813, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6302297734627832, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10435151994877942, "cosine_similarity": 0.30247149635473813, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6302297734627832, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.95936775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 301}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_060", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 in an unspecified logarithm base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 positive / 507 negative of 2212); program directionality is judged against that 77%-positive background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (e.g., G6PD, CAT, SOD1/2, TFAM, CPT1A, ABCA1, ATF4 were not supplied as RNA rows).", "Increased transcript abundance for lysosomal hydrolases, carriers and respiratory subunits is assumed to translate into increased protein and enzymatic capacity; no mitochondrial or lipogenic protein was independently quantified here (only protein_spot:050 lists MDH1 among candidates, non-significant), so capacity and flux are inferred, not observed.", "2D protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each; all candidates are retained and no spot is treated as confirmation of a single protein. The largest increases (protein_spot:043-046) list both ANXA1 (RNA +4.15) and TALDO1 (RNA -2.32) among candidates and are therefore directionally uninformative for either.", "The relative decrease in four mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed not to be the primary driver in this comparison; it may reflect compositional/normalization effects of a broadly upregulated selected list or probe-based 10X Flex quantification, and two mtDNA-encoded genes (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L) are increased.", "Reduced pentose-phosphate transcripts are assumed to indicate reduced reserve capacity for cytosolic NADPH regeneration under future challenge, not an ongoing redox failure in the measured mock condition; no GSH/GSSG, NADPH, ROS or lipid-peroxidation measurement is supplied.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some lipid substrate is supplied non-cell-autonomously; the microglial transcript state is assumed to reflect that steady-state exposure equally in both genotypes."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 not by an ongoing oxidative-stress lesion or peroxisomal failure, but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and sterol-lipogenesis (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1; 18/18 represented members positive vs a 77% positive selected-list background) and for lysosomal hydrolysis/acidification (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) rise together with a uniformly increased mitochondrial pyruvate-import/TCA/nuclear-encoded ETC program (47/47 represented members positive: gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:SLC25A1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ETFA), while committed glycolytic steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite higher glucose transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3). Thiol/peroxide defenses scale in parallel (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:GSS, gene:TXNDC17, gene:NNT, gene:FTH1, with gene:ACSL4 and gene:ALOX15 decreased), which we read as redox buffering matched to higher oxidative lipid-catabolic throughput (successful adaptation) rather than a stress response to damage. The one redox asymmetry is a lowered cytosolic NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate arm at the transcript level (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32) with no corresponding protein-spot increase (protein_spot:021, candidates G6PD/GSR/PGD/EPX/IFIT1, +0.263, not significant), predicting reduced antioxidant reserve that would be revealed only by a future oxidative or phagocytic challenge, not a defect measurable in the mock condition. Causality is not established; all statements are transcript/spot abundance, not measured flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with a larger fraction of respiration suppressed by acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or CPT1 inhibition (etomoxir), and lower glycolytic rate/extracellular acidification than APOE3. If APOE4 respiration is equal to or lower than APOE3 and is not preferentially MPC/CPT1-sensitive, the routing step (steps 3-4) is wrong and a mitochondrial-capacity-deficit model is favoured.", "Prospective challenge test: after an acute peroxide bolus or a myelin/apoptotic-cell phagocytic load, APOE4 cells should deplete GSH/NADPH and accumulate C11-BODIPY lipid peroxidation faster than APOE3 despite higher gene:PRDX3/gene:GPX4 transcripts, and 6-aminonicotinamide (G6PD/PGD inhibition) should sensitize APOE4 selectively. Equal or better APOE4 buffering, and no genotype-selective 6-AN effect, would falsify the narrowed-NADPH-reserve claim (step 6).", "Prospective baseline test that discriminates adaptation from damage: in mock, APOE4 should NOT show a substantial increase in 4-HNE adducts, protein carbonyls or mitoSOX signal relative to APOE3, and matrix peroxiredoxin protein should be higher. Clear baseline oxidative damage with unchanged or lower antioxidant protein would favour the failed-compensation alternative over adaptive buffering.", "Prospective causal test of the lysosome-to-mitochondria link: TFEB knockdown (or bafilomycin A1 / acid-lipase inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should reduce hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXA, CTSB assays), reduce neutral-lipid-derived respiration and collapse the APOE4-specific excess OCR toward APOE3 levels. Preserved excess respiration after blocking lysosomal catabolism would falsify step 2-3 coupling and imply an independent mitochondrial program.", "Prospective stoichiometry test of the main alternative: blue-native assembly assays and complex IV/V activity per unit nuclear-encoded subunit protein should be preserved in APOE4. If assembled complex IV/V activity is disproportionately low relative to nuclear-subunit protein (matching gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4 decreases), the mitonuclear-imbalance/failed-compensation mechanism should replace this one.", "Prospective peroxisome test (focus rejection is falsifiable): peroxisome number/import (PEX5-dependent PTS1 reporter) and very-long-chain fatty-acid C26:0 levels should be similar between genotypes; a clear VLCFA accumulation or PTS1 import defect in APOE4 would show peroxisomal capacity, not the lysosome-mitochondria axis, is the primary differentiator."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises the transcriptional set-point for lipid/lipoprotein internalization and sterol-fatty-acid synthesis and esterification (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), increasing the intracellular lipid-handling load (abundance measured; uptake flux inferred).", "A coordinated lysosomal-degradative expansion (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:GLA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GM2A, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:LAMP1) provides capacity to hydrolyse internalized membrane/lipid cargo into fatty acids, sphingoid bases and sterols.", "Liberated carbon is routed preferentially into mitochondria rather than to glycolytic lactate: mitochondrial pyruvate and citrate carriers plus TCA and electron-transfer flavoprotein transcripts increase (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:MDH1, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:ETFA) while the committed glycolytic kinases fall (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP) despite increased transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunit transcripts increase uniformly across all four complexes and the ATP synthase (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:NDUFB6, gene:SDHB, gene:UQCRC2, gene:UQCR11, gene:COX7A2, gene:COX6B1, gene:COX20, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:NDUFAF4), consistent with expanded (not necessarily realized) oxidative capacity and higher matrix electron flux.", "Higher electron and lipid flux raises the potential for matrix peroxide and lipid-peroxidation; APOE4 cells co-induce matrix and thiol peroxidases and glutathione/iron handling (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:PRDX2, gene:GPX4, gene:GSS, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:CYB5R3, gene:FTH1, gene:PCBP1) and lower peroxidation-prone lipid-remodelling enzymes (gene:ACSL4, gene:ALOX15), so the mock-state is redox-buffered rather than overtly damaged; compatible spot-level signals include protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5, +0.766, significant) and protein_spot:077 (candidates including PRDX2, +1.07, significant), both ambiguous in identity.", "Because the cytosolic NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate arm is transcriptionally lower (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) with no protein-spot support for a compensating increase (protein_spot:021, protein_spot:018, protein_spot:019, protein_spot:020, all non-significant), reductant supply for peroxiredoxin/glutathione recycling depends disproportionately on mitochondrial sources (gene:NNT, gene:ME1), predicting a narrowed reserve that becomes limiting only under an added oxidant or phagocytic-lipid load."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lipid-uptake/lysosome-fed, mitochondrially-oxidative cell state with matched thiol-peroxide buffering and a narrowed cytosolic NADPH reserve"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26755713916478974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23022531716240685, "cosine_similarity": 0.30231073802519404, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6224077669902913, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26755713916478974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23022531716240685, "cosine_similarity": 0.30231073802519404, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6224077669902913, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.9186975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 76}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_003", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, 100% adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directionality is judged against that 77%-positive background, and absent genes (e.g. CPT1A, MCOLN1, PSAP, GRN, most ribosomal/mitoribosomal genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Coherent transcript direction is descriptive, not a formal enrichment result; genes within a program are co-regulated and not independent, so nominal permutation values (respiratory chain 40/40 positive, p_pos\u003c1e-3; curated 98-gene endolysosomal set 33 of 36 represented positive, p_pos~0.02) are indicative only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to track enzyme and transporter protein availability; no hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo-degradation flux, lipid-droplet content, oxygen-consumption or substrate-tracing measurement was supplied, so 'increased throughput' is inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5); no spot identifies a single protein, so spot changes are treated as compatibility tests only and all candidate identities are retained.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increase is assumed to reflect increased CLEAR-network output; nuclear translocation and mTORC1 status were not measured.", "The direction lysosomal-cargo-load -\u003e mitochondrial oxidation is inferred from co-occurrence; the reverse (a primary bioenergetic/mitochondrial shift driving lysosomal expansion) cannot be excluded with these data.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured; genotype effects on microglia could be partly non-cell-autonomous, and any depth/compositional difference between genotypes could inflate a global positive shift.", "Reduced reserve under a future lipid or debris challenge is a prediction; the mock condition does not establish an ongoing degradative defect."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated cell-state change rather than a single bottleneck: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:COLEC12, gene:ABCA7) and for phagocytic/opsonic receptors (gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:MRC1) are higher together with a broad endolysosomal degradative module (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF, hydrolases gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, all ten supplied v-ATPase subunit rows (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C and seven further ATP6 rows), lysosomal solute carriers gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5) and with the single most internally consistent program in the data, mitochondrial oxidative catabolism (40/40 supplied NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDHB/CYCS/ETFA rows positive; gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:GLUD1; beta-oxidation gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1, gene:ETFA). We propose that elevated lipid-cargo influx drives a TFEB/MITF-associated expansion of lysosomal hydrolytic and acidification capacity whose hydrolysis products are routed to mitochondrial oxidation and to re-esterification/storage (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD), while the hydrolase repertoire is remodelled rather than uniformly raised (gene:CTSS -5.6, gene:IDS -1.6, gene:M6PR -1.7 against gene:IGF2R +2.0, with gene:CD74 +3.8 and gene:CIITA +1.5). This is a claim about coordinated increased catabolic throughput/adaptation in the measured mock condition, not an established lysosomal defect; degradative flux, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and oxygen consumption were not measured here, so causality and direction remain inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, live-cell degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching, BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester or myelin-debris clearance rate) and basal/maximal oxygen consumption with 13C/2H label transfer from lipid cargo into TCA intermediates should be equal to or higher in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows slower DQ-BSA dequenching, undegraded cargo accumulation and lower oxygen consumption despite the elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and respiratory-chain transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:NDUFA5), the 'increased throughput/adaptation' mechanism is falsified in favour of failed compensation.", "Prospective TFEB-dependence test: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown or constitutive mTORC1 activation in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase plus v-ATPase module (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1A) and reduce lipid-derived mitochondrial oxidation. Persistence of the module after TFEB loss would falsify step 2.", "Prospective coupling test: blocking cargo influx (SR-B1/CD36/LDLR blockade or lipoprotein-free medium) should reduce the lysosomal module and the respiratory-chain/TCA increase together. If the mitochondrial program stays elevated while the lysosomal program falls, the lysosome-upstream ordering is wrong and a primary bioenergetic mechanism is favoured.", "Prospective repertoire test: APOE4 microglia should show reduced CTSS-selective protease activity and accumulation of the CD74 p10 invariant-chain fragment relative to APOE3, despite higher total cathepsin B/D/L activity. Equal CTSS activity and normal CD74 processing would falsify the selective-remodelling step (gene:CTSS, gene:CD74, gene:CIITA).", "Prospective challenge test: under a myelin-debris or oxLDL load, APOE4 should show a lower incremental increase in degradative capacity and earlier lipid-droplet or undigested-cargo accumulation than APOE3, even though the mock state shows no clearance deficit. Identical challenge responses would remove the reduced-reserve component without affecting the mock-state claim.", "Prospective proteomic test: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS resolving the ambiguous spots (protein_spot:052 CTSL candidate, protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:027 CTSD candidates, protein_spot:055/057 CTSB candidates, protein_spot:006/007 GNS candidate, protein_spot:012 MAN2B1 candidate) should confirm higher mature cathepsin and glycosidase protein in APOE4; if these spots resolve instead to keratin/actin or other candidates with unchanged cathepsin protein, protein-level support for expanded hydrolytic capacity is withdrawn."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises the flux of lipoprotein- and phagocytic-cargo entering microglial endosomes: uptake and opsonic-receptor transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:COLEC12, gene:ABCA7, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:MRC1); receptor abundance is measured, uptake rate is inferred.", "The increased lipid/membrane cargo load engages a TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR-type transcriptional response (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), expanding lysosomal biosynthetic output rather than being limited by it.", "This expands luminal hydrolytic and acidification capacity: glyco- and sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:DNASE2), cathepsins (gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH), membrane/structural components (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3) and all supplied v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2), together with delivery/maturation machinery (gene:IGF2R, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1, gene:AP3D1, gene:PIK3C3, gene:VPS18, gene:ATG9A).", "Hydrolysis products (fatty acids, sterols, amino acids) leave the lysosome (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:NPC2) and are routed preferentially into mitochondrial oxidation: beta-oxidation/electron-transfer (gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1, gene:ETFA), TCA and anaplerosis (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:GLUD1), carriers/import (gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11, gene:TOMM22, gene:TUFM) and a uniformly positive respiratory-chain module (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B and 33 further NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5 rows).", "Overflow lipid is buffered by re-esterification and storage/desaturation rather than accumulating as free lipid (gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:MGLL), with modest sterol-synthesis and SREBP-arm transcripts also higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1).", "The expansion is selective, not global: gene:CTSS falls strongly while gene:CD74 and gene:CIITA rise and gene:M6PR falls against gene:IGF2R, predicting a repertoire shift toward bulk lipid/glycoconjugate catabolism and away from CTSS-dependent invariant-chain/antigen processing and away from some sulfatase steps (gene:IDS).", "The net measured phenotype is a DAM/lipid-processing-like state (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:FABP5, gene:TIMP2, gene:APOE) with retained homeostatic identity transcripts (gene:CSF1R, gene:IRF8, gene:MEF2C, gene:MAFB, gene:GPR34); reserve capacity under a future lipid challenge may nonetheless be lower, which the mock condition cannot test."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a coordinated high-throughput lipid-catabolic state: increased lipoprotein/phagocytic cargo influx with TFEB/MITF-associated endolysosomal expansion routed into mitochondrial oxidation, with selective loss of CTSS-type processing"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2696720007319578, "cosine_similarity": 0.30208425397168914, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6305695792880259, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24113835247203042, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2696720007319578, "cosine_similarity": 0.30208425397168914, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6305695792880259, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.466171, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 77}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_085", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so all set-level statements are made against the internal distribution of this list (median +1.46, 77% positive) rather than against an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified and effects are used only as ranks and signs.", "Elevated hydrolase, receptor and biosynthetic transcripts correspond to proportionally increased protein and enzymatic activity in the relevant organelle; this was not measured for any of these genes.", "TFEB and SREBP activity are inferred from coherence of their putative target transcripts, not from measured nuclear localization, cleavage state, or occupancy.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; the ANXA1 assignment for spots 043-047 is favoured only because the co-listed candidate TALDO1 has a negative RNA effect, and this remains an assumption.", "No lipid, cholesterol, organelle-imaging, flux, or lysosomal pH measurement is supplied; lysosomal retention, ER-accessible sterol depletion, and lipid-droplet expansion are predictions, not observations.", "Genotype comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, but replicate structure is not supplied, so effect precision and any batch or culture-composition confound cannot be assessed; causality is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells primarily because lipid delivered into an expanded endolysosomal compartment is not efficiently exported to the endoplasmic reticulum. The rate-limiting step is inferred sterol/lipid egress from the lysosome, not lipid supply, degradation capacity, or ER unfolded-protein signalling. Because the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool therefore stays low, SREBP-dependent uptake and biosynthesis transcripts remain de-repressed while esterification and storage transcripts rise, producing continued lipid accrual in lysosomes and lipid droplets. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; the transport step, sensor state, and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or restoring NPC1/NPC2 function) should bypass the lysosomal egress step and normalize SREBP-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, LDLR, SCD) and SOAT1/DGAT1 toward APOE3 levels while reducing lysosomal unesterified cholesterol, whereas blocking uptake instead (SCARB1 inhibition by BLT-1, or CD36 blockade) should lower total cell lipid without normalizing those SREBP targets. If cyclodextrin lowers lysosomal cholesterol yet leaves the SREBP-target elevation intact, or if uptake blockade alone normalizes it, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Imaging/biochemistry: filipin or anti-cholesterol probe staining should show greater unesterified cholesterol co-localizing with LAMP1 in APOE4 than APOE3, while the ER-accessible sterol pool (ALOD4/D4H probe accessibility) should be lower in APOE4 despite equal or greater total cellular cholesterol. Equal lysosomal cholesterol, or an equal-to-higher ER-accessible pool in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Lipidomic prediction for the same cultures: APOE4 microglia should show a higher cholesteryl-ester-to-free-cholesterol ratio and higher triacylglycerol, with a higher ceramide-to-sphingomyelin ratio and lower glucosylceramide consistent with elevated SMPD1, GBA and GBA2 transcripts. An unchanged esterification index would weaken step 5.", "Specificity test: TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module but should not by itself normalize the sterol-synthesis transcripts if the bottleneck is transport rather than degradative capacity; normalization of both by TFEB knockdown alone would favour a degradative-capacity model instead.", "Negative prediction against the ER-proteostasis alternative: APOE4 cells should not show increased BiP/GRP94 protein, increased XBP1 splicing, or increased eIF2-alpha phosphorylation under mock conditions, and PERK or IRE1 inhibition should not normalize the lipid-handling transcripts. Clear constitutive UPR activation with lipid transcripts corrected by UPR inhibition would refute this hypothesis in favour of an ER-stress-driven mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry a coordinately elevated lipoprotein/lipid-uptake receptor transcript set (SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of this differential-expression list, plus CD36, LDLR, TREM2, LRP3, APOE, ABCA7; 9/9 positive), which we interpret as increased uptake capacity, an inferred flux not measured here.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred activity): the endolysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript module is elevated well above the strong global positive shift of this selected list (18/18 positive, set mean +3.59 versus list mean +1.39, within-list permutation p = 0.0002; GBA, GAA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, LAMP1, SCARB2, with TFEB also elevated), consistent with an expanded, TFEB-biased degradative compartment.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): export of unesterified sterol from that compartment does not scale with influx. NPC2 is only +1.17 (35th percentile of this list, i.e. below its median) and NPC1, MCOLN1 and LIPA were not measured, so lysosomal cholesterol egress becomes rate-limiting relative to delivery and hydrolysis.", "Step 4 (inferred sensor state): retention of sterol in the lysosome keeps the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool low, so SCAP-SREBP2 proteolytic activation is not shut off; the sterol-synthesis and SREBP target transcript set is uniformly positive (11/11: HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, SCD, FADS1, SREBF1, SREBF2). SREBP cleavage and nuclear occupancy were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): the lipid that does reach the ER is diverted into esterification and glycerolipid storage rather than into the regulatory pool (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, SCD, CIDEB, ABHD5, MGLL; 11/11 positive, set mean +2.74, permutation p = 0.040), predicting expanded cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol pools.", "Step 6 (consequence): uptake, synthesis and storage therefore run without sterol feedback shutoff, and the membrane-repair/efferocytosis-associated protein ANXA1 rises at both levels (transcript +4.15, 89th percentile; ANXA1-containing protein spots 043-047 up, 8/9 ANXA1 spots reported significant), which we read as an inferred membrane-stress and phagocytic-load response secondary to the lipid-handling imbalance."], "title": "A lysosomal sterol-egress bottleneck keeps the ER-accessible cholesterol pool low in APOE4 microglia, locking in a futile uptake-synthesis-esterification cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37855850533545027, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28162810729900245, "cosine_similarity": 0.3006517353210548, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_085", "mean_absolute_error": 0.656883495145631, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37855850533545027, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28162810729900245, "cosine_similarity": 0.3006517353210548, "direction_accuracy": 0.24271844660194175, "mean_absolute_error": 0.656883495145631, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.59056, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 302}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_020", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77% positive); absent genes (e.g. CAT, G6PD, HMGCR, SQLE, PEX family, ABCA1, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged, and all program sign counts are judged against the 77% positive background, not 50/50.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects (range -7.94 to +15.46) are therefore not directly comparable in magnitude to the protein spots, which are log2 fold changes.", "The 77% positive bias may partly reflect composition, ambient RNA or normalization in the pseudobulk/10X Flex comparison; the mechanism relies on relative sign/effect contrasts (e.g. nuclear ETC up while MT-encoded down; HK2/PFKP down while transporters up), not on absolute up-regulation of any single program.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity, not activity: no degradative flux, fatty-acid or pyruvate oxidation rate, membrane potential, NADPH/GSH pool, lipid-droplet content or ROS measurement is supplied, so all routing and flux statements are inferred.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (69/92 spots list 5 candidates; 2-6 candidates each, with frequent KRT/ACTB contaminants); no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein, and bidirectional cathepsin/v-ATPase-candidate spots are treated as unresolved proteoform-level information.", "Genes are not independent (shared regulons, co-detection), so the descriptive sign statistics are coherence summaries, not formal enrichment tests.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some measured transcript differences may reflect altered astrocyte-microglia signalling rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change rather than by a single bottleneck: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors, TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, sterol handling/esterification, and nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC machinery are coherently higher, while glycolytic-entry (HK2, PFKP), cytosolic pentose-phosphate/NAD-salvage (TALDO1, PGD, NAMPT, NADK) and mitochondrially encoded subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are lower. We propose that increased routing of internalized lipid/membrane substrate through an expanded lysosomal compartment into mitochondrial oxidation is the primary axis; the modest rise in thiol/peroxide-detoxifying transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, TXNDC17, MSRA, GSS) is load-matched to this mitochondrial site rather than evidence of ongoing oxidative damage, and peroxisomal expansion is not supported (no PEX/plasmalogen/CAT transcript rows represented; ABCD1 and ACSL4 decreased). Only transcript and ambiguous 2D-gel spot abundances were measured; degradative flux, fatty-acid oxidation rate, NADPH/GSH turnover, ROS levels and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, pulse-chase of fluorescent myelin/oxLDL or DQ-BSA plus 13C-oleate tracing should show HIGHER cargo degradation rate and higher 13C label entry into TCA intermediates in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows slower cargo clearance with accumulating undigested lipid and no increase in TCA labelling, the 'increased routing/throughput' mechanism is wrong and a lysosomal-blockade/failed-compensation model should replace it.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: mitochondrial pyruvate-carrier inhibition (UK5099) or low-dose ETC inhibition should reduce phagolysosomal cargo degradation and viability disproportionately in APOE4 vs APOE3, whereas glycolysis inhibition (2-DG) should be relatively better tolerated by APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or opposite sensitivity would weaken the mitochondrial-routing step (Step 3).", "Prospective reserve test (challenge-only claim): PPP/NAD-salvage restriction (6-aminonicotinamide or FK866) or an acute peroxide/myelin challenge should induce more lipid peroxidation (C11-BODIPY) and more GSH depletion in APOE4 than APOE3, while unchallenged mock cultures show comparable basal ROS/GSH. Elevated basal ROS in mock, or equal sensitivity under challenge, would falsify the 'load-matched now, reduced reserve later' formulation of Step 5/6.", "Prospective sterol-routing test: delivering sterol directly to the ER-accessible pool (25-hydroxycholesterol or cholesterol-cyclodextrin) should normalize the APOE4 elevation of SREBP2 targets (LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24). Persistent elevation would indicate blocked ER sterol delivery rather than the proposed routing to ester/lysosomal pools, favouring a lysosomal cholesterol-trapping alternative.", "Prospective specificity test for the rejected focus: peroxisome-selective readouts (catalase activity, plasmalogen levels, C26:0 lysophosphatidylcholine, PMP70 puncta) should NOT differ appreciably between APOE4 and APOE3 at mock. A clear peroxisomal \u03b2-oxidation defect or catalase induction would reinstate the peroxisomal focus and weaken Step 5.", "Prospective identity resolution: targeted immunoblot/MS of the ambiguous spots should show that the strongly increased spot train (protein_spot:043-046) is ANXA1 rather than TALDO1, and that mature cathepsin B/D forms are increased in APOE4. If TALDO1 protein is instead increased while its transcript is decreased, the reduced cytosolic PPP-reserve component of Step 5 is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of scavenger/opsonic uptake receptors and secreted opsonins - gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, gene:FCGRT, gene:FCGR1A/FCGR1B/FCGR3A, gene:APOE (19/19 represented members positive vs a 77% positive selected-list background) - which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein and membrane/debris substrate to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (inferred routing): Substrate delivery is matched by a TFEB/MITF-associated expansion of the degradative compartment - gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:MITF, v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1E1, ATP6V0D1), and glycosidase/lipase/protease transcripts (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86) - so lysosomal catabolic capacity rises with, rather than behind, uptake capacity (exception: gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:M6PR, gene:IDS decreased).", "Step 3 (inferred flux): Catabolic products are routed to mitochondrial oxidation rather than to glycolysis: pyruvate/amino-acid entry and TCA transcripts rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:BCAT2 +6.42, gene:ACO2, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:SLC25A1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:MGLL) together with nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (52/56 represented OXPHOS/TCA members positive; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME), while glycolytic entry transcripts fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Step 4 (inferred sterol routing): Sterol is directed into lysosomal/ester and oxysterol pools rather than the ER-sensed pool: gene:SCP2 (+5.95), gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:NPC2, gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H, gene:ABCA7, gene:MYLIP rise while SREBP-axis transcripts remain co-induced (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1; 22/22 represented lipid/sterol members positive), i.e. continued sterol demand at the ER despite high uptake.", "Step 5 (load-matched redox, focus partially rejected): Peroxide/thiol-repair transcripts scale with the mitochondrial site of oxidative load (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:MSRA, gene:GSS, gene:SELENOW, gene:SELENOP, gene:FTH1, gene:CCS, gene:SLC31A2), with NADPH sourcing shifted toward mitochondrial/transhydrogenase routes (gene:NNT +2.88, gene:ME1) as cytosolic pentose-phosphate and NAD-salvage transcripts fall (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:NAMPT -2.62, gene:NADK -1.14); peroxisomal \u03b2-oxidation is not part of this axis (gene:ABCD1 -1.64, gene:ACSL4 -2.14; only gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:CROT, gene:AMACR weakly positive; catalase appears only inside the 3-candidate protein_spot:017).", "Step 6 (state consequence, partly prospective): The resulting state supports higher degradative-oxidative throughput in the measured mock condition, but its reserve is narrowed on two axes that are measured only as transcripts - reduced cytosolic NADPH/NAD-regenerating capacity (Step 5) and a nuclear/mitochondrial subunit imbalance (nuclear ETC up while gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) - a vulnerability we expect to become functionally visible only under phagocytic or oxidative challenge, not as an established ongoing defect at mock."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-substrate-driven phagolysosomal-to-mitochondrial catabolic state with glycolytic-entry downshift, not a peroxisomal or generic oxidative-stress state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2401598788908171, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23981017506075045, "cosine_similarity": 0.30061549514660285, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6266601941747573, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2401598788908171, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23981017506075045, "cosine_similarity": 0.30061549514660285, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6266601941747573, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.38486625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 78}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_072", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every |effect| exceeds 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive), so all enrichment statements are made against the within-dataset background of these same 2212 rows, not against an unbiased transcriptome. A module can therefore be 'up' in raw sign yet not distinguishable from background.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effects (log2) are never numerically compared, only compared in sign and rank.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features. No spot is treated as a unique protein identification; spot-level statements are used only as weak, explicitly ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and lagging proxy for the abundance of the corresponding functional protein pool; no lysosomal enzyme activity, luminal pH, lipid species, flux or localization measurement is present in these data.", "The hydrolase-versus-v-ATPase discrepancy is assumed to reflect a real capacity mismatch rather than differing transcript detection sensitivity or differing mRNA stability between the two gene families.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at day 30 under mock treatment with replicate number not supplied in the workbook, so between-line clonal and co-culture (astrocyte) effects cannot be excluded as contributors."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a demand/capacity mismatch inside the endolysosomal system: transcripts for cargo delivery and for CLEAR-network acid hydrolases are shifted far above the dataset-wide background shift, while the v-ATPase acidification module is not, so the rate-limiting step is inferred to be acid-dependent luminal hydrolysis of lipid/glycolipid cargo per unit delivered enzyme. The carbon that is liberated is inferred to be routed into an elevated mitochondrial carrier/TCA module and into SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1-supported re-esterification rather than into export, because the measured sterol-synthesis, sterol-sensing and lipid-efflux transcripts sit at or below the dataset median. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION. Restoring lysosomal acidification in APOE4 microglia (v-ATPase-assembly-competent conditions or acidic nanoparticle-mediated pH lowering, without changing sterol synthesis) should lower the steady-state CLEAR hydrolase transcripts gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA and gene:CTSB toward APOE3 levels and reduce lysosomal lipid substrate. If APOE4 lysosomal pH is already equal to APOE3 and forced acidification leaves the hydrolase transcripts elevated, the acidification-limited step (STEP 3) is falsified and the mechanism collapses to a generic biogenesis phenotype.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION AGAINST THE SIDELINED STEROL MODEL. Blocking the SREBP axis (SCAP/S1P inhibition or statin) should NOT normalize the CLEAR hydrolase module or the mitochondrial carrier/TCA module if the lysosomal bottleneck is upstream; it should only blunt gene:SCD and gene:DGAT1. If SREBP blockade does normalize the hydrolase and mitochondrial modules, the sterol-synthesis-driven alternative is favoured over this hypothesis.", "DIRECT CAPACITY TEST. Per-cell acid-hydrolase specific activity (GBA, HEXA, cathepsin B) in APOE4 microglia should be sub-proportional to their elevated transcript levels, and GBA/SMPD1 substrates (glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin) should accumulate. Finding activity and substrate clearance that scale proportionally with transcript would weaken STEP 2-3.", "CARGO-INFLUX TEST. Blocking SCARB1-mediated lipid uptake (SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1) should reduce delivered lysosomal lipid and lower CLEAR hydrolase induction in APOE4 more than in APOE3. No genotype-selective reduction would weaken STEP 1, which rests largely on the single strong observation gene:SCARB1.", "DISPOSAL-FATE TEST. APOE4 microglia should show higher neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content and lower cholesterol efflux to acceptors than APOE3 at baseline. Equal or greater efflux, or absent droplet accumulation, would falsify STEP 5.", "MITOCHONDRIAL COUPLING TEST. Inhibiting mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate carriers (MPC or SLC25A1) should selectively impair APOE4 microglia and further amplify their lysosomal substrate load. If APOE4 cells are no more sensitive than APOE3, STEP 4 is weakened and the mitochondrial module should be reinterpreted as an independent, parallel phenotype rather than a downstream consequence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux). APOE4 microglia carry a higher transcript pool for late-endosome/lysosome cargo delivery (gene:AP5M1, gene:ARFGEF1, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:RAB7A; set mean +4.88, permutation p=5e-4 against the within-dataset background) together with the near-top-ranked scavenger receptor transcript gene:SCARB1 (+8.22, 99.1st percentile). We infer, but did not measure, an increased rate of lipid-bearing cargo arriving at the late endosome/lysosome.", "STEP 2 (measured transcripts; inferred regulatory activity). The TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR regulon is the most coherently elevated degradative module (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:DNASE2; mean +4.29, p\u003c1e-4), with gene:TFEB (+2.38) and gene:MITF (+1.03) elevated. We interpret this as a sustained compensatory biogenesis signal (i.e., an unmet degradative demand), not as evidence of achieved degradation; TFEB nuclear localization and activity were not measured.", "STEP 3 (primary bottleneck; partly inferred). The proton-pumping/acidification module rises much less than the hydrolase module (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:CLCN7; mean +2.42, not separable from background p=0.087; hydrolase-minus-v-ATPase contrast p=0.027). Two significantly decreased 2D spots list ATP6V1E1 among their candidate genes (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065); these spots are multi-candidate and are NOT a unique identification of a V1 subunit. We propose that luminal pH / hydrolase specific activity, not enzyme supply, limits degradative throughput. Lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and lipid substrate pools were not measured here.", "STEP 4 (measured transcripts; inferred flux). Carbon liberated by the fraction of cargo that is degraded is inferred to be routed to mitochondria: the mitochondrial carrier/TCA module is the single most shifted metabolic module (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A37, gene:SLC25A46, gene:SLC25A51, gene:ACO2; mean +6.02, p\u003c1e-4). Respiration, TCA flux and citrate export are inferred, not observed.", "STEP 5 (measured transcripts; inferred flux/fate). Cytosolic carbon is inferred to be re-esterified and stored rather than exported: gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SCD (+4.17) and gene:DGAT1 (+1.72) are elevated, whereas the efflux/handoff transcripts that were measured sit at or below the dataset median (gene:APOE +1.24, 38th percentile; gene:SOAT1 +1.25, 39th percentile; gene:ABCA7 +2.14; gene:PLTP +1.06; set mean +1.42, p=0.49). Lipid droplet content and cholesterol efflux were not measured.", "STEP 6 (system-level consequence; inferred). The combination of continued cargo delivery, throughput-limited hydrolysis, and storage-biased rather than export-biased disposal produces a self-sustaining loop in which the CLEAR program stays chronically engaged in APOE4 microglia at baseline, which is the proposed differentiating state rather than an acute stimulus response."], "title": "A lysosomal degradative-throughput bottleneck, not sterol synthesis or efflux, distinguishes APOE4 microglia: acidification capacity lags a TFEB/CLEAR hydrolase surge, forcing mitochondrial anaplerosis and lipogenic re-esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12391537126610788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06548893006115421, "cosine_similarity": 0.3004730816946588, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6607961165048544, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12391537126610788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06548893006115421, "cosine_similarity": 0.3004730816946588, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6607961165048544, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0965305, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 303}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_048", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so all module statistics are conditional on that selection; the unspecified logarithm base is preserved and only monotone comparisons within the list are used.", "The global positive skew (median +1.46, 77% of rows positive) reflects a real or normalization-related baseline shift; module claims are made only relative to that shift, never against zero.", "Transcript differences for SREBP targets, esterification enzymes and lysosomal hydrolases translate at least partially into enzyme abundance and flux, which was not measured here.", "Protein spots are ambiguous mixtures; the ANXA1/TALDO1 spot train is assigned to ANXA1 only because gene:ANXA1 is up (+4.15) while gene:TALDO1 is down (-2.32); this assignment could be wrong.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid supply and some protein spots may be non-cell-autonomous or of astrocytic origin.", "No lipid, flux, enzyme-activity, organelle-fractionation or replicate-level data were supplied; lysosomal lipid content, ER sterol pool and acetyl-CoA are unmeasured inferred pools."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference is best explained by a lipid-supply bottleneck at the ER: transcripts for SREBP-driven sterol/fatty-acid synthesis, acyl-esterification and the citrate-to-cytosolic-acetyl-CoA supply route are coordinately higher in APOE4 (median RNA effect 2.93 vs 1.46 global, 19/19 up, permutation p=0.0055), together with a lysosomal hydrolase/endosomal-routing module, whereas de novo sphingolipid synthesis genes are not elevated above the global shift (median 1.27 vs 1.46, permutation p=0.69) and the glycosphingolipid-extending B4GALT5 is reduced. We therefore reject a sphingolipid-synthesis mechanism and propose that APOE4 cells behave as if ER-accessible sterol and monounsaturated acyl-CoA are limiting, disposing of internalised and newly made lipid into esterified storage pools and lysosomal hydrolysis rather than into expanded sphingolipid synthesis. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, localization and activity statements are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with cholesterol:methyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which reaches the ER-accessible pool directly) should normalize the APOE4 excess of SREBF1/SCD/LDLR/HMGCS1 transcripts, whereas the same cholesterol dose given as LDL (endolysosomal route) should not; if LDL and cyclodextrin cholesterol suppress the program equally in APOE4, the ER-delivery bottleneck is wrong.", "SCD inhibition or SCAP/SREBP blockade should selectively lower APOE4 triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass and the 16:1/18:1 fraction of glycerolipids toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the APOE4 neutral-lipid excess would weaken the mechanism and favour a lipolysis or uptake defect.", "Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 should show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol with monounsaturated acyl chains and only proportional, not selective, increases in sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide; a selective ceramide or hexosylceramide increase without neutral-lipid change would falsify the primary claim.", "Sphingolipid discriminator: myriocin (serine palmitoyltransferase inhibition) should reduce sphingolipid pools equally in both genotypes, while conduritol-B-epoxide (GBA inhibition) should produce a larger glucosylceramide increment in APOE4 if lysosomal glycosphingolipid flux is genuinely higher; equal CBE increments would show the hydrolase transcript rise is not matched by flux, and a genotype-selective myriocin effect would reinstate the rejected de novo synthesis mechanism.", "Blocking cargo delivery (phagocytosis/scavenger-receptor blockade, or removing astrocytes) should collapse the APOE4 excess of lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB) if that module is substrate-driven; unchanged hydrolase transcripts would indicate a cell-autonomous MiT/TFE difference upstream of lipid load."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred delivery): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for membrane- and lipoprotein-uptake and late-endosome routing components (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:ANXA1, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3), and the largest protein-spot changes in the dataset form a five-spot charge train whose only candidate with concordant RNA is ANXA1 (protein_spot:043-047); we infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of phosphatidylserine-exposing and lipoprotein-derived membrane lipid to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): a lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module is up (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:DPP7, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB; module median 2.17 vs 1.46 global, p=0.047), consistent with a MiT/TFE-type response to catabolic load; enzyme activity and lysosomal lipid content were not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck, inferred): the rate-limiting step is delivery of endolysosome-derived sterol and fatty acyl units to the ER sensing pool, so ER sensors report deficiency even though total cellular lipid load is not low.", "Step 4 (measured RNA): the ER responds with a coherent SREBP-type anabolic program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1) supported by carbon and reducing-equivalent supply for cytosolic acetyl-CoA (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): the newly made and salvaged acyl chains are routed into glycerolipid and sterol-ester synthesis and intracellular lipid transfer (gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:SCP2), which we infer produces a larger monounsaturated triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester pool in APOE4 rather than expanded membrane lipid.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, focus rejection): sphingolipid metabolism is skewed to catabolism and headgroup turnover, not synthesis: catabolic and transfer genes rise only in proportion to the general lysosomal module (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLTP, gene:ST3GAL5), while ER/Golgi synthetic steps are flat (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6) and gene:B4GALT5 falls, so ceramide/hexosylceramide handling is predicted to be flux-through rather than accumulation-by-synthesis."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a demand-side SREBP/citrate-acetyl-CoA lipogenic and esterification program while sphingolipid handling stays catabolic, not synthetic"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16877746187645387, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20018609637671608, "cosine_similarity": 0.30044805043531775, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6095145631067961, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16877746187645387, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20018609637671608, "cosine_similarity": 0.30044805043531775, "direction_accuracy": 0.1941747572815534, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6095145631067961, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.23834625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 304}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_091", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive, median +1.46, unspecified logarithm base); genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged, and program directions were judged against this positively skewed background rather than a 50/50 expectation.", "Curated program membership was fixed before effects were inspected and every represented member is reported, including discordant ones; coherence across members is descriptive and the genes are not independent, so no formal enrichment is claimed.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal, mitochondrial and lipid-handling protein machinery in these cells; no respiration, lipolysis, cholesterol-flux, lysosomal-pH or proteolysis measurement is supplied, so all flux, routing, localization and causal statements are inferred.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; each spot's full candidate list is retained and no spot is treated as evidence for a single named protein. The strongly increased ANXA1/TALDO1-containing spot cluster (protein_spot:043-047) is left unresolved, noting that gene:ANXA1 is +4.15 while gene:TALDO1 is -2.32.", "Reduced motility/effector transcripts are assumed to indicate reduced reserve that would be revealed by a future phagocytic or inflammatory challenge; no functional deficit is asserted for the measured mock condition.", "A global normalization or compositional shift could inflate the positive pole; this is partly controlled by spliceosome and proteasome members sitting near the background (MWU p ~ 0.5-0.8) while the mitochondrial set is far above it (MWU p ~ 3e-9), but it is not excluded."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated, transcript-level cell-state shift: raised lipid/lipoprotein-uptake, sterol-synthesis and lipid-esterification genes together with an expanded but compositionally remodeled lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program (TFEB, MITF up) and a near-uniform increase in mitochondrial substrate-carrier, TCA and electron-transport-chain transcripts, while the committed upper-glycolysis step and the actin/motility-effector-homeostatic module are reduced. We propose this is a coordinated re-routing of carbon toward lysosomal-mitochondrial oxidative catabolism (increased catabolic capacity/throughput), not a compensatory response to a mitochondrial or lysosomal bottleneck; the associated loss of motility/effector transcripts predicts reduced functional reserve that is expected to become apparent only under a phagocytic or inflammatory challenge, and is not claimed as an ongoing defect in the mock condition. All effects are measured abundances (RNA log fold change of unspecified base; protein-spot log2 fold change); flux, localization and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective: extracellular-flux measurement of APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 mock microglia should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption with a larger fractional drop after mitochondrial pyruvate-carrier inhibition (UK5099) or CPT1 inhibition (etomoxir), and a lower glycolytic (ECAR) contribution. Equal or lower APOE4 oxygen consumption, or unchanged sensitivity to UK5099/etomoxir despite the raised gene:MPC2/TCA/ETC transcripts, would weaken the increased-throughput claim and favor compensatory upregulation for a mitochondrial defect.", "Prospective: blocking lipid entry (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) or lysosomal acid lipase (lalistat) in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid/cholesteryl-ester content and blunt the mitochondrial ETC/TCA and lysosomal-hydrolase transcript increases. If these transcript programs remain elevated when lipid entry or lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked, the lipid-driven routing step is falsified and a lipid-independent driver of the mitochondrial program is implicated.", "Prospective: APOE4 microglia should show higher esterified/lysosomal-retained sterol with SREBP targets still induced; SOAT1 inhibition should lower cholesteryl esters and reduce gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS and gene:LDLR transcripts toward APOE3 levels. Unchanged SREBP targets after SOAT1 inhibition would falsify the sterol-sequestration step while leaving steps 1, 4 and 5 intact.", "Prospective: under a phagocytic or LPS challenge (not the supplied mock condition), APOE4 microglia should show lower bead/myelin uptake rate and reduced motility consistent with the depressed actin/effector transcripts, while retaining or exceeding APOE3 oxygen consumption. Normal or higher APOE4 phagocytosis and motility would falsify the predicted reserve cost of the state shift.", "Prospective: quantitative immunoblot resolution of the ambiguous spots should show increased mature CTSB/CTSD and increased ETC subunits (e.g., NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) protein in APOE4. If cathepsin and ETC proteins are unchanged or reduced despite the transcript increases, the transcript-to-machinery assumption fails and the mechanism should be restated at the transcriptional-state level only."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lysosomal delivery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:CD33), increasing the inferred flux of lipid cargo into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Increased endolysosomal lipid cargo is accompanied by an expanded lysosomal degradative program (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF; gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, and the lysosomal amino-acid exporter gene:SLC38A7 +7.46), with a changed composition rather than uniform scaling (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:IDS -1.56).", "ER-accessible sterol is inferred to remain below the sensing set point because sterol is esterified/stored and lysosomally retained, so the SREBP arm and storage enzymes stay on (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR; gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1).", "Catabolic products are routed into mitochondria rather than into committed glycolysis: mitochondrial carriers and import machinery rise (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:PRELID3B, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:PDP1, gene:GLUD1) while the committed upper-glycolytic steps fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) despite raised transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Mitochondrial oxidative machinery is coordinately increased across the TCA cycle and all ETC complexes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B; 54/55 curated mitochondrial members positive, median +2.88 versus +1.46 for the selected background), consistent with higher oxidative capacity/throughput.", "Higher oxidative load is met by increased antioxidant transcripts (gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:FTH1, gene:NNT), and antioxidant-containing protein spots are compatible in direction (protein_spot:077 candidates KRT1/PRDX2/KRT9/KRT10/RAB1A/ACTB +1.07; protein_spot:017 candidates CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5 +0.77); spot identities remain ambiguous and are used only as compatibility, not confirmation.", "Investment in this catabolic/oxidative state accompanies loss of the actin-motility and myeloid effector/homeostatic module (gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B -5.83, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:DOCK8, gene:RAC2, gene:SPN -7.26, gene:SEMA4A, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:TGFBR1, gene:CTSS; 12/21 negative, median -1.99, against a 77%-positive selected background), which we interpret as reduced motile/phagocytic reserve expected to be revealed by a future challenge rather than an established deficit in mock."], "title": "APOE4 iPSC-microglia occupy a lysosome-and-mitochondria-based lipid-catabolic cell state, with substrate routed away from committed glycolysis and away from the actin/motility effector module"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38405088062622306, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2917256167607698, "cosine_similarity": 0.29887753465875666, "direction_accuracy": 0.3074433656957929, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_091", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6552621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38405088062622306, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2917256167607698, "cosine_similarity": 0.29887753465875666, "direction_accuracy": 0.3074433656957929, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6552621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4545835, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 79}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 77.1% are positive); program directionality was therefore judged against that 77.1%-up background, and absent genes (e.g. PSAP, GRN, MCOLN1, PPARGC1A, TFAM, ribosomal genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and was preserved as reported; protein spots are log2. RNA and protein effects are therefore not placed on a common scale.", "Transcript increases are read as capacity/state changes; the inferred increases in lipid uptake, lysosomal hydrolytic flux and respiratory flux are NOT measured here and are assumed, not observed.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5) and keratins appear in 33 spots; no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein. Spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Set membership was defined a priori from standard pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge, no literature access) before looking at directions; no member was dropped to make signs agree.", "Genes within a program are not independent, so the concordance statistics quoted are descriptive, not formal enrichment tests; replicate structure is 'not supplied in the workbook'.", "The astrocyte co-culture means some cargo (astrocyte-derived lipoproteins, debris) is present in both genotypes; the genotype effect is assumed to act on handling of that shared cargo."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated, cargo-handling cell state rather than by a single failed step: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-scavenging surface receptors, endosome-to-lysosome trafficking, V-ATPase and acid hydrolases, and the entire nuclear-encoded TCA/electron-transport module are concordantly higher in APOE4, consistent with increased routing of lipid and membrane cargo into lysosomal hydrolysis and mitochondrial oxidation (a throughput/state change, inferred flux, not measured), while the actomyosin engulfment/motility module is reconfigured (ARHGDIA and Arp2/3 up; ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, FAM49B, RAC2, DOCK8 down) rather than uniformly suppressed, predicting a bias toward receptor-mediated small-cargo internalization with reduced actomyosin-dependent large-particle phagocytic reserve that would be revealed mainly under challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE (primary discriminator): in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, pulse-chase of fluorescent lipoprotein/lipid cargo (e.g. DiI-lipoprotein plus BODIPY-cholesteryl ester or DQ-BSA) should show BOTH faster internalization and faster lysosomal dequenching/hydrolysis in APOE4, and higher basal plus etomoxir/oligomycin-resolved oxygen consumption. If APOE4 instead shows equal-or-slower cargo degradation and unchanged or lower respiration despite the elevated hydrolase/OXPHOS transcripts, the increased-throughput reading fails and a failed-compensation/bottleneck model is favoured.", "PROSPECTIVE: blocking the lipid-acquisition step (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) in APOE4 microglia should reduce the elevated hydrolase (GAA, GBA, CTSB), V-ATPase (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A) and TCA/ETC (MDH1, OGDH, NDUFA5) transcripts toward APOE3 levels; persistence of these elevations after cargo restriction would refute the cargo-driven ordering of steps 1-5.", "PROSPECTIVE: partial V-ATPase or cathepsin inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1 or E64d/pepstatin) should cause disproportionate lipid-droplet/undigested-cargo accumulation in APOE4 relative to APOE3, because APOE4 is predicted to run at higher degradative load; equal sensitivity would weaken step 3.", "PROSPECTIVE (focus test): APOE4 microglia should be at-or-above APOE3 for receptor-mediated internalization of small cargo (pHrodo-labelled lipoprotein, transferrin) but below APOE3 for actomyosin-dependent tasks (large bead / synaptosome / apoptotic-cell engulfment, blebbistatin-sensitive spreading, directed migration), with reduced F-actin-rich phagocytic cup formation. If APOE4 large-particle engulfment and migration are equal or increased, step 6 is refuted and the cytoskeletal arm should be dropped from the mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE: BN-PAGE/complex-assembly and mtDNA copy-number measurement should show that the 38/38 nuclear ETC transcript increase in APOE4 is NOT matched by a proportional increase in assembled complex IV/V, because mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB) are lower; a proportional rise in assembled complexes would refute step 7 and argue for uncapped mitochondrial biogenesis instead.", "PROSPECTIVE (protein-level resolution of ambiguity): targeted immunoblot/PRM for ANXA1, TALDO1, CTSD, CTSB and ATP6V1E1 should show ANXA1 increased in APOE4 (explaining spots 043-047) while TALDO1 protein is not increased (its transcript is -2.32); if TALDO1 rather than ANXA1 is increased, the spot-based compatibility argument for the lipid/phagocytic reading is weakened.", "Causality is not established by these data; all statements above are proposed tests, and a null result in the first prediction would remove the central 'increased throughput' claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 raises the surface lipid/lipoprotein-acquisition module of microglia - gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:ITGB1 (+6.31), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:COLEC12 (+1.53), gene:ITGB5 (+1.35), gene:MERTK (+1.30), gene:TREM2 (+1.28), gene:APOE (+1.24), gene:C1QA/B/C (+1.13 to +1.25) - increasing the rate at which lipoprotein/lipid and membrane cargo is bound and internalized. Only receptor abundance is measured; uptake rate is inferred.", "STEP 2: Internalized cargo is routed through an expanded endosome-to-lysosome path: gene:DNM2 (+5.82), gene:CLTB (+2.10), gene:SNX3 (+3.95), gene:VPS26A (+4.86), gene:RAB7A (+2.65), gene:CHMP4B (+3.82), with gene:TFEB (+2.38) as a candidate coordinating input. This favours receptor/clathrin-dynamin-dependent internalization over actomyosin-driven engulfment.", "STEP 3: Lysosomal degradative capacity is raised in parallel: acid hydrolases gene:GAA (+9.96), gene:CTSK (+7.36), gene:GBA (+6.71), gene:NAGLU (+5.91), gene:HEXA (+5.68), gene:SMPD1 (+5.63), gene:CTSB (+5.52), gene:CTSD (+2.86) plus the acidification machinery gene:ATP6V1H (+6.88), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.23), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.51) and 6 further ATP6V/ATP6AP genes (9/9 represented up). Exceptions: gene:CTSS (-5.57), gene:IDS (-1.56).", "STEP 4: Hydrolysis-derived fatty acids and sterols are handled by an up-shifted esterification/storage and sterol arm - gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:DGAT1 (+1.72), gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:MGLL (+4.00), gene:CIDEB (+1.06), gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87) - and delivered to mitochondria via gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47), gene:MPC2 (+7.98), gene:SLC25A11 (+4.50), gene:SLC25A5 (+5.56).", "STEP 5: Mitochondrial catabolic machinery is coordinately higher: TCA/anaplerosis gene:MDH1 (+8.72), gene:OGDH (+8.56), gene:GOT1 (+6.43), gene:BCAT2 (+6.42), gene:DLD (+5.54), gene:ACO2 (+3.54), gene:IDH3G (+3.94), gene:GLUD1 (+3.17), gene:HADHA (+2.86) (13/13 represented up) and every represented nuclear-encoded ETC subunit (38/38 up; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:COX5B +2.33), with antioxidant genes gene:PRDX3 (+3.49), gene:GPX4 (+2.79), gene:PRDX2 (+4.41) consistent with higher oxidative load. Assembled complexes and respiration are not measured.", "STEP 6 (routing consequence, partially supported): the actin module is reconfigured, not deleted - gene:ARHGDIA (+10.61, a Rho-GTPase sequestering GDI), gene:ARPC1B (+2.15), gene:ARPC5 (+1.94), gene:CFL1 (+1.80) up, but gene:MYH9 (-6.38), gene:ACTB (-4.98), gene:FAM49B (-5.83), gene:MYO1F (-3.69), gene:ARHGAP30 (-5.16), gene:DOCK8 (-1.99), gene:RAC2 (-1.97) down - predicting preserved/increased receptor-mediated micro-scale uptake but reduced actomyosin-dependent large-particle phagocytosis and process motility reserve, a defect expected to become apparent mainly under a phagocytic or migratory challenge, not necessarily in the measured mock state.", "STEP 7 (constraint on the state): mtDNA-encoded subunits move oppositely to the nuclear ones - gene:MT-ATP6 (-3.35), gene:MT-CYB (-2.32), gene:MT-ND4 (-1.80), gene:MT-CO2 (-1.33) versus gene:MT-ND4L (+1.95), gene:MT-ND5 (+1.93) - so the nuclear-encoded oxidative expansion may exceed what mtDNA-encoded subunits can stoichiometrically support, capping realized respiratory gain even if capacity transcripts rise."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-cargo-driven state that co-expands endolysosomal hydrolytic and mitochondrial oxidative machinery, with receptor-biased rather than actomyosin-biased uptake"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25875087693386994, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2105200692223658, "cosine_similarity": 0.2988283476132692, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6261521035598705, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25875087693386994, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2105200692223658, "cosine_similarity": 0.2988283476132692, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6261521035598705, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.66157375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 80}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_078", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made relative to the strongly upward-shifted distribution of these selected rows (mean +1.39, 77% positive) and not to a whole-transcriptome background.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA log fold changes is unspecified, so effects are used ordinally (rank/percentile within the supplied rows) rather than as absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to translate into a proportionate change in enzyme protein and, at constant substrate supply, in catalytic capacity; neither enzyme activity nor pH-dependent activation was measured.", "Absence of a gene (e.g. ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2, SPHK1/2, CERT1, PSAP, GM2A) from the supplied rows is treated as 'not reported', not as 'unchanged'; the disposal arm is therefore only partially observed.", "No lipid, ceramide, sphingosine, cholesteryl-ester or lipid-droplet measurement was supplied; every statement about lipid pools, flux, membrane composition and organelle localization is inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and can represent proteoforms (e.g. pro- versus mature cathepsin); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and no spot is used as direct evidence for a sphingolipid enzyme.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, but microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous; replicate number was not supplied, so p-values are taken as reported.", "Direction of causality is assumed but not established: the hydrolase transcript increase could equally be a compensatory response to reduced lysosomal sphingolipid-degrading activity in APOE4 cells."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcriptional amplification of the lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic arm (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, NAGLU) that is far above the dataset-wide upward shift, while the ceramide-consuming and sphingoid-base disposal arm (CERS6, KDSR, CERK, SGPL1) sits at or below the dataset median and B4GALT5 is reduced. We hypothesise that this asymmetry increases hydrolytic flux from sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids into ceramide/sphingosine faster than these backbones can be re-exported, re-acylated into complex sphingolipids, or degraded, so that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia is clearance of ceramide/sphingoid base from the late-endosome/lysosome; the resulting ceramide-biased endolysosomal membrane composition, together with an expanded TFEB/v-ATPase/cathepsin compartment and a sterol/neutral-lipid storage program, is proposed to slow Rab7/retromer-dependent cargo egress and sustain a lipid-laden, mildly inflammatory microglial state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treat APOE4 and APOE3 microglia in parallel with (a) myriocin/serine-palmitoyltransferase inhibition (blocks de novo synthesis) and (b) combined acid sphingomyelinase plus glucocerebrosidase inhibition (blocks the hydrolytic arm). The mechanism predicts that (b) normalises the APOE4 ceramide excess and lysosomal lipid load while (a) has little effect on the genotype difference; if instead myriocin abolishes the APOE4-APOE3 lipid difference and hydrolase inhibition does not, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and a de novo synthesis mechanism should replace it.", "Lipidomic prediction: APOE4 microglia should show higher ceramide (notably C16:0/C18:0 species) and a higher ceramide/sphingomyelin and ceramide/hexosylceramide ratio, reduced LacCer, increased GM3 and increased cholesteryl ester/triacylglycerol relative to APOE3 under mock. Finding unchanged or lower ceramide with higher sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide would weaken the mechanism.", "Activity/direction test: enzymatic assays (4-MU-glucoside for GBA, 4-MU-sulfo/HEX substrate for HEXA/HEXB, ASM assay) in APOE4 cells should show activity increased or at least not decreased in proportion to the transcript increase. If activities are reduced despite elevated transcripts, the transcript signature is compensatory and the causal arrow in Step 3 is reversed.", "Rescue/epistasis: knockdown of SMPD1 or GBA (or GBA substrate-reduction upstream) in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal ceramide, reduce lipid-droplet/CE load and partially restore Rab7/retromer-dependent cargo egress (e.g. faster clearance of a fluorescent lipid or dextran cargo) without changing APOE transcript level; no change in cargo egress despite lowered ceramide would falsify Step 6.", "Compartment specificity: ceramide increase should be enriched in isolated late endosome/lysosome fractions rather than distributed evenly across membranes; a uniform whole-cell ceramide rise with no lysosomal enrichment would weaken the localization claim.", "Counter-prediction on the disposal arm: raising sphingoid-base disposal (SGPL1 overexpression or enhanced sphingosine export) should reduce the APOE4 lipid phenotype. Because gene:SPNS1 is already elevated (+2.58) in APOE4, if further boosting export gives no benefit, the bottleneck lies at ceramide rather than sphingosine egress and Step 4 must be narrowed accordingly."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and neutral-lipid storage are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, 99th percentile of the supplied rows; gene:SCD, gene:SREBF1, gene:DGAT1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2), consistent with increased delivery of membrane and lipoprotein lipid into the APOE4 endolysosomal system; the lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): a TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal biogenesis signature is present (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:TFEC) with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and cathepsins (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), indicating an expanded, acidified degradative compartment; acidification and hydrolase activity were not directly assayed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): within that compartment the sphingolipid hydrolase set is disproportionately elevated (mean +3.95 vs dataset mean +1.39; gene:GBA 98th, gene:NAGLU 96th, gene:HEXA 96th, gene:SMPD1 95th percentile), predicting increased hydrolysis of sphingomyelin to ceramide and of gangliosides/globosides/glucosylceramide to ceramide plus free sphingoid base.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred bottleneck): the arms that would consume or dispose of these products are not co-elevated - gene:SGPL1 (29th percentile), gene:CERS6 (27th), gene:CERK (38th), gene:KDSR (41st) - and gene:B4GALT5 is decreased (-1.88, 13th percentile), removing the GlcCer -\u003e LacCer outlet; acid ceramidase, sphingosine kinases, ceramide synthase 2, UGCG, SGMS1/2 and CERT were not among the supplied rows, so this arm is only partially observed.", "Step 5 (inferred lipid state, not measured): the imbalance is predicted to raise the ceramide/sphingomyelin and ceramide/hexosylceramide ratios and free sphingosine in late endosomes/lysosomes, with GM3 favoured (gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17) and cytosolic glycolipid transfer increased (gene:GLTP +2.38).", "Step 6 (inferred localization/routing): ceramide-enriched, cholesterol/CE-loaded late endosomal membranes are proposed to impair cargo egress; the elevated Rab7/retromer-associated transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3) are read as compensatory rather than as evidence of faster routing, and reduced gene:M6PR would further mis-route newly made hydrolases.", "Step 7 (inferred phenotype): the persistent lipid-laden endolysosomal state is proposed to maintain the low-grade inflammatory/chemokine bias seen at RNA level (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3, gene:GPNMB) without requiring an external stimulus."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matching ceramide/sphingoid disposal, creating a ceramide-biased endolysosomal bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24211682605324372, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24207106556201377, "cosine_similarity": 0.29734096037077684, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6388511326860842, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24211682605324372, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24207106556201377, "cosine_similarity": 0.29734096037077684, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6388511326860842, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.53412025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 305}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_094", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive), so direction is judged against that skewed background and absent canonical genes (GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, CS, PDHA1, IDH1/2, G6PD, ALDOA, PGK1, PC and others are not supplied) are unknown, not unchanged; the RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for the capacity of each step; no enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, metabolite pool, respirometry or isotope flux was measured, so 'routing' is inferred, not observed. In particular PDP1 mRNA is assumed to translate into greater PDH dephosphorylation, and MPC2 mRNA into greater assembled MPC1/MPC2 carrier (MPC1 was not supplied).", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 co-migrating candidate identities each (median 5); no spot uniquely identifies a metabolic enzyme, so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction and every candidate identity is retained.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript decreases are assumed to be biological rather than an artefact of 10X Flex probe coverage, ambient RNA, per-cell mitochondrial-content QC filtering or library-size normalisation; if they are technical, the mitonuclear-mismatch part of the mechanism fails while the nuclear carbon-routing part still stands.", "Genes are not independent (shared regulons, single-cell pseudoreplication, replicate number not supplied), so the direction counts reported are descriptive coherence, not a formal enrichment test.", "The reduced respiratory reserve is an expectation for a future challenge (LPS, phagocytic lipid load, galactose or oligomycin stress); nothing in the mock condition establishes an ongoing ATP or respiration deficit, and causality from APOE4 to any flux has not been established."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture), the dominant transcriptional difference is a coordinated re-routing of carbon rather than a bottleneck: glucose-uptake and lysosomal/glycogen carbohydrate-catabolic transcripts rise (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GYS1 +6.10) while the committed cytosolic glycolytic kinases and the oxidative pentose-phosphate arm fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14), and pyruvate/NADH delivery into mitochondria plus the TCA cycle and citrate export are coordinately raised (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72). The 32/32 positive nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02) are not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; only gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), so the predicted phenotype in this unchallenged condition is a shifted substrate-routing/biosynthetic state, whereas a shortfall of assembled respiratory capacity relative to the raised substrate load is predicted to appear only as reduced reserve under a future energetic challenge. Directions are stated on the supplied reported log-fold-change scale (base unspecified for RNA; log2 for protein spots); no flux, enzyme activity or metabolite pool was measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective 13C-glucose tracing in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher fraction of glucose carbon appearing in TCA intermediates (citrate, malate, glutamate m+2) and in de novo lipid, with a lower lactate/glucose ratio and lower 13C label in ribose-5-phosphate/PPP intermediates. If APOE4 cells instead show equal or higher lactate output and unchanged glucose-derived citrate labelling, the re-routing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should reverse the APOE4-specific increase in glucose-derived TCA/lipogenic labelling and in basal oxygen-consumption-linked ATP production, and should partially normalise neutral-lipid accumulation; if UK5099 changes APOE4 and APOE3 cells identically, MPC2 is not a load-bearing step.", "Prospective respirometry: APOE4 microglia should show basal respiration equal to or above APOE3 but a disproportionately smaller FCCP-stimulated maximal/spare capacity, i.e. an increased basal/maximal ratio; equal spare capacity would refute the mitonuclear-mismatch limb, whereas reduced basal respiration together with elevated lactate would favour the competing 'compensatory retrograde response to an existing OXPHOS defect' explanation instead.", "Prospective quantification of assembled complexes (BN-PAGE / mtDNA-encoded protein immunoblot for MT-CO1, MT-CYB, ATP6) should show mtDNA-encoded subunit protein and assembled complex III/IV/V levels flat or reduced in APOE4 despite increased nuclear-encoded subunit protein; matched increases in both would refute the stoichiometric-mismatch claim.", "Prospective challenge test: under LPS or a myelin/lipid phagocytic load, APOE4 microglia should show greater ISR induction (ATF4/DDIT3 protein, phospho-eIF2alpha) and a larger fall in ATP/oxygen consumption than APOE3, and this differential should be blunted by ISRIB or by restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit expression; an equal challenge response would weaken the reduced-reserve prediction.", "Prospective test of the substrate-supply limb: acute lysosomal alpha-glucosidase (GAA) or acid-lipase blockade should reduce mitochondrial substrate supply and TCA-labelling more in APOE4 than APOE3; no genotype difference would indicate the lysosomal program is a parallel phenotype rather than the fuel source for the oxidative shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype shifts microglial substrate acquisition toward glucose uptake and intracellular/lysosomal carbohydrate and lipid liberation rather than toward cytosolic glycolytic commitment: gene:SLC2A1 (+2.37), gene:SLC2A3 (+3.73), gene:SLC2A8 (+1.28), gene:GAA (+9.96, lysosomal glycogen hydrolysis), gene:GYS1 (+6.10), gene:UGP2 (+1.86), gene:SCARB1 (+8.22), gene:CD36 (+1.38), gene:MGLL (+4.00), alongside a broad lysosomal/v-ATPase program (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:TFEB +2.38).", "Flux through the committed upper-glycolytic steps and the oxidative pentose-phosphate arm is transcriptionally restrained (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14), so hexose entering the cell is less committed to lactate/NADPH-generating cytosolic routes; gene:PFKM (+2.41), gene:GPI (+2.06) and gene:ENO1 (+2.17) indicate the pathway is re-configured, not deleted.", "Pyruvate import and oxidative decarboxylation capacity are raised (gene:MPC2 +7.98; gene:PDP1 +3.00, whose product dephosphorylates and thereby de-represses pyruvate dehydrogenase; gene:DLD +5.54, the shared E3 subunit of PDH/OGDH), and cytosolic reducing equivalents are directed into mitochondria through the malate-aspartate shuttle (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75) instead of to cytosolic NAD+ regeneration.", "The TCA cycle and anaplerotic supply are coordinately increased (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SDHB +1.65, gene:ME1 +1.36; amino-acid anaplerosis gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS +1.35, gene:BCAT1 +1.32, gene:BCAT2 +6.42, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46), and part of the carbon is exported as citrate for lipid synthesis and storage (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:APOE +1.24), consistent with the lipid-accumulating APOE4 microglial phenotype.", "NADPH and redox support are correspondingly re-sourced away from the PPP toward mitochondria-linked routes (gene:NNT +2.88, gene:ME1 +1.36, gene:SHMT2 +2.22, gene:SHMT1 +3.28, gene:PSPH +3.54) with an increased mitochondrial peroxide-handling set (gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:GPX4 +2.79), as expected when more electron flow is routed through the matrix.", "Nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, import and carrier transcripts rise uniformly (32/32 positive: e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:CYCS +2.58; plus gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:CHCHD3 +3.59, gene:TUFM +6.46), but the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts do not follow (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33), predicting sub-stoichiometric assembly of complexes III/IV/V relative to the imported nuclear subunits and to the raised substrate load; a stress/integrated-response set is co-elevated (gene:DELE1 +4.82, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.51, gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:HSPA9 +2.35).", "Net predicted cell state in the measured mock condition: an oxidative/lipogenic, lysosome-fuelled APOE4 microglial state with reduced cytosolic glycolytic and PPP commitment; the mitonuclear subunit mismatch is predicted to manifest as reduced spare respiratory capacity and greater ISR activation only when an additional energetic or phagocytic-lipid challenge is imposed, not necessarily as an ATP deficit at baseline."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-route carbon from cytosolic glycolysis/PPP into mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and citrate-derived lipogenesis, with mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS subunits failing to scale with the nuclear program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2153415172834983, "cosine_similarity": 0.29730103450790124, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6242200647249191, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28810508437026916, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2153415172834983, "cosine_similarity": 0.29730103450790124, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6242200647249191, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2055335, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 81}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_016", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected significant-DE list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705/2212 positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; programs are judged against that 77%-positive, median +1.46 background, and genes absent from the list are unknown rather than unchanged - the absence of ISGs therefore argues that interferon signalling is not among the strongest represented differences, not that it is actively suppressed.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for machinery capacity, not for measured hydrolase activity, lipid flux, autophagic flux, oxygen consumption, membrane trafficking rate, or lysosomal pH; all flux and localization statements are inferred.", "2D protein spots are ambiguous (78/92 spots list \u003e=5 candidate genes; KRT1/KRT10/KRT9 appear in 33/30/14 spots, ACTB in 25) and are used only for compatibility, never to confirm an individual protein; spot-level effects are also predominantly positive (64/92), so single positive spots are weak evidence.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so the lipid cargo driving the state may be astrocyte- or medium-derived and partly non-cell-autonomous; the isogenic APOE4/APOE3 contrast localizes the genotype but not the lipid source.", "Reduced glycolytic/PPP and motility transcripts are treated as reduced reserve; an ongoing functional deficit in the mock condition is not claimed and would require challenge experiments.", "Causality is not established: TFEB, SREBF1 and receptor transcripts are correlated members of the state; the data cannot prove which is the initiating node."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the dominant APOE4-vs-APOE3 difference in these iPSC-microglia is a coordinated cell-state change in lipid handling: more cargo routed into the endolysosomal system, a MiT/TFE-type expansion of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (TFEB gene:TFEB +2.4, MITF +1.0; 29/32 represented lysosomal genes positive, median +2.0 vs list background 77% positive/median +1.46), SREBP1-type desaturation and esterification/storage routing at the ER (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2), and elevated mitochondrial TCA/ETC transcripts (17/17 OXPHOS and 10/10 TCA members positive) without the glycolytic/pentose-phosphate co-induction (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:PGD -1.3, gene:TALDO1 -2.3) or the interferon program (only gene:IFNAR1 +1.4 and gene:TMEM173 +1.2 represented; no ISGs in the supplied rows) expected for inflammatory activation. We interpret this as increased lipid-processing capacity/throughput in the measured mock condition, with reduced glycolytic-PPP and surveillance/motility reserve (gene:CTSS -5.6, gene:CSF1 -5.9, gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:RAC2 -2.0) that would be revealed only by a future lipid or immune challenge; a degradative bottleneck is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: in mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia, measured lysosomal hydrolase activities (4-MU assays for GBA/HEXB/GAA), LysoTracker/LAMP1 area and neutral-lipid (BODIPY) plus cholesteryl-ester/TAG lipidomic content should all be higher in APOE4, and basal oxygen consumption should be higher while glycolytic rate is not. If hydrolase activity and lysosomal content are unchanged or lower in APOE4 despite the elevated transcripts, the 'expanded processing capacity' reading fails and the failed-compensation/bottleneck alternative is favoured.", "Prospective perturbation 1: TFEB knockdown (or dominant-negative MiT/TFE) in APOE4 microglia should selectively collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C) and increase neutral-lipid accumulation in APOE4 more than in APOE3. If the lysosomal module is unaffected by TFEB knockdown, mechanism step 2 is wrong.", "Prospective perturbation 2: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition should, in APOE4 only, shift lipid from esterified stores toward free sterol/fatty acid and further raise SREBP-target and lysosomal transcripts; no genotype-selective response would weaken the ER-esterification routing step.", "Prospective challenge: after myelin-debris or oxLDL loading, APOE4 microglia should show equal or faster initial cargo internalization/degradation but greater persistent neutral-lipid retention and a blunted glycolytic (extracellular acidification) and phagocytic-burst response relative to APOE3. Equal lipid retention and equal glycolytic induction would weaken the 'reduced reserve' claim.", "Prospective interferon test (rejecting the assigned focus): with IFN-beta or poly(I:C) stimulation, ISG induction (MX1, IFIT1/3, ISG15, STAT1) should be comparable between genotypes and unbiased whole-transcriptome profiling of mock cells should show no coherent baseline ISG difference. A clear baseline ISG-high or ISG-suppressed signature in an unbiased measurement would contradict this hypothesis' rejection of an interferon-driven mechanism.", "Negative control prediction: the mechanism predicts no genotype difference in ER chaperone induction (HSPA5/HSP90B1/PDIA3 protein) in mock cells, consistent with spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 being flat-to-negative and non-significant; a strong APOE4 UPR-chaperone induction would indicate a proteostatic mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype increases delivery of lipid/lipoprotein and membrane cargo into the endolysosomal system: lipid- and lipoprotein-uptake receptor transcripts are elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:APOE +1.2) together with endolysosomal trafficking transcripts (gene:AP5M1 +9.8, gene:RAB28 +8.4, gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:SNX3 +3.9, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:RAB7A +2.7, gene:RAB32 +2.8). Uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured.", "Sustained luminal lipid/glycolipid substrate engages MiT/TFE-family transcriptional output (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF +1.0), coordinately raising acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.4, gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:NAGLU +5.9, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6V0C +3.5, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:HEXB +2.2, gene:LAMP1 +1.4, gene:NPC2 +1.2), i.e. expanded degradative machinery for sphingolipid/glycolipid and glycogen-derived cargo.", "Hydrolysis products are routed at the ER into desaturation, phospholipid remodelling and neutral-lipid storage rather than efflux: gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:FADS1 +1.6, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, with sterol-pathway members gene:DHCR24 +3.7, gene:DHCR7 +2.7, gene:LSS +2.3, gene:ACAT2 +2.0, gene:INSIG1 +1.9, gene:SREBF2 +1.1 (esterified lipid pools are inferred, not measured here).", "Fatty-acid-derived acetyl-CoA and reducing equivalents are consumed by an enlarged mitochondrial oxidative module (gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:GOT1 +6.4, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5, gene:ACO2 +3.5, gene:GLUD1 +3.2, gene:PDP1 +3.0, gene:HADHA +2.9, gene:SCP2 +5.9, gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:ATP5ME +5.2, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.7, gene:UQCRC2 +4.0, gene:COX7A2 +3.4), while glycolysis/PPP is not co-elevated (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:TALDO1 -2.3, gene:PGD -1.3), indicating routing toward oxidative lipid catabolism rather than the glycolytic bias of inflammatory activation.", "This lipid-processing state substitutes for, rather than accompanies, an inflammatory/interferon state: the interferon module is essentially unrepresented among the supplied differential rows (only gene:IFNAR1 +1.4, gene:TMEM173 +1.2), the NF-kB module does not exceed the 77%-positive list background (14/18 positive; gene:CXCL8 +3.1, gene:CCL2 +2.1, gene:MYD88 +2.3, gene:NLRP3 +1.1 up but gene:TNFAIP3 -1.0, gene:RELB -1.3, gene:CCL4 -1.5, gene:TRAF4 -7.2, gene:GSDMD -3.2 down), and surveillance/motility and secreted-protease transcripts are strongly reduced (gene:CTSS -5.6, gene:CSF1 -5.9, gene:MYH9 -6.4, gene:MYO1F -3.7, gene:RAC2 -2.0, gene:SPN -7.3).", "Consequence: in the mock condition APOE4 microglia are predicted to carry higher lysosomal and neutral-lipid content with higher oxidative and lower glycolytic/NADPH reserve; the functional cost (blunted phagocytic burst, blunted glycolytic switch, lipid retention) is a reduced reserve that a future lipid or immune challenge would expose, not an ongoing defect demonstrated by these measurements."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a MiT/TFE-associated lysosome-mitochondria lipid-processing state with ER esterification routing, not an interferon/inflammatory state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4052265258649337, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25301195515487046, "cosine_similarity": 0.29590067364554007, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6359126213592233, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4052265258649337, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.25301195515487046, "cosine_similarity": 0.29590067364554007, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6359126213592233, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.32448875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 82}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_165", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (median approximately +1.46, 77% positive, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05); all pathway claims therefore rest on rank/percentile comparisons within this list, not on absolute fold changes or on unbiased transcriptome coverage.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the corresponding protein and enzymatic capacity; no enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, sterol localization or lipid pool was measured in the supplied data.", "2-D protein spots have multiple candidate genes and cannot be assigned to a single protein; spot-level effects are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence, and keratins/actins in many spots are treated as probable contaminants or non-specific abundance.", "The lysosomal/CLEAR module is assumed to be a compensatory response to substrate load rather than a primary transcriptional gain-of-function; this direction is not established by the data.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 at day 30 under mock treatment with replicate number not supplied, so unmodelled clone, differentiation-efficiency, astrocyte co-culture composition or cell-composition effects could contribute to the shift.", "Lipid droplets, cholesteryl esters, ceramide and free cholesterol are inferred endpoints; none is present in the supplied observations and none is reported here as measured."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a higher lipoprotein/membrane-lipid load into the endolysosome (uptake-receptor transcripts led by SCARB1) and mount a coordinated CLEAR-type lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program (TFEB, GBA, SMPD1, GAA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A/1H/AP1), while the components that move catabolites out of the lysosome and deliver new hydrolases rank low within the same dataset (NPC2 low percentile, M6PR decreased, CTSS strongly decreased). The proposed rate-limiting step is therefore egress/handoff of lysosome-derived sterol and fatty acid into ER-accessible pools; sterol and fatty acid that do escape are shunted into desaturation and esterification (SCD, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1, MGLL) into neutral-lipid stores, so the ER sterol/lipid sensing pool remains unsatisfied and the SREBP-type lipogenic and uptake program (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS) stays on, creating a self-sustaining lipid-loading cycle. Only transcript and 2-D protein-spot abundances were measured; lipid pools, lysosomal pH, hydrolytic flux, localization and causal direction are inferred, not established. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus is rejected as primary: UPR transcripts are not enriched above the strong global positive shift of this selected DE list, several ERAD/translocon transcripts are decreased, and every protein spot whose candidate list contains an ER chaperone or PDI (HSPA5, HSP90B1, PDIA3) is non-significant and mostly negative.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: bypassing lysosomal sterol egress in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 protein supplementation) should, within 24-48 h, lower lysosomal filipin-positive free cholesterol, reduce neutral-lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX) area, and lower SREBF1, SCD, LDLR and DHCR24 transcripts toward APOE3 levels, while APOE3 cells change far less; if cyclodextrin clears lysosomal cholesterol but leaves the lipogenic transcripts and droplet burden unchanged, the proposed egress bottleneck and the feed-forward sensing loop are wrong.", "Second discriminating test (direction of the lysosomal program): TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, GAA, CTSB, ATP6V1A/1H) and worsen lipid retention (more droplets, more undigested cargo); if TFEB knockdown instead reduces lipid load, the CLEAR module is a driver rather than a compensation and this mechanism is falsified.", "Influx test: SCARB1 knockdown or blocking should reduce APOE4 lysosomal lipid loading and lower SCD/SREBF1 and hydrolase transcripts; no change would falsify Step 1 as the entry route and point instead to endogenous membrane turnover or de novo synthesis.", "Storage-versus-source test: acute SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition should shrink neutral-lipid stores while increasing free-cholesterol/ceramide toxicity readouts and leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcript excess essentially intact; normalization of the lysosomal transcript module by SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition would place esterification, not lysosomal egress, at the bottleneck.", "ER-proteostasis exclusion test: chemical chaperone (4-PBA/TUDCA), ATF6 inhibition or ISRIB should not correct the APOE4 lipid phenotype, and immunoblot should show no APOE4 increase in BiP/HSPA5 or GRP94/HSP90B1, consistent with the non-significant, mostly negative spots protein_spot:001, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:005 and protein_spot:016; a clear BiP/GRP94 protein increase or full rescue by UPR inhibition would reinstate the ER-proteostasis mechanism and weaken this one.", "Flux confirmation: DQ-BSA and BODIPY-LDL pulse-chase should show normal or increased internalization but delayed conversion of lysosomal lipid label into ER/droplet-accessible pools in APOE4; equal handoff kinetics between genotypes would weaken the central claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_165", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show markedly higher SCARB1 transcript (top ~1% of the supplied list) with smaller increases in ABCA7, LDLR, CD36 and TREM2, which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system; the lipid flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): A TFEB/MiT-associated CLEAR-type program is elevated (TFEB, MITF, TFEC) together with acid hydrolases (GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, MAN2B1, GLA, SGSH) and v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1E1, ATP6V0D1, ATP6AP1) plus LAMP1, SCARB2 and IGF2R; we infer this is a compensatory lysosomal-biogenesis response to lipid load rather than surplus degradative capacity.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): Within the same lysosomal module the sphingolipid/glycolipid hydrolases sit at extreme percentiles (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, plus CERS4/CERS6) while the catabolite-export and hydrolase-delivery components rank low (NPC2 at ~35th percentile, i.e. below the dataset median, M6PR decreased, CTSS strongly decreased). We propose that lumenal generation of free cholesterol, ceramide and fatty acid outpaces their export from the lysosome, making egress the rate-limiting step.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred destination): The fraction of lipid that reaches the cytosol/ER is preferentially desaturated and esterified rather than oxidized or effluxed: SCD, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1 and MGLL are up while ACSL4 and ACSL5 are down, which we infer channels fatty acid and cholesterol into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester stores (droplets were not measured here).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred sensing): Because sterol is sequestered in lysosomes and esterified stores, the ER regulatory sterol pool stays low, so the SREBP-type program remains active (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS), reinforcing Step 1 and closing a feed-forward lipid-acquisition cycle that is genotype-driven and independent of any exogenous stimulus (mock condition).", "Step 6 (consequence and boundary): The net predicted APOE4 state is lysosomes distended with poorly exported sterol/sphingolipid plus expanded neutral-lipid stores, with only a secondary, non-dominant ER-stress component (ATF6, DDIT3, MANF, CRELD2 elevated but within the global shift; SEL1L, EDEM1, DERL1, SEC62, SEC24D, PDIA3 decreased), so ER chaperone capacity is not the limiting node."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-catabolite egress, not ER proteostasis, is the APOE4 bottleneck: hydrolysis-versus-export imbalance drives esterification and a feed-forward lipogenic program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.47203965587268765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2322708423949099, "cosine_similarity": 0.294425426149887, "direction_accuracy": 0.41585760517799353, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_165", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6819320388349515, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.47203965587268765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2322708423949099, "cosine_similarity": 0.294425426149887, "direction_accuracy": 0.41585760517799353, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6819320388349515, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86782825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 306}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect|\u003e1, 77% positive, median +1.46), so only relative module position within this list is interpreted; the absolute upward shift is treated as a selection/normalisation artefact, not as evidence of global induction.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effects are used ordinally/comparatively, never converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for module capacity; no protein, enzymatic activity, luminal pH, lysosome number/volume, or localisation was measured for any lysosomal component here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; cathepsin- and ATP6V1E1-linked spots are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration and never as measured cathepsin or v-ATPase pools.", "Key genes for the mechanism (LIPA, NPC1, GRN, PSAP, LAMP2, MCOLN1, ASAH1, TPP1, CTSL) are absent from the supplied rows; their behaviour is unknown and could contradict the module contrast.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; genotype effects on astrocytic lipid supply are not separately measured and could drive the cargo-influx step.", "Statistical module tests are unweighted rank permutations over the supplied gene list, without replicate-level or cell-composition modelling (biological replicates were not supplied)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia raise endocytic/scavenger cargo-uptake and soluble acid-hydrolase transcripts far above the dataset-wide upward shift, while the acidification and lysosomal-membrane module (v-ATPase subunits, LAMP1, SCARB2, CLCN7, NPC2, CLN3) stays at background; we hypothesise that pH-dependent luminal processing capacity, not hydrolase gene dosage, is the rate-limiting step, so lipid/lipoprotein cargo is degraded and exported more slowly, keeping the ER-sensed sterol pool low and sustaining SREBP-target transcription. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating functional test: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, ratiometric lysosomal pH (LysoSensor/pHrodo) plus per-lysosome degradation rate (DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin B) and filipin/BODIPY-cholesterol in LAMP1+ compartments should show APOE4 lysosomes that are less acidic and/or slower per unit LAMP1 volume, with increased unesterified cholesterol, despite equal-or-higher cathepsin protein. If APOE4 lysosomal pH is equal or lower and per-lysosome DQ-BSA/Magic Red rates are equal or higher, the proposed bottleneck is falsified.", "Occlusion test: a sub-inhibitory bafilomycin A1 (or chloroquine) titration should move APOE3 microglia toward the APOE4 signature (hydrolase and SREBP-target transcripts up, cholesterol retained in LAMP1+ compartments) with a markedly smaller incremental effect in APOE4. Equal or larger dose responses in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue-specificity test: TFEB/TFE3 overexpression or lysosome re-acidification (acidic nanoparticles) should normalise APOE4 cholesterol egress and SREBP-target transcripts, whereas overexpressing a single hydrolase (GBA or GAA) should not. Equal rescue by single-hydrolase overexpression would falsify the capacity-mismatch step.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot/immunofluorescence should show v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1A, ATP6V1E1, ATP6V0D1) not increased in APOE4 while mature/pro cathepsin D and B ratios shift. Proportional increases of v-ATPase protein together with mature cathepsins would weaken step 3.", "Competing-mechanism test: Seahorse and mitonuclear protein stoichiometry should be measured in the same cells; if APOE4 microglia show a primary mitochondrial complex-assembly deficit with normal lysosomal pH and normal cargo-degradation kinetics, the mitochondrial program (TCA/OXPHOS transcripts up, mtDNA-encoded transcripts down) rather than lysosomal capacity should be adopted as the primary mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured (RNA): APOE4 microglia have higher transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake and endolysosomal delivery machinery (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36) versus a dataset median of +1.46. Inferred, not measured: increased flux of lipoprotein/membrane cargo into late endosomes/lysosomes.", "Measured (RNA): a coherent block of soluble acid hydrolase transcripts is elevated above the global shift (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.70, gene:NAGLU +5.90, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.60, gene:CTSB +5.50, gene:DPP7 +4.50, gene:CTSD +2.90, gene:HEXB +2.20; 18-gene module mean rank 0.685, permutation p=0.003), with gene:TFEB and gene:MITF also up. Inferred: a CLEAR/TFEB-like compensatory transcriptional response to cargo load.", "Measured (RNA): the acidification and lysosomal-membrane/transport module is not co-induced (gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.7, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.3, gene:ATP6V0D2 +1.1, gene:LAMP1 +1.4, gene:SCARB2 +1.1, gene:CLCN7 +1.1, gene:NPC2 +1.2, gene:CLN3 +1.2; 15-gene module mean rank 0.523, n.s.; hydrolase-vs-acidification median difference +1.14, label-permutation p=0.039). Inferred: proton-pumping, counter-ion and luminal-transport capacity per lysosome does not scale with hydrolase supply.", "Inferred bottleneck (activity/pH not measured): incompletely scaled acidification limits pro-hydrolase maturation and per-lysosome catalytic rate, so cargo residence time rises. Weak, non-identifying corroboration: cathepsin-candidate 2D spots split in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:052 +2.14 up; protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 down) and the two ATP6V1E1-candidate spots are both decreased (protein_spot:064 -1.20, protein_spot:065 -0.93); spot identities are ambiguous (each spot lists several candidate genes).", "Measured (RNA): sterol-synthesis/SREBP-target transcripts are elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:INSIG1 +1.87; 10-gene module mean rank 0.63, p=0.079, trend only). Inferred: the ER-accessible cholesterol pool is sensed as low despite increased cargo uptake, consistent with restricted lysosomal hydrolysis/egress rather than with cholesterol excess.", "Inferred consequence (not required by the chain): a strong nuclear-encoded TCA/OXPHOS transcript elevation (TCA module mean rank 0.91, p\u003c1e-4; 44-gene nuclear OXPHOS module 0.68, p=1e-4) with mostly decreased mtDNA-encoded transcripts is compatible with rerouted catabolic/energetic demand, but is also a competing primary mechanism and is not evidence for the lysosomal bottleneck."], "title": "Lysosomal acidification/membrane capacity fails to scale with cargo influx and hydrolase induction in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.318631613927556, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.04614780141477135, "cosine_similarity": 0.2939415274994436, "direction_accuracy": 0.5161812297734628, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mean_absolute_error": 0.5769029126213593, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.318631613927556, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.04614780141477135, "cosine_similarity": 0.2939415274994436, "direction_accuracy": 0.5161812297734628, "mean_absolute_error": 0.5769029126213593, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.83709125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 307}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_030", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (median +1.46; 77% positive); all set-level statements are made relative to that internal background, not against zero.", "Absence of a gene (e.g. CAT, G6PD, SOD1/2, NFE2L2, GSR, TXNRD1) from the supplied list is treated as 'not reported as differentially expressed', not as evidence of no biological change; this assumption is required for the 'PPP not compensating' step and is the weakest link.", "Transcript differences for peroxiredoxins, shuttles and PPP enzymes translate at least partly into protein and capacity differences; no protein measurement uniquely identifies any of these enzymes here.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each, so spots consistent with catalase (protein_spot:017), transketolase/aldolase (protein_spot:038) and transaldolase/annexin (protein_spot:043-046) are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Metabolic flux, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, peroxide levels, membrane potential, thiol oxidation state and enzyme localisation were not measured; all flux, activity and directionality statements are inferences.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous, and biological replicate number was not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia up-regulate transcripts for mitochondrial substrate oxidation and NADH shuttling together with a thiol-peroxidase (peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin/GPX4) module, while transcripts for the cytosolic pentose-phosphate arm (TALDO1, PGD) fall and NNT rises; we hypothesise that the resulting rate-limiting step is regeneration of reduced NADPH for thiol-peroxidase turnover, which becomes dependent on mitochondrial proton-motive force rather than on cytosolic PPP flux, making APOE4 microglia conditionally vulnerable to peroxide load and to ETC de-energisation. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is explicitly not implicated. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: NNT knockdown/knockout, or a low-dose protonophore (e.g. 0.5-1 uM FCCP) that collapses the proton-motive force without killing cells, should produce a significantly larger increase in cytosolic and mitochondrial roGFP2-Orp1/Grx1 oxidation and in BODIPY-C11 lipid peroxidation in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, and slower recovery after a bolus H2O2 challenge. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond equally, or APOE3 is more sensitive, the mitochondrial-NADPH-dependence step is falsified.", "Reciprocal prediction: pharmacological inhibition of the oxidative PPP (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide) should oxidise APOE3 microglia at least as much as APOE4 (APOE4 already having low PPP transcript levels). Greater APOE4 sensitivity to PPP inhibition than APOE3 would weaken the 'shift away from cytosolic PPP' claim.", "Direct bottleneck test: NADPH/NADP+ ratio measured in APOE4 versus APOE3 should be equal or lower in APOE4 at baseline despite higher peroxiredoxin protein, and 13C-glucose tracing should show equal or lower oxidative-PPP flux in APOE4. Higher NADPH/NADP+ and higher PPP flux in APOE4 would refute the bottleneck.", "Capacity test: supplementing NADPH-regenerating capacity (G6PD or NNT overexpression, or NAC/mitoTEMPO) should normalise the APOE4 peroxide-recovery kinetics and blunt part of the lysosomal/GPNMB-CTSD transcriptional program; failure to shift the lysosomal program would show that redox is parallel to, not upstream of, the lysosomal state.", "Negative prediction (peroxisome rejected): peroxisome number, PEX protein abundance and very-long-chain fatty-acid beta-oxidation flux (C26:0 turnover) should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3; a clear peroxisomal beta-oxidation deficit with normal peroxide handling would favour an alternative peroxisomal mechanism over this one.", "Protein-level test: immunoblot/2D-redox blot should show increased PRDX2/PRDX3 protein and an increased PRDX-SO2/3 hyperoxidised fraction in APOE4; increased total PRDX with no increase in hyperoxidised fraction and unchanged peroxide handling would weaken the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher RNA for mitochondrial oxidative and anaplerotic machinery and for NADH/carbon shuttles (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:MPC2, gene:GLUD1, gene:NDUFA5, gene:SDHB, gene:ATP5F1D). Inferred (not measured): greater electron flux into the respiratory chain and a more reduced matrix NADH pool.", "Inferred: higher matrix electron flux increases superoxide/H2O2 generation, raising the peroxide load that must be cleared by thiol peroxidases; no ROS species, peroxide concentration or oxidised-thiol pool was measured here.", "Measured: the antioxidant response detected at RNA level is thiol-peroxidase biased rather than canonically NRF2-driven (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GPX4, gene:MGST2, gene:GSS, gene:FTH1 all positive; no HMOX1/NQO1/GCLC/GCLM/SLC7A11 rows in the supplied differential list). Inferred: increased capacity, not increased activity, of peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin- and glutathione-dependent peroxide removal.", "Measured: transcripts of the cytosolic pentose-phosphate pathway are among the strongest decreases (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD), while the mitochondrial transhydrogenase gene:NNT is increased. Inferred: cytosolic NADPH-regenerating capacity is reduced and NADPH supply is re-partitioned toward the matrix, where NNT consumes the proton-motive force.", "Proposed bottleneck (inferred): reduction of oxidised peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin and glutathione, i.e. NADPH regeneration flux, not peroxidase protein abundance, limits peroxide clearance in APOE4 microglia; clearance therefore becomes conditional on mitochondrial membrane potential.", "Inferred consequence: a chronically oxidising cytosol with limited reserve promotes the lysosomal/lipid-handling state also seen at RNA level (gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB, gene:GPNMB, gene:SOAT1, gene:CYP27A1, gene:APOE); this ordering is a hypothesis, and the reverse order (lysosomal lipid handling driving redox demand) is not excluded by the data."], "title": "NADPH-regeneration bottleneck: APOE4 microglia run a mitochondrially fuelled, thioredoxin/peroxiredoxin-biased peroxide buffer while cytosolic pentose-phosphate transcripts fall"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1487009190886132, "cosine_similarity": 0.29358103954807185, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mean_absolute_error": 0.612873786407767, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07338551859099804, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1487009190886132, "cosine_similarity": 0.29358103954807185, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.612873786407767, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.679011, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 308}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level statements are made as rank enrichment within this list (median log fold change +1.46, 77.1% positive) rather than against a genome-wide null.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and effects up to |15| are retained as given; only signs and within-list ranks are interpreted, never absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partially informative of the corresponding protein and complex abundance; no mitochondrial, lysosomal or lipogenic protein was uniquely identified here (protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes and spot effects are uncorrelated with candidate-gene RNA, Pearson r = -0.05, n = 71), so the protein layer is not used as support.", "The four lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to reflect a genuine mitochondrial-genome expression or copy-number difference rather than a 10X Flex normalisation/ambient-RNA composition effect in which a lower mitochondrial read fraction mechanically inflates all nuclear genes; this is the main assumption at risk and is directly tested below.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so a fraction of the APOE4-vs-APOE3 signal may be non-cell-autonomous or contributed by contaminating astrocyte transcripts.", "Key nodes of the proposed route (CPT1A, ACLY, FASN, ACACA, NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2, mitoribosome and OXPHOS-assembly factors) were not supplied, so the chain is reconstructed from the flanking measured steps.", "Only one genotype pair, one timepoint (day 30) and one mock condition are represented; replicate structure is 'not supplied in workbook', so effect precision cannot be checked."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 by coordinately raising the nuclear-encoded substrate-oxidation program (pyruvate import, TCA, all measured structural subunits of ETC complexes I, III, IV and the F1Fo-ATP synthase) while the measured mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are lower. The proposed primary bottleneck is terminal oxidation at the mtDNA-encoded ETC core: nuclear machinery is transcriptionally expanded but cannot be assembled into proportionally more functional respiratory units, so acetyl-CoA/citrate-derived carbon entering mitochondria exceeds oxidative disposal capacity and is instead predicted to be exported and re-esterified through an up-regulated SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1 program with lipoprotein-lipid uptake via SCARB1, while a TFEB/MITF-driven lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase expansion handles the resulting lipid and organelle load. Respiration, assembly, flux, acetyl-CoA and neutral-lipid pools were not measured here; only transcript (and ambiguous protein-spot) abundances were, so causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING TEST: Seahorse respirometry plus BN-PAGE/immunoblot on isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, equal or higher nuclear-encoded subunit protein (NDUFB8, SDHB, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) but a reduced mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded protein ratio (MT-CO1 or MT-CO2 versus NDUFB8), less assembled complex I/IV, and reduced maximal and spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass. If APOE4 shows an unchanged or higher mtDNA-encoded:nuclear ratio and equal or greater maximal/spare respiration, the mitonuclear bottleneck is refuted and the coordinated nuclear up-shift should be reassigned to increased mitochondrial mass or to a normalisation artefact.", "Because mtDNA-encoded transcript depletion is claimed to be biological, mtDNA:nDNA copy-number ratio (qPCR) and per-cell mitochondrial read fraction should be lower in APOE4; if the mitochondrial read fraction differs but mtDNA copy number, MT-CO1 protein and respiration are all unchanged, the signal is a composition/normalisation artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "Lipid readout: APOE4 microglia should contain more neutral lipid (BODIPY/LipidTOX droplets, and cholesteryl-ester plus monounsaturated-TAG species by lipidomics) than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower neutral-lipid content in APOE4 weakens the storage arm.", "Blocking the proposed overflow route with the mitochondrial citrate-carrier inhibitor CTPI-2 or SLC25A1 knockdown, or with ACLY inhibition, should reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid content toward APOE3 with little effect in APOE3; if lipid droplets in APOE4 are unchanged by these perturbations, the citrate-export step is wrong even if the ETC bottleneck holds.", "SCD1 inhibition should preferentially deplete monounsaturated TAG/CE species and increase saturated-lipid stress markers in APOE4 relative to APOE3; no genotype-by-inhibitor interaction weakens the SREBF1/SCD arm.", "TFEB is predicted to be compensatory, not causal: TFEB knockdown should increase, not decrease, APOE4 lipid-droplet and undigested-substrate load, whereas TFEB overexpression should partially normalise it. If TFEB knockdown instead reduces APOE4 lipid accumulation, the lysosomal arm is a driver and this mechanism's ordering is wrong.", "Rescue directionality: supplying an oxidation bypass that does not require the mtDNA-encoded core (for example limiting exogenous lipoprotein/SCARB1 ligand supply, or expressing a mtDNA-independent alternative oxidase) should reduce APOE4 lipid storage; failure of any manipulation that restores respiration to reduce APOE4 neutral lipid would falsify the flux-diversion claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): all 38 measured nuclear-encoded structural subunits of complexes I/III/IV/V are higher in APOE4 (mean log fold change +2.81, 38/38 positive, binomial p ~5e-5 against the 77.1% positive background of this selected list), together with 12/12 measured TCA-cycle and mitochondrial-carrier genes (MPC2, MDH1, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, PDP1, SLC25A1, ACSS2). INFERRED: a transcriptional command to expand oxidative catabolism.", "MEASURED (RNA): 4 of 6 measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts are lower in APOE4 (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4). INFERRED (bottleneck): the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores that must partner with the nuclear subunits are limiting, so assembled, coupled respiratory-chain capacity does not scale with the nuclear program; ETC assembly, membrane potential and oxygen consumption were not measured.", "INFERRED: with pyruvate/acetyl-CoA supply raised (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, OGDH, MDH1 up) but terminal oxidation capacity-limited, TCA intermediates accumulate and citrate is exported (SLC25A1 up) and acetate/acetyl-CoA salvage increases (ACSS2 up), generating a cytosolic lipogenic acetyl-CoA pool. Neither citrate nor acetyl-CoA was measured, and ACLY/FASN/ACACA were not in the supplied rows.", "MEASURED (RNA): the sterol/fatty-acid anabolic and esterification module is uniformly higher in APOE4 (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR, INSIG1, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1; 16/16 measured members positive), together with the lipoprotein-lipid uptake receptor SCARB1 (largest lipid-gene effect in the list). INFERRED: increased monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis and re-esterification of fatty acids and sterols into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester, i.e. storage rather than oxidation; no lipid species were measured in this discovery set.", "MEASURED (RNA): TFEB and MITF are higher and 29 of 30 measured lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase/CLEAR genes are higher (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C). INFERRED: a compensatory (not driving) expansion of the degradative compartment responding to lipid and damaged-organelle load; lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and cargo flux were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): mitochondrial/peroxiredoxin antioxidant and stress-response genes are higher (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT, DDIT3). INFERRED: retrograde mitochondrial stress/integrated-stress signalling is the plausible driver of steps 1 and 5, closing a feed-forward loop in which stored, esterified lipid rather than oxidised lipid becomes the APOE4-specific end state."], "title": "Mitonuclear-discordant oxidative capacity in APOE4 microglia routes carbon into esterified lipid storage and a TFEB-expanded lysosomal compartment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3860078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20785096684182294, "cosine_similarity": 0.2932355580474375, "direction_accuracy": 0.3106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6286375404530744, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3860078277886497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20785096684182294, "cosine_similarity": 0.2932355580474375, "direction_accuracy": 0.3106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6286375404530744, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8919585, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 309}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_083", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified log base; program coherence is judged against that 77%-positive, large-effect background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "Increased hydrolase, v-ATPase and mitochondrial transcripts are assumed to translate into a proportional increase in the corresponding protein pools and in lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity and respiratory flux. None of these activities, nor lysosomal pH, cargo residence time, or lipid/undegraded-cargo content, were measured here; they are inferred, not observed.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increases are assumed to reflect increased MiT/TFEB transcriptional output; nuclear localization and mTORC1 status were not measured, so the coordinator identity is a hypothesis (mTOR pathway members are largely absent from the supplied list; gene:RRAGD +1.44 and gene:LAMTOR5 +1.69 are permissive but not diagnostic).", "The coupling of the lysosomal and mitochondrial modules is assumed to be a single coordinated cell-state program rather than two independent genotype effects; the data cannot separate these, and part of the uniform OXPHOS increase could reflect differences in mitochondrial content or in cell composition/maturation between genotypes rather than regulated coupling.", "Protein spots are treated as ambiguous multi-candidate features (2-6 candidates each); no spot is assigned to a single protein, and the overall up-skew of spots (38/47 significant spots positive) may partly reflect gel loading/normalization rather than biology.", "'Adaptive/increased throughput' applies to the measured mock condition only. Reduced spare capacity that would appear under an acute cargo challenge (myelin, oxLDL, apoptotic cells, Abeta) is a prospective prediction, not an observed defect.", "Descriptive module coherence (e.g. 39/39 OXPHOS positive; 31/33 CLEAR-core positive; 10/15 motility-module negative) is not a formal enrichment result: members of these modules are co-regulated and not independent, and membership lists were fixed before inspecting directions."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single rate-limiting lesion but by a coordinated cell-state shift: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, lysosomal membrane/transport proteins and late-endosome routing factors are broadly and strongly increased together with MiT/TFEB factors, and are matched by co-induction of mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS and metabolite-carrier transcripts, while a pre-specified leukocyte actin-motility/surveillance module (including the dominant microglial protease CTSS) is coordinately decreased. We propose that increased APOE4-associated lipid/membrane cargo load on the endolysosomal system drives a MiT/TFEB-type transcriptional expansion of degradative and downstream oxidative capacity (an adaptive, throughput-oriented configuration in the measured condition) with a shifted protease repertoire (CTSB/CTSD/CTSK/GBA/HEXA up, CTSS down), rather than an already-failed lysosomal bottleneck. Measured values are transcript and 2D protein-spot abundances only; degradative flux, acidification and protease activity were not measured, so causality and 'increased capacity' remain inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test (primary discriminator): in mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, measure bulk degradative flux directly (DQ-BSA dequenching rate, BODIPY-myelin or oxLDL clearance, LysoSensor/ratiometric lysosomal pH, and cathepsin B/D activity probes). The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows equal-or-higher per-cell degradative flux, equal-or-lower lysosomal pH and higher cathepsin B/D activity, with no accumulation of undegraded LC3-II/p62 or filipin-positive cargo. Observing higher lysosomal pH, lower cathepsin activity, or accumulated undegraded cargo despite the elevated transcripts would falsify the 'expanded, functioning capacity' reading and favour failed compensation.", "Prospective coordinator test: TFEB (and TFE3/MITF) knockdown or an mTORC1 agonist regimen in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase/lysosomal-membrane transcript increases; if the mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS increases (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, NDUF/ATP5 subunits) persist unchanged after that collapse, the proposed single coordinated program (Step 4 coupling) is wrong and the two modules are independent genotype effects.", "Prospective protease-repertoire test: despite globally higher cathepsin B/D activity, APOE4 microglia should show a selective CTSS-dependent deficit - reduced cleavage of a CTSS-preferred fluorogenic substrate, delayed invariant-chain (CD74/Ii p10) degradation and accumulation of Ii intermediates with reduced surface MHC-II peptide loading - rescuable by CTSS re-expression. Normal Ii processing and normal CTSS-substrate cleavage in APOE4 would falsify Step 5.", "Prospective reserve/challenge test: after an acute cargo load (myelin debris or apoptotic-neuron pulse), APOE4 microglia should clear the first pulse at least as fast as APOE3 but show earlier saturation (lipid-droplet/filipin accumulation, LysoTracker area, IL1B/CXCL8 release) at higher repeated loads; equal saturation thresholds in both genotypes would weaken the 'reallocated, load-driven state' interpretation.", "Prospective motility trade-off test: APOE4 microglia should show reduced process motility/chemotactic velocity and reduced pericellular proteolysis at baseline (live imaging, DQ-gelatin), and pharmacological or genetic blockade of lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) should reduce APOE4 fitness/survival more than APOE3 under lipid load. Equal motility and equal bafilomycin sensitivity would weaken Step 6.", "Prospective identity test for the ambiguous spots: targeted immunoblot/PRM on the strongest up spots (protein_spot:043-046) should show ANXA1 up (consistent with gene:ANXA1 +4.15) rather than TALDO1 up (gene:TALDO1 -2.32); and cathepsin-candidate spots should resolve as a pro-form/mature-form redistribution with unchanged or increased total CTSB/CTSD. Finding a genuine net decrease in total CTSB/CTSD protein would contradict Step 2."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (cargo load, inferred): APOE4 alters lipid/lipoprotein handling in microglia, increasing the lipid and membrane cargo retained in endosomes/lysosomes. Supported at transcript level by increased APOE (gene:APOE +1.24), scavenger/lipid-uptake and sterol-handling transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72); cargo mass itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (transcriptional expansion of lysosomal capacity): MiT/TFEB-family transcripts rise (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) with a coherent CLEAR-type output: acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:CTSH +1.54), all eight represented v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1F +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1 +1.68, gene:ATP6V1C1 +1.29, gene:ATP6V0D2 +1.12) and lysosomal membrane/transport proteins (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:CLN3 +1.17, gene:LAMTOR5 +1.69, gene:RRAGD +1.44).", "Step 3 (routing to the degradative compartment): late-endosome/lysosome delivery and positioning transcripts increase in parallel (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:RAB7B +1.40, gene:ARL8B +1.12, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:AP5S1 +4.39, gene:AP5Z1 +3.78, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:KIF5B +3.56, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:GNPTG +3.02), with mannose-6-phosphate receptor routing only partly aligned (gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:SPG11 -1.83, gene:AP1M1 -1.03).", "Step 4 (downstream consumption of catabolites): amino-acid/metal export and mitochondrial oxidative machinery are co-induced, consistent with catabolites being consumed rather than accumulating: gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC31A2 +11.85, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, and 39/39 represented OXPHOS subunits positive (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02).", "Step 5 (protease repertoire re-specification, not uniform increase): the dominant microglial cysteine protease falls sharply while bulk luminal hydrolases rise (gene:CTSS -5.57 versus gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36), predicting reduced CTSS-dependent pericellular/invariant-chain proteolysis; gene:CD74 +3.84 and gene:CIITA +1.50 are consistent with retained MHC-II input whose CTSS-dependent processing step is selectively reduced.", "Step 6 (resource trade-off in cell state): a pre-specified leukocyte actin-motility/surveillance module is coordinately decreased against the 77%-positive selected-list background (10/15 negative; gene:SPN -7.26, gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B -5.83, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:PLEK -2.53, gene:CSF1 -5.89, gene:SEMA4A -5.19, gene:HRH2 -5.42), i.e. APOE4 microglia sit in a degradation/oxidation-weighted state and a motility/immune-effector-weighted state is relatively down; exceptions gene:ARHGDIA +10.61, gene:MYO1D +6.53, gene:ARPC1B +2.15, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:ITGB1 +6.31 indicate an adhesion-biased rather than globally collapsed cytoskeletal program.", "Step 7 (state compatibility at protein level, not confirmation): 2D protein spots are ambiguous (every spot has 2-6 candidate identities; mean 4.8) and shift predominantly upward (38 of 47 significant spots positive). Spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal proteins occur in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14 CTSL-containing, protein_spot:053 +1.54 CTSD-containing, protein_spot:012 +0.68 MAN2B1-containing, protein_spot:013 +0.77 DPP7-containing, protein_spot:063 +0.68 GNS-containing versus protein_spot:058 -0.85 and protein_spot:069 -1.38 CTSD/CTSB-containing, protein_spot:067 -1.00 CTSB/HEXB-containing, protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93 ATP6V1E1-containing). This pattern is compatible with redistribution among pro-form/mature or charge variants under an expanded lysosomal program, and is not evidence for a net decrease of any named protein."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a MiT/TFEB-associated endolysosomal-plus-mitochondrial catabolic state with a re-specified protease repertoire, traded against the actin-based motility/surveillance program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2510984750581545, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1880342030471995, "cosine_similarity": 0.2928300910574354, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_083", "mean_absolute_error": 0.618084142394822, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2510984750581545, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1880342030471995, "cosine_similarity": 0.2928300910574354, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.618084142394822, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.400788, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 83}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_052", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1); enrichment statements are therefore relative to this biased background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The reported RNA effects carry an unspecified logarithm base and show a large global positive offset (median +1.459, 77% positive, with ACTB and MT-ATP6 strongly negative); all claims are made on within-dataset percentile ranks, which are invariant to that offset, and no absolute fold-change is asserted.", "Transcript rank is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/receptor capacity; protein abundance, enzyme activity, lipid pools, subcellular localisation and flux were not measured for any step.", "The 92 protein spots each carry 2-6 candidate genes and are dominated by ACTB/keratin candidates; no spot uniquely identifies a lysosomal or sterol protein, so no protein observation is used as evidence for or against this mechanism.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck are absent from the supplied rows (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, STARD3, LIPA, SCAP, INSIG2, HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1); the egress deficit is inferred from the measured members plus these gaps, not demonstrated.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex at a single day-30 mock timepoint; cell-state composition differences and ambient RNA between APOE4 and APOE3 wells could generate part of the coherent rank shift. Biological replicate number was not supplied.", "The comparison is genotype-associated and observational; no causal direction between uptake, hydrolase expression and sterol egress is established here."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a rank-coherent up-shift of lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts together with an extreme up-shift of the lipoprotein-lipid uptake receptor SCARB1, while transcripts of the endolysosomal cholesterol-egress/efflux arm (NPC2, OSBPL8, OSBPL1A, PLTP, APOE) stay at or below the global shift; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is egress of lipoprotein/membrane-derived cholesterol out of the endolysosome, so that catabolic input exceeds export capacity and the ER sterol pool is not raised (no SREBP-2 target repression signature), sustaining further uptake. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating imaging test: filipin (or equivalent free-sterol probe) co-stained with LAMP1 in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show a higher fraction of cellular free cholesterol inside LAMP1+ compartments in APOE4. If APOE4 lysosomal sterol fraction is equal to or lower than APOE3, the proposed egress bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating rescue test: acute relief of the lysosomal step with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 protein supplementation) should, in APOE4 but not APOE3, lower LAMP1+ sterol, raise the ER-accessible sterol pool, and de-repress nothing while instead lowering SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR) and lowering SCARB1. No genotype-specific change in these readouts after cyclodextrin would weaken the mechanism.", "Input test: SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade should reduce lysosomal neutral/free lipid load and partially normalise the APOE4 hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program toward APOE3. If the hydrolase program is unchanged by SCARB1 loss, lipoprotein-lipid uptake is not the input driving it and step 1 fails.", "Capacity test: acid hydrolase activity assays (GBA, GAA, acid sphingomyelinase) and LysoTracker/lysosomal pH measurement should be higher/more acidic in APOE4. Unchanged or reduced activity despite the rank-high transcripts would break the measured-abundance-to-inferred-capacity step.", "Order-of-events test: TFEB knockdown should suppress the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts without correcting APOE4 lysosomal cholesterol retention (predicting biogenesis is a response, not the bottleneck). If TFEB knockdown fully normalises lysosomal sterol, the bottleneck should be reassigned upstream to lysosomal biogenesis rather than to egress.", "Negative-control prediction from the rejected part of the focus: pharmacological block of de novo synthesis (statin, or SQLE inhibition) should not selectively normalise the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lysosomal phenotype, consistent with the absence of cholesterol-biosynthesis enrichment (set mean percentile 60.0, p_up = 0.18). A strong statin-specific rescue would favour a synthesis/sensing mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SCARB1 transcript is the highest-ranked sterol-related gene (gene:SCARB1, +8.22 in the reported log unit, 99.1st percentile of the 2212 supplied RNA rows, adjusted p 3.4e-117). Inferred, not measured: increased surface SCARB1 protein and increased selective uptake flux of lipoprotein-associated cholesteryl ester and phospholipid into APOE4 microglia.", "Measured: a rank-coherent set of lysosomal acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts sits far above the global shift (gene:GAA 99.7th, gene:GBA 97.9th, gene:CTSK 98.7th, gene:ATP6V1H 98.1st, gene:NAGLU 96.2nd, gene:HEXA 95.6th, gene:SMPD1 95.4th, gene:CTSB 94.9th, gene:ATP6V1A 89.2nd, gene:CTSD 75.9th; CLEAR-type 18-gene set mean percentile 71.5, rank-permutation p = 0.0006). Inferred, not measured: increased lysosomal number/acidification and increased acid hydrolase activity; TFEB nuclear translocation is inferred, not observed (gene:TFEB transcript is only at the 69th percentile).", "Inferred flux step: internalised lipoprotein and membrane lipid is delivered to this expanded acidic compartment and hydrolysed there, with SMPD1-dependent sphingomyelin turnover (gene:SMPD1) liberating free cholesterol into the lysosomal limiting membrane. Neither lipid species nor hydrolytic flux was measured.", "Measured contrast (the proposed bottleneck): the lysosomal sterol-egress/efflux transcripts do not scale with the catabolic arm - gene:NPC2 34.7th, gene:OSBPL8 12.7th (negative effect), gene:OSBPL1A 25.6th, gene:PLTP 27.2nd, gene:APOE 38.3rd percentile; the 7-gene egress/efflux set has mean percentile 42.9 (rank-permutation p_up = 0.74, i.e. no enrichment). Inferred: cholesterol handoff from the lysosomal lumen/membrane to ER and plasma membrane acceptors becomes limiting relative to input.", "Inferred consequence on the ER sterol sensor: with egress limiting, the ER-accessible sterol pool is not raised, so the SREBP-2 arm shows no repression signature (gene:SREBF2 27.5th, gene:HMGCS1 28.3rd, gene:LDLR 51.1st, gene:MYLIP 40.8th percentile), while the lipogenic/distal arm is high (gene:SREBF1 91.8th, gene:DHCR24 85.4th, gene:ERLIN1 83.3rd). The cell therefore continues to behave as sterol-demanding despite lysosomal lipid load.", "Inferred systems consequence: the cytosolic sterol carrier SCP2 is rank-high (gene:SCP2 96.3rd percentile) as a compensatory non-vesicular transfer route, but with the lysosomal egress step limiting the net result predicted is retention of free/esterified cholesterol and sphingolipid in APOE4 lysosomes rather than redistribution to the ER."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolytic capacity and SCARB1-dependent lipid uptake without a matched endolysosomal sterol-egress arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25875087693386994, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20867589450080054, "cosine_similarity": 0.29282559328256574, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6349805825242718, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25875087693386994, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20867589450080054, "cosine_similarity": 0.29282559328256574, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6349805825242718, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1322015, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 310}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_093", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 0.5, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directionality is therefore judged against a 77% positive background, and absent genes (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, SQSTM1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, most SREBP2 targets) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as an indicator of expressed capacity and of demand-driven transcriptional output, not of enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, protein delivery, localization or flux; gene:TFEB and gene:MITF transcript increases are used as markers of MiT/TFE-type output and do not demonstrate nuclear translocation or activity.", "The 92 protein rows are 2D-gel-type spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5) and no unambiguous protein assignment; they are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of an individual protein.", "The astrocyte co-culture and possible genotype-linked differences in cell-state composition (10X Flex, replicates not supplied) could contribute to apparent program shifts; no cell-composition or purity information was supplied.", "The inference that catabolic products are exported and oxidized rather than retained is a routing inference from co-elevated exporter and mitochondrial transcripts; no metabolite, lipid, flux or organelle-content measurement is supplied.", "Reduced reserve inferred from the narrowed repertoire (gene:CTSS, gene:M6PR, gene:CSF1 decreases) is a prediction about a future challenge, not an observed baseline defect. Unverified background knowledge (MiT/TFE control of CLEAR genes, APOE4 lipid phenotypes) is used only for interpretation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, multi-layer up-shift of the endolysosomal degradative module (acidification, glycosphingolipid/glycoconjugate hydrolases, cathepsins, lysosomal solute exporters, endosomal sorting adaptors) that is transcriptionally coupled to an expanded mitochondrial anaplerotic/TCA module and to lipid re-esterification and continued sterol acquisition. We propose this is an increased-throughput, altered-routing cell state (cargo-driven MiT/TFE-type output), not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck: measured transcript abundance indicates capacity and demand, while the decisive degradative and lipid fluxes are unmeasured. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in day-30 mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, per-cell lysosomal degradative flux measured with DQ-BSA dequenching, Magic Red cathepsin activity and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester or myelin-debris clearance should be equal or higher in APOE4, with equal or lower lysosomal pH (LysoSensor/ratiometric). If APOE4 instead shows reduced dequenching, higher lysosomal pH, and accumulation of undigested cargo, the increased-throughput/altered-routing claim is falsified and the competing degradative-bottleneck explanation is favored.", "Prospective coupling test: TFEB/TFE3 knockdown or a MiT/TFE dominant-negative in APOE4 microglia should collapse the coordinated hydrolase + v-ATPase + lysosomal-solute-carrier elevation (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:SLC38A7) and, if the proposed coupling holds, also lower the TCA/carrier transcripts (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH) and mitochondrial oxygen consumption. If the mitochondrial module and respiration are unchanged by MiT/TFE loss, mechanism step 4 is wrong and the two modules are parallel, not coupled.", "Prospective routing test: SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (or supplying ER-accessible sterol, e.g. 25-hydroxycholesterol) in APOE4 microglia should reduce the SREBP-type acquisition signature (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2, gene:DHCR24) and cholesteryl-ester content without lowering hydrolase transcripts. If hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts fall in parallel, the endolysosomal arm is a sterol-sensing readout rather than a cargo-load-driven program.", "Prospective reserve test: an acute cargo challenge (myelin debris, apoptotic neurons or oxLDL) should reveal earlier saturation in APOE4 than APOE3 - equal initial uptake and clearance rate but a lower maximal clearance and greater undigested-cargo accumulation - together with a smaller further induction of gene:GBA/gene:HEXA/gene:CTSB. If APOE4 shows the same or greater maximal clearance and normal further induction, the reduced-reserve component is falsified.", "Prospective specificity test: because gene:CTSS and gene:M6PR are decreased while other hydrolases increase, APOE4 microglia should show selectively reduced CatS-dependent invariant-chain/antigen processing (despite gene:CD74 +3.84) with preserved bulk proteolysis. Uniformly reduced hydrolase activity across substrates would contradict the proposed selective, MiT/TFE-shaped repertoire and favor a global lysosomal defect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia are biased toward a lipid/debris-handling activation state: scavenger and opsonic receptor and lipid-associated microglial transcripts are higher than APOE3 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:FABP5 +1.13), which we infer increases delivery of membrane-lipid and glycoconjugate cargo into endosomes (delivery rate itself not measured).", "Cargo load raises MiT/TFE-type transcriptional output (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03 as transcript-level markers only), coordinately elevating the CLEAR-type module: v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:CLCN7; 11/11 represented positive), glycosidase/sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:AGA, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH), cathepsins (gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSH, gene:DPP7) and endosomal sorting/adaptors (gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:AP3D1, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP4E1, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CCDC22, gene:IGF2R, gene:RAB7A, gene:CHMP4B).", "Lysosomal solute exporters and luminal-transport components are concurrently higher (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:LAPTM4A +2.90, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SLC66A1 +2.14, gene:TMEM192 +2.12), which we infer sustains cytosolic delivery of catabolic products rather than luminal accumulation; luminal content and export flux are not measured.", "The exported carbon is matched by an expanded mitochondrial import/anaplerotic/TCA module, the most magnitude-shifted program in the data (gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB, gene:GLS, gene:PCK2; 14/14 positive) with supporting respiratory-chain and mitochondrial-antioxidant transcripts (gene:NDUFA5 +7.30, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79).", "Liberated sterol and fatty acid are inferred to be re-esterified and stored and to be replaced by continued synthesis and uptake rather than to relieve ER sterol sensing: gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:NPC2 +1.17, gene:CH25H +1.62. The ER-accessible sterol pool is not measured; this arm is directionally coherent but its effect sizes are not distinguishable from the selected list background.", "Net predicted state in the mock condition: higher per-cell endolysosomal-to-mitochondrial catabolic throughput with a narrowed, specialized repertoire (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:IDS -1.56, gene:CSF1 -5.94, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:RAC2 -1.97), i.e. reduced reserve and reduced antigen-processing/homeostatic breadth that would be revealed mainly by a future cargo or immune challenge, not necessarily an ongoing degradative failure at baseline."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a MiT/TFE-associated high-capacity endolysosomal catabolic state whose lipid-derived carbon is routed to mitochondrial TCA and to re-esterified storage rather than to the ER regulatory sterol pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2982040112790911, "cosine_similarity": 0.2921624162645874, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6238608414239482, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2982040112790911, "cosine_similarity": 0.2921624162645874, "direction_accuracy": 0.1634304207119741, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6238608414239482, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.27756975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 84}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_158", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of a gene (e.g. ASAH1, PSAP, UGCG, SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, GALC) means it did not pass that selection, which we treat as 'no evidence of coordinate induction', not as a measured null.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified, so effects are used ordinally (ranks/percentiles) rather than as fold-change magnitudes; several values (up to ~15) are implausible as literal log2 pseudobulk ratios.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to translate into hydrolase protein and, with cofactors and luminal pH permitting, into enzymatic activity. This is unverified: the supplied protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel spots and do not confirm it (protein_spot:067 containing HEXB/CTSB is down, protein_spot:064/065 containing ATP6V1E1 are down, CTSD candidates appear in both up and down spots).", "Ceramide, sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, sphingosine, S1P, lysosomal pH, lysosome number and degradative flux were not measured in the supplied data; every statement about lipid pools, localisation, flux and rate limitation is inference.", "The comparison is stated as isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; we assume the differential list reflects microglial cell-intrinsic differences rather than differing astrocyte carry-over or cell-state composition (gene:S100B is strongly up, which is compatible with a composition/contamination confound).", "The list shows a strong global positive shift (77% of rows up, median effect ~+1.46), so only relative rank enrichment, not raw direction, is treated as informative.", "Causal direction is assumed but not established: the hydrolase induction could equally be a downstream compensatory response to a lipid load created elsewhere."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated up-shift of MiT/TFE-associated endolysosomal transcripts in which the sphingolipid-degradation ENTRY enzymes (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA) are among the most strongly elevated transcripts, whereas de novo/anabolic sphingolipid genes are not coordinately elevated and no terminal ceramide-clearing enzyme (acid ceramidase/prosaposin/GALC/ACER) appears among the selected differential results. We hypothesise that this asymmetry biases sphingolipid flux forward into the lysosomal lumen faster than ceramide can be cleared, so that per-lysosome ceramide disposal (not enzyme transcript abundance) is the rate-limiting step, with partial compensatory efflux/disposal (SPNS1, SGPL1, CERK) and re-routing of liberated lipid into sterol/neutral-lipid storage (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DGAT1, SOAT1, SCARB1). Ceramide and other lipid pools were NOT measured here; the lipid consequence is a prediction, not an observation, and causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted sphingolipidomics of day-30 mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (whole-cell and lysosome-enriched fractions) should show higher ceramide (notably C16:0/C24:1) and a higher ceramide:sphingomyelin ratio in APOE4, with sphingomyelin and hexosylceramide unchanged or lower. If instead sphingomyelin and hexosylceramide accumulate while ceramide is unchanged or lower, the 'entry-enzymes-fast, disposal-slow' direction is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: raising terminal ceramide-clearing capacity (ASAH1/acid-ceramidase overexpression, or saposin-D/prosaposin supplementation) in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal ceramide AND partially normalise the induced hydrolase module (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB) and the storage-lipid transcripts (DGAT1, SOAT1, SCD) toward APOE3. If ceramide falls but the hydrolase and lipid-storage transcript differences persist unchanged, the bottleneck is not terminal ceramide disposal and this mechanism is weakened.", "Reciprocal perturbation: functional inhibition or knockdown of acid sphingomyelinase (SMPD1) should reduce the APOE4 ceramide excess and the neutral-lipid storage program; if ceramide is unaffected, the glycosphingolipid (GBA/HEXA-HEXB) arm or non-lysosomal sources dominate, weakening the SMPD1-centred entry step.", "Enzyme-activity assay: per-cell acid sphingomyelinase, GBA and HEXA/HEXB activities should be measurably higher in APOE4 than APOE3, while acid ceramidase activity should not increase proportionally (ASM:acid-ceramidase activity ratio higher in APOE4). If hydrolase activities are unchanged or lower despite the transcript differences (as the ambiguous protein-spot data allow), the transcript-to-activity assumption fails and the mechanism is falsified in its present form.", "Regulator test: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase transcript differences (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V subunits) toward APOE3 levels while worsening, not relieving, lysosomal lipid accumulation. Persistence of the hydrolase differences after TFEB knockdown would falsify the proposed MiT/TFE-dependent step.", "Alternative-mechanism discriminator: lysosomal pH in APOE4 microglia should not be substantially more alkaline than APOE3. If APOE4 lysosomes are clearly less acidic, the parsimonious explanation becomes a v-ATPase/acidification defect driving compensatory CLEAR-gene induction, and the sphingolipid-specific bottleneck claim is weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_158", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for MiT/TFE-family regulators and CLEAR-type endolysosomal machinery (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF; v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C; gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU). Inferred: an expanded / more transcriptionally active endolysosomal transcriptional program, not a measured increase in lysosome number or degradative flux.", "Measured: within this program the sphingolipid-entry hydrolases are extreme outliers of the differential list (gene:SMPD1 95th, gene:GBA 98th, gene:HEXA 96th percentile of all reported effects; also gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2, gene:GLA), together with lipid-presentation/transfer transcripts (gene:GLTP, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2). Inferred: increased capacity to convert sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids to ceramide inside acidic compartments.", "Measured: the de novo/anabolic sphingolipid arm is not coordinately induced (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:ORMDL2 only modest; gene:B4GALT5 decreased; SPTLC/UGCG/SGMS/DEGS transcripts do not appear among the selected differential results). Inferred: the sphingolipid difference is catabolic/routing, not increased synthesis.", "Not measured / inferred bottleneck: no terminal ceramide-clearing transcript (ASAH1, PSAP, GALC, ACER family) is present in the supplied differential results, so entry-step induction is predicted to exceed ceramide-disposal capacity, producing luminal ceramide/sphingoid-base accumulation in APOE4 lysosomes.", "Measured, interpreted as partial compensation: transcripts for lysosomal sphingoid-base efflux and downstream disposal are modestly higher (gene:SPNS1, gene:SGPL1, gene:CERK), as are late-endosome/retromer and fusion components (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VAMP3). Inferred: attempted rerouting of sphingolipid catabolites out of the lysosome rather than resolution of the block.", "Measured: sterol/lipogenic and neutral-lipid storage transcripts are higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) while fatty-acid activation transcripts fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5). Inferred: lipid liberated from degraded membranes is esterified/stored rather than fully catabolised, a state expected to reinforce lysosomal lipid load.", "Predicted phenotype (not observed here): ceramide-enriched, functionally strained lysosomes in APOE4 microglia, which would explain why the largest genotype differences in this dataset lie in the lysosomal-hydrolase and lipid-storage programs rather than in classical inflammatory transcripts (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2 up but gene:CCL4, gene:RELB down)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia induce a lysosomal sphingolipid-entry catabolic module (SMPD1/GBA/HEXA-HEXB/GLA) without matched ceramide-disposal capacity, making terminal lysosomal ceramide clearance the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2315290034338884, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24134705294066075, "cosine_similarity": 0.29167219649489806, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_158", "mean_absolute_error": 0.643831715210356, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2315290034338884, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.24134705294066075, "cosine_similarity": 0.29167219649489806, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.643831715210356, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90546825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 311}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_018", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every supplied adjusted p value is below 0.05) with a strong positive offset (mean +1.39, 77% positive, unspecified logarithm base preserved); pathway claims are therefore made relative to the within-list distribution, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absolute directionality of the offset itself is not interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the amount of translated hydrolase; the mechanism explicitly assumes it does NOT track lumenal enzymatic activity, which was not measured.", "TFEB/MITF transcriptional activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, vesicular flux and all lipid species (glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2, sphingomyelin, ceramide) are inferred, not observed here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; assigning protein_spot:064/065 to v-ATPase V1E1 and protein_spot:067 to CTSB/HEXB is provisional, and the several cathepsin-D-containing spots move in both directions, so no net cathepsin-D abundance change is asserted.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal may derive from non-microglial cells or from genotype effects acting through astrocytes; replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size magnitudes are treated as unstable.", "APOE4 versus APOE3 comparison is isogenic, but no causality is established by these correlative measurements; the transcript module could equally be a parallel consequence of the genotype rather than a compensatory response."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 principally by a coordinated, TFEB/MITF-associated transcriptional up-scaling of the lysosomal glycosphingolipid catabolic module (GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLA, GBA2, SMPD1, NAGLU, MAN2B1, SUMF1) and of v-ATPase subunits, which we interpret as compensation for a bottleneck in lumenal hydrolytic throughput rather than as increased degradative flux: the hydrolase-delivery/activation arm (SCARB2, M6PR transcripts; v-ATPase-V1E1- and CTSB/HEXB-containing protein spots) does not rise in parallel, so glycosphingolipid substrate turnover is predicted to lag lipid input and glucosylceramide/GM2-type substrates should accumulate in the APOE4 endolysosome. De novo sphingolipid synthesis is not supported by these data and is not invoked.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, live-cell GBA activity (PFB-FDGlu) and beta-hexosaminidase activity (MUG/MUGS) per cell will increase far less than the corresponding transcript fold changes (predicted activity ratio below ~1.5-fold despite large transcript elevation), while lipidomics shows higher HexCer/GlcCer, GM2 or GA2 and sphingomyelin in APOE4. If GBA and HEXA/B activities scale in proportion to transcript and these glycosphingolipids are unchanged or reduced in APOE4, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Restoring throughput: augmenting lumenal GlcCer hydrolysis in APOE4 (recombinant GBA uptake, a GBA chaperone, or SCARB2 over-expression) should lower HexCer/GM2 and bring the CLEAR/hydrolase transcript module (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, ATP6V1A, TFEB targets) back toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the elevated transcript module after substrate normalisation would falsify the feed-forward step 6.", "Substrate-source test: limiting lipid input (SCARB1/CD36 blockade, delipidated medium, or myelin-free conditions) should attenuate both the hydrolase transcript module and the predicted glycosphingolipid excess in APOE4. If the module is unchanged, steps 1-2 are weakened and an APOE4-intrinsic transcriptional effect is favoured.", "Substrate-limb test: UGCG inhibition (eliglustat or GENZ-123346) should reduce HexCer/GM2 and normalise lysosomal morphology preferentially in APOE4; equal or greater effect in APOE3 would argue against a genotype-specific glycosphingolipid bottleneck.", "Acidification arm: APOE4 lysosomal pH measured ratiometrically should be equal to or higher (less acidic) than APOE3 despite higher v-ATPase transcripts. Finding APOE4 lysosomes more acidic with intact hydrolase activity would falsify the delivery/activation lag in step 4.", "Specificity control: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should collapse the hydrolase transcript module while worsening (not improving) glycosphingolipid accumulation. If TFEB knockdown reduces substrate accumulation, the compensatory interpretation is wrong and the module should instead be read as a driver."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid scavenging and lipogenic/sterol handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE), which we infer increases delivery of sphingolipid-rich membrane and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system; the lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred activity): Elevated gene:TFEB and gene:MITF transcripts accompany a coherent rise of CLEAR-type lysosomal genes; we infer increased TFEB/MITF transcriptional output. Nuclear localisation and phosphorylation state of TFEB were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA): The glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic module rises above the list-wide shift (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SUMF1), together with v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1).", "Step 4 (measured RNA and protein spots; inferred sub-proportional enzyme delivery): The routing/activation arm lags: gene:SCARB2 (LIMP-2, the GBA carrier) and gene:M6PR sit in the lowest third of this DE list, and protein spots whose candidate lists include v-ATPase V1E1 or CTSB/HEXB are reduced (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067). Because spots carry several candidate genes, this is suggestive, not identification of those proteins.", "Step 5 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Hydrolytic throughput per unit substrate therefore fails to keep pace with input, and glucosylceramide/HexCer, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin accumulate in the APOE4 lysosome. No lipid species was measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured RNA; inferred localization/routing): Accumulated glycosphingolipid is proposed to perturb endolysosomal membrane routing, consistent with elevated gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VAMP3 and gene:RAB32 transcripts, sustaining TFEB-driven transcription as a feed-forward loop and biasing APOE4 microglia toward a lipid-laden, degradation-limited state (gene:LGALS3, gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:FTH1, gene:CLEC7A, gene:TREM2)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-scale the lysosomal glycosphingolipid-hydrolase transcript module without matched delivery capacity, making lysosomal glucosylceramide/GM2 turnover the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06244328460091075, "cosine_similarity": 0.2915932619880355, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6338187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12489384484732119, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06244328460091075, "cosine_similarity": 0.2915932619880355, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6338187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7120245, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 312}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_062", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list-wide median is +1.46 (77% positive), so only within-list relative ranks (percentiles) are interpreted, never raw sign.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effects are on non-comparable scales and are never combined arithmetically.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes (mean 4.8) and are treated as ambiguous spot-pattern measurements; no spot is asserted to be a uniquely identified protein, and the divergent directions of same-candidate spots are consistent with, but do not prove, altered proteoform processing.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme supply only; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, proenzyme/mature ratio, protein localisation, autophagic flux, lipid and sterol pools, and secretion were not measured in this dataset and are inferred.", "The gene sets used for enrichment were assembled by the analyst after inspecting the data, so the permutation p-values are descriptive coherence statistics, not pre-registered tests.", "Biological replicate structure is not supplied ('not supplied in workbook'), so effect precision cannot be judged; protein p-values range up to 1.0 and 45/92 spots are not reported significant.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so an APOE4 effect may be non-cell-autonomous (astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply) rather than microglia-intrinsic.", "Background knowledge used to name the CLEAR/TFEB program, M6P-dependent hydrolase sorting and cathepsin pro/mature processing is unverified here because literature and database retrieval were disabled."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a coordinated, above-background elevation of acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts together with TFEB (a CLEAR-like compensatory program), while the 2D protein-spot pattern of hydrolase-containing spots redistributes rather than rising coherently. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the acidification-dependent maturation/delivery of pro-hydrolases into functional lysosomal enzyme, so degradative throughput per lysosome lags the transcript program; the assigned sterol-synthesis/trafficking/export focus is rejected because those gene sets show no enrichment above the list-wide positive shift and no protein-spot support. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: In matched APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia, immunoblot of cathepsin D and cathepsin B should show a higher pro-form/mature-form ratio in APOE4, and DQ-BSA or Magic-Red-derived hydrolase activity per LAMP1-positive volume should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite equal-or-higher CTSD/CTSB transcript. If mature-form protein and activity scale proportionally with the elevated transcripts, the maturation bottleneck is falsified.", "Ratiometric lysosomal pH (LysoSensor Yellow/Blue or pHrodo-dextran) should be measurably less acidic in APOE4; low-dose bafilomycin A1 should produce a smaller incremental rise in lysosomal pH and a smaller incremental drop in hydrolase activity in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal lysosomal pH and equal bafilomycin sensitivity would weaken the acidification-dependent step.", "TFEB overexpression (or mTORC1 inhibition) should raise hydrolase transcripts in both genotypes but should NOT normalise APOE4 degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching rate); if boosting the transcript program alone restores flux, the bottleneck is transcript supply and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Pro-cathepsin D released into conditioned medium (normalised to cell number) should be higher in APOE4, reflecting mis-sorted proenzyme; equal secretion would weaken the M6P-routing contribution.", "Re-running the 2D protein separation with immunodetection of cathepsin D should show that the up- and down-moving spots (protein_spot:053 vs protein_spot:069/protein_spot:058) correspond to different cathepsin D proteoforms; if the discordant spots instead resolve to unrelated candidate proteins (e.g. actins, keratins, 14-3-3), the spot-pattern evidence collapses.", "STEROL TEST (falsifies the assigned focus if it succeeds): statin treatment or an LXR agonist should not normalise the APOE4 hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program, and an unbiased transcriptome should show no coordinated SREBP2 target-set activation in APOE4; coordinated SREBP2 target induction with rescue by sterol manipulation would favour a sterol-synthesis mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mechanism_steps": ["An elevated endolysosomal substrate load in APOE4 microglia (inferred, not measured here) engages a CLEAR/TFEB-like transcriptional response: TFEB transcript is up (gene:TFEB) together with a coherent block of acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) that sits above the already-positive background of this selected DE list (hydrolase set mean percentile 0.68, permutation p=0.005; hydrolase+v-ATPase+TFEB set 0.65, p=0.002).", "Endolysosomal traffic and maturation machinery is simultaneously remodelled rather than uniformly boosted: RAB7A, AP3D1, AP5M1, AP5S1, IGF2R and GNPTG transcripts are high, whereas the cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript is low relative to background (gene:M6PR, percentile 0.15) and gene:AP1M1 is below background; we infer (not observe) an imbalanced M6P-dependent routing of newly synthesised pro-hydrolases.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK (inferred activity/flux, not measured abundance): acidification-dependent proteolytic maturation of pro-hydrolases into active mature enzyme inside the endolysosome. The transcript surge is therefore not converted proportionally into mature hydrolase activity.", "Consistent with a maturation/processing shift rather than a bulk abundance increase, protein spots whose candidate lists include the same hydrolase move in opposite directions (CTSD-containing protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:058 down; CTSB-containing protein_spot:055 and protein_spot:057 up versus protein_spot:067 down; ATP6V1E1-containing protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 down; ACP2-containing protein_spot:088 up versus protein_spot:086 down), and spot effects are uncorrelated with the transcript effects of their candidate genes (Pearson r = -0.05 over 71 spots). Because each spot has 2-6 candidate genes, these spots are treated as pattern-level, not protein-level, evidence.", "Because degradative flux per lysosome lags demand, undigested substrate persists and the CLEAR-like transcript program is sustained (feed-forward), while secretory/ER load rises (gene:ATF6, gene:DDIT3) and a chemokine-biased output is favoured (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2) without a coherent interferon signature (gene:IRF2 down, gene:IFI16 and gene:IRF5 below the list median).", "Sterol handling is positioned as a downstream consequence, not the driver: cholesterol-synthesis/SREBP transcripts are only marginally above background (mean percentile 0.62, p=0.077, driven by gene:SREBF1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7 while gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR sit at or below the list median), the sterol trafficking/export set is not enriched (mean percentile 0.47, p=0.62; gene:OSBPL8 down, gene:SCARB1 a lone extreme outlier), and no protein spot in the dataset lists any sterol-handling candidate gene."], "title": "A hydrolase-maturation bottleneck, not sterol synthesis, distinguishes APOE4 microglia: a CLEAR-like transcript surge that fails to convert into mature acid-hydrolase capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13076468633460103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06305345223597372, "cosine_similarity": 0.2885311020864315, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13076468633460103, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06305345223597372, "cosine_similarity": 0.2885311020864315, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.677035, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 313}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_027", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every gene has |effect| \u003e 1) with an unspecified logarithm base; set-level comparisons are therefore made against the list-internal background (median +1.46, 77% positive), not against an unbiased transcriptome, and the list-wide positive shift may be partly technical (composition, ambient RNA, normalization).", "Transcript abundance changes for hydrolases and acyltransferases translate into proportionate enzyme activity and flux; this is unverified here, as no enzyme-activity, lipidomic, or flux measurement is supplied.", "Absence of ASAH1, ACER3, SGMS1/2, SPHK1, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN and PLIN2 from the list means they did not pass the differential-expression filter, i.e. they are not coordinately up with the hydrolases; it does not establish that they are unchanged (background knowledge that these encode the ceramide/sphingosine disposal and lipid-transfer steps is unverified literature knowledge, not evidence from these files).", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as identification of a specific enzyme, and the proteomic layer also shows a global positive shift (median +0.49, 64/92 spots positive).", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcripts may derive from, or be induced by, the astrocyte partner or from APOE4-dependent differences in astrocyte-supplied lipoprotein lipid.", "Causality is not established: these are steady-state genotype-associated differences under mock treatment, with biological replicate number not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolic arm (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA, NAGLU, GAA, MAN2B1, SGSH, CTSB/CTSD, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB/MITF) that is not matched by an equivalent increase in the sphingoid-base disposal steps, while the fatty-acid activation/desaturation/esterification arm (SREBF1, SCD, ACSS2, SLC25A1, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, DGAT1, SOAT1, CHPT1, PCYT2, MGLL) is simultaneously elevated. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is intralysosomal ceramide/free-fatty-acid clearance: hydrolytic input from internalized membranes exceeds disposal capacity, and the surplus acyl chains are shunted into monounsaturated neutral-lipid storage and phospholipid re-acylation. All statements about flux, ceramide levels, lysosomal activity and localization are inferences from RNA abundance, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation A (SCD inhibition): treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with an SCD1 inhibitor (or SCD knockdown) should produce a genotype-selective effect in APOE4 -- greater loss of neutral-lipid droplet content, greater rise in saturated ceramide/diacylglycerol species and greater lysosomal membrane permeabilization/viability loss than in APOE3. If SCD inhibition affects both genotypes equally, or if APOE3 is more sensitive, the proposed acyl-salvage buffering step is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation B (input vs disposal): pharmacological inhibition of GBA (conduritol B epoxide) or SMPD1 knockdown should REDUCE the APOE4-specific ceramide excess and lipid-droplet load, whereas acid-ceramidase (ASAH1) overexpression should also reduce it; if instead ASAH1 overexpression fails to normalise APOE4 lipid-droplet content and lysosomal morphology, the ceramide-disposal bottleneck is falsified in favour of an upstream cargo-delivery or cholesterol-export bottleneck.", "Lipidomic prediction: untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher ceramide and hexosylceramide/GM2-type species and higher triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass with an increased MUFA:SFA ratio (16:1/16:0, 18:1/18:0) in APOE4. Finding lower ceramide, lower neutral lipid, or an unchanged MUFA:SFA ratio in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Functional prediction: pulse-chase of fluorescent sphingomyelin or of dye-labelled apoptotic-cell/myelin membrane should show faster initial hydrolysis but slower terminal clearance and greater intracellular retention of label in APOE4; equal or faster terminal clearance in APOE4 would weaken step 3.", "Selection-bias control: re-analysing an unfiltered whole-transcriptome table should retain the lysosomal glycolipid-hydrolase set above the global shift (set mean well above the transcriptome-wide mean). If the enrichment disappears once the differential-expression filter and global positive shift are removed, the entire hypothesis is unsupported.", "Counter-evidence stress test: gene:CTSS (-5.57), gene:M6PR (-1.72), gene:STX17 (-2.06) and gene:GPAT3 (-2.23) are inconsistent with uniform lysosomal/lipogenic upregulation. If autophagosome-lysosome fusion (STX17-dependent) rather than lipid disposal proves to be the limiting step -- e.g. LC3/p62 accumulation in APOE4 is rescued by STX17 restoration while ceramide and droplet phenotypes persist -- the primary bottleneck assignment should be replaced."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred program): A CLEAR/MiT-type lysosomal biogenesis program is transcriptionally elevated in APOE4 (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:SCARB2 +1.06), which we infer -- but did not measure -- increases lysosome number and acidification capacity.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Within that program the membrane-glycolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolases are disproportionately elevated (gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:SGSH +1.32; set mean +4.12 vs list-wide mean +1.39, permutation p=4e-4), which we infer raises the rate at which internalized membrane lipid is converted to ceramide, sphingoid bases and free fatty acid inside the lysosome.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; partly inferred from absence): The disposal side of this reaction is not coordinately raised -- the ceramidase/sphingosine-clearance genes ASAH1, ACER3, SGMS1/2, SPHK1 are absent from the supplied differential list and gene:SGPL1 is only +1.09, while ceramide-generating/consuming-but-retaining steps rise (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:GLTP +2.38). We therefore propose ceramide/sphingoid-base egress and deacylation as the rate-limiting step in APOE4; the ceramide pool itself was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Fatty acids released by steps 2-3 are re-activated and desaturated rather than fully oxidised: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 (set mean +2.85, permutation p=0.014), inferred to raise the monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply used to buffer saturated/ceramide-derived species.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux and localization): Acyl chains are re-esterified into storage and membrane lipids -- gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25 (neutral lipid), gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05 (phospholipid re-acylation/head-group synthesis), with turnover markers gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04, gene:PLA2G7 +1.13, gene:PLBD1 +1.68. We infer, but did not measure, increased lipid-droplet mass and altered PL acyl composition.", "Step 6 (consequence, inferred): The resulting lipid-laden, ceramide-pressured endolysosomal state is proposed to underlie the concurrent lipid-handling/activation signature (gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LGALS1 +2.75) and to reduce spare degradative capacity when new membrane cargo arrives; no functional degradation assay is present in these data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid catabolism faster than ceramide and fatty-acid disposal, forcing SCD/acyltransferase-dependent acyl salvage into neutral and remodeled glycerolipids"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3702507107779788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2177551805174164, "cosine_similarity": 0.2884437625515526, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6486666666666666, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3702507107779788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2177551805174164, "cosine_similarity": 0.2884437625515526, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6486666666666666, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2720355, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 314}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_040", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Reported RNA effects (unspecified logarithm base, preserved as reported) are comparable across genes within this list, so rank/percentile comparisons between nuclear OXPHOS and MT-encoded genes are meaningful despite the strong global upward shift (77.1% of 2212 rows positive).", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. PEX genes, most mitoribosomal genes, 7 of 13 MT-encoded genes) is treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Steady-state transcript ratio is used as a proxy for subunit supply ratio; this assumes no compensating APOE4-specific change in mitochondrial translation efficiency or subunit half-life, neither of which was measured.", "The nuclear-vs-MT discordance is biological rather than a technical artefact of 10X Flex probe capture, ambient RNA, or per-cell mitochondrial-fraction normalisation differences between genotypes.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified: protein_spot:017 (CAT among five candidates, +0.77) and protein_spot:077 (PRDX2 among six, mostly keratins, +1.07) are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, never as identified protein measurements.", "The antioxidant and ISR transcript increases are read as a response to, not a cause of, the respiratory imbalance; the temporal order was not measured.", "Causality has not been established by these data; all directional statements are hypothesised."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia coordinately elevate the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (OXPHOS structural/accessory subunits, TCA enzymes, SLC25 carriers, import machinery) while mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts for complexes V, III, IV and I (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) fall to the low tail of the same measured distribution. We hypothesise that this transcript stoichiometry mismatch is the primary bottleneck: it limits assembly of the mtDNA-core-dependent complexes so that respiratory capacity does not scale with the enlarged nuclear supply, increasing electron leak and matrix ROS, which is answered by a mitochondrial peroxiredoxin/glutathione/NADPH antioxidant program (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, GSS, MSRA, TXNDC17, NNT, FTH1) and a DELE1/PERK-associated integrated stress response (DELE1, EIF2AK3, DDIT3, SHMT2, NUPR1) plus a lysosomal-degradative program. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation and ether-lipid synthesis are explicitly rejected as the bottleneck: no PEX, AGPS, GNPAT, FAR1, ACOX2 or catalase RNA changes are present and ABCD1 is decreased.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: raising mtDNA-encoded core supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM overexpression, or mitochondrially targeted rescue of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB) should increase MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2 transcripts, increase fully assembled complex V and III on blue-native PAGE, and normalise PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4 and DDIT3 transcripts toward APOE3 levels. If MT transcripts rise but complex assembly, mtROS and the PRDX3/DDIT3 program are unchanged, the stoichiometry-imbalance bottleneck is falsified.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling should show that the ratio of assembled complex V, III and IV to nuclear-encoded subunit steady-state protein is lower in APOE4 than APOE3, with detectable sub-assemblies. If assembled complexes scale proportionally with the elevated nuclear subunit program, the mechanism is weakened.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (mtDNA copy number or TOMM20) should show lower ATP-linked and maximal respiration and a higher proton-leak fraction in APOE4 despite the higher nuclear OXPHOS transcript program. Equal or higher normalised ATP-linked respiration would weaken the mechanism.", "Compartment-resolved redox: mito-roGFP2-Grx1 / MitoSOX should be more oxidised in APOE4; a mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoTEMPO or MitoQ) should reduce PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4 and DDIT3 transcripts toward APOE3 levels, whereas an equipotent non-targeted antioxidant should not. If only the non-targeted antioxidant works, the mitochondrial origin of the ROS is falsified.", "Relay test: DELE1 or HRI/EIF2AK1 knockout should uncouple DDIT3 and NUPR1 induction from the OXPHOS imbalance without restoring respiration. Persistent DDIT3 induction after DELE1 loss would falsify step 6 while leaving steps 1-5 intact.", "Peroxisomal rejection test: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux markers (C26:0/C22:0 ratio, phytanic acid, plasmalogen C16:0 species) and catalase activity should be similar between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock. A large peroxisomal flux difference would mean the assigned peroxisomal focus was wrongly rejected and this hypothesis is misdirected.", "Because MT-ND5 (+1.93) and MT-ND4L (+1.95) run opposite to the other MT transcripts, targeted qPCR plus mtDNA copy-number assay should show that the discordance is transcript-specific (processing/stability) rather than uniform mtDNA depletion. Uniform loss of all 13 MT transcripts proportional to mtDNA copy number would replace this mechanism with simple mtDNA depletion."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia raise nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts above the already upward-shifted background of this selected DE list - 38/38 nuclear OXPHOS subunit genes positive (median +2.64 vs list median +1.46; Mann-Whitney p=1.0e-4; binomial vs 77.1% background up-rate p=1.2e-4), together with TCA/pyruvate genes (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, ACO2, IDH3B, IDH3G), SLC25 carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A46) and import/translation factors (HSPA9, TUFM).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, opposite sign): mtDNA-encoded transcripts sit in the low tail of the same distribution (median -1.56, median percentile 16 vs 73 for nuclear OXPHOS; nuclear vs MT Mann-Whitney p=9.1e-4), driven by MT-ATP6 (-3.35, adj p=9.1e-228), MT-CYB (-2.32), MT-ND4 (-1.80) and MT-CO2 (-1.33) - i.e. the catalytic cores of complexes V, III, I and IV.", "Step 3 (inferred, not measured): because complexes V, III and IV cannot be completed without their mtDNA-encoded cores, the mismatch caps the number of fully assembled complexes; the surplus nuclear subunits accumulate as sub-assemblies or are degraded rather than adding respiratory capacity. Assembled-complex amount, mtDNA copy number and mitoribosomal output were not measured here.", "Step 4 (inferred flux/redox): incomplete complex III/IV assembly with maintained upstream NADH/FADH2 supply (elevated TCA and complex I accessory transcripts) increases electron residence time at the CoQ/complex III steps, raising matrix superoxide, while limiting ATP synthase capacity lowers ATP-linked respiration per unit mitochondrial mass. ROS and respiration were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, consistent response): a mitochondrially weighted antioxidant/NADPH program is induced - PRDX3 (+3.49), PRDX5 (+1.96), PRDX2 (+4.41), GPX4 (+2.79), GSS (+2.11), MSRA (+2.60), TXNDC17 (+7.13), NNT (+2.90) - alongside iron-handling changes (FTH1 +2.53, SLC25A37 +4.53), all positive (7/7 antioxidant genes; Mann-Whitney vs high-confidence background p=1.7e-2). Whether this is sufficient to hold the thiol pool reduced is inferred, not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, stress relay): mitochondrial stress signalling markers rise - DELE1 (+4.79), EIF2AK3 (+1.53), DDIT3/CHOP (+2.79), SHMT2 (+2.24), NUPR1 (+1.19), HSPA9 (+2.40) - consistent with a chronic integrated stress response downstream of the imbalance; kinase activity and eIF2-alpha phosphorylation were not measured.", "Step 7 (measured RNA/protein, downstream): a lysosomal-degradative and lipid-handling program is elevated (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, ATP6V1A/1H/0C; median +2.10, p=5.0e-2) with APOE (+1.20) and TREM2 (+1.31), which we interpret as compensatory clearance of damaged mitochondria and oxidised lipid, providing the link from redox imbalance to the APOE4 lipid phenotype."], "title": "Mito-nuclear OXPHOS subunit stoichiometry imbalance, not peroxisomal metabolism, drives a mitochondrial-ROS/ISR state in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22347044271314107, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0502737503873524, "cosine_similarity": 0.2881016003916958, "direction_accuracy": 0.313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6006731391585761, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22347044271314107, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0502737503873524, "cosine_similarity": 0.2881016003916958, "direction_accuracy": 0.313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6006731391585761, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9343305, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 315}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_072", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base; only within-dataset relative ranks and module-versus-background comparisons are interpreted, never absolute fold sizes, and the global positive shift (median 1.46, 77% positive) is treated as a selection/normalization offset rather than a biological whole-transcriptome increase.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the capacity of a step; acidification, hydrolytic rate, sterol egress rate, ER sterol content, droplet content and localization are all inferred and unmeasured in the supplied data.", "2D protein spots carry several candidate genes each (e.g. protein_spot:052 lists ACTB, CTSL, TPM3, CLIC1, NT5C1A), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spots are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration of a redistribution of cathepsin-containing species, not as evidence for a specific protein's abundance.", "The APOE4-versus-APOE3 comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment or line background drives the differences; positive effects mean higher in APOE4.", "Absent genes (NPC1, ABCA1/ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, PLIN2, P2RY12/TMEM119) are missing by row selection, not measured as unchanged."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia, the transcriptional program for endolysosomal acidification and lipid-directed hydrolysis (v-ATPase subunits, GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB/CTSD, with TFEB and RAB7A) is coordinately elevated well above the global upward shift of these selected differential-expression rows, whereas the measured lysosome-to-ER lipid-transfer arm is not (NPC2 near the dataset median, OSBPL8 reduced). We propose that the primary bottleneck is egress of hydrolysis-derived sterol/lipid from the late-endosome/lysosome to the ER, so that ER-localized sensing continues to call for lipid supply (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACSS2 elevated) and surplus acyl/sterol flux is routed to esterification (DGAT1, SOAT1, ACAT2), producing a lipid-laden acidic compartment with reduced degradative headroom. All flux, localization and causal statements are inferred; no lipid, sterol, pH, or organelle measurement is supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: blocking lysosomal sterol egress in APOE3 microglia (U18666A, or NPC1/NPC2 knockdown) should phenocopy the APOE4 signature - coordinate induction of v-ATPase subunits plus GAA/GBA/HEXA/CTSB with sustained SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 - while APOE4 cells should show a blunted incremental response because the step is already limiting; if U18666A instead produces the APOE4-like induction equally in both genotypes, or fails to raise the v-ATPase/hydrolase module at all, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Relieving the bottleneck (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, recombinant NPC2, or OSBPL8 re-expression) in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 transcripts and shrink LAMP1+ compartment area and filipin-positive lysosomal sterol toward APOE3 values; unchanged SREBF1/SCD after demonstrated sterol mobilization would falsify the ER-sensing link (Step 4) even if Steps 1-3 stand.", "Direct measurement prediction on the unmeasured pools: APOE4 microglia should show higher filipin signal colocalized with LAMP1, higher cholesteryl-ester to free-cholesterol ratio, and higher 16:1/16:0 plus 18:1/18:0 desaturation indices than APOE3; equal lysosomal sterol with equal desaturation indices would falsify the core claim.", "Capacity test: partial v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1) or SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition should impair myelin- or apoE-lipoprotein-clearance and raise cell death preferentially in APOE4 relative to APOE3; equal sensitivity would argue the expanded acidic-hydrolase program is not load-driven compensation.", "Specificity test against a generic-amplification alternative: in a properly normalized whole-transcriptome APOE4-vs-APOE3 comparison of the same cells, the 25-gene acidification/hydrolase module must remain enriched against an expression-matched background; loss of enrichment there would show the module signal is an artifact of the selected-row global shift.", "Directionality test: SCD inhibition should increase ER-stress and saturated-lipid toxicity markers more in APOE4 than APOE3, since the desaturation arm is proposed to be a compensatory buffer; equal or greater protection in APOE4 would weaken Step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid internalization capacity, most strikingly SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, 99.1st percentile of the 2212 selected RNA rows) with ABCA7 and TREM2 also positive; increased uptake flux is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): a TFEB/MITF-associated endolysosomal program is coordinately elevated above the dataset-wide shift - all eight measured v-ATPase subunits are positive (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) together with lipid-directed hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) and gene:TFEB, gene:RAB7A; the 25-gene module median is 2.38 versus a global median of 1.46 (permutation p=0.023, Mann-Whitney p=0.0013).", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred bottleneck): the egress arm is not matched - gene:NPC2 sits at the 34.7th percentile (below the global median) and gene:OSBPL8, the only measured ER-anchored ORP-family lipid-transfer gene, is decreased (12.7th percentile); NPC1, STARD3, GRAMD1A/B and ABCA1/ABCG1 are absent from the supplied rows, so the export step is inferred as rate-limiting rather than demonstrated.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing state): rather than shutting down, the ER lipogenic-desaturation arm stays engaged (gene:SREBF1 91.8th, gene:SCD 89.1st, gene:DHCR24 85.4th, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACSS2 percentiles), consistent with an ER compartment that is not receiving lysosome-derived sterol/lipid even while the lysosome is expanding its catabolic machinery.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): surplus fatty-acyl and sterol species are predicted to be re-esterified and buffered (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACAT2 positive); neutral-lipid and droplet content are not measured here.", "Step 6 (consequence, inferred): the resulting enlarged, substrate-loaded acidic compartment lowers spare degradative capacity for further lipid/debris load, and the microglial protease repertoire shifts qualitatively rather than uniformly upward, marked by collapse of gene:CTSS (0.7th percentile) alongside gene:CSF1 loss."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand acidic-hydrolase capacity while lysosome-to-ER sterol/lipid egress lags, sustaining an ER lipogenic-desaturation program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36668759000110773, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1587986152135943, "cosine_similarity": 0.2877735110115127, "direction_accuracy": 0.3220064724919094, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6245922330097087, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36668759000110773, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1587986152135943, "cosine_similarity": 0.2877735110115127, "direction_accuracy": 0.3220064724919094, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6245922330097087, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.98516675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 316}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are therefore made relative to this internal background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene means it did not enter the selection rather than that it is unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme and transporter capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, lipid-droplet content, respiration or flux measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each, so no spot identifies a single protein; spots are used only as weak corroboration and never as the sole basis for a step.", "Astrocyte co-culture, unreported replicate number and possible library-size/composition normalisation differences could generate part of the uniform positive RNA shift; the mechanism assumes the relative ordering of pathways survives that shift.", "Causal direction (APOE4 genotype -\u003e uptake/lysosomal/lipogenic program -\u003e storage) is assumed, not demonstrated; the same pattern could be a compensatory response to pre-existing droplet load."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 coordinately raises transcripts for lipid uptake (SCARB1), lysosomal hydrolysis/acidification (TFEB, CTSB/CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H), TCA/anaplerotic carbon handling with citrate and malate/aspartate export (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, GOT1, SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and an SREBF1-anchored esterification module (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, DGAT1), while beta-oxidation transcripts are absent from the differential set and mtDNA-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation transcripts are lower (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4). We propose that the rate-limiting step is disposal of liberated fatty acid by mitochondrial beta-oxidation, so that fatty-acyl carbon is preferentially esterified into triacylglycerol/lipid droplets rather than oxidised. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; the flux, localisation and causal ordering below are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: with uniformly 13C-labelled palmitate or LDL, APOE4 microglia should show lower label appearance in CO2/TCA intermediates per unit fatty-acid taken up but higher label in triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester than isogenic APOE3; equal or higher oxidative labelling in APOE4 would weaken the oxidation-bottleneck claim.", "SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572) or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce BODIPY-positive lipid-droplet area in APOE4 towards APOE3 levels and increase free saturated acyl species; unchanged droplet area under both inhibitors would falsify the SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 esterification sink.", "SLC25A1 inhibition or ACSS2 knockdown should selectively lower de novo 13C-glucose/13C-acetate incorporation into palmitate and droplets in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would remove the citrate/acetyl-CoA supply step.", "Blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (lysosomal acid lipase inhibitor or v-ATPase inhibition) should shift APOE4 lipid from droplets to undegraded lysosomal lipid without reducing total lipid load; if droplets fall in parallel with lysosomal lipid, the lysosome-to-droplet routing step is wrong.", "Redox counter-test: NRF2 target transcripts (HMOX1, NQO1, GCLM, TXNRD1) should not be induced in APOE4, and N-acetylcysteine or catalase overexpression should not normalise droplet load; strong NRF2 induction plus antioxidant rescue would favour an oxidative-stress mechanism over this one.", "Raising oxidative disposal capacity (CPT1A overexpression or a mitochondrial uncoupler at non-toxic dose) should lower APOE4 droplet load without lowering SCARB1-dependent uptake; unchanged droplet load would weaken the bottleneck assignment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases scavenger-receptor and lipoprotein-handling transcript abundance (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:LDLR +1.50), which we infer raises lipid influx flux into microglia; influx itself was not measured.", "A coordinated TFEB-type lysosomal program (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1; v-ATPase subunit gene:ATP6V1H) expands the degradative compartment, inferred to liberate fatty acids, sphingoid bases and sterol from internalised lipid inside lysosomes.", "Mitochondrial substrate-entry and export transcripts rise far above the dataset background (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50), which we infer increases citrate/malate export and, with gene:ACSS2 (+2.93), cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability.", "Terminal fatty-acid disposal does not scale with this input: no carnitine-shuttle or acyl-CoA-dehydrogenase transcript reached the supplied differential set, gene:ACSL4 (-2.14) and gene:ACSL5 (-3.11) fall, and mtDNA-encoded respiratory transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80) are among the lowest values despite induction of nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts, indicating an inferred mito-nuclear stoichiometry imbalance rather than measured respiration.", "The SREBF1 esterification module (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25) then becomes the dominant sink: SCD-generated monounsaturated acyl-CoA plus glycerolipid acyltransferase capacity is inferred to esterify the excess acyl pool at the ER.", "Net inferred consequence in APOE4 versus APOE3: accumulation of triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester lipid droplets alongside an enlarged lysosomal compartment, with cytoskeletal/lysosomal protein-spot increases (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055) consistent with, but not diagnostic of, an expanded degradative-vesicular and actin remodelling state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lysosome-derived and citrate-derived carbon into SREBF1/SCD-dependent neutral-lipid storage because terminal fatty-acid oxidation is not co-scaled"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.41430971458110255, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2588822864754357, "cosine_similarity": 0.2873256124036482, "direction_accuracy": 0.32038834951456313, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6869514563106797, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.41430971458110255, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2588822864754357, "cosine_similarity": 0.2873256124036482, "direction_accuracy": 0.32038834951456313, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6869514563106797, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73151575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 317}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_055", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77.1% of rows are positive with median +1.46, so every module was judged relative to that internal background rather than to zero. If the true whole-transcriptome distribution is centred at zero, module-versus-background enrichment must be recomputed and could change.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2. RNA and protein effects are therefore not placed on a common scale.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme capacity. SREBP-1, SCD, DGAT1 and SOAT1 activities are set post-transcriptionally (SREBP cleavage, substrate supply, allostery); none of these were measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used to assert a specific protein's abundance.", "Neutral lipid, cholesteryl ester, triacylglycerol, ceramide, lipid-droplet number, sterol flux, cholesterol efflux (ABCA1/ABCG1 not in the list), oxidation rate and subcellular localisation are all unmeasured in the supplied data and appear only as inferences or predictions.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some lipid inflow may be non-cell-autonomous; the discovery data cannot separate microglial from astrocyte-derived lipid.", "Isogenic design is assumed to control genetic background, but replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so effect-size precision cannot be assessed."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia, the transcript module that stands out above the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list is the SREBP-1/desaturase/acyltransferase arm (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, FADS1, DGAT1, SOAT1, INSIG1), while lysosomal hydrolase and lipid-uptake transcripts are also raised. We hypothesise that the ER-localised desaturation/esterification node (SCD feeding DGAT1/SOAT1/AGPAT2) is the primary bottleneck: it is the dominant sink for fatty acid and sterol liberated by an expanded lysosomal catabolic compartment, so APOE4 microglia convert incoming lipid into esterified neutral lipid (triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester in droplets) rather than clearing it. All flux, localisation, enzyme activity and direction statements are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treat APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with an SCD inhibitor or a DGAT1 inhibitor (and the SOAT1 inhibitor avasimibe as a parallel arm). The mechanism predicts that neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content in APOE4 falls toward APOE3 levels while the lysosomal hydrolase transcripts GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB and CTSD remain elevated. If droplet content is unchanged, or if the lysosomal transcript elevation collapses in parallel (placing the lysosome upstream rather than downstream), the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Epistasis test: inhibit lysosomal hydrolysis/acidification (bafilomycin A1, or a GBA-selective inhibitor). The mechanism predicts partial reduction of APOE4 neutral-lipid storage from loss of substrate supply, but persistence of the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 transcript elevation. If SREBF1 and SCD normalise, SREBP-1 is downstream of lysosomal lipid release and step 4 (blunted ER feedback) fails.", "Feedback test: acute sterol/LDL loading should suppress SREBF1-target transcripts (SCD, LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1) less efficiently in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes would weaken the 'sensing does not register the load' step.", "Activation-state test: immunoblot for precursor versus cleaved nuclear SREBP-1. The mechanism requires higher nuclear (cleaved) SREBP-1 in APOE4. Higher precursor with no increase in the nuclear form would break the transcript-to-activity inference in step 1.", "Lipidomic prediction: APOE4 microglia should show increased cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol with an increased monounsaturated (18:1) to saturated (18:0) acyl ratio. Unchanged CE/TG and unchanged desaturation index would falsify the predicted flux consequence.", "Specificity check: the ER-proteostasis alternative predicts coordinated induction of HSPA5, XBP1s, HERPUD1, SEL1L, EDEM1 and PDIA family transcripts and increased ER chaperone protein. Observing that coordinated ERAD/chaperone induction in APOE4 would favour a UPR-primary mechanism over this lipid-partitioning mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts of the SREBP-1 lipogenic/acyl-remodelling module are higher in APOE4 (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, AGPAT2 +6.29, MBOAT2 +3.26, LPCAT1 +3.07, DGAT1 +1.72, FADS1 +1.59, SOAT1 +1.25, INSIG1 +1.87, unspecified log base); this module median (+3.07) exceeds the global median of the selected list (+1.46; permutation p=0.024). Inferred, not measured: correspondingly sustained nuclear SREBP-1 transcriptional output and higher SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1 enzymatic capacity at the ER.", "Measured in parallel: lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are high (GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1A +4.23, CTSD +2.86, GBA2 +2.63, TFEB +2.38, HEXB +2.17). Inferred: expanded lysosomal catabolic capacity that liberates fatty acids, sphingoid backbones and unesterified sterol into the cytosol/ER pool. This module is NOT statistically distinguishable from the global up-shift (permutation p=0.15), so it is treated as a concurrent, weaker-evidence module.", "Measured: lipid-uptake/transfer transcripts are raised (SCARB1 +8.22, SCP2 +5.95, LDLR +1.50, CD36 +1.38, NPC2 +1.17, ABCA7 +2.14, APOE +1.24) while the ER-endolysosome lipid-transfer gene OSBPL8 is down (-1.90) and long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases feeding oxidation are down (ACSL4 -2.14, ACSL5 -3.11). Inferred: lipid inflow to the ER is increased while the route toward beta-oxidation is not co-scaled.", "Bottleneck (inferred): because SREBF1-target transcripts remain high despite this liberated/imported lipid load, ER lipid-sensing feedback does not restrain anabolism; INSIG1 elevation is read as an SREBP target, not as evidence of pathway suppression. The SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1/AGPAT2 esterification node therefore becomes the dominant available sink and sets the rate of lipid disposal.", "Predicted flux consequence (inferred, unmeasured here): net partitioning of fatty acid and sterol into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester stored in cytoplasmic lipid droplets in APOE4, with an accompanying monounsaturated-acyl and remodelled-phospholipid shift (SCD, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, AGPAT2).", "Predicted secondary consequence (inferred): sphingolipid pool remodelling, since sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolases (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB) and ceramide synthases (CERS4 +2.52, CERS6 +1.06) are both raised while the ceramide-disposal genes ASAH1, UGCG and SGMS1/2 were not measured in this list; this arm is therefore explicitly under-determined."], "title": "Sustained SREBP-1 lipogenic/acyl-esterification capacity is the rate-limiting sink that routes lysosome-liberated and de-novo lipid into stored neutral lipid in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4675996012258612, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26388785292173933, "cosine_similarity": 0.28717016957448255, "direction_accuracy": 0.38996763754045305, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_055", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6458737864077669, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4675996012258612, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.26388785292173933, "cosine_similarity": 0.28717016957448255, "direction_accuracy": 0.38996763754045305, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6458737864077669, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03639275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 318}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_092", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2) means it was not in the supplied list and must not be read as unchanged or as an observed pool.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is used only as a monotonic ranking of effect size; the whole list is shifted positive (median +1.46, 1705/2212 up), so only within-list relative enrichment, not absolute direction, is treated as informative.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes; assigning any spot to a cathepsin or hydrolase is provisional, and spot-level directional splits are interpreted only as possible isoform/processing redistribution, not as identified proteins.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a lagging and imperfect proxy for enzyme activity; no enzyme activity, lipid, pH, lysosome number or flux measurement is supplied, so all activity, flux, localisation and causal statements are inferred.", "The RNA and protein modalities are assumed comparable in cellular origin; the culture is a microglia-astrocyte co-culture, and the protein spots may include non-microglial material, which would dilute or distort the discordance argument.", "Replicate number, dispersion and baseline expression are not supplied, so very large effects (up to 15.5) cannot be checked for low-count instability, and the multiple pathway sets tested here are not multiple-testing corrected.", "TFEB transcript elevation is assumed to reflect an engaged CLEAR programme; TFEB is regulated mainly by nuclear translocation, which was not measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily at the endolysosomal lipid-catabolism step: transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are raised well above the strong global positive RNA shift (a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR-type response to inferred higher luminal lipid substrate load, with elevated lipoprotein/scavenger uptake transcripts as one likely supply route), while the available protein-spot data give no evidence that mature hydrolase abundance scales with the transcript increase; the sterol-synthesis and sterol-export arm is at background and is therefore rejected as the distinguishing mechanism. The predicted consequence is retention of hydrolase substrate lipids (sphingomyelin, hexosyl-/glycosphingolipids, gangliosides, cholesteryl esters) in APOE4 endolysosomes. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of sorted APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia (mock) should show higher sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide/glucosylceramide, GM2/GM3 gangliosides and cholesteryl esters in APOE4, concentrated in a lysosome-enriched fraction. If these substrate classes are equal or lower in APOE4, the 'unmet substrate load' claim fails and the transcript rise instead reflects successfully increased catabolic flux.", "Enzyme activity assays (GBA, HEXA/B, acid sphingomyelinase, cathepsin B/D) per cell should rise far less than the corresponding transcript fold changes in APOE4, giving an activity-to-mRNA ratio below that of APOE3. If activity scales in proportion to transcript, Step 3 and the bottleneck placement are falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: compare reducing substrate influx (SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade, or blocking lipoprotein/phagocytic uptake) with increasing the transcriptional programme (TFEB overexpression) in APOE4 microglia. The mechanism predicts that influx reduction lowers lysosomal substrate lipids and normalises the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation, whereas TFEB overexpression raises those transcripts further without normalising substrate lipids. The opposite pattern - TFEB overexpression alone normalising lipids while influx reduction does not - would place the bottleneck at transcription/biogenesis and weaken this hypothesis.", "Directly augmenting mature enzyme (recombinant M6P-tagged hydrolase uptake, or a GBA chaperone such as ambroxol) should reduce lysosomal substrate lipid load and lower the compensatory hydrolase transcripts more in APOE4 than in APOE3. No genotype-selective benefit would weaken the mechanism.", "If the mechanism holds, blocking the ER re-esterification outlet (SOAT1 inhibition) in APOE4 should shift retained sterol from cholesteryl ester to free sterol without reducing total lysosomal lipid load; a fall in total lysosomal lipid load under SOAT1 inhibition would argue instead for an esterification-driven storage mechanism upstream of the lysosome.", "Sterol control test: neither the mevalonate-pathway transcripts present in the list nor sterol-export transcripts should distinguish the genotypes beyond the global shift. Finding coordinated, background-corrected suppression of SREBP-2 targets or of ABCA1/ABCG1 in an unbiased transcriptome would support a sterol-sensing mechanism instead of this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred flux, not measured): APOE4 microglia deliver more lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosome than APOE3; transcript-level support is SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22, 99th percentile of the DE list), with CD36, TREM2 and APOE transcripts also higher (gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE). Uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A coordinated CLEAR-type lysosomal program is transcriptionally elevated above the global shift - TFEB (gene:TFEB) plus acid hydrolases GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, GLA, CTSB, CTSD and v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, and the late-endosome GTPase RAB7A. Module median 2.02 versus a global DE-list median of 1.46 (bootstrap CI 1.68-2.38; Mann-Whitney p = 0.038 against all other genes; hydrolase-only subset p = 0.018).", "Step 3 (inferred activity, weakly supported): Mature hydrolase protein/activity is inferred not to rise in proportion to transcript. Across the 38 protein spots with a single RNA-matched candidate gene the RNA-protein rank correlation is essentially zero (Spearman -0.03, p = 0.88), and spots whose candidate lists contain CTSB/CTSD/HEXB split in direction (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.59, protein_spot:057 +0.59 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) despite CTSB and CTSD transcripts being strongly up. Spot identities are ambiguous, so this is supportive, not decisive. Enzyme delivery/maturation components are discordant rather than uniformly raised (gene:M6PR -1.72; gene:SCARB2 +1.06, below the global median).", "Step 4 (inferred localisation/pool): Substrate lipids therefore remain in the endolysosomal lumen rather than being hydrolysed and released to the ER-accessible pool. Consistent with an ER pool that is not sensing sterol excess, the SREBP-responsive arm is at, not below, background (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP +1.28, all near or below the global median of 1.46), i.e. no feedback shut-off of uptake or synthesis. This step rests on absence of suppression and is the weakest link.", "Step 5 (predicted lipid phenotype): Re-esterification and storage transcripts remain available (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), so retained sterol and sphingolipid substrate is predicted to accumulate as cholesteryl ester and as sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide/ganglioside species in APOE4 microglia, sustaining the compensatory TFEB/CLEAR loop as a steady state rather than resolving it.", "Step 6 (heterogeneity of the response): The lysosomal program is not uniformly raised - CTSS, a major microglial cathepsin, is strongly reduced (gene:CTSS -5.57, 0.7th percentile) and NPC2 is at background (gene:NPC2 +1.17) - so the mechanism is a selective hydrolase/acidification response with a specific loss of CTSS, not a global lysosome expansion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/CLEAR acid-hydrolase transcriptional response that is not matched at the mature-enzyme level, making endolysosomal lipid catabolic capacity the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08281948085514898, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09260664118275595, "cosine_similarity": 0.28581748512197414, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_092", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6600809061488673, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08281948085514898, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09260664118275595, "cosine_similarity": 0.28581748512197414, "direction_accuracy": 0.1262135922330097, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6600809061488673, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.52864575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 319}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_052", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |reported log fold change| \u003e= 1 and a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46); pathway claims therefore rest on within-list relative ranking and directional coherence, not on absolute up-regulation, and absence of a gene (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1, FDPS, SCAP) means unreported, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2 and are treated as non-uniquely identified (each spot lists up to six candidate genes), so no protein spot is used as evidence for a named protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal, uptake and sterol-pathway machinery; enzyme activity, cholesterol flux, subcellular localization, SREBP cleavage state and lipid pool sizes were not measured in this dataset.", "The SREBP-2 target signature (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR24, LSS, EBP, ACAT2) is assumed to report low ER-accessible sterol rather than a sterol-independent transcriptional drive (e.g. mTORC1/TFEB or genotype-linked chromatin effects).", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply lipoprotein cholesterol to microglia in both genotypes, so genotype differences reflect microglial handling rather than differing supply; supply was not measured.", "APOE4 protein is assumed to be expressed and secreted in both genotypes with the isogenic difference limited to the APOE allele, as stated in the supplied metadata."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) transcriptionally expand an acidic, hydrolase-rich endolysosomal compartment and a lipoprotein/scavenger uptake arm, while simultaneously maintaining a 'sterol-poor' ER transcriptional output (SREBP-2 target enzymes and LDLR up). The proposed primary bottleneck is the hand-off step that moves internalized cholesterol out of the late endosome/lysosome to the ER-accessible sterol pool; because that step is limiting, sensed ER sterol stays low, sterol import and post-squalene synthesis genes stay induced, and the excess cholesterol arriving in lysosomes is disposed of by esterification/storage and oxysterol formation rather than being sensed as sufficiency. Lysosomal cholesterol load, ER-accessible sterol, SREBP-2 processing, flux and causal direction are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Route-of-delivery discrimination: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with cholesterol that bypasses the lysosome (methyl-beta-cyclodextrin:cholesterol, delivered to the plasma membrane/ER) should suppress the SREBP-2 target set (LDLR, HMGCS1, INSIG1, DHCR24, LSS) and reduce nuclear SREBP-2 at least as strongly in APOE4 as in APOE3, whereas an equal cholesterol dose given as LDL/lipoprotein particles (lysosome-dependent) should suppress that set markedly less in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal suppression by both routes in both genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Egress rescue: relieving the proposed bottleneck with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin or NPC1 over-expression should, in APOE4 microglia only, lower LDLR/HMGCS1/DHCR24/SCARB1 transcripts toward APOE3 levels and reduce filipin-positive LAMP1+ cholesterol; failure to normalise the SREBP-2 target set despite clearing lysosomal cholesterol would falsify the link between the two.", "Pool measurement: APOE4 microglia should show higher unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1/LysoTracker-positive compartments and a higher cholesteryl-ester:free-cholesterol ratio, but lower ER-accessible cholesterol (mCherry-D4H or ALOD4 reporter) and more cleaved nuclear SREBP-2 than APOE3. Equal or higher ER-accessible sterol in APOE4 would weaken the central claim.", "Sensor epistasis: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should, in APOE4 cells, increase free cholesterol reaching the ER and suppress the SREBP-2 target set more than in APOE3; if SOAT1 inhibition leaves the SREBP-2 targets unchanged in both genotypes, the esterification-as-disposal step is not carrying the excess sterol.", "Specificity control: acute v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program in both genotypes but should not by itself normalise the APOE4 SREBP-2 target signature; if TFEB knockdown alone abolishes the sterol-gene difference, the lysosomal biogenesis program, not sterol egress, is the primary driver.", "Flux prediction: pulse-chase with [3H]- or BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester-labelled lipoproteins should show slower appearance of label in the ER/esterified pool per unit internalised label in APOE4; equal hand-off kinetics with equal internalisation would falsify the bottleneck assignment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show strongly increased transcripts for the lipoprotein/lipid uptake and handling arm (SCARB1 +8.22, ABCA7 +2.14, TREM2 +1.28, APOE +1.24, PLTP +1.06; RNA logarithm base as reported), consistent with (inferred) increased scavenger/lipoprotein-particle internalization.", "Measured: the degradative compartment program is coordinately induced above the global up-shift of this selected DE list (v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.53; hydrolases CTSK +7.36, CTSB +5.52, GBA +6.71, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSD +2.86, HEXB +2.17; TFEB +2.38, RAB7A +2.65, PIK3C3 +2.92; acid-hydrolase set permutation p=0.014, broad lysosome set p=0.005). Inferred: an enlarged, more acidic late-endosome/lysosome compartment that receives the internalized lipid cargo.", "Inferred bottleneck: export of unesterified cholesterol from that compartment to the ER (NPC1/NPC2- and membrane-contact-dependent) does not scale with the increased influx. The only measured components of this step move little relative to the list median (NPC2 +1.17, 35th percentile) or downward (OSBPL8 -1.90, 13th percentile), while NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 and ABCA1/ABCG1 were not reported at all.", "Consequence (measured transcriptional readout, inferred activity): the ER continues to signal sterol insufficiency, so SREBP-2-type targets remain induced - SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, HMGCS1 +1.08, LSS +2.27, EBP +1.34, DHCR7 +2.71, DHCR24 +3.69, ACAT2 +2.04 - i.e. import and post-squalene synthesis are turned on at the same time as uptake is high, a combination expected only if sensed ER sterol is low.", "Consequence: cholesterol that does reach the cytosolic/ER face is routed to storage and oxysterol disposal rather than to feedback shut-off - SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, AGPAT2 +6.29, plus CH25H +1.62, CYP27A1 +1.49, HSD3B7 +2.71 - together with a lipogenic SREBP-1 arm (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17) that supplies oleate for ester formation. Ester and droplet pools were not measured.", "Net inferred state: a futile uptake-synthesis-esterification cycle in APOE4 microglia in which sterol mass accumulates in lysosomal/ester compartments while the regulatory ER pool stays depleted, sustaining lysosomal expansion and diverting biosynthetic capacity; this is a candidate driver of the APOE4-specific microglial lipid phenotype but causal direction is not established by these data."], "title": "Lysosome-retained lipoprotein cholesterol keeps the ER sterol-sensing pool low in APOE4 microglia, driving a futile uptake-synthesis-esterification cycle"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24603072037809695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1988807259136896, "cosine_similarity": 0.2849313981342486, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_052", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6401165048543689, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24603072037809695, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1988807259136896, "cosine_similarity": 0.2849313981342486, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6401165048543689, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.54207375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 320}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_099", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook; all RNA statements are kept as relative comparisons against the dataset's own global median (+1.46) rather than absolute fold changes.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, so set-level enrichment is interpreted only against this selected background and could be affected by the selection rule.", "Only six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are supplied; their comparative decrease is assumed to reflect a real mitonuclear transcript imbalance rather than probe capture or ambient-RNA/normalisation artefact of the 10X Flex assay.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes and carriers; no ETC assembly, respiration, metabolite or lipid measurements are supplied, so all flux, localisation and directional statements are inferences.", "Protein spots average 4.8 candidate genes each and 39/92 contain keratins, so no spot is treated as identifying a single protein; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured transcripts may reflect non-cell-autonomous signalling or contaminating astrocyte reads; biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision is unknown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia coordinately raise nuclear-encoded TCA/electron-transport-chain and mitochondrial substrate-carrier transcripts while mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit transcripts are comparatively reduced; the resulting assembly-limited terminal oxidation is the primary bottleneck, so carbon delivered into the matrix is inferred to overflow as citrate/malate through SLC25A1/SLC25A11 into a cytosolic SREBF1-lipogenic and sterol-esterification program (SCD, DHCR24/DHCR7/LSS, ACAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1), producing an APOE4-specific neutral-lipid/esterified-sterol burden rather than a phagocytic-uptake defect. Causality is not established by these data; the directionality is proposed, not demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute inhibition or knockdown of the mitochondrial citrate carrier SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2) or of ACLY in APOE4 microglia should collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of neutral-lipid droplets and esterified sterol while leaving the nuclear-encoded ETC transcript elevation intact; if lipid accumulation is unchanged by blocking citrate export, the overflow-to-lipid arm of the mechanism is wrong.", "Respirometry plus BN-PAGE: APOE4 maximal (FCCP-stimulated) and complex I/IV-linked respiration per mitochondrial mass, and assembled complex I/IV/V holoenzyme levels, should NOT increase in proportion to the nuclear subunit transcript increase; a proportional or greater increase in assembled complexes and maximal respiration would falsify the assembly-limited bottleneck.", "ddPCR/RT-qPCR of mtDNA copy number and MT-ND4/MT-CO2/MT-ATP6 transcripts: APOE4 should show reduced mtDNA-encoded transcript per nuclear ETC transcript; genotype-equal mitonuclear ratios would remove the proposed bottleneck and favour a purely lysosomal or purely SREBF1-transcriptional explanation.", "13C6-glucose and 13C5-glutamine tracing: APOE4 should show increased M+2 enrichment in palmitate, cholesterol and cholesteryl ester with unchanged or reduced fractional 13CO2 release; absence of increased lipid labelling would weaken steps 3-5.", "SCD inhibition (A939572) should abolish the predicted genotype difference in monounsaturated triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-oleate species without normalising the OXPHOS transcript signature; persistence of the lipid difference would indicate a different esterification route.", "Specificity control against the assigned focus: phagocytic uptake assays (pHrodo beads/myelin, synaptosome engulfment) and F-actin/Arp2/3 cup imaging should show no APOE4 deficit large enough to explain the lipid phenotype; a strong uptake defect that is corrected by actin-pathway rescue and simultaneously normalises lipid load would favour an endocytic/cytoskeletal mechanism over this metabolic one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for mitochondrial substrate entry and matrix oxidation far above the strong global upward RNA shift (MPC2, PDP1, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, MDH1, GLUD1), implying increased delivery of pyruvate- and glutamate-derived carbon to the TCA cycle.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred assembly): nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts rise coherently (NDUF*, UQCR*, COX*, ATP5*; n=38, median +2.64 vs global median +1.46, Mann-Whitney z=+3.95) while the six measured mtDNA-encoded subunits are mostly negative (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2). Holoenzyme assembly requires both genomes, so mtDNA-encoded cores are proposed as the limiting component; complex assembly and respiration were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred metabolite state, not measured): with matrix input expanded but terminal oxidation assembly-limited, matrix NADH/acetyl-CoA and citrate are predicted to accumulate rather than being fully oxidised.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): the export/shuttle arm is transcriptionally expanded (SLC25A1 +4.47, SLC25A11 +4.50, MDH1 +8.72, GOT1 +6.43, ACSS2 +2.93), providing cytosolic acetyl-CoA and reducing equivalents for lipid synthesis; ATP-citrate lyase (ACLY) itself is not present in the supplied rows, so this step rests on carrier and shuttle transcripts only.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred activity): a lipogenic/sterol output program is induced above background (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.71, DHCR7 +2.74, LSS +2.28, ACAT2 +2.04, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, LPCAT1 +3.07), converting overflow carbon into monounsaturated fatty acids, sterols and esterified neutral lipid.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred substrate load): concurrently elevated lysosomal hydrolase and acidification transcripts (GAA, GBA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSK, HEXA, CTSD, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, TFEB) supply additional sphingoid, sterol and fatty-acid backbones to the same cytosolic esterification step, so the predicted net phenotype is APOE4-biased neutral-lipid droplet and cholesteryl/ceramide-ester accumulation; no lipid species were measured here."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch caps terminal oxidation in APOE4 microglia and reroutes mitochondrial carbon into SREBF1-driven lipid esterification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34267806373001514, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2792211586206719, "cosine_similarity": 0.2842421671170069, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mean_absolute_error": 0.677210355987055, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34267806373001514, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2792211586206719, "cosine_similarity": 0.2842421671170069, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "mean_absolute_error": 0.677210355987055, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.40586125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 321}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect units are a 'reported log fold change' of unspecified base; we therefore use within-dataset rank percentiles and set-versus-background comparisons rather than absolute fold magnitudes, and we do not convert or rescale the values.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome. Absence of HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, FDFT1, IDI1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, STARD3 and GRAMD1A-C rows is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change. Percentile statements are relative to this selected list only.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for protein capacity; activity, flux, membrane-contact-site localization and lysosomal pH are inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration or counter-evidence.", "No lipid, sterol, oxysterol or cholesteryl-ester measurement is present in the supplied data despite the experiment identifier; every statement about sterol pools is a prediction.", "RNA is attributed to microglia in an astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte contamination or astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply differences between genotypes are not excluded by the supplied metadata, and biological replicate number is stated as not supplied.", "The dataset shows a strong global upward shift (77.1% of rows positive, median +1.46), so 'gene is up' alone carries little information; only rank position relative to that shift is treated as evidence."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an imbalance within sterol handling rather than by a uniform lipid-program shift: transcripts for lipoprotein-sterol capture (SCARB1) and for the TFEB-type lysosomal degradative apparatus (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, v-ATPase subunits, RAB7A) are induced far above the dataset-wide upward shift (median rank percentile ~77), whereas the sterol-egress arm that moves lysosomal cholesterol to the ER and to acceptors (NPC2, OSBPL1A, OSBPL8, APOE, ABCA7, MYLIP) sits at or below the background median (~36th percentile). We propose that this scaling mismatch makes lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer rate-limiting, so sterol is inferred to be retained in the endolysosomal compartment and diverted into esters, leaving the ER-regulatory sterol pool chronically under-supplied and sustaining late cholesterol-synthesis, esterification and uptake transcripts (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, EBP, ACAT2, SOAT1, LDLR, INSIG1). Causality is not established by these data; the claim is a testable ordering of steps, not a demonstrated cause.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: relieving the proposed egress block should normalize the downstream module without touching the upstream one. Treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or supplying recombinant mannose-6-phosphate-tagged NPC2, should lower the sterol-synthesis/esterification/uptake transcripts (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, SOAT1, LDLR, INSIG1) toward APOE3 levels and reduce filipin-positive LAMP1+ puncta, while leaving the hydrolase/v-ATPase module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) largely unchanged and while producing a smaller effect in APOE3. If cyclodextrin/NPC2 does not lower those transcripts in APOE4, or lowers them equally in APOE3, the lysosomal-egress bottleneck is wrong.", "Imaging prediction: filipin or GRAMD1-based free-cholesterol sensors should show a higher fraction of unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1+ compartments and a lower ER/plasma-membrane accessible fraction in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal subcellular sterol distribution between genotypes would weaken steps 3-4 and would leave the transcript pattern better explained by a generic TFEB/degradative program.", "Sensor-state prediction: SREBP-2 precursor-to-nuclear-fragment ratio should shift toward the cleaved nuclear form in APOE4, and sterol repletion should collapse the DHCR24/DHCR7/LSS/LDLR difference. Unchanged or reduced SREBP-2 cleavage in APOE4 despite these transcripts would falsify step 5, and note that gene:SREBF2 (+1.06, 27.5th percentile) and gene:HMGCS1 (+1.08, 28.3rd percentile) are already only background-level, which is existing counter-evidence to a strong classical SREBP-2 starvation signature.", "Flux prediction: pulse-chase with [3H]- or fluorescent-cholesteryl-ester-loaded lipoproteins should show slower appearance of label in ER-esterified and plasma-membrane pools in APOE4 despite equal or greater initial uptake. Equal or faster lysosome-to-ER transfer kinetics in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck assignment.", "Upstream-dependence prediction: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade should reduce lysosomal sterol load, filipin puncta and the excess hydrolase transcripts selectively in APOE4. No genotype-selective effect of SCARB1 loss would weaken step 1 and would argue the lysosomal expansion is uptake-independent.", "Esterification prediction: the cholesteryl-ester to free-cholesterol ratio should be higher in APOE4, and SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should selectively increase free-cholesterol-dependent lysosomal membrane damage in APOE4. Equal ester ratios or an APOE3-biased response would weaken step 6.", "Specificity control: if the same rank-ordering (degradative module high, egress module low) is reproduced in an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement with matched sequencing depth and replicate structure, the mechanism survives; if the ordering disappears once the global upward shift and selection filter are removed, the mechanism is an artefact of the supplied selected row list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): SCARB1 transcript is the 19th-highest of 2212 selected differential rows (gene:SCARB1, effect +8.22, 99.1th percentile of the discovery effect distribution). We infer increased capacity for selective uptake of astrocyte-derived lipoprotein cholesteryl ester. Uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred compartment size): the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase module is coordinately induced well above the global shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:RAB7A, with gene:TFEB also up; set median +2.64, Mann-Whitney vs all rows p=1.8e-5). We infer an expanded, acidification-competent degradative compartment able to strip sterol from ingested sphingomyelin- and glycolipid-rich cargo. Lysosome number, pH and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, the proposed bottleneck): the lysosomal sterol-egress and transfer proteins are not scaled with the compartment. gene:NPC2 (+1.17, 34.7th percentile), gene:OSBPL1A (+1.03, 25.6th) and gene:OSBPL8 (-1.90, 12.7th) fall in the lower third of the same distribution; the degradative set versus this egress set differs at p=6.8e-5. We infer that transfer of free sterol out of the lysosomal lumen and across ER-endolysosome contacts becomes rate-limiting relative to inflow. Sterol localization was not measured, and NPC1, LIPA, STARD3 and GRAMD1A-C were absent from the supplied rows.", "Step 4 (inferred pool, not observed): as a consequence of steps 1-3 we predict a larger endolysosomal free-sterol pool and a smaller ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool in APOE4. No cholesterol, oxysterol or cholesteryl-ester measurement is supplied in this dataset, so this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, consistent downstream readout): a low ER-sterol setpoint keeps SREBP-responsive late-pathway and uptake transcripts on (gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, with gene:SREBF1 +4.67 and gene:SCD +4.17). SREBP-2 cleavage and nuclear localization were not measured; only transcript abundance was.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred diversion): sterol that does reach the ER is inferred to be esterified and stored rather than returned to regulatory or plasma-membrane pools (gene:SOAT1 +1.25 with adjusted p 1.8e-125, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.72), while oxysterol-generating and acceptor/efflux transcripts rise only to background levels (gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:CYP27A1 +1.49, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:MYLIP +1.28), i.e. the disposal arm does not keep pace with the capture and catabolism arms."], "title": "Lysosomal sterol egress is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: uptake and lysosomal lipid catabolism scale up while NPC2/ORP-dependent export does not"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23624598456596388, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22430064243692732, "cosine_similarity": 0.28368091244354143, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6301941747572816, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23624598456596388, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22430064243692732, "cosine_similarity": 0.28368091244354143, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6301941747572816, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6065585, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 322}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_011", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; every module is therefore judged against the internal background of this list (mean +1.39, 77% up, all |effect|\u003e1), not against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes are unusually large (range -7.9 to +15.5), so only direction and rank within the list are used; absolute fold changes are not interpreted.", "Transcript direction is assumed to track enzyme protein abundance and, less securely, catalytic activity and flux; no enzyme activity, metabolite, flux or lipid measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 3-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.9); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot direction is used only as weak concordance or discordance evidence.", "The 92 spots are globally up-shifted (mean +0.35, 64/92 positive) and the RNA list is globally up-shifted, so normalization or composition differences between genotypes could inflate any 'everything up' module; module-versus-background comparison is assumed to partially control this.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured, so extracellular lipoprotein supply is assumed present and APOE4-astrocyte-derived lipoproteins may contribute; the measured transcripts are assumed to be microglial.", "Single genotype pair, single timepoint (Day 30), replicate number not supplied, so the isogenic contrast is assumed to isolate APOE genotype rather than clone effects."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcript program that lowers glycolytic entry (HK2, HK3, PFKP), raises mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA and respiratory-chain components (MPC2, DLD, OGDH, ACO2, IDH3B, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11 and 38/38 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits) together with citrate export (SLC25A1) and an SREBF1-anchored esterification chain (ACSS2, SCD, GPAT4, AGPAT2, MBOAT1/2, DGAT1, SOAT1, TMEM159/LDAF1), while lipid-acquisition receptors (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, MRC1, ABCA7) and sterol-synthesis transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR24, EBP, INSIG1) are simultaneously elevated. The proposed primary bottleneck is that esterification into neutral lipid (AGPAT2/DGAT1 for acylglycerols, SOAT1 for cholesteryl ester) is the only measured expanded disposal route for this combined de-novo and uptake-derived acyl-CoA/sterol supply: catabolic alternatives are not coordinately raised (ACSL4, ACSL5 down; only ACOX1/HADHA/ETFA up; CPT1A and ATGL not measured) and the strongly induced lysosomal/TFEB hydrolase program is not mirrored by a consistent increase in hydrolase-candidate protein spots. We therefore predict that APOE4 microglia store excess carbon as triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester-rich lipid droplets with a secondary lysosomal lipid burden. Causality is not established by these association-level RNA and 2D-gel spot measurements; no lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: DGAT1 inhibition (e.g., A-922500) or DGAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should remove the majority (\u003e50%) of the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess in neutral-lipid droplet area/TAG mass (LipidTOX/BODIPY, lipidomics) while leaving the OXPHOS/TCA transcript module intact. If APOE4 lipid-droplet excess is unchanged by DGAT1 blockade but abolished by SOAT1 blockade, the acylglycerol arm is wrong and the mechanism must be restated as cholesteryl-ester dominated; if neither blockade changes it, the esterification-sink bottleneck is falsified.", "Stable-isotope tracing: U-13C-glucose and 13C-acetate label should appear at higher rates in TAG and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 than APOE3, with lower 13C-lactate release. Equal or lower de-novo lipid labelling in APOE4 despite the transcript module would weaken Steps 1-3.", "Citrate-export dependence: SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2) or ACSS2 inhibition should reduce de-novo lipogenic label and droplet excess more in APOE4 than APOE3. Genotype-equal sensitivity would weaken Step 2, which is already weak because ACLY was not measured.", "Uptake versus synthesis partition: culturing in lipoprotein-depleted medium should shrink but not abolish the APOE4 droplet excess. Complete abolition would reassign the mechanism to receptor-mediated uptake (SCARB1/CD36/LDLR) alone; unchanged excess would reassign it to de-novo synthesis alone.", "Transcription-factor dependence: SREBF1 knockdown should collapse SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/TMEM159 induction and equalize droplet content between genotypes. Persistence of the esterification module after SREBF1 knockdown would falsify the SREBF1 anchor.", "Bioenergetic test of Step 1: Seahorse should show higher basal and maximal OCR and lower ECAR/OCR ratio in APOE4. Lower OCR with unchanged ECAR in APOE4 would falsify the inferred oxidative shift and reduce the OXPHOS/TCA transcript module to a normalization artifact.", "Lysosomal capacity test: mature cathepsin B/D protein by immunoblot and DQ-BSA/lysosomal lipase activity should not increase in APOE4 in proportion to the CTSB/CTSD/GAA/GBA transcript increases, and LipidSpot-lysosome colocalization should be higher. Proportionally increased hydrolase protein plus faster lipid clearance in APOE4 would weaken Step 6 and argue for a competent, non-bottlenecked lysosome.", "Overall weakening result: if APOE4 and APOE3 microglia show identical neutral-lipid content, identical TAG/CE lipidomic profiles and identical lipogenic flux under mock conditions, the entire mechanism is falsified regardless of the transcript coherence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia lower transcripts for glycolytic committed steps (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08) while raising mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA machinery (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02) and every measured nuclear-encoded respiratory subunit (38/38 up, mean +2.81, permutation p~5e-4 against the list's own background). We infer, but do not measure, a shift of pyruvate carbon away from lactate toward mitochondrial oxidation.", "Step 2 (inferred supply, partly unmeasured): Elevated citrate/malate carriers (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50) plus cytosolic malate-aspartate/redox nodes (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43) and the acetate-to-acetyl-CoA route (gene:ACSS2 +2.93) are inferred to raise cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NADPH available for lipogenesis. ACLY, the canonical citrate-cleaving enzyme, was not measured, so this step is the weakest link in the chain.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): An SREBF1-anchored esterification module is up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:TMEM159 +1.15), consistent with increased monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply, glycerolipid acylation and lipid-droplet nucleation capacity.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux and localization): Lipid acquisition transcripts rise in parallel (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:ABCA7 +2.14) yet sterol-synthesis transcripts remain elevated (gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87) and gene:SOAT1 (+1.25) is up. We infer that incoming sterol is esterified/sequestered rather than reaching the ER regulatory sterol pool, so feedback suppression of synthesis fails; the free-sterol pool itself was not measured.", "Step 5 (bottleneck): Catabolic disposal is not expanded in proportion. Long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11), the oxidative set is weak and mixed (gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:HADHA +2.86 versus the two ACSLs; permutation p~0.78), and CPT1A/PNPLA2 were not measured. Esterification into neutral lipid therefore becomes the committed sink for the excess acyl-CoA and sterol.", "Step 6 (compensation with protein-level discordance): A lysosomal/TFEB-like program is strongly induced (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, 10/10 measured v-ATPase subunits up), which we read as load-driven compensation. Hydrolase-candidate protein spots do not move coherently upward (protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38, protein_spot:064 -1.20 versus protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54), so hydrolytic clearance capacity is inferred not to scale with the load; these spots contain several candidate genes each and do not identify a protein.", "Step 7 (predicted phenotype, unmeasured here): Net result is accumulation of triacylglycerol- and cholesteryl-ester-rich lipid droplets and lysosomal lipid burden in APOE4 microglia, with reduced glycolytic lactate output; no lipid or flux measurement exists in the supplied discovery data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia reroute pyruvate carbon into mitochondrial oxidation and citrate export, making SREBF1-driven neutral-lipid esterification the committed disposal sink for an expanded lipid load"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22688586936454602, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2336133809664291, "cosine_similarity": 0.28269264836479, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6470809061488674, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22688586936454602, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2336133809664291, "cosine_similarity": 0.28269264836479, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6470809061488674, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1859505, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 323}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_022", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong positive skew (median 1.46 reported log units, 77.1% positive, all adjusted p\u003c0.05); we therefore interpret direction by rank within this list rather than by raw sign, and assume that ranking is not itself driven by an expression-level-dependent normalisation artefact.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given; no conversion to a fold-change scale is assumed.", "Absence of a gene (HMGCR, SQLE, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2, STARD3/4, GRAMD1A/B) from the supplied rows is missing data, not evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme/transporter abundance; enzyme activity, organelle pH, lipid pools, sterol localisation and flux are all inferred and were not measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot effects (log2 scale) are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Microglial identity, astrocyte contamination in the co-culture and cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells are assumed not to explain the endolysosomal block; this is untested here.", "No lipid, sterol or lipidomic measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier, so every statement about cholesterol, cholesteryl ester or sphingolipid mass is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) carry a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1), endolysosomal biogenesis/acidification (TFEB, v-ATPase subunits, RAB7A, retromer/sorting-nexin genes) and luminal lipid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK), whereas transcripts for the lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer step (NPC2, OSBPL8, OSBPL1A) and the SREBP-2 sterol-sensing/synthesis arm (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR) are not co-scaled with that program. We hypothesise that the sterol/sphingolipid egress step, not uptake or hydrolysis, is the bottleneck, so APOE4 microglia should retain lipolysed sterol and sphingolipid inside LAMP1+ compartments and route it toward esterified storage rather than toward the ER regulatory pool. Causality is not established by these data; direction is inferred from a rank-based contrast within a selected differential-expression list.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: load APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with fluorescent/deuterated-cholesterol-labelled lipoproteins or acLDL, then measure (a) internalised label, (b) label remaining in LAMP1+ compartments and (c) arrival at the ER (SREBP-2 cleavage suppression, ACAT/SOAT-dependent cholesteryl-ester formation). The mechanism predicts APOE4 shows equal or greater uptake but a longer LAMP1-resident half-life and delayed ER arrival per unit internalised label. If ER delivery kinetics normalised to uptake are indistinguishable between genotypes, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is falsified and a simple increased-flux model is favoured.", "Filipin or D4H-sterol-biosensor imaging should show increased unesterified sterol in LAMP1+ puncta in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3, together with increased BODIPY/neutral-lipid stores. No genotype difference in lysosomal sterol despite the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript difference would weaken the mechanism.", "Epistasis with U18666A (NPC1 inhibition) or NPC2 knockdown: if egress is already limiting in APOE4, the drug should produce a sub-additive (occluding) increase in lysosomal sterol in APOE4 relative to the larger increment seen in APOE3. Fully additive effects in both genotypes would argue against egress being the APOE4-specific bottleneck.", "Relief test: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, NPC2 or OSBPL8/StART-domain overexpression should normalise lysosomal sterol, reduce neutral-lipid storage and dampen the TFEB/v-ATPase/hydrolase transcript module in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the hydrolase module after sterol load is relieved would indicate a sterol-independent, APOE4-intrinsic lysosomal program instead.", "Influx test: SCARB1 knockdown or blocking (e.g. BLT-1) in APOE4 should lower lysosomal sterol load and reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript module; if the module is unchanged after uptake is blocked, the proposed uptake-to-lysosome causal link fails.", "Sensing test: acute sterol depletion (statin plus lipoprotein-deficient serum) should induce SREBP-2 target transcripts (HMGCR, SQLE, LDLR) similarly or more strongly in APOE4 if the ER pool is merely under-supplied; a blunted SREBP-2 response in APOE4 would instead indicate defective sterol sensing and would require replacing the egress-bottleneck step with a sensing-defect step.", "Bioenergetic corollary: the elevated OXPHOS transcript block predicts higher basal and oligomycin-sensitive oxygen consumption in APOE4 that is partially reduced by bafilomycin A1 (v-ATPase inhibition). Equal oxygen consumption between genotypes, or no bafilomycin sensitivity difference, would weaken step 6 without necessarily refuting steps 1-5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SCARB1 RNA is 8.22 reported log units higher in APOE4 (99th percentile of the supplied RNA list). Inferred: increased surface scavenger-receptor-mediated delivery of astrocyte/lipoprotein-derived lipid into the endocytic pathway. Flux is inferred, not measured; ABCA1, ABCG1, LRP1, SORL1, NPC1 and LIPA are absent from the supplied rows.", "Measured: TFEB (2.38), RAB7A (2.65), AP5M1 (9.78), VPS26A (4.86), SNX3 (3.95) and v-ATPase subunit RNAs (ATP6V1H 6.88, ATP6V1A 4.23, ATP6V0C 3.51) are all above the strongly up-shifted background. Inferred: expanded late-endosome/lysosome number, acidification and hydrolase delivery capacity (organelle number, pH and localisation are not measured here).", "Measured: luminal hydrolase RNAs form the most coherent high-tail block (GAA 9.96, CTSK 7.36, GBA 6.71, HEXA 5.68, SMPD1 5.63, CTSB 5.52, CTSD 2.86; set median 4.19 vs background median 1.46, Mann-Whitney p=3.3e-4). Inferred: higher catabolic capacity for internalised glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and lipoprotein cargo, liberating unesterified sterol and ceramide in the lysosomal lumen. Enzyme activity and lipid pools are not measured.", "Measured: genes acting at the lysosome-to-ER sterol/lipid transfer step rank at or below the background shift (NPC2 1.17, 35th percentile; OSBPL1A 1.03, 26th; OSBPL8 -1.90, 13th; set median 1.33, not enriched, p=0.40; hydrolase set vs egress set p=2.4e-4). Inferred bottleneck: egress capacity is not scaled to the increased influx and hydrolysis, making transfer rate-limiting.", "Measured: the SREBP-2 sensing/synthesis arm is flat relative to background (SREBF2 1.06, 28th percentile; HMGCS1 1.08, 28th; LDLR 1.50, 51st; whole set not enriched, p=0.65), while esterification/storage genes sit near background (SOAT1 1.25, DGAT1 1.72). Inferred: the ER regulatory sterol pool is not strongly depleted and liberated sterol is preferentially esterified/stored rather than feeding an ER-sensed pool or a de novo synthesis response.", "Inferred consequence: APOE4 microglia sit in a high-influx, high-hydrolysis, low-egress endolysosomal steady state with sterol/sphingolipid retention and cholesteryl-ester/neutral-lipid storage; the parallel elevation of mitochondrial OXPHOS/TCA subunit transcripts (NDUFA5 7.31, MDH1 8.72, OGDH 8.65; 38-gene set median 2.64, p=1.0e-4) is proposed to reflect the ATP demand of sustained v-ATPase-driven acidification and membrane traffic, not a separate program."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal lipid-catabolic capacity without co-scaling sterol egress, making lysosome-to-ER sterol transfer the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23624598456596388, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20527689568957536, "cosine_similarity": 0.2825592417945142, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_022", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6352297734627832, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23624598456596388, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20527689568957536, "cosine_similarity": 0.2825592417945142, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6352297734627832, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.611143, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 324}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); absent genes (e.g. ASAH1, PSAP, GRN, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPHK1/2, NEU1, NPC1, CPT1A, HMGCR) are unknown, not unchanged, so 'coordinated' means coordinated among represented members against this positive-skewed background.", "The RNA logarithm base is not stated in the workbook; effects are treated as ordinal within this list, and no fold-change arithmetic is performed across modalities (protein spots are log2).", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for degradative and oxidative capacity only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, ceramide/GlcCer/GM2/SM pools, cholesteryl-ester load, autophagic and oxidative flux were not measured and are inferred, not observed.", "TFEB/MITF transcript increases are assumed to reflect, at least in part, increased CLEAR-network output; TFEB nuclear localisation and activity were not measured.", "Protein spots are ambiguous: 92 spots carry a mean of 4.8 candidate genes each and 60/92 include a keratin or actin candidate, so no spot is treated as evidence for an individual protein; spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so uptake-receptor and lipid-handling differences may partly reflect genotype-dependent astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply rather than a microglia-autonomous change.", "Isogenic design is assumed to make the contrast genotype-attributable; a single timepoint (day 30) and unreported replicate number prevent any statement about kinetics or stability of the state.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a directional hypothesis about routing, not a demonstrated flux."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state change in which raised lipid/particle uptake-receptor transcripts and a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal-biogenesis program (v-ATPase subunits plus acid hydrolases, dominated in effect size by the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolases GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLA and SMPD1) raise endolysosomal degradative capacity, while transcripts for retrograde/late-endosomal routing rise and lysosome-exocytosis and M6PR routing transcripts fall, and the resulting lipid catabolites are transcriptionally routed toward esterification/storage and mitochondrial TCA/beta-oxidation with concomitant loss of glycolytic/PPP transcripts. We claim increased catabolic routing and capacity (a coordinated adaptation to higher lipid cargo), not a demonstrated sphingolipid-specific bottleneck; no hydrolase activity, lipid pool, pH or flux was measured, so adequacy of this capacity in APOE4 is unresolved.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE, primary discriminator (measured condition): In mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, per-cell lysosomal hydrolase activities (4-MU GBA, beta-hexosaminidase, acid sphingomyelinase) and LAMP1+/LysoTracker lysosomal volume should be HIGHER in APOE4, with bulk GlcCer/LacCer/GM2/sphingomyelin equal or lower and ceramide equal or higher. If instead hydrolase activity is unchanged or lower while these substrates accumulate, the 'increased catabolic routing' claim is falsified in favour of failed compensation for a lysosomal defect.", "PROSPECTIVE: Pulse-chase of BODIPY-lactosylceramide, NBD-sphingomyelin or labelled myelin/oxLDL should show equal or faster degradation and lower residual undegraded cargo in APOE4; slower clearance with larger residual cargo would weaken steps 1-4.", "PROSPECTIVE perturbation of the proposed driver: TFEB knockdown (or nuclear-translocation block) should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript difference between genotypes (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H) and cause disproportionate glycosphingolipid/cholesteryl-ester accumulation in APOE4; persistence of the APOE4 hydrolase induction after TFEB loss would falsify step 2 as the driver.", "PROSPECTIVE metabolic test of step 6: APOE4 cells should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower extracellular acidification, be more sensitive to etomoxir/CPT1 or ETC inhibition and more tolerant of 2-deoxyglucose than APOE3; the opposite sensitivity pattern would falsify the routing-to-oxidation step.", "PROSPECTIVE challenge test of step 7 (reserve, not ongoing defect): under an added myelin/oxLDL load or GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide), APOE4 should show exaggerated GSL/cholesterol storage, lysosomal swelling and reduced further phagocytic uptake relative to APOE3; equal responses would confine the phenotype to a benign capacity shift and weaken the claim that the sphingolipid-hydrolase arm is load-bearing.", "PROSPECTIVE routing test: given gene:M6PR down and gene:IGF2R up, IGF2R knockdown should preferentially mis-sort newly synthesised hydrolases (increased extracellular CTSD/HEXB activity, reduced intracellular activity) in APOE4 relative to APOE3; no genotype difference would weaken step 4.", "PROSPECTIVE proteomic disambiguation: targeted MS/immunoblot for GBA, HEXB, CTSD (pro- vs mature), CTSB and ATP6V1E1 should show protein increases matching the transcript direction; if mature hydrolase protein is unchanged or reduced (as the significantly decreased hydrolase-containing spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:064/protein_spot:065 would allow), the capacity-increase interpretation is weakened and a post-transcriptional/failed-compensation model is favoured."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid- and particle-uptake/efferocytosis receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:STAB1, gene:COLEC12, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK with ligands gene:GAS6/gene:PROS1, gene:FCGR1A/gene:FCGR3A, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:ANXA1 +4.15), which is predicted (not observed) to increase delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): A CLEAR-type lysosomal biogenesis program is up: gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:MITF (+1.03), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6AP1), lysosomal membrane/solute genes (gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC17A5) and hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SGSH, gene:DNASE2, gene:SUMF1) = higher degradative capacity per cell.", "Step 3 (sphingolipid arm; measured transcripts): The largest-effect hydrolases in that set act on sphingolipids: gene:GBA (+6.71), gene:HEXA (+5.68), gene:SMPD1 (+5.63), gene:GBA2 (+2.63), gene:HEXB (+2.17), gene:GM2A (+2.01), gene:GLA (+1.53), with ceramide-handling/disposal transcripts gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1 up and LacCer synthase gene:B4GALT5 down (-1.88); this predicts increased hydrolysis of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid cargo to ceramide with routing to catabolism rather than re-synthesis of complex glycosphingolipids. This arm is a component of, not a separate driver from, Step 2.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts): Cargo routing genes shift toward late-endosome/lysosome delivery and retromer/retriever-dependent recycling (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ARL8B, gene:EPG5 +3.00, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:AP3D1 +4.42, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:IGF2R +2.02) while gene:M6PR (-1.72), gene:RAB27A (-2.52) and gene:STX17 (-2.06) fall, predicting hydrolase delivery biased to the IGF2R route and reduced lysosome-exocytosis/secretory release of undegraded cargo.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts): Liberated lipid is transcriptionally routed to neutral-lipid esterification/storage and re-synthesis (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:MGLL, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) rather than efflux-only handling.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts): Oxidative disposal capacity rises while glycolytic/PPP capacity falls (up: gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACO2, gene:UQCRC2, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:ATP5F1B; down: gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:NAMPT -2.62, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30), consistent with catabolite disposal by mitochondrial oxidation in the mock condition.", "Step 7 (predicted consequence, not measured here): the same state lowers spare capacity, so an added lipid or lysosomal challenge (myelin/oxLDL load, GBA or v-ATPase inhibition) should expose genotype-dependent sphingolipid/cholesterol storage and lysosomal stress in APOE4 even though the mock condition shows a coherent, apparently productive catabolic state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a cargo-driven endolysosomal catabolic state: coordinated CLEAR-type hydrolase/v-ATPase induction (with a prominent sphingolipid-hydrolase arm) coupled to lipid esterification and mitochondrial oxidative disposal rather than glycolysis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23883063176162167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23505084363539316, "cosine_similarity": 0.28162975235890164, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6338737864077669, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23883063176162167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23505084363539316, "cosine_similarity": 0.28162975235890164, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6338737864077669, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.6559105, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 85}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_029", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect| \u003e= 1 in an unspecified logarithm base; enrichment is judged only against the other supplied rows (background mean +1.39, 77% positive), not against an unbiased transcriptome, so all set statistics are relative and could shift with the full gene universe.", "Elevated hydrolase, V-ATPase and ESCRT/annexin transcripts index a coordinated MiT/TFE-linked program; TFEB activity, nuclear localization, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and membrane permeabilization are inferred and were not measured here.", "2D-gel spots contain several candidate genes; we assume that within the ANXA1/TALDO1 spot train (043-047) ANXA1 is the more plausible contributor because ANXA1 RNA is strongly positive while TALDO1 RNA is negative, but the spots remain non-uniquely identified and keratins/ACTB appear as candidates in most spots.", "APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are isogenic and processed together, so the global positive RNA shift is treated as a normalization/composition/ambient-RNA property of the supplied list rather than as evidence of genuine transcriptome-wide upregulation; replicate number is not supplied.", "Astrocyte co-culture and 10X Flex deconvolution do not selectively contaminate the microglial profile with astrocytic lysosomal transcripts.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 microglia accumulate cholesteryl esters and show lysosomal defects is unverified here (no literature access) and is used only for framing, not as evidence."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a strained degradative endolysosome: transcripts for acid hydrolases, V-ATPase subunits, late-endosomal/retromer sorting factors and an ESCRT-III/annexin membrane-damage-repair module are coordinately elevated far above the already positively shifted background, together with lipid-esterification transcripts, whereas phagocytic-receptor and actin/cytoskeletal transcripts are not enriched above background and include large decreases (MYH9, ACTB). We propose that lipid/membrane cargo delivered to APOE4 endolysosomes destabilizes the limiting membrane, so repair and biogenesis capacity, not cargo recognition or internalization, is the rate-limiting step; this predicts equal or greater cargo uptake but lower degradative flux per lysosome in APOE4. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: after a matched pulse of fluorescent lipid-rich cargo (myelin debris, oxLDL or apoptotic-cell membranes), APOE4 microglia should internalize an equal or greater amount per cell (uptake not limiting) but show lower per-particle degradation (DQ-BSA/pHrodo dequenching rate, slower cargo clearance in chase). If APOE4 instead shows reduced internalization with normal per-particle degradation, the uptake/actomyosin alternative is favoured and this mechanism is weakened.", "APOE4 lysosomes should be more damage-prone: after LLOMe or a lipid load, APOE4 should show more galectin-3-positive LAMP1 puncta and greater recruitment of CHMP4B/ALIX and ANXA1 to those puncta, and slower recovery of lysosomal acidification, than isogenic APOE3. Indistinguishable damage-sensor puncta and repair kinetics would weaken the mechanism.", "Blocking ESCRT-mediated repair (CHMP4B knockdown or dominant-negative VPS4) should disproportionately impair cargo degradation and lysosomal acidification in APOE4 relative to APOE3. Equal sensitization of both genotypes would weaken the claim that repair capacity is the operative bottleneck.", "Reducing the lipid load entering lysosomes (SOAT1/DGAT1 inhibition, cyclodextrin, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-dependent uptake) should lower the elevated hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts and the ANXA1/CHMP4B/LGALS3 module in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Persistence of the elevated program despite reduced lipid load would indicate a substrate-independent, cell-intrinsic transcriptional difference and weaken step 1-3 ordering.", "Because hydrolase transcripts exceed the corresponding 2D-spot behaviour, mature (processed) cathepsin B/D and HEXB protein and enzymatic activity per lysosome in APOE4 should be at most modestly increased and can be decreased, despite large transcript increases. Finding proportionate increases in mature enzyme and activity, with normal cargo clearance, would falsify the proposed flux limitation and instead support a simple, adequately compensated lysosomal expansion.", "Acute genotype-independent test of directionality: forcing the program (TFEB overexpression) in APOE3 should not by itself reproduce the APOE4 damage/repair signature unless lipid cargo is also supplied; if TFEB overexpression alone reproduces the full ANXA1/CHMP4B/LGALS3 module, the proposed substrate-driven damage step is unnecessary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid uptake and esterification/storage enzymes (SCARB1, CD36, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, LPCAT1). INFERRED: increased delivery of cholesterol/sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo into the endocytic route and its diversion into esterified/neutral-lipid stores rather than complete catabolism; no lipid species, lipid droplet or flux measurement is supplied.", "MEASURED (RNA): late-endosomal maturation and sorting transcripts are elevated (RAB7A, DNM2, VPS26A, VPS35L, SNX3, SNX15/16, VPS28, VPS37B). INFERRED: expanded late-endosome/lysosome compartment and increased demand on cargo sorting and receptor recycling; compartment size, position and fusion rates are not measured.", "BOTTLENECK (inferred): the limiting membrane of the cargo-loaded endolysosome becomes the rate-limiting element. MEASURED correlates are the coordinated rise of the damage/repair module ANXA1, ANXA6, CHMP4B, CHMP6, VPS37B/VPS28 (ESCRT-I/III components), LGALS3 (galectin damage sensor), SMPD1 and PRDX2, and the coherent upward shift of the ANXA1-containing 2D-gel spot train (spots 043-046, with spot 045 the largest positive protein effect). Membrane permeabilization, galectin puncta and repair events are inferred, not observed; the spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins.", "MEASURED (RNA): a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal biogenesis signature is elevated (TFEB, MITF, and hydrolases GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, MAN2B1, GLA plus V-ATPase subunits ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1E1/F, ATP6V0D1, ATP6AP1). INFERRED: a substrate- and damage-driven compensatory transcriptional response; TFEB nuclear translocation, lysosomal pH and hydrolase activity are not measured.", "MEASURED (protein spots, ambiguous identity): spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins/HEXB are not uniformly increased (052 and 053 up; 058, 067, 069 down; mean of lysosome-candidate spots +0.09 vs +0.42 for other spots), and CTSS RNA is strongly decreased while M6PR RNA is decreased. INFERRED: hydrolase transcript induction is not matched one-for-one by mature enzyme accumulation in the degradative compartment, consistent with a delivery/processing or turnover limitation downstream of transcription.", "PREDICTED CONSEQUENCE (not measured): net degradative flux per internalized particle is lower in APOE4, cargo residence time is longer, and the biogenesis/repair program is therefore sustained as a feed-forward, non-resolving state at day 30 under mock conditions.", "ALTERNATIVE ARM EVALUATED AND DOWN-WEIGHTED: the assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal focus is only partly supported. Phagocytic receptor transcripts rise (SCARB1, MERTK, TREM2, CD36, MRC1, C1QA/B/C) but not above the global positive shift (permutation p=0.19), and a core actin set is flat (mean -0.22, p=0.99) with large opposing members (ACTB, MYH9, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8 down; ARPC1B/4/5, CFL1, RHOA, ARHGDIA up). We therefore retain reduced actomyosin-dependent engulfment only as a competing hypothesis, discriminated by the predictions below."], "title": "APOE4 iPSC-microglia are bottlenecked at endolysosomal limiting-membrane integrity, not at phagocytic receptor or actin uptake machinery"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2453014806336078, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21249267215333573, "cosine_similarity": 0.2808291629973597, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6812686084142395, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2453014806336078, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.21249267215333573, "cosine_similarity": 0.2808291629973597, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6812686084142395, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86994125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 325}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_043", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all pathway statements are made relative to the strongly positive median of this list itself (median reported log fold change approximately +1.46), not relative to an unbiased genome background.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spot effects are log2 and are not on the same scale as the RNA column.", "Each 2D protein spot has several candidate genes, so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spot-level statements are treated as weak, ambiguity-limited evidence about proteoform distribution, not as protein quantification.", "Transcription-factor activity, hydrolase enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, lipid/sterol pool sizes, protein localisation and lysosomal membrane integrity were not measured in these data and are inferred.", "The transcript-versus-spot discordance reflects biology (delivery, maturation or turnover of lysosomal proteins) rather than purely technical differences between 10X Flex pseudobulk and 2D gel quantification.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal may derive from non-microglial RNA or ambient contamination; the mechanism assumes the lysosomal signature is microglia-intrinsic.", "Mock treatment is assumed to represent an unstimulated steady state rather than a latent stress response induced by the culture protocol."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells show a coordinate MiT/TFE (TFEB, TFEC, MITF) CLEAR-network transcript increase together with lysosomal-stress markers (GPNMB, LGALS3, ACP5) and an ER-sterol-deficiency transcriptional signature (SREBF1/2, LDLR, DHCR24, LSS, DHCR7, HMGCS1, INSIG1), while 2D protein spots containing cathepsins and V-ATPase V1 subunits are flat or reduced. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is mature luminal hydrolytic/acidification capacity per unit cargo, which fails to scale with the transcriptional response, so cargo residence time in the endolysosome is prolonged and cargo-derived sterol is not delivered to the ER; the transcriptional program is a compensatory readout of this shortfall rather than evidence of achieved extra capacity. Causal direction is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Functional capacity assay: in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, per-cell mature cathepsin B/D activity (BODIPY-FL-Pepstatin A, Magic Red or fluorogenic substrate) and DQ-BSA dequenching rate will be equal or LOWER in APOE4 despite the higher gene:CTSB and gene:CTSD transcripts. If cathepsin activity per cell scales upward in proportion to transcript, the bottleneck at step 3 is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: TFEB overexpression or Torin-1-mediated MiT/TFE activation will further raise CLEAR transcripts but will NOT normalise APOE4 cargo clearance (pulse-chase degradation of labelled myelin, AcLDL or synaptosomes), whereas directly restoring luminal capacity - acidic (poly-lactide/PLGA) nanoparticles that lower lysosomal pH, or endocytic delivery of active recombinant hydrolase - WILL normalise clearance. Full rescue by TFEB overexpression alone would show transcript supply was limiting and would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Lysosomal pH measured ratiometrically (LysoSensor or pHrodo/dextran) will be equal or HIGHER (less acidic) in APOE4 despite elevated gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A and gene:ATP6V0C transcripts. Significantly more acidic APOE4 lysosomes would weaken the acidification component of step 3.", "Cargo residence time: after a pulse of fluorescent cargo, APOE4 microglia will retain a larger undegraded intracellular fraction at 6-24 h chase and will show more filipin-positive free sterol overlapping LAMP1-positive compartments. Faster clearance in APOE4 would falsify the core claim.", "Sterol-egress test: methyl-beta-cyclodextrin, which bypasses lysosomal sterol export, will suppress the SREBP-2 target signature (gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2) selectively in APOE4. Failure to suppress would argue the SREBP signature is not caused by lysosomal sterol trapping and would weaken step 4.", "Proteoform test: immunoblot will show that the ratio of mature single-chain/heavy-chain cathepsin D to pro-cathepsin D, and of assembled V1-V0 V-ATPase to free V1 subunits, is NOT increased in APOE4, consistent with the divergent directions of cathepsin-D-containing spots (protein_spot:053 up, protein_spot:069 down). A proportional increase in mature enzyme would falsify step 3.", "Specificity control: the CLEAR transcript program and GPNMB/LGALS3/ACP5 induction will persist in APOE4 microglia cultured without astrocytes and in monoculture-purified microglia, showing it is cell-intrinsic. If it disappears without astrocytes, the co-culture confound explanation is favoured over the proposed mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured transcripts; inferred flux). APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/debris uptake and handling machinery (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:CD163, gene:CLEC7A, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "STEP 2 (measured transcripts; inferred transcription-factor activity). MiT/TFE family transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF) alongside a coordinate CLEAR-like transcript set (hydrolases gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:SMPD1, gene:DPP7, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DNASE2; membrane/ion machinery gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:CLN3, gene:CLCN7, gene:SLC38A7, gene:NPC2; V-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1). Transcription-factor activity itself is inferred, not measured.", "STEP 3 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK; measured spot abundance, inferred enzymatic capacity). The transcript program is not accompanied by a matched increase in the corresponding protein spots: spots whose candidate-gene lists include cathepsins or V-ATPase V1 subunits are flat or decreased (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:068, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:090, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:075), while other cathepsin-D-containing spots move upward (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:060, protein_spot:027), a pattern expected from proteoform redistribution rather than net accumulation. We therefore hypothesise that mature, correctly delivered luminal hydrolase and proton-pump capacity per unit cargo is the rate-limiting step. Spot identities are ambiguous (multiple candidate genes per spot) and enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH and protein localisation were not measured.", "STEP 4 (inferred consequence). Prolonged cargo residence time reduces hand-off of cargo-derived sterol from the late endosome/lysosome to the ER, so ER sterol sensing reports deficiency: gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP and gene:INSIG1 transcripts are all elevated, with alternative sterol-disposal routes gene:CYP27A1, gene:CH25H and re-esterification gene:SOAT1 also elevated.", "STEP 5 (inferred feed-forward). Elevated gene:LDLR plus elevated scavenger-receptor transcripts predict further cargo influx into a compartment whose degradative capacity has not scaled, reinforcing overload; the fusion/delivery arm is not co-upregulated (gene:STX17 is decreased; the UVRAG-containing protein_spot:011 is decreased), so cargo transfer into degradative compartments is not obviously accelerated.", "STEP 6 (measured transcripts; state readout). The resulting steady state is a lysosomal-stress / lipid-laden microglial phenotype: gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:LGALS1, gene:ACP5, gene:ITGAX, gene:FABP5 and gene:CLEC7A transcripts are elevated. These are markers of the state, not proof of impaired flux."], "title": "A MiT/TFE-driven lysosomal transcriptional program that is not matched at the hydrolase/V-ATPase protein level leaves APOE4 microglia with endolysosomal cargo-processing insufficiency and sterol trapped upstream of the ER"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05869839572224155, "cosine_similarity": 0.2804470107556185, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_043", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6387766990291263, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05869839572224155, "cosine_similarity": 0.2804470107556185, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6387766990291263, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0353055, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 326}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all RNA comparisons here are internal ranks and medians within the same unreported base, not absolute fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no gene has |effect| \u003c 1) with a strong positive bias (77% up, median +1.46); every pathway claim is therefore made relative to that internal background, and absence of a gene from the list means 'not supplied', not 'unchanged'.", "Protein spots carry a median of 5 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial and possibly poor proxy for enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, substrate delivery and lipid flux, none of which were measured.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the extremely small adjusted p-values (many \u003c 1e-100) may reflect cell-level rather than donor/line-level replication and are used only for ranking confidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoproteins; the inferred substrate influx assumes this external lipid source is equal for both genotypes.", "Key efflux and storage genes (ABCA1, ABCG1, NR1H3, LIPA, PLIN2, ASAH1, UGCG) are absent from the supplied list, so the efflux arm of the proposed imbalance is untested here."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinate, above-background induction of endolysosomal acid-hydrolase and lipogenic/sterol transcripts together with the scavenger receptor SCARB1, which we interpret as a compensatory TFEB-associated response to an increased endolysosomal lipid substrate load; we propose that per-lysosome hydrolytic flux (enzyme activity and substrate delivery, neither measured here) fails to scale with that load, so lipid-derived substrate is retained and the cells adopt a scavenger/lipid-handling microglial state rather than an interferon- or NF-kB-driven inflammatory state. Causality is not established by these correlative RNA and protein-spot measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown or pharmacological blockade of SCARB1 (or removal of lipoprotein/astrocyte-conditioned lipid supply) in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal lipid load (LipidSpot/filipin/LysoTracker, mass-spectrometric cholesteryl ester and sphingomyelin) and should blunt the APOE4-specific excess of GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, GAA and CTSB transcripts back toward APOE3 levels; if SCARB1 loss leaves both the lipid load and the hydrolase transcript excess unchanged, the uptake-driven demand step is wrong.", "Enzyme-activity test of the bottleneck: measured GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1 and CTSB catalytic activity per lysosome in APOE4 should increase far less than the corresponding transcript ratios (sub-proportional scaling) while their substrates (glucosylceramide, GM2, sphingomyelin, cholesteryl ester) accumulate; proportional activity gains with no substrate accumulation would falsify the proposed flux bottleneck.", "Rescue test: enhancing lysosomal catabolic flux (TFEB overexpression, mTORC1 inhibition, or recombinant/allosteric enhancement of the limiting hydrolase) should reduce lipid retention and normalize the SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24 lipogenic transcripts selectively in APOE4 and not in APOE3; an equal effect in both genotypes, or no reduction in APOE4 lipid load, weakens the mechanism.", "Counter-mechanism discrimination (interferon/NF-kB rejection test): JAK1/2 or IFNAR1 blockade and IKK/NF-kB inhibition should leave the APOE4 lysosomal-hydrolase and lipogenic transcript signature and the lipid load essentially unchanged; if either blockade normalizes them, an inflammatory/interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "Substrate-shift test: loading APOE3 microglia with myelin or oxidized-lipoprotein substrate should reproduce the APOE4 hydrolase-plus-lipogenic transcript pattern; failure to reproduce it would indicate an APOE4-intrinsic defect not explained by substrate load.", "Negative prediction: unbiased whole-transcriptome profiling of the same comparison should not reveal a coherent type-I interferon module (ISG15, IFIT1/3, MX1, OAS1, STAT1/2, IRF7) above the global shift; if a coordinate ISG module is present, this hypothesis's rejection of the interferon focus is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show markedly higher SCARB1 transcript (gene:SCARB1, +8.22, 99th percentile of the supplied differential list) with LDLR, COLEC12, CD36, MRC1, CD163 and TREM2 also positive; we infer, but did not measure, an increased influx of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): Acid hydrolase transcripts rise coherently and far above the global positive shift of the selected list (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17; set median +5.63 vs +1.46 global, Mann-Whitney p=1.6e-4), alongside gene:TFEB (+2.38) and v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1E1). We read this as a transcriptional demand signal for lysosomal biogenesis, not as evidence of increased enzyme activity.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck, inferred activity/flux): Functional hydrolytic flux per lysosome is proposed to lag behind this transcriptional amplification, because delivery/maturation components move in the opposite direction (gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:IDS -1.56, gene:CTSS -5.57) and because protein-spot data containing cathepsin candidates are split in direction (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down). Enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and substrate levels were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Lipogenic and sterol-handling transcripts remain high rather than being feedback-suppressed (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:ACAT2 +2.04; set median +2.27, p=0.054), consistent with continued monounsaturated-fatty-acid and sterol supply for re-esterification while catabolism is rate-limited.", "Step 5 (inferred state, not directly observed): The combination of higher influx and rate-limited catabolism is predicted to produce retention of sphingolipid and cholesteryl-ester substrate in APOE4 lysosomes; no lipid, lipid-droplet or cholesterol pool was measured in this dataset, so this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 6 (measured abundance): The transcriptional identity that accompanies this state is a scavenger/lipid-handling program among the statistically strongest rows (gene:GPNMB, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:APOE, gene:C1QA, gene:CLEC7A, gene:LGALS3, gene:PLA2G7, gene:SELENOP) rather than a coherent interferon program; only gene:IFNAR1, gene:TMEM173, gene:IFI16 and gene:IRF2 of a large canonical ISG panel appear, and the inflammatory/NF-kB set is statistically indistinguishable from the global shift (median +1.41 vs +1.46, p=0.35)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify lysosomal acid-hydrolase transcripts but the hydrolytic flux step, not hydrolase mRNA, is the bottleneck under increased scavenger-uptake and lipogenic load"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.044215984919688166, "cosine_similarity": 0.27999041218724235, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6494983818770226, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.044215984919688166, "cosine_similarity": 0.27999041218724235, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6494983818770226, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9273825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 327}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_077", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); program directions were judged against that selected-list background (median +1.46), and absent genes (e.g. LIPA, NPC1, PLIN2, ABCA1, CPT1A, ACLY, FASN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes (up to 15.5) are used only as ranks/directions, not as fold-change estimates; protein-spot effects are log2 of coarsely reported fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed here to track, in direction only, the corresponding enzyme/transporter capacity; no enzymatic activity, metabolite pool, lipid mass, lysosomal pH, membrane composition or flux was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each; all candidates are retained and no spot is treated as evidence for a specific protein. The repeated ANXA1/TALDO1/ACTB-containing spot series (protein_spot:041-047) is read as a proteoform train of uncertain identity, and the opposite-direction cathepsin-candidate spots are read as redistribution, not as net hydrolase loss.", "Descriptive program coherence (median-shift permutation against the supplied list) is not a formal enrichment test; genes within a program are not independent, and the endolysosomal and TCA medians are influenced by a few very large effects.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipid/lipoprotein; the uptake-driven step assumes such substrate is available in the mock condition.", "Causality is not established: the direction from APOE4 genotype to lipid routing is inferred from an isogenic comparison of steady-state abundances at a single timepoint."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change in lipid handling: transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein uptake, endolysosomal trafficking, MiT/TFEB-associated lysosomal biogenesis and lysosomal lipid hydrolases are higher, and the products of that catabolism are transcriptionally routed toward re-esterification (glycerolipid/acyl-transfer and cholesteryl-ester enzymes) and de novo sterol/desaturated-lipid synthesis supported by mitochondrial-to-cytosolic carbon export (MPC2, ACO2, SLC25A1, MDH1/GOT1, ACSS2), while transcripts for long-chain acyl-CoA activation and peroxisomal/beta-oxidation entry (ACSL4, ACSL5, ABCD1) and for committed glycolysis/oxidative-PPP steps (HK2, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1) are lower. The primary inferred change is altered routing/throughput of lipid carbon into storage and membrane lipid, not an established degradative bottleneck; the assigned membrane/acyl-remodeling program is present but, on its own, is not distinguishable from the selected-list background and is interpreted here as the downstream sink rather than the driver.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective tracing: in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, 13C/D-labelled oleate or lipoprotein-derived lipid should show greater label incorporation into triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and phosphatidylcholine/PE pools with equal or lower label appearance in CO2, acylcarnitines and ketones. If APOE4 instead shows equal or lower esterification label while unhydrolyzed substrate (glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin, free cholesterol) accumulates, the routing mechanism is weakened and a lysosomal degradative bottleneck is favored.", "Prospective activity assay in the same mock condition: bulk lysosomal degradative throughput (DQ-BSA/DQ-lipid dequenching, GBA/HEXB/cathepsin-B activity per cell) should be equal or higher in APOE4 despite the raised hydrolase transcripts. A measured decrease in degradative rate would show the transcript increase is failed compensation rather than increased throughput and would falsify the 'increased-throughput routing' framing.", "Prospective pharmacology: inhibiting the esterification/anabolic arm (DGAT1 or SOAT1 inhibition, or blocking citrate export with an SLC25A1 inhibitor, or ACSS2 inhibition) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content and blunt the SREBF-target transcript elevation preferentially in APOE4; no APOE4-selective effect on droplet content would weaken step 4-5.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not baseline): after a myelin-debris or apoptotic-neuron load, APOE4 should saturate earlier - greater undegraded cargo retention and greater droplet accumulation per unit cargo than APOE3 - while showing no such degradation deficit in the mock state. Equal handling under challenge would remove the reduced-reserve corollary without falsifying steps 1-5.", "Prospective proteoform test: 2D or intact-mass analysis with unambiguous identification should show that the APOE4 shift in cathepsin-candidate and ANXA1/TALDO1-candidate spot trains reflects redistribution among processed/modified forms rather than a net decrease in mature hydrolase protein; a uniform net loss of mature cathepsin B/D protein would support the competing bottleneck model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred uptake): higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein and debris receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C) plus endocytic-trafficking components (gene:AP5M1 +9.8, gene:AP5Z1, gene:DNM2, gene:RAB7A, gene:RAB28, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3) indicate increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal route in APOE4.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred capacity): a MiT/TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis signature (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:MITF, V-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A/1F/0D1/AP1/AP2, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2) accompanies broadly increased lysosomal hydrolase transcripts, with the glyco-/sphingolipid arm most strongly raised (gene:GBA +6.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:NAGLU +5.9, gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK); protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases change in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 up; protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), which is compatible with altered proteoform distribution/processing but does not confirm any single protein.", "Step 3 (inferred flux, not measured): hydrolysis of sphingolipid, glycerophospholipid and cholesteryl-ester cargo releases fatty acyl chains, sphingoid bases and sterol, whose intracellular handling/export transcripts are also up (gene:SLC38A7 +7.5, gene:NPC2, gene:SCP2 +6.0).", "Step 4 (routing choice): released acyl carbon is preferentially re-esterified rather than oxidized - acyl-transfer and glycerolipid enzymes are up (gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:MBOAT2 +3.3, gene:MBOAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2, gene:TAZ, gene:SOAT1) together with desaturation/elongation input (gene:SCD +4.2, gene:FADS1) and the sterol-synthesis program (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:ACAT2), while acyl-CoA activation and peroxisomal entry transcripts fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.1, gene:ACSL5 -3.1, gene:ABCD1 -1.6).", "Step 5 (carbon supply): mitochondrial oxidative/anaplerotic and carbon-export transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:GOT1 +6.4, gene:GLUD1, gene:NNT, with milder ETC increases), consistent with cytosolic acetyl-CoA/reducing-equivalent supply (gene:ACSS2 +2.9) for the anabolic arm, whereas oxidative-PPP transcripts are lower (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1).", "Step 6 (consequence in the measured condition): the APOE4 state is a continuously loaded, expanded lysosomal-lipid compartment with engaged membrane-damage/repair transcripts (gene:LGALS3 +2.4, gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:VPS37B +3.9, gene:ANXA1 +4.2, gene:ANXA6) and net storage/membrane-lipid deposition; reduced spare capacity for an added lipid load is predicted only under a future challenge and is not established as an ongoing degradative defect here."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a high-turnover endolysosomal lipid-processing state that routes released lipid carbon into re-esterification and sterol/membrane-lipid synthesis rather than oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3642044825167079, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22860728714267436, "cosine_similarity": 0.27678132067570577, "direction_accuracy": 0.30097087378640774, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6401132686084142, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3642044825167079, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22860728714267436, "cosine_similarity": 0.27678132067570577, "direction_accuracy": 0.30097087378640774, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6401132686084142, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.72500675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 86}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_046", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results in an unspecified logarithm base; only within-list rank comparisons against the global shift (77.1% of rows positive, median +1.46) are used, and RNA magnitudes are never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot values.", "Absence of a gene from the supplied rows (NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, STARD3, HMGCR, SQLE, PLIN2) means unmeasured or unselected, not unchanged; the egress-deficit claim rests only on the four measured egress genes and is therefore provisional.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not treated as identified proteins; no spot is used to assert a specific protein abundance.", "Transcript level is assumed to be a partial proxy for hydrolase and transporter protein capacity; post-transcriptional control, mannose-6-phosphate trafficking and pH-dependent activity could break this link.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some measured transcripts and any lipid readout may be influenced by, or contaminated with, astrocytic material.", "No lipid, flux, imaging or replicate information is supplied; causal direction between the lysosomal, SREBP and lipogenic modules is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by interferon or NF-kB activation (both gene sets sit at or below the global shift of this selected DE list) but by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36) and luminal acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase capacity (GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSK, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C; TFEB up) that is NOT accompanied by a comparable increase in the post-hydrolytic sterol-egress arm (NPC2, APOE, ABCA7, OSBPL1A all at or below the background rank; NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, STARD3 not present in the supplied rows). We hypothesise that export of lipoprotein-derived cholesterol out of the endolysosomal lumen, rather than uptake or hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step; the resulting ER-sensed sterol deficit drives a futile SREBP2 biosynthetic arm (SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, ACAT2 all positive) while SREBF1/SCD-driven monounsaturated fatty-acid supply channels the surplus into esterified neutral-lipid stores. All abundances are RNA (unspecified log base) or ambiguous protein spots; lipid pools, enzyme activities and organelle localisation were not measured and are inferred.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating mock APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or re-expressing NPC1/NPC2) should bypass the proposed egress block and, within 24-48 h, (a) lower lysosomal free-cholesterol staining (filipin/LAMP1 colocalisation) to APOE3 levels, (b) reduce total cholesteryl ester, and (c) DOWN-regulate the SREBP2 arm (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24) while leaving the hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) largely elevated. In contrast, SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should lower cholesteryl ester but INCREASE lysosomal/ER free cholesterol and suppress the SREBP2 arm. Observing the cyclodextrin and SOAT1 arms behave identically, or cyclodextrin failing to normalise the SREBP2 transcripts, weakens the egress-bottleneck mechanism.", "Lipidomic prediction: unperturbed APOE4 microglia will show a higher cholesteryl-ester/free-cholesterol ratio and a higher proportion of 18:1 (monounsaturated) acyl chains in cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol than APOE3, and lysosome-enriched fractions will be enriched in unesterified cholesterol. Equal or lower cholesteryl ester in APOE4, or no MUFA enrichment, would falsify Step 5.", "Enzyme-activity prediction: lysosomal GBA, GAA and HEXA activities and cathepsin B activity in APOE4 lysates should be equal to or higher than APOE3 (consistent with Steps 2). If these activities are instead reduced despite the large transcript increases, the mechanism must be reversed to a primary hydrolase-deficiency model.", "Lipogenic-alternative test: SCD inhibition or SREBF1 knockdown should reduce neutral-lipid droplet mass in APOE4 but should NOT normalise lysosomal free cholesterol or the SREBP2 arm. If SCD inhibition alone normalises lysosomal cholesterol, the primary bottleneck is lipogenic acyl-chain supply, not sterol egress, and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Interferon/inflammation negative control (rejection of the assigned focus): JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib), IFNAR1 blockade or IKK/NF-kB inhibition should not abolish the APOE4-versus-APOE3 lipid difference, and no canonical ISG module (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1-3, OAS1-3, STAT1/2, IRF7, CXCL10, GBP1/2, B2M) should be detectable as coherently induced in APOE4. If an interferon blockade normalises the lipid phenotype, or a genuine ISG module is found on unbiased whole-transcriptome re-measurement, this hypothesis should be replaced by an interferon-driven model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): Elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid receptors, led by SCARB1 (+8.22; rank 0.99 of the selected list) with LDLR and CD36 positive, are inferred to increase delivery of lipoprotein-derived cholesteryl ester and phospholipid into the endolysosomal system. Uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred capacity): A coherent acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase programme is elevated far above the global shift (13 hydrolases, median +5.52, median rank 0.95, permutation p\u003c5e-5; GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52; ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51), with TFEB (+2.38) consistent with a CLEAR-type biogenesis response. This is transcript abundance; hydrolase protein, maturation and enzymatic activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck, inferred): The egress/efflux arm does not co-scale. Every measured member sits at or below the background of this up-shifted list (NPC2 +1.17 rank 0.35, APOE +1.24 rank 0.38, ABCA7 +2.14, OSBPL1A +1.03; median rank 0.37 versus 0.95 for hydrolases, rank-sum AUC 0.88, permutation p=0.012), and NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN and STARD3 are absent from the supplied rows so their status is unknown. We propose that lysosomal-to-ER/plasma-membrane sterol export becomes rate-limiting, so unesterified cholesterol (and sphingolipid catabolites) accumulate in the lysosomal lumen. Lysosomal lipid content and localisation were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred signalling state): ER sterol sensors read this sequestered pool as a deficit, giving a uniformly positive SREBP2 arm (SREBF2 +1.06, INSIG1 +1.87, LDLR +1.50, HMGCS1 +1.08, LSS +2.27, DHCR7 +2.71, DHCR24 +3.69, EBP +1.34, ACAT2 +2.04, ACSS2 +2.93; 10/10 positive). This constitutes a futile feed-forward loop that adds further sterol on top of Step 1 rather than relieving the bottleneck.", "Step 5 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred lipid composition): SREBF1 (+4.67) and SCD (+4.17) are among the strongest lipogenic changes, with DGAT1 (+1.72) and SOAT1 (+1.25) present, so surplus sterol and fatty acid are predicted to be esterified with SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl chains into cytoplasmic cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol droplets. No lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred disposal limit, secondary): Nuclear-encoded oxidative transcripts rise (OGDH +8.61, MDH1 +8.72, MPC2 +8.02, ACO2 +3.54, GLUD1 +3.17, HADHA +2.86) while several mitochondrially encoded subunits fall (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80), a mito-nuclear mismatch that we infer limits oxidative disposal of the excess lipid and biases the cell toward storage. Respiration and beta-oxidation flux were not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolase and lipid-uptake programmes without matched sterol-egress capacity, creating a lysosomal cholesterol-export bottleneck that is diverted into SCD-derived neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2814311560757671, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18911200404077413, "cosine_similarity": 0.2766820338186641, "direction_accuracy": 0.27993527508090615, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_046", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6255728155339806, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2814311560757671, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18911200404077413, "cosine_similarity": 0.2766820338186641, "direction_accuracy": 0.27993527508090615, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6255728155339806, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.27896325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 328}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_058", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect| \u003e= 1 and a strong global positive shift (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base); set-level claims are therefore made relative to this shifted background, not to zero.", "Protein spots are mixtures with multiple candidate genes; the grouping of 'lysosomal-candidate' spots is a probabilistic label, and the transcript-protein discordance could arise from spot misassignment, isoform/charge shifts of pro- versus mature hydrolases, or a different sample preparation than the RNA measurement.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein synthesis rate; enzyme activity, luminal pH, cargo flux, lipid pools and TFEB localization were not measured and are inferred.", "Key sphingolipid genes (SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, ASAH1, GALC, PSAP, GRN, NPC1, MCOLN1) are absent from the supplied rows; their absence is treated as unmeasured, not as unchanged.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous or ambient-RNA contributions rather than microglia-intrinsic regulation.", "Background pathway knowledge used to group genes (CLEAR network, M6P routing, SREBP targets) is unverified literature recall, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a broad, coordinated transcriptional expansion of lysosomal acid hydrolases (including the glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolases GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, SMPD1 with the cofactor genes GM2A and SUMF1) and v-ATPase subunits together with TFEB/MITF/RRAGD transcripts, yet 2D-gel protein spots whose candidate constituents are lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are, as a group, not increased relative to other spots. We propose that the rate-limiting step is the supply of mature, correctly delivered luminal hydrolase and proton-pump protein per unit of endolysosomal lipid cargo, so hydrolytic capacity fails to scale with an APOE4-elevated lipid/lipoprotein load; the persisting undegraded luminal cargo keeps the CLEAR-like transcriptional program switched on. Sphingolipid catabolic transcripts rise as part of this general lysosomal program rather than as a selective sphingolipid signature, and de novo sphingolipid synthesis genes are not measured or not shifted, so a synthesis-driven sphingolipid mechanism is rejected. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, activity, localization and directionality statements are inferences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: supplying mature hydrolase protein directly (M6P-dependent uptake of recombinant GBA/HEXA/CTSD, or forced GNPTAB/IGF2R-dependent routing) should lower endolysosomal lipid/cargo load and dampen the CLEAR-like transcripts (TFEB targets, v-ATPase, hydrolases) in APOE4, whereas TFEB overexpression alone, which raises the same transcripts further, should not reduce cargo load. If TFEB overexpression alone fully clears the load, or enzyme supplementation leaves both load and transcripts unchanged, the delivery-bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Enzyme activity per mg protein for GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1 and CTSD in APOE4 should increase far less than the corresponding transcript fold changes (predicted below ~1.5-fold despite multi-fold RNA increases). Proportional or greater activity increases would weaken the mechanism.", "Pulse-chase of a fluorescent lipid cargo (e.g., BODIPY-LacCer or labelled oxLDL/myelin) should show delayed degradation and increased LysoTracker-positive area in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3, with the delay in the degradation phase rather than the internalisation phase. Equal degradation kinetics would falsify the capacity-gap step.", "Sphingolipid-focus test: blocking de novo sphingolipid synthesis with myriocin should not normalise the CLEAR-like transcripts or the lipid load, while GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) should exacerbate both. If myriocin corrects the phenotype, a synthesis-driven sphingolipid mechanism is favoured over this hypothesis.", "Sterol test: exogenous cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol should suppress SREBP-target transcripts in both genotypes but should not normalise hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts in APOE4. Normalisation of the lysosomal program by sterol loading would place the bottleneck upstream in sterol sensing instead.", "Proteomic test with unambiguous identification (targeted MS or immunoblot of mature versus precursor CTSD, HEXB, GBA and v-ATPase V1 subunits) should confirm that mature luminal forms are not increased in APOE4 despite elevated transcripts. Clear proportional increases in mature hydrolase protein would remove the central evidence for this hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake receptors and lipid handling genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), which we infer (not measure) increases delivery of sterol- and sphingolipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal lumen.", "A CLEAR-like transcriptional response accompanies this state: gene:TFEB, gene:MITF and the TFEB-target-associated gene:RRAGD are elevated and 40 of 43 detected lysosomal genes are above zero, including hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GM2A, gene:SUMF1) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V0D2). Only transcript abundance is measured; TFEB nuclear localization and mTORC1 activity are inferred, not observed.", "This transcript increase is not mirrored in the protein-spot data: spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases or v-ATPase subunits average near zero, and several such spots are significantly decreased (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:086), while other spots are on average increased. We infer a post-transcriptional bottleneck in synthesis, maturation, or mannose-6-phosphate-dependent routing of hydrolases into the lumen, consistent with decreased gene:M6PR despite increased gene:GNPTG and gene:IGF2R. Spot identity is ambiguous, so this step is an inference about a mixture, not an identified protein pool.", "Because luminal hydrolase and proton-pump protein per unit cargo does not scale with load, the hydrolysis flux for the substrates handled by GBA, HEXA/HEXB with GM2A, GLA and SMPD1, and for bulk protein cargo handled by CTSB/CTSD, remains limiting; undegraded glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin and associated sterol are predicted to accumulate in APOE4 endolysosomes. No lipid pool was measured here.", "Retention of lipid in the lumen is predicted to reduce sterol return to the ER, which is consistent with the simultaneous elevation of sterol-synthesis and SREBP-associated transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1) despite elevated uptake-receptor transcripts; this arm is suggestive only and is not statistically separable from the global upward RNA shift.", "Unmet degradative demand feeds back onto the CLEAR-like program, producing a stable APOE4 state of an expanded but functionally under-equipped endolysosomal system, accompanied by a shifted degradative repertoire (gene:CTSS strongly decreased while the CTSL-candidate spot protein_spot:052 is increased) and altered actin/motor transcripts (gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB decreased) that we infer slows cargo clearance rather than uptake."], "title": "A post-transcriptional lysosomal hydrolase-delivery bottleneck, not de novo sphingolipid synthesis, drives a self-reinforcing CLEAR-like endolysosomal program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04428903485350262, "cosine_similarity": 0.27591334829804887, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6357864077669902, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1258723184285345, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04428903485350262, "cosine_similarity": 0.27591334829804887, "direction_accuracy": 0.19741100323624594, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6357864077669902, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.04060875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 329}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_014", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705 positive / 507 negative, apparently an up-list and a down-list stored as paired workbook columns). The correct null for direction is therefore ~77% positive, not 50/50; program-level claims are judged against that skew.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, PDHA1, CS, CPT1A, MRPL/MRPS, ATF4, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged; absence cannot be used as evidence either way.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified ('reported log fold change') and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are not converted or compared across modalities with the log2 protein spots.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate with, but does not establish, enzyme activity, complex assembly, substrate flux or localisation; every flux statement above is inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (208 candidate genes across 92 spots, dominated by keratin/actin); no spot is treated as confirming an individual protein, and all candidate identities are retained.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels from a probe-based single-cell assay (10X Flex) may be biased by probe design, ambient RNA and QC filtering; the mito-nuclear discordance is therefore treated as a hypothesis-generating observation, not a measured deficit of mtDNA-encoded protein.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes; some measured signal could reflect non-microglial cells or genotype-dependent astrocyte cross-talk rather than cell-autonomous microglial rewiring.", "Coherent direction within a curated program is descriptive coherence under gene co-regulation, not a formal enrichment test with independent genes.", "Predicted reserve deficits (glycolytic burst, spare respiratory capacity) are properties of a future challenge; they are not claimed as ongoing defects in the mock condition."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated cell-state change in carbon routing rather than a single glycolytic block: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase, lipid handling, amino-acid/anaplerotic entry and essentially all represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits, assembly factors, import components and mitochondrial carriers are higher in APOE4, while the committed glucose-phosphorylating and upper-glycolytic/PPP steps (gene:HK2, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) are lower despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3). We propose APOE4 microglia route degradative (lipid/glycoconjugate) and amino-acid-derived carbon into an expanded mitochondrial oxidative program and de-emphasise glucose commitment at hexokinase; the four mtDNA-encoded transcripts that are lower (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4) make the expansion mito-nuclear discordant, so the state is predicted to have reduced glycolytic and respiratory reserve that a future challenge, not the mock condition, would expose. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity and complex assembly were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE stable-isotope tracing in mock-treated isogenic microglia: U-13C-glucose should give a LOWER fractional enrichment of citrate/malate/glutamate m+2 in APOE4 than APOE3, while 13C-glutamine (and 13C-leucine) should give equal or HIGHER enrichment of TCA intermediates in APOE4. If APOE4 instead shows equal or greater glucose-derived TCA labelling, the carbon-routing switch (steps 2-4) is wrong.", "PROSPECTIVE extracellular flux: under mock conditions APOE4 should show lower basal and lower compensatory ECAR (glycolytic rate) with equal or higher basal oxygen consumption than APOE3. Higher ECAR in APOE4 would falsify the low-glucose-commitment claim and favour a compensatory-glycolysis (failing-OXPHOS) model.", "PROSPECTIVE substrate-dependence test: acute lysosomal blockade (bafilomycin A1) or acid-lipase/GBA inhibition should reduce oxygen consumption and 13C-lipid-derived TCA labelling MORE in APOE4 than APOE3; no differential sensitivity would falsify the lysosome/lipid-fed step 1-2.", "PROSPECTIVE glucose-dependence test: 2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown should impair ATP/viability/phagocytic uptake LESS in APOE4 than APOE3 in the mock state. Greater APOE4 sensitivity would show glucose commitment is retained and weaken step 4.", "PROSPECTIVE mito-nuclear test: BN-PAGE/complex activity plus mtDNA copy number and mtDNA-encoded protein (MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) quantification. The mechanism predicts nuclear-subunit protein increase WITHOUT proportional complex IV/V activity increase in APOE4. If assembled complex I/IV/V activity scales with the nuclear transcript increase, step 6 (discordance) is falsified while steps 1-5 could still stand.", "PROSPECTIVE challenge test (reserve, not ongoing defect): on LPS or myelin/synaptosome load, APOE4 should show a blunted glycolytic burst and lower spare respiratory capacity than APOE3 despite the higher mock OXPHOS transcript program. Equal or greater reserve in APOE4 would refute the predicted liability and support successful adaptation with no cost.", "PROSPECTIVE identity test for ambiguous spots: targeted MS or western blot of the up spots protein_spot:043/044/045/046 should assign them to ANXA1 (transcript gene:ANXA1 up) rather than TALDO1 (transcript gene:TALDO1 down). Confirmation of TALDO1 protein increase would contradict the reduced-PPP element of step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases, sphingolipid/glycolipid catabolism and v-ATPase subunits (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:TFEB; 25 of 27 represented members positive), together with lipid uptake/storage/mobilisation transcripts (gene:CD36, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:MGLL, gene:ABHD5, gene:SOAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:APOE).", "Step 2 (inferred flux): this degradative/lipid-handling capacity increases the supply of catabolism-derived acetyl-CoA and fatty-acid/sphingoid carbon (supported but not proven by gene:ACSS2, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:FABP5), providing mitochondrial substrate that does not require glycolysis.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred routing): amino-acid and anaplerotic entry transcripts rise in parallel (gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1, gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:BCAT1, gene:BCAT2, gene:ABAT, gene:GOT1, gene:MDH1, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11), so TCA carbon is predicted to derive increasingly from glutamine/BCAA/GABA and citrate-malate shuttling rather than from glucose-derived pyruvate.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): glucose carbon commitment is selectively de-emphasised - hexokinase and upper-glycolytic/PPP transcripts fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1) while uptake capacity is retained or increased (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:SLC2A8, gene:SLC16A1) and the pyruvate that is formed is biased toward oxidation (gene:PDP1, gene:DLD, gene:PFKM, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1 up).", "Step 5 (measured abundance): the oxidative machinery is transcriptionally expanded - 38 of 38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS structural subunits are positive (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3, gene:SDHB, gene:CYCS) with assembly, import and carrier transcripts (gene:NDUFAF4, gene:COX20, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46) and TCA enzymes (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G) - i.e. increased oxidative capacity, not a demonstrated bottleneck.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, mito-nuclear discordance): the mtDNA-encoded core subunits are not co-increased (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 negative; only gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 positive), and mild mitochondrial-stress/redox/one-carbon markers accompany the state (gene:DDIT3, gene:ATF6, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:NUPR1, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:NNT, gene:SHMT1, gene:SHMT2, gene:PSPH), so holoenzyme stoichiometry - not subunit transcript supply - is predicted to cap realised respiration.", "Step 7 (consequence in the measured condition): the resulting state is a catabolism-fed, oxidative, low-glucose-commitment microglial phenotype with modest activation/phagocytic-receptor transcripts (gene:TREM2, gene:CD74, gene:ITGAX, gene:GPNMB, gene:C1QA, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2); its predicted liability - inability to mount a rapid glycolytic burst or to raise respiration further - is a reserve deficit revealed only by a future challenge, not an established defect under mock."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a catabolism-fed, low-glucose-commitment oxidative state: lysosomal/lipid and amino-acid carbon replaces hexokinase-committed glucose carbon feeding an expanded nuclear-encoded OXPHOS program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25501236938300775, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15443480907887555, "cosine_similarity": 0.27254269204128906, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6195436893203883, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25501236938300775, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15443480907887555, "cosine_similarity": 0.27254269204128906, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6195436893203883, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.913944, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 87}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_088", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adj p\u003c0.049, all |effect|\u003e=1.0) in an unspecified logarithm base; 77.1% of rows are positive, so concordant up-regulation was judged against that background and genes absent from the list (e.g. UGCG, ASAH1, GALC, PSAP, NPC1, SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Increased hydrolase, v-ATPase and TCA/ETC transcripts are assumed to translate into increased protein and enzymatic capacity; no hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, respiration, lipid mass or flux was measured, so all flux and routing statements are inferences.", "No protein spot has a unique identity (2-6 candidates each; mean 4.8); spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction, never as confirmation of an individual protein, and their mixed directions (e.g. protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 down with CTSB/CTSD/HEXB among candidates versus protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 up) are treated as unresolved.", "Primacy of the endolysosomal-sphingolipid arm over the equally coherent nuclear-encoded OXPHOS program cannot be established from these data; the mechanism is a coordinated cell state, and no single gene (including GBA or SMPD1) is claimed as the unique cause.", "Measurements are pseudobulk-like 10X Flex differences in astrocyte co-culture with unstated replicate numbers, so a global normalisation or cell-composition shift could inflate the positive skew and contribute to large-magnitude outliers.", "The mito-nuclear mismatch and B4GALT5 decrease are treated as predictions about reserve under a future challenge, not as evidence of an ongoing defect in the supplied mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated cell-state change in which lipid-rich endocytic cargo is routed into an expanded, acidified endolysosomal compartment whose sphingolipid-degrading arm is the most disproportionately induced module (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:SUMF1: 8/8 positive, median +4.13 versus a 77.1%-positive selected-list background with signed median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.002), while complex glycosphingolipid re-synthesis is not co-induced (gene:B4GALT5 -1.88; UGCG/SGMS not in the supplied list). We propose this represents increased catabolic and biosynthetic-disposal throughput (adaptation), not a demonstrated lysosomal bottleneck: acidification, cargo-routing, neutral-lipid esterification and nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC transcripts all rise in the same cells, whereas mtDNA-encoded subunits do not (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33), predicting a reserve limitation that would only be revealed by a future lipid or bioenergetic challenge. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, sphingolipid mass and flux were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective biochemistry in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show higher acid beta-glucocerebrosidase and acid sphingomyelinase activities and higher HexA/HexB activity per cell than APOE3, with lipidomics showing lower or unchanged glucosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin relative to ceramide (increased throughput). If APOE4 instead accumulate glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin with equal or lower hydrolase activity, the adaptive-throughput mechanism is wrong and a failed-compensation/bottleneck model is favoured.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: partial pharmacological inhibition of GBA (conduritol-B-epoxide) or SMPD1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should raise lysosomal glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin and reduce the APOE4-specific increase in neutral-lipid ester/droplet content and in fatty-acid-driven oxygen consumption, with little effect in APOE3. If neutral-lipid content and respiration are unchanged in APOE4 after this inhibition, the proposed routing link from lysosomal sphingolipid catabolism to esterification and oxidation fails.", "Prospective cargo-handling test: pulse-chase of fluorescently or isotopically labelled myelin or apoE-lipoprotein should show faster label clearance from LAMP1-positive compartments and greater appearance of label in cholesteryl/triacylglycerol ester and oxidative pools in APOE4. Slower clearance with cargo accumulation would refute the increased-throughput reading.", "Prospective challenge test of reserve: despite 44/44 positive nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts, APOE4 microglia should show reduced spare respiratory capacity (FCCP-stimulated OCR) and reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6) relative to nuclear-encoded subunits under lipid or bioenergetic load; equal or higher spare capacity and matched subunit stoichiometry would weaken step 7 while leaving steps 1-6 intact.", "Prospective protein-level resolution: unambiguous immunoblot or targeted MS in the mock condition should show increased CTSB, CTSD, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 protein in APOE4. If resolved measurements instead reproduce the decreases seen in the ambiguous protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065, the inferred expansion of degradative capacity is contradicted at the protein level."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid- and opsonin-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:APOE +1.24; 18/18 represented members positive), which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid cargo to the endolysosomal system (inferred flux, not measured).", "Step 2: Cargo routing and degradative-compartment machinery are concordantly increased (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:VPS37B +3.86, gene:VPS28 +2.36; 18/20 positive) together with a MiT/TFE-type lysosomal program (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:LAMP1 +1.38) and a fully concordant v-ATPase set (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30, plus six more; 10/10 positive), consistent with expanded acidified degradative capacity rather than failed acidification.", "Step 3 (focus module): Within that compartment the sphingolipid-catabolic steps are the highest-magnitude coherent block (gene:SMPD1 +5.63 sphingomyelin-\u003eceramide; gene:GBA +6.71 and gene:GBA2 +2.63 glucosylceramide-\u003eceramide; gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17 with cofactor gene:GM2A +2.01 for ganglioside stepwise degradation; gene:NAGLU +5.91 and gene:SUMF1 +2.01 for co-degraded glycosaminoglycan/sulfatase cargo), so we infer increased conversion of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids toward ceramide/sphingoid and fatty-acid products (inferred, not measured).", "Step 4 (routing asymmetry): Salvage back into complex glycosphingolipids is not matched at the transcript level (gene:B4GALT5 -1.88 for lactosylceramide synthesis; only gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17, gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27, whose module is statistically indistinguishable from the selected-list background, MW p=0.62), while ceramide-exit routes are modestly up (gene:CERK +1.23, gene:SGPL1 +1.09); we therefore infer net routing of sphingolipid carbon out of the membrane-glycosphingolipid pool rather than recycling into it.", "Step 5 (disposal of liberated lipid): Fatty-acid and sterol products are predicted to be buffered by esterification, acyl remodelling and desaturation, matching a fully concordant module (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:SOAT1 +1.25; 11/11 positive), i.e. increased flux into neutral-lipid ester pools (lipid mass and droplets were not measured).", "Step 6 (oxidative arm, parallel/downstream): Nuclear-encoded TCA and electron-transport transcripts rise broadly and are the single largest coherent program (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:CYCS +2.58, 44/44 represented members positive, MW p\u003c1e-4), consistent with expanded capacity to oxidise the carbon released in steps 3-5; this program is broad enough that it could equally be a parallel driver, so it is not claimed as strictly downstream.", "Step 7 (reserve, challenge-revealed only): mtDNA-encoded subunits move oppositely (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; 4/6 negative, binomial p=0.03 against the 77.1% positive background), predicting a mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch that limits spare respiratory capacity under a future lipid or bioenergetic challenge but is not evidence of an ongoing bioenergetic defect in the measured mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-centred sphingolipid-catabolic routing state coupled to lipid esterification and expanded nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3778292655909611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23175700701935595, "cosine_similarity": 0.2715852857070804, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6549190938511327, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3778292655909611, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23175700701935595, "cosine_similarity": 0.2715852857070804, "direction_accuracy": 0.284789644012945, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6549190938511327, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.49635125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 88}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_068", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so all enrichment statements are ranks within this biased list, not genome-wide enrichment; the log base and the 77%-positive global shift are treated as a list-level offset removed by rank-based comparison.", "Transcript changes for hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits and SNARE/exocyst components are assumed to translate into proportional changes in protein and in compartmental activity; no enzyme activity, pH, or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-assigning corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Ceramide, sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, ganglioside and sphingosine-1-phosphate pools are unmeasured in this dataset; their retention is a prediction, not an observation.", "Key nodes of the pathway (ASAH1, GALC, ARSA, NEU1, PSAP, UGCG, SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, SMPD3, SPHK1/2, NPC1, MCOLN1, ABCA1) are absent from the supplied rows, so the synthesis arm and the ceramide-disposal step are untested.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; a fraction of the transcriptional difference could reflect altered microglia-astrocyte interaction or cell-state composition rather than a microglia-intrinsic APOE4 effect.", "Causality is not established by this observational isogenic comparison; direction is asserted as a testable model only."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcriptional shift that raises endolysosomal sphingolipid-hydrolase and acidification capacity (SMPD1, GBA/GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, plus v-ATPase subunits and a TFEB-associated hydrolase program) together with expanded endosome-to-lysosome sorting machinery, while transcripts for exocytic/secretory SNARE-exocyst egress (RAB27A, STX16, STXBP5, VAMP2, EXOC3, EXOC6) are coordinately reduced. We hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck is vesicular export (lysosomal exocytosis and recycling-tubule/secretory egress) rather than hydrolytic capacity, so sphingolipid-derived ceramide and its degradation intermediates are predicted to be retained in the endolysosomal system of APOE4 microglia. Lipid pools, enzyme activities, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: triggering lysosomal exocytosis (e.g. MCOLN1/TRPML1 agonism or a controlled Ca2+ ionophore pulse) should release proportionally more hexosaminidase/beta-glucocerebrosidase activity and surface LAMP1 from APOE4 than APOE3 microglia and should shrink the APOE4 ceramide/hexosylceramide excess; if APOE4 releases the same or more hydrolase at baseline and gains nothing from stimulation, the egress-bottleneck step is refuted.", "Lipidomics of a lysosome-enriched fraction should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for ceramide and hexosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin. Finding accumulated substrate (sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, GM2) with unchanged or lower ceramide would instead support the competing 'reduced hydrolytic flux with compensatory transcriptional upregulation' model and weaken this mechanism.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show APOE4 acid sphingomyelinase, beta-glucocerebrosidase and beta-hexosaminidase activities per cell equal to or above APOE3, matching gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA and gene:HEXA/gene:HEXB. Activities significantly below APOE3 would falsify the 'hydrolase capacity is not limiting' premise.", "Knockdown of RAB27A or STX16 in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy a measurable part of the APOE4 endolysosomal sphingolipid retention and LAMP1-compartment expansion; no phenocopy would weaken step 4.", "Functional inhibition of acid sphingomyelinase (e.g. desipramine) should lower the APOE4 endolysosomal ceramide excess without correcting substrate uptake; if ceramide is unchanged, the SMPD1-driven generation step is wrong.", "Reducing substrate influx by blocking SCARB1/CD36-dependent lipid uptake should reduce both the lysosomal-hydrolase transcript elevation and the lipid retention in APOE4; persistence of the hydrolase program would indicate a load-independent, genotype-intrinsic transcriptional driver."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-membrane uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SCP2 +5.90, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer increases delivery of sphingomyelin- and glycosphingolipid-containing membrane into the endosomal system; no lipid uptake flux was measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Endosomal sorting/maturation genes are coordinately elevated relative to the rest of the supplied list (gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:AP3D1 +4.42, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS35L +3.54, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:ARL8B +1.12; family-level rank test p_up=0.010), consistent with cargo being biased toward late endosome/lysosome rather than fast recycling.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A TFEB-associated acidification and acid-hydrolase program is up (gene:TFEB +2.38; gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51; gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86), with the sphingolipid-degrading arm the highest-ranked sub-block (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53; rank test p_up=0.022 vs all supplied rows, p_up=0.055 vs other lysosomal genes).", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux; the proposed bottleneck): Transcripts for exocytic/secretory egress are coordinately reduced against a strongly up-shifted background (gene:STXBP5 -5.52, gene:STX16 -4.06, gene:EXOC6 -3.83, gene:RAB27A -2.52, gene:EXOC3 -2.13, gene:VAMP2 -1.85; unbiased SNARE/exocyst family rank test p_dn=0.0002), which we infer lowers Ca2+-triggered lysosomal exocytosis and secretory export of lysosomal contents per unit of hydrolase.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid pool): Routes that would consume or re-export ceramide backbone are not expanded: gene:B4GALT5 -1.88 and gene:M6PR -1.72, while the acid-ceramidase and sphingomyelin-resynthesis steps were not measured. We therefore predict, but do not observe, net retention of ceramide/hexosylceramide in APOE4 endolysosomes.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Sequestration of lipid away from ER sensing is offered as the reason a lipogenic/uptake program stays high despite lipid load (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LDLR +1.50), reinforcing substrate delivery in a feed-forward loop."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route sphingolipid-rich membrane into an expanded acid-hydrolase compartment while transcripts for exocytic egress fall, making vesicular export of endolysosomal sphingolipid catabolites the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21042720525791087, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08931614063618129, "cosine_similarity": 0.2711167419490659, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6328187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21042720525791087, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08931614063618129, "cosine_similarity": 0.2711167419490659, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6328187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.68461475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 330}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so absence of a gene means untested/not selected, not unchanged; all enrichment statements are made by rank within this list, not against a whole transcriptome.", "The reported log fold changes use an unspecified logarithm base and are treated only as ordered effect sizes; the strong global positive shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46) is assumed to be at least partly technical/compositional, which is why rank-based rather than sign-based inference is used.", "Increased hydrolase transcript abundance is assumed to increase mature lysosomal enzyme activity and hydrolytic flux; no enzyme activity, protein maturation or lysosomal pH measurement is supplied.", "NPC2 transcript rank is assumed to be an informative proxy for the capacity of the lysosomal sterol-egress step; this is weak, because NPC1 and other egress components were not measured and egress is largely post-transcriptionally and lipid-composition controlled.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each (e.g. spot 53, 55, 12 are only compatible with, not proof of, cathepsin D, cathepsin B and MAN2B1), so protein-level support is treated as ambiguous corroboration only.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; the transcript pool is assumed to be microglial, and astrocyte-derived lipoprotein supply is assumed comparable between the isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 conditions.", "No lipid, sterol, filipin, flux or imaging measurement is supplied; the lysosomal free-cholesterol pool and lipid droplets are inferred and were not observed in this dataset."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lysosomal acid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) and of the lipoprotein receptor SCARB1 is not matched by the sterol-egress arm (NPC2 sits near the bottom third of the same differential list). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is post-hydrolytic export of liberated unesterified cholesterol out of the endolysosome, so that sterol accumulates in the lysosomal lumen, the ER sterol pool is sensed as low, and SREBP2-axis and uptake transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR, INSIG1, SCARB1) remain elevated together with esterification/storage transcripts (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2) - a futile uptake-plus-synthesis loop. Only transcript abundances were measured; the sterol pools, hydrolase activity, egress flux and the causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: acutely bypassing the egress step (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or recombinant NPC2 / NPC1 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should lower filipin-positive lysosomal free cholesterol AND normalise the SREBP2-axis and uptake transcripts (SREBF2, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR, SCARB1) toward APOE3 within hours, while leaving the hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) still elevated. If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal sterol but the SREBP2/SCARB1 signature stays APOE4-high, the proposed egress bottleneck is not the node controlling the sterol sensor and the mechanism is weakened.", "Direct pool measurement: filipin or Nile-red imaging co-stained with LAMP1 should show a higher lysosome-localised unesterified cholesterol fraction and more lipid droplets in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock; equal or lower lysosomal free cholesterol despite higher measured hydrolase activity would falsify the sequestration step.", "Flux versus abundance: enzymatic assays (GBA, HEXA/B, acid sphingomyelinase, cathepsin B/D) should show the transcript increases translated into higher activity per cell in APOE4. If activities are unchanged or lower (e.g. blocked maturation or raised lysosomal pH), step 2 fails and an alternative 'transcriptional compensation for defective hydrolysis' model becomes preferred.", "Sensor test: SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) should raise ER-accessible cholesterol and suppress SREBP2 target transcripts more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3; an equal or larger suppression in APOE3 would argue the sterol sensor is not differentially mis-set by genotype.", "Specificity control: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase transcripts in APOE4 but, if egress rather than hydrolysis is limiting, should not by itself normalise lysosomal cholesterol load or the SREBP2/SCARB1 signature; full normalisation by TFEB knockdown alone would favour a primary CLEAR-program mechanism over the egress-bottleneck mechanism.", "Sterol-only alternative: if the whole-transcriptome (unfiltered) data show HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, CYP51A1 and IDI1 unchanged between genotypes, the SREBP2 arm of this mechanism is not coherently engaged and steps 5-6 must be discarded even if the lysosomal steps survive."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED: APOE4 microglia show markedly higher transcripts for lysosomal luminal hydrolases and for the v-ATPase subunit ATP6V1A and the CLEAR transcription factor TFEB, with GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1 and CTSB in the top 5% of the supplied differential list (reported log fold change 5.5-10.0, unspecified log base).", "INFERRED (activity/flux): the elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts translate into greater luminal hydrolytic flux, liberating more unesterified cholesterol and sphingolipid backbones from internalised lipoprotein and membrane cargo; hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity were not measured here.", "MEASURED, INTERPRETED AS A MISMATCH: within the same up-shifted differential list (median effect +1.46; 77% positive), the sterol-egress-associated transcript NPC2 is only +1.17 (35th percentile), i.e. it is not co-scaled with the hydrolases; NPC1, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied selected list and are therefore unmeasured, not unchanged.", "INFERRED (localization/bottleneck): the NPC2-dependent handoff of free cholesterol to the limiting membrane becomes rate-limiting relative to hydrolytic release, so free sterol and glycosphingolipid catabolites accumulate in the endolysosomal lumen rather than reaching the ER.", "INFERRED (signalling consequence): with ER-accessible sterol kept low, SCAP-SREBP2 processing stays permissive, sustaining SREBF2, HMGCS1, DHCR24, LSS, ACAT2, INSIG1 and LDLR transcripts and high SCARB1-mediated lipoprotein uptake despite an already high total cellular lipid load.", "INFERRED (downstream state): sterol and fatty acid that do reach the ER are diverted into esters and triacylglycerol (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2 transcripts up), producing a lipid-droplet-laden, lysosome-stressed APOE4 microglial state that co-exists with a modest inflammatory/DAM-like transcript shift (CXCL8, CCL2, ITGAX, CLEC7A, NLRP3, TREM2)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal hydrolase capacity faster than lysosomal sterol egress, sequestering cholesterol away from the ER sensor"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24798766754052357, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1950774834223574, "cosine_similarity": 0.27105203217670637, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6420129449838188, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24798766754052357, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1950774834223574, "cosine_similarity": 0.27105203217670637, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6420129449838188, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.661506, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 331}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_073", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; all inferences therefore use within-list rank contrasts between gene sets rather than absolute magnitudes, assuming the global shift and any normalization/compositional artifact affect the compared sets equally.", "Set membership was assigned from unverified background knowledge of lysosomal, trafficking, uptake-receptor and sterol pathways; no external database was consulted.", "Protein spots carry 2-8 candidate genes each (mean 4.8, dominated by keratin/actin contaminants), so spot changes are treated as weak, non-identifying evidence about the named proteins.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a necessary but not sufficient proxy for enzyme protein delivery; activity, luminal pH, fusion competence, cargo flux, lipid localization and lipid droplet content were not measured in these data.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous and the transcript profile may be affected by cross-cell ambient signal in 10X Flex data.", "NPC1, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1, TMEM175, ABCA1, LIPA, PLIN2 and autophagy effectors (SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B) are absent from the supplied list; their status is unknown and is not asserted."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia engage a TFEB/CLEAR-like transcriptional demand response that raises luminal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts far above the global expression shift, while the membrane/trafficking arm that converts those transcripts into functional lysosomal capacity (hydrolase-sorting receptors, LIMP-2/NPC2-type luminal handling, autophagosome-lysosome fusion) is not co-induced and is partly reduced, and lysosome-containing protein spots show no coherent increase. We propose that the rate-limiting bottleneck is delivered/functional endolysosomal capacity rather than cargo uptake, so lipid-rich cargo is retained in late endosomes/lysosomes; the consequent failure of sterol to reach the ER sensing pool keeps SREBP-type lipogenic and esterification transcripts elevated, producing a lipid-storage-biased microglial state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating measurement: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, per-lysosome mature hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXA, GAA, cathepsin B/D activity normalized to LAMP1+ organelle volume) and DQ-BSA or fluorescent-myelin pulse-chase degradation rate will be equal to or lower in APOE4 despite the \u003e2-fold higher hydrolase transcripts, with increased retained neutral-lipid/filipin signal in LAMP1+ compartments. If APOE4 lysosomes instead show proportionally increased activity and equal or faster cargo clearance, the capacity-bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Perturbation 1 (bypass the egress step): treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or restoring lysosomal delivery capacity by SCARB2/LIMP-2 overexpression, will reduce LAMP1-compartment lipid retention and lower the SREBP-type transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, LDLR) and the hydrolase/TFEB transcript excess toward APOE3 levels. If lipid retention is cleared but the hydrolase/CLEAR transcript excess persists unchanged, the proposed demand-feedback loop is weakened.", "Perturbation 2 (test demand vs cause): TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia will collapse the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript excess but will not correct, and should worsen, cargo retention and lipid-droplet load. If TFEB knockdown normalizes lipid load, the induction was a driver rather than a compensatory demand response and this mechanism is wrong.", "Perturbation 3 (uptake is not limiting): reducing cargo uptake (anti-TREM2 blockade or CD36 inhibition) will lower lipid load in both genotypes without abolishing the APOE4-specific hydrolase-versus-trafficking transcript imbalance; if the imbalance disappears with uptake blockade alone, cargo load rather than delivered capacity is the primary bottleneck.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: if pharmacological correction of the nuclear-encoded/mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS imbalance (the strongest competing signal here) normalizes lysosomal cargo clearance and the lipid-storage transcripts, the primary bottleneck is mitochondrial rather than endolysosomal and this hypothesis should be rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mechanism_steps": ["Cargo-uptake capacity is not the differentiating variable: canonical microglial uptake/opsonin receptor transcripts (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA) sit at or below the median of this differential-expression list, i.e. below the global positive shift, whereas luminal hydrolases sit far above it (rank AUC 0.83, z = +3.4 hydrolases vs uptake receptors).", "APOE4 cells engage a lysosomal-demand transcriptional program: gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are elevated together with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1) and a coherent luminal hydrolase block (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK), which ranks in the top ~28% of this list (set z = +2.8 in the high-confidence q\u003c1e-30 subset). Transcript abundance is measured; TFEB nuclear localization and hydrolase activity are inferred, not measured.", "The trafficking/membrane arm needed to convert that program into working capacity is not co-induced: gene:M6PR and gene:STX17 are decreased, and gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1 and gene:ARL8B rank at or below the list median despite the strong global upward shift (hydrolases vs lysosomal membrane/trafficking set, AUC 0.78, z = +2.6).", "Protein-level data do not show the increase predicted by the transcript program: the 17 spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal proteins (e.g. protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 with ATP6V1E1; protein_spot:067 with CTSB/HEXB; protein_spot:069, protein_spot:058 with CTSD/CTSB) have a median log2 change of 0.00 versus +0.485 for all other spots (AUC 0.37, z = -1.7), with both increases (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053) and decreases present. Spot identities are ambiguous, so this is treated as absence of coherent protein-level corroboration, not as proof of decreased enzyme.", "Inferred consequence (not measured here): degradative flux per lysosome and cargo egress do not keep pace with cargo load, so lipid-derived cargo is retained in the late endosome/lysosome compartment and the demand signal is sustained as a feed-forward loop.", "Inferred downstream readout consistent with retained lipid: the ER sterol/lipid sensing pool behaves as depleted, with gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1 and gene:LDLR elevated alongside esterification/handling transcripts gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:ABCA7 and gene:APOE, i.e. simultaneous lipid uptake/synthesis and storage rather than clearance."], "title": "Delivered lysosomal degradative capacity fails to scale with an induced luminal-hydrolase demand program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.021230789151131822, "cosine_similarity": 0.26836667049038104, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_073", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6314045307443367, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1086105675146771, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.021230789151131822, "cosine_similarity": 0.26836667049038104, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6314045307443367, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.91264725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 332}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_090", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list with 77% positive effects and an unspecified logarithm base; program directions were judged against that skewed background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. G6PD, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B, PEX genes, CAT RNA) are treated as unknown, not unchanged.", "Coordinated transcript increases for lysosomal, TCA/ETC and peroxide-removal proteins are assumed to translate into a corresponding increase in the respective protein pools and capacities; no degradative flux, respiration, NADPH/NADP+ ratio or peroxide measurement is supplied, so activity and flux remain inferred.", "Every protein spot carries 2-6 candidate identities; spots are used only for compatibility and contradiction (e.g. protein_spot:017 CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5 up; the protein_spot:043-047 train is equally ANXA1/ACTB/TALDO1) and never as confirmation of an individual protein.", "The mitochondrially biased reductant supply (gene:NNT, gene:ME1 up with gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT down) is assumed to indicate rerouting rather than a hidden compensatory response to an unmeasured cytosolic NADPH deficit.", "Effects reflect the isogenic APOE4/APOE3 genotype comparison in mock-treated day-30 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; the narrowed-reserve component is explicitly a prediction for a future challenge, not an observed baseline defect, and causal direction has not been established.", "The discordance between falling mtDNA-encoded (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB) and rising nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts is assumed not to abolish the inferred increase in oxidative throughput; if it does, the throughput step fails."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 not by a single failed enzyme but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and for the CLEAR-type endolysosomal degradative machinery are jointly higher (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A/H, gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1), and catabolic carbon is routed into mitochondrial oxidation (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, plus nuclear ETC subunits gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS). Thiol-peroxide-removal transcripts rise in proportion (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA), while cytosolic NADPH/NAD-supply transcripts do not (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT lower; gene:NNT and gene:ME1 higher). We therefore claim an adaptive, mitochondrially biased redox configuration with increased oxidative throughput in the measured condition, not an ongoing oxidative-stress bottleneck and not a peroxisomal defect; the predicted consequence is a shifted, narrower reductant reserve that would be revealed only by a future oxidative or lipid-load challenge. All statements refer to measured RNA and 2-D gel spot abundance; flux, activity and localization were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective NADPH-source discrimination: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, pharmacological or genetic inhibition of mitochondrial NADPH supply (NNT knockdown, or ME1 inhibition) should preferentially collapse mitochondrial glutathione/thioredoxin oxidation state (mito-roGFP2-Grx1 / MitoPY1) and viability in APOE4, whereas G6PD inhibition should affect the two genotypes comparably; equal NNT dependence, or greater APOE4 sensitivity to G6PD inhibition, would weaken the rerouting step.", "Prospective flux test of routing versus bottleneck: APOE4 microglia should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with greater etomoxir- or fatty-acid-dependent respiration and faster degradation of a fluorogenic lysosomal lipid/DQ-BSA cargo than APOE3; if APOE4 instead shows unchanged or lower respiration with slower cargo degradation and cargo accumulation, the failed-compensation (lysosomal insufficiency) alternative is favoured and this mechanism is falsified.", "Prospective challenge test of reserve: a peroxide, myelin-lipid or ferroptotic challenge (tert-butyl hydroperoxide, myelin debris load, RSL3) should reveal greater lipid-peroxidation and GSH depletion in APOE4 despite equal or higher baseline PRDX/GPX4 protein; equal challenge sensitivity would indicate no narrowed reserve.", "Prospective TFEB dependence: TFEB knockdown should reduce the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H) and blunt the mitochondrial TCA/beta-oxidation transcript elevation in APOE4; persistence of the mitochondrial program after TFEB knockdown would show the two arms are independent and would remove the causal link in step 3.", "Prospective protein-level resolution: targeted immunoblot or MS of the ambiguous spots should show that APOE4 elevation in protein_spot:043-047 tracks ANXA1 rather than TALDO1 (consistent with gene:TALDO1 -2.32); if instead TALDO1 protein is elevated, the cytosolic-PPP-downshift component of the mechanism is contradicted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises lipid/lipoprotein acquisition and endolysosomal delivery capacity at the transcript level (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:RAB7A, gene:DNM2, gene:MYO1D), increasing the lipid and membrane substrate load reaching lysosomes (load itself inferred, not measured).", "A CLEAR-type lysosomal biogenesis program accompanies this (gene:TFEB up), expanding hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript pools (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:SLC38A7, gene:AP5M1), i.e. increased degradative capacity rather than an inferred jam; gene:CTSS is the notable opposite exception.", "Products of this catabolism are routed into mitochondria: pyruvate/citrate carriers and shuttle enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1), TCA and anaplerotic enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:BCAT1, gene:BCAT2, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB) and fatty-acid oxidation/electron-transfer components (gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:PPARD) are uniformly increased, while committed glycolytic steps are mixed to lower (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3 down), indicating a shift of routing toward oxidative catabolism.", "Increased electron flux through the nuclear-encoded respiratory chain (gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS, gene:COX5B, gene:COX6C, gene:TUFM) is expected to raise mitochondrial superoxide/H2O2 production (inferred, not measured); the matched rise of the peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin/glutathione axis (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA, gene:CCS) represents successful adaptation, since these transcripts are up in proportion to the load rather than a distress signature exceeding the selected-list background.", "Reductant supply for this peroxide-removal capacity is rerouted: mitochondrial NADPH generators are higher (gene:NNT, gene:ME1, with citrate/malate cycling supported by gene:SLC25A1, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) while cytosolic pentose-phosphate and NAD-salvage transcripts are lower (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT); the ambiguous spots containing G6PD/PGD/GSR/TXNRD1 (protein_spot:021, protein_spot:018, protein_spot:019, protein_spot:014) show no significant change, compatible with an unchanged cytosolic arm.", "Consequently, in the mock condition APOE4 microglia sustain lipid catabolism, oxidative ATP production and peroxide clearance with a mitochondria-dependent reductant supply, but their reserve is predicted to be narrower and differently distributed, so an added peroxide, phagocytic-lipid or ferroptotic challenge, or blockade of mitochondrial NADPH, should unmask a deficit that is absent at baseline."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosome-to-mitochondria lipid-catabolic state in which NADPH support for peroxide removal is rerouted from the cytosolic pentose-phosphate arm to mitochondrial sources"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23348595059631502, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15514280090122304, "cosine_similarity": 0.26793771902609625, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6225533980582524, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23348595059631502, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15514280090122304, "cosine_similarity": 0.26793771902609625, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6225533980582524, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90845275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 89}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Increased receptor/opsonin/hydrolase transcript abundance is interpreted as increased pathway readiness/capacity, not as direct proof of increased binding or degradative flux.", "Decreased RAC2, DOCK8, and MYO1F transcripts are interpreted as a plausible constraint on the actin input/closure steps of phagocytosis, based on their unverified, literature-derived roles in myeloid actin signaling; this dataset does not measure GTP-loading, motor activity, or actual engulfment.", "Ambiguous protein spots (multi-candidate) are used only to check directional compatibility with RNA-level actin-program changes, not to confirm which specific protein changed.", "The mock (unchallenged) condition is assumed to show the transcriptional/proteomic state described here; whether an actual engulfment deficit exists would only be revealed under a functional or challenge assay, not established by these steady-state measurements."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, phagocytic pattern-recognition/opsonin receptors, complement, and endo-lysosomal maturation/hydrolase transcripts are coordinately elevated, indicating a shift toward an activated debris/lipid-handling transcriptional state; however, within the actin machinery required to convert receptor engagement into engulfment, RAC2 and its Rho-GEF DOCK8, plus the phagosome-closure motor MYO1F, are selectively reduced while Arp2/3 subunits and coronins are increased, so the upregulated recognition/degradation program is only partially coupled to productive actin-based engulfment rather than reflecting uniformly increased phagocytic throughput.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating: in a live-cell phagocytosis assay (e.g., pHrodo-labeled synaptosomes, myelin debris, or IgG/complement-opsonized beads) comparing APOE4 to APOE3 microglia at the same timepoint, if APOE4 cells show equal or higher actual particle uptake and phagosome closure kinetics than APOE3 despite the RAC2/DOCK8/MYO1F transcript deficits, this would weaken the proposed partial-uncoupling mechanism in favor of a uniformly increased-throughput (successful adaptation) account.", "Prospective: restoring RAC2 (or DOCK8) expression/activity in APOE4 microglia toward APOE3 levels should increase actin polymerization rate and particle engulfment relative to unmodified APOE4 cells, without requiring further change in receptor transcript levels; failure of engulfment to improve after RAC2/DOCK8 restoration would indicate the bottleneck (if any) lies elsewhere, such as in CTSS-dependent lysosomal proteolysis, and would weaken this specific mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with coordinated transcriptional upregulation of phagocytic recognition receptors and opsonins (TREM2, MERTK/GAS6, CD36, FCGR1A/FCGR3A, C1QA/B/C, STAB1, SCARB1, ABCA7, SIRPA), consistent with increased receptor-level readiness to bind lipoprotein/debris/complement-tagged material.", "In parallel, downstream Arp2/3-branching components and actin-severing/turnover factors (ARPC1B, ARPC4, ARPC5, CORO1B, CFL1, RHOA, FLNA) are also increased, consistent with an expanded actin-remodeling parts list.", "The Rho-GTPase RAC2 and its guanine-exchange factor DOCK8, which couple Fc/TREM2/integrin receptor engagement to Arp2/3-driven actin polymerization at the phagocytic cup in myeloid cells, are reduced (RAC2, DOCK8), representing a potential constraint at the receptor-to-actin signal-relay step.", "The unconventional myosin MYO1F, implicated in actin-based phagosome constriction/closure, is also reduced, representing a potential constraint at the mechanical closure step downstream of actin branching.", "Endo-lysosomal maturation genes (RAB7A, SNX3, SNX17, DNM2, CLTB, ITSN1, LAMP1) and several lysosomal hydrolases (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, HEXB, MAN2B1) are increased, indicating that once material is internalized, downstream trafficking/degradative capacity is not obviously limiting (with the exception of CTSS, which is reduced).", "The net predicted cell-state change is a receptor/opsonin- and degradation-primed microglial phenotype whose actual particle engulfment rate is not guaranteed to scale with receptor/opsonin transcript levels, because the RAC2/DOCK8 input and MYO1F closure step of the actin engine are reduced rather than increased.", "This pattern is consistent with either an ongoing partial engulfment constraint or a compensatory transcriptional response to a pre-existing actin-engine deficit; distinguishing these requires a direct functional readout not present in this dataset."], "title": "APOE4 microglia upregulate a phagocytic/opsonin/endo-lysosomal transcriptional program that is incompletely coupled to engulfment because the RAC2-DOCK8 actin-engine input and the MYO1F closure motor are selectively reduced"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.033268101761252444, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16401730068671322, "cosine_similarity": 0.26664242977459374, "direction_accuracy": 0.05663430420711974, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6345533980582524, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.033268101761252444, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16401730068671322, "cosine_similarity": 0.26664242977459374, "direction_accuracy": 0.05663430420711974, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6345533980582524, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.691401, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_040", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global upward shift (77% up, median 1.46); we therefore treat only within-list relative ranks, not raw direction, as informative, and assume this selection is not systematically biased for or against nuclear OXPHOS versus mtDNA-encoded genes.", "The 10X Flex probe-based measurements of MT- transcripts reflect genuine biological transcript abundance rather than probe-panel, ambient-RNA or mitochondrial-fraction QC/normalisation artefacts.", "Transcript changes are assumed to propagate at least partly to protein and to complex assembly; no mitochondrial protein, mtDNA copy number, complex assembly, respiration or ROS measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; spot 017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and spot 077 (candidates KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB) are treated as consistent with, but not evidence of, specific antioxidant protein identity, and the protein series also shows a global positive shift (median +0.48).", "The astrocyte co-culture and any APOE4/APOE3 difference in cell-state composition are assumed not to fully account for the mitonuclear rank pattern."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia raise nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, TCA and mitochondrial import/translation-factor transcripts while transcripts for the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits of complexes I, III, IV and V (MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) are reduced; we hypothesise that the resulting mismatch, not a lack of nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of functional respiratory complexes, producing partially assembled complexes, electron leak and a modest compensatory thiol-peroxidase/lysosomal response rather than increased coupled respiration. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex I, III, IV and V holo-complexes with accumulation of nuclear-subunit-containing sub-assemblies, despite equal or higher total nuclear subunit protein. Finding normal holo-complex levels and stoichiometry, or a proportional increase in holo-complexes, would weaken the mechanism.", "Respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20) should show unchanged or reduced ATP-linked and maximal respiration and increased proton leak in APOE4, with increased MitoSOX/mitochondrial peroxiredoxin oxidation (roGFP2-Orp1); an increase in ATP-linked respiration proportional to the nuclear OXPHOS transcript rise would falsify the bottleneck claim.", "Orthogonal quantification independent of 10X Flex (RT-qPCR/ddPCR or RNAscope for MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6, plus mtDNA copy number by qPCR) should confirm lower mtDNA-encoded core transcripts per mtDNA or lower mtDNA copy number in APOE4; equal mtDNA-encoded transcript levels by an orthogonal assay would remove the core premise, since MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are increased in the same list.", "Rescue test: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (mitochondrially targeted allotopic MT-ATP6/MT-ND4 expression, or restoring mtDNA copy number) should normalise holo-complex assembly, ROS and the lysosomal/v-ATPase transcript program in APOE4 microglia; if the lysosomal and inflammatory program persists unchanged after assembly is restored, the downstream steps are wrong even if the bottleneck exists.", "Specificity test versus the assigned redox/peroxisome focus: a mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ/SkQ1) should lower ROS and partially blunt the stress program without restoring holo-complex assembly, whereas peroxisomal proliferation or catalase overexpression should have little effect; a full rescue by peroxisomal manipulation would favour a peroxisomal rather than mitonuclear mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype drives a coordinated nuclear transcriptional program that raises transcripts for nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (37/37 selected subunits up, median effect 2.64 vs list median 1.46), TCA enzymes (7/7 up) and mitochondrial protein-import/translation factors (TOMM22, TIMM44, TUFM, NDUFAF4); this is measured transcript abundance, not measured protein or assembled-complex abundance.", "Supply of the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits is not matched: within each respiratory complex that contains an mtDNA-encoded member in the supplied rows, that member is the lowest-ranked transcript (MT-ND4 in CI, MT-CYB in CIII, MT-CO2 in CIV, MT-ATP6 in CV; combined rank probability ~2e-4 under random ordering).", "Because these four subunits are obligate catalytic cores, we infer (not measured) that holo-complex assembly, not nuclear subunit availability, becomes the flux-limiting bottleneck, so imported nuclear subunits accumulate as unincorporated sub-assemblies and ATP-linked respiration per unit mitochondrial mass fails to rise in proportion to the transcript program.", "Inferred consequence: incompletely assembled complex I/III intermediates increase univalent electron leak and superoxide production, an activity change that is not directly measured here.", "A limited compensatory antioxidant/repair response is suggested by increased mitochondrial and cytosolic thiol-peroxidase transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, GSS, FTH1) alongside decreased OXR1, although as a set these do not separate from the strong global upward shift of the selected list (p=0.17).", "Persistent bioenergetic insufficiency plus oxidative damage is proposed to drive the coherent TFEB-lysosomal/v-ATPase program (16 lysosomal genes up, p=0.0055) and a low-grade integrated stress/inflammatory signature (DDIT3, EIF2AK3, HIF1A, SLC2A1, CXCL8, NLRP3), i.e. degradative and glycolytic compensation rather than restored oxidative flux."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits respiratory-chain assembly in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20309788428165268, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010814239012273887, "cosine_similarity": 0.26652931889459425, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_040", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6070970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20309788428165268, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010814239012273887, "cosine_similarity": 0.26652931889459425, "direction_accuracy": 0.28640776699029125, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6070970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.86125425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 333}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_095", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, |effect| \u003e= 1.00) on an unspecified logarithm base; direction and rank are used, absolute magnitudes are not, and genes absent from the file (e.g. HSPA5, XBP1, HERPUD1, LAMP2, SQSTM1) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Programs are compared against the observed 77.1%-positive selected-list background (1705/2212 positive); the coherence reported is descriptive resampling, not a formal enrichment test, and co-regulated genes are not independent.", "Increased transcript abundance for v-ATPase subunits and hydrolases is assumed to translate into increased compartment number/enzyme content; this is inferred. Lysosomal pH, hydrolase catalytic activity, cargo degradation rate, autophagic flux, lipid flux and oxygen-consumption rate were not measured.", "Protein-spot identities are ambiguous (mean 4.8 candidates per spot; keratin/actin in most spots). Spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never as confirmation of a named protein; all candidate identities are retained.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at Day 30 in astrocyte co-culture under mock treatment, so astrocyte-derived lipid supply is part of the condition; effects at other timepoints or in monoculture may differ.", "The predicted capacity ceiling from the nuclear/mtDNA-encoded transcript mismatch is a reserve statement about a future challenge, not a claim of an ongoing bioenergetic or degradative defect in the measured mock condition.", "Causality is not established by these association measurements; the direction cargo-load -\u003e TFE-family program -\u003e mitochondrial scaling is a hypothesis about ordering."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state shift: transcripts for the whole endolysosomal degradative chain (TFE-family regulators, v-ATPase subunits, acid hydrolases, mannose-6-phosphate targeting, lysosomal solute carriers, late-endosomal delivery/sorting factors) are raised together with every represented nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation subunit and mitochondrial substrate carriers, indicating an expansion of degradative and oxidative *capacity* (a demand-coupled adaptation), whereas the canonical ER unfolded-protein/ERAD/COPII program is not coordinately induced (chaperone-bearing protein spots flat/non-significant; SEL1L, EDEM1, DERL1, SEC24D, SEC62, GOSR1 decreased). Because only abundance was measured, the realized degradative and respiratory flux is inferred, not observed, and a capacity ceiling is predicted to become visible only under a future lipid/phagocytic challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating: reducing lipid/lipoprotein cargo influx in APOE4 microglia (lipoprotein-depleted medium, or SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should lower the coordinated endolysosomal transcripts (TFEB, ATP6V1H/ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C, GAA, CTSB, HEXA) and LysoTracker/hydrolase-activity signal toward APOE3 levels. If the endolysosomal program persists unchanged when cargo is withdrawn, the demand-coupled ordering in steps 1-2 is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective: TFEB/TFE3 loss-of-function (siRNA or nuclear-translocation blockade) in APOE4 should selectively collapse the v-ATPase/hydrolase/lysosomal-transporter increases without abolishing the SREBF1/SCD sterol-lipid rises. Equal loss of both, or no loss of the lysosomal set, would falsify the TFE-family-associated step.", "Prospective, adaptation vs failed compensation: at baseline (mock), APOE4 microglia should show equal or faster degradation of a fluorescent quenched substrate (DQ-BSA), equal or lower lysosomal pH, and equal or higher basal/maximal oxygen-consumption rate than APOE3. Slower baseline substrate degradation, higher lysosomal pH, or lower basal OCR despite the elevated transcripts would refute 'expanded capacity' and support failed compensation.", "Prospective challenge test of the reserve claim: after myelin or oxLDL loading, APOE4 should show a smaller increment in spare respiratory capacity and earlier lipid/substrate accumulation than APOE3, tracking the mtDNA-encoded transcript lag (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4). Identical challenge responses in both genotypes would remove the predicted ceiling without removing the baseline expansion.", "Prospective test of the rejected ER branch: pharmacological UPR inhibition (PERK or IRE1 inhibitor) in mock APOE4 should not normalise the endolysosomal or nuclear-OXPHOS transcript differences; if it does, an ER-proteostasis mechanism upstream of the lysosomal program would be favoured over this hypothesis.", "Prospective proteomic test: targeted immunoblot/PRM for CTSB, CTSD, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 in APOE4 vs APOE3 should show increased mature protein consistent with transcripts; if instead these proteins are reproducibly decreased (as some ambiguous decreased spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064 would allow), the capacity-expansion interpretation fails and failed compensation becomes the better model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 alters lipid/lipoprotein cargo handling in microglia (inferred, not measured here); consistent selected-list rises in uptake and sterol/neutral-lipid processing transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2) accompany this state, although as a set they are not distinguishable from the 77%-positive selected-list background and therefore are supporting context rather than proof of increased lipid flux.", "Increased endolysosomal cargo load engages TFE-family-associated biogenesis: gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:TFEC (+1.65) and gene:MITF (+1.03) transcripts rise, and CLEAR-type targets rise coordinately (39/41 represented members positive, median +2.01; permutation p_posfrac = 0.002 against the selected-list background).", "Degradative capacity is scaled at every step: acidification (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2 \u2014 10/10 up), hydrolase content (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1), hydrolase targeting/maturation (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R, gene:SUMF1) and lysosomal efflux transport (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC15A3, gene:SLC36A4).", "Cargo delivery to that compartment is also up-scaled rather than blocked (gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2), so the pattern is expansion/re-routing of the degradative route, not loss of a single node.", "The ATP- and substrate-cost of v-ATPase-driven acidification and of catabolite oxidation is matched transcriptionally on the mitochondrial side: all 38 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are increased (gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:SDHB; median +2.64, permutation p \u003c 0.001) together with substrate supply and carriers (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11), while glycolytic transcripts are not coherently raised (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32) \u2014 an oxidative rather than glycolytic bias.", "The mitochondrial-genome arm does not follow the nuclear arm (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; exceptions gene:MT-ND5, gene:MT-ND4L up), so assembled respiratory-chain stoichiometry is predicted to lag the nuclear program; this defines the reserve limit that a future load challenge should expose, and is not evidence of an ongoing energetic failure in the mock condition.", "Consequently, in the measured mock condition APOE4 microglia are predicted to hold larger, more acidified, hydrolase-rich endolysosomes with oxidative ATP support, while an ER unfolded-protein response is not the driver: only scattered ER rows rise (gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79, gene:MANF +2.95, gene:DNAJC10 +4.73, glycosylation gene:DDOST +6.22, gene:MLEC +10.21) with ERAD and export rows falling (gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:SEC24D -1.39, gene:SEC62 -1.50, gene:GOSR1 -3.19) and chaperone-candidate spots unchanged (protein_spot:005, protein_spot:004, protein_spot:001, all non-significant)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a TFE-family-associated endolysosomal expansion state co-scaled with nuclear-encoded oxidative phosphorylation, not an ER unfolded-protein response"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2510984750581545, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1380809082621467, "cosine_similarity": 0.26487837135956455, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6215242718446602, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2510984750581545, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1380809082621467, "cosine_similarity": 0.26487837135956455, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6215242718446602, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.38304825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 90}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_066", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46); enrichment is therefore judged against this selected list, not against an unbiased transcriptome, and the global shift is assumed not to be a pure normalization artefact.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only for ranking, not for absolute fold-change claims.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the capacity (not the activity or flux) of the corresponding lysosomal, sterol-synthesis and oxidative machinery.", "2D protein spots have a median of 5 candidate genes each and heavy keratin/actin content; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are used only as weak corroboration.", "Lysosomal lipid content, unesterified cholesterol distribution, ER-accessible sterol, SREBP2 cleavage, TFEB localization, lysosomal pH and respiration were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred quantities in this model.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from ambient/contaminating non-microglial RNA; the microglial origin of the lipid and lysosomal signal is assumed but not demonstrated here.", "Background pathway membership assignments used to group genes are unverified literature knowledge applied locally, with no database or web retrieval."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 primarily by a bottleneck in export of lipid-derived sterol from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER, not by inflammatory or interferon activation. Transcripts for lipid uptake receptors, acid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, and SREBP-dependent sterol/fatty-acid synthesis are simultaneously higher in APOE4, a combination expected when internalized lipid is retained in the lysosome so that the ER-accessible sterol pool remains low; the coordinate rise in nuclear-encoded TCA/complex I transcripts is proposed as the ATP-supply arm of this compensating degradative state. Measured abundances are transcript and 2D-gel spot levels only; lysosomal lipid content, sterol flux, TFEB localization and respiration were not measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: Treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or restoring NPC1/NPC2 function) should relieve luminal sterol retention and selectively collapse the SREBP arm in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1, LDLR, SCD), while also lowering the hydrolase/v-ATPase set. If cyclodextrin demonstrably removes LAMP1-overlapping unesterified cholesterol yet the SREBP and CLEAR transcript sets remain APOE4-high, the ER-sensing bottleneck in Step 2/4 is wrong and the lipogenic arm is being driven independently.", "Filipin or a genetically encoded lysosomal sterol sensor should show more unesterified cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments of APOE4 than isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal sterol in APOE4 falsifies the primary bottleneck.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 should abolish the coordinate hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H) without abolishing the SREBP arm, and should worsen lysosomal lipid accumulation. If TFEB knockdown leaves the hydrolase set intact, Step 3 is misattributed.", "SOAT1/ACAT inhibition should raise ER-accessible sterol faster in APOE4 than APOE3 and suppress SREBP target transcripts more strongly in APOE4; an equal or smaller APOE4 response weakens the futile storage loop in Step 4.", "Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption in APOE4, and v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) should reduce that excess more in APOE4 than APOE3. Absence of any respiratory difference weakens Step 5 (a non-essential arm) but not the primary bottleneck; absence of both the respiratory difference and the lysosomal sterol difference falsifies the hypothesis as a whole.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL: Direct measurement of ISG protein/transcript output (STAT1 phosphorylation, MX1, IFIT1, ISG15) should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference under mock treatment. A clear constitutive ISG elevation would show the supplied gene list was simply depleted of ISGs and would reopen the interferon explanation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, reported log fold change, base unspecified). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery flux of lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK; inferred, not measured): Export of unesterified sterol and sphingolipid catabolites from the endolysosomal lumen to the ER/plasma membrane is rate-limiting in APOE4. NPC1 is absent from the supplied rows and NPC2 is the weakest member of the lysosomal set (gene:NPC2 +1.17, 35th percentile of the RNA list) while the hydrolases around it are at the 91st-100th percentile, so egress capacity is not scaled with catabolic capacity. Luminal lipid accumulation is a prediction of the model, not an observation.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity/localization): A coherent CLEAR/TFEB-like degradative program is transcriptionally elevated - gene:TFEB +2.38, acid hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, plus acidification subunits gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51 and gene:LAMP1 +1.38. We interpret this as compensation for retained substrate; TFEB nuclear translocation, hydrolase activity and lumenal pH were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred sensing state): Because ER-accessible sterol stays low, SREBP-dependent synthesis and storage transcripts remain high despite the raised lipid load - gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, with esterification/storage routes gene:DGAT1 +1.72 and gene:SOAT1 +1.25. Co-elevation of uptake, synthesis, storage and degradation is the discriminating signature: a cell whose ER sensed the incoming sterol would repress this arm.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Sustained acidification, hydrolase production and lipogenesis raise ATP and acetyl-CoA demand; nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery is coordinately higher (gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54; nuclear OXPHOS set n=38 median +2.64 vs list median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=7.8e-5). Respiratory flux was not measured, and mtDNA-encoded subunits are discordant (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35), so complex assembly stoichiometry may itself be strained.", "Step 6 (negative arm, measured): This state is not an interferon or inflammatory activation state. No canonical ISG module is present in the supplied rows (only gene:IFI16 +1.25), and cytokine/chemokine transcripts sit at the list background (n=11, median +1.59 vs +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.84; gene:CXCL8 +3.11 is offset by decreases elsewhere), so the assigned inflammatory/interferon focus is rejected as a primary mechanism."], "title": "A lysosomal sterol/lipid egress bottleneck, not interferon signaling, distinguishes APOE4 microglia: ER sterol sensing stays 'lipid-hungry' while a TFEB-like degradative program and OXPHOS transcripts are raised"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2341136506295462, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1824200136174565, "cosine_similarity": 0.26311811281854475, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6509093851132686, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2341136506295462, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1824200136174565, "cosine_similarity": 0.26311811281854475, "direction_accuracy": 0.18932038834951456, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6509093851132686, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.31502325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 334}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_066", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all pathway comparisons are made against the internal list-wide distribution (median +1.46, 77% positive), so 'enrichment' means departure from that biased background, not from a whole-transcriptome null.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are therefore not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot values and are not converted.", "Protein spots resolve multiple candidate genes; spots 017 and 077 are treated as consistent-with, not as identified CAT or PRDX2 protein measurements.", "Steady-state RNA abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein pools; no OXPHOS protein, complex-assembly, mtDNA copy number, respiration, ROS, mitophagic flux or lipid measurement is present in these data, so all activity, flux, localization and directionality statements are inferred.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; some transcripts and ambient signal may not be microglia-autonomous, and the global positive RNA shift could partly reflect normalization or cell-composition differences rather than genuine coordinate induction.", "The APOE4-versus-APOE3 comparison is isogenic, but with replicate structure not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be evaluated."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia up-regulate essentially the entire nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (39/39 detected nuclear OXPHOS subunit RNAs, TCA/pyruvate-import and mitochondrial-import RNAs) while mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit RNAs are not co-induced and are predominantly reduced (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2). We hypothesise that supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit availability, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of respiratory complexes, so the enlarged nuclear program yields sub-proportional assembled holoenzyme and ATP-linked respiration, increases matrix electron leak (matching elevated PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/PRDX2 RNA and PRDX2/CAT-containing protein spots), and drives a TFEB-associated lysosomal expansion and a storage-lipid bias. Causality is not established by these data; the interferon/inflammatory focus was tested and rejected as unsupported.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring mtDNA-encoded subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (e.g. TFAM or LRPPRC overexpression, or raising mtDNA copy number) should normalize assembled complex I/IV/V levels on BN-PAGE and restore ATP-linked oxygen consumption toward APOE3 WITHOUT lowering the elevated nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts; if assembled complexes and ATP-linked respiration are unchanged by this manipulation, or if the nuclear transcript elevation collapses with it, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "APOE4 microglia should show a lower ratio of mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript (ddPCR) and lower mtDNA copy number per nucleus than isogenic APOE3; equal or higher ratios would refute step 2.", "Assembled complex I, III, IV and V (BN-PAGE / in-gel activity) and ATP-linked OCR should be equal to or lower in APOE4 despite the higher nuclear subunit RNA; if assembled complex levels scale proportionally with the transcript increase, the mechanism is falsified.", "Mitochondrial matrix peroxide (mito-roGFP2-Orp1) and PRDX3 hyperoxidation should be higher in APOE4; scavenging with MitoQ or mitoTEMPO should reduce the lysosomal markers (LAMP1, CTSD) and neutral-lipid droplet load without normalizing nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. No change in lysosomal or lipid readouts under mitochondrial antioxidant would weaken steps 4-6 while leaving steps 1-3 intact.", "Low-dose complex I inhibition (rotenone) or mtDNA depletion in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 lysosomal-expansion and storage-lipid signature; failure to phenocopy argues the lipid/lysosomal phenotype is driven by an APOE4 mechanism independent of respiratory-chain assembly.", "Interferon-specific control prediction: type I/II interferon pathway output (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, STAT1 phosphorylation, secreted CXCL10) should NOT differ between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock; a clear APOE4 interferon signature at protein level would show the rejected focus mechanism was prematurely discarded."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcript program: every detected nuclear OXPHOS subunit RNA is higher than in APOE3 (39/39 up, median +2.64 vs list-wide median +1.46; complex I 21/21 up), together with TCA/carbon-entry RNAs (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, DLD, GOT1, ACO2) and mitochondrial import RNAs (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM8B). Measured quantity = RNA abundance only.", "The mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits are not co-scaled: MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 RNAs are lower in APOE4 (4/6 mtDNA transcripts down, versus a 77% up-rate for the list as a whole). We infer, but did not measure, a correspondingly limited pool of mtDNA-encoded core subunit protein.", "Inferred bottleneck: because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, the reduced core supply caps holoenzyme assembly, so the surplus nuclear-encoded subunits accumulate as unassembled or sub-assembly intermediates and ATP-linked respiration rises less than the transcript program predicts. Assembly state, respiration and ATP flux were not measured here.", "Inferred consequence: sustained carbon delivery into the matrix (MPC2, OGDH, GLS, GLUD1, SLC25A1/A11 RNAs up) against a constrained electron-transfer capacity increases reduced-CoQ/electron leak and matrix peroxide. Consistent with, but not proof of, this state, mitochondrial and cytosolic peroxide-handling RNAs are elevated (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4) and antioxidant-candidate protein spots are increased (spot 017 candidates CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5; spot 077 candidates including PRDX2).", "Inferred adaptive response: a TFEB-associated lysosomal/autolysosomal program is expanded (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1, and multiple v-ATPase subunit RNAs up), which we interpret as increased demand for turnover of damaged mitochondria and membrane lipid, not as demonstrated mitophagic flux.", "Inferred downstream lipid bias: with oxidative disposal of acetyl-CoA constrained, lipogenic/storage and sphingolipid RNAs are elevated (SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, ACSS2, DHCR24, SMPD1, CERS4), predicting increased neutral-lipid and ceramide storage in APOE4 microglia; lipid content itself is not measured in these data."], "title": "Mito-nuclear OXPHOS stoichiometry imbalance, not interferon signaling, is the primary bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3280471144260237, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08237212535385868, "cosine_similarity": 0.26248840784046906, "direction_accuracy": 0.3446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_066", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6533139158576051, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3280471144260237, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08237212535385868, "cosine_similarity": 0.26248840784046906, "direction_accuracy": 0.3446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6533139158576051, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.71016625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 335}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_058", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive); the reported logarithm base is unspecified, so effect sizes are used only as ranks/directions, not as fold-change magnitudes.", "Absence of SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, SGMS1/2, UGCG, ASAH1 and PSAP from the list means they were not selected, not that they are unchanged; no claim is made about their abundance.", "Transcript increases are assumed to translate into at least partially increased enzyme protein and activity, but activity, localisation and flux were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots containing lysosomal hydrolase candidates move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00), so the protein layer is treated as ambiguous corroboration only.", "The mock APOE4-vs-APOE3 comparison is isogenic, so the RNA differences are assumed to reflect genotype rather than line background; batch, ambient RNA and clone effects cannot be excluded from the supplied metadata (biological replicates not reported).", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured transcripts may reflect microglia-astrocyte interaction rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, imaging or flux measurement is supplied; the lysosomal sphingolipid pool itself is unobserved in this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia by an increased lysosomal sphingolipid degradative transcript module (GBA, GBA2, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLTP, NPC2, SUMF1, SPNS1, ST3GAL5) embedded in a broader TFEB/v-ATPase/cathepsin lysosomal program and elevated lipid-uptake receptor transcripts, while sphingolipid de novo/anabolic enzyme transcripts are not coordinately shifted and several TGN/post-Golgi routing transcripts are reduced; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing the genotypes is hydrolytic clearance of internalised sphingolipid within the endolysosome, so that APOE4 cells carry a higher steady-state lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin load that is only partially compensated by transcriptional induction of the catabolic machinery. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (or of isolated LAMP1 compartments) should show higher hexosylceramide, lactosylceramide/GM3 and sphingomyelin per cell in APOE4, with ceramide/sphingosine not proportionally raised. If APOE4 shows equal or lower glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin, the bottleneck claim fails.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: substrate-reduction with a glucosylceramide synthase (UGCG) inhibitor such as eliglustat/PPMP for 72 h should lower hexosylceramide/GM3 and selectively blunt the APOE4-specific elevation of the sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1) and of the v-ATPase/cathepsin module, collapsing the genotype gap. If the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript differences persist unchanged after effective substrate reduction, the mechanism is weakened and a substrate-independent, generic TFEB/lysosome-biogenesis or interferon-like driver is favoured.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show that GBA, beta-hexosaminidase and acid sphingomyelinase activity per cell rise less in APOE4 than the corresponding transcript ranks imply (capacity lagging transcription). Proportional or supra-proportional activity increases with no substrate accumulation would falsify the lag step.", "Loading APOE3 microglia with sphingolipid-rich cargo (myelin debris or apoptotic-neuron membranes) should reproduce the APOE4 sphingolipid-hydrolase signature in APOE3 cells; failure to reproduce it, while a generic lysosomal stressor does, would argue the signature is not substrate-driven.", "Restoring post-Golgi routing (e.g., STX16 or M6PR/IGF2R re-expression) should increase mature lysosomal hydrolase delivery and reduce glycosphingolipid load in APOE4 without lowering hydrolase transcripts; no change in lipid load would weaken the routing-limitation step while leaving the substrate-load step intact.", "TFEB knockdown should reduce hydrolase transcripts in both genotypes and disproportionately increase glycosphingolipid load in APOE4; an equal effect in both genotypes would argue against a genotype-specific compensatory role."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid and debris uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE). INFERRED: greater delivery flux of sphingolipid-rich membrane and lipoprotein cargo into the endolysosomal system; delivery flux itself was not measured.", "INFERRED bottleneck: the resulting lysosomal sphingolipid substrate load exceeds constitutive hydrolytic capacity, making intralysosomal sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis the rate-limiting step that distinguishes the genotypes.", "MEASURED (RNA): a coherent lysosome-biogenesis response accompanies this state (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA +9.96). INFERRED: TFEB/MiT-family-dependent transcriptional compensation; TFEB nuclear localisation and activity were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): within this program the sphingolipid catabolic arm is uniformly and strongly raised (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLTP, gene:NPC2, gene:SUMF1, gene:SPNS1, gene:SGPL1, gene:ST3GAL5), whereas the anabolic/de novo arm present in the list is only weakly shifted (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:ORMDL2, with gene:B4GALT5 decreased). INFERRED: sphingoid backbone handling is biased toward degradation and salvage re-acylation rather than de novo synthesis; enzyme activities and fluxes were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): several post-Golgi/TGN routing transcripts are decreased (gene:STX16 -4.06, gene:GOSR1 -3.19, gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:STX17 -2.06) alongside increased endosomal transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3). INFERRED: hydrolase sorting and autophagosome-lysosome fusion capacity do not scale with hydrolase transcript induction, so functional degradative capacity lags the transcriptional response; sorting efficiency and localisation were not measured.", "PREDICTED CONSEQUENCE (not measured here): APOE4 microglia accumulate lysosomal hexosylceramide, lactosylceramide/GM3 and sphingomyelin and show enlarged LAMP1 compartments, with sphingoid bases shunted into salvage ceramide (CERS4/CERS6) and S1P disposal (SGPL1) rather than export."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a lysosome-biased sphingolipid catabolic program without matched anabolic or TGN routing support, predicting a glycosphingolipid clearance bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10336742606062843, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03420372672467194, "cosine_similarity": 0.26165871335237795, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6491521035598705, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10336742606062843, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03420372672467194, "cosine_similarity": 0.26165871335237795, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6491521035598705, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.41191675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 336}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_045", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, no |effect| below 1) and 77% of rows are positive, so absolute direction may partly reflect selection or library normalisation; every claim above is therefore based on rank position relative to the internal global median rather than on raw sign or magnitude.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and was preserved; effect sizes are used only for ranking and are not converted to linear fold changes.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein. protein_spot:064/065 (candidates include ATP6V1E1, ANXA1, ARPC1B, GNPDA1, CBR1, PARP1, CAMK2A) and protein_spot:017 (CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but is not equivalent to, subunit protein synthesis; respiratory complex assembly state, membrane potential, electron leak, ROS, ATP flux, mitophagy and lysosomal degradative flux are all unmeasured and inferred.", "Unverified background knowledge is used for the assembly logic (complexes III/IV/V require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores; complex I contains mtDNA-encoded ND subunits) and for the caveat that probe-based 10X Flex chemistry may quantify mtDNA-encoded transcripts unreliably.", "Only six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are present in the supplied list and two of them (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L) are positive, so the mitonuclear contrast rests on a small, possibly non-representative sample.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes and replicate numbers are not supplied; genotype-driven signals cannot be separated from co-culture composition, ambient RNA or batch effects with these data.", "Correlation between APOE4 genotype and these measurements does not establish causality or direction."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated relative elevation of nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, assembly-factor and mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA transcripts that is NOT matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 are relatively lower). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores for complexes III, IV and V, so the expanded nuclear-encoded subunit pool cannot be assembled stoichiometrically; the inferred consequence is partly assembled, electron-leaky respiratory complexes that raise peroxide load (relative up-shift of PRDX2/PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/TXNDC17/MGST2 transcripts) and increase demand on lysosomal degradation of damaged mitochondrial membranes (relative up-shift of GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSK, SMPD1 and v-ATPase transcripts). Assembly state, electron leak, ROS, mitophagy flux and lysosomal degradative flux were not measured here; causality is not established. The assigned ER-proteostasis/UPR focus was tested and is not supported by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assembly test: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show that assembled complex IV and complex V (and complex III) holoenzyme per mitochondrial mass is equal or lower in APOE4 despite equal or higher levels of nuclear-encoded subunit protein (e.g. NDUFA/NDUFS, ATP5F1B, UQCRC2), i.e. a reduced assembled-holoenzyme : free-nuclear-subunit ratio. If APOE4 shows proportionally increased assembled holoenzyme with an unchanged assembly ratio, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: low-dose mitoribosome inhibition (doxycycline or chloramphenicol titration) should be selectively more damaging in APOE4 than APOE3 - a larger fractional drop in maximal and spare respiratory capacity and a larger induction of PRDX3/GPX4 and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts at matched drug exposure - because APOE4 is already core-subunit limited. Equal dose-response curves in the two genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Reciprocal rescue: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (increasing mtDNA copy number / TFAM or mitochondrial translation capacity, or mitochondrial transfer) should normalise the assembled-complex ratio and reduce the peroxiredoxin and lysosomal hydrolase transcript excess in APOE4 without changing nuclear OXPHOS transcript levels. No change in the redox/lysosomal readouts after successful rescue of assembly would falsify steps 4-6.", "Flux prediction: Seahorse profiling should show that APOE4 maximal oxygen consumption does not scale with its elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcript investment, with a higher proton-leak fraction and a lower ATP-linked : maximal OCR ratio; if APOE4 shows proportionally higher coupled respiration, the mechanism is weakened.", "Quantitative mitonuclear ratio: in an unbiased whole-transcriptome (non-probe) measurement plus mtDNA:nDNA qPCR, APOE4 should show a reduced mtDNA-encoded : nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript ratio, and this should not be explained solely by reduced mtDNA copy number per cell; equal ratios would indicate the observed MT down-shift is a probe/normalisation artefact and would remove the core of the hypothesis.", "Negative (focus-rejection) prediction: ER/UPR is not the driver - APOE4 microglia should show no increase in BiP/GRP94/PDI protein or XBP1 splicing, and PERK (GSK2606414) or IRE1 (4u8C) inhibition should not normalise the OXPHOS, redox or lysosomal transcript differences. Detection of a clear XBP1s/BiP induction that is required for these differences would overturn the choice of bottleneck in favour of the ER-proteostasis alternative."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred biosynthetic commitment): APOE4 microglia carry higher relative transcript levels for nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits and assembly factors (all 37 matched genes positive; median +2.64 vs global median +1.46; 29/37 above the global median, permutation p=0.002) and for mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA enzymes (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, DLD), with glycolytic commitment steps HK2 and PFKP relatively reduced. We infer, but did not measure, increased synthesis of nuclear-encoded respiratory subunits.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred limiting supply): the six measured mtDNA-encoded transcripts do not follow this shift (median -1.56; 4/6 negative against a 23% background negative rate, binomial p=0.028; nuclear-vs-mitochondrial contrast Mann-Whitney p=0.0011). We infer a shortfall of mitochondrially translated core subunits (COX1/2/3, CYB, ATP6, ND4) relative to their nuclear-encoded partners.", "Step 3 (inferred, unmeasured): because complexes III, IV and V require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores as assembly seeds, the mitonuclear mismatch makes core-subunit availability the bottleneck; nuclear-encoded modules accumulate as unassembled or sub-stoichiometric intermediates rather than increasing holoenzyme content proportionally.", "Step 4 (inferred, unmeasured): sub-stoichiometric and partially assembled complexes III/IV increase univalent electron leak and lower coupling efficiency, so the elevated TCA/NADH supply is converted into peroxide rather than proportionally increased ATP flux.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred antioxidant response): the peroxide load is buffered by a coordinated relative up-shift of thiol-peroxidase transcripts (TXNDC17, PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, MGST2; median +3.4, permutation p=0.013), consistent with a chronic, compensated redox burden rather than an acute one.", "Step 6 (measured RNA + ambiguous protein spots, inferred flux): damaged mitochondrial membranes and oxidised lipid increase substrate load on the endolysosomal system, matching the relative up-shift of lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GAA, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB; median +2.63, permutation p=0.032) and v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A); the two v-ATPase-candidate protein spots are lower in APOE4 (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), which is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, an unmet degradative demand.", "Step 7 (scope): microglial identity transcripts (TREM2, CSF1R, C1QA/B/C, AIF1, APOE) sit at or below the global median, so this is proposed as a metabolic/organellar state difference rather than a change in microglial identity or an interferon/inflammatory program."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: APOE4 microglia expand the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA program without matched mtDNA-encoded core subunits, creating an assembly bottleneck with redox and lysosomal consequences"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15851272015655576, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.004810866970757896, "cosine_similarity": 0.2595846939967616, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_045", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6146601941747573, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15851272015655576, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.004810866970757896, "cosine_similarity": 0.2595846939967616, "direction_accuracy": 0.2621359223300971, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6146601941747573, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.090464, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 337}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_079", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list in an unspecified logarithm base; effect sizes are used only for direction and rank, not as absolute fold changes, and are not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot scale.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, LIPA, PSAP, LAMP2, P2RY12) are unknown, not unchanged; program summaries therefore describe represented members only, and members were chosen from prior pathway knowledge (unverified, no literature access) before their directions were inspected.", "Coordinated transcript increases for hydrolases and SREBP targets are assumed to reflect at least partly proportional protein and pathway activity; abundance was measured, whereas uptake flux, hydrolase activity, TFEB nuclear localisation, SREBP2 cleavage, sterol localisation and beta-oxidation flux are inferred and unmeasured.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each and are dominated by keratin and actin candidates; no spot is treated as identification of a single protein, and multi-spot trains may reflect charge/processing redistribution rather than total abundance.", "Program sign enrichment is judged against the list's own 77% positive background and is descriptive only; co-regulated genes are not independent, so no formal enrichment claim is made.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid/lipoprotein supply and part of the transcriptional state may be non-cell-autonomous.", "The condition is mock: any reduced capacity for actin-dependent particulate clearance or for handling an acute lipid load is a prospective, challenge-revealed prediction, not an observed ongoing defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated lipid-handling cell-state change: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake receptors, late-endosomal-lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, sterol-esterification/efflux components, and mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS machinery are jointly higher, yet SREBP-target cholesterol-synthesis transcripts are also higher, which is the pattern expected when internalized sterol is retained in lysosomal/esterified/APOE-particle pools instead of equilibrating with the ER regulatory pool. We propose altered lipid routing plus expanded degradative capacity, not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck; the myeloid actomyosin/Rac motility module is coordinately lower, so the increase is in receptor/endolysosomal handling rather than in actin-driven large-particle engulfment. Causality is not established by these abundance measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective sterol-pool test: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, filipin/ALOD4-accessible plasma-membrane and ER sterol should be equal or lower while lysosomal and cholesteryl-ester pools are higher (LC-MS of free versus esterified sterol). If APOE4 shows higher ER-accessible cholesterol together with reduced nuclear SREBP2, the routing step is wrong and the data would instead indicate simple sterol overload.", "Discriminating perturbation 1 (routing): acute SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or NPC1/lysosomal-egress bypass with cyclodextrin should suppress SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, INSIG1) and reduce lysosomal-gene induction more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal suppression in both genotypes weakens the claim that routing, rather than global lipid load, differs.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (uptake versus engulfment): blocking scavenger-receptor uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should normalise the APOE4 lysosomal-hydrolase and TFEB-target transcript excess; in the same cells, DiI-LDL/soluble-cargo uptake should be higher in APOE4 while uptake of large actin-dependent cargo (myelin debris, 3 um beads, synaptosomes) is equal or lower, matching the reduced MYH9/RAC2/DOCK8/MYO1F module. Higher large-particle engulfment plus faster cargo degradation in APOE4 would falsify the routing-shift step and support increased generic phagocytic throughput.", "Capacity versus defect test: DQ-BSA proteolysis, LysoTracker volume, lysosomal pH and hydrolase enzyme assays (GBA, HEXA, GAA) should be equal or higher in mock APOE4 (successful expansion). If proteolytic capacity or hydrolase activity is lower despite higher transcripts, the mechanism must be revised toward a post-transcriptional lysosomal bottleneck.", "Flux test: 13C/3H-oleate and cholesterol tracing should show equal or greater lipid oxidation and TCA labelling in APOE4 (consistent with the uniformly higher TCA/OXPHOS transcripts) with concurrent accumulation of esterified sterol. Unchanged oxidative flux with unchanged sterol partitioning would reduce the mechanism to a transcript-only cell-state difference."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia express higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-binding surface receptors and clearance receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:ITGB5), increasing the inferred rate at which lipid cargo is directed into the endocytic route (uptake flux itself was not measured).", "Cargo is delivered along an endosome-to-lysosome route whose components are also higher (gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:AP5M1), with lysosomal biogenesis regulators up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF) and enzyme sorting machinery up (gene:GNPTG).", "The degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded: lipid- and glycan-directed hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits rise strongly and near-uniformly (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSD, gene:MAN2B1, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2), i.e. 22/23 represented members positive versus a 77% positive selected-list background.", "Sterol liberated in this compartment is inferred to be routed to storage/export rather than to the ER sensor pool (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1 up; gene:OSBPL8, a contact-site lipid-transfer protein, down -1.90), so the ER continues to read low sterol and SREBP-target and sterol-synthesis transcripts stay high (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:MYLIP).", "Sustained lipid catabolic and biosynthetic demand accompanies a uniformly higher mitochondrial oxidative program (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:UQCRC2, gene:SDHB, gene:COX6B1, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS; 14/14 positive) while glycolytic/PPP members are mixed (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32 versus gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:ENO1 up), consistent with oxidative handling of lipid-derived substrate.", "In parallel, the hematopoietic actomyosin/Rac motility module is lower (gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:FAM49B -5.83, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:ACTB -4.98, gene:SPN -7.26, gene:CTSS -5.57), so the predicted phenotype is a routing shift toward receptor-mediated/soluble lipid uptake and lysosomal processing, not a general increase in actin-driven engulfment of large particles.", "Net predicted state in mock: APOE4 microglia carry a larger lipid-loaded endolysosomal compartment with more esterified/lysosomal sterol and higher oxidative machinery, with reduced reserve for actin-dependent particulate clearance that would be revealed only by a future phagocytic or lipid-load challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route lipid into an expanded endolysosomal-oxidative compartment while ER sterol sensing still signals deficiency"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17570854384775603, "cosine_similarity": 0.2583537369607876, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_079", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6362783171521036, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2577724033526566, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17570854384775603, "cosine_similarity": 0.2583537369607876, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6362783171521036, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85752225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 91}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_082", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and 77% are positive. All statements are therefore made as percentile ranks WITHIN this shifted distribution, not as absolute fold changes, and the logarithm base of the RNA effects is left unspecified and is not converted.", "Genes absent from the supplied rows (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, IDI1, CYP51A1, NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, PLIN2, STARD3, OSBP, VAPA/VAPB, NR1H3) are assumed to be simply unselected. Their absence is NOT treated as evidence of no change and is not cited as an observation.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein amount and, more weakly, for pathway capacity. Hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, sterol localisation, esterification flux and efflux flux were not measured in these data and are inferred only.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is assigned to a single gene product in this hypothesis, and spot-level effects are used only as ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "No lipid, sterol, filipin, lipid-droplet or lipidomic measurement is supplied; the entire Step 6 endpoint is a prediction, not an observation.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30, in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; astrocyte-derived APOE and lipoproteins are assumed to be a shared, genotype-matched extracellular source, which the data cannot verify. Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional increase in lipoprotein/lipid cargo receptors and luminal lysosomal hydrolases that is NOT matched by the intra-lysosomal sterol-transfer and egress module (NPC2, ORP1L/OSBPL1A, OSBPL8). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is the handoff of catabolically liberated cholesterol out of the endolysosomal lumen to the ER, so that sterol is retained in the endolysosome, the ER sterol sensor is not reporting excess (SREBP-2 module transcripts remain positive rather than repressed), and the lipid that does reach the ER is diverted into SOAT1/ACAT2/DGAT1-dependent esterification supported by SREBF1/SCD-driven monounsaturated fatty-acid supply, predicting a cholesteryl-ester- and triacylglycerol-shifted lipidome with endolysosomal free-cholesterol retention. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION 1 (relieve the proposed bottleneck): supplying the egress step directly - 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC2 protein add-back / NPC1+NPC2 overexpression - in APOE4 microglia should (a) reduce filipin-positive free cholesterol in LAMP1-positive compartments toward APOE3 levels, (b) transiently REPRESS SREBP-2 targets (SREBF2, HMGCS1, LDLR, INSIG1) as sterol finally reaches the ER sensor, and (c) reduce the APOE4 excess of cholesteryl ester and lipid-droplet content. If cyclodextrin or NPC2 add-back leaves lysosomal free cholesterol and the cholesteryl-ester excess unchanged, the egress bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION 2 (separate input from bottleneck): SCARB1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should selectively reduce the APOE4-specific cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol excess WITHOUT normalising the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program. If SCARB1 knockdown abolishes the hydrolase induction as well, the receptor and hydrolase arms are one program rather than input and capacity, and Step 1/Step 2 must be merged; if it changes neither, Step 1 is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION 3 (test the escape valve): SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should collapse the APOE4 cholesteryl-ester pool and convert it into free cholesterol with increased APOE4-selective, but not APOE3-selective, membrane-cholesterol stress and lysosomal damage. If APOE4 cholesteryl-ester excess is SOAT1-independent, Step 5 is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING PREDICTION 4 (separate from the mitochondrial alternative): respiratory-chain inhibition or restoration of the APOE3 OXPHOS/TCA transcript state should NOT normalise lysosomal free cholesterol or the cholesteryl-ester excess; conversely Perturbations 1-3 should correct the lipid phenotype without normalising the OXPHOS/TCA transcript shift (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5). If the lipid phenotype tracks the OXPHOS manipulation instead, the mitochondrial-oxidation alternative supersedes this hypothesis.", "DIRECT MEASUREMENT PREDICTIONS: quantitative lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased cholesteryl esters (18:1-enriched), increased triacylglycerol, an increased ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio and reduced glucosylceramide. Immunoblot should show NPC2 and ORP1L protein at or below APOE3 levels while GBA/GAA/CTSB protein is above. The mechanism is weakened if (i) total and lysosomal free cholesterol are equal between genotypes, (ii) NPC2 or NPC1 protein is HIGHER in APOE4 despite the transcript rank, (iii) cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerol are unchanged or lower in APOE4, or (iv) SREBP-2 target proteins are reduced in APOE4, indicating the ER sensor already sees sterol excess."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (input, inferred flux from measured RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipid-cargo receptors, most strikingly SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22; 99.1st percentile of the supplied DE effect distribution), with CD36, ABCA7 and TREM2 also positive. We infer, but did not measure, an increased flux of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (degradative capacity, inferred activity from measured RNA): luminal acid-hydrolase transcripts are concentrated in the top decile of the shifted distribution (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86; set mean percentile 0.80, permutation p ~= 3e-4), alongside v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51) and gene:TFEB (+2.38). We infer increased hydrolytic and acidification capacity; enzyme activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (the proposed bottleneck, measured relative deficit): the module that moves liberated sterol out of the lysosomal lumen and across ER-lysosome contacts is not scaled with Steps 1-2. gene:NPC2 (+1.17) sits at the 35th percentile, gene:OSBPL1A/ORP1L (+1.03) at the 26th, and gene:OSBPL8 is negative (-1.90, 13th percentile); the hydrolase-set mean percentile exceeds the egress-set mean percentile by 0.46 (permutation p ~= 3e-4). We propose that sterol egress from the endolysosome, not sterol synthesis, is rate-limiting.", "Step 4 (consequence for sensing, inferred localization): if liberated cholesterol is retained in the endolysosome, the ER-resident SCAP/INSIG sensor does not register excess. Consistent with this, the SREBP-2 module is not repressed but remains modestly positive and below the global shift: gene:SREBF2 (+1.06, 28th percentile), gene:HMGCS1 (+1.08, 28th), gene:LDLR (+1.50, 51st), gene:INSIG1 (+1.87, 60th), gene:MYLIP (+1.28, 41st). Uptake is therefore not switched off, sustaining the load in Step 1.", "Step 5 (escape valve, inferred flux): lipid that does reach the ER is esterified and stored rather than exported. gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:ACAT2 (+2.04) and gene:DGAT1 (+1.72) are positive, and the monounsaturated fatty-acid supply arm is strongly positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, 92nd percentile; gene:SCD +4.17, 89th percentile), providing oleoyl-CoA for cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol synthesis.", "Step 6 (predicted lipid endpoint, not measured here): the net predicted APOE4 lipid state is elevated cholesteryl esters (enriched in 18:1 acyl chains) and triacylglycerol in cytosolic lipid droplets, elevated free cholesterol within LAMP1-positive compartments, and a sphingolipid shift toward ceramide at the expense of sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide (driven by gene:SMPD1 and gene:GBA), with no matched induction of an efflux arm in the supplied rows."], "title": "APOE4 microglia scale lysosomal lipid intake and hydrolysis without scaling lysosomal sterol egress, forcing lipid into ER esterification and storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22761510910903518, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2221152210965343, "cosine_similarity": 0.25826039699882736, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_082", "mean_absolute_error": 0.638948220064725, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22761510910903518, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2221152210965343, "cosine_similarity": 0.25826039699882736, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.638948220064725, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.68658475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 338}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_140", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not a whole transcriptome; enrichment statements are made only relative to that same selected background (mean +1.39, 77% positive), and the logarithm base is unspecified so only ranks/relative magnitudes are used.", "Transcript abundance of ETC/TCA and peroxiredoxin genes is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding protein amounts and pathway capacity; enzyme activity, respiratory flux, ROS production, NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG were not measured in these data.", "2D protein spots contain several candidate genes, so protein_spot:017 (CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and protein_spot:077 (KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB) are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only, never as measured catalase or peroxiredoxin-2 protein.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and astrocyte co-culture composition is comparable, so genotype rather than differentiation state or library depth drives the global positive RNA shift.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: all steps beyond the measured abundances are inferred and require perturbation testing."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated transcriptional up-shift of TCA-cycle and all electron-transport-chain complexes together with matrix/thiol-peroxidase and thioredoxin-linked antioxidant transcripts and NNT, while the cytosolic NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate arm (PGD, TALDO1, NADK) is transcriptionally down; we hypothesise that the resulting mismatch between an inferred higher mitochondrial peroxide flux plus an increased oxidisable-lipid handling load and a narrowed cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity is the rate-limiting bottleneck that makes APOE4 microglia thiol-redox fragile rather than globally antioxidant-deficient. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation/biogenesis is NOT supported as the driver in these data and is explicitly rejected.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute pharmacological block of cytosolic NADPH regeneration (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide, or NADK knockdown) should produce a significantly larger fall in cytosolic GSH/GSSG (Grx1-roGFP2) and a larger rise in C11-BODIPY lipid peroxidation and death in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia; equal genotype sensitivity would weaken the NADPH-bottleneck step.", "Rescue arm of the same test: raising cytosolic NADPH supply (G6PD or cytosolic IDH1 overexpression) should normalise APOE4 basal Grx1-roGFP2 oxidation and RSL3-induced lipid peroxidation without normalising the ETC/TCA transcript program; if redox parameters stay abnormal after NADPH restoration, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Source test: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ/MitoTEMPO) or complex-I site-IQ suppressor S3QEL should lower matrix HyPer7 oxidation and peroxiredoxin-3 hyperoxidation preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-selective effect would refute step 2.", "Flux test: Seahorse should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and higher proton-leak-corrected respiration in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or lower APOE4 respiration would refute step 1 and would reduce the ETC transcript up-shift to a compensatory or technical artefact.", "NNT dependency: NNT knockdown should selectively increase matrix peroxide and reduce survival in APOE4 relative to APOE3; no genotype interaction would weaken the proposed matrix-NADPH compensation.", "Rejection of the peroxisomal alternative: if peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0 lyso-PC clearance or catalase-targeted HyPer7) is the dominant difference, PEX5/ACOX1 knockdown should abolish the APOE4-APOE3 redox gap; the present data (only gene:ACSL4 down, few and mixed peroxisomal rows) predict this manipulation will NOT abolish it."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_140", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher steady-state transcripts for pyruvate import and TCA enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:SDHB) and for every sampled ETC subunit family (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS; 39/39 sampled OXPHOS rows positive, permutation p=1e-4). Inferred, not measured: higher respiratory electron flux and complex I/III electron leak.", "Inferred: greater matrix superoxide/H2O2 production per cell raises the peroxide load that must be cleared by thiol peroxidases; no ROS, O2 consumption or redox-couple measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Measured compensatory response: thiol-peroxidase/thioredoxin-system and methionine-sulfoxide-repair transcripts are up above the already up-shifted background (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:PRDX2, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GPX4, gene:MSRA, gene:GSS, gene:FTH1, gene:SELENOW; set permutation p=0.013, cytosolic-only subset p=0.003), together with gene:NNT, implying a shift of NADPH supply toward matrix transhydrogenase.", "Measured counter-directional step (proposed bottleneck): the cytosolic NADPH-supplying/PPP transcripts present in the data move down (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK; lower-tail permutation p=0.049) and gene:MSRB1 is down, so cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity is inferred to be reduced relative to peroxiredoxin/glutathione re-reduction demand.", "Measured parallel load: lipid uptake, desaturation, esterification and lysosomal lipid catabolism transcripts are up (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:APOE, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB), which is inferred to increase peroxidisable membrane/droplet lipid that must be repaired through GPX4-glutathione and NADPH-dependent cycling.", "Predicted emergent state: NADPH-dependent peroxide clearance, not antioxidant protein abundance, becomes rate limiting in APOE4; the cell is therefore expected to sit at a more oxidised cytosolic glutathione/thioredoxin potential with normal or elevated antioxidant enzyme levels, consistent with the modest up-shift of the catalase-containing and peroxiredoxin-containing 2D spots (protein_spot:017, protein_spot:077) and with unchanged/mixed G6PD-containing spots (protein_spot:018, protein_spot:021, protein_spot:019)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an oxidation-biased mitochondrial program whose peroxide load outstrips cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37095225787394304, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23498658163496855, "cosine_similarity": 0.2580969961366121, "direction_accuracy": 0.3414239482200647, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_140", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6555080906148867, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.37095225787394304, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.23498658163496855, "cosine_similarity": 0.2580969961366121, "direction_accuracy": 0.3414239482200647, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6555080906148867, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.579776, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 339}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_080", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are reported log fold changes of unspecified base; all statements are made in the reported log units and no linear fold change is claimed.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome, so every set statistic is computed against that selected background (median +1.46, 77% positive) rather than against zero.", "10X Flex probe-based counting of mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to be comparable between genotypes; MT- transcript levels are assumed to track, imperfectly, the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunit protein, which was not measured.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance; no enzymatic activity, respiration, membrane potential, ROS, NADPH, GSH/GSSG, mtDNA copy number or mitoribosome measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots are mixtures of candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous corroboration only; no spot is asserted to be a uniquely identified protein.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent difference in cell-quality filtering are assumed not to be the sole driver of the mitonuclear discordance; biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, nuclear-encoded TCA, carrier, import and OXPHOS-accessory transcripts rise coordinately while mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts do not; we hypothesise that this mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch is the rate-limiting bottleneck for assembling functional respiratory complexes, that it increases electron leak and matrix peroxide flux, and that APOE4 cells compensate by shifting peroxide-clearance reductant supply from the cytosolic pentose-phosphate route (transcripts reduced) to a proton-motive-force-dependent mitochondrial NNT/ME1-PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4 buffer, creating a self-limiting and fragile redox state rather than a peroxisomal one.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic NNT loss-of-function (or NNT knockdown) in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should cause a genotype-selective collapse of matrix NADPH/GSH ratio and a disproportionate rise in matrix-targeted peroxide reporter (MLS-HyPer7 / mitoSOX) in APOE4. If NNT loss affects both genotypes equally, or if APOE3 is hit harder, the proposed relocation of reductant supply into the matrix is falsified.", "Blue-native PAGE or complexome profiling should show a higher ratio of complex I/III/IV subassemblies to holo-complexes, and lower CI-linked respiration per unit nuclear-encoded subunit protein, in APOE4. Normal assembly stoichiometry and parity of mtDNA-encoded proteins would falsify the bottleneck step.", "Increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression or mtDNA copy-number restoration) should reduce matrix peroxide reporter signal and lower PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4 and NNT transcripts toward APOE3 levels. Failure of the antioxidant module to normalise despite restored mtDNA-encoded transcripts would weaken the causal chain.", "A matrix-targeted antioxidant (MitoTEMPO or MitoQ) should blunt the APOE4 antioxidant transcript module and partially normalise the lysosomal/lipid transcript program, whereas an equipotent cytosolic-restricted scavenger (NAC) should not. Equal efficacy of the cytosolic scavenger would place the oxidant source outside the matrix.", "Peroxisomal alternative test: catalase inhibition (3-aminotriazole) or ACOX1 inhibition in APOE3 microglia should NOT reproduce the APOE4 mitonuclear and matrix-antioxidant signature. If it does, the peroxisomal H2O2 source becomes the better explanation and this hypothesis should be rejected.", "Bulk or long-read RNA plus targeted proteomics of mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-CO1, MT-CYB, MT-ATP6) should reproduce the relative APOE4 deficit. If an orthogonal assay shows genotype parity for mtDNA-encoded transcripts and proteins, the mitonuclear-mismatch premise is falsified and the correlated antioxidant transcript rise would instead reflect a general mitochondrial-biogenesis program."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts: every measured nuclear OXPHOS accessory/structural subunit is higher (n=38, mean +2.81 log units, permutation p=0.0005 against the already up-shifted list background), together with TCA dehydrogenases (OGDH, MDH1, DLD, ACO2, IDH3B/G; mean +5.68, p=0.0005) and import/carrier machinery (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM8B, TIMM17B, SLC25A1/5/11/37/46; mean +3.39, p=0.0005). This is measured RNA abundance only.", "The mtDNA-encoded catalytic core does not follow: MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 sit in the lowest 5-19th percentile of the list (set mean -0.82 versus list mean +1.39, one-sided permutation p=0.021), with only MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 near the list median. We infer, but have not measured, a relative shortfall of mtDNA-encoded core subunits per unit of nuclear-encoded subunit supply.", "Inferred (not measured): the mismatch limits holo-complex assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V, leaving unmatched nuclear subunits and stalled assembly intermediates whose flavin/quinone sites leak electrons, so respiratory flux rises less than subunit abundance while superoxide/H2O2 production per unit flux rises. Assembly state, respiration and ROS were not measured here.", "A matrix-localised antioxidant and iron-buffering transcript module is coordinately elevated (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, GSS, TXNDC17, UCP2, FTH1, SLC25A37; mean +3.23, permutation p=0.009 against the up-shifted background), consistent with, but not proof of, an ongoing matrix peroxide load; the direction of causality between leak and antioxidant induction is not established by these data.", "Reductant supply is redirected: transcripts for cytosolic NADPH/NAD generation fall in a list where 77% of genes rise (PGD -1.30, TALDO1 -2.32, NADK -1.14, NAMPT -2.62; set mean -1.84, one-sided p=0.010), whereas the matrix NADPH producers NNT (+2.88) and ME1 (+1.36) rise. We infer a shift of peroxiredoxin/glutathione re-reduction onto NNT, whose activity is itself driven by the proton-motive force.", "Because the inferred NADPH buffer depends on the same proton-motive force that the mismatched, leak-prone electron transport chain supplies inefficiently, the bottleneck is self-reinforcing: any further loss of coupling should collapse matrix NADPH and peroxide clearance. Downstream lysosomal/lipid-handling transcript elevation (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1H, TFEB, SCD, SREBF1, SCARB1) is placed here as a consequence or parallel branch, not as evidence for the redox step.", "The peroxisomal arm is explicitly not the proposed source: peroxisomal biogenesis genes are absent from the supplied list and the few peroxisome-linked measurements are discordant (SCP2 +5.95, MPV17 +3.45, ACOX1 +1.24, AMACR +1.12 versus ABCD1 -1.64), so peroxisomal beta-oxidation-derived H2O2 is retained only as an untested alternative."], "title": "Mitonuclear subunit-supply mismatch makes APOE4 microglia dependent on a matrix NADPH/peroxiredoxin buffer"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18894694088542627, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09405002098817056, "cosine_similarity": 0.25568298362896474, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6194012944983819, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18894694088542627, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09405002098817056, "cosine_similarity": 0.25568298362896474, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6194012944983819, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.712256, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 340}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_047", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; all comparisons are made within this scale and no absolute fold change is claimed.", "The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect| \u003e 1), not an unbiased transcriptome, so pathway enrichment is judged by rank within this list, not against a genome background.", "The list carries a strong global positive shift (median effect +1.46; 1705/2212 rows positive), which may reflect normalization, ambient RNA or compositional differences rather than true global induction; conclusions therefore rest on effects relative to that median and on adjusted-p rank.", "Effect magnitude and adjusted p-value are essentially uncorrelated in this table (Spearman ~ -0.03), so very large reported effects (e.g. AGPAT2, GBA, SMPD1, SCARB1) are treated as less reliable than moderate effects with extreme significance (SCD, SOAT1, CTSD, CTSB, CTSH, SCARB2).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme activity and flux; desaturation index, acyl-CoA pools, lipid-droplet content, lysosomal pH and hydrolase activity were not measured here.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein observation is used as evidence for a specific enzyme.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed for pseudoreplication across cells.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be the main exogenous lipid source; genotype-dependent differences in the astrocyte compartment or in secreted APOE lipoprotein composition are an untested confounder."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes carry a transcriptional program of increased lipid/debris scavenging and lysosomal membrane-lipid hydrolysis together with increased re-esterification and acyl-chain remodeling (SREBF1, SCD, LPCAT1, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, SOAT1). We propose that the SREBP1-SCD step, which supplies monounsaturated acyl-CoA for lysophospholipid re-acylation and for neutral-lipid (TAG/cholesteryl-ester) esterification, is the principal bottleneck that determines whether the extra catabolic lipid load is safely stored or accumulates as saturated/lyso species; the RNA and ambiguous protein-spot data are correlative and do not establish causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) at a dose that is neutral for APOE3 microglia will cause a genotype-selective effect in APOE4 - greater increase in saturated lysophosphatidylcholine and saturated PC species, greater DDIT3/XBP1-splicing induction and greater viability loss - and co-supplementation with oleate will rescue APOE4 selectively. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond equivalently, and oleate gives no genotype-specific rescue, the SCD bottleneck is falsified.", "Lipidomics: APOE4 microglia will show a higher desaturation index (16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0) and higher MUFA-containing triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester content than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower desaturation index despite higher SCD RNA would falsify the transcript-to-flux step (Step 4).", "Source-of-lipid test: removing the exogenous membrane-lipid load (microglia mono-culture without astrocytes, lipid-depleted medium, or blockade of CD36/SCARB1/MERTK-dependent uptake) should reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess in CTSD/CTSB/GBA/SCD/SOAT1 transcripts by a substantial margin. Persistence of the full excess would indicate a cell-autonomous SREBP1 program rather than a catabolic-flux-driven one, weakening Steps 1-3.", "Lysosomal origin test: blocking lysosomal acidification or hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/SMPD1 inhibition) should shrink the APOE4-excess neutral-lipid pool if it derives from catabolized membrane cargo; if the excess pool is unchanged, the lipid is more likely de novo synthesized and Step 2 is not the source.", "Esterification-capacity test: combined DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition should shift APOE4 microglia disproportionately toward free cholesterol and free fatty acid accumulation with greater phagocytic and viability impairment than APOE3. Equal responses would argue the storage arm is not carrying an APOE4-specific load.", "Protein-level check: SCD, CTSD and SOAT1 protein must be higher in APOE4 by targeted immunoblot or targeted MS. Unchanged protein for SCD in particular would decouple the RNA signal from the proposed bottleneck.", "Negative control on alternatives: interferon and canonical inflammatory modules should not show a coherent APOE4 elevation relative to the list median; a strong genotype-driven interferon or IL1B/TNF program on independent measurement would favour an inflammatory rather than a lipid-handling primary mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid- and debris-uptake receptors and lipid carriers (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:COLEC12, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:SLCO2B1). Uptake flux itself was not measured; we infer an increased delivery of astrocyte- and debris-derived membrane lipid to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): The endolysosomal hydrolytic module is coordinately higher (gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSH, gene:SCARB2, gene:GPNMB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1), consistent with, but not proof of, increased hydrolysis of glycerophospholipid, sphingolipid and sterol-ester cargo, releasing free fatty acids, sphingoid bases and free cholesterol.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Liberated lipid must be re-esterified or exported. Transcripts for the esterification/remodeling arm are higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1, gene:CHPT1), indicating a shift of the released acyl and sterol pools toward re-acylation of lysophospholipids and toward TAG/cholesteryl-ester storage rather than immediate re-export.", "Step 4 (proposed bottleneck): Acyl-CoA activation is not uniformly increased (gene:ACSL5, gene:ACSL4 and gene:GPAT3 are lower), so the unsaturated acyl-CoA pool generated by SCD becomes the limiting input for LPCAT1/MBOAT2/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent esterification. SCD activity, desaturation index and acyl-CoA pool size were not measured; the bottleneck is inferred from transcript coherence only.", "Step 5 (predicted consequence): When catabolic lipid input exceeds SCD-supplied monounsaturated capacity, saturated fatty acids, lysophospholipids and free cholesterol transiently rise in the ER, producing low-grade membrane/ER stress and an antioxidant response; the elevated gene:DDIT3 and gene:GPX4 transcripts are compatible with this state but are not direct measurements of lipid stress.", "Step 6 (net phenotype): APOE4 microglia are predicted to sit in a MUFA-dependent, lipid-laden storage state in which esterification capacity, not uptake or hydrolysis, sets how much internalized membrane lipid can be buffered. Efflux and beta-oxidation genes (ABCA1, ABCG1, PNPLA2, CPT1A, PLIN2) are absent from the supplied rows, so an efflux/oxidation block is an untested alternative."], "title": "SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA is the rate-limiting sink for lysosome-derived membrane lipid in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2732525938780785, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20263644171339631, "cosine_similarity": 0.25459790812399097, "direction_accuracy": 0.2540453074433657, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6419352750809062, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2732525938780785, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20263644171339631, "cosine_similarity": 0.25459790812399097, "direction_accuracy": 0.2540453074433657, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6419352750809062, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.80525825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 341}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_093", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list with an approximate |log FC| \u003e= 1 floor and a 77% upward skew; all pathway statements here are relative comparisons within that list, not statements about the unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, LIPA, ASAH1, GRN, PSAP, ABCA1, PLIN2) means unmeasured here, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ordering and sign are used, not absolute fold changes.", "Protein spots are mixtures with a mean of 4.8 candidate genes each (39/92 contain a keratin), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; the ANXA1 spot train is treated as suggestive only, and RNA-protein concordance across spots is null (Spearman -0.06, sign agreement 0.48).", "Measured transcript or spot abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for protein activity, luminal enzyme maturation, lysosomal pH, degradative flux and lipid localisation, none of which were measured.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, and the cultures are microglia-astrocyte co-cultures, so ambient/cross-cell contamination and line-specific batch effects cannot be excluded as contributors to the global upward RNA shift.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment, and positive effects mean higher in APOE4."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 cells sit in a state in which lipid-rich endolysosomal cargo is cleared more slowly than it is delivered. The transcriptional data are dominated by a coordinated late-endosome/lysosome biogenesis module (hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, lysosomal transporters, late-endosomal trafficking; 52/56 curated members higher in APOE4, permutation p=0.0015 against the within-list background of 77% up) together with a lysosomal membrane damage/repair module (LGALS3, ANXA1, ANXA6, CHMP4B, SMPD1) and an SREBP-driven sterol/fatty-acid synthesis and LDLR uptake program, while phagocytic/scavenger uptake receptors are up only marginally (median +1.31, i.e. barely past the |log FC|\u003e=1 selection floor, permutation p=0.74 on magnitude). We propose that these coordinated abundance changes reflect a compensatory response to a downstream clearance/egress limitation rather than increased uptake drive; degradative flux, lysosomal pH, sterol egress and lipid pools were not measured here, so the mechanism is inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: pulse-chase of a quenched degradable cargo (DQ-BSA or fluorescently labelled myelin/apoptotic-neuron debris) with parallel LAMP1 volume imaging should show a lower per-lysosome (volume-normalised) dequenching/clearance rate constant in APOE4 than APOE3, with uptake rate in the first minutes equal or lower in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or faster volume-normalised clearance, or clearly greater initial uptake with unchanged clearance kinetics, the clearance-capacity bottleneck is wrong and an uptake-driven model is favoured.", "Damage-response test: baseline galectin-3 (LGALS3) and ESCRT (CHMP4B) puncta per cell, and their induction after a mild lysosomotropic challenge (LLOMe), should be higher in APOE4. Absence of any difference in galectin-3 puncta or repair kinetics would weaken step 3 and would argue that the LGALS3/ANXA1/CHMP4B transcripts reflect general activation rather than membrane stress.", "Load-relief test: culturing in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or removing the lipid cargo source, should collapse the coordinated hydrolase/v-ATPase/CLEAR transcript module and the SREBP target module in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels within 24-48 h without changing scavenger receptor transcripts. Persistence of the CLEAR module under low cargo load would indicate a cargo-independent, genotype-intrinsic TFEB set point and would weaken the load-limitation claim.", "Egress test: promoting lysosomal sterol egress (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC1/NPC2 augmentation) should normalise SREBP target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, HMGCS1) and reduce galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 while leaving TREM2/MERTK/MRC1 unchanged. If SREBP targets stay elevated after egress rescue, the ER-sterol-sensing arm of step 4 is falsified.", "Enzyme-maturation test: despite higher CTSB/CTSD/HEXA transcripts, mature (processed) cathepsin protein and in-cell cathepsin activity per lysosome should be equal or lower in APOE4, consistent with the lower M6PR transcript and the mixed direction of cathepsin-candidate spots. Finding proportionally increased mature cathepsin activity per lysosome would weaken the mismatch between transcript-level expansion and functional capacity."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred flux, not measured): APOE4 apolipoprotein delivered with internalised lipid changes the physical state of cargo reaching the late endosome/lysosome, so that per-particle luminal degradation and sterol/lipid egress are slower than in APOE3. Only APOE transcript abundance (gene:APOE, +1.24) is measured; cargo flux, lysosomal pH and lipid pools are not.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): the degradative arm is transcriptionally amplified, consistent with a TFEB/MITF-type CLEAR response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03): acid hydrolases (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1), lysosomal membrane transporters (gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SPNS1, gene:LAMP1, gene:TMEM192) and late-endosomal trafficking (gene:RAB7A, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:ARL8B).", "Step 3 (inferred localisation/mechanical stress): retained, poorly digestible lipid cargo perturbs the limiting membrane; the damage-sensing and membrane-repair machinery is co-induced (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:ANXA1 +4.15, gene:ANXA6 +1.77, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:SMPD1 +5.63), and the only coherent spot train in the 2-D gel data, whose shared candidate is ANXA1, is increased (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:047).", "Step 4 (inferred signalling): because sterol and lipid remain in the endolysosome, ER/SCAP-SREBP sensing continues to read low accessible sterol, so biosynthetic and uptake genes rise (gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1; and the SREBP1 arm gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1). This returns more lipid to the same limiting compartment, a feed-forward loop rather than a corrective one.", "Step 5 (bottleneck placement): the uptake arm is not the limiting node. Scavenger/phagocytic receptor transcripts are uniformly but weakly elevated (gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:CD36 +1.40, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX), i.e. their median effect is indistinguishable from the list background, whereas hydrolase/v-ATPase/trafficking effects are larger. Hydrolase delivery is also not coordinately increased (gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:IDS -1.56, gene:CTSS -5.57 are lower in APOE4), so more enzyme transcript need not mean more mature luminal enzyme.", "Step 6 (consequence): the predicted phenotype is an expanded but saturated endolysosomal compartment with reduced clearance per unit lysosome, which would be measurable as slower cargo degradation kinetics and increased galectin-3 puncta in APOE4 despite equal or greater lysosomal mass."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a load-limited endolysosome: cargo clearance capacity, not cargo uptake, is the bottleneck, driving a membrane-damage response and compensatory CLEAR/SREBP feed-forward"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10336742606062843, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.035963593680279626, "cosine_similarity": 0.2539446453868545, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6390970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10336742606062843, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.035963593680279626, "cosine_similarity": 0.2539446453868545, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6390970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.04489925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 342}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_087", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a reported log fold change of unspecified base; all conclusions use ranks and within-experiment relative comparisons only, and no fold change is converted to a linear scale.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every entry has |effect|\u003e1) with a strong global upward shift (median +1.46, 77% positive), so gene sets are tested against this filtered background rather than against zero; absence of a gene from the list is not evidence that it is unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy; complex assembly state, respiratory flux, mitochondrial mass, membrane potential, mitophagy flux, lysosomal proteolytic activity and protein localisation were not measured here and are labelled inferred throughout.", "Only six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are present and two of them (MT-ND4L, MT-ND5) run counter to the proposed direction, so the mtDNA-side evidence rests on a small, partly inconsistent set.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for any specific mitochondrial or lysosomal protein pool.", "The comparison is treated as a bulk-like contrast; differences in microglial state composition or in astrocyte carry-over between APOE4 and APOE3 co-cultures could generate apparently coordinated set-level shifts.", "Normalisation is assumed not to be dominated by the mitochondrial transcript fraction; if it is, the mitonuclear divergence could be a compositional artefact (see falsifiable prediction 5).", "The assigned lipid focus was tested and set aside: glycerolipid/acyl-remodelling genes (AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, GPAT4, DGAT1, SCD, FADS1, CHPT1, SREBF1, ACSL4/5) are not enriched above the global background (median +1.59, median rank 0.54, p=0.93), so lipid remodelling is treated as a co-occurring, non-primary feature rather than the bottleneck. No lipidomic measurement was supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 by a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes, import carriers, mitochondrial translation/insertion factors) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts, which instead sit at the low extreme of the same differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4), so that nuclear subunits accumulate as unassembled or partially assembled modules rather than as proportionally increased holoenzymes; the resulting turnover of defective mitochondrial material raises lysosomal hydrolase demand, which is mirrored by the coordinated induction of TFEB and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed as a testable model, and the alternative that the mitonuclear divergence is a compositional or normalisation artefact is explicitly retained.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: selectively raising mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (for example TFAM or LRPPRC/SLIRP overexpression, or allotopic/mitochondrially targeted expression of ATP6 and CYB) should, without further raising nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, increase assembled CIII/CIV/CV holoenzyme on BN-PAGE and raise coupled (oligomycin-sensitive) oxygen consumption in APOE4 toward APOE3. If holoenzyme levels and coupled respiration remain unchanged while the mtDNA-encoded transcripts rise, the mtDNA-supply bottleneck is falsified.", "Dose-response interaction: low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol (mitoribosome inhibition) should produce a significantly steeper loss of coupled respiration and a steeper rise in unassembled nuclear subunits in APOE4 than in APOE3 (genotype x dose interaction), because APOE4 is proposed to already sit at the mt-translation supply limit. Equal sensitivity in both genotypes weakens the mechanism.", "Assembly-state readout: complexome profiling or BN-PAGE of APOE4 versus APOE3 should show accumulation of nuclear-encoded assembly intermediates and subcomplexes with a holoenzyme:subunit ratio lower in APOE4. If instead fully assembled holoenzymes increase in proportion to the nuclear transcript elevation, step 3 is wrong and the data would instead indicate genuine successful biogenesis.", "Quality-control coupling: pharmacological or genetic blockade of mitophagy/autophagic delivery should raise the pool of unassembled OXPHOS subunits more in APOE4 than APOE3 and should blunt the APOE4 excess of lysosomal hydrolase induction. If lysosomal hydrolase induction in APOE4 is unaffected by mitophagy blockade, step 5/6 coupling is falsified and the lysosomal program should be reassigned to APOE4 lipid handling.", "Artefact control: absolute per-cell quantification independent of library normalisation (mtDNA copy number by ddPCR, spike-in normalised mt-transcript counts, or single-molecule FISH for MT-CO2/MT-ATP6) should confirm a genuine per-cell deficit of mtDNA-encoded transcripts in APOE4. If per-cell mtDNA-encoded transcript content is equal between genotypes, the entire mitonuclear divergence is a normalisation/composition artefact and the hypothesis fails.", "Specificity control: the lipid-remodelling alternative predicts that inhibiting SCD or DGAT1 would normalise the APOE4 transcriptional state. Under the present hypothesis these inhibitors should not restore coupled respiration or assembled complex levels; if they do, the mitonuclear model should be replaced by the lipid model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts relative to the whole differential-expression background of the same experiment - nuclear OXPHOS structural subunits (median effect +2.64 vs global median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=1.3e-4), TCA/carbon enzymes (MDH1, OGDH), and mitochondrial import/carrier components (TOMM22, TIMM44, SLC25A5, SLC25A46).", "Step 2 (measured abundance): In the same list, four of the six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are at the low tail (MT-ATP6 4.5th, MT-CYB 9.4th, MT-ND4 13.7th, MT-CO2 18.5th percentile of all measured gene effects), giving an mtDNA-encoded median at the 15.8th percentile (permutation p~0.014). MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 are the exception and lie near the middle of the distribution.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck, not measured): Because each of complexes I, III, IV and V requires mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits, we infer that the supply of these cores, not the supply of nuclear-encoded subunits, sets the ceiling on holoenzyme assembly in APOE4 cells; nuclear subunit input therefore exceeds usable core capacity.", "Step 4 (inferred compensatory response): The coordinated elevation of mitochondrial translation-elongation, ribosome-recycling, RNA-maturation and inner-membrane insertase transcripts (TUFM 97.4th, MTRES1 97.4th, OXA1L 93.4th, MRRF 76.4th, MTPAP 75.5th, GFM2 70.4th percentile; set median +3.48, p=6.8e-3) is interpreted as a retrograde attempt to raise output from the limiting mtDNA-encoded pool; it is an abundance measurement, not a measurement of translation rate.", "Step 5 (inferred flux/quality-control consequence): Unassembled or misassembled nuclear subunits and the mitochondria carrying them are inferred to be routed to autophagic-lysosomal degradation, consistent with elevated mitochondrial chaperone/stress transcripts (HSPA9, PRDX3, DDIT3, FIS1) rather than with a proportional increase in respiratory output.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, downstream load): The lysosomal catabolic arm is coordinately induced above background (lysosomal hydrolase set median +2.40, p=6e-3; GBA 97.9th, HEXA 95.6th, SMPD1 95.4th, CTSB 94.9th percentile, with TFEB at the 69th percentile), which we interpret as increased degradative load created by steps 3-5, superimposed on the known APOE4 lipid-handling phenotype (APOE, TREM2, ABCA7, SOAT1 all modestly up).", "Step 7 (predicted phenotype): The net inferred state is increased mitochondrial mass and biogenesis signalling with reduced assembled-complex-specific coupled respiration and chronic lysosomal burden, distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 microglia at baseline without any exogenous stimulus."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits OXPHOS complex assembly in APOE4 microglia and shifts catabolic load onto the lysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24816305431451463, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13804571770382124, "cosine_similarity": 0.2517636908489851, "direction_accuracy": 0.22491909385113268, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6263980582524271, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24816305431451463, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13804571770382124, "cosine_similarity": 0.2517636908489851, "direction_accuracy": 0.22491909385113268, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6263980582524271, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.4473845, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 343}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_118", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so absence of ASAH1, PSAP, GALC, NEU1, GLB1 and CTSA means 'no evidence of differential expression at the applied threshold', not measured constancy; the inferred imbalance rests on this weaker reading.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only the sign and the rank of effects relative to the other differentially expressed rows are used.", "Transcript increases translate into some increase in the corresponding lysosomal enzyme activity; no enzyme-activity, acidification or lipid measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous positional measurements, never as identified proteins.", "The global positive shift of the RNA list (about 77% of rows positive, median effect about +1.46) is at least partly technical/selection-driven, so all pathway claims are made relative to the other differentially expressed rows rather than to zero.", "Astrocyte co-culture, replicate number and any ambient-RNA correction are not documented in the supplied metadata; genotype effects are assumed not to be confounded by differing culture composition.", "APOE4-dependent lipid cargo delivery is background knowledge (UNVERIFIED, literature retrieval disabled) and is not evidenced by the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional induction of the acid hydrolases that generate ceramide from sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GLA, GBA2) together with v-ATPase/CLEAR-network transcripts, while the ceramide-consuming step (acid ceramidase/saposin arm) is not represented among the differentially expressed rows. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node in APOE4 microglia is lysosomal ceramide disposal, not sphingolipid de novo synthesis: lumenal ceramide/glycosphingolipid intermediates build up, and sphingoid base is shunted into salvage re-acylation and S1P-lyase disposal (CERS4/CERS6, CERK, SPNS1, SGPL1), which in turn remodels late-endosome/lysosome membranes and their sorting machinery (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, AP5M1, ARL8B). All statements about lipid pools, enzyme activity, flux and localisation are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia should show higher lysosome-associated ceramide and hexosylceramide/GM3-series glycosphingolipid per cell despite the higher hydrolase transcripts; if ceramide and glycosphingolipid levels are equal or lower in APOE4, the ceramide-node bottleneck is falsified.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: limiting substrate influx into the lysosomal sphingolipid arm with a glucosylceramide-synthase inhibitor (eliglustat/PPMP) should, in APOE4 but not APOE3, normalise the elevated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H) and reduce lysosomal ceramide, i.e. a genotype x drug interaction; if APOE3 responds equally, or APOE4 hydrolase transcripts are unchanged, the compensatory-induction step fails.", "Restoring the consuming step - acid-ceramidase or prosaposin supplementation/overexpression - should reduce lysosomal ceramide and lower the hydrolase transcript programme in APOE4 more than in APOE3; no genotype-selective effect would weaken step 3.", "Pharmacological stress of the same node (conduritol-B-epoxide against GBA, or low-dose bafilomycin) should produce a larger increase in undegraded glycosphingolipid and a larger loss of cargo clearance in APOE4 than in APOE3 (reduced spare degradative capacity); equal sensitivity of both genotypes would argue the pathway is not capacity-limited in APOE4.", "TFEB knockdown should abolish the coordinated hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation; if lysosomal ceramide and glycosphingolipid load are unchanged by that knockdown, the induction is not a compensatory response to substrate load and steps 2-3 are weakened.", "ALTERNATIVE-DRIVER TEST: if partial OXPHOS inhibition (oligomycin) in APOE3 microglia reproduces the lysosomal sphingolipid-hydrolase transcript signature, the oxidative-metabolism arm is upstream and the lysosomal bottleneck is demoted from primary.", "Quantitative western blotting or targeted proteomics of GBA, HEXA/B and SMPD1 (unambiguous, unlike the 2-D spots) should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 mature enzyme; if mature enzyme protein is unchanged or lower while transcripts are high, the transcript-to-activity assumption fails and the mechanism must be restated as a translation/maturation block."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_118", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4-dependent handling of lipoprotein/membrane cargo increases delivery of sphingomyelin- and glycosphingolipid-rich material to the microglial endolysosome (INFERRED; no lipid or uptake measurement is supplied; consistent with but not proven by the higher lipoprotein-receptor and APOE-pathway transcripts gene:SCARB1, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE).", "The cells respond with a CLEAR-type transcriptional programme: transcripts for lysosomal acid hydrolases and for v-ATPase subunits rise (MEASURED RNA: gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:TFEB, gene:MITF). Increased hydrolase activity and increased acidification are INFERRED, not measured.", "Within the sphingolipid arm this induction is asymmetric: the enzymes that produce ceramide are up, whereas the ceramide-consuming/cofactor step (ASAH1, PSAP, GALC, NEU1, GLB1, CTSA) does not appear among the supplied differential-expression rows. We therefore INFER a stoichiometric imbalance at the ceramide -\u003e sphingosine step and net lumenal accumulation of ceramide and of hexosyl-/ganglio-series intermediates (UNMEASURED pool).", "Sphingoid base and ceramide that do reach the cytosolic leaflet are handled by salvage and disposal rather than by de novo synthesis: transcripts for lysosomal sphingosine/lysolipid export (gene:SPNS1), ceramide re-synthesis (gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6), ceramide phosphorylation (gene:CERK), S1P degradation (gene:SGPL1) and glycolipid transfer (gene:GLTP) are increased, while head-group remodelling shifts (gene:ST3GAL5 up, gene:B4GALT5 down). Flux direction is INFERRED.", "Ceramide/glycosphingolipid enrichment of late-endosome and lysosome membranes changes their fusion and retrieval behaviour; transcripts for late-endosomal identity and retrieval/positioning machinery are co-elevated (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1, gene:ARL8B). Altered localisation and trafficking rates are INFERRED, not observed.", "Consistent with a hydrolysis/acidification-limited state rather than a simple 'more lysosomes' state, hydrolase protein spots do not move coherently upward: cathepsin-candidate spots rise at some positions and fall at others (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down) and a v-ATPase-candidate spot falls (protein_spot:064), which we INTERPRET as redistribution of proteoforms/processing states. Spot identities are ambiguous (multiple candidate genes per spot).", "The degradative programme is energetically supported by a concurrent increase in oxidative-metabolism transcripts; this is treated here as a permissive co-arm and an alternative primary driver, not as proven downstream of the lysosomal change."], "title": "Ceramide-node imbalance: APOE4 microglia induce lysosomal sphingolipid-cleaving hydrolases without matched ceramide-consuming capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0710777978805893, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09269441325885455, "cosine_similarity": 0.2474172004525188, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_118", "mean_absolute_error": 0.63542071197411, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0710777978805893, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09269441325885455, "cosine_similarity": 0.2474172004525188, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "mean_absolute_error": 0.63542071197411, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.95121725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 344}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_086", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (77% positive, mean +1.39 in an unspecified logarithm base); we therefore interpret only relative position within this list, assuming that rank within the list is informative even though absolute fold changes may be inflated by normalization or composition effects.", "Transcript abundance of hydrolases and lipogenic enzymes is assumed to track, at least monotonically, enzyme protein and catalytic capacity; no enzyme activity, lipid, lysosomal pH or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied.", "2D protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; spot changes are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration, and keratin-dominated spots are treated as likely contaminants.", "Measurements are attributed to microglia, although the culture also contains astrocytes and no purity or cell-type deconvolution information is supplied; replicate number is not supplied, so no independent statistical validation of the reported p-values was possible.", "The mock-treatment comparison is assumed to reflect a steady-state genotype difference rather than a transient handling effect; direction of causality between lysosomal load and the lipogenic program is assumed but not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, above-background elevation of lipid-uptake and acid-hydrolase transcripts (SCARB1, GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, CTSB, CTSK, CTSD, DPP7, RAB7A, TFEB) together with a selectively elevated SREBF1-SCD lipogenic arm (SREBF1, SCD, MGLL, DGAT1, ACAT2), while sterol-handling and receptor transcripts (SREBF2, SOAT1, NPC2, APOE, LDLR, CD36, TREM2) and canonical interferon and NF-kB/chemokine genes sit at or below the global positive shift of this differential-expression list; we propose that increased endolysosomal lipid influx and hydrolysis in APOE4 makes the capacity to desaturate and esterify liberated fatty acids (SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty acid synthesis feeding neutral-lipid droplets) the rate-limiting disposal step, producing a lipid-storage/lysosome-loaded phenotype rather than an inflammatory or interferon-activated one. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) in mock-treated isogenic microglia should produce a genotype x drug interaction, with APOE4 showing a larger loss of BODIPY-positive neutral lipid droplets, a larger rise in saturated:monounsaturated fatty-acid ratio, and a larger induction of lysosomal/ER stress readouts than APOE3. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond identically (no interaction), the proposed SCD bottleneck is weakened.", "Lipid-load challenge: loading with LDL, oxLDL or myelin debris should give APOE4 microglia greater LAMP1-positive lipid and droplet accumulation with slower clearance than APOE3; SCARB1 knockdown or blockade should normalize the difference. Equal accumulation and clearance would weaken step 1.", "Hydrolytic capacity: APOE4 microglia should show higher lysosomal enzyme activity or substrate turnover (DQ-BSA dequenching, GBA/HEXA/GAA activity assays, cathepsin B activity) than APOE3 under mock conditions. If hydrolase activity is unchanged or lower despite the transcript differences, step 2 is falsified.", "Negative prediction against the inflammatory/interferon alternative: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade should not normalize the lipid-droplet or lysosomal phenotype, and secreted CXCL10, IL6, IL1B and ISG protein levels should not be higher in APOE4 under mock. Detection of an APOE4-selective interferon or NF-kB secretome that precedes and drives the lipid changes would falsify the choice of bottleneck.", "Ordering prediction: acute pharmacological lysosomal inhibition (bafilomycin A1 or cathepsin inhibition) should reduce, not increase, the APOE4-selective SREBF1/SCD transcript elevation, indicating that lysosomal hydrolysis lies upstream of the lipogenic arm. If SREBF1/SCD elevation persists or increases when lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked, the proposed upstream-to-downstream order is wrong."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 raises transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and late-endosomal delivery (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:RAB7A +2.7), which we infer increases the rate of lipid entry into the endolysosomal compartment; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred capacity): A coherent block of acid-hydrolase and lysosome-biogenesis transcripts is elevated far above the list-wide shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD, gene:DPP7, gene:TFEB; set mean +3.8 versus list mean +1.4, permutation p=2e-4), consistent with increased hydrolytic capacity and a TFEB-type lysosomal program; enzyme activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Hydrolysis of ingested lipoprotein and membrane lipids liberates free fatty acids, sphingolipid backbones and unesterified sterol inside the lysosome. This intracellular lipid pool is not measured in the supplied data and is asserted as an inference, not an observation.", "Step 4 (measured RNA; inferred routing): The disposal route that is selectively raised is the SREBF1-SCD lipogenic/esterification arm (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:MGLL +4.0, gene:DGAT1, gene:ACAT2, gene:FABP5), whereas the sterol-export/sterol-synthesis-sensing arm is not raised relative to background (gene:SREBF2 +1.1, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:NPC2 +1.2, gene:APOE +1.2, gene:LDLR +1.5). We infer preferential routing of liberated fatty acids into monounsaturated fatty acids and neutral lipid droplets rather than sterol-driven efflux.", "Step 5 (bottleneck): Because desaturation/esterification capacity (SCD step) is finite, it becomes the rate-limiting node: when lysosomal hydrolytic input exceeds it, saturated fatty acid and unesterified sterol accumulate in lysosomal and ER membranes, sustaining lysosomal load and further TFEB-type hydrolase transcription as a feed-forward loop.", "Step 6 (alternative excluded on present evidence): The same cells show no interferon signature (only 3 of 82 canonical interferon/antiviral genes appear in the list, mean +1.3, i.e. at background) and no enrichment of NF-kB/chemokine genes (set mean +1.2, permutation p not significant, with gene:TNFAIP3, gene:RELB and gene:CCL4 negative), so we reject inflammatory/interferon activation as the primary differentiator; elevated gene:ANXA1 and protein spots whose candidate lists include ANXA1 are compatible with a non-inflammatory, resolution/efferocytosis-leaning state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a lysosomal lipid-catabolism state whose bottleneck is SREBF1/SCD-dependent desaturation and neutral-lipid storage, not interferon or NF-kB activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1451925562160765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08352921142569289, "cosine_similarity": 0.24655975836401972, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_086", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6292135922330097, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1451925562160765, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08352921142569289, "cosine_similarity": 0.24655975836401972, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6292135922330097, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9172865, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 345}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_099", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects use an unspecified logarithm base and come from a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; module direction, not magnitude, is treated as the interpretable quantity and the 77% positive background is used as the null.", "Transcript changes are taken as proxies for protein pools only where stated; RhoGDI1 protein level, the RhoGDI1:Rac stoichiometry, Rac-GTP loading, cup formation, phagosome closure and lysosomal activity were all inferred, not measured.", "Genes absent from the list (RAC1, CDC42, ACTR2/ACTR3, ITGAM, ITGB2, TYROBP) are treated as unmeasured, not unchanged; the mechanism assumes their protein pools are not raised enough to offset the inferred RhoGDI1 excess.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified, so no spot is used as evidence for a specific protein; spot-level and RNA-level effects are uncorrelated here (Spearman -0.06, p = 0.60).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and replicate structure is not supplied, so genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous or under-dispersed; the very large adjusted p-values suggest cell-level rather than replicate-level statistics.", "Global normalisation of a strongly up-shifted list can push abundant transcripts such as ACTB and MYH9 negative, so the actomyosin decreases are assumed to be at least partly genuine rather than purely compositional."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally expand the cargo-recognition (surface uptake receptors), endocytic coat/sorting and lysosomal-degradative modules almost unanimously, while the Rac1/Arp2/3-actomyosin module that executes particle engulfment is not co-upregulated and is instead dominated by a very large increase in the Rho-GDP-dissociation inhibitor transcript ARHGDIA together with decreases in hematopoietic Rac-pathway and contractile transcripts (RAC2, ARHGDIB, DOCK8, ARHGAP30, PAK2, PIK3CB, MYH9, ACTB, MYO1F). We propose that reduced availability of membrane-bound, GTP-loaded Rac at nascent phagocytic cups is the primary bottleneck, so APOE4 microglia bind and endocytose soluble/lipoprotein cargo at least as well as APOE3 but internalize large particulate cargo less efficiently per cell, while the downstream lysosomal and mitochondrial oxidative capacity they build up remains under-used for particulate substrate. Causality is not established by these data; this is a proposed, testable chain.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo test: in the same mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, per-cell internalisation of large particulate cargo (2-4 um pHrodo beads, pHrodo myelin, synaptosomes; 30-60 min, with 4 C surface-binding and cytochalasin-D controls) will be at least 25% lower in APOE4, while 4 C surface binding and uptake of soluble or lipoprotein cargo (10 kDa dextran, DiI-AcLDL) will be equal or higher. If particulate and soluble uptake are reduced together, or particulate uptake is unchanged or increased, the actin-engulfment bottleneck is wrong and a receptor- or lysosome-level explanation should be preferred.", "Node test: PAK-PBD pull-down or Rac-FRET will show lower active Rac-GTP and fewer F-actin-positive phagocytic cups in APOE4 despite equal or higher total Rac1 and RhoGDI1-bound Rac in the cytosolic fraction. Equal Rac-GTP and equal cup counts would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue and specificity: ARHGDIA knockdown, or expression of a Rac1 fast-cycling or CA allele, will restore APOE4 particulate uptake toward APOE3 without raising lysosomal hydrolase activity (DQ-BSA, Magic Red), whereas TFEB overexpression will raise degradative activity without restoring particulate uptake. Failure of ARHGDIA knockdown to rescue uptake would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Occlusion test: blebbistatin or Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) will collapse the APOE4-APOE3 particulate-uptake difference (no genotype-by-drug interaction). A preserved genotype difference under these inhibitors would indicate the limiting step is upstream of actomyosin.", "Downstream-capacity test: lysosomal acidification and cathepsin activity per cell will be equal or higher in APOE4 (consistent with the expanded degradative arm) even where particulate uptake is lower. Lower lysosomal activity in APOE4 would refute the uncoupling claim and favour a degradative-failure model instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred surface pool): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for cargo-recognition receptors and opsonins nearly unanimously (24/25 in a pre-specified receptor set positive; ITGA6, SCARB1, ITGB1, MERTK, GAS6, MFGE8, CD36, MRC1, TREM2), which we infer increases surface cargo-binding capacity; surface protein levels were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Endocytic coat/sorting and endolysosomal transcripts rise in parallel (AP5M1, DNM2, SNX3, RAB7A, TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GAA, GBA, ATP6V1H; 24/26 and 14/15 positive in the pre-specified sets), consistent with an expanded clathrin/sorting and acidic-degradative compartment; organelle number, pH and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, measured RNA, inferred activity): The actin-engulfment executor module does not follow this coordinated rise (pre-specified actin/Rac union 18/29 positive versus a 77% positive background, mean +0.23 versus +1.39). ARHGDIA is the third-largest positive change in the whole list while ARHGDIB, RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGAP30, PAK2, PIK3CB, MYH9, ACTB and MYO1F are negative. We infer, but did not measure, that a higher RhoGDI1-to-Rac ratio sequesters Rho-family GTPases in the cytosol and lowers the pool of prenylated, membrane-delivered Rac-GTP available at forming cups.", "Step 4 (inferred flux and localization): With cargo binding and degradative capacity up but Rac-GTP-driven actin polymerisation and MYH9-dependent contractility limited, phagocytic cup extension and closure become the slow step, so particulate internalisation per cell falls while receptor-mediated endocytosis of soluble and lipoprotein cargo, which is less dependent on the Rac/actomyosin executor, is preserved or increased.", "Step 5 (consequence, inferred): Flux is redirected toward the endocytic/lipoprotein route feeding an expanded lysosome, consistent with coordinate increases in lipid-handling and mitochondrial oxidative transcripts (APOE, ABCA7, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1; 38/38 OXPHOS transcripts positive), i.e. degradative and oxidative capacity is built while particulate clearance remains constrained. Lipid, ATP and oxygen-consumption pools were not measured here."], "title": "RhoGDI-constrained Rac/actomyosin engulfment is the rate-limiting step that uncouples an expanded uptake-receptor and endolysosomal program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0827456337924159, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1451945931693888, "cosine_similarity": 0.24541069858760983, "direction_accuracy": 0.0889967637540453, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_099", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6210614886731392, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0827456337924159, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1451945931693888, "cosine_similarity": 0.24541069858760983, "direction_accuracy": 0.0889967637540453, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6210614886731392, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6381795, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 346}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_067", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive, median effect +1.46 on an unspecified logarithm base); genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged, so all sign enrichments were judged against the 77.1% positive background and remain descriptive, not formal enrichment tests (genes within a program are not independent).", "Transcript increases are assumed to translate at least partly into more lysosomal, mitochondrial and lipogenic machinery; this is not demonstrated here and is the weakest link in the chain.", "Protein spots (92, log2 scale) carry 2-6 candidate identities each; no spot is treated as evidence for an individual protein. Cathepsin-containing spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:055 +0.58, protein_spot:057 +0.58, protein_spot:027 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38), which we read as compatibility with proteoform redistribution in an expanded lysosome, not as confirmation of increased hydrolase content.", "Lipid substrate is assumed to be supplied largely by the astrocyte co-culture and cell debris; no lipidomic, lipid-droplet, cholesterol, hydrolase-activity, oxygen-consumption or acetyl-CoA measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Effects are APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 under mock treatment only; nothing here reports behaviour under a lipid, myelin, amyloid or inflammatory challenge, and no reduced reserve under challenge is claimed.", "Causality and directionality among uptake, lysosomal expansion, oxidation and SREBP activation are inferred from co-directional abundance changes and cannot be established from this cross-sectional comparison."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, the transcriptional data describe a coordinated cell-state shift in which raised lipid/debris uptake-receptor transcripts accompany a coordinately expanded endolysosomal-degradative transcriptional program, a uniformly raised nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation and TCA/mitochondrial-carrier program, and an activated SREBP sterol/desaturation program; the most parsimonious reading is increased routing of internalised lipid through lysosomal catabolism into mitochondrial oxidation and acetyl-CoA-derived sterol/fatty-acid resynthesis (an adaptive throughput increase), not a discrete rate-limiting defect. Glycerolipid/acyl-chain remodelling enzymes are raised no more than the strongly positive selected-list background (13/16 positive vs 77.1% background positive, binomial p=0.48) and are therefore assigned as a downstream esterification consequence, so the assigned membrane-remodelling focus is rejected as the primary driver. All effects are measured abundances (RNA log fold change of unspecified base; protein-spot log2); every flux, enzyme activity, localisation and causal direction below is inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective state test in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: LAMP1/LysoTracker volume, neutral-lipid (BODIPY 493/503) content, basal and maximal oxygen consumption rate, and lysosomal hydrolase activity (Magic Red cathepsin B, fluorogenic GBA/HEXA substrates) should all be higher in APOE4. If hydrolase activity and oxygen consumption are equal to or lower than APOE3 despite the transcript increases, the increased-throughput mechanism is wrong and the failed-compensation alternative (transcriptional response to an unmet degradative demand) is favoured.", "Discriminating perturbation (lysosome-to-SREBP routing): 6-24 h of v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or lysosomal acid lipase inhibition (lalistat) should reduce SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR24, SCD) and 13C-acetate/glucose incorporation into sterol and phosphatidylcholine proportionally more in APOE4 than APOE3, with greater accumulation of undigested neutral lipid. Equal fractional responses in the two genotypes would weaken step 4-5 of the mechanism.", "Ordering test: SREBP inhibition (fatostatin) or SCD inhibition should reduce APOE4-selective membrane/lipid-droplet expansion and phagocytic capacity without lowering the lysosomal transcript module (TFEB, ATP6V1H, CTSB, HEXA); if the lysosomal module falls in parallel, the proposed upstream-to-downstream order is wrong.", "Uptake test: blocking cargo delivery (SCARB1/CD36 blockade or MERTK inhibition, or lipid-depleted medium) should lower ATP6V/hydrolase and SREBP transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the APOE4 lysosomal signature under lipid-depleted conditions would indicate a cell-intrinsic transcriptional set point rather than substrate-driven routing.", "Mitochondrial specificity: the mechanism predicts higher mitochondrial mass and coupled respiration in APOE4. Observing raised nuclear OXPHOS protein with unchanged or reduced respiration plus further loss of mtDNA-encoded transcripts (already gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32) would instead support mitonuclear imbalance/integrated-stress signalling (consistent with gene:DDIT3 +2.79) and weaken step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (uptake, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia transcribe more lipid/debris uptake and adhesion machinery than isogenic APOE3 (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ITGA6 +15.46, gene:ITGB1 +6.31, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:ITGAX +1.69, gene:FCGR1B, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24; 16/16 represented members positive, binomial p=0.016 vs the 77.1% positive background), which we interpret as increased delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (degradative compartment expansion): a TFEB-type endolysosomal program is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:CLN3, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, with hydrolases gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSH; 25/26 positive, binomial p=0.010; the single exception gene:CTSS -5.57), plus ESCRT/retromer/autophagy support (gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:VPS37B +3.86, gene:VPS35L, gene:ATG4D, gene:ATG9A, gene:PIK3C3); this is transcript-level capacity, not measured hydrolase activity.", "Step 3 (catabolic products oxidised): every represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit is raised (36/36 positive, binomial p=8.5e-5; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36) together with TCA and mitochondrial carriers (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56) and import machinery (gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44), consistent with increased oxidative and anaplerotic capacity rather than a block.", "Step 4 (acetyl-CoA supply to anabolism, inferred): raised citrate carrier (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47) and gene:ACSS2 +2.93 are proposed to increase cytosolic acetyl-CoA available for lipid synthesis.", "Step 5 (SREBP-dependent resynthesis): the sterol/desaturation program is uniformly higher (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:MYLIP +1.28, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59; 14/14 positive, binomial p=0.026), which we interpret as replacement of membrane sterol and monounsaturated acyl chains consumed by the expanded endolysosomal/phagocytic membrane.", "Step 6 (esterification as follower, focus rejected): esterification/remodelling enzymes are available and mostly raised (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04) but with clear exceptions (gene:GPAT3 -2.23, gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11) and no sign enrichment over background (13/16, p=0.48); acyl-chain remodelling is therefore modelled as capacity that follows steps 1-5, not as the initiating lesion.", "Step 7 (state read-out): the resulting state is a lipid-laden, degradation- and oxidation-biased microglial phenotype (gene:LGALS3 +2.37, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:NLRP3 +1.09) with reduced motility/homeostatic transcripts (gene:MYH9 -6.38, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:CORO2A -3.70, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.19, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.89), i.e. resources shifted from migration toward cargo processing."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a high-throughput uptake-to-lysosome-to-oxidation state that drives SREBP-dependent lipid resynthesis, with acyl-chain/glycerolipid enzymes as followers rather than drivers"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34659195805486837, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1774610828090332, "cosine_similarity": 0.24410849616170216, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6333139158576051, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34659195805486837, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1774610828090332, "cosine_similarity": 0.24410849616170216, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6333139158576051, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.45760425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 92}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_018", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all statements are made relative to the list-internal distribution (median effect +1.46, 77% positive), not to an unbiased zero baseline.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks/percentiles within the list are used for pathway comparisons.", "Transcript changes are assumed to translate, at least partially, into enzyme protein and catalytic activity at the lysosome; this is an inference and is directly contradicted at face value by the flat-to-lower lysosomal-hydrolase-containing protein spots.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, ambiguous evidence.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, flux, imaging or localization measurement is supplied; ceramide, hexosylceramide, sphingomyelin and sphingosine pools are inferred, never observed.", "Absence of a gene (e.g. ASAH1, UGCG, SPTLC1/2, PSAP, NPC1) from the rows means 'not reported', not 'unchanged'.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated at one timepoint (day 30) in microglia-astrocyte co-culture, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous via astrocytes.", "Causality is not established by these observational genotype-contrast data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) carry a coordinately elevated transcript program for the upper, ceramide-generating steps of lysosomal sphingolipid catabolism (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, with cofactor/transport genes GM2A, NPC2, SCARB2, GLTP) embedded in a broader lysosomal-acidification/hydrolase program, while the ceramide-disposal steps are not co-elevated (SGPL1 rises only to the 29th percentile of this list's shift; ASAH1, SPHK1/2, ACER3 are absent from the supplied rows) and salvage re-acylation genes (CERS4, CERS6, KDSR) are up. We hypothesise that this catabolism-skewed, exit-limited configuration raises lysosomal ceramide/hexosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin and re-routes sphingoid backbones into complex sphingolipids rather than terminal degradation, and that ceramide disposal capacity - not de novo serine-palmitoyltransferase flux - is the rate-limiting node. The assigned focus is only partly supported: sphingolipid turnover is supported, de novo synthesis and a sphingolipid-specific vesicular-routing defect are not.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of the same APOE4 vs APOE3 mock cultures should show a higher ceramide and hexosylceramide mole fraction and a lower sphingomyelin:ceramide ratio in APOE4, with total sphingolipid changed less than the individual species ratios. If ceramide and hexosylceramide are unchanged or lower, or if sphingomyelin rises relative to ceramide, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: raising ceramide-exit capacity in APOE4 cells (ASAH1 overexpression, or acid-ceramidase-directed rescue) should lower lysosomal ceramide, restore lysosomal degradative throughput (DQ-BSA and BODIPY-LacCer/myelin-debris clearance) and partially normalise the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program, without lowering SCARB1/CD36-dependent lipid uptake. If ASAH1 gain-of-function lowers ceramide but leaves degradative throughput and the lysosomal transcript program unchanged, the ceramide-exit bottleneck is wrong and a general lysosome-biogenesis or upstream-uptake mechanism is favoured.", "Blocking an upper step should move the phenotype in the opposite direction: acid sphingomyelinase inhibition (FIASMA, or SMPD1 knockdown) in APOE4 should lower ceramide and blunt the lysosomal transcript program while raising sphingomyelin; if SMPD1 loss raises ceramide or does not change it, step 2 is wrong.", "Enzyme-activity assays (4MU-glucoside for GBA, 4MU-GlcNAc for HEXA/B, ASM assay, acid ceramidase assay) should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 activity for GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 but no proportional increase in acid ceramidase activity. If acid ceramidase activity scales with the GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 increase, the exit-limitation claim fails; if none of the hydrolase activities is increased despite the transcript rise, the program is compensatory rather than executed and steps 2-5 must be reframed as substrate overload with unexecuted transcription.", "Specificity control: pharmacological GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) in APOE3 cells should raise glucosylceramide but should not reproduce the full APOE4 ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio shift; if it fully phenocopies the APOE4 lipid profile, the mechanism collapses to a single-enzyme glucocerebrosidase effect rather than the proposed exit-limited configuration.", "Negative/alternative-discriminating prediction: inhibiting de novo sphingolipid synthesis (myriocin, serine palmitoyltransferase) should NOT normalise the APOE4-APOE3 ceramide difference, because the de novo arm is not implicated. If myriocin abolishes the difference, the de novo arm rather than turnover is the driver and this hypothesis is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred substrate load): APOE4 cells show higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein-scavenging receptors and sterol/lipid-handling genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). We infer, but do not measure, an increased delivery of membrane- and lipoprotein-derived sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred enzyme activity): The ceramide-generating lysosomal hydrolases are among the most strongly and most significantly shifted rows (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA) together with cofactor/lipid-presentation genes (gene:GM2A, gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:GLTP) and general acidification/proteolysis genes (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA). Enzyme activity, protein amount and localization are inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck, partly inferred from absence): The exit route that consumes ceramide is not scaled with these upper steps. gene:SGPL1 rises far less than the list-wide shift, and no observation for acid ceramidase, sphingosine kinases or alkaline ceramidases is supplied; we therefore treat ceramide/sphingosine disposal capacity as the rate-limiting node and explicitly flag it as unmeasured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux direction): Salvage/re-acylation and headgroup-transfer genes are elevated (gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERK, gene:ST3GAL5, gene:GLTP) while the de novo arm is unmeasured, so the sphingoid backbone released in the lysosome is predicted to be recycled into ceramide and complex glycosphingolipids rather than cleared.", "Step 5 (inferred lipid state): The net predicted lipid consequence is a higher ceramide + hexosylceramide fraction and a lower sphingomyelin:ceramide ratio in APOE4 versus APOE3, i.e. a membrane-order and lysosome-membrane change, not a simple increase in total sphingolipid.", "Step 6 (inferred functional consequence, direction not established): Ceramide-enriched late endosome/lysosome membranes are predicted to lower per-lysosome degradative throughput, which is consistent with the compensatory character of the lysosomal transcript program and with protein-level evidence that hydrolase abundance does not follow the transcripts (protein_spot:067, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069). Whether ceramide causes the lysosomal transcript program or follows it is not resolved by these data."], "title": "Catabolism-skewed lysosomal sphingolipid turnover in APOE4 microglia: ceramide exit, not de novo synthesis, is the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22279658826570173, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13273457900807353, "cosine_similarity": 0.2419926975326843, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6608899676375405, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22279658826570173, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13273457900807353, "cosine_similarity": 0.2419926975326843, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6608899676375405, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73206, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 347}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Effect signs follow the supplied convention (positive = higher in APOE4 than APOE3); the RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported, so RNA and protein (log2) magnitudes are not directly comparable.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are relative to the other selected rows (list median +1.46, 77% positive), not to a genome-wide background, and absent genes (HK1, PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, G6PD, CS, MDH2, PDHA1, MPC1, CPT1A) are missing rather than unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance; enzyme activity, metabolite pools, flux, PDH phosphorylation and mitochondrial membrane potential were not measured and are inferred only.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as evidence for a specific metabolic enzyme here.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences (for example S100B +6.00) may reflect differing astrocyte contamination or ambient RNA rather than microglia-intrinsic biology; biological replicate number was not supplied, so the extremely small adjusted p-values may be inflated by pseudo-replication across cells.", "The genotype comparison is isogenic, so differences are attributed to APOE genotype rather than donor background, but no causal manipulation is present in these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily at the glucose-commitment step: HK2/HK3 and PFKP transcripts are among the most strongly reduced measurements while glucose-transporter transcripts are not reduced, and the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2 together with PDH-associated (DLD, PDP1), TCA (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3B/G, SDHB, MDH1), malate-aspartate (GOT1, MDH1), anaplerotic (GLS, GLUD1) and citrate-export (SLC25A1) transcripts are coordinately elevated far above the strong global upward shift of this selected gene list. We therefore hypothesise that APOE4 microglia carry a transcriptional program that constrains committed glycolytic flux at hexokinase and shifts carbon oxidation to mitochondrial pyruvate and amino-acid entry, reducing glycolytic reserve; this remains a correlational, RNA-level inference, and causality has not been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) in mock-treated APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should suppress basal and maximal oxygen consumption proportionally more in APOE4, and APOE4 should fail to compensate with the glycolytic (ECAR) rise seen in APOE3. If UK5099 lowers OCR equally in both genotypes, or if APOE4 shows an equal or larger compensatory ECAR increase, the MPC-dependence step is wrong.", "Extracellular flux profiling should show lower basal ECAR and, in particular, lower glycolytic capacity/reserve after oligomycin in APOE4 than APOE3, with unchanged or higher 2-deoxyglucose uptake. Equal or higher glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would falsify the hexokinase-bottleneck claim.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show reduced glucose-derived labelling of lactate and of citrate m+2 in APOE4, while U-13C5-glutamine tracing should show an increased fractional contribution to citrate m+4; if glucose-derived citrate labelling is unchanged or increased in APOE4, the bottleneck is not at glucose commitment.", "Direct assay of hexokinase activity and HK2 protein (immunoblot, unambiguous identification rather than 2D spots) should show lower activity in APOE4 lysates; equal total hexokinase activity, for example through HK1 compensation, would weaken the mechanism.", "Restoring HK2 expression in APOE4 microglia should raise ECAR and partially restore the LPS-induced glycolytic burst and cytokine induction toward APOE3 levels; no restoration of ECAR would weaken the causal ordering.", "Despite higher NDUF transcripts, blue-native in-gel complex I activity and assembled complex I/IV levels should not be proportionally higher in APOE4 and may be lower, reflecting the reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts; a proportional increase in assembled complex I activity would falsify the mitonuclear-imbalance step while leaving the glycolysis-commitment step intact.", "The pentose-phosphate arm should be functionally lower in APOE4: reduced 1-13C-glucose-derived CO2 release and lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio, with greater sensitivity to an oxidant challenge. Equal or higher PPP flux in APOE4 would contradict the predicted glucose-6-phosphate limitation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: HK2 (-3.67, adj p 7.7e-191, 3.6th percentile of this list), PFKP (-3.08) and HK3 (-1.12) transcripts are low in APOE4 while SLC2A1 (+2.37) and SLC2A3 (+3.73) transcripts are high; inferred (not measured): the capacity to phosphorylate imported glucose to glucose-6-phosphate, rather than glucose uptake itself, is the limiting step. HK1 was not measured, so total hexokinase pool and activity are unknown.", "Inferred consequence: reduced glucose-6-phosphate supply lowers committed glycolytic flux and its branch outputs; consistent with this, the non-oxidative and oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts TALDO1 (-2.32, adj p 1.6e-100) and PGD (-1.30) are also low, whereas glucose-6-phosphate-sparing glycogen synthesis transcripts GYS1 (+6.10) and UGP2 (+1.86) are high. NADPH output and lactate output were not measured.", "Measured: MPC2 (+7.98, 99th percentile), DLD (+5.54) and PDP1 (+3.00) transcripts are high; inferred: greater mitochondrial pyruvate import capacity and a more dephosphorylated (active) pyruvate-dehydrogenase state, directing residual pyruvate to acetyl-CoA rather than to lactate. PDH phosphorylation status and MPC flux were not measured.", "Measured: a coherent oxidative block is elevated well above the list-wide shift (mito-oxidative set mean +4.35 vs global mean +1.39, permutation p=1e-4): OGDH (+8.56), MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), ACO2 (+3.54), IDH3G (+3.94), IDH3B (+2.02), SDHB (+1.65), plus glutamine/glutamate anaplerosis (GLS +1.35, GLUD1 +3.17) and NNT (+2.88); inferred: APOE4 cells lean on mitochondrial substrate oxidation and malate-aspartate shuttling for ATP and redox balance.", "Measured: nuclear-encoded complex I subunits are coordinately elevated (21 NDUF genes, mean +2.99, permutation p=0.004) while most mtDNA-encoded core subunits measured are reduced (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 are exceptions); inferred: mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance means the elevated nuclear oxidative program need not translate into proportionally higher assembled respiratory-chain capacity. Complex assembly, membrane potential and respiration were not measured.", "Inferred net state: APOE4 microglia occupy a narrow metabolic envelope - low hexokinase-committed glycolysis with elevated but potentially assembly-limited oxidative machinery - together with an active citrate-export/lipogenic arm (SLC25A1 +4.47, ACSS2 +2.93, SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, ACAT2 +2.04, SOAT1 +1.25) that can consume mitochondrial citrate for lipid esterification. Predicted functional consequence: reduced glycolytic reserve and impaired ability to mount the rapid glycolytic burst that normally accompanies microglial activation, with increased dependence on MPC-mediated pyruvate and glutamine oxidation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose hexokinase-level glucose commitment and are transcriptionally rewired toward MPC2-dependent mitochondrial pyruvate/anaplerotic oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07268397149503378, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2615512303656196, "cosine_similarity": 0.2403859067384914, "direction_accuracy": 0.0970873786407767, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434304207119741, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07268397149503378, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2615512303656196, "cosine_similarity": 0.2403859067384914, "direction_accuracy": 0.0970873786407767, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434304207119741, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46243125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 348}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_096", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| \u003e= 1.0 in an unspecified logarithm base) and not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. ACLY, FASN, LIPA, PLIN2, ABCA1, most ISGs) means not reported, not measured-as-unchanged.", "The list is globally shifted upward (1705/2212 up, median +1.46), so only direction and within-list rank, not absolute magnitude, are used as evidence; the glycolysis/PPP decreases are treated as informative because they run against this shift.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, only as an inference, pathway flux; no metabolite, lipid, flux or droplet measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features (e.g. protein_spot:039 lists ALDOA, ARPC1B, GAPDH, ALDOC, KRT10); no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no spot is used as primary evidence.", "The two modalities may come from different assays/batches of the same APOE4-vs-APOE3 mock comparison; replicate numbers are 'not supplied in workbook', so uncertainty in both layers is under-quantified.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies extracellular lipoprotein/lipid; a lipid-free medium would change the balance between the uptake and de novo arms of the proposed mechanism."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a transcript pattern consistent with reduced glycolytic/pentose-phosphate carbon use and increased mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate handling plus lipid acquisition, feeding an SREBF1-driven esterification module in which SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA is the rate-limiting input for DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent neutral-lipid (triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester) droplet formation; the interferon/NF-kB inflammatory route is not supported as the differentiating mechanism in these data. Causality is not established: all statements about flux, esterification rate and droplet load are inferred from transcript abundance, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) in delipidated medium should abolish most of the APOE4-vs-APOE3 difference in BODIPY/LipidTOX neutral-lipid droplet area, and oleate add-back should restore it; if the APOE4 droplet excess persists under SCD inhibition with oleate withheld, the SCD/esterification bottleneck is wrong and an uptake- or clearance-limited mechanism is favoured.", "Lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show higher triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass with a shift toward 16:1/18:1 acyl chains; equal ester mass or a saturated-chain shift would weaken the mechanism.", "13C6-glucose or 13C-acetate tracing should show higher label incorporation into palmitate/oleate and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 despite lower glycolytic gene expression; equal or lower label flux into lipid would weaken the citrate/acetate-to-lipogenesis step.", "Combined DGAT1 + SOAT1 inhibition should equalise droplet load between genotypes while leaving SREBF1/SCD transcript differences intact; loss of the transcript difference or unchanged droplets would indicate the esterification step is not the controlling node.", "MPC inhibition (UK5099) or SLC25A1 blockade should reduce, not increase, APOE4 droplet load; an increase would falsify the proposed mitochondrial-carbon-to-lipid routing.", "Counter-focus test: type I interferon signalling should not be detectably elevated in APOE4 mock microglia (no increase in phospho-STAT1, ISG15/MX1/IFIT1 protein or a composite ISG score); a clear ISG elevation would show that the interferon axis, not lipid rerouting, differentiates the genotypes.", "If clearance rather than synthesis is limiting, LIPA/lysosomal acid lipase inhibition (lalistat) should enlarge droplets equally in both genotypes; a much larger APOE4-specific effect would favour a lysosomal-clearance bottleneck over the proposed SCD node."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: glycolytic and pentose-phosphate transcripts are lower in APOE4 (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) against a list in which 77% of genes are higher in APOE4; inferred: less glucose carbon is committed to lactate and to PPP-derived NADPH.", "Measured: mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate handling transcripts are higher (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72) together with gene:ACSS2 +2.93 and gene:ME1 +1.36; inferred: pyruvate/acetate carbon is preferentially routed to mitochondria and citrate/acetate export supplies a cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool with malic-enzyme NADPH (the ACLY step itself is not measured here).", "Measured: the lipogenic transcription-factor module and its targets are higher (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04); inferred: increased SREBP-1-dependent transcriptional drive on fatty-acid desaturation and on glycerolipid/sterol esterification.", "Bottleneck (inferred, not measured): SCD-generated oleoyl-CoA is the shared, rate-limiting substrate for DGAT1 (triacylglycerol) and SOAT1 (cholesteryl ester); its increased supply, not increased sterol synthesis (gene:HMGCS1 only +1.08, gene:SREBF2 +1.06), sets the rate of neutral-lipid ester formation in APOE4.", "Measured: lipid-acquisition receptors are higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28); inferred: increased delivery of exogenous sterol and fatty acid into the same esterification pool, adding to the endogenous route.", "Measured: a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript program is higher (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88); inferred: a compensatory catabolic response to increased lipid load rather than an independent driver; the lipolytic/efflux arm (LIPA, PLIN2, ACSL1, ABCA1/ABCG1) is not measured, so clearance capacity is unknown.", "Predicted cellular consequence (not measured here): APOE4 microglia carry a larger esterified neutral-lipid droplet pool than isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock conditions, with a shift of droplet composition toward monounsaturated triacylglycerol and cholesteryl oleate."], "title": "APOE4 microglia reroute carbon from glycolysis/PPP into an SREBF1-SCD esterification node, making monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply the bottleneck for neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24309529963445703, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20200198699067604, "cosine_similarity": 0.24017233776846686, "direction_accuracy": 0.21035598705501618, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_096", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6359514563106796, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24309529963445703, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20200198699067604, "cosine_similarity": 0.24017233776846686, "direction_accuracy": 0.21035598705501618, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6359514563106796, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.94106325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 349}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_029", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effect column (unspecified logarithm base, global mean +1.39 over 2212 selected differentially expressed rows) reflects genotype-associated expression differences and not only a normalisation/composition artefact; all set comparisons here are made against that shifted global background rather than against zero.", "The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list, so absence of a gene is uninformative and set means are conditional on selection.", "Transcript differences for the engulfment module translate at least partly into protein and, in turn, into Rho-GTPase activation and actomyosin mechanics; no GTP-loading, F-actin, or contractility measurement is supplied.", "2-D protein spots contain several candidate genes each (e.g. protein_spot:036 lists ACTR2, CAPG, ACTB, SERPINB1, KRT1), so no spot is treated as identifying a single protein; spot effects are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "The astrocyte co-culture contributes an unquantified fraction of the signal, and cell-state composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 cultures could generate part of the module-level shifts.", "No functional phagocytosis, lipid, imaging, or replicate-level data are supplied; the mechanism is a hypothesis about flux, not an observed flux."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, the APOE4 state is distinguished not by loss of cargo recognition or of lysosomal degradative capacity (both are transcriptionally higher than the global APOE4-vs-APOE3 shift) but by a selective transcriptional down-shift of the haematopoietic actin-remodelling module that executes phagocytic-cup extension and closure (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, MYO1F, PLEK, MYH9, ACTB, FAM49B) together with an extreme rise in the Rho-GTPase sequestering factor ARHGDIA. We hypothesise that this configuration makes actin-dependent internalization (post-binding, pre-phagosome closure) the rate-limiting step of cargo flux in APOE4 microglia, so that binding-competent, hydrolase-rich cells convert lipid acquisition from particle engulfment toward receptor-mediated soluble-lipoprotein uptake and de novo lipogenesis (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36, SREBF1, SCD, DGAT1, ACAT2, SOAT1), with the endolysosomal/hydrolase induction (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSK, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, ATP6V1H, TFEB, AP5M1, RAB7A) reflecting compensatory or independent endolysosomal expansion rather than a degradation defect. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are transcript and 2-D protein-spot abundances only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, RNAi/degron depletion of ARHGDIA, or expression of a RhoGDI-insensitive constitutively active RAC1/RAC2, should raise the internalized:bound ratio for pHrodo-labelled synaptosomes/myelin/beads toward APOE3 within hours, without increasing surface TREM2/CD36/MERTK or lysosomal hydrolase transcripts. If ARHGDIA depletion leaves the internalized:bound ratio unchanged while restoring Rac-GTP levels, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Binding-versus-internalization split (pH-quench or trypsin-strip assay): APOE4 should show equal or higher surface binding but a lower internalized fraction and fewer closed phagocytic cups (F-actin ring lifetime prolonged) than APOE3. Equal internalized fractions, or reduced binding rather than reduced internalization, would weaken the mechanism.", "Occlusion test: myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) should shift APOE3 toward the APOE4 uptake phenotype and produce a smaller incremental deficit in APOE4 (sub-additive dose-response). Fully additive, genotype-independent inhibition would argue the actomyosin step is not already limiting in APOE4.", "Degradation is not the bottleneck: once cargo is delivered intracellularly (e.g. by cargo-loaded liposome fusion or by bypassing engulfment with a soluble fluorogenic hydrolase substrate such as DQ-BSA or LysoSensor-based hydrolase assays), APOE4 should degrade cargo at least as fast as APOE3. Slower intracellular degradation in APOE4 would move the bottleneck downstream and falsify this hypothesis in favour of a lysosomal-dysfunction model.", "Lipid consequence: APOE4 neutral-lipid stores should be dominated by cholesteryl esters and MUFA-rich (SCD-product) species derived from soluble lipoprotein uptake and de novo synthesis, should be sensitive to SOAT1/DGAT1 or SCD inhibition, and should be relatively insensitive to blocking actin-dependent particle uptake (cytochalasin D). If APOE4 lipid excess is instead abolished by cytochalasin D to the same extent as in APOE3, particle uptake is still the dominant lipid route and the mechanism is weakened.", "Specificity control: the down-shifted module should be cytoskeleton-selective. Independent protein-level quantification should show reduced RAC2/DOCK8/MYH9 protein and normal-or-higher PTPRC, CSF1R, IRF8 and cathepsin/v-ATPase protein in APOE4. A uniform reduction of all myeloid proteins would favour a loss-of-microglial-identity or maturation-state explanation instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts encoding the myeloid-restricted Rho-GTPase/actin engulfment module are lower in APOE4 than the strongly positive global shift of this selected differential-expression list (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, MYO1F, PLEK, HCK; set mean -1.70 vs global +1.39, permutation p=0.0006), while non-cytoskeletal myeloid identity genes are not shifted (mean +0.42, p=0.14). Inferred: reduced steady-state RAC2/DOCK8-dependent GEF capacity at the plasma membrane; GTP-loading was not measured.", "Measured: ARHGDIA transcript is among the highest in the dataset (+10.61, 99.9th percentile) while ARHGDIB is negative. Inferred (not measured): a higher cytosolic RhoGDI1:Rho-GTPase buffering ratio that lowers the pool of membrane-deliverable, activatable RAC1/RAC2/CDC42; protein-level RhoGDI and GTPase loading are unmeasured pools.", "Measured: MYH9 (-6.38) and ACTB (-4.98) transcripts are in the bottom ~1.5% and the elongation/anti-capping factor VASP is low (-3.44), while severing/turnover factors CFL1, SSH1, TWF2 and Arp2/3 subunits ARPC1B/4/5 are positive. Inferred: a filament network biased toward short, capped, rapidly turned-over actin with reduced non-muscle myosin-IIA contractility, i.e. weaker pseudopod extension and phagocytic-cup closure; no F/G-actin ratio, cup imaging or contractility measurement is supplied.", "Inferred bottleneck: cargo that is bound at the surface is internalized less efficiently in APOE4. Recognition capacity is not obviously the limit, since receptor/opsonin transcripts are at or above the global shift (SCARB1 +8.22, ANXA1 +4.15, CD36, MERTK, TREM2, MRC1, C1QA/B/C, SIRPA), and degradative capacity is not obviously the limit, since lysosomal hydrolases are far above it (set mean +5.33, p=0.0001).", "Measured: soluble-lipid entry and lipogenic/esterification transcripts are elevated (SCARB1, LDLR, CD36, SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, ACAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, DHCR24) alongside endolysosomal expansion (TFEB, ATP6V1A/H, RAB7A, AP5M1, VPS26A, CHMP4B). Inferred flux consequence: lipid loading in APOE4 is shifted from particle-derived (phagocytic) input toward receptor-mediated/soluble and de novo routes, predicting cholesteryl-ester and MUFA-enriched neutral-lipid storage rather than membrane-lipid catabolites; no lipid species were measured here.", "Inferred systems consequence: a hydrolase-rich, contractility-poor microglial state that clears soluble ligands but accumulates uningested extracellular particulate cargo, providing a mechanism for the APOE4 phenotype under mock (unstimulated) conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are constrained at the actin-dependent internalization step: a RhoGDI-high / RAC2-DOCK8-myosin-II-low engulfment module limits particle uptake while recognition and endolysosomal degradative capacity are transcriptionally expanded"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2108056714544179, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19901550551904726, "cosine_similarity": 0.2380364152819062, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_029", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6187734627831715, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2108056714544179, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19901550551904726, "cosine_similarity": 0.2380364152819062, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6187734627831715, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.79242425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 350}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_067", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment is therefore judged only relative to the internal background of this list (global mean +1.39, 77% positive), and absence of a gene means it was not supplied, not that it is unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes reach |15|, so RNA effects are used as ranked, signed evidence and are not converted to fold changes or compared numerically with the log2 protein spots.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes; spot-level effects are treated as ambiguous, non-unique evidence about whether the hydrolase module is coordinately increased, and no individual protein is claimed to be measured.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a necessary but insufficient proxy for enzyme activity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, autophagic flux and every lipid species discussed here are inferred and were not measured in the supplied data.", "Positive effect means higher in APOE4; the comparison is isogenic, mock-treated, single timepoint (day 30), 2D microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so astrocyte cross-talk, replicate structure and dose dependence are unconstrained.", "The global upward RNA shift is assumed not to be entirely a normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-composition artifact; if it is, all absolute directions weaken and only relative enrichment survives."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase module (TFEB, MITF, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, NAGLU, GAA, MAN2B1, AGA, DPP7, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, SUMF1, SPNS1, ATP6V1A/1H/0C, ATP6AP1/2) together with higher transcripts for membrane- and lipoprotein-cargo uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, MERTK, ABCA7, APOE). We hypothesise that this reflects demand-driven compensation for a bottleneck at luminal hydrolysis of internalised sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo rather than an achieved increase in degradative flux, because 2-D spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases average only +0.17 log2 (15 up / 9 down) versus +0.35 for all spots while the same transcripts carry some of the largest positive RNA effects. Acyl-chain/glycerolipid remodeling genes are up only at the dataset-wide background rate and are treated as a downstream overflow route, not the bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: with cargo load matched (equal myelin or apoptotic-membrane feeding, or equal BODIPY-sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide dosing), per-cell fluorogenic activity of GBA (4-MU-beta-glucoside or LysoFQ-GBA), acid sphingomyelinase and HEXA/HEXB in APOE4 should be unchanged or lower than APOE3, and cargo clearance half-time longer, so that the transcript-to-activity ratio for these enzymes rises at least twofold in APOE4. If APOE4 hydrolase activity and clearance rate increase in proportion to the transcript elevation, the bottleneck claim is falsified and the data instead indicate genuinely enhanced catabolic capacity.", "Lysosomal pH or v-ATPase function should be measurably impaired or at best unchanged in APOE4 despite higher ATP6V1A/ATP6V1H/ATP6V0C/ATP6AP1 transcripts; finding APOE4 lysosomes more acidic than APOE3 with faster substrate turnover would weaken the mechanism.", "TFEB depletion (siRNA or degron) should erase the hydrolase transcript difference between genotypes and produce a genotype-by-TFEB interaction, with disproportionately greater undegraded cargo accumulation and death in APOE4; absence of such an interaction would weaken step 3.", "Augmenting luminal hydrolysis (recombinant or gene-delivered GBA plus acid sphingomyelinase, or acidifying nanoparticles) should normalise cargo clearance and reduce the CXCL8/CCL2 activation signature in APOE4 with little effect in APOE3; no genotype-selective rescue would weaken the mechanism.", "Focus-discriminating counter-test: inhibiting DGAT1 or SCD should not rescue APOE4 cargo clearance if the bottleneck is lysosomal hydrolysis. If DGAT1/SCD inhibition rescues while GBA/SMPD1 augmentation does not, the bottleneck is glycerolipid esterification and storage, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show accumulation of glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin and lactosylceramide species relative to total phospholipid; absence of any sphingolipid accumulation, or accumulation confined to triacylglycerol with normal sphingolipids, would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Independent quantification (targeted MS or western blot) should show that mature CTSB, CTSD, GBA and HEXB protein in APOE4 rises far less than their transcripts; concordant large protein increases would falsify the transcript-protein discordance central to step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher transcript abundance of cargo-uptake and lipid-handling receptors in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE) is inferred, not measured, to raise the delivery rate of membrane- and lipoprotein-derived lipid cargo into the endolysosomal system.", "Catabolism of that cargo requires luminal acid hydrolases acting on sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids; APOE4 shows coordinated induction of this module and of its acidification machinery (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:NAGLU, gene:GAA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:AGA, gene:DPP7, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:SUMF1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:SPNS1) alongside the CLEAR-network transcription factors gene:TFEB and gene:MITF; this set is enriched even against the strongly positive global RNA background.", "We infer that the transcript program is compensatory: measured protein-spot abundance for spots containing lysosomal hydrolase candidates is not coordinately raised (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:063, protein_spot:012 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:086 down), so mature hydrolase content and hence hydrolytic activity are not established to scale with transcript.", "Consequently the rate-limiting step is luminal hydrolysis/acidification after delivery, predicting persistence of undegraded sphingolipid-rich cargo in APOE4 lysosomes; this lipid pool was not measured in the supplied data and is inferred only.", "Lipid that escapes or bypasses the block is routed to esterification, desaturation and storage rather than to full catabolism, consistent with gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL, gene:SOAT1 and gene:DHCR24; because the acyl-remodeling gene set as a whole is not enriched above background (and gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3 fall), this is placed downstream of the bottleneck, not as its cause.", "ATP demand for v-ATPase-driven acidification and for the sustained biosynthetic program is met by an elevated mitochondrial/TCA transcript module (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2), an inferred metabolic accommodation rather than measured respiration.", "Unresolved degradative load is proposed to maintain a chronically activated microglial state (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NFKBIZ, gene:A2M, gene:TSPO up), while gene:CTSS and gene:IDS decreases show the response is selective and not a uniform lysosome-wide induction."], "title": "Lysosomal sphingolipid-hydrolase capacity, not glycerolipid acyl remodeling, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: a TFEB/MITF-associated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program is not matched at the protein-spot level"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13174315991581434, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.008404396815017812, "cosine_similarity": 0.23511690418606232, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6658446601941748, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13174315991581434, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.008404396815017812, "cosine_similarity": 0.23511690418606232, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6658446601941748, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.612687, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 351}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_015", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Functional gene annotations, SEL1L-HRD1 biology and the proposed stress-feedback connections are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was used. The supplied examples provide format guidance, not evidence for this experiment.", "SEL1L RNA reduction translates into a limiting reduction in functional SEL1L protein. Other required ERAD components remain sufficient for restoring SEL1L alone to materially improve clearance; otherwise the proposed single primary bottleneck is weakened.", "Compensatory changes do not preserve normal ERAD throughput: EDEM2, UBE2J1 and DNAJC10 RNA increase (gene:EDEM2, gene:UBE2J1, gene:DNAJC10), which is counter-evidence to a uniform ERAD collapse.", "The observed transcriptional changes reflect comparable microglial states under the matched mock condition. Cell-state composition, astrocyte interactions, clone or batch effects and normalization could instead contribute; independent biological replicate information was not supplied.", "The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, with 77.08% positive effects. Their logarithm base is unspecified. Missing genes, including ATF4, XBP1 and HSPA5, are absent from the selected rows and cannot be called unchanged, unexpressed or inactive.", "No uniquely identified protein or activity measurement validates the proposed SEL1L bottleneck. protein_spot:017 increases but has CAT, CORO1C and ENTPD5 as candidates; it does not establish ENTPD5 protein induction. All supplied spots have multiple candidates and no adjusted protein p-values are supplied.", "Lower secretory-pathway transcripts, including SEC24D and GOSR1 (gene:SEC24D, gene:GOSR1), could indicate a transport defect upstream of stress instead. Broad endolysosomal and mitochondrial RNA increases also permit a more general cell-state explanation.", "The discovery contains RNA expression and protein-spot abundance contrasts, not measured genomic variants. ERAD flux, secretion, protein localization, stress-sensor activation and client pools are inferred or prospective readouts, not observed modalities."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 microglia are hypothesized to have reduced SEL1L-dependent clearance of misfolded luminal glycoproteins through ER-associated degradation (ERAD), prolonging client residence in the ER and eliciting compensatory glycan-quality-control and stress-associated transcription. The abundance data motivate this mechanism but do not establish its causal direction or demonstrate impaired clearance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In independently replicated, matched APOE3 and APOE4 mock cultures, quantify SEL1L protein and pulse-chase a low-expression luminal glycoprotein ERAD reporter whose SEL1L dependence is first validated in these cells. APOE4 should have lower functional SEL1L and a longer reporter half-life at matched initial reporter abundance, with relatively preserved turnover of a cytosolic proteasome reporter. Unchanged SEL1L protein, normal or faster luminal-client clearance, or equally impaired cytosolic turnover would weaken the selective SEL1L bottleneck.", "Restore SEL1L in APOE4 to the APOE3 protein level. The model predicts faster luminal ERAD-reporter clearance and reduced DDIT3 RNA, whereas an equally expressed, experimentally validated HRD1-interaction-defective SEL1L comparator should fail to rescue. Lack of rescue despite restored functional SEL1L, or equal rescue by the inactive comparator, would weaken SEL1L as the primary bottleneck. Evaluate direct stress signaling separately using cleaved ATF6 and PERK/eIF2alpha phosphorylation; their activation is a prospective test, not an inference from sensor RNA.", "Reduce SEL1L in APOE3 to the APOE4 protein level established in the first experiment. This should prolong luminal-client half-life and increase stress-associated transcription; restoration with perturbation-resistant functional SEL1L should reverse both. Failure to phenocopy the APOE4 state, or failure of stress readouts to follow clearance changes, would weaken the proposed causal chain.", "Compare matched SEL1L and GOSR1 restoration in APOE4 while separately tracking misfolded-client degradation and ER-to-Golgi transit of a folding-competent secretory glycoprotein. SEL1L restoration should preferentially correct defective degradation and associated stress; improvement in secretion alone would not confirm the hypothesis. If GOSR1 restoration normalizes client clearance and stress while functional SEL1L restoration fails, a primary trafficking defect would be favored and this mechanism weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mechanism_steps": ["1. The observed reduction in SEL1L RNA in APOE4 versus APOE3 (gene:SEL1L) is proposed to lower functional SEL1L protein at the ER. This RNA-to-protein and localization link is an assumption, not a protein measurement.", "2. Reduced SEL1L becomes the primary bottleneck for delivery of misfolded luminal glycoproteins to the HRD1/SYVN1 ERAD machinery. Lower DERL1 and EDEM1 RNA (gene:DERL1, gene:EDEM1) is compatible with impaired disposal, but substrate recognition, retrotranslocation and degradation rates were not measured.", "3. Slower disposal prolongs the ER residence of misfolded glycoprotein clients. Their retention and abundance are predicted consequences; no retained-client or unfolded-protein pool was measured.", "4. Persistent client retention is proposed to elicit compensatory glycan-processing and folding-surveillance transcription, consistent with increased MLEC, UGGT1, DDOST, STT3A, ENTPD5 and DNAJB11 RNA (gene:MLEC, gene:UGGT1, gene:DDOST, gene:STT3A, gene:ENTPD5, gene:DNAJB11). These increases do not establish greater glycosylation flux or a higher secretory load.", "5. Compensation remains insufficient at the SEL1L-dependent disposal step, sustaining stress-associated transcription compatible with increased ATF6, EIF2AK3 and DDIT3 RNA (gene:ATF6, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3). Activation of ATF6 or PERK, and assignment to a specific unfolded-protein-response branch, remain unmeasured."], "title": "A SEL1L-dependent ER clearance bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01163023854736756, "cosine_similarity": 0.23339026425429477, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_015", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6161941747572816, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09001956947162426, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01163023854736756, "cosine_similarity": 0.23339026425429477, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6161941747572816, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.849375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_068", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so absolute effect sizes and the strong global positive shift (1705/2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base) are treated as non-informative; only within-table ranks/percentiles are used for inference.", "Transcript rank elevation of GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, HEXB, GM2A is assumed to reflect an active TFEB/CLEAR-type program rather than a difference in lysosome number alone, and it is assumed not to be fully mirrored by proportional increases in luminal enzyme activity.", "No lipid measurement is supplied: sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, ganglioside, ceramide and cholesterol pools, lysosomal pH, and enzyme activities are inferred, never observed.", "Key pathway genes are absent from the table (UGCG, SGMS1, ASAH1, PSAP, NPC1, GALC, SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, GRN, SQSTM1, MTOR), so both the synthesis arm and the saposin/cofactor arm are untested here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; assignments of spots to CTSD/CTSB/GNS/HEXB are ambiguous and are used only as weak, direction-mixed support, not as identified protein measurements.", "The microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes; some transcript signal could arise from non-microglial RNA or genotype-dependent differentiation state rather than from the proposed lysosomal mechanism.", "Effect direction is APOE4 higher than APOE3; no causal inference is claimed from these associations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the endolysosomal degradative program in which lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA) are among the most strongly elevated genes, while the de novo sphingolipid-synthesis transcripts that were measured are not elevated above the dataset background and the LacCer synthase B4GALT5 is reduced. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is luminal turnover capacity for sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid on intraluminal-vesicle membranes relative to the lipid cargo load: the CLEAR-type transcriptional response is compensatory and does not translate into matched hydrolytic flux, so sphingolipid-rich intraluminal membranes retain cholesterol in the lysosome, lower the ER regulatory sterol pool, and de-repress SREBP targets (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, HMGCS1, LDLR), creating a feed-forward lipid-loading loop. Abundances are measured; activity, flux, lipid pools, localization and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lysosome immunopurification (LysoIP) plus lipidomics in the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher hexosylceramide, GM2/GA2 and sphingomyelin AND higher unesterified cholesterol per LAMP1 in APOE4. If APOE4 lysosomes contain equal or lower sphingolipid and cholesterol despite the elevated hydrolase transcripts, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: 7-14 day glucosylceramide-synthase inhibition (eliglustat or Genz-123346) in APOE4 microglia should lower glycosphingolipid load and, secondarily, normalise both the CLEAR/hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB) and the SREBP targets (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24) toward APOE3 values, and reduce filipin-positive lysosomal cholesterol. If glycosphingolipids fall but SREBP targets and hydrolase transcripts remain APOE4-high, the sphingolipid-specific mechanism is wrong and a pan-lysosomal or sterol-transport-primary explanation is favoured.", "Specific activity assays on isolated lysosomes should show that GBA, HEXA and acid-sphingomyelinase activity per lysosome rises less than proportionally to the transcript differences, so that activity divided by substrate is lower in APOE4. Proportional or supra-proportional activity gain with normal substrate levels would refute the 'compensatory but insufficient' step.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase transcript elevation and worsen lysosomal sphingolipid/cholesterol accumulation; if hydrolase transcripts remain elevated after TFEB loss, step 2 is wrong.", "Occlusion test: pharmacological acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition (functional inhibitor, e.g. amitriptyline) should increase lysosomal cholesterol retention markedly in APOE3 but only weakly in APOE4 (already saturated). Equal-magnitude responses in both genotypes would weaken the claim that sphingolipid turnover is already limiting in APOE4.", "Providing an egress bypass (cyclodextrin or NPC2 overexpression) should reduce SREBP-target transcripts in APOE4 without lowering glycosphingolipid load; failure to reduce SREBP targets would break the proposed lysosome-to-ER sterol link (step 6)."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the flux of lipid-rich cargo into the late endosome/lysosome (inferred, not measured); transcripts for intraluminal-vesicle and late-endosomal routing machinery are elevated (gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS37B, gene:VPS28, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:ARL8B), consistent with expanded intraluminal membrane surface that must be degraded.", "A TFEB/MITF-associated CLEAR-type transcriptional response is engaged (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) and raises acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2); lysosomal genes are over-represented in the top decile of this selected DE table (7/29, binomial p=0.02).", "Within that program the sphingolipid-degradation arm is the most extreme: gene:GBA (98th percentile), gene:HEXA (96th), gene:SMPD1 (95th), with gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH also up, whereas the measured anabolic/backbone genes (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1, gene:ORMDL2) sit at or below the dataset median and gene:B4GALT5 is decreased, i.e. the transcriptional signature is turnover-weighted rather than synthesis-weighted.", "We infer that this transcript increase does not produce proportionally increased luminal hydrolytic capacity: the mannose-6-phosphate sorting receptor transcript gene:M6PR is decreased, the cholesterol-transfer protein transcript gene:NPC2 is only at the 35th percentile of this table, and cathepsin-candidate protein spots move in both directions (protein_spot:027, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down), a pattern compatible with altered maturation/processing rather than uniform enzyme gain.", "The predicted consequence (unmeasured here) is retention of sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and GM2/GA2 species on intraluminal membranes; because these lipids bind and shield cholesterol, cholesterol egress from the lysosome is slowed and the ER regulatory sterol pool falls.", "Low ER sterol de-represses SREBP processing, producing the observed lipogenic/sterologenic transcript elevation (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1), which sustains further lipid influx and esterification and feeds back onto the loaded lysosome.", "Chronic loaded-lysosome state accompanies a partial lipid-handling/primed microglial transcript pattern (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:TREM2); this step is the weakest and is offered as a consequence, not as evidence for the bottleneck."], "title": "Compensatory-but-insufficient lysosomal sphingolipid catabolism in APOE4 microglia sequesters cholesterol and de-represses SREBP"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.020483627580638392, "cosine_similarity": 0.22806944725586062, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_068", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378996763754045, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11056751467710371, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.020483627580638392, "cosine_similarity": 0.22806944725586062, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378996763754045, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.4972435, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 352}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_081", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not a whole-transcriptome measurement: the reported list contains 1705 positive and 507 negative entries occupying two separately ranked row blocks (rows 2-509 duplicated with one positive and one negative entry each; rows \u003e=510 exclusively positive), so the apparent global mean shift of +1.39 is treated as a list-composition artifact and only within-list, set-versus-background comparisons are interpreted.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and magnitudes reach |15|; effects are therefore used ordinally (direction and rank), not as calibrated fold changes, and the protein-spot column (log2) is not placed on the same scale.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme protein and, more weakly, for pathway activity; no flux, oxygen-consumption, lipid, protein-modification or localisation measurement is supplied, so every flux and direction statement is inference.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are treated as ambiguous and are not used as evidence for any specific enzyme.", "Key genes for the storage and disposal arms were not measured in this list (ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, CPT1A, ACLY, FASN, PKM, LDHA, G6PD, CS), so the hypothesis assumes their behaviour rather than observing it.", "The comparison is pseudobulk-like across an isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 microglia-astrocyte co-culture at day 30 with no replicate count supplied; the hypothesis assumes the differences are not dominated by differences in microglial maturation state or astrocyte carry-over.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: the data are observational genotype-associated differences, and the ordering of steps is a proposed, not demonstrated, chain."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally down-regulate the committed steps of glycolysis and the pentose-phosphate branch (HK2, PFKP, HK3, PGD, TALDO1) while coherently up-regulating the entire measured mitochondrial oxidative apparatus (38/38 OXPHOS subunit transcripts, MPC2, DLD, PDP1, OGDH, ACO2, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and a lysosomal/lipid-acquisition module (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, ABCA7, TFEB, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1H). We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is glucose-carbon entry into glycolysis at the hexokinase step, which forces APOE4 microglia to rely on lipid-derived carbon for mitochondrial oxidation; the resulting high fatty-acid throughput exceeds oxidative disposal and is buffered by SCD-dependent desaturation and esterification (SCD, SREBF1, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, DGAT1, SOAT1, ACSS2), predicting an APOE4 lipid phenotype of expanded monounsaturated triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage pools and a raised desaturation index. All fluxes, activities and directions are inferred; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating lipidomics prediction: APOE4 microglia should show a higher SCD desaturation index (16:1n7/16:0 and 18:1n9/18:0 ratios in the total and triacylglycerol fractions) and greater triacylglycerol plus cholesteryl-ester mass per cell than isogenic APOE3, with free saturated fatty acid not proportionally increased. An equal or lower desaturation index, or no increase in esterified storage lipid, would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating flux prediction: extracellular-flux and 13C tracing should show APOE4 with higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption, lower ECAR and lower glycolytic reserve, reduced 13C6-glucose enrichment into citrate/lactate, and increased 13C16-palmitate enrichment into TCA intermediates. Higher glycolytic flux or equal oxygen consumption in APOE4 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Perturbation prediction 1 (bottleneck test): pharmacological or genetic restriction of hexokinase flux (2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown) in APOE3 microglia should partially phenocopy the APOE4 lipid signature, increasing lipid-droplet content and the MUFA-triacylglycerol fraction and raising OXPHOS/TCA transcripts. Failure to shift APOE3 lipids in the APOE4 direction would argue the hexokinase step is not the driver.", "Perturbation prediction 2 (buffering test): SCD inhibition (A939572 or CAY10566) should collapse the APOE4-specific triacylglycerol/desaturation excess and cause disproportionately greater saturated-lipid stress and viability loss in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal responses in both genotypes would weaken step 5.", "Perturbation prediction 3 (substrate-supply test): blocking lipid input (SCARB1 blockade or antibody/receptor knockdown, or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should reduce the APOE4 excess in lipid droplets and blunt the TFEB-associated hydrolase transcript elevation and the OCR advantage. Persistence of the APOE4 lipid and respiratory phenotype under lipid-depleted conditions would show that lipid uptake is not the substrate source and would weaken step 4.", "Dependency prediction: CPT1 inhibition (etomoxir at fatty-acid-oxidation-selective dose) should lower oxygen consumption more in APOE4 than APOE3 and further increase APOE4 lipid-droplet content. An equal or larger effect in APOE3 would weaken the claim of lipid-fuelled respiration.", "Negative-control prediction: inflammatory activation is not the driver, so cytokine transcripts and secreted IL1B/TNF should not separate the genotypes under mock conditions; a strong APOE4 inflammatory secretome under mock would favour an inflammation-first alternative over this metabolic mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show lower transcripts for the committed glycolytic entry steps (gene:HK2 -3.67 with the 8th-most significant adjusted p-value in the list, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) and for pentose-phosphate enzymes (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32) even though glucose-transporter transcripts are higher (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73). Inference (not measured): glucose-6-phosphate production, glycolytic flux and glucose-derived NADPH are reduced, creating the primary bottleneck; the raised transporters are read as a compensatory response.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): every measured OXPHOS subunit transcript is higher in APOE4 (38/38 positive, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX5B +2.33, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:SDHB +1.65), together with mitochondrial carriers and import components (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A46 +8.77, gene:TOMM22 +4.63). Inference: increased mitochondrial oxidative and anaplerotic capacity, not necessarily increased mitochondrial mass per cell.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): pyruvate-handling and TCA/shuttle transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:IDH3B +2.02). Inference: whatever pyruvate is made is preferentially imported and oxidised, and malate-aspartate/citrate shuttling to the cytosol is increased, so the glycolytic restriction is not compensated by lactate fermentation.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): lipid-acquisition and lysosomal catabolic transcripts are raised (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24; gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23), as are mitochondrial fatty-acid-oxidation components (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24). Inference: increased delivery and lysosomal hydrolysis of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid supplies the fatty acids and acetyl units that substitute for glucose carbon.", "Step 5 (measured abundance): the lipogenic/esterifying arm is raised in parallel (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:MGLL +4.00). Inference: fatty acids arriving faster than they are oxidised are desaturated by SCD and esterified into triacylglycerol, phospholipid and cholesteryl ester rather than accumulating as free saturated fatty acid.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype, not measured here): the net APOE4 state is glucose-restricted, mitochondria- and lipid-dependent, with an expanded esterified storage-lipid pool that is enriched in monounsaturated acyl chains and cholesteryl esters, and a correspondingly higher SCD desaturation index."], "title": "APOE4 microglia restrict glucose commitment at hexokinase and run a mitochondria-dominant, lipid-fuelled program that buffers fatty acids as SCD-desaturated, esterified storage lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3799615995273788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28103494892034636, "cosine_similarity": 0.2266123439219674, "direction_accuracy": 0.2961165048543689, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6511650485436894, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3799615995273788, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.28103494892034636, "cosine_similarity": 0.2266123439219674, "direction_accuracy": 0.2961165048543689, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6511650485436894, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.25816625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 353}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_090", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (every row has |reported log fold change| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive), so only rank-based, within-list comparisons are interpreted; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance is used as an index of pathway demand/biogenesis, not of enzyme activity, assembled-complex amount, metabolic flux, or subcellular localization; no ROS, NADPH/NADP+, GSH/GSSG, oxygen-consumption or PRDX redox-state measurement is supplied.", "The discordance between nuclear-encoded and mtDNA-encoded ETC transcripts reflects genuine mitonuclear imbalance in APOE4 microglia rather than differential capture of polyadenylated mitochondrial transcripts, ambient RNA, or normalization artefact.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and cannot identify a protein uniquely; spot:077 (candidates include PRDX2), spot:017 (candidates include CAT) and spot:021 (candidates include G6PD, GSR, PGD) are treated as weak, non-attributable corroboration only.", "Microglial identity is comparable between genotypes despite the astrocyte co-culture; gene:S100B (+6.00) and gene:PTPRC (-1.50) leave a composition/contamination confound unresolved.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, and effect magnitudes are extreme (up to 15.5) with essentially no correlation between |effect| and significance (r = -0.04), so individual fold changes are treated as unreliable in magnitude but usable in rank."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation and TCA machinery (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunits (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2, all lower in APOE4). We propose that this mitonuclear subunit imbalance, not peroxisomal metabolism, is the primary bottleneck: it limits assembly of stoichiometric complex I/III/IV, increases electron leak and mitochondrial peroxide flux, and drives a compensatory thiol-peroxidase transcript response (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:MGST2) that is only partially reductant-supported because cytosolic NADPH/NAD-regenerating transcripts are lower (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT), leaving APOE4 microglia in a chronically thiol-oxidized, low-buffer-reserve state. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are selected differential-expression results plus ambiguous protein spots.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation 1 (phenocopy): pharmacologically or genetically creating mitonuclear imbalance in APOE3 microglia (e.g. low-dose chloramphenicol or doxycycline to block mitochondrial translation, or TFAM knockdown) should reproduce the APOE4 signature - increased PRDX2/PRDX3/TXNDC17/GPX4 transcripts and increased peroxiredoxin oxidation (PRDX dimer/monomer redox shift, PRDX-SO2/3 immunoblot) - without inducing inflammatory cytokine transcripts. If mitochondrial-translation blockade in APOE3 fails to induce the thiol-peroxidase transcripts, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation 2 (rescue that separates capacity from demand): raising reductant supply in APOE4 microglia (NAD/NADPH precursor such as nicotinamide riboside, or forced expression of mitochondrial TXNRD2/NNT) should normalise PRDX oxidation state and lower PRDX/TXN transcripts while leaving the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcript elevation intact; a mitochondria-targeted scavenger (MitoTEMPO/MitoQ) should do the same, whereas a peroxisome-targeted catalase should not. If cytosol-restricted antioxidants or peroxisomal catalase normalise the signature as effectively as mitochondria-targeted ones, a mitochondrial source is not the bottleneck.", "Assembly/function test: blue-native PAGE and respirometry should show that APOE4 microglia have equal or lower assembled complex I/IV and lower maximal (FCCP-stimulated) oxygen consumption and/or higher proton leak per unit of nuclear-encoded subunit protein than APOE3. Finding proportionally increased assembled complexes and increased spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 would falsify the imbalance step.", "Direct redox readout: APOE4 microglia should show higher steady-state matrix H2O2 (mito-roGFP2-Orp1 or HyPer7) and a lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio than isogenic APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal matrix H2O2 and equal NADPH/NADP+ would weaken the entire mechanism.", "Specificity/counter-test for the assigned focus: peroxisomal beta-oxidation should not be the differentiating axis - peroxisomal transcripts are not enriched (peroxisome set mean rank 40th percentile, p=0.78; gene:ABCD1 -1.64). Predict that C26:0 very-long-chain fatty-acid levels and peroxisome number/PEX5 import assays do not differ between genotypes; a clear peroxisomal import or VLCFA defect in APOE4 would favour the alternative peroxisomal mechanism over this one.", "Confound test: single-cell or nucleus-level reanalysis with strict microglial gating (and ambient-RNA correction) should retain the nuclear-OXPHOS-up/mtDNA-down discordance and the thiol-peroxidase enrichment. If either disappears after removing astrocyte-derived transcripts (gene:S100B) or ambient RNA, the signature is a composition artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (39 OXPHOS transcripts, median +2.64, mean rank 68th percentile of the differential list, permutation p\u003c1e-4) and TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:GLUD1 +3.17), while glycolytic entry transcripts are lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08). Inferred (not measured): a substrate/flux bias toward mitochondrial oxidation.", "Measured: mtDNA-encoded core subunits move oppositely (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; mean rank 28th percentile, p=0.03), i.e. nuclear and mitochondrial genomes are discordant within the same list. Inferred bottleneck: catalytic-core supply limits assembly of holo-complex I/III/IV relative to the enlarged nuclear-encoded accessory pool; assembled complex amounts and respiration were not measured.", "Inferred: partially assembled or accessory-subunit-excess respiratory complexes raise univalent electron leak at complex I/III, increasing matrix superoxide and H2O2. No ROS, oxygen-consumption or membrane-potential measurement is supplied.", "Measured response consistent with step 3: mitochondrial and cytosolic thiol-peroxidase and thioredoxin-system transcripts are among the most upward-shifted in the list (gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:TXNL1 +4.33, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:MGST2 +3.32, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX5 +1.96; mean rank 83rd percentile, p\u003c1e-3), together with gene:SELENOW, gene:CYB5R3, gene:MSRA and the matrix transhydrogenase gene:NNT. Inferred: increased peroxide-detoxification demand rather than increased detoxification capacity per se.", "Measured constraint: the NADPH/NAD-regenerating arm is not co-induced (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14, gene:NAMPT -2.62). Inferred: peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin re-reduction becomes reductant-limited, so peroxiredoxins accumulate in oxidized/hyperoxidized forms even though their transcripts rise; PRDX oxidation state was not measured.", "Measured co-signature: lysosomal/degradative and lipid-handling transcripts are shifted up (lysosomal set mean rank 68th percentile, p=0.003; gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:SCP2 +5.95) and ER/integrated-stress markers are up (gene:ATF6 +4.04, gene:DDIT3 +2.79), whereas inflammatory transcripts are not enriched (31 transcripts, mean rank 44th percentile, p=0.88). Inferred: the APOE4 state is a redox/proteostatic-metabolic state rather than a classical cytokine activation state."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance in APOE4 microglia creates a thiol-peroxidase demand that outruns NADPH-regenerating capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10567514677103718, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.020146160721796938, "cosine_similarity": 0.22554925717071947, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6058155339805825, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10567514677103718, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.020146160721796938, "cosine_similarity": 0.22554925717071947, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6058155339805825, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.009439, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 354}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_011", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Unverified background knowledge: MTERF4 supports mitochondrial ribosome maturation; respiratory complexes require coordinated mitochondrial and nuclear protein production; mitochondrial stress can promote compensatory transcription. No literature or external database was consulted.", "Lower MTERF4 RNA must produce a functionally limiting protein decrease, despite protein stability, reserve capacity and compensatory factors. This is the weakest necessary causal assumption; no supplied protein spot includes MTERF4 among its candidates.", "Higher nuclear respiratory RNA reflects compensation at least partly. Increased mitochondrial biogenesis or energy demand could instead explain it. Higher TUFM and GFM2 RNA (gene:TUFM, gene:GFM2) may preserve translation and oppose the proposed bottleneck.", "Mitochondrial RNA behavior is selective: gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 increase while four other supplied mitochondrial coding transcripts decrease. RNA processing, stability, mitochondrial content and cell composition could produce this pattern independently of mitoribosome limitation.", "These selected differential-expression rows do not measure an unbiased whole transcriptome. The RNA logarithm base remains unspecified; absent rows are unknown. RNA abundance does not establish protein abundance, activity, localization or flux. Protein-spot candidates do not identify unique proteins, and no unmeasured molecular pool is treated as observed.", "The isogenic comparison reduces genetic-background confounding, but comparable differentiation states and microglial attribution are assumed. Biological replicate counts are not supplied, and astrocyte-mediated effects remain possible. The TFEB feedback extension is less secure than the central maturation hypothesis."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced MTERF4 expression is hypothesized to make mitochondrial ribosome maturation the primary bottleneck. This would constrain mitochondrial translation and respiratory-complex assembly despite increased nuclear respiratory transcripts, with compensatory respiratory and lysosomal transcription distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3. Causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In independently replicated, matched differentiations, APOE4 should show lower mitochondrial MTERF4 protein, fewer translation-competent mitoribosomes, and lower nascent mitochondrial protein synthesis after accounting for mitochondrial mass and mature mitochondrial RNA abundance. Respiratory-complex assembly and ATP-linked or spare respiration should also be impaired. Adequate MTERF4 protein with normal or increased mitoribosome assembly and translation would weaken the primary bottleneck.", "Inducibly restore wild-type MTERF4 in differentiated APOE4 microglia to the measured APOE3 protein level, verifying mitochondrial localization. Compared with empty-vector and import-defective controls, this should restore mitoribosome assembly and mitochondrial translation before improving respiratory-complex assembly and respiration. Translation efficiency should improve without requiring an initial increase in the depleted mitochondrial RNAs, discriminating maturation limitation from transcript scarcity alone. Verified restoration that fails to rescue assembly and translation would weaken the mechanism; rescue only at supraphysiological expression would provide weak support.", "Titrate MTERF4 CRISPR interference in APOE3 to reproduce any verified APOE4 protein deficit. It should reproduce the translation and respiratory defects, followed by increased nuclear respiratory and TFEB-associated lysosomal RNAs; a CRISPR-resistant MTERF4 rescue should reverse these effects. Effects requiring much deeper depletion would weaken relevance to the observed comparison. If successful physiological MTERF4 rescue restores respiration in APOE4 but leaves the lysosomal signature intact after sufficient turnover time, the proposed downstream feedback link would be weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured entry point: MTERF4 RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:MTERF4). The proposed chain assumes that this lowers mitochondrial MTERF4 protein; its protein abundance and localization were not measured, and the upstream regulatory connection to APOE4 is unresolved.", "Primary inferred bottleneck: insufficient MTERF4 slows maturation of the mitochondrial large ribosomal subunit and formation of translation-competent mitoribosomes. The maturation role is unverified background knowledge; ribosome assembly was not measured.", "Inferred consequence: mitochondrial translation supplies insufficient mitochondrially encoded core subunits to match the demand implied by increased nuclear respiratory transcripts. Productive respiratory-complex assembly therefore falls short of the transcriptional program. Neither translation rates nor subunit protein stoichiometry were measured.", "Inferred functional consequence: impaired respiratory-complex assembly lowers ATP-linked respiration and respiratory reserve, creating energetic or proteostatic stress despite higher MPC2 and OGDH RNAs (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH). Respiration, ATP abundance and metabolic flux were not measured.", "Proposed feedback: mitochondrial stress induces compensatory nuclear respiratory transcription and a TFEB-associated lysosomal program. Higher respiratory, TFEB, proton-pump and hydrolase RNAs are measured (gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:GBA); feedback direction, TFEB nuclear activity and lysosomal flux remain inferred."], "title": "MTERF4-limited mitoribosome maturation in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07254097105573104, "cosine_similarity": 0.2247683243450192, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6271812297734628, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.053816046966731895, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07254097105573104, "cosine_similarity": 0.2247683243450192, "direction_accuracy": 0.09061488673139159, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6271812297734628, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.14722, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_187", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive, median +1.46), so all statements are enrichment relative to that already up-shifted background, not evidence of a whole-transcriptome shift; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Transcript abundance of nuclear-encoded subunits is assumed to track imported subunit protein supply, and mtDNA-encoded transcript abundance to track core subunit synthesis; neither protein pool, nor assembled complex, nor respiration was measured here.", "The six MT- rows are assumed to represent genuine mtDNA transcript differences rather than droplet ambient RNA, mitochondrial-content normalisation, or dissociation-stress artefacts of 10X Flex data; this is the weakest link in the chain (MT- set alone p=0.065, n=6 of 13 mtDNA genes).", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to differentially contaminate the APOE4 and APOE3 microglial profiles; no purity or cell-composition measure was supplied.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-uniquely identified (each has 2-6 candidate genes), so no spot is treated as evidence for or against a specific mitochondrial protein.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied; the very large reported effect magnitudes (up to +15.5) suggest low-replicate or pseudobulk inflation, so effect sizes are used only for ranking and set comparison, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Background knowledge used to define pathway membership and the OMA1-DELE1-HRI relay is unverified literature recall; no external database was consulted."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a coordinated nuclear transcriptional expansion of the mitochondrial import/translation/respiratory-subunit machinery (38/38 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts higher, median ~+2.6 versus a +1.46 list-wide median; NDUF family permutation p=0.012) that is not accompanied by higher mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (4 of 6 measured MT- transcripts lower, nuclear-versus-mtDNA contrast p~9e-4). We hypothesise that the resulting subunit stoichiometry mismatch, not lipid remodeling, is the rate-limiting step: assembly of mtDNA-core-containing complexes (I, III, IV, ATP synthase) becomes the bottleneck, so measured subunit transcript abundance overstates assembled-complex activity, mitochondrial stress signalling is engaged (DELE1 +4.82, DDIT3 +2.79, HSPA9 +2.35, SHMT2 +2.22), glycolytic compensation genes fall (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08), and carbon-handling and lysosomal catabolic capacity are re-routed. All directionality here is inferred from transcript abundance; no assembled complex, flux, or metabolite pool was measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: blue-native PAGE / in-gel activity or complexome profiling of isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a reduced ratio of assembled Complex I (and CI-containing supercomplex) to total NDUFS/NDUFB subunit protein, and reduced MT-CO1/MT-ND1 protein per nuclear-encoded subunit protein. If APOE4 shows assembled-complex levels and activity that scale proportionally with the elevated nuclear subunit abundance, the assembly-bottleneck claim is falsified and a simple mitochondrial-biogenesis-increase model should be preferred.", "Seahorse respirometry should show that APOE4 microglia have equal or lower maximal and spare respiratory capacity than APOE3 despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, plus lower glycolytic reserve (predicted from HK2/PFKP). Higher maximal respiration and normal glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy test: partial TFAM or POLRMT knockdown in APOE3 microglia (lowering mtDNA-encoded subunit supply without touching nuclear subunit genes) should reproduce the APOE4 signature \u2014 up-regulated nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts with DELE1/DDIT3/HSPA9/SHMT2 induction. Failure to induce the nuclear up-shift would argue the two arms are independently driven by APOE4 rather than causally linked.", "Rescue/specificity test: HRI (EIF2AK1) inhibition or DELE1 knockout in APOE4 microglia should reduce DDIT3 and SHMT2 without restoring assembled Complex I or respiration. If DDIT3 induction is instead abolished by PERK inhibition and is insensitive to DELE1 loss, the mitochondrial origin of the stress arm is wrong.", "Bottleneck-ordering test: pharmacological blockade of the lipogenic/acyl-remodeling branch (SCD or DGAT1 inhibition) is predicted not to normalise nuclear OXPHOS, MT- transcript, or DDIT3 levels in APOE4 microglia, whereas measures that restore mtDNA-encoded subunit supply should. If SCD/DGAT1 inhibition normalises the mitochondrial signature, the rejected lipid-remodeling mechanism should replace this one.", "Independent quantification of all 13 mtDNA-encoded transcripts by ddPCR normalised to mtDNA copy number should confirm a genuine APOE4 deficit in ND4/CYB/CO2/ATP6 per genome. If mtDNA-encoded transcripts per genome are equal or higher in APOE4, the central mitonuclear imbalance is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_187", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with higher transcript abundance across the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial module: every measured Complex I/III/IV/ATP-synthase subunit transcript is higher than in APOE3 (e.g. NDUFS7 +5.72, NDUFS8 +4.94, NDUFA5 +7.28, ATP5ME +5.24, UQCRC2 +4.03, COX7A2 +3.44), together with protein-import and mitochondrial translation support (TOMM22 +4.64, TIMM44 +2.53, TIMM8B +5.24, TUFM +6.46). This is measured abundance of transcripts, not of assembled complexes.", "The mtDNA-encoded core subunits required to nucleate those complexes are not co-elevated: MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33 (with MT-ND5 +1.93 and MT-ND4L +1.95 discordant). We infer a stoichiometric mismatch in which mtDNA-encoded core supply, not nuclear subunit supply, limits holoenzyme assembly \u2014 the proposed primary bottleneck. Assembly state itself is unmeasured.", "Assembly-limited complexes are predicted to accumulate unincorporated imported subunits in the matrix and inner membrane, engaging mitochondrial proteostatic and stress-relay signalling; consistent transcripts are HSPA9 +2.35 (matrix chaperone), DELE1 +4.82 (OMA1-DELE1-HRI relay component), DDIT3 +2.79 (ISR effector) and SHMT2 +2.22 (ISR/one-carbon output). Pathway activity, eIF2-alpha phosphorylation and OMA1 cleavage are inferred, not measured; OMA1 transcript is in fact lower (-1.39), which we attribute to post-translational rather than transcriptional regulation.", "Substrate delivery and anaplerosis are up-regulated in the same cells (MPC2 +7.98, MDH1 +8.72, OGDH +8.56, ACO2 +3.54, DLD +5.54, GLUD1 +3.17, SLC25A1 +4.47, SLC25A11 +4.47, SLC25A5 +5.60; TCA/carrier set median +3.55, p=1.6e-4), so we infer that TCA carbon entry is preserved or increased while ATP-coupled electron transport is assembly-limited, favouring citrate/malate export and biosynthetic use of carbon over net oxidative ATP yield.", "Compensatory fermentative capacity is not transcriptionally reinforced: hexokinase and phosphofructokinase transcripts are lower (HK2 -3.67, HK3 -1.12, PFKP -3.08) alongside pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD -1.30, TALDO1 -2.32); this hand-picked set is below background (median -1.30, p=0.012). We infer reduced spare glycolytic reserve, leaving APOE4 microglia energetically less flexible.", "Downstream, the cells expand lysosomal/catabolic capacity as an alternative substrate-mobilising route (CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.71, SMPD1 +5.63, HEXB +2.17, TFEB +2.38, ATP6V1A +4.23; lysosomal-catabolic set p=0.016), which we interpret as a consequence of the energetic/stress state rather than its cause. Degradative flux and lysosomal pH are unmeasured."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: APOE4 microglia up-regulate nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and TCA modules without matching mtDNA-encoded core subunits, making holoenzyme assembly the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10847656470210267, "cosine_similarity": 0.22287219897442248, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_187", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6220938511326861, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10847656470210267, "cosine_similarity": 0.22287219897442248, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6220938511326861, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.68799875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 355}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_088", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The unspecified-base RNA log fold changes are monotone in true fold change and comparable across genes within this selected differential-expression table; the table is biased toward significant genes, so all set statistics are judged against the table's own 77%-positive, median +1.46 background rather than against zero.", "Transcript increases in SMPD1/GBA/HEXA/HEXB/GM2A/GLA translate into increased ceramide-generating hydrolytic flux in acidified compartments; enzyme protein, activity, lumenal pH and lipid substrates were not measured.", "Ceramide and sphingoid-base clearance capacity (acid ceramidase, sphingosine kinases, sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide re-synthesis) does not increase proportionally in APOE4; these genes are absent from the supplied table, so this is an untested assumption, not an observation.", "Protein spots are mixtures with multiple candidate genes; the ANXA1, VPS26A/VPS29 and cathepsin attributions used above are provisional. The concurrent TALDO1 mRNA decrease (-2.32) is used only as a weak argument that spots 043-046 are more consistent with ANXA1 than TALDO1.", "The APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the metadata, so genotype rather than culture batch, astrocyte co-culture fraction or differentiation state drives the differences; replicate number is not supplied.", "Sphingolipid hydrolase induction is treated as a quantitatively leading component of, not a compartment separate from, the broader lysosomal program."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally amplify the endolysosomal sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis arm (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA) far above the already-positive differential-expression background, while the ceramide-consuming and sphingoid-base exit arm (SGPL1, CERK, CERS6, KDSR) is induced only at or below that background; the rate-limiting step is therefore ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal inside the late endosome-lysosome, and the inferred ceramide backlog, not a loss of hydrolytic capacity, drives the compensatory lysosome-biogenesis, membrane-repair and cargo-sorting changes seen in APOE4. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: augmenting ceramide clearance in APOE4 microglia (ASAH1 overexpression or recombinant acid ceramidase delivery) should reduce LAMP1-compartment volume, galectin-3/CHMP4B-ANXA1 damage-repair puncta and neutral-lipid load toward APOE3 levels while leaving APOE, GBA, HEXA and SMPD1 mRNA largely unchanged. If ceramide augmentation of clearance gives no rescue, or rescues only when hydrolase transcription is also suppressed, the disposal-bottleneck placement is wrong.", "Lysosome-enriched lipidomics of isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased ceramide and an increased ceramide-to-sphingomyelin ratio with decreased or unchanged HexCer/GM2 relative to their hydrolase capacity. Finding equal or lower lysosomal ceramide in APOE4, or accumulation of upstream glycosphingolipids with normal ceramide, would weaken the mechanism and favour a hydrolase-deficiency model instead.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show APOE4-increased acid sphingomyelinase, beta-glucocerebrosidase and beta-hexosaminidase activity per lysosome with flat acid ceramidase and sphingosine kinase activity; proportional scaling of ceramidase activity would falsify the imbalance step.", "Loading APOE3 microglia with short-chain ceramide or inhibiting acid ceramidase (carmofur) should phenocopy the APOE4 membrane-repair (CHMP4B, ANXA1) and sorting (M6PR/IGF2R, retromer) signature; failure to phenocopy weakens steps 5-6.", "TFEB knockdown separates biogenesis from disposal: it should lower the hydrolase mRNAs coordinately; the mechanism predicts membrane-damage and lipid-storage readouts are not corrected (and may worsen) in APOE4. Full normalisation of ceramide burden and damage markers by TFEB knockdown alone would support a generic lysosome-biogenesis explanation over a sphingolipid-disposal bottleneck.", "Blocking input flux (ASM inhibition, or GBA/HEXB knockdown) should lower APOE4 lysosomal ceramide and damage markers while increasing upstream sphingomyelin/ganglioside; if ceramide stays elevated after ASM inhibition, a de novo or salvage source is dominant and this hypothesis is weakened.", "If mitochondrial rescue (e.g. restoring OXPHOS complex assembly) normalizes the endolysosomal phenotype while ceramide manipulation does not, the alternative bioenergetic-primary model should replace this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases lipid/lipoprotein delivery into the microglial endolysosomal system (transcripts APOE, SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, LDLR up); substrate flux is inferred, no lipid pool was measured.", "A lysosome-biogenesis and acidification/maturation program is induced (TFEB, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6AP1, RAB7A, AP5M1, LAMP1, SLC38A7 transcripts up), expanding the degradative compartment; measured values are mRNA abundance, not enzyme activity or lumenal pH.", "Within that program the sphingolipid catabolic arm is disproportionately induced (SMPD1 +5.63, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, GBA2 +2.63, HEXB +2.17, GM2A +2.01, GLA +1.53; set mean +3.43 vs. DE-set median +1.46, permutation p about 0.014), predicting elevated flux of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids into ceramide.", "The disposal side of the same pathway is not matched: SGPL1 (+1.09, 29th percentile), CERS6 (+1.06, 27th), CERK (+1.23, 38th) and KDSR (+1.27, 41st) sit at or below the global positive shift, so per-molecule ceramide and sphingosine clearance capacity does not scale with input; ASAH1, SPHK1/2, SGMS1/2, UGCG and PSAP were not measured.", "The resulting inferred ceramide/sphingoid enrichment of late-endosomal and lysosomal limiting membranes raises membrane rigidity and permeabilization risk, engaging repair and stress machinery (CHMP4B +3.82, ANXA1 +4.15 RNA; ANXA1-candidate protein spots 043-046 are the largest positive spot changes, although spot identity is not unique).", "Altered limiting-membrane lipid composition and repair load bias hydrolase sorting and receptor recycling (M6PR -1.72 against IGF2R +2.02 and GNPTG +3.02; retromer/sorting transcripts VPS26A +4.86, SNX3 +3.95, with VPS26A- and VPS29-candidate spots 044 and 076 increased), so newly made hydrolase protein is not delivered in proportion to its mRNA - consistent with the split, partly decreased cathepsin-candidate spots.", "Excess lipid that cannot exit through the sphingolipid catabolic route is shunted into esterification and storage/desaturation (SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, SCD +4.17, SREBF1 +4.67), an inferred flux; neutral lipid was not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia induce lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis faster than ceramide disposal, creating a ceramide-backlogged, repair-dependent endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2372244581471772, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12272559946905864, "cosine_similarity": 0.22269184702109018, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6558543689320389, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2372244581471772, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12272559946905864, "cosine_similarity": 0.22269184702109018, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6558543689320389, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.56426325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 356}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_078", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77% of 2212 rows are positive with median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base, so all pathway statements are made relative to that internal shift and absolute magnitudes are not interpreted.", "Higher hydrolase transcript abundance is assumed to translate into higher delivered, active lysosomal hydrolase activity; this step is unmeasured, and the reduced gene:M6PR could instead divert newly made hydrolases to secretion.", "Key sphingolipid nodes (ASAH1, PSAP, SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPHK1, ACER1-3, DEGS1, GALC) are absent from the supplied rows; their absence from a selected DE list is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change, so the 'exit-arm not matched' claim rests on the measured SGPL1/CERK/CERS6/KDSR percentiles plus unmeasured nodes.", "The lysosomal up-program is assumed to be a genotype-driven cell-intrinsic difference, although the cultures contain astrocytes and any difference in microglial state, proliferation or dissociation stress could produce a similar coordinated signature.", "Protein spots are assumed to be mixtures; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein and no protein-level sphingolipid enzyme abundance is claimed.", "No lipid, activity, pH, flux or imaging measurement is supplied; ceramide, sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide and ganglioside pools are inferred targets of prediction, not observations, and causality is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinately elevated lysosomal acid-hydrolase transcript program that includes the sphingolipid catabolic branch (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA, GBA2, SUMF1) together with acidification and protease genes (ATP6V1A, ATP6AP1, ATP6V0D1, CTSB, CTSD, TFEB), whereas the transcripts of the ceramide-exit/salvage arm (SGPL1, CERK, CERS6, KDSR) sit at or below the dataset-wide positive shift and the re-glycosylation step B4GALT5 is reduced. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is ceramide disposal downstream of lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis, so that inferred sphingomyelin- and glycosphingolipid-derived ceramide accumulates in late endosomes/lysosomes and biases membrane routing (RAB7A, CHMP4B, VAMP3, SNX3, VPS26A, IGF2R up; M6PR down) and compensatory neutral-lipid/sterol handling (SREBF1, SCD, SOAT1, DGAT1, SCARB1 up). No lipid species were measured here; all lipid pools and all flux, activity, localisation and directionality statements are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of isogenic mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased total ceramide and free sphingosine with decreased sphingomyelin and decreased hexosylceramide/GM2-GM3 gangliosides (ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio up by a detectable margin). If APOE4 instead shows accumulated hexosylceramide/gangliosides with unchanged or lower ceramide (a classical storage pattern), or no sphingolipid difference at all, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: acute pharmacological or genetic block of the upstream hydrolysis step in APOE4 microglia (SMPD1 knockdown or functional inhibitor; GBA inhibition with conduritol-B-epoxide; hexosaminidase inhibition) should lower the APOE4 ceramide excess toward APOE3 levels while leaving the rest of the lysosomal transcript program largely intact. If ceramide stays elevated after combined SMPD1/GBA blockade, ceramide is coming from de novo synthesis or reduced acid ceramidase rather than from the hydrolase arm, and the mechanism is falsified.", "Opposite-direction test: relieving the exit bottleneck (acid ceramidase ASAH1 overexpression, or sphingosine-kinase-1 overexpression) should normalise APOE4 ceramide and rescue the associated endolysosomal phenotype; conversely APOE4 microglia should be hypersensitive to ASAH1 inhibition (carmofur) relative to APOE3 in viability and phagocytic assays. Equal sensitivity of both genotypes weakens the mechanism.", "Flux test: a pulse-chase with fluorescent or isotope-labelled sphingomyelin or lactosylceramide should show faster label appearance in ceramide and slower disappearance of the ceramide label in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal conversion rates would show the hydrolase transcript difference does not create a flux difference.", "Localisation and delivery test: given gene:M6PR down and gene:IGF2R up, immunostaining and medium assays should show whether the extra hydrolase is lysosome-delivered or secreted. If APOE4 conditioned medium contains disproportionately more hexosaminidase/GBA activity while intracellular activity is unchanged, the hydrolase increase does not raise intralysosomal flux and the central step fails.", "Specificity control: because non-sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSK) are up as strongly as the sphingolipid ones, TFEB knockdown should flatten the whole hydrolase program; if TFEB knockdown removes the transcript differences but leaves the APOE4 ceramide excess intact, the ceramide phenotype is TFEB-independent and this transcriptional framing is inadequate."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance than APOE3 for lysosomal acid hydrolases and for lysosomal acidification/protease genes (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:TFEB +2.38, in the unspecified reported log scale). Inferred, not measured: a correspondingly larger delivered, catalytically active lysosomal hydrolase pool.", "Inferred: within this general degradative program the sphingolipid branch (acid sphingomyelinase SMPD1; glucocerebrosidase GBA; beta-hexosaminidase HEXA/HEXB with its GM2 activator GM2A; alpha-galactosidase GLA; sulfatase maturation SUMF1) increases lumenal flux from sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and gangliosides toward ceramide.", "Measured contrast: transcripts of the ceramide-exit and salvage arm are not raised in proportion to the dataset-wide shift (gene:SGPL1 +1.09, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27, all near or below the 40th percentile of a distribution whose median is +1.46), and gene:B4GALT5 is reduced (-1.88) while gene:CERS4 (+2.52) and gene:GLTP (+2.38) are raised. Inferred: sphingosine phosphorylation/lyase-dependent exit and re-glycosylation of ceramide are limiting relative to ceramide production, with salvage re-acylation returning sphingoid base to ceramide.", "Inferred consequence (falsifiable, currently unmeasured): a net shift of the APOE4 sphingolipidome toward ceramide (and free sphingosine) with relative depletion of sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide and GM2/GM3-type gangliosides, concentrated in the late-endosomal/lysosomal membrane compartment.", "Inferred: ceramide enrichment of late-endosomal membranes changes intraluminal-vesicle formation and endolysosomal routing; consistent measured transcript changes are gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:VAMP3 +2.99, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:IGF2R +2.02 with gene:M6PR -1.72, which we read as a re-balanced, not simply increased, cargo-sorting and hydrolase-delivery route rather than as evidence of any measured cargo flux.", "Inferred: to buffer the excess hydrophobic backbone and the associated sterol/lipid load, APOE4 microglia raise esterification and lipid-uptake/lipogenic transcripts (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28), predicting coexistence of ceramide accumulation with neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet expansion rather than either alone.", "Weakly supported ancillary step (protein layer): two-dimensional protein spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases move in both directions (protein_spot:006 +0.58 and protein_spot:007 +0.58 containing GNS; protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:055 +0.58 containing CTSD or CTSB; protein_spot:058 -0.85 and protein_spot:067 -1.00 containing CTSB/CTSD/HEXB). We interpret this only as compatible with a redistribution among pro- and mature hydrolase forms, because each spot has several candidate genes and none is uniquely identified."], "title": "Ceramide-clearance bottleneck: APOE4 microglia raise lysosomal sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolase capacity without matching ceramide disposal, trapping ceramide in the endolysosomal system"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23428903740353726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14429950307523323, "cosine_similarity": 0.2214381072865698, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6616796116504855, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23428903740353726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14429950307523323, "cosine_similarity": 0.2214381072865698, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6616796116504855, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.42133425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 357}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_013", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive, median +1.46), not an unbiased transcriptome; every enrichment claim here is relative to that already up-shifted background, and absence of a gene (e.g. GRN, PSAP, NPC1, LIPA, LAMP2, MCOLN1, SQSTM1, MAP1LC3B, ATG5/7, MTOR) means not supplied, not unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA and protein effects (log2) are therefore not compared on a common numeric scale, only by direction and within-modality rank.", "Each protein spot carries 5-6 candidate genes and may contain several proteoforms; spot-level effects are not attributed to a single identified protein, and discordant spots sharing a candidate are treated as unresolved rather than as evidence of proteoform switching.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme delivery and activity; no acidification, hydrolase activity, cargo-degradation flux, lipid, or localization measurement is present in these files.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at one timepoint under mock treatment in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; replicate number is not supplied, astrocyte-derived or co-culture-dependent effects are not separable, and single-cell composition or ambient-RNA differences could contribute to the global positive shift.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 impairs microglial lipid handling and lysosomal function is unverified here (no literature access) and is used only to motivate, not to support, the claim."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by an unmet endolysosomal degradative demand: transcripts for soluble luminal acid hydrolases (notably the lipid/glycoconjugate-directed GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, plus CTSB/CTSD/CTSK) and V-ATPase subunits are selectively elevated far above the already up-shifted background of the supplied differential-expression list, while transcripts for lysosomal membrane/structural and hydrolase-sorting components and for phagocytic uptake receptors sit at or below that background, and multi-candidate 2D protein spots containing cathepsins, HEXB and a V-ATPase subunit show no coherent increase (several decrease). We propose that mature luminal hydrolytic capacity per lysosome, not cargo uptake and not transcription of hydrolases, is the bottleneck, so lipid-rich cargo is processed more slowly in APOE4, with overflow routed to esterification/storage and to elevated mitochondrial oxidative transcripts. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating cargo-flux test: after a pulse of a quenched degradation reporter plus lipid-rich cargo (DQ-BSA together with fluorescent myelin or acetylated-LDL), APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater internalization at short times but a lower dequenching/degradation rate per unit internalized cargo and greater residual undegraded substrate at 6-24 h than isogenic APOE3; if per-cargo degradation rate is equal or faster in APOE4, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Capacity-versus-transcript test: measured maximal acid hydrolase activities (GBA, HEXA, GAA, cathepsin B/D) per mg lysosome-enriched protein should increase far less than the corresponding transcript ratios, and mature (processed) hydrolase forms on immunoblot should not rise proportionally; proportional increases in mature enzyme and activity with normal cargo clearance would weaken the mechanism.", "Causal relief test: augmenting luminal capacity (recombinant/chaperone-boosted GBA or HEXA delivery, or acid-lipase-independent reduction of lipid cargo load) should normalize cargo clearance in APOE4 and, secondarily, reduce the hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript excess and the OXPHOS/TCA transcript excess; if the transcript program and oxidative program persist after cargo clearance is restored, the demand-driven step is wrong.", "Directionality test against the mitochondrial alternative: acute mitochondrial inhibition (oligomycin or UK5099) in APOE3 cells should not reproduce the APOE4 hydrolase/V-ATPase transcript signature, whereas low-dose V-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) in APOE3 cells should shift them toward the APOE4 pattern; the opposite result would place the mitochondrial change upstream and weaken this hypothesis.", "Uptake-specificity test: TREM2/MERTK-dependent uptake rate should be similar between genotypes (consistent with these receptor transcripts sitting at background), so any observed APOE4 cargo accumulation should be abolished by blocking degradation-independent routes only if uptake is unchanged; a large APOE4 increase in uptake rate would indicate an intake-driven rather than capacity-driven mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, not measured): APOE4 protein alters the composition and physical handling of lipid/lipoprotein cargo that enters or is generated inside microglial endosomes and lysosomes; no lipid, cargo-flux or APOE-protein pool was measured here, and the APOE transcript itself is only at background level (gene:APOE, percentile 0.38 of the supplied list).", "Step 2 (measured abundance): a MiT/TFE-type, CLEAR-like transcriptional demand signal is elevated - gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are positive and soluble luminal acid hydrolase transcripts are strongly enriched in the extreme upper tail of the supplied list (6/15 hydrolases above the 90th percentile of all 2212 rows, binomial p approx 2e-3), together with every measured V-ATPase subunit (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C highest).", "Step 3 (measured abundance, discordance): the organelle scaffold and hydrolase-delivery arm does not scale with this program - gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLCN7 sit at or below the list median, gene:M6PR (cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor) is decreased, and gene:CTSS is one of the most decreased rows, narrowing the microglial protease repertoire.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, cross-modality): hydrolase-containing 2D protein spots give no coherent abundance increase and split by proteoform - protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up but protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069 down, and both spots whose candidate lists include a V-ATPase subunit are down (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065); spot identities are ambiguous (5-6 candidate genes each), so this is a failure to confirm a protein-level increase rather than proof of a decrease.", "Step 5 (inferred activity/flux, not measured): consequently the delivered, mature, acid-active hydrolase pool rises much less than the transcript pool, so hydrolysis flux per unit internalized cargo falls in APOE4 and partly degraded lipid/glycolipid cargo persists in late endosomes/lysosomes; no degradation-rate, pH, or substrate measurement exists in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, consistent overflow): uptake is not co-amplified with degradation (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:C1QA all at background percentile 0.39-0.46), while esterification/lipogenic transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:SCP2, gene:DGAT1) and mitochondrial oxidative transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA and the nuclear OXPHOS module) are elevated, consistent with lipid overflow being stored and oxidised and with the ATP demand of sustained V-ATPase acidification.", "Step 7 (predicted phenotype): APOE4 microglia therefore accumulate undegraded endolysosomal cargo and clear a new cargo bolus more slowly per unit internalized material than APOE3, despite equal or greater expression of the hydrolase genes themselves."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a demand-driven luminal hydrolase program that is not matched at the organelle/protein level, making mature endolysosomal hydrolytic capacity the rate-limiting step for lipid/glycoconjugate cargo processing"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17198980910534284, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.026872750260234415, "cosine_similarity": 0.22022553292813324, "direction_accuracy": 0.17313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6576537216828479, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17198980910534284, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.026872750260234415, "cosine_similarity": 0.22022553292813324, "direction_accuracy": 0.17313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6576537216828479, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.064334, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 358}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_033", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment claims are made by rank comparison against this selected list only, and the true whole-transcriptome background is unknown.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and relative ordering are used for inference, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The global up-shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46) may partly reflect normalization, cell-composition or pseudobulk-depth differences between genotypes rather than true global induction; rank-based statistics were used because they are invariant to a uniform shift.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; assigning a spot to a lysosomal protein is a possibility, not an identification, and spot-level discordance is treated as weak evidence only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to reflect a transcriptional program but not enzyme activity, protein maturation, lysosomal delivery, luminal pH, or degradative flux, none of which were measured.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured signal could arise from non-microglial cells or from genotype-dependent astrocyte-microglia interaction rather than microglia-autonomous APOE4 effects.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported p-values cannot be independently assessed and multiple-testing burden across the ~15 gene sets I tested is not controlled.", "No lipid, cargo, pH, or flux measurement is present in the supplied data despite the experiment identifier referencing lipid; the cargo-load premise (Step 1) is unverified background reasoning."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated, background-corrected elevation of lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (with TFEB and late-endosome/Rab7 trafficking transcripts also elevated), which we interpret as a compensatory demand signal rather than achieved capacity, because protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal enzymes/subunits are not correspondingly elevated. We propose that the primary bottleneck is delivered, catalytically competent lysosomal degradative capacity per unit endolysosomal cargo - most specifically for glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin-type cargo - so that transcriptional upregulation is a response to, not a resolution of, undegraded luminal cargo. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in a matched pulse-chase of a defined lysosomal lipid cargo (e.g. fluorescent lactosylceramide or BODIPY-sphingomyelin) plus DQ-BSA proteolysis, APOE4 microglia should clear cargo more slowly per cell than isogenic APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts, i.e. measured acid GBA/HEXA-HEXB/GAA activity per cell should rise less than proportionally to the transcript difference. If APOE4 shows equal or faster cargo clearance and enzyme activities that scale with or exceed transcript increases, the degradative-capacity bottleneck is falsified and the transcript module should be reinterpreted as successful adaptation.", "TFEB dependence: knockdown or degron depletion of TFEB in APOE4 microglia should collapse the hydrolase plus v-ATPase transcript module substantially more than in APOE3 and should further increase undegraded cargo. If the hydrolase module is unchanged by TFEB loss, Step 3 is falsified.", "Capacity-supply rescue: raising delivered degradative capacity specifically (recombinant/overexpressed GBA or acid sphingomyelinase, or hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin cargo relief) should reduce cargo accumulation and lower the endogenous hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript module in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. Failure of the transcript module to fall after cargo relief would weaken the feedback-loop interpretation.", "Acidification dependence and mitochondrial coupling: partial v-ATPase inhibition (low-dose bafilomycin A1 or concanamycin) should be more toxic and should raise undegraded cargo more in APOE4 than APOE3; conversely, imposing lysosomal cargo overload on APOE3 microglia should reproduce part of the OXPHOS/TCA transcript elevation. If OXPHOS/TCA transcripts are unaffected by lysosomal load in APOE3, Step 6 coupling is rejected and a primary mitochondrial mechanism becomes the better explanation.", "Protein-level test of the discordance: targeted immunoblot or targeted mass spectrometry of mature CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXB, LAMP1 and ATP6V1A in APOE4 versus APOE3 should show protein increases that are absent or markedly smaller than the transcript increases, and an increased pro-form to mature-form ratio for cathepsins. If mature protein rises in proportion to transcript for all of these, Step 4 and the bottleneck framing are falsified.", "Specificity control: the enrichment of the lysosomal degradome above background should persist in an unbiased whole-transcriptome APOE4 versus APOE3 comparison with matched expression-level and detection-rate covariates. If it disappears under that background, the module is an artifact of the selected DE list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred, not measured): APOE4 alters the composition and/or clearance kinetics of lipid-rich endocytic and phagocytic cargo delivered to late endosomes/lysosomes in microglia, increasing luminal load of glycosphingolipid- and sphingomyelin-type substrates. No lipid, cargo-flux or luminal-pool measurement is supplied; this step is a premise, not an observation.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): The lysosomal degradome transcript module is elevated above the strong global up-shift of this selected DE list - sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid catabolic enzymes (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH, gene:GM2A, gene:GBA2) together with gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DNASE2 (rank-based enrichment z = +2.98 versus all supplied RNA rows; robust to leave-one-out).", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred regulator): This module is accompanied by elevated gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC, gene:MITF and by all supplied v-ATPase subunit transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6AP2, gene:ATP6V0D2), plus late-endosomal/lysosomal transport transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B, gene:VPS18, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:SLC17A5, gene:SLC38A7, gene:NPC2). We infer, but did not measure, MiT/TFE-family transcriptional activity and nuclear localization; transcript abundance is not activity.", "Step 4 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): Protein spots whose candidate-gene lists include lysosomal hydrolases or v-ATPase subunits are not elevated (median log2 = +0.07, 50% up, n = 20 spots) whereas the remaining spots are elevated (median +0.49, 75% up, n = 72; permutation p = 0.078). Because each spot has multiple candidate genes, this is a weak, non-identifying discordance signal, not proof that any specific lysosomal protein is unchanged.", "Step 5 (inferred): Consequently, achieved acid-hydrolase activity and cargo-clearance flux in APOE4 lysosomes fail to rise in proportion to hydrolase transcript demand, leaving undegraded glycosphingolipid/protein cargo and sustaining the transcriptional program as a feedback loop. Neither enzyme activity, luminal pH, cargo half-life, nor lysosomal localization was measured here.", "Step 6 (inferred coupling, alternative-explanation aware): The strongest single module in these data is nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:DLD; enrichment z = +3.95, higher than the lysosomal module). We propose this is at least partly coupled to the increased ATP demand of sustained v-ATPase-driven acidification and biosynthesis of the degradative machinery, but a primary, lysosome-independent mitochondrial reprogramming in APOE4 remains a fully viable competing explanation that these data cannot exclude."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a TFEB/CLEAR-like lysosomal-degradome transcript program that is not matched at the protein-spot level, indicating a glycosphingolipid-directed lysosomal degradative-capacity bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07827788649706457, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.001359410313269479, "cosine_similarity": 0.2198861770952619, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6498673139158576, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07827788649706457, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.001359410313269479, "cosine_similarity": 0.2198861770952619, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6498673139158576, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.60780325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 359}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_017", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks and module-versus-background contrasts are interpreted, not absolute fold magnitudes.", "The 77% upward skew of this selected differential-expression list may be technical (normalisation, ambient RNA from the astrocyte co-culture, or DE-list selection); the mechanism therefore rests only on enrichment ABOVE that global shift, and would be undermined if the shift is a gene-length/depth artefact that also correlates with lysosomal gene identity.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for compartment biogenesis; enzyme protein level, maturation, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, and cargo flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Elevated gene:TFEB RNA is assumed, not shown, to correspond to increased TFEB nuclear activity; mTORC1 status was not measured.", "No lipid species, lipid droplet, or lysosomal-load measurement is present in the supplied data despite the experiment identifier; all statements about lipid pools are predictions, not observations.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are not used as primary support.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so absence of a gene (e.g. P2RY12, LIPA, PSAP, UGCG) is uninformative and pathway coverage is incomplete.", "Genotype association is correlative; nothing here establishes that APOE4 causes the lysosomal state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase compartment (GAA, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1, MAN2B1, GLA, CTSB/CTSD/CTSH, DPP7, DNASE2, ATP6V1A/1E1/1F/1H/0D1, ATP6AP1, GPNMB, SCARB2, LAMP1, with TFEB RNA also elevated). We hypothesise this is a compensatory CLEAR-type response to a rate-limiting step in the hydrolysis and egress of internalised sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo, and that the accompanying acyl-remodelling/esterification genes (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, SCD, MGLL, CHPT1) are a downstream buffering sink rather than the primary lesion. Causality is not established by these data; the lysosomal lipid pool itself was not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: pulse-chase of a traceable membrane cargo (e.g. NBD- or BODIPY-sphingomyelin-labelled apoptotic-cell or myelin membrane) should show a LOWER fractional degradation rate per unit lysosomal volume in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher hydrolase transcripts. If APOE4 clears the cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3, the state reflects increased capacity rather than a bottleneck and the central claim is falsified.", "TFEB dependency: TFEB knockdown or a TFEB-nuclear-translocation block should collapse the hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript elevation preferentially in APOE4 and worsen cargo retention. Persistence of elevated GBA/HEXA/CTSD/GAA transcripts after effective TFEB loss would falsify the proposed transcriptional step.", "Phenocopy/rescue: sub-maximal pharmacological inhibition of GBA or SMPD1 in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 signature (GPNMB, CTSD, CTSB, LAMP1 induction plus hexosylceramide/sphingomyelin accumulation), and isogenic APOE4-to-APOE3 correction should normalise it. Failure of correction to normalise the hydrolase module would indicate a clone- or culture-specific effect rather than an APOE4 mechanism.", "Ordering test against the glycerolipid alternative: DGAT1 or SOAT1 inhibition should NOT abolish the lysosomal hydrolase elevation (it should leave it unchanged or exacerbate downstream lipotoxic markers). If blocking esterification removes the hydrolase/GPNMB signature, glycerolipid storage is upstream and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Lipidomic prediction: APOE4 microglia should show higher per-cell glucosylceramide, hexosylceramide and sphingomyelin, and a higher LysoTracker/LAMP1 volume fraction, at day 30 mock. Equal or lower sphingolipid substrate levels alongside the observed hydrolase induction would weaken the bottleneck interpretation.", "Specificity control: the inflammatory/interferon programme should remain at background in APOE4 (as observed for the inflammatory module); a strong concurrent IL1B/TNF/ISG induction on independent measurement would favour an inflammation-driven rather than lysosomal-load-driven explanation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the pervasive positive shift of this selected differential-expression list (median +1.46 in unspecified log units), lysosomal-compartment transcripts are elevated well above background (module median +3.69 vs background +1.38 among genes with adjusted p \u003c 1e-50; permutation p = 0.0004), including glycosidases and sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1) and cathepsins (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH).", "Inferred (transcriptional driver, not demonstrated): elevated gene:TFEB RNA together with v-ATPase subunit RNAs (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V0D1) and gene:GPNMB is consistent with a CLEAR-network output; nuclear TFEB localisation and lysosomal acidification were not measured.", "Inferred (bottleneck): the hydrolase programme is a compensatory response to a limiting step in degradation and egress of internalised sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid-rich membrane cargo. Hydrolase mRNA induction is not matched by mannose-6-phosphate-receptor-dependent delivery/retrieval and egress components (gene:M6PR RNA is decreased, gene:IDS decreased, gene:NPC2 only marginally above background), so measured hydrolase transcript abundance need not translate into proportional intralysosomal degradative flux.", "Inferred (downstream sink): fatty acid and sterol liberated by, or diverted from, this compartment are buffered by re-esterification and acyl remodelling (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:SCD, gene:MGLL, gene:CHPT1) and by lipid-export/handling transcripts (gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1). As a set these glycerolipid genes are NOT enriched above the global shift (module median +1.59 vs background +1.46, permutation p = 0.68), so they are treated as secondary, not causal.", "Inferred (phenotypic consequence): chronic occupancy of this state should manifest as slower per-cell clearance of internalised membrane lipid cargo and a higher steady-state lysosomal substrate load in APOE4, accompanied by the most statistically robust markers of the state (gene:GPNMB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:LGALS3, gene:GPX4), rather than as a classical inflammatory activation (inflammatory transcripts sit at background: module median +1.20)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a TFEB-associated acid-hydrolase-expanded state in which lysosomal sphingolipid/membrane-cargo catabolic throughput, not glycerolipid synthesis, is the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.03622498281517076, "cosine_similarity": 0.2196935405989363, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.672252427184466, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1232876712328767, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.03622498281517076, "cosine_similarity": 0.2196935405989363, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.672252427184466, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03597775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 360}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_070", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong upward bias (77% positive, median +1.46); all set-level claims are therefore rank-based relative to that biased background, and RNA magnitudes are not directly comparable with the log2 protein-spot values.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the corresponding enzyme/subunit protein capacity; no protein measurement for HK2, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NNT, PRDX3 or the ETC subunits is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; spots 017-022 and 077 are used only as absence/presence-of-change evidence for the sets containing CAT, G6PD, PGD and PRDX2, never as identified single proteins.", "NADPH, GSH/GSSG, peroxiredoxin oxidation state, ROS, respiration and PPP flux were not measured in this dataset; every statement about flux, oxidant tone and localisation is inferred.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript signal is assumed to be interpretable despite probe-based 10X Flex quantification, ambient-RNA effects and the internally inconsistent MT-ND4L/MT-ND5 increases; if mito reads are artefactual, only STEP 2 (not the NADPH bottleneck) is lost.", "Astrocyte co-culture may supply extracellular cysteine/glutathione precursors, so the microglial NADPH shortfall is assumed not to be fully buffered by the co-cultured astrocytes.", "Replicate number and any batch structure are not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values are taken at face value."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated transcript shift toward mitochondrial oxidative metabolism (nuclear-encoded ETC and TCA transcripts uniformly higher, mtDNA-encoded core subunits mostly lower) combined with a selective decrease in the glucose-6-phosphate-to-NADPH module (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1, NADK) against a strongly up-biased background; we hypothesise that the resulting limitation of cytosolic NADPH regeneration, not peroxidase protein scarcity, is the primary bottleneck that leaves the up-regulated thiol-peroxidase system (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS) unable to keep pace with electron-leak-derived H2O2, producing a chronically oxidised thiol tone that accompanies the lysosomal and lipogenic transcript expansion. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, ROS and redox-state statements are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: acute G6PD/oxidative-PPP inhibition (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide, doses that do not change viability) in mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should produce a genotype-selective increase in cytosolic and mitochondrial H2O2 reporter oxidation (roGFP2-Orp1 / HyPer7) and in the PRDX2/PRDX3 dimer-to-monomer plus sulfinylated fraction, i.e. a significantly larger increment in APOE4 than APOE3; an equal or smaller APOE4 increment would weaken the NADPH-bottleneck claim.", "RESCUE, direction-testing: raising cytosolic NADPH supply independently of glycolysis (ectopic cytosolic G6PD or NADP+-dependent IDH1 expression, or cytosolic TPNOX-inverse controls) should normalise the APOE4 H2O2 reporter ratio and reduce BODIPY-C11 lipid peroxidation and lipid-droplet load without normalising the nuclear-encoded ETC transcript elevation; if ETC transcripts must also normalise before oxidant tone falls, the bottleneck is misassigned.", "MECHANISM-SEPARATING CONTROL: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ/SkQ1) or low-dose complex I inhibition should blunt the oxidant phenotype only partially and should NOT abolish the genotype-selective sensitivity to PPP inhibition; complete rescue by MitoQ with no residual PPP-inhibition sensitivity would favour a pure mitochondrial-leak model over the NADPH-supply model.", "FLUX TEST: [1,2-13C2]glucose labelling should show a lower oxidative-PPP-to-glycolysis flux ratio and a lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions; equal or higher PPP flux/NADPH ratio in APOE4 directly falsifies STEP 4.", "STOICHIOMETRY TEST: BN-PAGE/complexome profiling should show APOE4 accumulation of nuclear-encoded complex I/III/V subassemblies relative to fully assembled holocomplexes, with unchanged or reduced mtDNA-encoded core subunit protein; balanced assembly with normal supercomplex levels would falsify STEP 2 while leaving STEPS 3-5 testable.", "NULL-RESULT CRITERION: if APOE4 cells show unchanged or more reduced PRDX/GSH redox couples and no greater NADPH dependence despite the transcript pattern, the hypothesis is rejected in favour of a primary lipid/lysosomal-storage mechanism (SREBF1, SCD, MGLL, CTSB, GBA) with redox changes as a secondary consequence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels than APOE3 for every measured nuclear-encoded ETC subunit (39/39 up, median +2.65 vs global median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=4.3e-5) and for TCA/matrix enzymes (OGDH, MDH1, DLD, ACO2, GOT1), while most measured mtDNA-encoded subunits are lower (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2).", "STEP 2 (inferred activity/stoichiometry): the nuclear-versus-mtDNA imbalance is inferred to give sub-stoichiometric assembly of complexes I, III and V relative to the enlarged nuclear subunit pool, favouring electron leak and superoxide/H2O2 production per unit respiratory flux; neither assembly state nor ROS was measured here.", "STEP 3 (measured abundance, counter-trend module): transcripts governing entry of glucose into hexose-phosphate and the oxidative pentose-phosphate/NADPH route are selectively lower (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, TALDO1 -2.32, PGD -1.30, HK3 -1.12, NADK -1.14; all in the bottom ~22% of a distribution where only 23% of rows are negative; module-vs-background one-sided p=9.2e-4), and the protein spots whose candidate lists include G6PD or PGD are unchanged and non-significant (spots 018-022).", "STEP 4 (inferred flux, primary bottleneck): reduced hexokinase/PFK-dependent G6P supply plus lower PGD/TALDO1/NADK transcripts are inferred to lower cytosolic NADPH regeneration rate, making TXNRD1/GSR-dependent re-reduction of peroxiredoxins and glutathione the rate-limiting step; NNT (+2.88) and ME1 (+1.36) are read as partial, mitochondrially biased compensation rather than restoration of cytosolic NADPH.", "STEP 5 (measured abundance vs inferred state): higher peroxidase-system transcripts (PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, GPX4 +2.79, GSS +2.11, FTH1 +2.53) increase catalytic protein capacity but, without matched reductant supply, are predicted to sit in a more oxidised/hyperoxidised steady state; the redox state itself is not measured in these data.", "STEP 6 (inferred downstream, direction unresolved): the resulting chronic H2O2/thiol-oxidation tone is proposed to act on the concurrently expanded lysosomal-lipid machinery (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V subunits; SREBF1, SCD, MGLL, DGAT1) to favour oxidised-lipid storage and impaired lysosomal turnover in APOE4; whether oxidative tone drives, follows, or merely accompanies this lipid/lysosomal program cannot be resolved from these cross-sectional data."], "title": "NADPH-regeneration shortfall (low upper-glycolytic/oxidative-PPP transcript module) makes peroxiredoxin/glutathione recycling the rate-limiting step against a raised mitochondrial oxidant load in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1811191522357198, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1956194562418779, "cosine_similarity": 0.21887021772457368, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6829190938511327, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1811191522357198, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1956194562418779, "cosine_similarity": 0.21887021772457368, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6829190938511327, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.90134175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 361}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_159", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression table, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment claims are therefore made only relative to the same table, using permutations stratified by source_row because effect sign is strongly structured by row position (rows \u003e800 are ~100% positive).", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and some magnitudes are implausibly large, so only sign, rank and set-level contrasts are used; no absolute fold change is asserted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein supply of the same module; no protein, activity, pH, localisation or flux measurement of the endo-lysosomal or actin machinery is present in these data.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-uniquely identified; each spot is treated as a mixture of candidate gene products, so no single protein's abundance is claimed as observed.", "The absence of co-elevation of the actin module is assumed to be informative, which requires that actin-module genes had comparable opportunity to enter the selected list; genes absent from the list are unmeasured here, not unchanged.", "Astrocyte co-culture, mock treatment and day-30 state are assumed comparable between genotypes, so that genotype rather than culture composition drives the contrast."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated, background-corrected elevation of endo-lysosomal transcripts (v-ATPase subunits, luminal hydrolases, RAB7A, retromer/retriever, ESCRT, TFEB/TFEC) and of surface uptake-receptor transcripts, while the actin-nucleation/actomyosin and WASH module is not co-elevated and several of its members are among the lowest-effect transcripts. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step for cargo handling in APOE4 microglia is therefore the actin/myosin-dependent step (phagocytic cup closure, phagosome/endosome motility and WASH-dependent retrieval from late endosomes), not degradative enzyme supply; the transcriptional endo-lysosomal expansion is proposed to be a compensatory, TFEB-associated response to cargo that dwells in the late compartment. Causality is not established by these data; all flux, activity, acidification and localisation statements are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acutely restoring endosomal actin capacity in APOE4 microglia (WASHC1/WASHC4 re-expression or an actin/Arp2/3-activating manipulation) should increase cargo throughput - faster clearance of internalised pHrodo-myelin or fluorescent beads and restored surface recycling of TREM2/CD36 - while leaving v-ATPase and hydrolase transcript levels initially unchanged; if throughput does not improve while actin polymerisation is demonstrably restored, the actin-step bottleneck is wrong.", "Reciprocal test: pharmacological Arp2/3 inhibition (CK-666) or myosin-II inhibition in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 pattern (raised LAMP1/v-ATPase and TFEB target expression with cargo retained in late compartments); failure to phenocopy weakens the claim that the actin step is the primary bottleneck.", "Functional prediction: per-cell uptake of a defined cargo in APOE4 should be equal to or lower than APOE3 despite higher receptor transcripts, while LAMP1+ compartment volume and undigested cargo per cell are higher; a proportional increase in uptake rate in APOE4 would weaken Steps 3 and 5.", "Degradation-versus-capacity prediction: DQ-BSA dequenching per unit internalised cargo should be equal or higher in APOE4 (hydrolase capacity not limiting) while bulk cargo clearance is slower; if DQ-BSA dequenching per internalised cargo is lower in APOE4, the bottleneck lies in degradative capacity or acidification, not in the actin step.", "Normalisation control: absolute quantification (spike-in normalised RNA, qPCR against invariant references, or protein blot for CTSB/ATP6V1A/LAMP1) should confirm genuine elevation of the endo-lysosomal module in APOE4; if the module is flat after spike-in normalisation, the entire signal is a compositional artefact of the selected list and the hypothesis fails.", "Specificity control: if the endo-lysosomal elevation cannot be separated from a general biogenesis shift - i.e. mitochondrial complex I and translation-initiation proteins rise to the same degree at the protein level - then the mechanism should be demoted to a non-specific cell-state difference rather than an endo-lysosomal bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_159", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred supply): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels than APOE3 for phagocytic/scavenger receptors (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:MRC1, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:ITGAX), giving an inferred increase in receptor supply; surface receptor protein, ligand binding and uptake rate were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred organelle program): The endo-lysosomal module is elevated after correction for the strong list-wide upward shift: v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6V1E1), luminal hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB), late-endosomal and sorting machinery (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:VPS37B, gene:AP3D1, gene:DNM2, gene:CLTB, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2), and the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors gene:TFEB and gene:TFEC. We infer expanded degradative-compartment biogenesis; lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity and organelle volume were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, negative result): The actin/actomyosin module is not co-elevated. Its members sit at or below the list background (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:FAM49B, gene:WASHC4, gene:SYNJ1 all negative) even though some nucleation subunits are positive (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC5, gene:CFL1). We infer that the actin-dependent capacity for cup closure, phagosome/endosome transport and WASH-driven retrieval does not scale with Steps 1-2.", "Step 4 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): 2D protein spots whose candidate lists contain actin and actin regulators shift in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:029, protein_spot:036, protein_spot:092 up; protein_spot:069, protein_spot:009, protein_spot:065 down), and cathepsin-containing spots also split (protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067 down). Because each spot has several candidate genes, this is read only as redistribution among cytoskeletal/hydrolase protein forms, not as a uniform increase of any named protein.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): With receptor and hydrolase supply raised but the actin step unchanged, internalised cargo per receptor is predicted to be limited and internalised material to dwell longer in a hydrolase-rich late compartment, with slower retromer/WASH-dependent retrieval of receptors and lipid-handling cargo to the surface.", "Step 6 (inferred feedback): Persistent cargo dwell in the late compartment sustains the TFEB/TFEC-associated lysosomal-biogenesis program (gene:TFEB, gene:TFEC) and the coordinately raised lipid-handling transcripts (gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:LDLR, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD), forming a self-reinforcing loop of degradative expansion without matched cargo throughput. No lipid, cholesterol or droplet measurement is present in these data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia scale up uptake-receptor and endo-lysosomal degradative transcripts without scaling the actin/myosin module, placing the rate limit on actin-dependent cargo internalization and endosomal retrieval"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09840121109182881, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09474870972824312, "cosine_similarity": 0.21831893620274354, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_159", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6320873786407767, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09840121109182881, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09474870972824312, "cosine_similarity": 0.21831893620274354, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6320873786407767, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1114575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 362}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every |effect| exceeds 1) with 77.1% positive values and a global median of +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base; all directional claims are therefore made relative to that global median, not to zero, and the global shift is assumed to be a shared normalisation/composition offset rather than a pathway signal.", "Steady-state transcript differences are assumed to track enzyme abundance and, at the pathway level, oxidative and glycolytic capacity; no enzyme activity, metabolite, flux, respiration, NADPH, redox or lipid pool was measured here.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-unique: each carries several candidate genes, so no spot is used to assign abundance to a single protein, and spot data are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "Cells are assumed to be correctly assigned microglia despite astrocyte co-culture; ambient RNA or imperfect demultiplexing in the 10X Flex data could inflate or distort shared metabolic transcripts.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the extremely small adjusted p-values are assumed to reflect cell-level rather than donor/line-level replication, and genotype and line background are assumed to be confounded only by the stated isogenic design.", "APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed to be at comparable differentiation stage and density at day 30, so that the metabolic contrast is not a maturation artefact."], "claim": "Relative to the strong global upward shift of this filtered APOE4-vs-APOE3 DE list, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally contract cytosolic glucose entry and pentose-phosphate throughput (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1 all below the global median) while coordinately elevating lysosomal acid hydrolases, mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA, beta-oxidation and every measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node is hexokinase/PFKP-level glucose-6-phosphate utilisation and its PPP branch; with that arm constrained, lysosomally released fatty acids, sphingoid bases and sterol become the dominant carbon/ATP source, and the fraction that exceeds mitochondrial oxidative disposal is re-esterified by an up-regulated SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1/DGAT1/SOAT1 acylation program into MUFA-enriched neutral lipid. All flux, activity, localisation and lipid-pool statements are inferred; only RNA effects and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Stable-isotope tracing: APOE4 microglia should show a lower fraction of [U-13C6]glucose carbon in lactate and in PPP-derived ribose-5-phosphate/nucleotides, and a higher fraction of 13C from [U-13C16]palmitate or lysosomally delivered lipoprotein lipid in TCA intermediates (citrate, malate, glutamate), than isogenic APOE3. Equal or higher glucose oxidation and lactate output in APOE4 would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Discriminating pharmacology: APOE4 microglia should be relatively resistant to 2-deoxyglucose or hexokinase inhibition and relatively hypersensitive (ATP, viability, phagocytic capacity) to oligomycin/rotenone, to CPT1 inhibition with etomoxir, and to lysosomal acid-hydrolase or v-ATPase blockade (bafilomycin A1, conduritol-B-epoxide). If APOE4 is instead the more 2-DG-sensitive genotype and no more oligomycin- or etomoxir-sensitive than APOE3, the mechanism is weakened.", "Lipidomic prediction for the planned lipid endpoint: mock APOE4 microglia should carry more triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester per cell and a higher MUFA:SFA ratio (16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 in TAG and phospholipids), with sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide depleted relative to ceramide. Finding accumulated sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide with unchanged or reduced neutral lipid would indicate a functional lysosomal block rather than the proposed hydrolysis-fed oxidative overflow and would weaken Steps 3-5.", "NADPH/redox test: G6PD or 6PGD inhibition, buthionine sulfoximine, or GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) should produce disproportionately greater lipid peroxidation (BODIPY-C11) and death in APOE4 than APOE3, and SCD inhibition should convert APOE4 stores to a saturated, more toxic profile. Equal sensitivity across genotypes would weaken Step 6.", "Specificity/artefact test: in an unbiased, spike-in- or absolute-normalised whole-transcriptome re-measurement, the glycolysis/PPP set should remain below and the TCA/OXPHOS/lysosome sets above the transcriptome-wide centre, while control modules that here sit at baseline (vesicle trafficking, proteasome, complement/phagocytic receptors) remain at the centre. If the metabolic separation disappears once the global shift is removed, the mechanism is not supported.", "Causal test of the bottleneck: restoring glycolytic/PPP capacity in APOE4 microglia (HK2 or G6PD overexpression, or methyl-pyruvate/nucleoside bypass) should reduce dependence on fatty-acid oxidation and shrink neutral-lipid stores without changing APOE genotype; no change in lipid stores would show the glycolytic node is not upstream."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Glycolytic entry isoforms and PPP enzymes sit below the global up-shift baseline (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30 versus a global median of +1.46 across 2212 rows). We infer reduced glucose-6-phosphate flux into both glycolysis and the pentose-phosphate branch, and therefore reduced cytosolic NADPH regeneration. G6PD, TKT and RPIA RNA are absent from the supplied list and cytosolic NADPH was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A mitochondrial oxidative program is coordinately elevated well above baseline: pyruvate import (gene:MPC2 +7.98), TCA/anaplerosis (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02), lipid oxidation and acetate salvage (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:FABP3 +1.35, gene:FABP5 +1.13), and 37/37 measured nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits positive (e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36). We infer increased mitochondrial oxidative capacity, not measured respiration.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux and localisation): An expanded lysosomal degradative module supplies the lipid substrate: gene:TFEB +2.38 with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51), acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17), lysosomal solute export (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:NPC2 +1.17) and lipid/lipoprotein uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38). Lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity and cargo delivery were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred coupling): Because the glycolytic/PPP arm is contracted (Step 1) while pyruvate import and oxidative machinery are elevated (Step 2), we infer that lysosome-derived acyl chains and sphingoid backbones (Step 3), rather than glucose, carry the dominant oxidative flux in APOE4 microglia.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid pools): Lipid arriving faster than it is oxidised is routed to storage: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, with sterol arm gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SREBF2 +1.06. We predict, but did not measure, increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester and a MUFA-shifted acyl profile.", "Step 6 (inferred vulnerability): A contracted PPP arm plus increased desaturation and lipid load should lower spare NADPH for glutathione/thioredoxin recycling; compensatory peroxide-handling transcripts are elevated (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:GPX4 +2.79). We infer, without redox measurement, that APOE4 microglia sit closer to a lipid-peroxidation threshold. A possible additional ceiling on respiration is that mtDNA-encoded subunits do not follow the nuclear subunits (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33, against gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95); this mitonuclear discordance is suggestive only and may be technical."], "title": "Hexokinase/PPP contraction makes lysosome-derived lipid the obligate mitochondrial fuel in APOE4 microglia, with overflow into re-esterified neutral lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4878983125946165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2804743947169879, "cosine_similarity": 0.21770934010036352, "direction_accuracy": 0.3802588996763754, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6677087378640777, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4878983125946165, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2804743947169879, "cosine_similarity": 0.21770934010036352, "direction_accuracy": 0.3802588996763754, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6677087378640777, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.35291025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 363}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_093", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are made only relative to the internal background of these 2212 rows, and the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and left unconverted.", "The direction of the nuclear-versus-mtDNA transcript split is robust to library-size normalisation because the two groups move oppositely within the same assay; absolute magnitudes are not assumed to be quantitative.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript level is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the availability of the corresponding mtDNA-encoded protein for assembly; probe-based 10X Flex capture of mitochondrial transcripts is assumed not to be systematically biased between the two isogenic genotypes.", "Reduced holo-complex assembly is assumed to be rate-limiting for respiratory flux in these cells rather than substrate supply; fatty-acid-oxidation transcripts were not enriched above background, consistent with but not proving this.", "Protein spots are ambiguous multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is assumed to identify a unique protein, and no ETC subunit was among the spot candidates (only MDH1, non-significant), so the protein layer cannot confirm or refute the assembly claim.", "Astrocyte co-culture and possible ambient RNA (e.g. gene:S100B, gene:A2M elevated) are assumed not to drive the mito-nuclear split; genotype-independent clone or maturation differences are assumed controlled by the isogenic design.", "Causality has not been established by these data; the mechanism is a proposed, testable ordering of events."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia amplify the nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation/TCA transcript program while transcripts for the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores of complexes I, III, IV and V (MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) are lower than in APOE3. We hypothesise that the limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for holo-complex assembly, so the extra nuclear-encoded subunits cannot be productively incorporated; the resulting stoichiometric mismatch produces unassembled subunit load, an integrated-stress/mitochondrial-proteostasis response, and a compensatory catabolic (mitophagy/lysosomal, lipid-handling) transcriptional arm. The lysosomal program is treated as a downstream compensatory arm, not the primary bottleneck, because lysosomal transcripts are not elevated above the strong global up-shift of this selected differential-expression list and the protein spots containing lysosomal candidates move in both directions.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: blue-native PAGE plus in-gel activity on APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex I, III2+IV and V per unit mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOM20 normalised), with an increased free/subassembly pool of nuclear-encoded subunits (e.g. NDUFB8, ATP5F1B) on denaturing follow-up. If assembled complex levels are equal or higher in APOE4 and no orphan subunit pool is detected, the mechanism is falsified.", "Metabolic flux: extracellular flux analysis should show lower FCCP-stimulated maximal oxygen consumption and lower spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass in APOE4, despite the higher nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts, and lower ATP-linked respiration relative to citrate synthase activity. Equal or greater maximal OCR per mitochondrial mass would weaken the mechanism.", "Causal-direction test on the supply step: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit output (TFAM or POLRMT overexpression, or mitochondrial transfer/mtDNA repletion) should raise assembled complex levels and lower DDIT3 and HSPA9 transcripts in APOE4; conversely, ISR suppression with ISRIB should reduce DDIT3 without restoring assembled complexes. If ISRIB alone normalises complex assembly, the causal arrow is inverted and the stress response, not core-subunit supply, is upstream.", "Discriminating test against the endolysosomal alternative: blocking lysosomal capacity in APOE3 microglia (bafilomycin A1 or TFEB knockdown) should not reproduce the signature nuclear-up/mtDNA-down transcript split, whereas inhibiting mitochondrial translation (chloramphenicol/doxycycline) in APOE3 should reproduce it. If lysosomal blockade alone reproduces the split, the lysosomal arm is upstream and this hypothesis should be replaced by a lysosomal-capacity mechanism.", "Independent quantification: RT-qPCR or a non-probe-based scRNA-seq chemistry should confirm lower MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 in APOE4, and should also show MT-ND4L consistent with MT-ND4 (they derive from one bicistronic transcript). Persistent discordance between MT-ND4 and MT-ND4L on an independent platform would indicate a quantification artefact and weaken the core observation.", "Specificity: mtDNA copy number per nuclear genome and mtDNA integrity should be equal or reduced in APOE4; if mtDNA copy number is substantially higher in APOE4 while mtDNA transcripts are lower, a transcription/turnover rather than a supply-limited assembly model is favoured."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA abundance: nuclear-encoded ETC and TCA transcripts are coordinately higher in APOE4 (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:COX6B1, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:ATP5ME, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2), together with mitochondrial import/translation-apparatus transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:TUFM, gene:OXA1L, gene:GFM2, gene:MTRES1, gene:MTPAP). Transcript abundance is measured; biogenesis rate and mitochondrial mass are inferred, not measured.", "Measured RNA abundance, opposite direction: the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores of four ETC complexes are lower in APOE4 (gene:MT-ND4 complex I, gene:MT-CYB complex III, gene:MT-CO2 complex IV, gene:MT-ATP6 complex V), with gene:MT-ATP6 among the most statistically confident calls in the dataset. Because this split is directional within the same assay, it is not explainable by a uniform library-size/normalisation shift.", "Inferred assembly bottleneck (not measured): each affected complex requires its mtDNA-encoded core for nucleation and stabilisation, so reduced core supply caps the number of assembled holo-complexes irrespective of the elevated nuclear-encoded accessory subunit transcripts. Predicted consequence is a pool of orphan/unincorporated nuclear-encoded subunits and reduced assembled complex I/III/IV/V per unit mitochondrial mass.", "Inferred proteostatic and stress response: orphan subunits and reduced coupling engage mitochondrial chaperone/import and eIF2alpha-kinase signalling, consistent with higher gene:HSPA9, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3, gene:SHMT2 and higher translation-factor transcripts (gene:EIF2A, gene:EIF4E, gene:EIF3L, gene:EIF2S3). Kinase activity, eIF2alpha phosphorylation and ATF4 protein are inferred, not observed.", "Inferred organelle remodelling: partial compensation by inner-membrane/cardiolipin and fission machinery (gene:TAZ, gene:PRELID3B, gene:SLC25A1, gene:CHCHD3, gene:CHCHD2, gene:FIS1, gene:SLC25A46), predicted to fragment and turn over mitochondria rather than restore per-complex flux.", "Downstream, secondary arm: increased demand for organelle and lipid turnover raises CLEAR-type and lysosomal/lipid transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:GPNMB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:APOE). This arm is placed downstream because it is not enriched over the list-wide up-shift and because acidification/hydrolase-containing protein spots are discordant (protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065 down, protein_spot:067 down, protein_spot:058 down versus protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 up).", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia carry more mitochondrial building blocks but less assembled, coupled respiratory chain per mitochondrion, with chronic low-grade mitochondrial stress signalling and increased reliance on lysosomal turnover. Flux, membrane potential and localisation are all inferred; none were measured here."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch: mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit supply, not lysosomal capacity, is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0547945205479452, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06451747566623327, "cosine_similarity": 0.2149054622517572, "direction_accuracy": 0.09223300970873786, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6234660194174758, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0547945205479452, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06451747566623327, "cosine_similarity": 0.2149054622517572, "direction_accuracy": 0.09223300970873786, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6234660194174758, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.78754325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 364}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_038", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (no |effect| below ~1.0; 1705/2212 positive; median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base), so 'increased' is interpreted as rank within this biased list, judged by permutation against the list's own distribution, not as an unbiased transcriptome-wide change.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme and SNARE protein amount; no protein, enzymatic-activity, localisation or lipid measurements for these genes are supplied, so flux, ceramide/sphingosine pools and lysosomal positioning are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:006/007/063 include GNS but also GSN, KRT and other proteins), so spot-level changes are treated as weak, non-gene-specific corroboration only.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; some transcript differences may reflect altered microglial state, maturation or co-culture cross-talk rather than a cell-autonomous APOE4 effect.", "Key nodes of the pathway were not measured (ASAH1, PSAP, UGCG, SGMS1/2, CERT1, SPTLC1/2, NPC1, GRN, MCOLN1, LAMP2, HOPS subunits, PLEKHM1), so the anabolic and sphingoid-base-salvage arms are only partly observable.", "The direction of causality between reduced trafficking transcripts and elevated hydrolase transcripts is assumed (routing limitation upstream of compensation) but is not established by the data; the reverse or a shared upstream driver remains possible."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference is best explained by a routing bottleneck rather than by an enzyme-capacity bottleneck: transcripts for lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, SMPD1, SUMF1) are coordinately high within the supplied differential-expression list (mean percentile rank 0.76, permutation p = 0.011) while the SNARE/fusion module that delivers cargo and newly made hydrolases to lysosomes (STX16, STX17, VAMP2, STXBP5, SEC22A, M6PR) is coordinately low (mean percentile rank 0.28, permutation p = 0.023) and the sphingolipid anabolic/glycosylation arm is not co-elevated (B4GALT5, ST3GAL2 low; CERS6, KDSR, SGPL1 below list median). We propose that limited membrane delivery to the degradative compartment restricts glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin turnover flux, and that the elevated hydrolase transcripts are a compensatory, TFEB-associated response to that limitation rather than evidence of increased degradation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of purified APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher glucosylceramide, lactosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin per cell despite the higher hydrolase transcript levels; if these species are equal or lower in APOE4, the high-enzyme/low-flux claim is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring STX17 (and/or STX16) expression in APOE4 microglia should increase sphingolipid catabolic flux and lower accumulated glycosphingolipids and should also reduce the compensatory hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB) toward APOE3 levels, whereas over-expressing GBA/HEXA or adding recombinant enzyme alone should NOT normalise the lipid pools. If enzyme supplementation alone normalises the lipids while SNARE restoration does not, the bottleneck is hydrolase capacity and this mechanism is rejected.", "Pulse-chase flux assay with BODIPY-lactosylceramide or NBD-sphingomyelin should show slower substrate clearance and slower arrival in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4 than APOE3; faster per-cell clearance in APOE4 would falsify the mechanism.", "TFEB knockdown should lower the hydrolase transcript elevation and worsen glycosphingolipid accumulation (consistent with compensation); if the hydrolase elevation persists unchanged after TFEB knockdown, the CLEAR-compensation step is wrong even if the routing defect stands.", "Sorting test: APOE4 cultures should show a higher ratio of secreted to cell-associated beta-hexosaminidase/GBA activity than APOE3; an unchanged ratio would weaken the M6PR-missorting sub-step while leaving the fusion sub-step testable.", "If pharmacological or genetic block of de novo sphingolipid synthesis (myriocin, SPTLC1 knockdown) normalises the APOE4 lipid and hydrolase-transcript phenotype, the bottleneck is synthesis rather than routing and this hypothesis is weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the load of sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo (myelin-like/plasma-membrane and apoptotic-debris membranes) entering the microglial endo-lysosomal system; this cargo pool is inferred, not measured here.", "Reduced abundance of transcripts encoding fusion and retrograde SNARE machinery (gene:STX17, gene:STX16, gene:VAMP2, gene:STXBP5, gene:SEC22A) and of gene:M6PR predicts lower rates of autophagosome/late-endosome-to-lysosome fusion and of mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery; this is inferred activity and localisation, not measured flux.", "Consequently, sphingolipid substrates and newly synthesised hydrolases are less efficiently co-localised in the acidified degradative lumen, so per-lysosome catabolic flux rises less than enzyme expression does (inferred; no lipid, activity or imaging data supplied).", "The resulting undegraded glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin load engages a TFEB/CLEAR-type compensatory transcriptional response, seen as elevated gene:TFEB together with hydrolase transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C); TFEB nuclear localisation and activity were not measured.", "The response is selectively catabolic rather than a general lipid program: de novo/glycosylation steps are flat or reduced (gene:B4GALT5, gene:ST3GAL2 low; gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:SGPL1 below the list median), so ceramide/sphingoid-base handling capacity is not expanded in proportion to the hydrolase arm.", "Net predicted state: normal-to-high hydrolase protein with sub-proportional intralysosomal flux, accumulation of GlcCer/LacCer/GM2/sphingomyelin in APOE4 microglia, and a measurable shift of hydrolase activity toward the extracellular medium if M6PR-dependent sorting is also impaired."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a catabolism-skewed sphingolipid transcript program with reduced SNARE-dependent lysosomal delivery: a high-enzyme / low-flux turnover bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.00399199843827393, "cosine_similarity": 0.21382006435269899, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6523171521035599, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.00399199843827393, "cosine_similarity": 0.21382006435269899, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6523171521035599, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.61450875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 365}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list in an unspecified logarithm base; 1705/2212 (77%) are positive, so coherent up-programs were judged against that background and only the glycolysis/PPP set deviates downward (6 up/6 down, permutation p_down=0.038). A housekeeping control set (16/16 spliceosome transcripts up) shows that up-coherence alone is weak evidence.", "Missing genes (e.g. SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1, ASAH1, PSAP, NEU1, GALC, NPC1, LIPA, GRN, SQSTM1, MCOLN1, G6PD) are unknown, not unchanged; the sphingolipid synthesis and autophagy arms are therefore untested rather than excluded.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the cell's investment in each machinery; no enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, degradative flux, lipid pool, respiration or NADPH measurement is supplied, so all flux and routing statements are inferences.", "2D protein spots are ambiguous (69/92 spots list 5+ candidate genes); no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein. Spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, preserving all candidate identities.", "Genes within a program are not independent (shared regulation, co-expression), so descriptive coherence and permutation statistics on this selected list are not formal enrichment results.", "The astrocyte co-culture and iPSC differentiation state are assumed comparable between genotypes; genotype-linked differences in cell-state composition (single-cell 10X Flex pseudobulk) could produce the same program-level pattern without any per-cell change."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated shift of transcriptional investment toward lipid/lipoprotein internalization, endosome-to-lysosome routing and lysosomal hydrolytic-acidification capacity (including the glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin hydrolase arm GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, SMPD1, GBA2, GLTP) coupled to mitochondrial carrier/TCA/ETC transcripts, while glycolytic-entry and pentose-phosphate transcripts (HK2, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD, NAMPT) fall against a strongly up-biased selected-DE background (1705/2212 positive). We interpret this as a substrate-driven, largely successful catabolic-oxidative adaptation rather than a demonstrated lysosomal bottleneck: no degradative flux, hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH or respiration was measured, and the predicted liability (low glycolytic/NADPH reserve) is latent at baseline and expected to appear only under phagocytic or oxidative challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective activity test in the same mock condition: APOE4 microglia should show equal or higher per-cell lysosomal hydrolase activity and cargo degradation (GBA and HEXA/HEXB fluorogenic activity, acid sphingomyelinase activity, DQ-BSA proteolysis rate, LAMP1/LysoTracker area) together with a higher basal OCR and OCR:ECAR ratio. If instead hydrolase activities and DQ-BSA degradation are lower in APOE4 with accumulation of glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin by lipidomics and no increase in oxygen consumption, the 'expanded, functioning catabolic-oxidative state' reading fails and a failed-compensation bottleneck becomes the better model.", "Prospective substrate-load test: after a pulse of fluorescent myelin, apoptotic-neuron or oxLDL cargo, APOE4 should internalize and clear more cargo per cell per hour than APOE3. Knockdown of the uptake step (SCARB1, or LDLR) should blunt the lysosomal/hydrolase transcript program (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1H). If clearance is slower in APOE4 or the lysosomal program is unaffected by blocking uptake, step 1-2 of the mechanism is wrong.", "Prospective reserve-versus-defect test: at baseline APOE4 and APOE3 should show similar viability and similar cargo handling, but under an oxidative/phagocytic challenge (LPS+phagocytic burst, or PPP inhibition with 6-aminonicotinamide/G6PDi, or 2-deoxyglucose) APOE4 should show greater NADPH/GSH depletion and greater loss of clearance capacity. Equal challenge tolerance would weaken the glycolytic/PPP-reduction branch (HK2, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD, NAMPT) without affecting steps 2-5.", "Prospective sphingolipid-branch test: pharmacological block of the lysosomal sphingolipid arm (conduritol-B-epoxide for GBA, or SMPD1 inhibition) should cause faster glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin accumulation and earlier lysosomal swelling in APOE4 than APOE3 because more substrate is being routed through that arm. If APOE4 instead accumulates these lipids equally or less, the branch is not carrying higher load and the focus branch should be dropped.", "Prospective proteoform test for the ambiguous spots: targeted immunoblot/MS of CTSD, CTSB, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 should show redistribution between pro- and mature/processed forms in APOE4 rather than a uniform decrease in total protein. A uniform decrease in total mature cathepsins and V-ATPase subunits would contradict the expanded-capacity interpretation and support a degradative bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid capture and sterol handling (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:APOE +1.2, gene:SOAT1, gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:NPC2), which we infer increases delivery of lipid cargo into the endosomal system; the delivery rate itself is not measured.", "Step 2: Endosome maturation and sorting capacity is coordinately increased (gene:RAB7A +2.7, retromer/retriever gene:VPS26A +4.9, gene:VPS35L +3.5, gene:SNX3 +3.9, ESCRT gene:CHMP4B +3.8, gene:VPS28, gene:VPS37B, adaptors gene:AP5M1, gene:AP3D1, gene:CLTB; 26/28 represented members positive, median +2.5), plus mannose-6-phosphate-dependent hydrolase delivery components (gene:GNPTG +3.0, gene:IGF2R +2.0), routing cargo and newly made hydrolases toward lysosomes.", "Step 3: A MiT/TFE-associated lysosomal-biogenesis-like program raises hydrolase and V-ATPase transcripts (gene:TFEB +2.4, gene:TFEC +1.7, gene:MITF +1.0; gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.4, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6V0C +3.5, gene:LAMP1 +1.4; 38/40 represented members positive), expanding nominal degradative and acidification capacity.", "Step 4 (assigned focus, retained only as a branch): within that program the glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic arm is uniformly up (gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:GBA2 +2.6, gene:GLTP +2.4, gene:HEXB +2.2, gene:GM2A +2.0, gene:SGPL1 +1.1, 9/9 positive), whereas de novo sphingolipid synthesis genes are mostly unmeasured in this selected list and the represented ones are indistinguishable from background (gene:CERS4 +2.5, gene:ORMDL2 +1.9, gene:KDSR +1.3, gene:CERK +1.2, gene:CERS6 +1.1, gene:B4GALT5 -1.9); we therefore infer increased catabolic/routing capacity for sphingolipids, not a synthesis-driven mechanism.", "Step 5: Catabolic products are inferred to be routed to mitochondria: pyruvate/citrate/malate carriers and TCA/ETC transcripts rise coherently (gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5, gene:SLC25A11 +4.5, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:DLD +5.5, gene:ACO2 +3.5, gene:IDH3G +3.9, gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7 +5.7, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.7; 60/63 represented members positive, median +2.7).", "Step 6: Investment in glycolytic entry and the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway is selectively reduced against the up-biased background (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, gene:NAMPT -2.6, gene:TALDO1 -2.3, gene:PGD -1.3, gene:HK3 -1.1; 6 up/6 down where the list background is 77% up), i.e. the state is oxidative-biased rather than glycolysis-supported.", "Step 7 (latent consequence, not observed here): the resulting cell state should have a lower glycolytic and NADPH-regenerating reserve, so an APOE4-specific deficit is predicted to emerge under phagocytic, inflammatory or oxidative challenge, not in the measured mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lipid-catabolic, endolysosomal-and-mitochondrial cell state with reduced glycolytic/PPP investment; the sphingolipid arm is part of the expanded degradative program, not an isolated lesion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2290458959494886, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19693624240991833, "cosine_similarity": 0.21169202373797663, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6436666666666667, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2290458959494886, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.19693624240991833, "cosine_similarity": 0.21169202373797663, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6436666666666667, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.11213725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 93}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_098", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up, all q\u003c0.05), so significance was judged by percentile rank within this list rather than by raw sign; the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given.", "Transcript level is assumed to be a partial proxy for the production capacity of the encoded protein; no hydrolase protein abundance, maturation state, enzymatic activity or lysosomal localisation was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 2-5 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration (e.g. CTSD/CTSB/GNS/HEXB candidate spots change in both directions).", "No lipid, lipidomic, imaging, secretion or flux measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier referring to lipids; every statement about glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin, GM2, ceramide, S1P, lysosomal pH or vesicle traffic is inferred.", "Replicate number is not supplied and the cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous; the comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at one timepoint under mock treatment, so no causal direction is established.", "The trafficking gene set was hand-assembled; only a family-level regex screen (golgins, SNAREs, adaptors, glycosidases) was used to check that the contrast is not purely cherry-picked."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated increase in transcripts for lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, GM2A) and for lipid-uptake receptors, while the endosome-to-trans-Golgi retrograde receptor-recycling arm (M6PR, STX16, GCC1, GCC2, AP1M1) and the GBA carrier SCARB2 are relatively depressed; we hypothesise that receptor-dependent delivery of hydrolases to the lysosomal lumen, not hydrolase transcription, is the rate-limiting step, so per-lysosome sphingolipid catabolic activity fails to match the incoming lipid load and sphingolipid turnover is diverted to non-lysosomal routes (GBA2, SPNS1-dependent sphingoid-base export, CERS4/CERS6 salvage re-acylation, ST3GAL5, GLTP). All lipid pools, enzyme activities, localisations and fluxes are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: LAMP1/Lyso-IP purification from isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show equal or lower mature GBA, ASM (SMPD1) and beta-hexosaminidase protein and enzymatic activity per lysosome in APOE4 despite the \u003e2-fold higher transcripts, with a higher secreted/intracellular hexosaminidase activity ratio in conditioned medium. If lysosomal activity rises in proportion to transcript and the secreted fraction is unchanged, the routing-bottleneck mechanism is refuted.", "Rescue: restoring retrograde delivery (M6PR or STX16 re-expression, GCC2 rescue) or bypassing it with exogenous recombinant glucocerebrosidase uptake should lower lysosomal HexCer/SM/GM2 and normalise enlarged lysosome morphology in APOE4 without changing hydrolase transcript levels; no lipid correction under enzyme replacement would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy: knockdown of STX16 or GCC1/GCC2 in APOE3 microglia should reduce lysosomal GBA and ASM activity and raise HexCer/SM; if M6PR recycling is impaired without any sphingolipid change, routing is not the limiting step for sphingolipid turnover.", "Substrate prediction: Lyso-IP lipidomics should show APOE4-selective enrichment of glucosylceramide/HexCer, sphingomyelin and GM2, with C16-C24 ceramides consistent with CERS4/CERS6 salvage re-acylation; equal or lower HexCer/SM in APOE4 would falsify Step 4.", "Shunt test: GBA2 inhibition or SPNS1 knockdown should worsen lipid load and the GPNMB/LGALS3 activation signature selectively in APOE4 and not APOE3; an equal effect in both genotypes would weaken the claim that these are compensatory bypass routes.", "Specificity control: if instead lysosomal acidification is defective (LysoSensor/LysoTracker ratiometric pH shifted in APOE4), the observed v-ATPase transcript increase argues against the proposed mechanism and favours an acidification-limited alternative."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein scavenging receptors (SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of this list, CD163, MRC1, COLEC12, CD36), which we infer increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived sphingolipid into the endolysosomal system; the lipid flux itself is not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A coordinated lysosomal-hydrolase transcript program is elevated above the strong global upward shift of this selected list (GBA +6.71, 97.9th percentile; SMPD1 +5.63, 95.4th; HEXA +5.68, 95.6th; CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GAA; v-ATPase ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C; TFEB), indicating increased capacity to synthesise, tag (GNPTG) and acidify, i.e. the bottleneck is not transcription or acidification machinery.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred transport): The receptor arm that retrieves and reloads hydrolase-sorting receptors at the trans-Golgi is selectively low (M6PR -1.72, 14.6th percentile, q=5e-92; STX16 -4.06, 2.8th; GCC1 -5.01, 1.5th; GCC2 -2.88, 6.1st; AP1M1 -1.03; GOLPH3L -7.40) and the GBA-specific carrier SCARB2 is flat relative to the list median (+1.06, 27th percentile). We hypothesise that reduced endosome-to-TGN receptor recycling limits the mannose-6-phosphate- and LIMP-2-dependent delivery of newly made sphingolipid hydrolases, so mature luminal enzyme per lysosome does not rise in proportion to transcripts and a larger fraction of hydrolase is missorted to the secretory route.", "Step 4 (inferred, unmeasured pools): Consequently, sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and GM2/ganglioside substrates accumulate in the APOE4 endolysosome lumen relative to APOE3; no lipid species were measured in this dataset, so this step is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Sphingolipid handling is shifted to non-lysosomal compartments: GBA2 (+2.63, cytosol-facing glucosylceramidase), SPNS1 (+2.58, lysosomal sphingoid-base exporter), GLTP (+2.38, cytosolic glycolipid transfer), ST3GAL5 (+2.17, ganglioside branch) and CERS4 (+2.52)/CERS6 salvage re-acylation are up, whereas the terminal disposal step SGPL1 sits low in the distribution (+1.09, 29th percentile), which we interpret as re-acylation and membrane re-routing of sphingoid bases rather than terminal clearance.", "Step 6 (correlative only): This lipid-handling state co-occurs with an activated, oxidative microglial signature (GPNMB, LGALS1, LGALS3, APOE, and protein spots containing ANXA1/CTSD/GNS candidates up; nuclear OXPHOS transcript set median +2.64, p=1e-4; HK2 -3.67), which we treat as an associated state, not a demonstrated consequence."], "title": "Retrograde endosome-to-TGN sorting-receptor deficit limits delivery of sphingolipid hydrolases in APOE4 microglia, shunting sphingolipid turnover to non-lysosomal routes"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09686888454011741, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.05407292969464526, "cosine_similarity": 0.2093992282787449, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6540226537216828, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09686888454011741, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.05407292969464526, "cosine_similarity": 0.2093992282787449, "direction_accuracy": 0.16019417475728157, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6540226537216828, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.98688725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 366}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_151", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; it is used only as a monotone effect size and as within-list percentile rank, never converted to a linear fold change.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; the correct null is the list itself (global median +1.46, 1705/2212 positive), so all enrichment claims are relative-rank claims within a biased and possibly normalization-shifted background.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance for the named steps; enzyme activity, metabolite pools, flux, and organelle localization were not measured and are inferred.", "Key steps of the proposed route are not measured in these files (ACLY, ACACA, FASN, CPT1A, ABCA1/ABCG1, lactate, acetyl-CoA, citrate, lipids); their behaviour is assumed, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (median 5) and no spot uniquely identifies a lipogenic, glycolytic or TCA enzyme, so the 2D-gel layer is treated as non-corroborating rather than as protein-level support.", "RNA from a microglia-astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be correctly assigned to microglia by 10X Flex demultiplexing, with no correction available for ambient RNA or for genotype-dependent differences in cell composition or RNA content.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic and the mock condition free of differential handling, as stated in the supplied metadata; replicate number is not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally in carbon routing: transcripts for the glycolytic investment steps (HK2, PFKP) are selectively depressed while mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA cycle and citrate/malate export transcripts (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, MDH1, SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and a cytosolic acetyl-CoA / SREBP1 lipogenic module (ACSS2, ACAT2, SREBF1, SCD, GPAT4, AGPAT2, DGAT1) are coordinately elevated above the strong global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list. We propose that the rate-limiting node distinguishing the genotypes is cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply from mitochondrial citrate export, which converts oxidative carbon into monounsaturated fatty acid and triacylglycerol synthesis rather than into ATP-linked respiration; the predicted (not measured) consequence is greater neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet storage in APOE4 microglia. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with uniformly labelled 13C6-glucose, APOE4 microglia should show a higher fractional 13C enrichment of palmitate/oleate in the triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester pools than isogenic APOE3, and a higher M+2 citrate-to-lactate labelling ratio. If de novo 13C incorporation into lipid is equal between genotypes and any lipid difference comes only from exogenous (unlabelled or 13C-oleate-traced) fatty acid retention, the mechanism is wrong and an uptake/efflux mechanism is favoured.", "Node test at the proposed bottleneck: inhibiting mitochondrial citrate export (SLC25A1 inhibitor CTPI-2) or cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation (ACLY inhibitor) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area and glucose-derived lipid labelling in APOE4 substantially more than in APOE3, and SLC25A1 knockdown should reproduce this. Equal or absent effect in APOE4 relative to APOE3 weakens the mechanism.", "Upstream test: MPC inhibition (UK-5099) should lower both TCA labelling and the APOE4 excess of glucose-derived lipid. If UK-5099 lowers TCA labelling but leaves the APOE4 lipid excess intact, mitochondrial pyruvate is not the carbon source and the mechanism fails at step 2-3.", "Bioenergetic mismatch prediction: despite elevated nuclear OXPHOS transcripts, APOE4 maximal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption should be no higher (or lower) than APOE3, consistent with the depressed mitochondrially encoded subunit transcripts. A proportional increase in respiration with no lipid or labelling difference would favour a simple 'more oxidative metabolism' explanation instead.", "Targeted protein test replacing the ambiguous spots: immunoblot or targeted MS should show higher SCD, SLC25A1 and SREBP1-cleaved-form abundance in APOE4; absence of any protein-level increase at these nodes while transcripts differ would break the transcript-to-enzyme assumption.", "Specificity test: SCD inhibition should convert the APOE4 lipid excess toward saturated species and raise ER-stress markers preferentially in APOE4; no genotype-selective response would argue the desaturation step is not carrying the flux."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_151", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the biased background of this DE list (global median effect +1.46), HK2 and PFKP transcripts are among the most depressed (gene:HK2 -3.67, 4th percentile, adj p 7.7e-191; gene:PFKP -3.08, 6th percentile), while glucose transporter transcripts are not (gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC2A1 +2.37). Inferred: glucose uptake is maintained but committed glycolytic flux to lactate is restricted in APOE4.", "Measured: mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and pyruvate-dehydrogenase-activating phosphatase transcripts are high (gene:MPC2 +7.98, 99th percentile; gene:PDP1 +3.00), together with TCA transcripts (gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1). Inferred (not measured): a larger fraction of pyruvate enters the mitochondrion and is oxidatively decarboxylated to acetyl-CoA in APOE4.", "Measured: the citrate/isocitrate carrier and the oxoglutarate-malate carrier transcripts are elevated (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, 91st percentile; gene:SLC25A11 +4.50). Inferred bottleneck: mitochondrial citrate export, not respiratory chain capacity, becomes the dominant exit route for TCA carbon, supplying cytosolic acetyl-CoA.", "Measured counter-constraint: mitochondrially encoded electron-transport subunit transcripts are not coordinately raised and several are among the most depressed (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80). Inferred: the nuclear oxidative transcript programme is a carbon-handling shift rather than a proportional increase in assembled ETC/ATP-synthase capacity; respiration is unmeasured here.", "Measured: cytosolic acetyl-CoA-consuming and lipogenic transcripts are elevated (gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72), whereas the sterol-synthesis arm is not enriched (gene:HMGCS1 +1.08 and gene:SREBF2 +1.06 lie below the global median). Inferred: an SREBP1/fatty-acid-biased, not sterol-biased, anabolic programme.", "Measured: long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts required to activate fatty acids for beta-oxidation are depressed (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11). Inferred: reduced re-activation and catabolic disposal of fatty acids, so newly made and desaturated acyl chains are preferentially esterified into triacylglycerol/droplets.", "Inferred outcome (prediction, not observed here): APOE4 microglia accumulate more glucose-carbon-derived neutral lipid, and the coincident lysosomal hydrolase transcript rise (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:HEXA, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB) represents a downstream storage/degradative load response rather than the primary lesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia divert glucose carbon from glycolytic exit into mitochondrial citrate export, creating an SREBF1-driven lipogenic sink"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07142857142857142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09993828851526014, "cosine_similarity": 0.20938528780413085, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_151", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6256990291262137, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07142857142857142, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09993828851526014, "cosine_similarity": 0.20938528780413085, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6256990291262137, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.802021, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 367}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_032", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; all inferences use within-dataset ranks/percentiles relative to the global shift, never absolute fold changes.", "The RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene means it was not selected, not that it is unchanged.", "The global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46, |effect| up to 15.5, with ACTB at -5.0) reflects normalisation or compositional structure rather than a true genome-wide induction, so only relative enrichment is interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is treated as enzyme supply, not as measured hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, localisation or lipid flux.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are heavily populated by keratin/actin contaminants; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein or as confirmation of any transcript.", "The APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed to contain comparable microglial and astrocytic proportions and comparable differentiation stage; this is not verified in the supplied data.", "No lipidomic, imaging, activity or flux measurements were supplied, so every substrate-load, ceramide and lysosomal-morphology statement is a prediction."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, direction-consistent elevation of transcripts encoding luminal lysosomal hydrolases that act on sphingolipids and glycoconjugates (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, GAA, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) together with v-ATPase subunits, while sphingolipid de novo synthesis transcripts and the SREBP-2 cholesterol-synthesis/efflux module are not coordinately shifted; we hypothesise this reflects a demand-driven compensatory response to an increased lysosomal sphingolipid substrate load, so that net lysosomal lipid-degradative flux, rather than enzyme transcript supply, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under mock conditions, live-cell fluorogenic hydrolase assays (4-MU-beta-glucoside for GBA, 4-MU-N-acetyl-beta-glucosaminide for HEXA/B, BODIPY-sphingomyelin for SMPD1) should show higher apparent Vmax in APOE4, yet targeted lipidomics should still show equal or higher accumulated glucosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin in APOE4 - the activity/substrate mismatch is the core claim. If APOE4 shows higher hydrolase activity together with lower or equal glycosphingolipid levels, the 'degradative flux is limiting' mechanism is falsified and the program is simply sufficient compensation.", "Removing the cargo should collapse the difference: culturing the same microglia without astrocytes or in lipoprotein-depleted medium should shrink the APOE4-vs-APOE3 gap in the hydrolase module (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA) by more than half. Persistence of the full gap in cargo-free conditions would weaken the demand-driven step and favour a cell-autonomous transcriptional difference.", "Sterol counterfactual: statin treatment or sterol depletion should not selectively rescue or reproduce the APOE4 hydrolase signature, and SREBP-2 targets (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1) should remain non-differential between genotypes. Finding a coordinated genotype difference in these SREBP-2 targets would support the rejected sterol focus over this mechanism.", "Partial GBA or SMPD1 inhibition (e.g. conduritol-B-epoxide, or acid sphingomyelinase knockdown) should exaggerate lysosomal lipid accumulation and enlarge LAMP1-positive compartments more in APOE3 than the already-loaded APOE4 (sub-additive interaction). An equal or larger increment in APOE4 would argue that these hydrolases are not operating near capacity in APOE4.", "TFEB knockdown should abolish most of the coordinated hydrolase transcript elevation in APOE4; if the hydrolase module remains elevated after effective TFEB loss, the CLEAR-like transcriptional step in this mechanism is wrong even if the flux bottleneck stands.", "General weakening result: if single-cell re-analysis shows the APOE4 and APOE3 samples differ mainly in microglia/astrocyte proportion or maturation stage, or if the hydrolase enrichment disappears after re-normalisation that removes the 77%-up global shift, the entire signature should be reattributed to composition or normalisation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the strong global positive shift of this selected differential-expression list (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% of rows positive), lysosomal sphingolipid/glycoconjugate hydrolase transcripts are consistently above background (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1 at the 95th-98th percentile; GBA2, HEXB, GM2A, GLA all above the global median; 7/7 concordant, binomial p=0.016; Mann-Whitney vs all rows p=0.012 for the sphingolipid catabolic set and p=0.004 for a broader acid-hydrolase set including GAA, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK).", "Measured, contrasting: sphingolipid de novo synthesis transcripts sit at the 39th background percentile and the core SREBP-2 sterol module (HMGCR, SQLE, MSMO1, FDFT1, IDI1, MVD, CYP51A1) plus ABCA1/ABCG1/NPC1 are absent from the differential list, with the sterol genes that are present centred at the 51st percentile; the induced program is therefore selectively degradative rather than biosynthetic or sterol-directed.", "Inferred (not measured): APOE4-associated lipid cargo delivered to microglial lysosomes (lipoprotein and membrane-derived sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, gangliosides) exceeds resting hydrolytic capacity, creating a substrate-load signal.", "Inferred (not measured): this load engages a CLEAR-like lysosome-biogenesis response; TFEB transcript is modestly above the global median (+2.38, 69th percentile) and v-ATPase subunit transcripts (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) are raised, which we interpret as attempted expansion of acidified degradative compartment rather than as demonstrated TFEB activation or measured lumenal pH change.", "Inferred flux/localisation consequence: hydrolase transcript induction only partially compensates, leaving elevated intralysosomal glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin and locally generated ceramide, i.e. enlarged lipid-laden late endosomes/lysosomes; no lipid species were measured in the supplied data, so this pool is predicted, not observed.", "Coupled, possibly parallel: mitochondrial complex I and TCA transcripts are above background (NDUF set n=21, median +2.66, p=0.001; MDH1 +8.7, OGDH +8.6, MPC2 +8.0), consistent with increased oxidative disposal demand for catabolic products, but we do not claim this is downstream of the lysosomal step.", "Because the compensation observed is transcriptional while ambiguous protein spots containing CTSD, CTSB, HEXB or ATP6V1E1 move in both directions, we place the bottleneck at realised degradative flux/enzyme activity, not at message abundance."], "title": "APOE4 microglia mount a selective lysosomal glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin catabolic program, indicating degradative flux (not sterol synthesis) as the limiting node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09099804305283757, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.061033171640252945, "cosine_similarity": 0.2091812514969944, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_032", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6568284789644013, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09099804305283757, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.061033171640252945, "cosine_similarity": 0.2091812514969944, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6568284789644013, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.554455, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 368}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_157", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a large global positive shift (median ~1.46); pathway claims rest on rank-percentile comparisons against that internal background, not on absolute fold-change magnitudes.", "Higher transcript abundance for TCA/ETC and V-ATPase/hydrolase genes reflects at least partly higher protein content and organelle capacity; enzyme activity, ATP flux, lysosomal pH, mitochondrial membrane potential and cargo-degradation rate were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may arise from altered microglia-astrocyte interaction or from cell-composition/normalisation effects rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 action.", "No lipidomic, metabolomic, flux or lysosomal-function measurement is supplied, so all statements about flux, localisation, ATP allocation and causal direction are inferred."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional shift toward mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA-cycle and electron-transport machinery together with an expanded endolysosomal/hydrolase and V-ATPase program, while the committed glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2) are lower; we hypothesise that oxidative-phosphorylation-derived ATP, rather than lipid remodeling or inflammatory activation, is the primary bottleneck that sets the sustainable rate of lysosomal acidification and cargo degradation in APOE4 cells, making them selectively vulnerable to acute respiratory-chain inhibition. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute ATP-synthase or complex I inhibition (oligomycin or rotenone) or mitochondrial pyruvate-carrier inhibition (UK5099) in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should produce a larger lysosomal alkalinisation (LysoSensor ratio) and a larger drop in DQ-BSA / pHrodo cargo-degradation rate in APOE4, together with a smaller compensatory ECAR increase; if APOE4 shows equal or greater glycolytic compensation and equal or smaller lysosomal pH and degradation change, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Seahorse profiling of mock cells should show higher basal and maximal OCR and lower glycolytic reserve in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or lower OCR with equal glycolytic reserve would weaken step 1-2.", "Independent protein/activity validation should show higher V-ATPase subunit protein and higher cathepsin B/D and beta-hexosaminidase activity per cell in APOE4; if these transcript increases are not accompanied by any increase in hydrolase activity, LysoTracker signal or lysosomal number, the endolysosomal expansion is transcript-only and the mechanism is weakened.", "Substrate-switch test: culture in galactose (forcing oxidative ATP production) should impair APOE4 cargo clearance and viability no more than APOE3 (APOE4 is already oxidative), whereas 2-deoxyglucose should impair APOE3 more; the opposite ordering would falsify the glycolysis-restraint element.", "Rescue test: mild ATP-supply support (methyl-pyruvate or NAD+ precursor supplementation) should normalise APOE4 lysosomal pH and degradation flux without normalising APOE4-specific identity transcripts such as gene:CTSS and gene:CSF1; normalisation of neither pool would weaken the mechanism, and normalisation of both would indicate a shared upstream driver instead of a metabolic bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_157", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with higher steady-state transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry and NADH-generating TCA enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G) and for respiratory-chain and mitochondrial-import subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:UQCRC2, gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM8B); this is measured abundance and only infers increased oxidative capacity, not measured flux.", "Committed glycolytic steps are transcriptionally restrained (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2 reduced) despite higher glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3), so the inferred capacity for compensatory glycolytic ATP production is limited relative to APOE3.", "In parallel the endolysosomal system is transcriptionally expanded: the TFEB-associated hydrolase and acidification module is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:MAN2B1, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), indicating inferred higher degradative load and higher demand on proton pumping. Two significant protein spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal/peroxisomal proteins are higher in APOE4 (protein_spot:053 contains CTSD; protein_spot:017 contains CAT), but spot identity is ambiguous and this is only weak corroboration.", "V-ATPase-driven acidification and endolysosomal maturation are ATP-consuming; with oxidative machinery up and glycolytic committed steps down, the inferred ATP supply for this compartment becomes disproportionately dependent on mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation - the proposed primary bottleneck.", "Operating near this supply ceiling is proposed to constrain cargo clearance flux, so any acute reduction of mitochondrial ATP output should convert into lysosomal alkalinisation and degradation failure faster in APOE4 than APOE3.", "Consistent with a resource-constrained rather than classically activated state, homeostatic/myeloid identity and inflammatory transcripts are not elevated and several are reduced (gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:CD200R1, gene:P2RY2, gene:CD69); this is a correlated observation, not evidence that the metabolic change caused the identity shift."], "title": "OXPHOS-dependent ATP supply is the rate-limiting node for an expanded endolysosomal degradative compartment in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19728242809142266, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18650777127279508, "cosine_similarity": 0.2082289527817183, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_157", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6290970873786408, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19728242809142266, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18650777127279508, "cosine_similarity": 0.2082289527817183, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6290970873786408, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.27107175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 369}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_071", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source workbook and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are treated as ranks/relative sizes, not as interpretable fold changes, and are not comparable with the protein log2 values.", "The 2212 RNA rows are pre-selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, all |effect|\u003e1, 77.1% positive), so only enrichment relative to this selected background is interpreted; absolute direction of the global shift may partly reflect selection or normalisation.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzyme/transporter pool; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, lipid species, membrane potential, pH or localisation was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; spot-level changes are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration (e.g. spots 043-046 share ANXA1 and TALDO1, whose RNA moves in opposite directions, gene:ANXA1 up and gene:TALDO1 down).", "Key nodes of the proposed chain were not measured at all in the supplied rows (ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, ACLY, FASN, CPT1A, MPC1, TYROBP), so lysosomal cholesterol egress, lipid-droplet storage and fatty-acid oxidation are inferred gaps, not observations.", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultures under mock treatment; genotype effects on microglia may be partly non-cell-autonomous, and mock-state differences may reflect developmental/differentiation divergence rather than steady-state metabolic regulation.", "Causality is not established: the comparison is observational between genotypes; the bottleneck assignment is a hypothesis to be tested, not a measured flux control coefficient."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, above-background transcriptional expansion of lysosomal degradative machinery (CLEAR-type hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits) together with the mitochondrial pyruvate/dicarboxylate-citrate carrier and TCA/malate-aspartate module; we hypothesise that lysosome-derived catabolic products are routed into mitochondria and that flux through the MPC2 / SLC25A1 / MDH1-GOT1 node is the rate-limiting step that determines whether this carbon is fully oxidised or exported as citrate for cytosolic acetyl-CoA-dependent lipid re-synthesis, with the transcriptional cost of a de-prioritised actin-motility and immune-secretory program. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, localisation, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: with U-13C6-glucose and, separately, 13C-labelled lipoprotein/oleate, APOE4 microglia should show a higher fraction of label from the lipid tracer (relative to the glucose tracer) appearing in TCA intermediates (citrate, malate, glutamate) and in newly synthesised fatty acid/sterol than APOE3. If APOE4 shows no increase in lipid-derived carbon entering TCA/lipids, or if glucose-derived labelling is instead increased, the lysosome-to-mitochondria routing claim is falsified.", "Bottleneck test: MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown, and separately SLC25A1 inhibition (CTPI-2), should produce a significantly larger reduction in oxygen consumption and in de novo lipid labelling in APOE4 than in APOE3 (genotype x drug interaction). An equal, genotype-independent response would weaken the assignment of the pyruvate/citrate node as the rate-limiting step.", "Upstream-dependency test: blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or acid hydrolysis (e.g. GBA inhibition) should selectively collapse the APOE4 excess in lipid-substrate-driven respiration and cause greater accumulation of undegraded lysosomal substrate in APOE4. If APOE4 respiration is unaffected by lysosomal blockade, the lysosome is not the substrate source.", "Abundance-to-function test: APOE4 microglia should show higher LysoTracker/DQ-BSA hydrolytic signal and higher cathepsin B/D and v-ATPase protein levels by immunoblot. Unchanged lysosomal protein and hydrolytic activity would show the transcript module is not reflected in the protein pool and would weaken step 1 (note the supplied 2D-spot data already argue this way: protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 and protein_spot:064 contain CTSB/HEXB/CTSD/ATP6V1E1 candidates and are decreased).", "Trade-off test: APOE4 microglia should show reduced random and chemotactic migration and reduced CSF1/CTSS-dependent secretory output at equal viability; if APOE4 migrates equally or faster, the resource-reallocation step 6 is falsified.", "Identity test for the protein arm: mass-spectrometric re-identification of protein_spot:043-046 should assign ANXA1 (RNA increased) rather than TALDO1 (RNA decreased). Assignment to TALDO1 would favour an alternative pentose-phosphate/redox mechanism over the mechanism proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits and for TFEB itself (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:SLC38A7, gene:TFEB; set mean +3.95 vs selected-row background +1.39, permutation p\u003c1e-4). Inferred: increased lysosomal degradative capacity and increased hydrolytic turnover of internalised lipid/membrane substrate, supported by (but not proven from) higher uptake-receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE).", "Inferred: catabolic products released from the lysosomal lumen (fatty acids, amino acids, sugars) must be re-imported into mitochondria or cytosolic anabolic pathways; this transfer step, not degradation itself, becomes limiting once hydrolase capacity is raised.", "Measured: transcripts for the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier, citrate and oxoglutarate carriers, malate-aspartate shuttle and TCA enzymes are among the most strongly increased in the dataset (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:BCAT2, gene:GLUD1; set mean +4.59, permutation p\u003c1e-4; MPC2/MDH1/OGDH at the 99th percentile of all measured rows). Proposed bottleneck (inferred, not measured): flux through the MPC2/SLC25A1/MDH1-GOT1 node.", "Measured: upper-glycolysis transcripts are discordant with the global upward shift (gene:HK2 -3.7, gene:PFKP -3.1, both in the lowest ~3% of rows) while respiratory-chain and translation-elongation transcripts are up (gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:TUFM). Inferred: reduced reliance on glycolytic pyruvate production, so lysosome- and amino-acid-derived carbon carries a larger share of mitochondrial substrate supply.", "Inferred branch point at the citrate node: carbon retained in the TCA cycle supports oxidation and NADPH/redox buffering (gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4 up), whereas citrate exported by SLC25A1 feeds cytosolic acetyl-CoA and a modest lipogenic/sterol program (gene:ACSS2, gene:ACAT2, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DHCR24, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). This lipogenic arm is directionally consistent but is NOT enriched above the already up-shifted background (permutation p=0.31-0.51) and is the weakest link in the chain.", "Measured: actin/motility and immune-secretory transcripts are at the extreme low end (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:FAM49B, gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:SPN, gene:SEMA4A; immune-secretory set mean -1.18, permutation p=0.0015). Inferred: the APOE4 state trades motility/secretory output for degradative-oxidative capacity, predicting lower migration and lower CSF1/CTSS-dependent secretory function at equal viability."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift to a lysosome-to-mitochondria catabolic state whose rate-limiting node is mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate carrier flux"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32039471255030827, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08697378504182089, "cosine_similarity": 0.20717319296895484, "direction_accuracy": 0.33818770226537215, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6409288025889968, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32039471255030827, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08697378504182089, "cosine_similarity": 0.20717319296895484, "direction_accuracy": 0.33818770226537215, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6409288025889968, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7161155, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 370}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_176", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (all adjusted p\u003c0.05 and all |effect|\u003e=1, 1705/2212 positive, median +1.46); direction of any single gene is therefore judged relative to this selected-list background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absence of a gene means it was not supplied rather than unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect values is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are treated as ranks/relative sizes only, and values above ~8 may reflect low-count pseudobulk instability.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, enzyme abundance and pathway capacity; enzyme activity, acetyl-CoA, malonyl-CoA, sterol, triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester pools, lipid-droplet content, respiration and lysosomal pH were not measured in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-specific corroboration.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture at day 30; astrocyte-derived lipid supply is assumed comparable between genotypes, which the data cannot verify.", "Direction of causality between the uptake, acetyl-CoA-supply, SREBF and lysosomal modules is assumed, not demonstrated; all four could be parallel outputs of an upstream APOE4 effect."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated anabolic lipid program: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake, TCA-cycle and citrate export, cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation, and SREBF-dependent sterol/monounsaturated-fatty-acid esterification enzymes are jointly higher, while fatty-acid activation and peroxisomal routing transcripts are lower. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting (bottleneck) node is the supply of cytosolic acetyl-CoA and SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA for DGAT1/SOAT1/AGPAT2-mediated esterification, which converts increased lipid influx into stored neutral lipid rather than oxidation or export, and that the accompanying lysosomal/v-ATPase transcript increase is a downstream compensatory response to this lipid load. Interferon and NF-kB inflammatory transcripts are indistinguishable from the background of the supplied differential list and are not proposed as drivers. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; enzymatic activity, metabolic flux, lipid pools, and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the proposed bottleneck (SLC25A1/citrate export or ACLY, and separately SCD) in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid-droplet and cholesteryl-ester content toward APOE3 levels while leaving lipoprotein uptake (DiI-LDL/HDL internalisation) largely intact. If lipid excess persists unchanged under these inhibitors but is abolished by blocking uptake (LDLR/SCARB1/CD36 knockdown), the bottleneck lies in influx, not in acetyl-CoA/MUFA supply, and this mechanism is weakened.", "Stable-isotope tracing (U-13C-glucose and 13C-acetate) should show greater label incorporation into APOE4 triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and sterol species than APOE3. Equal or lower de novo incorporation, with the APOE4 lipid excess derived only from exogenous lipid, would falsify Steps 3-5.", "SREBF1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/LPCAT1 module and the lipid phenotype together; loss of the transcript module without loss of the lipid phenotype would weaken the proposed SREBF-dependence.", "Discriminating test against the interferon/inflammatory alternative: JAK1/2 inhibition or IFNAR1 blockade should not normalise the APOE4 lipid phenotype or the SREBF module, consistent with the interferon/NF-kB gene set sitting at the background median of the supplied list (median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.72). If JAK inhibition does normalise the lipid difference, an interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "DGAT1 inhibition should redistribute APOE4 lipid from droplets into free fatty acid and lysophospholipid pools and increase lysosomal/v-ATPase reporter activity further; if lysosomal markers instead fall when droplets are blocked, the lysosomal module is upstream rather than compensatory (Step 6 would be reversed).", "If mitochondrial respiration measured by extracellular flux is not higher in APOE4, or if citrate/acetyl-CoA levels are equal between genotypes, Steps 2-3 lose their inferential basis even though the transcript differences remain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_176", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred influx): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28), which we infer, but did not measure, raises lipid and lipoprotein influx into the cell.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred pool): TCA-cycle and respiratory-chain transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:SDHB +1.65, plus 42/43 up in the NDUF/UQCR/COX/ATP5/TIMM/TOMM group, Mann-Whitney p=2.9e-5 versus the rest of the supplied list), consistent with a larger mitochondrial citrate/acetyl-CoA pool; no metabolite was measured.", "Step 3 (proposed bottleneck; measured abundance, inferred flux): Elevated gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47), gene:ACSS2 (+2.93) and gene:ACAT2 (+2.04) are proposed to raise cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability. Because ACLY, acetyl-CoA and malonyl-CoA were not measured, this step is the explicitly inferred rate-limiting node of the mechanism rather than an observation.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred transcriptional activity): An SREBF-type lipogenic program is coordinately higher (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87) together with its sterol arm (gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:EBP +1.34); a 21-gene anabolic lipid set is 21/21 up with median +2.65 versus a background median of +1.46 (one-sided Mann-Whitney p=3.3e-3).", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred esterification flux): The desaturation/esterification arm is uniformly higher (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:FADS1 +1.59), while long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases and peroxisomal import fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:ABCD1 -1.64). We infer, without lipidomic measurement, that carbon is partitioned into monounsaturated triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and remodelled phospholipid rather than into PUFA-CoA-dependent oxidation.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred compensation): Lysosomal acidification and hydrolase transcripts rise as a secondary response to the neutral-lipid and membrane load (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GAA +9.96); several protein spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins are higher (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54), but these spots contain multiple candidate genes and do not identify any protein uniquely."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route carbon into SREBF1-driven neutral-lipid esterification through a citrate/acetyl-CoA-to-MUFA supply bottleneck, not through interferon or inflammatory signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3534412731233615, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16380748664524586, "cosine_similarity": 0.20330993375954676, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_176", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6768964401294498, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3534412731233615, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16380748664524586, "cosine_similarity": 0.20330993375954676, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6768964401294498, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.98481425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 371}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance is treated as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity only; no flux, metabolite, oxygen-consumption, membrane-potential or ATP measurement is supplied, so all flux, localization and directional statements are inferred.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, so absent genes (e.g. HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, PKM, CS, PDHA1, TFAM, most MT- genes) are unmeasured rather than unchanged, and set-level means are compared against the list's own strongly positive background (median about +1.46) rather than against zero.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as given; magnitudes are used only for ranking and set comparison, not as literal fold changes.", "The 4/6 decrease in mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to reflect a real relative shortfall of MT-encoded subunits rather than a compositional/normalization artefact of a global increase in nuclear transcript content, or a probe-panel/3'-coverage quirk of the 10X Flex chemistry (unverified background knowledge); this assumption is the weakest link and is explicitly tested below.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:038 (candidates include ALDOA/ALDOC) and protein_spot:053 (candidates include CTSD) are treated as ambiguous, corroborative-at-best, and no protein-level measurement of any OXPHOS subunit is available.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on microglial metabolism may be partly non-cell-autonomous; APOE4 versus APOE3 is isogenic but replicate numbers were not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia raise the nuclear-encoded programme for delivering carbon to mitochondria (mitochondrial pyruvate carrier, PDH-activating and TCA/malate-aspartate-shuttle enzymes, mitochondrial carriers, import, mt-translation and OXPHOS assembly factors) while glycolytic committed-step transcripts are not raised and mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts are relatively lower; we hypothesise that the resulting shortfall of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for complexes III/IV/V, not substrate supply or glycolysis, is the rate-limiting step, so oxidative ATP flux per unit mitochondrial mass fails to scale with the increased carbon commitment and leaves APOE4 microglia with little glycolytic fallback. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Direct bottleneck test: in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, the ratio of mtDNA-encoded to nuclear-encoded OXPHOS protein (e.g. MT-CO1 and MT-ATP6 versus SDHA, NDUFB8, ATP5F1B), normalized to mtDNA copy number and mitochondrial mass, should be lower in APOE4, and blue-native PAGE should show increased complex IV/V subassemblies. If this ratio is equal or higher and holoenzymes are intact, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the MT- RNA decrease is better explained by compositional normalization.", "Capacity-versus-flux test: respirometry normalized to citrate synthase or TOMM20 should show that APOE4 does NOT gain proportional ATP-linked OCR or spare respiratory capacity despite the large nuclear OXPHOS transcript increase. Proportionally increased ATP-linked OCR in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should reduce OCR, lower the ATP/ADP ratio and raise AMPK phosphorylation substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3, with a smaller compensatory ECAR rise in APOE4 (consistent with low HK2/PFKP). Equal sensitivity, or a larger glycolytic ECAR compensation in APOE4, would falsify the carbon-commitment plus capped-glycolysis steps.", "Rescue prediction: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or POLRMT/TFB2M-driven boost of mtDNA transcription, or fusion/mitochondrial-biogenesis rescue) should selectively restore ATP-linked respiration and reduce the subassembly burden in APOE4 but have little effect in APOE3. No genotype-selective rescue would weaken the mechanism.", "Flux tracing: U-13C-glucose should give APOE4 microglia a higher fractional M+2 labelling of citrate/glutamate and a lower fraction of glucose carbon released as lactate than APOE3, with a compensating rise in 13C-glutamine contribution to the TCA pool. Higher lactate labelling and unchanged citrate labelling in APOE4 would falsify the substrate-use step.", "Negative control against a generic activation explanation: the mito-nuclear transcript gap should persist after normalizing to per-cell mitochondrial mass and should not be reproduced by simply activating APOE3 microglia (e.g. with LPS), which should instead raise HK2/PFKP and lactate output."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance for mitochondrial pyruvate entry and oxidation (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54), TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94) and the malate-aspartate/citrate shuttle (gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47); inferred (not measured): increased capacity for pyruvate import and NADH transfer into the matrix.", "Measured: glycolytic committed steps are not co-induced above the strongly positive global background (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08) although glucose uptake transporters rise (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73) and glycogen synthase rises (gene:GYS1 +6.10); inferred (not measured): glucose carbon is routed away from cytosolic lactate output toward storage and mitochondrial oxidation, i.e. a substrate-use shift rather than a Warburg-like shift.", "Measured: the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial support apparatus rises coordinately - OXPHOS structural subunits (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX5B, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5MC3), assembly and cofactor delivery (gene:COX20, gene:ANTKMT, gene:SLC31A2, gene:CCS), mitochondrial translation elongation/recycling (gene:TUFM, gene:GFM2, gene:MRRF), protein import (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9) and inner-membrane lipid handling (gene:TAZ, gene:PRELID3B); inferred: an attempted expansion of respiratory-chain biogenesis.", "Measured: mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts move in the opposite direction to this nuclear programme (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) against a global median RNA shift of about +1.46; hypothesised bottleneck (inferred, not measured): supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits becomes stoichiometry-limiting for assembly of complexes III, IV and V.", "Inferred consequence (not measured): nuclear-encoded modules accumulate faster than they can be matched with MT-encoded cores, so assembled holoenzyme, ATP-linked respiration and spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass do not scale with the increased carbon delivery, and electrons back up in the chain; the co-ordinate rise of gene:PRDX3, gene:NNT and gene:UCP2 is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, increased matrix redox/ROS load.", "Inferred compensation (not measured as flux): with committed glycolytic steps down (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP), cells cannot buffer the shortfall glycolytically and instead lean on anaplerosis/amino-acid oxidation (gene:GLS +1.35, gene:GLUD1 +3.17), adenine-nucleotide exchange (gene:SLC25A5 +5.56) and phosphagen buffering (gene:GAMT +7.98); the chronically strained, lysosome-loaded state (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:TFEB up) is a downstream correlate, not a demonstrated cause."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch caps oxidative ATP flux in APOE4 microglia that have committed carbon to mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06164383561643835, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03822249267507478, "cosine_similarity": 0.20125346780294295, "direction_accuracy": 0.10355987055016182, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6225566343042072, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06164383561643835, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03822249267507478, "cosine_similarity": 0.20125346780294295, "direction_accuracy": 0.10355987055016182, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6225566343042072, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6812435, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 372}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_087", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive) rather than an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against this in-list background by permutation, and the logarithm base of the reported effects is unspecified and preserved as given.", "The global upward shift may partly reflect normalisation or ambient-RNA differences; the mechanism therefore leans on the direction contrast (nuclear up vs mtDNA-encoded down) rather than on absolute up-regulation.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the availability of the corresponding subunit protein; no protein-level OXPHOS subunit, mtDNA copy number, assembly, respiration, membrane potential or ROS measurement is present in these data.", "Probe-based 10X Flex capture is assumed not to introduce a systematic APOE4-specific bias against mitochondrially encoded transcripts; this is an unverified technical assumption.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-identifying; no spot is used as primary support (e.g. protein_spot:077 lists PRDX2 among five keratin/actin candidates).", "Cells are astrocyte co-cultured, so a fraction of the RNA signal may not be microglia-intrinsic; genotype effects on the co-cultured astrocytes could contribute (unverified).", "Background pathway memberships (OXPHOS, TCA, CLEAR/lysosome, peroxiredoxin) are from unverified prior knowledge, not from any supplied annotation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a stoichiometric mismatch in respiratory-chain subunit supply: every measured nuclear-encoded complex I/III/IV/V subunit transcript is higher in APOE4 (37/37, median +2.64 in the reported log scale) together with TCA and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts, whereas four of six measured mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are among the most decreased genes in the list. We hypothesise that mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembling functional holo-complexes, so the enlarged nuclear/lysosomal catabolic program cannot be converted into proportionally increased coupled respiration, and the resulting electron leak drives the coordinated thioredoxin/peroxiredoxin and mitochondrial stress transcripts observed. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are transcript abundances (plus ambiguous protein spots), not assembly, flux, or localization.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: titrate a mitochondrial-translation inhibitor (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol) on isogenic APOE3 and APOE4 microglia. If mtDNA-encoded subunit supply is already limiting in APOE4, the incremental loss of maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) oxygen consumption per unit drug should be smaller in APOE4 than APOE3 (occlusion, left-shifted dose-response). If APOE4 is equally or more sensitive than APOE3, the bottleneck placement is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Rescue: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM over-expression, or restoring mtDNA copy number/mitochondrial transcription) should normalise the assembled-holocomplex-to-nuclear-subunit ratio and reduce PRDX3/GPX4/DDIT3 transcripts in APOE4 without lowering the nuclear OXPHOS transcript program. No change in assembled complex ratio after successful TFAM induction would weaken the mechanism.", "Assembly readout: blue-native PAGE/complexome of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show reduced fully assembled complex I, IV and V relative to total imported nuclear subunit protein (e.g. NDUFA/NDUFB, ATP5 subunits), with accumulated sub-assemblies, and reduced MT-CO2/MT-ATP6/MT-CYB protein. Equal or higher assembled holocomplex per mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 or mtDNA copy number normalised) in APOE4 would falsify the core claim.", "Functional prediction: APOE4 microglia should show a lower coupled ATP-linked respiration per mitochondrial mass and higher matrix-targeted ROS (MitoSOX / mito-roGFP) despite higher TCA and nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Equal ATP-linked respiration per mitochondrial mass with no redox difference would weaken the mechanism.", "Substrate-supply prediction: blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1 or a cathepsin B/D inhibitor) should reduce, not increase, the APOE4-specific redox and DDIT3/HSPA9 signature, because it lowers substrate delivery into a supply-limited chain. If lysosomal blockade increases the mitochondrial stress signature specifically in APOE4, the lysosome is better modelled as a failing sink than as a substrate source and step 1 would need revision.", "Alternative-mechanism test (assigned lipid focus): if the primary defect were acyl-chain remodelling/glycerolipid flux, APOE4 microglia should show a lipidomic shift in phospholipid acyl composition and neutral-lipid mass that is not corrected by restoring mitochondrial translation. Observing that lipid-droplet or acyl-composition differences persist unchanged while respiration and redox are fully rescued by TFAM/mito-translation support would show that the lipid axis is independent of, or upstream of, the proposed bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia up-regulate a substrate-mobilisation program: lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1) and the CLEAR-network regulator TFEB are coherently increased above the already up-shifted background of this differential-expression list (permutation p=0.003). Increased catabolic flux and delivery of lysosome-derived substrates to mitochondria is inferred, not measured.", "In parallel, mitochondrial carrier and TCA transcripts rise strongly (SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5, OGDH, MDH1; permutation p\u003c=0.0014), consistent with an inferred increase in carbon entry to the matrix; matrix metabolite pools were not measured.", "Nuclear-encoded OXPHOS structural subunits of complexes I, III, IV and V increase uniformly (37/37 up, mean +2.81, permutation p=0.0008), indicating an inferred increase in cytosolic synthesis of the imported half of each complex (import machinery TIMM8B, TOMM22, TIMM44 and the mitochondrial translation factor TUFM are also up).", "The mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores of complexes I, III, IV and V are not matched: MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 sit in the 4th-18th percentile of this list while the list median is +1.46. We infer a relative deficit of core subunits per available nuclear subunit, creating an assembly bottleneck in which sub-complexes and unassembled imported subunits accumulate or are degraded (protein-level assembly was not measured).", "Sub-stoichiometric, incompletely assembled complexes are predicted to leak electrons and to lower coupled ATP output per unit of imported carbon; the coordinated rise in matrix/thiol antioxidant transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4; set permutation p=0.013) and in mitochondrial chaperone/integrated-stress markers (HSPA9, DDIT3) together with the fission factor FIS1 is the inferred downstream readout of this redox and proteostatic strain.", "The persistent energetic shortfall sustains the lysosomal/TFEB and mitochondrial-biogenesis transcriptional response as a feed-forward loop, so APOE4 microglia sit in a chronically 'demanding but supply-limited' state rather than a simply hypermetabolic or simply hypometabolic one."], "title": "Mitonuclear subunit-supply bottleneck: APOE4 microglia expand a nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA and lysosomal catabolic program while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts fall, limiting respiratory-complex assembly"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14982931246012487, "cosine_similarity": 0.20007732463387318, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6453430420711974, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23739984492116825, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14982931246012487, "cosine_similarity": 0.20007732463387318, "direction_accuracy": 0.20711974110032363, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6453430420711974, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.565449, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 373}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_048", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all rows have |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and not an unbiased transcriptome; direction of a gene set is therefore only interpretable relative to the strongly positive background of this list (median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified log base).", "Transcript changes for GCC1, STX16, GOLPH3L and M6PR translate into reduced retrograde carrier formation and reduced M6P-receptor retrieval; no transport assay, receptor localisation or trafficking flux was measured.", "Protein spots are treated as mixtures of candidate proteins; the systematic decrease of lysosome-candidate-bearing spots is assumed to reflect lower abundance of at least one lysosomal component rather than a proteoform shift between spots.", "Genes absent from the list (for example ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, PSAP, SPTLC1/2, NPC1) are assumed to be either unchanged or unmeasured; their absence is not used as evidence of any change.", "Sphingolipid, cholesterol and other lipid pools are inferred targets of the mechanism and were not measured in this dataset; the co-cultured astrocytes are assumed not to dominate the microglial signal.", "The comparison is assumed to be isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 in mock condition as stated in the metadata, with replicate structure unreported."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells not by a deficit in sphingolipid hydrolase gene expression but by a rate-limiting failure of the STX16/GCC1/M6PR-dependent endosome-to-trans-Golgi retrieval step; reduced receptor recycling is proposed to lower the amount of newly made sphingolipid-degrading hydrolase protein that reaches the lysosomal lumen, so sphingolipid catabolic flux lags behind delivery of membrane substrate, and a MiT/TFE-driven increase in hydrolase, v-ATPase and lysosome-biogenesis transcripts arises as compensation rather than as evidence of increased degradative capacity. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, enzymatic activity and mature-protein content of GBA, HEXA/HEXB and acid sphingomyelinase measured in purified lysosomes will be equal or lower in APOE4 despite the higher transcripts, while the same activities in conditioned medium will be higher (missorted secretion). If lysosomal hydrolase activity rises in proportion to the transcript increase and medium activity is unchanged, the bottleneck as stated is wrong.", "Re-expression of GCC1 or STX16 (or otherwise restoring endosome-to-TGN retrieval) in APOE4 microglia will raise lysosomal hydrolase content, lower lysosomal sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide/GM2-GM3 content by lipidomics, and reduce TFEB-target transcripts, without altering APOE genotype. Verified restoration of retrieval with no change in lysosomal hydrolase content or sphingolipid load would weaken the mechanism.", "Knockdown of STX16 or GCC1 in APOE3 microglia will phenocopy the APOE4 pattern - increased hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts with unchanged or reduced lysosomal hydrolase protein and increased glycosphingolipid load. Absence of phenocopy would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating test against the substrate-side alternative: supplying active hydrolase directly to the lysosome by an M6PR-independent route (recombinant enzyme uptake or a lysosome-targeted GBA/HEXB construct) will normalise the sphingolipid load and lower TFEB-target transcripts in APOE4. If substrate load and TFEB targets remain elevated when lysosomal enzyme activity has been demonstrably restored, the primary defect lies downstream (for example in substrate delivery, saposin availability or lipid egress) rather than in hydrolase delivery.", "Discriminating test against the bioenergetic alternative: pharmacological inhibition of complex I or of mitochondrial pyruvate import in APOE3 microglia will not reproduce the transcript-high / lysosomal-protein-low discordance or the reduction of GCC1/STX16/M6PR transcripts. If it does, the lysosomal signature is better explained as a secondary consequence of the mitochondrial OXPHOS/TCA shift seen in these data.", "Because RAB27A and STX17 are lower, APOE4 microglia are predicted to release less sphingolipid per cell into extracellular vesicles or by lysosomal exocytosis than APOE3 despite an equal or larger intracellular pool. Increased sphingolipid secretion by APOE4 would weaken step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 cells show coordinated lower transcript levels for the retrograde endosome-to-TGN module - the tether GCC1 (gene:GCC1), the t-SNARE STX16 (gene:STX16), the Golgi PI4P effector paralogue GOLPH3L (gene:GOLPH3L) and the cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor M6PR (gene:M6PR) - in a differential-expression list in which 77% of rows are positive. Reduced retrieval flux and receptor localisation are inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred flux/localisation): Slower M6P-receptor retrieval to the TGN is proposed to reduce the number of sorting rounds per receptor, so a larger fraction of newly synthesised M6P-tagged sphingolipid hydrolases (acid sphingomyelinase, glucocerebrosidase, beta-hexosaminidase A/B, alpha-galactosidase A and the GM2 activator) escapes to the secretory route instead of reaching the endolysosomal lumen.", "Step 3 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): Consistent with reduced lysosomal hydrolase protein despite higher transcripts, every significantly decreased 2D protein spot carries a lysosomal hydrolase or v-ATPase subunit among its candidate genes (protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:086), and among significant spots those containing lysosomal candidates are shifted lower than those that do not. Spot identity is not unique, so this is corroborative, not definitive.", "Step 4 (inferred lipid pool, not measured here): If per-lysosome hydrolase content is limiting while phagocytic and autophagic membrane input continues, sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and GM2/GM3-series glycosphingolipids are predicted to accumulate in the APOE4 endolysosome. No lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred causal direction): Retained substrate is proposed to activate MiT/TFE-dependent lysosomal biogenesis, matching the elevated transcripts for TFEB (gene:TFEB), TFEC (gene:TFEC), MITF (gene:MITF), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), LAMP1 (gene:LAMP1), RAB7A (gene:RAB7A) and the sphingolipid and bulk hydrolases themselves (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GLA, gene:GM2A, gene:GBA2, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU). This is read as compensation; the data cannot exclude the reverse order.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Escape routes for the retained lipid are not co-ordinately raised - RAB27A (gene:RAB27A), required for lysosome-related organelle exocytosis, and STX17 (gene:STX17), required for autophagosome-lysosome fusion, are lower in APOE4 - so the proposed sphingolipid load is predicted to be retained intracellularly rather than secreted, alongside modestly elevated APOE itself (gene:APOE)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia have a retrograde endosome-to-TGN retrieval bottleneck that starves lysosomes of M6P-tagged sphingolipid hydrolases, forcing compensatory MiT/TFE transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.022605346516001306, "cosine_similarity": 0.19982137585150303, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_048", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6511877022653723, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07729941291585127, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.022605346516001306, "cosine_similarity": 0.19982137585150303, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6511877022653723, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46088175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 374}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_034", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects are log fold changes in an unspecified logarithm base; only their sign and rank within the supplied differential list are used, and no absolute fold change is claimed.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression subset, not an unbiased transcriptome; because 1705/2212 rows are positive (median +1.46), all pathway claims are made as rank comparisons against this same asymmetric list rather than against zero.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance and hence for maximal pathway capacity; flux, PDH phosphorylation state, metabolite pools, ATP, oxygen consumption and lactate output were not measured and are inferred only.", "HK2 and PFKP are assumed to carry a substantial share of glycolytic control in these microglia even though HK1, PFKL, ALDOA, GAPDH, PKM and LDHA are absent from the supplied list (absence is treated as 'not reported', not as 'unchanged').", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence that a specific enzyme changed in abundance.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so extracellular lactate, ketone and lipid supply differ from monoculture; the substrate-switch interpretation assumes such non-glucose substrates are available in this system.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are stated to be isogenic, so line-to-line genetic background is assumed not to drive the differences; replicate structure was not supplied and cannot be checked."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in carbon routing rather than in total substrate uptake: transcripts for the committed, rate-limiting cytosolic glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP) are among the most strongly reduced in the differential list while glucose transporters, mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), pyruvate dehydrogenase activation (PDP1, DLD), TCA enzymes (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3B/G), malate-aspartate shuttle components (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, SLC25A1) and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are coordinately elevated. We hypothesise that this transcriptional configuration reflects a state in which glucose-6-phosphate/fructose-6-phosphate throughput to pyruvate is the limiting cytosolic step, so APOE4 microglia sustain ATP and biosynthesis by oxidising non-glycolytic carbon (lysosomal glycogen/glycan and lipid-derived substrates, ketone bodies, acetate, glutamate/amino acids) in mitochondria, leaving them with little glycolytic reserve. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are steady-state transcript abundances and ambiguous protein-spot intensities, not flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in a Seahorse-style assay under mock conditions, APOE4 microglia should show a smaller glycolytic reserve (smaller ECAR rise after oligomycin) and a larger fractional ATP/viability loss after MPC inhibition (UK5099) or complex I inhibition (rotenone) than isogenic APOE3, while being relatively more tolerant of 2-deoxyglucose. If APOE4 instead shows equal or greater glycolytic reserve and equal or lower sensitivity to UK5099/rotenone, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "13C tracing: with U-13C-glucose, APOE4 microglia should show lower fractional 13C enrichment of lactate and of citrate/glutamate M+2 than APOE3, with compensating enrichment of TCA intermediates from 13C-glutamine, 13C-palmitate or 13C-beta-hydroxybutyrate. Equal glucose-derived citrate labelling in the two genotypes would weaken the mechanism even if the transcript differences replicate.", "Epistasis: restoring glycolytic commitment in APOE4 (HK2 or PFKP re-expression, or a PFK-bypass such as fructose-1,6-bisphosphate supplementation) should restore glycolytic reserve and reduce rotenone sensitivity without needing to lower TCA/OXPHOS transcripts; if HK2/PFKP restoration changes neither reserve nor rotenone sensitivity, the glycolytic step is not the bottleneck.", "Substrate-dependence: removing the proposed alternative carbon inputs (GAA inhibition or lysosomal acidification block, SCARB1 blockade, OXCT1 knockdown, or glutamine withdrawal) should reduce oxygen consumption and ATP more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal effects in both genotypes would argue that the up-shifted catabolic transcripts do not carry extra flux in APOE4.", "Protein-level test: targeted immunoblot or MS (not spot-level) should confirm lower HK2 and PFKP protein and higher MPC2, OGDH and MDH1 protein in APOE4; failure to confirm HK2/PFKP protein reduction would leave the bottleneck unsupported, and failure to confirm MDH1/OGDH would restrict the claim to transcriptional priming only.", "Specificity control: the nuclear-encoded OXPHOS up-shift should be accompanied by increased assembled complex I/IV activity; if mtDNA-encoded subunit protein (MT-CO2, MT-ATP6, consistent with their down-biased transcripts here) is limiting and respiratory-chain activity is actually unchanged or lower in APOE4, the mechanism should be revised toward a mito-nuclear stoichiometry imbalance rather than a completed oxidative shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): the committed glycolytic entry steps are transcriptionally down-biased in APOE4 relative to APOE3 (gene:HK2 effect -3.67, 3.6th percentile of the 2212 differential RNA rows; gene:PFKP -3.08, 5.5th percentile; gene:PFKFB2 -1.10), while facilitative glucose transporters are up (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73). Inferred, not measured: glucose is still imported but hexose-phosphate flux to pyruvate is throttled at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase.", "Step 2 (inferred flux consequence): with restricted glycolytic pyruvate and lactate output, cytosolic NADH must be re-oxidised by transfer into mitochondria rather than by lactate dehydrogenase; the malate-aspartate shuttle and citrate export modules are coordinately elevated (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47).", "Step 3 (measured, RNA; activity inferred): pyruvate that is produced is preferentially imported and decarboxylated rather than reduced to lactate - gene:MPC2 +7.98 (99th percentile), gene:PDP1 +3.00 (PDH phosphatase, predicted to raise the dephosphorylated/active PDH fraction), gene:DLD +5.54 (E3 shared by PDH and OGDH).", "Step 4 (measured, RNA): the TCA cycle and nuclear-encoded respiratory chain programs are coherently up-shifted relative to the whole differential list (TCA set median +4.74, permutation p=1e-4; 38 nuclear OXPHOS subunit genes median +2.64, permutation p=1.1e-3; e.g. gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20). Inferred: higher respiratory capacity per cell, not necessarily higher measured respiration.", "Step 5 (measured, RNA; substrate identity inferred): alternative carbon-entry routes into acetyl-CoA/2-oxoglutarate are up-biased, consistent with substrate switching - lysosomal glycogen/glycan catabolism (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52) with glycogen storage retained (gene:GYS1 +6.10), lipoprotein/lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22), fatty-acid oxidation electron transfer (gene:ETFA +3.55), ketone-body utilisation (gene:OXCT1 +4.72), acetate activation (gene:ACSS2 +2.93), and amino-acid supply/deamination (gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:SLC38A2 +4.45, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:SLC1A5 +1.55).", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): the resulting state is OXPHOS-dependent with low glycolytic reserve, so APOE4 microglia should be disproportionately impaired by mitochondrial pyruvate/ETC blockade and relatively tolerant of glycolysis blockade, and should show reduced capacity for the rapid glycolytic burst normally required for microglial activation.", "Step 7 (bottleneck statement): the single primary bottleneck proposed is cytosolic glycolytic commitment (hexokinase/PFK step); every downstream step above is a compensatory or permissive consequence, not an independent lesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose glycolytic commitment at HK2/PFKP and shift carbon entry to a mitochondrial oxidative program fed by lysosome- and amino-acid-derived substrates"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11681682236089058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14189056258612734, "cosine_similarity": 0.197353904508127, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6283559870550162, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11681682236089058, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14189056258612734, "cosine_similarity": 0.197353904508127, "direction_accuracy": 0.13915857605177995, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6283559870550162, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.51797625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 375}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_059", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) from co-cultured microglia, not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level statements are made relative to this list's own strongly positive background (median 1.46, 77% positive), and the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is left uninterpreted in absolute terms.", "Transcript changes are assumed to translate into proportional changes in the corresponding protein pools for the Rho-module genes; no protein measurement of RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIA or MYH9 abundance is available here, and GTP-loading, cup formation, uptake flux and phagosome pH are inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot uniquely identifies a protein, so spot directions are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Cell-type composition (microglia versus co-cultured astrocytes) and ambient RNA are assumed comparable between genotypes; no replicate structure or normalisation detail was supplied, so the reported p-values may be inflated by per-cell pseudoreplication.", "The strong global positive shift is assumed to be at least partly a compositional/normalisation effect, which makes negative effects conservative and positive effects harder to interpret."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 mainly by selective loss of the hematopoietic Rho/Rac-GTPase activation and actomyosin module (RAC2, DOCK8, MYH9, MYO1F, FAM49B/CYRIB, ARHGAP30, ACTB down against a strongly upward-shifted differential-expression background) together with a very large increase in the GDI-type sequestering regulator ARHGDIA, while recognition-receptor transcripts are not differentially enriched and endolysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and lipogenic transcripts are coordinately raised; we therefore propose that the rate-limiting step differentiating the genotypes is actin-dependent particle internalization (phagocytic-cup closure and macropinocytic/endocytic uptake flux), with the expanded degradative and lipid-handling program being a downstream or compensatory state rather than the bottleneck. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake assay: in a pulse (10-30 min) two-colour inside/outside phagocytosis assay with myelin, synaptosomes or opsonised beads, APOE4 microglia should show equal or greater surface-bound particles but a lower internalized:bound ratio than isogenic APOE3, while the per-phagosome degradation rate (DQ-BSA or pHrodo dequenching normalised to internalized cargo) is equal or higher. If APOE4 instead shows a normal internalized:bound ratio with slower per-phagosome degradation, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and a degradative/lysosomal bottleneck is favoured.", "Active-GTPase test: PAK-PBD and rhotekin-RBD pulldowns should show reduced GTP-Rac and GTP-Rho in APOE4 despite unchanged total Rac1/RhoA and unchanged or increased total actin and ARPC protein; equal active-GTPase loading would weaken the mechanism.", "Rescue: ARHGDIA knockdown, or expression of fast-cycling Rac1(F28L) or constitutively active Rac, in APOE4 microglia should restore the internalization index and cup F-actin without increasing surface TREM2/MERTK/CD36/SCARB1; failure to rescue uptake despite restored cortical F-actin would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy: CK-666 (Arp2/3) or blebbistatin (myosin-II) treatment of APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 low internalized:bound phenotype and, on prolonged treatment, a rise in cathepsin/v-ATPase transcripts; no phenocopy would weaken the causal ordering.", "Receptor-step control: flow cytometry of surface TREM2, MERTK, CD36, SCARB1 and ITGB1 should show no reduction in APOE4; a marked surface-receptor reduction would shift support to a recognition-step mechanism.", "Artefact control: if ACTB and MYH9 protein and total phalloidin-stained F-actin are unchanged between genotypes and spike-in-normalised RNA removes the global positive shift and the ACTB/MYH9 negative effects, the transcript evidence for this module would be attributed to composition/normalisation and the hypothesis substantially weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mechanism_steps": ["Recognition capacity is retained or increased in APOE4: transcripts for opsonic, scavenger and lectin receptors (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:ITGB1) are all positive, but as a set they are no higher than the global upward shift of this differential list (set median 1.35 vs global median 1.46), so cargo binding is inferred, not measured, to be at least as competent as in APOE3 and is not the differentiating step.", "The signal-to-cytoskeleton coupling module is selectively reduced: gene:RAC2 and its GEF gene:DOCK8, the cortical/contractile effectors gene:MYH9 and gene:MYO1F, the Rac-pathway regulators gene:FAM49B and gene:ARHGAP30, the leukocyte sialomucin gene:SPN and gene:ACTB itself are among the few strongly negative rows in a list where 77% of rows are positive; gene:ARHGDIA (RhoGDI-type sequestering regulator) is one of the largest positive effects.", "Inferred (not measured) consequence: a smaller GTP-loaded Rac/Rho pool and increased cytosolic sequestration of Rho-family GTPases, i.e. an activity-level rather than an abundance-level defect, consistent with Arp2/3 subunit transcripts (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5) and actin/ARPC5/profilin-containing protein spots (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:081, protein_spot:092) not being reduced.", "Reduced Rac-GTP-driven branched-actin polymerisation and reduced myosin-II contractility are predicted to lower phagocytic-cup closure and internalization flux per bound particle, while leaving surface binding and downstream phagosome maturation machinery intact.", "Downstream/compensatory arm: the endolysosomal degradative program is coordinately raised (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), as is a lipogenic/sterol program (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:SCP2, gene:DHCR24, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE), so degradative capacity is inferred not to be limiting.", "Net predicted phenotype: a mismatch state with competent recognition and elevated hydrolytic/lipid-storage capacity but low uptake flux, accompanied by a scavenger/lipid-laden marker shift (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS1, gene:CD163, gene:MRC1, gene:VAT1) and loss of homeostatic transcripts (gene:CSF1, gene:CTSS)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at Rho/Rac-GTPase-driven internalization, not at cargo recognition or lysosomal degradation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22761510910903518, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12308752368003238, "cosine_similarity": 0.19694795069386847, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_059", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6509676375404531, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22761510910903518, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12308752368003238, "cosine_similarity": 0.19694795069386847, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6509676375404531, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9627025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 376}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_103", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level claims are made relative to the internal background (global median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), not to an absolute zero.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effects is preserved; only ranks and within-dataset comparisons are used, so conclusions do not depend on the base.", "Transcript differences are assumed to translate, at least partially, into protein and enzymatic activity differences; hydrolase activity, acidification, lysosomal pH, cargo flux, lipid localization and lipid pool sizes were NOT measured here and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level directions are used only as weak, non-confirmatory context (e.g., ANXA1-containing spots up; ATP6V1E1- and CTSD/CTSB/HEXB-containing spots split in direction).", "Genes central to the proposed egress bottleneck (NPC1, PSAP, GRN, ASAH1, LIPA, MCOLN1, TMEM175, ABCA1/ABCG1, PLIN2) are absent from the supplied list; their absence is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change.", "The astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent difference in cell composition or sequencing depth could contribute to the global positive RNA shift; the mechanism relies on within-compartment contrasts that are partially protected from, but not immune to, that confound.", "The comparison is a genotype contrast at a single timepoint (Day 30, mock); no time course or intervention is present, so causal direction between the lysosomal state and the lipid-synthesis state is assumed, not shown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a selectively amplified luminal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcriptional program (GAA, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK; ATP6V1H/1A/0C; with TFEB/TFEC elevated) that is NOT accompanied by a proportional increase in limiting-membrane, sterol/lipid-egress and lysosome-reformation components (NPC2, LAMP1, SCARB2, LAPTM5, SPG11 all at or below the strongly up-shifted background). We propose that the primary bottleneck is therefore export of hydrolysis products (sterols, sphingoid/ceramide backbones, acyl chains) out of the endolysosomal lumen, not hydrolytic capacity; the retained catabolites are inferred to be re-routed into ER glycerolipid/neutral-lipid synthesis (AGPAT2, LPCAT1, SCD, DGAT1, SREBF1) and to sustain a chronic TFEB-associated lysosomal stress state at the expense of homeostatic microglial output (CSF1, CTSS strongly reduced). Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a directional hypothesis derived from selected differential-expression rows and ambiguous protein spots.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, boosting the hydrolytic arm (TFEB overexpression or mTORC1 inhibition) should further raise hydrolase transcripts/activity but should NOT normalize the APOE4-versus-APOE3 neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet excess, whereas relieving lysosomal lipid export (2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or NPC2/NPC1 supplementation-overexpression) should reduce it by \u003e50% of the genotype gap. If TFEB induction rescues the lipid phenotype and export relief does not, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Cargo-processing kinetics: DQ-BSA dequenching and BODIPY-LDL/myelin-debris degradation rates should be equal to or faster in APOE4 than APOE3, while post-degradation export is delayed (filipin- or GFP-D4H-positive unesterified sterol retained in LAMP1-positive compartments; delayed appearance of label in ER/lipid droplets). Slower DQ-BSA dequenching in APOE4 would show hydrolysis, not egress, is limiting and would weaken the mechanism.", "Lipidomic prediction for the same cells (mock, Day 30): APOE4 should show increased MUFA-rich triacylglycerol/diacylglycerol species (16:1, 18:1 acyl chains, consistent with SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1 induction), increased late-endosomal bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate, and a decreased sphingomyelin/ceramide ratio (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA induction). Finding higher sphingomyelin with lower ceramide, and no TAG increase, would falsify the inferred hydrolytic-flux and rerouting steps.", "Stoichiometry test: immunoblot/immunofluorescence should show increased GBA, HEXA/B, CTSB/CTSD and v-ATPase V1 protein per cell in APOE4, with unchanged or reduced LAMP1, NPC2 and SPG11 protein, i.e., hydrolase-to-membrane ratio increased. Unchanged or reduced hydrolase protein and activity despite elevated transcripts would break the transcript-to-capacity inference (the supplied protein-spot data, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065, protein_spot:067 and protein_spot:069, already give weak counter-evidence).", "Specificity test: CTSS knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the antigen-processing/secretory changes (CD74 handling) but NOT the lipid-droplet phenotype; if CTSS loss alone reproduces the lipid phenotype, the bottleneck is proteolytic rather than lipid-egress."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_103", "mechanism_steps": ["Cargo delivery arm: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid-cargo receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22; gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7 modestly above background). Inferred, not measured: increased flux of lipoprotein/membrane-lipid cargo into the endosomal system.", "Hydrolytic arm is selectively amplified: luminal acid hydrolases are shifted above the already up-shifted transcriptome background (set median 2.75 vs global median 1.46; Mann-Whitney p=5e-4; permutation p=0.015), together with v-ATPase subunits and the CLEAR transcription factors TFEB/TFEC. Inferred (not measured): higher acidification and higher acid-hydrolase activity per lysosome.", "Egress/limiting-membrane arm is not scaled: NPC2, LAMP1, SCARB2, LAPTM4B, LAPTM5 and SPG11 sit at or below the global median, and the AP-5 subunits (AP5M1, AP5S1, AP5Z1) are strongly up while their obligate partner SPG11 is down, an inferred stoichiometric imbalance in the AP-5/spatacsin lysosome-reformation module. Inferred: cargo/catabolite egress and lysosome reformation become rate-limiting relative to hydrolysis.", "Consequence 1 (localization, inferred): hydrolysis products accumulate in an expanding late-endosomal/lysosomal compartment; annexin-type membrane-repair/phagocytic proteins rise (gene:ANXA1 +4.15, with the four largest up-shifted protein spots all listing ANXA1 among candidates), consistent with increased endomembrane load or damage.", "Consequence 2 (flux, inferred): lipid that does reach the ER/cytosol is shunted into glycerolipid and neutral-lipid synthesis (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:MGLL +4.0), predicting MUFA-rich TAG/lipid-droplet accumulation rather than efficient sterol/fatty-acid disposal.", "Consequence 3 (state): the compartment stress sustains a TFEB/TFEC-associated program and a disease-associated-like shift (gene:LGALS3, gene:FTH1 up) while homeostatic/secretory microglial genes fall (gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:CTSS -5.57), so the lysosomal proteolytic repertoire is remodelled rather than uniformly increased."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify the acid-hydrolase arm of the endolysosome without matching cargo egress, making post-hydrolytic lipid export the rate-limiting step and diverting lipid into ER neutral-lipid synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.33226562788465086, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14604364014994212, "cosine_similarity": 0.19607749645043904, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_103", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6621650485436893, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.33226562788465086, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14604364014994212, "cosine_similarity": 0.19607749645043904, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6621650485436893, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3590475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 377}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_011", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1 on an unspecified log base, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with 1705/2212 positive; directional claims are therefore judged against that skewed background, and specifically against the internal sign-balanced block (rows 2-509, 507/1014 positive) where the uptake-receptor (14/14 up) and lysosomal (21/23 up) patterns remain coherent. Genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged (e.g. ABCA1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE were not supplied).", "Increased hydrolase, v-ATPase and receptor transcripts are assumed to translate into increased corresponding protein and organelle capacity; no lysosomal enzyme activity, acidification, phagocytic rate, SREBP-2 cleavage or TFEB nuclear localization was measured.", "Elevated SREBP-target transcripts are interpreted as an ER sterol-sensing pool that is not replete; the ER-accessible cholesterol pool itself was not measured and this inference could be wrong if the transcripts are driven by another regulator.", "2D-gel protein spots are multi-candidate (2-6 candidates, mean 4.8, no single-candidate spot); no spot is treated as identifying an individual protein, and 64/92 spots being positive mirrors the global up-skew.", "Storage-pool expansion is a prediction for the mock condition, not an observation; reduced reserve under a future lipid/debris challenge is not evidence of an ongoing defect in the measured condition.", "Replicate number, sequencing depth and normalization were not supplied; the very wide effect range (-7.9 to +15.5) suggests low-precision pseudobulk estimates, so single-gene magnitudes are used only qualitatively.", "Causality is not established: the comparison is a genotype contrast, and every step is inferred from steady-state abundance."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30) differ from APOE3 by a coordinated cell-state change rather than a single blocked step: transcripts for lipoprotein/debris uptake receptors (14/14 represented members up in the sign-balanced part of the selected list, e.g. gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163, gene:C1QA/B/C) and for the lysosomal/CLEAR hydrolase and v-ATPase machinery (21/23 up in that same balanced background, e.g. gene:GAA +10.0, gene:GBA +6.7, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:SMPD1 +5.6, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, with gene:TFEB +2.4 and gene:MITF +1.0) are jointly elevated, together with esterification/neutral-lipid-storage and MUFA-biasing enzymes (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCD up; gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 down) and with SREBP-target sterol-synthesis transcripts still elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:ACSS2, gene:EBP). We propose that in APOE4 the acquired lipid is preferentially routed to esterified/neutral-lipid stores and to the lysosomal compartment instead of to the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool, so acquisition and synthesis programs are not switched off; the predicted lipidomic consequence in this mock condition is enlarged, MUFA-enriched cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol pools and a larger lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid substrate load. This is an inferred routing and cell-state change, not a demonstrated degradative bottleneck and not established causality; all measurements are transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances, no lipid, flux, activity or localization measurement was supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminator (routing versus sterol deficit): loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with LDL or 25-hydroxycholesterol should suppress SREBP-2 target transcripts (gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1) markedly less in APOE4 while raising its cholesteryl-ester mass more. If APOE4 suppresses these targets as fully as APOE3 and shows equal or lower cholesteryl ester, the routing mechanism is wrong and a simple reduced-delivery/sterol-deficit explanation is favored.", "Prospective: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in mock APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester/TAG mass, raise ER-accessible cholesterol and reduce SREBP-2 target transcripts more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3. No genotype-differential response would weaken step 3-4.", "Prospective lipidomics on the same mock condition: APOE4 should show higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol mass with MUFA (16:1, 18:1) enrichment and relatively reduced PUFA-containing glycerophospholipids (consistent with gene:SCD up, gene:ACSL4/gene:ACSL5 down). Equal or lower neutral-lipid mass in APOE4 would falsify the storage-accumulation claim.", "Prospective activity test of capacity versus bottleneck: measured lysosomal hydrolase activities (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, cathepsin B/D) and DQ-BSA degradation rate should be equal or higher in mock APOE4 despite storage-lipid accumulation. If these activities are instead reduced, the mechanism should be replaced by a lysosomal degradative bottleneck model.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not present-state defect): after myelin-debris or oxLDL loading, APOE4 microglia should accumulate more undigested lysosomal lipid and show a smaller further induction of the CLEAR program (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H) than APOE3. Equal accumulation and equal inducibility would indicate successful adaptation with no reduced reserve.", "Prospective TFEB dependency: TFEB/MITF knockdown should preferentially reduce the lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts in APOE4 and increase lysosomal lipid storage; if these transcripts are TFEB-independent here, step 2 must be revised."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 raises receptor-mediated lipid/lipoprotein and debris uptake capacity in microglia: every represented uptake/opsonin receptor transcript is increased in the sign-balanced portion of the selected list (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:STAB1 +1.13, gene:FCGR1A +1.59, gene:ITGB5 +1.35, gene:C1QA/C1QB/C1QC, gene:APOE +1.24; also gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:LDLR +1.50).", "The increased cargo load is matched by a MITF/TFEB-associated expansion of lysosomal capacity at the transcript level: gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:CTSH, acidification subunits gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, plus gene:GNPTG (M6P tagging), gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:SLC38A7.", "Cargo lipid is routed into esterification and neutral-lipid storage rather than into the ER regulatory sterol pool: gene:SOAT1 +1.25 (cholesteryl-ester synthesis), gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29 (glycerolipid assembly), with an acyl-composition shift toward monounsaturated chains (gene:SCD +4.17 up; gene:ACSL4 -2.14 and gene:ACSL5 -3.11 down, gene:ALOX15 -3.63 down).", "Because the ER-accessible sterol pool is not replenished, SREBP-driven acquisition/synthesis transcripts remain elevated instead of being repressed by the extra uptake: gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34 (this arm sits mostly in the up-only part of the selected list, so it is supportive rather than decisive).", "Uptake plus continued synthesis plus routing to storage forms a feed-forward loop that enlarges esterified/neutral lipid and lysosomal substrate pools while the cell sustains, rather than fails, throughput: mitochondrial/TCA and oxidative transcripts are also up (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1), whereas upper glycolysis transcripts fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12) despite higher transporters (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) - a state consistent with oxidative handling of acquired lipid, not with a global collapse.", "Predicted (unmeasured here) lipid output of this state in the mock condition: higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol mass with MUFA (16:1/18:1) enrichment and relatively lower PUFA-containing species, higher lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid substrate load, and reduced reserve that would become a visible defect only under a lipid/debris challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a high-uptake endolysosomal lipid-routing state that diverts sterol into storage and lysosomal compartments while ER sterol sensing stays unsatisfied"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1618266070967027, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22266215411747095, "cosine_similarity": 0.1947640848967445, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_011", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6795760517799353, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1618266070967027, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22266215411747095, "cosine_similarity": 0.1947640848967445, "direction_accuracy": 0.21359223300970873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6795760517799353, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.91076125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 94}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_042", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased whole transcriptome; 77% of rows are positive and the median log fold change is +1.46, so all statements are made as within-list rank contrasts against that shifted background, never as raw up/down calls.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no fold-change conversion is used anywhere in the argument.", "Absence of a gene from the list (e.g. NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, PLIN2, STARD3, MCOLN1) is uninformative and is never read as 'unchanged'.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity only; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, TFEB nuclear localisation, SREBP cleavage, lipid flux and lipid pools were not measured and are labelled as inferred throughout.", "The protein-spot layer cannot corroborate or refute this hypothesis: each spot carries a mean of 4.8 candidate genes, keratin/actin dominate the candidate lists, and no spot lists any sterol-, lipoprotein- or lipid-metabolic candidate. Spots containing a lysosomal-hydrolase candidate are statistically indistinguishable from other spots (Mann-Whitney p = 0.27), so no protein observation ID is claimed as support.", "Gene sets were assembled from unverified background knowledge without database retrieval; set membership, not the data, is the main analyst degree of freedom.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some lipid cargo may be astrocyte-derived and part of the genotype effect could be non-cell-autonomous; no sorted or single-genotype-culture control is supplied.", "Causality is not established: this is a cross-sectional isogenic contrast, and reverse causation (an immune-effector shift driving lysosomal gene expression) is not excluded by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells not by a sterol-biosynthetic or SREBP-2 sensing drive (that arm sits at or below the list-wide median) but by a mismatch inside the endolysosome: transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid cargo delivery (SCARB1) and for acid hydrolases plus v-ATPase subunits are among the most strongly elevated in the dataset, whereas the transcripts encoding the post-hydrolytic sterol/lipid egress and hydrolase-sorting limb (NPC2, SCARB2, OSBPL1A, OSBPL8, M6PR) are at or below the median of the same up-shifted list. We propose that the rate-limiting step is export of liberated sterol and lipid out of the lysosomal lumen, so lipid is retained in lysosomes, the cell responds with an SREBP-1/desaturase-biased lipid-remodelling and neutral-lipid-storage program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, MGLL, DGAT1) rather than an SREBP-2 sterol-starvation program, and the microglial immune-effector program is relatively suppressed. Lysosomal lipid content itself was not measured; the bottleneck is inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 re-expression) in APOE4 microglia should bypass the proposed egress bottleneck and lower lysosome-localised unesterified cholesterol (filipin or a lysosome-targeted sterol sensor, with LAMP1 colocalisation) toward APOE3 levels, and should partially normalise the SREBF1/SCD/DHCR24/MGLL arm and the CTSS/CSF1 immune-effector transcripts, WITHOUT requiring any change in SCARB1. If cyclodextrin lowers lysosomal sterol yet leaves the SREBF1/SCD arm and the immune-effector suppression unchanged, Steps 4-6 are wrong.", "CARGO-INFLUX TEST: SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1 blockade in APOE4 microglia should reduce lysosomal lipid load and pull the CLEAR hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) back toward APOE3 values. If hydrolase transcripts are unmoved by loss of SCARB1-dependent uptake, Step 1 as the upstream driver fails.", "REJECTED-FOCUS TEST: A statin or an SQLE inhibitor should NOT normalise the APOE4 lysosomal or immune phenotype, because the SREBP-2/mevalonate arm is at or below the list median. If statin treatment does normalise the hydrolase and immune-effector transcript differences, the de novo sterol synthesis/sensing model that we reject is favoured over this trafficking-bottleneck model.", "CAPACITY-VERSUS-EGRESS TEST: Direct measurement should show APOE4 lysosomes with equal or greater mature hydrolase activity per lysosome (DQ-BSA, Magic Red cathepsin B, 4-MU-glycosidase assays) and equal or lower luminal pH than APOE3, together with higher retained lysosomal sterol. If APOE4 lysosomes are instead alkalinised and hydrolase-deficient, the bottleneck is degradation or acidification, not egress, and this hypothesis must be replaced.", "PROTEIN-LEVEL TEST: Targeted immunoblot or targeted MS (not 2D spots) should show NPC2 and SCARB2 protein unchanged or reduced in APOE4 while GBA, HEXA and CTSB mature forms are increased. A coordinated increase of NPC2/SCARB2 protein matching the hydrolases would remove the mismatch on which Step 3 depends.", "TIME-COURSE / DOSE TEST: Loading APOE3 microglia with exogenous lipoprotein or myelin should reproduce the APOE4 hydrolase-high / egress-flat transcript ratio; failure to reproduce it under matched lipid load would indicate an APOE4 effect that is not explained by lipid cargo burden."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia elevate transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid cargo capture, most conspicuously SCARB1 (99th percentile of the supplied differential list; gene:SCARB1), with CD36, MRC1 and TREM2 only near the list median. We infer, but did not measure, an increased rate of lipid delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA; inferred activity): A CLEAR/TFEB-type transcriptional response is engaged - TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF) together with a coherent block of acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:MAN2B1, gene:DPP7) and v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1). TFEB nuclear localisation, hydrolase protein maturation and luminal pH were not measured; increased hydrolytic capacity is inferred from transcript abundance only.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA contrast; the proposed bottleneck): The limb that moves sterol and lipid out of the lysosome and that routes new hydrolases into it does not scale with Step 2. NPC2, SCARB2, OSBPL1A sit in the lowest third of the up-shifted list (gene:NPC2, gene:SCARB2, gene:OSBPL1A), OSBPL8 and M6PR are frankly reduced (gene:OSBPL8, gene:M6PR), and the hydrolase block ranks significantly higher than this egress/sorting block (median percentile 71 vs 35). We propose lysosomal sterol/lipid egress, not hydrolysis, is rate-limiting for lipid clearance.", "STEP 4 (inferred pool, not observed): Liberated unesterified cholesterol and sphingolipid-derived products are retained in the lysosomal lumen and are delivered inefficiently to the ER sterol sensor. No lipid, filipin, or organelle-fractionation measurement is supplied, so this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "STEP 5 (measured RNA; discriminates two lipid programs): The transcriptional output is SREBP-1/desaturase- and storage-biased (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:MGLL, gene:DGAT1, gene:DHCR24, median percentile 67) rather than an SREBP-2 sterol-deficit program (gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:MYLIP, median percentile ~41). This argues the cells are lipid-loaded and remodelling, not cholesterol-starved, and is the reason we reject de novo sterol synthesis/sensing as the primary driver.", "STEP 6 (measured RNA; inferred functional consequence): Against the strong global up-shift of this selected list, the myeloid immune-effector program is relatively depressed (unbiased 21-gene myeloid set, permutation p_down = 0.042; illustrated by gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:SPN, gene:LAPTM5, gene:SEMA4A), while TCA/oxidative transcripts are strongly raised (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A46). We infer a lipid-burdened, catabolically biased, immunologically dampened APOE4 microglial state."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: CLEAR-amplified hydrolytic capacity outpaces an unscaled NPC2/SCARB2/OSBP sterol-export limb, not increased sterol biosynthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3127423106745929, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.02204738009220191, "cosine_similarity": 0.1927450983488346, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_042", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6182168284789644, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3127423106745929, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.02204738009220191, "cosine_similarity": 0.1927450983488346, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6182168284789644, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.16096075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 378}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_070", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect|\u003e1 in an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46); all pathway claims are therefore made relative to this internal background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and absent genes (CAT, SOD1/2, NFE2L2, HMOX1, GCLC/GCLM, TXNRD1, PEX genes, mitoribosome, TFAM) are treated as unmeasured rather than unchanged.", "Probe-based 10X Flex quantification of mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to be comparable between genotypes; if MT- probe capture, ambient-RNA correction or mitochondrial-fraction QC filtering differs between APOE4 and APOE3 libraries, the mitonuclear divergence could be technical.", "Increased subunit transcript abundance is assumed to raise the corresponding protein pools at least partially; no mitochondrial protein, assembled complex, respiration rate, mtDNA copy number, NAD(P)H or ROS measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes; protein_spot:077 (PRDX2 among KRT1/KRT9/KRT10/RAB1A/ACTB) and protein_spot:017 (CAT among CORO1C/ENTPD5) are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous; APOE4 astrocyte-derived lipoprotein or cystine supply could contribute to the microglial redox state.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so differences are attributed to APOE genotype rather than line background, but replicate structure was not supplied and per-gene effect sizes (up to |15|) are implausibly large for bulk log2 fold changes, suggesting a pseudobulk/statistical scale that should not be over-interpreted quantitatively."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia coordinately raise nuclear-encoded TCA-cycle, electron-transport-chain accessory-subunit, carrier and import transcripts without a matching rise in mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit transcripts; we hypothesise that the resulting shortfall of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not a lack of nuclear subunits, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of respiratory complexes, so that electron transfer is handled by an increased pool of incompletely assembled/electron-stalled Complex I, raising matrix superoxide/peroxide production and forcing a compensatory thiol-peroxidase and thioredoxin program (PRDX2/3/5, TXNDC17, GPX4, GSS, FTH1). Causality is not established by these data; the assembly, flux and ROS steps are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a normal or increased amount of nuclear accessory subunit protein but a reduced ratio of assembled Complex I holoenzyme (and supercomplex) to total NDUFA/NDUFB subunit protein, with accumulation of ~400-830 kDa CI assembly intermediates. If assembled CI holoenzyme, in-gel CI activity and supercomplex distribution are equal between genotypes, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Baseline matrix-targeted peroxide/superoxide reporters (MitoSOX, mito-roGFP2-Orp1, HyPer7) should read more oxidised in APOE4, and the difference should be largely abolished by the Complex I site-IQ-selective suppressor S1QEL1.1 but not by a site-IIIQo suppressor; no genotype difference in mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation, or equal reversal by S3QEL, would weaken the mechanism.", "APOE4 microglia should be hypersensitive to blockade of mitochondrial translation: 24-48 h doxycycline or chloramphenicol should cause a larger fractional loss of maximal/spare respiratory capacity and a larger rise in PRDX3 hyperoxidation (PRDX-SO2/3 immunoblot or dimer:monomer shift) in APOE4 than in APOE3. Equal sensitivity would argue against a mtDNA-encoded-subunit limitation.", "Conversely, relieving the bottleneck - boosting mitochondrial biogenesis/mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (e.g. TFAM overexpression, NAD+ precursor, or mtDNA-replete cybrid-style rescue) - should normalise the assembled-CI ratio and lower PRDX2/PRDX3/TXNDC17 transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3 without changing APOE expression itself.", "PRDX3 (or TXN2) knockdown should raise mitochondrial peroxide and reduce viability/phagocytic capacity significantly more in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia; equal sensitivity would indicate the antioxidant induction is not load-bearing compensation.", "Seahorse respirometry should show APOE4 with reduced spare respiratory capacity and increased basal ECAR/OCR ratio despite equal or higher nuclear-encoded CI subunit protein; higher maximal respiration in APOE4 would falsify the capped-capacity step.", "Because peroxisomal genes are not enriched here (ACOX1, SCP2, CROT, PRDX5, MPV17 up but ABCD1 down; set median +1.60 versus background +1.46, p=0.77), catalase inhibition (3-aminotriazole) is predicted NOT to differentially harm APOE4 microglia; a strong APOE4-selective effect would favour a peroxisomal rather than a Complex I origin of the oxidant load."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia transcriptionally up-regulate the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative module: 19/19 detected Complex I accessory/supernumerary subunits, other ETC subunits, TCA enzymes, inner-membrane carriers and import channels are all higher than APOE3 and higher than the strongly up-shifted background of this selected DE list (measured RNA: median ~+2.8 versus background median ~+1.46, n=52, permutation p\u003c5e-5).", "The mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunit transcripts do not follow: 4 of 6 detected MT- transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are lower in APOE4, giving a nuclear-versus-mitochondrial genome divergence (Mann-Whitney p~2e-4). We infer, but did not measure, a corresponding shortfall in mitochondrially translated core subunit protein.", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK (inferred): assembly of respiratory complexes, chiefly the membrane arm of Complex I (ND subunits) and the ATP synthase Fo rotor, becomes limited by mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply while nuclear accessory subunits are in excess, so a larger fraction of Complex I exists as partially assembled or supercomplex-poor intermediates. Only subunit transcripts, not assembled holoenzyme, were measured.", "Electron-stalled or incompletely assembled Complex I favours single-electron leak to O2 (inferred flux), increasing matrix superoxide and, after dismutation, matrix and cytosolic H2O2; steady-state ROS itself was not measured here.", "The cell buffers this peroxide by inducing thiol-peroxidase and thioredoxin-system transcripts (PRDX3 and PRDX5 matrix/mitochondrial, PRDX2 cytosolic, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4, GSS, MSRA, SELENOW) and the iron-sequestering FTH1; a protein spot whose candidate list contains PRDX2 is also increased, though the spot is not uniquely identified.", "Because peroxide detoxification through peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin and GPX4 consumes NADPH- and glutathione-derived reducing equivalents, and because assembled respiratory capacity is capped by step 3, the cells shift ATP demand toward glycolysis (HIF1A, SLC2A1, SLC2A3, ENO1, GPI up) and carry an increased lysosomal/lipid-catabolic load (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU up) - both inferred consequences, not measured fluxes."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch at Complex I assembly drives a chronic peroxide load and thiol-antioxidant compensation in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2595539637410922, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2330519314941634, "cosine_similarity": 0.18926430368729324, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6628608414239483, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2595539637410922, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2330519314941634, "cosine_similarity": 0.18926430368729324, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6628608414239483, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.661224, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 379}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_070", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows pass adjusted p\u003c0.05 and |effect|\u003e1), so all statements are relative ranks within that list, not whole-transcriptome enrichment; the logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and magnitudes are therefore not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, only loosely, pathway capacity; flux, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, GSH/GSSG ratio, peroxide levels, mitochondrial membrane potential and enzyme localisation were not measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous corroboration only; no spot is claimed to identify a unique protein.", "The overall differential list is up-shifted (about 77% positive, median effect about +1.46), so an absolute increase is uninformative and only above/below-list-median contrasts are used; this also assumes the up-shift is not an artefact that differentially distorts particular pathways.", "Key redox genes (G6PD, CAT, GSR, TXNRD1, SOD1/2, NFE2L2) are absent from the supplied list; their absence is treated as 'not reported', not as 'unchanged'.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous; replicate number is not supplied, so very large effects may be unstable."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcript program favouring mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA cycle and electron-transport subunits together with a strongly elevated peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin/glutathione-synthesis module, while the NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate and NAD-kinase transcripts are lower; we hypothesise that the resulting mismatch makes cytosolic NADPH supply (not peroxidase protein amount) the rate-limiting step for peroxide detoxification, so APOE4 microglia carry an oxidised, poorly buffered cytosolic thiol pool at baseline and are selectively vulnerable to further oxidant or PPP challenge. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is explicitly not proposed as the oxidant source and is not supported by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Compartment-resolved redox sensors (cytosolic vs mitochondrial roGFP2-Grx1 and roGFP2-Orp1) in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a more oxidised baseline and slower post-bolus-H2O2 recovery in the cytosol, with a smaller or absent difference in the matrix. If cytosolic recovery kinetics and baseline EGSH are indistinguishable between genotypes, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological block of the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide) at a dose that is near-neutral for APOE3 should produce a significant genotype x drug interaction in APOE4 (greater PRDX2 hyperoxidation by PRDX-SO2/3 immunoblot, lower NADPH/NADP+ by iNap or LC-MS, lower viability). Equal sensitivity of both genotypes would weaken the mechanism and favour a simple 'more antioxidant enzyme' interpretation.", "Restricting mitochondrial oxidative input (UK5099 to block the pyruvate carrier, or low-dose rotenone) should lower the APOE4 excess of peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin transcripts and PRDX hyperoxidation toward APOE3 levels; if the peroxiredoxin program is unchanged by these treatments, the proposed mitochondrial origin of the oxidant load (Steps 1-3) is wrong.", "Seahorse/13C tracing should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption, a higher OCR/ECAR ratio and higher fractional pyruvate oxidation in APOE4; if respiration is equal or lower despite the transcript pattern, the abundance-to-flux inference in Step 1-2 is refuted.", "Raising cytosolic NADPH supply (cytosolic IDH1 or G6PD overexpression, or ME1 restoration) should normalise cytosolic EGSH and oxidant resistance in APOE4 without reversing the TCA/ETC transcript signature; if such rescue does not improve oxidant handling, the NADPH-limitation step is falsified.", "NNT knockdown should selectively impair APOE4 (matrix oxidation, viability under peroxide) relative to APOE3; equal effects would argue against the proposed compartment shift of NADPH provisioning.", "Peroxisomal counter-test: peroxisome-targeted catalase overexpression or ACOX1 inhibition should have little effect on the genotype difference; a strong rescue by peroxisomal manipulation would favour a peroxisomal mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 cells show higher transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and TCA enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:MDH1) and lower transcripts for upper glycolysis (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP); we infer, but have not measured, an increased fraction of carbon oxidised in mitochondria rather than fermented.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): coordinated up-shift of electron-transport-chain subunit transcripts relative to the rest of the differential list implies greater respiratory chain content and electron flux, which is expected to raise matrix and cytosolic H2O2 delivery from complexes I and III; ROS production itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, compensatory response): the thiol-peroxidase/thioredoxin arm is disproportionately elevated (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GPX4, gene:MGST2, gene:GSS, gene:CYB5R3), consistent with an adaptive increase in peroxide-reducing capacity rather than with unopposed antioxidant loss.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck): every peroxiredoxin/glutathione turnover must be repaid by NADPH, yet the cytosolic NADPH- and NADP-supplying transcripts are reduced or not co-induced (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK down; gene:ME1 below the list median), so we propose that reductant regeneration, not peroxidase abundance, limits steady-state peroxide clearance in the cytosol.", "Step 5 (compartment shift): induction of gene:NNT suggests re-provisioning of NADPH inside mitochondria at the expense of proton-motive force, which would preferentially protect the matrix pool (gene:PRDX3) and leave the cytosolic thioredoxin/glutathione pool comparatively oxidised.", "Step 6 (predicted state, not observed): the predicted consequence is a lower cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratio, increased hyperoxidised PRDX2, and a reduced reserve for acute oxidant challenge in APOE4 microglia even under mock conditions; none of these pools were measured here.", "Step 7 (excluded branch): peroxisomal transcripts are not coherently changed (gene:ACOX1 is below the list median and gene:ABCD1 is decreased), so peroxisomal very-long-chain fatty-acid oxidation is proposed to be a consequence-neutral or slightly reduced pathway, not the oxidant source."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift catabolism from glycolysis to mitochondrial oxidation and expand thiol-peroxidase capacity, making cytosolic NADPH regeneration the redox bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.043052837573385516, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.023293327811075997, "cosine_similarity": 0.18827141795416844, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378381877022654, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.043052837573385516, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.023293327811075997, "cosine_similarity": 0.18827141795416844, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6378381877022654, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46433725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 380}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_163", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are selected differential-expression results from a two-block workbook (a paired up/down table of 1012 genes and an up-only list of 1200 genes); the apparent global positive shift (77% up, mean +1.39) is treated as a selection artifact, and all enrichment claims are made against block-matched backgrounds rather than against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes reach +15.5; magnitudes are used only for ranking within the same table, never as fold-change estimates or for cross-modality scaling against the log2 protein spots.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate (2-6 genes each) and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level statements are about the aggregate spot signal, and any assignment to CTSD, CTSB, CTSL, HEXB, ACP2, MAN2B1, GNS or ATP6V1E1 is provisional.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect and possibly non-monotonic proxy for the corresponding protein pool; here the measured spot-to-candidate-transcript correlation is essentially zero (r=-0.05 over 71 spots), so the transcript-protein uncoupling is assumed real rather than purely technical.", "Cargo influx rate, lysosomal pH, hydrolase enzymatic activity, autophagic flux, lysosome number and position, and all lipid and sterol pools are unmeasured in this dataset and are inferred quantities only.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed isogenic and equivalently differentiated at day 30; a difference in microglial maturation or in astrocyte co-culture composition could generate the same receptor/lysosome/mitochondria transcript pattern.", "Direction of causality between the receptor program, the lysosomal transcript program and the SREBP program is assumed, not established, by these steady-state mock-condition measurements."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by an endolysosomal cargo-processing bottleneck: uptake/opsonin-receptor and MiT/TFE-target hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are coordinately higher in APOE4, yet the 2D protein-spot data show no matched net increase in lysosomal hydrolase or V1-subunit spot abundance and instead a bidirectional redistribution of cathepsin-candidate spots, so functional degradative and acidification capacity per lysosome is predicted not to scale with the increased cargo load; the resulting retention of undigested lipid/sterol-rich cargo keeps ER-accessible sterol low and sustains SREBP-dependent lipogenic transcription. All flux, pH, activity, localization and causal-direction statements are inferences, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pulse-chase a defined degradable cargo (DQ-BSA, fluorogenic cathepsin B/L substrate, or labelled myelin/apoptotic-cell debris) in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia and normalise to internalised cargo and to LAMP1-positive volume. The mechanism predicts equal or greater initial uptake in APOE4 but a lower degradation rate per unit lysosomal volume and accumulation of undigested cargo. If APOE4 shows equal or faster per-lysosome hydrolysis, or lower uptake rather than slower degradation, the bottleneck as stated is wrong.", "TFEB gain-of-function discriminates transcript supply from post-transcriptional capacity: because the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript program is already elevated in APOE4, TFEB or TFE3 overexpression should give little additional cargo clearance in APOE4, whereas restoring acidification or hydrolase maturation (v-ATPase-supporting acidic nanoparticles, exogenous mature cathepsin/hydrolase supplementation) should. Substantial rescue of clearance by TFEB overexpression alone would weaken step 3.", "Lysosomal pH and V-ATPase assembly: ratiometric LysoSensor/pHLuorin measurement should show equal or higher steady-state lysosomal pH (less acidic) in APOE4 despite higher ATP6V1H/1A/0C transcripts, and no increase in membrane-associated V1 subunit protein. Finding APOE4 lysosomes more acidic with increased assembled V1 would falsify the acidification arm.", "Sterol-egress test of step 5: LDL loading should suppress SREBP2 target transcripts (LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7) less efficiently in APOE4 than APOE3, while cholesterol delivered so as to bypass the lysosome (methyl-beta-cyclodextrin-cholesterol) should suppress them equally in both genotypes. Equal suppression by LDL in both genotypes would weaken the lysosome-to-ER egress interpretation.", "Cathepsin maturation: immunoblot of CTSD and CTSB in APOE4 versus APOE3 should show a shifted pro-form to mature-form ratio (higher pro/intermediate fraction) with little change in total protein, matching the bidirectional cathepsin-candidate spot pattern (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down). Unchanged pro/mature ratios with unchanged total would leave the spot pattern unexplained and weaken step 3.", "Specificity control against the mitochondrial alternative: pharmacological restriction of oxidative phosphorylation should not reproduce the APOE4 lysosomal transcript signature in APOE3 cells, whereas cargo overload (myelin or oxLDL feeding) of APOE3 cells should. The reverse result would favour a primary mitochondrial or general stress mechanism over the endolysosomal bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_163", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for scavenger/opsonin/phagocytic receptors (SCARB1, CD36, MRC1, MERTK, GAS6, TREM2, C1QA/B/C, FCGR1A, GPR34, CD33, ITGA6); in the balanced up/down block of the source table 14/15 such genes fall on the up side (binomial p=0.001). We infer, but did not measure, a higher rate of lipoprotein/debris delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts): A coordinated MiT/TFE-type lysosomal-biogenesis transcript program accompanies this: TFEB and MITF up, acid hydrolases up (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, NAGLU, CTSB, CTSD, CTSH, CTSK; 12/14 up in the balanced block, p=0.013) and every measured v-ATPase subunit up (6/6 in the balanced block, p=0.031). This is transcript abundance only and does not establish lysosome number, acidification or hydrolase activity.", "Step 3 (measured protein spots, inferred capacity): The protein-spot layer does not mirror the transcript program. Spots whose candidate lists contain a lysosomal hydrolase average +0.17 log2 versus +0.35 for all spots and split in direction (CTSD/CTSL/CTSB-candidate spots 052, 053, 055, 057, 027 up but 058, 067, 069 down), and both ATP6V1E1-candidate spots (064, 065) decrease. Because spots are multi-candidate, we infer only that the total lysosomal-hydrolase/V1 protein pool is not coordinately raised and that hydrolase spot pattern (proform/glycoform/mature distribution) is shifted; per-lysosome hydrolytic and proton-pumping throughput is therefore predicted to lag cargo influx.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, inferred sorting): Hydrolase delivery and repertoire are internally discordant rather than uniformly boosted: M6PR (CD-MPR) is down while IGF2R (CI-MPR) is up, and the dominant microglial protease transcript CTSS and the sulfatase IDS are strongly down. We infer an imbalance in Golgi-to-endosome hydrolase sorting and a narrowed protease/sulfatase repertoire that further limits degradation of specific cargo classes.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred lipid pool): Despite elevated lipid-uptake receptor transcripts, SREBP-dependent cholesterogenic and lipogenic transcripts remain high (SREBF1, SREBF2, SCD, LDLR, INSIG1, LSS, DHCR7, ACAT2, HMGCS1, plus SOAT1 and APOE). We interpret this as low ER-accessible sterol despite high uptake, i.e. failed lysosome-to-ER sterol egress; no lipid or sterol pool was measured in this dataset.", "Step 6 (measured transcripts, parallel arm): A strong mitochondrial oxidative transcript program (OGDH, MDH1, MPC2, SLC25A46, NDUFA5, ATP5 subunits; TCA and OXPHOS sets enriched above the block-matched background, permutation p\u003c=0.005) accompanies the endolysosomal signature and is read as demand-side support for acidification and membrane traffic, or as an independent parallel difference; its causal relation to the lysosomal bottleneck is untested."], "title": "Cargo influx outpaces per-lysosome degradative throughput in APOE4 microglia: a transcript-rich but protein-uncoupled endolysosomal capacity bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.04311992311108163, "cosine_similarity": 0.18820194970551887, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_163", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434466019417475, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11741682974559686, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.04311992311108163, "cosine_similarity": 0.18820194970551887, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434466019417475, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1864455, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 381}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_018", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The panel-wide positive offset (median reported log fold change +1.46, 1705/2212 rows positive) is largely technical or compositional, so within-panel rank percentiles, not raw magnitudes, carry the genotype-specific signal; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome, so all set-level enrichment statistics are conditional on that selection and are descriptive only.", "Transcript rank is taken as a partial proxy for protein and functional capacity for both hydrolases and SNARE/sorting components; no protein-level measurement of any of these genes is available here.", "Protein spots each carry several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for a specific enzyme.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, pH, fusion-rate, secretion or localisation measurement is supplied; all flux, localisation and storage statements are inferred.", "Replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so uncertainty in individual effects cannot be assessed independently of the reported adjusted p-values, all of which are below 0.05 by construction.", "Astrocyte co-culture and the day-30 timepoint are assumed not to differ systematically between genotypes in a way that alone produces the SNARE-versus-hydrolase rank split."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, the RNA panel shows a coordinated relative increase in luminal acid hydrolase transcripts, led by the sphingolipid-degrading enzymes GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GBA2 and SMPD1, together with a relative decrease in the trans-Golgi/endosome SNARE and mannose-6-phosphate-receptor sorting module (STX16, GOSR1, BET1L, VAMP2, STX17, STXBP5, M6PR, SPG11). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglial sphingolipid turnover is not hydrolase gene expression or de novo sphingolipid synthesis but the SNARE- and CD-M6PR-dependent delivery of newly made hydrolases from the trans-Golgi network to an expanded late-endosomal/lysosomal compartment (RAB7A, VPS18, EPG5, VPS26A, SNX3, AP5M1 relatively increased), so that inferred per-lysosome sphingolipid catabolic flux fails to scale with the transcriptional program and undigested glycosphingolipid and sphingomyelin substrate is predicted to accumulate. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: re-expressing the Golgi-exit/retrieval module (STX16 or CD-M6PR) in APOE4 microglia, without changing hydrolase transcript levels, should raise intracellular GBA and beta-hexosaminidase activity per cell and accelerate clearance of a loaded fluorescent glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin substrate towards APOE3 levels; if instead only over-expression of GBA/HEXA/HEXB itself rescues clearance while STX16 or M6PR restoration does nothing, the delivery bottleneck is wrong and the bottleneck lies in enzyme amount.", "Secretion split: in APOE4 versus APOE3, the fraction of total beta-hexosaminidase and GBA activity recovered in conditioned medium should be higher, while cell-associated activity per unit transcript is equal or lower. If APOE4 intracellular hydrolase activity scales proportionally with the elevated transcripts and the secreted fraction is unchanged, the mechanism is weakened.", "Substrate clearance: pulse-chase of BODIPY-lactosylceramide or NBD-sphingomyelin should show slower endolysosomal degradation and greater residual undigested substrate in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase mRNA; equal or faster clearance in APOE4 falsifies the core claim.", "Fusion specificity: live-imaging or content-mixing assays should show reduced trans-Golgi-to-endosome carrier fusion and reduced STX17-dependent autophagosome-lysosome fusion in APOE4, with lysosomal pH (LysoSensor ratio) not significantly different, consistent with the v-ATPase transcripts sitting at panel background; if APOE4 lysosomes are markedly less acidic and pH correction alone normalises sphingolipid clearance, an acidification mechanism supersedes this one.", "Anabolic control: inhibiting de novo sphingolipid or glucosylceramide synthesis (myriocin or a UGCG inhibitor) should not normalise APOE4 lysosomal substrate accumulation if the defect is delivery-limited catabolism; full normalisation by synthesis blockade would favour an over-synthesis mechanism instead, which the flat anabolic transcript ranks here do not support.", "Genotype specificity: the hydrolase-high/SNARE-low rank split should reproduce in an independent isogenic APOE4 line and should be reversed by APOE4-to-APOE3 gene correction; failure to reproduce would indicate a clone- or batch-specific pattern rather than an APOE4 effect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia show relative increases, above the panel-wide upward offset, in transcripts for luminal sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GBA rank pct 98, gene:HEXA 96, gene:SMPD1 95, gene:GBA2 72, gene:HEXB 66, gene:GLA 52 by within-panel rank) and other acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD); this is abundance of message, not enzyme activity.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, contrast): transcripts of the sphingolipid de novo/anabolic arm are at or below the panel background (gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:ORMDL2, gene:ST3GAL5, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1) and gene:B4GALT5 is in the bottom decile, so the catabolic signal is not a mirror of increased sphingolipid synthesis (catabolic minus anabolic median rank difference 30 percentile points, permutation p = 0.018).", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): the module that moves M6P-tagged hydrolases out of the trans-Golgi and retrieves the sorting receptor is in the lowest deciles (gene:STX16 pct 3, gene:BET1L 3, gene:GOSR1 5, gene:STXBP5 1, gene:STX17 12, gene:VAMP2 13, gene:M6PR 15, gene:SPG11 14; SNARE set median pct 11.5, permutation p_down = 0.0014). We infer reduced trans-Golgi exit, reduced CD-M6PR retrieval and reduced autophagosome-lysosome (STX17-dependent) fusion capacity; fusion rates and receptor recycling were not measured.", "Step 4 (inferred flux): the mismatch between step 1 and step 3 makes hydrolase delivery, not hydrolase transcription, rate-limiting; predicted consequences are increased constitutive secretion of newly synthesised acid hydrolases and per-lysosome enzyme activity that does not scale with transcript level.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred compartment state): late-endosome/lysosome tethering, positioning and retrieval transcripts are relatively increased (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:EPG5, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:AP5M1, gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R), consistent with an expanded degradative compartment that continues to receive membrane and lipoprotein-derived cargo while luminal hydrolase supply lags.", "Step 6 (inferred lipid state, unmeasured): the resulting deficit in delivered GBA/HEXA/HEXB/SMPD1 activity is predicted to leave glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2-type glycosphingolipids and sphingomyelin partially undigested in the endolysosomal lumen; no lipid species were measured in this dataset, so this pool is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 7 (inferred feedback): luminal sphingolipid storage is proposed to sustain the compensatory TFEB-type hydrolase transcription seen here (gene:TFEB relatively increased) and to further impair SNARE-dependent fusion, giving a self-reinforcing loop in which more transcription yields no additional catabolic flux."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts while the trans-Golgi SNARE/M6PR delivery module is relatively suppressed, creating a hydrolase-delivery bottleneck rather than a synthesis bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0949119373776908, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.05753191128126758, "cosine_similarity": 0.1817664538132222, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6504692556634304, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0949119373776908, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.05753191128126758, "cosine_similarity": 0.1817664538132222, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6504692556634304, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.65314875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 382}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_143", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression result (every supplied effect has magnitude greater than 1 and 77 percent are positive), not an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement; enrichment is therefore judged against this already up-shifted background, and absence of a gene means it failed selection rather than that it is unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as given; only the sign and the rank ordering within the supplied list are interpreted, not the implied fold-change ratios.", "The apparent global positive shift (and the strongly negative ACTB row) may partly reflect normalisation, ambient RNA or cell-composition differences rather than true transcriptome-wide induction; the hypothesis rests on the contrast between endolysosomal arms within the same list, which is robust to a uniform additive shift.", "Protein spots carry three to six candidate genes each and no spot uniquely identifies a protein; spot changes are used only as weak, direction-ambiguous evidence against a uniform increase in lysosomal protease abundance.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to correlate with, but does not measure, enzyme activity, zymogen maturation, compartment pH, cargo flux or subcellular localisation.", "Microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on microglial transcripts may be partly non-cell-autonomous and partly driven by astrocyte-derived cargo or lipoproteins.", "No lysosomal pH, protease activity, cargo-clearance, imaging, autophagic-flux or lipid measurement is supplied, so the inferred cargo backlog is an unobserved pool.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the very large individual effect magnitudes may be unstable and are not treated as quantitative."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia selectively amplify the luminal catabolic arm of the endolysosomal system (acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts, with TFEB itself elevated) without co-scaling the cargo-delivery/fusion arm (M6PR, STX17, HOPS/adaptor components) or the luminal-export arm (NPC2, OSBPL8, CLN3). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step for endolysosomal cargo processing in APOE4 is therefore the handoff into and out of the acidified lumen rather than hydrolase abundance, so that expanded enzymatic capacity does not translate into faster cargo clearance, and the resulting persistent luminal cargo load sustains the CLEAR-type transcriptional response. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; degradative flux, compartment pH, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Cargo pulse-chase discriminator: loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a quenched degradation reporter (DQ-BSA) plus pHrodo-labelled myelin or apoptotic-cell cargo should show equal or greater initial internalisation and equal or greater per-lysosome hydrolase content in APOE4, but slower fractional clearance of internalised cargo between 4 and 24 hours and more undegraded cargo per LAMP1-positive compartment. If APOE4 clears cargo as fast as or faster than APOE3 with no increase in undegraded cargo, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Primary discriminating perturbation (handoff versus capacity): compare restoring the handoff arm (re-expression of STX17, or of M6PR/CD-MPR, or ARL8B/HOPS-driven fusion enhancement) against further expanding capacity (TFEB overexpression) in APOE4 microglia. The mechanism predicts that handoff restoration improves cargo clearance and lowers CLEAR-target transcripts, whereas TFEB overexpression raises hydrolase transcripts further without improving clearance. If TFEB overexpression alone normalises clearance while STX17/M6PR restoration does not, the bottleneck is hydrolytic capacity and this mechanism is weakened.", "Inhibitor-sensitivity test: graded pan-cathepsin or v-ATPase (bafilomycin A1) inhibition should cause a smaller incremental increase in undegraded cargo in APOE4 than in APOE3, because APOE4 clearance is already limited at a step other than hydrolysis. Greater APOE4 sensitivity to cathepsin inhibition would indicate that hydrolase capacity is limiting and would weaken the mechanism.", "Repertoire-shift test: substrate-specific fluorogenic assays should show reduced cathepsin-S-preferred cleavage in APOE4 despite increased cathepsin B/D-preferred cleavage, and reduced CTSS protein by targeted immunoblot. If cathepsin-S-type activity rises in parallel with cathepsin B/D activity, mechanism step 5 is falsified.", "Feed-forward test: reducing cargo influx (SR-B1/CD36 blockade, cytochalasin D, or cargo-free medium) should lower TFEB-target hydrolase transcripts in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels if the CLEAR response is demand-driven. If CLEAR transcripts remain elevated after cargo load is removed, the response is constitutive and mechanism step 6 is falsified.", "Specificity control: the arm-versus-arm contrast should persist after quantile or spike-in-anchored renormalisation of the RNA data and after restricting to genes with matched expression level. If the contrast disappears under renormalisation, the signal is a global-shift artefact and the hypothesis is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_143", "mechanism_steps": ["Capacity arm (measured as RNA abundance): APOE4 microglia show coordinated elevation of luminal acid hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, MAN2B1, AGA, GLA, DNASE2, SUMF1) and of v-ATPase subunit transcripts (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1E1/F, ATP6V0D1, ATP6AP1), together with elevated TFEB transcript. This is a transcript-level capacity signal; enzyme activity, protein maturation and lumen acidification were not measured.", "Handoff arm (measured as RNA abundance) is not co-scaled: the CD-MPR hydrolase-sorting receptor M6PR and the autophagosome-lysosome fusion SNARE STX17 are among the lower-ranked transcripts of the whole differential list, LAPTM5 and IDS are reduced, and most HOPS/SNARE/AP-1 components did not reach the differential-expression selection threshold. Within the endolysosomal genes present, catabolic+acidification transcripts are shifted higher than delivery+export transcripts.", "Export arm (measured as RNA abundance) is flat relative to the capacity arm: NPC2 and OSBPL8/CLN3 sit at or below the median of the selected list and NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1 did not pass selection, so catabolite and sterol efflux transcripts do not track the hydrolase increase.", "Inferred consequence (not measured): with more enzyme per compartment but unchanged handoff, cargo residence time rises and partially digested cargo accumulates per endolysosome; degradative flux per unit cargo is limited by delivery and emptying, not by hydrolysis.", "Inferred repertoire shift, not uniform expansion: the microglia-dominant protease transcript CTSS is strongly reduced while CTSB, CTSD and CTSK are increased, which we infer changes which substrates are efficiently cleaved even if bulk protease abundance rises. Protein spots whose candidate lists include CTSD/CTSB/CTSL change in both directions, which is consistent with proteoform redistribution but cannot identify a specific protein.", "Inferred feed-forward loop: persistent luminal cargo load maintains TFEB-type transcriptional output (elevated TFEB, MITF, RRAGD, LAMTOR5 transcripts), expanding capacity further without relieving the handoff bottleneck. Direction of this loop is not established by these data."], "title": "Arm-uncoupled endolysosome in APOE4 microglia: luminal hydrolase/acidification capacity is transcriptionally amplified while cargo handoff (delivery-fusion and luminal export) is not, making handoff the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10567514677103718, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.03920336114740805, "cosine_similarity": 0.17968368747828356, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_143", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268802588996764, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10567514677103718, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.03920336114740805, "cosine_similarity": 0.17968368747828356, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6268802588996764, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7252055, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 383}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_116", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05; 1705 of 2212 effects are positive; median +1.46), so enrichment is judged against the list median rather than against zero, and absence of a gene from the list cannot be read as 'unchanged'.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are used only as ranks within the list, never as literal fold-changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for hydrolase, v-ATPase and mitochondrial-carrier protein capacity; enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, membrane localisation and metabolic flux were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a measurement of a named protein, and the spot layer does not corroborate the RNA layer (Spearman rho = -0.06, n = 71 spots with an RNA-measured candidate).", "No lipid, cholesterol, filipin, lysosomal-pH or flux measurement is supplied despite the experiment identifier; lysosomal lipid retention is an inference and is not reported here as an observed pool.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex, so some transcript differences could reflect cell-composition or ambient-RNA differences rather than cell-intrinsic APOE4 effects.", "Correlational genotype comparison at a single timepoint (Day 30, mock); no causal ordering among steps 1-5 is established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated, non-inflammatory lipid-handling program: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake (SCARB1), endolysosomal hydrolysis and acidification (GBA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSK, GAA, HEXA, NAGLU, ATP6V1A) and mitochondrial anaplerotic/TCA carriers (MPC2, MDH1, GOT1, OGDH, SLC25A1) are among the strongest increases in the differential-expression list, whereas the post-hydrolysis lipid egress/re-esterification arm (NPC2, SOAT1, APOE) sits at or below the list median. We hypothesise that sterol/lipid export out of the endolysosomal lumen is the primary bottleneck in APOE4, and that the elevated hydrolase, v-ATPase and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts are a compensatory response to retained luminal lipid rather than evidence of restored clearance. The assigned interferon/inflammation focus is rejected: no canonical interferon-stimulated gene appears among 2212 significant rows and the inflammatory/interferon gene set is not enriched relative to the list median (Mann-Whitney p(greater)=0.95). Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: bypassing the proposed egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC2 protein supplementation / NPC1 overexpression), without touching uptake, should (a) reduce lysosomal unesterified sterol and neutral-lipid load (filipin/LipidSpot, lysosome-colocalised) and (b) bring the hydrolase/v-ATPase/TFEB transcript signature (GAA, GBA, CTSB, CTSK, HEXA, ATP6V1A, TFEB) back toward APOE3 levels. WEAKENS: if cyclodextrin clears lysosomal sterol but the hydrolase/TFEB signature remains APOE4-high, the compensatory logic of steps 3-4 is wrong and the hydrolase program is egress-independent.", "Reducing uptake (SCARB1 knockdown or BLT-1) in APOE4 should lower lysosomal lipid load and blunt the hydrolase/TFEB signature. WEAKENS: unchanged lipid load and unchanged hydrolase transcripts after effective SCARB1 loss would falsify step 1 as the source of the lipid flux.", "TFEB knockdown/knockout in APOE4 should selectively collapse the hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation while leaving SCARB1 elevated. WEAKENS: persistence of the hydrolase program after TFEB loss points to a different (e.g. post-transcriptional or STAT/MITF-independent) driver of step 4.", "13C-glucose/glutamine tracing plus respirometry should show, in APOE4 versus APOE3, greater UK5099-sensitive (MPC-dependent) pyruvate entry and greater citrate-derived lipogenic labelling, but no greater etomoxir-sensitive respiration. WEAKENS: if the APOE4 respiratory increase is etomoxir-sensitive and MPC-dependent flux is unchanged, step 5 is misassigned and the phenotype is beta-oxidation driven.", "NEGATIVE PREDICTION (tests the rejected focus): unstimulated APOE4 microglia should show no elevation of ISG protein or transcript (ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, STAT1 phosphorylation) and no elevated IL1B/TNF/CXCL10 secretion versus APOE3. WEAKENS/REVERSES: a reproducible spontaneous interferon signature or cytokine release in mock APOE4 would falsify step 6 and reinstate an interferon-driven mechanism.", "Immunoblot of cathepsin D and B should show redistribution between pro- and mature forms in APOE4 (consistent with the split direction of cathepsin-candidate spots protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up versus protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069 down) with total protein unchanged or increased. WEAKENS: a net decrease in total cathepsin D/B protein despite elevated transcripts would contradict the inferred increase in hydrolytic capacity in step 2.", "Live-cell lysosomal pH and DQ-BSA/BODIPY-cholesterol pulse-chase should show APOE4 lysosomes acidified at least as well as APOE3 but with slower sterol egress to ER (reduced ER cholesteryl-ester formation per unit uptake). WEAKENS: normal egress kinetics with impaired acidification would relocate the bottleneck to acidification/hydrolysis rather than export."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_116", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show the largest increases in lipid/lipoprotein uptake transcripts, with SCARB1 at the 99th percentile of the differential-expression list (gene:SCARB1, +8.22 in the reported, unspecified-base log unit) and CD36 modestly up; we infer, but did not measure, a higher rate of lipid delivery to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): Endolysosomal hydrolase and acidification transcripts rise coherently (gene:GAA 99.7th, gene:CTSK 98.7th, gene:GBA 97.9th, gene:NAGLU 96.2nd, gene:HEXA 95.6th, gene:SMPD1 95.4th, gene:CTSB 94.9th, gene:ATP6V1A 89.2nd percentile; set median 2.24 vs list median 1.46, Mann-Whitney p=7e-4), consistent with increased hydrolytic and proton-pumping capacity; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH and localisation were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): The export arm does not scale with steps 1-2. NPC2, the only measured luminal sterol-transfer gene, is at the 35th percentile (gene:NPC2), below the list median, and downstream cytosolic disposal genes are near-median (gene:SOAT1 39th, gene:DGAT1 57th, gene:APOE 38th). NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from the supplied rows. We therefore place the rate-limiting step at transfer of hydrolysis-derived sterol/lipid out of the lysosomal lumen, producing luminal lipid retention that is inferred, not observed.", "Step 4 (inferred causal direction, not established): Retained luminal lipid and the resulting lysosomal stress sustain a TFEB/MITF-type biogenesis response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03), so the hydrolase and v-ATPase elevation in step 2 is read as a compensatory output of the bottleneck rather than as evidence that clearance is restored.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): Mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate handling and TCA transcripts increase strongly (gene:MPC2 99th, gene:MDH1 99th, gene:OGDH 99th, gene:GOT1 97th, gene:DLD 95th, gene:SLC25A1 91st, gene:SLC25A46 99.5th; set median 3.54 vs 1.46, p=4e-5), while fatty-acid oxidation genes lag (gene:ACOX1 39th percentile, gene:HADHA 76th; CPT1A not measured) and gene:SCD is at the 89th percentile. We infer a glucose/glutamine-fed, citrate-exporting and lipid-storing state rather than increased beta-oxidation of the internalised lipid.", "Step 6 (negative arm, measured): This remodelling is not accompanied by interferon or NF-kB activation. No ISG15/MX1/MX2/IFIT/OAS/STAT1/STAT2/IRF7 row is present among 2212 significant genes; the only pathway-adjacent rows are near the list median (gene:IRF8 47th, gene:IFNAR1 48th, gene:TMEM173 37th percentile), and immune-activation genes gene:CSF1, gene:CTSS and gene:SEMA4A are in the bottom 1%. The phenotype is therefore classified as a lipid-clearance state, not an inflammatory or interferon state."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid egress, not uptake or hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia: a TFEB-type hydrolase/v-ATPase and TCA-anaplerosis compensation without interferon or NF-kB activation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24620610715208802, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05765187857822596, "cosine_similarity": 0.17717052358041194, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_116", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6417831715210356, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24620610715208802, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05765187857822596, "cosine_similarity": 0.17717052358041194, "direction_accuracy": 0.22168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6417831715210356, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.667042, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 384}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_117", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are relative to the supplied 2212-row background (median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base), not to a whole-transcriptome null.", "The relative decrease in the six mtDNA-encoded rows reflects a genuine reduction in mitochondrial transcript content per cell rather than the well-known scRNA-seq mitochondrial-fraction artefact (ambient RNA, dissociation stress, normalisation to a globally up-shifted library).", "Transcript abundance of nuclear OXPHOS, import and assembly genes is at least partially predictive of the corresponding protein import and assembly capacity; no mitochondrial protein pool, membrane potential, respiration rate or ROS level was measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:077 is treated only as weakly consistent with PRDX2, not as a PRDX2 measurement.", "Astrocyte co-culture, cell-composition differences between APOE4 and APOE3 wells, and clone-specific effects are not controlled in the supplied data and could generate the same relative pattern.", "The lysosomal and redox programs are read as downstream/compensatory; an alternative ordering in which a primary lysosomal or redox lesion drives the mitochondrial signature is not excluded by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia run an upregulated nuclear mitochondrial-biogenesis program (nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits, TOM/TIM import machinery, mitochondrial translation-elongation factors and assembly factors) while transcripts for mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits are relatively reduced. We hypothesise that the mtDNA-encoded subunit pool, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting input for holo-complex I/III/IV/V assembly, producing a low assembly efficiency per imported subunit, a chronic thiol/peroxide-defence response, and a compensatory TFEB-associated lysosomal-autophagic transcriptional program. Causality is not established by these data; the mtDNA-side measurement rests on only six mitochondrial transcripts and is technically vulnerable.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Complex-selective respirometry in permeabilised isogenic microglia: APOE4 should show reduced complex I- (pyruvate/malate) and complex IV- (TMPD/ascorbate) driven oxygen consumption per mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOMM20), while complex II- (succinate + rotenone) driven respiration is preserved or increased, because complex II is entirely nuclear-encoded. If complex II respiration per mitochondrial mass falls in proportion to complex I and IV, the mitonuclear-stoichiometry bottleneck is weakened in favour of a generalised mitochondrial-mass or membrane-potential defect.", "Blue-native PAGE plus immunoblot: APOE4 should show a reduced ratio of mt-encoded protein (MT-CO1, MT-CO2, MT-ND1) to nuclear-encoded protein (NDUFB8, NDUFS4, UQCRC2, SDHB) and accumulation of complex I/IV subassemblies relative to holoenzyme. If the mt-encoded:nuclear-encoded protein ratio and holoenzyme:subassembly ratio are indistinguishable from APOE3, the core claim is falsified even if the transcript pattern replicates.", "Discriminating perturbation: sub-lethal mitoribosome inhibition (doxycycline or chloramphenicol, 48-72 h) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature - induce nuclear OXPHOS, TOMM/TIMM, PRDX/GPX4 and TFEB/v-ATPase/hydrolase transcripts while lowering mt-encoded transcripts; conversely, raising mtDNA transcription capacity in APOE4 (TFAM overexpression, or mitochondrially targeted transcription rescue) should collapse the nuclear OXPHOS overshoot and the lysosomal program toward APOE3 levels. If mitoribosome inhibition in APOE3 fails to induce the nuclear OXPHOS and lysosomal signature, the proposed causal ordering is weakened.", "Technical discriminator: single-molecule FISH or a targeted assay for MT-CYB and MT-ATP6, plus mtDNA copy number by qPCR, in intact APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia. The mt-encoded reduction should persist after ambient-RNA correction and independent of dissociation. If the mt-transcript decrease disappears under ambient-RNA-corrected or fixation-based measurement, the bottleneck as stated is not supported.", "Negative prediction from the rejected lipid focus: unbiased lipidomics on the same cultures should NOT show a coherent APOE4 shift in glycerophospholipid acyl-chain saturation or triacylglycerol content that is proportionate to the isolated AGPAT2, SCD and SREBF1 transcript increases; a large, coherent acyl-chain remodelling shift would argue that a glycerolipid mechanism, not mitonuclear stoichiometry, is primary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_117", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated relative increase in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS structural subunits (38 rows, median +2.64 vs global median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=1.0e-4; all 21 NDUF rows positive), in mitochondrial protein-import and mitochondrial-translation components (TOMM22, TIMM44, TIMM8B, TUFM, GFM2, CHCHD3), and in assembly factors (NDUFAF4, COA1, COA8, ANTKMT). INFERRED: an upregulated nuclear arm of mitochondrial biogenesis; transcript abundance is not import flux or assembly rate.", "MEASURED (RNA): the mtDNA-encoded transcripts behave oppositely to this nuclear program (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; median -1.56, p=0.065, n=6, with MT-ND4L and MT-ND5 discordantly positive). INFERRED BOTTLENECK: the mt-encoded core catalytic subunit pool (protein level not measured) is the limiting input for assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V.", "INFERRED (not measured): nuclear subunits imported in excess of their mt-encoded partners accumulate as unassembled modules and subassemblies, so holo-complex I/III/IV per imported nuclear subunit falls even though nuclear subunit transcripts rise; complex II, which is entirely nuclear-encoded (SDHB +1.65), is predicted to be spared.", "INFERRED (not measured): electron transfer through incompletely assembled complex I/III increases superoxide and lipid-peroxide load. MEASURED correlate: every thiol/peroxide-defence row scored is above the global median (TXNDC17 +7.10, PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, GPX4 +2.79, FTH1 +2.53, PRDX5 +1.96; 8/8, p=2.5e-3), and one ambiguous protein spot containing PRDX2 among its candidates is up (protein_spot:077, +1.07).", "MEASURED (RNA): a lysosomal-autophagic program rises in parallel (TFEB +2.38, v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1H +6.88 / ATP6V1A +4.23 / ATP6V0C +3.51, hydrolases GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, NAGLU +5.91, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSK +7.36, CTSB +5.52; 28-row lysosome set median +1.99, p=5.8e-3). INFERRED: this is demand-driven compensation for damaged mitochondria and oxidised cargo, i.e. increased degradative capacity transcripts, not demonstrated increased degradative flux.", "NET STATE (inferred): APOE4 microglia occupy a high-biogenesis / low-assembly-efficiency mitochondrial state \u2014 a mitonuclear stoichiometry deficit rather than a global loss of mitochondrial gene expression \u2014 which is what distinguishes them from isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock treatment."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry deficit: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits OXPHOS assembly in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.050880626223091974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03076484021079697, "cosine_similarity": 0.17507198832382448, "direction_accuracy": 0.08576051779935275, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_117", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6305275080906149, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.050880626223091974, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03076484021079697, "cosine_similarity": 0.17507198832382448, "direction_accuracy": 0.08576051779935275, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6305275080906149, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.52926175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 385}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_167", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; module comparisons are therefore made against the internal background of that list (median effect approximately +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base, 77 percent positive), and absence of a gene (for example LIPA, PLIN2, ABCA1, FASN, LPCAT3) carries no information.", "The unspecified logarithm base and the very large reported effects (up to about +15.5) are taken at face value only as ranks/directions; no fold-change arithmetic is assumed.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least monotonically related to the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal and lipid-metabolic proteins in these cells; no enzyme activity, lipid species, organelle volume or flux was measured here.", "The coordinated lysosomal transcript module is assumed to reflect a MiT/TFE-type biogenesis response to lysosomal demand rather than an unrelated batch/composition effect of the strong global positive shift.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-uniquely identified: spots containing cathepsin candidates are treated as weak, non-assignable corroboration only, and keratin/actin-dominated spots are treated as uninformative.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to supply lipid/lipoprotein substrate similarly to both genotypes, so the genotype contrast is not simply a difference in extracellular substrate availability.", "The mock-treated day-30 state is assumed to be a steady state, so that transcript differences reflect a chronic set-point rather than a transient response."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally by an unusually coherent up-shift of lysosomal acidification and acid-hydrolase transcripts (the only module in these data that rises significantly above the strong global positive shift of this selected DE list). We propose this transcriptional program reports a rate-limiting step at lysosomal hydrolysis/clearance of internalized and autophagy-derived membrane lipid; the fatty acids and lysolipids that escape complete catabolism are inferred to be re-routed into monounsaturated, PUFA-poor glycerolipid via elevated SCD/SREBF1, LPCAT1/MBOAT1/MBOAT2 and AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1 transcripts, while ACSL4 and ACSL5 transcripts fall. Membrane acyl-chain remodeling is therefore proposed as a downstream consequence, not the primary bottleneck, because that gene set is not enriched relative to the global shift. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity, lipid composition, organelle load and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux test: pulse-chase APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with traceable membrane substrate (isotope- or fluorophore-labelled myelin, apoptotic-neuron membranes, or BODIPY-sphingomyelin). The mechanism predicts a genotype difference in clearance half-life with substrate retention in the LAMP1/TMEM192-positive compartment in APOE4 despite equal or greater initial internalization. If APOE4 clears the labelled substrate as fast as or faster than APOE3 with no increase in retained undegraded lipid, the lysosomal-bottleneck claim fails and the transcript module should instead be read as increased successful catabolic throughput.", "Capacity-stress test: sub-lethal v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or glucocerebrosidase inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) should produce a significant genotype x drug interaction, with APOE4 showing disproportionately greater LysoTracker/BODIPY-positive area, greater glucosylceramide and ceramide accumulation, and greater loss of subsequent phagocytic clearance. Equal effects in both genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "Compositional test: untargeted lipidomics on mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show (a) higher glucosylceramide/ceramide and cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol, and (b) a higher monounsaturated-to-polyunsaturated ratio with reduced 20:4-containing phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine. Finding no acyl-saturation shift would refute the downstream remodeling arm while leaving the lysosomal bottleneck testable; finding neither the sphingolipid nor the neutral-lipid increase would refute the hypothesis as a whole.", "Node-specific test: SCD inhibition (for example A939572) should be more toxic in APOE4 than APOE3, raising free fatty acid and lysophospholipid pools and ER-stress markers, and oleate supplementation should rescue that genotype-selective toxicity. Identical SCD-inhibitor sensitivity in the two genotypes would show that the esterification arm is not carrying an APOE4-specific load.", "Directionality test: TFEB knockdown should lower the lysosomal transcript module in both genotypes but worsen lipid and substrate accumulation preferentially in APOE4 (compensatory program). If TFEB knockdown instead normalizes APOE4 lipid accumulation, the program is driving rather than compensating and this mechanism's causal ordering is wrong.", "Specificity test: an APOE4-to-APOE3 isogenic gene correction, or APOE knockout in both backgrounds, should collapse the lysosomal-module difference; persistence of the module difference after removing APOE would indicate the phenotype is not APOE-genotype-driven in these cultures."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_167", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipid- and debris-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:APOE) and for endolysosomal delivery/maturation components (gene:RAB7A, gene:PIK3C3, gene:ATG9A). Inferred: the flux of membrane-derived lipid substrate reaching the lysosome per cell is increased or at least sustained; uptake rate itself was not measured, and reduced actomyosin transcripts (gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9) are counter-evidence to an uptake increase.", "Measured: a coherent, module-level up-shift of lysosomal acidification and acid-hydrolase transcripts (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:TMEM192, gene:SLC38A7, gene:NPC2) together with gene:TFEB. Inferred: a MiT/TFE-type biogenesis response that is compensatory, i.e. it is elicited by, and does not by itself relieve, an unmet demand for lysosomal lipid catabolism.", "Proposed primary bottleneck (inferred, not measured): the per-lysosome hydrolytic and product-egress capacity for sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid and phospholipid substrate is rate-limiting in APOE4, so substrate residence time and undegraded lipid content of the endolysosomal compartment rise despite the higher hydrolase transcript levels.", "Measured: sphingolipid-arm transcripts are raised (gene:SMPD1, gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6) alongside gene:GBA. Inferred: increased ceramide generation from sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide turnover within the acidic compartment, i.e. a shift of the sphingolipid pool toward ceramide and its salvage re-acylation, which is a candidate stressor of lysosomal membrane integrity.", "Measured: lipogenic and esterification transcripts rise (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:MGLL, gene:FABP5) while long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5) and gene:GPAT3 falls. Inferred: fatty acids released by lysosomal hydrolysis, plus de novo Delta-9 desaturation, are esterified preferentially as monounsaturated species into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester stores and phosphatidylcholine, with reduced re-activation of polyunsaturated fatty acids.", "Measured: Lands-cycle reacylation transcripts rise (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2) with only a modest gene:PLA2G7 change. Inferred: lysophospholipids generated during membrane turnover are reacylated with the MUFA-biased acyl-CoA pool, yielding phospholipids that are relatively saturated/monounsaturated and arachidonate-poor; raised gene:GPX4 with lowered gene:ACSL4 is consistent with a peroxidation-resistant, PUFA-poor membrane rather than a ferroptosis-primed one.", "Integrated consequence (inferred): APOE4 microglia occupy a storage-and-sequestration state - enlarged acidic compartment, neutral-lipid accumulation, stiffer MUFA/saturated membranes - in which further lipid or debris challenge is handled poorly, because the lysosomal step, not the esterification step, sets the ceiling."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lysosome-limited lipid catabolic state: a TFEB/v-ATPase-hydrolase transcriptional program marks a lysosomal degradation bottleneck whose spillover is re-esterified through an SCD/LPCAT1/AGPAT2-biased, PUFA-poor acyl-remodeling route"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19223313517704832, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08815000521022102, "cosine_similarity": 0.17497248829052142, "direction_accuracy": 0.2993527508090615, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_167", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7151650485436893, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19223313517704832, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08815000521022102, "cosine_similarity": 0.17497248829052142, "direction_accuracy": 0.2993527508090615, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7151650485436893, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.883423, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 386}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_084", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) with a strong global positive skew (77.1% positive, median +1.46), so only rank/permutation comparisons within the list are interpretable; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and magnitudes are treated as ordinal only.", "Absence of a gene from the list (e.g. GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, PDHA1, HK1, G6PD, MDH2, GOT2, CS) means it was not among the selected results, not that it is unchanged; whole-pathway statements about glycolysis are therefore capacity statements about the measured isoforms only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, for MPC2/PDP1/OGDH/MDH1, to track transport and catalytic capacity; enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, mitochondrial localisation, metabolite pools and flux were not measured.", "Protein spots each carry up to five candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as primary evidence here. The largest spot changes (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046) list both TALDO1 and ANXA1 among candidates, and gene:ANXA1 (+4.15) versus gene:TALDO1 (-2.32) makes ANXA1 the more parsimonious source, so these spots are not treated as pentose-phosphate evidence.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a measured difference may be partly non-cell-autonomous (e.g. altered astrocytic lactate or glutamine supply) rather than intrinsic to APOE4 microglia.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at a single timepoint under mock treatment with replicate number not supplied; correlation with genotype is assumed, causality is not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 by a coherent transcriptional re-partitioning of carbon: transcripts for the inducible, high-flux glycolytic isoenzymes (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2) and for oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate steps (PGD, TALDO1) are lower, while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import and PDH activation (MPC2, PDP1, DLD), TCA enzymes (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, IDH3B, SDHB, MDH1, GOT1, ME1), mitochondrial metabolite carriers (SLC25A1 citrate, SLC25A11 oxoglutarate/malate-aspartate, SLC25A5, SLC25A46), nuclear-encoded ETC subunits, amino-acid anaplerosis (GLUD1, BCAT2, GLS, SLC38A7, SLC38A2) and lysosomal/glycogen carbohydrate handling (GAA, GYS1, UGP2) are higher. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is reduced cytosolic glycolytic commitment capacity at the hexokinase/phosphofructokinase step, which forces resting APOE4 microglia into an oxidation-committed, mitochondria-dependent state with diminished capacity to mount a rapid glycolytic and PPP-NADPH burst. Causality is not established by these data; the transcript changes index capacity, not measured flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or MPC1/MPC2 knockdown should reduce basal and maximal oxygen consumption and basal ATP more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, and should trigger a larger compensatory extracellular acidification rise in APOE3 than in APOE4; conversely 2-deoxyglucose or PFKP/HK2 knockdown should reduce ATP and stimulated cytokine output more in APOE3 than in APOE4. If UK5099 and 2-DG affect the two genotypes equally, or if the genotype ordering is reversed, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Seahorse phenotype: resting APOE4 microglia should show a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio and a smaller glycolytic reserve (post-oligomycin ECAR minus basal ECAR) than APOE3. Equal or larger glycolytic reserve in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing: APOE4 should show lower fractional 13C enrichment of lactate and of PPP-specific products (ribose-5-phosphate, sedoheptulose-7-phosphate, and the m+1/m+2 ratio reporting oxidative PPP) but equal or higher 13C enrichment of citrate and malate per unit glucose consumed; parallel U-13C5-glutamine tracing should show a greater glutamine contribution to TCA intermediates in APOE4. Equal PPP labelling with equal TCA labelling would falsify steps 2 and 5.", "Redox readout: resting APOE4 microglia should have a lower NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratio and greater sensitivity to an acute oxidant or NADPH-consuming challenge; unchanged NADPH/NADP+ would weaken step 2 while leaving steps 3-4 intact.", "Proteomic/biochemical confirmation of the inferred step: MPC2 protein and dephosphorylated (Ser293) PDHA1 should be increased in APOE4 mitochondria, and immunocaptured PDH and OGDH specific activities should be higher. Unchanged MPC2 protein or unchanged/increased PDHA1 Ser293 phosphorylation in APOE4 would directly contradict step 3.", "Glycogen prediction: APOE4 microglia should contain more glycogen at rest and lose more viability or ATP on GYS1 knockdown or acid-glycogenolysis (GAA) inhibition than APOE3. Equal glycogen content would weaken step 2 without affecting steps 3-5.", "Functional consequence: on LPS or fibrillar-amyloid challenge APOE4 microglia should show a blunted early glycolytic switch (smaller ECAR rise in the first 60-90 min) with preserved or increased OCR relative to APOE3. A normal or exaggerated glycolytic switch in APOE4 would weaken the whole hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry lower transcript levels of the inducible high-flux glycolytic isoenzymes HK2 and PFKP and of the PFK2 isoform PFKFB2, while glucose transporter transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3) are higher; we infer, but did not measure, that glucose is taken up but committed to glycolysis at a lower maximal rate per cell.", "Step 2 (inferred partitioning): with reduced commitment at the HK/PFK step, glucose-6-phosphate carbon is inferred to be diverted away from the oxidative and non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (lower PGD and TALDO1 transcripts) and toward glycogen synthesis and lysosomal glycogen turnover (higher GYS1, UGP2 and strongly higher lysosomal alpha-glucosidase GAA), which buffers glucose carbon in a slower cycle rather than releasing it as cytosolic pyruvate.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): the pyruvate that is formed is preferentially routed into mitochondria - the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier subunit MPC2, the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1 and the E3 subunit DLD are all higher, from which we infer increased carrier-mediated pyruvate import and a more dephosphorylated (active) pyruvate dehydrogenase; PDH phosphorylation itself was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): TCA-cycle and shuttle capacity is coordinately raised (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, IDH3B, SDHB, MDH1, GOT1, ME1) together with the citrate carrier SLC25A1 and the oxoglutarate carrier SLC25A11, the cytosolic arms of the malate-aspartate shuttle (MDH1, GOT1) and the adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5, consistent with increased mitochondrial NADH supply and increased cytosol-mitochondrion redox and citrate exchange.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred substrate use): non-glucose anaplerotic inputs are also raised (GLUD1, GLS, BCAT2, and the amino-acid transporters SLC38A7 and SLC38A2), so TCA carbon in APOE4 is inferred to derive proportionally more from glutamate/glutamine and branched-chain amino acids and less from glycolytic pyruvate than in APOE3.", "Step 6 (predicted physiological state): the net resting phenotype is a higher oxidative-to-glycolytic ATP ratio with a small glycolytic reserve and a smaller PPP-derived NADPH pool, so APOE4 microglia should be disproportionately dependent on mitochondrial pyruvate/amino-acid oxidation for basal ATP and disproportionately impaired when a fast glycolytic or NADPH-consuming response is demanded. No ATP, NADPH, oxygen-consumption or metabolite measurement is present in these data."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift the glucose-6-phosphate branch point away from high-flux glycolysis/PPP toward mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation and anaplerosis, leaving low glycolytic and NADPH reserve at rest"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.030332681017612523, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05389022676891595, "cosine_similarity": 0.17003361740591127, "direction_accuracy": 0.05177993527508091, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_084", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6353624595469256, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.030332681017612523, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05389022676891595, "cosine_similarity": 0.17003361740591127, "direction_accuracy": 0.05177993527508091, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6353624595469256, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7894225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 387}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_057", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore comparisons of one selected set against the rest of the same selected list, and absence of a gene means not supplied rather than unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; all RNA effect comparisons are made on that unspecified common scale and only relative to the global median of the same list.", "The pronounced global positive RNA shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46) may partly reflect normalization, ambient-RNA or cell-composition differences rather than true global induction; the mechanism relies only on effects that exceed this shift.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with delay, the abundance of the corresponding ETC, v-ATPase and hydrolase protein complexes; no ETC or TCA protein was measured here.", "v-ATPase proton pumping is assumed to be a quantitatively important ATP sink in these microglia; this is background knowledge and is unverified in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot-level effects are treated as ambiguous and are not used to support the claim.", "Cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects on microglial RNA may be partly non-cell-autonomous.", "Lipid pools, lysosomal pH, ATP, oxygen consumption, autophagic and phagocytic flux, and cargo load were not measured in this experiment."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated, above-background up-shift of the nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation/TCA transcriptional program together with the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal acidification and hydrolase program, while glycolytic committed-step transcripts are not co-elevated. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting bottleneck differentiating the genotypes is the supply of mitochondrially derived ATP to v-ATPase-dependent lysosomal acidification, so that APOE4 degradative flux becomes disproportionately dependent on oxidative phosphorylation. Anabolic glycerolipid/acyl-chain remodelling is explicitly NOT supported as the primary axis in these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: at matched sub-lethal doses, acute ATP-synthase inhibition (oligomycin) will raise lysosomal pH and reduce degradative flux (LysoSensor/LysoTracker ratio; DQ-BSA dequenching rate) substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, while acute glycolytic inhibition (2-deoxyglucose) will produce a smaller relative deficit in APOE4 than in APOE3. If oligomycin sensitivity of lysosomal pH is equal or greater in APOE3, or if 2-DG sensitivity is equal or greater in APOE4, the oxidative-ATP-dependence mechanism is falsified.", "The bafilomycin-A1-sensitive fraction of basal oxygen consumption rate (Seahorse, acute v-ATPase block) will be a larger share of basal OCR in APOE4 than in APOE3. No genotype difference in the bafilomycin-sensitive OCR fraction would weaken the proposed coupling between the two up-shifted programs.", "TFEB knockdown or MiT/TFE-family inhibition will lower v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts in APOE4 towards APOE3 levels but will NOT normalise ETC/TCA transcripts if the mitochondrial arm is driven by demand rather than by shared transcriptional co-regulation. Coordinate loss of both modules after TFEB knockdown would instead indicate a single transcriptional driver and would require replacing the demand-coupling step.", "Quantitative proteomics or immunoblot of ETC subunits (e.g. NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1A) and of ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C will show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 at the protein level. Unchanged or reduced ETC and v-ATPase protein despite the transcript up-shift would remove the capacity step and weaken the mechanism; note the two ATP6V1E1-containing 2D spots here trend downward, so this test is genuinely at risk.", "Lipidomics will NOT show a coherent APOE4 increase in de novo glycerolipid synthesis or a systematic phospholipid acyl-chain desaturation shift proportional to the SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1 transcript effects; a strong, coherent glycerolipid-remodelling phenotype would indicate the assigned membrane-turnover mechanism was wrongly rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA, selected DE list): APOE4 microglia carry a coherent elevation of nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain and TCA/pyruvate-import transcripts relative to the strong global positive RNA shift (39/39 ETC-family rows above zero; set median +2.64 versus global median +1.46; permutation p=0.0013; Mann-Whitney p=2.9e-5).", "INFERRED (capacity, not flux): this transcript pattern reflects increased biogenesis/capacity of the oxidative ATP-generating machinery. Respiratory rate, ATP concentration and coupling efficiency were not measured and are not claimed as observed.", "MEASURED (RNA): in parallel, the TFEB/CLEAR lysosomal module is elevated above the same global background - the transcription factor TFEB itself, multiple v-ATPase V0/V1 subunits, and luminal hydrolases (glycosidases, sphingomyelinase, cathepsins) - together with late-endosomal/retromer/ESCRT trafficking transcripts.", "INFERRED (localization and demand): the v-ATPase is a major and continuously consuming ATP sink at the endolysosome; an expanded acidified, hydrolase-loaded compartment raises steady-state ATP demand at that membrane. The size of the endolysosomal cargo pool was not measured.", "INFERRED (source switching): because committed glycolytic steps are not co-elevated in APOE4 (HK2 and PFKP are among the strongly negative rows despite the global upward shift), the incremental ATP for acidification is proposed to be drawn from oxidative phosphorylation rather than from glycolysis; elevated PRKAA1 and HIF1A transcripts are consistent with, but do not demonstrate, an energy-demand signal.", "PREDICTED CONSEQUENCE (causal direction not established): APOE4 lysosomal pH maintenance and degradative flux become conditionally fragile - normal at baseline but selectively collapsing when mitochondrial ATP synthesis is acutely blocked - whereas APOE3 can buffer the same block glycolytically.", "SCOPE LIMIT: glycerolipid/acyl-chain genes contain individually large effects (AGPAT2, SCD, SREBF1, LPCAT1) but as a set are indistinguishable from the global shift (median +1.54 vs +1.46; p=0.46) and contain opposing members (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3 down), so membrane remodelling is treated as a permissive or downstream arm, not the bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift lysosomal acidification onto mitochondrial ATP: a coordinated OXPHOS/TCA and v-ATPase-CLEAR transcriptional up-shift creates oxidative-ATP dependence of degradative flux"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03718199608610567, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03783306911373295, "cosine_similarity": 0.16944104424341658, "direction_accuracy": 0.06310679611650485, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6304498381877023, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03718199608610567, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03783306911373295, "cosine_similarity": 0.16944104424341658, "direction_accuracy": 0.06310679611650485, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6304498381877023, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5772305, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 388}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Pathway assignments and the proposed inhibitory role of A20/TNIP1 are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "The lower TNFAIP3/TNIP1 transcripts translate into lower inhibitory capacity. Protein translation, stability, recruitment and activity could break this link; no spot has either gene among its candidates.", "A tonic TLR2 input exists under mock co-culture and the upstream machinery is functional. Its ligand, source and receptor engagement are unmeasured.", "Higher NFKBIB and ANXA1 RNA (gene:NFKBIB, gene:ANXA1) does not fully compensate for the proposed termination deficit. This is an assumption challenged by those observations, not evidence that compensation has failed.", "The genotype-associated pattern persists within comparable microglial states under matched astrocyte exposure. Different maturation, cell-state composition, astrocyte-derived inputs or normalization could instead explain the association.", "RNA effects retain their reported, unspecified logarithm base. The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so their upward skew cannot establish total cellular RNA gain and absent genes cannot establish unchanged expression or pathway suppression.", "Protein-spot abundance cannot be assigned to individual candidate proteins. No signaling kinetics, secretion, molecular pools, metabolic fluxes or additional modality measurements were supplied; the cross-sectional association does not establish causal direction."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 is hypothesized to reduce TNFAIP3/A20\u2013TNIP1-dependent signal-termination capacity relative to APOE3. This primary bottleneck would prolong tonic TLR2\u2013MYD88\u2013NF-\u03baB signaling and increase selected chemokine transcripts. The supplied abundance data motivate this mechanism; causality remains unestablished.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In matched APOE4 and APOE3 cultures, uniquely targeted assays should find lower A20 and/or TNIP1 protein availability consistent with the RNA-based bottleneck. Comparable or higher amounts of both, together with intact inhibitory recruitment and function, would weaken the proposed abundance-to-restraint link.", "After a brief TLR2 agonist pulse titrated to match the initial nuclear RELA response, washout and blockade of further receptor input should reveal slower peak-normalized nuclear RELA decay in APOE4. Identical decay despite a larger initial APOE4 response would favor increased input or sensitivity and weaken defective signal termination.", "Restoring endogenous TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 jointly to independently measured APOE3 protein levels should shorten the APOE4 signaling tail and lower nascent CCL2/CXCL8 transcription under mock conditions and after the pulse. Reciprocal partial depletion in APOE3 should reproduce persistence. Failure of a verified physiological rescue, or an apparent rescue explained by cell loss or general transcriptional suppression, would weaken the bottleneck.", "With verified target engagement and preserved viability, TLR2 blockade or IRAK4 inhibition should attenuate the genotype difference in NF-\u03baB persistence and chemokine transcription more than IFNAR1 blockade. Preferential correction by IFNAR1 blockade would weaken this inflammatory mechanism; failure of TLR2 blockade despite an IRAK4 response would weaken the nominated receptor input.", "The prolonged response and A20\u2013TNIP1 rescue should persist when both genotypes are compared within matched microglial states using the same astrocyte background. A phenotype that instead follows astrocyte-conditioned medium or disappears after state matching would weaken the proposed microglial termination defect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Assumed tonic inputs in mock co-culture engage TLR2\u2013TIRAP\u2013MYD88\u2013IRAK4 signaling. Increased RNA for these components (gene:TLR2, gene:TIRAP, gene:MYD88, gene:IRAK4) is compatible with greater signaling capacity, but receptor occupancy, protein abundance and pathway activity were not measured.", "Decreased TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 RNA (gene:TNFAIP3, gene:TNIP1) is proposed to lower functional A20\u2013TNIP1 restraint. Insufficient termination of receptor-proximal signaling is the single proposed bottleneck; neither inhibitory protein abundance nor complex function was measured.", "Weaker termination is inferred to extend IKK-dependent NF-\u03baB activity and nuclear residence after an input. Increased CHUK RNA (gene:CHUK) is permissive abundance evidence only; kinase activity and NF-\u03baB localization remain unmeasured.", "The prolonged transcriptional response is proposed to increase CCL2 and CXCL1/2/3/8 RNA (gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL1, gene:CXCL2, gene:CXCL3, gene:CXCL8), potentially supported by increased NFKBIZ RNA (gene:NFKBIZ). These measured transcripts do not establish chemokine secretion or inflammatory effector activity."], "title": "Reduced A20\u2013TNIP1 restraint prolongs inflammatory chemokine signaling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10261569599147806, "cosine_similarity": 0.16705633901212036, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6400388349514563, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10261569599147806, "cosine_similarity": 0.16705633901212036, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6400388349514563, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.7752545, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_016", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All gene-to-pathway assignments and molecular interactions used here are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "Lower TNFAIP3/TNIP1 RNA translates into lower effective A20\u2013ABIN1 feedback capacity. This assumption is essential and is unsupported by uniquely identified protein measurements.", "Mock co-culture supplies sufficient tonic TLR2/6 stimulation, and this branch contributes to the RNA differences. No endogenous ligand, signaling flux, or direct APOE4-to-TNFAIP3/TNIP1 regulatory link was measured.", "Higher NFKBIB and ANXA1 RNA (gene:NFKBIB, gene:ANXA1) does not fully compensate for the proposed feedback deficit. Lower RELB and CCL4 RNA (gene:RELB, gene:CCL4) argues against uniform inflammatory activation.", "The genotype contrast reflects a reproducible difference within comparable microglial states rather than differentiation, cell composition, astrocyte-derived cues, or batch alone. Biological replicate counts and sample-level measurements were not supplied.", "The 2,212 RNA observations are selected differential-expression rows with an unspecified logarithm base. Their upward skew is not evidence of increased total cellular RNA; absent rows are not evidence of unchanged or absent expression.", "All 92 protein spots have multiple candidate genes and cannot establish abundance changes in individual candidate proteins. No supplied spot lists the proposed A20\u2013ABIN1 or TLR2/6\u2013MYD88\u2013IRAK4 core components.", "An interferon-driven mechanism is not supported by a coherent response in the supplied rows, but missing selected RNA rows cannot establish interferon suppression. Lysosomal remodeling or broader cell-state changes could cause the inflammatory pattern without an A20\u2013ABIN1 bottleneck."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia may sustain more TLR2/6\u2013MYD88\u2013IRAK4-dependent NF-\u03baB signaling than APOE3 because A20\u2013ABIN1-mediated signal termination is limiting. The proposed primary bottleneck is reduced functional feedback capacity associated with lower TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 RNA, explaining increased CCL2 and CXCL8 transcription. Protein capacity, signaling duration, and causal direction remain unmeasured; this is a testable hypothesis, not established causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In new measurements, APOE4 should have lower A20\u2013ABIN1 protein capacity or impaired termination function and slower decay of nuclear RELA after a brief TLR2/6 agonist pulse and washout. Compare decay at matched early RELA activation to distinguish defective termination from increased input sensitivity. Normal termination despite verified RNA differences would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Restore TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 in APOE4 to physiological APOE3 protein levels, with matched expression controls and a validated feedback-defective control. Functional restoration should preferentially shorten the prolonged late RELA response and narrow the APOE4\u2013APOE3 difference in nascent CCL2/CXCL8 RNA, without requiring normalization of receptor RNA. Failure despite verified functional restoration, or the same rescue by the defective control, would weaken the mechanism.", "Partially repress TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 in APOE3 to reproduce the proposed APOE4 feedback deficit. With viable, matched microglial states and a shared ligand pulse, this should prolong late RELA activity and increase CCL2/CXCL8 transcription. Failure to phenocopy after confirmed loss of feedback capacity would weaken sufficiency.", "Compare acute IRAK4 inhibition with IFNAR1 blockade, verifying target engagement using appropriate control stimulation. IRAK4 inhibition should reduce the genotype difference in late RELA activity and CCL2/CXCL8 transcription more than IFNAR1 blockade. Persistence despite effective IRAK4 inhibition, or preferential elimination by IFNAR1 blockade, would weaken the proposed pathway and favor an alternative driver."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured TLR2, TLR6, CD14, MYD88, and IRAK4 RNA is higher in APOE4 (gene:TLR2, gene:TLR6, gene:CD14, gene:MYD88, gene:IRAK4). We infer that shared mock-culture cues can engage this receptor\u2013adaptor pathway; neither the cues nor receptor abundance, ligand occupancy, or kinase activity was measured.", "Measured TNFAIP3 and TNIP1 RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:TNFAIP3, gene:TNIP1). The central assumption is that these decreases reduce functional A20\u2013ABIN1 feedback capacity, making termination of receptor-proximal ubiquitin signaling the primary bottleneck. A20 and ABIN1 protein abundance and activity are not observed.", "Using unverified background knowledge about A20\u2013ABIN1 feedback, insufficient termination is predicted to prolong IKK-dependent RELA/NF-\u03baB activity after stimulation. Ubiquitin scaffolds, phosphorylation, and nuclear RELA residence are inferred intermediates, not measured molecular pools or activities.", "Longer integrated NF-\u03baB activity is proposed to increase CCL2 and CXCL8 transcription, consistent with their higher measured RNA (gene:CCL2, gene:CXCL8). Increased chemokine secretion or inflammatory effector function has not been demonstrated."], "title": "Reduced A20\u2013ABIN1 feedback prolongs tonic inflammatory signaling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10261569599147806, "cosine_similarity": 0.16705633901212036, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_016", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6400388349514563, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10261569599147806, "cosine_similarity": 0.16705633901212036, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6400388349514563, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.7377865, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_108", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive, median +1.46), so all enrichment statements are made against this shifted, pre-filtered background and not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA log fold changes is unspecified and is left untransformed; only ranks and signs are used for inference, protein spots are log2.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous proteoform-level measurements, never as identified proteins.", "Transcript increases are assumed to be at least partly compensatory (demand-driven) rather than evidence of increased achieved catabolic flux; enzyme activity, lipid species, lysosomal pH and localisation were not measured in this dataset.", "APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context; replicate number is not supplied, so effect precision cannot be judged and single-gene effects are used only as ranks within a coherent set.", "Astrocyte co-culture may contribute non-microglial RNA or protein signal; genotype effects are assumed to act mainly in microglia."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 shifts sphingolipid handling toward endolysosomal turnover rather than synthesis: transcripts for lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, GBA2) and for endolysosomal routing and acidification sit at the extreme upper tail of the differential-expression distribution, while de novo/glycosyl-transfer enzymes sit at background or below (B4GALT5, ST3GAL2 reduced). We hypothesise this transcriptional pattern is a compensatory response to increased lipid substrate delivery into the endolysosome, and that the rate-limiting step is realised luminal hydrolytic capacity (enzyme activity plus activator/deacylation and export arms, largely unmeasured here), so that APOE4 lysosomes carry a larger ceramide/hexosylceramide/sphingomyelin pool at equal or higher hydrolase transcript level. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial pharmacological inhibition of GBA (conduritol B epoxide) or knockdown of SMPD1 in the same isogenic pair should produce a genotype x inhibitor interaction, with APOE4 microglia showing a disproportionately larger rise in lysosomal hexosylceramide/sphingomyelin and a larger fall in degradative capacity (DQ-BSA dequenching) than APOE3, because APOE4 already operates near its hydrolytic reserve. Equal, purely additive effects in both genotypes would weaken the reserve-capacity bottleneck.", "Direct test of the transcript-to-activity gap: 4MU-based GBA and beta-hexosaminidase assays plus acid sphingomyelinase activity in lysosome-enriched fractions should show activity increases that are sub-proportional to the large transcript increases in gene:GBA, gene:HEXA and gene:SMPD1, together with net accumulation of ceramide and monohexosylceramide by lipidomics. Proportional activity increases with unchanged or reduced sphingolipid substrate levels would falsify the bottleneck as stated.", "Substrate-driven causality: lowering glucosylceramide input with a UGCG inhibitor (eliglustat/GENZ-123346) or blocking lipoprotein uptake should reduce the APOE4-specific elevation of hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H) toward APOE3 levels. Persistent hydrolase induction after verified substrate lowering would show the program is not substrate-driven and would break step 2.", "Specificity versus a generic CLEAR program: TFEB knockdown should remove hydrolase induction across substrate classes, but only the sphingolipid arm should show a genotype-selective substrate build-up; if APOE4 lysosomes accumulate glycosaminoglycan or glycogen substrates as strongly as sphingolipids (consistent with gene:NAGLU and gene:GAA being equally elevated), the sphingolipid-specific framing should be replaced by a generic lysosomal capacity mechanism.", "Routing prediction: live imaging should show slower RAB7A-positive late-endosome to lysosome cargo resolution and reduced lipid efflux in APOE4 despite higher gene:RAB7A and gene:VPS26A transcripts; equal or faster cargo resolution in APOE4 would weaken step 1 and step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_108", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid into the endolysosomal system. Measured: elevated transcripts for lipid uptake/handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE) and for endosome-to-lysosome routing (gene:DNM2, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:RAB7A, gene:VAMP3). Inferred, not measured: actual uptake flux, cargo composition and cargo localisation.", "Increased luminal lipid load engages a CLEAR-like lysosomal transcriptional response (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC, v-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C). Inferred: TFEB nuclear translocation and increased lysosomal acidification; only transcript abundance was measured.", "Within that response the sphingolipid-directed hydrolases are top-ranked rather than average: gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA and gene:HEXA fall in the top 5% of all 2212 selected DE rows, with gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GBA2 and gene:SUMF1 (sulfatase maturation) all positive. This is read as demand for sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid catabolism.", "The opposing anabolic/complex-glycosphingolipid arm is not co-induced: gene:B4GALT5 (-1.88) and gene:ST3GAL2 (-1.39) are reduced and gene:KDSR, gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:ORMDL2, gene:CERS4 lie near the global median (+1.46), so intermediates generated by hydrolysis cannot be efficiently re-routed into complex glycosphingolipids and are predicted to stall at the ceramide/monohexosylceramide level.", "Net clearance is therefore limited downstream of the induced enzymes, at the activity level: acid ceramidase, saposins/prosaposin, UGCG, SGMS1/2 and NPC1 are absent from the supplied rows, and the 2D protein spots containing lysosomal hydrolase candidates move in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:052 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:067 down), giving no protein-level confirmation that hydrolase capacity scales with transcript. We infer a transcript-to-activity gap as the bottleneck.", "The resulting endolysosomal sphingolipid retention keeps the TFEB-associated program on (feed-forward) and pushes APOE4 microglia toward a lipid-burdened, storage-like state (gene:GPNMB, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A modestly up) rather than a purely inflammatory one (gene:CCL4 -1.46, gene:CTSS -5.57). Lipid pool size, lysosomal pH and degradative flux were not measured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a substrate-driven, catabolism-biased lysosomal sphingolipid program whose limiting node is luminal ceramide/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis capacity, not sphingolipid synthesis"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1172414429716058, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.10976419279511014, "cosine_similarity": 0.16497039033389285, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_108", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6763624595469256, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1172414429716058, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.10976419279511014, "cosine_similarity": 0.16497039033389285, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6763624595469256, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.555397, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 389}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Background knowledge is unverified here: MTERF4 participates in mitochondrial large-ribosomal-subunit maturation; respiratory complexes require coordinated nuclear and mitochondrial subunit production; DELE1 can connect mitochondrial stress to integrated stress signaling. No literature or database retrieval was performed.", "Lower MTERF4 RNA must produce a functionally limiting reduction in correctly localized protein. The data do not establish this; it is the weakest necessary link and the principal perturbation target.", "The mitochondrial transcript pattern is mixed: gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 increase, and gene:TUFM and several other mitochondrial translation-related RNAs increase. The mechanism requires a maturation limitation despite those changes, not uniform suppression of mitochondrial transcription.", "RNA effects retain their unspecified logarithm base and describe selected differential-expression rows. Their 77.1% positive fraction is not evidence of an absolute whole-transcriptome increase; absent genes cannot be treated as unchanged or absent from cells.", "Differences must persist after accounting for viable microglial cell number, mitochondrial mass, differentiation state, astrocyte influence, and technical normalization. Isogenic context does not establish the proposed causal sequence or cell autonomy.", "All protein spots have multiple candidate genes and provide no uniquely assigned MTERF4 or respiratory-subunit confirmation. No mitochondrial translation, assembled-complex abundance, respiration, ATP pool, redox pool, lipid pool, or signaling activation was measured."], "claim": "Under mock treatment at day 30, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia are proposed to have an MTERF4-dependent mitochondrial ribosome maturation bottleneck that reduces mitochondrial translation and completed respiratory-complex assembly, eliciting mitochondrial stress signaling and compensatory nuclear respiratory transcription. This causal mechanism is a hypothesis, not an established result.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In matched APOE4 and APOE3 microglia, measure mitochondrial MTERF4 protein, mature mitoribosomes, nascent mitochondrial translation, assembled respiratory complexes, and oligomycin-sensitive oxygen consumption, with viable-cell and mitochondrial-mass normalization. APOE4 should have lower functional MTERF4, impaired maturation/translation, and reduced assembled-complex capacity. Equal or greater translation and respiratory assembly in APOE4 would strongly weaken the mechanism, even if its RNA pattern persists.", "After differentiation, restore correctly localized MTERF4 in APOE4 to the measured APOE3 protein level using titrated expression. Against vector and matched-expression localization-defective controls, functional MTERF4 should first improve mitoribosome maturation and mitochondrial translation, then respiratory-complex assembly and ATP-linked respiration, and subsequently reduce DELE1 cleavage and DDIT3 induction. Failure to restore maturation/translation after verified mitochondrial delivery and an adequate turnover interval would weaken the proposed primary bottleneck. This intervention distinguishes MTERF4 limitation from an accompanying transcriptional state change.", "Titrate MTERF4 knockdown in APOE3 to the APOE4 mitochondrial protein level, avoiding generalized toxicity. It should reproduce the maturation/translation defect and downstream respiratory stress; an interference-resistant, correctly localized MTERF4 construct should rescue it. Failure of matched partial depletion to reproduce the defect would weaken MTERF4 as the genotype-associated bottleneck.", "During successful MTERF4 rescue, mitochondrial translation should improve before the already elevated nuclear respiratory transcripts need to decline. Improvement confined to RNA levels, with unchanged maturation, translation, and respiration, would favor a compensatory transcriptional association over the proposed causal mechanism. Persistence of DELE1/DDIT3 signaling after recovery of mitochondrial assembly would specifically weaken the proposed downstream stress connection."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 is associated with lower MTERF4 RNA (gene:MTERF4, -2.110 reported log fold change; logarithm base unspecified). The proposed initiating defect is reduced functional mitochondrial MTERF4, making mitochondrial large-ribosomal-subunit maturation the single primary bottleneck. MTERF4 protein abundance, localization, and ribosome maturation were not measured.", "Defective ribosome maturation is proposed to lower mitochondrial translation and the supply of mitochondrially encoded respiratory core subunits. Reduced RNA for MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB, and MT-ND4 (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4) is compatible with restricted core-subunit supply, but does not measure translation or establish that MTERF4 caused these RNA changes.", "Insufficient mitochondrial core-subunit production is proposed to limit assembly of functional oxidative-phosphorylation complexes even as nuclear structural-subunit RNAs increase. All 36 represented nuclear structural-subunit RNAs are higher, including gene:NDUFS7, gene:SDHB, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX5B, and gene:ATP5F1B. Reduced assembled complexes and ATP-linked respiration are predictions, not measured outcomes.", "The proposed assembly defect generates mitochondrial proteostatic stress and engages DELE1-associated integrated stress signaling. Higher DELE1 and DDIT3 RNA (gene:DELE1, +4.823; gene:DDIT3, +2.789) is compatible with this response; DELE1 cleavage, signaling activity, and their causal relationship were not measured.", "Feedback compensation is proposed to raise nuclear respiratory, translation, substrate-oxidation, and antioxidant transcripts without resolving the maturation bottleneck. Higher gene:TUFM, gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, and gene:PRDX3 support the abundance pattern. Compensatory direction, oxidation flux, and oxidative damage remain inferred."], "title": "A mitochondrial ribosome maturation bottleneck linked to reduced MTERF4"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05965709670171745, "cosine_similarity": 0.16481857983712092, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6354983818770227, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05965709670171745, "cosine_similarity": 0.16481857983712092, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6354983818770227, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.9704014999999995, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All biochemical functions, panel memberships and causal connections are unverified background knowledge; only the supplied discovery observations provide experimental evidence. The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30 from the HPC stage. The measurements are RNA expression and protein-spot abundance, not genomic-variant measurements. Causality has not been established.", "All numerical RNA effects in this hypothesis retain the supplied reported log-fold-change scale with unspecified logarithm base; positive means higher in APOE4. The RNA input contains 2,212 selected differential-expression results, of which 1,705 (77.1%) are positive. Program coherence is descriptive against this selected background, not formal enrichment, and genes are not assumed independent. Unrepresented genes are unknown, not unchanged.", "The primary functional assumption is that the coordinated RNA changes translate into sufficient mature hydrolase activity, proton-pump function and vesicular retrieval for increased basal processing. Failed compensation for impaired acidification is a serious competing interpretation of the same RNA increases. Greater hydrolysis per internalized substrate and maintained lysosomal acidity are the decisive unknowns; a reduced reserve revealed only by future overload would not establish an ongoing mock-condition defect.", "Protein spots test compatibility but cannot identify individual-protein changes: protein_spot:044 is +2.379 log2 fold change with candidates [ANXA1, TALDO1, ACTB, VPS26A, BLVRA], and protein_spot:053 is +1.536 with candidates [TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1]. Their directions are compatible with retrieval/hydrolytic remodeling but do not confirm VPS26A or CTSD abundance or activity.", "Serious protein counter-evidence is preserved: protein_spot:064 is -1.202 log2 fold change with candidates [ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1], and protein_spot:065 is -0.926 with candidates [ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART]. These could reflect a pump-related discordance, but neither establishes reduced ATP6V1E1. protein_spot:058 is -0.848 with candidates [CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1], and protein_spot:067 is -1.000 with candidates [PSMA3, ACTG2, CTSB, HEXB, LRIF1]; they challenge a uniformly increased hydrolase-protein interpretation. All candidate identities are retained, and overlapping spots are not independent confirmations.", "Sparse, mixed synthetic observations do not establish increased de novo sphingolipid synthesis: gene:KDSR (+1.27), gene:CERS4 (+2.52), gene:CERS6 (+1.06), gene:ST3GAL5 (+2.17) and gene:ORMDL2 (+1.91) increase while gene:B4GALT5 (-1.88) decreases. Enzyme/regulator directions are not interchangeable with pathway flux. Missing ASAH1 and other turnover members preclude inferring complete ceramide disposal, sphingosine salvage or a particular lipid pool change.", "The strongest unexplained pattern is respiratory transcriptional remodeling: all 36 represented members of an 88-member nuclear respiratory-subunit query increase, including gene:NDUFA5 (+7.34) and gene:NDUFS7 (+5.68), whereas gene:MT-ATP6 (-3.35), gene:MT-CO2 (-1.33), gene:MT-CYB (-2.32) and gene:MT-ND4 (-1.80) decrease; gene:MT-ND4L (+1.95) and gene:MT-ND5 (+1.93) increase. This model does not explain the nuclear/mitochondrial discrepancy or assume increased ATP production. A broader cell-state or organelle-stress response could underlie both programs.", "Comparable viable microglial populations and astrocyte exposure are assumed. Biological replicate counts are not supplied; the available observations cannot separate within-cell regulation, cell-state proportions and co-culture contributions, or establish temporal ordering or a unique initiating gene."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, a coordinated phagolysosomal state is hypothesized to increase basal lysosomal processing of sphingolipid-containing membranes relative to APOE3. Increased acidification capacity, hydrolytic capacity and vesicular retrieval are proposed to keep pace with membrane delivery, sustaining greater turnover in the measured condition.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective basal-condition test: in matched day-30 mock cultures, use tracer-level sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide pulse-chases with equalized delivery and normalization to initially internalized substrate. Quantify intracellular substrate-to-product conversion and compartmental transit, separating hydrolysis from export or simple uptake, together with lysosomal pH. APOE4 should show faster fractional conversion with maintained acidic pH. Slower normalized conversion, particularly with more alkaline lysosomes, would weaken the mechanism and favor failed compensation; greater uptake alone would not satisfy this prediction.", "Prospective causal perturbation: after directly establishing lysosomal GBA activity, titrate GBA suppression in APOE4 to the APOE3 active-enzyme level while matching cargo delivery and viability. The proposed extra glucosylceramide-processing flux should fall toward APOE3, and a perturbation-resistant, lysosome-targeted wild-type GBA should restore it whereas a similarly localized catalytic-dead rescue should not. No APOE4 activity excess, or persistence of the flux difference after verified activity equalization, would weaken the GBA-mediated hydrolytic step. This test does not require GBA to be the unique upstream cause of the coordinated state.", "Prospective test against failed compensation: measure ATP6V1E1 protein specifically, V-ATPase assembly, lysosomal pH and basal cargo conversion, then titrate ATP6V1E1 restoration if a protein deficit is found. The selected mechanism predicts no pre-existing APOE4 basal acidification/clearance defect requiring rescue. Demonstrating such a defect and correcting both pH and slow sphingolipid conversion by restoration would directly weaken the selected mechanism. A phenotype appearing only under a new overload challenge would address reserve capacity, not establish the proposed basal flux direction."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["1. APOE4 biases the cells toward a membrane-uptake-associated state, represented by increased gene:TREM2 (+1.28), gene:MERTK (+1.30), gene:FCGR1A (+1.59), gene:C1QA (+1.25), gene:C1QB (+1.13), gene:C1QC (+1.17) and gene:CD36 (+1.38). The proposed functional consequence is greater delivery of membrane cargo to endolysosomes; these RNA observations establish neither receptor activity nor uptake rate.", "2. The coordinated state increases lysosomal biogenesis and acidification potential alongside delivery: gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:LAMP1 (+1.38), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.23), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.70), gene:ATP6V1H (+6.88), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.51) and gene:ATP6AP1 (+2.30) are increased. The causal proposal is that assembled, active proton pumps maintain an acidic processing compartment during basal turnover. TFEB localization, pump assembly, ATP availability and lysosomal pH remain unmeasured.", "3. Within that acidic compartment, the increased gene:SMPD1 (+5.63) and gene:GBA (+6.71) transcripts are proposed to yield more active sphingomyelin- and glucosylceramide-cleaving enzymes. Increased gene:HEXA (+5.68), gene:HEXB (+2.17) and gene:GM2A (+2.01) support the associated complex-glycosphingolipid processing arm. The hypothesized consequence is faster lysosomal substrate-to-product conversion under mock conditions. No sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, ceramide or other lipid pool, enzyme activity or reaction flux was measured.", "4. The same processing state extends to other incoming cargo through increased gene:CTSB (+5.52), gene:CTSD (+2.86), gene:GAA (+9.96) and gene:MAN2B1 (+1.81), linking the sphingolipid proposal to the broader represented lysosomal hydrolase program. Greater catalytic processing is inferred, not observed. Strongly decreased gene:CTSS (-5.57) requires selective lysosomal remodeling rather than uniform activation of every hydrolase.", "5. Increased gene:RAB7A (+2.65), gene:VPS26A (+4.86), gene:AP5M1 (+9.78), gene:AP5S1 (+4.39), gene:AP5Z1 (+3.78) and gene:IGF2R (+2.02) are proposed to support late-endosomal routing and retrieval of processing machinery, sustaining repeated rounds of membrane clearance. Decreased gene:M6PR (-1.72) is an exception to uniform receptor induction. Routing and localization are unmeasured; the net prediction is greater uptake-normalized basal sphingolipid processing with maintained clearance, without specifying a steady-state lipid concentration."], "title": "Coordinated lysosomal membrane recycling increases basal sphingolipid turnover in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1914115866041428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16186991303538092, "cosine_similarity": 0.16427826905513215, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6422880258899677, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1914115866041428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16186991303538092, "cosine_similarity": 0.16427826905513215, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6422880258899677, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.3628774999999997, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_028", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified, so only ranks and relative magnitudes within the supplied list are used. The down-regulated column is truncated at 507 rows versus 1705 up rows, so the apparent global positive shift is treated as list construction, not as a measured global induction.", "Absence of a gene (PSAP, ASAH1, UGCG, GALC, NEU1, CTSA, SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, MCOLN1, NPC1, GRN) from the supplied rows is treated as unmeasured or non-selected, never as evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase localisation, saposin processing and all lipid pools were not measured in this dataset and are inferred only.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as direct evidence for any named sphingolipid enzyme.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; astrocyte-derived lipid supply may contribute to the microglial state, and causality between APOE genotype and the lysosomal program is not established by these data.", "The hydrolase induction is not statistically distinguishable from a general lysosomal program (sphingolipid hydrolases versus other lysosomal hydrolases, Mann-Whitney p = 1.0); the hypothesis assumes the sphingolipid arm is the functionally limiting branch because of its unique dependence on saposins, GM2A and LIMP-2, which is background knowledge and unverified here."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 by a MiT/TFE-type transcriptional expansion of lysosomal hydrolases in which the sphingolipid-degrading arm (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GLA, SMPD1) is induced far more strongly than the machinery that presents membrane sphingolipids to those enzymes and delivers them to the lysosome (SCARB2, NPC2, GM2A near the bottom-to-middle of the up-regulated distribution; M6PR decreased; PSAP not among the differential rows); we hypothesise that this mismatch leaves in-situ glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin hydrolytic flux limited despite higher enzyme transcripts, so glycosphingolipid substrate is retained on intralysosomal membranes and is partly re-routed to non-lysosomal handling (GBA2, GLTP) and to GM3 rather than more complex glycosphingolipids (ST3GAL5 up, B4GALT5 down), while de novo sphingoid-base synthesis is not co-induced.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, restoring presentation/delivery capacity (PSAP or saposin-C supplementation, or SCARB2 over-expression) should lower glucosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin, raise in-situ lysosomal GBA and HEXA/B activity per unit enzyme protein, and dampen the hydrolase transcript program (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, GAA) toward APOE3, whereas over-expressing GBA alone (adding message/enzyme without presentation capacity) should not normalise the lipid load. If GBA over-expression alone normalises the lipid load and the transcript program while saposin/LIMP-2 supply does not, the presentation bottleneck is wrong and the mechanism is refuted.", "Lipidomics plus activity assay of the same mock APOE4 versus APOE3 cultures should show glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin higher in APOE4 while in-situ hydrolase activity rises proportionally less than the GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 transcript differences. If in-situ activity scales with transcript and no sphingolipid species is elevated, the mechanism is weakened.", "Blocking GBA2 (knockdown or inhibitor) or GLTP knockdown should worsen glucosylceramide accumulation and further raise the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program in APOE4 more than in APOE3; no genotype-selective effect would weaken the proposed non-lysosomal bypass step.", "Limiting exogenous lipid influx (lipoprotein-poor medium, SCARB1/CD36 blockade, or removal of astrocyte co-culture) should shrink the APOE4-specific hydrolase transcript program; persistence of the program under low lipid load would weaken the influx-driven substrate-load step.", "Because de novo synthesis transcripts sit at or below the up-row median, inhibiting serine palmitoyltransferase (myriocin) should have little effect on the APOE4 hydrolase program or on the accumulated glycosphingolipids; a large myriocin-sensitive reduction would favour a synthesis-driven alternative and weaken this mechanism.", "Immunostaining/fractionation should place the extra sphingolipid signal and the induced hydrolases in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4; if the excess enzyme is secreted or retained pre-lysosomally without any luminal lipid excess, the localisation step of the mechanism fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for MiT/TFE factors (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) and for a broad set of lysosomal acid hydrolases, with the sphingolipid arm at the 94th-97th percentile of all up-regulated rows (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:GBA2 +2.63). Inferred, not measured: this reflects an active CLEAR-type transcriptional response rather than more lysosomes per cell.", "Measured: the components that hand membrane-embedded sphingolipids to these hydrolases or deliver them scale much less - gene:SCARB2 +1.06 (6th percentile of up rows), gene:NPC2 +1.17 (15th), gene:LAMP1 +1.38 (30th), gene:GM2A +2.01 (52nd), and mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcripts diverge (gene:M6PR -1.72 versus gene:IGF2R +2.02). PSAP is absent from the supplied differential rows, so its saposin pool is unmeasured. Inferred: per-enzyme delivery and lipid-presentation capacity rises less than hydrolase message.", "Inferred (flux, not measured): because luminal hydrolysis of glucosylceramide, GM2 and sphingomyelin is presentation-limited at the intraluminal membrane interface, catalytic flux per unit transcript falls, and these lipids are retained in late-endosomal/lysosomal membranes. No lipid pool was measured here; this is a prediction, not an observation.", "Measured, interpreted as re-routing: the cytosol-facing glucosylceramidase transcript (gene:GBA2 +2.63) and the non-vesicular glycolipid transfer protein (gene:GLTP +2.38) rise, and lactosylceramide use shifts toward GM3 synthase (gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17) while gene:B4GALT5 falls (-1.88). Inferred: part of the glucosylceramide/lactosylceramide load bypasses the lysosomal lumen.", "Measured: substrate supply routes and endolysosomal membrane machinery are up (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:SNAPIN +2.69), whereas de novo sphingolipid synthesis transcripts sit at or below the median of the up rows (gene:KDSR +1.27, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:SGPL1 +1.09, gene:ORMDL2 +1.91; gene:CERS4 +2.52 is the exception). Inferred: the sphingolipid load is influx- and turnover-derived rather than synthesis-driven.", "Inferred consequence and causal direction (not established here): retained sphingolipid substrate sustains MiT/TFE signalling in a feed-forward loop, so the APOE4-versus-APOE3 steady state under mock treatment is a chronically induced but flux-limited lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic program with compensatory endolysosomal membrane remodelling."], "title": "Cofactor- and LIMP-2-limited intralysosomal sphingolipid presentation, not hydrolase message, is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0806871469187313, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.017599621443859625, "cosine_similarity": 0.16390663177321546, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6587249190938511, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0806871469187313, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.017599621443859625, "cosine_similarity": 0.16390663177321546, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6587249190938511, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1382335, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 390}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_180", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1.0 and adjusted p\u003c0.05) and are not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made relative to this selected background, which is itself shifted upward (mean +1.39, 77% positive), so only relative, within-list contrasts are interpreted.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs, ranks and within-list comparisons are used, never absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding proteins; enzyme activity, complex assembly state, metabolic flux, NADPH/GSH/thioredoxin redox state, H2O2 concentration and organelle localisation were not measured in this dataset and are inferred.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes; protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5), protein_spot:077 (candidates including PRDX2) and protein_spot:038 (candidates including TKT, ALDOA) are treated as ambiguous, weakly corroborating observations and not as identified proteins.", "The opposite behaviour of mtDNA-encoded versus nuclear-encoded subunit transcripts is assumed to reflect genuine biology rather than probe-set or ambient-RNA behaviour specific to the 10X Flex chemistry; only six mtDNA-encoded transcripts passed selection.", "The astrocyte co-culture and the microglial compartment are assumed to have been separated correctly, so the shift is intrinsic to APOE4 microglia rather than a change in cell-type composition or in astrocyte-derived signals.", "The assigned peroxisomal focus was rejected: no PEX transcript and no catalase transcript are in the list, ABCD1 is lower (-1.64), and the small peroxisomal set is not enriched (permutation p=0.68); the redox arm is retained on the thiol-peroxidase/NADPH axis instead."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells by a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain, TCA and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts that is not matched by the mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts, a stoichiometric imbalance predicted to raise electron leak; the cells raise thiol-peroxidase transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, TXNDC17, GPX4, GSS) but the NADPH-regenerating capacity that recycles these peroxidases is not raised (PGD, TALDO1, NADK lower), making NADPH-dependent peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin re-reduction the rate-limiting bottleneck and producing a persistent low-grade H2O2 tone with integrated-stress-response and SREBP-driven lipid-remodelling output. Causality is not established by these data; the electron leak, H2O2 concentration, assembly state, NADPH pool and enzyme activities are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial inhibition of NADPH supply (G6PD/PPP inhibition with 6-aminonicotinamide or DHEA) or of thioredoxin reductase (low-dose auranofin) at doses that are near-neutral in APOE3 should produce a markedly larger increase in cytosolic and mitochondrial H2O2 reporter oxidation (roGFP2-Orp1/mito-roGFP2-Orp1) and a larger shift of PRDX2/PRDX3 to the hyperoxidised/dimeric form in APOE4 microglia; equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the proposed NADPH-recycling bottleneck.", "Rescue prediction: raising cytosolic NADPH supply (G6PD overexpression) or expressing matrix-targeted catalase should normalise the PRDX2/PRDX3 oxidation state and lower DDIT3/ATF4-target transcripts and lipid-droplet content in APOE4 without reversing the nuclear ETC transcript increase; if ISR and lipid phenotypes persist despite a normalised peroxiredoxin redox state, the bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Assembly prediction: blue-native PAGE / complex I in-gel activity and quantitative measurement of mtDNA-encoded (MT-ND1, MT-CO2, MT-CYB) versus nuclear-encoded (NDUFA9, NDUFB8, UQCRC2) subunit proteins should show a lower mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded protein ratio and increased subassembly intermediates in APOE4; equal ratios and normal holo-complex profiles would falsify the mitonuclear-imbalance step even if the transcript pattern holds.", "Source-localisation prediction: MitoTEMPO or mitochondria-targeted catalase should reduce the APOE4-specific oxidative reporter signal and ISR markers more than an equipotent cytosolic antioxidant or an NADPH-oxidase inhibitor; greater efficacy of NOX inhibition would point to a NOX rather than a respiratory-chain source and weaken step 2.", "Functional prediction: Seahorse respirometry should show APOE4 microglia with unchanged or reduced maximal/spare respiratory capacity despite the higher nuclear ETC transcripts, i.e. transcript-protein-function uncoupling; a proportional increase in maximal respiration with no rise in peroxide reporter signal would argue for benign mitochondrial biogenesis and weaken the whole mechanism.", "Normalisation control: spike-in-normalised bulk RNA-seq or qPCR of the same lines should reproduce the divergence between nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts and mtDNA-encoded transcripts and the decrease in TALDO1/PGD; loss of this divergence after spike-in normalisation would indicate that the pattern is a composition/normalisation artefact of the selected single-cell list."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_180", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: nuclear-encoded ETC subunit and assembly-factor transcripts are uniformly higher in APOE4 (39/39 measured genes positive, mean log fold change 2.81 versus a selected-background mean of 1.39; permutation p=0.0002), together with TCA/NADH-generating transcripts (OGDH, MDH1, DLD, ACO2, IDH3B/G, GLUD1) and mitochondrial carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A46). Inferred: greater capacity and substrate delivery for matrix NADH production and respiratory-complex assembly.", "Measured: the mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts present in the dataset move oppositely (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 lower; only MT-ND4L, MT-ND5 higher; nuclear-versus-mtDNA mean difference 3.62, permutation p=0.0001). Inferred: mitonuclear subunit stoichiometry imbalance, i.e. nuclear modules in excess of mtDNA-encoded cores, favouring accumulation of partially assembled, electron-leak-prone complex I/III/IV intermediates. Assembly state itself was not measured.", "Measured: mitochondrial and cytosolic iron-handling transcripts are higher (SLC25A37 +4.48, SLC11A2 +1.77, FTH1 +2.53). Inferred: a larger labile/mitochondrial iron flux that converts leaked superoxide-derived H2O2 into damaging radicals; no iron pool or ROS species was measured.", "Measured: thiol-peroxidase and glutathione-synthesis transcripts are coordinately higher (TXNDC17 +7.10, PRDX2 +4.41, TXNL1 +4.33, PRDX3 +3.49, GPX4 +2.79, PRDX5 +1.96, GSS +2.11; set permutation p=0.004), with two ambiguous protein spots containing PRDX2 or CAT among their candidates also higher. Inferred: an adaptive antioxidant response to increased peroxide load; enzyme activity and oxidation state were not measured.", "BOTTLENECK (measured transcripts, inferred flux): the NADPH supply that regenerates reduced thioredoxin/glutathione is not scaled with the peroxidase increase - oxidative pentose-phosphate and NADP-supply transcripts are lower (TALDO1 -2.32, PGD -1.30, NADK -1.14) while only mitochondrial/malic routes rise (NNT +2.88, ME1 +1.36). Peroxiredoxin/GPX4 turnover therefore becomes NADPH-limited, leaving a standing H2O2 concentration despite higher peroxidase protein.", "Measured downstream: integrated-stress-response transcripts (EIF2AK3 +1.51, DDIT3 +2.79, SHMT2 +2.22, SHMT1 +3.28) and SREBP-driven lipogenic/sterol transcripts (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, INSIG1, LDLR) are higher while PUFA-activating and lipoxygenase transcripts are lower (ACSL4 -2.14, ALOX15 -3.63). Inferred: chronic oxidative tone drives ISR signalling and a monounsaturated-lipid/lipid-droplet remodelling programme that limits membrane PUFA peroxidation, accompanied by increased lysosomal/degradative transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1A; set permutation p=0.008)."], "title": "Mitonuclear ETC subunit imbalance with unmatched NADPH-dependent peroxiredoxin recycling sets a chronic oxidative tone in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21930731455156371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18087237557417488, "cosine_similarity": 0.16328596417606328, "direction_accuracy": 0.26537216828478966, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_180", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6970970873786407, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21930731455156371, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18087237557417488, "cosine_similarity": 0.16328596417606328, "direction_accuracy": 0.26537216828478966, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6970970873786407, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.33700525, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 391}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_058", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects use an unspecified logarithm base and the rows are selected differential-expression results (no |effect| below 0.25, 77% positive, mean +1.39), so only percentile rank within the supplied list, not the absolute magnitude or the bare sign, is treated as informative.", "Higher hydrolase transcript rank translates into higher mature, correctly delivered enzyme activity in the acidic compartment; this is inferred, not measured, and is directly challenged by the reduced gene:M6PR and gene:AP1M1 transcripts.", "Ceramide-clearing enzymes (ASAH1, PSAP, ACER3, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2, SPHK1/2, GALC, NPC1) were not measured; the bottleneck step assumes they are not proportionally co-induced.", "2-D protein spots contain several candidate genes each, so no spot uniquely identifies a hydrolase; spot changes are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, organelle-fractionation or flux measurement is supplied, so every statement about ceramide, sphingomyelin, hexosylceramide, localisation and direction of causation is a prediction.", "Transcripts are attributed to microglia rather than the co-cultured astrocytes, and the isogenic APOE4/APOE3 contrast is assumed free of clone- and batch-specific confounding."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, the transcript program that generates ceramide inside the endolysosome (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GBA2, GLA) is among the most strongly elevated members of an otherwise general lysosomal/CLEAR-type program, while the measured limbs that consume ceramide into complex glycosphingolipids (B4GALT5, ST3GAL5) are flat or reduced and endosomal routing transcripts favour the late-endosome/lysosome over Golgi-directed recycling (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, AP5Z1 up; M6PR, AP1M1, GOLPH3L down). We hypothesise, without claiming causality is established, that ceramide disposal (deacylation/salvage/export, whose enzymes are not present in this selected DE list) is the rate-limiting node, so APOE4 microglia should carry a higher lysosomal ceramide-to-sphingomyelin ratio and lower hexosylceramide/SM pools than APOE3 microglia. All enzymatic activity, flux, lipid pools and organelle localisation in this claim are inferred; only RNA and 2-D protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted sphingolipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia should show an increased ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio with reduced sphingomyelin and reduced hexosylceramide-to-ceramide ratio, with the ceramide excess enriched in a lysosome-enriched fraction. Finding higher sphingomyelin and higher hexosylceramide with unchanged or lower ceramide would falsify the core claim.", "Acid sphingomyelinase and glucocerebrosidase activity assays on APOE4 lysates should show higher activity per cell than APOE3. If activities are unchanged or lower despite the top-percentile gene:SMPD1 and gene:GBA transcripts, step 2 is broken and the alternative delivery/maturation bottleneck implied by gene:M6PR and gene:AP1M1 becomes the better model.", "Discriminating perturbation: raising ceramide disposal (ASAH1 overexpression or acid-ceramidase activation) should normalise the ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio and reduce lysosomal-damage and inflammatory readouts in APOE4 cells while leaving gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA and gene:TFEB transcript elevation intact. If ceramide falls but the phenotype is unchanged, ceramide is a bystander; if ceramide does not fall, the disposal bottleneck is wrong.", "Source discrimination: SMPD1 knockdown (or functional acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition) should remove most of the APOE4 ceramide excess, whereas conduritol-B-epoxide inhibition of GBA should convert the excess into glucosylceramide. If neither manipulation lowers ceramide but myriocin or a CERS inhibitor does, the ceramide arises de novo and steps 2-3 are falsified.", "Unbiased whole-transcriptome and proteome profiling should show ASAH1/PSAP not induced in proportion to SMPD1/GBA; strong co-induction of ASAH1 and PSAP together with unchanged lipid ratios would weaken the mechanism.", "Because the hydrolase induction is not sphingolipid-selective, a specificity test is required: if the ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio is unchanged while cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol pools rise (consistent with gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SCARB1), the dominant APOE4 lipid bottleneck is neutral-lipid storage rather than sphingolipid turnover, and this hypothesis should be replaced."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal biogenesis and acidification (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA) together with lipid uptake/esterification transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1). Inferred: an expanded degradative compartment receiving an increased flux of lipid cargo.", "Measured: within that program the acid hydrolases that liberate ceramide from sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids rank at the top of the distribution (gene:GBA 98th percentile, gene:HEXA 96th, gene:SMPD1 95th; gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA above the list median for GBA2/HEXB). Inferred: increased luminal capacity for acid sphingomyelinase and glucocerebrosidase reactions, i.e. increased ceramide production inside late endosomes/lysosomes.", "Measured: the measured anabolic limb that would drain ceramide/glucosylceramide into complex glycosphingolipids is not co-induced (gene:B4GALT5 at the 13th percentile; gene:ST3GAL5 only modestly above median), and ceramide-synthase/sphingoid-base transcripts are near or below the list median (gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERS4). Inferred: little re-routing of liberated ceramide into complex glycosphingolipids and only a modest de novo contribution.", "Inferred bottleneck (unmeasured pools): the enzymes that clear ceramide (acid ceramidase ASAH1, its activator PSAP, salvage via SGMS/UGCG) are absent from this selected DE list and are assumed not to be matched to the catabolic induction; catabolic input therefore exceeds disposal, producing net ceramide accumulation with reduced sphingomyelin and hexosylceramide.", "Measured routing shift: late-endosomal/retromer/ESCRT transcripts are elevated (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP5M1) while Golgi-directed sorting transcripts are reduced (gene:M6PR, gene:AP1M1, gene:GOLPH3L). Inferred: sphingolipid handling is displaced from the Golgi sphingomyelin-synthase route toward lysosomal catabolism, and hydrolase delivery/recycling is remodelled rather than simply scaled up.", "Inferred consequence: a raised lysosomal ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio lowers the threshold for lysosomal membrane damage and sustains the secretory/inflammatory transcripts seen here (gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:CD74, gene:C1QA), while elevated gene:SGPL1 with no measured sphingosine kinase suggests reduced S1P tone rather than a pro-survival S1P shift."], "title": "APOE4 microglia bias sphingolipid turnover into a lysosomal SM/glycosphingolipid catabolic limb, making ceramide disposal the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2447014732489015, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11666865366657996, "cosine_similarity": 0.16095208213124912, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_058", "mean_absolute_error": 0.676831715210356, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2447014732489015, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11666865366657996, "cosine_similarity": 0.16095208213124912, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.676831715210356, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.92002725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 392}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA effect values are log fold changes (APOE4 vs APOE3, mock) on an unspecified logarithm base, preserved as reported rather than converted; relative rank and sign, not the absolute base, are used for interpretation.", "The RNA observations are a pre-selected list of differentially expressed genes (all 2212 rows meet an internal significance criterion; 1705/2212, ~77%, are positive), so pathway-level positive skew must be judged against this ~77% positive background rather than a 50/50 null.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate gene identities each (mean 4.8) and are not resolved to single proteins; a spot's direction is treated as compatible or incompatible evidence for the pathway, never as confirmation of a specific candidate gene's protein level.", "Increased transcript abundance for a catabolic enzyme is treated as evidence of altered gene-expression program engagement, not as proof of increased enzymatic activity, substrate flux, or organelle-level lipid content.", "Absence of a gene from the RNA list (e.g., ASAH1, SPTLC1/2, UGCG were not found) is treated as unknown/unmeasured in this selected list, not as evidence the gene is unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-microglia display a coordinated transcriptional program that raises lysosomal sphingolipid-degrading enzymes and lipid-transfer/trafficking receptors together with a shift in endosomal small-GTPase expression away from exosome-secretory routing and toward late-endosome/lysosome maturation. This pattern is consistent with (but does not prove) a rerouting of sphingolipid-containing membrane cargo toward intracellular lysosomal processing rather than extracellular vesicle release in APOE4 microglia; whether this reflects increased throughput of a functioning pathway or a compensatory response to reduced catabolic efficiency cannot be resolved from these transcript/protein-spot data alone.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective and discriminating: if APOE4 and APOE3 microglia are metabolically labeled and subjected to lysosome-targeted lipidomics plus exosome-fraction lipidomics under the same mock condition, APOE4 cells should show a relative increase in lysosomal (intracellular) glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin turnover products and a decrease in exosome-associated sphingolipid/GBA or CTSB/CTSD enzymatic cargo relative to APOE3; if exosomal sphingolipid or hydrolase cargo is unchanged or increased in APOE4 despite the transcript pattern, the proposed routing-shift mechanism would be weakened in favor of a purely transcriptional or generalized-lysosomal-biogenesis explanation.", "Prospective: siRNA/CRISPRi knockdown of RAB27A in APOE3 microglia should partially reduce exosome output and should not, by itself, be sufficient to reproduce the full magnitude of GBA/SMPD1 transcript induction seen in APOE4 cells; if RAB27A knockdown alone recapitulates the entire APOE4 lysosomal transcript signature, that would suggest the sphingolipid enzyme induction is a downstream consequence of altered secretory routing rather than a co-regulated, genotype-driven program, requiring revision of the proposed step ordering."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with strong, coordinate up-regulation of lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolizing transcripts GBA (gene:GBA, effect +6.71), SMPD1 (gene:SMPD1, +5.63), GBA2 (gene:GBA2, +2.63) and GLA (gene:GLA, +1.53), plus the lysosomal glucocerebrosidase-trafficking receptor SCARB2 (gene:SCARB2, +1.06) and glycohydrolases HEXA/HEXB (gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17).", "In parallel, transcripts for lipid-transfer/lysosomal cofactors NPC2 (gene:NPC2, +1.17) and GLTP (gene:GLTP, +2.38), and de novo ceramide-synthesis genes CERS4/CERS6/KDSR (gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27) and the terminal degradation enzyme SGPL1 (gene:SGPL1, +1.09) are also increased, indicating that both synthesis- and catabolism-arm transcripts of the sphingolipid pathway move in the same (APOE4-up) direction rather than one arm being selectively suppressed.", "Glycosphingolipid-modifying glycosyltransferases show a mixed pattern: ST3GAL4 and ST3GAL5 increase (gene:ST3GAL4 +1.85, gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17) while ST3GAL2 and B4GALT5 decrease (gene:ST3GAL2 -1.39, gene:B4GALT5 -1.88), indicating non-uniform remodeling of glycosphingolipid head-group processing rather than a simple 'more of everything' shift.", "Endosomal/exosomal trafficking transcripts diverge: RAB27A, which supports multivesicular-body docking and exosome secretion, is reduced (gene:RAB27A, -2.52), while RAB7A (late endosome-to-lysosome maturation, gene:RAB7A, +2.65), RAB7B (gene:RAB7B, +1.40) and CHMP4B (ESCRT-III, multivesicular body formation, gene:CHMP4B, +3.82) are increased.", "Combined, higher lysosomal sphingolipid-hydrolase transcript capacity plus a shift from RAB27A-dependent exosome release toward RAB7A/CHMP4B-associated intraluminal vesicle formation and lysosomal maturation is compatible with a routing change that favors intracellular degradation of sphingolipid-bearing membranes over their export in extracellular vesicles.", "This transcript-level signature overlaps a broader, non-sphingolipid-specific lysosomal hydrolase increase (CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, CTSK +7.36, NAGLU +5.91, LAMP1 +1.38) and a notable exception (CTSS -5.57), so part or all of the sphingolipid-gene induction could instead reflect a generalized lysosomal biogenesis program rather than a sphingolipid-dedicated mechanism; supplied protein spots carrying CTSB/CTSD/HEXB as one of several candidate identities show both concordant (protein_spot:027, 053, 055, 057) and discordant (protein_spot:058, 067, 069, 090) directions, so protein-level confirmation of any single lysosomal or sphingolipid enzyme is not established.", "Because none of the sphingolipid-specific enzymes (GBA, SMPD1, GBA2, GLA, CERS4/6, KDSR, SGPL1, NPC2, GLTP, ORMDL2) appear among any protein-spot candidate list, and no sphingolipid species, enzyme-activity, or exosome-output measurements are supplied, the transcriptional pattern indicates altered pathway gene expression only; whether lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic flux, ceramide/glucosylceramide steady-state levels, or exosomal sphingolipid export are actually changed in APOE4 microglia under mock conditions remains unmeasured."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show coordinated induction of lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic/trafficking transcripts alongside reduced exosomal secretion machinery, favoring intracellular sphingolipid retention over vesicular export"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.030332681017612523, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.042879096148857945, "cosine_similarity": 0.1609075788908798, "direction_accuracy": 0.05177993527508091, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6336860841423948, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.030332681017612523, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.042879096148857945, "cosine_similarity": 0.1609075788908798, "direction_accuracy": 0.05177993527508091, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6336860841423948, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.7075843, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_089", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA log fold changes (base unspecified, preserved as reported) reflect real per-cell transcript differences between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia and are not dominated by ambient RNA from the astrocyte co-culture or by differences in microglial yield/maturation.", "Lower RAC2, DOCK8, MYO1F and MYH9 transcript abundance translates into lower protein abundance and lower active (GTP-loaded / membrane-associated) Rho-GTPase and assembled myosin-IIA at the phagocytic cup; none of these pools was measured.", "Increased ARHGDIA transcript increases functional Rho-GDI capacity rather than being compensatory to an already reduced GTPase pool with no net effect on effective signalling.", "The 2D-gel spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified; the ANXA1-attributed increases assume that ANXA1, whose transcript is up (+4.15), rather than TALDO1 (transcript -2.34) or keratin contaminants, drives protein_spot:043-046.", "The rows supplied are a selected differential-expression subset, so all set-level statements are made relative to the internal background of the supplied list, not to an unbiased transcriptome; sets are also limited by many members being absent from the list (e.g. RAC1, CDC42, ITGAM, ITGB2, WAS, CORO1A were not supplied).", "Transcript-level lysosomal expansion is treated as capacity, not as measured degradative flux; no lipid, lysosomal pH, cathepsin activity or phagocytosis assay is present in the supplied data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated reduction of hematopoietic-restricted Rho-GTPase/actomyosin transcripts (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, PLEK, MYO1F, ARHGAP30, FAM49B/CYRI-B, MYH9) together with a very high ARHGDIA transcript, while cargo-recognition receptors, clathrin/dynamin components and lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts are all elevated; we hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 is therefore actin-cup extension and myosin-IIA-dependent closure of large-particle phagocytosis (internalisation), not recognition and not lysosomal degradative capacity. Causality is not established by these data; the RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list and the protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel spots.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake assay: in a synchronized engulfment assay with large particles (pHrodo-labelled myelin, synaptosomes or IgG-opsonized beads), APOE4 microglia should bind cargo at 4 C at least as well as APOE3 (equal or higher surface-bound particles per cell) but internalise significantly fewer at 37 C, giving a higher surface-bound:internalised ratio and a higher fraction of open, unsealed F-actin/phospho-MLC2 cups by imaging. If APOE4 shows equal or greater internalisation index with normal cup closure kinetics, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Module-restoration perturbation: re-expressing RAC2 (or a constitutively active Rac allele) or knocking down ARHGDIA in APOE4 microglia should restore internalisation of large particles toward APOE3 levels without changing recognition-receptor transcripts (SCARB1, MRC1, CD36, TREM2). If ARHGDIA knockdown raises active Rac1 (pulldown) but does not rescue engulfment, or if RAC2 restoration has no effect, the Rho-GTDI/Rac arm of the mechanism is weakened.", "Phenocopy test: pharmacological myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin) or MYH9 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should reduce large-particle internalisation to APOE4 levels and abolish the genotype difference; if APOE3 engulfment in this assay is myosin-II-independent, the MYH9 step is not the bottleneck.", "Step-specificity control: fluid-phase and receptor-mediated endocytosis (dextran, transferrin) and degradation of already-internalised cargo (DQ-BSA dequenching, cathepsin B activity) should be equal or higher in APOE4, consistent with the elevated DNM2/CLTB and CTSB/CTSD/v-ATPase/TFEB transcripts. Finding a primary degradation or acidification deficit with normal internalisation would relocate the bottleneck to the lysosome and falsify this hypothesis as stated.", "Confound test: quantitative protein measurement (flow cytometry or immunostaining gated on microglia) should show lower RAC2, MYO1F and myosin-IIA protein per APOE4 microglial cell while pan-myeloid PTPRC/CD45 protein is comparable. If PTPRC, CD52 and other pan-hematopoietic markers are proportionally reduced at protein level, the transcript pattern more likely reflects a global myeloid-identity or ambient-RNA difference than a targeted cytoskeletal program, weakening the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: against a globally upward-shifted selected DE background (median reported log fold change +1.46, 77% positive), the myeloid-restricted Rho-GTPase/actomyosin module is uniformly and strongly negative (gene:RAC2 -1.97, gene:DOCK8 -1.99, gene:ARHGDIB -1.98, gene:PLEK -2.53, gene:MYO1F -3.69, gene:ARHGAP30 -5.16, gene:FAM49B -5.83, gene:MYH9 -6.38; 8/8 down, permutation p\u003c1e-4 versus the background distribution), whereas the ubiquitous nucleation module is up (gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5, gene:CFL1, gene:RHOA).", "Inferred activity/localisation (not measured): the extreme gene:ARHGDIA increase (+10.61, 99.9th percentile) together with reduced Rac-specific GEF input (gene:DOCK8) is predicted to shift Rho-family GTPases toward the inactive, GDI-bound cytosolic pool and to lower membrane-delivered active Rac at nascent phagocytic cups; no GTP-loading, F/G-actin ratio or membrane fraction was measured here.", "Inferred flux: reduced non-muscle myosin IIA (gene:MYH9; the only protein spots whose candidate list contains MYH9, protein_spot:010 and protein_spot:011, also trend down but are not significant) is predicted to limit the contractile closure/scission step of the cup, so engaged cargo is retained at the surface rather than converted to sealed phagosomes.", "The recognition/tethering arm is not limiting: uptake and bridging transcripts are uniformly elevated (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:SYK, gene:ANXA1 +4.15), and the strongly increased ANXA1-candidate spot series (protein_spot:045, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:043) is consistent with, though not proof of, higher annexin-A1 protein.", "Small-scale endocytic machinery is preserved or increased (gene:DNM2 +5.82, gene:CLTB +2.14), so the predicted defect is specific to large, actomyosin-dependent engulfment rather than to bulk membrane internalisation.", "The degradative compartment is transcriptionally expanded, not deficient (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB; curated lysosome/v-ATPase set mean +3.49, 26/26 positive, Mann-Whitney p=5e-4 versus background), so under this hypothesis the lysosome is downstream of, and not the cause of, the bottleneck; its expansion is interpreted as an unmet-capacity or lipid-driven compensatory state.", "Net predicted cellular phenotype: APOE4 microglia bind cargo at least as well as APOE3 but internalise fewer large particles per cell, accumulate surface-bound/unsealed cargo, and show relatively preserved fluid-phase uptake and degradation of the material that does reach the lysosome; the coincident gene:ITGA6 (+15.46) and gene:ITGB1 (+6.31) increase is interpreted as a shift of actin usage toward substrate adhesion."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose the myeloid-restricted RAC2/DOCK8-myosin-IIA actin module, creating a phagocytic-cup closure bottleneck upstream of an expanded degradative endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.036203522504892366, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03045688445721234, "cosine_similarity": 0.16064490923072178, "direction_accuracy": 0.061488673139158574, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_089", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6318220064724919, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.036203522504892366, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03045688445721234, "cosine_similarity": 0.16064490923072178, "direction_accuracy": 0.061488673139158574, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6318220064724919, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.67545625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 393}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA transcript-level log fold changes (logarithm base unspecified in the source data) are assumed to correlate directionally with corresponding protein abundance and enzymatic activity for ACOX1, SCP2, ABCD1, PRDX2/3/5, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4, MSRA, NNT, PGD, and CYBA; none of these enzymatic activities, NADPH/NADP+ ratios, or intracellular ROS/H2O2 levels were directly measured in this dataset.", "The peroxisomal beta-oxidation reaction catalyzed by ACOX1 is treated as an unverified, background-knowledge generator of H2O2 as a reaction byproduct; peroxisomal oxidative flux itself is not measured here.", "Protein_spot:017 and protein_spot:077 abundance increases are tentatively associated with CAT and PRDX2 respectively for interpretive purposes only; each spot has multiple candidate genes and the true contributing protein(s) are not identified by this data.", "The isogenic-comparison design (per discovery.json metadata) is assumed to isolate APOE4-genotype-associated transcriptional differences from clonal or culture-batch confounds, though biological replicate numbers are not supplied.", "The RNA observations represent a pre-selected list of differentially expressed genes (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) rather than an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement, so percentile comparisons are relative to this already-significant, positively-skewed subset, not to all expressed genes."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, a multi-gene panel of thiol- and peroxide-detoxifying transcripts (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4, MSRA, NNT) is elevated well above the already positive-skewed background of this differential-expression dataset, consistent with an inferred increase in intracellular peroxide/oxidative burden that provokes a compensatory redox-defense transcriptional response. A peroxisomal lipid-handling imbalance -- a large increase in SCP2 (intracellular sterol/lipid carrier) transcript together with reduced ABCD1 (peroxisomal very-long-chain fatty acid importer) transcript -- is a plausible but only partly supported candidate contributor to this burden, because the canonical peroxisomal beta-oxidation enzyme transcripts ACOX1 and CROT are only modestly increased, near the cohort median. No direct measurement of ROS, H2O2, NADPH ratios, or peroxisomal flux is available in this dataset; the proposed chain from peroxisomal lipid handling to oxidative burden to antioxidant transcript induction is inferred, not established, and causal direction is not determined by these correlational, cross-sectional measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: direct measurement of intracellular peroxide/ROS levels (e.g., a ratiometric H2O2 or general ROS probe) in APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia should show elevated peroxide burden in APOE4 at baseline, matching the antioxidant transcript signature; if peroxide/ROS levels are not elevated in APOE4 despite this transcript signature, the claim that these transcripts reflect compensation for oxidative stress would be weakened, suggesting instead a stress-independent APOE4 transcriptional program.", "If ACOX1 or SCP2 expression/activity is experimentally reduced (knockdown or pharmacological inhibition) in APOE4 microglia and this lowers the compensatory antioxidant module (PRDX2, PRDX3, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4) toward APOE3 levels, this would support a peroxisomal-oxidation-driven contribution to the redox burden; if such knockdown does not change antioxidant transcript levels, this specifically weakens the proposed peroxisomal-flux link while leaving open that the antioxidant induction stems from another source (e.g., CYBA/NADPH-oxidase-associated superoxide production).", "Restoring ABCD1 expression toward APOE3 levels in APOE4 microglia should, if the import/oxidation mismatch (SCP2 up, ABCD1 down) meaningfully contributes to peroxisomal oxidative burden, reduce measured peroxide levels and blunt the antioxidant transcript module; no change under ABCD1 restoration would weaken this specific sub-claim about the import/oxidation mismatch, without necessarily invalidating the broader observation of antioxidant transcript induction."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: SCP2 transcript is strongly increased (gene:SCP2, effect +5.95, ~96th percentile of the 2212-gene differential-expression set) while ABCD1 transcript is significantly decreased (gene:ABCD1, effect -1.64, ~15th percentile) -- a measured mismatch between a peroxisomal lipid-transfer gene and a peroxisomal fatty-acid-import gene.", "Measured RNA: canonical peroxisomal beta-oxidation transcripts ACOX1 (gene:ACOX1, +1.24, ~39th percentile) and CROT (gene:CROT, +1.03, ~25th percentile) are also significantly up but only modestly relative to the dataset's already positive-skewed background (median effect ~+1.46 across all DE genes), so this arm of evidence is weak and should not be over-weighted.", "Inferred (not measured): if these RNA changes translate proportionally into protein abundance and enzymatic activity, altered SCP2-mediated lipid trafficking combined with reduced ABCD1-dependent VLCFA import could shift peroxisomal fatty-acid handling and act as a candidate, unconfirmed source of peroxisomal H2O2 production via the ACOX1 oxidation step.", "Measured RNA: independent of the peroxisomal-flux question, a broad and internally consistent panel of thiol/peroxide-buffering transcripts is elevated well above the median: PRDX2 (+4.41, ~90th pct), PRDX3 (+3.49, ~83rd pct), PRDX5 (+1.96, ~62nd pct), TXNDC17 (+7.10, ~98th pct), TXNL1 (+4.33, ~90th pct), GPX4 (+2.79, ~75th pct), MSRA (+2.64, ~73rd pct), and the NADPH-supplying enzyme NNT (+2.88, ~76th pct). This coherent multi-gene enrichment above background is the strongest evidence in the dataset for an active redox-defense transcriptional program.", "Measured protein abundance (non-unique): protein_spot:017 (candidate genes include catalase, CAT; among others) is significantly increased (+0.766 log2FC, p=0.001), and protein_spot:077 (candidate genes include PRDX2; among others) is significantly increased (+1.07 log2FC, p=0.003); because each spot maps to multiple candidate genes, neither can be uniquely attributed to CAT or PRDX2.", "Counter-evidence (measured RNA): PGD, an oxidative pentose-phosphate-pathway NADPH source, is significantly decreased (gene:PGD, -1.30, ~19th pct), and CYBA, a subunit of superoxide-generating NADPH oxidase complexes, is increased (gene:CYBA, +1.32); the NADPH-supply and ROS-source picture is therefore mixed rather than uniformly protective, and part of the signature (CYBA) could indicate an additional or alternative ROS source rather than only compensation.", "Integrated (partly inferred) picture: the antioxidant/thiol-buffering transcript module is the most robust, above-background signal in this dataset; the peroxisomal beta-oxidation-flux link is a plausible but weakly supported upstream candidate (resting mainly on SCP2 and ABCD1, not on ACOX1/CROT), so the mechanism should be read as compensatory redox buffering in response to an inferred oxidative/peroxide burden, with peroxisomal lipid mishandling as one candidate but unconfirmed contributing source, not as an established peroxisome-to-ROS causal chain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a coordinated thiol/peroxide-buffering transcript program, with a candidate but weakly-supported peroxisomal lipid-handling imbalance (SCP2 up, ABCD1 down) as one possible upstream contributor"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.016425356319134145, "cosine_similarity": 0.16023637809041957, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6454951456310679, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.016425356319134145, "cosine_similarity": 0.16023637809041957, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6454951456310679, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6541759, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 3}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_067", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect| \u003e= 1 in an unspecified logarithm base, not an unbiased whole-transcriptome readout; set-level statements are made relative to the supplied rows only, and the global positive shift (77.1% of rows positive, mean +1.39) is treated as the null background rather than as biology.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding functional complexes; no protein, assembly, respiration, ATP, lysosomal-pH or flux measurement is supplied, so all activity, flux, localisation and direction statements are inferences.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for any specific gene product in this hypothesis.", "The v-ATPase is assumed to be a quantitatively major ATP sink in these cells and lysosomal acidification is assumed to be ATP-supply-sensitive; this is unverified background knowledge.", "Genotype effects are assumed to be at least partly microglia-intrinsic, although the cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so non-cell-autonomous astrocyte-derived effects cannot be excluded.", "Findings are assumed to hold at the single measured condition (mock, day 30 from HPC) and cannot be extended to stimulated states or other timepoints; replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision is unknown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of the lysosomal/CLEAR compartment (TFEB, MITF, v-ATPase subunits, acid hydrolases) together with reduced transcripts for the committed glycolytic steps (HK2, PFKP) and a uniform, set-coherent increase in mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/import and respiratory-chain complex I transcripts. We hypothesise that the resulting state makes mitochondrial complex I-driven ATP supply the primary bottleneck for v-ATPase-dependent lysosomal acidification and degradative flux in APOE4 but not APOE3 microglia. Only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured; respiration, ATP flux, lysosomal pH and proteolysis are inferred and untested here, and no causal direction is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: titrated complex I inhibition (piericidin A or low-dose rotenone) at doses that leave APOE3 lysosomal function intact should preferentially collapse APOE4 lysosomal acidification (LysoSensor/LysoTracker ratiometric pH) and proteolytic flux (DQ-BSA, bulk cathepsin activity, cargo clearance after myelin or pHrodo-bead feeding). If APOE4 and APOE3 are equally sensitive, or APOE3 is more sensitive, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Mirror-image prediction: glycolytic inhibition (2-deoxyglucose, or HK2/PFKP knockdown) should impair lysosomal acidification and degradative flux more in APOE3 than in APOE4. If APOE4 is the more 2-DG-sensitive genotype, step 2 and the bottleneck assignment are wrong.", "Direct flux test: Seahorse profiling should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption, higher oligomycin-sensitive respiration and a higher OXPHOS-derived share of total ATP production in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Unchanged or lower APOE4 respiration would falsify the core mechanism, because the entire chain rests on inferred flux rather than measured flux.", "Coupling test: acute v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1 should reduce oligomycin-sensitive respiration by a larger fraction in APOE4 than APOE3 (a larger share of oxidative ATP devoted to lysosomal pumping). No genotype difference would weaken the proposed ATP-supply coupling between steps 4 and 5.", "Upstream test: TFEB knockdown (or mTORC1 reactivation) in APOE4 should lower the v-ATPase and hydrolase transcript module; if the complex I/TCA transcript module falls in parallel, the two arms are co-regulated, whereas if it is unchanged the arms are independent and the mechanism must be restated as two parallel programs rather than a demand-driven coupling.", "Assembly/abundance check: BN-PAGE or complex I in-gel activity and NDUFS/NDUFA protein immunoblots should show increased assembled complex I in APOE4; increased transcripts with unchanged assembled complex I would break step 4.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: untargeted lipidomics should show no coherent APOE4 shift in glycerophospholipid class composition or acyl-chain unsaturation beyond what accompanies lysosomal expansion; a strong, coherent phospholipid-remodeling signature would indicate the membrane-remodeling mechanism was wrongly rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for the CLEAR/lysosome-biogenesis program - the transcription factors TFEB and MITF, multiple v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C), and acid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK) plus LAMP1 and RAB7A. Inferred, not measured: a physically larger and more hydrolase-loaded endolysosomal compartment with a correspondingly larger proton-pumping (ATP-consuming) load.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): Transcripts for the two committed, effectively irreversible glycolytic steps are lower in APOE4 (HK2, PFKP) even though glucose-uptake transcripts and HIF1A are higher (SLC2A1, SLC2A3, HIF1A). Inferred: reduced capacity to generate cytosolic glycolytic ATP per glucose taken up, so glycolysis cannot be the elastic ATP source for the enlarged lysosomal load. This step is the weakest link and is partly contradicted by the HIF1A/GLUT direction (see analysis.md).", "Step 3 (measured abundance): Carbon delivery into the matrix is transcriptionally reinforced - mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2, citrate/malate-aspartate/adenine-nucleotide carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A11, SLC25A5) and TCA-cycle enzymes (MDH1, OGDH, DLD, ACO2). Inferred: increased pyruvate oxidation and matrix NADH production; flux was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): The NADH-oxidising machinery is coherently increased - every detected complex I subunit is up (21/21; e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8) together with the assembly factor NDUFAF4, ATP-synthase subunits (ATP5ME, ATP5F1B), and matrix protein import (TOMM22, TIMM44). Inferred: greater complex I capacity, proton-motive force and oxidative ATP output; assembled-complex amount and respiration are not observed.", "Step 5 (inferred coupling, the proposed bottleneck): Because glycolytic commitment is transcriptionally down while lysosomal proton pumping is up, the ATP that maintains lysosomal lumenal acidity in APOE4 is preferentially supplied by complex I-driven oxidative phosphorylation. Complex I capacity therefore becomes the rate-limiting node controlling lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity and cargo degradation in APOE4.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): Increased electron flux is accompanied by higher matrix/membrane antioxidant transcripts (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4), consistent with, but not proof of, elevated respiratory-chain electron leak; APOE4 microglia are predicted to have little bioenergetic reserve, so any complex I restriction should convert directly into degradative (lysosomal) failure rather than being buffered by glycolysis.", "Step 7 (context, not a required link): Higher APOE, TREM2, ABCA7 and SCARB1 transcripts are consistent with an increased lipoprotein/scavenger cargo load reaching this compartment, which would raise the degradative demand the bottleneck must meet; the cargo itself was not measured."], "title": "Complex I-dependent oxidative ATP supply becomes the load-bearing energy source for an expanded lysosomal degradative compartment in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04512111129755865, "cosine_similarity": 0.15838478786713553, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6342880258899677, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04512111129755865, "cosine_similarity": 0.15838478786713553, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6342880258899677, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.466566, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 394}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_033", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (every row has |effect|\u003e1) and not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level enrichment was therefore tested against the supplied list itself, which is already shifted upward, and absolute enrichment against the true transcriptome cannot be computed from these files.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are not on the same scale as the protein log2 fold changes and the two modalities are compared only by direction.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes, so a decreased spot containing CTSB/HEXB/CTSD/ATP6V1E1 is treated as ambiguous directional counter-evidence, never as identification of a specific protein.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for the availability, not the activity, of the encoded machinery; no engulfment rate, actin or myosin activity, lysosomal pH, protease activity, cargo flux or subcellular localisation was measured in these data.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype is the intended variable, but a difference in microglial maturation state or in microglia/astrocyte composition between wells could also produce a coordinated leukocyte-module shift; the fact that CSF1R, C1QA/B/C, IRF8, AIF1, MS4A4A/MS4A6A and CD33 are all higher in APOE4 argues against simple loss of microglial content but does not exclude a state shift (S100B is +6.0).", "Causality has not been established by these observations; all directional and flux statements are hypotheses to be tested by the perturbations below."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by coordinated loss of a leukocyte actomyosin/engulfment transcript module (SPN, MYH9, FAM49B/CYRIB, ARHGAP30, MYO1F, RAC2, DOCK8, PTPRC, LAPTM5) together with loss of the dominant microglial endolysosomal protease transcript CTSS, while lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and TFEB transcripts rise no more than other broadly expressed housekeeping families and the corresponding protein spots do not rise. We therefore propose that the rate-limiting step is cargo capture and delivery into the degradative compartment (plus a shift in luminal protease composition), not the biosynthetic capacity of the lysosome; increased hydrolase transcript dosage is predicted to be insufficient to restore cargo clearance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating flux-versus-capacity test: in a pulse-chase with fluorogenic cargo (pHrodo/DQ-BSA-labelled myelin, apoptotic-cell membranes or oxLDL), APOE4 microglia should show a lower initial internalisation rate per cell than isogenic APOE3, while the degradation rate normalised to the amount actually internalised should be equal or greater. If APOE4 internalises cargo at the same or a higher rate but degrades each internalised unit more slowly, the delivery-bottleneck mechanism is falsified and a capacity/processing bottleneck is favoured instead.", "Capacity-augmentation test: raising lysosomal biogenesis in APOE4 microglia (TFEB overexpression or mTORC1 inhibition sufficient to raise hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts) should NOT normalise bulk cargo clearance or lipid accumulation. Full rescue of clearance by TFEB augmentation alone would weaken the mechanism.", "Phenocopy test: acute myosin-II inhibition (blebbistatin/para-nitroblebbistatin) or Rac1/WAVE-complex inhibition in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 cargo-clearance deficit without lowering hydrolase transcripts; failure to phenocopy would weaken step 2.", "Protease-composition test: APOE4 microglia should show selectively reduced CTSS-attributable proteolytic activity (loss of the CTSS-selective-inhibitor-sensitive fraction of Z-VVR-AMC cleavage, or reduced CTSS-cleaved substrate such as invariant-chain processing) despite unchanged or increased total cathepsin B/D activity. Equal or higher CTSS-selective activity in APOE4 would falsify step 3.", "Protein-level test of the capacity claim: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS in purified APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show that mature CTSB, CTSD, HEXB and ATP6V1E1 protein do not increase in proportion to their transcript increases. A proportional protein increase would weaken step 5 and reopen a genuine lysosomal-expansion interpretation.", "Specificity control: correcting for the list-wide up-shift, the leukocyte actomyosin module should remain an outlier in a properly normalised whole-transcriptome or spike-in-controlled measurement. If, in unbiased data, SPN/MYH9/FAM49B/ARHGAP30/CTSS are not reduced relative to a correctly normalised baseline, the primary evidence for this mechanism disappears."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: in a differential-expression list that is globally shifted upward (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, 77% positive, mean +1.39 in the unspecified reported log base), a coherent leukocyte actomyosin/adhesion/engulfment module is instead strongly reduced in APOE4 (module mean -3.8; SPN, MYH9, FAM49B, ARHGAP30, CTSS all in the bottom ~1st percentile of the list with adjusted p \u003c 1e-25; permutation p \u003c 2e-5 against the list background).", "Inferred (not measured): reduced Rac1-WAVE/CYRIB- and myosin-II-dependent force generation at the phagocytic cup lowers the rate of cargo engulfment, cup closure and phagosome scission, i.e. it lowers cargo flux entering the endolysosomal pathway; no engulfment rate, actin polymerisation or myosin activity was measured here.", "Measured: the endolysosomal protease repertoire is remodelled rather than uniformly expanded - CTSS falls (-5.57, 0.7th percentile) while CTSB, CTSD and CTSK rise, and the two mannose-6-phosphate receptors move oppositely (M6PR -1.72, IGF2R +2.02). Inferred: altered hydrolase sorting balance and a luminal protease composition that is shifted away from the CTSS-dependent activity that normally dominates microglial endolysosomal proteolysis.", "Measured: acid hydrolase, v-ATPase and CLEAR-annotated transcripts are elevated (lysosomal composite mean +2.71, permutation p ~0.001-0.009 versus list background; TFEB +2.38), but this elevation is not larger than that of unrelated broadly expressed families in the same list (EIF genes mean +3.86, p=0.0014; NDUF genes mean +2.99, p=0.0027), and it collapses when the three largest values are removed (p=0.11). Inferred: the apparent lysosomal-biogenesis signal is largely the global list-wide up-shift, not a pathway-specific induction.", "Measured counter-signal at the protein level: spots whose candidate lists include CTSB/HEXB (protein_spot:067, -1.00), CTSD/CTSB (protein_spot:058, -0.85), CTSD (protein_spot:069, -1.38) and ATP6V1E1 (protein_spot:064, -1.20; protein_spot:065, -0.93) are decreased in APOE4. Inferred: raised hydrolase transcripts are not converted into proportionally raised degradative protein pools, so hydrolase gene dosage is unlikely to be the limiting variable.", "Net inferred state (not measured here): internalised lipoprotein, lipid and membrane cargo enters the APOE4 endolysosomal system more slowly and is processed by a compositionally altered protease set, so cargo residence time and undegraded substrate load rise; the TFEB/CLEAR transcript rise is interpreted as a downstream or coincident response, not as evidence of restored degradative flux."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are limited at actomyosin-dependent cargo delivery into the endolysosome, not at lysosomal hydrolase capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.029354207436399216, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0406130819285512, "cosine_similarity": 0.1576156251617164, "direction_accuracy": 0.05016181229773463, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_033", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6334789644012945, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.029354207436399216, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0406130819285512, "cosine_similarity": 0.1576156251617164, "direction_accuracy": 0.05016181229773463, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6334789644012945, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8443325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 395}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |effect| \u003e= 1.00, 77% positive, mean +1.39); absence of a gene (e.g. G6PD, GSR, TXNRD1/2, CAT, SOD1/2, NFE2L2, HMOX1, SQLE, HMGCR) means it was not in the supplied selection, NOT that it is unchanged. All enrichment statements are made against the internal background of the supplied rows, not against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative ranking and set-versus-background comparisons are used, never absolute fold-change biology.", "The global positive RNA shift is treated as a possible normalization/compositional or selection artefact; the hypothesis relies on contrasts within the dataset (oxidative/thiol sets high, PPP genes low) rather than on the shift itself.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios, membrane potential, peroxide levels, lipid peroxidation and localization were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred only.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:017 (CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5) and protein_spot:077 (PRDX2 plus keratins) are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration and could equally reflect the non-redox candidates.", "Replicate number and dispersion were not supplied ('not supplied in workbook'), so effect sizes cannot be weighted by precision; the microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcriptional shift toward mitochondrial substrate oxidation and thiol-peroxidase capacity while the NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate/malic-enzyme arm is not co-induced (PGD, TALDO1, NADK below the internal background) and SREBP-type sterol/desaturation genes are up. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step for peroxide detoxification in APOE4 microglia is cytosolic and mitochondrial NADPH regeneration rather than peroxiredoxin/GPX4 protein amount, and that NNT up-regulation makes thiol-peroxidase recycling dependent on the mitochondrial proton-motive force, so that reductant demand from sterol and fatty-acid desaturation biosynthesis and from peroxide clearance become mutually competing. Causality is not established by these data; only steady-state RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Reductant-supply test: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, the NADPH/NADP+ ratio (and GSH/GSSG) should be lower in APOE4 at baseline despite the higher peroxiredoxin/GPX4 transcript levels. If APOE4 shows an equal or higher NADPH/NADP+ ratio, the central bottleneck claim is falsified.", "PMF-coupling discriminator: brief low-dose uncoupling (FCCP) or NNT knockdown should cause a markedly larger increase in 2-Cys peroxiredoxin hyperoxidation/dimer shift and in mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation in APOE4 than in APOE3. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond equally, the NNT/proton-motive-force dependence step is weakened and a simple 'more antioxidant protein' interpretation is favoured.", "Sufficiency test: G6PD knockdown (or 6-aminonicotinamide) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 peroxide-sensitivity and cholesteryl-ester/lipid-droplet phenotype, whereas restoring cytosolic NADPH in APOE4 (e.g. cytosolic IDH1 overexpression) should normalise it. Failure of both directions falsifies the NADPH-supply mechanism.", "Competing-sink test: blocking the sterol/desaturation sink (statin plus DHCR24 or SCD inhibition) should raise NADPH/NADP+ and lower basal peroxide and lipid-peroxidation signal in APOE4 more than in APOE3. No change in APOE4 redox readouts after removing the sink would weaken the competition step.", "Peroxisomal-alternative discriminator (rejecting the assigned peroxisome framing): the data contain no PEX transcripts, only marginal gene:ACOX1 (+1.24, 39th percentile) and gene:CROT (+1.03, 25th percentile) with gene:ABCD1 down (-1.64), so we predict that peroxisome number and very-long-chain fatty-acid (C26:0) beta-oxidation flux are NOT increased in APOE4. If APOE4 microglia show increased peroxisome biogenesis and VLCFA oxidation flux, a peroxisomal-proliferation mechanism should replace this one.", "Ferroptosis discriminator: because gene:ACSL4 (-2.14) and gene:ALOX15 (-3.63) are down, we predict APOE4 microglia are NOT more sensitive to RSL3/erastin-induced ferroptotic death despite the redox-supply constraint; observing frank ferroptosis sensitisation would indicate a different (lipid-peroxidation-execution) mechanism than the reductant-supply bottleneck proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for pyruvate entry and TCA/anaplerotic steps are among the most extreme in the dataset (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17; set mean +5.41 vs background +1.39, permutation p=1e-4), and 43 OXPHOS-subunit transcripts are shifted up (mean +2.30, p=0.009). Inferred (not measured): higher electron-donor supply and respiratory-chain capacity, hence a larger potential superoxide/H2O2 source and a larger proton-motive force.", "Measured: glycolytic transcripts are NOT co-elevated (gene:HK2 -3.67, glycolysis set mean +0.67, below background) and the NADPH-regenerating arm is shifted down (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14, gene:ME1 +1.36 i.e. at the background median; 4-gene mean -0.85, one-sided permutation p=0.048). Inferred: reduced cytosolic NADPH (and NADP+) regeneration capacity per unit of oxidative and biosynthetic demand. NADPH/NADP+ itself was not measured.", "Measured: thiol-peroxidase and thiol-repair transcripts are coherently high (gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:TXNL1 +4.33, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:MSRA +2.64, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:PRDX5 +1.96; set mean +3.60, p=0.008), with weak protein corroboration in spots containing PRDX2 and CAT among their candidates (protein_spot:077 +1.07; protein_spot:017 +0.77). Inferred: increased peroxide-reducing protein capacity, all of which is catalytically useless without NADPH-driven re-reduction by thioredoxin/glutathione reductases (whose transcripts are absent from the supplied selected rows).", "Measured: gene:NNT is up (+2.88, 76th percentile). Inferred: a larger fraction of mitochondrial NADPH is generated by proton-motive-force-driven transhydrogenation, so matrix peroxiredoxin (PRDX3/PRDX5) and GPX4 recycling becomes coupled to membrane potential and is predicted to collapse under mild uncoupling or complex-I inhibition.", "Measured: an SREBP-type lipogenic/sterol program is up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29; set mean +2.43, p=0.054). Inferred: a large, reductant-consuming biosynthetic sink (sterol reduction steps and desaturation) drawing on the same constrained NADPH/NADH pools.", "Measured: lysosomal/degradative transcripts are strongly up (gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:TFEB +2.38; set mean +2.92, p=0.001), alongside gene:APOE +1.24 and gene:SCARB1 +8.24. Inferred consequence: lipid entering APOE4 microglia is routed to sterol esterification/storage and lysosomal handling rather than to reductant-yielding oxidation, making the reductant-limited redox state and the lipid-accumulation phenotype two faces of the same bottleneck."], "title": "NADPH-supply, not antioxidant-enzyme abundance, is the redox bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: peroxiredoxin/GPX4 recycling is pushed onto proton-motive-force-dependent NNT while PPP capacity falls and sterol/desaturase synthesis competes for reductant"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42080825610161354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.182221866220788, "cosine_similarity": 0.1555359616445078, "direction_accuracy": 0.3187702265372168, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.700126213592233, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42080825610161354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.182221866220788, "cosine_similarity": 0.1555359616445078, "direction_accuracy": 0.3187702265372168, "mean_absolute_error": 0.700126213592233, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.350772, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 396}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_009", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the local background of these 2212 selected rows (median effect +1.46), not against zero.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; the very large magnitudes (up to +15.5) are treated as ranks/relative magnitudes, not as fold-change estimates.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance and, less securely, for pathway flux; no metabolic flux, acetyl-CoA pool, lipid-droplet or lipid-species measurement is supplied.", "ACLY, FASN, ACACA, CPT1A, PLIN2 and ABCA1 were not measured in the supplied rows, so the acetyl-CoA-to-malonyl-CoA-to-palmitate step, the beta-oxidation entry step and the droplet-coat and efflux steps are inferred gaps, not observations.", "2D-gel protein spots contain up to six candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence for any lipogenic enzyme.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic and equally represented (as stated in the context metadata); replicate number is not supplied, so nominal p-values cannot be re-derived.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so some lipid substrate supply may be non-cell-autonomous and the RNA signal is assumed to derive from the microglial compartment."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated transcriptional program that raises mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA carbon handling and citrate export capacity (MPC2, OGDH, ACO2, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A1) alongside an alternative cytosolic acetyl-CoA route (ACSS2), while lowering upper glycolysis (HK2, PFKP), and simultaneously raises an SREBF1-associated esterification module (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT2, CHPT1, SOAT1). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting, genotype-discriminating step is the supply of cytosolic acetyl-CoA from mitochondrial citrate export, and that this supply is consumed by SCD-dependent monounsaturated acyl chain production and glycerolipid/sterol-ester esterification, so APOE4 microglia store lipid (monounsaturated triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and remodelled phospholipid) instead of oxidising or exporting it. Causality is not established by these data; only steady-state RNA and 2D-gel protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer test: with U-13C-glucose (and separately 1,2-13C-acetate) labelling of mock-treated isogenic microglia, APOE4 cells should incorporate a higher fraction of label into cellular palmitate, oleate and triacylglycerol than APOE3 cells; if 13C incorporation into neutral lipid is equal or lower in APOE4 while stored lipid is still higher, the de novo/citrate-export mechanism is falsified and an uptake- or catabolism-driven explanation is favoured.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological inhibition of mitochondrial citrate export (CTPI-2) or SLC25A1 knockdown should collapse the APOE4-minus-APOE3 difference in neutral-lipid content without abolishing the difference in lysosomal hydrolase transcripts; persistence of the lipid difference under this block, or loss of the lysosomal transcript difference, would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572) should reduce APOE4 lipid storage and shift residual stored acyl chains toward saturated species; if the APOE4 lipid excess is unchanged in composition and amount under SCD inhibition, the SCD-dependent esterification step is wrong.", "Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show higher triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester with an increased monounsaturated-to-saturated acyl ratio and increased ceramide/hexosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin (consistent with elevated gene:SMPD1 and gene:GBA); an APOE4 lipid phenotype dominated instead by unchanged neutral lipid with only free-cholesterol or polyunsaturated phospholipid changes would weaken the mechanism.", "Blocking uptake (SCARB1 blockade or lipoprotein-depleted medium) should only partially reduce the APOE4 lipid excess, whereas combined SCARB1 blockade plus citrate-export inhibition should abolish it; if SCARB1 blockade alone abolishes the difference, the primary bottleneck is uptake, not cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply.", "Rejected alternative, testable: if quantitative phagocytosis/endocytosis assays (pHrodo bead, myelin or synaptosome uptake) show a large APOE4 deficit that fully accounts for the lipid phenotype, the cytoskeletal/phagocytic mechanism should be preferred over this metabolic one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher steady-state transcripts for the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and TCA/malate-aspartate enzymes (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) with lower upper-glycolytic transcripts (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP) are inferred to shift pyruvate away from lactate towards mitochondrial entry; the flux itself is not measured.", "Increased gene:SLC25A1 (mitochondrial citrate/malate carrier) transcript is inferred to raise citrate export capacity into the cytosol, with gene:ACSS2 providing a parallel acetate-derived cytosolic acetyl-CoA route; cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool size and ACLY were not measured and are inferred, not observed.", "Elevated gene:SREBF1 transcript is inferred to reflect increased SREBP-1 dependent transcriptional output, consistent with the coordinated rise of its canonical lipogenic targets rather than a general sterol program (gene:LDLR and gene:INSIG1 rise only modestly and cholesterol-synthesis genes are not enriched above the local background).", "The acetyl-CoA and malonyl-CoA-derived acyl chains are inferred to be desaturated by SCD (gene:SCD, one of the most significant single rows) and esterified through the glycerolipid pathway (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1), the Lands-cycle phospholipid remodelling enzymes (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1) and the sterol-esterifying enzyme (gene:SOAT1).", "In parallel, increased lipoprotein-lipid uptake capacity (gene:SCARB1) and an expanded lysosomal hydrolase/acidification program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) are inferred to deliver additional catabolically released fatty acids, sterols and sphingoid backbones to the same cytosolic esterification step.", "Because esterification capacity is upregulated while fatty-acid activation transcripts fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 decreased), the net predicted consequence is genotype-specific accumulation of stored neutral lipid enriched in monounsaturated (SCD product) species and of remodelled phosphatidylcholine, rather than increased complete beta-oxidation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial citrate-derived acetyl-CoA into SREBF1/SCD-dependent neutral-lipid esterification rather than complete oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3173115976812022, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16708108624834184, "cosine_similarity": 0.15529623225430253, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6852038834951456, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3173115976812022, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16708108624834184, "cosine_similarity": 0.15529623225430253, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6852038834951456, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2786065, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 397}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Unverified background knowledge: RAB27A can participate in docking and release of multivesicular-endosome-derived extracellular vesicles. The relevant sphingolipid cargo must use this route in these microglia, and other release machinery must not fully compensate.", "Unverified background knowledge: RAB7A participates in late-endosomal/lysosomal routing; SMPD1 and GBA can generate ceramide through sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide hydrolysis, respectively; the other cited hydrolases/cofactor participate in lysosomal glycosphingolipid processing. These functional assignments were not externally verified.", "The RAB27A RNA decrease must produce a limiting reduction in functional protein. None of the supplied protein spots lists RAB27A, SMPD1 or GBA among its candidates, and all spots have multiple candidate genes; they cannot confirm these protein changes.", "Cargo reaches sufficiently acidic lysosomes containing active, appropriately localized hydrolases. RNA abundance does not measure enzyme maturation, activity, lysosomal pH, lipid flux or compartmental lipid abundance.", "The hydrolase transcriptional program is partly a response to retention, rather than entirely an independent APOE4-associated differentiation or activation program. Higher TFEB RNA alone does not demonstrate TFEB activation.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base. Missing genes cannot be interpreted as unchanged or absent, and pathway direction counts are descriptive rather than unbiased enrichment evidence.", "The isogenic day-30 microglia/astrocyte co-culture comparison does not establish a microglia-intrinsic mechanism. Biological replicate information, baseline expression and cell-state proportions are unavailable; altered maturation, astrocyte input or broader organelle remodeling may explain the pattern."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 microglia are hypothesized to have a primary bottleneck in RAB27A-dependent release of sphingolipid-bearing late-endosomal extracellular vesicles. Reduced export retains endocytosed membrane for lysosomal processing, eliciting a compensatory hydrolase program and increasing the fraction of internalized sphingomyelin converted to intracellular ceramide. Vesicle release, lipid conversion and ceramide abundance were not measured; this causal mechanism remains unestablished.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Proposed pulse-chase experiment: under matched astrocyte conditions, load microglia with sphingomyelin labeled in its sphingoid backbone, match initial internalized tracer, and quantify tracer recovery over time in intracellular compartments and released extracellular vesicles per viable microglial cell. APOE4 should show lower fractional vesicle export and greater lysosomal residence/conversion into tracer-derived ceramide. Equal or higher fractional export, or no increase in intracellular tracer-derived ceramide despite verified substrate delivery, would weaken this mechanism.", "Discriminating causal perturbation: restore functional RAB27A in APOE4 microglia to the APOE3 protein level, with verified localization, an inactive control and matched uptake/viability. Restoration should increase fractional export and reduce intracellular tracer residence and ceramide conversion before hydrolase RNA normalizes; reciprocal RAB27A reduction in APOE3 should reproduce the partitioning defect. Failure of a verified functional rescue, or failure of reciprocal depletion to phenocopy the defect, would weaken RAB27A as the primary bottleneck.", "Branch-order test: selectively reduce SMPD1 activity in APOE4 microglia while leaving RAB27A unchanged. This should reduce conversion of preloaded labeled sphingomyelin into ceramide without correcting the primary fractional vesicle-export defect. If SMPD1 reduction alone restores export whereas functional RAB27A restoration does not, a hydrolase-driven routing change would be favored over the proposed causal order.", "Alternative-mechanism test: acutely inhibit de novo sphingolipid synthesis with verified target engagement while tracking preloaded sphingomyelin and controlling viability. This should not restore fractional export as effectively as RAB27A rescue. Normalized export after synthesis inhibition despite persistently reduced functional RAB27A would favor synthesis overload over the proposed release bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 versus APOE3 has lower RAB27A RNA (gene:RAB27A). The initiating inference is that this reduces correctly localized, functional RAB27A protein sufficiently to limit docking and release of late-endosomal extracellular vesicles; neither protein abundance nor docking activity was measured.", "This proposed release bottleneck reduces fractional export of sphingolipid-bearing membrane and prolongs its intracellular residence at matched uptake. Membrane retention and extracellular-vesicle cargo are predictions, not observations.", "Retained membrane becomes more available to the late-endosome-to-lysosome route. Higher RAB7A and LAMP1 RNA (gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1) is compatible with this routing capacity, but does not establish vesicle localization or delivery flux.", "Persistent cargo retention is proposed to elicit compensatory lysosomal gene expression. Higher TFEB, SMPD1, GBA, GM2A, HEXA, HEXB, GLA and acidification-subunit RNA is consistent with such a response (gene:TFEB, gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:GM2A, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H); TFEB nuclear activity and the direction of causation are inferred.", "If lysosomal acidity and mature hydrolase activity remain sufficient, prolonged substrate residence favors sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid hydrolysis, with more internalized sphingomyelin tracer converted to intracellular ceramide instead of exported. This predicts a change in cargo partitioning and turnover, without asserting an observed increase in any total lipid pool."], "title": "Reduced RAB27A-dependent vesicle release redirects sphingolipids toward lysosomal turnover"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.043052837573385516, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.030475742765668, "cosine_similarity": 0.15383661890908554, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6394789644012945, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.043052837573385516, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.030475742765668, "cosine_similarity": 0.15383661890908554, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6394789644012945, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8510975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Gene symbols parsed from observation IDs (e.g., gene:CTSB) correctly denote the canonical lysosomal/endosomal genes of the same name; no independent gene-function annotation was supplied with the file.", "Protein-spot candidate-gene lists represent plausible but unconfirmed identities; a spot cannot be attributed to a single protein, so protein-level claims are treated as weaker, associative evidence only.", "The RNA rows are a curated, differential-expression-selected subset (not an unbiased transcriptome), so the fraction and magnitude of lysosomal-gene induction may be inflated relative to a random gene set; no attempt is made to claim genome-wide enrichment statistics.", "Elevated transcript abundance is assumed to at least partially translate toward protein/enzyme production, but no direct enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, or cargo-degradation flux measurement is present in this dataset; all such flux/activity claims are explicitly inferred, not observed.", "The unspecified RNA log fold-change base is preserved as reported; relative comparisons within the dataset (which gene is larger/smaller) are valid regardless of base, but absolute fold-change magnitude interpretation is not made.", "No causal direction between APOE4 genotype and this transcriptional program is established by this cross-sectional discovery data; the described chain is a candidate mechanism, not a proven causal pathway."], "claim": "In APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-microglia/astrocyte co-cultures under mock treatment, a broad, coherent transcriptional program of lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits, together with the master lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors TFEB and MITF, is upregulated at the RNA level. This pattern is consistent with a compensatory increase in lysosomal biogenesis gene dosage that is occurring alongside, and may be attempting to offset, a discordant reduction in the exocytic/secretory-lysosome regulator RAB27A and the protease CTSS, plus mixed changes in mannose-6-phosphate-receptor trafficking genes (M6PR down, IGF2R up). We hypothesize that the primary bottleneck limiting endolysosomal cargo processing capacity in APOE4 microglia is not lysosomal hydrolase gene dosage itself (which is elevated) but a downstream step in cargo egress/exocytosis and selective proteolytic maturation (RAB27A- and CTSS-dependent), such that measured hydrolase transcript induction reflects an incompletely compensated processing deficit rather than restored degradative capacity.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown or pharmacological restoration of RAB27A activity (or CTSS re-expression) in APOE4 microglia, followed by a lysosomal cargo-clearance assay (e.g., DQ-BSA pulse-chase or fluorescent myelin/synaptosome degradation assay), should produce a measurable increase in degradation flux toward APOE3-like levels if RAB27A/CTSS is a rate-limiting bottleneck; failure of this rescue would weaken the hypothesized bottleneck role of RAB27A/CTSS specifically.", "If direct measurement of lysosomal proteolytic flux, lysosomal pH, or cathepsin enzymatic activity in APOE4 microglia is found to be equal to or greater than in APOE3 microglia (i.e., the elevated hydrolase/V-ATPase transcription fully and proportionally translates into increased functional degradative capacity with no evidence of cargo backlog), this would weaken the core claim that a downstream processing/exocytosis bottleneck exists despite transcriptional compensation.", "Bafilomycin A1 (V-ATPase inhibition) titrated to partially neutralize lysosomal pH should produce a disproportionately larger loss of cargo-clearance capacity in APOE4 than APOE3 microglia if APOE4 cells are already operating with a compensatory reliance on elevated V-ATPase subunit dosage; a similar or smaller relative loss in APOE4 would weaken this prediction."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 status is associated with strongly elevated RNA abundance of lysosomal hydrolases and structural/acidification genes (e.g., gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSH, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:MAN2B1, gene:SCARB2, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, gene:CLCN7, and all detected V-ATPase subunits gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F), measured as reported log fold change, not protein activity.", "The master lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factors TFEB and MITF are also elevated (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), consistent with (inferred, not measured) activation of a CLEAR-like transcriptional program, interpreted here as a compensatory response to unresolved cargo load rather than baseline homeostasis.", "Concurrently, transcripts governing lysosomal exocytosis/secretion (gene:RAB27A, down) and the cysteine protease gene:CTSS (down) are reduced, a discordant signal within the same pathway; retrograde/anterograde enzyme-trafficking receptor transcripts are also mixed (gene:M6PR down, gene:IGF2R up), so trafficking machinery does not scale uniformly with hydrolase transcription.", "Protein-spot abundance data show cathepsin-candidate spots moving in both directions (protein_spot:027, protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), which is consistent with (inferred) altered proteolytic maturation/processing (redistribution between precursor and mature forms) rather than a simple monotonic increase in total cathepsin protein; because each spot has multiple candidate genes, this cannot be attributed to a single identified protein.", "Retromer/sorting-related transcripts and protein spots (gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS18; protein_spot:044, protein_spot:075, protein_spot:076) are also altered, suggesting endosome-to-lysosome sorting components are part of the same discordant remodeling rather than isolated to hydrolases alone.", "Net inferred consequence (activity/flux not measured in this dataset): the combination of elevated hydrolase/V-ATPase gene dosage with reduced RAB27A/CTSS and mixed sorting-receptor transcripts is compatible with a model in which cargo degradation flux and/or lysosomal exocytic clearance remains rate-limited in APOE4 microglia despite, or because of, a compensatory transcriptional response, producing retained or altered undegraded cargo pools that are not directly observed here."], "title": "Compensatory TFEB/MITF-driven lysosomal biogenesis masks a downstream exocytosis/proteolysis bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03932955312787738, "cosine_similarity": 0.153650034395356, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6342880258899677, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03932955312787738, "cosine_similarity": 0.153650034395356, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6342880258899677, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5032483, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript abundance changes for TFEB, MITF, RAC2, ACTB, and the lysosomal/endosomal gene set are assumed to partially reflect corresponding changes in protein abundance or pathway activity; no protein-level measurement of TFEB, MITF, RAC2, or the endosomal trafficking proteins is available in this dataset to confirm this.", "The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected set of differentially expressed genes (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05 by construction), not an unbiased whole-transcriptome sample; percentile ranks are computed relative to this filtered set, not the full transcriptome, so 'enrichment' claims are relative to other already-significant hits, not to all expressed genes.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is not specified in the source data; relative percentile ranking rather than raw magnitude is used to reduce sensitivity to this ambiguity, but absolute fold-change comparisons (e.g., very large values such as DNM2 or VPS26A) are still reported at face value and may be inflated by a low-expression denominator.", "Each protein spot has multiple (3-6) candidate genes without unique identification; any protein-level agreement with a single candidate gene's RNA direction is treated as weak, non-exclusive corroboration rather than independent confirmation.", "No causal direction, cell-autonomous origin, or temporal order between the lysosomal-biogenesis and actin-suppression transcriptional signatures is established by this correlational, single-timepoint dataset."], "claim": "In isogenic Day-30 iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, APOE4 (relative to APOE3) shows a coordinated transcript-level increase in the MiT/TFE lysosomal biogenesis program (TFEB, MITF) and its downstream endo-lysosomal maturation/hydrolase targets (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, LAMP1, ATP6V0C, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1E1, NPC2, ABCA7), occurring together with a disproportionate reduction of core actin-engulfment transcripts (ACTB, RAC2, MYO1F, RAB27A) that lie in the extreme low tail of the measured differential-expression distribution. This pattern is consistent with (but does not prove) a mechanism in which lysosomal degradative/maturation capacity is transcriptionally primed in APOE4 microglia while the Rac2/actin-dependent step that forms and closes the phagocytic cup is comparatively under-supported, potentially limiting particle uptake independent of downstream degradative readiness.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction: in a live-cell phagocytic uptake assay (e.g., pHrodo-labeled synaptosome, myelin debris, or bead engulfment) paired with a downstream cargo-degradation readout in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, the mechanism predicts APOE4 microglia will show a reduced or unchanged initial particle engulfment/uptake rate relative to APOE3, while the intracellular degradation kinetics of already-internalized cargo (lysosomal clearance rate) will be equal to or faster in APOE4. Observing instead that APOE4 microglia show increased engulfment rate proportional to their increased lysosomal marker transcripts (i.e., both uptake and degradation move together) would weaken this mechanism and instead support a globally coordinated (non-bottlenecked) phagocytic upregulation.", "Perturbation prediction: restoring RAC2 activity (e.g., transducing constitutively active RAC2) or normalizing ACTB expression in APOE4 microglia is predicted to increase phagocytic engulfment rate toward APOE3 levels without requiring changes in TFEB/lysosomal gene expression. If this rescue fails to change engulfment rate, or if instead knocking down RAC2 in APOE3 microglia fails to reduce engulfment toward APOE4 levels, this would weaken the claim that reduced RAC2/ACTB transcript abundance is a limiting factor for engulfment capacity, suggesting the reduction is a downstream consequence rather than a contributing bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: TFEB and MITF transcripts are elevated in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), consistent with inferred (not directly measured) increased activity of the CLEAR/MiT-TFE lysosomal biogenesis transcriptional network.", "Measured: downstream CLEAR-network and endo-lysosomal maturation transcripts are elevated and sit in the upper 65th-95th percentile of the full measured differential-expression distribution, not merely at the dataset's global median shift (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:NPC2, gene:ABCA7) -\u003e inferred increase in endosome maturation and lysosomal hydrolytic/proteolytic transcript capacity.", "Measured: core actin monomer, Rho-family GTPase, and unconventional myosin transcripts required for actin-based particle engulfment and phagosome/secretory-lysosome trafficking are reduced to the extreme low tail (1st-10th percentile) of the same distribution (gene:ACTB, gene:RAC2, gene:MYO1F, gene:RAB27A) -\u003e inferred reduced transcript-level supply of the Rac2-actin engine that drives phagocytic cup formation and closure.", "Weak, non-specific protein-level corroboration: several 2D-gel protein spots that list ACTB or ACTG2 among 3-6 candidate genes show decreased abundance in the same direction as the ACTB transcript (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:079); because each spot cannot be attributed to a single gene, this is treated as suggestive only, not confirmatory.", "Inferred, unmeasured consequence: if transcript-level changes propagate to protein activity, the combination of a primed lysosomal maturation/degradation program with a comparatively suppressed actin/Rac2 engulfment machinery could produce an uncoupling in APOE4 microglia between phagocytic uptake capacity (potentially reduced or unchanged) and intracellular cargo-processing capacity (potentially increased) relative to APOE3.", "This uncoupling is proposed as a candidate primary bottleneck at the actin/Rac2-dependent engulfment step, positioned upstream of an otherwise upregulated lysosomal pathway; it does not establish that phagocytic flux is actually altered, only that the transcriptional inputs to the two steps move in opposite directions relative to the assay-wide background."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a transcriptionally uncoupled phagocytic program: TFEB/MITF-driven lysosomal biogenesis is induced while the core actin/Rac2 engulfment machinery is suppressed"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6346925566343042, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6346925566343042, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5138362, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_003", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The functional assignments of CTSS, CD74, CIITA, TFEB, and other pathway components are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "Lower CTSS RNA translates into lower mature CTSS activity in the relevant compartments. Transcript abundance alone does not establish protein abundance, protease maturation, localization, pH, or flux.", "Higher CD74 RNA increases substrate supply, and sufficient MHC-II machinery is present for invariant-chain processing to matter. MHC-II abundance, HLA-DM function, CD74 cleavage products, and antigen presentation were not supplied.", "Other proteases do not fully substitute for CTSS-dependent invariant-chain cleavage. Increased CTSB, CTSD, and CTSK RNA and the ambiguous CTSL-candidate spot protein_spot:052 leave compensation plausible.", "The genotype-associated expression pattern is not wholly explained by microglial state proportions, maturation, RNA normalization, or astrocyte-dependent effects. The comparison is described as isogenic, but biological replicate numbers and donor-level measurements are unavailable.", "The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, with an unspecified logarithm base; missing genes are unreported, not unchanged or absent. The broad positive skew is not evidence of globally increased RNA per cell.", "Each protein spot has multiple candidate genes, so spot effects cannot establish gene-specific protein abundance or RNA-protein discordance. Neither CTSS nor CD74 appears among those candidates. Lysosomal capacity, cargo pools, and causal direction remain unmeasured."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced CTSS expression is hypothesized to limit CTSS-dependent CD74 invariant-chain cleavage relative to CD74 supply, slowing MHC-II peptide-loading throughput despite broad lysosomal transcript induction. The primary bottleneck is this proteolytic processing step; reduced enzyme activity, retained cleavage intermediates, and impaired antigen presentation are predictions, not observed measurements or established causal effects.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In matched microglial states under the same mock co-culture conditions, APOE4 cells should show lower CTSS-selective enzymatic activity per viable cell and per lysosomal content, together with slower disappearance of MHC-II-associated CD74 cleavage intermediates in a pulse-chase normalized to starting CD74. Equal or higher CTSS activity and normal or faster fragment clearance would weaken the mechanism even if the RNA contrast reproduces.", "Restore lysosomally delivered, catalytically active CTSS in APOE4 microglia to the activity measured in APOE3, alongside a catalytically inactive CTSS control with matched abundance and delivery. Active CTSS should accelerate CD74-fragment clearance and improve processing-dependent peptide presentation without requiring reversal of the broad lysosomal RNA program. Failure to rescue after verified restoration of local CTSS activity, or equal rescue by inactive CTSS, would weaken CTSS cleavage as the primary bottleneck.", "Selective CTSS inhibition in APOE3 microglia, titrated to the CTSS activity measured in APOE4 and checked for off-target effects, should reproduce delayed CD74 processing. Failure to phenocopy that defect would weaken the proposed causal link.", "After controlling antigen uptake, viability, cell state, and surface MHC-II abundance, compare a validated processing-dependent whole-protein antigen with its cognate preprocessed peptide delivered by a protocol that loads accessible surface MHC-II. The APOE4 deficit and benefit of active CTSS restoration should be larger for whole-protein presentation, measured using the same cognate CD4 T-cell reporter. Comparable impairment of the peptide bypass, or an effect explained entirely by altered uptake, would weaken the processing-specific explanation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mechanism_steps": ["The APOE4-associated RNA pattern combines higher CD74 (+3.839) and CIITA (+1.496) with higher TFEB (+2.385) and LAMP1 (+1.377), in reported RNA log-fold-change units of unspecified base (gene:CD74, gene:CIITA, gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1). Increased synthesis and endolysosomal delivery of CD74-associated MHC-II complexes are inferred from this pattern, not measured.", "CTSS RNA decreases (-5.566; gene:CTSS), opposite to CTSB (+5.520), CTSD (+2.864), and CTSK (+7.363; gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK). The proposed causal link is that this selective transcript decrease lowers the amount of mature, active CTSS available in antigen-processing compartments; no CTSS protein abundance or activity measurement establishes that link.", "Assuming CTSS activity falls while CD74 supply increases, CTSS-dependent terminal invariant-chain proteolysis becomes rate-limiting. The role of CTSS in this cleavage is unverified background knowledge, and insufficient compensation by other proteases is an explicit assumption.", "Slow cleavage is predicted to prolong the residence of MHC-II-associated CD74 fragments, including a p10-like intermediate, and delay productive peptide loading. These molecular pools, their localization, and their turnover were not measured. Higher lysosomal machinery transcripts do not establish either functional compensation or a generalized loss of lysosomal capacity.", "Delayed loading is predicted to lower the efficiency of presenting selected processing-dependent protein antigens to cognate CD4 T cells. This functional outcome remains unmeasured, and the upstream route connecting APOE4 to selective CTSS repression is unresolved."], "title": "A selective CTSS bottleneck limits endolysosomal CD74 processing in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_003", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.685014, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_013", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["CTSS involvement in endolysosomal CD74/invariant-chain cleavage, CIITA involvement in MHC-II expression, and all other gene-function assignments are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "The selected RNA differences reflect relevant within-microglia biology rather than only cell-state composition, differentiation, astrocyte-derived effects or normalization. Biological replicate information and sample-level measurements are unavailable.", "The CTSS RNA decrease lowers active endolysosomal CTSS relative to CD74 processing demand, and the CD74 RNA increase raises substrate supply. Neither inference has protein-specific support: CTSS and CD74 are absent from all supplied protein-spot candidate lists.", "Other proteases do not fully compensate for CTSS-dependent invariant-chain cleavage. Their increased RNAs are substantive counter-evidence, and the hypothesis permits preserved or increased bulk lysosomal degradation.", "Functional MHC-II substrate is present. CTSS capacity remains limiting when antigen uptake, endolysosomal pH and delivery are matched; a primary acidification or trafficking defect is an alternative explanation rather than an established component of this mechanism.", "RNA effects retain their reported, unspecified logarithm base. All protein spots have multiple candidate genes, so spot changes establish neither individual protein abundance nor catalytic activity. No genomic variant measurements, molecular-pool measurements or flux measurements were supplied."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4-associated reduction of CTSS RNA is proposed to lower CTSS-dependent cleavage capacity for CD74/MHC-II invariant chain. This single primary bottleneck would impair invariant-chain removal and antigenic peptide loading despite increased abundance of several other lysosome-related RNAs. The proposed activity deficit and causal chain have not been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline test: in matched microglial states and with equal internalized antigen, APOE4 should show lower CTSS-specific endolysosomal activity, slower CD74-intermediate turnover and less antigenic peptide loading per available MHC-II. Measure CTSS activity with specificity controls, CD74 intermediates by pulse-chase, and compartment pH independently. Normal or higher CTSS activity together with normal CD74 processing would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Discriminating rescue: restore wild-type CTSS in APOE4 to the mature endolysosomal activity measured in APOE3, using a catalytically inactive CTSS construct as an expression and delivery control. At unchanged compartment pH, antigen uptake and CIITA/CD74 transcription, active CTSS should shorten CD74-intermediate persistence and improve antigenic peptide loading and presentation; inactive CTSS should not. Failure after verified restoration of mature, localized, active CTSS would strongly weaken the mechanism.", "Reciprocal perturbation: acutely reduce CTSS activity in differentiated APOE3 microglia to the APOE4 level using a selective intervention with verified target engagement. This should reproduce the CD74-processing delay and antigen-presentation deficit without requiring a fall in the broader lysosomal RNA program. Preserved processing despite the matched CTSS activity reduction would indicate compensatory capacity and weaken CTSS as the primary bottleneck.", "Alternative-explanation test: independently assess and, if abnormal, correct endolysosomal acidification or cargo delivery while tracking CTSS activity. Full correction of CD74 processing while CTSS activity remains at the proposed deficient APOE4 level, or failure of CTSS rescue whenever pH and delivery are controlled, would favor those alternatives and weaken a primary CTSS-capacity mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured transcriptional contrast: CTSS RNA is lower in APOE4, whereas CD74 and CIITA RNAs are higher (gene:CTSS, gene:CD74, gene:CIITA). These abundance differences motivate the mechanism; they do not identify how APOE4 regulates CTSS.", "Inferred primary bottleneck: lower CTSS RNA produces less mature, catalytically active CTSS in endolysosomes, reducing CTSS-dependent invariant-chain cleavage capacity. CTSS protein identity, maturation, localization and activity were not measured.", "Inferred substrate-capacity mismatch: if increased CD74 RNA increases invariant-chain supply, cleavage demand exceeds the reduced CTSS capacity. Increased CTSB, CTSD and CTSK RNAs provide potential compensation that the hypothesis assumes is insufficient for this particular processing step (gene:CD74, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK).", "Predicted processing consequence: incompletely cleaved CD74 intermediates persist on endosomal MHC-II complexes and delay invariant-chain removal. These intermediates and complexes are unmeasured molecular pools, not observed accumulations.", "Predicted functional consequence: delayed invariant-chain removal reduces antigenic peptide loading per available MHC-II and subsequent antigen presentation. Increased TFEB, LAMP1 and ATP6V1A RNAs can coexist with this selective defect, but do not establish lysosome number, acidification or degradative flux (gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A)."], "title": "A selective CTSS bottleneck in endolysosomal invariant-chain processing in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_013", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.9377415000000004, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All RNA effects quoted in the mechanism are reported log fold changes for APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment, with an unspecified logarithm base; they must not be converted to linear or log2 values. Protein effects alone are log2 fold changes. All abundance directions refer to APOE4 relative to APOE3.", "The RNA source is a selected differential-expression list: 1705/2212 rows (77.1%) are positive. Program coherence is compared with that background, without formal enrichment or gene-independence assumptions. The amino-acid/shuttle panel represents 10/26 queried members, all positive, median +3.81; pyruvate/PDH/TCA represents 8/30, all positive, median +3.74; lysosomal machinery represents 23/44, 22 positive and one negative, median +2.17. Panels overlap. Missing members, including unlisted partner subunits, are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transporter functions, GLS/GLUD1-to-TCA routing, respiratory coupling, redox shuttles and ATP-dependent lysosomal acidification are unverified background knowledge; no external literature or database was consulted. The causal ordering and increases in activity, flux and workload are hypothesis components, not measurements. No unique upstream regulator or exclusive carbon fuel is identified.", "The strongest competing interpretation is unsuccessful compensation for respiratory impairment. Four of six represented mitochondrial respiratory transcripts decrease, and lysosomal protein spots are mixed. The selected adaptation mechanism assumes adequate respiratory assembly, substrate supply and ATP delivery in the actual mock condition. Abundance data cannot distinguish these outcomes; a defect revealed only by a future challenge would not establish a baseline failure.", "Protein spots contain two to six candidate identities and may reflect mixtures or proteoforms. protein_spot:050 is \u22120.485 log2 fold change (ANXA1, KRT1, KRT10, MDH1, KRT9; p=.26), despite gene:MDH1 increasing; it cannot identify an MDH1 decrease. Supplied significance flags and p values are retained separately. No spot establishes any central enzyme activity.", "Coordinated lipid/cholesterol transcripts remain incompletely explained: gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SREBF1 +4.67 and gene:SCD +4.17 can accompany this state, but the mechanism does not determine their regulation or lipid routing. No lipid, glutamine, ATP or other molecular pool was measured.", "The working model attributes the state to microglial responses within the supplied co-culture. Unknown biological replication, baseline expression, microglial state proportions and astrocyte contributions limit that attribution. The prospective tests must resolve microglial metabolism and control cell number, viability and mitochondrial content. Causality has not been established."], "claim": "Under day-30 mock treatment in isogenic human iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 promotes a coordinated catabolic state in which increased GLS-dependent glutamine oxidation supplies usable mitochondrial ATP for expanded lysosomal work. The predicted outcome is maintained or increased constitutive lysosomal degradation, rather than an established energetic failure. This is a prospective causal hypothesis inferred from selected RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances; neither flux nor lysosomal function was measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline flux test: in matched day-30 mock co-cultures, substitute [U-13C5]glutamine isotopically without changing nutrient concentrations and resolve microglial labeling over time. The model predicts higher absolute oxidative glutamine flux in APOE4, including transfer through labeled glutamate/alpha-ketoglutarate into M+4 succinate, malate and first-turn citrate, accompanied by greater glutamine-supported ATP-linked respiration. Estimate flux using labeling kinetics, precursor enrichment, pool sizes and uptake/secretion rates; fractional labeling alone is insufficient. Parallel glucose tracing should quantify concurrent pyruvate use. Equal or lower oxidative glutamine flux, or increased labeling accompanied by reduced coupled ATP production, would weaken the selected adaptation mechanism and favor unsuccessful compensation.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: induce microglia-restricted GLS CRISPR interference using two independent guides in both genotypes during mock treatment, with matched target suppression and measurements before loss of viability. The model predicts a larger APOE4 decrease in glutamine oxidative flux and ATP-linked respiration, followed by higher lysosomal pH and slower degradation of a standardized cargo pulse after normalization for uptake. Rescue with CRISPRi-resistant active GLS, but not catalytically inactive GLS, should restore the sequence. Verified glutamine-flux suppression without the predicted APOE4 lysosomal effect would weaken the proposed metabolic support link; equal normalized responses in both genotypes would weaken the claim that it differentiates APOE4.", "Prospective throughput test: before GLS perturbation, quantify ratiometric lysosomal pH, lysosomal volume and uptake-normalized degradation kinetics under mock conditions. The selected mechanism predicts preserved acidification and maintained or increased clearance despite expanded lysosomal machinery. Baseline alkalinization and impaired clearance accompanied by low coupled respiration would contradict successful adaptation. A phenotype appearing only during nutrient starvation or another added stress would indicate reduced reserve and would not validate an ongoing defect or the proposed increased baseline throughput."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["1. APOE4 is proposed to increase constitutive endolysosomal workload as part of a coordinated microglial state. Higher receptor/recognition transcripts (gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:C1QA +1.25, gene:C1QB +1.13, gene:C1QC +1.17) accompany higher lysosomal-program transcripts (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86). These measured RNA changes motivate an inferred increase in ATP demand for substrate processing; increased cargo uptake, TFEB nuclear localization and degradation activity are not observations.", "2. Increased amino-acid acquisition and glutamine catabolism are proposed to supply that demand: gene:SLC1A5 +1.55 and gene:SLC38A2 +4.45 support greater transport capacity, while gene:GLS +1.35 and gene:GLUD1 +3.17 support conversion of glutamine through glutamate into mitochondrial alpha-ketoglutarate. gene:SLC38A7 +7.46 is compatible with altered intracellular amino-acid handling. Transport direction, enzyme activity and all substrate pools remain inferred. protein_spot:020 is +0.379 log2 fold change, with candidates GLUD1, FSCN1, ENO1, G6PD and EPX; its p=.011 and reported_significant=false make it ambiguous compatibility evidence, not GLUD1 protein confirmation.", "3. Glutamine-derived carbon is proposed to undergo increased oxidative TCA metabolism, supported at the RNA level by gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:IDH3G +3.94 and gene:SDHB +1.65. Higher gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50 and gene:SLC25A13 +1.75 are compatible with increased redox-shuttle capacity; shuttle direction and net flux are unknown. Concurrent pyruvate oxidation is compatible with gene:MPC2 +7.98 and gene:PDP1 +3.00. Mixed glycolytic RNA changes (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:HK2 \u22123.67, gene:HK3 \u22121.12, gene:PFKM +2.41, gene:PFKP \u22123.08) do not establish a glycolytic block or exclusive glutamine dependence.", "4. Oxidative carbon use is proposed to generate more coupled respiratory ATP during mock treatment. All 33 represented members of a 76-member nuclear respiratory-subunit panel increase, including gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX6B1 +2.60 and gene:ATP5F1B +2.65. However, gene:MT-ND4 \u22121.80, gene:MT-CYB \u22122.32, gene:MT-CO2 \u22121.33 and gene:MT-ATP6 \u22123.35 oppose gene:MT-ND4L +1.95 and gene:MT-ND5 +1.93. Successful throughput therefore requires adequate assembled respiratory complexes despite the RNA discordance; complex abundance, membrane potential, respiration and ATP production remain unmeasured.", "5. The additional usable mitochondrial ATP is proposed to sustain V-ATPase-dependent acidification and degradation by the expanded lysosomal machinery. Supporting RNA includes gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:HEXA +5.68 and gene:HEXB +2.17 together with the hydrolases in step 1. gene:CTSS \u22125.57 is an important exception. protein_spot:053 +1.536 log2 fold change (TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1) is compatible, but protein_spot:064 \u22121.202 (ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1) and protein_spot:067 \u22121.000 (PSMA3, ACTG2, CTSB, HEXB, LRIF1) challenge this step. Each spot retains all candidate identities and cannot establish an individual protein change. Increased lysosomal throughput is the proposed functional consequence, not a measured result."], "title": "Glutamine-supported mitochondrial ATP production sustains lysosomal remodeling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.026418786692759294, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0407011438550256, "cosine_similarity": 0.1532977966139802, "direction_accuracy": 0.045307443365695796, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6373851132686084, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.2454359999999998, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 4}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_054", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; all claims use within-list ranks and medians rather than absolute fold changes, so no base is assumed.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; 77.1% of effects are positive with median +1.459, so pathway claims are made only as displacement relative to this list-wide background, and absent genes (PKM, LDHA, GAPDH, G6PD, TFAM, POLG, PPARGC1A) are treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein and complex-assembly capacity; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, membrane potential, ROS and mtDNA copy number were not measured here.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as ambiguous; no spot is used as evidence for a uniquely identified mitochondrial protein.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcripts are assumed to be quantified comparably between genotypes; because they are among the most abundant transcripts, a compositional/normalisation difference between the two lines could mimic their relative decrease.", "Biological replicate structure is not supplied, so the reported p-values may reflect cell-level pseudoreplication rather than independent differentiations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated transcript up-shift of the machinery that delivers glucose-derived carbon into the mitochondrial matrix and oxidises it (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, ACO2, OGDH, IDH3B/G, SDHB, MDH1/GOT1 shuttle, SLC25A1/SLC25A11) together with nuclear-encoded electron transport chain subunits, while the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) sit at the bottom of the same distribution; we hypothesise that the resulting deficit of mtDNA-encoded core subunits is the rate-limiting step (bottleneck) for assembly of respiratory complexes, so that inferred substrate/electron delivery outruns assembled respiratory capacity in APOE4, producing a reduced-state, ROS-prone mitochondrial compartment that is poorly buffered because oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD, TALDO1) are concurrently among the lowest in the list. Causality is not established by these data; only relative abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in matched APOE4 and APOE3 microglia, extracellular flux analysis with U-13C glucose tracing should show APOE4 has equal or higher fractional m+2 labelling of citrate/glutamate and higher basal oxygen consumption, but lower FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration and lower spare respiratory capacity when normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20). If APOE4 maximal respiration per mitochondrial mass is equal to or greater than APOE3, the bottleneck step (Step 4/5) is falsified.", "Blue-native PAGE / in-gel activity of APOE4 versus APOE3 mitochondria should show reduced assembled complex I, III, IV and V holoenzyme relative to total nuclear-encoded subunit protein, with an increased unassembled nuclear-subunit pool. Normal holoenzyme stoichiometry would weaken the mitonuclear-imbalance mechanism and favour a purely transcriptional-compensation interpretation.", "Direct, composition-independent quantification (spike-in normalised RT-qPCR or single-molecule FISH) of MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 per cell, plus mtDNA copy number, should confirm a genuine APOE4 deficit. If per-cell mtDNA-encoded transcripts and mtDNA copy number are unchanged, the observed MT-gene decrease is a normalisation artefact and Step 4 fails.", "Blocking pyruvate entry with the MPC inhibitor UK5099 (or MPC2 knockdown) should reduce mitochondrial superoxide (MitoSOX) and 4-HNE adducts more in APOE4 than APOE3 without a proportionally larger ATP drop, because APOE4 electron supply is predicted to be in excess of assembled capacity. Equal or larger ATP loss in APOE4 with no ROS benefit would weaken Step 5.", "Because PGD/TALDO1 transcripts are low, APOE4 microglia should show lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio and lower oxidative pentose-phosphate flux (1,2-13C glucose) and greater viability loss after buthionine sulfoximine or menadione challenge; equal NADPH/NADP+ and equal stress sensitivity would falsify Step 3 while leaving Steps 1-2 intact.", "Raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (mitochondrially targeted TFAM overexpression or allotopic expression of an affected subunit) should selectively increase maximal respiration and lower ROS in APOE4 towards APOE3 values; no genotype-selective rescue would argue the difference lies upstream in substrate handling rather than in complex assembly."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry higher relative transcript levels for mitochondrial pyruvate import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54) and for TCA enzymes (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:SDHB), which we interpret as increased capacity, not measured flux, for routing pyruvate-derived carbon into the TCA cycle.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Upper glycolysis is not coordinately raised - gene:HK2 and gene:PFKP fall far below the list-wide median while glucose transporters gene:SLC2A1 and gene:SLC2A3 and gene:GPI, gene:PFKM, gene:ENO1 rise - consistent with glucose carbon being passed through to pyruvate oxidation rather than accumulating in a glycolytic/pentose branch; the branch-point split is inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred redox buffering): Oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1 lie at the 19th and 9th percentiles of the same effect distribution, so cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity is inferred to lag behind the raised mitochondrial oxidative program (NADPH itself was not measured).", "Step 4 (measured RNA, primary bottleneck): Nuclear-encoded respiratory subunit transcripts are coherently high (37 genes, median +2.64, permutation p = 0.0016 against the list background) whereas the six measured mtDNA-encoded subunits are low (median -1.56, p = 0.015; nuclear-minus-mitochondrial median difference +4.20, permutation p = 1e-4). We propose the limiting pool is the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core of complexes I, III, IV and V, creating mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance; unassembled nuclear subunits and assembly state were not measured.", "Step 5 (inferred activity/flux): With substrate delivery capacity raised but holoenzyme assembly limited by the mtDNA-encoded cores, matrix NADH/FADH2 supply is inferred to exceed assembled electron-transport capacity, giving a more reduced ubiquinone/NADH pool, lower spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass, and increased electron leak. No respirometry, membrane potential or ROS measurement is present in these data.", "Step 6 (measured protein spots, weak and ambiguous): Antioxidant-containing spots are modestly increased (protein_spot:017 candidates include CAT, protein_spot:077 candidates include PRDX2) and gene:PRDX3 and gene:GPX4 are above the list median, consistent with, but not diagnostic of, a chronic peroxide load arising from Step 5; each spot has several candidate genes and cannot identify a single protein."], "title": "Mitonuclear ETC subunit imbalance caps oxidative capacity in APOE4 microglia despite an up-shifted pyruvate-to-TCA carbon delivery program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.02837573385518591, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05041215502788233, "cosine_similarity": 0.15318495271008242, "direction_accuracy": 0.04854368932038835, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6344757281553398, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.02837573385518591, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05041215502788233, "cosine_similarity": 0.15318495271008242, "direction_accuracy": 0.04854368932038835, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6344757281553398, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.434309, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 398}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_050", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e= 1.00, no values between -1.004 and +1.000), so 77% of rows being positive is a selection/normalisation artefact as much as a biological global shift; every enrichment claim above is made against the internal background (median +1.46), not against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and values reach +15.46, which is implausible for a conventional log2 ratio of an abundant transcript; effects are therefore used ordinally (percentile ranks) and not as fold-changes.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel-style features with 2-6 candidate genes each (208 unique candidates over 92 spots, keratins and ACTB recurring), so no spot uniquely identifies a protein; spot-level statements are treated as weak, non-identifying evidence.", "Transcript increases are assumed to reflect at least a directional attempt to increase the corresponding activity; the bottleneck argument assumes that a genuine increase in lysosomal degradative capacity would have produced at least some coordinate increase in hydrolase-candidate spots.", "Pathway gene sets were defined by the analyst after inspecting top-ranked genes and were tested without correction for the number of sets tried, so the reported p-values are descriptive, not confirmatory.", "Key discriminating genes are absent from the supplied rows (ABCA1, NR1H3/LXR, PLIN2, CAT, SOD1/2, HMOX1, NQO1, GCLC, SLC7A11, LPCAT3, ACSL3, AIFM2, FASN, HMGCR, all PEX genes); their absence is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change.", "The cells are co-cultured with astrocytes and replicate numbers are not supplied, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous and their variance is unknown.", "No lipid, flux, activity, imaging or localisation measurement is supplied; every lipid-storage, degradation-rate and peroxidation statement is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, a strongly elevated scavenger-receptor/lipid-uptake transcript signal is accompanied by a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and V-ATPase transcript program that is NOT mirrored by any coordinate increase in protein spots whose candidate lists contain lysosomal hydrolases or V-ATPase subunits. We propose that luminal lysosomal degradation of internalized sphingolipid/sterol cargo is the rate-limiting step (the primary bottleneck), and that the resulting undegraded/recycled lipid carbon is diverted into SREBF1-SCD-CYB5R3-LPCAT1-dependent monounsaturated neutral-lipid and phospholipid storage rather than into peroxisomal beta-oxidation, yielding a peroxidation-resistant stored-lipid phenotype (ACSL4 and ALOX15 down, GPX4/PRDX/selenoprotein transcripts up). The assigned peroxisomal/oxidative-stress framing is rejected as primary: the peroxisomal transcript set is at background (Mann-Whitney p=0.46; ABCD1 -1.64, ACOX1 +1.24 versus a background median of +1.46) and no canonical NRF2/oxidative-stress transcripts (CAT, SOD1/2, HMOX1, NQO1, GCLC/GCLM, TXNRD1, SLC7A11) are present in the supplied rows. All statements are associative; causality is not established and all fluxes, activities and localizations below are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING (bottleneck test): direct lysosomal enzyme assays on APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia (GBA, HEXA/B, GAA, CTSB specific activity per lysosome, plus DQ-BSA/DQ-lipid degradation rate and LysoSensor pH) should show that APOE4 activity and degradation rate are flat or reduced despite the large transcript increases, with accumulation of the corresponding substrates (glucosylceramide, hexosylceramide, sphingomyelin). If APOE4 instead shows hydrolase activity and cargo-degradation rate increased in proportion to the transcripts, with no substrate accumulation, the primary bottleneck (Step 3) is refuted and the mechanism fails.", "DISCRIMINATING (rerouting test): SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content disproportionately in APOE4 relative to APOE3, shift the cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol pool toward saturated species, and increase C11-BODIPY lipid-peroxidation signal and ER-stress markers preferentially in APOE4. Equal effects in both genotypes, or no change in APOE4 droplet load, would weaken Steps 4 and 6.", "Lipidomics of the mock condition should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) cholesteryl esters and triacylglycerols and for hexosylceramide/sphingomyelin, without a dominant very-long-chain (C26:0) fatty-acid excess. A lipidome in which the APOE4/APOE3 difference is dominated by C26:0/VLCFA species would favour the rejected peroxisomal alternative over this mechanism.", "Ferroptosis challenge: APOE4 microglia should be relatively resistant to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) and to exogenous arachidonate/PUFA loading compared with APOE3, and this resistance should be abolished by SCD inhibition. Greater APOE4 sensitivity to RSL3 would falsify Step 6 (the peroxidation-resistance interpretation of ACSL4-down/ALOX15-down/GPX4-up).", "Capacity rescue: increasing lysosomal degradative capacity in APOE4 (TFEB overexpression combined with, or replaced by, recombinant GBA/acid-sphingomyelinase supplementation or acidifying nanoparticles) should lower stored cholesteryl ester and glycosphingolipid and secondarily lower SREBF1 and SCD transcripts. If TFEB overexpression raises hydrolase transcripts further without lowering stored lipid, the compensatory-transcription interpretation of Step 2 is supported but the capacity-limitation model must be revised toward a post-translational maturation or acidification defect.", "Quantitative immunoblot of individual hydrolases (CTSB, CTSD mature versus pro forms, HEXB, ATP6V1E1, GBA) should confirm that mature protein does not rise in APOE4 in proportion to transcript. Concordant protein increases matching the transcript ranks would show the protein-spot discordance was an artefact of spot ambiguity and would remove the main support for Step 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show a very high SCARB1 transcript effect (+8.22, 99.2nd percentile of the supplied rows) with smaller increases in CD36, LDLR, MERTK, TREM2, APOE and ABCA7. We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery flux of lipoprotein/lipid cargo into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (measured abundance): A coherent lysosomal luminal-hydrolase and acidification transcript program is elevated above the dataset background (GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1A +4.23, CTSD +2.86, GBA2 +2.63, TFEB +2.38; set median +3.54 versus background median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=0.0012). We read this as a compensatory transcriptional response, not as evidence of increased degradative capacity.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; inferred activity): Protein spots whose candidate gene lists include lysosomal hydrolases or V-ATPase subunits are not coordinately increased (mean +0.18 across 24 such spots versus +0.41 for the other 68 spots, Mann-Whitney p=0.55), and several are decreased (protein_spot:067 -1.00 with CTSB/HEXB candidates; protein_spot:058 -0.85 with CTSD/CTSB; protein_spot:064 -1.20 and protein_spot:065 -0.93 with ATP6V1E1). We infer that per-lysosome degradative capacity/activity does not scale with the transcript program, creating a luminal substrate backlog (glycosphingolipid, sphingomyelin, sterol ester cargo). Spot identity is ambiguous, so this step is the weakest link and is the one the discriminating experiment targets.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred flux): A lipogenic/desaturation-and-esterification arm is elevated above background (SREBF1 +4.67, CYB5R3 +4.66, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, LPCAT1 +3.07, CHPT1 +2.91, ACSS2 +2.93, ACAT2 +2.04, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25; set median +2.91, Mann-Whitney p=0.022). We infer increased monounsaturated fatty-acid supply (SCD with its CYB5R3/CYB5A electron-donor system) feeding esterification into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol droplets and PC remodeling, i.e. storage rather than disposal of the lipid load.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): The peroxisomal disposal route is not engaged: the peroxisomal transcript set sits at background (median +1.03, Mann-Whitney p=0.46), ABCD1 (very-long-chain acyl-CoA import) is decreased (-1.64, 15.6th percentile), ACOX1 (+1.24) and CROT (+1.03) are below the dataset median, and no PEX or CAT transcripts are supplied. We therefore infer that peroxisomal beta-oxidation is not the compensating sink for the excess lipid.", "Step 6 (measured abundance, inferred redox state): The lipid that accumulates is inferred to be peroxidation-resistant: ACSL4 (-2.14, 10.6th percentile) and ALOX15 (-3.63, 3.8th percentile) are among the more strongly decreased genes, while peroxide- and thiol-handling transcripts are above background (PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, SELENOW +5.47, GPX4 +2.79, MSRA +2.64, FTH1 +2.53, GSS +2.11; set median +2.79, Mann-Whitney p=0.0068). This is a lipid-peroxidation-defence configuration rather than an executed oxidative-stress response, since no NRF2 target transcripts are supplied and the single catalase-containing protein spot (protein_spot:017, +0.77) shares its identity with CORO1C and ENTPD5."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-catabolic throughput, not peroxisomal oxidation, is the APOE4 bottleneck: internalized lipid is rerouted into SREBF1/SCD-driven monounsaturated storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20836871838422627, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.014256957298804556, "cosine_similarity": 0.15188766896709183, "direction_accuracy": 0.24110032362459546, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7097669902912622, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20836871838422627, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.014256957298804556, "cosine_similarity": 0.15188766896709183, "direction_accuracy": 0.24110032362459546, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7097669902912622, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.46375075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 399}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_111", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all listed genes exceed |effect| 1, so enrichment was judged only against the internal background of this selected list (global mean effect +1.39 in the unspecified reported logarithm base, which is preserved and not converted).", "Measured transcript abundance is used only as a proxy for protein abundance and none of the activity, flux, assembly state, membrane potential or localisation statements are measured here; no metabolite, respirometry, mtDNA copy number or lipid measurement is present in the supplied data.", "The relative down-shift of MT- transcripts is assumed to reflect a genuine mitonuclear ratio difference rather than purely a library-size/compositional artefact of relative normalisation; this is the single most fragile assumption.", "The 92 protein spots have multiple candidate genes each and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used to assert a specific protein pool.", "Cells are a mixed microglia-astrocyte co-culture at one timepoint (Day 30) with unreported biological replicate structure, so genotype effects could be partly confounded by differences in culture composition or maturation state rather than cell-autonomous APOE4 action.", "Background pathway memberships (OXPHOS, TCA, lysosome, ISR) are unverified literature knowledge applied to gene symbols, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain, TCA and NADH-shuttle machinery (all 21 detected NDUF genes up; OGDH, MDH1, MPC2, DLD, GOT1, ACO2, SLC25A1/A5/A11 up) that is not accompanied by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 relatively lower). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for respiratory complex assembly: nuclear subunit and matrix-enzyme abundance rises with a lysosomal/lipid-catabolic substrate load, but assembled complex capacity cannot scale with it, so APOE4 microglia occupy a high-demand, assembly-limited oxidative state with a compensatory redox/proteostatic (HSPA9, PRDX3/PRDX5, GPX4, FTH1, DDIT3, EIF2AK3) and NADH-shuttle (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11) response and reduced reliance on committed glycolysis (HK2, PFKP, NAMPT down). Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute low-dose complex I inhibition (rotenone or piericidin) or MPC inhibition (UK5099) should reduce ATP-linked respiration, cellular ATP and phagocytic uptake substantially more in APOE4 than isogenic APOE3 microglia, whereas 2-deoxyglucose should be better tolerated by APOE4. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive to rotenone/UK5099 and more sensitive to 2-deoxyglucose, the assembly-limited oxidative mechanism is weakened.", "Respirometry: APOE4 microglia should show reduced maximal (FCCP-stimulated) and spare respiratory capacity per citrate-synthase activity or per mitochondrial mass, despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. Proportionally increased spare capacity would falsify Step 3.", "Assembly readout: blue-native PAGE or mitochondrial proteomics should show increased free/subassembled nuclear-encoded complex I subunits relative to assembled complex I and supercomplexes in APOE4, with mtDNA copy number and mt-transcripts per cell not increased. Normal holo-complex stoichiometry and unchanged nuclear-subunit-to-complex ratio would falsify the bottleneck.", "Normalisation control: absolute per-cell quantification (spike-in normalised RNA, or qPCR/smFISH on fixed cell numbers) should confirm nuclear OXPHOS transcripts up while MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-ND4/MT-CO2 are unchanged or reduced. If absolute counts show a uniform scaling of all nuclear transcripts with unchanged mtDNA-encoded transcripts, the compositional-normalisation explanation is favoured over the mitonuclear mechanism.", "Rescue: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM or mitochondrial transcription/translation support, or supplying an alternative oxidase such as NDI1/AOX to bypass assembly-limited complexes) should normalise spare respiratory capacity and reduce DDIT3/HSPA9/PRDX3 transcript elevation in APOE4 without altering the lysosomal-lipid gene programme. Rescue of the lysosomal programme instead of the redox/ISR programme would indicate the bottleneck lies upstream in lipid handling, not in respiratory assembly.", "Substrate dependence: in permeabilised-cell or substrate-restriction assays, APOE4 cells should show greater dependence on glutamine/fatty-acid-derived substrate and greater vulnerability to malate-aspartate shuttle inhibition (aminooxyacetate) than APOE3; equal shuttle dependence would weaken Step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_111", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia raise transcripts for lipid uptake and lysosomal catabolism (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR, TREM2, APOE; CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, GBA, HEXA, GAA, LAMP1, multiple ATP6V subunits, TFEB), which we infer increases delivery of lysosome-derived fatty-acid and acetyl-CoA substrate to mitochondria; substrate flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): Nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery is coordinately elevated above the strong upward shift of the selected DE list - complex I subunits (NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8, NDUFB6, NDUFA11), complex III/IV/V subunits (UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5ME, ATP5MC3), matrix enzymes (OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, DLD, MDH1, GOT1), the pyruvate carrier MPC2, and carriers SLC25A1/A5/A11 - consistent with an increased set-point for matrix NADH generation and oxidation.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred assembly): mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts do not follow (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 lower in APOE4). Because complexes I, III, IV and V each require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, we infer that assembled holo-complex number, not nuclear subunit abundance, becomes limiting, so respiration per unit of nuclear OXPHOS transcript falls.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred stress signalling): Assembly-limited electron transfer with sustained matrix input is inferred to produce unassembled-subunit and redox strain, matching the elevated mitochondrial chaperone/antioxidant/ISR transcripts HSPA9, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, TXNDC17, FTH1, DDIT3, EIF2AK3, ATF6 and elevated fission-associated FIS1.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred redox handling): Cytosolic NADH disposal is shifted onto the malate-aspartate shuttle (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11 strongly up) while committed glycolytic steps and NAD salvage are reduced (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2, NAMPT down) despite higher glucose transporters (SLC2A1, SLC2A3), which we interpret as reduced glycolytic ATP contribution rather than increased glycolytic flux.", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): The net predicted state is normal or only modestly increased basal respiration with reduced spare respiratory capacity and heightened sensitivity to complex I or pyruvate-carrier inhibition, narrowing the energetic reserve available for demand-driven microglial functions such as phagocytic clearance of lipid substrate."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch: APOE4 microglia expand nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts without matching mtDNA-encoded core subunits, creating an assembly-limited oxidative state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10070893180223756, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0994717772756465, "cosine_similarity": 0.1499394004188327, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_111", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6456925566343042, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10070893180223756, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0994717772756465, "cosine_similarity": 0.1499394004188327, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6456925566343042, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.791368, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 400}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_018", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 1705/2212 positive); directionality alone is weakly informative, so the argument rests on effect-size rank within this list and on modules that run against the 77% positive background. The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, UGCG, DEGS1, ASAH1, PSAP, GRN, LAMP2, MCOLN1, NPC1, MTOR) are unknown, not unchanged; no claim is made about de novo sphingolipid synthesis or about unmeasured lipid pools.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to translate partially into protein and enzymatic capacity. This is unverified here: 2D spots containing lysosomal candidates split in both directions, and every spot carries 2-6 candidate identities plus frequent keratin/actin contaminants, so no individual protein is treated as confirmed.", "Curated module membership was defined from standard pathway knowledge (unverified background knowledge) before inspecting directions; members were not chosen to make signs agree. Exception, disclosed: some secretory/motility candidates were first noticed in the top-40 down tail, so a prespecified-only subset was re-tested and only the exocytic/Golgi-transport module survived (11/18 down, p~0.001) while the actin/motility module did not (4/13 down, n.s.); the motility genes are therefore treated as descriptive, not as module-level evidence.", "Module statistics assume gene independence, which is false for co-regulated transcripts; the permutation and binomial values are descriptive calibrations against the selected list, not formal enrichment tests.", "Flux, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, cargo clearance rate, protein localization and lipid species are not measured in this dataset; all statements about routing, degradation and oxidative disposal are inferred.", "The protein-spot layer is assumed to derive from comparable APOE4-vs-APOE3 material; if it derives from a different sample set or condition, its compatibility value is further reduced.", "The mock condition contains no exogenous cargo challenge; any prediction of degradative insufficiency applies to a future challenge, not to the measured state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state change in membrane-cargo routing rather than by a single enzymatic lesion: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein internalization and esterification, for MiT/TFE-type lysosomal biogenesis (v-ATPase 20/20 up; hydrolases GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB in the extreme upper tail of the selected list), for hydrolase targeting/endosomal sorting, and for mitochondrial FAO/TCA/ETC are elevated, while the exocytic, TGN-retrieval and Golgi-directed transport limb is selectively reduced against a 77%-positive selected-list background (11/18 prespecified members negative, permutation p~0.001). We propose that a higher standing lipid/membrane cargo load in APOE4 drives one-way routing of cargo into an enlarged acidified degradative compartment whose catabolites are disposed of oxidatively, at the expense of secretory/recycling traffic. The sphingolipid arm (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, GBA2, SUMF1: 9/9 positive) is a prominent component but is not privileged: equally or more extreme non-sphingolipid hydrolases (GAA +9.96, CTSK +7.36, CTSB +5.52, NAGLU +5.87) argue against a sphingolipid-specific cause, and de novo sphingolipid synthesis genes (SPTLC1/2, SGMS1/2, UGCG, DEGS1, ASAH1) are absent from the supplied list and therefore unknown. Measured quantities are transcript and protein-spot abundances; degradative flux, acidification, lipid pools and localization are inferred, not observed, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective, discriminating (adaptation vs failed compensation): in day-30 mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, 4-MU activity assays for GBA, HEXA/HEXB and GAA plus mature CTSB/CTSD immunoblot and LysoTracker should show higher hydrolase activity and larger acidified compartment per cell, AND a pulse-chase of fluorescent myelin or oxLDL should be cleared at least as fast in APOE4. If activities and cargo clearance are unchanged or slower despite the elevated transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H), the successful-adaptation reading fails and failed transcriptional compensation for a degradative bottleneck becomes the better model.", "Prospective (step 4, oxidative disposal): after oleate or myelin loading, APOE4 microglia should show greater etomoxir-sensitive and bafilomycin-A1-sensitive oxygen consumption than APOE3, matching gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5. If APOE4 oxygen consumption is not higher and neutral lipid instead accumulates in droplets, step 4 is falsified and a storage rather than disposal model is favoured.", "Prospective (step 3, routing asymmetry): stimulus-evoked secretion and lysosome exocytosis (ATP- or LPS-evoked CTSS and CSF1 release, surface LAMP1 exposure) should be lower in APOE4 while internalisation and endosome-to-lysosome delivery are equal or faster, matching gene:RAB27A, gene:EXOC3, gene:EXOC6, gene:STXBP5, gene:STX16, gene:VAMP2 versus gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:GNPTG. Equal or increased evoked secretion in APOE4 would weaken the routing-bias step.", "Prospective (step 2, driver test): TFEB knockdown or MiT/TFE-family inhibition should collapse the v-ATPase and hydrolase module preferentially in APOE4 (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB) and precipitate lipid/substrate accumulation. If these transcripts are unaffected by TFEB loss, the biogenesis step must be replaced by a different driver.", "Prospective (focus test, sphingolipid specificity): selective GBA inhibition with conduritol-B-epoxide should not reproduce the APOE4 phenotype more than an equivalent block of a non-sphingolipid hydrolase arm (e.g. GAA or v-ATPase inhibition), and glucosylceramide/GM2/sphingomyelin should not be selectively elevated in mock APOE4. Selective sphingolipid substrate accumulation with GBA-inhibition phenocopy would instead support a sphingolipid-specific mechanism and refute the deliberately non-specific claim made here.", "Prospective (challenge-only prediction): APOE4 microglia should show reduced reserve, i.e. a larger drop in cargo clearance and viability than APOE3 under a myelin or apoptotic-cell challenge, even though the mock state shows no measured defect. Equal performance under challenge would weaken the reduced-reserve corollary without falsifying the mock-state description."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred load): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and for esterification/desaturation/storage (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, gene:APOE +1.2), consistent with (but not proof of) a larger standing delivery of lipid and membrane cargo into the endosomal system.", "Step 2 (biogenesis of degradative capacity): A MiT/TFE-type lysosomal module is coordinately up - gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC +1.65, gene:MITF +1.03; v-ATPase subunits 20/20 positive (gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1 +2.30); acid hydrolases occupy the extreme upper tail (gene:GAA +9.96 ~99.7th pct, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.87, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86), with sphingolipid cofactors/glycosidases (gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GM2A +2.01, gene:SUMF1 +2.01, gene:GLA +1.53). This is increased transcriptional capacity, not demonstrated enzymatic activity.", "Step 3 (routing bias toward terminal degradation): Forward hydrolase-targeting and endosome-to-lysosome machinery is up (gene:GNPTG +3.02, gene:IGF2R +2.02, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:CHMP4B +3.78, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SLC17A5 +2.16, gene:SPNS1 +2.58, gene:LAMP1 +1.38), whereas the exocytic/TGN-retrieval/Golgi-directed limb is selectively down against the up-skewed background (gene:GOLPH3L -7.36, gene:STXBP5 -5.51, gene:GCC1 -4.97, gene:STX16 -4.06, gene:EXOC6 -3.83, gene:RAB27A -2.51, gene:EXOC3 -2.09, gene:STX17 -2.06, gene:VAMP2 -1.79, gene:M6PR -1.72, gene:SEC24D -1.44, gene:TMED5 -1.49). Net predicted effect: cargo is committed to the lysosome rather than recycled or secreted.", "Step 4 (oxidative disposal of catabolites): Mitochondrial catabolic transcripts are uniformly and strongly up (24/24 represented positive, median +2.9, permutation p~0.002): gene:MDH1 +8.71, gene:OGDH +8.58, gene:MPC2 +8.00, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:DLD +5.51, gene:UQCRC2 +4.00, gene:ETFA +3.52, gene:ACO2 +3.51, gene:HADHA +2.89, gene:ACSS2 +2.87, gene:ATP5F1B +2.63, gene:ACOX1 +1.22, while glycolytic entry falls (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.06). This is compatible with fatty-acyl and carbon units released by degradation being oxidised rather than stored or fermented.", "Step 5 (state-level trade-off, not a proven bottleneck): The same cells reduce secreted/effector transcripts (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CSF1 -5.94, gene:SPN -7.27, gene:SEMA4A -5.16, gene:TGFBR1 -2.19) alongside gene:MYH9 -6.38 and gene:ACTB -4.98, i.e. traffic and biosynthetic output are reallocated from surveillance/secretion toward internal degradation and oxidation. In the mock condition we posit adaptation with maintained-or-increased throughput; any degradative insufficiency would be a reduced reserve revealed only by cargo challenge, and is not established by these data.", "Step 6 (protein-layer compatibility, not confirmation): 2D-gel spots are multi-candidate and give no consistent protein-level increase for hydrolases: spots containing lysosomal candidates split 15 up / 10 down (protein_spot:052 +2.14 [ACTB, CTSL, TPM3, CLIC1, NT5C1A], protein_spot:053 +1.54 [TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1] versus protein_spot:069 -1.38 [ACTB, CTSD, GPS2], protein_spot:067 -1.00 [PSMA3, ACTG2, CTSB, HEXB, LRIF1], protein_spot:064 -1.20 [ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1]). The mechanism therefore rests on transcript-level capacity plus the routing asymmetry, and predicts that hydrolase activity assays, not spot intensities, will adjudicate it."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a delivery-biased endolysosomal state: expanded acid-hydrolase/v-ATPase capacity (including the sphingolipid catabolic arm) coupled to mitochondrial oxidative disposal, with a reciprocally downshifted exocytic/Golgi-directed limb"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20591330354835136, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15322517722858509, "cosine_similarity": 0.14970954073296963, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6576957928802589, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20591330354835136, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15322517722858509, "cosine_similarity": 0.14970954073296963, "direction_accuracy": 0.15048543689320387, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6576957928802589, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.39162325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 95}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_132", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base and is preserved as reported; because these rows are a selected differential-expression list with a large global positive offset (median +1.459, 77.1% positive), only within-list rank/percentile comparisons are interpreted, never the raw sign of an individual gene.", "Absence of a gene (NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, HMGCR, SQLE, PSAP, GRN) from the supplied list means it was not reported as significantly differential; it is not treated as a measured unchanged pool.", "Transcript rank is assumed to correlate with protein and enzymatic capacity for the lysosomal module; this is unverified here, and no lysosomal enzyme activity, cholesterol, sphingolipid or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; no spot is used as evidence for a specific sterol or lysosomal protein. Spots 052/053/058/067/069 variously list CTSL/CTSD/CTSB/HEXB and change in opposite directions, so the proteomic layer is treated as uninformative for this mechanism.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins and extracellular lipid acceptors, so extracellular acceptor availability is assumed comparable between genotypes.", "Background knowledge that APOE4 protein is a poorer lipid acceptor/lipidation substrate than APOE3 is UNVERIFIED here (literature retrieval disabled) and is used only as motivation, not as evidence.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment is the assumed source of difference; biological replicate number was not supplied, so the reported p-values may be inflated by pseudo-replication across cells."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of lysosomal luminal hydrolase and v-ATPase/CLEAR capacity together with high SCARB1, while the transcripts encoding the lysosomal sterol egress and acceptor-mediated efflux arm (NPC2, APOE, OSBPL8, SOAT1, MYLIP; NPC1/LIPA/ABCA1/ABCG1 not reported as differential) are not co-elevated. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing the genotypes is post-hydrolytic export of cholesterol out of the endolysosome (NPC2/APOE-dependent egress plus acceptor-mediated efflux), not sterol synthesis, uptake, or hydrolysis; the resulting inferred sterol retention in the LAMP1+ compartment keeps ER-accessible cholesterol near normal (flat SREBP-2 core module) while sustaining a TFEB-type lysosomal program. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which bypasses NPC1/NPC2-dependent lysosomal cholesterol egress) or an LXR agonist that induces ABCA1/ABCG1 should, in APOE4 microglia, lower LAMP1-colocalised unesterified cholesterol AND normalise the elevated lysosomal module (GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, ATP6V1A, TFEB) toward APOE3 levels. If cyclodextrin depletes lysosomal cholesterol but leaves the hydrolase/CLEAR transcripts elevated, the proposed egress bottleneck is not driving the transcriptional state and the mechanism is weakened.", "RECIPROCAL PERTURBATION: pharmacological blockade of egress in APOE3 microglia (U18666A, NPC1 inhibition) should phenocopy the APOE4 lysosomal module within 24-72 h. Failure to reproduce it would weaken the mechanism.", "IMAGING: filipin or cholesterol-oxidase staining should show higher unesterified cholesterol per LAMP1+ compartment in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4 falsifies the central inference.", "COMPARTMENT DISCRIMINATION: an ER-accessible cholesterol probe (ALOD4/D4H) should be similar between genotypes despite higher lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4, matching the flat SREBP-2 module. If ER-accessible cholesterol is markedly lower in APOE4 with unchanged lysosomal cholesterol, the bottleneck is misassigned to egress rather than to ER supply.", "UPTAKE-VERSUS-EXPORT TEST: SCARB1 knockdown or lipoprotein-deficient medium should only partially normalise the APOE4 lysosomal module. Complete normalisation would indicate that substrate delivery, not export capacity, is the rate-limiting step and would displace this hypothesis.", "EFFLUX ASSAY: cholesterol efflux to exogenous apoA-I or HDL acceptors, per unit cell cholesterol, should be lower in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or higher efflux would weaken the mechanism.", "ACTIVITY-VERSUS-TRANSCRIPT CONTROL: measured GBA, HEXA/HEXB and acid sphingomyelinase activities and DQ-BSA degradative flux should be higher in APOE4. If activities are unchanged despite the transcript ranks, the finding is transcript-only and the capacity limb of the mechanism fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_132", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA, relative rank): APOE4 microglia show a lysosomal luminal-hydrolase and acidification module ranked far above the strong global positive offset of this differential-expression list (global median +1.459 in the unspecified log base; 77.1% of rows positive): GAA (pct 1.00), CTSK (0.99), ATP6V1H (0.98), GBA (0.98), HEXA (0.96), NAGLU (0.96), SMPD1 (0.95), CTSB (0.95), ATP6V1A (0.89), ATP6V0C (0.83), CTSD (0.76), RAB7A (0.73), TFEB (0.69).", "INFERRED (capacity, not flux): this pattern indicates increased lysosomal biogenesis and degradative capacity in APOE4. Increased capacity is treated here as a demand/compensation signal rather than the bottleneck itself; enzymatic activity and degradative flux were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA): SCARB1 is one of the highest-ranked transcripts (effect 8.22, pct 0.99), with modest positive scavenger/lipid-handling transcripts (COLEC12 1.53, SLCO2B1 1.49, CD163 1.38, MRC1 1.36, CD36 1.38). INFERRED: increased selective lipoprotein-lipid and cholesteryl-ester delivery into the endolysosomal system in an astrocyte co-culture that supplies lipoproteins.", "MEASURED (RNA, relative rank): the sterol egress/efflux arm is NOT co-elevated and ranks below the list median: NPC2 (pct 0.35), APOE (0.38), SOAT1 (0.39), MYLIP (0.41), OSBPL8 (0.13, the only negative member); as a set n=6, median percentile 0.37, permutation p=0.78 for up-shift. NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1, PSAP, GRN and STARD/GRAMD family members do not appear in the supplied differential list at all (not reported as changed; not evidence of an unchanged molecular pool).", "INFERRED (flux and localisation, not measured): net sterol flux into the late endosome/lysosome therefore exceeds NPC2/APOE-dependent egress and acceptor-mediated efflux, so unesterified cholesterol (with sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid) is predicted to be retained on and within the LAMP1+ compartment in APOE4. No lipid measurement is supplied in this dataset.", "INFERRED (sensing, consistent with data): because retained sterol is sequestered away from the ER, the ER sterol sensor is not driven to a starvation state, which is consistent with a flat SREBP-2 core module (SREBF2 pct 0.28, HMGCS1 0.28, LDLR 0.51, INSIG1 0.60; set n=4, median percentile 0.40, permutation p=0.70; HMGCR, SQLE, FDFT1, IDI1, MVD, MVK, PMVK absent from the list). Only post-squalene/pleiotropic enzymes rank high (DHCR24 0.85, DHCR7 0.73, LSS 0.67, ACAT2 0.63), which is counter-evidence against a clean SREBP-2 activation and argues the sterol difference is a trafficking, not a synthesis, difference.", "INFERRED (net state, causal direction not established): APOE4 microglia are hypothesised to occupy a stable export-limited state in which degradative and uptake capacity are up-regulated around a fixed egress step, reducing sterol handoff to extracellular acceptors and biasing the cell toward lysosomal lipid storage rather than sterol redistribution."], "title": "Export-limited lysosomal sterol handling in APOE4 microglia: degradative capacity is scaled up around an unscaled NPC2/APOE-dependent egress-and-efflux step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08512720156555773, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.02798979124125949, "cosine_similarity": 0.1473780726981417, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_132", "mean_absolute_error": 0.646336569579288, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.08512720156555773, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.02798979124125949, "cosine_similarity": 0.1473780726981417, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "mean_absolute_error": 0.646336569579288, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.09984325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 401}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_028", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Elevated transcript abundance translates into increased mature lysosomal enzyme content and activity; no enzyme activity, protein identity or localisation was measured in the supplied data.", "The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression selection (a gap between -1 and +1 in every effect implies a fold-change threshold), so absence of ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2, PSAP and SMPD3 from the file is interpreted as 'not selected as strongly differential', i.e. plausibly not co-induced. This is an assumption, not an observation; those pools were never measured here.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified, so effect magnitudes are treated as ordinal (rank/relative) rather than as absolute fold changes, and RNA and protein-spot log2 values are never compared on a common scale.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; any lysosomal or trafficking interpretation of a spot is provisional.", "The +1.39 mean of the supplied differential rows (77% positive) is treated as the correct internal background for set enrichment; if that global positive shift is a normalisation or composition artefact, all set-level enrichments including this one shrink.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are isogenic and the mock condition is matched, so the contrast reflects genotype rather than differentiation batch; replicate numbers were not supplied and could not be checked."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinately elevated endolysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcript module (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, SUMF1, with lysosome-delivery genes SCARB2, SPNS1, GLTP, RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3 and the lysosomal regulator TFEB), whereas the sphingolipid anabolic arm is not co-elevated and the lactosylceramide-synthesis step (B4GALT5) is reduced. We hypothesise that this asymmetry raises catabolic input into the endolysosomal ceramide pool faster than ceramide-consuming capacity (acid-ceramidase step, which is not represented in the supplied data), so ceramide becomes the rate-limiting node and accumulates while sphingomyelin and complex glycosphingolipids fall, biasing APOE4 microglial membrane and lipid-droplet handling. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is proposed as a testable model.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased total ceramide (and an increased ceramide:sphingomyelin ratio) with decreased sphingomyelin and decreased lactosylceramide/complex gangliosides, while glucosylceramide is unchanged or decreased. If ceramide is unchanged or lower, or if sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide are higher in APOE4, the mechanism is weakened.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: functional acid sphingomyelinase inhibition (desipramine/amitriptyline) or SMPD1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should lower the ceramide excess and restore the ceramide:sphingomyelin ratio toward APOE3 without normalising the sterol/lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1, SCP2, SCD) or the non-sphingolipid hydrolases (GAA, CTSK). Persistence of the ceramide excess after SMPD1 loss, or simultaneous normalisation of the sterol arm, would indicate that the entry point is not SMPD1 and would favour a generic TFEB-driven lysosomal-biogenesis or sterol-primary explanation.", "FLUX (not abundance) TEST: pulse-labelled NBD- or C17-sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide loading should be converted to ceramide faster in APOE4 than APOE3, and conduritol-B-epoxide block of GBA should cause a larger glucosylceramide build-up in APOE4. Equal conversion rates and equal inhibitor-induced accumulation would show no increased catabolic flux and would falsify steps 2-3.", "BOTTLENECK TEST: acid ceramidase (ASAH1) transcript, protein and activity should NOT be increased in APOE4 in proportion to SMPD1/GBA/HEXA, and lysosomal ceramide should rise. If ASAH1 activity is elevated proportionally and lysosomal ceramide is unchanged, the proposed ceramide bottleneck is wrong.", "RESCUE TEST: raising lysosomal ceramide-clearing capacity in APOE4 (ASAH1 overexpression, or recombinant acid ceramidase delivery) should reduce ceramide, restore sphingomyelin/complex glycosphingolipid balance and normalise lipid-droplet and endolysosomal-membrane phenotypes without changing the upstream hydrolase transcripts. No lipid or phenotypic correction would weaken the causal chain.", "SPECIFICITY TEST: TFEB knockdown should lower the entire hydrolase module (sphingolipid and non-sphingolipid alike). If sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts remain selectively elevated in APOE4 after TFEB knockdown, the module is not a simple downstream read-out of lysosomal biogenesis, which would strengthen the sphingolipid-specific reading; the converse would place the primary lesion upstream at TFEB/MITF."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA abundance only): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for the lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase set - GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, GLTP +2.38, GBA2 +2.63, HEXB +2.17, ST3GAL5 +2.17, GM2A +2.01, SUMF1 +2.01 (reported log units, base unspecified) - set mean +3.25 versus +1.39 for all supplied differential rows (permutation p = 0.0099, n = 10); the broader lysosomal hydrolase set (GAA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, NAGLU, ATP6V1A) and TFEB (+2.38) are also elevated, so this arm is part of a wider lysosomal transcriptional program rather than a uniquely sphingolipid response.", "INFERRED (protein content and localisation not measured): elevated hydrolase transcripts, together with elevated transcripts of hydrolase-delivery and late-endosome machinery (SCARB2 +1.06 for GBA delivery, VPS26A +4.86, SNX3 +3.95, RAB7A +2.65, AP5M1 +9.78, GLTP +2.38), increase the amount and lysosomal targeting of acid sphingomyelinase and glycosidase activity per cell.", "INFERRED (flux, not measured): increased SMPD1 activity converts endolysosomal sphingomyelin to ceramide, while GBA/GBA2 and the HEXA/HEXB/GM2A/SUMF1 glycosidase arm funnel glycosphingolipids down to glucosylceramide and then ceramide, so ceramide-generating flux rises.", "MEASURED counter-balance: the biosynthetic arm is not co-elevated - KDSR +1.27, CERS6 +1.06, CERK +1.23, ORMDL2 +1.91, CERS4 +2.52 (set mean +1.02, below the +1.39 background, permutation p = 0.64; catabolic minus anabolic difference +2.23, permutation p = 0.0086) - and B4GALT5 (lactosylceramide synthase) is decreased (-1.88), the only strongly down-regulated sphingolipid gene supplied.", "INFERRED BOTTLENECK (the limiting enzyme itself is NOT in the supplied data): with catabolic input up, salvage back into lactosylceramide/complex glycosphingolipids reduced, and no evidence in the supplied rows that acid ceramidase or ceramide re-acylation/transfer capacity scales in parallel, the ceramide-to-sphingosine step becomes rate limiting; downstream sphingosine egress capacity is transcriptionally elevated (SPNS1 +2.58, SGPL1 +1.09), which places the constriction at ceramide rather than at sphingosine export.", "INFERRED CONSEQUENCE (lipids not measured here): APOE4 endolysosomal membranes become ceramide-enriched and sphingomyelin/lactosylceramide-depleted, which is predicted to stiffen late-endosomal membranes, favour intraluminal vesicle formation and altered vesicular routing of internalised lipid, and act together with the elevated sterol/lipogenic transcripts (SREBF1 +4.67, SCP2 +5.95, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69) to shift APOE4 microglia toward a stored/neutral-lipid-biased state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate a lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic module without matching ceramide disposal or complex-glycosphingolipid resynthesis, making the ceramide node the flux bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2535077354798213, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07533094602282846, "cosine_similarity": 0.14736372530002356, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mean_absolute_error": 0.668084142394822, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2535077354798213, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07533094602282846, "cosine_similarity": 0.14736372530002356, "direction_accuracy": 0.215210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.668084142394822, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.65299725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 402}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_057", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705/2212 = 77% positive); programs are judged against that 77% up background, and absent genes (e.g. ACLY, FASN, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, ACSL1/3, G6PD, TKT, most autophagy and mitochondrial-dynamics genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; protein spots are log2. Effect magnitudes are therefore compared within-modality only, and very large RNA values (up to +15.5) are treated as direction plus rank, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken to indicate the direction of enzyme/transporter capacity, not measured enzyme activity, acyl-CoA pools, lipid species, membrane composition, respiration, or lysosomal flux; every flux, localization and routing statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "All 92 protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes each; zero uniquely assigned), so spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction, never to confirm an individual protein; all candidate identities are retained.", "Astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be a shared lipid/lipoprotein source for both genotypes, so the APOE4-APOE3 difference is attributed to microglial handling rather than to differing supply.", "Gene-set membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway/HGNC family lists before signs were inspected; all represented members are reported including opposite-sign ones, and genes within a program are co-regulated, so unanimity is descriptive coherence, not an independent-gene enrichment test.", "Causality between the mitochondrial-carbon arm and the lipogenic/remodeling arm is not established by these data; the mechanism assumes coupling but the direction could be reversed or both could be driven by a shared upstream regulator."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by a lipid-handling bottleneck but by a coordinated, adaptive increase in lipid throughput: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, endolysosomal hydrolysis, and ER glycerolipid re-synthesis are jointly elevated, while the acyl-donor arm is re-routed toward monounsaturated species (SCD, FADS1 up; ACSL4, ACSL5 down), and mitochondrial pyruvate entry with citrate/malate export (MPC2, OGDH, SLC25A1, MDH1, GOT1, ME1) plus uniformly increased nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcripts provide the acetyl-CoA/NADPH and redox support for this anabolic remodeling. The predicted consequence is a MUFA-enriched, arachidonate-poor membrane and neutral-lipid pool in the measured mock state, with reduced peroxidizable-lipid and lysosomal reserve revealed only by a future lipid or oxidative challenge.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher 16:1/18:1-containing PC/PE and triacylglycerol and a lower 20:4 (arachidonoyl) phospholipid fraction; if the arachidonoyl-phospholipid fraction is unchanged or higher in APOE4, the acyl-routing step is falsified.", "Prospective stable-isotope tracing (13C-glucose or 13C-acetate into glycerophospholipid and TG; D9-choline into PC) should show higher label incorporation per cell in APOE4, and 13C-glucose label should reach citrate and lipid more readily in APOE4; equal or lower incorporation despite the elevated transcripts would show that increased transcript abundance did not produce increased flux and would weaken the 'increased throughput' claim in favour of transcriptional compensation.", "Prospective SCD inhibition (or SCD knockdown) should preferentially collapse neutral-lipid droplet content and normalize the MUFA/PUFA phospholipid ratio in APOE4 toward APOE3; absence of a genotype-differential effect would weaken step 4.", "Prospective ACSL4 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore 20:4-phospholipid content and increase sensitivity to lipid-peroxidation challenge (e.g. GPX4 inhibition), without abolishing the uptake/lysosomal transcript differences; no change in 20:4-PL would falsify the ACSL4 arm while leaving the throughput claim intact.", "Prospective respirometry plus mtDNA-encoded protein quantification: the mechanism predicts APOE4 basal and maximal oxygen consumption at least equal to APOE3 despite the lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4); a reproducible APOE4 respiration deficit with reduced complex I/IV assembly would favour the competing mitonuclear-imbalance/failed-compensation explanation over this anabolic-supply mechanism.", "Prospective challenge (myelin debris, apoptotic-cell or oxLDL load): the mechanism predicts APOE4 initially clears more lipid but then accumulates droplets and shows earlier lysosomal-membrane stress than APOE3; equal handling under load would indicate the mock-state differences carry no functional consequence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases routing of extracellular lipid/lipoprotein into microglia: uptake and scavenging transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:SCARB1 +8.2, gene:ABCA7 +2.1, gene:LDLR +1.5, gene:CD36 +1.4, gene:MERTK +1.3, gene:TREM2 +1.3, gene:APOE +1.2, gene:PLTP +1.1; 12/13 queried members positive). Uptake flux itself is inferred, not measured.", "Endolysosomal degradative capacity expands in parallel rather than failing: gene:TFEB +2.4 with 8/8 V-ATPase subunits up (gene:ATP6V1H +6.9, gene:ATP6V1A +4.2, gene:ATP6V0C +3.5) and hydrolases gene:GAA +10.0, gene:CTSK +7.4, gene:HEXA +5.7, gene:CTSB +5.5, gene:CTSD +2.9, gene:NPC2 +1.2, so sterol/fatty-acid liberation and export from lysosomes is sustained or increased (gene:CTSS -5.6 is the exception).", "Liberated and imported lipid is re-esterified and rebuilt into membrane in an SREBF1-associated ER arm: gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:MBOAT2 +3.3, gene:MBOAT1 +2.6, gene:CHPT1 +2.9, gene:PCYT2 +1.0, gene:DGAT1 +1.7, gene:SOAT1 +1.3, with concurrent turnover enzymes gene:MGLL +4.0 and gene:PLA2G7 +1.1 - i.e. faster cycling of glycerophospholipid and neutral-lipid pools, not stalled synthesis.", "Acyl-chain composition of that cycle is re-routed: gene:SCD +4.2 and gene:FADS1 +1.6 increase while gene:ACSL4 -2.1 and gene:ACSL5 -3.1 decrease, biasing acyl-CoA supply toward 16:1/18:1 monounsaturated donors and away from ACSL4-dependent arachidonoyl-CoA activation for lysophospholipid re-acylation.", "Cytosolic carbon and reducing equivalents for this anabolic arm are supplied mitochondrially: gene:MPC2 +8.0, gene:OGDH +8.6, gene:SLC25A1 +4.5, gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:GOT1 +6.4, gene:ME1 +1.4, gene:GLS +1.4, with import machinery gene:TOMM22 +4.6, gene:TIMM8B +5.2 and 38/38 represented nuclear OXPHOS subunits positive (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7 +5.7, gene:CYCS +2.6). This pattern indicates increased oxidative/anaplerotic capacity supporting biosynthesis, not an energy-deficit compensation.", "The resulting APOE4 cell state in mock is a MUFA-enriched, arachidonate-poor, rapidly turned-over membrane and lipid-droplet pool coexisting with an activation-leaning but not homeostasis-collapsed microglial phenotype (gene:ITGAX +1.7, gene:CLEC7A +1.5, gene:LGALS3 +2.4, gene:GPNMB +1.1 up while gene:CSF1R +1.4, gene:MEF2C +1.3, gene:GPR34 +3.0, gene:IRF8 +1.4 remain up); functional fragility (reduced lysosomal and peroxidizable-lipid reserve) is predicted only under a future lipid or oxidative challenge and is not claimed for the measured condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a high-throughput lipid-influx-to-membrane-resynthesis state with MUFA-biased acyl routing, supplied by mitochondrial citrate/malate export"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09767197134733965, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06049554154719779, "cosine_similarity": 0.14432246917139363, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6425210355987054, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09767197134733965, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06049554154719779, "cosine_similarity": 0.14432246917139363, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6425210355987054, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.6305015, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 96}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_160", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source workbook and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are therefore not numerically comparable to the log2 protein-spot effects, and only within-modality relative comparisons are used.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the within-list background (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77% positive), not against zero.", "The strong global positive offset is treated as a normalisation/composition property of the list rather than as evidence of genuine transcriptome-wide upregulation.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the size of the corresponding nuclear-encoded protein pool; no protein-level or assembly-level measurement of any respiratory complex is available.", "mtDNA-encoded gene quantification by probe-based 10X Flex is assumed to be usable but noisy; the discordance between MT-ND4 and MT-ND4L, which share a bicistronic transcript, indicates the mtDNA arm rests on weak measurement (unverified background knowledge about Flex probe coverage).", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified; each carries several candidate genes, so spot 077 and spot 017 are treated as consistent-with, not evidence-of, PRDX2 and catalase protein increase.", "Respiratory flux, membrane potential, CoQ redox poise, superoxide/H2O2 levels, glutathione status, NADPH supply and complex assembly state are entirely unmeasured and are inferred only.", "Astrocyte co-culture means the sorted/annotated microglial signal may carry ambient or cross-cell contribution that cannot be assessed from the supplied file."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated, above-background induction of the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative program (TCA/anaplerosis, complex I-V structural subunits, SLC25 carriers, import and mitochondrial translation elongation factors) that is NOT accompanied by induction of the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits, several of which are reduced. We hypothesise that the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, not nuclear subunit availability, is the rate-limiting step for respiratory-complex assembly in APOE4, so imported nuclear subunits accumulate in sub-stoichiometric or unassembled modules, electron transfer downstream of complex I becomes flux-limited, and the resulting matrix hydrogen-peroxide load is buffered by an increased mitochondrial thiol-peroxidase system (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, MSRA). Assembly state, respiratory flux, membrane potential and ROS were not measured; only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were. No causality is established. The assigned peroxisomal arm of the focus is rejected as unsupported.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation in APOE3 microglia (low-dose chloramphenicol or doxycycline, titrated to reduce mtDNA-encoded subunit synthesis without killing cells) should phenocopy the APOE4 transcript signature - coordinated induction of nuclear NDUF/ATP5/COX/UQCR and TCA transcripts together with PRDX3/PRDX5 - whereas APOE4 cells should be relatively resistant because they already occupy that state. If APOE3 fails to acquire the nuclear-OXPHOS-up/peroxiredoxin-up signature under mitoribosome inhibition, the mitonuclear-imbalance bottleneck is falsified.", "SECOND DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION (causal ordering of the redox arm): a matrix-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ or mitoTEMPO) should normalise the PRDX3/PRDX5/PRDX2/GPX4/MSRA transcript elevation in APOE4 while leaving the TCA and nuclear ETC transcript elevation largely intact; a non-targeted cytosolic antioxidant (NAC) should do neither. If MitoQ equally normalises the TCA/nuclear-OXPHOS program, the proposed direction (assembly bottleneck upstream, redox response downstream) is wrong.", "ASSEMBLY TEST: blue-native PAGE/complexome profiling of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased nuclear-encoded subunits in low-molecular-weight sub-assemblies with an unchanged or reduced ratio of fully assembled CIII2/CIV/CV to complex-I-module content. Proportional scaling of all holo-complexes with the transcript increase would weaken the mechanism.", "FLUX TEST: extracellular flux analysis should show APOE4 with equal-or-higher basal oxygen consumption but reduced FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration and reduced spare respiratory capacity, with a higher proton-leak fraction; a proportional increase in maximal respiration in APOE4 would weaken the bottleneck claim.", "REDOX-STATE TEST: mito-roGFP2-Orp1 or MitoSOX in APOE4 should report a more oxidised matrix and higher basal peroxide, and 2D redox gels should show a larger hyperoxidised (acidic-shifted) PRDX2/PRDX3 spot train in APOE4. Equal matrix redox poise despite the transcript changes would remove the redox arm.", "RESCUE SPECIFICITY: supplying the limiting cores (allotopic nuclear-recoded MT-ATP6/MT-CYB expression, or mtDNA-replete cybrid rescue) should reduce the nuclear OXPHOS and peroxiredoxin transcript elevation in APOE4, whereas overexpressing an additional nuclear subunit (e.g. NDUFA5) should not.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL FOR THE ASSIGNED FOCUS: peroxisome-targeted catalase overexpression, or PEX-pathway readouts, should show no rescue and no APOE4-vs-APOE3 difference; a strong peroxisomal phenotype would show the mitochondrial localisation of the bottleneck is misassigned."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_160", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coherent transcript increase across nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery - TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (mean effect +4.3, n=11; permutation p=2e-4 against the +1.39 within-list background), structural subunits of complexes I-V (mean +2.8, n=37; permutation p=4e-4), mitochondrial solute carriers, protein-import components and mitochondrial translation-elongation factors.", "MEASURED (RNA), CONTRASTING: the mtDNA-encoded subunits present in the list are the only mitochondrial category shifted negative (mean -0.8, n=6; permutation p=0.02; nuclear-vs-mtDNA contrast p=1.1e-3), with MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 down while MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are up.", "INFERRED (not measured): because MT-CYB, MT-CO2/CO1 and MT-ATP6 form the catalytic and proton-translocating cores of complexes III, IV and V, their unchanged-to-reduced supply makes mtDNA-encoded core availability the assembly bottleneck; nuclear subunits are then predicted to accumulate as unassembled or sub-complex pools rather than as proportionally more holo-enzyme.", "INFERRED (flux/activity, not measured): with complex I and dehydrogenase input capacity raised (NDUF module, IDH3, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, MDH1, GLUD1, GOT1) but downstream CIII/CIV/CV capacity capped, the CoQ and complex-I flavin pools become more reduced during basal respiration, favouring one-electron leak to superoxide and its dismutation to matrix H2O2, and limiting spare respiratory capacity.", "PARTIALLY MEASURED (RNA + ambiguous spots): the cell compensates by raising thiol-peroxidase and repair transcripts concentrated in the matrix/IMS (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, MSRA) plus iron-sequestering FTH1; two significant protein spots whose candidate lists contain PRDX2 and CAT are increased, consistent with but not proof of increased peroxidase protein.", "INFERRED (net state): APOE4 microglia therefore occupy a high-oxidative-demand, redox-strained steady state in which peroxide handling is elevated while the OXR1 oxidative-damage-resistance transcript is strongly reduced, lowering the reserve against any further oxidative or phagocytic-burst load."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: APOE4 microglia scale up nuclear-encoded TCA/ETC machinery without matching mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, creating an assembly bottleneck and matrix peroxide load"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.02837573385518591, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03895743258269739, "cosine_similarity": 0.14323780125206, "direction_accuracy": 0.04854368932038835, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_160", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6352330097087379, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.02837573385518591, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03895743258269739, "cosine_similarity": 0.14323780125206, "direction_accuracy": 0.04854368932038835, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6352330097087379, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.50837025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 403}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_087", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with an unspecified logarithm base; 77.1% of selected rows are positive, so program directionality was judged against that 0.771 background, not 50/50. Genes absent from the list (e.g. HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, CPT1A, TFAM) are unknown, not unchanged, so 'routing away from efflux' is inferred from what is present and is not a measurement of ABCA1/ABCG1.", "All 92 protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate identities each, mean 4.8); no spot identifies a single protein. Spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction. The large increases at protein_spot:043-046 are consistent with, but do not prove, higher ANXA1 (RNA +4.15); the co-listed candidate TALDO1 has RNA -2.32, and other candidates (ACTB, POTEF, PSMD7, GALE) remain possible.", "Effect sizes are transcript abundance ratios only. Lysosomal degradative flux, lipolysis, cholesterol esterification, phospholipid acyl composition, autophagic flux, oxygen consumption, membrane turnover rate and protein activity were not measured; every 'flux', 'routing' and 'capacity' statement is inference, not observation.", "The measured comparison is mock-treated, isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3, day 30, iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes (10X Flex). Astrocyte-derived signal, differentiation-state or cell-composition differences between lines could contribute to a coordinated shift; replicate number was not supplied.", "The uniform positivity of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts (37/37) could partly reflect normalization, ambient RNA or a global depth/composition difference rather than mitochondrial biogenesis; the opposite direction of mtDNA-encoded transcripts partially argues against a purely technical global shift but does not exclude it.", "Reduced HK2/PFKP and lower mtDNA-encoded subunits are treated as a predicted reserve limitation revealed by a future challenge, not as an established ongoing bioenergetic defect in the measured mock condition.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a hypothesis about direction of information flow that requires the perturbations below."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 microglia differ from APOE3 not by a single failing enzyme but by a coordinated cell-state change: transcripts for lipid-cargo receptors, lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase (with TFEB/TFEC), mitochondrial TCA/beta-oxidation and all represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are higher, and in parallel SREBP-type lipogenic, sterol-synthetic, esterification and Lands-cycle acyl-remodeling transcripts are higher. The most parsimonious reading is increased lipid throughput with routing of lysosome-derived sterol and fatty acid into cholesteryl-ester/TAG storage and remodeled membrane phospholipid (so ER sterol sensing stays 'low'), not a degradative bottleneck; the discordant lower mtDNA-encoded subunits and lower inducible glycolytic isoforms (HK2, PFKP) predict reduced reserve that would be revealed only by a future challenge, not an ongoing energetic defect in the measured mock condition.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test (primary discriminator, mock condition): in mock APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia, DQ-BSA dequenching and BODIPY-C12/myelin pulse-chase clearance will be equal or higher in APOE4, and basal plus fatty-acid-dependent oxygen consumption will be higher. If instead APOE4 shows reduced DQ-BSA dequenching, accumulation of undigested LipidTOX-positive cargo and unchanged or lower basal OCR, the 'increased throughput/routing' mechanism is wrong and a failed-compensation (degradative bottleneck) model is favoured.", "Prospective lipidomics (mock): APOE4 will show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol relative to free cholesterol, and a higher monounsaturated/polyunsaturated acyl ratio in phosphatidylcholine species, consistent with gene:SCD and gene:LPCAT1/gene:MBOAT2 up and gene:ACSL4 down. Equal CE/TAG and unchanged PC acyl composition would falsify the routing/remodeling arm.", "Prospective SOAT1 inhibition (avasimibe) or SOAT1 knockdown in mock APOE4 microglia will raise ER-accessible free cholesterol and suppress the SREBP2-type transcripts (gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS) more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3. If those transcripts are insensitive to blocking esterification, the sterol-sequestration/mis-sensing step is falsified.", "Prospective challenge test (reserve, not ongoing defect): after myelin debris, oxLDL or LPS challenge, APOE4 will show lower spare respiratory capacity and reduced glycolytic compensation (consistent with gene:HK2, gene:PFKP down and gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4 down) together with greater cargo retention, even though mock-state clearance is equal or higher. Equal spare capacity and equal challenge clearance would remove the predicted latent limitation.", "Prospective identity resolution: immunoblot/targeted MS at protein_spot:043-046 must show increased ANXA1 protein in APOE4. If ANXA1 protein is unchanged and the spot increase is attributable to TALDO1 or an actin species, the membrane-repair/efferocytosis interpretation of those spots is withdrawn (the RNA-based mechanism would stand but lose its only protein-level support).", "Prospective TFEB dependence: TFEB/TFEC knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce the lysosomal-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H) and secondarily blunt the esterification/lipogenic arm (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SREBF1 targets). If the lipogenic arm is unaffected while lysosomal transcripts fall, the two arms are parallel rather than sequential and Step 3's causal ordering is falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia express higher levels of lipid-cargo uptake and opsonisation transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:MRC1, gene:APOE, gene:GPNMB), which we infer increases delivery of lipid-rich cargo to the endolysosome; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A broad lysosomal-catabolic program is elevated (45/45 represented members positive except gene:CTSS and gene:IDS; gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1, multiple ATP6V subunits, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:TFEC), plus endolysosomal trafficking (gene:RAB7A, gene:RAB32, gene:VPS26A, gene:VPS35L, gene:SNX3, gene:AP3D1, gene:AP5M1, gene:CHMP4B), i.e. expanded hydrolytic/sorting capacity that we infer raises the intracellular free fatty-acid, sphingoid and unesterified-sterol load.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred routing): That load is directed to storage and re-synthesis rather than to efflux: esterification transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:CIDEB), together with lipogenic/anaplerotic supply (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93) and sterol-synthetic SREBP2-type targets (gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:EBP, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2). Simultaneous high uptake/hydrolysis and an 'ER-sterol-low' transcriptional signature is the routing signature: sterol is diverted into esters/late endosomes instead of reaching the ER sensor pool (esterified pools were not measured).", "Step 4 (measured RNA): The same state remodels membrane glycerolipid: de novo/Lands-cycle acyltransferases and desaturation rise (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT4, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2) while long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11) and gene:GPAT3 -2.23 - predicting a shift in phospholipid acyl composition toward monounsaturated, LPCAT1-type species rather than simply more lipid of unchanged composition.", "Step 5 (measured RNA): Surplus acyl carbon feeds mitochondria: gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1, gene:CROT, with 37/37 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits positive (median ~+2.6; gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2), while inducible glycolytic isoforms fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:PFKFB2, gene:HK3). We infer a shift from inducible glycolysis toward oxidative lipid handling; respiration was not measured.", "Step 6 (measured RNA/protein, latent consequence): mtDNA-encoded subunits move oppositely (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33 vs gene:MT-ND5/ND4L up), so the expanded nuclear OXPHOS program is stoichiometrically unmatched; combined with lower HK2/PFKP this predicts reduced spare respiratory and glycolytic reserve that is latent under mock. The measured phenotype in mock is therefore a membrane/lipid-turnover cell state (consistent with gene:ANXA1 +4.15 and the ANXA1-candidate spots protein_spot:043/044/045/046 being among the largest protein increases) with a selectively rewired, not globally amplified, inflammatory output (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:NLRP1 up but gene:CSF1 -5.91, gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:CCL4, gene:CCL23, gene:TRAF4 down)."], "title": "APOE4 iPSC-microglia occupy a high-turnover endolysosomal lipid-processing state that routes catabolic sterol/fatty-acid output into esterification and acyl-chain remodeling rather than efflux, with mito-nuclear mismatch as a latent reserve limit"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36839530332681014, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18947665381497517, "cosine_similarity": 0.14289686839913845, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7378025889967638, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36839530332681014, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.18947665381497517, "cosine_similarity": 0.14289686839913845, "direction_accuracy": 0.2815533980582524, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7378025889967638, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.24240725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 97}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_039", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a curated differential-expression selection, not an unbiased transcriptome; the workbook contributes exactly one increased and one decreased gene per row for source rows 2-509 and increased genes only thereafter, so the apparent global positive shift (median +1.46) is treated as a selection artifact and all enrichment claims are made by rank within the increased list or by over-representation in the decreased list.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative ordering and sign are used, and the very large values (up to +15.5) are assumed to be monotone in true effect size even though effect magnitude is uncorrelated with adjusted p value (r = -0.03, all rows adjusted p \u003c 0.05).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for protein amount and none of the inferred quantities (Rac GTP loading, RhoGDI-Rac complex formation, F-actin at cups, internalization flux, lysosomal proteolytic flux, TFEB nuclear localization) were measured here.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate genes each and keratin-dominated candidate lists; they are treated as ambiguous corroboration only, never as identified proteins, and no unmeasured protein pool is claimed as observed.", "The comparison is assumed to be cell-intrinsic to microglia in the isogenic APOE4-vs-APOE3 pair; astrocyte co-culture, ambient RNA and unreported replicate structure could contribute genotype-associated signal that is not microglial.", "ARHGDIA is assumed to act, as in background knowledge (unverified here, literature retrieval disabled), as a cytosolic sequestering inhibitor of Rho-family GTPases rather than as a stabilizing chaperone that increases functional Rac availability."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 transcript state is discordant across the uptake pathway: cargo-recognition receptor transcripts are only marginally higher than APOE3 (bottom of the up-regulated list), the Rho-GTPase/actin module that builds phagocytic cups and ruffles is skewed against Rac-driven polymerization (ARHGDIA transcript among the largest increases; RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, FAM49B/CYRIB, MYH9, ACTB, MYO1F, VASP, ARHGAP30 in the decreased list), whereas late-endosome/lysosome maturation, acidification and hydrolase transcripts are among the largest increases. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step for extracellular cargo clearance in APOE4 microglia is actin-dependent internalization (cup formation/closure), not lysosomal degradative capacity, so that APOE4 cells bind cargo comparably but internalize it more slowly while carrying an enlarged, transcriptionally reinforced degradative compartment. Causality is not established by these data; the direction of the receptor/actin/lysosome relationships is inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating uptake-versus-degradation assay: pulse APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with pH-insensitive-labelled and pHrodo-labelled substrate (myelin, synaptosomes or IgG beads) at 4 C for binding then shift to 37 C. Prediction: comparable surface binding per cell (consistent with only marginal receptor transcript differences) but a lower internalized-to-bound ratio and slower initial internalization rate in APOE4, together with equal or higher per-particle degradation index (DQ-BSA or Magic Red signal per internalized particle). If APOE4 instead shows equal or faster internalization with a lower per-particle degradation index, the internalization-bottleneck claim is falsified and a lysosomal-degradation bottleneck is favoured.", "Causal test of the proposed actin node: ARHGDIA knockdown or expression of a GDI-insensitive/constitutively active Rac1 in APOE4 microglia should raise GTP-Rac pull-down signal, restore F-actin cup number and closure rate, and increase internalization toward APOE3 levels without normalizing lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, GBA, HEXA, GAA). No improvement in uptake despite confirmed Rac reactivation would weaken the mechanism; improvement that also normalizes hydrolase transcripts would argue the lysosomal program is downstream of uptake rather than parallel.", "Reciprocal test: in APOE3 microglia, ARHGDIA overexpression or low-dose Arp2/3 (CK-666) or myosin II (blebbistatin) inhibition should phenocopy the APOE4 internalization deficit (reduced internalized-to-bound ratio) while leaving lysosomal hydrolase activity per unit internalized cargo intact. Failure to phenocopy would weaken the mechanism.", "Directionality of the lysosomal program: blocking uptake in APOE4 microglia for 24-48 h (cytochalasin D or receptor blockade) should, if the degradative program is cargo-driven, reduce TFEB target transcripts (CTSB, GBA, HEXA, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels; persistence of the elevated hydrolase program under cargo deprivation would mean it is cargo-independent, weakening the compensatory element (but not the bottleneck element) of the hypothesis.", "Protein-level check that avoids spot ambiguity: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS in sorted microglia should show higher RhoGDI-1 and lower myosin-IIA and CYRIB protein in APOE4, with unchanged or higher LAMP1 and cathepsin B. Finding unchanged RhoGDI-1 protein despite the large ARHGDIA transcript difference, or higher myosin-IIA protein, would weaken step 2-3 of the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: engulfment/opsonin-receptor transcripts (TREM2, MERTK, CD36, MRC1, FCGR3A, C1QA, ITGAX, ITGB5) are higher in APOE4 only by small amounts and sit near the bottom of the up-regulated list (set mean rank 0.36 within the up list, permutation p_low approximately 0.005), indicating that cargo recognition capacity is not the axis being amplified.", "Measured: the Rho-GTPase/actin effector module is split, with ARHGDIA (RhoGDI-1) the third-largest increase in the whole discovery list (+10.61) while RAC2, ARHGDIB, DOCK8, FAM49B/CYRIB, MYH9, ACTB, MYO1F, VASP, ARHGAP30 and SPN are in the decreased list.", "Inferred activity/localization (not measured): a higher RhoGDI-1-to-Rac ratio with lower Rac2/DOCK8 GEF-module and lower WAVE-regulatory-complex component CYRIB shifts Rac toward the cytosolic, GDP-bound, GDI-sequestered pool, lowering membrane-localized GTP-Rac available to drive Arp2/3 branched-actin polymerization at nascent phagocytic cups and lamellipodia.", "Inferred flux (not measured): with reduced non-muscle myosin IIA (MYH9) and reduced beta-actin transcript, cup extension, closure and scission are slowed, so internalization flux per bound cargo particle falls even though surface binding sites are present; the uptake step becomes the bottleneck of the clearance pipeline.", "Measured: downstream endolysosomal machinery is transcriptionally amplified far above the typical up-regulated gene (up-list median +1.92): DNM2 +5.82, AP5M1 +9.78, RAB7A +2.65, VPS26A +4.86, SNX3 +3.95, CHMP4B +3.82 (endocytic/maturation set mean rank 0.75, p = 0.003), plus v-ATPase subunits ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C, hydrolases GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD and the lysosomal-biogenesis factor TFEB.", "Inferred state (not measured): the combination of a throttled entry step with an expanded acid-hydrolase and maturation program produces a degradation-competent but intake-restricted microglial state, in which per-cell clearance of extracellular material is reduced while intracellular lysosomal capacity and lipid-handling transcripts (SCARB1, ANXA1, LAMP1) are unchanged or higher; this predicts accumulation of uningested extracellular substrate rather than of undigested intracellular cargo."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are internalization-limited, not degradation-limited: a RhoGDI-high / Rac-effector-low actin state throttles phagocytic-cup uptake while the endolysosomal degradative program is transcriptionally expanded"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17086364139866336, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09493424478683285, "cosine_similarity": 0.14260074255659186, "direction_accuracy": 0.09870550161812297, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_039", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6432394822006472, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17086364139866336, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09493424478683285, "cosine_similarity": 0.14260074255659186, "direction_accuracy": 0.09870550161812297, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6432394822006472, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.64244075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 404}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_098", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the supplied workbook and is preserved as reported; all inference uses within-list ranks/percentiles rather than absolute fold changes.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) and show a strong global positive shift (77.1% up, median +1.46). We assume this shift is a selection/normalisation/compositional baseline rather than a true transcriptome-wide doubling, so only relative position within the list is interpreted.", "Transcript level is assumed to translate monotonically into enzyme protein and, at constant lysosomal pH and saposin/GM2A cofactor supply, into catabolic activity. Neither enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, nor cofactor levels are measured here.", "No lipid measurement of any kind is supplied: ceramide, sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, GM2, sphingosine and S1P pools are inferred, never observed.", "ASAH1, ACER3, SPHK1/2, SGPP1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2, CERT1, PSAP, GM2A, SPTLC1/2 and GALC do not appear in the supplied list; their absence means unmeasured or not differentially expressed, and cannot be read as evidence of no change. The bottleneck claim rests on SGPL1/CERK ranks plus this missing-data gap and is the weakest link in the chain.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a specific protein measurement.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of the RNA signal may be non-cell-autonomous or contributed by non-microglial transcripts; genotype is isogenic, which limits background-genetic confounding but not culture-composition confounding.", "Causal direction (APOE4 genotype -\u003e hydrolase transcription -\u003e ceramide -\u003e routing) is assumed for the purpose of prediction and has not been established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a selective transcriptional up-shift of the endolysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic hydrolases (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GBA2, ST3GAL5, SUMF1) that is not accompanied by an equivalent up-shift of the measured ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal arm (SGPL1, CERK sit below the list median; ASAH1, ACER3, SPHK1/2, SGPP1, UGCG, SGMS1/2 are absent from the supplied differential list and therefore unmeasured). We hypothesise that the resulting rate-limiting step is ceramide clearance from the late-endosome/lysosome limiting membrane, and that local ceramide accumulation biases membrane routing away from recycling/secretory export toward RAB7/retromer/ESCRT-associated degradative retention of lipid cargo. This is a proposed mechanism consistent with the supplied RNA ranks; causality is not established, and no lipid or flux measurement is supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia (whole cell and, decisively, magnetically isolated lysosome fractions) should show increased ceramide and a decreased sphingomyelin/ceramide, glucosylceramide/ceramide and GM2/GM3 ratio, with the ceramide increase concentrated in the lysosomal fraction. If lysosomal ceramide is unchanged or lower in APOE4, or if sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide are unchanged or higher, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, partial inhibition of acid sphingomyelinase (functional ASM inhibition, e.g. desipramine) combined with GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) should lower lysosomal ceramide and restore the routing readout - measured as recovery of recycling/export flux (surface re-appearance of an internalised labelled cargo or transferrin recycling rate) and reduced RAB7-positive/LAMP1-positive cargo dwell time - toward APOE3 values, while leaving SMPD1/GBA transcript levels unchanged. If ceramide falls but the routing readout in APOE4 remains unchanged, the ceramide-to-routing step is wrong even if the hydrolase step is right.", "Bottleneck test: direct assay of acid ceramidase activity and ASAH1/SPHK1/SGPL1 protein in the two genotypes. The mechanism requires that ceramide-clearance capacity does NOT rise in proportion to ASM/GBA/HEXA activity. If acid ceramidase activity in APOE4 rises by at least as large a factor as ASM and GBA activity, the proposed bottleneck is falsified and the sphingolipid arm should be reinterpreted as a balanced throughput increase.", "Rescue test: ASAH1 overexpression (or SGPL1 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should reduce lysosomal ceramide and normalise cargo recycling without normalising SMPD1/GBA/HEXA transcripts; failure to normalise routing despite verified ceramide reduction weakens the mechanism.", "Enzyme-level confirmation: 4-MU-based GBA and HEXA/HEXB activity assays and ASM activity should be higher in APOE4 lysates. This prediction is currently unsupported and partly opposed by the supplied protein data: spot 067 (-1.0, candidates include CTSB and HEXB) and spot 058 (-0.85, candidates include CTSD and CTSB) are decreased, while spot 052 (+2.14, includes CTSL) and spot 053 (+1.54, includes CTSD) are increased. If unambiguous, single-protein immunoblot or activity assays show no increase in GBA, HEXA and ASM protein or activity in APOE4, step 1 of the mechanism fails and the RNA signal should be treated as non-translated.", "Specificity control: the effect should be sphingolipid-directed rather than a generic lysosome-biogenesis programme. TFEB is only at the 69th percentile and the structural/membrane lysosomal genes LAMP1 (46th), SCARB2 (27th), NPC2 (35th), CLN3 (34th) and MITF (25th) are at or below the list median, so nuclear TFEB translocation and total lysosomal volume/number should be at most modestly changed while specific hydrolase activity per lysosome rises. If TFEB is strongly nuclear and lysosomal volume scales up in parallel, the simpler alternative - global CLEAR-network activation - better explains the data and this hypothesis should be abandoned."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: within a list whose global median log fold change is +1.46 (APOE4 \u003e APOE3), the sphingolipid-degrading acid hydrolases sit in the extreme upper tail - GBA (98th percentile), HEXA (96th), SMPD1 (95th) - with GLTP (69th), HEXB (66th), ST3GAL5 (66th), GBA2 (72nd) and SUMF1 (63rd, sulfatase-maturation cofactor) also above the median. Inferred, not measured: correspondingly higher acid sphingomyelinase, glucocerebrosidase and beta-hexosaminidase enzyme activity in the acidic compartment.", "Inferred flux: increased hydrolysis of sphingomyelin (SMPD1), glucosylceramide (GBA) and GM2/glycosphingolipids (HEXA/HEXB, ST3GAL5, GLTP-dependent presentation) raises the rate of ceramide generation on the luminal leaflet/limiting membrane of late endosomes and lysosomes.", "Proposed bottleneck: the exit route for that ceramide is not co-elevated. The only measured disposal enzyme, SGPL1, is at the 29th percentile (relative log fold change -0.37 versus the list median) and CERK is at the 38th; the anabolic/re-acylation arm (KDSR 41st, CERS6 27th, CERS4 71st, ORMDL2 61st) is at best flat. Ceramide-clearance capacity per unit of ceramide generated is therefore predicted to fall.", "Inferred membrane consequence: ceramide is a cone-shaped, non-bilayer-favouring lipid; its local accumulation is predicted to stabilise ordered microdomains, promote intraluminal-vesicle formation and stiffen the late-endosomal limiting membrane, changing which cargo can be sorted back out of the compartment. This is a physical inference, not an observation.", "Consistent routing signature in the measured RNA: degradative/retrograde and ESCRT machinery is high relative to the list median (VPS26A 93rd percentile, SNX3 88th, CHMP4B 87th, GOLPH3 85th, VAMP3 78th, RAB7A 73rd, RAB32 75th), whereas secretory/exocytic and Golgi-export components are at the extreme lower tail (GOLPH3L 0th, STXBP5 1st, RAB27A 8th). The inferred net effect is a shift of the endolysosomal balance from recycling/secretion toward degradative retention.", "Predicted cellular outcome: APOE4 microglia hold internalised lipid and membrane cargo longer in a ceramide-loaded acidic compartment. APOE RNA itself is only at the 38th percentile and LDLR at the 51st, so lipid export capacity is not scaled up with catabolic input, sustaining the lysosomal lipid load and providing a genotype-specific baseline stress that precedes any stimulus."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-shift lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matched ceramide disposal, biasing endolysosomal cargo toward degradative retention"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14552496352490582, "cosine_similarity": 0.14178272655598564, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6634563106796116, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14552496352490582, "cosine_similarity": 0.14178272655598564, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6634563106796116, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.42852625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 405}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_067", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level claims are therefore made against the internal empirical distribution of these 2212 rows (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77% positive), not against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative magnitudes and ranks within the supplied rows are used, and the very large values (up to +15.5) are treated as unreliable per gene but usable for set-level ranking.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme abundance; hydrolytic activity, luminal pH, lysosome number/size, lipid pool sizes, catabolite egress rate, respiration and complex assembly were not measured and are inferred.", "The 92 protein spots each map to several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; spots are used only as weak, non-attributed corroboration.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript quantification by probe-based 10X Flex, and ambient RNA from the co-cultured astrocytes, could bias the mito-nuclear contrast; this arm rests on only 6 measured MT- rows.", "No lipidomic, flux, imaging or functional measurement is supplied; APOE4 as a poorer lipid acceptor is unverified background knowledge, not evidence from this dataset.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a directional proposal consistent with the observed genotype-associated abundances."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, the transcriptional state that distinguishes isogenic APOE4 from APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is a selectively amplified acidified-lysosome / membrane-lipid-hydrolase program (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, NAGLU, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB) that rises far above the global upward shift of these selected DE rows, while transcripts for the lipid-egress/acceptor arm (APOE, NPC2, ABCA7, LAMP1, CLN3, SPNS1) rise only at or below the global shift; we propose the rate-limiting step is export/recycling of membrane-lipid catabolites out of the lysosome, so hydrolase induction is compensatory rather than evidence of increased end-to-end lipid clearance flux, and the coordinated rise of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts without a matching rise in mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts limits the oxidative sink for the released acyl chains. De novo glycerolipid synthesis and acyl-chain remodeling (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT2, CHPT1, DGAT1) is explicitly NOT proposed as the driver: as a set it is indistinguishable from the global shift.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating pulse-chase: after loading APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with fluorescently or isotopically labelled sphingomyelin/myelin membranes, APOE4 should show equal or faster intra-lysosomal hydrolysis (label converted to ceramide/sphingosine inside LAMP1+ compartments) but significantly delayed appearance of label in extra-lysosomal destinations (ER re-esterification, plasma membrane, medium). If hydrolysis is slower in APOE4, or if egress kinetics are indistinguishable between genotypes, the egress-bottleneck assignment in Step 3 is wrong.", "Acceptor rescue: supplying an exogenous lipid acceptor (apoA-I/HDL or lipid-free recombinant ApoE3) or ABCA1 overexpression should reduce the APOE4 excess of SMPD1, GBA, HEXA and v-ATPase transcripts and shrink LAMP1+ area toward APOE3 values; no normalization would weaken the compensatory-induction claim.", "Direction test of hydrolase induction: partial SMPD1/GBA inhibition or knockdown in APOE4 microglia should not reduce, and should if anything increase, lysosomal lipid accumulation and LAMP1+ area. If blocking these hydrolases reduces lysosomal expansion, hydrolase activity is driving the phenotype and the model is falsified.", "Mito-nuclear mismatch: BN-PAGE or MT-CO1/NDUFB8 protein ratio should show reduced assembled complex IV/V per nuclear-encoded subunit in APOE4, with lower maximal and spare respiration despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts. If assembled complexes and FCCP-stimulated respiration scale up with the nuclear transcript increase, Step 5 is falsified while Steps 1-3 can survive.", "Focus-rejection test: inhibiting SCD or DGAT1, or knocking down SREBF1, should not normalize the lysosomal hydrolase signature in APOE4 microglia, because the lipogenesis/acyl-remodeling set is not elevated above the global shift (set mean +1.69, permutation p=0.61). If SCD or SREBF1 inhibition abolishes the lysosomal signature, the primary bottleneck has been misassigned to lysosomal egress.", "Genotype specificity: the hydrolase-minus-egress transcript gap (+2.39 here) should be reproduced in an independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia pair under mock conditions; absence of the gap, or an equally large gap in a genotype-matched control comparison, would weaken the hypothesis."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits than APOE3 (lysosome set mean +2.85 vs global mean +1.39, permutation p=0.0015; hydrolase+acidification subset mean +4.32, p\u003c0.001), together with elevated TFEB; expansion and acidification of the compartment are inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): the membrane-lipid (sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid) hydrolase branch is the most elevated sub-branch (SMPD1 +5.63, GBA +6.72, HEXA +5.72, GBA2 +2.65, HEXB +2.24, GLA +1.51; set permutation p=0.024), indicating that the induced program is biased toward degradation of ingested and endogenous membrane lipid rather than bulk proteolysis (CTSS is decreased, -5.63).", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): transcripts for the lipid egress/acceptor arm rise only at or below the global shift (APOE +1.24, 38th percentile; NPC2 +1.17; ABCA7 +2.14; LAMP1 +1.38; CLN3 +1.17), and the hydrolase-minus-egress contrast is +2.39 (permutation p=0.0024). We propose that post-hydrolysis export/re-esterification of sphingoid bases, sterols and free fatty acids is the limiting step, so lysosomal lipid catabolites accumulate and drive the compensatory hydrolase/v-ATPase induction rather than being cleared by it.", "Step 4 (inferred flux): the accumulating catabolites raise demand for mitochondrial oxidation, matched by coordinated induction of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and TCA transcripts (nuclear OXPHOS subunit set mean +2.81, permutation p=0.0006; OGDH +8.61, MDH1 +8.72, MPC2 +8.00, SLC25A1 +4.53).", "Step 5 (secondary amplifier, measured RNA): the mtDNA-encoded core subunits do not follow (MT-ATP6 -3.42, MT-CYB -2.28, MT-ND4 -1.82, MT-CO2 -1.32; mtDNA set mean -0.82, p=0.048), predicting a mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch in which assembly of complexes III/IV/V, not nuclear subunit supply, caps the oxidative sink; assembled-complex levels and respiration were not measured.", "Step 6 (inferred cell state): the combination of a substrate-limited lysosome and a capped oxidative sink shifts APOE4 microglia away from homeostatic/secretory functions (CSF1 -5.86, CTSS -5.63) toward a storage-and-catabolism state, without requiring any change in de novo lipogenesis or acyl-chain remodeling."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a compensatory lysosomal membrane-lipid hydrolase program set by a limiting post-hydrolysis lipid egress step, with an unmatched mito-nuclear OXPHOS arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23295979027434183, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010629216488511315, "cosine_similarity": 0.14092711865406377, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6748122977346278, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23295979027434183, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010629216488511315, "cosine_similarity": 0.14092711865406377, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6748122977346278, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.81635125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 406}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_062", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so all program statements are made against that list's own background (77.1% positive, median |effect| 1.97); genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged. The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved, so RNA magnitudes are treated as ordinal only.", "Both modalities are globally skewed positive (RNA 1705/2212 positive; spots 64/92 positive, median +0.485 log2), so a possible normalization or composition offset exists; only sign coherence and magnitude relative to that background are interpreted.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme/carrier capacity in the same direction, but no flux, respiration, ATP, NADPH, metabolite or cholesterol pool was measured; oxidative throughput, lysosomal degradation rate and substrate routing are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (all 92 spots have 2-6 candidate genes; 60/92 include keratin/actin candidates), so no spot is assigned to a single protein; spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction. Multiple cathepsin-containing spots of both signs are assumed to reflect proteoform/co-migration heterogeneity rather than an unambiguous decrease.", "Genes within a program are not statistically independent (shared regulators, co-detection), so the quoted binomial and permutation p-values are descriptive coherence measures, not formal enrichment tests.", "The astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins and metabolites; some transcript differences may be secondary to genotype-dependent astrocyte-microglia exchange rather than microglia-intrinsic APOE4 effects.", "Any ATP-, redox- or degradative-reserve deficit is assumed to be revealed only under a future challenge; the measured mock condition is assumed to be a compensated steady state."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture) occupy a coordinated oxidation-committed cell state rather than a single bottlenecked pathway: transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases/v-ATPase and lysosomal solute export rise together with mitochondrial carrier/import machinery, TCA/anaplerotic enzymes and OXPHOS subunits (27/27 represented OXPHOS members positive, 12/12 TCA members positive with median effect +5.0 on the reported log scale, versus a selected-list background of 77.1% positive and median |effect| 1.97), while the committed cytosolic glucose steps and the pentose-phosphate branch are among the minority of decreased transcripts (HK2, HK3, PFKP, PGD, TALDO1) despite increased glucose transporters. We propose that degradative (lysosomal) substrate liberation plus increased mitochondrial import capacity re-routes catabolic carbon and reductive metabolism toward mitochondria; the assigned sterol focus is rejected as the primary driver because sterol synthesis, uptake, esterification and export transcripts move no more than the selected-list background (sign and magnitude indistinguishable) and no protein spot carries any sterol-pathway candidate. Increased abundance of transcripts is capacity, not measured flux; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective bioenergetics (primary discriminator): in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, extracellular-flux assay should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption and a lower ECAR/OCR ratio and lower glycolytic capacity in APOE4. If APOE4 shows equal or lower ATP-linked respiration together with the same transcript pattern, the mechanism is weakened and the failed-compensation alternative (transcriptional upregulation compensating for defective mitochondria) is favoured.", "Prospective substrate-routing test: 13C6-glucose tracing should show reduced APOE4 labelling of lactate and of PPP-derived ribose-5-phosphate/6-phosphogluconate, with equal or increased fractional TCA-intermediate labelling from glutamine/fatty-acid tracers. Preserved or increased glucose flux into lactate and PPP in APOE4 would falsify Step 4.", "Prospective pharmacological asymmetry: APOE4 cells should lose ATP/viability more than APOE3 upon MPC inhibition (UK5099) or ETC inhibition (oligomycin, rotenone), and less than APOE3 upon 2-deoxyglucose. Equal or greater 2-DG sensitivity in APOE4 with no differential oligomycin sensitivity would weaken the routing claim.", "Prospective lysosome-to-mitochondrion coupling test: acute lysosomal inhibition (bafilomycin A1, or cathepsin/lysosomal-lipase inhibition) should suppress oxygen consumption more in APOE4 than APOE3. No differential OCR suppression would falsify Step 1 to Step 2 coupling and reduce the mechanism to an autonomous mitochondrial program.", "Prospective challenge-revealed reserve (explicitly not a claim about the mock condition): oxidant challenge (menadione, H2O2) or G6PD inhibition (6-aminonicotinamide) should reduce APOE4 viability/GSH:GSSG more than APOE3. Equal sensitivity would leave Step 5 unsupported without disproving Steps 1-4.", "Prospective targeted protein test: quantitative immunoblot or targeted MS should show increased mature CTSD/CTSB, MPC2, OGDH and MDH1 protein in APOE4. If unambiguous quantification instead reproduces the negative direction of the cathepsin-containing spots protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 and the MDH1-containing protein_spot:050, the transcript-to-capacity assumption fails and the mechanism is weakened.", "Sterol-focus falsifier already partly met and further testable: filipin/cholesterol-ester quantification and SREBP2-target induction should show no greater APOE4 difference than the general transcriptional shift; a strong, selective cholesterol-sequestration phenotype (large lysosomal free-cholesterol increase with LDLR/HMGCR super-induction) would favour the rejected sterol mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured transcripts, inferred compartment expansion): APOE4 microglia show coherent elevation of lysosomal hydrolase, v-ATPase and lysosomal-transport transcripts plus the lysosomal-biogenesis factor TFEB (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:SLC38A7, gene:SLC17A5; 26/28 represented members positive, binomial p=0.044 against the 77.1% positive background), consistent with an enlarged degradative compartment that liberates amino acids and lipid-derived carbon. The liberated metabolite pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 2 (measured transcripts, inferred capacity): Transcripts for mitochondrial substrate carriers and protein-import machinery rise strongly - pyruvate carrier gene:MPC2 (+7.98), citrate carrier gene:SLC25A1, adenine-nucleotide carrier gene:SLC25A5, oxoglutarate carrier gene:SLC25A11, aspartate/glutamate carrier gene:SLC25A13, NAD+ carrier gene:SLC25A51, mitoferrin gene:SLC25A37, gene:SLC25A46, with gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:TUFM (11/13 represented SLC25 members positive). This increases the capacity to deliver pyruvate, amino-acid carbon and cofactors into mitochondria.", "Step 3 (measured transcripts, inferred oxidative capacity): TCA/anaplerotic and OXPHOS transcripts increase coherently above background - gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:BCAT2, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:GLUD1, gene:IDH3G, gene:IDH3B, gene:SDHB (12/12 positive, permutation p=2.5e-4 for magnitude) and gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFB2, gene:UQCRB, gene:ATP5F1B (27/27 represented OXPHOS subunits positive, binomial p=0.002), i.e. expanded oxidative machinery rather than an isolated stress marker.", "Step 4 (measured transcripts, routing change): In the same list, the committed cytosolic glucose steps and the pentose-phosphate branch fall - gene:HK2 (-3.67), gene:PFKP (-3.08), gene:HK3 (-1.12), gene:TALDO1 (-2.32), gene:PGD (-1.30) - while glucose transporters rise (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3) and gene:GPI, gene:PFKM, gene:ENO1 stay positive. Glycolysis/PPP is the only queried metabolic program with balanced-to-negative signs (5 of 10 negative versus 22.9% negative background), indicating de-commitment of glucose carbon to the cytosolic branch rather than reduced glucose access.", "Step 5 (measured transcripts, inferred redox partitioning): Reductive and peroxide-handling capacity shifts toward the mitochondrial compartment (gene:NNT, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:PRDX2, gene:GPX4, gene:GSS, gene:ME1, gene:TXNDC17 positive) while the cytosolic NADPH-generating PPP transcripts decline (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1).", "Step 6 (state and its consequence): The net APOE4 state is lysosome-fed and oxidation-committed. Lipid/sterol handling transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:SOAT1, gene:APOE, gene:NPC2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24, gene:SREBF2, gene:MYLIP, gene:CH25H, gene:CYP27A1) rise no more than list background and are treated as an accompanying supply arm, not the driver. In the supplied mock condition this predicts higher oxidative throughput and lower glycolytic/cytosolic-NADPH reserve; an actual deficit in ATP or redox buffering is predicted only under a future challenge (ETC inhibition, oxidant load), not asserted for the measured condition."], "title": "Lysosome-fed expansion of mitochondrial substrate import and oxidative catabolism, with de-commitment of cytosolic glycolysis/PPP, in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22254735442897758, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06672405871801097, "cosine_similarity": 0.1400668125912806, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_062", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6347411003236245, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22254735442897758, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06672405871801097, "cosine_similarity": 0.1400668125912806, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6347411003236245, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.271871, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 98}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive); pathway claims are therefore made only against this dataset's own background, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effect column is preserved; only signs, ranks and within-dataset comparisons are used, never absolute fold-change magnitudes.", "Probe-based 10X Flex quantification of mitochondrially encoded transcripts is assumed to be at least rank-faithful. This assumption is explicitly weak here: gene:MT-ND4 and gene:MT-ND4L come from one bicistronic transcript yet have opposite signs, and gene:MT-ND5 is also positive, so the mtDNA-side measurement may be partly technical.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein pool; no mitochondrial protein, assembled-complex, mtDNA copy-number, respirometry, ROS or lipid measurement was supplied.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins (each lists up to six candidate genes) and are not used as evidence for any specific enzyme in this mechanism.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any ambient-RNA contribution are assumed not to differ systematically between APOE3 and APOE4 wells; the global positive shift of the RNA list may instead reflect normalisation, capture depth or composition differences.", "Steady-state abundance differences are assumed to reflect the same cell state rather than a difference in microglial maturation stage at day 30."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a stoichiometric mismatch in respiratory-chain construction: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit, TCA-cycle and NADH-shuttle/carrier transcripts are coordinately higher (38/38 detected NDUF/UQCR/COX/SDH/ATP5 genes positive; MDH1, GOT1, OGDH, MPC2, SLC25A11 among the largest positive effects), while four of the six detected mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are among the most statistically extreme decreases. We hypothesise that mtDNA-encoded subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply or substrate supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembling complexes III, IV and V, so the elevated nuclear program does not translate into proportionally increased assembled holoenzyme; the resulting reduction pressure and stress relay is proposed to drive the co-observed redox (PRDX/TXN/GPX4), integrated-stress (DELE1, EIF2AK3, DDIT3, ATF6) and TFEB-associated lysosomal transcript increases. Causality is not established by these data; only steady-state RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Primary discriminating test: blue-native PAGE with in-gel activity and respirometry on APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show fewer fully assembled complex III2, IV and V holoenzymes and accumulated nuclear-subunit-containing subassemblies per unit mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase or TOMM20 normalised), with lower FCCP-stimulated maximal respiration and a higher proton-leak fraction, despite higher nuclear subunit transcripts. If assembled CIII/CIV/CV levels and CIV/CV in-gel activity per mitochondrial mass are equal or higher in APOE4, the proposed bottleneck is falsified.", "Independent re-measurement of mtDNA-encoded transcripts by probe-independent qPCR or RNA-FISH, normalised to mtDNA copy number, should show lower MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 per mtDNA in APOE4, and MT-ND4 and MT-ND4L should move concordantly. Unchanged mt-mRNA per mtDNA, or persistent MT-ND4/MT-ND4L discordance, would show the core observation is a quantification artifact and would collapse the mechanism.", "Occlusion test: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature (higher nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts, DDIT3, PRDX3, TFEB-target lysosomal genes) and should produce a markedly smaller incremental change in APOE4. If APOE3 fails to phenocopy while APOE4 responds fully, an mtDNA-expression bottleneck is unlikely.", "Ordering test: ISRIB or EIF2AK1/HRI knockdown should lower DDIT3 and other ISR targets without restoring assembled complex IV/V or mt-transcript levels. If ISR inhibition restores mt transcripts and complex assembly, the causal direction is reversed and the ISR is upstream, not downstream.", "Supply-side rescue: raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression or increased mtDNA copy number) should increase assembled CIV/CV and reduce DDIT3, PRDX3 and lysosomal-hydrolase transcripts more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or larger benefit in APOE3 would weaken the genotype-specific claim.", "Rejected-focus control: lipid-pathway transcripts (fatty-acid synthesis, acyl-chain remodelling, glycerolipid enzymes) are not shifted relative to this dataset's own background (median +1.66 versus +1.46 global, Mann-Whitney p = 0.48), so untargeted lipidomics should show no coherent phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine acyl-chain remodelling signature in APOE4; a strong, coherent acyl-chain remodelling signature with unchanged respiratory assembly would favour a membrane-remodelling mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: APOE4 microglia carry coordinately higher nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2 and 33 further members, all positive) plus higher TCA, pyruvate-import and malate-aspartate-shuttle transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACO2). Inferred, not measured: an increased nuclear mitochondrial-biogenesis and substrate-delivery program.", "Measured RNA: the mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2 and gene:MT-ND4 are decreased, several with the most extreme adjusted p-values in the dataset. Inferred, not measured: a reduced inner-membrane pool of mtDNA-encoded subunit protein; no mitochondrial protein, mtDNA copy number or mitochondrial translation rate was measured.", "Inferred bottleneck: because complexes III, IV and V each nucleate on an mtDNA-encoded core (cytb, COX1/2, ATP6/8), a deficit of these subunits stalls assembly; imported nuclear-encoded subunits then accumulate in subcomplexes or are degraded rather than increasing assembled holoenzyme, so respiratory capacity does not scale with the transcript up-shift.", "Inferred flux consequence: increased NADH/substrate delivery (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11) into a distally limited chain raises the reduced state of upstream carriers and the probability of electron leak. Consistent measured RNA correlate only: coordinated increases in gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GPX4; peroxide production and NAD+/NADH were not measured.", "Inferred signalling relay: mitochondrial stress engages an integrated-stress/UPR arm, matched by higher gene:DELE1, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3, gene:ATF6 and gene:SHMT2 transcripts. Kinase activation, eIF2-alpha phosphorylation and ATF4 protein were not measured, so pathway activity is inferred from abundance only.", "Inferred compensation: a TFEB-associated lysosomal-degradative program is raised (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:GAA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C; lysosomal set shifted above the dataset background, Mann-Whitney p = 0.007), which we interpret as increased mitophagic/catabolic capacity that stabilises an APOE4 microglial state with high degradative and low respiratory-assembly efficiency."], "title": "Mitonuclear subunit mismatch: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits respiratory-chain assembly in APOE4 microglia despite an up-shifted nuclear OXPHOS/TCA program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1914115866041428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09349258831903695, "cosine_similarity": 0.13694367302112717, "direction_accuracy": 0.13268608414239483, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6321456310679612, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1914115866041428, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09349258831903695, "cosine_similarity": 0.13694367302112717, "direction_accuracy": 0.13268608414239483, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6321456310679612, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.592743, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 407}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_076", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a large global positive shift (median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); enrichment is therefore judged against that list median, not against zero, and absence of a gene from the list is not evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for protein/pathway capacity, not for flux, enzyme activity, localisation, or causal direction; every activity, transport and compartment statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; spot-level effects are treated as ambiguous evidence and gene assignment (e.g. ANXA1 in spots 043-046) is a hypothesis, not a measurement.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype is the intended contrast; biological replicate number is not supplied, and astrocyte co-culture may supply lipoproteins that differ between wells.", "Key export/storage genes (NPC1, STARD3, ABCA1, ABCG1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE) are not present in the supplied rows, so the export-limitation step rests on NPC2, OSBPL8 and M6PR plus the untested assumption that these represent the wider export/sorting module."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in endolysosomal lipid handling, not in inflammatory or interferon signalling: transcripts for lipid uptake (SCARB1), acidification (ATP6V1H/ATP6V1A/ATP6V0C) and luminal hydrolysis (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB) are among the most strongly elevated rows in the differential list, whereas transcripts for post-hydrolysis lipid export and hydrolase-sorting machinery (NPC2, OSBPL8, M6PR) sit at or below the list median or are decreased. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is the handoff of hydrolysed sterol/sphingolipid out of the endolysosome, so lipid is retained in an expanded degradative compartment while the ER continues to run a lipogenic/sterol-completion program (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS). Interferon and NF-kB gene sets show no enrichment above the strong global positive shift of this differential list, so an inflammatory-activation mechanism is rejected for this comparison.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: bypassing lysosomal sterol export with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or NPC1/NPC2 overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, DHCR24, DHCR7, LDLR, SCARB1) toward APOE3 levels while leaving hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA) high. If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal lipid but SREBP targets stay elevated, the export-handoff bottleneck is wrong and a primary ER/SREBP-autonomous mechanism is favoured.", "Imaging test: filipin or LipidSpot staining with LAMP1 co-localisation should show more unesterified sterol/neutral lipid inside LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal lipid content in APOE4, despite the hydrolase and SCARB1 transcript increases, would weaken the mechanism.", "Capacity-versus-flux test: DQ-BSA and Magic Red cathepsin B assays plus LysoSensor should show equal or increased bulk proteolytic and acidification flux in APOE4 (capacity expanded, hydrolysis not limiting), while BODIPY-cholesterol efflux from lysosomes to ER/plasma membrane is slower. Slower bulk proteolysis in APOE4 would instead point to a hydrolysis or acidification bottleneck and falsify the chosen bottleneck.", "Test of the rejected focus: JAK1/2 inhibition (ruxolitinib) or IFNAR1 blockade should not measurably shrink the APOE4-versus-APOE3 transcriptional difference in these lysosomal and lipogenic genes. If JAK or IFNAR blockade normalises GBA, CTSB, ATP6V1H and SREBF1 differences, an interferon-driven mechanism should replace this one.", "Protein-identity test: MS or immunoblot resolution of 2D spots 043-046 should identify ANXA1 as the increased species. If TALDO1 (whose transcript is decreased) rather than ANXA1 accounts for those spots, the membrane-repair step is falsified without necessarily affecting the lysosomal steps.", "Rescue specificity: SOAT1 inhibition should convert stored cholesteryl ester back to free sterol and worsen the APOE4 lysosomal/membrane phenotype, whereas statin treatment should reduce the lipogenic transcripts but not the lysosomal lipid retention. Statin normalising lysosomal lipid retention would indicate synthesis, not export, is limiting."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mechanism_steps": ["Increased lipoprotein/lipid delivery capacity to the endolysosome in APOE4: SCARB1 transcript is the 99th-percentile row of the differential list (gene:SCARB1, +8.22 in the reported, unspecified-base log unit), with smaller increases for LDLR and CD36; uptake flux itself is not measured and is inferred.", "Coordinated expansion of degradative capacity: TFEB and CLEAR-type targets rise together - v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and luminal hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB) occupy the 83rd-100th percentiles of the list. Acidification and hydrolase activity are inferred, not measured.", "Bottleneck: the machinery that moves hydrolysed lipid out of the lysosome and that sorts new hydrolases into it is not scaled up. NPC2 (35th percentile), OSBPL8 (13th, decreased) and M6PR (15th, decreased) fall below the +1.46 median of this up-shifted list, while NPC1, STARD3, ABCA1/ABCG1 and LIPA were not measured. We infer reduced lysosome-to-ER/contact-site lipid transfer capacity relative to the enlarged influx and hydrolysis capacity.", "Consequence (inferred localisation, not measured): sterol and sphingoid products accumulate inside APOE4 endolysosomes instead of reaching the ER sterol-sensing pool; luminal lipid load is a prediction of the model, not an observation in these data.", "Because the ER sterol pool is not replenished, the lipogenic/sterol-completion program stays on: SREBF1 (92nd percentile), SCD (89th), DHCR24 (85th), DHCR7 (73rd), LSS (67th) and ACAT2 (63rd) are elevated, adding newly made lipid on top of retained lipid. Transcription-factor activity is inferred from target-gene abundance only.", "Membrane stress from this lipid load engages an annexin-type repair/remodelling response: ANXA1 transcript is at the 89th percentile and the four most strongly increased protein spots (protein_spot:045, :046, :044, :043) all contain ANXA1 among their candidate genes; the co-listed candidate TALDO1 has decreased RNA, making ANXA1 the more parsimonious contributor, though spot identity is not established.", "This lipid-handling divergence, rather than inflammatory activation, defines the APOE4 state here: an inflammatory/NF-kB gene set (28 measured rows) and the few available interferon-related rows show mean effects indistinguishable from the list background (permutation p = 0.51 and 0.44), and canonical type-I ISGs (ISG15, MX1/2, OAS1-3, IFIT1-3, STAT1/2, IRF7/9) are absent from the differential list entirely."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal uptake and hydrolase capacity while lysosomal lipid export/sorting lags, sustaining a lipogenic ER program rather than an interferon/NF-kB program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01996630641509613, "cosine_similarity": 0.13638636160787762, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_076", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6500032362459547, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23544289775874164, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01996630641509613, "cosine_similarity": 0.13638636160787762, "direction_accuracy": 0.20388349514563106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6500032362459547, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.87645725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 408}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_031", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, no |effect| below 1) and are treated as relative rank evidence within that list, not as an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base is unspecified and effect magnitudes are used only ordinally.", "The global list is shifted upward (1705/2212 positive, median +1.459), so every set claim is judged against that background by permutation rather than against zero.", "Higher transcript abundance is assumed to translate into higher protein and higher maximal catalytic capacity for the cited carriers and enzymes; no protein, activity, flux, metabolite or lipid measurement of these nodes is supplied.", "ACLY, FASN, ACACA, LIPA, ABCA1 and PLIN2 are absent from the supplied list, so the cytosolic acetyl-CoA-generating and droplet-coating steps are inferred, not observed; a pool of cytosolic citrate or acetyl-CoA is nowhere measured here.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:052 and protein_spot:053 are cited only as ambiguous, non-decisive corroboration because cathepsin genes are among their candidates.", "Mock-condition APOE4 versus APOE3 differences are assumed to arise cell-autonomously in microglia, although the culture contains astrocytes and no cell-type deconvolution of the protein spots is supplied.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect precision cannot be assessed and no causal direction is claimed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a strongly coherent upregulation of TCA-cycle and electron-transport transcripts together with the cytosolic carbon-export machinery (SLC25A1 citrate carrier, SLC25A11, MDH1, GOT1) and the SREBF1-SCD1 lipogenic/esterification arm. We hypothesise that citrate/reducing-equivalent export across the inner mitochondrial membrane is the rate-limiting node in APOE4: raising its capacity diverts oxidative carbon into cytosolic acetyl-CoA and SCD1-dependent monounsaturated acyl-CoA, which is esterified (AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT2) into a MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor neutral-lipid and phospholipid pool, with the concurrent lysosomal hydrolase increase (GBA, SMPD1, GAA, CTSB, CTSD) representing a downstream response to that lipid load rather than its cause. Transcript and spot abundances are measured; flux, enzyme activity, localization and causal direction are inferred and not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass with an increased desaturation index (18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0) and a decreased fraction of 20:4-containing PE/PI; finding no neutral-lipid increase, or a PUFA increase instead of a decrease, would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SLC25A1 (e.g. CTPI-2 or knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the excess neutral-lipid and MUFA phenotype toward APOE3 levels while leaving the TCA/ETC transcript module largely intact; if SLC25A1 inhibition normalises the transcript module but not the lipid phenotype, the proposed bottleneck is misplaced.", "Second discriminating perturbation: SCD1 inhibition should abolish the MUFA excess but should not reduce cytosolic citrate export or the OXPHOS transcript module, whereas ACLY inhibition should phenocopy SLC25A1 inhibition; if the lipid phenotype is ACLY-independent, the citrate route is wrong and an ACSS2/acetate or uptake-driven route should be favoured.", "13C-glucose and 13C-glutamine tracing should show greater label incorporation into palmitate/oleate and into cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or lower incorporation despite the higher transcript module would show the difference is capacity without flux and would weaken the mechanism.", "Respirometry should show equal or higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption in APOE4; a lower oxygen consumption rate with the higher OXPHOS transcript module would instead support a compensatory-dysfunction interpretation and weaken this hypothesis.", "Blocking esterification (DGAT1 plus SOAT1 inhibition) should redirect the excess acyl chains into free fatty acid and lysophospholipid pools and should not reduce the lysosomal hydrolase transcript increase if that increase is truly downstream of stored lipid; loss of the hydrolase phenotype under sterol-uptake blockade alone would instead favour a primary lysosomal/uptake mechanism.", "The mechanism predicts that the SCARB1-dependent sterol uptake arm is contributory but not necessary: SCARB1 knockdown should blunt cholesteryl-ester but not triacylglycerol excess; loss of both would favour an uptake-primary rather than an export-primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels across a mitochondrial oxidative module - TCA/pyruvate-entry genes (gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2) and complex I/ETC genes (gene:NDUFA5 and 62 further mitochondrial transcripts, 63/66 positive) - which we interpret, but have not measured, as increased mitochondrial oxidative capacity rather than increased flux.", "Step 2 (inferred bottleneck): Export of mitochondrial carbon and reducing equivalents to the cytosol is the proposed rate-limiting step; APOE4 raises the transcripts encoding this node (gene:SLC25A1 citrate carrier, gene:SLC25A11 oxoglutarate/malate carrier, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1), so an equivalent oxidative program is predicted to deliver more cytosolic citrate/acetyl-CoA precursor in APOE4 than in APOE3.", "Step 3 (inferred activation): Increased cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability, supplemented by the acetate route (gene:ACSS2), is predicted to sustain SREBP-1 processing and target-gene output; consistent with this, gene:SREBF1 and its canonical target gene:SCD are among the higher-ranked transcripts in the list.", "Step 4 (inferred acyl-chain bias): Elevated SCD1 activity with reduced long-chain/PUFA-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 both decreased) is predicted to shift the acyl-CoA pool toward monounsaturated 16:1/18:1 species and away from 20:4-containing species.", "Step 5 (inferred flux to storage): Increased glycerolipid and sterol esterification capacity (gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) plus phospholipid remodelling capacity (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2) channels these MUFA-rich acyl chains into triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and MUFA-remodelled phospholipids; increased lipoprotein/scavenger uptake capacity (gene:SCARB1) can add exogenous sterol substrate.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): The resulting esterified lipid load elicits a coordinated lysosomal hydrolase response (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD), which we place downstream of, not upstream of, the lipogenic shift.", "Step 7 (inferred trade-off): Carbon committed to export and esterification is unavailable for the homeostatic myeloid program, consistent with the strong decreases in myeloid identity/effector transcripts (gene:CTSS, gene:CSF1, gene:SPN); this step is the weakest and could equally reflect an independent identity change."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial carbon-export capacity (SLC25A1/malate-aspartate node), converting an upregulated TCA-ETC program into SREBP1-SCD1 monounsaturated lipogenesis and esterified lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42570062400768005, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20314933037436497, "cosine_similarity": 0.13486397129847932, "direction_accuracy": 0.3268608414239482, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mean_absolute_error": 0.695663430420712, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42570062400768005, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.20314933037436497, "cosine_similarity": 0.13486397129847932, "direction_accuracy": 0.3268608414239482, "mean_absolute_error": 0.695663430420712, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8522645, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 409}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_078", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strongly positive global mean (+1.39 in the unspecified reported log unit); all claims of pathway direction are therefore made relative to that selected background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript changes for M6PR, AP1M1, STX16, GOSR1, BET1L, VAMP2, STXBP5 and GCC2 translate into proportionally reduced protein and reduced TGN-export/retrograde carrier flux; none of these proteins, their localisation, or any transport rate was measured here.", "Hydrolase transcript induction reflects a TFEB/CLEAR-type compensatory response to luminal substrate rather than a genotype-driven increase in achieved catabolic flux; TFEB nuclear localisation and phosphorylation were not measured.", "No lipid species were measured in this dataset, so glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2, sphingomyelin and ceramide pools are inferred targets of the prediction, never observed quantities.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and cannot be assigned to a unique protein; spots containing CTSB/CTSD/HEXB candidates are treated as ambiguous and partly discordant rather than as hydrolase measurements.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the metadata, and the astrocyte co-culture contributes comparably to both genotypes; replicate number was not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be judged.", "Direction of causation between the sorting-module decrease and the hydrolase induction is assumed, not established; a cross-sectional genotype contrast cannot order these events."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the transcript program for lysosomal sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, HEXA/HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, GLA, SGSH, GM2A) is induced far above the already positive global shift of this selected differential-expression list, while the trans-Golgi export and endosome-to-TGN retrograde sorting module (M6PR, AP1M1, GOLPH3L, GCC2, STX16, GOSR1, BET1L, VAMP2, STXBP5) is coordinately reduced. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is not hydrolase gene dosage and not late-endosome/lysosome fusion capacity (RAB7A, ARL8B, EPG5, VPS18 are up), but SNARE- and MPR-dependent delivery of newly synthesised hydrolases from the TGN to endolysosomes; the resulting mismatch would leave per-lysosome glycosphingolipid-degrading activity subnormal despite elevated enzyme transcripts, and the hydrolase induction is read as a compensatory TFEB-associated response rather than as increased catabolic flux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring TGN export/retrograde sorting in APOE4 microglia (re-expression of M6PR plus STX16, or AP1M1 re-expression) should raise the endolysosome-associated fraction of GBA/HEXA/HEXB protein and their in-lysosome enzymatic activity, lower glucosylceramide and GM2/GA2 by lipidomics, and secondarily damp the TFEB-associated hydrolase transcript program, all without needing to change hydrolase transcription first. If M6PR/STX16 restoration normalises hydrolase localisation and activity but leaves glycosphingolipid levels and lysosome morphology unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Contrasting arm: over-expressing GBA or HEXA/HEXB cDNA in APOE4 microglia should NOT normalise glycosphingolipid load if delivery is limiting, because enzyme protein would remain mislocalised; measurable rescue by simple hydrolase over-expression would weaken the mechanism and favour a gene-dosage or activity-deficit model.", "Enzyme-activity versus abundance split: in APOE4 versus APOE3, mature lysosomal enzyme activity per lysosome (fluorogenic 4-MU-glucoside/4-MU-GlcNAc assays on purified lysosomes) should be equal or lower despite higher transcripts, and secreted (medium) hydrolase activity should be higher; equal secretion with proportionally higher lysosomal activity would falsify the delivery bottleneck and support genuine catabolic upregulation.", "Localisation test: pulse-chase or surface/medium capture of newly synthesised M6P-tagged cargo should show slower TGN exit and increased missorting in APOE4; unchanged kinetics would weaken step 2.", "Autophagy arm: STX17 reduction predicts delayed autophagosome-lysosome fusion (accumulated LC3-II/SQSTM1 without increased flux under bafilomycin); normal flux would weaken step 6 without necessarily refuting the sorting bottleneck.", "Specificity: blocking de novo sphingolipid synthesis with myriocin should have a smaller effect on the APOE4/APOE3 lipid difference than restoring the sorting module, since the biosynthetic transcript set is not enriched above background here; a large myriocin effect would favour a synthesis-driven alternative.", "Negative control for the global shift: gene sets matched for the same effect-size distribution but unrelated to endolysosomal sorting (for example mitochondrial NDUF genes, which are also up) should not show the paired up-hydrolase/down-SNARE pattern; if the up/down split is not reproducible in an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement of the same lines, the pattern is a selection artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype (isogenic, mock) lowers expression of the TGN-export/retrograde sorting module: the CD-mannose-6-phosphate receptor M6PR and the AP-1 mu subunit AP1M1 fall, together with the TGN golgin GCC2 and GOLPH3L, and with the SNARE/SM proteins that execute endosome-to-TGN and Golgi fusion (STX16, GOSR1, BET1L, VAMP2, STXBP5).", "Reduced abundance of these carriers and SNAREs is inferred (not measured) to lower the flux of M6P-tagged hydrolase cargo out of the TGN and to slow MPR retrieval, so a larger fraction of newly synthesised hydrolase protein is mistargeted or secreted rather than reaching the endolysosome lumen. Retromer/sorting-nexin transcripts (VPS26A, SNX3, IGF2R, GNPTG) rise, which we interpret as partial compensation on the retrieval and tagging arms.", "Delivery-limited hydrolase loading lowers lysosomal glycosphingolipid catabolic activity per lysosome (activity and flux inferred; no enzyme-activity or lipid measurement exists in this dataset), so glucosylceramide, GM2/GA2 gangliosides, sphingomyelin and heparan-sulfate-derived substrates are predicted, not observed, to accumulate.", "Luminal substrate load activates a TFEB/CLEAR-type transcriptional response, seen as coordinated induction of TFEB itself and of the sphingolipid-hydrolase and general hydrolase set (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, NAGLU, GLA, SGSH, GM2A, CTSB, CTSD, GAA) plus v-ATPase subunits; this is a compensatory feedback arm, not evidence of achieved turnover.", "Because the biosynthetic arm is unchanged relative to background (KDSR, CERS4, CERS6, ST3GAL5, CERK, ORMDL2 as a set are not enriched; SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1, CERT1, ASAH1, PSAP were not measured), continued ceramide and glycosphingolipid input meets a delivery-limited disposal step, and the imbalance, not synthesis rate, sets the steady-state lipid load.", "Downstream, late-endosome/lysosome fusion and positioning genes rise (RAB7A, ARL8B, EPG5, VPS18, CHMP4B) while the autophagosome-lysosome SNARE STX17 falls, predicting enlarged, substrate-loaded but fusion-competent lysosomes with impaired autophagic clearance, which we propose as the APOE4-specific cell state under mock conditions."], "title": "TGN-export/retrograde SNARE-sorting bottleneck uncouples an induced lysosomal glycosphingolipid-hydrolase program from sphingolipid turnover flux in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.09926767254633477, "cosine_similarity": 0.13392390903167656, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_078", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6588964401294498, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.07045009784735812, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.09926767254633477, "cosine_similarity": 0.13392390903167656, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6588964401294498, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.4446185, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 410}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Gene-to-function assignments and regulatory links are unverified background knowledge; literature and database retrieval were disabled. RNA rows are selected differential-expression results: 1,705/2,212 are positive (77.1%). Missing genes are unknown, not unchanged. Program coherence is descriptive, with correlated members and no formal enrichment inference. RNA effects cannot be converted to log2 or directly compared with protein-spot log2 effects.", "TFEB RNA reflects increased TFEB-dependent lysosomal output, and enough of the encoded machinery becomes correctly localized, assembled, and active to increase throughput. These are unmeasured assumptions. The data do not identify TFEB as a unique initiating cause or establish cell-intrinsic signaling independently of astrocytes.", "Constitutive extracellular cargo is available in the mock co-culture, and microglial viability, cell size, cargo supply, and cell-state composition do not alone explain the inferred throughput difference. No endogenous cargo abundance or accumulated substrate pool was supplied.", "Cytoskeletal remodeling remains sufficient for ordinary endocytic entry despite lower gene:ACTB, gene:MYH9, gene:RAC2 (-1.965), and gene:PAK2 (-1.366). Higher gene:ARHGDIA (+10.610) cannot establish Rho-family inhibition: lower gene:ARHGDIB (-1.980) and gene:FAM49B (-5.830) complicate that interpretation. These RNAs do not identify a rate-limiting phagocytic defect or establish effects on large-target ingestion.", "All 92 protein spots have multiple candidate identities. protein_spot:052 increases by +2.138 log2 (candidates ACTB, CTSL, TPM3, CLIC1, NT5C1A), and protein_spot:053 by +1.536 (TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1), compatible with remodeling but not confirmation of any named protein. Opposing protein_spot:064 is -1.202 (ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1), protein_spot:065 is -0.926 (ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART), and protein_spot:069 is -1.379 (ACTB, CTSD, GPS2). These may indicate altered species or a functional shortfall; they cannot be assigned uniquely or counted as independent confirmations.", "Failed compensation is the strongest functional alternative: increased lysosomal RNAs could coexist with poor acidification or delivery. Coordinated entry, sorting, pump, and hydrolase increases give a modest preference to increased processing, but the negative spots, gene:WASHC4, and gene:CTSS prevent a strong choice from abundance alone. Basal cargo-degradation flux is decisive and unknown.", "The strong respiratory pattern remains unexplained: 38/100 queried nuclear respiratory subunit/assembly genes are represented and all increase, while represented mitochondrial RNAs include gene:MT-ATP6 (-3.351), gene:MT-CO2 (-1.328), gene:MT-CYB (-2.322), gene:MT-ND4 (-1.802), gene:MT-ND4L (+1.951), and gene:MT-ND5 (+1.929). This does not demonstrate ATP sufficiency, respiratory failure, or a causal energy-supply branch of the selected mechanism."], "claim": "In mock-treated, day-30 APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 favors a TFEB-associated lysosomal biogenesis state that increases completed degradation of constitutively internalized cargo relative to isogenic APOE3. Endosomal sorting and local actin remodeling support this proposed increase in throughput. This is a causal hypothesis motivated by abundance patterns, not an established activity or flux difference.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective test in the same day-30 mock co-culture: track labeled endogenous astrocyte-derived cargo, verifying that labeling preserves astrocyte release and microglial state. With matched extracellular supply and viability, distinguish surface binding, internalization, and degradation using pulse-chase imaging plus a calibrated, pH-corrected proteolysis readout. APOE4 should complete more cargo degradation per microglial cell per hour without prolonged residence of internalized cargo. Equal or lower completed flux, particularly with longer residence despite increased lysosomal output, would weaken the selected mechanism and favor failed compensation.", "Prospective causal perturbation: partially suppress TFEB in APOE4 microglia using two independent CRISPRi guides, titrated to normalize lysosomal transcriptional output toward APOE3 while preserving viability. Include matched APOE3 controls and a guide-resistant TFEB rescue. The APOE4 excess in completed cargo degradation should diminish disproportionately as the expanded lysosomal output normalizes, and return with rescue. Persistence of excess flux after verified normalization of TFEB-dependent output, or reduced expression without the predicted functional difference, would weaken TFEB-dependent mediation. A nonspecific loss of flux in both genotypes would not establish the proposed mechanism.", "Prospective discriminator of compensation: independently measure calibrated lysosomal pH, mature cathepsin activity, and total active degradative compartment per viable cell under mock conditions. The model predicts a larger functional compartment with preserved acidification; it does not require a lower pH or faster cleavage per individual lysosome. Impaired acidification and lower active proteolysis despite the RNA program would weaken successful processing. A separate large-particle loading assay tests reserve only; failure confined to that challenge cannot establish a basal defect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["1. APOE4 biases microglia toward a lysosomal biogenesis state. Higher TFEB RNA (gene:TFEB, +2.385) and LAMP1 RNA (gene:LAMP1, +1.377) motivate the inference that greater TFEB-dependent transcriptional output expands the lysosomal compartment. TFEB nuclear localization, transcriptional activity, and organelle abundance were not measured; the initiating signal is unidentified. All RNA effects here retain the supplied, unspecified logarithm base.", "2. Coordinated membrane-entry and actin-turnover remodeling supplies this compartment with constitutive endocytic cargo: gene:DNM2 (+5.822), gene:CLTB (+2.099), gene:ARPC1B (+2.154), gene:ARPC4 (+1.928), gene:ARPC5 (+1.935), and gene:CFL1 (+1.801) increase. The proposed functional connection is greater support for endocytic budding and local actin turnover, not a measured increase in uptake. gene:ACTB (-4.975) and gene:MYH9 (-6.384) decrease, so uniform cytoskeletal activation is not inferred.", "3. Increased sorting machinery sustains delivery to, and membrane retrieval around, degradative compartments: gene:RAB7A (+2.654), gene:VPS26A (+4.865), gene:AP5M1 (+9.780), gene:AP5S1 (+4.390), and gene:AP5Z1 (+3.781). Their proposed cooperation with entry machinery maintains cargo passage through the endolysosomal system; increased retrieval transcripts alone do not establish forward flux. Decreased gene:WASHC4 (-2.102) is an opposing observation.", "4. The expanded compartment processes delivered cargo through increased acidification and hydrolytic capacity, inferred from gene:ATP6V1A (+4.225), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.698), gene:ATP6V1H (+6.880), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.507), gene:CTSB (+5.520), gene:CTSD (+2.864), gene:GAA (+9.961), gene:GBA (+6.713), and gene:HEXB (+2.171). This requires functional pumps and mature enzymes; gene:CTSS (-5.566) shows that protease remodeling is selective. Protein-spot compatibility and contradictions are retained in the assumptions.", "5. Coupling entry, sorting, and functional lysosomal capacity produces higher completed cargo degradation per viable microglial cell under the actual mock co-culture condition. This is the discriminating inferred outcome. No cargo pool, lysosomal pH, protease activity, or degradation flux was observed, and reduced reserve during a future large-particle challenge would not establish an ongoing defect in this condition."], "title": "APOE4 increases constitutive endolysosomal processing through coordinated lysosomal and trafficking remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06415463574936306, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0920263024326808, "cosine_similarity": 0.1296617719622654, "direction_accuracy": 0.05825242718446602, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6377864077669902, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06415463574936306, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0920263024326808, "cosine_similarity": 0.1296617719622654, "direction_accuracy": 0.05825242718446602, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6377864077669902, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.8128755000000005, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 5}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_064", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA effects are reported in an unspecified logarithm base; only signs, ranks and percentile positions relative to the dataset's own background (median +1.46) are used, never absolute fold magnitudes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a thresholded, selected differential-expression list (all adjusted p\u003c0.05, no |effect|\u003c1), so absence of a gene (e.g. HK1, PFKL, GAPDH, LDHA, PDHA1) means it did not pass the threshold, not that it was measured as unchanged; pathway enrichment is therefore tested within this biased list only.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; enzyme activity, phosphorylation state (e.g. PDH), metabolite pools, and metabolic flux were not measured and are inferred.", "Rank-based comparisons against the dataset's own background are assumed to be largely robust to per-cell library normalisation and to the global upward shift; absolute directionality of any single up-regulated gene is not.", "The 92 protein spots each carry several candidate genes and are not treated as identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for a named metabolic enzyme.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype-associated transcript differences could reflect altered astrocyte-microglia cross-talk (e.g. lactate or lipid supply) rather than microglia-autonomous rewiring.", "Causality is not established: the design is an observational isogenic genotype comparison under mock treatment."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a coordinated transcriptional reallocation of carbon handling: transcripts encoding the inducible cytosolic glucose-commitment and pentose-phosphate enzymes (HK2, PFKP, HK3, PFKFB2, PGD, TALDO1) are among the most strongly reduced genes in the dataset, while transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), pyruvate-dehydrogenase activation and lipoamide catabolism (PDP1, DLD), the TCA cycle (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, IDH3G, GOT1), TCA-intermediate carriers (SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits rise well above an already strongly upward selected-DE background. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 is reduced cytosolic glucose-commitment capacity, which makes ATP and biosynthetic supply disproportionately dependent on mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate and of lysosome/lipid/amino-acid-derived acetyl-CoA, leaving little glycolytic reserve for acute demand. Only transcript abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and protein levels of these enzymes are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Extracellular flux analysis of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a lower glycolytic reserve (ECAR increase after oligomycin) and a higher basal OCR:ECAR ratio in APOE4; if APOE4 shows equal or greater glycolytic reserve, the primary bottleneck is refuted.", "Discriminating perturbation: MPC inhibition with UK5099 (or PDHA1 knockdown) should lower ATP and basal OCR and reduce viability substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3, whereas 2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown should impair APOE3 more than APOE4; the reverse or equal sensitivities would weaken the mechanism.", "U-13C6-glucose tracing should show a higher fraction of glucose carbon in m+2 citrate and other TCA intermediates and a lower m+3 lactate fraction in APOE4; unchanged glucose-to-TCA labelling with unchanged lactate labelling would weaken step 2.", "Restoring HK2 (or PFKP) expression in APOE4 microglia should restore glycolytic reserve and reduce the OCR:ECAR ratio without requiring changes in TCA/OXPHOS transcripts; failure to restore reserve would place the bottleneck elsewhere.", "On acute immune challenge (e.g. LPS) APOE4 microglia should fail to mount the normal ECAR/lactate-secretion rise seen in APOE3 while showing a larger drop in ATP; an intact glycolytic switch in APOE4 would refute the vulnerability step.", "Immunoblot/activity assays should confirm lower hexokinase and PFK activity in APOE4 lysates; if HK2/PFKP protein and hexokinase activity are unchanged despite the transcript differences, the transcript-to-capacity inference fails.", "Blue-native PAGE/complex activity should show that assembled complex I/III/IV/V amounts and maximal (FCCP-uncoupled) respiration are not increased in proportion to the nuclear OXPHOS transcript program; a fully proportional increase in assembled complexes would refute the mito-nuclear limitation in step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for the inducible, rate-setting cytosolic glycolytic commitment steps and for pentose-phosphate enzymes are lower in APOE4 (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKFB2 -1.10, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30) while the median of all 2212 selected RNA rows is +1.46 in the same (unspecified-base) logarithm; these genes sit in the lowest ~4-22nd percentile of the effect distribution. Inferred (not measured): reduced maximal hexokinase/phosphofructokinase and PPP capacity, i.e. a lower ceiling on glucose-6-phosphate commitment and on glycolytic reserve.", "Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry and its oxidative disposal are near the top of the distribution (gene:MPC2 +7.98, 99th percentile; gene:DLD +5.54; gene:PDP1 +3.00) together with TCA enzymes and carriers (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50; set median +4.48 vs background +1.45, Mann-Whitney p=1e-05). Inferred: increased carrier-mediated pyruvate import and an increased PDH activation state (PDP1 is a PDH phosphatase; phospho-PDH was not measured), so pyruvate that is made is preferentially oxidised rather than exported as lactate.", "Measured: 39 nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain transcripts are coherently raised above background (median +2.64 vs +1.45, p=5.8e-05; e.g. gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:COX7A2 +3.36). Inferred: a nuclear-driven mitochondrial biogenesis/oxidative program, not a measurement of assembled complex amount or respiration rate.", "Measured: catabolic supply routes that feed acetyl-CoA independently of glycolysis are also raised (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:OXCT1 +4.72, gene:BCAT2 +6.42). Inferred: lysosome-, lipid-, ketone- and branched-chain-amino-acid-derived carbon is routed into the same mitochondrial pipeline, partially substituting for glycolytic carbon.", "Inferred consequence at steady state: under mock conditions glucose uptake capacity is preserved or increased (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73), so basal ATP demand can still be met, but with the commitment step limited the imported glucose is channelled into a narrow, oxidation-dependent pipeline rather than into a rapidly expandable glycolytic/PPP branch.", "Inferred vulnerability: because APOE4 cells lack the HK2/PFKP-dependent glycolytic reserve normally mobilised on immune activation, and because the mtDNA-encoded core subunits needed to assemble the up-regulated nuclear OXPHOS subunits are not concordantly raised (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; weak, n=6, p=0.065), the achievable respiratory ceiling may not expand in proportion to the nuclear program, predicting a narrow bioenergetic envelope and heightened sensitivity to mitochondrial inhibition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia trade glycolytic reserve for obligate mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation: low hexokinase-2/PFKP commitment capacity is the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19361776760329358, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16138575172945396, "cosine_similarity": 0.1274152243168901, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6663236245954692, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19361776760329358, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16138575172945396, "cosine_similarity": 0.1274152243168901, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6663236245954692, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.77270375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 411}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_060", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows up, median +1.46, all |effect|\u003e1) and an unspecified logarithm base; therefore only relative contrasts between gene sets within this table, not absolute directions, are treated as informative.", "Transcript differences for PGD, TALDO1, NADK, HK2, HK3 and PFKP translate into lower enzymatic capacity, and the corresponding metabolic flux is at least partly transcriptionally limited; no flux, NADPH, NADP+, GSH, GSSG, ROS or lipid-peroxide measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and not uniquely identified. The strongly increased spots protein_spot:045 and protein_spot:043 are assumed to reflect ANXA1 (gene:ANXA1 +4.15) rather than TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1 -2.32); if TALDO1 is the true species these spots are direct counter-evidence to Step 4.", "G6PD, IDH1, IDH2, GSR, CAT, TXN, TXNRD1, SOD1/2, GCLC/GCLM, NFE2L2 and TKT are absent from the supplied differential rows; absence is assumed to mean 'not selected/unchanged', not measured stability, so the supply arm is only partially observed.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid and antioxidant substrate (e.g. glutathione precursors) supply is non-cell-autonomous and could itself differ between genotypes.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so genotype rather than treatment is the presumed source of the difference, but batch, differentiation efficiency and cell-composition differences are not excluded by the supplied metadata (biological replicates not reported)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally expand NADPH-consuming processes (scavenger-mediated lipid uptake with lysosomal lipid catabolism, sterol/desaturation-type reductive lipid remodelling, and thiol/peroxide-detoxification enzymes) while transcripts for the glucose-6-phosphate-generating and oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate steps that regenerate cytosolic NADPH are lower than the strong global upward shift of this differential-expression set. We hypothesise that the primary genotype-differentiating bottleneck is cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity per unit peroxide and reductive-biosynthesis demand, leaving APOE4 microglia with a compensatorily up-regulated but supply-limited peroxiredoxin/GPX4 detox system that depends abnormally on mitochondrial NNT/malic-enzyme routes. All statements about flux, NADPH/GSH pool sizes, peroxide load and causal direction are inferences from RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances, not measurements; no redox metabolite, ROS or lipid-peroxidation measurement is present in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway (G6PDi-1, 6-aminonicotinamide, or G6PD/PGD knockdown) at a dose that is near-neutral for APOE3 should produce a significantly larger increase in lipid peroxidation (C11-BODIPY/MDA), a larger fall in NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG, and greater death in APOE4 microglia. Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes, or greater APOE3 sensitivity, would weaken the mechanism.", "Direct state test: baseline (mock) LC-MS or biosensor measurement should show lower NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios and higher oxidised-phospholipid content in APOE4 than APOE3 despite the higher PRDX2/PRDX3/GPX4/MSRA transcripts. If APOE4 shows equal or higher NADPH/NADP+ and no excess oxidised lipid, the supply-limitation claim fails and the redox transcripts should instead be read as a benign, globally driven up-shift.", "Compensation-route test: NNT knockdown or partial uncoupling/complex-I inhibition should selectively raise peroxiredoxin hyperoxidation (PRDX-SO2/3) and lipid peroxidation in APOE4; if the APOE4 excess vulnerability persists unchanged after NNT loss, the mitochondrial compensation step (Step 5) is wrong.", "Rescue test: supplying NADPH-sparing or NADPH-regenerating support (cell-permeable GSH ester, NAC, exogenous nicotinamide riboside, or SCD1 inhibition to lower reductive lipid demand) should normalise APOE4 lipid peroxidation and PRDX/GPX4 transcript induction toward APOE3. Failure to normalise the transcripts while lipid peroxidation falls would indicate the detox program is driven by something other than peroxide load.", "Flux test: 13C1/13C6-glucose tracing should show a lower oxidative-PPP contribution (lower 13CO2 release and lower m+? pattern in pentose phosphates) relative to glycolytic flux in APOE4. Equal or higher oxidative-PPP flux in APOE4 would directly falsify Step 4.", "Specificity test: blocking lipid uptake (SCARB1/CD36 blockade) should reduce the APOE4 peroxide-detox transcript signature and its PPP-inhibitor hypersensitivity; if the hypersensitivity is uptake-independent, the lipid-load origin of the demand (Steps 1-2) is wrong even if the NADPH bottleneck holds.", "Peroxisomal sub-claim (weak, explicitly testable): despite higher gene:SCP2, gene:ACOX1 and peroxisomal gene:PRDX5, the lower gene:ABCD1 predicts no increase, or a decrease, in peroxisomal very-long-chain fatty-acid beta-oxidation flux in APOE4 with C26:0 accumulation. Increased VLCFA oxidation flux with unchanged C26:0 would falsify the peroxisomal component while leaving the cytosolic NADPH bottleneck intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake receptors and the lipid-handling lysosomal program (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MRC1 +1.36, gene:CD163 +1.38, gene:COLEC12 +1.53, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:GPNMB +1.11, gene:TREM2 +1.28; gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:TFEB +2.38). Inferred, not measured: increased flux of exogenous and oxidation-prone lipid into the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred demand): NADPH-consuming reductive lipid remodelling transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SREBF1 +4.67). Inferred: increased cytosolic NADPH draw for desaturation and post-squalene sterol reduction.", "Step 3 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred demand): the thiol/peroxide-detoxification arm, whose turnover is NADPH-dependent, is uniformly higher (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:MSRA +2.64, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:SELENOP +1.12, gene:PLA2G7 +1.13, gene:EPHX1 +1.42, gene:AKR1B1 +1.13, gene:FTH1 +2.53); 15/15 such genes up versus a 77% background up-rate (binomial p=0.020). Inferred: elevated oxidised-lipid/peroxide processing load rather than merely higher enzyme protein.", "Step 4 (measured abundance -\u003e proposed bottleneck): the supply arm moves the other way. Both measured hexokinases and the main phosphofructokinase are down (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:PFKP -3.08), as are pentose-phosphate transcripts gene:PGD -1.30 and gene:TALDO1 -2.32 and gene:NADK -1.14, against a background median of +1.46. Median of the demand set (+2.79) versus the NADPH-producer set (-1.14) gives a gap of 3.93 log units (permutation p=0.012; Mann-Whitney p=0.013). Inferred, not measured: reduced glucose-6-phosphate entry into and cycling through the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway, i.e. lower cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity.", "Step 5 (inferred compensation and coupling): partial compensation is routed through mitochondria (gene:NNT +2.88, gene:ME1 +1.36, with broadly higher OXPHOS transcripts, e.g. gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98). Inferred: cytosolic and mitochondrial peroxiredoxin/glutathione recycling in APOE4 becomes disproportionately dependent on transhydrogenase and proton-motive-force-linked NADPH rather than on the pentose-phosphate pathway.", "Step 6 (predicted state, unmeasured): the net consequence is a lower NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratio and a smaller reserve of reducing equivalents per unit peroxide load in APOE4 than APOE3 at baseline, so the up-regulated PRDX/GPX4/MSRA transcripts are a compensatory response operating near its substrate limit, and APOE4 cells are selectively vulnerable to any further oxidative, lipid or mitochondrial challenge. Causality is not established by these data."], "title": "Cytosolic NADPH regeneration is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: a lipid-scavenging, reductive-detox demand program outruns a downshifted hexokinase/oxidative-PPP supply arm"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30519144851013547, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09722300893691446, "cosine_similarity": 0.12470354390847466, "direction_accuracy": 0.29449838187702265, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6751844660194175, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30519144851013547, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09722300893691446, "cosine_similarity": 0.12470354390847466, "direction_accuracy": 0.29449838187702265, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6751844660194175, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.89470625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 412}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_080", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every row has |effect| \u003e= 1) from a pseudobulk-style APOE4-vs-APOE3 contrast with unreported replicate number; the logarithm base is unspecified, so only signs and relative ranks within the table are used, never absolute fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for pathway capacity only; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, lipid pool sizes, organelle localization and oxidative damage are inferred and were not measured in these data.", "Gene sets used for coherence testing were assembled from background pathway knowledge (unverified, no literature retrieval) after inspecting the table, so the reported p-values are nominal and not corrected for set selection.", "The 70-80% upward skew of the selected RNA rows may be partly technical (normalization, ambient RNA, composition); direction contrasts within a pathway (e.g. gene:CTSB up versus gene:CTSS down) are weighted more than the global shift.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript signal (e.g. gene:APOE, gene:SCARB1) could include astrocyte-derived ambient RNA; cell-type purity was not supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features, not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is used as evidence that a specific protein changed.", "The comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, so the state is treated as a steady-state genotype difference, not a stimulus response."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcript state in which lysosomal hydrolase/acidification and lipid-uptake/esterification programs are elevated together with SREBP-axis sterol-synthesis transcripts, a combination most parsimoniously explained by a bottleneck in egress of lysosome-derived lipid (notably sterol) to the ER, so that total lipid load rises while the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool stays low; the resulting expanded, iron-associated peroxidizable lipid pool is met by an inferred defensive redox remodelling (higher peroxiredoxin/GPX4/glutathione-synthesis and ferritin-heavy transcripts with lower PUFA-activating and lipoxygenase transcripts) rather than by peroxisomal beta-oxidation, which is not supported here. All statements are associational; causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating trafficking test: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, cholesteryl-ester (esterified/free cholesterol ratio, or filipin-positive lysosomal sterol) should be higher while the ER-accessible cholesterol pool reported by an ALOD4/D4H sterol probe should be lower. If ER-accessible sterol is equal to or higher than APOE3 while SREBP-target transcripts remain elevated, the proposed egress bottleneck is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: acute SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) should, in APOE4 cells, lower cholesteryl-ester content, raise ER-accessible sterol and normalize SREBF2/LDLR/DHCR24 transcripts toward APOE3 levels. Persistent SREBP-target elevation after effective ACAT inhibition would weaken step 3.", "Phenocopy test: blocking lysosomal sterol export in APOE3 microglia (U18666A, or NPC1 knockdown) should reproduce the joint signature of higher lysosomal hydrolase plus higher SREBP-axis plus higher GPX4/PRDX2/PRDX3 transcripts. Reproducing the lysosomal and SREBP arms without the peroxide-defense arm would separate the redox response from the lipid bottleneck and falsify step 5 as a downstream consequence.", "Redox load test: baseline oxidized-lipid signal (C11-BODIPY 581/591 oxidized fraction or 4-HNE adducts) should be higher in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher GPX4/PRDX transcripts, and GPX4 and PRDX2 protein should be verifiably higher by targeted immunoblot. Equal or lower baseline lipid peroxidation together with unchanged GPX4/PRDX protein would reject the oxidative-load interpretation and leave only the lipid-trafficking arm.", "Substrate-supply test: because gene:ACSL4 and gene:ALOX15 are lower, APOE4 microglia should be relatively resistant to RSL3-induced ferroptotic death (higher LC50) yet more sensitive to combined GPX4 inhibition plus arachidonic-acid loading than APOE3. Equal RSL3 sensitivity with and without PUFA loading would falsify step 5.", "Reductant-routing test: NNT knockdown or inhibition should lower the NADPH/NADP+ ratio and the GSH/GSSG ratio more in APOE4 than in APOE3 cells. No genotype difference in this dependency would falsify step 6.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C22:0/C26:0 VLCFA ratio, catalase activity, PMP70 puncta) should not differ appreciably between genotypes; a clear peroxisomal flux deficit would indicate a different primary bottleneck than the one proposed."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits and for the CLEAR-network factors TFEB/MITF (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB, gene:MITF), which we interpret (inferred, not measured) as expanded lysosomal degradative capacity rather than a measured increase in lysosome number or hydrolase activity.", "Step 2 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): Scavenger-receptor uptake and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts are concurrently higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:SCP2, gene:NPC2), consistent with inferred routing of internalized lipid into cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol storage; the storage pool itself, efflux via ABCA1/ABCG1 and lysosomal acid lipase were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; inferred): Despite this lipid influx and storage signature, SREBP-axis transcripts are uniformly higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SREBF2, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:SCD, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1). We propose the rate-limiting lesion is lysosome-to-ER egress/handoff of liberated sterol, leaving the ER regulatory sterol pool functionally low (an inferred pool, not measured) and creating a feed-forward loop of continued uptake plus de-novo synthesis.", "Step 4 (inferred consequence): The enlarged, hydrolase-rich and iron-associated lipid compartment (gene:FTH1, gene:SLC25A37 higher) raises the inferred risk of non-enzymatic lipid peroxidation; no peroxide, malondialdehyde or 4-HNE measurement is present in these data.", "Step 5 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred activity): The cells display a peroxide-buffering, ferroptosis-resistant transcript configuration: thiol-peroxidase and glutathione-related transcripts up (gene:GPX4, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:MGST2, gene:GSS, gene:TXNDC17, gene:AKR1A1) while PUFA-CoA activation and enzymatic lipoxygenation transcripts are down (gene:ACSL4, gene:ALOX15, gene:ACSL5), which would lower the peroxidizable PUFA-phospholipid substrate supply.", "Step 6 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred rewiring): Reductant supply appears re-routed rather than simply increased, with mitochondrial/malic NADPH sources up (gene:NNT, gene:ME1) and oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate transcripts down (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1); NADPH/NADP+ ratio and GSH/GSSG were not measured.", "Step 7 (scope limit): A peroxisomal beta-oxidation mechanism is explicitly not adopted: no PEX biogenesis gene, CAT, ACOX2/3, ABCD2/3, HSD17B4 or ether-lipid gene is present in the supplied rows, and the two peroxisomal transporter/oxidase rows available point in opposite directions (gene:ABCD1 lower, gene:ACOX1 only modestly higher)."], "title": "Lysosomal lipid-egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia drives simultaneous sterol-synthesis induction and a ferroptosis-resistant peroxide-buffering shift"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25965550345235017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2030296108964039, "cosine_similarity": 0.12382280280654419, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_080", "mean_absolute_error": 0.683168284789644, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25965550345235017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2030296108964039, "cosine_similarity": 0.12382280280654419, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.683168284789644, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.10618675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 413}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all enrichment statements are made against the internal background of this list (median effect +1.46, all |effect|\u003e1), not against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative ranks within the list are interpreted, never absolute fold changes.", "The reduction in MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 reflects a genuine difference in mitochondrial transcript content per cell rather than a 10X Flex probe/normalisation or cell-quality artifact. MT-ND4L (+1.95) and MT-ND5 (+1.93) move the other way, and MT-ND4L shares a bicistronic transcript with MT-ND4, so this assumption is explicitly fragile.", "Transcript abundance of nuclear OXPHOS, TCA and carrier genes is taken as a proxy for subunit supply; protein abundance, import efficiency, assembly state and enzymatic activity of these components were not measured.", "mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass, membrane potential, oxygen consumption, ATP levels, acetyl-CoA/citrate pools, lipid-droplet content and lipid species were not measured in this dataset and are not claimed as observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous intensity measurements; no spot is assigned to a unique protein, and no spot uniquely reports an OXPHOS subunit.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous or reflect differences in microglial maturation state rather than a direct APOE4 effect on mitochondria.", "Causality is not established: the mitochondrial, lysosomal and lipogenic modules are simultaneous transcript observations and the assigned ordering is a hypothesis."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia coordinately raise nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, TCA-cycle and SLC25-carrier transcripts while transcripts for mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are lower than the strongly positive background of this differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the mtDNA-encoded core, not the nuclear-encoded accessory/matrix machinery, is the rate-limiting component for holo-complex assembly, so respiratory flux fails to scale with the expanded nuclear program; the resulting incompletely oxidised TCA carbon is exported as citrate (SLC25A1) and converted to cytosolic acetyl-CoA (ACSS2, MDH1-linked cycling), feeding a secondary SREBF1-driven lipogenic and glycerolipid/acyl-remodeling program (SCD, FADS1, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, DGAT1), together with a mitochondrial stress relay (DELE1, DDIT3). Only transcript abundances and ambiguous protein-spot intensities were measured; assembly state, flux, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: raising mtDNA-encoded core-subunit supply in APOE4 microglia (TFAM or mitochondrial-transcription boosting, mitochondrial transplantation, or allotopic nuclear-recoded MT-ATP6/MT-CYB expression) should restore assembled complex I/III/IV/V levels on blue-native PAGE and raise CI-linked and maximal oxygen consumption per unit citrate-synthase activity, and should secondarily lower SREBF1, SCD and DGAT1 transcripts and BODIPY-positive neutral-lipid area toward APOE3 levels. Restoration of assembled complexes without any reduction in the lipogenic program or lipid-droplet content would falsify the proposed downstream limb, and failure to change assembled complex levels at all would falsify the bottleneck itself.", "DIRECTIONALITY TEST: blocking the proposed carbon sink instead of the bottleneck (SLC25A1 inhibition or ACSS2 knockdown) should reduce neutral-lipid storage and SREBF1-target transcripts in APOE4 microglia while leaving the assembled-complex deficit and oxygen-consumption deficit unchanged. If these interventions also normalise respiration, the causal arrow is reversed (lipogenesis constrains respiration) and the hypothesis as ordered is wrong.", "QUANTITATIVE CONSEQUENCE: APOE4 microglia should show a lower ratio of fully assembled complex I to total NDUFA/NDUFB subunit protein, and higher steady-state levels of nuclear-encoded assembly subcomplexes, with mitochondrial mass (TOMM20, citrate synthase) equal to or greater than APOE3. Equal assembled:total ratios with equal respiration despite higher nuclear OXPHOS transcripts would weaken the mechanism and favour a purely transcriptional or maturation-state explanation.", "ARTIFACT CONTROL: targeted RT-qPCR or a non-3'-biased assay of MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 normalised to mtDNA copy number should reproduce the reduction in APOE4. If the mtDNA-encoded transcript difference disappears after mtRNA-fraction-aware renormalisation, or if MT-ND4 and MT-ND4L behave identically as expected for a shared bicistronic transcript, the core observation is a quantification artifact and the hypothesis collapses.", "SPECIFICITY: the effect should be genotype-linked in the isogenic pair, so APOE4-to-APOE3 gene correction in the same background should normalise the nuclear:mtDNA OXPHOS transcript ratio. Persistence of the ratio after correction would indicate a clone- or maturation-driven difference rather than an APOE4 mechanism.", "ALTERNATIVE-MECHANISM TEST: if lysosomal expansion is primary instead, v-ATPase or lysosomal-hydrolase inhibition should worsen the lipid phenotype without changing the assembled-complex deficit, whereas the present hypothesis predicts the complex deficit is upstream and unaffected by lysosomal manipulation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED (RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunits (gene:NDUFA5 +7.3, gene:NDUFS7 +5.7, gene:NDUFS8 +4.9, gene:NDUFB6 +4.6, gene:UQCRC2 +4.0, gene:ATP5ME +5.2, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.7, gene:COX7A2 +3.4, gene:SDHB +1.7; set mean +2.8 vs list background +1.39, permutation p=0.0004) and for TCA/carrier genes (gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:MDH1), whereas mtDNA-encoded core-subunit transcripts run against this global upward shift (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33).", "INFERRED (stoichiometry): the nuclear:mtDNA subunit supply ratio is skewed, so assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V becomes limited by the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core rather than by nuclear-encoded modules; this predicts accumulation of nuclear-encoded assembly intermediates and a lower ratio of holo-complex to total mitochondrial mass. No complexome, mtDNA-copy-number or subunit-protein measurement is present in this dataset.", "INFERRED (flux): electron transport and ATP-synthase capacity per mitochondrion do not rise in proportion to the expanded TCA/carrier transcript program, producing a partial oxidative bottleneck rather than complete respiratory failure.", "INFERRED (stress signalling): imbalanced/unassembled subunits and reduced electron flux engage a mitochondrial-stress-to-cytosol relay; consistent transcript changes are gene:DELE1 +4.8, gene:DDIT3 +2.8, gene:ATF6 +4.0, gene:EIF2AK3 +1.5. The transcript rise in gene:TUFM (+6.5) is read as compensatory upregulation of mitochondrial translation machinery, not as evidence of adequate mtRNA template supply.", "INFERRED (carbon rerouting): TCA carbon that cannot be fully oxidised is exported as citrate through the SLC25A1 carrier (gene:SLC25A1 +4.5) and, with cytosolic malate/acetate handling (gene:MDH1 +8.7, gene:ACSS2 +2.9), enlarges the cytosolic acetyl-CoA pool. Acetyl-CoA, malate and citrate pools were not measured.", "MEASURED (RNA) plus INFERRED (activity): a lipogenic and acyl-chain/glycerolipid remodeling program is co-elevated (gene:SREBF1 +4.7, gene:SCD +4.2, gene:FADS1 +1.6, gene:AGPAT2 +6.3, gene:LPCAT1 +3.1, gene:DGAT1 +1.7), which we place downstream of the oxidative bottleneck as a carbon sink favouring neutral-lipid storage and monounsaturated phospholipid remodeling over fatty-acid oxidation. This lipid arm is only nominally enriched against the biased background (mean +2.2, permutation p=0.12) and is therefore the weakest link in the chain.", "AMBIGUOUS PROTEIN LEVEL: one significantly increased 2D spot lists catalase among its candidate genes (protein_spot:017 +0.77, p=0.001), weakly compatible with increased peroxide handling; the spot contains CORO1C and ENTPD5 as alternative assignments and cannot be treated as an identified protein."], "title": "Mito-nuclear subunit imbalance is the assembly bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, diverting citrate-derived carbon into SREBF1 lipogenesis and membrane remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20633792415906657, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14785765020946978, "cosine_similarity": 0.1194452254478159, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6560582524271845, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20633792415906657, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.14785765020946978, "cosine_similarity": 0.1194452254478159, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6560582524271845, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.896303, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 414}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_026", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the source; all RNA statements are used as a monotone ranking against the dataset's own distribution (median +1.46, mean +1.39, 77% of rows positive), not as literal fold changes.", "The 2212 RNA rows are selected differential results with a floor of |effect| = 1, so absence of a gene (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, ASAH1, LIPA) means it was not among the selected rows, not that it is unchanged; the efflux-limitation step rests partly on this absence.", "Because the whole distribution is shifted upward, relative percentile rank rather than sign is treated as the evidence of pathway-specific regulation; permutation tests use the observed effect distribution as the null.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be an imperfect proxy for enzyme and transporter capacity; no activity, flux, localization or lipid-pool measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each (69 of 92 carry five), so no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein; spot-level claims are hypotheses about identity only.", "Cells are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect the co-culture partner or genotype-dependent lipid exchange between the two cell types rather than microglia-autonomous regulation.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed and pseudo-replication cannot be excluded.", "No causal direction is claimed: APOE4 could act upstream of the lipid-handling programme, or the programme could be a secondary adaptation to a different primary defect."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia not by an interferon or canonical inflammatory program (no ISG/GBP/HLA/STAT1 rows are present among 2212 selected differential rows, and STAT5A/B, STAT6, IRF2 and TNFAIP3 are down), but by a lipid-handling imbalance: transcripts for scavenger uptake (SCARB1) and for a coordinated TFEB/CLEAR-like lysosomal module (v-ATPase subunits plus acid hydrolases GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB) are among the most extreme in the dataset, while transcripts for lipid export/acceptor function are not coordinately raised; we hypothesise that post-hydrolytic lipid efflux is the rate-limiting node, so hydrolysed sterol and fatty acyl products are re-esterified by an up-regulated SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 arm and retained as cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol stores, keeping the ER-accessible sterol pool functionally low and sustaining SREBP-target expression. Causality is not established by these data; all statements about flux, localization and activity are inferences from RNA abundance.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Pharmacological SOAT1/ACAT inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition in mock APOE4 microglia should shrink neutral-lipid droplet content while raising unesterified cholesterol and lowering SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, SCD, LDLR); if efflux is truly limiting, the freed sterol should not be cleared unless an ABCA1-inducing LXR agonist is co-applied. If ACAT/DGAT1 inhibition leaves droplet load and SREBP targets unchanged in APOE4 cells, the esterification-storage step is off the causal path and the mechanism is weakened.", "SCARB1 knockdown or blockade in APOE4 microglia should lower cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol content and reduce TFEB-target hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) toward APOE3 levels. If SCARB1 loss leaves lysosomal hydrolase transcripts and lipid stores unchanged, uptake is not the upstream driver.", "Lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 cultures should show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol per cell, enriched in 16:1 and 18:1 monounsaturated species (SCD) and relatively depleted of arachidonate-containing species (ACSL4/ACSL5 down). Equal or lower cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol in APOE4, or an APOE4-specific PUFA enrichment, would falsify the storage arm.", "Because SMPD1, GBA and HEXA are up but no ceramide-disposal transcript (ASAH1, ACER, SPHK, SGPL1 beyond +1.09) is coordinately raised, ceramide should be increased and sphingomyelin decreased in APOE4 cells. Unchanged ceramide with reduced sphingomyelin would indicate disposal is not limiting for sphingolipids and would narrow the mechanism to the sterol arm.", "TFEB overexpression in APOE4 microglia should reduce, not increase, lipid-droplet burden if the lysosomal module is compensatory; an increase in stored lipid after TFEB overexpression would falsify the compensatory interpretation of step 2.", "NEGATIVE / REJECTION OF THE ASSIGNED FOCUS: targeted assay of ISG15, MX1, IFIT1, OAS1, GBP1, CXCL10 and HLA-DRA transcript and protein should show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 induction under mock, and JAK1/2 or TBK1 inhibition should not normalise the lysosomal-lipid transcript module. Detection of a coherent interferon signature, or reversal of the lysosomal-lipid programme by JAK or TBK1 inhibition, would falsify the claim that this phenotype is interferon-independent."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry a much higher SCARB1 transcript level (gene:SCARB1, +8.22 reported log units, 99.1st percentile of all 2212 selected rows) together with other uptake/opsonic receptor transcripts (gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:C1QA/B/C, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A). We infer, but do not measure, increased delivery of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A coherent lysosomal biogenesis module is raised well above the strongly up-shifted background (dataset median +1.46): TFEB (+2.38), v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51; set permutation p=0.047) and acid hydrolases (GAA +9.96, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.52; set permutation p=0.006; broader lysosome set p=0.0007). We interpret this as a compensatory expansion of degradative capacity in response to substrate load, not as the primary lesion.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck from absence and from low relative rank): The disposal/export arm is not coordinately induced. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PSAP, GRN, ASAH1, SPHK1/2 and S1PR rows are not present among the selected differential results, and the lipid genes that are present with acceptor/egress roles sit near or below the dataset median (APOE +1.24, 38th percentile; NPC2 +1.17, 34.7th; ABCA7 +2.14, 65th; efflux/acceptor set permutation p=0.46). We therefore propose lipid egress from the lysosome/cell as the limiting step. Absence from a filtered differential list is not a measurement of no change; this is the weakest link of the chain.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Storage/esterification capacity is raised (SREBF1 +4.67, 92nd percentile; SCD +4.17, 89th; AGPAT2 +6.29, 97th; LPCAT1 +3.07; DGAT1 +1.72; SOAT1 +1.25; ACAT2 +2.04; DHCR24 +3.69; set permutation p=0.013), while PUFA-CoA activation transcripts fall (ACSL4 -2.14, ACSL5 -3.11). We predict hydrolysis products are routed into monounsaturated cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol stores rather than exported or oxidised.", "Step 5 (inferred pool, not measured): Continued high expression of SREBP targets (SREBF1, SCD, LDLR, INSIG1, DHCR7, DHCR24) despite the large uptake signal implies that the ER-accessible regulatory sterol pool is not sensed as replete, consistent with sterol sequestration in lysosomes and droplets. Neither ER sterol nor droplet content is measured here.", "Step 6 (consequence, secondary): The resulting chronic lysosomal/droplet burden is accompanied by only a modest chemokine tone (CXCL8 +3.11, CXCL16 +3.66, CCL2 +2.12, NLRP3 +1.09, IL18 +1.46) with several NF-kB brakes raised (NFKBIL1 +4.41, NFKBIB +3.68, NFKBIZ +3.07) and no interferon module; the whole NF-kB/TNF set is not enriched over background (permutation p=0.61). Inflammation is therefore treated as a downstream, low-amplitude consequence rather than the differentiating mechanism.", "Step 7 (protein-level, ambiguous): Four independently reported spots whose shared top candidate is ANXA1 are increased (protein_spot:045 +3.05, protein_spot:046 +2.81, protein_spot:044 +2.38, protein_spot:043 +1.96) and ANXA1 RNA is +4.15 (88.8th percentile), while the alternative shared candidate TALDO1 has RNA -2.30; if the spots are ANXA1 this fits a phospholipid-binding, efferocytic, resolution-biased rather than interferon-activated state. Spot identity is not established."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand scavenger uptake and TFEB-type lysosomal hydrolysis without matched lipid export, making sterol/lipid efflux the limiting step and forcing re-esterification into stored neutral lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3545212864158328, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15164983701992898, "cosine_similarity": 0.11838707619004658, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_026", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7398673139158576, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3545212864158328, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15164983701992898, "cosine_similarity": 0.11838707619004658, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7398673139158576, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0421895, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 415}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected DE list (all |effect|\u003e=1, adj-p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified log base; program directionality was judged against that 77.1% background and absent genes (ACLY, ABCA1, ABCG1, CPT1A, NPC1, FASN) are unknown rather than unchanged.", "Transcript increases in SREBP targets, lysosomal hydrolases and OXPHOS subunits are taken as evidence of program engagement, not of measured enzyme activity, flux, protein level or organelle localization; SREBP proteolytic activation, ER sterol content, lipid-droplet content and respiration were not measured.", "Coherent SREBP-target induction is interpreted as low sensed ER sterol; an alternative cause (e.g. direct transcriptional or growth-factor input to SREBF1) cannot be excluded from these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D features; their direction is used only for compatibility/contradiction and no spot is read as identifying a single protein.", "Genes within a program are co-regulated and not independent, so the sign coherence reported is descriptive support, not a formal enrichment result, and causality is not established.", "The mitochondrial supply step assumes the induced TCA/citrate-carrier transcripts translate into greater acetyl-CoA/NADPH availability; the concurrent decrease in mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) makes this the weakest step."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, D30) differ from APOE3 by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state rather than by a single failed enzyme: the selected DE list shows concurrent induction of the lysosomal hydrolytic/v-ATPase program (including sphingolipid and glycosphingolipid hydrolases), of the full SREBP-1/2 target module (sterol synthesis, LDLR uptake, SCD/FADS1 desaturation), of glycerolipid esterification enzymes, and of mitochondrial TCA/citrate-export and nuclear OXPHOS machinery. We propose that APOE4's poorer lipid-acceptor function leaves lysosomally liberated sterol and fatty acid poorly exported, so ER sterol sensing stays 'low' despite lipid load; SREBP output plus mitochondrion-supplied acetyl-CoA/NADPH then drives desaturation and esterification of that lipid into MUFA-biased glycerolipids and cholesteryl esters (storage/membrane remodeling) instead of efflux. This describes increased lipid throughput with altered routing in the measured mock condition; it does NOT establish a rate-limiting defect, and no flux, sterol pool, droplet or respiration measurement was supplied.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective discriminating test: repleting ER-accessible sterol in mock APOE4 microglia (LDL loading, 25-hydroxycholesterol, or cyclodextrin bypass of lysosomal sterol export) should collapse the SREBP-target module (SREBF1, HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD) and the esterification arm (DGAT1, SOAT1, AGPAT2) toward APOE3 levels; if APOE4 SREBP targets remain elevated after sterol repletion, the sensing step and hence the mechanism are weakened.", "Prospective lipidomics on mock cells: APOE4 should show higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol per cell and a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio (16:1/18:1 versus 20:4 species) in phosphatidylcholine, with more BODIPY-positive droplets; equal neutral-lipid content and no MUFA shift would falsify the routing claim even though the transcripts differ.", "Prospective challenge test separating adaptation from failed compensation: after myelin-debris or apoptotic-neuron loading, APOE4 should clear and efflux cholesterol more slowly and accumulate more cholesteryl ester than APOE3 despite equal or higher lysosomal hydrolase transcripts; equal clearance and efflux would show the mock-state difference is successful adaptation, not reduced reserve.", "Prospective pharmacology: SCD or DGAT1 inhibition should preferentially raise free fatty acid, ER-stress markers (DDIT3, ATF6) and death in APOE4 over APOE3; equal tolerance would show that desaturation/esterification routing is not load-bearing in APOE4.", "Prospective control for the weakest step: Seahorse respirometry should show no more than a modest APOE4 increase in basal/maximal respiration; a clear decrease in respiration or in assembled complex IV/V despite 38/38 nuclear OXPHOS transcript increases would indicate mitonuclear imbalance (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4 down) and would require removing the acetyl-CoA/NADPH-supply step from the mechanism.", "Prospective specificity check: knock-in of APOE3 into the APOE4 line, or supplying exogenous lipidated APOE3 particles as an acceptor, should normalize the SREBP and esterification transcripts; failure to normalize would indicate an APOE-genotype effect acting independently of lipid acceptor function."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 apolipoprotein (gene:APOE transcript up, 1.24) is an inferior lipid/cholesterol acceptor, so sterol and fatty acid released inside the endolysosome are exported less efficiently than in APOE3 (inferred; efflux and extracellular lipid particles were not measured).", "The lysosomal degradative program is elevated: v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts (gene:GAA 9.96, gene:ATP6V1H 6.88, gene:CTSB 5.52, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB 2.38) together with lipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GBA 6.71, gene:HEXA 5.68, gene:SMPD1 5.63, gene:NAGLU, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA; 9/9 up), raising capacity to liberate fatty acid, ceramide and sterol from internalized membrane; gene:CTSS (-5.57) is a clear exception.", "ER sterol sensing nonetheless reads low, and the SREBP-1/2 target module is uniformly induced (gene:SREBF1 4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR24 3.69, gene:DHCR7, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR; 16/16 up against a 77% up-biased list background), accompanied by uptake/transport transcripts (gene:SCARB1 8.22, gene:CD36, gene:FABP3, gene:FABP5, gene:NPC2, gene:ABCA7).", "Mitochondrial carbon and reducing-equivalent supply transcripts rise in parallel (gene:MDH1 8.72, gene:OGDH 8.56, gene:MPC2 7.98, gene:GOT1 6.43, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1 4.47 citrate carrier, gene:ACSS2 2.93, gene:ME1, gene:NNT) alongside 38/38 nuclear OXPHOS subunits (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX5B), providing the acetyl-CoA and NADPH that lipogenesis requires (ACLY was not in the supplied list; supply is inferred, not measured).", "Liberated and newly made fatty acid is desaturated and esterified rather than left free: gene:SCD 4.17 and gene:FADS1 with glycerolipid/ester-forming enzymes gene:AGPAT2 6.29, gene:LPCAT1 3.07, gene:MBOAT2, gene:MBOAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1 and gene:SOAT1, while PUFA-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11; gene:GPAT3 -2.23 is a contrary member), predicting a MUFA-shifted acyl-CoA and phospholipid pool plus neutral-lipid (TAG/cholesteryl-ester) storage.", "Net cell state in mock: higher esterified/stored lipid, remodeled membranes and high hydrolytic-anabolic cycling, with less lipid returned to the extracellular acceptor pool; measured protein spots are compatible but ambiguous (lysosomal-hydrolase candidates rise in protein_spot:052, :053, :055, :057, :063, :006, :007 yet fall in protein_spot:058, :067, :069, each spot listing 3-5 candidates including actin/keratin, so no individual protein is confirmed).", "Consequence framed prospectively: because free-cholesterol export capacity is the arm that is not induced, APOE4 microglia should show reduced reserve under a lipid load (myelin debris, apoptotic neurons, LDL), which is a predicted challenge-revealed defect and not an ongoing defect demonstrated in the mock condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lysosome-to-SREBP lipid re-routing state: hydrolysed membrane lipid is re-esterified and desaturated rather than exported"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.45942103902817266, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22676966234752893, "cosine_similarity": 0.11816878731139308, "direction_accuracy": 0.3640776699029126, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7402556634304207, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.45942103902817266, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.22676966234752893, "cosine_similarity": 0.11816878731139308, "direction_accuracy": 0.3640776699029126, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7402556634304207, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.14396325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 99}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_050", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so set-level statements are made as percentile ranks within this biased list, not as whole-transcriptome enrichment; the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved rather than converted.", "Transcript abundance of TCA/ETC, peroxiredoxin and PPP genes is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the corresponding enzymatic capacity; no NADPH, NADP+, GSH/GSSG, H2O2, superoxide, lipid-peroxide, oxygen-consumption or lipid-droplet measurement is present in the supplied data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D features; spots 018/019/021 (G6PD, GSR, PGD among candidates), 077 (PRDX2 among candidates) and 017 (CAT among candidates) are treated as ambiguous, non-identifying evidence and none is claimed as a specific protein measurement.", "The APOE4 and APOE3 cultures are assumed to be comparable in cell composition and differentiation state; the workbook does not supply biological replicate numbers, and astrocyte co-culture could contribute genotype-dependent composition differences.", "Compartment assignment (cytosolic versus mitochondrial NADPH and peroxide handling) is inferred from canonical, unverified background knowledge of the listed genes, not from any localisation measurement here."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcriptional expansion of mitochondrial TCA/electron-transport and mitochondrial thiol-peroxidase machinery together with a coordinated reduction of cytosolic NADPH-supply transcripts (oxidative PPP and NADP+ synthesis). We hypothesise that this compartmental mismatch makes cytosolic NADPH-dependent peroxide and lipid-peroxide reduction the rate-limiting redox node in APOE4 cells, and that the observed suppression of PUFA-activating/oxygenating transcripts alongside induction of desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification transcripts is the downstream lipid consequence: incoming lipid is routed into monounsaturated, storage-form lipid rather than into oxidation. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a testable model, not a demonstrated chain.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial pharmacological or genetic block of the oxidative PPP (G6PDi-1, 6-aminonicotinamide, or G6PD knockdown) in isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should produce a selectively larger increase in C11-BODIPY lipid peroxidation and death in APOE4 at doses that barely affect APOE3; equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the proposed cytosolic NADPH bottleneck.", "Compartment-resolved sensors (cyto- and mito-targeted Grx1-roGFP2 and roGFP2-Orp1, plus cytosolic Apollo-NADP+) should show a more oxidised cytosolic glutathione pool and slower cytosolic recovery after a bolus of H2O2 or cumene hydroperoxide in APOE4, with mitochondrial oxidation equal or less affected; an APOE4 cytosolic pool that is equally or more reduced than APOE3 would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Suppressing mitochondrial electron leak (site-directed S1QEL/S3QEL, or low-dose complex I inhibition titrated to equal ATP) should lower mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation and reduce neutral-lipid droplet content selectively in APOE4; if droplet content is unchanged while mitochondrial oxidation falls, the load-to-lipid link in steps 2 and 5 fails.", "SCD inhibition (CAY10566) should reduce droplet content in APOE4 but increase lipid peroxidation and death more in APOE4 than APOE3, consistent with storage as protective sequestration; loss of droplets without any rise in peroxidation would weaken step 5.", "NNT knockdown should selectively increase PRDX3 dimer formation and mitochondrial peroxide signal in APOE4; no genotype difference would weaken the claim that the buffering response is NADPH-dependent and mitochondrially biased.", "Targeted immunoblot or PRM proteomics should show lower TALDO1, PGD and unchanged G6PD protein in APOE4; if TALDO1 protein is instead higher, matching the increased spots 043-046 whose candidate lists include TALDO1, the transcript-based supply-limitation argument is substantially weakened.", "Stable-isotope flux ([1,2-13C2]glucose, PPP versus glycolysis split; U-13C glutamine into TCA) should show a lower oxidative-PPP fraction and higher TCA labelling in APOE4; an unchanged or higher PPP fraction would falsify step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mechanism_steps": ["Load side (measured RNA, inferred flux): nuclear-encoded TCA, mitochondrial carrier and electron-transport transcripts are coordinately high in APOE4 relative to the global upward shift of this differential-expression set (OGDH, ACO2, MPC2, MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, NDUFS7, NDUFA5, NDUFS8, SDHB, UQCRB); we infer, but do not measure, increased electron delivery to complexes I/III.", "Inferred consequence: higher matrix electron flux raises univalent electron leak and matrix H2O2 production per cell; no ROS species, NAD(P)H pool or membrane potential was measured here.", "Buffering response (measured RNA and one ambiguous spot): mitochondrial and general thiol-peroxidase/repair transcripts rise (PRDX3, PRDX5, PRDX2, GPX4, MSRA, GSS, TXNDC17, TXNL1) together with the mitochondrial transhydrogenase NNT, indicating that peroxide handling is biased toward NADPH-dependent thioredoxin/peroxiredoxin systems, and mostly toward mitochondrially localised members.", "Primary bottleneck (measured RNA, inferred capacity): cytosolic NADPH regeneration is not scaled up with this demand. Against a set in which 77% of rows are positive, PGD, TALDO1, NADK and HK2 are all in the lowest quintile, and the 2D spots whose candidate lists include G6PD, GSR or PGD are unchanged, so no compensatory increase in cytosolic NADPH-supply protein is evident in the supplied data.", "Lipid consequence (measured RNA, inferred flux and localisation): with constrained cytosolic NADPH-dependent lipid-peroxide reduction, PUFA activation and oxygenation transcripts are low (ACSL4, ACSL5, ALOX15) while monounsaturated-lipid synthesis and esterification transcripts are high (SCD, SREBF1, DGAT1, SOAT1) with elevated microsomal electron-donor transcripts (CYB5R3, CYB5A, POR); we predict a shift of lipid into MUFA-enriched, droplet-stored species rather than oxidation.", "Substrate delivery: a coordinated lysosomal/degradative programme (GBA, CTSB, CTSD, HEXB, LAMP1, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H, TFEB, GAA) plus scavenger-receptor transcripts (CD36, SCARB1, TREM2) supplies more lipid into this constrained redox environment, sustaining storage rather than catabolism.", "Net predicted state: APOE4 microglia operate with less cytosolic NADPH/GSH reserve per unit peroxide load, so peroxide or PPP challenge should expose a selective APOE4 vulnerability with increased lipid peroxidation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand mitochondrial electron flux and thiol-peroxidase transcripts while cytosolic NADPH-supply transcripts fall, making cytosolic NADPH-dependent lipid-peroxide clearance the limiting node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2034763504781597, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17777149364196537, "cosine_similarity": 0.1175442872819164, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6836796116504854, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2034763504781597, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.17777149364196537, "cosine_similarity": 0.1175442872819164, "direction_accuracy": 0.23300970873786409, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6836796116504854, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2414205, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 416}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_063", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1 in an unspecified logarithm base) and not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. NPC1, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1) means 'not in the selected rows', not 'unchanged' and not 'not expressed'.", "A strong global positive shift exists in the selected rows (1705/2212 up, median +1.46), so directional agreement alone is weak evidence; only set-level enrichment above that background is treated as informative.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partly reflected in protein and enzymatic capacity; no hydrolase activity, acidification, lipid mass or localization measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is assumed to identify a single gene product, and spot-level direction is used only as a consistency check.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies the extracellular lipoproteins whose uptake is invoked in Step 1; the medium/lipoprotein composition and any astrocyte-genotype contribution are not measured here.", "Replicate number, normalization and possible ambient-RNA or compositional differences are not supplied; very large effects (e.g. +9 to +15) suggest low replication or sparse-count instability rather than true 1000-fold biology."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily in the terminal step of endolysosomal cargo processing: transfer of lipoprotein-derived unesterified cholesterol out of the late endosome/lysosome to the ER/plasma membrane is rate-limiting. The selected differential-expression data are consistent with a cell that simultaneously (i) expands lysosomal degradative machinery (TFEB/MITF, cathepsins and other acid hydrolases, v-ATPase subunits, HOPS/ESCRT/retromer/endosomal traffic genes), (ii) keeps or raises lipoprotein and phagocytic uptake receptor transcripts, and (iii) still expresses a sterol-synthesis/uptake (SREBP-type) program, i.e. the ER-accessible sterol pool behaves as if low while cargo-derived cholesterol accumulates upstream. Transcript abundance is measured; egress flux, lysosomal cholesterol localization, hydrolase activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation A (egress bypass): treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or re-expressing NPC1/NPC2, should lower LAMP1-colocalized filipin-positive cholesterol and normalize both the SREBP-type transcripts (HMGCS1, DHCR24, LDLR, SCARB1) and the CLEAR transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, ATP6V1A) toward APOE3 levels, with little effect in APOE3. If cyclodextrin clears lysosomal cholesterol but leaves the CLEAR and SREBP-type transcript differences intact, the sterol-egress bottleneck is not the driver.", "Discriminating perturbation B (load versus egress): culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake, should collapse the APOE4-specific lysosomal transcript expansion if the bottleneck is cargo load exceeding a fixed egress capacity. If the APOE4 CLEAR signature persists unchanged without extracellular lipoprotein cargo, the mechanism is wrong and a cargo-independent TFEB/mTORC1 setpoint difference should be preferred.", "Capacity test: DQ-BSA and BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester dequenching normalized per LAMP1 area should show equal or lower per-lysosome degradative/processing flux in APOE4 despite higher hydrolase transcripts; if per-lysosome flux scales up in proportion to hydrolase transcript levels, the 'capacity-limited' claim is weakened and the changes should be read as an adaptive increase in throughput.", "Sensor test: the ER-accessible cholesterol pool (ALOD4 or GRAM1b probe) should be lower in APOE4 while total and lysosomal cholesterol is equal or higher. Finding an equal or larger ER-accessible pool in APOE4 alongside the elevated SREBP-type transcripts would falsify Step 3 and favour an SREBF-independent explanation (e.g. transcriptional noise from the global up-shift, or SOAT1/MYLIP-driven ER sterol handling that already indicates sterol sufficiency).", "Specificity test: TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce CLEAR transcripts and worsen lysosomal cholesterol accumulation and DQ-BSA clearance (compensatory role). If TFEB knockdown reduces lysosomal cholesterol accumulation instead, the CLEAR expansion is causal rather than compensatory and the stated direction of Step 4 is wrong.", "Negative prediction: no coordinated inflammatory or glycolytic program should be required for the phenotype; in the supplied rows the inflammatory set (n=10, median +1.42) and glycolytic set (n=5, 3/5 up) show no enrichment above the global shift (permutation p = 0.58 and 0.92), so NF-kB or HIF1A inhibition should not normalize the lysosomal transcript signature."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia maintain or increase transcripts for lipoprotein/debris receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:COLEC12, gene:STAB1, gene:C1QA/B/C), which we infer sustains a high delivery rate of lipid-rich cargo into the endolysosomal system; cargo influx itself is not measured here.", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck, inferred): NPC-dependent export of unesterified cholesterol from the late-endosomal/lysosomal lumen to the ER is the rate-limiting step. Only the accessory carrier transcript gene:NPC2 (+1.17) and the lipid-transfer/contact-site genes gene:VPS13C (+2.66) and gene:OSBPL1A (+1.03) appear in the selected rows; NPC1 is absent from the supplied DE rows, so egress capacity is inferred, not observed.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): The ER sterol sensor behaves as if sterol-poor, sustaining an SREBP-type program - gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:ACAT2, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1 are all higher in APOE4 - which feeds back onto Step 1 as a feed-forward loading loop.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Luminal cholesterol/lipid load and reduced substrate clearance are inferred to activate a TFEB/MITF-CLEAR compensatory response: gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:MITF (+1.03) with coordinate elevation of acid hydrolases (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:MAN2B1, gene:AGA, gene:DNASE2), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2, all higher) and endosome-to-lysosome traffic genes (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS18, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:PIK3C3, gene:LAMP1, gene:IGF2R, gene:GNPTG).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred state): Expanded machinery does not resolve the load; APOE4 cells sit in a lipid-laden lysosomal-stress state marked by gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1 and gene:APOE, with loss of the homeostatic microglial hydrolase transcript gene:CTSS (-5.57), i.e. qualitative remodelling rather than uniform lysosomal up-regulation.", "Step 6 (measured protein spots, ambiguous identity): 2D protein spots whose candidate lists contain cathepsins move in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:055 +0.58 versus protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) while spots with a lysosomal sulfatase candidate rise (protein_spot:006, protein_spot:007, protein_spot:063). This spot redistribution is consistent with altered pro-form/mature-form partitioning of hydrolases, but the spots are not uniquely identified proteins and cannot establish which protein changed."], "title": "A late-endosomal/lysosomal sterol-egress bottleneck in APOE4 microglia drives compensatory CLEAR/v-ATPase expansion together with SREBP-type sterol-starvation transcription"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06262230919765166, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.009439670212814492, "cosine_similarity": 0.11702680781635662, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6399449838187702, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06262230919765166, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.009439670212814492, "cosine_similarity": 0.11702680781635662, "direction_accuracy": 0.10517799352750809, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6399449838187702, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8463985, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 417}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_100", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is not specified in the workbook; all RNA effects are used in the reported log unit and only compared with each other, never converted to fold change.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome. All pathway statements are therefore comparisons AGAINST the strongly positive list-wide background (mean +1.39, 77% positive), by permutation within the supplied rows, not against a genome.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel spots; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and no spot is used to assert a specific protein pool.", "The direction of the MT- rows is assumed to reflect real mitochondrial transcript abundance rather than probe-panel coverage, ambient RNA, or the mitochondrial-fraction QC filter typical of droplet/Flex single-cell pipelines. This assumption is the weakest link in the chain.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partially predictive of the corresponding protein pool; no OXPHOS, TCA, import, peroxisomal or antioxidant protein was measured in the supplied protein data.", "Assembly state, respiration, membrane potential, ROS, NADPH/GSH pools, lysosomal proteolytic capacity and mtDNA copy number are all INFERRED here and were not measured.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently interpreted; isogenic background is assumed as stated in the metadata.", "Causal direction from APOE4 genotype to the mito-nuclear mismatch is assumed, not established; the association is cross-sectional at a single day-30 timepoint under mock treatment."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coordinated transcript increase in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS accessory subunits, TCA enzymes and mitochondrial import/carrier machinery while glycolytic commitment transcripts fall and the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ATP6 fall. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for assembly of complexes III, IV and V, so the expanded nuclear-encoded module cannot be converted proportionally into functional respirasomes; the resulting partially assembled, electron-leaky machinery drives a low-grade thiol/peroxiredoxin response and increased lysosomal-degradative demand. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is not the driver. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: selectively raise mtDNA-encoded core supply in APOE4 microglia (e.g. TFAM or mitochondrial-translation-supporting intervention, or allotopic/complementation supply of the missing core subunits) without touching the nuclear module. The mechanism predicts a rise in assembled complex III/IV/V holoenzyme on blue-native PAGE and an increase in FCCP-stimulated maximal OCR toward APOE3 levels, WITHOUT normalisation of the elevated NDUF/TCA/SLC25A transcripts. If assembled holoenzyme and maximal respiration do not increase, or if the nuclear transcripts normalise in parallel, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Stoichiometry test: quantitative proteomics or immunoblot in APOE4 vs APOE3 should show increased nuclear-encoded accessory subunits (e.g. NDUFA/NDUFB, ATP5F1B, UQCRC2) but flat or reduced MT-CO2 / MT-CYB / MT-ATP6 protein, giving a decreased mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded subunit ratio. Equal ratios in the two genotypes would falsify the core claim.", "Sensitivity test: APOE4 microglia should lose maximal respiration at a LOWER dose of a mitochondrial translation inhibitor (doxycycline or chloramphenicol) than APOE3, because they already sit closer to the core-supply limit. Equal or greater APOE4 resistance would weaken the mechanism.", "Localisation test for the redox arm: any increased oxidant signal in APOE4 should be mitochondrially localised (MitoSOX, mito-roGFP2-Orp1) and not peroxisomal (peroxisome-targeted HyPer, catalase activity, C26:0 very-long-chain fatty acid levels). If the oxidant signal is peroxisomal or if C26:0 accumulates, the rejected peroxisomal alternative should replace this mechanism.", "Flux test: APOE4 should show unchanged or reduced ATP-linked OCR and reduced spare respiratory capacity despite higher mitochondrial mass markers, with an elevated proton-leak fraction; and, given HK2/PFKP down, no compensatory increase in ECAR. If APOE4 shows maximal OCR increased in proportion to the transcript-level mitochondrial expansion, the mechanism is falsified.", "Ordering test: acute pharmacological block of complex III or V in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the APOE4 signature order - lysosomal/TFEB and peroxiredoxin transcript rises downstream of the assembly defect. If lysosomal expansion precedes or is independent of the respiratory defect, step 6 must be demoted to a parallel, not downstream, arm.", "Negative control on the confound: qPCR of mtDNA copy number and bulk (non-droplet) measurement of MT-CYB/MT-CO2/MT-ATP6 transcripts should reproduce the decrease. If bulk RNA shows no mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit, the mismatch is a single-cell QC/normalisation artefact and the whole hypothesis fails."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial module - all 37 detected nuclear OXPHOS subunit rows are positive (mean +2.81 in the reported log unit; 21/21 NDUF rows positive, mean +2.99), together with mitochondrial import/carrier genes (TOMM22, TIMM8B, TIMM44, SLC25A46, SLC25A1, SLC25A5, SLC25A11, CHCHD3, COA8) and TCA/anaplerotic enzymes (MDH1, OGDH, MPC2, GOT1, DLD, ACO2, IDH3G, PDP1; median percentile rank 91 within the supplied list).", "STEP 2 (measured abundance, opposite direction): glycolytic commitment transcripts do not follow the list-wide upward shift (HK2 -3.67, PFKP -3.08, HK3 -1.09; glycolysis set mean +0.67 vs list mean +1.39). We INFER, but did not measure, that carbon is preferentially routed to mitochondrial pyruvate import and oxidation rather than to glycolytic lactate output.", "STEP 3 (measured abundance, the mismatch): the mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores of complexes III, IV and V are reduced against this rising background - MT-CYB -2.32 (padj 3.6e-64), MT-CO2 -1.33 (padj 1.3e-24), MT-ATP6 -3.35 (padj 9.1e-228), MT-ND4 -1.80 (padj 3.5e-125). The mtDNA-encoded arm therefore does not scale with the nuclear arm (mean of the six MT- rows -0.82 vs list mean +1.39, permutation p = 0.021 for being low).", "STEP 4 (inferred bottleneck, not measured): because complexes III, IV and V cannot be assembled without their mtDNA-encoded cores, we propose that core-subunit supply, not nuclear module abundance, limits mature respirasome formation in APOE4. The predicted consequence is accumulation of unassembled or sub-assembled nuclear modules and a reduced ratio of assembled holoenzyme to total OXPHOS protein. No assembly state, holoenzyme, protein-level OXPHOS pool, membrane potential or respiration measurement is present in the supplied data.", "STEP 5 (inferred activity): partially assembled complex III/IV and an ATP-synthase-limited proton circuit are expected to increase electron leak and superoxide production at the inner membrane. Consistent with a LOW-GRADE, mitochondrially biased redox response rather than a full antioxidant program, thiol/peroxiredoxin transcripts rise (TXNDC17 +7.10, PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, GPX4 +2.79, GSS +2.11, NNT +2.88) but the redox set as a whole is only marginal against the list background (n=19, mean +2.30, permutation p = 0.059), and OXR1 (-3.63) and MSRB1 (-2.44) run the other way.", "STEP 6 (inferred flux/localisation): sustained turnover of defective inner-membrane material increases autophagic-lysosomal demand, matching the coordinated lysosomal/v-ATPase transcript rise (TFEB +2.38, CTSB +5.52, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.66, SMPD1 +5.57, ATP6V1H +6.90, ATP6V1A +4.16, LAMP1 +1.44; set n=22, mean +2.87, permutation p = 0.004) and with a mild integrated-stress readout (DDIT3 +2.79, HSPA9 +2.35, SHMT2 +2.22). Whether lysosomal capacity, not just transcript abundance, is increased was not measured.", "STEP 7 (explicit rejection of the assigned focus): peroxisomal beta-oxidation is NOT the bottleneck. Only 7 peroxisome-related rows are present (SCP2 +5.95, MPV17 +3.45, ACOX1 +1.24, AMACR +1.12, CROT +1.03, ABCD4 +1.02, ABCD1 -1.64), their mean (+1.74) is indistinguishable from the list background (permutation p = 0.36), the ABCD1 very-long-chain fatty-acid importer is DOWN, and no PEX biogenesis or catalase transcript row exists in the supplied data."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch: APOE4 microglia up-regulate the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial module while mtDNA-encoded core subunits of complexes III/IV/V fall, making respirasome assembly the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22743972233504411, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12165827241256949, "cosine_similarity": 0.1103736856940314, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6527443365695793, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22743972233504411, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12165827241256949, "cosine_similarity": 0.1103736856940314, "direction_accuracy": 0.18446601941747573, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6527443365695793, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8306495, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 418}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_133", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global upward shift (77% positive, median +1.46), so only within-list rank contrasts, not absolute directions or set-level 'up' calls, are treated as informative.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and effects reach |15|; magnitudes are used only as ranks, never as literal fold changes, and no replicate count is supplied.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. NPC1, PSAP, GRN, ABCA1, ABCG1, LAMP2, STARD3) are unmeasured here, not unchanged; the export arm is therefore represented by only 9 measured genes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal proteins and hence organelle capacity; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, protein maturation and localisation were not measured.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; spot-level changes are used only as ambiguous, non-confirmatory context.", "The measurement is a mixed microglia/astrocyte co-culture at day 30, so some transcript differences may arise from altered cell-state composition or non-cell-autonomous astrocyte effects rather than from a cell-intrinsic APOE4 lysosomal defect.", "The catabolic and export gene sets were assembled by the analyst after inspecting the data, so the rank contrast is exploratory and needs independent replication."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia by scaling up endolysosomal cargo uptake, acidification and luminal hydrolase transcripts far more than the intraluminal lipid-transfer/export arm (NPC2, GM2A, SCARB2, CLN3, APOE, PLTP), which is hypothesised to leave hydrolysis products (unesterified cholesterol, sphingolipids) trapped in the lysosomal lumen; the resulting failure to deliver sterol to the ER is proposed to keep SREBP-type biosynthetic transcription and TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis switched on simultaneously. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treat APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (or express NPC2/PSAP), which bypasses the proposed luminal export block. Prediction: APOE4-specific reduction of filipin-positive lysosomal free cholesterol and normalisation of SREBP-target transcripts (LDLR, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, SREBF2) and TFEB targets toward APOE3, with SCARB1 unchanged. If lysosomal sterol falls but SREBP targets stay elevated, step 6 is falsified; if lysosomal sterol does not fall, the export-block premise is falsified.", "Capacity test: measure lysosomal pH (ratiometric dextran), Magic Red cathepsin B/L and DQ-BSA dequenching per LAMP1+ organelle. Prediction: APOE4 lysosomes are equally or more acidic with equal-or-higher hydrolase activity per organelle while accumulating cholesterol/BODIPY-sphingolipid. Finding a higher lysosomal pH or reduced cathepsin/DQ-BSA activity in APOE4 would refute the 'export-limited, hydrolysis-sufficient' bottleneck and favour a degradative-capacity failure instead.", "Load test: block cargo influx (SR-B1 inhibition/BLT-1 or SCARB1 knockdown, or lipoprotein-depleted medium). Prediction: the APOE4 excess in hydrolase/v-ATPase/TFEB transcripts and in lysosomal lipid content shrinks toward APOE3. Persistence of the transcript excess with influx blocked would show the programme is cargo-independent and weaken step 1.", "Genotype-swap test: introducing APOE3 (or APOE knockout rescue with APOE3) into the APOE4 background should reproduce the APOE3 export/biogenesis balance within days without altering the mitochondrial oxidative-phosphorylation transcript set; if the oxidative-phosphorylation set (the most statistically enriched set here, Mann-Whitney p=1.5e-4) reverses while lysosomal lipid content does not, the primary bottleneck should be reassigned to bioenergetic remodelling.", "Global weakening result: if quantitative lipidomics or imaging shows no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in lysosomal unesterified cholesterol, glucosylceramide or sphingomyelin content under mock conditions, the entire mechanism is refuted regardless of the transcript pattern."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_133", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein cargo receptors, most strikingly SCARB1 (top ~1% of the differential-expression list) with CD36, MRC1, TREM2, ABCA7 and APOE also positive; we infer, but do not measure, an increased rate of lipid-rich cargo delivery into the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): A lysosome-biogenesis/maturation signature is elevated (TFEB, MITF, RAB7A, IGF2R, GNPTG, LAMP1, AP5M1, SPNS1, SLC17A5), consistent with increased TFEB/MITF transcriptional drive and more or larger degradative compartments; organelle number, size and TFEB nuclear localisation are not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): Luminal acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts sit near the top of the shifted distribution (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, MAN2B1; ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C), so degradative and acidification capacity per compartment is inferred to be adequate or increased rather than deficient.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck, measured RNA contrast): The intraluminal lipid-transfer/export arm that must move the products of that hydrolysis out of the lumen (NPC2, GM2A, SCARB2, CLN3, APOE, PLTP, OSBPL1A/OSBPL8, M6PR) sits at or below the median of the same list (median rank percentile 27 vs 76 for the catabolic/acidification arm, Mann-Whitney p=0.002); we propose this export step, not hydrolysis, limits net lipid throughput in APOE4.", "Step 5 (inferred, unmeasured pool): Cholesterol and sphingolipid products therefore accumulate in the endolysosomal lumen and fail to reach the ER sterol sensor; no lipid pool was measured in this dataset, so this step is purely inferred.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, consistent readout): ER sterol under-supply keeps the SREBP-type programme on despite high uptake, with all 13 measured SREBP/sterol-lipogenic genes positive (SREBF1, SREBF2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP, SCD, ACSS2, SOAT1), while sustained luminal load feeds back on TFEB-driven biogenesis, producing a self-reinforcing lipid-storage state."], "title": "Post-hydrolytic lipid export from the endolysosome, not hydrolase or acidification capacity, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10371819960861056, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.13100915933567925, "cosine_similarity": 0.10053146735679472, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_133", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6767734627831715, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10371819960861056, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.13100915933567925, "cosine_similarity": 0.10053146735679472, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6767734627831715, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.805517, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 419}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_070", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e=1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 genes up, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); pathway claims therefore rest on medians and coherence relative to that background, not on direction alone.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for enzyme capacity; flux, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, GSH/GSSG, peroxiredoxin oxidation state, ROS levels, membrane potential and peroxide concentrations were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate; assignment of protein_spot:017 to catalase, protein_spot:077 to PRDX2 and protein_spot:074 to PRDX1/SOD2 is provisional and could instead reflect CORO1C/ENTPD5, keratin/actin contaminants or RAC2/RHOG respectively.", "The astrocyte co-culture and 10X Flex probe-based quantification mean that apparent global up-shifts, cell-composition differences and ambient RNA could inflate module-level coordination; the six MT-encoded transcripts are mixed (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB down; MT-ND4L, MT-ND5 up) and are not used as load-bearing evidence.", "Unverified background knowledge (not from these files): SCD, DHCR24/DHCR7 and glutathione/thioredoxin reductases are NADPH-dependent; peroxiredoxins are recycled by thioredoxin/TXNRD; NNT uses the proton-motive force to make matrix NADPH."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally expand mitochondrial substrate import, TCA and the complete nuclear-encoded electron-transport chain while simultaneously running an SREBP-driven sterol/monounsaturated-lipid biosynthetic program; because both an enlarged electron-leak surface and reductive lipogenesis draw on the same NADPH pool, and cytosolic pentose-phosphate transcripts (PGD, TALDO1) are the only reduced members of that pool's supply set, NADPH-dependent recycling of peroxiredoxins and glutathione peroxidase 4 (not enzyme abundance) becomes the limiting step for peroxide clearance. The induced PRDX2/PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/GSS/NNT transcripts and increased catalase- and peroxiredoxin-containing protein spots are read as a compensatory response to, not evidence of solved, this reductive-capacity deficit. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: blocking NADPH-consuming reductive lipid synthesis in APOE4 microglia (SCD inhibitor, e.g. CAY10566, or an HMGCR/DHCR24 inhibitor) at doses that do not change nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts should raise the NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios and lower PRDX2/PRDX3 hyperoxidation and roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation toward APOE3 levels. If redox readouts are unchanged while lipogenic flux is confirmed suppressed, the NADPH-allocation bottleneck is wrong and an enzyme-abundance or mitochondrial-assembly model should be preferred.", "Supplying NADPH independently of the pentose-phosphate arm (NNT overexpression, mitochondria-targeted NADPH generation, or NAC/GSH-ethyl-ester repletion) should normalise APOE4 peroxide tone without reducing oxygen consumption; if oxygen consumption must fall for ROS to normalise, the primary lesion is electron flux rather than reductive capacity.", "Knockdown of G6PD or PGD should be selectively toxic/oxidant-raising in APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia (genotype x knockdown interaction); absence of interaction weakens the mechanism.", "Seahorse respirometry plus MitoSOX/mito-roGFP should show higher basal and maximal respiration and higher mitochondrial superoxide in APOE4 under mock conditions; equal respiration with equal ROS would falsify step 1.", "Redox proteomics should show more oxidised (sulfinylated/dimeric) PRDX2/PRDX3 in APOE4 despite equal or higher total peroxiredoxin protein; equal oxidation fraction would contradict the compensatory-but-insufficient interpretation.", "Negative prediction distinguishing this from the assigned peroxisomal framing: peroxisome number, PEX gene expression, plasmalogen synthesis and peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux should NOT differ substantially between genotypes; a clear peroxisomal beta-oxidation or biogenesis defect would move the bottleneck out of the mitochondrial/NADPH node."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinate higher RNA for mitochondrial pyruvate import (MPC2), TCA enzymes (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, DLD, IDH3G) and all 38 detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (e.g. NDUFS7, NDUFA5, NDUFB8, UQCRC2, COX5B, ATP5F1B, SDHB). Inferred: a larger assembled respiratory chain and higher electron flux, hence a larger site for univalent O2 reduction at complexes I and III.", "Measured: SREBP-pathway RNAs are higher (SREBF1, SCD, FADS1, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, HMGCS1) alongside lipid-uptake and esterification RNAs (CD36, SCARB1, SOAT1, DGAT1, APOE, ABCA7). Inferred: increased flux through desaturation and post-squalene sterol reduction steps, each of which consumes NADPH stoichiometrically.", "Measured: among detected NADPH-supply transcripts only the cytosolic pentose-phosphate/non-oxidative arm members PGD and TALDO1 are lower, while alternative producers NNT, ME1 and SHMT1 are higher. Inferred: the cell is re-routing rather than expanding total NADPH supply, so cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ falls relative to demand even though enzyme capacity looks increased.", "Inferred (bottleneck): with peroxide production up and NADPH allocation contested, the glutathione-reductase / thioredoxin-reductase step that re-reduces oxidised PRDX and GPX4 becomes rate-limiting; peroxiredoxins accumulate in sulfenylated/hyperoxidised or dimeric form and matrix/cytosolic H2O2 rises transiently despite normal or elevated enzyme protein.", "Measured: compensatory antioxidant RNAs are higher (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS, NNT, FTH1) and protein spots whose candidate lists include CAT (protein_spot:017), PRDX2 (protein_spot:077) and PRDX1/SOD2 (protein_spot:074) are higher. Inferred: a feedback antioxidant program; spot identities are ambiguous because each spot has multiple candidate genes.", "Inferred (consequence): persistent low-grade oxidant tone favours channelling of taken-up lipid into SCD-dependent monounsaturated species and sterol esters/droplets (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1 RNA higher), which buffers peroxidisable substrate but further consumes NADPH, closing a self-reinforcing loop that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3 at baseline."], "title": "NADPH-limited thiol-peroxidase recycling: APOE4 microglia co-expand mitochondrial oxidative catabolism and reductive lipid/sterol synthesis, making NADPH allocation the rate-limiting node for peroxide detoxification"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22623047668278995, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08805201968982054, "cosine_similarity": 0.09962426911355374, "direction_accuracy": 0.3122977346278317, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_070", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6957702265372168, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22623047668278995, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08805201968982054, "cosine_similarity": 0.09962426911355374, "direction_accuracy": 0.3122977346278317, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6957702265372168, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.73503775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 420}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_001", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Only RNA expression and ambiguous protein-spot abundance were supplied. All biochemical roles, regulatory relationships and organelle couplings invoked here are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was used. RNA effects retain the supplied, unspecified logarithm base; protein-spot effects are log2 fold changes. Positive effects mean higher abundance in APOE4.", "The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, with 77.08% positive effects. Program coherence is descriptive relative to that background, not an enrichment test; queried genes absent from the list are unknown, and genes and overlapping programs are not independent. Replicate counts, baseline abundances and uncertainty intervals are unavailable.", "The proposed productive state requires the induced RNA program to yield appropriately localized, functional proteins and sufficient ATP. TFEB/MITF RNA abundance does not establish nuclear localization or transcriptional activity. Genotype-associated changes may reflect microglial state proportions or astrocyte-mediated influences rather than a uniform cell-autonomous response.", "The most serious alternative is unsuccessful compensation. Nuclear respiratory induction conflicts with gene:MT-ATP6 (\u22123.35), gene:MT-CO2 (\u22121.33), gene:MT-CYB (\u22122.32) and gene:MT-ND4 (\u22121.80); gene:MT-ND4L (+1.95) and gene:MT-ND5 (+1.93) increase. These RNA measurements cannot establish respiratory-complex assembly, a mitochondrial bottleneck, or ATP flux. The selected mechanism predicts sufficient basal energy supply but does not claim that this has been demonstrated.", "Protein spots provide compatibility and counter-evidence only. protein_spot:053 is +1.536 log2 fold change, candidates TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1; protein_spot:058 is \u22120.848, candidates CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1. protein_spot:064 is \u22121.202, candidates ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1; protein_spot:065 is \u22120.926, candidates ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART. All four are reported significant, but none confirms an individual protein increase or decrease. ATP6V1E1 loss and failed acidification therefore remain possibilities rather than observations.", "Increased lipid acquisition/synthesis RNA is compatible with membrane and substrate supply: gene:SOAT1 (+1.25), gene:NPC2 (+1.17), gene:SREBF2 (+1.06), gene:DHCR24 (+3.69), gene:SREBF1 (+4.67) and gene:SCD (+4.17). It does not establish lipid accumulation, cholesterol depletion, sterol-sensor activation or a lipid-export defect. Decreased glycolytic transcripts gene:HK2 (\u22123.67), gene:HK3 (\u22121.12) and gene:PFKP (\u22123.08) also prevent assuming uniformly increased glycolytic throughput.", "The mechanism does not explain the predominance of ER/Golgi-traffic decreases, including gene:GOLPH3L (\u22127.40), gene:GCC1 (\u22125.01) and gene:STX16 (\u22124.06), despite increases in gene:COPA (+4.27) and gene:ARFGEF1 (+7.68). No extra secretory-block mechanism is asserted. Temporal order, basal degradation flux and successful adaptation remain unresolved; challenge-only reserve loss would not demonstrate an ongoing defect under mock treatment."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 promotes a coordinated lysosomal recycling state relative to APOE3: cargo acquisition and endolysosomal biogenesis increase basal turnover, whose ATP demand induces nuclear oxidative-metabolism and redox support. Increased throughput and this causal direction are prospective hypotheses; the observed abundance program does not establish successful adaptation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective basal test: in matched day-30 mock cultures, measure calibrated lysosomal pH, uptake-normalized pulse-chase degradation at non-overloading tracer doses, and ATP-linked oxygen consumption, controlling for viable microglial number, state proportions and astrocyte contribution. APOE4 should show maintained acidic pH, greater cargo degradation per cell after accounting for uptake, and greater ATP-linked respiratory demand. Slower degradation with alkalinization and reduced ATP production would weaken the productive recycling mechanism and favor failed compensation. Lipid-cargo tracer cleavage can test the proposed lipid connection without treating any lipid pool as previously observed.", "Prospective regulatory perturbation: after differentiation, use inducible partial CRISPRi of TFEB and MITF, with guide-resistant rescue and viability controls, while retaining mock treatment. Verified suppression of the proposed lysosomal transcriptional program should reduce the APOE4 excess in basal cargo turnover and subsequently attenuate its nuclear respiratory/redox expression response; rescue should restore these differences. Persistence of the genotype-dependent turnover and metabolic responses despite effective target-program suppression would weaken the proposed regulatory and downstream causal chain.", "Prospective causal-direction perturbation: briefly titrate V-ATPase inhibition in both genotypes, verifying comparable suppression of acidification and excluding a direct mitochondrial drug effect with an orthogonal perturbation. Removing lysosomal ATP demand should preferentially reduce the predicted APOE4 excess in ATP-linked respiration before respiratory RNA changes. Persistence of the respiratory difference despite verified lysosomal inhibition would weaken the claim that lysosomal workload drives oxidative support. A response appearing only after a separate overload challenge would establish reserve behavior, not the predicted ongoing mock-condition mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mechanism_steps": ["In mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia, an inferred MiT/TFE-associated regulatory shift coordinates lysosomal biogenesis with cargo acquisition. Measured RNA increases include gene:TFEB (+2.38), gene:MITF (+1.03), gene:LDLR (+1.50), gene:SCARB1 (+8.22) and gene:CD36 (+1.38). Nuclear regulator activity and increased uptake are inferred, not observed; no unique initiating regulator is identified.", "This state is proposed to expand an acidification-competent endolysosomal compartment through coordinated sorting and proton-pump capacity. RNA increases in gene:LAMP1 (+1.38), gene:RAB7A (+2.65), gene:AP5M1 (+9.78), gene:AP5Z1 (+3.78), gene:VPS26A (+4.86), gene:ATP6V1A (+4.23), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.70), gene:ATP6V1H (+6.88), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.51) and gene:CLCN7 (+1.06) support the expression program; organelle mass, pump assembly and lumenal pH were not measured.", "With sufficient acidification, increased hydrolytic capacity is predicted to raise basal endolysosomal cargo turnover, including lipid breakdown and recycling. Supporting RNA includes gene:SMPD1 (+5.63), gene:GBA (+6.71), gene:HEXA (+5.68), gene:HEXB (+2.17), gene:CTSB (+5.52), gene:CTSD (+2.86) and gene:GAA (+9.96). This is selective remodeling: gene:CTSS (\u22125.57) and gene:IDS (\u22121.56) decrease. Higher cleavage flux, recycled substrates and depleted or accumulated lipid pools are not observed.", "The ATP cost of sustaining uptake and lysosomal acidification is proposed to induce oxidative-metabolism support, explaining a major downstream discovery pattern: all 34 represented members of a 77-member nuclear respiratory panel increase. Carbon-entry/TCA-linked RNA increases include gene:PDP1 (+3.00), gene:MPC2 (+7.98), gene:ACO2 (+3.54), gene:IDH3G (+3.94) and gene:OGDH (+8.56); respiratory examples are gene:NDUFA5 (+7.34), gene:NDUFS7 (+5.68), gene:SDHB (+1.65), gene:UQCRC2 (+4.02), gene:COX5B (+2.33) and gene:ATP5F1B (+2.65). The lysosomal-demand-to-respiration causal direction and increased ATP production remain unmeasured.", "Sufficient oxidative ATP supply would sustain the proposed increase in basal recycling, while a linked protective expression response limits the expected redox cost. gene:GSS (+2.11), gene:GPX4 (+2.79), gene:PRDX2 (+4.41) and gene:PRDX3 (+3.49) increase at RNA level. Greater oxidant production, antioxidant activity and successful buffering are predictions or assumptions, not measurements. The mechanism concerns ongoing mock-condition physiology and does not infer an existing defect from possible vulnerability to future overload."], "title": "APOE4 engages an oxidative lysosomal recycling state under mock treatment"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18456227153564966, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09884297478691302, "cosine_similarity": 0.09860104434047606, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_001", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6451197411003237, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18456227153564966, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09884297478691302, "cosine_similarity": 0.09860104434047606, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6451197411003237, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.8767475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All functional annotations and causal links are unverified background knowledge; only supplied RNA and spot abundance effects are observations. RNA is a selected list (1,705/2,212 positive), with unspecified logarithm base; protein effects are log2 changes. Missing rows are unknown. No enrichment or independent-gene inference is claimed.", "The model assumes the coordinated RNA response produces sufficient mature enzymes, assembled pumps, and respiratory activity to increase turnover during mock treatment. TFEB/MITF activity and the origin of the proposed cargo demand are unmeasured; astrocyte-mediated effects or a different distribution of microglial states could contribute.", "Protein compatibility is ambiguous: protein_spot:053 (+1.536 log2; TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1) and protein_spot:055 (+0.585; CAPZB, IFIT3, ACTG2, CLIC1, CTSB) cannot establish individual cathepsin increases or interferon activation. These candidate lists are preserved in full.", "Serious protein counter-evidence is protein_spot:058 (-0.848 log2; CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1), protein_spot:064 (-1.202; ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1), and protein_spot:065 (-0.926; ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART). Their full candidate lists prevent attributing loss to an individual hydrolase or pump subunit; they preserve failed compensation as a serious alternative.", "Decreased gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-CYB, and gene:MT-ND4 challenge functional respiratory expansion despite increased gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 and nuclear respiratory transcripts. Decreased gene:CTSS also limits generalized hydrolysis claims. Basal degradation, pH, and ATP-linked respiration must distinguish successful adaptation from compensation that fails to restore function.", "The mechanism leaves the separate sterol-synthesis pattern (increased gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, and gene:SREBF2) unexplained. No sterol pool is measured. The isolated increased gene:IFNAR1 and mixed inflammatory transcript pattern do not identify interferon activation or suppression.", "The functional claim concerns the actual mock condition. Failure only after a future high-load challenge would reveal limited reserve and would not establish a pre-existing defect. Biological replicate counts are unavailable, and the cross-sectional abundance data establish no causal ordering."], "claim": "In day-30 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes under mock treatment, APOE4 is hypothesized to increase bulk endolysosomal cargo turnover through coordinated lysosomal biogenesis and oxidative energy provision. This proposes successful adaptation in the measured condition, with TFEB/MITF as candidate mediators of the cell-state change; the discovery abundances do not establish functional activation or causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline discrimination: in matched day-30 mock cultures, use non-overloading tracer pulse-chase measurements normalized to initially internalized cargo, viable microglial number, and cell-state composition, with calibrated lysosomal pH and an orthogonal protease assay. APOE4 should show faster lysosome-dependent bulk cargo degradation at maintained acidic pH. Slower degradation or defective acidity in APOE4 would weaken successful adaptation and favor failed compensation, regardless of RNA induction.", "Prospective mediator perturbation: inducible TFEB/MITF suppression, with verified target engagement and maintained viability, should reduce the APOE4 excess in lysosomal target expression and uptake-normalized degradation; matched re-expression of perturbation-resistant factors should restore these endpoints. Persistence of the turnover difference despite effective suppression would weaken this proposed regulatory link. A similar nonspecific reduction in both genotypes without changing their difference would provide little support.", "Prospective energetic test: measure ATP-linked respiration in unchallenged mock cultures, then apply a brief, titrated inhibition of oxidative ATP synthesis after matching internalized cargo. The model predicts greater baseline oxidative ATP provision in APOE4 and a reduction of its excess cargo turnover when that provision is curtailed. Lower baseline oxidative ATP provision, or persistence of excess turnover despite verified respiratory inhibition and matched viability, would weaken the proposed energetic coupling. An effect appearing only during excessive cargo loading would not validate the baseline claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["1. An APOE4-associated change in cargo handling is proposed to increase endolysosomal delivery demand. Increased receptor and trafficking transcripts are compatible with this entry step: gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:CD36, gene:DNM2, and gene:RAB7A. Cargo uptake, extracellular cargo composition, and causal direction were not measured.", "2. Increased processing demand is proposed to recruit a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal transcriptional response. RNA increases in gene:TFEB (+2.385 reported log fold change), gene:MITF, gene:LAMP1, gene:PIK3C3, and gene:VPS18 support represented regulatory and delivery machinery. Nuclear localization and transcription-factor activity remain inferred, and these data cannot identify a unique upstream regulator.", "3. The response is proposed to expand functional acidification and bulk hydrolytic capacity. Increased gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1C1, gene:ATP6V1E1, gene:ATP6V1F, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V0D1, gene:ATP6V0D2, gene:ATP6AP1, gene:ATP6AP2, and gene:CLCN7 accompany increased gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, and gene:SMPD1. The model predicts competent acidic degradation under mock conditions; it does not treat pump assembly, enzyme maturation, or acidification as observed. Decreased gene:CTSS is an exception to uniform protease induction.", "4. The higher energetic cost of trafficking and acidification is proposed to recruit mitochondrial ATP provision. Increased pyruvate/TCA transcripts gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, and gene:OGDH accompany nuclear respiratory machinery represented by gene:NDUFA5, gene:SDHB, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX5B, and gene:ATP5F1B. This links the lysosomal program to the strong oxidative transcriptional program through ATP demand; respiration and ATP production remain prospective functional predictions.", "5. Increased cargo delivery, maintained lysosomal acidity, and oxidative energy supply are proposed jointly to produce faster uptake-normalized bulk cargo degradation in APOE4 than APOE3 during the existing mock condition. This endpoint is an inferred consequence to test, not a measured molecular pool or flux. The mechanism need not increase every substrate-specific lysosomal reaction."], "title": "APOE4 promotes lysosomal recycling sustained by oxidative metabolism"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18456227153564966, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09884297478691302, "cosine_similarity": 0.09860104434047606, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6451197411003237, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.18456227153564966, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09884297478691302, "cosine_similarity": 0.09860104434047606, "direction_accuracy": 0.11974110032362459, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6451197411003237, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.269856, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_038", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1705 up vs 507 down, median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base), so only rank/relative position within this list is interpretable; the catabolic-vs-disposal contrast is assumed to be robust to that global shift because both sets are drawn from the same list.", "Transcript increases for GBA, SMPD1 and HEXA/HEXB translate into at least partly increased mature, correctly delivered enzyme activity in an acidified compartment (unverified background knowledge: these are lysosomal luminal hydrolases requiring PSAP/saposins and M6P-dependent delivery).", "Key pathway nodes are absent from the supplied rows (UGCG, ASAH1, PSAP, SGMS1/2, SMPD3, SPHK1/2, DEGS1, SPTLC1/2, GALC, NEU1, GLB1, NPC1), so the ceramide-consuming step is inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel features with 2-6 candidate genes each; no spot uniquely identifies a sphingolipid enzyme, so protein-level support is treated as absent rather than confirmatory.", "No lipid measurement is supplied; ceramide, sphingosine, sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid pools are inferred, not observed.", "Replicate number is not supplied, and astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from a mixed population."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 raises transcripts for the lysosomal enzymes that hydrolyse sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB) far above the global upward RNA shift, while the measured downstream ceramide-disposal and re-glycosylation genes (SGPL1, CERK, CERS6, KDSR, B4GALT5) stay at or below that shift; we hypothesise that the resulting imbalance is the primary bottleneck, generating locally elevated ceramide/sphingosine in the late endosome-lysosome limiting membrane that stiffens it and slows cargo maturation and hydrolase-receptor recycling, rather than a general increase in degradative capacity.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (whole-cell plus a lysosome-enriched fraction, mock) should show higher ceramide and sphingosine with equal or lower sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide in APOE4. If instead sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide accumulate and ceramide is unchanged or lower, the direction of the mechanism is wrong (a hydrolysis block, not catabolic overdrive) and the hypothesis is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: sphingolipid-selective correction should rescue routing without normalising the general hydrolase program. ASAH1 (acid ceramidase) overexpression, or low-dose SMPD1 knockdown/GBA partial inhibition in APOE4 cells, should lower lysosomal ceramide and restore cargo transit (DQ-BSA dequenching kinetics, pHrodo-myelin/synaptosome degradation, LAMP1 compartment morphology) toward APOE3 while GAA, CTSB and CTSD transcript levels remain elevated. If routing is rescued only by TFEB knockdown (i.e. by flattening the whole hydrolase program) and not by ceramide-selective manipulation, the generic lysosomal-biogenesis alternative wins.", "Fluorogenic activity assays at pH 4.6 should show higher per-cell GBA and acid sphingomyelinase activity in APOE4; if activities are equal or reduced despite the transcript increases, the transcript signal is compensatory and the proposed increased flux step is not supported.", "Raising ceramide directly in APOE3 microglia (short C6-ceramide or SMPD1 overexpression) should phenocopy the APOE4 cargo-transit and endolysosome-morphology deficit; failure to phenocopy weakens the ceramide-loading step.", "Ceramide-sensitive membrane ordering in the LAMP1 compartment (e.g. Laurdan/Nile-red GP imaging or anti-ceramide immunostaining colocalised with LAMP1) should be higher in APOE4; unchanged ordering with elevated bulk ceramide would weaken the localisation step while leaving the flux claim intact.", "Because the RNA list is filtered and up-shifted, an unbiased re-quantification with spike-in or cell-number normalisation should still place GBA, HEXA and SMPD1 in the top decile and SGPL1/B4GALT5 in the bottom half; loss of that rank separation would remove the core evidence."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show markedly higher transcripts for lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:GLA +1.53; ranks 47-1150 of 2212) embedded in a broader acid-hydrolase/acidification signature (gene:GAA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1A); this is transcript abundance only, not enzyme activity.", "Inferred activity/flux: if even a fraction of these transcript increases is translated and delivered to an acidified compartment, flux from sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide/ganglioside into lysosomal ceramide rises.", "Measured contrast: the sphingolipid genes that consume or re-route ceramide/sphingosine sit at or below the global median shift (gene:SGPL1 +1.09 rank 1567, gene:CERK +1.23, gene:CERS6 +1.06, gene:KDSR +1.27) and the LacCer-synthesising step is the rare down gene (gene:B4GALT5 -1.88, rank 1927); catabolic \u003e disposal set difference is 1.41 log units (one-sided Mann-Whitney p=0.0035).", "Inferred pool (not measured here): ceramide and sphingosine accumulate in the late endosome/lysosome, with a shift of glycosphingolipid flux toward gangliosides rather than back into LacCer (gene:ST3GAL5 +2.17 up, gene:B4GALT5 down).", "Inferred biophysics/localization: ceramide-enriched, more ordered limiting-membrane microdomains reduce budding/tubulation and cargo-receptor recycling from the endolysosome; the down-regulated mannose-6-phosphate receptor transcript (gene:M6PR -1.72) and Golgi routing factor (gene:GOLPH3L -7.40) are consistent with, but do not prove, a routing constraint.", "Inferred phenotype: slower cargo transit through the endolysosomal system despite higher hydrolase transcript levels, so degradative throughput per cell is not proportionally increased; lipid-handling transcripts elsewhere (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17) are read as a co-occurring lipid-remodelling response, not as evidence of the sphingolipid bottleneck itself.", "Causal direction is unestablished: this cross-sectional isogenic comparison cannot separate an APOE4-driven cause from a compensatory response to a prior lipid-handling deficit."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic program that outpaces ceramide disposal, creating a ceramide-loaded late endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20493482996713805, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06090850891433567, "cosine_similarity": 0.09771663908264566, "direction_accuracy": 0.14724919093851133, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6871844660194175, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20493482996713805, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06090850891433567, "cosine_similarity": 0.09771663908264566, "direction_accuracy": 0.14724919093851133, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6871844660194175, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.56676275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 421}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_019", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only the sign, rank and relative enrichment of effects are interpreted, never absolute fold changes.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome, so all pathway statements are made relative to the supplied rows' own background (median +1.46, 77% positive) and could change under a different selection.", "The global positive RNA shift may be a normalisation, ambient-RNA or compositional artefact of the 10X Flex comparison; the hypothesis relies only on enrichment above that shift, not on the shift itself.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot is treated as a measured single-protein pool, and no ETC, TCA or transporter protein is measured at all.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be at least partially predictive of the corresponding protein and enzymatic capacity; this is untested here (spot effects vs mean RNA effect of their candidate genes: Pearson r = -0.05 across 71 spots).", "No respirometry, ATP, NAD(H), lysosomal pH, lipid, metabolite-flux or phagocytosis-rate measurement is supplied; every statement about flux, respiration, acidification and uptake is inference, not observation.", "Replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so the very small reported p-values cannot be checked for pseudoreplication across cells; the isogenic design is taken at face value.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects could be partly non-cell-autonomous or reflect differing astrocyte crosstalk."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative machinery (complex I and other ETC subunits, TCA enzymes, mitochondrial carriers and import components) together with a lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program, while hexokinase transcripts are reduced. We propose the rate-limiting node ('bottleneck') is mitochondrial pyruvate import and complex-I-dependent NADH oxidation: in APOE4 this pathway carries the ATP and redox load that in APOE3 can be shared with glycolysis, so lysosomal acidification and actin-dependent phagocytic uptake in APOE4 become disproportionately dependent on mitochondrial respiration. Phagocytic-receptor, endocytic-coat and actin transcript modules are NOT coordinately changed relative to the strong global positive shift in these selected DE rows, so the assigned phagocytic/cytoskeletal focus is rejected as the primary driver and enters the model only as an inferred downstream consequence. Abundance changes are measured; flux, respiration, lysosomal pH and uptake rates are inferred and untested here. No causality is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, acute mitochondrial pyruvate carrier inhibition (UK5099) or low-dose rotenone should cause a larger drop in ATP, in lysosomal acidification (LysoSensor/pHrodo ratio) and in bead/myelin/synaptosome uptake in APOE4, whereas equimolar 2-deoxyglucose should impair APOE3 more. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive to UK5099/rotenone and more sensitive to 2-DG, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Extracellular flux: APOE4 should show a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio and a reduced glycolytic reserve after oligomycin than APOE3. Equal OCR/ECAR and equal glycolytic reserve would weaken the mechanism.", "Assembly test: BN-PAGE/in-gel activity should show that assembled complex I and complex V rise less than the nuclear subunit transcript signature predicts, consistent with mtDNA-encoded core subunits limiting assembly. If assembled complex I activity scales proportionally with the nuclear transcript increase, step 3 is falsified (and the mitonuclear part must be dropped).", "Machinery-abundance control: quantitative protein/flow measurement of TREM2, CD36, SCARB1 surface levels and of ARPC2/ACTB protein should show no coordinated APOE4 increase; if phagocytic-receptor or Arp2/3 protein is strongly and coordinately increased in APOE4, the rejection of the phagocytic/cytoskeletal focus was wrong.", "Rescue: restoring glycolytic capacity (HK2 re-expression, or galactose-free high-glucose plus pyruvate withdrawal comparisons) should reduce APOE4's excess sensitivity to rotenone for uptake and acidification without normalising the ETC transcript signature. Failure to reduce the sensitivity gap would weaken the causal chain.", "Specificity: the lysosomal transcript program (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A) should be accompanied by increased cathepsin/hydrolase enzymatic activity in APOE4 lysates; unchanged hydrolase activity would show the lysosomal arm is transcript-only and weaken step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to a strong global positive shift in the selected RNA rows (median +1.46 in the reported log unit, 77% of 2212 rows positive), nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts are further increased (38/38 positive, median +2.64, Mann-Whitney p=1.0e-4 vs all rows), driven mainly by complex I subunits (21 NDUF rows, median +2.66).", "Measured: TCA-cycle and mitochondrial carrier/import transcripts are also increased above background (20 rows, median +3.83, p=1.5e-3; e.g. MPC2, MDH1, OGDH, ACO2, SLC25A5, TOMM22, TIMM8B), while hexokinase transcripts are decreased (HK2, HK3) against the positive background. Inferred: carbon entering as pyruvate is preferentially imported and oxidised, and cytosolic glycolytic entry capacity is comparatively low in APOE4.", "Inferred (not measured): the expanded nuclear oxidative program sets a respiration-dominant ATP and NAD+-regeneration regime; mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are not concordantly increased (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 decreased; MT-ND4L, MT-ND5 increased), so assembled holo-complex capacity may lag the nuclear subunit pool, keeping complex I/pyruvate oxidation as the limiting step rather than a surplus.", "Measured: lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts are increased above background (28 rows, median +1.91, p=1.9e-2; GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C, TFEB). Inferred: a larger acidified degradative compartment raises steady-state proton-pumping ATP demand.", "Inferred: with glycolytic entry limited and demand raised, a larger fraction of ATP for v-ATPase pumping and for Rho/Rac-driven actin turnover during phagocytic cup formation must come from mitochondrial oxidation in APOE4.", "Consequence and counter-evidence handled: phagocytic-receptor (23 rows, p=0.75), actin/cytoskeletal (27 rows, p=0.87) and endocytic-coat (36 rows, p=0.28) transcript sets are indistinguishable from the global shift, so we predict phagocytic/endocytic capacity in APOE4 is altered by energetic dependence and lysosomal load, not by changed abundance of the uptake machinery itself."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a nuclear-encoded oxidative-catabolic program that makes lysosomal and phagocytic work OXPHOS-dependent rather than glycolysis-supported"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20982719787320459, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05501100108384493, "cosine_similarity": 0.09724348986037509, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6745080906148867, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20982719787320459, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05501100108384493, "cosine_similarity": 0.09724348986037509, "direction_accuracy": 0.1553398058252427, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6745080906148867, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.74129475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 422}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_060", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; set-level enrichment is judged against this selected background (mean effect +1.39, 77% positive) rather than against zero.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only sign, rank and relative magnitude are used.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the capacity (not the flux) of the corresponding enzyme step; no NADPH, NADP+, GSH/GSSG, peroxide, respiration or lipid measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; protein_spot:017 (candidates include CAT) and protein_spot:077 (candidates include PRDX2) are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, and spots whose candidate lists include TALDO1/TKT/G6PD are treated as counter-evidence of equal ambiguity.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30 in astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived lipid supply and any cell-composition drift between genotypes are assumed not to be the sole source of the transcript differences.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a directional hypothesis, not a demonstrated causal chain."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 cells transcriptionally build up mitochondrial electron delivery (complete ETC/TCA plus malate-aspartate and citrate carriers) and a lipogenic desaturation program (SREBF1/SCD/FADS1/DGAT1/SOAT1) while transcripts for cytosolic NADP(H)/NAD(H) regeneration (PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NAMPT) fall against a globally upward-shifted differential-expression background; the proposed bottleneck is cytosolic NADPH-dependent reducing capacity, and the cells are hypothesised to compensate by leaning on mitochondrial NADPH/thioredoxin-peroxiredoxin buffering (NNT, PRDX3, PRDX5, TXNDC17, GPX4) and by suppressing polyunsaturated-fatty-acid activation (ACSL4, ALOX15 down) so that flux is routed into monounsaturated, peroxidation-resistant triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester stores. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is explicitly not proposed as the driver, because the peroxisomal gene set in these data is small, mixed in direction and not enriched.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological G6PD/oxidative-PPP inhibition (e.g. G6PDi-1) or NADK knockdown should lower the GSH/GSSG and NADPH/NADP+ ratios and reduce viability substantially more in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia under mock conditions. If APOE4 cells are equally or less sensitive, and their basal cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ is equal or higher than APOE3, the proposed NADPH bottleneck is wrong.", "SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) should, if desaturation is the dominant NADPH sink, partially normalise the APOE4 NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios and reduce neutral-lipid-droplet content in APOE4 more than APOE3; equal effects in both genotypes, or worsened APOE4 redox state without droplet change, would weaken step 2 and step 5.", "Direct redox readout: cytosolic roGFP2-Grx1/HyPer7 and mitochondrial matrix roGFP2-Orp1 should report a more oxidised cytosolic thiol pool and higher matrix peroxide tone in APOE4 despite the higher antioxidant transcripts; an unchanged or more reduced cytosolic probe signal in APOE4 would falsify the core claim that transcriptional antioxidant induction is a compensation for an actual oxidative burden.", "Bioenergetic test of step 1: Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and higher aminooxyacetate-sensitive (malate-aspartate-shuttle-dependent) respiration in APOE4; if ETC transcript elevation is not accompanied by any increase in respiration or shuttle-dependent flux, step 1 collapses to a non-functional transcript change.", "Lipidomic prediction: APOE4 droplet/neutral-lipid fractions should be enriched in 16:1 and 18:1 species with relatively lower PUFA-containing TAG/CE and no excess of oxidised phospholipid species; finding PUFA-rich, peroxidised lipid accumulation in APOE4 instead would falsify step 5 and favour a lipid-peroxidation/ferroptosis-priming model.", "Substrate-stress test: exogenous arachidonate or linoleate loading should trigger greater lipid peroxidation (C11-BODIPY) and death in APOE4, rescuable by ferrostatin-1 and by NADPH restoration (nicotinamide riboside or malic-enzyme/PPP support); absence of genotype-differential PUFA sensitivity would weaken step 6.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: peroxisomal beta-oxidation blockade (thioridazine-free approaches such as ACOX1 knockdown) or catalase overexpression should have little genotype-differential effect; a strong APOE4-specific effect would argue that the peroxisomal mechanism, not the NADPH bottleneck, is primary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 cells show higher transcript levels for every measured ETC subunit (e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:CYCS), TCA enzymes (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD) and the malate-aspartate/citrate carrier set (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5). We infer, but do not measure, increased transfer of cytosolic reducing equivalents into mitochondria and increased electron pressure at the respiratory chain.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): A SREBF1-anchored lipogenic/desaturation program is elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ME1), which we infer raises cytosolic NADPH consumption by stearoyl-CoA desaturase and fatty-acid elongation/desaturation reactions.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred pool): Against a background in which only 22.9% of selected RNA rows are negative, four cytosolic NADP(H)/NAD(H) supply transcripts are coordinately down (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT). We infer, and do not measure, a lowered cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ and NAD(H) buffering capacity relative to demand; this is the proposed primary bottleneck.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Compensation shifts toward mitochondrial and thiol-based buffering: gene:NNT (transhydrogenase-derived mitochondrial NADPH), gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA and gene:GPX4 are up, and gene:UCP2 is up (inferred mild uncoupling relieving membrane-potential-driven electron leak). Enzyme activity, thiol redox state and peroxide flux are not measured here.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid composition): With reducing capacity limiting, peroxidation-prone substrate handling is suppressed (gene:ACSL4 down, gene:ALOX15 down) while esterification into storage lipid is favoured (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1 up, with gene:SCD supplying monounsaturated acyl-CoA). We predict a monounsaturate-enriched, PUFA-poor lipid-droplet/cholesteryl-ester pool rather than a peroxidised-lipid pool.", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): The resulting state is a genotype-specific vulnerability: APOE4 microglia should tolerate normal culture (mock) but decompensate when cytosolic NADPH regeneration or desaturase capacity is blocked, or when exogenous PUFA load is imposed."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a mitochondria-loaded, NADPH-limited redox budget that diverts fatty acids into desaturated neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.027221873499981536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07111452323182246, "cosine_similarity": 0.09578310512690907, "direction_accuracy": 0.040453074433656956, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6442621359223301, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.027221873499981536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07111452323182246, "cosine_similarity": 0.09578310512690907, "direction_accuracy": 0.040453074433656956, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6442621359223301, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.630508, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 423}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_107", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46 in the unspecified log base); pathway claims are therefore made relative to that list background, not to an unbiased transcriptome, and could still be distorted by whatever normalisation produced the shift.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal and mitochondrial enzymes; no enzyme activity, lipid species, flux, pH or organelle measurement is present in these data.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes are used only for ranking and set comparison, not converted to fold changes.", "2D protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each; assignment of a spot to CTSB/CTSD/ANXA1 is a working assumption, and keratins/ACTB dominate the candidate lists, so protein evidence is treated as weak corroboration only.", "Cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some RNA signal may come from, or be shaped by, the astrocyte partner; cell-type purity per row is not supplied.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so the reported p-values cannot be independently weighted.", "Direction of causation is assumed for narrative clarity only; these are steady-state genotype-contrast measurements under mock treatment and cannot establish causality.", "The Agent tool was not available in this session; no independent reviewer sub-agents were used and no external literature or database was consulted (background pathway assignments are unverified prior knowledge)."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia sit in a higher membrane-lipid catabolic load state than APOE3: transcripts for lysosomal sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid/glycogen hydrolases (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, NAGLU, GAA, MAN2B1) and for v-ATPase, TFEB and endolysosomal trafficking components are coordinately elevated far above the strong positive background shift of this differential-expression list, and mitochondrial TCA/complex-I/lipid-transfer transcripts are elevated in parallel, whereas glycerolipid synthesis and Lands-cycle acyl-remodeling transcripts are only at list background. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node is the export/re-use hand-off of lysosome-derived lipid catabolites (sphingoid bases, free fatty acids, sterols) to ER re-esterification and mitochondrial beta-oxidation, so that increased hydrolase transcription is a compensatory response to, not a resolution of, a persistent endolysosomal membrane-lipid cargo burden. Causality is not established by these data; all statements about flux, localisation and direction are inferred, not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute pharmacological inhibition of lysosomal acid sphingomyelinase plus glucocerebrosidase (or dual GBA/SMPD1 knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should, within 24-48 h, collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in mitochondrial oxygen consumption rate and in TCA/complex-I transcript elevation, while further increasing lysosomal sphingomyelin and hexosylceramide. If the mitochondrial elevation persists unchanged after hydrolase blockade, the proposed lysosome-to-mitochondrion routing is wrong.", "Lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under mock conditions should show elevated ceramide, hexosylceramide and lyso-phosphatidylcholine relative to total phosphatidylcholine, with unchanged or only modestly changed bulk PC/PE mass. A finding of increased bulk PC/PE with normal ceramide and hexosylceramide would support the rejected de-novo acyl-remodeling alternative and weaken this mechanism.", "Stable-isotope tracing should show faster turnover of pre-labelled sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid, and increased 13C incorporation from liberated fatty acid into TCA intermediates, in APOE4, without a matched increase in labelled acyl incorporation into phosphatidylcholine sn-2 positions. Equal sphingolipid turnover rates in the two genotypes would falsify the bottleneck placement.", "Restoring acyl-CoA activation and re-esterification capacity (ACSL4/ACSL5 re-expression, or DGAT1-competent lipid-droplet buffering) should reduce free fatty acid and lyso-lipid accumulation and lower the compensatory hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript elevation in APOE4 without normalising APOE genotype. No change in hydrolase transcripts would weaken step 6.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should selectively blunt the GAA/GBA/HEXA/SMPD1/ATP6V transcript elevation; if these hydrolase transcripts remain elevated after TFEB loss, the proposed TFEB-type coordination in step 2 is wrong even if the catabolic-load claim survives.", "Immunoblotting should show that the divergent CTSB/CTSD 2D spots correspond to a shifted pro-form/mature-form ratio rather than a net loss of cathepsin protein in APOE4; a uniform net decrease of total cathepsin B and D protein would contradict step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_107", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 protein (APOE RNA itself modestly higher, gene:APOE) is inferred to deliver poorly re-solubilised lipid/lipoprotein cargo to the microglial endolysosome; the cargo pool itself was not measured here, only receptor/handling transcripts (gene:TREM2, gene:SCARB1, gene:ABCA7, gene:NPC2).", "Persistent lumenal membrane-lipid cargo is inferred to activate a TFEB-type lysosomal biogenesis program (gene:TFEB up), raising transcripts for the acidification machinery (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and for late-endosome/lysosome trafficking (gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1).", "The most strongly and coherently induced arm is lumenal glycosidase/sphingolipid hydrolase capacity (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1), predicting increased hydrolysis of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids to ceramide and sphingoid bases inside the lysosome; the lipid products are inferred, not measured.", "Protease output is remodelled rather than uniformly raised: cathepsin transcripts diverge (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSD up; gene:CTSS strongly down) and CTSB/CTSD-containing 2D spots move in both directions (protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:027 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), consistent with altered proform/mature spot distribution rather than a uniform abundance gain - spot identities are ambiguous (multiple candidate genes per spot).", "Catabolite disposal is biased toward mitochondria: TCA, pyruvate-import, complex-I and mitochondrial lipid-transfer/dynamics transcripts are coordinately elevated (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:ACO2, gene:MPC2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1, gene:PRELID3B, gene:SLC25A46, gene:SLC38A7).", "The re-esterification/acyl-remodeling arm is NOT proportionally engaged: although some lipogenic transcripts rise (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL), the set as a whole sits at list background and contains clear decreases (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3), so acyl-CoA activation capacity is predicted to limit re-incorporation of liberated fatty acids into glycerophospholipid/triacylglycerol.", "The predicted steady-state consequence is intracellular accumulation of lysosome-derived intermediates (ceramide, hexosylceramide, sphingosine, free fatty acid, lyso-phospholipid) per unit phosphatidylcholine in APOE4 microglia, with elevated oxidative disposal, rather than a net increase in bulk membrane phospholipid synthesis."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal sphingolipid/glycolipid hydrolysis and route catabolites to mitochondrial oxidation, with the hand-off out of the lysosome as the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2534800428312964, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.21043131943076523, "cosine_similarity": 0.09425132651705084, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_107", "mean_absolute_error": 0.734822006472492, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2534800428312964, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.21043131943076523, "cosine_similarity": 0.09425132651705084, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.734822006472492, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.66597225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 424}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_098", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and all |effect| \u003e= ~1; absence of a gene (e.g. SPTLC1/2, UGCG, SGMS1/2, DEGS1, PSAP, NEU1, MCOLN1, NPC1) means it was not in the supplied list, not that it is unchanged.", "Enrichment is judged against the supplied list's own strongly positive background (mean +1.39, 77% positive); if that global shift is a normalization or ambient-RNA artifact, absolute effect sizes are unreliable while relative set ranking is still interpretable.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2-D gel features; assignment of a spot change to a specific hydrolase is not possible, and spot movement can reflect proteolytic maturation or modification rather than total abundance.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for capacity only, not for enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, hydrolase localization or lipid flux; no lipid species, no enzyme activity and no lysosomal pH were measured in these data.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects may be partly non-cell-autonomous; replicate number and timepoint diversity are unknown, so the very large effect magnitudes may be inflated."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, the transcriptional difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia is concentrated in the lysosomal catabolic arm of sphingolipid metabolism (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, SMPD1, SUMF1) embedded in a broader CLEAR-type lysosome-biogenesis and late-endosomal routing program, while de novo sphingolipid synthesis genes are not coordinately induced and hydrolase-containing protein spots are not increased; the most parsimonious mechanism is that luminal glycosphingolipid degradation, not sphingolipid synthesis, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4 microglia, and the elevated transcripts represent a compensatory response whose hydrolytic capacity is limited downstream of mRNA. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological UGCG inhibition (eliglustat/Genz-123346) in APOE4 microglia should lower glucosylceramide-derived substrate load and selectively collapse the elevated lysosomal-hydrolase/CLEAR transcript module (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V0C) toward APOE3 levels, with a substantially smaller effect in APOE3; if UGCG inhibition leaves the APOE4 module unchanged, or lowers it equally in both genotypes, the glycosphingolipid-turnover bottleneck is weakened.", "Negative control perturbation: serine palmitoyltransferase inhibition (myriocin) should NOT normalize the APOE4 lysosomal module, because the de novo arm is not coordinately induced; strong myriocin-dependent normalization would favour a synthesis-driven mechanism and falsify the turnover framing.", "Untargeted or targeted lipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher substrate:product ratios across these hydrolase steps (GlcCer/ceramide, GM2:GM3 or GA2:LacCer, Gb3/LacCer, sphingomyelin/ceramide); equal or lower substrate:product ratios in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Enzyme-activity assays normalized to lysosomal protein (4-MU-beta-glucoside for GBA, 4-MU-GlcNAc for HEXA/HEXB, 4-MU-alpha-galactoside for GLA, acid sphingomyelinase assay) should show specific activity that is flat or increased far less than the \u003e=2-fold transcript change; activity increasing proportionally with mRNA would falsify the post-transcriptional bottleneck step.", "BODIPY-lactosylceramide or NBD-sphingomyelin pulse-chase should show slower conversion to downstream products and prolonged retention in LAMP1-positive compartments in APOE4; equal or faster clearance would falsify the flux claim.", "Blocking acidification with bafilomycin A1 should further raise the same hydrolase/CLEAR transcript set in both genotypes but with a smaller incremental rise in APOE4 (already partly engaged); an equal or larger incremental rise in APOE4 would argue the module is not already near its compensatory ceiling.", "If, instead, TFEB-independent inflammatory signalling drives the module, IKK/NF-kB or TLR blockade would abolish the hydrolase signature without changing glycosphingolipid substrate:product ratios; that outcome would favour the alternative inflammatory-state explanation over the turnover bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia sit in a lipid-handling / disease-associated-like transcriptional state relative to isogenic APOE3 (measured RNA: APOE, TREM2, ABCA7, ITGAX, CLEC7A, GPNMB up; CTSS strongly down). The state assignment is inferred; only transcript abundance is measured.", "Within this state a CLEAR-type lysosome-biogenesis module is coordinately elevated (TFEB and MITF transcripts up; GAA, CTSB, CTSD, LAMP1, SCARB2, IGF2R, GNPTG and several v-ATPase subunit transcripts up), enriched above the strong global positive RNA shift of this selected DE list (set mean ~3.1 vs background 1.39, permutation p~0.002). TFEB/MITF protein level, nuclear localization and transcription-factor activity are inferred, not measured.", "The hydrolase component is dominated by glycosphingolipid/sphingolipid catabolism and its activators/maturases (GBA, GBA2, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, GM2A, SMPD1, SUMF1; set mean 3.55, permutation p~0.008), whereas the de novo arm present in the list (KDSR, CERS4, CERS6, ORMDL2) is indistinguishable from background (mean 1.69, p~0.42) and complex-glycosphingolipid synthesis is discordant (ST3GAL5 and GLTP up, B4GALT5 down). This asymmetry places the genotype difference on turnover/routing rather than synthesis.", "Late-endosome/lysosome delivery and positioning machinery is co-elevated (AP5M1, AP5Z1, AP3D1, VPS26A, SNX3, RAB7A, ARL8B, EPG5; mean 3.91, p~0.002) while selected exocytic/secretory components fall (RAB27A, VAMP2) and CTSS, a secreted microglial protease, is the most strongly reduced protease transcript. Inferred consequence: cargo itineraries are biased toward the degradative branch and away from secretory/recycling release; no localization or flux was measured.", "Despite the transcript increases, protein spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases are not higher than other spots (mean +0.17 vs +0.42 log2, MWU p=0.44), cathepsin-candidate spots split in both directions (protein_spot:053 and :055 up, :058, :067 and :069 down) and an ATP6V1E1-candidate spot is down (protein_spot:064) although its ATP6V1E1 transcript is up. Because spots carry several candidate genes this is weak but consistent evidence that hydrolase protein/maturation does not scale with mRNA.", "Primary bottleneck (inferred): acid hydrolase capacity acting on glycosphingolipid-rich membrane cargo inside late endosomes/lysosomes. If capacity is limited post-transcriptionally (delivery, pro-enzyme maturation, saposin/activator availability, acidification), undegraded glucosyl-/galactosyl-ceramide, GM2/GA2, globotriaosylceramide and sphingomyelin persist and continue to drive the TFEB-type transcriptional response, a feed-forward compensatory loop rather than a demonstrated causal chain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate a TFEB-type lysosomal glycosphingolipid-catabolic and late-endosomal routing module without matching de novo sphingolipid synthesis or hydrolase protein gain, indicating a post-transcriptional bottleneck in luminal glycosphingolipid turnover"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14752796957501013, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.08680487216563154, "cosine_similarity": 0.09395143797664687, "direction_accuracy": 0.13268608414239483, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6648349514563107, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14752796957501013, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.08680487216563154, "cosine_similarity": 0.09395143797664687, "direction_accuracy": 0.13268608414239483, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6648349514563107, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.587561, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 425}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_072", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global upward skew (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46); pathway statements are therefore made relative to that skewed background, and absolute magnitudes are not interpretable as log2 fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme/transporter capacity; no protein, activity, flux, sterol mass, oxysterol level, or subcellular sterol localization was measured in the supplied data, so all compartmental and flux statements are inferences.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin-containing spots are used only as ambiguous, partly discordant corroboration and not as evidence for any single protein.", "Key nodes of the proposed bottleneck (NPC1, STARD3, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1, ABCG1, SOAT2, LIPA) are absent from the supplied list; their absence is assumed to reflect selection/detection of the differential list rather than proven invariance.", "The APOE3 and APOE4 lines are assumed truly isogenic and matched in differentiation stage and in astrocyte co-culture composition; replicate structure was not supplied, so 10X Flex ambient RNA, cell-composition and maturation differences cannot be excluded as partial contributors.", "APOE4 protein being a poorer lipid/cholesterol acceptor than APOE3 is background knowledge and is unverified within this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by running a high-throughput lipid-ingestion and lysosomal-hydrolysis program while the NPC-dependent hand-off of unesterified cholesterol from the late endosome/lysosome to the endoplasmic reticulum is not scaled with it; the resulting ER-accessible sterol shortfall keeps SCAP-SREBP-2-responsive transcripts (SREBF2, LDLR, INSIG1, HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP) and uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36) elevated at the same time as lysosomal hydrolase, oxysterol-generating and lipid-export transcripts, i.e. a 'sterol-loaded compartment / sterol-starved ER' mis-compartmentalization state rather than a simple increase or decrease in total cholesterol. Compartmental sterol distribution and all fluxes are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological block of NPC1-dependent egress with U18666A in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 transcript signature - coordinate induction of SREBF2/LDLR/INSIG1/DHCR24/HMGCS1 together with TFEB-driven lysosomal hydrolases (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA) and LGALS3/GPNMB - while shifting filipin/ALOD4 sterol from the ER/plasma-membrane-accessible pool into LAMP1-positive membranes. If U18666A-treated APOE3 cells move orthogonally to, or away from, the measured APOE4 signature, the bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Localization test: quantitative imaging with filipin plus a D4H/ALOD4 ER- and PM-accessible-cholesterol probe should show higher LAMP1-colocalized sterol and lower accessible sterol in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions. Equal or lower lysosomal sterol with unchanged accessible sterol would falsify the core claim, and enrichment of sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide instead of sterol would redirect the mechanism to a non-sterol lysosomal substrate.", "Sensor test: immunoblot of cleaved nuclear SREBP-2 relative to precursor should be higher in APOE4; if nuclear SREBP-2 is unchanged while the sterol-synthesis transcripts are still elevated, the transcript pattern is not driven by ER sterol sensing and Step 4 fails.", "Rescue test: 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or delivery of ER-accessible sterol (MbCD:cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol), should suppress the SREBP-2 target arm substantially more in APOE4 than in APOE3 and reduce LAMP1-sterol without first requiring loss of the lysosomal hydrolase program; equal suppression in both genotypes would indicate intact ER sterol delivery and weaken the mechanism.", "Disposal-arm test: culture medium and cell 27-hydroxycholesterol and 25-hydroxycholesterol should be higher in APOE4, and CYP27A1 knockdown should further raise LAMP1-sterol and further increase SREBP-2 targets. Unchanged oxysterols would falsify Step 5 (the mitochondrial/oxysterol overflow route) while leaving Steps 1-4 testable.", "Specificity control: if the lysosomal, sterol-response and OXPHOS transcript differences all collapse after per-cell library-size and ambient-RNA correction, or track with a maturation marker gradient, the observed pattern is a global expression-scale artifact rather than a sterol-trafficking mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry a markedly larger transcriptional program for endolysosomal degradation and biogenesis (TFEB, GAA, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, LAMP1, SCARB2, RAB7A, and the lysosomal-damage/lipid-stress markers LGALS3 and GPNMB), consistent with an expanded and more heavily loaded acidic compartment.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): scavenger/lipoprotein-uptake and lipid-handling receptors are simultaneously higher (SCARB1 very strongly, CD36, TREM2, APOE, NPC2), which should raise the delivery rate of sterol-containing cargo into that compartment; ingestion flux itself was not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred): the export arm of that compartment - NPC1/NPC2-, STARD3- and ORP-mediated transfer of unesterified cholesterol to ER membranes at membrane contact sites - is not coordinately increased (NPC1, STARD3, STARD4 absent from the supplied differential list; only NPC2 +1.17 and OSBPL1A +1.03, while OSBPL8 is -1.90), so cholesterol egress becomes rate-limiting relative to Steps 1-2 and sterol is predicted to accumulate in LAMP1-positive membranes with a reduced ER-accessible pool.", "Step 4 (inferred sensor state, measured output): a low ER sterol pool prevents INSIG-mediated retention of SCAP-SREBP-2, sustaining SREBP-2 processing; this is read out as coordinate elevation of SREBF2, LDLR, MYLIP, INSIG1 and post-squalene/steroidogenic-enzyme transcripts (HMGCS1, ACAT2, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24, EBP) together with SREBF1/SCD, producing a futile cycle in which the cell keeps importing and making sterol it cannot deliver to the ER.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred routes): overflow-disposal routes are engaged in parallel - esterification/storage (SOAT1, DGAT1), side-chain oxidation to oxysterols via mitochondrial CYP27A1 and CH25H supported by an unusually strong mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS transcript program (OGDH, MDH1 and the NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5 set), and acceptor-dependent efflux/redistribution (APOE, ABCA7, PLTP); these routes are inferred to be insufficient because the sterol-response arm remains on.", "Step 6 (consequence): chronic sterol/lipid mis-compartmentalization sustains lysosomal stress and a reactive lipid-handling microglial phenotype (LGALS3, GPNMB, ITGAX, CLEC7A) with low-grade chemokine output (CXCL8, CCL2), rather than a homeostatic surveillance state."], "title": "A late-endosomal/lysosomal cholesterol egress bottleneck keeps the ER sterol-sensing pool low in APOE4 microglia despite an expanded lysosomal-oxidative catabolic program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21000258464719565, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01769611412581943, "cosine_similarity": 0.09244609605463, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_072", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6504336569579289, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21000258464719565, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01769611412581943, "cosine_similarity": 0.09244609605463, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6504336569579289, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6302, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 426}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_094", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported log fold changes have an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global positive offset (median about +1.46 across 2212 rows), so only relative rank within the supplied distribution, not absolute sign or magnitude, is treated as interpretable.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway coherence is therefore assessed against the supplied rows as background, and absent genes (GAPDH, PKM, LDHA/LDHB, PDHA1, CS, MDH2, GOT2, CPT1A, TFAM) are treated as unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the abundance of the corresponding enzyme or carrier protein; no enzyme activity, metabolite level, respiration rate, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number or protein phosphorylation was measured here.", "Relative depletion of mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed to reflect a real mitochondrial-versus-nuclear transcript imbalance rather than a normalisation, ambient-RNA or cell-quality artefact of the 10X Flex pipeline; this assumption is not testable from the supplied data.", "Protein spots contain up to six candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak, non-decisive corroboration.", "Astrocyte co-culture means measured microglial transcripts may partly reflect non-cell-autonomous substrate supply (for example astrocytic lactate) that was not measured.", "Comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 under mock treatment at one timepoint, so no causal direction between APOE4 genotype and the metabolic program is established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a transcript program that biases carbon away from cytosolic glycolytic commitment and the pentose-phosphate branch and toward mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA turning and malate-aspartate NADH shuttling, while the mtDNA-encoded terminal-OXPHOS arm (most extremely MT-ATP6, with MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2) is relatively depleted; we hypothesise that this stoichiometric mismatch between an expanded nuclear-encoded oxidative apparatus and a limiting mtDNA-encoded complex III/V subunit supply is the primary bottleneck, so that increased substrate delivery is not converted into proportionally increased ATP-linked respiration, and instead engages an integrated stress response (DELE1, EIF2AK3, DDIT3) and a compensatory lysosomal catabolic program (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1H, TFEB). All statements about flux, activity and direction are inferred; only relative transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) during extracellular flux analysis should reduce basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption by a significantly larger fraction in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, and the compensatory glycolytic rise (ECAR, or extracellular lactate) should be smaller in APOE4, with a larger fall in ATP/ADP or a larger rise in AMPK activation. If APOE4 shows equal or smaller MPC-dependence of respiration, or a normal glycolytic compensation, the substrate-bias core of the mechanism is wrong.", "Mitonuclear bottleneck test: immunoblot or targeted proteomics of mtDNA-encoded MT-CO1/MT-ATP6 versus nuclear-encoded NDUFB8/ATP5F1B/SDHA, each normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20), should show a lower mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded ratio in APOE4, and complex V and complex III in-gel activity per mitochondrial mass should be lower while nuclear subunit content is equal or higher. If the ratio and complex V activity per mitochondrial mass are unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is falsified and the data would instead be explained by simple mitochondrial biogenesis or mass increase.", "Flux test: 13C6-glucose tracing should show, in APOE4 relative to APOE3, a higher M+2 enrichment of citrate, alpha-ketoglutarate and malate and a lower M+3 lactate fraction per unit glucose consumed, with reduced M+5/M+6 labelling of pentose-phosphate-derived ribose. Increased lactate labelling or increased PPP labelling in APOE4 would reject the carbon-redistribution claim.", "Causal-direction test: restoring complex V capacity (for example by rescuing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply, or by mild uncoupling to relieve the assembly-limited ATP synthase load) should lower the ISR transcripts DDIT3 and NUPR1 and reduce the lysosomal hydrolase program in APOE4 without reversing the APOE genotype; conversely ISRIB should blunt DDIT3 but should NOT normalise the mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded subunit ratio. If ISRIB normalises the OXPHOS subunit imbalance, the ISR is upstream rather than downstream and the step order is wrong.", "Substrate-dependence test: APOE4 microglia should lose more viability or ATP than APOE3 when glucose is replaced by galactose (forcing oxidative ATP production), and should be relatively protected by pyruvate or by a lysosomal-substrate-sparing condition; equal galactose sensitivity would weaken the mechanism.", "Lysosomal-compensation test: lysosomal acid alpha-glucosidase or v-ATPase inhibition (for example bafilomycin A1 at non-toxic dose) should reduce basal oxygen consumption more in APOE4 than APOE3; no genotype difference would weaken step 6 while leaving steps 1-4 intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype shifts the microglial transcriptional program so that nuclear-encoded mitochondrial substrate-entry components are relatively enriched: mitochondrial pyruvate carrier and PDH-supporting genes (gene:MPC2, gene:DLD, gene:PDP1), TCA enzymes (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3G) and metabolite carriers (gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46) sit in the top decile-to-quartile of the measured effect distribution.", "In parallel, the two committed cytosolic glycolytic control points that were measured (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP) and the non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD) are among the most relatively depleted rows, so we infer reduced glycolytic and PPP flux capacity per unit glucose uptake rather than reduced glucose transport (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3 are relatively increased).", "The cytosolic malate-aspartate arm (gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) together with gene:SLC25A11 and gene:SLC25A13 is inferred to move more cytosolic NADH into the matrix, further committing pyruvate to oxidation instead of to lactate; lactate dehydrogenase transcripts were not measured, so this step is inference, not observation.", "Nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunits are coordinately enriched (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B) and mitochondrial protein-import components are enriched (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:TIMM8B), whereas mtDNA-encoded subunits of complex V and III are relatively depleted (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2); we infer that assembly of complex V and complex III, and therefore ATP-linked oxygen consumption, is the rate-limiting step of the expanded oxidative program.", "The resulting energetic mismatch is inferred to activate the mitochondrial integrated stress response, consistent with relative enrichment of gene:DELE1, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3 and gene:NUPR1; this is a transcript-level inference because eIF2-alpha phosphorylation was not measured.", "Because glycolytic buffering capacity is transcriptionally reduced, the cells are inferred to recruit alternative catabolic carbon via a TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A) together with lipid/lipoprotein uptake (gene:SCARB1) and glycogen handling (gene:GYS1, gene:GAA), plus phosphagen buffering (gene:GAMT).", "Net predicted phenotype: APOE4 microglia are more dependent on mitochondrial pyruvate import for respiration, but have lower ATP-linked respiration and lower spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass than APOE3, with greater reliance on lysosomal catabolism to maintain the pool of oxidisable substrate."], "title": "Mitonuclear mismatch caps a pyruvate-oxidation-biased carbon program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10818594690396188, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010279912914365965, "cosine_similarity": 0.09172891506899089, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_094", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6441391585760518, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10818594690396188, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010279912914365965, "cosine_similarity": 0.09172891506899089, "direction_accuracy": 0.12944983818770225, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6441391585760518, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7476095, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 427}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_063", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The 2,212 RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0, adj. p \u003c= 0.05) whose logarithm base is unspecified; effects are compared only on that reported scale, and the 77.1 percent positive sign skew of the supplied list - not a 50/50 expectation - is the correct background for judging any program.", "Genes absent from the supplied list (e.g. LAMP2, NPC1, PSAP, GRN, G6PD, PDHA1, LDHA, PPARGC1A, most MT- genes) are unknown, not unchanged; program coverage is therefore partial and the descriptive resampling comparisons are not formal enrichment tests and do not treat genes as independent.", "The 6 supplied MT- rows are assumed to reflect genuine relative mtDNA-encoded transcript differences rather than probe-capture bias of the 10X Flex assay; if they are assay artefacts, step 4 collapses and the state becomes plain increased oxidative capacity.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding machinery; no enzyme activity, respiration, complex assembly, lysosomal proteolytic flux, NADPH/GSH pool or organelle localization was measured in this dataset.", "2D-gel spots contain 2-6 candidate proteins each and are treated only as compatibility tests; no spot is assigned to a single protein. The split CTSB spots (protein_spot:055/057 up vs 058/067 down), near-neutral CTSD spots and negative ATP6V1E1-containing spots mean protein-level lysosomal expansion is not demonstrated, and the up TALDO1-containing spots (protein_spot:041/045/047) cannot be separated from ANXA1/ACTB/PSMD7.", "The causal ordering in steps 1-2 (catabolic supply driving mitochondrial routing) is inferred from co-regulation; the reverse ordering, or a shared upstream regulator, is not excluded by these data.", "Reduced PPP/NADPH reserve is a prospective, challenge-revealed prediction; the mock data do not establish an ongoing oxidative or bioenergetic defect."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 not by a lysosomal blockade but by a coordinated cell-state shift: endolysosomal/CLEAR catabolic transcripts and lipid-uptake/handling transcripts are elevated together with mitochondrial import, malate-aspartate shuttle, pyruvate-carrier, TCA and nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts, while upper-glycolysis and pentose-phosphate transcripts move down against a strongly up-skewed selected-list background. Because the four most-reduced mtDNA-encoded ETC subunits are not co-up-regulated with the 38/38 up nuclear ETC subunits, the transcript state is better described as demand-driven routing of catabolism-derived carbon and reducing equivalents into mitochondria whose assembled complex capacity is not demonstrated, rather than as proven increased respiratory throughput; the accompanying loss of cytosolic NADPH-regenerating transcripts (TALDO1, PGD, HK2, PFKP) predicts reduced reserve that would be revealed by a future oxidative or lipid-load challenge, not necessarily an ongoing defect in mock. All statements are about measured transcript and protein-spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity, complex assembly and localization were not measured and causal direction is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective extracellular-flux assay on mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show higher basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption with equal or lower glycolytic (ECAR) contribution, and UK5099 inhibition of MPC should suppress OCR disproportionately in APOE4. If APOE4 OCR equals or falls below APOE3, or if MPC inhibition affects both genotypes equally, the routing step is weakened.", "Prospective mitonuclear test: BN-PAGE/immunoblot or quantitative proteomics of complexes I, III, IV and V in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 should show nuclear-encoded subunit protein rising more than mtDNA-encoded subunits (increased free/unassembled nuclear subunit pool, induction of mitochondrial stress markers). If nuclear and mtDNA-encoded subunit proteins rise in stoichiometric proportion and holo-complex levels increase accordingly, step 4 is falsified and the state is successful adaptation, not outrunning supply.", "Prospective 13C6-glucose tracing: APOE4 should show greater m+2 labelling of citrate/malate and reduced labelling of PPP intermediates (6-phosphogluconate, ribose-5-P) than APOE3. Equal or higher PPP labelling in APOE4 would falsify the PPP-displacement step.", "Prospective challenge, distinguishing reserve loss from ongoing defect: myelin-debris or oxLDL loading, or an H2O2 pulse, should lower GSH/GSSG and spare respiratory capacity more in APOE4 than APOE3 while mock baselines are similar; equal challenge responses would weaken step 6 without affecting the mock-state description.", "Prospective lysosomal-flux test of the supplier arm: DQ-BSA dequenching and cathepsin activity assays should show equal or increased, not decreased, degradative flux in mock APOE4. Reduced flux would refute the 'no lysosomal blockade' framing and favour the failed-compensation alternative; unchanged flux despite elevated hydrolase transcripts would make the CLEAR module transcript-only and remove it as a substrate supplier."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry an elevated endolysosomal/CLEAR-associated transcript module (hydrolases GAA, GBA, HEXA, NAGLU, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK; v-ATPase ATP6V1H, ATP6V0C, ATP6AP1; biogenesis/targeting TFEB, GNPTG, IGF2R) plus lipid-uptake and lipid-handling transcripts (SCARB1, SCP2, SREBF1, SCD, APOE, TREM2), consistent with a higher endolysosomal cargo-processing set-point (abundance measured; degradative flux inferred, not measured).", "Carbon and reducing equivalents derived from that catabolic input are routed toward mitochondria: mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2, oxoglutarate/malate carrier SLC25A11, adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5, cytosolic malate-aspartate arm MDH1 and GOT1, fatty-acid oxidation ETFA and HADHA, and glutamate entry GLUD1/GLS are all up, while hexose-committing HK2/HK3/PFKP and the PPP enzymes TALDO1 and PGD are down against a 77 percent-positive background - the only program in the list leaning negative.", "The mitochondrial protein-import and matrix chaperone machinery is co-elevated (TOMM22, TIMM44, HSPA9), and every represented nuclear-encoded ETC/ATP-synthase subunit is up (38/38; NDUFA5, NDUFS7, ATP5ME, ATP5MC3, COX8A), i.e. the nucleus mounts a coordinated oxidative-capacity program.", "mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits do not follow: MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are reduced (MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are exceptions). This mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch means imported nuclear subunits can exceed the mtDNA-encoded partners required for holo-complex assembly, so elevated nuclear ETC transcripts do not establish proportionally increased assembled ETC capacity.", "Net measured state in mock: a lipid/catabolism-fuelled, mitochondrially routed microglial state that retains homeostatic identity (CSF1R, GPR34, MEF2C up; no ISG rows; no DAM-style loss of homeostatic markers) rather than an inflammatory or degenerative switch.", "Predicted consequence, prospective and not observed here: with PPP transcripts down and NADPH supply shifted toward mitochondrial sources (NNT up), APOE4 microglia should show reduced cytosolic NADPH/GSH reserve and reduced spare respiratory capacity when challenged with lipid load or oxidant, while basal function in mock may be near-normal."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a catabolic-to-mitochondrial routing state in which a nuclear-encoded oxidative program outruns mtDNA-encoded subunit supply and displaces cytosolic PPP reserve"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22254735442897758, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10766157047415435, "cosine_similarity": 0.09132978696956436, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_063", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6561100323624596, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.22254735442897758, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10766157047415435, "cosine_similarity": 0.09132978696956436, "direction_accuracy": 0.17637540453074432, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6561100323624596, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.24059375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 100}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_178", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong positive shift (median +1.46 in the reported, base-unspecified logarithm; 1705/2212 rows positive), so all directional claims are made as percentile ranks within this list, and absence of a gene (ASAH1, SPHK1/2, SGMS1, UGCG, PSAP, NPC1, NEU1, GALC) means unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme capacity; hydrolase activity, protein amount, luminal pH, substrate delivery and lipid pools were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots carry a median of 5 candidate genes plus frequent keratin contaminants, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific hydrolase; they are used only as weak, non-confirmatory evidence about RNA-protein concordance.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes and profiled by 10X Flex, so some gene rows may carry ambient or non-microglial signal; replicate number is not supplied in the workbook.", "The comparison is a single genotype contrast at one timepoint (day 30, mock), so the proposed retention state is assumed to be steady-state rather than a transient developmental difference.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; magnitudes are not converted to fold changes."], "claim": "In isogenic mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 shifts the endolysosomal sphingolipid program toward luminal hydrolysis of sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA transcripts among the highest-ranked in the supplied differential-expression list) while the measured sphingoid-base disposal/anabolic arm (SGPL1, CERK, B4GALT5) sits at or below the background of this positively shifted list and salvage re-acylation genes (CERS4, CERS6) are up; the proposed rate-limiting step is therefore egress/disposal of lysosome-derived ceramide and sphingosine, not hydrolase capacity, so ceramide is predicted to be retained in endolysosomal membranes and to sustain a compensatory TFEB/MITF lysosomal-biogenesis and RAB7A/retromer routing program together with reduced RAB27A-dependent lysosome-related-organelle exocytosis. All lipid pools here are inferred; no lipid or enzyme-activity measurement is supplied and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of lysosome-enriched fractions from isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show higher ceramide (notably C16:0/C18:0 species, the CERS5/6- and CERS4-type products) and higher free sphingosine, with an unchanged or reduced sphingosine-1-phosphate/ceramide ratio and no proportional accumulation of the upstream substrates sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and GM2. If APOE4 lysosomes instead show accumulated sphingomyelin/glucosylceramide with unchanged or lower ceramide, the increased-hydrolysis step is wrong; if all sphingolipid species are unchanged while free cholesterol is elevated, the sterol arm (gene:SREBF1, gene:DHCR24) is the better explanation and this hypothesis fails.", "Discriminating perturbation: partial SMPD1 knockdown (or functional acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition) in APOE4 microglia should lower lysosomal ceramide and normalize the TFEB-target transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GAA, LAMP1) and pHrodo-bead/myelin clearance toward APOE3 levels, with little effect in APOE3. If SMPD1 knockdown lowers ceramide but leaves lysosomal expansion and clearance unchanged, the ceramide-to-phenotype link is broken; if it changes nothing at all in APOE4, Step 1 is not rate-contributing.", "Egress-restoration test: raising disposal capacity by ASAH1 or SPHK1 over-expression, or blocking salvage re-acylation with fumonisin B1, should reduce endolysosomal ceramide and improve degradative flux (DQ-BSA / Magic Red kinetics) in APOE4 more than in APOE3. Failure of any egress-side manipulation to reduce ceramide or restore flux would refute the 'exit is the bottleneck' claim and favour a generic TFEB-driven lysosome-biogenesis explanation.", "Enzyme-activity check: GBA, HEXA/HEXB and acid-sphingomyelinase activities measured in APOE4 lysates should be higher than APOE3, tracking the transcript ranks. Equal or lower activities despite higher transcripts would show the RNA changes do not translate into flux and would weaken the whole mechanism.", "Routing test: RAB27A re-expression in APOE4 should increase lysosomal exocytosis markers (surface LAMP1, extracellular hexosaminidase release) and partially lower intracellular sphingolipid load; if surface LAMP1 and enzyme release are already equal or higher in APOE4, Step 4 is refuted and should be dropped as a secondary route rather than rescuing the model."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_178", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 raises transcripts of lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases and cofactors - SMPD1 (+5.63, ~95th percentile of the supplied gene list), GBA (+6.71, ~98th), HEXA (+5.68, ~96th), HEXB (+2.17), GM2A (+2.01), GLA (+1.53), GBA2 (+2.63) - which we interpret as increased capacity, not measured activity, for converting sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids to ceramide inside the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux limit): The measured routes that consume or export sphingoid bases are not concordantly raised - SGPL1 (+1.09, ~29th percentile), CERK (+1.23, ~38th), B4GALT5 (-1.88, ~13th) - and the salvage arm CERS4 (+2.52) and CERS6 (+1.06) would re-acylate escaping sphingosine back to ceramide; ASAH1, SPHK1/2, SGMS1 and UGCG are absent from the supplied selected-DE rows and are treated as unmeasured, so disposal capacity is assumed (not observed) to be unchanged.", "Step 3 (inferred lipid state): The imbalance between Step 1 and Step 2 is proposed to raise steady-state ceramide (and sphingosine) in late-endosomal/lysosomal membranes of APOE4 microglia; this pool is inferred, not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Reduced RAB27A (-2.52, ~8th percentile) alongside up-regulated late-endosomal and retrieval machinery (RAB7A +2.65, VPS26A +4.86, SNX3 +3.95, CHMP4B +3.82) is interpreted as a shift away from lysosome-related-organelle exocytosis toward intracellular retention and recycling, removing the vesicular escape route for the excess sphingolipid.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Ceramide-loaded, poorly secreting lysosomes sustain a compensatory biogenesis program - TFEB (+2.38), MITF (+1.03), CTSB (+5.52), CTSD (+2.86), GAA (+9.96), ATP6V1A (+4.23), LAMP1 (+1.38), IGF2R (+2.02) - which expands the compartment without resolving the lipid load.", "Step 6 (predicted functional consequence): Net cargo-clearance flux per lysosome falls despite higher hydrolase transcripts; consistently, the ambiguous protein spots containing cathepsin/hexosaminidase candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:053 +1.54, protein_spot:052 +2.14 vs protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:069 -1.38), i.e. the RNA increase is not mirrored by a coherent protein-spot increase."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without a matched sphingoid-base exit route, creating a ceramide-retention bottleneck in the endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20199940922349813, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.007779163674875638, "cosine_similarity": 0.09012141419972126, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_178", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6505663430420712, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20199940922349813, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.007779163674875638, "cosine_similarity": 0.09012141419972126, "direction_accuracy": 0.1423948220064725, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6505663430420712, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.82070925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 428}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_130", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (77% up, median +1.46), so only rank/percentile comparisons within the list are interpreted, never the absolute sign or magnitude of a single gene.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effects are not converted to fold changes and RNA and protein-spot (log2) effects are never placed on a common scale.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with unknown lag, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, flux, ROS level, NAD(P)H ratio or organelle localisation was measured in this dataset.", "2D-gel protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; spot:017 (CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and spot:077 (PRDX2 among five keratin/actin candidates) are treated as ambiguous and non-decisive, and spots are used only as weak concordance/counter-evidence.", "Absent genes (CAT, SOD1, SOD2, GSR, G6PD, IDH1/2, TKT, LDHA, all PEX genes, MRPL/MRPS) are absent from the selected list, which is assumed to reflect selection/filtering rather than proven invariance.", "Astrocyte co-culture and unreported replicate structure are assumed not to differ systematically between the isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 arms; the comparison is assumed to be genotype-driven rather than clone- or batch-driven."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 cells carry a coordinately higher transcript program for lysosomal hydrolysis, mitochondrial substrate delivery and nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunits, while the transcripts for NADPH- and NAD+-regenerating steps (oxidative/non-oxidative pentose phosphate: PGD, TALDO1; NAD salvage/kinase: NAMPT, NADK) and for mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunits fall in the low tail of the same globally up-shifted differential list; we hypothesise that reductant (NADPH/NAD+) regeneration capacity, not oxidative capacity, is the limiting node, so APOE4 microglia sustain an increased peroxide/electron-leak load through thiol-peroxidase and one-carbon systems (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GSS, SHMT1/2) and have narrowed redox reserve. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation/biogenesis is explicitly not the mechanism here: the peroxisomal transcripts present are flat or low relative to background (ACOX1 at the 39th percentile, ABCD1 at the 16th) and catalase/PEX transcripts were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: NAD+/NADPH supply restriction should be selectively toxic to APOE4. Treating isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with the NAMPT inhibitor FK866 (low nM, 24-48 h) or the G6PD/PPP inhibitor 6-aminonicotinamide should lower viability, phagocytic uptake and maximal OCR substantially more in APOE4 than APOE3, and nicotinamide riboside or NMN supplementation should preferentially rescue APOE4. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive than APOE3 to FK866/6-AN, and NR gives no genotype-selective rescue, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Compartment-resolved redox: APOE4 microglia should show a lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio and a more oxidised glutathione/roGFP2-Grx1 and mito-roGFP signal, with increased PRDX3 dimer (hyperoxidised/dimeric) fraction on non-reducing blots, despite higher PRDX2/PRDX3 transcript levels. Unchanged or more reduced APOE4 redox sensors would weaken the mechanism.", "Mitonuclear test: BN-PAGE/complex-activity assays should show that the increase in nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts is not matched by proportional increases in assembled complex I/III/IV/V, and doxycycline-mediated mitoribosome inhibition or mtDNA depletion should exaggerate the APOE4-specific oxidative phenotype. Fully proportional complex assembly and a normal spare respiratory capacity in APOE4 would argue against step 3.", "Peroxisome rejection test: peroxisome-targeted catalase overexpression or ACOX1 inhibition should not normalise APOE4-selective redox or lysosomal phenotypes, whereas mitochondria-targeted catalase/MitoQ or MAS inhibition with aminooxyacetate should shift APOE4 more than APOE3. Selective rescue by peroxisomal catalase would refute the chosen mechanism in favour of the peroxisomal alternative.", "Substrate-source test: if the lysosome-to-mitochondria route supplies the oxidative load, blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or lysosomal acid lipase should reduce the APOE4-specific excess in basal OCR and mitochondrial superoxide toward APOE3 levels; no genotype-selective effect would weaken steps 1-2.", "Direction control: the mechanism predicts these differences persist under mock conditions in re-derived isogenic clones and pseudobulk-independent single-cell testing; if the ETC/lysosome coordinate signal disappears once the global positive shift is removed by re-normalisation or by using an unbiased whole-transcriptome comparison, the observation base itself is an artefact and the hypothesis is void."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_130", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance than APOE3 for lysosomal hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB; 27-gene set median +2.02 vs list median +1.46, rank-sum z=+3.0), and for scavenger/lipid-uptake and lipogenic transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD). Inferred, not measured: increased degradative flux and substrate liberation into the cytosol.", "Step 2 (measured, RNA): transcripts for carbon entry into mitochondria and TCA turning are among the highest in the list (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:GLUD1, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA; 14-gene set z=+4.1). Inferred: greater pyruvate/glutamate/acyl-CoA and cytosolic-NADH delivery to the matrix via the malate-aspartate shuttle; shuttle flux and NADH/NAD+ ratios were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured, RNA): all 38 detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts are higher in APOE4 (median +2.64, z=+4.0; gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:UQCRC2), together with mitochondrial import/translation machinery (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM8B, gene:TUFM, gene:HSPA9; z=+2.9), whereas four of six mtDNA-encoded core subunits sit in the bottom 5-19% of the list (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2). Inferred: a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch that favours partially assembled complexes and electron leak; complex assembly, membrane potential and superoxide were not measured.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured, RNA): the reductant-supply module is counter-directional in an otherwise up-shifted list (gene:PGD 19th, gene:TALDO1 9th, gene:NADK 21st, gene:NAMPT 7th percentile; set z=-2.5), while NNT and ME1 are only modestly positive. Inferred: cytosolic NADPH and total NAD(H) pool regeneration do not scale with the expanded oxidative programme, so glutathione/thioredoxin re-reduction becomes rate-limiting. The NAD(P)H pools themselves were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured, RNA; inferred consequence): buffering of the resulting peroxide load leans on thiol peroxidases and folate one-carbon NADPH generation (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:TXNL1, gene:GSS, gene:SHMT1, gene:SHMT2; set z=+2.8) with an integrated-stress-response tone (gene:DDIT3, gene:EIF2AK3). Elevated transcripts indicate demand/adaptive expression; peroxiredoxin oxidation state, and therefore antioxidant activity, is not measured.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype): under mock conditions APOE4 microglia are viable and even more oxidative, but their redox reserve is narrow, so NAD+- or NADPH-depleting and peroxide challenges should unmask a selective APOE4 deficit rather than a baseline one."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a lysosome-to-mitochondria oxidative catabolic program without scaling NAD(P)H supply, making cytosolic reductant regeneration the redox bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24417531292692832, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1129722206234334, "cosine_similarity": 0.08909815778806698, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_130", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6616278317152104, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24417531292692832, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1129722206234334, "cosine_similarity": 0.08909815778806698, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6616278317152104, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85089125, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 429}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_098", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript log-fold-changes (logarithm base not stated in the workbook; preserved as reported) track enzyme protein and catalytic activity at least ordinally; no enzyme activity, lipid pool, or subcellular localization was measured here.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive), so evidence is taken from rank within this biased set, not from sign alone.", "Absence of ASAH1/SPHK1/SPHK2/UGCG/SGMS/PSAP rows means 'not supplied', not 'unchanged'; the proposed bottleneck step is an inference about an unmeasured pool.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are treated as non-identifying; no spot is used as protein-level confirmation of any single enzyme.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some genotype-associated transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous.", "Ceramide generated in the lysosomal lumen is not freely exported without acid-ceramidase-dependent conversion, so a hydrolase/ceramidase imbalance translates into local accumulation."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia the input arm of lysosomal sphingolipid turnover is transcriptionally amplified (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB/GM2A, GBA2) as part of an MiT/TFE-type lysosomal program, while the ceramide-disposal arm is not coordinately induced (acid ceramidase/sphingosine-kinase transcripts absent from the supplied list, SGPL1 up only at the low end of the global shift, CERS4/CERS6 up favouring re-acylation, B4GALT5 down closing the anabolic exit to LacCer). We propose that ceramide/sphingosine egress from the late-endosome/lysosome is the rate-limiting step that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3, producing a ceramide-enriched late-endosomal membrane that biases RAB7/ESCRT-dependent routing (RAB7A, CHMP4B, VPS26A, SNX3, VAMP3) toward retention and intraluminal-vesicle/secretory disposal rather than completed clearance. Causality is not established by these data; the ceramide pool itself was not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (whole-cell and lysosome-enriched fractions) should show an increased ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio with C16:0-C20:0 ceramide species disproportionately raised and sphingomyelin lowered, while glucosylceramide is not increased. Finding accumulated glucosylceramide/hexosylceramide with unchanged or lowered ceramide would weaken the mechanism (it would indicate hydrolase transcripts are not converted into flux).", "Discriminating perturbation: raising ceramide-disposal capacity in APOE4 microglia (ASAH1 overexpression, or recombinant/chaperone-boosted acid ceramidase) should lower lysosomal ceramide, restore LysoTracker/LAMP1 morphology and cargo (myelin or apoptotic-cell) clearance rate toward APOE3 without lowering GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 transcripts; if ASAH1 gain-of-function leaves clearance and routing unchanged, the disposal-bottleneck claim fails.", "De novo synthesis discriminator: myriocin (serine palmitoyltransferase inhibition) should give little or no rescue of the APOE4 clearance/routing phenotype, whereas acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition (e.g. ARC39) should partially normalise the ceramide/SM ratio. Full rescue by myriocin with no effect of ARC39 would favour a de novo-synthesis mechanism instead and refute this hypothesis.", "Enzyme-activity test: in APOE4 lysates GBA, HEXA/B and acid-sphingomyelinase specific activities should be higher than APOE3 while acid ceramidase activity is not proportionally higher (activity ratio shifted \u003e1.5-fold). Proportional co-elevation of acid ceramidase would remove the proposed bottleneck.", "Routing test: APOE4 microglia should show increased ceramide-positive intraluminal-vesicle/exosome release (CD63/CHMP4B-dependent, blocked by GW4869 or CHMP4B knockdown) and slower retromer-dependent receptor recycling; unchanged secretion and normal recycling kinetics would weaken step 5.", "Specificity control: if the elevated hydrolase transcripts are purely a generic MiT/TFE output, then TFEB knockdown should lower GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 together with GAA/CTSK/NAGLU and should not selectively normalise sphingolipid species; a selective sphingolipid rescue by TFEB knockdown would instead support sphingolipid-specific regulation beyond the generic program."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts of MiT/TFE factors and lysosomal machinery (TFEB +2.38, MITF +1.03, ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86). Inferred: increased lysosomal biogenesis/acidification capacity, i.e. a standing lysosomal-stress or substrate-load response.", "Measured: within this program the sphingolipid-hydrolase transcripts sit in the extreme upper tail of the selected DE distribution (GBA +6.71, 98th pct; HEXA +5.68, 96th; SMPD1 +5.63, 95th; GBA2 +2.63; HEXB +2.17; GM2A +2.01; lipid-transfer/handling GLTP +2.38, NPC2 +1.17, SCARB2 +1.06). Inferred: increased hydrolytic flux from sphingomyelin and glyco-sphingolipids into lumenal ceramide.", "Inferred bottleneck (not measured): the deacylation/phosphorylation/export steps that clear ceramide (ASAH1, ACER3, SPHK1/2, SGPP1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, PSAP, GALC) have no rows in the supplied RNA list; the one measured exit enzyme, SGPL1 (+1.09), ranks at the 29th percentile of the global positive shift, and CERS4 (+2.52) and CERS6 (+1.06) favour re-acylation of salvaged sphingosine back to C16-C20 ceramide, while B4GALT5 (-1.88, 13th pct) reduces the LacCer/complex-glycosphingolipid escape route. Net predicted flux imbalance: ceramide/sphingosine accumulation in the late-endosome/lysosome.", "Inferred: ceramide enrichment, together with a concurrent sterol/neutral-lipid remodelling program (SREBF1 +4.67, SCD +4.17, DHCR24 +3.69, SOAT1 +1.25, DGAT1 +1.72, LDLR +1.50, ABCA7 +2.14), stiffens and reorganises limiting-membrane microdomains of the late endosome.", "Inferred localization/routing change: such membranes favour RAB7/ESCRT-dependent inward budding and retention over retromer-mediated recycling and terminal degradation, consistent with the coordinated rise of RAB7A (+2.65), CHMP4B (+3.82), VPS26A (+4.86), SNX3 (+3.95), VAMP3 (+2.99), VPS18 (+1.41).", "Inferred consequence: incomplete lipid clearance sustains the lysosomal program (feed-forward) and a low-grade secretory/inflammatory tone (CXCL8 +3.11, CCL2 +2.12, IL18 +1.46, NLRP3 +1.09) despite loss of the homeostatic protease CTSS (-5.57)."], "title": "Ceramide-disposal bottleneck downstream of an amplified lysosomal sphingolipid-hydrolysis program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23883063176162167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04077719309477147, "cosine_similarity": 0.08302647386247726, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_098", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6694692556634305, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23883063176162167, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.04077719309477147, "cosine_similarity": 0.08302647386247726, "direction_accuracy": 0.19093851132686085, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6694692556634305, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.96220925, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 430}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_150", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all set-level statements were therefore tested by permutation against the same selected list, and absence of a gene (e.g. any PEX gene, CAT, SOD1, SOD2, G6PD, TXNRD1, GSR) means not reported, not unchanged.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and effects range to +15.5, so effects are treated as ordered directional magnitudes only and are not converted to fold changes or compared quantitatively with the log2 protein spots.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, with unknown gain, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes; enzyme activity, metabolite fluxes, NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios, ROS levels and subcellular localisation are all inferred and none is measured here.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes; spot-level changes are treated as weak, non-identifying corroboration only.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcript differences may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect microglia-astrocyte cross-talk rather than APOE4-intrinsic biology.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values cannot be independently assessed and no causal direction is claimed."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcript increase in nuclear-encoded ETC/TCA components (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1) and in thiol-peroxidase/glutathione-system genes (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA), together with a decrease in pentose-phosphate and NAD(P) supply transcripts (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT). We hypothesise that this configuration increases peroxide-detoxification demand (which consumes NADPH) while reducing cytosolic NADPH-regenerating capacity, so cytosolic NADPH resupply, not antioxidant enzyme abundance, is the rate-limiting step that keeps APOE4 microglia in a chronically strained but basally compensated redox state, with the DELE1/CHOP stress relay (gene:DELE1, gene:DDIT3) engaged. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are steady-state abundances, not fluxes.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic blockade of the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway (G6PDi-1, 6-aminonicotinamide, or G6PD/PGD knockdown) at a dose that is near-neutral in APOE3 should produce a disproportionately large drop in GSH/GSSG and NADPH/NADP+ and a disproportionately large rise in cytosolic roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation in APOE4 microglia. If APOE4 and APOE3 respond equally, or APOE4 is more resistant, the NADPH-supply bottleneck is falsified.", "Direct state test: APOE4 microglia under mock conditions should show a lower cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ ratio and a more oxidised cytosolic thiol redox potential than isogenic APOE3, despite equal or higher peroxiredoxin/GPX4 protein. Equal or higher APOE4 NADPH/NADP+ would weaken the mechanism.", "Flux test: 13C-1,2-glucose tracing should show lower fractional oxidative-PPP flux in APOE4, while Seahorse should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption; higher PPP flux in APOE4, or no respiratory difference, would contradict steps 1 and 3.", "Source test: suppressing complex I reverse-electron-transport ROS (S1QEL1.1) or targeting catalase/peroxidase to mitochondria (mitoCAT, MitoTEMPO) should normalise DELE1/DDIT3 transcript levels and the peroxiredoxin transcript program in APOE4 more than in APOE3; no genotype-selective normalisation would argue that the antioxidant transcript increase is not driven by mitochondrial peroxide.", "Compensation test: NNT knockdown should be selectively deleterious (greater peroxide sensitivity, greater loss of viability) in APOE4 versus APOE3; equal sensitivity would refute the proposed matrix-biased compensation in step 4.", "Negative prediction that rejects the assigned peroxisomal focus: peroxisome number, catalase activity and plasmalogen or very-long-chain fatty-acid levels should not differ substantially between genotypes; a clear peroxisomal biogenesis or beta-oxidation defect would indicate an alternative mechanism to the one proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_150", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for 38/38 detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunits are higher in APOE4 (mean effect +2.81, minimum +1.03; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME) and six detected TCA genes are higher (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1). Inferred (not measured): greater assembled respiratory-chain content and electron flux, and therefore a higher rate of superoxide/H2O2 generation per cell; no mitochondrial membrane potential, oxygen consumption or ROS measurement is supplied.", "Inferred consequence: increased matrix and cytosolic peroxide load must be cleared by the thiol-peroxidase systems; measured transcript increases in gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:GSS and gene:MSRA are read as a demand-driven adaptive response rather than as proof of increased scavenging flux.", "Bottleneck (inferred activity from measured abundance): peroxiredoxin/glutathione-peroxidase turnover requires NADPH via thioredoxin reductase and glutathione reductase, but the cytosolic NADPH-regenerating and NAD(P)-synthesising transcripts are lower in APOE4 (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14, gene:NAMPT -2.62). We propose reduced oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate flux and a smaller cytosolic NADP(H) pool, so reductant resupply, not peroxidase protein level, limits peroxide clearance.", "Partial compensation shifted to the matrix: gene:NNT, gene:GLUD1, gene:SHMT1 and gene:SHMT2 transcripts are higher, consistent with a mitochondrially biased NADPH supply that leaves the cytosolic thiol pool least buffered; this compartment assignment is inferred, since no compartment-resolved NADPH or glutathione redox measurement is supplied.", "Downstream readout: the mitochondrial-stress relay and integrated stress response markers gene:DELE1 (+4.82) and gene:DDIT3 (+2.79), with gene:HSPA9 (+2.35), are elevated, consistent with persistent mitochondrial/oxidative strain rather than with an acute inflammatory program (gene:CCL4 and gene:RELB are lower; interferon genes are absent from the list).", "Membrane-lipid arm: the strain is buffered by remodelling rather than by ferroptotic execution - gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:SREBF1 (+4.67) and gene:GPX4 (+2.79) are higher while the peroxidation-substrate genes gene:ACSL4 (-2.14) and gene:ALOX15 (-3.63) are lower, and the lysosomal/lipid-catabolic program (gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB) is higher, predicting that APOE4 microglia are basally compensated but sensitised to any additional NADPH drain.", "Protein-level, ambiguous corroboration: protein_spot:077 (candidate list includes PRDX2) and protein_spot:017 (candidate list includes CAT) are increased and reported significant; these spots contain several candidate genes each and cannot be assigned to a unique protein."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial electron-transport and thiol-peroxidase transcript programs while lowering pentose-phosphate NADPH-regeneration transcripts, making cytosolic NADPH resupply the redox bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.252704648672599, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05330054473269614, "cosine_similarity": 0.07711443871949414, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_150", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6737346278317152, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.252704648672599, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05330054473269614, "cosine_similarity": 0.07711443871949414, "direction_accuracy": 0.22006472491909385, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6737346278317152, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.91924075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 431}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_060", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; relative comparisons between gene sets and the filtered background are therefore used, and absolute fold-change magnitudes are not interpreted.", "Transcript abundance changes for SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1 and the carrier/TCA genes are assumed to translate into proportionate enzyme and transport activity; none of these activities, metabolite pools, acyl-chain compositions or lipid droplets were measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and protein_spot:077 (candidates including PRDX2 and several keratins) are treated as ambiguous and non-decisive, and the ANXA1/TALDO1 spot train (e.g. protein_spot:045) is not used to infer TALDO1 protein direction.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 at one timepoint in astrocyte co-culture, so astrocyte-derived lipid supply and genotype-of-astrocyte effects are assumed constant across arms.", "Replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so gene-level significance is taken at face value and no independent variance estimate was possible."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coherent transcriptional up-shift of mitochondrial carbon-handling and citrate/malate export machinery together with lipoprotein-lipid uptake and an SREBP1-driven desaturation/esterification program and a TFEB-type lysosomal program; we hypothesise that monounsaturated fatty-acyl supply through SCD is the rate-controlling step that converts this excess acetyl-CoA and imported sterol/fatty-acid load into stored, esterified neutral lipid instead of oxidation or export, and that the modest antioxidant/peroxiredoxin changes are an adaptive consequence of handling this lipid load, not the primary lesion. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (or SCD knockdown) in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content and cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol mass substantially more than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, shift the acyl profile toward saturated species, and raise saturated-lipid ER-stress markers. If SCD inhibition lowers droplets equally in both genotypes, or fails to lower them in APOE4, the proposed SCD bottleneck is wrong.", "Isotope-flux test of the upstream arm: 13C-glucose or 13C-glutamine tracing should show greater label incorporation into palmitate/oleate and into cholesterol in APOE4 than APOE3, and this excess should be suppressed by citrate-carrier (SLC25A1) or ACLY inhibition. Equal or lower de novo lipogenic labelling in APOE4 would weaken steps 1-3.", "Esterification-versus-supply discrimination: SOAT1 or DGAT1 inhibition should redistribute lipid from esterified droplets to free sterol/free fatty acid and increase lipotoxic ER-stress readouts in APOE4 without reducing total lipid uptake; if instead total lipid content falls with no change in free-lipid stress markers, the storage-sink interpretation of step 4 is wrong.", "Redox-focus rejection test: APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should not differ substantially in steady-state cytoplasmic H2O2, protein carbonyls or catalase activity under mock conditions, and catalase overexpression or N-acetylcysteine should not normalise the lipid phenotype. Clear baseline oxidative damage in APOE4, or full lipid rescue by antioxidant treatment, would refute the claim that redox change is downstream and would favour an oxidative-stress-primary mechanism.", "Peroxisome test: peroxisomal beta-oxidation capacity (C26:0 breakdown, very-long-chain fatty-acid levels) should be at most modestly changed and should not correlate with droplet burden; a strong APOE4 peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect that explains droplet accumulation would refute the mechanism as formulated.", "Lysosome-direction test: lysosomal hydrolase activity per cell (CTSB, GBA, GAA) should be equal or higher in APOE4, consistent with compensatory TFEB-type induction; if activity is lower despite higher transcripts, the mechanism must be revised toward a primary lysosomal degradation block."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript abundance for mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA and inner-membrane carrier components (gene:MPC2, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1) and for OXPHOS subunits (gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5MC3). We infer, but do not measure, an increased capacity for citrate/malate export and cytosolic acetyl-CoA generation (gene:ACSS2 provides an additional acetate-derived route).", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the lipogenic transcription programme is engaged (gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1) in parallel with sterol-pathway and uptake transcripts (gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36), so cytosolic acetyl-CoA and imported lipoprotein lipid arrive together in the ER.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred flux): SCD-dependent desaturation (gene:SCD, supported by gene:FADS1 and gene:LPCAT1) gates conversion of the saturated acyl-CoA pool into monounsaturated acyl-CoA. This step is proposed to be rate-controlling because it is required both to relieve saturated-lipid ER stress and to supply the preferred substrates for esterification.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred localization/product): monounsaturated acyl-CoA is consumed by esterifying enzymes (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) to make triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester, which we predict accumulate as cytoplasmic lipid droplets; no lipid-droplet or lipid-species measurement is supplied, so droplet content is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred organelle state): a lysosomal/autophagolysosomal expansion programme is co-induced (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:ATP6V1A; ambiguous protein support at protein_spot:027 and protein_spot:053, whose candidate lists include CTSD), consistent with attempted degradative clearance of the accumulating lipid load rather than with a hydrolase deficit.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred redox consequence): peroxide-detoxifying and lipid-peroxidation-limiting transcripts rise (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4) while the polyunsaturated-acyl activating enzyme falls (gene:ACSL4) and cytosolic NADPH-generating pentose-phosphate transcripts fall (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD). We interpret this as a buffered, monounsaturated-biased lipid state with constrained cytosolic reducing power, not as evidence of frank oxidative damage."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route mitochondrial-derived carbon through an SREBP1/SCD desaturation bottleneck into esterified neutral lipid, with antioxidant genes as a downstream buffer rather than the driver"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15507883173946757, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10122099574646236, "cosine_similarity": 0.07664618038912131, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6729967637540453, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.15507883173946757, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10122099574646236, "cosine_similarity": 0.07664618038912131, "direction_accuracy": 0.1715210355987055, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6729967637540453, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4940755, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 432}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive); program directionality was judged against that 77.1% positive background, not against 50/50. Genes are not independent, so the coherence reported is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified ('reported log fold change'); effects are used on their reported scale only, and no absolute fold-change is claimed. Protein spots are log2.", "Missing rows (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, PLIN2, HMGCR, SQLE, PSAP, GRN, LPCAT3, MBOAT7) are unknown, not unchanged; the routing claim therefore does not rest on measured suppression of efflux or of any specific hydrolase.", "Transcript abundance is treated as capacity, not activity or flux. No lipid species, esterification rate, lysosomal pH, hydrolase activity, membrane composition or organelle localization was measured; the 'routing' step is an inference from the joint transcript pattern.", "All 92 protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities (keratins/actins dominate the candidate lists); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Spots are used only for compatibility/contradiction.", "Astrocyte co-culture means lipid substrate can be supplied in trans; a cell-autonomous APOE4 effect within microglia is assumed but not demonstrated by these data.", "Causality is not established: this is an isogenic association at one timepoint under mock treatment."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single enzymatic bottleneck but by a coordinated lipid-handling cell state: transcripts for lipid acquisition, endolysosomal acidification/hydrolysis, neutral-lipid esterification and Lands-cycle/CDP-choline phospholipid remodeling are jointly elevated, with de novo MUFA synthesis up (SCD) and PUFA-CoA activation down (ACSL4, ACSL5). We propose that internalized and hydrolysed lipid is routed preferentially into esterified storage and into newly remodeled, MUFA-enriched organelle membranes rather than into the ER regulatory sterol pool, so SREBP-1/2 target transcription stays on and feeds forward onto uptake and lipogenesis; this is increased throughput with a storage/biogenesis bias, not a demonstrated degradative block. All statements are about measured RNA/protein-spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity, lipid species and localization were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show higher cholesteryl-ester and triacylglycerol mass and a higher MUFA (16:1/18:1) to PUFA (20:4/22:6) ratio in PC/PE species. If neutral-lipid mass and phospholipid acyl composition are indistinguishable between genotypes, Steps 3 and 5 fail and the mechanism is substantially weakened.", "Prospective and discriminating: SOAT1 inhibition (e.g. avasimibe) with or without DGAT1 inhibition in mock APOE4 microglia should lower SREBP-2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24) and raise the free/ER-accessible cholesterol pool, while leaving v-ATPase and hydrolase transcripts (ATP6V1H, GBA, HEXA, CTSB) largely unchanged. If SREBP-2 targets remain elevated when esterification is blocked, the sterol is trapped upstream of the ER (a lysosomal handling block) and the esterification-routing account is wrong.", "Prospective flux test: pulse-chase of labelled lipoprotein/apoptotic-cell lipid should show equal or faster lysosomal hydrolysis in APOE4 with a larger fraction of label recovered as cholesteryl ester and TAG. Slower hydrolysis with accumulation of undegraded substrate would favour the failed-compensation alternative over increased throughput.", "Prospective challenge (reserve, not ongoing defect): SCD inhibition or arachidonate loading should selectively induce ER-stress markers and reduce viability in APOE4 relative to APOE3, since MUFA supply and reduced ACSL4/ACSL5 are proposed to buffer PUFA handling. Equal sensitivity of both genotypes would weaken Step 5.", "Prospective: knockdown of TFEB, or blockade of v-ATPase acidification, should reduce the esterification/lipogenic transcript arm (SOAT1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SREBF1, SCD) if hydrolysis supplies its substrate. Persistence of the lipogenic arm when lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked would show the two arms are independently driven and would break the proposed causal chain between Steps 2 and 3."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (capacity, measured as RNA): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipid/lipoprotein and phagocytic cargo receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:GAS6 +1.33, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:SCARB2 +1.06, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24; 10/10 represented members positive), inferred to raise lipid-cargo internalization capacity.", "Step 2: Cargo is delivered to an expanded degradative compartment. MiT/TFE and endolysosomal transcripts are uniformly up (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.70, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:PIK3C3 +2.92, gene:ATG9A, gene:ATG4A, gene:ATG4D, gene:ULK3) together with lipid-directed hydrolases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:MAN2B1 +1.81, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:NPC2 +1.17), inferred to increase hydrolytic capacity that liberates fatty acids and sterol; gene:CTSS -5.57 is the one strong exception.", "Step 3 (routing): Liberated fatty acid and sterol are directed into esterified storage and glycerolipid synthesis rather than back to the ER regulatory sterol pool or to efflux, indicated by gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT4 +1.12 with active turnover (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04); gene:GPAT3 -2.23 is the exception, and no efflux transporter (ABCA1/ABCG1) row was supplied, so efflux is unknown rather than unchanged.", "Step 4 (feed-forward): Because the ER regulatory sterol pool is not repleted, SREBP output remains induced: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:ME1 +1.36 (13/13 positive). This sustains Steps 1 and 3 rather than terminating them.", "Step 5 (acyl-chain and headgroup remodeling): New acyl chains are MUFA-biased (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59) and are inferred to be esterified into phospholipid through Lands-cycle and CDP-choline/ethanolamine routes (gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:CERS4 +2.52, gene:CERS6 +1.06), while PUFA-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases fall (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11). Predicted consequence: APOE4 membranes are shifted toward monounsaturated/saturated species with a lower arachidonate/DHA-containing phospholipid fraction.", "Step 6 (consequence in the measured condition): This lipid supply supports expansion of endolysosomal and mitochondrial membrane, accompanied by a uniformly elevated oxidative/mitochondrial transport program (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24; 44/44 positive) and a modest activation/secretory tone (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:CD74 +3.84, gene:ANXA1 +4.15). The state is compatible with sustained throughput; a rate-limiting defect would only be revealed by a lipid-load or PUFA challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a scavenge-hydrolyse-re-esterify routing state with MUFA-biased phospholipid remodeling that keeps SREBP output switched on"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43247609201344017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.211421522603542, "cosine_similarity": 0.07653595930248869, "direction_accuracy": 0.30097087378640774, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7464563106796116, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.43247609201344017, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.211421522603542, "cosine_similarity": 0.07653595930248869, "direction_accuracy": 0.30097087378640774, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7464563106796116, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.80049175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 101}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_087", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript changes for lipid enzymes are assumed to translate into proportional changes in enzyme protein and catalytic activity; no lipid enzyme abundance or activity is measured in the supplied data.", "No lipid species, lipid-droplet, membrane-order or flux measurement is supplied, so all statements about acyl-chain composition, esterification flux and membrane turnover are inferences, not observations.", "The RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global upward shift (1705/2212 rows positive, median 1.46), so evidence was assessed by within-list percentile rank rather than by sign; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and magnitudes are treated as ordinal only.", "Canonical partners of this pathway (ACLY, FASN, ACACA, ELOVLs, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, ACSL1/3, LIPA, PLIN2, ABCA1, SCAP, HMGCR) are absent from the supplied rows; their absence is treated as untested, not as evidence of no change.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; protein_spot:044/045/046 are interpreted as consistent with, but not proof of, increased ANXA1, because the co-candidate TALDO1 transcript is decreased (gene:TALDO1).", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 but the microglia are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects transmitted through astrocyte-derived lipoproteins cannot be separated from microglia-autonomous effects; replicate number is not supplied.", "Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is a directional hypothesis consistent with the observed associations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia express a coordinated SREBF1/SCD-linked esterification program (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, CHPT1) together with elevated scavenger/lysosomal lipid-hydrolase transcripts (SCARB1, GBA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, TFEB) and reduced PUFA-activation transcripts (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3, ALOX15), so that Delta-9 desaturation by SCD is proposed to be the rate-limiting node that converts internalized and lysosomally liberated fatty acids into monounsaturated di-/tri-acylglycerol and phosphatidylcholine species; the predicted consequence is a MUFA-enriched, arachidonate-poor membrane and lipid-droplet pool with increased membrane turnover capacity, not yet measured in this dataset.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) triacylglycerol and phosphatidylcholine species and a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio with reduced 20:4-containing PE/PI, plus higher neutral-lipid (BODIPY 493/503) content; an unchanged or PUFA-shifted phospholipid profile would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) at matched exposure should produce a genotype-by-drug interaction, collapsing the MUFA-TAG/PC excess and inducing ER stress or viability loss preferentially in APOE4; if APOE4 and APOE3 respond identically, SCD-gated MUFA supply is not the bottleneck and the mechanism fails.", "Stable-isotope tracing (U-13C-glucose or 13C-acetate) should show greater label incorporation into 18:1 and into TAG/PC in APOE4 than APOE3, and this excess should be blunted by SLC25A1 or ACLY inhibition; equal de novo labelling between genotypes would weaken the carbon-supply step.", "Restoring ACSL4 expression in APOE4 microglia should increase arachidonate-containing phospholipids and sensitivity to GPX4 inhibition, while ACSL4 knockdown in APOE3 should partially phenocopy the APOE4 lipid profile; no change in AA-phospholipids after ACSL4 manipulation would refute the PUFA-arm step.", "Blocking lysosomal substrate supply (lysosomal acid lipase or SCARB1 inhibition, or reducing astrocyte lipoprotein supply in monoculture) should reduce the APOE4-specific SCD and AGPAT2/DGAT1 transcript elevation; persistence of the lipogenic program under substrate restriction would indicate a cell-autonomous SREBP driver rather than the proposed catabolism-to-esterification coupling.", "Competing-model test: if respirometry shows the dominant APOE4 phenotype is increased OXPHOS capacity (consistent with the strongly ranked nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcripts) while SCD inhibition leaves lipid content and membrane order unchanged, the mitochondrial-biogenesis alternative should be preferred over this lipid-bottleneck mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mechanism_steps": ["Increased transcripts for lipid uptake and lysosomal catabolism (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA, gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB) are inferred to raise endolysosomal delivery and hydrolysis of lipoprotein-, membrane- and debris-derived lipid, liberating free fatty acids, sterols and sphingoid backbones into the cytosolic pool (flux inferred; no lipid or hydrolase-activity measurement is supplied).", "Elevated TCA/carrier transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A11) plus gene:ACSS2 are inferred to sustain cytosolic acetyl-CoA and NAD(P)H supply for de novo lipogenesis; the ACLY step itself is not present in the supplied rows and is assumed, not observed.", "Elevated gene:SREBF1 with the highest-ranking desaturase transcript gene:SCD is proposed to make Delta-9 desaturation the bottleneck step that sets the oleoyl/palmitoleoyl-CoA pool available for esterification; SCD protein and enzymatic activity were not measured.", "Downstream acyl-transfer and headgroup transcripts (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:MGLL, gene:TAZ) provide capacity to esterify that MUFA-CoA pool into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester stores and into Lands-cycle remodeling of phosphatidylcholine and phosphatidylethanolamine.", "Concurrently decreased gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3 and gene:ALOX15, with increased gene:GPX4, are inferred to lower activation and re-esterification of arachidonate-type PUFA into phospholipids, biasing the remodeled pool toward monounsaturated acyl chains and lowering peroxidizable substrate.", "The resulting inferred MUFA-rich, PUFA-poor membrane and droplet pool, together with increased phospholipid-binding and flippase-related transcripts (gene:ANXA1, gene:TMEM30A) and concordantly increased ANXA1-containing protein spots (protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046), is proposed to change membrane order, surface repair and phagocytic membrane turnover in APOE4 relative to APOE3 microglia."], "title": "SCD-gated monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply reroutes lysosome-derived lipid into MUFA-rich glycerolipids and away from PUFA remodeling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32586862607539785, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1423450169508767, "cosine_similarity": 0.0758538462861758, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6759223300970875, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32586862607539785, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1423450169508767, "cosine_similarity": 0.0758538462861758, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6759223300970875, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.19362425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 433}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_110", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with |effect| \u003e 1 in an unspecified logarithm base; magnitudes are treated as ordinal evidence of direction and coherence, not as calibrated fold changes, and the absence of a gene (e.g. CAT, SOD1, SOD2, NFE2L2, G6PD, TFAM, MDH2, GOT2) is uninformative rather than evidence of no change.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy for the capacity of a pathway; enzyme activity, metabolic flux, complex assembly state, submitochondrial localisation and ROS levels were not measured in this dataset and are stated as inferences.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features: protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5), protein_spot:077 (candidates KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB) and protein_spot:042 (candidates BLVRA, NCF4, ACTB, PTER, PRPF19) are consistent with, but do not uniquely identify, an antioxidant protein; they are treated as weak corroboration only.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels measured by probe-based single-cell chemistry in an astrocyte co-culture are assumed to reflect microglial mitochondrial transcript content rather than dissociation stress, ambient RNA, or probe-panel artefacts; mtDNA copy number was not measured.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are assumed truly isogenic and the comparison confounder-free apart from genotype; only one comparison (mock, day 30) is supplied, so no time course or dose response constrains the model.", "The coordinated up-shift is interpreted against the strong global positive bias of the supplied rows (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46); only sets that beat this background by permutation are treated as coherent."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia up-scale nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain subunits and matrix substrate-delivery carriers while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are relatively lower; we hypothesise that this stoichiometric mismatch leaves complexes I/III/IV assembly-limited, so the increased NADH input is disposed of inefficiently, raising matrix peroxide production (inferred, not measured) and shifting the cell onto an NNT/peroxiredoxin-3-dependent matrix NADPH buffer at a time when cytosolic pentose-phosphate and NAD-salvage transcripts are lower. The primary bottleneck is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits relative to the up-scaled nuclear program; matrix NADPH-dependent peroxide clearance is the downstream vulnerability. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is explicitly NOT proposed as the driver: the peroxisomal evidence in these data is sparse and internally inconsistent (ABCD1 lower, no catalase transcript row).", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Live redox imaging of matrix H2O2 (mito-roGFP2-Orp1 or MitoPY1) plus a PRDX3 redox-shift immunoblot in mock isogenic microglia should show a higher oxidised fraction in APOE4 than APOE3. If matrix H2O2 and PRDX3 oxidation are indistinguishable between genotypes, the central inferred electron-leak step is wrong and the mechanism is weakened.", "Blue-native PAGE / complexome or in-gel complex I and IV activity should show that assembled complex I/III/IV per unit nuclear-encoded subunit protein is LOWER in APOE4, with accumulation of assembly intermediates. If assembled complexes scale up in proportion to the elevated nuclear subunit transcripts, the mito-nuclear stoichiometry bottleneck is refuted and the observed OXPHOS up-shift should instead be read as a straightforward increase in respiratory capacity.", "Discriminating perturbation: limiting matrix reducing input with the MPC inhibitor UK5099 or the malate-aspartate shuttle inhibitor aminooxyacetate should shrink the APOE4-minus-APOE3 matrix H2O2 gap and reduce PRDX3 hyperoxidation within hours, without normalising the lysosomal transcript program (CTSK, GAA, GBA). If matrix peroxide in APOE4 is unchanged or increases under MPC/AOA block, the 'excess reducing equivalents into an assembly-limited chain' step fails.", "NNT knockdown (or NNT inhibition) should disproportionately raise matrix peroxide, PRDX3 oxidation and death in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia; an equal effect in both genotypes would falsify the claim that matrix NADPH is the limiting buffer in APOE4.", "Compartment-discriminating antioxidant rescue: mitochondria-targeted catalase or mitoTEMPO should normalise APOE4 phenotypes (matrix peroxide, ISR markers) whereas peroxisome-targeted catalase overexpression should not. If peroxisomal catalase rescues equally well, a peroxisomal-oxidase mechanism is the better explanation and this hypothesis should be discarded.", "Because ABCD1 transcript is lower and no catalase transcript row is present, the model predicts NO increase in peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux in APOE4 (C26:0 to C22:0 ratio unchanged or increased, i.e. reduced peroxisomal handling). Observing increased peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux with elevated catalase protein would support the rejected peroxisomal alternative instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_110", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: APOE4 microglia show coordinately higher nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts (38/38 matched rows positive, mean +2.80 in the reported log units) together with higher matrix substrate-delivery transcripts (pyruvate carrier MPC2, malate-aspartate shuttle components MDH1/GOT1/SLC25A11, citrate carrier SLC25A1, adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5, TCA/NADH-generating OGDH, DLD, ACO2, IDH3B/IDH3G, and glutamate anaplerosis GLUD1/GLS).", "Measured RNA counter-directional node: mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts run against this program (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 lower; MT-ND4L, MT-ND5 higher), while mitochondrial translation-elongation and carrier transcripts (TUFM, SLC25 family) are higher; we infer, but did not measure, that assembled complex I/III/IV holoenzyme abundance does not scale with the nuclear subunit increase.", "Inferred flux: an assembly-limited chain receiving increased NADH/FADH2 input keeps the CoQ pool and complex-I flavin/IQ sites more reduced, which raises the probability of single-electron transfer to O2 (superoxide, dismutated to matrix H2O2). Neither electron leak, membrane potential, nor ROS was measured here.", "Inferred compensation, measured only as RNA: matrix and lipid-peroxide clearance capacity is up-scaled (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS, TXNDC17, MSRA) and the mild-uncoupling relief valve UCP2 is higher; all of these consume NADPH or thiol reducing power per catalytic cycle.", "Inferred bottleneck on reductant supply: NNT (matrix NADH-\u003eNADPH transhydrogenase) and the mitochondrial NAD carrier SLC25A51 are higher while the cytosolic pentose-phosphate arm (PGD, TALDO1) and NAD salvage (NAMPT) are lower, so peroxide clearance is predicted to depend disproportionately on matrix NNT-derived NADPH and to be fragile when protonmotive force or NAD pools fall.", "Inferred sensitisation and output: higher mitochondrial iron import (SLC25A37) with higher ferritin-heavy-chain transcript (FTH1) makes any matrix peroxide more damaging, and the mitochondrial stress relay/ISR transcripts DELE1 and DDIT3 are higher, consistent with a chronic, unresolved low-grade oxidative state rather than an acute, resolving one. Causality and direction (APOE4 genotype -\u003e this state) are not established by these correlative data."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometry mismatch in APOE4 microglia creates an assembly-limited respiratory chain whose electron leak is buffered by an NNT/PRDX3-dependent matrix NADPH pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.016634050880626222, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.015895009349160442, "cosine_similarity": 0.07526916962398682, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_110", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6396440129449839, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.016634050880626222, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.015895009349160442, "cosine_similarity": 0.07526916962398682, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6396440129449839, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0042875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 434}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_090", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong global upward shift (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77.1% positive, median +1.46); we therefore judge pathways only by rank/position relative to this list, not by raw fold-change magnitude, and assume the ranking is not itself created by a compositional normalisation artefact.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least monotonically, the abundance of the corresponding enzyme; no enzyme activity, respiration, membrane potential, metabolite, ROS or flux measurement is supplied, so every flux, localisation and coupling statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "Protein spots have 2-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin/ANXA1 candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level direction is used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence.", "The observed mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 down; MT-ND5 up) are assumed to be unreliable in a probe-based 10X Flex assay, so no mito-nuclear stoichiometry claim is made.", "The two genotypes are assumed to be at a comparable differentiation state; the astrocyte co-culture is assumed not to be the source of the mitochondrial/lysosomal signal.", "Biological replicate number is 'not supplied in workbook', so the reported p-values cannot be independently weighted."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) show a coordinated transcript increase in the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase program and in nuclear-encoded TCA-cycle, mitochondrial-carrier/import and electron-transport-chain genes, while glycolytic rate-limiting transcripts are not co-induced (HK2 and PFKP decrease). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is mitochondrial pyruvate/NADH oxidation entry (MPC2 -\u003e TCA -\u003e complex I): APOE4 cells route an increased lysosomal catabolic load into mitochondrial oxidation and therefore depend disproportionately on this node for ATP and for the proton gradient that supports lysosomal acidification. The concurrent, comparatively modest induction of peroxiredoxin/GPX4/NNT transcripts is interpreted as buffering that scales with the oxidative shift, so unbuffered oxidative stress and peroxisomal beta-oxidation failure are rejected as the primary bottleneck. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, membrane potential, complex assembly, ROS and metabolite pools were not, and no causal direction is established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or sub-lethal complex I inhibition (piericidin A/rotenone) in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should produce a significantly larger genotype-specific drop in total ATP, in LysoSensor/LysoTracker-reported lysosomal acidification and in bead/myelin uptake-and-degradation in APOE4. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive than APOE3 on all three readouts, the proposed MPC2-TCA-complex I bottleneck is wrong.", "Capacity prediction: Seahorse respirometry should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a higher OXPHOS-derived ATP fraction in APOE4, with no increase in glycolytic capacity or reserve; equal OCR between genotypes, or a matched rise in ECAR/glycolytic capacity, would falsify the interpretation of the ETC/TCA transcript increase as expanded oxidative capacity and remove the 'no glycolytic compensation' premise.", "Redox discriminator (tests the assigned focus): MitoSOX/roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation, 4-HNE and protein-carbonyl levels should be at most modestly elevated in APOE4, and chronic N-acetylcysteine or MitoQ should NOT normalise the lysosomal or TCA/ETC transcript program. If antioxidant treatment collapses these programs, or if lipid peroxidation is grossly elevated, the primary bottleneck is oxidative stress rather than oxidative-flux dependence, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Coupling test: TFEB knockdown (or v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1) in APOE4 microglia should reduce not only the lysosomal transcripts but also the elevation of MPC2/OGDH/MDH1 and the nuclear-encoded ETC transcripts and lower maximal respiration; persistence of the full mitochondrial signature after lysosomal blockade would falsify mechanism step 2/5 while leaving steps 3-4 intact.", "Protein-level check: BN-PAGE/in-gel activity or immunoblot for NDUFB8, UQCRC2 and ATP5F1A should show higher assembled complex levels in APOE4. If the large nuclear transcript increase is not accompanied by any increase in complex protein or activity, the mechanism reduces to an unrealised transcriptional program and must be rewritten as an mtDNA-encoded-subunit or assembly limitation.", "Peroxisome negative control: peroxisome number (PMP70/catalase immunofluorescence), catalase activity and C26:0 very-long-chain fatty-acid levels should not differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 at this timepoint. A clear VLCFA accumulation with reduced peroxisomal beta-oxidation would revive the rejected peroxisomal mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lysosomal hydrolases and the v-ATPase (GAA, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, ATP6V1A, ATP6V1H) together with the lysosomal-biogenesis transcription factor TFEB, consistent with an expanded degradative compartment; the size of the lysosomal compartment, its acidification and its substrate load are inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): the products of this expanded catabolism (amino acids, sugars, fatty-acid- and sterol-derived acetyl units) are proposed to be delivered to mitochondria rather than exported, generating an increased demand for acetyl-CoA/NADH oxidation.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): the mitochondrial import/carrier machinery and the entire measured oxidative core are coordinately higher in APOE4 - pyruvate carrier MPC2, TCA enzymes (OGDH, MDH1, DLD, ACO2, IDH3G, IDH3B, GOT1, PDP1), carriers/translocases (SLC25A46, SLC25A1, TOMM22, TIMM44) and 38/38 measured nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8, ATP5ME, UQCRC2, COX7A2, SDHB). This is interpreted as an increase in oxidative capacity; assembled complex amounts, membrane potential and respiration were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured abundance, contrast): the glycolytic branch is not coordinately induced - the rate-limiting HK2 and PFKP transcripts are lower in APOE4 while only transporters/downstream enzymes (SLC2A1) rise - so we infer little compensatory capacity to make ATP without oxygen; this makes MPC2/TCA/complex I flux the proposed bottleneck rather than a redundant pathway.", "Step 5 (inferred coupling): mitochondrially generated ATP is required to run the v-ATPase; we therefore predict a feedback in which blocking the pyruvate/NADH oxidation node in APOE4 cells degrades lysosomal acidification and clearance more than in APOE3 cells, i.e. the two measured programs are functionally coupled rather than independently regulated.", "Step 6 (redox, secondary and explicitly demoted): mitochondrial and cytosolic thiol/lipid peroxide buffering transcripts (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, NNT, GSS, FTH1) are higher in APOE4 but are not enriched above the strong global upward shift of this selected DE list (Mann-Whitney p = 0.18), and the peroxisomal arm is unsupported (no PEX transcript in the list; ABCD1 decreased; ACOX1 only +1.2, below the list median). We therefore place matched redox buffering downstream of the oxidative shift and predict that oxidative damage is compensated at this timepoint, not causal."], "title": "APOE4 microglia become dependent on a lysosome-fed mitochondrial pyruvate/NADH oxidation node (MPC2-TCA-complex I) without compensatory glycolytic induction; redox buffering scales with, rather than fails ahead of, this shift"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.051160405601932184, "cosine_similarity": 0.07444294550470941, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6432265372168285, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06947162426614481, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.051160405601932184, "cosine_similarity": 0.07444294550470941, "direction_accuracy": 0.11650485436893204, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6432265372168285, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.714724, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 435}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_097", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; effect sizes are treated as ordinal and are compared against that 77%-positive selected background, not a 50/50 expectation. Genes absent from the list (e.g. LPCAT3, MBOAT7, PLA2G6, PNPLA2, LIPA, PLIN2, ACLY, FASN) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript increases are read as changes in enzyme/transporter capacity, not as demonstrated activity or flux; the decreases in ACSL4/ACSL5/GPAT3 are read as a change in acyl-CoA specification, not as a proven rate-limiting defect.", "SREBP activation is inferred from coordinate target-gene abundance; SREBP proteolytic processing, nuclear SREBP, SCAP/INSIG state and ER-accessible cholesterol were not measured.", "Lipid localization (lysosomal vs ER vs droplet sterol and acyl pools) is inferred, never observed; no lipidomic or imaging measurement is in the supplied data.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate identities each with frequent keratin/actin contamination; all candidate identities are retained and no spot is treated as confirmation of an individual protein. The spot panel contains no lipid-synthetic enzyme and no OXPHOS subunit among candidates, so it can only test compatibility, not confirm steps 3-5.", "Effects were measured in astrocyte co-culture at day 30 under mock treatment; observed differences are steady-state genotype differences and any claim about reduced reserve applies only to a future challenge, not to the measured condition.", "Program-level coherence is descriptive; member genes are co-regulated and non-independent, so no formal enrichment claim is made."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 shifts cells into a high-turnover lipid-routing state rather than an acute degradative bottleneck: transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and lysosomal lipid hydrolysis are coordinately higher while ER lipid-sensor output stays 'low' (SREBF1/SREBF2 and their sterol- and fatty-acid-synthesis targets are all higher), and the represented acylation machinery is biased toward monounsaturated/saturated re-esterification (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, CHPT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2 up; PUFA-preferring ACSL4 and ACSL5 down). The predicted consequence in the measured condition is a re-routed steady-state lipidome (higher MUFA:PUFA in glycerophospholipids, more neutral-lipid/droplet re-esterification, lysosome-retained sterol) supported by parallel expansion of mitochondrial oxidative and peroxide-defence capacity, with reduced spare capacity that a lipid challenge would expose. Measured values are transcript/spot abundances; flux, SREBP processing and lipid localization were not measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PROSPECTIVE lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a raised MUFA:PUFA ratio in glycerophospholipids (higher 16:1/18:1-containing PC/PE and higher TAG/CE) with lower 20:4- and 22:6-containing phospholipid species, even if total phospholipid is unchanged. If APOE4 shows equal or higher PUFA-phospholipid fraction, the acyl-chain-routing step (steps 3-4) is falsified.", "PROSPECTIVE SCD inhibition (or restored ACSL4 expression) in APOE4 microglia should collapse most of the genotype difference in phospholipid/TAG MUFA:PUFA composition; if the genotype lipid difference persists unchanged under SCD inhibition, the SREBP1-\u003eMUFA arm is not the primary driver.", "PROSPECTIVE sterol-sensing test: acute cholesterol or 25-hydroxycholesterol loading should suppress SREBP2 target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, DHCR7, INSIG1) less completely in APOE4 than APOE3, and ER-accessible cholesterol (ALOD4/perfringolysin probe) should be lower in APOE4 despite equal or greater total/lysosomal cholesterol. Equal suppression plus equal or higher ER-accessible cholesterol falsifies step 2.", "PROSPECTIVE discrimination of adaptation vs failed compensation: under mock conditions, degradation of a pulsed fluorescent lipid cargo (BODIPY-myelin or labelled apoptotic-cell membrane) should NOT be slower in APOE4 (adaptation/increased throughput), whereas the failed-compensation alternative predicts slower baseline clearance and cargo accumulation. Slower baseline degradation with accumulating undegraded cargo in mock APOE4 would favour the bottleneck alternative over this mechanism.", "PROSPECTIVE flux test: 13C-acetate or D2O labelling should show higher fractional synthesis and higher turnover (label incorporation and loss) of PC/PE MUFA species in APOE4 with no increase in complete fatty-acid oxidation to CO2 relative to synthesis. Equal labelling kinetics in both genotypes, or higher oxidation with unchanged re-esterification, would weaken the high-turnover re-acylation claim.", "PROSPECTIVE challenge-only prediction: myelin-debris or oxLDL loading should reveal reduced reserve in APOE4 (greater droplet/lysosomal lipid accumulation and impaired resolution) even though the mock condition shows no degradative failure; if APOE4 handles the load as well as APOE3, the reserve claim is falsified without falsifying steps 1-4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (capacity for lipid delivery/hydrolysis is higher): APOE4 microglia show coordinately higher transcripts for lipoprotein and lipid uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:MRC1, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7) and for the endolysosomal degradative system (gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NPC2, gene:LAMP1). This is inferred capacity, not measured uptake or hydrolytic flux.", "Step 2 (ER lipid sensing still reads 'low'): despite that uptake/hydrolysis capacity, gene:SREBF1 (+4.67), gene:SREBF2 and canonical SREBP targets (gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1) are all higher. Sterol delivery to the ER would be expected to suppress this arm, so liberated sterol/lipid is inferred (not observed) to be retained in lysosomal/droplet pools away from ER sensors, keeping SREBP output high.", "Step 3 (acyl-CoA entry is re-specified, not simply increased): sustained SREBP1 output raises de novo MUFA supply (gene:SCD +4.17) and the glycerolipid acylation/head-group machinery (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2), while the long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases gene:ACSL4 (-2.14, PUFA/arachidonate-preferring) and gene:ACSL5 (-3.11) and gene:GPAT3 (-2.23) fall.", "Step 4 (Lands-cycle remodeling is biased toward MUFA/saturate re-acylation): the represented deacylation/lipolysis routes (gene:PLA2G7, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5) run against re-acylation enzymes that are the MUFA/saturate-preferring ones (gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26); PUFA-preferring LPCAT3/MBOAT7 are absent from the supplied list and are unknown, not unchanged. Acyl chains liberated by lysosomal and neutral hydrolysis are therefore predicted to be recycled preferentially into MUFA-rich phospholipid and into TAG/CE (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1) rather than fully oxidized or effluxed.", "Step 5 (energetic and redox support for continuous turnover): mitochondrial oxidative capacity expands coordinately (38/38 represented OXPHOS subunits positive, median +2.64; e.g. gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:COX7A2) with gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) citrate carrier, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, plus peroxide defence (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:FTH1) and lower gene:ALOX15 (-3.63) - a peroxidation-averse, ATP/citrate-supplied configuration compatible with a continuously running acylation-deacylation cycle rather than with collapsing oxidative capacity.", "Step 6 (predicted cell state in the measured condition): a re-routed steady-state lipidome (higher MUFA:PUFA glycerophospholipids, increased neutral-lipid re-esterification, lysosome-retained sterol), a partially lipid-laden/DAM-like surface program (gene:GPNMB, gene:LGALS3, gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A), and membrane-remodeling-associated protein spots that are elevated (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, whose candidate identities include ANXA1 alongside TALDO1 and others). Degradative failure is NOT claimed for the mock condition; reduced reserve would be revealed only by a lipid challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia sustain a SREBP-driven, MUFA-biased glycerolipid re-acylation cycle coupled to expanded lysosomal hydrolase and OXPHOS capacity"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.33073330133293943, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16499023135934535, "cosine_similarity": 0.07398007173329232, "direction_accuracy": 0.3058252427184466, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7354239482200647, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.33073330133293943, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16499023135934535, "cosine_similarity": 0.07398007173329232, "direction_accuracy": 0.3058252427184466, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7354239482200647, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.2078375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 102}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_020", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The selected differential-expression rows are representative of the direction of change for the pathways scored; because 77% of the supplied RNA rows are positive, pathway claims are only made where the set mean exceeds this up-shifted background by permutation test.", "The unspecified-base RNA logarithm is monotone and consistent across all rows, so only relative comparisons between gene sets are used; no absolute fold-change is asserted.", "Relative depletion of mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflects a real mito-nuclear imbalance rather than a probe-panel or library-composition normalisation artefact of the 10X Flex assay.", "Increased transcript abundance for antioxidant, desaturase and esterification enzymes corresponds to increased enzyme capacity; enzyme activity, ROS flux, redox couple ratios, lipid droplet content and lipid peroxidation were not measured.", "Protein spots are mixtures of candidate proteins: spot 017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and spot 077 (candidates PRDX2, KRT1/9/10, RAB1A, ACTB) are treated as consistent-but-ambiguous corroboration only, not as identified catalase or peroxiredoxin-2 measurements.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent cell-composition or maturation differences are not the dominant source of the observed RNA differences."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative program (OXPHOS subunits, TCA enzymes) is transcriptionally raised while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are relatively lowered; we hypothesise that this stoichiometry mismatch is the primary bottleneck, yielding poorly matched respiratory-complex assembly and increased electron leak, so that peroxide/lipid-hydroperoxide buffering capacity (thiol peroxidases, GPX4, selenoproteins, ferritin) becomes limiting and the cells restrict peroxidation-prone acyl pools (ACSL4, ALOX15 down) while diverting fatty acid toward monounsaturated and esterified neutral lipid (SCD, DGAT1, SOAT1, SREBF1 up), producing the lipid-laden, lysosome-loaded APOE4 microglial state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant treatment (MitoQ/SkQ1 or mitochondria-targeted catalase expression) in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplet area (BODIPY 493/503) and C11-BODIPY oxidation toward APOE3 levels while leaving the nuclear/mtDNA transcript ratio essentially unchanged; if droplet content and lipid peroxidation are unchanged by mito-targeted antioxidants, or if a non-targeted antioxidant works equally well, the mitochondrial-leak bottleneck is weakened.", "Blue-native PAGE / western quantification should show a lower ratio of assembled complex I, III, IV and V (and of MT-CO1 protein) to nuclear-encoded subunits (NDUFB8, SDHA, UQCRC2) in APOE4 despite higher nuclear subunit transcripts, with reduced complex I- and complex IV-driven respiration and elevated mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation; equal assembled complex stoichiometry and equal matrix H2O2 would falsify steps 2-3.", "APOE4 microglia should be selectively more sensitive to SCD inhibition (CAY10566) and to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) than isogenic APOE3, showing greater lipid peroxidation and death; equal sensitivity would weaken the claim that peroxide buffering plus MUFA channelling is load-bearing.", "DGAT1 (or DGAT1+SOAT1) inhibition should block lipid droplet accumulation in APOE4 but increase C11-BODIPY lipid peroxidation and ferroptosis sensitivity rather than restore normal function, since storage is proposed to be protective downstream of the bottleneck; if DGAT1 inhibition normalises redox readouts and viability, the direction of causality in steps 5-6 is wrong.", "Rescuing the imbalance (e.g. raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply or lowering nuclear OXPHOS drive) should reduce both the antioxidant transcript program and the SCD/DGAT1 lipid program; if the lipid program persists while mitochondrial redox readouts normalise, an APOE4 lipid-handling defect independent of mitochondrial redox is the better explanation.", "Negative control internal to this hypothesis: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0/C22:0 ratio, catalase activity per peroxisome, PMP70 puncta) should NOT differ appreciably between genotypes; a strong peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect would indicate the assigned peroxisomal mechanism instead of this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred biosynthetic demand): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts - 39/39 detected OXPHOS subunit genes up (mean log FC 2.81 vs list background 1.39, permutation p=2e-4) plus TCA/matrix enzymes (MDH1, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, GOT1) - implying increased demand for respiratory-chain and matrix enzyme synthesis.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred assembly bottleneck): mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are not co-elevated and are mostly lower (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are exceptions), so the supply of catalytic core subunits, not of nuclear accessory subunits, is proposed to limit assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V. Assembled complex levels were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred flux, not measured): Mismatched subunit supply gives a higher fraction of partially assembled or kinetically inefficient complexes, increasing univalent electron leak and matrix/IMS superoxide-to-H2O2 flux; consistent transcriptional stress markers are present (DDIT3 +2.79, EIF2AK3 +1.51) but ROS itself was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred activity): The cell raises thiol-peroxide buffering capacity - PRDX2 +4.41, PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, TXNDC17 +7.10, TXNL1 +4.33, SELENOW +5.47, MSRA +2.64, GPX4 +2.79, and iron sequestration FTH1 +2.53 (set mean 3.23, permutation p=0.013 against the up-shifted background). Elevated transcripts are treated as increased capacity, not as demonstrated flux; MSRB1 (-2.44) is discordant.", "Step 5 (bottleneck consequence, inferred): Because peroxide/lipid-hydroperoxide detoxification remains rate-limiting relative to leak, the cell lowers the peroxidation-prone acyl supply - ACSL4 -2.14 (PUFA-CoA ligase) and ALOX15 -3.63 - and raises desaturation to monounsaturates (SCD +4.17), a composition change predicted to lower membrane PUFA peroxidation susceptibility.", "Step 6 (measured RNA, inferred lipid phenotype): Excess and MUFA-enriched fatty acid and sterol are esterified and stored rather than oxidised - SREBF1 +4.67, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, CIDEB +1.06, LDLR +1.50, CH25H +1.62 - predicting increased neutral-lipid droplet content in APOE4; lipid droplets were not measured here.", "Step 7 (measured RNA, inferred organelle load): Lipid and membrane load is routed to a strongly induced lysosomal/TFEB-linked degradative program (TFEB +2.38, GBA +6.71, SMPD1 +5.63, HEXA +5.68, CTSB +5.52, ATP6V1H +6.88; set mean 2.91, permutation p=9e-4) which we propose is a consequence rather than the initiating lesion, and which does not restore redox balance under mock conditions."], "title": "Mito-nuclear OXPHOS stoichiometry mismatch in APOE4 microglia drives a peroxide-buffering and MUFA/neutral-lipid sequestration program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.31650851087398, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13104637021046517, "cosine_similarity": 0.07391168009478942, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7278705501618123, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.31650851087398, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13104637021046517, "cosine_similarity": 0.07391168009478942, "direction_accuracy": 0.26375404530744334, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7278705501618123, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1608345, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 436}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_031", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects share one unspecified logarithm base and one direction convention (positive = higher in APOE4); because the whole set is shifted positive (median +1.46, 77 percent up), only percentile rank within the supplied distribution is treated as interpretable, not the absolute magnitude.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so set-level statistics describe coherence within the selected genes only and are not unbiased pathway enrichment; absence of ABCA1, ABCG1, NPC1, LIPA, GRN, PSAP and PLIN2 reflects list selection, not measured absence of change.", "Transcript abundance is used as a proxy for the capacity of a step; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH, lysosome number, sterol pools, lipid droplets and metabolic flux were not measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; spots 052 and 053 are treated only as weakly consistent, not as identified cathepsin measurements.", "Effects are assumed to reflect per-cell rewiring in the microglial population rather than a change in the proportion of a foamy/disease-associated subpopulation, or astrocyte ambient RNA from the co-culture; the data cannot distinguish these."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs APOE3) transcriptionally amplify lipoprotein scavenging (gene:SCARB1) together with a coordinated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:TFEB), while the transcripts serving export of lysosomal sterol are not coordinately raised above the strong global positive shift (gene:NPC2 at the 35th percentile of the measured distribution; NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1, ABCG1 not measured). We propose that the limiting step in APOE4 is not luminal hydrolysis but egress of sterol/lipid from the endolysosome to the ER and plasma membrane, so that internalised lipid is retained in an enlarged acidic compartment, ER sterol sensing is not satisfied (mild, not suppressed, SREBP2-target expression: gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1), and non-sterol catabolites are routed to mitochondrial oxidation (gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5F1B) rather than to glycolytic commitment (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP). Causality is not established by these data; the lipid pools themselves were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: treating APOE4 microglia with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin, or overexpressing NPC1/NPC2 (bypassing or restoring lysosomal sterol egress), should reduce lysosomal unesterified cholesterol (filipin) and LysoTracker signal toward APOE3 levels and lower the SREBP2 target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7) without requiring any reduction in hydrolase transcripts (GAA, GBA, CTSB). If cyclodextrin or NPC1/NPC2 restoration leaves the APOE4-APOE3 lipid and lysosomal difference intact, the egress-bottleneck mechanism is wrong.", "Reciprocal test: blocking egress in APOE3 microglia with the NPC1 inhibitor U18666A should phenocopy APOE4, i.e. raise lysosomal sterol load and induce the same hydrolase/v-ATPase/TFEB transcript module. Failure of APOE3 to phenocopy weakens step 3.", "Uptake dependence: SCARB1 knockdown or blockade of lipoprotein uptake should reduce lysosomal lipid load and shrink the APOE4-specific hydrolase program. If SCARB1 loss does not change lysosomal lipid or the hydrolase transcripts, step 1 is wrong.", "Functional direction of the lysosome: APOE4 lysosomes should be equally or more acidic and show equal or higher bulk hydrolase activity per lysosome; if APOE4 lysosomes are less acidic or hydrolase-deficient despite the transcript increase, the mechanism must be replaced by a hydrolysis-failure/compensatory-induction model.", "Metabolic corollary: Seahorse profiling should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with lower glycolytic reserve in APOE4, and this difference should be attenuated by inhibiting lysosomal lipolysis/autophagic substrate supply. Equal oxygen consumption between genotypes, or unchanged OCR after blocking lysosomal substrate supply, would falsify step 5 while leaving steps 1-4 intact.", "Artifact control: after normalising the RNA data to remove the global positive shift (e.g. median-centring or spike-in normalisation), the lysosomal hydrolase and nuclear OXPHOS modules should remain above the recentred null. If they lose separation, the module coherence is a normalisation artifact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher steady-state transcript levels of the scavenger receptor SCARB1 (99th percentile of all measured effects) and of CD36, which we infer, but did not measure, increases lipoprotein/lipid uptake flux into the endosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA; inferred compartment size and activity): A coordinated CLEAR-type program is elevated relative to the global shift - TFEB plus glycosidases and lipid hydrolases (GAA, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, HEXB, MAN2B1, SMPD1) and cathepsins (CTSB, CTSD), mean percentile 68 for the hydrolase set (permutation p = 0.009), together with v-ATPase subunits (ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C). We infer an expanded, acidified degradative compartment; lysosome number, pH and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred bottleneck): The lysosomal sterol-export arm is not coordinately amplified. NPC2 sits below the global median shift (35th percentile) and the mannose-6-phosphate receptor M6PR is strongly reduced (15th percentile), while NPC1, LIPA, ABCA1 and ABCG1 are absent from this selected differential-expression list. We propose that sterol/lipid egress from the endolysosome, not hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step in APOE4.", "Step 4 (inferred consequence, not observed): Internalised sterol and sphingolipid are retained in the enlarged acidic compartment. Consistent with a lysosome-to-ER delivery deficit, the SREBP2 biosynthetic module is not suppressed despite high uptake capacity (DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS, ACAT2, INSIG1, LDLR, HMGCS1 all positive; set mean percentile 56, permutation p = 0.28), and the esterification enzymes SOAT1 and DGAT1 are not elevated above the global shift (39th and 57th percentiles), i.e. lipid is predicted to accumulate in the lysosome rather than being efficiently re-esterified.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred flux): Non-sterol catabolic products (amino acids, fatty acids) feed mitochondrial oxidation: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts are the most coherent up-shifted module (39 genes, mean percentile 69, permutation p = 1e-4; OGDH and MDH1 at the 99th percentile), whereas committed glycolytic steps HK2 and PFKP fall in the bottom 6 percent. Metabolic flux was not measured, and mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) move in the opposite direction.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype): The net APOE4 state is a lipid-laden, hyper-degradative but export-limited microglial lysosome, which we predict is reversible by bypassing the egress step rather than by adding hydrolase capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand a scavenger-receptor/CLEAR-type endolysosomal degradative program whose rate-limiting step is sterol egress from the lysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23837831850238156, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.033115668333389164, "cosine_similarity": 0.07337938341953246, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_031", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6587864077669903, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.23837831850238156, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.033115668333389164, "cosine_similarity": 0.07337938341953246, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6587864077669903, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.31803325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 437}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Functional annotations and relationships involving TFEB, ATP-dependent acidification, respiratory ATP generation and hydrolase maturation are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was used. The initiating biochemical effect of APOE4 and the direction of organelle cross-regulation are not identified.", "RNA effects are selected differential-expression results expressed as reported log fold change with unspecified base, positive for APOE4 versus APOE3. The selected background is 1705 positive and 507 negative rows, not a 50/50 null. Missing genes are unknown. Protein effects are log2 spot-abundance changes. Program coherence is descriptive and genes or overlapping protein spots are not independent evidence units.", "Successful adaptation requires adequate respiratory assembly despite gene:MT-ATP6 (-3.351), gene:MT-CYB (-2.322), gene:MT-CO2 (-1.328) and gene:MT-ND4 (-1.802) decreases; gene:MT-ND4L (+1.951) and gene:MT-ND5 (+1.929) increase. These RNA changes are serious counter-evidence to simple oxidative activation, but do not themselves establish a respiratory bottleneck. Failed compensation remains a serious explanation of the same abundance pattern.", "Functional acidification is uncertain: protein_spot:064 is -1.202 (ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1), protein_spot:065 is -0.926 (ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART), and protein_spot:075 is -0.138 (SOD2, VPS29, CAP1, RAP1B, ATP6V1H), all log2 fold changes. Spots 064 and 065 carry reported-significant flags; 075 does not. All candidate identities remain possible, so these decreases challenge but cannot establish loss of a pump subunit.", "Hydrolase expansion is selective and activity remains uncertain: gene:CTSS is -5.566. protein_spot:058 is -0.848 log2 (CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1) and protein_spot:067 is -1.000 log2 (PSMA3, ACTG2, CTSB, HEXB, LRIF1); both carry reported-significant flags. Opposing spots may reflect candidate mixtures or protein forms and cannot resolve mature enzyme amounts.", "The attribution to a microglial state assumes comparable astrocyte exposure and adequate control of microglial substate composition. The isogenic comparison does not identify a unique upstream cause or exclude a broader differentiation shift. The mechanism leaves strong adhesion/cytoskeletal changes incompletely explained: gene:ITGA6 (+15.460), gene:ITGB1 (+6.315) and gene:ARHGDIA (+10.610) oppose gene:ACTB (-4.975) and gene:MYH9 (-6.384).", "The proposed increase in degradation concerns the measured mock condition. Reduced or increased reserve revealed only by a future overload challenge cannot validate this basal claim. No ongoing defect, unmeasured lipid or protein pool, localization change, or established causality is asserted as a measurement."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 is hypothesized to induce a coordinated catabolic state that increases basal lysosomal degradation by expanding acidification and hydrolase capacity, with oxidative metabolic recruitment supplying the associated ATP demand.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospectively, in independently replicated matched day-30 mock co-cultures, microglia-resolved assays should show maintained or more acidic lysosomes and higher basal lysosome-dependent turnover of pre-labelled endogenous long-lived proteins in APOE4, together with greater mitochondrial ATP contribution. A minimally perturbing, uptake-normalized cargo pulse-chase should also show faster processing, but this assay alone would establish processing capacity rather than basal flux. Basal alkalinization and slower turnover despite the elevated transcripts would weaken the selected mechanism and favor failed compensation. A difference appearing only under overload would not validate the claim.", "Prospectively, induce partial, microglia-restricted ATP5F1B knockdown after differentiation in both genotypes, with matched target suppression, a guide-resistant rescue and monitoring before viability or cargo uptake changes. If increased mitochondrial ATP sustains the APOE4 degradation advantage, verified reduction of that ATP contribution should preferentially reduce the advantage together with lysosomal acidification; rescue should restore the linked ATP and degradation phenotype. An unchanged genotype difference despite verified ATP suppression, or an effect explained entirely by cell loss or altered uptake, would weaken the proposed energetic causal link."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 is proposed to shift the basal microglial state toward endolysosomal processing. Higher RNA for TFEB (gene:TFEB, +2.385), LAMP1 (gene:LAMP1, +1.377), RAB7A (gene:RAB7A, +2.654) and VPS26A (gene:VPS26A, +4.865) supports coordinated compartment and routing remodeling. Increased TFEB nuclear activity and organelle capacity are inferred; TFEB is a candidate coordinator, not an identified unique cause. Increased receptor transcripts gene:SCARB1 (+8.223), gene:CD36 (+1.376) and gene:TREM2 (+1.282) are compatible with this state but do not demonstrate increased uptake.", "The proposed remodeling recruits oxidative metabolism to meet its ATP demand: nuclear respiratory transcripts gene:NDUFS7 (+5.675), gene:NDUFS8 (+4.933), gene:UQCRC2 (+4.021), gene:COX7A2 (+3.357) and gene:ATP5F1B (+2.647) increase, alongside gene:MPC2 (+7.980), gene:ACO2 (+3.537) and gene:OGDH (+8.558). Their conversion into increased mitochondrial ATP supply is a causal assumption; assembly, respiration and ATP production were not measured.", "This ATP supply is proposed to support greater functional lysosomal acidification capacity. Increased RNA for multiple pump components, gene:ATP6V1A (+4.225), gene:ATP6V1C1 (+1.289), gene:ATP6V1E1 (+1.698), gene:ATP6V1F (+1.697), gene:ATP6V1H (+6.880), gene:ATP6V0C (+3.507) and gene:ATP6V0D1 (+1.675), together with gene:CLCN7 (+1.062), is compatible with coordinated acidification machinery. Assembly and localization must increase sufficiently to maintain acidic processing compartments; neither lysosomal pH nor pump activity is observed.", "Within these acidic compartments, greater mature hydrolase capacity is proposed to increase macromolecule cleavage. Supporting RNA includes gene:CTSB (+5.520), gene:CTSD (+2.864), gene:GAA (+9.961), gene:GBA (+6.713), gene:HEXA (+5.677), gene:HEXB (+2.171), gene:SMPD1 (+5.633), gene:NAGLU (+5.910) and gene:MAN2B1 (+1.809). This requires successful enzyme delivery and maturation. protein_spot:053 (+1.536 log2 fold change; candidates TPM3, CTSD, YWHAG, YWHAE, KRT1) is compatible but cannot confirm CTSD abundance or activity.", "The coupled energy, acidification and hydrolysis changes are hypothesized to produce higher lysosome-dependent degradation in the actual basal mock condition, with faster processing at matched intracellular cargo input. This is the unmeasured functional consequence linking the represented programs; increased clearance, substrate accumulation or any molecular pool is not reported as observed."], "title": "Coordinated lysosomal remodeling increases basal degradation in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16792822065502344, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16661201193441857, "cosine_similarity": 0.07332471245744611, "direction_accuracy": 0.09385113268608414, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6430258899676375, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16792822065502344, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16661201193441857, "cosine_similarity": 0.07332471245744611, "direction_accuracy": 0.09385113268608414, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6430258899676375, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.691538, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_008", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an apparent |effect| \u003e= ~1 filter and a strong positive skew (mean +1.39, 77% up); enrichment claims are therefore made against the internal distribution of this list, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks and relative magnitudes within the RNA list are used, and RNA effects are never compared numerically with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly and with delay, the abundance of the corresponding lysosomal hydrolase protein and its enzymatic capacity; no enzyme activity, protein-level hydrolase abundance, saposin (PSAP) level, or lysosomal pH was measured here.", "ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2, PSAP, NEU1 and GALC are absent from the list; we assume absence means they did not pass the differential filter (approximately unchanged), which is an assumption, not an observation - they could also have been unmeasured or filtered for other reasons.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are dominated by keratin/actin candidates; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration or counter-evidence.", "No lipid, flux, imaging, or organelle-fractionation measurement is present in this dataset; ceramide accumulation, membrane order, cargo flux, TFEB localization and directionality are inferred and unproven.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from, or be influenced by, non-microglial signalling; genotype-driven cell-intrinsic causality is assumed but not established."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the sphingolipid-catabolic arm of the lysosomal program (SMPD1, GBA, GBA2, HEXA/HEXB, GM2A, GLA) is transcriptionally amplified far above the already-upward background of this differential-expression list, while the branches that would export or re-glycosylate the resulting ceramide/sphingosine are not co-amplified (B4GALT5 transcript is reduced; ASAH1, UGCG and SGMS1/2 are absent from the supplied list and therefore unmeasured) and the salvage re-acylation enzymes CERS4/CERS6/KDSR are up. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting bottleneck is ceramide/sphingosine disposal out of the late endosome-lysosome, and that the resulting inferred ceramide-enriched limiting membrane biases Rab7/retromer-dependent cargo routing (RAB7A, VPS26A, SNX3, CHMP4B up, M6PR down), producing the APOE4-specific endolysosomal phenotype rather than a simple increase in degradative capacity.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial inhibition of the induced hydrolytic input in APOE4 microglia - GBA inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) or functional acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition (desipramine/amitriptyline), at doses that do not raise lysosomal pH - should lower lysosomal ceramide and partially normalise Rab7/retromer-dependent routing readouts (CI-/CD-MPR recycling, DQ-BSA dequenching, LAMP1 organelle size and perinuclear clustering) in APOE4 with substantially smaller effects in isogenic APOE3. If these inhibitors fail to reduce ceramide or fail to improve APOE4 routing, or if they perturb APOE3 equally, the mechanism is weakened.", "Rescue at the bottleneck rather than the input: over-expression of ASAH1 (or of UGCG, diverting ceramide to glucosylceramide) in APOE4 microglia should relieve the routing/degradation phenotype without lowering GBA/HEXA/SMPD1 transcripts. No rescue by ASAH1/UGCG would falsify the 'disposal is limiting' claim even if the hydrolase induction is confirmed.", "Direct lipid test: targeted sphingolipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia at day 30 (mock) should show elevated ceramide, in particular the CERS4/CERS6-preferred C18-C24 and C16 species, and elevated sphingosine, with GlcCer/LacCer/GM2 flat or reduced (consistent with B4GALT5 down). Finding accumulated GlcCer/GM2 with unchanged or reduced ceramide would invert the model, indicating substrate-driven compensatory hydrolase induction rather than a ceramide bottleneck.", "Capacity test: measured GBA, HEXA/HEXB and acid sphingomyelinase enzymatic activities (not just transcripts) should be higher in APOE4 lysosomal fractions, while ASAH1 activity should be unchanged, giving an increased hydrolase-to-ceramidase activity ratio. Proportional ASAH1 up-regulation, or no activity difference despite the transcript differences, would weaken the mechanism and favour a purely transcriptional TFEB-program explanation.", "Specificity test against the alternative sterol model: SREBP2 pathway inhibition (e.g. statin or SREBP-cleavage blockade) should not correct the APOE4 endolysosomal routing readouts, whereas the sphingolipid manipulations above should. If sterol-pathway blockade corrects the phenotype and sphingolipid manipulation does not, the primary bottleneck is mis-assigned."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype drives a lysosome-biased transcriptional state in microglia (TFEB transcript up 2.38; broad lysosomal-hydrolase transcripts including GAA, CTSB, CTSK, NAGLU in the top decile of this list). Measured: transcript abundance only; TFEB nuclear localization and CLEAR-network activity are inferred, not observed.", "Within that program, the sphingolipid-hydrolase subset is disproportionately induced (SMPD1 5.63, GBA 6.71, HEXA 5.68, HEXB 2.17, GBA2 2.63, GM2A 2.01, GLA 1.53; set mean 3.77 versus list median 1.46, permutation p = 0.009). SCARB2 (GBA delivery receptor) and GLTP are also up. This raises the predicted capacity for sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid hydrolysis; enzyme activity and flux are inferred, not measured.", "The exits from ceramide are not co-induced: B4GALT5 (GlcCer to LacCer) transcript is down (-1.88), while CERS4 (2.52), CERS6 (1.06) and KDSR (1.27) favour re-acylation of sphingosine back to ceramide. The dominant ceramide-clearing enzyme ASAH1, plus UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2 and PSAP, are absent from the supplied differential list, so the disposal arm is unmeasured; we posit it is not proportionally increased.", "The mismatch between amplified hydrolytic input and unchanged disposal creates the primary bottleneck: net ceramide (and sphingosine) accumulation in the limiting and intraluminal membranes of APOE4 late endosomes/lysosomes. This lipid pool is inferred; no lipid species was measured in this dataset.", "Ceramide-enriched, more ordered endolysosomal membranes alter membrane-protein sorting and fission/scission platforms, which the transcriptome mirrors as a coordinated shift in Rab7/retromer/ESCRT routing genes (RAB7A 2.65, VPS26A 4.86, SNX3 3.95, CHMP4B 3.82, VAMP3 2.99, ARL8B 1.12; set mean 3.13, MWU p = 0.012) with reduced CD-MPR (M6PR -1.72) despite increased M6P-tagging and receptor transcripts (GNPTG 3.02, IGF2R 2.02). Cargo flux and organelle position are inferred, not observed.", "The rerouting feeds back on hydrolase delivery and substrate clearance, so APOE4 microglia sustain a high-hydrolase, low-throughput endolysosomal state; this is consistent with the mixed and internally contradictory 2-D protein-spot data for lysosomal candidates (protein_spot:044 and protein_spot:076 up, protein_spot:067 down), which we read as spot redistribution rather than uniform protein gain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia amplify lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matched ceramide disposal, creating a ceramide-loaded late-endosome/lysosome that reroutes retromer-dependent traffic"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0012446581791883981, "cosine_similarity": 0.07217985268991266, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6667508090614888, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0012446581791883981, "cosine_similarity": 0.07217985268991266, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6667508090614888, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.428211, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 438}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_090", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no |effect| below 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77 percent up) in an unspecified logarithm base; all directional claims are therefore made as percentile ranks within this list, not as absolute up- or down-regulation, and absence of a gene means not supplied, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, less securely, enzyme activity and flux; no hydroperoxide, GSH/GSSG, NADPH, labile iron, lipid-droplet or lipidomic measurement is present in these data, so all flux, localisation and redox-poise statements are inferred.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each (mean 4.8) and are not uniquely identified; spot 077 (PRDX2 among six candidates including keratins), spot 017 (CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5) and spot 042 (BLVRA, NCF4 and others) are treated as weak, ambiguous corroboration only, and TALDO1-containing spots are not treated as TALDO1 because ANXA1 (transcript +4.15) co-occupies them.", "Astrocyte co-culture means some measured RNA/protein signal may not be microglial in origin; replicate number and normalisation are not supplied, so effect sizes cannot be converted into calibrated confidence.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed genuinely isogenic and matched in differentiation stage, so the contrast reflects genotype rather than line drift or maturation-state differences."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated transcriptional state in which lysosomal/sphingolipid catabolic genes and thiol-peroxidase genes (GPX4, PRDX2/3/5, MGST2, GSS) are elevated relative to the strongly up-shifted global background, while the PUFA-peroxidation arm (ACSL4, ALOX15) is among the most suppressed genes. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step for APOE4 lipid handling is GPX4/peroxiredoxin-dependent reduction of phospholipid hydroperoxides: because that capacity is near its ceiling, fatty acid liberated from an expanded lysosomal lipid flux is diverted by SCD/SREBF1-driven monounsaturated synthesis into DGAT1/SOAT1 neutral-lipid storage rather than into oxidisable PUFA-containing membrane phospholipid. Peroxisomal beta-oxidation is explicitly rejected as the mechanism (no PEX gene measured; ACOX1, CROT, AMACR at or below the background percentile; ABCD1 decreased). The prediction is a low-damage but low-reserve redox state, i.e. conditional hypersensitivity to GPX4 or SCD inhibition rather than overt baseline oxidative injury. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: a GPX4 inhibitor dose-response (RSL3 or ML162) in mock-treated isogenic microglia should give a lower EC50 and faster C11-BODIPY581/591 oxidation in APOE4 than APOE3, fully rescued by ferrostatin-1 or liproxstatin-1. Equal or greater resistance of APOE4 to GPX4 inhibition would weaken the mechanism.", "SCD inhibition (for example CAY10566) should selectively convert the APOE4 storage phenotype into measurable lipid peroxidation and viability loss, with a smaller effect in APOE3; if APOE4 tolerates SCD inhibition as well as APOE3 does, the MUFA-diversion step fails.", "Untargeted lipidomics should show APOE4 with a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in phosphatidylethanolamine/phosphatidylcholine and in triacylglycerol, and lower arachidonoyl- and adrenoyl-PE, than APOE3. Finding APOE4 enriched in PUFA-PE with elevated baseline 4-HNE/MDA would falsify the peroxidation-avoidance framing and favour an overt oxidative-damage model.", "Baseline discrimination between adaptation and ongoing damage: ferrostatin-1 alone should not reduce APOE4 lipid-droplet area or restore APOE3-like transcript levels of GPX4/PRDX2/3/5 in mock conditions; if ferrostatin-1 alone clears droplets, ongoing peroxidation rather than pre-emptive avoidance is driving storage.", "ACSL4 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore PUFA-PE and sensitise the cells to ferroptosis without requiring any change in lysosomal hydrolase expression; no sensitisation would break the substrate-restriction step.", "Negative control for the rejected focus: PEX5 knockdown or ACOX1 inhibition should perturb lipid-droplet content and peroxidation similarly in APOE4 and APOE3. A selective APOE4 effect would indicate that peroxisomal beta-oxidation, not thiol-peroxidase capacity, is the true bottleneck and would require replacing this hypothesis.", "Because reducing-equivalent supply is rewired rather than lost, NNT or ME1 knockdown should sensitise APOE4 more than G6PD inhibition does; the opposite ordering would indicate a pentose-phosphate NADPH bottleneck instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, HEXB, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A) and TFEB are elevated in APOE4 relative to the global distribution of this differential-expression list. Inferred (not measured): increased flux of membrane glycosphingolipid/sphingomyelin and lipoprotein-derived lipid through the endolysosome, liberating free fatty acid and increasing labile-iron exposure.", "Inferred: fatty acid liberated in an iron-containing lysosomal compartment raises the demand for reduction of phospholipid hydroperoxides. Measured correlate: thiol-peroxidase and glutathione transcripts GPX4, PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, MGST2, GSS and the iron-sequestering FTH1 sit in the upper quartile of the effect distribution (set median percentile 0.76, permutation p about 0.03); PRDX2- and CAT-containing protein spots are increased, but spot identity is ambiguous.", "Measured: the enzymatic PUFA-peroxidation arm is suppressed against a background in which 77 percent of listed genes are up: ACSL4 (percentile 0.11) and ALOX15 (percentile 0.04). Inferred: reduced esterification of arachidonate/adrenate into phosphatidylethanolamine and reduced enzymatic lipid peroxidation, i.e. a lowered peroxidisable substrate pool rather than a lowered oxidant load.", "Measured: SREBF1, SCD, FADS1, DGAT1, SOAT1 and ACAT2 are increased. Inferred: acyl chains are channelled toward monounsaturated species and esterified into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl ester droplets, a storage route that is chemically resistant to propagation of lipid peroxidation.", "Inferred consequence (the bottleneck): with GPX4/PRDX capacity already recruited, APOE4 microglia can only expand lipid load safely by keeping it saturated/monounsaturated and sequestered; net measurable phenotype is lipid accumulation with little baseline peroxidation damage, and loss of reserve against any challenge that adds PUFA, iron or GPX4 inhibition.", "Reducing-equivalent supply is rewired rather than clearly limiting: NNT and ME1 transcripts are up while pentose-phosphate transcripts PGD and TALDO1 are down, and G6PD/PGD/GSR-containing protein spots are unchanged and non-significant. This step is stated as an open uncertainty, not as evidence for NADPH limitation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a peroxidation-avoidant lipid-handling state: GPX4/peroxiredoxin hydroperoxide-clearance capacity, not peroxisomal beta-oxidation, is the limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27352952036332756, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15491498905164297, "cosine_similarity": 0.067407047820567, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_090", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7165533980582524, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27352952036332756, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15491498905164297, "cosine_similarity": 0.067407047820567, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7165533980582524, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8071625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 439}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_074", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every adjusted p value is below 0.05) rather than an unbiased transcriptome, so enrichment is judged only against the list-internal median (+1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), and absent genes (GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, PDHA1, CS, MDH2, PDK1-4, TFAM) are treated as not supplied, not as unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only relative ranking within the list is used, and the very large magnitudes (up to 15.5) are not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme and subunit abundance; enzyme activity, metabolite concentration, respiratory flux, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial mass and submitochondrial localization were not measured here.", "The four reduced MT- transcripts are assumed to reflect reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit supply rather than a purely technical difference in mitochondrial-read fraction, ambient RNA, or per-cell normalization between the APOE4 and APOE3 libraries.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are assumed not to identify any single protein; they are used only as weak, non-attributable context.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture; the RNA comparison is assumed to reflect the microglial compartment, and any cross-feeding of lactate, glutamine or lipids by astrocytes is assumed to be equal between genotypes.", "Isogenic APOE4-versus-APOE3 differences at day 30 are assumed not to be dominated by differing differentiation efficiency or cell-state composition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded transcriptional program for TCA-cycle, malate-aspartate shuttle, mitochondrial-carrier, mitochondrial-translation and OXPHOS-subunit genes that rises well above the strong global positive shift of this differential-expression list, while the mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits of complexes I, III, IV and V (MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) are reduced. We hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is the supply of mtDNA-encoded core ETC subunits relative to the imported nuclear-encoded accessory subunits: nuclear-encoded machinery for carbon entry into mitochondria (PDP1-dependent pyruvate oxidation, glutamate/glutamine anaplerosis via GLS/GLUD1/GOT1, and MDH1/GOT1/SLC25A11/SLC25A13 shuttle flux) is expanded, but respiratory-chain assembly cannot scale with it, so APOE4 microglia are predicted to show increased mitochondrial substrate delivery with a disproportionately small increase (or a decrease) in coupled respiratory capacity, plus an integrated-stress/mitochondrial-stress readout (DDIT3). Reduced transcripts for the committed glycolytic kinases HK2 and PFKP, alongside increased glucose-transporter transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3), predict that glucose is not the substrate that is preferentially oxidised. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: supplying the mtDNA-encoded shortfall or bypassing it should relieve the bottleneck selectively in APOE4. Cybrid or allotopic/mitochondrially targeted re-expression of MT-ATP6 and MT-CYB (or transfer of APOE3 mitochondria into APOE4 microglia) should raise coupled oxygen consumption and the ATP-linked fraction in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels WITHOUT further increasing the nuclear TCA/OXPHOS transcripts, and should lower DDIT3. If coupled respiration stays unchanged after mtDNA-encoded subunits are restored, the proposed assembly bottleneck is wrong.", "Substrate-choice prediction: in Seahorse/isotope experiments, APOE4 microglia should depend more on glutamine than on glucose for oxidation. Uniformly labelled 13C-glutamine should give higher fractional labelling of TCA intermediates (citrate, alpha-ketoglutarate, malate, aspartate) in APOE4 than APOE3, while 13C-glucose labelling of those intermediates should be equal or lower; BPTES/CB-839 (GLS inhibition) or aminooxyacetate (GOT inhibition) should reduce basal OCR more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or greater glucose-derived TCA labelling in APOE4 would weaken steps 2 and 3.", "Capacity-versus-content prediction: BN-PAGE or complexome analysis should show that assembled complex I, III, IV and V holoenzymes are NOT increased in APOE4 in proportion to the increased nuclear-encoded subunit transcripts, with accumulation of nuclear-encoded subassemblies or free subunits; maximal FCCP-stimulated OCR per unit mitochondrial mass (citrate-synthase or TOM20 normalised) should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite the elevated transcript program. Finding proportionally increased assembled holoenzymes and proportionally increased maximal respiration would falsify the primary bottleneck.", "Glycolysis prediction: extracellular acidification rate and glycolytic capacity after oligomycin should be equal or lower in APOE4 despite higher SLC2A1/SLC2A3 transcripts, and hexokinase activity in lysates should be lower. Higher glycolytic rate and higher hexokinase activity in APOE4 would falsify the reduced-glucose-commitment step and favour a HIF1A-driven glycolytic-switch alternative.", "Counterfactual on the global shift: after re-normalising the same libraries with a method insensitive to total-RNA-content differences (e.g. spike-in or median-of-ratios pseudobulk), the nuclear-OXPHOS-versus-mtDNA divergence should persist as an opposite-direction pair. If the mtDNA-encoded transcripts are no longer reduced relative to nuclear OXPHOS after renormalisation, the mitonuclear-imbalance claim collapses to a normalisation artefact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for nuclear-encoded TCA and anaplerotic enzymes (OGDH, DLD, ACO2, IDH3G, GLUD1, GLS, GOT1, MDH1) and for amino-acid/mitochondrial carriers (SLC38A2, SLC1A5, SLC25A11, SLC25A13, SLC25A1, SLC25A5), with a set median far above the list-wide median.", "Step 2 (inferred flux and localization): the coordinated GOT1/MDH1/SLC25A11/SLC25A13 and GLS/GLUD1/OGDH pattern is interpreted as increased malate-aspartate shuttle and glutamate/glutamine-derived alpha-ketoglutarate entry into the TCA cycle, i.e. a shift of oxidised carbon away from glucose; this flux is inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): reduced HK2 and PFKP transcripts with increased SLC2A1/SLC2A3 transcripts are interpreted as reduced commitment of imported glucose to glycolytic pyruvate, while increased PDP1 transcript is interpreted as a bias toward dephosphorylated (active) pyruvate dehydrogenase for whatever pyruvate is formed.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit transcripts (NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8, NDUFB6, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5MC3, ATP5ME, CYCS, SDHB) and mitochondrial import/translation/insertion factors (TOMM22, TIMM44, TUFM, GFM2, MTPAP, OXA1L) are elevated, whereas mtDNA-encoded MT-ND4, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ATP6 are reduced.", "Step 5 (primary bottleneck, inferred): because each of complexes I, III, IV and V requires mtDNA-encoded core subunits, their relative shortfall is proposed to make holoenzyme assembly, not subunit import or substrate supply, the rate-limiting step; the elevated mitochondrial-translation transcripts are read as a compensatory response to, not a resolution of, this shortfall.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): substrate delivery that exceeds assembled respiratory capacity is predicted to produce a low ATP-linked-to-substrate-oxidation ratio, increased proton leak or reduced spare respiratory capacity, and a retrograde stress response consistent with the elevated DDIT3 transcript; HIF1A elevation is interpreted as part of this stress response rather than as evidence of a glycolytic switch."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch caps oxidative carbon disposal in APOE4 microglia despite an expanded anaplerotic/TCA program"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.01923132666957144, "cosine_similarity": 0.06603233192460879, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6405436893203883, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.01923132666957144, "cosine_similarity": 0.06603233192460879, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6405436893203883, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.33085425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 440}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_008", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA log-fold-change is treated as a proxy for enzyme abundance/activity change; this is not verified by matched protein data in this dataset and protein-spot evidence for CTSD- and CERK-candidate spots is mixed or discordant.", "The discovery RNA rows are pre-selected differential-expression hits (all reported as adjusted-p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased transcriptome sample, so the apparent enrichment of sphingolipid/lysosomal genes may partly reflect selection into the DE list rather than pathway-specific magnitude beyond the global positive skew (global RNA mean effect +1.39, median +1.46; sphingolipid-gene subset mean +2.33, median +1.53).", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes, so a spot's abundance change cannot be attributed to a single named sphingolipid enzyme with certainty.", "RAB7A/RAB27A/ARL8B transcript changes are assumed to be relevant to vesicular routing direction, but no direct measurement of exosome release, lysosomal ceramide content, or membrane trafficking flux is available in this dataset.", "No causal direction between APOE4 genotype and this transcriptional program is established; the pattern could reflect a compensatory response to prior lipid handling stress rather than a primary driver.", "The logarithm base for the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified in the source data and is not altered or assumed here beyond relative comparison."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus APOE3 isogenic iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, coordinated upregulation of lysosomal sphingolipid-catabolic transcripts (acid sphingomyelinase SMPD1, glucocerebrosidases GBA/GBA2, alpha-galactosidase GLA), ceramide-generating/salvage transcripts (CERS4, CERS6, KDSR, CERK), the S1P-degrading enzyme SGPL1, and late-endosomal/lysosomal maturation genes (RAB7A, ARL8B, LAMP1, NPC2, CTSD/CTSB), together with a strong reduction of the secretory-vesicle/exosome docking GTPase RAB27A, is consistent with a transcriptional program that increases lysosomal sphingolipid turnover flux and redirects sphingolipid-bearing membrane material toward intracellular lysosomal degradation rather than exosomal secretion. This is an association observed at the RNA/protein-spot level; no causal or lipidomic flux measurement is available.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SMPD1 (acid sphingomyelinase) in APOE4 microglia should reduce lysosomal ceramide accumulation and shift the RAB7A-high/RAB27A-low trafficking transcript signature toward the APOE3 pattern; if SMPD1 inhibition leaves ceramide levels and RAB7A/RAB27A transcript ratios unchanged, the SMPD1-centered bottleneck is weakened.", "Direct lipidomic profiling of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show an elevated ceramide/sphingosine-1-phosphate ratio and reduced sphingolipid cargo in secreted extracellular vesicles/exosomes relative to APOE3; absence of an elevated ceramide/S1P ratio or absence of reduced EV sphingolipid cargo would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring RAB27A expression/function in APOE4 microglia should increase exosomal secretion and reduce intracellular sphingolipid/ceramide retention without necessarily normalizing SMPD1, GBA, or CERS4/6 transcript levels; if RAB27A restoration fails to change intracellular ceramide retention, this would indicate the routing step is not the operative bottleneck and would dissociate turnover from routing in this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA log-fold-changes show large APOE4-vs-APOE3 increases in lysosomal hydrolases that cleave complex sphingolipids to ceramide: SMPD1 (sphingomyelin\u2192ceramide, gene:SMPD1), GBA and GBA2 (glucosylceramide\u2192ceramide, gene:GBA, gene:GBA2), and GLA (globotriaosylceramide pathway, gene:GLA).", "Concurrent increases in ceramide-synthesis/salvage transcripts CERS4, CERS6, KDSR and the ceramide-phosphorylating enzyme CERK (gene:CERS4, gene:CERS6, gene:KDSR, gene:CERK) suggest parallel upregulation of machinery that produces and further modifies ceramide, while increased ORMDL2 (gene:ORMDL2), a known negative-feedback regulator of serine palmitoyltransferase, points toward turnover/salvage rather than de novo synthesis as the dominant inferred route to the ceramide pool.", "Increased SGPL1 transcript (gene:SGPL1), which encodes the enzyme that irreversibly degrades sphingosine-1-phosphate, suggests (if transcript tracks activity) reduced capacity to regenerate S1P from degraded sphingolipids, nudging the inferred ceramide/S1P balance toward the ceramide-high side.", "Increased RAB7A and ARL8B transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:ARL8B) together with LAMP1, NPC2, CTSD and CTSB (gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB) indicate expanded late-endosome-to-lysosome maturation and lysosomal hydrolytic/positioning capacity, consistent with routing of sphingolipid-laden membranes toward intracellular degradation.", "In contrast, RAB27A transcript is strongly reduced (gene:RAB27A, effect -2.52), a GTPase required for secretory-lysosome/multivesicular-body docking and exosome release, suggesting reduced routing of these membranes toward extracellular secretion, favoring intracellular retention/degradation over export.", "Protein-spot evidence gives only partial, ambiguous support: CTSD-candidate spots move in both directions (protein_spot:027 +0.585 sig, protein_spot:053 +1.536 sig vs protein_spot:058 -0.848 sig, protein_spot:069 -1.379 sig) and the CERK-candidate spot (protein_spot:010, effect -1.0, p=0.41, not significant) trends opposite to the CERK RNA change, so protein-level confirmation of any single gene in this pathway is not established because spots have multiple candidate genes.", "Net inference: the transcriptional program is compatible with increased lysosomal sphingolipid turnover flux and a shift of sphingolipid-containing membrane traffic away from exosomal export toward lysosomal degradation in APOE4 microglia; this may plausibly (unmeasured) elevate intracellular ceramide pools and alter lysosomal membrane composition, but no ceramide, S1P, or vesicle-lipid abundance was directly measured."], "title": "APOE4 shifts microglial sphingolipid handling toward lysosomal ceramide-generating turnover and away from RAB27A-dependent exosomal export"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1939962337998006, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08879880904782489, "cosine_similarity": 0.06542643049494513, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_008", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6741067961165049, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1939962337998006, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08879880904782489, "cosine_similarity": 0.06542643049494513, "direction_accuracy": 0.12297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6741067961165049, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5300099, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 6}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_038", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with a strong global positive shift (mean +1.39, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base); all directional claims here are made on within-dataset rank, not on raw sign, and assume the selection did not preferentially enrich sphingolipid catabolic genes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and hydrolytic activity for SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB; this coupling is not measured here and is often broken for lysosomal hydrolases (activity depends on pH, saposins and lipid presentation).", "Key sphingolipid nodes were not measured in this panel (SPTLC1/2, ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, ACER3, GALC, PSAP, SPHK1, SGPP1, NPC1), so the de novo and acid-ceramidase arms are unconstrained; the bottleneck is placed downstream of hydrolysis by inference from the measured disposal/re-synthesis transcripts only.", "Protein spots carry 3-6 candidate genes each and are treated as non-identifying; no protein spot is used as evidence for a named sphingolipid enzyme.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes; the RNA comparison is assumed to be microglia-resolved (10X Flex) and not contaminated by astrocytic sphingolipid gene expression.", "No lipid, flux, pH, or imaging measurement is available, so ceramide accumulation, membrane order and impaired egress are inferences, and the APOE4-to-lysosome direction is a hypothesis, not an established causal chain."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 by a transcriptionally coherent expansion of the endolysosomal acid-hydrolase program in which the sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid-degrading arm (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA/HEXB, GBA2, GLA) is raised far above the dataset-wide upward shift while the transcripts that dispose of, or re-esterify, the resulting ceramide and sphingoid bases (SGPL1, CERK, CERS6, B4GALT5, ST3GAL2, NPC2) sit below the dataset median. We hypothesise that this asymmetry, not a change in de novo sphingolipid synthesis, is the primary bottleneck: hydrolytic input to the lysosomal ceramide pool exceeds its exit routes, so ceramide/sphingosine accumulates in late endosomes/lysosomes and degrades cargo-clearance and membrane-recycling flux, with TFEB/v-ATPase/RAB7A induction and SPNS1 up-regulation as compensatory responses. Causality is not established by these data; the ceramide pool itself was not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING: targeted sphingolipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (mock) should show increased total and C16/C24 ceramide and increased sphingosine with a decreased ratio of complex glycosphingolipids (lactosylceramide, GM3/GD3-series) to ceramide. If instead sphingomyelin and glucosylceramide accumulate with unchanged or lower ceramide, the catabolic-overload direction is wrong and the hydrolase transcript rise is better read as compensation for reduced enzyme activity.", "DISCRIMINATING RESCUE: increasing ceramide disposal in APOE4 microglia (ASAH1 or SGPL1 overexpression, or acid-ceramidase-directed enzyme supplementation) should lower endolysosomal ceramide and restore degradative flux (DQ-BSA dequenching, BODIPY-LacCer and myelin/synaptosome clearance) toward APOE3 without reducing SMPD1/GBA/HEXA transcript levels. Failure to improve flux while ceramide is demonstrably lowered would refute the bottleneck placement and point to a cholesterol- or v-ATPase-centred lesion instead.", "Partial pharmacological reduction of the input arm (functional ASM inhibition, or low-dose GBA inhibition) should reduce lysosomal ceramide and normalise lysosome size/LysoTracker signal in APOE4 but should worsen substrate clearance in APOE3; an identical response in both genotypes would argue the sphingolipid arm is not genotype-discriminating.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show GBA, ASM and beta-hexosaminidase specific activities elevated in APOE4 lysosomes in proportion to their transcripts; transcript-up/activity-flat results would break mechanism step 2.", "In an unbiased whole-transcriptome or proteome comparison of the same lines, SMPD1/GBA/HEXA should remain in the top decile after correcting for the global shift while SGPL1/B4GALT5/ST3GAL2 remain below median; if the sphingolipid hydrolases regress to the median once selection bias is removed, the whole hypothesis is weakened.", "Complementation prediction: restoring complex-glycosphingolipid regeneration (B4GALT5 re-expression) should partially normalise endolysosomal morphology and chemokine tone (CXCL8, CCL2) in APOE4; no effect would indicate the re-synthesis arm is a bystander."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype engages an endolysosomal degradative-capacity program in microglia: TFEB (gene:TFEB), v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), RAB7A (gene:RAB7A) and multiple acid hydrolases (gene:GAA, gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB) are raised above the dataset-wide positive shift. This is measured RNA abundance; increased lysosome number, acidification and hydrolase activity are inferred, not observed.", "Within this program the sphingolipid-catabolic arm is disproportionately raised (gene:SMPD1, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2, gene:GLA; median within-dataset rank ~0.80), inferring increased capacity to convert lumenal sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide and gangliosides into ceramide and sphingosine at the late endosome/lysosome.", "The routes that consume ceramide and sphingoid bases are not raised in proportion: sphingosine-1-phosphate lyase (gene:SGPL1), ceramide kinase (gene:CERK), ceramide synthase 6 (gene:CERS6) and the lipid-transfer partner NPC2 (gene:NPC2) rank below the dataset median, and re-synthesis of complex glycosphingolipids from ceramide/glucosylceramide is reduced (gene:B4GALT5, gene:ST3GAL2 are among the lowest-ranked transcripts in the panel). The two arms separate completely (Mann-Whitney U = 36/36, p = 0.0011).", "PRIMARY BOTTLENECK (inferred flux, not measured): net ceramide/sphingosine production inside the endolysosome exceeds its clearance, so the lumenal/limiting-membrane ceramide pool rises and complex glycosphingolipid regeneration falls. This is a flux and localization claim; no lipid species were measured in this experiment.", "Ceramide-enriched, order-increased endolysosomal membranes are predicted to slow cargo degradation, lipid egress and tubular recycling, i.e. reduced degradative flux despite greater hydrolase transcript abundance; the up-regulation of the lysosomal sphingoid-base exporter SPNS1 (gene:SPNS1) and of GM3 synthase (gene:ST3GAL5) is interpreted as a compensatory attempt to drain this pool.", "The resulting chronic endolysosomal stress plausibly sustains the modest NF-kB/chemokine tone seen here (gene:NFKBIZ, gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2) rather than an interferon program, and coexists with an SREBP/lipid-uptake shift (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCARB1) that would add further lipid load to the same compartment."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matching ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal, creating a ceramide-egress bottleneck in the endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010875320617456332, "cosine_similarity": 0.06477469527182604, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_038", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6950097087378642, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010875320617456332, "cosine_similarity": 0.06477469527182604, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6950097087378642, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.46025975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 441}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_034", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program directions were judged against that 77.1%-positive background, and genes absent from the list (e.g. all MRPL/MRPS, GAPDH, PKM, LDHA, G6PD, CPT1A) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding enzymes and transporters; no enzyme activity, respiration, NADPH pool, lactate output or metabolite flux was measured here, so all routing and capacity statements are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel proteoforms with 2-6 candidate identities each (KRT/ACTB contaminants dominate); no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot-level changes are used only for compatibility/contradiction testing.", "Genes within a program are not independent (shared regulation, shared amplification and normalization), so the coherence reported is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia co-cultured with astrocytes at day 30 under mock treatment; astrocyte-derived substrate supply and cell-composition differences between genotypes are assumed not to be the sole driver of the transcript differences.", "The reserve deficit is an explicitly prospective prediction under future challenge; the measured mock condition supports an altered, apparently sustained cell state rather than a demonstrated ongoing bottleneck."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 not by a single broken enzyme but by a coordinated cell-state shift: transcripts for lysosomal degradation, alternative carbon-substrate activation (lipid, ketone/acetate, branched-chain and glutamate carbon), mitochondrial carriers/import and the entire represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA machinery are higher, while the inducible glucose-committing steps (HK2, PFKP, PFKFB2, HK3) and the represented pentose-phosphate rows (PGD, TALDO1) are lower. We propose APOE4 cells route carbon toward lysosome- and lipid-derived oxidation in mitochondria and away from HK2/PFKP-driven glycolysis and glucose-derived NADPH production; in the measured mock state this is an adaptation with expanded oxidative machinery (measured abundance only), and the predicted cost is a reduced glycolytic/PPP reserve that would be revealed by an acute demand or oxidant challenge, not an established ongoing rate limitation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective extracellular-flux profiling of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher OCR/ECAR ratio, with respiration in APOE4 disproportionately reduced by lysosomal or lipolytic blockade (bafilomycin A1, DGAT/lipase or CPT1 inhibition). If APOE4 basal/maximal OCR is equal or lower than APOE3 and substrate dependence is unchanged, the lysosome-fed oxidative-routing mechanism is weakened.", "Prospective U-13C-glucose tracing should show a lower fractional contribution of glucose carbon to citrate/malate and lower oxidative-PPP flux (1,2-13C glucose labelling ratio) in APOE4, with total TCA intermediate pools maintained by lipid/amino-acid carbon. Unchanged or greater glucose contribution to TCA and PPP would falsify the routing claim.", "Prospective challenge with LPS or a zymosan phagocytic burst should reveal reduced glycolytic and NADPH reserve in APOE4 (blunted ECAR/lactate induction, greater NADP+/NADPH shift and greater sensitivity to H2O2 or buthionine sulfoximine) while mock ATP levels are comparable. Equivalent glycolytic induction and oxidant tolerance would refute the reserve limb without refuting the steady-state cell state.", "Prospective test of the competing mito-nuclear-imbalance model: BN-PAGE/complex-activity assays and quantitative mtDNA-encoded protein measurement in mock cells. If APOE4 shows reduced assembled complex III/IV/V or reduced mtDNA-encoded subunit protein despite the increased nuclear OXPHOS transcripts (gene:NDUFA5, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME) and the decreased gene:MT-ATP6/gene:MT-CYB/gene:MT-CO2, the present adaptation model should be replaced by a failed-compensation model.", "Prospective causal test: restoring glucose-committed flux in APOE4 (HK2 re-expression or PFKFB3 activation) should normalize the OCR/ECAR ratio and the challenge response without reversing the lysosomal-hydrolase transcript program; conversely HK2/PGD knockdown in APOE3 should partially phenocopy the APOE4 flux profile. No phenocopy in APOE3 would indicate the glycolytic/PPP rows are passengers of a broader state change rather than steps in the mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype raises a TFEB-associated lysosomal-degradative program (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU; 24/25 represented lysosomal rows positive), increasing the supply of lipid- and protein-derived catabolites to the cytosol (supply inferred, not measured).", "Enzymes that activate non-glucose carbon for mitochondrial entry are coordinately higher (gene:MGLL, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1, gene:ACSS2, gene:OXCT1, gene:BCAT2, gene:GLUD1, gene:GLS, gene:ABAT), so acetyl-CoA and alpha-ketoglutarate can be generated independently of glycolytic pyruvate.", "Mitochondrial import and carrier transcripts (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:TIMM17B, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A13, gene:SLC25A46) and matrix TCA transcripts (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:DLD, gene:MDH1, gene:PDP1) rise together with all 40 represented nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit/assembly rows (e.g., gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5ME, gene:ATP5F1B), expanding the capacity of the oxidative apparatus.", "In parallel the inducible, flux-setting glycolytic steps fall (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2, gene:HK3) while uptake and lower-pathway rows stay high (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:PFKM, gene:ENO1, gene:SLC16A1) and glycogen synthase rises (gene:GYS1), so glucose carbon is predicted to be routed to storage and to the oxidative pathway rather than to high-rate glycolysis and lactate output.", "The represented pentose-phosphate rows decrease (gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1), predicting lower glucose-derived NADPH regeneration capacity, which the cells offset in the measured condition with a higher thiol/peroxide-defence transcript set (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:GPX4).", "The resulting steady state is oxidative and catabolism-fed with an elevated inflammatory and phagocytic-receptor tone (gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:NFKBIZ, gene:TLR6, gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:TREM2, gene:CD33, gene:APOE); the predicted functional deficit is a diminished rapid glycolytic and NADPH reserve that appears only when an acute burst (LPS, phagocytic load, oxidant) is imposed."], "title": "APOE4 microglia occupy a lysosome-fed, substrate-diversified oxidative state with down-weighted glucose-committed glycolysis and pentose-phosphate branch"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2117841450356312, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05993698825154586, "cosine_similarity": 0.06410095078896615, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_034", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6686472491909385, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2117841450356312, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05993698825154586, "cosine_similarity": 0.06410095078896615, "direction_accuracy": 0.15857605177993528, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6686472491909385, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.450589, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 103}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_177", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a thresholded differential-expression selection (all |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive) and the logarithm base is unspecified; the mechanism relies on relative ordering and coherence within the list, not on absolute fold-change magnitudes.", "The global positive shift of the RNA list is at least partly biological rather than entirely a normalization or cell-composition artifact; pathway claims are made only for sets whose mean exceeds the +1.39 background mean.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme capacity; lysosomal acidification, hydrolase activity, acyl-CoA levels, esterification flux, and all lipid pools are inferred, not measured in this dataset.", "ACSL4 and ACSL5 are assumed to represent a meaningful share of long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase capacity in these microglia; ACSL1, ACSL3, ACSL6 and SLC27A transporters are absent from the supplied list and could compensate.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are treated as ambiguous; no spot is assigned to a specific lipid enzyme.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipid and lipoprotein to both genotypes comparably, so the genotype difference reflects intracellular handling rather than differing supply.", "Causality is not established by these data; the ordering hydrolysis -\u003e lipid load -\u003e lipogenic response is a hypothesis, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally amplify a lysosomal acidification/hydrolase module together with an ER glycerolipid re-acylation and desaturation module, while long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts (ACSL4, ACSL5) move in the opposite direction; we propose that acyl-CoA-dependent re-esterification, not hydrolysis, is the rate-limiting step, so that fatty acids and lyso-species liberated by elevated membrane-lipid turnover are incompletely re-esterified and are instead disposed of through desaturation and mitochondrial oxidation, producing a lyso-lipid/MUFA-shifted membrane state that distinguishes APOE4 from APOE3.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: blocking upstream lysosomal hydrolysis in APOE4 microglia (v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1, or selective GBA inhibition with conduritol-B-epoxide) should lower the inferred fatty-acid/lyso-lipid load and specifically reduce the APOE4-versus-APOE3 excess of SREBF1, SCD, LPCAT1, MBOAT2 and AGPAT2 transcripts within 24-48 h; if these lipogenic/remodeling transcripts stay elevated in APOE4 after lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked, the demand-driven step 3 is wrong and the lipogenic arm is autonomous.", "Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a higher lysophosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylcholine and lysophosphatidylethanolamine/phosphatidylethanolamine ratio and a higher 16:1 and 18:1 fraction in phospholipids, without a proportionate increase in triacylglycerol; a finding of increased triacylglycerol with unchanged or reduced lyso-species would weaken the acyl-CoA-limited re-esterification bottleneck.", "Raising acyl-CoA supply in APOE4 cells (ACSL1 or ACSL4 overexpression, or medium-chain fatty acid supplementation that bypasses long-chain activation) should normalize the lyso-lipid ratio and reduce the SCD-dependent monounsaturation shift, whereas ACSL inhibition with triacsin C should exaggerate both in APOE4 more than in APOE3; equal responses in the two genotypes would weaken the claim that this node is genotype-limiting.", "Stable-isotope tracing (13C-glucose or 13C-acetate versus pre-labelled membrane lipid) should show that a larger fraction of newly esterified fatty acid in APOE4 derives from recycled membrane lipid rather than de novo synthesis; if de novo label dominates the APOE4 excess, a simpler SREBP1-driven lipogenesis model would replace this turnover-limited model.", "Direct enzymatic test: total long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase activity and steady-state long-chain acyl-CoA levels should be lower in APOE4 than APOE3 despite higher acyltransferase transcripts; unchanged or higher activity and acyl-CoA levels in APOE4 would falsify the proposed bottleneck while leaving the lysosomal-catabolism observation intact."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_177", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia express a coordinated lysosomal degradative program (v-ATPase subunits, cathepsins, and glycosidase/sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts, with TFEB also elevated); we infer, but did not measure, increased lysosomal acidification and increased hydrolytic capacity toward internalized and autophagic membrane lipid.", "Increased hydrolytic capacity is inferred to raise flux of membrane-derived products - free fatty acids, sphingoid bases, and lysophospholipids - out of the endolysosome toward the ER; none of these lipid pools was measured here.", "This lipid load is inferred to drive the observed ER remodeling/lipogenic transcript program (SREBF1, SCD, FADS1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, SOAT1), i.e. a demand-driven attempt to re-acylate lysophospholipids and to esterify free fatty acids into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester.", "Bottleneck: activation of free fatty acid to acyl-CoA is not co-induced; ACSL4 and ACSL5 transcripts are lower in APOE4 while every measured acyltransferase step is higher, so acyl-CoA supply is proposed to cap Lands-cycle re-acylation and neutral-lipid esterification flux.", "The predicted consequence is a partially unbuffered pool of unesterified fatty acid and lysophospholipid, with SCD-driven monounsaturation acting as the main available detoxification route, i.e. a membrane and lipid-droplet composition shift rather than a simple increase in total lipid.", "Excess fatty acid that cannot be esterified is inferred to be routed to mitochondrial oxidation, consistent with the strongly coherent up-shift of nuclear-encoded OXPHOS and beta-oxidation-associated transcripts (HADHA, ETFA); the resulting lyso-lipid/MUFA membrane state and lysosomal load are proposed to underlie APOE4-specific microglial phenotypes such as altered APOE, ABCA7, TREM2 and CD36 expression."], "title": "Lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism outruns acyl-CoA-dependent re-esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3462873389210944, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.11617431169078897, "cosine_similarity": 0.06009649268931138, "direction_accuracy": 0.36245954692556637, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_177", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7707216828478964, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3462873389210944, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.11617431169078897, "cosine_similarity": 0.06009649268931138, "direction_accuracy": 0.36245954692556637, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7707216828478964, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88631, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 442}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_120", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Median-centring the selected differential-expression list is a valid way to remove the global upward shift (77.1% of RNA rows positive); the reported log base is left unspecified and only relative, centred ranks are interpreted.", "Steady-state transcript differences for these enzymes and carriers track, at least in rank order, the corresponding protein and catalytic capacity in day-30 microglia; no protein measurement of MPC2, NNT, PRDX3 or G6PD is available here.", "Protein spots are mixtures: each spot is treated as a weighted candidate set, and no spot is taken as identification of a single protein.", "The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list, so set-level enrichment statistics are conditional on that selection and are not whole-transcriptome enrichment.", "The mock-treated APOE4/APOE3 comparison is isogenic and the astrocyte co-culture contributes similarly to both genotypes, so the differences reflect microglial genotype rather than co-culture composition.", "No metabolite, NADPH/NADP+, glutathione, oxygen-consumption or ROS measurement is supplied; all flux, localisation and redox-state statements are inferences."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a transcriptional program that raises mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA-cycle and malate-aspartate/NADH-shuttle capacity and respiratory-chain subunits while lowering committed glycolytic and oxidative pentose-phosphate/NAD-kinase transcripts, and that simultaneously raises mitochondrial thiol-peroxidase and transhydrogenase transcripts. We hypothesise that the resulting bottleneck is cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity: APOE4 cells are predicted to meet a higher matrix peroxide load using NNT- and TCA-derived NADPH feeding peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin cycles, so their peroxide-handling capacity becomes conditionally dependent on proton-motive force and substrate oxidation rather than on the pentose-phosphate pathway. Redox state, NADPH pools, peroxide production and all fluxes are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute inhibition of the oxidative pentose-phosphate pathway (G6PD inhibitor or 6-aminonicotinamide) should oxidise the cytosolic roGFP2-Grx1 probe and deplete GSH LESS in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia, whereas inhibiting respiration-coupled NADPH supply (NNT knockdown, or the MPC inhibitor UK5099, or low-dose rotenone/FCCP) should oxidise the mitochondrial roGFP2-Orp1 probe and slow an H2O2-bolus clearance curve MORE in APOE4 than APOE3. The reversed sensitivity ordering, i.e. APOE4 being more PPP-dependent and less NNT/MPC-dependent, would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Stable-isotope tracing with [1,2-13C]/[6-13C] glucose plus [U-13C]glutamine should show a lower fractional oxidative-PPP flux and a higher fraction of pyruvate carbon entering the TCA cycle in APOE4; equal PPP fractional flux and equal pyruvate oxidation would weaken the mechanism.", "Extracellular flux analysis should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and a lower ECAR/OCR ratio in APOE4, and the APOE4 spare respiratory capacity should be disproportionately consumed by an H2O2 or menadione challenge; absence of any OCR/ECAR genotype difference would weaken the mechanism.", "Redox western blotting should show more hyperoxidised/dimeric PRDX3 (and PRDX2) per unit total peroxiredoxin in APOE4 after a peroxide bolus despite equal or higher peroxiredoxin protein; equal peroxiredoxin oxidation kinetics would weaken step 4-5.", "Supplying NADPH-sparing or NADPH-generating support (cell-permeable methyl-succinate, or nicotinamide riboside, or GSH ethyl ester) should normalise APOE4 peroxide-clearance kinetics and reduce lipid-peroxidation reporter (C11-BODIPY) signal without normalising the TCA/glycolysis transcript pattern; if the transcript pattern is required to change for rescue, the ordering of steps 2-5 is wrong.", "Negative control specific to the assigned focus: peroxisomal beta-oxidation should NOT be a major contributor - catalase or ACOX1 knockdown should not differentially impair APOE4, consistent with gene:ACOX1 and gene:CROT sitting at or below the centred median and gene:ABCD1 being reduced; a strong APOE4-selective effect of ACOX1 loss would favour a peroxisomal rather than a mitochondrial-NADPH mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_120", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA: after centring on the strong global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list (median +1.46 in the reported log unit), transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate entry and TCA/shuttle steps are coordinately high (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACO2, gene:SLC25A46; set mean +4.33 above median, permutation p\u003c1e-4), together with respiratory-chain and fatty-acid-oxidation-linked transcripts (gene:NDUFA5, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA).", "Measured RNA, opposite direction: committed glycolytic and oxidative pentose-phosphate/NAD-kinase transcripts are relatively low (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:PGD, gene:TALDO1, gene:NADK, gene:NAMPT, gene:ME1; set mean -1.85 below median, permutation p=0.02). Inference (not measured): cytosolic NADPH and NAD(H) regeneration capacity per unit oxidative load is reduced.", "Inferred flux/localisation: carbon oxidation is redirected from cytosolic glycolysis into the matrix, increasing electron flux through complexes I-III and therefore the rate of matrix superoxide/H2O2 generation. Neither flux nor peroxide production is measured in this dataset.", "Measured RNA compensation: matrix and cytosolic thiol-peroxidase/reductase transcripts rise above the global shift (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:PRDX2, gene:TXNDC17, gene:SELENOW, gene:GPX4, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA; set mean +1.6, permutation p=0.03), as does the mitochondrial transhydrogenase gene:NNT. Protein-spot support is weak and non-unique: a catalase-candidate spot (protein_spot:017) and a PRDX2-candidate spot (protein_spot:077) are increased, but both spots contain other candidate genes.", "Inferred consequence: because NNT-derived NADPH is charged by the proton-motive force and matrix NADPH also depends on TCA dehydrogenase flux, peroxiredoxin re-reduction in APOE4 becomes coupled to respiration instead of to the pentose-phosphate pathway; this is an adaptation that maintains basal redox tone but narrows the reserve.", "Inferred lipid coupling: a lipogenic/desaturase-biased transcript pattern (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD) plus increased lipoprotein/lipid-uptake (gene:SCARB1) and lysosomal-catabolic transcripts (gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:TFEB) place an additional NADPH demand on the same limited cytosolic pool, while a lipid-peroxidation-protective transcript pattern (gene:GPX4 and gene:FTH1 up, gene:ACSL4 and gene:ALOX15 down) is the predicted signature of chronic, contained peroxide/lipid-peroxide pressure rather than of overt oxidative damage."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift reductant supply from the cytosolic pentose-phosphate pathway to respiration-coupled mitochondrial NADPH, making thiol-peroxide clearance dependent on oxidative phosphorylation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19421777498799986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15410527040284314, "cosine_similarity": 0.05938011354297151, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_120", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6926472491909385, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19421777498799986, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15410527040284314, "cosine_similarity": 0.05938011354297151, "direction_accuracy": 0.23624595469255663, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6926472491909385, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9571675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 443}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_018", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with a strong global positive shift and an unspecified logarithm base; all pathway claims are therefore made on within-dataset percentile ranks rather than on raw fold changes.", "Transcript abundance changes are assumed to produce proportional changes in mature lysosomal enzyme activity; this is unverified here and is contradicted in part by 2D-gel spots (protein_spot:067 down contains HEXB and CTSB among five candidates, protein_spot:069 down and protein_spot:053 up both contain CTSD), so spot data are treated as non-identifying.", "Key sphingolipid nodes were not measured in this dataset (ASAH1, PSAP, GM2A, GALC, ARSA, NEU1, SPTLC1/2, DEGS1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPHK1/2, S1P receptors); the ceramide-clearance and de novo arms are therefore inferred from absence of evidence, not from measurement.", "No lipid, enzyme-activity, membrane-order or trafficking measurement is present in the discovery data; ceramide accumulation, GM3 shift, membrane rigidity and routing defects are all predictions, not observations.", "APOE4 versus APOE3 is an isogenic genotype contrast in mock-treated 2D microglia co-cultured with astrocytes at day 30; astrocyte-derived lipid supply is not measured and could contribute to the same transcriptional state.", "Biological replicate number is not supplied in the workbook, so significance values cannot be independently assessed and the very large reported RNA effect sizes (up to +15.5) suggest low-depth or pseudobulk instability."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia show a coordinated, above-background increase in transcripts for lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic enzymes (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GBA2, GLA) together with TFEB and v-ATPase subunit transcripts, while the measured ceramide-consuming/glycosylating steps (B4GALT5, CERK, CERS6) are not co-induced and B4GALT5 is one of the few strongly down-shifted transcripts; we hypothesise that the resulting imbalance raises sphingomyelin- and glycosphingolipid-to-ceramide flux inside late endosomes/lysosomes faster than ceramide can be re-glycosylated, phosphorylated or exported, so ceramide (and GM3) accumulates on endolysosomal membranes and impairs vesicular routing. Only transcript and 2D-gel spot abundances were measured; enzyme activity, lipid pools, flux and localisation are inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted sphingolipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show an increased ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio with reduced LacCer and preserved or increased GM3; if ceramide is unchanged or lower, or if sphingomyelin rises, the ceramide-bottleneck claim fails.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pharmacological inhibition of acid sphingomyelinase plus glucocerebrosidase (functional ASM inhibitor plus conduritol-B-epoxide) should lower endolysosomal ceramide and rescue the APOE4 routing/lysosomal-morphology phenotype, whereas blocking de novo synthesis with myriocin should not; if myriocin normalises ceramide while catabolic-enzyme inhibition does not, the mechanism is wrong and a de novo-synthesis mechanism should replace it.", "Direct enzyme-activity assays on APOE4 lysates should show higher acid sphingomyelinase, GBA and beta-hexosaminidase specific activity than APOE3; unchanged activities despite elevated transcripts would break the measured-abundance-to-inferred-activity step.", "TFEB knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce SMPD1/GBA/HEXA transcripts and lower the ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio toward APOE3 values; a fall in hydrolase transcripts without any lipid change would weaken the causal chain between hydrolase capacity and lipid pools.", "Ectopic B4GALT5 expression (restoring LacCer synthase) in APOE4 microglia should partially normalise the ceramide/LacCer balance and retrograde M6PR-cargo trafficking; no lipid or trafficking change would argue that the down-shifted B4GALT5 is incidental.", "If instead the dominant APOE4 difference is mitochondrial (nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts mean percentile 71, p=0.0002, against mitochondrially encoded MT- transcripts mean percentile 28), then correcting mito-nuclear imbalance, not sphingolipid catabolism, should reverse the phenotype; this is the main competing explanation this hypothesis must outperform."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["MEASURED: transcripts of the lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases SMPD1 (+5.63), GBA (+6.71), HEXA (+5.68), HEXB (+2.17), GBA2 (+2.63) and GLA (+1.53) are elevated in APOE4 versus APOE3; after correcting for the strong global upward shift of these selected DE rows (median +1.46, 77% positive) this six-gene set sits at mean percentile 79.8 (permutation p=0.004 against all measured genes, p=0.024 against a 23-gene lysosomal background), i.e. it exceeds even the general lysosomal program (TFEB +2.38, ATP6V1A +4.23, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86).", "INFERRED (activity): the transcript increase is assumed to translate into higher acid sphingomyelinase, glucocerebrosidase and hexosaminidase catalytic capacity per lysosome, raising hydrolytic flux from sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipids toward ceramide in the acidic compartment.", "MEASURED: the steps that would consume or re-route that ceramide are not co-induced - B4GALT5 (LacCer synthase) is -1.88 (percentile 13), CERK +1.23 (percentile 38) and CERS6 +1.06 (percentile 27) are below the global background, while the salvage-type ceramide synthase CERS4 (+2.52) and the ganglioside branch ST3GAL5 (+2.17) and the glycolipid-transfer protein GLTP (+2.38) are modestly up; de novo synthesis genes as a group are not enriched (mean percentile 48, p=0.57).", "INFERRED (flux/pool, primary bottleneck): ceramide disposal downstream of lysosomal hydrolysis becomes rate-limiting, so ceramide is predicted to accumulate on late-endosomal/lysosomal membranes and, via ST3GAL5 with reduced LacCer synthase, shift the residual glycosphingolipid pool toward GM3 rather than complex glycosphingolipids.", "INFERRED (localisation/routing): ceramide-enriched, rigidified endolysosomal membranes favour intraluminal-vesicle budding and impede retrograde and recycling traffic; transcript proxies consistent with an altered routing state are M6PR -1.72, OSBPL8 -1.90 and SYNJ1 -2.43 against elevated SNX3 (+3.95), VPS26A (+4.86) and RAB7A (+2.65), but no trafficking assay was performed.", "CONSEQUENCE: the APOE4-specific mock state is predicted to be a ceramide-high, sphingomyelin-low, LacCer-low endolysosomal lipid configuration maintained by a TFEB-associated transcriptional loop, rather than by increased de novo sphingoid-base synthesis."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis without matching ceramide-disposal capacity, creating a ceramide-loaded late-endosome/lysosome bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.02376372095932068, "cosine_similarity": 0.056977757969375466, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6963268608414239, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1990639884798582, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.02376372095932068, "cosine_similarity": 0.056977757969375466, "direction_accuracy": 0.13754045307443366, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6963268608414239, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84306975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 444}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_060", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and an overall positive shift (mean +1.39, 77.1% positive); all pathway statements are made relative to that internal background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for protein abundance only where no protein measurement exists; assembled-complex stoichiometry, superoxide production, peroxidase flux, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, glutathione redox state, lipid-droplet content and lysosomal flux are all unmeasured here.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes; PRDX2-, BLVRA-, TALDO1-, CAT- and cathepsin-linked spots are treated as ambiguous corroboration only, never as identified proteins.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript levels from a probe-based single-cell assay are assumed to reflect genuine mitochondrial transcript differences rather than probe-panel or ambient-RNA artefacts; only six MT- rows are available.", "The cultures are microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, so some differences (e.g. the very high S100B row) may reflect cell-composition rather than cell-intrinsic microglial state.", "Peroxisomal metabolism is assumed to be a secondary, not primary, node because only three peroxisome-related rows exist (ABCD1 negative, ACOX1 below the set median, SCP2 positive) with no PEX or catalase transcript rows."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and mitochondrial-import transcripts are coordinately elevated while most mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts are relatively reduced; we hypothesise that this mitonuclear imbalance, not increased peroxisomal beta-oxidation, is the rate-limiting step, producing assembly-limited complexes III/IV/V, increased matrix electron leak and superoxide production, an inferred rise in peroxiredoxin/glutathione-dependent matrix redox buffering with DELE1-linked stress signalling, and a compensatory shift of fatty acids into MUFA-enriched neutral-lipid stores that limits polyunsaturated-lipid peroxidation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating assembly test: blue-native PAGE/complexome profiling plus ddPCR of mtDNA copy number and mt-transcripts in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show lower assembled complex IV and V (and free nuclear-subunit subassemblies) per unit nuclear subunit protein in APOE4, with reduced MT-ATP6/MT-CYB transcript per mtDNA copy. Normal assembled-complex stoichiometry and normal mt-transcript levels would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Redox test: MitoSOX/mito-roGFP2-Orp1 and mitochondrial NADPH/NADP+ measurement should show higher basal matrix oxidation in APOE4; unchanged matrix oxidation despite the transcript pattern would weaken steps 2-3.", "Causal rescue: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ or mitoTEMPO), but not equimolar untargeted N-acetylcysteine, should lower DELE1/DDIT3/PRDX3 transcripts and reduce BODIPY-493 neutral-lipid and C11-BODIPY oxidised-lipid signal in APOE4 towards APOE3 levels; if lipid-droplet content is unchanged by mitochondrial ROS scavenging, the mitochondria-to-lipid link is broken.", "Substrate-diversion test: SCD inhibition (CAY10566) should raise C11-BODIPY lipid peroxidation and death selectively in APOE4; equal sensitivity in APOE3 would weaken step 5. Conversely, ACSL4 re-expression should reintroduce PUFA-CoA-dependent peroxidation preferentially in APOE4.", "Alternative-mechanism test: if instead APOE4 cells accumulate C26:0/C24:0 very-long-chain fatty acids with reduced peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux and normal mitochondrial superoxide, the peroxisomal (ABCD1-loss) explanation supersedes this hypothesis.", "Genotype-dose test: an APOE knockout or APOE4-to-APOE3 gene-corrected line should shift the nuclear-OXPHOS-up/mtDNA-down transcript ratio and the lipid-droplet phenotype in parallel; dissociation of the two (one normalised, the other not) would argue that they are independent consequences of genotype rather than steps in one chain."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred stoichiometry): APOE4 microglia raise nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit and mitochondrial protein-import transcripts (38/38 nuclear OXPHOS rows positive, median approx. +2.62 in the reported log unit; TOMM22, TIMM8B, TIMM44 positive), whereas 4 of 6 mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are negative against a background in which only 22.9% of rows are negative. The resulting subunit stoichiometry is inferred, not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred activity, unmeasured): Shortfall of mtDNA-encoded core subunits relative to imported nuclear subunits limits assembly of complexes III/IV/V, prolongs residence of reduced electron carriers in complexes I and III, and increases univalent electron leak to superoxide. No ROS, membrane-potential, respirometry or assembled-complex measurement is supplied.", "Step 3 (measured RNA/protein-spot abundance, inferred flux): Matrix and cytosolic thiol-peroxidase and iron-sequestration transcripts rise above the global shift (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS, NNT, FTH1; set mean +2.74 vs global mean +1.39, permutation p approx. 0.055), and a PRDX2-candidate protein spot plus BLVRA/TALDO1-candidate spots increase; spot identities are ambiguous, so increased peroxidase and NADPH-regenerating flux remains inferred.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred signalling): Mitochondrial stress relay and apoptotic-priming transcripts increase (DELE1 at the 93rd percentile, DDIT3, BAX, BID, APAF1), consistent with an integrated stress response emanating from dysfunctional mitochondria rather than from a general chaperone/proteasome program (chaperone and proteasome sets are not enriched).", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid flux): Peroxidation-prone substrate supply is reduced (ACSL4 and ALOX15 in the lowest ~11% and ~4% of rows) while monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis and esterification rise (SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SLC25A1, ACSS2, GPAT4), predicting diversion of fatty acids into MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol/lipid droplets.", "Step 6 (measured RNA/spots, inferred load): Lysosomal hydrolase transcripts rise coherently (set mean +2.88, permutation p approx. 0.006; GBA, SMPD1, TFEB), consistent with increased turnover of the stored and oxidised lipid load; cathepsin-candidate spots move in both directions, so lysosomal proteolytic capacity is not resolved."], "title": "Mitonuclear OXPHOS stoichiometry imbalance as the bottleneck driving a matrix-redox stress and anti-peroxidation lipid-storage state in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24959384115496805, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11784435970565718, "cosine_similarity": 0.05378246622207244, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_060", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6814660194174758, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24959384115496805, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11784435970565718, "cosine_similarity": 0.05378246622207244, "direction_accuracy": 0.2087378640776699, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6814660194174758, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.02286825, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 445}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_057", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an |effect| \u003e= 1 selection floor, so only rank position within this biased, upward-shifted set (not raw sign or magnitude) is treated as evidence of pathway-specific regulation; the logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is left unconverted.", "Transcript rank differences for SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1/MBOAT and the ACSL isoforms translate into proportional changes in the corresponding enzyme activities and lipid fluxes; no enzyme activity, protein-level or lipid-species measurement of these nodes is supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (median 5) and are not uniquely identified proteins; cathepsin- and annexin-containing spots are treated only as weak, non-attributable and internally inconsistent corroboration of altered lysosomal/membrane-associated protein content.", "SCD, not AGPAT2 or LPCAT1, is assumed to be the flux-limiting node because the downstream acyltransferase capacity is co-elevated while the desaturation step gates usable MUFA-CoA; this ordering is an assumption, not a measurement.", "The astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein lipid whose delivery differs between genotypes only through the measured uptake/catabolic machinery, and the mock condition reflects a steady state rather than a transient at day 30.", "Number of biological replicates is not supplied, so the reported adjusted p-values are taken at face value and no independent assessment of statistical power or pseudoreplication is possible."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia raise endolysosomal membrane-lipid catabolic capacity (cathepsins, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, v-ATPase subunits, TFEB) while transcriptionally lowering the measured long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases (ACSL4, ACSL5) that would re-activate salvaged fatty acids; the cell therefore depends on an SREBF1/SCD/ACSS2-driven de novo monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply routed through AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1 and the LPCAT1/MBOAT1/MBOAT2 re-acylation arm, so SCD-derived MUFA-CoA becomes the rate-limiting input that sets a MUFA-biased, PUFA-poor glycerolipid pool rather than restoration of the original membrane acyl composition. Causality is not established by these data; the mechanism is inferred from transcript ranks plus ambiguous protein-spot data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) or SCD knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the genotype difference in the lipid desaturation index (16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0 in phosphatidylcholine and triacylglycerol) and reduce APOE4-specific neutral-lipid accumulation, while adding exogenous oleate should rescue that reduction. If SCD inhibition lowers desaturation index equally in APOE4 and APOE3 without shrinking the genotype gap in esterified lipid, or if oleate fails to rescue, the SCD-bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a MUFA-shifted, PUFA-depleted phosphatidylcholine and TAG acyl profile with elevated lysophosphatidylcholine and elevated sphingomyelin-derived ceramide; a lipidome that is PUFA-enriched or acyl-composition-neutral would weaken the mechanism.", "Stable-isotope tracing should show a higher fraction of APOE4 glycerolipid acyl chains derived from 13C-acetate/de novo synthesis and a lower fraction derived from 13C-labelled exogenous palmitate or arachidonate salvage; equal salvage fractions between genotypes would falsify the ACSL-limited salvage step.", "Re-expression of ACSL4 (or ACSL5) in APOE4 microglia should restore PUFA incorporation into phospholipid and reduce dependence on SCD-derived MUFA, partially normalizing the lipid profile without normalizing lysosomal hydrolase transcripts; if ACSL re-expression instead normalizes the whole program including hydrolase transcripts, the causal ordering placing catabolism upstream is wrong.", "Blocking upstream catabolic input (v-ATPase inhibition with bafilomycin A1, acid sphingomyelinase inhibition, or SCARB1 blockade) should reduce the APOE4-specific induction of SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 at the transcript and lipid-flux level; unchanged SCD/AGPAT2 induction would indicate the lipogenic arm is driven independently, for example by a genotype-intrinsic SREBP-1 setpoint rather than by membrane turnover.", "Single-cell or bulk re-measurement of the unmeasured salvage/oxidation nodes (ACSL1, ACSL3, CPT1A, PLA2G4A, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, PLIN2, LIPA) should show that no compensating acyl-CoA synthetase is up-ranked in APOE4; finding ACSL1 or ACSL3 strongly elevated would remove the proposed re-activation bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): relative to the globally upward-shifted RNA background of this selected differential-expression set (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.459 in the reported, unspecified log base), a lysosomal/endolysosomal catabolic module sits in the upper tail (CTSK, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB at rank percentiles 95-99; module median percentile 70.8, permutation p=0.022), together with the lipid/lipoprotein receptor SCARB1 (percentile 99) and TFEB.", "Step 2 (inferred flux, not measured): higher hydrolase and v-ATPase transcript capacity is taken to increase acid-dependent turnover of internalized and autophagic membrane lipid, liberating free fatty acids, lysophospholipids, ceramide and sphingoid bases inside the lysosome. No lipid species, no hydrolase activity assay and no acidification measurement is supplied, so this flux step is an inference.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, direction against background): reuse of these liberated fatty acids requires re-activation to acyl-CoA, and the only two ACSL isoforms present in the data are strong low-tail outliers against the upward background (ACSL5 -3.115, percentile 5.3; ACSL4 -2.142, percentile 10.6). ACSL1 and ACSL3 are not measured, so the inference is a reduced, not abolished, salvage/PUFA re-activation capacity.", "Step 4 (inferred bottleneck): with salvage re-activation constrained, glycerolipid and phospholipid synthesis must draw on de novo acyl-CoA. SREBF1 (+4.67, percentile 92), SCD (+4.169, percentile 89) and ACSS2 (+2.935, percentile 77) form the supply arm; SCD-generated 16:1/18:1-CoA is proposed as the flux-limiting input because de novo saturated acyl-CoA must be desaturated before efficient esterification.", "Step 5 (measured capacity downstream): the acceptor machinery is present and high-ranking - AGPAT2 (+6.285, percentile 97), GPAT4, DGAT1 and CHPT1 for the phosphatidic-acid/DAG/TAG/PC arm, and LPCAT1 (+3.070), MBOAT2 (+3.260), MBOAT1 (+2.645) for Lands-cycle re-acylation of lysophospholipids; the combined SREBF1-MUFA-esterification module median percentile is 76.8 (permutation p=0.024).", "Step 6 (inferred lipidome and cell state, not measured): the predicted consequence is a MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor phosphatidylcholine and neutral-lipid pool with residual lysophospholipid, i.e. membrane acyl composition is remodeled rather than restored during turnover, which is proposed to alter lysosomal membrane properties and degradative throughput in APOE4 microglia."], "title": "SCD-dependent monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply is the bottleneck coupling elevated lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism to re-esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3221024258760108, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.024368704839213627, "cosine_similarity": 0.05134866579532171, "direction_accuracy": 0.2977346278317152, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7438187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3221024258760108, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.024368704839213627, "cosine_similarity": 0.05134866579532171, "direction_accuracy": 0.2977346278317152, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7438187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72079575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 446}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_093", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global upward skew (77.1% positive, median +1.46), so only enrichment relative to that list background, not absolute direction, is interpreted as pathway-specific.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes up to +15.5 with an unstated replicate number are treated as ranks, not as quantitative fold changes.", "Gene-set membership is curated by the analyst from background knowledge (unverified, no database or literature retrieval was permitted), so set boundaries, and therefore the enrichment p-values, are analyst-dependent and are not corrected for the number of sets examined.", "Increased hydrolase and V-ATPase transcript is assumed to reflect increased enzyme synthesis potential; enzyme activity, lysosomal pH, proteolytic maturation and organelle number were not measured and are inferred.", "Protein spots are assumed to be mixtures: each carries a mean of 4.8 candidate genes, so no spot is treated as identifying a specific protein, and spot direction is used only as weak corroborating or contradicting texture.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype effects are assumed to include non-cell-autonomous contributions (astrocytic APOE) that this design cannot separate.", "The APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed isogenic as stated, so the transcriptional differences are attributed to genotype rather than line background; no causal test is claimed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly in the balance of endolysosomal modules rather than in total lysosome content: transcripts for lumenal acid hydrolases (glycosidases, sphingolipid hydrolases and cathepsins) and for V-ATPase subunits are coordinately elevated above the strong global upward shift of this differential-expression list, together with the CLEAR-network regulators TFEB and MITF, whereas transcripts for lysosomal membrane transport, cargo delivery and autophagosome-lysosome fusion components are not (median +1.28 vs +2.17; hydrolase \u003e membrane one-sided Mann-Whitney p = 6.6e-3). We propose that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is post-hydrolytic export/handoff of lipid catabolites (principally unesterified sterol) out of the endolysosome, not the supply of hydrolytic enzyme; the hydrolase and V-ATPase induction is a compensatory CLEAR-type response that does not restore flux, and the resulting failure of lysosome-derived sterol to reach the ER sensor keeps SREBP-driven uptake and synthesis transcripts elevated, creating a futile loading cycle. All abundance statements refer to measured RNA log fold changes in an unspecified logarithm base; degradative flux, lysosomal pH, cargo localization, sterol pools and causal direction are inferred and were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation (primary): treat both genotypes with 2-hydroxypropyl-beta-cyclodextrin (which bypasses lysosomal sterol egress) versus TFEB overexpression or torin-1 (which amplify the hydrolase/CLEAR arm). If the bottleneck is export, cyclodextrin should normalize APOE4 SREBP target transcripts (LDLR, HMGCS1, DHCR7, DHCR24) and lysosomal cholesterol toward APOE3 while TFEB overexpression does not; if instead TFEB overexpression alone normalizes them and cyclodextrin does not, the bottleneck is hydrolytic capacity and this mechanism is wrong.", "Pulse-chase flux discrimination: with DQ-BSA or fluorogenic cathepsin substrates, the initial intralysosomal hydrolysis rate in APOE4 should be equal to or greater than APOE3, while transfer of BODIPY-cholesteryl-ester label from LAMP1+ compartments into the ER/ACAT-esterified pool should be delayed. A reduced initial DQ-BSA dequenching rate in APOE4 would place the defect upstream at hydrolysis and weaken the mechanism.", "Imaging: filipin-positive unesterified cholesterol and LysoTracker signal within LAMP1+ compartments should be higher in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions despite higher hydrolase transcript. Equal or lower lysosomal cholesterol in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Acidification control: steady-state lysosomal pH (ratiometric LysoSensor or pHrodo-dextran) should be comparable between genotypes, since all measured V-ATPase subunit transcripts are up. A substantially more alkaline APOE4 lysosome would relocate the bottleneck to acidification and weaken step 3 as written.", "Protein-level test of the transcript-protein mismatch: immunoblot and activity assay for cathepsin D/B and beta-hexosaminidase should show total mature enzyme and activity increased far less than the corresponding transcripts (gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB), with a shifted pro-form to mature-form ratio. Enzyme protein and activity rising in proportion to transcript would weaken the claim that hydrolase supply is not limiting.", "Rescue specificity: restoring the lagging arm (STX17 or M6PR re-expression, or enhancing lysosome-ER contact-site sterol transfer) should increase degradative flux in APOE4 more than in APOE3. Equal or greater benefit in APOE3 would argue the mismatch is not genotype-specific.", "Independent-cohort transcriptional test: in a second isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia dataset analysed with the same list-background correction, the lumenal hydrolase set should again rank above the lysosomal membrane/fusion set. Loss of that ordering would indicate the present separation reflects analyst set curation or the global shift rather than biology."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (inferred load, weakly supported): APOE4 microglia present an increased lipid/lipoprotein cargo burden to the endolysosome. Only transcripts of uptake and lipid-handling machinery are measured (gene:APOE, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2); the cargo pool itself, and any change in uptake rate, are not measured, and the broader phagocytic-receptor set sits exactly at the list background, so this step is the weakest link in the chain.", "Step 2 (measured RNA): A CLEAR/TFEB-type transcriptional module is engaged. gene:TFEB and gene:MITF are up, and lumenal acid hydrolase transcripts are enriched above the global list shift (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:CTSK, gene:NAGLU, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:DPP7, gene:CTSD, gene:HEXB, gene:MAN2B1, gene:AGA, gene:GLA, gene:SGSH; set median +2.17 vs list median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p = 5.8e-3). All eight measured V-ATPase subunits are up (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:ATP6V1E1). Elevated transcript is treated as increased enzyme synthesis potential, not as demonstrated hydrolase activity or acidification.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, the proposed bottleneck): The module that must move cargo in and catabolites out does not scale with the hydrolase module. Lysosomal membrane, transporter, tether and fusion transcripts have a markedly lower median (+1.28) than the hydrolase set (+2.17), and several fall below the list background or below zero: gene:STX17 (autophagosome-lysosome fusion), gene:M6PR (hydrolase sorting receptor), gene:LAPTM5, with only modest increases in gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:CLN3. We infer, but did not measure, that catabolite egress and cargo delivery are therefore rate-limiting relative to hydrolysis.", "Step 4 (inferred flux and localization): Consequently, sterol and sphingolipid catabolites liberated inside the endolysosome accumulate in the lumenal/limiting-membrane pool and are delivered inefficiently to the ER. No sterol, sphingolipid, pH or organelle-morphology measurement is supplied; this step is a prediction, not an observation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, directionally consistent only): The ER sterol sensor behaves as if cholesterol-deficient. SREBP pathway and downstream synthesis/uptake transcripts are elevated (gene:SREBF2, gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:LSS, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD), alongside esterification and storage genes (gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1). Because this set is not enriched relative to the global upward shift of the list, it corroborates rather than establishes the export block.", "Step 6 (inferred network consequence): Continued SREBP-driven uptake and synthesis returns lipid to an already export-limited compartment, so lysosomal degradative flux per unit cargo falls even though hydrolase transcript rises. Protein-level data do not show a matching expansion of the hydrolytic pool: spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins and other lysosomal enzymes run in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:027 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069, protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065 down), which is compatible with redistribution of processing forms rather than net accumulation, but the spots carry ~5 candidate genes each and cannot identify any single protein."], "title": "Export-limited endolysosome in APOE4 microglia: hydrolase/CLEAR arm scales up while the lysosomal membrane transport-and-fusion arm does not, stranding sterol catabolites away from the ER sensing pool"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06555772994129158, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.07519425095027944, "cosine_similarity": 0.0472074793339438, "direction_accuracy": 0.10841423948220065, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_093", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434627831715211, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06555772994129158, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.07519425095027944, "cosine_similarity": 0.0472074793339438, "direction_accuracy": 0.10841423948220065, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6434627831715211, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.896308, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 447}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_051", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; all pathway statements are made relative to the list's own strong positive shift (median +1.46) rather than to zero, and the logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and preserved as given.", "Transcript abundance is used only as a proxy for protein/complex abundance; no respiration, ROS, mtDNA copy number, membrane potential, complex-assembly, metabolite or lipid measurement is supplied, so flux, assembly state, localisation and ROS are inferred.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; assigning protein_spot:017 to catalase and protein_spot:077 to PRDX2 is provisional, and their candidate lists also contain unrelated proteins (CORO1C/ENTPD5; keratins, ACTB, RAB1A).", "The four decreased MT- transcripts are assumed to reflect genotype biology rather than differences in ambient RNA, mitochondrial-read fraction, dissociation stress or per-cell normalisation between the APOE4 and APOE3 10X Flex libraries; this assumption is the weakest link in the chain.", "Astrocyte co-culture contributions and replicate structure (not supplied in the workbook) are assumed not to be the dominant source of the genotype contrast."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) carry a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (TCA enzymes, mitochondrial carriers, import machinery, complex I/III/IV/V subunits) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts; we hypothesise that the resulting stoichiometric bottleneck in assembled electron-transport complexes increases electron leak relative to matrix peroxide-clearance capacity, so APOE4 microglia sit in a chronic mitochondrial-redox/integrated-stress-response state (elevated DELE1, EIF2AK3, DDIT3 transcripts; elevated peroxiredoxin/GPX4/NNT/ferritin transcripts and catalase- and PRDX2-containing protein spots), with compensatory lysosomal hydrolase induction and loss of several myeloid effector transcripts. Only abundances were measured; flux, assembly, ROS and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring mitochondrial-genome output in APOE4 microglia (TFAM or POLRMT overexpression, or NAD+ precursor supplementation sufficient to raise mtDNA-encoded transcripts/proteins) should raise assembled complex IV/V activity and lower DDIT3, DELE1 and peroxiredoxin transcripts and mitochondrial superoxide (MitoSOX); if mtDNA-encoded subunits are restored yet ISR and redox markers are unchanged, the mitonuclear bottleneck is not the driver.", "Epistasis test: ISRIB or HRI (EIF2AK1) inhibition should suppress DDIT3 induction while leaving the nuclear/mtDNA subunit-transcript ratio and mitochondrial superoxide unchanged, placing the ISR downstream; if ISRIB also normalises the mitochondrial transcript imbalance and ROS, the proposed direction is wrong.", "Direct measurement: blue-native PAGE / respirometry should show that APOE4 respiratory capacity and assembled complex I/IV/V levels are NOT increased in proportion to the ~1.3-log excess in nuclear subunit transcripts, with reduced spare respiratory capacity and elevated H2O2 efflux; proportional or greater increases in assembled complexes with normal ROS would refute the bottleneck.", "Redox dependence: matrix-targeted antioxidants (MitoQ, mitoTEMPO) or PRDX3 overexpression should reduce DELE1/DDIT3 transcripts and the lysosomal hydrolase elevation in APOE4 microglia, whereas cytosolic-only antioxidant or catalase overexpression should be markedly less effective; equal efficacy of cytosolic scavenging would argue for a non-mitochondrial ROS source.", "Specificity control: the same nuclear-mito/mtDNA transcript imbalance and DELE1/DDIT3 elevation should be reproduced in an independent isogenic APOE4 line and abolished by APOE4-to-APOE3 gene correction; persistence after correction would attribute the signature to clone or culture effects rather than APOE genotype.", "Protein-identity control: targeted immunoblot/PRM should confirm that the increased protein_spot:017 and protein_spot:077 signals correspond to catalase and PRDX2 rather than to co-migrating keratin/actin/coronin candidates; failure to confirm removes the only protein-level support for the antioxidant arm."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: relative to the strong global positive shift of this selected DE list (median +1.46 in the reported, unspecified-base log units), 71 nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcripts (NDUF*, ATP5*, COX*, UQCR*, SDHB, MDH1, ACO2, OGDH, DLD, IDH3B, MPC2, GLUD1, SLC25A family, TOMM22/TIMM44/TIMM8B, TUFM) are further elevated in APOE4 (median +2.80, permutation p \u003c 5e-5, 28% of the set in the global top decile).", "Measured, weaker and technically fragile: four of six mtDNA-encoded transcripts are reduced (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33) while MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L are increased, i.e. no matched increase of the mtDNA-encoded core subunits that partner the up-regulated nuclear subunits.", "Inferred (not measured): the mismatch between nuclear-encoded and mtDNA-encoded subunit supply limits assembly/turnover of complexes I, III, IV and V, so respiratory capacity rises less than the nuclear transcript program predicts and reduced upstream carriers increase univalent electron leak to superoxide.", "Inferred with abundance support: matrix peroxide clearance becomes the limiting step (primary bottleneck). Antioxidant/NADPH-linked transcripts are elevated above the global shift (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX2 +4.41, TXNDC17 +7.10, GPX4 +2.79, NNT +2.88, PRDX5 +1.96, FTH1 +2.53; set median +2.88, permutation p = 0.06), and protein spots whose candidate lists include catalase (protein_spot:017) and PRDX2 (protein_spot:077) are significantly increased.", "Inferred signalling consequence: chronic inner-membrane stress engages the OMA1-DELE1-HRI arm of the integrated stress response, consistent with elevated DELE1 (+4.82), EIF2AK3 (+1.51) and DDIT3/CHOP (+2.79) transcripts and elevated mitochondrial chaperone/one-carbon transcripts (HSPA9 +2.35, SHMT2 +2.22); OMA1 protease activity is set by proteolytic activation, not by its transcript level (OMA1 RNA -1.39).", "Downstream cell-state consequence: APOE4 microglia raise lysosomal hydrolase and TFEB transcripts (GAA +9.96, SLC38A7 +7.46, CTSK +7.36, GBA +6.72, HEXA +5.71, SMPD1 +5.63, CTSB +5.49, CTSD +2.87, TFEB +2.43), consistent with increased degradative/mitophagic demand, while several myeloid effector transcripts fall far below the global up-shift (CTSS -5.57, CSF1 -5.91, SPN -7.26, SEMA4A -5.23, ARHGAP30 -5.16), i.e. an ISR/redox-biased rather than effector-biased microglial state."], "title": "Mitonuclear imbalance in APOE4 microglia: an expanded nuclear-encoded oxidative program outruns mtDNA-encoded ETC subunits and matrix redox buffering, engaging a DELE1/ISR state"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21828268655614222, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05053582088637619, "cosine_similarity": 0.03959365634321045, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_051", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7032297734627831, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.21828268655614222, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05053582088637619, "cosine_similarity": 0.03959365634321045, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7032297734627831, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9161505, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 448}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_064", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway claims are therefore made only as rank/permutation comparisons against the list's own strongly positive background (median +1.46, 1705/2212 positive), and absolute up-regulation of any single set is not asserted.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and some magnitudes are implausibly large for log2; effect sizes are treated as ordinal/directional, not as literal fold changes.", "Steady-state transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for the corresponding protein and enzymatic capacity; no metabolite, tracer, oxygen-consumption, extracellular-acidification, mtDNA-copy-number or phospho-PDH measurement is supplied, so all flux, activity, localization and assembly statements are inferences.", "MPC2 transcript increase is assumed to indicate increased functional MPC1/MPC2 heterodimer; MPC1 is not in the supplied list.", "The mtDNA-encoded decrease is assumed to be biological rather than a 10X Flex ambient-RNA, probe-capture or QC-filtering artefact; only 6 mtDNA genes are present and 2 of them move upward, so this step is the weakest link.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and frequently include keratin/actin contaminants; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spots are used only as non-discriminating context.", "Differences are assumed to be at least partly cell-intrinsic to APOE4 microglia rather than solely a consequence of altered astrocyte co-culture cross-feeding or of a shifted microglial subpopulation composition in the isogenic lines.", "Causality is assumed nowhere: the APOE4/APOE3 comparison is observational and the ordering of steps is a hypothesis to be tested by perturbation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 by a coordinated carbon-routing shift: transcripts for the inducible high-flux upper-glycolytic isoenzymes HK2 and PFKP are among the strongest decreases, while glucose/monocarboxylate transporters, the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier MPC2, the PDH-activating phosphatase PDP1, the E3 subunit DLD, TCA-cycle and malate-aspartate/citrate carrier transcripts, and nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits are coordinately higher than the strongly upward-shifted background of this selected differential-expression list. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting node (bottleneck) is glucose commitment at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase: APOE4 microglia can still import glucose but cannot rapidly expand glycolytic flux, and therefore depend on mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate and of alternative substrates (acetate/ketone/glutamate/fatty acyl carbon, inferred from ACSS2, OXCT1, GLUD1, GLS, HADHA transcripts) for ATP. Because mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) move in the opposite direction to the nuclear-encoded accessory subunits, the extra oxidative demand is predicted to be served by stoichiometrically mismatched respiratory complexes, leaving APOE4 microglia with low glycolytic reserve and limited spare respiratory capacity. All statements about flux, enzyme activity, complex assembly and causal direction are inferences from steady-state RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown in mock-treated isogenic microglia should reduce basal and ATP-linked oxygen consumption, and reduce ATP/phagocytic capacity, significantly more in APOE4 than in APOE3. If APOE4 and APOE3 show equal or smaller APOE4 sensitivity to UK5099/MPC2 knockdown, the pyruvate-routing step and the whole mechanism are weakened.", "Uniformly labelled glucose tracing should show lower fractional lactate labelling and lactate secretion but higher glucose-derived M+2 citrate/glutamate labelling in APOE4 versus APOE3. Equal or higher lactate output together with no increase in glucose carbon entering the TCA cycle would falsify the carbon-rerouting claim.", "A glycolytic stress test should show reduced glycolytic reserve (oligomycin-stimulated extracellular acidification) in APOE4; re-expression of HK2 (or PFKP) in APOE4 microglia should restore glycolytic reserve and reduce dependence on MPC. Preserved or greater APOE4 glycolytic reserve, or no rescue by HK2 re-expression, would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Blue-native PAGE or in-gel activity assays normalised to mitochondrial mass (citrate synthase activity or TOMM20 protein) should show that assembled complex I/III/IV/V and spare respiratory capacity are NOT increased in APOE4 in proportion to the nuclear subunit transcript increase, with accumulation of nuclear-encoded subassemblies. If assembled complexes and spare respiratory capacity scale up with the nuclear transcripts, the mitonuclear-mismatch step is falsified even if the substrate-routing steps survive.", "Independent, non-10X quantification (RT-qPCR or long-read RNA on the same lines) of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB/MT-CO2 plus mtDNA copy number should reproduce a lower mtDNA-encoded transcript-to-nuclear-OXPHOS-transcript ratio in APOE4. Reproducing equal ratios would indicate the mtDNA signal is technical and would remove that step.", "Substrate-restriction test: in glucose-free medium supplied with pyruvate, acetate or beta-hydroxybutyrate, APOE4 microglia should maintain ATP and viability at least as well as APOE3 (relative advantage), whereas in medium where oxidative phosphorylation is blocked (oligomycin) and only glucose is available, APOE4 should fail earlier than APOE3. The opposite pattern would falsify the obligate-oxidation claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: glucose/monocarboxylate transporter transcripts are higher in APOE4 (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73, gene:SLC16A1 +1.12), so substrate entry across the plasma membrane is inferred not to be limiting.", "Measured and proposed bottleneck: the inducible upper-glycolytic isoenzymes are lower in APOE4 (gene:HK2 -3.67, padj 8e-191; gene:PFKP -3.08; gene:HK3 -1.12) against a list whose median change is +1.46, whereas only the non-inducible/other isoforms and downstream steps present in the list are higher (gene:PFKM +2.41, gene:GPI +2.06, gene:ENO1 +2.17). We infer reduced maximal glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-1,6-bisphosphate generating capacity, i.e. reduced glycolytic reserve rather than absent glycolysis; HK2/PFKP protein and glycolytic flux were not measured.", "Measured: transcripts routing pyruvate and its carbon into the matrix and through the TCA cycle are strongly increased (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:IDH3B +2.02, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:SDHB +1.65), together with malate-aspartate and citrate carriers (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13 +1.75, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47) and the adenine-nucleotide carrier gene:SLC25A5 +5.56. Inferred, not measured: higher pyruvate import, higher PDH activity (via PDP1-mediated dephosphorylation), higher cytosol-to-matrix reducing-equivalent transfer.", "Measured: transcripts for non-glucose carbon entry are also higher (gene:ACSS2 +2.93 acetate, gene:OXCT1 +4.72 ketone body, gene:GLUD1 +3.17 and gene:GLS +1.35 glutamine/glutamate, gene:HADHA +2.86 beta-oxidation). Inferred: APOE4 microglia broaden their catabolic substrate use to sustain the TCA cycle when glycolytic commitment is restricted; no metabolite or tracer data are supplied.", "Measured: nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunit and import/translation transcripts are coordinately higher than background (40-gene set median +2.64 vs +1.46, permutation P=0.0008; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:NDUFS8 +4.93, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX7A2 +3.36, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TIMM44 +2.46, gene:TUFM +6.46). Inferred: attempted expansion of respiratory-chain and import capacity, not a measurement of assembled complexes or of respiration.", "Measured, opposite direction: mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts are mostly lower (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; but gene:MT-ND5 +1.93 and gene:MT-ND4L +1.95 are higher; 6-gene median -1.56, permutation P=0.015). Inferred: a mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch that caps assembled complex I/III/IV/V per unit of nuclear subunit supply.", "Predicted consequence: APOE4 microglia sit in an oxidation-dependent, low-glycolytic-reserve state with limited spare respiratory capacity, making them disproportionately sensitive to MPC or ETC inhibition and unable to execute rapid glycolytic bursts; associated redox/antioxidant transcripts (gene:NNT +2.88) are consistent with, but do not demonstrate, increased matrix redox load."], "title": "Loss of inducible upper-glycolytic capacity (HK2/PFKP) forces APOE4 microglia into obligate mitochondrial pyruvate oxidation with mismatched ETC subunit supply"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.033268101761252444, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0589619918918539, "cosine_similarity": 0.030596939017818944, "direction_accuracy": 0.05663430420711974, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_064", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6398252427184465, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.033268101761252444, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0589619918918539, "cosine_similarity": 0.030596939017818944, "direction_accuracy": 0.05663430420711974, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6398252427184465, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.478073, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 449}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA transcript log-fold changes are assumed to plausibly reflect (but are not proven to reflect) corresponding changes in enzyme protein abundance and catalytic activity; no protein or activity measurement for these specific enzymes exists in this dataset.", "The RNA rows in discovery.json are pre-selected differential-expression results (not an unbiased whole-transcriptome survey), so pathway 'enrichment' is judged only relative to the distribution of this selected gene set, not the full transcriptome; the dataset itself is skewed toward positive effects (median +1.46), which limits how much specificity can be claimed for any single upregulated gene.", "Protein-spot observations cannot be attributed to a single gene because each spot lists multiple candidate genes, so no protein-level observation in this dataset can be treated as confirming or refuting a specific glycerolipid-metabolism enzyme.", "The logarithm base for the RNA 'reported log fold change' unit is unspecified and is not assumed to be log2 like the protein data; RNA and protein effect magnitudes are therefore not combined quantitatively, only compared qualitatively/directionally.", "No causal direction (APOE4 genotype -\u003e transcriptional change -\u003e lipid remodeling) is established; the data are cross-sectional differential expression under mock treatment at one timepoint."], "claim": "In APOE4 (vs APOE3) iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, coordinated upregulation of fatty-acid desaturase and Lands-cycle re-acylation transcripts (SCD, FADS1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2) together with downstream glycerolipid-synthesis and turnover transcripts (AGPAT2/4, GPAT4, DGAT1, ABHD5, MGLL) is consistent with a transcriptionally driven shift in acyl-chain remodeling capacity that could alter membrane glycerophospholipid saturation and neutral-lipid (triacylglycerol) turnover; this is an associative transcript-level pattern, not a demonstrated flux or causal mechanism.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted lipidomic profiling of glycerophosphatidylcholine species in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher unsaturation index (relative increase in mono/polyunsaturated PC species) consistent with elevated SCD/LPCAT1-mediated remodeling; failure to detect any shift in PC acyl-chain saturation would weaken this mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic inhibition of SCD in APOE4 microglia should blunt monounsaturated-acyl-CoA-dependent LPCAT1 remodeling flux and reduce the excess induction of the AGPAT2/DGAT1 glycerolipid-synthesis module toward APOE3-like levels; if the glycerolipid-synthesis transcript module remains elevated despite effective SCD inhibition, SCD would be excluded as the rate-limiting node and an SCD-independent driver (e.g., SREBF1-linked or GPAT/AGPAT-intrinsic) should be considered instead.", "Selective knockdown of LPCAT1 alone should decrease unsaturated PC species without normalizing ABHD5/MGLL/DGAT1-associated triacylglycerol turnover; if LPCAT1 knockdown also normalizes the TAG-turnover module, this would suggest a shared upstream transcriptional driver rather than an independent Lands-cycle bottleneck, weakening the proposed mechanism's specificity."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: fatty-acid desaturase transcripts SCD and FADS1 are elevated in APOE4 microglia (gene:SCD effect +4.17; gene:FADS1 effect +1.59), both statistically significant in this selected DE list.", "Inferred (not measured): if desaturase mRNA changes translate to proportional enzyme abundance/activity, this could raise the cellular pool of monounsaturated (and other desaturated) fatty acyl-CoA available as re-acylation substrate; no acyl-CoA pool or enzyme-activity measurement is present in this dataset.", "Measured: transcripts for Lands-cycle re-acylation enzymes LPCAT1, MBOAT1 and MBOAT2 are also elevated (effects +3.07, +2.65, +3.26), a pathway-coherent co-elevation alongside the desaturase transcripts.", "Inferred (flux/localization, not measured): coordinated desaturase + re-acylation transcript elevation is consistent with, but does not establish, increased Lands-cycle flux and a shift of membrane glycerophospholipid acyl chains toward higher unsaturation; no lipidomic or membrane-composition observation exists in this dataset to confirm this.", "Measured: downstream glycerolipid-synthesis transcripts AGPAT2, AGPAT4, GPAT4 and DGAT1 are elevated, while family member GPAT3 (-2.23) and fatty-acid-CoA ligases ACSL4 (-2.14) and ACSL5 (-3.12) are decreased, showing the response is isoform-specific rather than a uniform lipogenic upshift.", "Inferred bottleneck (not measured): given the magnitude of SCD and LPCAT1 induction relative to the overall positive skew of this selected-gene dataset (SCD at ~89th percentile, LPCAT1 at ~79th percentile of all reported RNA effects), SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA channeled through LPCAT1/MBOAT re-acylation is proposed as a candidate rate-limiting node linking transcriptional change to acyl-chain remodeling, upstream of the divergent ABHD5/MGLL/DGAT1 triacylglycerol-turnover changes.", "Caveat (measured, non-confirmatory): no protein-abundance or lipid-species observation in this dataset directly verifies enzyme-level or acyl-chain-level change; the one protein spot containing a related candidate gene (protein_spot:010, candidate list includes CERK among four other unrelated genes) shows a non-significant decrease and cannot confirm or exclude this transcript-based inference."], "title": "SCD/LPCAT1-driven acyl-chain remodeling as a bottleneck in APOE4 microglial glycerolipid handling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.04654211128752354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.045420220047296074, "cosine_similarity": 0.024935397053224104, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.644210355987055, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.04654211128752354, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.045420220047296074, "cosine_similarity": 0.024935397053224104, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "mean_absolute_error": 0.644210355987055, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6124156, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 7}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_027", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; direction and rank are used, absolute magnitudes are not converted, and the appropriate background is this list (1705/2212 = 77% positive, median +1.46), not a 50/50 expectation.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. FASN, ACLY, HMGCR, PLIN2, LIPA, NPC1, PSAP, MCOLN1, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, CPT1A, PLA2G4A) are unknown, not unchanged; several key steps of the proposed route are therefore unmeasured.", "Program membership was defined a priori from canonical pathway roles before reading directions; members were not chosen to make signs agree, and descriptive coherence here is not a formal enrichment result (genes are not independent; permutation against the selected list gave p_pos ~0.01 for lysosome, ~0.05 for SREBP, ~0.11 for glycerolipid, i.e. the glycerolipid/acyl set is suggestive but not statistically distinguishable from the list-wide positive bias).", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme capacity in the same direction; it does not establish enzyme activity, SREBP proteolytic activation, TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal acidification, lipid composition, droplet content, or any flux. No lipid, acyl-CoA or sterol pool was measured in this dataset.", "Protein-spot rows are 2D-gel spots with multiple candidate identities (median 5 candidates, keratin/actin-dominated); they are used only for compatibility testing and all candidate identities are retained. Spots containing cathepsin candidates change in both directions (protein_spot:052 +2.14 CTSL among candidates, protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:069 -1.38 both CTSD-containing, protein_spot:055/057 +0.59 and protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00 CTSB/HEXB-containing), so no individual protease is confirmed up or down.", "The astrocyte co-culture is assumed to be an ongoing external lipid/lipoprotein source; this was not measured here, and cell-composition or normalization asymmetry could contribute to the strong list-wide positive skew.", "The mock condition is assumed to be unchallenged steady state; reduced reserve inferred for challenge conditions is prospective and is not claimed as an ongoing defect in the measured condition."], "claim": "In mock-treated day-30 iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (vs isogenic APOE3, co-cultured with astrocytes), the dominant differentiating state is a coordinated increase in lipid handling capacity rather than a single failed step: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:TREM2, gene:CD36, gene:APOE), for TFEB/CLEAR-type lysosomal machinery (gene:TFEB +2.38 with 30/32 represented lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase rows positive, median +2.09), and for SREBP-driven lipogenesis and glycerolipid esterification/acyl remodeling (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:CHPT1 +2.91) are jointly elevated, while polyunsaturated acyl-CoA activation and lipoxygenation transcripts are among the minority of negative rows (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:ALOX15 -3.63) against a strongly positive selected-list background (1705/2212 rows positive). We propose that APOE4 increases lipid delivery into the lysosome-to-ER cycle and biases the acyl-CoA pool toward monounsaturated/saturated species that are esterified into triacylglycerol and into remodelled PC/PE, with anabolic carbon supplied by acetate/mitochondrial routes (gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43) rather than glycolysis/PPP (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, despite gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73). Causality is not established; all statements are transcript/spot abundance, not measured flux, composition or localization.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased triacylglycerol and increased monounsaturated (16:1/18:1) content in TAG and in PC/PE, with a reduced arachidonoyl (20:4)-phospholipid fraction and reduced lipid-peroxidation markers. If MUFA fraction and TAG are unchanged, or PUFA-phospholipids are increased, the acyl-chain-bias step (Step 4/5) is falsified.", "Prospective SCD inhibition (or DGAT1 inhibition) should be selectively costly in APOE4: SCD blockade should raise saturated-lipid/ER-stress markers and reduce droplet formation more in APOE4 than APOE3, and DGAT1 blockade should redirect acyl chains into phospholipid/lysosomal membrane accumulation. Equal or smaller responses in APOE4 than APOE3 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating adaptation vs failed compensation: pulse-chase clearance of labelled lipoprotein, myelin or apoptotic-cell lipid under mock conditions should be equal to or faster in APOE4 (expanded matched capacity). If APOE4 clears the same load more slowly at baseline, the 'increased throughput' framing is wrong and a degradation bottleneck is the better model.", "Prospective bafilomycin A1 or TFEB knockdown should cause disproportionately greater neutral-lipid and undigested-substrate accumulation in APOE4 than APOE3 (because APOE4 depends on the expanded lysosomal arm). If blocking lysosomal acidification changes APOE4 no more than APOE3, Step 2 is not load-bearing.", "Prospective enzymology: per-cell mature cathepsin B/D, GBA and HEXA/B activities should be increased in APOE4 despite the ambiguous 2D-spot directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055, protein_spot:057, protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069). Unchanged or decreased hydrolase activity with elevated transcripts would instead support a post-transcriptional lysosomal defect and weaken Step 2.", "Prospective tracer test of the carbon-supply step: 13C-acetate should contribute a larger fraction of newly synthesized fatty acid/sterol than 13C-glucose in APOE4 relative to APOE3, with reduced glucose-derived PPP flux. Equal acetate and glucose contributions would falsify Step 6 without necessarily affecting Steps 1-5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (increased routing in): APOE4 raises expression of lipoprotein/lipid-uptake receptors and lipid carriers (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:MERTK +1.30, gene:STAB1, gene:MRC1), plausibly increasing delivery of astrocyte-derived lipoprotein and membrane lipid to the endolysosomal system (inferred uptake flux, not measured).", "Step 2 (expanded degradative capacity): the endolysosomal/CLEAR program is coordinately elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38; hydrolases gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:NPC2; v-ATPase gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:ATP6V0C +3.51, gene:ATP6AP1; gene:LAMP1, gene:IGF2R, gene:SCARB2; trafficking gene:AP5M1 +9.78, gene:RAB28 +8.42, gene:VPS26A +4.86, gene:CHMP4B +3.82, gene:RAB7A +2.65, gene:SNX3 +3.95, gene:DNM2 +5.82), consistent with increased lysosomal biogenesis matched to the higher lipid load; exceptions gene:CTSS -5.57 and gene:M6PR -1.72.", "Step 3 (sterol released but re-esterified, keeping ER sensing pool low): sterol acyl-esterification and sterol-handling transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:CH25H +1.62, gene:NPC2 +1.17) while the SREBP program is uniformly positive (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:INSIG1 +1.87, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:LDLR +1.50; 12/12 represented rows positive), an inferred low-ER-sterol/lipogenic signalling state.", "Step 4 (acyl-chain bias): SREBP-linked desaturation and acetyl-CoA supply are up (gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ACSS2 +2.93) while polyunsaturated acyl-CoA activation and lipoxygenation are down (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:ALOX15 -3.63) with gene:GPX4 +2.79, predicting an acyl-CoA and membrane pool shifted toward monounsaturated, peroxidation-resistant species (composition inferred, not measured).", "Step 5 (esterification and phospholipid remodeling output): glycerolipid synthesis and Lands-cycle remodeling transcripts rise (gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:AGPAT4 +1.12, gene:CERS4 +2.52), with lipolytic cycling maintained (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04), so lysosome-derived and de novo acyl chains are routed into triacylglycerol stores and remodelled PC/PE rather than into oxidation (gene:CPT1A not supplied; gene:ACOX1 +1.24 only).", "Step 6 (carbon supply switch supporting anabolism): cytosolic glycolysis/PPP rows are the clearest negatively skewed program against the positive background (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:HK3 -1.12; 5 positive/6 negative) while pyruvate import and TCA/anaplerotic rows are uniformly positive (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:ATP5F1B +2.65, gene:SDHB +1.65), an inferred citrate/acetyl-CoA-based supply for the esterification program.", "Step 7 (state consequence, prospective): this MUFA-biased, storage-and-turnover state is expected to be self-consistent under mock conditions (no ongoing degradative failure is demonstrated), but to leave reduced reserve for PUFA-dependent and load-dependent responses; a defect would be revealed mainly under lipid or inflammatory challenge, not necessarily in the supplied condition."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a high-throughput lipid-routing state: lysosomal/CLEAR expansion coupled to SREBP-driven, MUFA-biased glycerolipid esterification and acyl-chain remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4396761806299154, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13076535012758805, "cosine_similarity": 0.023518698374353827, "direction_accuracy": 0.32524271844660196, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7413430420711974, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4396761806299154, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.13076535012758805, "cosine_similarity": 0.023518698374353827, "direction_accuracy": 0.32524271844660196, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7413430420711974, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8518945, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 104}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All functional annotations and causal connections use unverified background knowledge; no literature or databases were consulted. Discovery evidence consists only of selected differential RNA expression and protein-spot abundance, not genomic-variant measurements. Positive effects mean higher APOE4 abundance. RNA effects retain their unspecified reported logarithm base; protein-spot effects use log2 fold change.", "The complete RNA list is 1705 positive and 507 negative observations, so upward coherence is judged against a 77.1% positive selected-list background. Missing genes are unknown, not unchanged. Program coherence is descriptive; genes are not assumed independent and no enrichment or causal significance is established.", "The isogenic APOE4/APOE3 comparison supports a genotype-associated state, but does not identify the initiating receptor, direct biochemical action of APOE4, or a uniquely microglia-intrinsic cause. Replicate information, cell-state proportions and astrocyte contributions are not supplied.", "Productive basal processing is the central uncertain assumption. Transcript abundance does not establish enzyme activity, TFEB nuclear localization, acidification, respiration, ATP supply or flux. gene:SPG11 decreases despite higher AP5 subunit transcripts, challenging coordinated retrieval. Nuclear/mitochondrial respiratory RNA discordance could instead accompany functional failure. The model requires direct basal activity and flux tests.", "No membrane-lipid, lysophospholipid, free-fatty-acid, triglyceride, cholesterol or other molecular pool was measured. LIPA and PLA2G15 are absent from the selected list and their behavior is unknown. Replacement acyl chains need not originate from lysosomal cargo; the proposed coupling is through membrane-replacement demand. The model does not predict a universal change in lipid saturation or infer a rate-limiting defect from gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5 or gene:GPAT3 decreases. Higher gene:DGAT1 and gene:MGLL also permit neutral-glycerolipid storage/turnover; increased membrane replacement must be distinguished experimentally from preferential storage.", "Protein spots provide mixed compatibility, not protein-specific confirmation. protein_spot:057 is +0.585 log2 with candidates CLIC1, CTSB, CAPZB, ACTG2, MTMR3; protein_spot:058 is -0.848 with candidates CTSD, ACTB, CAPZB, CTSB, GSTO1. protein_spot:064 is -1.202 with candidates ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1; protein_spot:065 is -0.926 with candidates ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART. Every candidate is retained. The negative pump-candidate spots seriously challenge the productive-processing assumption if their changes can subsequently be assigned to the pump; they do not currently demonstrate pump loss.", "The strongest large-effect pattern left outside the mechanism is adhesion/cytoskeletal reorganization: higher gene:ITGA6, gene:ITGB1 and gene:ARHGDIA alongside lower gene:ACTB and gene:MYH9. It could reflect a broader cell-state or morphology change; the membrane-renewal hypothesis does not establish its cause."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 is hypothesized to increase basal membrane renewal through coordinated endolysosomal processing and replacement glycerophospholipid reacylation. Increased membrane-handling demand provides a common driver for the lysosomal, selective glycerolipid-remodeling and nuclear metabolic RNA programs. This is a tentative productive-throughput mechanism; abundance measurements do not establish the proposed activities, fluxes or causal direction.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective basal discrimination: in independent day-30 APOE4/APOE3 mock co-cultures, use non-loading tracer pulse-chases to measure lysosomal membrane-cargo clearance and fractional PC/PE acyl-chain replacement, normalized to cell number, precursor enrichment and matched initial cargo. APOE4 should show faster clearance and greater replacement, with lysosomal pH no less acidic and adequate basal ATP supply. Equal or slower turnover, particularly slower clearance with cargo retention despite elevated transcripts, would weaken the productive-renewal mechanism. Measure triglyceride labeling in parallel: increased uptake or neutral storage without increased membrane replacement would weaken the proposed routing. Lipid overload or other stress is not required for this prediction.", "Prospective acyl-routing perturbation: apply matched, experimentally verified partial CRISPRi of LPCAT1, MBOAT1 and MBOAT2, individually and combined, in otherwise mock cultures. The combined perturbation should reduce the APOE4 excess in tracer-measured lysophospholipid-to-PC/PE incorporation and membrane replacement at matched uptake and viability. Rescue with catalytically active enzymes should restore that excess more effectively than expression-matched inactive controls. Persistence of the excess despite verified suppression of the targeted activities would weaken the proposed reacylation route. A defect arising only after this perturbation demonstrates experimental dependence, not a pre-existing basal defect.", "Prospective coupling perturbation: acutely and partially inhibit lysosomal acidification, calibrating to comparable measured pH changes and controlling cargo uptake and viability. Suppressing lysosomal membrane processing should reduce the APOE4-specific excess in subsequent membrane-lipid replacement; washout should restore the coupling. If replacement remains elevated when lysosomal processing is demonstrably suppressed, the proposed lysosome-to-replacement-demand connection is weakened. Jointly observing preserved basal clearance and perturbation-sensitive replacement is required; sensitivity to inhibition alone cannot establish successful basal adaptation."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["1. Proposed initiating state: APOE4 increases constitutive lipid/membrane-cargo handling in day-30 mock microglia co-cultured with astrocytes. Higher RNA for lipid-handling receptors (gene:LDLR, gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36), gene:TREM2 and gene:APOE, together with late-endosomal/retrieval machinery (gene:RAB7A, gene:AP5M1, gene:AP5Z1, gene:AP5S1), motivates increased cargo delivery and membrane retrieval. These are measured transcripts; receptor uptake and trafficking rates, and the molecular link from APOE4 to this state, are inferred.", "2. Proposed productive processing: greater membrane-cargo delivery is accommodated by increased basal lysosomal processing. RNA increases in gene:TFEB, gene:LAMP1, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A and gene:ATP6V1E1 support coordinated degradative-capacity expression. The hypothesis predicts adequate acidification and faster cargo clearance in the actual mock condition; neither is measured. gene:CTSS decreases, so this is not uniform induction of every lysosomal function. This step does not equate glycosphingolipid degradation with demonstrated fatty-acid liberation.", "3. Proposed replacement routing: increased membrane processing creates membrane-replacement demand, met partly through glycerophospholipid synthesis and lysophospholipid reacylation. Higher RNA for gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1 and gene:MBOAT2 predicts increased incorporation of acyl chains into replacement phospholipids. Lower gene:GPAT3, gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 implies selective routing rather than uniform expression of all synthesis/activation routes. Higher gene:SCD and gene:FADS1 suggests altered acyl supply but does not determine net saturation or polyunsaturated-lipid abundance. Higher sterol-supply transcripts (gene:SREBF2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24) also fit replacement-membrane demand. These causal connections and increased reacylation flux are prospective, not observed lipid pools or established substrate sources.", "4. Proposed energetic coordination: the demand from trafficking, acidification and replacement synthesis induces a nuclear metabolic-capacity response, represented by higher gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX5B and gene:ATP5F1B. This connects the strong nuclear respiratory program to membrane renewal without assuming increased respiration from RNA alone. Lower gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2 and gene:MT-ATP6 challenges functional adequacy. The selected mechanism nevertheless predicts sufficient basal energy and lysosomal function for increased renewal under mock treatment; a failure exposed only by an experimental challenge would not establish an ongoing basal defect."], "title": "APOE4 increases constitutive lysosome-coupled membrane renewal"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14906029612672156, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1664984903191255, "cosine_similarity": 0.017793730342581915, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6594724919093852, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14906029612672156, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1664984903191255, "cosine_similarity": 0.017793730342581915, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6594724919093852, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.4887535, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_147", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (all |reported log fold change| \u003e= 1, adjusted p \u003c 0.05, logarithm base unspecified and preserved as reported); they are treated as a biased subset, so pathway claims are made by comparing sets against the list's own strongly positive background (77.1% of rows positive, median +1.46) rather than against zero.", "Relative transcript changes for nuclear OXPHOS subunits reflect at least partly a change in synthesis of the corresponding proteins; no mitochondrial protein was unambiguously quantified here.", "The reduced mtDNA-encoded transcripts reflect a real per-mitochondrion or per-cell deficit in mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply rather than solely a normalisation consequence of a lower mitochondrial RNA fraction in APOE4 cells (this assumption is the main vulnerability and is addressed by prediction 5).", "Protein spots are mixtures with 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence, never as identification of a specific protein pool.", "Astrocyte co-culture, day-30 timepoint and mock treatment are matched between genotypes so the isogenic APOE4/APOE3 contrast is not confounded by differing non-microglial content.", "Cardiolipin, phospholipid species, ROS, membrane potential, respiration, mtDNA copy number and complex assembly state were not measured in this dataset and are inferred quantities throughout."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily by a coordinated, uniformly positive nuclear-encoded mitochondrial program (38/38 detected NDUF/COX/UQCR/ATP5/SDH transcripts elevated, plus TCA, carrier, protein-import and inner-membrane phospholipid-handling transcripts) that is not matched by mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4 relatively reduced against a strongly upward-shifted differential-expression list). We hypothesise that the resulting mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance, not a deficit of nuclear subunit or cardiolipin-remodeling capacity, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of complexes III/IV/V, producing assembly-limited respiration, an inferred peroxide-handling response (PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, TXNDC17 transcripts) and a compensatory lysosomal-hydrolase expansion. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PREDICTION 1 (discriminating, assembly state): blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia will show an increased ratio of free or sub-assembly nuclear-encoded subunits to fully assembled complex III, IV and V holoenzymes, with mature holoenzyme per mitochondrial mass (citrate-synthase- or TOMM20-normalised) unchanged or reduced. If mature complexes III/IV/V scale up in proportion to the elevated nuclear subunit transcripts, the assembly-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "PREDICTION 2 (flux): respirometry normalised to mitochondrial mass will show reduced oligomycin-sensitive ATP-linked and maximal (FCCP) respiration in APOE4 despite the elevated nuclear program, with an increased fraction of proton leak. Higher normalised ATP-linked respiration in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "PREDICTION 3 (occlusion test): partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol) will produce a smaller incremental loss of ATP-linked respiration and a smaller incremental rise in the free-subunit pool in APOE4 than in APOE3, because APOE4 is already core-limited. Equal or greater sensitivity of APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "PREDICTION 4 (rescue, direction-specific): raising mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (TFAM overexpression, or mitochondrially targeted expression of ATP6/CYB) will selectively restore ATP-linked respiration and reduce the free-subunit pool in APOE4 while having little effect in APOE3; no genotype-selective rescue would weaken the mechanism.", "PREDICTION 5 (artifact control, the key alternative): spike-in-normalised or absolute quantification (ddPCR of MT-ATP6/MT-CYB per cell, mtDNA:nuclear DNA copy number) will show a genuine reduction in mtDNA-encoded transcript content per cell or per mtDNA copy in APOE4. If absolute mtDNA-encoded transcript levels and mtDNA copy number are unchanged and the apparent deficit disappears after spike-in normalisation, the observed discordance is a compositional artifact of the strongly upward-shifted list and the mechanism collapses.", "PREDICTION 6 (lipid arm, secondary): cardiolipin mass spectrometry will show altered cardiolipin acyl composition (increased remodeled tetralinoleoyl-type species or increased monolysocardiolipin:cardiolipin ratio) in APOE4, and TAZ or PRELID3B knockdown will worsen the APOE4 assembly and respiration phenotype more than the APOE3 one. Unchanged cardiolipin species and no genotype-selective effect of TAZ/PRELID3B knockdown would remove the lipid arm (steps 2) while leaving the mitonuclear-imbalance core intact.", "PREDICTION 7 (rejecting the assigned focus): if instead general glycerolipid/membrane turnover were the driver, APOE4 microglia would show increased neutral-lipid (triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet) content and increased de novo acyl-chain incorporation into glycerolipids by tracer labelling; the discovery data predict the opposite bias (reduced ACSL4/ACSL5/GPAT3 against a strongly upward list), so a clear APOE4 increase in de novo glycerolipid acylation flux would falsify the catabolic bias described in step 5."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_147", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA): APOE4 microglia carry a coordinately elevated nuclear-encoded mitochondrial transcript program - every detected nuclear OXPHOS subunit transcript is higher (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:ATP5ME, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:SDHB), together with TCA (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B), substrate carriers (gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A46) and import/translation machinery (gene:TOMM22, gene:TIMM44, gene:HSPA9, gene:TUFM). Transcript abundance is measured; mitochondrial mass, protein abundance and respiratory flux are inferred and unmeasured here.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA, inferred lipid flux): the inner-membrane lipid arm of the same program is co-elevated - gene:PRELID3B (phosphatidic-acid transfer to the inner membrane) and gene:TAZ (cardiolipin acyl-chain remodeling) with the cristae/scaffold transcripts gene:CHCHD3 and gene:PHB. We infer increased capacity for cardiolipin/PE remodeling of the inner membrane; no lipid species were measured in this dataset, so cardiolipin content and acyl composition are inferred, not observed.", "STEP 3 (measured RNA, primary bottleneck): mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts do not follow this program and move opposite to the global direction of the list (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4 lower; only gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 higher). We propose that supply of mtDNA-encoded cores - not nuclear subunits, cardiolipin remodeling or substrate delivery - limits maturation of complexes III, IV and V. Assembly state and holoenzyme levels are inferred, not measured.", "STEP 4 (inferred): imbalanced subunit supply leaves nuclear-encoded subunits in unassembled or sub-complex pools, lowering ATP-linked and maximal respiration per unit mitochondrial mass and increasing electron leak; consistent with this, peroxide-handling transcripts are elevated (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17) alongside quality-control transcripts (gene:FIS1, gene:HSPA9). Weak, ambiguous protein-spot support comes from protein_spot:017 and protein_spot:077, whose candidate lists include CAT and PRDX2 among other proteins.", "STEP 5 (measured RNA, partly measured protein): chronic partial bioenergetic insufficiency accompanies an expanded lysosomal/hydrolase program (gene:TFEB, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:ATP6V1A), i.e. catabolic membrane-lipid turnover rather than net de novo glycerolipid synthesis, since acyl-CoA and glycerol-3-phosphate acylation entry transcripts fall against the upward global trend (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3). Cathepsin-containing protein spots move in both directions (protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053 up; protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069 down), so lysosomal protein content is not established.", "STEP 6 (integration): the APOE4 state is therefore proposed to be assembly-limited and catabolically biased rather than transcriptionally deficient - the cell over-provisions nuclear respiratory and inner-membrane lipid machinery against a fixed mtDNA-encoded core supply."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometric imbalance: APOE4 microglia expand the nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and inner-membrane lipid-remodeling program while mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts fall, making mtDNA-encoded core supply the assembly bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36508141638666325, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0868329855897121, "cosine_similarity": 0.01669574840664697, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_147", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7130711974110032, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36508141638666325, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0868329855897121, "cosine_similarity": 0.01669574840664697, "direction_accuracy": 0.33171521035598706, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7130711974110032, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.98183275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 450}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_047", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46 in an unspecified logarithm base); pathway claims are therefore judged against that inflated background, not against zero.", "Transcript abundance of the named enzymes is assumed to track enzyme protein and catalytic capacity in these cells; no protein or activity measurement of any lipid enzyme is supplied, and one protein-spot train that could report a lysosomal protein moves downward (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069), so this assumption is untested.", "Lysosomal hydrolase transcript elevation is assumed to reflect increased membrane-lipid catabolic flux rather than compensation for reduced per-enzyme activity or for undigested substrate accumulation; the opposite (a degradation block) would invert the direction of Step 2 while preserving Steps 3-5.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes (mean 4.8 per spot) and are not uniquely identified proteins; the recurrent up-moving ANXA1-containing spot train (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046) is treated only as weak, ambiguous corroboration of altered phospholipid-binding protein abundance, since TALDO1, PSMD7 and ACTB are equally admissible assignments.", "APOE3 and APOE4 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated, and astrocyte co-culture contributes lipid substrate similarly to both genotypes; no co-culture composition or cell-fraction data are supplied.", "No lipidomic, free-fatty-acid, acyl-CoA, desaturation-index, lysosomal pH or flux measurement is present in the discovery data, so every acyl-species and rate statement in this hypothesis is a prediction."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally in glycerolipid handling of degraded membrane: a coordinately elevated lysosomal hydrolase/acidification transcript program (GBA, SMPD1, GAA, HEXB, CTSB/CTSD/CTSK, ATP6V subunits, TFEB) is inferred to raise the intracellular flux of free fatty acids, lyso-phospholipids and sphingoid backbones, and the rate-limiting disposal step becomes re-esterification through an SREBF1-associated monounsaturated re-acylation node (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, CHPT1, DGAT1) while the polyunsaturated-CoA channel is restricted (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3 transcripts lower). We predict this yields MUFA-biased, arachidonate-poor membrane and neutral-lipid pools in APOE4 and a selective dependence on SCD-derived 18:1-CoA. Transcript and protein-spot abundances are measured; all flux, acyl-species composition, localization and causal ordering are inferred and not established here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher SCD desaturation index (18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0) and higher MUFA-containing PC/PE/TAG, with lower 20:4-containing PI and PE. If the MUFA:SFA ratio is unchanged or 20:4-phospholipids are equal or higher in APOE4, the acyl-remodeling bottleneck is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) should produce a genotype x drug interaction, with APOE4 microglia accumulating disproportionately more unesterified saturated fatty acid and saturated lyso-PC, more LAMP1-positive membrane permeabilization (galectin-3 puncta) and greater viability loss than APOE3 at the same dose, rescued by exogenous oleate but not palmitate. Equal sensitivity of both genotypes, or rescue by palmitate, would weaken the mechanism.", "Causal ordering test: reducing upstream catabolic flux (bafilomycin A1 or acid-hydrolase inhibition, or removal of phagocytic membrane cargo) should lower the APOE4-specific elevation of SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 transcripts and of neutral-lipid staining. If these transcripts remain elevated when catabolic flux is blocked, the anabolic module is autonomous (e.g. direct SREBF1 activation) and Steps 1-2 as the driver are refuted.", "Channel-restriction test: ACSL4 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore 20:4 incorporation into phospholipids and lower the TAG/phospholipid ratio without normalizing lysosomal hydrolase transcripts. If ACSL4 re-expression changes neither acyl composition nor lipid-droplet load, Step 4 is not rate-relevant.", "Flux-tracing prediction: pulse-chase of isotopically labelled membrane cargo (labelled apoptotic-cell membranes or NBD-PC) should show faster and larger appearance of label in TAG and in MUFA-PC in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or slower label transfer into these pools would falsify the proposed increase in membrane turnover flux.", "Specificity prediction distinguishing this from a sterol mechanism: sterol-synthesis transcripts are not enriched above the global shift in these data, so LXR agonism or statin exposure should shift APOE4 toward APOE3 less than SCD inhibition or oleate loading does. If sterol manipulation dominates, an APOE4 cholesterol-handling mechanism should replace this one.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: the strongest global module here is nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts up with mitochondrially-encoded transcripts down. If Seahorse and mitochondrial-translation assays show a primary mitonuclear translation defect that persists when SCD is inhibited and oleate is supplied, the lipid bottleneck is secondary rather than primary."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal luminal hydrolases and V-ATPase subunits (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:GAA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A) together with gene:TFEB, consistent with an expanded acidic degradative compartment. Lysosomal number, pH and hydrolase activity were not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred flux): Degradation of glycerophospholipid and sphingolipid membrane cargo in this compartment is proposed to liberate a larger pool of free fatty acids and lyso-phospholipids per unit time in APOE4 than APOE3. No lipid species, free fatty acid pool or flux measurement is supplied.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): The disposal arm is transcriptionally biased toward monounsaturated re-esterification: gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2 (acetyl-CoA/desaturation supply), gene:AGPAT2 and gene:GPAT4 (de novo phosphatidic-acid backbone), gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2 (Lands-cycle lyso-lipid re-acylation), gene:CHPT1 (choline-phosphotransferase headgroup step) and gene:DGAT1 (triacylglycerol sink).", "Step 4 (measured abundance, inferred channel restriction): The competing polyunsaturated/alternative acylation route is transcriptionally down in the same cells (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, gene:GPAT3, gene:PNPLA1), so arachidonoyl-CoA generation and PUFA re-incorporation are predicted to be limited relative to APOE3.", "Step 5 (proposed bottleneck): Because oleoyl-CoA supply from SCD and its transfer by AGPAT2/LPCAT1/MBOAT1/2 set the maximum rate at which liberated fatty acids and lyso-lipids can be re-esterified, this node is the capacity-limiting step. Above it, unesterified fatty acid and lyso-phospholipid accumulate; below it, cargo is stored as MUFA-rich phosphatidylcholine/ethanolamine and triacylglycerol.", "Step 6 (predicted consequence, not observed): APOE4 membranes and lipid droplets are predicted to be enriched in 16:1/18:1 species and depleted of 20:4-containing phospholipids, altering membrane order, lysosomal membrane stability and eicosanoid precursor availability; the elevated gene:MGLL and gene:PLA2G7 transcripts indicate that this pool is also actively cycled rather than statically stored."], "title": "APOE4 microglia route an expanded lysosomal membrane-degradation flux through a monounsaturated re-acylation bottleneck (SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1-MBOAT), with ACSL4/ACSL5 loss closing the polyunsaturated channel"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32912712771849495, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.005938186067773208, "cosine_similarity": 0.01622374111201862, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7702912621359224, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32912712771849495, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.005938186067773208, "cosine_similarity": 0.01622374111201862, "direction_accuracy": 0.3155339805825243, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7702912621359224, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.76444375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 451}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05) with a list-wide positive shift (77% up, mean +1.39); all enrichment claims are made against that list background, not against an unbiased transcriptome, and the logarithm base of the reported fold changes is unspecified and left unconverted.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme abundance and, only as an explicit inference, for pathway capacity; no flux, NADPH/NADP+ or GSH/GSSG ratio, peroxiredoxin oxidation state, membrane potential or ROS measurement is present in these data.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified: spot 017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5, +0.77) and spot 077 (candidates including PRDX2, +1.07) are treated as consistent-but-ambiguous, never as measured catalase or peroxiredoxin-2 protein.", "The two genotypes are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the metadata, and the observed differences are not driven by differing microglia/astrocyte proportions, ambient RNA or normalisation asymmetry in the 10X Flex pseudobulk; biological replicate number is not supplied, so this assumption is untested.", "Key redox nodes (G6PD, TKT, IDH1, TXN, TXNRD1, GSR, SOD1, SOD2, CAT) are absent from the supplied RNA list; their absence is treated as unmeasured, not as unchanged."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain, TCA and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts together with a thiol-peroxidase transcript program (PRDX2/3/5, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4, MSRA, GSS, FTH1), but a coordinated decrease in cytosolic NADPH/NAD(H)-regenerating transcripts (PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NAMPT). We hypothesise that the resulting mismatch, not peroxisomal beta-oxidation and not NADPH-oxidase output, is the primary bottleneck: APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial peroxide production and peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin protein supply while shifting NADPH provision onto the proton-motive-force-dependent transhydrogenase NNT, so their peroxide-clearing flux becomes limited by, and coupled to, mitochondrial membrane potential rather than by cytosolic pentose-phosphate flux. Causality is not established by these data; the flux, redox-couple and localisation statements are inferences from transcript and spot abundance only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological or genetic blockade of cytosolic NADPH supply (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide) or of NAD salvage (FK866) should produce a markedly larger increase in cytosolic and mitochondrial H2O2 (roGFP2-Orp1/HyPer7), a larger 2-Cys peroxiredoxin dimer/hyperoxidation shift on non-reducing blots, a larger GSH/GSSG fall and greater viability loss in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia. Equal sensitivity of the two genotypes would weaken the mechanism.", "NNT knockdown or NNT inhibition should selectively raise matrix H2O2 and lower matrix NADPH (mito-iNap) in APOE4 but not APOE3; if NNT loss affects both genotypes equally, the proposed shift of NADPH provision onto NNT is wrong.", "Sub-uncoupling FCCP or oligomycin should collapse NADPH and hyperoxidise peroxiredoxins faster in APOE4 than APOE3, demonstrating the predicted membrane-potential coupling of antioxidant flux; comparable kinetics would falsify step 5.", "Respirometry and BN-PAGE should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption and higher assembled complex I/III/IV in APOE4; if respiration and complex assembly are unchanged or lower despite the transcript signature, the primary inference of expanded oxidative flux fails and the transcript pattern should be reattributed to compositional or normalisation artefact.", "Peroxisomal alternative is predicted to fail: APOE4 microglia should not show increased peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0 or pristanic-acid oxidation) or increased PMP70/catalase-positive peroxisome number; observing a clear peroxisomal flux increase, especially with elevated PEX/ACOX1/ABCD3 protein, would favour the rejected focus mechanism over this one.", "Targeted rescue: expressing a NADPH-independent peroxide sink (mitochondrially targeted catalase) or restoring PPP flux (G6PD/PGD overexpression) should normalise APOE4 peroxiredoxin oxidation state and phagocytic/lipid phenotypes without normalising the ETC transcript program; if rescue also requires lowering ETC transcripts, the bottleneck is upstream of where we place it."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for 48 ETC/TCA/mitochondrial-carrier components are uniformly higher in APOE4 (mean +3.43 in the reported log-fold-change units vs a +1.39 list-wide background, permutation p=2e-5), including NDUFA5, NDUFS7/8, UQCRC2, ATP5ME, COX7A2, OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, DLD, MPC2, SLC25A1/11/5. Inferred: larger assembled respiratory-chain and TCA capacity with increased pyruvate, citrate/malate and glutamate (GLUD1) electron input, hence higher electron flux into complexes I and III.", "Inferred (not measured): higher electron input at a given ATP demand increases superoxide/H2O2 generation at complex I/III; the matrix H2O2 load rises before any change in ATP output is required.", "Measured: a matched thiol-peroxidase and thiol-repair transcript set is elevated (TXNDC17 +7.10, PRDX2 +4.41, TXNL1 +4.33, PRDX3 +3.49, GPX4 +2.79, MSRA +2.64, FTH1 +2.53, GSS +2.11, PRDX5 +1.96; set mean +2.89, p=0.032). Inferred: an adaptive attempt to raise 2-Cys peroxiredoxin and glutathione-peroxidase capacity in matrix and cytosol.", "Measured counter-directional change: cytosolic NADPH/NAD supply transcripts are lower against a strongly up-shifted background (TALDO1 -2.32, NAMPT -2.62, PGD -1.30, NADK -1.14; set mean -1.84, p=0.009), while the mitochondrial NADPH/anaplerosis set is higher (NNT +2.88, GLUD1 +3.17, SLC25A1 +4.47, SLC25A11 +4.50; p=0.032). Inferred: reduced capacity to regenerate cytosolic NADPH and total NAD(H), with compensatory reliance on NNT.", "Bottleneck (inferred): peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin and glutathione peroxidase turnover requires NADPH-dependent reduction by TXNRD/GSR. Because NNT-derived NADPH is driven by the proton-motive force, APOE4 antioxidant flux becomes potential-dependent: any depolarisation or uncoupling should lower NADPH, hyperoxidise 2-Cys peroxiredoxins and raise H2O2 further, a self-reinforcing loop absent in APOE3.", "Downstream (inferred, partially measured): MSRB1 is lower (-2.44) despite MSRA being higher, predicting asymmetric methionine-sulfoxide repair; FTH1 (+2.53) and the mitochondrial iron importer SLC25A37 (+4.48) indicate re-routed iron handling, and ACSL4 (-2.14) with SCD (+4.17), DGAT1 (+1.72), SCARB1 (+8.22) predicts a more monounsaturated, storage-biased lipid pool that limits, rather than amplifies, membrane lipid peroxidation."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand mitochondrial oxidative capacity while lowering cytosolic NADPH/NAD regeneration, making peroxiredoxin recycling the redox bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3179392977144334, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15738947033794418, "cosine_similarity": 0.015102787290261868, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7586181229773463, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3179392977144334, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.15738947033794418, "cosine_similarity": 0.015102787290261868, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7586181229773463, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.85951675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 452}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_095", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so enrichment claims are made relative to that list's own strongly upward-shifted background (median log fold change about +1.46, 77 percent positive) and not to an unbiased transcriptome; the logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported.", "Probe-based 10X Flex quantification of mtDNA-encoded transcripts is assumed comparable between genotypes and not systematically biased by ambient RNA, probe capture, or per-cell normalisation differences.", "Transcript abundance for nuclear OXPHOS, import and lysosomal genes is assumed to track, at least in direction, the corresponding protein pools; no mitochondrial protein pool, assembled complex, respiration rate, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number or eIF2alpha phosphorylation was measured here.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level changes are used only as weak concordance or counter-evidence.", "Astrocyte co-culture and any genotype-dependent difference in microglial maturation or cell-cycle state are assumed not to be the sole driver of the mitonuclear discordance."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 mainly by a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS, TCA and mitochondrial protein-import transcripts while several mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts (MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ATP6, MT-ND4) are reduced; we hypothesise that the limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits, so imported nuclear subunits accumulate unassembled, and the resulting matrix/inner-membrane proteostatic strain engages a DELE1-linked integrated stress response (DDIT3 up) and a compensatory lysosomal-catabolic program (TFEB, CTSB, GBA, v-ATPase up), rather than an ER unfolded-protein or secretory-trafficking defect.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial inhibition of mitochondrial translation (low-dose doxycycline or chloramphenicol) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 signature, that is induce DELE1/DDIT3 and the TFEB-lysosomal genes while further raising nuclear OXPHOS transcripts; if APOE3 cells instead show no ISR or no lysosomal induction at doses that lower MT-CO2/MT-ATP6 protein, the mechanism is weakened.", "Blue-native PAGE plus complex-IV/V in-gel activity and Seahorse respirometry should show APOE4 microglia with lower assembled complex III/IV/V and lower maximal and spare respiratory capacity per mitochondrial mass despite higher nuclear subunit protein; equal or higher assembled holoenzyme and respiration in APOE4 would falsify the bottleneck.", "Immunoblot or proximity assay should detect a higher unassembled-to-assembled ratio for imported nuclear subunits (e.g. NDUFA/ATP5F1B) in APOE4; no accumulation of unassembled subunits would weaken step 3.", "ISR blockade (ISRIB, or EIF2AK1/HRI knockdown, or DELE1 knockdown) in APOE4 should reduce DDIT3 and blunt the lysosomal-catabolic transcript program without restoring the nuclear-to-mtDNA transcript ratio; if the nuclear/mtDNA ratio also normalises, the ISR is upstream rather than downstream and the causal ordering is wrong.", "The discordance must reproduce in total RNA-seq with spike-in or per-cell normalisation and in mtDNA copy-number and mt-protein measurements; if MT-encoded transcripts are unchanged or increased by a non-probe method, the primary observation is a platform artifact and the hypothesis fails.", "ER-focused alternative test: thapsigargin or tunicamycin challenge should reveal similar ER-stress sensitivity in APOE4 and APOE3, and HSPA5/HSP90B1/XBP1s protein levels should not differ at baseline; a clear baseline ER-proteostasis deficit in APOE4 would favour the rejected ER mechanism over this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for essentially all detected nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits (38/38 up; complex I, III, IV, V), TCA-cycle enzymes and mitochondrial import/translation-elongation components; this set is enriched above the strong global upward shift of the supplied differential-expression list (permutation p\u003c0.0001).", "Measured: in the same list, four mtDNA-encoded core subunits are reduced (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2), giving a nuclear-versus-mitochondrial transcript discordance (rank test p=1.8e-4); two mtDNA transcripts (MT-ND5, MT-ND4L) are increased and are explicit counter-evidence.", "Inferred (not measured): because complex III, IV and V holoenzymes require mtDNA-encoded catalytic cores, reduced availability of these cores makes core-subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply, the assembly bottleneck; imported nuclear subunits then remain unassembled in the matrix and inner membrane.", "Inferred flux/activity: unassembled subunits raise the load on matrix chaperones and proteases (HSPA9 transcript up is consistent but is abundance, not activity), lowering coupled respiratory flux per imported subunit and increasing electron leak.", "Inferred signalling: this inner-membrane/matrix strain engages the OMA1-DELE1-HRI branch of the integrated stress response; DELE1 and DDIT3 transcripts are elevated, consistent with, but not proof of, active eIF2alpha-phosphorylation signalling (ATF4 and phospho-eIF2alpha were not measured).", "Inferred adaptation: reduced oxidative ATP yield with only partial glycolytic compensation (SLC2A1/SLC2A3, PFKM, HIF1A up but HK2 and PFKP strongly down) is met by a TFEB-associated lysosomal-catabolic and lipid-mobilising program (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, v-ATPase subunits, SREBF1, ABCA7, TREM2 up), which is the APOE4-specific functional state at day 30."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS core subunit deficit limits assembly against an expanded nuclear mitochondrial program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12359229036665066, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.007442143543311528, "cosine_similarity": 0.01266686039482364, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_095", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6809741100323624, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.12359229036665066, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.007442143543311528, "cosine_similarity": 0.01266686039482364, "direction_accuracy": 0.11326860841423948, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6809741100323624, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.687909, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 453}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_027", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so enrichment is judged only against other differentially expressed genes, not against an unbiased transcriptome.", "The RNA effect column is a reported log fold change of unspecified base; only signs, ranks and within-list percentiles are used, never absolute fold changes.", "The strong global positive offset of the RNA list (mean +1.39, median +1.46, 77% positive) is treated as a list-level or normalization property, so 'up' alone is not evidence; only genes above the list median percentile are treated as elevated.", "Transcript differences for SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1 and CHPT1 are assumed to translate into proportionate enzyme activity and flux; no protein, activity, isotope-tracing or lipid measurement of these enzymes is supplied.", "Lysosomal hydrolase transcript elevation is assumed to reflect increased lipid catabolic flux rather than compensatory upregulation for impaired hydrolase function; both are compatible with the data.", "The comparison is assumed to reflect a within-cell metabolic difference between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia rather than a shift in the proportions of microglial or macrophage-like substates in the co-culture.", "Protein-spot rows are ambiguous (2-6 candidate genes per spot, dominated by keratin, actin, ANXA1 and TALDO1) and are treated as non-informative for this mechanism; no protein spot is claimed to identify a lipid enzyme.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipoprotein lipid; the uptake arm of the mechanism assumes this external lipid source is available and equal for both genotypes."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, an SREBF1-associated lipogenic arm centred on SCD raises the monounsaturated acyl-CoA pool while PUFA/long-chain acyl-CoA activation transcripts fall (ACSL4, ACSL5); this makes Delta9-desaturation the rate-controlling step that channels carbon delivered by elevated scavenger uptake and lysosomal lipid hydrolysis into AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent glycerolipid and cholesteryl-ester storage plus CHPT1-dependent PC synthesis, predicting a lipidome shifted toward MUFA-rich triacylglycerol, cholesteryl ester and phosphatidylcholine and away from polyunsaturated membrane phospholipid, rather than toward fatty-acid oxidation or efflux.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. CAY10566 or A939572) or SCD knockdown in APOE4 microglia should collapse the genotype difference in neutral lipid, lowering triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester mass and lipid-droplet number toward APOE3 levels and lowering the 18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0 ratios of total phospholipid, while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD) and uptake receptor transcripts (SCARB1, CD36) largely unchanged. If SCD inhibition instead leaves APOE4 droplet and neutral-lipid excess intact, or if it abolishes the lysosomal transcript difference as well, the bottleneck is misplaced and the mechanism is weakened.", "LIPIDOMIC PREDICTION: untargeted lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under mock conditions should show increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester fractions, increased abundance of 16:1- and 18:1-containing TAG, CE and PC species, and a decreased fraction of 20:4- and 22:6-containing phospholipids, with an increased MUFA:PUFA ratio in total phospholipid. Finding equal or higher PUFA-phospholipid fractions in APOE4, or no MUFA enrichment, would falsify the acyl-remodeling core of the claim.", "EPISTASIS PREDICTION: DGAT1 inhibition should redistribute the same MUFA carbon out of triacylglycerol into free fatty acid and phospholipid pools without normalizing the elevated MUFA:PUFA ratio, whereas SCD inhibition should normalize the ratio itself. If both perturbations produce identical lipidomic outcomes, esterification and desaturation cannot be ordered as proposed.", "SUFFICIENCY PREDICTION: loading APOE3 microglia with oleate should partially phenocopy the APOE4 neutral-lipid and MUFA-phospholipid profile without inducing the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program. Failure to phenocopy would indicate that MUFA supply is not the limiting input.", "FLUX PREDICTION: U-13C-acetate or D2O labelling should show higher fractional new synthesis of 16:1/18:1-containing TAG and PC in APOE4 than APOE3, and 13C-oleate pulse-chase should show slower oxidation and greater esterification of label in APOE4. Equal labelling kinetics between genotypes would weaken the inferred flux step.", "UPSTREAM-CONTROL PREDICTION: SREBP processing blockade (SCAP or S1P/S2P inhibition, or SREBF1 knockdown) should lower SCD, AGPAT2 and DGAT1 transcripts and reduce the neutral-lipid difference; if SCD and the neutral-lipid phenotype persist after SREBF1 loss, the proposed transcriptional origin of the bottleneck is wrong even if the SCD step itself survives.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL: the mechanism predicts no genotype difference in Lands-cycle-specific re-acylation flux into lyso-PC beyond what MUFA supply dictates; a measured increase in arachidonoyl re-acylation or in free arachidonate release would contradict the stated ACSL4-down arm."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:COLEC12, gene:MRC1, gene:CD163) and for lysosomal lipid hydrolases and their regulators (gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A). We infer, but have not measured, an increased flux of exogenous lipid through the endolysosome that liberates fatty acids and sterol into the cytosol.", "STEP 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): An SREBP1-type lipogenic program is transcriptionally elevated (gene:SREBF1) together with cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply genes (gene:SLC25A1, gene:ACSS2, gene:ACAT2), which we infer increases malonyl-CoA-dependent and acetate-dependent acyl-CoA generation; no FASN or ACACA row is supplied, so this step is inference from regulators only.", "STEP 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred enzymatic flux): Elevated gene:SCD is proposed to raise stearoyl/palmitoyl-CoA Delta9-desaturation, making 16:1- and 18:1-CoA the dominant esterifiable acyl species, while reduced gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 lower activation of polyunsaturated and very-long-chain fatty acids into CoA thioesters. Desaturation capacity, not substrate delivery, is proposed to set the rate of downstream esterification.", "STEP 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux and localization): MUFA-CoA is esterified through the glycerolipid pathway (gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT2, gene:AGPAT4) to phosphatidate and diacylglycerol, then partitioned by gene:DGAT1 to triacylglycerol, by gene:SOAT1 to cholesteryl ester, and by gene:CHPT1 to phosphatidylcholine; gene:SCP2 and gene:MGLL are consistent with active intracellular lipid transfer and acylglycerol turnover rather than inert storage.", "STEP 5 (inferred lipid phenotype): The net consequence is a MUFA-enriched neutral-lipid pool (droplet triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester) and a membrane phospholipid pool depleted of polyunsaturated species, with sterol handling biased toward esterification (gene:SOAT1) rather than efflux; no lipid, droplet, oxidation or efflux measurement is supplied, so this step is entirely predicted.", "STEP 6 (inferred functional consequence): Sequestration of catabolically liberated fatty acid as MUFA-rich neutral lipid, together with sustained lysosomal hydrolase expression, is proposed to keep APOE4 microglia in a lipid-loaded, uptake-competent but disposal-limited state under mock conditions."], "title": "SCD-dependent monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply is the bottleneck routing lysosomally liberated lipid into MUFA-enriched glycerolipid storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17234058265332497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.047450501588038915, "cosine_similarity": 0.012325948645630035, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7246569579288026, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17234058265332497, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.047450501588038915, "cosine_similarity": 0.012325948645630035, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7246569579288026, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.18009775, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 454}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_050", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong positive skew (77% of rows positive, median +1.46); pathway claims are therefore made relative to the list-wide central tendency, assuming that this internal reference approximates a neutral baseline.", "Transcript abundance for peroxidases and PPP enzymes is assumed to track the corresponding protein and, less safely, catalytic capacity; no enzyme activity, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, GSH/GSSG ratio, peroxide level or lipid-peroxidation measurement is present in the data.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; spot changes are treated as consistency checks only, never as identification of a single protein (e.g. protein_spot:017 contains CAT but also CORO1C and ENTPD5).", "The astrocyte co-culture and the mock condition are assumed comparable between APOE3 and APOE4 lines, so that genotype rather than differential astrocyte content drives the transcript differences.", "Mitochondrial-genome transcript ratios (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB) are assumed to be partly normalization-sensitive; they are used only as weak, internally inconsistent support."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia sit in a high oxidative-catabolism state (coherently elevated nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/TCA transcripts) and coordinately raise thiol- and selenium-dependent peroxidase transcripts (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, TXNDC17, SELENOW, MGST2, GSS), while transcripts for cytosolic NADPH-regenerating and pentose-phosphate steps are relatively reduced (TALDO1, PGD, ME1, NADK below the list-wide central tendency) and only the mitochondrial transhydrogenase NNT is raised. We hypothesise that NADPH-dependent recycling of peroxiredoxin/glutathione/thioredoxin couples, not peroxidase protein availability, is the limiting node in APOE4, and that the cells compensate by lowering polyunsaturated-lipid peroxidation substrate (ACSL4, ALOX15 down), increasing monounsaturated fatty-acid synthesis (SCD) and neutral-lipid/sterol esterification and lysosomal turnover (DGAT1, SOAT1, sterol-synthesis and lysosomal hydrolase transcripts up), producing the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype. Causality is not established by these data; the peroxisomal arm of the assigned focus (PEX genes, catalase, ABCD1/2, ether-lipid synthesis) is not supported and is rejected.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute pharmacological or genetic restriction of cytosolic NADPH regeneration (G6PD inhibition, e.g. G6PDi-1, or G6PD/PGD knockdown) in mock-treated co-cultures should cause a larger drop in GSH/GSSG and a larger rise in BODIPY-C11 lipid-peroxidation signal and cell death in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3 microglia; equal or smaller APOE4 sensitivity would weaken the NADPH-bottleneck claim.", "GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) or selenium withdrawal should sensitise APOE4 preferentially, and this sensitisation should be rescued by exogenous oleate or by NADPH-boosting manipulation (NAD kinase overexpression, malic-enzyme/IDH1 supply); failure of oleate or NADPH boosting to rescue would falsify the substrate-limitation step.", "SCD inhibition should convert the APOE4 storage phenotype into measurable peroxidation: reduced neutral-lipid droplet content with increased oxidised-phospholipid signal in APOE4 but not APOE3; if SCD inhibition reduces droplets equally in both genotypes without genotype-specific peroxidation, step 5 is wrong.", "NNT knockdown, or uncoupling with low-dose FCCP, should raise matrix H2O2 (mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation) selectively in APOE4; no genotype difference would weaken the proposed mitochondrial NADPH-sourcing step.", "Direct redox metabolomics should show APOE4 with equal or lower NADPH/NADP+ and equal or lower GSH/GSSG despite higher peroxidase transcripts; finding APOE4 with clearly higher NADPH/NADP+ and no elevation of peroxide or lipid-peroxidation markers would falsify the whole mechanism and favour a purely lysosomal/lipogenic (non-redox) explanation.", "Peroxisomal rejection test: catalase activity, plasmalogen (ether-lipid) levels and C26:0/C22:0 VLCFA ratios should not differ substantially between genotypes; a clear VLCFA or plasmalogen deficit in APOE4 would indicate the rejected peroxisomal mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia show coherently higher transcript abundance for nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and TCA/substrate-entry components (gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:MPC2, gene:ETFA, gene:HADHA); we infer, but do not measure, increased electron flux and therefore increased mitochondrial and cytosolic hydroperoxide production.", "Consistent with that inferred peroxide load, thiol/selenoperoxidase and repair transcripts are raised above the list-wide central tendency (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:SELENOW, gene:MGST2, gene:GSS, gene:MSRA); this is measured RNA abundance, not measured peroxidase activity.", "The reducing-equivalent supply that these enzymes require is not co-elevated: pentose-phosphate and cytosolic NADPH-linked transcripts sit at or below the central tendency of this differential list (gene:TALDO1, gene:PGD, gene:ME1, gene:NADK), and PPP-enzyme-containing protein spots are unchanged (protein_spot:018, protein_spot:021, protein_spot:019, protein_spot:022); we therefore propose NADPH regeneration, not peroxidase abundance, as the primary bottleneck.", "Elevated gene:NNT indicates a proposed shift of NADPH sourcing to the mitochondrial matrix, coupling peroxide clearance to proton-motive force and making cytosolic peroxiredoxin/glutathione recycling more sensitive to respiratory perturbation (inferred flux, not measured).", "Under a constrained NADPH budget the cells lower the peroxidation-prone lipid pool: transcripts for PUFA-CoA activation and lipoxygenation fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ALOX15) while monounsaturation rises (gene:SCD), reducing bis-allylic substrate per unit membrane lipid.", "Excess and oxidised lipid is diverted into esterified/stored and lysosomal compartments rather than oxidised: sterol-synthesis and esterification transcripts (gene:SREBF1, gene:DHCR24, gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:MGLL) and lysosomal hydrolase/biogenesis transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:TFEB) are elevated, which we propose is the transcriptional signature underlying the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise thiol/selenoperoxidase peroxide-clearance demand without matching cytosolic NADPH regeneration, forcing a monounsaturation-and-storage lipid strategy"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19449470147324888, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09604887070115467, "cosine_similarity": 0.003879441070440959, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7776601941747573, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.19449470147324888, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09604887070115467, "cosine_similarity": 0.003879441070440959, "direction_accuracy": 0.21197411003236247, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7776601941747573, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9746055, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 455}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA transcript fold-changes for HK2, PFKP, and the TCA/OXPHOS gene set are assumed to correlate directionally with the corresponding protein abundance and enzymatic activity in this iPSC-microglia/astrocyte co-culture system; this is not verified here because matching protein-spot data are sparse, multi-candidate, and largely non-significant.", "The discovery.json rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all entries carry adjusted p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased whole transcriptome; apparent pathway-level coherence could partly reflect selection for large fold-changes, and many core glycolysis/OXPHOS/beta-oxidation genes (e.g., PKM, LDHA, LDHB, GAPDH, PDHA1, PDHB, PDK1-4, CPT1A, TFAM, PPARGC1A, CS) are absent from the supplied list, leaving the pathway reconstruction incomplete.", "The unspecified RNA log fold-change base is preserved as reported; percentile comparisons use only the supplied numeric values without assuming base-10 or base-2.", "Protein-spot candidate-gene lists are ambiguous (3-5 genes per spot); no protein-spot signal is treated as uniquely identifying a specific metabolic enzyme.", "No claim of causality between APOE4 genotype and this transcript pattern is made; the isogenic mock-treatment comparison is a single timepoint (Day 30) snapshot and cannot establish direction of causation or persistence."], "claim": "In isogenic iPSC-derived microglia under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs APOE3) shows strong, coordinated transcript-level suppression of the glycolytic commitment enzymes HK2 and PFKP alongside strong upregulation of TCA-cycle, respiratory-chain, and adenine-nucleotide-carrier transcripts and increased glucose/monocarboxylate transporter transcripts; this pattern is consistent with (but does not prove) a shift in preferred routing of glucose-derived carbon from cytosolic glycolysis toward mitochondrial oxidative metabolism as a candidate bottleneck differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 microglia.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: measuring extracellular acidification rate (ECAR, glycolytic proxy) and oxygen consumption rate (OCR, mitochondrial proxy) in matched APOE3 vs APOE4 mock microglia should show a lower ECAR/OCR ratio in APOE4; restoring HK2 expression/activity in APOE4 microglia should raise ECAR toward APOE3 levels. If the ECAR/OCR ratio is unchanged or higher in APOE4, or HK2 restoration fails to shift ECAR, the proposed carbon-routing bottleneck would be weakened.", "Targeted protein quantification (e.g., western blot or targeted MS) for HK2, OGDH, and MDH1 in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should mirror the transcript directions (HK2 protein lower, OGDH/MDH1 protein higher) beyond the ambiguity of the current multi-candidate protein spots; if HK2 protein is unchanged or increased despite the strongly reduced mRNA, or if OGDH/MDH1 protein does not track the RNA increase, the inferred transcript-to-protein-to-flux chain would be weakened."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: gene:HK2 (log2FC -3.67, adj p=7.7e-191) and gene:PFKP (log2FC -3.08, adj p=2.0e-30) transcripts, encoding the first committed/rate-limiting glycolytic enzymes, fall in the bottom ~4-6th percentile of all 2212 measured RNA fold-changes, despite 77% of the full dataset showing positive fold-changes -- an outlier suppression against the dataset's overall positive skew.", "Inferred (not measured): lower HK2 transcript may reduce HK2 protein abundance and thus capacity to commit glucose to glycolysis at the hexokinase step; because HK2 protein can also physically associate with the outer mitochondrial membrane (VDAC), its reduction could additionally alter glycolysis-mitochondria coupling, a localization effect that is not assessed by any supplied observation.", "Measured: TCA-cycle and respiratory-chain transcripts are strongly upregulated and cluster in the top ~1-5th percentile of the whole distribution: gene:OGDH (+8.56, adj p=5.5e-62), gene:MDH1 (+8.72, adj p=2.1e-21), gene:ACO2 (+3.54, adj p=1.6e-37), gene:DLD (+5.54, adj p=2.8e-20), gene:SDHB (+1.65), gene:UQCRC2 (+4.02), gene:COX7A2 (+3.36), gene:ATP5F1B (+2.65), and the mitochondrial ADP/ATP carrier gene:SLC25A5 (+5.56).", "Measured: glucose transporter transcripts gene:SLC2A1 (+2.37) and gene:SLC2A3 (+3.73), plus the monocarboxylate transporter gene:SLC16A1 (+1.12), are also elevated, indicating increased transcriptional capacity for glucose/monocarboxylate uptake alongside gene:PDP1 (+3.00), a phosphatase that activates pyruvate dehydrogenase and would favor pyruvate entry into the TCA cycle over lactate production.", "Inferred (activity/flux, not measured): together these transcript changes are consistent with APOE4 microglia transcriptionally re-weighting glucose-carbon handling away from the glycolysis/lactate route and toward mitochondrial oxidation; no extracellular flux (ECAR/OCR), metabolite, or enzyme-activity data are supplied, so actual flux redirection is inferred, not observed.", "Counter-evidence/caveat: the shift is not pathway-uniform -- other glycolytic transcripts are simultaneously increased (gene:GPI +2.06, gene:PFKM +2.41, gene:ENO1 +2.17), indicating step/isoform-specific rather than whole-pathway suppression, and protein-spot measurements that include HK3 or MDH1 among their several candidate genes (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:024, protein_spot:050) are all non-significant and cannot be attributed to a single enzyme, so protein-level support for the RNA pattern is weak or absent."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show transcriptional down-weighting of the hexokinase/PFK glycolytic commitment step coupled to an extreme TCA-cycle/OXPHOS transcript program, suggesting a shift in glucose-carbon routing toward mitochondrial oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5138912, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": false, "centered_cosine_defined": false, "cohort_rank": 8}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_005", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA fold-change direction is treated as an approximation of transcriptional regulation and does not necessarily predict protein output, translation rate, or degradation flux.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (each linked to several candidate genes); the HSP90B1/HSPA5/PDIA3 signal in protein_spot:001, :004, :005, :016 cannot be attributed with certainty to those specific proteins rather than co-migrating candidates.", "The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered, selected differential-expression list rather than an unbiased whole-transcriptome measurement; absence of canonical UPR genes XBP1, ATF4, ERN1(IRE1), and HSPA5 from the RNA list does not indicate they are unchanged, only that they were not reported here.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect values is not specified; magnitudes are used only for relative ranking/comparison within this dataset, not converted into literal fold-change multiples.", "No direct measurement of protein folding state, ER stress resolution, secretion rate, or APOE protein levels is available; all statements about folding capacity, flux, or secretory consequences are explicitly inferred, not observed.", "The isogenic APOE3/APOE4 comparison is assumed to control for background genetic variation, but replicate number and single-cell versus bulk aggregation details are not supplied."], "claim": "In APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-microglia under mock treatment, the ATF6-PERK(EIF2AK3)-CHOP(DDIT3) unfolded-protein-response transcriptional module and ER folding/glycosylation genes are more highly expressed at the RNA level, but ambiguous protein-spot signals containing the chaperones GRP94(HSP90B1) and BiP(HSPA5) show no corresponding significant increase in abundance; this RNA-protein discordance is consistent with (but does not prove) an ER chaperone-capacity bottleneck that limits effective resolution of secretory-pathway proteostatic stress in APOE4 microglia, superimposed on directionally mixed remodeling of ERAD and coat-protein trafficking transcripts.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["If ER chaperone protein capacity is pharmacologically or genetically boosted in APOE4 microglia (e.g., BiP/GRP94 overexpression or chemical chaperones such as TUDCA/4-PBA), DDIT3/CHOP transcript induction should decrease toward APOE3 levels; if CHOP induction is unchanged or increases, the chaperone-capacity-bottleneck mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: selective PERK (EIF2AK3) kinase inhibition in APOE4 microglia should blunt DDIT3/CHOP transcriptional induction if the PERK arm drives this effector; if CHOP induction persists unchanged after PERK inhibition, this points to an ATF6-dominant or PERK-independent process and would weaken the PERK-specific portion of this mechanism.", "Direct, gene-specific quantification of BiP (HSPA5) and GRP94 (HSP90B1) protein (e.g., by targeted immunoassay rather than ambiguous 2D-gel spots) should show no significant increase, or a decrease, in APOE4 relative to APOE3; if such targeted assays instead show a clear, significant increase in chaperone protein matching the RNA-level UPR signature, the proposed RNA-protein discordance and the chaperone-capacity-bottleneck claim would be falsified."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured RNA increases in the UPR sensor/effector transcripts ATF6 (+4.04) and EIF2AK3/PERK (+1.51) together with the downstream effector DDIT3/CHOP (+2.79) indicate greater transcriptional engagement of this UPR arm in APOE4 microglia (gene:ATF6, gene:EIF2AK3, gene:DDIT3).", "Downstream ER-folding-support transcripts MANF (+2.95), CRELD2 (+1.01) and the oxidoreductase ERO1A (+1.21) are also elevated, consistent with an inferred attempt to increase ER oxidative-folding capacity (gene:MANF, gene:CRELD2, gene:ERO1A); this is a transcriptional signal, not a measured increase in folding flux.", "Despite this transcriptional signature, ambiguous protein spots whose candidate-gene lists include the chaperones GRP94 (HSP90B1) and BiP (HSPA5) show small, non-significant, and in two cases negative fold-changes (protein_spot:001 -0.49 p=0.11; protein_spot:004 -0.68 p=0.14; protein_spot:005 -0.14 p=0.25), i.e. no detectable increase in chaperone protein abundance.", "This RNA-versus-protein discordance is inferred (not measured) to reflect a bottleneck between UPR transcriptional induction and actual chaperone protein accumulation, potentially via PERK-associated translational attenuation, altered chaperone turnover, or a lag not captured at this single timepoint; causal direction is not established.", "Concurrent, direction-mixed transcriptional remodeling of ERAD and coat/cargo trafficking genes is observed (down: gene:SEL1L -2.09, gene:EDEM1 -1.37, gene:DERL1 -1.19, gene:SEC24D -1.39, gene:SEC22A -1.21, gene:TMED5 -1.52; up: gene:EDEM2 +1.96, gene:UBE2J1 +4.74, gene:UGGT1 +2.58, gene:COPA +4.27, gene:COPE +4.33, gene:TMED1 +3.01, gene:SEC22C +3.70), together with strong induction of N-glycosylation genes DDOST (+6.22) and STT3A (+3.39); this precludes a single clean 'more' or 'less' trafficking conclusion and is presented as a coherent-but-mixed contextual signal rather than a clean supporting arm.", "Given that APOE transcript itself is elevated (gene:APOE +1.24), increasing inferred biosynthetic/glycosylation/secretory burden on the ER, the hypothesized chaperone-capacity mismatch could plausibly constrain folding/export of secretory clients including APOE, but no secretion, folding-state, or flux measurement is available to confirm this inference."], "title": "UPR transcriptional induction outpaces chaperone protein accumulation, creating an ER proteostasis capacity bottleneck in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_005", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5271397, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": false, "centered_cosine_defined": false, "cohort_rank": 9}, {"id": "sonnet-original-b01-hyp_006", "cohort": "sonnet-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA transcript abundance changes for TNFAIP3, TMEM173, IFI16, NLRP1/NLRP3, and the chemokine/I\u03baB genes are assumed to partly track corresponding protein abundance and pathway activity; no protein-level measurement of A20, STING, IFI16, or inflammasome components is available in this dataset to confirm this.", "Background knowledge that A20/TNFAIP3 terminates NF-\u03baB/inflammasome signaling, that STING/IFI16 act as cytosolic nucleic-acid sensors, and that NFKBIB/NFKBID/NFKBIL1/NFKBIZ are NF-\u03baB-inducible I\u03baB-family genes is treated as unverified prior knowledge, not confirmed by this dataset.", "Protein_spot:055 (candidate genes CAPZB, IFIT3, ACTG2, CLIC1, CTSB) is treated as weak, non-unique corroborating evidence for an interferon-adjacent protein change; the spot is not uniquely attributable to IFIT3.", "The RNA rows analyzed are a pre-selected list of differentially expressed genes (all reported as adjusted-p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased whole-transcriptome sample, so pathway coherence estimates are conditioned on this selection and may not generalize to unmeasured genes.", "No biological replicate count is given (metadata marks it 'not supplied'), so the statistical robustness of individual gene-level effects cannot be independently verified beyond the reported p-values."], "claim": "In isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia under mock (unstimulated) conditions, reduced TNFAIP3 transcript co-occurs with a broad, internally consistent increase in transcripts encoding cytosolic nucleic-acid sensors (TMEM173/STING, IFI16), inflammasome-pathway genes (NLRP1, NLRP3, IL18), NF-\u03baB-responsive chemokines/cytokines (CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL3, CXCL8, CXCL16, CCL2, CCL13, TNFSF9, TNFSF12, TNFSF13), I\u03baB-family feedback genes (NFKBIB, NFKBID, NFKBIL1, NFKBIZ), and complement subunits (C1QA, C1QB, C1QC), together with reduced IRF2 and SOCS4. This pattern is consistent with, but does not prove, a partially disinhibited baseline inflammatory/danger-sensing transcriptional tone in APOE4 microglia, with TNFAIP3 loss as a plausible rate-limiting node.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["If TNFAIP3 (A20) protein/function is experimentally restored in APOE4 microglia (e.g., by re-expression or a deubiquitinase-activity-preserving approach), NF-\u03baB-responsive chemokine transcripts (CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL3, CXCL8, CCL2) and inflammasome-linked transcripts (NLRP3, IL18) should decrease toward APOE3-like levels; if these transcripts remain unchanged or increase further after A20 restoration, the proposed A20-centered bottleneck would be weakened.", "If STING (TMEM173) or IFI16 is knocked down or pharmacologically inhibited in APOE4 microglia, downstream NF-\u03baB-linked chemokine transcripts should partially normalize; if chemokine/cytokine transcripts are unaffected, this would argue against a STING/IFI16-to-NF-\u03baB link and favor an A20-independent or alternative upstream driver.", "Direct measurement of NF-\u03baB pathway activation (e.g., nuclear p65 localization or phospho-p65) in unstimulated APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show elevated baseline activation if this transcriptional signature reflects genuinely active signaling rather than differential mRNA stability or transcriptional noise; absence of elevated p65 activation despite these transcript differences would weaken the mechanistic link claimed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: TNFAIP3 (A20) transcript is significantly reduced in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia (gene:TNFAIP3, effect -1.05, padj 7.3e-16). A20 protein is a canonical deubiquitinase-based terminator of TLR/IL-1R/TNFR-driven NF-\u03baB and inflammasome signaling (background knowledge, unverified against this dataset).", "Inferred (not measured): if reduced TNFAIP3 mRNA is accompanied by reduced A20 protein/activity, the threshold for sustained NF-\u03baB and inflammasome-adjacent transcription downstream of tonic pattern-recognition receptor engagement would be lowered.", "Measured: transcripts for the cytosolic DNA/danger sensors TMEM173 (STING) and IFI16 are elevated in APOE4 (padj 1.6e-166 and 1.5e-225 respectively), indicating higher steady-state mRNA for the upstream sensing arm that A20-linked feedback normally restrains.", "Measured: inflammasome-associated transcripts NLRP1, NLRP3, and IL18 are elevated (effects 3.55, 1.09, 1.46; all padj \u003c5e-13), consistent with increased transcriptional priming of the inflammasome pathway, but inflammasome assembly/activity and IL-18 processing/secretion are not measured.", "Measured: a broad set of NF-\u03baB-responsive chemokine/cytokine transcripts (CXCL1/2/3/8/16, CCL2, CCL13, TNFSF9/12/13) and I\u03baB-family feedback genes (NFKBIB, NFKBID, NFKBIL1, NFKBIZ) are concordantly elevated, a pattern classically associated with active NF-\u03baB-driven transcription including its own delayed-feedback arm (background knowledge, unverified).", "Measured: IRF2 (a repressor of IRF-driven transcription) and SOCS4 are reduced (effects -1.17 and -1.44), which could remove additional inferred brakes on IRF/JAK-linked transcriptional output, though no direct IRF or JAK-STAT activity readout is available.", "Net inferred consequence: APOE4 microglia may occupy a transcriptionally 'primed' pro-inflammatory/danger-sensing state at mock baseline; this describes an association among measured transcripts, not a demonstrated increase in protein activity, secreted cytokine flux, subcellular localization, or causal direction, none of which are measured here."], "title": "Selective loss of the A20 (TNFAIP3) negative-feedback brake accompanies a coherent nucleic-acid-sensing / NF-\u03baB-adjacent transcriptional signature in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_006", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.5075968, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": false, "centered_cosine_defined": false, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "sonnet-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "sonnet-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA 'effect' values are log fold changes on an unspecified logarithm base; only sign and relative magnitude across genes (not the exact fold-change scale) are used for interpretation.", "The RNA rows are a curated, significant differential-expression subset (all 2212 rows have adjusted p\u003c0.05), not an unbiased whole transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g., PPARGC1A, TFAM, PINK1, most other mtDNA transcripts) means it is unmeasured or not selected, not that it is unchanged.", "Genes within a pathway are treated descriptively as a group but are not statistically independent observations; the evidence table is a coherence summary, not a formal pathway-enrichment test.", "Transcript-level increases or decreases are assumed only to reflect gene expression, not confirmed protein abundance, complex assembly, or metabolic flux; protein-spot candidates are multi-gene and ambiguous and are used only to test compatibility, not to confirm any single protein's change.", "Any inference of impaired mitochondrial genome expression or mtDNA copy number is indirect, based only on the direction of mtDNA-encoded transcripts, since mtDNA copy number, mitochondrial protein levels, and respiratory flux are not measured in this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 (vs isogenic APOE3) iPSC-microglia display a coordinated increase in nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain (ETC) and TCA-cycle transcripts together with a mitochondrial-genome-encoded ETC transcript deficit (majority-negative among the mtDNA-encoded set, against the dataset's strong positive background) and reduced hexokinase-2 (HK2) transcript. This transcript-level pattern is consistent with an attempted but incomplete nuclear compensatory response to impaired mitochondrial-genome-derived ETC subunit supply, accompanied by reduced glycolysis-mitochondria coupling capacity, rather than with an established increase in oxidative phosphorylation flux or a classic Warburg-type glycolytic shift. Whether respiratory or glycolytic flux is actually altered is not established by these transcript/protein-spot data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective/discriminating test: If mtDNA copy number and mitochondrially-translated protein levels (e.g., MT-CO1, MT-ATP6 protein) are measured in APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia and found to be unchanged or increased in proportion to the nuclear ETC transcript increase, this would weaken the mitonuclear-imbalance mechanism in favor of a purely nuclear transcriptional/activation explanation.", "Prospective/discriminating test: Direct measurement of basal and maximal oxygen consumption rate (e.g., Seahorse) in APOE4 vs APOE3 mock-treated microglia should show reduced or unchanged ATP-linked/maximal respiration relative to the degree of nuclear ETC transcript induction if the mechanism holds; a proportional increase in respiration matching the nuclear transcript increase would weaken the 'failed compensation' claim and instead support successful increased oxidative throughput.", "Prospective perturbation: Experimentally reducing mtDNA transcription/replication capacity (e.g., partial TFAM knockdown) in APOE3 microglia should reproduce the pattern of increased nuclear ETC/TCA transcripts, decreased mtDNA-encoded ETC transcripts, and increased DDIT3/HSPA9 seen in APOE4; failure to induce the nuclear compensatory transcripts under this perturbation would argue against the proposed retrograde-compensation link and favor the alternative that the metabolic transcript pattern is a downstream consequence of a broader, non-mitochondria-specific APOE4 activation state."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["In APOE4 microglia, transcripts encoding nearly all detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunits (complexes I, II, III, IV, V) and detected TCA-cycle enzymes are increased versus APOE3 (e.g., gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:OGDH, gene:MDH1, gene:ACO2), suggesting a nuclear transcriptional program directed at expanding oxidative-phosphorylation machinery capacity.", "In contrast, transcripts for several mitochondrial-DNA-encoded ETC subunits are reduced (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2), while two others in the same encoded set are increased (gene:MT-ND4L, gene:MT-ND5), yielding a majority-negative mtDNA-encoded subset that is a striking reversal of the dataset's strong overall positive bias (~77% of all selected RNA rows are positive).", "This nuclear-up/mtDNA-mixed-to-down asymmetry is a signature of mitonuclear protein/transcript imbalance, which can arise when mitochondrial genome expression, replication, or copy number is constrained relative to nuclear transcriptional drive for OXPHOS components; it does not by itself establish altered mtDNA copy number or ETC complex assembly, which are not measured here.", "Concurrent increases in the mitochondrial/integrated stress markers gene:DDIT3 (CHOP) and gene:HSPA9 (mtHSP70), plus the mitochondrial fission factor gene:FIS1, indicate that APOE4 microglia are transcriptionally engaging a mitochondrial stress/quality-control response, consistent with cells reacting to an ETC subunit supply mismatch rather than having already achieved a stable, higher-throughput oxidative state.", "The strong reduction of gene:HK2 (and gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2), alongside increases in glucose transporters and other glycolytic genes (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3, gene:GPI, gene:ENO1, gene:PFKM), produces a mixed rather than uniformly Warburg-like glycolytic transcript profile; because HK2 is the isoform most associated with mitochondrial (VDAC) coupling, its reduction argues against interpreting the glycolytic gene increases as a coherent compensatory shift away from oxidative metabolism.", "Protein-spot data relevant to these pathways (protein_spot:038 positive/significant vs protein_spot:039 negative/non-significant, both listing overlapping aldolase/GAPDH candidates; protein_spot:050 non-significant negative despite very strong positive gene:MDH1 RNA) are ambiguous and ambivalent, neither confirming nor cleanly falsifying the transcript-level pattern, and cannot be used to assign the change to a single named protein.", "Net inference: the combined nuclear-up/mtDNA-mixed/HK2-down/stress-marker-up transcript pattern is most consistent with an incomplete or unsuccessful compensatory attempt to sustain oxidative capacity in APOE4 microglia, rather than with confirmed increased oxidative flux, confirmed glycolytic flux increase, or an established functional respiratory defect."], "title": "APOE4 microglia show a mitonuclear ETC transcript imbalance with reduced HK2, consistent with a partial/failed compensatory mitochondrial response rather than increased oxidative or glycolytic throughput"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0, "cosine_similarity": 0.0, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6457022653721682, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 0.6530341, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": false, "centered_cosine_defined": false, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_041", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 genes, all |effect|\u003e=1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77% positive) on a reported logarithm of unspecified base; program directions were judged against that 77%-positive background, and genes absent from the list are unknown, not unchanged.", "Program membership was fixed from canonical pathway definitions before directions were inspected; represented members are only 20-75% of each queried set, and members are not statistically independent, so the coherence reported is descriptive, not a formal enrichment test.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme/carrier protein amount well enough to change lipid routing; no flux, respirometry, enzyme activity, lipid-droplet or lipidomic measurement is supplied, so 'routing' and 'capacity' are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2-6-candidate ambiguous (KRT1/KRT10/ACTB dominate candidate lists) and contain no OXPHOS, carrier or lipogenic enzyme candidate; they are used only for compatibility, never to confirm an individual protein.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 with astrocyte co-culture; differences in cell-type composition, capture depth or normalization between genotypes (a plausible cause of the global positive skew) are assumed not to generate the specific carrier/sterol/lysosome pattern.", "Any ATP-supply or phagocytic-clearance shortfall implied by the unmatched mtDNA-encoded transcripts is a predicted vulnerability under future challenge, not an ongoing defect demonstrated in this mock condition."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes) differ from APOE3 principally by a coordinated cell-state change in mitochondrial carbon handling: nuclear-encoded TCA, anaplerotic and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts (notably the citrate carrier SLC25A1, MPC2, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, MDH1/GOT1 shuttle) are elevated far above the up-biased selected-list background, and this configuration is coupled to an elevated SREBP-type sterol/monounsaturated-fatty-acid synthesis and acyl-remodeling program and to expanded lysosomal-hydrolase/v-ATPase transcripts. The predicted consequence is anabolic routing of mitochondrial carbon toward cytosolic sterol and MUFA-containing lipid production with increased lysosomal lipid catabolic capacity, rather than a demonstrated bioenergetic gain: mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ND4) move in the opposite direction, so increased assembled respiratory capacity is not established. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred and untested here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective isotope tracing (U-13C-glucose and U-13C-glutamine) in mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show greater 13C incorporation into cholesterol and into 16:1/18:1 fatty acids per unit citrate label in APOE4; equal or lower incorporation would weaken the routing mechanism.", "Prospective lipidomics of the same mock cultures should show APOE4 \u003e APOE3 for free cholesterol/cholesteryl esters and for MUFA-containing TAG/PC species, with an increased 18:1/18:0 desaturation index and relative depletion of 20:4-containing species; an APOE4 lipidome enriched in PUFA species or with lower cholesteryl esters would falsify the predicted lipid output.", "Prospective pharmacological test: inhibiting citrate export/cytosolic acetyl-CoA supply (SLC25A1 inhibitor CTPI-2 or ACLY inhibitor) or SCD should collapse the APOE4-vs-APOE3 sterol/MUFA lipid difference while leaving the lysosomal-hydrolase transcript elevation largely intact; if the lipid difference persists unchanged, the acetyl-CoA-routing step is wrong.", "Prospective bioenergetics/assembly test: despite the nuclear OXPHOS transcript elevation, APOE4 mock microglia should not show a proportional increase in assembled complex I/IV (BN-PAGE) or in maximal respiration; a large, matched increase in assembled complexes and maximal OCR would favor a straightforward increased-oxidative-throughput explanation over the routing-plus-mito-nuclear-mismatch mechanism.", "Prospective challenge test: on myelin- or apoptotic-cell-lipid loading, APOE4 microglia should accumulate more cholesteryl-ester-rich droplets and show impaired clearance kinetics relative to APOE3 even though lysosomal hydrolase transcripts are higher; equal or better clearance would indicate successful adaptation and weaken the predicted vulnerability."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype (mock, day 30, astrocyte co-culture) is associated with coordinated elevation of nuclear-encoded oxidative/TCA transcripts: all 37 represented nuclear OXPHOS subunit genes and all 11 represented TCA/anaplerotic genes are positive, with median effects (2.6 and 4.5 on the reported log scale) well above the selected-list median of 1.46 in a list that is already 77% positive (permutation P\u003c=0.003).", "Within that program the strongest members are carbon-routing components rather than terminal oxidases: mitochondrial pyruvate and metabolite carriers (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47 citrate carrier, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A5 +5.56) and cytosolic shuttle/anaplerotic enzymes (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.44, gene:GLUD1 +3.24, gene:GLS +1.40, gene:ME1 +1.36), consistent with a state configured to export mitochondrial citrate and regenerate cytosolic reducing equivalents.", "Exported citrate plus acetate salvage (gene:ACSS2 +2.93) supplies cytosolic acetyl-CoA to an elevated SREBP-type lipogenic program: gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR (10/10 represented sterol genes positive) and gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59.", "Newly made sterol and MUFA acyl chains are esterified and incorporated into glycerolipids/phospholipids by an up-shifted acylation/remodeling set (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:TAZ +3.26), while PUFA-preferring activation is reduced (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:GPAT3 -2.23), predicting a lipidome biased toward cholesterol/cholesteryl-ester and MUFA-containing species and relatively depleted of PUFA-containing species.", "In parallel, lysosomal catabolic capacity transcripts expand (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23; 25/27 represented members positive), providing degradative/recycling capacity for the increased sterol and sphingolipid load; gene:CTSS (-5.57) and gene:IDS (-1.56) are exceptions.", "The nuclear program is not matched by mtDNA-encoded transcripts (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80 against gene:MT-ND5 +1.93, gene:MT-ND4L +1.95), so the state should be read as altered carbon routing plus increased biosynthetic/degradative capacity, not as proven higher respiratory flux; any ATP-supply deficit would most likely be revealed only under a future energetic or phagocytic challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a mitochondrial carbon-export state that routes acetyl-CoA into sterol/MUFA lipid synthesis with parallel lysosomal expansion"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25458774877229257, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12724844353005088, "cosine_similarity": -0.0017206679397194175, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_041", "mean_absolute_error": 0.719453074433657, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.25458774877229257, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.12724844353005088, "cosine_similarity": -0.0017206679397194175, "direction_accuracy": 0.18770226537216828, "mean_absolute_error": 0.719453074433657, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.02211375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 105}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_148", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects (unspecified logarithm base, threshold |log FC| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) reflect real genotype-dependent expression differences and not only normalisation or composition artefacts, despite the strong list-wide upward shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46); all pathway claims are made relative to that shifted background, not to zero.", "Increased hydrolase mRNA is accompanied by increased mature enzyme in the acidic compartment; this was not measured, and the 2-D protein spots cannot test it.", "Genes absent from the supplied thresholded list (e.g. ASAH1, SGMS1, SPHK1/2, UGCG, PSAP, NPC1) were measured and fell below the |log FC| \u003e 1 threshold rather than being undetected; if they were simply not assayed, the 'unmatched disposal capacity' argument loses its main support.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are treated as non-identifying; no protein in this dataset is assigned to a single gene product.", "The lysosomal/sphingolipid transcript pattern is microglia-intrinsic rather than imposed by the co-cultured astrocytes, and reflects a steady state rather than a transient day-30 differentiation-stage difference.", "No sphingolipid, cholesterol or flux measurement is present in the supplied data; every lipid-pool and transport statement is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 cells by a selective, above-background transcriptional elevation of acidic-compartment sphingolipid hydrolases (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GLA, plus non-lysosomal GBA2) embedded in a partial TFEB/V-ATPase/cathepsin program, whereas the transcripts for ceramide- and sphingoid-base-consuming steps sit at or below the list-wide shift. We hypothesise that this asymmetry creates a flux imbalance in which ceramide disposal, not ceramide generation, is the bottleneck, producing ceramide/sphingosine build-up on late-endosomal and lysosomal membranes that slows Rab7/retromer-dependent cargo and lipid egress and keeps ER sterol sensing 'lipid-poor', sustaining the SREBP-driven uptake/synthesis program and a reactive microglial state. Causality is not established by these data; only mRNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured, and no sphingolipid species were measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Targeted sphingolipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs isogenic APOE3 microglia (mock, day 30) will show higher total and long-chain ceramide and higher sphingosine with a decreased sphingomyelin/ceramide ratio in APOE4; if ceramide and sphingosine are unchanged or lower, or sphingomyelin is higher, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Discriminating perturbation: lysosome-targeted acid ceramidase (ASAH1) overexpression, or ASM/SMPD1 knockdown, in APOE4 microglia will reduce the APOE4-APOE3 ceramide difference by at least half and restore endolysosomal cargo egress (faster DQ-BSA dequenching decay, restored Rab7-positive compartment size and myelin/apoptotic-cell clearance kinetics) while leaving TFEB target mRNA induction largely intact. If neither manipulation changes egress and only TFEB knockdown rescues it, the bottleneck is generic lysosome biogenesis and this sphingolipid-specific mechanism is wrong.", "Negative-control prediction that separates salvage from de novo synthesis: myriocin inhibition of serine palmitoyltransferase will not normalise APOE4 ceramide or the routing phenotype (consistent with unchanged SPTLC1/2 in the supplied list and elevated ORMDL2), whereas it would if de novo synthesis drove the phenotype; full myriocin rescue would weaken this hypothesis.", "Feed-forward loop test: lowering endolysosomal ceramide (ASAH1 overexpression or SMPD1 inhibition) will reduce SREBP-target transcripts (SREBF1, LDLR, DHCR24, SCD) and the CXCL8/CCL2/ITGAX reactive signature in APOE4 cells; unchanged SREBP targets after ceramide normalisation would falsify the sequestration loop while leaving the ceramide-accumulation core testable.", "Enzyme-level confirmation: acid sphingomyelinase and beta-glucocerebrosidase activity assays (fluorogenic substrate, acidic pH) on APOE4 vs APOE3 lysates will show higher activity in APOE4, matching the transcript direction; equal or lower activity would break the mRNA-to-activity assumption on which the whole chain rests."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_148", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for acidic-compartment sphingolipid hydrolases are elevated far above the list-wide upward shift (median log FC 4.13 for SMPD1/GBA/GBA2/HEXA/HEXB/GLA vs list median 1.46; permutation p=0.005), alongside TFEB, V-ATPase subunits and cathepsins (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK). Inferred, not measured: increased TFEB transcriptional activity and increased lysosomal hydrolase protein and enzymatic activity.", "Inferred flux step: higher acid sphingomyelinase and glycosidase capacity increases conversion of sphingomyelin and glyco-sphingolipids to ceramide inside the endolysosomal lumen and, via GBA2, at cytosol-facing membranes.", "Measured asymmetry: transcripts of the ceramide/sphingoid-base disposal and re-routing steps are not co-elevated - SGPL1 (log FC 1.09, 29th percentile of the list) and CERK (1.23, 38th) fall below the list median, and B4GALT5 is decreased (-1.88). Missing data: ASAH1, SGMS1, SPHK1/2, UGCG, PSAP, SPTLC1/2 are absent from the supplied thresholded differential list, so their status is unknown rather than unchanged.", "Predicted bottleneck: net ceramide (and sphingosine) accumulation in the limiting and intraluminal membranes of late endosomes/lysosomes because generation exceeds hydrolysis-to-sphingosine, phosphorylation and re-synthesis capacity. This lipid pool was not measured in this experiment.", "Inferred consequence on routing: ceramide-enriched, rigidified endolysosomal membranes impair tubulation-based recycling and cargo egress; the elevated Rab7/retromer-sorting transcripts (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:VPS35L) are read as compensatory demand on this step, not as evidence of increased transport flux.", "Inferred systemic loop: lipid retained in the endolysosome is poorly delivered to the ER, so sterol/lipid sensing remains permissive and the SREBP-linked uptake and synthesis program stays on (gene:SREBF1, gene:LDLR, gene:DHCR24, gene:SCD, gene:SCARB1, gene:ABCA7, gene:APOE), returning more substrate to the same bottleneck and maintaining a reactive, DAM-like transcriptional state (gene:ITGAX, gene:CLEC7A, gene:CXCL8, gene:CCL2, gene:NLRP3)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise endolysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts without matched ceramide-disposal capacity, making lysosomal ceramide clearance the rate-limiting step"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.044046020378464536, "cosine_similarity": -0.00191484185795132, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_148", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7074822006472492, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2137410921980578, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.044046020378464536, "cosine_similarity": -0.00191484185795132, "direction_accuracy": 0.16181229773462782, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7074822006472492, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.8512135, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 456}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_017", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all |log fold change| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) in an unspecified logarithm base; set-level direction and relative magnitude are interpretable, single extreme values are not, and absence of a gene means it was not selected, not that it is unchanged.", "The strong global upward skew (1705/2212 selected genes up; mean +1.39) is treated as a background offset, possibly of normalisation or composition origin, so lipid gene sets are judged against that background rather than against zero.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme activity and flux capacity for the acyltransferase, hydrolase and desaturase steps; no enzyme activity, metabolite, lipid species or organelle measurement was supplied.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; the ANXA1-containing spot train is only weak corroboration and the same spot set could reflect other candidates or proteoform shifts.", "Astrocyte co-culture means measured RNA may include or be influenced by non-microglial contribution; cell-type purity of the differential list is unverified.", "Background pathway assignments of genes to lysosomal, glycerolipid and Lands-cycle steps are unverified literature knowledge, not derived from the supplied files."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia show a coordinated transcriptional up-shift of lipid-uptake receptors and lysosomal lipid/glyco-hydrolases together with the glycerol-3-phosphate acylation and neutral-lipid esterification arm (GPAT4, AGPAT2, DGAT1, SOAT1) and the Lands-cycle re-acylation enzymes (LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2), while the PUFA-preferring ligase ACSL4 and the mitochondrially encoded OXPHOS transcripts fall. We hypothesise that the rate-controlling step distinguishing APOE4 is not lipid ingestion or hydrolysis but disposal of the liberated fatty acids: with oxidative and efflux routes not up-shifted, flux is diverted into SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA and re-esterification into triacylglycerol/sterol ester and into re-acylated phospholipid, producing MUFA-enriched, arachidonoyl-poor membranes and expanded neutral-lipid stores. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux; only RNA log fold changes and ambiguous protein-spot log2 fold changes were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: DGAT1 inhibition (with SOAT1 inhibition as a second arm) in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should, relative to APOE3, cause a disproportionate rise in free fatty acid and lysophospholipid, ER-stress and lipotoxicity readouts, and loss of neutral-lipid droplets, because re-esterification is the compensating disposal route. If DGAT1 inhibition merely removes droplets in APOE4 with no genotype-selective rise in free fatty acid, lysophospholipid or stress signalling, the bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester mass and a phospholipid acyl shift toward 16:1/18:1 species with reduced 20:4-containing PE and PI. Finding unchanged or increased arachidonoyl phospholipid, or no neutral-lipid increase, would weaken steps 4-5.", "Blocking upstream lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/SMPD1 inhibition) should reduce the downstream esterification program and droplet load selectively in APOE4; if DGAT1, AGPAT2, SCD and SREBF1 transcripts and droplet content are unaffected by upstream blockade, the proposed lysosome-to-esterification coupling fails.", "Stable-isotope tracing (13C/D-labelled lipoprotein lipid or oleate) should show higher label flow into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester in APOE4 with no matching increase in CO2/acid-soluble products from beta-oxidation. Equal or higher oxidative flux in APOE4 would contradict step 3.", "SCD inhibition should be selectively toxic to APOE4 microglia and should convert stored lipid toward saturated species with increased ER stress; equal tolerance in both genotypes would weaken the MUFA-channelling claim.", "At the protein level, LPCAT1, AGPAT2, DGAT1 and lysosomal hydrolase abundance should be higher in APOE4 by targeted immunoblot or targeted MS while ACSL4 is lower; unchanged protein for these enzymes despite the RNA differences would leave the mechanism unsupported, since only ambiguous multi-candidate spots were measured here.", "Functionally, APOE4 microglia should show slower phagocytic membrane turnover (myelin or synaptosome uptake-to-degradation kinetics) that is partially rescued by relieving the disposal bottleneck (fatty-acid oxidation or efflux support); no rescue would weaken step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred delivery): higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein uptake and intracellular lipid carriage (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:FABP3, gene:FABP5, gene:SCP2) are taken to indicate increased routing of exogenous and membrane-derived lipid to the endolysosome in APOE4; delivery flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): a coherent up-shift of lysosomal lipid and glycoconjugate hydrolases (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:MAN2B1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) with lysosome-biogenesis and maturation transcripts (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:RAB7A, gene:LAMP1) is interpreted as expanded lysosomal hydrolytic capacity generating free fatty acids, sphingoid bases and unesterified sterol. Hydrolase activity and luminal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, partly inference from missing data): disposal of this liberated acyl pool is rate-limiting. Long-chain acyl-CoA ligases that feed oxidation are down (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11) and mitochondrially encoded OXPHOS transcripts are down (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33) against a background in which 77% of selected genes are up; carnitine-shuttle and ABC-efflux genes are absent from the differential list, so their status is unknown rather than unchanged.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): the de novo glycerolipid acylation and esterification arm is up (gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:AGPAT4 +1.12, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25) together with the desaturase supplying monounsaturated acyl-CoA (gene:SCD +4.17) and acetyl-CoA/sterol regulators (gene:ACSS2, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:ACAT2), predicting diversion of surplus fatty acid into monounsaturated triacylglycerol and sterol ester rather than oxidation or efflux. Neutral-lipid mass and droplet number were not measured.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred membrane composition): phospholipid re-acylation and headgroup resynthesis transcripts rise (gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:TAZ +3.26) while gene:ACSL4 falls, which together predict a Lands-cycle bias that re-acylates lysophospholipids with 16:0/18:1 species at the expense of arachidonoyl-containing phosphatidylethanolamine and phosphatidylinositol. No lipidomic species were measured.", "Step 6 (consequence, inferred): a MUFA-enriched, PUFA-depleted membrane with expanded neutral-lipid stores lowers peroxidisable substrate (consistent with gene:GPX4 +2.79 and gene:ALOX15 -3.63) but stiffens membranes and sustains lysosomal lipid load, which we predict impairs phagocytic membrane turnover and cargo clearance in APOE4 microglia; the up protein spots containing ANXA1 (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046) are consistent with increased phospholipid-binding membrane-repair protein but are not uniquely identified."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are bottlenecked at fatty-acid disposal downstream of an amplified lysosomal lipid-hydrolysis program, forcing re-esterification into MUFA-rich glycerolipids and a PUFA-poor membrane"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42304212974928923, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2248041475662383, "cosine_similarity": -0.004792956106253256, "direction_accuracy": 0.2977346278317152, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7818608414239482, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.42304212974928923, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.2248041475662383, "cosine_similarity": -0.004792956106253256, "direction_accuracy": 0.2977346278317152, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7818608414239482, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.26711025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 457}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are therefore relative to the supplied rows only, and the logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified and is not assumed to be log2 or comparable in scale to the log2 protein-spot values.", "The dataset has a strong global upward shift (1705 of 2212 RNA rows positive, mean +1.39 in the reported log unit); pathway claims are only made where a curated set exceeds this background in a permutation test against the supplied rows.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and catalytic capacity for SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1 and the lysosomal hydrolases; none of these enzymes was measured as protein or activity here, and flux, acyl-chain composition, lipid-droplet content and subcellular localisation are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and cannot identify a unique protein; protein_spot:027, protein_spot:053 and protein_spot:055 are used only as weak, non-unique support for altered cathepsin-containing spots, and opposite-direction spots exist (protein_spot:058, protein_spot:067, protein_spot:069).", "No lipid, lipidomic, flux, imaging or replicate-level data were supplied, so the storage/turnover cycle and the saturated-lipid stress consequence are untested predictions.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture; clone-, differentiation- and co-culture-dependent confounders and any composition/normalisation effects (e.g. gene:CTSS and gene:ACTB strongly negative) cannot be excluded, and causal direction is not established."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally up-regulate lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism together with an SREBF1-associated glycerolipid re-esterification module (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, CHPT1), while PUFA/long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases (ACSL4, ACSL5) and GPAT3 fall; we hypothesise that the rate of SCD-dependent Delta-9 desaturation, feeding AGPAT2/DGAT1-mediated esterification, is the bottleneck that determines whether fatty acids liberated by lysosomal lipid turnover are safely stored as monounsaturated triacylglycerol and reacylated phospholipid, making APOE4 microglia selectively dependent on SCD activity and on a monounsaturated acyl-chain bias. Causality is not established by these data; the measurements are transcript and protein-spot abundances only.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: titrated SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) in mock-treated isogenic microglia should produce a larger genotype-specific effect in APOE4 than APOE3 - greater loss of neutral-lipid droplets, greater rise in saturated PC/PE and ER-stress markers, and greater viability loss - and this excess sensitivity should be reversed by exogenous oleate (18:1) but not by palmitate (16:0). If SCD inhibition affects both genotypes equally, or oleate fails to rescue APOE4 selectively, the SCD-gated bottleneck is falsified.", "Lipidomics of the same mock comparison should show, in APOE4, higher triacylglycerol mass and a higher monounsaturated:saturated ratio in TAG and in PC/PE, with lower 20:4-containing PI/PE species consistent with reduced ACSL4. Absence of any MUFA:SFA shift, or lower TAG in APOE4, would weaken the mechanism.", "DGAT1 inhibition should divert fatty acid away from storage and raise phospholipid saturation and lysosomal membrane stress selectively in APOE4; no genotype difference would weaken the esterification-sink step.", "Blocking the proposed upstream input (v-ATPase inhibition, GBA or SMPD1 inhibition, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-dependent uptake) should lower SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2 and DGAT1 transcripts and droplet load in APOE4 toward APOE3 levels. If the lipogenic transcripts are unchanged by these manipulations, the ordering (lysosomal catabolism upstream of re-esterification) is wrong and a cell-autonomous SREBP-1 activation model should replace it.", "SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 protein and enzymatic activity should be higher in APOE4 microglia. Unchanged protein or activity despite higher transcripts would weaken the whole chain, since only transcript abundance was observed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal lipid hydrolases and acidification/maturation machinery (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB) and for lipid-uptake/handling genes (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:FABP5). Inferred, not measured: increased degradative flux of internalised membrane lipid generating free fatty acids, sphingoid bases and lysophospholipids in the endolysosome.", "Measured: gene:SREBF1 is strongly increased together with canonical lipogenic targets (gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1). Inferred: increased SREBP-1 pathway output (nuclear SREBP-1 protein, processing and DNA occupancy were not measured).", "Measured: gene:SCD is high while gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 are decreased. Inferred: the activated acyl-CoA pool is biased toward monounsaturated (16:1/18:1) species and away from PUFA/very-long-chain species; this desaturation step is proposed as the rate-limiting node.", "Measured: the de novo glycerolipid arm is coordinately up (gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT2, gene:DGAT1) alongside headgroup transfer (gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2) and lysophospholipid reacylation (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2). Inferred: liberated fatty acids are channelled into phosphatidic acid, then into triacylglycerol storage and into rebuilt PC/PE with monounsaturated acyl chains (no lipid species were measured).", "Measured: gene:MGLL and gene:ABHD5 are increased, as are many oxidative-phosphorylation and beta-oxidation transcripts (gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA). Inferred: stored glycerolipid is continually re-hydrolysed and partly oxidised, i.e. a storage/turnover cycle rather than a terminal lipid sink.", "Predicted consequence of the bottleneck: whenever lysosomal lipid input exceeds SCD-dependent desaturation and AGPAT2/DGAT1 esterification capacity, saturated fatty acid and ceramide load in ER and lysosomal membranes rises, so APOE4 cells should be disproportionately sensitive to SCD or DGAT1 inhibition and disproportionately rescued by exogenous oleate."], "title": "SCD-gated monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply limits re-esterification of lysosome-derived fatty acids in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32531477310489976, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.089182991531877, "cosine_similarity": -0.009118548215659543, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7389061488673139, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.32531477310489976, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.089182991531877, "cosine_similarity": -0.009118548215659543, "direction_accuracy": 0.2783171521035599, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7389061488673139, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.24566275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 458}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_054", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and an overall positive shift; enrichment is therefore judged only by within-set rank, assuming the ranking of effects is meaningful even if the absolute scale and any global normalisation offset are not.", "Transcript abundance of MPC2, PDP1, MDH1/GOT1 and HK2/PFKP is assumed to track the corresponding protein content and, in turn, capacity for pyruvate import, PDH activation, NADH shuttling and glucose phosphorylation; no enzyme activity, phosphorylation state, metabolite pool or flux was measured here.", "Key nodes of the pathway (GAPDH, PKM, LDHA/B, PDHA1/PDHB, PDK1-4, CS, MDH2, IDH2, most OXPHOS subunits, CPT1A, HK1, PFKL) are absent from the supplied rows; the module is assumed to behave coherently despite these gaps.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes and are assumed not to identify any single protein; they are used only as weak, non-attributable corroboration or counter-evidence.", "The comparison is assumed to reflect isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 genotype effects in the microglia compartment rather than differences in astrocyte co-culture composition, cell-cycle/maturation state, or ambient-RNA/compositional bias of the 10X Flex data."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 transcriptional state is characterised by relative suppression of the committed cytosolic glucose-phosphorylation/PPP branch (HK2, HK3, PFKP, TALDO1, PGD all in the bottom decile of an otherwise strongly upward-shifted differential-expression set) together with coordinate elevation of the mitochondrial pyruvate carrier, PDH-activating phosphatase, malate-aspartate shuttle and TCA/carrier machinery (MPC2, PDP1, DLD, MDH1, GOT1, OGDH, ACO2, IDH3G, SLC25A1, SLC25A11) and of lysosomal glycan/glycogen and amino-acid mobilisation genes (GAA, GBA, CTSB, GYS1, UGP2, SLC38A7, GLUD1); we hypothesise that the primary bottleneck is hexokinase-level commitment of free glucose, so that APOE4 microglia become disproportionately dependent on MPC-dependent mitochondrial oxidation of carbon delivered from lysosomal/glycogen catabolism and amino-acid anaplerosis rather than from net cytosolic glycolytic flux. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, acute MPC inhibition (UK5099) or MPC2 knockdown should cause a proportionally larger fall in oxygen consumption rate and ATP-linked respiration in APOE4 than in APOE3; if the fractional OCR drop is equal or smaller in APOE4, the mitochondrial-pyruvate-entry step of the mechanism is weakened.", "Opposite-direction control: hexokinase-level blockade (2-deoxyglucose or HK2 knockdown) should impair ATP, phagocytic uptake and viability less in APOE4 than APOE3; greater APOE4 sensitivity to 2-DG would falsify the claim that glucose commitment is already the constrained branch in APOE4.", "13C tracing: with [U-13C6]glucose, APOE4 microglia should show lower fractional m+2 labelling of citrate/malate and lower lactate m+3 output per unit glucose, while [U-13C5]glutamine-derived m+4/m+5 TCA labelling and the OCR/ECAR ratio should be higher than APOE3; unchanged or higher glucose-derived m+2 in APOE4 would weaken the substrate-switch claim.", "Activity readout for the PDP1 step: APOE4 microglia should show reduced PDH-E1alpha Ser293 phosphorylation and higher PDH activity per mitochondrial mass; unchanged or increased phosphorylation would break the link between measured PDP1 transcript and inferred PDH activation.", "Lysosomal substrate supply: GAA knockdown, or lysosomal acidification blockade (bafilomycin A1) at doses that do not kill cells, should reduce basal and maximal respiration and lower TCA-intermediate labelling more in APOE4 than APOE3; equal or greater APOE3 dependence would falsify the lysosome-fed carbon step.", "Protein-level test with unambiguous identification: targeted proteomics or immunoblot should show higher MPC2, MDH1 and GOT1 protein and lower HK2 protein in APOE4; if MPC2/MDH1 protein is unchanged while glycolytic enzyme protein (e.g. ALDOA, PGAM1, consistent with the upward but ambiguous protein_spot:038 and protein_spot:072) is higher in APOE4, the transcript-to-protein assumption and the direction of the mechanism are refuted."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): relative to the global upward RNA shift of this selected DE set (median +1.46, 77% positive), transcripts for the committed glucose-phosphorylation and oxidative-PPP steps are selectively low in APOE4 (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08, gene:HK3 -1.12, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30; set median at the 5th percentile, permutation p = 0.007), while glucose transporters remain up (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3).", "Step 2 (inferred flux): if these transcript changes track enzyme content, glucose-6-phosphate production and the glycolysis/PPP branch point become rate-limiting in APOE4, so imported glucose is not efficiently committed to net cytosolic glycolytic ATP or NADPH production.", "Step 3 (measured abundance): genes supplying alternative carbon from the endolysosome and from amino acids are among the most strongly elevated (gene:GAA +9.96, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GYS1 +6.10, gene:UGP2 +1.86, gene:SLC38A7 +7.46, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, with gene:TFEB +2.39), consistent with an inferred increase in lysosomal glycan/glycogen hydrolysis and lysosomal amino-acid efflux.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): the mitochondrial pyruvate-entry and TCA/shuttle module is coordinately high (gene:MPC2 +7.98 [99th percentile], gene:DLD +5.54, gene:PDP1 +3.00, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3G +3.94, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47; set median at the 92nd percentile, permutation p = 5e-5).", "Step 5 (inferred activity/flux): elevated MPC2 plus elevated PDP1 (which dephosphorylates and activates pyruvate dehydrogenase) and elevated malate-aspartate shuttle components (MDH1/GOT1/SLC25A11) are predicted to raise mitochondrial pyruvate import, PDH activity and cytosolic-NADH transfer, biasing APOE4 carbon use toward mitochondrial oxidation and 2-oxoglutarate/citrate handling (gene:OGDH, gene:SLC25A1).", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): APOE4 microglia therefore run a lysosome- and anaplerosis-supplied, MPC-dependent oxidative programme with a narrow glycolytic reserve, predicting greater sensitivity to MPC or lysosomal-catabolism blockade and lesser sensitivity to hexokinase/glycolysis blockade than isogenic APOE3 microglia."], "title": "APOE4 microglia shift carbon entry away from hexokinase-level glycolysis toward lysosome- and amino-acid-fed mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA oxidation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1478048960602592, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08192263516436357, "cosine_similarity": -0.010589734604453676, "direction_accuracy": 0.10841423948220065, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_054", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6865339805825244, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1478048960602592, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08192263516436357, "cosine_similarity": -0.010589734604453676, "direction_accuracy": 0.10841423948220065, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6865339805825244, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.48002275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 459}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_184", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression set, not an unbiased transcriptome; inference is therefore about relative coherence of directions within this set, benchmarked against the list-wide median (+1.46) rather than against zero.", "The reported RNA effect units are log fold changes of unspecified base; only signs and within-dataset rank/magnitude comparisons are used.", "Transcript abundance is treated as a proxy for the size of the corresponding protein pool only when several members of a complex move together; no OXPHOS protein, assembly intermediate, mtDNA copy number, metabolite or flux was measured in these data.", "MT- transcript levels are assumed to report mitochondrial-genome expression rather than a probe-capture or normalisation artefact of the 10X Flex platform; this is unverified background knowledge and only 6 MT- rows are present, 2 of them positive (MT-ND4L, MT-ND5).", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each, so spots 038, 072 and 039 (ALDOA/ALDOC/TKT/SORD, PGAM1/CAPG, ALDOA/GAPDH/ALDOC) are used only as weak, non-identifying evidence that glycolytic-enzyme spot abundance is not coherently increased.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lactate/lipid; substrate availability is assumed comparable between APOE4 and APOE3 wells, which was not measured.", "Causality is not established: genotype, maturation-state differences and clone effects are confounded within a single mock comparison."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) show a coherent transcriptional expansion of the nuclear-encoded TCA/electron-transport-chain (ETC), mitochondrial import and assembly programme together with anaplerotic (glutamate/glutamine, GABA-shunt, ketone) carbon-entry genes, but the mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2, MT-ND4) are lower rather than higher. We hypothesise that the limiting step is supply of mtDNA-encoded core subunits for ETC holoenzyme assembly: nuclear subunit and substrate-entry capacity increase without a matched mitochondrial-genome contribution, so respiratory flux and ATP yield per unit of imported carbon do not rise proportionally, an unfolded/integrated stress response is engaged (DDIT3, EIF2AK3, serine/one-carbon genes), and glycolysis is not raised as a compensatory bypass (HK2, PFKP, HK3 lower). All statements about flux, assembly and causation are inferred, not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating test: blue-native PAGE / complexome profiling of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show equal or lower amounts of fully assembled complexes I, III, IV and V and accumulation of nuclear-subunit-containing assembly intermediates, despite higher nuclear subunit transcripts. If assembled holoenzyme levels scale up with the transcript increase and no intermediates accumulate, the assembly-bottleneck mechanism is falsified.", "Seahorse extracellular flux: APOE4 microglia should show unchanged or reduced maximal (FCCP-stimulated) oxygen consumption and reduced spare respiratory capacity, with no increase in glycolytic capacity after oligomycin, relative to APOE3. An increased maximal OCR proportional to the OXPHOS transcript increase would weaken the mechanism.", "Substrate-switch stress: replacing glucose with galactose (forcing oxidative ATP production) should selectively reduce APOE4 microglial ATP/viability; conversely, glutamine or beta-hydroxybutyrate withdrawal should impair APOE4 more than APOE3, consistent with the predicted reliance on GLUD1/GLS/OXCT1-dependent anaplerosis. Equal tolerance of galactose would argue against an oxidative-capacity limitation.", "Rescue: increasing mtDNA-encoded subunit supply (e.g. mitochondrially targeted expression of the limiting core subunit, or removing an inhibitor of mitochondrial translation) should normalise assembled complex levels, raise maximal OCR and lower DDIT3/SHMT2/PSPH transcripts in APOE4 cells. If DDIT3/SHMT2 remain elevated after complex assembly is restored, the ISR step is driven by something other than mitonuclear imbalance.", "Specificity control: mtDNA copy number and mitochondrial mass (TOMM20/citrate-synthase-normalised) should be similar or only modestly changed between genotypes; a large reduction in mitochondrial mass in APOE4 would explain the MT- transcript decrease trivially and would make the stoichiometry-imbalance claim unnecessary.", "Pharmacological ISR test: ISRIB or GCN2/PERK inhibition should reduce the serine/one-carbon and DDIT3 transcript signature without restoring assembled ETC complexes; restoration of respiration by ISRIB alone would place the ISR upstream and weaken the proposed ordering."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_184", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia transcriptionally expand the nuclear-encoded oxidative programme: 39/39 detected nuclear OXPHOS-subunit genes are higher (median +2.64 in the reported, base-unspecified log scale; permutation p=0.0007 against the list-wide median of +1.46), together with TCA/pyruvate-entry genes (MDH1, OGDH, GOT1, ACO2, IDH3G, MPC2, DLD, PDP1; median +5.54, p=0.0001) and mitochondrial import/assembly/carrier genes (TOMM22, TIMM44, HSPA9, PHB, TUFM, COX20, NDUFAF4, SLC25A1, SLC25A5).", "Carbon entry is inferred to be biased away from committed glucose catabolism toward amino-acid and ketone substrates: GLUD1, GLS, SLC1A5, ABAT and OXCT1 transcripts are higher, whereas hexokinase and PFK-platelet isoform transcripts (HK2, PFKP, HK3) are lower even against a list-wide upward shift; glucose transporter transcripts (SLC2A1, SLC2A3) remain higher, so uptake is not obviously the limiting step.", "The mtDNA-encoded catalytic core is discordant with the nuclear programme: MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 and MT-ND4 transcripts are lower (median of detected MT- transcripts -1.56, permutation p=0.014), which we propose leaves complexes I, III, IV and V assembly-limited despite excess nuclear subunits and import capacity.", "Unassembled or excess nuclear subunits and stalled assembly intermediates are hypothesised to trigger mitochondrial proteostatic and integrated stress signalling, consistent with higher HSPA9 and PHB and with the ATF4-type output DDIT3, EIF2AK3, SHMT1, SHMT2, PSPH and NUPR1; this signalling is inferred, no phosphorylated eIF2alpha or ATF4 pool was measured.", "Because respiratory ATP output per unit of TCA carbon is inferred to be capped by assembly, and because glycolytic commitment enzymes are not upregulated (no LDHA/PKM/PFKL rows and lower HK2/PFKP), APOE4 microglia are predicted to lack glycolytic reserve, i.e. reduced spare respiratory capacity without a compensating glycolytic bypass.", "The resulting redox/energetic strain is hypothesised to drive the observed antioxidant and uncoupling-associated transcripts (PRDX3, NNT, UCP2) and to co-occur with the APOE4 lipid-handling programme (APOE, ABCA7, TREM2), providing a metabolic context for, rather than a demonstration of, altered lipid processing."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry imbalance: APOE4 microglia expand nuclear-encoded oxidative machinery and non-glucose carbon entry while mtDNA-encoded ETC core subunit transcripts fall, making holoenzyme assembly the bottleneck"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.057656094228852046, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07334044631325974, "cosine_similarity": -0.016822788393700407, "direction_accuracy": 0.059870550161812294, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_184", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6657119741100324, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.057656094228852046, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07334044631325974, "cosine_similarity": -0.016822788393700407, "direction_accuracy": 0.059870550161812294, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6657119741100324, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.626941, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 460}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_030", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1.0 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05); absence of a gene therefore indicates a small or untested change, not absence of the transcript. Because 77% of rows are positive, we interpret ranks within this list rather than absolute magnitudes, and we assume the global shift is at least partly a normalisation or compositional artefact of the pseudobulk 10X Flex comparison.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effect is unspecified and is preserved as given; conclusions use direction and within-list percentile only.", "Transcript changes for ACSL4, SCD, LPCAT1, ALOX15 and GPX4 are assumed to move the corresponding enzyme activities in the same direction at day 30; none of these proteins was measured, and post-translational control (e.g. GPX4 turnover, PRDX hyperoxidation) could break this link.", "Protein spots are assumed to be non-unique: spots 017 and 077 are treated only as weakly consistent with increased catalase/PRDX2 pools, never as identified proteins.", "Microglia are assumed to be the source of the measured transcripts; astrocyte co-culture could contribute non-cell-autonomous signals or differing cell-state composition between genotypes.", "No lipid, NADPH, GSH/GSSG, iron or ROS measurement is supplied, so every flux, localisation and redox-state statement is inference, and no causal direction has been established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 not by mounting a canonical NRF2/oxidative-stress transcriptional response but by a selective remodeling of the peroxidizable lipid pool: transcripts for polyunsaturated fatty-acid (PUFA) activation and enzymatic lipid oxygenation (ACSL4, ACSL5, ALOX15) are among the few strongly reduced genes against a globally upward-shifted differential-expression list, while monounsaturated fatty-acid (MUFA) synthesis and phospholipid re-acylation (SCD, LPCAT1), thiol/phospholipid peroxidases (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, GPX4, GSS), iron sequestration (FTH1) and lysosomal/neutral-lipid handling (GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA, TFEB, SOAT1, DGAT1, SCARB1, SCP2) are elevated. We propose that the rate-limiting node is ACSL4-dependent activation of PUFA for incorporation into membrane phospholipids: with this step constrained, fatty-acid flux is redirected toward MUFA-containing phospholipids and toward esterified/lysosomally processed lipid, producing a membrane that resists peroxidation while lipid accumulates in storage and degradative compartments. All activities, fluxes and directions here are inferred; only RNA and ambiguous 2D-gel protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction (opposite to the 'APOE4 is oxidatively damaged and ferroptosis-prone' model): in mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia, a GPX4 inhibitor (RSL3 or ML-162) dose-response should show APOE4 to be equally or MORE resistant at low dose, with lower C11-BODIPY oxidation and lower malondialdehyde/4-HNE, because the ACSL4-dependent PUFA-phospholipid substrate pool is smaller. If APOE4 is instead markedly MORE sensitive to RSL3 and shows higher baseline C11-BODIPY oxidation, the proposed bottleneck (substrate limitation) is wrong and the alternative damage model should be preferred.", "Lipidomics of mock cultures should show a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in APOE4 phospholipids, specifically depletion of arachidonoyl/adrenoyl PE and PI species and enrichment of 16:1/18:1-containing PC/PE, together with increased cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol fractions. Unchanged or increased PUFA-PE species in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "SCD inhibition (A939572 or CAY10566) should preferentially affect APOE4: loss of the MUFA route should restore PUFA-phospholipid content, increase C11-BODIPY oxidation and reduce lipid-droplet number more in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal responses in both genotypes would weaken the claim that MUFA rerouting is the compensating flux.", "Restoring ACSL4 in APOE4 microglia (cDNA) should raise PUFA-phospholipid content and reduce neutral-lipid/lysosomal lipid accumulation, and conversely ACSL4 knockdown in APOE3 should phenocopy the APOE4 lipid distribution. Failure of ACSL4 manipulation to move lipid-droplet or CE content in either direction would falsify ACSL4 as the primary bottleneck.", "Corollary test of the regeneration constraint: G6PD/oxidative-PPP inhibition (G6PDi-1 or 6-aminonicotinamide) or NNT knockdown should lower the NADPH/NADP+ ratio and induce PRDX hyperoxidation (PRDX-SO2/3 immunoblot) more in APOE4 than APOE3. If APOE4 shows equal or higher NADPH/NADP+ and no differential sensitivity, step 6 is refuted while steps 1-5 can still stand.", "Direct redox check of the premise: APOE4 mock cultures should show a measurably increased peroxide tone (higher PRDX-SO2/3 fraction, more oxidised roGFP2-Orp1 or HyPer7 signal) despite unchanged canonical NRF2 target transcripts. If APOE4 and APOE3 are indistinguishable on all direct peroxide and thiol-redox readouts, the redox framing collapses and the lysosomal/TFEB lipid-handling programme should be taken as the primary mechanism instead."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): In APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia the selected differential-expression list is globally shifted upward (median +1.46 in the reported log unit; 77% of 2212 rows positive), so downward calls carry the most information. ACSL4 (gene:ACSL4, -2.14; 11th percentile of the list), ACSL5 (gene:ACSL5, -3.11) and ALOX15 (gene:ALOX15, -3.63; 4th percentile) are strongly down, while SCD (gene:SCD, +4.17), LPCAT1 (gene:LPCAT1, +3.07) and FADS1 (gene:FADS1, +1.59) are up.", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux): Reduced ACSL4 lowers the supply of PUFA-CoA available for Lands-cycle re-acylation, while elevated SCD and LPCAT1 favour incorporation of de-novo MUFA into phospholipids. The inferred consequence is a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in membrane glycerophospholipids and a smaller peroxidation-competent substrate pool; this lipid composition was not measured.", "Step 3 (inferred, enzymatic oxidation arm): Loss of ALOX15 transcript removes the principal enzymatic route for site-specific phospholipid/PUFA oxygenation, reinforcing the same reduction in oxidised-lipid generation. ALOX15 protein and oxylipins were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA plus ambiguous protein, defensive arm): Thiol- and phospholipid-hydroperoxide peroxidases are coordinately elevated (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:GSS +2.11; set-versus-background Mann-Whitney p=0.053) together with iron sequestration (gene:FTH1 +2.53). Two significant protein spots whose candidate lists include catalase and PRDX2 are increased (protein_spot:017 +0.77, p=0.001; protein_spot:077 +1.07, p=0.003), but each spot has 3-6 candidate genes and cannot identify a protein. We read this as evidence of a standing peroxide tone that the cell is buffering, not as proof of oxidative damage.", "Step 5 (inferred bottleneck consequence): Fatty acid and sterol carbon that is not routed into PUFA-phospholipid is predicted to accumulate as esterified and compartmentalised lipid. Consistent with this, sterol/neutral-lipid esterification and transport transcripts rise (gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SCP2 +5.95, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69), as do lysosomal hydrolase and TFEB-programme transcripts (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:GAA +9.96, gene:TFEB +2.38; set-versus-background p=2e-4). Lipid droplets, cholesteryl esters and lysosomal lipid load were not measured.", "Step 6 (inferred regeneration constraint, weakest link): The reductive demand of this state (GSH/PRDX recycling plus SCD desaturation and sterol reduction) is not matched by pentose-phosphate transcripts, since PGD (gene:PGD, -1.30) and TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1, -2.32) fall while mitochondrial NNT rises (gene:NNT +2.88). We therefore predict a lowered cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ ratio with partial mitochondrial compensation; no NADPH, GSH/GSSG or ROS measurement is supplied and this step is offered as a testable corollary rather than an established part of the chain."], "title": "Peroxidation-avoidant acyl-chain remodeling (ACSL4/ALOX15 down, SCD/LPCAT1 up) diverts fatty acids into stored and lysosomal lipid in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14599564302329876, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10801943111973375, "cosine_similarity": -0.020673251225293565, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8004433656957929, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.14599564302329876, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10801943111973375, "cosine_similarity": -0.020673251225293565, "direction_accuracy": 0.18122977346278318, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8004433656957929, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.163545, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 461}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_037", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript differences in the supplied selected DE list approximate directional differences in the corresponding enzyme protein amounts and activities; no enzyme protein or activity was measured here (protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and identify no lipid enzyme uniquely).", "The strong global positive shift of the RNA list (about 77% of rows positive, median about +1.46 in the unspecified log base) is at least partly a technical/compositional offset, so only within-list relative rank is treated as informative.", "The supplied rows are selected differential-expression results (all rows exceed |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05), so absence of a gene (e.g. ELOVL, LPCAT2/3, ACSL1/3/6, PLA2G4A) means unmeasured-or-unselected, not unchanged.", "ACSL4/ACSL5 transcript reduction translates into reduced cellular PUFA-CoA synthesis capacity that is not fully compensated by unmeasured ACSL isoforms or by FADS1-dependent PUFA synthesis (gene:FADS1 is up, which partly opposes this assumption).", "The APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison is isogenic as stated in the context, and astrocyte co-culture composition does not by itself generate the observed lipid-gene ranking.", "Reported log fold-change magnitudes are unreliable in absolute terms (they are uncorrelated with adjusted p-value and reach implausible values), so the hypothesis rests on sign and rank, not magnitude."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally up-regulate both lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism and an SREBF1-associated glycerolipid esterification/remodeling program, while transcripts for long-chain (PUFA-preferring) acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4 and ACSL5 and for GPAT3 are among the few strongly reduced genes. We hypothesise that the resulting acyl-CoA pool is biased toward SCD-derived monounsaturated species, so the increased reacylation and Kennedy-pathway capacity remodels phospholipids toward MUFA-containing species at the expense of arachidonoyl/PUFA phospholipids, with overflow esterified into neutral lipid. This is a proposed, not demonstrated, causal chain; all molecular evidence here is transcript abundance, and no lipid, acyl-CoA, flux or membrane-composition measurement is present in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher monounsaturated fraction in PC/PE (e.g. PC 32:1, 34:1) and a lower fraction of arachidonoyl species (e.g. PC/PE 38:4, 40:4), with increased TAG/CE. If PUFA-phospholipid species are unchanged or higher in APOE4, or the PL monounsaturation index is not raised, the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: supplementing free arachidonic acid (which must be activated by ACSL4/ACSL5) versus an ACSL-independent route should correct 20:4-phospholipid content much less efficiently in APOE4 than APOE3; equal correction in both genotypes would refute the proposed ACSL-dependent PUFA-activation bottleneck and leave only an SCD-overflow model.", "ACSL4 re-expression (or ACSL4-competent rescue) in APOE4 microglia should partially restore 20:4-phospholipid and lower the TAG/PL ratio without lowering SREBF1-target transcripts; no restoration of 20:4-PL would falsify Step 4.", "SCD inhibition should reduce neutral-lipid droplet content and the PL monounsaturation index preferentially in APOE4; if APOE4 droplets and membrane order are unaffected by SCD inhibition, Steps 1 and 6 are weakened.", "Pulse labelling with deuterated lysoPC or 13C-choline should show a faster PC reacylation/synthesis turnover rate in APOE4 (Steps 2-3); equal turnover rates would indicate the transcript changes are not reflected in flux.", "Protein-level validation: SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 protein should be higher and ACSL4 protein lower in APOE4 by targeted immunoblot; if ACSL4 protein is unchanged despite the transcript decrease, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Specificity control: if the same lipid-gene ranking pattern appears when comparing arbitrary sample subsets or is abolished by re-normalising away the global RNA shift, the pattern is a normalisation artefact rather than an APOE4 program."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): An SREBF1-associated lipogenic module is higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1). We infer, but did not measure, increased de novo synthesis of monounsaturated acyl-CoA (16:1/18:1) via SCD.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Lysosomal and lipolytic membrane-catabolic transcripts are among the highest-ranked genes (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB, gene:MGLL, gene:PLA2G7), together with lipid-uptake transcripts (gene:CD36, gene:FABP5, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7). We infer elevated turnover of internalised/self membrane lipid, which would generate lysophospholipid, DAG and MAG acceptors requiring reacylation.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): Esterification and remodeling capacity is coordinately higher (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2, gene:DGKA), i.e. both the Kennedy pathway and Lands-cycle reacylation arms.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred substrate limitation): Against a strongly up-shifted background list, gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 (and gene:GPAT3) sit in the bottom ~5-11th percentile. We propose that activation of long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids to PUFA-CoA, not esterification capacity, becomes the limiting input to the remodeling cycle in APOE4.", "Step 5 (predicted lipid-level consequence, unmeasured): With abundant MUFA-CoA and scarce arachidonoyl-CoA, LPCAT1/MBOAT-mediated reacylation and CHPT1-dependent PC synthesis should yield phospholipids enriched in 16:1/18:1 and depleted of 20:4-containing species, raising the membrane monounsaturation index without a proportional rise in saturated-chain PL.", "Step 6 (predicted downstream state, unmeasured): Excess MUFA-CoA that cannot be accommodated in phospholipid is predicted to be esterified into neutral lipid (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:CIDEB), giving droplet accumulation, while reduced arachidonoyl-phospholipid limits the releasable eicosanoid precursor pool and alters lysosomal/plasma-membrane biophysical properties, reinforcing the lysosomal program of Step 2."], "title": "MUFA-biased acyl-CoA supply (SCD up, ACSL4/ACSL5 down) is the bottleneck that redirects an up-regulated membrane-remodeling and glycerolipid-esterification program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2876804637595539, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08854473907491069, "cosine_similarity": -0.023830677735905775, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mean_absolute_error": 0.797336569579288, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2876804637595539, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08854473907491069, "cosine_similarity": -0.023830677735905775, "direction_accuracy": 0.23462783171521034, "mean_absolute_error": 0.797336569579288, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.94587075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 462}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_128", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (every |effect| exceeds 1) and the logarithm base is unspecified; ranks and directions are therefore used, and absolute fold changes are not interpreted.", "Absence of a gene from the list (e.g. ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1/2, PSAP, NPC1, VPS35) means not reported, not measured-and-unchanged; no claim is made about those pools.", "Transcript level is assumed to be at least a partial proxy for the abundance of the corresponding tethering/SNARE and hydrolase proteins; no protein measurement uniquely identifies any of these gene products here.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each, so spot changes are treated as consistent-or-inconsistent context only, never as identified protein abundances.", "The global positive shift of the RNA list is treated as a background to be controlled for by rank/percentile, not as a genuine transcriptome-wide induction.", "No lipid, flux, localization, imaging or enzymatic measurement is supplied, so every statement about ceramide/GSL pools, carrier fusion and hydrolase delivery is inferred, and the direction of causation between APOE4 genotype and this module is not established.", "Astrocyte co-culture, day-30 maturation state and unreported replicate structure are assumed not to differ systematically between APOE3 and APOE4 lines in a way that generates the specific five-gene TGN module signal."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, transcripts for the tethering/SNARE step that fuses endosome-derived retrograde carriers with the trans-Golgi network (GCC1, GCC2, STX16, GOSR1) and the TGN PI4P effector GOLPH3L are coordinately and exceptionally reduced against a strongly up-shifted differential-expression background, while carrier-forming machinery (VPS26A, SNX3, VPS53, WDR11, TBC1D23) and lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolases (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, GBA2) are up. We propose that the rate-limiting step is retrograde carrier fusion at the TGN, which restricts M6PR-dependent hydrolase re-sorting and the Golgi-side re-synthesis of complex sphingolipids, so that increased lysosomal sphingomyelin/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis is not matched by return of sphingoid backbones into complex sphingolipid pools; the resulting ceramide/sphingosine-biased, GSL-poor endolysosomal lipid state and the compensatory hydrolase/TFEB transcriptional program are the proposed APOE4-distinguishing state. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: knockdown of STX16 (or of GCC1/GCC2) in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 state - dispersal/reduction of TGN-localised M6PR, accumulation of retrograde carriers, and secondary induction of GBA/HEXA/SMPD1/CTSB transcripts with a rise in the ceramide-plus-GlcCer to complex-GSL/SM ratio; if STX16/GCC1/GCC2 loss changes M6PR localisation but leaves the sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts and the ceramide/GSL ratio unchanged, the proposed coupling between the fusion bottleneck and sphingolipid handling is wrong.", "Rescue: re-expressing STX16 plus GCC1/GCC2 (or GOLPH3L) in APOE4 microglia should restore TGN M6PR, normalise the hydrolase/TFEB transcriptional program and lower the ceramide/complex-GSL ratio without correcting APOE genotype; persistence of the hydrolase program after full restoration of retrograde fusion would weaken the mechanism.", "Lipidomics of sorted APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased ceramide and glucosylceramide relative to sphingomyelin and to LacCer/GM3, with the LacCer/GlcCer ratio reduced in line with B4GALT5; an APOE4 profile showing higher complex GSL and unchanged or lower ceramide would falsify the lipid-flux consequence.", "Because the model places the defect at fusion rather than hydrolase capacity, pharmacological substrate reduction (UGCG inhibition, e.g. eliglustat-class) should lower GSL load but NOT restore TGN M6PR localisation or normalise GCC1/GCC2/STX16/GOSR1-dependent retrograde transport of a marker cargo (Shiga-toxin B subunit or CI-M6PR); restoration of retrograde transport by substrate reduction alone would indicate the lipid state is upstream and would falsify the assigned bottleneck.", "Retrograde cargo assay: APOE4 microglia should show slowed endosome-to-TGN arrival of a retrograde reporter with normal or increased carrier budding (retromer/SNX3 puncta); equal arrival kinetics in APOE4 and APOE3 would directly weaken the primary bottleneck claim.", "The hydrolase induction is predicted to be compensatory, so acute TFEB inhibition in APOE4 cells should exaggerate the ceramide/GSL imbalance rather than relieve it; the opposite result would argue the hydrolase program is the driver, not the response."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_128", "mechanism_steps": ["Primary bottleneck (inferred activity, not measured flux): fusion of endosome-derived retrograde carriers with the TGN is limited in APOE4 microglia, indicated by coordinate transcript reduction of the golgin tethers GCC1 and GCC2 and the TGN SNAREs STX16 and GOSR1, plus the TGN PI4P effector GOLPH3L, all in the lowest ~6% of a distribution whose median is positive.", "Carrier generation upstream of that step is not reduced and may be increased (VPS26A, SNX3, VPS53, WDR11, TBC1D23 transcripts up), so the defect is placed at delivery/fusion rather than at cargo capture; unfused carriers are predicted to accumulate in the late endosomal compartment (localization inferred, not measured).", "Failure to retrieve mannose-6-phosphate receptors to the TGN (M6PR transcript down while IGF2R is up) is predicted to reduce per-receptor rounds of hydrolase sorting, lowering effective hydrolase delivery relative to demand (activity inferred; no hydrolase localization or enzymatic assay is supplied).", "A compensatory lysosomal biogenesis program is transcribed (TFEB, MITF, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0D1, ATP6AP1, CTSB, CTSD, GAA, LAMP1 up), with the sphingolipid catabolic arm particularly high (GBA, HEXA, SMPD1 at the 95-98th percentile of all measured effects; GM2A, HEXB, GLA, GBA2 also up).", "Sphingolipid salvage output is therefore biased toward simple species: sphingomyelin and glycosphingolipid hydrolysis feed ceramide/sphingosine, the lysosomal sphingoid exporter SPNS1 and ER re-acylation genes (CERS4, CERS6, KDSR) are up, and S1P disposal (SGPL1) is up, whereas the committed Golgi step to complex glycosphingolipids, B4GALT5, is the single down-regulated sphingolipid gene (12.9th percentile).", "Consequence (inferred lipid state, no lipidomics supplied): membranes of the late endosome/lysosome and TGN become relatively ceramide/GlcCer-enriched and complex-GSL/SM-poor; up-regulated GLTP (cytosolic glycolipid transfer) is interpreted as a non-vesicular bypass, and up-regulated ST3GAL5 as a substrate-starved downstream enzyme.", "Because SM and GSL levels feed back on TGN PI4P/GOLPH3-family-dependent export, the reduced GOLPH3L transcript and the lipid shift are proposed to reinforce the fusion/export bottleneck, giving a self-sustaining APOE4 endolysosomal state rather than a transient response."], "title": "A TGN-fusion bottleneck (GCC1/GCC2-STX16/GOSR1, GOLPH3L) uncouples endosome-to-Golgi retrograde return from an up-regulated lysosomal sphingolipid catabolic program in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17404829597902743, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.1168707063261689, "cosine_similarity": -0.03360204782161273, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_128", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7046278317152104, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17404829597902743, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.1168707063261689, "cosine_similarity": -0.03360204782161273, "direction_accuracy": 0.14563106796116504, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7046278317152104, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.5092995, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 463}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_087", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript log fold changes (logarithm base not specified in the file; magnitudes therefore used only as ranks and directions) translate into proportional changes in the corresponding enzyme abundance and catalytic activity; no protein spot in this dataset uniquely reports SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, ACSL4 or ACSL5, so this step is unverified here.", "The 92 protein spots each carry several candidate genes and cannot be treated as uniquely identified proteins; they are used only as ambiguous, non-confirmatory context.", "The RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression table (every retained gene has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 1200 rows contributing only an up-gene and 506 rows contributing one up- and one down-gene), so the 77% up-fraction is a table-construction feature and cannot serve as an unbiased transcriptome background for enrichment.", "Lipid classes, acyl-chain composition, lipid droplets, acyl-CoA pools, flux and subcellular localization were not measured in the supplied data and are inferred quantities only.", "Effects measured in astrocyte co-culture are attributed to the microglial genotype, although non-cell-autonomous astrocyte-derived APOE effects cannot be excluded; biological replicate structure is not supplied, so statistical independence is assumed but unverified.", "For genes whose source row carries both an up- and a down-regulated entry (including ACSL4, ACSL5, SCD, SREBF1, LPCAT1, SCARB1), the gene-to-effect assignment within the row is assumed correct."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia (astrocyte co-culture, day 30), the transcript program encoding lipid acquisition and glycerolipid acylation is coordinately raised (SCARB1, CD36, LDLR; SREBF1, SCD, FADS1, ACSS2; GPAT4, AGPAT2, DGAT1, CHPT1, PCYT2; LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2; MGLL, ABHD5) while the long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4 and ACSL5 and the alternative acyltransferase GPAT3 are lowered. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 is not total lipid flux but the species composition of the acyl-CoA pool feeding glycerolipid synthesis and Lands-cycle re-acylation: expanded SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply combined with reduced ACSL4-dependent polyunsaturated acyl-CoA activation should drive accelerated glycerolipid cycling into MUFA-enriched, arachidonate-poor phospholipids and triacylglycerol. Lipid composition, enzyme activity and flux were not measured here; this is an inference from transcript abundances and is not a demonstration of causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a higher fraction of 16:1/18:1-containing phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine and triacylglycerol species and a lower fraction of 20:4-containing phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine in APOE4; no shift, or an increased 20:4-phospholipid fraction, would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring polyunsaturated acyl-CoA supply in APOE4 cells (ACSL4 re-expression, or arachidonic-acid supplementation with ACSL4 intact) should raise the 20:4-phospholipid fraction toward APOE3 without normalising triacylglycerol mass; if 20:4-phospholipids stay low despite abundant substrate and ACSL4 activity, the bottleneck lies downstream in LPCAT/MBOAT acyl selectivity or in lysosomal turnover, not in acyl-CoA supply, and this hypothesis is wrong.", "Pharmacological SCD inhibition in APOE4 microglia should lower the 18:1/18:0 desaturation index and the MUFA fraction of newly synthesised phospholipid and reduce neutral-lipid staining; persistence of the MUFA-biased composition under effective SCD inhibition would falsify step 2.", "DGAT1 inhibition should shift labelled fatty acid from triacylglycerol into phospholipid and oxidation while leaving the phospholipid MUFA:PUFA ratio largely unchanged; if DGAT1 inhibition also normalises the MUFA:PUFA ratio, the storage branch rather than acyl-CoA composition is the primary node.", "Stable-isotope tracing (13C-acetate or D2O) should show higher fractional new synthesis of 18:1 chains and faster phosphatidylcholine deacylation/re-acylation turnover in APOE4 than APOE3; equal turnover rates would contradict the accelerated-cycling step.", "Targeted proteomics or activity assays should confirm higher AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1/SCD protein and lower ACSL4 protein in APOE4; unchanged protein or activity despite the transcript differences would break the RNA-to-activity assumption on which the whole mechanism rests."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mechanism_steps": ["Higher transcript abundance of scavenger/lipoprotein receptors (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR) and of lysosomal lipid hydrolases and lysosome-biogenesis regulators (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:LAMP1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:TFEB) is proposed to increase delivery and hydrolytic release of exogenous and membrane-derived lipid into the intracellular free fatty-acid pool (uptake and hydrolysis rates are inferred, not measured).", "A lipogenic/desaturase module (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:INSIG1) is proposed to raise the supply of 16:1/18:1 monounsaturated acyl-CoA, while reduced gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 are proposed to lower activation of polyunsaturated (notably arachidonoyl) fatty acids into CoA thioesters; ACSL4 substrate preference is unverified background knowledge.", "The acylation node is remodeled rather than simply amplified: gene:GPAT4 and gene:AGPAT2 rise and the paralogue gene:GPAT3 falls, which we interpret as an isoform switch that concentrates lysophosphatidate acylation at ER-resident enzymes, so newly formed phosphatidate inherits the MUFA-biased acyl-CoA composition (inferred flux, not measured).", "Downstream partitioning enzymes are raised (gene:DGAT1 for triacylglycerol, gene:CHPT1 and gene:PCYT2 for de novo phosphatidylcholine and phosphatidylethanolamine, gene:SOAT1 and gene:CIDEB for neutral-lipid handling), predicted to convert the MUFA-biased diacylglycerol pool into storage lipid and into new bulk membrane phospholipid rather than into polyunsaturated species.", "Lands-cycle re-acylation transcripts (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2) rise together with hydrolytic capacity (gene:MGLL, gene:ABHD5, gene:PLA2G7, gene:DDHD1), which we interpret as accelerated deacylation/re-acylation cycling of membrane phospholipids fed by the same MUFA-shifted acyl-CoA pool, progressively lowering the polyunsaturated fraction of phosphatidylcholine and phosphatidylethanolamine.", "The predicted consequence is a MUFA-enriched, arachidonate-poor membrane with a larger neutral-lipid pool; this composition is proposed to be the bottleneck for handling polyunsaturated, membrane-rich phagocytic cargo and for PLA2-dependent lipid mediator release, providing a candidate mechanistic difference between APOE4 and APOE3 microglia under mock conditions."], "title": "MUFA-biased acyl-CoA partitioning at the GPAT4/AGPAT2 acylation node redirects APOE4 microglial membrane lipid turnover away from PUFA phospholipid remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24497839973415056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08267270093975305, "cosine_similarity": -0.035038290829445824, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_087", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7376051779935274, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.24497839973415056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08267270093975305, "cosine_similarity": -0.035038290829445824, "direction_accuracy": 0.1779935275080906, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7376051779935274, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.02183725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 464}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_081", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are pre-selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and no replicate information, so only directions and relative ranks within the supplied set are interpreted; the strong global positive shift (77% of rows increased) is treated as a baseline against which enrichment is judged.", "Transcript abundance differences for RAC2/DOCK8/ARHGDIA are assumed to translate into a lower membrane-bound Rac-GTP pool; neither GTP loading, localisation, nor protein amount of any Rho-family GTPase was measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; no spot is used as evidence for a specific protein, and the near-zero RNA/spot concordance is treated as uninformative rather than confirmatory.", "No lipid, phagocytosis, migration, imaging, or lysosomal-function measurement is supplied; all flux, localisation, and functional statements are inferences to be tested, and no causal direction has been established by these data.", "The astrocyte co-culture and 10X Flex pseudobulk design could introduce composition or ambient-RNA differences between genotypes; the hypothesis assumes the myeloid-effector decrease is cell-intrinsic, supported by the fact that core myeloid identity transcripts are increased rather than diluted."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated transcriptional loss of the haematopoietic Rho/Rac-GTPase actomyosin effector module (RAC2, DOCK8, ARHGDIB, ARHGAP30, PLEK, MYO1F, MYH9, ACTB, FAM49B all reduced against a background in which 77% of the selected DE genes are increased) together with increased ARHGDIA and increased integrin/adhesion transcripts, while recognition receptors and lysosomal/degradative transcripts are increased. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 microglia is the amount of membrane-localised, GTP-loaded Rac available for actin-cup and lamellipodial remodeling: recognition and degradation capacity are raised but the actin execution step is throttled, predicting reduced internalisation and process motility per bound cargo rather than reduced cargo binding or reduced lysosomal hydrolysis.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 versus APOE3 mock microglia, a PAK-PBD (Rac-GTP) pull-down or biosensor plus membrane/cytosol fractionation should show a lower active and membrane-associated Rac fraction in APOE4 with comparable total Rac protein; siRNA knockdown of ARHGDIA, or expression of constitutively active Rac1, should restore bead/synaptosome internalisation and process motility in APOE4 to APOE3 levels without changing lysosomal hydrolase transcript levels. If Rac-GTP and membrane Rac are equal between genotypes, or if ARHGDIA knockdown fails to rescue uptake while still lowering ARHGDIA protein, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Two-step binding-versus-internalisation assay (pH-sensitive versus total-labelled cargo at 4 degrees C binding then 37 degrees C chase): APOE4 should show equal or higher surface binding but a lower internalised/bound ratio. Equal internalised/bound ratio, or reduced binding proportional to reduced uptake, would weaken the mechanism and favour a recognition-level or purely global-expression explanation.", "Live imaging should show reduced process velocity, fewer lamellipodial/filopodial extensions and larger, more stable focal adhesions in APOE4; an ITGA6/ITGB1-blocking antibody or low-dose Rho-kinase inhibition should partially restore motility. Unchanged motility and adhesion morphology would weaken the mechanism.", "Degradation-capacity control: DQ-BSA and cathepsin activity assays should be equal or higher per internalised cargo in APOE4, matching the increased hydrolase transcripts. If cathepsin/DQ-BSA activity is instead reduced in APOE4, the bottleneck would lie at lysosomal degradation rather than at Rac-dependent uptake, favouring a lysosomal-failure alternative.", "If a whole-transcriptome, spike-in or cell-number-normalised measurement of the same samples shows that the myeloid-effector transcripts are not reduced once the global shift is properly normalised, the primary evidence for this mechanism disappears."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 genotype is associated with reduced steady-state transcript levels of haematopoietic-restricted Rho/Rac cytoskeletal effectors and their activators (gene:RAC2, gene:DOCK8, gene:PLEK, gene:ARHGDIB, gene:ARHGAP30, gene:MYO1F, gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB), while ubiquitously expressed paralogues and regulators are increased (gene:ARHGDIA, gene:RHOA, gene:ACTG1, gene:ARHGAP1, gene:ARHGAP35); this is a measured abundance difference, not a measured activity difference.", "Inferred, not measured: the combination of lower RAC2/DOCK8 supply and higher ARHGDIA (a cytosolic sequestering GDI) lowers the fraction of Rho-family GTPase that is prenyl-anchored at the plasma membrane in the GTP-loaded state, reducing WAVE/Arp2/3-driven branched-actin protrusion and NMIIA (MYH9)-dependent contractile closure.", "In parallel, cargo recognition capacity is transcriptionally increased (gene:FCGR1A, gene:FCGR3A, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:MRC1, gene:TREM2, gene:CD36, gene:SCARB1, gene:LGALS3, gene:MFGE8, gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC), so the difference is unlikely to originate at ligand binding; inhibitory signalling transcripts are also raised (gene:CD47, gene:SIRPA), which would further raise the actin-remodeling threshold.", "Downstream degradative capacity is also transcriptionally increased (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H), so a degradation block is not the primary bottleneck; this pattern is instead consistent with compensatory or downstream-of-uptake adaptation.", "Inferred: constrained Rac-dependent remodeling with increased integrin/adhesion transcripts (gene:ITGA6, gene:ITGB1, gene:ZYX, gene:SDC4) biases APOE4 microglia toward a spread, substrate-anchored, hypomotile state with fewer dynamic surveying processes rather than toward loss of myeloid identity (gene:CSF1R, gene:AIF1, gene:MNDA, gene:MPEG1, gene:SYK, gene:C1QA remain increased).", "Functional consequence (inferred flux, not measured here): per unit of bound cargo, APOE4 microglia internalise less material and cover less territory per unit time; the transcriptional up-shift of hydrolases and mitochondrial substrate-oxidation genes reflects a cell that is primed to degrade but limited at intake."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are constrained at Rac/actomyosin-dependent engulfment execution, not at cargo recognition or lysosomal degradation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17869143004836982, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0035535193151623504, "cosine_similarity": -0.0405341785162542, "direction_accuracy": 0.11165048543689321, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_081", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6532394822006472, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.17869143004836982, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0035535193151623504, "cosine_similarity": -0.0405341785162542, "direction_accuracy": 0.11165048543689321, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6532394822006472, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.1082375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 465}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_053", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; pathway statements are enrichment relative to that biased list, and the logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified, so only signs and within-list ranks are used quantitatively.", "The list-wide positive shift (77% of rows positive, median +1.46) may reflect normalisation, ambient RNA or cell-composition asymmetry rather than uniform induction; the argument therefore rests mainly on rows that move against that shift (HK2, HK3, PFKP, mtDNA-encoded subunits) and on rank-based, background-matched tests.", "Transcript changes are assumed to translate at least partially into enzyme abundance and hence maximal capacity; no hexokinase, PFK, OXPHOS-complex or V-ATPase protein was uniquely measured, and no flux, ATP, membrane potential, pH or metabolite pool was measured in these data.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes each (frequent keratin and actin contaminants); spot-level directions are treated as weak, non-identifying evidence only.", "Key glycolytic reporters (HK1, PKM, GAPDH, LDHA, PFKFB3), mitoribosome and mtDNA-maintenance genes (MRPL/MRPS, TFAM, POLRMT) and lipid-droplet genes (PLIN2, LIPA, PNPLA2) are absent from the list; their absence is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change.", "Astrocyte co-culture, single-cell demultiplexing and unreported replicate structure could contribute genotype-associated composition differences that mimic a cell-intrinsic metabolic shift."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a transcriptional restriction of glycolytic commitment at hexokinase (HK2, HK3) plus PFKP, occurring against a list-wide upward RNA shift, while glucose-uptake and G6P-diverting transcripts rise and a nuclear-encoded TCA/OXPHOS program is coordinately elevated; because mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunits (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) move in the opposite, downward direction, the compensating oxidative arm is predicted to be assembly-limited, so APOE4 cells are inferred (not shown) to have less spare ATP-generating flexibility. We propose this energetic bottleneck, not an intrinsic loss of lysosomal biosynthetic capacity, is the differentiating mechanism; the elevated lysosomal-biogenesis transcripts are interpreted as demand/compensation. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: extracellular-flux profiling of mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show lower basal and lower oligomycin-stimulated ECAR and reduced glycolytic capacity/reserve in APOE4, together with equal or higher 2-NBDG glucose uptake; if APOE4 shows equal or greater glycolytic capacity, or lower glucose uptake, Steps 1-2 are weakened.", "Bypassing the hexokinase step with cell-permeable methyl-pyruvate (or galactose substitution) should rescue ATP-dependent phenotypes (pHrodo-bead acidification rate, DQ-BSA dequenching) preferentially in APOE4; equal rescue in APOE3, or no rescue in APOE4, weakens the energetic-bottleneck claim and favours a lysosome-intrinsic mechanism.", "2-deoxyglucose dose-response should make APOE3 microglia more sensitive than APOE4 (APOE4 being less glycolysis-dependent); equal or greater APOE4 sensitivity would falsify the proposed routing.", "HK2 re-expression in APOE4 (or HK2 knockdown in APOE3) should shift ECAR, lactate output and acidification capacity toward the opposite genotype; failure to move these readouts would show the HK2 transcript change is not rate-setting and would refute the chosen bottleneck.", "Mitonuclear test: BN-PAGE/immunoblot ratio of mtDNA-encoded (MT-CO2, MT-ATP6) to nuclear-encoded (NDUFA9, ATP5F1B) subunits, mtDNA copy number and mitochondrial translation labelling should be lower in APOE4; an unchanged ratio despite the RNA discordance would falsify Step 5 and reduce the mtDNA signal to a normalisation artefact.", "Rejection test for the assigned endolysosomal focus: if APOE4 microglia show intact or increased bulk cathepsin activity, normal lysosomal pH and normal DQ-BSA processing per lysosome at matched ATP, then lysosomal capacity is not the differentiator, as this hypothesis asserts; conversely, an isolated acidification defect that persists under methyl-pyruvate rescue would replace this hypothesis with a lysosome-primary mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia raise glucose-transporter transcripts (gene:SLC2A1 +2.37, gene:SLC2A3 +3.73), which we infer increases glucose import capacity; no uptake flux was measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, primary bottleneck): Both measured hexokinases and a phosphofructokinase isoform fall (gene:HK2 -3.67, adj p 7.7e-191, 41st smallest adjusted p of 2212 rows; gene:HK3 -1.12; gene:PFKP -3.08) despite 77% of rows being positive (median +1.46), so we infer reduced capacity to phosphorylate glucose and commit glucose-6-phosphate to lower glycolysis. Hexokinase protein and activity were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred routing): Transcripts of enzymes that consume or reverse G6P rise (gene:GYS1 +6.10, gene:UGP2 +1.86, gene:G6PC3 +1.23), consistent with inferred diversion of the smaller G6P pool toward glycogen/dephosphorylation rather than glycolytic ATP and lactate output; no metabolite pool was measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): A coherent nuclear-encoded oxidative program is elevated above the already-positive background (38 nuclear OXPHOS rows, median rank percentile 0.73, permutation p = 0.0011; 10 TCA/shuttle rows, rank percentile 0.93, p = 1e-4; gene:PDP1 +3.00 favouring PDH dephosphorylation; gene:MDH1, gene:GOT1 malate-aspartate shuttle; lipid-oxidation inputs gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:MGLL), which we read as an inferred shift of ATP production toward mitochondrial oxidation of pyruvate and lipid.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred stoichiometry): mtDNA-encoded catalytic core transcripts run counter to the global shift (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35 adj p 9e-228, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; 6 MT rows median rank percentile 0.16, p = 0.013), so we infer a mitonuclear stoichiometric mismatch that limits how much of the nuclear-encoded expansion becomes assembled, coupled respiratory chain and ATP synthase; assembled-complex amounts and respiration were not measured. gene:UCP2 (+2.38) and gene:PRKAA1 (+2.01) are consistent with, but do not demonstrate, reduced coupling efficiency and energy stress.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): Reduced glycolytic reserve (Step 2-3) plus an assembly-limited oxidative arm (Step 4-5) is predicted to narrow ATP headroom for the most ATP-expensive microglial work, notably V-ATPase-driven acidification and phagosome maturation; the elevated lysosomal-biogenesis transcripts (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSB, gene:ATP6V1H) are therefore interpreted as unmet demand rather than realised capacity, and are internally discordant (gene:CTSS -5.57, gene:M6PR -1.72; protein_spot:064 and protein_spot:065, whose candidate lists include ATP6V1E1, are decreased)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia restrict glucose commitment at the hexokinase step and rely on an oxidative program whose mtDNA-encoded core is under-represented, narrowing ATP headroom"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0855738759554814, "cosine_similarity": -0.04176646732312276, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_053", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6467605177993527, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0136986301369863, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0855738759554814, "cosine_similarity": -0.04176646732312276, "direction_accuracy": 0.024271844660194174, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6467605177993527, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.808537, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 466}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_097", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of FASN, ACLY, ACACA, ELOVL and LPCAT3 rows is uninformative and cannot be read as unchanged.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA effects is unspecified, so effects are used as signed, ranked evidence and not converted to fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and catalytic flux for SCD, ACSL4, LPCAT1/MBOAT1/2, AGPAT2 and DGAT1; no enzyme activity, acyl-CoA pool, phospholipid species or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so all flux, localization and composition statements are inferences.", "A strong global positive shift exists in these rows (77.1% of 2212 RNA rows positive, median +1.46), which may partly reflect normalization or RNA-content differences between genotypes; the mechanism therefore relies on within-pathway directional contrasts (e.g. SCD up versus ACSL4/ACSL5/GPAT3 down) rather than on the magnitude of any single up-regulated transcript.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; no spot in this dataset carries a lipid-metabolic candidate gene, so the protein layer neither supports nor contradicts the lipid enzymes and is not used as evidence here.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so part of the fatty-acid and lipoprotein supply is extrinsic and unmeasured; the genotype effect may act partly through astrocyte-derived lipid.", "The comparison is isogenic and observational; association with APOE4 genotype is what is measured, and causality is not established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily in the acyl-chain economy of their glycerolipids: a coordinated transcript shift toward SREBF1/SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty-acyl production together with reduced ACSL4/ACSL5 long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts is proposed to skew the acyl-CoA pool toward 16:1/18:1 and away from polyunsaturated species, while elevated lyso-phospholipid acyltransferase (LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2), head-group (CHPT1, PCYT2) and triacylglycerol-arm (AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1) transcripts route that pool into MUFA-enriched phospholipids and into a turning-over neutral-lipid store; the rate-limiting node is inferred MUFA-CoA supply at the SCD step, not the esterification enzymes themselves.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a higher SCD desaturation index (18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0) and a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in PC and PE, with reduced 20:4-containing PC/PE species. If the desaturation index and phospholipid MUFA:PUFA ratio are indistinguishable between genotypes, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) or SCD knockdown in APOE4 microglia should normalize both the phospholipid MUFA fraction and the neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content toward APOE3 values, with a markedly smaller effect in APOE3 cells. If instead DGAT1 inhibition (e.g. T863) normalizes neutral lipid while SCD inhibition leaves phospholipid composition unchanged, the bottleneck is downstream esterification/storage, not MUFA supply, and this hypothesis should be replaced.", "Pulse labelling with [13C]- or [d]-oleate and with [d]-arachidonate should show faster oleate and slower arachidonate incorporation into PC/PE in APOE4 than APOE3; equal incorporation rates for both tracers would weaken the Lands-cycle remodeling step.", "Restoring ACSL4 (re-expression) or supplying exogenous arachidonic acid to APOE4 microglia should raise PUFA-phospholipid content toward APOE3 without requiring changes in SCD; failure to raise PUFA-phospholipid content would weaken the ACSL4-limited polyunsaturated arm.", "Because the endolysosomal hydrolase program is treated as a supporting supply route rather than the primary lesion, TFEB knockdown should lower CTSB/CTSD/GBA/HEXA transcripts and lysosomal degradation capacity while leaving the phospholipid MUFA:PUFA difference largely intact. If the phospholipid composition difference disappears with TFEB knockdown, the primary bottleneck should be moved upstream to lysosomal membrane-lipid turnover.", "Immunoblot or targeted proteomics should show higher SCD protein in APOE4 microglia. Unchanged SCD protein and unchanged desaturase activity despite the transcript difference would weaken the first mechanism step."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SREBF1 and its lipogenic effector transcripts SCD, ACSS2 and FADS1 are higher in APOE4 than APOE3 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:FADS1 +1.59, all adjusted p \u003c 1e-40). Inferred (not measured): higher stearoyl-CoA desaturase flux raising the 16:1/18:1-CoA pool.", "Measured: ACSL4 and ACSL5 transcripts are lower in APOE4 (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, adjusted p 4.6e-3; gene:ACSL5 -3.11). Inferred: reduced activation of long-chain, preferentially polyunsaturated, fatty acids to acyl-CoA, so the usable acyl-CoA pool becomes MUFA-dominated rather than simply larger.", "Measured: lyso-phospholipid acyltransferase and head-group transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05). Inferred: increased deacylation-reacylation (Lands-cycle) throughput that stamps the MUFA-skewed acyl-CoA composition onto PC and PE, lowering the 20:4-containing phospholipid fraction. Phospholipid species themselves were not measured.", "Measured: the glycerol-3-phosphate/TAG arm is transcriptionally raised (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) with a hydrolytic counterpart (gene:MGLL +4.00), while GPAT3 and PNPLA1 fall (gene:GPAT3 -2.23, gene:PNPLA1 -1.55). Inferred: acyl-CoA in excess of membrane demand is esterified into a diacyl/triacylglycerol store that is simultaneously turned over; lipid-droplet content was not measured here.", "Measured: an endolysosomal degradative transcript program is also elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23), together with lipid-uptake and handling transcripts (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:FABP5 +1.13, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:SOAT1 +1.25). Inferred: higher membrane and lipoprotein-lipid turnover delivers fatty acids back to the acyl-CoA pool, sustaining step 4 rather than being the primary lesion.", "Consequence (inferred, testable): APOE4 microglial membranes carry a higher MUFA:PUFA phospholipid ratio and a larger esterified neutral-lipid pool than APOE3, which is expected to change membrane order, phospholipase-releasable PUFA substrate and phagosomal/lysosomal membrane handling; this lipid-compositional difference, rather than an inflammatory or interferon transcript program (which are not enriched above the global shift in these data), is proposed as the discriminating genotype phenotype."], "title": "SCD-biased monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply reroutes glycerolipid esterification and Lands-cycle membrane remodeling in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2965882657017317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08483568707835276, "cosine_similarity": -0.04361946924540386, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7626278317152103, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2965882657017317, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08483568707835276, "cosine_similarity": -0.04361946924540386, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7626278317152103, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.15905425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 467}, {"id": "astra-evidence-v2-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "astra-evidence-v2", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All pathway assignments and physiological links are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was used. Only the supplied RNA and protein-spot abundances are measured. Activity, localization, organelle mass, molecular pools, flux and causal direction remain unmeasured.", "The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results: 1,705 positive and 507 negative, with an unspecified logarithm base. Missing genes are unknown, not unchanged. The 77.1% positive selected-list background, overlapping programs and correlated mitochondrial transcripts prevent interpreting directional coherence as independent evidence or a formal enrichment result.", "The hypothesis assumes the mitochondrial RNA contrast reflects a biologically consequential difference in respiratory-component production within comparable microglia. Different mitochondrial content, RNA processing/stability, normalization, or microglial state composition could yield the contrast with normal respiratory function. Biological replicate information and baseline absolute expression are not supplied; the mixed co-culture context also leaves astrocyte-mediated contributions unresolved.", "Fully successful metabolic/lysosomal adaptation remains a serious alternative. Higher gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5, together with positive nuclear metabolic and lysosomal RNA, may accompany preserved or increased respiratory throughput. The selected mechanism specifically predicts persistent basal inefficiency and increased mitochondrial oxidant signaling; it must be weakened if these are absent. Reduced reserve seen only after a future stress challenge would not establish the claimed ongoing mock-condition defect.", "The strongest program left without a causal explanation is coordinated sterol acquisition/synthesis: gene:SCARB1 +8.223, gene:LDLR +1.501, gene:SREBF2 +1.064, gene:LSS +2.272, gene:DHCR24 +3.694 and gene:SOAT1 +1.254. It may accompany a broader membrane-handling state, but no sterol trapping, ER sterol depletion, excess cholesterol, SREBP cleavage or export failure is claimed. ABCA1, ABCG1 and NPC1 are absent from the selected RNA rows, so their behavior is unknown.", "Every protein spot has multiple candidate identities. Spot effects cannot establish individual protein abundance, respiratory-complex function, or RNA-protein concordance. The two ATP6V1E1-candidate decreases could also be compatible with a primary lysosomal problem, but they do not identify such a defect."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 isogenic iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, incomplete coordination of mitochondrial- and nuclear-encoded respiratory components causes lower respiratory assembly/coupling efficiency per unit mitochondrial mass. Mitochondrial redox stress then sustains compensatory nuclear oxidative-metabolism and TFEB-associated lysosomal transcription. This proposes an ongoing, incompletely corrected mitochondrial defect in the supplied condition; the abundance measurements prioritize this hypothesis but do not establish that defect or its causal direction.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline test: in independently differentiated, matched day-30 mock APOE4 and APOE3 co-cultures, measure microglial mitochondrial translation, assembled respiratory complexes, coupled mitochondrial ATP production per oxygen consumed, and mitochondrial peroxide. Report both per-cell values and values normalized to independently assessed mitochondrial mass, with comparable viability and microglial state. APOE4 is predicted to have poorer coordination of mitochondrial/nuclear respiratory protein production, lower assembled/coupled capacity per mass, and higher mitochondrial peroxide despite its positive nuclear RNA program. Normal or increased coupling with balanced assembly and no excess peroxide would favor successful adaptation and substantially weaken this mechanism. Higher oxygen consumption alone would not distinguish the explanations.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: express mitochondrially targeted catalase versus a catalytically inactive, identically targeted control in matched mock APOE4 and APOE3 microglia. After verifying that active catalase lowers mitochondrial peroxide without changing viability, mitochondrial mass or cargo uptake, predict a larger reduction in TFEB nuclear localization and the GAA/CTSB/ATP6V1A transcriptional response in APOE4. Full respiratory assembly rescue is not required by this perturbation. If peroxide is lowered but the genotype-associated TFEB/lysosomal response persists, the proposed mitochondrial-redox-to-lysosome causal connection is weakened; a cargo-driven adaptive state becomes more plausible. This intervention is a future test, not evidence that peroxide or TFEB activity was elevated in the supplied experiment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["1. APOE4-associated regulation produces opposing respiratory RNA changes: gene:MT-ND4 -1.802, gene:MT-CYB -2.322, gene:MT-CO2 -1.328 and gene:MT-ATP6 -3.351, while represented nuclear respiratory RNAs increase, including gene:NDUFS7 +5.675, gene:NDUFS8 +4.933, gene:UQCRC2 +4.021, gene:COX5B +2.333, gene:COX6B1 +2.604 and gene:ATP5F1B +2.647. These are reported RNA log fold changes with unspecified base. The initiating regulatory change is unidentified; these observations are RNA measurements, not mitochondrial genomic variants. Exceptions gene:MT-ND4L +1.951 and gene:MT-ND5 +1.929 preclude describing all mitochondrial transcription as suppressed.", "2. The proposed functional consequence is incomplete coordination of respiratory-complex production and assembly, leaving less efficient coupled ATP production despite increased nuclear respiratory expression. Coassembly of nuclear- and mitochondrial-encoded components is unverified background knowledge here. Unequal RNA changes alone cannot establish protein stoichiometry, a limiting subunit, translation failure, complex abundance or ATP flux; this is the central causal assumption to test under mock treatment.", "3. Persisting electron-transfer inefficiency is proposed to increase mitochondrial oxidant signaling and evoke antioxidant adaptation. Increased gene:PRDX3 +3.488, gene:GPX4 +2.791 and gene:PRDX2 +4.412 are compatible abundance evidence, not measurements of oxidants or antioxidant activity. protein_spot:077 rises +1.070 log2 fold change (p=0.003), but its complete candidate list is KRT1, PRDX2, KRT9, KRT10, RAB1A, ACTB; it cannot confirm PRDX2 protein induction.", "4. Respiratory/redox feedback sustains compensatory substrate-processing and nuclear respiratory transcription: gene:MPC2 +7.980, gene:DLD +5.539, gene:PDP1 +2.999, gene:ACO2 +3.537, gene:IDH3B +2.024, gene:IDH3G +3.942, gene:OGDH +8.558 and gene:SDHB +1.653 accompany the nuclear respiratory increases in step 1. The inferred purpose is to support oxidative energy production; increased pyruvate entry, TCA flux, oxygen consumption and restored whole-cell ATP supply have not been observed. Compensation is hypothesized to leave intrinsic coupling inefficient even if total ATP demand can still be met.", "5. Mitochondrial redox stress also drives a TFEB-associated lysosomal capacity response, plausibly increasing machinery for cellular material turnover: gene:TFEB +2.385, gene:LAMP1 +1.377, gene:ATP6V1A +4.225, gene:ATP6V1E1 +1.698, gene:ATP6V1H +6.880, gene:GAA +9.961, gene:GBA +6.713, gene:HEXA +5.677, gene:HEXB +2.171, gene:CTSB +5.520 and gene:CTSD +2.864. TFEB nuclear localization, lysosomal acidity, proteolytic flux and mitophagy are inferred or unknown, not observed. gene:CTSS -5.566 is an important exception. protein_spot:064 (-1.202 log2; ANXA1, GNPDA1, ATP6V1E1, CAMK2A, PARP1) and protein_spot:065 (-0.926 log2; ANXA1, ATP6V1E1, ARPC1B, CBR1, GART) challenge any assumption that increased acidification RNA guarantees increased pump protein; neither identifies which candidate changed."], "title": "Persistent respiratory inefficiency drives compensatory oxidative and lysosomal remodeling in mock APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.049551379093896536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03287259511007771, "cosine_similarity": -0.04518271691409841, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6639935275080906, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.049551379093896536, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03287259511007771, "cosine_similarity": -0.04518271691409841, "direction_accuracy": 0.07119741100323625, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6639935275080906, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.8223249999999998, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 10}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_027", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1, 77% positive); the reported logarithm base is unspecified and effects are used only as signed, ranked evidence, not as calibrated fold changes.", "Transcript abundance differences for lipid enzymes translate at least partly into protein and catalytic activity differences; no enzyme activity, no acyl-CoA pool, no lysophospholipid pool and no lipid species were measured in this dataset.", "Protein spots are mixtures of candidate genes (mean ~4.8 candidates per spot); protein_spot:044/045 (ANXA1 among candidates, up) and protein_spot:053 (CTSD among candidates, up) are treated as directionally consistent context only, not as identified proteins.", "The global positive shift of the selected RNA list is treated as a nuisance baseline; the mechanism relies on within-pathway directional discordance (SCD/LPCAT1 up versus ACSL4/ACSL5/ALOX15 down) rather than on overall up-regulation.", "Astrocyte co-culture and day-30 maturation state are assumed comparable between APOE3 and APOE4 arms, so the signature is attributed to genotype rather than to differing cell composition or maturation."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally up-regulate a coupled deacylation/re-acylation and glycerolipid-assembly module (PLA2G7, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, GPAT4, AGPAT2, DGAT1, CHPT1, PCYT2) on top of a strongly induced SREBF1-SCD lipogenic arm, while transcripts for long-chain PUFA activation (ACSL4, ACSL5) and PUFA oxygenation (ALOX15) fall. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is the acyl-CoA species available for sn-2 re-acylation in the Lands cycle: with endolysosomal membrane turnover elevated (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, LAMP1, RAB7A, PIK3C3, ATG4A/D) and re-acylation capacity raised, the re-acylation step is supplied predominantly by SCD-derived monounsaturated/saturated acyl-CoA rather than polyunsaturated acyl-CoA, producing membranes with lower PUFA content and shunting surplus acyl-CoA into triacylglycerol. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux and lipid composition; no lipid species were measured and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: Pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. CAY10566/A939572) in APOE4 microglia, with vehicle-treated APOE3 as reference, should lower the PC/PE MUFA:PUFA sn-2 ratio and TAG content toward APOE3 values and partially restore phagocytic membrane expansion, without abolishing the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program. If SCD inhibition leaves the APOE4 membrane acyl-chain profile and TAG load unchanged, the proposed MUFA-supply bottleneck is wrong.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show, in APOE4, increased 16:1/18:1-containing PC and PE species, decreased 20:4- and 22:6-containing PC/PE, and increased TAG and cholesteryl ester. Finding equal or higher PUFA-phospholipid in APOE4 would falsify the central claim, and would also be the expected outcome if the FADS1 increase (counter-evidence in this dataset) dominates.", "Re-expression of ACSL4 in APOE4 microglia (or supplementation with arachidonate at fixed BSA ratio) should restore PUFA-phospholipid and increase sensitivity to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3); if APOE4 cells are equally RSL3-sensitive to APOE3 at baseline and unaffected by ACSL4 restoration, the PUFA-limitation arm is not operating.", "Stable-isotope tracing (13C-acetate or D9-choline) should show a higher fraction of newly synthesised acyl chains and faster PC label turnover in APOE4 than APOE3; comparable turnover rates would weaken step 2 and step 4 (accelerated Lands cycle).", "LPCAT1 knockdown should increase steady-state lysophosphatidylcholine and reduce TAG accumulation in APOE4 more than in APOE3; equal responses in both genotypes would argue the re-acylation step is not differentially loaded.", "GENERAL WEAKENING RESULT: if lipidomics, acyl-CoA profiling and membrane-order (Laurdan GP) measurements all show no APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference while the transcript differences replicate, the mechanism should be rejected in favour of a transcript-level-only or compositional/technical explanation of the global RNA shift."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred demand): APOE4 microglia carry a higher endolysosomal/autophagic membrane-turnover transcript program (TFEB, CTSB, CTSD, GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, HEXB, LAMP1, SCARB2, ATP6V1A, RAB7A, PIK3C3, ATG4A, ATG4D, ATG9A) together with elevated lipid-uptake receptors (SCARB1, CD36, TREM2, MERTK, APOE, ABCA7). We infer, but did not measure, an increased flux of membrane phospholipid and of exogenous lipid through the endolysosome, which raises the requirement for phospholipid deacylation and resynthesis.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): Deacylation capacity is raised (PLA2G7 up, one of the highest-confidence rows), generating lysophospholipid acceptors; PC/PE head-group synthesis transcripts (CHPT1, PCYT2) are also up, consistent with increased phospholipid biogenesis demand rather than net membrane loss.", "Step 3 (PRIMARY BOTTLENECK, inferred): The acyl-CoA species supplied to sn-2 re-acylation is the limiting determinant of the resulting membrane. SREBF1 and SCD are strongly up (with INSIG1, LDLR, ACSS2, ACAT2, DHCR24, DHCR7, LSS), implying enlarged de novo saturated/monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply, whereas ACSL4 and ACSL5, which activate long-chain (including polyunsaturated) fatty acids, are down. We therefore predict a raised MUFA-CoA : PUFA-CoA ratio in the cytosolic acyl-CoA pool. This pool was not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Elevated lysophospholipid acyltransferase transcripts (LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2) act on this skewed acyl-CoA pool, so accelerated Lands-cycle turnover resolves into PC/PE/PS species enriched in 16:0/16:1/18:1 and depleted in 20:4/22:6 sn-2 chains.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Acyl-CoA that exceeds phospholipid re-acylation demand is routed through the glycerol-3-phosphate pathway (GPAT4, AGPAT2, DGAT1 up; MGLL up indicating concurrent hydrolysis) into triacylglycerol and cytoplasmic lipid droplets, and through SOAT1 into cholesteryl ester; this is the predicted overflow arm, not a measured lipid pool.", "Step 6 (predicted consequence): PUFA-poor, MUFA-rich membranes are less peroxidisable and less deformable. The reduced peroxidation substrate is consistent with the concurrent ALOX15 decrease and GPX4/PRDX2/PRDX3/PRDX5 increase, and predicts reduced arachidonate-derived eicosanoid capacity and impaired large-scale membrane deformation (phagocytic cup, lysosomal membrane expansion) in APOE4 relative to APOE3."], "title": "APOE4 microglia re-write phospholipid sn-2 acyl chains: SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA becomes the limiting input to an accelerated Lands cycle, diverting membrane turnover into MUFA-enriched phospholipid and triacylglycerol"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2661540449728612, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11166678160385109, "cosine_similarity": -0.04992273503156546, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_027", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7769611650485436, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2661540449728612, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11166678160385109, "cosine_similarity": -0.04992273503156546, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7769611650485436, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.87654675, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 468}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_097", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so absence of FASN, ACACA, ACLY, ELOVL5/6, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, PLIN2, LIPA, PSAP and NPC1 from the file is treated as uninformative rather than as evidence of no change; the module is judged only on the genes present.", "Transcript log fold changes (logarithm base unspecified and preserved as reported) are assumed to track enzyme protein abundance for the named lipid enzymes; no lipid-enzyme protein spot in the supplied 2-D gel data resolves any of them, so this link is untested here.", "Enzyme abundance is assumed to constrain pathway flux and acyl-CoA/lipid composition; substrate availability, allosteric control and lysosomal pH could dominate instead.", "The genotype-associated global upward shift of the supplied RNA effects (median about +1.46) is assumed to be a property of the selected list or of normalisation, so pathway coherence is judged relative to that shifted background rather than against zero.", "Protein spots are assumed to be mixtures: each spot has multiple candidate genes and is not treated as a uniquely identified protein; spot changes are used only as weak corroboration.", "Astrocytes in the co-culture are assumed to supply lipid substrate but not to be the source of the measured microglial RNA signal; cell-type purity of the 10X Flex data is not verifiable from the supplied file.", "No lipid, lipidomic, flux, membrane-order or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied; every statement about lipid composition, flux, localisation and direction of causation is inference."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally configure a high-turnover membrane-lipid cycle: lysosomal glycero-/sphingolipid hydrolase and lipid-uptake transcripts are elevated together with an SREBF1-linked glycerolipid synthesis module (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, DGAT1, CHPT1), while the acyl-CoA re-activation arm that returns polyunsaturated chains to phospholipids (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3) is down. We hypothesise that re-esterification acyl-chain selectivity, not total lipid synthetic capacity, is the rate-limiting step, so liberated fatty acids are re-esterified predominantly as SCD-derived monounsaturated species into phosphatidylcholine and triacylglycerol rather than being returned as polyunsaturated phospholipid chains, shifting APOE4 microglial membranes toward a more monounsaturated, neutral-lipid-loaded state. Lipids themselves were not measured here; the lipid state is inferred, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) or SCD knockdown in APOE4 microglia should genotype-selectively reduce the 18:1-containing phosphatidylcholine fraction and triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet content toward APOE3 levels, and partially restore 20:4/22:6 phospholipid species, with a substantially smaller effect in isogenic APOE3 cells. If SCD inhibition changes APOE3 and APOE4 equally, or fails to move the APOE4 phospholipid acyl-chain profile, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock-treated APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher monounsaturated PC/PE species and higher TAG, with lower polyunsaturated PC/PE species. Finding equal or higher polyunsaturated phospholipid content in APOE4 would falsify the acyl-chain-selectivity claim while leaving the general 'more lipid turnover' idea intact.", "Pulse labelling with deuterated arachidonic acid (d8-20:4) should show reduced incorporation into APOE4 phospholipids per unit uptake, and re-expression of ACSL4 in APOE4 cells should restore incorporation without normalising gene:SREBF1 or gene:SCD transcript levels. Normal d8-20:4 phospholipid incorporation in APOE4 would weaken step 4.", "Blocking the catabolic input arm (acid sphingomyelinase inhibition with amitriptyline, or GBA inhibition with conduritol B epoxide, or bafilomycin-mediated lysosomal acidification block) should reduce, not increase, the APOE4 excess of triacylglycerol and of SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1 transcripts. If the APOE4 monounsaturated shift persists unchanged when lysosomal hydrolysis is blocked, the catabolism-to-resynthesis coupling in steps 1-2 is not the substrate source.", "SREBP pathway inhibition (SCAP/S1P blockade, e.g. PF-429242, or SREBF1 knockdown) should coordinately lower SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1 and DGAT1 transcripts and reduce APOE4 neutral-lipid storage; if these transcripts remain elevated in APOE4 after SREBF1 knockdown, the module is driven by something other than SREBP-1 and step 3 fails.", "If the acyl-chain bottleneck is real, exogenous supply of preformed 20:4 lysophosphatidylcholine should normalise APOE4 membrane polyunsaturated phospholipid content and phagocytic membrane behaviour more effectively than supplying free arachidonic acid; equal efficacy of both would argue against a re-activation (ACSL) step limitation.", "Independent quantitative measurement (targeted MS or validated antibodies) should confirm higher SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 protein in APOE4 microglia; unchanged protein for these enzymes despite the transcript differences would break the assumed transcript-to-enzyme link."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal luminal hydrolases acting on membrane lipids and glycoconjugates (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GBA2, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:GAA) plus v-ATPase subunits and gene:TFEB, which we interpret as increased lysosomal degradative capacity for internalised and autophagic membrane; the actual hydrolytic flux and the released lyso-lipid/free-fatty-acid pools are inferred, not observed.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Elevated lipid-uptake receptor transcripts (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE) suggest increased delivery of exogenous, astrocyte- and lipoprotein-derived lipid into this degradative compartment, adding substrate to the same cycle.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred transcription-factor activity): gene:SREBF1 is strongly elevated with gene:INSIG1, gene:LDLR, gene:HMGCS1, gene:DHCR24 and gene:LSS, consistent with an SREBP-1-type lipogenic program that is not switched off by the incoming lipid load; SREBP proteolytic activation and nuclear localisation were not measured.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred acyl-CoA composition): the acyl-CoA pool feeding re-esterification is predicted to become monounsaturated-biased because gene:SCD (stearoyl-CoA desaturase) is high while the long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases with polyunsaturated preference, gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5, and gene:GPAT3 are down; this compositional shift is inferred and is the proposed bottleneck.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux): downstream glycerolipid and Lands-cycle acyltransferase transcripts are coordinately up (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2, gene:DGAT1) with gene:MGLL and gene:ACSS2, so the elevated but compositionally constrained acyl-CoA supply is channelled into phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine re-acylation and into diacylglycerol-to-triacylglycerol esterification.", "Step 6 (predicted lipid phenotype, not measured): the net result is APOE4 membranes enriched in 16:1/18:1-containing phospholipid species and depleted of 20:4/22:6-containing species, together with increased triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet storage and futile ATP expenditure on breakdown-and-resynthesis, which we propose underlies APOE4 microglial membrane-order and phagocytic-handling differences.", "Step 7 (consequence, inferred): because polyunsaturated chains are poorly re-esterified, released polyunsaturated fatty acids are preferentially oxidised or exported, which would explain the concurrent high mitochondrial/TCA transcripts (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2) without invoking a separate primary mitochondrial defect."], "title": "MUFA-biased acyl-chain re-esterification is the bottleneck coupling accelerated lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism to glycerolipid storage in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2588524166451279, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0931287679727003, "cosine_similarity": -0.05347687225615475, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7791974110032363, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2588524166451279, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0931287679727003, "cosine_similarity": -0.05347687225615475, "direction_accuracy": 0.20550161812297735, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7791974110032363, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.0702555, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 469}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_050", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-filtered differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e 1) in an unspecified logarithm base; effect signs and relative ranks are interpreted, absolute fold sizes are not.", "The global list is 77.1% up (median +1.46), so a set is only treated as informative if its median exceeds/falls below that background; all enrichment statements here are permutation tests against the supplied rows, not against a whole transcriptome.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme capacity in the same direction; no protein, activity, flux, NADPH/NADP+, GSH/GSSG, ROS, lipid-peroxide, oxygen-consumption or lipid-droplet measurement is supplied, so every flux, localisation and redox-state statement is an inference.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein, and spot-based support is weak and corroborative only.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. G6PD, CAT, NFE2L2, NQO1, HMOX1, GCLC, GSR, TXNRD1, SLC7A11) are treated as unmeasured/not-differential, not as unchanged or absent pools.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic and the astrocyte co-culture composition comparable between genotypes, as stated in the supplied context."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, the APOE4 transcriptome is coherently reconfigured toward mitochondrial substrate import, TCA and electron-transport capacity (MPC2, OGDH, DLD, ACO2, SLC25A5/SLC25A46, 38/38 OXPHOS rows up) together with thioredoxin/peroxiredoxin peroxide-removal transcripts (PRDX2, PRDX3, PRDX5, TXNDC17, TXNL1, GPX4, CYB5R3, FTH1), while the cytosolic pentose-phosphate/upper-glycolysis arm that normally regenerates cytosolic NADPH is down (TALDO1, PGD, HK2, HK3). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is cytosolic NADPH-dependent regeneration of reduced peroxiredoxin/glutathione rather than peroxide production itself; the cell compensates by (i) mitochondria-biased reducing-equivalent supply (MDH1, GOT1, SLC25A11, NNT, GLUD1, SHMT1/2, ME1) and (ii) lowering the peroxidisable substrate pool and diverting citrate-derived acetyl-CoA into MUFA-enriched, GPX4-protected storage lipid (SLC25A1, SREBF1, SCD, LPCAT1, DGAT1 up; ACSL4 and ALOX15 down), which we propose is the transcriptional basis of the APOE4 lipid-accumulation phenotype. Peroxisomal metabolism is explicitly rejected as the driver. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: partial inhibition or knockdown of G6PD/PPP flux (e.g. 6-aminonicotinamide or G6PD knockdown) at doses tolerated by APOE3 should selectively collapse the cytosolic thiol redox potential in APOE4 microglia (roGFP2-Grx1 or HyPer7 oxidation) and selectively sensitise APOE4 to a bolus peroxide/menadione challenge. If APOE4 is equally or less sensitive than APOE3, the cytosolic-NADPH-limitation bottleneck (Step 3) is wrong.", "SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) should, in APOE4 more than APOE3, increase C11-BODIPY oxidation and reduce neutral-lipid droplet content, and this should be rescued by exogenous oleate but not by linoleate. No genotype difference in peroxidation after SCD inhibition would refute Steps 5-6.", "Thioredoxin-reductase inhibition (auranofin) or NNT knockdown should produce a larger rise in mitochondrial H2O2 (mito-HyPer7) and a larger drop in viability in APOE4 than APOE3; equal responses weaken Step 4.", "Limiting mitochondrial oxidative flux (low-dose rotenone, MPC inhibition with UK5099, or MPC2 knockdown) should reduce both the inferred peroxide load and the APOE4 excess of lipid droplets/SREBF1-SCD transcripts toward APOE3 levels; if lipid droplets persist unchanged, the redox-to-lipid coupling in Step 6 is refuted and lipid accumulation is redox-independent.", "Direct measurement should show higher basal mitochondrial H2O2 and a lower NADPH/NADP+ ratio in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock conditions, with GPX4/PRDX2 protein confirmed by targeted immunoblot rather than 2D spots; an unchanged or higher APOE4 NADPH/NADP+ ratio would falsify the core claim.", "Peroxisome-specific rejection test: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C26:0 lyso-PC / very-long-chain fatty-acid load) and catalase activity should NOT differ substantially between genotypes; a large APOE4-specific peroxisomal defect would indicate the assigned peroxisomal mechanism instead of this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred capacity): APOE4 raises transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate/metabolite import and oxidative carbon flow (gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:DLD +5.54, gene:ACO2 +3.54, gene:IDH3B, gene:SLC25A5, gene:SLC25A46, gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA) and every OXPHOS subunit row in the list is up (median ~+2.6, 38/38 positive). We infer, but do not measure, increased electron flux and therefore a higher basal rate of matrix superoxide/H2O2 generation.", "Step 2 (measured RNA -\u003e inferred NADPH capacity): the cytosolic NADPH-regenerating pentose-phosphate arm and its glucose entry step are transcriptionally reduced against a globally up-shifted list (gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:PGD -1.30, gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:HK3 -1.12; G6PD absent from the supplied rows). We infer reduced cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity; NADPH/NADP+ was not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck): with peroxide production inferred up and cytosolic NADPH supply inferred down, the reduction of oxidised peroxiredoxin/thioredoxin and glutathione by NADPH becomes the limiting step of peroxide clearance, not the abundance of the peroxidases themselves.", "Step 4 (compensation, measured RNA): reducing-equivalent supply is re-routed to mitochondria-linked and one-carbon sources (gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43, gene:SLC25A11 +4.50, gene:SLC25A13, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:GLS, gene:SHMT1, gene:SHMT2, gene:ME1), and thiol-peroxidase machinery is raised above the global shift (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:TXNL1 +4.33, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:CYB5R3 +4.66, gene:FTH1 +2.53). Localisation of these pools (matrix vs cytosol) is inferred from annotation, not measured.", "Step 5 (substrate-side escape, measured RNA): rather than only detoxifying peroxide, APOE4 cells are predicted to lower the peroxidisable lipid substrate: gene:ACSL4 -2.14 and gene:ALOX15 -3.63 reduce inferred PUFA-CoA acylation and enzymatic lipid peroxidation, while gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07 and gene:GPX4 +2.79 favour monounsaturated, peroxidation-resistant membrane phospholipid.", "Step 6 (lipid sink, measured RNA -\u003e inferred flux): elevated gene:SLC25A1 (+4.47) is proposed to export TCA citrate for cytosolic acetyl-CoA, feeding a lipogenic and sterol programme (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1) and a raised lysosomal/hydrolase programme (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:TFEB, v-ATPase rows). Net inferred phenotype: APOE4 microglia buffer a higher oxidative load by shunting carbon into MUFA-rich neutral-lipid storage, i.e. lipid accumulation is a redox-coupled sink, not an independent defect."], "title": "APOE4 microglia raise mitochondrial oxidative flux while cytosolic pentose-phosphate NADPH supply falls, making thiol-peroxidase buffering capacity the bottleneck and forcing an SCD/MUFA lipid-storage escape route"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29728981279769595, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09248714385163578, "cosine_similarity": -0.054339302781831945, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_050", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7535760517799353, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29728981279769595, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.09248714385163578, "cosine_similarity": -0.054339302781831945, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7535760517799353, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.234919, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 470}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_036", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a filtered differential-expression list (every row has adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) with a list-wide positive shift (77.1% positive, median +1.46 in the unspecified reported logarithm base); module claims are therefore made relative to that shifted background by permutation, not against zero, and absence of a gene from the list means 'not in the selected rows', not 'unchanged'.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, less securely, catalytic flux; no enzyme activity, metabolite, lipid species, lipid-droplet, respirometry or localisation measurement is supplied, so all flux, oxidation, storage and lysosomal-egress statements are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; spot-level effects are used only as weak corroboration or counter-evidence, never as evidence that a named protein changed.", "Because APOE4 is the engineered variant and the comparison is isogenic and mock-treated, the direction APOE4 -\u003e lipid state is assumed rather than demonstrated; correlation across a single mock comparison cannot establish causality, and astrocyte co-culture means some transcripts may derive from or be driven by the astrocyte compartment.", "The magnitude scale is treated as unreliable at the extremes (effects up to +15.5 in an unspecified log base with no replicate count supplied); ranks and set-level coherence are trusted more than individual large values."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 primarily by a lipid-handling state, not by an inflammatory or interferon state: transcripts for lipoprotein/scavenger uptake, a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase program, SREBP-type lipogenic genes, and mitochondrial TCA/OXPHOS genes are coordinately higher, while committed glycolytic steps and the polyunsaturated-acyl/oxygenase arm are lower. We propose that the rate-limiting node in APOE4 is disposal of fatty acid and sterol liberated from internalised lipid, and that this disposal runs through SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA into esterified neutral lipid plus mitochondrial oxidation, because no ABCA1-type efflux arm appears in the measured rows. The canonical type I interferon module is absent from the selected differential-expression rows, so we explicitly reject an interferon-driven mechanism; chemokine transcripts are higher but no more than the list-wide upward shift.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. CAY10566/A939572) or SCD knockout in mock isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should produce a genotype-by-treatment interaction - a disproportionate loss of neutral-lipid droplets, a disproportionate rise in saturated acyl species and ATF4/CHOP-type stress, and disproportionate death in APOE4. If SCD inhibition affects both genotypes equally, or if APOE4 droplet content is unchanged, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Load-dependence test: culturing both genotypes in lipoprotein-depleted medium, or blocking SCARB1/CD36-mediated uptake, should collapse the APOE4 excess in lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts and in neutral lipid. Persistence of the APOE4 lysosomal program under lipid-free conditions would argue for a cell-autonomous TFEB set-point instead of the proposed load-driven chain.", "Flux test: respirometry should show higher basal and maximal oxygen consumption with a larger etomoxir- or UK5099-sensitive fraction and lower glycolytic rate in APOE4; inhibiting lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or glucocerebrosidase (conduritol B epoxide) should reduce the APOE4 oxidative advantage more than APOE3. Equal or lower APOE4 respiration would weaken steps 3 and 5.", "Interferon rejection test: unbiased profiling and phospho-flow of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show no elevation of ISG15, IFIT1, MX1, STAT1 or phospho-STAT1, and JAK1/2 inhibition should not normalise the lipid phenotype. A clear APOE4 ISG signature or JAK-dependent rescue of the lipid phenotype would falsify the explicit rejection of the interferon mechanism.", "Composition test: lipidomics should show an APOE4 shift toward monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester with reduced polyunsaturated phospholipid and reduced oxidised-PUFA species. Increased polyunsaturated phospholipid or increased lipid peroxidation in APOE4 would contradict step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lipid and lipoprotein internalisation receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer, but did not measure, to increase lipid delivery flux into the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (measured abundance, inferred capacity): a TFEB/MITF-associated lysosomal program is transcriptionally higher (gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03) together with acid hydrolases and the v-ATPase (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:SCARB2, gene:NPC2), consistent with expanded hydrolytic capacity; hydrolase activity, lysosomal pH and cargo clearance were not measured.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck, inferred flux): the liberated fatty acid and sterol must be disposed of. No ABCA1/ABCG1/NR1H3 efflux transcript appears in the supplied rows while the E3 ubiquitin ligase MYLIP (+1.28) is higher, so we propose that efflux is not the escape route and that disposal is limited at the desaturation-and-esterification node.", "Step 4 (measured abundance): that node is transcriptionally reinforced in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), predicting increased SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA channelled into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester rather than into free saturated acyl pools.", "Step 5 (measured abundance, inferred flux): the surplus acyl-CoA that is not esterified is inferred to be oxidised, since TCA and respiratory-chain transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:DLD, gene:GOT1, gene:MPC2; gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:UQCRC2, gene:ATP5ME) while committed glycolytic steps are lower (gene:HK2 -3.67, gene:PFKP -3.08). Respiration, ATP flux and substrate use were not measured.", "Step 6 (consequence for the assigned focus): the acyl pool is biased away from oxidisable polyunsaturated species and their oxygenation (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ALOX15 -3.63) while peroxide-handling and pro-resolving transcripts are higher (gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX3 +3.47, gene:ANXA1 +4.15, whose product is one candidate identity of the most strongly increased protein spots protein_spot:045, protein_spot:044). We therefore predict that APOE4 accumulates stored, relatively saturated/monounsaturated neutral lipid without engaging an interferon program (gene:IFI16 +1.25 and gene:IFNAR1 +1.41 only, with no ISG15/IFIT/MX/OAS/STAT1/HLA rows) and with chemokine transcripts (gene:CXCL8 +3.11) that do not exceed the list-wide upward shift; the NF-kB brake gene:TNFAIP3 is lower (-1.05), which is counter-evidence discussed in analysis.md."], "title": "APOE4 microglia are constrained at SCD-dependent monounsaturated fatty-acid disposal, not at interferon/NF-kB signalling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30102832034855814, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11147631018640687, "cosine_similarity": -0.05521795426353076, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_036", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7592653721682848, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30102832034855814, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11147631018640687, "cosine_similarity": -0.05521795426353076, "direction_accuracy": 0.24433656957928804, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7592653721682848, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.493041, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 471}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_077", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript changes for lipid enzymes translate at least partly into enzyme protein and catalytic capacity; no lipid-enzyme protein was uniquely identified in the supplied spot data.", "The reported RNA log fold changes (unspecified logarithm base, preserved as reported) are comparable in sign and rank across genes despite a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% of rows positive) in this selected differential-expression list.", "ACSL4 provides a non-redundant share of arachidonoyl-CoA in these microglia; ACSL1/ACSL3/ACSL6 and LPCAT2/LPCAT3 were absent from the supplied rows and are therefore unmeasured, not unchanged.", "Spots 043-046 reflect ANXA1 rather than the co-listed candidates; the alternative top candidate TALDO1 has discordant RNA (-2.32), which favours but does not prove the ANXA1 assignment.", "No lipid, acyl-species, flux or lipid-droplet measurement is present in the discovery data; every acyl-composition and flux statement is a prediction, not an observation.", "Astrocyte co-culture and APOE-genotype effects on lipoprotein-borne lipid delivery are assumed not to be the sole driver of the transcriptional pattern."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally upregulate endolysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism and glycerolipid re-esterification machinery while downregulating ACSL4/ACSL5, so the rate-limiting step becomes supply of polyunsaturated acyl-CoA for Lands-cycle reacylation; the resulting monounsaturated (SCD-derived) acyl-CoA bias is predicted to re-esterify lysophospholipids with 16:1/18:1 and shunt surplus fatty acid into triacylglycerol, shifting membrane phospholipid acyl composition away from arachidonoyl/PUFA species rather than restoring the original bilayer. Only RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, acyl-species and localization statements are inferred and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring ACSL4 (cDNA re-expression) or supplying arachidonate plus lyso-PC to APOE4 microglia should selectively raise 20:4-containing PC/PE species and lower the TG:phospholipid ratio in APOE4 but not APOE3 (genotype x treatment interaction). If ACSL4 restoration leaves the PC 20:4 fraction and TG pool unchanged, the proposed PUFA-acyl-CoA bottleneck is wrong.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show an increased MUFA:PUFA ratio in PC/PE, increased TG and lyso-PC/ceramide, with the largest species-level effects in 16:1/18:1-containing phospholipids. Equal MUFA:PUFA ratios between genotypes would weaken the mechanism even if lysosomal transcripts remain elevated.", "SCD inhibition should reduce MUFA-phospholipid and TG content and increase lyso-PC accumulation more in APOE4 than APOE3; an equal-magnitude effect in both genotypes would argue the SCD arm is not genotype-limiting.", "LPCAT1 knockdown should cause a larger rise in lyso-PC and a larger drop in phagocytic membrane expansion in APOE4 than APOE3; no genotype interaction would weaken step 2.", "Blocking lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or SMPD1/GBA activity should reduce the APOE4-specific free-fatty-acid and neutral-lipid load and blunt SREBF1/SCD transcript elevation; if neutral lipid and SCD remain elevated, the lysosome-to-esterification flux ordering in steps 1-4 is wrong.", "Immunoblot or targeted proteomics should confirm higher LPCAT1, AGPAT2, SCD and lower ACSL4 protein in APOE4; unchanged or opposite protein levels for ACSL4 and SCD would falsify the bottleneck assignment."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: transcripts for lysosomal lipid hydrolases and acidification subunits are elevated in APOE4 (SMPD1 +5.63, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, HEXB +2.17, CTSB +5.52, CTSD +2.86, PLBD1 +1.68, PLA2G7 +1.13, ATP6V1H +6.88, LAMP1 +1.38, RAB7A +2.65, TFEB +2.38). Inferred: increased hydrolytic capacity and increased flux of endocytosed/autophagic membrane lipid through the lysosome, liberating lysophospholipids, ceramide and free fatty acids.", "Measured: glycerolipid acylation and headgroup enzymes are coordinately elevated (LPCAT1 +3.07, MBOAT2 +3.26, MBOAT1 +2.65, AGPAT2 +6.29, GPAT4 +1.58, CHPT1 +2.91, PCYT2 +1.05, TAZ +3.26, DGAT1 +1.72). Inferred: raised capacity for reacylation of lysophospholipids and for de novo glycerolipid/TG synthesis; the actual reacylation rate was not measured.", "Measured: the acyl-CoA input side is directionally split against a strongly up-shifted background - SREBF1 +4.67 and SCD +4.17 (monounsaturated acyl supply) versus ACSL4 -2.14, ACSL5 -3.11, GPAT3 -2.23. Inferred bottleneck: activation of long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids to acyl-CoA (ACSL4-type) limits the PUFA-CoA pool available to LPCAT/MBOAT enzymes.", "Inferred consequence: lysophospholipids generated in step 1 are reacylated preferentially with SCD-derived 16:1/18:1 rather than 20:4/22:6, and fatty acid in excess of reacylation demand is esterified through AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1 into triacylglycerol and lipid droplets instead of returning to bilayer phospholipid.", "Inferred consequence: the PUFA-phospholipid pool that serves as substrate for regulated phospholipase-A2 release is reduced; the concurrent rise in ANXA1 (RNA +4.15; ANXA1-containing protein spots 043-046 up) is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, further restriction of phospholipase access to membrane phospholipid.", "Inferred systems-level outcome: APOE4 microglia sustain high membrane-lipid turnover with compositionally altered, more saturated recycled membrane and enlarged neutral-lipid stores, which would constrain membrane expansion and PUFA-dependent signalling during phagocytic or inflammatory demand even in the mock state."], "title": "PUFA-acyl-CoA-limited Lands-cycle reacylation diverts lysosome-derived fatty acids into MUFA phospholipids and triacylglycerol in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3503027729572056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010479751647136173, "cosine_similarity": -0.05598110356352636, "direction_accuracy": 0.33818770226537215, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8169546925566343, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3503027729572056, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.010479751647136173, "cosine_similarity": -0.05598110356352636, "direction_accuracy": 0.33818770226537215, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8169546925566343, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.49300975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 472}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all rows adjusted p\u003c0.05, all |effect|\u003e1) with a strong global positive shift (77.1% positive, median +1.46); enrichment claims are therefore made only relative to this list's own distribution, and absolute pathway 'up-regulation' cannot be established from these data.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; effect magnitudes (range -7.94 to +15.46) are treated as ordinal/relative, not as literal fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least in rank order, the supply of the corresponding nuclear-encoded mitochondrial proteins. Protein amount, complex assembly state, enzymatic activity, respiratory flux, ROS levels, redox couple ratios and subcellular localisation were NOT measured and are inferred.", "The mtDNA-encoded transcript deficit is assumed to reflect biology rather than probe-panel or ambient-RNA behaviour of the 10X Flex assay; only 6 MT- rows survived selection, so this assumption is load-bearing and is given an explicit falsification test.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features; no spot is treated as a uniquely identified protein, and spot-level directions are used only as weak corroboration, never as primary evidence.", "Cells were co-cultured with astrocytes, so a fraction of measured RNA/protein signal may not be microglial; genotype effects are assumed to be predominantly microglia-intrinsic.", "Key regulators and canonical antioxidant enzymes (NFE2L2, KEAP1, CAT, SOD1, SOD2, GPX1, TXNRD1, GCLC/GCLM, G6PD, TFAM, PPARGC1A, PINK1, all PEX genes) are absent from the supplied DE list; their status is unknown, not unchanged.", "No lipid, metabolite, flux, imaging or replicate-level data are supplied; every lipid-phenotype statement is a prediction, not an observation."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia coordinately elevate the nuclear-encoded TCA/oxidative-phosphorylation transcript program while mtDNA-encoded core catalytic subunit transcripts are not co-elevated (mostly reduced). We hypothesise that mtDNA-encoded subunit supply, not nuclear subunit supply, is the rate-limiting step for assembly of complexes I, III, IV and V; the resulting sub-stoichiometric/partially assembled complexes increase univalent electron leak, raising matrix H2O2/superoxide. This is inferred to be countered by an up-regulated matrix thiol-peroxidase and NADPH-regenerating antioxidant program (PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/MSRA/NNT/ME1) and, at the lipid level, by diverting polyunsaturated acyl chains away from oxidisable membrane phospholipids into monounsaturated/neutral storage lipid (SCD, SREBF1, DGAT1, AGPAT2, SOAT1 up; ACSL4, ALOX15 down), predicting increased neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet content and a more saturated/monounsaturated membrane lipidome in APOE4. Peroxisomal biogenesis and peroxisomal beta-oxidation are explicitly NOT supported as the driver in these data and are rejected as the primary mechanism. Causality is not established; all directional statements are hypotheses to be tested.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: treating isogenic APOE3 and APOE4 microglia with a mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (e.g. mitoTEMPO or mitochondrially targeted catalase) should selectively normalise the APOE4 neutral-lipid/lipid-droplet excess and the elevated MUFA:PUFA phospholipid ratio WITHOUT reversing the elevated nuclear OXPHOS/TCA transcript signature (gene:NDUFA5, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH). A non-targeted cytosolic antioxidant (e.g. N-acetylcysteine at matched trolox-equivalent capacity) should have a substantially smaller effect. If the lipid phenotype is unchanged by matrix-targeted antioxidant, or is equally corrected by the cytosolic antioxidant, the ROS-driven lipid arm is falsified.", "BOTTLENECK TEST: blue-native PAGE plus in-gel activity and quantitative immunoblot of an mtDNA-encoded subunit (MT-CO1, MT-CYB) versus nuclear-encoded subunits (NDUFB8, ATP5F1B, UQCRC2) should show, in APOE4, a REDUCED mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded protein ratio and reduced assembled holo-complex I/IV per unit nuclear subunit, together with an increased pool of unassembled nuclear subunit. If APOE4 shows equal or higher mtDNA:nuclear protein ratio and normal assembly, the primary bottleneck is falsified even if the transcript pattern replicates.", "TECHNICAL FALSIFICATION OF THE mtDNA ARM: RT-qPCR (or non-probe-based total RNA-seq) of MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-CO2 normalised to nuclear reference genes, plus mtDNA:nDNA copy-number qPCR, should reproduce the APOE4 deficit seen in gene:MT-ATP6 and gene:MT-CYB. If these transcripts are equal between genotypes by an orthogonal assay, the observation is a 10X Flex probe artefact and step 2 collapses.", "REDOX STATE: APOE4 microglia should show higher matrix oxidant tone by orthogonal readouts - mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation, MitoSOX, a lower mitochondrial GSH:GSSG ratio, and a shifted PRDX3 dimer:monomer (hyperoxidation) ratio - consistent with the transcript program at gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:NNT. Equal mito-roGFP2-Orp1 oxidation and equal PRDX3 dimer ratio between genotypes would weaken the mechanism at its central inferred step.", "LIPID VULNERABILITY: pharmacological SCD inhibition or GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) should produce a larger increase in C11-BODIPY oxidation and a larger viability loss in APOE4 than APOE3, because the hypothesised PUFA-sparing/neutral-storage buffer is being removed. If APOE4 is equally or LESS sensitive than APOE3 to SCD or GPX4 inhibition, the lipid-buffering interpretation is wrong.", "PEROXISOME REJECTION TEST (this focus is predicted NEGATIVE): peroxisome number/morphology (PMP70/catalase immunofluorescence), C26:0/C22:0 VLCFA ratio and peroxisomal beta-oxidation capacity should NOT differ substantially between APOE4 and APOE3 under mock conditions, and knockdown of a peroxisomal beta-oxidation enzyme should not preferentially rescue APOE4. If instead APOE4 shows a clear VLCFA accumulation and peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect that tracks the reduced gene:ABCD1 signal, the peroxisomal alternative would supersede the mitochondrial bottleneck proposed here.", "GENOTYPE SPECIFICITY: the mito-nuclear transcript discordance and the antioxidant-plus-neutral-lipid signature should be reproducible in independent isogenic APOE4/APOE3 microglia lines under mock conditions and should be attenuated in APOE-knockout controls. Absence of the discordance in an independent isogenic pair would indicate a line-specific rather than APOE4-driven effect."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show a coherent elevation of nuclear-encoded mitochondrial oxidative transcripts relative to the strongly right-shifted background of this selected DE list (38/38 nuclear OXPHOS subunit rows positive, median +2.64 in the reported log unit, permutation p\u003c0.001 against the list's own median of +1.46; TCA/anaplerotic rows 8/8 positive, median +4.74, p=0.0003). Inferred, not measured: increased nuclear-encoded subunit protein supply to mitochondria.", "Measured: mtDNA-encoded transcripts are discordant with this program (MT-ATP6 -3.42, MT-CYB -2.30, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; only MT-ND4L +2.05, MT-ND5 +1.86). Inferred PRIMARY BOTTLENECK: the supply of mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits (ND4, CYB, COII, ATP6) becomes rate-limiting for holo-complex assembly, so nuclear subunits accumulate as unassembled or partially assembled modules. Assembly state, complex activity and protein-level stoichiometry were NOT measured here.", "Inferred (not measured): sub-stoichiometric assembly of complex I and complex III raises the fraction of reduced flavin/quinone sites that leak single electrons to O2, increasing matrix superoxide and H2O2 flux per unit of respiratory protein. No ROS, membrane potential, or respiration measurement is present in these data.", "Measured as transcripts, activity inferred: a matrix/thiol antioxidant and NADPH-supply program is up (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, PRDX2 +4.41, GPX4 +2.79, MSRA +2.64, TXNDC17 +7.09, TXNL1 +4.33, SELENOW +5.47, NNT +2.88, ME1 +1.36, GSS +2.11, AKR1A1 +4.13, CYB5R3 +4.73, FTH1 +2.53; thiol/antioxidant set n=17, median +2.79, permutation p=0.014). A significant protein spot whose candidate list includes CAT (protein_spot:017, +0.77 log2, p=0.001) and one including PRDX2 (protein_spot:077, +1.07, p=0.003) are directionally consistent but are multi-candidate spots and are not uniquely identified proteins.", "Measured as transcripts: acyl-chain handling is remodelled toward oxidation-resistant species and neutral storage (SCD +4.17, SREBF1 +4.67, FADS1 +1.59, AGPAT2 +6.27, DGAT1 +1.72, SOAT1 +1.25, DHCR24 +3.69, SCARB1 +8.24, LDLR +1.50) while the PUFA-phospholipid/lipoxygenase arm is down (ACSL4 -2.14, ACSL5 -3.11, ALOX15 -3.62). Inferred flux: reduced esterification of PUFA into membrane phospholipids and increased triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage, i.e. lipid droplets act as an oxidant-buffering sink rather than a passive by-product.", "Inferred consequence at the lipid level: APOE4 microglia should carry more neutral lipid per cell with a lower PUFA:MUFA ratio in phospholipids, and their oxidised-lipid burden should be conditional on GPX4/SCD capacity rather than on peroxisomal capacity. Increased lysosomal/degradative transcripts (CTSB +5.52, GBA +6.71, HEXA +5.68, ATP6V1A +4.23, TFEB +2.38) are a plausible downstream turnover response but are not required by the core claim."], "title": "Mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch in APOE4 microglia: mtDNA-encoded core subunit supply limits respiratory-chain assembly, driving matrix oxidant stress and a PUFA-sparing neutral-lipid shift"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20176863715245724, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11821071754754929, "cosine_similarity": -0.058095433822545346, "direction_accuracy": 0.27346278317152106, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8766990291262136, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.20176863715245724, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.11821071754754929, "cosine_similarity": -0.058095433822545346, "direction_accuracy": 0.27346278317152106, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8766990291262136, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.03747425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 473}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_028", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment statements are conditional on this biased background and were computed as percentile ranks within the supplied list to absorb the strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% of rows positive).", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified, so effects are used ordinally (percentile ranks), never as absolute fold changes.", "Increased hydrolase transcript abundance is assumed to raise mature enzyme amount and acidic-pH catalytic activity at the late endosome/lysosome; this activity, its localization and the resulting flux are inferred, not measured.", "Sphingolipid pools (ceramide, sphingomyelin, GlcCer, LacCer, GM2, GM3, S1P) are unmeasured in the supplied data; all lipid statements are predictions.", "The claimed imbalance assumes UGCG, SGMS1/SGMS2 and ASAH1 - which are absent from the supplied rows - are not increased in proportion to the hydrolases; this is an untested assumption, unverified background knowledge is used for pathway topology.", "Protein spots each carry 3-6 candidate genes (mean 4.8) and do not uniquely identify a protein; no spot uniquely identifies SMPD1, GBA or HEXA, so protein-spot evidence is treated as ambiguous corroboration only.", "Replicate structure is 'not supplied in workbook' and cells are co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-associated differences may include clone, culture or non-cell-autonomous contributions despite the isogenic label; no causal direction is established."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, the APOE4 genotype is associated with a selectively upper-tail increase in transcripts encoding the acid sphingolipid-degrading hydrolases and their delivery/acidification machinery (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GM2A, GLA, GBA2; GNPTG, IGF2R, ATP6V1H, TFEB), while the ceramide-consuming return arm is not co-elevated (B4GALT5 is reduced; CERS6, CERK, SGPL1, KDSR sit below the median of this up-shifted list; UGCG, SGMS1/2 and ASAH1 were not measured). The primary bottleneck is therefore proposed to be the capacity to re-glycosylate/re-acylate or phosphorylate lysosome-derived ceramide and sphingosine, not hydrolase supply, which predicts a measurable ceramide-enriched, SM/GlcCer/LacCer-depleted endolysosomal lipidome and a ceramide-biased late-endosomal membrane that increases demand on ESCRT/retromer sorting and membrane repair. Causality is not established by these cross-sectional genotype-associated abundance differences.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted or targeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show higher total and LE/lysosome-enriched ceramide (with C16:0/C18:0 species favoured, matching elevated gene:CERS4 and gene:CERS6) and lower sphingomyelin, GlcCer, LacCer and GM2/Gb3, giving a ceramide/sphingomyelin ratio increased by at least ~1.3-fold. If ceramide is unchanged or lower and sphingomyelin is higher in APOE4, the mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: blocking de novo synthesis with myriocin (serine palmitoyltransferase inhibitor) should NOT abolish the APOE4-minus-APOE3 ceramide difference, whereas acid sphingomyelinase inhibition (functional ASM inhibitor, e.g. amitriptyline) or glucocerebrosidase inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide) SHOULD collapse that difference and restore sphingomyelin/GlcCer. The opposite outcome - myriocin abolishing the difference while ASM/GBA inhibition does not - would show a de novo rather than a salvage/catabolic driver and would falsify this mechanism.", "Acidic-pH enzyme activity assays on matched lysates should show higher specific ASM, glucocerebrosidase and beta-hexosaminidase activity per mg protein in APOE4. Equal activity despite the transcript difference would break the measured-abundance to inferred-activity step.", "Measuring the unmeasured return arm: if ASAH1 (acid ceramidase) and UGCG protein or activity are increased in APOE4 in proportion to the hydrolases, the proposed ceramide-disposal bottleneck is weakened even if the hydrolase transcript pattern replicates.", "Rescue test: enforced expression of UGCG or SGMS1 (or acid ceramidase) in APOE4 microglia should normalise ceramide and reduce the elevated late-endosomal repair/sorting markers (LGALS3-positive puncta, CHMP4B recruitment) without lowering SMPD1/GBA/HEXA transcripts. Failure to normalise ceramide or the routing readout while enzyme expression is confirmed would place the bottleneck elsewhere.", "Compartment test: immunostaining should localise the ceramide excess to RAB7A/LAMP1-positive compartments rather than the plasma membrane or ER. A plasma-membrane-restricted ceramide increase would contradict the lysosomal-hydrolase origin proposed here."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured abundance: APOE4 microglia show coordinated high-percentile increases in RNA for the acid sphingolipid catabolic module - SMPD1 (gene:SMPD1, +5.63, 95th percentile of the supplied DE distribution), GBA (gene:GBA, +6.71, 98th), HEXA (gene:HEXA, +5.68, 96th), HEXB (gene:HEXB), the GM2 activator GM2A (gene:GM2A), GLA (gene:GLA) and non-lysosomal GBA2 (gene:GBA2) - alongside hydrolase-tagging, receptor-mediated delivery and V-ATPase acidification transcripts (gene:GNPTG, gene:IGF2R, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:TFEB). Mean percentile rank of the 7-gene hydrolase set = 77.4 (permutation p ~0.006-0.013), the highest of the modules tested.", "Inferred activity/flux (not measured here): the additional hydrolase transcript output translates into more mature enzyme delivered to an acidified late endosome/lysosome, raising catabolic flux from sphingomyelin and from glycosphingolipids (GM2, Gb3, GlcCer) toward ceramide inside that compartment.", "Inferred bottleneck: the arm that removes ceramide is not proportionally increased. B4GALT5 (LacCer synthase) is the single down-regulated sphingolipid gene in the list (gene:B4GALT5, -1.88, 13th percentile), and gene:CERS6, gene:CERK, gene:SGPL1 and gene:KDSR fall at or below the median of an otherwise strongly up-shifted list, while UGCG, SGMS1/2 and ASAH1 are absent from the supplied rows. Ceramide/sphingosine disposal capacity is therefore proposed as the rate-limiting node.", "Predicted lipid consequence (unmeasured pool, inferred only): endolysosomal ceramide rises while sphingomyelin, GlcCer, LacCer and GM2/Gb3 fall; GM3 may rise because gene:ST3GAL5 (GM3 synthase) is elevated and its LacCer precursor supply, not the enzyme, becomes limiting.", "Inferred membrane and routing consequence: ceramide-rich, rigid microdomains in the late-endosomal limiting membrane bias budding, intraluminal-vesicle formation and cargo sorting. Consistent with increased demand on this machinery, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:CHMP4B, gene:RAB7A, gene:RAB32 and the membrane-damage sensor gene:LGALS3 are all above the median, and cytosolic glycolipid transfer capacity gene:GLTP is elevated.", "Post-transcriptional discordance: 2-D protein spots whose candidate lists include lysosomal hydrolases split in direction (protein_spot:053 +1.54 and protein_spot:055 +0.58 up; protein_spot:058 -0.85, protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38 down), so the transcript increase is not mirrored by a uniform increase in hydrolase spot abundance; this is compatible with altered proenzyme maturation or redistribution rather than a simple proportional protein gain, and it is the weakest link in the chain."], "title": "APOE4 microglia up-regulate the lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase module without a matching ceramide-return arm, predicting a ceramide-loaded, complex-glycosphingolipid-depleted endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16873130746224568, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.00789113960130006, "cosine_similarity": -0.059019984382104936, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_028", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7015016181229774, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.16873130746224568, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.00789113960130006, "cosine_similarity": -0.059019984382104936, "direction_accuracy": 0.08737864077669903, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7015016181229774, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72675375, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 474}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_047", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list in an unspecified logarithm base; direction and coherence across independently annotated pathway members are interpreted, not the absolute magnitudes, and the whole list is 77% positive so sign-coherence is judged against that skewed background, not 50/50.", "Absent genes (e.g. FASN, ACACA, HMGCR, NPC1, ABCA1, LPCAT3, PLIN2, CPT1A) are unknown, not unchanged; every step is therefore a prediction about flux inferred from partial transcript coverage.", "Transcript increases are assumed to translate into proportionate enzyme activity in at least the lysosomal-hydrolase and acyl-transferase arms; this is unverified, and the 2-D protein spots cannot confirm it because each spot carries 2-6 candidate identities.", "Protein spots are treated as compatibility tests only. Spots whose candidate lists include cathepsins/hydrolases move in both directions (protein_spot:052, :053, :055, :057 up; protein_spot:058, :067, :069, :064, :065 down), and the strongest up-spots (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046; effects +1.96 to +3.05) contain ANXA1 and TALDO1 among other candidates; no individual protein identity is claimed.", "The mock condition is assumed to be an unchallenged steady state, so the mechanism describes ongoing altered routing/throughput; any loss of reserve is prospective and would only appear under a lipid or phagocytic challenge.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some lipid supply is non-cell-autonomous; the transcript changes are assigned to the microglial compartment as reported but the lipid source is not resolved by these data.", "Causality is not established: only steady-state abundances in one genotype contrast are supplied, and the decisive quantities (lysosomal and ER free-sterol pools, phospholipid acyl composition, de novo lipogenic and lysosomal hydrolytic flux) were not measured."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 not by a single blocked step but by a coordinated cell-state shift in lipid routing: transcripts for lipid uptake receptors and for TFEB/MITF-type lysosomal hydrolase biogenesis are coherently elevated together with SREBP-driven de novo fatty-acid/sterol synthesis and glycerolipid acyl-transfer/re-esterification enzymes, while the PUFA-activating and PUFA-oxygenating arm (ACSL4, ALOX15, plus ACSL5, GPAT3) is reduced. We propose this constitutes increased flux of lipid through the endolysosome and back into newly esterified membrane and neutral-lipid pools with an altered acyl-chain input, predicting monounsaturated-enriched, arachidonate-depleted phospholipids and expanded TAG/CE stores in APOE4, rather than a failure of lysosomal degradative capacity in the measured condition. All statements are about measured transcript/spot abundance; flux, lipid species and localization were not measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine shifted toward 16:1/18:1 species with reduced 20:4-containing species, plus increased triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester. If APOE4 membranes are unchanged or arachidonate-enriched, the acyl-remodeling step (Step 5) fails and the mechanism is substantially weakened.", "Prospective 13C-acetate (or D2O) tracing should show higher incorporation into fatty acids, sterol and phospholipid in APOE4 than APOE3 under mock. Equal de novo flux despite elevated SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1 transcripts would show transcript elevation without functional activation and would favour a transcriptional-state-only explanation.", "Prospective pulse-chase of fluorescent or isotope-labelled myelin/lipoprotein cargo should show equal or faster clearance of the sphingolipid/glycolipid cargo in APOE4 at baseline, matching the elevated hydrolase program. Slower baseline clearance with accumulation of undegraded substrate would support the competing 'failed catabolic compensation / lysosomal sequestration' model instead.", "Prospective SCD inhibition or DGAT1 inhibition should be selectively deleterious in APOE4 (greater free-fatty-acid stress, lysosomal membrane damage, loss of viability) relative to APOE3, because the proposed routing loop depends on monounsaturate supply and esterification. No genotype-by-drug interaction would weaken the claim that this routing is load-bearing.", "Prospective restoration of ACSL4 (or supplementation with arachidonate) in APOE4 microglia should re-introduce arachidonoyl-phospholipid, restore stimulus-evoked eicosanoid release, and increase sensitivity to ferroptotic/peroxidative challenge without reversing the lysosomal hydrolase program. If ACSL4 restoration also normalises the lysosomal and SREBP programs, the causal ordering proposed here (Steps 1-4 upstream of Step 5) is wrong.", "Prospective free-cholesterol imaging (filipin) plus ER sterol-sensing readouts should show APOE4 sterol distributed into esterified/droplet pools with only modestly altered lysosomal free cholesterol. Marked lysosomal free-cholesterol accumulation with an NPC-like phenotype would favour the sequestration alternative over the increased-throughput mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (routing in): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid uptake and handling receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:PLTP +1.06, gene:NPC2 +1.17), together with phagocytic/opsonic transcripts (gene:C1QA, gene:C1QB, gene:C1QC, gene:MERTK, gene:MRC1, gene:FCGR1A), consistent with more lipid-laden cargo being delivered to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (degradative capacity): A coherent lysosomal-biogenesis (CLEAR-type) transcriptional program is elevated - gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MITF +1.03, gene:TFEC +1.65 with 23/23 represented hydrolase/v-ATPase members positive (e.g. gene:GAA +9.96, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:DPP7 +4.52, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:CTSD +2.86; exception gene:CTSS -5.57). This predicts increased hydrolysis of sphingolipid/glycolipid/phospholipid cargo and release of fatty acids and sterol, not a deficit of hydrolase expression.", "Step 3 (anabolic re-capture): Sterol and fatty-acid synthesis transcripts move up in parallel with uptake (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ME1 +1.36; gene:SREBF2 +1.06, gene:HMGCS1 +1.08, gene:ACAT2 +2.04, gene:LSS +2.27, gene:DHCR7 +2.71, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:EBP +1.34, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), supplying monounsaturated acyl-CoA and sterol for re-esterification rather than net export.", "Step 4 (acyl transfer and storage): Glycerolipid assembly and Lands-cycle remodeling transcripts rise (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGKA +1.53, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:PLA2G7 +1.13), routing liberated and newly made acyl chains into phosphatidylcholine/ethanolamine and into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester stores.", "Step 5 (acyl-chain bias): The polyunsaturate-activating and -oxygenating arm is selectively lower (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ALOX15 -3.63, with gene:ACSL5 -3.11, gene:GPAT3 -2.23, gene:PNPLA1 -1.55), so the acyl input to remodeling is predicted to shift toward SCD-derived 16:1/18:1 and away from arachidonate-containing phospholipid.", "Step 6 (cell-state consequence): The predicted product is an APOE4 microglial state with expanded lysosomal and neutral-lipid compartments and MUFA-enriched, PUFA-depleted membranes - intrinsically less peroxidizable (concordant but non-decisive gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:FTH1 +2.53, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10) and with reduced capacity to release arachidonate for eicosanoid signalling; increased fatty-acid and mitochondrial carbon-handling transcripts (gene:HADHA +2.86, gene:ETFA +3.55, gene:ACOX1 +1.24, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:GOT1 +6.43) are compatible with disposal of the extra acyl load. Reduced reserve would be expected only on future lipid challenge; the supplied mock data do not show an ongoing degradative bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a high-throughput lysosome-to-lipogenesis routing loop that remodels membranes toward MUFA-rich, PUFA-poor, storage-biased lipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3927094487316767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.149380871220321, "cosine_similarity": -0.05974566248703834, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7993980582524273, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3927094487316767, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.149380871220321, "cosine_similarity": -0.05974566248703834, "direction_accuracy": 0.24919093851132687, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7993980582524273, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.3683235, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 106}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_017", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All biochemical and pathway assignments are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was used. The supplied strong examples inform format only, and prior_hypotheses.json is empty.", "Lower ACSL4 transcript abundance reduces active enzyme capacity in the compartment supplying membrane reacylation. None of the supplied protein spots includes ACSL4, SCD, MBOAT1, MBOAT2 or LPCAT1 among its candidates, so the central RNA-to-enzyme links lack protein support.", "Other fatty-acid activating enzymes do not fully compensate for ACSL4. Missing genes in this selected differential-expression table are unknown, not absent or unchanged; ACSL5 reduction (gene:ACSL5) does not establish arachidonate specificity.", "The higher desaturation/remodeling transcripts translate into sufficient enzyme capacity and alternative acyl-donor availability. FADS1 induction (gene:FADS1) could instead sustain polyunsaturated substrate supply and counter the proposed imbalance.", "A genotype-associated activation defect persists after accounting for fatty-acid uptake, astrocyte substrate delivery, cell state and viable cell number. These alternatives are unresolved by the supplied isogenic comparison, which lacks biological replicate information.", "A reduced incorporation rate need not lower steady-state arachidonate-containing lipid abundance: reduced ALOX15 RNA and increased GPX4 RNA (gene:ALOX15, gene:GPX4) could alter oxidative loss. No lipid pool, oxidation rate or membrane-turnover flux was measured.", "RNA effects retain their unspecified logarithm base and are not converted to fold changes. Protein effects are spot-level log2 fold changes with multiple candidate genes and cannot identify individual protein abundance, activity or localization."], "claim": "In Day-30 mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced ACSL4-dependent arachidonate activation is the proposed primary bottleneck for membrane phospholipid reacylation. If lower ACSL4 RNA reduces enzyme capacity, limited arachidonoyl-CoA formation alongside an induced desaturation/remodeling program causes a lower arachidonate-to-oleate incorporation ratio in membrane glycerophospholipids. Enzyme activity, incorporation flux and lipid pools were not measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective flux test: in matched viable microglia across independent differentiations, use short arachidonate and oleate isotope-tracer time courses, measuring intracellular free-precursor enrichment, labeled acyl-CoAs and subsequent phosphatidylethanolamine/phosphatidylcholine labeling. After precursor normalization, APOE4 should show slower arachidonoyl-CoA formation and a lower arachidonate-to-oleate incorporation ratio. Equal or greater arachidonate activation and incorporation would weaken the mechanism even if steady-state lipid composition differs.", "Discriminating catalytic rescue: restore ACSL4 in APOE4 to the APOE3 active-protein level and compare with expression- and localization-matched catalytically inactive ACSL4 and vector controls. Wild-type ACSL4 should restore arachidonoyl-CoA formation first, then arachidonate incorporation, without requiring normalization of the elevated remodeling transcripts. Failure despite verified enzyme activity, or equal rescue by inactive ACSL4, would weaken an ACSL4 catalytic bottleneck.", "Reciprocal perturbation: titrate ACSL4 repression in APOE3 to the active-protein level measured prospectively in APOE4. It should reproduce the activation and incorporation defects under matched precursor supply; restoring an RNA-resistant functional ACSL4 should reverse them. Failure to phenocopy after confirmed target reduction would weaken the proposed causal chain.", "Substrate-supply discrimination: compare the genotypes under matched astrocyte conditions and matched intracellular arachidonate/oleate precursor enrichment. The activation defect should persist and remain selectively correctable by functional ACSL4. If equalizing precursor delivery alone eliminates the defect while ACSL4 activity remains lower, substrate availability or co-culture context is a better explanation than the proposed primary bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured anchor: ACSL4 RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:ACSL4; reported log fold change -2.142, logarithm base unspecified). The first inferred step is that this association translates into reduced ACSL4 catalytic capacity.", "Proposed primary bottleneck: reduced ACSL4 capacity slows activation of free arachidonate to arachidonoyl-CoA, restricting donor supply for phospholipid reacylation. This biochemical role is unverified background knowledge here; neither reaction flux nor the arachidonoyl-CoA pool is observed.", "RNA increases in SCD, MBOAT1, MBOAT2 and LPCAT1 (gene:SCD, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:LPCAT1) suggest a competing capacity for desaturation and phospholipid remodeling. Assuming the relevant enzymes are active, oleate-supported remodeling can continue while arachidonate activation is limiting; these transcripts do not establish enzyme activity or identical substrate preferences.", "During membrane turnover, this donor imbalance is predicted to lower arachidonate incorporation relative to oleate into phosphatidylethanolamine and phosphatidylcholine. Higher TFEB and RAB7A RNA (gene:TFEB, gene:RAB7A) provides turnover-related context, but turnover rate, enzyme localization and membrane composition are all inferred. The primary predicted difference is incorporation flux; no total phospholipid or neutral-lipid accumulation is asserted."], "title": "An ACSL4 activation bottleneck biases APOE4 membrane phospholipid reacylation"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022329505593915, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.003482081394189934, "cosine_similarity": -0.06512770788931317, "direction_accuracy": 0.032362459546925564, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6554142394822007, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.022329505593915, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.003482081394189934, "cosine_similarity": -0.06512770788931317, "direction_accuracy": 0.032362459546925564, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6554142394822007, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.1227350000000005, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 11}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_037", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have adjusted p \u003c 0.05 and |effect| \u003e= 1) in an unspecified logarithm base; only sign, rank and coherence relative to the list's own 77% positive background are used, not absolute fold magnitudes.", "Genes absent from the list (e.g. LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1, PLIN2, CPT1A, ASAH1, PSAP, SQSTM1) are unknown, not unchanged; the mechanism must not be read as asserting their behaviour.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to translate into at least proportional protein/enzyme capacity for the hydrolase, acyltransferase and SREBP-target modules; capacity is not activity and no hydrolytic, esterification, autophagic or oxidative flux was measured.", "Protein spots are ambiguous (2-6 candidate identities each, pervasive keratin/actin contamination); they are used only for compatibility or contradiction, never as identification of a single protein.", "Members of each program were fixed a priori from canonical pathway membership (unverified background knowledge) before signs were examined; no member was dropped to make directions agree, and the genes are not statistically independent, so coherence is descriptive, not a formal enrichment result.", "Genotype effects are assumed cell-intrinsic to the microglial compartment, although astrocyte co-culture supplies lipoproteins and could contribute; the mock condition is treated as a steady state, so any reduced reserve would only be revealed by a future lipid or phagocytic challenge and is not claimed as an ongoing defect.", "The alternative that this profile reflects a lysosomal degradative bottleneck with compensatory (insufficient) CLEAR induction is not excluded by these data; the decisive hydrolytic and esterification fluxes remain unknown."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia (co-cultured with astrocytes, day 30) differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated cell-state change in lipid handling rather than by a single defective enzyme: transcripts for lipid/membrane cargo uptake and endosomal sorting, for a CLEAR-like lysosomal acid-hydrolase and v-ATPase module (including the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolases GBA, SMPD1, HEXA/HEXB, NAGLU, GLA), and for glycerolipid acylation, neutral-lipid esterification and both SREBP arms are jointly elevated. We propose that increased delivery and hydrolysis of lipid-rich membrane cargo is coupled to re-esterification/resynthesis of the released fatty acid and sterol, so the ER-sensed sterol pool is not replenished and SREBP-driven de-novo synthesis (SCD, FADS1, ACSS2, HMGCS1, LSS, DHCR7/24, LDLR) continues alongside catabolism - a futile-cycle-like routing state, with acyl input biased toward newly made monounsaturated chains (SCD up) rather than reactivated long-chain fatty acid (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3 down). All measurements are transcript or 2D-gel spot abundances; no flux, activity, lipid species or localization was measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective pulse-chase in mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia with labelled membrane cargo (e.g. BODIPY/isotope-labelled myelin or apoptotic-cell membranes, NBD-sphingomyelin): APOE4 should show a faster rate of substrate hydrolysis and a larger fraction of released label appearing in cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol within 6-24 h, without accumulation of undegraded substrate in LAMP1+ compartments. Slower clearance with accumulation of undegraded cargo would falsify the increased-throughput routing model and favour a lysosomal bottleneck with failed compensation.", "Prospective SOAT1 (avasimibe) or DGAT1 inhibition: SREBP2-target transcripts (HMGCS1, LDLR, LSS, DHCR7, DHCR24) should be suppressed more strongly in APOE4 than APOE3, with a greater rise in free-sterol/ISR markers. Equal, genotype-independent suppression would weaken steps 3-4.", "Prospective lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia: higher cholesteryl ester and triacylglycerol with a shift of stored and phospholipid acyl chains toward 16:1/18:1 and away from ACSL4-dependent 20:4 species. Equal or increased PUFA-containing phospholipid in APOE4 would falsify step 5.", "Prospective SCD inhibition: APOE4 microglia should lose neutral-lipid storage and induce DDIT3/ISR and lipotoxicity markers more than APOE3; an equal response in both genotypes weakens the MUFA-bias step.", "Prospective v-ATPase inhibition (bafilomycin A1) or GBA/SMPD1 knockdown: APOE4 should be more sensitive than APOE3 in sphingolipid/glycolipid accumulation and in loss of the SREBP-target program, because more of its lipid supply passes through lysosomal hydrolysis; equal sensitivity would argue the lysosomal route is not the dominant lipid conduit in APOE4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (uptake/routing, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia increase transcripts for lipoprotein/membrane-cargo scavenging and recognition (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:ABCA7, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:PLTP, gene:ANXA1 +4.15, gene:LGALS3) and for endosome-to-lysosome sorting (gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A, gene:SNX3, gene:VPS35L, gene:VPS18), predicting greater delivery of lipid-rich membrane cargo to the endolysosome.", "Step 2 (capacity, not flux): a coordinated CLEAR-like module raises acid hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (27 of 28 represented members up; gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:NAGLU +5.91, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:HEXB, gene:GM2A, gene:GLA, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB +2.38), expanding capacity to hydrolyse ingested membrane sphingolipid, glycolipid and protein; gene:CTSS (-5.57) falls, marking a shift of microglial state rather than a global increase.", "Step 3 (routing of released lipid): released fatty acid and sterol are directed into esterification, storage and membrane resynthesis rather than into the ER regulatory pool - gene:SOAT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:AGPAT2 (+6.29), gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2 up, with lipolytic/recycling genes gene:MGLL (+4.00) and gene:ABHD5 also up.", "Step 4 (sensor consequence): because the ER-sensed sterol pool is not raised, both SREBP arms stay active - gene:SREBF2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:ACAT2, gene:LSS, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24, gene:EBP, gene:LDLR, gene:INSIG1 and gene:SREBF1 (+4.67) with gene:SCD (+4.17), gene:FADS1, gene:ACSS2 - so synthesis runs concurrently with catabolism instead of being switched off.", "Step 5 (acyl-chain bias): new glycerolipid draws preferentially on de-novo monounsaturated acyl-CoA (gene:SCD up) while activation of exogenous/recycled long-chain fatty acid is reduced (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11) and the GPAT isoform used switches (gene:GPAT3 -2.23 versus gene:GPAT4 +1.58), predicting MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poorer stored and membrane glycerolipid.", "Step 6 (energetic accompaniment, association only): the acidification and biosynthetic demand of this state accompanies a uniform rise in nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts (38/38 represented up, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:UQCRC2, gene:COX7A2, gene:ATP5F1B) while mtDNA-encoded transcripts skew down (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ND4); the mito-nuclear discordance is not explained by the mechanism and may be independent."], "title": "APOE4 microglia adopt a high-throughput lysosomal membrane-lipid turnover state in which liberated lipid is routed into esterification and de-novo MUFA-biased resynthesis, keeping ER sterol sensing low"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36601373555366834, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16547008860830048, "cosine_similarity": -0.06789474882097575, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7628090614886731, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36601373555366834, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16547008860830048, "cosine_similarity": -0.06789474882097575, "direction_accuracy": 0.2297734627831715, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7628090614886731, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8115335, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 107}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_030", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a preselected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e= 1) from a single-cell pseudobulk comparison, so absence of a gene (e.g. G6PD, GSR, TXNRD1, CAT, SOD2, NFE2L2) means 'not in the supplied list', not 'unchanged'; the mechanism is built only on genes that are present.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative ranks within this list are used, not absolute fold changes.", "The strong global up-shift (77% of listed genes positive, median +1.46) is treated as a possible normalization/compositional or selection artefact, so all set-level statements are made as ranks/percentiles against this same list rather than as raw directions.", "Transcript and spot abundances are assumed to be monotonically related to enzyme amount, but enzyme amount is assumed NOT to equal activity, flux, cofactor occupancy or subcellular localization; every flux, NADPH-pool and ROS statement in the mechanism is inferred, not measured.", "Protein spots contain multiple candidate genes and visible keratin/actin contaminants, so no spot is treated as a unique protein identification; spots are used only as weak concordance or counter-evidence.", "RNA and protein measurements are assumed to describe the same APOE4-vs-APOE3 isogenic contrast, although replicate numbers and whether the two modalities come from the same cultures are not supplied.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture; the pseudobulk signal is assumed to be dominated by microglia, which is not verified in the supplied data.", "NADPH pools, GSH/GSSG, peroxiredoxin oxidation state, peroxide production, lipid peroxidation and cell viability were not measured in this dataset."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinately expanded mitochondrial oxidative and lipid-desaturation/esterification transcriptional program together with coordinately reduced transcripts for cytosolic NADPH- and NADP-supplying enzymes (PGD, TALDO1, NADK, NAMPT). We propose that the limiting node is cytosolic NADPH regeneration capacity, not antioxidant enzyme abundance: raised NAD(P)H demand from SCD/cytochrome-b5-reductase desaturation and from glutathione/peroxiredoxin recycling, set against a constrained oxidative pentose-phosphate and NAD(P) salvage supply, leaves APOE4 microglia with a more oxidized cytosolic thiol pool and makes them selectively vulnerable to oxidant or PUFA challenge, which they pre-emptively offset by lowering peroxidizable substrate (ACSL4, ALOX15 down) and raising GPX4 and lipid-ester storage. Causality is not established by these correlative abundance measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Direct state measurement: in isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under mock conditions, cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios should be lower and cytosolic roGFP2-Grx1 / PRDX2 dimer fraction more oxidized in APOE4, despite equal or higher PRDX2/GPX4 protein. If APOE4 shows equal or higher NADPH/NADP+ and an equally or more reduced cytosolic thiol probe, the bottleneck claim is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation: partial inhibition of oxidative PPP flux (6-aminonicotinamide or G6PD knockdown) or of NAD salvage (FK866) should shift the dose-response curve for H2O2- or PUFA(arachidonate)-induced lipid peroxidation (BODIPY-C11) and death markedly further in APOE4 than APOE3 (genotype x inhibitor interaction). If APOE3 and APOE4 are equally sensitized, or APOE4 is more resistant, the supply-limitation step fails.", "Bottleneck vs enzyme-abundance discrimination: overexpressing GPX4 or PRDX2 should NOT normalize the APOE4 oxidized-thiol/lipid-peroxidation phenotype, whereas restoring reductant supply (G6PD overexpression, cytosolic IDH1 overexpression, or NMN/NR to raise the NAD(P) pool) should. Rescue by peroxidase overexpression alone, without any change in NADPH/NADP+, would weaken the mechanism and favour a simple antioxidant-capacity-deficit model.", "Demand arm: SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) should lower NAD(P)H consumption and partially restore APOE4 cytosolic thiol redox state and NADPH/NADP+ toward APOE3 without altering OXPHOS transcript levels. No redox improvement (or worsening) after SCD inhibition would falsify the desaturation-demand step.", "Mitochondrial arm: NNT or UCP2 knockdown should selectively increase matrix H2O2 (mito-HyPer7) and reduce viability in APOE4 relative to APOE3, consistent with these being compensatory. Equal effects in both genotypes would argue against the inferred higher basal mitochondrial peroxide flux.", "Peroxisomal alternative (explicitly not the primary claim): if catalase activity, peroxisomal H2O2 (px-HyPer7) and VLCFA C26:0 levels are unchanged between genotypes despite the ABCD1/ACOX1/SCP2 transcript pattern, that supports leaving the peroxisomal arm out of the mechanism; if instead peroxisomal H2O2 is strongly elevated and drives the phenotype, this hypothesis should be replaced by a peroxisome-centred one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mechanism_steps": ["An SREBF1-associated lipid program is transcriptionally elevated in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:SCP2 +5.95); we infer, but did not measure, increased desaturation and neutral-lipid esterification flux.", "SCD-catalysed desaturation withdraws cytosolic reducing equivalents through the cytochrome b5 / cytochrome b5 reductase relay, whose transcripts are also elevated (gene:CYB5R3 +4.66, gene:CYB5R1 +1.41), so the inferred electron drain on the cytosolic NAD(P)H pool rises.", "In the same cells, transcripts for cytosolic NADPH regeneration and NADP(H) pool maintenance fall against a strongly up-shifted background (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32, gene:NADK -1.14, gene:NAMPT -2.62; 4/4 down where only 23% of listed genes are down, binomial p=0.0028), and no compensating increase is seen in the ambiguous G6PD/PGD-containing protein spots (protein_spot:018, protein_spot:019, protein_spot:021, protein_spot:022). We infer reduced maximal cytosolic NADPH regeneration rate; the NADPH pool itself was not measured.", "Mitochondrial oxidative machinery is coordinately raised (gene:OGDH +8.56, gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:MPC2 +7.98, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:GLUD1 +3.17, gene:NDUFA5 +7.30, gene:ATP5MC3 +4.70), predicting greater electron flux and therefore greater matrix superoxide/H2O2 production per cell; peroxide production was not measured.", "The cell responds on the peroxide-removal side by raising thiol-peroxidase, glutathione-synthesis and matrix-reductant transcripts (gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:GSS +2.11, gene:MSRA +2.64, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:NNT +2.88, gene:UCP2 +2.38; consistent with the increased CAT- and PRDX2-containing spots protein_spot:017 and protein_spot:077). All of these are NADPH- or NADH-consuming, so higher enzyme abundance raises demand for reduced cofactor without raising its supply.", "Because reductant supply, not peroxidase abundance, is capped, APOE4 microglia additionally reduce the peroxidizable substrate pool (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ALOX15 -3.63) and divert fatty acid into monounsaturated and esterified stores, a substrate-avoidance strategy that is efficient at rest (mock) but has little reserve.", "Net predicted phenotype: at baseline APOE4 microglia are viable but operate with a lower cytosolic NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratio and a more oxidized peroxiredoxin pool than APOE3, and lose viability/accumulate lipid peroxidation disproportionately when PPP or NAD salvage flux is blocked or when an exogenous peroxide/PUFA load is applied."], "title": "Cytosolic NADPH regeneration is the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia: SREBF1/SCD-driven lipid desaturation and storage compete with thiol-peroxidase recycling against a shrinking oxidative-PPP/NAD kinase supply"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09875198463981094, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07718560779769704, "cosine_similarity": -0.06821027623866086, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7400161812297734, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.09875198463981094, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07718560779769704, "cosine_similarity": -0.06821027623866086, "direction_accuracy": 0.127831715210356, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7400161812297734, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.06120075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 475}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_088", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results with an unspecified logarithm base and a strong positive shift (77.1% positive, median +1.46); we assume rank position within this list, not raw sign, indicates relative up-regulation, and that absence of a gene (ASAH1, PSAP, UGCG, SGMS1/2, SPTLC1-3, CERT1, GALC, ARSA, MCOLN1) reflects non-selection rather than a measured null.", "We assume transcript changes translate at least partly into hydrolase protein and catalytic activity in the acidic compartment; no enzyme activity, protein-level identification or pH measurement is supplied, and the protein spots are multi-candidate and cannot identify any hydrolase uniquely.", "No lipid measurement of any kind is supplied: ceramide, sphingomyelin, glucosylceramide, lactosylceramide, ganglioside, sphingosine and S1P pools are inferred, never observed.", "We assume the astrocyte co-culture and mock condition affect APOE4 and APOE3 wells equally, so that the difference is genotype-driven; cell-composition or maturation differences between genotypes are not excluded by the supplied data.", "We assume the sphingolipid arm is a functionally limiting part of, rather than merely a passive passenger within, the broader lysosomal transcript up-shift; a permutation test cannot separate the two (see analysis.md), so this is the weakest assumption and the target of the discriminating prediction."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia carry a coordinately elevated endolysosomal sphingolipid hydrolase transcript program (SMPD1, GBA, HEXA, HEXB, GBA2, GLA, SUMF1, NPC2, GLTP) that is not matched by the transcripts of the routes that consume salvaged ceramide/sphingosine (B4GALT5 reduced, ORMDL2 raised, CERK and SGPL1 at or below the strongly up-shifted background). We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step distinguishing APOE4 from APOE3 is consumption of salvaged ceramide - principally Golgi re-synthesis of complex glycosphingolipids from ceramide/glucosylceramide - so that accelerated luminal hydrolysis produces a ceramide- and sphingosine-loaded, complex-glycosphingolipid-depleted endolysosomal membrane whose impaired fusion/egress sustains a compensatory TFEB/CLEAR-associated lysosomal biogenesis signature. Only transcripts and ambiguous protein spots were measured; enzyme activity, lipid pools, localization and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: in APOE4 microglia, selective inhibition or knockdown of SMPD1 plus GBA (or acid-sphingomyelinase inhibition with a FIASMA) should lower endolysosomal ceramide and restore lysosomal cargo degradation/egress kinetics (DQ-BSA dequenching, myelin or ApoE-lipoprotein clearance) toward APOE3 WITHOUT reducing TFEB target transcripts; if instead the phenotype is unchanged by hydrolase inhibition while TFEB knockdown removes both the hydrolase transcripts and the phenotype, the sphingolipid arm is a passenger of a generic CLEAR program and this mechanism is rejected.", "Lipidomics of sorted APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show increased ceramide (C16/C18 species matching CERS6/CERS4) and increased sphingosine with reduced lactosylceramide and downstream gangliosides; finding unchanged ceramide, or increased rather than decreased complex glycosphingolipids, weakens the mechanism.", "Restoring the proposed bottleneck - B4GALT5 over-expression or exogenous lactosylceramide/glucosylceramide supply - should normalise the complex-glycosphingolipid pool and lysosomal egress in APOE4 without lowering hydrolase transcripts; absence of rescue would falsify the assignment of the bottleneck to ceramide re-anabolism even if the hydrolase arm is genuinely elevated.", "Enzyme-activity assays should show higher acid sphingomyelinase and glucocerebrosidase activity per cell in APOE4; if activity is unchanged or lower despite the transcript differences - as the decreased hydrolase-candidate protein spots hint - the transcript-to-activity step of the chain fails.", "Because sphingosine export (SPNS1) is co-raised, blocking SPNS1 in APOE4 should aggravate, not relieve, the lysosomal phenotype; relief after SPNS1 blockade would indicate sphingosine export, rather than ceramide re-anabolism, is the limiting node and would require the mechanism to be revised."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia show transcripts for luminal sphingolipid hydrolases well above the already positive background of the supplied differential-expression list - SMPD1 (+5.63, 95th percentile of listed effects), GBA (+6.71, 98th), HEXA (+5.68, 96th), with GBA2, HEXB, SUMF1 and the cytosolic glycolipid transfer protein GLTP above the list median; TFEB and several v-ATPase subunit transcripts are also raised.", "Step 2 (inferred activity/flux): the raised hydrolase transcripts are assumed to increase acid sphingomyelinase, glucocerebrosidase and beta-hexosaminidase protein and catalytic activity inside late endosomes/lysosomes, accelerating conversion of sphingomyelin and glucosyl-/ganglio-series glycosphingolipids to ceramide and then sphingosine.", "Step 3 (measured, RNA): the routes that would consume this salvaged material are not co-elevated - B4GALT5 (lactosylceramide synthase) is reduced (-1.88, 13th percentile), ORMDL2, a brake on serine palmitoyltransferase, is raised (+1.91), and CERK (+1.23, 38th) and SGPL1 (+1.09, 29th) sit at or below the background of the list, while SPNS1 (lysosomal sphingosine exporter, +2.58, 72nd) and the ceramide synthases CERS4/CERS6 are the only clearly co-raised salvage components.", "Step 4 (inferred flux imbalance - the proposed bottleneck): production of ceramide/sphingosine in the endolysosomal lumen therefore exceeds its re-incorporation into complex glycosphingolipids at the Golgi and its catabolic disposal, so ceramide and sphingosine are predicted to accumulate in endolysosomal membranes while lactosylceramide/ganglioside output falls (ST3GAL5 is raised but is downstream of the reduced B4GALT5 step).", "Step 5 (inferred biophysics/localization): ceramide-enriched, complex-glycosphingolipid-poor limiting membranes are predicted to be more ordered and fusion-permissive but recycling-impaired, slowing cargo egress and tubulation from lysosomes and reducing plasma-membrane glycosphingolipid available for receptor microdomains.", "Step 6 (inferred feedback): the resulting persistent lipid-clearance deficit maintains TFEB/CLEAR-associated hydrolase and v-ATPase transcription (TFEB +2.38; ATP6V1H +6.88, ATP6V1A +4.23, ATP6V0C +3.51), giving a feed-forward transcriptional signature that is a consequence, not proof, of increased degradative capacity."], "title": "APOE4 microglia over-run the lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis arm relative to ceramide re-anabolism, creating a ceramide-loaded, complex-glycosphingolipid-poor endolysosome"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1574142450984012, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.07860788895643815, "cosine_similarity": -0.0692996113298641, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_088", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6842880258899676, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1574142450984012, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.07860788895643815, "cosine_similarity": -0.0692996113298641, "direction_accuracy": 0.11812297734627832, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6842880258899676, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.7045935, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 476}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_037", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effects (logarithm base not specified in the workbook; preserved as reported) reflect real steady-state transcript differences between isogenic APOE4 and APOE3 microglia and not only ambient-RNA or depth artefacts; the source rows are a selected differential-expression list (all |effect| \u003e 1, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05), so absence of a gene does not mean it is unchanged.", "Transcript abundance for these enzymes is a usable proxy for enzyme capacity; enzyme protein level, activity, substrate channelling and subcellular localisation were not measured here.", "ACSL4/ACSL5 decreases are not fully compensated by unmeasured isoforms; ACSL1 and ACSL3 are absent from the supplied list and their status is unknown, which is the weakest link in the bottleneck claim.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and cannot identify any specific lipid enzyme; they are used only as weak, ambiguous context, not as identification of a protein pool.", "The strong global upward shift of the list (77% of rows positive, median effect +1.46) means module-level statements are only meaningful relative to that within-list background, which is how all enrichment tests here were computed.", "No lipid, flux, membrane-order or organelle measurement exists in this dataset; all metabolite-level statements are predictions, not observations."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia run a higher-throughput membrane/lipid turnover cycle than isogenic APOE3 cells: transcripts for lipid uptake, endolysosomal lipid hydrolysis and lysophospholipid/glycerolipid re-acylation are coordinately elevated, while the ACSL4/ACSL5 step that activates polyunsaturated fatty acids to acyl-CoA is one of the few strongly reduced nodes. We hypothesise that long-chain PUFA-CoA supply is the rate-limiting input to re-acylation, forcing APOE4 cells to rebuild phospholipids from SREBF1/SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA and producing a measurable shift in membrane phospholipid acyl composition (higher MUFA, lower arachidonoyl species) rather than a net change in total lipid mass. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted phospholipidomics of isogenic mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia will show an increased MUFA/PUFA ratio in PC and PE (higher 16:0_18:1 and 18:1_18:1 species, lower 18:0_20:4 and 18:0_22:6 species) at approximately unchanged total PC+PE mass. If total phospholipid mass changes dramatically with no compositional shift, or the arachidonoyl species are higher in APOE4, the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. CAY10566/A939572) at matched exposure will disproportionately harm APOE4 cells - larger fall in PL 18:1 species, larger rise in saturated PL, greater ER-stress/viability penalty - because APOE4 re-acylation depends on de novo MUFA. Equal or lesser APOE4 sensitivity than APOE3 would falsify the proposed bottleneck.", "Rescue test: exogenous arachidonate loading alone will only partially normalise APOE4 arachidonoyl-PL, whereas arachidonate plus ACSL4 re-expression will restore it toward APOE3 levels. If arachidonate alone fully normalises PUFA-PL, the acyl-CoA activation step is not limiting and step 4 fails.", "Turnover test: pulse labelling with deuterated choline or 13C-acetate will show a higher fractional labelling rate of PC (faster phospholipid turnover) in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal turnover rates would remove the 'membrane turnover' premise and favour a purely bioenergetic or lysosomal-storage explanation.", "Upstream test: inhibiting lysosomal acidification (bafilomycin A1) or GBA will collapse the APOE4-specific lysophospholipid and MUFA-PL signature toward APOE3 values; no genotype-selective effect would indicate that the elevated hydrolase transcripts do not drive the compositional difference.", "Orthogonal falsifier: if respirometry shows a large APOE4 bioenergetic difference while lipidomics shows no acyl-chain compositional shift, the nuclear-OXPHOS module (the statistically strongest signal in this list) should be preferred over this lipid mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for lipoprotein/lipid scavenging and handling (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:LDLR, gene:NPC2, gene:APOE), which we infer, but did not measure, raises delivery of exogenous lipid and membrane to the endolysosomal compartment.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A coherent endolysosomal degradative module is up (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:GAA, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:NAGLU, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), consistent with increased hydrolysis of internalised glycerophospholipids and sphingolipids, generating lysophospholipids, diacylglycerol, ceramide and free fatty acid. Hydrolase activity and lysosomal pH were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): Re-acylation and head-group machinery is coordinately up (gene:AGPAT2, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2, gene:TAZ, gene:DGAT1), indicating raised capacity to re-esterify the liberated lyso-species back into phospholipid and neutral lipid.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred flux limitation): The acyl-CoA activation step feeding this re-acylation is selectively reduced - gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 sit in the lowest ~5-11 percent of an otherwise strongly upward-shifted list, together with gene:GPAT3 and gene:PNPLA1. Because ACSL4 preferentially activates arachidonate/PUFA, we propose PUFA-CoA supply becomes limiting relative to the elevated acyltransferase capacity.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred metabolite outcome): Compensatory de novo monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply is engaged (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:FADS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:HMGCS1, gene:SREBF2), so re-acylation is predicted to proceed with 16:1/18:1 chains.", "Step 6 (predicted, unmeasured): Net result is an APOE4 membrane phospholipid pool enriched in monounsaturated and depleted in arachidonoyl/PUFA species at roughly preserved total phospholipid mass, with a smaller PLA2-accessible arachidonate reservoir (gene:PLA2G7 up, gene:GPX4 up), altering membrane order, phagocytic membrane turnover and eicosanoid precursor availability. No lipid species was measured in this dataset."], "title": "Acyl-CoA-limited Lands-cycle re-acylation biases APOE4 microglial membrane turnover toward SCD-derived monounsaturated phospholipids"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30581914854336667, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.06992039363817266, "cosine_similarity": -0.07162054789226548, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7648187702265372, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30581914854336667, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.06992039363817266, "cosine_similarity": -0.07162054789226548, "direction_accuracy": 0.28317152103559873, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7648187702265372, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.9747985, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 477}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_057", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77 percent positive in the unspecified logarithm base), so only within-list rank comparisons are interpretable; we assume the rank contrast between the up-shifted MUFA/glycerolipid set and the down-shifted PUFA set is not produced by that shift.", "Transcript abundance changes are assumed to translate at least partly into enzyme protein and catalytic activity for SCD, AGPAT2, DGAT1, LPCAT1 and the lysosomal hydrolases; no protein or activity measurement for any of these enzymes is supplied.", "No lipid species, lipid droplet, desaturation index, membrane order, flux or localization measurement is supplied; every statement about fatty-acid release, esterification, droplet storage and membrane composition is an inference.", "Protein spots contain several candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; the annexin/ANXA1-containing spots are used only as weak, non-identifying consistency, not as evidence for a named protein.", "Absence of a gene from the list (for example FASN, ACACA, ELOVL5/6, DGAT2, LPCAT2/3, MBOAT7, PLA2G4A/PLA2G6/PLA2G15, ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, LIPA, NPC1, ABCA1, ABCG1, PLIN2/3) is assumed to mean not selected, not measured as unchanged.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are assumed isogenic as stated, cultured with astrocytes; astrocyte-derived ambient RNA and any depth or composition difference between genotypes are assumed not to be the sole driver of the direction-opposed gene sets.", "Very large effect magnitudes (up to +15.5) are assumed to arise partly from low-count pseudobulk estimation and are used for rank, not magnitude, inference."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia by running a higher-throughput membrane-lipid turnover cycle: transcripts for lysosomal luminal lipid hydrolases and v-ATPase subunits are coordinately elevated, and the acyl-CoA generated by this catabolism is inferred to be re-esterified through an SREBF1/SCD-supported, monounsaturate-biased glycerolipid and Lands-cycle route (SCD, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, CHPT1 up) while the polyunsaturate-channeling arm is coordinately reduced (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3, ALOX15, PLAA, PNPLA1 down). We propose Delta-9 desaturation capacity (SCD) is the rate-limiting node of this cycle, so APOE4 microglia are selectively dependent on it to esterify recycled fatty acid into neutral lipid and MUFA-containing phospholipid; the opposite direction of the PUFA arm makes this contrast robust to the strong global positive shift in the supplied differential-expression rows. All lipid pools, fluxes, droplets and enzyme activities are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (for example A939572 or CAY10566, dose-matched, mock conditions) should show a genotype-by-drug interaction, with APOE4 microglia losing more neutral-lipid stain, raising the saturated-to-monounsaturated ratio of phosphatidylcholine and triacylglycerol more, and inducing ATF4/DDIT3 and viability loss more than isogenic APOE3. If SCD inhibition produces statistically indistinguishable effects in APOE4 and APOE3 (no interaction), the claim that Delta-9 desaturation is the APOE4-specific bottleneck is falsified.", "Source-of-carbon discriminator: parallel U-13C-acetate (de novo route via ACSS2/SREBF1) and 13C- or D-labelled membrane-cargo (labelled myelin or labelled apoptotic-cell membrane) tracing, with and without lysosomal blockade (bafilomycin A1 or leupeptin plus pepstatin A). The mechanism predicts that the APOE4-specific excess of monounsaturated triacylglycerol is largely cargo-derived and is abolished by lysosomal blockade. If the APOE4 excess is instead almost entirely acetate-derived and unaffected by lysosomal blockade, Step 1 to Step 3 coupling is wrong and the mechanism should be replaced by a purely de novo lipogenic one.", "Lipidomic signature: untargeted lipidomics of the same mock cultures should show, in APOE4 relative to APOE3, higher monounsaturated glycerolipid species (for example TAG 52:2, PC 32:1, PC 34:1) and lower arachidonate-containing species (for example PC 38:4, PI 38:4) with a lower free-arachidonate and 12/15-lipoxygenase product level. Unchanged or higher PUFA-phospholipid in APOE4 would falsify the acyl-chain remodeling direction.", "Node ordering: ACSL4 re-expression in APOE4 microglia should restore PUFA-phospholipid content and reduce the MUFA bias without reversing the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program; conversely, GBA plus SMPD1 inhibition (conduritol-B-epoxide plus a neutral/acid sphingomyelinase inhibitor) should reduce the recycled fatty-acid supply and shrink the APOE4-specific neutral-lipid excess. If the lysosomal hydrolase program is itself abolished by ACSL4 re-expression, the proposed direction (catabolism upstream of remodeling) is wrong.", "Activity versus abundance: SCD protein and a cellular desaturation index (16:1/16:0 and 18:1/18:0) must be higher in APOE4; if SCD transcript elevation is not accompanied by any increase in desaturation index, the abundance-to-activity assumption fails and the bottleneck claim is weakened.", "Specificity control: the same lysosomal hydrolase and MUFA-remodeling contrast should be reproducible in a second isogenic APOE4/APOE3 pair and in monoculture microglia; if it disappears without astrocytes, an astrocyte-driven or ambient-RNA explanation supersedes the cell-intrinsic mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia elevate transcripts encoding lysosomal luminal hydrolases and the v-ATPase (GAA, CTSK, GBA, NAGLU, HEXA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, GBA2, HEXB, GLA, AGA, SGSH; ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C; TFEB), together with uptake/scavenger and endolysosomal trafficking transcripts (SCARB1, ITGB1, LGALS3, CD36, TREM2, RAB7A, LAMP1). We infer, but did not measure, increased degradative flux of glycerophospholipid- and sphingolipid-rich membrane cargo, releasing fatty acids, sphingoid bases and sterol.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): A lipogenic/desaturase program is co-elevated (SREBF1, INSIG1, LDLR, ACSS2, SCD, FADS1, and sterol arm DHCR24, LSS, ACAT2, HMGCS1). We infer increased capacity for acetyl-CoA-to-acyl-CoA conversion and, critically, for Delta-9 desaturation that supplies 16:1/18:1 monounsaturated acyl-CoA.", "Step 3 (bottleneck; inferred): SCD-generated MUFA-CoA is the limiting substrate for safe esterification of the fatty acid liberated in Step 1. Elevated glycerolipid-assembly transcripts (AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, MGLL, CHPT1) are inferred to direct this acyl-CoA into phosphatidic acid/diacylglycerol and onward into triacylglycerol storage and phosphatidylcholine, rather than into oxidation or efflux (APOE, ABCA7 rise only modestly, below the list-wide median rank).", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred membrane composition): Lands-cycle re-acylation transcripts rise (LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2) while polyunsaturate-selective activation and disposal transcripts fall (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3, ALOX15, PLAA, PNPLA1). We infer a shift of phospholipid sn-2 composition toward monounsaturated/saturated species and away from arachidonate-containing species, with reduced substrate flow to lipoxygenase products.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): The resulting membranes and lysosomal cargo are more saturated/monounsaturated and less PUFA-rich, which we infer stiffens and slows further hydrolysis of the recycled membrane, sustaining the elevated hydrolase program as a compensatory loop rather than resolving the load.", "Step 6 (inferred vulnerability): Because throughput depends on Delta-9 desaturation, constraining SCD should convert the recycled fatty acid load into saturated acyl-CoA and lipotoxic stress selectively in APOE4; the elevated DDIT3 and ATF6 transcripts are consistent with a pre-existing stress tone but do not demonstrate lipotoxicity."], "title": "SCD-dependent monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply is the bottleneck coupling an expanded lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolic program to MUFA-biased glycerolipid re-esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36234907506553926, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10836869504940579, "cosine_similarity": -0.07306873595693254, "direction_accuracy": 0.26537216828478966, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7835339805825242, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.36234907506553926, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.10836869504940579, "cosine_similarity": -0.07306873595693254, "direction_accuracy": 0.26537216828478966, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7835339805825242, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.29083425, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 478}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_127", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; enrichment was therefore judged against the supplied rows themselves, which are already shifted positive (median about +1.46, 77 percent positive).", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified, so magnitudes are treated as ranks and directions only, never as fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and catalytic activity for SCD, ACSL4, AGPAT2 and the LPCAT/MBOAT reacylases; no enzyme activity, acyl-CoA pool, flux or lipid measurement is present in these files.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; no spot was used to assert the abundance of any specific lipid enzyme.", "Astrocyte co-culture and APOE-dependent lipid exchange may supply exogenous fatty acids, so the intracellular acyl profile is not assumed to be cell-autonomous.", "Directionality (APOE4 genotype causing the lipid program versus a shared upstream cell-state difference) is assumed, not established."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from isogenic APOE3 microglia primarily in the composition of the cytosolic long-chain acyl-CoA pool feeding glycerolipid synthesis: transcripts for SREBF1 and the delta-9 desaturase SCD, for citrate/acetate-derived acetyl-CoA supply (SLC25A1, ACSS2), and for the glycerolipid acyltransferases AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1 and the Lands-cycle reacylases LPCAT1, MBOAT1 and MBOAT2 are higher, while the polyunsaturated-fatty-acid-preferring activating enzymes ACSL4 and ACSL5 and the PUFA-oxygenase ALOX15 are lower. We propose that monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply, rather than total lipid synthetic capacity, is the rate-limiting determinant, so that APOE4 membranes and neutral lipids are re-esterified with a monounsaturated- and saturated-skewed, arachidonate-poor acyl-chain profile while lysosomal lipid hydrolysis (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB, CTSD, ATP6V1A) keeps turnover high. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a higher desaturation index (18:1/18:0 and 16:1/16:0) and a higher fraction of monounsaturated glycerophospholipid species (for example PC 32:1, PC 34:1, PE 34:1, PE 36:1) and of triacylglycerols with low double-bond counts, together with reduced arachidonoyl-containing species (PI 38:4, PC 38:4, PE 38:4). If total and 20:4-containing phospholipid pools are unchanged or increased in APOE4, the acyl-remodeling bottleneck is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (for example A939572 or CAY10566) in APOE4 microglia should collapse the APOE4-versus-APOE3 difference in the desaturation index and in MUFA-PC/TAG species toward the APOE3 profile, without abolishing the transcriptional elevation of AGPAT2, LPCAT1 and DGAT1. If SCD inhibition lowers total lipogenesis but leaves the APOE4-specific acyl-chain composition difference intact, the proposed bottleneck is wrong and a general capacity model is favoured.", "Restoring ACSL4 in APOE4 microglia should selectively re-load 20:4 into phospholipids and increase BODIPY-C11 oxidation after GPX4 inhibition; unchanged 20:4-phospholipid content after ACSL4 restoration would falsify the PUFA-activation arm of the mechanism.", "Blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or conduritol-B-epoxide for GBA) should shift sphingolipid and hexosylceramide species but should not normalize the glycerophospholipid MUFA ratio; if it does normalize the glycerophospholipid acyl profile, the primary bottleneck is lysosomal catabolism rather than acyl-donor composition.", "Stable-isotope tracing with 13C-acetate or D9-choline should show higher label incorporation into APOE4 monounsaturated PC and TAG species and a shorter phospholipid acyl half-life; equal incorporation rates and equal turnover would weaken the high-flux remodeling claim even if steady-state pools differ.", "Immunoblot or targeted proteomics should show increased SCD and AGPAT2 protein and decreased ACSL4 protein in APOE4; a purely transcriptional change with unchanged protein for SCD and ACSL4 would weaken the mechanism, since no supplied protein spot uniquely identifies these enzymes."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_127", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: SREBF1, SLC25A1 and ACSS2 RNA are higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, unspecified log base). Inferred, not measured: greater cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability and a more active SREBP-1 lipogenic transcriptional output.", "Measured: SCD and FADS1 RNA are higher (gene:SCD +4.17, 89th percentile of the supplied rows). Inferred: increased delta-9 desaturase activity and expansion of the 16:1- and 18:1-CoA pool relative to saturated and polyunsaturated acyl-CoAs. Acyl-CoA pools themselves were not measured.", "Measured: ACSL4 and ACSL5 RNA are lower (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ACSL5 -3.11, 11th and 5th percentiles) and ALOX15 is lower (gene:ALOX15 -3.63). Inferred: reduced activation of arachidonate and other PUFAs to acyl-CoA, so PUFA donors for esterification and for oxygenation are scarce. This step, together with step 2, is the proposed primary bottleneck: acyl-donor species composition, not acyltransferase capacity.", "Measured: acyltransferase transcripts along both the de novo Kennedy pathway and the Lands remodeling cycle are elevated (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26). Inferred: increased flux from lysophosphatidic acid to phosphatidic acid, diacylglycerol, triacylglycerol and phosphatidylcholine, and increased reacylation of lysophospholipids, which stamps the MUFA-skewed donor pool onto phospholipid sn-2 positions and neutral lipid.", "Measured: lysosomal and neutral lipid hydrolase transcripts are high (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:TFEB +2.38, gene:MGLL +4.00), while lipid uptake receptor transcripts are high (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:ABCA7 +2.14). Inferred: faster deacylation and lysosomal breakdown of membrane lipids that regenerates lysophospholipid and monoacylglycerol acceptors, so the system behaves as a high-turnover remodeling cycle rather than pure net storage. Membrane turnover rate was not measured.", "Predicted lipid-level consequence (not measured here): a higher desaturation index and a shift of phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine and triacylglycerol toward monounsaturated species with depletion of arachidonoyl-containing phospholipids; the concurrent elevation of gene:GPX4 is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, a peroxidation-resistant PUFA-poor membrane state."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a MUFA-biased acyl-CoA bottleneck that reprograms glycerolipid synthesis and membrane acyl-chain remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3168592844219621, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.028199556822789056, "cosine_similarity": -0.07321205176702422, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_127", "mean_absolute_error": 0.788588996763754, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3168592844219621, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.028199556822789056, "cosine_similarity": -0.07321205176702422, "direction_accuracy": 0.2766990291262136, "mean_absolute_error": 0.788588996763754, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.89716225, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 479}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_017", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, |effect| \u003e 1) in an unspecified logarithm base; 77.1% are positive, so coordinated positive direction alone is weak evidence and only sign-discordant members within a pathway and very large effects were treated as informative.", "Missing genes (e.g. FASN, ACACA, ACLY, LIPA, PLIN2, ABCA1, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, ASAH1, UGCG, core ATG genes) are unknown, not unchanged; the lipogenic and autophagy arms are therefore only partially observed.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and, less securely, activity; no acyl-CoA pool, lipase activity, lysosomal pH, autophagic flux, lipid-droplet or lipidomic measurement is supplied, so routing and flux are inferred, not observed.", "Protein spots are 2D-gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each; no spot is treated as identifying a single protein. Spots consistent with cathepsins/HEXB are bidirectional (protein_spot:052 +2.14, protein_spot:053 +1.54 vs protein_spot:067 -1.00, protein_spot:069 -1.38) and the two spots listing ATP6V1E1 are negative (protein_spot:064, protein_spot:065), so the protein layer does not confirm the lysosomal transcript program.", "The strongest up spots (protein_spot:043-047, up to +3.05 log2) list ANXA1 and TALDO1 among five candidates each; they are treated as compatible with membrane-remodelling/NADPH-redox demand, not as identification of either protein.", "SCD-derived monounsaturated chains, and not an unmeasured exogenous MUFA supply from co-cultured astrocytes, are assumed to dominate the predicted acyl shift.", "Effects reported as APOE4 minus APOE3 in isogenic lines under mock treatment; no replicate count is supplied, so effect-size precision is unknown."], "claim": "In mock-treated iPSC-derived APOE4 microglia (day 30, astrocyte co-culture), the transcript data describe a coordinated cell-state change rather than a single bottleneck: lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase and sphingolipid-catabolic transcripts (gene:TFEB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:ATP6V1H) rise together with an SREBP-1/MUFA arm (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:ACSS2, gene:DHCR24) and with glycerolipid acyltransferase/remodeling transcripts (gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:DGAT1, gene:CHPT1), while the long-chain/PUFA-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 and gene:GPAT3 fall. We hypothesise that APOE4 shifts lipid routing: membrane and lipoprotein-derived lipid is turned over in an expanded endolysosomal compartment, and the liberated plus newly desaturated acyl chains are preferentially re-esterified into monounsaturated glycerophospholipids, triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester (gene:SOAT1) instead of being re-activated as PUFA-CoA for polyunsaturated phospholipid re-acylation. The predicted mock-state lipidome is MUFA/TAG/CE-shifted and sphingolipid- and PUFA-phospholipid-depleted. Flux, enzyme activity and lipid pools were not measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of the same mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher MUFA(16:1/18:1)-to-PUFA(20:4/22:6) ratio in PC and PE, increased TAG and cholesteryl ester, and decreased sphingomyelin and hexosylceramide. If PUFA-phospholipids are unchanged or higher and no MUFA shift or neutral-lipid increase is detected, the routing mechanism is falsified.", "Discriminating perturbation (prospective): SCD inhibition (e.g. CAY10566) in mock APOE4 microglia should collapse the MUFA/PUFA phospholipid ratio and reduce TAG toward APOE3 values while leaving lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GBA, HEXA, CTSB) largely elevated. If SCD inhibition normalises the lysosomal program but not the lipidome, the causal order is reversed and the mechanism is weakened; if it changes neither, the SREBP-1/SCD arm is not the routing driver.", "Restoring ACSL4 (or supplying arachidonate) in APOE4 microglia should selectively restore PUFA re-acylation into PE/PI without normalising lysosomal transcripts; failure to restore PUFA-phospholipids would refute the ACSL4-dependent re-acylation step.", "Acute GBA inhibition (conduritol B epoxide) or bafilomycin A1 should cause a larger relative accumulation of glucosylceramide/sphingomyelin in APOE4 than APOE3 if the sphingolipid catabolic transcripts reflect higher ongoing hydrolytic flux; equal accumulation would show the increased transcripts are not accompanied by increased flux.", "Challenge-only prediction (not a claim about the mock state): myelin-debris or palmitate loading should saturate droplet/oxidative handling and lower eicosanoid output earlier in APOE4; if APOE4 instead clears the load faster with equal PUFA mediator output, the state is successful adaptation rather than biased routing."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 increases the flux of lipid and membrane material entering the endolysosomal system in mock conditions; consistent transcript increases in uptake/recognition receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:MERTK, gene:GAS6, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE) are compatible with, but do not measure, higher uptake.", "A coordinated lysosomal-biogenesis program is transcriptionally elevated (gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:CTSK, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSH, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:VPS26A and six v-ATPase subunits including gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C), giving 24/25 represented members positive against a 77% positive selected-list background.", "Within this compartment the sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid catabolic arm is the most extreme (gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA2, gene:HEXB, gene:NPC2), predicting net hydrolysis of sphingomyelin and hexosylceramides and release of fatty acids and sphingoid bases; hydrolase activity itself is not measured.", "In parallel the ER lipogenic sensing arm is induced (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:ACSS2, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:DHCR7, gene:LSS, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LDLR), i.e. cells behave as if the ER regulatory sterol/unsaturated-lipid pool is not sated even while catabolism and cholesterol esterification (gene:SOAT1) rise, implying retention of lipid in lysosomal/neutral-lipid pools rather than a fed ER pool (inferred).", "Acyl-chain routing is remodelled asymmetrically: de novo/Kennedy and Lands-cycle acyltransferases increase (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2, gene:TAZ) while the PUFA-preferring activators gene:ACSL4 (-2.14) and gene:ACSL5 (-3.11) and gene:GPAT3 (-2.23) decrease, favouring incorporation of SCD-derived 16:1/18:1 chains over arachidonate/DHA re-acylation.", "Released saturated/monounsaturated fatty acid is partly oxidised and supports a high-capacity mitochondrial transcript program (gene:HADHA, gene:ETFA, gene:ACOX1 with 40/40 represented OXPHOS members positive, e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:ATP5ME +5.20), so the state is throughput-shifted rather than demonstrably blocked.", "Net predicted phenotype in the measured mock condition: MUFA-enriched PC/PE, increased TAG/DAG and cholesteryl ester, reduced sphingomyelin/hexosylceramide and reduced arachidonate/DHA-containing phospholipids, with reduced PUFA reserve that would become functionally visible mainly under a future inflammatory or lipid-load challenge."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an expanded lysosomal lipid-catabolic state coupled to SREBP-1/SCD-supplied MUFA re-esterification, biasing acyl-chain routing into storage and MUFA-phospholipids"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29746519957168704, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16553130172746552, "cosine_similarity": -0.07578061654258063, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8363689320388349, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.29746519957168704, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16553130172746552, "cosine_similarity": -0.07578061654258063, "direction_accuracy": 0.2524271844660194, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8363689320388349, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.30665075, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 108}, {"id": "opus-original-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript log fold changes track enzyme protein level and catalytic activity; no enzyme activity, flux or lipid-species measurement is supplied, so all acyl-chain composition statements are inferred, not observed.", "The logarithm base of the RNA rows is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only ranks and directions within the supplied rows are interpreted, not absolute fold magnitudes.", "The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, 77% positive, median +1.46), so a positive effect is only informative relative to this shifted background; percentile ranks rather than raw signs are used.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified proteins; they are cited only as ambiguous, mixed-direction context, never as measurement of a named protein pool.", "ACSL4/ACSL5 substrate preference for polyunsaturated fatty acids and SCD product identity (oleate) are background biochemical knowledge, unverified within this dataset (literature retrieval disabled).", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so genotype-driven lipid supply from astrocytes may contribute to the microglial transcript state; the comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment only.", "The lysosomal arm is assumed downstream/compensatory; the data cannot order it relative to the lipid arm."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally reconfigure the acyl-CoA selection step of glycerolipid acylation: transcripts for polyunsaturated-fatty-acid-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases (ACSL4, ACSL5) are among the most strongly reduced rows measured, while the monounsaturated-fatty-acid-generating desaturase SCD, the lipogenic factor SREBF1, and the glycerolipid/Lands-cycle acyltransferases AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1 and the choline-phosphotransferase CHPT1 are increased. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step in APOE4 is the supply of arachidonoyl-/PUFA-CoA for sn-2 reacylation rather than total acylation capacity, so that abundant oleoyl-CoA is preferentially fixed into phospholipids and triacylglycerol, yielding more saturated/monounsaturated, PUFA-poor membranes and increased neutral-lipid storage; the coordinate induction of lysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, GBA, HEXB, SMPD1, ATP6V subunits, TFEB) is interpreted as a downstream compensatory response to altered membrane lipid handling, not as an independent primary lesion. Lipid species, enzyme activities and fluxes were not measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: restoring ACSL4 (re-expression, or supplying arachidonate/lysoPC-arachidonoyl to bypass the activation step) in APOE4 microglia should renormalise phospholipid PUFA content (PC/PE 38:4, 40:6) and reduce lipid-droplet triacylglycerol WITHOUT lowering SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 transcripts. If ACSL4 restoration leaves membrane PUFA fraction and droplet load unchanged while SCD inhibition alone normalises them, the bottleneck is MUFA overproduction rather than PUFA-CoA supply and this hypothesis is falsified as stated.", "Untargeted lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in PC and PE (increase in 34:1/36:1, decrease in 38:4/40:6) plus increased TAG and cholesteryl ester. Absence of any MUFA:PUFA shift, or a shift in the opposite direction, weakens the mechanism.", "AGPAT2 or DGAT1 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should reduce neutral-lipid droplets and partially normalise the TFEB-associated lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (CTSB, GBA, SMPD1); no change in those transcripts would argue the lysosomal arm is primary and independent, contrary to step 6.", "Targeted immunoblot/immunoassay should show lower ACSL4 protein and higher SCD and AGPAT2 protein in APOE4; unchanged ACSL4 protein despite the transcript decrease would break the first assumption and weaken the bottleneck claim.", "Because ACSL4-dependent arachidonoyl-CoA supply is proposed to be limiting, APOE4 microglia should release less arachidonate-derived eicosanoid upon acute stimulation than APOE3 despite comparable stimulus-response transcript induction; equal or greater eicosanoid release would weaken the mechanism.", "Membrane-order reporters (e.g. Laurdan generalised polarisation) should show higher lipid order in APOE4 plasma/endolysosomal membranes, reversible by arachidonate supplementation; unchanged order would weaken step 4."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: an SREBP1-type lipogenic transcript program is higher in APOE4 (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:SCP2 +5.95, all above the 89th percentile of the supplied rows). Inferred: increased de novo monounsaturated fatty-acid (oleoyl-CoA) generation and increased lipid uptake capacity.", "Measured: transcripts for the PUFA/arachidonate-preferring long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases are reduced (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, 10.6th percentile; gene:ACSL5 -3.11, 5.3rd percentile) in a dataset where only 23% of rows are negative. Inferred: reduced arachidonoyl-CoA/PUFA-CoA availability for esterification, creating the proposed bottleneck at sn-2 acyl-donor selection.", "Measured: glycerolipid backbone and Lands-cycle reacylation transcripts are increased (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, 97th percentile; gene:LPCAT1 +3.07; gene:MBOAT2 +3.26; gene:MBOAT1 +2.65; gene:GPAT4 +1.58; gene:CHPT1 +2.91; gene:PCYT2 +1.05). Inferred: acylation and phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine synthesis capacity is not limiting, so the enlarged MUFA-CoA pool is preferentially incorporated at sn-1/sn-2 positions.", "Inferred (not measured): the imbalance between step 2 and step 3 shifts membrane phospholipid composition toward 34:1/36:1-type monounsaturated species and away from arachidonoyl/docosahexaenoyl species, increasing acyl-chain order and lowering membrane deformability; no lipidomic measurement is supplied to confirm this.", "Measured: neutral-lipid handling transcripts are increased (gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:ABHD5 +1.04) while gene:GPAT3 (-2.23) and gene:PNPLA1 (-1.55) are decreased. Inferred: excess MUFA-diacylglycerol is diverted into triacylglycerol/cholesteryl-ester storage with active monoacylglycerol recycling, buffering free fatty-acid load.", "Measured: lysosomal hydrolase, sphingolipid-hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts plus gene:TFEB are increased (gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSK +7.36, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:HEXB +2.17, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:ATP6V1A +4.23, gene:TFEB +2.38), with gene:CTSS strongly decreased (-5.57). Inferred: a compensatory degradative/membrane-turnover response to PUFA-poor, storage-biased membranes; the opposite direction of CTSS and of several cathepsin-containing protein spots shows this arm is not uniform.", "Inferred consequence (untested here): altered phagosomal and lysosomal membrane composition constrains lipid clearance and eicosanoid-precursor release in APOE4 microglia even without an inflammatory stimulus (gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:APOE +1.24 are only modestly changed relative to the dataset median)."], "title": "ACSL4-limited PUFA-acyl-CoA supply with expanded MUFA/glycerolipid acylation capacity drives MUFA-biased membrane remodeling and neutral-lipid diversion in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28572351659712736, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07057845570086234, "cosine_similarity": -0.07613137515773798, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.806378640776699, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.28572351659712736, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.07057845570086234, "cosine_similarity": -0.07613137515773798, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.806378640776699, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.905647, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 480}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_002", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All pathway assignments and molecular relationships involving cholesterol trafficking, SCAP/SREBP2, feedback inhibition and lysosomal compensation are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "The selected RNA differential-expression rows describe a response within comparable microglial states. Cell-state proportions, proliferation, RNA normalization, culture effects and astrocyte-derived signals could instead produce the pattern. Isogenic status is supplied context, not a genomic measurement.", "Slower cholesterol delivery is upstream of the transcriptional response. Increased biosynthetic demand, generalized lysosomal adaptation or altered extracellular cholesterol supply remain competing explanations.", "Increased INSIG1, CH25H and CYP27A1 RNA does not necessarily produce enough functional feedback inhibition to suppress the proposed response; increased NPC2 RNA is assumed to be compensatory. Effective inhibition or increased transport would oppose the mechanism.", "RNA effects retain their reported, unspecified logarithm base. Missing RNA rows, including NPC1, SCAP, HMGCR, SQLE, ABCA1 and ABCG1, are unknown rather than unchanged. The selected RNA results cannot establish a whole-transcriptome shift.", "No supplied protein spot uniquely identifies a protein, and none contains a candidate from the queried sterol panel. The hypothesis does not infer a particular V-ATPase defect from ambiguous spots. Cholesterol pools, synthesis and export fluxes, organelle localization, pH and regulatory activity are unmeasured."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, APOE4 is hypothesized to reduce delivery of endocytosed cholesterol from late endosomes/lysosomes to the endoplasmic reticulum relative to APOE3 at matched uptake and cell state. This single primary bottleneck would sustain an ER sterol-sensing response and increased sterol-synthesis transcripts while favoring lysosomal cholesterol retention. The abundance data motivate this mechanism but do not establish transport impairment, cholesterol accumulation, or causality.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In matched APOE3 and APOE4 microglial states sharing a controlled astrocyte background and defined extracellular acceptors, pulse-chase endocytosed labeled cholesterol and normalize to the amount internalized at chase start. APOE4 should show slower ER arrival and longer lysosomal residence, together with greater nuclear processed SREBP2. Measure organelle-resolved tracer distribution and ER-accessible cholesterol independently of esterification. Normal or faster ER delivery with no increased lysosomal residence would weaken the primary bottleneck; no increased SREBP2 processing would weaken the sensing link.", "Discriminating perturbation: compare lysosome-routed cholesterol delivery with a validated route that supplies cholesterol to the ER while bypassing lysosomes, using matched delivered amounts, timing, carrier controls and viability. After verifying ER delivery, bypass should preferentially correct the APOE4 sensing response: nuclear processed SREBP2 should fall before HMGCS1, DHCR7 and DHCR24 RNA, whereas lysosome-routed delivery should correct it more slowly or incompletely. Equal route responses together with normal endocytic ER-delivery kinetics would favor increased demand; failure of verified ER replenishment to suppress sensing would weaken the proposed chain.", "Causal-order perturbation: partially suppress SREBF2 in both genotypes and repeat the uptake-normalized tracer experiment at an early time before major cholesterol-pool remodeling. Synthetic-enzyme transcripts should decrease, but the APOE4 delay in lysosome-to-ER delivery should persist. Rapid normalization of delivery solely after SREBF2 suppression would favor synthesis-driven overload over a primary transport bottleneck and weaken this mechanism."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mechanism_steps": ["Primary bottleneck, inferred: APOE4-associated cellular changes slow cholesterol delivery from late endosomes/lysosomes to the ER. The supplied measurements do not identify the responsible transport component or demonstrate reduced delivery.", "Inferred sensing consequence: reduced delivery lowers ER-accessible cholesterol sufficiently to permit SCAP-dependent processing and nuclear activity of SREBP2. Increased SREBF2 and INSIG1 RNA (gene:SREBF2, gene:INSIG1) is compatible with a feedback response; neither SREBP2 processing nor ER cholesterol was measured.", "Proposed transcriptional consequence: increased SREBP2 activity promotes sterol synthesis and uptake capacity. The measured RNA increases in gene:ACAT2, gene:HMGCS1, gene:LSS, gene:EBP, gene:DHCR7, gene:DHCR24 and gene:LDLR support this response, but do not demonstrate enzyme abundance, synthesis flux or lipoprotein uptake.", "Inferred compartmental consequence: continued endocytic cholesterol input, potentially reinforced by the increased LDLR transcript, exceeds the reduced delivery capacity and prolongs lysosomal cholesterol residence. Lysosomal retention and the distribution of cholesterol between organelles are predictions, not observed molecular pools.", "Proposed compensatory consequence: prolonged lysosomal cargo residence induces a lysosomal handling program, consistent with increased gene:NPC2, gene:TFEB and gene:LAMP1 RNA. Increased handling transcripts need not restore transport, allowing the inferred ER sensing response to persist; TFEB localization and lysosomal function remain unmeasured."], "title": "Delayed lysosome-to-ER cholesterol delivery sustains a sterol-sensing response in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.13189011030908038, "cosine_similarity": -0.08665288623770698, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_002", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6462847896440129, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0273972602739726, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.13189011030908038, "cosine_similarity": -0.08665288623770698, "direction_accuracy": 0.04692556634304207, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6462847896440129, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.588513, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 12}, {"id": "opus-evidence-v2-b02-hyp_010", "cohort": "opus-evidence-v2", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (2212 rows, all |effect|\u003e1, all adjusted p\u003c0.05, 77.1% positive) in an unspecified logarithm base; program coherence is judged against that 77% positive background, and canonical members absent from the list (e.g. CAT, SOD1/2, GSR, G6PD, HMOX1, NQO1, GCLM, TXNRD1, all PEX genes, 7 of 13 mtDNA-encoded genes) are unknown, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, but does not measure, ETC assembly, peroxidase flux, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, desaturase activity or membrane acyl composition; every activity/flux statement in the mechanism is inferred.", "The mtDNA-encoded decrease is assumed to be biological rather than an artifact of the probe-based 10X Flex assay, ambient-RNA content or differing mitochondrial-transcript fraction between genotypes; this assumption is load-bearing for steps 2-3.", "Protein spots are 2-D gel spots with 2-6 candidate identities each (median 5) and are used only for compatibility, never as confirmation of a single protein: protein_spot:077 (+1.07, significant; PRDX2/RAB1A/ACTB) is compatible with increased peroxiredoxin but cannot be assigned; protein_spot:017 (+0.77; CAT/CORO1C/ENTPD5) is compatible with, but does not demonstrate, higher catalase; protein_spot:074 (+0.38, ns) and protein_spot:075 (-0.14, ns) both contain SOD2 with opposite signs, so SOD2 is untested; protein_spot:021 (+0.26, ns; G6PD/GSR/PGD) gives no support for increased pentose-phosphate protein, consistent with gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1 being down. Spot-to-gene mapping is unreliable in general here (gene:ACTB is -4.98 while ACTB-containing spots run both directions).", "Isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 comparison in mock, day 30 microglia-astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte contribution to the sorted/measured pool and replicate structure are not supplied, so cell-composition differences cannot be excluded as a partial contributor.", "Causality is not established by these correlative abundance data; the mechanism is a testable proposal."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) run an expanded nuclear-encoded OXPHOS/assembly/import transcriptional module that is not matched by the mtDNA-encoded core subunit pool (gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 lower). We propose this stoichiometric mismatch increases electron-leak-prone respiratory-chain intermediates per unit ETC protein, and that the cell compensates by shifting reducing power toward matrix peroxide removal (gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:TXNDC17, gene:GPX4, gene:MGST2, gene:NNT, gene:ME1; cytosolic PPP transcripts gene:PGD and gene:TALDO1 lower) and by remodeling membrane acyl composition toward monounsaturated, less peroxidizable species (gene:SCD up, gene:ACSL4 down, gene:ALOX15 down, MUFA-preferring gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, cardiolipin remodeling gene:TAZ), with surplus lipid routed to esterified storage and lysosomal turnover (gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:TFEB and the lysosomal hydrolase/v-ATPase set). The predicted lipid endpoint is a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in glycerophospholipids and cardiolipin with no rise in oxidized-PUFA species in mock, i.e. a costly but currently successful adaptation rather than a demonstrated ongoing oxidative defect; the ETC flux, ROS production rate, NADPH/NADP+ ratio and assembled-complex stoichiometry were not measured and remain the decisive unknowns.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 mock microglia should show a higher MUFA:PUFA acyl ratio in PC/PE and in cardiolipin, larger MUFA-rich TAG/CE pools, and no increase in oxidized-PUFA phospholipids or 4-HNE adducts. Finding equal MUFA:PUFA ratios, or increased oxidized-PUFA species in APOE4 under mock, would weaken the mechanism.", "Prospective: blue-native PAGE / quantitative proteomics should show a lower mtDNA-encoded:nuclear-encoded subunit ratio (e.g. MT-CO2 or MT-ATP6 versus NDUFB8/UQCRC2/ATP5F1B) and an increased pool of unassembled complex intermediates in APOE4, with mtDNA copy number not proportionally increased. Equal subunit stoichiometry and normal assembly would falsify steps 1-3 and favor simple mitochondrial biogenesis.", "Prospective discriminating perturbation: SCD inhibition (or ACSL4 re-expression) should selectively sensitize APOE4, not APOE3, microglia to peroxidation and GPX4-inhibitor (RSL3)-induced death and should reveal PUFA-phospholipid peroxidation; if APOE4 and APOE3 are equally sensitized, the peroxidation-avoidance arm is wrong.", "Prospective: a mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (e.g. MitoQ or mitoTEMPO) applied to APOE4 microglia should reduce the PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/TXNDC17 and SCD/LPCAT1 transcript elevations and shift the lipidome back toward APOE3; no normalization would argue the redox arm is a bystander of a mitochondrial biogenesis or sterol/lysosomal program.", "Prospective: acute oxidant or PUFA (arachidonate) challenge should uncover reduced reserve in APOE4 (greater peroxide accumulation, larger NADPH drop, greater viability loss) even though mock-state markers are compensated; equal challenge responses would remove the reduced-reserve claim without necessarily refuting the mock-state description.", "If a rescue of mtDNA-encoded subunit expression (e.g. TFAM or mitochondrial-translation restoration) normalizes the nuclear ETC, peroxiredoxin and SCD/ACSL4 changes, the proposed causal ordering is supported; if it changes nothing, the mitonuclear mismatch is a correlate, not the driver."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured, RNA): APOE4 microglia show a coordinated increase of nuclear-encoded ETC subunits, assembly factors and mitochondrial import/translation machinery (47 of 48 represented members positive, median reported logFC +2.62; e.g. gene:NDUFA5 +7.34, gene:NDUFS7 +5.68, gene:ATP5ME +5.20, gene:UQCRC2 +4.02, gene:COX20 +3.07, gene:TOMM22 +4.63, gene:TUFM +6.46), well above the 77% positive rate of this selected differential-expression list.", "Step 2 (measured, RNA): the mtDNA-encoded core subunits that are represented go the other way (gene:MT-ATP6 -3.35, gene:MT-CYB -2.32, gene:MT-ND4 -1.80, gene:MT-CO2 -1.33; only gene:MT-ND4L and gene:MT-ND5 positive), creating a mitonuclear transcript-pool mismatch.", "Step 3 (inferred, not measured): unmatched nuclear subunit supply raises the fraction of incompletely assembled complex I/III/IV/V intermediates and thereby the superoxide/peroxide generated per unit ETC protein; no ROS or assembly measurement is supplied, so this step is a hypothesis, not an observation.", "Step 4 (measured, RNA; activity inferred): reducing power and peroxide removal are re-directed to the matrix - gene:PRDX3 +3.49, gene:PRDX5 +1.96, gene:PRDX2 +4.41, gene:TXNDC17 +7.10, gene:TXNL1 +4.33, gene:GPX4 +2.79, gene:MGST2 +3.32, gene:FTH1 +2.53, with mitochondrial NADPH sources gene:NNT +2.88 and gene:ME1 +1.36 and shuttle components gene:MDH1 +8.72, gene:GOT1 +6.43 up, while cytosolic pentose-phosphate transcripts fall (gene:PGD -1.30, gene:TALDO1 -2.32). Abundance is measured; peroxidase flux is inferred.", "Step 5 (measured, RNA; lipid state inferred): acyl-chain input is biased away from peroxidizable PUFA - gene:SCD +4.17 with MUFA-preferring remodeling enzymes gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:CHPT1 +2.91 and cardiolipin remodeling gene:TAZ +3.26, against reduced PUFA activation and oxygenation (gene:ACSL4 -2.14, gene:ALOX15 -3.63).", "Step 6 (measured, RNA): fatty acid and sterol surplus is routed to esterified stores and lysosomal turnover (gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:SOAT1 +1.25, gene:MGLL +4.00; gene:TFEB +2.38 with gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88; sterol module gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:DHCR24 +3.69, gene:LDLR +1.50, gene:SCP2 +5.95), which sustains membrane and cristae expansion without releasing free PUFA into peroxidation-prone pools.", "Step 7 (predicted phenotype): in the mock condition the buffered state is compensated - elevated MUFA:PUFA ratio in PC/PE and cardiolipin, larger MUFA-rich TAG/CE pools, and no excess oxidized-PUFA lipids - while reserve against an added oxidant or PUFA load is reduced; that reserve deficit is a future-challenge prediction, not an established ongoing defect."], "title": "Mitonuclear stoichiometry mismatch in APOE4 microglia drives matrix-directed peroxide buffering and a MUFA-biased, peroxidation-resistant lipid remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.355425912934313, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16434660493544434, "cosine_similarity": -0.08980764443029805, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7746440129449839, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.355425912934313, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.16434660493544434, "cosine_similarity": -0.08980764443029805, "direction_accuracy": 0.21844660194174756, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7746440129449839, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.5990575, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 109}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_007", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All enzyme functions, substrate preferences and pathway assignments used here are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "Lower ACSL4 RNA produces lower relevant protein activity and makes arachidonate activation limiting. Protein abundance, catalytic activity and subcellular localization of ACSL4 are not established by these data.", "Other acyl-CoA synthetases do not fully compensate, and arachidonate delivery or downstream acyltransferase activity is not the dominant constraint. ACSL5 reduction could instead indicate a broader activation defect; the proposed arachidonate selectivity requires testing.", "The acyltransferase and synthesis RNA changes can support membrane replenishment with alternative donors. Their induction could instead reflect successful compensation, unrelated cell-state changes or increased de novo synthesis; expression differences do not specify enzyme stoichiometry or flux.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, with an unspecified logarithm base and a broad positive shift. They do not measure absolute total RNA, and absence of a gene from the supplied rows does not mean unchanged expression or absent function.", "Each protein spot has multiple candidate genes. No spot identifies an ACSL4 protein change or provides direct confirmation of the proposed bottleneck; discordant candidate-containing spots cannot resolve individual protein abundance.", "The isogenic comparison is interpreted within the supplied astrocyte co-culture context. Biological replicate counts, baseline expression and cell-state composition are unavailable, so clone, maturation, co-culture and normalization effects remain alternatives to the proposed genotype-associated mechanism."], "claim": "Under mock treatment at day 30, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia are hypothesized to have an ACSL4-dependent arachidonate-activation bottleneck. This would limit reincorporation of recycled arachidonate into membrane glycerophospholipids and favor replacement by alternative acyl chains during remodeling. The associated RNA pattern motivates this mechanism; causality and the predicted lipid changes have not been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Future tracer test: with matched extracellular loading and intracellular precursor exposure, APOE4 cells should show a larger reduction in early arachidonate-to-arachidonoyl-CoA formation and subsequent incorporation into existing membrane glycerophospholipids than in the corresponding oleate route. A backbone/acyl-chain pulse-chase should separate remodeling from de novo synthesis. Unchanged arachidonate activation and reincorporation, or a difference fully explained by uptake, would weaken the proposed activation bottleneck; equally reduced oleate flux would weaken its arachidonate selectivity.", "Discriminating perturbation: restore wild-type ACSL4 in APOE4 cells to a concurrently measured APOE3 reference protein level, and compare with an abundance- and localization-matched catalytically inactive ACSL4 control. Active ACSL4 should preferentially restore arachidonate activation and membrane reincorporation and increase the arachidonoyl-to-oleoyl ratio in remodeled phospholipids. Failure to rescue reincorporation after confirming restored catalytic activity, or equal rescue by inactive ACSL4, would weaken the mechanism.", "Reciprocal perturbation: titrated ACSL4 CRISPR interference in APOE3 cells should reproduce the arachidonate activation and remodeling defect at comparable loss of ACSL4 activity, while matching precursor uptake, viability and microglial state. Failure to phenocopy despite verified activity reduction would weaken ACSL4 as the primary bottleneck. These proposed experiments are predictions, not supplied measurements."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["1. Measured: ACSL4 RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:ACSL4, -2.142 reported log fold change, base unspecified). Inferred: this reduces functional ACSL4 capacity, the single primary bottleneck. Lower ACSL5 RNA (gene:ACSL5, -3.115) is consistent with reduced fatty-acid activation capacity but does not establish the specificity or activity of either enzyme.", "2. Unverified background knowledge assigns ACSL4 a role in activating arachidonate to arachidonoyl-CoA. The proposed capacity reduction would restrict activation of arachidonate released during membrane turnover and its delivery to reacylation reactions. Neither arachidonoyl-CoA availability nor turnover-derived arachidonate was measured.", "3. Measured increases in LPCAT1, MBOAT1 and MBOAT2 RNA (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2) are compatible with maintained or increased remodeling capacity. Inferred: this capacity cannot fully restore arachidonoyl incorporation when activation of that substrate is limiting; higher transcripts alone establish neither compensation nor reacylation flux.", "4. Higher SCD, AGPAT2 and CHPT1 RNA (gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:CHPT1) motivates a proposed alternative-acyl-chain replacement route. Using unverified background assignments for desaturation and glycerophospholipid assembly, available non-arachidonoyl donors, including oleoyl donors, would support membrane replenishment while arachidonate activation remains constrained. Donor supply, enzyme localization and assembly rates are inferred.", "5. The predicted consequence is less arachidonate reincorporation into existing membrane glycerophospholipids and a lower arachidonoyl-to-oleoyl acyl-chain ratio in the remodeled membrane fraction of APOE4 cells. This is an unmeasured, testable compositional difference; it does not imply an observed decrease in total phospholipid abundance."], "title": "ACSL4-limited arachidonate recycling biases APOE4 membrane remodeling"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.024286452756341614, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01878804075924193, "cosine_similarity": -0.09076098844848877, "direction_accuracy": 0.03559870550161812, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6728090614886731, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.024286452756341614, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.01878804075924193, "cosine_similarity": -0.09076098844848877, "direction_accuracy": 0.03559870550161812, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6728090614886731, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.7579890000000002, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 13}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_007", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results (no |effect| below ~1 is present), so set-level claims are only interpretable relative to the supplied background (mean +1.39, 77% positive), not as unbiased transcriptome statistics.", "The reported RNA effect is a log fold change of unspecified base; only ranks, signs and relative magnitudes are used, and no conversion to linear fold change is made.", "Transcript changes in ACSL4/ACSL5 translate into reduced total long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase capacity; ACSL1, ACSL3 and ACSL6 were not measured, so compensation by unmeasured isoforms would break this assumption.", "Protein spots carry several candidate genes; the ANXA1 and cathepsin attributions are provisional. For the ANXA1 spots the co-candidates ACTB and TALDO1 have decreased transcripts, which is why ANXA1 is favoured, but this is not identification.", "Hydrolase, acyltransferase and lipogenic transcript levels are used as proxies for enzymatic activity and flux; no lipid, ceramide, free fatty-acid, acyl-CoA or lysosomal pH measurement was supplied.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment in astrocyte co-culture; astrocyte-derived lipid supply differences and cell-composition or normalization effects that could generate the global positive RNA shift are not controlled in the supplied data.", "Association only; no perturbation in the supplied data establishes direction of causality."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes show a coordinated, above-background transcriptional expansion of endolysosomal lipid uptake and sphingolipid/glycosphingolipid hydrolysis together with a counter-directional loss of long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts (ACSL4, ACSL5). We propose that acyl-CoA charging of fatty acids liberated by this accelerated lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism is the primary bottleneck, so that salvaged acyl chains cannot be efficiently returned to phospholipids; the cell compensates through an SREBF1/SCD-driven de novo monounsaturated route feeding AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1/LPCAT1-MBOAT2 acylation, predicting a membrane phospholipid pool remodeled toward monounsaturated, PUFA-poor species with increased neutral-lipid and lysosomal lipid intermediates. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia under mock conditions should show phospholipid (PC/PE) species shifted toward monounsaturated (e.g. 18:1-containing) and away from arachidonoyl/docosahexaenoyl species, with increased triacylglycerol and increased lysophospholipid and free fatty-acid fractions. Finding unchanged or higher PUFA-phospholipid content in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Discriminating perturbation: restoring ACSL4 (and/or ACSL5) expression in APOE4 microglia, or bypassing the charging step with an exogenous PUFA supply under ACSL-competent conditions, should re-normalize PUFA-phospholipid content, lower free fatty-acid/lysolipid load and reduce lysosomal enlargement, while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcript program (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, CTSB) largely intact. If PUFA-phospholipid re-acylation is unchanged after ACSL4 restoration, or if measured total ACSL enzymatic activity is equal between genotypes, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Occlusion test: pan-ACSL inhibition (e.g. triacsin C) should shift phospholipid composition and neutral-lipid synthesis substantially less in APOE4 than in APOE3, because APOE4 is already acyl-CoA limited; equal or larger sensitivity in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Reciprocal test: ACSL4/ACSL5 knockdown in APOE3 microglia should phenocopy the APOE4 phospholipid composition shift and lipid-droplet increase without requiring the APOE4 allele; failure to phenocopy would argue for an APOE4-specific step upstream of acyl-CoA supply.", "Flux-source test: inhibiting lysosomal sphingolipid hydrolysis (GBA and/or SMPD1 inhibition or knockdown) in APOE4 should reduce ceramide and free fatty-acid load and blunt the compensatory SREBF1/SCD/DGAT1 induction; unchanged lipogenic induction would indicate that the lipogenic arm is driven independently of lysosomal catabolite handling and would weaken step 5.", "Specificity test: the strongly increased sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts should be matched by increased enzymatic activity (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA assays) and by increased, not decreased, lysosomal ceramide/glucosylceramide turnover; if hydrolase activity is unchanged despite the transcript increase, the inferred catabolic flux, and hence the load on the bottleneck, is not supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA; inferred cargo flux): transcripts for scavenger/lipoprotein and phagocytic lipid-uptake receptors are higher in APOE4 (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:MERTK, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:ABCA7). We infer, but did not measure, increased delivery of membrane and lipoprotein lipid cargo to the endolysosomal system.", "Step 2 (measured RNA and protein spots; inferred hydrolytic flux): a lysosome biogenesis/acidification and hydrolase program is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) with the sphingolipid/glycosidase arm the single most coherent set (gene:GBA, gene:GBA2, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:NAGLU, gene:SGSH, gene:MAN2B1, gene:NPC2, gene:GAA); cathepsin-candidate protein spots protein_spot:052, protein_spot:053, protein_spot:055 are also increased. Increased hydrolytic activity and flux are inferred, not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA and protein spots; inferred localization/activity): ANXA1 transcript is high (gene:ANXA1) and the protein spots whose candidate lists contain ANXA1 are among the largest increases (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:047), consistent with increased Ca2+-dependent phospholipid-binding membrane-repair/turnover capacity at damaged endolysosomal and plasma membranes; spot identity is ambiguous and localization was not measured.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred capacity): against a strongly up-shifted differential-expression background (77% of rows positive), long-chain acyl-CoA synthetase transcripts fall (gene:ACSL4 at the 11th percentile, gene:ACSL5 at the 5th percentile). We infer reduced capacity to re-activate liberated fatty acids, especially the PUFA species preferred by ACSL4, into acyl-CoA for Lands-cycle re-acylation.", "Step 5 (measured RNA; inferred flux and composition): a compensatory de novo lipogenic/acylation arm is elevated (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:FADS1, gene:INSIG1, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:AGPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2), with increased monoacylglycerol lipase transcript (gene:MGLL). We infer that acylation demand is met by newly made monounsaturated acyl chains rather than by salvaged PUFA, and that surplus acyl flux is routed to triacylglycerol.", "Step 6 (inferred outcome, unmeasured pools): the imbalance predicts intralysosomal accumulation of sphingoid/ceramide and unesterified fatty-acid or lysolipid intermediates and a phospholipid pool shifted toward monounsaturated species; the disposal enzymes for these pools (ASAH1, UGCG, SGMS1/2, PSAP, NPC1, LIPA) were not measured here. The parallel mito-nuclear discordance (nuclear-encoded OXPHOS transcripts up, mitochondrially encoded gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CO2 down) is treated as a downstream or parallel readout, not as evidence for the lipid bottleneck."], "title": "APOE4 microglia expand lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism but restrict long-chain acyl-CoA re-activation, making fatty-acid re-esterification the rate-limiting step of membrane turnover"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34167189750027693, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0008398242409010031, "cosine_similarity": -0.0915543354896359, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_007", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8647313915857605, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.34167189750027693, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0008398242409010031, "cosine_similarity": -0.0915543354896359, "direction_accuracy": 0.3300970873786408, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8647313915857605, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.93140325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 481}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_017", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (no |effect| below ~1 is present) with an unspecified logarithm base; only the sign and the within-list rank of each effect are used, not the absolute magnitude.", "The strong global positive shift (77% of rows up, median +1.46) is at least partly a normalisation/compositional feature, so pathway claims rest on rank position within this list rather than on raw fold changes.", "Transcript abundance is taken as a proxy for enzyme abundance and, less securely, for enzymatic activity; no SCD, ACSL4, LPCAT1, AGPAT2 or DGAT1 protein or activity measurement exists in these data.", "Acyl-CoA species, lysophospholipids, phospholipid acyl composition, diacylglycerol, triacylglycerol and lipid-droplet content were not measured; all statements about them are predictions.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified, so no spot is used as evidence for a specific lipid enzyme.", "ACSL4 substrate preference for arachidonate and SCD product specificity for 16:1/18:1 are unverified background knowledge, not supported by the supplied data.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are isogenic and mock-treated as stated in the context, so genotype rather than treatment or line background drives the comparison."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia carry a coordinated SREBF1/SCD-associated lipogenic-acylation transcriptional program together with reduced ACSL4/ACSL5 transcripts, while lysosomal lipid-hydrolase transcripts are also elevated. We hypothesise that the resulting rate-limiting step is the composition of the cytosolic long-chain acyl-CoA pool feeding lysophospholipid re-acylation (LPCAT1/MBOAT1/MBOAT2) and de novo glycerolipid acylation (GPAT4/AGPAT2/DGAT1): a monounsaturated (SCD-derived 16:1/18:1) rather than polyunsaturated (ACSL4-dependent 20:4) acyl-CoA supply. This predicts that APOE4 membrane phospholipids are re-acylated with more monounsaturated and fewer arachidonoyl chains and that hydrolysis-released fatty acids are preferentially re-esterified into diacylglycerol/triacylglycerol, rather than that APOE4 microglia simply make more total lipid. Lipid composition itself was not measured here, and no causal direction is established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show a higher monounsaturated fraction (e.g. PC/PE 32:1, 34:1) and a lower arachidonoyl fraction (e.g. PC/PE 38:4) in phospholipids, with increased triacylglycerol. Equal or PUFA-shifted phospholipid acyl composition in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "DISCRIMINATING PERTURBATION: SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) in APOE4 microglia should normalise the MUFA-containing phospholipid and triacylglycerol fraction toward APOE3 while leaving the lysosomal hydrolase transcript elevation (GBA, SMPD1, CTSB, CTSD, TFEB targets) largely intact. If SCD inhibition also abolishes the lysosomal transcript signature, the lysosomal program is upstream and the acyl-supply bottleneck is not primary; if SCD inhibition changes neither lipid composition nor droplet content, the mechanism fails.", "Stable-isotope tracing (13C-acetate or D2O) should show increased label incorporation into 16:1/18:1-containing phospholipid and triacylglycerol species in APOE4, i.e. increased flux and not only increased transcripts. Unchanged incorporation despite elevated SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1 transcripts would falsify the inferred activity step.", "Restoring ACSL4 expression in APOE4 microglia should raise arachidonoyl-phospholipid content and increase sensitivity to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3-induced lipid peroxidation) relative to unmodified APOE4. If APOE4 cells are already more RSL3-sensitive than APOE3 at baseline, the reduced-PUFA-supply inference is wrong.", "LPCAT1 knockdown should cause a larger accumulation of lysophosphatidylcholine in APOE4 than in APOE3, because the re-acylation step is predicted to carry more flux in APOE4. Equal lysoPC accumulation in both genotypes would argue against increased Lands-cycle flux.", "DGAT1 inhibition should shift the excess acyl-CoA into phospholipids and free fatty acid rather than reducing total lipid synthesis in APOE4; a proportional drop in total glycerolipid synthesis instead would indicate that acyl-CoA supply, not esterification routing, is saturated."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for the SREBP-1 axis and its cytosolic acetyl-CoA/citrate supply arm (gene:SREBF1, gene:ACSS2, gene:SLC25A1) and for the desaturase SCD (gene:SCD) and desaturase FADS1 (gene:FADS1). We infer, but do not measure, increased SCD enzymatic activity and increased 16:1/18:1-CoA production.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): transcripts for the two ACSLs present in the data fall (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5). Because ACSL4 preferentially activates arachidonate, we infer reduced arachidonoyl-CoA availability; this is an inference about a molecular pool that was not measured.", "Step 3 (bottleneck, inferred): the acyl-CoA pool composition, not total acylation capacity, becomes the rate-limiting determinant of glycerolipid acyl chains, because lysophospholipid acyltransferase and glycerolipid acyltransferase transcripts are simultaneously elevated (gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4), i.e. enzyme capacity is unlikely to be limiting while substrate identity is skewed.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux/localisation): elevated lysosomal and neutral-lipid hydrolase transcripts (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:LAMP1, gene:TFEB, gene:MGLL) indicate an increased membrane-lipid catabolic load; we infer that liberated lysolipids and free fatty acids re-enter the Lands cycle and the glycerolipid pathway rather than being oxidised or exported.", "Step 5 (inferred output): re-esterification through AGPAT2/GPAT4 and DGAT1 (gene:DGAT1) and phosphatidylcholine completion via CHPT1 (gene:CHPT1) channels the MUFA-biased acyl-CoA into diacylglycerol/triacylglycerol and into PC/PE species with fewer polyunsaturated chains.", "Step 6 (predicted phenotype, unmeasured): a PUFA-poor, MUFA-rich membrane with increased neutral-lipid storage should show reduced substrate for lipid peroxidation; the elevated GPX4 transcript (gene:GPX4) is consistent with, but does not demonstrate, such a state."], "title": "MUFA-biased acyl-CoA supply through the Lands cycle re-acylation step remodels APOE4 microglial membrane and storage glycerolipids"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.262415537421999, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05821776930710775, "cosine_similarity": -0.09265407041339896, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_017", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7626925566343042, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.262415537421999, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05821776930710775, "cosine_similarity": -0.09265407041339896, "direction_accuracy": 0.20064724919093851, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7626925566343042, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72731275, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 482}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_047", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA effects are 'reported log fold change' of unspecified base, so only rank and sign, not absolute magnitude, are interpreted; all enrichment claims are made against the list's own median (+1.46) because 1705/2212 rows are positive.", "The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression result, not an unbiased transcriptome; absence of LPCAT3, MBOAT7, ACSL1, ACSL3, ELOVL and PLIN genes from the file is treated as missing data, not as evidence of no change.", "Transcript level is assumed to track enzyme activity for ACSL4/ACSL5, SCD and the acyltransferases; no protein, activity, isotopic-flux, membrane-order or lipidomic measurement of these pools is supplied.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each and are treated as non-identifying corroboration only; no protein spot is claimed to identify a specific lipid enzyme.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so astrocyte-derived lipoprotein PUFA could partly bypass the proposed cell-autonomous bottleneck; the hypothesis assumes such rescue is incomplete.", "Direction of causality between the APOE4 allele and the lipid-enzyme program is unestablished; the transcriptional changes could be a consequence rather than a cause of an altered lipid state."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia transcriptionally raise both membrane-catabolic capacity (endolysosomal hydrolases, v-ATPase) and glycerolipid re-esterification capacity (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, CHPT1, DGAT1) while lowering the long-chain polyunsaturated acyl-CoA ligases ACSL4 and ACSL5. We hypothesise that PUFA-acyl-CoA regeneration, not lysophospholipid supply or acyltransferase capacity, is the rate-limiting step of this remodeling cycle, so lysophospholipids generated by accelerated membrane turnover are reacylated preferentially from the expanded SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl-CoA pool. The predicted, currently unmeasured consequence is an APOE4 membrane phospholipidome depleted of 20:4/22:6 chains and enriched in 16:1/18:1, with surplus acyl flux diverted through AGPAT2/DGAT1 into triacylglycerol. This is an association-based mechanistic proposal; causality has not been established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating tracer experiment: pulse APOE4 and isogenic APOE3 microglia with equimolar D-labelled arachidonate (20:4) and D-labelled oleate (18:1). The bottleneck model predicts a genotype-specific defect, i.e. reduced labelled-20:4 incorporation into PC/PE in APOE4 with preserved or increased labelled-18:1 incorporation (interaction between genotype and fatty-acid species). Equal incorporation of both tracers, or a proportional reduction of both, would weaken the mechanism and favour a general membrane-turnover or uptake defect.", "Untargeted lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia under mock treatment should show decreased 20:4/22:6-containing PC and PE species, increased 16:1/18:1-containing species, and increased TAG mass. Unchanged or increased PUFA-phospholipid fraction would falsify the composition claim even if the transcript pattern replicates.", "Rescue: doxycycline-inducible ACSL4 expression (or supplementation with arachidonoyl-CoA-generating conditions) in APOE4 microglia should restore PUFA-phospholipid content and reduce TAG toward APOE3 levels without normalising the lysosomal transcript module. Failure to restore PUFA-phospholipid content would place the bottleneck elsewhere (e.g. at LPCAT3/MBOAT7 or at PUFA uptake).", "SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572) should reduce MUFA-phospholipid and TAG and increase membrane order defects preferentially in APOE4; an equal effect in APOE3 would argue the MUFA arm is not genotype-selective.", "Functional test: APOE4 microglia should show lower membrane fluidity (higher lipid-order probe GP value) and reduced phagocytic uptake of a deformability-demanding cargo, both partially reversed by exogenous arachidonate loading. Unchanged membrane order despite an altered lipidome would weaken step 6.", "Negative control that would weaken a competing cholesterol-centric explanation: the sterol uptake/efflux module (SCARB1 excepted) sits at the list median (CD36, LDLR, SOAT1, APOE, TREM2, NPC2), so if cholesterol-esterification flux, not acyl-chain composition, is found to be the dominant APOE4 difference, this hypothesis is superseded."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 cells show coordinated elevation of endolysosomal hydrolase and v-ATPase transcripts (CTSB, CTSD, GBA, HEXA, SMPD1, ATP6V1H, ATP6V1A, ATP6V0C) plus RAB7A, PIK3C3 and CHMP4B, all far above the strongly positive global median of this selected list. We infer, but do not observe, increased flux of internalised and autophagic membrane through acidified compartments, which liberates lysophospholipids and free fatty acids.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): A lipogenic/acylation module is coordinately elevated relative to the same global median (SREBF1, SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, CHPT1, DGAT1, GPAT4), together with cytosolic acetyl-CoA suppliers SLC25A1 and ACSS2. We infer increased capacity for de novo monounsaturated acyl-CoA production and for lysophospholipid/lysophosphatidate acylation.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): ACSL4 and ACSL5 transcripts are among the lowest-ranked lipid genes in the list, while every acceptor-side acyltransferase measured is up. Because ACSL4 is the principal ligase that re-activates arachidonate and other long-chain PUFAs (unverified background knowledge), we propose that re-entry of liberated PUFA into the acyl-CoA pool becomes rate-limiting, whereas MUFA-CoA supply is not.", "Step 4 (inferred composition): With acceptor and MUFA-CoA supply in excess and PUFA-CoA limiting, LPCAT1/MBOAT1/MBOAT2-mediated Lands-cycle reacylation and CHPT1-mediated de novo PC synthesis are predicted to install 16:1/18:1 chains, producing phosphatidylcholine and phosphatidylethanolamine pools depleted of 20:4/22:6. No lipid species were measured here.", "Step 5 (inferred flux partitioning): Surplus acyl-CoA and diacylglycerol are predicted to be routed by AGPAT2 and DGAT1 into triacylglycerol, with MGLL (strongly elevated) recycling diacylglycerol-derived fatty acid, giving a storage-biased rather than oxidation-biased disposal of turnover-derived lipid.", "Step 6 (inferred functional consequence): A PUFA-poor, MUFA-rich, more ordered membrane with a reduced peroxidisable substrate pool is predicted to lower eicosanoid precursor release and reduce the membrane deformability needed for phagocytic cup formation; the concurrent fall in ALOX15 and rise in GPX4 transcripts are consistent with reduced peroxidisable PUFA load but do not demonstrate it."], "title": "ACSL4/ACSL5 loss creates a PUFA-acyl-CoA bottleneck that redirects high-flux membrane turnover into MUFA-biased Lands-cycle reacylation in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2657017317136211, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03303798161074564, "cosine_similarity": -0.09469745331234986, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_047", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7729708737864078, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.2657017317136211, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.03303798161074564, "cosine_similarity": -0.09469745331234986, "direction_accuracy": 0.2168284789644013, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7729708737864078, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72361875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 483}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_071", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; module enrichment was therefore assessed by rank statistics against the 2212 supplied genes only, and absence of a gene (e.g. ABCA1, ABCG1, CPT1A, NPC1, PLIN2) means 'not supplied', not 'unchanged'.", "The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and preserved as reported log units; relative ordering, not absolute fold change, is used.", "The strong global positive RNA shift (mean +1.39, 77% of rows positive) is treated as a background offset that all module statistics are corrected against; if that offset is technical (depth, ambient RNA, cell-size normalisation) it inflates every 'up' module equally but should not create the observed contrast between up-shifted lysosomal/mitochondrial modules and down-shifted glycolytic/myeloid modules.", "Protein spots contain 2-6 candidate genes each and are not uniquely identified; they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration and never as evidence for a specific protein.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme amount; enzymatic activity, lysosomal pH, organelle volume, lipid flux, acyl-chain composition and droplet content were not measured in this dataset.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so lipid substrate supply may be partly non-cell-autonomous and genotype effects may be indirect.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so per-gene effect precision cannot be independently verified."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 chiefly by a coordinated transcriptional expansion of endolysosomal lipid hydrolysis together with mitochondrial oxidative and antioxidant machinery, while glycolytic and myeloid-activation transcripts are not raised. We hypothesise (not demonstrated) that lysosomal liberation of fatty acids and sterols outpaces terminal oxidative disposal, so the surplus is re-esterified through an up-regulated SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/DGAT1/SOAT1 acylation arm, predicting an APOE4-specific gain of monounsaturated-enriched triacylglycerol and cholesteryl-ester neutral lipid with relative depletion of polyunsaturated acyl species. All statements about flux, enzyme activity, organelle content and causal order are inferences from RNA and ambiguous protein-spot abundance, not measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: co-treating APOE4 and APOE3 microglia with a SOAT1 inhibitor (avasimibe) plus a DGAT1 inhibitor should abolish most of the APOE4-minus-APOE3 excess in neutral-lipid droplet mass and cholesteryl-ester/triacylglycerol content, and convert it into an APOE4-selective rise in free cholesterol and free fatty acid with greater cytotoxicity. If APOE4 droplet excess persists unchanged under combined esterification blockade, the esterification-sink step is wrong.", "SCD inhibition should shrink the APOE4-specific gain in 16:1/18:1-containing triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester and sensitise APOE4 more than APOE3 to saturated fatty-acid load; equal genotype responses would weaken the desaturation-dependent buffering step.", "Blocking lysosomal hydrolysis upstream (bafilomycin A1, or conduritol-B-epoxide/GBA plus HEXA inhibition) should reduce the APOE4-APOE3 difference in neutral lipid; if the lipid difference is unchanged or increased, the lysosome-derived-substrate step is wrong and a biosynthetic or efflux-defect model is favoured.", "Direct biochemical test of the direction of the bottleneck: APOE4 microglia should show higher, not lower, lysosomal hydrolase activity (GBA, HEXA, acid lipase) and higher LysoTracker/LAMP1 organelle volume than APOE3. Finding equal or reduced hydrolase activity and undigested substrate accumulation would falsify the 'increased hydrolysis, limited disposal' direction in favour of a lysosomal-deficiency model.", "Metabolic-flux test: 13C/2H tracing should show higher fractional oxidation of fatty-acid-derived carbon into TCA intermediates in APOE4 with a simultaneously higher fraction re-esterified into triacylglycerol; if APOE4 shows lower oxygen consumption and lower TCA labelling despite the higher TCA/ETC transcripts, the compensatory-capacity interpretation fails and a post-transcriptional mitochondrial defect model should replace it.", "Rescue test: enhancing terminal disposal (LXR agonist-driven efflux to an extracellular acceptor, or CPT1-independent medium-chain fatty-acid supply) should reduce APOE4 droplet excess without lowering lysosomal hydrolase transcripts; failure to reduce droplets would weaken the disposal-limited framing.", "Independent proteomic identification (LC-MS/MS rather than spots) should confirm increased lysosomal hydrolase and mitochondrial matrix protein abundance in APOE4; failure to confirm at protein level would restrict the claim to a transcriptional program only."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lysosomal hydrolases and acidification/positioning machinery (gene:GAA, gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:SMPD1, gene:NAGLU, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C, gene:LAMP1, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB). Inferred: an expanded, more acidified degradative compartment with greater hydrolytic capacity.", "Measured: lipoprotein/lipid uptake and intralysosomal sterol-handling transcripts are higher (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:LDLR, gene:ABCA7, gene:NPC2, gene:APOE), and sphingolipid catabolic transcripts are coordinately higher (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB). Inferred: increased delivery and hydrolysis of lipoprotein- and membrane-derived lipid, liberating free fatty acids, sphingoid bases and unesterified sterol inside lysosomes.", "Measured: mitochondrial pyruvate/TCA/electron-transport and carrier transcripts are strongly higher (gene:MPC2, gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:GOT1, gene:DLD, gene:ACO2, gene:NDUFA5, gene:NDUFS7, gene:NDUFS8, gene:COX5B, gene:ATP5F1B, gene:SLC25A11, gene:SLC25A46, gene:TUFM) whereas upper-glycolysis transcripts are lower (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP, gene:HK3). Inferred: a demand-driven, compensatory bias toward mitochondrial oxidative disposal rather than glycolysis; this oxidative capacity is the proposed rate-limiting sink.", "Bottleneck (inferred): oxidative disposal does not match the liberated lipid load; consistent with an oxidative burden, antioxidant and metal-handling transcripts rise (gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:GPX4, gene:TXNDC17, gene:CCS, gene:SELENOW, gene:NNT), and redox/pentose-phosphate candidate proteins are over-represented among increased protein spots (protein_spot:017, protein_spot:038, protein_spot:042, protein_spot:077).", "Measured: the acyl-CoA/glycerolipid/sterol esterification arm is coordinately higher (gene:SREBF1, gene:SCD, gene:AGPAT2, gene:GPAT4, gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:CHPT1, gene:DGAT1, gene:SOAT1, gene:ACSS2, gene:SCP2), while gene:ACSL4 and gene:ALOX15 are lower. Inferred: surplus fatty acid is desaturated to monounsaturates and esterified into triacylglycerol and cholesteryl ester, with reduced channelling of polyunsaturated acyl-CoA into membrane phospholipid.", "Predicted lipid phenotype (not measured here): APOE4 microglia accumulate more neutral-lipid droplet material enriched in 16:1/18:1 acyl chains and cholesteryl esters, with a lower polyunsaturated phospholipid fraction, relative to isogenic APOE3.", "Correlated state change (measured RNA, causal role not established): myeloid activation/motility transcripts are lower (gene:CSF1, gene:SPN, gene:SEMA4A, gene:CTSS, gene:PTPRC), consistent with a lipid-buffering rather than acutely inflammatory microglial state under mock conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run an expanded lysosomal lipid-catabolic program whose terminal fatty-acid disposal is limiting, shunting lipid into SCD/DGAT1/SOAT1-dependent monounsaturated neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38023852601262786, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1496840990993516, "cosine_similarity": -0.09701635739561863, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_071", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8116893203883495, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.38023852601262786, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1496840990993516, "cosine_similarity": -0.09701635739561863, "direction_accuracy": 0.2702265372168285, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8116893203883495, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.62912975, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 484}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_097", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression set, not an unbiased transcriptome; the list is 77% up-regulated with median effect +1.46, so only within-pathway contrasts (up-ranked LPCAT1/MBOAT/AGPAT2 versus bottom-decile ACSL4/ACSL5/GPAT3) are treated as informative, not the shared upward direction.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; ranks and percentiles, not absolute fold changes, carry the argument.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme protein and catalytic capacity for these lipid enzymes; no enzyme activity, acyl-CoA pool, phospholipid species or lipid-droplet measurement is present in these data.", "Reported substrate preferences (ACSL4 for arachidonate, LPCAT1 for saturated/monounsaturated sn-2, MBOAT2 for oleate, DGAT1 for triacylglycerol) are unverified background knowledge, not measured here.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified; assigning the up-shifted spots protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046 mainly to ANXA1 rather than co-listed TALDO1 rests on the opposing RNA direction of TALDO1 (-2.32) and remains an assumption.", "Microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some measured RNA/protein signal may not be microglia-autonomous, and no lipidomic, flux or imaging modality is supplied."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the rate-limiting step distinguishing them from isogenic APOE3 cells is acyl-chain selection during glycerolipid (re)acylation: an expanded SREBF1/SCD-driven monounsaturated acyl-CoA arm feeding GPAT4-AGPAT2-CHPT1/DGAT1 and LPCAT1/MBOAT-dependent reacylation, combined with a contracted ACSL4/ACSL5 polyunsaturated acyl-CoA arm, is proposed to shift newly made and remodelled membrane phospholipid toward saturated/monounsaturated species and to divert liberated fatty acid into triacylglycerol, while transcripts for lysosomal membrane-lipid hydrolysis are simultaneously high. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux and composition; none of the lipid pools, enzyme activities or causal directions were measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) in mock-treated isogenic pairs should have a genotype-selective effect - APOE4 microglia should lose a larger fraction of triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet content and show a larger rise in saturated-fatty-acid stress and lysosomal-hydrolase transcripts than APOE3, because the monounsaturated arm is proposed to be the load-bearing route. If SCD inhibition produces indistinguishable responses in APOE4 and APOE3, the mechanism is weakened.", "Lipidomics of the same cultures should show, in APOE4, higher 16:0/18:1-containing phosphatidylcholine and phosphatidylethanolamine species and triacylglycerol, with a reduced fraction of 20:4- and 22:6-containing phospholipid. Equal or higher polyunsaturated phospholipid fraction in APOE4 would falsify the acyl-chain-selection bottleneck.", "Restoring the polyunsaturated arm - ACSL4 re-expression, or supplementation with arachidonic acid or 20:4-lysophosphatidylcholine - should normalise the phospholipid polyunsaturated fraction and reduce lipid-droplet load in APOE4 without requiring reduction of GBA/HEXA/CTSB transcripts. No compositional rescue would weaken step 3.", "Directionality test: blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA inhibition) should not abolish the SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2/LPCAT1 transcript elevation if acyl selection is the primary bottleneck; if the entire lipogenic program collapses, the lysosomal arm is upstream and this hypothesis should be replaced by a lysosome-primary mechanism.", "Membrane-order reporters (e.g. Laurdan generalised polarisation) should show higher lipid order in APOE4 phagosomal/lysosomal membranes, reversible by oleate or SCD-independent unsaturated-lipid supplementation; unchanged or lower order in APOE4 would weaken step 5.", "Protein-level follow-up with unique identification (targeted MS or immunoblot) should confirm SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1 and DGAT1 protein increases in APOE4; unchanged protein for these enzymes despite the transcript ranks would weaken the transcript-to-capacity assumption."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry a coordinated lipogenic transcript program - SREBF1 (gene:SREBF1, +4.67, 92nd percentile of this differential-expression list), the citrate carrier SLC25A1 (gene:SLC25A1, +4.47), ACSS2 (gene:ACSS2, +2.93), SCD (gene:SCD, +4.17) and FADS1 (gene:FADS1, +1.59). We infer, but did not measure, increased cytosolic acetyl-CoA-to-monounsaturated fatty acyl-CoA flux.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): transcripts for lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism are among the most extreme in the list - GAA (gene:GAA, +9.96), CTSK (gene:CTSK, +7.36), GBA (gene:GBA, +6.71), SCP2 (gene:SCP2, +5.95), HEXA (gene:HEXA, +5.68), SMPD1 (gene:SMPD1, +5.63), CTSB (gene:CTSB, +5.52), plus the uptake receptor SCARB1 (gene:SCARB1, +8.22). We infer elevated hydrolytic turnover of internalised and autophagic membrane, releasing free fatty acid, sphingoid base and sterol into a re-esterification demand.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): acyl-CoA selection at the (re)acylation step is proposed to be limiting and asymmetric. The saturated/monounsaturated-preferring arm is up - LPCAT1 (gene:LPCAT1, +3.07), MBOAT2 (gene:MBOAT2, +3.26), MBOAT1 (gene:MBOAT1, +2.65), AGPAT2 (gene:AGPAT2, +6.29, 97th percentile), GPAT4 (gene:GPAT4, +1.58) - whereas the long-chain polyunsaturated acyl-CoA arm is among the few strongly down transcripts in a list that is 77% up: ACSL4 (gene:ACSL4, -2.14, 11th percentile), ACSL5 (gene:ACSL5, -3.11, 5th percentile), GPAT3 (gene:GPAT3, -2.23, 10th percentile).", "Step 4 (inferred): phosphatidic acid and diacylglycerol produced by GPAT4/AGPAT2 are routed onward by the Kennedy pathway (CHPT1, gene:CHPT1, +2.91; PCYT2, gene:PCYT2, +1.05) into phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine, and by DGAT1 (gene:DGAT1, +1.72) into triacylglycerol; MGLL (gene:MGLL, +4.00) indicates accompanying monoacylglycerol turnover. The predicted consequence is expanded neutral-lipid storage carrying 16:0/18:1 chains.", "Step 5 (inferred composition, not measured): the phospholipid sn-2 pool shifts toward 16:0/18:1 and the 20:4/22:6-containing phospholipid pool contracts, increasing acyl-chain order of plasma, phagosomal and lysosomal membranes and lowering the arachidonate reservoir available for phospholipase-dependent release.", "Step 6 (inferred feedback): more ordered, PUFA-poor limiting membranes degrade internalised lipid less efficiently, so the high hydrolase/v-ATPase transcript program (gene:GBA, gene:HEXA, gene:CTSB, gene:GAA) is sustained rather than resolving, and phospholipid-binding annexin ANXA1 rises (gene:ANXA1, +4.15; candidate-ambiguous spots protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045 and protein_spot:046, +1.96 to +3.05 log2), consistent with but not proof of altered membrane surface handling."], "title": "Acyl-CoA selection at the reacylation step biases APOE4 microglial glycerolipid synthesis toward saturated/monounsaturated chains"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10284126573865524, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.041168826507451295, "cosine_similarity": -0.10739385247693022, "direction_accuracy": 0.1407766990291262, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7660388349514563, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.10284126573865524, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.041168826507451295, "cosine_similarity": -0.10739385247693022, "direction_accuracy": 0.1407766990291262, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7660388349514563, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.88357025, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 485}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_097", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA effect column is a log fold change of unspecified base; we use ranks and percentiles within the supplied rows rather than absolute magnitudes, and treat the 15.5-to-minus-7.9 range as scale-uncalibrated.", "The 2212 RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, so the 77 percent positive, median +1.46 shift is treated as the null background against which module ranks are compared; no claim is made about absolute global transcription.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme activity for SCD, ACSL4, AGPAT2, DGAT1 and the LPCAT/MBOAT acyltransferases. This assumption is untested here: no enzyme activity, acyl-CoA pool, lipid species, droplet image or flux measurement is supplied.", "Protein spots are mixtures of candidate proteins; the ANXA1 assignment for the up-shifted spot train is only plausible because gene:ANXA1 is high while gene:TALDO1 is low, and it is not an identification.", "The MUFA/storage module was assembled after inspecting the data, so its permutation p-value (0.0079) is descriptive rather than confirmatory.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture; the RNA and spot signals are assumed to be dominated by microglia, which the supplied metadata does not verify.", "Replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size precision cannot be judged."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-derived microglia, APOE4 shifts the transcriptional set-point of fatty-acyl handling: transcripts for citrate/acetate-derived lipogenic supply (SLC25A1, ACSS2), the SREBF1-SCD desaturation arm, and glycerolipid esterification/remodeling enzymes (AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2) are among the highest-ranked changes, while the polyunsaturated-fatty-acid-preferring acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4 and ACSL5 are among the lowest. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step differentiating APOE4 from APOE3 is PUFA-CoA activation (ACSL4-type) relative to a raised monounsaturated acyl-CoA supply, so that acyl chains liberated by increased lysosomal/lipoprotein-derived lipid turnover are re-esterified into MUFA-enriched triacylglycerol and saturated/MUFA phospholipids rather than re-inserted as PUFA into membrane phospholipids. The predicted, currently unmeasured consequence is an APOE4 lipidome with higher neutral-lipid mass and 16:1/18:1 content and lower 20:4/22:6 phospholipid content. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Primary discriminating prediction: untargeted lipidomics of the same APOE4 versus APOE3 mock cultures should show higher triacylglycerol mass and a higher 16:1+18:1 fraction in TG and in PC/PE, with a lower 20:4- and 22:6-containing phospholipid fraction, and an increased TG-to-phospholipid ratio. If PUFA-phospholipid content is unchanged or higher in APOE4, or if TG mass is not increased, the mechanism is falsified.", "SCD inhibition (for example A939572 or CAY10566) in APOE4 microglia should lower TG mass and the MUFA fraction toward APOE3 values while leaving lysosomal hydrolase transcripts (GBA, SMPD1, CTSB) largely unchanged. Failure to reduce TG would indicate the neutral lipid derives from uptake rather than from desaturation-driven esterification and would weaken step 3-5.", "Restoring ACSL4 (overexpression) in APOE4 microglia should increase 20:4 incorporation into PC/PE and reduce the TG-to-phospholipid ratio. If ACSL4 restoration does not raise PUFA-phospholipids while exogenous arachidonate supplementation does, the bottleneck lies upstream of acyl activation and step 4 is wrong.", "Stable-isotope tracing with 13C-acetate or 13C-glucose plus 13C-oleate should show greater label enrichment into 18:1-containing TG and DAG in APOE4 than APOE3 within 24 h. Equal or lower enrichment in APOE4 would weaken steps 2, 3 and 5.", "DGAT1 inhibition should not normalise the phospholipid acyl profile but should redirect labelled acyl chains toward oxidation or free fatty acid accumulation; if DGAT1 inhibition instead restores PUFA-phospholipids, the proposed ordering of the bottleneck (activation before esterification) is incorrect.", "If lipidomics instead shows the dominant APOE4 difference to be accumulated glucosylceramide, sphingomyelin or cholesteryl ester with no acyl-chain saturation shift, the alternative lysosomal-catabolism-limited mechanism should replace this one."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipid/lipoprotein capture and lysosomal hydrolysis (gene:SCARB1 is the 19th highest of 2212 rows; gene:CD36, gene:TREM2, gene:APOE, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:TFEB). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery of membrane- and lipoprotein-derived lipid to the endolysosome and therefore a larger intracellular free fatty acid and sphingoid-base load.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): TCA/oxidative and citrate-export transcripts are the most coherently elevated module (gene:MDH1, gene:OGDH, gene:ACO2, gene:MPC2, gene:SLC25A1; permutation p=0.0003 against the selected-row background) while glycolytic transcripts trend low (gene:HK2, gene:PFKP). We infer increased cytosolic acetyl-CoA availability from citrate and acetate (gene:ACSS2) rather than from glucose; acetyl-CoA and acyl-CoA pools were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred activity): The SREBF1 arm is elevated relative to the sterol arm (gene:SREBF1 at the 92nd percentile versus gene:SREBF2 at the 28th), with gene:SCD at the 89th percentile. We infer a raised Delta-9 desaturation capacity and hence a MUFA-CoA-dominated acyl-CoA pool.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred activity): gene:ACSL4 and gene:ACSL5 are in the bottom 11 percent of an otherwise upward-shifted distribution (only 23 percent of rows are negative). We propose that reduced ACSL4-type PUFA activation is the limiting step for Lands-cycle reacylation, so lysophospholipids are preferentially reacylated by the elevated gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT1 and gene:MBOAT2 with saturated/monounsaturated chains.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred flux and localisation): Surplus MUFA-CoA is channelled into de novo glycerolipid synthesis and storage through gene:AGPAT2 (97th percentile), gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1 and gene:CIDEB, with gene:MGLL and gene:ABHD5 indicating altered droplet lipolysis; the net predicted outcome is accumulation of MUFA-rich triacylglycerol in cytosolic droplets. Droplet number, size and lipid species were not measured here.", "Step 6 (consequence, partly measured): Membrane phospholipids become PUFA-poor and more saturated, which we expect to reduce membrane deformability and eicosanoid precursor availability and to increase demand for annexin-dependent membrane repair/trafficking; gene:ANXA1 is at the 89th percentile and the ANXA1-containing 2D spot train (protein_spot:043, protein_spot:044, protein_spot:045, protein_spot:046, protein_spot:041) is the strongest positive protein signal, although those spots also contain TALDO1 and are not uniquely identified."], "title": "APOE4 microglia divert fatty-acyl flux from PUFA phospholipid remodeling into MUFA-rich storage glycerolipids via an ACSL4-limited, SCD/AGPAT2-favoured acylation node"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26339401100321236, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06727803528700992, "cosine_similarity": -0.11314475001348269, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_097", "mean_absolute_error": 0.769546925566343, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.26339401100321236, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.06727803528700992, "cosine_similarity": -0.11314475001348269, "direction_accuracy": 0.2022653721682848, "mean_absolute_error": 0.769546925566343, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.19666625, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 486}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_077", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (every row has |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% up), so 'up' is the background state; the hypothesis assumes the relative magnitudes and the specific down-shifts (ACSL4, ACSL5, GPAT3) carry information beyond that shift.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no conversion to fold change is assumed.", "Transcript increases are assumed to translate into increased enzyme protein and catalytic activity in the same direction; no protein, phosphorylation, localization or activity measurement for any lipid enzyme is present in these data.", "Acyl-CoA species, lysophospholipid, phospholipid, triacylglycerol, sphingolipid and cholesterol pools, membrane order and lipid flux are all inferred; none were measured in the supplied files.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate 2D-gel features dominated by keratin and actin candidates; none is treated as a uniquely identified lipid enzyme and none is used as evidence for this mechanism.", "Astrocyte co-culture may supply exogenous lipids and APOE-containing particles, so intrinsic microglial synthesis versus imported lipid cannot be separated from these data.", "Direction of causality (APOE4 genotype -\u003e lipid program, versus a shared upstream state) is assumed, not established; biological replicate number is not supplied, so effect-size reliability cannot be assessed."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, a coordinated transcriptional increase in lipogenic carbon supply (SLC25A1, ACSS2), the SREBF1 axis, and the desaturation/re-esterification machinery (SCD, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, AGPAT2, GPAT4, DGAT1, CHPT1), together with reduced long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases ACSL4 and ACSL5, biases the cytosolic acyl-CoA pool toward monounsaturated species; because membrane lipid turnover is simultaneously elevated (SMPD1, GBA, CTSB, LAMP1, TFEB, SCARB1 transcripts up), the acyl-CoA-selective re-acylation step becomes the rate-limiting node that determines APOE4-specific membrane and lipid-droplet acyl composition (MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor) rather than total lipid amount. All acyl-CoA pools, lipid species, fluxes and enzyme activities are inferred, not measured here; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia should show a higher 16:1/18:1-containing fraction of PC and PE and a lower 20:4/22:6-containing fraction, with an increased TAG/phospholipid ratio. If APOE4 phospholipids are instead PUFA-enriched or the MUFA:PUFA ratio is indistinguishable between genotypes, the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. CAY10566/A939572) or SCD knockdown should produce a significant genotype x treatment interaction, normalizing the APOE4 MUFA:PUFA phospholipid ratio and lipid-droplet content toward APOE3 with a larger effect in APOE4. If SCD inhibition changes both genotypes equally (no interaction), or leaves the genotype difference intact, the SCD-supplied acyl-CoA bottleneck is falsified.", "Pulse labelling with alkyne- or 13C-oleate should show faster incorporation into PC and TAG and faster label turnover in APOE4 than APOE3, and LPCAT1 knockdown should selectively cause lysophosphatidylcholine accumulation and loss of 18:1-PC in APOE4. Equal oleate incorporation rates between genotypes, or an APOE3-dominant LPCAT1 dependence, would weaken the re-acylation-bottleneck claim.", "Alternative-mechanism discrimination: blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/SMPD1 inhibition) should reduce recycling of labelled membrane lipid into PC but should NOT by itself normalize the MUFA:PUFA ratio, whereas SCD inhibition should. If lysosomal blockade abolishes the genotype lipid difference while SCD inhibition does not, the primary bottleneck is catabolic turnover rather than acyl-CoA-selective re-acylation.", "Re-expression of ACSL4 in APOE4 microglia should restore arachidonoyl-phospholipid content and increase sensitivity to ferroptosis inducers (e.g. RSL3) relative to control APOE4 cells. No change in 20:4-phospholipids or ferroptosis sensitivity after ACSL4 restoration would weaken Step 2.", "Enzyme-level validation: LPCAT1, MBOAT2, AGPAT2, SCD and SMPD1 protein should be higher in APOE4 by targeted immunoblot or targeted MS. If these proteins are unchanged despite the transcript differences, the transcript-to-activity assumption fails and the mechanism should be rejected in its current form."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred activity): APOE4 microglia show higher transcripts for lipogenic carbon supply and the SREBP-1 axis (gene:SLC25A1 +4.47, gene:ACSS2 +2.93, gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:INSIG1 +1.87), which we infer raises cytosolic acetyl-CoA available for de novo acyl-chain synthesis; acetyl-CoA and malonyl-CoA pools were not measured.", "Step 2 (inferred acyl-CoA composition): Increased SCD (+4.17) with modest FADS1 (+1.59) and decreased ACSL4 (-2.14) and ACSL5 (-3.11) are predicted to shift the long-chain acyl-CoA pool toward 16:1/18:1 monounsaturated species and away from arachidonoyl/PUFA-CoA, since ACSL4 preferentially activates PUFAs (unverified background knowledge). Acyl-CoA species were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred flux): Lysosomal and membrane lipid hydrolase transcripts are high (gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:GBA2 +2.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:LAMP1 +1.38, gene:TFEB +2.38) alongside lipid-uptake receptors (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:ABCA7 +2.14, gene:APOE +1.24), which we infer increases the rate at which lysophospholipids and free fatty acids are generated and must be re-esterified.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck): The acyl-CoA-selective re-acylation step becomes rate-limiting and composition-setting: Lands-cycle acyltransferases (gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65) re-acylate lysophospholipids from the MUFA-biased acyl-CoA pool, while the glycerolipid arm (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:DGAT1 +1.72) and the CDP-choline terminal step (gene:CHPT1 +2.91) route the remaining acyl-CoA into phosphatidic acid, diacylglycerol, phosphatidylcholine and triacylglycerol.", "Step 5 (predicted lipid phenotype, unmeasured): Net output is a higher MUFA:PUFA ratio in APOE4 phospholipids and a larger neutral-lipid (TAG/DAG) buffer with rapid TAG cycling (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04, gene:SOAT1 +1.25), i.e. altered acyl-chain identity and membrane order rather than simple lipid accumulation.", "Step 6 (downstream, correlative only): Reduced PUFA-phospholipid content and altered membrane order are proposed to modify receptor-platform and phagocytic/lysosomal membrane behaviour and to co-occur with the elevated chemokine transcripts observed (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CXCL16 +3.66, gene:CCL2 +2.12); this coupling is a correlation in these data, not a demonstrated causal link."], "title": "SREBF1/SCD-biased acyl-CoA supply makes lysophospholipid re-acylation (LPCAT1/MBOAT) the bottleneck that remodels APOE4 microglial membranes toward monounsaturated glycerolipids"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.262240150648008, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08520936142543871, "cosine_similarity": -0.11450070819558264, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8368349514563107, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.262240150648008, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.08520936142543871, "cosine_similarity": -0.11450070819558264, "direction_accuracy": 0.1925566343042071, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8368349514563107, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.6587475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 487}, {"id": "opus-original-b04-hyp_074", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 4, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (every row exceeds |effect| 1) with a strong global positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive); we therefore treat only within-list rank position, not raw sign, as evidence, and assume this shift is largely technical/compositional rather than a true transcriptome-wide induction.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are not numerically comparable to the protein-spot log2 values.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track enzyme abundance and, less securely, catalytic capacity; hexokinase activity, glucose-6-phosphate, NADPH, lactate and respiration were not measured in this dataset.", "HK1, the constitutive hexokinase, is absent from the supplied list; we assume its absence means it was not called differentially expressed, so total hexokinase capacity is assumed, not shown, to fall.", "Protein spots contain 3-6 candidate genes each (median ~5, dominated by keratins/actin); they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration and never as evidence for a named protein.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture and may supply lactate, ketones or lipids that are not measured; genotype effects on microglia could be partly astrocyte-mediated.", "Replicate number is not supplied and only one timepoint under mock treatment is available, so state stability and effect-size reliability cannot be assessed."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 principally at the glucose-to-glucose-6-phosphate step: transcripts for the inducible hexokinases HK2/HK3 and for the phosphofructokinase isoform PFKP and the oxidative/non-oxidative pentose-phosphate enzymes PGD and TALDO1 are lower, while glucose transporters, mitochondrial pyruvate import, TCA-cycle, nuclear-encoded electron-transport and glutamine/lipid-catabolic transcripts are higher than the strong global upward shift of this selected differential-expression list. We hypothesise that this transcriptional configuration reflects a state in which hexokinase capacity, not glucose supply, limits glycolytic and pentose-phosphate flux, so APOE4 microglia meet acetyl-CoA and ATP demand by oxidising non-glycolytic carbon (glutamine/glutamate, fatty-acid- and ketone-derived acetyl-CoA), producing an oxidation-committed, glycolytically inflexible metabolic state. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; flux, enzyme activity, metabolite pools and causal direction are inferred, not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating substrate test: in extracellular-flux assays on isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia, APOE4 oxygen consumption should be disproportionately suppressed by the glutaminase inhibitor CB-839 and by the mitochondrial pyruvate-carrier inhibitor UK5099, whereas APOE3 extracellular acidification should be disproportionately suppressed by 2-deoxyglucose; if 2-DG-sensitive glycolytic rate and glycolytic reserve are equal or higher in APOE4, or if CB-839/UK5099 sensitivity is identical between genotypes, the mechanism is weakened.", "Stable-isotope tracing: [1,2-13C]glucose should give a lower pentose-phosphate-derived m+1 lactate fraction and lower m+2 citrate enrichment in APOE4, while [U-13C]glutamine should give higher m+4 citrate/malate enrichment; equal glucose- and glutamine-derived TCA labelling would falsify the substrate-switch step.", "Bottleneck test: hexokinase enzymatic activity and steady-state glucose-6-phosphate should be lower in APOE4 despite equal or higher 2-NBDG/glucose uptake; if uptake-normalised hexokinase activity and G6P are unchanged (e.g. because HK1 dominates), the chosen bottleneck is wrong even if the oxidative transcript program stands.", "Rescue: HK2 re-expression (or bypassing the step with cell-permeable G6P precursor/mannose-free G6P delivery) in APOE4 microglia should restore glycolytic reserve and speed NADPH/GSH recovery after a menadione or diamide challenge; failure to restore either readout while HK2 protein is confirmed to rise would weaken the causal chain.", "Demand test beyond the mock state: on acute LPS or ATP challenge, APOE4 microglia should mount a smaller and slower ECAR/lactate burst than APOE3 while showing an equal or larger fall in OCR reserve; an equal or larger glycolytic burst in APOE4 would contradict the inflexibility claim.", "Capacity-versus-transcript test: despite higher nuclear ETC transcripts, assembled complex I/III/IV activity and maximal FCCP-stimulated respiration per mitochondrial mass should be no more than modestly increased (and possibly reduced) in APOE4, consistent with the lower mtDNA-encoded transcripts; a large proportional increase in assembled complex activity would argue that the state is expanded oxidative capacity rather than constrained substrate use."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mechanism_steps": ["APOE4 microglia carry lower transcript abundance of the inducible hexokinases HK2 (effect -3.67, 3.6th percentile of the list) and HK3 and of PFKP, while glucose-transporter transcripts SLC2A1/SLC2A3 are above the list median; we infer that glucose uptake is not the limiting step but that the phosphorylation step generating glucose-6-phosphate becomes rate-limiting (inferred activity/flux, not measured).", "Reduced glucose-6-phosphate supply, together with lower PGD and TALDO1 transcripts, is inferred to shrink flux through the oxidative and non-oxidative pentose-phosphate branch and hence NADPH/ribose-5-phosphate regeneration capacity; no NADPH, G6P or ribose pool was measured here.", "To sustain acetyl-CoA and ATP with less glycolytic pyruvate, the mitochondrial pyruvate-import and pyruvate-dehydrogenase-supporting machinery is transcriptionally raised (MPC2 +7.98, DLD +5.54, PDP1 +3.00), i.e. whatever pyruvate is made is preferentially routed to full oxidation rather than to lactate or to biosynthesis.", "TCA-cycle and nuclear-encoded electron-transport transcripts rise coherently above the global shift (OGDH, MDH1, ACO2, IDH3G, NDUFA8, COX7A2, ATP5MC3; set mean rank 0.71, Mann-Whitney p = 2e-4), which we interpret as increased demand for, and attempted expansion of, oxidative capacity.", "Carbon for that oxidation is drawn from non-glucose substrates: glutamine/glutamate uptake and deamination/transamination transcripts (SLC1A5, SLC38A2, GLS, GLUD1, GOT1) and lipid/ketone catabolic transcripts (OXCT1, ACAT2, HADHA, ETFA) are elevated, alongside an SREBP-lipogenic and lysosomal program (SREBF1, SCD) that would supply and recycle lipid substrate in the astrocyte co-culture.", "mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts move oppositely (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80), so the nuclear oxidative program is predicted to be only partly realised as assembled respiratory complexes; the net inferred phenotype is a narrow, substrate-dependent oxidative state with little glycolytic or pentose-phosphate reserve to buffer an acute demand or oxidant challenge."], "title": "Hexokinase-limited glucose commitment with compensatory anaplerotic mitochondrial oxidation in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11937377690802348, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.25566915675171564, "cosine_similarity": -0.12009613748197372, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_074", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6586731391585761, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.11937377690802348, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.25566915675171564, "cosine_similarity": -0.12009613748197372, "direction_accuracy": 0.19902912621359223, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6586731391585761, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.72922725, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 488}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_057", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript differences in this selected DE list track enzyme protein amount and, at least ordinally, catalytic capacity; no enzyme activity, protein level, flux or lipid species was measured in the supplied data.", "The unspecified logarithm base of the RNA effect column is consistent across all rows, so only ranks and signs relative to the list-wide background (mean +1.39, 77% positive) are interpreted, not absolute fold changes.", "The RNA rows are pre-filtered differential-expression results (all |effect|\u003e1 and adjusted p\u003c0.05), so set-level enrichment is judged against the list background rather than against an unbiased transcriptome; absence of a gene (e.g. FASN, ACACA, ELOVL5/6, LPCAT3, MBOAT7, CPT1A, ABCA1, PLIN2, LIPA) means untested, not unchanged.", "ACSL4 down and SCD up are assumed to shift the acyl-CoA pool composition available to the Lands cycle and to de novo glycerolipid synthesis; this compositional inference is not measured.", "Protein-spot observations carry multiple candidate gene assignments and contain no unambiguous lipid-metabolic enzyme, so they are not used as evidence for or against the lipid steps.", "Astrocyte co-culture supplies exogenous lipid; the microglial and astrocytic contributions cannot be separated in the supplied summaries.", "Genotype-linked differences observed at a single timepoint (Day 30) are assumed not to be a developmental-stage artefact of differentiation timing."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia transcriptionally amplify lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism (sphingolipid/glycosidase/cathepsin arm) together with scavenger-receptor lipid uptake, while the re-esterification step that returns liberated fatty acids to glycerolipids is remodeled toward monounsaturated acyl-CoA: SCD and the AGPAT2/GPAT4/DGAT1/LPCAT1/MBOAT acylation machinery are elevated whereas the PUFA-preferring ligase ACSL4 and GPAT3 fall against a strongly upward global background. We propose that acyl-CoA selection at reacylation, not hydrolysis capacity, is the rate-limiting/compositional bottleneck, so turned-over membrane lipid is rebuilt as MUFA-enriched phospholipid and neutral lipid rather than re-forming PUFA-containing phospholipid, yielding a stiffer, peroxidation-resistant, storage-biased membrane state in APOE4.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566) in mock-treated isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should produce a genotype-selective effect - a larger drop in MUFA-containing PC/PE and TAG species and a larger increase in lysosomal free-fatty-acid/undigested-lipid load (LAMP1+ BODIPY area) in APOE4 than APOE3. If SCD inhibition changes lipid composition and lysosomal load equally in both genotypes, the MUFA-reacylation bottleneck is not the APOE4-differentiating node and the mechanism is weakened.", "Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a higher MUFA(16:1/18:1)/PUFA(20:4,22:6) ratio in PC and PE and a higher TAG:phospholipid ratio in APOE4. Equal or lower MUFA:PUFA ratio in APOE4 phospholipids would directly falsify Step 5.", "Restoring ACSL4 (cDNA re-expression) in APOE4 microglia should increase 20:4 incorporation into phospholipid (measured by D8-arachidonate pulse) and increase sensitivity to the GPX4 inhibitor RSL3 relative to APOE4 controls. No change in PUFA-phospholipid labelling would weaken the claim that ACSL4 loss constrains acyl-CoA selection.", "Sequence test: blocking upstream lysosomal hydrolysis (bafilomycin A1, or conduritol-B-epoxide against GBA) should lower SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 transcripts and reduce neutral-lipid re-esterification in APOE4 if catabolism drives the anabolic arm. If SREBF1/SCD/AGPAT2 remain elevated after lysosomal blockade, Step 3 is wrong and SREBP activation is instead upstream or parallel, not downstream of turnover.", "Isotope tracing (U-13C-palmitate pulse-chase, or 13C-glucose) should show a greater fraction of TAG and PC acyl chains in APOE4 derived from recycled/pre-existing lipid than from de novo synthesis, with faster label turnover through the phospholipid pool. Equal recycling fractions with only de novo differences would favour a pure SREBP-lipogenesis explanation over the turnover-coupled remodeling proposed here.", "Counter-prediction that would weaken the whole model: if APOE4 microglia show increased complete fatty-acid oxidation (Seahorse etomoxir-sensitive OCR, or 14C-palmitate to CO2) rather than increased esterification, the elevated gene:HADHA, gene:ACOX1 and nuclear OXPHOS transcripts would be the dominant fate of liberated fatty acid and the storage/remodeling bottleneck would not hold."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels of lipoprotein/lipid uptake and lysosomal delivery components (gene:SCARB1, gene:CD36, gene:APOE, gene:TREM2, gene:ABCA7, gene:RAB7A), which we infer increases substrate delivery of membrane-derived and extracellular lipid to the endolysosome; uptake flux itself was not measured.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred activity): the CLEAR/lysosomal hydrolase module is coordinately higher (gene:TFEB, gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:GLA, gene:GAA, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK, gene:ATP6V1H, gene:LAMP1, gene:NPC2), which we infer raises hydrolysis of sphingolipid and glycerophospholipid headgroups and liberates free fatty acids and sphingoid bases inside lysosomes; no lipid, enzyme-activity or lysosomal pH measurement is supplied.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred causal direction): the liberated lipid load is inferred to engage a lipogenic/esterification transcriptional response (gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:ACSS2, gene:MGLL), providing acyl-CoA and glycerolipid-synthesis capacity for re-esterification rather than efflux.", "Step 4 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred composition): acyl-CoA selection at the reacylation node is skewed toward monounsaturates, because gene:SCD (89th percentile of this DE list) and the acylation enzymes gene:AGPAT2 (97th), gene:LPCAT1, gene:MBOAT2, gene:MBOAT1, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1, gene:CHPT1, gene:PCYT2 are up while the PUFA/arachidonate-preferring ligase gene:ACSL4 (11th percentile), gene:ACSL5 and gene:GPAT3 are down against a background in which 77% of listed genes are positive.", "Step 5 (inferred consequence): consequently re-formed phosphatidylcholine/phosphatidylethanolamine and triacylglycerol pools are predicted to be MUFA-enriched and PUFA-poor, with more carbon diverted into neutral-lipid storage; membrane and lipid-droplet composition were not measured here.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): MUFA-biased, ACSL4-low membranes are predicted to resist lipid peroxidation, consistent with the elevated antioxidant transcripts gene:GPX4, gene:PRDX2, gene:PRDX3, gene:PRDX5, gene:FTH1, and to sustain the inflammatory tone seen as gene:CXCL8, gene:CXCL16, gene:CCL2, gene:IL18, gene:NLRP3 rather than to trigger ferroptotic loss."], "title": "MUFA-biased reacylation is the bottleneck coupling elevated lysosomal membrane-lipid catabolism to glycerolipid re-esterification in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3969002695417789, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1736816473158343, "cosine_similarity": -0.12044426407385754, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_057", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8121812297734627, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.3969002695417789, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1736816473158343, "cosine_similarity": -0.12044426407385754, "direction_accuracy": 0.2313915857605178, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8121812297734627, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.17248875, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 489}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_037", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome; 100% of rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and adjusted p \u003c 0.05, and the list is globally shifted upward (median +1.46, 77% positive). We therefore treat within-list rank/percentile, not raw magnitude, as the evidence, and assume that rank is comparable across the selected genes.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effect column is unspecified and is preserved as reported; no conversion between the RNA scale and the log2 protein-spot scale is assumed.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme capacity. No enzyme activity, acyl-CoA, phospholipid, ceramide, triacylglycerol or free fatty-acid pool was measured in this dataset; all flux, membrane composition, localisation and directionality statements are inferences.", "Protein spots are not uniquely identified proteins: each spot lists several candidate genes (e.g. protein_spot:044/045 list ANXA1 together with TALDO1, ACTB and others; protein_spot:067 lists CTSB and HEXB together with PSMA3 and ACTG2). They are used only as weak, ambiguous corroboration and can equally be explained by the non-lipid candidates.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 vs APOE3 under mock treatment at day 30, in microglia co-cultured with astrocytes; astrocyte-derived lipid supply is unmeasured and could drive part of the microglial signature.", "Correlation only: nothing in these data establishes that the APOE4 allele causes the lipid-enzyme transcript pattern, nor the ordering of the steps."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-microglia (vs isogenic APOE3) display a coherent transcriptional state combining elevated lysosomal membrane-lipid hydrolase transcripts with elevated glycerolipid acylation and SREBF1/SCD lipogenic transcripts, while the polyunsaturated-fatty-acid-preferring acyl-CoA synthetase ACSL4 (and ACSL5) rank near the bottom of the shifted distribution. We hypothesise that the rate-limiting step is PUFA-acyl-CoA supply for Lands-cycle reacylation: catabolised membrane fatty acids are re-esterified predominantly with SCD-derived monounsaturated chains by AGPAT2/GPAT4/LPCAT1/MBOAT1-2/CHPT1/TAZ and shunted into DGAT1-dependent neutral lipid, so APOE4 membranes and stored glycerolipids are rebuilt with monounsaturated rather than polyunsaturated acyl chains. Only transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances were measured; all flux, acyl-chain composition, localisation and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["PRIMARY DISCRIMINATOR: Untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show a shift of PC and PE species toward monounsaturated chains (e.g. 32:1/34:1/36:1) with reduced polyunsaturated species (38:4/38:6/40:6) and increased triacylglycerol, with the PUFA/MUFA ratio in phospholipids reduced by a clearly measurable margin. If phospholipid PUFA content is unchanged or higher in APOE4, the acyl-remodelling bottleneck is falsified even though the transcript pattern stands.", "PERTURBATION 1 (SCD inhibition): Pharmacological SCD1 inhibition should produce a genotype x drug interaction, normalising the PC/PE MUFA fraction and reducing neutral-lipid/droplet load selectively in APOE4. Equal effects in APOE3 and APOE4, or no change in the APOE4 acyl profile, would weaken the mechanism.", "PERTURBATION 2 (relieving the bottleneck): Supplying arachidonate/docosahexaenoate, or restoring ACSL4 expression, in APOE4 microglia should re-populate PUFA-containing PC/PE, lower SREBF1 and SCD transcripts (STEP 6 loop), and increase sensitivity to GPX4 inhibition. Failure of PUFA supplementation to enter phospholipids would instead indicate that reacylation, not acyl-CoA supply, is limiting and would refute the ACSL4-centred bottleneck.", "PERTURBATION 3 (supply arm): Blocking lysosomal hydrolysis (e.g. GBA inhibition or v-ATPase blockade) or DGAT1 inhibition should reduce APOE4 triacylglycerol/droplet accumulation and blunt the acyl re-esterification signal, and pulse-chase with labelled membrane lipid should show faster label transit from phospholipid into triacylglycerol in APOE4. If labelled membrane lipid turnover rates are identical between genotypes, STEP 1-2 flux is not increased and the model collapses to a purely biosynthetic change.", "SPECIFICITY / COUNTER-MODEL TEST: If the APOE4 phenotype is driven instead by the equally coherent lysosomal-hydrolase or nuclear-OXPHOS transcript modules alone, then SCD or DGAT1 inhibition will not change lysosomal proteolytic capacity or mitochondrial respiration, whereas rescue of lysosomal function will normalise the lipid-enzyme transcripts. Observing lipid normalisation only after lysosomal rescue would demote acyl remodelling to a downstream consequence.", "NEGATIVE CONTROL: Proteomic or activity confirmation should show ACSL4 protein/activity reduced and SCD protein increased in APOE4. Unchanged ACSL4 protein despite the transcript decrease would remove the proposed bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mechanism_steps": ["STEP 1 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcript levels for lysosomal glyco-/sphingo-/phospholipid and protein hydrolases (gene:GBA, gene:SMPD1, gene:HEXA, gene:HEXB, gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) and the lysosomal-biogenesis factor gene:TFEB, which we interpret as increased lysosomal catabolic capacity for internalised and autophagic membrane lipid. The rate of lipid delivery and hydrolysis (flux) was not measured.", "STEP 2 (inferred flux): Increased hydrolysis liberates free fatty acids and sphingoid/ceramide backbones inside the endolysosome; these must be re-exported and re-activated to acyl-CoA before they can re-enter glycerolipid synthesis. Free fatty-acid and acyl-CoA pools were not measured.", "STEP 3 (BOTTLENECK; measured abundance -\u003e inferred activity): The acyl-CoA activation step is biased against polyunsaturates. gene:ACSL4 (-2.14, 11th percentile of the shifted RNA distribution) and gene:ACSL5 (-3.11, 5th percentile) are among the lowest-ranked genes, whereas gene:SCD (+4.17, 89th pct), its regulator gene:SREBF1 (+4.67, 92nd pct) and the cytosolic acetyl-CoA source gene:ACSS2 (+2.93, 77th pct) rank high. We infer a monounsaturated-enriched, PUFA-depleted acyl-CoA pool; enzyme activity and acyl-CoA speciation were not measured.", "STEP 4 (measured abundance -\u003e inferred flux): Glycerolipid acylation and headgroup machinery is transcriptionally raised (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29 / 97th pct, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:TAZ +3.26, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:GPAT4, gene:DGAT1). With the acyl-CoA pool of STEP 3, de novo synthesis and Lands-cycle reacylation regenerate PC/PE (and, via TAZ, cardiolipin) with monounsaturated rather than polyunsaturated chains, and gene:DGAT1 plus gene:MGLL (+4.00, 88th pct) route surplus acyl flux through a triacylglycerol/lipid-droplet cycle.", "STEP 5 (inferred consequence): Net acyl-chain remodelling toward 16:1/18:1-containing glycerophospholipids and neutral lipid changes bilayer packing and curvature and lowers the esterified PUFA reservoir available for release and oxygenation. No lipid species, membrane order, or droplet measurement is present in this dataset.", "STEP 6 (inferred feed-forward loop): Because polyunsaturated fatty acids normally suppress SREBP-1 processing and SCD expression, a persistently PUFA-poor lipid pool would keep gene:SREBF1/gene:SCD induced, stabilising the MUFA-biased recycling state rather than restoring the APOE3 acyl profile. This loop is a prediction, not an observation.", "STEP 7 (peripheral, weak): Increased gene:SCARB1 (+8.22, 99th pct) and the ambiguous membrane-associated protein spots protein_spot:044/protein_spot:045 (candidate genes include ANXA1, whose RNA is +4.15) are consistent with, but do not establish, higher membrane/lipid trafficking load feeding STEP 1."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a MUFA-biased membrane-lipid recycling cycle: high lysosomal lipid catabolism plus SREBF1/SCD-driven re-esterification with a PUFA-CoA supply bottleneck (ACSL4-low)"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30235756747775355, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0747481694587505, "cosine_similarity": -0.12305017395996805, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mean_absolute_error": 0.9021100323624596, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.30235756747775355, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0747481694587505, "cosine_similarity": -0.12305017395996805, "direction_accuracy": 0.2588996763754045, "mean_absolute_error": 0.9021100323624596, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84829475, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 490}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_037", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Transcript differences in this selected differential-expression list track enzyme protein and catalytic capacity; no enzyme activity, acyl-CoA, lysophospholipid, phospholipid, cardiolipin or triacylglycerol pool was measured in the supplied data, so all flux and composition statements are inferred.", "The unspecified-base RNA logarithm is monotone in fold change, so only ranks and signs of effects are used; the strong global positive shift (77% of 2212 rows positive, median +1.46) is treated as a normalisation/selection artefact, and pathway claims rest on rank position within the list rather than absolute direction.", "The RNA rows are pre-filtered differential results (all adjusted p \u003c 0.05, all |effect| \u003e 1), so absent genes (FASN, ACACA, LPIN1, PLIN2, CPT1A, ELOVLs, FADS2, PPARG, NR1H3) are non-informative rather than unchanged.", "Protein spots carry a median of five candidate genes each and are keratin/actin dominated; they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration and never as evidence for a specific protein.", "Astrocytes in the co-culture supply lipids and may themselves differ, so part of the microglial lipid-handling signal could be a response to an altered extracellular lipid environment rather than a cell-autonomous APOE4 program.", "Curated gene sets were assembled after inspecting effect sizes, so their permutation p-values are optimistic; the unbiased gene-family scan of glycerolipid enzymes was not significant against the already-differential background."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic iPSC-microglia, APOE4 cells transcriptionally configure a futile membrane-lipid turnover cycle: lysosomal/phospho- and sphingolipid hydrolase transcripts (GBA, SMPD1, HEXA, GAA, CTSB, CTSD, CTSK, MGLL) and an SREBF1-linked acylation module (SCD, AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2, GPAT4, CHPT1, DGAT1, TAZ) are jointly high while PUFA-preferring long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases (ACSL4, ACSL5) and GPAT3 are low. We hypothesise that the SCD-dependent supply of monounsaturated acyl-CoA is the bottleneck that determines the fate of acyl chains liberated by this elevated turnover, biasing reacylation of lysophospholipids and triacylglycerol esterification toward MUFA-rich, PUFA-poor glycerolipids. The measurements are transcript and ambiguous protein-spot abundances only; flux, enzyme activity, lipid composition and causal direction are inferred, not observed.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD inhibition (e.g. A939572/CAY10566, 24-48 h) or SCD knockdown in mock-treated APOE4 microglia should produce a genotype-selective effect - a larger fractional drop in 16:1/18:1-containing PC, PE and TAG species, a larger rise in lysoPC/PC ratio and saturated-species load, and larger loss of BODIPY-positive lipid droplets in APOE4 than in isogenic APOE3. If SCD inhibition affects APOE3 and APOE4 equally, the proposed MUFA-CoA bottleneck is wrong.", "Lipidomics without perturbation: untreated APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show an increased MUFA:PUFA acyl ratio in PC/PE and increased TAG mass. Finding no shift, or a PUFA-enriched APOE4 membrane, would weaken the mechanism even if the transcript pattern replicates.", "Flux, not pool: pulse-chase with a labelled phospholipid or NBD-PC, or D2O/13C-acetate labelling, should show faster label transit from PC to lysoPC and back into PC/TAG in APOE4 (higher turnover at similar steady-state mass). Equal turnover rates with equal pools would falsify the futile-cycle claim and favour a static compositional difference.", "Epistasis between the two arms: inhibiting the lysosomal arm (bafilomycin A1, or GBA/SMPD1 inhibition) should reduce the APOE4 excess of MUFA-rich re-esterified species if the arms are coupled as proposed. If lysosomal blockade leaves the acylation-derived lipid signature unchanged, the hydrolysis-to-reacylation coupling in Steps 1-3 is wrong and the acylation module is an independent SREBF1 effect.", "LPCAT1 or AGPAT2 knockdown in APOE4 microglia should raise lysophospholipid levels and impair phagocytic membrane expansion more than in APOE3; unchanged lysophospholipid handling would weaken Step 3.", "Protein-level check: targeted immunoblot or targeted MS should confirm higher SCD, AGPAT2 and LPCAT1 protein in APOE4; transcript-only changes with unchanged protein would weaken the whole mechanism because the supplied protein spots cannot identify these enzymes."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured abundance): APOE4 microglia show higher transcript levels for lysosomal and neutral-lipid hydrolases that degrade membrane lipids - GBA (gene:GBA), SMPD1 (gene:SMPD1), HEXA (gene:HEXA), GAA (gene:GAA), CTSB/CTSD/CTSK (gene:CTSB, gene:CTSD, gene:CTSK) - together with v-ATPase subunits (gene:ATP6V1H, gene:ATP6V1A, gene:ATP6V0C) and TFEB (gene:TFEB). Inferred, not measured: increased lysosomal hydrolytic flux releasing fatty acids, sphingoid bases and lysophospholipids.", "Step 2 (inferred flux constraint, primary bottleneck): the liberated and de-novo acyl pool must be re-activated and re-esterified. ACSL4 and ACSL5 transcripts are low (gene:ACSL4, gene:ACSL5, both in the bottom decile of this differential list) while SCD is high (gene:SCD) under an elevated SREBF1 program (gene:SREBF1, gene:INSIG1, gene:DHCR24, gene:LDLR). We propose that SCD-derived 16:1/18:1-CoA, rather than ACSL4-derived polyunsaturated acyl-CoA, becomes the dominant acyl donor - the rate-limiting routing node of the cycle.", "Step 3 (measured abundance, inferred activity): the glycerolipid acylation machinery is coordinately high - AGPAT2 (gene:AGPAT2), GPAT4 (gene:GPAT4), LPCAT1 (gene:LPCAT1), MBOAT1/MBOAT2 (gene:MBOAT1, gene:MBOAT2), CHPT1 (gene:CHPT1), TAZ (gene:TAZ) - predicting increased Lands-cycle reacylation capacity for lysophosphatidylcholine/lysophosphatidylethanolamine and increased de-novo phosphatidic-acid to diacylglycerol flux.", "Step 4 (inferred composition change): coupling steps 2 and 3 predicts remodelled bilayers enriched in monounsaturated and depleted of arachidonoyl/docosahexaenoyl species, with the ether/PC arms (CHPT1, MBOAT1/2) and cardiolipin remodelling (TAZ) drawing on the same MUFA-CoA pool.", "Step 5 (inferred storage sink): DGAT1 (gene:DGAT1) and MGLL (gene:MGLL) are high while GPAT3 (gene:GPAT3) is low, predicting a fast triacylglycerol esterification/hydrolysis cycle that buffers surplus acyl chains as lipid droplets rather than allowing free-fatty-acid or lysolipid accumulation; MGLL-driven re-release keeps flux, not net storage, elevated.", "Step 6 (functional consequence, inferred): MUFA-rich, PUFA-poor lysosomal and plasma membranes change membrane order and lysolipid clearance, which we propose sustains the APOE4 lysosomal-degradative phenotype (Step 1) as a self-reinforcing loop; the loop, not any single enzyme, is the candidate APOE4-versus-APOE3 differentiator under mock conditions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia run a high-turnover membrane lipid cycle in which SCD-supplied monounsaturated acyl-CoA is the rate-limiting routing node for Lands-cycle reacylation and neutral-lipid storage"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4245744563010006, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1379100153659499, "cosine_similarity": -0.17727084022269765, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_037", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7885566343042071, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.4245744563010006, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.1379100153659499, "cosine_similarity": -0.17727084022269765, "direction_accuracy": 0.25080906148867316, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7885566343042071, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4708715, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 491}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_067", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; all directional claims are therefore made as percentiles within this biased row set (median row = +1.46 in the unspecified reported log base), not as absolute up/down calls.", "The logarithm base of the RNA effects is unspecified and some magnitudes exceed +15, so only the rank/percentile of an effect is treated as interpretable, never the fold change.", "Transcript abundance for SCD, ACSL4, LPCAT1, MBOAT1/2 and AGPAT2 is assumed to track enzyme protein and, at least monotonically, enzymatic capacity; no protein or activity measurement for any of these enzymes exists in the supplied data.", "Lands-cycle flux requires a phospholipase A2 deacylation arm that is not represented in these rows (PLA2G4A, PLA2G6 and PLA2G15 are absent; PLA2G7 sits at percentile 0.32), so increased remodeling flux is inferred from reacylation-side capacity alone.", "No lipid, fatty-acid or membrane-order measurement of any kind is present in the supplied files; the MUFA:PUFA composition claim is entirely a prediction, not an observation.", "Protein spots carry 2-6 candidate genes each and are dominated by keratin and actin candidates, so they are used only as weak, non-identifying corroboration of altered lysosomal protease proteoform distribution and never as evidence for a named lipid enzyme.", "APOE4 and APOE3 lines are assumed truly isogenic and equally differentiated, so that the differences are not clone or maturation artefacts; replicate number is stated as not supplied in the workbook."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia differ from APOE3 principally at the acyl-CoA selection step of glycerophospholipid remodeling: an SREBF1/ACSS2/SCD-associated monounsaturated fatty-acid supply arm and the reacylation machinery (AGPAT2, LPCAT1, MBOAT1, MBOAT2, CHPT1) are transcriptionally elevated above the strong global positive shift of this dataset, while the polyunsaturated acyl-CoA arm (ACSL4, ACSL5) and the PUFA-consuming lipoxygenase ALOX15 are among the most reduced rows. We hypothesise that this transcriptional configuration raises the MUFA:PUFA ratio of newly made and re-acylated membrane phospholipids in APOE4 microglia, and that MUFA-CoA availability plus LPCAT/MBOAT reacylation capacity, rather than bulk lipid synthesis or degradation, is the rate-limiting node. Causality is not established by these data; membrane lipid composition itself was not measured here.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: pharmacological SCD1 inhibition (e.g. A939572 or CAY10566) applied to mock-treated APOE4 and APOE3 microglia should lower the phospholipid MUFA:PUFA ratio and rescue the APOE4-specific lysosomal lipid and phagocytic phenotype with a significantly larger effect in APOE4 than in APOE3 (genotype x drug interaction). If SCD inhibition changes the two genotypes equally, or fails to alter PC/PE acyl composition in APOE4, the proposed bottleneck is wrong.", "Shotgun lipidomics of APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia should show increased 16:1- and 18:1-containing PC and PE species and decreased 20:4- and 22:6-containing PC and PE species, i.e. a raised MUFA:PUFA ratio in the diacyl phospholipid pool. Finding no difference, or a PUFA increase, would falsify the core claim.", "Stable-isotope pulse (13C- or D-labelled oleate and arachidonate, or D9-lysoPC) should show faster oleate incorporation into PC and slower arachidonate incorporation into PC/PE in APOE4 than APOE3. Equal or slower oleate incorporation in APOE4 would weaken Steps 2-4.", "Knockdown of LPCAT1 or MBOAT2 in APOE4 microglia should reduce reacylation of exogenous lysoPC into PC and normalize the MUFA:PUFA ratio; if reacylation flux is unchanged after knockdown, the reacylation step is not rate-limiting.", "Re-expression of ACSL4 in APOE4 microglia should restore PUFA-phospholipid content and increase sensitivity to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3); APOE4 cells at baseline should be relatively resistant to RSL3 compared with APOE3. Equal RSL3 sensitivity across genotypes would weaken Step 2.", "Discrimination against the competing 'primary mitochondrial/lysosomal biogenesis' explanation: SCD inhibition should shift membrane composition and the APOE4 phenotype without substantially reversing the OXPHOS transcript module, whereas TFEB knockdown should collapse the lysosomal hydrolase module while leaving the SREBF1/SCD/LPCAT1 module intact. If the acyl-remodeling transcripts are fully TFEB-dependent, they are a downstream readout rather than a bottleneck and this hypothesis should be demoted.", "Immunoblot or targeted proteomics must confirm that SCD and LPCAT1/AGPAT2 protein are higher and ACSL4 protein lower in APOE4; absence of the ACSL4 protein decrease would remove the only measured brake in the mechanism and weaken it substantially."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): APOE4 microglia show elevated transcripts for the lipogenic/desaturation arm - SREBF1 (percentile 0.92 of all measured rows), SCD (0.89) and ACSS2 (0.77) - consistent with, but not proof of, increased SREBP-1-directed cytosolic acetyl-CoA use and stearoyl-CoA desaturation.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred flux): the polyunsaturated/long-chain acyl-CoA activating enzymes ACSL4 (percentile 0.11) and ACSL5 (0.05) and the arachidonate-directed enzyme ALOX15 (0.04) are among the strongly negative rows, which we interpret as reduced PUFA-CoA generation and reduced PUFA consumption by oxygenases; the acyl-CoA pool is therefore inferred to shift toward 16:1/18:1 species.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): the reacylation and headgroup-completion enzymes AGPAT2 (0.97), MBOAT2 (0.81), LPCAT1 (0.79), CHPT1 (0.77) and MBOAT1 (0.73) are coordinately elevated above the dataset median, giving increased Lands-cycle and CDP-choline-branch capacity that must draw on the acyl-CoA pool defined in Steps 1-2.", "Step 4 (bottleneck, inferred): because reacylation capacity is up while PUFA-CoA supply is down, the composition of the phospholipid product - not its total amount - becomes the constrained variable; APOE4 phospholipids are predicted to be MUFA-enriched and PUFA-depleted relative to APOE3.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred demand): a coordinated rise in lysosomal membrane-lipid hydrolases (GAA 1.00, GBA 0.98, HEXA 0.96, SMPD1 0.95, CTSB 0.95, CTSD, with TFEB 0.69; permutation p = 0.003 versus the dataset background) indicates increased catabolic processing of internalized membrane lipid, which supplies the lysophospholipid and sphingoid substrates that the Step-3 enzymes reacylate, closing a turnover loop.", "Step 6 (inferred consequence): a MUFA-shifted, PUFA-poor bilayer has higher acyl-chain order and lower oxidizability; together with DGAT1 (0.57) and MGLL (0.88) elevation, excess fatty acid is predicted to be routed to neutral-lipid storage and turnover rather than into PUFA-phospholipid, giving the APOE4-specific lipid-droplet-and-lysosome phenotype without a proportional change in APOE transcript itself (APOE percentile 0.38, i.e. below the dataset median)."], "title": "APOE4 microglia bias phospholipid reacylation toward SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl chains while losing ACSL4-dependent polyunsaturated acyl-CoA supply"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27069563933094565, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05599841862804143, "cosine_similarity": -0.1874010510022573, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_067", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8436828478964401, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27069563933094565, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.05599841862804143, "cosine_similarity": -0.1874010510022573, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8436828478964401, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.307204, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 492}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_021", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list (1706 up-entries versus 506 down-entries in the same workbook rows), so the apparent global positive shift is treated as a list-construction/normalisation feature; all enrichment claims are made relative to this internal list background, not to an unbiased transcriptome.", "The logarithm base of the reported RNA fold changes is unspecified and is preserved as reported; only signs and relative ranks are used, and the absolute magnitudes (up to |15|) are not interpreted as literal fold changes.", "Steady-state transcript differences are assumed to track enzyme and transporter abundance for these metabolic genes; no enzyme activity, metabolite pool, ATP level, NADPH level, oxygen consumption, membrane potential, mtDNA copy number or lactate output was measured here.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes (frequently keratin/actin/ANXA1 co-candidates) and cannot identify a specific enzyme; no protein spot is used as evidence for or against any single enzyme in this hypothesis.", "The comparison is isogenic APOE4 versus APOE3 in astrocyte co-culture at day 30 with no replicate count supplied; differences could reflect altered microglial state composition rather than uniform per-cell rewiring, and astrocyte-derived signals may contribute.", "Direction of causality (APOE4 genotype -\u003e metabolic rewiring) is assumed for framing but is not established by these association data."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia differ from APOE3 mainly by a coordinated transcriptional shift of catabolic capacity away from the committed, inducible cytosolic glucose steps (HK2, HK3, PFKP) and the oxidative pentose-phosphate branch (PGD, TALDO1) toward mitochondrial pyruvate/citrate/malate transport, TCA and amino-acid anaplerosis (MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, MDH1, GOT1, OGDH, ACO2, DLD, GLUD1, BCAT2) and toward every measured nuclear-encoded electron-transport-chain subunit; the proposed primary bottleneck is glycolytic commitment at hexokinase/phosphofructokinase, so APOE4 microglia should have little glycolytic reserve and should be disproportionately dependent on mitochondrial carbon oxidation for ATP and on non-PPP routes for NADPH. All statements about flux, ATP and NADPH are inferred, not measured; causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Extracellular flux (Seahorse) on mock APOE4 versus isogenic APOE3 microglia: APOE4 should show a higher basal OCR/ECAR ratio and a markedly smaller glycolytic reserve, i.e. a blunted ECAR and lactate rise after oligomycin or after LPS/phagocytic challenge. Equal or larger glycolytic induction in APOE4, with no OCR difference, would weaken the mechanism.", "Stable-isotope tracing: [U-13C6]glucose should give lower m+2 citrate/malate fractional enrichment in APOE4, while [U-13C5]glutamine (and [13C]leucine) should give higher TCA enrichment; unchanged or higher glucose-derived TCA labelling in APOE4 would falsify the fuel-switch step.", "Discriminating perturbation: APOE4 microglia should be selectively more vulnerable to blockade of mitochondrial carbon entry or oxidation (MPC inhibition with UK5099, glutaminase inhibition with CB-839, or low-dose oligomycin) - larger drops in ATP, phagocytic uptake and viability than APOE3 - while 2-deoxyglucose or hexokinase inhibition should injure APOE3 more; conversely, cell-permeable methyl-pyruvate or dimethyl-alpha-ketoglutarate should rescue APOE4-specific deficits whereas extra glucose should not. If APOE4 is instead the genotype protected by UK5099/CB-839 and harmed by 2-DG, the bottleneck assignment is wrong.", "Redox test of the PPP arm: APOE4 should show lower NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG and greater sensitivity to the G6PD inhibitor 6-aminonicotinamide or to BSO, with a weaker PMA-induced oxidative burst. Normal NADPH/NADP+ and normal 6-AN sensitivity would weaken the PPP-restriction step.", "Mitonuclear step: immunoblot/BN-PAGE should show increased nuclear-encoded subunit protein (e.g. NDUFS7/NDUFB8, UQCRC2, ATP5F1B) but disproportionately low mtDNA-encoded subunits (MT-CO1, MT-ATP6) and no proportional rise in complex I/IV in-gel activity per unit mitochondrial mass in APOE4. Finding proportional increases in both nuclear- and mtDNA-encoded subunits with matched activity would refute the mismatch step (while leaving the fuel-switch step intact).", "Overall weakening result: if APOE4 microglia show unchanged or higher HK2/PFKP protein, unimpaired glycolytic induction, and no increase in TCA/ETC protein or respiration relative to APOE3, the hypothesis as a whole should be rejected."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: in APOE4 versus APOE3 microglia (mock) the transcripts for the committed/inducible glycolytic entry steps HK2, HK3 and PFKP and for the oxidative pentose-phosphate enzymes PGD and TALDO1 are lower, whereas glucose uptake and mid-pathway transcripts (SLC2A1, GPI, ENO1) are higher; inferred: glucose can still be taken up but its commitment to glycolysis and to G6P shunting is capacity-limited.", "Measured: transcripts for mitochondrial pyruvate and organic-acid carriers and TCA/redox-shuttle enzymes (MPC2, SLC25A1, SLC25A11, MDH1, GOT1, DLD, OGDH, ACO2) are among the largest increases in the whole differential-expression list; inferred: expanded capacity for pyruvate import, citrate export and malate-aspartate shuttling of cytosolic NADH.", "Measured: anaplerotic amino-acid catabolism transcripts (GLUD1, GLS, BCAT2, ABAT) are all higher; inferred: glutamate/glutamine and branched-chain amino acids, rather than glucose, supply a larger share of TCA carbon in APOE4.", "Measured: all 38 detected nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts (e.g. NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8, UQCRC2, COX7A2, ATP5ME, ATP5MC3, SDHB) are higher, together with mitochondrial import components (TOMM22, TIMM8B) and the adenine-nucleotide carrier SLC25A5; inferred: a coordinated attempt to expand oxidative-phosphorylation capacity per cell.", "Measured: four of six detected mtDNA-encoded subunit transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2) are lower while nuclear subunits rise; inferred: mitonuclear subunit stoichiometry is mismatched, so the transcriptional expansion may not translate proportionally into assembled, functional complexes.", "Bottleneck (inferred): with glycolytic commitment down and OXPHOS output constrained by core-subunit supply, APOE4 microglia have narrow metabolic reserve; the higher NNT, PRDX3 and GPX4 transcripts are interpreted as compensation for reduced PPP-derived NADPH rather than as evidence of increased NADPH.", "Predicted functional consequence: on acute demand (inflammatory or phagocytic challenge) APOE4 microglia should fail to execute the normal glycolytic switch, lean further on mitochondrial oxidation, and show earlier ATP/redox strain in energy-expensive functions."], "title": "APOE4 microglia lose inducible glycolytic/pentose-phosphate capacity and become obligately dependent on mitochondrial oxidative-anaplerotic catabolism"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06701620943026991, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0759221667625066, "cosine_similarity": -0.1914425587811826, "direction_accuracy": 0.025889967637540454, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_021", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6912038834951456, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.06701620943026991, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.0759221667625066, "cosine_similarity": -0.1914425587811826, "direction_accuracy": 0.025889967637540454, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6912038834951456, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.17660325, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 493}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_024", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified in the workbook and is preserved as reported; only the sign and the rank/percentile of each effect relative to the whole list are used, not the absolute fold change.", "The RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, not an unbiased transcriptome; because 77% of listed genes are positive (median +1.46), every directional statement here is made relative to that global centre by permutation against the listed genes, and absolute up/down calls would be misleading.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to be a partial proxy for enzyme abundance, and enzyme abundance a weaker proxy for activity and flux; no metabolite, isotope-tracing, oxygen-consumption or extracellular-acidification measurement was supplied, so all flux, localisation and ATP-ceiling statements are inferred, not observed.", "The 92 protein spots have multiple candidate genes each and are not treated as identified proteins; no protein spot is used as evidence for or against a specific enzyme in this mechanism.", "mtDNA-encoded transcript fractions in 10X Flex data are assumed to reflect biology rather than differential cell-quality filtering or ambient RNA; this is not verifiable from the supplied file and mtDNA copy number was not measured.", "The culture is a microglia-astrocyte co-culture, so genotype-associated differences in astrocyte-derived lactate/ketone supply, or in cell-type mixing/ambient RNA, could contribute to the observed gene shifts (unverified background knowledge).", "Causality is not established: APOE4 genotype is the only manipulated variable, and no intermediate step of the proposed chain has been perturbed here."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-microglia, the committed entry step of glucose into glycolysis (hexokinase, with PFKP and the pentose-phosphate arm) is transcriptionally down-shifted relative to the strongly positive global RNA shift, while glucose transporters, mitochondrial substrate carriers, TCA/anaplerotic enzymes and alternative-substrate catabolic enzymes are up-shifted; we hypothesise that glucose-6-phosphate production, not glucose uptake, is the primary bottleneck, redirecting carbon to mitochondrial oxidation of glutamate/BCAA/ketone-derived substrates, and that this compensation is capped because mtDNA-encoded core subunits (notably MT-ATP6) are not co-elevated with their nuclear-encoded partners. This is a hypothesis about inferred flux; only transcript and protein-spot abundances were measured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating prediction (uptake vs phosphorylation): APOE4 microglia will show equal or greater glucose uptake but reduced trapping of phosphorylated tracer - i.e. equal/higher initial 2-NBDG or 18F-FDG influx with lower steady-state FDG-6-phosphate retention and lower glucose-driven ECAR and glycolytic capacity - versus isogenic APOE3. If APOE4 shows equal or higher FDG-6-P retention and equal/higher glycolytic ECAR, the primary bottleneck claim is wrong and the mechanism is falsified.", "Substrate-swap prediction: replacing glucose with galactose, or withdrawing glucose while supplying glutamine plus beta-hydroxybutyrate, will impair viability/phagocytic index less in APOE4 than in APOE3; conversely, withdrawing glutamine and ketones will impair APOE4 more. If APOE4 is equally or more sensitive to glucose withdrawal than APOE3, the substrate-shift step is weakened.", "13C tracing prediction: with U-13C-glucose, APOE4 will show lower fractional m+2 enrichment of citrate/malate; with 13C-glutamine or 13C-beta-hydroxybutyrate, APOE4 will show higher fractional enrichment of TCA intermediates. Equal glucose-derived m+2 enrichment in both genotypes would weaken steps 2-4.", "Rescue prediction: hexokinase-2 re-expression in APOE4 microglia will restore ECAR, raise the NADPH/NADP+ and GSH/GSSG ratios, and reduce the relative dependence on OXCT1/GLUD1-supplied carbon; failure of HK2 re-expression to restore any of these while glucose uptake is unchanged would falsify hexokinase as the primary bottleneck and point instead to a downstream (PFK/GAPDH) or purely mitochondrial lesion.", "Mito-nuclear prediction: normalised to mtDNA copy number, APOE4 will show a selective deficit in MT-ATP6/MT-CYB transcript and in assembled complex V (BN-PAGE, oligomycin-sensitive respiration) despite equal or higher nuclear-encoded ATP5F1B/COX7A2 protein. If MT-ATP6 transcript and complex V assembly are proportional to nuclear subunit levels after mtDNA-copy normalisation, step 5 is falsified while steps 1-4 could still stand.", "Demand-challenge prediction: under an acute ATP-demanding stimulus (bead/myelin phagocytosis or LPS), APOE4 microglia will show a smaller rise in ATP/ADP ratio and smaller spare respiratory capacity than APOE3; equal spare capacity and equal ATP/ADP dynamics would weaken step 6."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred capacity): glucose import capacity is not the limitation - SLC2A1 (gene:SLC2A1, +2.37) and SLC2A3 (gene:SLC2A3, +3.73) sit at/above the global centre of the selected DE list (median +1.46).", "Step 2 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred flux): the committed phosphorylation/priming steps are down-shifted - HK2 (gene:HK2, -3.67, 3.6th percentile of all listed genes), HK3 (gene:HK3, -1.12), PFKP (gene:PFKP, -3.08). We infer reduced glucose-6-phosphate generation and reduced glycolytic and pentose-phosphate flux, supported by TALDO1 (gene:TALDO1, -2.32) and PGD (gene:PGD, -1.30). Hexokinase activity, G6P pool and flux were not measured.", "Step 3 (measured RNA, inferred substrate routing): mitochondrial carriers and matrix dehydrogenases are strongly up-shifted - MPC2 (gene:MPC2, +7.98), SLC25A1 (+4.47), SLC25A11 (+4.50), SLC25A5 (+5.56), OGDH (+8.56), MDH1 (+8.72), GOT1 (+6.43), ACO2 (+3.54), IDH3G (+3.94), DLD (+5.54); the pre-specified 9-gene TCA set is up relative to the global shift (permutation p = 0.003). We infer increased mitochondrial carbon import and TCA/malate-aspartate cycling.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred substrate choice): enzymes for non-glucose carbon are up-shifted - OXCT1 (+4.72, ketone-body utilisation), GLUD1 (+3.24), BCAT2 (+6.43), GLS (+1.44), ABAT (+1.54), HADHA (+2.86), ETFA (+3.50) (set permutation p = 0.048). We infer that glutamate/BCAA/ketone/fatty-acid carbon substitutes for glucose carbon in the TCA cycle.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred stoichiometric cap): nuclear-encoded OXPHOS subunits and mitochondrial import/translation genes are up (TOMM22 +4.63, TIMM44 +2.46, TUFM +6.46, ATP5MC3 +4.70, COX7A2 +3.36, UQCRC2 +4.02) while mtDNA-encoded core transcripts are down-shifted (MT-ATP6 -3.35, MT-CYB -2.32, MT-ND4 -1.80, MT-CO2 -1.33; mtDNA set permutation p = 0.040; nuclear-vs-mtDNA contrast permutation p = 0.012). We infer a mito-nuclear stoichiometric mismatch that limits assembly/turnover of complexes III-V, so the increased substrate oxidation is not fully converted into ATP output.", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): APOE4 microglia therefore have low glycolytic reserve and low NADPH-generating pentose-phosphate capacity, are substrate-shifted toward mitochondrial oxidation of non-glucose carbon, and carry a reduced ceiling on oxidative ATP production - a state predicted to fail selectively under acute high-ATP demand (phagocytosis, inflammatory activation) or when non-glucose substrates are withdrawn."], "title": "Hexokinase-level restriction of glucose commitment forces APOE4 microglia onto mitochondrial non-glucose carbon, against an unmatched mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS core"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1605250526160322, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.09061702817904298, "cosine_similarity": -0.19671088387710492, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_024", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6895210355987056, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.1605250526160322, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.09061702817904298, "cosine_similarity": -0.19671088387710492, "direction_accuracy": 0.13106796116504854, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6895210355987056, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.975523, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 494}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_014", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Unverified background knowledge: hexokinases phosphorylate glucose; glutaminase and glutamate dehydrogenase can route glutamine carbon through glutamate to alpha-ketoglutarate; the listed TCA enzymes and pyruvate-entry regulators have their conventional biochemical roles. These functional annotations were not supplied or externally verified.", "RNA reductions translate into lower functional HK2/HK3 capacity. HK1, whose RNA row is absent from these selected differential-expression results, does not compensate sufficiently. Absence is not evidence of absent expression or unchanged abundance.", "Higher glutamine-related RNA yields sufficient functional capacity for net oxidative glutamine use in the available culture medium. Substrate availability, uptake, metabolite pools, isotope labeling, and flux were not measured.", "Mitochondria retain enough function for substrate supply to be the primary constraint. Mixed mitochondrial-encoded respiratory RNA changes leave primary mitochondrial dysfunction as an alternative explanation.", "The selected RNA results reflect comparable microglial states and are not chiefly explained by cell-state composition, astrocyte influence, normalization, or batch effects. The upward bias of the selected rows is not a measured global increase in total cellular RNA. Replicate counts and baseline expression are unavailable; the RNA logarithm base remains unspecified.", "All protein spots have multiple candidate genes, so their abundance changes cannot establish HK2, HK3, GLS, or GLUD1 protein changes. No protein activity, subcellular localization, phosphorylation state, or causal direction is established by these data."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 microglia are hypothesized to have lower functional hexokinase capacity, principally through reduced HK2, which limits glucose phosphorylation and increases the fractional contribution of glutamine to mitochondrial carbon metabolism relative to APOE3. The primary bottleneck is glucose phosphorylation. Higher oxidative-metabolism RNA is compatible with compensation but does not establish increased respiration; the proposed causal chain remains unproven.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In matched APOE3 and APOE4 cultures, prospectively quantify HK isoenzyme protein abundance and hexokinase activity, then perform separate time courses with uniformly carbon-13-labeled glucose and glutamine, measuring precursor enrichment, uptake, secretion, and TCA labeling. After accounting for pool dilution and viable cell number, APOE4 should have lower glucose-phosphorylation capacity, lower glucose-derived TCA carbon contribution, and higher fractional glutamine contribution. Equal or higher effective glucose phosphorylation together with no shift toward glutamine would weaken the mechanism; no absolute increase in respiration or glutamine flux is required.", "Titrate catalytically active HK2 restoration in APOE4 to the APOE3 hexokinase-activity range, using an expression- and localization-matched catalytically inactive HK2 control. Only active HK2 should increase glucose-derived TCA labeling and reduce fractional glutamine use and glutaminase dependence. Failure despite verified restoration of glucose phosphorylation, or equal rescue by inactive HK2, would weaken the proposed catalytic bottleneck.", "With matched target engagement and early measurements before loss of viability, partial GLS inhibition or GLS knockdown should cause a larger decrease in oxidative TCA carbon flux and ATP-linked respiration in APOE4 than APOE3; active HK2 restoration should reduce this difference. Measure flux with isotope and uptake/secretion constraints rather than inferring it from labeling fractions alone. No genotype difference, or dependence that persists after verified HK2 rescue, would weaken the predicted glutamine dependence.", "As a downstream bypass test, provide pyruvate and verify its cellular uptake and mitochondrial carbon entry. Relative to extra glucose, pyruvate should better restore glucose-limited oxidative output and reduce the effect of GLS inhibition in APOE4. Persistent impairment despite verified pyruvate entry and adequate substrate delivery, especially together with failure of active HK2 rescue, would favor an intrinsic mitochondrial defect over the proposed upstream bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: HK2 and HK3 RNA decrease in APOE4 (gene:HK2, gene:HK3). Inferred: these changes lower functional hexokinase capacity, with HK2 providing the principal loss; neither HK2 protein abundance nor enzyme activity was measured specifically.", "Measured: SLC2A1 and SLC2A3 RNA increase (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3). Inferred: transporter induction does not overcome the phosphorylation bottleneck, reducing glucose trapping and glucose-derived glycolytic pyruvate supply despite this transcriptional response. Transport rates, glucose-6-phosphate abundance, and glycolytic flux were not measured.", "Measured: SLC1A5, SLC38A2, GLS, and GLUD1 RNA increase (gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1). Inferred: the corresponding transport and conversion capacity permits glutamine to supply glutamate and then alpha-ketoglutarate, bypassing glucose phosphorylation. Net transport and reaction directions are assumptions.", "Measured: ACO2, OGDH, and SDHB RNA increase (gene:ACO2, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB). Inferred: retained mitochondrial oxidative capacity can process glutamine-derived carbon through the TCA cycle. These RNA changes could be compensatory and do not demonstrate enzyme activity, respiratory-complex assembly, or increased absolute TCA flux.", "Inferred consequence: glutamine supplies a larger fraction of mitochondrial carbon, making APOE4 cells more dependent on glutaminase when glucose phosphorylation is limiting. Increased MPC2, PDP1, and DLD RNA (gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1, gene:DLD) makes an upstream substrate-supply constraint plausible while leaving open the possibility of greater glucose oxidation; active HK2 restoration is predicted to relieve the proposed dependence."], "title": "A glucose-phosphorylation bottleneck shifts mitochondrial carbon use toward glutamine in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.14585821071911523, "cosine_similarity": -0.20568604569109009, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_014", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6517702265372168, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.14585821071911523, "cosine_similarity": -0.20568604569109009, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6517702265372168, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8012935, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 14}, {"id": "opus-original-b03-hyp_100", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 3, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The unspecified-base 'reported log fold change' values are monotonic in true fold change and comparable across rows; set-level claims are made only relative to the global distribution of the same rows, because 77% of RNA rows are positive (median +1.46) and an overall normalization/composition shift cannot be excluded.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, so the antioxidant/OXPHOS sets are treated as relative enrichments among measured rows, not as whole-transcriptome pathway activation; unmeasured genes (SOD1/2, CAT RNA, GSR, TXNRD1, G6PD RNA, NFE2L2, PEX genes) are absent, not unchanged.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, imperfectly, the abundance of the corresponding proteins; no enzyme activity, ROS level, NADPH/NADP+ ratio, GSH/GSSG ratio, peroxiredoxin oxidation state, mtDNA copy number or complex assembly state was measured, so all flux, localization and redox-state statements are inferred.", "2D protein spots are multi-candidate; spot effects are used only as weak, non-identifying support (e.g. G6PD-containing spots as a ceiling argument) and never as proof that a named protein changed.", "Astrocyte co-culture and 10X Flex ambient signal are assumed not to generate the specific mitonuclear directional contrast (nuclear ETC up, mtDNA-encoded down) reported here.", "The APOE3/APOE4 lines are isogenic as stated, so genotype rather than background drives the contrast; replicate number was not supplied."], "claim": "Under mock conditions, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia up-regulate nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain and mitochondrial-carrier transcripts without a matching increase in mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts; the resulting inferred rise in matrix peroxide flux is met by a coordinated thiol-peroxidase/glutathione transcriptional program (PRDX2/3/5, GPX4, MGST2, GSS, TXNDC17, TXNL1, NNT, SLC25A11) whose regeneration capacity is limited because cytosolic oxidative-pentose-phosphate/NADPH-supplying components do not scale (PGD and TALDO1 transcripts fall well below the global upward shift; G6PD/PGD-containing protein spots are at or below the spot-level median). Peroxisomal beta-oxidation/biogenesis genes show no coherent shift, so the redox bottleneck is placed at mitochondrial peroxiredoxin/GPX4 re-reduction rather than at peroxisomal metabolism. Causality is not established by these data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating perturbation: acute G6PD inhibition (G6PDi-1) or NNT knockdown in the isogenic pair should produce a genotype x treatment interaction - APOE4 microglia should shift their PRDX3 dimer/monomer redox blot ratio toward the oxidized form, lose matrix NADPH/NADP+, and lose viability at doses tolerated by APOE3. Absence of an interaction (equal sensitivity) would weaken the reductant-limitation bottleneck.", "Compartment discrimination: matrix-targeted HyPer7/roGFP2-Orp1 should report a higher steady-state oxidation in APOE4 than APOE3, while a peroxisome-targeted (SKL) reporter should not differ, or differ less. If the peroxisomal reporter shows the larger genotype difference, the mitochondrial placement of the bottleneck is wrong and a peroxisomal mechanism should be preferred.", "Stoichiometry test: qPCR/RNAscope of mtDNA-encoded transcripts normalized to mtDNA copy number plus blue-native PAGE should show, in APOE4, reduced fully assembled complex I/IV relative to the increased nuclear-encoded subunit protein. Proportional scaling of mtDNA-encoded transcripts and normal assembly would falsify step 2.", "Rescue test: mitochondria-targeted antioxidant (MitoQ or mito-TEMPO) or NAD(P)H-restoring treatment should normalize the APOE4-high PRDX3/PRDX5/GPX4/MGST2 transcript signature and reduce lipid-peroxidation (C11-BODIPY, 4-HNE adducts) toward APOE3 levels; a general (non-targeted) antioxidant such as extracellular catalase should be less effective. No normalization by mitochondrially targeted antioxidants would weaken the mechanism.", "Negative prediction: peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux (C22:0/C24:0 or pristanic acid handling) and PEX-dependent import should not differ substantially between genotypes; a clear peroxisomal beta-oxidation defect in APOE4 would falsify the explicit rejection of the peroxisomal arm.", "Load test: a phagocytic/oxidative challenge (myelin debris or synaptosome load) should cause disproportionate GSH depletion and lipid-droplet accumulation in APOE4; equal handling would weaken the claim that reductant supply is already near capacity in the mock state."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: nuclear-encoded ETC subunit transcripts are coherently higher in APOE4 (38/38 rows positive, set mean +2.81 vs global median +1.46, Mann-Whitney p=7.8e-05), together with mitochondrial solute carriers (SLC25A1/5/11/37/46). Inferred: increased demand for respiratory complex assembly and matrix substrate/ion flux.", "Measured: mtDNA-encoded transcripts (MT-ATP6, MT-CO2, MT-CYB, MT-ND4) are lower in APOE4 against a strongly upward global background (set mean -0.82, centred -2.28). Inferred (not measured): stoichiometric mismatch between nuclear and mitochondrial-genome-encoded core subunits, partially assembled complexes I/III/IV and increased univalent electron leak.", "Inferred flux: elevated matrix superoxide/H2O2 production; no ROS, GSH/GSSG or NADPH pool was measured in this dataset.", "Measured response: coordinated increase of matrix- and membrane-directed thiol peroxidases and glutathione machinery (PRDX3 +3.49, PRDX5 +1.96, PRDX2 +4.41, GPX4 +2.79, MGST2 +3.32, GSS +2.11, TXNDC17 +7.10, TXNL1 +4.33) plus NADPH/GSH-supporting transport and transhydrogenase (NNT +2.88, SLC25A11 +4.50); set mean +3.69, p=6.0e-04 versus all other rows. Inferred: a compensatory antioxidant program rather than raised catalytic turnover per se.", "Measured constraint: cytosolic oxidative-PPP/reductant-supply rows move opposite to the global shift (PGD -1.30, TALDO1 -2.32; set centred -2.21), and the four protein spots whose candidate list includes G6PD (spots 018, 020, 021, 022) are at or below the spot median (+0.485). Inferred: NADPH regeneration does not scale with peroxiredoxin/GPX4 demand, making thiol re-reduction the rate-limiting step and producing a chronically more oxidized peroxiredoxin/glutathione pool.", "Measured iron/lipid arm: SLC25A37 (mitoferrin-1) +4.48 and FTH1 +2.53 raise matrix iron-handling capacity, while PUFA-peroxidation substrate genes fall (ACSL4 -2.14, ALOX15 -3.63) and monounsaturated/storage lipogenesis rises (SCD +4.17, SREBF1 +4.67). Inferred: cells defend membranes by lipid remodelling and storage instead of expanding reductant supply.", "Predicted consequence (inferred, not shown here): under this reductant-limited state APOE4 microglia are hypersensitive to any further NADPH drain (G6PD/NNT inhibition, phagocytic oxidative burst, lipid load), with lysosomal/degradative up-regulation (CTSB +5.52, TFEB +2.38) as a downstream consequence of oxidized-lipid and damaged-organelle turnover."], "title": "Mitonuclear ETC-subunit mismatch makes NADPH-dependent thiol-peroxidase recycling, not peroxisomal catabolism, the rate-limiting redox node in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13131853930509912, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0348532779965595, "cosine_similarity": -0.21047788647444093, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_100", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7542006472491909, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.13131853930509912, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.0348532779965595, "cosine_similarity": -0.21047788647444093, "direction_accuracy": 0.156957928802589, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7542006472491909, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.84134175, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 495}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_018", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Background biochemical annotations are unverified here: B4GALT5/B4GALT6 synthesize lactosylceramide from glucosylceramide, ST3GAL5 uses lactosylceramide to synthesize GM3, and lysosomal GBA and nonlysosomal GBA2 hydrolyze glucosylceramide. No literature or database retrieval was performed.", "The B4GALT5 RNA decrease produces a functionally limiting enzyme decrease, while the GBA/GBA2 RNA increases produce greater relevant catalytic capacity. No protein spot has any of these three genes or ST3GAL5 among its candidates.", "B4GALT6 does not compensate, and glucosylceramide supply, UDP-galactose supply and Golgi substrate access are sufficient for B4GALT5 capacity to control this branch. B4GALT6, UGCG and SLC35A2 are absent from selected RNA rows; absence does not establish unchanged or absent expression.", "Substrate exchange allows the synthetic and hydrolytic branches to compete. Distinct cellular compartments preclude inferring this competition merely from transcript directions; transport, lysosomal pH and enzyme maturation remain unmeasured.", "The selected differential-expression results reflect a reproducible microglial difference rather than cell-state composition, normalization, maturation or astrocyte-mediated effects alone. Biological replicate counts and cell-level expression are not supplied; an isogenic comparison does not establish the proposed causal chain."], "claim": "In mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia, reduced active Golgi B4GALT5 is proposed to limit glucosylceramide-to-lactosylceramide conversion, restricting precursor supply for GM3 synthesis despite higher ST3GAL5 RNA. Increased GBA/GBA2-dependent hydrolytic capacity is proposed to favor conversion of accessible glucosylceramide back to ceramide relative to downstream glycosphingolipid synthesis. B4GALT5 capacity is the single primary bottleneck; these flux and activity differences remain unmeasured, and causality is not established.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Prospective baseline test: in matched mock-treated APOE3 and APOE4 co-cultures, quantify active Golgi B4GALT5 and use a stable-isotope precursor pulse-chase with time-resolved glucosylceramide, lactosylceramide and GM3 measurements to estimate precursor-to-product conversion. Control precursor enrichment, uptake, cell number, viability and maturation; endpoint ratios alone are not flux. APOE4 should show reduced B4GALT5 capacity and slower glucosylceramide-to-lactosylceramide conversion with reduced downstream GM3 labeling. Normal or increased capacity and conversion would weaken the primary bottleneck.", "Discriminating rescue: restore correctly localized, catalytically active B4GALT5 in APOE4 microglia to the APOE3 level, with matched inactive-enzyme and vector controls. Active B4GALT5 should increase lactosylceramide and GM3 synthesis from the labeled precursor; inactive B4GALT5 should not. ST3GAL5 elevation alone should not fully normalize both conversion steps while B4GALT5 remains limiting. Failure of active B4GALT5 rescue after confirming activity and substrate access, or full normalization by ST3GAL5 alone, would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Reciprocal perturbation: reduce B4GALT5 activity in APOE3 microglia to the measured APOE4 level while keeping astrocyte conditions fixed. This should reproduce slower lactosylceramide synthesis and lower downstream GM3 labeling. Lack of a phenotype despite verified enzyme reduction would argue against B4GALT5 controlling this branch in these cells.", "Hydrolytic-branch test: prospectively trace isotopically labeled glucosylceramide to ceramide with verified comparable delivery to the relevant compartments, and separately inhibit GBA and GBA2 with confirmed target engagement. APOE4 should have greater inhibitor-sensitive glucosylceramide hydrolysis relative to lactosylceramide synthesis. No increase in this hydrolytic branch would weaken the proposed diversion component, even if the B4GALT5 synthesis bottleneck remains supported."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mechanism_steps": ["The APOE4-associated state includes lower B4GALT5 RNA (gene:B4GALT5, reported log fold change -1.880; base unspecified). The proposed causal link is a reduction in active, correctly localized Golgi B4GALT5; enzyme abundance, activity and localization were not measured.", "Reduced B4GALT5 catalytic capacity is hypothesized to restrict glucosylceramide conversion to lactosylceramide. This requires sufficient glucosylceramide and sugar-donor supply and insufficient compensation by B4GALT6; none of those conditions is established by the supplied measurements.", "Higher GBA and GBA2 RNA (gene:GBA, +6.713; gene:GBA2, +2.632, on the reported RNA log scale) is hypothesized to increase hydrolysis of accessible glucosylceramide to ceramide in their respective compartments, competing with the restricted synthetic branch. Access through lipid transfer and endolysosomal routing is assumed, not observed; no particular vesicular defect is required.", "Restricted lactosylceramide supply is then hypothesized to limit ST3GAL5-dependent GM3 production despite higher ST3GAL5 RNA (gene:ST3GAL5, +2.168). The predicted outcome is reduced precursor conversion into lactosylceramide and GM3 relative to glucosylceramide hydrolysis, without asserting any measured change in total lipid pools."], "title": "A B4GALT5 bottleneck restricts lactosylceramide and GM3 synthesis in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.021351032012701693, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.25467741256531146, "cosine_similarity": -0.2114270505650412, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_018", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6603365695792881, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.021351032012701693, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.25467741256531146, "cosine_similarity": -0.2114270505650412, "direction_accuracy": 0.02912621359223301, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6603365695792881, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.4272885, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 15}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_004", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All biochemical pathway assignments and enzyme-function relationships are unverified background knowledge; no literature, database, or external feature list was consulted. Only RNA expression and ambiguous protein-spot abundance were supplied.", "The HK2/HK3 RNA reductions lower effective glucose-phosphorylation activity enough to control carbon supply. HK1, HKDC1, and GCK are absent from the selected RNA rows, which does not establish their absence or unchanged expression; their activity could compensate.", "Transporter and glutamine-pathway RNA increases can translate into sufficient functional capacity, but protein abundance, catalytic activity, substrate availability, localization, and flux were not measured. The response may instead be compensatory transcription without increased substrate use.", "Hexokinase is the dominant limiting step. Lower PFKP and PFKFB2 RNA could instead impose a downstream glycolytic limitation, although higher PFKM RNA makes that interpretation uncertain (gene:PFKP, gene:PFKFB2, gene:PFKM).", "Enough mitochondrial function remains for glutamine-supported respiration. Lower mitochondrial-encoded RNA could indicate a competing primary respiratory defect, while higher pyruvate-utilization RNA could support preserved glucose oxidation (gene:MT-ND4, gene:MT-CYB, gene:MT-CO2, gene:MT-ATP6, gene:MPC2, gene:PDP1).", "Astrocyte-derived lactate or other substrates do not fully bypass the glucose-phosphorylation deficit. Higher SLC16A1 and OXCT1 RNA supports considering alternative substrate routes, without measuring transport direction or ketone use (gene:SLC16A1, gene:OXCT1).", "The contrast reflects a microglial metabolic state rather than only cell-state composition, maturation, astrocyte carryover, or RNA normalization. Biological replicate counts, raw counts, baseline expression, and cell proportions are unavailable. The selected RNA rows are broadly upshifted and cannot establish transcriptome-wide induction or pathway enrichment.", "Protein spots cannot validate individual enzyme changes: the two spots containing HK3 among their candidates have nominal p values of 0.110 and 0.520 (protein_spot:001, protein_spot:024). RNA effects retain their unspecified logarithm base; only protein-spot effects are explicitly log2."], "claim": "Under mock treatment, APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia are hypothesized to have insufficient HK2/HK3-supported glucose-phosphorylation capacity relative to APOE3. This single primary bottleneck reduces glucose-derived glycolytic carbon supply and increases reliance on glutamine-derived alpha-ketoglutarate to sustain TCA turnover and residual mitochondrial respiration. The abundance measurements motivate this mechanism but do not establish its causal direction or metabolic fluxes.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In prospective matched mock cultures, microglia-resolved, time-resolved [U-13C6]glucose and separate [U-13C5]glutamine tracing should reveal lower glucose-phosphorylation throughput and a larger glutamine contribution to TCA carbon in APOE4. Estimate contributions using precursor enrichment, pool sizes, and substrate uptake/secretion rather than interpreting a single labeling fraction as flux. Resolve or control astrocyte substrate exchange. Unchanged effective hexokinase activity and glucose throughput, or no increase in glutamine contribution, would weaken the proposed chain.", "Discriminating rescue: titrate microglia-specific active HK2 to restore APOE3-range total hexokinase activity in APOE4 and compare with catalytically inactive HK2 matched for abundance and localization. Active HK2 should increase glucose-derived pyruvate and TCA labeling and reduce the glutamine contribution; inactive HK2 should not. Failure to restore glucose carbon use despite verified enzymatic rescue would weaken the claim that hexokinase is the primary bottleneck; equal rescue by inactive HK2 would favor a noncatalytic mechanism.", "With verified GLS target engagement, acute GLS suppression should cause a larger fractional loss of mitochondrial oxygen consumption in APOE4 than APOE3 before viability changes. Restoring active HK2 should reduce this genotype difference; matched inactive HK2 should not. Equivalent GLS sensitivity across genotypes, or persistent excess sensitivity after restored glucose throughput, would weaken the proposed hexokinase-to-glutamine dependency.", "Test the bypass alternative with separate [U-13C3]lactate tracing under controlled astrocyte exchange. If the carbon replacing glucose in APOE4 is predominantly lactate-derived and GLS suppression has little effect, that result would weaken the glutamine-specific mechanism even if glucose phosphorylation is reduced."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured starting pattern: APOE4 has lower HK2 and HK3 RNA (gene:HK2, gene:HK3) despite higher glucose-transporter RNA (gene:SLC2A1, gene:SLC2A3). The proposed translation of this pattern into lower effective hexokinase catalytic capacity is inferred; neither glucose transport nor enzyme activity was measured.", "Primary bottleneck, inferred using unverified biochemical background: insufficient hexokinase activity limits phosphorylation of imported glucose to glucose-6-phosphate, reducing glucose-derived glycolytic pyruvate supply. This predicts altered carbon flow; it does not assert that the glucose-6-phosphate pool was measured or must be depleted.", "Proposed compensatory substrate use: higher RNA for amino-acid transport and glutamine catabolism (gene:SLC1A5, gene:SLC38A2, gene:GLS, gene:GLUD1) permits glutamine conversion through glutamate to alpha-ketoglutarate to carry a larger share of mitochondrial carbon input. The transport, enzyme reactions, and compensatory causal link are unverified background or inference, not measured activity.", "Proposed downstream routing: higher TCA-related RNA (gene:ACO2, gene:IDH3B, gene:IDH3G, gene:OGDH, gene:SDHB) is compatible with processing glutamine-derived carbon through the TCA cycle. Maintaining this route is hypothesized, without claiming increased total TCA flux, respiratory-complex assembly, mitochondrial abundance, or respiration.", "Predicted functional consequence: APOE4 microglia become more dependent than APOE3 on GLS-supported carbon input to maintain residual respiration. Restoring effective glucose phosphorylation should lessen that dependence, placing the hexokinase bottleneck upstream of the proposed substrate substitution."], "title": "Hexokinase-limited glucose use creates glutamine dependence in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.14946450628087826, "cosine_similarity": -0.24227166807177453, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_004", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6578381877022653, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.14946450628087826, "cosine_similarity": -0.24227166807177453, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6578381877022653, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.1955185000000004, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 16}, {"id": "opus-original-b02-hyp_030", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 2, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is preserved as reported; RNA effects are therefore compared only with each other and never converted or compared in magnitude with the log2 protein-spot effects.", "The supplied RNA rows are a selected differential-expression list, not an unbiased transcriptome, so absence of a gene (for example NQO1, HMOX1, TXNRD1, GCLM, ATF4, all PEX genes) means it was not selected, not that it is unchanged.", "The whole RNA list carries a large positive shift (median +1.46, 77% positive); subtracting that median is assumed to be an adequate first-order correction for compositional or normalisation bias, and pathway claims are made only on median-centred values.", "Transcript abundance is assumed to track, at least ordinally, the availability of the corresponding protein; no protein-level measurement of any respiratory-chain subunit, peroxiredoxin, NNT or catalase pool is present in these data, and matrix H2O2, NADH/NAD+, NADPH/NADP+, membrane potential, complex assembly state and respiratory flux are all inferred, never observed.", "Protein spots carry multiple candidate genes and are not uniquely identified proteins; protein_spot:017 (candidates CAT, CORO1C, ENTPD5), protein_spot:077 (candidates including PRDX2 amid keratins) and protein_spot:074 (candidates including SOD2, PRDX1) are treated as at best weak, non-identifying corroboration.", "Astrocytes are present in the co-culture, so a fraction of the transcriptional difference may be non-cell-autonomous or reflect altered cell-type mixture; replicate structure is not supplied, so the reported p-values cannot be re-assessed.", "Causal direction is assumed, not demonstrated: the data are a single mock-treatment cross-sectional contrast at one timepoint (day 30)."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, the nuclear-encoded oxidative-phosphorylation program (especially complex I), mitochondrial protein import and TCA/substrate-entry genes are selectively elevated above the strong global positive RNA shift, while the mtDNA-encoded core subunit transcripts MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4 and MT-CO2 are relatively depleted. We propose that the availability of mtDNA-encoded catalytic core subunits, not the supply of nuclear-encoded accessory subunits or of respiratory substrate, is the rate-limiting step for building functional respiratory complexes in APOE4 cells; the resulting stoichiometric mismatch is predicted to leave nuclear-encoded subunits in unassembled or partially assembled modules, to increase electron leak per unit of NADH delivered, and to raise mitochondrial-matrix peroxide load. The transcriptional response to that inferred load is matrix-restricted (PRDX3, PRDX5, NNT, GPX4, FTH1, SLC25A37) together with a peroxidation-resistant membrane configuration (SCD up, ACSL4 down), and explicitly not a canonical NRF2 antioxidant battery, not an oxidative pentose-phosphate expansion (PGD and TALDO1 are down) and not a peroxisomal program (ABCD1 down, ACOX1 at background, OXR1 strongly down, no PEX gene in the differential list). Causality is not established by these data; the mitonuclear ratio is measured only as relative transcript abundance in a selected differential-expression list and could also be produced by compositional normalisation.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating measurement of the mitonuclear ratio: quantify MT-ATP6, MT-CYB and MT-ND4 transcripts per cell by spike-in-normalised ddPCR or single-molecule FISH and normalise to mtDNA copy number and to mitochondrial mass (TOMM20 or citrate synthase). The mechanism predicts that APOE4 has fewer mtDNA-encoded core transcripts per mtDNA genome and/or reduced mtDNA copy number. If mtDNA-encoded transcripts per genome and per mitochondrion are equal between genotypes, the mitonuclear step is refuted and the apparent MT decrease is attributable to the global compositional shift.", "Assembly discriminator: blue-native PAGE or complexome profiling of isolated mitochondria should show, in APOE4, an increased ratio of free or subassembled nuclear-encoded complex I modules (NDUFA5, NDUFS7, NDUFS8 immunoreactivity in low-molecular-weight species) to fully assembled complex I. If assembled complex I scales proportionally with subunit abundance and no subassembly accumulates, the bottleneck claim fails.", "Functional discriminator: extracellular flux analysis normalised to mitochondrial mass should show in APOE4 lower maximal and spare respiratory capacity and higher proton leak despite the elevated TCA transcript program, plus hypersensitivity to sub-maximal piericidin A or rotenone. Equal or higher spare respiratory capacity per unit mitochondrial mass in APOE4 would weaken the mechanism.", "Compartment-specific redox discriminator: matrix-targeted roGFP2-Orp1 (or MitoPY1) should be more oxidised at baseline in APOE4, while cytosolic roGFP2-Orp1 and an ARE/NRF2 reporter should show little or no genotype difference. Knockdown of PRDX3 or of NNT should selectively raise matrix peroxide and reduce viability in APOE4 relative to isogenic APOE3. Equal cytosolic and matrix oxidation, or an equal PRDX3-knockdown effect in both genotypes, would refute the matrix-restricted buffering step.", "Substrate-supply test: MPC inhibition with UK5099, or forcing glutamine-only oxidation, should shrink the APOE4-minus-APOE3 matrix peroxide difference; if blocking pyruvate entry leaves the redox gap unchanged, the proposed link from increased NADH delivery to leak is wrong.", "Peroxidation-dependence test: APOE4 should be more sensitive than APOE3 to GPX4 inhibition (RSL3) and rescued by ferrostatin-1 or by mitoTEMPO, and this differential should be abolished by SCD inhibition equalising the MUFA/PUFA balance. No genotype difference in RSL3 sensitivity would weaken the lipid-remodelling step.", "Explicit rejection test for the assigned focus: catalase activity, ACOX1 activity, peroxisome number per cell and plasma-membrane C26:0-lysoPC should not differ appreciably between genotypes. If instead peroxisomal beta-oxidation flux or catalase capacity is the dominant genotype difference, this hypothesis is wrong and a peroxisomal mechanism should replace it."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured: APOE4 microglia show coordinated elevation of nuclear-encoded respiratory-chain transcripts, strongest for complex I (21 NDUF genes, mean +1.53 above the global median shift, Mann-Whitney p=1e-3; whole nuclear OXPHOS set n=37-44, p~5e-5), together with mitochondrial import/chaperone genes (TOMM22, TIMM44, HSPA9, PHB, TUFM) and TCA/anaplerotic genes (MPC2, OGDH, MDH1, GOT1, DLD, GLUD1, ACO2, IDH3G; 10/11 above the global median, p=2e-4). Control gene families (ZNF, PSM, SLC, MED) sit at or below the global median, so this is not simply the global shift.", "Measured contrast: mtDNA-encoded transcripts move in the opposite direction relative to the nuclear program (MT-ATP6, MT-CYB, MT-ND4, MT-CO2 all below the global median; nuclear-encoded versus mtDNA-encoded OXPHOS contrast p=7e-4), with MT-ND5 and MT-ND4L near the median as internal counter-evidence.", "Inferred (not measured): the mismatch between rising nuclear-encoded accessory/assembly-factor supply and falling mtDNA-encoded core supply makes core subunit availability the limiting step for assembly of complex I, complex III and the ATP synthase, so assembled holo-complex abundance rises less than subunit transcript abundance and unassembled nuclear-encoded modules accumulate.", "Inferred flux: elevated pyruvate and glutamate entry (MPC2, GOT1, GLUD1, GLS, OGDH, MDH1 transcripts) increases NADH delivery onto a complex I whose assembled capacity is constrained, raising the matrix NADH/NAD+ reduction pressure and the probability of single-electron leak to O2 at the flavin and quinone sites.", "Inferred redox consequence with measured transcriptional correlate: increased matrix superoxide/H2O2 is met by a compartment-restricted buffering program - PRDX3 (matrix peroxiredoxin), PRDX5, GPX4, the NADPH-regenerating transhydrogenase NNT, and iron handling (FTH1, SLC25A37) - rather than by cytosolic NRF2 targets, which are absent from the differential list, while OXR1, MSRB1, PGD and TALDO1 are down.", "Measured lipid correlate, inferred function: SCD up and ACSL4 down are predicted to shift membrane acyl composition toward monounsaturated species and lower the peroxidisable PUFA pool, so APOE4 cells tolerate the higher leak but become disproportionately dependent on GPX4/PRDX3/NNT capacity; the concurrent lysosomal-catabolic and lipid-uptake rise (SCARB1, GBA, HEXA, CTSB, GAA, ATP6V1A, TFEB, SREBF1) is interpreted as substrate supply into this state, not as its cause."], "title": "Mitonuclear subunit-supply imbalance makes complex I assembly the bottleneck in APOE4 microglia, buffered by a matrix peroxiredoxin/NNT program rather than by NRF2 or peroxisomes"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.146798729830521, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.046225905776747074, "cosine_similarity": -0.2487228266923392, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_030", "mean_absolute_error": 0.7708932038834951, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.146798729830521, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.046225905776747074, "cosine_similarity": -0.2487228266923392, "direction_accuracy": 0.17475728155339806, "mean_absolute_error": 0.7708932038834951, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.972167, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 496}, {"id": "opus-original-b05-hyp_077", "cohort": "opus-original", "batch": 5, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["The reported RNA log fold changes (logarithm base not specified in the workbook; treated as monotonic effect sizes only, never exponentiated) track the direction of the corresponding enzyme protein abundance and activity. No acyl-CoA synthetase, desaturase or acyltransferase protein was uniquely identified in the supplied protein-spot data, so every enzyme activity in this mechanism is inferred, not observed.", "The RNA rows are a pre-selected differential-expression list (all 2212 rows have |effect| \u003e 1 and 77.1% are positive), so directional coherence within a pathway is informative only relative to that up-biased background; no unbiased whole-transcriptome enrichment can be computed here.", "No lipid, acyl-CoA, fatty-acid or membrane-order measurement is present in the supplied files. The central claim about MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor lipid is a prediction about an unmeasured pool, not an observation.", "ACSL4 and ACSL5 are assumed to be the dominant PUFA-activating acyl-CoA synthetases in this cell state; ACSL1/ACSL3/ACSL6 were not present in the supplied rows, so redundancy cannot be excluded.", "Protein spots are multi-candidate and cannot be assigned to single gene products; they are used only as counter-evidence and consistency checks, never as identification.", "The microglia were co-cultured with astrocytes, so some transcript differences may reflect non-cell-autonomous or mixed-population effects rather than microglial genotype alone.", "Causality is assumed only as a hypothesis; the discovery data are a single genotype contrast and establish association, not direction."], "claim": "In mock-treated isogenic APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia, the transcriptional state is configured for high membrane-lipid turnover (elevated lipid-uptake receptor, lysosomal hydrolase and glycerolipid acyltransferase transcripts) while the transcripts encoding the long-chain acyl-CoA synthetases that preferentially activate polyunsaturated fatty acids (ACSL4, ACSL5) are among the most strongly decreased. We hypothesise that PUFA activation to acyl-CoA is the rate-limiting node of this cycle, so fatty acids liberated by lipolysis and lysosomal hydrolysis are re-esterified mainly with SCD-derived monounsaturated acyl chains, producing MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor phospholipids and neutral lipid. This is a proposed, not established, causal chain; no lipid species were measured in the supplied data.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["Discriminating lipidomics: untargeted lipidomics of mock APOE4 vs APOE3 microglia should show an increased ratio of monounsaturated (16:1, 18:1) to polyunsaturated (18:2, 20:4, 22:6) acyl chains in phosphatidylcholine, phosphatidylethanolamine and triacylglycerol, with the largest shift in the lysophospholipid-derived (Lands-cycle) PC pool. If the PUFA-containing phospholipid fraction is unchanged or higher in APOE4, the mechanism is falsified.", "Bottleneck test by rescue: restoring ACSL4 (inducible expression, or ACSL4 plus arachidonate supplementation) in APOE4 microglia should normalise the PUFA-phospholipid fraction and membrane order without needing to change SCD. If ACSL4 restoration leaves the MUFA/PUFA ratio unchanged, the bottleneck is misplaced and the mechanism is weakened.", "Discriminating perturbation separating this mechanism from a lysosome-primary alternative: pharmacological SCD inhibition should shrink the MUFA-rich phospholipid and triacylglycerol excess and raise free saturated fatty acid and ER-stress markers preferentially in APOE4, whereas inhibiting lysosomal hydrolysis (for example GBA or acid lipase inhibition) should lower total lipid turnover in both genotypes but should NOT normalise the APOE4 MUFA/PUFA acyl ratio. The reverse outcome (lysosomal blockade normalises the acyl ratio, SCD inhibition does not) would favour lysosomal substrate supply as the true bottleneck and falsify this hypothesis.", "Functional consequence: APOE4 microglia should be relatively resistant to ferroptosis induced by GPX4 inhibition (consistent with gene:ACSL4 down, gene:ALOX15 down, gene:GPX4 up) yet show reduced phagosomal and lysosomal membrane expansion capacity in a myelin- or synaptosome-uptake assay. Equal or greater ferroptosis sensitivity in APOE4 would weaken the acyl-chain arm of the mechanism.", "Protein-level check: quantitative targeted proteomics or immunoblot should confirm lower ACSL4 and higher SCD protein in APOE4. If ACSL4 protein is unchanged or increased despite the transcript decrease, the transcript-to-activity assumption fails and the proposed bottleneck collapses."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mechanism_steps": ["Step 1 (measured RNA, inferred flux): APOE4 microglia carry higher transcripts for lipid uptake and lysosomal lipid catabolism (gene:SCARB1 +8.22, gene:CD36 +1.38, gene:APOE +1.24, gene:TREM2 +1.28, gene:GBA +6.71, gene:HEXA +5.68, gene:SMPD1 +5.63, gene:CTSB +5.52, gene:CTSD +2.86, gene:ATP6V1H +6.88, gene:TFEB +2.38). We infer, but did not measure, an increased delivery and hydrolysis of membrane and lipoprotein lipid that raises the intracellular free fatty-acid and lysolipid load.", "Step 2 (measured RNA, inferred enzyme activity): the SREBP-1/desaturation arm is up (gene:SREBF1 +4.67, gene:SCD +4.17, gene:FADS1 +1.59, gene:ACSS2 +2.93), which we infer increases conversion of saturated acyl-CoA to monounsaturated (16:1/18:1) acyl-CoA.", "Step 3 (primary bottleneck; measured RNA, inferred capacity): gene:ACSL4 (-2.14) and gene:ACSL5 (-3.11) sit in the 11th and 5th percentile of an observation list that is 77% positive, so their decrease runs against the global upward shift. We propose that reduced ACSL4/ACSL5 protein activity limits (re)activation of polyunsaturated fatty acids to acyl-CoA, making PUFA-CoA the scarce substrate of the remodeling cycle.", "Step 4 (measured RNA, inferred flux partitioning): downstream acylation capacity is not limiting, because glycerolipid and Lands-cycle acyltransferase transcripts are raised (gene:AGPAT2 +6.29, gene:GPAT4 +1.58, gene:AGPAT4 +1.12, gene:DGAT1 +1.72, gene:LPCAT1 +3.07, gene:MBOAT2 +3.26, gene:MBOAT1 +2.65, gene:CHPT1 +2.91, gene:PCYT2 +1.05, gene:SOAT1 +1.25), with gene:GPAT3 (-2.23) the isoform exception. With a MUFA-skewed acyl-CoA pool, these steps re-esterify liberated glycerol backbones and lysophospholipids preferentially with monounsaturated chains.", "Step 5 (measured RNA, inferred lipid composition): free PUFA released by neutral and secreted lipases (gene:MGLL +4.00, gene:ABHD5 +1.04, gene:PLA2G7 +1.13) is poorly recycled once ACSL4/ACSL5 capacity falls; the parallel loss of the PUFA-oxygenating enzyme transcript (gene:ALOX15 -3.63) and the rise of the phospholipid-hydroperoxide reductase transcript (gene:GPX4 +2.79) are consistent with a cell that handles less peroxidisable esterified PUFA.", "Step 6 (inferred phenotype): the predicted MUFA-enriched, PUFA-poor membrane and neutral-lipid pool (with gene:CIDEB +1.06 and gene:DGAT1 supporting droplet-directed storage) increases membrane acyl-chain order and lowers the deformable, PUFA-containing phospholipid fraction available for lysosomal and phagosomal membrane expansion, which we propose contributes to the lysosomal-stress and inflammatory transcript signature in APOE4 (gene:CXCL8 +3.11, gene:CCL2 +2.12, gene:DDIT3 +2.79)."], "title": "An ACSL4/ACSL5-limited PUFA-acyl-CoA step diverts APOE4 microglial membrane turnover into SCD-derived monounsaturated glycerolipid"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27069563933094565, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.014948930456390367, "cosine_similarity": -0.25523165297758815, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_077", "mean_absolute_error": 0.8882653721682847, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.27069563933094565, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.014948930456390367, "cosine_similarity": -0.25523165297758815, "direction_accuracy": 0.19579288025889968, "mean_absolute_error": 0.8882653721682847, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 1.735048, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 497}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_010", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["All enzyme functions, compartment assignments, and redox feedback relationships invoked here are unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "The contrast is an isogenic APOE genotype comparison, but the measurements are selected differential RNA-expression rows and ambiguous protein-spot abundances, not genomic variants. RNA logarithm base is unspecified and is not converted to fold ratios or compared numerically with protein log2 effects.", "Lower PGD RNA corresponds to lower active cytosolic PGD and sufficiently constrains flux despite substrate availability and regulation. This is the essential untested assumption, not evidence of an observed NADPH shortage.", "Higher ME1 RNA (gene:ME1; +1.356) and NNT RNA (gene:NNT; +2.880) do not fully restore cytosolic reductive reserve. Their activities and compartmental coupling are unknown; complete compensation would undermine the claim.", "The antioxidant response is partly compensatory rather than wholly protective or a secondary consequence of altered maturation, lysosomal remodeling, ER stress, or astrocyte signaling. GPX4 induction and lower ACSL4 RNA (gene:ACSL4; -2.142) could instead reduce oxidative susceptibility.", "Protein spots cannot identify the limiting enzyme: PGD is one of five candidates in protein_spot:021 (+0.263 log2, p=0.24) and protein_spot:022 (0.000 log2, p=0.86). Neither supports a uniquely identified PGD decrease. protein_spot:017 (+0.766 log2, p=0.001) and protein_spot:077 (+1.070 log2, p=0.003) have CAT and PRDX2 among three and six candidates, respectively; their increases are only compatible context for antioxidant adaptation.", "The strong positive shift among selected RNA rows limits pathway specificity. Missing genes are absent from the supplied differential-expression list, not proven unchanged or unexpressed. Biological replicate counts, baseline expression, enzyme activities, metabolic flux, and redox measurements are unavailable.", "A primary peroxisomal defect is not required: lower ABCD1 RNA (gene:ABCD1; -1.639) contrasts with higher ACOX1 RNA (gene:ACOX1; +1.242), while most queried peroxisomal machinery is absent from the selected rows. These data establish neither peroxisomal import failure nor increased peroxisomal peroxide production."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced PGD-dependent cytosolic NADPH regeneration is hypothesized to be the primary bottleneck limiting glutathione recycling. Higher antioxidant transcripts represent an incompletely compensating response, leaving less capacity to recover from an equal oxidant load. This mechanism is proposed, not causally established; neither diminished NADPH nor oxidative damage was measured.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In independent matched isogenic differentiations under the supplied day-30 mock/co-culture conditions, APOE4 should have lower directly assayed PGD catalytic capacity and slower cytosolic NADPH and glutathione-redox recovery after a brief standardized diamide pulse and washout. Compare recovery at matched initial glutathione-sensor oxidation and control viability and cell state. A basal NADPH deficit is not required. Equal or higher PGD capacity together with indistinguishable recovery would weaken the proposed bottleneck.", "Discriminating rescue: restore active PGD in APOE4 to the measured APOE3 physiological activity range, comparing an expression-matched catalytically inactive PGD and vector control. Active PGD should preferentially normalize glutathione-redox recovery after equal initial oxidation; inactive PGD should not. This tests reductive regeneration independently of how much endogenous peroxide is produced. If verified active PGD restoration fails to improve recovery, or inactive PGD rescues equally, the proposed catalytic mechanism is weakened.", "Reciprocal perturbation: partially reduce PGD in APOE3 to the activity measured in APOE4 and test the same recovery kinetics. The reduction should reproduce the loss of redox reserve, and an interference-resistant active PGD should rescue it. Failure to phenocopy at the matched activity, particularly alongside a failed APOE4 rescue, argues against PGD as the primary bottleneck.", "To test the proposed feedback direction, restore PGD activity before the antioxidant transcriptional difference develops and follow redox recovery and the cited GSS/GPX4/peroxiredoxin RNAs over time. Improved recovery should precede attenuation of part of that transcriptional response. Persistent full induction despite sustained normalization of redox recovery would weaken the feedback step and favor a separate cell-state or stress program."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured starting point: PGD RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:PGD; reported log fold change -1.304, base unspecified). The proposed causal link is that this reduces PGD protein catalytic capacity; the supplied protein spots do not establish that link.", "Primary bottleneck, inferred: reduced PGD capacity limits cytosolic NADPH regeneration when reductive demand rises. Lower NADK RNA (gene:NADK; -1.137) is compatible with constrained NADP(H) support, but neither NADP(H) pool size nor pathway flux was measured. Alternative NADPH sources must fail to compensate fully for PGD to be limiting.", "Inferred consequence: slower cytosolic NADPH replenishment restricts glutathione-reductase-mediated recycling of oxidized glutathione, delaying restoration of reduced glutathione after oxidation. Glutathione abundance, redox state, and reductase activity are unmeasured.", "Inferred functional consequence: delayed glutathione recycling limits sustained glutathione-dependent peroxide reduction, including the GPX4 reaction, despite higher GSS and GPX4 RNA (gene:GSS; +2.111; gene:GPX4; +2.791). These RNA increases establish neither enzyme activity nor effective peroxide clearance.", "Proposed feedback: peroxide-related demand contributes to compensatory antioxidant transcription, consistent with higher PRDX2, PRDX3, and PRDX5 RNA (gene:PRDX2; +4.412; gene:PRDX3; +3.488; gene:PRDX5; +1.958). Compensation may preserve basal redox state while leaving reduced reserve. Feedback direction, compartment-specific oxidation, and a peroxisomal peroxide source are not established."], "title": "PGD-limited cytosolic redox reserve in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03773584905660377, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.004648166916808413, "cosine_similarity": -0.3150875722155095, "direction_accuracy": 0.014563106796116505, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_010", "mean_absolute_error": 0.726873786407767, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03773584905660377, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.004648166916808413, "cosine_similarity": -0.3150875722155095, "direction_accuracy": 0.014563106796116505, "mean_absolute_error": 0.726873786407767, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 3.0804245, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 17}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_020", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Enzyme functions, pathway assignments, compartmentation, and proposed regulatory feedback use unverified background knowledge; no literature or database retrieval was performed.", "RNA effects retain the supplied unspecified logarithm base. The 2,212 RNA rows are selected differential-expression results, so absent genes are unknown and the global upward skew is not evidence of whole-transcriptome activation.", "The decrease in PGD RNA translates into a decrease in active enzyme with appreciable control over cytosolic NADPH regeneration. NADP+ availability, substrate delivery, and other enzymes do not become independent dominant bottlenecks in the proposed PGD rescue experiment.", "Peroxide turnover is sufficient to expose limited recycling reserve, and ME1/NNT or other unmeasured routes do not fully compensate. Successful compensation would oppose the claim.", "Higher antioxidant RNA can be compensatory, but it could instead reflect successful protection, a different cell state, or a consequence of another stress source. Lower ACSL4 RNA (gene:ACSL4) also argues against assuming increased lipid-peroxide injury.", "All protein spots have multiple candidates. PGD-candidate spots (protein_spot:021, protein_spot:022) do not establish lower PGD protein; upward TALDO1-candidate spots, including protein_spot:045, oppose a simple transcript-to-protein interpretation if TALDO1 contributes to those spots. Protein abundance, activity, and localization remain unresolved.", "The proposed genotype-associated effect persists after matching microglial identity, viable cell numbers, maturation, and astrocyte exposure. Biological replicate information is missing, and the isogenic context does not establish the proposed causal chain."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, we hypothesize that reduced PGD-dependent cytosolic NADPH regeneration is the primary bottleneck limiting glutathione/thioredoxin recycling relative to APOE3. Increased antioxidant transcripts may represent incomplete compensation, predicting reduced peroxide-buffering reserve. This is an abundance-supported hypothesis; deficient NADPH, oxidative injury, and causality have not been demonstrated.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In a future mock-condition comparison with matched viable microglial identity and astrocyte exposure, APOE4 should have lower specifically identified PGD protein/activity and slower cytosolic NADPH and glutathione-redox recovery after a standardized sublethal peroxide pulse. Normal PGD activity together with preserved recovery would weaken the proposed primary bottleneck, even if antioxidant RNA remains elevated.", "Restore catalytically active PGD in APOE4 to the measured APOE3 activity range, with expression-matched inactive PGD, empty-vector, and active GSS-overexpression controls. Active PGD should improve cytosolic NADPH recovery and reduced/oxidized glutathione recovery more than inactive PGD or GSS alone, without requiring immediate reversal of antioxidant RNA induction. Failure after verified PGD activity restoration would weaken PGD limitation; comparable rescue by GSS alone without improved NADPH recovery would favor a different limiting step.", "Partially reduce PGD activity in APOE3 to the APOE4 activity range established in the first experiment. This should reproduce delayed redox recovery, reversible by a knockdown-resistant active PGD construct. Failure to reproduce the phenotype at matched PGD activity and viability would weaken the proposed mechanism; effects appearing only after severe depletion would not support the genotype-level claim."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured starting point: PGD RNA is lower in APOE4 (gene:PGD, -1.304 reported log fold change). We infer that this lowers functional 6-phosphogluconate dehydrogenase capacity enough to constrain oxidative pentose-phosphate-pathway NADPH regeneration. Lower NADK and TALDO1 RNA (gene:NADK, -1.137; gene:TALDO1, -2.315) provides related metabolic context; neither establishes flux, and TALDO1 does not directly generate NADPH.", "Proposed biochemical consequence: under ongoing peroxide turnover, inadequate cytosolic NADPH regeneration limits glutathione reductase and thioredoxin reductase recycling of their oxidized substrates. Their activities and the relevant reduced/oxidized molecular pools were not measured.", "Proposed compensatory response: higher GSS, GPX4, and PRDX2 RNA (gene:GSS, +2.111; gene:GPX4, +2.791; gene:PRDX2, +4.412) reflects increased antioxidant investment, but additional synthesis or peroxide-reducing enzymes cannot fully restore recycling if reductant regeneration remains limiting. The feedback direction and protein/activity changes are inferred.", "Proposed incomplete bypass: higher ME1 and NNT RNA (gene:ME1, +1.356; gene:NNT, +2.880) may increase alternative reducing capacity, but the hypothesis requires that this compensation remains insufficient in the cytosol. NNT is assigned a mitochondrial role from unverified background knowledge; localization and intercompartmental compensation were not measured.", "Predicted functional outcome: APOE4 microglia have less reserve for restoring a reduced cytosolic environment after a matched mild peroxide pulse, despite increased antioxidant transcripts. Delayed redox recovery is a prospective phenotype; neither elevated peroxide nor an altered glutathione or NADPH pool is an observed discovery result."], "title": "PGD-limited cytosolic NADPH regeneration reduces peroxide-buffering reserve in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03773584905660377, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.004648166916808413, "cosine_similarity": -0.3150875722155095, "direction_accuracy": 0.014563106796116505, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_020", "mean_absolute_error": 0.726873786407767, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.03773584905660377, "centered_cosine_similarity": 0.004648166916808413, "cosine_similarity": -0.3150875722155095, "direction_accuracy": 0.014563106796116505, "mean_absolute_error": 0.726873786407767, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.9105999999999996, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 18}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_009", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Background knowledge is unverified here: MYH9 encodes non-muscle myosin IIA, actomyosin force can contribute to phagocytic cup closure, and the named recognition, actin and trafficking components have the proposed roles. Dependence on myosin IIA may vary with cargo and receptor route.", "The MYH9 RNA decrease lowers the relevant functional motor pool enough to limit engulfment. protein_spot:010 and protein_spot:011 both decrease but have multiple candidate genes and nominal p values 0.41 and 0.32; they do not establish MYH9 protein depletion.", "Preserved binding and cup initiation are testable assumptions. Increased recognition-component RNA cannot establish preserved surface receptors or exclude a receptor-level defect.", "Compensation is incomplete. ACTG1, ARPC4, ARPC5 and MYL12A RNA increase (gene:ACTG1, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5, gene:MYL12A); many ACTB-candidate spots increase. Missing MYH10 and MYH14 RNA rows mean their changes are unknown, not that alternative myosin isoforms are absent.", "The selected differential-expression rows are not an unbiased transcriptome. Their upward skew, unspecified RNA logarithm base and absent replicate-level data prevent inference of absolute RNA content or robust population-level effect precision.", "The association is not wholly explained by microglial maturation, viability, cell-state proportions or astrocyte-mediated effects. The isogenic comparison alone does not establish a direct, cell-autonomous APOE4-to-MYH9 causal chain.", "An alternative upstream Rho-family regulatory defect could dominate: ARHGDIA RNA increases and RAC2 RNA decreases (gene:ARHGDIA, gene:RAC2), but GTPase activity is unmeasured. The MYH9 restoration experiment must discriminate a motor limitation from this alternative.", "Only RNA expression and ambiguous protein-spot abundance are observed. Phagocytosis, force, subcellular localization, enzymatic activity, molecular pools and fluxes remain unmeasured; APOE genotype labels define the comparison and are not supplied genomic-variant measurements."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, reduced MYH9-dependent non-muscle myosin IIA contractile capacity is hypothesized to be the primary bottleneck in sealing large phagocytic cups. This would reduce internalization per bound particle despite increased RNA abundance for several recognition and trafficking components. Neither this functional deficit nor its causal attribution has been established by the supplied abundance measurements.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["In independently replicated, matched day-30 cultures, measure initial binding, cup initiation and sealing of identically opsonized large particles using a pH-insensitive cargo label, extracellular quenching or differential extracellular staining, and live cup imaging. APOE4 should show longer-lived unsealed cups and fewer internalized particles per initially bound particle. Comparable sealing and internalization after controlling for binding, viable cell number and cell size, or a defect entirely explained by binding, would weaken the mechanism.", "First quantify MYH9 protein specifically, then titrate wild-type MYH9 restoration in APOE4 microglia to the APOE3 level. Restoration should improve cup sealing and internalization per bound particle without requiring increased binding. An equally expressed, localization-competent ATPase-defective MYH9 control should fail to rescue. Failure of verified functional restoration to improve closure, or equal rescue by the motor-defective control, would weaken the proposed motor bottleneck; unchanged baseline MYH9 protein and cup motor recruitment would also weaken its initiating link.", "After establishing the protein difference, selectively reduce MYH9 in APOE3 microglia to the measured APOE4 level. This should reproduce delayed sealing with relatively preserved binding; an RNA-interference-resistant wild-type rescue should reverse it. Failure to phenocopy under conditions preserving viability, or an effect explained solely by cell loss or adhesion failure, would weaken the mechanism.", "Use the same receptor-targeting coating on large and small particles, and separately assess degradation conditional on the amount already internalized. The predicted APOE4 deficit and MYH9 rescue should be more pronounced for large-particle sealing than for small-particle uptake or degradation per internalized cargo. Normal sealing with selectively impaired post-entry degradation, particularly after MYH9 restoration, would favor a downstream explanation and weaken this mechanism.", "As a competing-mechanism test, compare calibrated MYH9 restoration with partial ARHGDIA normalization while directly measuring cup-associated Rac activation. If cup initiation is defective and ARHGDIA normalization restores uptake whereas verified MYH9 restoration does not, an upstream Rho-regulatory limitation would be favored over the proposed primary contractile bottleneck."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mechanism_steps": ["The APOE4-associated state has lower MYH9 RNA abundance (gene:MYH9; reported log fold change -6.384, base unspecified). The proposed initiating link is a corresponding reduction in functional myosin IIA availability; this protein-level consequence and causal direction are inferred.", "Cargo recognition and initial cup assembly remain sufficiently competent to initiate engulfment. Increased TREM2, MERTK, SYK and ARPC1B RNA (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:SYK, gene:ARPC1B) makes this plausible but does not establish receptor surface abundance, signaling activity or actin polymerization.", "Lower functional myosin IIA availability reduces motor recruitment and contractile force at initiated cups. Lower ACTB RNA (gene:ACTB) could increase vulnerability, but neither total actin abundance nor the filamentous-actin pool is measured. Motor-dependent force generation is the single proposed primary bottleneck.", "Insufficient contractile force delays cup sealing, particularly for large particles, leaving more cargo surface-accessible after binding. Cup persistence, sealing kinetics and reduced internalization are predicted phenotypes, not supplied observations.", "Fewer sealed phagosomes reduce delivery of external particulate cargo into downstream compartments, even though DNM2 and RAB7A RNA increase (gene:DNM2, gene:RAB7A). This predicted reduction in cargo flux does not establish impaired lysosomal digestion or any change in a lipid pool."], "title": "Reduced MYH9-dependent contractility limits phagocytic cup closure in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.2631651901672481, "cosine_similarity": -0.3472661325428677, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_009", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6606699029126213, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.0, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.2631651901672481, "cosine_similarity": -0.3472661325428677, "direction_accuracy": 0.0016181229773462784, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6606699029126213, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.6345650000000003, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 19}, {"id": "astra-forecast-v3-b01-hyp_019", "cohort": "astra-forecast-v3", "batch": 1, "hypothesis": {"assumptions": ["Unverified background knowledge: MYH9 encodes nonmuscle myosin-IIA, whose motor function can contribute to phagocytic cup mechanics; the importance of this function depends on cargo, receptor and geometry. No literature or database verification was performed.", "The MYH9 RNA decrease translates into a functionally limiting protein change despite protein persistence and possible compensation by other myosin isoforms or increased light-chain expression. Neither MYH10 nor MYH14 appears in the selected RNA rows; their expression and compensation are unknown.", "Binding and early cup initiation remain sufficiently intact that closure is the principal rate-limiting step. Increased receptor and branching-component transcripts may instead accompany other defects or an overall cell-state change.", "The abundance pattern reflects relevant changes within microglia rather than being dominated by cell-state proportions, astrocyte contributions, normalization or batch effects. The isogenic design does not establish cell-autonomous causation, and biological replicate counts are not supplied.", "RNA effects retain their reported logarithmic scale with unspecified base. The selected differential-expression rows cannot establish a whole-transcriptome increase or pathway enrichment; missing genes are not known to be unchanged.", "Protein spots have multiple candidate genes and cannot identify individual protein changes. The two MYH9-candidate spots are nonsignificant and do not validate a MYH9 protein decrease. Functional molecular pools, activity, localization, uptake, organelle pH and lipid abundance are unmeasured."], "claim": "In day-30, mock-treated APOE4 versus APOE3 iPSC-derived microglia co-cultured with astrocytes, I hypothesize that reduced MYH9 expression limits functional nonmuscle myosin-IIA at phagocytic cups. This single contractile bottleneck delays cup sealing and reduces particulate-cargo internalization despite higher RNA abundance for several recognition, actin-branching and endolysosomal components. The functional deficit and causal chain remain unestablished.", "falsifiable_predictions": ["With equally opsonized particles of matched chemistry, live imaging and a pH-insensitive extracellular-quenching assay should reveal longer initiation-to-sealing times and fewer sealed phagosomes per bound particle in APOE4, with a larger deficit for large particles. Initial binding should be relatively preserved. Normal sealing kinetics, or a defect confined to binding, would weaken the proposed closure bottleneck.", "Restoring wild-type MYH9 in APOE4 to the experimentally measured APOE3 protein level should shorten cup-sealing time and increase internalization per bound particle, without requiring receptor RNA normalization. A matched-expression motor-inactive MYH9 control should fail to rescue. Verify protein abundance, cup localization, viability and cell size. Failure of functional MYH9 restoration to rescue, or equivalent rescue by the motor-inactive control, would weaken the motor-dependent mechanism.", "Partial MYH9 CRISPR interference in APOE3, calibrated to the experimentally established APOE4 protein level, should reproduce the closure defect; an interference-resistant wild-type construct should reverse it. Preserved closure despite verified depletion would weaken MYH9 limitation as the primary bottleneck.", "Following particles whose sealing has been independently confirmed, ratiometric measurements should show relatively preserved post-entry acidification compared with the entry deficit. Normal cup closure coupled to selectively defective post-entry acidification would favor a downstream explanation and weaken this mechanism. Acidification-sensitive fluorescence alone should not be used to infer internalization."], "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mechanism_steps": ["Measured association: the APOE4 condition has lower MYH9 RNA, accompanied by lower ACTB and MYO1F RNA (gene:MYH9, gene:ACTB, gene:MYO1F). These observations identify a possible vulnerability in the machinery generating and transmitting force; they do not establish its upstream cause.", "Inferred abundance-to-function link: lower MYH9 RNA reduces the supply of functional myosin-IIA available at phagocytic cups, making MYH9-dependent contractile capacity the primary bottleneck. Myosin-IIA protein abundance, cup localization and motor activity have not been measured.", "Proposed retained early steps: cargo binding and initial actin-cup formation remain sufficiently available to expose the closure bottleneck. Higher receptor and Arp2/3-subunit RNAs are compatible with this ordering, but do not demonstrate receptor surface abundance or actin nucleation activity (gene:TREM2, gene:MERTK, gene:FCGR1A, gene:ARPC1B, gene:ARPC4, gene:ARPC5).", "Inferred mechanical consequence: inadequate myosin-IIA motor force slows constriction and sealing of initiated cups, especially around mechanically demanding particles. Open cups and reduced sealing efficiency are predictions, not supplied observations.", "Inferred flux consequence: fewer bound particles become sealed intracellular phagosomes, reducing particulate-cargo delivery to lysosomes. Higher DNM2, RAB7A, TFEB and ATP6V1A RNA cannot by itself establish, or guarantee rescue of, this entry flux (gene:DNM2, gene:RAB7A, gene:TFEB, gene:ATP6V1A)."], "title": "A MYH9-dependent contractile bottleneck delays phagocytic cup closure in APOE4 microglia"}, "score": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.014150943396226415, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.2289534357664513, "cosine_similarity": -0.3606422488509565, "direction_accuracy": 0.006472491909385114, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_019", "mean_absolute_error": 0.6711359223300971, "by_modality": {"lipid_abundance": {"balanced_direction_accuracy": 0.014150943396226415, "centered_cosine_similarity": -0.2289534357664513, "cosine_similarity": -0.3606422488509565, "direction_accuracy": 0.006472491909385114, "mean_absolute_error": 0.6711359223300971, "n_features": 618}}}, "cost_usd": 2.8575285, "duplicate": false, "cosine_defined": true, "centered_cosine_defined": true, "cohort_rank": 20}], "note": "Previously inspected development panel. Scores rank hypothesis-predictor pairs, not causal validity. Astra and Claude use different predictors and harnesses. Ongoing batches are excluded from this fixed snapshot."};
